Admin = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Admin) (d:ancestor of Jesus in the genealogy of Luke, son of Arni and father of Amminadab) (r:42.3.33)
Adna = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Adna) (d:name of two men, one who had married a foreign wife in the time of Ezra and a priest of the family of Harim) (e:Harim’ suante sung panin ~) (r:16.12.15/15.10.30) (q:draft)
Adnah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Adnah) (d:name of two men, a commander of Manasseh who joined David at Ziklag and a commander of Judah under Jehoshaphat) (r:14.17.14/13.12.20)
Adohijah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Adonijah) (d:Adonijah, the son of David whom Joab supported, as spelled in 1 Kings 2.28) (r:11.2.28)
Adonibezek = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Adoni-Bezek) (d:Canaanite king of Bezek, defeated and captured by the men of Judah) (r:7.1.5/7.1.6)
Adonijah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Adonijah) (d:name of several men, among them the fourth son of David, born to Haggith, who tried to make himself king) (r:10.3.4/11.1.18)
Adonikam = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Adonikam) (d:head of a family that returned from the exile in Babylon) (r:15.8.13)
Adoniram = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Adoniram) (d:son of Abda, the official in charge of forced labour under David and Solomon) (r:11.4.6/10.20.24)
Adonizedek = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Adoni-Zedek) (d:king of Jerusalem who led five Amorite kings against Gibeon and was defeated by Joshua) (r:6.10.1/6.10.3)
Adoram = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Adoniram/Adoram) (d:the official in charge of forced labour, stoned to death when King Rehoboam sent him to Israel, Adoniram in the NIV) (e:aana tawh nasemte a uk ~ sawl a) (r:11.12.18) (q:draft)
Adoram = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Adoraim) (d:town in Judah fortified by Rehoboam, Adoraim in the NIV) (e:~, Lakhish, Azekah) (r:14.11.9) (q:draft)
Adoriam = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Adoraim) (d:town in Judah fortified by Rehoboam) (r:14.11.9)
Adorniram = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Adoniram) (d:Adoniram, the official of Solomon in charge of forced labour, as spelled in 1 Kings 5.14) (r:11.5.14)
Adramittium = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Adramyttium) (d:seaport in the Roman province of Asia, home port of the ship on which Paul began his voyage to Rome) (r:44.27.2)
Adrammelek = (t:name) (w:Adrammelek) (d:name of a god of Sepharvaim to whom children were burned, and of a son of Sennacherib who killed his father) (r:12.17.31/23.37.38)
Adriel = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Adriel) (d:son of Barzillai of Meholah, to whom Merab the daughter of Saul was given as wife) (r:10.21.8/9.18.19)
Adullam = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Adullamite) (d:of Adullam, used with mi for a person from that town, as Hirah the friend of Judah) (r:1.38.1/1.38.20)
Adullam = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Adullam) (d:town in the lowland of Judah, near the cave where David hid from Saul) (r:9.22.1/6.15.35)
Adummim = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Adummim) (d:pass on the border between Judah and Benjamin, on the way up from Jericho) (r:6.15.7/6.18.17)
af = (t:see) <Sha-af>
afas = (t:see) <Kai-afas>
