Afik = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Aphek) (d:town in the territory of Asher whose people were not driven out) (r:7.1.31)
afrah = (t:see) <Bethle-afrah>
After = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ater) (d:Ater, head of a family of temple gatekeepers that returned from exile, as spelled in Ezra 2.42) (r:15.2.42)
Agabas = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Agabus) (d:Christian prophet from Judea who foretold a great famine and the arrest of Paul) (r:44.21.10/44.11.28)
Agag = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Agag) (d:king of the Amalekites, taken alive by Saul) (r:9.15.8)
agate = (t:n) (c:stone) (w:agate) (d:English loanword for a precious stone, used with suang, stone, or suangmanpha, precious stone) (e:~ suang leh amethist suang/jakinth suang, ~ suang leh amethist suang | jacinth, agate and amethyst/a thumna-ah ~ suangmanpha | the third was agate) (r:2.39.12/2.28.19/66.21.19) (q:draft)
Agee = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Agee) (d:a Hararite, father of Shammah, one of the mighty men of David) (r:10.23.11)
agik = (t:n) (w:weight) (d:gik, heavy, with the prefix a written joined: heaviness, weight; agik tehna is the measuring of weight) (e:asau tehna, ~ tehna, atam tehnate/~ tehna, atam tehnate ah | in measuring weight and quantity) (s:gikzah/gihna) (b:gik) (r:3.19.35) (q:draft)
Agrippa = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Agrippa) (d:King Herod Agrippa II, before whom Paul made his defence at Caesarea) (r:44.26.19/44.26.27)
Agur = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Agur) (d:son of Jakeh, whose sayings are in Proverbs 30) (e:Jakeh’ tapa ~’ thugente) (r:20.30.1) (q:draft)
ah = (t:ppm) (d:postpositional marker indicating place or time) (e:Koi lai-~ om hiam/Zeisu Oliv Mual ~ a pai hi | Jesus went to the Mount of Olives/Efesa khua ~ ka om ding hi | I will stay at Ephesus/Kumpipa’ kongtual-~ Mordekai om hi | Mordecai was at the gate of the king/Moses in Topa mai-~ amau’ thu gen hi | Moses brought their case before the Lord) (r:43.8.1/1.1.2/46.16.8/17.2.19/4.27.5)
Ahab = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ahab) (d:king of Israel, son of Omri and husband of Jezebel) (e:~ a sih khit ciangin) (r:12.1.1/11.22.40) (q:draft)
ahang = (t:n) (w:reason/cause) (d:hang, reason, with the prefix a written joined: its reason, the reason for it; ahang kan is to ask the reason why) (e:kuamah in ~ a kan thei kei hi/A bawl nate kuamah in ~ a kan thei kei hi | no one can ask the reason for what he does) (b:hang) (r:27.4.35) (q:draft)
