aman = (t:adv) (w:truly/verily/rightly) (d:In truth, a with man, true; Ke’n aman takpi kong cih-inah is the fixed phrase truly I tell you, and aman takin means rightly.) (e:Ke’n ~ takpi kong cih-inah/~ takin thu na khen un | judge rightly/~ takpi-in kong ci hi | truly I tell you/Hih pa in ~ takpi-in kamsangpa ahi hi | this man truly is the prophet) (s:takpi/taktak/mantakin/taktakin) (b:man) (r:40.25.12/43.7.24/40.18.13/43.7.40) (q:draft)
aman = (t:adj) (w:true/right/just) (d:True or right, a with man; said of a word or a testimony, and aman lo means not right, unjust.) (e:~ lo thukhen mangpa’ thugenna/Ama teci pan’na thu ~ hi | his testimony is true/Tua thu ~ hi | that is right/Na teci pan’na ~ kei hi | your testimony is not true/thu khatpeuh ~ hiam, man lo hiam | whether a thing is right or not right) (s:man/maan) (a:manlo) (b:man) (r:42.18.6/43.19.35/43.13.13/43.8.13/42.12.57) (q:draft)
Amana = (t:name) (c:mountain) (w:Amana) (d:mountain in the Anti-Lebanon range, named together with Senir and Hermon) (e:~ Mual dawn panin hong taisuk inla) (r:22.4.8) (q:draft)
amanin = (t:conj) (w:because) (d:Because, a spelling of manin after ahih; ahih amanin, usually written ahih manin, means because it is so.) (e:nusia khin ahih ~ amah mu zo lo) (b:manin) (r:28.5.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
amanlangin = (t:adv) (w:soon/quickly/at once/immediately) (d:Quickly or soon, manlangin written together with the prefix a.) (e:note kiangah ~ kong sawl ding hi) (s:pahpah/thakhatin) (a:damdamin) (b:manlangin) (r:50.2.23) (q:draft)
amanpha = (t:adj) (w:precious/valuable/costly) (d:Precious or costly, manpha written together with the prefix a and placed before the noun, as in amanpha sing, costly wood.) (e:ahoih ~ nate a dimin om hi/~ sing tawh, sumngo tawh, sik tawh | with costly wood, bronze and iron) (b:manpha) (r:20.24.4/66.18.12) (q:draft)
Amariah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Amariah) (d:name of several men, among them a priest descended from Aaron, son of Meraioth) (r:13.6.7/16.12.2)
amasa = (t:adv) (w:first/at first/at the beginning/before) (d:First or at first, masa written together with the prefix a; amasa bangin means as before and amasa sanga means than the first.) (e:lo khawh lawhte in ~ bangin ahih zel/~-a eite tungah Kha Siangtho a hong tun’ mah bangin | as the Holy Spirit came on us at the beginning/~-in amau kiangah a pai zawh thu | how he first went to them/~ sanga a tam zaw galkap | an army larger than the first) (a:anung/nunungin) (b:masa) (r:40.21.36/44.11.15/44.15.14/27.11.13) (q:draft)
Amasa = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Amasa) (d:name of two men, among them the son of Abigail and Jether, a nephew of David and commander of the army of Absalom) (e:Judahte sam dingin ~ pai hi) (r:10.20.5/13.2.17) (q:draft)
Amasa = (t:adv) (w:first/first of all/at first) (d:A masa, first, written as one word at the start of a sentence; Amasa bel-a and Amasa belin mean first of all.) (e:~ bel-a theih ding akilawm thu/~-in tate kivak kham ta hen | first let the children eat their fill/~ belin Judah mi, a nung ciangin Grik mi | first the Jew, then the Greek/~-a ka kihutna thu ka gen lai takin | when I made my first defense) (a:anung/nunungin) (r:61.3.3/45.2.10/41.7.27/55.4.16) (q:draft)
Amasai = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Amasai) (d:name of several Levites, among them a son of Elkanah of the clan of Kohath) (r:13.6.25/13.6.35)
