Amashsai = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Amashsai) (d:priest, son of Azarel, who lived in Jerusalem in the time of Nehemiah) (r:16.11.13)
Amasiah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Amasiah) (d:son of Zikri, a commander in the army of King Jehoshaphat of Judah) (r:14.17.16)
amau = (t:pron) (w:those/they/their/them) (d:Third person plural pronoun, they or them; before a noun, often written amau’ with an apostrophe, it means their.) (e:Moses in Topa mai-ah ~’ thu gen hi | Moses brought their case before the Lord/~ gamtatna bangin thukkik in | pay them back according to their deeds/~ laitheipa khat in Zeisu ze-et a | one of them, an expert in the law, tested Jesus/~ aw kiza lo hi | their voice is not heard) (s:amaute) (r:4.27.5/25.3.64/40.22.35/19.19.3)
Amau = (t:pron) (w:their/they/them) (d:Third person plural, amau written with a capital at the start of a sentence or a line of verse; before a noun it means their, and before kiangah it means to them.) (e:~ lungsim tung uhah ka gelh ding hi/~ khe un mi sisan suah dingin a manlang | their feet are swift to shed blood/~ kiangah Moses leh Elijah kilang a | Moses and Elijah appeared to them/~ paina lampi-ah kisiatna leh gimna a dim hi | ruin and misery fill their ways) (s:Amaute) (b:amau) (r:58.10.16/45.11.27/45.3.15/40.17.3/45.3.16) (q:draft)
amaute = (t:pron) (w:they) (d:Third person plural pronoun, amau with the plural te; as the subject it is usually followed by in.) (e:~ in sikha sa uh a/gilkial dangtakin ~ sibup uh hi | hungry and thirsty, they grew faint/~ in Isaak leh Rebekah’ nuntakna haksasak uh hi | they made life bitter for Isaac and Rebekah/a genna thu ~ in a thei kei uh hi | they did not understand what he said) (b:amau) (r:42.24.37/19.107.5/1.26.35/42.2.50)
amaute = (t:pron) (w:them) (d:Third person plural pronoun as the object of a verb or before tawh, with, and kiangah, to.) (e:Pasian in ~ thupha pia a/thong sungah ni thum sung ~ koih hi | he put them in prison for three days/tua Topa in ~ zahko hi | the Lord scoffs at them/~ tawh na gamta khawm kei un | do not be partners with them) (b:amau) (r:1.1.22/1.42.17/19.2.4/49.5.7)
Amaute = (t:pron) (w:they/them/their) (d:Amaute written with a capital at the start of a sentence or line; they, them or their depending on its place in the sentence.) (e:~ puan bangin na zial ding hi/~ in sawtpi a tam khit uh ciangin | after they had stayed a long time/~ khan’sih uh a, zumhuaipi-in bei uh hi | they die young and end in shame/~’ om laitakin Baruk kiangah | in their presence, to Baruch/~ phuisam in la | curse them) (s:Amau) (b:amaute) (r:58.1.12/24.51.14/44.15.33/18.36.14/24.32.13/25.3.65) (q:draft)
amauteng = (t:pron) (w:they themselves/all of them/by themselves) (d:Amau, they, with teng, all: they as a group; with guak or bek it means by themselves, alone.) (e:~ guak a om laitakin/~ in a puante a hawm uh hi | they divided his clothes among themselves/~ guak mualtung khatah a paipihto hi | he led them up a mountain by themselves/~ bek a om theih nadingun | so that they could be by themselves) (b:amau) (r:41.13.3/41.15.24/41.9.2/42.9.10) (q:draft)
Amaw = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Amaw) (d:the people or land where Balaam lived, near the Euphrates; the NIV has in his native land) (e:~ mite’ gam Gun gei Pethor-ah) (r:4.22.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
amawkna = (t:adj) (w:vain/worthless/empty) (d:Vain or worthless, mawkna written together with the prefix a; amawkna kamsiate is worthless coarse talk.) (e:~ kamsiate zong paaikhia un) (b:mawkna) (r:49.5.4) (q:draft)
amawknapi = (t:n) (w:nonsense/vanity/empty thing) (d:Something wholly vain or empty, nonsense; amawkna with the strengthening suffix pi.) (e:~ tawh hehnep nong sawm uh hi) (s:hawmpi/thumawkna) (b:amawkna) (r:18.21.34) (q:draft)
Amaziah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Amaziah) (d:name of several men, among them a king of Judah, son of Joash, and a priest of Bethel in the time of Amos) (r:12.14.1/12.12.21)
ameet = (t:n) (w:interest/usury) (d:Interest on a loan, meet written together with a, its; ameet la means take interest.) (e:Leiba ~ kilakna phiat ni/ama tung panin ~ akhang la kei un | do not take interest or profit from him/~ na kila uh hi | you are charging one another interest) (s:amet/met) (b:meet) (r:16.5.10/3.25.36/16.5.7) (q:draft)
Amelek = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Amalek) (d:Amalek, the people descended from a grandson of Esau; Amelek mi is an Amalekite) (e:Keimah in ~ mi ka hi hi) (r:10.1.8) (q:draft)
Amelekte = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Amalekites) (d:the Amalekites, a people of the desert south of Canaan and enemies of Israel) (b:Amelek) (r:10.1.1/9.30.1)
