anduh = (t:v) (w:be hungry for food/crave food) (d:an, food, with duh, want or crave: hunger for food; anduh gilkial lohna is a place where nobody goes hungry for bread) (e:~ gilkial lohna Egypt gamah) (r:24.42.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
Anem = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Anem) (d:Levitical town in the territory of Issachar, given to the descendants of Gershon) (r:13.6.73)
Aner = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Aner) (d:Amorite ally of Abram, brother of Mamre and Eshkol; also a Levitical town in the territory of Manasseh) (r:1.14.24)
aneu = (t:adj) (w:small/the small) (d:neu, small, with the prefix a: that which is small, the small one; mostly in the pair alian aneu, great and small alike) (e:ganhing alian ~, sim zawh loh-a a tam/alian ~-in thupha hong pia ding hi | he will bless small and great alike/A hau a zawng, alian ~ | rich and poor, great and small) (s:neu) (a:alian) (b:neu) (r:19.104.25/19.115.13/23.19.15) (q:draft)
ang = (t:n) (w:bosom/lap/arms/breast) (d:the front of the body where a child or loved one is held: the lap, the arms, the breast; ang sungah is in the lap or at the breast) (e:Ka ~-ah ka ngaihno hong lup/Na ~ sungah meikuang pom lecin | if you hold fire in your lap/Simeon in Zeisu a ~-ah pomin | Simeon took Jesus in his arms/a nute uh ~ ah a si uh hi | they die in their mothers’ arms/ka nu’ ~ sungah muanhuai-in | safe at my mother’s breast) (s:angsung) (r:22.1.13/42.2.28/20.6.27/25.2.12/19.22.9) (q:draft)
angah = (t:adv) (w:in the arms/at the bosom/in the lap) (d:ang, bosom or lap, with the marker ah, in or at: in the arms, at the breast; angah tawi is take up in the arms) (e:Naomi in naungeek la-in a ~ tawi a/a koih khit ciangin a ~ tawi-in | after placing him there he took him in his arms/ama tapa si keima ~ hong koih hi | she laid her dead son at my breast) (b:ang) (r:8.4.16/41.9.36/11.3.20) (q:draft)
Angawi = (t:v) (w:grind grain) (d:an, grain, with gawi, grind: grind grain; here written as one word with a capital at the start of a sentence) (e:~ khawm numei nih in) (r:40.24.41) (q:draft, low confidence)
angawina = (t:n) (w:mill/hand mill/grinding place) (d:the place or tool for grinding grain, from an gawi, grind grain, with the noun suffix na; angawina suang is a millstone) (e:a lian ~ suang tawh kibang suang khat/~ suang bangin sakin | hard as a millstone/amah in thong sung ~-ah an gawi hi | he ground grain at the mill in the prison/~ suang gingte ka gingsak nawn kei ding | I will no longer let the sound of the millstones be heard) (r:66.18.21/7.16.21/18.41.24/24.25.10) (q:draft)
angkawm = (t:n) (w:adultery/adulterer) (d:unfaithfulness to a husband or wife, and a person guilty of it; angkawm ahi is commits adultery and angkawm hat is given to adultery) (e:a kiteengte in ~ ahi uh hi/A vekpi-un ~ hat hi khin uh a | they are all adulterers) (s:angkawmna/palhngulhna) (r:40.19.9/24.9.2) (q:draft)
angkawmin = (t:v) (w:commit adultery) (d:angkawm, commit adultery, with the linking ending in, which joins it to the following verb) (e:tual that-in, ~, a hi lopi kiciam-in/~, numei paktatte’ inn-ah a hon om uh hi | they committed adultery and crowded into the houses of prostitutes) (b:angkawm) (r:24.7.9/24.23.14/24.5.7) (q:draft)
angkawmna = (t:n) (w:adultery) (d:angkawm, commit adultery, with the noun suffix na: the act of adultery) (e:na ~, na hukna) (s:palhngulhna) (b:angkawm) (r:24.13.27) (q:draft)
angkawmsak = (t:v) (w:cause to commit adultery/make an adulteress) (d:angkawm, commit adultery, with the causative sak: make someone commit adultery) (e:midang tawh a zi ~ a suak hi) (b:angkawm) (r:40.5.32) (q:draft)
angkawmte = (t:n) (w:adulterers) (d:angkawm, commit adultery, with the plural te: people who commit adultery) (e:mun khempeuhah ~ a dim hi) (b:angkawm) (r:24.23.10) (q:draft)
angsung = (t:n) (w:self-interest/own good/own advantage) (d:literally the inside of the bosom: what is for oneself; angsung ding bek is only for oneself, and angsung ngaihsun is think of one’s own good) (e:note’ ~ ding bek zong kei unla/keima ~ ngaihsun loin | not thinking of my own good/amau ~ ding bek ngaihsunin | thinking only of themselves/amau’ ~ ding bek khualna-in | caring only for their own interest) (r:46.10.24/36.3.4/46.10.33/55.3.2) (q:draft)
angsung = (t:n) (w:bosom/breast/arms) (d:ang, bosom, with sung, inside: the bosom or arms where a child is held or nursed) (e:~ panin a kilakhia/Amaute in a ~ uhah na tapate tawi-in | they will carry your sons in their arms) (s:ang) (r:23.28.9/23.49.22) (q:draft)
angtan = (t:see) <angtan'pih>
angtan'pih = (t:n) (w:pride) (d:what someone is proud of, from angtang, be proud, with pih; Jakob' angtan'pih is the pride of Jacob) (e:Ama itpa Jakob’ ~ ahi | the pride of Jacob, whom he loved) (r:19.47.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
angtang = (t:v) (w:boast/be proud/glory in) (d:be proud of or boast in someone or something; before a suffix the form is angtan, as in angtanpih and angtanhuai) (e:kote ka ~ ngitnget uh a) (s:kisathei/kisial/kiphasak) (a:kiniamkhiat) (r:19.44.8) (q:draft)
angtanhuai = (t:adj) (w:honourable/a matter of pride) (d:angtan, the form of angtang, be proud, used before a suffix, with huai, worthy of: bringing honour, something to be proud of) (e:nang a dingin ~ mahmah hi) (s:pahtawihuai) (a:maizumhuai/zumhuai) (r:42.14.10) (q:draft)
angtanpih = (t:v) (w:be proud of/take pride in/boast of) (d:angtan, the form of angtang, boast, used before a suffix, with pih: be proud of someone or something; also said of the thing one is proud of, Israel-te’ angtanpih, the pride of Israel) (e:note ka hong ~ mahmah hi/Ama it Israel-te’ ~ | the pride of Israel, whom he loves) (s:kisaktheihpih/kiphatsakpih/kisialhpih) (r:50.4.1/19.47.4) (q:draft)
angvan = (t:n) (w:partiality/favoritism/favor) (d:taking the side of one person over another; angvan nei is show partiality, and angvan nei lo is impartial) (e:Thukhenna ah ~ na nei kei ding uh hi/~ nei loin, sumgolh a la lo | showing no partiality and taking no bribe/Pasian in kuamah ~’ tuam nei loin | God shows no favoritism to anyone/~ tuam na nei kei ding uh hi | you shall not show partiality) (s:angvanna/khentuam/deidanna) (r:5.1.17/5.10.17/44.10.34/5.16.19) (q:draft)
angvan = (t:v) (w:favor/show partiality/take the side of) (d:take the side of someone, either unfairly, show partiality, or in kindness, show favor) (e:amah na ~ hun ding hi ta hi/Pasian ~ ding a, ama ading gensak ding | will you favor God and argue his case/note kong ~ nawn kei ding hi | I will show you favor no more) (s:maipha) (r:19.102.13/18.13.8/24.16.13) (q:draft)
angvanin = (t:v) (w:be partial to/favor/take the side of) (d:angvan, show partiality or favor, with the linking suffix in, which joins it to the following verb) (e:Mi mawhte ~ diksak ding hoih lo a/kote hong ~ na hong gualzosak hi | favoring us, you give us victory) (b:angvan) (r:20.18.5/19.89.17) (q:draft)
angvanna = (t:n) (w:partiality/favouritism/favour) (d:angvan, favor or take sides, with the noun suffix na: the taking of one person’s side, partiality or favor; angvanna zang and angvanna nei are show partiality) (e:migilote tungah ~ zang ding na hi/A simthamin ~ na zat uh leh | if you secretly show partiality/~ na nei kei ding uh hi | you shall not show partiality/nangma ~ tawh kote nong gualzo sak hi | by your favor you give us victory) (s:khentuam/deidanna/guptuam) (b:angvan) (r:19.82.2/5.16.19/18.13.10/19.89.17) (q:draft)
anhai = (t:n) (w:glutton) (d:one who is greedy for food, from an, food, with hai, be greedy for; paired with zuhai, drunkard) (e:amah in ~ zuhai ahi hi/~ thadah mi ahi uh hi | they are lazy gluttons/Zuhai, ~ pa | a drunkard and a glutton) (r:5.21.20/56.1.12/42.7.34) (q:draft)
anhaihna = (t:n) (w:sifting of grain/sieve) (d:an, grain, with haih, sift or winnow, and na: the sifting of grain; anhaihna ciang is the tool it is done with, a sieve in the NIV) (e:~ ciang tawh an a kihaih mah bangin) (s:haihna) (r:30.9.9) (q:draft)
