anhuanna = (t:n) (w:cooking) (d:anhuan, cook food, with the noun suffix na: cooking; anhuanna beel is a cooking pot) (e:Hih khuapi in ~ beel tawh kibang a) (s:huanna) (b:anhuan) (r:26.11.3) (q:draft)
anhuanpa = (t:n) (w:cook) (d:anhuan, cook food, with -pa, a man: the man who cooks) (e:Tua ciangin Samuel in ~ kiangah/~ in a khe leh a kawngsa la-in | the cook took up the leg and the meat on it) (s:huanpa) (b:anhuan) (r:9.9.23/9.9.24) (q:draft)
aniam = (t:adv) (w:low) (d:niam, low, with the prefix a written as one word) (b:niam) of position or state
