ankan = (t:n) (w:roasted grain/parched grain) (d:an, grain, with kan, roast dry: grain roasted dry and eaten as ready food) (e:Hih ~ seu khat leh hih anlum/silngo sawhloh moh leh ~ ne uh hi | they ate unleavened bread and roasted grain/leh ~ lawh nga | and five measures of roasted grain/an, ~, bepi leh basan | flour, roasted grain, beans and lentils) (r:9.17.17/6.5.11/9.25.18/10.17.28) (q:draft)
ankante = (t:n) (w:roasted grain/parched grain) (d:ankan roasted grain, with the plural te) (e:tua pa in ~ tua nu a pia hi) (b:ankan) (r:8.2.14) (q:draft)
ankhamin = (t:v) (w:be gorged with food/overeat) (d:an, food, with kham, be sated or drunk, and the linking suffix in; zukham ankhamin is drunk and gorged) (e:zukham ~ ommawk leh) (r:42.12.45) (q:draft, low confidence)
Ankhamna = (t:name) (w:Ankhamna) (d:not a proper name: ankhamna, having plenty to eat, written with a capital at the start of a sentence, the opposite of gilkialna, hunger) (r:50.4.12)
ankhamvalte = (t:n) (w:leftovers/leftover food) (d:the food left over after eating one's fill: an food, kham be sated, val surplus, with the plural te) (e:a ~ zong la-in a pia hi) (s:khamvalte) (r:8.2.18) (q:draft)
ankhing = (t:n) (w:food/grain) (d:food or grain as a thing lent, named beside sumgum, money, in the law against lending at interest; the part khing is not explained by the verse) (e:sumgum hitaleh, ~ hitaleh) (r:5.23.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
ankholna = (t:n) (w:grain storage/storehouse) (d:an, food or grain, with kholna, storing: the storing of grain; ankholna inn is a storehouse or granary) (e:Josef in ~ innte khempeuh hongin) (r:1.41.56) (q:draft)
