ankung = (t:n) (w:vegetation) (d:an, food or grain, with kung, plant: the green plants of the field taken together) (e:~ khempeuh a dumsakpa in Topa ahi hi/~ tunga guahzu bang ta hen | let it be like rain falling on the plants) (r:38.10.1/5.32.2)
ankung = (t:n) (w:crop) (d:the grain plant growing in the field; ankung ding lai is standing grain) (e:~ ding laite tungah phiaukawi/~ ding laite na at kei ding uh hi | you must not reap the standing grain/a kisattan ~ bangin keu pah hi | they wither at once like cut grain/~ natna ahi a | or a disease of the crops) (r:5.16.9/5.23.25/18.24.24/11.8.37)
