anla = (t:v) (w:reap/harvest) (d:an, grain, with la, take: gather in the grain; anla pa is the reaper and anla nasemte are the harvesters) (e:~ nasemte pen vantung mite ahi hi/Khaituh pa le ~ pa | the sower and the reaper/~ dingin phiaukawi a tawite | those who hold the sickle to reap/~ pa thaman a kipiak mah bangin | as the reaper is given his wages) (s:at/aat) (a:tuh/vawh) (r:40.13.39/43.4.36/24.50.16) (q:draft)
anlak = (t:n) (w:harvest/reaping) (d:the gathering in of the grain; anlak hun is harvest time and anlak na sem is work at the harvest) (e:tuk ~ hun ciangin bangmah nei lo/lo pawi hun leh ~ hun | seedtime and harvest/lo khawh hun leh ~ hunin na tawlnga ding uh hi | in plowing time and at harvest you shall rest/gil kialpi-in ~ na sem uh hi | they work at the harvest and go hungry) (s:atna) (r:20.20.4/41.12.2/1.8.22/2.34.21/18.24.10) (q:draft)
anlakna = (t:n) (w:harvest/harvesting) (d:anlak, harvest, with the noun suffix na: the gathering of the crop, and the crop gathered) (e:ama ~ ah a anpalte ahi uh hi/Amaute’ ~ lo mitsuan inla | watch the field where they are harvesting/na ~ uh hangin lungdamna tawh kikonate | the shouts of joy over your harvest/Na ~ pan leh na suknate panun | from your harvest and from your presses) (s:atna) (b:anlak) (r:24.2.3/23.16.9/8.2.9/2.22.29) (q:draft)
anlate = (t:n) (w:harvesters/reapers) (d:those who cut and gather the grain, from an la, reap grain, with the plural ending -te) (e:a pa kiang ~ lakah pai hi/Boaz in ~ a uk a nasempa kiangah | Boaz said to the servant in charge of the harvesters/~’ nung lo sungah ansangte a tawm hi | she gleaned in the field behind the harvesters/Anlak hun ciangin ~ kiangah | at harvest time, to the harvesters) (s:atte) (b:anla) (r:12.4.18/8.2.5/8.2.3/40.13.30) (q:draft)
anletui = (t:n) (w:food and drink/food and water) (d:an, food, le, and, tui, water, written as one word: food and drink) (e:amaute ~ tawh a vak hi/~ zong a ne kei hi | he did not eat or drink anything/~ tawh Israel mite na dawn lo uh a | they did not meet the Israelites with food and water/kuamah in ~ a lui kei ding uh a | no one will offer them food and drink) (s:nekledawn) (r:11.18.4/44.9.9/16.13.2/24.16.7) (q:draft)
anli = (t:n) (w:self-sown grain) (d:grain that comes up by itself without being sown; anli pote, the things that grow from it) (e:kumin ~ pote na ne ding uh a) (r:23.37.30) (q:draft, low confidence)
