anvai = (t:n) (w:powder)
anvai = (t:n) (w:cornflour/cornstarch/maize starch)
anvaite = (t:n) (w:chaff) (d:anvai, chaff, with the plural te) (e:~ a zapsiang dingin a nung huih) (s:ansite) (b:anvai) (r:24.4.11) (q:draft)
anvak = (t:v) (w:feed/pasture/tend) (d:give food to and look after, said of animals) (e:lonona munah tuunote ~ bangin) (s:vaak) (r:28.4.16) (q:draft)
anvakna = (t:n) (w:banquet/giving of a meal/feeding) (d:anvak, give food to, with the noun suffix na: the giving of a meal to guests; anvakna pawi, a banquet) (e:Tua bangin ~ pawi na bawl ciangin/na ~ thaman a ngahkik na hi ding hi | you will have received back the reward for your meal) (s:lawmvakna) (b:anvak) (r:42.14.13/42.14.12) (q:draft)
anvui = (t:n) (w:ear of grain/head of grain) (d:an, grain, with vui, ear: grain still in the ear) (e:leh ~ athak a van sungah hong pua hi) (s:buhvui) (r:12.4.42) (q:draft)
anvuite = (t:n) (w:ears of grain/heads of grain) (d:anvui, ear of grain, with the plural te; the NIV has leftover grain) (e:~ lakah a sang hong tawmsak in) (s:buhvuite) (b:anvui) (r:8.2.2) (q:draft)
anzapna = (t:n) (w:winnowing fork/winnowing fan) (d:the tool for winnowing grain: an, grain, and zap, fan, with the noun suffix na) (e:a khutah ~ tawi-in a ante zap a) (s:lawhpi) (r:40.3.12) (q:draft)
ap = (t:v) (w:dedicate/consecrate/entrust/commit/hand over) (d:hand over or entrust to someone, especially give over to God or set apart as holy; ki-ap is dedicated or devoted) (e:amaute in letsongte ~ uh hi/Topa tungah a inn a ~ ciangin | when he dedicates his house to the Lord/a neih khempeuh Josef khut sungah ~ hi | he entrusted all he had to Joseph/Topa tungah na vai teng ~ in | commit all your affairs to the Lord) (r:13.26.27/3.8.10/3.27.14/1.39.6/19.37.5) (q:draft)
apa = (t:n) (w:male) (d:a male animal, pa with the prefix a; the opposite is anu, a female one) (e:biak nadingin keel ~ khat/a sitbang lo tuuno ~ nih | two male lambs without defect/a sitbang lo ~ khat na pia ding uh hi | you must offer a male without defect) (a:anu) (b:pa) (r:3.9.3/3.3.6/3.14.10/3.22.19) (q:draft)
apang = (t:adj) (w:aside) on one side
Apangtatte = (t:n) (w:adulterers/adulterous people) (d:plural with te, used to address unfaithful people; the build of the word is not confirmed) (e:~ aw, leitung tawh kipawlna in) (s:angkawmte) (r:59.4.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
apawl = (t:n) (w:every kind/all sorts) (d:pawl, group or kind, with the prefix a; doubled as apawl apawl or apawl pawl it means of every kind, in every way) (e:nopna ~ pawl hong pia ta hen/vasa ~ ~ khempeuh | birds of every kind/kihhuai gilo bawlna ~ ~ a piangsak uh hi | they bring about every kind of vile evil deed/Kote in bawlsiatna ~ ~ ka thuak uh hangin | though we suffer every kind of affliction) (s:namciat) (b:pawl) (r:53.3.16/59.3.7/59.3.16/47.4.8) (q:draft)
apawlah = (t:adv) (w:in every kind) (d:a pawl, a group or kind, with the place marker ah; the doubled apawl apawlah means in every kind of) (e:thu ahoih apawl ~ note hong kipsak) (b:apawl) (r:53.2.17) (q:draft, low confidence)
apawlpawl = (t:adj) (w:of many kinds/all kinds of/various) (d:placed after a noun: of every sort, kind by kind; pawlpawl with the prefix a) (e:ze-etna ~ na thuak uh ciangin/Ganhing ~ khempeuh | all kinds of animals/pilna ~ tawh note sungah om ta hen | let it dwell in you with all wisdom/gamtatpha ~ tawh na dim mahmah nadingun | so that you abound in every good work) (s:namcin/atuamtuam) (b:pawlpawl) (r:59.1.2/59.3.7/51.3.16/47.9.8) (q:draft)
apawlpawlte = (t:n) (w:all kinds/various kinds) (d:pawl, group or kind, doubled, with the prefix a and the plural suffix te; follows a noun, every kind of it, ahoih na apawlpawlte is every good work) (e:kha la leh phatna la ~ tawh/ahoih na ~ a sep theih nading a | so that he can do every kind of good work) (b:apawlpawl) (r:49.5.19/55.3.16) (q:draft)
apawlte = (t:n) (w:every kind/each kind) (d:a pawl, a group or kind, with the plural te; the doubled apawl apawlte means every kind of) (e:thungaih lohna apawl ~ in thuak ding) (b:apawl) (r:58.2.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
Apelles = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Apelles) (d:Christian in Rome whom Paul greets as tested and approved in Christ) (r:45.16.10)
Apfia = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Apphia) (d:Christian woman greeted in the letter of Paul to Philemon) (r:57.1.2)
apha = (t:adj) (w:good) (d:a pha written as one word; also stands alone as that which is good) (e:thuman leh ~ lungsim tawh thu/Tua ahih ciangin ci ~ hi | so then, salt is good/hehpihna thupha tawh ~ lametna | good hope by grace/~ leh asia thei hi | he knows good and evil) (s:ahoih) (a:asia) (b:pha) (r:42.8.15/42.14.34/53.2.16/1.3.22) (q:draft)
aphuai = (t:see) <bil-aphuai>
apian = (t:see) <apian'cil>
apian'cil = (t:n) (w:creation/beginning) (d:the time something first came into being: a pian come into being, with cil beginning; lei apian'cil a kipan, since the creation of the world) (e:lei ~ a kipan kilangin a kimu hi | has been clearly seen since the creation of the world) (s:piancil) (r:45.1.20) (q:draft)
apiang = (t:v) (w:be born/be descended) (d:the prefix a written together with piang, be born or come into being; mi thagolte sung panin apiang is one born from among the giants) (e:mi thagolte sung panin ~ ahi hi) (b:piang) (r:10.21.20) (q:draft)
apin = (t:v) (w:hand over/entrust/deliver) (d:ap, give into the charge of someone, with the linking ending in, used when another action follows) (e:thukhente in palikte kiangah hong ~/thukhente in palikte khut sungah hong ~ | the judge hands you over to the officers/hih sumte a cingin amaute tungah ~ | handing this money over to them in full) (b:ap) (r:42.12.58/45.15.28/40.5.25) (q:draft)
apin = (t:v) (w:consecrate/dedicate) (d:ap in the sense of setting apart for God, with the linking ending in) (e:Jessi le a tapate ~) (s:siangthosakin) (b:ap) (r:9.16.5) (q:draft)
Apis = (t:name) (w:Apis) (d:the sacred bull god of Egypt, named in the prophecy of Jeremiah against Egypt) (e:na bawngtal pasian uh ~ guallelin taimang) (r:24.46.15) (q:draft)
apkhapna = (t:n) (w:panic/terror) (d:sudden great fear that spreads among many people) (e:mite lakah ~ om hi/tua khuapi langpan’in ~ lianpi piangsak a | he caused a great panic against that city/a khuapi sung khempeuh ah sidek tak-a ~ om hi | there was a deadly panic throughout the city) (s:patauhna) (r:9.14.15/9.5.9/9.5.11) (q:draft)
apkhawm = (t:v) (w:dedicate together/consecrate together) (d:ap, dedicate, with khawm, together: dedicate or consecrate along with other things or people) (e:kham tawh Topa’ tungah a ~ hi/a puante uh tawh a ~ hi | he consecrated them together with their garments) (b:ap) (r:13.18.11/3.8.30) (q:draft)
apkik = (t:v) (w:hand back/give back/return) (d:ap, hand over or entrust, with kik, back) (e:kiang mahah na ~ kei ding uh hi/ka topa’ khut sungah nong ~ loh nading | that you will not hand me back to my master/Topa’ tungah a ~ a ta’ tang dingin | in place of the child she gave back to the Lord) (s:piakik) (b:ap) (r:5.23.15/9.30.15/9.2.20) (q:draft)
Apkikna = (t:n) (w:dedication/rededication) (d:apkik, hand back, with the noun suffix na; Biakinn Apkikna Pawi is the Festival of Dedication of the temple) (e:Biakinn ~ Pawi bawl hun hong tung a) (r:43.10.22) (q:draft)
apna = (t:n) (w:dedication/consecration) (d:the act of giving something over to God or to a sacred use; often written ki-apna, being dedicated) (e:milim ~ dingin milim mai-ah/lungdamna lianpi tawh Pasian’ inn ~ bawl uh hi | they celebrated the dedication of the house of God with great joy/ni sagih sung biakna tau ~ bawlin | dedicating the altar for seven days/Israel makaite ~ biakna ahi hi | it was the dedication offering of the leaders of Israel) (b:ap) (r:27.3.3/26.43.26/15.6.16/4.7.84) (q:draft)
apnate = (t:n) (w:those entrusted) (d:ap, hand over or entrust, with na and the plural te: here the people into whose hands the money was given) (e:sum a ~ uh tung panin amaute in) (b:ap) (r:12.12.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
