bai = (t:adj) (w:lame/crippled) (d:unable to walk properly; as a verb, be lame, limp) (e:a khe a langnih-in a ~ hi/amah a khete ~ hi | he is lame in his feet/a khete a ~ tapa khat | a son who was lame in his feet/a liam a ~, ahih kei leh a cina | the injured, the lame or the sick) (s:khebai/khezaw/khelbai) (r:10.9.13/1.32.31/10.9.3/10.4.4/39.1.13) (q:draft)
baih = (t:adv) (w:early/soon/quickly) (d:placed after a verb: early, soon or quickly; tho baih is rise early) (e:Thong sunga kikhum mite kikhah ~ ding hi/zingsangin Jakob tho ~ a | Jacob rose early in the morning/tu ni-a hong hici ciah ~ na hi uh hiam | have you come home so early today/Kei kiangah na hong pai ~ theih nadingin | so that you can come to me quickly/ni hong tung ~ ding hi | the day will come soon) (s:tungin/pak) (r:23.51.14/2.2.18/1.28.18/55.4.9/29.3.14) (q:draft)
baih = (t:adj) (w:easy) (d:not hard to do; baih zaw means easier) (e:Bang ci leng a ~ zaw hiam/nang adingin ~ zaw ding hi | it will be easier for you/a lampi ~ a, mi tampi in a zui uh hi | the road is easy, and many follow it/a ~ lua mahmah nasep ahi hi | it is a very easy task) (s:ol) (a:haksa/hak) (r:40.9.5/2.18.22/40.7.13/23.49.6) (q:draft)
baihin = (t:adv) (w:early) (d:baih with the adverb ending in; tho baihin is rising early) (e:Joshua tho ~ mite sam a/A zing ciangin mite tho ~ | the next day the people rose early/Hezekiah tho ~ khuapi sung ukna-za neite khawm a | Hezekiah rose early and gathered the city officials/Zingsangin tho ~, leengguite a sel nai hiam | let us rise early and see whether the vines have budded) (s:tungin) (b:baih) (r:6.8.10/7.21.4/14.29.20/22.7.12) (q:draft)
baihlam = (t:see) <baihlam-a>
baihlam-a = (t:adv) (w:easily/hastily/quickly) (d:baihlam, easy, with a: in an easy or hasty way, said of wealth gained too soon) (e:A ~ hauh pakna in) (r:20.20.21) (q:draft)
baihna = (t:n) (w:ease/quickness) (d:noun form of baih, easy or soon, placed after a verb: zol baihna is being easy to persuade, sih baihna is dying early) (e:sih ~ ding lampi zuatna ahi hi/lungnemna ahi hi, zol ~ ahi hi | it is gentle, it is easily persuaded) (b:baih) (r:20.7.27/59.3.17) (q:draft, low confidence)
baihsa = (t:adj) (w:ready/prepared) (d:usually as a baihsa-in, in readiness) (e:a ~-in om un/sakolte a ~-in kikoih a | the horses are made ready/Ka thu a gen dingin a ~-in ka om | I am ready to state my case/Tu-in na khempeuh a ~-in om hi | everything is now ready) (s:kigingsa/kithawisa) (b:baih) (r:2.19.15/20.21.31/18.13.18/42.14.17) (q:draft)
baihta = (t:adv) (w:soon) (d:baih, soon, with ta, which marks that the time has now come; pai baihta ding, will come or go soon) (e:Kei a hong pai ~ ding ka hi hi/Kei ka hong pai ~ ding a | I am coming soon/Kei a pai ~ ding ka hi a | I am soon to go/hong tung ~ ding a | it will come soon) (b:baih) (r:66.22.7/18.10.21/66.22.12/35.2.3) (q:draft)
baihte = (t:adj) (w:quick/easy) (d:baih, quick, easy, with the plural te; a heh baihte, those who are quick to get angry, the hot-tempered) (e:a heh ~ khial thei tawntung hi) (b:baih) (r:20.29.22) (q:draft)
baihzaw = (t:adj) (w:easier/more bearable) (d:baih, easy, with zaw, more; used after sangin, than) (e:kalaoh khat a lut ding ~ lai hi/Sodom khuamite’ thuakna ~ lai ding | it will be more bearable for the people of Sodom/van leh lei a man’than nading a ~ ding hi | it is easier for heaven and earth to pass away/cih ding koi ~ ahi hiam | which is easier to say) (s:olzaw) (a:haksazaw) (b:baih) (r:41.10.25/40.11.22/40.11.24/42.16.17/40.9.5) (q:draft)
baikna = (t:n) (w:worship/offering) (d:in baikna tau, altar; apparently a misprint of biakna, as biakna tau stands earlier in the same verse) (e:~ tau simah bawngtal khat) (r:4.23.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
baiknate = (t:n) (w:offerings) (d:in meihal baiknate, burnt offerings; apparently a misprint of biaknate) (e:na meihal ~ uh leh thunuam-a) (b:baikna) (r:4.10.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
baina = (t:n) (w:laming/crippling) (d:bai, be lame, with the noun suffix na; liamna baina is being wounded and crippled, struck down) (e:liamna ~ ka tuah uh hangin) (b:bai) (r:47.4.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
baite = (t:see) <khe-baite>
bak = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:bat) (d:the bat, listed among the unclean flying creatures) (e:huihtun leh ~ ahi hi) (r:3.11.19/5.14.18) (q:draft)
bak = (t:n) (w:piece/portion) (d:counting word for a piece of meat: sa bak khat, one piece of meat) (e:anlum lum khat, sa ~ khat) (s:baak) (r:13.16.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
bak = (t:v) (w:hold up to/put to) (d:hold something up against the mouth) (e:ama kamah a ~ uh hi) (s:tahto) (r:43.19.29) (q:draft, low confidence)
bakbak = (t:adv) (w:ravenously/greedily) (d:describes greedy, tearing eating; a ne bakbak, one that devours ravenously, said of a wild animal) (e:a ne ~ keivom hi a) (r:1.49.27) (q:draft, low confidence)
