betkhiatsakin = (t:v) (w:striking out of/knocking out) (d:betkhiatsak with the linking ending in: striking a thing so that it falls from the hand) (e:na tawi na thal hong ~) (b:betkhiatsak) (r:26.39.3) (q:draft)
betna = (t:n) (w:hunting/hunt/catching) (d:bet, hunt, with the noun ending na: the hunting or catching of animals; sa betna is hunting game and nga betna is fishing) (e:a sa ~ panin a sanggampa Esau/gamlak a sa ~ panin | from hunting game in the open country/a nga ~ uhah a puante uh | their clothes, at their fishing) (s:sabet) (b:bet) (r:1.27.30/3.17.13/1.25.29/43.21.7) (q:draft)
Betonim = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Betonim) (d:town east of the Jordan in the territory of Gad) (r:6.13.26)
betsak = (t:v) (w:have struck/order to strike) (d:bet, slap, with the causative sak: have someone struck, said when ordering others to strike a person) (e:A muk na ~ un) (b:bet) (r:44.23.2) (q:draft)
betsan = (t:v) (w:clap at) (d:bet, strike or clap, with san, at someone: khut betsan is to clap the hands at someone in scorn) (e:awi-in khut a ~ uh hi) (b:bet) (r:25.2.15) (q:draft)
Beza = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Bezer) (d:city of refuge in the wilderness plateau east of the Jordan, in the territory of Reuben; elsewhere spelled Bezer) (e:mualzang sehnel gam ~ khua) (r:5.4.43) (q:draft)
Bezai = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Bezai) (d:head of a family that returned from the exile with Zerubbabel, and a leader who sealed the covenant with Nehemiah) (r:16.10.18/15.2.17/16.7.23)
Bezalel = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Bezalel) (d:son of Uri of the tribe of Judah, the craftsman chosen to make the tabernacle and its furnishings) (r:2.31.2/13.2.20/2.38.22)
Bezek = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Bezek) (d:place where Judah defeated Adoni-Bezek, and where Saul mustered Israel before relieving Jabesh Gilead) (r:7.1.5/9.11.8/7.1.4)
Bezer = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Bezer) (d:city of refuge in the wilderness plateau east of the Jordan, in the territory of Reuben; also a man of the tribe of Asher) (r:6.21.36/5.4.43/6.20.8/13.7.37)
bi = (t:v) (w:touch) (d:touch something lightly, as the seraph touches the lips of the prophet with a live coal) (e:Amah in ka muk hong ~ a/Amah in ka kam hong ~ a | he touched my mouth) (s:khoih/sukha) (r:23.6.7) (q:draft)
bi = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:hay/thatch grass/grass) (d:dry grass such as is used for thatch, named between wood and straw as a building material) (e:sing, ~, lopa, a nam tuamtuam) (r:46.3.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
bia = (t:v) (w:worship) (d:bow down to and serve God or a god; biak is the form used before endings such as na and nading) (e:a lu kunin Topa ~ a/Saul in Topa ~ hi | Saul worshiped the Lord/a kisung tua milim ~ uh hi | they worshiped that cast idol/ama khe-ngakna-ah va ~ ni | let us go and worship at his footstool/Na Topa Pasian na ~ ding hi | you shall worship the Lord your God) (r:1.24.26/9.15.31/19.106.19/19.132.7/40.4.10)
bia = (t:n) (w:veneration/worship) (d:the act of worshipping, reverence shown to God or a god)
biabia = (t:v) (w:keep worshipping/worship continually/go on serving) (d:bia, worship, said twice for an action that goes on and on) (e:na milimte uh ~ un/a sun a zanin Pasian ka ~ uh a | day and night we keep worshipping God) (s:biakbiak) (r:26.20.39/44.26.6) (q:draft)
biaibuai = (t:adv) (w:billowing/in a cloud) (d:describes smoke rising thickly; kahto biaibuai is to rise in a billowing cloud) (e:van lamah kahto ~ hi/paknamtui hal khute van lamah kahto ~ hi | the smoke of the burning incense rose billowing to the sky) (r:26.8.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
biak = (t:v) (w:worship) (d:form of bia, worship, used before endings and following words such as nading, na, theih and khit) (e:Pasian ~ nading mite a zol hi/Zeisu a ~ khit uh ciangin | after they had worshiped Jesus/milim ~ nadingin | in order to worship idols/keimah hong ~ theih nadingin ka mite paisak in | let my people go so that they may worship me) (b:bia) (r:44.18.13/26.16.21/42.24.52/2.8.1) (q:draft)
biak = (t:v) (w:offer/sacrifice) (d:make an offering to God, as in meihal biak nading, for a burnt offering, and khialhna hanga biak nading, for a sin offering) (e:khialhna hanga ~ nadingin keel a pa khat/Meihal ~ nading ahi a | whether it is for a burnt offering/meihal ~ nading sing la-in | he took the wood for the burnt offering/an tawh ~ nadingin an bung khat | one ephah for a grain offering) (s:biakpiak) (b:bia) (r:4.7.16/4.15.8/1.22.6/26.45.24) (q:draft)
biakbiak = (t:v) (w:keep worshipping/worship) (d:biak, worship, said twice for an action that goes on) (e:thei lo napi-in na ~ uh Pasian) (s:biabia) (r:44.17.23) (q:draft)
biakbuak = (t:adv) (d:descriptive word after kang, white, said of a cloud: brilliantly or billowing white; the exact sense is not certain) (e:a kang ~ om a/meiipi a bang a kang ~ om a | there was what looked like a white cloud) (r:66.14.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
biakbuk = (t:n) (w:tabernacle) (d:the tent of worship that Israel carried through the wilderness, from biak, worship, and buk, tent or booth) (e:Kohathte beh in ~ leitaw lam pangah/~ khetphimte leh huang khetphimte | the tent pegs of the tabernacle and of the courtyard/~ kongkhak ding kongpuankhai a mun-ah khai hi | he hung the curtain at the entrance of the tabernacle/nitumna lam ~ nungah giahphual satin | camping on the west, behind the tabernacle) (s:Puanbuk) (r:4.3.29/2.35.18/2.40.28/4.3.23) (q:draft)
Biakbuk = (t:n) (w:tabernacle) (d:biakbuk, tabernacle, written with a capital at the start of a sentence or for the tabernacle of Moses) (e:Moses in ~ le biakna-in a kizang/~ adingin a po to ding khuampeekte | upright frames for the tabernacle/~ leh buk tual kimkot ading khetphimte | the tent pegs of the tabernacle and of the surrounding courtyard/~ khuampeekte na bawl ding hi | you shall make the frames of the tabernacle) (b:biakbuk) (r:58.9.21/2.26.15/2.38.20/2.26.18) (q:draft)
biakha = (t:v) (w:worship/fall into worshipping) (d:biak, worship, with kha, happen to: come to worship; milim biakha nawn lo is no longer worship idols) (e:milim ~ nawn lo ding uh hi) (s:biakkhak) (r:28.14.8) (q:draft)
biakhawm = (t:v) (w:worship together) (d:bia, worship, with khawm, together) (e:Assiria mite tawh ~ ding uh hi/Assiria mite tawh ~ ding uh hi | they will worship together with the Assyrians) (s:biakkhop) (b:bia) (r:23.19.23) (q:draft)
biakin = (t:n) (w:temple/house of worship) (d:a spelling of biakinn, from biak, worship, and inn, house) (e:~ sungah laizial sunga/~ beelte, Babilon khua panin kila kik | the articles of the temple brought back from Babylon) (s:biakinn) (r:24.36.8/24.27.16) (q:draft)
biakinn = (t:n) (w:temple/sanctuary) (d:house of worship, from biak, worship, and inn, house: the temple in Jerusalem, or the sanctuary where God is present) (e:na ~ sungah nangma itna kip/nisuahna lam kongpi tawnin ~ sungah lut hi | entered the temple through the east gate/Judah gam in ama ~ suak a | Judah became his sanctuary/Jerusalem-a na ~ hangin | because of your temple at Jerusalem) (s:biakinnpi/biakin) (r:19.48.9/19.73.17/26.43.4/19.114.2/19.68.29) (q:draft)
Biakinn = (t:n) (w:temple) (d:biakinn written with a capital, the temple in Jerusalem) (e:le ~ sungah thu ka hilh a/~ nasemte sung panin | from among the temple servants/siampite in Thuciamna Singkuang la-in ~-ah paipih uh hi | the priests took the ark of the covenant and brought it to the temple/~ kiimah Jesuh a vak kawikawi laitakin | while Jesus was walking about in the temple courts) (b:biakinn) (r:43.18.20/11.8.3/15.2.43/41.11.27) (q:draft)
biakinnah = (t:n) (w:to the temple/in the temple) (d:biakinn, temple, with the place marker ah) (e:ama pasian ~ paipih a/Babilon gam ama pasian ~ paipih a | he carried them off to the temple of his god in Babylonia) (b:biakinn) (r:27.1.2) (q:draft)
biakinncing = (t:n) (w:temple guard) (d:one who guards the temple, from biakinn, temple, and cing, guard; biakinncing palikte are the temple guards and biakinncing palikmangte their officers) (e:~ palikte pawlkhat a sawl uh hi/~ palikmangte tawh va kiho uh a | went and talked with the officers of the temple guard/~ palikte khat in Jesuh beeng a | one of the temple guards slapped Jesus/~ palik pawlkhat tawh hiam tawi-in | with some temple guards, carrying weapons) (r:43.7.32/42.22.4/43.18.22/43.18.3) (q:draft)
biakinnpi = (t:n) (w:temple/sanctuary) (d:biakinn, temple, with pi, great: the great house of worship, the temple) (e:Topa sungah a siangtho ~ ahi hi/vantungah a om ~ sung pan | from the temple in heaven/~ kipuahkik ding hi | the sanctuary will be restored/~ a kihong ka mu hi | I saw the temple opened) (s:biakinn) (b:biakinn) (r:49.2.21/24.17.12/66.14.17/27.8.14/66.15.5) (q:draft)
Biakinnpi = (t:n) (w:temple/sanctuary) (d:biakinnpi written with a capital, the temple in Jerusalem) (e:a ~ nangawn a susia hi/~ sungah lut uh a | they entered the temple/~ ah kuamah a pai nawn kei hi | no one comes to the temple any more/Rom kumpite in i ~ hong suksiat sakin | the Romans will destroy our temple) (b:biakinnpi) (r:25.2.1/25.1.4/25.1.10/43.11.48) (q:draft)
biakinnsung = (t:n) (w:inside of the temple/temple) (d:biakinn, temple, with sung, inside: the interior of the temple; also simply the temple) (e:ka min tawh a kilo ~ nangawnah/~ panin Topa in kei hong hopihna ka za | I heard the Lord speaking to me from inside the temple/~ nasemte in a huanna anbuk | the kitchen where those who serve in the temple cook/minthanna vang tawh ~ a kidimna ka mu hi | I saw the temple filled with the glory) (r:24.32.34/26.44.4/26.43.6/26.46.24/26.43.5) (q:draft)
biakinnte = (t:n) (w:temples/sanctuaries) (d:plural of biakinn: temples, sanctuaries, or the buildings of the temple) (e:Izipt pasiante kibiakna ~ mei tawh a halsak/na ~ uh gamkhing ka suaksak ding a | I will lay waste your sanctuaries/hih ~ bangzah takin lian a | how great these temple buildings are) (b:biakinn) (r:24.43.13/3.26.31/41.13.1) (q:draft)
biakinntual = (t:n) (w:temple court/courtyard) (d:the open court of the temple, from biakinn, temple, and tual, court; biakinntual sungnung is the inner court and biakinntual puanung the outer court) (e:~ sungnung teng dimin meiipi kai hi/~ puanung lutna gei-ah hong paipih a | he brought me to the entrance of the court/~ puanung ciang dongah kiza a | was heard as far as the outer court/~ sungnung ah pai-in | going into the inner court) (r:26.10.3/26.44.21/26.8.7/26.10.5/26.44.27) (q:draft)
biakkhak = (t:v) (w:fall into worshipping/worship) (d:biak, worship, with khak, happen to: come to worship; biakkhak loh nading is so as not to fall into worshipping) (e:milim na ~ loh nadingun na kidawm un/tuate na ~ loh nadingun kingaihsun un | take care that you do not come to worship them) (s:biakha) (r:62.5.21/5.11.16) (q:draft)
biakkhop = (t:v) (w:worship together with/worship alongside) (d:biak, worship, with khop, form of khawm, together) (e:kei tawh nong ~ dingun) (s:biakhawm) (r:2.20.23) (q:draft)
biakna = (t:n) (w:religion) (d:a system of belief and worship) (e:Na ~ bang ahia? | What is your religion?/Amaute ~ thu leh a sisa mi khat | about their religion and a dead man/ama ~ in a mawkna ahi hi | his religion is worthless) (b:biak) (r:44.25.19/59.1.26)
biakna = (t:n) (w:offering/sacrifice) (d:something given to God in worship, an offering or sacrifice) (e:khialhna hanga ~ dingin keel a pa khat/A maan ~ piaknate lui un la | offer right sacrifices/tuate tungah ~ pia-in paknamtui hal lai uh hi | they still offered sacrifices and burned incense there/a tanute uh dawi ~-in nei uh hi | they sacrificed their daughters to demons) (s:biakpiakna/kithoihna) (b:biak) (r:4.7.46/19.4.5/12.14.4/19.106.37) in this sense more exactly <biakpiakna>
biakna = (t:n) (w:worship) (d:worship or religious observance, as in biakna ngeina regulations for worship and milim biakna idolatry) (e:thuciamna masa in ~ ngeina ahi zongin/milim ~, mibumna | idolatry, witchcraft/na ~ munte uh ka et ciangin | as I looked at your places of worship) (s:kibiakna) (b:biak) (r:58.9.1/48.5.20/44.17.23) in this sense more exactly <biakpiakna>
biaknatau = (t:n) (w:altar) (d:raised place on which offerings are made, from biakna, offering, and tau, altar) (e:~ kimkotah na theh ding hi/biakbuk kongkhak mai-ah meihal ~ koihin | set the altar of burnt offering in front of the entrance to the tabernacle/Amah in sumngo ~, a dung tong sawmnih | he made a bronze altar twenty cubits long/~ kimkotin pai un | go around the altar) (s:tau) (r:2.29.16/14.4.1/2.40.6/19.118.27) (q:draft)
biaknataute = (t:n) (w:altars) (d:plural of biaknatau, altar) (e:Amah in gamdang ~ leh mual dawn-a/paknamtui ~ zong la khia hi | he also removed the incense altars) (s:taute) (b:biaknatau) (r:14.14.3/14.14.5) (q:draft)
biaknate = (t:n) (w:offerings/sacrifices) (d:plural of biakna, offering; meihal biaknate are burnt offerings) (e:A ki-ap ~ in bawngtal zaguk/na meihal ~ uh ka mai-ah om ngitnget hi | your burnt offerings are ever before me/Topa tungah meihal ~ pia-in | offering burnt offerings to the Lord/na meihal ~ uh na piak loh nadingun | so that you do not offer your burnt offerings) (s:biakpiaknate/kithoihnate/piaknate) (b:biakna) (r:14.29.33/5.12.13/19.50.8/9.6.15) (q:draft)
biaknate = (t:n) (w:places of worship/shrines) (d:plural of biakna in the sense of a place of worship; mual tunga biaknate, the places of worship on the hills, are the high places) (e:Mual tunga ~ koih khia lo hi/mual tunga ~ ah biakna pia uh hi | they offered sacrifices at the high places/mual tunga ~ kilakhia lo hi | the high places were not removed) (b:biakna) (r:12.14.4/11.3.2/12.15.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
biaknopna = (t:n) (w:desire to worship/devotion) (d:biak, worship, and nop, want, with the noun suffix na: the wish to worship; milim biaknopna lungsim is a heart set on worshipping idols) (e:milim ~ lungsim ka beisak ding hi/nakpitakin milim ~ lungsim nei uh ahih manin | because they have a heart set on worshipping idols) (r:38.13.2/28.5.4) (q:draft)
biakpiak = (t:v) (w:sacrifice/offer) (d:give an offering in worship, from biak, worship, and piak, give; also names the act, as in nitak biakpiak hun, the time of the evening sacrifice) (e:nitak ~ hun ciangin/~ hun dong mateng | until the time of the sacrifice/meihal ~ nadingin ama ading tuuno hong pia ding | will provide the lamb for the burnt offering/thunuam-a ~ nadingin bawngtal nih | two oxen to be sacrificed as a fellowship offering) (s:biak) (r:15.9.5/4.7.29/11.18.29/1.22.8) (q:draft)
biakpiakna = (t:n) (w:sacrifice/offering) (d:what is given to God in worship, from biak, worship, and piakna, giving; thunuam-a biakpiakna is a fellowship offering) (e:Topa in ~ sangin/~ sa a om lai teng | any meat of the sacrifice that is left/Tu ni-in ~ ka bawl a | today I made a sacrifice/Topa in migilote’ ~ kihhuai sa a | the Lord detests the sacrifice of the wicked) (s:biakna/kithoihna) (r:20.21.3/3.7.17/20.7.14/20.15.8) (q:draft)
biakpiaknate = (t:n) (w:sacrifices/offerings) (d:plural of biakpiakna, sacrifice) (e:Na ~ khempeuh amah in hong phawk hen/meihal biaknate leh ~ | burnt offerings and sacrifices/A man ~ lui unla | offer right sacrifices/amau’ ~ go nawn lo ding uh hi | they shall no longer offer their sacrifices) (s:biaknate/kithoihnate) (b:biakpiakna) (r:19.20.3/9.15.22/19.4.5/3.17.7) (q:draft)
biakpih = (t:v) (w:join in worshipping/worship) (d:biak, worship, with pih, along with: worship together with others, in the verses always the idols or gods of other people) (e:amau’ pasiante ka ~ kei ding hi/amau’ milimte a ~ uh hi | they worshiped their idols/Israel mite’ milim biakte ~ lo a | he does not worship the idols of the Israelites/Assiria milimte nangawn va ~ hi | she even went and worshiped the idols of Assyria) (b:biak) (r:19.16.4/26.23.7/19.106.36/26.18.15) (q:draft)
biaksa = (t:v) (w:worshipped/formerly worshipped) (d:biak, worship, with sa, already done: that was worshipped before) (e:a na ~ pasian man lote) (b:biak) (r:30.2.4) (q:draft)
biaksiam = (t:v) (w:worship rightly/be devout) (d:biak, worship, with siam, be skilled at: worship rightly, said of women who are devoted to God) (e:Pasian a ~ numeite’ kizep nading) (r:54.2.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
biakte = (t:n) (w:objects of worship/idols) (d:plural of biak, the things that are worshipped; milim biakte are idols) (e:Israel mite’ milim ~ biakpih lo a/A milim ~ uh tawh zong kininsak kei un | do not defile yourselves with their idols/sing a kibawl milim a ~ uh | the idols made of wood that they worship) (b:biak) (r:26.18.6/26.20.18/66.9.20) (q:draft)
biaktheih = (t:v) (w:be able to worship/can worship) (d:biak, worship, with theih, can; biaktheih nading, so that one may worship) (e:Topa ka ~ nadingin kei hong lehzuihkik in/na Pasian ka ~ nadingin kei hong zuikik in | come back with me so that I may worship your God) (b:biak) (r:9.15.25/9.15.30) (q:draft)
biaktheihna = (t:n) (w:right to worship/worship) (d:biaktheih, be able to worship, with the noun suffix na: the right or the means to worship) (e:a man taktakin ~ nei-in) (b:biaktheih) (r:45.9.4) (q:draft)
biang = (t:n) (w:cheek) (d:the side of the face below the eye) (e:ka ~ ciangah ka tawi a/a khitui a ~ tungah a tak kauhkauh hi | her tears run down her cheeks/na ~ uh hong beeng ahi zongin | or slaps you on the cheek/Israel makaipa’ ~ ciang tawh sat ding uh hi | they will strike the ruler of Israel on the cheek with a rod) (s:paang) (r:28.11.4/47.11.20/25.1.2/33.5.1) (q:draft)
biangte = (t:n) (w:cheeks) (d:plural of biang, cheek) (e:A ~ pen paknamtui) (b:biang) (r:22.5.13) (q:draft)
bianuam = (t:v) (w:want to worship/be willing to worship) (d:bia, worship, with nuam, want to) (e:ka pasian ~ loin) (r:27.3.14) (q:draft)
biasak = (t:v) (w:make worship/cause to worship) (d:bia, worship, with sak, cause) (e:leitung mi khempeuh a ~ hi/om mi khempeuh, aana tawh a ~ hi | by its authority it made all the people there worship) (b:bia) (r:66.13.12) (q:draft)
biate = (t:n) (w:worshipers) (d:those who worship, bia with the plural ending te; milim biate are idolaters) (e:Baal a ~ khempeuh adingin puante/Amah a ~ in Kha leh thuman thutak tawh | those who worship him, in spirit and in truth/mi that theite, milim ~ | murderers, idolaters/huaiham-a duhhopte, milim a ~ | the greedy, idolaters) (b:bia) (r:12.10.22/66.22.15/43.4.24/46.5.11) (q:draft)
