Bihah = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Bilhah) (d:a spelling of Bilhah, a town of the tribe of Simeon) (r:13.4.29)
biing = (t:n) (w:horn/flask) (d:a horn or flask that holds oil, in sathau biing; also a measure of oil) (e:hih sathau ~ tawi-in Ramothgilead-ah va pai in/puanbuk panin sathau ~ la-in Solomon nilh hi | took the horn of oil from the tent and anointed Solomon/a sathau ~ sunga sathau la-in | taking the oil in his horn/sathau ~ la-in ama lu tungah sung inla | take the flask of oil and pour it on his head) (s:bing) (r:12.9.1/9.16.13/11.1.39/12.9.3) (q:draft)
biingah = (t:n) (w:into the horn/in the flask) (d:biing, horn or flask for oil, with the place marker ah) (e:Na sathau ~ sathau thun inla) (b:biing) (r:9.16.1) (q:draft)
biingta = (t:n) (w:log/small measure of oil) (d:a small measure of oil, used for the Hebrew measure log in Leviticus 14, about a third of a litre) (e:sathau ~ khat la ding hi/sathau ~ panin kimkhat la-in | taking some of the log of oil/tuuno apa khat la-in sathau ~ khat tawh | one male lamb together with a log of oil) (r:3.14.10/3.14.15/3.14.12) (q:draft)
bikbek = (t:adv) (w:completely/absolutely/totally/entirely/wholly/fully/thoroughly) (d:placed after a verb or describing word: completely, tightly, with nothing left over; khua mial bikbek is pitch dark) (e:khua mial ~ a suah ma-in/Tuipi tung tengah khua mial ~ a | darkness lay over the whole surface of the deep/ciampek tawh khen ~ a | she fastened it tight with the pin/khat leh khat kithuapcip ~ ahih manin | because they are joined so tightly to one another/kip tak-a a kilam ~ ahi hi | it is built firm and compact) (r:24.13.16/18.41.16/1.1.2/7.16.14/19.122.3)
