bil = (t:n) (w:ear) (d:the organ of hearing) (e:Zak nading ~ a nei teng in/~ in a zak cim thei lo hi | the ear never has enough of hearing/~ in thu ngai tel hilo ahi hiam | does not the ear test words/Mi khatpeuh in ~ a neih leh | if anyone has an ear) (r:40.13.9/21.1.8/18.12.11/66.13.9) (q:draft)
bil-aphuai = (t:adj) (w:resounding/noisy) (d:describes a gong, zam; apparently bil, ear, with a phuai: loud or harsh on the ear) (e:a ~ zam le daltuah kitum) (r:46.13.1) (q:draft, low confidence)
bilah = (t:n) (w:in the ear/in the hearing of/to the ears) (d:bil, ear, with the place marker ah: in or to the ears, in the hearing of) (e:Hih thute amaute’ ~ genin/Launa ding awging a ~ za ngitnget ding a | terrifying sounds will keep ringing in his ears/na kiphatsakna ka ~ hong tunkhitna hangin | because your arrogance has reached my ears) (b:bil) (r:5.31.28/12.19.28/18.15.21) (q:draft)
bilbah = (t:n) (w:earring) (d:ornament worn in the ear; contains bil, ear) (e:Ishmael mite ahih manin ~ nei uh hi/kizepna kham ~ tawh kibang hi | is like an ornamental gold earring/~ tualte, taaute leh mai-sitnate | the earrings, bracelets and veils) (r:7.8.24/20.25.12/23.3.19) (q:draft)
bilbahte = (t:n) (w:earrings/rings) (d:plural of bilbah, an ornament worn in the ear) (e:amau’ bil-a om kham ~ sutkhia-in/Nakbahte, ~ leh na khuk ding kumpi lukhu | nose rings, earrings and a crown for your head/na top uh lak panin ~ hong pia un | give me the earrings from your plunder) (b:bilbah) (r:2.32.3/26.16.12/7.8.24) (q:draft)
