Bokhim = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Bokim) (d:place where the angel of the Lord rebuked Israel and the people wept) (r:7.2.5/7.2.1)
bokin = (t:v) (w:fall down/prostrate oneself/bow down) (d:bok, fall face down, with the linking ending in: falling down before someone, usually followed by bia, worship) (e:a khe mai-ah ~ a bia hi/~ Pasian a bia ding hi | he will fall down and worship God/upa sawmnih leh lite in ~ | the twenty-four elders falling down/Nangmah in ~ hong bia leteh | if you bow down and worship me/a kiangah tai a, ~ | he ran to him and fell down) (s:boksukin/kunin) (b:bok) (r:44.10.25/41.5.6/46.14.25/66.4.10/40.4.9) (q:draft)
boksak = (t:v) (w:make kneel/make fall down/make lie down) (d:bok, lie face down, with the causative sak: make an animal kneel down, or make a person fall at the feet of another) (e:amah in a kalohte ~ hi/na khephung uhah ka ~ ding a | I will make them fall down at your feet) (b:bok) (r:1.24.11/66.3.9) (q:draft)
boksuk = (t:v) (w:fall facedown/bow down/prostrate oneself) (d:bok with suk, downward: throw oneself down with the face to the ground, in worship, fear or pleading) (e:Moses leh Aaron ~ uh hi/Kumpi khempeuh ama mai-ah ~ uh hen la | may all kings bow down before him/a lu kunin ~ hi | he bowed his head and fell facedown/Moses in tua thu a zak ciangin ~ hi | when Moses heard this he fell facedown/mai lamah tomkha pai-in lei-ah ~ a | going a little farther he fell to the ground) (s:bok/maipuk/kunsuk) (a:dingto) (b:bok) (r:4.14.5/19.72.11/4.22.31/4.16.4/41.14.35) (q:draft)
boksukin = (t:v) (w:fall facedown/bow down/prostrate oneself) (d:boksuk, fall with the face to the ground, with the linking ending in: falling facedown and then doing the next action) (e:mai lamah tomkha pai-in ~/Gera’ tapa Shimei kumpipa’ mai-ah ~ | Shimei son of Gera fell prostrate before the king/Kei zong leilakah ~ ka kiko a | I too fell facedown on the ground and cried out/Moses in tua thu a zak ciangin ~ | when Moses heard this he fell facedown/kihta ahih manunah ~ a om lai takun | while they were bowed down in fear) (s:bokin/kunin) (b:boksuk) (r:40.26.39/4.16.4/10.19.18/26.11.13/42.24.5) (q:draft)
bokvak = (t:v) (w:crawl/move along the ground) (d:move along the ground on the belly or on short legs, as snakes, lizards and insects do; a bokvak ganhing is a crawling creature) (e:a ~ ganhing khat hita leh/a ~ ganhing bangin hong awmtal ding uh a | they will go on their bellies like crawling creatures/a ~ a nin ganhing a sisa hita leh | or the carcass of an unclean crawling creature/Leitunga ~ a, a hontat ganhing | a creature that crawls and swarms on the ground/leitungah a ~ khatpeuh peuh tawh a kibang | like anything that crawls on the ground) (s:awmtal) (r:3.22.5/33.7.17/3.5.2/3.11.44/5.4.18)
bokvak = (t:v) (w:creep/move along the ground) (d:of small animals and reptiles, move close to the ground; a bokvak ganhingte are the creatures that move along the ground) (e:leh a ~ ganhingte amau nam ciatin/Ganhing khempeuh, a ~ khempeuh, vasa khempeuh | all the animals, all the creeping things, all the birds/leitungah a ~ peuhmah ama' nam ciat | everything that creeps on the ground according to its kind/gamsate tawh, ~ ganhingte tawh | with wild beasts and with creeping creatures/leh a ~ ganhingte, leh ngasate thu gen hi | he spoke of creeping things and of fish) (s:hontat) (r:1.1.24/1.8.19/1.7.14/44.11.6/11.4.33)
bokvakte = (t:n) (w:crawl/creeping things/creatures that move along the ground) (d:bokvak, creep, with the plural te, used as a noun: the creatures that creep on the ground) (e:Mihing, ganhing, a ~ leh huih lak vasate/leitunga a ~ khempeuh' tungah ukna neisak ni | let us make them rule over all that creep on the ground/leitungah a ~ khempeuh' tung | over all that creep on the ground) (b:bokvak) (r:1.7.23/1.1.26/1.1.30) plural form of <bokvak>
bom = (t:n) (w:cluster/bunch) (d:a bunch of fruit growing together; leenggah bom is a cluster of grapes) (e:leenggah ~ panin kingah a) (s:bawk) (r:23.65.8) (q:draft)
bomah = (t:n) (w:at the crossroads/at the corner) (d:bom with the place marker ah; lamka bomah, at the place where roads meet, a crossroads or street corner) (e:Lamka ~ ding un la, khuadak un/kikhopna inn sung leh lamka ~ dingin | standing in the synagogues and on the street corners) (r:24.6.16/40.6.5) (q:draft)
bomte = (t:n) (w:clusters/bunches) (d:bom, cluster, with the plural te) (e:a ~ leenggah suakin min pah hi) (s:bawkte) (b:bom) (r:1.40.10) (q:draft)
Borashan = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Bor Ashan) (d:town in the south of Judah to which David sent a share of the plunder) (r:9.30.30)
bot = (t:v) (w:pull up/uproot/pluck out) (d:pull a plant or a fixed thing out by the root; bot khia is pull out and bot to is pull up) (e:Tahum kungte va ~ le-ung nong awi hiam/Va ~ kei un | do not go and pull them up/a omsa ki thumte a ~ khia hi | it uprooted three of the earlier horns/ka phuh sate ka ~ khia kik hi | I uproot again what I planted/a na khempeuh ~ to a | he pulled up everything with it) (s:botkhia/zunglot/bawh) (a:suan) (r:40.13.28/27.7.8/40.13.29/24.45.4/7.16.3) (q:draft)
both = (t:see) <Bethmarka-both>
botin = (t:v) (w:pluck/pull out/pull up) (d:bot, pull out by the root, with the linking ending in, which joins it to the following verb: pulling up plants, pulling out hair) (e:ka sam leh ka khamul ~/Amaute in singkungnote ~ ne uh a | they pull up small shrubs and eat them) (b:bot) (r:15.9.3/18.30.4) (q:draft)
botkhawm = (t:v) (w:uproot together/pull up along with) (d:bot, pull up, with khawm, together: pull up one plant along with another) (e:taang kung tawh na ~ kha ding uh hi/taang tawh na ~ kha ding uh hi | you may uproot the wheat along with them) (b:bot) (r:40.13.29) (q:draft)
botkhia = (t:v) (w:uproot/pull out/pluck out) (d:pull something out from where it is fixed, as plants, teeth or feathers) (e:humpinelkai khanglai hatute ~ in/Lopa kungte ~ a, mei tawh a hal | the weeds are pulled up and burned with fire/Asherah biakna songte ~-in | uprooting the Asherah poles/ka suan ding a, ka ~ kei ding hi | I will plant them and not uproot them/tua gam ka ~ ding a | I will uproot that nation) (s:bot/zunglot/bawhkhiat) (a:suan/phut) (b:bot) (r:19.58.6/40.13.40/33.5.14/24.24.6/24.12.17) (q:draft)
botsat = (t:v) (w:snap/break off/tear apart) (d:bot, pull, with sat, cut: break a rope, cord or chain by pulling it apart) (e:mimkhau bangin khauhualte ~ ziau hi/a kitah bangin thalkhaute ~ hi | he snapped the bowstrings as a thread snaps/amau a kihennate a ~ hi | he broke their chains) (s:sutat) (r:7.16.12/19.107.14/7.16.9) (q:draft)
botsatin = (t:v) (w:snapping/tearing apart) (d:botsat, break by pulling, with the linking ending in) (e:a kihen simin a sikkhaute ~) (s:sutatin) (b:botsat) (r:41.5.4) (q:draft)
botsatkhia = (t:v) (w:break off/break away/tear off) (d:botsat, break by pulling, with khia, out or off) (e:amau a kihennate ~ hi) (s:sutat) (b:botsat) (r:19.107.14) (q:draft)
botto = (t:v) (w:pull up/tear loose) (d:bot, pull up, with to, upward) (e:a na khempeuh ~ a) (b:bot) (r:7.16.3) (q:draft)
