bu = (t:v) (w:hide/hide oneself) (d:hide oneself, go into hiding so as not to be seen or found) (e:leivui sungah ~ in/huan sung singte' lakah ~ uh hi | they hid among the trees of the garden/Tua ahih ciangin David lo sungah ~ hi | so David hid in the field/Jordan nisuahna lam ahi Kherith lui-ah ~ in | hide in the Kerith Ravine east of the Jordan/ama kiang panin ka ~ thei ding hi | I could hide from him/lau-in taimangin a ~ uh hi | in fear they fled and hid) (s:butawm/busim/bucip) (a:kilang) (r:23.2.10/1.3.8/9.20.24/11.17.3/19.55.12/27.10.7)
Bu = (t:n) (w:book) (d:bu, book, written with a capital as part of a title: La Bu is the Book of Psalms) (e:David mahmah in La ~ sungah) (s:Laibu) (b:bu) (r:42.20.42) (q:draft)
bu-mek = (t:v) (w:reach into a nest/rob a nest) (d:bu, nest, with mek: feel in a bird's nest to take what is in it; the same word is also written bumek) (e:Vasa ~ bangin mihingte’ hauhna) (s:bumek) (r:23.10.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
bua = (t:v) (w:pour out/shed/spill) (d:pour out a liquid; also used of blood being shed, water being spilled and the Spirit being poured out) (e:ka Kha ka ~ ding hi/misiangthote’ sisan leh kamsangte’ sisan a ~ uh a | they shed the blood of holy people and prophets/lei lakah a ~ tui tawh i kibang hi | we are like water spilled on the ground/Pasian’ hehna hai sagihte leitungah ~ un | pour out the seven bowls of the wrath of God on the earth) (s:bung/buak) (r:29.2.29/66.16.6/10.14.14/66.16.1) (q:draft)
buah = (t:v) (w:pour/water) (d:pour a liquid over something, water the ground; tui-buah is a drink offering poured out to God) (e:lei maitang khempeuh a ~ hunin/tua tungah tui-~ na sung kei ding hi | you shall not pour a drink offering on it/tui-~ dingin leenggahzu bung khat sehli suah sehkhat | a quarter of a hin of wine as a drink offering/tui ~ nadinga kizang keute | the bowls used for drink offerings/khaici vawhin tui na ~ nadingun | to sow seed and water it) (s:buak/bua) (r:1.2.6/2.30.9/4.15.5/24.52.19/5.11.10)
buahna = (t:n) (w:watering/irrigating) (d:buah, pour water on, with the noun suffix na: the watering of sown land, or the place that is watered) (e:na khe tawh tui na ~ uh) (b:buah) (r:5.11.10) (q:draft)
buai = (t:v) (w:be troubled/be in turmoil/be in an uproar/riot) (d:be disturbed or confused, of a person's mind or of a crowd or city) (e:Susa khuapi sung ~ mahmah hi/Mihonpite hong ~ kha ding ahih manin | because the crowds might riot/ama dikna lungsim nakpi-in a ~ hi | his righteous soul was greatly troubled/Tua innpi sungah mihonpi ~ ngeingai uh a | in that building the crowd was in confusion/Jerusalem khuasung ~ mahmah hi | the city of Jerusalem was in an uproar/ahih hangin ~ hun sung ahi ding hi | but it will be a time of trouble) (s:gamlum/patau) (a:daih) (r:17.3.15/41.14.2/61.2.8/44.19.32/44.21.31/27.9.25) (q:draft)
buai = (t:v) (w:contend with/be occupied with) (d:with tawh, be taken up or entangled with someone) (e:tawh ~ paisuak lo ding hi) (r:1.6.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
buaigawp = (t:v) (w:be in panic/be in utter confusion) (d:buai, be troubled, with the intensifier gawp; with sak, throw into panic) (e:amaute ~ sak hi) (b:buai) (r:9.7.10) (q:draft)
buaina = (t:n) (w:trouble/commotion/turmoil/panic) (d:buai, be troubled, with the noun suffix na: trouble, disorder or unrest among people) (e:~ tawh kipelh hi/leilu lam gam panin ~ lianpi khat hong pai | a great commotion is coming from the land of the north/thongcingte lakah ~ lianpi hong om hi | there was a great commotion among the guards/gam khempeuh ah ~ om hi | there was turmoil in all the lands/lungdamna om nawn loin ~ bek | no more joy but only panic) (s:gamlumna/patauhna) (a:lungmuanna/daihna) (r:20.12.13/24.10.22/44.12.18/14.15.5/26.7.7) (q:draft)
buaisak = (t:v) (w:trouble/disturb/terrify/stir up) (d:buai, be troubled, with the causative sak: throw a person or a town into fear or disorder) (e:launa in hong ~ hi/Pasian in lungkhamna nam khempeuh tawh ~ ahih manin | because God troubled them with every kind of distress/Khuasung khempeuh ~ henhanin | throwing the whole town into an uproar) (s:nawngkaisak/lungkhamsak/patausak) (a:daisak) (b:buai) (r:18.22.10/14.15.6/44.17.5) (q:draft)
buaisakgawp = (t:v) (w:throw into panic/throw into confusion) (d:buaisak, trouble, with the intensifier gawp) (e:Filistia-te thawn gawpin amaute ~ a) (s:amkhamsak) (b:buaisak) (r:9.7.10) (q:draft)
buaisakin = (t:v) (w:disturbing/troubling) (d:buaisak, trouble, with the linking ending in) (e:a thugenna uh tawh note hong ~) (b:buaisak) (r:44.15.24) (q:draft)
buaisakna = (t:n) (w:insurrection/disturbance/stirring up) (d:buaisak, trouble or stir up, with the noun suffix na; mi buaisakna, stirring up the people, an uprising) (e:Mi ~ le mi thahna hangin/khua sungah mi a ~ hang | because of his stirring up people in the city) (b:buaisak) (r:42.23.25/42.23.19) (q:draft)
buak = (t:v) (w:pour/pour out/water) (d:pour a liquid onto something, or water a field; the form of bua used when the thing poured on is named) (e:lo khempeuh tui a ~ hi/gunte leh cikte tungah a ~ leh | when he poured it on the rivers and springs/a lu tungah a ~ hi | she poured it on his head/a hun hunin tui ka ~ hi | I water it at its times/ama tawi hai huih lakah a ~ leh | when he poured his bowl into the air) (s:bung) (b:bua) (r:18.5.10/66.16.4/40.26.7/23.27.3/66.16.17) (q:draft)
buakhia = (t:v) (w:pour out/spill) (d:bua, pour, with khia, out: of blood and water, of the inner parts of a body spilling out, and also of anger) (e:tui bangin leitungah na ~ ding uh hi/a gil khempeuh a ~ hi | all his intestines spilled out/Jerusalem kimkot-ah tui bangin amaute’ sisan ~ uh a | they poured out their blood like water around Jerusalem/a hehna khempeuh siit nawn loin hong ~ a | he poured out all his anger) (s:sungkhia) (b:bua) (r:5.12.24/25.4.11/44.1.18/19.79.3) (q:draft)
buakin = (t:v) (w:pouring) (d:buak, pour, with the linking ending in) (e:ama lu tungah ~ amah nam a) (b:buak) (r:9.10.1) (q:draft)
buakkhiat = (t:v) (w:pour out) (d:buak, pour, with khiat, out, the form used before a following word; tui buakkhiat bangin, like water poured out) (e:Tui ~ bangin kei hong kibuakhia a/tui ~ bangin amaute’ sisan buakhia uh a | they poured out their blood like water poured out) (b:buak) (r:19.22.14/19.79.3) (q:draft)
buakna = (t:n) (w:pouring) (d:buak, pour, with the noun suffix na: the act of pouring a liquid on something) (e:ka pum tungah a hong ~ in) (b:buak) (r:40.26.12) (q:draft)
buakna = (t:n) (w:dump/heap) (d:place where something is poured or thrown out; nin buakna, rubbish heap) (e:nin ~ lak thai-in an a zong uh hi) (s:ninbuakna) (b:buak) (r:25.4.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
buakpa = (t:n) (w:waterer/one who waters) (d:buak, pour or water, with pa, the man who does it; tui buakpa, the one who waters) (e:a suanpa leh tui ~ in) (s:tuibuakpa) (b:buak) (r:46.3.8) (q:draft)
buaksuk = (t:v) (w:pour down/pour on/pour out) (d:buak, pour, with suk, downward: pour something down on a person or thing) (e:a lu tungah a ~ hi/amau’ gitlohna amau tung mahah ka ~ ding hi | I will pour out their own wickedness on them) (s:buasuk/sungsuk/bungsuk) (b:buak) (r:40.26.7/24.14.16) (q:draft)
buaksukin = (t:v) (w:pouring down/pouring on) (d:buaksuk, pour down, with the linking ending in) (e:uliante tungah simmawhna ~) (b:buaksuk) (r:19.107.40) (q:draft)
bual = (t:n) (w:pool/pond/lake) (d:a body of standing water, natural or made, such as a pool, pond or lake) (e:~ nuainung tuite na khawm a/Hebru pau-in Bethzatha kici ~ khat a om hi | there is a pool called Bethzatha in Hebrew/Gibeon ~-ah amaute dawntuah uh hi | they met them at the pool of Gibeon/Samaria ~ gei-ah leeng sil uh a | they washed the chariot by the pool of Samaria) (s:bualtui/tuibeem/lipi) (r:23.22.9/5.33.23/43.5.2/10.2.13/11.22.38) (q:draft)
bual = (t:v) (w:wallow/roll) (d:roll about in mud, dust or ashes) (e:buan lakah a ~ kik hi/ama’ luak lakah a ~ ding a | he will wallow in his own vomit/vut lakah ~ uh hi | they roll in ashes) (r:61.2.22/26.27.30/24.48.26) (q:draft)
Bual = (t:n) (w:pool) (d:bual, pool, capitalised in the name of a place: Siloam Bual, the Pool of Siloam; Kumpipa’ Bual, the Pool of the King) (e:Siloam ~-ah na mai va phiat in/Tuinak Kongpi leh Kumpipa’ ~-ah ka paisuak hi | I went on to the Fountain Gate and the Pool of the King/kumpipa’ huan gei-a Shelah ~ a kulh | the wall of the Pool of Shelah by the garden of the king) (b:bual) (r:43.9.7/16.2.14/16.3.15) (q:draft)
bualah = (t:n) (w:to the pool/in the pool) (d:bual, pool, with the place marker ah) (e:Siloam ~ pai in la) (b:bual) (r:43.9.11) (q:draft)
bualbual = (t:adv) (w:unintelligibly/stammeringly) (d:describes speech that cannot be understood; pau bualbual, babble or stammer) (e:a pau ~, mi kihisakte) (r:23.33.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
bualkik = (t:v) (w:wallow again/go back to wallowing) (d:bual, wallow, with kik, again) (e:buannawng lak mahah ~ veve hi) (b:bual) (r:61.2.22) (q:draft)
bualte = (t:n) (w:pools/ponds) (d:bual, pool, with the plural te) (e:amau’ gunte, amau’ luite, amau’ ~/~-a om tuite siang lo ding a | the water in the pools will not become fresh) (s:bualtuite/tuilite) (b:bual) (r:2.7.19/26.47.11) (q:draft)
bualtui = (t:n) (w:pool/pond/swamp) (d:bual, pool, with tui, water: a pool of standing water) (e:gamlak pen ~ ka suaksak ding a/a sa mahmah sehnelte ~ hong suak ding a | the burning sand will become a pool/Sia aw, ~ a kilawh ciangin | Sir, when the pool is stirred) (s:bual/tuibeem/lipi) (r:23.41.18/23.14.23/23.35.7/43.5.7) (q:draft)
bualtuite = (t:n) (w:pools/ponds) (d:bualtui, pool of standing water, with plural te) (e:sehnel gam pen ~ suaksak a/~ ka kangsak ding hi | I will dry up the pools/tua mun pen ~ tawh kidim sak hi | they fill that place with pools) (s:bualte/tuilite) (b:bualtui) (r:19.107.35/23.42.15/19.84.6) (q:draft)
buan = (t:n) (w:mud/mire/clay) (d:wet soft earth; also clay used for building and for making bricks) (e:Zeisu in ~ bawlin mit a vaksak/a tuite in ~ leh ninte laamto uh hi | its waters cast up mud and dirt/kongzing ~ bangin a kisik gawp | trampled like mud in the streets/Leiseek seek dingin ~ cilin | treading the clay to make bricks/cil tawh ~ a bawl khit ciangin | after he made mud with the saliva) (s:buannawng/buannawi) (r:43.9.14/23.57.20/33.7.10/34.3.14/43.9.6) (q:draft)
buang = (t:part) (w:except/unless) (d:limiting and emphatic particle: lo buang, except or apart from; kei buang leh, unless; after a verb, at least or after all) (e:a hih kei ~ leh Izipt kumpipa/Joshua lo ~ amaute khat beek om nawn lo | except Joshua not one of them was left/tanh dingte lo ~ bangmah ka la kei ding | I will take nothing except the shares/Topa in amaute a piak khiat kei ~ leh | unless the Lord had given them up/amah in kumpipa’ tanu hi ~ hi | she is after all the daughter of a king) (r:2.3.19/1.39.9/4.26.65/1.14.24/5.32.30/12.9.34) (q:draft)
buangawpin = (t:v) (w:rape/violate/abuse) (d:assault a woman violently; apparently buan with the intensifier gawp and the suffix in) (e:ka zineu ~ tu-in amah si hi) (r:7.20.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
buangin = (t:conj) (w:unless/except) (d:after a negative clause with loh or kei: unless, if not) (e:a tui i peek loh ~) (s:lohbuang) (b:buang) (r:26.47.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
buangin = (t:conj) (w:since/seeing that) (d:after a positive clause: since it is so; hi kei buangin teh asks surely it is not) (e:kei hong koih na hih ~/Kei nong cihna hi kei ~ teh | surely it is not me you mean) (b:buang) (r:6.15.19/41.14.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
buangun = (t:part) (w:now that/seeing that) (d:buang, the emphatic particle meaning after all, with the plural ending un: seeing that you have done something) (e:hong tung khin na hih ~/hong tung khin na hih khit ~ | now that you have come) (b:buang) (r:1.18.5/1.18.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
buanin = (t:v) (w:force/seize) (d:take hold of a person by force and overpower them, with the linking ending in; in the verses of forcing a woman, rape) (e:tua numei ~ luppih a/mipa in tua nu ~ a luppih leh | if the man forces her and lies with her) (r:5.22.28/7.19.24/5.22.25) (q:draft, low confidence)
buannawi = (t:n) (w:mud/soft mud) (d:mud made by wetting earth; compare buan mud) (e:a cil sia-in ~ bawl a/a mipa’ mitah tua ~ a nuhkawmin | smearing that mud on the eyes of the man) (s:buan/buannawng) (r:43.9.6) (q:draft)
buannawng = (t:n) (w:mud/mire) (d:deep soft mud) (e:~ sungah kei hong lawn a/~ panin amah in kei hong kaikhia-in | he pulled me out of the mire/konglak ~ bangin a tuancil dingin | to trample them like mud in the streets/~ thuk sungah ka tum a | I sink in deep mire/~ lak mahah bualkik veve hi | it goes back to wallowing in the mud) (s:buan/nawng) (r:18.30.19/19.40.2/23.10.6/19.69.2/61.2.22) (q:draft)
buante = (t:n) (w:mud/mire) (d:buan mud with the plural te; kongzing buante is the mud of the streets) (e:kongzing ~ bangin amaute ka lawnkhia hi/kongzing ~ bangin amaute tuankhamin ka sikcipsuk hi | I trampled them down like the mud of the streets) (b:buan) (r:19.18.42/10.22.43) (q:draft)
buasak = (t:v) (w:spill/pour out) (d:bua pour out, with the causative sak: let a liquid run out onto the ground) (e:a natui leilakah ~ hi) (b:bua) (r:1.38.9) (q:draft)
buasuk = (t:v) (w:pour down/shower down) (d:bua pour out, with suk downward: pour down from above like rain) (e:vantungte in thumanna ~ ta un) (s:buaksuk/zusuk) (b:bua) (r:23.45.8) (q:draft)
buatbuatin = (t:adv) (w:hastily/hurriedly) (d:describes the way a garment is thrown on; apparently in haste) (e:a puan silh ~ tui sungah a leengkhia) (r:43.21.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
bubu = (t:v) (w:hide/keep hiding) (d:bu, hide, doubled for continued action) (e:vasa bangin nang na ~ niloh hi) (s:bucip) (r:22.2.14) (q:draft)
bucip = (t:v) (w:hidden/hide oneself/stay hidden/go into hiding) (d:bu, hide, with cip, tightly: hide oneself completely, stay in hiding) (e:a kua sungah ~ uh hi/nangmahmah a ~ Pasian na hi hi | you are a God who hides himself/nang bang tanvei ~ den ding na hi hiam | how long will you hide yourself/Migilote a liat ciangin midangte ~ uh a | when the wicked rise to power others go into hiding/bang hangin nang ~ khong na hi hiam | why do you hide yourself) (s:busim/butawm) (a:kilang) (b:bu) (r:18.37.8/23.45.15/19.89.46/20.28.28/19.10.1)
buh = (t:n) (w:grain) (d:grain growing in the field or gathered at harvest; buh at is reap grain and buh lei is a grainfield) (e:~, leenggah tui, sathau leh tuuno/Bawng in ~ a cil lai takin | while the ox is treading out the grain/~ at nasem ding mi hong sawl in | send workers to reap the grain/Nipi ni khatvei, ~ lei-ah a vak leh | one Sabbath as he walked through the grainfield) (s:antang) (r:24.31.12/46.9.9/40.9.38/40.12.1)
buhcil = (t:v) (w:thresh/thresh grain) (d:buh, grain, with cil, tread; buhcil mi, a thresher) (e:lokho mi leh ~ mi in) (s:ancil) (r:46.9.10) (q:draft)
buhcilna = (t:n) (w:threshing sledge) (d:tool for threshing grain) (e:ha a nei ~-in kong bawl ding hi/Masala-te pen ~ tawh kicil lo a | caraway is not threshed with a sledge) (b:buhcil) (r:23.41.15/23.28.27) (q:draft)
buhcilna = (t:n) (w:threshing floor) (d:place where grain is threshed, also buhcilna phual) (e:Atad’ ~ phual a tun’ uh ciangin/Atad’ ~-ah tua banga kahna a muh uh ciangin | when they saw such weeping at the threshing floor of Atad) (s:ancilna/buhphual) (b:buhcil) (r:1.50.10/1.50.11) (q:draft)
buhcilnapei = (t:n) (w:threshing wheel/wheel of a threshing cart) (d:buhcilna, threshing, with pei, wheel) (e:a sakol tawh ~ a kihualsak ciangin) (r:23.28.28) (q:draft)
buhhum = (t:n) (w:grain/wheat/kernel of grain) (d:grain as it is sown, sifted or winnowed; buhhum khat is a single grain) (e:~ khat in lei tungah kia-a/Satan in ~ bangin nang hong haih nuam hi | Satan wants to sift you like wheat) (s:buhtang/mangbuh) (r:43.12.24/42.22.31) (q:draft)
buhhumte = (t:n) (w:grain) (d:plural of buhhum, grain) (e:~ tuipi sungah khia-in) (s:antangte) (b:buhhum) (r:44.27.38) (q:draft)
buhkung = (t:n) (w:straw/stubble) (d:the dry stalks of grain left after harvest, used as fodder and quickly burned up by fire) (e:kalaohte adingin ~ leh gan-an pia a/Ama adingin sikte, ~ bangin nip a | to him iron is as soft as straw/a buhtu dingun ~ a kaikhawm dingin | to gather stubble for their straw/amaute pen ~ tawh kibang uh a | they are like stubble) (s:buhtu) (r:1.24.32/18.41.27/2.5.12/23.47.14)
buhkungte = (t:n) (w:straw/stalks of grain) (d:buhkung, straw, with the plural te) (e:Huih in a letkhiat ~ bang/sing, lopa, ~ a lam a om leh | if anyone builds with wood, hay or straw/ninkholna dum sungah ~ a kisikcip bangin | as straw is trampled down in the manure pit) (b:buhkung) (r:18.21.18/46.3.12/23.25.10) (q:draft)
buhlei = (t:n) (w:grainfield/field of grain) (d:buh, grain, with lei, ground: a field where grain is growing) (e:~ ah a vak leh) (r:42.6.1) (q:draft)
buhleiah = (t:n) (w:in the grainfield/through the grainfield) (d:buhlei, grainfield, with the place marker ah: in or through the grainfield) (e:Nipi ni khatvei ~ a vak leh) (b:buhlei) (r:41.2.23) (q:draft)
buhlom = (t:n) (w:sheaf) (d:bundle of cut grain stalks) (e:lo lai-ah ~ i hen a/keima' ~ tho-in ding tang hi | my sheaf rose and stood upright/ancilna phual-ah ~ a tun’ mah bangin | like sheaves brought to the threshing floor/~ atsa kinusia bangin kuamah in a khawm kei | like cut sheaves left behind that no one gathers) (s:anlom) (r:1.37.7/18.5.26/24.9.22) (q:draft)
buhlomte = (t:n) (w:sheaves) (d:buhlom, sheaf, with the plural te: bundles of cut grain) (e:~ pua-in innah hong ciah ding hi/tua kiim-ah note’ ~ kikhawm a | your sheaves gathered around it/a puak ~ in bawngleeng a netcip suk bangin | as the sheaves loaded on a cart press it down) (s:anlomte/anphalte) (b:buhlom) (r:19.126.6/1.37.7/30.2.13) (q:draft)
buhneel = (t:n) (w:flour/fine flour/dough) (d:grain ground fine, and the dough made from it; also written buhnel) (e:Numei khat in ~ seeng thum/sathau, ~, mangbuh, bawng, tuu | oil, fine flour, wheat, cattle, sheep/A kipia masa ~ a sian’tho leh | if the dough offered first is holy) (s:buhnel/annel) (r:42.13.21/66.18.13/45.11.16) (q:draft)
buhnel = (t:n) (w:flour) (d:buh, grain, with nel, fine: grain ground fine, flour; also written buhneel) (e:numei khat in ~ seeng thum) (s:buhneel/annel) (r:40.13.33) (q:draft)
buhphal = (t:n) (w:sheaf/sheaves of grain) (d:in the verse something of grain that burns, where the English has a torch among sheaves; exact sense not confirmed) (e:tulak kang leh ~ kang ka bangsak) (r:38.12.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
buhphual = (t:n) (w:threshing floor) (d:buh grain with phual place: the place where grain is threshed and winnowed; in Zechariah 12.6 a place of grain that is on fire, where the NIV has sheaves) (e:ama ~ zap siang ding a/tulak kang le ~ kang ka bangsak ding a) (s:ancilna/buhcilna) (r:40.3.12/38.12.6) (q:draft)
buhsi = (t:n) (w:chaff) (d:the light husks of grain that the wind blows away) (e:huihpi in a mutkhiat ~ bangin) (s:ansi/anvai/buhvai) (r:18.21.18) (q:draft)
buhtang = (t:n) (w:grain/corn) (d:the kernels of grain used as food, as against buhtu, the straw) (e:Izipt gamah ~ a om thu/Buhtu leh ~ bangci kibat theih ding ahi hiam | how can straw be like grain) (s:antang) (r:44.7.12/24.23.28) (q:draft)
buhtu = (t:n) (w:straw/stubble) (d:dry stalks of grain, used as fodder and in brick making) (e:mangbuhham leh ~ zong paipih uh hi/Note ~ kong pia kei ding hi | I will not give you straw/~ na pia nawn kei ding uh hi | you shall no longer give straw/~ bangin a kattum ding hun | the time when they burn up like stubble) (s:buhkung) (r:11.4.28/2.5.12/2.5.10/2.5.7/39.4.1) (q:draft)
buhvai = (t:n) (w:chaff) (d:the husks of grain that the wind blows away) (e:huih in ~ a mut bangin/huih in ~ a mutmang bangin | as the wind blows chaff away) (s:buhsi/ansi/anvai) (r:24.13.24) (q:draft)
buhvui = (t:n) (w:head of grain/ear of grain) (d:buh, grain, with vui, ear: the head of a grain plant that holds the kernels) (e:a nungzuite in ~ zut uh a/a hoih ~ sagih kung khat tungah vui hi | seven good heads of grain grew on one stalk/~ lo-in a ne uh hi | they picked heads of grain and ate them/nisuahna huihpi in a theemsak ~ hawm sagihte | the seven empty heads of grain withered by the east wind) (s:anvui/mangbuhvui) (r:42.6.1/1.41.5/40.12.1/1.41.27) (q:draft)
buhvuite = (t:n) (w:heads of grain/ears of grain) (d:buhvui, head of grain, with the plural te) (e:a nungzuite in ~ a zut uh hi) (s:anvuite/mangbuhvuite) (b:buhvui) (r:41.2.23) (q:draft)
bui = (t:adj) (w:maimed/crippled) (d:of a hand or foot: cut off, missing or useless) (e:ka taklam khut ~ ta hen/khut langkhat ~-in nuntakna sungah lut lecin | if you enter life with one hand maimed/khe langkhat ~-in nuntakna sungah lut lecin | if you enter life with one foot crippled) (a:cingtak) (r:19.137.5/40.18.8/41.9.43/41.9.45) (q:draft)
buisum = (t:v) (w:be crippled/be maimed/wither) (d:of a hand or arm, lose its power and become useless) (e:ka taklam khut ~ ta hen/ka khutte ~ hen la | may my hands become useless) (r:19.137.5/18.31.22) (q:draft, low confidence)
buite = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:moles) (d:plural of bui, a burrowing animal, named together with bats; a different word from bui maimed) (e:~ leh bakte paih ding uh hi/~ le bakte a paih ding uh hi | they will throw them to the moles and bats) (b:bui) (r:23.2.20) (q:draft)
buk = (t:v) (w:cover/take cover/hide/take shelter) (d:hide oneself or take shelter in a place, as in a field, in the dark or under wings; buk nading is a place of refuge) (e:lo sungah ka ~ theih nadingin | so that I may hide in the field/Gamtatsia mite a ~ theih nadingun | where evildoers could hide/ama khate nuai-ah ~ nading na mu ding hi | under his wings you will find refuge/ka liim nuai-ah nong ~ kei uhleh | if you do not take shelter in my shade) (s:bu) (r:9.20.5/18.34.22/19.91.4/7.9.15)
buk = (t:v) (w:rule over/control/lie in wait/crouch/lurk) (d:in Genesis 4.7 said of sin that crouches at the door to master a person; elsewhere of a lion or an enemy that lies in wait for someone) (e:Limtakin na hih kei le nang hong hih nuamin mawhna in hong ~ a/Amaute kikai khawmin hong ~ uh hi | they gather together and lurk for me/mizawngte man dingin ~ a | he lies in wait to catch the poor/keimah a hong that dingin hong ~ uh hi | they lie in wait to kill me) (s:uk) (r:1.4.7/19.56.6/19.10.9/19.119.95)
Buk = (t:n) (w:tabernacle/booth/tent) (d:buk, tent or booth, written with a capital at the start of a sentence, for the tabernacle, and in Buk Pawi, the Festival of Tabernacles) (e:a kibawl ding ~ Pawi kipan ding a/Judah mite’ ~ pawikham ding a nai zo hi | the Jews' Festival of Tabernacles was near/~ sungah biakna nasem mite | those who minister in the tabernacle/~ tual kiim-a khuampi khempeuh | all the posts around the courtyard of the tabernacle) (s:biakbuk) (r:26.45.25/43.7.2/58.13.10/2.27.17) (q:draft)
bukah = (t:n) (w:in the tent/to the tent/at the tabernacle) (d:buk, tent, hut or booth, with the place marker ah; mostly in kikhopna bukah, at or into the tent of meeting, and siahdonna bukah, at the tax booth) (e:kikhopna ~ nasem dingin Levi mite pai ding/kikhopna ~ bawngtal sisan kimkhat paipihin | bringing some of the bull's blood into the tent of meeting/siahdon’na ~ tu-in a om a mu hi | he saw him sitting at the tax booth/Kikhopna ~ no mihing thumte hong pai un | come to the tent of meeting, you three) (r:4.8.15/3.4.16/42.5.27/4.12.4) (q:draft)
bukbuk = (t:v) (w:shrink back/hide away) (d:apparently buk doubled: hide or shrink away in shame; in the verse negated, not be ashamed before him) (e:i ~ loh nadingin) (r:62.2.28) (q:draft, low confidence)
bukin = (t:v) (w:lying in wait/in ambush/hiding) (d:buk, lie hidden, with the linking ending in: lying in wait in order to attack, or hiding) (e:Lampi-ah ~ thah ding a vaihawm uh/Khua neute sungah mi ~ tu a | he sits lying in wait for people in the villages/Pai-in leenggui lote-ah ~ | go and hide in the vineyards/ahih kei leh ~ a khawh a | or throws something at him from ambush) (s:buksimin/pangsimin) (b:buk) (r:44.25.3/19.10.8/7.21.20/4.35.20) (q:draft)
Bukki = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Bukki) (d:name of two men: a leader of the tribe of Dan, son of Jogli, and a priest descended from Aaron, son of Abishua and father of Uzzi) (r:4.34.22/13.6.5)
Bukkiah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Bukkiah) (d:a son of Heman, one of the Levite musicians appointed by David) (r:13.25.4)
bukkong = (t:n) (w:tent entrance/tent door) (d:the doorway of a tent; kikhopna bukkong is the entrance to the tent of meeting) (e:kikhopna ~ Moses kiangah Aaron a ciahkik hi/kikhopna ~ nangma kiangah mihon khempeuh hong kikhawm ding | the whole community shall gather before you at the entrance to the tent of meeting/kikhopna ~, siampipa kiangah tuate paipih ding hi | she shall bring them to the priest at the entrance to the tent of meeting/kikhopna ~, Topa’ kiangah hong paipih ding hi | he shall bring it to the Lord at the entrance to the tent of meeting) (r:4.16.50/3.14.23/4.10.3/3.15.29/3.19.21) (q:draft)
bukkongah = (t:adv) (w:at the entrance of the tent/at the tent door) (d:bukkong tent entrance with the place marker ah; kikhopna bukkongah is at the entrance to the tent of meeting) (e:kikhopna ~ mihonte kikhawm hi/kikhopna ~ Israel mihonte khempeuh khawm in | gather the whole community of Israel at the entrance to the tent of meeting/Topa’ mai kikhopna ~ tuate koih ding hi | he shall set them before the Lord at the entrance to the tent of meeting/kikhopna ~ a paipih kei leh | if he does not bring it to the entrance of the tent of meeting) (b:bukkong) (r:3.8.4/3.16.7/3.8.3/3.17.9) (q:draft)
bukmun = (t:n) (w:tent site/place of a tent) (d:buk, tent, with mun, place: the place where a tent stands) (e:Na ~ khan inla) (r:23.54.2) (q:draft)
bukna = (t:n) (w:refuge/shelter/hiding place) (d:buk, hide or take shelter, with the noun suffix na: a place of shelter or hiding; bukna khuapi is a city of refuge) (e:huihpi guahpi panin ~ leh belhna/note’ ~ khuapi gukte hi ding hi | they will be your six cities of refuge/Nangmah in keima adingin ~ mun na hi a | you are a hiding place for me/tai-in ~ na zong ding hi | you will flee and seek refuge) (s:belhna/hutna) (b:buk) (r:23.4.6/4.35.13/19.32.7/34.3.11) (q:draft)
buknapa = (t:n) (w:refuge) (d:bukna, refuge, with pa: the one who is a refuge, said of God) (e:a sungah ka ~) (s:belhpa) (b:bukna) (r:10.22.3) (q:draft)
buknasa = (t:adj) (d:buk hide or take shelter, with na and sa already done: describes the place in which someone had been hiding) (e:amaute a ~ leihawm sungah lawnsuk uh) (b:bukna) (r:6.10.27) (q:draft)
bukno = (t:n) (w:hut/shelter/booth) (d:buk hut with -no small; galvilna bukno is a watchtower) (e:ama ading ~ khat a lam hi/galvilna ~ akipan kulh a nei khuapi dongin | from watchtower to fortified city/Sehnel gamlakah khawl nading ~ khat | a hut to lodge in in the desert) (s:sawlbuk) (b:buk) (r:32.4.5/12.18.8/24.9.2) (q:draft)
buksim = (t:v) (w:ambush/lie in wait) (d:hide in order to attack by surprise) (e:Gutate bangin nang hong ~ a/a nungah na ~ ding uh hi | you shall lie in ambush behind it/Beth-el leh Ai kikalah a ~ dingin koih hi | he set them to lie in ambush between Bethel and Ai/Siriate in hong ~ uh ahih manin | because the Arameans are lying in wait) (s:pangsim) (r:20.23.28/6.8.4/6.8.12/12.6.9) (q:draft)
buksimin = (t:v) (w:lying in wait/in ambush) (d:buksim lie in wait, with the linking ending in) (e:Khuaneute sungah mi a ~ tu a/amah in ~, mizawngte a man dingin buk a | lying in wait, he hides to catch the poor) (s:pangsimin/bukin) (b:buksim) (r:19.10.8/19.10.9) (q:draft)
buksimna = (t:n) (w:ambush/place of ambush) (d:buksim lie in wait, with the noun suffix na: the lying in wait or the place of it) (e:na ~ panun note na kipan ding/A ~ ding uh munah amaute pai-in | they went to the place of their ambush) (s:pansimna) (b:buksim) (r:6.8.7/6.8.9) (q:draft)
buksimte = (t:n) (w:men in ambush/ambushers) (d:buksim, lie in ambush, with the plural te: those who lie in wait) (e:Tua ciangin a ~ diangkhia pah uh a/A ~ in khuapi a lak khitna | that the men in ambush had taken the city) (s:pangsimte) (b:buksim) (r:6.8.19/6.8.21) (q:draft)
bukte = (t:n) (w:tents/shelters/booths) (d:buk, tent or hut, with the plural te) (e:ka ~ hong kisuksiat sak a/Isaak leh Jakob tawh ~ sungah teengkhawm uh hi | he lived in tents with Isaac and Jacob/Jakob’ suante’ ~ ka lamkik ding a | I will rebuild the tents of Jacob's descendants) (s:puanbukte) (b:buk) (r:24.4.20/11.20.16/58.11.9/24.30.18) (q:draft)
bukte = (t:n) (w:ambushers) (d:those lying in wait, from buk lie in ambush, after a) (e:a omna panun a ~ ding khia pah) (s:buksimte/pangsimte) (b:buk) (r:6.8.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
buktual = (t:n) (w:courtyard/court) (d:the open court around the tabernacle, the tent of meeting) (e:kikhopna ~ sung a siangtho mun khatah/~-a a kikhaite | the curtains of the courtyard/Biakbuk le ~ kimkota ding khetphimte khempeuh | all the tent pegs for the tabernacle and the surrounding courtyard/a kimkot-a om ~-a khuampite a bullente tawh | the posts of the surrounding courtyard with their bases) (s:tual) (r:3.6.26/4.3.37/4.3.26/2.38.20/4.4.32) (q:draft)
bul = (t:n) (w:base/bottom/foot) (d:the lower end or the part where something starts, as in liang bul the shoulder joint and teipi bul the shaft of a spear) (e:khuampeek khat ~-ah bullen nih mah bawl hi/mual ~-ah na ding uh hi | you stood at the foot of the mountain/ka liang ~ panin kilong khia ta hen | let it fall from my shoulder joint) (a:dawn) (r:2.36.26/18.31.22/5.4.11) (q:draft)
Bul = (t:name) (w:Bul) (d:the eighth month of the old Hebrew calendar, the month in which Solomon finished the temple; not the common word bul, base) (e:a kha giatna ahi ~ kha-in) (r:11.6.38) (q:draft)
bulah = (t:n) (w:at the base/at the foot/at the bottom) (d:bul base with the place marker ah) (e:biakna tau ~ a sisan sung khia hi/~ a si a om laiteng sung ding hi | he shall pour out the rest of the blood at the base/biakna tau ~ a site sung khia-in | pouring out the blood at the base of the altar) (b:bul) (r:3.9.9/3.4.30/3.8.15) (q:draft)
bulh = (t:v) (w:set/put/fasten/put on/attach) (d:put or fasten one thing on another: fit a door, mount a stone, attach a ring, put a bit, chains or sandals on) (e:Sakol uk nading kamkaih ~ leeng/kongkhakte ka ~ khin a | I had set the doors in place/amau khe ah kol a ~ hi | he fastened their feet in the stocks/awmdal mongah tua kual nihte na ~ ding hi | you shall fasten the two rings to the corners of the breastpiece/a pang-ah teembaw kongkhak ~ in | put a door in the side of the ark) (a:sut) (r:59.3.3/1.6.16/16.7.1/44.16.24/2.28.23)
bulhin = (t:v) (w:putting on/fastening on/fitting) (d:bulh, put or fasten something on, with the connective in that links it to the next action) (e:amah kol ~ thong sungah koih hi/na khedapte uh na khe uh-ah ~ | with your sandals on your feet/ama tungah a awmdal ~ | putting the breastpiece on him/na nak-ah sikkawi ~ | putting a hook in your nose) (b:bulh) (r:14.16.10/3.8.8/2.12.11/23.37.29) (q:draft)
bulhna = (t:n) (w:putting on/fastening) (d:noun form of bulh, put on or fasten; kol bulhna and sikkol bulhna are being put in chains or in the stocks) (e:sikkol ~ le thongkiatna zong a thuak/a kol ~ panin Jeremiah a khahkik ciangin | when he released Jeremiah from the stocks/amaute in kol ~ thuak ding uh a | they will suffer being put in chains) (b:bulh) (r:58.11.36/24.20.3/28.11.7) (q:draft)
bulhsa = (t:see) <bulhsa-in>
bulhsa-in = (t:v) (w:chained/fettered) (d:bulh, put on or fasten, with sa, already done, and the suffix in; kol bulhsa-in, having been put in chains) (e:khuamial sungah kol ~ a omsak hi) (r:61.2.4) (q:draft)
bulhsak = (t:v) (w:put on) (d:bulh, put on, with sak, for another: put a ring or sandals on someone) (e:a khe-ah khedap zong ~ un/Josef' khut-ah ~ a | he put it on Joseph's hand/Khedap zong ~ un | put sandals on him too) (s:butsak) (a:sutsak) (b:bulh) (r:42.15.22/1.41.42/42.15.23) (q:draft)
bulhsakin = (t:v) (w:putting on/fitting with) (d:bulh fasten or put on, with sak, done for another person, and the linking ending in: putting sandals on someone) (e:a kibawl khedap hong ~) (s:butsakin) (b:bulhsak) (r:26.16.10) (q:draft)
bulhzo = (t:v) (w:be able to fasten/be able to put on) (d:bulh, put or fasten, with zo, be able) (e:sikkawi ~ ding na hiam) (b:bulh) (r:18.41.2) (q:draft)
buliahna = (t:see) <buliahna-ah>
buliahna-ah = (t:n) (w:in a hiding place/in a hidden place) (d:buliahna, a place where something is hidden, with the place marker ah) (e:ciangin ~ a koih kei a) (r:42.11.33) (q:draft)
bulkip = (t:n) (w:firm foundation/foundation/secure footing) (d:a base that stands firm, of a building or of faith) (e:a zui lote pen ~ a nei lo/Pasian in geelin a lam, ~ a nei khuapi | the city with foundations, planned and built by God/itna thu-ah zung thuk kha-in ~ na neih nadingun | so that you may be rooted and established in love/na ~ panun na pukkhak loh nadingun | so that you do not fall from your secure footing) (s:bulpi/innbul) (r:42.6.49/58.11.10/49.3.17/61.3.17) (q:draft)
bullen = (t:n) (w:base/socket) (d:the foot piece in which a post or frame of the tabernacle stands) (e:khuampi thum leh ~ thum tawh/khuampeek khat bul-ah ~ nih mah bawl hi | he made two bases under each frame/ngun tawh kibawl a ~ sawmli | forty silver bases/~ sawm-le-guk om-in | there being sixteen bases) (r:2.38.14/2.36.26/2.36.30) (q:draft)
bullente = (t:n) (w:bases/sockets) (d:the bases in which the posts of the tabernacle stand) (e:a khuampite leh a ~ tawh/Buktual kimkot-a khuampite leh a ~ tawh | the posts of the surrounding courtyard with their bases/a ~ sumngo hi ding hi | their bases shall be bronze/a zawlte, a khuampite, khuam ~ tawh | its crossbars and posts with the post bases) (b:bullen) (r:2.35.17/4.3.37/2.27.17/4.4.31) (q:draft)
bulllente = (t:n) (w:bases/sockets) (d:the bases in which the frames of the tabernacle stand; spelling of bullente with three l, probably a misprint) (e:amah in a ~ koihin) (r:2.40.18) (q:draft)
bulom = (t:n) (w:heap/lump) (d:in nin bulom, a heap or lump of dirt, where the English has dust and ashes; exact sense not confirmed) (e:nin ~ bang lel ka hi ta hi) (r:18.30.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
bulomtang = (t:n) (w:heap/pile) (d:in nin bulomtang, a heap of rubble or ruins) (e:hih inn in nin ~ suak ding hi/a sawt loin nin ~ suak ding hi | before long it will become a heap of rubble/kulh a nei khuapite nin ~-in na hei nading | that you should turn fortified cities into heaps of rubble/Mawhna ~ sung panin suakin | born out of a heap of sin) (r:11.9.8/18.15.28/12.19.25/43.9.34) (q:draft)
bulphuh = (t:v) (w:base on/rely on/make the foundation) (d:take something as the basis or the main thing) (e:I upna a ~ ding ihi hi/Thukham zuihna ~ ding ihi hiam | are we to rely on keeping the law/ki-itna na ~ un | make love your foundation/sunglam hoihna na ~ zaw un | rather make inner beauty the main thing) (s:siksan) (r:45.3.27/51.3.14/60.3.4) (q:draft)
bulphuhin = (t:v) (w:based on/on the basis of) (d:bulphuh, take as the basis, with the linking suffix in; placed after the thing that is the basis) (e:mite’ nasepna ~ a teel hi loin/upna ~ thuciamna kipia hi | the promise is given on the basis of faith/Pasian in mihingte’ nasepna ~ a teel hileh | if God chose on the basis of people's works) (b:bulphuh) (r:45.11.6/45.4.16) (q:draft)
bulphuk = (t:v) (w:cut down at the root/fell) (d:bul base with phuk cut down: fell a tree at its foot) (e:sing a ~ dingin hei tawh) (s:phuk) (r:42.3.9/40.3.10) (q:draft)
bulpi = (t:n) (w:foundation/base) (d:the base on which a building or the earth rests; innkiu suang bulpi is the cornerstone) (e:leitung pen ama ~ tungah na phut hi/inn a ~ kipan hi | the foundation of the house was laid/nangmah in leitung ~ na koih a | you laid the foundations of the earth/a inn ~ leivui ahi | the foundation of their house is dust) (s:innbul/bulkip/tawphah) (b:bul) (r:19.104.5/11.6.37/19.102.25/18.4.19) (q:draft)
bulpipen = (t:n) (w:main point/very foundation) (d:bulpi, foundation, with pen, most: the most basic thing, the heart of a matter) (e:a thu ~ in) (b:bulpi) (r:21.12.13) (q:draft)
bulpite = (t:n) (w:foundations/bases) (d:bulpi, foundation, with the plural te) (e:mual ~ zong lingin kising damdam hi/~ kisusia leh | if the foundations are destroyed/vantung ~ liingin taang hi | the foundations of the heavens shook/lei ~ a guakin om hi | the foundations of the earth were laid bare) (s:nuaiphahte) (b:bulpi) (r:19.18.7/19.11.3/10.22.8/10.22.16) (q:draft)
bulsel = (t:n) (w:branch/shoot/sprout) (d:bul base with sel sprout: a new shoot growing from the stock; in Isaiah 4.2 the Branch of the Lord) (e:~ pen mel hoihin minthang ding a) (r:23.4.2) (q:draft)
bulsum = (t:n) (w:stump) (d:the part of a tree left in the ground after it is cut down) (e:lei sungah a ~ a si zongin/a ~ om laite mei tawh a kihal kik | the stumps that remain being burned again) (s:singbul) (r:18.14.8/23.6.13) (q:draft)
bulte = (t:n) (w:foundations/bases) (d:plural of bul, base; leitung bulte is the foundations of the earth, and of a wheel the hubs) (e:leinuai-a leitung ~ a kivel theih ciang/a kalhna ~ khempeuh a kisung ahi hi | their hubs were all cast) (b:bul) (r:24.31.37/11.7.33) (q:draft)
buluah = (t:v) (w:plunder/loot) (d:take all of another's possessions by force) (e:ka neihsa teng uh ~ khin uh hi) (s:sut) (r:19.44.10) (q:draft)
buluh = (t:v) (w:raid/attack/plunder) (d:fall on someone to rob) (e:a buluhte in ~ ding a/gutate in ~ ding hi | robbers will attack him) (s:luh) (r:1.49.19/18.15.21) (q:draft)
buluh = (t:n) (w:robber) (d:in guta buluh, thief and robber) (e:mi in guta ~ ahi hi/a guta a ~ ahi hi | he is a thief and a robber) (s:misuam/galgu) (r:43.10.1) (q:draft)
buluhte = (t:n) (w:robbers/raiders/bandits) (d:buluh, robber, with the plural te; often paired as guta buluhte, thieves and robbers) (e:guta ~ omna na suaksak tazen uh/guta ~ ahi uh hi | they are thieves and robbers/A ~ in Gad sim ding a | raiders will attack Gad/misuam ~’ bukna mun | a den of robbers) (s:misuamte/suamte) (b:buluh) (r:42.19.46/1.49.19/43.10.8/24.7.11) (q:draft)
bum = (t:n) (w:sorcery/magic/spell) (d:magic used to harm or control someone; bum siam, enchanter) (e:~ a zang, van a kah/khut siampa leh ~ siamte lakhia hi | he takes away the skilled craftsman and the enchanters/~ siamna nei a, minamte zolin a khem hi | skilled in sorcery, she lured and deceived the nations) (s:mibum/bumna) (r:5.18.11/23.3.3/34.3.4) (q:draft)
bum = (t:v) (w:bewitch/cast a spell on) (d:put a person under a spell; mi bum theite are those who practise sorcery) (e:mitphial siamte, mi ~ theite/note a kua in hong ~ hiam | who has bewitched you/mi ~ theipa ahi Elimas | Elymas the sorcerer/mi ~ thei mi, milim bia mi | sorcerers, idolaters) (r:27.2.2/66.22.15/48.3.1/44.13.8/66.21.8) (q:draft)
bumek = (t:v) (w:reach into a nest/rob a nest) (d:bu, nest, with mek: feel in a bird's nest to take what is in it; the same word is also written bu-mek) (e:Vasa ~ bangin mihingte’ hauhna) (r:23.10.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
bumna = (t:n) (w:witchcraft/sorcery) (d:bum, bewitch, with the noun suffix na; mi bumna, casting spells on people) (e:milim biakna, mi ~, kilangbawlna) (s:mibumna/khongkhaina) (b:bum) (r:48.5.20) (q:draft)
bumnate = (t:n) (w:sorceries/magic arts) (d:plural of bumna, sorcery) (e:mi ~, numei leh pasal mawhnate) (s:aisannate) (b:bumna) (r:66.9.21) (q:draft)
bun = (t:v) (w:take hold/stick fast/penetrate) (d:of a weapon, bite into what it strikes; of rust or scum, cling so fast that it cannot be cleaned off) (e:thaltangte in zong ~ zo lo hi/Namsau tawh a kisut hangin ~ zo lo a | though a sword strikes it, it does not go in/a kang-op in ~ lua ahih manin | because its deposit clings so fast) (r:18.41.26/26.24.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
Bunah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Bunah) (d:son of Jerahmeel, of the tribe of Judah) (r:13.2.25)
bung = (t:n) (w:hin/bath/ephah) (d:a measure of capacity, used for the Hebrew hin and bath of oil or wine and for the ephah of grain) (e:leh oliv thau ~ khat/~ tawh teh-in ~ sawm ciangin beem khat-a seh | measured by the bath, ten baths making one homer/an ~ khat pai leh sathau bing khat pai | an ephah of grain and a hin of oil) (r:2.30.24/26.45.14/26.45.24) (q:draft)
bung = (t:v) (w:empty/pour out) (d:tip the contents out of a vessel; bung khia is empty out) (e:tuikuang sungah a tui ~ pak a/a thawl a hawm dong ~ khia-in | emptying her jars until they are empty/singkuang sunga sum teng ~ khia-in la uh a | they emptied out all the money in the chest and took it) (r:1.24.20/24.48.12/14.24.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
bungbu = (t:adv) (w:headlong/head first) (d:used with verbs of falling or pushing) (e:Thangsiahna ngen sungah ~ tuk a/a ~-in kia a | he fell headlong/khua omna mual dawn kui-ah ~ sawnkhiat dingin | to push him headlong off the brow of the hill) (r:18.18.8/44.1.18/42.4.29) (q:draft)
bungkhia = (t:v) (w:pour out/empty out) (d:bung tip out with khia out: tip the contents out of a vessel or a chest) (e:tua sung panin hong ~ dinga/singkuang sunga sum teng ~-in la uh a | they emptied out all the money in the chest and took it/a thawl a hawm dong ~-in | emptying her jars until they are empty) (s:buakhia/sungkhia) (b:bung) (r:19.75.8/14.24.11/24.48.12) (q:draft)
bungpi = (t:n) (w:bath/large measure) (d:bung, a measure for liquids, with pi big: a large measure of oil, where the NIV has bath) (e:oliv thau ~ tul sawmnih dim) (b:bung) (r:11.5.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
bungsuk = (t:v) (w:empty into/pour down) (d:bung, empty out, with suk, downward) (e:a tui ~ pak a) (b:bung) (r:1.24.20) (q:draft)
bungte = (t:n) (w:bottles/boxes/containers) (d:plural of bung, here a small container: paknamtui bungte are perfume bottles) (e:paknamtui ~ leh a kivom aite) (b:bung) (r:23.3.20) (q:draft)
Bunni = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Bunni) (d:name of several men in the time of Nehemiah, among them a Levite who led the people in prayer) (r:16.11.15/16.10.15)
bunzaw = (t:v) (w:go deeper/affect more) (d:bun go in or take effect, with zaw more: sink in more deeply, said of a rebuke) (e:khatvei taina in ~ hi) (b:bun) (r:20.17.10) (q:draft)
bunzo = (t:v) (w:pierce/penetrate/take effect) (d:bun go in, with zo be able: be able to pierce; in the verse negated, of weapons that cannot pierce at all) (e:thaltangte in zong ~ tuan het lo hi/Namsau tawh a kisut hangin ~ vet lo a | though a sword strikes it, it cannot pierce at all) (s:sunlet/pailet) (b:bun) (r:18.41.26) (q:draft)
bup = (t:adj) (w:entire/whole/complete) (d:complete, with no part left out; a bup-in is as a whole, entirely) (e:tuutal a ~-in na hal ding hi/Asa’ lungsim Topa tungah thuman ~ hi | Asa's heart was wholly true to the Lord/Eufrates Gungal gam ~ tungah aana zang uh a | they held power over the whole of Trans-Euphrates) (s:buppi) (r:2.29.18/11.15.14/15.4.20)
bup = (t:adj) (w:whole/entire) (d:placed after the noun it describes: minam bup is the whole nation) (e:Minam ~ vun ki-atna a man khit/na minam ~-un note kong paikhiatpih hi | I brought your whole nation out/Na minam ~-un keima neihsa hong guksak | your whole nation is robbing me) (s:buppi) (r:6.5.8/30.3.1/39.3.9)
bupa = (t:n) (w:captain/centurion/officer) (d:commander of a unit of men, pa marks a man; galkap bupa is a centurion) (e:galkap ~ kiangah a vaikhak hi/mi sawmnga a uk ~ leh zalian a neipa | the captain of fifty and the man of rank/Galkap ~ in tua thu a zak ciangin | when the centurion heard this/ama tungah a om ~ a lungkimsak theih nadingin | so as to please his commanding officer) (s:galkapbu) (r:44.24.23/23.3.3/44.22.26/55.2.4) (q:draft)
bupah = (t:adv) (w:throughout/over the whole) (d:bup whole with the place marker ah, after a noun: leitung bupah is in the whole earth) (e:leitung ~ na kahna aw uh kiza hi/leitung ~ a hong tung ding lungkhamna | the trouble that is coming on the whole earth/a lo ciing ~ kiak dim a | his whole field was full of thorns/meihal biakpiakna ~ na lungkim ding a | you will delight in whole burnt offerings) (b:bup) (r:24.46.12/66.3.10/20.24.31/19.51.19) (q:draft)
bupin = (t:adv) (w:wholly/entirely/as a whole) (d:bup whole with -in; a minam bupin is the whole nation, a bupin hal is burn it whole) (e:A minam ~ Jordan a galkah khit/Topa’ tungah a ~ meihal biakna-in a pia hi | he offered it whole to the Lord as a burnt offering/Na pumpi ~ hell khuk sungah hong kikhul sangin | than for your whole body to be thrown into hell/kei zong a minam ~ susia loin | I too will not destroy the whole nation) (b:bup) (r:6.4.1/2.29.18/9.7.9/40.5.30/23.65.8) (q:draft)
bupkhat = (t:n) (w:one whole/single unit) (d:bup, whole, with khat, one: one complete piece) (e:biakbuk puan ~ a suak hi) (r:2.36.13) (q:draft)
buppi = (t:adj) (w:whole/entire) (d:bup, whole, with pi: the whole of something; placed after the noun, as leitung buppi, the whole world) (e:Tu-in leitung ~ in kampau khat/Israel mihon ~ phun uh a | the whole community of Israel grumbled/Hadadezer’ galkap ~ David in a zawhna thu | that David had defeated the whole army of Hadadezer/Pawlpi ~ akipan tua thu a zate khempeuh | the whole church and all who heard this) (s:bup) (b:bup) (r:1.11.1/2.16.2/10.8.9/44.5.11) (q:draft)
buppiak = (t:v) (w:offer/give wholly/surrender) (d:bup whole with piak give: give oneself over completely) (e:na pumpi uh ~ unla/na pumpi uh na ~ uh mah bangin | just as you gave your bodies over) (r:45.6.19) (q:draft)
buppite = (t:adj) (w:whole/entire) (d:buppi whole with the plural te, after a noun for a group of people; mihon buppite is the whole assembly) (e:mihon ~ in Rimmon Suangpi-a om) (b:buppi) (r:7.21.13/4.1.17) (q:draft)
bupun = (t:adv) (w:as a whole/all together/entirely) (d:bup, whole, with the plural ending un; follows a group noun: a innkuan bupun, his whole household) (e:a innkuan ~ Pasian bia uh hi/Pasian in a innkuan ~ hehpihna thupha pia tahen | may God show mercy to his whole household/na minam ~ note kong paikhiatpih hi | I brought your whole nation out/Na minam ~ keima neihsa hong guksak | your whole nation is robbing me) (b:bup) (r:44.10.2/39.3.9/55.1.16/30.3.1) (q:draft)
busak = (t:v) (w:hide/conceal) (d:causative of bu, hide: put someone into hiding) (e:misite’ gam sungah hong ~ in/tua nu in inndei sungah mi ~ hi | she had men hidden in the room) (s:seel) (b:bu) (r:18.14.13/7.16.9) (q:draft)
busim = (t:v) (w:hide/lie hidden) (d:bu, hide, with sim, secretly: hide oneself, stay unnoticed) (e:muh loh dingin ~ thei ding ahi hiam/a ~ thei kei hi | he could not stay hidden/A ~ mite inndei sungnungah om uh hi | the men in hiding were in the inner room) (s:bu) (r:24.23.24/41.7.24/7.16.12) (q:draft)
butawm = (t:v) (w:hide oneself/hide) (d:bu, hide, with tawm, do by or for oneself) (e:keimahmah ka ~ hi) (s:bu) (r:1.3.10) (q:draft)
bute = (t:n) (w:officers/commanders) (d:Plural of bu, an officer: palik bute are the officers who serve the magistrates, and galkapte le a bute are the soldiers and their commanders.) (e:Palik ~ in hih thu/thukhen mangte in palik ~ pai sakin | the magistrates sent the officers/galkapte le a ~ le Jew mi palikte | the soldiers, their commander and the Jewish officers/galkapte leh ~ a manlangin kisam a | he at once called soldiers and officers) (s:palikbute) (r:44.16.38/43.18.12/44.16.35/44.21.32) (q:draft)
bute = (t:n) (w:those who hide/those in hiding) (d:Bu, hide or take shelter, with the plural te: those who are hiding, as in leihawm sunga bute, those hiding in caves.) (e:leihawm sunga ~ khempeuh pulnatna tawh si) (b:bu) (r:26.33.27) (q:draft, low confidence)
butsak = (t:v) (w:put on/slip on) (d:Put a ring or bracelet on the hand or arm of another person; built with the causative sak.) (e:a khut tungah taute ka ~ hi/Ama khut ah zungbuhte hong ~ un | put rings on his hand/tua numeite’ khutah tau ~ uh a | they put bracelets on the hands of those women) (r:1.24.47/42.15.22/26.23.42) (q:draft)
butsakin = (t:v) (w:putting on/put on) (d:Butsak, put a bracelet or ring on another person, with the linking ending in that joins it to the next verb.) (e:tau hong ~ khainiang kong oksak hi) (b:butsak) (r:26.16.11) (q:draft)
Buz = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Buz) (d:name of two men, a son of Nahor the brother of Abraham and a man of the tribe of Gad; also an Arabian people named with Dedan and Tema) (r:1.22.21)
Buzi = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Buzi) (d:priest, the father of the prophet Ezekiel) (r:26.1.3)
cangin = (t:adv) (w:at that time/then) (d:Found once in tua cangin, at that time; probably another spelling or a misprint of ciangin.) (e:tua ~ Hushah mi Sibbekai in) (s:ciangin) (r:10.21.18) (q:draft, low confidence)
Christian = (t:n) (w:Christian) (d:A follower of Christ; the English word taken over unchanged.) (e:Antiok khua-ah ~ a kici masa bel hi/kei ~ nong suaksak dektak hi | you almost make me a Christian/~ ahihna hangin gimna a thuak | suffers for being a Christian) (r:44.11.26/44.26.28/60.4.16) (q:draft)
Christiante = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Christiante/Christians) (d:the Christians, followers of Christ) (b:Christian) (r:42.24.9)
ci = (t:v) (w:command/order) (d:say as an order; ci-in after the quoted words reports the command that was given) (e:~-in note thu kong pia hi/~-in a vaikhak uh hi | they gave the order, saying) (r:5.19.7/44.16.35)
ci = (t:v) (w:say/tell) (d:say; stands after the words quoted, as in a ci hi, he said, and ci-in, saying) (e:na Pasian un ~ hi/a ~ Saddusite in | the Sadducees, who say/~-in Pasian in a min a phuak hi | saying so, God gave him the name/~-in a dong hi | he asked, saying) (r:1.21.24/23.40.1/40.22.23/58.5.10/41.10.3)
ci = (t:ppm) (d:postpositional marker to indicate objective case) (e:~ ahih ciangin)
Ci = (t:n) (w:salt) (d:Ci, salt, written with a capital in place names: Ci Tuipi is the Salt Sea or Dead Sea, Ci Kuam the Valley of Salt and Ci Khuapi the City of Salt.) (e:gamgi in ~ Tuipi mong/Nibshan, ~ Khuapi, leh En-gedi | Nibshan, the City of Salt and En Gedi/~ Kuam-ah Edom mite tulsawm leh tulgiat that hi | he killed eighteen thousand Edomites in the Valley of Salt) (b:ci) (r:6.15.2/13.18.12/6.15.62/10.8.13) (q:draft)
cia = (t:prep) (w:as big as/the size of/as much as) (d:Placed after a thing to give size or extent by comparison, as in khut peek cia, a handbreadth wide; bang cia-in asks how big.) (e:khut peek ~ a pha zawl khat/ankamtang khat ~ bang upna | faith the size of a mustard seed/Leitung bang ~-in lian ding cih | how big the earth is/khut peek ~ bang a zai geihual | a rim a handbreadth wide) (r:2.37.12/18.38.18/42.17.6/26.40.43) (q:draft)
ciah = (t:v) (w:return/go home/go back) (d:go back to one's home or to the place one came from) (e:Zekhariah innah a ~ hi/Na puanbuk uhah ~ un | return to your tents/mi khempeuh amau innah a ~ uh hi | everyone went to his own home/Balak zong a ~ hi | Balak also went home) (s:ciahkik/paikik/kilehkik) (r:42.1.23/40.9.7/5.5.30/43.7.53/4.24.25)
ciahhak = (t:v) (w:be long in returning/return late) (d:Ciah, return, with hak, slow or late: be a long time in coming back.) (e:Ka topa hong ~ ding hi) (r:40.24.48) (q:draft)
ciahin = (t:v) (w:returning/going home/coming back) (d:Ciah, return or go home, with the linking ending in: returned and then did the next thing.) (e:Hathak zong ~ Mordekai’ thugen teng/Kei tawh innah hong ~ an ne in | come home with me and eat/khua hong vak ciangin numei hong ~ | at daybreak the woman came back/Esau gamlak panin hong ~ | Esau came back from the open country) (s:ciahkikin/paikikin) (b:ciah) (r:17.4.9/1.25.29/11.13.15/7.19.26) (q:draft)
ciahkhawm = (t:v) (w:return together/go back together) (d:Ciah, return, with khawm, together: go back together with others.) (e:nang tawh kong ~ ding uh hi/innah hong ~ ding uh hi | they will return home together) (b:ciah) (r:8.1.10/38.10.9) (q:draft)
ciahkhia = (t:v) (w:leave/go away/depart) (d:Ciah, go home or return, with khia, out: go out and away from a place.) (e:lungnuam takin na ~ theita ding uh hi/van tampi tawh a ~ dingin | to go away with many goods) (b:ciah) (r:44.16.36/26.38.13) (q:draft)
ciahkhiasak = (t:v) (w:send away/send off/dismiss) (d:Ciahkhia, leave, with the causative sak: let or make someone go on his way.) (e:Moses in a sungpa ~ a/Tua ciangin mihonpite ~ a | then he sent the crowds away/lungnuam takin amah ~ khin hi | he has sent him away in peace/Abraham’ nasempa le a nungzuite tawh ~ uh hi | they sent her off with Abraham’s servant and his men) (s:ciahsak/paikhiasak) (b:ciahkhia) (r:2.18.27/41.8.10/10.3.23/1.24.59) (q:draft)
ciahkhiat = (t:v) (w:leave/depart/go away) (d:Form of ciahkhia, leave, used before ding, ciangin and khit.) (e:Kikhopna inn panin a ~ uh ciangin/Amaute kiang panin ka ~ ding uh hun | the time for us to leave them/Tua thudong mite a ~ khit ciangin | after those messengers had left) (s:paikhiat) (b:ciahkhia) (r:44.13.43/44.21.5/40.11.7) (q:draft)
ciahkhin = (t:v) (w:have returned/have gone back) (d:Ciah, return, with khin, already done: have gone back.) (e:amaute lungdamin ~ uh ahih manin) (b:ciah) (r:11.1.45) (q:draft)
ciahkik = (t:v) (w:return/go back/come back) (d:Ciah, return, with kik, back or again: go or come back to where one was.) (e:Israel upate giahphual ah a ~ uh hi/gam vaanna panin amaute hong ~ uh hi | they came back from exploring the land/Moses kiangah Aaron ~ hi | Aaron returned to Moses/a vanglian Pasian kiangah ~ ding hi | will return to the Mighty God) (s:ciah/paikik/kilehkik) (b:ciah) (r:4.11.30/1.3.19/4.13.25/4.16.50/23.10.21)
ciahkikin = (t:v) (w:returning/going back/coming back) (d:Ciahkik, return, with the linking ending in that joins it to the next action: returned and then.) (e:ama sungah hong ~ amah hingkik hi/khuapi sungah nang ~ Absalom kiangah | you go back into the city and to Absalom/Judah kiangah amah ~ | he went back to Judah/Note hong ~ Topa mai-ah na kap uh hi | you came back and wept before the Lord) (s:ciahin/paikikin) (b:ciahkik) (r:11.17.22/1.38.22/10.15.34/5.1.45) (q:draft)
ciahkikna = (t:n) (w:return/going back/coming back) (d:Ciahkik, return, with the noun suffix na: the act of going or coming back.) (e:Gath-ah Shimei pai-in a ~ thu/ama gamah a ~ ding lungsim ka guan ding | I will put it in his mind to return to his own country/nangma lamah hong ~ dingun | so that they would return to you) (s:paikikna) (b:ciahkik) (r:11.2.41/23.37.7/16.9.26) (q:draft)
ciahkiksak = (t:v) (w:send back/let return/make return) (d:Ciahkik, return, with the causative sak: send someone back or let him go back.) (e:a sanggamte tawh tangvalpa ~ in/ama omna munah ~ un | let it go back to its own place/nuntakna ama sungah hong ~ in | let his life return to him/nong kuanna lampi lam mahah nang kong ~ ding hi | I will make you return by the way you came) (s:ciahsakkik/paisakkik/sawlkik) (b:ciahkik) (r:1.44.33/23.37.29/9.5.11/11.17.21) (q:draft)
ciahkiksakin = (t:v) (w:letting return/let go back) (d:Ciahkik, return, with the causative sak and the linking ending in: allowing someone to go back.) (e:ka sanggamte kiangah kei hong ~) (b:ciahkiksak) (r:2.4.18) (q:draft)
ciahkikte = (t:n) (w:those who returned/returned exiles) (d:Ciahkik, return, with the plural te: the people who came back, said of the exiles who returned from Babylon.) (e:Biakinn nasemte sung panin a hong ~/Jerusalem leh Judah ah a ~ hi a | they are the ones who returned to Jerusalem and Judah) (b:ciahkik) (r:16.7.46/15.2.1) (q:draft)
ciahpa = (t:n) (w:one who has returned/one who has come back) (d:Ciah, return, with pa, the man who does it: the man who has come back.) (e:galphual panin hong ~ ka hi hi) (b:ciah) (r:9.4.16) (q:draft)
ciahpah = (t:v) (w:go home at once/return immediately) (d:Ciah, go home, with pah, at once: go home straight away.) (e:tho-in a inn-ah a ~ hi/a inn-ah ~ vingveng hi | he rushed home/Amah zong a inn-ah ~ a | she too went home at once/lungdam mahmahin a inn-ah ~ a | full of joy he went home at once) (r:40.9.7/41.7.30/17.6.12/40.13.44) (q:draft)
ciahpahin = (t:v) (w:going away at once/returning immediately) (d:Ciahpah, go home at once, with the linking ending in that joins it to the next action.) (e:a muh ciangin ~ a neih khempeuh) (b:ciahpah) (r:40.13.46) (q:draft)
ciahpih = (t:v) (w:bring back/take back/take home) (d:Ciah, go home, with pih, together with: take or bring someone or something along to one’s home or back to a place.) (e:Jerusalem ah Absalom ~ hi/na innah tua numei na ~ ding a | you shall bring that woman to your home/gamlapi panin an hong ~ hi | she brings food from afar/Israel panin numeino khat ~ uh a | they took a young girl away from Israel/Israel gamah na ~ in | take them to the land of Israel) (b:ciah) (r:10.14.23/1.14.16/5.21.12/20.31.14/12.5.2/40.2.20) (q:draft)
ciahpihin = (t:v) (w:taking home/bringing back/carrying off) (d:Ciahpih, take home with one, with the linking ending in; another verb follows.) (e:a inn-ah amaute ~ an a pia hi/kido-in amau’ ganhingte ~ | fought and carried off their livestock/na inn uhah a gan ~ | taking the animal home with you/Assiria-ah Israel mite ~ | taking the Israelites away to Assyria) (b:ciahpih) (r:44.16.34/9.23.5/5.22.2/12.17.6) (q:draft)
ciahpihkik = (t:v) (w:bring back/take back) (d:Ciahpih, take along home, with kik, back: bring or take someone or something back.) (e:nang kiangah amah hong ~ loin/I sepsate i ~ theih bangmah om lo hi | there is nothing of what we worked for that we can take back/siampi liante kiangah a ~ dingin | to take them back to the chief priests/a kipaikhiatpih mite ka ~ ding hi | I will bring back those who were taken away) (b:ciahpih) (r:1.43.9/21.5.15/44.9.21/36.3.19) (q:draft)
ciahpihna = (t:n) (w:taking back/carrying off) (d:Ciahpih, take back with one, with the noun suffix na: the act of taking someone away to one’s own place.) (e:Babilon-ah a ~ thu gen in) (b:ciahpih) (r:26.17.12) (q:draft)
ciahpihte = (t:n) (w:things brought home/what is brought in) (d:ciahpih, bring home, with the plural te: the things one has brought back) (e:amau’ ~ a bawl uh ciangin) (b:ciahpih) (r:2.16.5) (q:draft)
ciahpihto = (t:see) <ciahpihto-in>
ciahpihto-in = (t:v) (w:bringing back up/taking back up) (d:ciahpih, bring back, with to, upward, and the suffix in) (e:~ Zorah le Eshtaol kikal-a om) (r:7.16.31) (q:draft)
ciahsak = (t:v) (w:send away/dismiss/send home) (d:Ciah, go home, with the causative sak: let or make someone go home; followed by kik, send back.) (e:siah a puak mite ~ hi/An ne loin innah ka ~ leh | if I send them home without eating/amau’ gam ciatah, mite ~ hi | he sent the people away, each to his own land/Joshua in mite a ~ ciangin | when Joshua had dismissed the people) (s:paisak/ciahkhiasak/paikhiasak) (b:ciah) (r:7.3.18/57.1.12/41.8.3/6.24.28/7.2.6) (q:draft)
ciahsakin = (t:v) (w:sending away/sending off/sending home) (d:Ciahsak, send away, with the linking ending in that joins it to the next action.) (e:lampi dangah ~ na suaktasak a/zingsang ciangin nang hong ~ | in the morning I will send you on your way) (b:ciahsak) (r:59.2.25/9.9.19) (q:draft)
ciahsakkik = (t:v) (w:send back/let return/send away) (d:Ciahsak, send home, with kik, back or again: send someone back or let him return.) (e:a guak ~ uh hi/Ka topa’ kiangah hong ~ un | send me back to my master/a gam uhah ka ~ ding hi | I will bring them back to their own land/lencipin a ~ nawn kei uh hi | they hold them fast and no longer let them go back) (s:ciahkiksak/paisakkik/sawlkik) (b:ciahsak) (r:41.12.3/24.23.3/1.24.54/24.50.33) (q:draft)
ciahsakna = (t:n) (w:sending away/dismissal) (d:Ciahsak, send away, with the noun suffix na: the sending away of someone, in Isaiah 50.1 of a wife sent away in divorce.) (e:Amah ka ~, na nu a kimakna lai) (s:sawlkhiatna) (b:ciahsak) (r:23.50.1) (q:draft)
ciahsan = (t:v) (w:leave/desert/separate from) (d:Ciah, go home, with san, away from: go off and leave someone behind.) (e:Zi in a pasal ~ kei tahen/Pamfilia gam panin ~ ahih manin | because he had deserted them in Pamphylia/~ leh zong pasal nei loin om paisuak hen | if she does leave, let her stay without a husband/a pa’ inn-ah amaute ~ hi | he left them and went to his father’s house) (s:nusia/taisan/paisan) (b:ciah) (r:46.7.10/44.15.38/46.7.11/7.14.19) (q:draft)
ciahsuakpah = (t:v) (w:go straight home at once) (d:Ciah, return, with suak, straight through, and pah, at once: go straight home without stopping.) (e:Na khua-ah ~ inla) (r:41.8.26) (q:draft)
ciahsuk = (t:v) (w:go down home/go home/return down) (d:Ciah, go home or return, with suk, downward: go down to one’s home.) (e:Na inn-ah ~ in la/Bang hangin na inn-ah ~ lo na hi hiam | why did you not go down to your house/ama inn-ah ~ lo hi | he did not go down to his house/Amah in amaute tawh ~ khawm a | he went down with them) (a:ciahto) (b:ciah) (r:10.11.8/42.2.51/10.11.10/10.11.9) (q:draft)
ciahto = (t:v) (w:go up home/go back up/come up) (d:Ciah, return, with to, upward: return or go home to a higher place.) (e:Gibeah-a a inn-ah Saul zong ~ hi/Lung nuamin na inn-ah ~ ta in | go up to your home in peace/Manlangin i pa kiangah va ~ unla | hurry and go up to our father/Babilon panin kei tawh hong ~ khawm | came up with me from Babylon) (a:ciahsuk) (b:ciah) (r:9.15.34/43.6.62/9.25.35/1.45.9/15.8.1) (q:draft)
ciahzawh = (t:v) (w:after returning/have gone home) (d:ciah, return, with zawh, after finishing: in the verse, counting days from when they had gone) (e:A ~ uh a ni thum ni ciangin) (r:42.2.46) (q:draft, low confidence)
ciak = (t:v) (w:growl/snarl) (d:Make the low rough sound of lion cubs.) (e:humpino bangin a ~ lualua ding uh hi) (r:24.51.38) (q:draft)
ciakciak = (t:v) (w:chatter/babble) (d:talk on and on, said of fools who multiply words) (e:Mihaite in thu gengenin ~ uh hi) (r:21.10.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
ciakkik = (t:v) (w:return/come back) (d:Said of those who came back from captivity; apparently another spelling or a misprint of ciahkik.) (e:sal suahna panin hong ~ mi khempeuh) (s:ciahkik) (r:37.2.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
cial = (t:v) (w:hire) (d:Engage someone to work or to fight for pay.) (e:nasem dingte ~ dingin zingsanga a kuankhia/galhang mi tul zakhat zong ~ hi | he also hired a hundred thousand fighting men/a gen ding mite a ~ sim uh a | they secretly hired men to say it) (s:guai) (r:40.20.1/14.25.6/44.6.11) (q:draft)
cial = (t:n) (w:step/stair/level) (d:One step of a stairway, kahlei cial, or one level of a building.) (e:kahlei ~ guk mong ciatah khat ciat/kahlei ~ sawm om hi | there were ten steps/Tua inn pen ~ thum a pha | that building had three levels) (r:14.9.19/26.40.49/26.42.3) (q:draft)
cialin = (t:v) (w:hiring/hire) (d:Cial, hire, with the linking ending in: hiring someone and then going on to the next action.) (e:amah in kei hong ~ kei in/amaute in mi ~ sumgolh pia uh a | they hired men and gave them a bribe) (b:cial) (r:7.18.4/44.6.11) (q:draft)
cialna = (t:n) (w:hiring/hire) (d:Cial, hire, with the noun suffix na: the hiring of people, or what is spent to hire them.) (e:thu ngaihsun thei lo mite ~ hi/siavuante ~-in a zat hangin | though she spent it on hiring doctors) (s:guaihna) (b:cial) (r:7.9.4/42.8.43) (q:draft)
cialpa = (t:n) (w:employer/one who hires) (d:Cial, hire, with pa, the man who does it: the one who hires or sends a worker.) (e:mi thadah in a ~ a nasak hi) (b:cial) (r:20.10.26) (q:draft)
cialte = (t:n) (w:hired men/mercenaries/hired workers) (d:Cial, hire, with the plural te: those who are hired; galkap cialte are mercenaries.) (e:A galkap ~ nangawn amau lakah/nai nga lai takin a ~ in hong pai | those hired at about five o’clock came/numei tawh kibang a galkap ~ uh | their hired soldiers, who are like women) (s:thacialte) (b:cial) (r:24.46.21/40.20.9/24.50.37) (q:draft)
cialte = (t:n) (w:levels/storeys) (d:Plural of cial, step or level: the floors of a building.) (e:a tunga ~ pen a nuai-ate sangin) (b:cial) (r:26.42.3) (q:draft)
ciam = (t:v) (w:promise/swear/vow) (d:Give one’s word or swear an oath; often with thu, as in thu ciam, make a promise on oath.) (e:ci-in thu a ~ hi/Moses tungah ka ~ bangin | as I promised Moses/Pasian tungah thu na ~ ciangin | when you make a vow to God/amah sangin a lianzaw tawh ~ ding om lo | there was no one greater to swear by) (s:kiciam/kamciam) (r:40.14.7/58.6.13/6.1.3/21.5.4) (q:draft)
ciam = (t:v) (w:taste/sample) (d:Try a little food or drink.) (e:khuaizu tawm khat ka ~ hi/mite khat beek in an ~ lo uh hi | not one of the people tasted food/bang mah ~ thei lo ding | must not taste anything) (s:ciap) (r:9.14.43/42.14.24/9.14.24/32.3.7) (q:draft)
ciamciam = (t:todo) (q:draft, doubled form after khemzawh thu mah, of the treacherous who go on betraying; meaning of the word itself not clear from the verse)
ciamin = (t:v) (w:swearing/promising/vowing) (d:Ciam, promise or swear, with the linking ending in; often after thu or kam.) (e:kiciamna khat tawh kam ~/Topa in David tungah kam ~ | the Lord promised David/Nangmah in thu ~ | you yourself declared/~ a lungsim kikheel nawn lo ding hi | he has sworn and will not change his mind) (s:kiciamin/kamciamin) (b:ciam) (r:4.30.10/58.7.21/10.3.18/4.14.17) (q:draft)
ciamin = (t:v) (w:tasting/taste) (d:Ciam, taste, with the linking ending in.) (e:vantung hehpihna ~, Kha Siangtho tawh) (b:ciam) (r:58.6.4) (q:draft)
ciamkha = (t:v) (w:taste/get a taste of) (d:Ciam, taste, with kha, which shows that the action comes to happen: get to taste.) (e:ka an ~ lo ding uh hi) (r:42.14.24) (q:draft)
ciamkha = (t:v) (w:pledge/promise) (d:Ciam, promise, with kha: happen to give one’s word, as in kam ciamkha.) (e:a lohsak dingin kam na ~ hiam) (r:20.6.1) (q:draft)
ciamkhawm = (t:v) (w:make a covenant together/vow together) (d:Ciam, promise, with khawm, together: join with others in making a promise.) (e:Topa’ tungah ~ dih ni) (b:ciam) (r:24.50.5) (q:draft)
ciamkholh = (t:v) (w:appoint beforehand/fix in advance) (d:Ciam, promise, with kholh, beforehand; a ciamkholh ni is the appointed day.) (e:hun ding a ~ ni a tun ciangin) (r:44.12.21) (q:draft)
ciamna = (t:n) (w:promise/oath/vow) (d:Ciam with the noun suffix na: what someone has promised or sworn.) (e:na ~ bangin na itna kip/a ~ bangin a bawl thei ding hi | he is able to do as he promised/a ~ a pelh leh phamawh lo hi | if he breaks his oath it does not matter) (s:kiciamna/kamciamna) (b:ciam) (r:19.119.41/45.4.21/40.23.18) (q:draft)
ciamna = (t:n) (w:will/testament) (d:In sih ciamna, a will that takes effect at death.) (e:sih ~ lai-at mi a sih phot kul/sih khit ciangin sih ~ lai a kip ding hi | a will is in force after death) (b:ciam) (r:58.9.16/58.9.17) (q:draft, low confidence)
ciamnasa = (t:adj) (w:promised) (d:Ciam, promise, with na and sa, already done: describes what has been promised, here the place the Lord promised.) (e:~ munah i paito ding hi) (s:kamciamsa) (b:ciamna) (r:4.14.40) (q:draft)
ciamnui = (t:v) (w:joke/jest) (d:Speak in fun and not seriously; compare ciamnuih, jest.) (e:a mak dingte tungah a ~ bang lel hi) (r:1.19.14) (q:draft)
ciamnuih = (t:n) (w:mockery/ridicule/jest) (d:Mockery or joking at someone’s expense: ciamnuih bawl is mock or make fun of someone, ciamnuih-a neih is treat as a laughingstock.) (e:kei nong ~ bawl uh hi/kei hong ~ bawl ta uh hi | now they mock me/mite lakah ~-a neih-in kote nong bawl khin hi | you have made us a laughingstock among the peoples/Isaac a ~ bawlna Sarah in a mu hi | Sarah saw him mocking Isaac) (r:18.12.5/18.30.1/19.44.14/1.21.9) (q:draft)
ciamnuihbawl = (t:v) (w:mock/ridicule/make fun of) (d:Ciamnuih, mockery, with bawl, make: make fun of someone.) (e:hong simmawh bawlin hong ~ lel uh hi/luhgawpin a ~ khuapite tungah | to the towns that were plundered and ridiculed) (s:zahko/nuihsan) (b:ciamnuih) (r:26.36.3/26.36.4) (q:draft)
ciamnuihna = (t:n) (w:laughingstock/object of ridicule/byword) (d:A person or people that others make fun of.) (e:leitung bup in ~-in a hong nei/paunak, leh ~ na suak ding uh hi | you will become a byword and an object of ridicule/amau’ ~ bek ka suak ta hi | I have become nothing but their laughingstock) (b:ciamnuih) (r:25.3.14/5.28.37/18.30.9) (q:draft)
ciamnuihna = (t:n) (w:joke/jest) (d:Something said or done in fun: ka ciamnuihna hi is I was only joking.) (e:ka ~ hi, a cipa pen) (b:ciamnuih) (r:20.26.18) (q:draft)
ciampa = (t:n) (w:one who promised/promiser) (d:Ciam, promise, with pa, the man who does it: he who made the promise, said of God.) (e:thu a ~ in thumanpa ahi ci-in/a ~ in a ciamna bangin a bawl thei | he who promised is able to do as he promised) (b:ciam) (r:58.11.11/45.4.21) (q:draft)
ciampak = (t:v) (w:vow hastily/promise rashly) (d:Ciam, promise or vow, with pak, quickly: make a vow in haste.) (e:tungah thu mawk ~ kei in) (r:21.5.2/21.8.2) (q:draft)
ciampek = (t:n) (w:pin/loom pin) (d:The pin of a loom, with which the woven cloth is beaten tight.) (e:Amah in ~ tawh khen bikbek a/a ~, a siambu, leh a siam kai khia hi | he pulled up the pin, the loom and the fabric) (r:7.16.14/7.16.13) (q:draft)
ciampel = (t:v) (w:break one's word/break a promise/go back on an oath) (d:Ciam, promise, with pel, miss: fail to keep a promise; mostly negated, as in ciampel lo, keep one’s word.) (e:amah ~ lo ding hi/hong ~ kei ta in | do not break your promise to us/ama nat nading nangawn-ah a ~ lo mi | one who keeps his word even when it hurts) (r:4.30.2/24.14.21/19.15.4) (q:draft)
ciampelin = (t:v) (w:breaking one's word/treacherous) (d:Ciampel, break a promise, with the linking ending in; in a list of faults, treacherous.) (e:~, thu khual loin, kiphasak gawpin) (b:ciampel) (r:55.3.4) (q:draft)
ciampelna = (t:n) (w:faithlessness/breach of promise) (d:ciampel, break a promise, with the noun suffix na) (e:gamtatsiatna, ~, midangte khual lo) (b:ciampel) (r:45.1.31) (q:draft)
ciamsa = (t:v) (w:promised/sworn) (d:Ciam with sa for a completed act: already promised; na ciamsa bangin is as you promised.) (e:na ~ bangin kei hong honkhia in/Amah in hong ~ bangin | as he promised/a pu a pate uh tungah a ~ bangin | as he had sworn to their ancestors/hong ~ thu Topa in hong bawl nadingin | that the Lord will do what he has promised) (s:kiciamsa) (b:ciam) (r:19.119.154/2.12.25/6.21.44/23.38.7) (q:draft)
ciamsiatna = (t:n) (w:curse) (d:A curse, or an oath that brings harm; ciamsiatna ngah is be cursed.) (e:Kanaan in ~ ngah ta hen la/hong simmawhte in ~-in ka min zang uh hi | those who mock me use my name as a curse/gamlak ganhing khempeuhte sangin ~ na ngah zaw hi | you are cursed more than all the wild animals) (s:samsiatna/hamsiatna) (r:1.9.25/1.3.14/19.102.8) (q:draft)
ciamsiatsa = (t:adj) (w:cursed) (d:ciamsiat, curse, with sa, already done: that has been cursed) (e:Topa in a ~ leitang panin) (r:1.5.29) (q:draft)
ciamteh = (t:v) (w:note/mark/record/consider) (d:Take note of something, keep it in mind or put it on record.) (e:ama thute na lungsimah ~ in/tua mi na ~ un | take note of that person/nangmah in mawhnate ~ lecin | if you kept a record of sins/hun ~ nadingin khapi na bawl a | you made the moon to mark the seasons) (r:18.22.22/19.130.3/53.3.14/19.104.19) (q:draft)
ciamtehin = (t:v) (w:noting/recording/marking/registering) (d:Ciamteh, note or record, with the linking ending in that joins it to the next verb, often gelh, write.) (e:minam khempeuh ~ gelh ding hi/a gen uh thute ~ gelh kei in | do not write down what they said/na lungsim uhah ~ na ngaihsun ding uh hi | you shall fix them in your hearts and think on them/Nangmah in tuate a ni ~ | do you count their days) (b:ciamteh) (r:19.87.6/66.10.4/5.11.18/18.39.2) (q:draft)
ciamtehna = (t:n) (w:mark/seal/sign) (d:A mark put on something to show whose it is or to close it: a seal on a scroll, a mark on the body, a sign.) (e:lak panin ~ a ngah mi/sahang ~ nei-in | having the mark of the beast/Tuuno in nihna ~ a hon’ ciangin | when the Lamb opened the second seal/na khut tung-a om ~ lim | a sign on your hand) (s:ciaptehna) (b:ciamteh) (r:66.7.4/3.19.28/66.16.2/66.6.3/2.13.16) (q:draft)
ciamtehna = (t:n) (w:record/register/account) (d:A written record: khang ciamtehna is a genealogy and sum ciamtehna lai an account of money.) (e:Zeisu Khazih’ khang ~ lai inah/hong ciahkik masate’ khang ~ laibu ka mu hi | I found the genealogical record of those who returned first/amaute sum ~ lai a en hi | he went through their accounts/Na sumkep ~ lai hong pia in | give me the account of your management) (s:kiciamtehna/thuciamtehna) (b:ciamteh) (r:40.1.1/16.7.5/40.25.19/42.16.2) (q:draft)
ciamtehnate = (t:n) (w:seals/marks/signs) (d:Plural of ciamtehna: the seals on a scroll, marks borne on the body, signs set up on a road.) (e:ka pumpi tungah Zeisu’ ~ ka pua hi/~ hong dingin na kilawm hi | you are worthy to open its seals/Lampi-ah ~ bawl unla | set up signs on the road) (b:ciamtehna) (r:48.6.17/66.5.2/66.5.9/24.31.21) (q:draft)
ciamtehnate = (t:n) (w:records) (d:plural of ciamtehna: things noted down and kept) (e:tua ~ lim takin kikem hi) (b:ciamtehna) (r:28.13.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
ciamtehpa = (t:n) (w:one who reckons/one who regards) (d:Ciamteh, note or consider, with pa, the one who does it: said of God, who counts things not yet existing as existing.) (e:a piangsa bangin a ~ Pasian ahi) (b:ciamteh) (r:45.4.17) (q:draft)
ciamtehsa = (t:v) (w:marked/noted beforehand/predestined) (d:Ciamteh, mark, with sa for a completed act: already marked out.) (e:Pasian in a ~ mite a sam hi/tanglai peka eite hong ~ bangin | as we were marked out long ago/sun a ~ teng zan-in inn luh uh a | the houses they marked by day they break into at night) (b:ciamteh) (r:45.8.30/18.24.16/49.1.11) (q:draft)
ciamtehsak = (t:v) (w:mark/count against) (d:Ciamteh, mark or record, with sak: put a mark on someone, or hold a sin on record against someone.) (e:Topa in a mawhnate a ~ loh mipa/a taltang tungah ahi zongin a ~ hi | or on the forehead, he had them marked) (b:ciamteh) (r:45.4.8/66.13.16) (q:draft)
ciamtehteh = (t:v) (w:keep remembering/keep on record) (d:Ciamteh, note or record, with the last syllable repeated for continued action: go on holding in mind.) (e:mawhna ~ kei in) (r:23.64.9) (q:draft)
ciamzah = (t:n) (w:amount promised/promised sum) (d:ciam, promise, with zah, amount) (e:piak dinga a sum ~ thute khempeuh) (r:17.4.7) (q:draft)
ciamzo = (t:v) (w:have sworn/have promised) (d:Ciam, swear, with zo, done and settled; thu or kam stands before it.) (e:ka nasem David tungah thu ka ~ hi/Topa in thu ~ a | the Lord has sworn/Na nasempa David tungah thu na ~ hi | you have sworn to your servant David/Topa in kam ~ hi | the Lord has given his word) (s:kiciamzo) (b:ciam) (r:19.89.3/38.2.5/19.110.4/19.132.10) (q:draft)
cian = (t:v) (w:build up/pile up/heap) (d:Pile up a heap or build up a wall; written with a final apostrophe in the text.) (e:eima tha tawh kulh ~’ i zo/An ~’ bangin amaute ciang un | pile them up like heaps of grain/amau’ kulh ~’ tungah ngia khat kah leh | if a fox climbed on the wall they are building) (r:16.4.10/24.50.26/16.4.3) (q:draft)
cian = (t:adv) (w:carefully/intently/clearly) (d:Stands after a verb of looking, thinking or knowing: closely and thoroughly.) (e:a gamtat nading ngaihsun ~ hi/vantungah a et ~ lai takun | while they were looking intently into the sky) (r:20.14.15/44.1.10) (q:draft)
ciang = (t:prep) (w:as far as/up to/until) (d:Marks the point reached in place or time, often followed by dong.) (e:Jerusalem ~ dong hong tung hi/kum sawmthum-le-nga ~ dong gal kidona om nawn lo | there was no more war until the thirty-fifth year/tui in ka ngawng ~ hong tum ta hi | the water has come up to my neck/A kha sawmna ~ dong tuite kiamkiam lai hi | the waters kept going down until the tenth month) (s:dong/tan) (r:14.12.4/14.15.19/19.69.1/1.8.5) (q:draft)
ciang = (t:conj) (w:when) (d:At the time that; a short form of ciangin.) (e:gimna a thuak ~ nangawn-un/a kisuam ni zing ~ kuama’ theih ma-in | the day after he was killed, before anyone knew) (r:18.36.13/20.30.22/24.41.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
Ciang = (t:n) (w:scepter/rod/staff) (d:Ciang, rod, written with a capital; ukna ciang is the scepter of a ruler.) (e:Dikna ahi ukna ~ in) (b:ciang) (r:58.1.8) (q:draft)
cianga = (t:conj) (w:when/after/at the time of) (d:ciang with a, joining a time clause to the words that follow: when; khit cianga means after) (e:Seth a suah khit ~ Adam/an leh leenggahtui a hauh ~ | when grain and new wine abound/pumpi a thah khit ~ bangmah ahih zo lo | after killing the body can do nothing more/kum sawmnga a phak uh ~ kipan | from the time they reach fifty years) (b:ciang) (r:1.5.4/24.17.17/19.4.7/42.12.4/4.8.25) (q:draft)
ciangah = (t:conj) (w:at/up to/as far as) (d:ciang with the place marker ah: at or up to the point named, in place or extent) (e:a kawng ~ at khiatsakin amaute sawlkhia hi/Sidon ~ a gamgi om ding hi | his border will reach as far as Sidon/ka biang ~ ka tawi a | I lifted them to my cheek/Siampipa’ muh theihna ~ | as far as the priest can see) (b:ciang) (r:10.10.4/1.49.13/28.11.4/3.13.12)
ciangbek = (t:prep) (w:only up to/only as far as) (d:ciang, up to, with bek, only: no further than the number or point named) (e:Sagihvei ~ maisak in kong ci kei) (r:40.18.22) (q:draft)
ciangciang = (t:adv) (w:as far as/up to/to the full extent) (d:doubled ciang, every point reached: tu ciangciang is thus far, zah ciangciang is as much as, and a ciangciang-ah is on every side) (e:i tunna ~ panin mainawt ciat ni/amaute’ telzawh zah ~ thu a gen hi | he spoke the word as much as they could understand/Tu ~ Topa in eite hong huh hi | thus far the Lord has helped us/Gaza kiim ~ dong lei pan-a piangte susia uh | they ruined the crops all the way to Gaza) (s:zahzahin) (r:50.3.16/9.7.12/41.4.33/7.6.4) (q:draft)
ciangduai = (t:n) (w:rod) (d:a rod or stick used for beating as punishment) (e:mihaite’ nungzang ah ~ kinga hi/keimah in mite’ ~ tawh | I, with the rod of men/Mi a thusim lote in ~ thuak a | mockers suffer the rod) (s:ciangpum) (r:20.10.13/10.7.14/20.19.29)
ciangin = (t:adv) (w:afterwards/later) (d:after nung or khit: a nung ciangin is afterwards, later on) (e:A nung ~ Hit mite gamah tua mipa pai-in | afterwards that man went to the land of the Hittites/a nung ~ minthan’na tawh keimah nong sang ding hi | afterwards you will take me into glory/Hadassah, a nung ~ Esther a kici | Hadassah, afterwards called Esther) (s:nungciangin/tuazawh) (r:7.1.26/19.73.24/17.2.7)
ciangin = (t:adv) (w:then) (d:after tua, that: tua ciangin is then or and then, the usual way to begin the next step of a story) (e:Tua ~ Elihu in/Tua ~ Job in thu gen kik a | then Job spoke again/Tua ~ Jair si-in Kamon-ah kivui hi | then Jair died and was buried in Kamon/Tua ~ Elihu mah in | then Elihu also) (r:18.34.1/18.3.2/18.27.1/7.10.5/18.35.1)
ciangin = (t:conj) (w:and/when) (d:joins a clause to what follows: when or after this happened, and then) (e:tua ~ khuavak om pah hi/Moses in tua thu a zak ~ boksuk hi | when Moses heard this, he fell facedown/amaute khemna a theih ~ | when he perceived their trickery) (r:1.1.3/4.16.4/42.20.23) as in Let there be light, and there was light"
cianginleitungah = (t:phrase) (w:then on the earth) (d:the two words ciangin, when or after, and leitungah, on the earth, printed as one word) (e:Ni sagih khit ~ tuiciin tung hi) (r:1.7.10) (q:draft)
ciangka = (t:n) (w:pass/entrance) (d:a narrow way through hills or into a place) (e:Hamath khua lutna ~ panin/Mikmash paina ~ a cing dingin | to guard the pass to Mikmash/Jonathan in a ngimna ~ a pang khatah | on one side of the pass Jonathan meant to cross) (s:mualciang) (r:30.6.14/9.13.23/9.14.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
Ciangka = (t:n) (w:pass) (d:ciangka written with a capital: the narrow way through the hills at Mikmash) (e:Mikmash paina ~ a cing dingin) (b:ciangka) (r:9.13.23) (q:draft)
ciangkang = (t:n) (w:stick/rod) (d:a plain stick or dry rod) (e:~ khat khiakin tua munah lawn a/masala-te ~ tawh kisatkhia a | caraway is beaten out with a rod/~ tawh sat hong sawm na hi hiam | do you come to strike me with sticks/ka khut ka khete ~ bang hi | my hands and feet are like sticks) (s:ciangkhut) (r:12.6.6/9.17.43/23.28.27/18.17.7) (q:draft)
ciangkangte = (t:n) (w:rods/sticks/branches) (d:plural of ciangkang; the rods, peeled to show white, that Jacob set before the flocks) (e:mai-ah tua ~ koih lo hi/tui luang sungah a ~ koih hi | he placed the rods in the watering troughs/tuuhonte tua ~’ mai-ah omkhawm uh a | the flocks mated in front of the rods) (s:ciangkhutte) (b:ciangkang) (r:1.30.42/1.30.38/1.30.41/1.30.39) (q:draft)
ciangkhaite = (t:n) (w:carrying poles/baskets) (d:plural; apparently ciang, stick, with khai, hang: a load carried on a pole, where the English has basket) (e:na ~ uh kong khahsak hi) (r:19.81.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
ciangkhut = (t:n) (w:staff/rod/stick/scepter) (d:a stick carried in the hand: a walking staff, a shepherd’s rod or a ruler’s scepter) (e:Topa mai panin ~ la hi/hih ~ na khut sungah na tawi ding hi | you shall take this staff in your hand/Amah in a ~ tawh a sat ciangin | when he strikes with his rod/Tua na gelh ~ nihte | the two sticks you have written on) (s:ciangkang) (r:4.20.9/17.8.4/2.4.17/23.30.31/26.37.20) (q:draft)
ciangkhutah = (t:n) (w:on the goad/on the staff) (d:ciangkhut, staff, with the place marker ah; ciangkhutah sik phuh, fix an iron point on a goad) (e:~ sik phuh thaman mat khat) (b:ciangkhut) (r:9.13.21) (q:draft)
ciangkhutin = (t:n) (w:as a rod/as a club) (d:ciangkhut, staff or rod, with the suffix in) (e:molhtum le ~ ka zat ahi hi) (b:ciangkhut) (r:23.10.5) (q:draft)
ciangkhutte = (t:n) (w:staffs/rods) (d:plural of ciangkhut, staff or rod) (e:Aaron’ ciangkhut in amau’ ~ valh tum hi/Topa ’ mai-ah ~ koih hi | he placed the staffs before the Lord/kumpi ciangkhut leh amau ~ tawh | with the royal scepter and their staffs) (s:ciangkangte) (b:ciangkhut) (r:2.7.12/4.17.7/4.21.18) (q:draft)
ciangkik = (t:v) (w:rebuild/repair/build up again) (d:build up again a wall that is broken, from ciang, build a wall, and kik, again) (e:Jerusalem kulhpite ~ ta in/Gamdang mite in na kulhte ~ ding a | foreigners will rebuild your walls/a kicimte ~ lo uh ahih manin | because they did not repair the broken parts) (s:ciangpha/lamkik/bawlkik) (a:sucim) (r:19.51.18/23.60.10/26.13.5) (q:draft)
ciangpha = (t:v) (w:rebuild/repair) (d:ciang, build up a wall, with pha, good: repair a broken wall and make it sound again) (e:nadingin Jerusalem kulh ~ ni/a cimsa kulh khempeuh ~-in | repairing all the broken wall) (s:ciangkik/lampha/bawlpha) (a:sucim) (r:16.2.17/14.32.5) (q:draft)
ciangpi = (t:n) (w:basket/measuring basket) (d:a large basket; in the vision of Zechariah 5 the ephah measuring basket) (e:tua ~ sungah numei khat tu hi/~ sungah tua numei hensuk kik a | he pushed the woman back into the basket/Van lamah tua ~ leh’pih to uh hi | they lifted the basket up toward the sky/Tua in ~ hi a | it is a basket) (s:seeng) (r:38.5.7/38.5.6/38.5.8/38.5.9) (q:draft)
ciangpum = (t:n) (w:rod/cane) (d:a stick used for beating) (e:~ tawh sat nadingin thu a pia) (s:ciangduai) (r:44.16.22) (q:draft)
ciangtan = (t:n) (w:limit/set measure/fixed extent) (d:a fixed limit, especially of time; hun ciangtan is an appointed length of time) (e:ka mong leh ka hun ~ zah/hun ~’ khat a kipia hi | a fixed period of time was given/Na hehna in ~ hun nei thei lo ding | will your anger have no limit/a ~ khengvalin a gamta ka hi kei uh | we are not going beyond the limit) (r:19.39.4/25.5.22/27.7.12/47.10.14) (q:draft)
ciangtan = (t:v) (w:set a limit/determine/fix/ration) (d:fix the measure or limit of a thing, such as the length of a life or a ration of food) (e:Nangmah in na ~ khin a/a annek a tuidawnte uh ~ ding uh hi | they will ration their food and drink) (s:khentat) (r:18.14.5/26.4.16) (q:draft)
ciangtang = (t:n) (w:shuttle) (d:in siam ciangtang, the shuttle of a weaver's loom) (e:siam ~ sangin manlang zaw a) (r:18.7.6) (q:draft)
ciangte = (t:n) (w:builders) (d:those who build up a wall, apparently cian build up with the plural te; kulh ciangte is the builders of the wall) (e:Kulh ~ in na a sep kawmun/kulh ~ mai-ah nang hong kosia uh | they insulted you before the builders of the wall) (s:lamte) (r:16.4.18/16.4.5) (q:draft)
ciangto = (t:v) (w:build up/raise) (d:ciang build a wall, with to upward: build a wall up high) (e:a sang mahmahin ~ hi) (b:ciang) (r:14.33.14) (q:draft)
ciangun = (t:ppm) (w:when/after) (d:postpositional marker indicating its been done) (e:zatui anek ~ a cidam/kong sap ~ hong dawng in | answer us when we call/amaute in kei hong muh ~ hong lupeisan uh hi | when they see me they shake their heads/Faro’ kiang panin a paikhiat ~ | when they left Pharaoh) (b:ciang) (r:1.3.5/19.20.9/19.109.25/2.5.20)
ciangzo = (t:v) (w:be able to build up) (d:of a wall; apparently cian, build up, with zo, be able, and not the word ciang, until) (e:kulh a ~ ding) (r:26.22.30) (q:draft, low confidence)
ciangzum = (t:n) (w:goad) (d:ciang, stick, with zum, pointed: the pointed stick used to drive oxen) (e:Bawngtal in a hawlte’ ~ peek) (r:44.26.14) (q:draft)
cianna = (t:n) (w:building/rebuilding) (d:cian build up with the noun suffix na; kulh cianna is the building of the wall) (e:Hih kulh ~-ah kei mahmah in zong/kote’ kulh ~ thu a zak ciangin | when he heard of our building the wall/phung a ~ ding | to build a ramp) (s:lamna) (b:cian) (r:16.5.16/16.4.1/26.21.22) (q:draft)
cianpi = (t:n) (w:siege ramp/mound) (d:cian, pile up, with pi, great: a great heap of stones raised against a city wall) (e:suang ~ khat bawl uh a) (b:cian) (r:10.20.15) (q:draft)
ciantakin = (t:adv) (w:clearly/fully/for certain) (d:cian carefully or clearly, with takin which makes an adverb) (e:hoihsakna thu ~ thei ta uh hen/nading thu a ~ hong lahna) (s:teltakin) (b:cian) (r:45.14.5/49.4.30) (q:draft)
ciap = (t:v) (w:taste) (d:try the taste of food or drink) (e:Leii in an a ~ mah bangin/Pawi ukpa in tui a ~ ciangin | when the master of the banquet tasted the water/An na ~ uh ciangin | when you taste food/na khat peuhpeuh ahi zongin ka ~ taak leh | if I taste anything at all) (r:18.12.11/43.2.9/18.34.3/10.3.35) (q:draft)
ciapkhit = (t:v) (w:after tasting/have tasted) (d:ciap, form of ciam, taste, with khit, after finishing) (e:a ~ ciangin a dawn nuam kei hi) (r:40.27.34) (q:draft)
ciapna = (t:n) (w:tasting) (d:ciap taste, with the noun suffix na: the act of tasting) (e:hih khuaizu tawmno khat ka ~ hangin) (b:ciap) (r:9.14.29) (q:draft)
ciaptehna = (t:n) (w:mark/seal) (d:a mark or seal put on a thing or a person to show whose it is) (e:keima ~ ahi hi/a taltang uhah ~ a neih nadingun | to receive a mark on their foreheads/Tuuno in ~ sagihna a hon ciangin | when the Lamb opened the seventh seal/a taltang uhah ~ i bawl khit matengin | until we put a seal on their foreheads) (s:ciamtehna) (r:53.3.17/66.13.17/66.13.16/66.8.1/66.7.3) as in put a mark on objects
ciat = (t:adv) (w:each/every one) (d:placed after a noun or verb to show that it applies to each one separately) (e:kha li nei ~ uh hi/nomau neihsa ~ na ngah kik ding uh hi | each of you will get back your own property/ama van ~ a pua ding uh hi | each should carry his own load/a zang nih ~ om ding hi | there shall be two projections each) (s:tek/tuak) (r:26.1.6/3.25.13/48.6.5/2.26.17) (q:draft)
ciatah = (t:adv) (w:each to/each in) (d:to or in each one's own, placed after a noun of place) (e:amau khua ~ a pai uh hi/amau’ gam ~, mite ciahsak hi | he sent the people away, each to his own land/amau’ gamh ~ pai uh hi | they went each to their own inheritance/Hih khuapite in a kiim ~ lonona gam nei hi | each of these towns had pastureland around it) (b:ciat) (r:42.2.3/6.24.28/7.2.6/6.21.42) (q:draft)
ciatciat = (t:adj) (w:own) (d:doubled ciat, each: each one’s own, said of every kind or every land separately) (e:nam ~/gam ~/amau’ gam ~ uhah ka koihkik ding hi | I will bring them back, each to their own land) (r:24.12.15/1.1.12)
ciatciatin = (t:phrase) (w:to its kind/each according to its kind) (d:ciatciat with the ending in, after nam, kind: each according to its own kind) (e:amau’ nam ~ piangsak hi) (b:ciatciat) (r:1.1.12)
ciatin = (t:det) (w:each) (d:ciat, each, with the ending in: each one separately, as in min ciatin, each by name) (e:tuate amau min ~ a sam hi/a tuute a min ~ a sap ciangin | when he calls his sheep each by name) (b:ciat) (r:19.147.4/43.10.3)
ciatin = (t:adv) (w:according to/each according to) (d:after nam, kind, or beh, clan: each according to its own) (e:nam ~ Pasian in piangsak hi/amau nam ~ leitung in piangsak hen | let the land produce them according to their kinds/amau’ beh ~ Hori mite’ sung pan ukpite | the Horite chiefs according to their clans/amau tawh kituak ~ thupha a piak | the blessing given as was fitting for each) (b:ciat) (r:1.1.25/1.1.11/1.1.24/1.36.30/1.49.28)
ciatna = (t:n) (d:ciat, each, with the noun suffix na, placed after a verb: the fact or the way of each one doing it) (e:theihna i neih ~ thu i thei hi/meivak khuam a kizat ~ bangin | according to the use of each lampstand) (b:ciat) (r:46.8.1/13.28.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
ciatte = (t:pron) (w:each of them/each one) (d:ciat each, with the plural ending te: each one of several) (e:a kizompih ~ lamah a kha nihte) (b:ciat) (r:26.1.23) (q:draft, low confidence)
ciatun = (t:adv) (w:each/every one) (d:ciat, each, with the plural ending un: each of them in his own way) (e:amau’ hoihsak bang ~ gamta uh hi/na gamtatnasa bang ~ thu kong khen ding hi | I will judge each of you according to your ways/amau’ hoihsak bang ~ mi khempeuh gamta uh hi | everyone did as each saw fit) (s:tek) (b:ciat) (r:7.17.6/26.18.30/7.21.25) (q:draft)
cici = (t:v) (w:keep saying/say again and again/urge) (d:reduplicated ci say; hong cici kei in is do not keep telling me) (e:nading ahi zongin hong ~ kei in/~ khem a, a paikhiat khit ciangin | he keeps saying so to deceive, and after he has gone away) (s:cihcih) (r:8.1.16/19.70.4/20.20.14) (q:draft)
cidam = (t:adj) (w:healthy/well) (d:in good health; cidam lo is sick) (e:~ lo mi tampi sathau tawh zutin/annek tuidawn kicingin ~ hi | well fed and healthy/Nang ~ na ut hiam | do you want to get well/Amah a ~ hiam | is he well) (a:cina) (r:41.6.13/18.21.24/43.5.6/1.29.6) (q:draft)
cidamin = (t:adv) (w:in good health/healthy/safe and sound) (d:cidam, healthy, with the ending in: in good health, unharmed) (e:a vekpi-in ~ thahat kim uh hi/mi khempeuh ~ a ciahkik uh hi | all the people returned safely/a pumpi uh ~ zol hilhial hi | their bodies are healthy and sleek/Nang ~ nong khangto a | you grew up healthy) (s:damin) (b:cidam) (r:19.105.37/42.15.27/6.10.21/19.73.4/26.16.7) (q:draft)
