cidamna = (t:n) (w:health/healing) (d:noun from cidam be healthy; cidamna ngah is to be healed) (e:mite in zong ~ a ngah uh hi/nopsakna leh ~ na ngah nading thu ka ngen hi | I pray that you may have well-being and health/guh leh tangte adingin ~ ahi hi | it is health to the bones/note tungah ~ hong tun’ ding hi | it will bring healing to you) (s:damna) (a:cinatna/natna) (b:cidam) (r:42.6.18/24.8.15/64.1.2/20.16.24/39.4.2) (q:draft)
cidamsak = (t:v) (w:make healthy/give health/make well) (d:causative of cidam, healthy) (e:Lungnopna in pumpi ~ a/Note hong thahatsakin hong ~ ding hi | he will make you strong and healthy) (s:damsak) (b:cidam) (r:20.14.30/23.66.14) (q:draft)
cidamsakin = (t:v) (w:making healthy/giving health) (d:cidamsak, make healthy, with the suffix in) (e:A mite ~ hauhna le lungmuanna) (b:cidamsak) (r:24.33.6) (q:draft)
cidamsakkik = (t:v) (w:restore to health/make well again) (d:cidamsak, make healthy, with kik, again) (e:note kong ~ ding a) (s:damsakkik) (b:cidamsak) (r:24.30.17) (q:draft)
Cidamsuak = (t:v) (w:be healed/become well) (d:cidam healthy with suak become; here a command, be well) (e:~ inla, lungnuam takin va ciah in) (r:41.5.34) (q:draft)
cidamte = (t:n) (w:the healthy/healthy ones) (d:cidam with the plural te: those that are healthy, said of people, animals and sound trees) (e:a ~ zong an vak lo hi/singkung ~ in gah limci gah a | healthy trees bear good fruit) (a:cinate) (b:cidam) (r:38.11.16/42.5.31/40.7.17) (q:draft)
cidamzaw = (t:adj) (w:healthier) (d:cidam, healthy, with zaw, more) (e:kumpi an nete sangin ~ uh a) (b:cidam) (r:27.1.15) (q:draft)
cih = (t:ppm) (d:postpositional marker to indicate objective case) (e:Bang hang hiam ~ leh/Bang hang hiam na ~ leh | for, if you ask why/Zeisu in a ~ ciangin | when Jesus said/Bang hang hiam na ~ uh leh | for, if you all ask why) (r:1.2.3/4.1.48/58.12.29/43.6.41/49.2.14)
cihbangin = (t:adv) (w:as said/according to what is said) (d:cih, say, with bangin, as, written as one word; na cihbangin, as you say) (e:Na ~ hong hih in) (r:1.18.5) (q:draft)
cihcih = (t:v) (w:keep saying/say again and again) (d:cih, form of ci say, doubled to show repeated or continued saying) (e:hong ~ sung teng, sun leh zanin/Tawlkhat a ~ pen bang a cihnopna ahi hiam | what does he mean by saying a little while) (s:cici) (r:19.42.3/43.16.18) (q:draft)
cihin = (t:v) (w:say/declare/tell) (d:cih with the suffix -in; in the formula kong cihin ah, I say to you, introducing a statement) (e:keimah in kong ~ ah/Topa Pasian in ka ~ ah | this is what the Lord God says/Ke’n kong ~-ah, a neihsa khempeuh | I tell you, all his possessions/Topa in kong ~-ah, launa, dum le thangte | the Lord declares: terror, pit and snare) (b:cih) (r:26.32.3/42.12.44/26.31.15/24.48.43) (q:draft)
cihin = (t:v) (w:kindling/lighting) (d:of a fire; mei cih, light a fire) (e:tua gam mite in mei ~) (r:44.28.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
cihinah = (t:v) (w:say/tell) (d:cihin with ah, in the formula kong cihinah, I say to you, introducing a statement) (e:Ke’n kong ~, Kha Siangtho hangin) (b:cihin) (r:48.5.16) (q:draft)
cihkha = (t:v) (w:do to/do anything to) (d:cih do or say, with kha happen to: used with bang or bangmah, do something to someone, usually harm) (e:tua mipa bangmah ~ kei in/note bang hong ~ ka hi hiam | what have I done to you) (r:40.27.19/33.6.3) (q:draft)
cihkhak = (t:v) (w:might say/happen to say) (d:cih, say, with khak, form of kha, happen to: of something one fears others may say) (e:a ~ ding uh launa tawh) (s:genkhak) (r:6.22.25) (q:draft)
cihkhit = (t:v) (w:have said/finish saying) (d:cih, form of ci, say, with khit, finish; before ciangin or phetin: after or as soon as someone has said; in Acts 10:16 of a thing having been done) (e:a ~ phetin amah in khua mukik/a thumveina dong a ~ ciangin | after it had happened a third time/a ~ uh ciangin | after they had said) (s:genkhit) (r:41.10.52/44.19.15/44.10.16) (q:draft)
