cihmawhna = (t:n) (w:distress/need/scarcity/hardship) (d:state of being helpless and in want) (e:amaute’ ~ a don hi/amau ~ panin amah in honkhia hi | he delivered them from their distress/zawn’na leh ~ in migilo gutate bangin | poverty and scarcity like wicked thieves/~ in hong khuhcip hi | scarcity overwhelms us) (s:gentheihna/haksatna/kisapna) (a:cihtheihna) (b:cihmawh) (r:19.106.44/20.6.11/19.107.6/20.24.34) (q:draft)
cihmawhnate = (t:n) (w:needs/distresses/hardships) (d:plural of cihmawhna distress or need) (e:buaina, ~ hong tungsak ding hi/amau ~-ah huh le-uhcin | if you help them in their needs) (s:haksatnate/kisapnate) (b:cihmawhna) (r:5.28.20/47.8.14) (q:draft)
cihmawk = (t:v) (w:say/happen to say) (d:cih say, with mawk carelessly or without ground: say something that does not hold, as in even if it should say) (e:a ~ hangin pumpi na khat ahihna) (r:46.12.15/46.12.16) (q:draft)
