daisak = (t:v) (w:still/calm/quiet) (d:make waves, noise or anger die down; dai, be quiet, with the causative sak) (e:na sin so-na na ~ hi/a tuihualte a saan’ ciangin na ~ hi | when its waves rise you still them/puannuai tawi in sinsona ~ hi | a gift carried under the cloak calms fierce anger/khualmite’ gamlumna na ~ hi | you silence the uproar of foreigners/A kihtakhuai na hehna ~ inla | turn from your fierce anger) (s:damsak/daihsak/daaisak/gamdaisak) (b:dai) (r:19.85.3/19.89.9/20.21.14/23.25.5/2.32.12) (q:draft)
daisakin = (t:v) (w:dishonoring/putting to shame/profaning) (d:form of daisak with the linking suffix in, dishonouring and then going on to the next action) (e:ka min hong ~ kei hong hehsak uh hi/amaute ~ sawl khia hi | he sent them away in disgrace) (b:daisak) (r:26.20.27/13.19.4) (q:draft)
daisakpa = (t:n) (w:one who stills/one who calms) (d:daisak, still, with pa marking a man: the one who stills) (e:mi gamlumte a ~ aw) (b:daisak) (r:19.65.7) (q:draft)
daisaksa = (t:adj) (w:profaned/desecrated) (d:daisak profane, with sa already done: that has been profaned) (e:lakah na ~ uh a lian ka min) (b:daisak) (r:26.36.23) (q:draft)
