daitak-a = (t:adv) (w:quietly/in quiet) (d:dai, quiet, with tak and linking a; daitak-a om is be at rest) (e:~ om hithiat theihna) (s:daitakin) (r:18.3.26) (q:draft)
daitakin = (t:adv) (w:quietly/calmly/silently/peacefully) (d:dai quiet with takin, which makes an adverb) (e:~ Pasian bek ka ngak hi/note in ~ na om ding uh kilawm hi | you ought to stay calm/ka omna panin ~ ka en ding hi | I will look on quietly from my dwelling place/~ a tawlngakna munah om ding uh hi | they will live in places of undisturbed rest) (s:daitak-a/hithiat/dide) (b:dai) (r:19.62.5/44.19.36/23.18.4/23.32.18) (q:draft)
daite = (t:n) (w:pans/shallow vessels) (d:plural, after the name of a vessel: sikbeel daite, pans; kuang daite, shallow bowls or firepans) (e:sikbeel ~ sungah siangtho piaknate huan uh a/meiam luahna kuang ~, kuangte, belte | the firepans, the bowls, the pots) (r:14.35.13/24.52.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
daite = (t:n) (d:in meima daite, a kind of sore named among the diseases of Egypt, perhaps tumors or festering sores) (e:leh meima ~ leh meima lip neite) (r:5.28.27) (q:draft, low confidence)
daitui = (t:n) (w:dew) (d:drops of water that settle on the ground and the grass during the night) (e:giahphual tungah ~ a kiat ciangin/giahphual kiim-ah ~ kia hi | dew lay around the camp/na tungah vantung ~ hong pia hen la | may he give you the dew of heaven/lopa tunga ~ taak bangin deihhuai hi | it is as pleasant as dew on the grass) (s:daingo) (r:4.11.9/28.6.4/2.16.13/1.27.28/20.19.12) (q:draft)
