dal = (t:v) (w:shield/protect/defend/screen) (d:stand between someone and danger, as a shield does; also put a screen in front of a thing) (e:Topa aw, kote hong ~ in la/bangin deihsakna tawh na ~ hi | you shield them with favor as with a shield/Jakob Pasian min in nangmah hong ~ | may the name of the God of Jacob protect you/na nung na mai uhah ka hong ~ ding hi | I will shield you behind and before/puan tawh singkuang na ~ ding hi | you shall screen the ark with the curtain) (s:huu) (r:19.12.7/19.20.1/19.5.12/23.58.8/2.40.3) (q:draft)
dal = (t:n) (w:tin) (d:the metal, named in a list between iron and lead) (e:sumngo, sik, ~, leh haknaw/ngun, sik, ~, leh haknawte hong pia uh hi | they gave silver, iron, tin and lead/sumngo, ~, sik, hak, leh ngun | copper, tin, iron, lead and silver) (r:4.31.22/26.27.12/26.22.18) (q:draft)
dal = (t:n) (w:sheet/piece/copy) (d:counting word for flat things such as sheets of cloth and copies of a written document; puan dal is a curtain) (e:puan ~ ngate khat leh khat khuituahin/puan ~ sawm tawh biakbuk bawl uh hi | they made the tabernacle with ten curtains/gam khempeuh ah ~ khat ciat kipuakin | one copy each being sent to every province/amah in puan ~ sawm-le-khat bawl hi | he made eleven curtains) (r:2.36.16/17.3.14/2.36.8/2.36.14) (q:draft)
daldal = (t:adv) (w:brightly/dazzlingly) (d:placed after tee shine: gleaming and flashing brightly) (e:sumngo zut siang bangin tee ~ a/na mangin a tee ~ milim lian mahmah khat | in your dream a great statue that shone brightly) (r:27.10.6/27.2.31) (q:draft)
