dapphah-in = (t:v) (w:using as a backing/laying against) (d:dap, pad, with phah, lay under, and linking in: with the door behind the ear as a support) (e:kongkhak ~ a bil na vut) (r:5.15.17) (q:draft, low confidence)
dapphahin = (t:v) (w:using as a backing/laying against) (d:dap, pad, with phah, lay under, and linking in: with the door behind the ear as a support) (e:kongkhak ~ a bil na vut) (r:5.15.17) (q:draft, low confidence)
dapphahte = (t:n) (w:saddle blankets/saddle cloths) (d:dap pad with phah spread and the plural te: cloths spread on the back of a horse for riding) (e:sakol ~ hong pia uh hi) (r:26.27.20) (q:draft)
daptakin = (t:adv) (w:silently/speechlessly/in silence) (d:dap silent or dumbfounded, with takin which makes an adverb: without saying a word, in wonder or dismay) (e:mipa in ~ tua nu na en hi/cih nading mel thei loin ~ ka om hi | not knowing what to say, I was speechless) (b:dap) (r:1.24.21/27.8.27) (q:draft)
Dara = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Darda) (d:son of Zerah and grandson of Judah) (r:13.2.6)
Darda = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Darda) (d:wise man, one of the sons of Mahol, whose wisdom Solomon surpassed) (r:11.4.31)
Darias = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Darius) (d:name of several kings, among them Darius the Mede in the book of Daniel and the king of Persia under whom the temple was rebuilt) (r:27.9.1/27.5.31)
darik = (t:n) (w:daric) (d:a Persian gold coin, used in counting gold given for the temple) (e:kham ~ tul sawmnih/kham ~ tulkhat a man tawh kibawl kuang-uk sawmnih | twenty bowls of gold worth a thousand darics/kham talen tulnga leh kham ~ tulsawm | five thousand talents and ten thousand darics of gold) (r:16.7.72/15.8.27/13.29.7) (q:draft)
Darius = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Darius) (d:name of several kings of Media and Persia, written <Darias> in the Bible text)
Darkon = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Darkon) (d:ancestor of a family among the descendants of the servants of Solomon who returned from the exile) (r:15.2.56/16.7.58)
Dathan = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Dathan) (d:son of Eliab of the tribe of Reuben, who rebelled against Moses with Korah and Abiram and was swallowed by the earth) (r:4.16.1/19.106.17)
dau = (t:n) (w:fortune/prosperity) (d:used with pai go in the expression dau pai, prosper or fare well; a dau pai lo is he does not prosper) (e:tua ciangin amah a ~ pai a/mipa a ~ pai lo ding a | the man will not prosper/Nang hong itte a ~ uh pai ta hen | may those who love you prosper/ka ~ hong pai sak ding hi | he will make me prosper) (s:maa) (r:13.29.23/20.28.13/19.122.6/7.17.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
daupai = (t:v) (w:prosper/succeed/do well) (d:be prosperous, secure and at peace; daupai sak make someone prosper) (e:amah a ~ ding hi/nang hong ~ sak ding hi | they will make you prosper/na hihna khempeuh uhah na ~ theih nadingun | so that you may prosper in everything you do/Bang hangin migilote ~ uh a | why do the wicked prosper) (s:maavang/cithei) (r:23.48.15/20.3.2/5.29.9/24.12.1) (q:draft)
daupaina = (t:n) (w:prosperity/success/well-being) (d:the state of doing well and thriving) (e:~ hong pia in/migilote’ ~ ka muh ciangin | when I saw the prosperity of the wicked/~ leh matutsak zawhna ka nei hi | I have prosperity and success/nangma teel mite’ ~ ka muh theih nading | that I may see the prosperity of your chosen ones) (s:maavanna/cihtheihna) (a:kamsiatna) (b:daupai) (r:19.118.25/19.73.3/20.8.18/19.106.4) (q:draft)
daupainate = (t:n) (w:blessings/prosperity/good things) (d:plural of daupaina prosperity) (e:Israelte tungah ka piak ~ khempeuh) (b:daupaina) (r:9.2.32) (q:draft)
daupaisak = (t:v) (w:make prosper/give success) (d:cause to succeed or flourish; daupai with the causative sak) (e:hih peuhmah Topa in ~ hi/kote hong ~ in | grant us success/Amah in mimawhte ~ lo a | he does not make the guilty prosper/nakpitakin hong ~ ding hi | he will make you prosper greatly) (s:citheisak/tuahphasak/telhsak) (b:daupai) (r:1.39.23/5.30.9/19.118.25/18.36.6) (q:draft)
daupaisakpa = (t:n) (w:one who makes prosper) (d:daupaisak, make prosper, with pa marking a man: the one who gives success) (e:amaute a ~ in Pasian hi a) (b:daupaisak) (r:18.22.18) (q:draft)
David = (t:name) (c:male) (w:David) (d:son of Jesse of Bethlehem, the shepherd who became the second king of Israel) (r:19.72.20/8.4.17)
dawh = (t:v) (w:draw/pull out/unsheathe) (d:pull something out or back, most often draw a sword from its sheath; khut dawh tum kik is to draw the hand back in) (e:namsau a ~ khit ciangin/keimah in namsau ka ~ khitna | that I have drawn the sword/a namsau puak a ~ khit ciangin | after he drew the sword he carried/a khut a ~ tum kik lai takin | just as he drew his hand back in) (s:dok) (a:siatkik) (r:40.26.51/26.21.5/43.18.10/1.38.29) (q:draft)
dawh = (t:v) (w:hold out/offer/stretch out) (d:hold out a part of the body or a thing toward someone, to receive or to offer it; bil dawh, hold out the ear, is to listen or pay attention, and ngawng dawh, hold out the neck, is to risk one's life) (e:na bil uh na ~ kei uh hi/Na puansilh hong paipih in la hong ~ in | bring your shawl and hold it out/Hong satte tungah ka nung ka ~ a | I offered my back to those who beat me/a langkhat zong na ~ lai zaw in | hold out the other one too/amau ngawng a ~ ngamte ahi uh hi | they are people who dared to risk their necks) (r:24.25.4/8.3.15/23.50.6/40.5.39/45.16.4) (q:draft)
dawhin = (t:v) (w:hold out/stretch out) (d:form of dawh, hold out, with the linking suffix in; khut dawhin ngen, ask with the hand held out, is to beg) (e:a khut ~ hehpihna a ngen hi/khut ~ ngen hen la | let them beg with the hand held out) (s:zanin) (b:dawh) (r:44.3.3/19.109.10) (q:draft)
dawhkhiat = (t:v) (w:pull out/snatch out) (d:dawh, pull, with khiat, out: pull or snatch something out, as out of a fire) (e:meiphual sung panin ~ bangin) (s:kaikhia) (b:dawh) (r:65.1.23) (q:draft)
dawhkik = (t:v) (w:revoke/withdraw/recall) (d:dawh, pull out, with kik, back: take back or cancel a written order) (e:a laigelhte ~ nadingin lai khat gelhsak in) (s:dokkik) (b:dawh) (r:17.8.5) (q:draft)
dawhlai = (t:v) (w:hold out also/offer as well) (d:dawh, hold out, with lai, still or besides: hold out the other one too) (e:a langkhat zong na ~ un) (r:42.6.29) (q:draft)
dawhna = (t:n) (w:vat) (d:dawh, hold out to receive, with the noun suffix na; leenggahtui dawhna is the vat that catches the juice from the winepress) (e:leenggahtui ~ dim letin a luang) (b:dawh) (r:29.3.13) (q:draft)
dawhsa = (t:adj) (w:drawn/unsheathed) (d:dawh, draw, with sa, already done: of a sword, drawn from its sheath) (e:a khut sungah namsau ~ tawh/namsau ~ tawi-in lampi ah a ding | standing in the road holding a drawn sword) (s:kidoksa) (b:dawh) (r:6.5.13/4.22.31/4.22.23) (q:draft)
dawi = (t:n) (w:demon/evil spirit/devil) (d:an evil spirit; dawi hawlkhia is to drive out a demon and dawi lut is to be possessed by one) (e:~ mangpa suangin dawite a hawlkhia hi/~ tampi hawlkhia uh a | they drove out many demons/kihhuai ~ kha a lut mi khat | a man possessed by an unclean demon spirit/note lakah khat in ~ hilo ahi hiam | is not one of you a devil) (s:dawigilo/dawilawm/khagilo) (r:40.9.34/42.4.33/41.6.13/43.6.70) (q:draft)
dawibia = (t:adj) (w:heathen/pagan/uncircumcised) (d:spirit-worshipping, from dawi spirit and bia worship; used in the Bible for the uncircumcised and for those who do not know God) (e:hih ~ Filistiapa in kua ahi hiam/~ numeite nuamin diang kha ding | the daughters of the uncircumcised might rejoice/Hih ~ mite hong pai-in | these uncircumcised men will come/~ mite le a nin mite | the uncircumcised and the unclean) (r:9.17.26/10.1.20/9.31.4/23.52.1) (q:draft)
dawibiakna = (t:n) (w:demon worship/pagan worship) (d:dawi, demon or spirit, with biakna, worship; dawibiakna mun is a pagan shrine and dawibiakna tau a pagan altar) (e:a om ~ munte a phelkhia hi/~ tau tungah paknamtui a hal mite | people who burn incense on pagan altars/beel sungah ~ sa mehtui a koih mite | people who keep broth of meat from pagan worship in their pots) (r:12.23.8/23.65.3/23.65.4) (q:draft)
dawibiate = (t:n) (w:pagans/heathens/Gentiles) (d:dawibia with the plural te: those who worship spirits, used for the nations who do not know God) (e:Pasian a thei lo ~ in/A beisa hunah ~’ gamtat bangin | in the past, the way the pagans live/Thu um lo ~ bangin gamta nawn kei un | no longer live as the unbelieving Gentiles do/na luah gam sungah ~ hong pai uh hi | the nations have come into your inheritance) (s:lawkite) (b:dawibia) (r:52.4.4/19.79.1/60.4.3/49.4.17) (q:draft)
dawigilo = (t:n) (w:evil spirit/demon) (d:dawi, spirit, with gilo, evil; dawigilo lut is to be possessed by an evil spirit) (e:~ a lut mite tungah/~ lutpa in tuate tungah diangin | the man with the evil spirit jumped on them/a paikhia ~’ khate ahi uh hi | they are spirits of demons that go out) (s:dawi/dawilawm/khagilo) (r:44.19.13/66.16.16/44.19.16/66.16.14) (q:draft)
dawigilote = (t:n) (w:demons/evil spirits/devils) (d:dawigilo, evil spirit, with the plural te) (e:~ a biakna uh ahi hi/Topa’ hai leh ~’ hai | the cup of the Lord and the cup of demons/Note ~ tawh na kipawl ding uh | that you be partners with demons/~’ thuhilhna ahi zongin a ngai ding uh a | they will listen to the teachings of demons) (s:dawite) (b:dawigilo) (r:46.10.20/66.18.2/46.10.21/54.4.2) (q:draft)
dawilawm = (t:n) (w:demon/evil spirit) (d:an evil spirit that takes hold of a person; dawilawm nei is to have a demon, to be demon-possessed) (e:Keimah in ~ nei ka hi kei hi/Nang ~ nei na hi hi | you have a demon/Amah ~ nei mihai ahi hi | he is demon-possessed and mad/Tua thu in ~ neite’ thu ahi kei hi | these are not the words of people who have a demon) (s:dawi/dawigilo/khagilo) (r:43.8.49/43.10.20/43.7.20/43.10.21) (q:draft)
dawilok = (t:v) (w:be disturbed/be alarmed) (d:said of the heart: be shaken, disturbed or frightened; a sin a dawilok tuan loh is that its heart is not disturbed at all) (e:a sin a ~ tuan loh) (s:patau) (r:23.31.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
dawilutna = (t:n) (w:demon possession) (d:dawi evil spirit, lut enter, with the noun suffix na; before mipa, the man possessed by an evil spirit) (e:~ mipa in amaute buan gawpin) (r:44.19.16) (q:draft)
Dawimang = (t:n) (w:prince of demons/ruler of demons) (d:dawi demon with mang lord or chief; dawimang lianpen pa is the chief ruler of the demons) (e:~ lianpen pa min tawh) (r:40.9.34) (q:draft)
dawimangpa = (t:n) (w:devil) (d:the devil, chief of the evil spirits; dawi evil spirit and mang chief, with pa for a male person) (e:~ in Topa kiang pan paikhia a/~ in Zeisu paipihto a | the devil led Jesus up/~’ kheemna thuak nadingin | to be tempted by the devil/Tahum tang vawh galpa in ~ hi | the enemy who sows the weeds is the devil) (r:40.4.11/42.4.5/40.4.1/40.13.39) (q:draft)
Dawimangpa = (t:n) (w:devil/evil one) (d:the devil, literally the chief of the demons; written with a capital letter as a title or at the start of a sentence) (e:~ hun na pia kei un/~’ kheemna na nan’ zawh nadingun | so that you can stand against the devil's schemes/~’ khut sungah a om | are in the hand of the evil one/~ Satan ahi, tanglai gulpi manin | he seized the ancient serpent, who is the devil, Satan) (r:49.4.27/59.4.7/49.6.11/62.5.19/66.20.2) (q:draft)
dawite = (t:n) (w:demons/evil spirits) (d:dawi, demon, with the plural te; dawite hawlkhia is to drive out demons) (e:Dawi mangpa suangin ~ a hawlkhia hi/~ hawlkhiat theihna thu a neih nading uh | so that they would have authority to drive out demons/Beelzebub suangin ~ a hawlkhia hi | he drives out demons by Beelzebul/Ahi zongin ~ in amau kiangah | but the evil spirits said to them) (s:dawigilote) (b:dawi) (r:40.9.34/41.3.11/41.3.15/40.12.24/44.19.15) (q:draft)
dawivai = (t:adj) (w:demonic) (d:of or from evil spirits) (e:a ~ ahi hi) (r:59.3.15) (q:draft)
dawivei = (t:adj) (w:demon-possessed/possessed) (d:dawi, evil spirit: troubled or held by an evil spirit; dawivei mi is a person possessed by a demon) (e:kikhopna inn sungah ~ mi khat hong lut a/~ pa a damnazia thute | how the demon-possessed man was healed/~, pau theilo mi khat | a demon-possessed man who could not speak/tua ~ mite’ thu le a thupiang khempeuh | the news of the demon-possessed men and all that happened) (r:41.1.23/40.9.32/42.8.36/40.8.33) (q:draft)
Dawiveite = (t:n) (w:demon-possessed people) (d:dawivei possessed by a demon with the plural te, at the start of a sentence) (e:~ in hih bangin thu gen thei lo hi) (r:43.10.21) (q:draft)
dawizek = (t:adj) (w:unclean/defiled) (d:ritually unclean, of a thing that may not be eaten or touched) (e:ama a dingin a ~ hi pah hi/ama thu-in a ~ om het lo hi | nothing is unclean in itself) (s:nin) (a:siang) (r:45.14.14) (q:draft)
dawk = (t:v) (w:project/jut out/stick out/come out) (d:stand out from a surface or line, said of a tower, a cliff, the end of a staff) (e:Geba mai leitaw lamah ~ hi/a lian tausang ~ panin | from the great projecting tower/a bem a ~ tungah om hi | it was on the rounded part that juts out) (s:dawkkhia) (r:9.14.5/16.3.27/11.7.20) (q:draft)
dawk = (t:n) (w:bay/inlet) (d:in tuipi dawk or tui dawk, a part of the sea that juts into the land) (e:Jordan tun’na tuipi ~ panin kipan hi/Ci Tuipi ~ leilu lamah gamgi tawp hi | the border ends at the northern bay of the Salt Sea/tui ~ khat a mu uh hi | they saw a bay) (s:tuidawk) (r:6.15.5/44.27.39/6.18.19) (q:draft)
dawkin = (t:v) (w:jut out/project/come forward) (d:form of dawk, stick out, with the linking suffix in; of a crag, stand out toward a place; mai dawk is to step forward) (e:Mikmash mai leilu lamah ~/Kha khat hong mai ~ Topa mai-ah ding a | a spirit came forward and stood before the Lord) (b:dawk) (r:9.14.5/11.22.21) (q:draft)
dawkkhia = (t:v) (w:project/stick out/come out) (d:dawk emerge with khia out) (e:inn panin hong ~) (b:dawk) (r:16.3.25) (q:draft)
dawkkikto = (t:v) (w:rise up again/come up again) (d:dawk emerge, kik again, to upward) (e:a hong ~ nawn kei ding) (r:24.51.64) (q:draft)
dawksa = (t:see) <dawksa-in>
dawksa-in = (t:adj) (w:bared/exposed/uncovered) (d:dawk stick out or show, with sa already done and the linking ending in: with a part of the body left showing) (e:tangguak kheguakin, tawbo ~) (r:23.20.4) (q:draft)
dawksak = (t:v) (w:lay bare/expose/put out) (d:make something show or stick out, dawk with the causative sak) (e:khat in a khut ~ hi/a khuapi bulpite ka ~ ding hi | I will lay bare the foundations of her city/a bul ~ ding a sawm ka hi hi | I intend to lay its foundation bare) (b:dawk) (r:1.38.28/33.1.6/26.13.14) (q:draft)
dawksakin = (t:v) (w:stretch out/put out/extend) (d:dawk stick out, with the causative sak and the linking ending in: holding out the tip of a staff) (e:a khut sunga om ciangkhut dawn ~) (b:dawksak) (r:7.6.21) (q:draft)
dawkto = (t:v) (w:rise up/come up) (d:dawk emerge with to upward) (e:a hong ~ kik nawn kei) (a:tumsuk) (b:dawk) (r:24.51.64) (q:draft)
dawktoh = (t:v) (w:rise up/tower/jut up) (d:dawk jut out, with toh upward: stand up high above the surroundings, said of a mountain) (e:tuipi tungah sangpi-in a ~ bangin) (b:dawkto) (r:24.46.18) (q:draft)
dawl = (t:n) (w:deck) (d:a deck of a ship, one of the storeys of the ark) (e:a ~ nuainung, a ~ nihna leh/leh a ~ thumnate bawl in | and make the third deck) (r:1.6.16)
dawl = (t:n) (w:floor) (d:a floor or storey of a building) (e:A ~ nuainung pen lut nadingin/A ~ nuainung pen tong nga zai-in | the lowest floor was five cubits wide/a ~ nuainung panin a tungnung dongin | from the lowest floor to the top one) (r:11.6.8/11.6.6/26.41.7)
dawl = (t:n) (w:level) (d:one of the levels of a building, counted one above another) (e:a ~ laita-ah kahlei zui-in kipai-in/Hih inndei neute ~ thum pha a | these side rooms were on three levels/tua inndei ~ thumte pen | those rooms on the three levels) (s:cial) (r:11.6.8/26.41.6/26.42.6)
dawm = (t:v) (w:spare/deal gently with/be lenient with) (d:treat with care or mercy, hold back from harming; in oaths hong dawm kei ta hen is may he not spare me, and dawm loin is without mercy) (e:Amah in amaute ~ loin tampi that hi/note hong ~ tuan lo ding hi | he will not spare you either/Pasian in kei hong ~ kei ta hen | may God not spare me/tangvalpa Absalom hong ~ mahmah un | deal very gently with the young man Absalom/hehpih lo, ~ lo, it loin ka siasak ding | I will destroy them without pity, mercy or love) (s:hehpih) (r:7.15.8/9.14.44/45.11.21/10.18.5/24.13.14) (q:draft)
dawmin = (t:v) (w:deal gently with/treat with care) (d:dawm treat with care, with the linking ending in: gently, considerately) (e:na zite uh ~ na hehpih un/khat leh khat ~ na ki-it ta un | love one another tenderly) (b:dawm) (r:60.3.7/45.12.10) (q:draft)
dawn = (t:v) (w:drink) (d:take a drink; tui dawn is to drink water and zu dawn to drink wine or beer) (e:an ne-in tui ~ hi/Bang ~ ding i hi hiam | what are we to drink/zukhamte tawh an ne, zu ~ khawm a | he eats and drinks with drunkards/keelte’ sisan ~ ding ka hi hiam | do I drink the blood of goats/an ne lo, tui ~ loin a om hi | he did not eat or drink) (r:11.13.19/40.24.49/2.15.24/19.50.13/44.9.9) (q:draft)
dawn = (t:v) (w:meet/welcome/go to meet) (d:go out to meet someone who is coming) (e:a ~ dingin a paikhia uh hi/giahphual pua-ah a ~ dingin paikhia uh hi | they went outside the camp to meet them/lungdamna tawh a ~ dingin hong pai hi | he came gladly to meet him/Pasian’ vantungmite in amah ~ hi | the angels of God met him/Piter a tum ciangin Kornelias in ~ a | when Peter came in, Cornelius met him) (s:dawntuah/kimu) (r:43.12.18/4.31.13/7.19.3/1.32.1/44.10.25) (q:draft)
dawn = (t:n) (w:top/tip/end) (d:the top or tip of something, as in mual dawn, mountain top, ciangkhut dawn, the tip of a staff, and vun dawn, foreskin) (e:mual ~ panin amaute awng sak un/Sinai Mual ~-ah Topa hong paisuk hi | the Lord came down on the top of Mount Sinai/a naungek vun ~ ki-at ding hi | the baby's foreskin shall be cut/a khutsunga om a ciangkhut ~ dawk sakin | putting out the tip of the staff in his hand) (s:khung) (a:bul/taw) (r:23.42.11/3.12.3/2.19.20/9.14.27) (q:draft)
dawna = (t:n) (w:top/summit/tip) (d:dawn, top, with the ending a, at or on the top of; mual dawna biakpiakna munte are the hilltop places of worship, the high places) (e:innkhum ~ vasa khat guak a om/teembaw ~ tuang tawh na kibang ding hi | you will be like one riding on top of a ship/Khuampi lu ~ om khuamluzepna | the capital on top of the pillar/mual ~ biakpiaknate kilakhia lo hi | the hilltop places of worship were not removed) (b:dawn) (r:19.102.7/14.14.3/20.23.34/11.7.18/14.20.33) (q:draft)
dawnah = (t:prep) (w:on top of/at the top of) (d:dawn, top, with the place marker ah, placed after the noun) (e:Mual ~ a om khua/A khuampite ~ unok pak a kibawl om hi | on top of the pillars there was lily work/Peor mual ~ Balaam paipih hi | he took Balaam to the top of Mount Peor/khainiangte bawlin khuampite ~ koih hi | he made chains and put them on top of the pillars) (s:tungah) (a:phungah) (b:dawn) (r:40.5.14/11.7.19/11.7.22/4.23.28/14.3.16) (q:draft)
dawndawn = (t:v) (w:drink and drink/keep drinking) (d:dawn drink said twice, for drinking freely or again and again) (e:khamtheihzu ~ ni/tui i dawn bangin siatna i ~ a | we drink up evil as we drink water/si ding ihih ciangin nene-in ~ ni | since we are going to die, let us eat and drink) (r:23.56.12/18.15.16/23.22.13) (q:draft)
dawng = (t:v) (w:answer/reply) (d:give an answer to a person or to a question) (e:Job in Topa ~ a/ka thudotnate hong ~ in | answer my questions/kamkhat beek ~ kik thei lo a | could not answer back even one word/ka ~ ta hi | I will answer now/Amah ~ kei un | do not answer him) (s:dawngkik) (a:dong/dot) (r:18.40.3/24.21.3/18.40.7/40.22.46/18.32.20/12.18.36) (q:draft)
dawngdawng = (t:v) (w:keep answering/answer again and again) (d:dawng answer, doubled: go on answering what is asked) (e:hai thudotna ~ lecin, nang zong) (r:20.26.4) (q:draft)
dawngin = (t:v) (w:answer/reply) (d:form of dawng with the linking suffix in, answering, usually before the words spoken) (e:Hit mite in Abraham ~/amah in kei hong ~ | and he answered me/Jonathan in Saul ~ | Jonathan answered Saul/Tua ciangin mite in ~ | then the people answered) (s:dawngkikin) (b:dawng) (r:1.23.5/8.3.5/19.34.4/9.20.28/6.24.16) (q:draft)
dawngkik = (t:v) (w:answer/reply/answer back) (d:dawng, answer, with kik, back: give an answer in return) (e:Zeisu in kam khat beek ~ lo a/Kei nong sap leh kong ~ ding a | call to me and I will answer you/ci-in ka ~ hi | I replied, saying/Tua bangin siampi ukpa na ~ hiam | is that how you answer the high priest) (s:dawng) (a:dong) (b:dawng) (r:41.15.5/24.33.3/38.4.5/43.18.22) (q:draft)
dawngkikin = (t:v) (w:answering/replying) (d:dawngkik answer back, with the linking suffix in: answered and went on to say) (e:a nasempa in Saul ~/Kumpipa in amah ~ | the king answered him) (s:dawngin) (b:dawngkik) (r:9.9.8/11.2.31) (q:draft)
dawngthei = (t:v) (w:be able to answer) (d:dawng answer with thei can) (e:thu a ~ mihing sagih sangin) (b:dawng) (r:20.26.16) (q:draft)
dawnin = (t:v) (w:drink) (d:form of dawn with the linking ending in, used before a following verb) (e:lampi gei-a luitui ~ thahat ding/mite in an ne, tui ~, kipi | people were eating, drinking and marrying/amaute in ne-in ~ lungdam uh hi | they ate and drank and were happy/Ka topa in hih hai sung panin ~ | my master drinks from this cup) (b:dawn) (r:19.110.7/21.3.13/40.24.38/11.4.20/1.44.5) (q:draft)
dawnin = (t:v) (w:answer/reply) (d:form of dawng, answer, with the linking ending in) (e:amaute ngawh ~ khangham mite’ ngaihsut) (r:14.10.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
dawnin = (t:v) (w:meet/welcome) (d:form of dawn, meet, with the linking ending in) (e:Pasian’ mual-ah amah ~ amah nam hi/Ka sanggampa Esau in note hong ~ | when my brother Esau meets you/Topa in Balaam na ~ ama kiangah | the Lord met Balaam and said to him/Melkhizedek in Abraham na ~ thupha a pia hi | Melchizedek met Abraham and blessed him/a hong tun’ ciangin ~ na tungsak un | when he comes, welcome him) (s:dawntuahin) (b:dawn) (r:2.4.27/1.32.17/4.23.16/58.7.1/51.4.10) (q:draft)
dawnkei = (t:v) (w:not drink) (d:dawn drink with the negative kei, used in a prohibition) (e:zu ahi zongin ~ in la) (r:7.13.7) (q:draft)
dawnkha = (t:v) (w:get to drink/drink) (d:dawn drink with kha, which shows that the action comes to happen; with kei, never get to drink) (e:a zu na ~ kei ding uh hi/a leenggahzu na ~ kei ding uh hi | you will not get to drink their wine) (r:33.6.15/30.5.11) (q:draft)
dawnkhawm = (t:v) (w:drink together/drink with) (d:dawn, drink, with khawm, together; often paired with nekhawm, eat together) (e:an nekhawm tui ~ na hi uh hiam/nekhawm ~ dingin na tu kei ding hi | you shall not sit down to eat and drink together/dawigilote’ hai na ~ zo kei ding uh hi | you cannot also drink the cup of demons/kha tawh kipawl tui a ~ uh | they all drank the spiritual drink together) (b:dawn) (r:42.5.30/24.16.8/46.10.21/46.10.4) (q:draft)
dawnkhawmin = (t:v) (w:drinking together) (d:dawn drink, khawm together, with the linking suffix in) (e:an nekhawm tui ~ ka om) (b:dawnkhawm) (r:44.10.41) (q:draft)
dawnkhia = (t:v) (w:bud/sprout/put out shoots) (d:dawn, the tip or shoot of a plant, with khia out) (e:Israel palhin ~ ding a) (b:dawn) (r:23.27.6) (q:draft)
dawnkhop = (t:v) (w:drink together with/drink along with) (d:dawn drink with khop together; here swallow something along with the water) (e:tui tawh na ~ khak loh) (r:40.23.24) (q:draft, low confidence)
dawnkik = (t:v) (w:drink again) (d:dawn, drink, with kik, again) (e:leenggahzu thak ka ~ ni matengin/leenggahzu ka ~ nawn kei ding hi | I will not drink wine again) (b:dawn) (r:41.14.25/40.26.29) (q:draft)
dawnkikna = (t:n) (w:answer/reply) (d:dawnkik answer back with the noun suffix na) (e:A mantakin ~ pen lawm taktak hihna/A thu za khin nai lopi-in ~ pen | to answer before hearing the matter out/Topa’ hong ~ bangbang ka hong gen ding hi | I will tell you whatever the Lord answers) (s:thudawnna) (a:thudotna/dotna) (b:dawnkik) (r:20.24.26/24.42.4/20.18.13) (q:draft)
dawnkim = (t:v) (w:all drink) (d:dawn drink with kim all, every one drinks) (e:hai panin a ~ uh hi) (r:41.14.23) (q:draft)
dawnna = (t:n) (w:drinking/drink) (d:the act of drinking, from dawn drink; dawnna hai is a drinking cup) (e:leenggahtui thak ~ in nungakte thadimsak ding/an nekna, tui ~-ah a kip kei hi | it does not rest on eating and drinking/Kumpi Solomon’ ~ haite khempeuh kham hi | all King Solomon's drinking cups were gold/Sa nekna, leenggahtui ~-a kipan | from eating meat and drinking wine on) (s:tuidawnna) (b:dawn) (r:38.9.17/45.14.21/45.14.17/14.9.20) (q:draft)
dawnna = (t:n) (w:meeting/place of meeting) (d:the act or place of going to meet someone, from dawn meet, welcome) (e:Martha’ ~ munah a om lai hi) (b:dawn) (r:43.11.30) (q:draft, low confidence)
dawnngeek = (t:n) (w:tender shoot/tender sprig) (d:dawn top or tip with ngeek tender, the soft topmost shoot of a tree) (e:a ~ khat ka satkhia ding) (s:dawnngek) (r:26.17.22) (q:draft)
dawnngek = (t:n) (w:tender shoot/tender sprig) (d:dawn top or tip with ngek tender, the soft topmost shoot of a tree) (e:a ~ khat ka satkhia ding) (s:dawnngeek) (r:26.17.22) (q:draft)
dawnngekte = (t:n) (w:shoots/tender shoots) (d:dawnngek, the young tender tip of a branch, with the plural te) (e:a ~ in Gunpi lam zuan hi) (b:dawnngek) (r:19.80.11) (q:draft)
dawnpah = (t:v) (w:answer promptly/reply at once) (d:dawn, the form of dawng answer used before a suffix, with pah at once) (e:A hun mahin ~ theihna lungkimhuai a/a kilawm kammal tawh ~ theihna | being able to answer at once with a fitting word) (r:20.15.23) (q:draft)
dawnpawlte = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:melons) (d:named after cucumbers in the list of the foods of Egypt, where the English has melons; with the plural te) (e:ngasate, tangmaite, ~, lo-uih neute) (r:4.11.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
dawnsak = (t:v) (w:give to drink/make drink) (d:dawn, drink, with the causative sak: give someone a drink or make someone drink) (e:tui bek hong ~ in/tua numei a tuisia ~ ding a | he shall make the woman drink the bitter water/ut lopipi-in tuikha hong ~ a | he made me drink bitter water against my will/note in Nazir mite, leenggahzu na ~ uh a | you made the Nazirites drink wine/gutui ka ~ ding hi | I will make them drink poisoned water) (s:tulh) (b:dawn) (r:27.1.12/4.5.24/25.3.15/30.2.12/24.9.15) (q:draft)
dawnsakin = (t:v) (w:giving to drink) (d:dawn drink, the causative sak, with the linking suffix in) (e:savun thawl hongin ~ amah a khuhkik) (b:dawnsak) (r:7.4.19) (q:draft)
dawnsim = (t:v) (w:drink secretly/drink in secret) (d:dawn drink with sim secretly; of stolen water in the proverb) (e:Tui ~, khum diak a) (r:20.9.17) (q:draft)
dawnte = (t:n) (w:drinkers/those who drink) (d:dawn, drink, with the plural te: those who drink; in an nek tui dawnte also the eating and drinking itself) (e:Leenggahzu tampi a ~/No leenggahzu ~ aw, thuumin tau un | you drinkers of wine, wail/ka si a ~ in kei sungah om a | those who drink my blood remain in me/A an nek a tui ~ uh zong | their eating and their drinking too) (b:dawn) (r:23.5.22/29.1.5/43.6.56/38.7.6) (q:draft)
dawnte = (t:n) (w:tops/tips/ends) (d:dawn, top or tip, with the plural te, as in mual dawnte, mountain tops, bil dawnte, ear lobes, and khutpi dawnte, tips of the thumbs) (e:amau' taklam khutpi ~ leh/tua kha ni khat ni-in mual ~ kidawk hi | on the first day of that month the mountain tops appeared/Israel mualsang ~ en in la | look toward the mountain heights of Israel/leitung mualsang ~ hong siksuk ding hi | he will tread on the heights of the earth) (a:bulte) (b:dawn) (r:2.29.20/1.8.5/26.6.2/33.1.3) (q:draft)
dawntheihna = (t:n) (w:ability to answer/being able to answer) (d:dawn, the form of dawng answer used before a suffix, with theih can and the noun suffix na) (e:thudotna haksa nonote ~/dotnate limtakin Jesuh in a ~ a muh ciangin | when he saw that Jesus had answered the questions well) (r:27.5.12/41.12.28) (q:draft)
