deda = (t:adv) (d:follows a word for something flat or wide, such as peek, zai or kizal, and stresses how broadly it spreads; a peek deda is the wide sheet of Acts 10, lupna zai deda a wide bed) (e:na lupna zai ~ tungah/tua a peek ~ kilato kik hi | the sheet was taken up again/sikli a nei a peek ~ khat | a wide sheet with four corners/Tua a peek ~ tung, limtakin ka et ciangin | when I looked closely at the sheet) (r:23.57.8/44.10.16/44.11.10/44.10.11/44.11.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
