deih = (t:v) (w:want/desire/wish) (d:wish to have something or wish that something happens; the thing or clause wanted comes before it) (e:nong ngaih ding uh ka ~ hi/thei loin na om ding uh ka ~ kei | we do not want you to be unaware/Koi lai takah hong bawlsak le-ung na ~ hiam | where do you want us to prepare it/ama ~ taamtaak leh taaksan singte | the cedar and juniper logs he wanted) (s:lunggulh) (r:18.32.10/11.5.10/52.4.13/42.22.9)
deihdeih = (t:n) (w:desire/whatever one desires/wish) (d:deih want said twice, with a before it: the very thing or everything that one wants) (e:mihoihte in a ~ uh ngah uh hi/tu-in na ~ uh na theita ding uh hi | now you will come to know what you are asking for/ka ~, ka lametet bulpi ahi hi | is my desire and my chief hope) (s:deihna) (r:20.10.24/47.13.3/50.1.20) (q:draft)
deihdeihin = (t:adv) (w:as much as one wants/freely/liberally) (d:deihdeih, whatever one wants, with the adverb ending in: without limit, as much as anyone wishes) (e:tawh kituakin ~ zu kizang hi) (s:ututin) (b:deihdeih) (r:17.1.7) (q:draft)
deihdeihte = (t:n) (w:desires/all that is desired) (d:deihdeih, what one desires, with the plural te: all that is desired) (e:Israel-te’ ~ kua’ tungah om) (s:deihnate) (b:deihdeih) (r:9.9.20) (q:draft)
deihgawh = (t:v) (w:covet/crave/desire greedily) (d:want strongly something that belongs to another or that is not good to want) (e:Dangka a ~ Farisaite in/ngun ahi zongin, puan ahi zongin ka ~ kei hi | I have not coveted silver or clothing/Na vengte’ inn na ~ kei ding hi | you shall not covet your neighbor’s house/Note in na ~ uh hangin na ngah kei uh hi | you covet but you do not get) (s:duhgawh/iplah) (r:42.16.14/44.20.33/2.20.17/59.4.2) (q:draft)
deihgawhna = (t:n) (w:evil desire/lust/craving/covetousness) (d:deihgawh covet with the noun suffix na: strong desire, in the verses mostly evil desire) (e:~ atuam atuam zui-in/adang ~ lutin thu depgawp a | desires for other things come in and choke the word/note in ~ na zuih nadingun | so that you obey its desires/~ thu tu-in zui loin | no longer following evil desires) (s:lunggulhna) (b:deihgawh) (r:55.3.6/45.6.12/41.4.19/60.1.14) (q:draft)
deihgawhnate = (t:n) (w:evil desires/lusts/cravings) (d:plural of deihgawhna: strong, mostly sinful desires) (e:Leitung leh leitung ~ in a mangthang ding/pumpi tawh kipawl ~ khempeuh | all the desires that belong to the body/gal a bawl thei na ~ uh pan | from your desires that wage war) (s:lunggulhnate/deihluatnate) (b:deihgawhna) (r:62.2.17/60.2.11/59.4.1) (q:draft)
deihhuai = (t:adj) (w:pleasant/pleasing) (d:deih want with huai, worthy of: good to have or to look at, giving pleasure) (e:A ~, nek dinga a hoih singkung/lopa tunga daitui taak bangin ~ hi | it is pleasant like dew on the grass) (b:deih) (r:1.2.9/20.19.12)
deihhuai = (t:adj) (w:satisfying/acceptable/pleasing) (d:found good enough to be accepted, pleasing to the one who receives it; deihhuai sa is to find something pleasing) (e:nong thoihnate uh ~ ka sa kei hi | I do not find your sacrifices pleasing) (s:lungkimhuai) (b:deih) (r:24.6.20)
deihhuai = (t:adj) (w:attractive/lovely/desirable) (d:worth wanting because of beauty or value; with zaw, more desirable than something else) (e:Rachel mel hoih-in ~ hi/vantung aksi bangin na ~ hi | you are as lovely as the stars of heaven/ngun sangin thu theihna ~ zaw hi | understanding is more desirable than silver/khuapi ~ khempeuh zo-in | conquering every choice city) (s:ngaihbaang) (a:muhdahhuai/kihhuai) (b:deih) (r:1.29.17/22.6.4/20.16.16/12.3.19)
deihhuaina = (t:adj) (w:desired/desirable) (d:deihhuai desirable with the suffix na: the quality that makes a thing or person wanted) (e:tua singkung a ~ a muh ciangin/ama’ limin ~ mel nei lo a | his form had no beauty to make him desirable) (b:deihhuai) (r:1.3.6/23.53.2)
deihhuaizaw = (t:adj) (w:more desirable/more precious) (d:deihhuai desirable with the comparative zaw; the thing it is compared with takes sang or sangin, than) (e:sang ahi zongin tuate ~ a) (s:manphazaw) (b:deihhuai) (r:19.19.10) (q:draft)
deihin = (t:v) (w:wanting/desiring/wishing for) (d:deih want with the linking ending in: wanting something, used before a following verb) (e:tua nu ~ na zi dingin/ka lungsim in ~, Pasian kiangah thu ka ngetsak hi | with my heart’s desire I pray to God/note neihsate ~, a zong ka hi kei hi | I am not one who seeks you because I want your possessions/a lawn’ nading ~ Zeisu kiangah hong paipih uh | they brought them to Jesus, wanting him to touch them/kisikkikna a ngah nadingun ~ | wanting them to come to repentance) (s:lunggulhin) (b:deih) (r:5.21.11/45.10.1/47.12.14/41.10.13/61.3.9) (q:draft)
deihkik = (t:v) (w:want again/desire again) (d:deih want with kik again: want someone or something a second time) (e:Kumpipa in a ~ kei leh) (b:deih) (r:17.2.14) (q:draft)
deihlam = (t:n) (w:that one wants/the fact of wanting) (d:deih want with lam, which turns the clause into the thing that is known: ka deihlam is that I want) (e:ka ~ hong thei na hih leh/Sum lam lopi-in sum ka ~) (r:40.25.26/42.19.22) (q:draft)
deihlohna = (t:n) (w:what is not wanted/ungodliness) (d:deih want, loh not, with the noun suffix na; Pasian’ deihlohna is what God does not want, ungodliness) (e:Pasian’ ~ tawh kipawl) (r:65.1.18) (q:draft)
deihlua = (t:v) (w:want too much/be greedy for/love excessively) (d:deih want with lua too much; with sum, be a lover of money) (e:sum a ~ lo mite hi ding/Mi pawlkhat in sum ~ liang uh ahih manin | because some people are so eager for money) (s:deihgawh) (b:deih) (r:54.3.3/54.6.10) (q:draft)
deihluat = (t:v) (w:want too much/crave/love excessively) (d:form of deihlua used before leh, in and mahmah and in dependent clauses; also as a noun, craving) (e:hih leitung nate a ~ leh/amaute in gamlak ah ~ mahmah na nei uh a | in the desert they had a great craving) (s:duhluat) (b:deihlua) (r:62.2.15/19.106.14) (q:draft)
deihluatin = (t:v) (w:desiring too much/loving too much) (d:deihluat desire too much, with the linking ending in: loving something too much) (e:kizom lo thute ~ nei kei un) (b:deihluat) (r:62.2.15) (q:draft)
deihluatna = (t:n) (w:zeal/strong desire/eagerness/excessive love) (d:deih want, luat too much, with the noun suffix na: a very strong desire for something; sum deihluatna is the love of money) (e:Topa’ ~ in hih thu hong tungsak ding hi/Nangma inn ka ~ mei bangin ka sungah sa a | zeal for your house burns in me like fire/Topa a’ ding ka ~ hong thei in | see my zeal for the Lord/Sum ~ in siatna namkim piangsak hi | the love of money produces every kind of evil) (s:kinna) (b:deihluat) (r:23.37.32/19.69.9/12.10.16/54.6.10) (q:draft)
deihluatnate = (t:n) (w:excessive desires/lusts) (d:deihluat desire excessively, with the noun suffix na and the plural te) (e:piangsak thei duhluatna le ~ panin) (s:deihgawhnate) (b:deihluatna) (r:61.1.4) (q:draft)
deihna = (t:n) (w:desire/will/wish/purpose) (d:deih want with the noun suffix na: what someone wants; Pasian’ deihna is the will of God and lungsim deihna the desire of the heart) (e:na lungsim ~ nang hong pia ding hi/Ama lungsim’ ~ nang in na piakhin a | you have granted him his heart’s desire/~ amaute tungah a kigen mateng | until his will was made known to them/ama ~ bangin na a sem dingin | to do the work according to his wish) (s:utna/lunggulhna) (b:deih) (r:19.37.4/25.3.37/19.21.2/3.24.12/10.19.18) (q:draft)
deihnate = (t:n) (w:desires/wishes/will) (d:plural of deihna: the things someone wants; Pasian’ deihnate is what God wills) (e:keima ~ a tawp dongin a zui mi/migilopa’ ~ tangtungsak kei in la | do not fulfil the desires of the wicked/Pasian’ ~ na thei uh a | you know God’s will/ka ~ nong kicingsak ding hi | you shall meet my wishes) (s:lunggulhnate) (b:deihna) (r:66.2.26/19.140.8/45.2.18/11.5.9) (q:draft)
deihpa = (t:n) (w:one who wants/one who upholds) (d:deih want, with pa marking a man: the man who wants something; thutang a deihpa is the one who wants justice) (e:thutang a ~ na mudah uh) (b:deih) (r:30.5.10) (q:draft)
deihpha = (t:v) (w:devote oneself to/be diligent in) (d:meaning taken from the context, set the heart fully on something) (e:hih nate ~ in la) (r:54.4.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
deihsak = (t:v) (w:wish for/want for/desire for/care for) (d:want something for another person or want another to do or be something, care for someone’s good; deihsak-a satna is beating out of care, discipline) (e:midik na hih ding kong ~ hi/na ngah nadingun ka hong ~ uh hi | we wish that you may obtain it/~-a satna in mihoih suaksak thei hi | discipline given out of care can make a person good/tua bang mite a’ ding thupha a ~ mite | those who wish blessing on such people/siatna ni hong tun’ ding ka ~ loh lam | that I have not wished for the day of disaster to come) (b:deih) (r:18.33.32/20.22.15/58.6.12/63.1.11/24.17.16) (q:draft)
deihsakin = (t:v) (w:wishing for/desiring for) (d:deihsak, want something for someone, with the linking ending in: wishing it for them) (e:a ngah nading ~ lungsim takpi) (b:deihsak) (r:45.10.1) (q:draft)
deihsakluatna = (t:n) (w:zeal/jealousy) (d:deihsak want for someone, luat exceedingly, with the noun suffix na; intense concern for someone) (e:cihtaklohna hangin ~ tawh a hong) (r:26.5.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
deihsakna = (t:n) (w:favor/goodwill/kindness) (d:deihsak, wish someone well, with the noun suffix na: favor or goodwill shown to someone) (e:dal bangin ~ tawh na dal hi/nong ~ tawh mual kip bangin kei nong phut | by your favor you set me firm like a mountain/ama ~ in khang tawntung ading ahi hi | his favor is for a lifetime/i hoih nading hong ~ hi a | it is his goodwill for our good) (s:maipha) (b:deihsak) (r:19.5.12/19.30.5/19.30.7/20.27.6) (q:draft)
deihsaknate = (t:n) (w:wishes/will) (d:deihsak want for someone, with the noun suffix na and the plural te; the things one wishes for another) (e:nadingin a ~ thei nuam lo) (s:deihsakte) (b:deihsakna) (r:18.21.14) (q:draft)
deihsakte = (t:n) (w:wishes/will) (d:deihsak want for someone, with the plural te; the things one wishes for another) (e:ding a ~ thei nuam lo) (s:deihsaknate) (b:deihsak) (r:18.21.14) (q:draft)
deihsakzaw = (t:v) (w:would rather/wish more) (d:deihsak, want something for someone, with the comparative zaw: wish one thing for them more than another) (e:uh ka hong ~ hi) (b:deihsak) (r:46.14.5) (q:draft)
deihtakin = (t:adv) (w:earnestly/eagerly/with care) (d:deih want with takin, which makes an adverb: with real desire, earnestly, or out of care for someone) (e:kiangah ~ thu ka ngen hi/~ pangbetna in mihoih suaksak thei hi | discipline given with care can make a person good) (b:deih) (r:27.9.3/20.22.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
deihte = (t:n) (w:those who want/those who love/those who desire) (d:deih with the plural te; after a possessive, the ones someone wants or chooses) (e:Pilna a ~ in kithuhilh ding ut a/Nangma thu a ~ in lungnopna lianpi ngah uh | those who love your law have great peace/Keima siat nading a ~ nungkiksak in la | turn back those who desire my ruin/dam nading a ~ a damsak hi | he healed those who wanted healing) (b:deih) (r:20.12.1/43.5.21/19.119.165/19.70.2/42.9.11) (q:draft)
deihteng = (t:n) (w:all that one wants/whatever one wishes) (d:deih want with teng all; mi a deihteng is all the people he wanted) (e:miliante in amau’ ~ pulak uh a/mi a ~ ama kiangah a sam hi | he called to him all those he wanted/a ~ bek uh hong guksak ding | they would steal only as much as they wanted/Pasian’ ~ sep ding a hanciamte | those who strive to do all that God wants) (b:deih) (r:33.7.3/41.3.13/31.1.5/40.5.6) (q:draft)
deihthuah = (t:v) (w:want more/want in addition) (d:deih want with thuah in addition: desire still more on top of what one has) (e:huaihamin gam a ~ manun/Na dangdang ~ ngitngetna sangin | than always wanting more and other things) (r:30.1.13/21.6.9) (q:draft)
deihzaw = (t:v) (w:prefer/would rather/like more) (d:deih, want, with comparative zaw; the thing it is compared with takes sangin, than) (e:thuman genna sangin zuauna na ~ hi/biakpiakna sangin, thuman thutang ~ hi | he prefers what is right and just to sacrifice/Ngun sangin kong thuhilhnate ~ un la | prefer my instruction to silver/nangma thupiakna ke’n ka ~ hi | I love your commands more) (s:utzaw/nuamzaw/teelzaw) (b:deih) (r:19.52.3/20.21.3/20.8.10/19.119.127) (q:draft)
deihzawkna = (t:n) (w:preference/preferring) (d:deihzaw prefer, in the form deihzawk, with the noun suffix na: liking one more than another) (e:keimah sangin milim a ~ uh hangin/~ hangin a it nu’ tapa pen | out of preference, the son of the wife he loves) (r:26.6.9/5.21.16) (q:draft)
deina = (t:n) (w:partition/division/separation) (d:what divides one space from another; deina puan is the dividing curtain of the temple and deina kulh a separating wall) (e:Tua laitakin biakinn sung ~ puan/tua ~ kulh pen | that dividing wall) (s:khenna) (b:dei) (r:40.27.51/26.42.20) (q:draft)
deipi = (t:n) (w:main hall/main room) (d:dei room with pi great; biakinn deipi is the main hall of the temple) (e:Biakinn ~ kongkhak khuamte/hih biakinn ~ sung lutna-a kongkhakte tungah | on the doors leading into this main hall of the temple) (s:inndeipi) (b:dei) (r:26.41.21/26.41.25) (q:draft)
deisung = (t:n) (w:bedroom/inner room) (d:the inner room where the bed is; a lupna deisung is his bedroom) (e:a lupna ~ a lupna tungah) (r:10.4.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
deite = (t:n) (w:rooms/chambers) (d:plural of dei: the rooms or chambers of a building) (e:teembaw sungah a ~ bawl in/biakinn ~ sungah a teengte ahi uh hi | they lived in the rooms of the temple/biakinn tualte le biakinn ~ kemin | in charge of the temple courts and rooms/amaute in a ~ bawl uh hi | they made the rooms) (s:inndeite) (b:dei) (r:1.6.14/13.9.33/13.23.28/14.31.11)
dek = (t:part) (w:almost/nearly/about to) (d:placed after a verb to show that the action is about to happen or nearly happens: si dek, about to die; hi dek lo is far from it, not at all) (e:tua a tanu si ~ tak hi/si ~ takin a gim mahmah hi | he was so ill that he almost died/Tua ni sagih a cin’ ~ tak ciangin | when the seven days were nearly over/khua a mial ~ zo hi | it is almost dark/cina-in a si ~ tak hi | he was sick and about to die) (r:42.8.42/41.14.34/50.2.27/44.21.27/42.24.29/42.7.2) (q:draft)
Dekapolis = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Decapolis) (d:region of ten Greek cities, most of them east of the Jordan and the Sea of Galilee) (r:41.7.31/40.4.25)
dekdak = (t:adv) (w:very) (d:placed after khum, sweet, to strengthen it: very sweet, as sweet as honey) (e:khuaizu bangin khum ~ a) (r:66.10.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
dekdek = (t:adv) (w:almost/nearly/about to) (d:placed after a verb, the action is on the point of happening or has just barely happened) (e:teembaw a kisia ~ hi/a khuapite maimang ~ hi | her cities are close to perishing/siatna lianpi khat i tungsak ~ hi | we are about to bring a great disaster/tuihualte in gunkuang tum ~ a | the waves nearly swamped the boat) (s:dektak) (r:32.1.4/24.14.2/24.26.19/40.8.24) (q:draft)
dekdekte = (t:n) (w:those about to/those on the point of) (d:dekdek almost, about to, with the plural te: a si dekdekte is those who are about to die, the perishing) (e:A si ~, khamtheihzu pia) (b:dekdek) (r:20.31.6) (q:draft)
deklo = (t:todo) (q:draft, the function of dek with lo in phunphun huai pah deklo hi is not clear from the single verse)
dekna = (t:n) (w:being about to/being on the point of) (d:dek almost, about to, with the noun suffix na: ka sih dekna is my being close to dying, faint with love in the English) (e:lungzuangin ka sih ~ na gensak un) (b:dek) (r:22.5.8) (q:draft)
dektak = (t:adv) (w:almost/nearly/about to) (d:follows the verb or quantity; si dektak is at the point of death) (e:ka khe taal ~ hi/Zan a bei ~ hi, sun hong nai zo hi | the night is nearly over, the day is near/khuazang ~ a kikhawm uh hi | almost the whole city gathered/nai nih sung ~ aw kikhatin a kiko uh hi | they shouted with one voice for about two hours/En in, ni tum ~ hi | look, the sun is about to set) (s:dekdek) (r:19.73.2/14.32.24/45.13.12/44.13.44/44.19.34/7.19.9) (q:draft)
dektaka = (t:adv) (w:almost/nearly) (d:dektak almost, with the linking suffix a before a noun phrase) (e:si ~ sukkhakna liamma a nei) (b:dektak) (r:66.13.3) (q:draft)
dektakin = (t:adv) (w:almost/nearly) (d:dektak almost, with the adverb suffix in; let dektakin, nearly overflowing, to the brim) (e:Tuate in let ~ a dimsak) (b:dektak) (r:43.2.8) (q:draft)
dektakna = (t:n) (w:being almost/nearness) (d:dektak almost, with the noun suffix na; sih dektakna, being close to death) (e:sih ~ tamvei ka tuakzaw hi) (b:dektak) (r:47.11.23) (q:draft)
dektaksa = (t:see) <dektaksa-in>
dektaksa-in = (t:adv) (w:almost/nearly) (d:dektak almost, with sa already and the adverb suffix in; a si dektaksa-in, left nearly dead) (e:a si ~ a paisan uh) (r:42.10.30) (q:draft)
dektakta = (t:adv) (w:almost now/about to) (d:dektak almost, with ta marking a change now under way) (e:Ni tum ~ a) (b:dektak) (r:24.6.4) (q:draft)
Delaiah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Delaiah) (d:name of several men, among them a priest in the time of David and an official of King Jehoiakim who urged him not to burn Jeremiah’s scroll) (r:13.3.24/13.24.18)
deldel = (t:adv) (w:tremblingly) (d:placed after ling, tremble, to picture the shaking: ling deldel is to shudder) (e:umin lau-in ling ~ uh hi) (r:59.2.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
delh = (t:v) (w:pursue/chase/go after) (d:run after someone in order to catch or drive them off; also strive after a goal such as peace) (e:Jordan lamah ngahmun dong ~ uh hi/Abimelek in amah ~ a, a mai-ah amah tai hi | Abimelek chased him, and he fled before him/Asahel in Abner ~ a | Asahel chased Abner/nopna zong in la, ~ in | seek peace and pursue it/a galte un ~ ding uh hi | their enemies will pursue them) (s:nungdelh/nawhdelh) (r:6.2.7/25.3.66/7.9.40/10.2.19/19.34.14/28.8.3) (q:draft)
delhin = (t:v) (w:pursuing/chasing) (d:form of delh with the linking ending in, used before a following verb) (e:ka galte ~ ka susia a/amaute in ~ man uh a | they chased him and caught him/Ka galte ~ ka pha a | I pursued my enemies and overtook them/Benjamin mite ~ tuancilin vatgawp uh hi | they chased the Benjamites, trampled them and struck them down) (b:delh) (r:10.22.38/7.1.6/19.18.37/7.20.43) (q:draft)
delhkek = (t:v) (w:pursue/chase down) (d:delh pursue with kek, whose force is not clear from the verse) (e:Amaute ~ inla) (r:25.3.66) (q:draft, low confidence)
delhkhia = (t:v) (w:drive out/chase away/drag away) (d:delh pursue with khia out: chase someone out of a place or off a path) (e:lam pamah hong ~ a) (s:hawlkhia) (b:delh) (r:25.3.11) (q:draft)
delhlup = (t:v) (w:fall on and crush/bury under) (d:press down on and cover, said of a tower falling on people; delh here means press down, as in delhphah) (e:a ~ mi sawm leh giatte) (s:denlup) (r:42.13.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
delhmang = (t:v) (w:chase away/drive off/frighten away) (d:delh chase with mang away: chase something until it is gone) (e:tuate a ~ ding kuamah om lo/humpi in a ~ tuu tawh a kibang uh | they are like sheep that a lion has chased away/a hong paito humpi in a ~ bangin | as a lion coming up chases them away) (s:taimangsak) (r:24.7.33/24.50.17/24.49.19) (q:draft)
delhna = (t:n) (w:pursuit/pursuing/chasing) (d:delh pursue with the noun suffix na: the act of chasing after someone; a delhna panin means from pursuing) (e:Abner a ~ panin Joab ciahkik hi/David a ~ panin Saul kileh kik a | Saul turned back from pursuing David/Filistiate a ~ panun Israelte hong ciahkik uh a | the Israelites came back from chasing the Philistines) (b:delh) (r:10.2.30/19.35.6/9.23.28/9.17.53) (q:draft)
delhphah = (t:n) (w:bed/bedding) (d:what is spread under a person to lie on) (e:thante pen nangma ~ hi a/~ puan khat la-in | he took a bed cloth) (s:lupphah) (r:23.14.11/12.8.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
delhphah = (t:v) (w:lie on/overlay) (d:lie on top of someone; delhphah kha is lie on him by accident) (e:Amah in ~ kha ahih manin) (r:11.3.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
delhphahin = (t:v) (w:lying on) (d:delhphah with the linking suffix in, with one side of the body pressed down, said of lying on the left or right side) (e:na veilam pang ~ lum in/na taklam ~ na kihei leuleu ding a | you shall turn over again and lie on your right side/Na veilam ~ na lup hun | the time that you lie on your left side) (b:delhphah) (r:26.4.4/26.4.6/26.4.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
delhphahkha = (t:v) (w:lie on/overlay) (d:press down on by lying over, with kha showing it happened by accident) (e:Amah in ~ ahih manin) (r:11.3.19) (q:draft)
delhphahpuan = (t:n) (w:thick cloth/blanket) (d:a thick cloth of the kind spread on a bed) (e:~ khat la-in tui sungah) (r:12.8.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
delhsak = (t:v) (w:cause to pursue/send after) (d:delh pursue with the causative sak: make something go after someone, as a sword sent after those who flee) (e:namsau ka nung ~ ding hi) (b:delh) (r:26.12.14) (q:draft)
delhsuk = (t:v) (w:chase down/pursue downward) (d:delh pursue with suk downward) (e:mualtung panin hong ~ uh a) (b:delh) (r:25.4.19) (q:draft)
delhte = (t:n) (w:pursuers/those who pursue) (d:delh pursue with te, the ones who pursue) (e:a ~ a paikhiat phetin/a ~ a ciahkik mateng nithum sung | for three days, until the pursuers returned/kei hong ~ khempeuh kiang panin | from all who pursue me/amau a ~ na lawn hi | you hurled their pursuers) (b:delh) (r:6.2.7/19.7.1/6.2.22/16.9.11) (q:draft)
Delilah = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Delilah) (d:woman of the Valley of Sorek whom Samson loved and who betrayed him to the Philistines) (r:7.16.4/7.16.10)
dem = (t:v) (w:contend with/defy/challenge) (d:set oneself against someone as a rival or opponent; in many verses, against God) (e:nang in Vanglian Pasian na ~ hi/nang hong ~ mite ke’n ka ~ ding a | I will contend with those who contend with you/a minthang ama omna ~ uh ahih manin | because they defy his glorious presence/Vanglianpa a ~ mipa in hih bang thute thuak hi | the man who defies the Almighty suffers such things) (s:langpang) (r:18.40.2/18.15.25/23.49.25/23.3.8) (q:draft)
Demas = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Demas) (d:fellow worker of Paul who later deserted him and went to Thessalonica) (r:55.4.10/51.4.14) (q:draft)
Demetrias = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Demetrius) (d:name of two men: a silversmith of Ephesus who stirred up a riot against Paul, and a believer commended in 3 John) (r:44.19.24/44.19.38)
demin = (t:v) (w:opposing/defying/contending/striving) (d:dem, contend with or rival, with the linking ending in) (e:amaute in kei hong ~/kei hong ~, keima thu na ngaih kei lai uhleh | if you remain hostile to me and still do not listen to me/Topa ~ a kiliansak uh hi | defying the Lord, they exalted themselves/semin, ~ ka om hi | I work and strive) (b:dem) (r:26.20.8/51.1.29/3.26.21/24.48.42) (q:draft)
demlai = (t:v) (w:still oppose/continue to defy) (d:dem contend with, defy, with lai still: keep on being hostile) (e:kei na hong ~ uhleh) (r:3.26.23/3.26.27) (q:draft)
demna = (t:n) (w:hostility/opposition/rivalry) (d:dem contend with, defy, with the noun suffix na) (e:kei hong ~ uh hangin/kei hong ~-in Khrih thu a hilh uh hi | they preach Christ out of rivalry against me) (s:langpanna/kidemna) (b:dem) (r:3.26.40/50.1.17) (q:draft)
demnopna = (t:n) (w:defiance/obstinacy/rebelliousness) (d:dem defy with nop want to and the noun suffix na: the wish to oppose; demnopna lungsim is a defiant, obstinate heart) (e:~ lungsim nei uh hi/amaute in ~ lungsim nei-in nang hong lehdo uh hi | with defiant hearts they rebelled against you) (r:26.3.7/16.9.26) (q:draft)
demte = (t:n) (w:opponents/foes/those who defy) (d:dem contend with, defy, with the plural te: those who set themselves against someone) (e:amah a ~ koihkhong lo a) (s:langpangte/galte) (b:dem) (r:34.1.2) (q:draft)
demzawh = (t:v) (w:be able to compete with) (d:dem compete with zawh, a form of zo be able) (e:sakol bangci ~ ding na hiam) (r:24.12.5) (q:draft)
demzo = (t:v) (w:be able to stand against/be able to compete with) (d:dem contend with, with zo be able; demzo nawn lo is no longer able to stand against someone) (e:Moses ~ nawn lo uh hi) (b:dem) (r:2.9.11) (q:draft)
den = (t:adv) (w:always/continually/constantly) (d:placed after a verb: keep on doing, or remain so without change) (e:ama ompihna zong ~ un/ni sawmli sung om ~ hi | it remained for forty days/keimah hong kem ~ ding hisak in | may they always protect me/Tua bangin om ~ hi | so it always was/mei kikuangsak ~ ding hi | the fire shall be kept burning continually) (s:niloh/ngitnget/gige) (r:13.16.11/19.7.11/1.7.17/19.40.11/4.9.16/3.6.12) (q:draft)
den = (t:v) (w:throw down/hurl/stone) (d:form of deng written with a final apostrophe before ding, na and nading: hurl a thing to the ground or strike with stones) (e:suang tawh amah ~’ ding gen uh hi | they spoke of stoning him/migilote leilak ~’na hi | he casts the wicked to the ground/leilak kong ~’ nading a | I will throw you on the open field/keimah leilak ~’ nadingin hong en uh hi | they watch to throw me to the ground) (s:deng/deeng) (r:19.147.6/9.30.6/26.32.4/19.17.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
denarias = (t:n) (w:denarius) (d:a Roman silver coin; denarias peek khat is one denarius) (e:~ peek khat hong paipih uh hi/~ peek khat ka et dingin hong paipih un | bring me a denarius to look at/~ peek khat hong lak un | show me a denarius) (r:40.22.19/41.12.15/42.20.24) (q:draft)
deng = (t:v) (w:stone/pelt/throw at) (d:throw something at; suang tawh deng is to stone) (e:suang tawh amah ~ ding uh hi/khatvei suang tawh hong ~ uh hi | once they pelted me with stones/Paul suang tawh a ~ uh a | they stoned Paul/mawhna a nei het lo pa in ~ masa un | let the one who has no sin throw first/nasemte khempeuh suang tawh ~ hi | he pelted all the officials with stones) (s:deeng/den) (r:4.15.35/10.16.6/47.11.25/44.14.19/43.8.7) (q:draft)
dengawp = (t:v) (w:stone/pelt) (d:den throw at with gawp showing violent or thorough action) (e:suang tawh amaute a ~ khak ding) (s:denggawp) (b:den) (r:44.5.26) (q:draft)
dengawpna = (t:n) (w:throwing down/dashing down) (d:dengawp throw violently, with the noun suffix na; with ding, will throw down forcefully) (e:amah in leilak ~ ding hi) (b:dengawp) (r:23.28.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
dengcip = (t:v) (w:fall on/bury/crush under) (d:deng, strike or fall on, with cip, tightly: fall on something and cover it completely, as people call on the hills to fall on them) (e:Hong ~ un) (s:cipnelh) (b:deng) (r:28.10.8) (q:draft)
denggawp = (t:v) (w:beat down/batter/stone/pelt) (d:deng, strike or throw at, with gawp, severely: batter a person with stones or, of hail, beat down plants and animals) (e:khat suang tawh na ~ uh hi/suang tawh Paul ~ uh a | they stoned Paul/Gialpi in gamlak kung khempeuh ~ a | the hail beat down every plant of the field/a leengguite uh gial tawh ~ a | he battered their vines with hail) (s:satgawp) (b:deng) (r:40.21.35/19.78.47/44.14.19/2.9.25) (q:draft)
dengin = (t:v) (w:stoning/throwing at/pelting) (d:deng, throw something at, with the linking ending in: throwing at someone and going on to a further action; suang tawh dengin is stoning) (e:suang tawh amaute ~ namsau tawh/suangte tawh amah ~ leivui a theh | throwing stones at him and scattering dust/mihonte in suang tawh nang hong ~ | the mob will stone you) (b:deng) (r:26.23.47/10.16.13/26.16.40) (q:draft)
dengkha = (t:v) (w:hit/strike) (d:deng, throw at, with kha, which shows that the action reaches its mark: hit someone with something thrown or rolled) (e:mi a ~ dingin suang a khukte) (r:20.26.27) (q:draft)
dengkham = (t:v) (w:crack/break open) (d:deng, strike, with kham, broken: strike a thing so that it cracks, as a millstone dropped on a skull) (e:a lu guh ~ hi) (r:7.9.53) (q:draft)
dengkhia = (t:v) (w:sweep away/beat down/knock away) (d:deng, pelt or strike, with khia, out or away: said of hail that beats on a shelter and carries it off) (e:na zuau buk uh ~ ding a) (b:deng) (r:23.28.17) (q:draft)
