dengzan = (t:v) (w:dash to pieces/smash/crush) (d:deng, throw or strike, with zan, broken in pieces: smash a thing to pieces by throwing it down or by falling on it) (e:leilakah amaute na ~ ding hi/amaute lei-ah na ~ ding hi | you will dash them to the ground/suang a kiat leh zong ~ gawp ding hi | if the stone falls on him it will crush him) (s:satnen/dengvuigawp) (r:19.2.9/40.21.44) (q:draft)
dengzanin = (t:v) (w:smashing/dashing to pieces) (d:dengzan dash to pieces, with the linking suffix in: smash and go on to the next action) (e:a biakna songte uh ~/Amaute’ biakna taute phelkhia-in, a biakna songte ~ | breaking down their altars and smashing their sacred stones) (s:satnenin/dengtanin) (b:dengzan) (r:5.7.5/5.12.3) (q:draft)
denin = (t:adv) (w:continually/steadily/fixedly) (d:den, always, with the ending in, placed after a verb: keep on doing it without a break; en denin is look with a fixed gaze) (e:a etna mun mah en ~/a tawntungin kei hong hehsak ~ | continually provoking me) (s:gige) (b:den) (r:12.8.11/23.65.3) (q:draft)
