don = (t:v) (w:pay attention/heed/regard/care for) (d:give attention or care to a person or a word; don lo is ignore or disregard) (e:ka thugente ~ in la/zuauthute a ~ loh nadingin | so that they pay no attention to lies/A pil peuhmah in hih thute ~ hen la | let whoever is wise heed these things/a thupiaknate khempeuh ~ nawn lo uh hi | they no longer heeded any of his commands/patau kohna za napi-in ~ lo ahih manin | because he heard the alarm but did not heed it) (s:thudon/ngai/awlmawh) (r:20.4.20/18.34.27/2.5.9/19.107.43/26.33.5) (q:draft)
dona = (t:n) (w:fighting/war/warfare/attack) (d:the act of fighting against someone, often as gal dona, warfare; do, fight, with the noun suffix na) (e:gal ~ a theihtheih nading/gal ~ bangci mavan’ hiam cih dong hi | he asked how the war was going/Ammon mite a ~ panin Joab ciah-in | Joab returned from fighting the Ammonites/gal ~-ah nasem dingin a baihsa-in a om | ready to serve in war) (s:galdona/kidona/simna/galkidona) (a:kilemna) (b:do) (r:7.3.2/10.11.7/10.10.14/13.7.11) (q:draft)
dong = (t:prep) (w:until/till/as far as) (d:marks the limit reached in time or place, placed after the word or clause it limits; often follows ciang) (e:zingsang khuavak ~ mi khat in/kum sawmthum-le-nga ciang ~ gal kidona om nawn lo | there was no more war until the thirty-fifth year/a nitak ~ a nin hi ding hi | he will be unclean until evening/Babilon kumpi a suah ~ kumpi innah Daniel a om | Daniel stayed at the palace until he became king of Babylon) (s:ciang/tan) (a:kipan) (r:1.32.24/14.15.19/3.14.46/27.1.21) (q:draft)
dong = (t:v) (w:ask/inquire/question) (d:put a question to someone or seek advice; the form dot is used in dependent clauses) (e:ci-in a ~ hi/ci-in amah ka ~ hi | I asked her, saying/A numei sam-in amah i ~ ding hi | let us call the girl and ask her/siampite’ ngaihsutna ~ in | ask the priests for their opinion/na pa ~ in, hong lak ding hi | ask your father and he will tell you) (s:thudong/kan) (a:dawng) (r:42.15.26/1.24.47/1.24.57/37.2.11/5.32.7) (q:draft)
donga = (t:prep) (w:until/up to/to) (d:dong, until, with a, joining the phrase to what follows; tu ni donga a om is which is there to this day) (e:tu ni ~ a om suang honpi/Johan hun ~ a piang ding thute a genkhol hi | they foretold what would happen up to the time of John/na pu na pate in tu ni ~ a kholte | what your fathers have stored up to this day/amah in tu ~ Ammon mite’ pian’na pupi ahi hi | he is the ancestor of the Ammonites to this day) (b:dong) (r:6.7.26/1.19.38/40.11.13/12.20.17) (q:draft)
dongah = (t:prep) (w:as far as/up to/until) (d:dong with the locative suffix ah, marking the limit reached; often after ciang) (e:Bashan gam Salekah ~ Reubente’ gal khatah/khuapi sunga kahna in vantung ~ kiza to hi | the crying in the city was heard up to heaven/kulh kongpi lutna ~ mi tampi liamin tuk hi | many fell wounded all the way to the entrance of the gate/nisuahna lam manawhin Tui Kongpi ~ pai uh hi | they went on eastward as far as the Water Gate) (b:dong) (r:13.5.11/1.13.12/9.5.12/7.9.40/16.12.37) (q:draft)
dongin = (t:prep) (w:until/till/up to) (d:dong, until, with the linking suffix in: up to a point in time, a place or an amount) (e:a sih ni ~ ta nei lo hi/Pentekost pawikham ni ~ Efesa khua ah ka om | I will stay in Ephesus until the day of Pentecost/zingsang a kipan nitak ~ | from morning till evening/ka gam langkhat ~ kong pia ding hi | I will give you up to half my kingdom/tua in tu ni ~ tua lai-a a om | it stands there to this day) (a:kipan) (b:dong) (r:10.6.23/46.16.8/2.18.13/41.6.23/1.35.20) (q:draft)
dongkhak = (t:v) (w:block/obstruct/silence) (d:stop or shut off: block a road, or stop the mouth of someone so that he has no answer) (e:Saddusite kam Zeisu in a ~/ka mite’ lampi a ~ thei ding na khempeuh | everything that could block the way of my people) (s:khaktan/khakcip) (r:40.22.34/23.57.14) (q:draft)
dongkhakin = (t:v) (w:silencing/blocking) (d:dongkhak, stop or silence, with the linking suffix in) (e:Saddusi mite’ thudotna Jesuh in ~) (b:dongkhak) (r:40.22.34) (q:draft)
dongkhin = (t:v) (w:have asked/be engaged to) (d:dong, ask, with khin, already; lawm dongkhin is having already asked for a woman in marriage) (e:Tenpih dingin lawm ~ napi-in) (b:dong) (r:46.7.36) (q:draft, low confidence)
dongkik = (t:v) (w:ask again/ask further/ask in return) (d:dong, ask, with kik, again or back) (e:ci-in a ~ uh hi/amaute in Topa kiangah ~ uh a | they inquired further of the Lord/David in Topa thu ~ hi | David inquired of the Lord again/ci-in a ~ leuleu hi | he asked him yet again/hih thu tawh kisai Jesuh kiangah a ~ uh hi | they asked Jesus again about this matter) (a:dawngkik) (b:dong) (r:43.1.25/9.10.22/9.23.4/41.14.61/41.10.10) (q:draft)
