dung = (t:n) (w:length) (d:the long side of a thing or its measure from end to end, paired with vai for the width) (e:a ~ khap khat, a vai khap khat/gam ~ gam vai kan tanin pai in | walk through the length and breadth of the land/A inn ~ tong sawmkua hi a | the building was ninety cubits long/Tua puan a ~ tong sawmnih-le-giat | the curtain was twenty-eight cubits long) (s:dunglam/sauna) (a:vai/vailam) (r:2.28.16/1.13.17/26.41.12/2.36.9) (q:draft)
dunga = (t:prep) (w:along/on the shore of) (d:dung, length, with a: along the length of something; tuipi dunga is along the sea, on the coast) (e:Tuipi ~ a teeng mite in/San Tuipi gei ~ om Eloth nai-a | near Elath on the shore of the Red Sea/tuipi ~ teeng mite lau-in patausak ding hi | it will make those who live along the sea tremble with fear/tuipi ~ a om mite tawh | with the peoples who live along the sea) (s:dungah) (b:dung) (r:23.24.15/11.9.26/26.26.15/26.27.3) (q:draft)
dungah = (t:prep) (w:along/alongside) (d:dung, length, with the place marker ah: along the length of a river, a shore or a border) (e:tuipi gei leh Jordan ~ teeng uh hi/Arnon gun ~, Moab gam kisiatna thu va gen un | announce along the Arnon river that Moab is destroyed/Johan in Jordan gun ~ vak kawikawi a | John went about along the Jordan river/gamgi in Enshemesh tuite ~ pai-in Enrogel-ah tawp hi | the boundary ran along the waters of En Shemesh and ended at En Rogel) (s:dunga) (b:dung) (r:4.13.29/24.48.20/42.3.3/6.15.7) (q:draft)
dunglam = (t:n) (w:length/long side) (d:dung, length, with lam, side or direction: the measure or the side along the length of a thing) (e:A ~ pen gambup nisuahna gamgi panin/Puanbuk puan a ~ | the length of the tent curtain) (s:dung/saulam) (a:vailam/zailam) (r:26.48.8/2.26.13) (q:draft)
dungteng = (t:n) (w:whole length/all along) (d:dung, length, with teng, all: the full stretch along something, such as the whole coast of the sea) (e:Tuipi Lian ~ ahi hi/Tuipi Lian le a gei ~ na nei ding uh hi | you shall have the Great Sea and its whole shore) (b:dung) (r:6.15.12/4.34.6) (q:draft)
dup = (t:adj) (w:dark/blackened/livid) (d:of the face, turned dark; dup is also part of colour words such as dupsan purple) (e:a mai uh ~ khin a) (r:25.4.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
dupsan = (t:adj) (w:purple) (d:the colour purple, said of cloth and yarn and listed with a dum, blue, and a ausan, scarlet) (e:a tungah puan a ~ khat phah ding/a dum, a ~, a ausan khaute | blue, purple and scarlet yarn/a dum leh a ausan leh a ~ puante | blue, scarlet and purple cloth) (s:sandup) (r:4.4.13/2.35.6/14.3.14) (q:draft)
dupsante = (t:adj) (w:purple) (d:dupsan purple with the plural te, which belongs to the whole phrase: puan dupsante is purple garments) (e:khainiangte leh puan ~) (b:dupsan) (r:7.8.26) (q:draft)
Dura = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Dura) (d:plain in the province of Babylon where Nebuchadnezzar set up the gold image) (r:27.3.1)
e = (t:intj) (d:exclamation placed after a word of address, as in Nu e, oh mother, a cry of dismay where the English has how awful) (e:Nu ~! Tua ni lianpi hong tung) (r:24.30.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
eb = (t:see) <Ze-eb>
Ebal = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ebal) (d:son of Shobal, a descendant of Seir the Horite; also the mountain near Shechem where the curses were read) (r:1.36.23)
Ebar = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Eber) (d:son of Shelah and father of Peleg in the genealogy of Jesus in Luke, elsewhere written Eber) (e:Peleg in ~’ ta hi) (r:42.3.35) (q:draft)
Ebed = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ebed) (d:name of two men: the father of Gaal, who rose against Abimelek, and a man who returned from Babylon with Ezra) (e:Zebul in ~ tapa Ga-al’ kammalte) (r:7.9.30/15.8.6) (q:draft)
Ebedmelek = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ebed-Melek) (d:Cushite official in the palace of King Zedekiah who had Jeremiah lifted out of the cistern) (r:24.38.12/24.38.8)
Ebenezer = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Ebenezer) (d:place where Israel camped before the Philistines captured the ark; also the stone Samuel set up to mark the help of the Lord) (r:9.5.1/9.7.12)
Eber = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Eber) (d:son of Shelah and father of Peleg, an ancestor of Abraham; also the name of several other men) (r:13.1.18/13.1.25)
Ebes = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Ebez) (d:town in the territory of Issachar) (r:6.19.20) (q:draft)
Ebez = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Ebez) (d:town in the territory of Issachar) (r:6.19.20)
Ebiasaf = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ebiasaph) (d:Levite of the family of Korah, ancestor of temple singers and gatekeepers) (r:13.6.23/13.6.37)
Ebron = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Ebron/Abdon) (d:town on the border of the territory of Asher, where the NIV reads Abdon) (e:~, Rehob, Hammon, Kanah) (r:6.19.28) (q:draft)
Ebronah = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Abronah) (d:place where the Israelites camped in the wilderness, between Jotbathah and Ezion Geber) (r:4.33.34/4.33.35)
eden = (t:see) <Beth-eden>
Eden = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Eden) (d:the land in the east where God planted the garden for the first man and woman) (e:~ huan) (r:1.2.15/1.2.8)
Eder = (t:name) (c:tower) (w:Eder) (d:Migdal Eder, the tower beyond which Jacob pitched his tent after Rachel died) (r:1.35.21)
Eder = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Eder) (d:town in the far south of Judah; also the name of a Benjamite and of a Levite, son of Mushi) (r:6.15.21)
Edom = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Edom) (d:another name of Esau, son of Isaac; also the land and the people descended from him, south of the Dead Sea) (r:1.36.1)
Edomte = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Edom/Edomites) (d:the people of Edom, descendants of Esau) (b:Edom) (r:4.24.18)
Edor = (t:see) <Edor-ah>
Edor-ah = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Endor) (d:Endor, the town where Saul consulted a medium, written here with the place marker ah, at Endor) (e:~ vankah thei khat om hi) (r:9.28.7) (q:draft)
Edrei = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Edrei) (d:city of Og king of Bashan, where Israel defeated him; also a town in the territory of Naphtali) (r:4.21.33/6.19.37)
ee = (t:intj) (d:exclamation of astonishment or scorn uttered by passers-by at a ruin) (e:lamdang sa-in ~! ci ding uh hi) (s:eh) (r:11.9.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
eek = (t:n) (w:dung/rubbish) (d:apparently the same word as ek, dung, with a long vowel; here of things counted as worthless) (e:nadangte khempeuh ~ hi ci-in ka ngaihsun hi) (s:ek) (r:50.3.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
eeka = (t:n) (w:acre) (d:a measure of land, the English word acre; another spelling of eka) (e:leenggah lo ~ sawm in phelpi khat) (s:eka) (r:23.5.10) (q:draft)
eekkholna = (t:n) (w:manure pile/dunghill) (d:eek, dung, with khol, heap or store, and the noun suffix na) (e:~ ading ahi zongin apha kei hi) (s:ninkholna) (r:42.14.35) (q:draft)
een = (t:v) (w:envy/be jealous of) (d:feel ill will because of what another person has or is; written een’ before a following word, and een’na is envy) (e:amaute in Zeisu a ~’ man-unah/siampi liante in Zeisu a ~’ manun ah | because the chief priests envied Jesus/Amau sungah ~’na om nadingin | so that there would be envy in them/note in ~’na lungsim na neih nadingun | so that you would have an envious heart) (s:eng/hazat/haza) (r:40.27.18/45.11.14/41.15.10/45.11.11/45.10.19) (q:draft)
eengin = (t:v) (w:being jealous/envying) (d:eeng, a spelling of eng, envy, with the linking suffix in: being jealous, and so doing a further action) (e:Ahih hangin Judah mite in ~) (r:44.17.5) (q:draft)
Efah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ephah) (d:son of Midian, grandson of Abraham and Keturah; also the concubine of Caleb and a son of Jahdai) (r:1.25.4/13.2.47)
Efai = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ephai) (d:man of Netophah whose sons came to Gedaliah at Mizpah) (e:Netofah khua ~’ tate) (r:24.40.8) (q:draft)
Efer = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Epher) (d:son of Midian, grandson of Abraham and Keturah; also a family head in the half-tribe of Manasseh) (r:1.25.4)
Efesa = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Ephesus) (d:city in the Roman province of Asia where Paul worked and to whose church he wrote) (r:55.4.12/44.19.28)
Efesdammim = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Ephes Dammim) (d:place in Judah between Sokoh and Azekah where the Philistines camped before David fought Goliath) (r:9.17.1)
Effatha = (t:name) (w:Ephphatha) (d:Aramaic word spoken by Jesus to a deaf man, meaning be opened) (r:41.7.34)
Efifaz = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Eliphaz) (d:son of Esau and Adah, a spelling of Eliphaz) (r:1.36.4)
Eflal = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ephlal) (d:man of Judah, descendant of Jerahmeel, son of Zabad and father of Obed) (r:13.2.37)
Efod = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ephod) (d:father of Hanniel, the leader of the tribe of Manasseh at the dividing of the land) (r:4.34.23)
Efrah = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Ephrath) (d:older name of Bethlehem, on the road to which Rachel was buried) (r:1.48.7)
Efraim = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ephraim) (d:younger son of Joseph, ancestor of the tribe of Ephraim; also the tribe and its land) (r:1.41.52/1.46.20)
Efraimte = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Ephraim/Ephraimites) (d:the people of the tribe of Ephraim) (b:Efraim) (r:28.13.1/7.12.4)
Efrat = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Ephrath) (d:older name of Bethlehem, near which Rachel died; also written Efrath) (e:amaute ~ panin a gamla sim lai) (r:1.35.16/1.35.19) (q:draft)
Efrath = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Ephrath) (d:older name of Bethlehem, near which Rachel died; also the wife of Caleb and mother of Hur) (r:1.35.16/1.48.7)
Efrathah = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Ephrathah) (d:name of the district of Bethlehem in Judah, the home of the family of David) (r:33.5.2)
Efron = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ephron) (d:Hittite, son of Zohar, who sold Abraham the field and cave of Machpelah) (r:1.23.8/1.23.14)
Eglah = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Eglah) (d:wife of David and mother of Ithream) (r:10.3.5/13.3.3)
eglaim = (t:see) <En-eglaim>
Eglaim = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Eglaim) (d:town of Moab named in the lament of Isaiah over Moab) (r:23.15.8)
Eglath = (t:see) <Eglath-shelishiah>
Eglath-sheli-shiah = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Eglath Shelishiyah) (d:place in Moab named in the oracles against Moab) (e:Horonaim khua leh ~ khua dongah) (r:24.48.34) (q:draft)
Eglath-shelishiah = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Eglath Shelishiyah) (d:place in Moab named in the oracles against Moab) (r:23.15.5) (q:draft)
Eglathshelishiah = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Eglath Shelishiyah) (d:place in Moab named in the oracles against Moab) (r:24.48.34/23.15.5)
Eglon = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Eglon) (d:Canaanite city in the lowland of Judah taken by Joshua; also the king of Moab killed by Ehud) (r:6.15.39/6.10.3)
Egypt = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Egypt) (d:country on the Nile where the Israelites were slaves until the Lord brought them out; also written Izipt) (r:2.12.1)
Egypt = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Egypt) (d:son of Ham, ancestor of the Egyptians) (r:1.10.6)
eh = (t:intj) (d:exclamation of surprise or of correcting oneself, as between two numbers in the sayings of Proverbs 30: three, no, four; also a cry of people shocked at a ruin) (e:thum om a, ~! li hizaw/thu thum, ~! thu li om a | three things, no, four things/a thupi suak mahmah thum, ~! li om a | three that are very stately, no, four/lamdangsa-in, ~! ci ding uh hi | they will be appalled and say Eh) (s:ee) (r:20.30.18/46.1.16/20.30.21/20.30.29/11.9.8) (q:draft)
Ehi = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ehi) (d:son of Benjamin) (e:Naaman, ~, Rosh, Muppim) (r:1.46.21) (q:draft)
ehna = (t:n) (w:splitting/chopping) (d:eh, the form of ek split used before a suffix, with the noun suffix na: sing ehna is the splitting of logs) (e:sing ~ mahah liam ding hi) (r:21.10.9) (q:draft)
Ehud = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ehud) (d:judge of Israel, a left-handed man of Benjamin who killed Eglon king of Moab) (e:~ a sih khit ciangin Israel mite) (r:7.4.1/7.3.26) (q:draft)
ei = (t:pron) (w:we/us) (d:first person plural including the hearer, the short form of eite; before hong and tawh it is the object, us) (e:~ pai ding/Satan in ~ hong zawh khak ding | that Satan might get the better of us/Mi honte’ Topa in ~ tawh omkhawm a | the Lord of hosts is with us/~ pawl nihte in Kha Siangtho khat tawh | we, both groups, by one Spirit) (s:eite) (r:49.2.18/47.2.11/19.46.11)
Eijah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Elijah) (d:the prophet Elijah, as the name is spelled in Matthew 11:14) (r:40.11.14)
Eilishah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Elishah) (d:son of Javan, grandson of Japheth) (r:1.10.4)
eima = (t:pron) (w:ours) (d:what belongs to us, used with aa or a’, belonging to: eima aa hi is it is ours) (e:hih gamin ~ aa hi taktak hi | this land is truly ours/leitang pen ~ a’ hi lai hi | the land is still ours/ama luah ding gamh ~ a’ suak ding hi | his inheritance will become ours) (b:ei) (r:26.33.24/14.14.7/41.12.7)
eima = (t:det) (w:our/our own) (d:ei, we, with ma: belonging to us, placed before a noun; eima adingin is for ourselves) (e:i sanggampa, ~ ci-le-sa ahi hi/Jakob’ Pasian in ~ belh ahi hi | the God of Jacob is our refuge/Tui sung en leeng ~ maitang i muh bangin | as we see our own face when we look into water/~ luah ding amah in hong teelsak hi | he chose our inheritance for us) (b:ei) (r:1.37.27/20.27.19/19.46.7/19.47.4)
eimah = (t:det) (w:ours) (d:possessive use of the emphatic pronoun eimah: our own, belonging to us ourselves) (e:~ ki-ukzawhna hoihzaw hi | ruling our own selves is better) (b:ei) (r:20.16.32)
eimah = (t:pron) (w:our/ourselves/we ourselves) (d:emphatic first person plural pronoun that includes the hearer, ei with the emphatic mah: we ourselves, us; before a noun, our own) (e:amah in ~ huhpa leh i lum/ci leng ~ mah kikheem i hi a | if we say so, we deceive ourselves/lungkhamna ~ bek in i theih hi a | only we ourselves know the sorrow/~ hong suunin mihing bawl ni | let us make man to be like us) (s:eimau) (b:ei) (r:19.33.20/62.1.8/20.14.10/1.1.26)
EIMAH = (t:todo) (q:draft, part of KEIMAH printed as K EIMAH in Exodus 3.14, keimah I myself used for the divine name I AM, not a word by itself)
eimau = (t:pron) (w:ourselves/us/our own) (d:emphatic first person plural pronoun that includes the hearer: we ourselves, us, our own; eimau sungah means in us, and eimau san ciatah each to our own way) (e:amaute zong ~ sungah om-in/eite khempeuh ~ san ciatah i pai khin hi | we have all gone, each to our own way) (s:eite/eimah) (r:43.17.21/23.53.6) (q:draft)
eimaute = (t:pron) (w:we/us/ourselves) (d:eimau, the emphatic first person plural pronoun that includes the hearer, with the plural ending te; English has we, us or our according to its place in the sentence) (e:amaute leh ~ atuam atuam khen loin) (s:eite) (b:eimau) (r:44.15.9) (q:draft)
eite = (t:pron) (w:we/us/our) (d:first person plural including the hearer; whether English has we, us or our depends on its place in the sentence) (e:~ in Topa’ pum tung nate/~ ading | for us/~ i pai ding hi | we shall go/~ neihsa | ours/~ in amah i it hi | we love him/Horeb ah ~ tawh thuciamna khat bawl hi | he made a covenant with us at Horeb) (s:eimau) (b:ei) (r:49.5.30/58.10.15/62.4.19/5.5.2)
Eite = (t:pron) (w:we/us/our) (d:eite, the first person plural pronoun that includes the hearer, written with a capital at the start of a sentence or a quotation; English has we, us or our according to its place in the sentence) (e:~ mai-ah a lamdang hi/~ in Topa’ pum tung nate i hi hi | we are members of the body of the Lord/~ in i pumpi i teldot leh | if we examined ourselves/~ a hong piak thuciamna | the promise he gave us/~’ Pa leh Pasian tungah | to our God and Father) (b:eite) (r:41.12.11/45.9.29/49.5.30/46.11.31/62.2.25/50.4.20) (q:draft)
EITE = (t:pron) (w:our/we/us) (d:eite, the first person plural pronoun that includes the hearer, written in capitals within the name The Lord Our Righteousness) (e:Topa IN ~’ DIKTATNA AHI HI | The Lord is our righteousness) (r:24.23.6) (q:draft)
ejaakan = (t:see) <Ben-ejaakan>
ek = (t:n) (w:dung/excrement/waste) (d:the solid waste of a person or an animal; bawng ek is cow dung, and mihing ek human excrement) (e:Mihing’ ~ tangin bawng’ ~ na zang ding/kihei-in na ~ uh na vuk ding uh hi | turn and cover up your excrement/a vun, a sa leh a ~ | its hide, its flesh and its dung/amau’ ~ mah ne-in | eating their own excrement/Gamlaka kitha ~ bangin | like dung spread on the open field) (s:eklei) (r:26.4.15/26.4.12/5.23.13/3.8.17/12.18.27/24.9.22) (q:draft)
ek = (t:n) (w:dross/slag) (d:the waste that is separated from a metal when it is refined; sik-ek is the dross of iron) (e:Ngun a ~ teng paaikhia lehang/migilote khempeuh sik-~ bangin na ngaihsun hi | you regard all the wicked as dross) (s:saam-ek) (r:20.25.4/19.119.119) (q:draft)
eka = (t:n) (w:acre) (d:a measure of land, from the English word acre; also spelled eeka and ekah) (e:leenggah lo ~ sawm in phelpi khat/lo ~ khat dung zui-in | along the length of a one-acre field) (s:eeka/ekah) (r:23.5.10/9.14.14) (q:draft)
ekah = (t:n) (w:acre) (d:a measure of land, the English word acre; another spelling of eka) (e:lo ~ khat dung zui-in) (s:eeka) (b:eka) (r:9.14.14) (q:draft)
Ekanah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Elkanah) (d:name of several Levites of the line of Kohath, usually spelled Elkanah) (r:13.6.23/13.6.35)
Ekbatana = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Ecbatana) (d:capital city of Media, where the scroll with the decree of Cyrus was found) (r:15.6.2)
ekbuk = (t:n) (w:latrine/toilet) (d:a place used as a toilet; built from ek, dung, and buk, a hut or shelter) (e:tuni dongin ~ a suaksak uh hi) (r:12.10.27) (q:draft)
Eker = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Eker) (d:son of Ram and grandson of Jerahmeel, of the tribe of Judah) (e:Maaz, Jamin, leh ~ ahi uh hi) (r:13.2.27) (q:draft)
ekkeu = (t:n) (w:dried dung) (d:human or animal dung that has dried, gathered and burned as fuel; built from ek, dung, and keu, dry) (e:mihing ~ khawmin tuate mei-in) (r:26.4.12) (q:draft)
ekkhamin = (t:v) (w:chopping up/splitting) (d:chopping or splitting wood into pieces, as for a fire; built from ek, split, and kham, with the linking ending in, and also written as two words, ek khamin) (e:a leeng singte ~ a bawngpite/~ a bawngpite Topa’ tungah meihal biakna-in | chopping it up, they offered the cows to the Lord as a burnt offering) (r:9.6.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
eklei = (t:n) (w:dung/manure) (d:dung, also dung put on the soil to make it fertile; eklei sung is to put manure on, to fertilize) (e:kimkot to-in ~ ka sung ding hi/lei maitang tungah ~ tawh kibang ding hi | will be like dung on the surface of the ground/~ dingin zong kibawl thei lo | nor can it be made into manure) (s:ek) (r:42.13.8/12.9.37/42.14.35) (q:draft)
eknel = (t:n) (w:cud) (d:food that an animal brings back from its stomach to the mouth to chew again; eknel hai is to chew the cud) (e:Bilpi in ~ a hai hangin/a khecin a ka, ~ a hai peuhmah | any that has a split hoof and chews the cud/~ hai lo ahih ciangin | because it does not chew the cud/~ a hai lo ganhing peuhmah | every animal that does not chew the cud) (r:3.11.6/3.11.3/3.11.7/3.11.26) (q:draft)
Ekron = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Ekron) (d:one of the five chief cities of the Philistines, on the border of Judah and Dan) (r:6.15.45/6.19.43)
ekte = (t:n) (w:dung/offal/intestines) (d:ek, dung, with the plural ending te: the dung and waste parts of an animal that are burned outside the camp) (e:a vun leh a ~/a sa leh a ~ mei tawh kihal ding hi | its flesh and its dung shall be burned with fire/a ~ tawh na maitang uh hong zut gawpin | smearing your faces with their dung) (b:ek) (r:2.29.14/39.2.3/3.16.27) (q:draft)
ekte = (t:n) (w:splitters) (d:as the second part of sing-ekte, those who split wood: ek, split, with the plural ending -te) (e:sing-~, sing ehna mah-ah liam ding hi) (r:21.10.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
el = (t:v) (w:envy/be malicious toward/be hostile to) (d:bear ill will toward someone or act as a rival; mi a el teci is a malicious witness, and el pau is to speak with malice; most occurrences of these letters are not this word but the last part of Hebrew names such as Beth-el and Jezre-el) (e:Mi a ~ tecite hong kipan uh a/amah a ~ a zipih | the fellow wife who was her rival/mi thusim loin ~ pau uh a | they scoff and speak with malice) (s:een/eng/haza) (r:19.35.11/9.1.6/19.73.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
El = (t:see) <El-Elohe>
El-Elohe = (t:name) (w:El Elohe Israel) (d:first part of El-Elohe-Israel, the name Jacob gave to the altar he set up) (e:~-Israel ci-in min phuak hi) (r:1.33.20) (q:draft)
El-Elohe-Israel = (t:name) (c:land) (w:El Elohe Israel) (d:name that Jacob gave to the altar he set up near Shechem) (r:1.33.20)
El-paran = (t:name) (c:place) (w:El Paran) (d:place at the edge of the wilderness, the farthest point Kedorlaomer reached in the land of the Horites) (e:om ~ dong hong zo uh hi) (r:1.14.6) (q:draft)
Ela = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ela) (d:father of Shimei, one of the district governors of Solomon) (e:Benjamin gam sungah ~’ tapa Shimei) (r:11.4.18) (q:draft)
Ela = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Elam) (d:the land of King Kedorlaomer, written Ela in one text of Genesis 14:9 and Elam elsewhere) (r:1.14.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
Elah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Elah) (d:name of several men, among them a king of Israel, son of Baasha, and a son of Caleb) (e:ama tangin a tapa ~ in uk hi) (r:11.16.6/13.4.15) (q:draft)
Elah = (t:name) (c:valley) (w:Elah) (d:valley in Judah where Israel camped against the Philistines and David fought Goliath; Elah kuam is the Valley of Elah) (e:~ kuam-ah giahphual sat uh a) (r:9.17.2) (q:draft)
elaiah = (t:see) <Re-elaiah>
