ethuai = (t:see) <lam-ethuai>
etin = (t:v) (w:looking/gazing) (d:et, look, with the linking ending in; etin nei is keep looking at with desire; also the second part of hyphenated words such as ze-etin, testing) (e:leenggahzu san ~ nei kei in/Milimte ~ na nei nawn kei ding | you will no longer look with longing at the idols) (b:et) (r:20.23.31/26.23.27) (q:draft)
etkak = (t:v) (w:compare) (d:form of enkak, compare, used before ciangin and in dependent clauses) (e:numei dangte i ~ ciangin) (s:genteh/tehkak/tehpih/enteh) (r:26.16.51) (q:draft)
etkakna = (t:n) (w:standard/comparison/figure of speech) (d:etkak, compare, with the noun suffix na: something to compare with, a standard measure; etkakna lim-in is by way of comparison, figuratively) (e:a kizang ding ~ pen beem hi ding/~ lim-in ci leng | to speak by way of comparison) (b:etkak) (r:26.45.11/58.11.19) (q:draft)
etkawmin = (t:v) (w:while looking at) (d:et, form of en, look, with kawm, while, and the linking suffix in: looking at someone while doing something else) (e:a nungzuite a ~ Peter lehtai a) (r:41.8.33) (q:draft)
etkik = (t:see) <ki-etkik>
etlawm = (t:adj) (w:lovely/beautiful/fair) (d:pleasant to look at; et, look, with lawm, fitting) (e:Jerusalem khuapi bangin na ~ a/na teen’na mun bangzah takin ~ ahi hiam | how lovely is your dwelling place/Tumkung bangin na ~ a | you are lovely like a palm tree/a ~ a ngawng zangah kol bulhin | putting a yoke on her fair neck) (s:melhoih/meelhoih/ngaihhuai) (a:melsia) (r:22.6.4/19.84.1/22.7.7/28.10.11) (q:draft)
etlawmin = (t:adv) (w:beautifully/handsomely) (d:etlawm, lovely to look at, with the suffix in: in a way that is beautiful to see) (e:A khutte ~ hi linlian a) (b:etlawm) (r:22.5.14) (q:draft)
etlawmna = (t:n) (w:beauty/splendour/loveliness) (d:etlawm, beautiful, with the noun suffix na: the quality of being lovely to look at) (e:a ~ in kumpipa’ mit la vangvang hi/A ~ teng a maiman’ ciangin tau ding uh hi | they will wail when all its splendour is gone) (s:melhoihna/meelhoihna) (b:etlawm) (r:22.7.5/28.10.5) (q:draft)
etlawmsak = (t:v) (w:make beautiful/adorn/grace) (d:etlawm, lovely to look at, with the causative sak) (e:kizepna khi bangin hong ~ ding hi/Nang a hong ~ mite in amaute ahi uh hi | they were the ones who made you beautiful) (s:zep/zeem) (b:etlawm) (r:20.1.9/26.27.11) (q:draft)
etna = (t:n) (w:looking/watching/oversight) (d:et, look, with the noun suffix na: the act of looking at or looking out for something; etna sunga om is under the care of someone) (e:ka ~-in ka mitte a thazaw hi/Josef’ ~ sunga om peuhmah | whatever was under the care of Joseph) (b:et) (r:19.119.123/1.39.23) (q:draft)
etnate = (t:see) <ze-etnate>
etnopin = (t:v) (w:desire to look at/look at with desire) (d:et, form of en, look, with nop, want to, and the linking suffix in; etnopin nei is keep wanting to look at) (e:Numei bekbek ~ nei uh a) (r:61.2.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
etphat = (t:v) (w:check/inspect/look over) (d:look over a group carefully to see who is there; et, the form of en, look, used before a suffix, with phat) (e:siampite ka ~ ciangin Levi mite) (s:vel) (r:15.8.15) (q:draft)
etsa = (t:see) <kize-etsa>
etsak = (t:v) (w:look at/look upon/pay attention to) (d:et, look, with sak: turn the eyes to someone or something, often as a favour to the one who asks) (e:ka tapa nong ~ nadingin kong thum hi/kote a hong hu ding pa hong ~ inla | look on the one who shields us/mit sunga ninthem tang ~ na hi hiam | do you look at the speck in the eye) (b:et) (r:42.9.38/19.84.9/42.6.41) (q:draft, low confidence)
etsat = (t:v) (w:loathe/detest/despise) (d:look on with disgust, turn away from; paired with muhdah, hate, and etsat muhdahna is malice) (e:Na muhdah na ~ mite khut sungah/~ muhdahna tawh a dim uh hi | they are full of malice) (s:mudah/hua/kih) (a:it) (r:26.23.28/45.1.29) (q:draft)
etsathuai = (t:adj) (w:detestable/disgusting/loathsome) (d:etsat, look on with disgust, with huai, deserving of: fit to be loathed) (e:hong teelpa a ~ ahi hi) (s:kihhuai/muhdahhuai/mudahhuai) (a:ithuai) (r:23.41.24) (q:draft)
etsuk = (t:v) (w:look down/look down into) (d:et, form of en, look, with suk, downward: look down at or down into something) (e:Hankhuk sung a ~ ciangin/han sung a ~ ciangin | when he looked down into the tomb/Amaute in leilak a ~ hangun | though they look down at the earth) (s:khuadaksuk) (a:ettoh/dakto/khuadakto) (b:et) (r:43.20.5/23.8.22/42.24.12) (q:draft)
etteh = (t:n) (w:example/model/pattern) (d:someone or something that others look at to copy or to take warning from; et, look, with teh, measure; etteh dingin is as an example for) (e:midangte’ ~ dingin ka bawl ding hi/tuute’ ~ dingin a gamtate na hi un | be people who live as examples to the flock/a dingin ~ hoih na suak uh hi | you became a good example to them/thu um mite’ ~ dingin na om in | be an example for the believers) (s:limpha/gentehna/limlahna) (r:26.14.8/52.1.7/60.5.3/54.4.12) (q:draft)
ettehin = (t:see) <ki-ettehin>
