Gaddel = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Gaddiel) (d:son of Sodi, the man sent from the tribe of Zebulun to explore Canaan) (r:4.13.10)
Gaddi = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Gaddi) (d:son of Susi, the man sent from the tribe of Manasseh to explore Canaan) (e:panin Susi’ tapa ~) (r:4.13.11) (q:draft)
Gaddiel = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Gaddiel) (d:son of Sodi, the man sent from the tribe of Zebulun to explore Canaan) (r:4.13.4)
Gadi = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Gadi) (d:father of Menahem king of Israel) (r:12.15.17/12.15.14)
gah = (t:n) (w:bearing/bearing fruit) (d:The bearing of fruit; gah is used after the noun gah like a verb, as in gah gah, bear fruit.) (e:singkungte ~ ta-in/kha khatin pawl khat ciat a ~ thei hi | it can bear one crop every month/kungte in amau’ gah ~ ding uh hi | the trees will bear their fruit) (r:29.2.22/66.22.2/3.26.4)
gah = (t:n) (w:fruit/crop/produce) (d:The fruit or crop that a tree, plant or field bears; also the result of work or conduct.) (e:lei pan-a piang ~ piakna/a ~ sungah tang a om | with seed in its fruit/A ~ hoih lo kung khempeuh | every tree whose fruit is not good/Theikung a cingpa in a ~ ne a | the one who tends a fig tree eats its fruit) (s:singgah) (r:1.4.3/1.1.11/40.7.19/20.27.18)
Gaham = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Gaham) (d:son of Nahor by his concubine Reumah) (r:1.22.24)
Gahar = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Gahar) (d:ancestor of a family of temple servants who returned from the exile) (r:15.2.47/16.7.49)
gahin = (t:n) (w:by the fruit/by its fruit) (d:The noun gah, fruit, with the marker in showing means: by its fruit, as a tree or a person is known.) (e:a kung a ~ kithei hi/lungsim uh a ~ na thei ding uh hi | you will know their hearts by their fruit/a pianzia pen a ~ hong kithei hi | its nature is known by its fruit) (b:gah) (r:40.12.33/40.7.20) (q:draft)
gahin = (t:v) (w:bearing fruit/yielding/bear fruit) (d:The verb gah, bear fruit, with the linking ending in; it often follows the noun gah, as in gah gahin, bearing fruit.) (e:Leitang in gah ~/hih Lungdamna Thu in a gah ~ | this gospel is bearing fruit/gamtat hoihna apawlpawl ahi gah ~ | bearing fruit in every kind of good conduct/Singkungte tampi tak ~ | the trees bearing much fruit) (b:gah) (r:3.25.19/51.1.6/51.1.10/26.34.27) (q:draft)
gahkhak = (t:v) (w:happen to bear fruit/have fruit) (d:Built from gah, bear fruit, and khak, a form of kha, happen to; a gahkhak leh means in case it has fruit.) (e:a ~ leh ci-in a lo dingin) (r:41.11.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
gahkhia = (t:v) (w:yield/bring forth/produce) (d:Built from gah, bear fruit, and khia, out: bring forth a crop, said of the land.) (e:ama hauhna ~ khin hi) (s:gahsak/piangsak) (b:gah) (r:19.67.6) (q:draft)
gahlo = (t:adj) (w:fruitless/not bearing fruit) (d:Built from gah, bear fruit, and the negative lo; said of a branch that bears no fruit.) (e:Kei tungah a ~ hiangte khempeuh) (a:gahpha) (b:gah) (r:43.15.2) (q:draft)
gahpha = (t:adj) (w:fruitful/bearing well) (d:Built from gah, fruit, and pha, good; said of a vine or tree that bears much fruit.) (e:na leenggui uh ~ mahmah ding hi/A ~ leenggah lo thu la-in sa un | sing a song about the fruitful vineyard/a hing dikdek a ~ oliv kung | a green and fruitful olive tree/a ~ mahmah leenggui tawh kibang hi | is like a very fruitful vine) (a:gahlo) (r:39.3.11/23.27.2/24.11.16/28.10.1) (q:draft)
gahphat = (t:v) (w:bear well/be fruitful) (d:Form of gahpha, bear good fruit, used before a noun such as hun, time: a gahphat hun is the time when it bears well.) (e:Singkung a ~ hun laitakin phuktan ni) (b:gahpha) (r:24.11.19) (q:draft)
gahsak = (t:v) (w:produce/bear/make bear fruit) (d:Built from gah, bear fruit, and the causative sak: make a crop or fruit come, said of the soil or of people.) (e:Lei in ama thuin ~ hi/tampi gah a ~ thei mipawl dangte | other people who can produce much fruit) (s:gahkhia/piangsak) (b:gah) (r:41.4.28/40.21.43) (q:draft)
gahta = (t:see) <gahta-in>
gahta-in = (t:v) (w:bear fruit/be bearing fruit) (d:Built from gah, bear fruit, ta, now or already, and the linking ending in: the trees are now bearing fruit.) (e:nota a, singkungte ~, theigah le leenggah) (r:29.2.22) (q:draft)
gahte = (t:n) (w:fruits/crops/produce) (d:Plural of gah: the fruits or crops of land, trees or work.) (e:leitang in ama ~ hong piangsakin/lokho mi in a ~ a ngah masapen | the farmer is the first to receive the crops/amau sepna ~ kauphe pia hi | he gave the produce of their work to the locust/A min ma-in a ~ a pulh leenggui | a vine that sheds its fruit before it ripens) (s:singgahte) (b:gah) (r:3.26.4/1.1.12/55.2.6/19.78.46/18.15.33)
gahteng = (t:n) (w:all the fruit/the whole fruit) (d:Built from gah, fruit, and teng, all: all the fruit of a tree or vine.) (e:A tehteng heuhsiang inla, a ~ thehthang in/huihpi hong nung a, a ~ keutumsak hi | the wind blew and dried up all its fruit) (b:gah) (r:27.4.14/26.19.12) (q:draft)
gahthei = (t:v) (w:can bear/be able to bear) (d:Built from gah, bear fruit, and thei, can; used in questions about what a tree can bear.) (e:theikung in oliv hong ~ a/leenggui in theipum hong ~ ahi hiam | can a grapevine bear figs) (s:gahzo/gahtheih) (b:gah) (r:59.3.12) (q:draft)
gahtheih = (t:v) (w:be able to bear fruit) (d:Built from gah, bear fruit, and theih, be able; the form used before nading, so that it can bear.) (e:Singgah limci a ~ nadingin) (s:gahzo/gahthei) (b:gah) (r:40.12.33) (q:draft)
gahto = (t:v) (w:bear fruit upward/bear fruit above) (d:Built from gah, bear fruit, and to, upward; set against taking root downward.) (e:a tung lamah gah hong ~ ding hi/gah na ~ kik ding uh hi | they will bear fruit upward again) (b:gah) (r:12.19.30/23.37.31) (q:draft)
gahzo = (t:v) (w:be able to bear fruit/manage to bear fruit) (d:Built from gah, bear fruit, and zo, be able; bangmah gahzo lo is bear nothing at all.) (e:depgawp ahih manin bangmah ~ lo hi) (s:gahtheih/gahthei) (b:gah) (r:41.4.7) (q:draft)
gai = (t:v) (w:conceive/become pregnant) (d:Conceive a child, become or be pregnant; gai kik is conceive again.) (e:Leah ~ kik a/Hagar luppih a, Hagar ~ hi | he slept with Hagar and Hagar conceived/ama zi Elisabeth a ~ hi | his wife Elizabeth became pregnant/Amah ~ leuleu-in tapa khat nei a | she conceived again and had a son) (s:naupaai/paii) (r:1.30.19/1.30.5/1.16.4/42.1.24/1.29.34)
Gaia = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Gaius) (d:Gaius of Derbe, a companion of Paul on his journey through Macedonia to Asia) (r:44.20.4) (q:draft)
Gaias = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Gaius) (d:name of several early Christians, among them the host of Paul in Corinth and the friend to whom the third letter of John is written) (r:45.16.23/64.1.1)
gaih = (t:v) (w:eat up/finish off/consume) (d:eat until nothing is left) (e:antang amaute in a ~ khit uh ciangin/Kauphe in gamsung lopate a ~ khit ciangin | when the locusts had eaten up the grass of the land/nasemte khempeuh in ~ zawh lohin an khamval nei uh | all the hired men have more food than they can finish) (s:netum/nektum/nemang) (r:1.43.2/30.7.2/42.15.17) (q:draft)
gaih = (t:v) (d:used after nungkik, draw back, in nungkik gaih-in, said of people who shrink back or flee from a sight, what gaih itself adds is not clear) (e:Nang hong mu khempeuh nungkik ~-in) (r:34.3.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
gaihgaih = (t:adv) (d:placed after kisat beat: throbbing or sounding again and again like the strings of a harp, said of a grieving heart) (e:bangin ka lungsim kisat ~ a/keimahmah zong ka kisat ~ hi | I myself also throb again and again) (r:23.16.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
gaihin = (t:v) (d:gaih with the linking suffix in, used after nungkik, draw back, of people who shrink back or flee from a sight; what gaih itself adds is not clear) (e:Nang hong mu khempeuh nungkik ~) (b:gaih) (r:34.3.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
gaihsak = (t:v) (w:devour/eat up/consume) (d:gaih, eat up, finish off, with sak, which here shows the action is done to the loss of another) (e:na bawng honte uh hong ~ ding uh a/na an huante uh hong ~ ding uh a | they will eat up your food gardens/dawn ding bawngnawite hong ~ mang ding uh hi | they will consume the milk you were to drink) (s:netum/nektum/nemang) (b:gaih) (r:24.5.17/26.25.4) (q:draft)
gaihsakmang = (t:v) (w:eat up/consume entirely) (d:gaih, eat up, with sak and mang, away: eat up all that belongs to someone else) (e:dawn ding bawngnawite hong ~ ding uh hi) (r:26.25.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
gaikikin = (t:v) (w:conceive again) (d:gai, conceive, with kik, again, and the linking suffix in) (e:Tua ciangin Gomer ~ tanu khat nei hi) (r:28.1.6) (q:draft)
gaina = (t:n) (w:conception/pregnancy) (d:gai, conceive, with the noun suffix na: what she has conceived) (e:Ama ~ in Kha Siangtho in a gaisak) (b:gai) (r:40.1.20) (q:draft)
gaisak = (t:v) (w:cause to conceive/make pregnant) (d:gai, conceive, with the causative sak) (e:Kha Siangtho in a ~ hi) (b:gai) (r:40.1.18/40.1.20) (q:draft)
gaisakin = (t:v) (w:cause to conceive/make pregnant) (d:gaisak, cause to conceive, with the linking suffix in) (e:Topa in tua nu ~ amah in) (b:gaisak) (r:8.4.13) (q:draft)
gaisakna = (t:n) (w:causing to conceive) (d:gaisak, cause to conceive, with the noun suffix na: the fact of having been made pregnant) (e:Kha Siangtho in amah a ~ thu) (b:gaisak) (r:40.1.18) (q:draft)
gaite = (t:n) (w:pregnant women/expectant mothers) (d:gai be pregnant, conceive, with the plural te; used after nupi, women) (e:nupi ~ leh nau suak ding) (b:gai) (r:24.31.8) (q:draft)
gaizawh = (t:v) (w:after conceiving) (d:gai, conceive, with zawh, after or having finished; a gaizawh kha guk is the sixth month after she conceived) (e:Elizabeth a ~ kha guk a cin ciangin) (r:42.1.26) (q:draft, low confidence)
gak = (t:v) (w:fasten/tie/gird) (d:tie or fasten one thing onto another, as a belt round the waist, a cord on a turban or rings on the legs of a table) (e:dial tawh a kawng a ~ hi/khau dum khat tawh dialpi tungah na ~ ding hi | you shall fasten it on the turban with a blue cord/a khe lite-ah a kualte ~ hi | he fastened the rings to the four legs/a lukhute uh na ~ ding hi | you shall fasten their caps on) (s:khih) (a:sut/phel) (r:43.13.4/2.28.37/2.37.13/2.29.9) (q:draft)
gakapte = (t:n) (w:soldiers/warriors) (d:apparently a misprint of galkapte, soldiers) (e:Amaute in a thahat ~ hi a) (s:galkapte) (r:26.32.29) (q:draft, low confidence)
gakcip = (t:v) (w:bind fast/entangle/hold fast) (d:gak, tie, with cip, tightly: bind fast so that there is no getting free, said of ropes, snares, death and sin) (e:thangkhau in amah ~ hi/Sihna khau in kei hong ~ hi | the cords of death bound me fast/Amau’ mawhna in amaute ~ a | their sins bind them fast/ama khut le a khete a ~ khit ciangin | after he had bound his own hands and feet) (s:hencip/lencip) (a:sut) (b:gak) (r:18.18.9/19.116.3/28.7.2/44.21.11) (q:draft)
gakcipsak = (t:v) (w:fasten tight/make fast) (d:gakcip, bind fast, with sak: have the feet fastened in the stocks) (e:sungah a khe uh a ~ hi) (b:gakcip) (r:44.16.24) (q:draft)
gakin = (t:v) (w:gird/tie round/fasten) (d:gak tie round the waist with the linking ending in, tying or having tied a belt or sash) (e:kawnggakte tawh amaute ~/amah in a kawng ~ | girding his waist/a kawnggak tawh ~, a puantualpi silh sak a | tying the sash round him, he put the robe on him/a awmah kham kawnggak ~ | with a golden sash tied round his chest) (b:gak) (r:3.8.13/11.18.46/3.8.7/66.1.13) (q:draft)
gakkhawm = (t:v) (w:tie together/bind together) (d:gak, tie, with khawm, together) (e:khaudum khatin a kual tawh ~ ding uh hi) (s:henkhawm/henkop) (b:gak) (r:2.28.28) (q:draft)
gakna = (t:n) (w:band/fastening/waistband) (d:gak, fasten, with -na: the thing used to fasten or bind round, such as a band on a post or the waistband of a garment) (e:ngun tawh kibawl ~ tawh kigak/tuate’ ading ~ bawl hi | he made bands for them/hoih taka a kigan siampipuan ~ tawh | with the skillfully woven waistband of the ephod) (b:gak) (r:2.27.17/2.29.5/2.38.28) (q:draft)
gaknate = (t:n) (w:bands/fillets) (d:plural of gakna: the bands that fasten round the posts of the tabernacle court, named beside the hooks) (e:a ~ in ngun ahi hi/a ~ kham hi a | their bands were gold/a khuamlu zepnate leh a ~ a kizutna | the overlay of their tops and their bands) (b:gakna) (r:2.38.12/2.38.10/2.36.38/2.38.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
gal = (t:n) (w:war/battle) (d:war or battle, fighting between peoples; gal kido is to fight a war and gal sim to attack in war) (e:Gam sungah ~ simna aw kiza a/~ kido ni-in nungkik uh hi | they turned back on the day of battle/~ kidona om nawn lo hi | there was no more war) (s:galdona/kidona/galkidona) (a:kilemna) (r:24.50.22/19.63.10/19.78.9/14.15.19) (q:draft)
gal = (t:n) (w:enemy/foe) (d:one who is against another and seeks to harm him, a single enemy or the enemy in war) (e:Judah mite’ ~ ahi Haman’ neihsa khempeuh/~ bangin hong ngaihsun na hi hiam | do you consider me an enemy/A khakbel a ~ ahi sihna | death, the last enemy/ka ~ na suak hi | you have become my enemy) (s:galpa/galmi) (a:lawm) (r:17.8.1/40.10.36/18.13.24/46.15.26/18.16.8) (q:draft)
gal = (t:n) (w:other side) (d:the far side of a river, lake or sea, as in gal khat across) (e:Tuili ~ khat Gerasa gamah/Jordan gun ~ khat, Atad’ buhcilna phual | across the Jordan, the threshing floor of Atad/lui ~ khatah puak hi | he sent them across the stream/Jordan ~ khat Moab gam leizangah | in the plains of Moab across the Jordan) (s:galkhat) (r:41.5.1/1.50.10/1.32.23/4.22.1) (q:draft)
Gal = (t:n) (w:enemy/adversary) (d:gal written with a capital in the title Khrih Gal, the enemy of Christ, the antichrist) (e:thugente pen Khrih’ ~ hi a/Khrih’ ~ ahi uh hi | they are the antichrist) (s:galpa) (b:gal) (r:62.2.22/63.1.7) (q:draft)
Gal = (t:n) (w:war) (d:gal written with a capital in the book title Topa Gal Laibu, the Book of the Wars of the Lord) (e:~ Laibu sungah) (b:gal) (r:4.21.14) (q:draft)
galah = (t:prep) (w:across/beyond/on the other side of) (d:gal the far side with the place marker ah; follows the name of a river or land, as in Jordan gun galah, across the Jordan; a galah, to the other side) (e:Jordan gun ~ Zeisu pai kik a/Galile gam ~ Geresa gam a tung uh a | they reached the region of Gerasa across from Galilee/Jordan ~ kumpipa a paipih dingin | to bring the king across the Jordan/nisuahna lam ~ pai-in Janoah a tung hi | passing over to the east side it reached Janoah) (s:galkhatah) (b:gal) (r:43.10.40/42.8.26/10.19.15/6.16.6) (q:draft)
Galal = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Galal) (d:name of two Levites who lived in Jerusalem after the exile, one of them a son of Jeduthun) (r:13.9.16/13.9.15)
Galatia = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Galatia) (d:Roman province in the middle of Asia Minor, where Paul travelled and founded churches) (r:44.16.6/44.18.23)
galbanum = (t:n) (w:galbanum) (d:a fragrant gum used in making the holy incense, the foreign name kept as it is) (e:onikh leh ~) (r:2.30.34) (q:draft)
galbawl = (t:v) (w:oppose/attack/be hostile to) (d:gal enemy with bawl make: act as an enemy toward someone) (e:amah ~ nawn kei in/Judah in Efraim ~ nawn lo ding hi | Judah will no longer be hostile to Ephraim/Keimah hong ~, hong umcih mi tulsawm tampite | the tens of thousands who attack me and surround me/thukawi mite na ~ hi | you oppose the crooked) (s:langpang/langpan) (a:kilem) (b:gal) (r:18.22.21/19.3.6/23.11.13/19.18.26) (q:draft)
galbawlna = (t:n) (w:enmity/hostility) (d:galbawl be hostile with the noun suffix na: acting as an enemy toward someone) (e:~ tawh a khut-in tumin) (s:galneihna/kigalneihna/kilemlohna) (a:kilemna) (b:galbawl) (r:4.35.21) (q:draft)
galbawlte = (t:n) (w:enemies/adversaries) (d:galbawl be hostile with plural te: those who act as enemies toward someone) (e:Judah mi a ~ kisusia ding hi) (s:galte/langpangte) (a:lawmte) (b:galbawl) (r:23.11.13) (q:draft)
galdaihna = (t:n) (w:peace/rest from war) (d:gal, war or enemy, with daihna, calm: freedom from enemies and fighting) (e:ama kiimah ~ pia hi/Topa in ama tungah ~ hun pia | the Lord gave him a time of rest from war/ama kiim mun khempeuhah ~ om hi | there was peace on every side of him/Topa in a kiim uhah amaute ~ a pia hi | the Lord gave them rest on every side) (s:kilemna) (a:galdona/galkidona) (r:14.20.30/14.15.15/14.14.6/11.4.24) (q:draft)
galdal = (t:n) (w:armor/defence) (d:gal war with dal shield: what protects in battle; galdal thep beside awmdal, the breastplate, is the armor worn on the body) (e:a ~ thep leh a awmdal kikal) (r:14.18.33) (q:draft)
galdalna = (t:n) (w:fortification/stronghold/defence) (d:something that keeps the enemy out; galdalna kulhpi is a fortress and galdalna inn a citadel) (e:a ~ kulhpite khempeuh balzan gawpin/a sangpi-ah kiptakin ~ a bawl thei | she can build a firm stronghold on high/khuapi kimkotah ~ a phut uh hi | they set up siege works all around the city/~ inn a uk Hananiah | Hananiah who commanded the citadel) (b:galdal) (r:25.2.2/16.7.2/24.51.53/24.52.4) (q:draft)
galdalnate = (t:n) (w:armor/battle dress) (d:galdalna defence with plural te: the pieces of armor a fighter wears) (e:a ~ tungah a namsau khih a) (b:galdalna) (r:9.17.39) (q:draft)
galdalte = (t:n) (w:defences/bulwarks/towers) (d:galdal with plural te: the defensive works of a city, named beside its walls) (e:A ~ uh cim khin a) (b:galdal) (r:24.50.15) (q:draft)
galdo = (t:v) (w:fight/wage war/go to battle) (d:gal enemy with do fight; galdo dingin is for battle, for war) (e:~ dingin a kuan thei pasal peuhmah/leitung lungsim ngimna tawh ~ ka hi kei uh hi | we do not wage war with the aims of the world/~ mite a phazah a gawm pia hi | he gave the total number of the fighting men/Israel mite ~ dingin kithawisa-in | the Israelites, ready for battle) (s:galsim/kido/galkido) (a:kilem) (r:4.1.45/13.12.25/47.10.3/10.24.9/2.13.18) (q:draft)
galdona = (t:n) (w:battle/war/warfare) (d:galdo, fight, with the noun suffix na: war or a battle; galdona aw is the battle cry) (e:~ panin a hong ciah mi tul tampi/tua gam in ~ panin tawlnga hi | the land had rest from war/~ ah a kuan galkapte tungah | to the soldiers who had gone into battle/Judah mite in a ~ aw kiko uh hi | the men of Judah raised the battle cry) (s:galkidona/kidona/gal) (a:kilemna/galdaihna) (b:galdo) (r:4.31.14/41.13.7/6.14.15/4.31.21/14.13.15) (q:draft)
Galdona = (t:name) (w:Galdona)
galdonate = (t:n) (w:wars/battles) (d:plural of galdona: wars; galdonate nei is to have wars, to be at war) (e:tu-a kipanin ~ na nei ding hi) (s:galkidonate) (b:galdona) (r:14.16.9) (q:draft)
Galeed = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Galeed) (d:name Jacob gave to the heap of stones set up as a witness between him and Laban in the hill country of Gilead) (r:1.31.47/1.31.48)
galet = (t:see) <galet-in>
galet-in = (t:v) (w:see from afar/look at from a distance) (d:gal, the far side, with et, form of en, look, and the linking suffix in) (e:gamlapi pan ~ hopihin) (s:galmuhin) (r:58.11.13) (q:draft)
galgim = (t:n) (w:scent of battle) (d:gal, war, with gim, smell) (e:ma-un ~ za uh a) (r:18.39.25) (q:draft)
galgu = (t:n) (w:robber/bandit) (d:gal enemy with gu steal: an armed robber; galgu mat bangin is as if catching a robber, where the NIV has leading a rebellion) (e:~ mat bangin kei man dingin) (s:misuam/buluh/misuampa) (r:41.14.48/40.26.55) (q:draft)
galgumat = (t:n) (d:in galgumat bangin, as if to seize a robber or rebel; apparently gal, enemy, gu, thief, and mat, seize) (e:Note in ~ bangin kei man dingin) (r:42.22.52) (q:draft, low confidence)
galhang = (t:n) (w:warrior/valiant fighter/brave man) (d:one who is brave in war, also used to describe a person as valiant) (e:~ pente nangawn, tai mang ding/A thahat a ~ Eliada | Eliada, a strong and valiant warrior/a thahat ~ mite ahi uh hi | they were strong and valiant men/~ mihing tulsawm leh tulgiat tuk uh hi | eighteen thousand valiant men fell) (s:galhangpa/hangpa/galkappa) (r:30.2.16/7.20.44/14.17.17/14.14.8) (q:draft)
galhangpa = (t:n) (w:warrior/mighty man) (d:galhang warrior with pa, which marks a man) (e:~ kiang panin nate kilakhia zo ding/~’ khut sunga om thaltangte tawh kibang hi | are like arrows in the hand of a warrior/A ~’ mat salte kilakhia ding a | the captives of the warrior will be taken from him) (s:galhang/hangpa/thahatpa) (b:galhang) (r:23.49.24/19.120.4/19.127.4/23.49.25) (q:draft)
galhangte = (t:n) (w:warriors/brave men/mighty men) (d:plural of galhang: warriors, men who are brave in battle) (e:~ huhna ngenin kiko uh a/na ~ a thanem ding uh hi | your warriors will lose their strength/a thahat ~, mi minthangte | brave warriors, famous men/na ~ hong paipih suk in | bring down your warriors) (s:hangte/thahatte) (b:galhang) (r:23.33.7/24.48.14/31.1.9/13.5.24/29.3.11) (q:draft)
galhat = (t:adj) (w:mighty in battle/strong in war) (d:gal, war, with hat, strong; a galhat man is because of his strength in war) (e:~ Topa ahi hi/A ~ man leh galkap tampi a thahna hangin | because of his might in war and his killing of many soldiers) (r:19.24.8/27.11.12) (q:draft)
galhatna = (t:n) (w:military strength/might in war) (d:galhat strong in war with the noun suffix na) (e:~ khempeuh ka sumai ding hi/A ~ hang le galkap tampi a thahna hangin | because of his might in war and his killing of many soldiers) (b:galhat) (r:28.1.5/27.11.12) (q:draft)
galhiam = (t:n) (w:weapon/armor/arms) (d:gal, war, with hiam, weapon: a weapon or the arms and armor of a fighter; galhiam tawi is armed, and galhiam puapa an armor-bearer) (e:Tu-in ~ a tawi Dan mi zagukte/a khut lang khat uhah ~ tawi uh hi | they held a weapon in the other hand/dikna ~ ziat lam leh vei lamah | weapons of righteousness in the right hand and in the left/Joab’ ~ puapa | the armor-bearer of Joab/~ a tawi thei khempeuh kisamkhia uh a | all who could bear arms were called out) (s:galvan) (r:7.18.16/47.6.7/16.4.17/13.11.39/12.3.21) (q:draft)
galhiamin = (t:n) (w:as a weapon) (d:galhiam, weapon, with the marker in: as weapons, by way of weapons) (e:~ tua thute zang inla) (b:galhiam) (r:54.1.18) (q:draft)
galhiamte = (t:n) (w:weapons) (d:plural of galhiam: weapons of war) (e:namsau leh ~ kuaitan hi/~ bangci-in sia | how the weapons of war have perished/ama hehna ~ gamlapi van mong panin | the weapons of his wrath from the far end of the heavens/sih theihna ama ~ a baihsa-in koih zo hi | he has made ready his deadly weapons) (s:galvante/hiamte) (b:galhiam) (r:19.76.3/10.1.27/23.13.5/19.7.13) (q:draft)
Galile = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Galilee) (d:region in the north of the land of Israel, west of the lake of the same name, where Jesus grew up and began his work) (e:Judah gam pan ~ gamah a paikik hi) (r:43.4.2/41.1.28) (q:draft)
Galilee = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Galilee) (d:region in the north of the land of Israel, west of the lake of the same name, where Jesus grew up and began his work) (r:43.7.9/42.8.26)
