Galille = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Galilee) (d:Galilee, the northern region of Israel, here the home of Judas the Galilean who led a revolt) (r:44.5.37)
galin = (t:adv) (w:in war/as an enemy) (d:gal with the marker in; galin do is to fight against, to make war on) (e:Pasian’ mite ~ do a/Na gam sung uhah ~ na si ding uh hi | you will die by war in your land/Hadadezer pen Toi tawh ~ kido ngei zel hi | Hadadezer had often been at war with Toi/Khazih’ singlamteh ~ do-in a gamta mi tampi | many who live as enemies of the cross of Christ/a nu leh a pate ~ a do ding uh a | they will rise against their parents as enemies) (b:gal) (r:27.7.21/26.11.10/10.8.10/50.3.18/41.13.12) (q:draft)
galkah = (t:v) (w:cross/cross over/pass over) (d:go across to the other side of a river, lake or boundary) (e:Jordan a ~ khit uh ciangin/a ~ khit ciangin a teen’na khua-ah a tung hi | after crossing over he came to his own town/sihna panin nuntakna ah i ~ zo hi | we have passed from death to life/Israelte khempeuh leikeu tungah a ~ sung | while all Israel was crossing on dry ground) (s:kantan) (r:6.4.1/40.9.1/62.3.14/6.3.17) (q:draft)
galkahin = (t:v) (w:cross over/cross/go across) (d:galkah with the linking suffix in, crossing over, followed by another verb) (e:hua mite kiangah ~ amaute kiangah/~ Nun tapa Joshua kiangah tung uh hi | crossing over, they came to Joshua son of Nun/Siria gam ~ Tai-ar khua-ah ka khawl uh hi | crossing to Syria we landed at Tyre/Ammon mite sim dingin ~ | crossing over to fight the Ammonites) (b:galkah) (r:9.14.8/6.2.23/44.21.3/7.12.1) (q:draft)
galkahpih = (t:v) (w:take across/bring over) (d:galkah cross over with pih, together with: cross a river with someone, take them across) (e:kumpipa innkuante a ~ ding leh) (b:galkah) (r:10.19.18) (q:draft)
galkahsak = (t:v) (w:send across/let cross/take across) (d:galkah, cross over, with the causative sak) (e:mi khat zong ~ lo uh hi/a neih khempeuh zong ~ hi | he also sent across all that he had) (b:galkah) (r:7.3.28/1.32.23) (q:draft)
galkap = (t:n) (w:soldier) (d:a man who serves in an army) (e:~ khat in a pang teipi tawh sun/Khazih Zeisu’ ~ siampa bangin | like a good soldier of Christ Jesus) (s:galkappa) (r:43.19.34/55.2.3) (q:draft)
galkap = (t:n) (w:army/host) (d:a body of soldiers, the whole fighting force of a king or people; vantung galkap is the host of heaven) (e:mi thahat ~ khempeuh sawl hi/Hadadezer’ ~ buppi David in a zawhna thu | that David had defeated the whole army of Hadadezer/vantung ~ tampite in thakhatin hong kikhawm uh a | suddenly a great heavenly host gathered/~ a ukte khempeuh a ukpi ahi hi | he was chief of all the army officers) (s:galkapte) (r:13.19.8/42.2.13/10.8.9/13.27.3) (q:draft)
Galkap = (t:n) (w:warrior/soldier) (d:galkap written with a capital in Galkap Inn, the House of the Heroes in Jerusalem) (e:~ Inn ciang dong puah hi) (b:galkap) (r:16.3.16) (q:draft)
galkapbu = (t:n) (w:centurion/army officer) (d:commander of a body of soldiers, galkap, soldier, with bu) (e:Rom mi ~ khat ama kiangah hong pai-in/~ Kornelias kici mi khat a om hi | there was a centurion named Cornelius/Tua khua sungah Rom mi ~ khat om a | in that town there was a Roman centurion) (s:bupa/galkapmang) (r:40.8.5/42.7.2/44.10.1) (q:draft)
galkapbute = (t:n) (w:army officers/centurions/captains) (d:plural of galkapbu; in these verses the leaders of bodies of soldiers, named beside galkapte, the soldiers) (e:Paul in ~ khat samin ama kiangah/galkap mangpa in ~ nih samin | the commander called two centurions/gam sung khuaneu-a om ~ khempeuh | all the army officers who were in the villages of the land/thakhatin ~ le galkapte samin | at once calling officers and soldiers) (s:galkapmangte) (b:galkapbu) (r:44.23.17/24.40.13/44.23.23/44.21.32) (q:draft, low confidence)
galkapmang = (t:n) (w:army officer/commander/captain) (d:galkap, soldier, and mang, chief: an officer who commands soldiers) (e:leh a ~ khempeuh leh kumpi/amah tawh a omkhawm ~ khempeuh | all the army officers who were with him/kumpi cing ~ Nebuzaradan | Nebuzaradan, commander of the royal guard/a ~ lian penpa | his supreme commander) (s:galkapbu/galkapmangpa/bupa) (r:24.26.21/24.41.11/24.40.1/12.18.17) (q:draft)
galkapmangpa = (t:n) (w:commander/army officer/captain) (d:galkapmang, army officer, with pa marking a man) (e:a ~ na kaplet hi) (s:galkapmang/bupa) (b:galkapmang) (r:35.3.14) (q:draft)
galkapmangte = (t:n) (w:commanders/officers/generals/captains) (d:army officers; galkap soldier, mang chief, with the plural ending te) (e:a ~, a leeng ukte leh a sakol tuangte/amaute’ munah ~ koih in | put officers in their place/~’ thupiakna awging za uh hi | they hear the shout of the commanders/kumpite le miliante, ~, mihaute le mi vangliante | the kings and the great, the generals, the rich and the mighty) (s:galkapbute/ukte) (b:galkapmang) (r:11.9.22/66.6.15/11.20.24/18.39.25) (q:draft)
