galkhatah = (t:prep) (w:across/beyond/on the other side of) (d:galkhat with ah, at or to the other side) (e:Jordan ~ pai-in Jerikho na tung uh/Eufrates ~ na pu na pate uh teeng ngei a | your ancestors once lived beyond the Euphrates/lui ~ puak a | he sent them across the stream/Eder tausang ~ a puanbuk a lam hi | he pitched his tent beyond the tower of Eder) (s:galah) (b:galkhat) (r:6.24.11/40.8.28/6.24.2/1.32.23/1.35.21) (q:draft)
galkidalna = (t:n) (w:armor/tunic) (d:gal, war, with kidal, shield oneself, and the noun suffix na: what a man wears for protection in battle; the NIV has tunic) (e:a ~ le a namsau nangawn) (r:9.18.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
galkido = (t:v) (w:be at war/wage war/fight) (d:gal, war, with kido, fight each other, also used as a noun, war) (e:Siria kumpipa Hazael tawh ~ dingin/Siria leh Isarel ~ loin om uh hi | Aram and Israel were without war/Efraim mite, ~ ni-in nungkik uh hi | the men of Ephraim turned back on the day of battle/amaute in ~ ding utna tengin nei uh hi | they want nothing but war) (s:galdo/kido/galsim) (a:kilem) (r:12.8.28/11.22.1/19.78.9/19.120.7) (q:draft)
