galmatin = (t:adv) (w:as captives/captive/into captivity) (d:galmat captive with in; in the state of a prisoner of war, with verbs of carrying off or being) (e:i zite ~ om uh hi/a mite ~ Kir-ah pua a | he carried its people captive to Kir/Jerusalem panin Babilon ah amah in ~ la hi | he took them captive from Jerusalem to Babylon/Israel mite, ~ kipaipih ding hi | the Israelites will be led away captive) (s:salin) (b:galmat) (r:14.29.9/14.28.17/12.16.9/12.24.15/30.7.17) (q:draft)
galmatte = (t:n) (w:captives/prisoners) (d:plural of galmat, people taken in war) (e:~ leh a lak uh nate nusia uh hi/na ~ paikhiatpih in, Abinoam’ tapa aw | lead away your captives, son of Abinoam/hih lai-ah ~ nong tun’pih kei ding uh hi | you must not bring the captives here) (s:salte/saltangte) (b:galmat) (r:14.28.14/4.31.12/7.5.12/14.28.13) (q:draft)
