galmuh = (t:v) (w:see from afar/see at a distance) (d:gal, across or far off, with muh, see) (e:Abraham le Lazaras a omkhawm a ~ hi/Israel mi a madawk pente ~ thei hi | he could see the nearest of the Israelites from afar/A teh a no theikung khat ~ ahih manin | because he saw in the distance a fig tree in leaf/a tun ma-in a pa in na ~ a | before he arrived his father saw him from afar) (r:42.16.23/4.22.41/41.11.13/42.15.20) (q:draft)
