galpanna = (t:n) (w:stronghold/outpost/military post) (d:Gal, war, with pan, take up a position, and the noun suffix na: a place held by soldiers; galpanna mun is a stronghold or outpost and galpanna phual a military camp.) (e:na ~ munte uh ka phelkhia ding hi/a ~ munah a paisuk uh hi | they went down to the outposts/~ teng mei tawh kihalin | all the positions were burned with fire) (s:galpan'na/galpanmun/phualkip) (r:33.5.11/7.7.11/24.51.32) (q:draft)
galphual = (t:n) (w:battlefield/battle/battle line) (d:Gal, war, with phual, place: the place where the fighting is.) (e:~ panin hong puakhia in/~ sungah mi tulli bang that uh hi | they killed about four thousand men on the battlefield/tu ni-in ~ panin kong tai hi | today I fled from the battle line/mihonte ~ ah pai-in | as the army was going out to the battlefield) (s:galsung) (r:14.18.33/9.4.2/9.4.16/9.17.20) (q:draft)
