gelhsa = (t:adj) (w:written) (d:already written; what someone has written, gelh with sa for a finished action) (e:~ laibu panin keimah hong phiat in/Ka ~ in ka ~ hi | what I have written, I have written/Pasian’ kamsangte’ ~ Lai Siangtho | the Scriptures written by the prophets of God/Judah mi Mordekai in a ~ bang | as Mordecai the Jew had written) (s:kigelhsa) (b:gelh) (r:2.32.32/43.19.22/40.26.56/17.9.31) (q:draft)
gelhsak = (t:v) (w:have written/cause to write/write for) (d:gelh write with sak: have something written, or write it for someone) (e:lai khat ~ in/mihing sawmsagih leh sagih a min ~ hi | he wrote down for him the names of seventy-seven men/hih lai malte tua khut a hong ~ hi | he made that hand write these letters/nang a dingin hong ~ leng hoih ding hi | it would be good for me to write it down for you) (b:gelh) (r:17.8.5/7.8.14/27.5.24/42.1.3) (q:draft)
gelhsakin = (t:v) (w:have written/cause to write) (d:form of gelhsak with the linking suffix in, having something written and then going on to the next action) (e:Pilat in lai khat ~/Moses in kimakna lai ~ masak thei hi | Moses allowed a man to write a certificate of divorce and send her away) (b:gelhsak) (r:43.19.19/41.10.4) (q:draft)
gelhte = (t:n) (w:those who write/writers) (d:gelh, write, with plural te: those who write something) (e:nenniamna thu a ~ in gimna ngah) (s:laigelhte/atte) (b:gelh) (r:23.10.1) (q:draft)
gelhte = (t:n) (w:things written/what is written) (d:gelh, write, with plural te: the things that someone writes) (e:hih lai ka hong ~ pen) (b:gelh) (r:46.14.37) (q:draft)
