Gemariah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Gemariah) (d:name of two men in Jeremiah: a son of Shaphan the secretary, who urged the king not to burn the scroll, and a son of Hilkiah sent to Babylon by Zedekiah) (r:24.36.11/24.36.25)
gen = (t:v) (w:tell/say/speak) (d:say or tell something in words; the basic verb of speaking, as in thu gen, speak a word) (e:Pa thu a ~ ahih lam/kua in hong ~ ahi hiam | who told you/Thuman thutak ka ~ ciangin | when I tell the truth/Thuman na ~ ciangin | when you speak what is right/a leii in thutang ~ hi | his tongue speaks what is just) (s:ci) (r:43.8.27/1.3.11/43.8.45/20.23.16/19.37.30)
gen = (t:v) (w:inform) (d:tell someone a piece of news or report it to them, with kiangah for the person told) (e:Kumpi David kiangah ~ zel uh hi/a sanggam nihte kiangah ~ hi | he told his two brothers/kei kiangah hong ~ lo na hi hiam | did you not tell me) (s:zasak/theihsak) (r:10.17.17/1.9.22/1.12.18)
genbaang = (t:v) (w:blame) (d:find fault with someone in words; genbaang lo is blameless, with nothing to be blamed for) (e:~ lo/lungsim uh a siangtho leh ~ lo | hearts pure and blameless) (s:paubaang) (r:50.1.9)
genbeh = (t:v) (w:say in addition/testify further/add) (d:gen, say, with beh, in addition) (e:bawlna tawh hong ~ lai hi) (s:genthuah) (r:58.2.4) (q:draft)
genbelin = (t:adv) (w:as the subject of speech) (d:always with nei, have: genbelin nei is have something as the matter one keeps speaking about, speak of, testify to) (e:midang kiangah ~ ka nei uh hi/Eite in ~ i neih a hong tung ding leitung | the world to come, of which we are speaking/tua nuntak tawntungna pen ~ nei-in | testifying to that eternal life) (r:62.4.14/58.2.5/62.1.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
gendai = (t:v) (w:slander/revile/blaspheme) (d:speak evil of someone; gendai-mawhna is the sin of speaking against God, blasphemy) (e:mi a ~ thei mi/Amaute in mi ~ thei mi | they are slanderers/midangte a ~ loh theih nading | so that they do not slander others/ci-in ~-mawhna lianpi a bawl uh | they committed great blasphemy) (s:gensia/kosia) (a:phat) (r:55.3.3/16.9.18/45.1.30/56.2.3) (q:draft)
gendaina = (t:n) (w:slander/reviling) (d:gendai with the noun suffix na) (e:note lakah kitotna, ~, nakpi-a hehna | among you quarrelling, slander, fierce anger) (s:gensiatna) (a:phatna) (b:gendai) (r:47.12.20) (q:draft)
gengen = (t:v) (w:mention/tell again and again/proclaim) (d:gen, say, doubled: speak of something repeatedly, keep telling or proclaiming it) (e:tua thute na ~ ding uh hi/sepnate ka ~ ding hi | I will proclaim his deeds/Ni simin thu ~ a | day after day they pour forth speech/kong ~ hangin hong ngai tuan loin | though I spoke to you again and again you did not listen) (b:gen) (r:5.6.7/19.118.17/19.19.2/24.7.13)
gengenin = (t:v) (w:keep talking/talk on and on) (d:gen, say, doubled and with the linking suffix -in: saying again and again, at length) (e:Mihaite in thu ~ ciakciak uh hi/Bangtanvei thu ~, kei hong gimsak ding | how long will you torment me with talk/Ahi zongin Paul in thu ~ | but as Paul went on speaking/minthanna thu ~ na vangliatna thu sutsut | telling of the glory and recounting your might) (s:paupau) (b:gengen) (r:21.10.14/18.19.2/44.24.25/19.145.11) (q:draft)
gengenna = (t:n) (w:words/talk) (d:gengen, say repeatedly, with the noun suffix na: what one keeps saying) (e:Thu na ~ uh tawh Topa) (b:gengen) (r:39.2.17) (q:draft)
genhak = (t:adj) (w:obstinate/stubborn/hard) (d:gen, speak, with hak, difficult: hard to speak to or reason with) (e:a ~ mite lam nga-in/a ~ naupangte in gimna ngah ta hen | woe to the obstinate children/mi ~ mahmah na hihna ka hong thei | I knew that you are a very hard man) (s:lungkhauh) (r:23.65.2/40.25.24/23.30.1) (q:draft)
genhuaina = (t:n) (w:cause for complaint/something to object to) (d:something that deserves to be spoken about; in the verse a question, is there anything to object to) (e:~ bang om ahi hiam) (r:46.9.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
genin = (t:v) (w:tell/speak/say) (d:form of gen with the linking suffix in, telling or speaking and then going on to the next action) (e:keimah in thu ~ amah ka sam a/thu ~ gamta un | speak and act/Pasian’ min dingin a man lo ~ | speaking what is not right on behalf of God/Jezebel’ thu zong Topa in ~ | the Lord also speaks concerning Jezebel) (b:gen) (r:23.48.15/19.145.11/59.2.12/18.13.7/11.21.23) (q:draft)
geninah = (t:v) (w:say/tell/speak) (d:gen, say, with inah, the ending that introduces the words that follow: says as follows, speaking thus) (e:keimah Paul in kong ~/Johan’ thu a ~ | he spoke about John, saying/Thugentehna adang a ~ | he told another parable, saying/leitung mi bangin thu ka ~ | I speak in a human way) (s:cihinah) (r:48.5.2/40.13.33/40.11.7/48.3.15) (q:draft)
genkha = (t:v) (w:say/happen to say) (d:gen, say, with kha, which marks something one comes to do, often without meaning to or wrongly) (e:kilawm zahval ~ ka hih manin/hih bang thu hong ~ thei ding a | may come to say such a thing to you) (s:cikha) (r:18.40.5/53.2.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
genkhak = (t:v) (w:happen to say/say) (d:form of genkha, gen say with kha, come to do, used before loh, uh leh and the like) (e:a sia-in a ~ loh theih nadingun/ci-in a hong ~ uhleh | if they come to say that to you) (b:genkha) (r:45.14.16/24.38.25) (q:draft)
genkhawm = (t:v) (w:talk together/converse) (d:gen, speak, with khawm, together) (e:maitang kimu-in thu ~ dingin) (s:kiho/kihokhawm) (b:gen) (r:63.1.12) (q:draft)
genkhawmin = (t:v) (w:talk together/discuss) (d:genkhawm with the linking ending in, used before a following verb) (e:Jew mite tawh zong thu ~ kisel uh) (b:genkhawm) (r:44.9.29) (q:draft)
genkhia = (t:v) (w:declare/proclaim/speak out/utter) (d:gen, say, with khia, out) (e:Vantungte in ama thumanna ~ a/Minam dangte lakah ama minthanna ~ unla | declare his glory among the nations/Ka thuakzo nawnkei a, ka ~ ta ding hi | I can bear it no longer, I will speak out/sunga thu om pen kam in a ~ hi | the mouth speaks out what is within) (s:pulak/tangko) (b:gen) (r:19.97.6/11.4.32/13.16.24/18.32.20/40.12.34) (q:draft)
genkhiat = (t:v) (w:tell/declare/speak out/pronounce) (d:gen speak with khiat, out; form of genkhia used before another word such as ding, theih or a noun) (e:a ~ thukhennate phawk un/Hih ko thu na ~ kei nak leh | if you do not tell this matter of ours/keimah phatna a ~ theih nadingun | so that they may declare my praise/zanin na thumanna ~ dingin a kilawm hi | it is fitting to declare your faithfulness at night) (b:genkhia) (r:13.16.12/6.2.14/23.43.20/19.92.1) (q:draft)
genkhiate = (t:n) (w:those who declare/those who acknowledge) (d:genkhia, declare, with the plural te: the ones who speak it out) (e:keima mi ahihna mi’ theihin a ~ | those who declare before people that they are mine) (b:genkhia) (r:42.12.8) (q:draft)
genkhiatna = (t:n) (w:proclaiming/speaking out/declaration) (d:genkhiat speak out with the noun suffix na) (e:kammal ka ~ hangin ni simin/kei’ thugen bangin a ~ uh | their declaring it as if it were my word) (s:pulakna) (b:genkhiat) (r:24.20.8/24.23.30) (q:draft)
genkhiatsawn = (t:v) (w:tell to others/pass on/relate) (d:genkhiat, speak out, with sawn, on to others) (e:Mite kiangah ~ dingin a kiphal lo) (s:gensawn) (r:47.12.4) (q:draft)
genkhin = (t:v) (w:have told/have spoken) (d:gen, tell, with khin, already or completely: the telling is finished) (e:A hun ma-in kong ~ hi/tamveipi ka hong ~ a | I have told you many times/teltakin hong ~ ahih manin | because he has told me clearly/hih thute khempeuh hong ~ ka hih manin | because I have told you all these things) (s:genzo) (b:gen) (r:41.13.23/23.24.3/50.3.18/61.1.14/53.2.5) (q:draft)
genkhit = (t:v) (w:finish saying/have said) (d:gen, say, with khit, finished, mostly in a genkhit ciangin, after he had said) (e:Hih thu a ~ ciangin/Hih thuteng a ~ ciangin mihonte a ciahsak hi | after he had said this he dismissed the crowd/hanthotna tampi a ~ ciangin Grik gamah pai | after speaking much encouragement he went to Greece/Hih thu a ~ nipikal khat bang khit ciangin | about a week after he said this) (s:cihkhit) (r:44.1.9/44.19.41/44.20.2/42.9.28) (q:draft)
genkhol = (t:v) (w:foretell/prophesy/tell beforehand) (d:gen, tell, with khol, beforehand: tell a thing before it happens, prophesy) (e:Thu khempeuh kong ~ zo hi/a siat nading thu ~ in | prophesy its destruction/giahphual ah thu a ~ uh hi | they are prophesying in the camp/hong tun’ ma-in no kiangah kong ~ hi | I tell you before it comes) (s:hilhkhol) (r:41.13.23/44.3.24/26.28.21/4.11.27/43.13.19) (q:draft)
genkholh = (t:v) (w:foretell/tell beforehand/promise) (d:form of genkhol used before a noun or in a dependent clause, what was said beforehand) (e:na ~ mah bangin/kam uh tawh a ~ mah bangin | as he foretold by their mouths/Kamsangte hong ~ thu khempeuh | all that the prophets have foretold/a kamsangte tungah a ~ bangin | as he had said through his prophets) (s:hilhkholh) (b:genkhol) (r:42.2.29/42.24.25/44.3.21/40.1.22) (q:draft)
genkholhna = (t:n) (w:prophecy/prediction/divination) (d:telling a thing beforehand) (e:mai lam thu ~ ahih kei leh/maangmuhna man lo ahi a, ~ man lo | false vision and false prediction/a piang ding nate ~ thute a zui mi | the one who keeps the words of prophecy of things to come) (s:thugenkholhna) (b:genkholh) (r:3.19.26/54.4.14/26.12.24/66.22.7) (q:draft)
genkholhnate = (t:n) (w:prophecies/predictions/visions) (d:genkholhna, a thing told beforehand, with plural te; also of warnings and threats made in advance) (e:~ a tung om lo hi/amaute daantah ding ka ~ | my warnings that I would punish them/thu ~ imcip kei in | do not seal up the words of prophecy) (b:genkholhna) (r:26.12.22/66.22.10/26.6.10) (q:draft)
genkholhsa = (t:v) (w:foretold/said beforehand) (d:genkholh, tell beforehand, with sa, already done: a genkholhsa bangin is as he had foretold) (e:Topa in a ~ bangin Babilon kumpipa in/ci-in a ~ thu ahi hi | it is what he said beforehand/ci-in ka hong ~ uh ahi hi | we told you so beforehand/a kamsangpa tungah a ~ bang a tun’ nading | to fulfil what he had foretold through the prophet) (b:genkholh) (r:12.24.12/40.21.4/45.9.29/52.3.4) (q:draft)
genkholhsakna = (t:n) (w:prophecy/foretelling) (d:genkholh, foretell, with the causative sak and the noun suffix na: what was caused to be spoken beforehand) (e:ci-in a ~ thu a tun nading) (s:genkholhna) (r:40.13.35) (q:draft)
genkholin = (t:v) (w:prophesying/foretelling) (d:genkhol with the linking suffix in; thu genkholin, prophesying) (e:amaute tawh mailam thu ~ mi tuamdang khatin/Jehoshafat langpangin thu ~ | prophesying against Jehoshaphat/laiza lasakna tawh mailam thu ~ | prophesying to the music of harps) (b:genkhol) (r:9.10.6/14.20.37/9.10.5) (q:draft)
genkholkhin = (t:v) (w:have already told beforehand/have foretold) (d:genkhol, tell beforehand, with khin, already done) (e:A hun ma-in hong ~ ka hih manin) (s:genkholzo) (b:genkhol) (r:40.24.25) (q:draft)
genkholpa = (t:n) (w:foreteller/one who foretold) (d:genkhol, foretell, with pa for a man: the one who told it beforehand) (e:thu a ~ pen keimah ka hihna) (b:genkhol) (r:23.52.6) (q:draft)
genkholzo = (t:v) (w:have foretold/have prophesied) (d:genkhol, foretell, with zo for a completed action) (e:ci-in a ~ uh hi) (s:genkholkhin) (b:genkhol) (r:24.28.8) (q:draft)
genkik = (t:v) (w:say again/speak again/repeat/report back) (d:gen with kik again; also to go on speaking) (e:Topa in Ahaz kiangah thu ~ a/Topa kiangah tua thute ~ hi | he repeated those words before the Lord/Tua ciangin Job in thu ~ a | then Job spoke again/thuman bang hiam cih na ~ theih nadingun | so that you can report back what is true) (s:cikik/genpha) (b:gen) (r:23.7.10/18.27.1/9.8.21/20.22.21) (q:draft)
genkikin = (t:see) <genkikin-ah>
genkikin-ah = (t:v) (w:say again/repeat/tell again) (d:gen, say, with kik, again, and the ending in-ah that introduces the words spoken: I say again as follows) (e:tu-in ka hong ~) (r:48.5.21) (q:draft)
genlo = (t:v) (w:not tell/not speak) (d:gen, tell, with lo, not) (e:Thuman ~ teci in daan tuak) (b:gen) (r:20.19.5) (q:draft)
genloh = (t:v) (w:not tell/not speak) (d:form of genlo used before nading: so as not to speak) (e:ka thu a ~ nadingun thu na pia uh) (b:genlo) (r:30.2.12) (q:draft)
genmun = (t:v) (w:speak often) (d:gen, speak, with mun; in the verse negated with lo, did not speak much, seldom spoke) (e:Topa in thu ~ lo a) (r:9.3.1) (q:draft, low confidence)
genna = (t:n) (w:saying/speaking/statement/testimony) (d:what is said or the act of saying it; thu genna, testimony) (e:Amau kiangah a ~ thu amaute in/Josef suan minamte’ ~ man hi | what the tribe of the descendants of Joseph says is right/thuman ~ sangin zuauna na deihzaw hi | you love falsehood rather than speaking the truth/a ~ uh khatlekhat kituak lo hi | their statements did not agree with one another) (s:thugenna/cihna) (b:gen) (r:42.2.50/5.17.6/4.36.5/19.52.3/41.14.56) (q:draft)
gennasa = (t:v) (w:told/spoken of) (d:genna with sa, already done: that has been told before, as the place God had told of) (e:~ mun amaute a) (b:genna) (r:1.22.9) (q:draft)
gennate = (t:n) (w:words/sayings/things said) (d:plural of genna; what someone has said) (e:Khuamial lakah no kiangah ka ~/kamsangte’ thu ~ um kei un | do not believe the words of the prophets/Ka ~ man hi | what I said is true/Na bil sung uhah kong ~ | what I say in your ears) (s:thugente/kammalte) (b:genna) (r:40.10.27/23.48.6/24.27.14) (q:draft)
Gennesaret = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Gennesaret) (d:fertile plain on the north-west shore of the Sea of Galilee; the Lake of Gennesaret is another name for that sea) (r:40.14.34/42.5.1)
Gennesareth = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Gennesaret) (d:spelling of Gennesaret, the plain on the north-west shore of the Sea of Galilee) (r:41.6.53)
gennop = (t:v) (w:want to say/mean) (d:gen, say, with nop, wish; gennop thu is what someone wants to say or means) (e:keima ngaihsutna ka ~ thu in/~ mahmah na neih leh hong gen in | if you have something you want to say, tell me/Tu-in ka hong ~ thu in | now what I mean is this/amaute in Jesuh’ ~ thu a theithei tuan kei | they did not understand what Jesus meant) (s:gennuam/cihnop) (r:46.7.12/43.10.6/18.33.32/48.3.17) (q:draft)
gennopna = (t:n) (w:meaning/what is meant) (d:gennop, want to say, with the noun suffix na: what one means to say) (e:pawlpi a ki-itna a ~ ahi hi) (s:cihnopna) (b:gennop) (r:49.5.32) (q:draft)
gennuam = (t:v) (w:want to say/want to tell/wish to speak) (d:gen, say, with nuam, want) (e:Bang hong ~ na hi hiam/Gentail mite tungah thu ka hong ~ hi | I want to speak to you Gentiles/Sia aw, bang hong ~ na hi hiam | Teacher, what do you want to tell me/note kiangah hong ~ ka hih manin | because I wanted to speak to you) (s:gennop/cinuam) (r:44.23.19/45.11.13/42.7.40/44.28.20) (q:draft)
genpa = (t:n) (w:speaker/teller) (d:gen, say, with pa, the man who says or speaks, as in zuau genpa, a liar, and thuman a genpa, one who tells the truth) (e:thuman a ~ na hua uh hi/zuau ~ hihna sangin mizawng hihna hoihzaw | better to be poor than a liar/hih thute a ~ in a bangci mi | what kind of man was the one who told these things/kei kiangah hong ~’ aw a za kei uh | they did not hear the voice of the one speaking to me) (s:thugenpa) (b:gen) (r:30.5.10/20.19.22/12.1.7/44.22.9) (q:draft)
genpha = (t:v) (w:say again/repeat) (d:gen say with pha: tell something that has been told before) (e:khitui tawh ka hong ~ kikkik hi/cih thute ~ sansan nawn kei ni | let us not go over these things again) (s:genkik) (r:50.3.18/58.6.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
genpih = (t:v) (w:speak to/talk with/tell) (d:gen speak with pih together with: speak to a person, talk a matter over with him) (e:amah thu ~ ding uh hi/Mi khatpeuh in thu hong ~ leh | if someone speaks a word to you/David kiangah thu tuam ~ un la | speak to David privately/sawm le nihte tawh tuamtonin thu ~ a | he took the Twelve aside and spoke to them) (s:hopih/paupih) (b:gen) (r:5.25.8/9.18.22/18.4.2/40.20.17) (q:draft)
genpihpih = (t:v) (w:keep urging/keep speaking to) (d:genpih, speak to, with pih repeated for speaking again and again) (e:Thu ka ~ uh hangin) (s:hopihpih) (b:genpih) (r:44.21.14) (q:draft)
gensa = (t:v) (w:spoken/said/promised) (d:already spoken, gen with sa marking a completed action; a gensa thu, the word spoken before) (e:David tungah na ~ thu kipsak in/Moab tawh kisai-in thu a ~ ahi hi | it is the word he spoke concerning Moab/Kong ~ thute khempeuh laibu khat sungah khum in | write in a book all the words I have spoken to you/kamsangpa Jeremiah in a ~ bangin | as the prophet Jeremiah had said/Pasian in a ~ hunin | at the time God had said) (s:cihsa) (b:gen) (r:11.8.26/40.2.17/23.16.13/24.30.2/1.21.2) (q:draft)
gensak = (t:v) (w:speak for/plead for) (d:speak on behalf of someone) (e:kumpipa kiangah kong ~ ding hi/Faro’ kiangah thu nong va ~ ding uh kong thum | I beg you to speak to Pharaoh for me/ama adingin zuauthu ~ ding na hi uh hiam | will you speak deceitfully for him) (s:thumsak) (b:gen) (r:11.2.18/18.13.8/1.50.4/18.13.7) (q:draft)
gensak = (t:v) (w:let speak/have speak) (d:allow or cause someone to speak) (e:kei thu hong ~ dih un/thu hong ~ in la, nang’ hong dawng in | let me speak, and you answer me/na nasemnu kam khat ~ in | let your servant speak a word/ama muh bangbang ~ in | have him report whatever he sees) (s:pausak) (b:gen) (r:18.13.13/1.18.32/18.13.22/10.14.12/23.21.6) (q:draft)
gensakin = (t:v) (w:let speak/have speak) (d:gensak with the linking ending in, used before a following verb) (e:Amah ~ pulaksak unla) (b:gensak) (r:23.44.7) (q:draft)
gensate = (t:n) (w:things said/words spoken) (d:gensa spoken with the plural te: what someone has said) (e:Na ~ khat beek siit kei in/a thu ~ dokkik loin | he does not take back his words/a siatna ding ka ~ ka tungsak ding a | I will bring about the disaster I have spoken) (s:gennate) (b:gensa) (r:17.6.10/23.31.2/24.39.16) (q:draft)
gensawn = (t:v) (w:pass on/relay/report/proclaim) (d:gen, say, with sawn, onward: tell to others what one has heard; mi' gensawn is what people report, hearsay) (e:tuipi gei-a omte kiangah va ~ un/note tungah ka hong ~ a | I passed it on to you/kumpipa kiangah a ~ hi | she reported it to the king/Ni dangin mi’ ~ bekin nang kong thei a | before I knew you only by what people reported) (s:hilhsawn) (r:24.31.10/46.15.3/17.2.22/18.42.5) (q:draft)
gensia = (t:v) (w:slander/speak evil of/blaspheme) (d:speak badly of someone; also grumble against) (e:a leii tawh ~ loin/A topa kiangah sila khat ~ kei in | do not slander a servant to his master/a ukpa na ~ kei ding uh hi | you must not speak evil of the ruler/Nang in kua zahko-in kua ~ na hi hiam | whom have you ridiculed and blasphemed) (s:kosia/gendai) (a:phat) (r:19.15.3/66.13.6/20.30.10/44.23.5/23.37.23) (q:draft)
gensiam = (t:v) (w:be skilled in speaking/be clever at saying) (d:gen, speak, with siam, be skilled; in the verse of one clever at saying things that belittle others) (e:thu ~ mi hi loin thuman thutak) (r:54.3.11) (q:draft)
gensiamna = (t:n) (w:skill in speaking/clever speech) (d:gensiam with the noun suffix na; zuau gensiamna is skill in telling lies) (e:Zuau ~ zangin minam dangte tawh) (b:gensiam) (r:27.11.23) (q:draft)
gensiapa = (t:n) (w:slanderer) (d:gensia, slander, with pa for a man) (e:Mi ~ leitungah kip sak kei in) (b:gensia) (r:19.140.11) (q:draft)
gensiasiate = (t:n) (w:gossips/slanderers) (d:gensia, speak evil of, with sia repeated and the plural te: those who keep speaking ill of others) (e:Mi a ~ tungah thusim kigen ngam lo) (s:gensiate/kosiate) (r:20.11.13) (q:draft)
gensiat = (t:v) (w:slander/speak evil of/speak against) (d:form of gensia used before endings such as nading and uh ciangin) (e:eite hong ~ nading thu ngah loin/i galte in hong ~ theih loh nading | so that our enemies cannot slander us/ka nasem Moses ~ ding lau lo | not afraid to speak against my servant Moses/Thukham na ~ uhleh | if you speak against the law) (s:kosiat) (b:gensia) (r:56.2.8/44.18.6/54.5.14/4.12.8/59.4.11) (q:draft)
gensiate = (t:n) (w:slanderers/those who speak evil of/blasphemers) (d:gensia with the plural te, those who speak against someone) (e:Kha Siangtho a ~ in maisak nading/kei hong ~’ tungah | on those who speak evil of me/mi a ~ in mihai ahi hi | whoever slanders people is a fool/a huaihamte, zukhamte, mi ~ | the greedy, drunkards, slanderers) (s:kosiate) (b:gensia) (r:42.12.10/19.109.20/20.10.18/46.6.10) (q:draft)
gensiatkhak = (t:v) (w:speak evil of/malign) (d:gensiat, speak evil of, with khak, come to do or happen to do) (e:thu a ~ loh nadingun numei khanghamte) (r:56.2.3) (q:draft)
gensiatna = (t:n) (w:slander/gossip/evil speaking/blasphemy) (d:speaking evil of someone; Pasian gensiatna is blasphemy) (e:~ om kei leh kitotna bei hi/mawhna leh Pasian ~ khempeuh | all sins and blasphemies against God/a thuhilhna in ~ a thuak loh nadingin | so that the teaching may not be slandered/Kei hanga note in ~, bawlsiatna | when because of me you suffer insult, persecution) (s:gendaina) (a:phatna) (b:gensiat) (r:20.26.20/41.3.28/54.6.1/40.5.11) (q:draft)
gensiatnate = (t:n) (w:slanders/evil words) (d:gensiatna with plural te: the evil things said against someone) (e:note a hong ~ uh ka thei hi/Pasian a ~ uh hangin | because of the evil things they said against God) (b:gensiatna) (r:66.2.9/65.1.15) (q:draft)
gensiatsak = (t:v) (w:cause to be slandered/bring slander on) (d:gensiat, slander, with the causative sak) (e:hong ~ lohna dingin sila khempeuh) (b:gensiat) (r:54.6.1) (q:draft)
gentaak = (t:adj) (w:worth mentioning/of account) (d:gen, speak, with taak, worthy; in the verses always negated, gentaak lo, not worth mentioning, of no account) (e:pumpi na bangmah ~ lo i sakte/mi-a ~ lote tawh | with those who are of no account as a people/Amaute a mi-in tawmin, ~ loin peemta hi uh a | when they were few in number, of no account, and strangers) (s:gentham) (r:46.12.23/5.32.21/13.16.19) (q:draft)
Gentail = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Gentile) (d:a person or people not of the Jewish nation; Gentail mi is a Gentile, Gentail pawlpite are the Gentile churches) (r:49.2.11/45.16.4)
Gentaile = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Gentiles) (d:the Gentiles, the nations other than the Jews) (b:Gentail) (r:42.22.25)
Gentailte = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Gentiles) (d:the Gentiles, all the peoples who are not Jews; Gentail with the plural te) (b:Gentail) (r:44.15.19/64.1.7)
gentawmin = (t:v) (w:make up/speak of one's own invention) (d:gen, speak, with tawm, of one's own making, and the linking ending in) (e:lungsim bangin thu ~, maangmu kineih uh) (r:26.13.3) (q:draft)
gente = (t:n) (w:words/sayings) (d:the things that someone says, as in kong gente what I say to you) (e:kong ~ mangngilh ngei kei in/Hilkiah’ tapa Jeremiah thu ~ hih bang ahi hi | these are the words of Jeremiah son of Hilkiah/~ bek keimah in ka gen ding hi | I will say only what he says) (s:thugente/gennate) (b:gen) (r:20.2.1/4.24.13/24.1.1) (q:draft)
gente = (t:n) (w:speakers/tellers) (d:those who say or tell something; thuzuau gente are liars) (e:ahi zongin thuzuau ~ lawnkhia hi/thuhoih lo a ~’ leei ki-attan ding hi | the tongue of those who speak what is not good will be cut off) (b:gen) (r:20.22.12/19.63.11/20.10.31) (q:draft)
genteh = (t:v) (w:compare/liken) (d:describe one thing by likening it to another, with tawh for the thing it is compared to) (e:bang tawh ka ~ ding hiam/Pasian Gam bang tawh ka ~ ding hiam | what shall I compare the kingdom of God to/suangkhi leh limlangte tawh ~ theih hi lo a | it cannot be compared with coral and jasper) (s:tehkak/tehpih) (r:40.11.16/42.13.20/41.4.30/18.28.18) (q:draft)
gentehin = (t:v) (w:take as an example/compare) (d:genteh with the linking ending in: using someone as an illustration) (e:keimah leh Apollos ~ kong hilh hi) (b:genteh) (r:46.4.6) (q:draft)
gentehna = (t:n) (w:example/illustration) (d:genteh, compare, with the noun suffix na: a case told as an example or illustration, also a person held up as a byword) (e:pilna a hoihna ~ a hoih khat/i theihtheih ngei ~ khat ka hong zang ding | I will use an everyday example/amau adingin ~ ka suak veve hi | I have become a byword to them/numeite in amah ~ khatin nei uh a | women held her as a byword) (s:etteh) (b:genteh) (r:21.9.13/48.3.15/19.69.11/26.23.10)
gentel = (t:v) (w:explain/expound/state clearly) (d:gen tell with tel clear, tell a matter so that it is understood) (e:Moses in hih thu ~ a/a khiatna ka ~ ding hi | I will explain its meaning/tua khuapi upate kiangah a thu ~ ding hi | he shall state his case to the elders of that city/ama tungah a ~ theih loh | that he could not explain to her/hong ~ thei khat beek om lo hi | there was not one who could explain it to me) (s:hilhtel) (r:5.1.5/14.9.2/19.49.4/6.20.4/1.41.24) (q:draft)
gentelna = (t:n) (w:explanation/clear statement) (d:gentel explain with the noun suffix na) (e:Na thute ~ in khua vaksak a/ci-in ~ om lopi-in thongkia mi khat | a prisoner without any statement of the charges/amaute kiangah ~ khat ka nei hi | I gave them an explanation) (s:hilhtelna) (b:gentel) (r:19.119.130/44.25.27/48.2.2) (q:draft)
genteng = (t:n) (w:all that is said/everything said) (d:gen, say, with teng, all: all that someone says or has said) (e:Pasian in nang tungah hong ~/na thuzuau ~ uh tawh mihoihte na lunggimsak uh | with all the lies you told you grieved the righteous/ka ~ amaute in hong genthei ding uh hi | they can tell you all that I said) (b:gen) (r:5.5.27/43.18.21/26.13.22) (q:draft)
genthaang = (t:v) (w:spread abroad/disclose/make known) (d:tell something to others so that it becomes known, of a secret) (e:thusim midang tungah ~ kei in) (s:genthang) (a:seel) (r:20.25.9) (q:draft)
gentham = (t:adj) (w:worth mentioning/of account) (d:gen say with tham worth; bangmah gentham lo is of no account at all) (e:bangmah ~ lo uh a/nangma muhna-ah bangmah ~ lo hi | it is as nothing in your sight/~ ka sa het kei hi | I do not consider it worth mentioning at all) (s:gentaak) (r:19.105.12/45.8.18/19.39.5) (q:draft)
genthang = (t:v) (w:proclaim/spread abroad/publish) (d:tell something widely so that it becomes known everywhere, of good news or of slander) (e:Ashkelon kongzing ah ~ kei in/mi khempeuhte tungah suahtakna na ~ ding uh hi | you shall proclaim liberty to all the people/a paikhiat uh ciangin ~ uh hi | when they go out they spread it around/minamte lakah ka minthan’na ~ ding uh hi | they will proclaim my glory among the nations/Jerusalem khuasung khempeuhah thu na ~ uh a | you have spread the teaching all over Jerusalem) (s:tangko/genthaang) (a:seel) (r:10.1.20/3.25.10/19.41.6/23.66.19/44.5.28) (q:draft)
genthangin = (t:v) (w:proclaim/spread abroad) (d:genthang with the linking ending in, used before a following verb) (e:a thu ~ a kizeelsak hi) (b:genthang) (r:41.1.45) (q:draft)
genthangna = (t:n) (w:proclamation/report) (d:genthang, make known by telling, with the noun suffix na: what is proclaimed or spread about) (e:tua ni mahin ~ na bawl ding uh/~ thu ka zakna in thuhoih hi lo hi | the report I hear being spread is not good) (s:taangkona) (b:genthang) (r:3.23.21/9.2.24) (q:draft)
genthei = (t:adj) (w:distressed/afflicted/miserable/poor) (d:suffering hardship or anguish, often paired with cimawh, needy) (e:~ ka hih manin kei hong hehpih/kei ~-in ka cimawh a | I am poor and needy/galte khempeuh zahhuai in ~ mahmah ding uh hi | all my enemies will be ashamed and greatly distressed) (s:cimawh/zawng) (r:19.31.9/19.109.22/19.6.10) (q:draft)
genthei = (t:v) (w:can tell/be able to say) (d:gen, tell, with thei, be able) (e:nang kiangah hong ~ ding uh hi/a gennop nak-uhleh hong ~ ding uh hi | they can tell you if they are willing/bangci-in thuhoih ~ mah ding na hi uh hiam | how can you say anything good/ka genteng amaute in hong ~ ding uh hi | they can tell you all that I said) (s:cihthei) (b:gen) (r:9.25.8/44.26.5/40.12.34/43.18.21) (q:draft)
gentheih = (t:v) (w:be able to tell/be able to say/can be told) (d:gen tell with theih can; gentheih loh is beyond telling) (e:Lungdamna Thu na ~ nading uh hunhoih/Na sepnate khempeuh ka ~ nadingin | so that I may tell of all your deeds/cih bangin kuama ~ hi lo hi | no one can say/bang hiam cih nong ~ kei uhleh | if you cannot tell me what it is) (s:genzawh) (b:gen) (r:42.21.13/28.9.9/19.73.28/42.17.21/7.14.13) (q:draft)
gentheih = (t:v) (w:suffer/be in trouble/be in distress) (d:form of genthei used before hun and na; ka gentheih hunin, in my time of trouble) (e:ka ~ hunin keima belh na hi hi) (b:genthei) (r:19.59.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
gentheihna = (t:n) (w:misery/hardship/suffering/distress) (d:genthei, distressed, with the noun suffix na: a state of misery, hardship or affliction) (e:~ thuak se loin si hiat uh hi/lunggimna leh ~ thonginn sungah | in a prison of bitterness and hardship/ka ~ hangin ka tha kiam a | my strength fails because of my affliction/Israelte’ ~-ah amah dah hi | he was grieved at the misery of Israel) (s:haksatna/gimna/cihmawhna) (a:nopsakna) (b:gentheih) (r:18.21.13/7.10.16/25.3.5/19.31.10) (q:draft)
gentheisak = (t:v) (w:afflict/cause distress/make suffer) (d:genthei distressed with sak, cause) (e:na pumpi uh ~ kei un) (s:gimsak) (b:genthei) (r:21.11.10) (q:draft)
gentheite = (t:n) (w:the poor/the weak/the afflicted) (d:genthei, distressed, with the plural te) (e:Mi ~ a khual mi in thupha) (s:cimawhte/mizawngte) (a:haute) (b:genthei) (r:19.41.1) (q:draft)
genthuah = (t:v) (w:add/say further/say more) (d:add to what has been said) (e:amah in bangmah ~ lo hi/Uliante in mite kiangah thu ~ lai-in | the officers shall say further to the people/nang tungah bang ~ nawn ding ahi hiam | what more can he say to you/bangmah ~ ding nei lo uh hi | they had nothing to add) (s:genbeh/cithuah) (r:5.5.22/43.6.65/5.20.8/10.7.20/48.2.6) (q:draft)
