giahpih = (t:v) (w:stay the night with/camp out with) (d:giah, stay the night, with pih, together with: of shepherds staying out at night with their flocks) (e:a tuuhonte a ~ tuucing pawlkhat) (b:giah) (r:42.2.8) (q:draft)
giak = (t:v) (w:spend the night/lodge/stay overnight) (d:stay somewhere for the night, as a traveller or a guest; the form giah is used before nading and in giahphual, camp) (e:leenggui lo-ah va ~ ni/tua nu kiangah a ~ dingin amah pai hi | he went in to spend the night with her/gam sungah ka ~ ding hi | I would stay in the wilderness/Oliv kici mualah a ~ hi | he spent the night on the hill called Olives/kongzingah ~ kei hamtang in | only do not spend the night in the square) (s:giah/taam/zintun) (r:22.7.11/1.32.21/7.16.1/19.55.7/42.21.37/7.19.20) (q:draft)
giakin = (t:v) (w:spend the night/stay overnight) (d:giak, spend the night, with the linking ending in, used before a following verb: staying out at night) (e:gam lakah ~ amau tuu honte) (b:giak) (r:42.2.8) (q:draft)
giakkhawm = (t:v) (w:stay the night together/lodge with) (d:giak, spend the night, with khawm, together: stay the night with someone as a guest) (e:Kote tawh hong ~ in/amaute tawh ~ dingin inn sungah a lut hi | he went into the house to stay the night with them/an ne, tui dawnin ~ uh hi | they ate, drank and stayed the night together/amah tawh a ~ dingin Peter in amaute a sam | Peter invited them to stay the night with him) (b:giak) (r:42.24.29/7.19.4/44.10.23) (q:draft)
gial = (t:adj) (w:speckled/spotted/streaked/dappled) (d:of an animal, marked with spots or stripes of another colour; a dung gial is streaked, and a bem gial is spotted) (e:a lina, sakol ~ in kai hi/tuuhon khempeuh in a ~ ta nei hi | all the flocks bore speckled young/sakol dang a san, a ~, a kang om | there were other horses, red, dappled and white/tuu a puang leh a ~ khempeuh | every speckled and spotted sheep) (s:puang/gialbem) (r:38.6.3/1.30.39/1.31.8/38.1.8/1.30.32) (q:draft)
gial = (t:n) (w:hail/hailstone) (d:frozen rain that falls as balls of ice; gialpi is heavy hail) (e:mei leh ~, tuikhal leh vuuk/a leengguite uh ~ tawh denggawp a | he struck down their vines with hail/~ a kikholna mun va mu ngei | have you seen the storehouses of the hail/sisan tawh kihel ~ leh mei leitungah kia-in | hail and fire mixed with blood fell on the earth) (s:gialpi) (r:19.148.8/23.32.19/19.78.47/18.38.22/66.8.7) (q:draft)
gialbem = (t:adj) (w:spotted/speckled) (d:gial spotted with bem round: marked with round spots; kamkei gialbem is the leopard) (e:kamkei ~ pen keelno tawh) (s:puang) (r:23.11.6) (q:draft)
gialheek = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:poplar/willow) (d:a tree that grows beside streams, usually with kung, tree; also written gialhek) (e:lui gei-a ~ kungte in/lui tui luang gei-a a om ~ kungte bangin | like poplar trees beside flowing streams) (s:gialhek) (r:18.40.22/23.44.4) (q:draft)
