gialpite = (t:n) (w:hailstones) (d:gialpi, large hail, with the plural te: hailstones) (e:~ in tua kulh kha-in) (b:gialpi) (r:26.13.11) (q:draft)
gialte = (t:adj) (w:speckled/streaked/dappled) (d:plural form of gial, animals with a marked or patterned coat, a dung gialte are the streaked ones) (e:sakol ~ leitaw lam/A dung ~ na thaman hi ding hi | the streaked ones shall be your wages/keeltal a dung gial leh a bem ~ | the male goats that were streaked and spotted) (b:gial) (r:38.6.6/1.31.8/1.30.35) (q:draft)
giat = (t:num) (w:eight) (d:the number eight; a ni giat ni is the eighth day, and sawm leh giat is eighteen) (e:ni ~/A ni ~ ni-in a naungek vun dawn ki-at ding | on the eighth day the foreskin of the baby is to be cut/kum sawm leh kum ~ sung | for eighteen years) (r:1.17.12/3.12.3/7.3.14)
giatna = (t:num) (w:eighth) (d:giat, eight, with the ordinal ending na; sawm-le-giatna is eighteenth) (e:a ~ Abijah tung/Peullethai a ~ ahi hi | Peullethai was the eighth/a kha ~ adingin | for the eighth month/a sawm-le-~ Happizzez tung | the eighteenth fell to Happizzez) (b:giat) (r:13.24.10/13.12.12/13.26.5/13.27.11/13.24.15) (q:draft)
giatte = (t:num) (w:the eight/eight) (d:giat, eight, with plural -te: the eight persons or things; also ends larger numbers such as sawm-le-giatte, the eighteen) (e:hih mihing ~ nei hi/mi ~ tui tawh a gup nading teembaw | the ark in which eight people were saved through water/a delhlup mi sawm leh ~ | the eighteen people it crushed) (b:giat) (r:1.22.23/42.13.4/60.3.20) (q:draft)
