giksak = (t:v) (w:make heavy/make heavier) (d:gik, heavy, with the causative sak: make a load or yoke heavy) (e:Ka pa in na hakkol uh ~ hi/Na pa in ka hakkol uh ~ hi | your father made our yoke heavy/Ka pa in note’ hakkol ~ hi | my father made your yoke heavy/khangham mite tungah na hakkol na ~ mahmah hi | on the aged you made your yoke very heavy) (a:zangsak) (b:gik) (r:14.10.14/23.47.6/14.10.10/11.12.14) (q:draft)
gikzah = (t:n) (w:weight) (d:gik, heavy, with zah, amount: how much something weighs) (e:sumngo a ~ kithei zo lo hi/a kizang a ~ tawh kizui-in | according to the weight in use) (s:gihna) (r:14.4.18/1.23.16) (q:draft)
gikzaw = (t:adj) (w:heavier) (d:gik, heavy, with the comparative zaw; the thing compared takes sangin, than) (e:Tuipi sehnel khempeuh sangin ~ ding/mihaite’ pian’sak lungkhamna ~ lai hi | the vexation a fool causes is heavier still) (a:zangzaw) (b:gik) (r:18.6.3/20.27.3) (q:draft)
gil = (t:n) (w:belly/stomach/womb) (d:the belly or stomach, and also the womb; gil sungah is inside the belly, and gil kial is be hungry) (e:a ~ sungah a kha mahmah an/ngapi’ ~ sungah ni thum a om | was three days in the belly of the great fish/a ~ sungah tapeeng om hi | there were twins in her womb/ka ~ sunga om naungeek | the baby in my womb) (s:gilsung) (r:18.20.14/40.12.40/1.25.24/42.1.44)
