gilvah = (t:v) (w:be full/be satisfied/be well fed) (d:have eaten enough, the opposite of gilkial be hungry) (e:amaute in ne-in ~ uh hi/hong pai-in ne-in a ~ ding uh hi | they will come and eat and be satisfied/Tuhunin a ~ note in | you who are well fed now/kham theih zu ne-in ~ ni | let us drink our fill of strong drink) (s:vah) (a:gilkial) (r:19.78.29/20.27.7/5.14.29/42.6.25/23.56.12) (q:draft)
