Gitlohna = (t:n) (w:wickedness/evil) (d:gitlohna written with a capital at the start of a sentence or a line of verse) (e:~ thu na mudah hi/~ thu tam ding ahih manin | because wickedness will increase/~ in lungmuan’na piangsak lo a | wickedness does not bring security/~ na lel kei un | do not be overcome by evil) (b:gitlohna) (r:58.1.9/40.24.12/20.12.3/45.12.21) (q:draft)
gitlohnate = (t:n) (w:wicked deeds/evil ways/sins) (d:gitlohna, wickedness, with the plural te: the wicked things a person does) (e:a ~ uh panin kihei ta uh hen/na ~ uh sungah si-in na om | you were dead in your wicked deeds/a ~ a bei matengin zong in | search out his wicked deeds until none are left/a ngaihsutsa uh ~ semkhia uh hi | they carry out the evil they have planned) (s:gilohnate/hoihlohnate) (b:gitlohna) (r:32.3.8/66.18.5/49.2.1/19.10.15/33.2.1) (q:draft)
gitna = (t:n) (w:goodness/kindness) (d:goodness or kindness shown in what one does, the opposite of gitlohna, wickedness; gitna bawl is do good) (e:Gitlohna peelin, ~ bawl hen/amah in ama ~ hong lakin | he has shown his kindness/lungduaina, mi hehpihna, ~, diktatna | patience, kindness, goodness, faithfulness) (s:migitna/phatna) (a:gitlohna) (b:git) (r:60.3.11/48.5.22/44.14.17) (q:draft)
gitnat = (t:adj) (w:good/sound) (d:form used before lohna; gitnat lohna in the verse is failure or loss) (e:~ lohna pen Gentail) (b:gitna) (r:45.11.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
gitta = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:sparrow) (d:a small bird of little value, sold cheaply in the market) (e:~ tampi sangin na manpha zaw uh hi/tua ~ khat beek lei tungah kia mawk lo | not one of those sparrows falls to the ground/Pasian in ~ khat beek mangngilh lo hi | God does not forget even one sparrow) (s:kawlgit) (r:40.10.31/40.10.29/42.12.6) (q:draft)
Gittaim = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Gittaim) (d:town in Benjamin to which the people of Beeroth fled, lived in again after the exile) (r:10.4.3/16.11.33)
gittate = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:sparrows) (d:gitta with the plural te) (e:tua ~ khat nangawn lei-ah) (b:gitta) (r:40.10.29) (q:draft)
giugiau = (t:adv) (w:intently/steadily) (d:placed after a verb for an action kept up steadily or intently: en giugiau, keep watching, phawk giugiau, keep in mind) (e:ka phawk ~ thu khat in/hong en ~ uh a | they kept watching me) (r:25.3.21/38.11.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
Gizon = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Gizon) (d:home of Hashem, one of the mighty warriors of David, called the Gizonite in the NIV) (r:13.11.34)
go = (t:v) (w:slaughter/kill/butcher) (d:kill an animal for food or for sacrifice) (e:keel khat ~ uh a/nangmah in bawngtal na ~ ding hi | you shall slaughter the bull/leibeel sungah a vasa khat ~ ding a | he shall kill one bird in a clay pot/khialhna hanga biakna bawngno ~ hi | he slaughtered the calf of the sin offering) (s:gawh) (r:1.37.31/2.29.11/3.14.50/3.9.8) (q:draft)
Goah = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Goah) (d:place near Jerusalem, named with the hill of Gareb in the prophecy of the rebuilt city) (r:24.31.39)
Gob = (t:see) <Gob-ah>
Gob-ah = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Gob) (d:the place name Gob with the marker ah, at Gob: a place where Israel fought the Philistines in the time of David) (e:Filistiate tawh ~ gal kidona om kik hi) (r:10.21.18/10.21.19) (q:draft)
Gog = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Gog) (d:name of two men: the ruler of Meshek and Tubal from the land of Magog in the prophecy of Ezekiel, and a descendant of Joel in the tribe of Reuben) (e:Tubal minamte a ukpipa ~ aw) (r:26.38.3/13.5.4) (q:draft)
Goi = (t:see) <Goi-im>
Goi-im = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Goyim) (d:kingdom of King Tidal, an ally of Kedorlaomer in the time of Abraham; also a kingdom defeated by Joshua; the name means nations) (e:~ kumpipa Tidal, Shinar kumpipa Amrafel) (r:1.14.9/1.14.1) (q:draft)
goih = (t:v) (w:miss/long for) (d:feel the absence of someone or something and long for them) (e:nakpitakin ka hong ~ hi/zong a ~ beek kei ding uh hi | they will not even miss it) (r:50.4.1/24.3.16) (q:draft)
goiim = (t:see) <ha-goiim>
Goiim = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Goyim) (d:spelling of Goyim without the hyphen, the kingdom of King Tidal in the time of Abraham) (r:1.14.1)
goin = (t:v) (w:slaughtering/killing) (d:go, slaughter an animal, with the linking ending -in before the next verb) (e:Moses in ~ a si tawmkhat la-in/tuu thaute ~ a sa na ne uh | you slaughter the fat sheep and eat the meat/a tanote uh ~ beel sungah a huan | they killed their children and cooked them in a pot/Paisan Pawi bawlna ganhing ~ nomau mah kisian’suah un | slaughter the Passover animals and consecrate yourselves) (b:go) (r:3.8.23/26.34.3/25.4.10/14.35.6) (q:draft)
gokhawm = (t:v) (w:slaughter together/kill together) (d:go slaughter with khawm together: kill two animals at the same time) (e:ni khat sungin na ~ kei ding) (b:go) (r:3.22.28) (q:draft)
gol = (t:adj) (w:big/large/thick) (d:big, large or thick in size; gol zaw is bigger and a gol mahmah is very big) (e:ankung khempeuh sangin ~ zaw a/tua suang in a ~ mahmah suang ahi hi | that stone was a very large stone/ka pa’ kawng sangin ~ zaw hi | it is thicker than the waist of my father/hiang ~ a meeng thei hi | it can put out big branches) (s:lian/lianpi) (a:neu) (r:41.4.32/11.12.10/41.16.4) (q:draft)
gol = (t:v) (w:grow up/grow big/grow) (d:become big: of a child, grow up; of a tree, grow large; gol sak is make or let grow) (e:Naupang a ~ ciangin ni khat/tapa Shelah a ~ mateng | until son Shelah grows up/khangkhangin ~ semsema, vantung dong banto | it grew bigger and bigger until it reached the sky/gamlak singte lakah khang sakin ~ sak hi | he lets it grow big among the trees of the forest) (s:khangto) (r:12.4.18/1.38.11/27.4.11/23.44.14) (q:draft)
Golan = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Golan) (d:city in Bashan in the territory of Manasseh, a city of refuge east of the Jordan given to the Levites) (r:5.4.43/13.6.71)
golbel = (t:adj) (w:greatest/biggest) (d:gol, big, with bel, most) (e:a neubel akipan a ~ dongin) (s:golpen/lianbel/lianpen) (a:neubel) (r:58.8.11) (q:draft)
Golgotha = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Golgotha) (d:place outside Jerusalem where Jesus was crucified; the name means the place of the skull) (r:40.27.33/41.15.22)
golhguk = (t:n) (w:bribe) (d:money or a gift given in secret to win someone over; golhguk pia is give a bribe, golhguk la is take a bribe) (e:zum nasemte ~ pia uh hi/thutangte’ lang ah ~ a la lo mi | one who takes no bribe against the innocent/a khut taklam uh ~ tawh a kidimte | those whose right hands are full of bribes/tua bangin thugen dingin ~ a na pia | they had given him a bribe to speak so) (s:sumgolh) (r:15.4.5/19.15.5/19.26.9/16.6.12) (q:draft)
Goliath = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Goliath) (d:Philistine giant from Gath whom David killed with a sling and a stone) (r:9.17.4)
golin = (t:adj) (w:large/big/thick) (d:gol with the linking suffix in, followed by a second description or a verb; a golin ka is open wide) (e:tua hai ~ thuk mahmah hi/hiangte zong ~ sau mahmah hi | its branches too were big and very long/a khate ~ a mul a pha mahmah | with big wings and very thick feathers/Na kam uh a ~ ka un | open your mouths wide) (s:lianin) (b:gol) (r:26.23.32/26.31.5/26.17.7/19.81.10) (q:draft)
golna = (t:n) (w:size/measurement) (d:gol, be big, with the noun suffix na: how big a thing is, its size or measurements) (e:a vekpi-in a ~ kikim hi/galvilna inndei neute pen a ~ kikim a | the guard rooms were all the same size/Biakna-tau ~ pen hih bang hi ding hi | these shall be the measurements of the altar/a ~ leh a neuna tawh kizui-in | according to how large or small they are) (a:neuna) (b:gol) (r:26.46.22/26.43.13/26.40.10/16.12.44) (q:draft)
golpen = (t:adj) (w:greatest/largest/biggest) (d:gol, big, with pen, most; a golpen pan a neupen dong means from the greatest to the least) (e:khaikung khempeuh lakah a ~ pawl/a ~ pana kipan a neupen dongin | from the greatest to the least/a khankhit ciangin ankung lakah a ~ suak | when it has grown it becomes the largest of the plants) (s:golbel/lianpen/lianbel) (a:neupen) (b:gol) (r:41.4.32/32.3.5/40.13.32) (q:draft)
golpi = (t:adj) (w:large) (d:gol, big, with pi, great: very large, said of things such as a river, a tree, an image or a chain) (e:gun ~ ahi Eufrates gun/ankam tang hong khangin kung ~ hong suak a | the mustard seed grew and became a large tree/milim ~ khat bawlsak a | he had a large image made/sikkhau khainiang ~ khat a tawi ka mu hi | I saw him holding a great chain) (s:lianpi) (a:neu) (r:5.1.7/42.13.19/27.3.1/66.20.1) as in objects
golpi = (t:adj) (w:great) (d:very large, said of living creatures such as sea monsters and beasts) (e:tuipi ganhing ~ Rahab thatlum hi/sa ~ li hong pusuakto uh hi | four great beasts came up/ganhing ~ ngaihsun dih in | consider the great beast/ganhing ~ Rahab na sugawp a | you crushed the great beast Rahab) (s:lianpi) (r:18.26.12/19.89.10/27.7.3/18.40.15) as in creatures
golpite = (t:adj) (w:large) (b:golpi) as in objects, plural form of <golpi>
golpite = (t:adj) (w:great) (e:tuipi ganhing ~ leh amau nam ciatin/taaksing kungte lakah vasa ~ in bu tom uh hi | the large birds nest among the juniper trees/tua munah kalaoh-vasa ~ teengin | the great owls will live there) (b:golpi) (r:1.1.21/19.104.17/23.13.21) as in creatures, plural form of <golpi>
golsak = (t:v) (w:enlarge/make big/let grow big) (d:gol, big, with the causative sak: make something big or let it grow big) (e:Bang cia-in ~ ding cih kua in seh/na mitte zemin na ~ hangin | though you paint your eyes and make them look large/gamlak singte lakah khangsakin ~ hi | he lets it grow big among the trees of the forest) (b:gol) (r:18.38.5/24.4.30/23.44.14) (q:draft)
golzaw = (t:adj) (w:bigger/larger/greater) (d:gol big with zaw more; inndei golzaw, the larger room, renders portico) (e:liatna in leitung sangin ~ a/a hong piapa in khialhna ~ a nei hi | the one who handed me over has the greater sin/Hih inndei ~ a teh ciangin tong giat | when he measured this larger room it was eight cubits/a ~ ukna za a pia hi | he gave them a higher office of rule) (s:lianzaw) (a:neuzaw) (b:gol) (r:18.11.9/26.40.8/43.19.11/27.3.30) (q:draft)
golzawte = (t:n) (w:greater ones/older ones/bigger ones) (d:golzaw bigger with the plural te; the greater among a group, and of sons the older ones) (e:a tapa ~ khempeuh that khin uh hi/a ~ in tulkhat val uk uh hi | the greater ones commanded over a thousand) (s:lianzawte) (a:neuzawte) (b:golzaw) (r:14.22.1/13.12.14) (q:draft)
