Gommorahte = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Gomorrah) (d:Gomorrah with the plural te, spelled with a double m in this verse: Sodom and Gomorrah named together as cities) (r:1.14.11)
Gomorrah = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Gomorrah) (d:city of the plain near the Dead Sea, destroyed together with Sodom by burning sulfur for its wickedness) (r:1.19.24)
gong = (t:n) (w:mouth/opening) (d:the mouth or opening of a sack, a well, a cave or a vessel) (e:tuikhuk ~ panin suang a kikhuk mateng/tuikhuk ~ tungah phah a | she spread it over the mouth of the well/amau’ sum ciat a van ~ ciatah koih in | put the money of each man in the mouth of his sack) (r:1.29.8/6.10.18/10.17.19/1.44.1) (q:draft)
gongah = (t:n) (w:in the mouth/at the opening) (d:gong, the mouth or opening of a sack, cave or vessel, with the place ending -ah) (e:a van ~ a sum mu hi/suangtum lianpite leihawm ~ koih uh hi | they put large stones at the mouth of the cave/ka van ~ na om | it is in the mouth of my sack/A ~ lim kigelhte om hi | there were engravings around its opening) (b:gong) (r:1.42.27/6.10.27/1.42.28/11.7.31) (q:draft)
gongbakte = (t:n) (w:pitchers/jars/flagons) (d:found only in thawl gongbakte, the vessels used for pouring out drink offerings) (e:tuibuahna thawl ~ koih ding uh hi/tuiphih nadingin a thawl ~ leh a kung-ukte | its pitchers and bowls for pouring out offerings/thawl ~ kham citak tawh bawl hi | he made the pitchers of pure gold) (r:4.4.7/2.25.29/2.37.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
gopa = (t:n) (w:one who slaughters/sacrificer) (d:go slaughter with pa, the man who does it; a gopa, he who slaughters an animal for sacrifice) (e:bawngtal a ~ in mihing zong that hi/tuuno a ~ in ui ngawng zong tan hi | he who slaughters a lamb also breaks the neck of a dog) (b:go) (r:23.66.3) (q:draft)
