Grikte = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Greeks) (d:Grik with the plural te: the Greeks) (b:Grik) (r:44.17.4)
gu = (t:v) (w:steal/kidnap) (d:take what belongs to another; of a person, kidnap) (e:Na na ~ kei ding hi/Rachel in a pa’ inn sung pasiante ~ hi | Rachel stole the household gods of her father/bang hangin ka pasiante ~ na hi hiam | why did you steal my gods/Mi khat ~ a, amah in a zuak | whoever kidnaps a person and sells him) (r:2.20.15/5.5.19/1.31.19/1.31.30/2.21.16) (q:draft)
gu = (t:n) (w:poison/venom) (d:the poison of a snake; gu nei and gu-pha describe a venomous snake) (e:amau’ leenggahzu in gulpi ~ leh/gulpi’ ~ bang ~ nei uh a | they have venom like the venom of a snake/gul ~ nei bangin hong tu ding hi | it will bite like a venomous snake/mite lakah gul ~-phate khah a | he sent venomous snakes among the people/~ a nei gulte ka sawl ding hi | I will send venomous snakes) (s:gulgu) (r:5.32.33/4.21.6/19.58.4/20.23.32/5.32.24) (q:draft)
guah = (t:n) (w:rain) (d:water that falls from the sky; guah zu is rain falls and guah zusak is send rain) (e:zan sawmli sung leitungah ~ zu hi/Amah in leitungah ~ zusak a | he sends rain on the earth/Leilu lam huih in ~ a zuksak bangin | as the north wind brings rain/~ nunung hong zu lo hi | the late rain has not fallen) (s:guahtui/guahzu) (r:1.7.12/18.5.10/20.25.23/24.3.3)
guahciin = (t:n) (w:dripping rain/leak) (d:guah, rain, as its first part: rain that keeps dripping through a leaky roof) (e:a theu thei lo ~ tawh kibang hi/theu hun mel a nei lo ~ tawh kibang hi | is like a dripping rain that never stops) (r:20.19.13/20.27.15) (q:draft)
guahin = (t:n) (w:rain/as rain) (d:guah rain with the marker in: the rain as that which falls, with the verb zu fall) (e:leitungah ~ hong zusuk a/tuinakah ~ zu a | it falls as rain at the source) (b:guah) (r:21.11.3/21.1.7) (q:draft)
guahmal = (t:n) (w:raindrop/rain) (d:guah rain with mal, a single one: drops of rain) (e:~ bangin zu-in) (r:5.32.2) (q:draft)
guahpi = (t:n) (w:heavy rain/downpour/rainstorm) (d:guah rain with pi great) (e:Tu-in ~ ka zusak ding a/~ huging om hi | there is the sound of heavy rain/Leitaw lam pan ~ hong zu a | heavy rain comes from the south/huihpi ~ panin bukna leh belhna hi ding | it will be a shelter and refuge from storm and rain) (b:guah) (r:26.13.11/18.37.9/11.18.41/23.4.6) (q:draft)
guahte = (t:n) (w:rains/rain) (d:guah, rain, with the plural te: the rains) (e:vantung pan-a ~ kikhawlsak hi/~ tang dingin leivui leh sehnel hong zusak ding hi | he will send down dust and sand in place of rain) (b:guah) (r:1.8.2/5.28.24) (q:draft)
guahtui = (t:n) (w:rain/rainwater/shower) (d:guah rain and tui water) (e:~ tawh na nipsak a/tua tuite ~-in a bawl hi | he makes those waters into rain/hong zu ~ in amaute kawt ciimsak a | the falling rain drenches them/thupha ~ ka zusak ding hi | I will send down showers of blessing) (s:guah/guahzu) (r:19.65.10/18.36.27/18.24.8/26.34.26) (q:draft)
guahtuite = (t:n) (w:rains/showers) (d:guahtui with the plural te) (e:A tungah a kia ~ hupin) (s:guahte) (b:guahtui) (r:58.6.7) (q:draft)
guahzu = (t:n) (w:rain/shower) (d:guah, rain, and zu, fall: falling rain) (e:lei a kawtsak ~ tawh kibang/an lak hun-a ~ bangin | like rain at harvest time/lo-a ante a susia gawp ~ tawh kibang hi | is like a driving rain that destroys the crops in the field/ankung tunga ~ bang ta hen | let it be like rain on the plants) (s:guah/guahtui) (r:19.72.6/19.84.6/20.26.1/20.28.3/5.32.2) (q:draft)
guahzu = (t:v) (w:rain) (d:of rain, to fall) (e:Phalbi veng ta a, ~ nawn lo hi/Tua gam sungah ~ lo ahih manin | because no rain fell in that land) (r:22.2.11/11.17.7) (q:draft)
guahzuk = (t:n) (w:rain/rainfall) (d:the falling of rain; form of guahzu used before nading and before nouns) (e:Kua in ~ nading tuilam bawlsak a/~ nadingin khuaphialepte bawl a | he makes lightning for the rain/~ laitak zong ahi hi | it is also the rainy season/~ loh nadingin vantung khak theihna | power to shut the sky so that no rain falls) (b:guahzu) (r:18.38.25/19.135.7/15.10.13/66.11.6) (q:draft)
guahzukna = (t:n) (w:rainfall/falling of rain) (d:guahzuk with the noun suffix na) (e:Kua in ~ ding tui lampi bawlsak a) (b:guahzuk) (r:18.38.25) (q:draft)
guahzusak = (t:v) (w:make rain fall/send rain) (d:guahzu, rain, with the causative sak) (e:mihing khempeuh adingin ~ hi) (b:guahzu) (r:18.36.28) (q:draft)
guai = (t:v) (w:hire/pay/bribe) (d:engage or win someone over with money or gifts) (e:Dangka-in kong ~ ding uh hi/bangzahin nong ~ ding uh hiam | how much will you pay me/mun khempeuh panin mi na ~ zaw hi | you rather hire men from everywhere) (s:cial) (r:42.22.5/26.16.33/40.26.15) (q:draft)
guaih = (t:v) (w:pay/hire) (d:form of guai used before words such as ding and hangin: pay someone or engage them with money) (e:sum tawh ~ dingin thuciam/a neihsa tengin zatote a ~ hangin | though she paid the doctors with all she had) (b:guai) (r:42.22.5/42.8.43) (q:draft)
guaihna = (t:n) (w:payment/hire/fee) (d:guaih pay or hire with the noun suffix na; in the verses, money paid to win a lover) (e:Nang tungah sum tawh ~ hong kipia loin/pasalte sum tawh na ~ kong khawlsak ding hi | I will put a stop to your paying men with money) (b:guaih) (r:26.16.34/26.16.41) (q:draft, low confidence)
guaizaw = (t:v) (w:hire instead/bribe rather) (d:guai, hire or bribe, with zaw, rather) (e:mun khempeuh panin mi na ~ hi) (b:guai) (r:26.16.33) (q:draft)
guak = (t:v) (w:uncover)
guak = (t:adj) (w:only) (d:no more than, placed after the word it limits: khat guak is only one) (e:teci khat ~ kicing lo ding | only one witness is not enough/mittang khat ~ tawh nuntakna sungah na tum | you enter life with only one eye/ka ciangkhut ~ tawh hih Jordan ka kantan hi | I crossed this Jordan with only my staff/nasepna-za khat ~ a neih loh uh | they do not have only one function) (r:5.19.15/40.18.9/1.32.10/45.12.4)
guak = (t:adj) (w:alone) (d:by oneself, with no one else; follows a pronoun or a name, as amah guak, he alone) (e:Mipa amah ~ a om ding hoih lo/Jakob amah ~ bek om lai hi | Jacob was left all alone/nang ~ hong hi a, kuamah tawh hong pai lo | you come alone and no one comes with you/mual tungah amah ~ a kahto kik hi | he went up the mountain again by himself) (s:guakbek/khatguak) (r:1.2.18/1.32.24/9.21.1/43.6.15)
guak = (t:adv) (w:just) (d:merely, no more than: kei guak hi lo is not just I) (e:kei ~ hi lo, Gentail pawlpite khempeuh in | not just I but all the Gentile churches/Keima thu ~ tawh ka hihtheih bangmah om lo hi | just by myself I can do nothing) (r:45.16.4/43.5.30)
guak = (t:adv) (w:solo/single-handed) (d:doing something by oneself, without the help of others) (e:midang khat amah ~ hong tai | another man comes running alone/keimah ~ in leenggah cil bangin minamte ka cil hi | I alone have trodden the nations like grapes/Kei ~ in hih mite khempeuh ka si zo kei | I cannot carry all these people by myself) (r:10.18.26/23.63.3/4.11.14)
guak = (t:adj) (w:naked) (d:without clothes; pum guak and ci guak are the naked body) (e:~tang/Na pum ~-a a om kimlai | while your body was naked/gilkialna leh dangtakna, pum ~-a omna | hunger and thirst and nakedness/A ci ~-a a omna uh a tuam dingin | to cover their naked bodies) (s:guaktang/tangguak) (r:26.16.8/5.28.48/2.28.42)
guak = (t:adj) (w:bare/empty) (d:with nothing on it or in it: khe guak is barefoot, khut guak is with bare or empty hands, guh guak is bare bones) (e:khe ~ leh guaktangin ka vak ding/a khut ~ tawh humpinelkai balzan hi | he tore the lion apart with his bare hands/khe ~ leh lu tuamsa-in a pai kawmin kap hi | he wept as he went barefoot with his head covered/khut ~ tawh a ciahsak uh hi | they sent him away empty-handed/a guh ~ bekin om hi | he is nothing but bare bones) (r:33.1.8/7.14.6/10.15.30/41.12.3/18.33.21)
guakbek = (t:adj) (w:alone/lonely/by oneself) (d:guak alone with bek only: all alone) (e:Khuamial ciangin Jesuh ~ gamlakah om a/kei ~ hi-in gimna ka thuak hi | I am lonely and suffer affliction) (s:khatguak) (r:40.14.23/19.25.16) (q:draft)
guakin = (t:adv) (w:alone/only/empty) (d:guak with in: by oneself, with nothing else, as amah guakin he alone, guh guakin only bones, khut hawm guakin empty-handed) (e:lei tungah amah ~ a om hi/khut hawm ~ na paisak kei ding hi | you shall not send him away empty-handed/Amah ~ hong pai ahih leh | if he comes alone/amah ~ paikhia ding hi | he shall go out alone) (b:guak) (r:41.6.47/5.15.13/2.21.3/2.21.4) (q:draft)
guakkik = (t:v) (w:return empty/come back empty) (d:guak bare or empty with kik back: come back with nothing done, said of a bow and a sword in battle) (e:namsau zong hong ~ lo hi/Jonathan’ thaltang ~ lo a | the arrow of Jonathan did not come back empty) (b:guak) (r:10.1.22) (q:draft)
guaksuak = (t:v) (w:be put to shame/be left empty) (d:guak, bare or empty, with suak, become: come away with nothing, be disappointed; with sak, strip bare) (e:Nangmah hong muang uh a, ~ lo uh hi/Esau’ suan le khakte khempeuh ka ~ sak a | I strip all the descendants of Esau bare) (r:19.22.5/24.49.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
guaksuaksak = (t:v) (w:strip bare/send away empty/disappoint) (d:guaksuak with the causative sak: leave someone bare or with nothing) (e:meigong numeite ka ~ ngei kei hi/Esau’ suanlekhakte khempeuh ka ~ a | I strip all the descendants of Esau bare) (b:guaksuak) (r:18.31.16/24.49.10) (q:draft)
guaktang = (t:adj) (w:naked) (d:without clothes; guaktang-in om is be naked, and guaktang omna is nakedness) (e:ahi zongin ~-in na om hi/a pa uh’ ~ omna khuh uh hi | they covered the nakedness of their father/~ mahin i ciahkik hi | naked we go back/a ~ in om ahih manin a maizum hi | she is ashamed because she is naked) (s:tangguak) (b:guak) (r:26.16.7/14.28.15/1.9.23/21.5.15/25.1.8)
Guaktang = (t:adj) (w:naked) (d:guaktang written with a capital at the start of a line of verse) (e:~ mahin ka ciahkik ding hi) (b:guaktang) (r:18.1.21) (q:draft)
guaktanga = (t:adj) (w:naked) (d:guaktang, naked, with the linking a before om, be: guaktanga omna is nakedness) (e:Na ~ na omna kua in hong gen/~ na omna uh na kisel nadingun | so that you may cover your nakedness/a ~ om nupi leilakah a tucip tawh kibang | like a naked woman sitting on the ground) (b:guaktang) (r:1.3.11/66.3.18/23.3.26)
guaktangin = (t:adj) (w:naked) (d:guaktang with the ending in, used with om, be: guaktangin om is be naked) (e:Mipa leh a zi ~ om uh a/Ham in a pa ~ a omna mu a | Ham saw his father lying naked/tua zan tawntung a ~ om hi | he lay naked all that night/ka ~ ka om hi | I was naked) (s:tangguak) (b:guaktang) (r:1.2.25/1.9.22/9.19.24/1.3.10)
guaktangin = (t:adj) (w:stripped) (d:with the clothes taken off by force, as a punishment or a disgrace) (e:a ~ ka om sak ding a | I will leave her stripped/na ~ hong koih ding | they will leave you stripped/~ maizumna tawh salin pai un | go into captivity stripped and in shame) (b:guaktang) (r:28.2.3/26.16.39/33.1.11)
guaktangin = (t:adj) (w:nude/bare) (e:khe guak leh ~ ka vak ding hi/a suah lai-in a ~ a om mah bangin | as bare as when she was born/bangmah nei loin ~ i suah | we are born bare, having nothing/nu sung panin ~ ka suak a | I came bare from the womb of my mother) (b:guaktang) (r:33.1.8/28.2.3/21.5.15/18.1.21)
guaktangun = (t:adj) (w:naked) (d:guaktang, naked, with un, the marker in with plural agreement: being naked, said of more than one person) (e:a ~ a om lam uh kithei uh/na ~ om-in, maizum-in na om ding uh | you will be naked and ashamed) (b:guaktang) (r:1.3.7/25.4.21) (q:draft)
gual = (t:n) (w:row/line/course/rank) (d:things set side by side in a line: a row of stones, a course of a wall, a stack of loaves, a rank of soldiers) (e:a ~ thumna in jakinth suang/suang ~ li-in na bulh ding hi | you shall mount four rows of stones/~ khatah guk om ding hi | there shall be six in each row/a kiseek suang ~ thum leh taamtaak sing ~ khat | three courses of dressed stone and one of cedar) (r:2.28.19/2.39.10/2.28.17/3.24.6/11.6.36) (q:draft)
gualgual = (t:see) <gualgual-in>
gualgual-in = (t:adv) (w:in rows) (d:gual, row, repeated, with in: row by row) (e:mangbuhte a ~ tuhin) (r:23.28.25) (q:draft, low confidence)
gualgualin = (t:adv) (w:in rows) (d:gual, row, repeated, with in: row by row) (e:mangbuhte a ~ tuhin) (r:23.28.25) (q:draft, low confidence)
gualin = (t:adv) (w:in ranks/in battle array/in line) (d:gual, row, with the ending -in: drawn up in rows; a gualin pang means take up battle positions) (e:Baaltamar-ah a ~ pang uh hi/Gibeah-ah a ~ va naih uh hi | they drew near in battle line at Gibeah/A ~ a kisuan a leenggah huan sungah | into her vineyard planted in rows/~ a cingte lak panin a pua-ah amah paikhiatpih un | bring her out from between the ranks) (b:gual) (r:7.20.33/7.20.20/24.5.10/14.23.14) (q:draft)
gualkhat = (t:n) (w:one line/one row) (d:gual row or line with khat one; gualkhat khit gualkhat, line upon line) (e:~ khit ~, thukhat khit thukhat) (r:23.28.10/23.28.13) (q:draft)
guallel = (t:v) (w:be defeated/be subdued/lose) (d:be beaten in a fight or contest, the opposite of gualzo, win; guallel-in is in defeat, laid low) (e:Israel mite mai-ah Midiante ~ uh a/Israel mite mai-ah Ammon mite ~ hi | the Ammonites were subdued before the Israelites/Amaute ~ ding a, kongzing buan bangin a kisik gawp | they will be defeated and trampled like mud in the street/~-in leivui lakah ka om hi | I lie in the dust defeated) (a:gualzo/gualzawh) (r:7.8.28/19.119.25/7.11.33/33.7.10/18.16.15) (q:draft)
guallelh = (t:v) (w:be defeated/lose) (d:form of guallel used before ciangin and ding and inside noun phrases: guallelh maizumna is the shame of defeat) (e:A ~ uh ciangin amaute in/na mi Israelte a ~ ciangin | when your people Israel are defeated/a langpangte a ~ ding | that his adversaries will be defeated/~ maizumna ka thuak loh nadingin | so that I may not suffer the shame of defeat) (s:lel) (a:gualzawh) (b:guallel) (r:66.12.8/11.8.33/19.112.8/19.119.80) (q:draft)
guallelhna = (t:n) (w:defeat) (d:the state of being beaten by an opponent) (e:na ~ uh a kilang mahmah hi/ka galte a ~ ka mu khin hi | I have seen the defeat of my enemies/Benjamin mite in a ~ uh kimu uh hi | the Benjamites saw that they were defeated/amaute’ ~ tu-in eima hauhna suak ding hi | their defeat will now become our wealth) (s:lelhna) (a:gualzawhna) (b:guallelh) (r:46.6.7/7.20.36/19.54.7/26.26.2) (q:draft)
guallelhsak = (t:v) (w:defeat/cause to be defeated) (d:guallelh, be defeated, with the causative sak) (e:a galte a ~ ding hun) (a:gualzawhsak) (b:guallelh) (r:23.61.2) (q:draft)
guallelin = (t:v) (w:being defeated/laid low/in defeat) (d:guallel, be defeated, with the linking ending in) (e:~ leivui lakah ka lum hi/a galte uh mai-ah ~ | being defeated before their enemies/na bawngtal pasian uh Apis ~ taimang ahi hiam | has your bull god Apis fled in defeat/leivui lakah ~ ka lum uh hi | we lie defeated in the dust) (b:guallel) (r:19.119.25/14.6.24/24.46.15/19.44.25) (q:draft)
guallelsak = (t:v) (w:cause to be defeated/overthrow/make fall) (d:guallel, be defeated, with sak, cause) (e:gal kidona-ah amah na ~ hi/na galte uh mai-ah note hong ~ ding hi | he will cause you to be defeated before your enemies/Nangma’ mai-ah amaute ~ in la | let them be overthrown before you/Galte gualzo a, ei hong ~ a | the enemy has won, and he has made us lose) (a:gualzosak) (b:guallel) (r:19.89.43/24.18.23/5.28.25/25.2.17) (q:draft)
gualnop = (t:v) (w:make merry/frolic/enjoy oneself) (d:have fun or pleasure, often in company; also used as a noun for pleasure or merriment) (e:i ~ ding hong deihin/~ nadinga na bawl Awle | Leviathan, which you made to frolic/deihgawhna a pawlpawl leh ~ uukna’ sila | slaves of all kinds of passions and of the love of pleasure) (s:gualnuam/kigualnop) (r:19.137.3/19.104.26/56.3.3) (q:draft)
gualnopna = (t:n) (w:celebration/merrymaking/rejoicing/entertainment) (d:gualnop, make merry, with the noun suffix na: merrymaking, the noise and pleasure of a feast or celebration; gualnopna bawl is to celebrate) (e:~ aw kiza ding hi/~ zong a bawl kei hi | he held no entertainment either/a tha neih zah uh tawh ~ bawl uh hi | they celebrated with all their might/~ leh lungdamna awte | the sounds of merrymaking and gladness) (s:kipahna) (a:dahna) (b:gualnop) (r:24.30.19/27.6.18/13.13.8/24.7.34) (q:draft)
gualnuam = (t:v) (w:make merry/revel/celebrate) (d:enjoy oneself in company with feasting, dancing or play) (e:Mi ~ mawkmawkte tawh ka kikhawl kei a/mite tu suk uh a, ~ mahmah uh hi | the people sat down and made very merry/a ~ dingin kikhawm uh hi | they assembled to celebrate/Kumpi David laamin a ~-a om a mu hi | she saw King David dancing and celebrating) (s:gualnop/kigualnop) (r:24.15.17/2.32.6/7.16.23/13.15.29) (q:draft)
gualnuamin = (t:v) (w:make merry/celebrate) (d:gualnuam with the linking ending in: while making merry) (e:Amaute ~ numeite khatlekhat in) (b:gualnuam) (r:9.18.7) (q:draft)
gualnuamte = (t:n) (w:merrymakers/the joyful) (d:gualnuam, make merry, with the plural te) (e:a ~’ lamna-ah na va kihel ding hi | you will go and join the dance of the merrymakers) (s:lungdamte) (a:dahte) (b:gualnuam) (r:24.31.4) (q:draft)
gualpihte = (t:n) (w:companions/fellows) (d:those of the same company or rank, with the plural te) (e:na ~ tungah kikhaito-in lungdamna sathau) (s:lawmte/pawlte) (r:19.45.7) (q:draft)
gualtut = (t:v) (w:sit in rows/sit in groups) (d:gual, row, with tut, sit) (e:cih bangin a honhonin a ~ uh hi) (r:41.6.40) (q:draft)
gualzawh = (t:v) (w:win/be victorious/triumph over) (d:form of gualzo used before ni, ding, nading and the like; before a noun it can be read as victory, as gualzawh ni, day of victory) (e:~ lungdamna la kisa a/ka ~ ni-in pahtawina ngah ding uh hi | on the day of my victory they will receive honor/Ka ~ ding hun hong naita hi | the time of my victory has drawn near/Sakol galkap in ~ nadingin a mawkna lametna hi a | a war horse is a vain hope for victory) (a:guallelh) (r:19.118.15/17.9.1/26.39.13/23.51.5/19.33.17) (q:draft)
gualzawhna = (t:n) (w:victory/triumph/deliverance) (d:gualzawh, win, with the noun suffix na: victory over an enemy, and so also deliverance; gualzawhna tawh is in triumph) (e:Kumpite tungah ~ a piapa/ngaihsut siamnate tawh ~ kingah hi | victory is won through wise counsel/kei hong mudahte pen ~ tawh ka en ding hi | I will look in triumph on those who hate me/Filistia gam tungah ~ tawh ka awng hi | over Philistia I shout in triumph) (s:zawhna) (a:guallelhna/lelhna) (r:19.144.10/20.24.6/19.118.7/19.60.8) (q:draft)
gualzawhsak = (t:v) (w:make victorious/bring to victory) (d:gualzawh, win, with the causative sak) (e:Thuman thutang a ~ mateng) (a:guallelhsak) (b:gualzawh) (r:40.12.20) (q:draft)
gualzo = (t:v) (w:be victorious/triumph/prevail/win) (d:win in battle, in a contest or in a dispute; also succeed or prosper) (e:Topa suang uh ahih manin ~ uh a/Pasian thahatin ~ tawntung a | God is strong and always victorious/ka galte ka tungah ~-in lungdam sak kei in | do not let my enemies triumph over me and rejoice/thatang hatna tawh mi ~ lo ding hi | it is not by strength that a person prevails/Thukhenna na thuak ciangin na ~ ding hi | you will prevail when you are judged) (a:guallel) (r:14.13.18/19.25.2/18.12.16/9.2.9/45.3.4) (q:draft)
gualzosak = (t:v) (w:give victory/make victorious/cause to triumph) (d:gualzo, win, with the causative sak: make someone win, give victory to someone) (e:David a paina peuhpeuhah ~ hi/a vangliatna tawh amah ~ ding hi | he will give him victory by his power/Nangmah in ama galte na ~ a | you have given his foes the victory/kote hong angvanin na hong ~ hi | by your favor you give us victory) (a:guallelsak) (b:gualzo) (r:13.18.13/18.17.4/19.20.6/19.89.42/19.89.17) (q:draft)
gualzote = (t:n) (w:the victorious/victors/those who overcome) (d:gualzo, win, with the plural te: those who win or overcome) (e:a ~ khempeuh zong kei tawh/a ~’ ngah lukhu a ngah kei ding hi | he will not receive the crown that victors receive/A ~ pen ka Pasian’ sutpi-in ka bawl ding a | those who are victorious I will make pillars of my God) (s:galzote) (b:gualzo) (r:66.3.21/55.2.5/66.3.12) (q:draft)
guam = (t:n) (w:valley/ravine) (d:low ground between hills, often paired with mual, hill) (e:mual teng ~ teng na sisan tawh/mual leh ~ a omna leitang | a land of hills and valleys/~ sungah tua mualte luang suk ding hi | those mountains will flow down into the valley/Mual khempeuh leh ~ khempeuh ah | on all the mountains and in all the valleys) (s:kuam/mualkuam) (a:mual) (r:26.32.6/5.11.11/33.1.4/26.31.12) (q:draft)
guamah = (t:n) (w:in the valley/in the valleys) (d:guam, valley, with the place marker ah) (e:mual leh ~ a luang luituite) (b:guam) (r:5.8.7) (q:draft)
guamte = (t:n) (w:valleys/ravines) (d:plural of guam) (e:mual leh ~ kilang khia sak a/mualte kahto-in, ~ kiasuk hi | they went up the mountains and down the valleys/mual lian leh mual neute, luite leh ~ | the mountains and hills, the ravines and valleys) (s:kuamte) (a:mualte) (b:guam) (r:18.38.14/19.104.8/26.36.4) (q:draft)
guamteng = (t:n) (w:all the valleys/every valley) (d:guam, valley, with teng, all; paired with mualteng, all the hills) (e:mualteng ~ na sisan tawh kidim ding hi/Mualteng ~, na sa ka dimsak ding hi | I will fill all the hills and valleys with your flesh) (a:mualteng) (b:guam) (r:26.32.6/26.32.5) (q:draft)
guamthuk = (t:n) (w:deep valley/deep ravine/deep hollow) (d:guam, valley, with thuk, deep; a hiding place in the verse, where the NIV has deep caves) (e:~ sungah bu un) (r:24.49.30) (q:draft)
guan = (t:v) (w:put into/give/bestow/impose) (d:put something into or upon someone, as a spirit, wisdom, strength or a burden) (e:Pasian in thuman mite pilna ~ a/kumpi lukhu hoih kong ~ hi | I put a beautiful crown on you/ka kam sungah hong ~ thu | the word that he puts in my mouth/ngaihsutna ka sungah hong ~ in | put a spirit within me) (s:guat) (r:20.2.7/19.51.10/26.16.12/4.23.12) (q:draft)
guang = (t:v) (w:put in/pack/load/fill) (d:put something into a bag, container or place) (e:Balaam’ kamah thu ~ a/late tungah tuate ~ hi | she loaded them on donkeys/sal-a pai dingin na van ~ in | pack your belongings to go into exile/amau’ puak zawh zakzah ~ in la | fill them with as much as they can carry) (s:thun) (r:4.23.5/26.12.4/9.25.18/1.44.1) (q:draft)
guangin = (t:v) (w:put in/load/pack) (d:guang, put something into a container or place, with the linking suffix in: putting in and then doing the next action) (e:ama kam sungah thu ~/a puak hak van ~ | packing loads that are hard to carry/tua sunin ka van ~ | I packed my things during the day/a bilvangte sungah kilhnate ~ | putting the clasps into the loops) (b:guang) (r:4.23.16/40.23.4/26.12.7/2.26.11) (q:draft)
guangpa = (t:n) (w:one who put in) (d:guang, put in, with pa for a man: the one who put the words into her mouth) (e:hih thute a ~ in amah ahi hi) (b:guang) (r:10.14.19) (q:draft)
guangsuk = (t:v) (w:put down into/bring down into) (d:guang, put in, with suk, downward) (e:kikona ka ~ ding hi) (b:guang) (r:23.43.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
guanin = (t:v) (w:give/bestow/supply) (d:form of guan with the linking suffix in, bestowing and then going on to the next action) (e:Pasian in mi khat neihlelam ~/a kisam khaici hong ~ a pungsak ding hi | he will supply the seed you need and increase it/a kisam thuhoihte khempeuh note tungah hong ~ | equipping you with every good thing you need/amaute sungah ka thukhamte ~ | putting my laws within them) (b:guan) (r:21.5.19/47.9.10/58.13.21/58.10.16) (q:draft)
guanthei = (t:v) (w:can lay on/be able to impose) (d:guan, put upon, with thei, be able; mawhna guanthei, be able to charge with guilt) (e:kua in mawhna ~ nawn ding ahi hiam) (b:guan) (r:45.8.33) (q:draft)
guanzaw = (t:v) (w:clothe all the more/provide all the more) (d:guan, put upon or provide, with zaw, more) (e:note hong ~ kan ding hi lo) (s:guatzaw) (b:guan) (r:42.12.28) (q:draft)
guanzo = (t:v) (w:have provided/have clothed) (d:guan, put upon or provide, with zo for a completed action) (e:innkuan buppi puanlum ~ ahih manin) (b:guan) (r:20.31.21) (q:draft)
guat = (t:v) (w:put in/lay on/endow with) (d:put something into or upon a person, as God gives skill, a task or a spirit) (e:Topa in siamna leh pilna a ~ mi/Eite sungah a hong ~ kha | the spirit he has put in us/Pasian in tua bang nasep ei tungah hong ~ pen | that God has laid such work on us/amau’ ngaihsutna-ah siamna a ~ mi | those in whose minds he has put skill) (s:guan) (r:2.36.1/21.1.13/59.4.5/2.36.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
guatsa = (t:v) (w:have put in/have endowed with) (d:guat, put in or endow, with sa, already done: of the skill that God has put into the craftsmen) (e:hih theihna lungsim ka ~) (b:guat) (r:2.28.3) (q:draft)
guatzaw = (t:v) (w:clothe all the more/provide all the more) (d:guat, put upon, with zaw, more) (e:note hong lim ~ ding ahih manin) (s:guanzaw) (b:guat) (r:40.6.30) (q:draft)
Gudgodah = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Gudgodah) (d:place in the wilderness where the Israelites camped on their journey, before Jotbathah) (r:5.10.7)
guh = (t:n) (w:bone) (d:one of the hard parts that form the frame of the body; also used of all the bones of a body together) (e:Amah in a ~ khempeuh kem hi/a ~ guak bekin om hi | he is nothing but bones/hazatna in ~ muatsak natna ahi hi | envy is a disease that rots the bones/Ka ~ khempeuh ka sim thei hi | I can count all my bones) (s:saguh) (r:19.34.20/2.12.46/18.33.21/20.14.30/19.22.17)
Guh = (t:n) (w:bone) (d:guh, bone, capitalised in the place name Lutang Guh, the Skull, Golgotha; lutang guh is skull) (e:Golgotha a kici Lutang ~ mualah/~ leh thaguite tawh | with bones and sinews) (b:guh) (r:43.19.17/42.23.33/18.10.11) (q:draft)
guhguak = (t:n) (w:bare bones/skin and bones) (d:guh, bone, with guak, bare or only: nothing but bones, said of a wasted body) (e:gawngin na ~ bekun na om ding) (r:20.5.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
guhguakin = (t:adv) (w:nothing but bones/as bare bones) (d:guh, bone, with guak, bare, and the ending in: reduced to bones only, said of starving people) (e:a ~ a om uh hi) (b:guhguak) (r:25.4.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
