gupna = (t:n) (w:salvation) (d:gup, save, with the noun suffix na: salvation; gupna ngah is receive salvation, be saved, and gupna thu is the message of salvation) (e:a kipte in ~ a ngah ding/Pasian’ ~ thu a thei ding uh hi | they will know the salvation of God/tuni-in hih inn sungah ~ a tung hi | today salvation has come to this house/~ ngahte tawm ding ahi uh hiam | will those who are saved be few) (s:hotkhiatna/gupkhiatna/hotna) (r:40.24.13/49.6.17/42.3.6/42.19.9/42.13.23) (q:draft)
Gupna = (t:n) (w:salvation) (d:gupna written with a capital; Gupna a ngah, receive salvation, be saved) (e:~ a ngah ding uh hi/~ sik-lukhu khu un la | put on the helmet of salvation/~ ngah nadingin kam tawh kipulak hi | one confesses with the mouth to be saved/~ a ngah mite | those who were being saved) (s:hotkhiatna/gupkhiatna) (b:gupna) (r:44.2.21/66.7.10/49.6.17/45.10.10/44.2.47) (q:draft)
guptuam = (t:n) (w:partiality/favouritism) (d:gup, save, with tuam, separately: favouring one person over another; in the pair guptuam paihtuam, favouring one and rejecting another) (e:kuamah ~ paihtuam nei hetloin) (s:khentuam/angvanna/deidanna) (r:54.5.21) (q:draft)
