hai = (t:n) (w:cup/bowl) (d:a cup to drink from, or a bowl; also the cup-shaped ornaments on the lampstand) (e:khomun ne in, ~ dawn ta hen/Faro’ khut tungah ~ pia hi | he put the cup into Pharaoh’s hand/ka ~ a dimlet hi | my cup overflows/ama tawi ~ ni tungah a buak leh | when he poured out his bowl on the sun) (r:46.11.28/1.40.21/19.23.5/66.16.8) (q:draft)
hai = (t:adj) (w:foolish/senseless/stupid) (d:lacking sense or wisdom; also used as a verb, be foolish, and hai gamtat is act foolishly) (e:Ta ~ in a pa dahsak a/A lungtom mite ~ gamtat a | quick-tempered people act foolishly/Ka mite ~ uh a, kei hong thei lo uh hi | my people are foolish; they do not know me/Ka ~ lua a, mihing ka sun kei hi | I am too stupid to count as a man) (s:haihuai/haivai/mawl) (a:pil) (r:20.17.25/20.14.17/24.4.22/20.30.2) (q:draft)
haibawl = (t:v) (w:dishonour/treat as a fool/treat with contempt) (d:hai foolish with bawl, treat: treat someone as a fool) (e:tapate in a pate ~ a) (s:simmawh/simmawhbawl) (a:zahtak/pahtawi) (b:hai) (r:33.7.6) (q:draft)
haiciam = (t:v) (w:pledge rashly/promise foolishly) (d:hai foolish with ciam promise; kam a haiciam is give one's word as surety for another) (e:kam a ~ leh) (r:20.20.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
haigamtatna = (t:n) (w:folly/outrage/disgraceful act) (d:hai foolish with gamtatna conduct: a shameful deed) (e:amah in Israel sungah ~ hong tun’ hi) (s:haina/haitatna) (r:1.34.7) (q:draft)
haih = (t:v) (w:winnow/sift) (d:toss or shake grain to separate it from the chaff; also used of sifting people) (e:ancilna-ah mangbuhham ~ hi/Satan in buhhum bangin nang hong ~ nuam hi | Satan wants to sift you like wheat/amaute na ~ ding uh a | you will winnow them/minam dangte lakah ka ~ ding hi | I will sift them among the nations) (s:zap/zapsiang) (r:8.3.2/42.22.31/23.41.16/30.9.9) (q:draft)
haihna = (t:n) (w:sieve/winnowing) (d:haih, winnow or sift, with the noun suffix na: the thing in which or the act by which something is sifted) (e:thuak siatnate ~ sungah a haih hi) (b:haih) (r:23.30.28) (q:draft)
haihuai = (t:adj) (w:foolish/senseless) (d:hai, foolish, with huai, worthy of: foolish, or seeming foolishness to someone; thu haihuai is senseless talk) (e:Gentail mite a dingin a ~ thu ahi hi/a ~ mahmahin ka gamta khin hi | I have acted very foolishly/thu lamlakte in thu ~ gen uh hi | the counsellors give senseless advice/Tua bang ngaihsutna ~ mahmah hi | such thinking is very foolish) (s:hai/haivai) (a:pil) (r:46.1.23/23.19.11/13.21.8/46.15.36) (q:draft)
haihuaina = (t:n) (w:foolishness/folly/stupidity) (d:Foolishness or madness; haihuai, foolish, with the noun ending na.) (e:a hoihlohna leh a ~ ka thei khia hi) (s:haina/haitatna) (a:pilna) (b:haihuai) (r:21.7.25) (q:draft)
haihuaipi = (t:n) (w:utter foolishness/object of mockery) (d:haihuai foolish with pi great; said of idols, a thing that is wholly foolish and fit to be mocked) (e:a ~ hi a, a kidaantah ni ciangin) (b:haihuai) (r:24.10.15/24.51.18) (q:draft, low confidence)
haikhak = (t:v) (d:in suangtang haikhak, said of gravel got into the mouth with food; perhaps bite on by accident) (e:suangtang ~ tawh a kibang ahi hi) (r:20.20.17) (q:draft, low confidence)
hailawh = (t:v) (w:go mad/become foolish) (d:become mad or senseless as the result of something) (e:hoi dangdangin a ~ ding uh hi/amau lehdona hangin ~ uh hi | they became fools through their rebellion/milimte a ~ uh hi | they go mad over idols) (r:24.25.16/19.107.17/24.50.38) (q:draft)
hailua = (t:adj) (w:very foolish/too foolish) (d:hai foolish with lua, very or too much) (e:tua zahta-in ~ uh ahih manin) (b:hai) (r:45.1.24) (q:draft)
hailuat = (t:adj) (w:very foolish/too foolish) (d:form of hailua used before man, because) (e:a ~ manun suakkhia loin) (b:hailua) (r:28.13.13) (q:draft)
hailuatna = (t:n) (w:great folly/excessive foolishness) (d:hai foolish with luat, form of lua too much, and the noun ending na) (e:ama ~ in hankhuk sung a tun hi) (b:hailuat) (r:20.5.23) (q:draft)
haina = (t:n) (w:folly/foolishness) (d:The state of being foolish, or a foolish act; hai, foolish, with the noun ending na.) (e:Ka ~ hangin ka liamnate/lungtomna in ~ kilatna hi | a quick temper shows folly/mihaite in ~ thu gen hi | fools speak folly/Pasian’ ~ in mite’ pilna sangin a pilzaw | the foolishness of God is wiser than human wisdom) (s:haitatna/haihuaina/pillohna) (a:pilna) (b:hai) (r:19.38.5/46.1.25/20.14.29/20.15.2) (q:draft)
hainate = (t:n) (w:follies/foolish things) (d:haina, foolishness, with the plural te; thu kidong hainate, foolish questions or controversies) (e:Thu kidong ~ leh khangciamtehna laite) (b:haina) (r:56.3.9) (q:draft)
haipa = (t:n) (w:fool/foolish man/madman) (d:hai foolish with pa, marking a man) (e:Mi ~ aw, tu nitakin na kha/Bang hangin hih mi ~ nang kiangah hong pai | why did this madman come to you) (s:mihaipa/mihai) (a:mipilpa) (b:hai) (r:42.12.20/12.9.11) (q:draft)
haipa = (t:n) (w:glutton/drunkard) (d:in an hai zu haipa, a man greedy for food and for wine; this hai is to crave food or drink) (e:Hihpa in an hai zu ~ hi/Hih pa in an hai, zu ~ hi | this man is a glutton and a drunkard) (s:zuhai) (r:42.7.34/40.11.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
haipau = (t:v) (w:speak foolishly/talk nonsense/play the fool) (d:hai foolish with pau speak) (e:Kiphasakin na ~ ngei a/Topa aw, ka ~ kha hi | Lord, I have spoken foolishly/Amaute kiphasakin ~ uh a | they boast and talk foolishly) (r:20.30.32/18.40.4/61.2.18) (q:draft)
haipaute = (t:n) (w:foolish talkers/chattering fools/babblers) (d:hai foolish with pau speak and te, those who: people who talk foolishly or too much) (e:mi ~ tawh kikhawl kei in/a ~ in lungkhamna tuak hi | chattering fools come to trouble) (b:haipau) (r:20.20.19/20.10.8) (q:draft)
haipi = (t:n) (w:goblet/large cup/bowl) (d:hai, cup, with pi, big; in the verses the cup of God's wrath) (e:ka hehna ~ na dawn nawn kei ding/hoina ~ a tawdat dongin a dawn khin | who drained the goblet of staggering to its dregs/khut sungah tua ~ ka koih ding hi | I will put that goblet into the hands) (b:hai) (r:23.51.22/23.51.17/23.51.23) (q:draft)
haipite = (t:n) (w:bowls/basins/dishes) (d:hai cup or bowl with pi large and the plural te) (e:kham ~ leh a gihna ciat/ngun ~ leh a gihna ciat | each silver dish and its weight) (b:haipi) (r:13.28.17) (q:draft)
haisak = (t:v) (w:make foolish/drive mad/make senseless) (d:hai, foolish or mad, with the causative sak) (e:Pasian in leitung pilna a ~ hilo ahi hiam/a sakol tung tuangte uh ka ~ ding hi | I will drive their riders mad/uliante zu kham sakin ~ uh a | they made the princes drunk with wine and senseless) (s:haitatsak) (b:hai) (r:46.1.20/38.12.4/28.7.5) (q:draft)
haisapi = (t:adj) (w:as a fool) (d:hai foolish with sa and pi; ka haisapi mahin, even as the fool I am taken to be) (e:ka ~ mahin hong sang veve un) (r:47.11.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
haitat = (t:v) (w:act foolishly/behave like a fool) (d:hai, foolish, with tat, act; a haitat ngei is the foolish thing done before) (e:lampi-ah a pai kawm nangawnin ~ uh a/mihaite a ~ ngei bangin ta kik zel hi | fools keep repeating the folly they have done) (r:21.10.3/20.26.11) (q:draft)
haitatin = (t:v) (w:acting foolishly/foolish) (d:haitat, act foolishly, with the linking ending in) (e:eite zong nidangin ~) (b:haitat) (r:56.3.3) (q:draft)
haitatna = (t:n) (w:folly/foolishness/foolish behaviour) (d:Foolish behaviour or madness; haitat, act foolishly, with the noun ending na.) (e:amau’ ~ hangin gimna ngah hi/~ themno khat in pilna lianpen susia thei hi | a little folly can ruin the greatest wisdom/kamsang Balaam’ ~ a khawlsak hi | it restrained the madness of the prophet Balaam) (s:haina/haihuaina) (a:pilna) (b:haitat) (r:20.19.3/21.10.1/61.2.16) (q:draft)
haitatnasate = (t:n) (w:foolish deeds/follies) (d:haitatna foolish behaviour with sa, already done, and plural te: the foolish things someone has done; the English has detestable practices here) (e:gitlohna leh a ~ uh hangin) (r:26.6.9) (q:draft)
haitatsak = (t:v) (w:make foolish/cause to act foolishly) (d:haitat, act foolishly, with the causative sak) (e:na minthanna in nang hong ~ hi) (s:haisak) (b:haitat) (r:26.28.17) (q:draft)
haite = (t:n) (w:cups/bowls/goblets) (d:Plural of hai, cup or bowl: drinking cups, and the bowls used in the temple.) (e:tua ~ tawh zu a dawn uh hi/Kumpi Solomon’ dawnna ~ khempeuh kham hi a | all King Solomon’s drinking cups were gold/vutluahnate zong, leh ~ lakhia uh hi | they took away the censers and the bowls/a ~, a nunte leh a pakte | its cups, buds and blossoms) (b:hai) (r:27.5.3/12.25.15/11.10.21/2.25.31) (q:draft)
haite = (t:n) (w:fools/the foolish) (d:hai foolish with plural te, foolish people; numei haite, foolish women) (e:numei ~ in innsung susia hi/a ~ mipilte’ sila suak tawntung ding hi | the fool will always be servant to the wise/ta ~ bek in a nu simmawh hi | only a foolish child despises his mother/Tua ciangin a ~ in a pilte kiangah | then the foolish ones said to the wise ones) (s:mihaite) (a:mipilte/pilte) (b:hai) (r:20.14.1/20.11.29/20.15.20/40.25.8) (q:draft)
haivai = (t:adj) (w:foolish/senseless/meaningless/absurd) (d:hai foolish with vai affair: of a foolish kind, making no sense) (e:a ~, a mawkna taktak ahi hi/huaihamna a ~ thute-ah awkcipin | caught in the foolish things of greed) (s:haihuai) (r:21.8.14/54.6.9) (q:draft)
haizan = (t:v) (w:chew/eat solid food) (d:of food, to chew it and get it down; haizan zo lo is not yet able to take solid food; how the word is built is not certain) (e:Tu-in na ~ zo kei uh hi/Note in an ~ zo nai lo | you were not yet able to eat solid food) (r:46.3.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
hak = (t:adj) (w:slow/hard/difficult) (d:Placed after a verb: slow or hard to do, as in heh hak, slow to anger, tel hak, hard to understand, and pai hak, slow in coming.) (e:tel ~ lua hi/a tel ~ thu zong a om hi | there are also things that are hard to understand/Topa heh ~ a, a itna kip lianin | the Lord is slow to anger and great in steadfast love/a puak ~ van midangte na suat uh | you load others with burdens hard to carry/Ka topa hong pai ~ ding hi | my master will be slow in coming) (s:haksa) (a:baih) (r:21.7.24/19.103.8/61.3.16/4.14.17/42.11.46/40.24.48) (q:draft)
hak = (t:v) (w:open/be open) (d:Of the eyes, to open or be open; mit hak is to open the eyes, and of God to look with attention.) (e:tu-in na mit ~ in la/naupang sagih vei hetchiai-in a mit ~ hi | the boy sneezed seven times and opened his eyes/Ama mit ~ a, Piter a muh ciangin | she opened her eyes, and when she saw Peter/na mitte hong ~ in la, hong mu in | open your eyes and see/a thawh ciangin a mit ~ a | when he got up he opened his eyes) (a:mitsi) (r:14.6.40/12.4.35/44.9.41/12.19.16/44.9.8) (q:draft)
Hakaliah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hakaliah) (d:father of Nehemiah) (r:16.1.1/16.10.1)
Hakhilah = (t:name) (c:mountain) (w:Hakilah) (d:hill in the Desert of Ziph facing Jeshimon, where David hid from Saul) (r:9.26.1/9.23.19)
hakin = (t:v) (w:be open/open) (d:hak, of the eyes be open, with the linking suffix in) (e:Tu-in ka mitte ~ hih lai munah) (b:hak) (r:14.7.15) (q:draft)
hakin = (t:adj) (w:slow/hard/dull) (d:hak slow or hard to do with the linking suffix in; theih hakin, being slow to understand) (e:Tuate lungsim in theih ~/heh ~, a lian mahmah itna kip tawh | slow to anger, with very great steadfast love) (b:hak) (r:47.3.14/19.103.8) (q:draft)
Hakkatan = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hakkatan) (d:father of Johanan, the head of the family of Azgad who returned from Babylon with Ezra) (r:15.8.12)
Hakkefirim = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Hakkefirim) (d:place on the plain of Ono where Sanballat and Geshem asked Nehemiah to meet them; the NIV translates the name as one of the villages) (r:16.6.2)
Hakkofirim = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Hakkofirim) (d:spelling of Hakkefirim in Nehemiah 6:2, a place on the plain of Ono where Sanballat and Geshem asked Nehemiah to meet them) (r:16.6.2)
hakkol = (t:n) (w:yoke) (d:The wooden bar laid on the neck of a working animal; also a picture of servitude under a ruler.) (e:Babilon kumpipa’ ~ ka kuaitan zo hi/ka ~ puak nop a, ka van zong a zang | my yoke is easy to carry and my burden is light/Savun khau tawh a kithuah ~ bawl in | make a yoke fastened with leather straps/Jeremiah’ ngawng panin a ~ lakkhiat sak a | he took the yoke off the neck of Jeremiah) (s:kol) (r:24.28.2/40.11.30/24.27.2/24.28.10) (q:draft)
hakkolte = (t:n) (w:yokes) (d:Plural of hakkol, yoke; breaking the yokes is a picture of setting people free from slavery.) (e:keimah in note’ ~ kuaitanin/amau’ ngawng panin a ~ uh ka kuaihtan sak ding | I will break their yokes from off their necks) (s:kolte) (b:hakkol) (r:3.26.13/24.30.8) (q:draft)
Hakkoz = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hakkoz) (d:priest whose family received the seventh priestly division in the time of David; also the grandfather of Meremoth who repaired part of the wall of Jerusalem) (r:16.3.21/13.24.10)
Hakmoni = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hakmoni) (d:father of Jehiel who cared for the sons of King David; Jashobeam, chief of David’s mighty warriors, is called a Hakmonite) (r:13.27.32/13.11.11)
hakna = (t:n) (w:delay/lateness/slowness) (d:hak slow with the noun suffix na; being slow or late in doing something, placed after the verb) (e:Moses hong tun’suk ~ mite in/an na nek ~ in a mawkna ahi hi | your eating late is in vain) (b:hak) (r:2.32.1/19.127.2) (q:draft)
haknaw = (t:n) (w:lead) (d:the heavy soft metal) (e:tui sungah ~ bangin amaute tum uh/sumngo, sik, dal, leh ~ | bronze, iron, tin and lead/Tua ciangpi a sin in ~ kibawl ahi hi | the cover of the basket was made of lead) (r:2.15.10/4.31.22/38.5.7) (q:draft)
haknawte = (t:n) (w:lead) (d:haknaw lead with plural te, closing a list of metals) (e:dal, leh ~ hong pia uh hi) (b:haknaw) (r:26.27.12) (q:draft)
haksa = (t:adj) (w:hard/difficult) (d:Hard to do, to bear or to understand; nasep haksa is hard labour, and thu-haksa is a riddle or hard saying.) (e:pen ~ lua mahmah ahih manin/Leitungah mihing in nasep ~ nei a | on earth mortals have hard service/Vantung Gam sung lut nading a ~ mahmah hi | it is very hard to enter the kingdom of heaven/note adingin a ~ lua hi lo a | it is not too hard for you) (s:hak) (a:baih/ol) (r:27.2.11/18.7.1/40.19.23/5.30.11) (q:draft)
haksak = (t:v) (w:open/cause to open) (d:hak, of the eyes be open, with the causative sak: open someone's eyes) (e:Pasian in ama mit ~ a) (b:hak) (r:1.21.19) (q:draft)
haksakna = (t:n) (w:trouble/hardship/harm) (d:noun built on haksa hard; a hardship or trouble that one meets) (e:~ na tuah ciangin na lung a kiat/a ~ khempeuh panun amaute honkhia hi | he delivers them from all their troubles/Ama thu a mangte in ~ tuak kha lo ding hi | whoever obeys his command will meet no harm) (s:haksatna/lungkhamna) (a:nopna/nopsakna) (r:20.24.10/19.34.17/21.8.5) (q:draft)
haksalua = (t:adj) (w:too hard/too difficult) (d:haksa hard with lua, too much) (e:a ~ khat beek om lo hi/note a dingin a ~ thu khat peuhpeuh | any matter that is too hard for you) (b:haksa) (r:24.32.17/5.17.8) (q:draft)
haksapi = (t:adj) (w:very hard/very difficult) (d:haksa with pi, great; haksapi-in and haksapi-a mean with great difficulty, by hard toil) (e:~-in a kham uh hi/~-a hauh tohna in khang semsem hi | wealth gathered by hard toil grows more and more/mun khatah ~-in ka tung uh hi | with difficulty we reached a place/amaute thu ~ sungah om a hih lam uh | that they were in great trouble) (b:haksa) (r:44.14.18/20.13.11/44.27.8/2.5.19) (q:draft)
haksapipi = (t:see) <haksapipi-in>
haksapipi-in = (t:adv) (w:with great difficulty/hardly) (d:haksa, hard, with pipi, very great, and the adverb marker in) (e:~ Nidas khuapi santak ka tung uh hi/~ ka tung leuleu uh hi | with great difficulty we arrived/gunkuang a siatloh nadingin ~ ka huzo uh hi | with great difficulty we managed to save the lifeboat) (r:44.27.7/44.27.8/44.27.16) (q:draft)
haksasak = (t:v) (w:make hard/make bitter/embitter) (d:haksa hard with the causative sak) (e:Isaak leh Rebekah’ nuntakna ~ uh hi/nasep namkim khempeuh tawh amau’ nuntakna ~ uh hi | they made their lives hard with every kind of work) (b:haksa) (r:1.26.35/2.1.14) (q:draft)
haksat = (t:n) (w:trouble/distress/hardship) (d:form of haksa used before a noun, as in haksat hun, time of trouble) (e:ka ~ hun ciangin nangma tungah kong ngen/~ hunin hong huh pahpahpa ahi hi | he is the one who readily helps us in time of trouble/~ hun ciangin kei tungah hong ko un | call on me in the day of trouble/~ hun ciangin mun muan’huai ahi hi | he is a stronghold in times of trouble) (b:haksa) (r:19.86.7/19.46.1/19.50.15/19.9.9) (q:draft)
haksate = (t:adj) (w:hard/difficult/harsh) (d:haksa, hard, with plural -te, placed after a plural noun: thudotna haksate, hard questions) (e:thudotna ~ tawh amah a ze-et dingin/thu ~ bek Moses tungah puak uh a | they brought only the hard cases to Moses/gimna ~ na thuak manun | because you suffer hard trials) (b:haksa) (r:11.10.1/11.12.4/2.18.26/60.4.12) (q:draft)
haksatna = (t:n) (w:trouble/hardship/difficulty/distress) (d:Trouble or hardship that a person goes through; haksat, a form of haksa, hard, with the noun ending na.) (e:ama ~ khempeuh panin honkhia hi/ama mai-ah ka ~ ka gen hi | before him I tell my trouble/lampi-ah amau' tungah a tung ~ khempeuh | all the hardships that came on them along the way/Tua ~ hun khit ciangin ni hong mial ding | after that time of distress the sun will be darkened) (s:lungkhamna/gentheihna/haksakna) (a:nopna/nopsakna) (r:19.34.6/2.18.8/19.142.2/41.13.24) (q:draft)
haksatnate = (t:n) (w:troubles/hardships/difficulties) (d:plural of haksatna) (e:a beisa huna ~ kimangngailh khin a/Na thuak ding uh ~ kihta kei un | do not be afraid of the hardships you are about to suffer/Siatna leh ~ amaute tungah a tun’ ciangin | when disasters and troubles come upon them/amau’ nasep ~ mu hi | he saw their hard labours) (s:lungkhamnate/cihmawhnate) (a:nopnate) (b:haksatna) (r:23.65.16/55.4.5/66.2.10/5.31.21/2.2.11) (q:draft)
haksazaw = (t:adj) (w:harder/more difficult/worse) (d:haksa, hard, with zaw, more; used after sangin, than) (e:thuak ding ~ lai ding hi/Meshek gam sungah tenkhak sangin ~ a | it is harder than living in the land of Meshek) (a:olzaw/baihzaw) (b:haksa) (r:42.10.12/42.10.14/19.120.5) (q:draft)
haktawm = (t:v) (w:wake up/come awake) (d:probably hak, be awake or open the eyes, with tawm, of oneself; a haktawm bangin, as if waking up) (e:Tua laitakin a ~ bangin Jesuh) (r:42.24.31) (q:draft, low confidence)
hakte = (t:n) (w:hard things/secrets/mysteries) (d:hak hard to do with plural te; thu theih hakte, the things that are hard to know, are the secrets or mysteries) (e:Vantung Gam thu theih ~ na theih nadingun/Pasian’ Gam thu theih ~ na theih nadingun | so that you may know the secrets of the kingdom of God) (s:thusimte/thuthukte) (b:hak) (r:40.13.11/41.4.11) (q:draft)
Hakufa = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hakupha) (d:ancestor of a family of temple servants who returned from the exile) (r:15.2.51/16.7.53)
hakzo = (t:v) (d:probably hak, open the eyes, with zo, be able: be able to keep the eyes open; the NIV has their eyes fail) (e:a ~ kei uh hi) (b:hak) (r:24.14.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
hal = (t:v) (w:burn) (d:Burn something with fire, such as an offering, incense, a house or a town.) (e:mei tawh na ~ ding uh hi/tua tungah a namtui paknamtui ~ hi | he burned fragrant incense on it/Baal inn sunga a om khuampi paikhiatpihin ~ uh hi | they brought out the pillar in the temple of Baal and burned it/a ki-at nente leh a thau ~ hi | he burned the pieces and the fat) (a:phelh/sumit) (r:3.8.32/2.40.27/12.10.26/3.8.20) (q:draft)
Halah = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Halah) (d:region of Assyria where the king of Assyria settled the exiled Israelites) (r:12.18.11/12.17.6)
Halak = (t:name) (c:mountain) (w:Halak) (d:mountain rising toward Seir that marked the southern limit of Joshua’s conquests) (r:6.11.17)
Halek = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Helek) (d:son of Gilead and descendant of Manasseh, ancestor of the Helekite clan) (r:6.17.2)
Halhul = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Halhul) (d:town in the hill country of Judah) (r:6.15.58)
Hali = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Hali) (d:a town in the territory of Asher) (e:A gam in Helkath, ~, Beten, Akshaf) (r:6.19.25) (q:draft)
halin = (t:v) (w:burning/setting on fire) (d:hal burn with the linking ending in, used when another action follows in the same sentence) (e:Pasian’ inn ~ Jerusalem kulh nusia uh/kei’ adingin mun khempeuh ah paknamtui ~ | burning incense for me in every place/na bawlsa uh bawngno, mei tawh ~ sukhamin | the calf you had made I burned with fire and crushed/Keimah in tua khuapite mei tawh ~ | I will burn those cities with fire) (b:hal) (r:14.36.19/11.11.8/39.1.11/5.9.21/28.8.14) (q:draft)
halkhawm = (t:v) (w:burn together/burn along with) (d:hal, burn, with khawm, together) (e:meihal biakna tawh tuate ~ hi/le an tawh a biaknate ~ in | and burn the grain offerings with them) (b:hal) (r:3.9.14/12.16.15) (q:draft)
hallam = (t:v) (w:burn) (d:hal burn with lam, the fact that: that someone burns something) (e:pasian dangte kiangah paknamtui a ~ a thei) (r:24.44.15) (q:draft)
Hallelujah = (t:intj) (w:Hallelujah) (r:66.19.1/66.19.4) praise the Lord
Hallelujah = (t:n) (w:Praise the Lord)
Hallohesh = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hallohesh) (d:father of Shallum, the ruler of a half-district of Jerusalem who repaired the wall; also a leader who sealed the covenant under Nehemiah) (r:16.3.12/16.10.24)
hallum = (t:v) (w:burn to death) (d:hal, burn, with lum, to death) (e:a pa mei tawh a ~ uh hi/a hing tangun ~ ding uh hi | they will burn them alive) (s:kanglum/katlup) (r:7.15.6/26.23.25) (q:draft)
hallup = (t:v) (w:burn/burn to death/burn up) (d:Burn a person in fire as an offering; probably the form of hallum, burn to death, used before nading.) (e:mei sungah a ~ nading uh) (r:24.7.31) (q:draft)
hallupna = (t:n) (w:burning) (d:hallup, burn in fire, with the noun suffix na) (e:mei sungah a ~ ding uh) (b:hallup) (r:24.7.31) (q:draft)
halna = (t:n) (w:burning) (d:the act or place of burning, mostly in paknamtui halna the burning of incense) (e:paknamtui ~ leh tuidawn biakna/siangtho munah paknamtui ~ leh meihal biaknate | the burning of incense and the burnt offerings in the holy place/paknamtui ~ ding biakna taute khempeuh | all the altars for burning incense) (s:meihalna) (b:hal) (r:24.44.18/14.29.7/14.30.14) (q:draft)
halnelh = (t:v) (w:burn down over/burn upon) (d:hal burn with nelh, over or upon: burn something down on top of someone) (e:Na inn tawh nang kong ~ ding uh hi) (r:7.12.1) (q:draft)
Halohesh = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hallohesh) (d:spelling of Hallohesh in Nehemiah 10:24, a leader who sealed the covenant under Nehemiah) (r:16.10.24)
halpa = (t:n) (w:one who burns/burner) (d:hal burn with pa, the man who does it) (e:Tuate a ~ in ama puante sawpin/Hih gamsung a ~ in Topa ahi keimah ka hihna | that the one who burns this land is I, the Lord) (b:hal) (r:3.16.28/26.20.48) (q:draft)
halsak = (t:v) (w:burn/burn down/set on fire) (d:hal burn with sak; mei tawh halsak, burn with fire) (e:mei tawh a leengte uh ~ hi/a giahphual khempeuhte uh mei tawh ~ uh a | they burned all their camps with fire/a innte uh ~ hen | let them burn down their houses/mei tawh ka lo hong ~ ahi uh hiam | why have they set my field on fire) (b:hal) (r:6.11.9/26.23.47/4.31.10/10.14.31) (q:draft)
halte = (t:n) (w:those who burn) (d:hal burn with te, the ones who; in the verse those who burned incense) (e:paknamtui a ~ zong hawlkhia hi) (b:hal) (r:12.23.5) (q:draft)
haltui = (t:v) (w:melt/smelt) (d:hal, burn, with tui, liquid: melt metal by fire) (e:ka hehna tawh kong ~ ding hi/meikhuk-a ~ bangin | as when melting in a furnace) (s:tuisak/suangtui) (r:26.22.21/23.1.25) (q:draft)
haltuina = (t:n) (w:smelting/melting) (d:haltui, melt by fire, from hal burn and tui liquid, with the noun ending na; sik haltuina meikhuk is an iron-smelting furnace) (e:sik ~ meikhuk tawh a kibang) (b:haltui) (r:24.11.4) (q:draft)
haltum = (t:v) (w:burn up/burn down/consume) (d:destroy completely by fire) (e:inn lian khempeuh amah in ~ hi/a khing om lai peuhmah na ~ ding uh hi | you must burn up whatever is left over/leengte mei tawh ~ hi | he burns the chariots with fire/laizial kumpipa in a ~ khit ciangin | after the king had burned up the scroll) (s:kangtum/kattum) (r:12.25.9/19.83.14/2.12.10/19.46.9/24.36.27) (q:draft)
haltumin = (t:v) (w:burning up/setting on fire) (d:haltum, burn up, with the linking ending in) (e:Keimah in Egypt gam ~) (b:haltum) (r:26.30.8) (q:draft)
haltumna = (t:n) (w:burning down/destruction by fire) (d:haltum, burn up, with the noun suffix na; haltumna thuak is be burned down) (e:mei tawh ~ thuak loin) (b:haltum) (r:24.38.17) (q:draft)
haltumsak = (t:v) (w:burn down/have burned up/destroy by fire) (d:haltum burn up with the causative sak) (e:a khua a ~ hi/a khuapi a ~ ding hi | he will have her city burned down) (b:haltum) (r:40.22.7/38.9.4) (q:draft)
halungvei = (t:adj) (w:charging/ranging/raging) (d:said of a bear, set beside a hungry lion: on the prowl or ready to attack; the exact sense and the parts of the word are not confirmed) (e:leh vompi ~ tawh kibang hi) (r:20.28.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
ham = (t:v) (w:bray/bellow/low/cry) (d:of an animal or bird, utter its cry) (e:a nek lai takin ~ a/Amaute ganhing bangin gamlakah ~ uh a | they brayed like animals in the wilderness/Peengkul a kitum ciangin ~ uh a | when the trumpet sounds they snort/a pai kawmin ~ uh hi | they lowed as they went/singhiangte lakah amaute ~ zaizai uh hi | they sing among the branches) (r:18.6.5/18.30.7/18.39.25/9.6.12/19.104.12) (q:draft)
ham = (t:adj) (w:old/aged/elder) (d:advanced in age; a moi a ham means young and old) (e:a ~ pen panin kipanin a moi pen/Abraham leh Sarah teek uh a, a kum uh ~ hi | Abraham and Sarah were old and advanced in years/a teek ahi a, a ~ ahi zongin khasiat lo hi | he spared neither the old nor the aged/numei leh pasal, a moi a ~ | men and women, young and old) (s:teek/khangham) (a:moi/khangno) (r:1.44.12/6.6.21/1.18.11/14.36.17) (q:draft, low confidence)
Ham = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ham) (d:second son of Noah, father of Cush, Egypt, Put and Canaan; the land of Ham is a name for Egypt) (r:1.6.10)
Haman = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Haman) (d:son of Hammedatha the Agagite, chief official of King Xerxes, who plotted to destroy the Jews) (r:17.7.1) (q:draft)
Hamath = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hamathites/Hamath) (d:city and kingdom on the Orontes in Syria, north of Israel; its people, the Hamathites, descended from Canaan) (r:13.1.16)
Hamathzobah = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Hamath Zobah) (d:city or region north of Israel that Solomon captured) (r:14.8.3)
hamciam = (t:v) (w:try/strive/make an effort) (d:the same meaning as hanciam, and probably another spelling of it) (e:na suahtak nadingin ~ in/ka utut ka sep ding ka ~ hi | I tried to do whatever I wished) (s:hanciam/hahkat) (r:20.6.5/21.2.3) (q:draft)
Hamgam = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Ham) (d:place east of the Jordan where Kedorlaomer defeated the Zuzites; Ham with gam, land) (r:1.14.5)
hamham = (t:v) (w:cry/chatter) (d:ham, of a bird utter its cry, doubled for a repeated or continued sound) (e:gun vapi bangin ahi zongin ka ~ a) (r:23.38.14) (q:draft)
hamin = (t:adj) (w:old) (d:ham, old, with the suffix -in; found in the set phrase a moi a hamin, young and old alike) (e:a moi a ~ mi khempeuh in/khuapi mite a moi a ~ gimsakin | he afflicted the people of the city, young and old/a moi a ~, tangguak kheguakin | young and old, stripped and barefoot) (b:ham) (r:1.19.4/9.5.9/23.20.4) (q:draft)
Hammath = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Hammath) (d:fortified town in the territory of Naphtali) (r:6.19.35)
Hammeda = (t:see) <Hammeda-tha>
