Hammuel = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hammuel) (d:son of Mishma, a descendant of Simeon) (r:13.4.26)
hamna = (t:n) (w:bleating/lowing/neighing/cry) (d:the cry of an animal, such as the bleating of sheep, the lowing of cattle or the neighing of horses; ham, cry, with the noun ending na) (e:ka zak bawngtalte’ ~ bang ahi hiam/ka bil-a tuu ~ | the bleating of sheep in my ears/a sakol hatte’ ~ awging in | the sound of the neighing of their strong horses) (b:ham) (r:9.15.14/24.8.16) (q:draft)
Hamnath = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Hammath) (d:spelling of Hammath in Joshua 19:35, a fortified town of the tribe of Naphtali) (r:6.19.35)
Hamor = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hamor) (d:Hivite ruler, father of Shechem, from whose sons Jacob bought a piece of land) (r:1.34.6/1.34.18)
hampen = (t:adj) (w:oldest/eldest) (d:ham, old, with pen, most: the oldest of a group, set against moipen, the youngest) (e:a moipen panin a ~ dongin/a ~ panin kipanin a moipen tawh tawp a | beginning with the oldest and ending with the youngest) (s:upen/upapen/teekpen) (a:moipen/neupen/khangnopen) (b:ham) (r:12.3.21/1.44.12) (q:draft)
hampha = (t:adj) (w:fortunate/blessed/happy) (d:having good fortune or blessing; mi hampha is a fortunate or blessed person, and hampha kisa is to count oneself fortunate) (e:ama suan-le-khakte mi ~ ahi uh hi/~ ka kisa mahmah hi | I count myself very fortunate/Na zite mi ~ | how fortunate your wives are/a ~ gam ahi hi | it is a fortunate land) (s:lungdamhuai) (a:kamsia/tuahsia) (r:20.20.7/21.4.2/44.26.2/14.9.7/21.10.17) (q:draft)
hamphat = (t:v) (w:benefit/gain/have an advantage) (d:form of hampha used before nading and zawkna; hamphat nading means for the benefit of someone, and hamphat zawkna is the advantage one has over another) (e:no Gentail mite’ ~ nading hi a/mipilpa a ~ zawkna bang om tuan ahi hiam | what advantage does the wise man have/keima ~ nading bang la ka hi hiam | did I take anything for my own gain) (s:phattuam) (b:hampha) (r:45.11.28/21.6.8/47.12.17) (q:draft)
hamphatna = (t:n) (w:advantage/benefit/right/privilege) (d:hamphat with the noun ending na: an advantage or benefit that falls to someone, or a right that is due to them) (e:Vun ki-at hangin ~ a om hiam/Bangmah ~ nei tuan lo hi ung | we have no advantage at all/note in ~ nihvei na ngah nadingun | so that you might benefit twice/amau’ adinga kilawm ~ ngah sak in | let them receive the rights that are due to them) (s:phattuamna/noptuamna/meetna) (a:supna) (b:hamphat) (r:45.3.1/20.31.9/45.3.9/47.1.15) (q:draft)
hamphatnate = (t:n) (w:rights/privileges/benefits) (d:plural of hamphatna: the rights or benefits that someone is entitled to or receives) (e:i ~ hong paihkhiatsakin/hih ngahtheih ding ~ khempeuh ka la kei a | I have not used any of these rights I could claim/Khuapi Siangtho sungah na ngah ding uh ~ | the share you would receive in the Holy City) (s:phattuamnate) (b:hamphatna) (r:25.3.35/46.9.15/66.22.19) (q:draft)
hamphazaw = (t:adj) (w:more fortunate/better off/happier) (d:hampha, fortunate, with zaw, more: better off or more blessed than another, who is named with sangin, than) (e:a si khinsa mite ~ ka sa hi/gal sungah a site ~ lai hi | those who die in battle are better off/Pasian’ thu za-in a zuite ~ lai hi | those who hear the word of God and obey it are more blessed/ko Jew mite ~ ka hi uh hiam | are we Jews any better off) (b:hampha) (r:21.4.2/42.11.28/25.4.9/45.3.9) (q:draft)
hampheng = (t:n) (w:hut/booth/shelter) (d:a small rough shelter, as in a field or for livestock) (e:tangmai lo sunga ~ bangin/a ganhingte’ ading ~ lam hi | he built shelters for his livestock) (s:bukno/sawlbuk) (r:23.1.8/1.33.17) (q:draft)
Hamran = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hemdan) (d:son of Dishon, a descendant of Seir the Horite; the NIV writes Hemdan) (r:13.1.41)
hamsia = (t:n) (w:curse) (d:evil called down on someone, the opposite of thupha, blessing; hamsia ngah is to be cursed, and hamsia tawh kiciam is to swear with a curse) (e:thupha khat leh ~ khat ka koih hi/~ tawh a kiciam hi | he swore with a curse/Ebal Mual tungah ~ na koih ding uh hi | you shall set the curse on Mount Ebal/na pusuah ciangun zong ~ mah na ngah ding | you will be cursed when you go out too) (s:samsia/hamsiatna/samsiatna) (a:Thupha) (r:5.11.26/5.28.19/41.14.71/5.11.29) (q:draft)
hamsiat = (t:v) (w:curse) (d:call down evil on someone; the form of hamsia used before endings and other words such as loin, nadingin and -in) (e:~ loin thupha na pia un/kei hong ~ teitei uh hi | they all keep on cursing me/a min uh ~ nadingin a kizang hi | their name is used as a curse/a Pasian uh ~-in van dak ding | cursing their God, they will look up to heaven) (s:haamsiat/phuisam/kosia) (a:thupha) (b:hamsia) (r:45.12.14/23.8.21/24.15.10/24.25.18) (q:draft)
hamsiat = (t:n) (w:curse) (d:a curse laid on someone; hamsiat thuak means be cursed, be under a curse) (e:Pasian’ ~ thuak ahi hi/paihkhiatna thuakin ~ a thuak nadingin | to be rejected and come under a curse) (s:hamsiatna/hamsia/samsiatna) (a:Thupha) (b:hamsia) (r:5.21.23/58.6.8) (q:draft)
hamsiate = (t:n) (w:curses) (d:hamsia, curse, with the plural te) (e:hih ~ laibu khat sungah gelhin) (s:hamsiatnate/samsiatnate/haamsiatnate) (a:thuphate) (b:hamsia) (r:4.5.23) (q:draft)
hamsiatin = (t:v) (w:cursing/curse) (d:hamsiat, curse, with the linking ending in) (e:a Pasian uh ~ vandak ding uh hi) (s:samsiatin/phuisamin) (b:hamsiat) (r:23.8.21) (q:draft)
hamsiatna = (t:n) (w:curse) (d:hamsiat, curse, with na: a curse or the state of being cursed; hamsiatna thuak is be accursed) (e:tua mi in ~ thuak ta hen/Ka suah ni in ~ thuak ta hen | cursed be the day I was born/Khazih tawh kikhenin ~ thuak dingin | to be cut off from Christ and cursed/~’ tate ahi uh hi | they are children of a curse) (s:samsiatna/hamsia/haamsiatna) (a:Thupha) (b:hamsiat) (r:46.16.22/66.22.3/24.20.14/45.9.3/61.2.14) (q:draft)
hamsiatnate = (t:n) (w:curses) (d:hamsiatna, curse, with the plural te) (e:leitung gam khempeuhah a pai ding ~/amau’ hong ~ kei’ tungah hong tung ta hen | may their curses come upon me) (s:samsiatnate/hamsiate/haamsiatnate) (a:thuphate) (b:hamsiatna) (r:38.5.3/24.15.11) (q:draft)
hamsiatsak = (t:v) (w:make worse off/put at a disadvantage) (d:probably hamsia, unfortunate, with the causative sak; the NIV has were you inferior) (e:pawlpi dangte sangin kong ~ zawkna bangmah) (r:47.12.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
hamtang = (t:adv) (w:deliberately/wilfully/insistently) (d:placed after a verb, shows that the action is done on purpose, with determination or in spite of a warning; with kei it makes a firm prohibition) (e:mualtung gamah na kuanto ~ uh hi/mawhna i bawl ~ lai leh | if we deliberately go on sinning/huh ngen dingin pai ~ hi | he was set on going to ask for help/ci-in Lot sawl ~ uh hi | they urged Lot insistently/kongzingah giak kei ~ in | on no account spend the night in the square) (s:teitei) (r:5.1.43/28.5.11/58.10.26/1.19.15/7.19.20) (q:draft)
hamtang = (t:adv) (w:surely/certainly/without fail) (d:placed after a verb, shows that the event is certain to happen) (e:Migilote in daan a thuak ~ nading/eite kiangah amah hong pai ~ ding hi | he will surely come to us/thaman ngah ~ ding ahihna phawk un | know that he will certainly receive a reward/ze-etna hong piang ~ ding hi | temptations are bound to come) (s:pelmawh/takpi) (r:20.11.21/28.6.3/41.9.41/42.17.1) (q:draft)
hamte = (t:n) (w:cries/calls/cooing) (d:ham, of a bird or animal utter its cry, with plural te; vakhu hamte, the cooing of doves) (e:gam sung tengah vakhu ~ kiza ta hi) (b:ham) (r:22.2.12) (q:draft)
hamte = (t:n) (w:rough places) (d:in lei hamte, the rough or uneven parts of the ground that are to be made smooth) (e:Lei ~ a kinelsak ding hi) (r:42.3.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
hamu = (t:n) (w:small coin/small sum of money) (d:a small silver coin or sum of money, perhaps a half as mat is a quarter; it stands for the two-drachma temple tax, a day's wage, two pennies and two-thirds of a shekel) (e:tang pawta thumah ~ man hen/biakna innpi siah ~ liau lo ahi hiam | does he not pay the temple tax of a hamu/Gitta nga ciangin ~-in kizuak lel | five sparrows are sold for just a hamu) (r:66.6.6/9.13.21/40.17.24/42.12.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
Hamul = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hamul) (d:son of Perez and grandson of Judah, ancestor of the Hamulite clan) (r:13.2.5/4.26.21)
Hamutal = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Hamutal) (d:daughter of Jeremiah of Libnah, wife of King Josiah and mother of the kings Jehoahaz and Zedekiah) (r:12.23.31/12.24.18)
han = (t:n) (w:tomb/grave/sepulchre) (d:the place where a dead person is buried, a tomb or grave; han sung is the inside of the tomb and han kong its entrance) (e:~ sungah lut a/Mari-te ~ kongah tu-in a om uh hi | the Marys were sitting at the entrance of the tomb/Lazaras ~ sungah ni li a pha zo | Lazarus had already been four days in the tomb/teek sihin ~ na zuan ding hi | you will go to the grave in old age) (s:hankhuk/hanphual/kivuina) (r:43.20.6/42.24.2/40.27.61/43.11.17/18.5.26) (q:draft)
hana = (t:n) (w:toothache/aching tooth) (d:ha tooth with na, pain; the NIV has a broken tooth) (e:~, ahih kei leh khebai tawh kibang hi | is like a toothache or a lame foot) (b:ha) (r:20.25.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
hanah = (t:n) (w:tomb/grave) (d:han, tomb, with the place marker ah: to the tomb, in the grave) (e:nisuah lai takin ~ a pai uh/zingtungin ~ pai uh a | they went to the tomb early in the morning/Pasian’ mipa a kivuina ~ kei hong vui un | bury me in the grave where the man of God is buried/nangma liatna ~ kipaipih suk hi | your pomp is brought down to the grave) (b:han) (r:41.16.2/23.14.11/42.24.22/11.13.31) (q:draft)
Hanamel = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hanamel) (d:son of Shallum and cousin of the prophet Jeremiah, who sold Jeremiah his field at Anathoth) (r:24.32.7/24.32.9)
Hanan = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hanan) (d:name of several men, among them a chief of the tribe of Benjamin and Levites and leaders who sealed the covenant in the time of Nehemiah) (e:Shebaniah, Hodiah, Kelita, Pelaiah, ~) (r:16.10.10/13.8.23) (q:draft)
