Hananiahte = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hananiah) (d:Hananiah with the plural te, Hananiah and those with him; here a priest who blew a trumpet at the dedication of the wall of Jerusalem) (b:Hananiah) (r:16.12.41)
hanciam = (t:v) (w:try/strive/make an effort) (d:make an effort to do or reach something; it often follows a purpose clause with dingin or nadingin) (e:khiatna thei nuamin ka ~ hi/keimah lausak dingin a ~ kamsangnu Noadiah | the prophetess Noadiah, who tried to frighten me/Topa i theih zawh nadingin ~ ni | let us strive to know the Lord/a ~ mi tawh zong a kikum kei hi | nor does it depend on the one who strives) (s:hahkat/hamciam) (r:27.8.15/20.2.2/16.6.14/28.6.3/45.9.16) (q:draft)
hanciamciam = (t:v) (w:keep striving/try hard/seek earnestly) (d:hanciam, strive, with the last part doubled for effort kept up) (e:A siansuah dingin kong ~ hangin/a ~ uh ngah lo uh hi | they did not obtain what they kept striving for) (r:26.24.13/45.11.7) (q:draft)
hanciamin = (t:v) (w:striving/trying hard/making every effort) (d:hanciam, strive, with the linking ending in: striving, with great effort, while going on to the next action) (e:nakpi takin ~ ka lungsim ka pia a/nakpitakin ~ na a sem ihi hi | we labour and strive hard/mi khempeuh phattuam nading ~ | striving for the good of everyone/Daniel a suahtak theih nading lampi ~ | making every effort to find a way to rescue Daniel) (b:hanciam) (r:21.7.25/27.6.14/54.4.10/46.10.33) (q:draft)
hanciamna = (t:n) (w:purpose/plan/scheme/plot) (d:what someone intends and strives to bring about: of God, his purpose or plan; of an enemy, a scheme or plot) (e:Ama ~ eite in i thei hi/Pasian’ ~ a kikheel zo lo | God's purpose cannot be changed/Pasian’ ~ leh theihkholhna hangah | by God's purpose and foreknowledge/Judah mite’ ~ hoih lo | the evil plots of the Jews) (s:ngimna/geelna/tupna) (b:hanciam) (r:47.2.11/49.1.11/58.6.17/44.2.23/44.20.19) (q:draft)
hanciamna = (t:n) (w:effort/struggle/striving) (d:hanciam, strive, with the noun ending na: the act of striving hard, a struggle) (e:Nakpi tak-a ~ tawh ka sanggamnu ka zo hi) (s:hahkatna) (b:hanciam) (r:1.30.8) (q:draft)
hanciamnate = (t:n) (w:efforts/endeavours/intentions) (d:plural of hanciamna: things one strives for; in the letters also the purposes or motives of the heart) (e:ka sepna le ka ~ a mawkna suak lo/minamte’ ~ vutlevai a suak hi | the efforts of the nations turn to ashes/lungsim ngaihsutnate leh ~ khempeuh a thei thei hi | it can discern all the thoughts and intentions of the heart) (s:ngimnate) (b:hanciamna) (r:50.2.16/46.4.5/24.51.58/58.4.12) (q:draft)
hanciampa = (t:n) (w:one who strives/one who tries) (d:hanciam, strive, with pa marking a man: the man who tries to do something) (e:siatsak ding a ~ pen) (b:hanciam) (r:20.28.10) (q:draft)
hanciamsak = (t:v) (w:make strive/make work hard) (d:hanciam, strive, with the causative sak) (e:nakpitakin ~ lua ahih manin) (b:hanciam) (r:26.29.18) (q:draft)
hanciamte = (t:n) (w:those who strive/those who seek) (d:hanciam, strive, with the plural te: people who make an effort for something, used as a hanciamte after the thing they seek) (e:siatna a ~ in siatna mah ngah hi/Thuhoih a ~ in pahtakna ngah a | those who seek good find favour/Thu man-a gamtat ding a ~ nungta ding a | those who strive to live rightly will live/Pasian’ deihteng sep ding a ~ | those who strive to do what God wants) (b:hanciam) (r:20.11.27/20.11.19/40.5.6) (q:draft)
hancingte = (t:n) (w:tomb guards/guards) (d:han, tomb, with cing, guard, and plural te: those who guard a tomb) (e:~ kimkhat khua sungah lut uh a/~ in zong vantungmi kihta-in liing uh a | the guards too shook for fear of the angel) (r:40.28.11/40.28.4) (q:draft)
Hane = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Hanes) (d:spelling of Hanes in Isaiah 30:4, a town in Egypt to which the envoys of Judah came) (e:amau’ tangmite in ~ khua a va phak) (r:23.30.4) (q:draft)
Hanes = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Hanes) (d:town in Egypt to which the envoys of Judah came seeking help) (r:23.30.4)
hang = (t:n) (w:reason) (d:the reason or cause of something; bang hang hiam asks why) (e:Bang ~ hiam na cih uh leh/a ~ hong gen lo ding na hi hiam | will you not tell me the reason/a ~ khat peuhpeuh ahi zongin | or any cause whatever) (s:ahang) (r:45.6.7/10.13.4/10.15.4)
hang = (t:v) (w:complain) of dissatisfaction or annoyance
hang = (t:adj) (w:brave/daring/courageous) (d:not afraid in the face of danger; often paired with thahat, strong) (e:~ un la, thahat un/Thahat in la, ~ in | be strong and courageous/mi ~ khat peuhpeuh ahi zongin | or any brave man/a thahat a ~ galkapte | strong and brave soldiers) (s:hangsan) (a:meidawi/lau) (r:10.13.28/5.31.7/9.14.52/14.17.13)
hanga = (t:prep) (w:because of/for/on account of) (d:hang, reason, with a, joining it to the noun before; khialhna hanga biakna is a sin offering, and bang hanga asks why) (e:khialhna ~ biak nadingin keel a pa khat/tua in khialhna ~ biakna ahi hi | it is a sin offering/Bang ~ ka min hong dong na hi hiam | why do you ask my name/Pasian’ hehna ~ a kisehsa hun | the time appointed because of God's wrath/Topa ~ thongkia keimah in | I, a prisoner for the Lord) (b:hang) (r:4.7.16/45.5.15/3.4.24/1.32.29/27.8.19/49.4.1) (q:draft)
hangah = (t:prep) (w:because of/through/by) (d:placed after a noun to give the reason or the means, like hangin) (e:Kha Siangtho ~ nungta i hih leh/A thu ~ gimna ahi zongin | whether trouble because of the word/hehpihna ~ a kiteelsa kimkhat | a remnant chosen by grace/Zeisu Khazih ~ thupha Lungdamna Thu kihilhin | the good news of peace was preached through Jesus Christ) (b:hang) (r:48.5.25/45.11.5/40.13.21/44.10.36) (q:draft)
hangin = (t:ppm) (w:even though/although/though) (d:placed after a verb, shows that what follows happens in spite of it; after a noun the same word means because of) (e:a kicih ~, khat beek nunghei lo/Hong huh un ci-a ka kiko ~ | even though I cry out for help/amah in Hannah a it ~ | although he loved Hannah/nuntak nading zia a theih ~ | though he knows how to live) (r:34.2.8/25.3.8/9.1.5/21.6.8)
hanginah = (t:prep) (w:because of/on account of) (d:hangin with the ending -ah, placed after a noun to give the reason; tua thu hanginah means that is why) (e:Tua thu ~ note lakah thanem/Amaute in amah ~ a lungkia uh hi | they took offence because of him/tua noptuamna thute ~ a lungdam uh hi | they were glad because of those encouraging words/ama ~ gimna thuak nading | to suffer for his sake) (b:hangin) (r:46.11.30/44.26.6/40.13.57/44.15.31/50.1.29) (q:draft)
hanginah = (t:conj) (w:although/even though) (d:after a verb: although that was done, what follows is contrary to what might be expected) (e:amah ka dot ~) (s:zongin/napi/hinapi) (b:hangin) (r:42.23.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
hangkeu = (t:see) <hangkeu-in>
hangkeu-in = (t:v) (w:roasted/roasting) (d:hangkeu, roast over the fire, with the linking ending in: having roasted it; set against meat that is raw or boiled in water) (e:a sa ~ ne ding uh a/a sungkuate tawh ~, na ne ding uh hi | you shall eat it roasted with its inner parts) (r:2.12.8/2.12.9) (q:draft)
hangpa = (t:n) (w:brave man/warrior/mighty man) (d:hang brave with pa, a man; galkap hangpa and gal hangpa are a valiant warrior) (e:a kihtak huai gal ~ bangin/galkap ~ ama hatna tawh kihonkhia zo lo hi | a warrior cannot save himself by his own strength) (s:galhangpa/thahatpa/galhang) (b:hang) (r:24.20.11/19.33.16) (q:draft)
hangsak = (t:v) (w:make brave/embolden/encourage) (d:hang, brave, with the causative sak; lungsim hangsak means take courage, take heart) (e:na lungsim ~ in/Na lungsim uh ~ un | take courage/na lungsim uh ~ ta un | take heart, all of you/na lungsim uh ~ un la lau kei un | take courage and do not be afraid) (s:thakhauhsak/lungkipsak) (a:lungkiasak/lausak) (b:hang) (r:19.27.14/40.14.27/19.31.24/38.8.13) (q:draft)
hangsakin = (t:v) (w:taking courage/making brave) (d:hangsak, make brave, with the linking ending in; na lungsim hangsakin, taking heart) (e:na lungsim ~) (b:hangsak) (r:19.27.14) (q:draft)
hangsan = (t:adj) (w:bravely/dauntlessly/brave/bold) (d:brave and bold; mi hangsan is a brave man) (e:mite mi ~ ahihna thei uh hi) (r:10.17.10)
hangsana = (t:adv) (w:harshly/fiercely/brazenly) (d:hangsan, here harsh or fierce, with a, used before a verb; hangsana kosiate are those who revile others harshly, the slanderers of the NIV) (e:milim a biate, ~ kosiate) (b:hangsan) (r:46.5.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
hangsankhak = (t:v) (w:be bold/have to be bold) (d:hangsan, bold, with khak, happen to: come to act boldly or sternly) (e:ka hong ~ loh nadingin) (r:47.10.2) (q:draft)
hangsante = (t:adj) (w:fierce/bold) (d:hangsan, bold or fierce, with the plural te; gul hangsante, fierce snakes, the vipers of the NIV) (e:gul ~’ gu a om hi) (b:hangsan) (r:45.3.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
hangtakin = (t:adv) (w:boldly/fearlessly/bravely) (d:hang, brave, with takin, which makes an adverb) (e:Topa’ min tawh ~ thu a hilh hi/kikhopna inn sungah ~ kha thum sung thu hilh | he taught boldly in the synagogue for three months/~ Pilat kiangah hong pai-in | he went boldly to Pilate/lungdamna thusim ~ ka hilhkhiat theih nadingin | so that I may fearlessly make known the mystery of the gospel) (a:laukawmin/laukawm) (r:44.9.28/47.3.12/44.19.8/41.15.43/49.6.19) (q:draft)
hangte = (t:n) (w:the brave/mighty ones/warriors) (d:hang, brave or strong, with the plural te; it follows a noun, as in galkap hangte, brave soldiers, and gal hangte, warriors) (e:A galkap ~ khempeuh uh thahsak un/mi a ~ om hi ci-in a theihna munah | at the place where he knew the brave men were/a sakol ~ koptaina ging hi | the galloping of his mighty horses resounded) (s:galhangte/thahatte) (r:24.50.27/10.11.16/7.5.22) (q:draft)
hangun = (t:prep) (w:because of) (d:hang, reason, with the plural ending un, placed after a noun when those concerned are several: because of) (e:Tua ahih ciangin na mawhna ~/ka khialhna ~ daan hong pia kei in | do not punish us for our sin/na khialhna ~ a zah sagih vei-in | seven times over for your sins/tuate na zuihna ~ | because you follow them) (b:hang) (r:33.6.13/4.12.11/3.26.18/5.7.12) (q:draft)
hangun = (t:conj) (w:although/though) (d:hang with the plural ending un, placed after a verb when those concerned are several: although they do so, what follows is otherwise) (e:huh ding a nget ~ Pasian in pia lo hi/Mei panin khatvei a suahtak khit ~ | although they have once escaped from the fire/aksite lakah bu na bawl ~ | though you make your nest among the stars/Tapa tampi a neih ~ | though he has many sons) (s:zongin/napi/hinapi) (b:hang) (r:18.35.12/19.49.11/26.15.7/31.1.4/18.27.14) (q:draft)
hanhan = (t:adv) (w:fleetingly/swiftly) (d:expressive word after pai, go: passing quickly by, as a shadow does) (e:Niliim bangin a pai ~) (r:21.6.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
hanhanin = (t:adv) (w:fleetingly/swiftly) (d:hanhan with the adverb ending in; pai hanhanin, passing quickly by like a shadow) (e:niliim bangin pai ~ mangthang uh hi) (b:hanhan) (r:18.14.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
hankhuk = (t:n) (w:grave/tomb/pit) (d:the pit of a grave, from han, grave, and khuk, pit) (e:amau’ ~ sung ciat uhah/Sihna ~ panin kua suakta zo ahi hiam | who can escape from the grave of death/a luang paipihin ~ sungah a vui uh hi | they took his body and buried it in a tomb) (s:han/hanphual) (r:23.14.18/26.37.13/19.89.48/41.6.29) (q:draft)
Hankhukte = (t:n) (w:tombs/graves) (d:plural of hankhuk, the pit of a grave) (e:~ zong kihong a) (s:hante) (r:40.27.52) (q:draft)
hankuang = (t:n) (w:coffin/bier) (d:the box or frame on which a dead body is laid and carried) (e:Kumpipa David in ~ zui hi/Izipt ~ sung khatah amah kikoih hi | he was placed in a coffin in Egypt/a ~ va len a | he went and touched the bier) (r:10.3.31/1.50.26/42.7.14) (q:draft)
hanna = (t:n) (w:courage/bravery/boldness) (d:hang, brave, with the noun ending na: courage; lungsim hanna is courage of heart, and hanna bei is to lose courage) (e:amau’ lungsim ~ a bei hi/mite’ lungsimah ~ bei hi | courage failed in the hearts of the people/thu nget ding ~ lungsim hong nei hi | he has found the courage to pray/ka lungsim ~ hong maimangsak hi | he has made my courage vanish) (s:ngamna/kithamuanna) (a:launa/meidawina) (r:19.107.26/18.23.16/6.2.11/13.17.25) (q:draft)
Hannah = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Hannah) (d:wife of Elkanah and mother of the prophet Samuel) (r:9.1.2/9.1.20)
Hannathon = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Hannathon) (d:town on the northern border of the territory of Zebulun) (r:6.19.14)
Hanniel = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hanniel) (d:name of two men: the son of Ephod, leader of Manasseh who helped to divide the land, and a son of Ulla of the tribe of Asher) (r:4.34.23/13.7.39)
Hanok = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hanoch/Hanok) (d:name of two men: a son of Midian and grandson of Abraham, and the eldest son of Reuben, ancestor of the Hanokite clan) (r:1.25.4/1.46.9)
hanphual = (t:n) (w:tomb/grave/burial place) (d:han grave with phual, place or site) (e:siatna bawlte tawh ~ kibang/a ~ le a luang kisialzia khempeuh | the tomb and how his body was laid) (s:han/hankhuk/kivuina) (r:23.53.9/42.23.55) (q:draft)
hansuah = (t:v) (w:stir up/urge/encourage/exhort) (d:move people to act by words, whether stirring them up to do wrong or urging and encouraging them to do good) (e:siampi liante in mihonpi a ~ uh hi/an ne dingin Paul in mi khempeuh ~ a | Paul urged everyone to eat/thu-um mite a ~ khit ciangin | after he had encouraged the believers/Gentailte a ~ uh hi | they stirred up the Gentiles) (s:hanthawn/hanthot) (r:41.15.11/44.20.2/44.27.33/44.14.2) (q:draft)
hansuahin = (t:v) (w:urging/encouraging/stirring up/inciting) (d:hansuah with the linking suffix -in; with zol it means urge strongly, and it is also used of stirring up a crowd or pressing someone hard) (e:keimah in ~ kong zol hi/~ ka zol uh hi | we urge them/na do nadingun ~ ka hong gelh hi | I write urging you to contend/laitheite leh Farisaite in nakpi-in ~ | the teachers of the law and the Pharisees pressing him hard) (b:hansuah) (r:49.4.1/42.11.53/53.3.12/65.1.3) (q:draft)
hansuahna = (t:n) (w:exhortation/encouragement/urging) (d:hansuah, urge, with the noun ending na: words that stir someone up to act or to stand firm) (e:~ kam na thuak siam un/Khazih sungah ~ ahi zongin | whether encouragement in Christ/kipsakna thu, ~ thu, nopsakna thute | words of strengthening, encouragement and comfort/mi ~ leh thuhilhnate hahkatin om in | devote yourself to exhorting people and to teaching) (b:hansuah) (r:58.13.22/46.14.3/50.2.1/54.4.13) (q:draft)
Hansunga = (t:n) (w:in the grave/in the realm of the dead) (d:han grave with sung inside and the ending a, in or of; written with a capital for the realm of the dead) (e:~ misite’ khate kihanthawn a) (r:23.14.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
hante = (t:n) (w:tombs/graves) (d:han, tomb, with the plural te) (e:mual tunga om ~ mu hi/~ sung panin a guhte la sak a | he had the bones taken out of the tombs/Tua ~ a pualam a hoih uh hangin | though those tombs look fine on the outside/a ~ uh ama kimkotah om hi | their graves are all around her) (s:Hankhukte) (b:han) (r:12.23.16/19.49.11/40.23.27/26.32.23) (q:draft)
hanthawn = (t:v) (w:stir up/incite/encourage/urge) (d:move someone to act, whether stirring up to fight or to do wrong, or encouraging in good work) (e:a sim dingin David ~ hi/amaute do dingin ka ~ hi | I stir them up to fight against them/Media kumpite a ~ hi | he has stirred up the kings of the Medes/kote in amah ka ~ uh hi | we urged him) (s:hansuah/hanthot) (a:lungkiasak) (r:13.21.1/14.35.2/23.13.17/24.51.11/47.8.6) (q:draft)
hanthawnin = (t:v) (w:encouraging/urging/inciting) (d:hanthawn, encourage or stir up, with the linking ending in) (e:pawlpite ~ a thahatsak hi/~ thakhauhsak in | encourage and strengthen him/citakin a om nadingun ~ tha pia uh a | encouraging them to remain faithful, they gave them strength/amaute’ lang khatah David ~ | inciting David against them) (b:hanthawn) (r:44.15.41/10.24.1/5.3.28/44.14.22) (q:draft)
hanthot = (t:v) (w:urge/encourage/stir up/exhort) (d:push someone on to act, for good or for evil) (e:mite taii-in na ~ ciangin/Ama zi Jezebel in a ~ Ahab bangin | like Ahab, whom his wife Jezebel urged on/ka ~ zel hangin | though I kept urging him/Midangte ~ theih nading siamna | the gift of being able to encourage others) (s:hanthawn/hansuah) (r:56.2.15/11.21.25/46.16.12/45.12.8) (q:draft)
hanthotna = (t:v) (w:strengthened) (e:Lunghiang mite na ~) (b:hanthot) (r:18.4.3)
hanthotnate = (t:see) <hanthotnate-ah>
hanthotnate-ah = (t:n) (w:in exhortations/to exhortation) (d:hanthotna, exhortation or encouragement, with the plural te and ah, in or to) (e:le ~ tavuan na la in) (r:54.4.13) (q:draft)
Hanun = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hanun) (d:name of several men, chiefly the king of the Ammonites, son of Nahash, who shamed the envoys of David) (r:10.10.1/10.10.4)
hanzia = (t:n) (w:exploit/brave deed/valour) (d:the way of being brave, with zia, manner) (e:Mi thahat thumte’ ~ tu-a bang ahi hi) (r:10.23.17) (q:draft)
hapaak = (t:n) (w:white teeth/teeth) (d:ha tooth with paak, white) (e:Na ~ singsengte zong) (r:22.4.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
Happizzez = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Happizzez) (d:priest in the time of David to whom the eighteenth lot fell for service in the temple) (r:13.24.15)
Hara = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Hara) (d:place in the Assyrian empire to which the king of Assyria exiled the tribes east of the Jordan) (r:13.5.26) (q:draft)
Haradah = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Haradah) (d:place where the Israelites camped in the wilderness, between Mount Shepher and Makheloth) (r:4.33.24/4.33.25)
Haran = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Haran) (d:name of two men: the son of Terah, brother of Abram and father of Lot, who died in Ur of the Chaldeans; and a son of Caleb by his concubine Ephah) (r:1.11.28)
Harar = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Harar) (d:home of several of the mighty warriors of David, who are called Hararites in the NIV) (r:10.23.33/13.11.35)
Harbona = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Harbona) (d:one of the seven eunuchs who served King Xerxes; he pointed out the pole Haman had set up for Mordecai) (r:17.7.9/17.1.10)
Haref = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hareph) (d:descendant of Caleb in the tribe of Judah, founder of Beth Gader) (r:13.2.51)
Harhaiah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Harhaiah) (d:father of Uzziel the goldsmith, who repaired part of the wall of Jerusalem) (r:16.3.8)
Harhas = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Harhas) (d:ancestor of Shallum, the husband of the prophet Huldah; called Hasrah in 2 Chronicles 34:22) (r:12.22.14)
Harheres = (t:name) (c:mountain) (w:Mount Heres) (d:place near Aijalon and Shaalbim where the Amorites held out against the Israelites) (r:7.1.35)
Harhur = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Harhur) (d:ancestor of a family of temple servants who returned from the exile) (r:15.2.51/16.7.53)
Harif = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hariph) (d:ancestor of a family that returned from the exile, and a leader of the people who sealed the covenant in the time of Nehemiah) (r:16.10.19)
Harifa = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hatipha) (d:spelling of Hatipha in Nehemiah 7:56, ancestor of a family of temple servants who returned from the exile) (r:16.7.56)
Harim = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Harim) (d:name of several men, among them the head of the third division of priests in the time of David and the ancestor of a family that returned from the exile) (e:a thumna ~ tung, a lina Seorim tung) (r:13.24.8/15.2.32) (q:draft)
Harnefer = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Harnepher) (d:son of Zophah, of the tribe of Asher) (r:13.7.36)
Harnerfer = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Harnepher) (d:spelling of Harnepher in 1 Chronicles 7:36, a son of Zophah of the tribe of Asher) (r:13.7.36)
Harod = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Harod) (d:spring where Gideon and his men camped before the battle with Midian; also the home of Shammah and Elika, two of the mighty warriors of David) (r:7.7.1/10.23.25)
Haroeh = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Haroeh) (d:descendant of Shobal, the founder of Kiriath Jearim, in the tribe of Judah) (r:13.2.52)
Harosheth = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Harosheth/Harosheth Haggoyim) (d:town in the north of Canaan where Sisera, the commander of the army of King Jabin, was based; in full Harosheth Haggoyim) (r:7.4.2/7.4.13)
harp = (t:n) (w:harp/lyre) (d:stringed instrument, a loanword from English; mostly in harp lasakna, the harp as an instrument of music) (e:~ lasaknate leh laiza lasaknate/githa lasakna leh ~ lasakna tawh | with the lyre and the harp/tamngai leh ~ lasakna aw tawh | to the sound of the pipe and the harp/~ zang sawm khausai lasakna | a harp of ten strings) (r:14.20.28/19.108.2/19.150.3/18.21.12/19.144.9) (q:draft)
harpte = (t:n) (w:harps) (d:harp with the plural te) (e:Pasian’ lasakna ~ tawi-in) (b:harp) (r:66.15.2) (q:draft)
Harsha = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Harsha) (d:ancestor of a family of temple servants who returned from the exile) (r:15.2.52/16.7.54)
Harum = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Harum) (d:father of Aharhel, in the tribe of Judah) (r:13.4.8)
Harumaf = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Harumaph) (d:father of Jedaiah, who repaired the wall of Jerusalem opposite his own house) (r:16.3.10)
Haruz = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Haruz) (d:man of Jotbah, father of Meshullemeth and grandfather of King Amon of Judah) (r:12.21.19)
Hasadiah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hasadiah) (d:son of Zerubbabel, a descendant of King David) (r:13.3.20)
Hashabiah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hashabiah) (d:name of several men, most of them Levites, among them the son of Kemuel who was officer over the tribe of Levi in the time of David) (r:13.6.45/16.10.11)
Hashabnah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hashabnah) (d:leader of the people who sealed the covenant in the time of Nehemiah) (r:16.10.25)
Hashabneiah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hashabneiah) (d:name of two men: the father of Hattush who repaired the wall of Jerusalem, and a Levite who led the people in praise) (r:16.3.10/16.9.5)
Hashbaddanah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hashbaddanah) (d:man who stood at the left of Ezra when he read the Law to the people) (r:16.8.4)
Hashem = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hashem) (d:Gizonite whose sons were among the mighty warriors of David) (r:13.11.34)
Hashmonah = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Hashmonah) (d:place where the Israelites camped in the wilderness, between Mithkah and Moseroth) (r:4.33.29/4.33.30)
Hashub = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hasshub) (d:spelling of Hasshub in Nehemiah 11:15, a Levite, son of Azrikam and father of Shemaiah) (r:16.11.15) (q:draft)
Hashubah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hashubah) (d:son of Zerubbabel, a descendant of King David) (r:13.3.20)
Hashum = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hashum) (d:ancestor of a family that returned from the exile; also a man who stood beside Ezra at the reading of the Law, and a leader who sealed the covenant) (r:15.10.33/16.10.18)
Hasrah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hasrah) (d:keeper of the wardrobe, ancestor of Shallum, the husband of the prophet Huldah; called Harhas in 2 Kings 22:14) (r:14.34.22)
Hassena = (t:see) <Hassena-ah>
Hassena-ah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hassenaah) (d:man or family whose sons rebuilt the Fish Gate of Jerusalem in the time of Nehemiah) (e:~’ tapate in Ngasa Kongpi bawl uh hi) (r:16.3.3) (q:draft)
Hassenaah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hassenaah) (d:man or family whose sons rebuilt the Fish Gate of Jerusalem in the time of Nehemiah) (r:16.3.3)
Hassenuah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hassenuah) (d:name of two men of Benjamin: an ancestor of Sallu, and the father of Judah who was over the New Quarter of Jerusalem) (r:13.9.7/16.11.9)
Hasshub = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hasshub) (d:name of several men, among them a Merarite Levite, father of Shemaiah, and the son of Pahath-Moab who repaired part of the wall of Jerusalem) (r:13.9.14/16.10.23)
Hassofereth = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hassophereth) (d:ancestor of a family of descendants of the servants of Solomon who returned from the exile) (r:15.2.55)
Hasufa = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hasupha) (d:ancestor of a family of temple servants who returned from the exile) (r:15.2.43/16.7.46)
hat = (t:adj) (w:strong/mighty/powerful) (d:strong, said of a person, an arm, an enemy, the wind or a city; often with tha, strength, as in a tha hat, his strength is great; after a verb it means do something fast or much, as in tai hat, run fast) (e:Amaute a Hupa in a tha ~ a/a ~ mahmah ka khut tawh | with my very mighty hand/A ~ ka galte panin kei hong honkhia a | he rescued me from my powerful enemies/nitumna huihpi ~ mahmah khat nungsak a | he made a very strong west wind blow/kei ka tha ~ lai a | I am still strong) (s:thahat/vanglian) (a:thanem) (r:20.23.11/19.24.8/24.21.5/10.22.18/2.10.19/6.14.11) (q:draft)
hatang = (t:n) (w:teeth/tooth) (d:ha, tooth, with tang, a single grain or piece: the teeth as separate pieces, called the grinders in Ecclesiastes 12) (e:an hai nadingin na ~ tawm lua ta-in) (s:hate) (r:21.12.3) (q:draft)
hate = (t:n) (w:teeth) (d:ha, tooth, with the plural te) (e:amau kam sunga ~ sutan in la/a ~ bawngnawi sangin paak zaw ding hi | his teeth will be whiter than milk/a kihtakhuai a ~ om ahih manin | because its fearsome teeth are there/Pasian in amau ~ suktan sakin | God breaks their teeth) (s:hatang) (b:ha) (r:19.58.6/1.49.12/18.41.14/18.4.10) (q:draft)
Hathak = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hathak) (d:one of the eunuchs of King Xerxes, assigned to attend Queen Esther, who carried messages between her and Mordecai) (r:17.4.5/17.4.9) (q:draft)
hathat = (t:adv) (w:quickly/swiftly) (d:hat, strong or fast, doubled, after a verb: with speed or force; hong tung hathat is come on quickly, and ham hathat is said of war horses crying out at the trumpet) (e:nai mahmahin hong tung ~ hi/Peengkul a kitum ciangin ham ~ uh a | when the trumpet sounds they cry out loudly) (r:36.1.14/18.39.25) (q:draft, low confidence)
Hathath = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hathath) (d:son of Othniel, in the family of Kenaz of the tribe of Judah) (r:13.4.13)
Hatifa = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hatipha) (d:ancestor of a family of temple servants who returned from the exile) (r:15.2.54/16.7.56)
hatin = (t:adj) (w:strong/mighty/being strong) (d:hat, strong, with the linking suffix in: being strong; a tha hatin is being strong in body) (e:~ a vanglian Topa/Amah a tha ~ zong kizahtak a | she is strong and also respected/a tha ~ a gualzo pa hi ding hi | being strong, he will be the victor/Tua bang hi leh note tha ~ | then you will be strong) (b:hat) (r:19.24.8/20.31.25/19.110.7/15.9.10) (q:draft)
Hatita = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hatita) (d:ancestor of a family of temple gatekeepers who returned from the exile) (r:15.2.42/16.7.45)
hatkik = (t:v) (w:become strong again/regain strength) (d:hat, strong, with kik, again; a tha hatkik means his strength came back) (e:a tha hong ~ hi/tua ciangin a tha ~ hi | then his strength came back) (s:khauhkik) (b:hat) (r:44.9.19/9.14.27) (q:draft)
hatkikna = (t:n) (w:becoming strong again/renewal of strength) (d:hatkik, become strong again, with the noun suffix na) (e:ka tha a ~ mu un) (b:hatkik) (r:9.14.29) (q:draft)
hatlua = (t:adj) (w:too strong/very strong) (d:hat, strong, with lua, too much: too strong for someone, or very strong) (e:kei adingin amaute ~ uh hi/huihpi ~ ahih manin teembaw a kisia dekdek hi | the storm was so strong that the ship was about to break up/~ ahih manin kuamah in hih zo lo hi | he was so strong that no one could subdue him) (b:hat) (r:10.22.18/32.1.4/41.5.4) (q:draft)
hatluate = (t:n) (w:those too strong/the very strong) (d:hatlua, too strong, with the plural te) (e:ama a dingin a ~ kiang panin) (b:hatlua) (r:19.35.10) (q:draft)
hatna = (t:n) (w:strength/power/might) (d:hat, strong, with the noun suffix na: the strength or power of God, a person or a nation) (e:Topa leh ama ~ zong un la/Pasian’ ~ pahtawi un | proclaim the power of God/na ~ hangin nang hong kipahtawi ta hen | be exalted in your strength/~ bulpi ahi a thalpite ka kuaitan ding hi | I will break the bow, the mainstay of their might) (s:thahatna/vangliatna) (a:thanemna) (b:hat) (r:13.16.11/19.29.1/19.68.34/19.21.13/24.49.35) (q:draft)
hatnate = (t:n) (w:strength/might/powers) (d:hatna, strength, with the plural te) (e:vangliatna leh ~ om tawntung ta hen/~ uh leh na neihsate uh na suan’ manun | because you trust in your strength and your riches/Israelte’ tha ~ hong suksiatsak gawp a | he has utterly broken the strength of Israel) (s:thahatnate/vangliatnate) (b:hatna) (r:66.7.12/24.48.7/25.2.3) (q:draft)
hatpa = (t:n) (w:strong man/strong one/mighty one) (d:hat, strong, with pa, marking a man; ka gal hatpa is my powerful enemy) (e:mi ~’ inn sungah tumin/Ka gal ~ kiang pan | from my powerful enemy) (s:thahatpa) (b:hat) (r:41.3.27/19.18.17) (q:draft)
hatpen = (t:adj) (w:strongest/mightiest) (d:hat, strong, with pen, most; after another verb it means most of all, as in khem hatpen, most deceitful) (e:Ganhing lak pan a ~/na khempeuh lakah a khem ~ hi a | it is the most deceitful of all things/i makai ~ teng i sawl ding hi | we will send our strongest leaders/amaute lakah a ~ teng thatin | killing the strongest among them) (s:thahatpen) (b:hat) (r:20.30.30/24.17.9/33.5.5/19.78.31) (q:draft)
hatpente = (t:n) (w:the strongest/the sturdiest) (d:hatpen, strongest, with the plural te) (e:amau lak pan-a a ~ that-in) (s:thahatpente) (b:hatpen) (r:19.78.31) (q:draft)
hatsak = (t:v) (w:strengthen/make strong) (d:hat, strong, with the causative sak: give strength to a person, the body or the heart) (e:khuk zaw mite na ~ ngeite ngaihsun in/Zeisu’ tha a ~ hi | he strengthened Jesus/pilna in mi khat ~ zaw hi | wisdom makes one person stronger/mihing lungsim a ~ ding an | food to strengthen the human heart/lawmte’ limbawlna in tha ~ hi | the kindness of friends gives strength) (s:thahatsak/khauhsak/thakhauhsak) (a:thanemsak) (b:hat) (r:18.4.4/42.22.43/21.7.19/19.104.15/20.27.9) (q:draft)
hatsakpa = (t:n) (w:one who makes strong/giver of strength) (d:hatsak, make strong, with pa marking a male person) (e:sakolte a ~ in nang na hi hiam) (b:hatsak) (r:18.39.19) (q:draft)
hatte = (t:n) (w:strong ones/the mighty/champions) (d:hat, strong, with the plural te: after a noun, the strong ones of that kind; after a verb, those who are quick or good at doing it, as in a tai hatte, the fast runners) (e:Bashan gam bawngtal ~ in kei hong umcih/A tai ~ nangawn suakta zo lo ding a | even the swift will not escape/kham theih zu nek a ~ | those who are champions at drinking strong drink/galsim ~ ka hi uh hi | we are men valiant in battle/Israel mite’ galkap ~ bang ding uh a | the people of Israel will be like mighty warriors) (s:thahatte) (a:thanemte) (b:hat) (r:19.22.12/30.2.15/30.2.14/23.5.22/24.48.14/38.10.7) (q:draft)
Hattil = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hattil) (d:ancestor of a family of descendants of the servants of Solomon who returned from the exile) (r:15.2.57/16.7.59)
Hattush = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hattush) (d:name of several men, among them a descendant of David who returned from the exile with Ezra, and a priest who returned with Zerubbabel) (r:13.3.22/16.12.2)
hatu = (t:see) <hatu-te>
hatu-te = (t:n) (w:fangs) (d:hatu, fang, a kind of ha tooth, with the plural te) (e:humpinelkai khanglai ~ botkhia in) (r:19.58.6) (q:draft)
hatute = (t:n) (w:fangs) (d:hatu, fang, a kind of ha tooth, with the plural te) (e:humpinelkai khanglai ~ botkhia in) (r:19.58.6) (q:draft)
hatzaw = (t:adj) (w:stronger) (d:hat, strong or fast, with zaw, more; the thing compared is followed by sangin, than) (e:Amah sangin ~ i hi hiam/amah sangin a ~ mi hong pai a | someone stronger than he comes/mite’ thahatna sangin a ~ hi | it is stronger than human strength/a galte sangin amaute ~ sak hi | he made them stronger than their foes/amah a tai ciangin, sakol sangin ~ hi | when she runs she is faster than the horse) (s:thahatzaw/vanglianzaw) (b:hat) (r:46.10.22/10.13.14/42.11.22/46.1.25/19.105.24/18.39.18) (q:draft)
hatzawpa = (t:n) (w:the stronger one/stronger man) (d:hatzaw, stronger, with pa marking a man) (e:amah sangin a ~ in) (b:hatzaw) (r:18.5.5) (q:draft)
hatzo = (t:v) (w:be strong enough/be strong) (d:hat strong with zo, be able; a lungsim hatzo nai lote, those whose mind is not yet strong) (e:a lungsim ~ nai lote in) (b:hat) (r:46.8.10) (q:draft)
hau = (t:adj) (w:rich/wealthy) (d:rich, or as a verb be rich; after a noun it means have much of it, as in sum hau, rich in money) (e:semsem lecin na ~ ding hi/ganhing, ngun, leh kham ~ mahmah hi | he was very rich in livestock, silver and gold/sathau namtui nilhte ~ lo hi | those who love perfumed oil will not be rich/siahdongte’ ukpa ahih manin sum a ~ hi | as chief of the tax collectors he was rich/A ~ a zawng a kilamdan’na om lo hi | there is no difference between rich and poor) (s:sumhau) (a:zawng) (r:20.20.13/1.13.2/20.21.17/42.19.2/20.22.2) (q:draft)
hauh = (t:v) (w:be rich/become rich/grow rich) (d:form of hau, be rich, used before words such as ciang, nading, nop and hangin) (e:Mi khatpeuh a ~ ciang ahi zongin/nang in na ~ nadingin | so that you may become rich/Bangzahin a ~ hangin Solomon nangawn | not even Solomon, however rich he was/haksapi-a ~ tohna in khang semsem hi | wealth gained by hard work keeps growing/~ nop manin mihaute letsong pia leeng | one who gives gifts to the rich in order to get rich) (a:zawn) (b:hau) (r:19.49.16/20.23.4/66.3.18/42.12.27/20.13.11/20.22.16) (q:draft)
hauhlawh = (t:v) (w:get rich from/profit by/be enriched) (d:hauh, be rich, with lawh, as a result: become rich by means of something or someone) (e:sumbawlin a ~ mite in/Nangma van hauhna in, kumpi dangte ~ hi | by your wealth of goods the other kings were enriched/Ka mite’ mawhna amaute in ~ uh a | they grow rich on the sins of my people/leitung sumbawlte in a ~ uh hi | the merchants of the earth grew rich from it/a meet lakna tawh ~ uh hi | they get rich by the interest they take) (s:kihauhlawh) (r:66.18.15/26.27.33/28.4.8/66.18.3/26.22.12) (q:draft)
hauhna = (t:n) (w:wealth/riches/abundance) (d:hauh, be rich, with the noun suffix na: wealth, riches, or a time of plenty) (e:~ leh pahtawina zong hong pia hi/thanuamna in ~ hi | diligence brings wealth/Mite in a ~ uh muangin | people trusting in their wealth/kum sagih sung ~ hong tung ding a | seven years of plenty will come) (s:neihsa) (a:zawnna) (r:20.3.16/1.41.53/20.10.4/19.49.6/1.41.29) (q:draft)
hauhnate = (t:n) (w:riches/wealth) (d:hauhna, wealth, with the plural te) (e:Migilopa in a guksa ~ luakhia kik a/ama ~ a muang | he trusted in his riches/~, neihnate, leh pahtawina zong | riches, possessions and honor too/a kip lo ~ muan le suanin neikha loin | not putting their hope in uncertain riches) (s:neihsate) (b:hauhna) (r:18.20.15/19.52.7/14.1.12/54.6.17) (q:draft)
hauhnateng = (t:n) (w:all the wealth/all the riches) (d:hauhna, wealth, with teng, all) (e:Egypt’ ~ a sumai dingin/~ un a mawhnateng uh loh zo lo hi) (b:hauhna) (r:26.30.10/28.12.8) (q:draft)
hauhnop = (t:v) (w:want to be rich/desire wealth) (d:hauh, be rich, with nop, want; hauhnop manin is out of the wish to get rich) (e:~ manin mizawngte’ neihsa laksak/~ mana kidemna hangin | because of rivalry that comes from wanting to be rich/~ manin mihaute letsong pia leeng | one who gives gifts to the rich in order to get rich/~ hangin na deih khempeuh na ngah ngei kei | though you want to be rich you never get all you desire) (s:haunuam) (r:20.22.16/20.23.4/21.4.4/21.5.10) (q:draft)
hauhnopna = (t:n) (w:desire for riches/love of wealth) (d:hauhnop, want to be rich, with the noun suffix na) (e:hih leitung lunghihmawhna, ~, le deihna dang a tuamtuamte | the worries of this world, the desire for riches and all kinds of other desires) (b:hauhnop) (r:41.4.19) (q:draft)
hauhpakna = (t:n) (w:getting rich quickly/quick wealth) (d:hauh, be rich, with pak, quickly, and the noun suffix na: wealth gained in a hurry) (e:A baih lamin ~ pen/Ol takin ~ oltak mahin kiamkik pah a | wealth gained easily dwindles just as easily) (r:20.20.21/20.13.11) (q:draft)
hauhpen = (t:adj) (w:richest) (d:hauh, be rich, with pen, most) (e:Amah in a ~ pen laitak leh) (s:haupen) (b:hauh) (r:27.11.2) (q:draft)
hauhsakna = (t:n) (w:making rich/giving of plenty) (d:hauh be rich with the causative sak and the noun ending na; an hauhsakna is making rich in grain, a plentiful harvest given) (e:an ~ tawh thupha hong pia kha ding hi) (r:29.2.14) (q:draft)
hauhtheih = (t:v) (w:be able to get rich/can become rich) (d:hauh, be rich, with theih, can; used before nading, as in hauhtheih nading, in order to be able to get rich) (e:na ~ nadingun kei kiang panin/biakna pen ~ nading lampi bekin a ngaihsun mite | those who think godliness is only a way to get rich) (b:hauh) (r:66.3.18/54.6.5) (q:draft)
hauhtohna = (t:n) (w:growing rich/gaining of wealth) (d:hauh, be rich, with to, upward, and the noun suffix na: wealth built up step by step) (e:haksapi-in ~ khangto semsem hi) (r:20.13.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
hauin = (t:v) (d:in hu hauin, said of one who suffers on account of others; the NIV has because of them) (e:amaute’ hu ~ siatna ngah lawh hi) (r:19.106.32) (q:draft, low confidence)
haukhin = (t:adj) (w:already rich) (d:hau rich with khin, already or completely) (e:~ na kisa uh hi) (b:hau) (r:46.4.8) (q:draft)
haukikin = (t:v) (w:becoming rich again/prospering) (d:hau rich with kik, again, and the linking ending in) (e:amahmah hong ~ a tanhzo dingin) (r:3.25.26) (q:draft)
haulua = (t:adj) (w:too rich/very rich) (d:hau, rich, with lua, too much) (e:a ~ lo, a zawnglua loin/~ leng nang hong nialin | if I am too rich I may disown you) (a:zawnglua) (b:hau) (r:20.30.8/20.30.9) (q:draft)
haunuam = (t:v) (w:want to be rich) (d:hau, rich, with nuam, want) (e:a ~ mite in ze-etna a tuamtuam thuak a) (s:hauhnop) (r:54.6.9) (q:draft)
haupa = (t:n) (w:rich man) (d:hau, rich, with pa, marking a man; also mi haupa and sum haupa) (e:A ~ in tuuhon leh bawnghon tampi nei hi/a min Josef kici sum ~ khat | a rich man named Joseph/mi ~’ inn-ah zin khat hong tung a | a traveler came to the house of the rich man/a ~’ haina phawkkhia veve hi | he sees through the folly of the rich man) (s:mihaupa) (a:zawngpa/mizawngpa) (b:hau) (r:10.12.2/40.27.57/10.12.4/20.28.11) (q:draft)
haupen = (t:adj) (w:richest/wealthiest) (d:hau, rich, with pen, most) (e:Job in a ~ khat ahi hi/Mi ~ ahi Taia mite in | the people of Tyre, the richest of people) (s:hauhpen) (a:zawngpen) (b:hau) (r:18.1.3/19.45.12) (q:draft)
Hauran = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Hauran) (d:region south of Damascus and east of the Jordan, on the north-eastern border of the land in the vision of Ezekiel) (r:26.47.16/26.47.18)
hausa = (t:n) (w:chief/ruler/headman) (d:the head of a village or community, a ruler; hausa pa is the chief as a man) (e:Tua lai takin ~ khat in/tua tuikulh ~ pa Publias’ lo a om hi | there was the estate of Publius, the chief of that island/kikhopna inn-ah ahi a, ~ zumah ahi zongin | whether to the synagogue or to the court of the ruler) (s:ukpa/makai/ulian) (r:42.18.18/44.28.7/42.12.11) (q:draft)
hausa = (t:adj) (w:rich/wealthy) (d:hau, rich, with sa, already: being rich; a hausa-in is as a rich man) (e:a ~-in a lumkik nawn kei ding/Amaute a ~-in lum uh a | they lie down rich) (s:hau/sumhau) (a:zawng) (b:hau) (r:18.27.19) (q:draft)
hausak = (t:v) (w:make rich/enrich/prosper) (d:hau, rich, with the causative sak; hausak kik is make rich again, restore the fortunes of) (e:Kei hong itte ka ~ a/Pasian in hong ~ tawntung ding hi | God will always make you rich/Topa in note nakpitakin hong ~ ding hi | the Lord will make you very prosperous/Israel mite ka ~ kik ding a | I will restore the fortunes of the people of Israel) (a:zawngsak) (b:hau) (r:20.8.21/24.49.6/47.9.11/5.28.11/24.33.7) (q:draft)
hausakin = (t:v) (w:making rich/enriching) (d:hausak, make rich, with the linking suffix in) (e:na suhna uh tawh na mite uh ~/migilote khantosak a, ~ liansak ahi hiam | does he make the wicked prosper, enrich them and make them great) (b:hausak) (r:35.2.9/18.21.7) (q:draft)
hausakkik = (t:v) (w:restore the fortunes of/make rich again/restore) (d:hausak, make rich, with kik, again) (e:a ngei bangsakin ka ~ ding hi/Judah mite le Israel mite ka ~ ding a | I will restore the fortunes of Judah and Israel/amaute ka ~ ding a, ka hehpih ding hi | I will restore their fortunes and have compassion on them/hih gam ka ~ ding hi | I will restore the fortunes of this land) (b:hausak) (r:24.48.47/24.33.7/24.33.26/24.33.11) (q:draft)
hausapa = (t:n) (w:chief/ruler) (d:hausa, chief, with pa marking a man: the chief or ruler of a place) (e:tuikulh gam sung ~ a om hi/~ in tua thu a zak ciangin | when the ruler heard this/~ in a gam a ngah khit ciangin | after the ruler had received his kingdom) (b:hausa) (r:44.28.7/42.18.23/42.19.15)
hausapa = (t:n) (w:extremely rich) (b:hausa)
hausate = (t:n) (w:rulers/chiefs/lords) (d:hausa, chief, with the plural te) (e:a ~ in amau tungah a mang uh a/Gentaile’ ~ in amau tungah a mang uh a | the rulers of the Gentiles lord it over them) (s:uliante/ukte) (b:hausa) (r:40.20.25/42.22.25) (q:draft)
hauta = (t:adj) (w:rich now/become rich) (d:hau rich with ta, showing a state now reached) (e:Tu-in i ~ hi) (b:hau) (r:38.11.5) (q:draft)
haute = (t:n) (w:the rich/rich people) (d:hau, rich, with the plural te: those who are rich; usually in sum haute, those rich in money) (e:Sum ~ khut guak tawh a paikhiasak/Sum ~ in note hong bawlsia uh a | the rich oppress you/Na mi ~ uh mi zawngte tungah tatsia mahmah | your rich people are very violent toward the poor/no sum a ~ aw | you who are rich in treasures) (s:mihaute/sumhaute) (a:zawngte/mizawngte) (b:hau) (r:42.1.53/59.5.1/59.2.6/33.6.12/24.51.13) (q:draft)
hauzaw = (t:adj) (w:richer/wealthier/have more) (d:hau, rich, with zaw, more: richer, or have more of something; after sangin it means richer than) (e:dangte khempeuh sangin ka ~ hi/a dangteng sangin a ~ ding hi | he will be richer than all the others/A neite kipia beh ding a, a ~ ding hi | whoever has will be given more and will have plenty/nupi sangin ta ~ ding hi | she will have more children than the woman) (b:hau) (r:21.2.7/40.13.12/27.11.2/48.4.27) (q:draft)
Havilah = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Havilah) (d:land rich in gold around which the river Pishon flows; also the name of a son of Cush and of a son of Joktan) (r:1.2.11/1.25.18)
