hawh = (t:v) (w:visit/call on/go to see) (d:go to see a person or a place: visit, call on; said of God, come to his people to help them) (e:Na vengte inn-ah ~ mun lua kei in/tua gam numeite' kiangah ~ dingin paikhia hi | she went out to visit the women of the land/ka kiangah nong ~ uh hi | you came to visit me/Note' kiangah Pasian hong ~ ding a | God will come to you/a zi kiangah a ~ dingin | to visit his wife) (s:veh) (r:20.25.17/1.34.1/40.25.36/1.50.25/7.15.1) (q:draft)
hawhbaih = (t:v) (w:come soon/visit soon) (d:hawh, visit, with baih, early or soon: come to visit soon) (e:kei ka hong ~ ding a) (r:46.4.19) (q:draft)
hawhin = (t:v) (w:visit/come to) (d:form of hawh with the linking suffix in, visiting and then going on to the next action) (e:Mary kiangah ~ Jesuh’ hihna a mu/minam dangte kiangah ~ a kikholh ding | to visit and associate with other nations/ama kiangah ~, amah tawh ka omkhawm ding | we will come to him and live with him/Israel mite kiangah Topa ~ | the Lord had visited the Israelites) (b:hawh) (r:43.11.45/43.14.23/44.10.28/2.4.31) (q:draft)
hawhkhit = (t:v) (d:hawh, go, with khit, finished: have gone a distance; gunkuang a hawhkhit uh ciangin is when they had gone on in the boat, where the NIV has when they had rowed) (e:gunkuang a ~ uh ciangin) (r:43.6.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
hawhkik = (t:v) (w:visit again/come back/return) (d:hawh, visit, with kik, again or back: come back to see people one has visited before) (e:note kiangah ka hong ~ ding hi/note kiangah ~ ding nakpitakin ka hanciam uh hi | we tried hard to come to you again/Note kiangah hong ~ nuam ka hih manun | because we wanted to come to you again/note kiangah ka hong ~ ciangin | when I come to you again) (b:hawh) (r:44.18.21/52.2.18/52.2.17/50.1.26) (q:draft)
hawhkikin = (t:v) (w:visiting again/going back to visit) (d:hawhkik, visit again, with the linking ending in) (e:i sanggamte kiangah va ~) (b:hawhkik) (r:44.15.36) (q:draft)
hawhna = (t:n) (w:visit/visitation/coming) (d:hawh, visit, with the noun suffix na: a visit or a coming to someone) (e:Pasian hong ~ hun na thei kei hi/Joram’ kiangah a ~ tawh | through his visit to Joram) (b:hawh) (r:42.19.44/14.22.7) (q:draft)
hawhna = (t:n) (w:rudder) (d:in the account of the shipwreck, the steering gear of the ship that the sailors untied: the rudder or the ropes that held it) (e:a ~ a phel uh a) (s:heina) (r:44.27.40) (q:draft, low confidence)
