hawhsim = (t:v) (w:visit secretly) (d:hawh, visit, with sim, secretly) (e:Jesuh kiangah a va ~ ngei Nikodemas) (r:43.7.50) (q:draft)
hawhsuk = (t:v) (w:go down to visit/visit) (d:hawh, visit, with suk, downward: go down to see someone) (e:Jehoram’ tapa Ahaziah ~ hi) (b:hawh) (r:14.22.6) (q:draft)
hawhte = (t:n) (w:guests/visitors) (d:hawh, visit, with te, those who: people who have come as guests or visitors) (e:a ~ en dingin a lut ciangin/Jerusalem-a ~ lakah | among those visiting Jerusalem) (s:zinte/leenglate) (b:hawh) (r:40.22.11/42.24.18) (q:draft)
hawi = (t:v) (w:spare/leave alone/let grow) (d:leave untouched: spare people from harm, and of hair leave it uncut so that it grows long) (e:A tangvalte uh ~ kei un la/a sam a sau-in ~ ding hi | he must let his hair grow long/a sau lua-in zong ~ lo ding uh hi | nor are they to let it grow too long) (r:24.51.3/26.44.20/4.6.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
hawk = (t:v) (w:roar) (d:of a lion, give a loud deep cry; also said of enemies and of the Lord) (e:humpinelkai ~ leh sabawh nuam bangin/humpi bangin a ~ khawm ding uh a | they will roar together like lions/a lauhuai humpinelkai ~ bang hi | is like the roar of a fearsome lion/amau sa ngah nadingin ~ uh a | they roar for their prey) (s:ngik) (r:19.22.13/26.19.7/24.51.38/20.20.2/19.104.21) (q:draft)
hawk = (t:v) (w:skin/flay) (d:strip the hide from an animal; a vun hawk is to take its skin off) (e:Levi mite in savun a ~ lai takun/ganhing a vun ~-in semnen ding hi | he shall skin the animal and cut it into pieces/a vun ~ khin zo lo uh a | they were not able to finish skinning them) (r:14.35.11/3.1.6/14.29.34) (q:draft)
hawkgawp = (t:v) (w:roar loudly/roar mightily/growl) (d:hawk, roar, with gawp, done with force: roar loudly or fiercely) (e:nasia takin hong ~ ding a/nakpi takin a ~ uh hi | they roared fiercely) (b:hawk) (r:24.25.30/24.2.15) (q:draft)
hawkguam = (t:n) (w:ravine/gully/pit) (d:a narrow, deep hollow cut by water; also a narrow pit that one falls into) (e:Amaute ~ sung leh luihawm sung/tangciak theihna ~ tawh kibang hi | is like a narrow pit/a nihun ~ sungah kiakhawm ding uh hi | both will fall into a pit) (s:gum) (r:18.30.6/20.23.27/40.15.14) (q:draft)
hawkguamah = (t:n) (w:into a pit/in a ravine) (d:hawkguam, ravine or pit, with ah, in or into) (e:a nih tuakun ~ kiakhawm ding uh hi) (b:hawkguam) (r:42.6.39) (q:draft)
