hawkkhiatsak = (t:v) (w:strip off/strip) (d:hawkkhiat, take off, with sak: take the clothing or covering off someone) (e:Assiria mite in a puan ~ uh a/a puanpi ~ uh hi | they stripped him of his robe/na puan teng kong ~ ding a | I will strip off all your clothes/Kua in ama puan tungnung ~ zo a | who can strip off its outer coat) (a:silhsak) (b:hawkkhiat) (r:26.23.10/1.37.23/26.16.37/18.41.13) (q:draft)
hawkkhiatsakin = (t:v) (w:strip off/tear off/take off) (d:hawkkhiatsak, strip clothing or a covering off someone, with the linking suffix in) (e:Na puante hong ~/Na ai khipte uh zong hong ~ | tearing off your veils as well/a puanteng ~ a guaktangin ka omsak ding a | I will strip off her clothes and leave her naked) (b:hawkkhiatsak) (r:26.23.26/26.13.21/28.2.3) (q:draft)
hawklam = (t:n) (w:trench/ditch/channel) (d:a channel dug in the ground that can hold water) (e:a ~ zong tui tawh kidim hi/a lian ~ khat biakna tau kimkotah bawl hi | he made a large trench around the altar/~ sunga om tui nangawn | even the water in the trench) (s:tuilam) (r:11.18.35/11.18.32/11.18.38) (q:draft)
hawkmai = (t:v) (w:strip bare/glean clean) (d:pick a vineyard over so that nothing is left) (e:na leenggui lo uh ~ loin) (r:3.19.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
hawkna = (t:n) (w:roar/roaring) (d:hawk, roar, with the noun suffix na: the roar of a lion) (e:humpinelkaite’ ~ za un/a ~ a kizak nawn loh nadingin | so that his roar would be heard no more/migilote ~ dai ta a | the roaring of the wicked has fallen silent) (b:hawk) (r:38.11.3/26.19.9/18.4.10) (q:draft)
hawksak = (t:v) (w:make roar/cause to roar) (d:hawk, roar, with the causative sak: make something roar, said of the waves of the sea) (e:tuipi tok gawpin tuihualte a ~) (b:hawk) (r:23.51.15) (q:draft)
