hawksan = (t:v) (w:roar at) (d:hawk, roar, with san, at or against: roar at someone) (e:a galte uh ka ~ gawp ding/humpinelkai khanglai khat in, amah ~ hi | a young lion roared at him/kei’ lang khatah pangin hong ~ uh a | they stand against me and roar at me/a galte in amah ~ uh a | his enemies roared at him) (b:hawk) (r:28.11.10/7.14.5/24.12.8/24.2.15) (q:draft)
hawksuk = (t:v) (w:roar down/roar) (d:hawk, roar, with suk, downward: roar from a high place) (e:Zion Mual panin Topa hong ~ a) (b:hawk) (r:30.1.2/29.3.16) (q:draft)
hawktui = (t:n) (w:torrent/stream/flood water) (d:water rushing down a gully or stream bed) (e:~ in tua inn a nawt hangin/ka khitui ~ luang a bang hi | my tears flow like a torrent/~ nin, ahih kei leh tui uih tawh kibang hi | is like a muddied stream or foul water) (s:tuikhang) (r:42.6.48/25.3.48/20.25.26) (q:draft)
hawl = (t:v) (w:drive/drive out/drive away) (d:make people, animals or a vehicle move on: drive; with khia drive out, with kik drive back) (e:Anak suan-le-khakte ~ khia hi/ka ~ khiatna gamte panin | from the lands where I have driven them/amaute doin ka ~ khia zo kha ding hi | perhaps I can fight them and drive them out/ni khat sung kinak ~ lua leh | if they are driven too hard for one day/amah in nakpi takin ~ hi | he drives furiously) (s:nawh) (r:6.15.14/2.14.25/24.23.3/4.22.11/1.33.13/12.9.20) (q:draft)
hawlkhia = (t:v) (w:drove out/drive out/drive away/cast out) (d:hawl, drive, with khia, out: force a person, a people or an evil spirit to leave a place) (e:dawi tampi ~ uh a/sum zuakte ~ a | he drove out those who were selling/Abram in tuate ~ hi | Abram drove them away/minamte ~-in, tua leenggui na suan hi | you drove out the nations and planted the vine/thukhenna tokhom kiang panin a ~ hi | he drove them from the judgment seat) (s:nawhkhia/suankhia/notkhia) (a:kaikhawm) (b:hawl) (r:41.6.13/1.3.24/42.19.45/1.15.11/19.80.8/44.18.16) to cause or force someone or something to leave
hawlkhiamang = (t:v) (w:drive out completely/drive away) (d:hawlkhia, drive out, with mang, away so as to be gone: drive out completely) (e:~ khin lo uh hi/na ~ uh a, amaute na don kei uh hi | you have driven them away and have not cared for them) (r:6.17.13/24.23.2) (q:draft)
hawlkhiasak = (t:v) (w:let drive out/cause to be driven out) (d:hawlkhia, drive out, with the causative sak: let someone drive another away) (e:migilote, hong ~ kei in) (b:hawlkhia) (r:19.36.11) (q:draft)
hawlkhiat = (t:v) (w:drive out/cast out/expel) (d:form of hawlkhia used before a following word such as theihna, matengin or leh) (e:dawite ~ theihna thu/kote nong ~ leh | if you drive us out/a galte a ~ matengin | until he has driven out his enemies/Israel mite’ mai-ah a ~ minamte | the nations he had driven out before the Israelites) (s:nawhkhiat/suankhiat) (b:hawlkhia) (r:41.3.15/40.8.31/4.32.21/12.21.2) (q:draft)
hawlkhiatna = (t:n) (w:driving out/expulsion/banishment) (d:hawlkhiat, drive out, with the noun suffix na: the act of driving people out, banishment; before gam, the land to which they were driven) (e:eite hong ~ gam khempeuh pana/minamte ~ tawh | by driving out nations/sihna ahi a, ~ ahi a | whether death or banishment/amaute a ~ in hih minamte’ gitlohna hang ahi hi | he drives them out because of the wickedness of these nations) (s:nawhkhiatna) (b:hawlkhiat) (r:24.16.15/5.9.4/13.17.21/15.7.26) (q:draft)
