hihloh = (t:v) (w:not be) (d:hi, be, with loh: not being, used before nading or hangin) (e:Nidangin Pasian’ mi na ~ uh hangin/amau’ sila na ~ nadingun | so that you would not be their slaves/kei pen bangmahpi ka ~ hangin | even though I am nothing/Khrih na hih leh na ~ nong gen nadingin | to tell us whether you are the Christ or not) (s:ahihloh) (r:60.2.10/3.26.13/47.12.11/40.26.63) (q:draft)
hihlohlam = (t:n) (d:the fact of not being or not doing, hih with loh not and lam; with ka, na or a before it and phawk notice or thei know after it, where English says that I am not, that I was not) (e:ka ~ a phawk ding uh hi/anlum thu a gen ka ~ | that I was not speaking about bread) (r:26.6.10/40.16.11) (q:draft)
hihlohna = (t:n) (w:not being) (d:hi, be, with loh, not, and the noun suffix na: the fact that someone is not something; ka hihlohna thu, that I am not) (e:Note pen muantheih ding na ~ uh/a bawl ding ka ~ thu | that I am not the one doing it/a kisial khial ka ~ uh hong kilang hi | it has been shown that we did not boast wrongly) (s:ahihlohna) (a:hihna) (r:23.48.8/26.36.32/47.7.14) (q:draft)
hihlum = (t:v) (w:kill/strike down/put to death) (d:hih, do, with lum, dead: do to death, kill) (e:Pai in, amah ~ in) (s:thatlum) (r:10.1.15) (q:draft)
hihmanun = (t:conj) (w:because) (d:hih with man reason and un, the plural ending with in: because you did or are so; also written na hih manun in the same verse) (e:singkungte phuk na ~ note zong) (r:35.2.17) (q:draft, low confidence)
hihmawh = (t:v) (w:be concerned/be anxious/worry) (d:used after lung heart, lung hihmawh; another spelling of himawh) (e:lung ~ dingin ngaihsun lo hi) (s:himawh/lunghihmawh) (r:1.39.6) (q:draft)
hihmawhhuai = (t:adj) (w:worrying/to be feared) (d:hihmawh, be anxious, with huai, worthy of; lung hihmawhhuai hi is it is a thing to be anxious about) (e:phak zawh loh khak ding lung ~ hi) (s:lunghihmawhhuai) (r:58.4.1) (q:draft)
hihna = (t:n) (d:the fact of being, noun form of hi be, used where English says that someone is or will do something, as in Topa ka hihna that I am the Lord) (e:hong paipih na ~ ka thei hi/Topa ka ~ thu na thei ding hi | you will know that I am the Lord/Pasian ka ~ thei un | know that I am God/mi lehdo thei na ~ uh | that you are rebels) (s:hihlam/ahihna) (a:hihlohna) (r:18.30.23/37.2.21/26.16.62/19.46.10/23.48.8) (q:draft)
hihna = (t:n) (w:deed/doing/action) (d:what someone does, noun form of hih, do; na hihna khempeuh is all that you do) (e:Pa’ ~ a muh bangin a bawl thei hi | he can do only what he sees the Father doing/na ~ khempeuh uhah Topa Zeisu’ min suangin | in all that you do, in the name of the Lord Jesus/i ~ khempeuh ah | in everything we do) (s:gamtatna/bawlna) (r:27.9.14/50.2.14/43.5.19/51.3.17/21.12.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
hihnasa = (t:n) (w:what was done/deeds/doings) (d:hihna, deed, with sa, already done: the things someone has done) (e:A pu David’ ~ khempeuh bangin/Jerikho leh Ai tungah Joshua ~ thu | what Joshua had done to Jericho and Ai/Assiria kumpite in gam khempeuh a ~ | what the kings of Assyria have done to all the countries) (s:gamtatnasa) (b:hihna) (r:14.29.2/6.9.3/12.19.11) (q:draft)
hihnasate = (t:n) (w:deeds/things done) (d:hih, do, with na, sa, already done, and plural te: the things someone has done) (e:gamdang mi khempeuh tungah ka ~ uh/a khan lai-a na ~ | what you did in their days) (s:gamtatnasate) (b:hihnasa) (r:14.32.13/19.44.1) (q:draft)
hihnate = (t:n) (w:deeds/doings/actions) (d:plural of hihna; the things someone does or has done) (e:ka ~ khempeuh a kilawm mah ahihna/Mite in Jesuh’ ~ khempeuh lamdangsa-in | while people marveled at all that Jesus did/a lauhuai ~ khempeuh | all the awesome deeds) (s:gamtatnate/bawlnate) (b:hihna) (r:26.14.23/42.9.43/5.34.12) (q:draft)
hihnop = (t:v) (w:want to do/wish to do) (d:hih, do, with nop, the form of nuam, want, used before a noun or loh; na hihnop khempeuh is all that you want to do) (e:na ~ khempeuh na hih theihna/ka ~ loh siatnate ka gamta zawsop hi | the evil I do not want to do, I keep on doing/Na ~ peuhpeuh uh hih unla | do whatever you want to do/Hihte pawl pen note’ ~ pawl ahi hi | these are the things you love to do) (s:gamtatnop/sepnop) (r:18.42.2/45.7.19/21.11.9/30.4.5) (q:draft)
hihnopte = (t:n) (w:things one wants to do/wishes) (d:hihnop, want to do, with the plural te: the things he wants to do) (e:Ama ~ kuamah in khaktan zo lo hi) (b:hihnop) (r:18.23.13) (q:draft)
hihnopteng = (t:n) (w:all that one wants to do) (d:hihnop, want to do, with teng, all of it: everything one wants to do) (e:Ka ~ hihkha loin) (b:hihnop) (r:45.7.15) (q:draft)
hihnu = (t:pron) (w:she/her/this woman) (d:hih, this, with nu marking a woman: this woman, she, said of a woman who is present or being spoken about) (e:~ koi ah om a hiam?/A unau sagih mahin ~ tenpih ciat khin uh | all seven brothers had married her/mun khempeuhah ~’ thu kiphawkin | she will be remembered everywhere) (s:tuanu) (r:42.20.33/41.14.9)
hihpa = (t:pron) (w:he/him/this man) (d:hih, this, with pa marking a man: this man, he, said of a man who is present or being spoken about) (e:~ koi ah om a hiam?/~ in dangka tawi sawm a nei zo hi | he already has ten minas/Topa in ~ zong teel lo hi | the Lord has not chosen this one either/~ koipan hong pai cih i thei hi | we know where this man comes from) (s:tuapa) (r:42.19.25/1.5.29/9.16.8/43.7.27)
HIHPA = (t:pron) (w:this man/he) (d:hihpa written in capitals in the inscription on the cross) (e:~ IN JUDAHTE’ KUMPIPA HI) (r:42.23.38) (q:draft)
hihpak = (t:v) (w:do quickly/do at once) (d:hih, do, with pak, at once, used in commands: hihpak in, do it without delay) (e:Na hih ding peuhpeuh ~ in/hih dingin na ngim pen ~ in | do what you have come to do) (s:sempah) (r:43.13.27/40.26.50) (q:draft)
hihpih = (t:v) (w:be together with) (d:hih, the form of hi be, with pih together with; sila ka hihpih is the one who is a servant along with me, my fellow servant) (e:nasem khawm sila ka ~) (r:51.4.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
hihsa = (t:v) (w:had done) (d:hih, do, with sa, already: what someone has done, placed before the noun it describes or before khempeuh, all) (e:ama ~ nasep khempeuh/A pa Amaziah’ ~ khempeuh bangin | just as his father Amaziah had done/Saul tungah Filistiate’ ~ thu khempeuh | all that the Philistines had done to Saul/Ama ~ a lamdang nasepte phawk un la | remember the wonders he has done) (s:bawlnasa) (r:1.2.2/14.26.4/13.10.11/13.16.12)
hihsak = (t:v) (w:do for/do to) (d:hih, do, with sak: do something for or to another person; with lo, not let someone act against another) (e:eite’ adingin bang hong ~ thei lel ding/Note adingin bang hong ~ ding ka hi hiam | what shall I do for you/na deih khempeuh nangma adingin kong ~ ding hi | whatever you desire I will do for you/amaute Saul ~ lo hi | he did not let them attack Saul) (r:28.10.3/10.21.3/10.19.38/9.24.7) (q:draft)
hihsakna = (t:n) (w:deed done for someone/what was done for) (d:hihsak, do for, with the noun suffix na: what one person has done for another) (e:kei adinga hong ~ hang hi) (b:hihsak) (r:2.13.8) (q:draft)
hihsan = (t:n) (w:here/this place) (d:hih this with san place, used as hihsan takah, right here, at this very place) (e:~ takah kong pai nawn loh nading) (b:hih) (r:43.4.15/43.6.9) (q:draft)
hihsate = (t:n) (w:deeds/things done) (d:hihsa with plural te: what someone has done) (e:ama ~ ngaihsunsun ding uh hi/a ~ ama tung mah ah kithukkik ding | what he has done will be paid back to him/na ~ mu dih in | consider what you have done) (s:hihnasate/gamtatnasate) (b:hihsa) (r:19.64.9/24.2.23/23.3.11) (q:draft)
hihtakpi = (t:v) (w:really be/truly be) (d:hih, be, with takpi, truly; na hihtakpi leh is if you really are) (e:nang na ~ leh/Pasian’ Tapa na ~ leh | if you really are the Son of God) (r:40.14.28/40.27.40) (q:draft)
hihte = (t:pron) (w:these) (e:~ pen Pasian nasepna hi/~ in Edom ukpite ahi uh hi | these were the chiefs of Edom/~ in Korahte beh ahi hi | these were the Korahite clans/~ in na nek loh dingte uh ahi hi | these are the ones you must not eat) (s:hite) (a:tuate) (b:hih) (r:13.1.54/1.9.19/2.6.24/5.14.12) plural form of <hih>
Hihte = (t:pron) (w:these) (d:hihte, these, written with a capital at the start of a sentence or of quoted speech) (e:~ in makai nei lo hi/~ in amaute’ min ahi hi | these are their names/~ in to nei lo hi | these have no master) (b:hihte) (r:11.22.17/11.4.8/14.18.16) (q:draft)
hihthei = (t:v) (w:can do/be able to do) (d:hih, do, with thei, can) (e:Pasian in na khempeuh ~ hi/Pa aw, na khempeuh na ~ hi | Father, you can do all things/a siazaw a ~ nawn lote | those who can do nothing worse after that) (s:hihzo) (r:40.19.26/41.14.36/42.12.4) (q:draft)
hihtheih = (t:v) (w:can do/be able to do) (d:form of hihthei used before nading, zah or leh; ka hihtheih zahin, as much as I can) (e:ka ~ zahin ka hanciam ding hi/Na ~ leh kote hong hehpih inla | if you can do anything, take pity on us/a ~ zahzah ciang a hih khinta ahi hi | she has done what she could/mihingte’ ~ bangmah om lo hi | there is nothing that human beings can do) (s:hihzawh) (b:hihthei) (r:61.1.15/41.14.8/41.9.22/43.6.63) (q:draft)
hihtheihna = (t:n) (w:ability/power to do/right to do) (d:hihtheih, can do, with the noun suffix na: what one is able or allowed to do) (e:a ~ khempeuhah Jesuh a ze-et khit ciangin/Ka ut peuhpeuh ka ~ ding thu om hi | I have the right to do whatever I want) (s:hihzawhna) (b:hihtheih) (r:42.4.13/46.10.23) (q:draft)
hihzah = (t:adv) (w:so many/so much/such) (d:hih, this, with zah, amount: as many or as great as this; hihzah tak nalamdangte is miracles as great as these) (e:Ama khut tawh ~ tak nalamdangte/~ tak nalamdangte bangci a bawl thei hiam | how can he do such great miracles) (s:hizah) (r:41.6.2) (q:draft)
hihzahta = (t:adv) (w:so many/this much) (d:hihzah, this much, with ta: as many as these; kampau hihzahta is so many words as these) (e:Kampau ~ hong kidawng lo ding) (s:hizah) (b:hihzah) (r:18.11.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
hihzaw = (t:v) (w:do more/do rather) (d:hih, do, with zaw, more or rather: do more than others, or do one thing rather than another) (e:Topa hehsak nading tam ~ hi/tuidawn biakna ka ~ ding uh hi | we will rather go on pouring out drink offerings/note tungah hong nak ~ kan ding uh | they will do even more to you) (s:bawlzaw/semzaw) (r:11.16.33/24.44.17/42.23.31) (q:draft)
hihzawh = (t:v) (w:be able to do/can do) (d:hih, do, with zawh, the form of zo, be able, used before ding, zah or nakleh: what one has the power to do) (e:amau ~ zah ciat hanciamin/Na ~ ding ahih nakleh | if it is in your power to do it/Tua bangin na ~ nakleh | if you are able to do so/Mihingte’ ~ ding hi lo mah hi | it is not something men can do) (s:hihtheih/bawltheih) (r:44.11.29/20.3.27/18.40.14/40.19.26) (q:draft)
hihzawhna = (t:n) (w:ability/gift) (d:hihzawh, be able to do, with the noun suffix na: what one is able to do; Pasian’ piak hihzawhna is a gift given by God) (e:Pasian’ piak ~ a tuamtuam nei a) (s:hihtheihna) (b:hihzawh) (r:46.7.7) (q:draft)
hihzia = (t:n) (w:way of doing/doing) (d:hih, do, with zia, manner: the way someone does a thing) (e:Nangma ~ hoih lo hi) (s:gamtatzia) (r:2.18.17) (q:draft)
hihzo = (t:v) (w:be able to do/accomplish/manage) (d:hih, do, with zo, be able: succeed in doing; hihzo kei means cannot do) (e:Pasian in a ~ hi/Ahih hangin a ~ kei uh hi | but they could not do it/Bangmah ~ kei ning | I cannot do anything/hih zawh loh pen Pasian in ~ hi | what cannot be done, God can do/lungsim a om hangin ka ~ kei hi | though the desire is there, I cannot do it) (s:hihthei/semzo/bawlzo) (r:45.8.3/32.1.13/23.3.7/42.18.27/45.7.18) (q:draft)
hikcip = (t:v) (w:grow stiff/freeze/cramp) (d:said of a hand that has grown tired and stiff and stays clenched) (e:a khut a ~ mateng) (s:khikcip) (r:10.23.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
hikeileh = (t:conj) (w:otherwise/if not/or else) (d:hi, be, with kei, not, and leh, if: if it is not so; usually follows tua, that, as tua hikeileh, otherwise) (e:Tua ~ amaute in amau tung mahah/Tua ~ khamlua-in na lua ding hi | otherwise you will have too much and vomit/Tua ~ note kong balgawp ding hi | otherwise I will tear you to pieces/Tua ~ amah thakhatin hong tungin | otherwise he will come suddenly) (r:2.28.43/5.8.12/20.25.16/19.50.22/41.13.36) (q:draft)
hikha = (t:v) (w:may be/turn out to be/happen to be) (d:hi, be, with kha, which marks what may happen or turn out; hikha thei is may well be) (e:sihna lampi ~ thei hi/Hong thangsiahna ~ thei ding ahih manin | because it may turn out to be a trap for you/thukhenna a thuak mite ~ thei ding hi | they may become people who come under judgment/gimna a thuakte na ~ kei un | do not be among those who suffer) (r:20.14.12/20.23.3/54.3.6/60.4.15) (q:draft)
hikhathei = (t:v) (w:may be/might be) (d:hikha, may be, with thei, can: perhaps it is so) (e:phot ding kisam ~ ding hi) (s:hithei) (b:hikha) (r:11.18.27) (q:draft)
hikhawm = (t:v) (w:be together/be jointly) (d:hi, be, with khawm, together: be something together with others, or be two things at the same time) (e:Note tawh kumpi ~ ding ihih manin/to nih’ sila ~ thei lo hi | cannot be the slave of two masters at once) (b:hi) (r:46.4.8/40.6.24) (q:draft)
hikhin = (t:v) (w:already be/have become) (d:hi be with khin, already, marking a state that has been reached) (e:na suahtheih ding uh hun ~ napi-in/ama mi siangthote ~ na hih manun | because you are already his holy people/kumpi vive ~ hi lo ahi hiam | are they not all kings already/a sihzawh a sawtpi ~ napi-in | though it is already long since he died) (s:suakkhin) (b:hi) (r:58.5.12/51.3.12/23.10.8/58.11.4) (q:draft)
Hikiah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hilkiah) (d:spelling of Hilkiah in some verses; name of several men, among them the father of Eliakim, the palace administrator of King Hezekiah) (r:13.6.13/13.6.45)
hikim = (t:v) (w:be fully/all be) (d:hi, be, with kim, complete: be so fully, or all be so) (e:a cingtaak mi ~ dingin) (r:47.13.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
hil = (t:see) <sia-hil>
hileh = (t:conj) (w:if/if only) (d:if it were so; closes a conditional clause, if or unless; tua hileh, then, in that case; alone after a noun, a wish, if only it were) (e:Topa in kei hong huh lo ~/Topa in hong panpih lo ~ | if the Lord had not been on our side/Amaute a pil ~ | if only they were wise/keima deih bangin Israel a gamta ~ | if only Israel would walk as I wish/Pasian in ka deihna hong pia ding ~ | if only God would grant what I long for) (s:ahihleh) (r:19.94.17/20.2.9/19.124.1/5.32.29/19.81.13/18.6.8) (q:draft)
hilel = (t:v) (w:be only/be merely/be just) (d:hi, be, with lel, only: is nothing more than) (e:Amah khutsiampa ~ a/Milim a bawl khutsiamte pen mi ~ uh hi | the craftsmen who make idols are only men/Khut sunga tawizawh ganhing ~ napi-in | though it is only a creature that can be held in the hand/Mary a kici nu ~ hi lo ahi hiam | is she not just the woman called Mary) (s:hibek) (r:41.6.3/20.30.28/23.44.11/40.13.55) (q:draft)
Hilen = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Hilen) (d:town in the hill country of Judah given to the descendants of Aaron, called Holon in the book of Joshua) (r:13.6.58)
hileng = (t:conj) (w:if I were/if I had) (d:hi be with leng, the conditional ending for a first person singular subject) (e:nuam a sa lo ~) (r:19.119.92) (q:draft)
hilh = (t:v) (w:teach/preach/instruct) (d:teach or instruct someone, and so preach; thu hilh is to teach or preach the word) (e:kikhopna inn sungah thu a ~ hi/Hih thute vaikhak in la, ~ in | command and teach these things/tua gamah Lungdamna Thu a ~ uh hi | there they preached the gospel/na ngeina kipte kei hong ~ in | teach me your decrees) (s:thuhilh/sinsak) (a:sin) (r:42.13.10/54.4.11/44.14.7/19.119.12) (q:draft)
hilha = (t:v) (w:teach) (d:hilh teach with the linking a before kinei, as thugen-a kinei in the same verse: be trying to teach) (e:naungekte a ~ kinei ahi hiam) (b:hilh) (r:23.28.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
hilhbawl = (t:v) (w:admonish/warn/instruct) (d:hilh, teach, with bawl, do: treat someone by instructing or warning him) (e:mi khat hihna tawh ~ zaw un) (b:hilh) (r:53.3.15) (q:draft)
hilhel = (t:adv) (w:alongside/parallel) (d:follows paikhawm go together, said of a wall that runs along a row of rooms; exact meaning not certain) (e:tua inngualte tawh a paikhawm ~) (r:26.42.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
hilhhelh = (t:adv) (d:expressive adverb after dawn or dawng, shoot, picturing young shoots that sprout and spread freely) (e:a huan sungah a dawn ~ kungno/oliv-no dawng ~ tawh kibang ding uh hi | they will be like sprouting olive shoots) (r:18.8.16/19.128.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
hilhhilh = (t:v) (w:preach/proclaim/keep teaching) (d:hilh, teach, doubled for an action that goes on: keep teaching or preaching) (e:Khrih upna thu mah a ~ hi/a thu ka hong ~ uh Pasian’ Tapa | the Son of God whom we preached to you/Tua Pasian’ thu pen kote’ ~ | that word of God is what we proclaim) (s:thuhilh/taangko) (r:48.1.23/45.10.8/47.1.19) (q:draft)
hilhhuai = (t:adj) (w:that ought to be taught/worthy to be told) (d:hilh teach with huai, worthy of) (e:tua thu in a ~ ahih mah bangin) (r:49.6.19) (q:draft)
hilhial = (t:adv) (d:follows zol, said of a healthy, well-fed body, apparently sleek or smooth all over; exact meaning not certain) (e:a pumpi uh cidamin zol ~ hi) (r:19.73.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
hilhin = (t:v) (w:teaching/preaching/instructing) (d:hilh with the linking ending in, used when another verb follows: teaching, and) (e:Pasian’ thu ~ kum khat leh kha guk/thu ~ Jerusalem khuapi zuanin a zin hi | teaching, he travelled on toward Jerusalem/kikhopna innte ah thu ~ a om hi | he went on preaching in the synagogues/thu ~ dawite a hawlkhia hi | he preached and drove out demons) (s:thuhilhin) (b:hilh) (r:44.18.11/42.13.22/42.4.44/41.1.39) (q:draft)
hilhinah = (t:v) (w:taught/said in teaching) (d:form of hilh teach that closes a clause introducing the words spoken next: he taught them, saying; found in the 1932 text) (e:thugentehna tawh thu tampi a ~/mihonpi leh a nungzuite thu a ~ | he taught the crowds and his disciples, saying) (b:hilhin) (r:40.13.3/40.23.1) (q:draft, low confidence)
hilhkhia = (t:v) (w:proclaim/make known) (d:hilh, teach, with khia, out: teach or tell out openly) (e:Lungdamna Thu a ~ dingin kiging un) (s:genkhia/taangko) (b:hilh) (r:49.6.15) (q:draft)
hilhkhiat = (t:v) (w:proclaim/make known) (d:form of hilhkhia used before another word such as theih) (e:hangtakin ka ~ theih nadingin) (s:genkhiat) (b:hilhkhia) (r:49.6.19) (q:draft)
hilhkhol = (t:v) (w:warn/forewarn/tell beforehand) (d:hilh, tell, with khol, beforehand: tell someone of a danger before it comes) (e:Mi gilo khat ~ napi-in/paisuk in la mite ~ in | go down and warn the people/Mipa in thupi takin kote hong ~ a | the man warned us solemnly/na Kha Siangtho tawh amaute na ~ hi | by your Holy Spirit you warned them) (s:theikholsak) (r:26.3.19/1.43.3/2.19.21/16.9.30) (q:draft)
hilhkhol = (t:v) (w:prophesy/testify/foretell) (d:tell a message beforehand, as in thu hilhkhol, prophesy; also bear witness against someone) (e:thu a ~ ding uh hi/Na tapate na tanute un thu ~ ding uh | your sons and daughters will prophesy/Jakob’ suan leh khakte ~ un | testify against the descendants of Jacob/hong tung ding thu ~ dinga hong pai | come to tell beforehand what will happen) (s:genkhol/kamsang) (r:44.2.18/30.3.13/44.2.17/27.10.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
hilhkholh = (t:v) (w:warn/forewarn/tell beforehand) (d:form of hilhkhol, tell beforehand, used in dependent clauses and before words such as bangin, nading and hangin) (e:A hong ~ bangin a thokik zo hi/a nuntak theihna dingin thu na ~ kei leh | if you do not warn him so that he may live/eite ~ nadingin lai sungah a kiciamteh | written down as a warning for us/mi khempeuh ka hong ~ nopna panin | I want to warn everyone) (s:genkholh) (b:hilhkhol) (r:40.28.6/26.3.18/46.10.11/66.22.18) (q:draft)
hilhkholhna = (t:n) (w:warning/forewarning) (d:telling of something before it happens; hilhkholhna lim is a sign that warns beforehand) (e:ama ~ hangin mite lau mahmah/Nang tungah kong piak ~ khempeuh | every warning that I give you/amaute pen ~ a suak uh hi | they became a warning/vantung leh leitungah ~ lim ahi | warning signs in the heavens and on the earth) (s:thupiakkholhna) (b:hilhkholh) (r:18.33.16/29.2.30/26.33.7/4.26.10) (q:draft)
hilhkholhnate = (t:n) (w:warnings/admonitions) (d:plural of hilhkholhna: things taught or told beforehand as a warning) (e:amaute tungah a piak ~ simmawh uh hi/Nangma tungah ka hong gen ~ khempeuh | all the warnings that I speak to you/leh na ~ zong don lo uh hi | they paid no attention to your warnings either) (b:hilhkholhna) (r:12.17.15/26.3.17/16.9.34) (q:draft)
hilhkholhsa = (t:adj) (w:foretold/told beforehand/declared in advance) (d:hilhkholh tell beforehand with sa, already done) (e:Sau veipi lai-a a hong ~ bangin/A beisa hunah ka hong ~ bangin | as I warned you before) (b:hilhkholh) (r:25.2.17/7.2.15/48.5.21) (q:draft)
hilhkholin = (t:v) (w:warning) (d:hilhkhol, warn, with the linking suffix in, usually before the words spoken) (e:Ahi zongin amaute ~ amaute kiangah/Amaute limtakin ~ | warn them solemnly, and) (b:hilhkhol) (r:16.13.21/9.8.9) (q:draft)
hilhkik = (t:v) (w:teach again) (d:hilh teach with kik again) (e:thu a ~ ngei loh nadingun) (b:hilh) (r:44.5.40) (q:draft)
hilhna = (t:n) (w:teaching/instruction/correction) (d:hilh, teach, with the noun suffix na: what is taught, and also the correction given by a father or teacher) (e:i Pasian’ ~ ngai un/Ta pil in a pa’ ~ mang a | a wise son heeds his father's instruction/Nang na ~ thu thak | this new teaching of yours/~ a mang nuamte mipil ahi hi | those who are willing to heed correction are wise) (s:thuhilhna/kihilhna) (b:hilh) (r:23.1.10/20.13.1/44.17.19/20.15.5) (q:draft)
hilhnasa = (t:v) (w:taught before/preached earlier) (d:hilh teach with na and sa already, placed before a noun of place: where one has taught earlier) (e:Topa’ thu i ~ khuate-ah) (b:hilh) (r:44.15.36) (q:draft)
hilhnate = (t:n) (w:teachings/instructions) (d:plural of hilhna: the things that someone teaches) (e:hong ~ zui in la/na pa uh’ hong ~ ngai un | listen to your father's instruction/Kong ~ kem tawntung in | keep my teachings always) (s:thuhilhnate/kihilhnate) (b:hilhna) (r:18.22.22/20.7.3/20.4.1) (q:draft)
hilhpa = (t:n) (w:teacher/instructor/speaker) (d:hilh, teach or tell, with -pa marking a man: the man who teaches or tells, used as a hilhpa) (e:a ~ tungah a hoihna a om khempeuh/pilna leh siamna a ~ ahi hi | he is the one who teaches wisdom and understanding/a hong ~ ading kei in mipil lo bang | to the one who speaks to me I am like an ignorant man) (s:thuhilhpa/siapa) (b:hilh) (r:48.6.6/46.14.11/20.2.6) (q:draft)
hilhsa = (t:v) (w:taught/preached) (d:hilh, teach, with sa, already done: what has been taught or preached before) (e:ka hong ~ uh lungdamna thu/ka Pa’ hong ~ teng bek | only what my Father has taught me/Note tungah ka hong ~ uh thute | the things that we taught you) (b:hilh) (r:48.1.8/43.8.28/53.3.6) (q:draft)
hilhsak = (t:v) (w:teach/instruct/have someone teach) (d:hilh, teach, with sak: teach for the good of someone, or cause someone to be taught) (e:thukhamte amaute ~ un/naupang ka bawl nading uh hong ~ in | teach us how to bring up the child/a upate pen pilna ~ a | he taught his elders wisdom/a gamtat loh nadingun hong ~ hen | let him warn them so that they do not act so) (s:sinsak) (b:hilh) (r:12.17.27/7.13.8/19.105.21/42.16.28) (q:draft)
hilhsawm = (t:v) (w:intend to teach/try to teach) (d:hilh, teach, with sawm, intend or attempt) (e:kote tungah thu hong ~ na hi hiam/Grik mite kiangah thu ~ hi ding ahi hiam | does he intend to teach the Greeks) (r:43.9.34/43.7.35) (q:draft)
hilhsawn = (t:v) (w:teach/pass on/teach in turn) (d:hilh, teach, with sawn, onward: teach to others what one has been taught) (e:Ka hong gensa thute na ~ in/midangte a ~ thei ding mite’ tungah | to people who will be able to teach others/a tate a ~ dinga a sawl | he commanded them to teach their children/a tate uh a ~ theih nadingun | so that they may teach their children) (s:gensawn) (r:54.4.11/55.2.2/19.78.5/5.4.9) (q:draft)
hilhsim = (t:v) (w:teach in secret) (d:hilh teach with sim, secretly) (e:thu ka ~ ngei kei hi) (r:43.18.20) (q:draft)
hilhte = (t:n) (w:teachings/instructions) (d:hilh, teach, with plural te: the things that someone teaches, as in kong hilhte, what I teach you) (e:kong ~ thei in la/kong ~ khempeuh lim takin, ciamteh un | take careful note of all that I teach you) (s:hilhnate/thuhilhnate) (b:hilh) (r:20.2.1/20.4.2) (q:draft)
hilhte = (t:n) (w:teachers/preachers) (d:hilh, teach, with plural te, used as a hilhte: those who teach or preach) (e:Lungdamna Thu a ~ in/Pasian’ thu a ~ pen mite tungah thugen hi | those who teach God's word speak to people/no kiangah hong pai thuzuau ~ | teachers of lies who come to you) (s:thuhilhte/siate) (b:hilh) (r:46.9.14/46.14.3/40.7.15) (q:draft)
hilhtel = (t:v) (w:explain/make clear/expound) (d:hilh, teach, with tel, clear: teach or tell a matter so that the hearer understands) (e:Mi khatpeuh in hong ~ lohpi-in/Pasian’ thu paiziate a mantakin a ~ uh hi | they explained the way of God accurately/tua maangmuhna thu ka hong ~ laitakin ciamteh in | take note as I explain the vision to you) (s:gentel) (r:44.8.31/44.18.26/27.9.23) (q:draft)
hilhtelna = (t:n) (w:explanation/interpretation) (d:hilhtel, explain, with the noun suffix na) (e:Hih ~ kei a hong kipia hi) (s:gentelna) (b:hilhtel) (r:27.7.23) (q:draft)
hilhtheih = (t:v) (w:be able to teach/be able to proclaim) (d:hilh, teach, with theih, form of thei, be able, used before nading or hun) (e:Mite kiangah Khrih’ thusim ~ nadingin/Thu ka ~ hun ding ciangin | whenever I am able to speak the word/Gentail mite lakah ka ~ nadingin | so that I might preach among the Gentiles) (b:hilh) (r:51.4.3/48.1.15/49.6.19) (q:draft)
hilhzawhin = (t:adv) (w:teachably) (d:hilh teach with zawh be able and the ending in; hilhzawhin om lo is not able to be taught, unteachable, where the NIV has hearts that are hard) (e:~ na om loh manun Moses in/Note, ~ om lo na hih manun | because you were unteachable) (r:40.19.8/41.10.5) (q:draft)
hilhzo = (t:v) (w:have taught/have shown) (d:hilh, teach or show, with zo, marking an act as carried through) (e:Na pilna ding lampi kong ~ a/Nebukhadnezzar kumpipa tungah a hong ~ hi | he has shown it to King Nebuchadnezzar) (b:hilh) (r:20.4.11/27.2.28) (q:draft)
Hilkiah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hilkiah) (d:name of several men, among them the high priest who found the Book of the Law in the days of King Josiah, and the father of the prophet Jeremiah) (r:13.6.13/13.6.45)
Hillel = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hillel) (d:father of Abdon, the judge of Israel from Pirathon) (r:7.12.13/7.12.15)
hilo = (t:part) (w:not) (d:is not, the negative of hi be written as one word; hilo ahi hiam at the end of a question means is it not so) (e:bil in thu ngai tel ~ ahi hiam/amaute in a gensia uh ~ ahi hiam | are they not the ones who slander/a cimawhte dahpih ~ ka hi hiam | have I not grieved for the poor/a sunglam zong bawl ~ ahi hiam | did he not make the inside also) (b:hi) (r:18.12.11/59.2.7/18.30.25/42.11.40) (q:draft)
Hilo = (t:part) (w:no/not) (d:hilo written with a capital at the start of a reply; Hilo hi means no, it is not so) (e:~ hi, nangma tung panin hihte/~ hi, ka tapate aw | no, my sons/~ hi; Topa na’ ka sem ding uh hi | no, we will serve the Lord/~ hi, bang hang hiam cih leh | not at all, because) (b:hilo) (r:10.24.24/9.2.24/6.24.21/11.1.43) (q:draft)
hilopi = (t:adv) (w:though not so/falsely) (d:hilo is not with pi; of something that is not so or not rightly so, often as hilopi-in, although it is not) (e:kei’ khialhna hang ~-in/thu a ~-in gen ding | to speak of his word what is not so/Kei’ ngimna ~-in thu vaihawmna a semkhia | carrying out plans that are not my purpose) (b:hilo) (r:19.59.4/23.32.6/23.30.1) (q:draft, low confidence)
hilote = (t:n) (w:those who are not/things that are not) (d:hi be with lo not and the plural te, used after a: the ones that are not) (e:pasian a ~ tawh ka hazat nading/Keima mi pawl a ~ thupha pia-in | blessing those who are not my people/pasian a ~’ siampi suak pahpah hi | he becomes a priest of what are not gods/sihna zah ciang mawhna a ~ ka cihna | I mean sins that do not lead to death) (b:hilo) (r:5.32.21/62.5.16/45.10.19/14.13.9) (q:draft)
Himah = (t:intj) (w:certainly/yes indeed) (d:hi be with the emphatic mah; Himah hi is a reply meaning it is indeed so) (e:~ hi, Kumpipa aw) (r:27.3.24) (q:draft)
himaw = (t:intj) (d:word expressing surprise, joy or sudden emotion)
himawh = (t:v) (w:be anxious/worry/fear) (d:used after lung heart, lung himawh, be anxious, afraid or in doubt; usually written as one word, lunghimawh) (e:nakpi takin ka lung ~ uh a/lung ~ sak loin amau tawh na paikhawm in | go with them without hesitating) (r:6.9.24/44.11.12) (q:draft)
himawhsak = (t:v) (w:make anxious/cause concern) (d:himawh with sak cause, used after lung heart: ka lung hong himawhsak, it troubled me) (e:tua thu in ka lung hong ~ hi) (b:himawh) (r:26.36.21) (q:draft)
himawk = (t:v) (d:hi be with mawk, in a question of surprise or reproach at something thoughtless: bang himawk ahi hiam, what ever is this; exact force not certain) (e:i gamtat bang ~ ahi hiam/thei lo ~ hi lo na hi uh hiam | are you too so lacking in understanding) (r:2.14.5/41.7.18) (q:draft, low confidence)
Himenaius = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hymenaeus) (d:false teacher at Ephesus whom Paul names with Alexander and with Philetus in his letters to Timothy) (r:54.1.20/55.2.17)
hin = (t:v) (w:live/be alive) (d:shortened form of hing, written with an apostrophe before another word, as in ka hin’ lai teng as long as I live and hin’na life) (e:Ka ~’ lai teng Topa/ka ~’ theih nadingun khaici hong pia in | give us seed so that we may live/Naungek a ~’ lai-in an tangin ka kap hi | while the child was alive I fasted and wept/damkik a, a ~’ theih nadingin | so that she may be healed and live) (s:nuntak/nungta) (a:si) (r:19.146.2/45.8.11/1.47.19/10.12.22/41.5.23) (q:draft)
hin = (t:n) (w:life/soul) (d:shortened form written with an apostrophe, the living self) (e:Ka ~’ gim mahmah hi) (s:hinna/nuntakna) (a:sihna) (r:19.6.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
hinapi = (t:conj) (w:although/though/yet) (d:hi, be, with napi, though: even though being so; mostly written hinapi-in after a noun or a clause) (e:Grik mi ~-in a vun ki-atsak tuan lo/Amah, Pasian’ Tapa ~-in | though he was the Son of God/A thahat lo ganhing ~-in | though they are creatures of little strength/a hoih gamta nuam ~-in | although I want to do what is good/Kei a thuman ~ zuauthu genin hong seh hi | though I am right, I am counted a liar) (s:napi) (r:48.2.3/20.30.26/58.5.8/45.7.21/18.34.6) (q:draft)
hing = (t:adj) (w:alive/living) (d:living, not dead; a hing lai mite are those who are still alive) (e:Ai kumpipa ~ mat uh a/A ~ lai mite sangin | than those who are still alive/tu ni-in na ~ lai uh hi | you are still alive today) (s:nungta) (a:sisa) (r:6.8.23/21.4.2/5.4.4)
hingim = (t:v) (w:be in anguish/be troubled) (d:hin soul or life with gim be weary or troubled, written together; elsewhere hin’ gim) (e:Ka ~ mahmah hi) (s:lunggim) (r:19.6.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
hingin = (t:adv) (w:alive/living) (d:hing alive with the ending -in; a hingin man is to capture alive) (e:a ~ amaute man un/Amalekte kumpipa Agag a ~ man a | he took Agag king of the Amalekites alive/eite a ~ hong nawmvalh khin ding uh hi | they would have swallowed us alive/Hih leenggui ~ khang zo ding ahi hiam | will this vine live and thrive) (s:hingtangin) (b:hing) (r:11.20.18/9.15.8/19.124.3/26.17.9) (q:draft)
hingkhawi = (t:v) (w:spare/leave alive/keep alive) (d:let a person live instead of killing, from hing alive and khawi keep) (e:Kuamah ~ kei un la/a kizomte khempeuh Joshua in ~ hi | Joshua spared all who belonged to her/numei ahi a, pasal ahi zongin ~ loin | leaving neither man nor woman alive/amah in amaute khat zong ~ lo hi | he left not one of them alive) (s:hinkhawi/nungtasak) (a:that/thatlum) (r:26.9.5/6.6.25/9.27.9/12.10.14) (q:draft)
hingkhawm = (t:v) (w:live together/live with) (d:hing, live, with khawm, together) (e:Amah tawh i ~ ding hi/amah tawh ei zong i ~ ding hi | we too will live with him/note na hin uhleh ~ | to live with you if you live) (s:hinpih) (a:sikhawm/sihkhawm) (b:hing) (r:55.2.11/45.6.8/47.7.3) (q:draft)
hingkhia = (t:v) (w:give birth/bring forth/deliver) (d:hing, alive, with khia, out: bring a child out alive, be delivered of a child; also used as a figure of speech) (e:zuauthu a ~ hi/a ~ zo lo nupi tawh i kibang hi | we are like a woman who has no strength to give birth/huih bek a ~ tawh ka kibang uh hi | we are like one who gave birth only to wind/Sila a suak tate a ~ nu Hagar | Hagar, the woman who bears children to be slaves) (b:hing) (r:19.7.14/23.37.3/23.26.18/48.4.24) (q:draft)
hingkik = (t:v) (w:come back to life/rise again/revive) (d:hing, alive, with kik, again) (e:sihna pan a ~ Zeisu Khazih/Tanglai kamsangte khatpeuh a ~ hi | one of the prophets of long ago has come back to life/Amaute si a, ~ lo ding uh hi | they are dead and will not live again/a pa uh Jakob’ lungsim ~ hi | the spirit of their father Jacob revived) (s:thokik/hinkik/nungtakik) (a:si) (b:hing) (r:55.2.8/11.17.22/42.9.19/23.26.14/1.45.27) (q:draft)
hingkikin = (t:v) (w:coming back to life/rising again) (d:hingkik with the linking ending in, used when another verb follows: come back to life, and) (e:a sisa mi khat ~ amaute kiangah/mi khat hong ~ amaute kiangah a va gen | someone comes back to life and goes to tell them) (s:thokikin) (b:hingkik) (r:42.16.30/42.16.31) (q:draft)
hingkiksak = (t:v) (w:raise to life/raise/bring back to life) (d:hingkik, come back to life, with sak, cause: make someone live again) (e:Pasian in sihna panin amah ~ a/a ni thum ni-in Pasian in ~ hi | on the third day God raised him to life/Pasian in sihna panin hih Jesuh ~ a | God raised this Jesus from the dead/nangmah in kei nong ~ ding a | you will bring me back to life/singkung keute a ~ Topa | the Lord who makes dry trees live again) (s:thokiksak/hinkiksak/hingsakkik/nungtasakkik) (a:sisak) (b:hingkik) (r:44.13.30/44.3.15/46.15.4/44.2.32/19.71.20/26.17.24) (q:draft)
hingkiksakin = (t:v) (w:raising to life/bringing back to life) (d:hingkiksak, raise to life, with the linking ending in: having raised to life) (e:Sihna panin amah ~ minthanna a pia) (s:hingsakkikin) (b:hingkiksak) (r:60.1.21) (q:draft)
hinglai = (t:adj) (w:still alive/living/surviving) (d:hing, alive, with lai, still: a hinglai mite are the living, those still alive) (e:A ~ mite sangin a si khinsa/tuni-in na ~ uh hi | you are still alive today/a sisa humpinelkai sangin a ~ ui hoihzaw hi | a living dog is better than a dead lion/tuni-a a ~ eite khempeuh tawh | with all of us who are alive today) (s:ahing/nungta) (a:sisa) (r:21.4.2/5.4.4/21.9.4/5.5.3) (q:draft)
hingmat = (t:v) (w:take alive/capture alive) (d:hing, alive, with mat, catch) (e:amaute in tua mite ~ uh hi/Adang tul sawm ~ uh a | they captured another ten thousand alive/le mi tul zakhat ~ uh hi | and they took a hundred thousand people alive/Galte in a sal dingin ~ ta le-uh zong | even if their enemies take them alive as captives) (r:12.10.14/14.25.12/13.5.21/30.9.4) (q:draft)
hingmatin = (t:v) (w:taking alive/capturing alive) (d:hingmat, take alive, with the linking ending in: having taken alive) (e:Ai kumpipa ~ Joshua kiangah) (b:hingmat) (r:6.8.23) (q:draft)
hingsak = (t:v) (w:make alive/give life/preserve/sustain) (d:hing, alive, with sak, cause: make someone live or keep someone alive; with kik, bring back to life) (e:na thu omsa bangin kei hong ~ in/Tapa in zong ama deihte a ~ thei hi | the Son also gives life to those he wishes/Topa in amah hu-in ~ hi | the Lord protects him and keeps him alive/leitungah a om lai mi a ~ ding | to keep alive a remnant on earth) (s:nuntaksak/hinsak/nungtasak) (a:sisak/that) (b:hing) (r:19.119.25/43.5.21/19.41.2/1.45.7) (q:draft)
hingsakin = (t:v) (w:raising to life/making alive) (d:hingsak with the linking ending in, used when another verb follows: make alive, and) (e:Cinate damsakin, misite ~, miphakte damsakin/sihna panin Khrih ~ | raising Christ from the dead) (b:hingsak) (r:40.10.8/49.1.18) (q:draft)
hingsakkik = (t:v) (w:bring back to life/raise again/revive) (d:hingsak, make alive, with kik, again) (e:Topa in thatin ~ a/kei zong sihna panin hong ~ ding hi | he will raise me too from death) (s:hingkiksak/thokiksak/hinkiksak/nungtasakkik) (b:hingsak) (r:9.2.6/50.3.10) (q:draft)
hingsakkikin = (t:v) (w:bringing back to life/reviving) (d:hingsakkik, bring back to life, with the linking ending in) (e:note hong ~, na gam uhah) (s:hingkiksakin) (b:hingsakkik) (r:26.37.14) (q:draft)
hingsakthei = (t:adj) (w:life-giving/able to give life) (d:hingsak make alive with thei can; mi a hingsakthei is that which can make people live) (e:mi a ~ a namtui mahmah) (b:hingsak) (r:47.2.16) (q:draft)
hingsuan = (t:n) (w:rival wife/rival) (d:a second wife taken while the first is living, here the sister of the wife) (e:a sanggamnu a ~ dingin) (s:zipih) (r:3.18.18) (q:draft, low confidence)
hingtangin = (t:adv) (w:alive/while still living) (d:used as a hingtangin: in a living state, without first being killed) (e:Leinuai-ah a ~ amaute paisuksak in/a ~ Leinuai-ah a tumsuk uhleh | if they go down alive into the world of the dead/nomau mahmah a ~ Pasian tungah na kipiak nadingun | that you offer your very selves alive to God/a ~ mei sungah a hal bangin | as he burned them alive in the fire) (s:hingin) (r:19.55.15/45.12.1/4.16.30/24.29.22) (q:draft)
hingtangun = (t:adv) (w:alive/while still living) (d:in a hingtangun, while still alive, said of more than one who is thrown, burnt or swallowed up without first being killed) (e:a ~ Leinuai-ah tumsuk uh hi/meiphualpi sungah a ~ kilawn hi | they were thrown alive into the lake of fire/a ~ hallum ding uh hi | they will burn them alive) (s:hingin) (r:4.16.33/66.19.20/26.23.25) (q:draft)
hingte = (t:n) (w:the living/living ones) (d:hing, alive, with plural te; a hingte gam is the land of the living; also said of green, living plants) (e:A ~ gam sungah/lokung ~ bangin keutum ding uh hi | they will wither like green plants/a ~’ leitang panin nang hong zunglot ding hi | he will uproot you from the land of the living/a ~’ leitangah keima tanh na hi hi | you are my portion in the land of the living) (a:misite/sisate) (b:hing) (r:19.27.13/19.37.2/19.52.5/19.142.5) (q:draft)
hinin = (t:adv) (w:in life/alive) (d:hin live with the ending in; a sih a hinin, in death and in life) (e:A sih a ~ amaute kikhen lo a) (b:hin) (r:10.1.23) (q:draft)
hinkep = (t:v) (w:keep alive/preserve) (d:hin, live, with kep, the form of kem, keep, used before another word: keep someone alive) (e:amaute a ~ theih nadingin) (s:hingsak/nuntaksak) (r:19.33.18) (q:draft)
hinkhawi = (t:v) (w:spare/let live/keep alive) (d:hin, live, with khawi, keep: leave someone alive and not kill him) (e:Kuamah ~ kei unla/kuamah ~ lo a | he spared no one/Hih mipa ~ ding kilawm lo hi | this man ought not to be left alive) (s:hingkhawi/nungtasak) (a:that/thatlum) (r:26.9.5/19.78.50/44.25.24) (q:draft)
hinkhiatna = (t:n) (w:delivery/bringing to birth) (d:hin, live, with khiat, out, and the noun suffix na: the bringing forth of a child alive) (e:amaute ~ ding thatang om lo hi) (s:nausuahna) (r:12.19.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
hinkhiatsak = (t:v) (w:bear/give birth to) (d:hin live with khiat out and sak, bring children forth alive for someone) (e:hih mite hong ~ ahi hiam) (r:23.49.21) (q:draft, low confidence)
hinkik = (t:v) (w:live again/come back to life/rise) (d:hin, live, with kik, again: rise from death) (e:Sihna panin a ~ khit ciangin/Jesuh a ~ khitna thu | the news that Jesus had come back to life/Jesuh a ~ sakna tawh | by raising Jesus to life) (s:hingkik/thokik/nungtakik) (a:si) (b:hin) (r:44.10.41/42.24.23/44.13.32) (q:draft)
hinkikna = (t:n) (w:resurrection/coming back to life) (d:noun form of hinkik, live again) (e:misite zong ~ om hi/A site ~ om lo ding hileh | if there were no resurrection of the dead/a ~ pen Pasian’ vangliatna hang ahi hi | his coming back to life is by the power of God/a sisate nangawn a ~ hong hita ding hi | it will be life again even for the dead) (s:thawhkikna) (a:sihna) (b:hinkik) (r:46.15.21/46.15.30/47.13.4/45.11.15) (q:draft)
hinkiksak = (t:v) (w:restore to life/raise/bring back to life) (d:hinkik, come back to life, with the causative sak: bring a dead person back to life) (e:a tapa a ~ numei kiangah/Pasian in sihna panin a ~ Jesuh | Jesus, whom God raised from the dead/Elisha in a ~ a tapa zong | also her son, whom Elisha restored to life/a tapa a ~ numei in kumpipa kiangah | the woman whose son he had brought back to life, before the king) (s:hingkiksak/thokiksak/hinsakkik) (a:sihsak) (b:hinkik) (r:12.8.1/44.13.37/12.8.5) (q:draft)
hinkiksakna = (t:n) (w:raising to life/resurrection) (d:hinkiksak, restore to life, with the noun suffix na: the act of raising someone from death) (e:sihna panin amah a ~ tawh kisai-in) (s:thawhkiksakna/thawhsakkikna) (b:hinkiksak) (r:44.13.34) (q:draft)
hinlai = (t:v) (w:be still alive) (d:hin, live, with lai, still: be still alive; a hinlai means while someone was still living) (e:Naungek a ~ nangawnin) (s:nungtalai) (r:10.12.18) (q:draft)
hinna = (t:n) (w:life/living) (d:noun form of hin, live: life, being alive; sihna le hinna is death and life, and a hinna dingun means so that they may live) (e:mipilte a dingin ~ tuinak bang hi/sihna ahi a, ~ ahi zongin piangsak thei | can bring about death or life/si loin a ~ dingun hih un | do this so that they may live and not die/hih leitung a ~ pen kei a dingin | life in this world, for me) (s:nuntakna) (a:sihna) (b:hin) (r:20.16.22/20.18.21/4.4.19/21.2.17) (q:draft)
