hoihbek = (t:adj) (w:moderate/just right/due) (d:hoih good with bek only: only as much as is good; a hoihbek takin is in due measure) (e:a ~ takin, hehlua loin) (r:24.10.24) (q:draft, low confidence)
hoihbekin = (t:adv) (w:moderately/modestly/humbly) (d:hoihbek with in: keeping to what is fitting, without pride) (e:a ~ om ding hoihzaw tham hi) (b:hoihbek) (r:20.11.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
hoihbekzah = (t:n) (w:the right amount/due measure) (d:hoihbek just right with zah amount: just as much as is good, said of rain) (e:a ~ hong zusak hi) (r:29.2.23) (q:draft, low confidence)
hoihhoih = (t:adj) (w:well/safe/all right) (d:hoih, good, doubled: asked of a person, whether he is well and unharmed) (e:Tangvalpa Absalom a ~ hiam) (s:hoihkim) (r:10.18.29/10.18.32) (q:draft)
hoihin = (t:adv) (w:well/rightly) (d:hoih, good, with the adverb suffix in: well, in a good way; a hoihin gen is to speak well of someone) (e:David thu a ~ genin/a ~ gamta-in lungnuam takin kong sawlkhiat | we treated you well and sent you away in peace/na lungsim a ~ bawl in la | set your heart right) (s:hoihlamin/phatakin) (a:sialamin) (b:hoih) (r:9.19.4/18.11.13/1.26.29) (q:draft)
hoihin = (t:adj) (w:good) (d:hoih with the linking suffix -in, good and, joined to a following descriptive word) (e:Topa ~ thutang hi/na thugente ~ man hi | your claims are good and right/bangzahin ~ nuam ahi hiam | how good and pleasant it is) (b:hoih) (r:19.25.8/10.15.3/19.133.1) (q:draft, low confidence)
hoihkan = (t:v) (w:be better still/be far better) (d:hoih good with kan exceed: surpass in goodness) (e:bangzahin ~ ding ahi hiam) (r:45.11.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
hoihkhop = (t:adj) (w:considerable/a good deal of/enough) (d:hoih good with khop enough; a hoihkhop khat, a fair amount of time or distance) (e:note kiangah hun ~ khat ka om nuam hi/a ~ khat a gamla, thallot khat tan bangah | a good way off, about a bowshot away/a ~ bek zah ne in | eat just enough) (r:46.16.7/1.21.16/20.25.16) (q:draft)
hoihkim = (t:adj) (w:all well/all right) (d:hoih good with kim complete: well in every way) (e:Thu a ~ hiam) (s:hoihhoih) (r:12.5.21) (q:draft)
hoihlam = (t:adj) (w:favorable/good) (d:hoih, good, with lam, side: on the good side, favorable to a person) (e:a khiatna a ~ hi/kumpipa’ adingin a ~ ding ahi hi | it is favorable for the king) (r:1.40.16/14.18.12) (q:draft)
hoihlamin = (t:adv) (w:favorably/for good/well) (d:hoihlam, the good side, with -in: in a good way, in favour; a hoihlamin gen is to speak favorably) (e:a ~ gen in/eite a dingin na khempeuh a ~ piangsak hi | for us he makes all things turn out for good/thu a ~ a heisakkik ding hi | he will turn things back to good/na dahna uh Pasian in a ~ hong zang | God used your sorrow for good) (s:hoihin/phatakin) (a:sialamin) (b:hoihlam) (r:11.22.13/47.7.9/45.8.28/18.33.26) (q:draft)
hoihlo = (t:adj) (w:bad/not good/evil) (d:hoih, good, with the negative lo, written as one word: not good, bad) (e:na om dan ~ panun) (s:gilo/siat) (a:hoih) (b:hoih) (r:24.15.7) (q:draft)
hoihlohna = (t:n) (w:wickedness/evil/badness) (d:hoih, good, with loh, not, and the noun suffix na: the state of not being good, wicked ways) (e:a ~ uh panin a kihei/amau’ ~ tawh migilote kisusia hi | the wicked are destroyed by their own wickedness/haina a ~ leh a haihuaina | the badness and the madness of folly) (s:gitlohna/siatna) (r:24.36.7/20.11.3/21.7.25) (q:draft)
hoihlohnate = (t:n) (w:wicked deeds/evils) (d:plural of hoihlohna, hoih good with loh not and the noun suffix na: things that are not good, wrongdoing) (e:Topa in na ~ uh leh) (s:gitlohnate/gilohnate) (a:hoihnate) (b:hoihlohna) (r:24.44.22/26.23.48) (q:draft)
hoihlote = (t:adj) (w:bad/evil/wicked) (d:hoihlo, not good, with the plural te; mi hoihlote, evil people, evildoers) (e:Pasian in mi ~ thei takpi hi/mi ~ a hanthawn zawlai uh hi | they even encourage evildoers/na gamtat ~ uh kipuah pha un | reform your evil deeds/a nuntakna ~ panin kikhel sakin | turning them from their evil way of life) (s:gilote/siate) (a:hoihte) (b:hoihlo) (r:18.11.11/24.23.14/24.35.15/24.23.22) (q:draft)
hoihlua = (t:adj) (w:too good/overrighteous) (d:hoih good with lua too much; hoihlua kisa is think oneself too good) (e:Tua ahih ciangin ~ kei inla/amaute ~ kisa uh a | they think themselves too good) (b:hoih) (r:21.7.16/18.30.10) (q:draft)
hoihmah = (t:adj) (w:quite good/right/acceptable) (d:hoih good with the emphatic mah; a hoihmah kisa is think oneself to be doing right) (e:a ~ kisa na hi uh hiam) (b:hoih) (r:39.1.8) (q:draft)
hoihmahin = (t:adv) (w:as right/as quite good) (d:hoihmah with in; a hoihmahin kingaihsun is consider oneself to be doing right) (e:a ~ kingaihsun na hi uh hiam) (b:hoihmah) (r:39.1.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
