Horonaim = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Horonaim) (d:town in the south of Moab, named in the prophecies against Moab; Horonaim khuami renders Horonite, the title of Sanballat) (r:24.48.34/10.13.34)
Horonain = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Horonaim) (d:spelling of Horonaim in Jeremiah 48:3 and 48:5, a town in the south of Moab) (r:24.48.3/24.48.5)
Hosah = (t:name) (c:male/place) (w:Hosah) (d:Levite gatekeeper of the family of Merari in the time of David; also a town on the border of Asher near Tyre) (r:13.26.10/6.19.29)
Hosanna = (t:name) (w:Hosanna) (d:Hebrew shout of praise meaning save now, cried by the crowd when Jesus entered Jerusalem) (r:41.11.9/41.11.10)
Hosea = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hosea) (d:prophet in the northern kingdom of Israel, son of Beeri; also the Bible book that bears his name) (r:28.1.1/28.1.3)
Hoshaiah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hoshaiah) (d:name of two men: a leader of Judah at the dedication of the wall of Jerusalem, and the father of Azariah in the time of Jeremiah) (r:16.12.32/24.42.1)
Hoshama = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hoshama) (d:son of Jehoiachin, the exiled king of Judah) (r:13.3.18)
Hoshea = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hoshea) (d:name of several men, among them the son of Nun whom Moses renamed Joshua and the last king of Israel, son of Elah) (r:4.13.8)
hot = (t:v) (w:row/paddle) (d:move a boat forward with oars; gunkuang hot is to row a boat) (e:tai thum bang a ~ khit uh ciangin/lei lamah a ~ teeiteei uh hi | they kept rowing hard toward land/tuipi thukna gamlapi-ah hong ~ a | they rowed you far out to the deep sea/gunkuang ~ a gim mahmah a om uh | they were worn out with rowing the boat/khuapi mite in nang hong ~ uh a | the men of the city rowed you) (r:43.6.19/32.1.13/26.27.26/41.6.48/26.27.8) (q:draft)
hot = (t:v) (w:save/rescue/deliver) (d:save someone from danger; often followed by khiat, out, as in hot khiat, save out of) (e:lauhuaina pan a ~ bangin/a hong ~ theih leh | if they are able to save you/Israelte bangci ~ khiat ding ka hi hiam | how am I to save Israel/mi khat a nuntakna ~ ding maw | to save the life of a person) (s:honkhia/hon/gum) (r:38.9.16/24.2.28/7.6.15/41.3.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
Hotham = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hotham) (d:name of two men: a son of Heber of the tribe of Asher, and an Aroerite whose sons were among the mighty warriors of David) (r:13.7.32/13.11.44)
Hothir = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hothir) (d:son of Heman, a temple musician in the time of David) (r:13.25.4)
hotkhiat = (t:v) (w:save/deliver/rescue/redeem) (d:form of hotkhia, save or deliver, used before a following word such as ding, nading or a noun; hong hotkhiat ding is often rendered salvation) (e:Israelte na ~ ding leh/Jerusalem a ~ nadingin | in order to deliver Jerusalem/ama ~ vangliatna muang lo uh hi | they did not trust his power to save/eite hong ~ theih nadingin | so that he may rescue us/Saul’ khut sung panin amah a ~ ni-in | on the day he delivered him from the hand of Saul) (s:honkhia/suaktasak) (r:7.6.36/19.119.166/12.18.35/19.78.22/9.7.8/10.22.1) (q:draft)
hotkhiatkik = (t:v) (w:rescue again/save again) (d:hotkhiat, rescue, with kik, again: rescue someone once more) (e:na ~ zelzel kul ding hi) (b:hotkhiat) (r:20.19.19) (q:draft)
hotkhiatna = (t:n) (w:salvation/deliverance/rescue) (d:hotkhiat, save, with the noun suffix na: the act of saving, or the state of being saved from danger or sin) (e:Na ~ ka ngak hi/A ni ni-in ama ~ thu gen un | proclaim his salvation day after day/nangma ~ sungah ka lungdam ding hi | I will rejoice in your salvation/note in ~ na ngah ding uh hi | you will be rescued) (s:gupna/hotna/gupkhiatna/kihotkhiatna) (b:hotkhiat) (r:1.49.18/13.16.23/19.13.5/9.11.9) (q:draft)
Hotkhiatna = (t:n) (w:Salvation) (d:hotkhiatna, salvation, written with a capital as the name given to the walls of Zion) (e:nangmah in na kulhte pen ~) (b:hotkhiatna) (r:23.60.18) (q:draft)
hotkhiatsa = (t:adj) (w:redeemed/saved/delivered) (d:hotkhiat with sa, already done; placed before the noun for the one who has been saved) (e:nangma ~ ka nuntakna zong nuam-in awng ding hi/~ mite in tua lampi tawnin hong ciah ding | the redeemed will return along that road/na ~ Israel mite’ mawhna hong maisak inla | forgive the sin of your people Israel, whom you have redeemed/a thahat na khut tawh ~ na nasemte | your servants whom you redeemed by your mighty hand) (s:tatkhiatsa) (b:hotkhiat) (r:19.71.23/5.21.8/23.35.9/16.1.10) (q:draft)
Hotkhiatte = (t:n) (w:the redeemed/the saved) (d:hotkhiat save or redeem with the plural te: those who are redeemed) (e:A Siangtho Mi, Topa ’ ~ kici ding a) (s:tatkhiatsate) (r:23.62.12) (q:draft)
hotna = (t:n) (w:saving/salvation/deliverance) (d:hot, save, with the noun suffix na: the act of saving someone) (e:nong ~ hangin ka nuam ding hi/a tha zawngkhal kei nong ~ | your saving of the one who has no strength) (s:hotkhiatna/gupna) (b:hot) (r:19.9.14/18.26.2) (q:draft)
hotnop = (t:v) (w:want to save/wish to rescue) (d:hot, save, with nop, want: want to save someone) (e:Pasian in a ~ leh tu-in) (r:40.27.43) (q:draft)
hotte = (t:n) (w:rowers/oarsmen) (d:hot, row, with the plural te: those who row a boat) (e:Nang hong ~ in tuipi thukna gamlapi-ah) (b:hot) (r:26.27.26) (q:draft)
Hovadiah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hodaviah) (d:son of Hassenuah of the tribe of Benjamin; spelling of Hodaviah in 1 Chronicles 9:7) (r:13.9.7)
hu = (t:n) (w:breath) (d:the air that a living being breathes in and out; nuntakna hu is the breath of life) (e:nuntakna ~ a om peuhmah si hi/nuntakna ~ dok kik hi leh | if he took back the breath of life/Ka ~ nangawn hong sang sak man lo a | he does not even let me catch my breath/Pasian’ ~, ka nak-ah ka diik lai teng | as long as I breathe the breath of God in my nostrils) (s:husan/husanna) (r:1.7.22/18.34.14/18.9.18/18.27.3) breath of life
hua = (t:det) (w:that/yonder/that over there) (d:points to something far from both speaker and hearer; hua lai-ah and hua lamah mean over there, in contrast with hih, this) (e:~ lai-ah a om hi/kei leh tangvalpa ~ lamah pai-in | I and the boy will go over there/En un, ~ mite | look at those people/pawlkhat hih lamah pawlkhat ~ lamah om hi | some were on this side and some on that side/~ mite kiangah galkah-in | crossing over to those men) (s:hia) (r:40.24.23/19.104.26/1.22.5/4.23.24/6.8.22/9.14.8) (q:draft)
hua = (t:v) (w:hate/detest/abhor) (d:feel strong dislike for someone or something; the form used before a noun or another verb is huat) (e:thuman a genpa na ~ uh hi/Israelte’ kiphatsakna ka ~ a | I abhor the pride of Israel) (s:mudah/kih) (a:it) (r:30.5.10/30.6.8) (q:draft)
huai = (t:part) (d:suffix added to a verb or adjective, worthy of or causing that feeling, as in kihtak-huai fearsome, lauhuai dreadful and muanhuai trustworthy) (e:A lian a kihtak-~ ama min/a bawlnate ah amah dipkuat-~ hi | he is awesome in his deeds/nang zahtak-~ mahmah teh | you are greatly to be feared/note in a cikzet-~ na hi ding uh hi | you will be a thing of horror) (r:19.99.3/35.1.7/19.66.5/19.76.7/5.28.25) (q:draft)
huaiham = (t:adj) (w:greedy/covetous) (d:eager to have more than one needs; also used of greed or craving itself, as in huaiham luatna, great greed) (e:A ~ mi in kitotna piang sak a/thuman lopi tawh sum zongin a ~ uh hi | they are greedy for dishonest gain/a ~ mi in kiphasakin omkhong thei lo a | the greedy man is arrogant and cannot rest/Amaute ~ luatna in | in their great greed) (a:cingh) (r:20.28.25/46.6.10/24.6.13/35.2.5/61.2.3) (q:draft)
huaihamin = (t:adv) (w:greedily/in greed) (d:huaiham, greedy, with the suffix in: in a greedy way, out of greed) (e:~ gam a deih thuah manun/~, kisialin, kihisakin, mi zahko-in | greedy, boastful, proud and abusive) (s:duhgawhin) (b:huaiham) (r:30.1.13/55.3.2) (q:draft)
huaihamna = (t:n) (w:greed/covetousness/craving) (d:huaiham, greedy, with the noun suffix na: the strong wish to have more than one needs) (e:~ bei ngei lo a/Note in ~ khempeuh kikemin na tang un | be on your guard against all kinds of greed/ka lungsim sungah ~ apawlpawl a piangsak hi | it produced in me every kind of coveting/duhgawh ~ tawh, hazatna tawh | with greed and with envy) (s:duhhopna/deihgawhna/duhluatna) (b:huaiham) (r:18.20.20/41.7.22/42.12.15/45.7.8/45.1.29) (q:draft)
huaihamnate = (t:n) (w:greed/covetous desires) (d:plural of huaihamna: kinds or acts of greed) (e:han’ sanna leh ~ a dim hi/Numei tawh khialhna, lunggulh kihhuaina, apawl pawl ~ | sexual immorality, impurity and every kind of greed) (b:huaihamna) (r:40.23.25/49.5.3) (q:draft)
huaihampa = (t:n) (w:greedy man/covetous man) (d:huaiham, greedy, with pa, a man: a greedy man) (e:ngah nading a ~ in) (b:huaiham) (r:19.10.3) (q:draft)
huaihamte = (t:n) (w:the greedy/greedy people) (d:huaiham, greedy, with the plural te: greedy people) (e:a gutate, a ~, zukhamte) (s:duhhopte) (b:huaiham) (r:46.6.10) (q:draft)
huaina = (t:part) (d:the suffix huai, worthy of or causing, with the noun suffix na: makes a noun for the thing or quality that causes the feeling named, as in muan huaina, safety, a place that can be trusted) (e:lamdangsak ~ ahi ci-in ngaihsun kei un/muan’~ mun-ah amaute paipih | he led them to a safe place/na zum ~ uh hong za khin uh a | they have heard of your shame/nalamdang leh dipkuat ~ apawl pawlte | all kinds of signs and wonders) (b:huai) (r:60.4.12/19.78.53/24.46.12/53.2.9) (q:draft)
huainuam = (t:v) (w:want to gather/long to shelter) (d:huai, gather under the wings as a hen covers her chicks, with nuam want) (e:na mite ka ~ tawntung a) (r:40.23.37/42.13.34) (q:draft)
huaipi = (t:part) (d:huai, worthy of or causing a feeling, with pi great: a kihtak huaipi is a very fearful thing, great terror) (e:a kihtak ~ hong tung hi) (b:huai) (r:18.20.25) (q:draft, low confidence)
huaisa = (t:see) <huaisa-in>
huaisa-in = (t:v) (w:regarding as/deeming) (d:huai worthy of with sa consider and in: muhthadah huaisa-in is considering something detestable, hating it) (e:puante nangawn uh muhthadah ~) (r:65.1.23) (q:draft, low confidence)
huaisak = (t:see) <muan'huaisak>
huaite = (t:part) (d:the suffix huai, worthy of or causing a feeling, with plural te: those who are, or things that are, fearsome, trustworthy and so on; written joined to the word before or separate) (e:ka gal kihtak ~ kiang panin/nalamdangte leh dipkuat ~, vangliatnate tawh | with signs, wonders and miracles/Kulh muan’~ zong nuihsan lel uh a | they laugh at fortified cities too/mi kihtak-~ in keimah hong langpangin kikaikhawm uh hi | fierce men gather together against me) (b:huai) (r:19.17.8/47.12.12/35.1.10/19.59.3) (q:draft)
huaizaw = (t:part) (d:huai, worthy of or causing, with zaw, more: placed after a verb, more worthy of that action, more to be, as in hehpih huaizaw more to be pitied and ngaih huaizaw more worth listening to) (e:mi khempeuh sangin a hehpih ~ mi/dam taka a gen hiathiat ngaih ~ hi | what is said quietly is more worth hearing/A dangte sangin nakpi takin a kihtak ~ hi | it was far more fearsome than the others/Kain’ piakna sangin a santheih ~ biakpiakna | an offering more acceptable than that of Cain) (b:huai) (r:46.15.19/21.9.17/27.7.20/58.11.4) (q:draft)
hualin = (t:v) (w:rolling/having rolled) (d:hual, roll, with the linking ending in, used when another verb follows: roll a stone and then do something) (e:suangtum khat ~ a kongvang a hu hi/suangtum lianpi khat ~ a han kongvang hucipin | rolling a big stone to close the entrance of his tomb) (r:41.15.46/40.27.60) (q:draft)
hualte = (t:n) (w:waves/breakers) (d:plural of hual, wave; tuipi hualte are the waves of the sea) (e:tuipi ~ sangin vanglian zaw hi/tuipi ~ piangsaka, huihpi nungsak hi | he raised the waves of the sea and made the storm blow/huihpi dai sak a tuipi ~ a bei hi | he stilled the storm and the waves of the sea ceased/tuipi ~ bangin hong kuan henhan ding uh hi | they will come up like the waves of the sea) (s:tuihualte) (r:19.93.4/19.107.25/19.107.29/26.26.3) (q:draft)
huam = (t:v) (w:contain/include/take in) (d:hold within itself, as in huam zo lo, cannot contain; in lists of towns, take in or include) (e:hih keima lamsa inn in hong ~ zo lo/vantung a sangpen in nang hong ~ zo lo | the highest heaven cannot contain you/Idalah, le Bethlehem khuate zong ~ a | it also included the towns of Idalah and Bethlehem/Judah minamte’ gam sung khenkhat hong ~ hi | it took in part of the territory of the tribe of Judah) (r:14.6.18/6.19.46/11.8.27/6.19.15/6.19.9) (q:draft)
huam = (t:n) (w:area/bounds/territory) (d:the area that something takes in, in huam sungah, within: gamgi huam sungah, within the borders of) (e:Amau’ gamgi ~ sungah amau’ ten’na/Israel gamgi ~ sungah kei hong zon’ niloh | searching for me within the borders of Israel/Timnathheres-a ama luahna ~ sungah a vui uh hi | they buried him within his inheritance at Timnath Heres/Jezre-el ~ sungah Jezebel ne ding uh hi | they will eat Jezebel within the bounds of Jezreel) (r:13.6.54/9.27.1/7.2.9/11.21.23) (q:draft)
huamin = (t:v) (w:including/covering) (d:huam, include, with the linking ending in: so as to take in, here one name for each of the twelve tribes) (e:minam sawm le nih a ~ a kigelh) (b:huam) (r:2.39.14) (q:draft)
huamkha = (t:v) (w:involve/include/take in) (d:huam include with kha reach, touch: take in or affect all of a group) (e:amaute khempeuh ~ ahih manin) (r:4.15.26) (q:draft)
huamkhak = (t:v) (w:include/cover/apply to) (d:form of huamkha used before another word; a huamkhak mite are the people who come under it) (e:Thuciamna masa in a ~ mite) (b:huamkha) (r:58.9.15) (q:draft)
huamkhin = (t:v) (w:include all/cover completely) (d:huam, include, with khin, completely: take in everything, leave nothing out) (e:na khempeuh a ~ hita hi/a vekpi-in a ~ ahihna kitel hi | it is clear that everything is included) (b:huam) (r:58.2.8/46.15.27) (q:draft)
huamsung = (t:n) (w:sphere/domain/midst) (d:huam, the area that something takes in, with sung, inside: the space within the bounds of something) (e:Amau’ aana neih ~ bekah om loin/Topa’ minthanna ~ panin amaute kihawlkhia ding a | they will be driven out from the presence of the glory of the Lord/Tua upate’ ~, ganhing lite le kumpi tokhom kikalah | in the midst of the elders, between the four living creatures and the throne) (r:65.1.6/66.5.6/53.1.9) (q:draft)
huamteng = (t:n) (w:whole area/all the territory) (d:huam area with teng all: everything within the bounds of, here of the city) (e:leitang le khuapi ~ a kilakkhiat) (b:huam) (r:26.48.21) (q:draft, low confidence)
huan = (t:n) (w:garden) (d:a piece of ground, often enclosed, where trees, flowers and food plants are grown; Eden huan is the garden of Eden) (e:Eden-ah ~ khat bawl hi/a ki-umcip ~ hi a | she is a garden locked up/ka ~ sungah nek theih namkim kidim hi | my garden was full of every kind of food plant/A ~ sungah a tuu cing a | he tends his flock in his garden) (s:huansung) (r:1.2.8/22.4.12/21.2.5/22.6.2)
huan = (t:n) (w:lawn)
Huan = (t:n) (w:garden/paradise) (d:huan capitalised in a name: Eden Huan, the Garden of Eden; Pasian’ Huan, the paradise of God) (e:Eden ~ panin mipa a sawlkhia hi/Pasian’ ~ sunga om nuntakna singgahte | the fruit of the tree of life in the paradise of God/Eden ~ nisuahna lamah a koih hi | he placed them on the east side of the Garden of Eden) (b:huan) (r:1.3.23/66.2.7/1.3.24) (q:draft)
huana = (t:n) (w:in the garden/of the garden) (d:huan, garden, with the place marker a: that is in the garden) (e:Eden ~ singkungte nangawn/Pasian’ ~ singkungte zong tua zahin hoih ngei lo | no tree in the garden of God was ever so beautiful) (b:huan) (r:26.31.18/26.31.8) (q:draft)
huanah = (t:n) (w:in the garden/into the garden/in the field) (d:huan, garden, with the place ending ah: in or into the garden; also of a field or grove where something is grown) (e:Mi khat in ~ a cin ankam tang/singno ~ ka paisuk hi | I went down to the grove of young trees/Ka ngaihno, ka ~ hong paisak unla | let my beloved come into my garden/tua ~ a hong pai uh hi | they came to that garden/Pasian’ ~ a om taamtak hoihte | the fine cedars in the garden of God) (b:huan) (r:42.13.19/22.4.16/22.6.11/43.18.3/26.31.8) (q:draft)
huang = (t:n) (w:court/courtyard/enclosure) (d:an enclosed open space beside a building, such as the courts of the temple or the courtyard of a prison; often as huang sung, inside the court) (e:Jeremiah thong ~ sungah kikalh/i Pasian’ ~ sungah amaute palh uh hi | they flourish in the courts of our God/biakbuk khetphimte leh ~ khetphimte | the tent pegs of the tabernacle and of the courtyard/~ sung leh lote panin uiphukte si hi | the frogs died in the courtyards and the fields) (s:huangsung/inntual/tual) (r:24.39.15/19.92.13/2.35.18/2.8.13) (q:draft)
huangsung = (t:n) (w:courtyard/court/enclosure) (d:the space inside a wall or fence, huang with sung inside; also the bounds or area set for something) (e:Topa’ ~ ka lunggulh mahmah a/Biakinn ~ a lut ciangin | when he entered the temple courts/thong ~ mahah ka omlai hi | I remained in the courtyard of the guard/thong ~ panin kei a hong lakhia uh hi | they took me out of the courtyard of the guard) (s:huang/inntual/tual) (r:19.84.2/24.38.28/43.2.14/24.39.14) (q:draft)
huanhuan = (t:v) (w:cook/prepare food) (d:huan, cook, doubled for an action that is going on: be busy cooking) (e:an a ~ laitakin Peter in) (s:anhuan) (r:44.10.10) (q:draft)
huanin = (t:v) (w:cooking/boiling) (d:huan, cook food by boiling, with the linking ending -in before the next verb) (e:tui tawh ~ ahi zongin ne loin/Khatvei Jakob in meh ~ a om laitakin | once while Jacob was cooking stew/ka tapa ~ amah ka ne uh hi | we cooked my son and ate him/a sate bawngtal kolte tawh ~ mite tungah pia | he cooked the meat with the yokes of the oxen and gave it to the people) (r:2.12.9/12.6.29/1.25.29/11.19.21) (q:draft)
huanna = (t:n) (w:cooking/place for cooking) (d:huan, cook or boil, with -na: the cooking of food; a huanna mun is the place where something is cooked, a huanna anbuk a kitchen) (e:a kipia sate a ~ mun/biakinn sung nasemte in a ~ anbuk ahi hi | these are the kitchens where those who serve in the temple cook/Hih khuapi pen an ~ beel tawh kibang hi | this city is like a cooking pot/biakna sa ~-in nei ding uh hi | they will use them for cooking the meat of the sacrifice) (s:anhuanna) (r:26.46.20/26.46.24/26.11.3/38.14.21) (q:draft)
huanpa = (t:n) (w:baker/cook) (d:in an huanpa, the man who cooks or bakes food: huan, cook, with pa, a man) (e:an piapa leh an ~/an ~ kikhai lum hi | the baker was hanged/kumpipa’ an piapa leh a an ~ in | the cupbearer of the king and his baker) (s:anhuanpa) (r:1.40.5/1.40.1/1.41.13) (q:draft)
huanpipa = (t:n) (w:chief baker/chief cook) (d:used as an huanpipa, the chief baker or head cook: huan, cook, with pi, chief, and pa, a man) (e:an piapipa leh an ~ la khia hi/Josef khiat mah bangin an ~ khailum hi | he hanged the chief baker, just as Joseph had interpreted/kei leh an ~ inncing mangpa’ inn sungah | me and the chief baker, in the house of the captain of the guard/An piapipa leh an ~ ahi | the chief cupbearer and the chief baker) (r:1.40.20/1.40.2/1.40.22/1.41.10) (q:draft)
huansa = (t:adj) (w:cooked/baked/prepared) (d:huan, cook, with sa, already: food that has been cooked; an huansa, cooked food) (e:an ~ namkim Faro’ adingin om hi/ka ~ ka an ne-in | eat the food I have prepared/na ~ bek mah na ne thei ding | you may eat only what you have cooked) (s:kihuansa) (r:1.40.17/20.9.5/2.12.16) (q:draft)
huansung = (t:n) (w:garden/inside of a garden) (d:huan, garden, with sung, inside: the garden as an enclosed place) (e:kumpipa’ ~ tawnin kulh tegel/Uzza’ ~ ama hanah amah kivui a | he was buried in his tomb in the garden of Uzza/ka ~ hong tungzo ing | I have come into my garden/ama gamlakte Eden ~ ka bangsak ding a | I will make her wilderness like the garden of Eden) (s:huan) (r:24.39.4/12.21.18/12.21.26/22.5.1/23.51.3) (q:draft)
huante = (t:n) (w:gardens/groves) (d:huan, garden, with plural -te; oliv huante are olive groves) (e:gun gei-a om ~ tawh kibang hi/Na ~ uh leh na leenggui lote uh | your gardens and your vineyards/oliv ~ leh leenggui lote | olive groves and vineyards) (b:huan) (r:4.24.6/30.4.9/12.5.26) (q:draft)
huantui = (t:v) (w:smelt/melt out) (d:melt metal out of ore; apparently huan cook, heat with tui liquid) (e:suang sung panin sumsan ~ uh hi) (s:haltui) (r:18.28.2) (q:draft)
