Innah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Imnah) (d:a Levite, father of Kore; apparently a misprint of Imnah) (e:Levi mi ~ tapa Kore in) (r:14.31.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
innbul = (t:n) (w:foundation/base) (d:inn, house, with bul, base: the base on which a building stands) (e:thong ~ zong liing a/~ suangnuai phahin kizang lo ding hi | it will not be used as a foundation stone) (s:bulpi/tawphah) (r:44.16.26/24.51.26) (q:draft)
inncin = (t:see) <inncin'na>
inncin'na = (t:n) (w:guarding/guard duty) (d:inncing, guard, with the noun suffix na: the keeping of guard; inncin'na inndei is the guardroom) (e:~ inndei sungah tuate koihkik zel) (s:inncinna) (r:11.14.28) (q:draft)
inncing = (t:n) (w:guard/palace guard/bodyguard) (d:one who guards a house or palace; inncing mangpa is the captain of the guard and inncing a ukte the commanders of the guard) (e:~ mangpa’ inn sungah/~ a ukte’ khut sungah tuate ap hi | he entrusted them to the commanders of the guard/inn kongkhak a cing ~ uliante’ khut sungah | into the hands of the guard commanders who kept the palace door/Izipt gamsunga ~ mang | the captain of the guard in Egypt) (s:cingpa) (r:1.40.3/14.12.10/11.14.27/1.37.36) (q:draft)
inncingte = (t:n) (w:guards) (d:inncing, guard, with the plural te: the guards of a palace) (e:~ in tuate pua-in) (s:cingte) (b:inncing) (r:11.14.28) (q:draft)
inncinna = (t:n) (w:guarding/guard duty) (d:inncing, guard, with the noun suffix na: the keeping of guard; inncinna inndei is the guardroom) (e:~ inndei sungah tuate koihkik zel) (s:inncin'na) (r:11.14.28) (q:draft)
inndap = (t:n) (w:ceiling/roofing) (d:the boards that cover a room overhead, from inn, house, and dap, line with boards; inndap bawl is to roof or ceil a house) (e:taamtaak peekte tawh ~ bawl hi/inn sual panin ~ innsunte dongin | from the floor of the house to the ceiling) (s:innsun) (r:11.6.9/11.6.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
inndei = (t:n) (w:room/chamber) (d:a room or chamber in a house, palace or temple; inndei sung is the inside of a room and lupna inndei a bedroom) (e:Hih ~ golzaw a teh ciangin/hong pai-in ~ sungah lut a | he came and went into the room/~ sung panin Tobiah’ van teng ka lawnkhia hi | I threw all Tobiah’s goods out of the room/Kumpi tanu a ~ sungah | the king’s daughter in her chamber) (s:dei) (r:26.40.8/11.6.30/12.4.11/16.13.8/19.45.13) (q:draft)
inndeineu = (t:n) (w:small room) (d:inndei, room, with neu, small: a small room) (e:kawm a nei ~ khat bawlin) (r:12.4.10) (q:draft)
inndeipi = (t:n) (w:main hall/portico/great room) (d:inndei, room, with pi, great: a large hall; in Ezekiel the main hall or portico of the temple) (e:Hih ~ sung kawmte tungah/~ kongpi mah-ah pusuak ding hi | he shall go out by the same portico gateway/Amah hong pai ciangin ~ tawnin | when he comes, by way of the portico) (s:deipi) (b:inndei) (r:26.41.26/26.41.23/26.46.8/26.44.3) (q:draft)
inndeite = (t:n) (w:rooms/chambers/storerooms) (d:inndei, room, with the plural te: the rooms of a building, in the temple also the storerooms) (e:inn sung vankoihna ~ a uk dingin/A cial tungnung-a om ~ pen | the rooms on the upper floor/~ a bawl nading uh Hezekiah in thupia hi | Hezekiah gave orders to prepare rooms/hih ~ mai-ah zong lampi khat om hi | in front of these rooms too there was a passage) (s:deite) (b:inndei) (r:16.13.4/11.6.29/26.42.5/14.31.11/26.42.11) (q:draft)
inndung = (t:n) (w:length of the building) (d:inn, house, with dung, length: the length of a building, set against its vai, the width) (e:hih ~ tong za khat hi a) (r:26.42.2) (q:draft)
inngualte = (t:n) (w:rows of rooms/rows of houses) (d:inn house with gual row and plural te: rooms or buildings standing in a row) (e:tua ~ tawh a paikhawm) (r:26.42.7) (q:draft)
innhikpi = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:chameleon) (s:thankik)
innhikpi = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:lizard/great lizard) (d:a large lizard, named among the unclean creatures that move along the ground) (e:savokphual, zusa, ~ nam khempeuh) (s:tangteuh) (r:3.11.29)
Innhikte = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:lizards/lizard) (d:a small creature that can be held in the hand and yet lives in the palaces of kings; apparently innhik with the plural suffix te; the NIV has lizard and older versions spider) (e:~: khut sunga tawi zawh ganhing) (r:20.30.28) (q:draft, low confidence)
innkalte = (t:n) (w:beams/rafters) (d:the timbers laid across a house to carry the ceiling or roof, with the plural te) (e:~ leh taamtaak peekte tawh inndap bawl) (s:innkamte) (r:11.6.9) (q:draft)
innkam = (t:n) (w:beam/rafter/timber) (d:a large beam of wood in the frame of a house) (e:a ~ khat kidawh khiatsakin/taamtaak ~ kikhung tungah kilam hi | it was built on cedar beams laid across/inn kawm sungah ~ nan’na a lut loh nadingin | so that the beam supports would not go into the walls of the house) (r:15.6.11/11.7.2/11.6.6) (q:draft)
innkamte = (t:n) (w:beams/rafters/joists) (d:innkam, beam, with the plural te: the timbers that carry the roof or floor of a house) (e:~ in zong kikopih ding uh hi/inn lam nadingin ~ lei nadingin | to buy beams for building the houses/~ khungin taamtak peekte tawh inndap a bawl hi | he laid the beams and made the ceiling with cedar planks) (s:innkalte) (b:innkam) (r:35.2.11/11.6.9/14.34.11) (q:draft)
innkhangte = (t:n) (w:neighbours below) (d:those whose houses are on the lower side of one's own; innsak and innkhang together are the neighbours on either side) (e:a innsak a ~’ kiangah) (r:24.22.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
innkhuam = (t:n) (w:pillar/post/foundation) (d:inn, house, with khuam, post: the post that carries a house; in the letters of Paul the foundation on which a building is set) (e:Zeisu Khazih longal ~ dang kuamah in/taamtaak kungte, i ~ hi-in | cedars are the posts of our house/~ lianpipite leilak kiden’ nading hi | the great pillars will be thrown to the ground/kamsangte in a phuhsa ~ tungah | on the foundation laid by the prophets) (s:khuam/khuampi) (r:46.3.11/26.26.11/22.1.17/49.2.20) (q:draft)
innkhuampi = (t:n) (w:pillar/main pillar) (d:innkhuam, house post, with pi, great: a main pillar of a house) (e:a ~ sagih a phut hi) (s:khuampi) (b:innkhuam) (r:20.9.1) (q:draft)
innkhuamte = (t:n) (w:pillars/supports/posts) (d:innkhuam, house post, with the plural te: the posts or supports of a building) (e:Topa’ biakinn le kumpipa’ ~) (s:khuamte/khuampite) (b:innkhuam) (r:11.10.12) (q:draft)
innkhum = (t:n) (w:roof/housetop) (d:the top of a house; innkhum zang is the flat roof, innkhum dawn the rooftop) (e:~ tungah a omte in zong/~ dawn-a vasa khatguak om tawh ka kibang hi | I am like a lone bird on a rooftop/kumpi ~ zang huan sungah vak a | he was walking in the garden on the palace roof/~ vumah kiko-in na gen un | proclaim it from the rooftops) (s:khum/innkhumzang/tungkhum) (r:40.24.17/19.102.7/27.4.29/40.10.27) (q:draft)
innkhumdawn = (t:n) (w:rooftop/housetop/roof) (d:innkhum, roof, with dawn, top: the top of the roof of a house) (e:~ zangah na taangko un) (s:innkhum/innkhumzang) (r:40.10.27) (q:draft)
innkhumzang = (t:n) (w:roof/housetop) (d:the flat top of a house, where people can walk or stay) (e:~ kiu khat-a tang teen’ hoihzaw/~ amaute kiangah amah paito a | she went up to them on the roof/~ leh kongzing lampi kituahnate ah | on the roofs and at the street crossings) (s:innkhum/khumzang) (r:20.21.9/6.2.8/23.15.3) (q:draft)
innkhumzanga = (t:n) (w:on the roof/on the housetop) (d:innkhumzang, roof, with the place marker a) (e:~ lopate bangin a om laitak/Samuel in ~ Saul samin | Samuel called to Saul on the roof/a khan khit ma-a a vul, ~ lopa | grass on the roof that withers before it grows) (s:innkhumzangah/khumzanga) (b:innkhumzang) (r:12.19.26/9.9.26/19.129.6) (q:draft)
innkhumzangah = (t:n) (w:on the roof/on the housetop/to the roof) (d:innkhumzang, the flat roof of a house, with the place ending -ah) (e:~ Peter a kahto hi/~ Absalom’ adingin puanbuk khat lam uh hi | they pitched a tent for Absalom on the roof/~ Saul a dingin lupna khat na kiphah a | a bed had been spread for Saul on the roof/ama giahna ~ puato-in | he carried him up to the roof room where he was staying) (s:innkhumzanga/khumzangah) (b:innkhumzang) (r:44.10.9/10.16.22/9.9.25/11.17.19) (q:draft)
innkiim = (t:see) <innkiim-ah>
innkiim-ah = (t:adv) (w:around the house) (d:innkiim, the surroundings of a house, with ah, at) (e:kote’ omna ~ hong pang uh hi) (r:7.20.5) (q:draft)
innkim = (t:n) (w:surroundings of the house) (d:the area all around a house, here the temple; probably the same word as innkiim) (e:biakna tau leh ~ ah koih hi) (r:14.23.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
innkiu = (t:n) (w:corner of a house) (d:inn house with kiu corner; innkiu suang is the cornerstone) (e:~ suang bulpi suak khin ta hi/A nung ciangin ~ suang a piang hi | afterwards it became the cornerstone/Na suangte ~ suangin kiciang lo ding a | none of your stones will be used for a cornerstone/Amaute sung panin ~ suang | from among them the cornerstone) (r:19.118.22/41.12.10/24.51.26/38.10.4) (q:draft)
innkiunuai = (t:n) (w:cornerstone/foundation of the corner) (d:inn house, kiu corner, nuai under; innkiunuai suang is the cornerstone) (e:Khazih in tua ~ suang ahi hi) (r:49.2.20) (q:draft)
innkongah = (t:adv) (w:at the doorway/to the door of the house) (d:innkong, the doorway of a house, with ah, at or to) (e:innsung panin ~ siampipa paikhia ding a) (r:3.14.38) (q:draft)
innkuan = (t:n) (w:family) (d:the people of one house and line, parents and children together) (e:~ ciat tawh ahi/A khedap a kikaih khiatsak mipa’ ~ | the family of the man whose sandal was pulled off/Midian ~ sungah a beh lutang | head of a clan in a Midianite family) (s:innkuanpih) (r:2.1.1/5.25.10/4.25.15)
innkuan = (t:n) (w:household) (e:~ ading cik ciangin/a ~ sung kisapna teng sem a | she sees to all the needs of her household/ka ~ teng na si sak khin hi | you have destroyed my whole household/A ~ sung a uk khial mite | those who mismanage their household) (s:innsung/innkuansung) (r:1.30.30/1.20.18/20.31.27/18.16.7/20.11.29)
innkuanin = (t:adv) (w:family by family/by households) (d:innkuan, family, with in: by family; doubled as innkuan innkuanin, one family after another) (e:a innkuan ~ hong pai ding hi) (s:innkuankuanin/innkuankuan) (b:innkuan) (r:6.7.14) (q:draft)
innkuankuan = (t:adv) (w:family by family/by families) (d:innkuan, family, doubled: each family in turn; often with -in or -un added) (e:a ~ leh a beh beh-in/Mite a ~-un, a milip-in a puanbuk kongah | the people, every family, all of them at their tent doors/a beh tawh kizui-in a ~-in | by their clans, family by family/amau’ ~ leh a beh beh-in sim in | count them by their families and clans) (s:innkuankuanin/innkuankuanun) (r:4.4.42/4.1.2/4.11.10/4.2.34/4.4.22) (q:draft)
innkuankuanin = (t:adv) (w:family by family/by families/by clans) (d:innkuankuan, each family in turn, with -in) (e:a beh tawh kizui-in a ~/Levi mite, a behbeh, a ~ | the Levites, clan by clan, family by family/Gam sung khempeuhah a ~ dahin kap ding uh | throughout the land they will mourn, family by family/beh sung panin a ~ hong pai ding hi | from the clan they shall come forward family by family) (s:innkuankuan/innkuankuanun/innkuanin) (b:innkuankuan) (r:4.2.34/4.3.15/38.12.12/6.7.14) (q:draft)
innkuankuanun = (t:adv) (w:family by family/by their families) (d:innkuankuan with un, the plural marker uh joined with in) (e:Mite a ~ a milipin/Topa’ thupiakna tawh a ~ a sim Levi mi | the Levites counted family by family at the Lord’s command) (s:innkuankuanin/innkuankuan) (b:innkuankuan) (r:4.11.10/4.3.39) (q:draft)
innkuanmi = (t:n) (w:household members/people of the household) (d:innkuan household with mi, person) (e:a ne ding ~ a tawmluat leh) (b:innkuan) (r:2.12.4) (q:draft)
innkuanpih = (t:n) (w:family) (e:tu-a kipanin ~ nga a om/mi khempeuh a ~ ciat tawh paipih to hi | he brought up every man with his family/Na pa’ ~ mite khempeuh’ sihna | the death of all your father’s family) (s:innkuan) (r:42.12.52/10.2.3/9.22.22)
innkuanpih = (t:n) (w:relative) (d:a person who belongs to the same family; innkuanpih mite are the members of a family) (e:kumpipa’ ~ mite khat la-in | he took a member of the royal family/ama ~ mite mah hong hi ding hi | they will be the members of his own household) (s:tanau) (r:26.17.13/40.10.36)
innkuanpihte = (t:n) (w:families/family members/household) (d:innkuanpih, family, with the plural te: families, or the members of one family) (e:i pa leh na ~ uh la un/note leh na ~ na lungdam ding uh hi | you and your families shall rejoice/ka ~ lakah khualmi ka suak hi | I have become a stranger among my own family/ama ~ mah a gal hong suak ding hi | his own family members will become his enemies) (s:innkuante) (b:innkuanpih) (r:1.45.18/5.12.7/19.69.8/40.10.36)
innkuanpite = (t:n) (w:household/whole family/family members) (d:all the members of a household; Genesis 46:31 has innkuanpite and innkuanpihte side by side for the same thing, so probably innkuanpih, family member, with plural -te) (e:nang leh na ~ leh na neih khempeuh/Rahab, leh a pa ~ | Rahab and her father’s household/a sanggamte leh a pa’ ~ kiangah | to his brothers and his father’s household/note leh na ~ na lungdam ding uh hi | you and your household shall rejoice) (s:innkuante/innkuansung) (b:innkuan) (r:1.45.11/5.11.6/6.6.25/1.46.31/5.14.26) (q:draft)
innkuansung = (t:n) (w:household/family) (d:innkuan, family, with sung, inside: those who belong to one house and family) (e:a tate le a ~ hoihtakin a ukzote/a ~ kisapna teng sem a | she sees to all the needs of her household/Faro in zong Josef ~ thu na thei hi | Pharaoh too learned about Joseph’s family/amau ~ ukin a om ding uh | that they should manage their own households) (s:innkuan/innsung) (r:54.3.12/20.31.27/44.7.13/54.5.14) (q:draft)
innkuante = (t:n) (w:household/family/house) (d:innkuan, family, with the plural te: the members of a family or household; Aaron innkuante is the house of Aaron) (e:Aaron ~ in ci ta uh hen/Onesiforas’ ~ na hopihsak in | greet the household of Onesiphorus/na pa’ ~ na si taktak ding uh hi | your father’s family will surely die/nang leh na ~ in an ne ding uh | you and your family shall eat) (s:innkuanpite) (b:innkuan) (r:19.118.3/55.4.19/9.22.16/5.15.20) (q:draft)
innlak = (t:n) (w:relative/kin) (d:of the father's family; innlak pa is an uncle, innlak nu an aunt, innlak sanggampa a cousin) (e:ka ~ sanggampa Hanamel tawh/a ~ sanggampa in tanh thei ding hi | his cousin may redeem him/tua nu in nangma ~ nu ahi hi | she is your aunt/a ~ pa Abihail’ tanu Esther | Esther, the daughter of his uncle Abihail) (s:tanau) (r:24.32.12/3.25.49/3.18.14/17.2.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
innlam = (t:n) (w:building/house-building/builder) (d:inn, house, with lam, build: the building of houses, and those who build; innlam siamte are skilled builders and lei-le-suang innlam siamte stonemasons) (e:lei-le-suang ~ siamte zong puak hi/tua khuam phuhsa tungah ~ a zom hi | he continues the building on the foundation already laid/leilesuang ~ a siamte, le khutsiamte zong a puak | he also sent skilled stonemasons and craftsmen) (s:innlamna/lamna) (r:10.5.11/44.4.11/46.3.10/13.14.1) (q:draft)
innlam = (t:n) (w:way home) (d:the direction of one's house) (e:a ~ zon’na in gim ding uh) (r:21.10.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
innlamna = (t:n) (w:house-building/construction) (d:innlam building of houses, with the noun suffix na) (e:~ panin a meet i ngah ding) (s:innlam/lamna) (b:innlam) (r:26.11.3) (q:draft)
innlamte = (t:n) (w:builders) (d:innlam, house-building, with the plural te: those who build houses) (e:khutsiamte leh ~ tungah pia uh hi/No ~ in na nilkhiat uh suangtum | the stone you builders rejected/Solomon’ mi ~, Hiram’ mi ~ leh Gebal mite | Solomon’s builders, Hiram’s builders and the men of Gebal/~’ sepna a mawkna ahi hi | the builders’ work is in vain) (s:lamte) (b:innlam) (r:14.34.11/12.22.6/44.4.11/11.5.18/19.127.1) (q:draft)
innlelo = (t:n) (w:home/homestead/house and land) (d:inn house, le and, lo field written as one word: a home of one's own with its land; innlelo nei lo is homeless) (e:a tenna ding ~ guan a/~ nei loin ka omna | my being without a home) (r:19.68.6/25.3.19) (q:draft)
innliim = (t:n) (w:portico/porch/colonnade) (d:the roofed porch at the front of a building, in the verses that of the temple; also spelled innlim) (e:Inn mai-a ~ in inn vai tawh/Solomon’ ~ ah a kawi pai hi | he was walking in Solomon’s Colonnade/A mai lamah khuampite a nei ~ om a | in front of it was a portico with pillars/~ kongkhakte zong khakin meivakte sumit uh a | they shut the doors of the portico and put out the lamps) (s:innlim) (r:14.3.4/43.10.23/11.7.6/14.29.7) (q:draft)
innlim = (t:n) (w:portico/porch) (d:the roofed porch at the front of a building, in the verses that of the temple; also spelled innliim) (e:~ kongkhakte zong khakin/Biakinn mai-a ~ in inn zaina zahin | the portico at the front of the temple, as wide as the house/~-a om khuampi dawnah | on top of the pillars in the portico/a khuampite biakinn ~-ah phut hi | he set up the pillars at the portico of the temple) (s:innliim) (r:14.29.7/11.6.3/11.7.19/11.7.21) (q:draft)
innlimah = (t:adv) (w:at the portico/to the portico) (d:innlim portico with the place marker ah) (e:biakinn ~ khuampite a phut hi/Topa’ ~ amaute hong pai uh hi | they came to the portico of the Lord) (b:innlim) (r:11.7.21/14.29.17) (q:draft)
innluah = (t:v) (w:inherit/be heir) (d:take over the house and property of the family as heir; innluah mi or innluah pa is the heir and innluah za the right of the heir) (e:thuciamna bangin ~ mi na hi uh hi/tapa tawh ~ khawm thei lo ding hi | he cannot inherit together with the son/annek khat tawh ~ za a zuak mi | one who sold his birthright for a single meal/amaute in ~ pa zong susia ding uh hi | they will destroy the heir as well) (s:luah) (r:48.3.29/48.4.30/58.12.16/10.14.7) (q:draft)
innluahna = (t:n) (w:inheritance) (d:innluah, inherit, with the noun suffix na: what is received as an heir) (e:~ in thukham tawh kipawl ahih leh) (s:luahna/gamhluahna) (b:innluah) (r:48.3.18) (q:draft)
innluahpa = (t:n) (w:heir) (d:innluah, inherit the house, with pa, a man: the son who inherits) (e:Pasian hangin ~ zong na hi uh hi/~ in sum khempeuh a ukpa ahih hangin | although the heir is owner of everything/amaute in ~ zong susia ding uh hi | they will destroy the heir as well) (s:gamhluahpa) (b:innluah) (r:48.4.7/48.4.1/10.14.7) (q:draft)
innluahza = (t:n) (w:birthright/right of the firstborn) (d:the right of the firstborn son to inherit the house, from innluah, inherit, and za, rank) (e:Na ~ hong pia lecin/~ pen Josef’ aa ahi hi | the birthright belonged to Joseph/Jakob' tungah a ~ zuak hi | he sold his birthright to Jacob/kei’ adingin ~ bang-a kimang ahi hiam | what use is the birthright to me) (r:1.25.31/13.5.2/1.25.33/1.25.32) (q:draft)
innmong = (t:n) (w:end of the house) (d:inn house with mong, end or edge) (e:Eliashib’ ~ ciang dong) (r:16.3.21) (q:draft)
innpi = (t:n) (w:temple/great house/hall) (d:inn, house, with pi, great: a great house or main hall; biakna innpi is the temple and Pasian’ innpi the house of God) (e:Biakna ~ dalna puan/Pasian’ ~ a uk siampi ukpa | the high priest who rules over the house of God/Tua kham a siangthosak biakna ~ | the temple that makes the gold sacred/taaksan tawh a ~ kawm dapin | he paneled the walls of the main hall with juniper) (b:inn) (r:42.23.45/58.10.21/40.23.17/14.3.5) (q:draft)
innpite = (t:n) (w:palaces/great houses) (d:innpi, a great house such as a palace or temple, with plural te) (e:Saiha tawh kibawl ~ panin/~ a do khuampite hong lawngsak in | let me feel the pillars that hold up the great house) (b:innpi) (r:19.45.8/7.16.26) (q:draft)
innpua = (t:see) <innpua-ah>
innpua-ah = (t:adv) (w:outside/outside the house) (d:innpua, the outside of a house, with ah, at) (e:~ om uh hi) (s:pualamah) (a:innsunga) (r:42.8.20) (q:draft)
innsa = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:livestock) (d:inn, house, with sa, animal: animals kept at the house, set against gamsa, wild animals) (e:~, gamsa, leh a bokvak ganhingte/~ khempeuh amau’ nam ciat | all livestock according to their kinds) (s:gan) (a:gamsa) (r:1.1.24/1.7.14)
innsa = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:pet)
innsak = (t:n) (w:neighbour above) (d:the house or people on the upper side of one's own; innsak and innkhang together are the neighbours on either side) (e:a ~ a innkhangte’ kiangah) (b:inn) (r:24.22.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
innsate = (t:n) (w:livestock/cattle/domestic animals) (d:innsa, animal kept at the house, with plural -te; set against gamsate, the wild animals) (e:Gamsate leh ~ khempeuh/vasate, ~, gamsate | birds, livestock and wild animals/a om gamsate leh ~ khempeuh phawk hi | he remembered all the wild animals and livestock that were there) (s:gankhawite) (a:gamsate) (b:innsa) (r:19.148.10/1.7.21/1.8.1) (q:draft)
innsia = (t:n) (w:ruins/ruined house) (d:inn, house, with sia, spoiled: houses fallen into ruin; innsia losia is ruined houses and fields, a heap of ruins) (e:~ lakah a om ngiate tawh/Babilon khuapi pen ~ losia suak ding a | Babylon will become a heap of ruins) (r:26.13.4/24.51.37) (q:draft)
innsualte = (t:n) (w:floors) (d:inn, house, with sual, floor, and the plural te: the floors of the rooms of a house) (e:inndei sung ~ amah in kham tawh) (s:sualte) (r:11.6.30) (q:draft)
innsun = (t:n) (w:ceiling/ceiling beam/rafter) (d:the top of a room or the beams there; sual panin innsun dong, from floor to ceiling) (e:Amah in sual panin ~ dong/a sual panin a ~ ciang dong | from its floor to its ceiling) (s:inndap) (a:sual) (r:11.6.16/11.7.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
innsung = (t:n) (w:household/family/home) (d:inn, house, with sung, inside: the inside of a house, and so the home and the people who live in it) (e:numei haite in ~ susia hi/man lo-a sum ngahna in ~ lungkham sak a | dishonest gain brings trouble to the household/thuman mite’ ~ thupha a pia hi | he blesses the home of the righteous/ka ~ uhah gamdang mite a teeng uh hi | foreigners live in our homes) (s:innkuan/innkuansung) (r:20.14.1/20.15.27/20.3.33/25.5.2) (q:draft)
innsunga = (t:adv) (w:in the house/in the household) (d:innsung, the inside of a house or a household, with the place ending a; innsunga om, who or which is in the house) (e:a ~ om mi khempeuh tui kiphum/kikhopna ~ om mi khempeuh a heh mahmah uh | everyone in the synagogue was furious/Pasian’ ~ a om oliv kung | an olive tree in the house of God/na ~ om khempeuh | everything that is in your house) (s:Innsungah) (a:innpua-ah) (b:innsung) (r:44.16.15/12.20.17/42.4.28/19.52.8) (q:draft)
Innsungah = (t:adv) (w:into the house/in the house/indoors) (d:innsung, the inside of the house, with the place marker ah, here at the start of a sentence) (e:~ Jesuh a tumkhit ciangin/~ Peter a lut ciangin | when Peter came into the house/~ a tumkhit uh ciangin nungzuite in | when they had gone into the house, the disciples/~ a lut mi khempeuh in | all who come into the house) (s:innsunga) (a:innpua-ah) (r:41.9.28/41.10.10/40.17.25/42.11.33) (q:draft)
innsungmang = (t:n) (w:court official/eunuch/palace officer) (d:innsung, the inside of the house, with mang, officer: an official who serves inside the royal house, in the Bible often a eunuch) (e:kumpipa’ ~ Hegai’ kep dingin/~ lian pen Ashpenaz thu a pia hi | he gave orders to Ashpenaz, the chief court official/kumpipa’ ~ Shaashgaz in kem hi | Shaashgaz, the king’s eunuch, kept charge of them/Babylon kumpipa’ inn sungah ~ nasep kisemsak ding hi | they will be made to serve as eunuchs in the palace of the king of Babylon) (r:17.2.3/27.1.3/17.2.14/23.39.7) (q:draft)
innsungmangte = (t:n) (w:court officials/eunuchs/attendants) (d:innsungmang, court official, with the plural te: the officials who serve inside a royal house, often eunuchs) (e:kumpipa’ ~ hong pai a/Vashti in ~’ thupuak kumpipa’ sapna a nial hi | Vashti refused the king’s summons brought by the eunuchs/kumpipa ~ lak panin Hathak a kici mipa samin | she summoned Hathak, one of the king’s eunuchs/kumpipa’ na a sem ~ lakah Harbona in | Harbona, one of the eunuchs attending the king) (b:innsungmang) (r:17.6.14/17.1.12/17.4.5/17.7.9) (q:draft)
innsunte = (t:n) (w:ceiling beams/rafters) (d:innsun, ceiling beam, with the plural te) (e:a ~, a sangkilte, a kawmte/inn sual panin inndap ~ dongin | from the floor of the house to the ceiling beams) (s:innkamte) (b:innsun) (r:14.3.7/11.6.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
innte = (t:n) (w:houses/buildings) (d:inn, house, with the plural te: houses, or the buildings of a town) (e:kulhpi siate puah nadingin ~ na phel hi/~ a kilam om nai lo hi | the houses had not yet been built/Hih a lian mahmah ~ na mu uh hiam | do you see these great buildings/David khuapi sungah ~ lam hi | he built houses in the City of David) (b:inn) (r:23.22.10/16.7.4/41.13.2/13.15.1) (q:draft)
innteek = (t:n) (w:house owner/householder/master of the house) (d:the person to whom a house belongs; innteek pa is the man who owns the house, also the master for whom someone works) (e:a ~ pa kiangah/~ pa a heh suak a | the owner of the house became angry/~ pa in vokcing dingin ama lo-ah a sawl | his master sent him to his fields to feed pigs/a ~ pa Jason le midang pawlkhat kaikhia-in | they dragged out Jason, the owner of the house, and some others) (s:teekpa) (r:42.22.11/42.14.21/42.15.15/44.17.6) (q:draft)
inntual = (t:n) (w:courtyard/court) (d:inn, house, with tual, open ground: the open space in front of or enclosed by a house, palace or temple) (e:~ lai zangah mei cih uh a/Piter in siampi ukpa’ ~ dongin | Peter, right up to the courtyard of the high priest/~ laita panin Isaiah a paikhiat ma-in | before Isaiah had left the middle court/siampite’ ~, leh ~ lian | the courtyard of the priests and the large court) (s:tual/huang) (r:42.22.55/41.14.66/41.14.54/12.20.4/14.4.9) (q:draft)
inntualah = (t:adv) (w:in the courtyard/into the courtyard) (d:inntual courtyard, the open space before a house, with the place marker ah) (e:Piter ~ a tut lai takin/galkapte in gam ukpa’ ~ Jesuh paipih uh a | the soldiers led Jesus into the governor’s courtyard/Tua khuami khempeuh a ~ hong kikhawm uh hi | the whole town gathered in his courtyard/A nuai-a ~ Peter a om laitakin | while Peter was below in the courtyard) (b:inntual) (r:40.26.69/41.15.16/41.1.33/41.14.66) (q:draft)
inntualte = (t:n) (w:courts/courtyards) (d:inntual, courtyard, with plural te) (e:Ka inn leh ka ~ a bawl dingpa/~ leh inndeite kemin | looking after the courtyards and the rooms) (s:tualte) (b:inntual) (r:13.28.6/13.23.28) (q:draft)
inntuan = (t:v) (w:divide the inheritance/give a share of the property) (d:literally set up a separate house; give a brother his share of the family property) (e:kei hong ~ nadingin hong gensak in) (r:42.12.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
innveng = (t:n) (w:neighbourhood/neighbour) (d:the houses near one's own and those who live there) (e:Mikah’ ~ a om mite) (s:veng) (r:7.18.22) (q:draft)
innvengte = (t:n) (w:neighbors) (d:plural of innveng: people who live in the houses nearby) (e:a ~’ zite mawhpih uh a/Mi khempeuh in a ~ uh khem ciat uh | everyone deceives his neighbor/a ~’ sa a ne ding uh hi | they will eat the flesh of their neighbors/a ~’ kiangah a awzol uh hangin | though they speak kindly to their neighbors) (s:vengte/veengte) (b:innveng) (r:24.29.23/24.9.8/24.9.5/24.19.9) (q:draft)
innzom = (t:n) (w:next door/adjoining house) (d:inn house with zom, join; innzom a vengte are the nearest neighbours) (e:amau’ ~ a vengte tawh) (r:2.12.4) (q:draft)
insek = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:insect) (d:apparently the English word insect; insek ganhing, insect creatures, of small winged creatures) (e:Kha a nei ~ ganhing khempeuh/Kha a nei ~ ganhing a siangte khempeuh | all winged insects that are clean) (r:5.14.19/5.14.20) (q:draft, low confidence)
Iob = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Jashub) (d:third son of Issachar, written Iob in the Hebrew text of Genesis 46:13 and Jashub in the NIV) (r:1.46.13)
ip = (t:n) (w:bag/purse/sack) (d:a bag or sack for carrying goods or money; dangka-ip is a purse and thung-ip a travelling bag) (e:Na ~ sung uhah tawisuang nam nih/a paatsa ~ leh a paatsa leenggahzu um | worn-out sacks and old wineskins/sumte amaute in simin ~ tawh tun uh hi | they counted the money and put it into bags/a ~ sungah tuate koih hi | he put them in his bag) (r:5.25.13/12.12.10/6.9.4/9.17.40) (q:draft)
ip = (t:v) (w:hold back/restrain/keep in/conceal) (d:hold in, as words or anger, or keep a matter hidden; pau ip, to hold the tongue) (e:pau ~ theite mipil hi/Pasian in thu a ~ manin minthang a | it is the glory of God to conceal a matter/Kua in a kam ~ zo nawn ding | who can keep from speaking/Amah in, a sin sona ~ lo a | he did not hold back his anger/Ama hoih lohna a ~ nop hangin | though he wants to conceal his malice) (s:im/seel) (a:pulak/genkhia) (r:20.10.19/20.25.2/18.4.2/19.78.50/20.26.26) (q:draft)
ipbawl = (t:v) (w:hold back/conceal/keep to oneself) (d:ip, hold in or conceal, with bawl, do: keep something back; ipbawl loin is without holding back, openly) (e:na ~ loin a siangtakin na genkhia) (s:im) (a:pulak) (b:ip) (r:43.1.20) (q:draft)
ipcip = (t:v) (w:keep hidden/hold back/shut up) (d:ip hold in or conceal with cip, tightly; ki-ipcip, hold oneself back) (e:selcipin ~ ding ahi hi/Pasian in a ~ Pasian’ pilna thusim | the secret wisdom of God that God has kept hidden/a lungsim sung uhah a ~ uh thute | the things they keep hidden in their hearts/nangmah ki-~ niloh ding na hi hiam | will you go on holding yourself back) (s:imcip/seelcip) (a:pholak) (b:ip) (r:27.12.9/46.2.7/46.4.5/23.64.12) (q:draft)
ipcipte = (t:n) (w:secrets/hidden things) (d:the things kept hidden; ipcip with the plural te) (e:a ~ uh kipholak ding a) (s:thusimte) (b:ipcip) (r:46.14.25) (q:draft)
Iphtah = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Iphtah) (d:town in the western foothills of Judah)
ipin = (t:see) <ki-ipin>
ipip = (t:see) <ki-ipip>
ipipna = (t:see) <ki-ipipna>
iplah = (t:v) (w:desire/covet/lust after) (d:long for something or someone as too precious to do without) (e:Amau’ meel hoihna ~ kha kei in/numei dangte’ ngaihban’na ~ ding na hi hiam | why desire the bosom of another woman/tuate ka ~ a, ka la hi | I coveted them and took them) (s:lunggulh/deihgawh/duhgawh) (r:20.6.25/20.5.20/6.7.21) (q:draft)
iplah = (t:v) (w:spare/hold dear) (d:value something too much to lose it; iplah loin means without sparing, mercilessly) (e:~ loin a kidengkham beel) (s:siit) (r:23.30.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
iplahin = (t:v) (w:coveting/desiring) (d:iplah, covet, with the linking suffix in: coveting something and then acting on it, as in iplahin la, covet and take) (e:tuate ~ ka lakha hi/nate khat peuhpeuh ~ la kha-in | coveting and taking any of the things) (b:iplah) (r:6.7.21/6.6.18) (q:draft)
iplahkha = (t:v) (w:lust after/covet/desire) (d:iplah, covet, with kha, happen to: come to desire in the heart; used with kei in as a prohibition) (e:Amau’ melhoihna ~ kei inla) (s:duhgawhkha) (r:20.6.25) (q:draft, low confidence)
ipna = (t:see) <ipna-in>
ipna-in = (t:n) (w:holding in/restraining) (d:ip hold in, with the noun suffix na and in, by or from: from holding it in) (e:ka ki-ip ~ ka gim lua a) (r:24.20.9) (q:draft)
ippi = (t:n) (w:sackcloth/sack) (d:ip, bag, with pi, big: a large sack; ippi puan is sackcloth, the coarse cloth worn in mourning and repentance) (e:ahih manin ~ puan silh un la/~ puan silhin vut lakah a tu hi | he put on sackcloth and sat in the dust/a kawng uhah ~ puan a teeng uh hi | they wear sackcloth around their waists/a neupen dongin ~ puan a silh uh hi | down to the least they put on sackcloth) (s:puanham/puanhampi/khautang) (b:ip) (r:24.4.8/27.9.3/32.3.6/24.48.37/32.3.5) (q:draft)
ipsung = (t:n) (w:bag/inside of a bag) (d:ip, bag, with sung, inside: the inside of a bag, where weights or money are carried) (e:Na ~ uhah tawisuang nam nih) (r:5.25.13) (q:draft)
ipte = (t:n) (w:bags/sacks/purses) (d:ip bag with the plural te; khutkhai ipte, handbags or purses) (e:puanza neute, puanpite leh khutkhai ~/Amau' ~ antang tawh dipsakin | filling their bags with grain) (b:ip) (r:23.3.22/1.42.25) (q:draft)
iptheite = (t:n) (w:those who can hold back) (d:ip hold in, thei be able, with the plural te; pau iptheite are those who can hold their tongue) (e:pau ~ mipil hi) (r:20.10.19) (q:draft)
ipzo = (t:v) (w:restrain/hold back/keep in) (d:ip, hold in, with zo, be able: manage to hold back anger or words; ki-ipzo is hold oneself back) (e:mipilte in a hehna uh ~ hi/Kua in a kam ~ nawn ding ahi hiam | who can still hold back his mouth) (b:ip) (r:20.12.16/18.4.2) (q:draft)
