Ishvah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ishvah) (d:second son of Asher) (r:1.46.17/13.7.30)
Ishvi = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ishvi) (d:name of two men: a son of Asher, ancestor of the Ishvite clan, and a son of King Saul) (r:1.46.17/13.7.30)
Iskah = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Iscah/Iskah) (d:daughter of Haran, sister of Milkah and of Lot) (r:1.11.29)
Iskariot = (t:name) (w:Iscariot) (d:second name of Judas, the disciple who betrayed Jesus) (r:43.12.4/42.6.16)
Iskarot = (t:name) (w:Iscariot) (d:spelling of Iskariot in one verse, the second name of Judas who betrayed Jesus) (r:40.10.4)
Ismakhiah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ismakiah) (d:one of the overseers of the temple offerings under King Hezekiah) (r:14.31.13)
Israel = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Israel) (d:the name God gave to Jacob, son of Isaac, the ancestor of the twelve tribes) (r:1.32.28/1.35.10)
Israel = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Israel) (d:the nation and land of the descendants of Jacob; after Solomon also the northern kingdom as distinct from Judah) (r:9.11.7/10.21.5)
Israelmite = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Israelites) (d:Israel with mite, people: the people of Israel) (b:Israel) (r:11.6.1)
Israelte = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Israelites) (d:Israel with the plural te: the people of Israel) (b:Israel) (r:10.17.26/7.9.22)
Isreal = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Israel) (d:misspelling of Israel found in a few verses) (r:26.34.14/13.22.9)
Issaiah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ishiah) (d:one of the Korahite warriors who joined David at Ziklag) (r:13.12.6)
Issak = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Isaac) (d:spelling of Isaak found in a few verses: the son of Abraham and father of Jacob) (e:Jakob in ~’ ta hi) (r:42.3.34/11.18.36) (q:draft)
Issakhar = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Issachar) (d:son of Jacob and Leah, ancestor of the tribe of Issachar; also the tribe and its territory) (r:1.30.18/2.1.3)
Issakharte = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Issachar) (d:Issakhar with the plural te: the people of the tribe of Issachar) (b:Issakhar) (r:13.6.72)
Isshiah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ishiah) (d:name of several men, among them a chief of the tribe of Issachar and two Levites in the time of David) (r:13.7.3/13.24.21)
Isshijah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ishijah) (d:descendant of Harim who had married a foreign wife in the time of Ezra) (r:15.10.31)
Issiah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ishiah) (d:a Levite, second son of Uzziel of the family of Kohath) (r:13.23.20)
it = (t:v) (w:love/hold dear) (d:love a person, God or a thing; ka it, whom I love, also renders dear or beloved, and it zaw is love more) (e:Mikhat in Pasian a ~ leh/nang kong ~ hi | I love you/Kei nong ~ uh leh | if you love me/Rebekah in Jakob ~ hi | Rebekah loved Jacob/ka pasal in kei hong ~ taktak ding hi | my husband will truly love me) (a:mudah/hua) (r:46.8.3/59.1.16/19.18.1/43.14.15/1.25.28/1.29.32) (q:draft)
Itali = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Italy) (d:the land of Italy, spelled as it is said in Zolai) (r:58.13.24)
Italy = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Italy) (d:the land of Italy, where the city of Rome lies) (r:44.27.6/44.27.1)
itbawlin = (t:adv) (w:lovingly/in love) (d:it, love, with bawl, treat, and the linking suffix in: treating someone with love) (e:amaute nakpitakin ~ zahtak un) (r:52.5.13) (q:draft)
itdiak = (t:v) (w:love especially/love most) (d:it love with diak, particularly) (e:a ~ a nungzuite khat) (r:43.13.23) (q:draft)
Ithai = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ithai) (d:one of the mighty warriors of David, from Gibeah in Benjamin) (e:Gibeah khuami Ribai’ tapa ~) (r:13.11.31) (q:draft)
Ithamar = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ithamar) (d:youngest son of Aaron, a priest) (r:4.3.2)
Ithiel = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ithiel) (d:a man of the tribe of Benjamin, ancestor of Sallu who lived in Jerusalem after the exile) (r:16.11.7)
Ithlah = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Ithlah) (d:town in the territory allotted to the tribe of Dan) (r:6.19.42)
Ithmah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ithmah) (d:a Moabite, one of the mighty warriors of David) (e:Jeribai leh Joshaviah, leh Moab mi ~) (r:13.11.46) (q:draft)
Ithnan = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Ithnan) (d:town in the far south of Judah) (r:6.15.23)
Ithra = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ithra/Jether) (d:an Ishmaelite, father of Amasa; the NIV has Jether) (e:Ishmael mi ahi ~ min nei mi khat’ tapa) (r:10.17.25) (q:draft)
Ithran = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ithran) (d:name of two men: a son of Dishon the Horite in Edom, and a descendant of Asher) (r:1.36.26/13.7.37)
Ithream = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ithream) (d:sixth son of David, born in Hebron to his wife Eglah) (r:10.3.5/13.3.3)
Ithri = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Ithrite) (d:name of a clan; Ithri mi is an Ithrite and Ithri mite the Ithrites) (e:~ mi Ira, ~ mi Gareb) (r:10.23.38/13.2.53) (q:draft)
ithuai = (t:adj) (w:beloved/lovable/dear) (d:it, love, with huai, worthy of: worthy of love, dear) (e:a ~ khuapi a uum uh ciangin) (r:66.20.9) (q:draft)
itin = (t:v) (w:loving/love) (d:it, love, with the linking suffix in: loving someone and so doing what follows; itin nei is hold dear) (e:amah bek ~ nei in/mi peemte ~ an leh puan a pia hi | loving the foreigners he gives them food and clothing/Amah in na pate uh ~ | because he loved your ancestors/khat ~ a khat mudah a | loving one and hating the other/amah in tua numei ~ | he loved that young woman) (a:mudahin) (b:it) (r:20.5.15/62.5.2/5.10.18/5.4.37/5.21.15/1.34.3) (q:draft)
itkik = (t:v) (w:love again/reaffirm love) (d:it love with kik, again) (e:Amah na ~ ding uh) (b:it) (r:47.2.8) (q:draft)
itluat = (t:n) (w:darling/beloved/dearly loved one) (d:it, love, with luat, very much: one who is greatly loved; a word of address in love poetry, as itluat aw) (e:hong zui in, ~ aw/~ aw, hong paikik in | my beloved, come back/~ aw, na ngaihbaang a | my darling, how lovely you are) (s:ngaihno/lungtup) (r:22.2.10/22.4.10/22.2.17/22.4.1) (q:draft)
itluatna = (t:n) (w:great love/deep love) (d:it love with luat very much and the noun suffix na; said of the Lord's zeal for Jerusalem, where the NIV has jealousy) (e:Jerusalem mite ka ~ hangin/hih banga ka ~ in | this great love of mine) (r:38.8.2) (q:draft)
itna = (t:n) (w:love/kindness) (d:it, love, with the noun suffix na: the love of God and of people; itna kip is steadfast love or kindness) (e:~ lungsim tawh na khempeuh na hih un/ka ~ sungah om un | remain in my love/Ama ~ kip kho tawntung hi | his steadfast love endures forever/amah a ~ hangin | because of his love for her) (a:muhdahna) (b:it) (r:46.16.14/65.1.2/43.15.9/19.118.2/1.29.20) (q:draft)
itnakip = (t:n) (w:unfailing love/steadfast love) (d:itna love with kip, firm or lasting) (e:a ~ sungah lametna a neite) (r:19.33.18) (q:draft)
itnasa = (t:n) (w:former love/love once shown) (d:itna love with sa already: the love a person had or showed before) (e:amah a ~ sangin lianzaw hi/Na nasempa David na ~ hong phawk in | remember your love for your servant David) (b:itna) (r:10.13.15/14.6.42) (q:draft)
itnate = (t:n) (w:love/acts of love) (d:plural of itna; ki-itnate is love for one another) (e:lungduaina leh ~ don lo na hi hiam/Na ki-~ uh lungsim takpi tawh hi sak unla | let your love for one another be sincere) (b:itna) (r:45.2.4/45.12.9) (q:draft)
itpa = (t:n) (w:beloved/loved one/dear one) (d:it, love, with -pa for a man: the man whom someone loves) (e:na ~ cina-in a om hi/Ka muan’, ka lawm ~, keima an a nepa | my trusted and beloved friend, who ate my bread/Ama ~ Jakob’ angtan’pih ahi | the pride of Jacob, his beloved) (b:it) (r:43.11.3/19.47.4/19.41.9) (q:draft)
itpa = (t:n) (w:the one who loves/lover) (d:it, love, with -pa for a man: the man who loves someone, as in ei hong itpa, he who loved us) (e:Ei hong ~ hangin) (a:mudahpa) (b:it) (r:45.8.37) (q:draft)
itpen = (t:adj) (w:dearest/most beloved/favourite) (d:it, love, with pen, most: the most loved, dearest) (e:a nu’ ta ~ khat ahi hi/na lawm ~ dingin nei in | take her as your dearest friend) (b:it) (r:22.6.9/20.7.4) (q:draft)
Ittai = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ittai) (d:man from Gath who stayed loyal to David and commanded part of his army during the revolt of Absalom; also one of the mighty warriors of David, son of Ribai from Gibeah) (r:10.15.19/10.15.22) (q:draft)
itte = (t:n) (w:beloved/loved ones/dear friends) (d:those who are loved, as in ka itte, my beloved) (e:Ka ~ aw, hih nih veina lai/Ka ~ aw, milim biakna na taisan un | my dear friends, flee from idolatry/na ~ lang pangin thu kikum uh hi | they plot against those you love/na ~ hita leh, na mudahte hita leh | whether those you loved or those you hated) (a:muhdahte) (b:it) (r:61.3.1/24.11.15/46.10.14/19.83.3/26.16.37) (q:draft)
itte = (t:n) (w:those who love) (d:the ones who love someone, as in kei hong itte, those who love me) (e:Kei hong ~ ka hausak a/Kei hong ~ ka it a | I love those who love me/Topa in amah a ~ khempeuh kem a | the Lord watches over all who love him/nang hong ~ na mudah hi | you hate those who love you) (a:mudahte) (b:it) (r:20.8.21/20.2.8/20.8.17/19.145.20/10.19.6) (q:draft)
itteng = (t:n) (w:all the loved ones/all the dear ones) (d:it love with teng, all; a lawm itteng, all his close friends) (e:le a lawm ~ a inn-ah) (b:it) (r:44.10.24) (q:draft)
itthei = (t:v) (w:be able to love) (d:it love with thei, be able) (e:lungsim tak tawh ~ khinta) (b:it) (r:60.1.22) (q:draft)
Iturea = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Iturea) (d:region north-east of Galilee ruled by Philip the tetrarch) (r:42.3.1)
itzaw = (t:v) (w:love more/prefer) (d:it, love, with zaw, more: love one more than another; the one compared takes sang or sangin, than) (e:nang hong ~ na hi hiam/Zion kulh kongpi ~ hi | he loves the gates of Zion more/Rebekah in Jakob ~ hi | Rebekah loved Jacob more/Absalom’ tanu Ma-akah ~ hi | he loved Maakah daughter of Absalom more) (s:deihzaw) (b:it) (r:43.21.15/19.87.2/1.25.28/14.11.21) (q:draft)
itzawkna = (t:n) (w:greater love/loving more) (d:it love with zaw, more, and the noun suffix na: the fact of loving one more than others) (e:amah a ~ a sanggamte in) (r:1.37.4) (q:draft)
itzawte = (t:n) (w:those who love more) (d:itzaw love more with plural te, used with sangin than) (e:a tanu a ~ kei tawh kilawm lo hi/Kei sangin a nu a pa a ~ | those who love father or mother more than me) (b:itzaw) (r:40.10.37) (q:draft)
