Judah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Judah) (d:son of Jacob and Leah, ancestor of the tribe of Judah) (r:1.35.23)
Judah = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Judah) (d:the territory of the tribe of Judah, later the southern kingdom with Jerusalem as its capital) (r:9.22.5/11.14.21)
Judahmite = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Judah/people of Judah) (d:Judah with mite, people: the people of Judah, taken into exile) (b:Judah) (r:25.1.3)
Judahte = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Jews) (d:Judah with the plural te: the Jews, the people of Judah) (b:Judah) (r:44.14.5)
JUDAHTE = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Jews) (d:Judahte, the people of Judah, the Jews, written in capitals in the notice on the cross) (e:HIHPA IN ~’ KUMPIPA HI) (r:42.23.38/41.15.26) (q:draft)
Judas = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Judas) (d:name of several men, among them Judas Iscariot, the disciple who betrayed Jesus, and Judas son of James) (r:42.6.16/43.12.4)
Judea = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Judea) (d:the southern region of the land of Israel in New Testament times, around Jerusalem) (r:40.24.16/42.7.17)
Judith = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Judith) (d:Hittite wife of Esau, daughter of Beeri) (r:1.26.34)
Julia = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Julia) (d:a Christian woman in Rome greeted by Paul) (e:Filologas, ~, Nereas leh a sanggamnu) (r:45.16.15) (q:draft)
Julias = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Julius) (d:Roman centurion of the Imperial Regiment who took Paul as a prisoner to Rome) (r:44.27.1/44.27.3)
Junias = (t:name) (w:Junia) (d:a believer in Rome greeted by Paul together with Andronicus, once in prison with him) (r:45.16.7)
Jushabhesed = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Jushab-Hesed) (d:a descendant of David in the family of Zerubbabel) (r:13.3.20)
Justas = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Justus) (d:name of three men: Joseph called Barsabbas, Titius Justus of Corinth, and Jesus called Justus) (r:44.1.23/44.18.7)
Juttah = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Juttah) (d:town in the hill country of Judah, given to the priests) (r:6.15.55/6.21.16)
K = (t:todo) (q:draft, first letter of KEIMAH printed as K EIMAH in Exodus 3.14, keimah I myself used for the divine name I AM, not a word by itself)
ka = (t:det) (w:my) (d:first person singular possessive placed before a noun) (e:~ Pasian/leh ~ lawmte bei ta hi | and my friends are gone/a om lai takin ~ paknamtui hong kizeel hi | while he was there my perfume spread its fragrance/ci-in ~ Topa kiangah a ci hi | he said to my Lord) (r:18.19.14/22.1.12/42.20.43)
ka = (t:v) (w:spread out)
Ka = (t:pron) (w:I/my) (d:first person singular placed before a verb or noun, I before a verb and my before a noun; capitalised at the start of a sentence or line) (e:~ ziat lamah na tu in/~ thuak zo nawn kei a | I can bear it no longer/~ taklam ah tu in | sit at my right hand/na khe nuai-ah ~ koih matengin | until I put them under your feet) (b:ka) (r:58.1.13/18.21.2/18.32.20/44.2.35) (q:draft)
kaai = (t:v) (w:form/gather/hang over) (d:of cloud or mist, form and hang in the sky; meii kaai loh ni is a day without cloud) (e:amaute pen zingsang a ~ meiilum/meii ~ loh ni zingsang-a nitaang khia | the sun rising on a cloudless morning/meiingo hong ~ vatin amaute hong khuh a | a bright cloud suddenly formed and covered them) (r:28.13.3/10.23.4/40.17.5) (q:draft)
kaaisak = (t:v) (w:spread out/make form) (d:kaai, of cloud, form and hang, with sak, cause: make a cloud spread over) (e:a liah dingin meiipi ~ a) (b:kaai) (r:19.105.39) (q:draft)
kaaito = (t:prep) (w:up) (d:of mist, rising up from the ground: kaai, of cloud or mist forming, with to, upward) (e:leitung panin meiilum ~-in) (b:kaai) (r:1.2.6)
kaam = (t:n) (w:luck) (d:the luck that comes to a person; kaam pha is good luck) (r:1.30.11)
kaam = (t:n) (w:fortune) (d:what happens to a person by chance, good or bad) (r:1.30.11)
kaam = (t:n) (w:karma)
Kaam = (t:n) (w:fortune/luck) (d:kaam written with a capital at the start of speech; Kaam pha, good fortune) (b:kaam) (r:1.30.11) (q:draft)
kaam pha = (t:phrase) (w:good fortune/good luck) (d:said when something lucky happens, as Leah says at the birth of Gad) (r:1.30.11)
kaan = (t:adj) (w:white/gray) (d:form of kaang, white, used before another word; here of hair turned white in old age) (e:teek-a ka sam a ~’ hun) (r:19.71.18) (q:draft)
kaang = (t:adj) (w:white) (d:white in colour, of a horse, hair, wool or a patch of skin; a kaang a suah is turn white) (e:sakol ~ tungah tuangin/a vun sungah a bawk ~ omin | there is a white swelling in the skin/tuumul bangin hong ~ ding hi | they will become white like wool/keimah teekin ka sam ~ ta hi | I am old and my hair has turned white) (s:kang/ngo) (a:vom) (r:66.19.14/3.13.16/3.13.10/23.1.18/9.12.2) (q:draft)
kaangin = (t:adv) (w:white) (d:kaang, white, with the adverbial ending in; vuk bangin kaangin is as white as snow) (e:vuk bangin ~ a phakin paikhia hi) (b:kaang) (r:12.5.27) (q:draft)
kaangte = (t:n) (w:white parts/white ones) (d:kaang, white, with the plural te: the white parts of something) (e:a ciangkang ~ kidawksak hi) (b:kaang) (r:1.30.37) (q:draft)
kaangto = (t:v) (w:rise up/rouse oneself) (d:of a lion, get up; parallel to thoto in the same verse) (e:humpinelkai bangin ~ hi) (s:thoto) (r:4.23.24) (q:draft, low confidence)
kaat = (t:n) (c:stone) (w:sulfur/brimstone) (d:the burning mineral rained down in judgment, often named with meikuang fire) (e:~ leh meikuang zusak hi/leitang pen ~ suak ding hi | the land will turn into sulfur/migilote tungah mei-am le ~ zusak ding a | he will rain coals and sulfur on the wicked/van panin ~ leh meikuang hong kiasuk a | sulfur and fire fell from heaven) (s:kat) (r:1.19.24/23.34.9/19.11.6/42.17.29) (q:draft)
kabankel = (t:n) (c:stone) (w:carbuncle/beryl) (d:the third stone of the first row of the breastpiece, from English carbuncle; kabankel suang) (e:leh ~ suang gual khat) (s:karbankel/karbankal) (r:2.39.10) (q:draft)
Kabbon = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Cabbon/Kabbon) (d:town in the western foothills of Judah) (r:6.15.40)
kabom = (t:n) (w:junction/crossroads/centre) (d:the place where roads meet; lam kabom) (e:a kituahna lam ~ san-a teeng mite) (s:lamka) (r:26.38.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
kabomah = (t:adv) (w:at the crossroads) (d:kabom junction with ah, at; lam kabomah) (e:Lam ~ ding unla khuadak un) (b:kabom) (r:24.6.16) (q:draft)
Kabul = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Kabul) (d:town on the border of Asher; also the district in Galilee that Solomon gave to Hiram) (r:6.19.27)
Kabze = (t:see) <Kabze-el>
Kabze-el = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Kabzeel) (d:town in the far south of Judah near the border of Edom, home of Benaiah) (e:~ khuami Benaiah in gal a hang) (r:10.23.20/6.15.21) (q:draft)
Kabzeel = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Kabzeel) (d:town in the far south of Judah near the border of Edom, home of Benaiah) (r:6.15.21/10.23.20)
Kademah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Kedemah) (d:youngest son of Ishmael) (r:1.25.15)
kadesh = (t:see) <Meribath-kadesh>
Kadesh = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Kadesh) (d:place in the wilderness on the southern border of Canaan where Israel camped, also called Kadesh Barnea) (r:5.1.46/1.14.7)
Kadesh-barnea = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Kadesh Barnea) (d:place in the wilderness south of Canaan from which Moses sent men to look over the land) (r:4.32.8/6.10.41) (q:draft)
Kadeshbarnea = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Kadesh Barnea) (d:place in the wilderness south of Canaan from which Moses sent men to look over the land) (r:5.1.2/4.34.4)
Kadmiel = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Kadmiel) (d:Levite who returned from the exile with Zerubbabel and helped lead the worship) (r:16.12.8/16.10.9)
Kadmon = (t:name) (c:land/people) (w:Kadmonites) (d:one of the peoples whose land God promised to Abraham) (r:1.15.19)
Kaftor = (t:name) (c:male/land) (w:Caphtorim/Caphtor/Caphtorites) (d:the land the Philistines came from, and its people, descended from Egypt; Kaftor mite are the Caphtorites) (r:1.10.14)
kah = (t:v) (w:weep/mourn/lament) (d:form of kap, weep, used before other words: kah hun is a time to weep, kah la is a lament song) (e:amau zite in ~ zo lo uh hi/a ~ nading mun zong hi | he looked for a place to weep/Moses hangin a ~ khit uh ciangin | when they had finished weeping for Moses/tamlawhna ~ la khat sa in | sing a song of lament) (s:thuum) (a:nuih/nui) (r:19.78.64/21.3.4/1.43.30/5.34.8/26.27.2) (q:draft)
kah = (t:v) (w:climb/go up/ascend) (d:go up onto a hill, a wall, a ladder or a boat; gal kah is go out to battle) (e:mual tungah kuate ~ ding ahi hiam/galkapte bangin kulh tungah hong ~ uh hi | they scale the wall like soldiers/Tunglam bekah na ~ ding uh a | you will only go upward/Ammon mite kiangah Jefthah gal ~ hi | Jephthah went out to fight the Ammonites) (s:kahto/paito) (a:kumsuk/paisuk/kahsuk) (r:19.24.3/29.2.7/5.28.13/7.11.32) (q:draft)
Kah = (t:v) (w:weep/lament) (d:kah written with a capital at the start of a sentence, and in Kah La, the Laments, a book of lament songs) (e:~ La sungah tuate kikhum hi/~ hun om a, nuih hun om hi | there is a time to weep and a time to laugh) (a:nuih) (b:kah) (r:14.35.25/21.3.4) (q:draft)
kahbia = (t:adj) (w:mongrel/of mixed descent) (d:of people, of mixed or illegitimate birth; kahbia mite) (e:Ashdod khuapi-ah ~ mite teeng ding a) (r:38.9.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
kahdan = (t:n) (w:how to wail/way of weeping) (d:kah weep with dan, manner) (e:na tanute uh ~ hilh un la) (r:24.9.20) (q:draft)
kahin = (t:v) (w:climbing/going up/mounting) (d:kah, climb or go up, with the linking ending -in before the next verb; also of taking the throne) (e:a leeng tungah ~ Jezre-el ah pai hi/Ka khuadakna tausang tungah ~ | climbing up on my watchtower/a mun dang panin ~ a lut mite | those who climb in by another way/A pa’ kumpi tokhom ah Jehoram ~ a kip ciangin | when Jehoram had ascended his father’s throne and was established) (s:kahtoin) (b:kah) (r:12.9.16/35.2.1/43.10.1/14.21.4) (q:draft)
kahin = (t:v) (w:weeping/mourning) (d:kah, weep, with the linking ending -in) (e:Jesuh ~ a tamlawh numei pawlkhat) (s:kapin) (b:kah) (r:42.23.27) (q:draft)
kahkahna = (t:see) <kahkahna-in>
kahkahna-in = (t:n) (w:weeping/much weeping) (d:kah, form of kap weep, doubled for weeping that goes on, with the noun suffix na and the marker in; by or from continual weeping) (e:Ka ~ ka mit paatgawp ta a/~ ka lupna kawt dikdek hi | I drench my couch with weeping/Ka ~ ka mai khempeuh san gawp a | my face is all red from weeping) (r:25.2.11/19.6.6/18.16.16) (q:draft)
kahkawmin = (t:adv) (w:while weeping) (d:kah weep with kawm, while, and in) (e:a ~ hankhuk sung lamah) (r:43.20.11) (q:draft)
kahkawmun = (t:adv) (w:while weeping) (d:kah, weep, with kawm, while, and un marking a plural subject: while they were weeping) (e:a ~ Peter kiangah a lak uh hi) (r:44.9.39) (q:draft)
kahkhiato = (t:v) (w:climb out/climb up) (d:kah, climb, with khia, out, and to, upward: climb up out of a pit or hole) (e:Dum sung panin a hong ~ mite) (r:24.48.44) (q:draft)
kahla = (t:n) (w:lament/dirge/song of mourning) (d:kah, weep, with la, song: a song of mourning for the dead) (e:hih ~ tawh David kap a/hih ~ a kihilh nading thu pia hi | he ordered that this lament be taught) (s:tamlawhna) (r:10.1.17/10.1.18) (q:draft)
kahlei = (t:n) (w:stairs/steps/stairway) (d:a flight of steps, a stairway or ladder for going up; kahlei cial is a single step) (e:a dawl laita-ah ~ zui-in kipai-in/Levi mite’ ~ tungah | on the stairs of the Levites/leitungah ~ khat kiphutin | a stairway set up on the earth/~ cial sawm om hi | there were ten steps) (r:11.6.8/16.9.4/1.28.12/26.40.49) (q:draft)
kahna = (t:n) (w:weeping/crying/wailing) (d:kah, weep, with the noun suffix na: weeping or wailing; kahna aw is the sound of weeping) (e:thuumna leh ~ aw bek ka za/Topa in ka ~ aw a za zo hi | the Lord has heard the sound of my weeping/leenggui lo khempeuh ah ~ aw ging ding hi | there will be wailing in all the vineyards/tua khua sungah ~ aw | the sound of weeping in that city) (s:thuumna) (a:nuihna/lungdamna) (b:kah) (r:18.30.31/40.13.50/19.6.8/30.5.17/23.65.19) (q:draft)
kahnate = (t:n) (w:weeping/mourning) (d:plural of kahna) (e:~ lungdamna ka suaksak ding a) (b:kahna) (r:24.31.13) (q:draft)
kahpihto = (t:see) <kahpihto-in>
kahpihto-in = (t:v) (w:taking up/carrying up) (d:kah climb with pih, together with, to, upward, and in: climbing up with someone) (e:innkhum zangah ~ innkhum hong let uh a) (s:kahtohpihin) (r:42.5.19) (q:draft)
kahsiam = (t:adj) (w:skilled at wailing) (d:kah weep with siam, skilful) (e:a ~ tata vaikhak un) (r:24.9.17) (q:draft)
kahsuk = (t:v) (w:descend/climb down/go down) (d:kah climb with suk, downward; kahsuk kahto, going down and going up) (e:Mihing Tapa tungah ~ kahto a) (s:kumsuk/paisuk) (a:kahto) (b:kah) (r:43.1.51) (q:draft)
kahte = (t:n) (w:mourners/those who weep) (d:kah weep with the plural te; misi kahte, those who mourn the dead) (e:Misi ~ hehnem dingin) (s:kapte) (b:kah) (r:24.16.7) (q:draft)
kahto = (t:v) (w:go up/ascend/climb/rise) (d:kah, climb, with to, upward: go or climb up to a higher place, as a mountain, a ship or heaven; also of smoke rising) (e:Zeisu mual tungah ~ a/teembaw tungah ka ~ uh a | we went aboard the ship/Vantungah kua in a ~ ding hiam | who will ascend into heaven/meiite’ tung pekah ka ~ ding a | I will ascend above the clouds/meikhu in a tawntungin a ~ hi | the smoke goes up forever) (s:paito) (a:kahsuk/kumsuk/paisuk) (b:kah) (r:43.6.3/45.10.6/44.21.6/23.14.14/66.19.3) (q:draft)
kahtoh = (t:v) (w:go up/climb/ascend) (d:form of kahto used before endings such as ciangin and lai takin) (e:Gunkuang tungah a ~ ciangin/biakna innpi-ah a ~ lai takun | as they were going up to the temple/A sang munah amah a ~ ciangin | when he ascended on high/ka biakna tau tung ~ nading kahlei | steps for going up to my altar) (s:paitoh) (b:kahto) (r:40.14.32/49.4.9/44.3.1/49.4.8/2.20.26) (q:draft)
kahtohna = (t:n) (w:ascent/way up/pass) (d:place where a road climbs, a slope or mountain pass) (e:Heres ~ lam tawnin ciahkik hi/Luhith mual ~ lampi-ah | on the road going up the hill of Luhith/Amor mite’ gamgi in Akrabbim ~ | the border of the Amorites, from the ascent of Akrabbim) (s:paitohna) (b:kahtoh) (r:7.8.13/24.48.5/7.1.36) (q:draft)
kahtohpih = (t:v) (w:take up/bring up/lead up) (d:kahtoh go up, with pih, together with: go up with someone, take a person up to a high place) (e:a sangpen munah a ~ khit ciangin/a sangpenna munah a ~ khit ciangin | after he had taken him up to the highest point) (b:kahtoh) (r:40.4.5/42.4.9) (q:draft)
kahtohpihin = (t:v) (w:taking up/bringing up) (d:kahtohpih take up, with in) (e:khuakulh tungah ~ kulh pualamah) (s:kahpihto-in) (b:kahtohpih) (r:44.9.25) (q:draft)
kahtoin = (t:v) (w:going up/rising) (d:kahto go up, with in) (e:Mihingte’ kha van-ah ~) (b:kahto) (r:21.3.21) (q:draft)
kahtokik = (t:v) (w:go back up/ascend again) (d:kahto go up, with kik, again or back) (e:ama omna ngeiah a ~) (b:kahto) (r:43.6.62) (q:draft)
kahtosak = (t:v) (w:have come up/make go up/take up) (d:kahto go up, with sak, cause: cause or let someone climb up, as into a chariot) (e:ama kiangah Benhadad ~ hi) (b:kahto) (r:11.20.33) (q:draft)
kahzaw = (t:v) (w:weep more) (d:kah weep with zaw, more) (e:nang a dingin ka nak ~ hi) (s:kapzaw) (b:kah) (r:24.48.32) (q:draft)
kahzo = (t:v) (w:be able to weep/weep for) (d:kah weep with zo, be able) (e:misite ~ nawn lo ding uh hi) (b:kah) (r:18.27.15) (q:draft)
kai = (t:v) (w:pull/draw/drag) (d:draw something toward oneself or along behind; also lead away a person who has been seized, and of horses drawing a chariot) (e:mi khempeuh keima kiangah ka ~ ding hi/A leeng masa pen sakol san in ~ a | red horses pulled the first chariot/Ama lunggulhna in ~ a | his own desire drags him away/ka khamul hong ~ mite tungah | to those who pulled out my beard/amaute’ lungsim nangma lamah ~ in | draw their hearts toward you) (r:43.12.32/38.6.2/59.1.14/23.50.6/13.29.18) (q:draft)
kai = (t:v) (w:form/gather/come over) (d:of cloud, mist, dew, sweat or a rainbow: form, gather or settle; meiipi kai is clouds gather, daitui kai is dew falls, khua-ul kai is sweat breaks out) (e:biakinn sungah meiipi hong ~ a/biakinntual sungnung teng dimin meiipi ~ hi | a cloud filled the inner court/Hi mipa tungah daitui ~ hen | let the dew fall on this man/na puan sungah khua-ul ~-in na om hi | you sweat in your clothes/Mual tungah meiipi a ~ bangin | as thick cloud gathers on the mountains) (r:26.10.4/42.12.54/26.10.3/27.4.15/18.37.17/29.2.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
Kai = (t:see) <Kai-afas>
Kai-afas = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Caiaphas) (d:high priest in Jerusalem at the time of the trial of Jesus, son-in-law of Annas) (e:siampi ukpa ~ kiangah) (r:43.18.24/43.11.49) (q:draft)
Kaiafas = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Caiaphas) (d:high priest in Jerusalem at the time of the trial of Jesus, son-in-law of Annas) (r:40.26.57/40.26.3)
kaigawmin = (t:v) (w:pulling/pulling together) (d:kai pull with gawm, together, and in; of a new patch pulling on old cloth) (e:a lui ~ a vang a gol semsem) (r:40.9.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
kaigawpin = (t:v) (w:dragging/hauling off) (d:kai pull with gawp, roughly, and in) (e:zuma thukhente mai-ah hong ~) (r:42.12.58) (q:draft)
kaih = (t:n) (w:share/portion/due) (d:the part that a person regularly receives by right, as the priests' share of the offerings) (e:siampite’ ~ hi ding hi/nang leh na tapate’ ~ ding ahih manin | because it is your share and your sons’ share/na suan na khakte’ ~ ahi tawntung dingin | as the perpetual share of your descendants/a siangtho pen ama ~ ahih manin | because it is his most holy share) (s:tanh) (r:5.18.3/3.24.9/3.10.13/4.18.8) (q:draft)
kaih = (t:v) (w:pull/draw/lead) (d:form of kai pull, draw, used before another word, as in kaih khiat draw or lead out and a kaih leeng the chariot they pull; leh kaih is pull back) (e:Sakol vomte in a ~ leeng pen/Kei hong sawl Pa in a ~ loh mite | those whom the Father who sent me does not draw/ganhing ~ bangin khauzen tawh | with cords, as one leads an animal/sih nading mun a zuan mipa leh ~ in | hold back the one heading for death/ka khut tawh ka ~ lai a | when I led them by my hand) (b:kai) (r:38.6.6/6.8.6/43.6.44/23.5.18/20.24.11/58.8.9) (q:draft)
kaihkhiat = (t:v) (w:pull out/drag out/lead out) (d:form of kaikhia, pull or lead out, used before words such as hun, bang, khit and nading) (e:innpi sung pan a ~ khit uh ciangin/a khut uh tawh ka ~ huna | when I led them out by the hand/sikkawi tawh note hong ~ hun ding | the time when they drag you out with hooks/amaute mite mai-ah ~ nading a zong uh hi | they sought to bring them out before the people/ganhing sisa ~ bangin | like dragging out a dead animal) (b:kaih) (r:44.21.30/24.31.32/30.4.2/44.17.5/30.4.3) (q:draft)
kaihkhiatna = (t:n) (w:pulling out/means of pulling out) (d:kaihkhiat pull out, with the noun suffix na) (e:khau tawh kei hong ~ ding uh) (b:kaihkhiat) (r:24.38.11) (q:draft)
kaihkhiatsakin = (t:v) (w:pulling off/taking off) (d:kaihkhiat pull out, with sak, for or from someone, and in; of a sandal taken off a man's foot) (e:a khe panin a khedap ~) (b:kaihkhiat) (r:5.25.9) (q:draft)
kaihkhiattoh = (t:v) (w:pull up/bring up) (d:kaihkhiat pull out, with toh, upward) (e:Sikkeuka in a ~ khempeuh) (b:kaihkhiat) (r:9.2.14) (q:draft)
kaihkhop = (t:v) (w:gather/assemble/muster/bring together) (d:form of kaikhawm used before another word such as hun, pawi, ciangin or kik; an kaihkhop pawi is the Feast of Ingathering) (e:gan ~ hun hi lo hi/Bezek-ah amaute a ~ ciangin | when he mustered them at Bezek/Israel gam sunga om gamdang mite a ~ nadingun | to assemble the foreigners living in Israel/ka ~ kik hun hong tung ding hi | the time will come when I gather them again/note kong ~ khit ciangin | after I have gathered you) (a:thehthang) (r:1.29.7/9.11.8/13.22.2/33.4.6/26.20.41) (q:draft)
kaihkhopkik = (t:v) (w:gather again/bring back together) (d:kaihkhop gather, with kik, again) (e:note kong thehthangna panin kong ~ ciangin) (s:kaikhawmkik) (b:kaihkhop) (r:26.20.34) (q:draft)
kaihkhopna = (t:n) (w:ingathering/gathering/gleaning) (d:kaihkhop, gather, with the noun suffix na: the gathering in of a crop; kaihkhopna pawi is the Feast of Ingathering) (e:kum bei ciangin ~ pawi na bawl ding uh hi/Efraim leenggah sang ~ in | the gleanings of Ephraim’s grapes) (b:kaihkhop) (r:2.23.16/7.8.2) (q:draft)
kaihkhoppih = (t:v) (w:gather with/help gather) (d:kaihkhop gather, with pih, together with: gather along with someone) (e:kei hong ~ lo peuhmah/tuute hong ~ lo peuhmah | whoever does not gather the sheep with me) (a:thehthang) (b:kaihkhop) (r:40.12.30/42.11.23) (q:draft)
kaihkhopsa = (t:adj) (w:gathered/accumulated/collected) (d:kaihkhop gather, with sa, already done: that has been gathered) (e:amau’ ~ neihsa khempeuh) (b:kaihkhop) (r:1.12.5) (q:draft)
kaihkhopsakin = (t:v) (w:gathering in for/hauling in for) (d:kaihkhop gather, with sak, for someone, and in) (e:Lo-a na an piangte hong ~) (b:kaihkhop) (r:18.39.12) (q:draft)
kaihkhopte = (t:n) (w:collection/things gathered) (d:kaihkhop gather, with plural te: the things that have been gathered; na milim kaihkhopte is your collection of idols) (e:na milim ~ kihonsak in) (b:kaihkhop) (r:23.57.13) (q:draft)
kaihkik = (t:v) (w:draw back/bring back/reconcile) (d:kaih pull or draw, with kik, back) (e:ama kiangah a ~ ding) (b:kaih) (r:51.1.20) (q:draft)
