kaikhawmkik = (t:v) (w:gather again/gather back) (d:kaikhawm, gather, with kik, again: bring back together those who were scattered) (e:lak panin kote hong ~ in/Egypt mite ka ~ ding a | I will gather the Egyptians again/gamte panin ka ~ ding a | I will gather them again from the lands) (s:kaihkhopkik) (b:kaikhawm) (r:19.106.47/26.29.13/24.23.3) (q:draft)
kaikhawmpa = (t:n) (w:one who gathers/gatherer) (d:kaikhawm gather with pa, the man who does it) (e:tawm a ~’ aa dim lah lo hi/a tam a ~ aa dim val lo a | the one who gathered much did not have too much) (b:kaikhawm) (r:2.16.18/47.8.14) (q:draft)
kaikhawmsak = (t:v) (w:gather/have gathered) (d:kaikhawm gather, with sak, cause: have people gathered together, as by sending messengers) (e:a teelsa mite a ~ ding hi/a teel mite khempeuh a ~ ding hi | he will have all his chosen ones gathered) (b:kaikhawm) (r:40.24.31/41.13.27) (q:draft)
kaikhawmte = (t:n) (w:those who gather/gatherers/collectors) (d:kaikhawm, gather, with plural -te: the people who gather or collect something) (e:a ~ in keima biakinn huang sungah/sehsawm suah sehkhat a ~ in Levi mite | the Levites are the ones who collect the tithe) (b:kaikhawm) (r:23.62.9/16.10.37) (q:draft)
kaikhia = (t:v) (w:pull out/draw out/drag out/drag off) (d:kai, pull, with khia, out: pull, draw or drag someone or something out of a place) (e:tui thukpi panin kei hong ~ hi/pasal leh numeite ~ a | he dragged off men and women/ngabengte in tui geiah ~ uh a | the fishermen pulled it up on the shore/khua nawlah a ~ uh hi | they dragged him outside the city/vantung aksi sehthum suah sehkhat ~ a | it swept away a third of the stars of heaven) (b:kai) (r:10.22.17/44.8.3/40.13.48/44.14.19/66.12.4) (q:draft)
