kal = (t:v) (w:demand/require) (d:claim what is owed or due, as a debt, a vow, tribute or obedience; the form before another word is kalh) (e:hong ~ teekteek ding a/kei’ khut sung panin amah nong ~ ding hi | you shall require him from my hand/no tung panin bang dang hong ~ ahi hiam | what else does he require of you/ngun talen zathum leh kham talen sawmthum ~ hi | he demanded three hundred talents of silver and thirty of gold/bangmah ka ~ nawn kei ding uh hi | we will demand nothing more) (r:5.23.21/5.10.13/1.43.9/12.18.14/16.5.12) (q:draft)
