kamphen = (t:n) (w:interpreter) (d:one who puts the speech of one language into another) (e:Amaute’ kikalah ~ khat om ahih manin) (r:1.42.23/46.14.28) (q:draft)
kampi = (t:n) (w:lips/mouth/mere words) (d:in a kampi bek, with the mouth only: words spoken without the heart behind them) (e:a ~ bek tawh thuhoih gen a/a ~ bek uh tawh amah phatkhem uh a | they flattered him with their mouths only/i ~ bek tawh ki-it loin | let us not love with words only) (b:kam) (r:20.26.24/28.10.4/19.78.36/62.3.18) (q:draft)
kamsak = (t:v) (w:satisfy) (d:in na hukna teng na kamsak hi, you satisfied all your lust; perhaps for khamsak, make full) (e:na hukna teng na ~ hi) (r:23.57.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
kamsan = (t:v) (w:prophesy) (d:form of kamsang written with a final apostrophe before ding or the ending -na: speak a message from God; with -na it means prophecy or prophesying) (e:~’ ding na ut takpi ta un/~’na na nei thei uh hi | you can prophesy/Kha Siangtho tawh kidim a, ~’na tawh | filled with the Holy Spirit, with prophecy/mi khat kiangah ~’na thu | to another, prophecy) (s:genkhol) (r:46.14.39/42.1.67/46.14.31/46.12.10) (q:draft)
kamsang = (t:v) (w:prophesy) (d:speak a message from God; the same word is also the noun prophet, as in kamsang Haggai, the prophet Haggai) (e:thum ahi zongin ~ uh hen la/na tapate un ~ ding uh a | your sons will prophesy/upna zah bangin ~ na sem ni | let us prophesy according to our faith) (s:genkhol) (r:46.14.29/29.2.28/45.12.6)
Kamsang = (t:n) (w:prophet) (d:kamsang written with a capital as a title before a name, the prophet) (e:~ Iddo’ Tangthu sungah kigelh hi/~ Habakkuk in hih bangin thu ngen hi | the prophet Habakkuk prayed in this way/~ zuautheite hong piang ding uh a | false prophets will arise/~ mi in pawlpi a kipsak hi | the one who prophesies builds up the church) (s:kamsangpa) (b:kamsang) (r:14.13.22/14.32.32/35.3.1/40.24.11/46.14.4) (q:draft)
Kamsanga = (t:n) (w:seer/prophet) (d:Kamsang prophet with the ending a, as; Kamsanga kineipa is one who makes himself out to be a prophet) (e:~ kineipa aw) (b:Kamsang) (r:30.7.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
kamsangin = (t:n) (w:as a prophet) (d:kamsang, prophet, with the suffix -in, as; kamsangin om, act as a prophet, prophesy) (e:~ Samuel a kikipsakna thei uh hi/mite in ~ ngaihsun uh ahih manin | because the people considered him a prophet/~ a om uh hun lai takin | during the time they are prophesying/Mi khempeuhte in ~ a om lai takin | while everyone is prophesying) (b:kamsang) (r:9.3.20/66.11.6/40.14.5/46.14.24) (q:draft)
kamsangna = (t:v) (w:prophesy)
kamsangnu = (t:n) (w:prophetess/woman prophet) (d:kamsang, prophet, with -nu marking a woman) (e:~ Huldah kiangah pai uh hi/~ tawh ka lumkhawm a | I lay with the prophetess/hih ~ hong pai-in Pasian tungah lungdamna ko a | this prophetess came and gave thanks to God/keimah lausak dingin a hanciam ~ Noadiah | the prophetess Noadiah, who tried to frighten me) (b:kamsang) (r:12.22.14/16.6.14/23.8.3/42.2.38) (q:draft)
kamsangpa = (t:n) (w:prophet) (d:kamsang, prophet, with pa marking a man: a man who speaks messages from God) (e:amah in ~ khat hi a/~ Joel in a hilh ngeisa thu ahi hi | this is what the prophet Joel spoke of/~ Hananiah a si ta hi | the prophet Hananiah died/~ Samuel dongin thukhen mangte a pia hi | he gave them judges until the prophet Samuel) (b:kamsang) (r:1.20.7/24.37.6/44.2.16/24.28.17/44.13.20)
Kamsangpa = (t:n) (w:prophet) (d:kamsangpa written with a capital, the Prophet; pa marks a man) (e:Hih pa pen ~ taktak hi/~ Isaiah’ Lai Siangtho a kipiak ciangin | when the scroll of the prophet Isaiah was handed to him/~ in ama omna gamah minthan’na ngah lo hi | a prophet has no honour in his own country) (b:kamsangpa) (r:43.7.40/42.4.17/43.4.44) (q:draft)
kamsangte = (t:n) (w:prophets) (d:kamsang, prophet, with the plural te) (e:Topa in ~ ahi a nasemte’ tung tawnin/ka ~ tungah siatna hih kei un | do my prophets no harm/Moses leh Pasian’ ~ a nei uh hi | they have Moses and the prophets of God/tua thu in ~ thu tawh kibang hi | this agrees with the words of the prophets) (b:kamsang) (r:12.21.10/46.14.32/13.16.22/42.16.29/44.15.15) (q:draft)
Kamsangte = (t:n) (w:prophets) (d:kamsangte written with a capital) (e:~ in amaute kiangah/~ hong genkholh thu khempeuh | all that the prophets have foretold/~ leh siampite in mawhna a bawl manun | because the prophets and priests sinned) (b:kamsangte) (r:24.14.13/42.24.25/25.4.13) (q:draft)
kamsanngte = (t:n) (w:prophet/prophets/seers) (d:spelling of kamsangte, prophets, found in Micah 3:7, where the English versions have seers) (e:~ in maizumna thuak ding uh a) (r:33.3.7)
Kamsanngte = (t:n) (w:prophets/seers) (d:apparently a misprint of Kamsangte) (e:~ in maizumna thuak ding uh a) (b:kamsanngte) (r:33.3.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
kamsia = (t:n) (w:evil speech/harsh words/bad language) (d:kam, mouth, with sia, bad: evil or hurtful speech) (e:~ in lung gimsak hi/~ pau kei uh hen la | let them not speak evil/kiphatsakna ~ a pau ka za hi | I heard it speaking boastful, evil words) (s:kamguh/pausia) (a:kamhoih/kamkhum) (r:20.15.4/60.3.10/27.7.11) (q:draft)
kamsia = (t:adj) (w:unfortunate/unlucky/wretched) (d:having bad fortune, in a wretched state; used in a cry of misery, woe is me) (e:Kei a ~ hi’ng) (s:tuahsia) (a:hampha) (r:33.7.1) (q:draft, low confidence)
kamsiam = (t:n) (w:smooth talk/fine words/compliment) (d:kam mouth with siam skilled; pleasant or skilful speech, and as a verb speak kindly to or greet) (e:~ leh kamzol tawh a pha mite/na ~ ngah teng maimang ta ding hi | all your fine words will be wasted/Na sanggamte tung bekah na ~ uh leh | if you greet only your own brothers) (s:kamkhum/kamzol) (r:45.16.18/40.5.47/20.23.8) (q:draft)
kamsiamna = (t:n) (w:eloquence/gracious speech) (d:kamsiam, skilled in speech, with the noun suffix na: eloquent or gracious speech) (e:~ leh pilna tawh Pasian’ teci thu/~ in kumpipa’ lawm hong suaksak hi | gracious speech makes one the friend of the king/Mihoihte in a ~ bangun thaman sang a | the good are rewarded for their gracious speech) (b:kamsiam) (r:46.2.1/20.22.11/20.13.2) (q:draft)
kamsiat = (t:n) (w:disaster/misfortune/calamity) (d:form of kamsia, unfortunate, used before a noun; kamsiat ni, the day of disaster) (e:Ka ~ ni-in amaute in kei hong simgawp a/Amaute in ka ~ ni-in kei hong neh uh hangin | though they attacked me on the day of my disaster) (s:tuahsiatna/kamsiatna) (b:kamsia) (r:10.22.19/19.18.18) (q:draft)
kamsiate = (t:n) (w:coarse talk/bad words/foul language) (d:kamsia, evil or foul speech, with the plural te: coarse or indecent talk) (e:amawkna ~ zong paaikhia un la) (b:kamsia) (r:49.5.4) (q:draft)
kamsiatna = (t:n) (w:misfortune/hardship/adversity) (d:trouble or ill fortune that befalls someone; kamsiatna tuak is meet with misfortune, and kamsiatna thuak tahen is a curse on someone) (e:khang tawntungin ~ tuak kei ning/Kote’ tuah khak ~ khempeuh na thei hi | you know all the hardships that have come on us/Mi khempeuh tungah ~ vive tung hi | misfortune comes to everyone/Kei’ ~-ah a lungdamte maizumsak in | put to shame those who rejoice at my misfortune) (s:tuahsiatna/haksatna/gentheihna) (a:daupaina) (b:kamsiat) (r:19.10.6/4.20.14/21.9.11/19.35.26) (q:draft)
kamsiatnate = (t:n) (w:afflictions/misfortunes/hardships) (d:kamsiatna, misfortune, with the plural te: the troubles a person goes through) (e:ka ~ nong don khin a) (s:tuahsiatnate/haksatnate) (a:daupainate) (b:kamsiatna) (r:19.31.7) (q:draft)
kamsung = (t:n) (w:mouth/inside of the mouth) (d:kam, mouth, with sung, inside: the inside of the mouth; kamsung panin is out of the mouth) (e:humpinelkai ~ panin a hong honkhia thei hiam/a ~ panin a kangtum mei pusuak a | consuming fire came out of his mouth/na ~ uh le na lungsim sung uhah om | it is in your mouth and in your heart/Tua thute a ~ pan a pusuah ma-in | before the words had left his mouth) (s:kam) (r:27.6.20/66.19.21/10.22.9/5.30.14/27.4.31) (q:draft)
kamtai = (t:n) (w:messenger/envoy) (d:one sent to carry a message, a messenger or envoy; kamtai sawl is send a messenger) (e:Minamte lakah ~ khat kisawl zo a/~ khat Job kiangah hong tungin | a messenger came to Job/Huihte nangma ~ dingin na bawl a | you make the winds your messengers/Babilon gamah ~ paisak pah hi | she at once sent messengers to Babylon) (s:taangmi/palai/laitai) (r:31.1.1/20.13.17/18.1.14/19.104.4/26.23.16) (q:draft)
kamtaipa = (t:n) (w:messenger) (d:kamtai, messenger, with pa, the man: the man sent with a message) (e:a ~ in laikhak khat hong pia hi/amah in ~ thuhilhin | he instructed the messenger/Tua ahih ciangin ~ pai a | so the messenger set out/keima sawl ka ~ bangin kua a bil ngong | who is deaf like the messenger I send) (s:taangmi) (b:kamtai) (r:16.6.5/10.11.22/10.11.19/23.42.19) (q:draft)
kamtaite = (t:n) (w:messengers/envoys) (d:kamtai, messenger, with the plural te; kamtaite sawl is send messengers) (e:Sihon kiangah ~ sawl a/Ammon mite kumpipa kiangah ~ sawl kik a | he sent messengers back to the king of the Ammonites/Filistia mite’ hong sawl ~ | the envoys sent by the Philistines/a sanggampa Esau' kiangah ~ ma sawl a | he sent messengers ahead to his brother Esau) (s:tangmite/taangmite/laitaite) (b:kamtai) (r:4.21.21/7.11.14/23.14.32/1.32.3) (q:draft)
kamtam = (t:adj) (w:talkative/loud/noisy) (d:kam, mouth or word, with tam, many: given to much or noisy talk; kamtam sak is make someone loud) (e:Leenggahzu in mi ~ sakin/a ~, zumna meel thei lo numei tawh kibang | is like a loud woman who knows no shame/~ nuam se loin hoihtakin om hithiatna | living quietly without being eager to talk much) (a:dai) (r:20.20.1/20.9.13/52.4.11) (q:draft)
kamte = (t:n) (w:words/talk) (d:kam, word, with the plural te: things said, as in muhdahna kamte, words of hatred, and a mawkna kamte, empty talk) (e:muhdahna ~ pau-in kei hong gensia uh a/a mawkna ~ na tang in | avoid empty talk/Pasian’ hehpihna phatna ~ zang un | use words of thanksgiving to God/mihingte’ hong hilh pilna ~ a zang hi loin | not using words of wisdom taught by men) (s:kammalte/thute) (b:kam) (r:19.109.3/55.2.16/49.5.4/46.2.13) (q:draft)
kamte = (t:n) (w:languages/tongues) (d:kam, speech, with the plural te: the languages spoken by different peoples, and the tongues spoken in the church) (e:mipawl, mihon, gam, ~ ahi uh hi/mipawlte, gamte, ~, kumpi tampite thu tawh kizomin | concerning many peoples, nations, languages and kings/tua ~ a khiatna gen theite | those who can interpret those tongues) (s:paute) (b:kam) (r:66.17.15/66.10.11/46.12.30) (q:draft)
kamthakin = (t:adv) (w:in new tongues/in a new language) (d:kam, speech, with thak, new, and the adverb suffix in: speaking in a language new to the speaker) (e:~ a pau ding uh hi) (r:41.16.17) (q:draft)
kamtuam = (t:n) (w:tongues/other language/strange tongue) (d:kam, speech, with tuam, different: a language not one's own, the speaking in tongues of the New Testament; kamtuam tawh pau is speak in tongues) (e:~ tawh a gen mi in/tua mite in ~ tawh pau-in | those people were speaking in tongues/amaute in ~ pau thei-in | they were able to speak in tongues/~ tawh pau ding na khaam kei un | do not forbid speaking in tongues) (s:pautuam/paudang) (r:46.14.4/44.10.46/44.19.6/46.14.39) (q:draft)
kamun = (t:n) (w:mouth) (d:kam, mouth, apparently with the plural marker un: their mouths, what they say) (e:Amaute a ~ hoih khem napi-in) (b:kam) (r:26.33.31) (q:draft, low confidence)
kamzol = (t:n) (w:flattery/flattering words/smooth talk) (d:kam, word, with zol, persuade: pleasant words used to win someone over or deceive) (e:kamsiam leh ~ tawh/phat khemna ~ leh lungsim nam nih tawh pau | they speak with flattering words and a double heart) (s:kamsiam/kamneel/thuzol/mawkphatna) (r:45.16.18/19.12.2) (q:draft)
kan = (t:v) (w:search/look for) (d:look for someone or something that is lost or wanted, or look closely into a matter) (e:ding ~ dingin ngaihsun lo uh hi/Mi khempeuh in nang hong ~ uh hi | everyone is looking for you/Simon’ inn hong ~ kawikawi uh a | they searched around for the house of Simon/limtak ~ dih un | search it out carefully) (s:zon) (r:26.34.6/41.1.37/44.10.17/24.2.10)
kan = (t:v) (w:explore) (d:look into something thoroughly in order to understand it) (e:a thu ~ ding ka ngaihsun hi | I set my mind to explore the matter/gam sung omzia lim a ~ dingin | to look into the sign that had appeared in the land) (s:kansim) (r:21.1.13/14.32.31)
kan = (t:v) (w:ask) (d:ask or inquire about a matter, often as thu kan; Topa kiangah thu kan is inquire of the Lord) (e:thu ~ dingin amah pai hi/Pasian’ deihna ~ dingin | to inquire about the will of God/hun beisa thu tu-in ~ un la | ask now about the days that are past/Kei thu hong ~ lo mite tungah | to those who did not ask for me/Tangvalpa kua tapa ahi hiam ~ in | find out whose son the young man is) (s:dong/dot/thukan) (a:dawng) (r:1.25.22/5.4.32/2.18.15/45.10.20/9.17.56)
