kang = (t:v) (w:burn/scorch/consume) (d:be burned or scorched by fire; of fire, burn something up) (e:na khe ~ loin om ding ahi hiam/mei hong paikhia-in amaute ~ a | fire came out and burned them up/na puan ~ loin om ding ahi hiam | will your clothes not be burned/meikuang bangin gamsung ~ a | the land is scorched as by a flame) (s:kat/kuang) (r:20.6.28/3.10.2/20.6.27/23.9.19) (q:draft)
kang = (t:v) (w:dry up/stop flowing) (d:of water, tears or a flow of blood, dry up or stop flowing) (e:Ka khitui ~ thei loin/San Tuipi thuhilh a, tua tuipi ~ hi | he rebuked the Red Sea and it dried up/Nimrim lui tuite ~ hi | the waters of Nimrim are dried up/khitui luangluang hen la, ~ ngei kei ta hen | let my tears keep flowing and never stop) (s:keu) (r:25.3.49/19.106.9/23.15.6/24.14.17) (q:draft)
kangcip = (t:v) (w:dry up/run dry) (d:kang, dry up, with cip, completely: of streams, rivers and the sea, run completely dry) (e:Lui tui khempeuh ~ khin a/tuipi ~ pah a | the sea dries up at once/Nail gun tuithukte ~ ding hi | the depths of the Nile will dry up/a tuite hong ~ hi | its waters dried up) (s:keucip/keutum) (b:kang) (r:29.1.20/34.1.4/38.10.11/66.16.12) (q:draft)
kangcipin = (t:v) (w:drying up/running dry) (d:kangcip, dry up completely, with the linking suffix in: drying right up) (e:guntui ~ keu ding hi) (b:kangcip) (r:23.19.5) (q:draft)
kangcipsak = (t:v) (w:dry up/make run dry) (d:kangcip, dry up completely, with sak, cause: make a river or the sea dry right up) (e:gunpite zong ~ hi) (s:keutumsak/kangsak/keusak) (b:kangcip) (r:34.1.4) (q:draft)
kanggawp = (t:v) (w:scorch/sear/burn badly) (d:kang, burn, with gawp, severely: of the sun or great heat, scorch people badly) (e:a satna tawh mite a ~ hi/Nisa in mite ~ ahih manin | because the heat of the sun scorched the people) (b:kang) (r:66.16.8/66.16.9) (q:draft)
kanghul = (t:v) (w:singe/be singed) (d:of hair, be singed or slightly burned by fire) (e:mei in ~ lo a) (r:27.3.27) (q:draft)
kangin = (t:v) (w:burning/blazing) (d:kang, burn, with the linking suffix in, joining it to the next verb: burning, on fire) (e:~ a vom khit ciangin/mei in ~ a kuang zuazua khat | something all ablaze with fire/mei in mual ~ na kuang hi | the mountain was ablaze with fire) (b:kang) (r:26.15.5/66.8.8/5.9.15) (q:draft)
kangin = (t:adj) (w:white/turned white) (d:kang, white, with the linking suffix in: being or turning white, said of hair or of skin) (e:vuk bangin ~ a phakin a paikhia hi/A samte tuumul bangin ~, khuavak bangin pak a | his hair was white like wool, bright as light/Tua mun a om a multe ~ | the hair in that spot having turned white) (b:kang) (r:12.5.27/3.13.3/66.1.14/3.13.25) (q:draft)
kangin = (t:v) (w:rising/going up) (d:kang, rise, with in joining it to the next verb) (e:van lamah ~ a kahtoh ciangin) (r:26.1.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
kangkha = (t:v) (w:scorch/burn) (d:kang burn, with kha, happen to touch: of heat, strike and scorch someone) (e:a sa in zong ~ nawn lo) (r:66.7.16) (q:draft)
kanglum = (t:v) (w:burn to death/consume) (d:kang burn, with lum, to death: of fire, kill by burning) (e:Mei in a tangvalte ~ a) (r:19.78.63) (q:draft)
kangpah = (t:v) (w:dry up at once/stop at once) (d:kang dry up or stop flowing, with pah, immediately: said of a flow of blood) (e:thakhatin a siluang a ~ hi) (s:khawlpah) (r:42.8.44) (q:draft)
kangsa = (t:adj) (w:white) (d:kang, white, with sa, already: that which is already white, said of hair) (e:a ~ vomsak thei loin) (a:vom) (b:kang) (r:40.5.36) (q:draft)
