kangsak = (t:v) (w:burn/set on fire) (d:kang, burn, with sak, cause: set something on fire so that it burns) (e:Tai-ar khuapi kulh ka ~ ding a/Judah gamsung ka ~ ding a | I will set the land of Judah on fire/mei a ~ pa in | the one who started the fire) (s:halsak/kuangsak) (b:kang) (r:30.1.10/30.2.5/2.22.6) (q:draft)
kangsakin = (t:v) (w:turning white/making white) (d:kang white, with sak cause and the connective in: making something white, as a skin disease does the hair) (e:tua in a multe ~ a bawk sungah) (b:kang) (r:3.13.10) (q:draft)
kangsakpa = (t:n) (w:one who started the fire) (d:kangsak cause to burn, with pa, the man who: the man who set something on fire) (e:mei a ~ in a cing takin) (b:kangsak) (r:2.22.6) (q:draft)
