kangtumsak = (t:v) (w:burn up/consume) (d:kangtum, burn up, with sak, cause: make something burn up completely, set it on fire and destroy it) (e:a inn lianpite uh ka ~ ding hi/meikuang sungah lawnin ~ in | throw them into the fire and burn them up/Teman gam sung khempeuh ka ~ ding a | I will burn up all the land of Teman/A saguhte ~ un | burn up the bones) (s:haltum/kattumsak) (b:kangtum) (r:28.8.14/26.24.10/26.5.4/30.1.12) (q:draft)
kangtumsakin = (t:v) (w:burning up/burning away) (d:kangtumsak, burn up, with the linking suffix in: said of a refiner burning away the dross) (e:A ninte ~, ngunte a siangsakpa bangin) (s:haltumin) (b:kangtumsak) (r:39.3.3) (q:draft)
kangtumthei = (t:v) (w:able to burn up/scorching) (d:kangtum burn up completely, with thei, can: able to consume, said of a fire) (e:na a ~ meikuang tawh kibang hi) (b:kangtum) (r:20.16.27) (q:draft)
