kat = (t:n) (c:stone) (w:sulfur/brimstone) (d:sulfur, the yellow mineral that burns, named together with mei, fire, in scenes of judgment; also written kaat) (e:mei-am leh ~ zusak ding a/mei, meikhu leh ~ ahi gimna pawl thum | the three plagues of fire, smoke and sulfur/mei leh ~ guah bangin hong zu a | fire and sulfur came down like rain) (s:kaat) (r:19.11.6/66.9.18/42.17.29) (q:draft)
kat = (t:v) (w:burn/consume/burn up) (d:said of fire, burn something or burn it up; also be on fire, and in 1 Corinthians 7:9 burn with desire) (e:mei in a ~ bangin/Mei in mual a ~ lai takin | while the mountain was burning with fire/mei in a ~ loh mite a en uh hi | they looked at the men the fire had not burned/A ~ sangin kiteeng leh a phazaw hi | it is better to marry than to burn) (s:kang/kattum) (r:26.22.31/38.11.1/5.5.23/27.3.27/46.7.9) (q:draft)
kat = (t:v) (w:be split/be divided) (d:form of ka, be split, used before hangin: said of a hoof that is cloven, as in khecin a kat hangin, though its hoof is divided) (e:a khecin a ~ hangin/a khecin a ~ hangin eknel hai lo ahih manin | because, though its hoof is divided, it does not chew the cud) (r:3.11.7/5.14.8) (q:draft)
kate = (t:n) (d:ka, be split or forked, with plural te: khecin kate are the animals whose hoof is divided) (e:khecin ~ lak pan hita leh) (b:ka) (r:3.11.4) (q:draft)
katlup = (t:v) (w:burn to death) (d:kat burn, with lup, a form of lum, to death: of fire, kill by burning) (e:Topa’ mei in a ~ mite’ hangin) (s:hallum/kanglum) (r:3.10.6) (q:draft)
katna = (t:n) (w:burning/fire/flames) (d:kat, burn, with the noun suffix na: mei katna is the burning of a fire, the flames, and katna khu the smoke of a burning) (e:mei ~ pan a pusuak meikhu/a khuapi ~ khu a muh uh ciangin | when they see the smoke of the burning city/ama pumpi mei ~ tawh a kipelh mah bangin | like one who himself escapes through the flames/Tua khuapi a ~ khu tatsat loin | the smoke of that burning city without end) (s:meikatna/kattumna) (b:kat) (r:66.18.9/46.3.15/66.18.18/66.19.3) (q:draft)
katna = (t:n) (w:fork/branching/parting) (d:kat, be split, with -na: the place where a road divides in two) (e:Tua lampi a ~ munah ciamtehna khat phut) (b:kat) (r:26.21.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
katsak = (t:v) (w:scorch/cause to burn) (d:kat burn, with sak, cause: make fire burn someone) (e:ni in mite mei a ~ nading) (b:kat) (r:66.16.8) (q:draft)
Kattath = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Kattath) (r:6.19.15)
kattheih = (t:v) (w:can burn/can devour) (d:kat, burn, with theih, the form of thei, can, used before nading: so that fire may be able to burn something) (e:kungte a ~ nadingin na kongpite) (b:kat) (r:38.11.1) (q:draft)
