kattumna = (t:n) (w:burning/burning up) (d:kattum burn up, with the noun suffix na: the fact of having been burned up by fire) (e:kulhkongpite mei in a ~ thu) (s:katna/meikatna) (b:kattum) (r:16.1.3) (q:draft)
kattumsa = (t:adj) (w:burned/burned up) (d:kattum burn up, with sa, already done) (e:mei in a ~ a kongpite ka en hi) (s:kangtumsa) (b:kattum) (r:16.2.13) (q:draft)
kattumsak = (t:v) (w:burn up/scorch) (d:kattum, burn up, with sak: of fire, burn up something that belongs to someone, as the branches of a tree) (e:a hiangte mei in a ~) (s:kangtumsak) (b:kattum) (r:18.15.30) (q:draft)
