kawcik = (t:adj) (w:narrow) (d:narrow, with little room, of a path, a gate or a place; also said of a heart that holds back its affection) (e:mun ~ khatah na ding leuleu hi/a pang tuakah phung a omna lam ~ ah | in a narrow path with a wall on each side/Kote’ adingin mun ~ lua hi | this place is too narrow for us/ki-itna hehpihna-ah na ~ uh hi | it is in your own affection that you are narrow) (s:kawciik) (a:tanzau/zai) (r:4.22.26/47.6.12/4.22.24/23.49.20) (q:draft)
kawcikah = (t:adj) (w:narrow) (d:kawcik narrow, with ah, at or in: in a narrow place) (e:a omna lam ~ vantungmi) (b:kawcik) (r:4.22.24) (q:draft)
kawcikin = (t:adj) (w:narrow) (d:kawcik narrow, with the linking suffix in: being narrow) (e:tun nading kong ~ a lampi haksa) (b:kawcik) (r:40.7.14) (q:draft)
kawi = (t:v) (w:embrace/hug) (d:put the arms around someone; ngawng kawi is throw the arms around the neck of someone) (e:Paul’ ngawng ~-in a nam uh hi/amah ngawng ~ a, pom cipin nam a | he threw his arms around his neck, held him close and kissed him/a taklam khut-in kei hong ~ hi | his right arm embraces me/amah in amaute nam-in ~ hi | he kissed them and embraced them) (s:pom) (r:44.20.37/20.7.13/1.33.4/22.2.6/1.48.10) (q:draft)
