kawi = (t:v) (w:turn/curve/go around) (d:go in a bend or roundabout way rather than straight, of a boundary that turns or of someone walking about, as in kawi pai) (e:Rimmon-ah pai lai-in Neah lamah ~ hi/gamgi in Azmon panin Izipt Lui lamah ~-in | the boundary turns from Azmon toward the Wadi of Egypt/gamsung tengah ~ pai-in a mangthang uh hi | they wander off into the wasteland and perish/leilu lam manawhin ~-in, Enshemesh-ah paisuak a | it curved northward and went on to En Shemesh) (s:kihei) (r:6.19.13/43.10.23/4.34.5/18.6.18/6.18.17) (q:draft)
kawihei = (t:v) (w:distort/twist) (d:kawi, crooked, with hei, turn: twist the meaning of words to suit oneself) (e:thu a ututun a ~ uh bangin) (s:lumlet) (r:61.3.16) (q:draft)
kawikawi = (t:adv) (w:about/around/to and fro) (d:here and there, back and forth, placed after a verb of movement) (e:gam khatah a vak ~ lai takun/a kimkot ah a tu mite en ~ a | he looked around at those sitting about him/sunthapai-in kapin ka vak ~ hi | all day long I go about weeping/mi lakah a vak ~ hi | he went about among the people) (r:19.105.13/1.8.7/41.3.34/19.38.6/24.37.4) (q:draft)
kawikawina = (t:n) (d:kawikawi about, here and there, with na; follows a verb and makes a noun of doing that action all around or to one another, as gen kawikawina telling around and zon kawikawina searching about) (e:Gam sung teng a zon’ ~ uhah/a mangmat uh a gen ~ uh tawh | by the dreams they tell one another/khualmite tawh na khialh ~ | your going astray here and there with strangers/Gamlakah a vak ~ mi khat in mu a | a man found him wandering about in the fields) (b:kawikawi) (r:26.39.15/24.3.13/24.23.27/1.37.15) (q:draft)
