kawikawipa = (t:n) (d:kawikawi about, with pa, the man who: in pai kawikawipa, he who walks about) (e:laizangah a pai ~’ thupiakna in) (b:kawikawi) (r:66.2.1) (q:draft)
kawikawisak = (t:v) (w:make wander) (d:kawikawi about, with sak, cause: in vak kawikawisak, make someone wander about) (e:gamlakah amaute vak ~ hi) (s:vakvaisak) (b:kawikawi) (r:4.32.13) (q:draft)
kawikawite = (t:n) (w:those who go about) (d:kawikawi about with te marking the people who do so; pai kawikawite, those who go around, gensia kawikawite, those who go about slandering) (e:Mi a gensia ~ muanhuai thei lo hi/Khuasung cing a, pai ~ ka tuak a | I met the watchmen who go about the city) (b:kawikawi) (r:20.20.19/22.3.3) (q:draft)
kawina = (t:n) (w:crookedness/perversity) (d:from kawi crooked; lungsim kawina, a perverse heart) (e:Lungsim ~ ka deih het kei a) (b:kawi) (r:19.101.4) (q:draft)
kawina = (t:n) (w:embrace/embracing/hug) (d:from kawi embrace; ngawng kawina, putting the arms round the neck) (e:ama hong ~ khut in sikkhau bangin/i galte’ hong ngawng ~ in | the embraces of our enemies) (b:kawi) (r:21.7.26/20.27.6) (q:draft)
