kensang = (t:n) (w:steep bank/high cliff/precipice) (d:ken or keen, cliff, with sang high: a high steep bank or cliff) (e:~ tung pan taisuk uh a/vok honpite ~ tung pan taisukin | the herd of pigs rushed down the steep bank) (s:keen) (r:42.8.33/41.5.13) (q:draft)
