kep = (t:v) (w:keep/take care of/look after) (d:form of kem used before words such as ding, theih and hun) (e:a bangci ~ theih ding hiam/Topa na Pasian un a ~ leitang ahi hi | it is a land the Lord your God cares for/ganhing khat peuhpeuh ~ dingin a piak a | he gives any animal to be kept/kei hong ~ nadingin ka koih nop hangin | though I wanted to keep him to look after me) (r:54.3.5/2.22.7/5.11.12/2.22.10/57.1.13) (q:draft)
kepdiak = (t:v) (w:take special care of) (d:kep keep or look after, with diak, especially) (e:limtakin i ~ ding a kisamin) (r:46.12.24) (q:draft)
kepna = (t:n) (w:care/keeping/custody) (d:kep keep with na: the act of looking after, or the charge someone has) (e:nangma hong ~ hangin ka nungta hi/Gershon mi Jehiel’ ~ sung | in the custody of Jehiel the Gershonite/Shelomoth leh a sanggamte’ ~ sungah om hi | they were in the care of Shelomith and his relatives) (b:kep) (r:18.10.12/13.26.28/13.29.8) (q:draft)
kepsa = (t:adj) (w:kept/preserved) (d:kep keep, with sa, already done: that has been kept) (e:ka ~ Israel mite/ka ~ na sum tawi hiah a om hi | here is your money that I have kept) (b:kep) (r:23.49.6/42.19.20) (q:draft)
kepsak = (t:v) (w:entrust/give into the care of) (d:have someone keep or look after a thing) (e:a sum a ~ nasemte in/Pasian in kei hong ~ Lungdamna Thu | the gospel that God entrusted to me) (s:kemsak/keemsak) (b:kep) (r:42.19.15/54.1.11) (q:draft)
kepsak = (t:v) (w:keep for/look after for) (d:keep or tend something on behalf of another) (e:na tuuhonte uh hong ~ ding a/a thatte’ puante nangawn ka ~ hi | I even guarded the clothes of those who killed him/Pasian in ama vangliatna tawh a hong ~ ahi hi | which God keeps for you by his power) (b:kep) (r:23.61.5/60.1.5/44.22.20) (q:draft)
kepsakna = (t:n) (w:thing entrusted/deposit) (d:kepsak entrust, with the noun suffix na; na kepsakna is the entrusting of a thing to someone for keeping) (e:na ~ thu-ah ahi zongin) (b:kepsak) (r:3.6.2) (q:draft)
kepsakte = (t:n) (w:things entrusted/pledges) (d:kepsak entrust, with plural te; puan kepsakte are garments given into keeping as security for a loan) (e:a puan ~ uh phah uh hi) (b:kepsak) (r:30.2.8) (q:draft)
kepsakzo = (t:v) (w:be able to keep for/be able to guard) (d:kepsak keep on behalf of another, with zo, be able) (e:tua Ni dong hong ~ ding hi) (b:kepsak) (r:55.1.12) (q:draft)
kepte = (t:n) (w:pearls) (d:pearls, with the plural te; listed with gold and precious stones as costly goods and adornment) (e:kham, suangmanpha, le ~ tawh a kizem/a suangmanphate, a ~, a puanpakte | precious stones, pearls and fine linen) (r:66.18.16/66.18.12) (q:draft)
keptuam = (t:v) (w:withhold/keep back) (d:kep keep, with tuam, apart: keep something back for oneself) (e:amah in a ~ bangmah om lo) (s:humcip/kemcip) (r:1.39.9) (q:draft)
