keu = (t:v) (w:dry/dry up/wither) (d:be or become dry, said of water, land and plants; lei keu is dry land) (e:Nail gun tuite ~ ding a/ni sawmnih-le-sagih ni-in leitung ~ hi | on the twenty-seventh day the earth was dry/leitung pan in tuite a ~ mateng | until the water had dried up from the earth/Lei sunga ama zungte ~ in | his roots dry up in the ground/Tui om lohna lei ~ gamah | in a dry land without water) (s:kang) (a:kawt) (r:23.19.5/1.8.7/1.8.14/18.18.16/26.19.13)
keucip = (t:v) (w:dry up/be parched/wither) (d:keu dry with cip completely: dry right up, of streams, seed and pasture) (e:Nail gun hiangte kiamin ~ ding a/khai kituhte lei sungah ~ a | the seeds shrivel in the ground/Ka gam sung bang tanvei ~ ding ahi hiam | how long will my land lie parched/lonona khempeuh ~ ahih manin | because all the pastures are dried up) (s:kangcip/keugaw/keutum) (b:keu) (r:23.19.6/29.1.17/24.12.4/29.1.20) (q:draft)
keucipin = (t:v) (w:dry up/be parched) (d:keucip dry right up, with the linking suffix in) (e:a kituh khempeuh ~ huih in leenkhia-in) (b:keucip) (r:23.19.7) (q:draft)
keugaw = (t:v) (w:dry up/wither/be parched) (d:become completely dry; also describes waterless land) (e:guah a khaktan ciangin leitung ~ a/lopa kung in ~ a | the plant withers/a vun uh sing bangin ~-in | their skin has become as dry as a stick/Leitung vulin ~ a | the earth dries up and withers) (s:keucip/keutum/vulgawp) (r:18.12.15/38.9.11/59.1.11/25.4.8/23.24.4) (q:draft)
keugawgam = (t:n) (w:wilderness/desert) (d:keugaw dry and parched, with gam land: dry waterless country) (e:a lian a lipkhaphuai ~ i nawk hi) (r:5.1.19) (q:draft)
keugawp = (t:v) (w:dry up/be parched) (d:keu, dry, with gawp, thoroughly: become badly dried out) (e:guahzu lo ahih manin lei a ~ hi/lonona gam teng ~ a | the pastures dry up/a kinusia a ~ gam tawh kibang hi | it is like a deserted, parched land) (s:keugaw/keucip) (b:keu) (r:24.14.4/30.1.2/29.2.3) (q:draft)
keugawpin = (t:v) (w:dry up/wither) (d:keugawp dry up badly, with the linking suffix in) (e:Bashan gam ~ Karmel Mual kausan a) (b:keugawp) (r:34.1.4) (q:draft)
keuh = (t:v) (w:hatch/brood) (d:of a bird, sit on eggs and hatch them) (e:tua lai-ah tui-in ~ ding a) (s:op) (r:23.34.15) (q:draft)
keuhin = (t:v) (w:hatch/brood) (d:keuh hatch, with the linking suffix in) (e:bu tomin, tui-in, ~, ama kha liimah) (b:keuh) (r:23.34.15) (q:draft)
keuhkeuh = (t:adv) (d:placed after a verb to picture an action that goes on in quick repeats, as blood dripping or a person shaking) (e:Galte in note hong liingsak ~ ding/thaltang muk-ah si taak ~ a) (r:35.2.7/18.20.25) (q:draft, low confidence)
keuhsak = (t:v) (w:hatch) (d:keuh hatch, with sak, cause: bring eggs to hatching) (e:ama’ tui lopi ~ dinga a op) (b:keuh) (r:24.17.11) (q:draft)
keumang = (t:v) (w:dry up/wither away) (d:keu, dry, with mang, away: dry up completely, of pastures and trees) (e:singkung khempeuh ~ khinta hi/gamlak lonona munte a ~ hi | the pastures in the wilderness are withered/epel kungte a kipan singkung khempeuh ~ khin hi | the apple trees and all the other trees are dried up) (s:keutum/keucip/keugaw) (r:29.1.19/24.23.10/29.1.12) (q:draft)
keuna = (t:n) (w:drought/dryness/dry place) (d:noun from keu dry; khua keuna is drought, gam keuna or mun keuna dry land) (e:khua ~ tawh kisai-in/mun ~-ah vakin khawl nading a zong hi | it goes through dry places seeking rest/gam ~ sungah a an ding zong | seeking their food in the dry land/Sehnel gam ~ sungah | in the dry desert land) (b:keu) (r:24.14.1/28.13.5/42.11.24/18.24.5) (q:draft)
keuneute = (t:n) (w:small bowls/basins) (d:apparently keu bowl with neu small and plural te: vessels used in the temple service) (e:Biakpiakna a kizang ~, mei-am luahna kuangdaite) (r:24.52.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
keusak = (t:v) (w:dry up/make dry/wither) (d:keu dry with the causative sak: make water, land or plants dry) (e:na gunte ka ~ ding hi/a po kungte khempeuh ka ~ ding hi | I will dry up all their vegetation/A bual ka ~ ding a | I will dry up her sea/Tuumul tung bek ~ inla | make only the fleece dry) (s:kangsak/keutumsak) (a:kawtsak) (b:keu) (r:23.44.27/43.13.5/23.42.15/24.51.36/7.6.39) (q:draft)
keusakin = (t:v) (w:drying up/withering) (d:keusak make dry, with the connective in) (e:singkung hingte ~, singkung keute) (b:keusak) (r:26.17.24) (q:draft)
keuta = (t:v) (w:be dry/be parched) (d:keu dry, with ta, now or already: has become dry) (e:ka gim a, ka dang ~ hi) (b:keu) (r:19.69.3) (q:draft)
keute = (t:n) (w:cups/small bowls) (d:drinking vessels, named beside hai and kuang) (e:hai leh ~ ka pia a/um-le-beel, kuang leh ~ | pots, bowls and cups/tui buah nadinga kizang ~ zong a la uh hi | they also took the bowls used for drink offerings) (r:24.35.5/23.22.24/24.52.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
keute = (t:adj) (w:dry) (d:dry ones, keu with plural te, said of straw, grass and ground) (e:meikuang sungah lopa ~ a kattum bangin/mei in buhkung ~ kangtum a | fire burns up the dry straw/kua in lei ~ tui buak ahi hiam | who waters the dry ground/singkung ~ a hingsak kik | he makes the dry trees live again) (b:keu) (r:23.5.24/18.38.27/26.17.24) (q:draft)
keutum = (t:v) (w:wither/dry up) (d:dry out completely, said of plants) (e:lopa bangin ka ~ a/lokung hingte bangin ~ ding uh hi | like green plants they will wither/gamlak sing khempeuh ~ ding hi | all the trees of the field will wither/leengguite ~ a, oliv kungte keugaw ahih manin | because the vines wither and the olive trees dry up) (s:vul/keugaw/keumang/vulgawp) (r:19.102.4/19.37.2/26.31.15/29.1.10) (q:draft)
keutumin = (t:v) (w:withering/drying up) (d:keutum wither, with the connective in) (e:Leengguite ~ leenggahzu tawm semsem a/zing ciangin ~ meikhuk sungah a kikhultum lopa kungte | grass that withers tomorrow and is thrown into the oven) (b:keutum) (r:23.24.7/42.12.28) (q:draft)
keutumna = (t:n) (w:withering/drought/blight) (d:keutum wither, with the noun suffix na: a drying up of crops, listed among plagues) (e:leh ~, leh huihpi mutgawpna) (b:keutum) (r:5.28.22) (q:draft)
keutumpah = (t:v) (w:wither at once/dry up at once) (d:keu dry, with tum, completely, and pah, immediately) (e:a kat ciangin a ~ uh hi) (r:41.4.6) (q:draft)
keutumsak = (t:v) (w:make wither/dry up/wither) (d:keutum, wither away, with the causative sak) (e:a gah teng ~ hi/lopa bangin amaute kituancil-in ~ in | make them wither like trampled grass) (s:keusak) (b:keutum) (r:26.19.12/19.58.7) (q:draft)
Keziah = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Keziah) (d:the second daughter born to Job after his trials) (r:18.42.14)
kha = (t:n) (w:spirit/soul) (d:the spirit or soul of a person, and the Spirit of God; kha an is spiritual food) (e:a vekpi-un ~ an a nekhawm uh/Topa Pasian hangin ka ~ a nuam hi | my spirit rejoices in the Lord God/Topa’ ~ in kei tungtawnin thu hong gen a | the Spirit of the Lord spoke through me/Topa’ ~ in khauhtakin nang hong uk ding a | the Spirit of the Lord will come powerfully upon you) (r:1.1.2/46.10.3/42.1.47/10.23.2/9.10.6)
kha = (t:n) (w:moon) (d:the moon, often named together with ni, the sun, and aksi, the stars) (e:Ni leh ~ mial a/nangmah in ni leh ~ na bawl hi | you made the sun and the moon/na bawlsa ~ leh aksite | the moon and the stars you have made/zan pen ~ leh aksite a uksakpa tungah | to him who made the moon and stars rule the night) (s:khapi) (r:29.3.15/19.8.3/19.74.16/19.136.9)
kha = (t:n) (w:month) (d:a month of the year; kha khat is one month and kha masa the first month) (e:Filistia gam sungah ~ sagih sung om hi/~ thum sung seel hi | she hid him for three months/amah tawh ~ khat om hi | he stayed with him for a month/kum khat sungah a ~ masa hi ding hi | it shall be the first month of the year) (r:2.13.4/9.6.1/2.2.2/1.29.14/2.12.2)
kha = (t:part) (d:particle suffixed to verbs to convey the meaning of "happened") (e:nek ~, dawn~, hih~ pen hoih lo hi/amah si ~ ding ci-in lau hi | he feared that he too might die/ama' tungah siatna tung ~ ding ci-in lau hi | he feared that harm might come to him/Rebekah a noh laitak mu ~ hi | he happened to see him caressing Rebekah/Ka pa in kei hong lawng ~ leh | if my father happens to touch me) (r:18.21.25/1.38.11/1.42.4/1.26.8/1.27.12)
khaam = (t:v) (w:forbid/prohibit/stop/restrain) (d:tell someone not to do a thing, or hold a person or thing back; khaam zo is be able to stop) (e:Mordekai in ~ ahih manin/Kamtuam tawh pau ding na ~ kei un | do not forbid speaking in tongues/kuamah in hong ~ zo kei ding hi | no one will be able to stop me/A huk lai-in kua in ~ zo ding hiam | in her heat who can restrain her) (a:phal) (r:17.2.10/46.14.39/47.11.10/24.2.24) (q:draft)
khaam = (t:v) (w:celebrate) (d:with pawi, feast: hold a celebration, as zawhna pawi a victory feast) (e:singlamteh hangin zawhna pawi a ~ hi) (r:51.2.15) (q:draft, low confidence, one verse only)
khaamin = (t:v) (w:at the cost of/staking) (d:khaam, apparently stake or give as the price, with the linking ending in; luang khaamin, at the cost of the life of) (e:A tacil luang ~ tua khuapi bulpi) (b:khaam) (r:6.6.26) (q:draft, low confidence)
khaangkham = (t:v) (w:split open/crack open) (d:said of the ground torn open; with sak, cause to split) (e:lei na ~ sak khin hi) (s:khangkham) (r:19.60.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
khaap = (t:n) (w:span/handbreadth) (d:the width of the outstretched hand used as a measure) (e:ama ~ tawh vantungte teh) (s:khap) (r:23.40.12) (q:draft)
khade = (t:n) (w:crescent moon/crescent/new moon) (d:the moon in its curved shape; khade lim tawh a kibang kizepnate are crescent-shaped ornaments) (e:~ lim tawh a kibang kizepnate) (r:7.8.21/23.3.18) (q:draft, low confidence)
