khagawp = (t:v) (w:be very bitter) (d:kha be bitter, with gawp, severely: said of drink that has turned bitter) (e:zu khempeuh kisia-in ~ ta hi) (r:23.24.9) (q:draft)
khagilo = (t:n) (w:evil spirit) (d:kha, spirit, with gilo, evil: an evil spirit that comes upon a person and troubles him) (e:ama kiang panin ~ kihemkhia hi/Pasian kiang panin ~ in Saul hong bawhin | an evil spirit from God came upon Saul/Abimelek leh Shekhem mite kikalah ~ sawlin | sending an evil spirit between Abimelek and the people of Shechem) (s:dawi/dawigilo) (r:9.16.23/9.18.10/7.9.23) (q:draft)
khaging = (t:n) (w:sound of wings) (d:kha, wing, with ging, sound: the noise made by beating wings) (e:amaute’ leenna a ~ uh ka za hi/Tua a ~ in tuipi ging | that sound of wings, like the roar of the sea) (r:26.1.24) (q:draft)
khaguh = (t:n) (w:jawbone/jaw) (d:the jawbone or jaw of a person or an animal; la khaguh is the jawbone of a donkey) (e:la ~ thak khat mu a/sikkawi tawh a ~ sunlet zo ding | be able to pierce its jaw with a hook/a la ~ paai khia hi | he threw away the donkey jawbone/La ~ khat tawh mihing tulkhat ka that | with one donkey jawbone I killed a thousand men) (r:7.15.15/18.41.2/7.15.17/7.15.16) (q:draft)
khaguk = (t:n) (w:six months/half a year) (d:kha, month, with guk, six, written here as one word: six months, in kumthum leh khaguk, three years and six months) (e:kumthum leh ~ tawntung leitungah guah) (r:59.5.17) (q:draft)
khah = (t:v) (w:release/set free/let go/spare) (d:let go of someone who is held: release a prisoner, set a captive free, let a person leave, or spare a place from destruction) (e:Pilat in Zeisu ~ nuamin amaute kiangah/a leiba khempeuh maisakin a ~ hi | he cancelled all his debt and let him go/tua mite in a ~ uh hi | those people let them go/mihingte a ukpa in amah ~ hi | the ruler of peoples set him free/amaute’ hangin tua mun buppi ka ~ ding hi | I will spare the whole place for their sake) (s:suaktasak/suahtaksak) (a:mat/khum) (r:42.23.20/40.18.27/41.11.6/19.105.20/1.18.26) (q:draft)
khah = (t:v) (w:let loose/send out/send/put in) (d:let something go out or in among others, as a bird from the ark, animals among people or dust into water) (e:humpinelkaite amaute lakah ~ hi/no lakah gul kong ~ ding hi | I will send snakes among you/teembaw panin vakhu ~ leuleu hi | he again sent the dove out of the ark/nga beng tampi ka ~ ding a | I will send many fishermen) (r:12.17.25/4.5.17/24.8.17/1.8.10/24.16.16) (q:draft)
khahin = (t:v) (w:release/set free/let loose) (d:khah with the linking suffix in, letting go or setting free before another verb; of a judge, acquitting; of animals or anger, letting loose) (e:a dikpa ~ a mawhpa lelsak a/Kua in ~ a ut utin vaksak | who let it loose to roam as it pleases/amaute tungah ka hehna ~ | pouring out my anger on them/note lakah gamsate hong ~ | letting wild animals loose among you/a ganhing ~ midang khat’ lo-ah a tat leh | if he lets his animal loose and it grazes in the field of another) (b:khah) (r:5.25.1/18.39.5/26.22.31/3.26.22/2.22.5) (q:draft)
khahkhia = (t:v) (w:send out) (d:khah, let go, with khia, out: send out or let loose, as wild animals or anger) (e:gamsa kihtakhuaite ~-in | sending out fearsome wild beasts/Na hehna na ~ a | you unleashed your anger/note tungah ka hehna kong ~ ding a | I will pour out my anger on you) (s:sawlkhia) (r:26.14.15/2.15.7/23.1.24)
khahkhia = (t:v) (w:to cause/set free/release/rescue) (d:set free or bring out from the power of another: release a prisoner or a slave, rescue from the hand of an enemy) (e:Topa in thongkiate ~ hi | the Lord sets prisoners free/amau’ sal hih na panin note kong ~ ding hi | I will free you from being their slaves/a kinengniam mite ~-in | setting the oppressed free/Esau’ khut sung pan, kei hong ~ in | rescue me from the hand of Esau) (s:suaktasak/suahtaksak/honkhia) (a:mat) (r:19.146.7/2.6.6/23.58.6/1.32.11)
khahkhiat = (t:v) (w:release/set free/let go) (d:form of khahkhia, release or set free, used before words such as nading, ding, khit and sa) (e:mi that khat a ~ nadingin Pilat kiangah/note a dingin mi khat ka ~ a ngeina | the custom that I release one man to you/Khrih in eite hong ~ khitna hangin | because Christ has set us free/hih numei ~ ding kilawm hi lo ahi hiam | should not this woman be set free) (s:suaktasak/suahtaksak) (b:khahkhia) (r:44.3.14/24.34.11/43.18.39/48.5.1/42.13.16) (q:draft)
khahkhiatna = (t:n) (w:deliverance/rescue/release) (d:khahkhiat, set free, with the noun suffix na: the act of setting free or rescuing; also the sending out of something) (e:note ~ ding thahatna nei lo/Izipt mite’ khut sung panin amah in amaute a ~ | his rescuing them from the hand of the Egyptians/keima ~ bei ngei lo ding hi | my deliverance will never end/keima ~ om tawntung ding a | my deliverance will last forever) (s:hotkhiatna/suahtakna/suahtaksakna) (b:khahkhiat) (r:23.50.2/2.18.9/23.51.6/23.51.8) (q:draft)
khahkhiatsa = (t:adj) (w:set free/released/freed) (d:khahkhiat, set free, with sa, already done: that has been set free) (e:a ~ uh numei le pasal silate/na ~ uh sila numei le pasalte | the male and female slaves you had set free) (b:khahkhiat) (r:24.34.11/24.34.16) (q:draft)
khahkhong = (t:v) (w:let go unpunished/spare/tolerate/acquit) (d:leave someone alone without punishing or stopping them; mostly used with a negative) (e:amah ~ loin, amah na iim kei/Pasian in ~ loin hell khuk sungah khia a | God did not spare them but cast them into hell/a mawhte ka ~ kei ding hi | I will not let the guilty go unpunished/hih mite na hici ~ ding kilawm lo hi | it is not right to tolerate these people like this/Pasian in tanglai mite ~ loin | God did not spare the people of long ago) (a:daanpia) (r:5.13.8/33.6.11/61.2.4/29.3.20/17.3.8/61.2.5) (q:draft)
