khate = (t:n) (w:spirits/souls) (d:plural of kha, spirit: spirits, also the spirits of the dead) (e:thong sungah a kikhum ~ kiangah thu/sawltak nasem ~ hilo ahi uh hiam | are they not ministering spirits/si ~ tawh a kiho | one who speaks with the spirits of the dead) (b:kha) (r:60.3.19/58.1.14/5.18.11) (q:draft)
khate = (t:n) (w:months) (d:plural of kha, month) (e:Note in nite, ~, hunte, kumte) (b:kha) (r:48.4.10) (q:draft)
Khate = (t:n) (w:souls/lives) (d:khate written with a capital; plural of kha, spirit or soul) (e:nuntakna ~ a man mi in mipil/~ in Pasian tawh kipawl hiam | whether the spirits are from God) (b:khate) (r:20.11.30/62.4.1) (q:draft, low confidence)
khatguak = (t:adj) (w:alone/solitary/single) (d:khat one with guak, only: one by itself) (e:innkhum dawn-a vasa ~ om tawh) (s:guak) (r:19.102.7) (q:draft)
khathei = (t:adv) (w:perhaps/maybe/probably) (d:placed after the verb to say that something may well happen or be so, often followed by ding) (e:suante’ tungah kiheikik ~ ding hi/damzo ~ lai ding hi | perhaps she may yet be healed/eite hong ngaihsun ~ ding hi | perhaps he will take notice of us/a gitlohna uh pan kihei ~ ding uh hi | perhaps they will turn from their evil) (r:11.12.26/32.1.6/24.51.8/24.26.3) (q:draft)
khathum = (t:n) (w:three months) (d:kha month with thum three, written as one word) (e:Jerusalem ah ~ sung uk hi/Jerusalem ah ~ leh nisawm sung uk hi | he reigned in Jerusalem three months and ten days) (r:14.36.2/14.36.9) (q:draft)
khatin = (t:prep) (w:into) (d:khat, one, with in: into one, as in make into a woman or shape into another pot) (e:nakguh pen numei ~ bawl a/beel dang ~ a sek pha hi | he shaped it into another pot/ciangkhut nihte ciangkhut ~ ka bawl ding a | I will make the two sticks into one stick/amaute mi honpi ~ khangsak in | make them grow into a great multitude) (r:1.2.22/24.18.4/26.37.19/1.48.16)
khatin = (t:num) (w:single/solitary/sole) (d:khat, one, with in: with, on or in a single one, as zawl khatin, on a single pole, and ni khatin, for one day) (e:mi nih in zawl ~ a zawng uh hi | two men carried it on a single pole/Ni ~ peek khat hong pia ning | I will pay a denarius for one day) (b:khat) (r:4.13.23/40.20.2)
