khatpa = (t:pron) (w:the one/the other/one man) (d:khat, one, with pa marking a man: one of two men, or the other one) (e:khat in a ~ satin that hi/~’ min in Peleg ahi hi | the name of the one was Peleg/adang ~’ khe a kuaitan uh hi | they broke the legs of the other man/a ~’ zi hong pai a | the wife of one of them comes) (b:khat) (r:10.14.6/13.1.19/43.19.32/5.25.11) (q:draft)
khatpeuh = (t:pron) (w:anyone) (d:khat, one, with peuh, any: anyone, or any one thing; mi khatpeuh is any person) (e:Mi ~ in ama nuntakna/bil a nei mi ~ a om leh | if there is anyone who has ears/mi ~ in Topa tungah a piak theih ding | which anyone may present to the Lord) (r:41.8.37/41.4.23/3.7.11)
khatpeuhah = (t:det) (w:in any/at any/at every) (d:khatpeuh, any one, with the place ending -ah, after a noun of place: in or at any such place; mun khatpeuhah means anywhere, wherever) (e:a siangtho mun ~ na ne ding/amah i muhna mun ~ | wherever we find him/Khua ~ na lut uh ciangin | when you enter any town/leh kongkiu ~ mi ngakin om niloh hi | and at every corner she waits for people/gam ~ gal ka tunsak ciangin | when I bring war on any land) (b:khatpeuh) (r:3.10.14/20.7.12/10.17.12/42.9.4/26.33.2) (q:draft)
khatpeuhin = (t:adv) (w:at any/at some) (d:khatpeuh, any one, with the time marker in: ni hun khatpeuhin, on some day and hour or other) (e:a uploh ni hun ~) (b:khatpeuh) (r:40.24.50) (q:draft, low confidence)
