khatvei = (t:adv) (w:once/once more/again) (d:one time, from khat, one, and vei, time; with kik on the verb it means once more, and at the start of a story it means on one occasion) (e:~ kun kikin a khutme tawh/Mite in ~ bek si-in | people die only once/ka siangthona tawh ~ ka kiciam khin hi | I have sworn once by my holiness/Zeisu in ~ nakpi-in a kiko kik | Jesus cried out loudly once more/~, nihvei bang taai-in na hilh khit ciangin | after you have warned him once or twice) (r:43.8.8/41.14.39/58.9.27/19.89.35/40.27.50/56.3.10) (q:draft)
khatveina = (t:n) (w:first time) (d:khatvei, once, with the ending na: the first time something is done) (e:tapate a ~ na na paisak hi) (b:khatvei) (r:44.7.12) (q:draft)
khatveivei = (t:adv) (w:sometimes/at times) (d:khatvei once, with vei repeated: now and then) (e:~ midikte’ in migilote’ daantuah ding teng tuak | sometimes the righteous get the punishment due to the wicked) (s:veivei) (r:21.8.14) (q:draft)
khatzong = (t:pron) (w:even one/a single one) (d:khat, one, with zong, even; with om lo it means there is not even one) (e:a simloh ~ om lo hi) (s:khatbeek) (r:6.8.35) (q:draft)
