khaudum = (t:n) (w:blue cord) (d:khau, cord, with dum, blue: a blue cord or blue thread) (e:~ khat tawh dialpi tungah na gak ding/~ tawh a bilvangte na bawl ding hi | you shall make its loops with blue cord/~ khatin a kual tawh gakkhawm ding uh hi | they shall tie it to the rings with a blue cord) (r:2.28.37/2.28.28/2.26.4) (q:draft)
khauh = (t:adj) (w:hard/stiff/unyielding/strong) (d:hard, firm or strong, not giving way; lung khauh and lungsim khauh mean stubborn or hard-hearted, and khauh takin means firmly or severely) (e:Faro’ lungsim ~ lai a/lung ~ nawn kei un | do not be stubborn any longer/a khete sikzawl bangin ~ hi | its legs are hard like iron rods/a lian a ~ huihpi in mualte semkhamin | a great and strong wind tearing the mountains) (s:thakhauh) (a:nem/neem) (r:2.7.13/5.10.16/18.40.18/11.19.11) (q:draft)
