khauhna = (t:n) (w:hardness/stubbornness/firmness) (d:khauh, hard, with the ending na: the quality of being hard or unyielding; lungsim khauhna is stubbornness of heart, and in Philippians 3:6 it stands for zeal) (e:amau lungsim ~ bangin ka tasak hi/hih mihingte’ lungsim ~ hita leh a gitlohna uh | the stubbornness of this people or their wickedness/sik bangin a hoih khop khat ~ ciang a nei ding hi | it will have some of the hardness of iron/Ka lungsim ~ tawh ka gamta zongin | even though I walk in the stubbornness of my heart) (s:lungkhauhna) (a:nemna) (b:khauh) (r:19.81.12/5.9.27/27.2.41/5.29.19) (q:draft)
