khawh = (t:v) (w:cultivate) (d:prepare and work land or plants so that they bear a crop) (e:Ka ~ leitang ka guk ahih a/mihing in a ~ dingin ankungte | plants for people to cultivate/khuapi sungah a teengmite in a ~ ding leitang | land for the people living in the city to cultivate/Lo na ~ lohna uh ah buh at dingin | to reap in a field you did not cultivate) (s:ciin) (b:kho) (r:18.31.38/19.104.14/26.48.18/43.4.38)
khawhcip = (t:v) (w:pin/spear fast) (d:thrust a spear through someone so that he is fixed to the wall or the ground) (e:Kawm tawh David ka ~ ding hi/kawm tawh David ~ dingin khawh hi | he thrust to pin David to the wall) (r:9.18.11/9.19.10) (q:draft)
khawhcipsak = (t:v) (w:let pin/pin) (d:khawhcip, pin with a spear, with sak; hong khawhcipsak in, let me pin him) (e:khatvei bek hong ~ in) (b:khawhcip) (r:9.26.8) (q:draft)
khawhin = (t:v) (w:throw at/hurl at) (d:khawh, throw or thrust something at a person, with the linking suffix in; a different word from khawh, farm) (e:na khatpeuh tawh amah ~) (r:4.35.22) (q:draft, low confidence)
khawhkha = (t:v) (w:hit/strike) (d:khawh, throw or thrust a spear, with kha, reach the mark: hit someone with a thrown spear) (e:amah a ~ dingin ama lamah) (r:9.20.33) (q:draft)
khawhkik = (t:v) (w:farm again/plough again) (d:khawh farm with kik, again: work the field again for the next crop; lo khawhkik hun is the time to plough again) (e:ma-in lo ~ hun tungin) (b:khawh) (r:30.9.13) (q:draft)
khawhlawh = (t:v) (w:farm as a tenant/work land for hire) (d:work the land of another man for a share of the crop; lo khawhlawh is a tenant farmer and khawhlawh sak is let land out to tenants) (e:lo ~ dangte khosak ding hi/~ sakin gam dangah a pai hi | he let it out to tenants and went to another country) (r:40.21.41/42.20.9/40.21.33) (q:draft)
khawhlawhsak = (t:v) (w:rent out/let out to tenants) (d:khawhlawh, farm as a tenant, with the causative sak: give land to others to farm) (e:midangte ~ ding hi/a lo, midangte a ~ ding hi | he will let his field out to others/lo khawhlawhte ~ a, amah gam dangah a pai | he let it out to tenant farmers and went to another country) (s:lawhsak) (b:khawhlawh) (r:42.20.16/41.12.1/41.12.9) (q:draft)
khawhlawhsakin = (t:v) (w:rent out/let out to tenants) (d:khawhlawhsak, let land out to tenants, with the linking ending in: having let it out) (e:lo khote ~ gamdang ah pai a/lo khote ~ gamdangah a pai hi | he let it out to farmers and went to another country) (b:khawhlawhsak) (r:42.20.9/41.12.1) (q:draft)
khawhlawhte = (t:n) (w:tenants/tenant farmers/hired workers) (d:khawhlawh, one who works land for its owner, with the plural te; said after lo, field) (e:Tua lo ~ in a nasempa man uh a/Lo ~ in a nasemte na manin | the tenants seized his servants/lo ~ in a tapa a muh uh ciangin | when the tenants saw the son/lo ~’ khut tung panin a gah ngah dingin | to collect the fruit from the tenants) (s:lawhte) (b:khawhlawh) (r:41.12.3/41.12.2/40.21.35/42.20.14) (q:draft)
khawhlet = (t:v) (w:pierce through/spear through) (d:khawh in the sense spear or stab, with let, right through: stab so that the weapon goes through) (e:teipi lingnei tawh a lutang ~ zo ding/Ngasa khawhna teipi tawh a vun ~ zo ding | can you pierce its hide with fishing spears) (s:sunlet) (r:18.41.7) (q:draft)
khawhletzo = (t:v) (w:be able to pierce through) (d:khawhlet pierce through with zo, be able) (e:teipi lingnei tawh a lutang ~ ding) (s:sunletzo) (b:khawhlet) (r:18.41.7) (q:draft)
khawhna = (t:n) (w:cultivating/tilling/ploughing) (d:khawh, work the soil, with the ending -na; lo khawhna tu is the tool for tilling a field, a plowshare or hoe) (e:Lo ~ tuute namsau-in seek un la/a lo ~ tu, a tu-zum, a hei | their plough points, mattocks and axes/a namsaute uh lo ~ tu-in seek ding uh a | they will beat their swords into ploughshares) (b:khawh) (r:29.3.10/9.13.20/33.4.3) (q:draft)
khawhna = (t:n) (w:spearing/piercing) (d:in ngasa khawhna teipi, a spear for spearing fish, a harpoon) (e:Ngasa ~ teipi tawh a vun khawhlet) (r:18.41.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
khawhsa = (t:n) (w:produce/crops/harvest) (d:khawh farm with sa, already done: what one has grown; khawhsa tawh biakna, offering of produce) (e:na ~ uh sehsawm suah sehkhat/Ka ~ ante midangte’ nek suak hen la | may others eat the crops I have grown/~ tawh biakna na deih kei hi | you did not desire an offering of produce) (b:khawh) (r:5.26.12/18.31.8/19.40.6) (q:draft)
khawhsak = (t:v) (w:make plough/farm for) (d:khawh, farm or work the land, with sak: make an animal or person work the land, or in Luke 17:7 work the land for someone) (e:kol bulhin lo ~ ding ka ngaihsun hi/na lo uh hong ~ ahi a | whether he ploughs your field for you) (b:khawh) (r:28.10.11/42.17.7) (q:draft)
khawhsakte = (t:n) (w:field workers/those who work the land for) (d:khawhsak, work the land for someone, with the plural te; the English has the workers who mowed your fields) (e:Na lo uh a hong ~ a thaman) (b:khawhsak) (r:59.5.4) (q:draft)
khawhsate = (t:n) (w:produce/crops) (d:khawhsa, what one has grown, with the plural te) (e:a ~ uh khawmin) (b:khawhsa) (r:16.13.15) (q:draft)
khawi = (t:v) (w:spare/keep alive/let live) (d:keep and not kill, often as hing khawi, keep alive; in Ecclesiastes 3:3 it is the opposite of killing) (e:Numei aisannu na hing ~ kei ding uh/amaute khat zong hing ~ lo hi | he did not leave even one of them alive/amaute in eite hong ~ leh eite i nungta | if they spare us we shall live/Numei khempeuh hing ~ na hi uh hiam | have you kept all the women alive/Gawh hun om a, ~ hun om hi | there is a time to kill and a time to spare) (s:nungtasak) (a:that) (r:2.22.18/12.10.14/12.7.4/4.31.15/21.3.3) (q:draft)
khawi = (t:v) (w:keep/rear/raise) (d:keep and look after an animal or a person in one's charge: vasa khawi is a pet bird, sila-in khawi is keep as a slave; in Numbers 6:5 of letting the hair grow long) (e:vasa ~ bangin bawl zong ding/a mipih Judah mite sila-in ~ thei lo ding | no one may keep fellow Jews as slaves/amah in a sam a sau-in ~ ding hi | he shall let his hair grow long/gan ~ nading munin hoihsa mahmah uh hi | they found it a very good place for keeping livestock) (s:khoi) (r:18.41.5/24.34.10/24.34.8/4.6.5/4.32.1) (q:draft, low confidence)
khawikik = (t:v) (w:keep again/take back) (d:khawi keep, with kik, again; sila-in khawikik, keep as a slave again) (e:sila-in ~ thei nawn lo ding hi) (b:khawi) (r:24.34.10) (q:draft)
khawilevulh = (t:n) (w:nurture/rearing) (d:khawi rear, le and, vulh feed: the rearing and feeding of young; the English has blessings of the breast and womb) (e:~ le tuletate) (r:1.49.25) (q:draft, low confidence)
khawilo = (t:v) (w:not spare) (d:khawi, keep alive, with lo, not; hin’ khawilo, did not keep alive) (e:kuamah hin’ ~ a) (b:khawi) (r:19.78.50) (q:draft)
khawipa = (t:n) (w:breeder/keeper) (d:khawi, keep or rear, with pa marking a man; tuu khawipa is a man who raises sheep) (e:Mesha in tuu ~ ahi hi) (b:khawi) (r:12.3.4) (q:draft)
khawite = (t:n) (w:domestic animals/livestock/pets) (d:khawi, rear or keep animals, with plural -te: animals that are kept; gan khawite is livestock and ui khawite are house dogs) (e:na gan ~ ka that khin ding hi/a gan ~ uh keek tawh a denglum hi | he struck down their livestock with lightning/ui ~ piak ding kilawm lo hi | it is not right to give it to the dogs) (s:gankhawite/innsate) (b:khawi) (r:26.32.13/40.15.27/19.78.48/40.15.26) (q:draft)
khawk = (t:n) (w:section/portion/plot/column) (d:one marked-off part of something longer or larger, as a stretch of wall, a plot of land or a column of writing) (e:~ dang khat sung puah uh hi/Eliashib’ inn kongkhak ciang dong ~ khat sung puah hi | he repaired a section as far as the door of the house of Eliashib/~ thum ~ li bang a sim khit ciangin | when he had read three or four columns) (r:16.3.11/24.36.23/16.3.20) (q:draft)
khawkte = (t:n) (w:sections/panels/compartments) (d:plural of khawk, a section or enclosed part; tuu-khawkte are sheep pens) (e:tuate in a ~ nei-in/tuute adingin tuu-~ bawl uh hi | they built pens for the sheep/leengpei lite in a ~’ nuai-ah om hi | the four wheels were under the panels) (b:khawk) (r:11.7.28/4.32.36/11.7.32) (q:draft)
khawl = (t:v) (w:accompany)
khawlcip = (t:v) (w:stand still/stop completely/come to a standstill) (d:khawl, stop or rest, with cip, firmly: stop completely and stay still, as the sun and moon in the sky or a work that is halted) (e:tuipi ~ thei lo a/Kha aw, Aijalon Kuam-ah ~ in | moon, stand still over the Valley of Aijalon/ni leh kha a omna san-ah ~ uh hi | sun and moon stood still in their place on high/kum nihna dong tua bangin ~ phot hi | so it stood still until the second year) (s:dinkhawl) (b:khawl) (r:23.57.20/15.4.24/6.10.12/35.3.11) (q:draft)
khawlei = (t:n) (d:see <khawlei-uikai>) (e:~ uikai a pai nading lampi) (r:18.38.32)
Khawlei = (t:n) (c:star) (w:the Bear) (d:first part of Khawlei-uikai, the constellation of the Bear, also written as two words) (e:~ uikai a pai nading lampi) (b:khawlei) (r:18.38.32/18.9.9) (q:draft)
khawlei uikai = (t:n) (d:see <khawlei-uikai>)
khawlei-uikai = (t:n) (c:star) (w:the Bear) (d:the constellation of the Bear, the Great Bear, named in the book of Job)
khawlin = (t:v) (w:stop/cease/turn from) (d:khawl with the ending -in: stopping, leaving off, before the next action) (e:tawlkhat ~ ngai in la/Ramah a lam ~ Tirzah ah om hi | he stopped building Ramah and stayed in Tirzah/a gitlohna ~ a man a hoih-in gamta leh | if he turns from his wickedness and does what is right/a gamtat hoih ~ mawhna a bawl ciangin | when he stops doing good and commits sin) (b:khawl) (r:18.37.14/11.15.21/26.33.19/26.18.26) (q:draft)
khawlmun = (t:n) (w:haven/resting place/harbour) (d:khawl stop or rest, with mun place; teembaw khawlmun is a place where ships stop) (e:amah in teembaw ~ suak ding a) (s:khawlna) (r:1.49.13) (q:draft)
Khawlmun = (t:n) (w:haven/resting place/lodging place) (d:khawlmun, a place to stop and rest, capitalised in place names: Khawlmun Nuam, Fair Havens; Khimham Khawlmun, Geruth Kimham) (e:Lasia khua tawh kinai ~ Nuam kici mun/Khimham ~-ah a khawl uh hi | they stopped at Geruth Kimham) (b:khawlmun) (r:44.27.8/24.41.17) (q:draft)
khawlmunte = (t:n) (w:harbours/resting places) (d:khawlmun, a place to stop and rest, with the plural te; of ships, a harbour) (e:~ om nawn lo ahih manin) (b:khawlmun) (r:23.23.1) (q:draft)
khawlna = (t:n) (w:rest/resting place/stopping place/harbour) (d:khawl, stop or rest, with the ending na: the act of stopping, or a place to stop and rest; teembaw khawlna mun is a harbour and teembaw khawlna sikkawi is an anchor) (e:Krete gam teembaw ~ mun hi a/Tua teembaw ~ munah phalbi sung tawntung om huai lo | that harbour was not fit to stay in all winter/teembaw ~ sikkawi li a khia uh a | they dropped four anchors/gialpi leh vanging a ~ Faro in a muh ciangin | when Pharaoh saw that the hail and thunder had stopped) (s:khawlmun/tawlngakna) (b:khawl) (r:44.27.12/20.26.2/44.27.29/2.9.34) (q:draft)
khawlpah = (t:v) (w:stop at once/stop immediately) (d:khawl stop with pah, at once) (e:si puate zong a ~ uh hi/a siluang ~ a | her bleeding stopped at once) (r:42.7.14/41.5.29) (q:draft)
khawlpak = (t:v) (w:stop/break off) (d:khawl stop, with pak, for a while or promptly: leave off a quarrel) (e:a nasiat ma-in kitot ~ in) (r:20.17.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
khawlsak = (t:v) (w:stop/halt/detain) (d:make someone or something stop or rest; khawl with sak, cause) (e:Mangpa in leeng ~ a/Amah in mihingte’ nasep ~ a | he stops the work of people/Nong ~ zongin na an ka ne kei ding hi | though you detain me I will not eat your food/gunkuang tui geiah a ~ uh hi | they brought the boat to rest at the shore) (s:tawpsak) (b:khawl) (r:44.8.38/18.37.7/7.13.16/41.6.53) (q:draft)
khawlsakin = (t:v) (w:stopping/making rest) (d:khawlsak, make stop or rest, with the linking suffix in) (e:amah in a puate tawlkhat ~/nisim biakna piaknate nangawn ~ | stopping even the daily offerings) (b:khawlsak) (r:10.6.13/27.8.11) (q:draft)
khawlsakna = (t:n) (w:stopping) (d:khawlsak make stop, with the noun suffix na; teembaw khawlsakna sikkawipi, the iron hook for stopping a ship, is an anchor) (e:teembaw ~ sikkawipi li khiasuk uh a) (b:khawlsak) (r:44.27.29) (q:draft)
khawm = (t:adv) (w:along/together/side by side) (d:after a verb, doing the action together with others or jointly) (e:ama min pahtawi ~ ni/Samul leh khau, a kigan ~ puan | cloth of wool and linen woven together/adangte tawh kisim ~ lo hi | they were not counted along with the others/amaute tawh ka luah ~ kei ding uh hi | we will not inherit together with them) (s:khawmin/khop) (r:19.34.3/5.22.11/4.1.47/4.32.19)
khawma = (t:adv) (w:together) (d:khawm with the linking a; ding khawma om, be standing together with) (e:amaute tawh ding ~ om a muh uh ciangin) (b:khawm) (r:44.4.14) (q:draft)
khawmin = (t:v) (w:gather/assemble/bring together) (d:khawm, gather, with the linking suffix in: gathering people or things together before a following action) (e:Jehu in mi khempeuh ~ amaute kiangah/Topa na Pasian un tua lai panin note hong ~ | the Lord your God will gather you from there/Amaute in a sanggamte uh ~ amau kisian’suah uh a | they gathered their brothers and consecrated themselves/Mi a siang khat in bawngla vute ~ | a clean man shall gather the ashes of the heifer) (b:khawm) (r:12.10.18/2.35.1/5.30.4/14.29.15/4.19.9) (q:draft)
khawmin = (t:adv) (w:together) (d:khawm, together, with the ending in, after another verb: doing it together with others) (e:mite tawh kei kap ~/Na an uh a gilkialte tawh ne ~ | eating your food together with the hungry/Judah in a sanggampa Simeon tawh pai ~ | Judah went together with his brother Simeon/Sanggam pasalte teng ~ | when brothers live together) (s:khawm) (b:khawm) (r:18.30.25/23.58.7/7.1.17/5.25.5) (q:draft)
khawmkhawm = (t:v) (w:gather/gather together) (d:khawm, bring together, said twice: keep gathering; set against kithehthangsak, scatter) (e:Keimah tawh a ~ lote in) (a:kithehthangsak) (b:khawm) (r:40.12.30/42.11.23) (q:draft)
khawmkik = (t:v) (w:gather again/gather up/collect) (d:khawm gather with kik, again or back) (e:a khamvalte uh ~ uh a/Israel-te a kiteelkhia mi tul sawmthum ~ hi | he again gathered thirty thousand chosen men of Israel) (s:kaikhawmkik) (b:khawm) (r:40.14.20/10.6.1) (q:draft)
khawmkikin = (t:v) (w:gather again/gather back) (d:khawmkik with the linking suffix in) (e:Amaute ka thehthangna gam panin ~) (b:khawmkik) (r:26.11.17) (q:draft)
khawmluzepna = (t:n) (w:capital) (d:the ornamental top of a pillar; apparently another spelling of khuamluzepna, which stands in the same verse) (e:lu dawnah a om ~ nihte) (s:khuamluzepna) (r:14.4.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
khawmna = (t:n) (w:togetherness/fellowship) (d:khawm, together, with the noun suffix na, after a verb: the doing of something together, as kipawl khawmna, fellowship, and gamtat khawmna, acting together) (e:kipawl ~, khomun balnenna leh thungetna/kamsangte tawh a gamtat ~ | his acting together with the prophets/Lungdamna Thu ka hilh ~-ah hong huhin | helping me in teaching the gospel together) (b:khawm) (r:44.2.42/9.10.11/50.4.3) (q:draft)
khawmnate = (t:n) (w:meetings/gatherings) (d:khawmna, doing together, with the plural te; kikhop khawmnate are the meetings together) (e:eite in kikhop ~ pelh loin om ni) (b:khawmna) (r:58.10.25) (q:draft)
khawmpa = (t:n) (w:fellow/companion/co-worker) (d:khawm together with pa, the man: after a verb, the man who does it together with someone; nasem khawmpa is a fellow worker) (e:kei tawh nasem ~ lang pang in/Kote tawh Khazih’ nasem ~ Urbanas | Urbanus, our fellow worker in Christ) (b:khawm) (r:38.13.7/45.16.9) (q:draft)
khawmpih = (t:adv) (w:together with/along with/fellow) (d:khawm, together, with pih, with someone: after a verb, do it together with someone or share in it; after a noun, a fellow, as in galkap khawmpih fellow soldier) (e:Ankuang ka sawk ~ pa in/thu upna-ah galkap ~ Arkhippas-te tungah | to Archippus, our fellow soldier in the faith/gimna na hong thuak ~ uh mah bangin | just as you share in our sufferings/Jordan Gun galkhatah na om ~ ngei pa | the man who was with you across the Jordan) (s:khoppih) (b:khawm) (r:40.26.23/57.1.2/47.1.7/43.3.26) (q:draft)
khawmpihpa = (t:n) (w:one who shares with/fellow) (d:khawmpih, do together with someone, with pa, the man: the man with whom one does it, as the one who dips in the dish with me) (e:kei tawh ankuang ka sawk ~ ahi hi/Kei tawh kuang sungah an ka sawk ~ in | the one who dips food in the bowl with me) (b:khawmpih) (r:41.14.20/40.26.23) (q:draft)
khawmpihte = (t:n) (w:companions/guests/those together with) (d:khawmpih, do together with someone, with the plural te: the people with whom one does it; a tut khawmpihte, those who sat at table with him, his guests) (e:a tut ~ a zahtak manin/sabuai ah a tut ~ a zahtak manin | because he respected those sitting at table with him) (b:khawmpih) (r:40.14.9/41.6.26) (q:draft)
khawmsa = (t:adj) (w:already together) (d:khawm, together, with sa, already done; lum khawmsa is having lain together with someone) (e:pasal tawh a lum ~ numei khempeuh) (b:khawm) (r:7.21.11) (q:draft)
khawmsak = (t:v) (w:gather/assemble/bring together) (d:khawm, together, with the causative sak: make people or things come together, collect or assemble them) (e:Israel mite leh kamsangte ~ hi/an khempeuh amaute ~ in la | let them collect all the food/anlomte lakah a kiate hong ~ in | let me gather what has fallen among the sheaves/amau mah buhtu ~ tawm un | let them gather straw themselves) (s:kaikhawm/khopsak) (a:thehthang/khenthang) (b:khawm) (r:11.18.20/1.41.35/8.2.7/2.5.7) (q:draft)
khawmsak = (t:part) (d:placed after a verb: cause or allow someone to do the action together with others) (e:gamh luah ~ hi/tua lai-ah nang tawh ding ~ in | have them stand there together with you/amaute kikum ~ un | let them take counsel together/Paul leh Barnabas tawh pai ~ leng a hoih hi | it is good to send them along with Paul and Barnabas) (b:khawm) (r:18.42.15/47.4.14/4.11.16/23.45.21/44.15.22) (q:draft, low confidence)
khawmsate = (t:n) (w:those joined together) (d:khawmsa, already together, with the plural te; a gawm khawmsate are those who have been joined together) (e:Pasian in a gawm ~ mite in) (b:khawmsa) (r:40.19.6) (q:draft)
khawmte = (t:n) (w:those together with/companions/fellow) (d:khawm, together, with plural -te, placed after a verb: the people who do the action together, as an ne khawmte, those eating together) (e:Amah tawh an ne ~ in/Zeisu tawh a kikhai ~ in zong a zahko | those crucified with Jesus also mocked him/amah tawh a ding ~ a mu uh hi | they saw those standing with him/Khazih tawh a ngah ~ i hi ding hi | we shall be sharers with Christ) (s:omkhawmte) (b:khawm) (r:42.7.49/58.3.14/41.15.32/42.9.32) (q:draft)
khawng = (t:part) (w:about/or so/approximately) (d:placed after a number, a time or an item to make it approximate) (e:tua lai-ah kha li sung ~ om hi/mi sawmthum-le-guk ~ thatin | killing about thirty-six men/khatvei nihvei ~ Jerusalem pua lamah giak uh hi | once or twice they spent the night outside Jerusalem/mihing sawmnih leh nga ~ na om a | there were about twenty-five men/ni sawm le ni nih ~ pha pan hi | it is only about twelve days) (r:7.19.2/44.24.11/6.7.5/16.13.20/26.8.16) (q:draft)
khawng = (t:v) (w:charge/sell dear) (d:ask a high price for goods) (e:sum tampi i ~ nuam hi) (r:30.8.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
khawngah = (t:ppm) (w:on/around/among/somewhere at) (d:khawng, thereabouts, with the place marker -ah: at or on such places, here and there on, as inn tung khawngah, up on the houses) (e:kulh tung ~ tai zaizai uh hi/Inn tung ~ kahto ngeingai uh a | they climb up onto the houses/gamlak le mualtung ~ vak kawikawi-in | wandering about in deserts and on mountains/han lak ~ om tawntung hi | he always stayed among the tombs/ka khe kiang ~ hong tu in | sit down somewhere by my feet) (b:khawng) (r:29.2.9/58.11.38/42.8.27/59.2.3) (q:draft)
khawngai = (t:adj) (w:desolate/forlorn/lonely) (d:sad and alone like one bereaved) (e:Tamar lungzuang ~-in a om hi/ka ~ mahmah hi | I am utterly forlorn) (r:10.13.20/19.35.12) (q:draft)
khawngin = (t:part) (w:about/around) (d:khawng, approximately, with in, placed after a time: at about that time) (e:nai guk kikal ~ a nungzuite kiang) (b:khawng) (r:41.6.48) (q:draft)
khawngte = (t:part) (w:and the like/such things as) (d:khawng placed after each item of a list of examples, with the plural te after the last item) (e:sumngo kibawl beellekuang ~ sawp ding) (b:khawng) (r:41.7.4) (q:draft)
khawphelep = (t:n) (w:lightning/flash of lightning) (d:a flash of lightning; khawphelep bangin tang is shine like lightning) (e:A maitang in ~ bangin tang a) (s:khuaphialep/khuaphia/keek) (r:27.10.6) (q:draft)
khazap = (t:n) (w:wing) (d:the wings in motion; khazap ging is the sound of beating wings) (e:Kherubte’ ~ ging pen/A ~ ging in | the sound of their wings) (s:khaphung) (r:26.10.5/66.9.9) (q:draft)
khazapna = (t:n) (w:beating of wings/flapping) (d:khazap, wing, with the noun suffix na: the moving of the wings and its sound) (e:huihlakah a ~ le leengpei gingte) (s:zapna) (b:khazap) (r:26.3.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
khazel = (t:part) (d:placed after a verb, kha, happen to, with zel, again or in turn: might also come to do) (e:min kong daisak ~ ding hi) (r:20.30.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
khazenzen = (t:adv) (w:by any chance/ever) (d:kha, happen to, with zenzen, by chance; with leh, if it should ever happen that) (e:siatna tung ~ leh) (r:1.42.38) (q:draft)
Khazih = (t:name) (w:Christ) (d:the Christ, the Messiah, title of Jesus as the one anointed by God) (r:44.8.5/46.1.4)
khe = (t:n) (w:foot/leg) (d:the foot or the whole leg of a person or an animal; khe li is four legs, and the leg of a table is also khe) (e:khut hoih lo, ~ hoih lo/Na ~ in nang hong puksak leh | if your foot causes you to stumble/Amau ~ un mi sisan suah dingin a manlang | their feet are swift to shed blood/~ li nei-in kha a nei ganhing | winged creatures that have four legs) (r:3.21.19/41.9.45/45.3.15/3.11.23) (q:draft)
khe-baite = (t:n) (w:the lame/lame people) (d:khe, foot, with bai, lame, and the plural te) (e:mittawte leh ~, biakna innpi sungah) (s:khebaite/khezawte/khelbaite) (r:40.21.14) (q:draft)
khebai = (t:adj) (w:lame/crippled) (d:khe, foot or leg, with bai, lame: unable to walk properly; also a lame foot or a lame person) (e:~ mi tampi in damna a ngah uh hi/a ~ a mittaw | lame or blind/a nu gil sung pan a ~ mi khat | a man lame from his mother’s womb/~ mipa pen sakhi bangin diangin lam ding a | the lame man will leap like a deer) (s:bai/khezaw/khelbai) (r:44.8.7/5.15.21/44.3.2/23.35.6) (q:draft)
Khebaipa = (t:n) (w:lame man) (d:khebai lame with pa, which marks a man) (e:~’ khe, kiman’na om loin) (r:20.26.7) (q:draft)
khebaite = (t:n) (w:the lame/lame people) (d:khebai, lame, with the plural te) (e:mipoite, ~ leh mittawte na sam in/~’ adingin khe ka hi hi | I was feet to the lame/keimah in ~ kaikhawmin | I will gather the lame/~ nangawnin van ngah ding uh hi | even the lame will take plunder) (s:khe-baite/khezawte/khelbaite) (b:khebai) (r:42.14.13/33.4.6/18.29.15/23.33.23) (q:draft)
Khebar = (t:name) (c:river) (w:Kebar) (d:river or canal in Babylonia beside which Ezekiel lived among the exiles and saw his visions) (r:26.1.1/26.10.15)
khebom = (t:n) (w:paw/leg of an animal) (d:the paw or lower leg of an animal; in Amos 3:12 the two legs of a sheep saved from a lion) (e:amau’ ~ tawh a paite khempeuh/tuu ~ nih ahi a | two legs of a sheep) (s:khecin) (r:3.11.27/30.3.12) (q:draft)
khebuh = (t:n) (w:anklet/bangle) (d:ornament worn by women on the foot or ankle; khe is foot) (e:~ hoihte, lutuam leh khade lim) (r:23.3.18) (q:draft)
khebui = (t:see) <khebui-in>
khebui-in = (t:adj) (w:crippled/maimed in the foot) (d:khe foot with bui maimed and the linking ending in: being without a foot; paired with khutbui, maimed in the hand) (e:khutbui ~ nuntakna sungah na tum leh) (r:41.9.46/41.9.44) (q:draft)
khecin = (t:n) (w:hoof/paw/claw) (d:the hoof or claws of an animal foot; a khecin a ka means it has a divided hoof) (e:a ~ a ka/a ~ ka lo ahih ciangin | because it does not have a divided hoof/sumngo ~ a nei sapi lina | the fourth beast, which had bronze claws/muvanlai’ ~ bangin a hong sau hi | they grew long like the claws of an eagle) (s:khebom) (r:3.11.3/9.17.37/3.11.6/27.7.19/27.4.33) (q:draft)
khecinte = (t:n) (w:hooves/hoofs/claws) (d:khecin, hoof or claw, with the plural te) (e:a ki leh a ~ tawh a kim/amau sakolte’ ~ pen meisuang bangin sak a | the hooves of their horses are hard as flint/a ~ nangawn hawkkhiatsak zawsop hi | he even tears off their hooves) (b:khecin) (r:19.69.31/23.5.28/38.11.16) (q:draft)
khedap = (t:n) (w:sandal/shoe) (d:footwear, a sandal or shoe; khedap bulh is put on sandals, khedap suah is take them off, and khedap khau is the sandal strap) (e:~ bulh un la, puanak na silh/na ~ na suah in | take off your sandals/Ama ~ khau phel ding nangawnin ka kilawm kei | I am not worthy even to untie the strap of his sandal/Edom gam tungah ka ~ ka lawn hi | on Edom I toss my sandal) (r:41.6.9/44.7.33/43.1.27/19.60.8) (q:draft)
khedapkaihte = (t:n) (w:sandals) (d:khedap, sandal, with kaih and the plural te; apparently sandals that are strapped on) (e:~ pia-in an leh tui vaak uh) (s:khedapte) (r:14.28.15) (q:draft)
khedapte = (t:n) (w:sandals/shoes) (d:khedap, sandal, with the plural te) (e:na ~ suahkhia in/a paatsa, a kiphop ~ bulhin | wearing worn and patched sandals/na ~ uh sia nai lo hi | your sandals have not worn out/Dangka-ip, thung-ip, ~ keng loin | without purse, bag or sandals) (s:khedapkaihte) (b:khedap) (r:2.3.5/6.9.5/5.29.5/42.22.35) (q:draft)
Khedorla = (t:see) <Khedorla-omer>
Khedorla-omer = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Kedorlaomer) (d:king of Elam who led the alliance of four kings that was defeated by Abram) (e:kum sawm-le-nih sung ~’ khut nuai-ah om uh a) (r:1.14.4/1.14.1) (q:draft)
Khedorlaomer = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Chedorlaomer/Kedorlaomer) (d:spelling of Khedorla-omer, the king of Elam who led four kings and was defeated by Abram) (r:1.14.1)
kheek = (t:v) (w:change/exchange) (d:put one thing in the place of another, as clothes; with tawh, exchange something for something else) (e:na puante uh ~ un/amaute pen puan bangin na ~ a | you change them like a garment/thuman thutak pen thuzuau tawh a ~ uh a | they exchanged the truth for a lie/tuate a milim tawh a ~ uh hi | they exchanged it for images of these) (s:khek/kheel/khel/laih) (r:1.35.2/45.1.25/19.102.26/45.1.23) (q:draft)
kheek = (t:v) (w:spin/twist) (d:twist fibre into thread or cord) (e:Amah in khau ~-in/na lah sem lo, khau lah ~ lo uh | they neither labor nor spin thread) (r:20.31.19/40.6.28) (q:draft)
kheekin = (t:v) (w:spinning/twisting) (d:kheek, spin thread, with in) (e:Amah in khau ~ a puan ding) (b:kheek) (r:20.31.19) (q:draft)
kheekna = (t:n) (w:exchange/substitute) (d:kheek exchange with the noun suffix na: the exchanging, or the thing given in exchange; a kheekna ganhing is the animal put in its place) (e:tua ganhing leh a ~ ganhing) (s:khekna) (b:kheek) (r:3.27.10/19.106.20) (q:draft)
kheekte = (t:n) (w:changers/exchangers) (d:kheek change with the plural te: those who change; dangka kheekte are the money changers) (e:dangka ~’ sabuaite leh vakhu zuakte’ tutphahte) (b:kheek) (r:40.21.12/41.11.15) (q:draft)
kheel = (t:v) (w:change/alter) (d:lungsim kheel is to change the mind, to relent) (e:a lungsim hong ~ kik a/Amah in hun leh khuahunte ~ | he changes times and seasons/ka kam pauna ka ~ nuam hi | I want to change my tone/paikhia thute ka ~ kei ding hi | I will not alter the words that have gone out/ama ngaihsutna ~ lo ding hi | he will not change his mind) (s:khel/khek/kheek) (r:30.7.3/27.2.21/48.4.20/19.89.34/19.110.4) (q:draft)
kheelin = (t:v) (w:changing/altering) (d:kheel, change, with the ending -in, linking to the next verb; lungsim kheel means change one's mind, relent) (e:i Pasian in a lungsim ~/amaute’ mai-ah a gamtat ~ | changing his behaviour before them/A kihtakhuai na hehna daisak inla, na lungsim ~ | turn from your fierce anger and relent/a lungsim uh ~ Pasian a up uhleh | if they change their minds and believe God) (s:khelin) (b:kheel) (r:29.2.14/9.21.13/2.32.12/45.11.23) (q:draft)
kheelkik = (t:v) (w:change back/relent/revoke) (d:kheel change with kik, back again; lungsim kheelkik, change one's mind) (e:Topa in zong a lungsim hong ~ a/ke’n ka ~ thei kei hi | I cannot change it back/a gensa thu a ~ ding hi | he will take back what he has pronounced/na lungsim uh na ~ leuleu uh a | but you changed your minds again) (s:khelkik) (b:kheel) (r:30.7.3/4.23.20/24.26.13/24.34.16) (q:draft)
kheelsak = (t:v) (w:change/transform) (d:kheel, change, with sak: make something change, as when a person is given a new name) (e:a min Zedekiah-in ~ hi/ama min Jehoiakim ci-in ~ hi | he changed his name to Jehoiakim/Joshua ci-in a min ~ hi | he changed his name to Joshua/pawi bawlna hunte ~ ding hanciam ding a | he will try to change the festival times/a minthang pumpi tawh hong ~ ding hi | he will change ours into a glorious body) (s:khelsak/kheksak) (b:kheel) (r:12.24.17/50.3.21/12.23.34/4.13.16/27.7.25) (q:draft)
kheelzo = (t:v) (w:be able to change/resist) (d:kheel, change, with zo, be able: be able to alter what was said or decided) (e:Pasian’ cihsa kua in ~ ding) (b:kheel) (r:45.9.19) (q:draft)
kheem = (t:v) (w:lie/deceive) (d:say what is false to someone, deceive or mislead; in the Gospels also tempt, as the devil does) (e:midangte ~ kei in/kuamahpeuh ~ kei in/nang in Kha Siangtho ~ a | you have lied to the Holy Spirit/Kuamah in note bangmah hangin hong ~ kei hen | let no one deceive you in any way/tua mi in ama pumpi a ~ hi | that person deceives himself/ni sawmli tawntung dawimangpa in a ~ hi | for forty days the devil tempted him) (s:khem/zuau) (r:41.13.5/43.7.47/44.5.3/53.2.3/48.6.3/42.4.2)
kheem = (t:n) (w:deceit) (d:deceiving, pretence; mi kheem is a deceiver and it kheem is love that is only pretended) (e:mi ~ tampi | many deceivers/it ~ lo it takpina | sincere love without pretence/unau it ~ bang hi loin | not with a pretended brotherly love) (s:kheemna/khemna) (r:63.1.7/47.6.6/60.1.22)
kheembawlin = (t:v) (w:tricking/by deceit) (d:kheem, deceive, with bawl, do, and in: by using trickery) (e:Zeisu bangci ~, a mat khit uh) (r:40.26.4) (q:draft)
kheemin = (t:v) (w:deceiving/cheating) (d:kheem, deceive, with the ending -in, linking to the next verb) (e:thukhamna tawh hong ~ hong that hi/midangte ~, amau mahmah zong a kikheem ding | deceiving others and being deceived themselves/Kuamah ~ a sum ka la kei uh hi | we have cheated no one of his money/leitungah a om mite ~ | deceiving those who live on the earth) (s:khemin) (b:kheem) (r:45.7.11/55.3.13/47.7.2/66.13.14) (q:draft)
kheemna = (t:n) (w:deceit/deception/trickery/scheme) (d:kheem, deceive, with the noun suffix na: deceit, a trick or scheme used to mislead someone) (e:na leii un ~ khang sak hi/Dawimangpa’ ~ na nan’ zawh nadingun | so that you can stand against the schemes of the devil/ama sungah ~ om lo Israel mi taktak | a true Israelite in whom there is no deceit/~ tawh note hong man hi ta leng | though I caught you by trickery) (s:khemna/khemsiamna/ngian/zuautatna) (b:kheem) (r:19.50.19/49.6.11/43.1.47/47.12.16) (q:draft)
kheemna = (t:n) (w:temptation) (d:being enticed or tested to do wrong; kheemna thuak is to be tempted, as in the Lord's Prayer) (e:~ hong thuaksak kei in/~ tawh na kipelh theih nadingun thu ngen un | pray that you may escape temptation/dawimangpa’ ~ thuak nadingin | to be tempted by the devil/Dawimangpa in ~ a vekpi-in ahih khit ciangin | when the devil had finished all his tempting) (s:zolna/ze-etna) (b:kheem) (r:40.6.13/40.26.41/40.4.1/42.4.13) (q:draft)
kheempa = (t:n) (w:deceiver) (d:kheem, deceive, with pa: the man who deceives) (e:mihonpite a ~ ahi hi) (s:khempa) (b:kheem) (r:43.7.12) (q:draft)
kheemte = (t:n) (w:deceivers/deceitful people) (d:kheem, deceive, with the plural te; mi kheemte are people who deceive) (e:mi ~ leh thutang lote kiang panin) (s:khemte/mikhemte/mikheemte) (b:kheem) (r:19.43.1) (q:draft)
kheengcip = (t:v) (w:be callous/be hardened/be closed up) (d:said of the heart that does not understand) (e:thu theithei loin ~ a) (r:19.119.70) (q:draft, low confidence)
Khefarammoni = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Kephar Ammoni) (d:town in the land of the tribe of Benjamin) (r:6.18.24)
