kheging = (t:n) (w:footsteps/sound of feet/sound of marching) (d:khe, foot, with ging, sound: the sound made by feet or hooves) (e:lam paina ~ na zak ciangin/a topa’ ~ hong kiza hilo ahi hiam | is not the sound of his master’s footsteps heard/kongkhak hong tun a ~ a zak ciangin | when he heard the sound of her feet reaching the door/sakol koplenna ~ | the sound of galloping horses) (r:10.5.24/12.6.32/11.14.6/34.3.2) (q:draft)
khegingte = (t:n) (w:sound of hooves/footsteps/clatter) (d:kheging, the sound made by feet or hooves, with plural te) (e:Sakol ~ za-in, sakol leeng gingte/A leeng ~ bang hangin hici zekai hiam | why is the clatter of his chariots so late) (b:kheging) (r:24.47.3/7.5.28) (q:draft)
kheguak = (t:adj) (w:barefoot) (d:khe foot with guak bare) (e:tangguak leh ~ tawh lam pai hi/~ tawh kum thum sung lam a pai | he walked barefoot for three years) (r:23.20.2/23.20.3) (q:draft)
kheguakin = (t:adv) (w:barefoot) (d:kheguak barefoot with the ending in; paired with tangguak, naked) (e:tangguak ~, tawbo dawksa-in) (b:kheguak) (r:23.20.4) (q:draft)
kheh = (t:v) (w:peel/strip) (d:strip the bark from a stick so that the white wood shows) (e:a kang mun a om dingin ~ a) (r:1.30.37) (q:draft)
khehsa = (t:adj) (w:peeled/stripped) (d:kheh peel with sa, already done) (e:Amah in a ~ ciangkangte) (b:kheh) (r:1.30.38) (q:draft)
khei = (t:v) (w:pick out/extract) (d:dig out a thorn that is stuck in the flesh) (e:ling om a ~) (r:20.26.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
khek = (t:v) (w:change/exchange/substitute) (d:to put one thing in the place of another, as clothes, skin or an animal for offering) (e:a puan a ~ khit ciangin/a vun uh a ~ thei uh hiam | can they change their skin/Na thu paizia ~ nadingin | in order to change the course of things/laih lo, ~ lo ding hi | he shall not exchange or substitute it/nangma nuntakna ~ nadingin mihingte ka pia hi | I give people in exchange for your life) (s:kheek/kheel/khel/laih) (r:1.41.14/24.13.23/10.14.20/3.27.10/23.43.4) (q:draft)
khekhap = (t:n) (w:footstep/footprint/way) (d:footprint; used for the way of life of someone that another person follows) (e:a pa’ ~ khempeuh tawn a/Israel kumpite’ ~ zui hi | he followed the ways of the kings of Israel/Jeroboam’ ~ mah tawnin | walking in the very steps of Jeroboam/ka ~ nangawn na entel hi | you examine even my footprints) (s:sul) (r:12.21.21/18.13.27/14.28.2/11.15.34) (q:draft)
khekhapte = (t:n) (w:footprints/footsteps) (d:khekhap footprint with the plural te) (e:na ~ kimu lo hi) (b:khekhap) (r:19.77.19) (q:draft)
khekhapteng = (t:n) (w:footsteps/ways) (d:khekhap, footstep, with teng, all: the whole way of life of someone that another follows) (e:Na unu’ ~ mah tawn na hih manin) (b:khekhap) (r:26.23.31) (q:draft)
khekhat = (t:n) (w:one foot) (d:khe foot with khat one; found in khekhat khai bangin, as if lifting one foot, said of people who come together as one man) (e:mi khempeuh ~ khai bangin hong kikhawmtuah/~ khai bangin Jerusalem-ah hong kituah diam uh hi | they gathered in Jerusalem as one man) (r:16.8.1/15.3.1) (q:draft, low confidence)
khekna = (t:n) (w:exchange/substitute/substitution) (d:khek, put one thing in the place of another, with the ending -na: the act of exchanging or the thing given instead; khekna-in means in exchange for) (e:na ganhing ~-in an kong pia ding hi/a ganhingte uh ~-in | in exchange for their livestock/tua leh a ~ pen a siangtho hi ding | both it and its substitute shall be holy/tua ganhing le a ~ ganhing | that animal and the animal substituted for it) (s:kheekna) (b:khek) (r:1.47.16/3.27.33/1.47.17/3.27.10) (q:draft)
kheksak = (t:v) (w:change/alter) (d:khek, change, with the causative sak: make something change) (e:A meel ~ gawpin na hawl mang hi) (s:kheelsak/khelsak) (b:khek) (r:18.14.20) (q:draft)
khel = (t:v) (w:change/alter) (d:make different; lungsim khel is change one's mind, relent) (e:Topa in a lungsim ~ a/paikhia thute ka ~ kei ding hi | I will not alter the words that have gone out/na gamtatziate uh ~ un la | change your ways/Bang hangin na lungsim ~ ziauziau na hi hiam | why do you change your mind so lightly/a gamtatna a ~ nading na hilh kei leh | if you do not warn him to change his ways) (s:kheel/khek/kheek) (r:2.32.14/19.89.34/24.26.13/24.2.36/26.33.8) (q:draft)
khel = (t:n) (w:hip/thigh) (d:the hip; khel thagui is the tendon of the hip, khelkom the hip socket) (e:a ~ thagui tung a sukna hang/~ thagui ne lo uh hi | they do not eat the hip tendon) (s:khelpi) (r:1.32.32) (q:draft)
khel = (t:v) (w:gouge out/pluck out) (d:dig or scoop out, as an eye; found with khia, out, written khel khia or as one word khelkhia) (e:note’ taklam mittang khempeuh ~ khia-in | gouging out the right eye of every one of you/Hih mite’ mit ~ khia ding na hi hiam | will you gouge out the eyes of these men/va-ak in a mittang ~ khiatsakin | the ravens will peck out his eye) (s:khelkhia) (r:9.11.2/20.30.17/4.16.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
Khelal = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Kelal) (d:man of the family of Pahath-Moab who had married a foreign wife in the time of Ezra) (r:15.10.30)
khelbai = (t:adj) (w:lame/crippled) (d:khel hip with bai lame: lame in the hip or leg) (e:poina a nei, mittaw, ~) (s:bai/khebai/khezaw) (r:3.21.18) (q:draft)
khelbaite = (t:n) (w:the lame/lame people) (d:khelbai, lame, with the plural te) (e:Mittawte leh ~ zong hong kihel ding) (s:khebaite/khe-baite/khezawte) (b:khelbai) (r:24.31.8) (q:draft)
khelbawl = (t:v) (w:mock/mistreat/abuse/trouble) (d:treat someone wrongly or with mockery, abuse; also trouble or unsettle someone) (e:Zeisu a ~ khit uh ciangin/Note hong ~ mi in kuakua ahih hangin | whoever it is that is troubling you/I mipihte na khemgawpin na ~ a | he deceived and mistreated our people/kei hong ~ kha ding hi | they may come and abuse me) (s:zahko/bawlsia) (a:pahtawi) (r:41.15.20/44.7.19/48.5.10/13.10.4) (q:draft)
khelguh = (t:n) (w:hip bone/hip) (d:khel hip with guh bone) (e:amah tawh a kilaina-in Jakob’ ~) (r:1.32.25) (q:draft)
khelin = (t:v) (w:changing/relenting) (d:khel, change, with in; lungsim khelin is changing the mind, relenting) (e:na lungsim ~ na) (s:kheelin) (b:khel) (r:2.32.12) (q:draft)
khelkhia = (t:v) (w:gouge out/pluck out/put out) (d:take out an eye by force) (e:a mitte ~ uh a/~ inla paai in | gouge it out and throw it away/Na mittang in hong puksak leh, na ~ in | if your eye causes you to stumble, pluck it out/Zedekiah’ mitte ~ uh a | they put out the eyes of Zedekiah) (r:7.16.21/40.5.29/41.9.47/12.25.7) (q:draft)
khelkhiat = (t:v) (w:gouge out/pluck out/put out) (d:form of khelkhia used before sak and other following words: take out an eye by force) (e:Zedekiah’ mittang a ~ sak khit ciangin/va-ak in a mittang ~ sakin | the ravens will peck out his eye) (b:khelkhia) (r:24.39.7/20.30.17) (q:draft)
khelkhiatsak = (t:v) (w:gouge out/put out) (d:khelkhiat gouge out with sak: put out the eyes of someone) (e:Zedekiah’ mittangte a ~ khit ciangin) (s:khelsak) (b:khelkhiat) (r:24.39.7/24.52.11) (q:draft)
khelkhin = (t:v) (w:have changed) (d:khel, change, with khin, already or completely) (e:ka thaman sawmvei ~ a) (b:khel) (r:1.31.7) (q:draft)
khelkik = (t:v) (w:change back/reverse/relent) (d:khel, change, with kik, back: change what was said or decided, change one's mind) (e:keimah in ka ~ thei kei hi/ka ngaihsut sa ka ~ ding hi | I will relent from what I had planned/ka lungsim zong ka ~ kei ding hi | I will not change my mind either/a gensa pen a ~ ding hi | he will take back what he has pronounced) (s:kheelkik) (b:khel) (r:4.23.20/24.26.13/24.26.3/24.4.28) (q:draft)
khelkikin = (t:v) (w:changing back/reversing) (d:khelkik, change back, with in; lungsim khelkikin is changing the mind again) (e:a lungsim uh ~ a khahkhiatsa uh) (b:khelkik) (r:24.34.11) (q:draft)
khelkikzaw = (t:v) (w:relent instead/change back rather) (d:khelkik, change what was said, with zaw, rather) (e:tunsak dingin a gensa ~ hi lo ahi hiam) (b:khelkik) (r:24.26.19) (q:draft)
khelkom = (t:n) (w:hip socket/hip joint/hollow of the thigh) (d:the socket of the hip, where the thigh bone joins the body; khel is hip) (e:amah in a ~ sung suksak hi/~ tunga a om khel thagui | the tendon that is on the hip socket) (r:1.32.25/1.32.32) (q:draft)
khelmang = (t:v) (w:change/do away with) (d:khel, change, with mang, away: change something so that the old is gone) (e:ngeina khempeuh ~ ding hi) (r:44.6.14) (q:draft)
khelpi = (t:n) (w:hip/thigh) (d:khel hip with pi, big: the hip or upper thigh) (e:A ~’ hangin amah bai) (s:khel) (b:khel) (r:1.32.31) (q:draft)
khelpilna = (t:n) (w:wiles/trickery/cunning) (d:cunning used to mislead others; in Numbers 25:18 the tricks by which the Midianites deceived Israel) (e:amaute in a ~ uh tawh note) (s:khemsiamna/ngian) (r:4.25.18) (q:draft, low confidence)
khelsak = (t:v) (w:change/alter) (d:khel change with sak: change something for someone, as a name) (e:ama min Jehoiakim-in ~ hi) (s:kheelsak/kheksak) (b:khel) (r:14.36.4) (q:draft)
khelsak = (t:v) (w:gouge out/put out) (d:khel gouge out with sak: put out the eyes of someone) (e:Zedekiah’ mittang a ~ khit ciangin) (s:khelkhiatsak) (b:khel) (r:24.52.11) (q:draft)
kheltat = (t:adj) (w:insolent/lawless) (d:said of a person in a list of wrongdoers; the exact sense is not clear from the verse) (e:Pasian mudah mi, ~ mi, kisathei mi) (r:45.1.30) (q:draft, low confidence)
kheltatna = (t:n) (w:wickedness/lawlessness/iniquity) (d:kheltat with the noun suffix na) (e:kihhuaina leh ~’ sila-ah | as slaves to impurity and lawlessness) (s:gitlohna) (a:dikna) (b:kheltat) (r:45.6.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
Khelub = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Kelub) (d:name of two men: a man of Judah, brother of Shuhah and father of Mehir, and the father of Ezri, an officer of David) (e:Shuhah’ sanggampa ~ in Mehir’ pa hi a) (r:13.4.11/13.27.26) (q:draft)
Khelubai = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Caleb) (d:son of Hezron of the tribe of Judah, elsewhere called Caleb) (r:13.2.9)
Kheluhi = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Keluhi) (d:descendant of Bani who had married a foreign wife in the time of Ezra) (r:15.10.35)
khem = (t:v) (w:deceive/trick/mislead) (d:make someone believe what is not true; hong khem is deceive me or us, and khem zo is succeed in deceiving) (e:Gulpi in kei hong ~ a/Jakob in Aram mi Laban ~ a | Jacob deceived Laban the Aramean/Bang hangin kei hong ~ na hi hiam | why have you deceived me/mi tampi a ~ ding uh hi | they will deceive many) (s:kheem/zuau/lehhek/khembawl) (r:1.3.13/1.31.20/9.28.12/40.24.11)
khem = (t:v) (w:cheat/defraud) (d:deceive someone in order to take what is his, as a trader does with false scales) (e:Nangmah in kote nong ~ kei a | you have not cheated us/kua ~ ka hi hiam | whom have I cheated/a hong leite i ~ nuam hi | we want to cheat those who buy from us/mi ~ ding nuam a sa uh hi | they love to defraud people) (r:9.12.4/9.12.3/30.8.5/28.12.7)
khem = (t:v) (w:lie) (d:say what is not true; after another verb, do the action falsely, as phat khem, praise insincerely, and tai khem, pretend to flee) (e:Kha Siangtho ~ na hi hiam | have you lied to the Holy Spirit/a kam uh tawh amah phat ~ uh a | with their mouths they flattered him falsely/ci ~ uh hi | they say so falsely/a kampi uh tawh phat ~ uh a | with their mouths they bless falsely) (s:zuau) (r:44.5.3/19.78.36/26.13.6/19.62.4)
khembawl = (t:v) (w:deceive/trick/use deception) (d:khem, deceive, with bawl, do or treat: deal deceitfully with someone, play a trick on them) (e:amaute in ~ ding vaihawm uh a/Ka thuhilhna uhah mite ~ loin | in our teaching we do not deceive people) (s:khem/lehhek) (b:khem) (r:6.9.4/47.4.2) (q:draft)
kheme = (t:n) (w:toe) (d:a toe of the foot, as khutme is a finger of the hand) (e:a khe lang tuakah ~ guk/khe lang tuakah zong ~ guk mah a nei | he also had six toes on each foot) (r:10.21.20/13.20.6) (q:draft)
khemete = (t:n) (w:toes) (d:kheme, toe, with the plural te) (e:A khepek leh a ~ khen khat sik/A ~ khenkhat sik hi a | the toes were partly iron) (b:kheme) (r:27.2.41/27.2.42) (q:draft)
khemgawpin = (t:v) (w:deceiving utterly/dealing treacherously) (d:khem, deceive, with gawp, thoroughly, and the linking suffix in: deceiving someone badly, and then doing the next thing) (e:I mipihte na ~ na khelbawl a) (s:lehheekin) (r:44.7.19) (q:draft)
khemhat = (t:v) (w:be deceitful/be given to deceiving) (d:khem, deceive, with hat, be given to: be in the habit of deceiving others) (e:sanggamte khempeuh ~ ciat uh a) (r:24.9.4) (q:draft)
khemin = (t:v) (w:deceiving/cheating) (d:khem, deceive, with the linking suffix in: deceiving or having deceived someone, followed by another verb; kei hong khemin is deceiving me) (e:na pa un kei hong ~/kei hong ~ tua thukham tawh a hong that hi | it deceived me and through the commandment killed me/a vengpa ~, ahih kei leh a na sutin | deceiving his neighbour or robbing him/Mi khatpeuh ~ a na ka laksak leh | if I have cheated anyone and taken his things) (s:kheemin) (b:khem) (r:1.31.7/1.31.26/45.7.11/3.6.2/42.19.8) (q:draft)
khemkhem = (t:v) (w:keep deceiving/betray) (d:khem, deceive, said twice: go on deceiving again and again) (e:mi khemte in ~ lai-in sia semsem uh a) (r:23.24.16) (q:draft)
khemkhemin = (t:v) (w:deceiving) (d:khemkhem, go on deceiving, with the linking suffix in: deceiving others all the while) (e:amaute in mi ~, amaute mah in) (b:khemkhem) (r:55.3.13) (q:draft)
khemna = (t:n) (w:deceit/deception/trickery) (d:khem, deceive, with the noun suffix na: deceit, a trick, the act of deceiving; khemna tawh is by deceit) (e:Zeisu in amaute ~ a theih ciangin/a lungsim-ah ~ a om lo mi | one in whose heart there is no deceit/Na sanggampa in ~ tawh hong pai-in | your brother came with deceit/Ama kammalte in siatna leh ~ vive hi | his words are nothing but evil and deceit) (s:kheemna/khemsiamna) (a:thutak/cihtakna) (b:khem) (r:42.20.23/1.27.35/19.32.2/19.36.3) (q:draft)
khemnateng = (t:n) (w:deceits/lies) (d:khemna, deceit, with teng, all: all their deceits) (e:a ~ uh tawh a uliante uh) (s:zuaupiteng) (b:khemna) (r:28.7.3) (q:draft)
khemnop = (t:v) (w:want to deceive) (d:khem, deceive, with nop, want to: want to deceive someone) (e:nang hong ~ manin a mitheek hong pia-in) (r:20.6.13) (q:draft)
khemnop = (t:adj) (w:easily deceived/gullible) (d:khem deceive with nop in the sense easy: easy to deceive; said of a silly dove) (e:a ~ kawl vakhu hai tawh kibang hi) (r:28.7.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
khemnopna = (t:n) (w:deceitfulness/intent to deceive) (d:khemnop want to deceive with the noun suffix na; khemnopna lungsim is a mind bent on deceiving) (e:ngimna hoih lo le ~ lungsim tawh/mi ~ lungsim a neite a mudah hi | he detests those who have a mind to deceive) (b:khemnop) (r:52.2.3/19.5.6) (q:draft)
Khemosh = (t:name) (w:Chemosh) (d:god of the Moabites, for whom Solomon built a place of worship near Jerusalem) (r:7.11.24/4.21.29)
Khemoshpasian = (t:name) (w:Chemosh) (d:Chemosh, the god of the Moabites, written together with pasian, god) (r:24.48.13)
khempa = (t:n) (w:deceiver/cheat) (d:khem, deceive, with pa, a man: a man who deceives, as in mi khempa) (e:tua mi ~ in/mi ~ in samsiatna thuak ta hen | let the cheat be cursed/Kuamah in hong khem nai loh mi ~ aw | you deceiver whom no one has yet deceived) (s:kheempa) (b:khem) (r:40.27.63/39.1.14/23.33.1) (q:draft)
khempeh = (t:det) (w:all) (d:apparently a misprint or short form of khempeuh, all) (e:tuate ~ a minin a kilo khia) (r:15.10.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
khempeuh = (t:pron) (w:every/all/everyone/everything) (d:all, every: placed after a noun, as mi khempeuh, all people or everyone, and thu khempeuh, everything) (e:kha a nei vasate ~ amau nam ciatin/Mi ~ in a ne uh a | they all ate/Pasian in hih thute ~ gen a | God spoke all these words/Thu ~ kong genkhol zo hi | I have told you everything beforehand) (r:1.1.21/41.6.42/2.20.1/41.13.23)
khempeuh = (t:adv) (w:entirely) (d:wholly, all of it without exception) (s:vek-in)
khempeuha = (t:det) (w:every/all/throughout) (d:khempeuh with the ending a, in or of: mun khempeuha is in every place, everywhere) (e:Mun ~ om Jew mite lakah/ama gam sung ~ mitphial siamte | the magicians in his whole kingdom/mun ~ ama galte khempeuh | all his enemies on every side/Mun ~ numeite in amah gentehna khatin nei uh a | women everywhere made her a byword) (b:khempeuh) (r:44.24.5/9.14.47/27.1.20/26.23.10) (q:draft)
khempeuhah = (t:adv) (w:entirely/throughout/everywhere) (d:khempeuh, all, with the place marker ah: in all of, throughout; mun khempeuhah is everywhere) (e:Izipt gamsung ~ kum sagih sung/gam ~ ama min a thang hi | his fame spread throughout the land/leitung ~ na min bangzahin lian | how great is your name in all the earth/amau omna kiim ~ tuate kiasak hi | he made them fall all around their dwellings) (b:khempeuh) (r:1.41.29/6.6.27/19.8.9/19.78.28)
khempeuhah = (t:pron) (w:every/in all) (d:khempeuh, all, with the marker ah: in every, in all; na khempeuhah is in everything) (e:Topa in na ~ Abraham thupha pia hi | the Lord blessed Abraham in everything/sepna ~ Pasian in nang hong ompih hi | God is with you in all you do) (b:khempeuh) (r:1.24.1/1.21.22)
Khempeuhah = (t:adv) (w:everywhere/on every side) (d:khempeuh all with the place marker ah, written with a capital in the name Mun Khempeuhah Launa, Terror on Every Side) (e:Mun ~ Launa | Terror on Every Side) (b:khempeuhah) (r:24.20.3) (q:draft)
khempeuhin = (t:pron) (w:all/the whole) (d:khempeuh all with the ending in, which marks the group as the doer or the span as the setting: all of them, throughout all) (e:Israel mihon ~ hih ding uh hi/Judah kumpite’ hun sung ~ | throughout all the days of the kings of Judah) (b:khempeuh) (r:2.12.47/12.23.22) (q:draft)
khempeuhleh = (t:phrase) (w:all and) (d:khempeuh, all, written together with leh, and) (e:gam ~ Hazazontamar gam-a a teng) (r:1.14.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
khempeuhte = (t:pron) (w:every/all/everyone) (d:khempeuh, all, with the plural te: all of them, everyone) (e:Mi ~ in kisim dingin amau khua/Ama thu a za ~ in | everyone who heard him/Mipawl ~ mai-ah na bawl gupna | the salvation you prepared before all peoples/sabuai leh a nazat ~ | the table and all its utensils) (b:khempeuh) (r:42.2.3/42.2.47/42.2.31/2.39.36)
khemsa = (t:see) <khemsa-in>
khemsa-in = (t:v) (w:being deceived/deceived) (d:khem, deceive, with sa, already done, and the connective in; after a possessor and before om kei un it means do not be deceived by) (e:Hezekiah’ ~ om kei un/Sanggamte aw, mite’ ~ om kei un | brothers, do not be deceived by people/Sumgolh’ ~ ta kei in la | do not be deceived by a bribe/mi’ ~ ta kei un | do not be deceived by anyone) (r:12.18.29/18.36.18/59.1.16/42.21.8) (q:draft)
khemsiamna = (t:n) (w:craftiness/cunning/deceit) (d:khem deceive with siam skilled and the noun suffix na: skill in deceiving) (e:ama nasemte, ~ tawh a bawl dingin/amau’ ~ in a mawkna ahi hi | their cunning comes to nothing) (s:khemna/ngian) (r:19.105.25/19.119.118) (q:draft)
khemte = (t:n) (w:deceivers/those who deceive/the treacherous) (d:khem, deceive, with the plural ending -te; mi khemte are people who deceive others) (e:mi ~ leh khemna a thuakte/Mi ~ le thutang lote kiang panin | from deceitful and unjust people/Tua bang mite pen mi ~ hi a | such people are deceivers/mi thatte le mi ~ pen | murderers and deceivers) (s:kheemte/mikhemte) (b:khem) (r:18.12.16/23.24.16/19.43.1/63.1.7/19.55.23) (q:draft)
khemtheih = (t:v) (w:be able to deceive/can deceive) (d:khem, deceive, with theih, the form of thei, can, used before another word: a khemtheih nawn loh nadingin is so that he can deceive no more) (e:minam tuamtuamte a ~ nawn loh nadingin) (b:khem) (r:66.20.3) (q:draft)
khemul = (t:n) (w:hair of the legs/leg hair) (d:khe foot or leg with mul body hair; renders the Hebrew hair of the feet, where the NIV has private parts) (e:a sam leh a ~ mettol ding a) (r:23.7.20) (q:draft)
khemzawh = (t:v) (w:deceive/beguile/take in) (d:khem, deceive, with zawh, form of zo, manage: succeed in deceiving, take in) (e:zuau ngian tawh Eve a ~ bangin/a ~ mite in phawkkha lo uh hi | the people she has taken in do not realise it) (s:khemzo) (r:47.11.3/20.9.18) (q:draft)
khemzo = (t:v) (w:deceive/succeed in deceiving/outwit) (d:khem, deceive, with zo, be able, succeed) (e:mi tampi a ~ ding uh hi/mihoih pawlkhat a ~ uh hi | they deceive some good people/Galte in amah ~ ngei lo ding a | enemies will never outwit him/Na pawl teng in nang hong ~ uh a | all your allies have deceived you) (s:khemzawh/khem) (b:khem) (r:41.13.6/31.1.3/45.16.18/19.89.22/31.1.7) (q:draft)
khen = (t:v) (w:divide/separate) (d:divide into parts or groups, or separate one thing from another) (e:kalaohte pawl nih-in ~ hi/van kuumpi nuai-a om tuite ~ hi | he separated the waters under the vault/Sun leh zan a ~ dingin | to separate day and night/numei-nasem nihte lakah naupangte ~ hi | he divided the children among the two female servants) (s:khenkhia/hawm) (a:gawm/kaikhawm) (r:1.32.7/1.1.7/1.1.14/1.33.1)
khen = (t:v) (w:hammering/hammer/nail) (d:drive in with a hammer; khen kip is nail something firmly in place) (e:tua milim siktukkilh tawh ~ kip uh hi | they nailed the idol down firmly with nails) (s:kilh) (r:23.41.7)
Khen-anah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Kenaanah) (d:father of Zedekiah, the false prophet in the time of King Ahab) (e:~’ tapa Zedekiah a nai-ah hong pai-in) (r:14.18.23) (q:draft)
Khena = (t:see) <Khena-anah>
Khena-anah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Kenaanah) (d:name of two men: the father of the false prophet Zedekiah, and a son of Bilhan in the tribe of Benjamin) (e:Tua ciangin ~’ tapa Zedekiah) (r:11.22.24/13.7.10) (q:draft)
Khenaanah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Kenaanah) (d:name of two men: the father of the false prophet Zedekiah, and a son of Bilhan in the tribe of Benjamin) (r:13.7.10/14.18.10)
Khenani = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Kenani) (d:a Levite who led the people in prayer in the time of Nehemiah) (e:Sherebiah, Bani, leh ~ ding uh a) (r:16.9.4) (q:draft)
Khenaniah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Kenaniah) (d:chief of the Levites who led the singing when David brought up the ark; also an Izharite appointed with his sons as official and judge over Israel) (r:13.15.22/13.26.29)
khencip = (t:v) (w:nail fast/crucify) (d:khen, hammer, with cip, firmly: nail fast, as on a cross) (e:singlamteh tungah a ~ zo uh hi) (s:kilhcip) (b:khen) (r:48.5.24) (q:draft)
Khene = (t:name) (w:Khene) (d:first part of the name Khene-anah, Kenaanah, the father of the false prophet Zedekiah)
Khene-anah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Kenaanah) (d:father of Zedekiah, the false prophet in the time of King Ahab) (e:~’ tapa Zedekiah in ama adingin) (r:11.22.11) (q:draft)
kheng = (t:v) (w:pass by/go past/go beyond) (d:go past a person, a place or a boundary) (e:suang milimte ~ a/na nasempa hong ~ kei in | do not pass your servant by/a taina bukna khuapi gamgi ~ in a pai a | he goes beyond the boundary of the city of refuge/vantung ~ a, pai Siampi Ukpa lian | the great high priest who has passed through the heavens) (s:khengsuak/nawkkha) (r:7.3.26/1.18.3/4.35.26/58.4.14) (q:draft)
khengak = (t:n) (w:footstool/footrest) (d:khe foot with ngak: a place to rest the feet; khengak nading, for a footstool) (e:i Pasian’ ~ nadingin tawlngakna) (s:khengakna) (r:13.28.2) (q:draft)
khengakna = (t:n) (w:footstool) (d:khe, foot, with ngakna, rest: the place where the feet rest) (e:kham a kibawl ~ khat nei-in/ama ~ munah bia un | worship at his footstool/leitung pen keima ~ ahi hi | the earth is my footstool/Pasian’ ~ mah hi veve hi | it is the footstool of God) (s:khengak/sikna) (b:khengak) (r:14.9.18/19.99.5/23.66.1/40.5.35) (q:draft)
khengin = (t:v) (w:going beyond/passing/beyond) (d:kheng, pass, with the linking suffix in: going past a place or over a limit, and then doing the next thing; often translated beyond) (e:Damaskas ~ gam khatah/Jordan ~ ka pai thei kei ding hi | I cannot go across the Jordan/David’ inn ~ nisuahna lam manawhin | passing the house of David toward the east/mun khatna leh mun nihna ~ | passing the first and the second post) (b:kheng) (r:30.5.27/42.3.13/5.4.22/16.12.37/44.12.10) (q:draft)
khengkhin = (t:v) (w:have passed/be already past) (d:kheng, pass, with khin, already) (e:Ni hun nangawn ~ ahih manin) (s:khengta) (b:kheng) (r:44.27.9) (q:draft)
khenglah = (t:v) (w:be captivated by/be taken in by) (d:used with kei in, do not; the exact sense is not clear from the verse) (e:hong zawlmitna ~ kei in) (r:20.6.25) (q:draft, low confidence)
khenglahkha = (t:v) (w:be captivated by/be taken in by) (d:khenglah with kha, happen to; used with kei in, do not; the exact sense is not clear from the verse) (e:hong zawlmitna ~ kei in) (r:20.6.25) (q:draft, low confidence)
khengsuak = (t:v) (w:pass by/go past) (d:kheng, pass, with suak, come out: go on past someone or something) (e:Amaute a ~ ding bangin pai a) (s:kheng) (r:41.6.48) (q:draft)
khengsuakin = (t:v) (w:passing over/passing by) (d:khengsuak, pass by, with in) (e:amah in ~, suakta sak ding hi) (b:khengsuak) (r:23.31.5) (q:draft)
khengta = (t:v) (w:have passed/have come to pass) (d:kheng, pass, with ta, now or already) (e:nate in hong ~ a) (s:khengkhin) (b:kheng) (r:23.42.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
khengto = (t:see) <khengto-in>
khengto-in = (t:v) (w:passing up beyond/going above) (d:kheng, pass, with to, upward, and in) (e:a sangpen dawn nangawn ~ na paito hi) (r:49.4.10) (q:draft)
khengval = (t:v) (w:go too far/overstep/be presumptuous) (d:go beyond what is right or allowed; khengval lua, go much too far) (e:Levi’ tapate aw, ~ lua uh teh/man’ lohna tawh a ~ a, gamta mipa | the man who acts presumptuously and does not obey) (r:4.16.7/5.17.12) (q:draft)
Khengval = (t:name) (w:Khengval) (d:the verb khengval, go too far, written with a capital at the start of a sentence: Khengval lua uh teh, you have gone too far)
khengvala = (t:adv) (w:presumptuously/going too far) (d:khengval, overstep, with a, joining it to the next verb) (e:man lohna tawh a ~ a gamta mi) (s:khengvalin) (b:khengval) (r:5.17.12) (q:draft)
khengvalin = (t:adv) (w:presumptuously/excessively/beyond the limit) (d:khengval go beyond with in; doing more than is right or allowed) (e:a ~ gamta ngam nawn lo ding/A ~ gamta kei un | do not go beyond the limit/a ~ a pai mite | those who run ahead/a ~ kizepna a tuamtuamte zang loin | not using all kinds of excessive adornment) (s:khengvala) (b:khengval) (r:5.17.13/54.2.9/46.4.6/63.1.9) (q:draft)
khengvallua = (t:v) (w:go much too far/overstep greatly) (d:khengval, go too far, with lua, too much) (e:Levi’ tapate aw, ~ uh teh) (b:khengval) (r:4.16.7) (q:draft)
khenin = (t:v) (w:dividing/separating) (d:khen, divide, with the linking suffix in: dividing or separating, and then doing the next action) (e:pawl thumin ~, amaute khempeuh’ tungah/Amaute in seh sagihin ~ | they are to divide it into seven parts/amah leh a nasemte ~ amaute zo a | he and his servants divided up and defeated them/amau’ nitna panin ~ na kem ding uh | you shall keep them separate from their uncleanness) (b:khen) (r:7.7.16/6.18.5/1.14.15/3.15.31) (q:draft)
khenin = (t:v) (w:judging/deciding) (d:khen, judge, with the linking suffix in; thu khenin is judging a matter, giving a verdict) (e:thu a tangin ~, khat leh khat tungah/na gamtatnasate uh hangin thu hong ~ | judging you for your conduct) (s:thukhenin) (b:khen) (r:38.7.9/26.7.8) (q:draft)
khenin = (t:adv) (w:in divisions/group by group) (d:in the doubled form a khen khenin, divided into groups, division by division) (e:Note a khen ~ na beh uh tawh) (b:khen) (r:14.35.4/14.26.11) (q:draft)
khenkhak = (t:v) (w:judge/condemn) (d:thu khen, judge, with khak, happen to; thu khenkhak loh nading is so as not to come under judgment) (e:thu hong ~ loh nadingin khatlekhat) (r:59.5.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
khenkham = (t:v) (w:divide/split/part) (d:split in two so that there is a way through; said of the sea) (e:tuipi tungah na khut zan-in ~ in/vangliatna tawh tuipi na ~ a | by your power you split the sea) (s:phelkham/khenkhia) (r:2.14.16/19.74.13) (q:draft)
khenkhamin = (t:v) (w:dividing/splitting apart/breaking down) (d:khenkham, split apart or break in pieces, with the linking suffix in) (e:ama mite’ mai-ah tuite ~) (b:khenkham) (r:23.63.12/24.18.7) (q:draft)
khenkhat = (t:det) (w:some/part of/partly) (d:a part of a whole; repeated, partly one thing and partly another) (e:~ sik leh ~ tungman kigawm ahi hi/a neihsa leitang ~ a zuak leh | if he sells part of his land/Judah minam’ gamsung ~ hong suak hi | it became part of the territory of Judah/~ Joab’ ukna nuai-ah | one part under the command of Joab) (s:kimkhat/pawkhat) (r:27.2.33/3.25.25/6.19.9/10.18.2) (q:draft)
khenkhawm = (t:v) (w:judge together/decide together) (d:khen, in thu khen, judge, with khawm, together) (e:le keimah in a ~ ka hih manun) (b:khen) (r:43.8.16) (q:draft)
khenkhenin = (t:adv) (w:by divisions/group by group) (d:khen, divide, said twice, with in: each in its own division) (e:Note a ~ na beh uh tawh) (s:pawlpawlin/honhonin) (r:14.35.4) (q:draft)
khenkhente = (t:n) (w:divisions/groups) (d:khen, divide, said twice, with the plural te: the several divisions of a body of people) (e:Levi mi a ~ om hi) (s:khente/khennate) (r:13.28.21) (q:draft)
khenkhia = (t:v) (w:separate/split/set apart) (d:take one thing away from another so that they are apart; set people or things apart for a purpose) (e:Levi mite na ~ ding a/Pasian in khuamial panin khuavak ~ hi | God separated the light from the darkness/Jakob in tuunote ~ a | Jacob set the lambs apart/mite kiang panin note a hong ~ Topa | the Lord who set you apart from the peoples) (s:tuamkoih/tengkhia) (a:gawm/koihkhawm) (b:khen) (r:1.1.4/4.8.14/1.30.40/3.20.24)
khenkhia = (t:v) (w:divide/part) (d:split something so that it opens, as God parted the sea) (e:Amah in tuipi ~-in amaute kantansak a) (s:khenkham/phelkham) (b:khen) (r:19.78.13)
khenkhia = (t:v) (w:break up) (b:khen)
khenkhiasak = (t:v) (w:separate out/remove/set apart) (d:khenkhia, separate, with sak, cause or let: have something separated out) (e:le a puang khempeuh hong ~ in) (b:khenkhia) (r:1.30.32) (q:draft)
khenkhiat = (t:v) (w:set apart/separate/divide off) (d:form of khenkhia used before another word or before the command ending un) (e:ka sapsa bangin hong ~ un/a tuam ~ uh ngun leh kham | the silver and gold they had set apart/Israel gam pawlkhat ~ ding kipan hi | he began to cut off parts of Israel) (s:tuamkoih) (b:khenkhia) (r:44.13.2/4.31.42/15.8.25/12.10.32) (q:draft)
khenkhiatna = (t:n) (w:separation/setting apart) (d:khenkhiat set apart with the noun suffix na: the act of setting apart) (e:kiang panin hong ~) (b:khenkhiat) (r:4.16.9) (q:draft)
khenkhit = (t:v) (w:have decided/have judged) (d:khen divide or decide, with khit finish; thu a khenkhit uh ciangin, when they had decided the matter or passed sentence) (e:thu a ~ uh ciangin/a si dingin thu a ~ uh ciangin | when they have condemned him to die) (s:khentatzo) (r:44.27.1/40.20.18) (q:draft)
khenkhit = (t:v) (w:have passed/pass through/get past) (d:leave a place behind after going past or through it: said of passing guard posts and of travelling through a region) (e:a nihna a ~ uh ciangin/Pisidia gam a ~ uh ciangin | after they had passed through Pisidia) (s:khengkhin) (r:44.12.10/44.14.24) (q:draft, low confidence)
khenkip = (t:v) (w:nail down/drive in firmly/fasten) (d:khen hammer with kip firm: fix in place with nails, or drive in as a peg) (e:tua milim siktukkilh tawh a ~ uh hi/vankhaina bangin ka ~ ding a | I will drive him in like a peg/na khetphimte ~ in | make your tent pegs firm) (s:kilh) (r:23.41.7/23.22.23/23.54.2) (q:draft)
khenna = (t:n) (w:judgment/decision/verdict) (d:the deciding of a matter, often as thu khenna) (e:thu a manin a ~ ka thei hi/thu na hong ~-ah pauna ding bangmah om lo hi | there is nothing to blame in your judging/kei le ka leenggui lo kikalah thu nong ~ | that you judge between me and my vineyard) (s:thukhenna) (b:khen) (r:19.140.12/20.16.2/19.51.4/23.5.3) (q:draft)
khenna = (t:n) (w:division/separation) (d:khen, divide, with the noun suffix na: a part or group into which people are divided, or a dividing into groups) (e:kongcingte a kiseh ~ ahi hi) (s:kikhenna) (b:khen) (r:13.26.19) (q:draft)
khennate = (t:n) (w:judgments/decisions) (d:plural of khenna in the sense of thu khenna, deciding a case) (e:thupiakna leh thuman ~ a sem hi/thu a tangin ka ~ ka sep khiat theih nadingin | so that I may carry out my just judgments) (s:thukhennate) (b:khenna) (r:5.33.21/26.39.21) (q:draft)
khennate = (t:n) (w:divisions/groups) (d:plural of khenna, a part into which people are divided) (e:Kongcingte a kiseh ~ in) (s:khente/kikhennate) (b:khenna) (r:13.26.1) (q:draft)
khennih = (t:n) (w:two parts/two halves) (d:khen, divide, with nih, two; khennih suah is make into two parts) (e:gal sunga a kimante ~ suahin) (s:phelnih) (r:4.31.27) (q:draft)
khennihte = (t:n) (w:two divisions/two companies) (d:khennih, two parts, with the plural te) (e:biakinn a cing no a ~ in) (b:khennih) (r:12.11.7) (q:draft)
khenpa = (t:n) (w:judge/one who decides) (d:in thu khenpa, the one who decides a matter; pa marks a male person) (e:thu a ~ in Pasian ahi hi/Pasian in a tang-a thu ~ hi a | God is one who judges justly/Mawhsakna thu a ~ in kua ahi hiam | who is the one who condemns/eite thu hong ~ mai-ah | before him who judges us) (s:thukhenpa) (b:khen) (r:19.75.7/19.7.11/45.8.34/58.4.13) (q:draft)
khensak = (t:v) (w:judge/decide/settle) (d:with thu: decide a matter for someone, give judgement) (e:mizawngte’ thu a manin ~ leh/mite’ thu a manin ~ hi | he judges people fairly/a ~ dingin ama kiangah Israel mite pai uh hi | the Israelites went to her to have their cases decided/Mite’ thu amaute ~ tawntung in | let them always judge the cases of the people) (s:thukhen) (b:khen) (r:20.29.14/7.4.5/26.18.8/2.18.22) (q:draft)
khensakin = (t:v) (w:judge/decide) (d:khensak, decide a matter for someone, with the linking ending in: giving judgement, and then going on to the next action) (e:thukhente in amau’ thu ~, a dikpa khahin) (b:khensak) (r:5.25.1) (q:draft)
khensakzaw = (t:v) (w:judge rather/judge instead) (d:khensak, decide a matter for someone, with zaw, rather: be the one who judges instead of another) (e:Pasian’ mi siangthote ~ loin) (b:khensak) (r:46.6.1/46.6.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
khensat = (t:v) (w:decide/determine/resolve) (d:make up the mind firmly about what to do; lungsim khensat is resolve) (e:a pai nading thu ka ~ hi/ka gensa, ka ~ sa hi-a | I have spoken, I have decided/siat nadingin ka lungsim ka ~ khin zo hi | I have resolved to do it harm/kumpipa in na ~ peuhpeuh a sem dingin | to do whatever the king decides) (s:khentat) (r:44.25.25/24.4.28/24.21.10/10.15.15)
khensatin = (t:v) (w:deciding/having decided) (d:khensat, decide, with in; thu khensatin is having made a decision) (e:ci-in thu ~ lai ka khak khinzo) (b:khensat) (r:44.21.25) (q:draft)
khensatna = (t:n) (w:decision) (d:khensat, decide, with the noun suffix na: what has been decided) (s:thukhensatna/khenna)
khensatsa = (t:adj) (w:decided/determined) (d:khensat decide with sa, already done: what has been decided beforehand) (e:ka gensa, ka ~ hi a/na vangliatna tawh na ~ thu khempeuh | everything you had decided by your power) (b:khensat) (r:24.4.28/44.4.28) (q:draft)
khensuk = (t:v) (w:drive down/hammer down) (d:khen hammer with suk, downward: drive a peg down into something) (e:a paang-ah ~ hi) (b:khen) (r:7.4.21) (q:draft)
khenta = (t:v) (w:judge/decide) (d:khen, in thu khen, judge, with ta, now, in a command) (e:nong muhna bangbangin thu ~ in) (b:khen) (r:27.1.13) (q:draft)
khentat = (t:v) (w:determine/resolve) (d:settle firmly in the mind what will be done) (e:Mi khempeuh beisak ding ka ~ zo hi/amaute daan piak ding ka ~ khin a | I have determined to punish them/zon’ ding a lungsim uhah a ~ khin mite | those who had set their hearts on seeking him) (s:khensat) (r:1.6.13/23.65.6/14.11.16)
khentat = (t:v) (w:decide/make up the mind) (e:a zakna tawh thu ~ lo ding hi/Ka lungsim ka ~ zo hi | I have made up my mind/thu ~ thei nai loin | not yet able to decide matters/nangma lungsim ~ ding ahi hi | it is for you to decide) (s:khensat) (r:23.11.3/10.19.29/14.13.7/18.34.33)
khentatin = (t:v) (w:deciding firmly/resolving) (d:khentat, decide, with in) (e:a lungsimah khauhtakin ~, a lungsim) (b:khentat) (r:46.7.37) (q:draft)
khentatna = (t:n) (w:determination/resolve/decision) (d:khentat, decide, with the noun suffix na: a firm decision; lungsim khentatna is what the mind has resolved) (e:zuih ding a lungsim a ~ a muh ciangin/Ka lungsim ~ in hih bang ahi hi | this is what I have resolved/hong suksiat ding a lungsim a ~ ka thei hi | I know that he has determined to destroy you/A kumpipa in lungsim ~ nei thei a | its king is able to make up his mind) (s:khensatna) (b:khentat) (r:8.1.18/15.7.13/14.25.16/21.10.17)
khentatzo = (t:v) (w:have decided/have made up one's mind) (d:khentat, decide, with zo, which marks the act as completed; lungsim khentatzo is to have made up the mind) (e:Ka lungsim ka ~ hi) (b:khentat) (r:10.19.29) (q:draft)
khentawm = (t:v) (w:settle oneself/decide for oneself/judge for oneself) (d:khen judge with tawm, by oneself: settle a matter or pronounce a judgement oneself) (e:nangmahmah in na ~ hi/nomau mah in ~ un | settle it yourselves) (r:11.20.40/44.18.15) (q:draft)
khente = (t:n) (w:divisions/groups) (d:khen, divide, with plural -te: the groups into which people are divided, as the divisions of the priests or of the army) (e:siampite leh Levi mi a ~/kumpipa’ na a sem a ~ sungah uliante | the commanders of the divisions that served the king/siampite le Levi mi a ~ om hi | the divisions of the priests and Levites are there) (b:khen) (r:13.28.13/13.27.1/13.28.1/13.28.21) (q:draft)
khentel = (t:v) (w:discern/distinguish/tell apart/understand) (d:tell one thing clearly from another, and so understand or decide; khentel theihna is discernment or good judgment) (e:a nuam lo ~ thei nawn ka hi hiam/amaute in bangmah ~ thei lo uh hi | they cannot understand anything/Hih mite in ~ theihna nei lo | this people has no discernment/thu ~ theihna leh theihna hong hilh in | teach me good judgment and knowledge/ka ciahpih ding dawn’ nading ~ in | decide what answer I should take back) (s:khenthei/theitel) (r:10.19.35/46.12.10/23.44.18/23.27.11/19.119.66/13.21.12) (q:draft)
khentelna = (t:n) (w:distinction/telling apart) (d:khentel tell one from another, with the noun suffix na) (e:leh mipha leh misia ~/a nin vasa leh a siang ~ na bawl ding | you shall make a distinction between unclean birds and clean) (b:khentel) (r:27.11.35/3.20.25) (q:draft)
khenthang = (t:v) (w:scatter/divide/disperse) (d:khen divide with thang, abroad: divide and scatter among others; parallel to thehthang) (e:amaute ka ~ ding a) (s:thehthang) (a:kaikhawm) (r:1.49.7) (q:draft)
khenthei = (t:v) (w:discern/distinguish/recognize/tell apart) (d:khen divide with thei know or be able, tell one thing from another; thu khenthei is be able to judge) (e:a man lo na ~ uh hi/a pha le a sia a ~ dingin | to discern good and evil/Saul in David’ aw ~ a | Saul recognized the voice of David/Levi mi tangval’ aw khat ~ uh hi | they recognized the voice of a young Levite) (s:khentel/theitel) (b:khen) (r:45.2.18/9.26.17/10.14.17/7.18.3) (q:draft)
khentheih = (t:v) (w:be able to judge/be able to tell apart) (d:khen divide or judge, with theih can, the form used before nading and ding) (e:thu ~ nading aana ama tungah/adangte bangci ~ ding na hi uh hiam | how will you be able to tell the others apart/ahi leh ahi lo ~ nading siamna | the gift of telling whether it is so or not/thu neuneute leltak na ~ zawk kan ding uh | all the more you should be able to judge small matters) (b:khen) (r:43.5.27/46.12.10/62.4.2/46.6.3) (q:draft)
khentheita = (t:v) (w:can now distinguish/be able to tell apart) (d:khenthei, distinguish, with ta, now or already) (e:a lim le a lim lo a ~) (b:khenthei) (r:58.5.14) (q:draft)
khentuam = (t:n) (w:partiality/favouritism) (d:khen, divide, with tuam, separate: treating people differently; mi khentuam nei lo is showing no partiality) (e:mi ~ nei loin Pasian’ lampi) (s:angvanna/deidanna) (r:42.20.21) (q:draft)
khenuai = (t:n) (w:sole of the foot/sole) (d:khe, foot, and nuai, under: the underside of the foot; with ah, under the feet) (e:na ~ panun na luzang dong uhah/Ka ~ tawh Egypt lui khempeuh ka keusak hi | with the soles of my feet I dried up all the rivers of Egypt/A ~ a kipan a luzang dongin | from the sole of his foot to the top of his head/minamte i ~-ah amah in hong zawhsak hi | he subdued the peoples under our feet) (s:khepeek) (r:5.28.35/19.47.3/12.19.24/10.14.25) (q:draft)
khenzaw = (t:v) (w:judge rather/judge instead) (d:khen, in thu khen, judge, with zaw, rather) (e:thu taktak siksanin thu ~ un) (b:khen) (r:43.7.24) (q:draft)
khenzia = (t:n) (w:way of judging/manner of judging) (d:khen, in thu khen, judge, with zia, manner) (e:thu na ~ uh tawh kizui-in) (r:40.7.2) (q:draft)
khenzo = (t:v) (w:be able to separate/separate) (d:khen, divide, with zo, be able) (e:itna tawh hong ~ het lo ding hi/sihnate khat peuhpeuh in hong ~ ding ahi hiam | can any of these, even death, separate us) (b:khen) (r:45.8.39/45.8.35) (q:draft)
khenzo = (t:v) (w:settle/decide/pass judgement/decree) (d:with thu, matter: thu khenzo means settle a case or give the verdict) (e:kiciamna bek in thu ~ hi/Topa in nang tungah thu hong ~ hi | the Lord has passed judgement on you/Pasian in thu a ~ hi | God has decreed it) (b:khen) (r:20.18.18/36.2.5/27.9.26) (q:draft)
khep = (t:v) (w:fold/fold up/roll up) (d:fold cloth over on itself) (e:puanbuk mai-ah na ~ ding hi/puan ~ bangin na ~ ding a | you will roll them up like a robe) (r:2.26.9/58.1.12) (q:draft)
khepeek = (t:n) (w:foot/sole of the foot) (d:the flat part of the foot, from khe foot) (e:a ~ leh a siakmit guh hat a/na ~ nuai-a leivuite na singkhia un | shake off the dust under your feet/Ka ~ uh ah hong belh no khua leivui | the dust of your town that clings to our feet) (s:khenuai/khepek) (r:44.3.7/42.9.5/42.10.11) (q:draft)
khepeekte = (t:n) (w:feet/soles of the feet) (d:khepeek, sole of the foot, with the plural te) (e:a ~ uh bawng khe tawh kibang hi) (s:khepekte) (b:khepeek) (r:26.1.7) (q:draft)
khepek = (t:n) (w:foot) (d:the foot itself, the part below the leg) (e:A ~ leh a khemete khen khat/a ~ uh tawh kizom ngaltak tawn a neite | those that have jointed legs above their feet) (s:khepeek) (r:27.2.41/3.11.21) (q:draft)
khepekte = (t:n) (w:feet) (d:khepek, the foot below the ankle, with plural te; set beside khete, legs) (e:a ~ uh bawng khe tawh kibang hi/a ~ khenkhat sik leh khenkhat tungman kigawm | its feet partly of iron and partly of clay) (s:khepeekte) (b:khepek) (r:26.1.7/27.2.33) (q:draft)
khephung = (t:n) (w:feet/foot) (d:khe foot with phung: the place at the feet of someone, where a person bows down) (e:na ~ ah hong kun uh a/na ~ uhah ka boksak ding a | I will make them fall down at your feet) (r:5.33.3/66.3.9) (q:draft)
khephungah = (t:n) (w:at the feet) (d:khephung, the place at the feet of someone, with ah, at) (e:a ~ hong bok a) (b:khephung) (r:41.5.33) (q:draft)
khepi = (t:n) (w:big toe) (d:khe foot with pi great, as khutpi is the thumb) (e:a taklam ~ nuh ding hi/leh a taklam ~ nuh hi | and put it on the big toe of his right foot/amau’ taklam ~ dawnte nuhin | putting it on the tips of their right big toes/A khutpite leh a ~ a ki-attan kumpi sawmsagihte | seventy kings whose thumbs and big toes were cut off) (b:khe) (r:3.14.14/3.8.23/2.29.20/7.1.7) (q:draft)
khepite = (t:n) (w:big toes/great toes) (d:khepi, big toe, with plural -te; paired with khutpite, thumbs) (e:a khutpite leh a ~ attan uh hi/amau’ taklam khutpite leh amau’ taklam ~ | the thumbs of their right hands and the big toes of their right feet) (b:khepi) (r:7.1.6/3.8.24) (q:draft)
Kheran = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Cheran/Keran) (d:son of Dishon, a descendant of Seir the Horite in Edom) (r:1.36.26/13.1.41)
Khereth = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Kerethites) (d:people of the southern coast near the Philistines; with the Pelethites they formed the guard of David under Benaiah) (r:10.8.18/10.20.23)
Kherith = (t:name) (c:river) (w:Kerith) (d:ravine with a brook east of the Jordan, where Elijah hid during the drought) (r:11.17.3/11.17.5)
kherub = (t:n) (w:cherub/cherubim) (d:winged heavenly being; two golden cherubim stood on the cover of the ark and two of olive wood in the temple) (e:oliv sing tawh ~ nih bawl a/kham tawh ~ nih na bawl ding hi | you shall make two cherubim of gold/sing ~ nih bawlin kham tawh tuate zut hi | he made two wooden cherubim and overlaid them with gold/Mong khatah ~ khat | one cherub at one end) (r:11.6.23/11.6.26/2.25.18/14.3.10/2.25.19) (q:draft)
Kherub = (t:n) (w:cherub) (d:winged heavenly being, here written with a capital letter) (e:Amah ~ khat tungah tuangin/Amah in ~ khat tungah tuangin hong leeng a | he mounted a cherub and flew/~ adang khat zong tong sawm mah sau hi | the other cherub was also ten cubits) (r:10.22.11/11.6.26/19.18.10/11.6.25)
kherubte = (t:n) (w:cherubim/cherubs) (d:plural of kherub: the winged heavenly beings, and the figures of them in the tabernacle and temple) (e:Amah in kham tawh tua ~ zut hi/Tua ~ gei-ah leengpei khat ciat omin | beside each of the cherubim was a wheel/~ gel asauna leh a pian’ lim kibang hi | the two cherubim were alike in size and shape/Hih ~’ khate in tong sawmnih huam hi | the wings of these cherubim spanned twenty cubits) (b:kherub) (r:11.6.28/26.10.18/26.10.9/11.6.25/14.3.13) (q:draft)
Kherubte = (t:n) (w:cherubim) (e:~ tungah tu hi/Nang, ~ tunga tu-pa aw | you who sit enthroned on the cherubim/~ tungah a tu Vanglianpen Topa | the Lord Almighty who sits enthroned on the cherubim) (b:Kherub) (r:19.99.1/2.25.20/19.80.1/9.4.4) plural form of <Kherub>
