khete = (t:n) (w:feet/legs) (d:plural of khe: the feet, and also the legs of a person or animal) (e:A ~ sik tawh kibawl a/ka ~ kisuipuk dektak a | my feet had almost slipped/Ama ~ pen kolte in nasak a | they hurt his feet with shackles/a sungkuate leh a ~ sawp a | he washed the inner parts and the legs) (b:khe) (r:27.2.33/19.105.18/19.73.2/3.9.14) (q:draft)
khetphim = (t:n) (w:peg/tent peg/nail) (d:pin driven in with a hammer; puanbuk khetphim is a tent peg) (e:puanbuk ~ khat la a/Amah in puanbuk ~ a khutin zam a | she reached out her hand for the tent peg/a paang-ah puanbuk ~ tawh si-in na om hi | he lay dead with the tent peg in his temple) (s:singzum) (r:7.4.21/2.38.31/7.5.26/7.4.22) (q:draft)
khetphimte = (t:n) (w:tent pegs/pegs/stakes) (d:plural of khetphim, the pegs driven into the ground to hold a tent) (e:na ~ kip sak in/biakbuk ~ leh huang ~, leh amau’ khaute | the pegs of the tabernacle and of the courtyard, and their ropes/kimkot ading ~ khempeuh in sumngo ahi hi | all the pegs for the surrounding court were of bronze) (b:khetphim) (r:23.54.2/2.38.20/2.35.18) (q:draft)
