khinin = (t:adv) (w:already/completely) (d:khin, already, with the linking ending in: having done something, and then going on to the next action) (e:Ka tha bei ~ hong kinengcip hi/Pasian’ thu a hoihna phawk ~ | having tasted the goodness of the word of God/Leenggui lo kho ~ | having planted a vineyard/Inn thak lam ~ | having built a new house/Jakob’ suanlekhakte thatmang ~ | having wiped out the descendants of Jacob) (b:khin) (r:19.38.8/58.6.5/5.20.6/5.20.5/24.10.25) (q:draft)
khinkhia = (t:v) (w:remove/take away/expel/depose) (d:khin, move, with khia, out: move a person or thing out of its place, as idols from a land, a people from the sight of God or a ruler from office) (e:a pate’ bawlsa milim khempeuh ~ hi/ka muhna panin Judah zong ka ~ ding a | I will remove Judah also from my sight/kumpite ama panmun ciat panin ~ in la | remove the kings from their posts/a pi Ma-akah zong ~ hi | he also deposed his grandmother Maakah/Topa in gamlapi-ah mite ~-in | the Lord sending the people far away) (s:koihkhia/paaikhia/nilkhia/lakhia) (r:11.15.12/12.23.27/11.20.24/11.15.13/23.6.12) (q:draft)
khinkhian = (t:adv) (w:quietly/calmly/still) (d:after a verb for doing something silently and without moving; om khinkhian, keep calm; im khinkhian, keep hidden) (e:Mipilte in a theihna uh im ~ a/pau loin om ~ in | keep silent/Kidawm in la, om ~ in | be careful and keep calm/namsau in ngak ~ a | the sword lies in wait) (s:khikhe/dide/daitakin) (r:20.12.23/23.7.4/20.17.28/18.15.22) (q:draft)
khinkhiat = (t:v) (w:remove/take away) (d:form of khinkhia, remove, used before another word such as bangin or khit) (e:Israel ka ~ bangin/Tua pa a ~ khit ciangin | after he had removed that man) (b:khinkhia) (r:12.23.27/44.13.22) (q:draft)
khinkhiatna = (t:n) (w:removal/removing) (d:khinkhiat remove with the noun ending na; a khinkhiatna ding, in order to remove) (e:amaute a ~ ding) (s:lakkhiatna) (b:khinkhiat) (r:12.24.3) (q:draft)
khinmang = (t:adv) (w:completely/entirely/utterly) (d:placed after a verb: the action takes in the whole and nothing is left over) (e:namsau tawh that ~ uh hi/a neih a lam khempeuh a laksak ~ hi | he took away all her treasures/gun-a ngahmun teng la ~ uh a | they have seized all the river crossings/cihna thu in huam ~ hi | this saying sums it all up) (s:mangkhin) (r:6.11.11/45.13.9/25.1.10/24.51.32) (q:draft)
Khinnereth = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Kinnereth) (d:fortified town of Naphtali on the Sea of Galilee, which is also called the Sea of Kinnereth) (r:6.19.35)
Khinneroth = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Kinnereth) (d:another spelling of Kinnereth, the town and district by the Sea of Galilee) (r:6.11.2/11.15.20)
khinpa = (t:n) (w:the man who has) (d:khin, already, with pa, man, after a verb: the man who has done or undergone it) (e:zia a thuak ~ in keimah ka hi hi) (b:khin) (r:25.3.1) (q:draft)
khinsa = (t:adv) (w:already) (d:placed after a verb to show that the action is already done and its result remains, often before a noun: a si khinsa mite, those who have already died) (e:a si ~ mite/tua biakna a nusia ~ mite | those who have already abandoned that faith/laibu sunga keima thu a kigelh ~ bangin | as it is already written about me in the book/lei hoihna sungah a kisuan ~ ahi hi | it had already been planted in good soil/a kihih ~ mawhna | sins already committed) (s:khinzo) (b:khin) (r:21.4.2/26.17.8/27.11.32/19.40.7/45.3.25) (q:draft)
khinsate = (t:part) (w:those who have already) (d:khinsa, already completed, with plural -te: placed after a verb, those who have already done it; a si khinsate are those who have already died) (e:Mi a si ~ hingkik thei lo/Leihawm sunga pai ~ lak panin | from among those who have gone down to the pit/mi a si ~ hong tho ding ahi hiam | will those who have died rise up/A tawpkik ~ a kisik kik nadingin) (b:khinsa) (r:18.14.13/19.88.10/19.30.3/58.6.4) (q:draft)
khinsim = (t:v) (w:move secretly/shift by stealth) (d:khin move with sim secretly: move a thing from its place without being seen, as a boundary stone) (e:gisuangte ~ uh a) (r:18.24.2) (q:draft)
khinta = (t:v) (w:completed/finished) (d:khin, already, with ta: be finished, be fully done) (e:nasem ~/Pasian in a nasepte zo ~ a | God had finished his work/Man ~ hi | it is finished) (s:mankhin) (b:khin) (r:19.88.4/1.2.2/43.19.30)
khinta = (t:adj) (w:finished) (e:man~) (s:kiman/zawhsa) (b:khin)
khinta = (t:part) (d:particle suffixed to form verb past tense) (e:kong pia ~ hi/tuite kiam ~ hi | the waters had gone down/Satan’ nung a zui dingin kipan ~ uh hi | they have already begun to follow Satan/ama neihsa dingin Israel teel ~ hi | he has chosen Israel as his own possession/a sia suak ~ hi | it has become a ruin) (b:khin) (r:54.5.15/1.8.3/19.135.4/23.64.11)
khinte = (t:n) (d:those who have already done the action; khin already, joined to the verb before it, with the plural te: a thokik khinte, those who have risen again) (e:Sihna panin a thokik ~ ahih manin/Khrih tawh a thokik ~ na hih manun | since you have been raised with Christ/Lungpilna lamah a khan’ ~ bang un | in your thinking be like adults/Kei a hong mu ~ in | those who have seen me) (b:khin) (r:42.20.36/51.3.1/46.14.20/43.14.9) (q:draft)
khinzo = (t:adv) (w:already) (d:khin, already, with zo, have done: placed after a verb to mark the action as fully completed) (e:Moab gam kisia ~ a/note a siang na suak ~ uh hi | you are already clean/Josef pen Egypt-ah na om ~ hi | Joseph was already in Egypt/ama thusim kei tungah hong hilh ~ hi | he has made his mystery known to me/tacil pen Topa a’ hi ~ | the firstborn already belongs to the Lord) (s:khin/khinsa) (b:khin) (r:24.48.20/43.15.3/2.1.5/49.3.3/3.27.26) (q:draft)
Khios = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Chios) (d:island in the Aegean Sea that Paul passed on his voyage to Miletus) (r:44.20.15)
khip = (t:v) (w:put on the head/wear on the head) (d:form of khim, put on a headdress; dial khip is a turban, a cloth worn on the head) (e:a lu tungah a ~ ding uh aite/na dial ~ la khia in | take off your turban) (r:26.13.18/26.21.26) (q:draft)
khipkhep = (t:adv) (w:completely/utterly) (d:after dai, be still: perfectly calm, dead silent) (e:huihnung khawlin dai ~ pah hi) (r:41.4.39) (q:draft, low confidence)
khipsak = (t:v) (w:put on the head of) (d:khip put on the head with sak for another: put a turban or headdress on someone) (e:dial siangtho a ~ ding uh) (s:khusak/khuksak) (b:khip) (r:38.3.5) (q:draft)
khipte = (t:n) (w:veils/head coverings/kerchiefs) (d:khip, put on the head, with plural te: things worn over the head; here in ai khipte, where ai is divination) (e:Na ai ~ uh zong) (b:khip) (r:26.13.21) (q:draft)
Khirs = (t:n) (w:Christ) (d:the Christ, title of Jesus; a rare spelling beside Khazih and Khrih) (e:Jesus ~/Zeisu ~’ Kha Siangtho huhna hang | through the help of the Spirit of Jesus Christ) (r:50.1.19)
khirsoprase = (t:n) (c:stone) (w:chrysoprase) (d:precious stone, the tenth foundation stone of the new Jerusalem, where the NIV has turquoise) (e:a sawmna in ~ suangmanpha) (r:66.21.20) (q:draft)
Khislev = (t:name) (w:Kislev) (d:ninth month of the Hebrew calendar, falling in November and December) (r:16.1.1/38.7.1)
Khislon = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Kislon) (d:father of Elidad, the leader of Benjamin chosen to help divide the land of Canaan) (r:4.34.21)
