khit = (t:part) (d:particle suffixed to form verb past tense) (e:an nek ~ ciang/Tua thu a gen ~ ciangin | after he had said this/sawtpi a tam ~ uh ciangin | after they had stayed a long time/Ahab a sih ~ ciangin | after Ahab died) (r:43.7.9/44.15.33/12.1.1)
khit = (t:conj) (w:after) (d:in khit ciangin, after: placed after a verb, a noun of time or tua, that) (e:Tua ~ ciangin khan’ khinin teek sih ta hi/Hih thute ~ ciangin | after these things/Tua ~ ciangin Kanaan mite kizelthang hi | after that the Canaanite clans scattered/Tua zawh ni sawm ~ ciangin | ten days after that) (s:khitzawh/tuzawh) (a:mapekin) (r:18.42.17/1.15.1/1.10.18/24.42.7)
khit = (t:adj) (w:later) (e:Tawlkhat ~ ciangin | some time later) (s:tuzawh) (r:7.11.4)
khita = (t:prep) (w:after) (d:khit after with the ending a: coming after a person in time, ama khita a tate, his children after him) (e:ama ~ a tate/note’ ~ na tate uh tungah | to your children after you) (s:khitah/nunga/nungah) (a:ma) (b:khit) (r:1.18.19/5.4.40) (q:draft)
khitah = (t:prep) (w:after) (d:after a person in time or succession, khit with the place marker ah) (e:ama ~ a tapa koihin/kei’ ~ zong kuamah om lo ding hi | nor will there be anyone after me/ama ~ a suanlekhakte tungah | to his descendants after him/nangma ~ zong nang tawh a kibang | anyone like you after you) (s:khita/nunga/nungah) (a:ma) (b:khit) (r:11.15.4/4.25.13/23.43.10/11.3.12) (q:draft)
khite = (t:n) (w:necklaces) (d:khi, necklace, with the plural te: necklaces, listed among gold ornaments with armlets, bracelets, rings and earrings) (e:leh ~ ka muh ciat uh/bilbahte, le ~ ka muh ciat uh | earrings and necklaces that each of us acquired) (b:khi) (r:4.31.50) (q:draft)
khitin = (t:conj) (w:after/once) (d:khit, finish, with the linking suffix in: after doing or becoming something; a teek khitin is after growing old, in old age) (e:a teek ~ ka topa tawh tapa khat/ka topa zong a teek ~ nopsakna nei ding | to have pleasure after my lord too has grown old/a teek ~ amah tawh tapa khat ka nei | I have borne him a son in his old age/a teek ~ a neih a tapa ahi hi | he was the son born to him in his old age) (s:khitzawh) (b:khit) (r:1.24.36/1.21.7/1.18.12/1.37.3) (q:draft)
khitlam = (t:n) (d:the fact that an action is already done: khit, finish, with lam, placed after a verb and before a word of seeing or knowing, as in a sih khitlam a mu, see that she has died) (e:a sih ~ a muh uh ciangin/Jonathan a paikhiat ~ thei lo uh hi | they did not know that Jonathan had left/amah a nusiat ~ amah in thei lo hi | he did not know that he had left him/a nek ~ uh kuamah in thei lo hi | no one could tell that they had eaten them) (r:44.5.10/9.14.3/7.16.20/1.41.21) (q:draft)
Khitlish = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Chitlish/Kitlish) (d:town in the western foothills of Judah, listed with Kabbon and Lahmas) (r:6.15.40)
khitna = (t:n) (d:the fact of having already done something, khit with the noun suffix na; a thah khitna thu is the news that he had killed; a khitna also means the last one, as in dangkasan a khitna, the last penny) (e:Topa siampite a thah ~ thu/namsau tawh kamsangte khempeuh a thah ~ thu | how he had killed all the prophets with the sword/a ciam leitangah ka tun’ ~ uh thu | that we have come to the land he swore to give/gamkhing a suahsak ~ hong en un | come and see the desolations he has brought) (b:khit) (r:9.22.21/11.19.1/5.26.3/19.46.8) (q:draft)
khitphet = (t:adv) (w:as soon as/just after) (d:khit, finished, with phet, just: the moment something is done; followed by ciangin) (e:na zak ~ uh ciangin/tum theih dang gingte na zak ~ uh ciangin | as soon as you hear the other instruments) (r:27.3.15) (q:draft)
khitsa = (t:part) (w:already) (d:khit, finish, with sa: placed after a verb for something already done or completed beforehand; often describes a following noun) (e:tuate khempeuh na theih ~ uh ahi hi/A thuteng ka hong gen ~ hinapi | although I have already told you everything/Topa in ama’ tunga a gen ~ thu khempeuh | all the words the Lord had spoken to him/a zawh ~ a nasep adingin | for the work they had now completed) (b:khit) (r:18.27.12/24.36.4/43.9.27/44.14.26) (q:draft)
khitsate = (t:n) (w:things already done/finished work) (d:khitsa, already done, with the plural te: the things one has been doing; ama sep khitsate is the work he had been doing) (e:ama' sep ~ Pasian in zo a) (b:khitsa) (r:1.2.2) (q:draft)
khitui = (t:n) (w:tears/tear) (d:the water that runs from the eyes when one weeps; khitui luang is shed tears) (e:Ka ~ kang thei loin/ka ~ guntui luang a bang hi | my tears flow like a river/amaute’ dawn dingin ~ tampi na pia hi | you have given them many tears to drink/zan sialin ka ~ in ka lupphah tum a | all night long my tears flood my bed) (r:25.3.49/19.6.6/25.3.48/19.80.5) (q:draft)
khituite = (t:n) (w:tears) (d:khitui, tear, with the plural te) (e:ka ~ hong kangsak a/ka ~ na thawl sungah thun in | put my tears in your bottle/na ~ ka mu khin hi | I have seen your tears) (b:khitui) (r:19.116.8/12.20.5/19.56.8) (q:draft)
khitzawh = (t:conj) (w:after) (d:khit, finish, with zawh: placed after a verb or after tua, once the action is over; tua khitzawh phetin is immediately after that) (e:Tua ~ phetin ak hong khuangta hi/Ama sih ~ ni sawmli sung | for forty days after his death/sihna panin Jesuh a kithawhkiksak ~ nungzuite tungah | to the disciples after Jesus was raised from the dead) (s:khitin) (r:40.26.74/44.1.3/43.21.14) (q:draft)
khiukheuna = (t:n) (w:destitution/utter poverty) (d:follows zawn, poor: the state of being very poor; khiukheu seems to be a word that strengthens zawng, poor) (e:citak-a zawn’ ~ hoihzaw hi) (s:zawnna) (a:hauhna) (r:20.19.1) (q:draft, low confidence)
