Khloe = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Chloe) (d:woman whose household brought Paul news of the quarrels in the church at Corinth) (r:46.1.11)
kho = (t:v) (w:farm/practise farming/plow/till) (d:work the land, plow or cultivate a field; almost always in lo kho, farm a field, and lo khopa is a farmer) (e:lo ~ ding, an hau ding/leitang a ~ ding mi om lo | there was no one to work the ground/lo ~ dingin lo nasep a sem mite | the workers who farmed the land/Ka bawngla tawh lo ~ khawm lo hi le-uhcin | if you had not plowed with my heifer/tua lo a ~ dingin losapte sawl a | he sent tenants to farm that vineyard) (s:khawh) (r:13.27.26/1.2.5/7.14.18/22.8.11)
kho = (t:adj) (w:strong/well built/firm/secure) (d:firm, strong and lasting; kho takin is firmly and kip kho is stand firm, endure) (e:ama kumpi gam ~ takin lenkip hi/Na omna mun ~ a | your dwelling place is secure/Migilote’ lam innte ~ lo a | the houses the wicked build are not firm/Ama itna kip ~ tawntung hi | his love endures forever) (s:kip) (r:14.1.1/4.24.21/18.27.18/19.118.2)
khoh = (t:v) (w:urge/press/entreat) (d:press someone strongly to do or not to do something; also invite pressingly) (e:Zeisu nakpi-in a ~ uh ciangin/laizial a hal loh nading a ~ uh hangin | although they urged him not to burn the scroll) (s:khosak/hanthawn) (r:42.24.29/24.36.25) (q:draft)
khohsa = (t:adj) (w:invited) (d:khoh, urge or invite, with sa for a completed action: already invited; a khohsa mite is those who have been invited) (e:a ~ mite a sam dingin/a ~ mite in na thusim lo uh a | those who were invited paid no attention/ci-in a ~ mite a samsak hi | he had those who had been invited called) (s:khohsaksa) (b:khoh) (r:40.22.3/42.14.17/40.22.5) (q:draft)
khohsaksa = (t:adj) (w:invited) (d:khoh, urge or invite, with sak and sa, already done: ka khohsaksa mite is those I have invited) (e:Ka ~ mite kiangah/Ka ~ mite kiangah hih bangin va gen un | go and tell those I have invited) (s:khohsa) (r:40.22.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
khohsate = (t:n) (w:invited guests/those invited) (d:khoh, urge or invite, with sa, already done, and plural te: those who have been invited to a feast) (e:a ~ kiangah gen dingin/a ~ a sapsak hangin a hawh nuam kei | though he sent for those invited they would not come/ci-in ka ~ va hilh kik un | go and tell those I have invited once more) (s:kisamte/sapsate) (b:khohsa) (r:42.14.17/40.22.3/40.22.4) (q:draft)
khoi = (t:v) (w:bring up/rear/nurture/care for) (d:look after and feed a child, a young animal or a person in need; often paired with vaak, feed) (e:ama ta bangin a vaak a ~ hi/Humpinelkai dangte tawh kikhawlin, a note ~ hi | she lay among the lions and reared her cubs/zintun’na innah paipihin a ~ hi | he brought him to an inn and took care of him/Amaute in ta a ~ uh hangin | even if they bring up children/a tate a ~ thei, zin a do thei | able to bring up her children and to show hospitality) (s:khawi) (r:44.7.21/26.19.2/42.10.34/28.9.12/54.5.10) (q:draft)
khoih = (t:v) (w:touch/nudge) (d:touch someone with the hand, here as a secret sign) (e:a khut tawh hong ~ hi/hong su-in, a khut tawh hong ~ hi | he signals, and motions with his fingers) (r:20.6.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
khoina = (t:n) (w:care/support/help) (d:khoi, care for, with the noun suffix na: the care or support given to someone; here paired with vaak, feed) (e:nong ~ uh a kicing lote/kei nong vaak, nong ~ uh a kicing lote | what was lacking in your feeding and caring for me) (s:kepna) (b:khoi) (r:50.2.30) (q:draft)
khoisa = (t:adj) (w:reared/brought up) (d:khoi, rear, with sa, already done: whom one has brought up) (e:na ~ tapate khempeuh lak panin) (b:khoi) (r:23.51.18) (q:draft)
khoisak = (t:v) (w:nurse for/bring up for) (d:khoi, rear, with sak, for someone: nurse or bring up a child on behalf of another) (e:kei adingin hong ~ in/nang adingin naupang hong ~ dingin naucing khat | a nurse to nurse the child for you/hihte kua in hong ~ ahi hiam | who brought these up for me) (b:khoi) (r:2.2.9/23.49.21/2.2.7) (q:draft)
khokhawm = (t:v) (w:plow together/farm together) (d:kho, farm, with khawm, together: plow a field with two animals yoked together) (e:lo na ~ kei ding uh hi/le la khat tawh lo na ~ kei ding | you shall not plow with a donkey yoked alongside) (b:kho) (r:5.22.10) (q:draft)
khol = (t:v) (w:store/store up/lay up) (d:put food or goods away to keep for later use) (e:khuakhal sunga a nek ding ~ zo uh hi/khuapite sungah an ~ hi | he stored the food in the cities/tuipi sehnel zahin antang tampi ~ hi | he stored up grain as plentiful as the sand of the sea/zong la in la, ~ in | take it and store it away) (s:koihkhol/kem) (r:20.30.25/1.6.21/1.41.48/1.41.49)
khol = (t:v) (w:save/save up/lay up) (d:put money or wealth aside for the future; sum khol is save money) (e:sum ~ ding/a tapate ading sum a ~ uh hi | they save up money for their sons/vantungah na sum uh ~ un | store up your treasure in heaven/hih leitungah na sum uh ~ kei un | do not store up your treasure on this earth) (r:47.12.14/40.6.20/40.6.19)
kholcipte = (t:n) (w:hoarders/those who store up) (d:khol, store, with cip, tightly, and the plural te: those who hoard things for themselves) (e:bekin a ~ pen/amau a’ ding bekin a ~ pen | those who store up only for themselves) (r:42.12.21) (q:draft)
kholh = (t:adv) (w:beforehand/in advance/ahead) (d:placed after a verb for doing something ahead of time: theih kholh foreknow, ngaihsut kholh think out beforehand; a form of khol) (e:Pasian in a theih ~ ama mite/ci-in na ngaihsut ~ loh nadingun | so that you do not think it out beforehand/kam tawh a gen ~ mah bangin | as he said beforehand by their mouth/vantungmi in a phuah ~ mah bangin | as the angel had named him beforehand) (b:khol) (r:45.11.2/42.21.14/42.1.69/42.2.21) (q:draft)
kholh = (t:v) (w:send food to/share food with) (d:take or send a share of food to others who have none) (e:midangte a ~ ding leh lungdam-a om dingin/a nei zo lote zong va ~ un | send some also to those who have nothing) (r:16.8.12/16.8.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
kholhna = (t:n) (d:noun form of kholh, beforehand, placed after a verb: an act done in advance, as thupiak kholhna revelation, thugen kholhna foretelling, kisak kholhna readiness) (e:Topa’ thupiak ~ bangin/Pasian’ thupiak ~ hangin | by the revelation of God/mai lam thugen ~ leh khongkhaina zang a | he practised omens and witchcraft/Lungdamna Thu-a kipan kisak ~ khedap bulh un | put on the shoes of readiness that comes from the gospel) (b:kholh) (r:52.4.15/49.6.15/49.3.3/14.33.6) (q:draft)
Kholhna = (t:n) (d:kholhna written with a capital in a title; Thugen Kholhna, foretelling, is the prophecy of Ahijah) (e:Mi Ahijah’ Thugen ~ sung) (b:kholhna) (r:14.9.29) (q:draft)
kholhnate = (t:n) (w:predictions/divinations/warnings) (d:kholh beforehand with na and the plural te, after a verb of speaking: things said in advance, as thugen kholhnate predictions and hilh kholhnate warnings) (e:a thugen ~ uh zong thu zuau ahi hi/na thugen ~ uh zuauthu ahi hi | your predictions are lies/note kong hilh ~ tel takin thei un | know well the warnings I give you) (s:genkholhnate) (b:kholhna) (r:26.13.6/24.42.19/26.13.7) (q:draft)
kholhsa = (t:adv) (w:beforehand/in advance/already) (d:kholh, beforehand, with sa: follows a verb and marks the action as already done ahead of time) (e:Pasian’ teel ~ a teci/Taanglai pek panin ka geel ~ hi | I planned it long ago/Pasian’ kamsangte gelh ~ thu khempeuhte | everything the prophets of God wrote beforehand/Israel kumpipa David in a geel ~ bangin | as David king of Israel had prescribed) (s:kholsa) (b:kholh) (r:44.10.41/12.19.25/42.18.31/15.3.10) (q:draft)
kholhsak = (t:adv) (w:beforehand for/in advance for) (d:kholh beforehand with sak for someone, after a verb: koih kholhsak is lay up or reserve for someone ahead of time) (e:vantungah thaman lianpi hong kikoih ~/khuamial sahpi omna mun a koih ~ hi | he has reserved a place of thick darkness for them) (b:kholh) (r:40.5.12/61.2.17) (q:draft)
kholhsakna = (t:n) (w:preparing beforehand/provision made in advance) (d:kholhsak, beforehand for someone, with the noun suffix na: a bawl kholhsakna mun is the place made ready in advance for her) (e:a bawl ~ mun gamlakah tai a/Pasian in ama a dingin a bawl ~ mun | the place God had prepared for her) (b:kholhsak) (r:66.12.6) (q:draft)
kholhte = (t:n) (w:things said beforehand/predictions) (d:kholh, beforehand, with the plural te, after a verb: thugen kholhte is the words spoken beforehand, predictions) (e:kamsang siangthote’ thugen ~/na thugen ~ uh thu zuau ahi hi | your predictions are lies) (b:kholh) (r:61.3.2/26.13.7) (q:draft)
kholin = (t:adv) (w:beforehand/in advance) (d:khol, beforehand, with the linking suffix in: follows a verb whose action is done ahead of time, before a further action) (e:amaute limtakin hilh ~/ci-in Lai Siangtho in thei ~ | Scripture, knowing this beforehand/a kipi mo bangin kiging ~ | made ready beforehand like a bride) (r:9.8.9/48.3.8/66.21.2) (q:draft)
kholin = (t:v) (w:store up/store) (d:khol, store, with the linking suffix in, before a further action) (e:Faro’ ukna nuai-ah antangte ~/amau ading a bulpi pha zong ~ | also storing up a good foundation for themselves) (b:khol) (r:1.41.35/54.6.17) (q:draft)
khollo = (t:adv) (w:not much/not very/hardly) (d:follows a verb or a describing word: not particularly, not to any great degree) (e:bangmah thupi ~ hi/A tuite ama a’ bangin ngaihsun ~ a | she hardly thinks of her young as her own/hih ka hong laigelh pen sau ~ ahih manin | because this letter of mine is not very long/a nasepna uh sau tung ~ ding hi | their work will not get very far) (r:47.10.10/58.13.22/18.39.16/55.3.9) (q:draft)
kholloh = (t:adv) (w:not much/not very/hardly) (d:form of khollo used before hangin, bang and te) (e:mite zong ka donnop ~ hangin) (b:khollo) (r:42.18.4/46.12.24) (q:draft)
khollohte = (t:n) (d:kholloh, not much, with plural te, after a verb: the ones that are not much so; thupi i sak khollohte, the parts we do not think very important) (e:na thupi i sak ~/I pumpi na hoih i sak ~ pen | the parts of our body we do not think very presentable) (b:kholloh) (r:46.12.24/46.12.23) (q:draft)
khollote = (t:n) (w:those who hardly/those who do not much) (d:khollo not much with plural te: a paupau khollote is those who do not talk much) (e:a paupau ~ thu mu taktak hizaw hi) (b:khollo) (r:20.17.27) (q:draft)
kholna = (t:n) (w:storehouse/treasury/store) (d:khol, store, with the noun suffix na: the storing of something or the place where it is stored; sum kholna is a treasury or treasure) (e:na sum ~ munah/sumpi ~ sungah koih ding kilawm lo hi | it is not right to put it into the treasury/a na hoih ~ vantung note adingin | the heavens, his storehouse of good things, for you/leenggahzu ~ beelpi ah na pai uh ciangin | when you went to the wine vat) (s:sumkholna/vankoihna) (b:khol) (r:42.12.34/40.27.6/5.28.12/37.2.16) (q:draft)
kholnapi = (t:n) (w:great heap/heap) (d:kholna storing place with pi great: nin kholnapi is a great rubbish heap, where the NIV has heap of ruins) (e:nin ~ khatin piangsak den hi) (b:kholna) (r:6.8.28) (q:draft, low confidence)
kholpa = (t:n) (w:one who does beforehand) (d:khol, beforehand, with pa, the man who, after a verb: thu pia kholpa, he who warns, a om kholpa, he who stands ready) (e:thukhen dingin a om ~ mai-ah/vantung pan thu hong pia ~ kiang pan | from him who warns us from heaven) (r:60.4.5/58.12.25) (q:draft, low confidence)
kholsa = (t:n) (w:stores/treasure/what is stored up) (d:khol, store, with sa, already done: things that have been laid up, stores or treasure) (e:a ngahsa uh leh a ~ uh na tampite/Ama ~ khempeuh kisusia a | all his treasures are destroyed/Na ~ nate kua in luah ding hiam | who will get the things you have stored up) (b:khol) (r:23.15.7/18.20.26/42.12.20) (q:draft)
kholsa = (t:adv) (w:beforehand/in advance/already) (d:follows a verb: done or made ready ahead of time, as kigelh kholsa written beforehand and kiseh kholsa determined beforehand; kholsa-a om is be prepared) (e:a kiseh ~ bang a/tua ni ciangin a kigelh ~ khempeuh | on that day all that has been written beforehand/note a ~-a na om loh uh | that you are not prepared) (s:kholhsa) (r:27.11.36/40.26.24/42.21.22/47.9.4) (q:draft)
kholsak = (t:adv) (w:beforehand/in advance) (d:khol, beforehand, with sak, for someone, after a verb: hilh kholsak is warn someone beforehand) (e:mi sawlin hilh ~ hi/a om mite kiangah mi sawlin hilh ~ hi | he sent men to warn the people there beforehand) (r:12.6.10) (q:draft)
kholsate = (t:n) (w:stores/things stored up) (d:kholsa, what is stored up, with the plural te) (e:tuni donga a ~/na pate in tu ni dong a, a ~ | what your fathers have stored up to this day) (s:kholte) (b:kholsa) (r:23.39.6) (q:draft)
kholte = (t:n) (w:things stored up/stores) (d:khol store with the plural te: the things that have been stored) (e:tu ni donga a ~ Babilon ah/na pate in tu ni donga a ~ | what your fathers have stored up to this day) (s:kholsate) (b:khol) (r:12.20.17) (q:draft)
kholte = (t:n) (w:those who store/those who gather in) (d:khol store with the plural te: the people who have gathered and stored the crop) (e:a ~ in ne-in Topa phat ding/a ~ in ne-in Topa phat ding a | those who gather it in will eat it and praise the Lord) (b:khol) (r:23.62.9) (q:draft)
kholteng = (t:n) (w:all that is stored up) (d:khol, store, with teng, all: the whole of what one has laid up) (e:a hoih a ~ suahkhia a/migilote in gitlohna a ~ a suahkhia ahi hi | the evil man brings out the evil he has stored up) (b:khol) (r:40.12.35) (q:draft)
kholzaw = (t:v) (w:store up instead/store up) (d:khol, store, with zaw, rather: store up there instead) (e:note a dingin ~ un/mun vantungah note a dingin ~ un | store up for yourselves in heaven instead) (b:khol) (r:40.6.20) (q:draft)
kholzo = (t:v) (w:manage to store/store up) (d:khol, store, with zo, be able: succeed in storing up) (e:a nek ding uh ~ uh hi/khuakhal sungin a nek ding uh ~ uh hi | they manage to store up their food in summer) (b:khol) (r:20.30.25) (q:draft)
khom = (t:v) (w:last/be enough for) (d:of food or goods, be enough to last through a length of time) (e:kum thum sung ~ ding an hong piang ding hi/ni nih ~ ding an hong pia hi | he gives you food to last two days/Kum tampi sung ka ~ ding annek tuidawn | food and drink to last me many years) (r:3.25.21/2.16.29/42.12.19) (q:draft)
khomun = (t:n) (w:bread/loaf) (d:bread or a loaf of bread; khomun pum khat is one loaf and silngo om lo khomun is unleavened bread) (e:A ta in ~ ngen leh/Nuntakna ~ ka hi hi | I am the bread of life/~ pum khat bek a nei uh hi | they had only one loaf/tua ~ ko hong pia tawntung in | always give us this bread) (s:anlum/moh/tangho) (r:40.7.9/43.6.48/41.8.14/43.6.34) (q:draft)
Khomun = (t:n) (w:bread) (d:khomun written with a capital at the start of a sentence or in the name Silngo om lo Khomun, the Unleavened Bread of the festival) (e:Silngo om lo ~ nek kipat ni-in/~ pum nga leh ngasa tawn nih | five loaves and two fish/~ a ne pasal bek tul nga a pha | the men alone who ate the bread numbered five thousand) (b:khomun) (r:40.26.17/40.16.12/40.14.17/41.6.44) (q:draft)
khomunte = (t:n) (w:loaves/bread) (d:khomun, loaf, with the plural te; here the consecrated bread set before God) (e:a kikoih ~ a om uh hi/sabuai leh Pasian mai-ah a kikoih ~ | the table and the loaves set before God) (s:anlumte) (b:khomun) (r:58.9.2) (q:draft)
khon = (t:v) (w:collect/levy) (d:collect money or a tax from people) (e:Israel mihonte tung panin a ~) (r:14.24.6) (q:draft)
khong = (t:n) (w:sorcery/soothsaying) (d:used with khai: khong khai means practise sorcery or soothsaying, and khong khaite are those who do so) (e:~ khaite leh ai saante’ thu ngai/ai a saan, ~ a khai | who practises divination or sorcery) (s:khongkhai) (r:5.18.14/5.18.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
khong = (t:adv) (w:just/merely) (d:after a verb: merely staying in that state without doing anything more, as in bu khong, stay hidden, and en khong, only look on) (e:nang bu ~ na hi hiam/bang tanvei hong en ~ ding na hi hiam | how long will you only look on/i mawhnate hong en ~ phot hi | for a time he merely looked on at our sins/A om ~ thei lo | who cannot stay still) (r:19.10.1/19.35.17/45.3.25/35.1.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
khongin = (t:adv) (w:free of charge/for free/without paying) (d:always in a khongin: as a free gift, without payment or wages) (e:a ~ tui ka pia ding hi/Kuama an a ~ ka ne kei uh hi | we did not eat anyone’s food without paying/thaman ngen loin, a ~ Lungdamna Thu hilh ding | to preach the gospel free of charge, asking no pay/nuntakna tui a ~ hong la ta uh hen | let them take the water of life as a free gift) (r:66.21.6/53.3.8/46.9.18/66.22.17) (q:draft)
khongkhai = (t:n) (w:astrology/sorcery/enchantment) (d:occult art; khongkhai siamte and khongkhai theite, those skilled in it, stand for the astrologers and enchanters of Babylon and Egypt) (e:leh ~ siamte a samsak hi/milimte leh ~ theite, vankah theite leh aisan theite | idols and enchanters, mediums and diviners/mitphial siamte, ~ siamte leh aksi et siamte’ ukpi | chief of the enchanters, astrologers and star readers) (s:khong) (r:27.2.2/27.2.10/27.5.11/23.19.3) (q:draft, low confidence, exact kind of art not clear from the verses)
khongkhaina = (t:n) (w:witchcraft/sorcery) (d:khongkhai with the noun suffix na: the practice of the occult art) (e:leh ~ zang a/mai lam thugen kholhna leh ~ zang a | he practised omens and witchcraft) (s:bumna) (b:khongkhai) (r:14.33.6) (q:draft)
khongkhaite = (t:n) (w:sorcerers/soothsayers) (d:khongkhai, sorcery or soothsaying, with plural te: those who practise it, named beside aisante, diviners) (e:~ le aisante thu ngai uh hi/nisuahna lam gam ~ leh Filistia mite bangin | like the soothsayers of the east and the Philistines) (s:khongkhaitheite) (b:khongkhai) (r:5.18.14/23.2.6) (q:draft)
khongkhaithei = (t:n) (w:astrologer/enchanter/soothsayer) (d:khongkhai, occult art, with thei, know: one who knows that art) (e:a hong gen thei ding ~/~, mitphial siam, aisan siam kuamah om lo hi | there is no enchanter, magician or diviner) (b:khongkhai) (r:27.2.27) (q:draft, low confidence, exact kind of art not clear from the verse)
khongkhaitheite = (t:n) (w:astrologers/enchanters/soothsayers) (d:khongkhaithei, one who knows the occult art, with the plural te) (e:mitphial siamte, ~, aksi et siamte/aisan theite, mitphial siamte, ~, aksi et siamte khempeuh | all the magicians, enchanters, astrologers and diviners) (s:khongkhaite) (b:khongkhaithei) (r:27.4.7) (q:draft, low confidence, exact kind of art not clear from the verse)
khongkhakah = (t:n) (w:at the doorway/at the door) (d:door or doorway with the place marker ah; the same verse writes kongkhak for door) (e:inn ~ a zineu lumin/en in, inn ~ a zineu lumin | there lay his concubine at the doorway of the house) (s:kongkhakah) (r:7.19.27) (q:draft, low confidence, perhaps a spelling of kongkhak)
khop = (t:adv) (w:together/along with) (d:placed after a verb, the action is done together with someone; form of khawm used before words such as ding, sangin and man) (e:zi gilo tawh teen’ ~ sangin/Tua mipa tawh a om ~ | to stay together with that man/ten’ ~ theih dingin amau’ neihsate tam lua hi | their possessions were too many for them to live together/kei tawh nong biak ~ dingun ngun pasiante | silver gods to worship alongside me) (s:khawm) (a:tuamin) (r:20.21.19/2.20.23/1.36.7/2.2.21) (q:draft)
khop = (t:adv) (w:enough/sufficiently) (d:placed after a describing word or a verb: to a sufficient degree; sauvei khop is long enough and kham khop is enough to satisfy) (e:sauvei ~ na pai khin ta uh hi/a hoih ~ zah bek ne in | eat only as much as is good/ni khat kham ~ ding kaikhawm ding uh hi | they shall gather enough for one day/a kham ~ ngah zo tuan lo hi | he never gets enough to be satisfied) (r:5.2.3/21.6.7/20.25.16/2.16.4) (q:draft)
khop = (t:v) (w:collect/gather) (d:bring together or gather in people, money or a harvest; the form of khawm used before words such as uh, ding and nading) (e:mite tung panin a ~ uh/sehsawm suah sehkhat a ~ uh ciangin | when they collect the tithes/mi honte ~ nading leh giahphual nusiat nadingin | for calling the people together and for breaking camp) (s:kaikhawm/khon) (r:12.22.4/16.10.38/4.10.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
khopa = (t:ppm) (d:postpositional marker to indicate objective case) (e:lo ~/Kain in lo ~ ahi hi | Cain was a tiller of the soil/Nakpi tak-a lo ~ hau mahmah a | one who works his land hard is very well off/Lo ~ in khaici dingin lo kho niloh | the farmer plowing all the time for sowing) (r:1.4.2/20.28.19/23.28.24)
khopa = (t:part) (d:particle suffixed to a noun to form verb past tense) (e:a kipat ~)
khopkhat = (t:adv) (w:somewhat/to some extent/a fair way) (d:placed after a describing word: to some degree, a certain amount; a gamla khopkhat, some distance away) (e:a gamla ~ a tun uh ciangin/a hoih ~ ciang khauhna a nei ding hi | it will have strength to some extent) (s:deuh) (r:7.18.22/27.2.41) (q:draft)
khopna = (t:n) (w:being together/union) (d:khop, together, with -na, placed after a verb: the doing of it together, as kipawl khopna, an alliance, and lup khopna, lying together as man and wife) (e:tua kipawl ~ kip lo ding a/lup ~ ding thu neihna khiam lo ding hi | he shall not reduce her marital rights/Lungdamna Thu khan’sakna-ah na kipawl ~ uh thu | your partnership in spreading the gospel/a om ~ om nawn lo hi | none of them were left together) (b:khop) (r:27.11.6/2.21.10/50.1.3/9.11.11) (q:draft)
khopna = (t:n) (w:gathering/collecting) (d:khop, gather, with -na: the gathering in of a harvest) (e:na pawi lohna munah na ~) (s:kaihkhopna) (b:khop) (r:40.25.24) (q:draft, low confidence)
khoppih = (t:adv) (w:together with) (d:placed after a verb, the action is done together with someone or something: lup khoppih lie with, sleep with; meek khoppih mix with) (e:pasal khat in a lup ~ leh/a meek ~ ding sathau hai khat | a measure of oil to mix with it/Hong kilup ~ lohna mun koi lai takah om | where is there a place you have not been lain with) (s:khawmpih) (b:khop) (r:3.19.20/26.46.14/24.3.2) (q:draft)
khopsak = (t:v) (w:gather/assemble/bring together) (d:khop, gather, with the causative sak: cause people to come together) (e:mi sawmsagih hong ~ in/Israel upate’ sung panin mi sawmsagih hong ~ in | gather for me seventy of the elders of Israel) (s:kaikhawm/khawmsak) (a:thehthang) (b:khop) (r:4.11.16) (q:draft)
khopsakin = (t:v) (w:gathering/assembling) (d:khopsak, gather, with the linking suffix in, before a further command) (e:sung panin mi sawmsagih hong ~/mi sawmsagih hong ~, kikhopna bukah amaute paipih inla | gather seventy men and bring them to the tent of meeting) (s:kaikhawmin) (b:khopsak) (r:4.11.16) (q:draft)
khopte = (t:n) (w:those gathered/those assembled) (d:khop, gather, with the plural te: the ones whom someone has gathered together) (e:leh Levi mi a ~ in/Aaron’ suante leh Levi mi a ~ in | the descendants of Aaron and the Levites whom he gathered) (b:khop) (r:13.15.4) (q:draft)
khopzah = (t:n) (w:as much as/enough for) (d:khop, enough, with zah, amount: khe a ta khopzah is as much ground as a foot can stand on) (e:khe a ta ~ zong no/khe a ta ~ zong no kong pia kei | I will not give you even enough to set a foot on) (r:5.2.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
Khorazin = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Chorazin) (d:town in Galilee near Capernaum that Jesus rebuked for not repenting) (r:42.10.13/40.11.21)
khosak = (t:v) (w:let farm/lease out) (d:kho, farm, with the causative sak: have someone else work a field or vineyard) (e:khawhlawh dangte ~ ding hi/lo khawhlawh dangte ~ ding hi | he will let other tenants farm the vineyard) (b:kho) (r:40.21.41) (q:draft)
khosak = (t:v) (w:urge/press/warn) (d:press someone strongly to do or not to do a thing) (e:ci-in nakpitakin a ~ uh hi/hong kilak het kei in, ci-in nakpitakin a ~ | they strongly urged him not to show himself) (s:khoh) (r:44.19.31) (q:draft, low confidence)
khotakin = (t:adv) (w:firmly/fast/steadfastly) (d:kho, firm, with takin, which makes an adverb: firmly; often with len, hold) (e:upna thu ~ lenin ka zokhin hi/Amah in lungsim ~ sep ding kipan a | he set to work with a firm heart/kiptak ~ i letkip ding kisam hi | we must hold on firmly/~ a len uh hi | they held to it firmly) (s:kiptakin/khauhtakin) (b:kho) (r:55.4.7/58.2.1/14.32.5/17.9.28) (q:draft)
khote = (t:n) (w:farmers/tillers/plowmen) (d:kho, farm, with the plural te: those who work the land, in lo khote, farmers or tenants) (e:Lo ~ in lei a kuih bangin/Lo ~ aw, dah un | despair, you farmers/tua lo a en dingin lo ~ sawl a | he sent farmers to look after the vineyard/lo ~ khawhlawhsakin gamdang ah pai a | he rented it to farmers and went abroad) (s:lokhote) (b:kho) (r:19.129.3/29.1.11/22.8.11/42.20.9) (q:draft)
khotte = (t:n) (w:proceeds/money collected) (d:in sum khotte, the money got in, here from selling possessions; khot seems to be the form of khon, collect, used before te) (e:tungah na sum ~ pia in/na sum ~, mizawngte tungah va pia lecin | if you give the proceeds to the poor) (s:sumkhotte) (r:42.18.22/40.19.21) (q:draft, low confidence)
khozo = (t:v) (w:restrain/hold back/withstand) (d:manage to check or hold back someone, by urging or by force; kho, urge or restrain, with zo, be able) (e:a biak loh nadingun a ~ liailiai uh/mihonte a gamdaih nadingin ~ a | he restrained the crowd so that they grew quiet/ahih manin amah a ~ ding | so that any could withstand him) (s:khamzo) (r:44.14.18/27.8.4/44.19.35) (q:draft, low confidence)
Khrih = (t:name) (w:Christ) (d:Christ, the Messiah, title of Jesus as the one anointed by God; the spelling used beside Khazih) (r:46.1.6/44.8.5)
khrisolait = (t:n) (c:stone) (w:chrysolite) (d:a precious stone, the seventh foundation stone of the new Jerusalem, counted among the suangmanpha, precious stones) (e:a sagihna-ah ~ suangmanpha/topaz, le jasper, ~, beryl, le onik | topaz and jasper, chrysolite, beryl and onyx) (s:khrysolite) (r:66.21.20/26.28.13) (q:draft)
khrisoprase = (t:n) (c:stone) (w:chrysolite/chrysoprase/turquoise) (d:precious stone, the tenth foundation stone of the new Jerusalem; chrysoprase, where the NIV has turquoise) (e:a sawmna-ah ~ suangmanpha | the tenth was chrysoprase) (r:66.21.20)
Khristian = (t:name) (w:Christian) (d:a follower of Christ, the name first given to the disciples at Antioch; also describes a thing as Christian, as in Khristian mipih, fellow Christian) (r:62.2.9/64.1.5)
Khristianpihte = (t:n) (w:fellow Christians/brothers and sisters) (d:Khristian with pih fellow and te plural: those who are Christians together with one; stands where the NIV has brothers and sisters) (e:Kei tawh a omkhawm i ~ in zong/bang hangin na ~ uh tungah thu khen a | why do you judge your fellow Christians/i ~ i puksak khak loh nading | so that we do not cause our fellow Christians to fall) (r:48.1.2/45.14.10/45.14.13) (q:draft)
Khristiante = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Christians) (d:Khristian with the plural te: Christians, believers in Christ; often stands where the English has brothers and sisters or in the Lord) (e:hih lai-a om ~ a tamzaw in) (b:Khristian) (r:50.1.14/64.1.8) (q:draft)
khrysolite = (t:n) (c:stone) (w:chrysolite) (d:precious stone, first of the fourth row on the breastpiece, where the NIV has topaz) (e:gual lina in ~ suang) (s:khrisolait) (r:2.28.20) (q:draft)
khu = (t:n) (w:smoke) (d:smoke rising from a fire or from incense; more often in the compound meikhu) (e:selkeu kikhul ~ tawh kibang hi/paknamtui ~ in zong tua vantungmi khut sung pan | the smoke of the incense also, from the hand of the angel/vanah a ~ kahto ngitnget ding hi | its smoke will rise up forever/a khuapi katna ~ a muh uh ciangin | when they see the smoke of the burning city) (s:meikhu) (r:18.41.20/66.8.4/23.34.10/66.18.18) (q:draft)
khu = (t:v) (w:smoke/smolder) (d:give off smoke, smolder; said twice, khu khu, for smoldering on and on) (e:mei beel ~ leh a kuang meivak/a hehna uh mei bangin ~ ~ a | their anger smolders like a fire) (r:1.15.17/28.7.6) (q:draft)
khu = (t:v) (w:wear/put on) (d:put on or wear something on the head, such as a hat, crown or helmet) (e:Gupna sik-lukhu ~ un la/David in tua lukhu ama lu tungah ~ hi | David put that crown on his own head/kham kumpilukhu a ~ upa sawmnih leh li | twenty-four elders wearing gold crowns/kham tawh kibawl kumpi lukhu lianpi ~-in | wearing a large crown of gold) (r:49.6.17/13.20.2/66.4.4/17.8.15) (q:draft)
khua = (t:ppm) (d:word indicating a particular mood of light or dark) (e:~mial/~vak/Ni tumin ~ a mial khit ciangin | when the sun had set and it was dark/Topa in ~ mialsak a | the Lord makes it dark/Zingsang ~ vak ciangin | when it grew light in the morning/~ a dam ciangin mi nih lumkhawm leh | when it is cold, if two lie down together) (r:1.15.17/24.13.16/1.19.15/21.4.11)
khua = (t:n) (w:city/town) (d:a town or city, a place where many people live together; khua sung is inside the town and khua mite are its people) (e:~pi/Tua ~ sungah lungdamna tampi a piang hi | there was great joy in that city/Zeisu in ~ nawl ah a paikhia hi | Jesus went out of the city/~ zangpi-in kongkhak kiangah a kikhawm uh hi | the whole town gathered at the door) (s:khuapi) (r:44.8.8/41.1.33/41.11.19)
khua = (t:n) (w:village) (d:a village or small settlement, often said with neu, small, or no, little) (e:~no/~neu/~ta/a khuapite leh a ~ neute tawh | with its towns and its villages/~ sungah na lut kei in | do not go into the village) (s:khuaneu) (r:6.15.45/41.8.26)
khua = (t:n) (w:seasonal/season) (d:the weather or time of year, in khua hun, season) (e:~hun/tuate pen pawi hun leh ~ hun | let them mark festival times and seasons) (r:1.1.14)
Khua = (t:n) (w:town/city/village) (d:khua written with a capital, in a title or at the start of a sentence; Shiloh Khua Mi is the man of the town of Shiloh, the Shilonite) (e:le Shiloh ~ Mi Ahijah’ Thugen/~ sung upate a kikhop ciangin | when the elders of the town gathered/~ khat sungah a lut lai takin | as he was going into a village) (b:khua) (r:14.9.29/18.29.7/42.17.12) (q:draft)
khua niim = (t:n) (w:gloom/overcast) (d:dull, overcast weather, when the sky is dark with cloud) (e:sanin ~ ahih manin guah zu/~ leh khuamial in khuhcip hen | let gloom and darkness cover it) (r:40.16.3/18.3.5)
khua-ul = (t:n) (w:sweat/perspiration) (d:the moisture that comes out of the skin in heat or hard work; khua-ul kai is to sweat) (e:na maitang-ah ~ tawh an na ne ding/~ in lei tungah sisan malgol bangin a kia hi | his sweat fell to the ground like great drops of blood/na puan sungah ~ kai-in na om hi | you swelter in your clothes/~ a suaksak thei kawnggak gak lo ding | they must not wear a belt that makes them sweat) (r:1.3.19/42.22.44/18.37.17/26.44.18) (q:draft)
Khuabul = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Khuabul/Foundation) (d:the Foundation Gate in Jerusalem, Khuabul Kulh kongpi, where a third of the guards were posted when Joash was made king) (r:14.23.5)
khuacing = (t:n) (w:guard/town guard/watchman) (d:khua, town, with cing, guard: one who keeps watch over a town or a post; khuacing mite are the men of an outpost) (e:~ mite in Jonathan leh a galhiam/~ dingte seh un la | appoint those who are to be guards) (s:galvil) (r:9.14.12/16.7.3) (q:draft)
khuacingin = (t:v) (w:guarding/keeping guard/defending) (d:khuacing, guard a town, with the linking ending in: keeping guard over a town, defending it) (e:Israel khempeuh tawh ~ Joram om hi) (b:khuacing) (r:12.9.14) (q:draft)
khuacingte = (t:n) (w:garrison/outpost/watchmen/guards) (d:plural of khuacing, those who guard a town; a body of soldiers stationed in a place) (e:Efraim khuapite sungah ~ koih hi/Filistia ~ Bethelehem ah om uh hi | the Philistine garrison was at Bethlehem/Geba-ah a om Filistia ~ zo hi | he defeated the Philistine outpost at Geba/kulhzang-a a kileh den ~ in | the watchmen who go about on the walls) (s:galvilte/cingte) (b:khuacing) (r:14.17.2/22.5.7/10.23.14/9.13.3) (q:draft)
khuadak = (t:v) (w:look/look up/look around) (d:khua, the surroundings, with dak, look: raise the eyes and look around; khuadak to is look up and khuadak kawikawi is look all around) (e:Ka ~ leh saki li ka mu hi/ka kongvangneu panin ka ~ a | I looked out through my window/amaute a ~ uh leh | when they looked up/Tua lai mun panin ~ kawikawi a | from there it looks all around) (s:dak/en) (r:38.1.18/20.7.6/40.17.8/18.39.29) (q:draft)
khuadakdak = (t:v) (w:keep looking/look and look) (d:khuadak, look, with dak repeated for an action that goes on: keep looking) (e:ngenin ka ~ uh a) (s:etet/enen) (r:25.4.17) (q:draft)
khuadakin = (t:v) (w:looking/looking up/looking around) (d:khuadak, look, with in, the linking form before a following verb: looking up or around and then doing something) (e:Filistiapa ~ David a muh ciangin/amaute ~ thuciamna singkuang a muh uh ciangin | when they looked up and saw the ark of the covenant/Ka kiim ka pam ~ ka en kawikawi a | I look all around me/amah ~ khuapi panin mite a kuankhia mu a | he looked and saw the people coming out of the city) (s:dakin/enin) (b:khuadak) (r:9.17.42/9.6.13/19.142.4/7.9.43) (q:draft)
khuadakna = (t:n) (w:watch/lookout/looking out) (d:khuadak, look around, with the noun ending na: keeping a lookout; khuadakna tausang is a watchtower) (e:Ka ~ tausang tungah) (s:galvilna) (b:khuadak) (r:35.2.1) (q:draft)
khuadaksuk = (t:v) (w:look down) (d:khuadak, look, with suk, downward: look down from a higher place) (e:Araunah a ~ ciangin kumpipa) (s:ensuk/etsuk) (a:khuadakto) (b:khuadak) (r:10.24.20) (q:draft)
khuadakto = (t:v) (w:look up/lift the eyes) (d:khuadak, look around, with to, up) (e:Na kimkotah ~ inla mu in/nisuahna lamah ~ inla | look toward the east/Jesuh ~-in numei kiangah | Jesus, looking up, to the woman) (s:dakto/ento/khuadaktoh) (a:khuadaksuk) (b:khuadak) (r:23.49.18/5.3.27/43.8.10) (q:draft)
khuadaktoh = (t:v) (w:look up) (d:khuadak, look, with toh, upward: the form of khuadakto used before leh) (e:Ka ~ leh gun gei-ah tuutal khat/a ~ leh, ama mai-ah mi thum na ding hi | when he looked up, three men were standing before him/Joshua a tun ciangin a ~ leh | when Joshua arrived and looked up) (s:ettoh/khuadakto) (a:khuadaksuk) (b:khuadakto) (r:27.8.3/1.18.2/6.5.13) (q:draft)
khuadakzo = (t:v) (w:be able to look) (d:khuadak look with zo be able; with nawn lo, no longer able to look) (e:~ nawn lo zah dongin) (b:khuadak) (r:25.4.17) (q:draft)
khuadam = (t:n) (w:cold/cold weather) (d:khua, the weather, with dam, cold: cold weather or the feeling of cold) (e:~ lai taka puan suahkhiat/~ thuakna, puan nei lo-a omna | enduring cold and being without clothing/khuavak, ~, vukkiat cihte om nawn lo ding | there will be no more light, cold or frost) (s:votna) (r:20.25.20/47.11.27/38.14.6) (q:draft)
khuadampi = (t:n) (w:great cold/bitter cold) (d:khuadam, cold, with pi, great: severe cold) (e:~ lakah silh ding nei loin) (b:khuadam) (r:18.24.7) (q:draft)
khuadang = (t:n) (w:another town/other town) (d:khua town with dang other) (e:~ khatah tai un) (r:40.10.23) (q:draft)
khuadangte = (t:see) <khuadangte-ah>
khuadangte-ah = (t:n) (w:to the other towns/in the other villages) (d:khuadang other town with plural te and the place marker ah) (e:Hih kiimnai-a om ~ pai ni) (r:41.1.38) (q:draft)
khuadon = (t:v) (w:expect/watch/be on the lookout) (d:in the verse with lo: khuadon lo is not expecting, not watching) (e:~ lo leh a theih loh kalin) (r:40.24.50) (q:draft, low confidence)
khuadum = (t:n) (w:blue yarn/blue material) (d:the material of which the loops of the tabernacle curtains were made) (e:~ tawh a bilvangte bawl hi) (r:2.36.11) (q:draft, low confidence, perhaps a misprint for khau dum, blue thread)
khuagei = (t:n) (w:vicinity/outskirts/edge of town) (d:khua, town, with gei, edge or side: the area at the edge of a town) (e:Bethany ~ ciang amaute paipih a) (s:khuanawl/khuakiim) (r:42.24.50) (q:draft)
khuahek = (t:n) (w:conduct/manner/behaviour) (d:paired with gamtat, way of living) (e:a gamtat a ~ uh a zahtakhuai) (r:56.2.3) (q:draft, low confidence, meaning taken from the pairing with gamtat)
khuahsak = (t:v) (w:harden/strengthen) (d:make hard or strong: lungsim khuahsak, harden the heart, tha khuahsak, strengthen; the same in meaning as khauhsak) (e:na lungsim uh na ~ kei un/amah tha ~ zaw loin gimsak zaw hi | he troubled him rather than strengthening him) (s:khauhsak) (r:58.3.7/14.28.20) (q:draft)
khuahun = (t:n) (w:state/condition)
khuahun = (t:n) (w:climate)
khuahun = (t:n) (w:weather) (d:the state of the weather at a given time; khuahun hoih is good weather) (e:~ hoih dong a ngak mi in) (r:21.11.4)
khuahunte = (t:n) (w:seasons/times) (d:plural of khuahun: the seasons of the year, in hun leh khuahunte, times and seasons) (e:Amah in hun leh ~ kheel) (s:hunte) (b:khuahun) (r:27.2.21) (q:draft)
khuai = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:bee) (d:the honey bee; khuai hon is a swarm of bees and khuaizu is honey) (e:~ bangin hong delhin hong zo uh hi/sungah ~ honkhat leh khuaizu om hi | in it were a swarm of bees and honey) (s:khuaipi) (r:5.1.44/7.14.8) (q:draft)
khuaibu = (t:n) (w:honeycomb/bees' nest) (d:khuai, bee, with bu, nest: the comb in which bees store honey) (e:sakin ~ sungah diah a) (s:khuailuzu) (r:9.14.27) (q:draft)
khuailuzu = (t:n) (w:honeycomb/honey from the comb) (d:honey still in the comb, named beside khuaizu, honey, as the sweetest of foods) (e:khuaizu leh ~ tak sangin zong/Ka khuaizu leh ka ~ ka ne a | I have eaten my honey and my honeycomb/~ in i kam-ah khum mahmah hi | honey from the comb is very sweet in our mouth) (s:khuaibu/khuaipizu) (r:19.19.10/20.24.13/22.5.1) (q:draft)
khuaimeivak = (t:n) (w:candle/lamp) (d:khuai bee, wax, with meivak lamp: khuaimeivak vakna khuam is a lampstand) (e:~ vakna khuamte) (r:24.52.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
khuainun = (t:n) (w:wax/beeswax) (d:the wax made by bees, which melts before the fire) (e:mei mai-ah ~ a tui bangin/mualliante in ~ bangin tui suak uh hi | the mountains melt like wax/ka lungtang ~ bang a | my heart is like wax/Meikhuk sunga ~ kikoih bangin | like wax put into a furnace) (r:19.68.2/19.97.5/19.22.14/33.1.4) (q:draft)
khuaipi = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:bee) (d:a swarming, stinging bee; khuaipi nam tunpi is used for the hornet) (e:~ bangin kei hong umcih uh a/a gam panun ~ hon bangin hong pai nadingun | to come from their land like a swarm of bees/amaute lakah ~ nam tunpi khah ding hi | he will send the hornet among them) (s:khuai) (b:khuai) (r:19.118.12/23.7.18/5.7.20) (q:draft)
khuaipizu = (t:n) (w:honey/honeycomb) (d:khuaipi, bee, with zu, liquid: honey, the honeycomb of the NIV) (e:Kam khum in ~ bang hi a) (s:khuaizu/khuailuzu) (r:20.16.24) (q:draft)
khuaisuahna = (t:n) (w:loss/bereavement) (d:the losing of a child by death, in ta khuaisuahna, loss of children) (e:ta ~ leh meigon’na) (r:23.47.9) (q:draft)
khuaisuahte = (t:n) (w:those bereaved/those who have lost) (d:khuaisuah, lose a child by death, with te: people who have lost a child) (e:a tacil a ~ bangin) (r:38.12.10) (q:draft)
khuaizu = (t:n) (w:honey) (d:khuai, bee, with zu, liquid: honey; the promised land is described as flowing with bawngnawi leh khuaizu, milk and honey) (e:bawngnawi leh ~ a luan’na hih gam/~ sangin ka kam-ah khumzaw hi | sweeter than honey to my mouth/lei lakah ~ om hi | there was honey on the ground/~ khum ahih manin ne in | eat honey, for it is sweet) (s:khuaipizu) (r:24.32.22/19.119.103/9.14.25/20.24.13) (q:draft)
khuak = (t:v) (w:hew/chisel/carve/cut out) (d:cut into rock or a hard surface, as a tomb in rock; khuak-in at is to engrave) (e:a ~ han sungah amaute in vui/na om nading suang a ~ mipa aw | you who carve your dwelling in the rock/biakna tau kite tungah ~-in ki-at hi | it is engraved on the horns of the altars) (r:14.16.14/23.22.16/24.17.1) (q:draft)
khuakehte = (t:n) (w:hamlets/countryside/farms) (d:named after khuapi city and khuaneu village as the smallest kind of settlement) (e:le ~ a a paina khempeuhah) (r:41.6.56) (q:draft, low confidence)
khuakhal = (t:n) (w:summer) (d:the hot, dry season of the year, summer; in some verses the NIV has spring) (e:~ sungin a nek ding uh/~ a nai zo hi ci-in | that summer is near/phalbi hun leh ~ hunte na bawl khin hi | you made both winter and summer/~ ciangin Siria kumpipa nangmah do-in | in the spring the king of Aram will attack you) (s:khualkhal) (a:phalbi) (r:20.6.8/42.21.30/19.74.17/11.20.22) (q:draft)
khuakhua = (t:see) <khuakhua-in>
khuakhua-in = (t:adv) (w:town by town) (d:khua town repeated, with in) (e:tua gam a ~ a ciaptehna uh) (r:6.18.9) (q:draft)
khuakiim = (t:n) (w:vicinity/surrounding area) (d:khua town with kiim around: the country round a town) (e:Taia ~ gamah a pai hi/Taia ~ gam panin Jesuh paikhia a | Jesus left the vicinity of Tyre) (s:kiimnai/khuagei) (r:41.7.24/41.7.31) (q:draft)
khuakin = (t:v) (w:engraving/carving) (d:khuak carve with linking in: khuakin ki-at is be engraved) (e:tau kite tungah ~ ki-at hi) (b:khuak) (r:24.17.1) (q:draft)
khuakongpi = (t:n) (w:city gate/gate) (d:khua, town, with kongpi, main gate: the gate of a walled town) (e:a ~ a kikalhna siktawnte) (s:kulhkongpi/kongpi) (r:24.51.30) (q:draft)
khuakongpite = (t:n) (w:city gates/gates) (d:plural of khuakongpi: the gates of a walled town) (e:a sang mahmah ~ zong mei tawh) (s:kulhkongpite/kongpite) (b:khuakongpi) (r:24.51.58) (q:draft)
khuakulh = (t:n) (w:city wall/wall) (d:khua, town, with kulh, wall: the wall built round a town for its defence) (e:~ khat ka kan thei hi/Damaskas ~ kongpi cingsak a | he had the gate of the wall of Damascus guarded/zanin ~ tungah kahtohpihin | taking him up onto the city wall by night/Kei, ~ ka hi a | I am a wall) (s:kulh/khuakulhpi/khuapikulh) (r:19.18.29/10.22.30/47.11.32/44.9.25/22.8.10) (q:draft)
khuakulhah = (t:n) (w:on the city wall/at the wall) (d:khuakulh city wall with the place marker ah) (e:Bethshan ~ ama luang a suang uh hi) (b:khuakulh) (r:9.31.10) (q:draft)
khuakulhpi = (t:n) (w:city wall) (d:khuakulh, city wall, with pi, great: the great wall round a town) (e:Babylon ~ tungah dial khai unla/Tua ciangin ~ kiphulet a | then the city wall was broken through/Babylon ~ kicim khinta hi | the wall of Babylon has fallen/sumngo a kibawl ~ kong bangsak ding a | I will make you like a fortified wall of bronze) (s:kulhpi/khuapikulh/khuakulh) (b:khuakulh) (r:24.51.12/24.52.7/24.51.44/24.15.20) (q:draft)
khual = (t:v) (w:journey) (d:away from home, on a journey: used with zin, travel, as in khual gamlapi-ah zin, go on a long journey) (e:ka pasal ~ gamlapi-ah zin a/ka khedapte uh ~ gamlapi zinna-in | our sandals, by the very long journey/Gedor lutna lamah ~ zin uh a | they travelled toward the entrance of Gedor) (s:zin) (r:20.7.19/6.9.13/13.4.39)
khualkhal = (t:n) (w:summer) (d:the dry season: khualkhal hun is summertime; written khuakhal elsewhere) (e:~ hun-a ansi zap bangin) (s:khuakhal) (a:phalbi) (r:27.2.35) (q:draft, perhaps a misprint for khuakhal)
khualmi = (t:n) (w:stranger/foreigner/sojourner) (d:khual, away from home, with mi, person: someone living in a place that is not his own) (e:meigong numei leh ~ thatlum uh a/ka innkuanpihte lakah ~ ka suak hi | I have become a stranger among my own family/note lakah ~ khat hong peem leh | when a foreigner comes to live among you/~ na hih laitakin hong mu-in | seeing you when you were a stranger) (s:peemta/mikhual/gamdangmi/khualmipa) (b:khual) (r:19.94.6/4.15.26/19.69.8/3.19.33/40.25.38) (q:draft)
khualmipa = (t:n) (w:foreigner/sojourner/stranger) (d:khualmi, foreigner, with pa, which marks a man: a foreigner living among the people) (e:amah tawh a om ~ tawh ahi zongin/amaute’ lakah a peem ~ a dingin | for the foreigner residing among them/~ innkuan khatpeuh peuh tungah | to any member of the foreigner’s family) (s:khualpa/khualmi) (b:khualmi) (r:5.1.16/4.15.29/3.25.47) (q:draft)
khualmite = (t:n) (w:strangers/foreigners/sojourners) (d:plural of khualmi: people from elsewhere who live among another people) (e:~ in na neih khempeuh uh la ding/~ in a om lai sunsunte sut ta hen | may strangers plunder what he has left/nangma mai-ah ~ le pemtate ka hi uh hi | we are foreigners and strangers before you/Nang in ~’ gamlumna na daisak hi | you silence the uproar of foreigners) (s:peemtate/mikhualte/khualte) (b:khualmi) (r:20.5.10/4.35.15/19.109.11/13.29.15/23.25.5) (q:draft)
khualna = (t:n) (w:concern/regard/consideration/sake) (d:khual, have regard for, with the noun suffix na: care or regard for someone; ka khualna-in means for the sake of) (e:tua bang ~ thei lo uh hi/Keimah nong ~-un tangvalpa Absalom hong dawm mahmah un | for my sake be gentle with the young man Absalom/Topa i Pasian’ inn ka ~-in | for the sake of the house of the Lord our God/ka nasempa David ka ~-in | for the sake of my servant David) (s:thukhualna/kikhualna) (r:20.29.7/19.122.8/10.18.5/19.122.9/23.37.35) (q:draft)
khualpa = (t:n) (w:foreigner/stranger/sojourner) (d:khual, away from home, with pa, which marks a man: a man from elsewhere living among the people) (e:amah tawh a om mi ~ tawh) (s:khualmipa/khualmi) (b:khual) (r:5.1.16) (q:draft)
khualte = (t:n) (w:strangers/foreigners/sojourners) (d:khual with the plural te; in mi khualte, people from elsewhere who live among another people) (e:a hong peem mi ~ leh note/a peem mi ~ sung pan hita leh | or from the foreigners residing among them) (s:khualmite/peemtate) (b:khual) (r:3.25.45/3.17.10) (q:draft)
khualte = (t:n) (w:those who have regard for/those who consider) (d:khual, have regard or concern for, with te, those who) (e:Mi genthei a ~ thupha ngah) (b:khual) (r:19.41.1) (q:draft)
khualum = (t:v) (w:be warm/keep warm) (d:khua, the weather or surroundings, with lum warm: feel warm) (e:khat guak bangci ~ theih ding/~ gilvah takin om in | keep warm and well fed) (r:21.4.11/59.2.16) (q:draft)
khualutna = (t:n) (w:town entrance/entrance to the town) (d:khua town with lutna entering: Hamath khualutna is the entrance of Hamath, the NIV Lebo Hamath) (e:Hamath ~ tawh a kitang ciang) (r:26.47.20) (q:draft)
khualzin = (t:v) (w:travel) (d:khual, away from home, with zin, travel: go on a journey) (e:A ~ sung tawntung uh/Abram in a ~ zom lai a | Abram continued his journey/Beth-el panin amaute ~ hi | they set out from Bethel/a siang mi khat ~ lo napi-in | though a clean person is not on a journey) (s:zin/lampai) (r:2.40.36/4.9.13/1.12.9/1.35.16)
khualzin = (t:v) (w:tour)
khualzin = (t:v) (w:trip) (e:Na ~ nadingun lam-an bawl un la | prepare provisions for your journey) (r:6.9.11)
Khualzin = (t:v) (w:travel) (d:khualzin written with a capital at the start of a sentence or in a place name, as Khualzin Mite’ Kuam, the valley of the travellers) (e:a om ~ Mite’ Kuam a cihna sungteng/~ mi khempeuh ka inn-ah ka tungsak tawntung a | I always took every traveller into my house/~ ka hih lai takin zin nong do uh hi | when I was a stranger you welcomed me) (b:khualzin) (r:26.39.11/18.31.32/40.25.35) (q:draft)
khualzinin = (t:v) (w:travelling/on a journey) (d:khualzin, travel, with in joining it to the next verb: while travelling, on a journey) (e:~ gamlapi-ah a om ahi zongin/Samaria mi khat in ~ a pai lai takin | as a Samaritan was travelling/Hih gam sungah ~ hanthotna tampi | travelling through that region with many words of encouragement/zan hita leh ~ a pai theih nadingun | so that they could travel on even by night) (s:zinin) (b:khualzin) (r:4.9.10/42.10.33/44.20.2/2.13.21) (q:draft)
khualzinna = (t:n) (w:journey/travel) (d:khualzin, travel, with the noun suffix na: a journey) (e:Jakob in a ~ zom a/nang adingin ~ haksa lua ding hi | the journey will be too hard for you/A gamla na ~ tawh nang na gim a | you wearied yourself with your long journey) (s:zinna/lampaina) (b:khualzin) (r:1.29.1/1.24.21/11.19.7/23.57.10) (q:draft)
khualzinpa = (t:n) (w:traveler/wayfarer) (d:khualzin travel with pa, a man: a man on a journey) (e:~ khuapi kongzingah mu hi/ama kiangah a tung ~’ adingin | for the traveller who had come to him) (b:khualzin) (r:7.19.17/10.12.4) (q:draft)
khualzinpihte = (t:n) (w:traveling companions/fellow travelers) (d:khualzin travel with pih, together with, and plural te) (e:nang le na ~ khempeuh/Makedonia pana Paul’ ~, Gaias leh Aristarkhus | Paul’s travelling companions from Macedonia, Gaius and Aristarchus) (r:44.27.24/44.19.29) (q:draft)
khualzinte = (t:n) (w:travelers/wayfarers/strangers) (d:khualzin, travel, with plural -te: people on a journey) (e:Ka inn-ah ~ ka tungsak a/~ lam gei-ah pial uh hi | travellers turned aside to the byways/Tema khua mi ~ in zong | the travellers of Tema too/~, mi peemte bang ahi note | you who are like travellers and sojourners) (b:khualzin) (r:18.31.32/7.5.6/18.6.19/60.2.11) (q:draft)
khualzinzin = (t:v) (w:travel) (d:khualzin with the last part doubled: travel about, keep travelling) (e:~ mite tawh kiho ngei lo) (b:khualzin) (r:18.21.29)
Khualzinzin = (t:v) (w:travel) (d:khualzinzin written with a capital at the start of a sentence; khualzin with the last part doubled, travel about) (e:~ mite tawh kiho ngei lo) (b:khualzinzin) (r:18.21.29) (q:draft)
khuam = (t:n) (w:pillar/post/pole) (d:an upright post or pillar: a house post, a doorpost, a pole, or a stone set up as a memorial) (e:Na inn kongkhak ~ tung uh leh/sun-a meii ~ leh zan-a mei khuamte | the pillar of cloud by day and the pillars of fire by night/ka phuhsa hih suangcian leh ~ mu in | see this heap and this pillar that I have set up/~ khat tungah khai hi | he put it up on a pole) (s:khuampi/innkhuam) (r:5.6.9/2.13.22/1.31.51/4.21.9) (q:draft)
khuami = (t:n) (w:townsman/inhabitant/citizen) (d:khua, town, with mi, person: a person of a town or village; after a place name it means a person from that place) (e:Karmel ~ Hezro, Arbi mi Pa-arai/Shekhem ~ khempeuh huau-in gen un | say in the hearing of all the citizens of Shechem/Nebo ~ sawmnga-le-nih ahi hi | the men of Nebo were fifty-two/Netofah ~ Maharai | Maharai the Netophathite) (b:khua) (r:10.23.35/15.2.29/7.9.2/10.23.28) (q:draft)
KHUAMI = (t:n) (w:townsman/person of) (d:khuami written in capitals in the inscription on the cross; after a place name, a person from that town) (e:NAZARETH ~ ZEISU AHI HI | he is Jesus of Nazareth) (r:43.19.19) (q:draft)
khuamial = (t:n) (w:dark) (d:the state of being without light; khuamial ding is it will be dark) (e:Ama buk sungah ~ ding a/na lamet uh khuavak pen ~ bikbek a suah ma-in | before the light you hope for turns to utter darkness) (s:khim) (a:khuavak) (r:18.18.6/1.1.4/24.13.16)
khuamial = (t:n) (w:darkness) (d:khua, the surroundings, with mial, dark: darkness, the absence of light) (e:khuavak leh ~ khen hi/~ in amah a zo zo kei hi | the darkness has not overcome it/a thuk semsem ~ sungah a hong hawlkhia hi | he has driven me into ever deeper darkness/~ tawh a vialcippa | the one who wrapped it in darkness) (s:khuamialna/mialna/khim) (a:khuavak) (r:18.26.10/1.1.4/43.1.5/25.3.2/18.38.9)
khuamialna = (t:n) (w:darkness) (d:khuamial, dark, with the noun suffix na: darkness, also as a picture of trouble and of not seeing) (e:lungkhamna leh ~ hong tung zawsop hi/khuavakna mun panin ~-ah kihawl khia ding hi | he is driven from the place of light into darkness/A thuk tuipi tung tengah ~ om a | darkness was over the surface of the deep/gamdai takin tu in la, ~ sungah pai in | sit in silence and go into darkness) (s:khuamial/mialna) (a:khuavakna) (b:khuamial) (r:18.30.26/1.1.2/18.18.18/23.47.5)
khuamialpi = (t:n) (w:deep darkness/thick darkness) (d:khuamial, darkness, with pi, great: deep darkness) (e:~ sungah nong paihdak) (s:khuazing) (b:khuamial) (r:19.44.18) (q:draft)
khuamin = (t:adv) (w:as a pillar) (d:khuam pillar with the marker in: set up as a pillar) (e:suang khat la-in ~ phut hi/lukhamin a zat suang la-in ~ phut a | he took the stone he had used as a pillow and set it up as a pillar/~ ka phuhsa hih suang | this stone that I have set up as a pillar) (b:khuam) (r:1.31.45/1.28.18/1.28.22) (q:draft)
khuamin = (t:n) (w:name of the town) (d:khua town and min name written as one word) (e:a masa-in tua ~ pen Luz ahi hi) (r:1.28.19) (q:draft)
khuamite = (t:n) (w:inhabitants/townspeople/citizens) (d:plural of khuami: the people of a town or city) (e:Judah minamte leh Jerusalem ~ in/a innkuanpihte le a ~ kihta lua ahih manin | because he was very afraid of his family and the townspeople/Shekhem ~ tungah kumpi-in na bawl uh hi | you have made him king over the citizens of Shechem) (s:khuapihte/teengte) (b:khuami) (r:24.11.9/38.13.1/7.6.27/7.9.18) (q:draft)
khuamkua = (t:n) (w:post hole/foundation hole) (d:khuam post with kua hole: the hole dug for a house post) (e:a ~ ding suangsung thukpi tak) (r:42.6.48) (q:draft, low confidence)
khuamlu = (t:n) (w:capital/top of a pillar) (d:khuam, pillar, with lu, head: the top of a post or pillar) (e:a ~ zepnate a kizutna zong ngun/a ~ zepnate leh a gaknate | the overlay of their tops and their bands) (s:khuampiluzang/khuamluzepna) (r:2.38.17/2.38.19) (q:draft)
khuamluzepna = (t:n) (w:capital) (d:the ornamental top of a pillar, from khuam pillar, lu head and zepna decoration) (e:khuampite dawnah a om ~ kuak nihte/a dawn tuakah tong nga a pha ~ | a capital five cubits high on top of each/a kisung sumngo ~ nih zong bawl hi | he also made two capitals of cast bronze) (s:khuamlu/khuampiluzang) (r:11.7.41/11.7.16/14.3.15) (q:draft)
khuamluzepnate = (t:n) (w:capitals/pillar tops) (d:plural of khuamluzepna: the ornamented heads of pillars or posts) (e:khuampi dawnah a om ~ tong li pha/a ~ le a gaknate a kizutna ngun | their tops and their bands were overlaid with silver) (b:khuamluzepna) (r:11.7.19/2.38.19) (q:draft)
khuampeek = (t:n) (w:frame/board) (d:khuam, post, with peek, flat board: an upright wooden frame or board of the tabernacle wall) (e:amah in ~ guk bawl hi/a ~ nih na bawl ding hi | you shall make two frames/leitaw lam pang adingin ~ sawmnih hi ding hi | there shall be twenty frames for the south side) (r:2.36.27/2.26.23/2.26.18) (q:draft)
khuampeekte = (t:n) (w:frames/boards) (d:plural of khuampeek: the upright wooden frames that form the walls of the tabernacle) (e:Biakbuk ~ na bawl ding hi/Amah in ~ kham tawh zutin | he overlaid the frames with gold/a ~ phut a, a zawlte khumin | he set up its frames and put in its crossbars) (b:khuampeek) (r:2.26.18/2.26.15/2.36.34/2.40.18) (q:draft)
khuamphuhna = (t:n) (w:foundation) (d:setting up of house posts, the foundation someone has laid) (e:Midangte ~ tungah ka lam loh) (r:45.15.20) (q:draft)
