Khuampi = (t:n) (w:pillar) (d:khuampi written with a capital at the start of a sentence or in Khuampi Innpi, the Hall of Pillars built by Solomon, colonnade in the NIV) (e:amah in ~ Innpi bawl hi/~ khat a sauna in tong sawm-le-giat hi a | one pillar was eighteen cubits high) (b:khuampi) (r:11.7.6/11.7.15) (q:draft)
khuampiluzang = (t:n) (w:top of the pillar/capital) (d:khuampi main pillar with luzang top of the head) (e:biakinn ~ nakpitakin satgawp in) (s:khuamluzepna/khuamlu) (r:30.9.1) (q:draft)
khuampite = (t:n) (w:pillars/posts) (d:plural of khuampi: the pillars of a building, the posts of the tabernacle court, and in poetry the pillars of the earth and the sky) (e:Tua bangin ~ a bawl man khin hi/a ~ kiliing hi | its pillars tremble/vanpi a pua ~ a tai ciangin | when he rebukes the pillars that hold up the heavens/a ~ leh a bullente tawh | with its posts and its bases) (s:khuamte/innkhuamte) (b:khuampi) (r:11.7.22/18.26.11/18.9.6/2.35.17) (q:draft)
khuamte = (t:n) (w:pillars/posts) (d:plural of khuam: pillars or posts, also the posts of a door frame, kongkhak khuamte) (e:ama gihna tawh a ~ luai hi/biakinnpi sunga a om sumngo ~ | the bronze pillars that were in the temple/A luai ~, ngun tawh kizut a | its posts were overlaid with silver/a ~ sawmnih leh a bullente sawmnih | its twenty posts and twenty bases) (s:khuampite/innkhuamte) (b:khuam) (r:7.16.29/22.3.10/24.52.17/2.27.10) (q:draft)
khuamu = (t:v) (w:see/have sight) (d:khua, the surroundings, with mu, see: have sight; khuamu thei lo is unable to see, blind) (e:milim a biate in ~ thei lo) (s:mu) (r:23.44.9) (q:draft)
khuamuh = (t:v) (w:see/have sight) (d:khua, the surroundings, with muh, a form of mu see; in the verses always khuamuh nading, for seeing) (e:Topa in ~ nading mit/mit ~ nadingin nuh ding mit-za | salve to put on the eyes so that they see/zan ciangin ~ nadingin mei om sak hi | at night he gave fire to see by) (b:khuamu) (r:20.20.12/66.3.18/19.105.39) (q:draft)
khuamui = (t:n) (w:twilight/dusk/nightfall) (d:the time just after sunset when the light is fading; khuamui hun is the hour of dusk) (e:~ hun laitak ahi hi/a gawh ding hun nitak ~ | the time to slaughter them, at evening twilight/~ ciangin note in sa na ne ding uh | at twilight you will eat meat) (a:phalvak/khuavakkuan) (r:20.7.9/2.12.6/2.16.12) (q:draft)
khuan = (t:v) (w:crow) (d:of a rooster; the form of khuang used before ma-in, before, and laitak, at the time of) (e:tuzan ak a ~ ma-in thumvei/Ak ~’ ma-in nang in thumvei nong nial ding | before the rooster crows you will deny me three times/aak nihvei a ~’ ma-in | before the rooster crows twice/ak ~’ laitak ahi zongin | or at the time the rooster crows) (r:40.26.34/41.14.30/40.26.75/41.13.35) (q:draft)
khuan = (t:v) (w:stretch out) (d:stretch out the legs, in the phrase khe khuan; said of a bed too short to stretch out on) (e:khe ~’ nadingin lupna tom lua a) (r:23.28.20) (q:draft, low confidence)
khuan = (t:n) (w:permission/leave) (d:leave to go, asked of a superior; khuan ngen is to ask for leave) (e:kumpipa kiangah a ~ ka ngen a) (s:phalna) (r:16.13.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
khuanai = (t:n) (w:vicinity of a town/near the town) (d:khua town with nai near: the area close to a town; Jerusalem khuanai is near Jerusalem) (e:Bethfage le Bethany ~ a tun ciangin/Jerusalem ~, Bethfage khua a omna Oliv Mual | near Jerusalem, at the Mount of Olives where Bethphage is/Jerusalem ~, Bethfage le Bethany khuaneute a omna | near Jerusalem, where the villages of Bethphage and Bethany are) (s:khuagei) (r:42.19.29/40.21.1/41.11.1) (q:draft)
khuanawl = (t:n) (w:outskirts/edge of town/outside the town) (d:the outer edge of a town or village and the area just beyond it) (e:~ inn tawpna-ah amaute khawl uh hi/~ gampa lakah a om hi | he stayed outside the town in lonely places/a vekpi-un ~ ciang hong zui uh hi | they all came with us to the edge of the town/pawlpi mite in ~ ciang va kha uh a | the church people saw them off to the edge of the town) (s:khuagei) (a:khuasung) (r:10.15.17/44.21.5/41.1.45/44.15.3) (q:draft)
khuanawlah = (t:adv) (w:outside the town/out of the town) (d:khuanawl, the edge of a town, with ah, to or at) (e:khut lenin ~ a paipih hi/~ a kaikhia uh hi | they dragged him out of the town/Amaute dingin ~ Jesuh paipih uh a | they got up and took Jesus out of the town) (b:khuanawl) (r:41.8.23/44.14.19/42.4.29) (q:draft)
khuaneu = (t:n) (w:village/small town) (d:khua, town, and neu, small; set against khuapi, city) (e:khuapi leh ~ ah pai kawikawi a/a kimkot ~ leh lo lai-ah pai-in | going to the surrounding villages and fields/ki-uum lo ~ tampite | many unwalled villages/gamsung khuapi, ~ khempeuh ah vak kawikawi a | he went about all the towns and villages of the land) (a:khuapi) (r:42.13.22/41.6.36/5.3.5/40.9.35) (q:draft)
khuaneupen = (t:n) (w:smallest town/very small town) (d:khuaneu, small town, with pen, most: the smallest of the towns) (e:Judah gamah ~ khat na hi a) (b:khuaneu) (r:33.5.2) (q:draft)
khuaneute = (t:n) (w:villages/settlements) (d:small towns around a larger town) (e:Be-ersheba leh a ~/khuapi lote leh a ~ | the fields of the city and its villages/a khuapite leh a ~ tawh | with their towns and their villages/Netofah mite’ ~ panin | from the villages of the Netophathites) (a:khuapite) (r:16.11.27/13.6.56/6.13.28/16.12.28) (q:draft)
khuang = (t:n) (w:drum/timbrel/tambourine) (d:a drum or hand drum, played with singing and dancing) (e:~ leh laamna tawh amah phat un/a khut-ah ~ khat tawi hi | she took a timbrel in her hand/~ leh laiza tawh kong kha ding hi | I would have sent you off with timbrels and harps/Lungdamna ~ gingte daii-in | the joyful timbrels are stilled) (s:khuangneu/khuangno) (r:19.150.4/19.149.3/2.15.20/1.31.27/23.24.8) (q:draft)
khuang = (t:v) (w:crow) (d:of a rooster) (e:thakhatin aak a ~ hi/ak a ~ pah hi | at once a rooster crowed/Tua phetin nihveina aak a ~ hi | just then the rooster crowed the second time/a paikhiat khit ciangin aak a ~ hi | after he went out the rooster crowed) (r:43.18.27/40.26.74/41.14.72/41.14.68) (q:draft)
khuangbai = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:cricket) (d:a kind of hopping insect that may be eaten, named with the locusts and grasshoppers) (e:~ nam khempeuh) (r:3.11.22) (q:draft, low confidence)
khuangin = (t:v) (w:calling/hooting/crowing) (d:khuang crow, call, with linking in; here of a bird calling in the window) (e:tawlet-ah keising ~) (b:khuang) (r:36.2.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
khuangneu = (t:n) (w:timbrel/tambourine/small drum) (d:khuang drum with neu small) (e:harp lasakna, ~, tamngai) (s:khuangno/khuang) (r:9.10.5) (q:draft)
khuangneute = (t:n) (w:timbrels/tambourines) (e:a tanu ~ tawh lamsa-in hong paikhia hi/harp lasakna leh ~ leh daltuahte | harps, timbrels and cymbals/~, kuangtuahte leh daltuahte tumin | playing timbrels, sistrums and cymbals) (s:khuangte) (b:khuangneu) (r:7.11.34/13.13.8/10.6.5) (q:draft)
khuangno = (t:n) (w:timbrel/tambourine/small drum) (d:khuang drum with no small) (e:La khat phuangin, ~ tumin) (s:khuangneu) (b:khuang) (r:19.81.2) (q:draft)
