khukah = (t:adv) (w:into the pit/in the pit/to the den) (d:khuk pit, hole, with the place marker ah; humpinelkai koihna khuk is the den of lions and mei khuk a fire pit or oven) (e:humpinelkai koihna ~ a va pai pah hi/mei ~ kikhul thei lopate | grass that can be burned in the oven) (b:khuk) (r:27.6.19/40.6.30) (q:draft)
khukawm = (t:v) (w:wearing/while wearing) (d:khu, wear on the head, with kawm, while: having something on the head while doing something else) (e:ling lukhu ~ leh puansan silhkawmin/Jesuh zong ling lukhu ~ | Jesus too, wearing the crown of thorns) (r:43.19.5) (q:draft)
khukdin = (t:v) (w:kneel/kneel down) (d:go down on the knees to pray, to worship or to plead; before in, a or ni it is written with an apostrophe) (e:eite hong Bawl Topa mai-ah ~’ ni/Pa Pasian mai-ah ~’in thungenin ka om hi | I kneel before God the Father and pray/a mai-ah ~’in a bia uh hi | they knelt before him and worshiped him/tui dawn dingin ~’ suk uh hi | they knelt down to drink water) (r:19.95.6/49.3.14/41.15.19/7.7.6)
khukdinin = (t:v) (w:kneeling/kneeling down) (d:khukdin, kneel, with the linking suffix in: kneeling, followed by another verb such as pray, worship or beg) (e:~ thu ngen a/a mai-ah ~ hong thum hi | kneeling before him she begged/~ thu ka ngen uh hi | we knelt and prayed/amah ~ van lamah a khut zan hi | he knelt and spread his hands toward heaven/upate in zong ~ Pasian a bia uh hi | the elders too knelt and worshiped God) (b:khukdin) (r:42.22.41/40.20.20/44.21.5/14.6.13/66.5.14) (q:draft)
khukdinna = (t:n) (w:kneeling) (d:khukdin, kneel, with the noun suffix na: kneeling; a khukdinna mun is the place where he was kneeling) (e:zan sa-in a ~ mun/a ~ mun Topa’ biakna tau mai panin | from before the altar of the Lord where he had been kneeling) (b:khukdin) (r:11.8.54) (q:draft)
khukhu = (t:v) (w:smolder/keep smoking) (d:khu, give off smoke, said twice for an action that goes on: keep smoking, smolder) (e:uh mei bangin ~ a/a hehna uh mei bangin ~ a | their anger smolders like a fire) (r:28.7.6) (q:draft)
khukin = (t:n) (w:on the knees/with the knees) (d:khuk, knee, with in marking the means: on the knees or with the knees) (e:ka khut le ka ~ ka thoto a/ka ~ ka thoto a, ling kankan kawmin | I rose on my knees, trembling) (b:khuk) (r:27.10.10) (q:draft)
khukkhia = (t:v) (w:roll away/roll off) (d:khuk, roll, with khia, out or away: roll a heavy thing away from its place, as the stone from the mouth of a well) (e:tuikhuk kong panin suang ~ uh a/tuikhuk gong panin suang ~ a | he rolled the stone away from the mouth of the well/mual dawn panin nang hong ~-in | rolling you down from the mountain top) (s:likkhia/zialkhia) (r:1.29.3/1.29.10/24.51.25) (q:draft)
khuksa = (t:n) (w:what was spun/spun yarn) (d:khuk, spin thread, with sa for a finished action: thread or yarn that has been spun) (e:~ a dum, a dupsan/amau’ ~ a dum, a dupsan | what they had spun, blue and purple) (r:2.35.25) (q:draft)
khuksak = (t:v) (w:crown/put on the head) (d:put a crown or headdress on the head of another person; from khu, wear on the head, with the causative sak) (e:a nu in amah a ~ Kumpi lukhu/a hoih kumpi lukhu ~ nading | to put a beautiful crown on them) (s:khusak) (r:22.3.11/23.61.3) (q:draft)
khuksak = (t:v) (w:count against/charge with/impute) (d:hold a wrong against someone; mawhna khuksak is count sin against a person) (e:Topa in mawhna a ~ loh mi) (r:19.32.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
khuksate = (t:n) (w:things spun/spun yarns) (d:khuksa, what was spun, with the plural te) (e:~ a dum, a dupsan/amau’ ~ a dum, a dupsan | the things they had spun, blue and purple) (b:khuksa) (r:2.35.25) (q:draft)
khuksung = (t:n) (w:pit/depths) (d:khuk, pit, with sung, inside: in the verses always hell khuksung, the pit of hell, where the NIV has destruction or curse) (e:mi peuhpeuh hell ~ tung ta hen/Hell ~ a tung ding uh ahi hi | they are bound for the pit of hell/hell ~ a tung ding ahi A Gilopa | the Evil One who is bound for the pit of hell) (r:48.1.9/50.3.19/53.2.3) (q:draft)
khukte = (t:n) (w:knees) (d:plural of khuk, knee; weak or shaking knees are a picture of fear and of lost strength) (e:a no ~ kipsak un/An ngolhna hangin ka ~ zaw a | my knees are weak from fasting/a ~ kikalah a maitang phum hi | he put his face between his knees/tha a nei lo ~ na khauhsak un | strengthen your weak knees) (b:khuk) (r:23.35.3/58.12.12/19.109.24/11.18.42) (q:draft)
khukte = (t:n) (w:pits) (d:plural of khuk in the sense of pit or hole in the ground; kultal khukte are tar pits) (e:tua ~ sungah kia uh a/Siddim Kuam in kultal ~ tawh kidim hi | the Valley of Siddim was full of tar pits) (r:1.14.10) (q:draft)
khukzaw = (t:adj) (w:weak-kneed/faltering) (d:khuk, knee, with zaw, weak: khukzaw mite are those whose knees give way) (e:~ mite na hatsak ngeite ngaihsun in/~ mite na hatsak ngeite | the weak-kneed whom you used to strengthen) (b:khuk) (r:18.4.4) (q:draft)
khul = (t:v) (w:throw in/cast in/put on the fire) (d:throw or put something into a fire or a furnace) (e:meiphual sungah a ~ ding uh hi/bawngla a kihalna sungah tuate ~ ding hi | he shall throw them onto the burning heifer/mei tungah a ~ lai takin | just as he was putting it on the fire/mei phualpi sungah a ~ uh hi | they threw them into the great furnace) (r:40.13.42/4.19.6/44.28.3/27.3.21) (q:draft)
khulin = (t:v) (w:throwing in/casting in) (d:khul, throw into a fire, with the linking suffix in) (e:mei sungah ~ mei in a kangtum hi/mite in khawm uh a, mei sungah ~ | people gather them and throw them into the fire) (b:khul) (r:43.15.6) (q:draft)
khulna = (t:n) (w:being thrown in/casting in) (d:khul, throw into a fire, with the noun suffix na; khulna thuak is be thrown into the fire) (e:hell meikuang sungah ~ thuak thei ding hi/meikuang sungah ~ na thuak sangin | than for you to be thrown into the fire/a tawpna-ah meikhuk ~ a thuak ding hi | in the end it will be thrown into the furnace) (b:khul) (r:40.5.22/40.18.9/58.6.8) (q:draft)
khulsak = (t:v) (w:throw in/cast in) (d:khul, throw into a fire, with sak: throw into the fire things that belong to someone) (e:mei-ah hong ~ ding uh hi/na sidar khuam hoihpente hong phuksakin mei-ah hong ~ | they will cut down your best cedar posts and throw them into the fire) (b:khul) (r:24.22.7) (q:draft)
khulte = (t:n) (w:those who throw in) (d:khul, throw into a fire, with te, those who: the men who threw them in) (e:a ~ nangawn meikuang in hullum hi) (b:khul) (r:27.3.22) (q:draft)
khum = (t:adj) (w:sweet/pleasant) (d:sweet in taste; of speech pleasant or smooth, as in kam khum, sweet words) (e:Tui dawnsim, ~ diak a/Nangma thute ~ mahmah a | your words are very sweet/khuaizu ~ ahih manin ne in | eat honey, for it is sweet/A kampaute ~ zungzung a | his speech is most sweet/Kam ~ in nuntakna piangsak a | sweet words bring life) (r:20.9.17/22.5.16/19.119.103/20.24.13/20.15.4) (q:draft)
khum = (t:v) (w:put in/shut in/imprison/insert/pen up) (d:put inside something: a person into prison, an animal into a pen or cage, poles into rings, or words into a book) (e:thong sungah a ~ uh hi/kualte sungah a zawlte a ~ hi | he put the poles into the rings/a note inn ah ~ uh hi | they shut up their calves at home/Bawm sungah ~ uh a | they put him in a cage/laibu khat sungah ~ in | write them in a book) (s:khumcip/kalhkhum) (a:khah/khahkhia) (r:44.5.18/2.37.5/9.6.10/26.19.9/24.30.2) (q:draft)
khum = (t:n) (w:roof/housetop) (d:the top covering of a building; inn khum is the roof of a house, and inn khum nuai, under the roof, means inside the house) (e:inn ~ tungah a om mi in/Keima inn ~ nuai-ah nong lut dingin | for you to come under my roof/a bulpi nangawn a kipan a ~ dong | from the foundation to the eaves) (s:innkhum/khumzang/innkhumzang) (r:42.17.31/42.7.6/11.7.9) (q:draft)
khumah = (t:n) (w:on the roof) (d:khum, roof, with the place marker ah: tausang khumah is on the roof of the tower) (e:tausang ~ amaute om uh hi/kikhaknelh uh a, tausang ~ amaute om uh hi | they shut themselves in and were on the roof of the tower) (s:khumzangah/innkhumzangah) (r:7.9.51) (q:draft)
khumcip = (t:v) (w:shut in/confine/keep in custody/pen up/isolate) (d:khum, put in, with cip, tightly: keep a person or an animal shut up, as a prisoner in custody, a sick person apart from others, or a bull in its pen) (e:amaute in tua mipa ~ uh hi/a neipa in a ~ kei leh | if the owner does not keep it penned up/siampipa in ni sagih sung ~ ding hi | the priest shall isolate him for seven days/amah a nin ahih manin ~ lo ding hi | he shall not isolate him, for he is unclean) (s:kalhkhum) (a:khahkhia) (b:khum) (r:3.24.12/2.21.36/3.13.26/3.13.11) (q:draft)
khumcipin = (t:v) (w:taking captive/confining) (d:khumcip, shut in, with the linking suffix in: shutting in, taking captive) (e:lungsim khempeuh manin ~/~ Khazih’ thu ka ngaisak uh hi | taking them captive, we make them obey Christ) (b:khumcip) (r:47.10.5) (q:draft)
khumdawnte = (t:n) (w:battlements/pinnacles) (d:khum, roof, with dawn, top, and the plural te: the topmost parts of the walls or roofs of a city) (e:Na ~ suangmanpha tawh) (r:23.54.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
khumdiak = (t:adj) (w:especially sweet/sweeter) (d:khum, sweet, with diak, especially: all the sweeter) (e:Tui dawnsim, ~ a, an neksim/Tui dawnsim, ~ a | stolen water is especially sweet) (s:khumzaw) (r:20.9.17) (q:draft)
khumhak = (t:adj) (w:hard to put through/hard to put in) (d:khum, put in, with hak, hard to do: a khumhak sangin is than it is hard to put through, said of a camel and the eye of a needle) (e:phim vangah a ~ sangin/Sai khat phim vangah a ~ sangin | than it is hard for a camel to go through the eye of a needle) (r:42.18.25/40.19.24) (q:draft)
khumialna = (t:n) (w:darkness/gloom) (d:darkness, named together with distress and gloom; apparently the same word as khuamialna) (e:lungkhamna leh ~, lungzing-a gimna/lungkhamna leh ~, lungzing-a gimna bek om hi | there is only distress and darkness and fearful gloom) (s:khuamialna/khuamial/mialna) (a:khuavak) (r:23.8.22) (q:draft, perhaps a misprint for khuamialna)
khumin = (t:v) (w:putting in/inserting/shutting in/imprisoning) (d:khum, put in, with the linking suffix in: the action is followed by another) (e:thong tawngnung sungah ~/a zawlte ~, a khuampite phut hi | he inserted the crossbars and set up the posts/thong sungah ~, a sih dongin ka bawlsia hi | I threw them into prison and persecuted them to death/thong sungah ~ a nutsiat mi khat | a man whom he left shut in prison) (b:khum) (r:44.16.24/2.40.18/44.22.4/44.25.14) (q:draft)
khumkhelh = (t:v) (w:surpass/exceed/excel) (d:be greater than all others; the thing in which one is greater is marked by tawh) (e:leitung kumpi khempeuh ~ hi/hauhna leh pilna tawh leitung kumpi khempeuh ~ hi | he surpassed all the kings of the earth in riches and wisdom) (s:khumlet/khuplet/khupnelh) (r:11.10.23/14.9.22) (q:draft)
khumlet = (t:v) (w:surpass/exceed) (d:be greater than, surpass; the other text of this verse has khuplet) (e:Egypt pilna khempeuh ~ hi/Egypt pilna khempeuh ~ hi | it surpassed all the wisdom of Egypt) (s:khuplet/khumkhelh/khupnelh) (r:11.4.30) (q:draft)
khumna = (t:n) (w:sweetness) (d:khum, sweet, with the noun suffix na: sweetness of taste, and in kam khumna pleasantness of speech) (e:ka ~ leh ka gah hoihte nusia-in/amau’ kam ~, zaknophuai kisa semsem hi | the sweetness of their speech is found more and more pleasant to hear) (b:khum) (r:7.9.11/20.16.21) (q:draft)
khumna = (t:n) (w:imprisonment/shutting in/confinement) (d:khum, put in, with the noun suffix na: the act or the place of shutting in; thong sung khumna is being put in prison and bawng khumna is a cattle stall) (e:thong sung ~/Bawng ~ panin a kikhah bawngnote bangin | like calves let out of the stall) (s:thongkiatna) (b:khum) (r:47.6.5/39.4.2) (q:draft)
khumsak = (t:v) (w:imprison/have put in prison/have shut in) (d:khum, put in, with the causative sak: have someone put in, as into prison) (e:thong sungah a ~ hi/thongah a kia dingin a ~ hi | he had him thrown into prison/ka paisak mateng dongin ka ~ hi | I had him held until I could send him) (b:khum) (r:40.14.3/40.18.30/44.25.21) (q:draft)
khumte = (t:adj) (w:sweet/choice) (d:khum, sweet, with the plural te: leenggahzu khumte is the sweet, choice wine) (e:in leenggahzu ~ hawm masakin nei uh/Midangte in leenggahzu ~ hawm masakin nei uh a | others serve the choice wine first) (b:khum) (r:43.2.10) (q:draft)
khumzang = (t:n) (w:roof/rooftop/housetop) (d:the flat top of a building, from khum, roof; biakinn khumzang is the roof of the temple) (e:biakinn ~ a sangpen munah/biakinn ~ a sangpenna munah a kahtohpih khit ciangin | when he had taken him up to the highest point of the temple roof) (s:innkhumzang/innkhum/khum) (r:40.4.5/12.23.12/42.4.9) (q:draft)
khumzanga = (t:n) (w:on the roof) (d:khumzang, roof, with the ending a, located on) (e:inndei tungnung ~ a om biakna taute/Ahaz’ inndei tungnung ~ a om biakna taute | the altars on the roof of the upper room of Ahaz) (s:khumzangah/innkhumzanga/khumah) (b:khumzang) (r:12.23.12) (q:draft)
khumzangah = (t:n) (w:on the roof/to the roof/in the vault) (d:khumzang, roof or vault, with the place marker ah: kulh kongpi khumzangah is on the roof of the gateway and van khumzangah in the vault of heaven) (e:galvilpa kulh kongpi ~ paito a/Van ~ Pasian a pai kawmin | as God walks about in the vault of heaven) (s:innkhumzangah/khumah/khumzanga) (b:khumzang) (r:10.18.24/18.22.14) (q:draft)
khumzaw = (t:adj) (w:sweeter/more delightful) (d:khum, sweet, with zaw, more: sweeter than something, which is followed by sangin) (e:khuaizu sangin ka kam-ah ~ hi/nong itna in leenggahzu sangin ~ hi | your love is sweeter than wine/khuailuzu tak sangin zong ~ hi | sweeter even than honey from the comb/Khuaizu sangin bang ~ a | what is sweeter than honey) (s:khumdiak) (b:khum) (r:19.119.103/22.1.2/19.19.10/7.14.18) (q:draft)
khun = (t:v) (w:lean on/walk with) (d:support oneself on a staff or stick; ciangkhut khun mi is a person who walks with a stick) (e:ciangkhut ~ mi ahi a/a phak mi ahi a, ciangkhut ~ mi | one who has leprosy, one who leans on a staff) (r:10.3.29) (q:draft)
khung = (t:v) (w:set/lay across/put up) (d:put something long in position before or across: lay a choice before people, put up a parapet round a roof, stretch chains across a room) (e:na innkhum zangah tangban na ~ ding hi/nuntakna lampi leh sihna lampi ka ~ hi | I set before you the way of life and the way of death/kham khainiang ~ a, kham tawh a zut hi | he stretched gold chains across and overlaid it with gold) (r:5.22.8/24.21.8/11.6.21) (q:draft, low confidence)
khung = (t:n) (w:top/upper end) (d:the upper end of something, the opposite of taw, the bottom; a taw panin a khung dongin is from bottom to top; in Ezekiel 40:6 the top of the steps of a gateway, where the NIV has threshold) (e:kahto-in a ~ a tun’ ciangin/A taw panin a ~ dongin | from the bottom to the top) (s:dawn) (a:taw) (r:26.40.6/26.20.47) (q:draft, low confidence)
khungah = (t:n) (w:at the top/in the tops) (d:khung, top, with the place marker ah: at the top, as in the tops of trees) (e:~ lam paina kheging na zak ciangin/Lungli kungte’ ~ lam paina kheging | the sound of marching in the tops of the poplar trees) (b:khung) (r:10.5.24) (q:draft)
khungin = (t:v) (w:laying across/stretching out/setting in place) (d:form of khung with the linking suffix in: laying or stretching something long across, such as a beam, a chain or a measuring line) (e:amaute in a zawlte ~ a kongkhakte/innkamte ~ taamtak peekte tawh inndap a bawl hi | he laid the beams and made the ceiling with cedar planks/kham khainiang ~ kham tawh zut hi | he stretched gold chains across and overlaid it with gold/khau ~ laikung tawh ciamteh hi | he stretches a line and marks it with a pen) (b:khung) (r:16.3.3/23.44.13/11.6.9/11.6.21) (q:draft)
khungnung = (t:adj) (w:uppermost/farthest) (d:khung, upper end, with nung, last: at the very end; leilu lam a khungnung pen is the part farthest to the north, the northern frontier) (e:Leilu lam a ~ penah Dan minamte) (r:26.48.1/26.48.23) (q:draft, low confidence)
khungnungpen = (t:adj) (w:farthest/uppermost/outermost) (d:khungnung, at the upper end, with pen, most: leilu lam a khungnungpen is the far north) (e:Leilu lam a ~ ah Dan minamte) (b:khungnung) (r:26.48.1) (q:draft, low confidence)
khunin = (t:v) (w:leaning on) (d:khun, lean on a staff, with the linking suffix in) (e:ciangkhut ~ pai ding uh hi/teek lua kisa-in ciangkhut ~ pai ding uh hi | being very old, they will walk leaning on a staff) (b:khun) (r:38.8.4) (q:draft)
khup = (t:v) (w:cover over/close over) (d:cover something from above so that it is closed in; in the verse with nelh, completely) (e:leitang in amaute ~ nelh a) (s:khuhcip) (r:4.16.33) (q:draft, low confidence)
khup = (t:v) (w:turn face down/lower/fold down) (d:turn or lay something downward: of wings, lower or fold them; ka khup lamin is with my face to the ground) (e:a kha uh ~ a/ka ~ lamin lei lakah ka tuksuk a | I fell face down on the ground) (r:26.1.24/27.10.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
khupcip = (t:v) (w:close up/shut up) (d:khup, cover or close, with cip, tightly: laibu khupcip is close up the book) (e:tun mateng laibu ~ inla/laibu ~ inla, a tungah ciaptehna koih in | close up the book and put a seal on it) (a:hon) (b:khup) (r:27.12.4) (q:draft)
khupin = (t:v) (w:closing/folding down/turning down) (d:khup with the linking suffix in: closing a book, or folding wings down to cover the body) (e:a laibu ~ biakinn nasempa tungah/a laibu ~ biakinn nasempa tungah pia kikin | he closed the book and gave it back to the attendant/~ a pumpi uh tuam uh hi | folding them down they covered their bodies) (b:khup) (r:42.4.20/26.1.11) (q:draft)
khuplamin = (t:adv) (w:face down/prone) (d:khup, turn face down, with lam, side, and in: with the face to the ground) (e:ka ~ leilakah tuksukin khua/~ leilakah tuksukin khua ka phawk nawn kei hi | I fell face down on the ground and knew nothing more) (s:maipukin) (r:27.10.9) (q:draft)
khuplet = (t:v) (w:surpass/overwhelm/overthrow) (d:get the better of something completely: of wisdom, surpass that of others; of victory, swallow up death; of arguments, overthrow them) (e:Izipt pilna khempeuh ~ hi/Sihna maimangin gualzawhna in ~ hi | death is gone, swallowed up by victory/a kiphasak ngaihsutnate ahi zongin ~ gawpin | overthrowing also the thoughts that exalt themselves) (s:khumlet/khumkhelh/khupnelh) (r:11.4.30/46.15.54/47.10.5) (q:draft)
khupna = (t:n) (w:conclusion/closing/end) (d:khup, close, with the noun suffix na, what closes or covers a thing: pawi khupna the closing of a festival, khupna suang the capstone of a building, thugen khupna the conclusion of a speech) (e:a ~ suang na ciang ding hi/pawi ~ a thupi kikhopna khat om hi | there was a solemn assembly to close the festival/Jesuh in a thugen a ~-in | Jesus, as the conclusion of what he said) (s:tawpna/thukhupna) (a:kipatna) (b:khup) (r:38.4.7/16.8.18/42.12.21) (q:draft)
khupnelh = (t:v) (w:surpass/exceed/overshadow) (d:khup, cover, with nelh, completely: be greater than all others, overshadow them) (e:leitung kumpi khempeuh ~ hi/hauhna leh pilna tawh leitung kumpi khempeuh ~ hi | he surpassed all the kings of the earth in riches and wisdom) (s:khumkhelh/khuplet/khumlet) (r:14.9.22) (q:draft)
khupnelhin = (t:v) (w:closing over/covering over) (d:khupnelh, cover over completely, with the linking suffix in; said of the earth closing over people) (e:Leitang in amaute ~/amaute ~ mihonpite’ lak panin amaute bei uh hi | it closed over them and they perished from among the community) (b:khupnelh) (r:4.16.33) (q:draft)
khusa = (t:see) <khusa-in>
khusa-in = (t:v) (w:wearing on the head/having on the head) (d:khu, put on the head, with sa for a completed action and the linking ending in: having something on the head, such as a hat, a crown or ashes) (e:silhsa leh lukhu ~ hencip uh a/na lu tungah vut ~ nong paikhia ding hi | you will go out with ashes on your head/a kumpi lukhu ~ ama kiangah a paipih nadingun | to bring her to him wearing her royal crown) (r:27.3.21/24.2.37/17.1.10) (q:draft)
khusak = (t:v) (w:put on the head/crown) (d:khu, wear on the head, with the causative sak: put a hat or a crown on the head of another person) (e:ling tawh kigaan lukhu a ~ uh hi/ama lu tungah kham siang lukhu na ~ hi | you placed a crown of pure gold on his head/dialpi tungah kumpi lukhu siangtho na ~ ding hi | you shall put the sacred crown on the turban/minthan’na leh pahtawina na ~ hi | you crowned him with glory and honor) (s:khuksak) (r:41.15.17/19.21.3/2.29.6/58.2.7) (q:draft)
khusakin = (t:v) (w:putting on the head of/crowning) (d:khusak, put something on the head of another person, with the linking ending in) (e:kumpi lukhu amah ~ Vashti’ taangin/a lu tungah sumngo lukhu ~, sikpuan silhsak hi | he put a bronze helmet on his head and dressed him in armor/kumpi lukhu amah ~ Vashti’ taangin kumpinu suaksak hi | he put the royal crown on her and made her queen in place of Vashti) (b:khusak) (r:17.2.17/9.17.38) (q:draft)
khut = (t:n) (w:hand) (d:the hand of a person; also said of the power or the work of someone, as in khut tawh bawl, make by hand) (e:Na ~ in hong puksak leh/~ hoih lo, khe hoih lo | a crippled hand or a crippled foot/ka ~ tawh kong gelh hi | I write to you with my own hand/Na ~ tawh na bawlsate khempeuh | all that you made with your hands) (r:41.9.43/3.21.19/46.16.21/19.8.6)
khuta = (t:n) (w:in the hand/on the hand) (d:khut, hand, with the ending a, in or on: in the hand, on the hand) (e:kumpipa in a ~ a tawi kumpi ciangkhut/na ~ kibulh kolte | the chains fastened on your hands) (b:khut) (r:17.5.2/24.40.4) (q:draft)
khutah = (t:n) (w:in the hand/into the hand/at the hand) (d:khut, hand, with the place ending ah: in, into or at the hand of someone) (e:galte’ ~ pia hi/na ~ ka ciangkhut tawi-in pai in | take my staff in your hand and go/a ~ teipi khat tawi-in | taking a spear in his hand/ka taklam ~ tu in | sit at my right hand) (b:khut) (r:19.78.61/12.4.29/4.25.7/19.110.1) (q:draft)
khutbuh = (t:n) (w:ring/finger ring) (d:a ring worn on the finger, from khut, hand; kham khutbuh is a gold ring) (e:Kham ~ bulh a, puanhoih a silh/Kham ~ bulh a, puanhoih a silh mi | a man wearing a gold ring and fine clothes) (s:zungbuh) (r:59.2.2) (q:draft)
khutbui = (t:adj) (w:maimed in the hand/one-handed) (d:khut, hand, with bui, maimed: having a hand cut off or useless; paired with khebui, maimed in the foot) (e:~ khebui-in nuntakna sungah na tum leh) (r:41.9.44/41.9.46) (q:draft)
khutcinte = (t:n) (w:fingernails/nails) (d:khutcin, fingernail, with the plural te) (e:a ~ muvanlai khecin bangin/a ~ muvanlai’ khecin bangin a hong sau hi | his nails grew long like the claws of an eagle) (r:27.4.33) (q:draft)
khutdawh = (t:n) (w:alms/begging) (d:what is asked for with the hand held out, from khut, hand, and dawh, hold out; khutdawh ngen is to beg) (e:mittaw khat in ~ ngenin lam geiah/amah in ~ ngen mi ahih lam | that he was a man who begged/biakna innpi-a lut mite kiangah ~ ngen dingin | to beg from those going into the temple/mittaw ~ ngen khat lampi geiah a tu hi | a blind beggar was sitting by the roadside) (s:ngettawm) (r:42.18.35/44.3.2/43.9.8/41.10.46) (q:draft)
khutdawhin = (t:v) (w:begging) (d:khutdawh, alms, with the marker in: khutdawhin ngen is ask for alms, beg) (e:a mittaw ~ a ngen Bartimias/~ a ngen Bartimias, lampi gei-ah na tu hi | Bartimaeus, who begged for alms, was sitting by the roadside) (b:khutdawh) (r:41.10.46) (q:draft)
khutdim = (t:n) (w:handful) (d:as much as a hand holds, from khut, hand, and dim, full) (e:phawkna-in ~ khat la-in/tua sung panin a ~ la-in | taking a handful of it/beel sungah annel ~ khat | a handful of flour in a jar/biakna annel ~ khat | a handful of the offering flour) (s:khutkuak) (r:3.5.12/3.6.15/3.9.17/11.17.12) (q:draft)
khute = (t:n) (w:smoke/clouds of smoke) (d:khu, smoke, with the plural te: smoke or a rising cloud, as of incense or of dust) (e:paknamtui hal ~ van lamah kahto biaibuai/paina leivui ~ in khuapi tuamcip ding hi | the clouds of dust from their passing will cover the city/tuutal-a biakna ~ tawh | with the smoke of offerings of rams) (s:meikhute) (b:khu) (r:26.8.11/26.26.10/19.66.15) (q:draft)
khute = (t:n) (w:smoking ones/smoldering) (d:khu, give off smoke, with te: things that are smoking; sing tumbang a khute are smoldering stubs of firewood) (e:sing tumbang nih a ~ tawh kibang/sing tumbang nih a ~ tawh kibang lel | only like two smoldering stubs of wood) (b:khu) (r:23.7.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
khuthawm = (t:n) (w:empty hand) (d:khut, hand, with hawm, empty; in the verses always khuthawm guakin, empty-handed) (e:~ guakin na paisak kei ding hi/mihaute, ~ guakin a paikhiasak hi | he has sent the rich away empty-handed/~ guakin kei nong sawlkhia taktak ding hi | you would surely have sent me away empty-handed) (r:5.15.13/42.1.53/1.31.42) (q:draft)
khutin = (t:n) (w:with the hand/by the hand) (d:khut, hand, with the marker in, showing the hand as the doer or the means of an action) (e:a taklam ~ hong kawi hi/ka ~ ka gelh | I write with my own hand/Jesuh in naupang a ~ lenin | Jesus took the boy by the hand/a ~ lawhpi a tawi hi | he holds a winnowing fork in his hand) (b:khut) (r:22.8.3/48.6.11/41.9.27/42.3.17) (q:draft)
khutkhai = (t:n) (w:handbag/purse) (d:khut, hand, with khai, hang or carry; khutkhai ip is a bag carried in the hand) (e:puanpite leh ~ ipte/pawi puante, puanza neute, puanpite leh ~ ipte | the fine robes, the capes, the cloaks and the handbags) (r:23.3.22) (q:draft)
khutkuak = (t:n) (w:hollow of the hand/cupped hand/handful) (d:khut, hand, with kuak, hollow: the hollow of the hand and what it holds) (e:ama ~ sungah tuite tehin/Kua in ama ~ sungah tuite tehin | who has measured the waters in the hollow of his hand/~ a dim zawh taak leh | if it were enough to fill the hollow of the hand) (s:khutdim) (r:23.40.12/11.20.10) (q:draft)
khutlaam = (t:v) (w:raise the hand/swear with uplifted hand) (d:khut, hand, with laam, lift: raise the hand as the sign of an oath) (e:tungah ~ a, ka ciam leitangah) (r:2.6.8) (q:draft)
khutlamen = (t:n) (w:palm reading/soothsaying) (d:apparently reading the hand, a kind of fortune-telling; khutlamen theite are those who practise it, where the NIV has mediums) (e:na ~ theite uh leh) (r:24.27.9) (q:draft, low confidence, kind of divination guessed from khut hand and en look)
khutlekhe = (t:n) (w:hands and feet/limbs) (d:khut, hand, le, and, khe, foot, written as one word: the limbs of the body) (e:a ~ a zaw/a ~ a zaw, kum giat sung tawntung | paralyzed in his limbs for eight whole years/maihem, le ~ saulua | disfigured, or with a limb too long) (r:44.9.33/3.21.18) (q:draft)
khutlekhezaw = (t:adj) (w:paralyzed/paralytic) (d:khut le khe, hand and foot, with zaw, weak: unable to move the limbs; khutlekhezaw mi is a paralyzed person) (e:~ mi khat a lupna pheek tawh/~ mipa kiangah | to the paralyzed man/Jesuh kiangah ~ mi khat a paipih dingin | to bring a paralyzed man to Jesus/a mittaw, a khebai, ~, cina tampi | many sick people, the blind, the lame, the paralyzed) (b:khutlekhe) (r:42.5.18/41.2.3/41.2.5/43.5.3) (q:draft)
khutlet = (t:n) (w:handle) (d:in the clay's complaint that the thing made has no khutlet; the NIV reads has no hands) (e:bawl in ~ nei lo hi) (r:23.45.9) (q:draft, low confidence, handle or hands)
khutlum = (t:n) (w:hand/hands) (d:the hand as that which kills or does violence; after a possessive, with in or tawh: at the hands of) (e:kote’ ~-in na si ding hi/a that nuamte’ ~-in amaute ka sisak ding hi | I will make them die at the hands of those who want to kill them/hehpihna a nei lo mite’ ~ tawh | at the hands of people without mercy) (r:24.11.21/24.19.7/20.5.9) (q:draft)
khutlumin = (t:adv) (w:by the hand of/at the hands of) (d:khutlum with the marker in, by means of: after a possessive, killed at the hands of someone) (e:kote’ ~ na si ding hi/a thatnuamte’ ~ amaute ka sisak ding hi | I will make them die at the hands of those who want to kill them) (b:khutlum) (r:24.11.21/24.19.7) (q:draft)
khutme = (t:n) (w:finger) (d:a finger of the hand; taklam khutme is the finger of the right hand that the priest dips in blood or oil) (e:Pasian’ ~ tawh dawite ka hawlkhiat leh/siampipa in a sisan sungah a ~ diahin | the priest shall dip his finger in the blood/a ~ tawh a si tawm khat la-in | taking some of the blood on his finger/sathau tawmkhat a taklam ~ tawh | some of the oil with his right finger) (r:42.11.20/3.14.27/3.4.17/4.19.4) (q:draft)
khutmeno = (t:n) (w:little finger/finger) (d:khutme, finger, with no, small: the little finger, also a single finger) (e:Ka ~ in ka pa’ kawng sangin/~ in ka pa’ kawng sangin gol zaw hi | my little finger is thicker than the waist of my father/ka ~ khat zong ka zankhia kei ding hi | I would not lift even one finger) (b:khutme) (r:11.12.10/40.23.4/10.18.12) (q:draft)
khutmete = (t:n) (w:fingers) (d:plural of khutme, finger) (e:Na ~ zan in la/Na ~’ nasepna | the work of your fingers/ka ~ galkap nadinga a hilh | who trains my fingers for battle/a ~ tawh a bawlsate | what their fingers have made) (b:khutme) (r:43.20.27/19.8.3/19.144.1/23.2.8) (q:draft)
khutngakna = (t:n) (w:laying on of hands) (d:khut, hand, with ngakna, the laying on: placing the hands on someone to bless or to appoint) (e:pawlpi upate’ ~ tawh/kuama tungah a manlangin ~ nei kei in | do not be quick to lay hands on anyone/baptaiznate thuhilhna, ~, misite’ thawhkikna | teaching about baptisms, the laying on of hands, the resurrection of the dead) (r:54.4.14/54.5.22/58.6.1) (q:draft)
khutnuai = (t:n) (w:subjection/power/control) (d:literally under the hand: the power or rule of someone; khutnuai mi is a subject or vassal, and khutnuai-ah koih is bring under control) (e:ama ~ mi suak a, ama tungah/Mawhna ~-ah leitung mi khempeuh a om hi | the whole world is under the power of sin/amaute’ ~ mi suak uh hi | they became subject to them/Moab gam pen Israel-te’ ~ a suak hi | Moab became subject to Israel) (r:12.17.3/49.5.24/48.3.22/10.10.19/7.3.30) (q:draft)
khuto = (t:v) (w:rise as smoke/go up in smoke/smoke upward) (d:khu, smoke, with to, upward: go up as smoke) (e:van lamah ~ tawntung hi/khu tatsat loin van lamah ~ tawntung hi | its smoke goes up toward heaven for ever without ceasing) (b:khu) (r:66.19.3/22.3.6) (q:draft)
khutpeek = (t:n) (w:palm/open hand) (d:the flat inner side of the hand, the open hand; khutpeek zan is hold out the hands) (e:ka ~ sungah nang kong gelh khinzo a/ni khat tawntung ka ~ ka zan hi | all day long I have held out my hands/Kimkhat in ~-in a beeng uh hi | others slapped him with the open hand/a khete le a ~ simloh | except her feet and the palms of her hands) (r:23.49.16/45.10.21/40.26.67/12.9.35) (q:draft)
khutpeek = (t:n) (w:handbreadth) (d:the width of a hand used as a measure; khutpeek cia is one handbreadth) (e:A sahna in ~ mai cia ahi hi/~ cia a zai zawl peek khat | a rim one handbreadth wide/leitang ~ cia nangawn pia lo napi-in | though he gave him not even a handbreadth of ground) (s:khutpeekmai) (r:11.7.26/2.25.25/44.7.5) (q:draft)
khutpeekmai = (t:n) (w:handbreadth) (d:khutpeek, palm, with mai, face: the width of the palm as a measure) (e:A tuikuang sahna ~ cia ahi hi) (s:khutpeek) (r:11.7.26) (q:draft)
khutpi = (t:n) (w:thumb) (d:the big finger of the hand, from khut, hand, with pi, big; named together with khepi, the big toe) (e:a taklam ~ leh a taklam khepi/a taklam ~, leh a taklam khepi | his right thumb and his right big toe/taklam ~ dawnte | the tips of the right thumbs) (b:khut) (r:3.8.23/3.14.14/2.29.20) (q:draft)
khutpite = (t:n) (w:thumbs) (d:plural of khutpi, thumb) (e:a ~ leh a khepite attan uh hi/amau’ taklam ~ leh amau’ taklam khepite | their right thumbs and their right big toes/A ~ leh a khepi a ki-attan kumpi sawmsagihte | seventy kings with their thumbs and big toes cut off) (b:khutpi) (r:7.1.6/3.8.24/7.1.7) (q:draft)
khutsiam = (t:adj) (w:skilled/skillful) (d:skilled with the hands, from khut, hand, and siam, skilled; khutsiam mi is a craftsman and khutsiam nasep is craft work) (e:~ mi a om lai teng/~ mipa khat amah in zong hi | he looks for a skilled craftsman/Gebal khuapi mi ~ mahmahte | the highly skilled men of Gebal/theihna leh ~ nasep khempeuh tawh | with knowledge and all kinds of craftsmanship) (s:siam) (r:24.52.15/26.27.9/23.40.20/2.35.31) (q:draft)
khutsiamna = (t:n) (w:skill/craftsmanship) (d:khutsiam, skilled with the hands, with the noun suffix na) (e:lungsim siamna leh ~ tawh a kibawl/mi lungsim siamna leh ~ tawh a kibawl | made by human design and skill) (s:siamna) (b:khutsiam) (r:44.17.29) (q:draft)
khutsiampa = (t:n) (w:craftsman/carpenter/skilled workman) (d:khutsiam, skilled with the hands, with pa marking a man: a man who makes things by hand, especially of wood) (e:~ in a hei tawh milimin a bawl hi/Amah in ~’ tapa hilo ahi hiam | is he not the son of the carpenter/Amah ~ hilel a | he is only the carpenter/~ khut tawh a kibawl | made by the hands of a craftsman) (b:khutsiam) (r:24.10.3/40.13.55/41.6.3/5.27.15) (q:draft)
khutsiamte = (t:n) (w:craftsmen/artisans/carpenters/skilled workers) (d:khutsiam, skilled with the hands, with the plural ending te: people who make things by hand) (e:~ leh sikseekte tulkhat/~ pen mi hi lel uh hi | the craftsmen are only human/a hoih takin ~ bawlsak uh hi | they have craftsmen make them skilfully/tua sum in ~, innlamte | that money to the carpenters and the builders) (b:khutsiam) (r:12.24.16/13.22.15/23.44.11/28.13.2/12.22.6) (q:draft)
khutsung = (t:n) (w:hand/grasp/power) (d:khut, hand, with sung, inside: the hand as that which holds, so the grasp or power of someone; mostly in khutsung panin, out of the hand of) (e:ama tapa’ ~ panin kumpi gam la-in/amaute’ ~ panin Jesuh a suakta hi | Jesus escaped from their hands/Migilote’ ~ panin nang kong suaktasak ding a | I will free you from the hands of the wicked/a ~ panin khuavak taangkhia a | light flashed from his hand) (r:11.11.35/12.18.29/43.10.39/24.15.21/35.3.4) (q:draft)
khutsunga = (t:adv) (w:in the hand/in the palm/held in the hand) (d:khutsung, the inside of the hand, with the place marker a: in the hand or palm, held by someone) (e:a ~ om suang khat tawh/galhang pa’ ~ a om a thaltangte | the arrows in the hand of a warrior/a veilam ~ om sathau sungah | into the oil in his left palm/a ~ om thuciamna suangpek nih | the two tablets of the covenant in his hand/a ~ Filistia-pa’ lutang tawh | with the head of the Philistine in his hand) (b:khutsung) (r:4.35.17/19.127.4/3.14.16/2.32.15/9.17.57) (q:draft)
khutte = (t:n) (w:hands) (d:khut, hand, with the plural te: the hands, or the arms, of a person) (e:A zaw ~ khauhsak un la/na ~ uh laamto un la | lift up your hands/vuttui tawh ka ~ sawp ta leng zong | even if I wash my hands with cleansing powder/ama' ~ len uh hi | they held up his hands) (b:khut) (r:23.35.3/19.134.2/18.9.30/2.17.12) (q:draft)
khuttum = (t:n) (w:fist) (d:the closed hand; khuttum zial is to clench the fist, khuttum tawh tum is to strike with the fist, and khuttum cia is the size of a fist) (e:Pasian langpangin a ~ a lahsan/ama' ~ tawh ahi zongin tumin | or hitting him with his fist/~ cia bang meii tawmno khat | a small cloud about the size of a fist/ka ~ ka zial ding hi | I will clench my fist) (r:18.15.25/11.18.44/2.21.18/26.22.13) (q:draft)
khuttung = (t:n) (w:hand) (d:khut, hand, with tung, on: the hand as the place where something is held; khuttung panin is from the hand of someone) (e:Topa’ ~ panin tua hai ka la/na ~ panin hai la-in dawn ding uh a | they will take the cup from your hand and drink/Ka ~ panin hehna tawh a kidim hih leenggahzu | from my hand this wine filled with wrath) (s:khutsung) (r:24.25.17/24.25.28/24.25.15) (q:draft)
khutun = (t:n) (w:in their hands/with their hands) (d:khut, hand, with un, the plural uh joined with the marker in: in or with their hands) (e:a veilam ~ meilah tawi-in/a taklam ~ a tum ding uh peengkul tawi | holding in their right hands the trumpets they were to blow/tua gam singgah pawlkhat a ~ hong tawi-in | bringing some of the fruit of that land in their hands) (b:khut) (r:7.7.20/5.1.25) (q:draft)
khutzaw = (t:adj) (w:with a withered hand/paralyzed) (d:khut, hand, with zaw, weak: having a weak or withered hand; khutzaw khezaw, weak in hand and foot, means paralyzed) (e:Jesuh in ~ mipa kiangah/~ khezaw mite zong kidamsak hi | the paralyzed were also healed/dawivei mi, sibup mi, ~ khezaw mi | the demon-possessed, those having seizures and the paralyzed) (b:khut) (r:41.3.3/44.8.7/40.4.24) (q:draft)
khutzepin = (t:v) (w:folding the hands/with folded hands) (d:khut, hand, with zep, fold, and the linking suffix in: with the hands folded, doing no work) (e:~ ommawkna hangin) (r:20.24.33) (q:draft)
Khuza = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Chuza) (d:manager of the household of Herod Antipas and husband of Joanna, one of the women who supported Jesus) (e:Herod’ nasempa ~’ zi Joanna leh Susanna) (r:42.8.3) (q:draft)
khuzaw = (t:see) <khuzaw-in>
khuzaw-in = (t:v) (w:smoking/smoldering/burning) (d:khu, smoke, with zaw and the linking suffix in: of anger, smoking or burning against someone like the smoke of a fire) (e:langkhatah ~, hih laibu sunga kigelh/meikhu bangin tua mipa’ langkhatah ~ | smoking against that man like the smoke of a fire) (r:5.29.20) (q:draft, low confidence)
ki = (t:n) (w:horn) (d:the horn of an animal; in the visions of Daniel a horn stands for a king) (e:na ~ uh tawh si gawpin/gamsialte’ ~ panin | from the horns of the wild oxen/Na muh ~ nih a nei tuutal | the ram with two horns that you saw/a mit kikal-a po ~ in | the horn that grows between its eyes) (s:kii/saki) (r:26.34.21/19.98.6/19.22.21/27.8.20/27.8.21) (q:draft)
ki = (t:part) (d:prefix on a verb showing that the action is done to oneself or to one another, or that it is passive; it is written with a hyphen before a vowel, as in ki-it, love one another) (e:Ute naute ~-itna kip ta hen/khat leh khat na ~-it un | love one another/nang na ~-it bangin na vengte na it in | love your neighbor as you love yourself/amaute khat leh khat ~-en uh a | they looked at one another) (r:58.13.1/4.18.14/43.13.34/40.19.19/1.42.28) (q:draft)
ki-atkeh = (t:v) (w:cut oneself/gash oneself) (d:at, cut, and keh, split, with the reflexive prefix ki: cut one's own body, as was done in mourning for the dead) (e:hangin note ~ loin) (s:kikui/kikuiliam) (r:5.14.1) (q:draft)
ki-atmang = (t:v) (w:be mown/be cut away) (d:at, cut, with the passive prefix ki and mang, away or gone: be cut and taken away, as hay from a field) (e:Lopate ~ khin a) (r:20.27.25) (q:draft)
ki-atnente = (t:n) (w:pieces/cut pieces) (d:at, cut, with ki, nen, into small bits, and the plural te: the pieces into which a slaughtered animal is cut) (e:a lu le a ~ le a thau) (s:sanente/sabakte) (r:3.8.20) (q:draft)
ki-enpha = (t:v) (w:examine oneself/look well at oneself) (d:en, look, with ki, oneself, and pha, well: look carefully at one's own conduct) (e:limtakin ~ kikin Topa’ lamah kiheikik ni) (s:kisittel/kiteldot) (r:25.3.40) (q:draft)
ki-etkik = (t:v) (w:be searched/be looked at again/be re-examined) (d:et, look, with the passive prefix ki and kik, again: be looked at again, said of records that are searched) (e:laibute a ~ theih nadingin) (s:kikan) (r:15.4.14) (q:draft)
ki-ettehin = (t:v) (w:comparing oneself) (d:etteh, compare, with ki, oneself, and the linking suffix in: comparing oneself; tawh marks the one compared with) (e:midangte tawh ~ kisial kei hen) (s:kitehin) (r:48.6.4) (q:draft)
ki-eu = (t:v) (w:be hewn/be cut out) (d:eu, hew or prise out, with the passive prefix ki; ki-eu khiat is be cut out of the rock) (e:note hong ~ khiatna suangpi) (s:kikhuak) (r:23.51.1) (q:draft)
ki-ipin = (t:v) (w:restraining oneself/holding oneself back) (d:ip, hold in, with ki, oneself, and the linking suffix in: holding oneself back, keeping one's anger in) (e:ahihleh ~ a hehna damsak hi) (s:kikhamcipin/kikhamcip-in) (r:20.29.11) (q:draft)
ki-ipip = (t:v) (w:hold oneself back/restrain oneself) (d:ip, hold in, repeated, with ki, oneself: keep holding something in, as anger; ki-ipip zo nawn lo is can hold back no longer) (e:ka hehna ka ~ zo nawn kei hi) (r:24.15.6) (q:draft)
ki-ipipna = (t:n) (w:holding back/self-restraint/forbearance) (d:ip, hold in, repeated, with ki, oneself, and the noun suffix na: holding oneself in again and again, patience with others) (e:ka ~-in ka gimlua a/a ~ mite tungah | toward the people he was patient with) (s:kidekna) (r:24.20.9/45.9.22) (q:draft)
ki-ipzote = (t:n) (w:those who can restrain themselves) (d:ki-ip, restrain oneself, with zo, be able, and the plural te; kampau a ki-ipzote are those who can guard their speech) (e:Kampau a ~ lungkhamna tawh kipelh hi) (r:20.21.23) (q:draft)
ki-uatsaknate = (t:n) (w:pride/arrogance/boasting) (d:plural with te of ki-uatsakna, pride or boasting; used beside kisaktheihna, pride) (e:Jerusalem khuate’ ~ ka susia ding hi) (s:kiphatsaknate/kisaktheihna/kiliatsakna) (r:24.13.9) (q:draft)
ki-uktawm = (t:v) (w:control oneself/be self-controlled) (d:uk, rule, with ki, oneself, and tawm, by oneself: keep one's own body under control) (e:Nomau pumpi ~ thei-in pilvang unla) (s:kikemzo) (r:60.4.7) (q:draft)
ki-umcip = (t:v) (w:be enclosed/be shut in/be besieged) (d:um, surround, with cip, tightly, and the passive prefix ki; a ki-umcip before a noun means enclosed, as a garden, or besieged, as a city) (e:a ~ huan hi a/a ~ khuapi bangin kinusia hi | she is left like a besieged city) (s:kiumcih/kikhumcip) (r:22.4.12/23.1.8) (q:draft)
ki-upmawhnate = (t:n) (w:suspicions/mutual suspicion) (d:upmawh, suspect, with ki, each other, the noun suffix na and the plural te: suspicions that people have of one another) (e:a sia lamin ~ piangsak uh a) (r:54.6.4) (q:draft)
kia = (t:v) (w:fall/drop) (d:fall down or drop from a height; said of a person, of rain and of seed that falls on the ground; the form kiat is used before leh and ciangin) (e:lei tam lohna suang lakah ~ a/ama tawhsa gum sung mah ah amah ~ hi | he falls into the pit he has dug/kumpi khat peuhpeuh bangin na ~ ding uh hi | you will fall like any other ruler/pawn lak lopa tunga guah ~ | rain falling on a mown field/Kimkhatte ling lakah ~ a | some fell among thorns) (s:puk/tuk) (a:tho) (r:40.13.5/19.7.15/19.82.7/19.72.6/40.13.7) (q:draft)
kiak = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:thistle/brier) (d:a thorny weed that grows on neglected land, usually named together with ling, thorn) (e:~ leh ling po ta hen/ling leh ~ po ding hi | thorns and thistles will grow/a locing bup-ah ~ dim a | the whole field was full of thistles) (s:thangling/sialtalling) (r:18.31.40/28.10.8/20.24.31)
kiakhawm = (t:v) (w:fall together/fall in together) (d:kia, fall, with khawm, together: fall into something together; thong a kiakhawm is to be in prison together with someone) (e:leihawm sungah a ~ ding uh hi/a nih tuakun hawkguamah ~ ding uh hi | both will fall into a pit/nang tawh thong a ~ ding | to go to prison with you/Kei tawh thong a ~ Aristarkhas | Aristarchus, who is in prison with me) (s:tukkhawm/pukkhawm) (b:kia) (r:40.15.14/42.22.33/42.6.39/51.4.10) (q:draft)
kiakhia = (t:v) (w:fall off/fall from/drop off) (d:kia, fall, with khia, out or away: fall off from a person or place) (e:Elijah tung panin a ~ puan tawm a/ama tung panin a ~ Elijah’ puan la-in | taking the cloak of Elijah that had fallen from him/Assiria-te’ vangik ~ ding hi | the burden of the Assyrians will fall away) (b:kia) (r:12.2.13/23.14.25/12.2.14) (q:draft)
kiakhin = (t:v) (w:have fallen/have fallen off) (d:kia, fall, with khin, already or completely: have fallen off) (e:na lu tung pan-un ~ zo hi) (b:kia) (r:24.13.18) (q:draft)
kiakte = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:thistles) (e:Ling le ~, nang a dingin/~ nang’ adingin hong pokhiasak ding a | it will produce thistles for you) (b:kiak) (r:1.3.18) plural form of <kiak>
kial = (t:n) (w:famine/hunger) (d:a time when there is no food in the land, and the hunger it brings; kial tung is a famine comes) (e:~ hun ciangin tampi nei uh hi/tua gamah nakpi-in ~ tung a | a severe famine came on that land/khuapi sungah ~ nasia lua ahih manin | because the famine in the city was very severe/Mun khat khatah ~ hong tung ding a | famines will come in various places) (s:kialpi/gilkialna) (r:19.37.19/42.15.14/24.52.6/40.24.7) (q:draft)
kial = (t:v) (w:be hungry/hunger/go hungry) (d:be in need of food, usually in the phrase gil kial, the stomach is hungry) (e:Zeisu a gil ~ hi/Amaute gil ~ lo, dangtak lo ding uh a | they will neither hunger nor thirst/a mawk omte a gil ~ hi | the idle go hungry/a ni a cin’ ciangin a gil ~ hi | when the days were over he was hungry) (a:gilvah/vah) (r:40.21.18/20.19.15/23.49.10/42.4.2) (q:draft)
kialin = (t:v) (w:being hungry/going hungry) (d:kial, be hungry, with the linking suffix in; usually gil kialin, being or going hungry) (e:a tawpna-ah gil ~ sih lawh uh hi/Peter a gil ~ an duh mahmah hi | Peter became hungry and wanted food very much/gil ~, dangtakin, puansilh nei loin | hungry, thirsty and without clothing/mihoihte a gil ~ koih lo a | he does not let the righteous go hungry) (b:kial) (r:21.4.5/46.4.11/44.10.10/20.10.3) (q:draft)
kiallai = (t:v) (w:be still hungry) (d:kial, be hungry, with lai, still: be hungry still, even after eating) (e:na gil uh ~ veve ding hi/a gil uh ~ veve hi | they are still hungry) (r:33.6.14/23.9.20) (q:draft)
kialna = (t:n) (w:hunger/starvation) (d:kial, be hungry, with the noun suffix na: the state of being hungry) (e:Eite i ~ amaute in thei uh hi) (s:gilkialna) (b:kial) (r:12.7.12) (q:draft)
kialo = (t:v) (w:not fall) (d:kia, fall, with the negative lo written as one word; lei-ah kialo ding is will not fall to the ground, said of a hair of the head and of a word that will not fail) (e:samzang khat zong lei-ah ~ ding hi/Topa’ kammal khat zong lei-ah ~ ding hi | not one word of the Lord will fall to the ground/ama samzang khat zong leilakah ~ ding a | not one of his hairs will fall to the ground/amau a’ ding gamhluah bangmah ~ hi | no inheritance had fallen to them) (b:kia) (r:10.14.11/12.10.10/11.1.52/7.18.1) (q:draft)
kialpi = (t:n) (w:famine/severe famine) (d:kial, famine, with pi, great: a great famine in a land) (e:Amah in leitungah ~ tungsakin/Tu-in gamsungah ~ nasia semsem hi | now the famine in the land grew more and more severe/Tu-in Samaria ah ~ nasia hi | now the famine was severe in Samaria/~ tawh kong that ding a | I will kill you with famine) (s:kial/gilkialna) (b:kial) (r:19.105.16/1.43.1/11.18.2/23.14.30) (q:draft)
kialpite = (t:n) (w:famines/famine) (d:kialpi, famine, with the plural te) (e:pulnatna le ~ tawh na sih nadingun/~ in ni khat sungin a tung ding | famines will come in a single day) (b:kialpi) (r:24.34.17/66.18.8) (q:draft)
kiam = (t:v) (w:decrease/recede/go down/diminish) (d:become less in amount, number or strength; said of flood water that goes down, of a people or herd that grows fewer, and of flesh that wastes away) (e:~ kei un la, pung zaw un/leitung panin tuite ~ khinta hi | the water had receded from the earth/A ci a sa khempeuh ~ a | all his flesh wastes away/Pasian in leitungah huih nungsak a, tui ~ hi | God sent a wind over the earth and the water receded) (a:pung/khang) (r:24.29.6/1.8.3/1.8.11/18.33.21/1.8.1) (q:draft)
kiamgawp = (t:v) (w:waste away/fail/be greatly reduced) (d:kiam, decrease, with gawp, severely: of strength or the body, fail or waste away) (e:ka tha ~ ta a/ka pumpi silesa zong ~ khinta hi | my body too has wasted away) (b:kiam) (r:19.31.10/19.109.24) (q:draft)
kiamin = (t:v) (w:dwindling/decreasing) (d:kiam, decrease, with the linking suffix in: dwindling, growing less) (e:Nail gun hiangte ~ keucip ding a) (b:kiam) (r:23.19.6) (q:draft)
kiamkiam = (t:v) (w:keep going down/recede steadily) (d:kiam, decrease, repeated to show that it goes on little by little) (e:leitung panin tuite ~ hi/kha sawmna ciang dong tuite ~ lai hi | the water kept going down until the tenth month) (r:1.8.3/1.8.5) (q:draft)
kiamkik = (t:v) (w:dwindle again/decrease again) (d:kiam, decrease, with kik, back or again: grow less again, said of wealth quickly gained) (e:oltak mahin ~ pah a) (b:kiam) (r:20.13.11) (q:draft)
kiamsak = (t:v) (w:reduce/decrease/diminish) (d:kiam, become less, with the causative sak: make less, or let become fewer) (e:a man na ~ ding uh hi/amau’ bawngte zong ~ lo hi | he did not let their herds grow fewer/nuntakna a ~ ding cisa natna | a fever that will drain life away) (s:tawmsak/khiam) (a:pungsak/khangsak) (b:kiam) (r:3.25.16/19.107.38/3.26.16) (q:draft)
kiamsuk = (t:v) (w:sink/go down/subside) (d:kiam, go down, with suk, downward: sink or subside, as the Nile after its flood) (e:leitung khempeuh khang toin ~ ding hi/leitung buppi khang toin ~ ding hi | the whole land will rise and then sink) (a:khangto) (b:kiam) (r:30.8.8/30.9.5) (q:draft)
kiamvat = (t:v) (w:subside suddenly/abate at once) (d:kiam, decrease, with vat, suddenly: go down all at once, said of a fever that leaves) (e:a cisa hong ~ hi) (r:43.4.52) (q:draft)
kiang = (t:n) (w:presence/side) (d:the place beside or with someone; mostly in kiangah, to, and kiang panin, from) (e:Topa ~ panin kha gilo in/Kumpipa ~ pan migilote nilkhia lehang | if the wicked are removed from the presence of the king/ka ~ panin ka tapa la-in | taking my son from my side/ka galte ~ panin ka suakta hi | I am saved from my enemies) (r:9.16.14/44.17.33/20.25.5/11.3.20/19.18.3) (q:draft)
kianga = (t:prep) (w:to/beside/near/with) (d:kiang with the suffix a, used where the phrase describes a following noun or verb, as in pasian kianga thu nget, praying to God, and a kianga ding, standing beside him) (e:pasian ~ thu a nget a mu/a ~ ding a nasemte khempeuh | all his servants who stood beside him/Topa in Moses’ ~ a gensa thute khempeuh | everything the Lord had said to Moses/a ~ dingte khat in | one of those standing near him/Faro’ ~ kong gen bangin | as I said to Pharaoh) (b:kiang) (r:27.6.11/43.18.22/10.13.31/2.4.30/41.14.47/1.41.28) (q:draft)
kiangah = (t:prep) (w:to/beside/with) (d:kiang, presence or side, with the place marker ah: to, beside or with a person; it follows the person who is spoken to or approached) (e:Pasian ~ ngen in/ama ~ hong ciahkik nawn lo hi | it did not come back to him again/a misi nusia-in Hit mite’ ~ va pai a | leaving his dead, he went to the Hittites/kei ~ om in | stay with me/Na ~ mi tulkhat | a thousand at your side) (b:kiang) (r:2.6.10/5.2.17/1.8.12/1.23.3/1.29.19/19.91.7)
kiangahhong = (t:phrase) (w:to me) (d:kiangah, to or beside, run together with hong, toward the speaker; elsewhere written as two words, probably a printing error) (e:tuate kei’ ~ puak in | bring them to me) (r:1.27.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiangpan = (t:prep) (w:from) (d:from a person, from the presence of someone; kiang with pan, more often written kiang panin) (e:Pasian ~ hong kipia Kha i ngah zo hi/silate nangawn a topa’ ~ suakta hi | even the slaves are free from their master/a nute ~ paikhia-in ciahkik nawn lo uh hi | they leave their mothers and do not return/kei in ka Pa ~ thu ka ngah bangin | as I have received authority from my Father) (r:46.2.12/18.3.19/18.39.4/66.2.27) (q:draft)
kiangpanin = (t:prep) (w:from/away from) (d:from a person or from the presence of someone; kiangpan with the suffix in) (e:Absalom’ ~ ka tai lai-in) (b:kiangpan) (r:11.2.7) (q:draft)
kiasak = (t:v) (w:cause to fall/bring down/send down) (d:kia, fall, with the causative sak: make fall, bring a person down from a high place, or send down hail or birds from the sky) (e:kumpi tokhom tung pan ~ a/a tam mahmah gialpi ka ~ ding hi | I will send down a very heavy hailstorm/kua in a hong ~ zo ding hiam | who can bring me down/a kisia dingin amaute ~ in | make them fall to their ruin) (s:puksak/tuksak) (a:khangtosak) (b:kia) (r:42.1.52/2.9.18/31.1.3/19.35.8) (q:draft)
kiasakin = (t:v) (w:sending down/causing to fall) (d:kiasak, cause to fall, with the linking suffix in) (e:vantung panin mei ~ tua mite/gialpi ~, tua kulhpi ka susia ding hi | sending down hail, I will destroy that wall) (b:kiasak) (r:42.9.54/26.13.13) (q:draft)
kiasuk = (t:v) (w:fall down/come down/go down/descend) (d:kia, fall, with suk, downward: fall or come down from a higher place) (e:a thukna sungah amaute ~ uh hi/Amau bawlsa gum sungah minamte ~ uh a | the nations have fallen into the pit they made/inn thuap thum tung pan ~ a | he fell down from the third story/hel khua dongin na ~ ding hi | you will go down to Hades) (s:tuksuk) (a:kahto/paito) (b:kia) (r:2.15.5/19.104.8/19.9.15/44.20.9/42.10.15) (q:draft)
kiasukin = (t:v) (w:falling down) (d:kiasuk, fall down, with the linking suffix in) (e:meikuang bangin hong ~ gunte le) (s:tuksukin) (b:kiasuk) (r:66.8.10) (q:draft)
kiat = (t:v) (w:fall) (d:form of kia, fall, used before leh, ciangin, sangin, manin and other endings) (e:leibeel khatpeuh peuh sungah a ~ leh/tua dum sungah a ~ leh | if it falls into that pit/hel khua sungah na ~ sangin | than that you fall into hell/Tua singkung a ~ manin | because that tree fell) (b:kia) (r:3.11.33/20.23.27/2.21.33/40.5.29/26.31.16) (q:draft)
kiat = (t:v) (w:lose heart/falter/grow faint) (d:used with lung, heart: lung a kiat, the heart falls, means one is discouraged or grows faint) (e:na lung a ~ leh/ka lung a ~ ciangin, Topa ka phawk a | when my heart grew faint, I remembered the Lord) (s:lungkiat/lungkia) (b:kia) (r:20.24.10/32.2.7) (q:draft)
kiat = (t:v) (w:shave/shave off/scrape) (d:cut hair off close with a blade, or scrape a surface; kiat khia is shave off or scrape away) (e:khamul nawlhui zong ~ loin/na sam leh na khamul ~ khia in | shave off your hair and your beard/leitang khempeuh ~ khia-in suangtumte bek om lai ding | all the soil will be scraped away and only bare rock will be left) (s:met/meet) (r:3.21.5/26.5.1/26.26.4) (q:draft)
kiate = (t:n) (w:those that fall/fallen ones/what has fallen) (d:kia, fall, with the plural te: things that have fallen, as seed, grapes or crumbs) (e:Ling lakah a ~ in/Lei hoih ah a ~ in | those that fell on good soil/leenggah a ~ zong | also the grapes that have fallen/a topa sabuai panin anneng ~ | the crumbs that fall from the table of their master) (b:kia) (r:41.4.18/40.15.27/42.8.15/3.19.10) (q:draft)
kiatin = (t:v) (w:shaving/scraping) (d:kiat, shave or scrape, with the linking suffix in; said of shaving the hair and of scraping the walls of a house) (e:amah in a mul ~ a puan/a inn ~ a zut khit ciangin | after the house is scraped and plastered) (s:metin) (b:kiat) (r:1.41.14/3.14.43) (q:draft)
kiatkhia = (t:see) <kiatkhia-in>
kiatkhia-in = (t:v) (w:scraping away/scraping off) (d:kiat, scrape, with khia, out or away, and the linking suffix in: scraping something away) (e:leitang khempeuh ~ a suangtumte bek) (r:26.26.4) (q:draft)
kiatkhiat = (t:v) (w:scrape off/be scraped off) (d:kiat, scrape, with khiat, off or away; a kiatkhiat is what has been scraped off) (e:amaute in a ~/a ~, a kizutna themte | the bits of plaster that were scraped off) (b:kiat) (r:3.14.41) (q:draft)
kiatkhiatsak = (t:v) (w:have shaved off/cause to be shaved off) (d:kiatkhiat, shave or scrape off, with the causative sak: have something shaved off) (e:a khamul uh alang ciat ~ a) (b:kiatkhiat) (r:10.10.4) (q:draft)
kiatna = (t:n) (w:fall/downfall) (d:the act of falling, from kiat, fall, with the noun suffix na; za kiatna is loss of office and thong kiatna is being put in prison) (e:a ~ ging in minam khempeuh lok gawp/keekkia bangin Satan a ~ ka mu hi | I saw Satan fall like lightning/a gilo uliante’ za ~ mu ding uh hi | they will see the downfall of the wicked rulers/a ~ mun ama kiangah a lah ciangin | when he showed him the place where it fell) (s:pukna/tukna) (b:kiat) (r:26.31.16/20.29.16/42.10.18/12.6.6) (q:draft)
kiatna = (t:n) (w:razor) (d:in mul kiatna, a tool for shaving hair, from kiat, shave, with the noun suffix na) (e:lu tungah mul ~ kitah lo ding hi) (s:mulkiatna) (b:kiat) (r:4.6.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiatpih = (t:v) (w:fall together with/share a fall with) (d:kiat, form of kia, fall, with pih, together with; thong kiatpih is to be in prison together with someone, a fellow prisoner) (e:thong ka ~ Epafras a kipan) (b:kiat) (r:57.1.23) (q:draft)
kiatsak = (t:v) (w:cause to fall/bring down/send down) (d:kiat, fall, with the causative sak: make fall or send down; thong kiatsak is put in prison and za kiatsak is remove from a position) (e:vantung panin leitung dongin mei a ~ dongin/Kei thong nong ~ nadingin | that you should put me in prison/Sumkepna za hong ~ khit ciangin | after I am removed from my post as manager/a susia dingin gialpi ka ~ hangin | though I sent hail to destroy them) (s:puksak/tuksak) (b:kiat) (r:66.13.13/24.37.18/42.16.4/37.2.17) (q:draft)
kiatsakin = (t:v) (w:having scraped/causing to be scraped) (d:kiat, scrape, with the causative sak and the linking suffix in: having something scraped) (e:a innsung kimkot ~) (b:kiat) (r:3.14.41) (q:draft)
kiatsiang = (t:v) (w:shave clean/shave off) (d:kiat, shave, with siang, clean: shave away all the hair or beard) (e:a khamul uh ~ uh hi) (s:metkhia/mettol) (b:kiat) (r:24.48.37) (q:draft)
kiattheihna = (t:n) (d:kiat, fall, and theih, can, with the noun suffix na: the possibility of falling; kiattheihna ding gum is a pit that one can fall into) (e:~ ding gum tawh kibang a) (r:20.23.27) (q:draft)
kibaang = (t:v) (w:be put on/be laid on/be worn) (d:baang, put on, with the passive prefix ki: of a yoke, be laid on an animal; of clothing, be put on a person) (e:kol a ~ ngei lo bawngpi/puan zong note tungah ~ lo ding hi | nor shall such a garment be put on you) (b:baang) (r:9.6.7/3.19.19) (q:draft)
kibalnen = (t:v) (w:be torn to pieces/be cut in pieces) (d:balnen, tear in pieces, with the passive prefix ki; often followed by gawp, violently) (e:Josef ~ gawp a hihna/a kua sung, sa ~ tawh kidimsak ngei hi | he filled his den with torn flesh/a om leh ~ gawp ding a | if there is any, he will be cut to pieces) (s:kibalzan) (b:balnen) (r:1.37.33/27.3.29/34.2.12) (q:draft)
kibalnengawp = (t:v) (w:be torn to pieces/be cut in pieces) (d:kibalnen, be torn to pieces, with gawp, violently) (e:a om leh ~ ding a) (s:kibalzan) (b:kibalnen) (r:27.3.29) (q:draft)
kibalzan = (t:v) (w:be torn to pieces/be torn) (d:balzan, tear apart, with the passive prefix ki: said of a person or animal torn by a wild beast) (e:amah ~ khin taktak hi/a ~ ganhing ditkikna | restitution for the animal that was torn) (s:kibalnen) (b:balzan) (r:1.44.28/2.22.13) (q:draft)
kibang = (t:prep) (w:like) (d:be like; the thing compared with is followed by tawh, so that tawh kibang means is like) (e:sum zuakpa tawh ~ hi/mun kolhna-a om simbu tawh ka ~ hi | I am like an owl among the ruins/Judah pen humpinelkai tawh ~ a | Judah is like a lion/Izipt leitang tawh ~ lo hi | it is not like the land of Egypt) (s:kisun) (r:40.13.45/19.102.6/1.49.9/5.11.10)
kibang = (t:adj) (w:same/alike) (d:the same, not different; a kibang before a noun means the same, as in ngeina a kibang khat, one and the same law) (e:adingin a ~ thu khat/ngeina a ~ khat na nei ding uh hi | you are to have one and the same law/nang na ~ ngitnget a | you remain the same/a dangte mah tawh ~ hi | it was the same as the others) (s:kikim) (a:tuam) (r:4.15.16/3.24.22/19.102.27/26.40.35)
kibang = (t:n) (w:similar) (d:something that is like another; tawh a kibang khat is one that looks like) (e:hih innpi tawh a ~ inn khat/mihing meel tawh a ~ khat | one who looked like a man/sapi vompi tawh a ~ khat ka mu hi | I saw one that looked like a bear) (r:11.7.8/26.10.10/27.8.15/27.7.5)
kibanga = (t:adj) (w:like/similar/alike) (d:kibang, be alike, with the linking ending a before another verb; tawh kibanga kibawl means made to be like, as in ngen tawh kibanga kibawl, made like a net, the network on the temple pillars) (e:Pasian tawh a ~ kibawl mi thak/ngen tawh ~ kibawl nihte | the two sets made like a net/ngen tawh ~ kibawl khat adingin | for each one made like a net) (b:kibang) (r:49.4.21/11.7.41/11.7.42) (q:draft)
kibangbang = (t:v) (w:remain the same/stay as it is) (d:kibang, be the same, with bang repeated: go on being the same, remain as it is) (e:leitung ~ niloh hi) (r:21.1.4) (q:draft)
kibangin = (t:adv) (w:alike/likewise/in the same way) (d:kibang, be alike, with the suffix in: alike, equally; after tawh, in the same way as) (e:tua tawh ~ a piang ding hi/a neu a lian a ~ | young and old alike/amaute in a ~ tang ding uh hi | they will share alike/Pasal tawh ~ thacingin, thahat un | be courageous like men, be strong) (b:kibang) (r:42.17.30/13.26.13/9.30.24/46.16.13) (q:draft)
kibangkha = (t:v) (w:seem/appear like/look like) (d:kibang, be like, with kha, happen to: after tawh, may seem to be) (e:A tung hak tawh a ~ ahi zongin/tangtun zo lo tawh ka ~ uh ahi zongin | though we may seem to have failed) (r:35.2.3/47.13.7) (q:draft)
kibangkim = (t:adj) (w:all alike/all the same/equal) (d:kibang, same, with kim, all: all alike, all the same) (e:ni khempeuh ~ hi/I vekpi-in gim hong kipiakna ~ hi | we are all under the same punishment/a ~ na hi uh hi | you are all alike) (s:kikim) (r:45.14.5/48.3.28/42.23.40) (q:draft)
kibanglai = (t:v) (w:still be like) (d:kibang, be like, with lai, still: after tawh, still be like) (e:puannin tawh ~ veve hi) (r:23.64.6) (q:draft)
kibangmah = (t:see) <kibangmah-in>
kibangmah-in = (t:adv) (w:in the same way/just the same) (d:kibang same with the emphatic mah and the suffix in; another spelling of kibangmahin) (e:kiangah a ~ na gen ding uh hi) (s:kibangmahin) (r:1.32.19) (q:draft)
kibangmahin = (t:adv) (w:in the same way/just the same) (d:kibang same with the emphatic mah and the suffix in) (e:a ~ na gen ding uh hi) (s:kibangmah-in) (r:1.32.19) (q:draft)
kibangsak = (t:v) (w:make equal/make like/make the same) (d:kibang, be alike, with the causative sak: make or treat one as the same as another; tawh marks the one compared with) (e:nisa thuak kote tawh hong ~ hi/huih letkhiat ansite tawh ~ in | make them like chaff blown by the wind/a gindan na ~ kei ding hi | you shall not make the signal the same/tu-ma-kuakte tawh ~ uh hi | they made it like furrows) (s:bangsak/batsak/kikimsak) (b:kibang) (r:40.20.12/19.35.5/4.10.7/19.129.3) (q:draft)
kibangsakin = (t:v) (w:likening/making equal/comparing) (d:kibangsak, make like, with the linking suffix in; tawh marks the one compared with) (e:kua tawh hong ~ kua tawh) (b:kibangsak) (r:23.46.5) (q:draft)
kibangta = (t:v) (w:be like now/have become like) (d:kibang, be like, with ta, marking a state now reached: after tawh, have become like) (e:naupang tawh ka ~ hi) (s:bangta) (b:kibang) (r:19.131.2) (q:draft)
kibangte = (t:n) (w:those that are like/those that seem) (d:kibang, be like, with the plural te: those that are like or seem; it follows tawh) (e:ginalo tawh a ~ a kimanna) (b:kibang) (r:46.12.22) (q:draft)
kibangzaw = (t:v) (w:be more like/be rather like) (d:kibang, be like, with zaw, more or rather: after tawh, be more like) (e:awle tawh na ~ hi) (b:kibang) (r:26.32.2) (q:draft)
kibaptaiz = (t:v) (w:be baptized) (d:baptaiz, baptize, a loanword from English, with the passive prefix ki: be baptized) (e:Zeisu’ min sungah a ~ uh hi/Jordan gun sungah ama khut tungah ~ uh hi | they were baptized by him in the Jordan River/Tua thu a mang mite in ~ uh a | those who accepted the message were baptized/kua min tawh na ~ uh hiam | in whose name were you baptized) (s:kituiphum/kiphum) (b:baptaiz) (r:44.19.5/44.2.41/40.3.6/44.19.3) (q:draft)
kibaptaizna = (t:n) (w:baptism) (d:kibaptaiz, be baptized, with the noun suffix na: the baptism that one receives) (e:ama sihna sungah ~ i ngah hi) (s:kituiphumna/baptaizna/tuiphumna) (b:kibaptaiz) (r:45.6.3) (q:draft)
kibaptaizte = (t:n) (w:those who are baptized) (d:kibaptaiz, be baptized, with the plural te) (e:a ~ in gupna a ngah ding) (b:kibaptaiz) (r:41.16.16) (q:draft)
kibasak = (t:v) (w:owe one another/be in debt to each other) (d:ba, owe, with ki, each other, and sak: owe one another something) (e:bangmah na ~ kei un) (r:45.13.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
kibat = (t:prep) (w:like) (d:used with tawh, with: be like someone or something) (e:Pasian tawh na ~ ding lamtak uh/ama maitang in vantungmi’ maitang tawh a ~ lam | that his face was like the face of an angel/paisukte tawh ka ~ loh nadingin | so that I will not be like those who go down/amah tawh na ~ nadingun hanciam un | strive to be like him) (s:kibang/kisun) (r:1.3.5/44.6.15/19.143.7/49.5.1)
kibat = (t:conj) (w:as) (d:with tawh: being as another is, or seeming as if something were so) (e:amah tawh ~ ding a lamen khempeuh | all who hope to be as he is/a hi thei lo ding tawh a ~ hangin | though it seems as if it cannot be) (r:62.3.3/38.8.6)
kibat = (t:adj) (w:similar/alike) (d:alike, the same as each other; a kibat kei leh is if they are not alike) (e:na lungsim ngaihsutna uh a ~ kei leh | if your thinking is not alike) (s:kibanga/kisun) (a:tuam) (r:50.3.15)
kibatlohna = (t:n) (w:difference/unlikeness) (d:the fact of not being alike, a difference: kibat be alike, loh not, with the noun suffix na) (e:Egypt numeite a ~ hang ahi hi) (s:kilamdanna/kideidanna) (a:kibatna) (r:2.1.19) (q:draft)
kibatna = (t:n) (w:likeness/resemblance/similarity) (d:how one thing is like another, or what two have in common; tawh a kibatna is likeness to something) (e:mi bawlsiapa a ~ uh khat om hi/Mi tawh ~-ah a suak hi | he was made in human likeness/nomau leitang tawh a ~ mun | a place like your own land) (s:batna) (a:kibatlohna/kilamdanna) (b:kibat) (r:20.29.13/50.2.7/12.18.31) (q:draft)
kibatnate = (t:n) (w:equality/likenesses) (d:kibatna, likeness, with the plural te: the ways in which one is like or equal to another, as in Pasian tawh kibatnate, equality with God) (e:Pasian tawh ~ ka khah kei ding) (b:kibatna) (r:50.2.6) (q:draft)
kibatpih = (t:v) (w:be like/be alike with/be equal to) (d:kibat be like with pih together with: be like another; ka kibatpih ding, one for me to be like, my equal) (e:ka ~ dingin kua tawh hong enteh ding) (b:kibat) (r:23.46.5) (q:draft)
kibawl = (t:v) (w:be made/be prepared/be done) (d:passive of bawl, make or do: be made, prepared or done; with tawh, made of or prepared with something) (e:Kham tawh ~ a kiphut kizepna/hih nazatte khempeuh ~ ding hi | all these utensils are to be made/Mual liante a ~ ma-in kei ka suak khin | before the great mountains were made I was born/sathau tawh a ~ annel hi ding hi | it is to be fine flour prepared with oil/Tu ni-a a ~ bangin | as has been done today) (b:bawl) (r:2.28.13/14.4.21/2.25.39/20.8.25/3.2.5/3.8.34) (q:draft)
kibawla = (t:v) (w:made/arranged/prepared) (d:kibawl be made with the linking a; kibawla a om, be in a prepared state) (e:hih na khempeuh ~ a om ciangin) (b:kibawl) (r:58.9.6) (q:draft)
kibawlbawl = (t:v) (w:make oneself/keep making oneself) (d:ki oneself with bawl make, repeated: be making oneself into something) (e:dingin a ~ ahi uh hi) (s:kibawltawm) (b:kibawl) (r:59.4.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
kibawlin = (t:v) (w:being made/be made/be prepared) (d:form of kibawl, be made, with the linking suffix in: being made, and then going on to what follows) (e:Salem khua sungah ama omna ~/a kop-a kikhuk puan hoihte tawh ~ | made with finely twisted linen/a dum, a dupsan, a ausan khaute tawh ~ | made with blue, purple and scarlet yarn/a kigan puan hoihte tawh ~ | made with finely woven linen) (b:kibawl) (r:19.76.2/2.28.8/2.36.8/2.39.5) (q:draft)
kibawlkhol = (t:v) (w:be prepared/be made ready) (d:passive ki with bawlkhol, prepare beforehand: be made ready in advance) (e:Topa ading a ~ mite) (b:bawlkhol) (r:42.1.17) (q:draft)
kibawlkholsa = (t:adj) (w:prepared beforehand/made ready) (d:kibawlkhol, be prepared in advance, with sa, already: prepared and waiting) (e:note ading a ~ Gamah hong pai/a ~-a om gupkhiatna i ngah nadingin | so that we receive the salvation that is ready) (s:kithawisa) (b:kibawlkhol) (r:40.25.34/60.1.5) (q:draft)
kibawlna = (t:n) (w:doing/making/performing) (d:noun form of kibawl, be made or done: the act, place or means of something being done; pawi kibawlna inn is a house where a feast is held) (e:Pawi ~ innah na pai kei ding/kilemna a ~ tua ante ne ding uh hi | they shall eat the food with which atonement was made/hih nalamdang a ~ mipa | the man on whom this miracle was done/Tua din’nate a ~ zia in hih bang ahi hi | this is how the stands were made) (b:kibawl) (r:24.16.8/2.29.33/44.4.22/11.7.28) (q:draft)
kibawlpha = (t:v) (w:be reformed/be renewed/be put right) (d:bawlpha put right with ki, passive or of oneself: mend one's ways under correction, or be made new) (e:amaute ~ tuan lo uh hi/pilna maan adingin a ~ mithak | the new self that is renewed for true knowledge) (s:kipuahpha/thaksuak) (b:bawlpha) (r:24.2.30/51.3.9) (q:draft)
kibawlphat = (t:v) (w:be repaired/be rebuilt/reform) (d:form of kibawlpha used before kik, hun and similar words: be put right again, of a broken jar, a ruined city or a person who mends his ways) (e:khuapi a ~ hun hong tung ding/Mite a ~ kik kei leh | if people do not reform/a ~ kik theih nawn loh bangmahin | just as it can no longer be repaired) (s:kilamkik) (b:kibawlpha) (r:24.31.38/24.19.11/19.7.12) (q:draft)
kibawlsa = (t:adj) (w:made/prepared/furnished/already done) (d:kibawl, be made, with sa, already done: made, prepared or finished beforehand; a kibawlsa na is the thing that has been made) (e:a ~ dei tungnung a lian khat/a ~ suangte tawh kilam hi | it was built with stones already dressed/a ~ na in a bawlpa tawh kisai-in | the thing made, speaking of its maker/a ~ nate-ah kisathei loin | not boasting in work already done) (s:kithawisa) (b:kibawl) (r:42.22.12/23.29.16/11.6.7/47.10.16) (q:draft)
kibawlsak = (t:v) (w:be made for/be prepared for) (d:kibawl, be made, with sak: be made or done on behalf of someone, as atonement made for the people) (e:nangma adingin na suah ni-in hong ~ hi/kum khatin khat vei kilemna a ~ theih nadingin | so that atonement may be made once a year/a leipa in khang tawntungin a neih dingin ~ ding hi | it shall be made the buyer’s to own permanently) (b:kibawl) (r:26.28.13/3.16.34/3.25.30) (q:draft)
kibawlsakna = (t:n) (d:that by which something is made for someone: kibawlsak be made for, with the noun suffix na; of the ram with which atonement is made for a person) (e:adingin kilemna a ~ ahi kilemna tuutal) (b:kibawlsak) (r:4.5.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
kibawlsia = (t:v) (w:be persecuted/be mistreated/be harmed) (d:bawlsia, mistreat, with the passive ki: be treated badly, harmed or persecuted by others) (e:lo dangah nang hong ~ ding hi/note hong ~-in hong kithat ding a | you will be persecuted and killed/keima hangin note hong kimanin hong ~ ding hi | because of me you will be seized and persecuted/tuhunin zong eite hong ~ hi | now too we are persecuted) (s:kibawlsiat/kinengniam) (b:bawlsia) (r:8.2.22/40.24.9/42.21.12/48.4.29) (q:draft)
kibawlsia = (t:v) (w:hurt each other/wrong one another) (d:bawlsia, mistreat, with ki in its sense of each other: hurt or wrong one another) (e:khat leh khat na ~ uh hiam) (b:bawlsia) (r:44.7.26) (q:draft)
kibawlsiat = (t:v) (w:be persecuted/be mistreated) (d:passive of bawlsiat; with hong, to be persecuted by others) (e:Khua khatah note hong ~ leh/pawlpite kimkhat a ~ theih nadingin thu pia a | he gave orders so that some of the church could be persecuted/delhin hong ~ hangin hong nusia kei hi | though we are hunted and persecuted, he has not abandoned us/Hong ~ leh, ka thuak uh hi | when we are persecuted, we endure) (s:kibawlsia/kinengniam) (b:bawlsiat) (r:40.10.23/46.4.12/44.12.1/47.4.9) (q:draft)
kibawlsiatna = (t:n) (w:persecution/torment/mistreatment) (d:the persecution or torment that people suffer; also of people provoking or harming one another, khat leh khat kibawlsiatna) (e:Stefen tungah ~ thu hangin/Pasian’ mite ~ a bei ciangin | when the persecution of God’s people ends/Khat leh khat ~, khat leh khat kihazatna | provoking one another, envying one another) (s:bawlsiatna/gimsakna) (b:bawlsiatna) (r:44.11.19/66.14.11/27.12.7/48.5.26) (q:draft)
kibawlsiatnate = (t:n) (w:acts of mistreatment/wrongs done to one another) (d:kibawlsiatna with plural te) (e:thuman lohna, leh ~ ka deih kei hi) (b:kibawlsiatna) (r:38.8.17) (q:draft)
kibawltawm = (t:v) (w:make oneself/make oneself out to be) (d:bawltawm with ki, of oneself: make oneself into something, as unclean by what one touches, or like an angel in appearance) (e:vantungmi tawh a kibangin ~ thei hi/nomau mah a kihhuai-in na ~ kei ding uh a | you shall not make yourselves detestable) (s:kibawlbawl) (b:bawltawm) (r:47.11.14/3.11.43) (q:draft)
kibawltawm = (t:adj) (w:artificial/man-made) (d:a kibawltawm before a noun: made by people, not natural) (e:a ~ bual leh Galkap Inn) (b:bawltawm) (r:16.3.16) (q:draft)
kibawlte = (t:n) (w:things made/carved figures) (d:things that are made, fashioned or carved, as lim kibawlte carved figures) (e:lim ~ tawh kidim a/tuate tungah unok pak a ~ om hi | on them were shapes made like lilies/om nate khempeuh adingin a ~ | the things made for all the hosts) (b:kibawl) (r:26.41.17/11.7.19/12.23.4) (q:draft)
kibawlzawh = (t:v) (w:have been made/be established) (d:kibawl be made with zawh, finished; a kibawlzawh, after it was made) (e:tua thuciamna a ~ kum zali) (r:48.3.17) (q:draft)
kibeh = (t:v) (w:be related/be kin) (d:beh clan with ki, one another: belong to the same family; a kibeh is a relative) (e:eite a ~ i hi hi/Piter in a bil a satpa tawh a ~ | a relative of the man whose ear Peter cut off) (b:beh) (r:1.13.8/43.18.26) (q:draft)
kibeh = (t:v) (w:be added/increase) (d:in kibeh laplap, keep being added, pile up) (e:a mawkna thu mah ~ laplap hi) (r:21.5.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
kibehlap = (t:v) (w:be added/be joined) (d:be added to a number or group; tawh names what one is added to) (e:mi tulthum bang a ~ uh hi/numei tampi in Topa tawh a ~ uh hi | many women were added to the Lord/note’ hamphatna a ~ nading ka deihna hizaw hi | what I want is for your credit to be added to/Kammal kibang zong tampi a ~ hi | many similar words were added) (b:behlap) (r:44.2.41/44.5.14/50.4.17/24.36.32) (q:draft)
kibehlaplap = (t:v) (w:keep increasing/be added more and more) (d:kibehlap, be added, with its last syllable repeated: keep being added, grow more and more in number or amount) (e:a neihsa ~ ahih manin/Absalom tawh a om mite ~ hi | Absalom’s followers kept increasing/a nini-in mi a ~ hi | people were added day by day/numei pasal tampi tak hong ~ uh hi | more and more men and women were added) (b:behlaplap) (r:1.26.13/44.5.14/10.15.12/44.16.5) (q:draft)
kibehlapsak = (t:v) (w:add to/cause to be added) (d:kibehlap be added with the causative sak: add people to a group) (e:a ngah mi ~ tawntung hi/ni simin Pasian in a ~ hi | God added them day by day) (b:kibehlap) (r:44.2.47) (q:draft)
kibehlapto = (t:v) (w:be added on/be heaped upon) (d:kibehlap be added with to, upward or on top) (e:keima dahna ~ sawnsawn ding) (b:kibehlap) (r:50.2.27) (q:draft)
kibeimangsak = (t:v) (w:be destroyed/be wiped out/perish) (d:passive ki with beimangsak, destroy) (e:Topa a nusiate pen ~ ding hi) (s:kisusia/kisiat) (b:beimangsak) (r:23.1.28) (q:draft)
kibeisak = (t:v) (w:be wiped out/be exterminated/be brought to an end) (d:passive ki with beisak, bring to an end: be wiped out or made to cease) (e:leitung kipahna ~ ta hi/hehpihna ngah loin a ~ theih nadingin | so that they might be wiped out without mercy/leitung panin note hong ~ thei hi | you could have been wiped off the earth) (s:kiphiat/kibeimangsak) (b:beisak) (r:23.24.11/6.11.20/2.9.15) (q:draft)
kibet = (t:v) (w:be struck/be slapped) (d:passive ki with bet strike) (e:kei hong ~ nadingin thu na pia hi) (s:kisat) (b:bet) (r:44.23.3) (q:draft)
kibet = (t:v) (w:be uprooted/be plucked up) (d:with khiat, out: be pulled up out of the ground) (e:Amaute a ~ khiat nading) (s:kibotkhia/kisuankhia) (a:kisuan) (r:24.31.28) (q:draft, low confidence)
kibetkhiatna = (t:n) (w:uprooting/plucking out) (d:the act of being pulled up or out, with the noun suffix na) (e:Amaute a ~ ding le) (r:24.31.28) (q:draft, low confidence)
kibia = (t:v) (w:be worshipped) (d:passive of bia, worship: be worshipped) (e:a ~ na khempeuh ahi zongin/tua biakinn sungah kei hong ~ ding a | I will be worshipped in that temple) (b:bia) (r:53.2.4/11.9.3) (q:draft)
kibia = (t:v) (w:offer oneself) (d:give oneself as an offering to God) (e:ama pumpi kipia-in, ~-in, eite tangding) (r:49.5.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
kibiakna = (t:n) (w:worship) (d:the worshipping of God or a god; kibiakna mun is the place where he is worshipped, a sanctuary) (e:nangmah hong ~ mun susia uh hi/Pasian a ~ mun mual dawnah David a tun’ ciangin | when David reached the hilltop where God was worshipped/keimah hong ~ mun na zahtak ding uh hi | you shall revere my sanctuary) (s:biakna) (b:biakna) (r:19.74.7/3.19.30/10.15.32) (q:draft)
kibiakna = (t:n) (w:offering) (d:what is offered to the Lord in worship) (e:Topa a ~ na pia ding uh hi/mei tawh kihal keimah hong ~ an | the food offered to me by fire) (s:biakna) (b:biakna) (r:4.18.28/4.28.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
kibiaknate = (t:n) (w:offerings/sacrifices) (d:kibiakna offering with plural te: the things offered in worship; keimah hong kibiaknate, the offerings made to me) (e:keimah hong ~ khempeuh/keimah hong ~ le ka thupiak ahi keimah hong kipiakte | my sacrifices and the offerings I commanded) (s:biaknate/kithoihnate) (b:kibiakna) (r:9.2.28/9.2.29) (q:draft)
kibokcip = (t:v) (w:be brought low/be pressed down) (d:be bowed down flat; used with kikun, be bent over) (e:hong ~ sak hi) (r:19.38.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
kibokcipsak = (t:v) (w:bring very low/press down) (d:kibokcip be pressed down with the causative sak) (e:keimah hong kikunsak a, hong ~ hi) (b:kibokcip) (r:19.38.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
kibom = (t:v) (w:hang on/cling to) (d:hang together on something like a bunch, as vessels hung on a peg; perhaps from bom, cluster) (e:ama tungah ~ ding uh hi) (r:23.22.24) (q:draft, low confidence)
kibotkhia = (t:v) (w:be uprooted/be pulled up/be torn out) (d:passive ki with botkhia, pull out: be pulled up by the roots, or be torn out of its place) (e:a suan loh kung khempeuh ~ ding hi/singkung zung bawh bangin mawhneite ~ ding hi | sinners will be torn out like an uprooted tree/Zung tawh ~-in tuipi sungah na po in | be uprooted and grow in the sea/ama ukna ~-in midangte’ tungah kipia ding hi | his rule will be uprooted and given to others) (s:kizunglot/kisuankhia/kidokkhia/kizungbawh) (a:kisuan) (b:botkhia) (r:40.15.13/20.2.22/42.17.6/27.11.4) (q:draft)
kibottat = (t:v) (w:be broken/snap/be torn apart) (d:of a cord or snare: be pulled until it breaks, from bot, pull) (e:thangkhau ~ a, eite i suakta) (s:kitat/kitan) (r:19.124.7) (q:draft)
Kibrothhattaavah = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Kibroth Hattaavah) (d:camp of Israel in the wilderness between Sinai and Hazeroth, where the people who craved meat were buried) (r:4.33.16/4.33.17)
Kibrothhattavah = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Kibroth Hattaavah) (d:camp of Israel in the wilderness before Hazeroth, named graves of craving because the people who craved meat were buried there) (r:4.11.34/4.11.35)
kibu = (t:v) (w:be hidden) (d:passive ki with bu, hide: be hidden or kept secret) (e:a ~ bangmah om lo hi) (s:kiseel/kiliah) (a:kilang/kilak) (b:bu) (r:41.4.22) (q:draft)
kibua = (t:v) (w:be poured out/be shed) (d:passive of bua, pour: be poured out or shed, said of blood, water or anger) (e:Sisan ~ loin mawhna maisakna/note tungah ka hehna hong ~ ding hi | my wrath will be poured out on you/Hih hai in note ading a ~ | this cup, poured out for you/Tui bangin kei hong ~ khia a | I am poured out like water) (s:kibuak/kibuakhia) (b:bua) (r:58.9.22/24.42.18/42.22.20/19.22.14) (q:draft)
kibuai = (t:v) (w:be in uproar/be in confusion) (d:buai, be troubled, with ki: be in disorder and noise, said of a crowd) (e:Mihon ~ lua a) (s:kigamlum/gamlum) (b:buai) (r:44.21.34) (q:draft)
kibuaigawp = (t:v) (w:be thrown into confusion) (d:kibuai be in confusion with gawp, violently) (e:maizumin ~ sak in) (b:kibuai) (r:19.70.2) (q:draft)
kibuaigawpsak = (t:v) (w:throw into confusion/confound) (d:kibuaigawp be thrown into confusion with the causative sak) (e:thah hong sawmte maizumin ~ in) (b:kibuaigawp) (r:19.70.2) (q:draft)
kibuaisak = (t:v) (w:be thrown into confusion/be troubled) (d:passive ki with buaisak, trouble, disturb) (e:amaute a bei matengin ~ ding hi) (b:buaisak) (r:5.7.23) (q:draft)
kibuak = (t:v) (w:be sprinkled/be poured/be shed) (d:passive of buak: a liquid is poured or sprinkled on someone, blood is shed) (e:ama tungah tui ~ lo ahih manin/A nuntakna uh, tui ~ huan bang ahi ding a | their life will be like a watered garden/ka hehna leh ka thangpaihna a ~ mah bangin | as my anger and wrath were poured out) (s:kitheh/kibua/kiluan) (b:buak) (r:4.19.20/44.22.20/24.31.12/24.42.18) (q:draft)
kibuak = (t:v) (w:sprinkle on oneself/put on oneself) (d:throw dust or ashes over oneself as a sign of grief) (e:a lu tung uhah lei ~ uh hi/a puan balkekin puanhampi silhin vut ~ a | he tore his clothes and put on sackcloth and ashes) (b:buak) (r:16.9.1/17.4.1) (q:draft)
kibuakhia = (t:v) (w:be poured out/spill out) (d:kibua, be poured, with khia, out: be poured or spilled out) (e:biakna tau panin a vutte ~ hi/a tunga om vutte ~ ding hi | the ashes on it will be poured out/biakna tau tungah ~ ding a | it shall be poured out on the altar/Tui buakkhiat bangin kei hong ~ a | I am poured out like water) (s:kibua/kibuak) (b:kibua) (r:11.13.5/5.12.27/11.13.3/19.22.14) (q:draft)
kibuakin = (t:v) (w:sprinkling on oneself/throwing on oneself) (d:kibuak with the linking suffix in: putting dust or ashes on oneself as a sign of grief) (e:a lutang uhah leivui ~/khautang puan silhin, vut tawh ~ | wearing sackcloth and covered with ashes) (b:kibuak) (r:66.18.19/42.10.13) (q:draft)
kibuakna = (t:n) (w:place of pouring out/dump/heap) (d:kibuak, be poured out, with the noun suffix na: the place where something is poured or thrown out; vut kibuakna is the ash heap) (e:vutte a ~ kuam buppi leh/vut a ~-ah kihal ding hi | it shall be burned on the ash heap/dawn ding biakna a ~ innte khempeuh | all the houses where drink offerings were poured out) (b:kibuak) (r:24.31.40/3.4.12/24.19.13) (q:draft)
kibuan = (t:v) (w:be raped/be violated/be mistreated) (d:be seized and used with violence; said of women when a city is taken) (e:numeite zong ~ ding hi/a hong ~ gawp hi | you have been violently mistreated) (s:kibuansak) (r:38.14.2/24.13.22) (q:draft)
kibuansak = (t:v) (w:be violated/be raped/be ravished) (d:kibuan, be violated, with sak: said of women forced by men) (e:a zite uh ~ ding hi/ka ta nungakte uh a hong ~ hi | our young daughters have been violated/Zion mual-ah ka zite uh hong ~ a | our wives have been violated on Mount Zion) (s:kibuan) (b:kibuan) (r:23.13.16/25.5.11) (q:draft)
kibuasa = (t:adj) (w:shed/poured out) (d:kibua be poured out, with sa for a completed action; said of blood) (e:a ~, kiciamna si ahi hi/leitungah a ~ miphate’ si khempeuh | all the blood of the righteous shed on earth/mi tampite’ mawhna kimaisak nading a ~ | poured out for the forgiveness of many people’s sins/leitung pian’ akipan a ~ Pasian’ kamsangte khempeuh’ si | the blood of all God’s prophets shed since the world began) (b:kibua) (r:41.14.24/42.11.50/40.23.35/40.26.28) (q:draft)
kibulh = (t:v) (w:be put on/be fastened/be chained) (d:passive ki with bulh, put on or fasten: be fixed onto something, set in a mounting or grafted in; kol kibulh and sikkol kibulh mean be put in chains) (e:sikkol ~ thei lo hi/kham tawh zepna sungah tuate ~ ding hi | they are to be set in gold settings/na khete kol ~ lo hi | your feet were not fettered/en in, na khuta ~ kolte | see, the chains fastened on your hand/amau pum tungah pehin ~ a | grafted and joined onto their trunk) (s:kihen) (a:kisutkhia) (b:bulh) (r:55.2.9/11.7.28/2.28.20/10.3.34/24.40.4/45.11.17) (q:draft)
kibulhin = (t:v) (w:be bound/be chained) (d:kibulh, be fastened on, with the linking suffix in: being bound, said of chains or fetters put on a person) (e:sikkol ~ gimna thuakin/A miliante, sikkol ~ kipua khia a | her great men were put in chains and carried off/leinuai khuamial sungah sikkol ~ | bound in chains in the darkness below) (b:kibulh) (r:19.107.10/65.1.6/34.3.10) (q:draft)
kibulhsa = (t:adj) (w:fastened on/set in place/chained) (d:kibulh be put on with sa, already: of lamps set on a stand, or of people put in chains) (e:meivak a ~ tawh a meivakte/Amaute sikkhau ~-in hong pai ding uh a | they will come over in chains) (b:kibulh) (r:2.39.37/23.45.14) (q:draft)
kibulhtawm = (t:v) (w:commit oneself/set oneself/attach oneself) (d:kibulh be fastened with tawm, of oneself: fix oneself on a course of one's own accord) (e:hoih lohna-ah amah ~ hi) (r:19.36.4) (q:draft)
kibulphuh = (t:v) (w:be taken as the basis/be based on) (d:passive ki with bulphuh base on) (e:nomau kampau mah hong ~ ding hi) (b:bulphuh) (r:40.12.37) (q:draft)
kibuluh = (t:v) (w:be plundered/be ransacked) (d:passive ki with buluh, plunder: be raided and stripped of goods) (e:No hong buluhte ~ ding a/Ahih hangin Esau, ~ khin zo a | but Esau has been ransacked) (s:kiluh/kisut) (b:buluh) (r:24.30.16/31.1.6) (q:draft)
kibum = (t:v) (w:be bewitched/be put under a spell) (d:passive ki with bum bewitch) (e:Jakob mite a ~ nading om lo a) (b:bum) (r:4.23.23) (q:draft)
kibup = (t:adv) (w:wholly/entirely) (d:ki oneself with bup whole; in kibup piak, give oneself wholly, devote oneself, elsewhere written as one word kibuppiak) (e:Levi mite a ~ piak theih nadingun) (b:bup) (r:14.31.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
kibuppiak = (t:v) (w:devote oneself/give oneself wholly) (d:ki oneself with buppiak give wholly) (e:Levi mite a ~ theih nadingun) (s:kipumpiak) (b:buppiak) (r:14.31.4) (q:draft)
