kici = (t:v) (w:be called) (d:passive of ci, say: be called by a name or title) (e:thusia bawl mi ~ hi/Eurakuilo ~ huihpi in lei lam panin nung a | a wind called the Northeaster blew from the land/Golgotha ~ mun a tun’ uh ciangin | when they came to the place called Golgotha/a kilakhia ahih manin Numei ~ ding hi | she shall be called woman because she was taken out) (s:kilo/kiphuak) (b:ci) (r:20.24.8/1.2.23/44.27.14/40.27.33)
kici = (t:v) (w:be named) (d:have as a name; a kici min nei is bearing the name) (e:Barnabas in Marka ~ Johan sap ding/Mikah a ~ min nei mi khat om hi | there was a man named Micah/a khat Medad ~ a | the other was named Medad) (s:kiphuak/kilo) (b:ci) (r:44.15.37/7.17.1/4.11.26)
kiciahpih = (t:v) (w:be brought back/be taken home) (d:passive ki with ciahpih, take home or take along: be taken back, or be taken away to another place; with kik, be brought back again) (e:amah pua-in ~ hi/pawlkhat, galmatin gam dangah ~ ding hi | some will be taken as captives to other lands/Babilon panin salte a ~ kik ciangin | when the exiles were brought back from Babylon/a hong ~ kik khin na hi uh hi | you have now been brought back) (s:kipuakik) (b:ciahpih) (r:14.25.28/60.2.25/42.21.24/15.1.11) (q:draft)
kiciahsak = (t:v) (w:be sent back/be sent away) (d:passive ki with ciahsak, send away) (e:a mun dang khatah ~ a) (s:kisawlkhia) (b:ciahsak) (r:17.2.14) (q:draft)
kicial = (t:adj) (w:hired) (d:passive of cial hire; a kicial is a hired hand, a kicial nasem a hired worker) (e:a ~ nasempa in a thaman a ngak/Peemta hita leh a ~ nasem hita leh | whether a temporary resident or a hired worker/Amah in a ~ hi a | he is a hired hand/a ~ nasemte dah ding hi | the hired workers will grieve) (b:cial) (r:18.7.2/43.10.13/2.12.45/23.19.10) (q:draft)
kicialtawm = (t:v) (w:be hired/hired) (d:of a person who works for wages and is not the owner; a kicialtawm tuucingpa, the hired shepherd) (e:a ~ tuucingpa in ngia khawng) (r:43.10.12) (q:draft)
kiciam = (t:v) (w:swear/take an oath/vow/promise) (d:ciam, promise, with ki: bind oneself by an oath or vow; min tawh kiciam is swear by a name) (e:na thute zuih ding ka ~ hi/Ka ~ ding hi | I will swear/ama min tawh na ~ ding uh hi | you shall swear by his name/A hi lopi-in na ~ kei in | do not swear falsely/Tuam om dingin a ~ hun sung teng | all the time of his vow to be set apart) (s:ciam/thuciam) (b:ciam) (r:19.119.57/1.21.24/5.10.20/40.5.33/4.6.5) (q:draft)
kiciamin = (t:v) (w:swearing/taking an oath/with an oath) (d:kiciam with the linking ending -in: swearing, with an oath) (e:ci-in ~ a nial hi/ama' tungah amah ~ | he swore to him/hehna so a, amah ~ | his anger burned and he swore/Isaak tungah ~ a khapna | the oath he swore to Isaac/Kumpi Solomon Topa tawh ~ | King Solomon swore by the Lord) (b:kiciam) (r:40.26.72/4.32.10/1.25.33/13.16.16/11.2.23) (q:draft)
kiciamna = (t:n) (w:oath/vow/promise) (d:kiciam, swear, with the noun suffix na: an oath, vow or solemn promise that someone has made) (e:Tua mite in ~ om loin/nang tunga ka ~ ka zuih kul hi | I must keep my vows to you/Hih ~ note bek tawh a bawl hi lo a | he makes this oath not with you alone/~ tawh kipawl tate i hi hi | we are children of promise) (s:ciamna/kamciamna/khapna/thuciam) (b:kiciam) (r:58.7.20/19.56.12/5.29.14/48.4.28) (q:draft)
kiciamnasa = (t:n) (w:oath sworn/what was sworn) (d:kiciamna with sa, already done: the oath a person has already made, or the thing sworn about) (e:a man loin a ~ na/a ~ hang le a leenglate’ maitang a zahtakna hangin | because of his oath and his regard for his guests/ka ~ uh bangin ka sem taktak ding uh hi | we will surely do as we have vowed) (b:kiciamna) (r:3.6.5/40.14.9/41.6.26/24.44.25) (q:draft)
kiciamnate = (t:n) (w:oaths/vows/covenants) (d:kiciamna, oath, with the plural te: oaths or vows made, and also covenants between parties) (e:Pasian tawh na ~ na tungsak in/mi ahih hangin ~ a kibawl khit ciangin | even a human covenant, once it has been made/thu ~ ahi zongin, Thukham koihna ahi zongin | the covenants and the giving of the law) (s:thuciamnate) (b:kiciamna) (r:40.5.33/48.3.15/45.9.4) (q:draft)
kiciampak = (t:v) (w:swear rashly/vow thoughtlessly) (d:kiciam swear with pak quickly: take an oath without thinking) (e:a theih lohin a ~ khak leh) (b:ciampak) (r:3.5.4) (q:draft)
kiciampha = (t:v) (w:swear/make an oath) (d:kiciam swear with pha; kiciampha kik, swear again, reaffirm an oath) (e:David tungah ~ kik hi) (r:9.20.17) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiciamsa = (t:v) (w:sworn/vowed/promised on oath) (d:kiciam swear with sa already: having sworn or vowed; before a noun, that was promised on oath) (e:Topa a ~ leitangah va pai-in/amaute tungah piak dingin na ~ gamah | into the land you swore to give them/Topa in amaute tungah a ~ bangin | as the Lord had sworn to them/Thu ~ mi li ka nei uh hi | we have four men who have made a vow/nidang lai-a a ~ bangin | according to the vow he had made earlier) (s:ciamsa) (b:kiciam) (r:5.8.1/44.21.23/16.9.15/7.2.15/44.18.18) (q:draft)
kiciamsak = (t:v) (w:make swear/put under oath) (d:kiciam, swear, with the causative -sak: make someone take an oath) (e:Ka topa in kei hong ~ a/nang hong ~ bangin na pa vui in | bury your father as he made you swear/siampipa in tua numei ~ ding a | the priest shall put the woman under oath/Pasian tawh a ~ Kumpi Nebukhadnezzar | King Nebuchadnezzar, who had made him swear by God) (b:kiciam) (r:1.24.37/1.50.6/4.5.21/14.36.13) (q:draft)
kiciamsakin = (t:v) (w:making swear/putting under oath) (d:kiciamsak make swear with the linking ending in) (e:siampipa in amah ~/Topa tawh hong ~ | I made you swear by the Lord) (b:kiciamsak) (r:4.5.19/11.2.42) (q:draft)
kiciamte = (t:n) (w:those who swear/those who have sworn) (d:kiciam, swear, with the plural te: the people who take an oath) (e:Vantung gam tawh a ~ in/Biakna innpi tawh a ~ in | those who swear by the temple/Tua banga a ~ a kisim ciangin | when those who had sworn this were counted/biakna tau tawh a ~ in | those who swear by the altar) (b:kiciam) (r:40.23.22/44.23.13/40.23.21/40.23.20) (q:draft)
kiciamteh = (t:v) (w:be recorded/be listed/be reckoned/be credited) (d:passive ki with ciamteh, note or record: be written down, listed or remembered, and so be counted as something, as faith is counted as righteousness) (e:ama tangding dikna-in a ~ hi/hong tung ding khang mite’ adingin hih thu ~ hen | let this be written for a future generation/a pu a pate’ mawhna ~ hen la | may the sin of his fathers be remembered/note aa-in ~ ding hi | it will be reckoned as yours/a beisa nate ~ nawn lo | the former things will no longer be remembered) (s:kigelh) (b:ciamteh) (r:45.4.22/13.5.7/19.102.18/19.109.14/4.18.27/23.65.17) (q:draft)
kiciamtehin = (t:v) (w:being remembered/being noted) (d:kiciamteh be recorded with the linking suffix in; kiciamtehin om, be kept in mind) (e:tua khuapi ~ a om hi) (b:kiciamteh) (r:66.16.19) (q:draft)
kiciamtehna = (t:n) (w:record/register/registration) (d:noun from kiciamteh be recorded; what is written down, such as a family list or genealogy) (e:Nahum’ mangmuhna a ~ lai ahi hi/khang ~ ah amau’ min a zon’ uh hangin | though they searched for their names in the family record/a khang tangthu peuhmah a ~ om lo | there is no record of his genealogy/a mi phazah zui-in a ~ bangin | as they were registered by number) (s:ciamtehna/sazian) (b:kiciamteh) (r:34.1.1/13.7.9/15.2.62/58.7.3/13.23.24) (q:draft)
kiciamtehsa = (t:adj) (w:recorded/written down/marked out) (d:kiciamteh be recorded with sa, already) (e:om dingin a ~ mite khempeuh/tanglai pek a, a ~ mi kimkhat | certain people written about long ago) (b:kiciamteh) (r:23.4.3/65.1.4) (q:draft)
kiciamtehsak = (t:v) (w:be numbered/be recorded) (d:kiciamteh be recorded with sak, on someone's behalf) (e:nangawn uh hong ~ hi) (s:kisim) (b:kiciamteh) (r:40.10.30) (q:draft)
kiciamtehte = (t:n) (w:those listed/those recorded/those registered) (d:kiciamteh be recorded with te: the people whose names are written down) (e:a ~ lakah a kihelte) (b:kiciamteh) (r:4.11.26) (q:draft)
kiciamzaw = (t:v) (w:swear instead/swear rather) (d:kiciam swear with zaw, rather or instead) (e:ci-in a ~ ding uh hi) (b:kiciam) (r:24.23.8) (q:draft)
kiciamzo = (t:v) (w:have sworn) (d:kiciam swear, with zo for an action already carried out) (e:pasian ahi lopite peuh tawh ~ uh hi/amaute tungah i ~ a | we have sworn to them/mihonte’ makaite ~ uh ahih manin | because the leaders of the assembly had sworn/Hih bangin kong hihna ding thu ka ~ a | I have sworn that I will do this for you) (s:ciamzo) (b:kiciam) (r:24.5.7/6.9.19/6.9.18/26.37.14) (q:draft)
kician = (t:adj) (w:firm/sure/sound/well-founded) (d:firm and reliable: said of a place that holds, of a plan or a matter that is well grounded, and of a hope or a house that is sure) (e:~ om lopi-in galsim dingin kipan kei in/a ~ mun khatah vankhaina bangin | like a peg in a firm place/innkuan ~ khat kong phuhsak ding a | I will build you a lasting house/Tua i lametna ~ mahmah a | that hope of ours is very firm) (s:kip/kiptak) (b:cian) (r:20.20.18/23.22.23/11.11.38/58.6.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiciang = (t:v) (w:be laid/be built up/be built) (d:of stones or a wall, be laid one on another and built up in courses) (e:suang khat tungah suang ~ khat beek/Kulh ~ khinin, kongkhakte ka bulh khin a | when the wall had been built and I had set up the doors/Khaukhai zang-a a ~ kulh gei khatah | beside a wall built with a plumb line/Na suangte innkiu suangin ~ lo ding a | your stones will not be laid as cornerstones) (s:kilam) (a:kicim) (r:41.13.2/16.7.1/30.7.7/24.51.26) (q:draft)
kiciangin = (t:v) (w:piled up/lying one upon another) (d:kiciang, be laid one on another, with the linking ending in; said here of corpses lying in heaps) (e:~ vum venvan) (b:kiciang) (r:34.3.3) (q:draft)
kiciangkik = (t:v) (w:be built up again/be rebuilt) (d:kiciang, be built up in courses, with kik, again; said of a city wall) (e:khuapikulh zong ~ ding hi) (s:kilamkik/kiciankik) (b:kiciang) (r:38.1.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiciangtan = (t:v) (w:be fixed/be set/be determined/be limited) (d:of an amount, a number or a limit, be laid down beforehand; a kiciangtan zah is the fixed or allotted amount) (e:a nuntak ding kha phazah ~ khin hi/Faro’ tung panin a ~ zah an ngah uh a | they received the fixed amount of food from Pharaoh/ka ni zah ding a ~ laitakin | when the number of my days was fixed/hih theih ding zah ~ sa na hi hiam | do you think what he can do is limited) (s:kiseh/kisehkhol) (b:ciangtan) (r:18.14.5/1.47.22/19.139.16/4.11.23) (q:draft)
kiciangtansa = (t:adj) (w:appointed/fixed/set) (d:kiciangtan, be fixed, with sa, already done; a kiciangtansa hun is the appointed time) (e:a ~ hun hong tung khin hi) (s:kisehsa/sehsa) (b:kiciangtan) (r:19.102.13) (q:draft)
kiciangte = (t:n) (w:those laid/those built up) (d:kiciang be laid with te: in suang kiciangte, the stones that had been laid in a building) (e:suang ~ kongzing lakah a kithehthang hi) (b:kiciang) (r:25.4.1) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiciangto = (t:v) (w:be piled up/be built up high) (d:kiciang be built up in courses, with to upward; of waters heaped up and of walls rising to the sky) (e:Na nak ging tawh tuite ~ a/van banin kulhpi a ~ khuapite | cities with walls built up to the sky) (b:kiciang) (r:2.15.8/5.9.1) (q:draft)
kiciankik = (t:v) (w:be rebuilt/be built again) (d:said of city walls being built up again; perhaps another spelling of kiciangkik) (e:kulh uh a ~ ding hun hong tung ding a) (s:kiciangkik/kilamkik) (r:33.7.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiciansak = (t:v) (w:make sure/ascertain/find out for certain) (d:kician, sure, with the causative sak: make a matter sure by finding out more about it) (e:Pai-in va ~ lai un) (b:kician) (r:9.23.22) (q:draft)
kicici = (t:v) (w:be said again and again/keep being said) (d:passive ki with cici, keep saying) (e:a ~ zuauthute um kei un) (b:cici) (r:24.7.4) (q:draft)
kicih = (t:v) (w:be said/be called/be told) (d:form of kici used before nouns and endings: a kicih is what is said or what someone is called, and bang kicih ding is what is to be done with someone) (e:hih bangin hong ~ leh/a ~ zan beimang hen | may the night on which it was said perish/na ta ~ nadingin ka kilawm kei hi | I am not worthy to be called your son/Amah bang ~ ding cih tel takin kigen lo | it was not made clear what should be done to him/hong ~ ding hoihzaw hi | it is better to be told) (s:kigen) (b:kici) (r:6.22.28/18.3.3/42.15.19/4.15.34/20.25.7) (q:draft)
kicih = (t:v) (w:be used as fuel/be burned) (d:be put on a fire as fuel, as in mei-in kicih; sing a kicih mei is a wood fire) (e:mei-in ~ ding hi/sing a ~ mei tungah amah in hal ding hi | he shall burn it on a wood fire/mite pen mei-a ~ sing tawh kibang uh hi | the people are like wood used as fuel for the fire) (s:kihal/kikhul) (r:23.9.5/3.4.12/23.9.19) (q:draft)
kiciHebru = (t:phrase) (w:called Hebrew) (d:kici, be called, run together with the name Hebru, Hebrew; two words printed as one, probably a printing error) (e:Puah a ~ mi naudomte' kiangah | to the Hebrew midwives, one of them called Puah) (r:2.1.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
kicihna = (t:n) (w:name/title/saying) (d:kici, be called or be said, with the noun ending na: what a person or place is called, or the fact that something is said; kicihna ngah is be called, and a kicihna za is hear it said) (e:Nang Judah mi ~ ngah a/A nungta Pasian’ tapate ~ a ngah ding uh hi | they will be called sons of the living God/Pasian in amau Pasian a ~ maizum loin | God is not ashamed to be called their God/a ~ za uh hi | they heard it said) (b:cihna) (r:45.2.17/45.9.26/58.11.16/11.16.16) (q:draft)
kicihnopna = (t:see) <kicihnopna-a>
kicihnopna-a = (t:adv) (w:meaning himself/with reference to himself) (d:ki oneself, cihnopna what one means to say, with a: as something meant of oneself) (e:Amah a ~ a gen hiam) (r:44.8.34) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiciing = (t:adj) (w:cultivated/planted) (d:of an olive tree, grown and tended by people, as opposed to gamlak, wild) (e:A ~ oliv kung a hiangte kisatkhia-in/note’ pianngei ahi lo a ~ oliv kung tungah | onto a cultivated olive tree not yours by nature) (r:45.11.17/45.11.24) (q:draft)
kicil = (t:v) (w:be trodden/be trampled/be threshed) (d:passive ki with cil, tread out: said of grapes in a winepress and of grain on a threshing floor) (e:buhcilna tawh ~ lo a/leenggah in khua pua lam phualah ~ hi | the grapes were trodden in the press outside the city) (r:23.28.27/66.14.20) (q:draft)
kicilgawp = (t:v) (w:be trampled down/be threshed hard) (d:kicil be trodden or threshed with gawp severely) (e:sual tunga ancil bangin a ~ ding hi) (b:kicil) (r:24.51.33) (q:draft)
kicilna = (t:n) (w:treading/pressing) (d:kicil be trodden with the noun suffix na; leenggahzu kicilna phual is the winepress) (e:leenggahzu ~ phual amah in a cil hi) (b:kicil) (r:66.19.15) (q:draft)
kicilsa = (t:adj) (w:threshed/trampled/crushed) (d:kicil be threshed with sa already done) (e:A ~, a kiseepsa keima mite aw) (b:kicil) (r:23.21.10) (q:draft)
