kicimgawp = (t:v) (w:collapse utterly/crumble/be broken down) (d:kicim collapse with gawp, completely) (e:Thebes khuapikulh khempeuh ~ ding a/ama aw ging khiasak a, leitung ~ hi | he raises his voice and the earth crumbles) (b:kicim) (r:26.30.16/19.46.6) (q:draft)
kicimin = (t:v) (w:being broken down/collapsing) (d:kicim collapse with the linking ending in) (e:Jerusalem kulh ~ kulhkongpite mei in) (b:kicim) (r:16.1.3) (q:draft)
kicimmang = (t:v) (w:collapse completely/crumble away) (d:kicim collapse with mang, away or to nothing) (e:kulh le phung khempeuh ~ ding uh hi) (s:cimzan) (r:26.38.20) (q:draft)
kicimsa = (t:adj) (w:broken down/collapsed/fallen) (d:kicim collapse with sa already done) (e:a ~ Jerusalem kulhpi) (s:cimsa) (b:kicim) (r:16.2.13) (q:draft)
kicimsuk = (t:v) (w:collapse down/fall down upon) (d:kicim collapse with suk downward) (e:tungah a innpi ~ hi) (b:kicim) (r:7.16.30) (q:draft)
kicimte = (t:n) (w:breaches/fallen parts/ruins) (d:kicim collapse with the plural te: the parts of a wall that have fallen down) (e:a ~ ciangkik lo uh) (b:kicim) (r:26.13.5) (q:draft)
kicin = (t:v) (w:be complete/be perfect/be full/be accomplished) (d:be complete or fulfilled; written with a final apostrophe before words such as nading, khit and mateng, and with na it forms the noun kicinna, completeness) (e:Note lungdamna a ~’ nadingin/na an nek ding a ~’ ciang bekin | only when you have enough to eat/thu khempeuh a ~’ matengin | until everything is accomplished/Note thungaihna in a ~’ khit ciangin | once your obedience is complete) (b:cin) (r:62.1.4/46.13.10/20.24.27/40.5.18/47.10.6) (q:draft)
