kidawkkhia = (t:v) (w:come to light/be exposed/be detected) (d:kidawk appear with khia, out) (e:ama mawhna ~ lo a) (s:kilangkhia) (b:kidawk) (r:19.36.2) (q:draft)
kidawksak = (t:v) (w:expose/make appear/lay bare) (d:kidawk appear with sak cause: make something show) (e:a ciangkang kaangte ~ hi) (s:dawksak/pholak) (a:seel) (b:kidawk) (r:1.30.37) (q:draft)
kidawm = (t:v) (w:be careful/beware/take heed/guard oneself) (d:watch oneself so as not to fall into something bad; with loh nadingin it is be careful not to, and with an object it is beware of someone) (e:na kihei khak loh nadingin ~ in/Topa na mangngilh khak loh nading uh ~ un | be careful that you do not forget the Lord/a inn vengte uh ~ uh hen la | let them beware of their neighbors/Jerusalem khuapi aw, ~ in | O city of Jerusalem, take warning) (s:kidop/kikem) (r:18.36.21/5.6.12/24.9.4/24.6.8) (q:draft)
kidawmin = (t:v) (w:being careful/taking heed/watchfully) (d:kidawm be careful with the connective in) (e:Mipilte ~ siatna panin kihem a/na thuhilhnate-ah hoihtakin ~ om lecin | if you keep careful watch over your teaching) (s:kikeemin) (b:kidawm) (r:20.14.16/54.4.16) (q:draft)
kidawng = (t:v) (w:be answered) (d:passive of dawng answer; hong kidawng lo ding, will go unanswered) (e:hong ~ lo ding sa a/simmawh kampaute hong ~ mawh ding sa na hi hiam | do you think your mocking words cannot be answered) (b:dawng) (r:18.11.2/18.11.3) (q:draft)
kidawng = (t:v) (w:answer one another/call to each other/answer oneself) (d:reciprocal or reflexive of dawng answer) (e:khat leh khat ~ a/amah leh amah ~ hi | she answers herself/ci-in ka ~ hi | so I answered myself/ci-in a ~ kik ding uh hi | so they will answer in reply) (b:dawng) (r:19.42.7/7.5.29/21.2.15/24.22.9) (q:draft)
kidawngin = (t:adv) (w:responsively/answering one another) (d:kidawng answer one another with the connective in: of singing, one group answering the other in turn) (e:lungdam kohna a ~ sa uh a) (b:kidawng) (r:15.3.11) (q:draft)
kidawngkik = (t:v) (w:be answered/answer back/reply) (d:kidawng with kik back: the answer that is given in return to a question) (e:ci-in a ~ ding uh hi/ci-in ~ ding hi | so the answer will be) (s:dawngkik) (b:kidawng) (r:24.22.9/30.6.10) (q:draft)
kideek = (t:v) (w:restrain oneself/hold oneself back) (d:the 1977 spelling; the 1932 text has kidek) (e:a ~ kei uh hi) (s:kidek/ki-ipip) (r:24.14.10) (q:draft)
kideeng = (t:v) (w:be stoned/be pelted) (d:passive ki with deeng throw at; suang tawh kideeng lum, be stoned to death) (e:suang tawh ~ lum ta hen) (s:kideng) (b:deeng) (r:58.12.20) (q:draft)
kideidan = (t:v) (w:be distinguished/be treated differently) (d:passive ki with deidan discriminate; kideidan loin is without distinction, alike) (e:a siang ~ loin a kibangin/~ loin na ne thei ding uh hi | you may eat it without distinction) (s:kikhentel) (b:deidan) (r:5.12.22/5.12.15) (q:draft)
kideidanna = (t:n) (w:distinction/difference/discrimination) (d:kideidan with the noun ending na: treating people differently from one another; kideidanna om lo is there is no distinction) (e:cih bangin ~ om nawn lo a/Jew mi le Gentail mi a ~ om lo | there is no distinction between Jew and Gentile/Israel minam sung panin kuamah ~ om loin | with no distinction among any from the tribes of Israel) (s:deidanna/kilamdanna) (b:kideidan) (r:48.3.28/45.10.12/26.48.19) (q:draft)
kideih = (t:v) (w:be wanted/be desired) (d:passive ki with deih want; a kideih lo is unwanted, rejected) (e:a ~ lo ngun a kici) (b:deih) (r:24.6.30) (q:draft)
Kideih = (t:v) (w:desire each other/love each other) (d:deih want or like with the prefix ki, each other; written with a capital in a heading) (e:Nungak leh Tangval A ~ Tuakna) (b:kideih) (r:22.7.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
kideihsakin = (t:v) (w:wishing for one another) (d:ki each other with deihsakin wishing for; thupha kideihsakin, wishing one another well) (e:khatlekhat thupha ~ a om uh hi) (b:deihsakin) (r:44.2.47) (q:draft, low confidence)
kideina = (t:n) (w:partition/dividing off) (d:deina partition with ki: the place where a room is divided off, as by the temple curtain) (e:Tua Siangtho Mun a ~ zomah) (b:deina) (r:58.9.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
kidek = (t:v) (w:restrain oneself/hold oneself back) (d:hold oneself back from doing something; a kidek kei uh hi is they do not restrain themselves) (e:a ~ kei uh hi) (s:kideek/ki-ipip) (r:24.14.10) (q:draft)
kidekna = (t:n) (w:self-control/self-restraint) (d:kidek restrain oneself with the noun suffix na) (e:~ thu leh hong tung ding) (s:ki-ipipna/khamna) (b:kidek) (r:44.24.25) (q:draft)
kidelh = (t:v) (w:be chased/be hunted/be pursued) (d:passive ki with delh, chase: be chased or hunted; also of chariots rushing along one after another) (e:A ~ sanang leh a cing om lo/Gutate otkhai-in a ~ bangin | as thieves are chased with shouting/galkapna-ah a ~ sakolleengte’ gin tawh kibang hi | like the sound of chariots rushing into battle/nang hong ~ hi | you are pursued) (b:delh) (r:23.13.14/18.30.5/66.9.9/22.1.9) (q:draft)
kidelhin = (t:v) (w:being pursued/being chased) (d:kidelh, be chased, with the linking ending in: being pursued, while being chased) (e:amaute ~ tulnih kithat hi/Gidom ciang dong nakpi takin amaute ~ | they were pursued hard as far as Gidom) (b:kidelh) (r:7.20.45) (q:draft)
kidem = (t:v) (w:compete/contend/vie/race) (d:dem, contend with, with ki, each other: strive to outdo one another, as in a race or contest; tai kidem is run a race) (e:mite tawh tai ~ a/mi khat in tai a ~ ciangin | when someone competes in a race/khat leh khat kitehin ~ uh a | they measure and compete with one another/pahtakna lukhu ngah nadingin i ~ hi | we compete to get a crown of honour) (s:kituh) (b:dem) (r:24.12.5/55.2.5/47.10.12/46.9.25) (q:draft)
kidemin = (t:v) (w:competing/striving/pressing on) (d:kidem, compete, with the linking ending in: striving as in a race, here of pressing on toward the goal) (e:~ kung dongin hahkatin ka tai hi) (b:kidem) (r:50.3.14) (q:draft)
kidemna = (t:n) (w:rivalry/competition/envy/selfish ambition) (d:kidem, compete, with the noun suffix na: striving to outdo one another, rivalry or selfish ambition; tai kidemna is a running race) (e:hauh nop man-a ~ hangin/hazatna leh ~ siatna a om leh | if there is envy and selfish ambition/tai ~-ah zo tawntung lo a | do not always win the race/Tai ~-ah mi khat bek in thaman a ngah | in a race only one gets the prize) (s:demna) (b:kidem) (r:21.4.4/21.9.11/59.3.14/46.9.24) (q:draft)
kidempih = (t:v) (w:compete with/rival/be a rival of) (d:kidem, compete, with pih, together with: have someone as a rival; i kidempih is the one we compete with) (e:i ~ Jerusalem khuapi zancip gawp hi/Sum bawlna lam-a i ~ Jerusalem khuapi | Jerusalem, the city that is our rival in trade) (b:kidem) (r:26.26.2) (q:draft)
kidemte = (t:n) (w:competitors/contestants/runners) (d:kidem, compete, with te, those who: people who take part in a contest; tai kidemte are those who run a race) (e:a ~ khempeuh in na khempeuh/Tai ~ khempeuh a tai uh hangin | though all who run in the race run) (b:kidem) (r:46.9.25/46.9.24) (q:draft)
kiden = (t:v) (w:be thrown down/be dashed down/throw oneself) (d:den, throw down, with ki, passive or reflexive: be dashed down or throw oneself down; written kiden’ before gawp, nading and na, and leilak kiden’na-in is throwing oneself to the ground) (e:tuipi sung ~’na in/a naungeekte uh leilak ~’ gawp nading hi | their infants will be dashed to the ground/a naungeekte uh lei ~’ nading a | their little ones will be dashed to the ground/Kei zong leilak ~’na-in ka boksuk hi | I too threw myself to the ground facedown/Suntangpi-in amaute khuamial sung ~’na a | at midday they plunge into darkness) (s:kikhiasuk/kilawnsuk) (b:den) (r:41.11.23/18.41.28/23.13.16/28.13.16/26.44.4/18.5.14) (q:draft)
kideng = (t:v) (w:be stoned/be pelted) (d:deng, throw at, with the passive ki: have stones thrown at one; suang tawh kideng is be stoned and kideng lum is be stoned to death) (e:Suang tawh Naboth ~ zo hi/a bawngtal ~ lum ding a | the bull is to be stoned to death/amah suang tawh ~ lum ahih kei leh | he is to be stoned to death, or else/bawngtal ~ lum ding a, a neipa zong kithat | the bull is to be stoned and its owner also put to death) (s:kideeng/kidenglum) (b:deng) (r:11.21.14/2.21.28/2.19.13/2.21.29) (q:draft)
kidengawpna = (t:n) (w:being dashed down/dashing to pieces) (d:dengawpna, throwing down violently, with the passive ki: being dashed to the ground; with ding, will be dashed down) (e:a naungekte uh leilak ~ ding hi) (b:dengawpna) (r:23.13.16) (q:draft)
kidengin = (t:v) (w:being stoned/being pelted) (d:kideng, be stoned, with the linking ending in; suang tawh kidengin si is die by being stoned) (e:Naboth suang tawh ~ a sihna) (b:kideng) (r:11.21.15) (q:draft)
kidengkham = (t:v) (w:be smashed/be shattered/be dashed to pieces) (d:dengkham, from deng strike and kham break, with the passive ki: be smashed to pieces, said of a clay pot) (e:iplah loin a ~ beel) (s:kisukham/kitamkham) (b:dengkham) (r:23.30.14) (q:draft)
kidenglum = (t:v) (w:be stoned to death/be stoned) (d:denglum, kill by throwing, with the passive ki: be put to death by having stones thrown, usually with suang tawh, with stones) (e:suang tawh amaute ~ ding hi/a bawngtal ~ ding a | the bull is to be stoned to death/suang tawh ~ ahih kei leh kikaplum ding hi | he is to be stoned or shot dead/tua mual a sukkhak le ~ ding hi | if it touches the mountain it must be stoned to death) (s:kideng/kideeng) (b:denglum) (r:3.20.27/2.21.28/2.19.13/58.12.20) (q:draft)
kidenna = (t:v) (w:throw oneself down/fall upon/plunge into/be dashed down) (d:hurl oneself or be hurled onto or into something, as into the sea or to the ground; leilak kidenna is fall or be thrown to the ground; this is the spelling of the 1932 text, the 1977 text writes kiden’na) (e:Kei zong leilak ~-in ka boksuk hi/mualte tuipi sung a ~ zongin | though the mountains fall into the sea/Innkhuam lianpipite leilak ~ ding hi | the great pillars will fall to the ground/amah a langpangte leilak ~ uh hen | may his opponents fall to the ground/Paul le Silas khe kiang va ~-in | throwing himself at the feet of Paul and Silas) (b:kiden) (r:26.44.4/41.11.23/19.46.2/26.26.11/19.72.9/44.16.29) (q:draft, low confidence)
kidiah = (t:v) (w:dip oneself/be dipped/be soaked) (d:diah, dip or soak, with ki: dip oneself in water, or be dipped or soaked in a liquid such as water or blood) (e:Jordan sungah sagih vei ~ hi/Sisan sungah a ~ puantualpi khat silh a | he wears a robe dipped in blood/Amau gam pen sisan tawh ~ ding a | their land will be soaked with blood/tua na pen tui sungah ~ ding a | that article is to be put in water) (b:diah) (r:12.5.14/6.3.15/66.19.13/23.34.7/3.11.32) (q:draft)
kidiahin = (t:v) (w:wallowing/soaked/steeped) (d:kidiah, be dipped or soaked, with the linking ending in: lying soaked in blood, or being steeped in drink) (e:ama sisan sungah Amasa ~ om hi/zu leh sa tawh ~ a om lai takun | while they are steeped in drink and feasting) (b:kidiah) (r:10.20.12/34.1.10) (q:draft)
kidiik = (t:v) (w:sob/groan) (d:weep or groan aloud; probably the same word as kidik) (e:zak dingin zong na ~ kei ding a) (s:kidik) (r:26.24.17) (q:draft, low confidence)
kidik = (t:v) (w:sob/weep bitterly/mourn) (d:weep with heavy sobs, often together with kap, weep) (e:bang hangin kapin ka ~ hiam/bang hangin kapkap-in ka ~ hiam | why must I go on weeping and sobbing/khitui luangin nakpitakin ka ~ ding hi | I will sob bitterly with tears flowing/Mite’ zakin zong na ~ kei ding a | you shall not sob in the hearing of people) (s:kidiik/thuum) (r:19.42.9/24.13.17/19.43.2/26.24.17) (q:draft)
kidikdik = (t:v) (w:keep sobbing/go on mourning) (d:kidik, sob, said twice to show that the weeping goes on and on) (e:kunin ka ~ hi/bang hangin kapin ~ ka hi hiam | why must I go on weeping and sobbing) (r:19.35.14/19.43.2) (q:draft)
kidiksak = (t:v) (w:consider oneself righteous/justify oneself) (d:ki, oneself, with diksak, declare righteous: regard oneself as being in the right) (e:Amaute ~ a, midang khempeuh) (s:kitangsak) (b:diksak) (r:42.18.9) (q:draft)
kidiksakin = (t:v) (w:justifying oneself) (d:kidiksak, make oneself out to be in the right, with the linking ending in) (e:Job amah ~ Pasian mawhsak zawsop hi) (b:kidiksak) (r:18.32.2) (q:draft)
kidim = (t:v) (w:fill/be filled/be full) (d:dim, full, with ki: be filled or be full, with tawh for what fills) (e:Piter in Kha Siangtho tawh ~ a/lungdamna leh Kha Siangtho tawh a ~ uh hi | they were filled with joy and the Holy Spirit/leitung in ngongtatna tawh ~ hi | the earth was full of violence/a hawklam zong tui tawh ~ hi | the trench too was filled with water) (b:dim) (r:44.4.8/44.13.52/1.6.11/11.18.35)
kidimin = (t:v) (w:being filled/filled with/full of) (d:kidim, be filled, with the linking ending in: being full of or filled with something, with tawh for what fills) (e:Kha Siangtho tawh ~ om un/amaute khempeuh in Kha Siangtho tawh ~ | all of them were filled with the Holy Spirit/hehpihna leh thuman thutak tawh ~ | full of grace and truth/Siatna bekbek tawh ~ | filled with nothing but ruin) (b:kidim) (r:49.5.18/44.6.8/44.2.4/43.1.14/25.3.47) (q:draft)
kidimkik = (t:v) (w:be filled again) (d:kidim, be filled, with kik, again: become full once more, here of a land full of the noise of many people) (e:husa tawh ~ ding hi) (b:kidim) (r:33.2.12) (q:draft)
kidimna = (t:n) (w:being filled/filling) (d:kidim be filled with the noun suffix na: the fact of being full) (e:a ~ ka mu hi) (b:kidim) (r:26.43.5) (q:draft)
kidimsak = (t:v) (w:fill/be filled) (d:kidim, be filled, with the causative sak: fill someone or something, or be filled, with tawh for what fills) (e:lungkhamna tawh hong ~ hi/Ama galte maizumna tawh ka ~ ding a | I will fill his enemies with shame/a pum khempeuh natna tawh ~ hi | his whole body is filled with pain/hehna tawh hong ~ na hih manin | because you have filled me with indignation) (s:dimsak) (b:kidim) (r:18.9.18/26.9.9/19.132.18/18.33.19/24.15.17) (q:draft)
kidimte = (t:n) (w:those who are filled/those full of) (d:kidim be filled with the plural te: people or things that are full of something, here hands full of bribes) (e:golhguk tawh a ~ tawh) (b:kidim) (r:19.26.9) (q:draft)
kidin = (t:see) <kidin'sak>
kidin'sak = (t:v) (w:be set up/be erected) (d:of a tent or building, be made to stand, be put up; written kidinsak in the other text) (e:Biakbuk a ~ ni-in meii in | on the day the tabernacle was set up, the cloud) (s:kidinsak/kidingsak) (r:4.9.15) (q:draft)
kiding = (t:v) (w:stand/be stood up) (d:ki with ding stand; kiding sak is be made to stand upright) (e:a khe nih in ~ sak a) (r:27.7.4) (q:draft)
kidingsak = (t:v) (w:be set up/be made to stand/be erected) (d:dingsak, make stand, with the passive ki: of a tent, be set up; of a person, be made to stand before others) (e:biakbuk na ~ khin hi/Pilat mai-ah Jesuh ~ ahih manin | as Jesus was made to stand before Pilate/mihing bangin a khe nihin ~ a | it was made to stand on two feet like a man/Khuampite kikalah amah ~ hi | he was made to stand between the pillars) (s:kidinsak/kiphut) (b:dingsak) (r:4.10.21/7.16.25/40.27.11/27.7.4) (q:draft)
kidinsak = (t:v) (w:be set up/be erected) (d:of a tent or building, be made to stand, be put up) (e:Biakbuk a ~ ni-in meii in) (s:kidingsak/kidin'sak) (r:4.9.15) (q:draft)
kido = (t:v) (w:fight/wage war/battle) (d:do, fight, with ki, each other: fight or be at war, with tawh for the opponent; gal kido is fight a battle) (e:Abimelek tawh ~ hi/Amalek mite tawh ~ in | fight with the Amalekites/Hih kumpite khempeuh tawh sauveipi sung Joshua ~ hi | Joshua fought all these kings for a long time/Efraim tulak-ah gal ~ uh hi | they fought the battle in the forest of Ephraim/Kua in amah tawh ~ zo ding hiam | who can fight against it) (s:galkido/galdo/kitawng) (a:kilem) (b:do) (r:7.9.39/6.11.18/2.17.9/10.18.6/66.13.4) (q:draft)
kido = (t:v) (w:host one another/show hospitality) (d:in zin kido, receive one another as guests, offer hospitality to each other) (e:khat leh khat zin na ~ un) (b:do) (r:60.4.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
kidoin = (t:v) (w:fighting each other/contending/opposing) (d:kido, fight each other, with the linking ending in: fighting, contending with or opposing someone) (e:kumpite khat leh khat ~/Mikhael nangawn in Dawimangpa tawh ~ | even Michael, contending with the devil/Satan in amah leh amah ~ kikhen leh | if Satan fights against himself and is divided) (b:kido) (r:12.3.23/65.1.9/41.3.26) (q:draft)
kidok = (t:v) (w:be withdrawn/be revoked/be taken back) (d:dok, draw out, with the passive ki; kidok kik is be taken back again, be revoked, said of a decree or a promise) (e:a thu a ~ kik ngei kei hi/lai pen ~ kik thei nawn lo | the document can no longer be taken back) (s:kidokkik/kikhelkik) (b:dok) (r:45.11.29/17.8.8) (q:draft)
kidokik = (t:v) (w:fight again/be at war again) (d:kido, fight each other, with kik, again: go to war once more) (e:Israel-te tawh ~ uh a) (b:kido) (r:10.21.15) (q:draft)
kidokkhia = (t:v) (w:be pulled up/be pulled out) (d:kidok, be drawn, with khia, out: be pulled out of the ground, said of tent pegs) (e:a khetphimte ~ ngei loin) (s:kibotkhia/kidawh) (b:kidok) (r:23.33.20) (q:draft)
kidokkik = (t:v) (w:be revoked/be withdrawn/be taken back) (d:kidok, be drawn, with kik, back: be taken back, said of a sealed decree that cannot be undone) (e:~ thei nawn lo ahih manin/a kithuh khinsa lai pen ~ thei nawn lo | a sealed document can no longer be revoked) (s:kikhelkik) (b:kidok) (r:17.8.8) (q:draft)
kidoksa = (t:adj) (w:drawn/unsheathed) (d:kidok be drawn out, with sa for a completed action; of a sword out of its sheath) (e:a ~ namsau khat omin/namsau, a ~ namsau, a kikeek thal | the sword, the drawn sword, the bent bow) (s:dawhsa) (b:kidok) (r:13.21.16/23.21.15) (q:draft)
kidom = (t:v) (w:be lifted up/be raised) (d:dom, lift up, with the passive ki: be lifted or raised from the ground) (e:leitung panin ~ kaang to a) (s:kidomto) (b:dom) (r:27.7.4) (q:draft)
kidomkaang = (t:v) (w:be lifted up/be raised off) (d:kidom be lifted with kaang, raised clear of the ground; followed by to upward) (e:tua ganhing ~ to-in) (s:kidomto) (r:27.7.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
kidomto = (t:v) (w:be lifted up/be raised) (d:domto, lift up, with the passive ki: be lifted or raised, here of a lid) (e:tua ciangpi sin pen ~ a) (s:kidom/kilaamto) (a:kikoihsuk) (b:domto) (r:38.5.7) (q:draft)
kidomto = (t:v) (w:lift one another up/encourage one another/spur one another on) (d:domto, lift up, with ki, one another: build each other up, encourage each other toward what is good) (e:khat leh khat ~ ni) (s:kihanthawn/kihansuah) (b:domto) (r:58.10.24) (q:draft)
kidon = (t:v) (w:care for oneself/heed one another) (d:don care for, with ki, which turns the action on oneself or on each other; note bek a kidon, who care only for yourselves; kidon lohna, not heeding one another) (e:tuute don loin note bek a ~/sanggam tawh kitotna in ~ lohna piangsak hi | a quarrel with a brother brings disregard for each other) (b:don) (r:26.34.10/20.18.19) (q:draft)
kidona = (t:n) (w:war/battle/fighting) (d:kido, fight each other, with the noun suffix na: war, a battle or fighting; often gal kidona) (e:Rehoboam leh Jeroboam kikalah ~ om hi/gal ~ om nawn lo hi | there was no more war/gal ~ thu khempeuh David kiangah gen hi | he told David all about the battle/gal ~-ah amah na guallel sak hi | you made him lose in battle) (s:galkidona/galdona/gal) (a:kilemna) (b:kido) (r:11.15.6/14.15.19/10.11.18/19.89.43) (q:draft)
kidonate = (t:n) (w:wars/battles/fightings) (d:plural of kidona; gal kidonate is the fighting of war) (e:gal ~ eite tungah hong tungsak hi) (s:galkidonate/galdonate) (b:kidona) (r:23.42.25) (q:draft)
kidong = (t:v) (w:ask one another/question each other/discuss) (d:dong, ask, with ki, each other: ask or question one another, discuss or argue over a matter) (e:khat leh khat a ~ uh hi/amaute tawh bang thu ~ na hi uh hiam | what are you arguing about with them/biakna innpi sungah ding-in a ~ uh hi | standing in the temple they asked one another) (s:kidot/kikum) (b:dong) (r:42.22.23/41.9.10/41.9.16/43.11.56) (q:draft)
kidong = (t:v) (w:be betrothed/be pledged in marriage/be asked in marriage) (d:of a girl, to have been asked for as a wife; a kidong nai lo nungak is a virgin not yet betrothed) (e:a ~ nai lo nungak khat tuakin/a ~ nai lo nungak khat zolin | seducing a virgin who is not yet betrothed) (s:kingai) (b:dong) (r:5.22.28/2.22.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
kidongin = (t:v) (w:questioning one another/disputing/arguing) (d:kidong, question one another, with the linking ending in: disputing or arguing over a matter) (e:amaute tawh thu kikum ~ a om uh/Zeisu hangah ~ a mawhsak uh hi | disputing over Jesus, they accused him/note kuamah in ~ thu kikhensak kei un | let no one question and judge you) (s:kinialin) (b:kidong) (r:41.9.14/44.25.19/51.2.16) (q:draft)
kidongsa = (t:adj) (w:betrothed/engaged/pledged in marriage) (d:kidong, be asked in marriage, with sa for a completed action: of a woman already promised to a man) (e:a ~ nungak khat gam lakah tuakin/A ~ nungak khat om a | if there is a virgin who is betrothed/a ~ a lawmnu Mari tawh | with Mary, who was betrothed to him) (b:kidong) (r:5.22.25/42.2.4/5.22.23) (q:draft)
kidongte = (t:n) (w:those questioning each other/those debating) (d:kidong ask one another with the plural te; thu kidongte may also be read as the questions that were asked) (e:thu ~ Zeisu in kituak mahmahin) (b:kidong) (r:41.12.28) (q:draft, low confidence)
kidongzaw = (t:v) (w:ask one another/keep asking each other) (d:kidong ask one another with zaw, which seems to add rather or instead) (e:ci-in na ~ ding uh hi) (s:kidong/kidot) (b:kidong) (r:24.23.35) (q:draft, low confidence)
kidop = (t:v) (w:be careful/take heed/watch oneself) (d:take care to do or to avoid something; with nak leh, if only one is careful to; with kei leh, unless one takes care) (e:zuih ding na ~ nak leh/gamtat ding a ~ nak uh leh | if only they are careful to walk/Na ~ kei leh nang kong taisan ding a | if you do not take heed I will turn away from you/na zuih khak loh nading na ~ kei leh | unless you take care not to follow them) (s:kidawm/kikem/kingaihsun) (r:13.22.13/20.22.25/11.8.25/24.6.8) (q:draft)
kidophuai = (t:v) (w:must be careful/ought to take heed) (d:kidop be careful with huai, worthy of or needing to be done) (e:lungsim takpi tawh ~ hi) (r:58.2.1) (q:draft)
kidopzawh = (t:v) (w:be able to restrain oneself/keep in check) (d:kidop be careful with zawh be able; with kampau, keep control of the tongue) (e:kampau a ~ kei leh) (r:59.1.26) (q:draft)
kidosak = (t:v) (w:set against each other/cause to fight) (d:kido fight each other with the causative sak) (e:tanute le nute a ~ ding/Tate le pate a ~ ding | to set sons against fathers/Mi khat leh khat ka ~ hi | I set people against one another) (s:kitawngsak) (a:kilemsak) (b:kido) (r:40.10.35/38.8.10) (q:draft)
kidot = (t:v) (w:be asked/be questioned) (d:dot, ask, with the passive ki: be asked or questioned) (e:Tua bangin a ~ ciangin siampite in/satna tawh Paul thu a ~ nadingin | so that Paul would be questioned under flogging) (b:dot) (r:37.2.12/44.22.24) (q:draft)
kidot = (t:v) (w:ask one another) (d:dot ask, with ki in the sense of each other) (e:Note khatlekhat na ~ uh) (s:kidong) (b:dot) (r:43.16.19) (q:draft)
kidotna = (t:n) (w:questioning/controversy/dispute) (d:kidot, ask one another, with the noun suffix na: questioning or dispute; thu kidotna is debate over questions) (e:Judah ngeina thu leh thu ~ khempeuh/thu ~ in kitotna piangsak thei hi | disputes over questions can produce quarrels/Hih bang thu ~ a pianna mun | the place where this questioning took place) (s:thukidotna/kinialna) (b:kidot) (r:44.26.3/55.2.23/43.1.28) (q:draft)
Kidron = (t:name) (c:valley) (w:Kidron) (d:valley with a seasonal stream on the east side of Jerusalem, between the city and the Mount of Olives) (r:43.18.1/10.15.23)
kigaan = (t:v) (w:be plaited/be twisted together/be woven) (d:be plaited or woven together; ling tawh kigaan lukhu is a crown plaited of thorns) (e:ling tawh ~ lukhu a khusak) (s:kigan) (r:41.15.17) (q:draft)
kigaih = (t:v) (w:shudder/be appalled/be horrified) (d:be struck with horror or dread at what one sees or hears, often with lau, fear, or lamdang sa, be astonished) (e:kumpite lau-in ~ ding uh hi/lamdang sa-in ~ ding uh hi | they will be astonished and appalled/a za peuhmah ~-in launa tawh liing uh hi | all who hear of it shudder and tremble with fear) (s:lipkhap/mulkim/dipkua) (r:26.32.10/18.18.20/36.2.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
kigaih = (t:v) (w:be chewed/be consumed) (d:of food in the mouth) (e:Sa a ~ ma) (b:gaih) (r:4.11.33) (q:draft, low confidence)
kigaihin = (t:v) (w:startled/appalled/shuddering) (d:kigaih, shudder, with the linking ending in: startled, struck with horror) (e:~ a lau uh hi/a za peuhmah ~ a ling uh hi | all who hear of it shudder and tremble) (b:kigaih) (r:42.24.37/18.18.20) (q:draft)
kigak = (t:v) (w:be strapped on/be girded/be banded) (d:gak, bind round, with the passive ki: be fastened round with a band or belt) (e:gakna tawh ~ ding hi/khuamte khempeuh ngun tawh kibawl gakna tawh ~ hi | all the posts were banded with silver bands/a kawng tungah a ~ | strapped at his waist) (b:gak) (r:2.27.17/10.20.8/2.38.17) (q:draft)
kigakin = (t:v) (w:girding oneself/tying on) (d:kigak gird oneself with the connective in) (e:saihadial kawnggak tawh ~, saihadial dialpi) (b:kigak) (r:3.16.4) (q:draft)
kigakna = (t:n) (w:girding/belting) (d:kigak gird oneself with the noun suffix na; a kigakna kawnggak is the belt he ties round himself) (e:amah a ~ kawnggak tawh kibang) (b:kigak) (r:19.109.19) (q:draft)
kigal = (t:v) (w:be at enmity/be enemies) (d:be enemies of each other; kigal neihna is enmity or ill will held against someone) (e:a vengpa tawh ~ neihna nei lo/a beisa hunah amah tawh ~ neihna om lopi-in | without having had enmity with him in the past) (s:kigalbawl) (a:kilem) (b:gal) (r:5.19.6/5.19.5) (q:draft)
kigal = (t:adv) (w:opposite/facing each other) (d:across from one another; kigal sai is to stand or be placed facing each other) (e:amaute tawh ~ sai-in nasem uh hi/A geihual nuai a ~ sai a pang tuakah | on the two opposite sides below the molding) (r:16.12.9/2.30.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
kigalbawl = (t:v) (w:be enemies/be hostile to each other) (d:ki each other with galbawl act as an enemy) (e:Pilat kilem loin ~ uh a) (s:kigal) (a:kilem) (b:galbawl) (r:42.23.12) (q:draft)
kigaldo = (t:v) (w:wage war/fight against) (d:ki with galdo fight, make war against each other, with tawh for the opponent) (e:galkapte tawh ~ dingun a kikhawm) (s:galkido/kido/galdo) (b:galdo) (r:66.19.19) (q:draft)
kigalging = (t:v) (w:prepare for battle/get ready/arm oneself) (d:make oneself ready for war, from gal, war, and kiging, get ready) (e:a ~ sa-in om un la/~ un, ahih hangin lungkiatna na thuak veve ding | prepare for battle, yet you will still be dismayed) (s:kiging/kigin/kithawi) (r:26.38.7/23.8.9) (q:draft)
kigalneih = (t:v) (w:be at enmity with/be an enemy of) (d:hold someone as an enemy, with tawh; kigalneihna is enmity) (e:Pasian tawh a ~ dingin) (s:kigal) (r:59.4.4) (q:draft)
kigalneihna = (t:n) (w:enmity/animosity/hostility) (d:kigalneih, be enemies of one another, with the noun suffix na: enmity between people, or toward God) (e:Pasian tawh ~ ahih lamtak/khagilo sawlin ~ omsak hi | he sent an evil spirit and caused enmity) (s:galneihna/kilangneihna) (a:kilemna) (b:kigalneih) (r:59.4.4/7.9.23) (q:draft)
kigalsai = (t:v) (w:be opposite/face each other) (d:lie facing something across a space, tawh marks what is faced; kigalsai-in is used like the English preposition opposite) (e:sabuai tawh a ~-in/a geihual nuai a ~ a pang tuakah | on the two opposite sides below the molding/a ~-in Jonathan tu-in | Jonathan sat opposite/Bethpeor tawh a ~ kuam sungah | in the valley opposite Beth Peor/amaute tawh a ~-ah siampite in peengkulte tum | opposite them the priests blew the trumpets) (s:kitang/kimaituah/kimaingat) (r:2.40.24/2.30.4/9.20.25/5.4.46/14.7.6) (q:draft)
