kigamgi = (t:v) (w:border/share a boundary with) (d:ki with gamgi border: have a common border, with tawh) (e:Manasseh tawh ~ ding uh hi) (b:gamgi) (r:26.48.5) (q:draft)
kigamla = (t:v) (w:be far from/be distant/keep away) (d:gamla, far, with ki: be at a distance from someone or something, used with tawh; kigamla lo is not far, near) (e:kei tawh ~ om kei in/Jerusalem khua tawh tai nih dektak a ~ hi | it was nearly two miles from Jerusalem/a lungsim uh nang tawh ~ hi | their hearts are far from you/tui gei tawh ~ lo | not far from the shore) (a:kinai) (b:gamla) (r:19.22.11/23.54.14/43.11.18/24.12.2/43.21.8) (q:draft)
kigamlasak = (t:v) (w:make far from/draw away from) (d:kigamla be far from with sak cause: make people distant from God) (e:Pasian tawh mite a ~ semsem) (b:kigamla) (r:55.2.16) (q:draft)
kigamlat = (t:v) (w:be far from/be absent/be distant) (d:form of kigamla, be far from, used before hangin and similar words) (e:note tawh a ~ hangin) (b:kigamla) (r:46.5.3) (q:draft)
kigamlate = (t:n) (w:those who are far from/those far away) (d:kigamla be far from with te, those who) (e:nang tawh a ~ kisia ding uh/Dikna tawh a ~, a lungsim khauh mite aw | you stubborn-hearted who are far from righteousness) (b:kigamla) (r:19.73.27/23.46.12) (q:draft)
kigamlum = (t:v) (w:be in uproar/be stirred up) (d:gamlum, be in uproar, with ki: be thrown into commotion, said of a whole town) (e:Khuazangin ~ a) (s:kibuai) (b:gamlum) (r:44.21.30) (q:draft)
kigamta = (t:v) (w:be done/be acted/be dealt with) (d:gamta, act, with the passive ki: a thing is done, or a person is dealt with in a certain way) (e:na deih bangin ~ hen/Israel sungah tua bangin ~ lo hi | such a thing is not done in Israel/hih ngeina tawh kizui-in ~ ding hi | it is to be dealt with according to this rule/Gitloh Gamtatna ~ khinta a | lawlessness is already at work) (s:kihih/kisem) (b:gamta) (r:40.6.10/10.13.12/2.21.31/53.2.7) (q:draft)
kigamtatna = (t:n) (w:being done/doing) (d:gamtatna action with the passive ki: the fact that a deed is done) (e:na a ~ thu a om) (b:gamtatna) (r:5.17.4) (q:draft)
kigamtatnate = (t:n) (w:deeds done/acts/practices) (d:plural of kigamtatna: the things that are done; with thuman lo, acts of injustice, oppressions) (e:a ~ khempeuh ka ngaihsun kik) (b:kigamtatna) (r:21.4.1) (q:draft)
kigan = (t:v) (w:be woven/woven) (d:gan, weave, with the passive ki: of cloth or a garment, be woven; kigan khawm is woven together) (e:a ~ khawm puan na silh kei ding hi/kala-oh mul ~ puan silh a | he wore clothing woven of camel hair/hoih tak-a ~ puante | finely woven garments) (s:kiphan/kigaan) (b:gan) (r:5.22.11/2.39.22/41.1.6/2.31.10) (q:draft)
kigankhawm = (t:v) (w:be woven together) (d:kigan be woven with khawm together) (e:Samul le khau a ~ puan) (b:kigan) (r:5.22.11) (q:draft)
kigawh = (t:v) (w:be slaughtered/be sacrificed/be killed) (d:gawh slaughter with ki-, here passive: of animals killed for food or sacrifice) (e:Paisan tuuno a ~ ni/Paisan tuuno a ~ nading | when the Passover lamb had to be sacrificed/a ~ ni a tun’ mateng tuam koih in | set them apart until the day of slaughter/meihal biakna a ~ nading munah go ding hi | he is to slaughter it where the burnt offering is slaughtered) (s:kigo/kithat) (b:gawh) (r:41.14.12/24.12.3/42.22.7/3.4.24) (q:draft)
kigawhna = (t:n) (w:slaughtering/being slaughtered) (d:kigawh be slaughtered with na; a kigawhna mun is the place where an animal is slaughtered) (e:meihal biakna a ~ munah/Meihal biakna a ~ mun Topa mai-ah | before the Lord at the place where the burnt offering is slaughtered) (s:gawhna) (b:kigawh) (r:3.4.33/3.6.25) (q:draft)
kigawi = (t:v) (w:rattle/clatter/grind together) (d:knock or grind against each other with a noise, of bones or wheels) (e:a ~ ziazua a ging ka za a/a pei ~ gingte a zak uh ciangin | when they hear the rumble of its wheels/sakol kisatna a ging, leh leengpei ~ | the crack of whips and the clatter of wheels) (b:gawi) (r:26.37.7/34.3.2/24.47.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
kigawi = (t:v) (w:be ground) (d:of grain at the mill, with sak, be made to grind) (e:aana tawh an ~ sak a) (b:gawi) (r:25.5.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
