kigawisak = (t:v) (w:be made to grind) (d:kigawi with causative sak: be put to grinding grain at the mill) (e:aana tawh an ~ a) (b:kigawi) (r:25.5.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
kigawite = (t:n) (w:rumblings/rattlings) (d:kigawi rattle or grind together with the plural te; a pei kigawite is the rumbling of its wheels) (e:a pei ~ a zak uh ciangin) (b:kigawi) (r:24.47.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
kigawivui = (t:v) (w:be crushed/be ground) (d:passive ki with gawivui crush fine; of fresh heads of grain) (e:phawk nadingin a ~ an pawlkhat/a ~, mei tawh a kihangkeu na pia ding | you shall offer it crushed and roasted in the fire) (s:kisuvui) (b:gawivui) (r:3.2.16/3.2.14) (q:draft)
kigawlmek = (t:v) (w:be strangled) (d:passive ki with gawlmek, squeeze the neck; of animals killed without their blood being drained) (e:a ~ sa khat peuhpeuh/a si luangkhiasak loin a ~ sate | meat of animals strangled without draining the blood) (b:gawlmek) (r:44.15.29/44.15.20) (q:draft)
kigawm = (t:v) (w:hold fast) (b:gawm)
kigawm = (t:adv) (w:together) (d:after the things named, taken or joined together) (e:Itna kip leh thutakna ~ ding a/kumpi li ~ leh kumpi nga ~ kido | four kings together fought against five kings together/sik leh tungman ~ milim khete | the feet of the statue, of iron and clay together) (s:khawm) (b:gawm) (r:19.85.10/1.14.9/27.2.34)
