kigawmsak = (t:v) (w:let join/include/count among) (d:kigawm, be joined, with sak, cause: allow someone to be counted with a group) (e:ei minamte tawh hong ~) (s:kihelsak) (b:kigawm) (r:39.2.12) (q:draft)
kigawmsakte = (t:n) (w:those joined together/what has been joined) (d:kigawmsak, cause to be joined, with the plural te: those whom someone has joined together) (e:Pasian in a ~ mite in) (b:kigawmsak) (r:41.10.9) (q:draft)
kigawt = (t:v) (w:deny oneself/afflict oneself/humble oneself) (d:reflexive form of gawt with ki, usually followed by tawm, by oneself: deny or afflict oneself, said of fasting on the Day of Atonement) (e:nomau mah na ~ ding uh hi/nomau na ~ tawm ding uh hi | you must deny yourselves/tua ni-in amahmah a ~ tawm lo peuhmah | anyone who does not deny himself on that day/amah a ~ tawm nadingin | in order to deny herself) (s:kigim/kigimtawm) (b:gawt) (r:3.16.31/4.29.7/3.23.29/4.30.13) (q:draft)
kigeel = (t:v) (w:be designed/be planned) (d:passive of geel, design, with ki; hoih taka a kigeel is skilfully designed, said of woven work) (e:Hoih taka a ~, a dum) (b:geel) (r:2.39.3) (q:draft)
kigeelna = (t:n) (w:design/arrangement/plan) (d:kigeel, be designed, with the noun suffix na: the way a thing is laid out) (e:a na khempeuh a ~) (s:geelna) (b:kigeel) (r:26.43.11) (q:draft)
kigeelnate = (t:n) (w:designs/arrangements/plans) (d:plural of kigeelna) (e:amaute in a ~ thei-in) (s:kigelnate/geelnate) (b:kigeelna) (r:26.43.11) (q:draft)
kigelh = (t:v) (w:be written/be recorded) (d:passive of gelh, write: be written or recorded, as in a book or in Scripture; ci-in a kigelh hi closes a quotation, so it is written) (e:Hih laibu sungah a ~ lo lim dang/ci-in Lai Siangtho sungah a ~ hi | so it is written in Scripture/Israel Kumpite’ Laibu sungah ~ hi | they are written in the book of the kings of Israel/Tua a ~ laimal in hi bang ahi hi | this is the inscription that was written/a mawhsakna lai a tungah a ~ hi | the notice of the charge against him was written above him) (s:kiciamteh) (a:kiphiat) (b:gelh) (r:43.20.30/14.16.11/45.10.11/27.5.25/41.15.26) (q:draft)
kigelha = (t:v) (w:be written/be inscribed) (d:kigelh, be written, with the linking a before om: being written on something) (e:min tawh ~ a om mi) (b:kigelh) (r:66.14.1) (q:draft)
kigelhin = (t:v) (w:be written/be engraved) (d:kigelh, be written, with the linking ending in: being written or engraved, written and then) (e:minte zong ~ a om hi/Hih lai pen Kumpipa Ahasu-eras’ min tawh ~ | this letter was written in the name of King Xerxes/a lang nih tuakah lai ~ | with writing on both sides/kham tawh a kizepna sungah a minte ~ | their names engraved in the gold settings) (b:kigelh) (r:66.21.12/17.8.10/17.3.12/26.2.10/2.39.6) (q:draft)
kigelhkhol = (t:v) (w:be written beforehand/be written in advance) (d:kigelh, be written, with khol, beforehand: be written before the thing happens) (e:Ama thu a ~ a) (r:44.13.29) (q:draft)
kigelhkholh = (t:v) (w:be written beforehand) (d:form of kigelhkhol used before mah bangin) (e:sungah a ~ mah bangin Pasian in) (b:kigelhkhol) (r:44.13.32) (q:draft)
kigelhna = (t:n) (w:writing/written record/inscription) (d:kigelh, be written, with the noun suffix na: that in which something is written; kigelhna laibu is the book in which it is written) (e:ci-in ~ lai a tungah a om hi/a ~ laibu leitungah ta zo lo ding hi | the world could not hold the books in which it was written/a nungta mite a ~ laibu a dang khat | another book, in which the living are written/min thak ~ suangpak | a white stone with a new name written on it) (s:gelhna/laigelhna) (b:kigelh) (r:42.23.38/43.21.25/66.20.12/66.2.17) (q:draft)
kigelhsa = (t:adj) (w:written/prescribed) (d:kigelh, be written, with sa for a completed state: already written; a kigelhsa bangin means as prescribed) (e:a ~ bangin kham meivakkhuam sawm bawl/a ~ thu in a tangtung ding hi | the saying that is written will come true/a sung leh a pua a ~ laibu khat | a scroll written on the inside and the outside/keima thu a ~ khempeuh a tangtung ding hi | everything written about me must be fulfilled) (s:gelhsa) (b:kigelh) (r:14.4.7/66.5.1/46.15.54/42.24.44) (q:draft)
kigelhte = (t:n) (w:writings/things written/engravings) (d:kigelh, be written, with the plural te, used as a noun: the things that are written or engraved) (e:Moses’ thukham laibu sunga ~ khempeuh/A vangah lim ~ om hi | there were engravings around its opening/a thu ~ hangin amaute thanuamin | they were glad because of the words written/kamsangte’ laibu sunga a ~ khempeuh zong ka um hi | I also believe everything written in the books of the prophets) (s:gelhte) (b:kigelh) (r:6.23.6/2.32.16/11.7.31/44.15.31/44.24.14) (q:draft)
kigelnate = (t:n) (w:designs/arrangements/plans) (d:plural noun from kigeel be designed; spelled kigeelnate in the other text) (e:amaute in a ~ thei-in) (s:kigeelnate/geelnate) (r:26.43.11) (q:draft)
kigen = (t:v) (w:be told/be reported/be said) (d:passive of gen, say or tell: be said, told or reported to someone) (e:innkuante sungah hih thu ~ hi/amaute tungah a ~ mateng | until it was made clear to them/a muanhuai mite tung bekah thusim ~ ngam hi | a secret can be told only to trustworthy people/a nung ciangin a ~ ding nate-ah | to the things that would be spoken later/tel takin ~ lo ahih manin | because it had not been clearly stated) (s:kikoh) (b:gen) (r:12.7.11/1.31.22/3.24.12/20.11.13/58.3.5/4.15.34) (q:draft)
kigengen = (t:v) (w:be told again and again/be talked about/be spoken of) (d:passive ki with gen, say, repeated: be told again and again, of news or deeds that go on being talked about) (e:a vanglian na bawl nate ~ ding hi/tu-a bangin hih thu a ~ lai ahi hi | this story is still being told to this day/na minthanna teng hong ~ hi | your glories are spoken of/kei tungah hong sepnate ~ ding hi | what she has done for me will be told) (b:gengen) (r:19.145.4/40.28.15/19.87.3/41.14.9) (q:draft)
kigengenna = (t:n) (w:report/talk/fame) (d:kigengen, be told again and again, with the noun suffix na: the fact that someone keeps being talked about) (e:Jesuh thu a ~ thu a za hi) (b:kigengen) (r:41.6.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
kigenin = (t:v) (w:being told/being reported) (d:kigen be told with the connective in) (e:no kiangah hong ~ tua thu) (b:kigen) (r:5.17.4) (q:draft)
kigenkhol = (t:v) (w:be foretold/be told beforehand) (d:passive of genkhol, foretell, with ki: be told before it happens) (e:a ~ bangin a hong pai ding) (b:genkhol) (r:40.11.14) (q:draft)
kigenkik = (t:v) (w:be said again/be repeated/be told again) (d:kigen, be said, with kik, again: be said or told once more) (e:sun khuavak sungah ~ ding a/Hih thu mah na ~ a | this same thing is said again) (b:kigen) (r:42.12.3/58.4.5) (q:draft)
kigenna = (t:n) (w:mention/report/being told) (d:kigen, be told, with the noun suffix na: the telling of a thing, or the place or person it is told to) (e:hih thu a ~ mi peuhpeuh lau ding/ci-in a ~ thu a zak bek uh ahi hi | they only heard the report/mang leh a khiatna a ~ a zak ciangin | when he heard the telling of the dream and its meaning/ci-in hong ~ ka za hi | I have heard it said of you) (b:kigen) (r:23.19.17/6.9.10/48.1.23/7.7.15/1.41.15) (q:draft)
kigennate = (t:n) (w:things said/what was said/sayings) (d:kigenna with the plural te: the things that are said or told about someone) (e:ama thu a ~ khempeuh/ci-in a beisa hun-ah hong ~ man hi | the things said of you in the past are true) (s:kigente/gennate) (b:kigenna) (r:42.24.27/26.36.13) (q:draft)
kigenpa = (t:n) (w:the one spoken of/the one foretold) (d:kigen, be told, with pa, man: the man who is spoken of or foretold) (e:a ~ Eijah in amah ahi hi | he is the Elijah who was spoken of) (s:cihpa) (b:kigen) (r:40.11.14) (q:draft)
kigensa = (t:v) (w:said before/already told/spoken) (d:kigen, be said, with sa, already: said or told earlier; before a noun, as in a kigensa thu, the word spoken before) (e:a ~ bangin amaute a gamtat nadingun/naungeek thu ~ thu teng a zasak uh hi | they made known what had been told about the child/a ~ thu genkholhna kam bangin | in keeping with the prophecies once spoken/A ~ bangin sawlbuk lam nadingin | as has been said, to build shelters) (s:gensa) (b:kigen) (r:15.10.5/42.2.17/54.1.18/16.8.14) (q:draft)
kigensak = (t:v) (w:be spoken for/be spoken on behalf of) (d:passive ki with gensak speak for: have a word put in for someone) (e:thu khat hong ~ ding na ut hiam) (b:gensak) (r:12.4.13) (q:draft)
kigensia = (t:v) (w:be blasphemed/be slandered/be spoken evil of) (d:passive of gensia, speak evil of: be slandered or blasphemed) (e:Gentailte lakah Pasian’ min ~ hi) (a:kiphat) (b:gensia) (r:45.2.24) (q:draft)
kigensia = (t:v) (w:slander one another/speak evil of one another) (d:gensia, speak evil of, with ki, one another) (e:khatlekhat ~ kei un) (s:kikosia) (b:gensia) (r:59.4.11) (q:draft)
kigensiatna = (t:n) (w:being spoken against/denunciation) (d:passive ki with gensiatna evil speaking: the things said against a person; in this verse the oracles spoken against the king) (e:amah a ~ thute) (b:gensiatna) (r:14.24.27) (q:draft, low confidence)
kigensiatnate = (t:n) (w:slanders/evil speakings) (d:plural of kigensiatna, speaking evil of one another) (e:huaihamna, le ~ na omsak nawn kei un) (s:gensiatnate) (b:kigensiatna) (r:60.2.1) (q:draft)
kigentawm = (t:v) (w:speak for oneself/testify about oneself) (d:kigen with tawm, by oneself: speak on behalf of oneself, be a witness for oneself) (e:Kei le kei a ~ ka hih hangin/Nang le nang a ~ na hih manin | because you testify about yourself) (r:43.8.14/43.8.13) (q:draft)
kigente = (t:n) (w:words spoken/things said) (d:kigen, be told, with the plural te: the things that are said or told; often follows thu) (e:Thu ~ ngai-in/pilna thu hong ~ ngai in | listen to the words of knowledge spoken to you/Topa thu a ~ a zak ciangin | when he heard what was said about the Lord/a ~ ka um kei hi | I did not believe the things that were said) (s:kigennate/gennate) (b:kigen) (r:20.19.20/66.1.3/20.23.12/44.13.12/11.10.7) (q:draft)
kigentel = (t:v) (w:give account of oneself/explain oneself) (d:ki oneself with gentel explain: state clearly what one has done) (e:a va ~ ciat ding ihi hi) (b:gentel) (r:45.14.12) (q:draft)
kigenzo = (t:v) (w:be told fully/be reported) (d:kigen be told with zo, showing the telling was completed) (e:kei kiangah hong ~ hi) (b:kigen) (r:8.2.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiget = (t:v) (w:be castrated/castrate oneself) (d:be castrated; a kiget mi is a eunuch) (e:amaute mah ~ ta uh hen/ka thuciamna a lenkip a ~ mite tungah | to the eunuchs who hold fast to my covenant/a ~ mipa in | the eunuch) (s:kigettawm) (r:48.5.12/23.56.3/23.56.4) (q:draft)
kigettawm = (t:v) (w:be made a eunuch/castrate oneself) (d:related to geh eunuch; tawm usually shows that the subject acts on himself, while the NIV has made eunuchs by others) (e:pawlkhatte a ~ om a) (s:kiget) (r:40.19.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
