kigo = (t:v) (w:be slaughtered/be killed) (d:passive of go, slaughter, with the prefix ki: said of animals killed for sacrifice or food) (e:Topa mai-ah bawngtal ~ ding hi/kipaipihin ama mai-ah ~ ding hi | it is to be taken out and slaughtered in his presence/eite Paisan’ Tuuno a ~ zo hi | our Passover lamb has been sacrificed/Na muh tangpi-un na bawngtal uh ~ ding a | your ox will be slaughtered before your eyes) (s:kigawh) (b:go) (r:3.4.15/4.19.3/46.5.7/5.28.31) (q:draft)
kigozo = (t:v) (w:be slaughtered in sufficient number/be slaughtered) (d:kigo, be slaughtered, with zo, be able or complete: whether enough can be slaughtered) (e:amau a dingin ~ ding ahi hiam) (b:kigo) (r:4.11.22) (q:draft, low confidence)
kigu = (t:v) (w:be stolen/be carried off) (d:passive of gu, steal; kigu-khia is be stolen away) (e:ama' tung panin a ~ ahih leh/sun-a ~ hita leh zan-a ~ hita leh | whether stolen by day or stolen by night/Keimah biak nadingin a ~ ganhing khatpeuh | any stolen animal, to worship me/nang kiang panin a ~ | that was stolen from you) (b:gu) (r:2.22.12/1.31.39/39.1.13/7.17.2) (q:draft)
kiguai = (t:v) (w:be hired/be paid) (d:passive of guai, hire, with ki: be hired or paid for a service) (e:Numei paktatte sum tawh ~ a) (b:guai) (r:26.16.33) (q:draft)
kiguaihna = (t:n) (w:hire/earnings) (d:in a kiguaihna sum, the money a prostitute is paid for hiring out the body) (e:A paktatnu a ~ sum ahi a) (b:guaihna) (r:5.23.18) (q:draft, low confidence)
kigual = (t:v) (w:line up/be arrayed/draw up in ranks) (d:stand in rows, as an army drawn up for battle or people walking in procession; kigual deudau is in long lines) (e:Filistia mite ~ uh a/keimah do dingin mi tampi ~ deudau uh hi | many are lined up to fight against me/mihon ~ deudaute lakah | among the crowd walking in long lines) (s:kikhung) (b:gual) (r:9.4.2/19.55.18/19.45.14) (q:draft)
kigualnop = (t:v) (w:make merry/rejoice together) (d:gualnop, make merry, with ki; kigualnop sakna is merrymaking or rejoicing) (e:~ sakna a) (b:gualnop) (r:20.14.13) (q:draft)
kiguan = (t:v) (w:be given/be supplied/be assigned) (d:passive of guan, put or give, with ki: be provided for someone or laid on someone as a duty) (e:numeite tungah paknamtui tuamtuamte ~ hen/zingsang simin kong a hon’ dingin nasep ~ hi | the work of opening the gate each morning was assigned/galdo dingin galhiam ~ hi | they were supplied with weapons for battle/meilah kuang a ~ note khempeuh aw | all you who provide yourselves with flaming torches) (b:guan) (r:17.2.3/13.9.27/4.31.5/23.50.11) (q:draft)
