kiguksak = (t:v) (w:be stolen from/be robbed of) (d:passive ki with guk, steal, and sak: have something stolen from one) (e:hong ~ lai-in a gu pa) (r:7.17.2) (q:draft)
kigum = (t:v) (w:save oneself) (d:gum, save, with ki, oneself; often with pumpi, body: save your own self) (e:na pumpi ~ in/ama pumpi ~ zo lo hi | he cannot save himself/ama pumpi ~ ta hen | let him save himself/nangma pumpi ~ in, singlamteh tung panin hong kumsuk in | save yourself and come down from the cross) (s:kigumkhia/kihontawm) (b:gum) (r:42.23.37/41.15.30/41.15.31/42.23.35) (q:draft)
kigumkhia = (t:v) (w:save oneself/rescue oneself) (d:gumkhia, rescue, with the reflexive ki: save oneself out of danger) (e:mite lak panin ~ un/keimahmah khut tawh ka ~ hi | I saved myself with my own hand) (s:kigum/kihontawm) (b:gumkhia) (r:44.2.40/23.63.5) (q:draft)
kih = (t:v) (w:abhor/detest/loathe) (d:feel strong dislike or disgust for someone or something) (e:ama luah minamte a ~ hi/keimah in note kong ~ kei ding hi | I will not abhor you/Zuaunate zadahin ka ~ a | I hate and detest falsehood/amaute in an peuhmah ~ uh hi | they loathed all food/Amaute in kei hong ~ uh a | they detest me) (s:mudah/hua) (a:it/deih) (r:19.106.40/3.26.11/19.119.163/19.107.18/18.30.10) (q:draft)
kihaamsiatna = (t:n) (w:curse/object of cursing) (d:a person or place that people name when they curse, another spelling of kihamsiatna) (e:mite’ ~ suakin kuamah teeng nawn lo hi/leitung gam khempeuhte’ ~-in ka zangsak ding hi | I will make it a curse among all the nations of the earth/ci-in ~-in a zang ding uh hi | they will use it as a curse) (s:kihamsiatna/hamsiatna/samsiatna) (b:haamsiatna) (r:24.44.22/24.26.6/24.29.22) (q:draft)
kihah = (t:v) (w:be tended/be pruned/be dressed) (d:of vines; a kihah lo leenggui is a vine left untended) (e:a ~ lo leengguite panin zong) (b:hah) (r:3.25.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihah = (t:v) (w:be forced/be compelled) (d:in kihah piak, of drink pressed on a guest) (e:zu nekna zia pen ~ piak cih) (b:hah) (r:17.1.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
