kihalin = (t:adv) (w:at a distance/far off/apart) (d:kihal, keep apart, with in: keeping a distance from someone; often with gamla, far) (e:Piter in gamla sim ~ a zui hi/gamla sim a ~ Zeisu zui a | he followed Jesus at a distance/amaute kikalah saupi a ~ | with a wide space between them) (r:42.22.54/9.26.13/41.14.54) (q:draft)
kihalin = (t:v) (w:be burned/be set on fire) (d:kihal, be burned, with the linking ending in: being burned) (e:gal pan’na teng mei tawh ~/meikhuk sungah ~ a ngun teng a kilak khit ciangin | after being burned in the furnace and the silver taken out) (b:kihal) (r:24.51.32/26.22.18) (q:draft)
kihalkik = (t:v) (w:be burned again) (d:kihal, be burned, with kik, again) (e:mei tawh a ~ bangin amaute zong) (b:kihal) (r:23.6.13) (q:draft)
kihallum = (t:v) (w:be burned to death) (d:passive of hallum, burn to death, with ki; mei tawh kihallum is be burned to death with fire) (e:mei tawh ~ ding hi/Tua nu mei tawh ~ ding hi | that woman must be burned to death with fire) (b:hallum) (r:3.20.14/3.21.9) (q:draft)
kihalna = (t:n) (w:burning/place of burning) (d:kihal, be burned, with the noun suffix na: the burning of something; kihalna mun is the place where it is burned, the hearth of an altar) (e:ganhing ~ mun in tong li sang ding a/bawngla a ~ sungah tuate khul ding hi | he is to throw them onto the burning heifer/amau a ~ mei mit ngei lo ding a | the fire that burns them will never go out/paknamtui a ~ biakna tau | the altar where incense is burned) (s:kikhulna/halna) (b:kihal) (r:26.43.15/4.19.6/23.66.24/42.1.11) (q:draft)
kihalna = (t:n) (w:distance/gap/space between) (d:the space kept between two things) (e:tong tulnih bang ~ om ding hi) (s:gamlatna) (r:6.3.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihalnelhin = (t:v) (w:be burned up/burn oneself up) (d:kihal be burned with nelh, apparently completely, and in: being burned up with the house) (e:amah mei-in ~ a si hi) (r:11.16.18) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihalsak = (t:v) (w:keep apart/leave a space between) (d:make a gap between things, which are named with kikal, between) (e:hon khat leh hon khat kikal ~ un) (r:1.32.16) (q:draft)
kihalsak = (t:v) (w:be burned/be set on fire) (d:kihal, be burned, with sak: be set on fire by someone) (e:A innte uh ~ a) (b:kihal) (r:24.51.30) (q:draft)
kihalsan = (t:adj) (w:glowing/red-hot/burnished) (d:kihal, be burned, with san, red: heated in the fire until it glows; said of bronze) (e:sumngo ~ tawh a kibang khe/meikhuk sunga a ~ sumngo bangin | like bronze glowing in a furnace/pumbukah a ~ sumngo bang a | like bronze glowing in a furnace) (b:kihal) (r:66.2.18/26.1.27/66.1.15) (q:draft)
kihaltum = (t:v) (w:be burned up/be set on fire/be consumed) (d:passive of haltum, burn up, with ki: be completely burned) (e:amaute mei tawh ~ siang hi/khuaneute ~ ding hi | its villages will be burned up/ham bangin ~ ding hi | they will be consumed like dry grass/meikhuk sunga a ~ lingkungte | thornbushes burned up in a furnace/a sang mahmah khuakongpite zong mei tawh ~ ding hi | her high gates too will be burned with fire) (s:kikhultum) (b:haltum) (r:10.23.7/24.49.2/34.1.10/23.33.12/24.51.58) (q:draft)
kihaltumna = (t:n) (w:being burned/burning) (d:passive ki with haltum burn up and the noun suffix na: being given over to be burned) (e:nasepna hangin ~ ka thuak ahi zongin) (b:kihaltum) (r:46.13.3) (q:draft)
kihamsiatna = (t:n) (w:curse/object of cursing) (d:a person or place that people name when they curse; kihamsiatna-in zang is use as a curse) (e:mite in ~-in a zat dingun/leitung gam khempeuhte’ ~-in ka zangsak ding hi | I will make it a curse among all the nations of the earth/~-in hong zangin hong zahko ding uh hi | they will use you as a curse and mock you) (s:kihaamsiatna/hamsiatna/samsiatna) (b:hamsiatna) (r:24.24.9/24.26.6/24.42.18) (q:draft)
kihanga = (t:v) (w:be laid on a fire/be roasted) (d:said of fish and bread lying on burning coals; exact sense of the root not confirmed) (e:ngasa leh khomun ~ om a mu) (r:43.21.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihangkeu = (t:v) (w:be roasted/be parched) (d:of grain, be dried by roasting over fire) (e:a ~ na pia ding hi) (r:3.2.14) (q:draft)
kihangsak = (t:adj) (w:courage) (d:the call to make oneself brave; kihangsak in means take courage) (e:~ in, i mite ading leh i) (s:hang) (b:hangsak) (r:10.10.12)
kihangsak = (t:adj) (w:brave/plucky/fearless/valiant/valorous/intrepid/heroic) (d:hangsak, make brave, with ki, oneself: showing courage and not giving way to fear) (e:lau kei in. ~ in) (s:hang) (a:lau/meidawi) (b:hangsak) (r:27.10.19)
Kihangsak = (t:v) (w:be strong/be brave/take courage) (d:kihangsak, make oneself brave, at the start of a sentence; Kihangsak in is the command be strong) (e:~ in, i mite ading leh) (s:kipasalsak/Kihat) (b:kihangsak) (r:10.10.12/27.10.19) (q:draft)
kihansuah = (t:v) (w:encourage one another/exhort one another) (d:hansuah, urge on, with ki in the sense of each other: encourage one another) (e:khat leh khat ~ un la/nisimin khat leh khat ~ un | encourage one another daily/a pha-a gamtat nadingin ~ nading | to spur one another on toward good deeds) (s:kihanthawn/kidomto) (b:hansuah) (r:52.5.11/58.3.13/58.10.24) (q:draft)
kihanthawn = (t:v) (w:encourage one another/spur one another on) (d:hanthawn, stir up, with ki, one another: urge each other on to do something good) (e:i sep nadingin ~ ciat ni/khatlekhat ~ semsemzaw ni | let us encourage one another all the more) (s:kihansuah/kidomto) (b:hanthawn) (r:58.10.24/58.10.25) (q:draft)
kihanthawn = (t:v) (w:be stirred up/rouse oneself) (d:hanthawn, stir up, with ki, oneself: be roused or rouse oneself to act; often followed by tawm, by oneself) (e:Hansunga misite’ khate ~ a/Nangmah ~ tawm inla, dingtangto in | rouse yourself and stand up/nangmah na ~ tawm ding a | you will rouse yourself) (s:kisosuah/thotawm) (b:hanthawn) (r:23.14.9/26.38.14/23.51.17) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihanthawnin = (t:v) (w:taking courage/rousing oneself/encouraging one another) (d:kihanthawn with the linking suffix in: the person or group gathers courage and then goes on to act) (e:Israel mite ~ a ni masa/Amaziah ~ a mite paikhiatpih a | Amaziah took courage and led out his men/khatlekhat ~ na kihuh ciat ta un | encourage one another and help each other/khatlekhat ~ na kihuhzaw un | encourage one another and help each other more) (b:kihanthawn) (r:7.20.22/14.25.11/52.5.11/58.3.13) (q:draft)
kihanthawntawm = (t:v) (w:rouse oneself/stir oneself up) (d:kihanthawn, rouse oneself, with tawm, by oneself: stir oneself into action; the NIV has take notice here) (e:nangmah na ~ ding a) (s:kisosuah/thotawm) (r:26.38.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
Kihat = (t:v) (w:be strong/strengthen oneself) (d:hat, strong, with ki, oneself, written with a capital at the start of a sentence; Kihat sak in means make yourself strong) (e:~ sak in, zahtakna ngah pa aw) (s:kithakhauhsak) (r:27.10.19) (q:draft)
kihatsak = (t:v) (w:strengthen oneself/make oneself strong) (d:hatsak, strengthen, with ki, oneself; with tawm, by one's own effort: build up one's own power or position) (e:Abner amahmah ~ tawm hi) (s:kithakhauhsak) (b:hatsak) (r:10.3.6) (q:draft)
kihau = (t:v) (w:be had in plenty/be abundant) (d:hau, rich, with ki: of grain or a harvest, be got in abundance) (e:bawngtal’ tha tawh an ~ hi) (b:hau) (r:20.14.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihau = (t:v) (w:pretend to be rich) (d:in kihau sak, make oneself out to be rich, the opposite of kizawngsak, pretend to be poor) (e:zawng napi-in ~ sak uh a) (s:kihausak) (a:kizawngsak) (b:hau) (r:20.13.7) (q:draft)
kihauh = (t:v) (w:be plentiful/abound) (d:of food or harvest, be in abundance; a kihauh kum is a year of plenty) (e:A ~ kum sagih sungin/An a ~ luat manin | because the grain is so plentiful) (b:hauh) (r:1.41.47/30.9.13) (q:draft)
kihauhlawh = (t:v) (w:get rich by/be enriched by) (d:hauhlawh, get rich from, with ki; kihauhlawh tuan lo means one is none the richer for it) (e:zong ~ tuan lo hi) (a:kizawnlawh) (b:hauhlawh) (r:20.22.16) (q:draft)
kihausak = (t:v) (w:pretend to be rich/make oneself out to be rich) (d:hausak, make rich, with ki, oneself: act as if one were rich) (e:zawng napi-in ~ uh a) (s:kihau) (a:kizawngsak) (b:hausak) (r:20.13.7) (q:draft)
kihawk = (t:v) (w:be stripped off/be torn off) (d:passive ki with hawk strip off; said of skirts) (e:na nik hong ~ gawp sak a) (b:hawk) (r:24.13.22) (q:draft)
kihawkgawp = (t:v) (w:be torn off/be stripped off violently) (d:kihawk be stripped off with gawp, roughly or thoroughly) (e:na nik hong ~ a) (b:kihawk) (r:24.13.22) (q:draft)
kihawkkhia = (t:v) (w:be plundered/be robbed/be stripped away) (d:hawkkhia, strip off, with passive ki: have one's goods taken by force) (e:mi a neihsa ~ a) (s:kisut/kiluh) (b:hawkkhia) (r:19.12.5) (q:draft)
kihawl = (t:v) (w:be driven/be driven out/be banished) (d:passive of hawl, drive: usually with khia, be driven out of a place; hong kihawl gawpgawp is be driven hard) (e:khuamialna-ah ~ khia ding hi/Na omna panin kei hong ~ khia hi | I have been driven out from your presence/tua mipa ~ khia ding hi | that man shall be driven out/nakpi takin a hong ~ gawpgawp hi | we are driven very hard) (s:kinotkhia/kinawhkhia/kisawnkhia) (b:hawl) (r:18.18.18/32.2.4/3.17.4/25.5.5) (q:draft)
kihawlkhia = (t:v) (w:be driven out/be cut off/be banished) (d:hawlkhia, drive out, with passive ki: be driven out of a place, or be cut off from one's people) (e:ama mite lak panin ~ ding hi/hih leitung ukpa ~ ding hi | the ruler of this world will be driven out/amau’ teen’na mun panin ~ ta hen | may they be driven from their homes/ama mite kiang panin ~ ding hi | he shall be cut off from his people) (s:kinotkhia/kinawhkhia/kisawnkhia) (b:hawlkhia) (r:3.7.27/18.30.8/43.12.31/19.109.10/3.23.29) (q:draft)
kihawlkhiat = (t:v) (w:be driven out/be expelled) (d:form of kihawlkhia used before words such as khit, theih and nading) (e:dawi a ~ khit ciangin/Ama sung panin dawi a ~ khit phetin | as soon as the demon was driven out of him/sal suaksa mihonte panin a ~ theih nading | so that he could be expelled from the assembly of the exiles/note a pualamah hong ~ ciangin | when you are driven outside) (b:kihawlkhia) (r:40.12.43/15.10.8/40.9.33/42.13.28) (q:draft)
kihawlkhiate = (t:n) (w:exiles/outcasts/those driven out) (d:kihawlkhia, be driven out, with te, those who: people driven from their land) (e:Israel mi a ~ kaikhawmin/a ~ leh gimna ka thuaksak mite | the exiles and those I have made to suffer) (s:hawlkhiatte) (b:kihawlkhia) (r:23.11.12/33.4.6) (q:draft)
kihawlkhiatna = (t:n) (w:being driven out/expulsion) (d:kihawlkhiat be driven out, with the noun suffix na; before a noun of place, the place from which or to which one was driven) (e:Hih mipa a ~ thu Jesuh in/Hong ~ inn mahah lutkik ning | I will go back into the house I was driven from/A sung panin dawi sagih a ~ Mary | Mary, from whom seven demons had been driven out) (s:kisuankhiatna) (b:kihawlkhiat) (r:43.9.35/42.11.24/42.8.2) (q:draft)
kihawm = (t:v) (w:be divided/be distributed/be shared out) (d:hawm, distribute, with passive ki: of land, spoils or goods, be divided and shared out) (e:luah dingin leitang ~ ding hi/leitang pen aisaanna tawh ~ ding hi | the land shall be divided by lot/galte’ neihsate ~ keek ding a | the goods of the enemy will be divided up/leitang a ~ ciangin | when the land is divided) (b:hawm) (r:4.26.53/17.1.7/4.26.55/23.33.23/26.45.1) (q:draft)
kihawmin = (t:v) (w:being distributed/being issued/being sent out) (d:kihawm, be distributed, with the linking suffix in: said of an order sent out to every province) (e:gam khempeuhah ~ mi khempeuh kitheisakin) (b:kihawm) (r:17.8.13) (q:draft)
kihawmkeek = (t:v) (w:be divided up/be shared out) (d:kihawm be divided with keek, apart into portions; said of spoils) (e:galte’ neihsate ~ ding a) (r:23.33.23) (q:draft)
kihawmkhia = (t:v) (w:be issued/be published/be distributed) (d:hawmkhia, give out, with passive ki: of an order or letter, be sent out and made known to the people) (e:Susa khuapi panin a ~ ahi hi/Susa khua panin a ~ lai dal khat | a copy of the writing issued from Susa/Tua bang thupiakna lai ~ khinzo ta hi | such a decree had already been published) (b:hawmkhia) (r:17.3.15/17.4.8/27.6.10) (q:draft)
kihawmkik = (t:v) (w:be distributed/be sent out) (d:kihawm be distributed with kik again or in turn; said of letters sent to each official) (e:uliante tungah lai ~ a) (b:kihawm) (r:17.8.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihawmna = (t:n) (w:sharing/distribution) (d:kihawm be shared out with the noun suffix na) (e:a ~ thu ngaihsunin) (s:hawmna) (b:kihawm) (r:47.8.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihawmsak = (t:v) (w:be distributed/be divided out/be sent out) (d:passive ki with hawmsak distribute; of land shared out by lot and of letters sent round) (e:a gamh uh ~ ding hi/laitaite kituangsakin lai ~ hi | the letters were sent out by mounted couriers) (b:hawmsak) (r:4.26.56/17.8.10) (q:draft)
kihawmsuak = (t:v) (w:be emptied/be laid waste) (d:hawmsuak become empty with ki; kihawmsuak sakin is being made utterly empty) (e:Leitung ~ sakin kisiacip ding hi) (s:kisiacip) (b:hawmsuak) (r:23.24.3) (q:draft)
kihaza = (t:v) (w:envy one another/be jealous of one another) (d:haza envy with ki, one another) (e:kuamah i ~ kei ding hi/khatlekhat ~-in kitawng kiselin na om uh | you envy one another and quarrel) (b:haza) (r:48.5.26/46.3.3) (q:draft)
kihazatna = (t:n) (w:envy of one another/mutual jealousy) (d:hazatna, envy, with ki, each other: jealousy between people) (e:khat leh khat ~ tangin) (b:hazatna) (r:48.5.26) (q:draft)
kihazatnate = (t:see) <kihazatnate-in>
kihazatnate-in = (t:n) (w:jealousies/envyings) (d:plural of kihazatna envy of one another, with in: in or by jealousies) (e:kitotna le ~ i hun beisak kei ni) (r:45.13.13) (q:draft)
kihbawl = (t:v) (w:scorn/abhor/loathe) (d:kih, detest, with bawl, do to: treat with loathing) (e:zong ~ lo hi) (s:mudah/hua) (b:kih) (r:19.22.24) (q:draft)
