kiheek = (t:v) (w:betray one another/be betrayed/be handed over) (d:reciprocal or passive of heek in its sense of betraying, handing a person over to those who will harm him) (e:khat leh khat a ~ ding uh hi/khat leh khat sih nadingin a ~ ding uh | they will betray one another to death) (s:kilehhek/kilehheek) (b:heek) (r:40.24.10/42.9.44/41.13.12) (q:draft)
kiheekgawp = (t:v) (w:be twisted/be wrung violently) (d:ki with heek twist and gawp, roughly; with sak, cause trees to twist) (e:singkungte ~ sak a) (b:kiheek) (r:19.29.9) (q:draft)
kiheekheek = (t:v) (w:writhe/twist about) (d:ki with heek twist doubled: twist oneself again and again, as in labour pains) (e:naupaii-in ka ~ uh a) (s:kipeek/kitom) (r:23.26.18) (q:draft)
kiheh = (t:v) (w:be angry with oneself/be angry at each other) (d:ki with heh angry; kiheh tawm is be angry with oneself) (e:Nomau tungah ~ tawm kei un) (b:heh) (r:1.45.5) (q:draft)
kihehnem = (t:v) (w:comfort oneself/be comforted/comfort one another) (d:hehnem, comfort, with ki, oneself or one another: be comforted, console oneself, or comfort each other) (e:note khat leh khat na ~ un/Amnon thu-ah ~ hi | he was consoled about Amnon/nangmah thah ding vaihawmna tawh amah ~ hi | he consoles himself with the plan to kill you/Titu hong tun’na hang bekin hong ~ hi loin | we were comforted not only by the coming of Titus) (s:kinem/kinuamsak) (b:hehnem) (r:52.4.18/10.13.39/1.27.42/47.7.7) (q:draft)
kihehnep = (t:v) (w:be comforted/be encouraged) (d:passive ki with hehnep comfort; lungsim kihehnep nadingin is so that hearts may be encouraged) (e:lungsim ~ nadingin) (s:kinem) (b:hehnep) (r:51.2.1) (q:draft)
kihehnepna = (t:n) (w:comfort/consolation/encouragement) (d:hehnepna, comfort, with ki: the comfort a person receives, or the comforting of one another) (e:ka thuakna-ah keima ~ hi a/Tua hi leh keima ~ hi ding a | then this would be my consolation/Kicin’na, ~ na nei un | be made complete and comfort one another) (b:hehnepna) (r:19.119.50/47.13.11/18.6.10) (q:draft)
kihehpih = (t:v) (w:have compassion on one another/be kind to one another) (d:hehpih pity with ki, one another) (e:Khat leh khat na ~ un) (b:hehpih) (r:49.4.32) (q:draft)
kihehpih = (t:v) (w:be shown mercy/be pitied) (d:passive ki with hehpih pity; kihehpih hetloin is without any mercy) (e:~ hetloin sihna kithuaksak hi) (b:hehpih) (r:58.10.28) (q:draft)
kihehpihin = (t:v) (w:having compassion on one another/being kind to one another) (d:kihehpih with the connective in) (e:khatlekhat ~, dikna na kibawl uh hi/khatlekhat ~, lungsim nem tawh na kihozaw unla | be kind to one another and speak gently to each other) (b:kihehpih) (r:50.2.1/49.4.32) (q:draft)
kihehtawm = (t:v) (w:be angry with oneself) (d:ki with heh angry and tawm, toward oneself) (e:tungah ~ kei un) (r:1.45.5) (q:draft)
kihei = (t:v) (w:turn/turn round/turn back/return) (d:turn oneself round or toward something; with lamah or kiangah, turn to a person or direction; kihei kik means turn back) (e:Topa lamah ~ kik ni/mipa lau-in ~ a | the man was startled and turned over/leilu lamah ~ un | turn to the north/Topa kiangah a ~ uh ciangin | when they turn to the Lord) (s:kileh) (b:hei) (r:25.3.40/42.9.55/8.3.8/5.2.3/47.3.16) (q:draft)
Kihei = (t:v) (w:turn/turn back) (d:kihei written with a capital at the start of a sentence or of quoted speech, mostly as a command) (e:~ un la, gal tai un/~ in la siampite hih in | turn and strike down the priests/~ in la, ka nungah hong tuang in | turn and ride behind me/~ kikna leh khawlna bek tawh | only by turning back and rest) (b:kihei) (r:24.49.8/9.22.18/12.9.18/23.30.15) (q:draft)
kiheihei = (t:v) (w:turn to and fro/keep turning) (d:hei turn with ki, turn oneself, repeated to show that the action goes on; of a door on its hinges) (e:mi thadahpa a lupna tungah ~ hi/Kongkhak in kawmheek tungah a ~ lel bangin | as a door keeps turning on its hinges) (b:heihei) (r:20.26.14) (q:draft)
kiheikhia = (t:v) (w:turn away/turn aside/step aside) (d:turn oneself away from a place or person; also turn away in disloyalty) (e:kiang pan ~ nai lo hi/Jeroboam’ khialhnate panin Jehu ~ lo hi | Jehu did not turn away from the sins of Jeroboam/~ inla, hih lai-ah ding in | step aside and stand here/note hong thupiakna panin na ~ pak uh hi | you quickly turned aside from what he commanded you) (s:pialkhia) (b:kihei) (r:24.4.8/10.18.30/12.10.29/5.9.16) (q:draft)
kiheikhial = (t:adj) (w:perverse/wayward) (d:kihei turn with khial wrong: turned the wrong way) (e:A ~, a lehdo numei’ tapa aw) (r:9.20.30) (q:draft)
kiheikhiat = (t:v) (w:turn away/turn aside) (d:form of kiheikhia used before loh, theih and nading: turn away from a person, or of anger, turn away from those it rested on) (e:Kei’ kiang panin a ~ loh nadingun/a hehna eite tung pan a ~ theih nadingin | so that his anger may turn away from us/Topa kiang panin amah a ~ a | he turned away from the Lord/kong thupiakna panin na ~ uh le | if you turn away from what I command you) (b:kiheikhia) (r:24.32.40/14.29.10/14.25.27/5.11.28) (q:draft)
kiheikik = (t:v) (w:turn back/return/revert/repent) (d:kihei, turn, with kik, back or again: turn back to a person or away from a way of life) (e:a topa uh lamah ~ ding a/nangma lamah mimawhte hong ~ ding uh hi | sinners will turn back to you/kumpigam in David innkuan ah ~ kha thei ding hi | the kingdom may well go back to the house of David/a siatna panin a ~ leh | if it turns back from its evil) (s:kilehkik) (b:kihei) (r:11.12.27/24.15.7/19.51.13/11.12.26/24.18.8) (q:draft)
kiheilo = (t:v) (w:not turn/not turn aside) (d:kihei turn with the negative lo) (e:vei lam-ah hita leh ~ uh a) (b:kihei) (r:9.6.12) (q:draft)
kiheina = (t:n) (w:turning/turn/conversion) (d:kihei turn with na: a turning, the place one turns to, a turn of events, or a turning to God) (e:Gentailte ~ thu a zaksak uh ciangin/ka ~ peuhah Topa in nang thupha hong pia hi | wherever I turned the Lord blessed you/Topa in a pian’sak thu ~ ahi hi | it was a turn of events brought about by the Lord) (b:kihei) (r:44.15.3/9.14.47/1.30.30/11.12.15) (q:draft)
kiheisak = (t:v) (w:turn/make turn/turn back) (d:kihei with causative sak: cause a person, a heart or an animal to turn toward or away from something; kiheisak kik is bring back) (e:a pumpi khempeuh i ~ thei hi/nang hong zahtakte kei lamah hong ~ in | turn those who fear you toward me/amau lungsim uh amah in ~ hi | he turned their hearts/amau Topa Pasian kiangah a ~ kik ding hi | he will turn them back to the Lord their God) (b:kihei) (r:59.3.3/19.105.25/19.119.79/42.1.16) (q:draft)
kiheisan = (t:v) (w:turn away from/turn aside from) (d:kihei, turn, with san, away from someone, leaving him behind) (e:Hong ~ uh a, hong paisan uh hi) (s:lehngatsan/paisan) (b:kihei) (r:24.5.23) (q:draft)
kiheite = (t:n) (w:those who turn) (d:kihei turn with te, those who: people who turn to God) (e:Pasian kiangah hong ~ bawlsia loin/ama lamah a lungsim uh tawh a ~ | those who turn to him with their hearts) (b:kihei) (r:44.15.19/19.85.8) (q:draft)
kihel = (t:v) (w:be mixed/mingle/be mingled) (d:be mixed with something, which is named with tawh; also of peoples mingling with each other) (e:zatui kha tawh ~ leenggahtui/ka tui dawnte khitui tawh ~ hi | my drink is mixed with tears/sathau a ~ hita leh | whether it is mixed with oil/gamdang mite tawh a ~ suak ta hi | it has become mixed with foreign peoples) (r:41.15.23/15.9.2/19.102.9/3.7.10) (q:draft)
kihel = (t:v) (w:be included/take part/join in/be among) (d:be one of a group or join in what it does; kihel lo is not counted among, and kihel loin is without, apart from) (e:Pasian ~ loin kua in an ne-in/mipilte’ lak-a ~ theihna ahi hi | it is being able to be among the wise/kumpipa zong tua lakah hong ~ hi | the king too joined in among them/a gual nuamte’ laamna-ah na va ~ ding hi | you will go and join the dance of the joyful) (r:21.2.25/4.23.9/20.15.31/28.7.5/24.31.4) (q:draft)
kihelh = (t:v) (w:alternate/be set by turns) (d:of two kinds of things, be placed one after the other in turn; a form of kihel be mixed) (e:gah khat, cih bangin ~ hi/a kimkot khempeuh ah ~ to dimdiam hi | they alternated evenly all the way round) (s:kilaih) (b:kihel) (r:2.39.26/26.41.18) (q:draft)
kihelhsak = (t:v) (w:alternate/set by turns) (d:kihelh alternate with causative sak: place two kinds of things one after the other) (e:cih bangin na ~ ding hi) (b:kihelh) (r:2.28.34) (q:draft)
kihelhto = (t:v) (w:alternate/follow one after another) (d:kihelh alternate with to, onward in sequence) (e:a kimkot khempeuhah ~ dimdiam hi) (b:kihelh) (r:26.41.18) (q:draft)
kihelin = (t:v) (w:mingling/joining/being included) (d:kihel with the linking suffix in; with tawh it is mixing with something or joining someone) (e:Minam dangte tawh ~/Satan zong amaute lakah hong ~ | Satan also came among them/sisan tawh ~ leitungah a kiasuk hi | mixed with blood, it fell on the earth/a kisiansuahna uhah nang zong va ~ | you too go and join in their purification) (b:kihel) (r:19.106.35/18.2.1/66.8.7/44.21.24) (q:draft)
kihelkhawm = (t:v) (w:be mixed together/be alloyed) (d:kihel be mixed with khawm, together; of metals melted together) (e:sik le sumngo ~ kuaitan zo zaw/sik, hak, le ngun a ~ sung panin | from iron, lead and silver mixed together) (b:kihel) (r:24.15.12/26.22.18) (q:draft)
kihelkhawm = (t:v) (w:take part in together/share in) (d:join in two things at once) (e:A nih tuakah ~ lehang) (b:kihel) (r:46.10.22) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihelkim = (t:v) (w:be fully mixed/be well mixed) (d:kihel be mixed with kim, completely; of wine mixed with spices) (e:a ~ ngiingei hai khat om a) (r:19.75.8) (q:draft)
kihelkim = (t:v) (w:take part from each/be included from all) (d:kihel take part with kim, every: let each group be represented) (e:beh tuamtuamte sung pan ~ un) (r:14.35.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihelpih = (t:v) (w:be mixed with) (d:kihel be mixed with pih together with; na kihelpih na nin is the impurity that is mixed in with you) (e:na ~ na nin khempeuh uh) (b:kihel) (r:23.1.25) (q:draft)
kihelsak = (t:v) (w:be counted among/let take part/include) (d:kihel be included with sak cause: cause or allow someone to be included) (e:Mawhneite lakah amah ~ hi/Biakinn lamna-ah ko zong hong ~ un | let us too take part in building the temple) (b:kihel) (r:42.22.37/15.4.2) (q:draft)
kihelte = (t:n) (w:those included/those among/those mixed) (d:kihel with te plural: people counted among a group, or things mixed with something) (e:a kiciamtehte lakah a ~ hi uh a/galmatte lak-a ~ khat ahi hi | he was one of those among the captives/an nel moh sathau lim tak-a ~ | loaves of fine flour well mixed with oil/a thahatte lakah amaute a ~ ahi uh hi | they were among the warriors) (b:kihel) (r:4.11.26/3.7.12/17.2.6/13.12.1) (q:draft)
kihem = (t:v) (w:depart/turn away/withdraw/separate oneself) (d:move oneself away from a place, a group or evil) (e:Siatna panin ~ in la/~ un, ~ un, Babilon panin paikhia un | depart, depart, go out from Babylon/hih mihonte lak panin ~ un | separate yourselves from this assembly/Joab ~ khia-in Israel sung khempeuh ah pai a | Joab left and went through all Israel/Mipilte in Topa zahtakin siatna panin ~ a | the wise fear the Lord and turn from evil) (r:19.37.27/4.16.21/23.52.11/13.21.4/20.14.16) (q:draft)
kihemin = (t:v) (w:departing/moving away/being removed) (d:kihem with the linking suffix in: the moving away is followed by another action) (e:Hih lai panin ~ nisuahna lamah/mual liante ~, mual neute a kikhin zongin | though the mountains depart and the hills be moved) (b:kihem) (r:11.17.3/23.54.10) (q:draft)
kihemkhia = (t:v) (w:depart/withdraw/turn away) (d:kihem, move away, with khia, out; with panin, move away from a person, a task or evil) (e:Siatna panin ~ in la/Saul kiang panin amah ~ khin ta hi | he had departed from Saul/nasepna panin amau ~-in | retiring from the service/amaute kiang panin ~ in | keep away from them) (s:pialkhia) (r:19.34.14/9.18.12/4.8.25/20.1.15) (q:draft)
kihen = (t:v) (w:be bound/be tied/be chained) (d:hen, bind, with passive ki: be tied or chained; also of what is bound in heaven, the opposite of kiphel, be loosed) (e:Na khutte ~ lo hi/vantungah a ~ ding hi | it will be bound in heaven/Piter sikkhau nih tawh ~ a | Peter was bound with two chains/kolbulh leh sikkhau tawh tamveipi a ~ ngei hangin | though he had often been bound with fetters and chains) (s:kikhih) (a:kiphel) (b:hen) (r:10.3.34/40.16.19/40.18.18/44.12.6/41.5.4) (q:draft)
kihencip = (t:v) (w:be bound/be tied up) (d:hencip, bind fast, with passive ki: be tied up tightly; in Job 5:16 of the unjust being silenced) (e:Amaute lah ~ lo a/Eufratis Gun lianpi-ah a ~ vantungmi lite | the four angels bound at the great river Euphrates/thuman lote ahih leh ~ hi | as for the unjust, they are shut up) (s:kikhih) (b:hencip) (r:27.3.25/18.5.16/66.9.14) (q:draft)
kihencipna = (t:n) (w:bondage/being bound/bond) (d:kihencip be bound fast with the noun suffix na) (e:Hih a ~ panin Sabbath ni-in/sanggamnu ahi zongin ~ om lo hi | nor is the sister under bondage) (b:kihencip) (r:42.13.16/46.7.15) (q:draft)
kihenin = (t:v) (w:being bound/being tied) (d:kihen, be bound, with the linking suffix in; with tawh, being bound to someone) (e:a pasal tawh ~ a om hi) (b:kihen) (r:46.7.39) (q:draft)
kihenna = (t:n) (w:bonds/chains/imprisonment) (d:kihen, be bound, with the noun suffix na: the state of being bound, or the cords and chains that bind) (e:hong ~ khaute sut un/~ ka thuak lai takin | while I am suffering imprisonment/~ leh thong sung khiat nadingte | chains and imprisonment/hong ~ khau sutat-in | breaking the cords that bound you) (s:kikhihna/sikkol) (b:kihen) (r:23.52.2/50.1.17/44.20.23/24.2.20) (q:draft)
kihennate = (t:n) (w:chains/bonds/fetters) (d:plural of kihenna, that which binds) (e:amau a ~ botsatkhia hi) (s:kikhihnate) (b:kihenna) (r:19.107.14) (q:draft)
kihensa = (t:see) <kihensa-in>
kihensa-in = (t:adv) (w:bound/already bound) (d:kihen be bound with sa already and in: in a bound state) (e:Kai-afas kiangah ~ Zeisu a paisak hi) (r:43.18.24) (q:draft)
kihente = (t:n) (w:bundles/pouches) (d:kihen be tied with the plural te: things tied up; sum kihente are bundles or pouches of money) (e:sum ~ a muh uh ciangin) (b:kihen) (r:1.42.35) (q:draft)
kihep = (t:v) (w:part from/separate from) (d:seen only in kihep khiat, go away from someone) (e:amah a ~ khiat khit phetin) (r:11.20.36) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihepkhiat = (t:v) (w:withdraw/go away/depart) (d:leave a person or place; form used before ciangin and khit) (e:Tua lai panin amah a ~ ciangin/ama kiang panin Siriate a ~ khit uh ciangin | after the Arameans had withdrawn from him/Ama kiang panin amah a ~ khit phetin | as soon as he had left him) (r:12.10.15/14.24.25/11.20.36) (q:draft)
kihhuai = (t:adj) (w:detestable/disgusting/unclean/abominable) (d:so unclean or wicked that it is to be loathed; said of forbidden food, idols and sinful acts) (e:A ~ na khatpeuh peuh/tua in a ~ ahi hi | that is detestable/note’ adingin a ~ ahi hi | they are detestable to you/Ammon mite’ aa ahi a ~ Milkom | Milkom, the detestable god of the Ammonites) (s:muhdahhuai/nin) (a:siangtho) (r:5.14.3/42.4.33/3.18.22/3.11.20/11.11.5) (q:draft)
kihhuaina = (t:n) (w:abomination/detestable thing/impurity) (d:kihhuai, detestable, with the noun suffix na: something disgusting or unclean, or the state of being so) (e:Pasian mai-ah ~ ahi hi/amau tegel ~ a gamta khin uh ahi hi | both of them have done what is detestable/A kisia thei ~ in a kilawm lo munah | the abomination that causes desolation, in a place where it should not be) (s:muhdahhuaina/nitna) (a:siangthona) (b:kihhuai) (r:42.16.15/52.4.7/3.20.13/41.13.14) (q:draft)
kihhuainate = (t:n) (w:abominations/detestable things/detestable practices) (d:plural of kihhuaina: detestable things, acts or idols) (e:hih ~ khempeuh hih uh a/minamte’ ~ zui uh hi | they followed the detestable practices of the nations/Na ~ uh kei kiang pan na paihkhiat uh a | you put your detestable things away from me) (s:kihhuaite) (b:kihhuaina) (r:3.18.27/66.17.5/14.36.14/24.4.1) (q:draft)
Kihhuainate = (t:n) (w:abominations/detestable things) (d:kihhuainate written with a capital in a title) (e:leitung ~’ Nu Babilon Khuapi) (b:kihhuainate) (r:66.17.5) (q:draft)
kihhuaisa = (t:v) (w:detest/regard as detestable) (d:kihhuai, detestable, with sa, consider: find something loathsome) (e:Topa in migilote’ ngaihsutna ~ a) (s:mudah/hua) (b:kihhuai) (r:20.15.26) (q:draft)
kihhuaisak = (t:v) (w:defile/pollute/make detestable) (d:kihhuai, detestable, with causative sak: make a thing or oneself unclean) (e:a pumpi uh ~ a) (s:ninsak/nitsak) (a:siansuah/siangthosak) (b:kihhuai) (r:65.1.8) (q:draft)
kihhuaisapa = (t:n) (w:one who abhors/one who detests) (d:kihhuaisa regard as detestable with pa, the man who does so) (e:Milim a ~ aw) (b:kihhuaisa) (r:45.2.22) (q:draft)
kihhuaite = (t:n) (w:detestable things/abominations) (d:kihhuai with plural te; also follows a noun as detestable, said of several things) (e:gamtatna a ~ zuih ding na kisin kei/minamte’ gamtatna a ~ mah bangin | following the detestable practices of the nations/hih a ~ khatpeuh a hihte peuhmah | everyone who does any of these detestable things) (s:kihhuainate) (b:kihhuai) (r:5.18.9/12.21.2/3.18.29) (q:draft)
kihial = (t:v) (w:be rolled up) (d:passive ki with hial roll up, as a weaver rolls up cloth) (e:ka nuntakna ~ khin a) (s:kizial) (b:hial) (r:23.38.12) (q:draft)
kihih = (t:v) (w:be done) (d:hih, do, with passive ki: something is done, or is done to or for a person, who is named with tungah) (e:Israelte sungah tua bang ~ lo hi/Amah a that mipa tungah tua bangin ~ ding hi | so it will be done for the man who kills him/note’ tungah bang hong ~ lai ding ahi hiam | what more will be done to you/bangci ~ ding ahi hiam | what must be done) (s:kisem) (r:10.13.12/9.17.27/19.120.3/17.1.15) (q:draft)
kihihna = (t:n) (w:quarrel/conflict/fight) (d:kihih, do to one another, with na: a clash or dealings between two sides) (e:khatlekhat i ~ ding bang om/Efesa khuamite tawh ka ~ uhah | in my fight with the people of Ephesus) (b:kihih) (r:14.35.21/46.15.32) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihihsak = (t:v) (w:be proud/boast/be arrogant) (d:carry oneself proudly; kihihsak pih is boast in or put trust in something) (e:pawlkhat in sakolte ~ pih hi/a ~ pai kuahkuah aklui | a strutting rooster/~ pau in, kiphatsakna leh simmawhna tawh kam a pau | speaking arrogantly, with pride and contempt/na minthan’ nading leh na ~ nadingin | for your glory and your splendor) (s:kiphasak/kisathei) (a:kiniamkhiat) (r:19.20.7/20.30.31/19.31.18/18.40.10) (q:draft)
kihihsak = (t:v) (w:be done for) (d:passive of hihsak: something is done for or on behalf of a person, who is named with ading) (e:amau’ adingin ~ hi/tua nu adingin bang ~ ding ahi hiam | what can be done for her/bang hong ~ ding deih na hi hiam | what do you want to be done for you) (b:hihsak) (r:1.42.25/12.4.14/12.4.13) (q:draft)
kihihsakna = (t:n) (w:pride/arrogance/haughtiness) (d:kihihsak, be proud, with the noun suffix na: pride that makes oneself out to be great) (e:~ tawh gamta na hi hiam/kiphatsakna leh ~, gamtatsia leh thuzuau ka mudah hi | I hate pride and arrogance, evil conduct and lies/~ in kitotna bek piangsak thei a | arrogance produces nothing but strife/na kam sung pan ~ gingkhiasak kei in | do not let arrogance come out of your mouth) (s:kiphatsakna/kiliatsakna/kisaktheihna) (a:kiniamkhiatna) (b:kihihsak) (r:12.19.22/20.8.13/20.13.10/9.2.3) (q:draft)
kihihsaknate = (t:n) (w:arrogance/insolence/proud acts) (d:plural of kihihsakna, from kihihsak be proud) (e:a kiphatsakna, a ~) (s:kiphatsaknate) (b:kihihsakna) (r:23.16.6) (q:draft)
kihihsakpih = (t:v) (w:trust in/boast in/take pride in) (d:kihihsak be proud with pih: be proud of something and rely on it) (e:mi pawlkhat in sakolte ~ hi/Topa i Pasian’ min bek i ~ hi | we trust only in the name of the Lord our God) (s:kisaktheihpih/kiphatsakpih/kisialhpih) (b:kihihsak) (r:19.20.7) (q:draft)
kihihthei = (t:v) (w:can be done/be permissible) (d:kihih be done with thei be able) (e:a ~ khempeuh hihna in) (b:kihih) (r:46.10.23) (q:draft)
kihil = (t:v) (w:be shown/be made known) (d:be shown or made known by a sign, probably a form of kihilh, be told; bang limin hong kihil ding asks by what sign something will be made known) (e:bang limin hong ~ ding cih/bang limin a hong ~ ding hiam | by what sign will it be shown) (r:40.24.3/42.21.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihilh = (t:v) (w:be taught/be preached/be told) (d:passive of hilh, teach: be taught, told or preached; Lungdamna Thu kihilh means the gospel is preached) (e:mipawl khempeuh a ~ ding hi/na gamtat nadingin thu hong ~ ding hi | you will be told what you must do/thu a ~ bangin a gen uh a | they said as they were instructed/leitung khempeuhah Lungdamna Thu ~ ding hi | the gospel will be preached in the whole world) (b:hilh) (r:41.13.10/23.28.26/44.9.6/40.28.15/40.24.14) (q:draft)
Kihilhhilh = (t:v) (w:be taught again and again/be rebuked often) (d:kihilh, be taught, with hilh doubled for a repeated action: be taught or corrected again and again; written with a capital at the start of the sentence) (e:~ napi-a a mang nuam lote) (r:20.29.1) (q:draft)
kihilhin = (t:v) (w:teaching one another/instructing one another) (d:kihilh with the linking suffix in, here with ki in the sense of each other: teaching one another) (e:note khat leh khat ~/pilna tawh khatlekhat thu ~ na kitai un | teach and admonish one another with wisdom) (b:kihilh) (r:51.3.16) (q:draft)
kihilhin = (t:v) (w:being preached/being proclaimed) (d:kihilh with the linking suffix in, here passive: a message being taught or announced) (e:thupha Lungdamna Thu ~) (b:kihilh) (r:44.10.36) (q:draft)
kihilhna = (t:n) (w:instruction/discipline/correction/teaching) (d:kihilh, be taught, with the noun suffix na: the teaching or correction that one is given; thu kihilhna zui is follow instruction) (e:thu ~ a zui mi in/~ zui lo mi in zawn’na leh mindaina ngah | one who does not follow instruction gets poverty and shame/thu ~ zuihna in lungnopna hi | following instruction brings contentment/~ na ngah khit uh mah bangin | just as you were taught) (s:thuhilhna/hilhna) (b:kihilh) (r:20.13.18/20.10.17/20.13.13/51.2.6) (q:draft)
kihilhnate = (t:n) (w:instructions/teachings) (d:kihilhna, instruction, with the plural te: the things that are taught to someone) (e:Hong ~ zui-in pilna ngah un la/Hong ~ lencip in la khahsuah kha kei in | hold on to instruction and do not let it go) (s:hilhnate/thuhilhnate/kihilhte) (b:kihilhna) (r:20.8.33/20.4.13) (q:draft)
kihilhsa = (t:adj) (w:trained/taught) (d:that has already been taught or trained, sa marks a completed action) (e:nangmah hong ~ thute/a ~ ama' mi zathum leh sawm-le-giatte | his 318 trained men/Note tungah a hong ~ bangin | as you were taught/lim takin a ~, an a cil nuam bawngla | a well-trained heifer that loves to thresh) (s:kiseksa) (b:kihilh) (r:42.1.4/1.14.14/51.2.7/28.10.11) (q:draft)
kihilhsak = (t:v) (w:let teach/have oneself taught) (d:hilhsak cause to teach with ki oneself; the verse follows the older English wording, let your right hand teach you awesome deeds) (e:na taklam khut nangmah ~ in) (b:hilhsak) (r:19.45.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihilhte = (t:n) (w:teachings/instruction/things taught) (d:kihilh be taught with the plural te: the things one is taught) (e:hong ~ mang lecin) (s:kihilhnate/hilhnate) (b:kihilh) (r:20.19.20) (q:draft)
kihilhtelna = (t:n) (w:explanation/what has been explained) (d:passive ki with hilhtelna explanation: the explaining that was given to someone) (e:thu a hong ~ in a maan) (b:hilhtelna) (r:27.8.26) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihilhthei = (t:v) (w:be able to teach one another/be able to instruct each other) (d:ki each other with hilh teach and thei be able) (e:khatlekhat zong a ~ dingin) (b:kihilh) (r:45.15.14) (q:draft)
kihilkik = (t:v) (w:go back/return) (d:meaning taken from the verse, not to go back to Herod; with kik back; the relation to kihil be made known is not clear) (e:Herod kiangah a ~ loh nadingun) (r:40.2.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihilna = (t:n) (w:sign/symbol/omen/warning) (d:a sign or indication of what will happen, also a warning that is given, as in a dream; kihilna lim in Numbers is an omen sought by divination) (e:a hun danga bangin ~ lim/mite sungah lim leh ~ ka hi uh hi | we are signs and symbols among the people/a mang sung mahah a ~ bangin | as he was warned in a dream) (b:kihil) (r:4.24.1/23.8.18/40.2.22) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihing = (t:v) (w:be kept alive/be made alive) (d:passive of hing; kihing khawi is to be spared and allowed to live, kihing kiksak is to be raised to life again) (e:a ni thum ni-in ~ kiksak ding hi/kei hong ~ khawi lai hi | my life was still spared/mihing hita leh ~ khawi lo ding hi | a person shall not be allowed to live/ni thum ni-in hong ~ kiksak ding hi | on the third day I will be raised to life) (a:kithat) (b:hing) (r:40.17.23/2.19.13/1.32.30/40.16.21) (q:draft)
kihingkik = (t:v) (w:be raised to life again/be made alive again) (d:ki with hingkik come back to life; followed by sak, be raised again) (e:si-in a ~ sakpa a dingin) (b:hingkik) (r:47.5.15) (q:draft)
kihingkiksak = (t:v) (w:be raised to life/be raised from the dead) (d:passive of hingkiksak, make alive again) (e:sihna panin Khrih ~ khin a/misite a ~ lo ding hileh | if the dead are not raised/Khrih tawh a kizom khempeuh zong ~ ding hi | all who are joined to Christ will also be made alive/Pasian tawh eite i kipawl theih nadingin ~ hi | he was raised so that we may be reconciled with God) (s:kihingsakkik/kithokiksak) (b:hingkiksak) (r:45.6.9/46.15.16/46.15.22/45.4.25) (q:draft)
kihingsakkik = (t:v) (w:be raised to life/be brought back to life) (d:passive ki with hingsakkik bring back to life) (e:misite ~ a) (s:kihingkiksak/kithokiksak) (b:hingsakkik) (r:42.7.22) (q:draft)
kihisak = (t:v) (w:be proud/be arrogant/be haughty) (d:think much of oneself, be proud or arrogant; mi kihisak is a proud person, the opposite of one who humbles himself) (e:mi kimkhat in a ~ uh hi/Mi ~ tawh kipawlin van kisutte ngahna sangin | than to share plunder with the proud/amaute ~ zo nawn lo uh hi | they could no longer raise their heads/Topa in a ~ mite mudah a | the Lord detests the proud) (s:kiphasak/kiliansak/kisathei) (a:kiniamkhiat/kiniamsak) (r:46.4.18/20.21.24/20.16.19/7.8.28/20.16.5) (q:draft)
kihisakin = (t:v) (w:be arrogant/be proud/be haughty) (d:kihisak with the linking suffix in) (e:amaute ~ na thupiaknate don lo uh hi/kote’ pute pate ~ lung khauh uh a | our ancestors became arrogant and stiff-necked/Amaute ~ ka deih loh nate gamta uh | they were haughty and did things I detest/note ~ na kisial uh hi | you boast in your arrogance) (s:kiphasakin) (a:kiniamkhiatin) (b:kihisak) (r:16.9.29/26.16.50/16.9.16/59.4.16) (q:draft)
kihisakte = (t:n) (w:the proud/the arrogant/the haughty) (d:kihisak, be proud, with the plural te: people who think highly of themselves) (e:mi ~ bang mahin sim lo a/mi ~ ka eng hi | I envied the arrogant/a ~ in siat ding a manawh | the proud are heading for ruin/mi ~, kei lang pangin hong tho hi | the arrogant rise up against me) (s:kiphasakte/kiliansakte) (a:kiniamkhiatte) (b:kihisak) (r:20.3.34/20.18.12/19.73.3/19.86.14) (q:draft)
kiho = (t:v) (w:talk together/converse/speak with) (d:talk with one another; the person spoken with is marked by tawh, with) (e:Zeisu tawh a ~ uh hi/Nang tawh a ~ keimah in | I who am speaking with you/Tua nu kumpipa tawh ~-in a om lai takin | while she was still speaking with the king/David leh Saul a ~ khit a kipanin | after David had finished talking with Saul) (s:kihokhawm/kihopih/kihoho) (r:40.17.3/7.14.7/43.4.26/11.1.22/9.18.1) (q:draft)
kihoho = (t:v) (w:converse/talk together/commune) (d:talk with one another at length, kiho with ho repeated for an action that goes on; in Psalm 77:6 of communing with one's own heart) (e:Kamkhum tawh i ~ ngei hi/ka lungsimah ka ~ a | I commune with my own heart/ka galte ~-in | my enemies talking together) (s:kiho/kihokhawm) (b:hoho) (r:19.55.14/19.77.6/19.71.10) (q:draft)
kihoin = (t:v) (w:talking with/speaking with) (d:kiho talk together with the connective in) (e:Zeisu tawh ~ Jerusalem khuapi-ah/inn kongkhak-ah amah tawh ~ | speaking with him at the entrance of the house) (b:kiho) (r:42.9.31/1.43.19) (q:draft)
kihokhawm = (t:v) (w:talk together/speak with) (d:kiho converse with khawm together) (e:amah tawh na ~ thei ding hi) (s:kiho/kihopih) (b:kiho) (r:26.24.27) (q:draft)
kihon = (t:v) (w:be saved/be rescued/be delivered) (d:passive of hon, save: be saved or rescued, with panin for the enemy or danger) (e:ka galte kiang panin kei hong ~ hi/na langte panun note hong ~ ding hi | you will be saved from your enemies/Tua bangpi-in kote hong ~ ding ahi hiam | how then can we be saved/eite lah hong ~ nai kei lailai hi | and we are still not saved) (s:kihonkhia/kihotkhiat) (b:hon) (r:10.22.4/4.10.9/23.64.5/24.8.20) (q:draft)
kihon = (t:v) (w:be opened/open) (d:passive of hon, open; of a door or a way) (e:Topa hangin kei ading kongkhak a ~/Kiu un; kongkhak hong ~ ding hi | knock, and the door will be opened to you/a kiute khempeuh a dingin kong ~ ding hi | to everyone who knocks the door will be opened/Sabbath bei khit mateng a ~ loh nadingin | so that they would not be opened until the Sabbath was over) (s:kihong) (a:kikhak) (b:hon) (r:47.2.12/44.14.27/42.11.9/42.11.10/16.13.19) (q:draft)
kihona = (t:n) (w:conversation/talk/talking together) (d:kiho talk together with na: the talking, or with mun the place where they talked) (e:kumpipa tawh a ~ a za sim kuamah/amah tawh a ~ munah suang khuam khat phut | set up a stone pillar where he had talked with him/Jesuh in hih amaute’ ~ thu thei ahih manin | because Jesus knew of this discussion of theirs/mihonte lakah kam ~ tampi om a | there was much talk among the crowds) (s:kihopihna) (b:kiho) (r:24.38.27/1.35.14/40.16.8/43.7.12) (q:draft)
kihong = (t:v) (w:open/be opened) (d:be open or be opened, said of a container, a door or gate, a tomb, the sky, and of eyes and ears; a kihong before a noun means open) (e:A kisin cip lo a ~ beel/mittawte’ mit ~ ding a | the eyes of the blind will be opened/En un, van ~ a | look, heaven is open/Sabbath ni le Khadet ni-in ~ ding hi | it is to be opened on the Sabbath and at the New Moon) (s:kihon) (a:kikhak) (r:4.19.15/40.27.52/23.35.5/44.7.56/26.46.1)
kihong = (t:v) (w:extend)
kihongin = (t:v) (w:opening/being opened) (d:kihong, be opened, with the linking suffix in: the opening is followed by what happens next) (e:lei ~ Dathan valhtum a/mipa’ bil ~, a leii zong hong kol a | the man's ears were opened and his tongue was loosened/vantung ~ ka et leh | heaven stood open, and as I looked/Vantungah a om Pasian’ biakinnpi ~ | the temple of God in heaven was opened) (b:kihong) (r:19.106.17/41.7.35/66.19.11/66.11.19) (q:draft)
kihongkek = (t:v) (w:be broken open/burst open) (d:kihong open with kek, apparently split or wide apart; said of city walls or gates) (e:A kulhpite tu-in ~ a) (r:26.26.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihongsa = (t:adj) (w:open/opened) (d:kihong be opened, with sa for a completed action; a kihongsa hankhuk, an open grave) (e:a ~ hankhuk tawh kibang hi/Amau gawlgui un a ~ hankhuk ahi uh hi | their throats are open graves/vantungah kong a ~-in a om ka mu hi | I saw a door standing open in heaven) (s:honsa) (a:khaksa) (b:kihong) (r:19.5.9/45.3.13/66.4.1) (q:draft)
kihongsak = (t:v) (w:open/let open) (d:kihong open with causative sak: cause to open up) (e:leitang ~ unla) (b:kihong) (r:23.45.8) (q:draft)
kihongtawm = (t:v) (w:open by itself/open of its own accord) (d:kihong open with tawm, by itself) (e:ama thu-in hong ~ a) (r:44.12.10) (q:draft)
kihonkhia = (t:v) (w:be saved/be rescued/escape) (d:passive of honkhia, rescue: be saved or delivered out of danger) (e:ama hatna tawh ~ zo lo hi/thu khauhpa’ mat mite ~ zo ding ahi hiam | can the captives of the fierce be rescued/Tua ni ciangin Judah mite ~ ding a | in those days Judah will be saved/amaute in hong ko uh a, amaute ~ hi | they cried out to you and were saved) (s:kihon/kihotkhiat) (b:honkhia) (r:19.33.16/23.49.24/24.33.16/19.22.5) (q:draft)
kihonkhiazo = (t:v) (w:be delivered/be saved/be safe) (d:kihonkhia, be rescued, with zo for a completed action: have been delivered, be safe) (e:Hong ~ hi | we are delivered) (b:kihonkhia) (r:24.7.10) (q:draft)
kihonsak = (t:v) (w:be saved by/let save) (d:honsak, cause to save, with ki: let oneself be saved by someone; used in taunts such as let your idols save you) (e:na milim kaihkhopte ~ in/mite ding sak in la, nangmah ~ in | let those people stand up and save you/a hong hon thei ahihleh ~ ta un | if they can save you, let them save you) (b:honsak) (r:23.57.13/23.47.13/24.2.28) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihontawm = (t:v) (w:save oneself/deliver oneself) (d:hon save with ki and tawm by oneself) (e:amau leh amau ~ thei lo uh hi) (r:23.47.14) (q:draft)
kihonthahna = (t:n) (w:slaughter/massacre) (d:apparently ki with hon in numbers, that kill and the noun suffix na: killing of many together) (e:Tua banga ~ panin pawlkhat ka suaktasak) (r:26.6.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihopih = (t:v) (w:greet one another/speak with/have fellowship with) (d:speak with each other; in the letters, greet one another and share fellowship) (e:a siangtho kinapna tawh na ~ un/a siangtho napna tawh na ~ ciat un | greet one another with a holy kiss/note tawh maitang kimu-a ~ ding ka lamen hi | I hope to talk with you face to face/ama Tapa Zeisu Khazih tawh ka ~ uh | we have fellowship with his Son Jesus Christ) (s:kiho/kihokhawm) (b:hopih) (r:52.5.26/62.1.3/46.16.20/63.1.12) (q:draft)
kihopihin = (t:v) (w:greeting one another/talking with one another) (d:kihopih speak with each other with the connective in) (e:khat leh khat ~ i kikup khop ding/Unau ki-itna tawh khatlekhat ~ na kinam un | greet one another with a kiss of brotherly love) (b:kihopih) (r:64.1.14/47.13.12) (q:draft)
kihopihna = (t:n) (w:talking with/conversation) (d:kihopih speak with and the noun suffix na) (e:numei tawh a ~ lamdang a sa) (s:kihona) (b:kihopih) (r:43.4.27) (q:draft)
kihot = (t:v) (w:be rowed) (d:passive of hot, row a boat) (e:gal gunkuang hong ~ nawn lo ding) (b:hot) (r:23.33.21) (q:draft)
kihot = (t:v) (w:be tossed/be stirred up) (d:of water driven about in a storm) (e:Tui ~ pha mahmaha kiliing) (r:44.27.18) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihothei = (t:see) <kihothei-in>
kihothei-in = (t:v) (w:be able to talk together/have fellowship) (d:kiho converse with thei be able and in; in this verse, having fellowship with one another) (e:khat leh khat ~, a Tapa) (r:62.1.7) (q:draft)
kihotheihna = (t:n) (w:fellowship/communion) (d:kiho talk together with theih can and the noun suffix na: being able to speak with one another, fellowship) (e:Kha Siangtho tawh ~ ahi zongin/Kha Siangtho’ ~ ahi zongin | and the fellowship of the Holy Spirit) (r:50.2.1/47.13.14) (q:draft)
kihotkhiana = (t:n) (w:salvation/deliverance) (d:being saved, from hotkhia save; ka kihotkhiana ki is the horn of my salvation) (e:ka lum leh ka ~ ki) (s:kihotkhiatna/hotkhiatna) (r:10.22.3) (q:draft)
kihotkhiat = (t:v) (w:be saved/be rescued/be redeemed) (d:hotkhiat save with ki-, here passive; the form used before words such as theih and ding) (e:Kote hong ~ theih nadingin na maitang/nang hong ~ nadingin | so that you may be saved/note hong ~ ding hun hong naita | the time of your redemption is near/Note a hong ~ theih nading thu | the way for you to be saved) (s:kihonkhia/kihon) (b:hotkhiat) (r:19.80.19/42.21.28/24.4.14/44.16.17) (q:draft)
kihotkhiatna = (t:n) (w:salvation/deliverance/rescue) (d:being saved or delivered; used also of God as the one who saves) (e:keima ~ ama tung pan hong pai hi/Ka suangpi, ka ~, ka munkip muan’huai | my rock, my salvation, my secure fortress/a sathau nilhpa’ ~ buk ahi hi | he is a fortress of salvation for his anointed/ka ~ Pasian | the God of my salvation) (s:hotkhiatna/gupna/hotna/kihotkhiana) (b:hotkhiatna) (r:19.62.1/19.28.8/19.62.6/19.18.46) (q:draft)
kihozaw = (t:v) (w:speak to one another/talk together) (d:kiho converse with zaw, apparently rather or instead; here speak to each other with a gentle heart) (e:lungsim nem tawh na ~ unla) (b:kiho) (r:49.4.32) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihta = (t:v) (w:fear/be afraid of/dread) (d:be afraid of someone or something, the thing feared standing before the verb; kihta kei un means do not be afraid) (e:mi tulsawm tampite ka ~ kei hi/namsau ~-in nungkik lo uh hi | they do not turn back for fear of the sword/kuamah a ~ lo humpinelkai | the lion that fears no one/Lau kei un la, amaute ~ kei un | do not be terrified, do not be afraid of them/Pasian’ daan piak ding ~ ka hih manin | because I feared punishment from God) (s:lau) (r:19.3.6/42.18.2/18.39.22/20.30.30/5.1.29/18.31.23) (q:draft)
kihtak = (t:v) (w:fear/dread/be afraid of) (d:form of kihta, fear, used before nouns and endings: na kihtak mite are the people you fear, and kihtak-huai is fearsome or awesome) (e:Kuamah ~ nei loin nuam takin/kei nong ~ nading om lo a | there is no reason for you to fear me/note’ ~ Izipt natnate | the diseases of Egypt that you dreaded/na ~ mite’ khut sungah | into the hands of those you fear/Ka ~ hong kikonate heikhia in | take away the disgrace I dread) (b:kihta) (r:18.11.19/18.33.7/5.28.60/24.39.17/19.119.39) (q:draft)
kihtakhuai = (t:adj) (w:awesome/fearful/dreadful/terrible) (d:causing fear or awe, from kihtak, fear, with huai, worthy of; said of God, of darkness, wild beasts and judgments) (e:A heh ciangin ~ mahmah a/a lian a ~ ahi Pasian | a great and awesome God/ama' tungah a ~ khuamial sahpi om hi | a thick and dreadful darkness came over him/Van panin ~ nate leh lim lianpite | fearful events and great signs from heaven) (s:lauhuai/mulkimhuai) (r:18.41.10/5.7.21/1.15.12/42.21.11) (q:draft)
kihtakhuaina = (t:n) (w:dreadfulness/terror) (d:kihtakhuai fearful with the noun suffix na: the fear one inspires in others) (e:Na ~ leh na kisaktheihna in) (b:kihtakhuai) (r:24.49.16) (q:draft)
kihtakhuaipen = (t:adj) (w:most terrible/most fearful/most ruthless) (d:kihtakhuai, fearful, with the superlative pen) (e:a ~ minam a galkapte) (b:kihtakhuai) (r:26.30.11) (q:draft)
kihtakhuaite = (t:adj) (w:fearsome/dreadful/dangerous) (d:kihtakhuai with the plural te, which belongs to the whole phrase: gamsa kihtakhuaite are fierce wild beasts) (e:a that dingin gamsa ~) (b:kihtakhuai) (r:26.14.15) (q:draft)
kihtakin = (t:v) (w:fearing/dreading/in fear of) (d:kihtak fear with the connective in; kihtakin nei is hold in dread) (e:hong kampau ding ~ ka nei) (b:kihtak) (r:18.31.34) (q:draft)
kihtakna = (t:n) (w:fear/dread/reverence) (d:kihtak, fear, with the noun suffix na: fear or dread of someone, also reverent fear of God; the one feared stands before the word) (e:~ leh launa tawh ka nungta uh hi/Midangte ~ in hong lunghimawhsak a | fear of others brings anxiety/note tungah amah ~ hong tung ding | dread of him will fall on you/Israel mite ~ tawh Moab mite a kidim hi | Moab was filled with dread of the Israelites/~ zahtakna lungsim tawh | with reverence and awe) (s:launa) (a:hanna) (b:kihtak) (r:25.3.47/45.3.18/20.29.25/18.13.11/4.22.3/58.12.28) (q:draft)
kihtaktak = (t:v) (w:dread/fear greatly) (d:kihtak with its last syllable repeated; a kihtaktak is the very thing that someone fears) (e:na ~ uh namsau in Izipt gamah/Ka ~ ka tungah hong tung a | what I feared has come upon me/Migilote tungah a ~ uh tung a | what the wicked dread comes upon them) (s:laulau) (b:kihtak) (r:24.42.16/20.10.24/18.3.25) (q:draft)
kihtakte = (t:n) (w:things feared/what one fears) (d:kihtak fear with the plural te: the things that someone is afraid of) (e:Amaute’ ~ kihta kei un la) (b:kihtak) (r:23.8.12) (q:draft)
kihtalua = (t:v) (w:be very afraid/be terrified) (d:kihta, fear, with lua, too much or exceedingly) (e:Hancingte in ~ uh ahih manin) (s:laulua) (b:kihta) (r:40.28.4) (q:draft)
kihtate = (t:n) (w:those who fear) (d:kihta, fear, with the plural te: the people who fear; Pasian a kihtate, those who fear God) (e:lakah Pasian a ~ aw) (s:laute/zahtakte) (b:kihta) (r:44.13.26) (q:draft)
kihtazaw = (t:v) (w:fear rather/fear more) (d:kihta, fear, with zaw, more or rather) (e:susia thei pa na ~ un) (b:kihta) (r:40.10.28) (q:draft)
kihtha = (t:v) (w:loathe/find repulsive) (d:feel disgust at something, here at food) (e:lim pen nangawn a ~ suak hi) (r:18.33.20) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihu = (t:v) (w:be protected/be defended/be rescued) (d:passive of hu, defend or shield; kihu tawm is defend oneself) (e:Lungkhamna a tuah loh nadingun midikte ~ a/Gensiatna pan nang hong ~ ding a | you will be protected from slander/na nuntakna hong ~ ding hi | your life will be spared/amahmah ~ tawm tahen | let him defend himself) (b:hu) (r:20.11.8/18.5.21/24.38.20/7.6.31) (q:draft)
kihuaina = (t:n) (w:impurity/uncleanness) (d:something disgusting or unclean, here impure motives; apparently kih, loathe, with huai and the noun suffix na) (e:zuauthu hilhna, ~, kheemna tawh) (s:kihhuaina) (r:52.2.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihual = (t:v) (w:be braided/be twisted) (d:be twisted together like the strands of a rope) (e:a ~ kham citak khainiang na bawl ding hi/khau banga a ~, kham citak khainiang nih | two chains of pure gold, braided like a rope/a ~ khainiangte | the braided chains) (s:kihuiheek/kiheek) (r:2.28.22/2.28.14) (q:draft)
kihual = (t:v) (w:unite/be knit together/embrace) (d:be bound up with one another, as hearts that are knit together or as righteousness and peace that embrace) (e:thumanna leh kilemna ~ ding uh hi/note tawh ka lungsim ~ khawm ding hi | my heart will be knit together with yours) (r:19.85.10/13.12.17) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihualsak = (t:v) (w:roll over/drive over) (d:with sak cause: make the wheel of a threshing cart roll round over the grain) (e:a ~ ciangin amah in) (r:23.28.28) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihuan = (t:v) (w:be cooked/be boiled) (d:passive of huan, to cook; before a noun it means cooked, as in a kihuan an, cooked food) (e:tau beel tawh a ~ ahih leh/sikbel dai sunga ~ an tawh biakna ahih leh | if it is an offering of food cooked in a pan/a sunga om sa ~ tawh i kibang hi | we are like the meat cooked in it/a ~ an khat peuhpeuh | any cooked food) (r:3.6.28/3.2.7/26.11.3/37.2.12) (q:draft)
kihuanna = (t:n) (w:cooking/being cooked) (d:kihuan be cooked with the noun suffix na; a kihuanna leibeel is the clay pot in which it was cooked) (e:a ~ leibeel kisukham ding hi) (b:kihuan) (r:3.6.28) (q:draft)
kihuansa = (t:adj) (w:boiled/cooked) (d:kihuan be cooked, with sa for a completed action; in Ezekiel 27:18 said of iron, apparently worked or wrought) (e:Siampipa in a ~ tuutal liang/a ~ sik, thaksiing leh thalsiingte | wrought iron, cassia and calamus) (s:huansa/minsa) (b:kihuan) (r:4.6.19/26.27.18) (q:draft)
kihuau = (t:v) (w:whisper/whisper together) (d:speak in a low voice to one another; in the verses always kihuau sim, whisper in secret) (e:Mite’ ~ simna tampi ka za a/innsung tawngah na ~ simnate uh | what you have whispered in the inner rooms) (s:kihuauhuau) (b:huau) (r:24.20.10/42.12.3) (q:draft)
kihuauhuau = (t:v) (w:whisper together/whisper among themselves) (d:huau whisper said twice, with ki one another) (e:keima thu ~ uh a) (s:kihuau) (r:19.41.7) (q:draft)
kihuauna = (t:n) (w:whispering) (d:kihuau whisper to one another, with the noun suffix na) (e:mi tampi’ ~ ka za hi/nasemte a ~ uh David in a muh ciangin | when David saw the servants whispering) (b:kihuau) (r:19.31.13/10.12.19) (q:draft)
kihubing = (t:v) (w:be stopped/be shut/be silenced) (d:of the mouth, be stopped up so that it cannot speak) (e:kamte ~ ding hi/zuauthu a gen kam khempeuh ~ ding hi | every mouth that speaks lies will be stopped) (r:19.63.11) (q:draft)
kihuh = (t:v) (w:be helped/help one another) (d:huh, help, with ki: passive, be helped, or with ciat or khat leh khat, help one another) (e:kei hong ~ a/a lamdangpi khatin ~ ahih manin | because he was wonderfully helped/~ nading ka nget nading kuamah om lo hi | there is no one I can ask for help/khatlekhat kihanthawnin na ~ ciat ta un | encourage and help one another) (b:huh) (r:19.28.7/14.26.15/18.6.13/52.5.11) (q:draft)
kihuhin = (t:v) (w:helping one another) (d:kihuh with the linking suffix in; after khat leh khat, helping each other) (e:khat leh khat ~ na pua un) (b:kihuh) (r:48.6.2) (q:draft)
kihuhna = (t:n) (w:help/aid/mutual help) (d:help that is given to someone, or helping one another) (e:tung panin eite hong ~ hong pai hi/Nang hong ~ lum, leh na gualzawhna namsau | your shield of help and your sword of victory/Khatlekhat ~ tawh na ki-itna uh kilangsak un | show your love by helping one another/ka mipihte a ~ sumte | money to help my people) (b:huhna) (r:19.124.8/49.4.2/5.33.29/44.24.17) (q:draft)
kihuhsak = (t:v) (w:let help/have helped) (d:kihuh, be helped, with the causative sak: let someone be helped by another) (e:Amaute thosakin note ~ unla) (b:kihuh) (r:5.32.38) (q:draft)
kihuhzaw = (t:v) (w:help one another rather/help one another more) (d:kihuh with zaw, more or rather; after khatlekhat, help each other) (e:khatlekhat kihanthawnin na ~ un) (b:kihuh) (r:58.3.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
