kikhak = (t:v) (w:be shut/be closed/be locked) (d:khak, shut, with the passive ki: of a door, a gate or an opening, be shut) (e:Sun lai takin kongkhak ~ ngei lo hi/tui thukte leh vantung kongvangneute ~ a | the deep springs and the windows of heaven were closed/Negeb gam khua kongpite lah ~ a | the gates of the towns of the Negev are shut/Tu-in kong ~ zo hi | the door is already shut/a delhte a paikhiat phetin kulh kongpi ~ hi | as soon as the pursuers had gone out the gate was shut) (s:kikalh/kikhakcip) (a:kihon/kihong) (r:66.21.25/1.8.2/24.13.19/42.11.7/6.2.7) (q:draft)
