kikhatsak = (t:v) (w:unite/make one) (d:kikhat, be one, with the causative sak: make the mind, purpose or way of life one and the same) (e:na ngimna uh na ~ nadingun/a nuntak dan uh zong ka ~ ding hi | I will also make their way of life one) (s:kipawlsak) (a:kikhensak) (b:kikhat) (r:46.1.10/24.32.39) (q:draft)
kikhawh = (t:v) (w:be thrust at/be speared) (d:passive of khawh, thrust or hurl a spear) (e:teipi tawh a ~ ciangin) (b:khawh) (r:18.41.29) (q:draft, low confidence)
kikhawh = (t:v) (w:dart/flash) (d:shoot about like flames, of chariots) (e:Meikuang bangin ~ uh a) (r:34.2.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
kikhawhkhia = (t:v) (w:rush out/pour out/flee away) (d:of water, rush or drain away from its place) (e:panin tui a ~ bangin/awging a zak uh ciangin ~ uh hi | at the sound they took to flight) (b:kikhawh) (r:34.2.8/19.104.7) (q:draft)
kikhawhsak = (t:v) (w:be farmed for/be cultivated for) (d:of land, be worked for someone; a kikhawhsak mite, those for whom it is farmed) (e:a ~ mite a dingin) (r:58.6.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
kikhawi = (t:v) (w:be kept/be reared/be bred) (d:khawi, keep and look after an animal, with the prefix ki: of horses kept in the royal stable) (e:kumpi sakol bukah a ~ kumpipa’ sakolte) (b:khawi) (r:17.8.10) (q:draft)
kikhawl = (t:v) (w:accompany/keep company with/associate with) (d:be in the company of someone and go about with them; the companion is marked by tawh, with) (e:amaute tawh ~ kei in/Mipil tawh ~ lecin na pil ding a | if you keep company with the wise you will be wise/mihai tawh ~ lecin gimna na thuak ding hi | if you keep company with fools you will suffer harm/Mi gualnuam mawkmawkte tawh ka ~ kei a | I did not keep company with revelers) (s:kikholh/kipawl) (b:khawl) (r:20.24.1/20.13.20/24.15.17)
kikhawl = (t:n) (w:companion) (d:one who keeps company with another; a kikhawl mi is a companion of the person or group named with tawh) (e:a kipawl, a ~ ta ka hi hi/lawm gina lo tawh a ~ mi | a companion of worthless friends/numei paktat tawh a ~ mi in | a companion of prostitutes) (s:kikhawlpa/kikholhpih/lawm) (b:khawl) (r:18.30.29/20.28.7/20.29.3)
kikhawla = (t:v) (w:keeping company/associating) (d:kikhawl, accompany, with the linking a: going about with someone and then doing something) (e:numei gilote tawh ~ na sum) (b:kikhawl) (r:42.15.30) (q:draft)
kikhawlin = (t:v) (w:keeping company/being together/associating) (d:kikhawl with the linking ending in: being together with, tawh marks the companion) (e:Thu um khempeuh ~ omkhawm uh a/mizawngte tawh ~ mi neu-a om hoihzaw hi | it is better to be lowly in the company of the poor/Humpinelkai dangte tawh ~, a note khoi hi | living among the other lions she reared her cubs/mawhneite tawh ~ an nangawn nekhawm hi | he keeps company with sinners and even eats with them) (s:kipawlin) (b:kikhawl) (r:44.2.44/20.16.19/26.19.2/42.15.2) (q:draft)
kikhawlpa = (t:n) (w:friend/companion) (d:kikhawl, keep company, with pa marking a man: a man who keeps company with someone, used with tawh) (e:nangmah a hong zahtakte tawh a ~ ka hi hi/a kikholhpih nop loh mite tawh a ~ | a friend of people others will not associate with/vantungmi le i pute tawh a ~ ahi hi | he was the one who was with the angel and our ancestors) (s:lawmpa/kikholhpihpa) (b:kikhawl) (r:19.119.63/42.7.34/44.7.38) (q:draft)
kikhawlpih = (t:n) (w:companion/friend) (d:kikhawl, keep company, with pih, together with: a person one keeps company with) (s:kikhawlpa/kikholhpih/lawm)
kikhawlsak = (t:v) (w:be stopped/be detained/be made to cease) (d:khawlsak, make stop, with the passive prefix ki: be stopped, or be kept back in a place) (e:vantung pan-a guahte ~ hi/Topa mai-ah a ~, Saul’ nasemte mi khat | one of the servants of Saul, detained before the Lord/a nasep ~ lo ding hi | her work will not be stopped) (s:kitawpsak/kikhaktan) (b:khawlsak) (r:1.8.2/9.21.7/42.10.42) (q:draft)
kikhawlsak = (t:v) (w:make keep company with/seat with/let associate with) (d:kikhawl, keep company, with the causative sak: let or make someone be in the company of the people named with tawh) (e:a gilo mite tawh hong ~ kei in/uliante tawh ~ a | he seats them with princes) (b:kikhawl) (r:19.141.4/19.113.8) (q:draft)
kikhawlte = (t:n) (w:companions/partners/associates) (d:kikhawl, keep company, with the plural te: those who keep company with the person or group named with tawh) (e:gutate tawh a ~ ahi hi/Hih pa zong Jesuh tawh a ~ khat hi | this man too is one of those who were with Jesus) (s:kikholhpihte/lawmte) (b:kikhawl) (r:23.1.23/42.22.56) (q:draft)
kikhawlthei = (t:v) (w:be able to associate/be willing to associate) (d:kikhawl, keep company, with thei, can) (e:mineute tawh ~ unla) (s:kipawlthei) (b:kikhawl) (r:45.12.16) (q:draft)
kikhawm = (t:n) (w:gather/assemble/come together) (d:come together in one place, of people, animals or water) (e:kongkhak kiangah a ~ uh hi/musanete hong ~ ding uh hi | the vultures will gather/tuite mun khatah ~ hen la | let the waters be gathered in one place/mihonpite khatvei a ~ kik uh hi | the crowd gathered once again) (r:41.1.33/1.1.9/40.24.28/41.3.20)
kikhawm = (t:n) (w:group) (s:pawl)
kikhawm = (t:v) (w:attend church/gather for worship) (d:to go church) (e:thu ngai dingin khuazang dektak a ~ uh hi | almost the whole town gathered to hear the word) (r:44.13.44)
kikhawmin = (t:v) (w:gather/assemble/come together) (d:kikhawm with the linking ending -in: gathering, having assembled) (e:Israel upate ~ Ramah-a Samuel kiangah/Israel mite ~ Elah kuam-ah giahphual sat uh a | the Israelites assembled and camped in the Valley of Elah/mi tampi ~ a om uh a mu hi | he found many people gathered/nitak an nekna lianpi-ah ~ hong pai un | come and gather for the great supper) (b:kikhawm) (r:9.8.4/9.17.2/44.10.27/66.19.17) (q:draft)
kikhawmkik = (t:v) (w:gather again/assemble again) (d:kikhawm, gather, with kik, again) (e:mihon tampi hong ~ uh a/ama kiangah mihonpi hong ~ zel ahih manin | because the crowd kept gathering to him again) (b:kikhawm) (r:41.10.1/41.3.20) (q:draft)
kikhawmsak = (t:v) (w:gather/assemble/call together) (d:kikhawm, gather, with the causative sak: make people come together, call them together) (e:galkap khempeuh a ~ uh hi/Mite nangma kim-ah ~ in la | gather the peoples around you/Armageddon a kici munah a ~ uh hi | they gathered them at the place called Armageddon/Farisaite in upa vaihawmte ~ uh a | the Pharisees called the council together) (s:kikhopsak/kaikhawmsak) (a:kikhenthangsak) (b:kikhawm) (r:41.15.16/19.7.7/66.16.16/43.11.47) (q:draft)
kikhawmsakin = (t:v) (w:gathering/being gathered) (d:kikhawmsak, gather, with the linking suffix in) (e:mi namkim ~ gancingpa in) (b:kikhawmsak) (r:40.25.32) (q:draft)
kikhawmte = (t:n) (w:assembly/those gathered/congregation) (d:the people who have come together, kikhawm with plural te) (e:mi ~ a paikhia sak hi/David in a ~ khempeuh tungah | David, to all who were gathered/Israel a ~ khempeuh thupha pia-in | blessing the whole assembly of Israel/Israel mihon ~ khempeuh’ mai-ah | before the whole assembled community of Israel) (b:kikhawm) (r:44.19.41/13.29.20/11.8.55/4.14.5) (q:draft)
kikhawmtuah = (t:v) (w:gather together/assemble/unite) (d:come together in one place or as one group, also to join against someone) (e:ka paang a beng dingin hong ~ uh hi/khe khat khai bangin hong ~ diam hi | they came together as one man) (s:kisutuah) (a:kikhenthang) (r:18.16.10/16.8.1) (q:draft)
kikhawng = (t:v) (w:fetch/be sold for) (d:khawng, ask a price, with the prefix ki: of goods, bring a certain price when sold) (e:sum tampi tak ~ ding a/Kizuak le ngun peek zathum val ~ ding a | if sold it would fetch more than three hundred silver coins) (b:khawng) (r:40.26.9/41.14.5) (q:draft)
kikheek = (t:v) (w:exchange places/change with each other) (d:kheek, exchange, with ki, each other) (e:Note leh kei ~ thei hi lehang) (s:kikhek) (b:kheek) (r:18.16.4) (q:draft)
kikheel = (t:v) (w:change/be changed) (d:kheel, change, with the prefix ki: become different or be changed; kikheel ngei lo is never changing) (e:Thukham zong ~ loin a om thei/mi tuamdang khatin na ~ ding hi | you will be changed into a different person/Amaute puan bangin a ~ ding uh hi | they will be changed like a garment/mitphiat kikalin eite khempeuh i ~ ding hi | in the twinkling of an eye we will all be changed) (s:kikhel/kilamdang) (b:kheel) (r:58.7.12/40.18.3/9.10.6/58.1.12/46.15.52) (q:draft)
kikheela = (t:v) (w:turning/changing) (d:kikheel, change, with the linking a: turning and so being forgiven) (e:~ amau mawhna uh a kimaisak loh nadingin) (b:kikheel) (r:41.4.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
kikheelin = (t:v) (w:changing/turning/repenting) (d:kikheel, change, with the linking suffix in: of a change of mind or a turning from wrong ways, followed by what happens next) (e:a lungsim ~ a kuankik hi/Note ~ naupang na bat kei uhleh | unless you change and become like children/i gitlohna panin ~ thupha a hong piaktheih nadingin | so that he could bless us as we turn from our wickedness/amah ~ a nuntak theih nadingin | so that he may change and live) (b:kikheel) (r:40.21.29/40.18.3/44.3.26/26.3.18) (q:draft)
kikheelsak = (t:v) (w:change/transform) (d:kheelsak, make something change, with the prefix ki; of customs changed and of the body transformed) (e:ngeina a ~ ding hi/a suahsak nadingin hong ~ ding hi | he will transform us to make it so) (b:kheelsak) (r:44.6.14/50.3.21) (q:draft)
kikheelsakin = (t:v) (w:turning/making change) (d:kikheelsak with the linking suffix in: making someone turn from wrong ways) (e:na khialhna uh pan hong ~) (b:kikheelsak) (r:44.3.26) (q:draft)
kikheem = (t:v) (w:be deceived/deceive oneself) (d:kheem, deceive, with the prefix ki: be deceived, or deceive oneself) (e:Na ~ kei un/eimah mah ~ i hi a | we deceive ourselves/amau mahmah zong a ~ ding uh hi | they themselves too will be deceived/tua mi in a ~ suak a | that person ends up deceiving himself) (s:kikhemtawm) (b:kheem) (r:46.15.33/62.1.8/55.3.13/59.1.26) (q:draft)
kikheemin = (t:v) (w:deceiving oneself) (d:kikheem, deceive oneself, with the linking suffix in) (e:pumpi uh ~ thungaite bek hi kei un) (b:kikheem) (r:59.1.22) (q:draft)
kikheemna = (t:n) (w:deception) (d:kikheem, deceive, with the noun suffix na: the deceiving of people) (e:~ zang loin) (s:kheemna/khemna) (b:kikheem) (r:47.4.2)
Kikheemna = (t:n) (w:deception) (d:kikheemna written with a capital at the start of a sentence) (e:~ zang loin Pasian’ thu im loin) (s:kheemna/khemna) (b:kikheemna) (r:47.4.2) (q:draft)
kikheen = (t:v) (w:be driven in/be fastened) (d:of a peg, be driven into a firm place) (e:a ~ vankhai in lel ding hi) (r:23.22.25) (q:draft, low confidence)
kikhek = (t:v) (w:be exchanged/change places) (d:khek, exchange, with the prefix ki: be exchanged for another thing, or of two parties, be in each other's place) (e:adang tawh zong ~ thei lo/Note le keimah a ~ thei hi lehang | if you and I could change places) (s:kilaih/kikheek) (b:khek) (r:26.48.14/18.16.4) (q:draft)
kikhekna = (t:n) (w:exchange/transfer) (d:kikhek, be exchanged, with the noun suffix na: the exchanging or handing over of property) (e:tatna leh ~ thu-ah ngeina) (s:khekna/kheekna) (b:kikhek) (r:8.4.7) (q:draft)
kikhel = (t:v) (w:change/be changed/be altered) (d:khel, change, with the prefix ki: become different or be altered, or change one’s own ways; kikhel thei lo is unchangeable) (e:na gamtatnate uh ~ un/thupiakna ~ kik thei lo hi | the decree cannot be changed again/~ kikin a kaang a suah leh | if it changes again and turns white/a gimnam zong ~ ngei lo hi | its aroma too has never changed) (s:kikheel/kilamdang) (b:khel) (r:24.7.3/27.6.15/3.13.16/24.48.11) (q:draft)
kikhelgawp = (t:v) (w:be greatly changed/be altered) (d:kikhel, change, with gawp, violently or thoroughly; of the face, lose its colour and look) (e:ka mel ~ ahih manin) (b:kikhel) (r:27.10.8) (q:draft)
kikhelin = (t:v) (w:changing/turning from one's ways) (d:kikhel change with the linking suffix in) (e:amah ~ a nuntak theihna dingin) (b:kikhel) (r:26.3.18) (q:draft)
kikhelin = (t:adv) (w:in turns/in shifts/by rotation) (d:taking each other's place in turn) (e:kha khatin tul sawm a ~ puak) (b:kikhel) (r:11.5.14) (q:draft)
kikhelkhel = (t:v) (w:be changed) (d:doubled form of kikhel, change) (e:tua nate khempeuh ~ ding uh hi) (r:58.1.12) (q:draft)
kikhelkik = (t:v) (w:be changed/be revoked/turn back) (d:kikhel, change, with kik, back or again: of a decree or a word, be altered or revoked; of people, turn from their ways) (e:a hawmkhiatsa thupiakna ~ thei lo hi/amau’ gamtatnasa panin ~ nuam lo uh hi | they would not turn back from what they had done/a ~ ngei nawn lo ding thukip | a firm word that will never be revoked) (b:kikhel) (r:27.6.15/66.9.20/23.45.23) (q:draft)
kikhelna = (t:n) (w:change/changing) (d:kikhel, change, with the noun suffix na) (e:Sang Penpa khut taklam a ~ in) (b:kikhel) (r:19.77.10) (q:draft)
kikhelpak = (t:v) (w:be changed in a moment/be changed quickly) (d:kikhel, change, with pak, for a moment or quickly) (e:mitphiat kikal sungin i ~ ding hi) (s:kikhelvat) (r:46.15.52) (q:draft)
kikhelsak = (t:v) (w:turn/make change) (d:kikhel, change one's ways, with the causative sak: make someone turn away from a way of life or conduct) (e:panin zong ~ khinzo ding uh hi) (b:kikhel) (r:24.23.22) (q:draft)
kikhelsakin = (t:v) (w:turning/making change) (d:kikhelsak with the linking suffix in: making someone turn from a way of life) (e:a hoih lote panin ~) (b:kikhelsak) (r:24.23.22) (q:draft)
kikhelvat = (t:v) (w:be changed suddenly) (d:kikhel, change, with vat, all at once) (e:thakhatthu-in a ~ ding ihi hi) (s:kikhelpak) (r:46.15.51) (q:draft)
kikhem = (t:v) (w:deceive each other/cheat each other/take advantage of each other/be deceived) (d:khem, deceive, with the prefix ki: deceive or cheat one another, or be deceived) (e:khat leh khat na ~ kei ding uh a/khat leh khat ~ loin | without cheating one another/a ~ tuak ding uh hi | they will deceive each other/na khem nawn loh ciangin nang hong ~ ding hi | when you stop betraying you will be betrayed) (b:khem) (r:3.19.11/3.25.17/27.11.27/23.33.1) (q:draft)
kikhemgawp = (t:v) (w:be cheated/be oppressed) (d:be badly deceived or wronged, of foreigners; khem, deceive, with ki and gawp, violently or thoroughly) (e:Pemtate ~ a) (b:kikhem) (r:26.22.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
kikhemin = (t:v) (w:be deceived/be enticed/deceive oneself) (d:kikhem with the linking ending in, joining it to the next verb; nang leh nang kikhemin, deceiving yourself) (e:Nang leh nang ~/Na lungsim uh hong ~ | your hearts being enticed/Kamsang khatpeuh peuh ~ | any prophet, being enticed) (b:kikhem) (r:24.37.9/5.11.16/26.14.9) (q:draft)
kikhemnate = (t:n) (w:deceits/frauds/lies) (d:kikhem, deceive each other, with the noun suffix na and the plural te) (e:kisukcipna le ~ veng lo hi) (b:kikhem) (r:19.55.11) (q:draft)
kikhemtawm = (t:v) (w:deceive oneself) (d:khem, deceive, with ki and tawm, do to oneself) (e:amahmah a ~ hi lel a) (s:kikheem) (r:59.1.26) (q:draft)
kikhemzo = (t:v) (w:can be deceived/can be fooled) (d:khem, deceive, with the passive ki and zo, be able) (e:Pasian a ~ dingin ngaihsunkha kei un) (b:kikhem) (r:48.6.7) (q:draft)
kikhen = (t:adj) (w:divided/separated/parted) (d:khen, divide, with the prefix ki: divided or separated from one another) (e:Gamkhat sung mi kilem loin a ~ leh/ama’ hunin leitung ~ hi | in his time the earth was divided/Ami kilem lo a ~ inn sung | a household divided and not at peace/na gam ~ kham a | your kingdom is divided) (s:kikhensak) (b:khen) (r:41.3.24/1.10.25/41.3.25/27.5.28)
kikhenin = (t:v) (w:divided into/separating/being apart) (d:kikhen, be divided, with the linking suffix in: dividing or being apart, followed by what comes of it) (e:gun hong ~ lii hong pha hi/meikuang tawh kibang leiite ~ | tongues like flames of fire separating/Satan le Satan ~ kido le-uh | if Satan is divided and fights against Satan/kulh tungah ~ khat leh khat i kigamla hi | spread out along the wall we are far from each other) (b:kikhen) (r:1.2.10/44.2.3/41.3.26/16.4.19)
kikhenin = (t:v) (w:into parts) (d:kikhen with the linking suffix in, of a hoof that is split into two parts) (e:a khecin ~ a khecin nih-in a ka) (b:kikhen) (r:5.14.6)
kikhenkhia = (t:v) (w:be cut off/be separated/be alienated) (d:khenkhia, separate off, with the passive prefix ki: be cut off or separated from one’s people, from God or from an inheritance) (e:ama mite kiang panin ~ ding hi/Nidang lai-inah Pasian tawh ~-in | once you were alienated from God/tua mipa ~ siang ding hi | that man must be completely cut off/luahna panin amau’ aa ~ ding hi | their property will be taken from the inheritance) (b:khenkhia) (r:1.17.14/51.1.21/4.15.31/4.36.4) (q:draft)
kikhenlawh = (t:v) (w:part company/separate) (d:kikhen, separate, with lawh, as a result of something, here of a quarrel) (e:kinial uh ahih manin ~ uh a) (r:44.15.39) (q:draft)
kikhenna = (t:n) (w:division/separation/dissension) (d:kikhen, be divided, with the noun suffix na: a parting or split between people or within a group) (e:pawlpi sungah ~ a om ding hi/~ leh pukna a bawl thei mite | those who cause divisions and stumbling/note lakah pawl ~ om hi | there are divisions among you/hehna, huaihamna, ~, pawltuam lungsim neihna | rage, selfish ambition, dissension, factions) (s:khenna) (a:kikhatna) (b:kikhen) (r:46.11.19/45.16.17/46.11.18/48.5.20) (q:draft)
kikhenna = (t:n) (w:divorce) (d:separation of husband and wife; kikhenna lai is a certificate of divorce) (e:~ lai pia-in zi mak nading | to divorce a wife by giving a certificate of divorce/~ lai pia-in, a zi ma hen | let him give a certificate of divorce and divorce his wife/~ lai pia ta hen | let him give a certificate of divorce) (s:kimakna/makna/kimaakna) (b:kikhen) (r:41.10.4/40.19.7/40.5.31) (q:draft)
Kikhenna = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Kikhenna/Sela Hammahlekoth) (d:place in the Desert of Maon where Saul broke off his pursuit of David, called Kikhenna Mual, Hill of Parting) (r:9.23.28)
kikhennate = (t:n) (w:divisions/groups) (d:plural of kikhenna: the groups into which the priests were divided for their service) (e:siampite a pawlpawlin a ~) (s:khennate/khente) (b:kikhenna) (r:14.8.14) (q:draft)
kikhensa = (t:adj) (w:divorced/separated) (d:kikhen, separate, with sa, already done; pasal tawh a kikhensa numei, a woman divorced from her husband) (e:Pasal tawh a ~ numei) (b:kikhen) (r:42.16.18) (q:draft)
kikhensak = (t:v) (w:separated/separate/divide) (d:kikhen, be separated, with the causative sak: make things or people separate from each other) (e:mite in ~ kei uh hen/tua van kuumpi in tui leh tui ~ hen | let that vault separate water from water/Ka tate tawh kei nong ~ zo uh hi | you have separated me from my children/mi khempeuh a tuam tuakin hong ~ ding hi | he will separate all people one from another) (a:kikhatsak/kigawmsak) (b:kikhen) (r:1.1.6/41.10.9/1.42.36/40.25.32)
kikhensak = (t:adj) (w:divided) (s:kikhen) (b:kikhen)
kikhensakin = (t:v) (w:dividing/parting) (d:kikhensak, make separate, with the linking suffix in) (e:Amah in tuipi ~ amaute kantansak a) (b:kikhensak) (r:19.78.13) (q:draft)
kikhensakzo = (t:v) (w:be able to separate/separate) (d:kikhensak, separate, with zo, be able) (e:tawh hong ~ het lo ding hi/bangin Khrih’ itna tawh hong ~ ding ahi hiam | what can separate us from the love of Christ) (b:kikhensak) (r:45.8.38/45.8.35) (q:draft)
kikhenta = (t:v) (w:be weaned/be separated) (d:kikhen, be separated, with ta marking a change that has taken place; nawi tawh kikhenta, parted from the breast, is weaned) (e:nawi tawh a ~ naupang bangin) (b:kikhen) (r:19.131.2) (q:draft)
kikhentan = (t:v) (w:be cut off/be parted/be divided) (d:of flowing water, be stopped and separated) (e:Jordan a galkah ciangin Jordan tuite ~ hi/thuciamna singkuang mai-ah Jordan tuite ~ hi | the waters of the Jordan were cut off before the ark of the covenant) (s:kikhentat) (r:6.4.7) (q:draft)
kikhentat = (t:v) (w:be cut off) (d:of flowing water, be parted and cut off completely) (e:a luangsukte ~ siang hi) (s:kikhentan) (r:6.3.16) (q:draft)
kikhentel = (t:v) (w:be discerned/be distinguished/be told apart) (d:khentel, tell apart, with the passive prefix ki: be discerned or distinguished) (e:Kha Siangtho bek tawh ~ thei/a hoih leh a hoih lo lam a ~ | the good and the bad are told apart) (b:khentel) (r:46.2.14/27.12.10) (q:draft)
kikhenthang = (t:v) (w:be scattered/be divided/split up) (d:separate from one another, of people dispersing or forming factions) (e:kithutuak loin a ~ kik uh hi/na omna ciat uhah na ~ ding uh a | you will be scattered, each to his own place/Izipt gam khempeuhah mite ~ uh hi | the people scattered all over Egypt/amah hangin thu kituak loin a ~ uh hi | they were divided because of him) (s:kithehthang) (a:kikhawmtuah/kikhat) (b:khenthang) (r:43.10.19/42.1.51/43.16.32/2.5.12/43.7.43) (q:draft)
kikhenthangsak = (t:v) (w:scatter) (d:kikhenthang, be scattered, with the causative sak) (e:a ~ gam ukte in) (s:thehthang) (a:kikhawmsak) (b:kikhenthang) (r:24.23.1) (q:draft)
kikhenthangte = (t:n) (w:scattered people/exiles/outcasts) (d:kikhenthang, be scattered, with plural te: those who have been scattered) (e:Israel a ~ a kaikhawm Topa Pasian in/Judah mi a ~ kaikhawm ding hi | he will gather the scattered people of Judah) (s:kihawlkhiate) (b:kikhenthang) (r:23.56.8/23.11.12) (q:draft)
kikhentung = (t:v) (w:be newly weaned/be just separated) (d:kikhen, be separated, with tung, just now; nawi tawh a kikhentung, just weaned from the breast) (e:nawi tawh a ~ naungeekte) (r:23.28.9) (q:draft)
kikhep = (t:v) (w:be folded/fold) (d:be folded over double, of cloth; also of the leaves of a folding door) (e:a ~ ciangin a dung khap khat/a dang kongkhak a pek nihte zong ~ hi | the two leaves of the other door also folded) (b:khep) (r:2.39.9/11.6.34) (q:draft)
kikhepin = (t:v) (w:fold/be folded) (d:kikhep with the linking ending in; of the two leaves of a folding door) (e:kongkhak a pek nihte ~) (b:kikhep) (r:11.6.34) (q:draft)
kikhia = (t:v) (w:be thrown/be cast/be put) (d:be thrown or dropped down into a place such as a pit, the sea or a prison) (e:khihin tuipi sungah ~ leh/Johan thong sungah ~ nai lo hi | John had not yet been put in prison/humpinelkai koihna khuk sungah ~ ding hi | he shall be thrown into the lions’ den/Kote hong kisatin, thongah hong ~-in | we were beaten and thrown into prison) (s:kilawn/kipaai) (r:41.9.42/43.3.24/27.6.7/47.6.5) (q:draft)
kikhia = (t:v) (w:accuse each other/be accused/go to law) (d:bring a charge against one another or hand one another over, or be charged, before a judge or master) (e:thu-um lote mai-ah na ~ tazen uh hi/a topa’ sumteng phengzat gawp hi, ci-in ~ hi | he was accused of wasting the money of his master/Unau khatlekhat a sih nadingun ~ ding uh a | brothers will hand each other over to death/Thukhen zumah ~ nu’ng | let us face each other in court) (r:46.6.6/42.16.1/41.13.12/23.50.8) (q:draft)
kikhial = (t:v) (w:be a mistake/be done in error/err) (d:khial, be wrong, with the prefix ki: something is done wrongly without intending it) (e:a ~ hi kha ding hi/mi honte’ phawk lohin a ~ ahih leh | if it is done in error without the community knowing) (b:khial) (r:1.43.12/4.15.24) (q:draft)
kikhiam = (t:v) (w:be reduced/be lessened/be diminished) (d:khiam, reduce, with the passive prefix ki: be made less) (e:nangma sehna zah panin ~ ding hi/them khat zong hong ~ lo ding hi | it will not be reduced even a little) (a:kibehlap) (b:khiam) (r:3.27.18/2.5.11) (q:draft)
kikhiamin = (t:v) (w:be diminished/decrease/be brought low) (d:kikhiam, be reduced, with the linking ending in: of a people, becoming fewer and weaker) (e:dahna tawh ~ a kiniamkoih ciangin) (b:kikhiam) (r:19.107.39) (q:draft)
kikhiasuk = (t:v) (w:be thrown down/be hurled down/be cast down) (d:khiasuk, throw down, with the passive ki: be thrown or hurled down into a place, as the earth, the sea, a pit or darkness) (e:leitungah a ~ hi/khuamialna sungah ~ ding hi | they will be thrown down into darkness/tuipi thuk sungah ~ le | if he were thrown into the deep sea/leihawm sungah amaute khempeuh ~ a | they are all thrown into pits/Leitungah a ~ zo hi cih | that he had been thrown down to the earth) (s:kilawnsuk) (b:khiasuk) (r:66.12.9/9.2.9/40.18.6/23.42.22/66.12.13) (q:draft)
kikhiat = (t:v) (w:be thrown/be cast/be put) (d:khiat, throw, with the passive ki: be thrown or put into a place such as a prison, a pit or hell; the form used before sangin, khit and lam) (e:Thong sungah Johan a ~ khit ciangin/hell sungah hong ~ sangin | than to be thrown into hell/tuikhuk sungah Jeremiah a ~ lam | that Jeremiah had been put into the cistern/khut kim khe kimin hong ~ sangin | than to be thrown in with both hands and both feet) (b:khiat) (r:41.1.14/41.9.45/24.38.7/40.18.8) (q:draft)
kikhiatlam = (t:v) (w:be thrown/be put) (d:kikhiat, be thrown into a place, with lam, the fact that: that someone has been thrown in) (e:kei hong ~ a za hi) (r:24.38.7) (q:draft)
kikhiatna = (t:n) (w:being thrown/being cast) (d:kikhiat, be thrown, with the noun suffix na; kikhiatna thuak, suffer being thrown in) (e:a hing tangin ~ a thuak uh hi) (b:kikhiat) (r:66.19.20) (q:draft)
kikhih = (t:v) (w:be bound/be tied/bind oneself) (d:khih, tie, with ki, passive or reflexive: be tied with ropes, be bound to a person, or bind oneself; kikhih tawmna is a pledge by which a person binds himself or herself) (e:khauhual tawh nang hong ~ ding a/a pasal tawh a ~ khawm hi | she is bound to her husband/amah a ~ tawmna kamciamnate | the pledges by which she bound herself/kam ciamin amah a ~ tawmna | binding herself by a spoken oath) (s:kihen) (a:kikhah/kiphel) (b:khih) (r:26.3.25/4.30.10/45.7.2/4.30.5) (q:draft)
kikhiha = (t:v) (w:bound/tied) (d:kikhih, be bound, with the linking a; kikhiha om, be in bonds) (e:~ a om vantungmi lite khah un) (b:kikhih) (r:66.9.14) (q:draft)
kikhihin = (t:v) (w:be tied/be tethered/be fastened) (d:kikhih with the linking ending in: being tied, having something tied on) (e:suang lianpi khat ~ tuipi sungah/bangmah om lo, ahih hangin sakolte ~ | nothing was there, only the horses tethered/a khut nih tuakin sikkhau ~ | both his hands bound with chains/ngun kualte ah ~ a kikhai | fastened to silver rings and hung) (s:kihenin) (b:kikhih) (r:41.9.42/12.7.10/44.12.6/17.1.6) (q:draft)
kikhihkhawm = (t:v) (w:be tied together/be tied to) (d:kikhih, be tied, with khawm, together) (e:teembaw tawh a ~ gunkuang) (b:kikhih) (r:44.27.16) (q:draft)
kikhihna = (t:n) (w:bonds/chains/imprisonment) (d:the state of being bound or tied, or that which binds) (e:Kei’ thuak ~ na ngaihsun un/Lungdamna Thu hangin ~ ka thuak lai takin | while I am in chains for the gospel/mawhna ~ na thuak hi | you are held captive by sin/a ~ phel thei na hi hiam | can you loosen its bonds) (s:kihenna) (a:suahtakna) (r:51.4.18/44.8.23/57.1.13/18.38.31) (q:draft)
kikhihnate = (t:n) (w:bonds/bindings/chains) (d:kikhihna with plural te: the things by which someone is bound) (e:amah a ~ a khut panin tolhkhia hi/Keimah hong ~ nong sutkhiatsak zo hi | you have loosed my bonds) (s:kihennate/hennate) (b:kikhihna) (r:7.15.14/19.116.16) (q:draft)
kikhihsa = (t:adj) (w:tied/bound/tied up) (d:kikhih, be tied, with sa, already: tied up or bound, of an animal on a rope or a prisoner) (e:lano khat ~ a muh uh ciangin/Jesuh a ~ mahin siampi lianpen pa Kaiafas kiangah | Jesus, still bound, to Caiaphas the high priest/khau ~ a, om lano khat | a colt that is tied up) (s:khihsa) (b:kikhih) (r:41.11.4/43.18.24/42.19.30) (q:draft)
kikhihtawm = (t:v) (w:bind oneself/obligate oneself) (d:khih, bind, with ki and tawm, do to oneself; of binding oneself by a pledge) (e:kamciamna tawh amah ~ a) (r:4.30.3) (q:draft)
kikhim = (t:v) (w:be charmed) (d:of a snake, be brought under control by a charmer; a kikhim zo lo, that cannot be charmed) (e:A ~ zo lo gul guneite) (r:24.8.17) (q:draft, low confidence)
kikhin = (t:v) (w:move/be moved/be removed/shift) (d:move or be moved from its place; kikhin kawikawi, move about here and there) (e:mual neute a ~ zongin/Pasian’ deihna zui-in ~ kawikawi hi | they move about here and there at God’s direction/mualte ~ khia ding sa na hi hiam | do you think the rocks should be moved away/a ~ thei lo puanbuk | a tent that cannot be moved/ka ~ theih loh nadingin | so that I will not be shaken) (r:23.54.10/18.37.12/18.18.4/23.33.20/44.2.25) (q:draft)
kikhinin = (t:v) (w:move/shift/withdraw) (d:move from one place to another, form with the linking suffix -in) (e:meii khuam ~ amaute’ nungah ding a/A mual kimkhat leilu lamah ~ | half of the mountain moving northward/Tua ahih ciangin, leitung ~ | therefore, though the earth gives way) (b:kikhin) (r:2.14.19/38.14.4/19.46.2) (q:draft)
kikhit = (t:v) (w:be finished/be completed/be over) (d:khit, finish, with the passive ki: come to an end, be completed) (e:tua thu a ~ matengin/a pawi bawl uh vial khat a ~ ciangin | when a round of their feasting was over) (b:khit) (r:42.12.50/18.1.5) (q:draft)
kikho = (t:v) (w:be plowed/be tilled/be cultivated) (d:kho, till, with the passive ki: of land, be plowed or dug for sowing) (e:lo khawh bangin Zion ~-in/a ~ nai lo, khaici a kivawh nai lo | not yet plowed and not yet sown/tu-peek tawh a ~ ngei mual neute-ah | on the hills once tilled with the hoe/Lo dingin Zion mual a ~ ding hi | Mount Zion will be plowed as a field) (b:kho) (r:33.3.12/26.36.9/5.21.4/23.7.25/24.26.18) (q:draft)
kikho = (t:v) (w:be restrained/be held back) (d:be stopped from doing something) (e:piak ding uh mite ~ hi/Tua bang numei ~ thei lo a | such a woman cannot be restrained) (r:2.36.6/20.27.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
kikhoi = (t:v) (w:be cared for/be nurtured/be nourished) (d:khoi, care for or bring up, with the passive ki: be looked after and fed) (e:a pa inn sungah a ~ hi/vakin a ~ nadingin | so that she might be fed and cared for) (b:khoi) (r:44.7.20/66.12.6) (q:draft)
kikhol = (t:v) (w:be stored/be laid up/be kept) (d:khol, store, with the passive ki: of grain or goods, be put by for later; also of water, pile up in a heap) (e:na tampi a ~ zo hi/sau veipi a ~ a luite ne-in | eating the old harvest stored for a long time/a ~ an ahi a | whether it is stored grain/note ading vantungah a ~ lametna | the hope stored up for you in heaven/a lomin ~ a | it piled up in a heap) (b:khol) (r:42.12.19/3.26.10/2.22.6/51.1.3/6.3.16) (q:draft)
kikholcip = (t:v) (w:be hoarded/be stored up) (d:kikhol, be stored, with cip, tightly, fast: be laid up and held back) (e:tuate ~ mawk loin) (b:kikhol) (r:23.23.18) (q:draft)
kikholh = (t:v) (w:associate with/keep company with/mix with) (d:be in the company of others; the other person is marked by tawh with) (e:migilote tawh ~ nuam sa a/Numei tawh a mawhte tawh na ~ loh nadingun | that you should not associate with the sexually immoral/note tawh tawlkhat i ~ khit ciangin | after we have spent some time together with you/minam dangte kiangah hawhin a ~ ding | to visit and associate with other nations) (s:kipawlpih) (r:18.34.8/46.5.9/45.15.24/44.10.28) (q:draft)
kikholh = (t:v) (w:mate/breed) (d:of animals, come together to breed) (e:Ganhonte ta nei dingin a ~ hunin) (r:1.31.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
kikholhna = (t:n) (w:company/association/keeping company) (d:kikholh, keep company, with the noun suffix na: keeping company with someone; the other party is marked by tawh, with) (e:Mipha lote tawh ~ hangin) (b:kikholh) (r:46.15.33) (q:draft)
kikholhna = (t:n) (w:sending of food to one another/exchange of gifts) (d:sharing portions of food with each other at a feast) (e:anlimnono ~ ni-in zang uh hi) (r:17.9.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
kikholhpih = (t:n) (w:companion/associate/friend) (d:a person one keeps company with; also as a verb, associate with) (e:~ mi in ama lawmte langpangin/nangmah a hong zahtak khempeuhte’ ~ ka hi hi | I am a companion of all who fear you/khuamial bek, keima ~ ahi hi | darkness alone is my companion/amah leh a ~ mite’ khe sil nadingin | to wash his feet and the feet of the men with him) (s:lawm/kikhawlpih) (a:gal) (b:kikholh) (r:19.55.20/19.119.63/19.88.18/1.24.32) (q:draft)
kikholhpihpa = (t:n) (w:companion/friend) (d:kikholhpih, companion, with pa marking a man) (e:a milip in a ~) (s:lawmpa) (a:galpa) (b:kikholhpih) (r:2.32.27) (q:draft)
kikholhpihte = (t:n) (w:companions/associates/friends) (d:plural of kikholhpih, one who keeps company with a person) (e:David le a ~ a gilkial laitakun/Sanggamte leh ~ ka khualna-in | for the sake of my brothers and companions/Amah in a ~ leh Samaria galkapte’ kiangah | he to his associates and the army of Samaria/Ka ~ in kei hong pelh dingin | so that my companions shun me) (s:lawmte/kithuahpihte) (a:galte) (b:kikholhpih) (r:40.12.3/19.122.8/16.4.2/19.88.8) (q:draft)
kikholin = (t:v) (w:be stored/be kept in reserve) (d:kikhol, be stored, with the linking ending in) (e:Hihte kei kiangah ~) (b:kikhol) (r:5.32.34) (q:draft)
kikholna = (t:n) (w:storehouse/storing) (d:kikhol, be stored, with the noun suffix na; a kikholna mun, the place where something is stored) (e:gial a ~ mun va mu ngei) (s:kholna/kikoihna) (b:kikhol) (r:18.38.22) (q:draft)
kikholpih = (t:v) (w:associate with/keep company with) (d:ama kikholpih mite, his companions or fellows; apparently the same word as kikholhpih) (e:ama ~ mite khempeuh in) (r:23.44.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
kikhom = (t:v) (w:last/be enough for) (d:khom, be enough to last, with the prefix ki: of fuel, last through a length of time) (e:kum sagih sung ~ ding hi) (b:khom) (r:26.39.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
kikhong = (t:see) <kikhong-in>
kikhong-in = (t:v) (w:slipping off/flying off) (d:of an axe head, coming loose from its handle; with the linking suffix in) (e:a heitang a ga panin ~ a vengpa) (r:5.19.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
kikhongin = (t:v) (w:slipping off/flying off) (d:of an axe head, coming loose from its handle; with the linking suffix in) (e:a heitang a ga panin ~ a vengpa) (r:5.19.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
kikhop = (t:v) (w:gather/assemble/come together/meet) (d:form of kikhawm used before ciangin, lai and similar words) (e:Note na ~ uh ciangin/Farisaite a ~ lai takun | while the Pharisees were gathered together/Topa’ an ne dingin na ~ uh ciangin | when you gather to eat the Lord’s meal/Jerusalem ah a hong ~ nading uh | that they should assemble in Jerusalem) (s:kikaihkhop) (a:kikhenthang) (b:khop) (r:46.11.20/40.22.41/46.11.33/15.10.7) (q:draft)
kikhopna = (t:n) (w:meeting/assembly/congregation) (d:a gathering of people or the place of it, as in kikhopna buk tent of meeting and kikhopna inn synagogue) (e:mipi ~ sungah Topa Pasian phat un/~ buk kongah Israel mihonte khempeuh | the whole community of Israel at the entrance to the tent of meeting/kote ~-ah meivak tampi a om hi | there were many lamps where we were meeting/~ buk kong Moses kiangah Aaron ciahkik hi | Aaron returned to Moses at the entrance to the tent of meeting) (s:kikaihkhopna) (r:19.68.26/4.16.43/3.8.3/44.20.8/4.16.50) (q:draft)
kikhopnate = (t:n) (w:assemblies/meetings/convocations) (d:plural of kikhopna, a gathering for worship; a siangtho biak kikhopnate are sacred assemblies) (e:a siangtho biak ~ ahi hi/thupi tak-a na ~ uh mawhna tawh kidim | your solemn assemblies are full of sin/na biak ~ uhah ka lung a kim kei | I take no pleasure in your religious assemblies/Zion Mual tung khempeuh leh ama ~ tungah | over all of Mount Zion and over its assemblies) (s:khawmnate) (b:kikhopna) (r:3.23.4/23.1.13/30.5.21/23.4.5) (q:draft)
kikhoppina = (t:n) (w:great assembly/general assembly) (d:kikhop, gather, with pi, great, and the noun suffix na) (e:ta-upa pawl a ~ leh pawlpi-ah) (r:58.12.22) (q:draft)
kikhopsak = (t:v) (w:gather together/call together/assemble) (d:kikhop with the causative sak: make people come together) (e:mi honpi a ~ khit uh ciangin/tua bang nasemte a ~ khit ciangin | after he had called together the workers of that trade/Paul in Judah mi upate a ~ khit ciangin | after Paul had called together the Jewish elders/siampi liante leh upate a ~ khit ciangin | after he had the chief priests and elders assemble) (s:kikhawmsak/khawmsak) (a:kikhenthangsak) (b:kikhop) (r:44.15.30/44.19.25/44.28.17/44.22.30) (q:draft)
kikhosate = (t:n) (w:those invited) (d:the people who had been invited to a feast; with sa, already done, and the plural te) (e:a ~ ahih uh leh) (r:42.14.24) (q:draft, low confidence)
kikhuak = (t:v) (w:be hewn/be cut out/be dug out) (d:khuak, hew, with the passive ki: be cut or dug out of rock, of a tomb or cistern; suang kikhuak is cut out of rock) (e:suang ~ ama han thak sungah sial a/mi kivui ngei lohna suang ~ han sungah | in a rock-cut tomb where no one had been buried/suang ~ tuibeemte, leenggui lote | rock-cut cisterns, vineyards/suang ~ ama han sungah sialin | laying it in his tomb cut out of rock) (b:khuak) (r:40.27.60/16.9.25/42.23.53/41.15.46) (q:draft)
kikhualna = (t:n) (w:sake/benefit/regard) (d:khualna, regard, with the prefix ki: regard for oneself or care shown for someone; keimah ka kikhualna, for my own sake) (e:Keimah ka ~, keimah ka kingaihsutna-in/note a’ ding a ~ hi a | it is for your benefit/itna tawh khatlekhat ~-in zangzaw un | rather use it to care for one another in love) (b:khualna) (r:23.48.11/47.4.15/48.5.13) (q:draft)
kikhuang = (t:v) (w:stretch oneself out/lie stretched over) (d:lay oneself at full length upon someone, used with tungah) (e:paito-in ama tungah ~ hi/ama tungah amah ~ a | he stretched himself out on him) (r:12.4.35/12.4.34) (q:draft)
kikhuangin = (t:v) (w:stretching oneself out/lying stretched over) (d:kikhuang with the linking suffix in: stretching one's body over someone) (e:naupang tungah amah thum vei ~/tangvalpa tungah bokin ~ kawi a | he bent over the young man, stretched himself on him and embraced him) (b:kikhuang) (r:11.17.21/44.20.10) (q:draft)
kikhuatin = (t:v) (w:scrape oneself/scratch oneself) (d:khuat, scratch or scrape, with the reflexive prefix ki and the linking ending in) (e:tua tawh ~ vut lakah tu hi) (r:18.2.8) (q:draft)
kikhuh = (t:v) (w:cover oneself/be covered/veil oneself) (d:khuh, cover, with the reflexive ki: cover oneself, as with a veil; a tung kikhuh nading is a covering over oneself) (e:a kikhuhna puan la-in ~ hi/a tung ~ nadingin meii sahpi | thick clouds as a covering over him) (b:khuh) (r:1.24.65/10.22.12) (q:draft)
kikhuhna = (t:n) (w:covering/veil) (d:something to cover oneself with; kikhuhna puan is a veil or shawl) (e:a ~ puan la-in kikhuh hi/a ~ puan suahkhia-in | taking off her veil/na ~ puan lakhia in la | take off your veil/dialkhipte leh ~ puante | the headbands and the shawls) (b:kikhuh) (r:1.24.65/1.38.19/23.47.2/23.3.23) (q:draft)
kikhui = (t:v) (w:be sewn/be stitched/be embroidered) (d:passive of khui sew; phim tawh kikhui, worked with a needle, embroidered; kikhui tuah, sewn together) (e:phim tawh ~-in a kizem kawnggak khat/phim tawh ~-in a kizem kongpuankhai khat | a curtain embroidered with a needle/a kigan puan hoihte phim tawh ~-in a kizem | woven fine linen embroidered with a needle/amah in a ~ tuah a nihna puan | the second set of curtains that were sewn together) (b:khui) (r:2.28.39/2.36.11/2.26.36/2.38.18) (q:draft)
kikhuituah = (t:v) (w:be joined together/be coupled/be sewn together) (d:khuituah, sew together, with the passive ki: of cloth or curtains, be fastened one to another to form one set) (e:khat leh khat ~ ding hi/A ~ puan khat nawl-ah a bilvang sawmnga bawlin | making fifty loops on the edge of one joined set of curtains/a ~ a nihna dalna puan nawl-ah | on the edge of the second joined set of curtains/a ~ masa puan a nawlnung pen | the end curtain of the first joined set) (b:khuituah) (r:2.26.3/2.36.12/2.26.10/2.26.5/2.36.11) (q:draft)
