kikoihna = (t:n) (w:storehouse/storage place/container) (d:the place or vessel in which something is put or kept, often followed by mun place or by the name of the container) (e:Vuk a ~ mun-ah va lut ngei a/thuciamna a ~ singkuang | the ark in which the covenant is kept/a ki-ap letsongte a ~ khempeuh | all the treasuries of the dedicated gifts/biakinn um-le-beelte a ~ inndeite | the rooms where the temple articles are kept) (s:koihna) (b:kikoih) (r:18.38.22/14.6.11/13.26.26/16.10.39) (q:draft)
kikoihsa = (t:adj) (w:set in place/made ready/appointed) (d:kikoih, be put, with sa, already: already set in place, made ready or appointed) (e:a baihsa-in a na ~ inndei tungnung/Mi khempeuh a dingin sehkholhin a ~ sihna-ah | to the death appointed beforehand for everyone) (b:kikoih) (r:41.14.15/18.30.23) (q:draft)
kikoihsak = (t:v) (w:be laid up for/be placed for/have placed) (d:kikoih, be put, with sak: something is put or kept for someone, or laid on someone) (e:vantungah a hong ~ tua lametna/a awm tung uhah a ~ kawmin | being laid on their chests) (b:kikoih) (r:51.1.5/26.32.27) (q:draft)
kikoihsuk = (t:v) (w:be put down/be brought low/be humbled) (d:koihsuk, put down, with the passive prefix ki) (e:a niamin ~ ding hi) (s:kiniamkhiat/kiniamkoih) (a:kilaamto) (b:koihsuk) (r:23.2.17) (q:draft)
kikoihte = (t:n) (w:things put/things stored) (d:kikoih, be put or kept, with plural te: the things that were placed or stored, as in sum kikoihte, the money that was put there) (e:mun sunga sum ~ leh/i van sunga sum ~’ hangin | because of the silver that was put in our sacks) (b:kikoih) (r:23.45.3/1.43.18) (q:draft)
kikoin = (t:v) (w:crying out/shouting) (d:kiko, cry out, with the linking suffix in) (e:ci-in ~ mi tampite sung pan) (b:kiko) (r:42.4.41) (q:draft)
kikokhia = (t:v) (w:cry out/shout out) (d:kiko, cry out, with khia, out: let out a loud cry) (e:Samuel a muh ciangin a gingin ~ hi/Jehoshafat ~ a, Topa in amah huh hi | Jehoshaphat cried out and the Lord helped him/numei nausuak ding bangin ka ~ ding a | I will cry out like a woman in labour/nakpi tak le nasia takin ~-in | crying out loudly and bitterly) (s:awngkhia) (b:kiko) (r:9.28.12/14.18.31/23.42.14/1.27.34) (q:draft)
kikoko = (t:v) (w:keep crying out/keep shouting) (d:kiko, cry out, with the last syllable doubled for repeated action: keep on crying out) (e:i nung zui-in ~ ahih manin/tua mi tegel a ~ loh nadingun | so that the two men would stop shouting/Huhna ding ngenin amaute ~ uh a | they kept crying out for help) (r:40.15.23/40.20.31/19.18.41) (q:draft)
kikokona = (t:see) <kikokona-in>
kikokona-in = (t:n) (w:from crying out/by calling out) (d:kiko, cry out, doubled for continued action, with the noun suffix na and in, by or because of) (e:Ka ~ ka gim a) (r:19.69.3) (q:draft)
kikol = (t:see) <kikol-awk>
kikol-awk = (t:v) (w:be hindered/be held back) (d:be kept from doing something; with sak, let something hinder) (e:bangmah ~ sak kei in) (r:4.22.16) (q:draft)
kikol-awksak = (t:v) (w:let hinder/let hold back) (d:kikol-awk, be hindered, with the causative sak; bangmah kikol-awksak kei in is let nothing keep you back) (e:bangmah ~ kei in) (r:4.22.16) (q:draft)
kikona = (t:n) (w:cry/shout/outcry/shouting) (d:kiko, cry out, with the noun suffix na: a loud cry, whether for help, in distress or in joy; lungdam-a kikona is a shout of joy) (e:Amaute’ ~ leh hih thute ka zak ciangin/na kam-ah lungdam-a ~ hong omsak ding hi | he will fill your mouth with shouts of joy/Pasian aw, ka ~ aw hong za in | O God, hear my cry/Israel mite’ ~ kei’ kiang hong tung khin a | the cry of the Israelites has reached me) (s:otna/awtna) (b:kiko) (r:16.5.6/18.8.21/19.61.1/2.3.9) (q:draft)
kikonate = (t:n) (w:shouts/cries) (d:kikona, shout, with the plural te) (e:lungdamna tawh ~ dai ta hi) (b:kikona) (r:23.16.9) (q:draft)
kikonate = (t:n) (w:reproaches/insults/taunts) (d:with hong, the things shouted against a person, reproach or disgrace) (e:Ka kihtak hong ~ heikhia in/hong ~ na phawk kha nawn kei ding hi | you will no longer remember the reproaches against you) (s:zahkonate/simmawhnate) (b:kikona) (r:19.119.39/23.54.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
kikop = (t:v) (w:be allied/join with/be together with) (d:be joined with someone as a pair, used with tawh; kop, pair, with the prefix ki) (e:Siriate pen Efraim mite tawh ~/amaute tawh eite i ~ ciangin | when we are joined together with them/Topa tawh a ~ lopi-in | without being together with the Lord) (s:pangkhawm) (b:kop) (r:23.7.2/12.18.25/58.11.40) (q:draft)
kikopa = (t:n) (w:one who cries out/one calling) (d:kiko, cry out, with pa marking a man: the man who is calling) (e:Gampa lakah a ~’ aw in/ci-in gam sungah a ~ ka hi hi | I am the one calling in the wilderness) (b:kiko) (r:41.1.3/40.3.3/43.1.23) (q:draft)
kikopih = (t:v) (w:cry out along with/echo) (d:kiko, cry out, with pih, together with: join in the cry of another) (e:innkamte in zong ~ ding uh hi) (b:kiko) (r:35.2.11) (q:draft)
kikopin = (t:adv) (w:together with/in union with) (d:kikop, be joined with, with in; used with tawh) (e:Khrih tawh ~ Pasian a’ ding) (b:kikop) (r:45.15.17) (q:draft)
kikosak = (t:v) (w:cry out/let cry out) (d:kiko, cry out, with sak; here a command to cry aloud to the Lord) (e:Topa tungah ~ in) (s:kikokhia) (b:kiko) (r:25.2.18) (q:draft)
kikosia = (t:v) (w:slander one another/insult one another) (d:kosia, speak abusively against, with the reciprocal prefix ki; kikosia kik is return an insult) (e:khat leh khat na ~ kei un/Kitawng thuk kei un, ~ kik kei un | do not hit back, do not return an insult) (s:kigensia) (b:kosia) (r:59.4.11/60.3.9) (q:draft)
kikosiat = (t:v) (w:be reviled/be insulted/be cursed) (d:form of kikosia used before ciangin; here of being spoken evil of by others) (e:Hong ~ ciangin thupha pia-in) (s:kisamsia/kizahko) (b:kikosia) (r:46.4.12) (q:draft)
kikosiatna = (t:n) (w:reproach/insult/shame) (d:kikosiat, be reviled, with the noun suffix na) (e:hong ~ paulamin kong ci hi) (b:kikosiat) (r:47.11.21) (q:draft, low confidence)
kikoto = (t:v) (w:call out/cry out) (d:kiko, cry out, with to, upward: cry up from below) (e:taw panin ka hong ~ hi) (s:kikokhia) (b:kiko) (r:25.3.55) (q:draft)
kikpa = (t:n) (d:kik, again or back, with pa, the male one who: placed after a verb, the one who does it again; a puah kikpa is the one who restores) (e:lote a puah ~ in Topa ahi) (b:kik) (r:26.36.36) (q:draft)
kiksak = (t:part) (d:placed after a verb: cause to do or be again, from kik, again or back, with causative sak; nungta kiksak is bring back to life) (e:Pasian in a nungta ~ a/leivui na suak ~ a | you turn them back to dust/misite na hing ~ un | bring the dead back to life/a kisiamai-sate ding ~ ding uh hi | they will raise up again what was ruined) (b:kik) (r:44.13.30/19.90.3/40.10.8/23.61.4) (q:draft)
kiksakin = (t:part) (d:kiksak, cause to do again, with the linking suffix in; tho kiksakin is raising back to life) (e:sihna pan tho ~ minthan’na a pia hi) (b:kiksak) (r:60.1.21) (q:draft)
kiksakpa = (t:n) (d:kiksak, cause to do again, with pa, the male one who; a tho kiksakpa is the one who raised from death) (e:sihna pan a tho ~ i up leh) (b:kiksak) (r:45.4.24) (q:draft)
kikte = (t:part) (d:kik, again or back, with the plural te after a verb: those who do the action again or in turn, as in a bangsak kikte, those who restore, and a khang kikte, those who grow up after) (e:a khang ~ in phawk nawn lo/mun siate a ngei a bangsak ~ hong kici | you will be called restorers of ruined places/a ciap khit ciangin a tawp ~ | those who stop again after tasting) (b:kik) (r:21.1.11/23.58.12/58.6.4) (q:draft)
kikuai = (t:see) <kikuai-tan>
kikuai-tan = (t:v) (w:be broken off/snap off) (d:of the branches of a vine; the English has withered) (e:A hiangte ~ a) (s:kikuaitan) (r:26.19.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
kikuaihtansak = (t:v) (w:be broken/be snapped off) (d:kuaihtansak, cause to break in two, with the passive prefix ki; of an arm) (e:a ban ~ hi) (s:kikuaitan) (b:kuaihtansak) (r:24.48.25) (q:draft)
kikuaitan = (t:v) (w:be broken/be snapped) (d:kuaitan, break in two, with the prefix ki; of a bone or a branch) (e:A guh khat beek a ~ kei ding hi/A hiangte ~ a, keu-in kihaltum hi | its branches were broken off, dried up and burned) (s:kitan/kikuai-tan) (b:kuaitan) (r:43.19.36/26.19.12) (q:draft)
kikuaitansa = (t:adj) (w:broken/splintered) (d:kikuaitan, be broken, with sa, already done: that has been broken, of a reed) (e:a ~ pumpeng ciangkhut tawh a kibang) (s:kitansa) (b:kikuaitan) (r:23.36.6) (q:draft)
kikual = (t:v) (w:coil/be coiled) (d:kual, ring or around, with ki; of a serpent, with vial) (e:a ~ vial gulpi ahi tuipi ganhing) (s:kikualvial) (b:kual) (r:23.27.1) (q:draft)
kikualvial = (t:v) (w:coil/twist round) (d:of a serpent that winds itself in rings) (e:a ~ gulpi ahi awle) (s:kikual) (r:23.27.1) (q:draft)
kikuan = (t:v) (w:go/go out) (d:kuan, set out for a task, with the prefix ki used without a named subject: people go out to work) (e:nasemin ~ nawn lo hi) (b:kuan) (r:18.24.18) (q:draft)
kikuangsak = (t:v) (w:be kept burning) (d:kuangsak, make burn, with the passive prefix ki: of a fire, be kept burning) (e:mei ~ tawntung ding hi/Biakna tau tunga mei ~ den ding hi | the fire on the altar must always be kept burning/tua biakna tau tungah mei ~ den ding hi | the fire must be kept burning on that altar) (a:kimitsak) (b:kuangsak) (r:3.6.13/3.6.12/3.6.9) (q:draft)
kikuantawh = (t:v) (w:be kindled/be aroused/flare up) (d:of anger rising against someone) (e:hehna hong ~ a) (r:19.106.40) (q:draft, low confidence)
kikui = (t:v) (w:cut oneself/gash oneself) (d:kui, cut the skin, with the reflexive prefix ki; done to the body as a sign of mourning) (e:a pumpi uh a ~ gawp sa-in) (s:kikuiliam/kikuisak) (b:kui) (r:24.41.5) (q:draft)
kikuikham = (t:v) (w:be ripped open/be cut open) (d:said of pregnant women killed in war) (e:a nupi naupaaite uh ~ ding hi) (b:kuikham) (r:28.13.16) (q:draft)
kikuiliam = (t:v) (w:cut oneself/gash oneself) (d:wound one's own body by cutting) (e:suang hiamte tawh amah a ~ hi) (s:kikui/kikuisak) (b:kuiliam) (r:41.5.5) (q:draft)
kikuisak = (t:v) (w:cut oneself/gash oneself) (d:kikui, cut oneself, with sak; a pumpi a kikuisak is he cut his own body) (e:suang tawh a pumpi a ~ hi) (s:kikui/kikuiliam) (b:kikui) (r:41.5.5) (q:draft)
kikum = (t:v) (w:discuss/reason together/confer) (d:talk a matter over with one another; thu kikum is discuss a matter) (e:ci-in khat leh khat a ~ uh hi/bang hangin khat leh khat na ~ uh hiam | why are you discussing among yourselves/hong pai in la, hih thu ~ ni | come and let us discuss this matter/na ngaihsutna uh gen un la, hih lai-ah ~ un | give your opinion and discuss it here) (s:kikup/kikumkhawm) (r:40.16.7/44.17.17/40.16.8/16.6.7/7.20.7) (q:draft)
kikumin = (t:v) (w:confer/discuss/consult together) (d:connective form of kikum, usually thu kikumin, having talked a matter over) (e:a nasemte tawh thu ~/Abner in Israel upate tawh thu ~ | Abner conferred with the elders of Israel/Tua bangin kiho-in thu ~ a om laitakun | while they were talking and discussing/amaute ~ a vaihawm uh hi | they consulted together and made plans) (s:genkhawmin) (b:kikum) (r:12.6.8/10.3.17/42.24.15/43.11.53) (q:draft)
kikumkhawm = (t:v) (w:reason together/discuss together) (d:kikum, discuss, with khawm, together) (e:hong pai unla, thu ~ ni) (s:kikum) (b:kikum) (r:23.1.18) (q:draft)
kikumkum = (t:v) (w:keep discussing/talk over/confer) (d:kikum, discuss, with the last syllable doubled for continued action: keep talking a matter over) (e:hih thupiangte ~ uh hi/keimah hong thahnopna thu ~ uh hi | they keep plotting together to kill me/a tunsak nading thu a ~ uh ahi hi | they were talking about how he would fulfil it) (s:kihoho) (r:42.24.14/19.71.10/42.9.31) (q:draft)
kikumpah = (t:v) (w:discuss at once/begin to discuss) (d:kikum, discuss, with pah, straight away) (e:khatlekhat a ~ uh hi) (r:42.6.11) (q:draft)
kikunsak = (t:v) (w:be bowed down/be made to stoop) (d:kun, bow or stoop, with the prefix ki and the causative sak) (e:keimah hong ~ a, hong kibokcipsak hi) (r:19.38.6) (q:draft)
kikup = (t:v) (w:discuss/consult/talk together) (d:talk a matter over with one another, often as thu kikup) (e:mite tawh thu a ~ khit ciangin/A ~ lai takun Zeisu in va nai a | while they were talking Jesus came near/lam na pai lai takun na ~ uh thu | the matter you are discussing as you walk/khat leh khat kihopihin i ~ khop ding | we will talk together face to face) (s:kikum/kiho) (r:14.20.21/42.24.15/42.24.17/64.1.14) (q:draft)
kikupna = (t:n) (w:consultation/discussion/deliberation) (d:noun from kikup, talking a matter over together; kikupna nei is to hold a consultation) (e:makai khempeuh tawh ~ khat nei hi/kumpipa in thu ~ khat bawl a | the king held a consultation/galkap a ukte in thu ~ nei uh hi | the army officers were holding a council/Mihonpite ~ thu a theih uh ciangin | when they learned what the crowd was saying) (b:kikup) (r:13.13.1/11.12.28/12.9.5/43.7.32) (q:draft)
kikzo = (t:part) (d:kik, again or back, with zo, be able, after a verb: be able to do again or back; kikzo nawn lo is no longer able to do again) (e:a ding ~ nawn lo dingin/a gam panin hong kuankhia ~ nawn lo hi | he could no longer march out from his land/kua in kaiton ~ ding ahi hiam | who is able to turn it back) (b:kik) (r:5.33.11/12.24.7/23.14.27) (q:draft)
kil = (t:adj) (w:wavy/curly) (d:of hair; kil thiuhtheuh describes long hair that falls in waves) (e:A sam sau-in ~ thiuhtheuh a) (r:22.5.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
kila = (t:v) (w:be taken/be captured/be seized) (d:la, take, with the passive prefix ki: be taken or chosen, of a city be captured, also of goods brought in from elsewhere) (e:Babilon khuapi ~ ta hi/khat ~ a, khat kinusia ding hi | one will be taken and the other left/Faro’ inn sungah tua nu ~ hi | the woman was taken into the house of Pharaoh/aisanna tawh Benjamin minam ~ hi | the tribe of Benjamin was taken by lot) (s:kilak) (a:kinusia) (b:la) (r:24.51.41/14.9.28/40.24.40/1.12.15/9.10.20) (q:draft)
kilaak = (t:v) (w:appear/present oneself) (d:show oneself before someone, as before God at the yearly feasts) (e:kum khat in thum vei ~ ding uh hi/Pasian mai-ah amau ciat ~ uh hi | they each presented themselves before God/a guakin kuamah hong ~ lo ding hi | no one shall appear before me empty-handed/amah hong ~ ciangin kua nungtazo ding | who can survive when he appears) (s:kilak/kilang) (r:2.23.17/23.1.12/6.24.1/2.34.20/39.3.2) (q:draft)
kilaakin = (t:v) (w:appear/present oneself) (d:kilaak, show oneself, with the linking ending in) (e:Moab amahmah hong ~) (s:kilangin/kilakin) (b:kilaak) (r:23.16.12) (q:draft)
kilaam = (t:v) (w:be lifted up/be raised) (d:found with to, upward: kilaam to is be lifted up) (e:a lianin kikoihin ~ to ding a) (r:23.52.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
kilaamto = (t:v) (w:be lifted up/be raised high) (d:laamto, lift up, with the prefix ki: be lifted up or raised high, said of gates, of a head held high and of tall trees) (e:Taanglai kong khakte aw, ~ un/ka galte tungah ka lu ~-in | my head being lifted up above my enemies/a sang, a ~, Lebanon mual taamtak kung khempeuh | all the tall and lofty cedars of Lebanon/amah a lianin kikoihin ~ ding a | he will be raised and lifted up) (s:kilamto/kidomto) (a:kikoihsuk/kiniamkhiat) (b:laamto) (r:19.24.7/23.2.13/19.27.6/23.52.13) (q:draft)
kilah = (t:v) (w:show oneself/appear/be shown/be revealed) (d:form of kilak used before khit, ni, leh and ciangin) (e:siampipa kiangah a ~ khit ciangin/Israel mite kiangah a ~ ni matengin | until the day he appeared to Israel/mualte tungah lan khat hong ~ ciangin | when a banner is raised on the mountains/Nungzuite kiangah Jesuh a ~ laitakin | when Jesus appeared to the disciples) (s:kilat) (b:lah) (r:3.13.7/42.1.80/23.18.3/43.20.24) (q:draft)
kilahkhiat = (t:v) (w:be revealed/be shown forth) (d:lahkhiat, reveal, with the prefix ki; the form used before ding and hun) (e:upna thu a ~ ding ngakna-in/Pasian’ tate a hong ~ hun ding | the time when the children of God are revealed) (s:kilangkhia) (b:lahkhiat) (r:48.3.23/45.8.19) (q:draft)
kilahna = (t:n) (w:appearing/showing/manifestation) (d:the act of showing oneself or of being shown; kilahna mun is the place where someone appeared, and lim kilahna is an example shown to others) (e:David tungah Topa a ~ mun/hih thute in eite adingin lim ~ ahi hi | these things are examples for us/A ~ thu in hih bang ahi hi | this is how he appeared) (s:kilatna/kilakna) (b:kilah) (r:14.3.1/46.10.6/43.21.1) (q:draft)
kilahsa = (t:v) (w:appeared/have appeared) (d:kilah, show oneself, with sa for a completed action; a kilahsa bangin, as he had appeared) (e:ama tungah a ~ bangin Solomon tungah) (s:kilangsa) (b:kilah) (r:11.9.2) (q:draft)
kilai = (t:v) (w:fight/struggle/wrestle) (d:fight or wrestle with one another, come to blows; with tawh, struggle with someone) (e:Hebru mi nih na ~ uh hi/a khangham ciangin zong Pasian tawh ~ hi | as a grown man he struggled with God/Mi khat leh khat a ~ ciangin | when two men fight each other/mite tawh na ~ khin a, na zo hi | you have struggled with men and have won) (s:kido) (r:2.2.13/28.12.3/5.25.11/1.32.28) (q:draft)
kilaigawp = (t:v) (w:struggle together/jostle) (d:kilai, fight with one another, with gawp, roughly or violently) (e:Ama sungah a naute ~ hi) (b:kilai) (r:1.25.22) (q:draft)
kilaih = (t:v) (w:be replaced/be exchanged/alternate) (d:passive of laih, replace: one thing is put in the place of another; kilaih sak, take in turn) (e:anlum a lum lai tawh a ~ pah ding/sithei nawn lo pumpi tawh a ~ theih nadingin | so that it may be exchanged for the body that cannot die/khat kiteel a, ~ sak niloh uh hi | one was chosen, taking them in turn) (s:kikhek) (b:laih) (r:9.21.6/13.24.6/47.5.4) (q:draft)
kilaihsak = (t:v) (w:take in turn/alternate) (d:kilaih, be exchanged, with the causative sak: one is taken from one side and then one from the other) (e:~ niloh uh hi) (b:kilaih) (r:13.24.6) (q:draft)
kilailawh = (t:v) (w:fight/struggle with one another) (d:paired with kitawng, quarrel) (e:kitawngin na ~ uh hi) (s:kilai/kido) (r:59.4.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
kilaina = (t:n) (w:fight/fighting/wrestling) (d:kilai, fight or wrestle, with the noun suffix na: a fight, or the act of wrestling) (e:kitotna le ~ koi panin hong piang/amah tawh a ~-in Jakob’ khelguh kilawi hi | as he wrestled with him the hip of Jacob was put out) (s:kidona) (b:kilai) (r:59.4.1/1.32.25) (q:draft)
kilaithang = (t:v) (w:attack one another/fight one another) (d:with khat leh khat, one another, of people in panic who turn on each other) (e:khat leh khat ~ gawp ding uh hi) (r:38.14.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
kilak = (t:v) (w:appear/show oneself/be shown/be revealed) (d:lak, show, with the prefix ki: show oneself to someone, appear, or be shown and made known) (e:tawh a pumpi a ~ hi/siampipa kiangah ~ ding hi | he must show himself to the priest/Mual tungah nang’ tunga hong ~ hih nate | these things that were shown to you on the mountain/Filistia khuacingte kiangah amau tegel va ~ uh hi | the two of them showed themselves to the Philistine guards/A ~ lo ding a kisincip bangmah om lo hi | nothing is concealed that will not be disclosed) (s:kilang/kilaak) (a:kiseel) (b:lak) (r:41.16.12/2.25.40/3.13.19/9.14.11/42.12.2) (q:draft)
kilak = (t:v) (w:be taken/be captured) (d:lak, take, with the passive prefix ki: be taken, said of a city captured in war) (e:Jerusalem khua a ~ ciang dong/Ashdod khua a ~ khit ciangin | after the town of Ashdod was captured/Jerusalem khua a ~ laitakin | when Jerusalem was taken/Jerusalem khuapi a ~ zawh | after the city of Jerusalem was taken) (s:kila) (b:lak) (r:24.38.28/23.20.3/24.39.3/26.40.1) (q:draft)
kilakhawm = (t:v) (w:be taken together/be caught up together) (d:kila, be taken, with khawm, together) (e:sisa mite tawh hong ~ ding a) (b:kila) (r:52.4.17) (q:draft)
kilakhia = (t:v) (w:taken out/be taken away/be removed) (d:lakhia, take out, with the passive prefix ki: be taken out of or away from a place or a person) (e:a neihsa nangawn ~ ding hi/mipa’ sung panin a ~ ahih manin | because she was taken out of man/mual tunga biaknate ~ lo hi | the high places were not removed/Pasian Gam note kiang pan ~ ding a | the kingdom of God will be taken away from you) (s:kikoihkhia) (b:lakhia) (r:40.13.12/1.2.23/12.15.4/40.21.43)
kilakhia = (t:v) (w:draw/be drawn out) (d:be drawn out of something, as milk from the breast or pieces of meat from a pot) (e:Ang sung panin a ~ nawi | milk drawn from the breast/Beel sunga sate khat khatin ~ a | the pieces of meat in the pot are drawn out one by one) (r:23.28.9/26.24.6)
kilakhia = (t:v) (w:pull/be pulled out/be snatched away) (d:be pulled up or snatched away from where it was) (e:ka omna inn kibotkhia-in kei kiang panin ~ hi | my house is pulled up and taken from me/a han sung uh panin ~ ding a | they will be pulled out of their graves/tua naungek pen thakhatin ~-in | the child was suddenly snatched away) (r:23.38.12/24.8.1/66.12.5)
kilakin = (t:v) (w:show/appear/present oneself) (d:kilak, show or appear, with the linking ending in; khat leh khat tungah kilakin, showing to one another) (e:tungah itna leh hehpihna ~/omna mai-ah ~ tua lai-ah a om tawntung dingin | presenting him before the Lord to stay there always) (s:kilangin) (b:kilak) (r:38.7.9/9.1.22) (q:draft)
kilakkhiat = (t:v) (w:be taken away/be removed/be lifted) (d:passive of lakkhiat, take away: be taken away, removed or lifted; the form used before a following word such as ciangin, khit, kei leh or ni) (e:ahih hangin meii a ~ kei leh/Lam lianpi panin amah a ~ khit ciangin | after he was removed from the road/puanbuk tung san panin meiipi a ~ ciangin | when the cloud lifted from above the tent/a thaute a ~ mah bangin | just as the fat is removed) (b:lakkhiat) (r:2.40.37/53.2.7/10.20.13/4.12.10/3.4.31) (q:draft)
kilakkhiatsak = (t:v) (w:be taken away/be removed) (d:kilakkhiat, be taken away, with sak; of a kingdom taken from a king and of sin removed) (e:Na kumpi gam hong ~ zo hi/Jakob’ mawhna kimaisakin a mawhna ~ hi | the guilt of Jacob is forgiven and his sin removed) (b:kilakkhiat) (r:27.4.31/23.27.9) (q:draft)
kilakkik = (t:v) (w:appear again/show oneself again) (d:kilak, show oneself, with kik, again) (e:Vashti a ~ nawn loh nadingin) (s:kilangkik/kilatkik) (b:kilak) (r:17.1.19) (q:draft)
kilaklo = (t:v) (w:not be shown/not be given) (d:kilak, be shown, with lo, not, written as one word; of a sign that will not be shown) (e:adang hong ~ ding hi/Jonah lim simloh a dang ~ ding hi | no other sign will be given except the sign of Jonah) (b:kilak) (r:40.12.39/40.16.4) (q:draft)
kilakmang = (t:v) (w:be taken away/be carried off) (d:be taken so that it is gone, of herds taken as plunder) (e:a bawnghonte uh ~ sak ding hi) (r:24.49.32) (q:draft)
kilakna = (t:n) (w:appearance/appearing/showing oneself) (d:kilak, show oneself, with the noun suffix na: an appearing, the occasion on which someone shows himself or is made known) (e:a nungzuite kiangah thumvei a ~ ahi hi/khomun a balnen lai takin a ~ thu | how he was made known when he broke the bread) (s:kilahna/kilatna) (b:kilak) (r:43.21.14/42.24.35) (q:draft)
kilakna = (t:n) (w:taking/charging) (d:the act of something being taken; leiba ameet kilakna, the charging of interest on a debt) (e:Leiba ameet ~ phiat ni) (s:lakna) (b:kilak) (r:16.5.10/3.16.27) (q:draft)
kilaksa = (t:v) (w:shown/have been shown) (d:kilak, be shown, with sa for a completed action; hong kilaksa bangin, as it was shown to you) (e:nang tungah hong ~ bangin kibawl ding hi) (b:kilak) (r:2.27.8) (q:draft)
kilaksak = (t:v) (w:be robbed of/be deprived of/be taken from) (d:have something taken away from one: laksak, take from someone, with the passive prefix ki; a no a kilaksak vompi is a bear robbed of her cubs) (e:A no a ~ vompi bangin/a neihsa sunsun nangawn ~ ding hi | even what he has will be taken from him/a ciam bangin a neihsa ~ takpi ding hi | what he has will surely be taken as he pledged/a sum a pai khempeuh a ~ zo hi | all his treasures have been taken away) (s:kiguksak) (b:laksak) (r:28.13.8/20.20.16/40.13.12/31.1.6) (q:draft)
kilaksakmang = (t:v) (w:be carried off/be taken away) (d:have something taken away for good, said of herds carried off as plunder) (e:a bawnghonte uh ~ ding hi) (s:kituahmang) (b:laksakmang) (r:24.49.32) (q:draft)
kilaktawm = (t:v) (w:present oneself/show oneself) (d:go and show oneself to someone of one's own accord) (e:Ahab kiangah amah a ~ dingin Elijah) (r:11.18.2) (q:draft)
kilaktoh = (t:v) (w:be taken up/be lifted up) (d:be taken upward: of Jesus and Enoch taken up to heaven, and of the cloud lifting from the tent) (e:a tunglam a ~ ni dong/Vantungah ~ ding hun | the time to be taken up to heaven/Tua bangin Jesuh a ~ ciangin | as Jesus was taken up/meii a ~ khit ciangin | after the cloud had lifted) (s:kilato) (b:kilak) (r:44.1.2/42.9.51/44.1.10/4.9.17) (q:draft)
kilam = (t:v) (w:be built/be set up) (d:lam, build, with the passive prefix ki: of a house, a temple or a city, be built) (e:Pilna tawh inn ~ a/innte a ~ om nai lo hi | no houses had been built yet/Topa min adingin inn ~ nai lo | no house had yet been built for the name of the Lord/sumgolh tawh ~ innte mei in kangtum hi | fire burns up the houses built with bribes) (a:kisusia) (b:lam) (r:20.24.3/2.40.17/16.7.4/11.3.2/18.15.34) (q:draft)
kilamdan = (t:v) (w:differ/be different) (d:be different from one another; in the verses it occurs in the noun kilamdan'na, difference or distinction) (e:a zawng a ~’na om lo hi/a ~’na khat ka bawl ding hi | I will make a distinction/meel ~’na tawh a pumpi a kilak hi | he showed himself in a different form/a ~’na na mu kik ding uh hi | you will again see the difference) (s:kilamdang) (b:lamdan) (r:20.22.2/39.3.18/2.8.23/41.16.12) (q:draft)
kilamdang = (t:v) (w:be different/differ/be changed/be transfigured) (d:be or become different from something, with tawh for what it differs from; of the face or appearance, be changed) (e:amaute mai-ah a meel ~ a/sila tawh a ~ kei hi | he is no different from a slave/aksite a vangliatna in atuam tuamin a ~ hi | the stars differ from one another in splendor/kumpigam dangte tawh a ~ mahmah ding hi | it will be very different from the other kingdoms) (s:kilamdan) (b:lamdang) (r:40.17.2/48.4.1/46.15.41/27.7.23) (q:draft)
kilamdangin = (t:adv) (w:differently/distinctly/with a distinction) (d:kilamdang, be different, with the ending in: in a different way, so that one can be told from another) (e:Israel mite a ~ Topa in bawl hi/a aw a ~ a gin’ kei leh | if its sound does not ring distinctly/kei tawh a ~ | differently from me) (b:kilamdang) (r:2.11.7/46.14.7/48.5.10) (q:draft)
kilamdangsak = (t:v) (w:transform/make different/confuse/confound) (d:kilamdang, be different, with the causative sak: of oneself, be transformed; of speech, make it differ so that it is confused) (e:na lim uh na ~ un/a pau uh ~ in | confound their speech) (b:kilamdang) (r:45.12.2/19.55.9) (q:draft)
kilamdanna = (t:n) (w:difference/distinction) (d:kilamdan, differ, with the noun suffix na: what makes two things or groups different; a kilamdanna bawl is make a distinction) (e:a zawng a ~ om lo a/kuamah a ~ om loin | there being no difference for anyone/a ~ khat ka bawl ding hi | I will make a distinction/keima nasepna le leitung kumpite’ nasepna a ~ | the difference between serving me and serving the kings of the earth) (s:kibatlohna) (a:kibatna) (b:kilamdan) (r:20.22.2/26.44.23/45.3.22/2.8.23/14.12.8) (q:draft)
kilamen = (t:v) (w:hope/expect/think) (d:lamen, hope, with the prefix ki: hope or expect for oneself that something will happen, after a clause with dingin) (e:inn-ah a si dingin ka ~ hi/Pasal nei dingin ~ ing ci mah leng zong | even if I said I hope to have a husband/kimu baih thei dingin ~ ka hih manin | because I hope to see you soon/Bang khat peuhpeuh ngah ding, ci-in ~ ahih manin | because he expected to get something) (b:lamen) (r:18.29.18/8.1.12/64.1.14/44.3.5) (q:draft)
kilamet = (t:v) (w:expect/hope for) (d:lamet, hope or expect, with the prefix ki) (e:An hau dingin na ~ uh hangin) (b:lamet) (r:37.1.9) (q:draft)
kilamin = (t:v) (w:be built/be built up) (d:kilam, be built, with the linking ending in, joining it to the next verb) (e:Tua inn pen suang lianpite tawh ~/suang hoih mahmahte tawh ~ tua biakinn | that temple built with very fine stones/zung kha-in, ~ omin | being rooted and built up) (b:kilam) (r:15.5.8/42.21.5/51.2.6) (q:draft)
kilamkik = (t:v) (w:be rebuilt) (d:lamkik, rebuild, with the passive prefix ki: of a city or temple, be built again) (e:hih khuapi ~ lo ding hi/Ka biakinn a ~ nading | for my temple to be rebuilt/Judah khuapite ~ ding a | the towns of Judah shall be rebuilt/Jerusalem ~ ding a | Jerusalem shall be rebuilt) (s:kiciangkik) (b:lamkik) (r:15.4.21/27.9.25/38.8.9/23.44.26/23.44.28) (q:draft)
kilamkikna = (t:n) (w:rebuilding/restoration) (d:kilamkik, be rebuilt, with the noun suffix na: the building again of a house or temple) (e:biakinn a ~ ding le a nate/Pasian’ inn a ~ thute | the records of the rebuilding of the house of God/Pasian’ inn a ~ ding amah in thupia hi | he gave the order for the house of God to be rebuilt) (s:lamkikna) (b:kilamkik) (r:15.5.9/14.24.27/15.5.13) (q:draft)
kilamna = (t:n) (w:building/being built) (d:kilam, be built, with the noun suffix na) (e:amaute a ~ ding le a kiphuh) (b:kilam) (r:24.31.28) (q:draft)
kilamsa = (t:adj) (w:built) (d:kilam, be built, with sa, already done: that was built, placed before the thing built) (e:a ~ inn a lamkik ka hi uh hi) (s:lamsa) (b:kilam) (r:15.5.11) (q:draft)
kilamsang = (t:v) (w:exalt oneself/be exalted) (d:lift oneself up high or be lifted up high; the opposite of kiniamkhiat, humble oneself) (e:A kiniamkhiat peuhmah a ~ ding hi/a ~ peuhmah in niamkhiatna a thuak ding hi | whoever exalts himself will be humbled) (s:kisangsak/kiliansak) (a:kiniamkhiat) (r:40.23.12) (q:draft)
kilamto = (t:v) (w:be raised/be lifted up/be upraised) (d:passive of lamto, lift up; of a hand held up, also of trees standing high) (e:ama khut ~ lai hi/a sang, a ~, Lebanon mual taamtaak singkungte | the tall and lofty cedars of Lebanon) (b:lamto) (r:23.9.12/23.2.13) (q:draft)
kilang = (t:v) (w:appear/be revealed/be shown/be seen) (d:become visible or known; of a person or an angel, appear to someone; a kilang lo is what is not seen) (e:tahum zong hong ~ hi/Amau kiangah Moses leh Elijah ~ a | Moses and Elijah appeared to them/meel lamdangin ~ uh a | they appeared in a wondrous form/A ~ lona-ah a muthei na Pa | your Father who sees what is unseen) (s:kilak/kidawk) (a:kiseel) (r:40.13.26/45.1.18/40.17.3/42.9.30/40.6.18) (q:draft)
kilanga = (t:adv) (w:openly/evidently/plainly) (d:kilang, appear, with a: in a way that can be seen) (e:a ~ na zuih uh ahi zongin) (b:kilang) (r:47.9.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
kilangbawlna = (t:n) (w:opposition/hostility/enmity) (d:langbawlna, opposition, with the prefix ki: being set against one another, or being opposed by others) (e:milim biakna, mi bumna, ~, kitotna/nakpitakin hong ~ hangin | in spite of the strong opposition against us) (s:kilangneihna/kigalneihna) (a:kilemna) (b:langbawlna) (r:48.5.20/52.2.2) (q:draft)
kilangin = (t:adv) (w:openly/publicly/visibly) (d:kilang, appear, with the ending in, used as a kilangin: in a way that is seen by all, not in secret) (e:amah in a ~ thu a hilh hangin/Leitung mite mai-ah a ~ ka gen zo hi | I have spoken openly before the people of the world/a ~ Zeisu a pai nawn kei hi | Jesus no longer went about openly/a ~ a mang kei uh hi | they did not follow him openly) (s:langtangin) (a:simthamin/thusimin) (b:kilang) (r:43.7.26/43.18.20/43.11.54/43.12.42) (q:draft)
kilangin = (t:v) (w:appear/be revealed) (d:kilang, appear, with the linking suffix in: appearing and then going on to the next action) (e:kei' tungah hong ~ kei thupha hong pia/vantungmi ama tungah ~ | the angel appeared to him/zanin Solomon’ tungah Topa ~ | the Lord appeared to Solomon at night/amau kiangah ni sawmli tawntung ~ | appearing to them over forty days) (b:kilang) (r:1.48.3/7.6.12/14.7.12/44.1.3) (q:draft)
kilangkhem = (t:v) (w:pretend/make a false show/be hypocritical) (d:kilang, appear, with khem, deceive: put on a good appearance that is not true; a hoihin a kilangkhem are those who only seem good, hypocrites) (e:a hoihin a ~ note’ thu) (s:kineihkhem) (r:41.7.6) (q:draft)
kilangkhia = (t:v) (w:be revealed/come to light/be shown) (d:kilang, appear, with khia, out; kilangkhia sak, bring to light, uncover) (e:thuman i hihna hong ~ sak zo hi/a bukna munte uh ka ~ sak hi | I have uncovered their hiding places/Khuavak in mualleguamte ~ sak a | the light makes the hills and valleys stand out) (b:kilang) (r:24.51.10/24.49.10/18.38.14) (q:draft)
kilangkik = (t:v) (w:appear again/reappear) (d:kilang, appear, with kik, again: come into view once more) (e:Elijah hong ~ hi/dahna hong ~ hi | grief appears again/khatvei hong ~ ding ahih manin | because it will appear once more) (s:kilakkik) (b:kilang) (r:42.9.8/66.17.8/20.14.13) (q:draft)
kilanglo = (t:adj) (w:not obvious/not apparent/unseen) (d:kilang, appear, with the negative lo) (e:a ~ gamtatna hoih a kiseel) (b:kilang) (r:54.5.25) (q:draft)
kilangneih = (t:adj) (w:unfriendly/hostile/at enmity) (d:being enemies of one another, used with tawh for the other party) (e:Pasian tawh eite i ~ laitakin) (r:45.5.10)
kilangneihna = (t:n) (w:enmity/hostility) (d:kilangneih, be at enmity, with the noun suffix na: the state of being enemies of one another) (e:Khrih in ~ beisak a/kikalah ~ ka koih ding hi | I will put enmity between/amah tawh ~ a om lo | having no enmity with him) (s:kigalneihna/galneihna/kilemlohna) (a:kilemna) (b:kilangneih) (r:49.2.16/1.3.15/5.4.42)
kilangpang = (t:v) (w:oppose each other/be in conflict) (d:langpang, oppose, with the reciprocal prefix ki) (e:hih nih tegel a ~ niloh) (b:langpang) (r:48.5.17) (q:draft)
kilangsa = (t:v) (w:appeared/revealed) (d:kilang, appear, with sa, already done: that has appeared) (e:kote kiangah hong ~ tua nuntak tawntungna) (s:kilahsa) (b:kilang) (r:62.1.2) (q:draft)
kilangsak = (t:v) (w:reveal/show/make known) (d:kilang, appear, with the causative sak: make something seen or known) (e:na vaang tawh ka dikna ~ in/Faro’ tungah hong ~ khin hi | he has revealed it to Pharaoh/ka Pa’ minthan’na na ~ ding uh a | you will show the glory of my Father/Pasian in a kitel takin hong ~ ding hi | God will make it clear to us) (s:lakkhia) (a:seel) (b:kilang) (r:19.54.1/1.41.25/43.15.8/50.3.15) (q:draft)
kilangsakin = (t:v) (w:revealing/showing/making known) (d:kilangsak, reveal, with the linking ending in, joining it to the next verb) (e:ama minthan’na ~ a nungzuite in/ama ngaihsutna mihingte tungah ~ | revealing his thoughts to mankind/Pasian a thumanna ~ a min thangsak semsem | showing the truthfulness of God and making his name more famous/Pasian’ minphatna ~, khat leh khat na kimang un | accept one another, showing forth the praise of God) (b:kilangsak) (r:43.2.11/45.3.7/30.4.13/45.15.7) (q:draft)
kilangsakkik = (t:v) (w:make appear again/show again) (d:kilangsak, cause to appear, with kik, again; of Christ shown alive after his death and of his future appearing) (e:Jesuh hong ~ ding hi/amah hingkik sakin hong ~ hi | he raised him to life and made him appear again) (b:kilangsak) (r:54.6.15/44.10.40) (q:draft)
kilangsakte = (t:n) (w:those who show/those who make known) (d:kilangsak, make known, with the plural te) (e:a hoihna a ~ ahi ding uh) (b:kilangsak) (r:56.2.10) (q:draft)
kilangte = (t:n) (w:things that appear/what is seen) (d:kilang appear with te, those which; a pua lama kilangte is what shows on the outside) (e:a pua lama ~ en a/kote maitangah a ~ in tawlkhat bek kip a | the things that appear before us last only a short while) (b:kilang) (r:9.16.7/47.4.17) (q:draft)
kilangtuam = (t:v) (w:show oneself separately/appear specially) (d:appear to some apart from others) (e:kote tungah bangci-in hong ~ thei ding) (r:43.14.22) (q:draft)
kilangzaw = (t:v) (w:appear more/be more evident) (d:kilang, appear, with zaw, more) (e:ahihna hong ~ kan lai hi) (b:kilang) (r:45.7.13) (q:draft)
kilangzo = (t:v) (w:have appeared/have been revealed) (d:kilang appear with zo, marking the action as accomplished) (e:ko kiangah hong ~ hi/Hebru mite’ Pasian, kote’ kiangah hong ~ hi | the God of the Hebrews has appeared to us/Pasian tawh kipawl theih nading lampi hong ~ a | the way to be united with God has been revealed) (b:kilang) (r:2.5.3/45.3.21/2.3.18) (q:draft)
kilat = (t:v) (w:appear/be revealed) (d:form of kilang, appear, used before a following word such as ciangin, ni, hun, ding or nading) (e:Mihing Tapa a ~ ni ciangin/aksi ~ hun | the time the star appeared/mite a hong itna hong ~ ciangin | when his love for people appeared/ama tungah ma thak a ~ ciangin | when raw flesh appears on him/Pasian’ tate a ~ ding lamenin | hoping for the children of God to be revealed) (r:42.17.30/3.13.14/40.2.7/56.3.4/45.8.19) (q:draft)
kilate = (t:n) (w:things taken/plunder/spoil) (d:kila be taken with te, those which) (e:galte’ na a ~ sung panin) (b:kila) (r:9.30.26) (q:draft)
kilate = (t:n) (w:channels/canals) (d:in lei zui-a tui kilate, waters that are led along the ground) (e:Lei zui-a tui ~ uihin) (b:kila) (r:23.19.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
kilatkhak = (t:v) (w:be exposed/come to light) (d:kilat, appear, with khak, happen to: of wrong deeds, come to be seen) (e:a siatna uh a ~ ding ut lo) (s:kipholak) (r:43.3.20) (q:draft)
kilatkhiat = (t:v) (w:be manifested/be shown forth) (d:kilat, appear, with khiat, out; kilatkhiat nading is for the showing forth, where the English has manifestation) (e:Kha Siangtho’ ~ nading mikim tungah) (s:kilahkhiat) (b:kilat) (r:46.12.7) (q:draft)
kilatkik = (t:v) (w:appear again/reappear/be revealed again) (d:kilat appear with kik, again; used of the return of Christ) (e:Jesuh Khrih hong ~ ding ngakin/Khrih hong ~ ciangin | when Christ appears again/I Topa Jesuh hong ~ Ni dongin | until the Day our Lord Jesus appears again/na khat peuhpeuh tungah a ~ leh | if it reappears on any article) (s:kilakkik) (b:kilat) (r:46.1.7/3.13.57/62.2.28/54.6.14) (q:draft)
kilatna = (t:n) (w:revelation/appearing/display/sight) (d:kilat, appear, with the noun suffix na: the showing or becoming visible of something, also the thing that is seen) (e:lungtomna in haina ~ hi/Zeisu Khazih hong ~ hangin | through the revelation of Jesus Christ/Tua bang a ~ in kihtakhuai mahmah | the sight was so terrifying/ka tanu’ nungakna a ~ limte | the signs that show the virginity of my daughter) (s:kilahna) (b:kilat) (r:20.14.29/45.16.25/58.12.21/5.22.17) (q:draft)
kilato = (t:v) (w:be taken up/be lifted up) (d:kila, be taken, with to, up: be taken upward, as into heaven) (e:Zeisu vantung lamah ~ a/amaute tawh kikhen a, vantungah ~ hi | he parted from them and was taken up into heaven/tua na vantungah a ~ kik hi | that thing was taken back up to heaven/sihna tawh kipelhin a ~ hi | he escaped death and was taken up) (s:kilaktoh) (b:kila) (r:44.1.9/42.24.51/44.10.16/58.11.5) (q:draft)
kilatosak = (t:v) (w:take up/take away) (d:kilato, be taken up, with the causative sak; of God taking Enoch) (e:Pasian in amah ~ ahih ciangin) (b:kilato) (r:58.11.5) (q:draft)
kilatsak = (t:v) (w:show/reveal/make manifest/demonstrate) (d:kilat, appear, with the causative sak: make something plain to see, often before nading) (e:ama Tapa kei sungah a ~ ciangin/amah thuman ahihna a ~ nadingin | in order to show that he is just/a kisikna uh a ~ nadingun | so that they show their repentance/a cihtakna uh a ~ nadingun | so that they show their faithfulness) (s:lakkhia) (a:seel) (b:kilat) (r:48.1.16/47.2.8/45.3.26/44.26.20/56.2.10) (q:draft)
kilatsakna = (t:n) (w:showing/proof) (d:kilatsak, make plain to see, with the noun suffix na; teci kilatsakna, the showing of proof, stands where the English has character) (e:Thuakzawhna in teci ~ a piangsak hi) (b:kilatsak) (r:45.5.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
kilausak = (t:v) (w:be terrified/be made afraid) (d:lausak, frighten, with the prefix ki) (e:Amaute nakpitakin ~ ding a) (s:laugawp) (b:lausak) (r:23.44.11) (q:draft)
kilawh = (t:v) (w:spread) (d:of a skin disease, spread to other parts of the body) (e:mun khat bekah omin a ~ kei leh/a cithak ~ loin | the sore not having spread) (s:kizelh) (r:3.13.23/3.13.32) (q:draft)
kilawh = (t:v) (w:be picked/be gleaned) (d:of fruit, be gathered; kilawh kik, be gone over again, gleaned) (e:a sanghte a ~ kik bangin) (r:24.6.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
kilawhgawp = (t:v) (w:break out/spread all over) (d:kilawh, spread, of a skin disease, with gawp, severely: of boils breaking out on people and animals) (e:meimatum piangsakin ~ hi/mihing le ganhing tungah meimatum suakin ~ ding hi | boils will break out all over people and animals) (b:kilawh) (r:2.9.10/2.9.9) (q:draft)
kilawi = (t:v) (w:be out of joint/be dislocated/be disabled) (d:of bones or limbs, be put out of place) (e:ka guh ka tang khempeuh ~ khin hi/Jakob’ khelguh ~ hi | the hip of Jacob was put out of joint/A khe zawte in a ~ taktak loh nading | so that the lame may not be truly disabled) (s:kilong) (r:19.22.14/1.32.25/58.12.13) (q:draft)
kilawi = (t:v) (w:be lacking/be without/be deserted) (d:be missing or empty of something; kilawi ngei kei is never be without, and a kilawi mun is a deserted place) (e:Amau phualpi a ~ mun suak hen la/~ ngei kei hen | may it never be without/a gah tawh zong ~ ngei lo ding hi | it will never be without fruit/mi tampi a omna kumpi khuapi ~ ding hi | the royal city full of people will be deserted) (s:tasam) (r:19.69.25/10.3.29/26.47.12/23.32.14) (q:draft)
kilawm = (t:adj) (w:suitable/fitting/proper) (d:right or fitting for a person or a purpose; a kilawm mah bangin is as is fitting) (e:mipa’ adinga a ~, a huh ding/Topa sungah a ~ mah bangin | as is fitting in the Lord/Pahtawina in thutangte tawh ~ kituak hi | praise befits the upright/ukna lim a om nading a ~ hi | it is fitting that there be a sign of authority) (s:hoihtuak) (r:1.2.20/51.3.18/19.33.1/46.11.10)
kilawm = (t:adj) (w:fit for/worthy/deserving) (d:good enough or deserving to do or receive something; after a verb with ding, worthy to do it) (e:phel ding nangawnin ka ~ kei hi/en dingin a ~ mi khat beek | even one person worthy to look inside/Tua inn a ~ leh | if that house is worthy) (r:43.1.27/66.5.4/40.10.13)
kilawma = (t:adv) (w:fittingly/becomingly) (d:kilawm, suitable, with a; a mel kilawma om is of fair appearance) (e:a mel ~ om pawlpi) (b:kilawm) (r:49.5.27) (q:draft, low confidence)
kilawmin = (t:adv) (w:properly/fittingly/decently) (d:kilawm, suitable, with the ending in, often as a kilawmin: in a fitting and proper way) (e:a ~ na gamtat nading zia/sun laitak mah bangin ~ gamta ni | let us behave properly as in the daytime/A ~ thu a dawngthei mihing sagih | seven people who can answer fittingly/thuman, thutang, a ~ a gamtat theih nading | to be able to act truly, justly and properly) (s:kituakin) (a:kilawmlopi-in) (b:kilawm) (r:20.5.2/45.13.13/20.26.16/20.1.3) (q:draft)
kilawmlopi = (t:see) <kilawmlopi-in>
kilawmlopi-in = (t:adv) (w:unjustly/improperly/unfairly) (d:kilawm, suitable, with the negative lo, pi and in: in a way that is not right at all) (e:a ~ hong hih kei un) (a:kilawmin) (r:18.6.29) (q:draft)
kilawmna = (t:n) (w:fittingness/seemliness/beauty) (d:the quality of being fitting or presentable; a kilawmna om lo means it is not fitting) (e:mihaite’ adingin a ~ om lo hi/A ~ nei lo nate in | the parts that have no seemliness/a ~ a meelte zong a mangthang thei hi | its beauty of appearance also perishes/a ~ a om lo mite | people who have no fitness) (b:kilawm) (r:20.26.1/46.12.23/59.1.11/56.1.16) (q:draft)
kilawmpen = (t:adj) (w:most worthy/most suitable/fittest) (d:kilawm, suitable, with pen, most) (e:a hoihpen leh a ~ teelin) (b:kilawm) (r:12.10.3) (q:draft)
kilawmtatna = (t:n) (w:fellowship/friendship) (d:being on friendly terms with someone, with tawh for the other person) (e:kei tungah ~ tawh a khut taklam/Topa tawh ~ in amah a zahtakte’ ading hi | friendship with the Lord is for those who fear him/Kei kiangah ~ tawh keimah huh dingin | to me in friendship to help me) (a:kilangneihna) (r:48.2.9/19.25.14/13.12.17) (q:draft)
kilawmte = (t:n) (w:those who deserve/those who are due/what is fitting) (d:kilawm with the plural te; after a verb with ding, the people or things for whom the action is fitting) (e:Zahtak ding a ~ na zahtak ta un/Kihtak ding a ~ na kihta un | fear those who are due fear/Gentailte tungah uk ding a ~ | those regarded as fit to rule over the Gentiles/nang in na bawl dinga ~ | the things you ought to do) (b:kilawm) (r:45.13.7/41.10.42/57.1.8) (q:draft)
kilawmzah = (t:n) (w:due amount/as much as is fitting) (d:kilawm, fitting, with zah, amount: as much as one deserves or ought) (e:a theih dingin a ~ a thei nai lo/kote’ tuah dinga ~ gimna hong tuaksak loin | not bringing on us the punishment we deserved) (r:46.8.2/15.9.13) (q:draft)
kilawmzaw = (t:adj) (w:more fitting/more proper) (d:kilawm, fitting, with zaw, more: more suitable or right; in questions, how much more ought) (e:ka ngah ding uh ~ hilo ahi hiam/Nang in kei nong tuiphum dingin a ~ kimlai | while it is more fitting for you to baptize me/amah sangin a ~ numei khat | a woman more worthy than she/a sepsak ding uh a ~ ahi hi | it is more fitting that they serve them) (s:taakzaw) (b:kilawm) (r:46.9.12/40.3.14/17.1.19/54.6.2) (q:draft)
kilawmzo = (t:v) (w:be worthy/be fit/deserve) (d:kilawm, worthy, with zo, be able: mostly with a negative, not be worthy to do something) (e:a sutsak ding nangawnin ka ~ kei hi/a kimu dingin zong ~ kisa lo | not considering myself worthy even to meet/a tawisak ding nangawnin ka ~ nai kei hi | I am not yet worthy even to carry them) (b:kilawm) (r:41.1.7/42.7.7/40.3.11) (q:draft)
kilawn = (t:v) (w:be thrown/be cast) (d:lawn, throw, with the passive prefix ki; with suk, be thrown down, and with khia, be thrown out) (e:meiphualpi sungah ~ hi/leitung panin migilote ~ khia-in | the wicked being thrown out of the land/ama lutang hong ~ suk ding hi | his head will be thrown down to you/ninlom lakah hong ~ khia ding hi | you will be thrown out onto the rubbish heap) (s:kipaai) (b:lawn) (r:66.20.15/10.20.21/20.2.22/30.4.3) (q:draft)
kilawng = (t:v) (w:be touched) (d:lawng, touch, with the prefix ki; khut tawh kilawng, be touched with the hand) (e:khut guak tawh amaute ~ ngam lo a/khut tawh a ~ kha thei mei kang mualah | to a burning mountain that can be touched with the hand) (s:kisukkhak) (b:lawng) (r:10.23.6/58.12.18) (q:draft)
kilawnin = (t:v) (w:being thrown/thrown) (d:kilawn, be thrown, with the linking suffix in) (e:meikhuk sungah ~ a kangtum hi) (b:kilawn) (r:43.15.6) (q:draft)
kilawnkeek = (t:v) (w:be thrown down/be torn down) (d:of the stones of a building thrown down so that none is left on another; used with mang) (e:zah dongin ~ mang ding hi) (s:kiphelkeek) (r:40.24.2) (q:draft)
kilawnkhia = (t:v) (w:be thrown out/be cast out/be hurled out) (d:lawnkhia, throw out, with the passive prefix ki: be thrown or driven out) (e:A kithat amau’ mite ~ ding a/hih leitung a ukpa ~ ding hi | the ruler of this world will be thrown out/amah leh a tate ~ a | he and his children are thrown out/ka daantah ni ciangin a ~ ding uh hi | on the day I punish them they will be cast out) (s:kipaaikhia) (b:lawnkhia) (r:23.34.3/24.22.28/43.12.31/24.6.15) (q:draft)
kilawnsuk = (t:v) (w:be thrown down/be hurled down/be cast down) (d:lawnsuk, throw downward, with the passive prefix ki: be thrown down) (e:Hell khuk sungah hong ~ ding hi/a vantung mite tawh leitungah ~ hi | he was thrown down to the earth with his angels/tuipi sungah ~ hi | it was thrown down into the sea/nang kiangah ama lutang hong ~ ding hi | his head will be thrown down to you) (s:kikhiasuk) (b:lawnsuk) (r:40.11.23/66.12.9/66.8.8/10.20.21) (q:draft)
kilawnthal = (t:v) (w:be overthrown/be destroyed) (d:lawnthal, overthrow, with the prefix ki; of cities thrown down) (e:Admah le Zeboiim bangin a ~ gawp) (s:kisusia) (b:lawnthal) (r:5.29.23) (q:draft)
kilawnto = (t:see) <kilawnto-in>
kilawnto-in = (t:v) (w:be thrown up/be tossed up) (d:kilawn, be thrown, with to, up, and the linking ending in; of sailors lifted high by the waves) (e:vanah ~, a thukna-ah kiasuk uh hi) (r:19.107.26) (q:draft)
kileh = (t:v) (w:return/turn back) (d:turn round and go or come back; often followed by kik, back, or hei, around) (e:note kiangah hong ~ kik ta hen/amaute a beitum mateng ka ~ kei hi | I did not turn back until they were destroyed/Khaldea mite hong ~ kikin | the Chaldeans coming back/kei tawh hong ~ kik in | come back with me) (s:kihei/nungkik/ciahkik) (r:40.10.13/10.22.38/24.37.8/9.15.30) (q:draft)
kileh = (t:v) (w:go back and forth/go to and fro) (d:with kawikawi, turn this way and that, of people going about and of hills swaying) (e:Saul kiang panin David ~ kawikawi hi/mualneute ~ kawikawi uh hi | the hills sway to and fro/Jerusalem khua sungah ~ kawikawi un | go up and down through Jerusalem/~ kawikawi ding uh hi | they will go here and there) (r:9.17.15/24.4.24/24.5.1/27.12.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
kilehbulh = (t:v) (w:be contrary/contradict/be opposite) (d:be the opposite of something, used with tawh; here of deeds that go against what is claimed) (e:a gamtatnate uh tawh ~ hi) (s:kilehngat) (r:56.1.16) (q:draft)
kilehbulhin = (t:adv) (w:contrary to/in opposition to) (d:kilehbulh, be contrary, with in; used with tawh) (e:thuman tawh a ~ a gamta mite) (b:kilehbulh) (r:54.1.10) (q:draft)
kilehdo = (t:v) (w:contend with/strive against/rebel against) (d:lehdo, rebel, with the prefix ki; used with tawh) (e:beelseek pa tawh a ~ lei beel) (b:lehdo) (r:23.45.9) (q:draft)
kilehhawl = (t:v) (w:be driven back/be routed) (d:of soldiers beaten and forced to turn back) (e:A galkapte uh ~ a) (r:24.46.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
kilehheek = (t:v) (w:be betrayed/be handed over) (d:lehheek, betray, with the passive prefix ki) (e:migilote’ khut sungah ~ zo hi) (b:lehheek) (r:41.14.41) (q:draft)
kilehhei = (t:v) (w:turn around/turn back/turn about) (d:turn oneself round; often followed by kik, back: turn back from a pursuit or return to a former way) (e:Israel mite hong ~ uh a/amah a delhna panin ~ kik uh hi | they turned back from pursuing him/hong ~ kikin Kareah’ tapa Johanan a beel | turning round, they joined Johanan son of Kareah/mawhna lamah ~ khinzo uh a | they have turned back to sin) (s:kihei/kilehkik) (b:lehhei) (r:7.20.41/14.18.32/24.41.14/24.11.10) (q:draft)
kilehhek = (t:v) (w:be betrayed/betray one another) (d:lehhek, betray, with the prefix ki: be betrayed, or with khatlekhat, betray each other) (e:Topa Jesuh a ~ ding nitakin/khatlekhat kimudahin khatlekhat ~ ding uh hi | they will hate one another and betray one another) (s:kiheek) (b:lehhek) (r:46.11.23/40.24.10) (q:draft)
kilehin = (t:v) (w:return/turn back) (d:kileh, turn back, with the linking ending in: going back and then) (e:~ Jordan gunpang ah ding hi) (b:kileh) (r:12.2.13) (q:draft)
kilehkik = (t:v) (w:return/turn back/come back) (d:kileh with kik, back or again; also of turning back to God) (e:Amah hong ~ nawn kei ding a/kei’ kiangah hong ~ un | return to me/hong ~ nuam lo uh hi | they refuse to return/hehna ~ lo ding hi | the anger will not turn back) (s:ciahkik/kihei/nungkik) (b:kileh) (r:24.22.11/24.4.1/24.8.5/24.23.20) (q:draft)
kilehkiksak = (t:v) (w:make turn back/cause to withdraw) (d:kilehkik, turn back, with the causative sak) (e:amah ~ thei kha ding hi) (b:kilehkik) (r:24.21.2) (q:draft)
kilehngat = (t:v) (w:turn away from/be opposed to/be contrary) (d:face the opposite way from someone or something, used with tawh) (e:Topa tawh a lungsim a ~ mi in/Thukham le Pasian’ thuciamnate a ~ ahi uh hiam | are the Law and the promises of God opposed/na kha nuntakna uh tawh a ~ pumpi’ deihnate | the desires of the body that are against your soul) (s:kilehbulh) (b:lehngat) (r:24.17.5/48.3.21/60.2.11) (q:draft)
kilehngatin = (t:adv) (w:contrary/in opposition/hostilely) (d:facing against someone, used with tawh and pai: walk contrary to, be hostile toward) (e:kei tawh ~ na pai lai uh leh/kei zong note tawh a ~ pai-in | I too will walk contrary to you/note tawh a ~ ka heh ngawh pah ding | in my anger I will turn against you/kei tawh ~ pai-in | walking contrary to me) (s:kilehbulhin) (b:kilehngat) (r:3.26.27/3.26.24/3.26.28/3.26.21) (q:draft)
kilehsuk = (t:v) (w:rush back and forth/go to and fro) (d:kileh, go back and forth, with suk, down; paired with kilehto) (e:kongzing lakah ~ kilehto uh a) (b:kileh) (r:34.2.4) (q:draft)
kilehto = (t:v) (w:rush back and forth/go to and fro) (d:kileh, go back and forth, with to, up; paired with kilehsuk) (e:lakah kilehsuk ~ uh a) (b:kileh) (r:34.2.4) (q:draft)
kilei = (t:v) (w:be bought/be purchased) (d:lei, buy, with the passive prefix ki: be bought; with tawh for the price) (e:kham tawh a ~ zo hi lo a/man tawh a ~ zo mi na hi uh | you are people bought with a price/sum tawh a ~ sila peuhmah | any slave bought with money/Pasian’ hehpihna dangka tawh ~ thei hi | the gift of God can be bought with money) (a:kizuak) (b:lei) (r:18.28.15/46.7.23/2.12.44/44.8.20) (q:draft)
kileikik = (t:v) (w:be bought again) (d:kilei, be bought, with kik, again) (e:hih gamah lo ~ ta ding hi) (b:kilei) (r:24.32.43) (q:draft)
kileina = (t:n) (w:purchase/buying) (d:kilei, be bought, with the noun suffix na: the buying of something; kileina lai is a deed of purchase) (e:Baruk kiangah ~ lai ka piak khit ciangin/tua ~ laite tunga a min uh a gelh | who wrote their names on the deed of purchase) (s:leina) (b:kilei) (r:24.32.16/24.32.12) (q:draft)
kileinapa = (t:n) (w:seller) (d:the man from whom a thing was bought; kileina, purchase, with pa, the male one) (e:a lo pen a ~) (s:zuakpa) (b:kileina) (r:3.27.24) (q:draft)
kileipa = (t:n) (w:bought slave/one who is bought) (d:kilei, be bought, with pa marking a man: a man bought with money, set beside one born in the household) (e:na sum tawh a ~ hita leh) (b:kilei) (r:1.17.13) (q:draft)
kileitawi = (t:v) (w:lend to one another) (d:leitawi, loan, with the reciprocal prefix ki: lend to each other, as in khatlekhat kileitawi) (e:ngahkik dingin khatlekhat ~ uh hi) (b:leitawi) (r:42.6.34) (q:draft)
kileizo = (t:v) (w:can be bought) (d:kilei, be bought, with zo, be able: used with hi lo for what cannot be bought at any price) (e:kham tawh a ~ hi lo a/Ofir kham tawh pilna a ~ hi lo | wisdom cannot be bought with the gold of Ophir/suangmanpha pen tawh zong a ~ hi tuan lo | nor can it be bought with precious stones) (s:leizawh) (b:kilei) (r:18.28.15/18.28.16) (q:draft)
kilelsak = (t:v) (w:let oneself be defeated/pretend to be beaten) (d:lelsak, defeat, with the reflexive prefix ki: let oneself be beaten; with khem, deceive, pretend to be beaten in order to draw the enemy out) (e:amau mai-ah ~ khem uh a/gamlak lamah tai-in a ~ khemte | those who pretended to be beaten and fled toward the wilderness) (b:lelsak) (r:6.8.15/6.8.20) (q:draft)
kilem = (t:v) (w:be at peace/be reconciled/make peace) (d:be on good terms with one another, not at war or in a quarrel; used with tawh for the other party, and kilem nading thu is an offer of peace) (e:mi khempeuh tawh na ~ un/Pasian tawh ~ in la | be at peace with God/Solomon le Hiram ~ uh a | Solomon and Hiram were at peace/Kido hun om a, ~ hun om hi | there is a time for war and a time for peace/~ nading thu gen un | make an offer of peace) (a:kido/kigal) (r:45.12.18/40.5.24/18.22.21/11.5.12/21.3.8/5.20.10) (q:draft)
kilemin = (t:v) (w:at peace/reconciled/in peace) (d:kilem, be at peace, with the linking ending in: being at peace or reconciled with someone, mostly before om, live) (e:khat leh khat ~ om un/a pasal tawh ~ omkik hen | let her be reconciled to her husband/kithutuakin ~ na semkhawm ding uh hi | they will work together in agreement and peace/Pasian tawh ~ pawlkhatin na om nadingun | so that you may be at peace and one with God) (b:kilem) (r:41.9.50/46.7.11/38.6.13/47.5.20) (q:draft)
kilemkik = (t:v) (w:be reconciled/be at peace again) (d:kilem, be at peace, with kik, again or back: be at peace again after a quarrel or enmity; used with tawh for the other party) (e:amah tawh ~ theih nading hong omsak/Pasian tawh a ~ ta ihi hi | we are now reconciled with God/a ~ ding uh ka thum nuam hi | I plead with them to be reconciled/kei hong langpang mite tawh ka ~ theih nadingin | so that I might be reconciled with the people who oppose me) (b:kilem) (r:51.1.20/45.5.1/50.4.2/45.10.21) (q:draft)
kilemkim = (t:v) (w:be in harmony together/agree all alike) (d:of the parts of the body all being at one with each other, where the English has have equal concern for each other) (e:a vekpi-in a ~ uh hi) (r:46.12.25) (q:draft, low confidence)
kilemlo = (t:v) (w:be at odds/not be at peace/oppose) (d:kilem, be at peace, with the negative lo: be against someone, used with tawh; the English has resist) (e:migilote tawh ~ uh hi) (a:kilem) (b:kilem) (r:20.28.4) (q:draft)
kilemlohna = (t:n) (w:hostility/enmity/discord) (d:the state of not being at peace with one another; kilemlohna bawl is rebel, and kilemlohna that is put an end to hostility) (e:Khazih in singlamteh hangin ~ thatin/~ bawlin a hehsak mite kua ahi hiam | who were those who rebelled and made him angry) (s:kilangneihna/kigalneihna/galneihna) (a:kilemna) (r:49.2.16/58.3.16) (q:draft)
kilemna = (t:n) (w:atonement/reconciliation) (d:kilem, be at peace, with the noun suffix na: the putting right of people with God, by sacrifice in the law and through Christ in the letters; kilemna bawl is make atonement) (e:note adingin ~ bawl nadingin keel a pa khat/siampipa in amau adingin ~ bawl sak ding hi | the priest shall make atonement for them/Biakna tau adingin ni sagih sung ~ bawlin | making atonement for the altar for seven days/~ ka va bawl thei kha ding hi | perhaps I can make atonement/tua ~ thu tawh kipawl nasepna | the ministry of reconciliation) (s:mawhphelna) (b:kilem) (r:4.28.30/4.28.22/3.4.20/2.29.37/2.32.30/47.5.18) (q:draft)
kilemna = (t:n) (w:peace) (d:being on good terms after or instead of fighting, often as gal kilemna; kilemna bawl is make peace) (e:Israel kumpipa tawh zong ~ bawl hi/Gal ~ a deih lo mite lakah | among those who do not want peace/amaute in kei tawh ~ bawl-in | let them make peace with me/gal ~ a ngaihsun mi ka hi hi | I am a man who seeks peace) (s:gallemna/galdaihna) (a:kidona/kilemlohna) (b:kilem) (r:11.22.44/19.120.6/23.27.5/19.120.7) (q:draft)
kilemsa = (t:see) <kilemsa-in>
kilemsa-in = (t:adv) (w:reconciled/at peace) (d:kilem, be at peace, with sa, already, and the ending in: having been put right with someone; the English has justified) (e:Pasian tawh a ~ a inn-ah ciah) (r:42.18.14) (q:draft)
kilemsak = (t:v) (w:reconcile/make peace between) (d:kilem, be at peace, with the causative sak: bring two parties back to peace, often followed by kik, again; hong kilemsak is he reconciled us) (e:tapate leh pate lemtuahin ~ kik ding hi/Pasian in Khazih hangin amah tawh hong ~ a | God reconciled us to himself through Christ/Mi kitawng ~ kik theite | those who can reconcile people who quarrel/ama Tapa’ sihna hangin amah tawh hong ~ | he reconciled us to himself through the death of his Son) (b:kilem) (r:39.4.6/47.5.18/40.5.9/45.5.10) (q:draft)
kilemsakkik = (t:v) (w:reconcile/bring back to peace) (d:kilemsak, reconcile, with kik, again; of the one who makes peace between two parties) (e:Pasian le mite a hong ~ thei/pate le tate lemtuahin a ~ ding hi | he will reconcile fathers and children) (b:kilemsak) (r:54.2.5/39.4.6) (q:draft)
kilemsakkikin = (t:v) (w:reconciling/bringing back to peace) (d:kilemsakkik, reconcile, with the linking suffix in) (e:Pate le tate ~) (b:kilemsakkik) (r:42.1.17) (q:draft)
kilemsakna = (t:n) (w:reconciliation) (d:kilemsak, reconcile, with the noun suffix na) (e:tua ~ thu kote hong pia hi) (s:kilemna/gallemna) (b:kilemsak) (r:47.5.19) (q:draft)
kilemte = (t:adj) (w:at peace/secure) (d:kilem, be at peace, with the plural te: gam kilemte are lands that are at peace and feel secure) (e:gam ~ nangawn a sim ding hi) (b:kilem) (r:27.11.24) (q:draft, low confidence)
kilen = (t:v) (w:hold one another/embrace) (d:len, hold, with the reciprocal prefix ki) (e:khatlekhat ~ kikawi-in a kap uh hi) (s:kikawi) (b:len) (r:44.20.37) (q:draft)
kilenin = (t:v) (w:holding/being held) (d:kilen with the linking suffix in; a khut kilenin is holding him by the hand) (e:a khut ~ a paipih dingin) (b:kilen) (r:44.13.11) (q:draft)
kilenkhiatsak = (t:v) (w:be blown away/be driven away) (d:of smoke made to fly off) (e:Meikhu a ~ bangin amaute hawlkhia ding) (r:19.68.2) (q:draft)
kilensa = (t:see) <kilensa-in>
kilensa-in = (t:v) (w:holding one another/hand in hand) (d:len, hold, with the reciprocal prefix ki, sa for a completed action and the linking ending in; khut kilensa-in, holding hands) (e:a lawmpa tawh khut ~) (r:22.8.5) (q:draft)
kiletna = (t:n) (w:handshake/clasping of hands) (d:found in khut kiletna, the giving of the hand to one another as a sign of fellowship) (e:Barnabas tawh khut ~ hong bawl uh) (r:48.2.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
kilh = (t:v) (w:nail/fasten) (d:fasten something with nails so that it cannot be moved) (e:sik tawh a ~ uh hi) (s:khen) (r:24.10.4) (q:draft)
kilhcip = (t:v) (w:nail fast/crucify) (d:kilh, nail, with cip, tightly; singlamteh tungah kilhcip is nail to the cross) (e:singlamteh tungah Jesuh ~ uh a/Jesuh’ taklamah khat, a veilamah khat ~ uh hi | they crucified one on his right and one on his left) (s:khencip) (b:kilh) (r:42.23.33) (q:draft)
kilhcipin = (t:v) (w:nailing/nailing fast) (d:kilhcip, nail fast, with the linking suffix in) (e:singlamteh tungah ~ a beisak ta hi) (b:kilhcip) (r:51.2.14) (q:draft)
kilhna = (t:n) (w:clasp/hook/fastener) (d:kilh, fasten, with the noun suffix na: a small hook or pin that holds two pieces together, as the gold and bronze clasps of the tabernacle curtains) (e:kham ~ sawmnga bawlin/sumngo ~ sawmnga bawlin | make fifty bronze clasps/amah in ~ sawmnga sumngo tawh bawl hi | he made fifty clasps of bronze) (b:kilh) (r:2.36.13/2.26.6/2.26.11/2.36.18) (q:draft)
kilhnate = (t:n) (w:clasps/hooks/nails) (d:kilhna, fastener, with the plural te: the clasps that join the tabernacle curtains, and in one verse the nails of the temple) (e:~ tawh puante khat leh khat kimatsak hi/a bilvangte sungah ~ guangin | put the clasps into the loops/A ~-ah dalna puan khai sukin | hang the curtain from the clasps/A ~ a gihna in kham shekel sawmnga | the weight of the nails was fifty shekels of gold) (b:kilhna) (r:2.36.13/14.3.9/2.26.11/2.26.33) (q:draft)
kiliah = (t:v) (w:be hidden/be concealed) (d:liah, cover or hide, with the passive prefix ki: be out of sight or kept from someone, with kiang pan or mai-ah for the one it is hidden from) (e:nangma kiang pan ~ lo hi/Mual dawnah a om khua ~ zo lo hi | a town on a hilltop cannot be hidden/ka guh ka taang, na mai-ah ~ lo hi | my bones were not hidden from you/keima lampi ~ a | my way is hidden/i maitang hong ~ nawn loin | our faces no longer being covered) (s:kiseel/kibu) (a:kilang) (b:liah) (r:19.69.5/40.5.14/19.139.15/23.40.27/47.3.18) (q:draft)
kiliahin = (t:v) (w:being hidden/being covered) (d:kiliah, be hidden, with the linking suffix in; of the light of understanding, where the English has darkened) (e:pilna khuavak ~ Pasian’ nuntakna tawh) (b:kiliah) (r:49.4.18) (q:draft)
kiliahna = (t:n) (w:veil/covering/screen) (d:kiliah, be covered, with the noun suffix na: something that screens or hides; kiliahna puan is a veil over the face) (e:~ puan tawh a maitang khuhkik hi/a maitang-ah ~ puan khat koih hi | he put a veil over his face/a ~ puan a lakhia hi | he took off his veil/a ~ puan a kilakhia pan ahi hi | only then is the veil taken away) (s:khuhna/dalna) (b:kiliah) (r:2.34.35/2.34.33/47.3.16/47.3.14) (q:draft)
kiliamsak = (t:v) (w:hurt one another/harm/be wounded) (d:liamsak, wound, with the prefix ki: with khat leh khat, hurt one another; of one person, be wounded) (e:khat leh khat ~ lo ding uh a/eite’ khialhna hangin amah ~ a | he was wounded for our transgressions/amaute ~ lo, kisusia lo ding uh hi | they will neither harm nor destroy) (b:liamsak) (r:23.11.9/23.53.5/23.65.25) (q:draft)
kilian = (t:v) (w:make oneself great/be haughty) (d:lian, great, with the reflexive prefix ki: found in kilian sak, exalt oneself or be arrogant, and kilian ngaihsut, think oneself great) (e:~ sakin a kiphasak mite ahi/~ ngaihsutzaw kha kei un | do not think of yourselves too highly) (s:kiphasak/kihisak) (a:kiniamkhiat) (b:lian) (r:20.21.24/45.12.3) (q:draft)
kiliansak = (t:v) (w:exalt oneself/be proud/be haughty/be exalted) (d:liansak, make great, with the prefix ki: make oneself great, be proud or set oneself up against someone; of a name or a kingdom, be made great) (e:Topa dem-in ~ uh hi/ka lungsim ~ nawn lo a | my heart is no longer proud/amah in Topa langpanin ~ hi | he has exalted himself against the Lord/Ka mihingte’ tungah nang ~ lai-in | you still exalt yourself over my people/nangma min ~ tawntung ding a | your name will be great forever) (s:kiphasak/kihisak/kisathei) (a:kiniamkhiat/kiniamsak) (b:liansak) (r:24.48.42/19.131.1/24.48.26/2.9.17/10.7.26) (q:draft)
kiliansakin = (t:v) (w:exalting oneself/being haughty) (d:kiliansak, exalt oneself, with the linking suffix in: putting oneself forward, behaving haughtily) (e:Haggith’ tapa Adonijah amahmah ~/~ a kiphasak mite ahi hi | they are people who are haughty and proud) (b:kiliansak) (r:11.1.5/24.48.29/20.21.24) (q:draft)
Kiliansakin = (t:name) (w:Kiliansakin) (d:the verb kiliansakin, exalting oneself, written with a capital at the start of a sentence; not a proper name) (r:24.48.29)
kiliansakte = (t:n) (w:those who exalt themselves/the proud) (d:kiliansak, exalt oneself, with the plural te: people who make themselves great, usually as a kiliansakte) (e:A ~ khempeuh in niamkhiatna thuak ding/Kei tunga hong ~ | those who exalt themselves over me/a ~ pen kiniamkhiatsuk ding a | those who exalt themselves will be humbled) (s:kiphasakte/kihisakte/kisatheite) (a:kiniamkhiatte) (b:kiliansak) (r:40.23.12/19.35.26/42.18.14) (q:draft)
kiliatsak = (t:v) (w:exalt oneself/be lifted up) (d:liatsak, make great, with the reflexive prefix ki; of the heart being lifted up over others) (e:ama lungsim a ~ loh nading/ama lungsim a ~ toh loh nading | so that his heart is not lifted up) (s:kiliansak/kiphasak) (a:kiniamkhiat) (b:liatsak) (r:5.17.19/5.17.20) (q:draft)
kiliatsakna = (t:n) (w:arrogance/pride/haughtiness) (d:kiliatsak, exalt oneself, with the noun suffix na: thinking oneself great and looking down on others) (e:Mite’ ~ kiniamkhiat ding a/~ tawh sucip dingin mi tawng uh hi | with arrogance they threaten oppression/a kisatheite’ ~ ka niamkhiat ding hi | I will humble the arrogance of the proud/~ lungsim a nei mite a thehthang hi | he has scattered those who are proud in heart) (s:kiphatsakna/kihihsakna/kisaktheihna) (a:kiniamkhiatna/kiniamsakna) (b:kiliatsak) (r:23.2.17/19.73.8/23.13.11/42.1.51) (q:draft)
kiliin = (t:v) (w:sway/shake/tremble) (d:liin, tremble, with the prefix ki; of a reed moving in the water) (e:tui sunga pumpeng a ~’ mah bangin | like a reed swaying in the water) (s:kiliing/kiling) (b:liin) (r:11.14.15) (q:draft)
kiliing = (t:v) (w:shake/tremble/quake) (d:liing, tremble, with the prefix ki: shake or be shaken, of the earth, mountains, the powers of heaven or the heart) (e:Topa mai-ah mualte ~ hi/leitung a ~ ding hi | the earth will tremble/Amah ~ lo taktak ding a | he will surely never be shaken/vanah a om vangliatnate a ~ ding uh hi | the powers in the heavens will be shaken/amah leh a mihingte’ lungsim ~ hi | his heart and the hearts of his people shook) (s:kiling/liing/kilok) (a:kip) (b:liing) (r:7.5.5/19.112.6/24.49.21/41.13.25/23.7.2) (q:draft)
kiliingsak = (t:v) (w:shake/make tremble) (d:kiliing, shake, with the causative sak) (e:kumpi gamte ~ gawp hi) (s:kilingsak/lingsak) (b:kiliing) (r:23.23.11) (q:draft)
Kilikia = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Cilicia) (d:Roman province on the south-east coast of Asia Minor, whose chief city was Tarsus, the home town of Paul) (r:48.1.21/44.6.9)
kilikkhia = (t:v) (w:be rolled away) (d:likkhia, roll away, with the passive prefix ki: of the stone rolled off from the opening of the tomb) (e:Han vang pan suang ~ a/tua suangpi ~ a, om a mu uh hi | they saw that the large stone had been rolled away/hankhuk kihukna suangtum a ~ khin a mu hi | she saw that the stone covering the tomb had been rolled away) (b:likkhia) (r:42.24.2/41.16.4/43.20.1) (q:draft)
kilim = (t:todo) (q:draft, found only in thupha hong kilim piak, be blessed, Deuteronomy 7.14; what kilim adds is not clear)
kilin = (t:v) (w:shake/quake/sway) (d:short form of kiling, written kilin with an apostrophe before the next word) (e:a tunga teengte khempeuh a ~’ ciangin/tui sunga pumpeeng a ~’ mah bangin | like a reed swaying in the water/a ~’ theih nadingin | so that they shake) (s:kiling/kiliing) (r:19.75.3/11.14.15/30.9.1) (q:draft)
kiling = (t:v) (w:be shaken/be moved/shake) (d:be made to shake or lose firmness, of the earth, a mountain, a building or a person; ka kiling kei ding is I will not be shaken) (e:ka ~ kei ding hi/leitung bulpite khempeuh ~ hi | all the foundations of the earth are shaken/a mual buppi nakpitakin ~ hi | the whole mountain shook violently/Misite’ gam ~ a | the realm of the dead trembles/Ka ~ ngei kei ding hi | I will never be shaken) (s:kiliing/kilok/liing) (a:kip) (r:19.16.8/19.96.10/19.82.5/2.19.18/18.26.5/19.30.6) (q:draft)
kilinggawp = (t:v) (w:be shaken violently/be shaken/quake) (d:kiling, be shaken, with gawp, thoroughly: be shaken violently) (e:vantung bulpite ~ hi/amaute’ kikhopna mun hong ~ hi | the place where they were meeting was shaken/leitung bulpite khempeuh a ~ hi | all the foundations of the earth are shaken) (s:kilokgawp) (b:kiling) (r:10.22.8/44.4.31/19.82.5) (q:draft)
kilingin = (t:v) (w:tremble/shake) (d:kiling, be shaken, with the linking ending in; of the earth trembling) (e:a et ciangin tua leitung ~/Leitung a et ciangin tua lei ~ | when he looks at the earth it trembles) (b:kiling) (r:19.104.31) (q:draft)
kilingsak = (t:v) (w:shake/cause to shake/let be shaken) (d:kiling, be shaken, with the causative sak: make something shake, or let someone be shaken; a kilingsak zo lo is that cannot be shaken) (e:biakinn kongkhak khuam bulpite ~ a/a ~ zo lo Pasian’ gam | the kingdom of God that cannot be shaken/thumante cik mahin a ~ ngei kei ding hi | he will never let the righteous be shaken/a ~ lo nate kip lai ding | the things that are not shaken will remain) (s:lingsak/kiliingsak) (b:lingsak) (r:23.6.4/58.12.28/19.55.22/58.12.27) (q:draft)
kilingsakin = (t:v) (w:being shaken) (d:kilingsak, cause to shake, with the linking suffix in) (e:a kipiangsak nate ~ kipaikhia ding a) (b:kilingsak) (r:58.12.27) (q:draft)
kilkel = (t:adv) (d:intensifier after a descriptive word, with the sense of clear, fresh or gleaming: siang kilkel is perfectly clear, vot kilkel is cool and clear, hing kilkel is fresh and green, kipuah kilkel is polished bright) (e:a vot ~ luite kang ngei/lopano a hing ~ tawh kibang ding hi | will be like fresh green grass/hoih takin kipuah ~ hi | it is polished until it gleams/Kristal suangmanpha bangin siang ~ hi | it is as clear as crystal/limlang bangin siang ~ hi | it is as clear as glass) (r:24.18.14/23.66.14/26.21.9/66.21.11/66.21.18) (q:draft, low confidence)
kilo = (t:v) (w:be called/be named/be mentioned) (d:of a name, be spoken or used: min kilo is the name is called or mentioned, min tawh a kilo is called by the name of, and a min-a kilo is mentioned by name) (e:a min ~ kha nawn lo ding hi/ka min tawh a ~ biakinn sung | in the temple that bears my name/amau’ sanggamte’ min tawh amaute ~ ding hi | they will be called by the names of their brothers/Isaak tawh na suan-le-khakte’ min ~ ding hi | through Isaac your offspring will be named/a min-a ~ hih khuapite | these towns mentioned by name) (s:kici) (r:28.2.17/24.32.34/1.48.6/1.21.12/13.6.65) (q:draft)
kiloh = (t:v) (w:be paid/be repaid) (d:loh, pay off, with the passive prefix ki; kiloh sak is make someone pay) (e:azah sagih-in ~ sak a) (b:loh) (r:20.6.31) (q:draft)
kilohsak = (t:v) (w:be made to pay/be made to repay) (d:lohsak, pay for, with the passive prefix ki) (e:a zah sagihin ~ a) (b:lohsak) (r:20.6.31) (q:draft)
kilok = (t:v) (w:be shaken/be tossed/quake/be rough) (d:be moved to and fro, of the earth quaking or of water stirred up by the wind; tui kilok is a wave or rough water) (e:nung ahih ciangin tui a ~ hi/leitung kip a, ~ ngei lo ding hi | the earth is firm and will never be moved/tui nakpi-in ~ a | the water was very rough/a ~ tuipi tawh kibang uh hi | they are like the tossing sea/leitung kisingin ~ a | the earth trembled and quaked) (s:kiling/kiliing/kising) (a:kip) (b:lok) (r:43.6.18/13.16.30/40.14.24/23.57.20/10.22.8) (q:draft)
kilokgawp = (t:v) (w:be shaken violently/be tossed about) (d:lokgawp, shake violently, with the passive prefix ki: of the earth, a boat or water thrown about by wind or earthquake) (e:Leitung khangkhamin ~ ding a/tui hong ~ hi | the water grew rough/gunkuang a ~ hi | the boat was tossed about/nakpitakin ~ a, vantung bulpite kilinggawp hi | it quaked violently and the foundations of the heavens shook) (s:kilinggawp) (b:lokgawp) (r:23.24.19/43.6.18/40.14.24/10.22.8) (q:draft)
kilokha = (t:v) (w:be mentioned/be invoked/be called on) (d:kilo, be named, with kha: of a name being spoken at all; with nawn lo, never be mentioned again) (e:a min ~ nawn lo ding hi) (r:28.2.17) (q:draft)
kilokhia = (t:v) (w:be designated/be called out) (d:kilo, be named, with khia, out; a minin a kilokhia, singled out by name) (e:a minin a ~ midang omlai hi/tuate khempeuh a minin a ~ ahi hi | all of them were designated by name) (b:kilo) (r:13.16.41/15.10.16) (q:draft)
kilokna = (t:n) (w:surge/current/tossing) (d:kilok, be tossed, with the noun suffix na; tui kilokna is moving water, a current or surf) (e:Tui ~ nih kituahna mun) (b:kilok) (r:44.27.41) (q:draft)
kiloksak = (t:v) (w:stir up/trouble/shake) (d:kilok, be shaken, with the causative sak; of stirring the water of a pool) (e:zel a, tui a ~ hi) (b:kilok) (r:43.5.4) (q:draft)
kilokzo = (t:v) (w:can be shaken) (d:kilok, be shaken, with zo, be able; with ngei lo, can never be shaken) (e:a phuhsa sutpi ~ ngei lo ding) (b:kilok) (r:55.2.19) (q:draft)
kilomin = (t:v) (w:huddle together/crowd together) (d:of people gathered close in a heap; compare lom, heap) (e:sawlkawm nuai-ah ~ omkhawm uh hi) (b:lomin) (r:18.30.7) (q:draft)
kilong = (t:v) (w:come off/be detached/be dislocated) (d:of an arm coming away from the shoulder, with khia, out) (e:ka liang bul panin ~ khia ta) (r:18.31.22) (q:draft)
kilongkhia = (t:v) (w:come off/fall out of joint) (d:kilong with khia, out; of an arm coming away from the shoulder) (e:ka liang bul panin ~ tahen) (b:kilong) (r:18.31.22) (q:draft)
kilosa = (t:adj) (w:named/specified) (d:kilo, be named, with sa, already done; a min kilosa, whose names have been called) (e:a min ~ hih mite khawmin) (b:kilo) (r:4.1.17) (q:draft)
kilote = (t:n) (w:those called/those named) (d:kilo, be called or named, with plural te: those whose names are given, those called by a name) (e:keima min tawh a ~ khempeuh/Hih min ~ khempeuhte | all these who are listed by name) (s:kicite) (b:kilo) (r:23.43.6/13.9.9) (q:draft)
kiluah = (t:v) (w:be inherited/be passed down) (d:passive of luah, inherit: property comes down from parents or from one generation to the next) (e:pate tung panin a ~ hi a/khang khat pan khang khatah a ~ suksuk ding | to be passed down from generation to generation) (b:luah) (r:20.19.14/26.44.28) (q:draft)
kiluan = (t:v) (w:be poured/flow) (d:ki with luan, a form of luang flow: of molten gold poured for an image; in Joel 2:30 of blood being shed) (e:kham a ~, a kisung na milimte/sisan ~’ sakna, meikatna | bloodshed and fire) (b:luan) (r:23.30.22/29.2.30) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiluangkhiasak = (t:v) (w:be drained/be made to flow out) (d:luangkhiasak, make flow out, with the passive prefix ki; of the blood of a slaughtered animal) (e:a si ~ loin gawlmek a kigo) (b:luangkhiasak) (r:44.21.25) (q:draft)
kiluansak = (t:v) (w:be shed/be poured out) (d:kiluan, flow, with the causative sak; of blood) (e:sisan a ~ khit ciang bekin) (b:kiluan) (r:58.9.22) (q:draft)
kiluansakna = (t:n) (w:shedding/flowing) (d:with sisan, blood: sisan kiluansakna is bloodshed, where the English has only blood) (e:Sisan ~, meikatna le meikhu sahpi/sisan ~, meikatna le meikhu lompi | bloodshed, fire and billows of smoke) (b:kiluansak) (r:44.2.19/29.2.30) (q:draft)
kiluh = (t:v) (w:be plundered/be ransacked/be looted) (d:luh, plunder, with the passive prefix ki: of a city, houses or people stripped by raiders; often followed by gawp, thoroughly) (e:innte ~ gawpin/Jerusalem khuapi ~ gawpin | the city of Jerusalem will be plundered/ama mite pen a ~, a kisut mite hi a | his people are a people plundered and looted) (s:kisut/kibuluh) (b:luh) (r:38.14.2/23.42.22/38.14.1) (q:draft)
kiluhgawp = (t:v) (w:be plundered/be ravaged/be sacked) (d:kiluh, be plundered, with gawp marking a thorough or violent action) (e:Khaldea gam ~ ding a/a kisusia, a ~, a kinusiacip khuapite | the cities that were ruined, plundered and deserted) (b:kiluh) (r:24.50.10/26.36.35) (q:draft)
kiluhin = (t:v) (w:be plundered/be looted) (d:kiluh, be plundered, with the linking ending in) (e:inn ~, a zite uh kibuansak ding hi) (b:kiluh) (r:23.13.16) (q:draft)
kilui = (t:v) (w:be served/be set before) (d:lui, serve food, with the passive prefix ki: of food, be laid out in front of someone to eat, with mai-ah, before) (e:nek dingin a mai-ah an ~ hi/na mai uhah hong ~ khempeuh | whatever is set before you/a kisiit pen nang mai-ah hong ~ hi | what was kept has been set before you/Amau’ mai-a ~ ante | the food set before them) (r:1.24.33/46.10.27/9.9.24/19.69.22) (q:draft)
kilukham = (t:v) (w:be laid under the head/be used as a pillow) (d:lukham, pillow, with the prefix ki; of the swords of buried warriors, with sak) (e:a namsau uh ~ sakin) (b:lukham) (r:26.32.27) (q:draft)
kilukhamsakin = (t:v) (w:having laid under the head) (d:kilukham with the causative sak and the linking suffix in) (e:a namsau uh ~) (b:kilukham) (r:26.32.27) (q:draft)
kilukhuhsa = (t:see) <kilukhuhsa-in>
kilukhuhsa-in = (t:v) (w:with head covered/having covered the head) (d:lu, head, and khuh, cover, with the reflexive prefix ki, sa for a completed action and the linking ending in; a sign of grief or shame) (e:Haman ahih leh ~ a thuum kawmin) (r:17.6.12) (q:draft)
kilumlet = (t:v) (w:be overthrown/be overturned) (d:lumlet, overturn, with the passive prefix ki; gam kilumlet is an uprising in the land) (e:gam ~ nading thu ahi zongin) (b:lumlet) (r:42.21.9) (q:draft)
kilumletin = (t:v) (w:be overturned/overturn) (d:kilumlet, be turned over, with the linking ending in; of a tent knocked over) (e:puanbuk ~ lei lakah kiphah hi) (b:kilumlet) (r:7.7.13) (q:draft)
kilumletsak = (t:v) (w:turn upside down/throw into disorder) (d:kilumlet, be overturned, with the causative sak) (e:gam khempeuh a ~ hih mite in) (b:kilumlet) (r:44.17.6) (q:draft)
kilumsak = (t:v) (w:be made to lie down/be laid down to sleep) (d:lumsak, make lie down, with the passive prefix ki) (e:galkap nih kikalah ~ a) (b:lumsak) (r:44.12.6) (q:draft)
kilung = (t:v) (d:lung, heart or mind, with the reciprocal prefix ki; found with tuak: kilung tuak is be of one mind with one another) (e:khat leh khat ~ tuakin na om) (b:lung) (r:45.15.6) (q:draft)
kilungdamsak = (t:v) (w:be pleased/be made glad/rejoice) (d:lungdamsak, make glad, with the prefix ki: of God, be pleased; of a person, make oneself glad, rejoice) (e:Upna loin Pasian ~ zo lo hi/kiniamsakna a thuakna ah ~ thei ta hen | let him be glad in his humiliation) (b:lungdamsak) (r:58.11.6/59.1.10) (q:draft)
kilunggim = (t:v) (w:be troubled/lose heart) (d:lunggim, be troubled, with the prefix ki; kilunggim sak kei in is do not let yourself be troubled) (e:ahih manin ~ sak kei in) (b:lunggim) (r:23.7.4) (q:draft)
kilunggimsak = (t:v) (w:trouble oneself/make oneself anxious) (d:lunggimsak, make heavy in heart, with the reflexive prefix ki) (e:Note ~ kei un la) (s:kilungkhamsak) (b:lunggimsak) (r:21.11.10) (q:draft)
kilunggulh = (t:v) (w:lust for one another/desire one another) (d:lunggulh, desire, with the reciprocal prefix ki: desire one another sexually; kilunggulh luatna, too much desire of woman and man for each other, is lust) (e:khat leh khat ~ uh a/nu leh pa ~ luatna | excessive desire of man and woman for each other) (b:lunggulh) (r:45.1.27/51.3.5) (q:draft)
kilunggulhna = (t:n) (w:lust/desire for one another) (d:kilunggulh, desire one another, with the noun suffix na; of sexual desire) (e:pasal le pasal ~ ciang dong/~ hang bek tawh a pumpi uh a zat | using their bodies only out of lust) (b:kilunggulh) (r:65.1.7/52.4.4) (q:draft)
kilunghimawh = (t:v) (w:worry/be troubled) (d:lunghimawh, worry, with the prefix ki used without a named subject: one has worry or sorrow) (e:Pil semsem lehang ~ semsem a) (b:lunghimawh) (r:21.1.18) (q:draft)
kilungkhamsak = (t:v) (w:distress oneself/be upset) (d:lungkhamsak, make troubled, with the reflexive prefix ki; with kei in, do not let yourself be troubled) (e:Hih thu hangin nangmah ~ kei in) (s:kilunggimsak) (b:lungkhamsak) (r:10.11.25) (q:draft)
kilungkim = (t:v) (w:be content with one another/be satisfied with each other) (d:lungkim, be satisfied, with the reciprocal prefix ki; with lo, have a grievance against one another) (e:khatlekhat a ~ lo na om uh) (b:lungkim) (r:51.3.13) (q:draft)
kilungnemsak = (t:v) (w:be humbled/be made low) (d:lungnemsak, make gentle or lowly in heart, with the passive prefix ki: be brought low, where the English has in his humiliation) (e:A ~ lai takin midangte in) (r:44.8.33) (q:draft, low confidence)
kilungnuamsak = (t:v) (w:comfort oneself/set one's mind at ease) (d:lungnuamsak, make glad or at ease, with the reflexive prefix ki) (e:Bangbang hitaleh ~ in, ka sanggamnu aw) (b:lungnuamsak) (r:10.13.20) (q:draft)
kilungsim = (t:n) (w:ill will/malice) (d:found in kilungsim neihna, holding something in the heart against one another, where the English has malice) (e:kitotna, kikona, ~ neihna khempeuh beisak) (r:49.4.31) (q:draft, low confidence)
kilungso = (t:v) (w:fret/be vexed) (d:lungso, be hot in heart, with the reflexive prefix ki: work oneself into anger or worry; found in kilungso tawmsak, make oneself fret) (e:Nangmah ~ tawmsak ke’n/siatna a bawlpa tungah nangmah ~ tawmsak kei in | do not fret over the one who does evil) (b:lungso) (r:19.37.8/19.37.7) (q:draft)
kilungsosak = (t:v) (w:fret/vex oneself) (d:kilungso fret, with the causative sak: make oneself angry or worried) (e:nangmah ~ kei in la) (b:kilungso) (r:19.37.1/19.37.8) (q:draft)
kilungtuak = (t:v) (w:agree together/be of one mind/conspire) (d:lung, mind, and tuak, agree, with the reciprocal prefix ki: be of the same mind with one another to do something, here to do wrong) (e:bang hangin ~ na hi uh hiam) (s:kithukhat/kithukim/kithutuak) (r:44.5.9) (q:draft)
kilup = (t:v) (w:be lain with/be ravished) (d:Lup, lie down, with the prefix ki; kilup khoppih means be lain with, in the sense of sexual intercourse.) (e:Hong ~ khoppih lohna mun) (b:lup) (r:24.3.2) (q:draft)
kilutpih = (t:v) (w:be brought in/be taken in) (d:Passive of lutpih, bring in, with the prefix ki: be carried or brought into a place, said of goods taken into a town.) (e:khua sungah van hong ~ loh nadingin) (s:kitumpih) (b:lutpih) (r:16.13.19) (q:draft)
kilutsak = (t:v) (w:be let in/be admitted/be welcomed in) (d:Passive of lutsak, let in, with the prefix ki: be allowed to enter or be received into a place.) (e:kongpi-ah kuamah ~ lo ahih manin/tawntung nuntakna inn-ah hong ~ theih nadingin | so that you may be welcomed into eternal dwellings) (b:lutsak) (r:17.4.2/42.16.9) (q:draft)
kim = (t:n) (w:surroundings/area around) (d:The area round about a person or place; kim-ah or kim-a after a noun means around it, as in khua kim, the country round a town.) (e:Mite nangma ~-ah kikhawmsak in la/Amah a zahtakte’ ~-ah | around those who fear him/hih khuapite’ ~-a om khua neute khempeuh | all the villages around these towns/a ~-a ama galte khempeuh panin | from all his enemies around him) (s:paam) (r:19.7.7/19.34.7/6.19.8/10.7.1) (q:draft)
kim = (t:adv) (w:every/all/fully) (d:Placed after a noun or verb: all of them without exception, each one, or the action done in full.) (e:khialhna nam ~ na tang un/a vekpi-in tung ~ hi | every one of them came true/tua bangin na bawl ~ ding hi | you shall do so for each one/Ka na khempeuh na zawt ~ khit hangin | now that you have searched through all my goods/misia, mipha, hong encik ~ hi | he keeps watch on all, the wicked and the good) (s:vekpi/vekin) (r:52.5.22/46.12.26/6.21.45/4.15.12/1.31.37/20.15.3) (q:draft)
kim = (t:n) (w:half/middle/part) (d:The middle or half of something: zan kim lai is the middle of the night, kim ciang is halfway up, and kim khat is a part of or some of.) (e:zan ~ lai takin amah tho-in/Van ~ lai-ah ni khawlin | the sun stopped in the middle of the sky/biakna tau ~ ciang a bat suk theih nadingin | so that it reaches halfway up the altar/a khuampeek ~ ciang a banto pen | the one that runs along the middle of the frames) (s:kimciang) (r:11.3.20/42.13.30/6.10.13/2.27.5/2.26.28) (q:draft, low confidence)
kima = (t:adj) (w:divorced) (d:Said of a woman who has been put away by her husband; often listed beside meigong, widow.) (e:meigong ahi a, a ~ ahi zongin/a ~ numei a tenpih pasal | the man who marries a divorced woman/Tua a ~ numei a tenpihte | those who marry that divorced woman) (s:maksa/kikhensa) (r:3.22.13/4.30.9/42.16.18/40.5.32) (q:draft)
kima-sialh = (t:v) (w:boast/brag) (d:Boast about oneself or about what is still to come; compare kisialh, boast.) (e:Zing ciang hun-a ding ~ kei in) (s:kisialh/kisial/kiphasak) (r:20.27.1) (q:draft)
kimaakna = (t:n) (w:divorce) (d:Divorce, a spelling of kimakna with a long vowel; kimaakna lai is a certificate of divorce.) (e:khialhna hangin ~ lai pia-a ka hawlkhiat) (s:kimakna/makna/kikhenna) (r:24.3.8) (q:draft)
kimah = (t:prep) (w:around/round about) (d:Kim, surroundings, with the place marker ah, placed after a noun: around it, on every side of it.) (e:biakna tau ~ na theh ding hi/Amah in ama ~ mi khawmin | he gathered men around him/Tua khuapi ~ a lian a sang khua kulh | around that city a great, high wall/khua ~ a om kum nih nuaisiah pasalno khempeuh | all the boys of two years and under in the surrounding area) (s:kiimah/kiima) (b:kim) (r:2.29.20/11.11.24/66.21.12/40.2.16) (q:draft)
kimai = (t:v) (w:face each other/face) (d:Mai, face, with the prefix ki, each other: written before ngat, turn toward, or tuah, meet, to say that two parties face each other.) (e:khat leh khat ~ tuah ni/amaute khat leh khat ~-ngat ding uh hi | they are to face each other/Topa in ~ tuahin note hong hopih hi | the Lord spoke with you face to face/a vom khempeuhte’ ~ ngatsak hi | he made them face all the dark animals) (s:kimaituah/kimaingat) (b:mai) (r:14.25.17/1.30.40/2.25.20/5.5.5) (q:draft)
kimaingat = (t:v) (w:face each other/face one another) (d:Maingat, face, with the reciprocal prefix ki: face one another, said of the two cherubim on the ark.) (e:amaute khatlekhat ~ uh hi/amaute khat leh khat ~ uh hi | they faced each other/amaute khatlekhat ~ ding uh hi | they are to face each other) (s:kimaituah/kitang/kigalsai) (b:maingat) (r:2.37.9/2.25.20) (q:draft)
kimaisak = (t:v) (w:be forgiven) (d:Passive of maisak, forgive, with the prefix ki; mawhna kimaisak means sins are forgiven, and with khat leh khat it means forgive one another.) (e:Na mawhna ~ zo hi/Ama mawhnasa khempeuh ~ ding a | all his past offences will be forgiven/Ama khialhna ~ a | his transgression is forgiven/mi tampite’ mawhna ~ nading a kibuasa | poured out for the forgiveness of the sins of many) (s:maitheih) (b:maisak) (r:42.7.48/19.32.1/26.18.22/40.26.28) (q:draft)
kimaisakin = (t:v) (w:being forgiven/being pardoned/forgiving one another) (d:Kimaisak with the linking suffix in: being forgiven or forgiving one another; in Romans 2.15 excusing one another.) (e:hih thu hangin Jakob’ mawhna ~/Ama gimna hun bei ta a, ama mawhna ~ | her time of hardship is over and her sin is pardoned/khatlekhat na mawhna uh ~ na kihuh ciat un | forgive one another’s sins and help each other/kimawhsakin ahi zongin, ~ ahi zongin | whether accusing or excusing one another) (a:kimawhsakin) (b:kimaisak) (r:23.27.9/23.40.2/45.2.15/51.3.13) (q:draft)
kimaisakna = (t:n) (w:forgiveness) (d:Kimaisak, be forgiven, with the noun suffix na; mawhna kimaisakna is the forgiveness of sins.) (e:mawhna ~ thu nomau kiangah hong kihilh/mawhna ~ a ngah ding uh a | that they may receive forgiveness of sins/Israel mipawl kisikkikna leh mawh ~ thu | repentance and forgiveness of sins for Israel) (s:maisakna/mawhmaisakna/maitheihna) (b:kimaisak) (r:44.13.38/44.5.31/44.26.18) (q:draft)
kimaisakte = (t:n) (w:those who are forgiven) (d:Kimaisak, be forgiven, with the plural te: those who are forgiven.) (e:tawmno bek a ~ in a itna) (b:kimaisak) (r:42.7.47) (q:draft)
kimaitaisak = (t:v) (w:cheer oneself up/put on a cheerful face) (d:Maitaisak, make cheerful, with the reflexive prefix ki: make one’s own face bright, put on a smile.) (e:Ka dahnate kimangngilh bawlin ~ ding) (b:maitaisak) (r:18.9.27) (q:draft)
kimaituah = (t:v) (w:face each other/meet face to face/confront) (d:stand face to face with someone, as opponents in battle or in court) (e:khat leh khat gal sungah ~ uh hi/a mawhsak mite tawh ~ sak a | letting him meet his accusers face to face/Galvil leh galvil ~ hi | guard stood facing guard) (s:kimaingat/kitang/kigalsai/kimai) (r:14.25.21/44.25.16/13.26.16) (q:draft)
kimaituahin = (t:v) (w:facing each other/face to face/opposite each other) (d:Kimaituah with the linking suffix in: facing one another, face to face.) (e:khat leh khat ~ gal kido uh hi/Topa in ~ note hong hopih a | the Lord spoke to you face to face/Amaute in ~ ni sagih sung giahphual satin | they camped opposite each other for seven days) (b:kimaituah) (r:12.14.11/11.20.29/5.5.4) (q:draft)
kimaizumsak = (t:v) (w:be put to shame/be shamed) (d:Passive of maizumsak, put to shame, with the prefix ki; with lo, not be put to shame.) (e:Siatna hun ciangin amaute ~ lo a) (s:kizahhuaisak/kiminsia-sak/kimindaisak) (b:maizumsak) (r:19.37.19) (q:draft)
kimakai = (t:v) (w:be led/be guided) (d:Makai, lead, with the passive prefix ki: be led; kimakai sak means let oneself be led, and kimakai khial sak let oneself be led astray.) (e:Kha Siangtho ~ sakin/hih bangin ~ khial sak kei un | do not let yourselves be misled like this) (b:makai) (r:49.4.3/14.32.15) (q:draft)
kimakna = (t:n) (w:divorce) (d:Makna, divorce, with the prefix ki; kimakna lai is a certificate of divorce.) (e:Moses in ~ lai gelhsakin masak thei hi/na nu a ~ lai koi-ah om ahi hiam | where is your mother’s certificate of divorce/midang tawh a khialhna hangin ~ lai pia-in | giving her a certificate of divorce because of her adultery) (s:kimaakna/makna/kikhenna) (b:makna) (r:41.10.4/23.50.1/24.3.8) (q:draft)
kimamsak = (t:v) (w:be straightened/be made straight) (d:Passive of mamsak, straighten, with the prefix ki: be made straight.) (e:A kawisate ~ thei lo a) (s:kitangsak) (b:mamsak) (r:21.1.15) (q:draft)
kiman = (t:adj) (w:finished/completed/done) (d:Brought to an end, said of work, an offering or a period of time; kiman khin is completely finished.) (e:tuate ~ khin hi/Biak piakna a ~ ciangin kumpipa | when the offering was finished, the king/Ni guk sungin nasep ~ ding hi | work shall be done for six days/biakbuk nasep khempeuh ~ hi | all the work of the tabernacle was finished) (s:khinta/zawhsa) (r:14.29.29/1.2.1/2.35.2/2.39.32)
kiman = (t:v) (w:arrested/be caught/be captured) (d:Passive of man, catch: be caught, arrested or taken captive; sal-in kiman is be taken as a captive.) (e:Paul ~ ahih ciangin/amah ~ leh, azah sagih-in kiloh sak a | if he is caught, he must pay sevenfold/a ~ mi peuhmah namsau tawh si ding hi | everyone who is caught will die by the sword/thal zat kul loin amaute ~ hi | they were captured without a bow being used/Pasian’ thuciamna singkuang zong ~ hi | the ark of God was also captured) (s:kimat) (a:kikhah) (r:20.6.31/23.13.15/23.22.3/9.4.11)
kimancip = (t:v) (w:be held captive/be seized) (d:Mancip, seize and hold fast, with the prefix ki: be held captive; a kimancip before a noun means captive.) (e:A ~ Jerusalem mite aw) (b:mancip) (r:23.52.2) (q:draft)
kimang = (t:v) (w:be of use/be used/be in effect) (d:Be of use or be in use; mostly negative, bangmah-a kimang lo is worthless, of no use; also last or stay in use for a time.) (e:Bangmah-a ~ lo pasian kua in bawl a/Na-a ~ lo nasempa khuamial pua lamah hawlkhia un | throw the worthless servant out into the darkness/i nai-a om i vengpa ~ zaw hi | a neighbour who is near is of more use/kei’ adingin innluahza bang-a ~ ahi hiam | of what use is the birthright to me/lenggah lawh hun dong ~ ding a | it will last until the grape harvest) (s:phatuam/kizang) (r:23.44.10/20.12.19/40.25.30/20.27.10/1.25.32/3.26.5) (q:draft)
kimangin = (t:v) (w:being used/being in effect) (d:Kimang, be in use, with the linking suffix in; said of a gift that is in use only for a time.) (e:tawlkhat sung bek ~) (b:kimang) (r:46.13.8) (q:draft)
kimangngailh = (t:v) (w:be forgotten) (d:A spelling of kimangngilh: be forgotten, said of past troubles that are no longer remembered.) (e:a beisa huna haksatnate ~ khin a) (s:kimangngilh) (a:kiphawk) (r:23.65.16) (q:draft)
kimangngilh = (t:v) (w:be forgotten) (d:Passive of mangngilh, forget, with the prefix ki: be forgotten; kimangngilh bawl is make oneself forget.) (e:migilote ~ pah hi/hauhna ngeisa khempeuh Izipt gamsungah ~ ding hi | all the former abundance in Egypt will be forgotten/mai lam hun-ah i vekpi-in hong ~ lel ding hi | in days to come we will all be forgotten/mi cimawhte ~ den lo ding a | the needy will not always be forgotten/Ka dahnate ~ bawlin | making myself forget my sorrows) (s:kimangngailh) (a:kiphawk) (b:mangngilh) (r:20.10.7/1.41.30/21.2.16/19.9.18/18.9.27) (q:draft)
kimangngilhkha = (t:v) (w:be overlooked/be forgotten by chance) (d:Be forgotten or passed over by chance; said of dead bodies left unburied because no one noticed them.) (e:a ~ siluanghawmte zongin a phum dingin) (r:26.39.14) (q:draft)
kimangpah = (t:v) (w:be used straight on/continue in use) (d:kimang, be used, with pah, straight away; of the existing priests simply being kept in use) (e:siampi omsa a ~ ding ahi hi) (r:58.7.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
kimangthangsak = (t:v) (w:be cut off/be destroyed) (d:Passive with ki of mangthangsak, cause to perish: be destroyed, be cut off from one’s people.) (e:amau pawl lak pan ~ ding hi) (b:mangthangsak) (r:44.3.23) (q:draft)
kimangzaw = (t:v) (w:be more useful/be better) (d:Kimang, be of use, with zaw, more: be of more use, be better.) (e:a om i vengpa ~ hi) (b:kimang) (r:20.27.10) (q:draft)
kimanin = (t:v) (w:being caught/being captured/being arrested) (d:Kiman, be caught, with the linking suffix in that joins it to the next verb: being caught, arrested or captured.) (e:Na kampauna hangin nang hong ~/hong ~ ama’ khut sungah nang hong kipia | you will be captured and given into his hand/Note hong ~ thukhen zumah hong kipaipih ding a | you will be arrested and brought before the courts/Jerusalem khua-ah hong ~ thongah hong kikoih a | I was arrested in Jerusalem and put in prison) (b:kiman) (r:20.6.2/24.34.3/41.13.9/44.28.17) (q:draft)
kimanna = (t:n) (w:use/usefulness/value) (d:What something is good for; a kimanna om lo or kimanna nei lo means useless, worthless.) (e:a ~ om lo ahih manin/Hih mite’ ngeinate a ~ om lo hi | the customs of these peoples are worthless/mite’ upna pen a ~ om loin | faith would be of no value/Khebai pa’ khe a ~ om loin | the lame man’s legs being useless) (s:manphatna) (r:58.7.18/32.2.8/24.10.3/45.4.14/20.26.7) (q:draft)
kimansiang = (t:v) (w:be completed/be finished) (d:Kiman, finished, with siang, clean: be wholly finished, said of work carried through to the end.) (e:nasep khempeuh ~ hi) (s:kizawh/kizo) (b:kiman) (r:14.8.16) (q:draft)
kimante = (t:n) (w:captives/those captured/prisoners) (d:Kiman, be taken, with the plural te: those who have been captured; sal-a kimante are people taken captive, and after a battle the word also covers the plunder taken.) (e:sal-a a ~ tungah suahtakna thu/a kithatte leh a ~ | the slain and the captives/gal sunga a ~ khennih suahin | dividing what was taken in the battle into two parts/sal-a ~ khempeuh hih munah hong la kik | bring all the exiles back to this place) (s:salte/saltangte/galmatte) (b:kiman) (r:23.61.1/4.31.27/5.32.42/24.28.6) (q:draft)
kimanzo = (t:v) (w:can be caught) (d:Kiman, be caught, with zo, be able or enough: said of fish, whether enough could be caught.) (e:khamzah ding ~ ding ahi hiam) (b:kiman) (r:4.11.22) (q:draft)
kimap = (t:v) (w:be spared) (d:Be spared, be left alive; na nuntakna hong kimap ding means your life will be spared.) (e:na nuntakna hong ~ ding hi/uliante na belh leh na nuntakna hong ~ ding a | if you surrender to the officers your life will be spared) (s:kisiit/kisuaktasak) (r:24.38.20/24.38.17) (q:draft)
kimasa = (t:adj) (w:divorced) (d:Kima, divorced, with the completive suffix sa: said of a woman who has been sent away by her husband.) (e:Meigong numei, a ~ numei, a kininsaksa numei/Meigong numei ahi a, a ~ numei ahi zongin | whether a widow or a divorced woman) (s:maksa/kikhensa) (b:kima) (r:3.21.14/26.44.22) (q:draft)
kimat = (t:v) (w:arrest/seize/be arrested/be caught) (d:Passive of mat, seize, with the prefix ki: be arrested, be caught or be taken captive.) (e:Paul ~ nading thu, Moses ~ sawm ahih man in/Peter a ~ khit ciangin thongah kikoih a | after Peter was arrested he was put in prison/Guta khat a ~ cianga a zum bangin | as a thief is ashamed when he is caught/Jesuh a ~ theih nading a hanciam uh hi | they looked for a way to arrest Jesus/Johan a ~ khit ciangin Zeisu Galile gamah pai a | after John was arrested Jesus went to Galilee) (s:kiman) (a:kikhah) (r:44.12.4/24.2.26/41.12.12/41.1.14)
kimat = (t:adj) (w:sticky/adhesive/gluey/joined/attached) (d:Holding or sticking to each other; said of parts that are joined or fitted together.) (e:sing leh sing ~/a kual masa-ah a dawn ~ hi | their tops were joined at the first ring/a mong nihte-ah a ~ liangkaihna puan nih | two shoulder pieces attached at its two ends/sik leh tungman a ~ theih loh mah bangin | just as iron and clay cannot hold together) (r:2.36.29/2.28.7/27.2.43)
kimatcip = (t:v) (w:stick fast/be sealed/be tightly joined) (d:Kimat, hold together, with cip, firmly: be stuck fast or tightly closed, said of a hand stuck to a sword, a sealed book and scales shut together.) (e:a khut a namsau-ah ~ hi/a ~ laibu sunga thu om tawh a kibang | like the words in a sealed scroll/suang bangin sakin ~ bikbek ciat hi | each shut tightly together, hard as stone) (s:kisiincip) (b:kimat) (r:10.23.10/23.29.11/18.41.15) (q:draft)
kimatheih = (t:v) (w:be known beforehand/be foreseen) (d:Theih, know, with ma, before, and the prefix ki: be known beforehand; a kimatheih lo is something that cannot be known in advance.) (e:cih a ~ lo mah ahi hi) (r:10.11.25) (q:draft, low confidence)
kimatin = (t:v) (w:be joined to/adjoin/be attached to) (d:Kimat, be joined, with the linking suffix in; after tawh it means next to or connected with.) (e:Hih kawm tawh a ~ biakinn kimkotah inndei/keima biakinn kongkhuam leh kongzawlte tawh ~ bawl uh a | they built theirs right next to my threshold and doorposts/lampi tawh a ~ inndei gol khat om a | there was a large room adjoining the passage/a pumpi khempeuh kizom ~ | the whole body joined and held together) (s:kigizawng) (b:kimat) (r:26.41.5/49.4.16/26.43.8/26.40.38) (q:draft)
kimatna = (t:n) (w:capture/arrest/seizure) (d:Kimat, be caught, with the noun suffix na: the fact of being caught or taken.) (e:Johan’ ~ thu Zeisu in a zak ciangin/Pasian’ thuciamna singkuang a ~ | the capture of the ark of God/a zuau kamsangpa in ~ a thuak khit ciangin | after the false prophet was captured/Ama’ behpa sal-in a ~ | his relative’s being taken captive) (s:matna) (b:kimat) (r:40.4.12/9.4.19/66.19.20/1.14.14) (q:draft)
kimatsak = (t:v) (w:fasten together/join/couple) (d:Kimat, hold to each other, with the causative sak: join things so that they hold together, as curtains with clasps.) (e:puante khat leh khat ~ hi/puanbuk a ~ dingin | to fasten the tent together/dalna puan khat leh khat na ~ ding hi | you shall fasten the curtains to one another/a mong leh a mong ~ uh a | their wings touched tip to tip) (s:zom) (b:kimat) (r:2.36.13/2.26.11/2.36.18/2.26.6/26.1.9) (q:draft)
kimatsakin = (t:v) (w:fastening together/joining) (d:Kimatsak, join things so that they hold together, with the linking suffix in; said of foxes tied tail to tail.) (e:a meite leh a meite ~) (b:kimatsak) (r:7.15.4) (q:draft)
kimawhsak = (t:v) (w:condemn oneself/blame oneself/accuse one another) (d:Mawhsak, accuse or condemn, with the prefix ki: with amah le amah condemn oneself, with khat leh khat accuse one another.) (e:amah le amah a ~ ahi hi/amah le amah a ~ lote | those who do not condemn themselves/amaute in khat leh khat ~ ta uh hen | let them bring charges against one another/Khat leh khat na ~ nading uh a om ciangin | when you have a grievance against one another) (a:kimaisak) (b:mawhsak) (r:45.14.23/51.3.13/45.14.22/44.19.38) (q:draft)
kimawhsakin = (t:v) (w:condemning one another/accusing/condemning oneself) (d:Kimawhsak, condemn oneself or accuse one another, with the linking suffix in.) (e:khatlekhat ~ thu kikhen kei unla/~ ahi zongin, kimaisakin ahi zongin | whether accusing or excusing one another/Kei mahmah zong ~ thu ka kikhen kei hi | I do not even judge myself) (a:kimaisakin) (b:kimawhsak) (r:45.14.13/46.4.3/45.2.15) (q:draft)
kimawhsakna = (t:n) (w:accusation/charge/blame) (d:An accusation made against someone; also the condemning of oneself in the heart, a guilty conscience.) (e:a ~ lai pia loin paisak leng/Sodom leh Gomorrah a ~ lianin | the outcry against Sodom and Gomorrah is great/ahi lo ~ na thuak uh leh | if you suffer false accusation/ka lungsim sungah ~ a om lohna dingin | so that there is nothing in my heart to accuse me) (s:mawhsakna/mawhzonna) (b:mawhsakna) (r:44.25.27/40.5.11/1.18.20/44.24.16) (q:draft)
kimawhsaknate = (t:n) (w:accusations/charges) (d:Kimawhsakna with the plural te: the things a person is accused of.) (e:amah a ~ kam khat beek dawng/A mawkna-a hong ~ thei khin na hih ciangin | since you know the charges made against me without cause/kei hong ~ nangma mai-ah pheltheih nading hun | a chance to answer before you the charges against me) (s:mawhsaknate/mawhzonnate) (b:kimawhsakna) (r:40.27.14/25.3.59/44.24.10) (q:draft)
kimawk = (t:adv) (w:idly/without cause) (d:the prefix ki joined to mawk, idly or for no reason, and written before the verb that ki belongs to: kimawk tot, quarrel for no reason; kimawk hoho, chat idly with one another; kimawk phat, praise oneself emptily) (e:mi tawh ~ hoho kei un/mi khatpeuh tawh thu om lopi-in ~ tot kei in | do not quarrel with anyone without cause/amah ~ phat tawm hi | he flatters himself) (s:mawk) (b:mawk) (r:42.10.4/20.3.30/19.36.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
kimawkphat = (t:v) (w:flatter oneself) (d:Mawkphat, praise idly or flatter, with the reflexive prefix ki: flatter oneself.) (e:manin amah ~ tawm hi) (b:mawkphat) (r:19.36.2) (q:draft)
kimawksai = (t:v) (w:spring/go off) (d:of a trap, spring shut with nothing in it) (e:thang ~ ahi hiam) (r:30.3.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
kimawktot = (t:v) (w:quarrel without cause/accuse for no reason) (d:Mawk, idly or without reason, with kitot, quarrel: pick a quarrel with someone for no reason.) (e:thu om lopi-in ~ kei in) (r:20.3.30) (q:draft)
kimawl = (t:v) (w:play/sport/perform) (d:Play, as children do; also perform or hold a contest for others to watch.) (e:gulgilo’ kuavangah ~ ding a/Samson a ~ lai takin a en | watching while Samson performed/a naupangte uh tai khia-in ~ uh a | their children run out and play/eite mai-ah ~ sak ni | let us have them compete before us) (r:23.11.8/7.16.25/7.16.27/18.21.11/10.2.14) (q:draft)
kimawlin = (t:v) (w:playing/play) (d:kimawl, play, with the linking ending in: playing) (e:numei naupang ~ phezaizai ding uh hi) (b:kimawl) (r:38.8.5) (q:draft)
kimawlna = (t:n) (w:game/contest/sport) (d:kimawl, play, with the noun suffix na: a contest in which athletes compete) (e:~ sungah a kihel mi khempeuh in/~ ngeina zui lopi-in | without following the rules of the contest/tua ~-ah a kihel zo lo mi | one who is not able to take part in that contest) (b:kimawl) (r:46.9.25/55.2.5/46.9.27) (q:draft)
kimawlsak = (t:v) (w:make perform/make play) (d:kimawl, play or perform, with the causative sak: have someone perform or hold a contest before onlookers) (e:Samson a ~ laitakin a en/eite’ mai-ah ~ ni | let us have them compete before us) (b:kimawl) (r:7.16.27/10.2.14) (q:draft)
kimawlte = (t:n) (w:those who play/ones playing) (d:kimawl play, with the plural te: the ones who are playing, here of children) (e:a tu naupang a ~ tawh kibang) (b:kimawl) (r:42.7.32/40.11.16) (q:draft)
kimciang = (t:n) (w:middle/halfway/half) (d:The halfway point of the height or extent of a thing; kim, middle, with ciang, as far as.) (e:biakna tau ~ a batsuk theih nadingin/A khuampeekte’ ~ takah | right at the middle of the frames/nasep a ~ bang kizo hi | about half of the work was finished) (s:kim) (r:2.27.5/16.4.6/2.36.33) (q:draft)
kimeekcip = (t:v) (w:be crushed) (d:Be squeezed or pressed flat, be crushed; passive with the prefix ki.) (e:vasa bu bangin a ~ thei) (r:18.4.19) (q:draft)
kimeeltheih = (t:v) (w:be acquainted/know each other) (d:A spelling of kimeltheih: know one another by sight, be acquainted; tawh marks the other person.) (e:siampi ukpa tawh ~ a/siampi ukpa tawh a ~ nungzuipa paikhia a | the disciple who was known to the high priest went out) (s:kimeltheih) (r:43.18.15/43.18.16) (q:draft)
kimeetsak = (t:v) (w:be shorn/be sheared) (d:Passive with ki of meetsak, have the wool cut off: be shorn.) (e:a mul a ~ tuuno) (s:kimet) (b:meetsak) (r:44.8.32) (q:draft)
kimeltheih = (t:v) (w:be acquainted/get acquainted/be associated) (d:Meltheih, know by face, with the reciprocal prefix ki: know each other, be acquainted; tawh marks the other person.) (e:Kefas tawh ~ nadingin/Tobiah tawh a ~ siampi Eliashib | Eliashib the priest, who was closely associated with Tobiah) (s:kimeeltheih) (b:meltheih) (r:48.1.18/16.13.4) (q:draft)
kimemat = (t:v) (w:be connected/have to do with each other) (d:of two things, belong together or rest on one another; here said of keeping the law and faith, with lo: have nothing to do with each other) (e:upna thu na ~ kha lo hi) (r:48.3.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
kimematna = (t:n) (w:claim/connection/share) (d:kimemat be connected with, with the noun suffix na: something that ties a person to a matter and gives a right in it) (e:bangmah ~ na nei kei uh hi) (b:kimemat) (r:16.2.20) (q:draft, low confidence)
kimet = (t:v) (w:be shaved/be shorn) (d:Passive of met, shave or shear, with the prefix ki: of hair or wool, be cut off.) (e:a ~ khit ciangin/Ka sam ~ leh ka hatna in kei hong nusia | if my hair is shaved my strength will leave me/a mul a ~ khin phet | whose wool has just been shorn) (s:kikiat/kimeetsak) (b:met) (r:7.16.22/22.4.2/7.16.17) (q:draft)
kimetcip = (t:v) (w:collapse/sink down/be levelled) (d:said of the age-old hills before God, in parallel with kitamkham crumble; how the word is built is not certain) (e:a om tawntung mualneute ~ hi) (r:35.3.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
kimetmai = (t:v) (w:be shaved off/be cut off) (d:Passive with ki of met, shave: of a beard, be shaved clean away.) (e:khamul khempeuh ~ hi) (r:23.15.2) (q:draft)
kimettol = (t:v) (w:be shaved bald/be shaved) (d:Passive of mettol with the prefix ki: of the head, be shaved completely, as a sign of mourning.) (e:Dahna limin lu khempeuh ~ a) (b:mettol) (r:23.15.2) (q:draft)
kimettolsak = (t:v) (w:be shaved bald/have the head shaved) (d:kimettol be shaved bald, with sak: have the hair shaved off completely, as a sign of mourning) (e:A sam uh ~ ding a) (b:kimettol) (r:26.7.18) (q:draft)
kimin = (t:adv) (w:fully/completely/in full/all) (d:Kim, complete, with the suffix in: the whole of it, with nothing and no one left out; often as a kimin.) (e:sawm-ah khat a ~ hong paipih un/Moses in Israel mite tungah a thu a ~ a gen hi | Moses told the Israelites everything in full/Israel mi khempeuh, a mi ~ | all the Israelites, every one of them/Pasian’ pianzia a ~ a neih nading | to have the nature of God in its fullness/Kumpipa’ thupiakna kithei ~ | when the king’s order had been made known to all) (s:vekpi/vekin) (b:kim) (r:39.3.10/4.29.40/14.31.1/51.1.19/17.2.8) (q:draft)
kimindaisak = (t:v) (w:be dishonoured/be disgraced/be put to shame) (d:Passive with ki of mindaisak, bring a name into disgrace.) (e:hong kipahtawi-in hong ~ zel a) (s:kizahhuaisak/kiminsia-sak) (a:kipahtawi) (b:mindaisak) (r:47.6.8) (q:draft)
kiminsia = (t:see) <kiminsia-sak>
kiminsia-sak = (t:v) (w:be put to shame/be disgraced) (d:Be given a bad name: min, name, with sia, bad, and the causative sak, passive with ki.) (e:zahhuai-in ~ khin ahih ciangin) (s:kizahhuaisak/kimindaisak/kimaizumsak) (a:kipahtawi) (r:19.71.24) (q:draft)
kiminthan = (t:see) <kiminthan'sak>
kiminthan'sak = (t:v) (w:be glorified/be honoured) (d:Passive of minthangsak, glorify; minthang is shortened to minthan before sak.) (e:Ama sungah Pasian a ~ leh/amah a ~ theih nadingin | so that he may be glorified) (s:kiminthangsak/kiminthansak/kithangsak) (a:kimindaisak) (r:43.13.32/23.61.3) (q:draft)
kiminthangsak = (t:v) (w:be glorified/be honored) (d:Passive of minthangsak, glorify, with the prefix ki: be glorified, be honoured.) (e:Tu-in Mihing Tapa ~ a/mite khempeuh mai-ah keimah hong ~ ding hi | I will be honoured in the sight of all the people/Israel sungah amah ~ ding hi | he will be glorified in Israel/ama sungah Pasian a ~ ding hi | God will be glorified in him) (s:kiminthansak/kithangsak/kipahtawi) (a:kimindaisak) (b:minthangsak) (r:43.13.31/3.10.3/23.44.23) (q:draft)
kiminthansak = (t:v) (w:be glorified/be made famous) (d:Passive with ki of min, name, than, be renowned, and the causative sak: be made famous, be glorified.) (e:amah a ~ theih nadingin) (s:kiminthangsak/kithangsak) (a:kimindaisak) (r:23.61.3) (q:draft)
kiminthansakna = (t:n) (w:glorification/display of splendour) (d:Kiminthansak, be glorified, with the noun suffix na: that by which someone is glorified.) (e:keimah hong ~ ding ka nasempa) (b:kiminthansak) (r:23.49.3) (q:draft)
kimitsak = (t:v) (w:be put out/be extinguished/be quenched) (d:Passive of mitsak, put out, with the prefix ki: of a fire or of anger, be put out; mostly negative, kimitsak lo ding hi, it shall not go out.) (e:~ lo ding hi/ka hehna kitawhkuang ding a, ~ lo ding hi | my anger will burn and will not be quenched/mei kikuangsak den ding hi; ~ lo ding hi | the fire must be kept burning; it must not go out) (s:kisumit/kisukmit) (a:kitawhkuang) (b:mitsak) (r:3.6.13/12.22.17/3.6.12) (q:draft)
Kimittawsak = (t:v) (w:blind oneself/make oneself blind) (d:Mittaw, blind, with the prefix ki, oneself, and the causative sak: make oneself blind.) (e:~ unla a mittaw hi un) (r:23.29.9) (q:draft)
kimkhat = (t:det) (w:some/some of) (d:An indefinite number or part of a group or thing, placed after the noun; repeated, some and others; of a divided thing it can be one half.) (e:a um lo mi ~ a om hi/amah in zong singgah ~ a pasal pia a | she also gave some of the fruit to her husband/Mi ~ in tua upna a nial uh a | some have rejected that faith/~ in tam, ~ in tawm kaikhawm hi | some gathered much, some little) (s:khenkhat/pawkhat) (r:43.6.64/1.3.6/54.1.19/2.16.17)
kimkhat = (t:prep) (w:among) (d:Some among a group, placed after the noun that names the group.) (e:Khlo-e te innkuanpih ~ in hong zasak uh hi | some from Chloe’s household have informed me/Tua munah a tu laitheite ~ in | some of the teachers of the law sitting there/Na tapa’ zawl-aikungte ~ kei hong pia in | give me some of your son’s mandrakes/mi ~ in a kihisak uh hi | some people have become arrogant) (r:46.1.11/41.2.6/1.30.14/46.4.18)
kimkhatte = (t:prep) (w:among) (d:Some among a group, placed after the noun that names the group; also one half, as in Manasseh minam kimkhatte, the half-tribe of Manasseh.) (e:Ko pawlpi numei ~ zingtungin hanah pai uh a | some of our women went to the tomb early in the morning/Judah gam panin mi ~ hong pai uh a | some people came from Judea/Mi ~ heh uh a | some of the people were angry/Manasseh minam ~ tungah ka pia hi | I gave it to the half-tribe of Manasseh) (b:kimkhat) (r:42.24.22/44.15.1/41.14.4/5.3.13)
kimkhattte = (t:prep) (w:among) (d:A spelling of kimkhatte found once, at the start of a sentence: some among them.) (e:~ in lei hoihna-ah kia a, kung po a | some fell on good soil and grew up) (r:42.8.8)
Kimkhattte = (t:det) (w:some/others) (d:Some of them, here some of the seed; apparently a misprint of kimkhatte.) (e:~ in lei hoihna-ah kia a) (b:kimkhattte) (r:42.8.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
kimkot = (t:adv) (w:around/on all sides/round about) (d:On every side of a person or thing; written after a noun or after a, often with the endings a or ah.) (e:a ~ a en hi/a ~-a om ama langpangte kangtum hi | it burns up his foes on every side/Buk tual ~-a a kikhaisukte khempeuh | all the curtains around the courtyard/Havilah gambup ~-a luang pen ahi hi | it is the one that flows around the whole land of Havilah/a ~ ah a tu mite en kawikawi a | looking at the people seated around him) (s:kiim) (r:41.5.32/19.97.3/2.38.16/1.2.11/41.3.34)
kimkota = (t:prep) (w:around/surrounding) (d:Kimkot, around, with the ending a that links it to the following noun: that which is around.) (e:Jerusalem khua ~ kulh khempeuh a susia hi/biakinn kawm leh a ~ inndei neute | the temple wall and the small rooms around it/Buktual ~ khuampite le a bullente | the posts of the surrounding courtyard with their bases/Jerusalem ~ kulhpi lam a zawh mateng | until he finished building the wall around Jerusalem) (s:kiima/kiimah) (b:kimkot) (r:24.52.14/26.41.12/26.41.8/4.3.37/11.3.1) (q:draft)
kimkotah = (t:adv) (w:around/on every side) (d:Kimkot, around, with the place marker ah: on every side of the thing named before it.) (e:a ~ kham tawh a geihual khat bawl/biakna tau tung ~ a si theh hi | he splashed its blood against the altar on all sides/biakna tau ~ tui luang a | the water ran down around the altar/Mual ~ dalnate bawl in la siangthosak in | put limits around the mountain and set it apart as holy) (s:kiim) (b:kimkot) (r:2.37.11/3.8.19/11.18.35/2.19.23)
kimkotin = (t:adv) (w:around/round about) (d:Kimkot, around, with the suffix in; after a noun, going or lying all around it.) (e:biaknatau ~ pai un/Judah mite in Zeisu ~ hong kikhawm uh a | the Jews gathered around Jesus/Edom gam leh Moab gam ~ pai-in | going around the lands of Edom and Moab/tuikuangpi ~ um gahte kibawl hi | gourds were made all around the Sea) (s:kiim) (b:kimkot) (r:19.118.27/7.11.18/43.10.24/11.7.24) (q:draft)
kimkotteng = (t:adv) (w:all around/on every side) (d:Kimkot, around, with teng, all: the whole surrounding of a thing, placed after the thing surrounded.) (e:Biakinn ~ a lei kitawito a/ka ~ taang pempam hi | there was bright light all around me) (b:kimkot) (r:26.41.8/26.1.4) (q:draft)
kimlai = (t:conj) (w:while/while still/although) (d:Placed after a descriptive word or clause: while still being so, even though it is so; often followed by hi napi, although.) (e:A pil lo ~ pil a kisapa sangin/a ding thei ~ mahin a sa uh muat mang | their flesh will rot away while they are still standing/Sun ~ hi napi ama adingin khuamial bang a | though it is still day, it is like darkness to her/a hing ~ hi napi | though still alive) (s:laitakin/laitak) (r:20.26.12/18.8.12/38.14.12/24.15.9/20.1.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
kimlaipi = (t:conj) (w:even while/while) (d:Kimlai, while, with the intensive pi: at the very time that something is so.) (e:numei nin nei ~ buan uh hi) (b:kimlai) (r:26.22.10) (q:draft)
kimna = (t:n) (d:kim all, complete, with the noun suffix na, placed after a verb: the doing of it in full, to every one or in every detail; tunpih kimna is the bringing of all of them) (e:ka tunpih ~ hangin) (b:kim) (r:26.39.28/12.16.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
kimnai = (t:see) <kimnai-a>
kimnai-a = (t:adv) (w:nearby/in the vicinity) (d:Kim, around, with nai, near, and the place ending a; a kimnai-a om means which is close by.) (e:amah in a ~ om) (r:12.23.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
kimpipa = (t:n) (w:king) (d:apparently a misprint of kumpipa, the king) (e:Judah ~ Jekoniah leh Judah gam) (s:kumpipa) (r:24.28.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
kimsak = (t:v) (w:please/satisfy/delight) (d:make the heart content: kim, complete, with the causative sak, used after lung or lungsim, heart, as in ka lung hong kimsak, it pleases me) (e:na lung hong ~ ding hi/amah in ka lung hong ~ mahmah hi | she pleases me very much/mite lungsim uh ~ bang hi loin | not as pleasing the hearts of people) (s:lungkimsak) (r:20.29.17/7.14.3/52.2.4) (q:draft)
kimsak = (t:v) (w:set on edge) (d:of something sour acting on the teeth, as vinegar does) (e:Leenggah tuithuk in ha ~ a) (r:20.10.26) (q:draft, low confidence)
kimtakin = (t:adv) (w:fully/completely/in full) (d:kim, complete, with takin, which makes an adverb: in full, with nothing lacking; usually written a kimtakin) (e:a ~ na ngahtheih nadingun/Pasian’ pianzia khempeuh a ~ nei a | he has all the nature of God in full/sazian a ~ hong pia in | give me the account in full/amau’ sep dingteng a ~ a sep uh ciangin | when they fully do all the work they have) (s:kicingin/kimin) (b:kim) (r:63.1.8/51.2.9/42.16.2/45.13.6) (q:draft)
kimte = (t:det) (w:all/every) (d:kim with the plural te, placed after a noun; minam kimte is all nations) (e:minam ~ tunga ka thukhen nading ni/Minam ~ aw | all you nations/leitunga om minam ~ | all the nations living on the earth/minam ~, minam tuamtuamte | all nations and the various peoples) (b:kim) (r:31.1.15/19.96.7/27.6.25/27.7.14) (q:draft)
kimu = (t:v) (w:meet) (d:see each other, come together with someone: mu, see, with the reciprocal prefix ki; tawh marks the person met) (e:Elijah tawh ~ dingin Ahab pai hi/Ahaz tawh ~ dingin | to meet Ahaz/amah tawh ~ dingin Jakob kiangah va pai hi | he went to Jacob to meet with him/ute naute tawh ~-in | meeting with the brothers and sisters) (s:kituah/tuak) (b:mu) (r:11.18.16/23.7.3/1.34.6/44.16.40)
kimuan = (t:see) <kimuan'na>
kimuan'na = (t:n) (w:confidence/self-confidence/trust) (d:what a person relies on; ei leh ei kimuan'na is trust in oneself) (e:Ei leh ei ~ in haina hi a/na ~ uh bang suang na hi uh hiam | on what do you base this confidence of yours/ci-in ~ lungsim tawh i gen thei hi | so we can say with a confident heart/Ama ~ maimom khau bang hi lel a | what he trusts in is only like a spider thread) (s:kimuanna/muanna) (r:20.28.26/12.18.19/58.13.6/18.8.14) (q:draft)
kimuang = (t:v) (w:be confident/rely on oneself/trust in oneself) (d:muang trust, with the reflexive prefix ki; kimuang takin is confidently) (e:~ takin Pasian kiangah/ci-in na ~ uh hi | so you are confident/kote’ thatang ~ loin | not relying on our own strength) (b:muang) (r:49.3.12/47.1.9/45.2.20) (q:draft)
kimuangmawh = (t:v) (w:doubt one another/suspect one another) (d:reciprocal ki with muangmawh doubt, be unsure of) (e:a nungzuite ~ ciatin) (r:43.13.22) (q:draft)
kimuanna = (t:n) (w:confidence/trust/self-reliance) (d:muanna, trust, with the prefix ki: trust in oneself, confidence; kimuanna lungsim is a confident heart) (e:Ei le ei ~ haina hi a/ci-in ~ lungsim i nei hi | this is the confidence we have/Ama ~ maimom khau bang hi lel a | what he trusts in is only like a spider thread/~ lungsim tawh hehpihna tokhom va zuan ciat ni | let us approach the throne of mercy with confidence) (s:kimuan'na/muanna) (b:muanna) (r:20.28.26/62.5.14/18.8.14/58.4.16) (q:draft)
kimudah = (t:v) (w:be hated/be detested) (d:passive of mudah, hate: be hated by others) (e:ngaihsutna hoih lo a neite ~ hi/Hong kinusia, hong ~ | you were forsaken and hated) (b:mudah) (r:20.14.17/23.60.15) (q:draft)
kimudah = (t:v) (w:hate one another/loathe oneself) (d:with khat leh khat, hate each other; with tawm, loathe oneself) (e:khat leh khat a ~ ding uh hi/khat-le-khat ~ mi i hi ngei hi | we were once people who hated one another/amau mahmah ~ tawm ding uh hi | they will loathe themselves/nomau mahmah na ~ tawm ding uh hi | you will loathe yourselves) (s:kimuhdah) (b:mudah) (r:40.24.10/26.36.31/56.3.3/26.6.9) (q:draft)
kimudahin = (t:v) (w:hating one another) (d:kimudah hate each other, with the linking ending in) (e:khatlekhat ~ khatlekhat kilehhek ding) (b:kimudah) (r:40.24.10) (q:draft)
kimudahsak = (t:v) (w:set at odds/cause to hate each other) (d:kimudah hate each other, with the causative sak) (e:lawmta ki-it kimlai ~ hi) (b:kimudah) (r:20.16.28) (q:draft)
kimudahtawm = (t:v) (w:loathe oneself/hate oneself) (d:kimudah hate, with tawm, oneself, by oneself) (e:nomau mah na ~ ding uh hi/amau mahmah ~ ding uh hi | they will loathe themselves/nomau mahmah na ~ ding uh hi | you will loathe yourselves) (r:26.20.43/26.36.31/26.6.9) (q:draft)
kimuh = (t:v) (w:be found/be seen/appear) (d:passive form of muh see, used before endings such as theih, leh and ciangin) (e:A ~ theih hun lai-in/nungakna lim a ~ kei leh | if no proof of virginity is found/mi khat beek a ~ zawh loh maninah | because not even one person could be found/meii sungah sakhituihup a ~ leh | when the rainbow appears in the clouds/A gupa a ~ kei leh | if the thief is not found) (b:muh) (r:23.55.6/1.9.14/5.22.20/66.5.4/2.22.8) (q:draft)
kimuh = (t:v) (w:meet/see each other) (d:form of kimu used before endings such as ciangin) (e:Topa tawh a ~ uh ciangin/Amah tawh na ~ ciangin | when you meet him/Jesuh tawh ~ ding a hanciam hi | he tried to see Jesus/Amau tawh a ~ ciangin | when he met them) (b:kimu) (r:40.28.17/2.7.16/42.9.9/24.41.6) (q:draft)
kimuhdah = (t:v) (w:hate each other) (d:reciprocal ki with muhdah hate; kimuhdah sak is cause to hate each other, set at odds) (e:lawmta ki-it kimlai ~ sak hi) (s:kimudah) (b:muhdah) (r:20.16.28) (q:draft)
kimuhdahna = (t:n) (w:being hated/hatred/bitterness) (d:kimuhdah with the noun suffix na: the state of being hated or unloved, and also hatred between people) (e:Leah a ~ a theih ciangin/Keimah hong ~ thu Topa in za khin | the Lord has heard that I am hated) (s:muhdahna) (a:itna) (b:kimuhdah) (r:1.29.31/49.4.31/1.29.33) (q:draft)
kimuhmawh = (t:v) (w:overlook/turn a blind eye/ignore) (d:with bawl, do: act as if one had not seen a wrong) (e:tuapa ~ bawlin amah a thah kei uh leh/Khialhna ~ bawlna in buaina piangsak a | overlooking wrongdoing causes trouble) (r:3.20.4/20.10.10) (q:draft)
kimuhna = (t:n) (w:being found/where it is found) (d:kimuh, be found or be seen, with -na: the place, the person or the way in which something is found or seen) (e:tua hai a ~ penpen kithat hen/a ~ mi peuhmah kithat ding hi | anyone with whom he is found shall be put to death/a ~ penpen ka sila hi ding a | the one with whom it is found will be my slave/a ~ ding a lampi thei lo uh a | they do not know the way to where it is found) (b:kimuh) (r:1.44.9/18.28.13/2.21.16/1.44.10) (q:draft)
kimuhnop = (t:v) (w:long to see/wish to meet) (d:kimuh meet, see each other, with nop wish; used with tawh for the person) (e:note tawh ka ~ zong kum) (r:45.15.23) (q:draft)
kimuhpih = (t:v) (w:meet/meet with/come across) (d:kimuh meet, with pih together with; na kimuhpih peuhpeuh, anyone you meet) (e:Na ~ peuhpeuh tungah na pumpi na kipia) (b:kimuh) (r:26.16.25) (q:draft)
kimuhsuk = (t:v) (w:be seen below/be looked down on) (d:kimuh be seen, with suk downward; of land that can be seen from a height) (e:sehnel gam a ~ theihna Pisgah mual) (b:kimuh) (r:4.21.20) (q:draft)
kimukhia = (t:v) (w:be found out/be discovered/be discerned) (d:passive of mukhia, find out, with the prefix ki: come to light, be found out or recognised) (e:a gamtatna panun ~ thei hi/kumpi dona a om ngitngetna thu ~ hi | it was found that there has always been revolt against kings/kua in ama khialhnate ~ thei hiam | who can discern his own errors/A kihhuaina teng ~ pah hinapi | though all her filthiness was plainly seen) (s:kitheikhia/kiphawkkhia) (b:mukhia) (r:20.20.11/15.4.19/19.19.12/25.1.9) (q:draft)
kimukik = (t:v) (w:be seen again/be found again) (d:passive of mukik see again, with the prefix ki; kimukik ngei nawn lo is never to be found again) (e:~ ngei nawn lo ding hi) (b:mukik) (r:66.18.21/18.20.8) (q:draft)
kimukik = (t:v) (w:meet again/see each other again) (d:kimu meet, with kik again) (e:note tawh ~ ding ihih manin) (b:kimu) (r:43.16.22) (q:draft)
kimusa = (t:adj) (w:seen/already seen) (d:kimu be seen, with sa marking what has already happened) (e:gam lam pan a ~ aksi in) (b:kimu) (r:40.2.9) (q:draft)
kimusak = (t:v) (w:show/let see/be shown) (d:cause people to see a thing) (e:Judah mite khempeuh ~ in/ama khut a viik sukna ~ ding hi | he will show his arm coming down) (s:kilangsak) (b:musak) (r:24.43.9/23.30.30) (q:draft)
kimusak = (t:v) (w:bring to meet/bring before) (d:kimu meet with the causative sak, with tawh for the person met) (e:miliante tawh ~ thei hi) (b:kimu) (r:20.18.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
kimut = (t:v) (w:be blown/be sounded) (d:passive of mut blow, of a trumpet) (e:Peengkul hong ~ ciangin) (s:kitum) (b:mut) (r:23.18.3) (q:draft)
kimute = (t:n) (w:things found/things seen) (d:kimu be seen or found, with the plural te: the things that were found, here the wrongs found in a king) (e:amah a hoih lohna a ~) (b:kimu) (r:14.36.8) (q:draft)
kimuthei = (t:adj) (w:visible/seen) (d:that can be seen; the opposite is kimu thei lo, unseen) (e:a ~ nate a mitsuan ka hi kei uh a/a ~ hitaleh a kimu thei lo hitaleh | whether visible or invisible/A ~ nate tomno sung bek kimang a | the things that are seen last only a short time/a ~ nate a kisialhpih mite | people who boast in things that can be seen) (b:muthei) (r:47.4.18/51.1.16/48.6.12) (q:draft)
kimutheite = (t:n) (w:visible things/things seen) (d:kimuthei visible, with the plural te) (e:a om khempeuh a ~) (b:kimuthei) (r:51.1.16) (q:draft)
kimuzo = (t:v) (w:be found/can be found) (d:passive of muzo find; kimuzo nawn lo, could no longer be found) (e:Amah ka zonzon hangin ~ nawn lo hi/a citak takpi ding mi ~ ding ahi hiam | can a truly faithful person be found) (s:kiphawkkhia) (b:muzo) (r:19.37.36/20.20.6) (q:draft)
kimvel = (t:v) (w:go around/march around/encircle) (d:go all the way round a place, as Israel marched around Jericho for seven days) (e:ni sagih sung a ~ khit uh) (r:58.11.30) (q:draft)
kin = (t:v) (w:heed/care about/be zealous for/be eager) (d:give attention or care to something, be concerned or eager about it; kin lo means ignore or neglect, kin ngaihsut means press or treat as urgent) (e:nangma thu ~ lo uh ahih manin/Paubaan’na a om lo thu bek ka ~ ding | I will care only for what is blameless/hih kammalte khempeuh na ~ ding uh | you shall heed all these words/Eite’ Pasian’ inn ~ loin i om kei ding hi | we will not neglect the house of our God) (s:awlmawh/thudon) (r:19.119.139/20.18.2/19.101.2/5.12.28/16.10.39) (q:draft)
kin = (t:v) (w:move/shift/move on) (d:change place, go from one spot to another; nunglamah kin means draw back) (e:Tua ganhingte a ~ ciangin/amau a ~ uh ciangin | when they moved/nisuahna lam mual-ah amah ~ kikin | he moved on again to the hills on the east/Hih lai panin hua lai-ah ~ in | move from here to there) (r:26.1.19/18.38.11/26.10.16/1.12.8/40.17.20) (q:draft)
Kinah = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Kinah) (d:town in the far south of Judah, toward the border of Edom) (r:6.15.22)
kinai = (t:v) (w:be near/be close) (d:be near to a place or to each other, used with tawh; khat leh khat kinai, come near one another) (e:Lasia khua tawh ~ Khawlmun Nuam kici/Salim tawh ~ Ainon khua-ah | at Aenon near Salim/thahna mun tawh ~-ah huan khat om a | near the place of execution there was a garden/Tuu Kongkhak tawh ~ | near the Sheep Gate) (a:kigamla) (b:nai) (r:44.27.8/2.14.20/43.3.23/43.19.41/43.5.2) (q:draft)
kinai = (t:adj) (w:close/near) (d:of kinship, closely related; a kinai beh, a close relative) (e:na pa tawh a ~ beh numei/na nu tawh a ~ beh numei ahi hi | she is a close relative of your mother/amaute in nangmah tawh a ~ beh numei | they are women closely related to you) (b:nai) (r:3.18.12/3.18.13/3.18.17) (q:draft)
kinaih = (t:v) (w:draw near each other/close in/draw up) (d:ki each other with naih approach: of two armies, come up close to one another for battle) (e:a kido dingin ~ uh hi) (b:naih) (r:9.17.21) (q:draft)
kinailua = (t:adj) (w:too closely related) (d:kinai closely related, with lua too much; si kinailua mi, a person too near in blood) (e:amaute in si ~ mi tawh) (b:kinai) (r:3.20.12) (q:draft)
kinaina = (t:n) (w:relationship/kinship/closeness) (d:kinai be near or closely related, with the noun suffix na; tawh marks the other person) (e:amah tawh a ~ zia) (b:kinai) (r:17.8.1) (q:draft)
kinaipen = (t:adj) (w:nearest/closest) (d:kinai, be near, with pen, most; used with tawh for the place it is nearest to) (e:a kithat mipa tawh a ~ khuapi upate/omna tawh a ~ khuapi upate in | the elders of the town nearest to where he lies/Na omna uh tawh a ~ kulh vang | the gap in the wall nearest to where you are) (s:naipen) (a:gamlapen) (b:kinai) (r:5.21.6/5.21.3/30.4.3) (q:draft)
kinaipih = (t:n) (w:close relative/near kin) (d:one who is closely related, also used before a noun as closely related) (e:A ~ pen khat in a phu la-in/na ~ na behte uh | your closely related kin/ka ~ pen nangmah na om hi | you are my nearest relative/Ama innkuan sunga a ~ a beh khatpeuh in | any close relative in his family) (s:tanau) (b:kinai) (r:4.35.19/3.18.6/24.32.7/3.25.49) (q:draft)
kinaipihpen = (t:n) (w:nearest relative/closest kin) (d:kinaipih close relative, with the superlative pen) (e:lak panin ka ~ nangmah na om) (b:kinaipih) (r:24.32.7) (q:draft)
kinaita = (t:v) (w:have come near/be now close) (d:kinai be near, with ta marking a change now reached) (e:lei tawh ~ hi hang) (b:kinai) (r:44.27.27) (q:draft)
kinak = (t:adv) (w:hard/greatly/tightly) (d:ki with nak, strongly, placed before a verb: kinak hawl be driven hard, kinak mat hold fast to each other, kinak lin be greatly shaken) (e:ni khat sung ~ hawl lua leh/Tuate ~ mat lua ahih manin | because they hold so fast to each other/kei ka ~ lin' kei ding hi | I will not be greatly shaken) (r:1.33.13/18.41.17/19.62.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
kinakko = (t:v) (w:shout loudly/cry out) (d:kinak strongly with ko shout: shout hard; with semsem, all the more) (e:ci-in a ~ zaw semsem uh hi/amah ~ semsem a | he shouted all the more) (r:41.15.14/42.18.39) (q:draft)
kinam = (t:v) (w:kiss each other) (d:reciprocal ki with nam kiss, smell) (e:khatlekhat kihopihin na ~ un) (r:47.13.12) (q:draft)
kinamin = (t:v) (w:kissing each other/with a kiss) (d:kinam with the connective in; greeting one another with a kiss) (e:ki-itna lungsim tawh ~ na kihopih un/amau khat leh khat ~ | they kissed each other/Khristian ki-itna tawh khatlekhat ~ na kihopih un | greet one another with a kiss of Christian love/note khatlekhat ~ na kihopih un | greet one another with a kiss) (b:kinam) (r:52.5.26/9.20.41/60.5.14/45.16.16) (q:draft)
kinangin = (t:v) (w:leaning on/supporting oneself on) (d:reflexive ki with nang prop up, support, and the linking ending in) (e:a ciangkhut dawnah ~ Pasian a bia) (r:58.11.21) (q:draft)
kinapna = (t:n) (w:kiss) (d:napna kiss, with the reciprocal prefix ki: the kissing of one another as a greeting) (e:a siangtho ~ tawh na kihopih un/Khat leh khat siangtho ~ tawh na kihopih un | greet one another with a holy kiss) (b:napna) (r:52.5.26/45.16.16) (q:draft)
kinawh = (t:v) (w:hurry) (d:act or come without delay; hong kinawh in is hurry here, come quickly) (e:hong ~ in/Hong ~ in la hong ciah in | hurry and come back/~ in la, tua lai-ah tai in | hurry and flee there/Levi mite ~ lo uh hi | the Levites did not hurry) (s:nawhtat) (a:zekai) (r:9.20.38/14.35.21/9.23.27/1.19.22/14.24.5)
kinawh = (t:adv) (w:quickly) (d:kinawh, hurry, used before another action: in a hurry, at once) (e:David a muh ciangin ~ a/Kumpipa’ thupiakna tawh laitaite ~ sawl a | at the command of the king the couriers were sent off in haste) (s:manlang) (r:9.25.23/17.3.15)
kinawhin = (t:adv) (w:quickly/in haste/hurriedly) (d:form of kinawh with -in, hurrying to do the next action) (e:Tua ciangin Abigail ~/Abigail ~ ding-in la tungah tuang a | Abigail quickly got up and mounted a donkey/hong ~ keimah dawn dingin hong pai lo hi lecin | if you had not come quickly to meet me/~, nangma thupiaknate zuih ding ka zekai kei hi | I hurry and do not delay to obey your commands) (s:manlangin) (b:kinawh) (r:9.25.18/19.119.60/9.25.42/9.25.34) (q:draft)
kinawhkhia = (t:v) (w:be driven out/be banished) (d:passive with ki of nawhkhia drive out) (e:amaute ~ gawpin a tuk ding) (b:nawhkhia) (r:24.23.12) (q:draft)
kinawhna = (t:n) (w:haste/hurrying) (d:kinawh hurry, with the noun suffix na) (e:Ka ~ ding Pasian in kei) (b:kinawh) (r:14.35.21) (q:draft)
kinawhsa = (t:see) <kinawhsa-in>
kinawhsa-in = (t:adv) (w:in haste/hurriedly) (d:kinawh hurry with sa and the adverb ending in: in a hurried state) (e:~ na paikhia kei ding uh hi) (r:23.52.12) (q:draft)
kinawhsak = (t:v) (w:hurry/make haste/hasten) (d:kinawh hurry with sak; va kinawhsak un, go and have them hurry, said of fetching the wailing women quickly) (e:Va ~ un la) (b:kinawh) (r:24.9.18) (q:draft)
kinawlkhin = (t:v) (w:be set aside/be discarded) (d:passive with ki of nawlkhin put aside, reject) (e:om lo ahih manin ~ hi) (b:nawlkhin) (r:58.7.18) (q:draft)
kinawmsawm = (t:see) <kinawmsawm-in>
kinawmsawm-in = (t:v) (w:collapsing/being brought down) (d:said of those who sink down and fall, with the linking ending in; the exact sense of the base is not certain) (e:Amaute ~ puk ding uh a) (s:kinawmsawmin) (r:19.20.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
kinawmsawmin = (t:v) (w:collapsing/being brought down) (d:said of those who sink down and fall, with the linking ending in; the exact sense of the base is not certain) (e:Amaute ~ pukgawp ding uh a) (s:kinawmsawm-in) (r:19.20.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
kinawmvalh = (t:see) <kinawmvalh-in>
kinawmvalh-in = (t:v) (w:being swallowed up) (d:passive with ki of nawmvalh swallow whole, with the linking ending in) (e:Israel khempeuh ~ kisusia ding a) (s:kinawmvalhin) (r:28.8.8) (q:draft)
kinawmvalhin = (t:v) (w:being swallowed up) (d:passive with ki of nawmvalh swallow whole, with the linking ending in) (e:Israel khempeuh ~ kisusia ding a) (s:kinawmvalh-in) (r:28.8.8) (q:draft)
kinawngkai = (t:v) (w:be disturbed/be troubled) (d:ki with nawngkai be troubled; kinawngkai sak, be caused trouble) (e:a ~ sak nawn loh nadingin) (b:nawngkai) (r:13.17.9) (q:draft)
kinawngkaisak = (t:v) (w:be disturbed/be troubled) (d:passive of nawngkaisak trouble, disturb, with the prefix ki) (e:a ~ nawn loh nadingin) (b:nawngkaisak) (r:10.7.10/13.17.9) (q:draft)
kinawtkhia = (t:v) (w:be scoured off/be rubbed off/be removed) (d:passive of nawtkhia, here in the sense rub or scrape out: of the burnt crust in a cooking pot) (e:a kang-op a ~ ngei lo beel) (b:nawtkhia) (r:26.24.6) (q:draft)
kinawtngil = (t:adj) (w:polished/burnished) (d:rubbed until it shines, said of metal) (e:a ~ sumngo tawh kibang uh hi/a ~ thaltang bangin kei hong bawl a | he made me like a polished arrow/mi thah nadingin ~ a | it is polished for killing/sumsan ~ tawh kibangin | like burnished metal) (s:zutsiang) (r:26.1.7/23.49.2/26.21.28/26.8.2) (q:draft)
kine = (t:n) (w:food) (d:what is eaten: ne, eat, with the prefix ki, used before a noun as in a kine an, food that is eaten) (e:A ~ an nam khempeuh zong/a om a ~ thei ding an tungah | on any food in it that may be eaten/An khempeuh a ~ thei ding ahi hi | all food may be eaten) (b:ne) (r:1.6.21/3.11.34/45.14.20)
kineh = (t:v) (w:come close/go near/keep close) (d:ki with neh press close: get close up to a person or place, with tawh for a person) (e:Tua bang numei tawh ~ kha kei un/Krete tuikulh a ~ thei zahzahin | as close to the island of Crete as possible) (b:neh) (r:20.5.8/44.27.13) (q:draft)
kinehcipin = (t:v) (w:crowding together/pressing on one another) (d:reciprocal ki with neh press and cip tightly, and the linking ending in; of a packed crowd) (e:gawp dongin ~ a om laitakin) (r:42.12.1) (q:draft)
kinehkha = (t:v) (w:come close to/get near) (d:ki with neh come near, press close, and kha happen to; used with tawh and kei as a warning not to get near someone) (e:Tua bang numei tawh ~ kei unla) (r:20.5.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
kinehlua = (t:v) (w:be too crowded/press too closely) (d:kineh press close together with lua too much: of a crowd, packed so tight that no one can get through) (e:mihonpi ~ ahih manin/mihon ~ uh ahih manin | because the crowd was packed too tightly) (b:kineh) (r:41.2.4/42.8.19) (q:draft)
kinei = (t:v) (w:consider oneself/claim to be) (d:after a word with -a: regard oneself as, or set oneself to do, what is named; mipil-a kinei, think oneself wise) (e:mipil-a ~ na hih leh/a ci-a ~ na hih uh leh | if you claim, saying/hih mite zong thumu-in ~-in | these people too, claiming to be dreamers) (s:kisa) (b:nei) (r:18.34.16/29.3.4/23.36.7/65.1.8) (q:draft)
kinei = (t:v) (w:be held/be had/be done) (d:passive of nei: be had, held or carried out, as a feast, an inquiry or a custom) (e:kum simin a ~ pawi thum/thukanna ~ ding hi | an inquiry shall be held/a siangtho-in ~ ding hi | they will be held as holy/thupha piakna-in ~ ding uh hi | they will be regarded as a blessing) (b:nei) (r:14.8.12/3.19.20/38.14.20/38.8.13) (q:draft)
kineih = (t:v) (w:pretend/feign/pose as) (d:make oneself out to be what one is not; follows the thing pretended) (e:A thuum mi bangin ~ in la/Amnon lumin a cina ~ hi | Amnon lay down and pretended to be ill/numei dang khatin ~ hi | she pretended to be another woman/a kilehkik hong ~ bek hi | she only pretended to return to me) (s:kineihkhem) (r:10.14.2/24.3.10/10.13.6/11.14.5) (q:draft)
kineihin = (t:v) (w:pretending/feigning) (d:kineih with the linking in, pretending to do or be something) (e:a zahtakbawl ~ a mai-ah a kun uh hi/a cingin a theinuam ~ | pretending to want to know more exactly/Zuau thu tawh maangmu ~ | pretending to see visions, with lies/thuthei ~ mi khem theite | those who deceive people by pretending to know) (b:kineih) (r:41.15.19/44.23.20/26.13.9/55.3.13) (q:draft)
kineihin = (t:v) (w:going to law/disputing) (d:in thu kineihin, having a dispute or lawsuit with one another) (e:khatlekhat thu ~ zum na kitun uh a) (r:46.6.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
kineihkhem = (t:v) (w:pretend/be hypocritical/be false) (d:put on a false appearance to deceive; mihoih a kineihkhem mi is a hypocrite, kamsang kineihkhem a false prophet) (e:Kamsang ~ mi tampi hong piang ding/mihoih a ~ mite aw | you hypocrites/lungsim takpi tawh thudong a va ~ dingin | to go and pretend to ask sincerely/leitungah kamsang a ~ tampi hong om khinta hi | many false prophets have come into the world) (s:kineih) (r:40.24.11/40.15.7/42.20.20/62.4.1) (q:draft)
kineihkhemin = (t:v) (w:pretending/under false pretences) (d:kineihkhem pretend, with the linking ending in) (e:thu um mi ~ kote lakah) (b:kineihkhem) (r:48.2.4) (q:draft)
kineihkhemna = (t:n) (w:hypocrisy/pretence) (d:kineihkhem, pretend, with the noun suffix na: a show of goodness that is not real) (e:mawhna le ~ bek a om hi/gitlohna, zuauna, ~, huaihamna | malice, deceit, hypocrisy, envy/Amau’ ~ tawh kizui-in | in keeping with their hypocrisy) (s:simtatna/kineihna) (b:kineihkhem) (r:40.23.28/42.12.1/60.2.1/42.20.47) (q:draft)
kineihkhemte = (t:n) (w:pretenders/hypocrites/false ones) (d:plural; those who pretend to be what they are not, as in kamsang kineihkhemte false prophets) (e:Kamsang a ~ in leitung thu gen uh a/sawltak a ~ hi uh a | they are false apostles/a ~ in na lungsim uh siangsak un | you double-minded, purify your hearts/le kamsang ~ hong piang ding a | and false prophets will appear) (s:simtatte) (b:kineihkhem) (r:62.4.5/41.13.22/47.11.13/59.4.8) (q:draft)
kineihlai = (t:v) (w:still claim to be/still pretend to be) (d:kineih make oneself out to be, with lai still) (e:kamsang a ~ teitei leh) (r:38.13.3) (q:draft)
kineihna = (t:n) (w:dispute/lawsuit) (d:in thu kineihna, a case that people have against one another: thu neihna, lawsuit, with the reciprocal prefix ki) (e:Mite kikalah thu ~ om a) (b:neihna) (r:5.25.1) (q:draft)
kineihna = (t:n) (w:pretence/show) (d:kineih pretend, with the noun suffix na) (e:~ tawh saupipi thu na ngen uh hi) (s:kineihkhemna) (b:kineih) (r:40.23.14) (q:draft)
kineihnate = (t:n) (w:disputes/lawsuits) (d:plural of kineihna; thu kineihnate are the cases people have against one another) (e:Kei guak in note’ thu ~) (b:kineihna) (r:5.1.12) (q:draft)
kineihnuam = (t:v) (w:want to make oneself/claim to be) (d:kineih make oneself out to be, with nuam want) (e:hinapi-in Pasian na ~ hi) (r:43.10.33) (q:draft)
kineihpih = (t:v) (w:go to law with/dispute with/confront) (d:in thu kineihpih, have a case against someone in court: kineih as in kineihna dispute, with pih together with) (e:thukhen zumah thu ~ theih hi lo hi) (r:18.9.32) (q:draft)
kineipa = (t:n) (w:pretender/self-styled man) (d:man who makes himself out to be what is named, kinei claim to be with pa marking a man; kamsanga kineipa, you who call yourself a seer) (e:Kamsanga ~ aw, na Judah gamah ciah) (b:kinei) (r:30.7.12) (q:draft)
kineite = (t:n) (w:those regarded as/those considered) (d:kinei be held or regarded as, with te; the ones who are counted as, or count themselves as, something) (e:Mi hoih-a ~ in lamdang hong sa uh a/khua mu thei a ~ | those who consider themselves able to see/makai lian a ~ tawh | with those regarded as great leaders/zato siam-a ~ tawh na kibang uh hi | you are like those who claim to be skilled doctors) (b:kinei) (r:18.17.8/18.13.4/43.9.39/48.2.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
kinek = (t:v) (w:be eaten) (d:passive of ne eat, in the form used before bang, leh and nouns) (e:A ni thum ni-in a ~ peuhmah leh/Sanang ahi a, sakhital ahi zongin a ~ mah bangin | just as gazelle or deer is eaten/biakpiakna sa khatpeuh peuh a ~ leh | if any of the offering meat is eaten/sakhi ahi zongin a ~ bangin | as deer is eaten) (b:nek) (r:3.19.7/5.12.22/3.7.18/5.15.22) (q:draft)
kinek = (t:v) (w:devour one another/eat each other) (d:reciprocal of ne eat) (e:na kipeh, na ~ uh leh) (b:nek) (r:48.5.15) (q:draft)
kinelsak = (t:v) (w:be made smooth/be smoothed) (d:nel fine or smooth with the causative sak and passive ki: of rough ground) (e:a leihumte ~ ding hi) (r:42.3.5) (q:draft)
kinem = (t:v) (w:be comforted/be consoled) (d:nem soft, gentle, with the prefix ki: be soothed; kinem zo lo is cannot be comforted) (e:ahih manin ~ zo lo hi/om lo ahih ciangin ~ zo lo hi | since they are no more, she cannot be comforted) (s:kihehnem) (b:nem) (r:24.31.15/40.2.18) (q:draft)
kinemang = (t:v) (w:be eaten up/be devoured/be destroyed) (d:passive of nemang, eat up, with the prefix ki: be grazed bare or devoured, said of a vineyard whose hedge is taken away) (e:ka lakhia ding a, ~ ding hi) (b:nemang) (r:23.5.5) (q:draft)
kinen = (t:see) <kinen'niamna>
kinen'niamna = (t:n) (w:oppression) (d:nen’niam, oppress, with the prefix ki and the noun suffix na: the state of being pressed down by an enemy) (e:cih leh Israel a ~) (s:kinetniamna/kisukcipna) (a:suahtakna) (r:12.13.4) (q:draft)
kinen'niamnate = (t:n) (w:oppressions/acts of oppression) (d:kinen'niamna oppression, with the plural te) (e:buaina lianpite, ~ hong mu in) (s:kinenniamnate/kisukcipnate/bawlsiatnate) (r:30.3.9) (q:draft)
kinencip = (t:v) (w:oppress each other) (d:nencip, press down or oppress, with the reciprocal prefix ki: people oppress one another) (e:~ gawp ding uh hi/mi khempeuh in a veengte ciat, ~ gawp | everyone will oppress his own neighbour) (b:nencip) (r:23.3.5) (q:draft)
kinengcip = (t:v) (w:be crushed/be pressed down) (d:passive of nengcip, crush or press hard, with the prefix ki: of a person, be utterly crushed; of a measure of grain, be pressed down) (e:Kei hong ~ gawpin/Ka tha bei khinin hong ~ hi | my strength is gone and I am crushed/teh hoih bek tham lo, a ~ | not only a good measure, but pressed down) (b:nengcip) (r:19.38.8/42.6.38) (q:draft)
kinengniam = (t:v) (w:be oppressed/be mistreated/be afflicted) (d:passive of nengniam, oppress, with the prefix ki; a kinengniam mite are the oppressed) (e:a ~ mi khempeuh adingin/amaute kum zali sung ~ ding | they will be oppressed for four hundred years/Topa aw, kei hong ~ hi | Lord, I am oppressed/A zawng, a cimawh, a ~ mite | the poor, the needy, the oppressed/a ~ mite tungah amau’ kisapnate | to the oppressed what they need) (s:kinenniam/kibawlsia/kisikcip) (a:suakta) (b:nengniam) (r:19.103.6/1.15.13/23.38.14/23.26.6/23.58.10) (q:draft)
kinengniamin = (t:v) (w:being oppressed/oppressed) (d:kinengniam, be oppressed, with the linking ending in: being oppressed, followed by another verb) (e:note hong ~ hong kisugawp tawntung/note hong ~ na nate uh hong kisut niloh ding | you will be oppressed and robbed day after day/Amah ~ gimna a kithuaksak hangin | though he was oppressed and made to suffer) (b:kinengniam) (r:5.28.33/23.53.7/5.28.29) (q:draft)
kinengniamte = (t:n) (w:the oppressed/oppressed people) (d:kinengniam be oppressed, with the plural te: those who are oppressed) (e:Topa in a ~ a dingin/a ~ a suaktasak ding | to set the oppressed free) (a:nengniamte) (b:kinengniam) (r:19.103.6/42.4.18) (q:draft)
kinenniam = (t:v) (w:be oppressed/be afflicted) (d:passive of nenniam, press down or oppress, with the prefix ki) (e:Ahih hangin amaute a ~ ciangin) (s:kinengniam/kisikcip) (b:nenniam) (r:2.1.12) (q:draft)
kinenniamnate = (t:n) (w:oppressions/acts of oppression) (d:kinenniam be oppressed, with the noun suffix na and the plural te) (e:buaina lianpite le ~ hong mu un) (s:kinen'niamnate/kisukcipnate) (b:kinenniam) (r:30.3.9) (q:draft)
kinet = (t:v) (w:oppress/press down) (d:first part of kinet niamna, oppression, written as two words in one verse; the usual spelling is kinetniamna in one word) (e:cih leh ~ niamna bekbek tawh/~ niamna bekbek tawh a dim hi | it is full of nothing but oppression) (r:24.6.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
kinetniamna = (t:n) (w:oppression) (d:netniamna oppression with the prefix ki: people oppressing one another, or the state of being oppressed) (e:~ bekbek tawh a kidim hi/Thumanin gamta unla, ~ kheel un) (s:kinen'niamna/kisukcipna) (a:suahtakna) (b:netniamna) (r:24.6.6/23.1.17) (q:draft)
kineu = (t:n) (w:little horn/small horn) (d:ki, horn, with neu, small: the little horn seen in the visions of Daniel) (e:tua ~ in kiphatsakna kamsia a pau/a dang ~ khat hong po a | another little horn came up/~ dang khat hong kipan a | another little horn came forth) (r:27.7.11/27.8.9/27.7.8) (q:draft)
kineu = (t:v) (w:be small in one's own eyes/think oneself small) (d:neu, small, with the reflexive prefix ki, used with ngaihsut, think: na kineu ngaihsut, you thought of yourself as small) (e:Nang na ~ ngaihsut hun a om hangin) (b:neu) (r:9.15.17) (q:draft, low confidence)
kineubawl = (t:v) (w:be degraded/be belittled/be humiliated) (d:passive of neubawl, make small: be made little of or disgraced in the eyes of others) (e:na sanggampa uh a ~ suak ding hi) (a:kipahtawi) (b:neubawl) (r:5.25.3) (q:draft)
kinga = (t:v) (w:rest on/be set on/come to rest) (d:be placed so as to rest or lie on something, with tungah, on; of a hand, be laid on someone) (e:Ararat mual tungah teembaw ~ hi/Bawngtal sawm-le-nihte tungah tua tuikuangpi ~ a | the Sea rested on the twelve bulls/ama' tungah eite’ khut ~ kei hen | let our hand not be laid on him/a leengpeite leilak ah ~ hi | the wheels rested on the ground/mihaite’ nungzang ah ciangduai ~ hi | a rod falls on the back of fools) (r:1.8.4/14.4.4/1.37.27/26.1.15/20.10.13) (q:draft)
kingah = (t:v) (w:be obtained/be gained/be received/be won) (d:passive of ngah, get, with the prefix ki: something is got, won or received; with pan or panin, from) (e:lungsim niamkhiatna tawh pilna ~ hi/ngaihsut siamnate tawh gualzawhna ~ hi | victory is won through wise counsel/Topa kiang pan bekin thutang ~ hi | justice is obtained only from the Lord/thukham zuihna hangin dikkisakna ~ leh | if righteousness were gained by keeping the law/Laodikia khua pan a ~ ding lai | the letter to be received from Laodicea) (b:ngah) (r:20.11.2/20.24.6/20.29.26/48.2.21/51.4.16) (q:draft)
kingahin = (t:v) (w:being obtained/being received) (d:kingah be obtained, with the linking ending in) (e:Pasian tawh kipawl theihna ~) (b:kingah) (r:48.2.16) (q:draft)
kingahkik = (t:v) (w:be received back/be received in reply) (d:kingah be obtained, with kik back, again) (e:tung pan thu a ~ hun dong) (b:kingah) (r:15.5.5) (q:draft)
kingahsak = (t:v) (w:be given/be granted) (d:passive of ngahsak cause to receive: be made to receive a share) (e:ngahte mah amah zong ~ a) (s:kipiak) (b:ngahsak) (r:5.33.21) (q:draft, low confidence)
kingahte = (t:n) (w:spoils/things obtained) (d:kingah be obtained, with the plural te; gal sunga a kingahte, what was taken in war) (e:Gal sunga a ~ khen nih) (b:kingah) (r:4.31.27) (q:draft)
kingahzo = (t:v) (w:can be had/can be obtained) (d:kingah be obtained, with zo be able) (e:numei paktat khat ~ a) (b:kingah) (r:20.6.26) (q:draft)
kingai = (t:v) (w:be betrothed/be lovers/love each other) (d:love each other as man and woman, be promised to each other in marriage; with tawh for the partner) (e:Mari in Josef tawh ~ a/Josef min neipa tawh a ~ nungak | a virgin pledged to a man named Joseph/mi tampi tawh ~ khin zo napi | though you have had many lovers/numei khat tawh va ~ in | go and love a woman) (a:kimudah) (r:40.1.18/24.3.1/42.1.27/28.3.1) (q:draft)
kingai = (t:v) (w:be heard/be listened to) (d:passive of ngai, listen, with the prefix ki: of a prayer or voice, be heard) (e:na thungetna uh hong ~ ding) (s:kiza) (b:ngai) (r:23.58.4) (q:draft)
kingaih = (t:v) (w:love each other/be lovers) (d:form of kingai used as a verbal noun, being in love with someone, with tawh: nang tawh kingaih, to be in love with you) (e:nang tawh ~ nuam mahmah hi) (b:kingai) (r:22.4.10) (q:draft)
kingaihna = (t:n) (w:love/courtship) (d:the love of a man and a woman for each other) (e:nungak leh tangval a ~ zia/ko’ ~ nong suknawi loh nadingun | so that you do not disturb our love) (s:itna) (a:kimuhdahna) (b:kingaih) (r:20.30.19/22.2.7) (q:draft)
kingaihsun = (t:v) (w:consider oneself/think oneself/regard oneself) (d:ngaihsun, think, with the reflexive prefix ki: think of oneself as being something, with a describing word followed by in or bangin) (e:a si khin ta-in ka ~ hi/kote pen kauphe bang lelin ka ~ uh a | we seemed to ourselves like mere grasshoppers/nang a suakta tuan dingin ~ kei in | do not think that you will escape/Nangmah mah a pilin ~ tawm kei in | do not think yourself wise) (s:kisa) (b:ngaihsun) (r:25.3.54/20.30.13/4.13.33/17.4.13/20.3.7) (q:draft)
kingaihsun = (t:v) (w:be careful/take heed/watch oneself) (d:as a command, kingaihsun in or kingaihsun un, watch yourselves; with loh nadingun, be careful not to do something) (e:na piak loh nadingun ~ un/Levi mite na mangngilh loh nadingun ~ un | be careful not to neglect the Levites/tuate na biak khak loh nadingun ~ un | be careful not to worship them/nang hong teel khin ahih manin tu-in ~ in | since he has chosen you, consider now) (s:kidawm/kikem) (b:ngaihsun) (r:5.12.13/5.11.16/5.12.19/13.28.10) (q:draft)
kingaihsunin = (t:v) (w:considering oneself/thinking oneself) (d:kingaihsun, consider oneself, with the linking ending in; after a phrase with bangin or in it is regarding oneself as such) (e:Pasian tawh a kikim bangin ~/A hin’ lai-in amah a lungdamin ~ | while he lives he counts himself blessed/a thupi diakin ~ | thinking themselves very important) (b:kingaihsun) (r:41.2.7/19.49.18/51.2.18) (q:draft)
kingaihsunin = (t:v) (w:being remembered/being called to mind) (d:kingaihsun in its passive sense, be called to mind, with the linking ending in) (e:mawhnate kum simin ~ a om hi) (s:kiphawkin) (b:kingaihsun) (r:58.10.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
kingaihsut = (t:v) (w:think of oneself/think of one another/regard oneself) (d:ngaihsut think with ki, turned back on oneself or shared between people; form used before ding, nading and zawh) (e:No-le-no na ~ ding zah/thu a thei-in a ~ leh | if he thinks that he knows something/leitung ngeina-ah a pilin na ~ uhleh | if you think you are wise by the ways of this world/khat leh khat a ~ ciat nadingun | so that they each care for one another) (b:ngaihsut) (r:45.12.3/46.12.25/46.8.2/46.3.18) (q:draft)
kingaihsut = (t:v) (w:be remembered/be thought of/be understood) (d:passive use; a kingaihsut nadingin, so that she is remembered; a kingaihsut zawh loh, what cannot be made sense of) (e:hih numei a ~ nadingin/a ~ zawh loh hangin ka lungkia kei uh hi | though perplexed, we do not despair) (s:kiphawk) (b:ngaihsut) (r:41.14.9/47.4.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
kingaihsutna = (t:see) <kingaihsutna-in>
kingaihsutna-in = (t:adv) (w:for one's own sake) (d:kingaihsutna, thought or regard for oneself, with in, because of: keimah ka kingaihsutna-in, for my own sake) (e:keimah ka ~ hih bangin kong hih hi) (r:23.48.11) (q:draft)
kingaihsutnate = (t:n) (w:thoughts) (d:kingaihsutna thought, thinking, with the plural te) (e:amau ~ in khat leh khat) (s:ngaihsutnate) (b:kingaihsut) (r:45.2.15) (q:draft)
kingaihsutsak = (t:v) (w:be counted as/be credited/be reckoned) (d:kingaihsut, be considered, with sak: be reckoned or counted as something; piakkhongin kingaihsutsak lo is not counted as a gift) (e:ahih manin piakkhongin ~ lo hi) (b:kingaihsut) (r:45.4.4) (q:draft)
kingak = (t:v) (w:wait for one another/be waited for) (d:ngak, wait, with the prefix ki: wait for one another; of a person, be waited for and so be given time) (e:khat leh khat na ~ kim un/kuamah ~ loin na manek tek uh a | without waiting for anyone you each eat first/hun tawmvei sung a ~ lai nadingin | so that he might be given a little more time) (s:kingakkim) (b:ngak) (r:46.11.33/27.2.16/46.11.21) (q:draft)
kingak = (t:v) (w:lean on/lean against) (d:form of kinga, rest on, used before theih and nading: lean the weight of the body against something) (e:Ka ~ theih nadingin) (s:kingam/kingap) (b:kinga) (r:7.16.26) (q:draft, low confidence)
kingakkim = (t:v) (w:wait for one another) (d:reciprocal ki with ngak wait and kim complete: wait until all are present) (e:uh ciangin ~ dimdiam un) (s:kingak) (r:46.11.33) (q:draft)
kingakna = (t:n) (w:stand/base) (d:a stand on which a thing rests, said of the wheeled bronze stands that held the basins of the temple) (e:amah in a ~ sawm bawl hi/sumngo kibawl tuikuang a ~ sawm | ten bronze stands for the basins/Leengpei zawlte a ~ tawh sakhat mah hi | the axles of the wheels were one piece with the stand/a ~ kungte tankhia-in | cutting off the side panels of the stands) (b:ngakna) (r:11.7.37/11.7.43/11.7.27/11.7.32/12.16.17) (q:draft)
kingaknate = (t:n) (w:stands/supports/bases) (d:plural of kingakna, a thing that something rests on; in the verses the movable stands under the temple basins and the base of a table) (e:tuikuang a ~ le tuate tungah/a ~ tungah a om tuikuang sawmte | the ten basins that were on the stands/Tua a ~ hih bangin kibawl hi | this is how the stands were made/tuikuangpi khat, le a ~ | the Sea and the stands) (b:kingakna) (r:14.4.14/24.27.19/11.7.43/11.7.28/12.25.16) (q:draft)
kingam = (t:v) (w:lean/lean on/prop oneself) (d:rest the weight of the body on something for support, with tungah or ah for what is leaned on) (e:a leeng sungah Israel kumpipa ~ hi/Saul a teipi tungah ~ hi | Saul was leaning on his spear/A inn tungah ~ a, a inn hoi hi | he leans on his house, but it gives way/Israel a ciangkhut dawnah amahmah ~ suk hi | Israel leaned down on the top of his staff/an a nek lai takin a ang-ah ~ a | while eating he leaned on his breast) (s:kingap/kingak) (r:14.18.34/1.47.31/10.1.6/18.8.15/43.21.20) (q:draft)
kingamin = (t:v) (w:leaning on/leaning against/propped up) (d:kingam with the connective in: resting one's weight on a person or thing) (e:a ciangkhut dawnah ~ Pasian bia a/Zeisu’ ang ah ~ lum a | lying back against the breast of Jesus/a leeng sungah Israel kumpipa ~ om hi | the king of Israel stayed propped up in his chariot/Zeisu’ ang-ah lumin, ~ a om hi | he was reclining, leaning on the breast of Jesus) (b:kingam) (r:58.11.21/11.22.35/43.13.25/43.13.23) (q:draft)
kingap = (t:v) (w:lean on/rest on) (d:put one's weight on something for support, with tungah on) (e:Nangma tungah amaute hong ~ uh ciangin) (s:kingam/kingak) (r:26.29.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
kingapna = (t:n) (w:leaning) (d:kingap lean on, with the noun suffix na; before a noun, the one on whom someone leans) (e:a ban tungah kumpipa a ~ galkap ukpa/A khut tungah a ~ pa, a ukpa | the officer on whose hand he leaned) (b:kingap) (r:12.7.2/12.7.17) (q:draft)
kingapnapa = (t:n) (w:man leaned on) (d:kingapna leaning, with pa marking a man: the officer on whose arm the king leaned) (e:a khut tungah a ~ ahi) (b:kingapna) (r:12.7.17) (q:draft)
kingawh = (t:adv) (w:forcibly/by force/violently) (d:ki with ngawh roughly, placed before a verb: kingawh laksak, be taken away by force) (e:na la uh hong ~ laksak ding a) (b:ngawh) (r:5.28.31) (q:draft)
kingeina = (t:v) (w:wear habitually/be accustomed to) (d:be used to a thing, elsewhere written in one word as kingeinaseh; here of cursing worn habitually like a garment) (e:puansilh bangin samsiatna ~ seh hi) (s:kingeinaseh) (r:19.109.18) (q:draft, low confidence)
kingeinaseh = (t:v) (w:be used to/be accustomed to) (d:be used to or accustomed to a thing; with lo or kei, not be used to it) (e:amah ~ lo ahih manin/bang hang hiam cih leh ka ~ kei hi | because I am not used to them/milim biakna thu-ah ~ lua khin uh | they have become so accustomed to idol worship) (s:kingeina) (r:9.17.39/46.8.7) (q:draft)
kingen = (t:v) (w:be asked/be requested/be demanded) (d:passive of ngen, ask, with the prefix ki: be asked for or demanded; hong kingen is asked leave of me, a kingen thungetna is the prayer that is offered) (e:ama' tungah a ~ zahzah/lim takin kei tungah David hong ~ hi | David earnestly asked leave of me/hih lai munah a ~ thungetna | the prayer offered in this place/amaute tung panin sazian ~ lo ding | no account will be demanded of them/ngahte tung panin tampi ~ ding hi | much will be demanded from those who received) (b:ngen) (r:2.21.30/9.20.28/14.7.15/12.22.7/42.12.48) (q:draft)
kingensak = (t:v) (w:pray) (d:in thu kingensak in, let prayer be made, let them pray: thu ngen pray, with ki and sak let) (e:nangma tungah thu ~ in) (b:kingen) (r:19.32.6) (q:draft)
kinget = (t:v) (w:be asked for/be demanded/be prayed) (d:form of kingen, passive of ngen ask, used before leh and ciangin) (e:tatkhiatna sum a ~ leh/Upna tawh thu a ~ ciangin | when prayer is offered in faith) (b:nget) (r:2.21.30/59.5.15) (q:draft)
kingetsak = (t:v) (w:pray for one another/be prayed for) (d:ngetsak, ask on behalf of someone, with the prefix ki: with thu, pray for one another; of prayer or blessing, be asked for someone) (e:khat leh khat ading thu na ~ un/Ama adingin thu ~ tawntung hen | may prayer be made for him continually/ama adingin thupha ~ ta hen | may blessing be asked for him) (b:ngetsak) (r:59.5.16/19.72.15) (q:draft)
kingim = (t:v) (w:be purposed/be planned/be determined) (d:passive of ngim purpose, with the prefix ki) (e:leitung buppi a dingin a ~ ahi hi) (s:kigeel/kiciangtan) (b:ngim) (r:23.14.26) (q:draft)
kingim = (t:v) (w:be aimed at) (d:passive of ngim aim at, with the prefix ki; of a tree, have the ax aimed at its root) (e:hei tawh ~ zo hi) (b:ngim) (r:40.3.10) (q:draft)
kingimzo = (t:v) (w:be aimed at already) (d:kingim be aimed at, with zo marking completion; of a tree with the ax laid to its root) (e:bulphuk dingin hei tawh ~ hi) (b:kingim) (r:42.3.9) (q:draft)
kinial = (t:v) (w:argue/dispute/contend) (d:nial, dispute, with the reciprocal prefix ki: argue with one another; tawh marks the other party and thu the matter) (e:Pasian tawh hih thu ka ~ nuam hi/Mi khat in Pasian tawh thu ~ ding hi leh | if someone wished to dispute with God/Zeisu tawh thu a ~ uh ciangin | when they argued with Jesus/tua mite tawh tampi a ~ | they argued much with those men/thuum lo, tau lo, ~ loin na hih un | do it without grumbling or arguing) (s:kiseel/kitot) (a:kithukim) (b:nial) (r:18.13.3/50.2.14/18.9.3/41.8.11/44.15.2) (q:draft)
kinial = (t:v) (w:be denied/be disowned/be set aside) (d:passive of nial, deny or refuse, with the prefix ki) (e:Pasian’ vantungmite mai-ah ~ ding hi/Pasian Lai Siangtho ~ lo ahih ciangin | since Scripture cannot be set aside) (b:nial) (r:42.12.9/43.10.35) (q:draft)
kinialin = (t:v) (w:arguing/disputing/debating) (d:kinial argue, with the linking ending in; thu kinialin, arguing over a matter) (e:mite tawh thu ~ a om hi/Na mite thu ~ a kitot loh nadingun | so that your people do not quarrel, arguing over words) (b:kinial) (r:44.9.29/55.2.14) (q:draft)
kinialkha = (t:v) (w:refuse each other/deprive each other) (d:reciprocal ki with nial refuse and kha happen to) (e:lupkhop ding ~ kei un) (r:46.7.5) (q:draft)
kinialna = (t:n) (w:argument/dispute/quarrel/controversy) (d:kinial, argue, with the noun suffix na: arguing between people; Topa a kinialna thu is the case the Lord brings against his people) (e:~ khempeuh kiciamna in a beisak hi/hehna, ~ om loin | without anger or disputing/Topa a ~ thu ngai un | hear the case of the Lord/kuamah tawh ka ~ hong mu kei uh hi | they did not find me arguing with anyone) (s:kitotna/kiselna/kiseelna) (a:kithukimna/kilemna) (b:kinial) (r:58.6.16/54.2.8/33.6.2/44.24.12) (q:draft)
kinialnate = (t:n) (w:arguments/disputes/controversies) (d:plural of kinialna) (e:thu ~ na pelh in) (s:kitotnate/kiselnate/kiseelnate) (b:kinialna) (r:55.2.23/54.6.20) (q:draft)
kiniam = (t:v) (w:be brought low/be humbled) (d:niam, low, with the prefix ki; in the verses always with koih, put: kiniam koih is be brought low, by enemies, hardship or God) (e:mihaute ~ koih suk hi/Mite’ kiliatsakna pen ~ koih ding a | the arrogance of people will be brought low/Midiante hangin Israelte ~ koih mahmah hi | Israel was brought very low because of Midian/kei hong ~ koih ciangin | when I was brought low/Nang hong ~ koih khit nungsang | now that you have been laid low) (s:kiniamkoih/kiniamkhiat) (a:kilamsang/kipahtawi) (b:niam) (r:21.10.6/19.116.6/23.2.11/7.6.6/23.14.8) (q:draft)
kiniamkhiat = (t:v) (w:humble oneself/be humbled/be brought low) (d:niamkhiat, bring down, with the prefix ki: humble oneself before God or people, or be humbled; before a noun, humble, as in lungsim kiniamkhiat mite, the humble in heart) (e:lungsim ~ mite a man-ah paipih-in/Topa mai-ah na ~ un | humble yourselves before the Lord/a kiphasakte ~ suk hi | the proud are humbled/A ~ peuhmah a kilamsang ding hi | whoever humbles himself will be exalted/na theih hangin na ~ tuan kei hi | though you knew, you have not humbled yourself) (s:kiniamsak/kiniam/kiniamkoih) (a:kiphasak/kiliansak/kilamsang) (r:19.25.9/23.5.15/59.4.10/40.23.12/27.5.22) (q:draft)
kiniamkhiatin = (t:v) (w:humbling oneself/humbly) (d:connective form of kiniamkhiat, humbling oneself or humbly, followed by another verb) (e:tawmkhat bek ~ Jerusalem ah hong pai uh hi/Israel uliante leh kumpipa ~ | the leaders of Israel and the king humbled themselves/ka mite amau mahmah ~ | my people humbling themselves/Kote ~ om napi-in | though we have humbled ourselves) (s:kiniamsakin) (b:kiniamkhiat) (r:14.30.11/14.12.6/14.7.14/23.58.3) (q:draft)
kiniamkhiatna = (t:n) (w:humility/lowliness/humbling oneself) (d:kiniamkhiat, humble oneself, with the noun suffix na: a humble attitude toward God and other people) (e:~ in pahtawina hong ngah sak hi/~ le khitui naptui tawh | with humility and with tears/~ tawh Pasian’ thu man’ ding | to obey God with humility/~ puan bangin silhin | putting on humility like a garment) (s:kiniamsakna) (a:kiphatsakna/kiliatsakna) (b:kiniamkhiat) (r:20.15.33/38.9.9/44.20.19/33.6.8/60.5.5) (q:draft)
kiniamkhiatsuk = (t:v) (w:be humbled/be brought low) (d:kiniamkhiat be humbled, with suk downward) (e:a kiliansakte pen ~ ding a) (s:kiniamkoih) (a:kilamsang) (b:kiniamkhiat) (r:42.18.14) (q:draft)
kiniamkhiatte = (t:n) (w:the humble/the lowly) (d:plural of kiniamkhiat, those who humble themselves) (e:a ~ tungah maipha pia hi/A ~ in zahtakna ngah uh a | the humble receive honor/a ~ in pahtawina ngah ding hi | the humble will gain honor/a ~ khempeuh a lianin kibawl ding hi | all who humble themselves will be made great) (s:kiniamsakte) (a:kiphasakte/kiliansakte/kihisakte) (b:kiniamkhiat) (r:20.3.34/42.18.14/20.18.12/20.29.23/40.23.12) (q:draft)
kiniamkoih = (t:v) (w:be brought low/be humbled) (d:be put in a low and helpless state by enemies or hardship) (e:kei hong ~ ciangin amah in hong huh hi/kei hong ~ mahmah hi | I am brought very low/hong ~ ahih manin kote a huh dingin | to help us, for we are brought low/Midian-te’ hangin Israel-te ~ mahmah a | Israel was brought very low because of Midian) (s:kiniam/kiniamkhiat) (a:kilamsang) (b:niamkoih) (r:19.116.6/7.6.6/19.142.6/19.79.8) (q:draft)
kiniamsak = (t:v) (w:humble oneself/submit/be humble/be made low) (d:niamsak, make low, with the prefix ki: make oneself low before another, submit; of hills, be made low) (e:ama khut vanglian nuai-ah na ~ un/Thumang-in ama pumpi a ~ hi | obediently he humbled himself/mual liante leh mual neute ~ ding hi | mountains and hills will be made low/Mi ~ sanggamte in | believers of humble state) (s:kiniamkhiat) (a:kiliansak/kiphasak) (b:niamsak) (r:60.5.6/49.5.21/50.2.8/23.40.4/59.1.9) (q:draft)
kiniamsakin = (t:v) (w:humbling oneself/with humility) (d:kiniamsak humble oneself, with the linking ending in) (e:Lungsim ~, khitui luangin Judah) (s:kiniamkhiatin) (b:kiniamsak) (r:44.20.19) (q:draft)
kiniamsakna = (t:n) (w:humility/lowliness/humiliation) (d:kiniamsak, humble oneself, with the noun suffix na: humility, or being brought low; often with lungsim or lung, heart) (e:Na khempeuh panin ~ tawh/na kizep nadingun ~ na silh un | clothe yourselves with humility/Sumhau sanggam in ~ a thuakna ah | the rich believer in his humiliation/Lung ~ deih un | desire lowliness of heart) (s:kiniamkhiatna) (a:kiphatsakna/kiliatsakna) (b:kiniamsak) (r:49.4.2/59.1.10/60.5.5/45.12.16) (q:draft)
kiniamsakte = (t:n) (w:those who humble themselves) (d:kiniamsak humble oneself, with the plural te) (e:bangin lungsim a ~ in) (s:kiniamkhiatte) (b:kiniamsak) (r:40.18.4) (q:draft)
kinil = (t:v) (w:be tossed/be thrown about) (d:passive with ki of nil throw; kinil kawikawi, be tossed to and fro) (e:lam peuhah a ~ kawikawi tuihualte) (b:nil) (r:59.1.6) (q:draft)
kinilh = (t:v) (w:be anointed) (d:passive of nilh, anoint, with the prefix ki: have oil put on one for an office; sathau a kinilh siampi is the anointed priest) (e:sathau a ~ siampipa in/kumpi-in David sathau a ~ khitna thu | the news that David had been anointed king/sathau ~ a ki-ap siampipa in | the priest who is anointed and ordained/Sathau a ~ kherubte | anointed cherubs) (s:kinuh) (b:nilh) (r:3.4.16/4.3.3/10.5.17/3.16.32/26.28.14) (q:draft)
kinilhin = (t:v) (w:being anointed/anointed) (d:kinilh be anointed, with the linking ending in) (e:amaute sathau ~ a kikipsak nading ahi hi) (b:kinilh) (r:2.29.29) (q:draft)
kinilhna = (t:n) (w:anointing) (d:kinilh, be anointed, with the noun suffix na; sathau kinilhna, anointing with oil) (e:amau’ sathau ~ in amau’ khang tawntungin/kumpi-in David sathau a ~ thu | the news that David had been anointed king) (s:nilhna) (b:kinilh) (r:2.40.15/13.14.8) (q:draft)
kinilhpa = (t:n) (w:anointed one) (d:kinilh be anointed, with pa for a man: sathau kinilhpa, the one anointed with oil, the Anointed One) (e:sathau ~ thuman lopi-in kithat ding hi/sathau ~’ ukpa hong pai dong | until the Anointed One, the ruler, comes) (s:nilhpa) (b:kinilh) (r:27.9.26/27.9.25) (q:draft)
kinilkhia = (t:v) (w:be cast out/be driven away/be exiled) (d:passive of nilkhia cast out; a kinilkhia Israelte, the outcasts of Israel) (e:amah in a ~ Israelte kaikhawm hi) (s:kinotkhia) (b:nilkhia) (r:19.147.2) (q:draft)
kinim = (t:adj) (w:dyed/colourful) (d:of cloth, coloured; puan kinim, coloured garments) (e:a kinusia puan ~ a kizemte/a ~ a kizem puan nihte | two dyed and embroidered cloths) (r:7.5.30) (q:draft, low confidence)
kinimte = (t:adj) (w:dyed/colourful) (d:kinim dyed with the plural te, of garments: the coloured ones) (e:a kinusia puan ~ Sisera adingin) (b:kinim) (r:7.5.30) (q:draft)
kinin = (t:v) (w:be concerned about/care about/give heed to) (d:kin, heed, with in; kinin nei is have concern for something) (e:Topa’ thu bek ~ nei uh hi/hih leitung vai ~ nei uh a | they are concerned about the affairs of this world/mi cimawhte’ thungetna ~ | heeding the prayer of the destitute) (b:kin) (r:46.7.32/19.102.17/46.7.33) (q:draft)
kinin = (t:v) (w:defile oneself/become unclean) (d:nin, unclean, with the reflexive prefix ki; kinin tawmsak is make oneself unclean) (e:nomau na ~ tawmsak kei ding uh hi/ganhing khatpeuh peuh tawh note na ~ tawmsak | make yourselves unclean by any creature) (s:kininsak/kinitsak) (a:kisiangsak/kisiangtho) (b:nin) (r:3.11.43/3.11.44) (q:draft)
kininsak = (t:v) (w:defile oneself/make oneself unclean) (d:ninsak, make unclean, with the reflexive prefix ki: make oneself unclean, by idols, sexual sin or contact with the dead) (e:a milimte uh tawh na ~ hi/amahmah zong ~ lo ding hi | he must not make himself unclean/tua nu tawh na ~ kei ding hi | you shall not defile yourself with her/Milim biakna tawh amaute ~ uh hi | they defile themselves with idol worship) (s:kinitsak/kininsaktawm/kidaisak) (a:kisiangsak/kisiansak) (b:ninsak) (r:26.23.30/3.21.11/3.18.20/28.6.10) (q:draft)
kininsakin = (t:v) (w:defiling oneself/being defiled/being desecrated) (d:kininsak with the linking ending in: making oneself unclean, or of a holy place, being made unclean) (e:tua nu amahmah ~ a pasal tungah/nangmah vak vai a, nang leh nang ~ | you have gone astray and defiled yourself/Ka biakinn ~, Israel gam kisusia-in | my sanctuary being desecrated and the land of Israel laid waste/ama mite lakah va ~ | defiling himself among his people) (b:kininsak) (r:4.5.27/26.25.3/4.5.20/3.21.4) (q:draft)
kininsaksa = (t:adj) (w:defiled) (d:kininsak, be made unclean, with the completive suffix sa; of a woman who has been defiled) (e:numei paktat ahih kei leh a ~ numei/a kimasa numei, a ~ numei, numei paktat | a divorced woman, a defiled woman, a prostitute) (a:siangtho) (b:kininsak) (r:3.21.7/3.21.14) (q:draft)
kininsaktawm = (t:v) (w:defile oneself/make oneself unclean) (d:ninsak defile with ki and tawm, by one's own doing: bring uncleanness on oneself) (e:noleno a ~ na hi uh hi/milim biakna tawh nangmah ~ na hih manin | because you defile yourself with idol worship) (s:kininsak) (r:26.20.31/26.22.3) (q:draft)
kinit = (t:v) (w:defile oneself/make oneself unclean) (d:the form of kinin used before tawmsak; ki with nit unclean) (e:na ~ tawmsak uh leh) (s:kinin) (b:nit) (r:3.11.43) (q:draft)
kinitsak = (t:v) (w:defile oneself/be defiled) (d:nitsak, make unclean, with the prefix ki: make oneself unclean, or of a person or holy place, be made unclean) (e:amahmah a ~ ciangin/Ka biakinn a ~ ciangin | when my temple is defiled/a mawhna uh tawh a ~ loh nadingun | so that they no longer defile themselves with their sins/tua nu a ~ khit ciangin | after she has been defiled) (s:kininsak) (a:kisiangsak) (b:nitsak) (r:4.5.29/26.20.7/26.7.22/26.14.11/5.24.4) (q:draft)
kinkhawm = (t:v) (w:move together/move along with) (d:kin move, with khawm together) (e:ciangin leengpeite tawh ~ a) (b:kin) (r:26.1.19) (q:draft)
kinkhia = (t:v) (w:move away/move off/get away) (d:shift out of the place where one is, with khia out; as a command, go away; of a mountain, be moved from its place) (e:a omna uh pan a ~ uh hi/Satan aw, ka nungah ~ in | get behind me, Satan/ama omna panin amah ~ thei lo hi | it cannot move from its place/mualte a ~ dingin ngaihsun na hi hiam | do you think the mountains should be moved) (b:kin) (r:66.6.14/40.17.20/41.8.33/23.46.7/18.18.4) (q:draft)
kinkhiat = (t:v) (w:turn away/move away/depart) (d:kin move with khiat out, away; used with kiang pan, from) (e:Pasian kiang pan na ~ loh nadingun) (b:kin) (r:58.3.12) (q:draft)
kinlo = (t:v) (w:not be moved/not be shaken) (d:kin move, with the negative lo written as one word) (e:ka thuciamna ~ ding hi) (b:kin) (r:23.54.10) (q:draft)
kinloin = (t:v) (w:neglecting/not caring about) (d:kin heed with lo not and the linking ending in: without care for, neglecting) (e:Pasian’ biakinn ~ i om kei ding hi/Adangte in ahihleh Jesuh Khrih thu ~ | the others do not care about the things of Jesus Christ) (b:kin) (r:16.10.39/50.2.21) (q:draft)
kinna = (t:n) (w:zeal/concern/eagerness) (d:kin, care about or be eager, with the noun suffix na) (e:~ puan tawh kitun ding hi/lungsim takpi tawh ~ na nei uh a | you had true earnestness/na hong ~ uh na hong lah nading uh hun | an opportunity to show your concern for me) (b:kin) (r:23.59.17/50.4.10/47.7.11) (q:draft)
kinnamon = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:cinnamon) (d:a fragrant spice and the tree it comes from, kinnamon kung; the English word) (e:thalsing leh ~ kung/oloes paknamtui leh ~ paknamtui tawh | with perfume of aloes and cinnamon) (s:sinnamon) (r:22.4.14/20.7.17) (q:draft)
kinolh = (t:v) (w:be rejected/be turned away) (d:passive of nolh, reject, with the prefix ki: be turned away in shame) (e:a ci mite ~ ding a) (a:kisan) (b:nolh) (r:23.42.17) (q:draft)
kinomsak = (t:v) (w:be soothed/be softened/be moistened) (d:passive of nomsak moisten: of wounds, be softened with oil) (e:sathau tawh ~ lo hi) (b:nomsak) (r:23.1.6) (q:draft)
kinophuah = (t:v) (w:name oneself/call oneself/take a name) (d:with min tawh and amahmah, give oneself an added name; phuah is give a name) (e:Israel min tawh amahmah ~ ding hi) (r:23.44.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
kinopmawhna = (t:n) (w:ill feeling/resentment/discord) (d:ill feeling toward others, a mind that is not at ease with them; lungsim kinopmawhna is resentment in the heart, named beside kitotna, quarrelling) (e:kitotna le lungsim ~ nei hetloin) (s:kilemlohna) (r:54.2.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
kinot = (t:v) (w:be pushed/be driven) (d:passive with ki of not, push or drive; kinot khia is be driven out or cut off) (e:gamlapi-ah kei hong ~ khia hi) (s:kihawl/kisawn) (b:not) (r:19.31.22) (q:draft)
kinotkhia = (t:v) (w:be driven out/be driven away/be routed) (d:passive of notkhia, drive away) (e:Egypt gam panin amaute ~ a/Israelte mai-ah amaute ~ hi | they were routed before the Israelites/amaute ~ gawpin a tuk ding uh hi | they will be driven out and will fall) (s:kihawlkhia/kinawhkhia) (b:notkhia) (r:2.12.39/9.7.10/24.23.12) (q:draft)
kinotsuk = (t:v) (w:be pushed down/be driven down) (d:kinot be pushed, with suk downward; paired with kinotto, be driven this way and that) (e:hong ~ hong kinotto kawikawi hi) (b:kinot) (r:46.4.11) (q:draft)
kinotto = (t:v) (w:be pushed up/be driven up) (d:kinot be pushed, with to upward; paired with kinotsuk, be driven this way and that) (e:hong kinotsuk hong ~ kawikawi hi) (b:kinot) (r:46.4.11) (q:draft)
kinsak = (t:v) (w:move/remove/shift) (d:kin, move, with causative sak: make something change its place) (e:mual ~ zawh nading upna) (b:kin) (r:46.13.2) (q:draft)
kinsak = (t:v) (w:make heed/cause to care about) (d:kin, heed or care about, with causative sak; hong kinsak kei in, do not let me give my attention to) (e:kei hong ~ kei in la) (b:kin) (r:19.119.37) (q:draft, low confidence)
kinuai = (t:v) (w:swirl/churn) (d:of a storm, whirl round and round, with nainai) (e:A hehna hong ~ nainai-in hong paikhia ta a) (r:24.30.23/24.23.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
kinuai = (t:v) (w:be fondled/be squeezed/be rubbed) (d:passive with ki of nuai, rub or press; with gawp, roughly) (e:na nawi hong ~ gawpsakin) (s:kinuaigawp) (r:26.23.21) (q:draft, low confidence)
kinuai = (t:v) (w:be subdued/be made subject) (d:in the compound kinuai-siah, be put under) (e:gam sung khempeuh ~-siah hi | the whole land is subdued) (s:kinuaisiah) (b:nuai) (r:13.22.18) (q:draft, low confidence)
kinuaigawp = (t:v) (w:be fondled/be squeezed) (d:passive with ki of nuai rub, knead, with gawp roughly, thoroughly) (e:na nawi hong ~ sakin) (s:kinuai) (r:26.23.21) (q:draft)
kinuaisiah = (t:v) (w:be subdued/be subjugated/be brought low) (d:passive of nuaisiah, subdue; a kinuaisiah mite, those who are cast down) (e:Tua bangin Filistia mite ~ hi/a ~ mite a hehnem thei Pasian | God who is able to comfort the downcast/ama mite’ mai-ah gam sung khempeuh ~ hi | the whole land is subdued before his people/tua ciangin Fillistiate ~ hi | then the Philistines were subjugated) (s:kizo/kizawh/guallel) (a:gualzo) (b:nuaisiah) (r:13.20.4/47.7.6/13.22.18) (q:draft)
kinuam = (t:v) (w:be glad/be pleased) (d:impersonal ki with nuam be glad: there is gladness, people rejoice) (e:hong pai mite hangin ~ mahmah hi) (b:nuam) (r:45.10.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
kinuamsak = (t:v) (w:take heart/cheer up/be comforted) (d:with lung or lungsim heart: nuamsak gladden with ki oneself, cheer oneself, take courage) (e:na lung ~ in/Ka ta aw, na lungsim ~ in | take heart, my child) (a:lungkia) (b:nuamsak) (r:40.9.22/40.9.2) (q:draft)
kinuh = (t:v) (w:be anointed/rub on oneself/be smeared) (d:passive of nuh, rub on: of oil or ointment put on a person or thing; sathau kinuh is be anointed or rubbed with oil) (e:kisilin sathau ~ in la/Biakna tau sathau a ~ ni-in | on the day the altar was anointed/Saul’ lum, sathau ~ lo hi | the shield of Saul, not rubbed with oil/ninna tawh ~ loin | not smeared with filth) (s:kinilh/kizut) (b:nuh) (r:8.3.3/4.7.10/10.1.21/61.3.14) (q:draft)
kinuihsan = (t:v) (w:be laughed at/be mocked/be scorned) (d:passive of nuihsan; also laugh among themselves) (e:Eite hong ~ kha ding ahih ciangin/~ lel ding hi | he would only be laughed at/hong thusimlohna tawh amau ~ uh hi | they laugh among themselves in scorn of us) (s:kisimmawh/kizahko/kiphitsan) (b:nuihsan) (r:1.38.23/22.8.7/19.80.6) (q:draft)
kinung = (t:adv) (w:later/afterwards) (d:ki with nung, after, placed before a verb: kinung theih be known later, kinung latsak show afterwards) (e:damdamin hong ~ theih hi/kei adingin hong ~ latsak ding hi | it will show for me later/a ~ piak Thukham | the law that was given later/a vun a ~-at ahi hi | he was circumcised afterwards) (b:nung) (r:54.5.24/1.30.33/48.3.17/45.4.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
kinung = (t:v) (w:turn the back) (d:only in kinung hei, turn one's back to flee) (e:na galte khempeuh uh ~ hei-in | all your enemies turning their backs) (s:lehngat) (b:nung) (r:2.23.27) (q:draft, low confidence)
kinungkiksak = (t:v) (w:be turned back/be driven back) (d:passive of nungkiksak turn back) (e:khempeuh maizumin ~ ta hen) (s:kilehhawl) (b:nungkiksak) (r:19.129.5) (q:draft)
Kinungleh = (t:name) (w:Kinungleh)
Kinunglehhei = (t:v) (w:look back/turn back) (d:turn oneself round to look back, from nung back, leh opposite and kihei turn; written with a capital at the start of a sentence, and Kinunglehhei kik lo is without turning back) (e:~ kik lo uh hi) (r:24.46.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
kinungsik = (t:v) (w:regret afterwards/be sorry later) (d:nung after with kisik regret: come to regret a thing once it is done) (e:na ~ kha ding hi) (s:kisik) (r:20.20.25) (q:draft)
kinungta = (t:v) (w:live) (d:impersonal ki with nungta, live: people live, one lives; sauveipipi kinungta is people live very long) (e:a, sauveipipi ~ ding hi/sauveipipi ~ ding hi | people will live very long) (b:nungta) (r:23.65.20) (q:draft)
kinusia = (t:v) (w:be left/be abandoned/be deserted/be forsaken) (d:passive of nusia, leave: be left behind when others are taken, or of a city or a wife, be abandoned) (e:khat kila-in khat ~ ding hi/lungdamna khuapi, tu-in ~ ta hi | the city of joy is now abandoned/~-a a dah zi bangin | like a wife deserted and grieving/Ashkelon khuapi ~ ding hi | the city of Ashkelon will be abandoned) (s:kinusiacip/kikoihkhong) (a:kila) (b:nusia) (r:42.17.35/24.49.25/23.54.6/36.2.4) (q:draft)
kinusiacip = (t:v) (w:be forsaken/be deserted/be abandoned/be neglected) (d:kinusia with cip completely: be left entirely alone) (e:Bang hangin Pasian’ inn ~ ahi hiam/Thuman mi a ~ hita leh | the righteous being forsaken/Ashkelon khuapi ~ ding hi | the city of Ashkelon will be deserted/kumpi nihte’ gam ~ ding hi | the land of the two kings will be deserted) (s:kinusia/kikoihkhong) (b:kinusia) (r:16.13.11/19.37.25/38.9.5/23.7.16) (q:draft)
kinusiacipin = (t:v) (w:being deserted/being abandoned/left desolate) (d:kinusiacip be deserted, with the linking ending in) (e:Leitang ~ om mawk hi/kisusia a, ~ gamkhing suak hi | it is destroyed, deserted and has become a waste/biakna munte ~, Israel mite’ siangtho munte kisusia ding | the places of worship will be deserted and the holy places of Israel destroyed) (b:kinusiacip) (r:23.33.9/34.2.10/30.7.9) (q:draft)
kinusiacipsak = (t:v) (w:leave deserted/make desolate) (d:kinusiacip be left behind for good, with the causative sak) (e:lampite uh ka ~ a) (b:kinusiacip) (r:36.3.6) (q:draft)
kinusialai = (t:v) (w:be still left/remain) (d:kinusia be left, with lai still) (e:khuapi sunga a ~ mite) (s:omlai/suaktalai) (r:24.52.15) (q:draft)
kinusiasa = (t:adj) (w:abandoned/desolate/deserted) (d:kinusia be left, with sa marking what has already happened) (e:a ~ lote a puah kikpa) (s:simtham) (b:kinusia) (r:26.36.36) (q:draft)
kinusiat = (t:v) (w:be left/be deserted/lie desolate) (d:form of kinusia, be left or deserted, used before words such as sung and dong) (e:leitang a ~ sung khempeuh/note hong ~ dong matengin | until you are left) (b:kinusia) (r:14.36.21/23.30.17) (q:draft)
kinusiate = (t:n) (w:plunder/spoil/things left behind) (d:goods left behind; van kinusiate is the plunder of a captured city) (e:khuapi sunga van ~ i la hi/van ~ tungah mite va leengin | the people pounced on the plunder/Amaute in van ~ mu-in hawm hilo ahi hiam | are they not finding and dividing the spoil) (s:vankinusiate/kilate) (b:kinusia) (r:5.3.7/6.8.27/9.14.32/7.5.30) (q:draft)
kinzaw = (t:v) (w:care more for/love more) (d:kin care about, be eager for, with zaw more) (e:hih leitung thu ~ ahih manin) (s:itzaw) (b:kin) (r:55.4.10) (q:draft)
kiomsak = (t:v) (w:be established/be set in place) (d:passive with ki of omsak cause to be, put; kiomsak kik, be restored) (e:biakinn sungah nasepna ~ kik hi) (b:omsak) (r:14.29.35) (q:draft)
kip = (t:v) (w:be established/stand firm/endure) (d:stand firm and last: of a house, a throne or an inheritance be established; of a word or of love, hold and endure; kip den and kip tawntung are endure forever) (e:ngaihsut siamna tawh inn ~ hi/amah hangin na khempeuh a ~ hi | in him all things hold together/vantungah nangma thu ~ tawntung hi | your word stands firm forever in heaven/amau’ gamh in ~ den ding hi | their inheritance will endure forever/zong a ~ zo kei ding hi | it too will not be able to stand) (s:kikip) (a:kiling) (r:20.24.3/58.13.1/51.1.17/19.119.89/19.37.18/41.3.25) (q:draft)
kip = (t:adj) (w:steadfast/unfailing/firm/lasting) (d:placed after a noun: itna kip is steadfast love and ngeina kip a lasting ordinance) (e:nangma itna ~ ka ngaihsun uh hi/Ama itna ~ kho tawntung hi | his steadfast love endures forever/ka topa Abraham’ tungah itna ~ hong lak in | show steadfast love to my master Abraham/biakna ngeina ~ khatin | as a lasting ordinance) (s:kiptak/kician) (r:19.48.9/19.118.2/1.24.12/2.12.14) (q:draft)
kipaai = (t:v) (w:be thrown/be thrown away/be cast out) (d:passive of paai, throw: be thrown down or thrown away; kipaai mang is be cast away, and na kipaai in is throw yourself) (e:kikai tal-in ~ ding hi/a theih loh gamah ~ mang ahi hiam | is he cast away into a land he does not know/Ama luanghawm lampi-ah ~ a | his body was thrown down on the road/tuipi sungah na ~ in | throw yourself into the sea) (s:kilawn/kipaih) (b:paai) (r:24.22.19/24.22.28/11.13.24/40.21.21) (q:draft)
kipaaidak = (t:v) (w:be thrown out/be cast out and exposed) (d:passive with ki of paai throw away, with dak; of a body left lying in the open) (e:tuam dingin a ~ ding hi) (s:kipaidak) (r:24.36.30) (q:draft, low confidence)
kipaaikhia = (t:v) (w:be taken away/be removed/be excluded/be cast out) (d:ki- passive form of paaikhia; also be cast up on a shore) (e:tua a kisitna a ~ hi/Thu-upna tawh ~ hi | it is excluded by faith/tuikulh khatpeuh tungah i ~ ding hi | we will be cast up on some island/Khazih hangin ~ zo hi | it is taken away through Christ) (s:kilakkhiat/kipaikhia) (b:paaikhia) (r:47.3.16/45.3.27/44.27.26/47.3.14) (q:draft)
kipaaina = (t:n) (w:conception/being conceived) (d:passive ki with paai carry in the womb and the noun suffix na; kei hong kipaaina naugil, the womb in which I was conceived) (e:kei hong ~ naugil na khakcip lo) (s:kipaiina/gaina) (r:18.3.10) (q:draft)
kipaaithang = (t:v) (w:be strewn/be thrown about/lie scattered) (d:of dead bodies, be thrown out and left lying about; also written kipaithang) (e:Jerusalem khua kongzing lakah ~ dinga/ek bangin misiluang a ~ ding a | dead bodies will lie strewn like dung) (s:kipaithang/kithehzak) (r:24.14.16/24.9.22) (q:draft)
kipaaksak = (t:v) (w:make glad/gladden/give joy) (d:kipaak, a spelling of kipak rejoice, with the causative sak: make someone glad) (e:na nasempa hong ~ in/kote hong ~ in | make us glad/lungdamna tawh amah na ~ hi | you have made him glad with joy) (s:kipaksak/lungdamsak/nuamsak) (a:dahsak) (r:19.86.4/19.21.6/19.90.15) (q:draft)
kipah = (t:v) (w:rejoice/be glad) (d:form of kipak rejoice used before endings such as uh and nading) (e:lungdamin na ~ uh hangin/Na nu leh na pa a ~ nadingin | so that your mother and father may be glad) (a:dah) (r:24.50.11/20.23.25) (q:draft)
kipahna = (t:n) (w:gladness/joy/rejoicing) (d:kipah, be glad, with na; often paired with lungdamna) (e:Lungdamna leh ~ hong pia in la/lungdamna leh ~ awte | the sounds of joy and gladness/leitung ~ kibeisak ta hi | the gladness of the earth is banished/a dahnate uh ~ ka suaksak ding hi | I will turn their sorrows into gladness) (s:kipakna/lungdamna/nuamna) (a:dahna) (b:kipah) (r:19.51.8/23.24.11/24.25.10/24.31.13) (q:draft)
kipahtawi = (t:v) (w:be exalted/be honored/be lifted high) (d:passive form with ki of pahtawi honor, exalt) (e:na hatna hangin nang hong ~ ta hen/tu-in kei hong ~ ta ding hi | now I will be exalted/amah vanglianin, ~ ding hi | he will be mighty and honored/innkuan khempeuh sung panin a ~ pen ahi hi | he was the most honored of the whole household) (s:kisangsak/kizahtak/kisangtawi) (a:kisimmawh) (b:pahtawi) (r:19.21.13/19.12.8/23.33.10/19.112.9/1.34.19) (q:draft)
kipahtawina = (t:n) (w:glory/honor/being honored) (d:kipahtawi be honored, honor oneself, with the noun suffix na: the honor one receives or gives oneself, also that by which someone is honored) (e:ka ~ a mawkna hi ding hi/pasiante leh mite a ~ ahi ka thaunate | my oil, by which gods and men are honored) (s:pahtawina/minthanna) (a:minsiatna) (b:kipahtawi) (r:43.8.54/7.9.9) (q:draft)
kipahtawisak = (t:v) (w:bring honour to/cause to be honoured) (d:kipahtawi be honoured, with the causative sak) (e:Amaute ka ~ ding a) (a:neusak) (b:kipahtawi) (r:24.30.19) (q:draft)
kipahtawite = (t:n) (w:honored ones/the renowned) (d:kipahtawi be honored, with the plural te: those who are honored) (e:leitungah a ~ ahi/leitung a, a ~ vulgawp hi | the exalted of the earth wither) (b:kipahtawi) (r:23.23.8/23.24.4) (q:draft)
kipai = (t:v) (w:go/set out) (d:pai go with the prefix ki, used impersonally or passively: one goes, people set out; kipai khiatpih, be carried away) (e:a thumna ah ~ hi/A ~ khiat ciangin amau masa ding uh hi | when the setting out comes, they shall go first/note zong hong ~ khiatpih ding hi | you too will be carried away/~ thei ding hi ci-in ngaihsunin | thinking that they would be able to go on) (b:pai) (r:11.6.8/4.2.9/24.48.7/44.27.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
kipaidak = (t:v) (w:be thrown out/be cast aside/be left lying) (d:be thrown away and left lying in the open, of an unwanted child or of dead bodies) (e:gamlakah nang hong ~ lel hi/khuapi kongzingah a luanghawm uh ~ ding hi | their bodies will lie thrown out in the street of the city/vukngo’ tuam dingin ~ ding hi | it will be thrown out for the frost to cover) (s:kipaaidak/kilawnkhia) (b:paidak) (r:26.16.5/66.11.8/24.36.30) (q:draft)
kipaih = (t:v) (w:be thrown out/be cast away/be rejected) (d:passive of paih, throw away; mostly with khia, out: kipaih khiatsak is be thrown out and kipaih khiatna is rejection) (e:A bu a ~ khiatsak ciangin/migilote’ thahatna ~ khiatsak ding a | the strength of the wicked will be cast away/Tua mite ~ khiatna un | by the rejection of those people) (s:kipaimang/kilawnkhia/kinolh) (b:paih) (r:23.16.2/45.11.15/19.37.17) (q:draft)
kipaihkhiat = (t:v) (w:be thrown out/be cast away/be dropped) (d:passive of paihkhiat, throw away; form used before words such as ciangin, ding and theih) (e:A hoih lo teng a ~ theih nadingin/Tua nung a ~ ciangin | then, when he was put out/Pasian’ Thukham neupen a ~ ding sangin | than for the least part of the law of God to be dropped) (b:paihkhiat) (r:30.9.9/44.7.21/42.16.17) (q:draft)
kipaihna = (t:n) (w:dumping place/throwing away) (d:kipaih be thrown away with the noun suffix na; nin kipaihna phualpi, a heap where rubbish is thrown) (e:nin ~ phualpi suak ding a) (b:kipaih) (r:33.3.12) (q:draft)
kipaihpehsakin = (t:v) (w:crossing) (d:making the hands cross over each other, with the causative sak and the linking ending in) (e:ahih manin, a khut ~) (s:pehsakin) (r:1.48.14) (q:draft)
kipaii = (t:v) (w:be conceived) (d:passive of paii conceive, of a child) (e:Pasal naungek khat ~ hi/amah a ~ ma-in | before he was conceived) (b:paii) (r:18.3.3/42.2.21) (q:draft)
kipaiikhia = (t:v) (w:be thrown away/be thrown out) (d:passive with ki of paii throw, with khia out) (e:a ~ hiangte bangin) (s:kilawnkhia) (r:43.15.6) (q:draft)
kipaiina = (t:n) (w:conception/being conceived) (d:kipaii be conceived, with the noun suffix na; kei hong kipaiina naugil, the womb in which I was conceived) (e:kei hong ~ naugil na khakcip lo) (s:kipaaina/gaina) (b:kipaii) (r:18.3.10) (q:draft)
kipaikhia = (t:v) (w:be thrown down/be thrown out/be removed/be driven away) (d:be cast away or put out of its place) (e:a ~ mite a thahat minamte/biakna maan lei lakah a ~ hi | true worship was thrown to the ground/a kipiangsak nate kilingsakin ~ ding a | created things will be shaken and removed/khuapi panin amaute ~ sak hi | they were drawn away from the city) (s:kipaaikhia/kilawnkhia) (r:33.4.7/27.8.12/58.12.27/7.20.31) (q:draft)
kipaikhiasak = (t:v) (w:be sent away/be drawn out/be made to go out) (d:passive of paikhiasak send away, make go out, with the prefix ki) (e:na nu uh ~ hi/khuapi panin amaute ~ hi | they were drawn away from the city) (s:kisawlkhia/kiciahsak) (b:paikhiasak) (r:23.50.1/7.20.31) (q:draft)
kipaikhiat = (t:v) (w:set out/march out) (d:impersonal ki with paikhiat go out: when the setting out takes place) (e:A ~ ciangin amau masa ding) (s:kuankhiat) (b:paikhiat) (r:4.2.3) (q:draft)
kipaikhiatpih = (t:v) (w:be taken away/be carried off/be led out) (d:passive of paikhiatpih; in the verses mostly of people taken away into exile) (e:Jerusalem khua panin ~ khin zo hi/nangma tapate kimkhat ~ ding a | some of your own sons will be taken away/Gam dangah ~ ngei lo a | she has never been taken away to another land/Amah a ~ lai takin | just as she was being brought out/nopsakna tawh hong ~ ding hi | you will be led out in peace) (s:kipuakhia/kikai) (b:paikhiatpih) (r:24.29.2/23.39.7/24.48.11/1.38.25/23.55.12) (q:draft)
kipaikhiatsak = (t:v) (w:be put outside/be sent out) (d:passive with ki of paikhiatsak make go out) (e:a pualamah a ~ khit ciangin) (s:kisawlkhia) (b:paikhiatsak) (r:40.9.25) (q:draft)
kipaimang = (t:v) (w:be thrown away/be cast away/be discarded) (d:passive of paimang throw away, with the prefix ki; also written kipaai mang) (e:a theih loh uh gamah ~ ahi hiam/kuama’ deih loh a ~ beel kitam | a broken pot thrown away that no one wants) (s:kipaih/kipaai) (b:paimang) (r:24.22.28) (q:draft)
kipaipih = (t:v) (w:be brought/be taken) (d:passive of paipih, take along: be brought or led to someone or somewhere) (e:siampipa kiangah ~ ding hi/ama mai-ah a ~ nadingin thu a pia hi | he gave the order for them to be brought before him/kikhopna buk kongah amah ~ ding a | he shall be brought to the entrance of the tent of meeting/Samaria ah ~ hi | he was brought to Samaria) (s:kitunpih/kitut) (b:paipih) (r:3.13.9/40.9.32/27.3.13/4.6.13/11.22.37) (q:draft)
kipaipihin = (t:v) (w:being brought/being taken/being led) (d:kipaipih, be brought, with the linking ending in: being brought, after which another action follows) (e:giahphual pua lamah ~ ama mai-ah kigo/tua a lutang hong ~ numei kiangah kipia a | his head was brought and given to the girl/Jehu kiangah amah ~ kithat hi | he was brought to Jehu and killed/Aaron tapate hong ~ | the sons of Aaron being brought forward) (b:kipaipih) (r:4.19.3/40.14.11/14.22.9/3.8.24) (q:draft)
kipaipihna = (t:n) (w:being brought/being taken) (d:kipaipih, be brought or taken, with the noun suffix na; salin kipaipihna, being led away as captives) (e:salin ~ a thuak ding uh hi/meihal biakna a ~ munah | at the place where burnt offerings are brought/ama mai-ah a ~ ding thu a pia hi | he gave the order for them to be brought before him) (b:kipaipih) (r:42.21.24/15.6.3/27.3.13) (q:draft)
kipaisak = (t:v) (w:be sent/be allowed to go) (d:passive of paisak, send or let go) (e:Topa’ omna-ah amaute bek ~ hi/uliante tungah lai ~ hi | letters were sent to the nobles) (s:kisawl) (b:paisak) (r:26.40.46/17.3.12) (q:draft)
kipaithang = (t:v) (w:be strewn/be thrown about/lie scattered) (d:of dead bodies, be thrown down and left lying about) (e:misi luang ~ ding a/a milimte uh mai-ah ~ gawp ding hi | they will lie strewn before their idols/Jerusalem khua kongzing lakah ~ ding a | they will be thrown out in the streets of Jerusalem) (s:kipaaithang/kithehzak) (r:24.9.22/26.6.4/24.14.16) (q:draft)
kipaithangin = (t:v) (w:being strewn/flung about) (d:kipaithang be strewn, with the linking ending in) (e:mun citengah ~ gamdai ding hi) (b:kipaithang) (r:30.8.3) (q:draft)
kipak = (t:v) (w:rejoice/be glad/be joyful) (d:be glad and show it; very often paired with lungdam, as in lungdamin kipak, rejoice and be glad) (e:eite lungdamin i ~ ding hi/amau Kumpipa’ sungah Zion mite ~ ta hen | let the people of Zion be glad in their King/Topa sungah lungdamin ~ un | rejoice and be glad in the Lord/Vantungmite ~ hen la, leitung lungdam hen | let the heavens rejoice and the earth be glad/lungdamin ka ~ lai veve ding hi | yet I will still rejoice) (s:lungdam) (a:dah) (r:19.118.24/19.122.1/19.149.2/19.32.11/19.96.11/35.3.18) (q:draft)
kipakin = (t:adv) (w:gladly/joyfully/rejoicing) (d:kipak, rejoice, with the linking ending in: gladly, with joy; often paired as lungdamin kipakin, and kipakin diang is leap for joy) (e:lungdamin ~ om un/lungdamin ~ pawi bawlna hun | a time of joyful and glad feasting/ka Pasian hangin ~ ka diang ding hi | I will leap for joy because of my God/~ na diang uh a | you leapt for joy) (s:lungdamin/lungdamtakin) (a:dahin) (b:kipak) (r:29.2.21/38.8.19/23.61.10/26.25.6) (q:draft)
kipakna = (t:n) (w:gladness/joy/rejoicing) (d:kipak, rejoice, with the noun suffix na: gladness; often paired as lungdamna leh kipakna, joy and gladness) (e:amaute in lungdamna leh ~ ngahin dahna leh khuisatna/nangma minamte’ ~ sungah ka lungdam theih nading | that I may share in the joy of your nation/lungdamna le ~ tawh | with joy and gladness) (s:kipahna/lungdamna/nuamna) (a:dahna) (b:kipak) (r:23.51.11/19.106.4/14.7.10) (q:draft)
kipaksak = (t:v) (w:make glad/make rejoice/gladden) (d:kipak rejoice, with the causative sak) (e:lungdamna tawh amah na ~ hi/na nasempa keimah hong ~ ta in | make me, your servant, glad) (s:kipaaksak/lungdamsak/nuamsak) (a:dahsak) (b:kipak) (r:19.21.6/19.109.28) (q:draft)
kipakta = (t:v) (w:be approved/be honoured/be esteemed) (d:be well regarded by others, passive of pakta) (e:ama gamah ~ ngei lo hi/amah a kiphattawm ciangin a ~ hi lo a | he is not approved when he praises himself/kuamah peuh ama khua-ah ~ ngei lo hi | no one is ever accepted in his own town/beh lutangte a ~, a thahat galhangte | heads of families, honoured men and strong warriors) (s:kizahtak/kisangtawi) (a:kisimmawh) (b:pakta) (r:43.4.44/47.10.18/42.4.24/13.7.40) (q:draft)
kipalsat = (t:v) (w:be broken/be violated/be transgressed) (d:passive of palsat, break a law or an agreement) (e:Topa aw, na thu ~ khin ahih ciangin/Thuciamnate kipeksat-in, thukimnasate ~ a | the covenants are set aside and the agreements broken) (b:palsat) (r:19.119.126/23.33.8) (q:draft)
kipan = (t:v) (w:begin/start) (d:start to do something or come into being; after a verb with ding, begin to do; with panin, start from a place) (e:leh dahna a ~ hi/kum sagih kialpi hong ~ hi | the seven years of famine began/a min lawh ding ~ uh | they began to call on his name/suankhiat ding ~ in | begin to take possession/leitaw lam a sun tuidawk panin ~ hi | it started from the southern bay) (s:kipat) (a:tawp/bei) (r:41.14.33/1.41.54/1.4.26/5.2.31/6.15.2) (q:draft)
kipan = (t:prep) (w:from/since) (d:starting from, placed after a time or place word and a) (e:Zingsang a ~ nitak dong/kum kipat-a ~ kum bei dongin | from the beginning of the year to the end of the year/Tanglai pek-a ~ | from long ago/Topa in hih thu Moses tungah a gen-a ~ | since the Lord said this to Moses) (s:akipan/panin/pan) (a:dong) (r:25.3.63/5.9.24/5.11.12/18.20.4/6.14.10) (q:draft)
kipana = (t:v) (w:begin) (d:kipan begin with the linking a: having begun, and then) (e:Thukhen nading hun ~ laibute a kiphen) (b:kipan) (r:27.7.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
kipangsak = (t:v) (w:be deployed/be stationed) (d:passive of pangsak post: of soldiers, be drawn up against an enemy) (e:a do dingin amaute ~ hi) (b:pangsak) (r:13.19.11) (q:draft)
kipanin = (t:ppm) (w:from/since) (d:postpositional marker equivalent to the locative preposition, "from") (e:tua mun a ~/Tua ni a ~ Saul in David encik hi | from that day on Saul kept watching David/tu-a ~ a tawntungin Topa muang in | trust the Lord from now on and forever/ka khangno lai-a ~ nong thuhilh a | you have taught me since my youth) (b:kipan) (r:9.18.9/19.131.3/19.71.17)
kipankhia = (t:v) (w:come out from/proceed from/begin) (d:kipan, begin, with khia, out: start out from a place or source, used with panin) (e:lungsim panin hong ~ hi a/awging le vanging hong ~ a | rumblings and thunder came out/Heshbon khua panin meikuang hong ~ veve hi | yet a fire has gone out from the town of Heshbon/ci-in a kigelhna tawh hong ~ hi | it begins with what is written) (b:kipan) (r:40.15.18/66.4.5/24.48.45/41.1.3) (q:draft)
kipankik = (t:v) (w:begin again) (d:kipan begin, with kik again) (e:thuhilh ding ~ leuleu hi) (b:kipan) (r:41.4.1) (q:draft)
kipanta = (t:v) (w:have begun) (d:kipan begin, with ta marking a change now reached) (e:Uk ding hun hong ~ hi) (b:kipan) (r:41.1.15) (q:draft)
kipanto = (t:v) (w:start upward/rise from) (d:kipan begin, with to upward; of rooms that start from a raised base) (e:inndei neute ~ pan hi) (b:kipan) (r:26.41.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
kipap = (t:v) (w:be struck/be beaten against) (d:of a boat hit by breaking waves) (e:tui kilok in gunkuang ~ a) (s:kisat) (r:41.4.37) (q:draft, low confidence)
Kipasal = (t:v) (w:act like a man/be manly) (d:pasal, man, with the prefix ki; found only with sak in Kipasal sakin, showing oneself a man, brace yourself like a man in the NIV; also written as one word Kipasalsakin) (e:~ sakin dingto in la) (r:18.40.7/18.38.3) (q:draft)
kipasalsak = (t:v) (w:be brave/act like men/be courageous) (d:pasal man with ki and sak: make oneself a man, show courage) (e:i Pasian’ khuapite adingin ~ ni) (s:Kihangsak) (r:10.10.12) (q:draft)
kipasalsakin = (t:adj) (w:courageous) (d:kipasalsak, show oneself a man, with the linking suffix in: bracing oneself like a man) (e:~ dingto inla, kong thudot dingte hong dawng) (b:kipasalsak) (r:18.38.3) convey a negative sense
Kipasalsakin = (t:adv) (w:like a man/manfully/bravely) (d:kipasalsak, show oneself a man, with the linking suffix in; written with a capital at the start of a sentence, brace yourself like a man in the NIV) (e:~ dingto inla, ka thudotnate hong dawng in) (s:hangtakin) (b:kipasalsakin) (r:18.40.7/18.38.3) (q:draft)
kipat = (t:v) (w:begin/start/open/first) (d:form of kipan, begin, used before words such as ciangin, cil and ni; a kipat cil-in is in the beginning, and ni kipat ni is the first day of the week) (e:a ~ cil/Tuate khempeuh in gimna ~ cilna ahi hi | all these are the beginning of sufferings/Kitot i ~ ciangin | when we start a quarrel/Ni sagih lakah ni ~ ni | on the first day of the week) (s:kipan/kisin) (a:tawp) (r:1.1.1/40.24.8/20.17.14/41.16.2)
kipatcil = (t:n) (w:beginning/first) (d:a kipatcil-in is in the beginning, a kipatcil lai is at first) (e:a ~ lai sangin a nunung lamah/A ~-in Thu a om hi | in the beginning was the Word/a ~ pek a kipanin i neihsa thupiakna | a command we have had from the very beginning/a ~-a kipan tu dongin | from the beginning until now) (s:kipatna/cilna/patna) (a:tawpna) (r:66.2.19/43.1.1/63.1.5/50.1.3) (q:draft)
kipatin = (t:v) (w:beginning/when beginning) (d:kipat begin with the linking ending -in; uk ding a kipatin means when he began to reign) (e:uk ding a ~ kum giat pha a/Gam uk dingin a ~ David kum sawmthum pha | David was thirty years old when he began to reign/uk ding a ~ Saul kum sawmthum pha hi | Saul was thirty years old when he began to reign/uk ding a ~ kum sawmnih-le-thum pha hi | he was twenty-three years old when he began to reign) (b:kipat) (r:14.34.1/10.5.4/9.13.1/14.36.2) (q:draft)
kipatkhiatna = (t:n) (w:origin/starting point) (d:kipatkhiat start out, with the noun suffix na; kipatkhiatna mun, the place something comes from) (e:Leitung khuavak hong ~ mun ahi a) (s:piankhiatna) (r:18.38.19) (q:draft)
kipatma = (t:adv) (w:before the beginning/before it begins) (d:kipat begin, with ma before) (e:tua pawi ~ hun sungin) (r:43.11.55) (q:draft)
kipatna = (t:n) (w:beginning/start) (d:kipat, begin, with the noun suffix na: the beginning or source of something; a kipatna leh a tawpna is the beginning and the end) (e:Topa zahtakna in pilna ~ hi a/a ~ leh a tawpna ka hi hi | I am the beginning and the end/Lungdamna Thu a ~ in hih bang hi | the beginning of the good news is this/tuinak ~ dong lei sung to uh a | they dig into the earth as far as the sources of the springs) (s:patna/cilna/kipatcil) (a:tawpna/beina) (b:kipat) (r:20.9.10/41.1.1/66.22.13/18.28.11) (q:draft)
Kipatna = (t:n) (w:beginning) (d:kipatna written with a capital as a title of God, the Beginning, standing for Alpha) (e:na khempeuh a ~ le a Tawpna) (a:Tawpna) (b:kipatna) (r:66.1.8) (q:draft)
kipatsa = (t:adj) (w:already begun) (d:kipat begin, with sa marking what has already happened; hong kipatsa bangin, as he had already begun) (e:kiangah hong ~ bangin hih hehpihna) (b:kipat) (r:47.8.6) (q:draft)
kipatthakna = (t:n) (w:new beginning/fresh start) (d:kipat begin with thak new and the noun suffix na) (e:mite a ~ ding lahna lim) (r:23.6.13) (q:draft)
kipattung = (t:n) (w:beginning/very start) (d:kipat begin with tung at first; a kipattung lamin, at the beginning) (e:manin a ~ lamin hih thute) (s:kipatna/kipatcil) (r:43.16.4) (q:draft)
kipatun = (t:n) (w:beginning/start) (d:the start of something, here of speaking; probably the same as kipattung) (e:Thugen a ~ bang tum lo) (s:kipattung) (r:21.10.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
kipau = (t:v) (w:speak to one another/be spoken) (d:pau, speak, with the prefix ki: speak with each other; kipau thei lo, that cannot be put into words) (e:thuman thutak kam ~ un/muk tawh ~ thei lo tauna tawh | with groans that cannot be put into words/a ~ paunam thei kei leng | if I do not know the language that is spoken) (s:kiho) (b:pau) (r:38.8.16/45.8.26/46.14.11) (q:draft)
kipawl = (t:v) (w:consort/keep company with) (d:Keep company with someone and live as one of their kind; the companion is marked by tawh, with.) (e:ngiate leh kalaoh vasate tawh a ~/mi gilopa tawh na ~ kei ding uh hi | you shall not join with a wicked man/Guktakna sunga ~ mipa | a man who is partner in a theft) (s:kikhawl) (r:18.30.29/2.23.1/20.29.24)
kipawl = (t:v) (w:associate/join/belong to) (d:Be on the side of a person or group, join them or belong to them; used with tawh, with, as in Pasian tawh kipawl, belong to God.) (e:thusim neite tawh ka ~ kei hi/A hehbaih mite tawh ~ kei in la | do not make friends with hot-tempered people/Galile mi Zeisu tawh na ~ hi | you were with Jesus of Galilee/Ahaziah tawh ~ na hih manin | because you have allied yourself with Ahaziah/Pasian tawh ~ lo na hih uh ciangin | because you do not belong to God) (s:kikhawl/kikholh) (r:19.26.4/20.22.24/40.26.69/14.20.37/43.8.47)
kipawl = (t:v) (w:mix) (d:Mix with other people, go among them and share their company.) (e:Midang tawh a ~ thei phalote pen | those who cannot mix with others) (r:20.18.1)
kipawlbawl = (t:v) (w:become friends/make friends) (d:Kipawl, associate, with bawl, make or treat as: become friends with each other; its opposite in the same verse is kigalbawl, be enemies.) (e:tegel kilem kikin ~ uh hi) (a:kigalbawl) (b:kipawl) (r:42.23.12) (q:draft)
kipawlin = (t:v) (w:join/ally with/unite/band together) (d:Form of kipawl with the linking ending in, joining it to the next verb; the partner is marked by tawh, with.) (e:mi namdangte tawh ~ tua mite/~ mi khat bang uh hi | they united as one man/Korah tawh ~ Topa langpangin a kikaikhawm mihonte | the company that banded together with Korah against the Lord/a om lai minamte tawh ~ amaute tawh kitengin | allying with the remaining nations and intermarrying with them/Khrih tawh ~ na nuntakna uh | your life in union with Christ) (s:kikhawlin) (b:kipawl) (r:28.7.8/7.20.11/4.27.3/6.23.12/50.2.1) (q:draft)
kipawlkha = (t:v) (w:join with/get involved with) (d:Kipawl, associate, with kha, happen to: get involved with someone; mostly negative, as in kipawlkha kei in, do not join with them.) (e:amau a langpangte tawh ~ kei in) (r:20.24.21) (q:draft)
kipawlkhawm = (t:v) (w:become allies/form an alliance/unite) (d:Kipawl, associate, with khawm, together: join together as allies.) (e:kumpipa in a ~ theih nadingin) (b:kipawl) (r:27.11.6) (q:draft)
kipawlkhawmna = (t:n) (w:alliance/union) (d:Kipawlkhawm, become allies, with the noun suffix na: an alliance between two parties.) (e:tua ~ kip lo ding a) (s:kipawlna) (b:kipawlkhawm) (r:27.11.6) (q:draft)
kipawlkhin = (t:v) (w:be already united/have been joined) (d:kipawl, join or associate, with khin, already done; used with tawh, with) (e:Pasian tawh ~ na hih manun) (b:kipawl) (r:45.8.10) (q:draft)
kipawlna = (t:n) (w:alliance/treaty/union/fellowship) (d:A joining together of people or nations, an alliance or fellowship; kipawlna bawl means make an alliance, and the partner is marked by tawh, with.) (e:Assiria tawh ~ bawl uh a/Ahaziah tawh ~ a bawl hi | he made an alliance with Ahaziah/Baasha tawh na ~ va sutat in | go and break your treaty with Baasha/ama Tapa Zeisu Khazih tawh ~ sungah | into fellowship with his Son Jesus Christ) (s:kipawlkhawmna/kizopna) (a:kikhenna) (b:kipawl) (r:28.12.1/46.1.9/14.20.35/14.16.3) (q:draft)
Kipawlna = (t:n) (w:Union) (d:kipawlna, union, written with a capital as the name of one of the two staffs of the shepherd in Zechariah) (e:~ a kici ciangkhut la-in ka kuaitan leuleu a/a khat pen ~ ci-in min ka phuak hi | the other I named Union) (b:kipawlna) (r:38.11.14/38.11.7) (q:draft)
kipawlnate = (t:n) (w:joints/joinings/connections) (d:plural of kipawlna, a joining; here the places where bones and sinews of the body join) (e:a taang tawh a ~ hangin) (b:kipawlna) (r:51.2.19) (q:draft)
kipawlpih = (t:v) (w:associate with/ally with/mix with) (d:kipawl associate, with pih together with; a kipawlpih, those one has joined with) (e:A ~ mi namdangte in) (s:pawlpih) (b:kipawl) (r:28.7.9) (q:draft)
kipawlpihte = (t:n) (w:allies/friends/associates) (d:kipawlpih, be allied with, with plural te: those who are joined with someone) (e:hih mite pen Abram’ ~ ahi hi/Ka ~ ka sapsap hangin | though I called to my allies/A ~ khempeuh in amah khemin | all her friends have deceived her) (s:lawmte) (a:galte) (b:kipawlpih) (r:1.14.13/25.1.19/25.1.2) (q:draft)
kipawlsa = (t:adj) (w:joined/united) (d:kipawl, join, with the completive suffix sa: having been joined; Pasian tawh a kipawlsa mite, people who have been united with God) (e:Pasian tawh a ~ mite) (b:kipawl) (r:46.6.11) (q:draft)
kipawlsak = (t:v) (w:unite/join) (d:kipawl, join, with the causative sak: cause to be joined with someone) (e:Khrih Jesuh tawh a hong ~ Kha Siangtho) (b:kipawl) (r:45.8.2) (q:draft)
kipawlte = (t:n) (w:those who belong to/associates/companions) (d:Kipawl, belong to or associate with, with the plural te: the people who are joined to someone or something, used with tawh, with.) (e:Topa tawh ~ in Topa tawh lungsim khat/Zeisu tawh ~ dah a | those who had been with Jesus were mourning/Thukham tawh ~ bek in gamh a luah uh leh | if only those who live by the law are heirs/siampi ukpa leh amah tawh ~ hong pai uh a | the high priest and his associates came) (s:kipawlpihte) (b:kipawl) (r:46.6.17/41.16.10/45.4.14/44.5.21) (q:draft)
kipawlthei = (t:v) (w:be able to associate/can be united) (d:kipawl with thei, be able to join or have fellowship with; in the 1977 text Pasian tawh kipawlthei renders being justified, put right with God) (e:Midik le mimawh bangci-in ~ ding a/upna hangin Pasian tawh ~ a | are put right with God through faith/tu-in Pasian tawh ~ ihih manin | since we are now put right with God/amah tawh i ~ kik hi | we can be united with him again) (s:kikhawlthei) (b:kipawl) (r:47.6.14/45.9.30/45.5.9/45.3.24) (q:draft)
kipden = (t:v) (w:endure/remain firm/last for ever) (d:Kip, be firm, with den, always: stand firm for ever, last without end.) (e:amau’ gamh ~ ding hi) (s:kipsuak) (r:19.37.18) (q:draft)
kipeek = (t:v) (w:roll about/writhe/thrash) (d:Roll or thrash about on the ground, said of a person in a convulsion; with sawnsawn, over and over.) (e:cilphuan bua-in a ~ sawnsawn hi) (r:41.9.20) (q:draft)
kipeh = (t:v) (w:be grafted/be grafted in) (d:passive of peh, graft: a branch is joined onto another tree) (e:Eite tawh hong ~ theih nadingin/gamlak oliv hiangte tawh ~ hi | they are grafted together with wild olive branches/ngeina zui loin nang hong ~ leh | if you were grafted in contrary to nature) (b:peh) (r:45.11.19/45.11.24/45.11.17) (q:draft)
kipeh = (t:v) (w:bite each other) (d:with khat leh khat, one another; said of people who attack each other) (e:khat leh khat na ~, na kinek uh leh) (s:kipetkha) (r:48.5.15) (q:draft)
kipehthei = (t:v) (w:can be grafted/be grafted) (d:kipeh, be grafted, with thei, be able) (e:oliv kung tungah hong ~ ahihleh) (b:kipeh) (r:45.11.24) (q:draft)
kipei = (t:v) (w:whirl/spin/swirl) (d:of a whirlwind, turn round and round; pei is wheel) (e:huihpi nungin pingpei ~ a) (b:pei) (r:34.1.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
kipeksat = (t:see) <kipeksat-in>
kipeksat-in = (t:v) (w:be broken) (d:passive of peksat, break, with the linking ending in; said of a treaty or agreement) (e:Thuciamnate ~, thukimnasate kipalsat a) (s:kipalsat) (r:23.33.8) (q:draft)
kipeksatin = (t:v) (w:be broken) (d:passive of peksat, break, with the linking ending in; said of a treaty or agreement) (e:Thuciamnate ~, thukimnasate kipalsat a) (s:kipalsat) (b:peksatin) (r:23.33.8) (q:draft)
kipelh = (t:v) (w:escape/be free from/keep away from/avoid) (d:Stay clear of something bad or get away from it; the thing avoided is marked by tawh, as in lungkhamna tawh kipelh, be kept from trouble.) (e:lungkhamna tawh ~ hi/thuman mite, buaina tawh ~ hi | the truthful escape trouble/Pasian’ thukhenna tawh na ~ ding | you will escape God’s judgment/mawhsakna tawh a ~ nadingun | so that they may be free from blame) (s:suakta) (b:pelh) (r:20.21.23/20.12.13/45.2.3/54.5.7) (q:draft)
kipelhin = (t:v) (w:escape/be free from/avoid) (d:kipelh, be free from, with the linking ending in, joining it to the next verb; used with tawh for the thing escaped) (e:upna hangin sihna tawh ~ a kilato hi/kisiat gawpna tawh note in ~ | you, having escaped the corruption/lungsim kiliatsakna tawh ~ | keeping free from arrogance of heart) (b:kipelh) (r:58.11.5/61.1.4/54.6.17) (q:draft)
kipelhkhia = (t:v) (w:be released from/be freed from) (d:kipelh, be free from, with khia, out; used with tawh for the thing one is freed from) (e:tua numei in thukham tawh a ~ a) (b:kipelh) (r:45.7.3) (q:draft)
kipelhkik = (t:v) (w:be averted/be turned back/be revoked) (d:kipelh, be kept away, with kik, back; said of an evil plan that is to be undone) (e:a ~ theih nadingin va thum hi) (b:kipelh) (r:17.8.3) (q:draft)
kipelhna = (t:n) (w:avoiding/escape/turning away) (d:Kipelh, keep clear of, with the noun suffix na: the avoiding of something or escape from it, used with tawh.) (e:sihna thang tawh ~ ahi hi/Topa zahtakna in siatna tawh ~ hi | the fear of the Lord is the way to avoid evil/mawhnopna lungsim tawh ~ a ngah khinta | have already been freed from the sinful mind) (s:pelhna) (b:kipelh) (r:20.13.14/20.16.6/51.2.11) (q:draft)
kipelhsak = (t:v) (w:keep from/spare from/turn away from/take away) (d:cause to pass by or be kept away from someone, from kipelh; with a negative, not let go of a promise) (e:Hih hai kei tawh ~ in/sihna thang tawh ~ hi | it keeps one from the snares of death/ka thuciamna ka ~ kei ding hi | I will not let go of my promise/hih hai kei tawh hong ~ in | take this cup from me) (b:kipelh) (r:41.14.36/20.14.27/19.89.33/42.22.42) (q:draft)
kipelhsakna = (t:n) (w:sparing/deliverance) (d:kipelhsak, keep from, with the noun suffix na: being spared from something, with tawh) (e:sihna tawh nong ~ ding ahi hi) (b:kipelhsak) (r:17.7.3) (q:draft)
kipelhzaw = (t:v) (w:rather be spared/rather keep free from) (d:kipelh, be free from, with zaw, more or rather; used with tawh) (e:tuate tawh ~ le-uh hoih ka sa hi) (b:kipelh) (r:46.7.28) (q:draft)
kipengsak = (t:v) (w:be exempted/be made free from) (d:passive of pengsak: be released from a duty or a tax) (e:siah khempeuh ~ ding hi) (b:pengsak) (r:9.17.25) (q:draft)
kipetkha = (t:v) (w:bite each other) (d:ki, each other, with pet, bite, and kha, happen to) (e:khatlekhat kiphuai-in ~ le-uhcin) (s:kipeh) (r:48.5.15) (q:draft)
kiphah = (t:v) (w:be spread/be laid out) (d:be spread or laid flat, as a bed, paving stones or a body on the ground) (e:Saul adingin lupna khat na ~ a/suang a ~ lampi om hi | there was a pavement laid with stone/Leilakah na pumpi ~ ding a | your body will lie spread on the open field/puanbuk kilumletin lei lakah ~ hi | the tent overturned and lay flat on the ground) (b:phah) (r:9.9.25/26.40.17/26.29.5/7.7.13) (q:draft)
kiphal = (t:v) (w:be allowed/be permitted) (d:Passive of phal, allow: be allowed or permitted; with lo, not be allowed.) (e:thu a gen ding uh ~ lo hi/vantungah zong ~ ding hi | it will be allowed in heaven also/pai dingin kei hong ~ lo ahih manin | because I am not allowed to go/a zawhgawp theih nading zong ~ hi | it was also allowed to conquer them) (a:kikham) (b:phal) (r:46.14.34/40.18.18/24.36.5/66.13.7) (q:draft)
kiphamat = (t:v) (w:follow one upon another/overtake one another) (d:in a ciah leh a kuan kiphamat, those leaving and those setting out catch up with each other: said of people or messengers coming and going without a break) (e:a ciah leh a kuan ~ uh a/Mi a ciah leh a kuan ~ uh ahih manin | because people were coming and going without a break) (r:24.51.31/41.6.31) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiphamawh = (t:v) (w:be necessary/be obliged) (d:from phamawh, necessary; with hi lo, there is no obligation to do something) (e:gamtat ding a ~ hi lo hi) (s:kisam) (b:phamawh) (r:45.8.12) (q:draft)
kiphamawhte = (t:n) (w:those addicted/those dependent on) (d:people who cannot do without something; zunek kiphamawhte, those addicted to drinking wine) (e:zunek ~ ahih loh nading) (b:kiphamawh) (r:56.2.3) (q:draft)
kiphan = (t:v) (w:be woven/be embroidered) (d:of cloth, be woven or worked with a pattern) (e:a kizem a ~ puan hoihte la-in/a lu pan a taw dongin a ~ ahi hi | it was woven from top to bottom) (r:26.16.18/43.19.23) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiphasak = (t:v) (w:be proud/be arrogant/boast) (d:Think highly of oneself, be proud or boastful; a kiphasak mite are the proud.) (e:A ~ mite en in la/amah a lungkhauhin ~ a | he became hard-hearted and proud/kiliansakin a ~ mite ahi hi | they are the arrogant and proud people/a ~ thei kei hi | it is not proud/a ~ leh a kiliansak khempeuh | all the proud and lofty) (s:kisathei/kihisak/kiliansak/kiphatsak) (a:kiniamkhiat/kiniamsak) (r:18.40.11/19.75.4/27.5.20/20.21.24/46.13.4/23.2.12) (q:draft)
kiphasakin = (t:v) (w:be proud/boast/exalt oneself) (d:kiphasak with the linking suffix -in, being proud and then doing the next action; also proudly) (e:na lungsim uh ~ kei nong mangngilh/~ a tonu simmawh bawl hi | she became proud and despised her mistress/Amaute ~ haipau uh a | they speak proud and foolish words/a ~ a gamtate a neusak hi | he humbles those who walk in pride) (b:kiphasak) (r:28.13.6/1.16.4/61.2.18/27.4.37) (q:draft)
kiphasaknate = (t:n) (w:pride/boastings) (d:kiphasak, be proud, with the noun suffix na and the plural te) (e:Mi liante’ ~ a beisak nading) (s:kiphatsaknate) (b:kiphasak) (r:23.23.9) (q:draft)
Kiphasakpa = (t:n) (w:proud man/vain man/foolish person) (d:kiphasak be proud or boast, with pa marking a man; used in address) (e:~ aw, gamtatna hoih om loin) (r:59.2.20) (q:draft)
kiphasakte = (t:n) (w:the proud/the arrogant) (d:kiphasak with plural te, those who are proud; often mi kiphasakte) (e:Pasian in mi ~ niamkhiat a/Topa in mi ~’ inn phelkhiatsak a | the Lord tears down the house of the proud/Mi ~ hawlkhia lecin | if you drive out the proud) (s:kihisakte/kisatheite/kiliansakte) (a:kiniamkhiatte) (b:kiphasak) (r:18.22.29/20.15.25/20.22.10) (q:draft)
kiphasakteng = (t:n) (w:the arrogant/all the proud) (d:kiphasak, be proud, with teng, all: after mi, all the people who are proud) (e:mi ~ mah in thupha ngahin) (b:kiphasak) (r:39.3.15) (q:draft)
kiphat = (t:v) (w:be praised/be commended) (d:Passive of phat, praise: be praised or commended.) (e:Pasian min ~ tawntung ta hen/lei nop hun-a a zuak pahte ~ hi | those who sell readily are praised/Topa Jesuh’ min nakpitakin a ~ semsem hi | the name of the Lord Jesus was praised more and more/min ~ ta hen | may the name be praised) (s:kipahtawi) (a:kisamsia) (b:phat) (r:27.2.20/20.11.26/44.19.17/18.1.21) (q:draft)
kiphat = (t:v) (w:commend oneself/praise oneself) (d:Reflexive of phat, praise: praise or commend oneself, often with amahmah, himself, or amah leh amah.) (e:amahmah a ~ mi in san’ huai lo hi/amah leh amah a ~ mi khempeuh | everyone who exalts himself/komau pumpi uh ~ kik ka hi kei uh hi | we are not commending ourselves again) (s:kiphattawm) (a:kiniamkhiat) (b:phat) (r:47.10.18/42.18.14/47.5.12) (q:draft)
kiphatin = (t:v) (w:being praised/praised) (d:kiphat be praised, with the linking ending in) (e:Mipilte ~ kipahtawi a) (b:kiphat) (r:20.12.8) (q:draft)
kiphatna = (t:n) (w:praise/commendation) (d:praise that someone receives; kiphatna lai is a letter of recommendation) (e:nangmah hong ~ in zong a zel hi/Mite’ hehna in nangmah hong ~ piangsak ding a | human wrath will bring you praise/keimah hong ~ ka ngaihsutna-in | for the sake of my praise/~ lai note kiangah | letters of recommendation to you) (s:phatna/minphatna) (b:phatna) (r:19.48.10/47.3.1/19.76.10/23.48.9) (q:draft)
kiphatnate = (t:n) (w:praises) (d:kiphatna praise, with the plural te) (e:nangmah a hong ~ phawk kikkik inla/keimah hong ~ bang ka ngah sak kei hi | I will not give away my praises) (s:phatnate) (b:kiphatna) (r:19.9.14/23.42.8) (q:draft)
kiphatphat = (t:v) (w:be praised again and again/be praised continually) (d:passive of phatphat keep praising) (e:nangma nasepnate ~ ding a) (b:phatphat) (r:19.145.4) (q:draft)
kiphatsak = (t:v) (w:boast/be proud/be arrogant) (d:praise oneself; before pau or gamtat it means speak or behave proudly) (e:na ~ gamtat nawn kei ding uh/na ~ paunate khempeuh | all your boastful words/Amau’ ~ pauna hangun | because of their insolent words/na ~ theih nading uh a thu om lo hi | you have no reason to boast) (s:kiphasak/kisathei/kihisak/kisialh) (a:kiniamkhiat) (b:kiphat) (r:33.2.3/19.17.10/26.35.13/28.7.16/45.11.18) (q:draft)
kiphatsak = (t:v) (w:cause to be praised) (d:ki- form of phatsak, let someone or something be praised) (e:mi cimawhte nangma min ~ in) (b:phatsak) (r:19.74.21) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiphatsakna = (t:n) (w:pride/arrogance/boasting) (d:Kiphatsak, be proud, with the noun suffix na: a high opinion of oneself, pride or boasting.) (e:~ in pukna hong piang sak hi/~ tawh mi tampi in kei hong do hi | in their pride many attack me/~ sangin lungduaina hoihzaw hi | patience is better than pride/~ tawh kam pau kei un | do not speak with arrogance) (s:kisaktheihna/kihihsakna/kiliatsakna/kisialhna) (a:kiniamkhiatna) (r:20.16.18/19.75.5/19.56.2/21.7.8) (q:draft)
kiphatsaknate = (t:n) (w:pride/arrogance/boastings) (d:Kiphatsakna, pride, with the plural te: acts or kinds of pride.) (e:a ~ uh a lakkhia ahi hi/a ~ uh Pasian in niamsuk sak ding hi | God will bring down their pride) (s:kiphasaknate) (b:kiphatsakna) (r:18.36.9/23.23.9/23.25.11) (q:draft)
kiphatsakpih = (t:v) (w:take pride in/boast of) (d:kiphatsak with pih: be proud on account of something; before a noun or standing alone, the thing one is proud of, the pride) (e:a ~ uh kizepna a manphate/na ~ uh note’ vangliatna susia-in | breaking the power you are proud of/Khaldel mite’ vangliatna leh ~ | the power and pride of the Chaldeans/a ~ kumpi lukhu | the crown they are proud of) (s:kisaktheihpih) (b:kiphatsak) (r:26.7.20/3.26.19/23.13.19/23.28.3) (q:draft)
kiphattawm = (t:v) (w:commend oneself/praise oneself/boast) (d:Kiphat, praise oneself, with tawm, by oneself: praise or commend oneself.) (e:nangma kamin ~ kei in/Kote in ko-le-ko ~ ka hi uh hiam | are we commending ourselves/mi khat peuhpeuh amah a ~ ciangin | when anyone commends himself/Midangte in hong phat lohbuang nangmah ~ kei in | let others praise you, do not praise yourself) (s:kiphat) (r:20.27.2/47.10.18/47.3.1) (q:draft)
kiphatte = (t:n) (w:those who commend themselves) (d:kiphat, praise oneself, with the plural te) (e:Amau mah a ~ tawh) (b:kiphat) (r:47.10.12) (q:draft)
kiphawk = (t:v) (w:be remembered/be missed) (d:Passive of phawk, remember: be remembered or be missed; with nawn lo, be forgotten.) (e:amah ~ tawntung ding hi/Misi bangin kei hong ~ nawn lo hi | I am forgotten like a dead man/Nang hong ~ theih nadingin | so that you will be remembered/nang hong ~ ding hi | you will be missed) (a:kimangngilh) (b:phawk) (r:19.112.6/9.20.18/19.31.12/23.23.16) (q:draft)
kiphawkin = (t:v) (w:be remembered/be realised) (d:kiphawk, be remembered or noticed, with the linking ending in, joining it to the next verb) (e:hih nite ~ a kitan’ nading/hihnu’ thu ~ kei tungah hong sepnate kigengen ding hi | what she has done for me will be told in memory of her/a zak uh thute hangin a mawhna uh ~ | their sin is brought home to them by what they hear) (b:kiphawk) (r:17.9.28/41.14.9/46.14.24) (q:draft)
kiphawkkha = (t:v) (w:be remembered/come to mind) (d:Passive of phawkkha, call to mind: be remembered or come to mind; mostly with nawn lo, be remembered no more.) (e:A beisa nate ~ nawn lo a/Amah ~ nawn lo a | he is remembered no more/kiciamteh nawn lo ding a, ~ nawn lo ding hi | they will not be recorded nor come to mind) (a:kimangngilh) (b:phawkkha) (r:21.1.11/23.65.17/18.24.20) (q:draft)
kiphawkkhia = (t:v) (w:be found/be discovered) (d:passive of phawkkhia, find out: come to light, here of something found written in a book) (e:a kihel ngei loh nading thu ~ hi) (s:kimukhia) (b:phawkkhia) (r:16.13.1) (q:draft)
kiphawkmawh = (t:v) (w:overlook/pretend not to notice/hold back) (d:with bawl, do: act as if one had not noticed a wrong, let it pass) (e:mi’ hong hehsaknate ~ bawlna in minthan’na hi/Kong ~ bawl nawn kei ding a | I will not overlook it any longer) (s:kimuhmawh) (r:20.19.11/26.24.14) (q:draft)
kiphawkna = (t:n) (w:memory/remembrance) (d:the fact of being remembered; with bei or beisak, the memory of someone is wiped out) (e:leitung panin amah a ~ bei ta hen/mite lakah amaute a ~ ka beisak ding hi | I will wipe out their memory among mankind/khang tawntungin nangmah hong ~ a kip hi | your renown endures through all generations) (s:phawkna) (b:kiphawk) (r:19.109.15/5.32.26/19.102.12) (q:draft)
kiphawkphawk = (t:v) (w:be long remembered/be remembered continually) (d:Passive of phawkphawk, keep remembering: be remembered for a long time.) (e:mipilte zong ~ tuan lo hi/Mihoihte ~ a, migilote kimangngilh pah hi | the good are long remembered, the wicked are soon forgotten) (a:kimangngilh) (b:phawkphawk) (r:21.2.16/20.10.7) (q:draft)
kiphawksak = (t:v) (w:cause to be remembered/keep in memory/be remembered) (d:kiphawk be remembered with sak causative) (e:Israel min ~ nawn kei ni/khang tawntungin nangma min ka ~ ding hi | I will make your name remembered through all generations/ama gamtatnasate ~ lo ding hi | his deeds will not be remembered/mite a mawhna uh a ~ kikkik ahi hi | people are reminded of their sins again and again) (b:kiphawk) (r:19.83.4/19.45.17/26.18.24/58.10.3) (q:draft)
kiphawktel = (t:v) (w:realise/perceive/know clearly) (d:phawktel, realise, with the prefix ki) (e:ama kumpigam a liatsakna ~ hi) (s:phawktel) (b:phawktel) (r:10.5.12) (q:draft)
kipheek = (t:adj) (w:braided/plaited) (d:said of hair, with sam) (e:a ~ sam tawh ahi zongin) (r:54.2.9) (q:draft)
kiphel = (t:v) (w:be loosed/be untied/be taken down) (d:Passive of phel, undo: be untied or loosed, or of a tent, an altar or a building be taken down.) (e:vantungah a ~ ding hi/Biakbuk a ~ khit ciangin | after the tabernacle was taken down/vantungah zong a ~ ding hi | it will be loosed in heaven also/ama biakna tau ~ khin hi | his altar has been torn down) (a:kihen) (b:phel) (r:40.18.18/4.10.17/40.16.19/7.6.31) (q:draft)
kiphel = (t:v) (w:split apart/split open) (d:Written before kham in kiphel kham, split open, said of the ground; the joined spelling is kiphelkham.) (e:amau’ nuai-ah lei ~ kham hi) (s:kiphelkham) (b:phel) (r:4.16.31) (q:draft)
kiphel = (t:v) (w:defend oneself/clear oneself) (d:speak to free oneself from a charge or to prove innocence) (e:a ~ nading thu hong gen a/ko bangci ~ theih ding ka hi uh hiam | how can we clear ourselves/amah a ~ theih nading thugenna hun | a chance to speak in his own defence/a mawhna thu uhah ~ nading a paulap | an excuse to clear themselves of their sin) (s:kihut/kisut) (b:phel) (r:44.26.1/1.44.16/44.25.16/43.15.22) (q:draft)
kiphelh = (t:v) (w:be quenched/be put out) (d:passive of phelh quench, of a fire) (e:mei a ~ zo kei ding hi) (s:kisumit/kimitsak/kisukmit) (a:kitawh) (b:phelh) (r:24.17.27) (q:draft)
kiphelh = (t:v) (w:clear oneself/defend oneself) (d:form of kiphel used before nading: mawhna kiphelh nading, to clear oneself of a charge) (e:tu-ni ka mawhna ~ nading) (b:kiphel) (r:44.22.1) (q:draft)
kiphelhna = (t:n) (w:defence) (d:kiphelh, clear oneself, with the noun suffix na; mawhna kiphelhna, clearing oneself of a charge) (e:mawhna ~ thu a gen lai takin) (s:kiphelna) (b:kiphelh) (r:44.26.24) (q:draft)
kiphelhzo = (t:v) (w:can be quenched/can be put out) (d:kiphelh, be quenched, with zo, be able; with kei, unquenchable) (e:a mei a ~ kei ding hi) (b:kiphelh) (r:24.17.27) (q:draft)
kiphelin = (t:v) (w:splitting apart/being split) (d:kiphel split apart, with the linking ending in) (e:biakna tau ~ a tunga om vutte/lim khat a piaksa tawh kizui-in biakna tau zong ~ | the altar also split apart according to the sign he had given) (b:kiphel) (r:11.13.3/11.13.5) (q:draft)
kiphelkeek = (t:v) (w:be demolished/be torn down) (d:passive of phelkeek, tear down; said of altars) (e:Biakna taute ~ ding a) (s:kiphelkek/kiphelkhia) (a:kilam) (b:phelkeek) (r:26.6.4) (q:draft)
kiphelkek = (t:v) (w:be demolished/be torn down) (d:passive of phelkek tear down, of altars and buildings) (e:Biakna taute ~ ding a/a ~ gawp hun hong tung ding hi | the time will come when they are thrown down completely) (s:kiphelkeek/kiphelkhia) (a:kilam) (b:phelkek) (r:26.6.4/41.13.2) (q:draft)
kiphelkekmang = (t:v) (w:be thrown down/be torn down completely) (d:passive of phelkek, tear down, with mang, away or gone) (e:om nawn loin ~ ding hi) (r:42.21.6) (q:draft)
kiphelkham = (t:v) (w:be split apart/split open) (d:passive of phelkham, split open; said of the ground or the earth) (e:amau’ nuai-ah lei ~ hi/kilok gawp ding a, ~ ding hi | it will be violently shaken and split apart/Suang tawh a kidenglum, sing-at tawh a ~ | stoned to death, sawn in two) (s:khangkham) (b:phelkham) (r:4.16.31/23.24.19/58.11.37) (q:draft)
kiphelkhamin = (t:v) (w:be divided/be split apart) (d:kiphelkham with the linking in, being split or divided up) (e:Na gam ~ midang tungah kipia ding a/a gammite ~ pawlkhat le pawlkhat kido le-uh | if its people are divided and fight one another/innkuan khat ahi zongin ~ kido le-uh | or if a household is divided and fights) (s:kikhenthang) (b:kiphelkham) (r:30.7.17/11.13.5/42.11.17/40.12.25) (q:draft)
kiphelkhia = (t:v) (w:be thrown down/be torn down/come loose) (d:be taken apart or broken off, of stones of a building or of chains) (e:sikkhau khempeuh a ~ hi/A ~ loin suang khat tungah suang kiciang khat beek | not one stone left on another that is not thrown down/Baal biakna tau ~-in | the altar of Baal had been torn down/a ~ lo ding suang khat | one stone that will not be thrown down) (s:kiphelkek) (b:phelkhia) (r:44.16.26/41.13.2/7.6.28/42.21.6) (q:draft)
kiphellah = (t:v) (w:defend oneself/clear oneself) (d:apparently kiphel, defend oneself against a charge, with lah; the verse says there will be nothing to answer for when one is accused) (e:na ~ ding khat beek om lo ding hi) (r:45.3.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiphelna = (t:n) (w:defense/clearing of oneself) (d:answering an accusation, usually mawh kiphelna) (e:ka mawh ~ thu kong gen ding hi/Judah mite in hong mawhsakna ~ thu | my defence against what the Jews accuse me of/mite mai-ah mawh ~ thu a gen nop hangin | though he wanted to make a defence before the people) (s:kiphelhna) (b:kiphel) (r:44.24.10/44.26.2/44.19.33) (q:draft)
kiphelphel = (t:v) (w:keep defending oneself/defend oneself) (d:kiphel, defend oneself, doubled for a repeated action; used with mawhna) (e:ka mawhna uh a ~ bang khatin) (r:47.12.19) (q:draft)
kiphelsa = (t:adj) (w:open/opened) (d:kiphel, be untied or loosed, with the completive suffix sa; said of a scroll that lies open) (e:a om laizial ~ pen va la in) (b:kiphel) (r:66.10.8) (q:draft)
kiphelsak = (t:v) (w:be torn down/be broken down) (d:said of an altar; from kiphel, be taken down, with sak) (e:ama biakna tau a ~ ahi hi) (b:kiphel) (r:7.6.31) (q:draft)
kiphen = (t:v) (w:be opened) (d:passive of phen, open; said of a book or scroll) (e:Laibute zong ~ uh hi/adang laibu khat a ~ hi | another book was opened/Thukhenna ding hun kipan a, laibute a ~ hi | the time of judgment began and the books were opened) (s:kihon) (b:phen) (r:66.20.12/27.7.10) (q:draft)
kiphenin = (t:v) (w:be open/lie open) (d:kiphen, be opened, with the linking ending in; said of a book or scroll) (e:khut sungah ~ a om laibu) (b:kiphen) (r:66.10.8) (q:draft)
kiphiat = (t:v) (w:be swept) (d:be swept clean, said of a house) (e:tua inn awngin, ~ kipuah a) (b:phiat) (r:40.12.44) (q:draft)
kiphiat = (t:v) (w:be annulled/be wiped out/be blotted out) (d:be done away with, said of an agreement or of people) (e:na thuciamna uh ~ ding a/Judah leh Israel a kipawlna ~ hi | the union between Judah and Israel was annulled/Ama min Israel panin a ~ loh nadingin | so that his name will not be blotted out from Israel) (s:kiphiatkhia/kibeisak) (b:phiat) (r:23.28.18/38.11.14/5.25.6) (q:draft)
kiphiatkhia = (t:v) (w:be wiped out/be blotted out/be swept away) (d:Passive of phiatkhia, wipe out: be wiped out, blotted out or swept away.) (e:leitung panin amaute ~ hi/Keima mai-ah amaute’ min ~ lo ding a | their name will not be blotted out from before me/note hong ~ kha ding ahih manin | lest you be swept away/na nihun hong ~ ding hi | both of you will be swept away) (s:kiphiat) (b:phiatkhia) (r:1.7.23/23.48.19/4.16.26/9.12.25) (q:draft)
kiphiatsak = (t:v) (w:be blotted out/be wiped out) (d:kiphiat be wiped out with sak: let them be wiped out, here of names in a book) (e:laibu sung panin amaute ~ in la) (b:kiphiat) (r:19.69.28) (q:draft)
kiphin = (t:v) (w:provoke each other) (d:ki, each other, with phin, provoke) (e:Kuamah kiphasak loin, khatlekhat ~ loin) (b:phin) (r:48.5.26) (q:draft)
kiphitsan = (t:v) (w:be hissed at/be scorned/be scoffed at) (d:passive of phitsan, hiss or scoff at; simmawhna tawh a kiphitsan, an object of scorn) (e:simmawhna tawh a ~ den ding gam/a lipkhaphuai, simmawhna tawh a ~ | an object of horror and scorn) (s:kinuihsan/kisimmawh) (b:phitsan) (r:24.18.16/24.51.37) (q:draft)
kipho = (t:v) (w:be spread out/be exposed/be laid bare) (d:passive of pho spread out: be laid out in the open where all can see) (e:Pasian mai-ah ~ laakin a om hi/van-a om nate khempeuh’ mai-ah a ~ khia ding hi | they will be exposed before all the things in the sky) (s:kipholak) (b:pho) (r:58.4.13/24.8.2) (q:draft)
kiphokhia = (t:v) (w:be exposed/be spread out) (d:kipho, be spread out, with khia, out: be laid out in the open) (e:khempeuh mai-ah a ~ ding hi) (s:kipholak) (b:kipho) (r:24.8.2) (q:draft)
kipholaak = (t:v) (w:be disclosed/be revealed/be made known) (d:said of a secret that is brought into the open) (e:a ~ lo ding thusim bangmah) (s:kipholak/kilang) (a:kiseel) (r:42.8.17) (q:draft)
kipholak = (t:v) (w:be exposed/be revealed/be uncovered) (d:passive of pholak, expose: be laid open for all to see, of sin, shame or a secret; amah leh amah a kipholak is expose oneself) (e:Na mawhna teng uh tu-in hong ~ hi/Na paktat gamtatna teng hong ~ ding hi | all your prostitution will be exposed/Pasian’ mite tungah a ~ ta ahi hi | it has now been disclosed to God's people/a kiseel peuhmah khatvei teitei a ~ ding | whatever is concealed will surely be brought into the open) (s:kipholaak/kilang/kilangkhia) (a:kiseel/kiseelcip) (b:pholak) (r:26.21.24/26.23.29/51.1.26/41.4.22) (q:draft)
kiphong = (t:v) (w:be awakened/be woken) (d:passive of phong, wake: be woken from sleep) (e:a ihmu kimlai a ~ bang) (b:phong) (r:38.4.1) (q:draft)
kiphop = (t:v) (w:be patched/be mended) (d:passive of phop mend; a kiphop khedap, a patched sandal) (e:a ~ khedapte bulhin) (b:phop) (r:6.9.5) (q:draft)
kiphopte = (t:adj) (w:patched/mended) (d:kiphop be patched, with the plural te: the patched ones, here of wineskins) (e:a kikeek leh a ~ guangin) (b:kiphop) (r:6.9.4) (q:draft)
kiphu = (t:v) (w:collide/run into each other/stumble against) (d:ki each other with phu push against: knock against one another) (e:khat leh khat ~ kha-in) (s:kiphukha) (b:phu) (r:24.46.12) (q:draft)
kiphu = (t:v) (w:head into/face) (d:with huih wind: of a ship, hold its way against the wind) (e:huih ~ zo nawn lo ahih ciangin) (b:phu) (r:44.27.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiphuah = (t:v) (w:be named/be given a name) (d:passive of phuah, give a name; used with min, name) (e:ci-in min a ~ masakna mun) (s:kiphuak) (b:phuah) (r:44.11.26) (q:draft)
kiphuahna = (t:n) (w:naming/being named) (d:kiphuah, be named, with the noun suffix na; hong kiphuahna min, the name by which you are called) (e:Note hong ~ min ngaih) (b:kiphuah) (r:59.2.7) (q:draft)
kiphuai = (t:see) <kiphuai-in>
kiphuai-in = (t:v) (w:tear at each other/devour each other) (d:said of wild animals attacking one another, with the linking ending in; the verse pairs it with kipetkha, bite each other, and it is not clear which of the two is bite and which is devour) (e:gamsa bangin khatlekhat ~ kipetkha le-uhcin) (r:48.5.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiphuak = (t:v) (w:be named/be called) (d:passive of phuak, give a name: be given a name, usually after min, name) (e:ama min Zerah ~ hi/a min Johan ~ ding hi | he is to be named John/Marah ci-in min ~ hi | it was given the name Marah/ama' min Jakob ~ hi | he was named Jacob) (s:kiphuah/kici) (b:phuak) (r:1.38.30/42.1.60/2.15.23/1.25.26) (q:draft)
kiphuakpa = (t:n) (w:one who is named/the man called) (d:kiphuak be named, with pa for a man: the man to whom a name was given) (e:Belteshazzar ci-a a ~ Daniel sam sak in) (b:kiphuak) (r:27.5.12/27.4.8) (q:draft)
kiphuh = (t:v) (w:be laid/be founded/be set) (d:of a foundation, be laid; of a pillar, be set on its base) (e:inn bulpi a ~ ni-a kipan a kizawh dongin/biakinn bulpi a ~ khit | after the foundation of the temple was laid/a bulpi a ~ nai loh hangin | though its foundation had not yet been laid/hih inn bulpi a ~ a muh uh ciangin | when they saw the foundation of this house being laid) (s:kiphut) (b:phuh) (r:14.8.16/37.2.18/15.3.6/15.3.12) (q:draft)
kiphuhna = (t:n) (w:settling/resting) (d:kiphuh be set down, with the noun suffix na; a kiphuhna mun, the place where a thing comes to rest, here of the cloud) (e:meii a ~ munah Israel mite in) (b:kiphuh) (r:4.9.17) (q:draft)
kiphuk = (t:v) (w:be cut down/be felled) (d:passive of phuk, fell: of a tree or a wooden idol, be cut down; kiphuk tan is be cut right off) (e:Gamlakah sing khat ~ a/A gah hoih lo kung khempeuh ~ tan a | every tree that does not bear good fruit is cut down/a kung sangte ~ ding a | the tall trees will be felled/gammang tupi sing teng ~ ta hi | the dense forest has been cut down/Asherah milim ~ a | the Asherah pole was cut down) (s:kiphukmang/kiphukpai) (a:kisuan) (b:phuk) (r:24.10.3/40.7.19/23.10.33/38.11.2/7.6.28) (q:draft)
kiphukha = (t:v) (w:jostle one another/collide/stumble over one another) (d:phukha knock against, with the reciprocal prefix ki) (e:kuamah a ~ om lo uh hi/Na galkapte uh khatlekhat ~-in | your warriors stumbling over one another) (s:kiphu) (b:phukha) (r:29.2.8/24.46.12) (q:draft)
kiphukin = (t:v) (w:being cut down/cut down and) (d:kiphuk be cut down, with the linking ending in) (e:~ meikhuk sungah kikhul hi/Gah hoih a gah lo singkung khempeuh ~ | every tree that does not bear good fruit is cut down and/Gah limci a gah lo singkungte ~ | trees that do not bear good fruit are cut down and) (b:kiphuk) (r:40.7.19/42.3.9) (q:draft)
kiphukmang = (t:v) (w:be cut down/be felled) (d:passive of phukmang: of trees, be cut down and cleared away) (e:gammang tupi singteng ~ khinta hi) (s:kiphuk/kiphukpai) (b:phukmang) (r:38.11.2) (q:draft)
kiphukna = (t:n) (w:felling/cutting down) (d:kiphuk, be cut down, with the noun suffix na; said of trees) (e:kei a dingin a ~ ding thu pia in) (b:kiphuk) (r:11.5.6) (q:draft)
kiphukpai = (t:v) (w:be cut down/be felled/be cast down) (d:passive of phukpai cut down) (e:hong bangci ~ ahi hiam) (s:kiphuk/kiphukmang) (b:phukpai) (r:23.14.12) (q:draft)
kiphuksa = (t:adj) (w:cut down/felled) (d:kiphuk, be cut down, with the completive suffix sa; said of a tree) (e:A ~ singkung nangawn in) (b:kiphuk) (r:18.14.7) (q:draft)
kiphulet = (t:v) (w:be broken through/be breached) (d:passive of phulet; said of a city wall) (e:Tua ciangin khuakulhpi ~ a) (s:kiphutlet) (b:phulet) (r:24.52.7) (q:draft)
kiphum = (t:v) (w:be baptized) (d:passive of phum, immerse: be baptized, often with tui, water; baptism is kiphumna) (e:Khrih sungah a ~ note in/Topa Jesuh’ minin tui a ~ uh hi | they were baptized in the name of the Lord Jesus) (s:kibaptaiz/kituiphum) (b:phum) (r:48.3.27/42.12.50/44.19.5) (q:draft)
kiphum = (t:v) (w:be buried) (d:passive of phum, bury: of a dead person, be laid in a grave) (e:gamlak ama inn sungah amah ~ hi/Moab gam kuamah amah ~ hi | he was buried in a valley in the land of Moab/kumpite’ han sungah ~ lo hi | he was not buried in the tombs of the kings/kikaikhawm loin ~ lo ding uh | they will not be gathered up or buried) (s:kivui/kivuk) (b:phum) (r:11.2.34/5.34.6/14.21.20/24.25.33) (q:draft)
kiphumcip = (t:v) (w:be buried/be hidden/be overwhelmed) (d:passive of phumcip bury, submerge, with the prefix ki: be covered over completely and so hidden; of a person in sorrow, be swallowed up by it) (e:a ~ nate hong suahkhia uh hi/dah mahmahin ~ a | be overwhelmed by great sorrow) (s:kivukcip/kiseelcip) (b:phumcip) (r:18.28.11/47.2.7) (q:draft)
kiphumin = (t:v) (w:be baptized) (d:kiphum, be baptized, with the linking ending in) (e:keima min tawh a ~ na kigen kha ding) (b:kiphum) (r:46.1.15) (q:draft)
kiphumna = (t:n) (w:burial/grave) (d:being buried; kiphumna mun and kiphumna hankhuk are the place where someone is buried) (e:amah a ~ mun kuamah in thei lo hi/Note na ~ uh hankhuk hong hon’sakin | when I open your graves) (s:kivuina) (b:kiphum) (r:5.34.6/26.37.13) (q:draft)
kiphumna = (t:n) (w:plunging in/meddling) (d:throwing oneself into something, such as a quarrel of other people) (e:lo kitotna sunga va ~ in) (b:kiphum) (r:20.26.17) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiphumpah = (t:v) (w:be baptized at once) (d:kiphum, be baptized, with pah, immediately; used with tui, water) (e:Saul zong tui ~ a) (r:44.9.18) (q:draft)
kiphumzo = (t:v) (w:be able to be baptized) (d:kiphum, be baptized, with zo, be able) (e:gimna-ah ~ ding na hi uh hiam) (b:kiphum) (r:41.10.38) (q:draft)
kiphunsan = (t:v) (w:grumble against each other/complain against each other) (d:phunsan, grumble against, with the prefix ki, each other) (e:Note khatlekhat ~ kei un/ci-in a ~ uh hi | they grumbled among themselves, saying/khat leh na ~ kei un | do not grumble against one another) (b:phunsan) (r:43.6.43/59.5.9/43.6.42) (q:draft)
kiphunsanna = (t:n) (w:grumbling/complaint/murmuring) (d:kiphunsan grumble against each other, with the noun suffix na) (e:Jew mite kikalah ~ thu hong om hi) (s:phunsanna/phunna) (b:kiphunsan) (r:44.6.1/47.12.20) (q:draft)
kiphupai = (t:v) (w:stumble over each other/fall over each other) (d:ki each other with phu push against and pai go: run into one another while fleeing) (e:amaute khat leh khat ~ ding uh hi) (s:kiphukha/kiphu) (r:3.26.37) (q:draft)
kiphusak = (t:v) (w:smash together/dash against each other) (d:kiphu collide with the causative sak: make people strike against one another) (e:amaute khat leh khat ka ~ ding a) (b:kiphu) (r:24.13.14) (q:draft)
kiphut = (t:v) (w:be set up/be established/be founded) (d:passive of phut, set up: of a foundation, be laid; of a throne, be established; of a post, be set firmly in place) (e:bang tungah ~ ahi hiam/Na bulpi ~ ding hi | your foundation will be laid/kumpi tokhom khat ~ ding a | a throne will be established/inn bulpi ~ khin ahih manin | because the foundation of the house had been laid) (s:kiphuh) (b:phut) (r:18.38.6/23.16.5/23.44.28/15.3.11) (q:draft)
kiphutin = (t:v) (w:being set up/set firmly) (d:kiphut be set up, be established, with the linking ending in) (e:leitungah kahlei khat ~/khuam bangin ~, kipna tawh na up uh leh | if you believe with firmness, set firm like a post) (b:kiphut) (r:1.28.12/51.1.22) (q:draft)
kiphutkik = (t:v) (w:be laid again/be set up again) (d:kiphut, be set up or founded, with kik, again; said of the foundation of the temple) (e:Na bulpi ~ ding hi) (b:kiphut) (r:23.44.28) (q:draft)
kiphutlet = (t:v) (w:be broken through/be breached) (d:said of a city wall; the other Bible text has kiphulet in the same verse) (e:Tua ciangin khua kulhpi ~ a) (s:kiphulet) (r:24.52.7) (q:draft)
kiphutte = (t:n) (w:settings) (d:kiphut be set in place, with the plural te: the gold settings in which stones are set) (e:a ~’ tungah na bulh ding hi) (b:kiphut) (r:2.28.14) (q:draft)
kiphuzo = (t:v) (w:be able to head into) (d:kiphu, head into, with zo, be able; huih kiphuzo nawn lo, no longer able to sail against the wind) (e:huih ~ nawn lo ahih manin) (b:kiphu) (r:44.27.7) (q:draft)
kipi = (t:v) (w:marry/take a wife) (d:take a husband or wife; paired with kiteeng or kiteengsak for marrying and being given in marriage; a kipi mo is a bride being wed) (e:a thokik mite ~ kiteengin a om/tui dawnin, ~, kiteengsakin a om uh hi | they were drinking, marrying and giving in marriage/a ~ mo bangin kiging kholin | made ready like a bride being wed/~-in a kiteengsak kei ding uh hi | they will neither marry nor be given in marriage) (s:zinei) (r:42.20.35/66.21.2/40.24.38/41.12.25) (q:draft)
kipia = (t:v) (w:given/be given/be allotted) (d:passive of pia, give: be given, handed over or allotted to someone) (e:amah ~ hi/Samson’ zi pen a moliahpa’ zi dingin ~ hi | Samson's wife was given to his companion as wife/mizawngte a ~ thei hi | it could be given to the poor/khuapi sawm ~ hi | ten towns were allotted) (a:kilakhia) (b:pia) (r:7.14.20/1.9.2/40.26.9/13.6.61)
Kipia = (t:v) (w:given/dedicated) (d:capitalised in an inscription: Topa-a’ dingin A Kipia, given over to the Lord, NIV Holy to the Lord) (e:dingin A ~) (b:kipia) (r:38.14.20) (q:draft)
kipiak = (t:v) (w:be given/be handed/be presented) (d:form of kipia used before endings such as ciangin, leh and ding) (e:Vantung panin a ~ kei leh/a neite a ~ beh ding hi | those who have will be given more/David tungah a ~ ding lai takin | at the time she was to be given to David/meihal biakna a ~ peuhpeuh ciangin | whenever burnt offerings were presented) (b:kipia) (r:43.3.27/42.4.17/41.4.25/9.18.19/13.23.31) (q:draft)
kipiakhawm = (t:v) (w:be offered together/be given along with) (d:passive of piakhawm, give together; said of an offering that goes with another) (e:tua tawh a ~ ding leenggahzu tawh biakna) (b:piakhawm) (r:3.23.13) (q:draft)
kipiakhia = (t:v) (w:be given/be given back/be returned) (d:passive of piakhia; of property returned to its owner in the jubilee year) (e:Kha Siangtho ~ nai lo hi/jubili ciangin tuate ~ ding hi | they are to be returned in the Jubilee/Jubilee kum ciangin tua leitang ~ ding a | in the Jubilee year that land will be returned) (s:kipiakik) (b:piakhia) (r:43.7.39/3.25.31/3.25.28) (q:draft)
kipiakhiate = (t:n) (w:things given/things devoted) (d:kipiakhia, be given, with the plural te: the things that are given over, here to God) (e:keima a dingin a ~ khempeuh) (b:kipiakhia) (r:26.44.29) (q:draft)
kipiakik = (t:v) (w:be given back/be returned/be restored) (d:passive of piakik give back, with the prefix ki) (e:jubilee kum ciangin ~ ding hi/umlebeelte zong ~ ding hi | the articles are also to be returned/jubili ciangin ~ lo ding hi | it is not to be returned in the Jubilee) (s:kipiakhia) (b:piakik) (r:3.25.33/15.6.5/3.25.30) (q:draft)
kipiakna = (t:n) (w:gave/giving/self-giving) (d:kipiak, be given, with the noun suffix na: the giving of an offering or of oneself) (e:a hun lian laitakin a hong ~ pen/~ ding Hezekiah in thu a pia hi | Hezekiah gave the order for it to be offered/Na khangno lai-a nong ~ | how you gave yourself to me in your youth) (b:kipia) (r:54.2.6/14.29.27/24.2.2)
kipiakna = (t:part) (d:particle conveying the meaning "give, given" used in combination with verb)
kipiaknate = (t:n) (w:things given/gifts/what was given) (d:kipiak, be given, with the noun suffix na and plural te: gifts offered to God, or with thu, the commands given to someone) (e:letsong tampi a ~ a gen uh ciangin/ama' tunga thu ~ Israel mite' kiangah a gen ciangin | when he told the Israelites what he had been commanded/Khrih tungah na ~ uh | your devotion to Christ) (b:kipiak) (r:42.21.5/2.34.34/47.11.3) (q:draft)
kipiaksa = (t:adj) (w:given/commanded) (d:kipiak, be given, with the completive suffix sa; thu a kipiaksa bangin, as was commanded) (e:tawntung dingin thu a ~ mah bangin/Israelte tungah thu a ~ bangin | as was commanded to Israel) (b:kipiak) (r:3.6.22/19.122.3) (q:draft)
kipiaksak = (t:v) (w:be given a share/be provided for) (d:kipiak, be given, with sak; with lo, be left out when things are given out) (e:meigong numeite uh hong ~ lo hi) (b:kipiak) (r:44.6.1) (q:draft)
kipiakte = (t:n) (w:offerings/things given) (d:kipiak, be given, with the plural te: the things that are given to someone) (e:keimah hong ~ thusim loin) (b:kipiak) (r:9.2.29) (q:draft)
kipiakzia = (t:n) (w:way of being given/how something is given) (d:kipiak, be given, with zia, manner; gimna a kipiakzia, how punishment is dealt out) (e:khuapi gimna a ~ ding) (b:piakzia) (r:66.17.1) (q:draft)
kipialsak = (t:v) (w:be led astray/be turned aside) (d:pialsak lead astray with ki: lam kipialsak, let oneself be turned off the way) (e:lam ~ kei in) (b:pialsak) (r:18.36.18) (q:draft)
kipian = (t:v) (w:be created/be made) (d:found in kipian'sak, be created: pian, come into being, with the prefix ki and causative sak) (e:Khazih in leitung a ~’sak ma-in/a ~’sak lai-a vantung leh leitung tangthu | the account of heaven and earth when they were created) (b:pian) (r:60.1.20/1.2.4) (q:draft)
kipiangsak = (t:v) (w:create/be created/be made) (d:passive of piangsak, create: be brought into being, be made) (e:Amah tawh leitung ~ hi/Thu tawh na khempeuh a ~ hi | through the Word all things were made/pasal hangin numei a ~ hizaw hi | rather woman was created for man/na hu na san’khiat ciangin amaute a ~ hi a | when you send out your breath they are created) (s:kibawl) (b:piangsak) (r:43.1.10/19.104.30/43.1.3/46.11.9)
kipiangsakin = (t:v) (w:institute/bring about) (d:kipiangsak, cause to come into being, with the linking ending in; here of the Passover being held for the first time) (e:a thahkhak loh nadingin Paisan Pawi ~) (b:kipiangsak) (r:58.11.28) (q:draft, low confidence)
kipiangsaksa = (t:n) (w:created thing/creature) (d:kipiangsak, be created, with the completive suffix sa: what has been created) (e:akipan a ~ khat beek in) (b:kipiangsak) (r:45.8.39) (q:draft)
kipiansak = (t:n) (w:generation) (e:Hihte pen, a ~ lai-a vantung le leitung tangthu ahi hi/Mual liante a ~ ma | before the mountains were brought forth/leitung a ~ ma-in | before the world was created) (b:piansak) (r:1.2.4/19.90.2/43.17.5)
kipiansakin = (t:v) (w:created) (d:kipiansak, be created, with the linking ending in: when they were created) (e:Amaute a ~ amah in amaute) (b:kipiansak) (r:1.5.2)
kipiansakna = (t:n) (w:creation) (d:kipiansak, be created, with the noun suffix na: the creating of someone, also the thing from which or the purpose for which one was made) (e:amah a ~ leitang a kho dingin/Mihing hong ~ a thu bulpi pen | the chief purpose for which man was created) (b:kipiansak) (r:1.3.23/21.12.13)
kipiasa = (t:v) (w:given/already given) (d:kipia with -sa for a completed action; what has been given, often before a noun) (e:hong ~ bek ahih manin/note tungah hong ~ a siangtho sa | the holy meat given to you/Pasian’ tungah a ~, Pasian tawh a kipawlsa mite | people given over to God and joined with God/Milim biakna-in a ~ an khat peuhpeuh | any food offered to idols) (b:kipia) (r:46.4.7/3.10.17/46.6.11/44.15.29) (q:draft)
kipiasak = (t:v) (w:make give/impose/let give) (d:have something given: of tribute, impose it on a land; with lo, not be allowed to give) (e:kham talen khat siah ~ hi/biakna hong ~ lo ahi hiam | why are we kept from presenting the offering) (b:kipia) (r:12.23.33/4.9.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
kipiasawn = (t:v) (w:be handed on/be passed on) (d:passive of piasawn, pass on; of the law, given on through a go-between) (e:Moses tungah hong ~ hi) (b:piasawn) (r:48.3.19) (q:draft)
kipiatawm = (t:v) (w:give oneself/give oneself up/sell oneself) (d:hand oneself over for a purpose or for others; also bring a thing on oneself) (e:tua Jesuh hong ~ a/nangmah ~ na hih manin | because you have sold yourself/Jesuh Khrih amahmah a hong ~ ahi hi | Jesus Christ gave himself for us/amahmah mawhsak thukhenna a ~ ahi hi | he brings judgment on himself) (s:kipumpiak) (r:54.2.6/11.21.25/11.21.20/48.1.4/46.11.29) (q:draft)
kipiate = (t:n) (w:those given/things given) (d:people or things that are given, handed over or allotted to someone) (e:ama tungah a ~ ahi hi/Merari beh tuamtuamte’ ading khuapi a ~ | the towns allotted to the Merarite clans/biakna ~ a ne uh hi | they ate the sacrifices that were offered) (b:kipia) (r:4.3.9/6.21.40/19.106.28) (q:draft)
kipiathuah = (t:v) (w:be given more/be added/be given in addition) (d:passive of piathuah give in addition, with the prefix ki) (e:a neisate ~ ding a/a neisate tungah ~ ding a | more will be given to those who have/thuciamna banah hong ~ hi a | it was added to the promise) (s:kibehlap) (b:piathuah) (r:40.25.29/48.3.19/42.19.26) (q:draft)
kipiazah = (t:n) (w:amount given/number given) (d:kipia, be given, with zah, amount: as many as are given or offered) (e:tuutal a ~ tawh kizui-in) (r:26.45.24) (q:draft)
kipiazaw = (t:v) (w:be given rather/be given more) (d:passive of piazaw give rather or more, with the prefix ki; kipiazaw kan ding is will be given all the more) (e:mizawngte tungah ~ lo ahi hiam/gimna ~ kan ding hi | punishment will be given all the more) (b:piazaw) (r:43.12.5/20.11.31) (q:draft)
kipiazo = (t:v) (w:have been given/be given) (d:kipia, be given, with zo marking the action as completed) (e:Media le Persia-te a ~ hi) (b:kipia) (r:27.5.28) (q:draft)
kipilsak = (t:v) (w:be conceited/think oneself wise) (d:pil, wise, with ki and sak: make oneself out to be wise, be wise in one's own eyes) (e:~ se kei un/Hih mi ~ thu mawk gengen pa in | this man who thinks himself wise and babbles) (s:kiphasak) (a:kiniamsak) (b:pilsak) (r:45.12.16/44.17.18) (q:draft)
kipin = (t:adv) (w:firmly/steadfastly) (d:kip with the ending -in: standing firm, being established, before the next verb) (e:upna tawh ~ Dawimangpa na nial un/Topa sungah ~ om un | stand firm in the Lord/amah innkuan ~ ka bawl ding a | I will firmly establish his house/Rehoboam’ ukna ~ a thahat ciangin | when Rehoboam's rule was established and strong) (s:kiptakin) (b:kip) (r:60.5.9/14.12.1/50.4.1/9.2.35) (q:draft)
kipina = (t:n) (w:marrying/marriage) (d:kipi, marry, with the noun suffix na; paired with kiteen'na for marrying and being given in marriage) (e:Thawhkik ni ciangin ~) (b:kipi) (r:40.22.30) (q:draft)
kipkhin = (t:v) (w:stand firm/be firmly established) (d:kip, be firm, with khin, already done) (e:na upna uhah ~ na hih manun) (b:kip) (r:47.1.24) (q:draft)
kipna = (t:n) (w:firmness/steadfastness/stability) (d:being firm and lasting; lung kipna or lungsim kipna is firmness of heart; also what builds a person up) (e:Lung ~ tawh nuntakna na ngah ding/lungsim ~ siklum bangin eite ading a om hi | it is for us like an anchor that keeps the soul firm/midang ading ~ a piang kei hi | the other person is not built up/pawlpite in lungkimin ~ a ngah uh hi | the churches had peace and were strengthened) (s:lungkipna) (b:kip) (r:42.21.19/58.6.19/46.14.17/44.9.31) (q:draft)
kipoisak = (t:v) (w:be injured/be hurt) (d:passive of poisak injure) (e:a poisak bangin amah ~ ding hi) (b:poisak) (r:3.24.20) (q:draft)
kipsa = (t:adj) (w:established/made firm) (d:kip be established with sa, already: standing firm from before) (e:na tokhom a ~ hi a) (s:kipsaksa) (b:kip) (r:19.93.2) (q:draft)
kipsak = (t:v) (w:establish/make firm/confirm) (d:kip, be firm, with the causative sak: make firm, set up to last) (e:nang tawh ka thuciamna ka ~ ding hi/nangmah in leitung na ~ a | you established the earth/Thuman-a gamtatna bek in kumpi ~ ahih manin | because only right conduct establishes a king/gunte tungah ~ hi | he established it on the rivers) (s:phut) (a:susia) (b:kip) (r:1.6.18/24.33.2/19.119.90/20.16.12/19.24.2)
kipsakin = (t:v) (w:establish/strengthen/confirm) (d:kipsak with the linking ending in: making firm, establishing and) (e:Amaute in pawlpi omsate ~ Siria gam/amah in vantungah meiite ~ | when he established the clouds above/note hong ~ thu hoih lote tawh hong kipelhsak ding | he will strengthen you and keep you from evil/nasem dingin ~, na siangthosak ding hi | ordain them to serve and consecrate them) (b:kipsak) (r:44.15.41/20.8.28/53.3.3/2.28.41) (q:draft)
kipsakna = (t:n) (w:strengthening/establishing/confirmation) (d:the act of making someone or something firm) (e:~ thu, hansuahna thu, nopsakna thute/a puk mite na thugenna tawh na ~ | your words supported those who stumbled) (s:thahatsakna) (b:kipsak) (r:46.14.3/18.4.4) (q:draft)
kipsakna = (t:n) (w:ordination/consecration) (d:the setting apart of priests for their office, as in kipsakna tuutal, the ram of ordination) (e:Nangmah in ~ tuutal la-in/a tuutal dang, ~ tuutal pia hi | he presented the other ram, the ram of ordination/~ tuutal panin Moses tanh ahi hi | it was Moses' share of the ordination ram) (b:kipsak) (r:2.29.31/3.8.22/3.8.29) (q:draft)
kipsaknate = (t:n) (w:supports/stays) (d:kipsakna with plural te: the parts that hold something firm, as the supports of a stand) (e:a ~ leh a khawkte tungah/a din’na dawnah a ~ leh a khawkte | the supports and panels at the top of the stand) (b:kipsakna) (r:11.7.36/11.7.35) (q:draft)
kipsakpa = (t:n) (w:establisher/one who makes firm) (d:kipsak establish, with pa for a male person: he who sets a thing firm, said of God) (e:khuampite a ~ in keimah ka hi hi) (b:kipsak) (r:19.75.3/23.45.18) (q:draft)
kipsaksa = (t:adj) (w:established/appointed) (d:kipsak with sa, already done: that has been established) (e:ka ~ thuciamna lim ahi hi/amaute-a’ dingin a ~ ngeina bangin | according to the regulations established for them/Judah kumpite in a ~ milim biate’ siampite | the idol priests appointed by the kings of Judah) (s:kipsa) (b:kipsak) (r:1.9.17/13.24.19/12.23.5) (q:draft)
kipsaksuak = (t:v) (w:establish for ever/establish permanently) (d:kipsak, establish, with suak, right on without end) (e:na suanlekhakte a ~ ding ahi hi) (r:9.13.13) (q:draft)
kipsuak = (t:v) (w:endure/remain/last forever) (d:stay firm and continue without end) (e:Khapi bangin tua pen ~ ding a/Ama hauhna-ah mi ~ thei lo a | man in his wealth cannot endure/tuni dongin tua min ~ hi | that name has remained to this day/tua hi leh na ~ ding hi | then you will remain forever) (s:omsuak) (a:beimang) (r:19.89.37/19.49.12/12.14.7/19.37.27) (q:draft)
kiptak = (t:adj) (w:firm/secure/steadfast) (d:kip, firm, with tak, truly: really firm, genuine; also used as an adverb, firmly) (e:~ khotakin i letkip ding kisam hi/note’ upna zong a ~ mah ahi hiam | whether your faith too is truly firm/thuman tak, ~, thutang takin | in a truthful, firm and just way) (b:kip) (r:58.2.1/60.1.7/24.4.2) (q:draft)
kiptaka = (t:adv) (w:securely/firmly/at rest) (d:kiptak, firm or secure, with the ending a) (e:~ na om nading uh gam) (s:kiptakin) (b:kiptak) (r:5.28.65) (q:draft)
kiptakin = (t:adv) (w:firmly/steadfastly) (d:kip with takin, which makes an adverb: in a firm, unshaken way) (e:Topa’ thu-ah ~ om na hih manun/~ a nial ding uh hi | they will firmly resist/ama kumpi gam ~ kiphut hi | his kingdom was firmly established/i neih lungmuanna ~ i let ciat nakleh | if we each hold firmly the confidence we have) (s:kipin) (b:kip) (r:52.3.8/27.11.32/11.2.12/58.3.14) (q:draft)
kipte = (t:adj) (w:firm/established/fixed) (d:plural of kip; ngeina kipte, the established customs, renders decrees, statutes and laws) (e:Nangmah ngeina ~ zuihna-ah/na ngeina ~ kei hong hilh in | teach me your decrees/vantung leh leitung ngeina ~ | the fixed laws of heaven and earth) (b:kip) (r:19.119.5/19.119.138/19.119.12/24.33.25) (q:draft)
kipte = (t:n) (w:those who stand firm) (e:A bei dongin a ~ in) (b:kip) (r:40.24.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiptheih = (t:v) (w:be able to remain/be maintained) (d:kip, be established, with theih, the form of thei, be able, used before nading) (e:beh sungah a ~ nadingin) (b:kip) (r:8.4.5) (q:draft)
kipua = (t:v) (w:be carried/be borne) (d:passive of pua carry; kipua khia is to be carried away) (e:hihte tawh sabuai ~ ding hi/Kumpinu kimanin ~ khia a | the queen is seized and carried away/a neihsa khempeuh uh ~ khia-in | all their wealth is carried away/Naupangte nangawn sila dingin a ~ khia hi | even the children are carried off as slaves) (b:pua) (r:2.25.28/34.2.7/26.30.4/25.1.5) (q:draft)
kipuah = (t:v) (w:be polished/be put in order/be made ready) (d:passive of puah: be repaired, tidied or prepared for use) (e:Tua namsau limtakin ~ a/kitat hiamin ~ siang hi | it is sharpened and polished clean/tua inn awngin, kiphiat ~ a | that house empty, swept and put in order/khuaphia bangin a tee zialzial dingin ~ hi | it is polished to flash like lightning) (s:kipuahsiang) (b:puah) (r:26.21.11/42.11.25/40.12.44/26.21.10) (q:draft)
kipuahin = (t:v) (w:adorning oneself/beautifying oneself) (d:kipuah put in order, here of women making themselves beautiful, with the linking ending in) (e:kha guk sung ~/a kilawm a kituak bekin kizemin ~ | dressing and adorning themselves only in a fitting way) (b:kipuah) (r:17.2.12/54.2.9) (q:draft)
kipuahkik = (t:v) (w:be restored/be repaired again) (d:passive of puahkik renovate; of the sanctuary, where the NIV has be reconsecrated) (e:biakinnpi ~ ding hi) (b:puahkik) (r:27.8.14) (q:draft)
kipuahna = (t:n) (w:cosmetics/beauty treatment/adornment) (d:kipuah, make oneself ready, with the noun suffix na: something used to prepare and beautify the body, such as cosmetics) (e:paknamtui tuamtuamte le ~ dangte tawh) (s:kizepna) (b:kipuah) (r:17.2.12) (q:draft)
kipuahpha = (t:v) (w:reform/mend one's ways/put right) (d:puahpha, repair well, with ki, oneself: put one's own conduct right, mend one's ways) (e:na gamtat hoih lote uh ~ un/Na omzia uh na ~-in | put your ways right) (s:kibawlpha) (b:puahpha) (r:24.35.15/47.13.11) (q:draft)
kipuahphasak = (t:v) (w:let oneself be transformed/be made new) (d:kipuahpha, put oneself right, with the causative sak: let another, here God, put one right) (e:na lungsim uh kikheelin Pasian ~ un) (b:kipuahpha) (r:45.12.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
kipuahphat = (t:v) (w:make amends for/make good/pay for) (d:form of kipuahpha, put oneself right, used before leh and ding; with mawhna sin, make amends for it) (e:a mawhna a ~ uh leh/a mawhna uh a ~ ding uh kisam hi | they must make amends for their sin) (b:kipuahpha) (r:3.26.41/3.26.43) (q:draft, low confidence)
kipuahsiang = (t:v) (w:be polished/be made clean) (d:passive of puahsiang; said of a sword made ready for use) (e:kitat hiamin ~ hi) (s:kipuah) (b:puahsiang) (r:26.21.11) (q:draft)
kipuak = (t:v) (w:be carried/be borne) (d:passive of puak, carry: be carried from one place to another) (e:a ~ ciangin biakna tau pang nihte-ah/Babilon ah a ~ ni ding hong tung ding | the day will come when it is carried to Babylon/Jerusalem biakinn ah ~ kik ding a | they shall be carried back to the temple in Jerusalem) (s:kipua) (b:puak) (r:2.27.7/12.20.17/15.6.5) (q:draft)
kipuak = (t:v) (w:be sent/be brought/be delivered) (d:passive of puak, send or deliver: of a gift, a message or goods, be sent or brought to someone) (e:Gentailte kiangah ~ ding a/letsong a hong ~ ahi hi | it is a gift that has been sent/letsong hong ~ ding hi | gifts will be brought/nangma kiangah hong ~ ding a | they will be brought to you) (s:kisawl/kipaipih) (b:puak) (r:44.28.28/12.17.33/1.32.18/23.18.7/23.60.7) (q:draft)
kipuakhia = (t:v) (w:be carried away/be taken out/be carried off) (d:passive of puakhia, carry out: be carried or taken out of a place, often of people and goods taken away to another land) (e:Tuate Babilon khua-ah ~ ding a/giahphual pua lamah ~ ding hi | it shall be taken outside the camp/Kumpinu kimanin ~ a | the queen is seized and carried away/tua milim ~ ding hi | that idol will be carried away) (s:kipuakkhia/kipaikhiatpih) (a:kipuakik) (b:puakhia) (r:24.27.22/3.16.27/34.2.7/28.10.6) (q:draft)
kipuakik = (t:v) (w:be carried back/be brought back) (d:passive of puakik, carry back) (e:Jerusalem biakinn-ah ~ ding a) (s:kitutkik) (a:kipuakhia) (b:puakik) (r:15.6.5) (q:draft)
kipuakin = (t:v) (w:being sent/sent) (d:kipuak be sent, with the linking ending in) (e:dal khat ciat ~ tua thu pen) (b:kipuak) (r:17.3.14) (q:draft)
kipuakkhia = (t:v) (w:be carried away/be deported/be sent into exile) (d:passive of puakkhia carry away) (e:hong ~ sal tang mi khempeuhte’ tungah) (s:kipuakhia) (a:kipuakik) (b:puakkhia) (r:24.29.4) (q:draft)
kipuakkhiat = (t:v) (w:be carried away/be taken away/be deported) (d:form of kipuakkhia used before endings such as dong and nawn) (e:sal tang dingin a ~ dong/Babylon khua-ah a ~ nawn lohna dingin | so that they are no longer carried off to Babylon) (b:kipuakkhia) (r:24.1.3/24.27.18) (q:draft)
kipuakna = (t:n) (w:being carried off/deportation) (d:kipuak be carried or sent, with the noun suffix na; a kipuakna gam, the land to which people were carried away as captives) (e:galmatin a ~ gamah amaute in) (s:puakkhiatna) (b:kipuak) (r:14.6.37) (q:draft)
kipuasak = (t:v) (w:be made to carry/be loaded) (d:passive of puasak make carry) (e:sing kitomsakin a lelhpipi-un a ~ hi) (b:puasak) (r:25.5.13) (q:draft)
kipuaseh = (t:v) (w:be cut off/be excluded/be banned) (d:be put outside and shut out from a place or a people; in the Psalms of the wicked being cut off) (e:cih leh migilote ~ ding a/ama samsiatte ~ ding hi | those he curses will be cut off/migilo’ tate ~ ding hi | the children of the wicked will be cut off/biakinn panin amah ~ hi | he was shut out from the temple) (s:kihawlkhia/kikhenkhia) (r:19.37.9/14.26.21/19.37.22/19.37.28) (q:draft)
kipuasehin = (t:v) (w:being cut off/being shut out/banished) (d:kipuaseh be shut out, with the linking ending in; a kipuasehin koih, leave someone in banishment) (e:a hawlkhiatpa a ~ a koih loh nadingin) (b:kipuaseh) (r:10.14.14) (q:draft)
kipuk = (t:v) (w:fall/stumble/fall away) (d:fall or stumble; also fall away from faith or come to ruin; built on puk, fall) (e:awk-in lei lakah ka ~ hi/Note na ~ loh nadingun | so that you will not fall away/a ~ thei kei ding hi | he will not stumble/lamlak ding a nei lo mihingte ~ uh | a people without guidance falls/kuamah ~ loin tua nopsakna sunga tum nadingin | so that no one falls but enters that rest) (s:kia/tuk) (a:tho) (b:puk) (r:25.1.13/43.16.1/43.11.9/20.11.14/58.4.11) (q:draft)
kipukin = (t:v) (w:falling/stumbling) (d:kipuk fall, stumble, with the linking ending in) (e:Jerusalem khua ~ Judah gam kia hi/mipawl khempeuh ~ a kisia uh hi | all the nations have fallen and are ruined) (b:kipuk) (r:23.3.8/66.18.3) (q:draft)
kipukna = (t:n) (w:stumbling block/cause of stumbling) (d:kipuk stumble with the noun suffix na: a thing that makes people fall) (e:Judah mite ading ~ ahi hi/~ ahi zongin, daantatna ahi zongin | whether a stumbling block or a retribution) (s:puktheihna) (b:kipuk) (r:46.1.23/45.11.9) (q:draft)
kipuksa = (t:adj) (w:fallen) (d:kipuk, fall, with the completive suffix sa) (e:A ~ David’ buk ka lamkik ding hi) (s:cimsa/kicimsa) (b:kipuk) (r:44.15.16) (q:draft)
kipuksak = (t:v) (w:be thrown down/be dashed to the ground) (d:passive of puksak, cause to fall; used with leitungah, to the ground) (e:na tate leitungah a ~ ding ni) (b:puksak) (r:42.19.44) (q:draft)
kipuksuk = (t:v) (w:fall on/throw oneself down) (d:puksuk fall down with ki oneself; with sak, let oneself fall on something) (e:a namsau tungah ~ sakin a si hi/~ sakin amah tawh a sikhawm hi | he fell on it and died with him) (b:puksuk) (r:13.10.5/9.31.5) (q:draft)
kipulaakin = (t:v) (w:confess to each other) (d:ki, each other, with pulaak, confess, and the linking ending in; kipulakin in the other Bible text) (e:khat leh khat na mawhna uh ~) (s:kipulakin) (r:59.5.16) (q:draft)
kipulak = (t:v) (w:be proclaimed/be made known/be confessed/make oneself known) (d:passive or reflexive of pulak, declare: be proclaimed or confessed openly; of a person, make oneself known) (e:keima min a ~ theih nadingin/Gupna ngah nadingin kam tawh ~ hi | one confesses with the mouth to be saved/amah a ~ ciangin kuamah dang om lo | no one else was there when he made himself known/a sanggamte tungah i pupi Josef na ~ a | our ancestor Joseph made himself known to his brothers) (s:kitaangko/kitangko) (b:pulak) (r:2.9.16/45.10.10/1.45.1/44.7.13) (q:draft)
kipulakin = (t:v) (w:confess to each other) (d:ki, each other, with pulak, confess, and the linking ending in) (e:khatlekhat tungah na mawhna uh ~ thu) (s:kipulaakin) (b:kipulak) (r:59.5.16) (q:draft)
kipum = (t:v) (w:be united/be one whole) (d:in kipum khat, being as one, in unity) (e:Tapa theihna ah ahi zongin, ~ khatin) (s:kikhat) (r:49.4.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
kipumpei = (t:v) (w:reel/shake/tremble) (d:of the earth, shake and rock; perhaps pum whole with pei turn) (e:Ama hehna hangin leitung ~ in) (s:kiliing/kiling) (r:19.18.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
kipumpiak = (t:v) (w:give oneself/give oneself wholly) (d:give one's whole self for others) (e:Jesuh amahmah hong ~ a) (s:kipiatawm/kibuppiak) (r:56.2.14) (q:draft)
kipumsil = (t:v) (w:bathe/wash the whole body) (d:pum, the whole body, with sil, wash, and ki, oneself: wash one's whole body, bathe) (e:puante sawpin tui sungah ~ ding a/A ~ khinsa mite siangthota ahih manin | because those who have bathed are already clean) (s:kisil) (r:4.19.8/4.19.7/43.13.10) (q:draft)
kipung = (t:v) (w:increase/multiply/be fruitful) (d:pung increase with ki; kipung thei lo, nothing can thrive or bear young, said of a barren land) (e:hih gamah ~ thei lo hi) (b:pung) (r:12.2.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
kipusuahpih = (t:v) (w:be taken outside/be put out) (d:passive of pusuahpih, bring out) (e:sawltakte a ~ nadingin thu pia a) (b:pusuahpih) (r:44.5.34) (q:draft)
kipusuak = (t:v) (w:come out/come forth) (d:pusuak, come out, with the prefix ki; followed by sak, cause to come forth, rouse) (e:misi uliante ~ sak hi) (b:pusuak) (r:23.14.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
kipusuaksak = (t:v) (w:be brought out/be roused) (d:kipusuak, come forth, with the causative sak: be made to come forth; said of the dead being roused) (e:misi uliante ~ hi) (s:kithawhthawi) (b:kipusuak) (r:23.14.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
kipzaw = (t:adj) (w:more lasting/firmer/more steadfast) (d:kip firm, lasting, with zaw more; of a friend, closer) (e:sanggam sangin ~ hi/a hoihzaw, a ~ nate a nei | having better and more lasting things) (b:kip) (r:20.18.24/58.10.34) (q:draft)
kipzo = (t:v) (w:be able to stand/stand firm/endure) (d:kip stand firm with zo be able; kipzo lo, cannot stand) (e:tua innkuan ~ lo ding hi/kido le-uh ~ lo ding uh a | if they fight each other they cannot stand) (b:kip) (r:41.3.25/41.3.26) (q:draft)
