Kiriathjearim = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Kiriath-jearim/Kiriath Jearim) (d:town on the border of Judah and Benjamin, also called Kiriath Baal, where the ark of the covenant stayed for twenty years) (r:6.15.60/6.18.15)
Kiriathsannah = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Kiriath-sannah/Kiriath Sannah) (d:another name of Debir, a town in the hill country of Judah) (r:6.15.49)
Kiriathsefer = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Kiriath Sepher) (d:earlier name of Debir, a town in the hill country of Judah captured by Othniel) (r:7.1.11/6.15.16)
kisa = (t:v) (w:consider oneself/think oneself) (d:placed after a describing word, as in pil kisa, think oneself wise, and thuman kisa, think oneself right) (e:amau mah thuman ~ tawntung a/ngah dingin kilawm ~ lo na hih uh ciangin | since you do not consider yourselves worthy to receive it/pasian zahin a pil ~ na hih manin | because you think yourself as wise as a god/Mihaite a pil ~ kha ding uh ahih manin | because fools may think themselves wise/pilna a nei na ~ mah uh hi | you surely think you have wisdom) (s:kingaihsun/kinei) (r:20.12.15/18.12.2/44.13.46/26.28.6/20.26.5) (q:draft)
kisa = (t:v) (w:be sung) (d:of a song, as in la kisa) (e:lungdamna la ~ ding a/Judah gam sungah hih la ~ ding hi | this song will be sung in the land of Judah/gualzawh lungdamna la ~ a | songs of victory and joy are sung/nangmah phatna la ~ hi | songs of praise to you are sung) (r:24.30.19/23.26.1/19.118.15/19.8.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisaal = (t:v) (w:be pressed out/be cleansed) (d:said of a wound, with nai, pus: have the pus pressed out; written kisal in the other Bible text) (e:tuate pen a nai ~ lo) (s:kisal) (r:23.1.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisaan = (t:v) (w:be cast) (d:passive of saan, cast; used with ai, lot) (e:Haman’ muhin ai ~ a) (b:saan) (r:17.3.7) (q:draft)
kisai = (t:v) (w:concern/relate to/be about) (d:be connected with; the phrase tawh kisai or tawh kisai-in means concerning, about) (e:Hih thu tawh ~-in siampite’ ngaihsutna dong in/Gamdangte’ thu tawh ~-in Topa in Jeremiah hopih hi | the Lord spoke to Jeremiah concerning the nations/Jerusalem khua tawh ~ Amoz’ tapa Isaiah muhna thu | what Isaiah son of Amoz saw concerning Jerusalem/zi tawh ~ thu a dot uh ciangin | when they asked about his wife) (r:37.2.11/24.46.1/23.2.1/1.26.7) (q:draft)
kisaite = (t:n) (w:matters concerning/things relating to) (d:kisai, concern, with plural te; tawh kisaite, the things that concern or have to do with) (e:ka bawlsate tawh ~-ah thu hong pia ding/kamciamna tawh ~ ahi zongin kip lo ding hi | the things concerning her pledge shall not stand either) (b:kisai) (r:23.45.11/4.30.12) (q:draft)
kisaizaw = (t:v) (w:depend rather on/relate rather to) (d:kisai concern with zaw more, rather: tawh kisaizaw, has to do with this and not with that) (e:Pasian’ hehpihna bek tawh ~ hi/Pasian’ sapna tawh ~ hi | it depends rather on the call of God) (b:kisai) (r:45.9.16/45.9.11) (q:draft)
kisak = (t:v) (w:be about to/intend/get ready) (d:after a verb with ding: be on the point of doing something, mean or prepare to do it; kisak lai takin is just as one was about to) (e:kam pau ding a ~ lai takin/kikhopna sungah lut ding a ~ ciangin | when he was about to go into the assembly/Tua nu in paipih dingin a ~ lai takin | just as she was going to bring it/Paul that ding a ~ lai takun | just as they were about to kill Paul/thuum dinga na ~ lai takin | just as you began to pray) (s:kithawi) (r:44.18.14/66.10.4/44.19.30/11.17.11/44.21.31/27.9.23) (q:draft)
kisak = (t:v) (w:consider oneself/think oneself/claim) (d:form of kisa used before words such as hangin and ciangin; thei a kisak is to think that one knows; kisak theihna is pride and kisak theihpih is to boast of or take pride in something) (e:Mipilte in thei a ~ hangun/pasian bangin pil na ~ hangin | though you think yourself as wise as a god/zumhuaina thuak dinga kilawm a ~ manun | because they counted themselves worthy to suffer disgrace) (s:kingaihsun/kinei) (b:kisa) (r:21.8.17/23.60.15/26.28.2/44.5.41) (q:draft)
kisak = (t:v) (w:be sung) (d:said of a song, la) (e:Topa phatna-in la a ~ ciangin) (b:kisa) (r:14.5.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisakna = (t:n) (w:claim/conviction/considering oneself) (d:kisak consider oneself, with the noun suffix na: what one holds oneself or a thing to be; thuman kisakna is the claim to be in the right) (e:thuman ka ~ ka khia ngei kei ding/man a ~ bangun gamta lo uh ahih manin | because they do not act as they hold to be right) (b:kisak) (r:18.27.6/54.1.19) (q:draft)
kisaktheih = (t:v) (w:boast/be proud/take pride) (d:think highly of oneself; form used before endings such as loh and nading) (e:Kuamah in a ~ loh nadingin/~ na’ng thu a om hi | he has something to boast about/ka ~ hangin zumna ka thuak kei ding hi | though I boast I will not be ashamed/kei zong a neukha ka ~ na’ngin | so that I too may boast a little) (s:kiphasak/kisathei/kihisak/kiliansak) (a:kiniamkhiat) (r:49.2.9/45.4.2/47.10.8/47.11.16) (q:draft)
kisaktheihna = (t:n) (w:pride/boasting/conceit) (d:thinking too highly of oneself and showing it) (e:~ in siatna hong tuak sak a/Na ~ uh a hoih kei hi | your boasting is not good/Judah mite’ ~ leh Jerusalem khua mite’ ki-uatsaknate | the pride of Judah and the great pride of Jerusalem/~ lungsim ka neih loh nadingin | so that I would not become conceited) (s:kiphatsakna/kihihsakna/kiliatsakna/kisialhna) (a:kiniamkhiatna) (b:kisaktheih) (r:20.16.18/46.5.6/24.13.9/47.12.7) (q:draft)
kisaktheihpih = (t:v) (w:boast of/be proud of/take pride in) (d:be proud on account of something, such as wealth or strength) (e:na hauhna na ~ hi/tampi a neihna uh a ~ hangun | though they boast of their great riches/bang hangin na hatna ~ na hi hiam | why do you boast of your strength/Na mel hoihna na ~ kha a | you became proud of your beauty) (s:kisialhpih/kiphatsakpih/kihihsakpih/angtanpih) (b:kisaktheih) (r:26.28.5/19.49.6/24.49.4/26.28.17) (q:draft)
kisaktheihpihin = (t:v) (w:boast of/be proud of) (d:kisaktheihpih, take pride in, with the linking ending in) (e:mi khatpeuh ~ mi khatpeuh na simmawhbawl) (b:kisaktheihpih) (r:46.4.6) (q:draft)
kisaktheihpihna = (t:n) (w:pride/boast/thing boasted of) (d:kisaktheihpih take pride in, with the noun suffix na: what one is proud of) (e:a ~ teng uh bei ding hi) (b:kisaktheihpih) (r:26.30.18) (q:draft)
kisal = (t:v) (w:be pressed out/be cleansed) (d:said of a wound, with nai, pus: have the pus pressed out; written kisaal in the other Bible text) (e:Tuate pen a nai ~ lo) (s:kisaal) (r:23.1.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisam = (t:v) (w:need/lack/be necessary/be needed) (d:be without something that is wanted or required: of a person, need or lack; of a thing, be needed or missing; ding kisam is it is necessary to) (e:bangmah ka ~ kei ding hi/mul eng a zon’ ding ~ lo hi | he does not need to look for yellow hair/a neu kha beek ~ loin | not lacking even a little/biakinn sunga nasep a ~ dangte | the other work that is needed in the temple/tung pan na khat ka ~ hi | I require one thing of you) (s:kul/kiphamawh/tasam) (r:19.23.1/15.6.9/3.13.36/59.1.4/26.44.14/10.3.13) (q:draft)
kisam = (t:v) (w:be invited/be called/be summoned) (d:passive of sam, call) (e:A ~ mite a tam hangin/A ~ mi zanihte Jerusalem panin Absalom tawh pai | two hundred invited men went with Absalom from Jerusalem/khit ciangin a ~ mite in ne uh hi | afterwards those who are invited eat/~ mite lak tutna bul-ah mun khat pia hi | he gave him a place at the head of those invited) (s:kilo) (b:sam) (r:40.22.14/10.15.11/9.9.13/9.9.22) (q:draft)
kisamin = (t:v) (w:call to each other/be called) (d:kisam, call or be called, with the linking ending in; khat leh khat kisamin is calling to one another) (e:Amaute khat leh khat ~/Kiteelkhia, ~, thuman mi ahi | chosen, called and faithful) (b:kisam) (r:23.6.3/66.17.14) (q:draft)
kisamkhia = (t:v) (w:be summoned/be called out/be called up) (d:be called to come out and gather, as men for war) (e:a zui dingin Abiezer mite ~ hi/Gilgal-ah Saul a pawm dingin mite ~ hi | the people were summoned to join Saul at Gilgal/galhiam a tawi thei khempeuh ~ uh a | all who could bear arms were called up/Efraim mite khempeuh ~ a | all the men of Ephraim were called out) (b:kisam) (r:7.6.34/9.13.4/12.3.21/7.7.24) (q:draft)
kisamkik = (t:v) (w:be called back/be summoned again) (d:passive of samkik call back) (e:a deih leh a minin ~ hi/a dah mahmah zi a ~ bangin | like a deeply grieved wife who is called back) (b:samkik) (r:17.2.14/23.54.6) (q:draft)
kisamsak = (t:v) (w:let be lacking/leave wanting/lose) (d:kisam, lack, with causative sak; found with lo or kei: let nothing be lacking, lose none) (e:amaute in bangmah ~ lo uh hi/khat zong ka ~ kei hi | I have not lost even one/na hong piaksate khat zong ka ~ kei hi | I have not lost one of those you gave me) (b:kisam) (r:11.4.27/43.17.12/43.18.9) (q:draft)
kisamsia = (t:v) (w:be cursed) (d:passive of samsia, curse) (e:gam lakah zong hong ~ ding hi/Tu-in note hong ~ a | now you are under a curse/a zuak nuam lote ~ a | those unwilling to sell are cursed/Tu-in a ~ hih numei mu un la | now see to this cursed woman) (b:samsia) (r:5.28.16/6.9.23/20.11.26/12.9.34) (q:draft)
kisamsiat = (t:v) (w:curse/be cursed/be accursed) (d:form of kisamsia, be cursed, used before hi and ciangin; hong kisamsiat is you are cursed or we are cursed) (e:tu-in nang hong ~ hi/Hong ~ ciangin thupha ka lehpiak uh a | when we are cursed we bless in return/a ~, a kiphasakte na thuhilh hi | you rebuke the accursed and the arrogant) (b:samsiat) (r:1.4.11/19.119.21/46.4.12)
kisamsiatna = (t:n) (w:curse/cursing) (d:kisamsiat curse with the noun suffix na: a curse spoken against someone) (e:Thu om lopi-in hong ~ in) (s:samsiatna/hamsiatna) (b:kisamsiat) (r:20.26.2) (q:draft)
kisamte = (t:n) (w:guests/those invited/those called) (d:kisam be invited, be called, with the plural te) (e:A ~ in tokhom sangbel a teel uh/a ~ adingin Pasian’ vangliatna leh Pasian’ pilna ahi | to those who are called it is the power of God and the wisdom of God/Tua pawi siim dingin a ~ lakah | among those invited to that feast) (s:leenglate/zinte) (b:kisam) (r:42.14.7/46.1.24/42.14.8) (q:draft)
kisamzah = (t:n) (w:amount needed/as much as is needed) (d:kisam, be needed, with zah, amount) (e:an le sathaute, nisimin a ~) (r:26.45.25) (q:draft)
kisamzaw = (t:v) (w:be more necessary) (d:kisam, be necessary, with zaw, more) (e:nate in a ~ ahi hi) (s:kulzaw) (b:kisam) (r:46.12.22) (q:draft)
kisan = (t:v) (w:be accepted/be received) (d:written kisan’ before theih, leh and similar words; of an offering or a person, be accepted) (e:note hong ~’ theih nadingin na pia ding/hehpihna phatin a ~’ leh | if it is received with thanksgiving/~’ theih nadingin kikhopna buk kong-ah pia ding hi | he shall offer it at the entrance to the tent of meeting so that it may be accepted) (a:kinolh) (r:3.19.5/54.4.4/3.1.3) (q:draft)
kisanek = (t:v) (w:eat one another's flesh/devour one another) (d:sa flesh and nek eat, with the reciprocal prefix ki) (e:khat leh khat ~ un) (s:kinek) (r:38.11.9) (q:draft)
kisang = (t:v) (w:accept/be accepted/be acceptable) (d:of an offering or a person, be accepted; kisang lo is not accepted and kisang thei is acceptable) (e:hong ~ zo lo ding hi/a kihhuai ahi hi; ~ lo ding hi | it is detestable; it will not be accepted/kilemna bawl nadingin ~ ding hi | it will be accepted to make atonement/thuciamna biak nadingin ~ zo lo hi | it cannot be accepted for a vow/nang hong ~ lo ding ahi hiam | will you not be accepted) (a:kinolh) (r:3.22.20/1.4.7/3.19.7/3.1.4/3.22.23)
kisangsak = (t:v) (w:be exalted/be lifted up/be made high) (d:sangsak, make high, with the prefix ki: be lifted high or exalted, said of God, of a mountain and of the proud) (e:mual neute tungah ~ ding hi/Minamte lakah keimah hong ~ a | I am exalted among the nations/a ~ leh a sangte khempeuh niamkhiat suk ding | all that is exalted and high will be brought low/nang a lutangin hong ~ hi | you are exalted as head) (s:kipahtawi/kilamsang) (a:kiniamkhiat/kiniam) (r:23.2.2/19.46.10/23.2.12/13.29.11) (q:draft)
kisangsakte = (t:n) (w:the lofty/the tall ones/those lifted up) (d:kisangsak with plural te: those that are made high or make themselves high) (e:a ~ a niam-in kikoih ding hi) (b:kisangsak) (r:23.10.33) (q:draft)
kisangtawi = (t:v) (w:be exalted/be highly regarded/be honoured) (d:sang high and tawi hold up, with the prefix ki: be held in high regard) (e:minam khempeuh muhna ah amah ~ hi) (s:kipahtawi/kizahtak) (a:kisimmawh) (r:14.32.23) (q:draft)
kisangthei = (t:v) (w:be acceptable/can be accepted) (d:kisang, be accepted, with thei, be able; said of an offering) (e:a ~ ding biakpiakna hong pia uh hi) (b:kisang) (r:39.1.11) (q:draft)
kisangtosak = (t:v) (w:be raised up/be lifted up) (d:passive of sangtosak, raise up; said of valleys) (e:Kuamthuk khempeuh ~ ding a) (a:kiniamsak) (b:sangtosak) (r:23.40.4) (q:draft)
kisanna = (t:n) (w:casting) (d:with ai, the casting of lots or taking of omens, divination; from kisaan, be cast, with the noun suffix na) (e:hih bangin ai a ~ pen) (s:saanna) (r:26.21.23) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisansak = (t:v) (w:be dyed red/be made red) (d:passive of sansak, make red; a kisansak tuutal vunte, ram skins dyed red) (e:a ~ tuutal vunte, keel vunte/~ tuutal vunte leh keel vunte tawh puanbuk khuhna | a tent covering of ram skins dyed red and of goat skins/~ tuutal vunte leh savunte tawh a kibawl khuhna | the covering made of ram skins dyed red and of hides) (b:sansak) (r:2.25.5/2.26.14/2.39.34) (q:draft)
kisap = (t:v) (w:need/be needed/lack) (d:form of kisam, need, used before nouns and words such as zah and hun: what someone needs or lacks, or the time when a thing is needed) (e:ama ~ zah na leitawi ding uh hi/na ~ sing peuhmah Lebanon panin kong phuk ding | we will cut from Lebanon all the logs you need/A ~ hun hunin thupha guahtui ka zusak ding | I will send showers of blessing whenever they are needed/na hoih a ~ uh om lo hi | they lack no good thing/a ~ khempeuh kumpipa in a pia tawntung hi | the king always gave him all he needed) (r:5.15.8/26.34.26/14.2.16/19.34.10/24.52.34) (q:draft)
kisap = (t:v) (w:be called/be invited/be summoned) (d:form of kisam, be called, used before ciangin, hangin and loh: be called, invited or summoned; also be called by a name) (e:hong ~ laitakin na omzia uh mah bangin/tampi a ~ hangin tawm bek a kiteel hi | many are invited but few are chosen/Mopawi khatpeuhah hong ~ ciangin | when you are invited to a wedding feast/teci pang dingin a ~ ciangin | when he is called to testify/a pai dingin hong ~ loh zawh ni sawmthum | thirty days since I was called to go) (s:kilo) (b:sap) (r:46.7.24/17.4.11/40.22.14/42.14.8/3.5.1) (q:draft)
kisapa = (t:n) (w:one who considers himself/one who thinks himself) (d:kisa with pa marking a man; pil a kisapa is the man who thinks himself wise) (e:A pil lo kimlai pil a ~ sangin) (b:kisa) (r:20.26.12) (q:draft)
kisapna = (t:n) (w:need/lack/want) (d:kisap, need, with the noun suffix na: what a person needs or lacks; kisapna nei lo is lack nothing) (e:mite’ ~ bangin a hawmsak uh hi/na ~ khempeuh ka en ding hi | I will look after all your needs/amah a zahtakte in ~ nei lo hi | those who fear him lack nothing/note ~ khempeuh Khazih Zeisu sungah hong kicingsak ding | he will meet all your needs in Christ Jesus) (s:tangsapna/kitangsapna/cihmawhna) (b:kisap) (r:44.2.45/50.4.19/7.19.20/19.34.9) (q:draft)
kisapnate = (t:n) (w:needs) (d:kisapna, need, with the plural te: the things a person needs) (e:amau’ ~ na piak uh leh/~ a ngah nadingun | so that they may have what they need/a ~ khempeuh na huh ta un | help her in all that she needs/a lawmte in a ~ a piaktheih nadingin | so that his friends might provide for his needs) (s:cihmawhnate) (b:kisapna) (r:23.58.10/56.3.14/45.16.2/44.27.3) (q:draft)
kisasak = (t:v) (w:make oneself feel) (d:sasak, cause to feel, with ki, oneself; lamdang kisasak, be amazed, make oneself wonder) (e:Lamdang ~ unla lamdang a sa hi un) (b:sasak) (r:23.29.9) (q:draft)
kisat = (t:v) (w:be beaten/be struck/be battered) (d:passive of sat, beat or strike: be beaten; khat leh khat kisat is strike one another; said of the heart, pound or throb) (e:kongpite ~ khamin kisia hi/En in, na nasemte hong ~ hi | look, your servants are being beaten/kumminte molhtum tawh ~ hi | cumin is beaten with a stick/laiza la sakna bangin ka lungsim ~ gaihgaih a | my heart throbs like the playing of a harp/note hong ~ beh lailai nadingin | that you should be beaten still more) (b:sat) (r:23.24.12/23.1.5/2.5.16/23.28.27/23.16.11) (q:draft)
kisate = (t:n) (w:those who consider themselves) (d:kisa with plural te, placed after a describing word: people who think themselves so, as mipil a kisate, those who think themselves wise) (e:siam a ~ in gimna ngah ta hen/mipil a ~ amah in a don lohna | he has no regard for those who think themselves wise/amah bek thupi a ~ hi a | they think only themselves important/Kha thu lamah zawngkhal a ~ | those who consider themselves poor in spirit) (b:kisa) (r:23.5.21/18.37.24/20.18.1/40.5.3) (q:draft)
kisate = (t:n) (w:songs sung) (d:in la kisate, the songs that are sung) (e:la ~ za thei nawn loin) (b:kisa) (r:21.12.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisatgawp = (t:v) (w:be beaten/be struck hard/strike one another) (d:kisat, be beaten, with gawp marking a thorough or violent action; amau le amau kisatgawp, strike each other down) (e:mihon mai-ah hong ~ hi/khatlekhat namsau tawh ~ ding uh hi | they will strike one another down with the sword/amau le amau ~ sak hi | he made them strike each other down/amah kihen cipin ~ ding a | he shall be bound and beaten) (b:kisat) (r:44.16.37/7.7.22/26.38.21/15.6.11) (q:draft)
kisathei = (t:v) (w:boast/be proud/be arrogant) (d:boast or be proud of oneself; a kisathei mi is one who boasts, and Topa sungah kisathei is boast in the Lord) (e:Topa sung bekah ~ ta hen/kuamah a ~ ding a om kei hi | no one may boast/~ kei un, bang hang hiam cih leh | do not be arrogant, because/na ~ uh hi | you are proud) (s:kiphasak/kihisak/kiphatsak) (a:kiniamkhiat/kiniamsak) (b:kisa) (r:47.10.17/46.1.29/24.13.15/46.5.2) (q:draft)
kisatheikha = (t:v) (w:be arrogant/become proud) (d:kisathei, be proud, with kha, happen to: fall into pride; kisatheikha loin is without becoming arrogant) (e:a hau mite ~ loin) (r:54.6.17) (q:draft)
kisatheipa = (t:n) (w:boaster/one who boasts) (d:kisathei, boast, with pa marking a man: the man who boasts) (e:Thukham suangin a ~ aw) (b:kisathei) (r:45.2.23) (q:draft)
kisatheisak = (t:v) (w:make proud/puff up) (d:kisathei, be proud, with the causative sak) (e:theihna in mite ~ a) (b:kisathei) (r:46.8.1) (q:draft)
kisatheite = (t:n) (w:the proud/the arrogant/those who boast) (d:kisathei, boast or be proud, with the plural te: people who are proud or who boast, usually as a kisatheite) (e:A ~ na mit tawh kituak lo hi/A ~ Pasian in kham a | God opposes the proud/A ~ in Pasian hangah kisathei ta hen | let those who boast boast in God/Pasian in a ~ a kham hi | God opposes the proud) (s:kiphasakte/kihisakte/kiliansakte) (a:kiniamkhiatte/lungniamsakte) (b:kisathei) (r:19.5.5/59.4.6/46.1.31/60.5.5) (q:draft)
kisatin = (t:v) (w:be beaten/be struck) (d:kisat, be beaten, with the linking ending in: being beaten, and) (e:a koih mite ~/Kote hong ~, thongah hong kikhia-in | we were beaten and thrown into prison/~ amah a sih leh | if he is struck and dies) (b:kisat) (r:2.5.14/47.6.5/2.22.1) (q:draft)
kisatkham = (t:v) (w:be smashed/be broken down/be broken open) (d:passive of satkham, smash by striking: be broken down or burst open by blows) (e:paknamtui taute ~ ding hi/kulh kongpite ~ a | the gates are broken open) (s:kisukham/kidengkham/kisatvui) (b:satkham) (r:26.6.4/34.2.6) (q:draft)
kisatkhia = (t:v) (w:be broken off/be cut off) (d:passive of satkhia, strike off: said of branches cut from a tree) (e:a hiangte a ~ ahi hi/oliv kung a hiangte ~-in | the branches of the olive tree being broken off/a up lohna hangun a ~ hi | they were broken off because of their unbelief/note zong hong ~ ding hi | you also will be cut off) (s:kisattan) (b:satkhia) (r:45.11.19/45.11.22/45.11.17/45.11.20) (q:draft)
kisatkhia = (t:v) (w:be beaten out/be threshed out) (d:of grain or seed, be knocked out with a stick) (e:masala-te ciangkang tawh ~ a) (b:satkhia) (r:23.28.27) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisatlum = (t:v) (w:be struck dead/be killed/be dashed to death) (d:passive of satlum, strike dead: be killed by a blow or with the sword) (e:namsau tawh a ~ a om hi/a tate uh ~ hi | their children were dashed to death) (s:kithat/kithatlum) (b:satlum) (r:58.11.37/34.3.10) (q:draft)
kisatna = (t:n) (w:beating/blow/lash) (d:the act of beating or of being struck; kisatna ciang is the rod one is beaten with and kisatna ma is a wound from a beating) (e:zavei a ~ sangin/kei hong ~ ciang | the rod that strikes me/note hong ~ ciangkhut a kitan manin | because the rod that struck you is broken/sakol ~ a ging | the sound of horses being whipped) (s:satna/vuakna) (b:kisat) (r:20.17.10/18.9.34/23.14.29/34.3.2) (q:draft)
kisatnen = (t:v) (w:be smashed to bits/be shattered) (d:passive of satnen, smash into small bits) (e:inn neute ~ ding hi) (s:kisatvui/kisatkham) (b:satnen) (r:30.6.11) (q:draft)
kisatnim = (t:v) (w:be crushed/be bruised) (d:be beaten down and crushed by blows) (e:eite’ mawhna hangin amah ~ hi/amah a ~ ding pen | that he should be crushed) (s:kisuzan) (b:satnim) (r:23.53.5/23.53.10) (q:draft)
kisatpuk = (t:v) (w:be struck down/be defeated) (d:passive of satpuk, strike down) (e:note hong ~ kha ding ahih manin) (s:kizo/guallel) (a:gualzo) (b:satpuk) (r:4.14.42) (q:draft)
kisattan = (t:v) (w:be cut off/be cut down) (d:passive of sattan, cut off; a kisattan ankung is a stalk of grain that has been cut) (e:a ~ ankung bangin keu pah hi) (s:kisatkhia) (b:sattan) (r:18.24.24) (q:draft)
kisatvui = (t:v) (w:be smashed to powder/be crushed/be broken down) (d:passive of satvui, beat to dust) (e:a paknamtui taute uh ~ gawp ding) (s:kisatkham/kisatnen) (b:satvui) (r:26.6.6) (q:draft)
kisatzan = (t:v) (w:be pressed/be beaten/be crushed) (d:passive of satzan, beat to pieces; a kisatzan sathau is oil from beaten or pressed olives) (e:an tawh biakna-in a ~ sathau/a ~ singgah thau | oil of pressed olives) (s:kisuzan) (b:satzan) (r:4.28.5/2.29.40) (q:draft)
kisatzanin = (t:v) (w:be smashed to pieces/be broken down) (d:kisatzan with the linking ending in: being smashed to pieces, and) (e:inn liante ~ inn neute kisatnen ding hi) (b:kisatzan) (r:30.6.11) (q:draft)
kisau = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:grasshopper) (d:found in kauphe kisau, a kind of locust or grasshopper that may be eaten, the last of the four kinds named in Leviticus 11:22) (e:kauphe ~ nam khempeuh ahi hi) (r:3.11.22) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisawh = (t:v) (w:be leavened/be mixed with/be salted) (d:passive of sawh, mix in: silngo a kisawh is leavened, made with yeast; gu kisawh tui is poisoned water; of salt, be salted) (e:Silngo a ~ peuhmah nane kei ding uh hi/mei tawh cisawh bangin a ~ ding uh hi | they will be salted with fire as with salt/tuate silngo ~ lo hi | they were without yeast/gu ~ tui ka dawnsak ding hi | I will make them drink poisoned water) (s:kihelpih) (b:sawh) (r:2.12.20/41.9.49/2.12.39/24.23.15) (q:draft)
kisawhkha = (t:v) (w:touch/come into contact with/be stained by) (d:with tawh, with: come into contact with a thing and so be affected or defiled by it) (e:mawhna tawh ~ nawn lo uh hi/leitung siatnate tawh ~ loin | without being stained by the evils of the world/a nin na khat peuhpeuh tawh a ~ sa | meat that touches anything unclean) (s:lawngkha/sukha) (r:60.4.1/3.7.19/59.1.27) (q:draft)
kisawk = (t:v) (w:revel/carouse) (d:said of men and women at a feast after drinking; the verse has it for indulging in revelry and the exact sense is not certain) (e:numei pasal ~ ngeingai uh hi) (s:gualnuam/noptat) (r:2.32.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisawl = (t:v) (w:be sent/be ordered) (d:passive of sawl, send or order: be sent on an errand or as an envoy, or be given a task to do) (e:A ~ kei leh/nasep khatpeuh peuh zong ~ lo ding hi | nor shall any duty be laid on him/gam khempeuh ah thugen dingin mi khat ~ hi | a man was sent to speak to all the nations/that lum dinga a ~ kumpi cing Ariok | Arioch the king's guard, who was sent to kill) (s:kipuak/kipaisak) (b:sawl) (r:45.10.15/24.49.14/5.24.5/27.2.14) (q:draft)
