kisawlteng = (t:n) (w:all that one is told to do) (d:kisawl, be ordered, with teng, all) (e:hong ~ na sepkhit uh ciangin) (b:kisawl) (r:42.17.10) (q:draft)
kisawlzo = (t:v) (w:have been sent/be sent) (d:kisawl be sent, with zo marking the action as done) (e:Minamte lakah kamtai khat ~ a/thu a gen dingin kei hong ~ hi | I have been sent to speak) (b:kisawl) (r:31.1.1/27.10.11) (q:draft)
kisawm = (t:v) (w:be plotted against/be planned against) (d:passive of sawm, intend or plan to do something; in Acts 9:24 of the plan to kill Saul) (e:Saul in amah a ~ lamtak na phawk hi) (b:sawm) (r:44.9.24) (q:draft, low confidence)
