kiselin = (t:v) (w:disguise/hide) (d:with mel, appearance: hiding what one looks like, disguising oneself) (e:na mel ~ Jeroboam’ zi na hih lam) (r:11.14.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiselna = (t:n) (w:dispute/argument/strife/controversy) (d:arguing against one another; kam kiselna is a quarrel in words) (e:nungzuite lakah ~ khat hong om hi/ci-in ~ thu hong piang hi | a dispute arose, saying/a haihuai thu ~ | foolish controversies/ngongtatna leh kam ~ ka mu hi | I see violence and strife) (s:kiseelna/kitotna/kinialna) (b:kisel) (r:42.9.46/19.55.9/42.22.24/56.3.9) (q:draft)
kiselnate = (t:n) (w:disputes/arguments) (d:kiselna dispute, with the plural te) (e:thu kikup thu ~ na pelh in) (s:kiseelnate/kinialnate/kitotnate) (b:kiselna) (r:55.2.16) (q:draft)
kiselsimna = (t:n) (w:hiding/hiding place) (d:the act or place of hiding oneself secretly; a kiselsimna mun is the place where someone hides) (e:a ~ mun khempeuh hong ciamteh un la) (s:bukna) (r:9.23.23) (q:draft)
kiselte = (t:n) (w:hidden things/what is hidden) (d:kisel, be hidden, with the plural te: the things that are hidden) (e:khuamial sunga ~ thei a/khuamial lakah a ~ | what is hidden in darkness) (s:kiseelte/thusimte) (r:27.2.22/46.4.5) (q:draft)
kisem = (t:v) (w:be done/be carried out/be performed) (d:passive of sem, work or do, with the prefix ki: be done or carried out) (e:thu a manin ~ ngei lo hi/a kisemsa bangin hong ~ kik ding hi | what has been done will be done again/inn lamkik ~ suak a | the rebuilding has gone on/note lakah lungduai takin hong ~ a | were done among you with patience) (s:kihih/kisep) (b:sem) (r:35.1.4/47.12.12/21.1.9/15.5.16) (q:draft)
kisem = (t:v) (w:be cut up/be cut in pieces) (d:in kisem nen, be cut into small pieces, said of a slaughtered animal) (e:Tuutal a ~ nen ciangin) (r:3.8.20) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisemin = (t:v) (w:be done/be carried on) (d:kisem with the linking ending in: being done, and) (e:hih inn lim takin ~ amau’ makaihna tawh) (b:kisem) (r:15.5.8) (q:draft)
kisemkhia = (t:v) (w:be carried out/be accomplished) (d:passive of semkhia with the prefix ki) (e:Topa’ deihna bangin ~ hi) (b:semkhia) (r:20.16.9) (q:draft)
kisemnen = (t:v) (w:be cut into pieces/be cut up) (d:passive of semnen with the prefix ki) (e:Tuutal a ~ ciangin) (b:semnen) (r:3.8.20) (q:draft)
kisemsa = (t:v) (w:done/have been done) (d:kisem be done, with sa, already: what has been done) (e:a ~ bangin hong kisem kik ding hi) (b:kisem) (r:21.1.9) (q:draft)
kisemsak = (t:v) (w:be made to work/be made to serve) (d:passive of semsak make work, with the prefix ki) (e:sila bangin na ~ hi/innsung mang nasep ~ ding hi | they will be made to serve as palace officials) (b:semsak) (r:1.49.15/23.39.7) (q:draft)
kisemsakte = (t:n) (w:forced labourers/those made to work) (d:kisemsak, be made to work, with plural te; aana tawh na a kisemsakte, those who are made to work by force) (e:aana tawh na a ~ a uk ahi hi/aana tawh na ~ a uk nasep ukpa Hadoram | Hadoram, who was in charge of the forced labour) (b:kisemsak) (r:10.20.24/14.10.18) (q:draft)
kisen = (t:see) <kisen'na>
kisen'na = (t:n) (w:storing place/storage/archive) (d:place where things are kept; a kisen'na inn is a house where documents or treasures are stored) (e:lai manphate a ~ innte sung kizong hi | the houses where the valuable documents were stored were searched) (s:kisenna) (r:15.6.1) (q:draft)
kiseng = (t:v) (w:be put in/be deposited/be stored) (d:passive of seng; in Ezra 8:33 of silver, gold and vessels handed over in the temple, where the NIV has weighed out) (e:kham leh um-le-beelte ~ hi) (b:seng) (r:15.8.33) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisenna = (t:n) (w:storing place/storage/archive) (d:place where things are kept; a kisenna inn is a house where documents or treasures are stored) (e:lai manphate a ~ innte sung) (s:kisen'na) (r:15.6.1) (q:draft)
kisep = (t:v) (w:be done/be carried out) (d:passive of sep, work or do: na a kisep is work that is done) (e:Thutangin na a ~ ciangin/Hih thute khempeuh a ~ khit ciangin | after all these things had been done/Na a ~ theih nading hun ni guk | six days on which work can be done/bang zahin hanciamin a ~ hangin | however hard the effort that was made) (s:kisem/kihih) (b:sep) (r:20.21.15/14.32.1/15.9.1/42.13.14/26.24.12) (q:draft)
kisepna = (t:n) (w:work/doing/being done) (d:kisep, be done or worked on, with the noun suffix na: the carrying out of a work or of deeds) (e:Pasian’ inn a ~ khawl hi/a muhdahhuai gamtatnate a ~ hangin | because of the detestable deeds that are done) (b:kisep) (r:15.4.24/26.9.4) (q:draft)
kisepsak = (t:v) (w:serve one another) (d:sepsak serve, with the reciprocal prefix ki; with khatlekhat, one another) (e:khatlekhat na na ~ un) (b:sepsak) (r:60.5.5) (q:draft)
kisepsak = (t:v) (w:be served) (d:passive of sepsak; a na a kisepsak pasian are the gods that were served) (e:a na a ~ na pu na pate) (b:sepsak) (r:6.24.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisepsakna = (t:n) (w:forced labour/being made to work) (d:sepsak make work, with the prefix ki and the noun suffix na: work that one is made to do) (e:A haksa nasep hong ~) (b:kisepsak) (r:23.14.3) (q:draft)
kisepsep = (t:v) (w:be at work/keep on working) (d:sep work, doubled and with the prefix ki, for an action that goes on) (e:sih nading a ~ laitakin) (r:47.4.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
Kish = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Kish) (d:name of several men, among them a man of Benjamin, the father of King Saul) (e:Saul’ pa ~ leh Abner’ pa Ner) (r:9.14.51/13.23.21) (q:draft)
Kishi = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Kishi) (d:Levite of the clan of Merari, father of the temple musician Ethan) (r:13.6.44) (q:draft)
