Kishon = (t:name) (c:river) (w:Kishon) (d:river in the north of Israel where the army of Sisera was swept away) (r:7.4.13/7.5.21)
kisi = (t:v) (w:face each other/confront/meet in battle) (d:come face to face as opponents, in battle or in court; khatlekhat kisi ni is let us face each other) (e:khatlekhat ~ ni/khat leh khat mai kituahin ~ ni | let us meet each other face to face/khatlekhat gal sungah ~ uh hi | they faced each other in battle/Thukhen zumah kei tawh ~ nung | let us meet at the place of judgment) (s:kimaituah) (r:14.25.17/23.41.1/12.14.8/14.25.21) (q:draft)
kisia = (t:n) (w:damage) (d:damage or ruin that has come on something; also used as a verb, be ruined or perish) (e:na tampi ~ hi) (b:sia) (r:24.50.22)
kisiacip = (t:v) (w:be laid waste/be completely ruined/collapse) (d:kisia, be ruined, with cip, completely: be utterly ruined, said of the earth or a city) (e:Leitung kihawmsuak sakin ~ ding hi/Khuapi hawm suak pen ~ suk a | the desolate city lies in ruins/khuapi sehsawmsuah sehkhat tang ding ~ a | a tenth of the city collapsed) (s:kisiagawp) (b:kisia) (r:23.24.3/23.24.10/66.11.13) (q:draft)
kisiagawp = (t:v) (w:corrupt/be ruined/be laid waste) (d:kisia, be ruined, with gawp, thoroughly: be badly ruined or spoiled; of the earth, be corrupt) (e:leitung en a, a ~ mu hi/Babilon puk a, ~ hi | Babylon has fallen and is broken/a nop mahmah a gam uh ~ hi | their very pleasant land is laid waste/Mual le tausangte zong ~ ding a | hill and watchtower too will be ruined) (s:kisiacip) (b:kisia) (r:1.6.12/24.51.8/24.25.37/23.32.14)
kisiah = (t:v) (w:be set/be laid) (d:siah, set a trap, with the passive prefix ki: of a trap or snare, be set; thang kisiah is a trap is set) (e:a pai nading lampi-ah thang ~ hi/na kimkotah thang hong ~ a | snares are set all around you) (b:siah) (r:18.18.10/18.22.10) (q:draft)
kisiahin = (t:v) (w:be set/be laid) (d:kisiah, be set, with the linking ending in; thang kisiahin is snares being set, and then) (e:Migilote’ lampi-ah thang ~ so kidawh a) (b:kisiah) (r:20.22.5) (q:draft)
kisiahna = (t:n) (w:setting/laying) (d:kisiah, be set, of a trap, with the noun ending na; hong kisiahna ngenthang is the net that is set for me) (e:hong ~ ngenthang panin kei hong lakhia in) (b:kisiah) (r:19.31.4) (q:draft)
kisiak = (t:v) (w:be swept away/be driven out/be banished) (d:be swept or cleared out of a place; found in kisiak khia, with khia, out) (e:gam sung panin ~ khia mang ding hi/Ama mai-ah galkap honpite ~ khia ding a | the great armies will be swept away before him/thuciam mi khempeuh zong ~ khia mang ding hi | everyone who swears an oath will also be banished) (s:kihawlkhia) (r:38.5.3/27.11.22) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisiakhin = (t:v) (w:be corrupted/be ruined) (d:kisia, be ruined, with khin, already; of a person, warped or corrupted) (e:Tua bang mite a ~ hi a) (b:kisia) (r:56.3.11) (q:draft)
kisiakkhia = (t:v) (w:be banished/be swept out/be driven out) (d:kisiak be swept away, with khia, out) (e:thuciam mi khempeuh zong ~ mang ding) (s:kisiakmang/kihawlkhia) (b:kisiak) (r:38.5.3) (q:draft)
kisiakmang = (t:v) (w:be banished/be swept away) (d:kisiak be swept away, with mang, away, out of sight) (e:gam sung panin ~ ding hi) (s:kisiakkhia/kihawlkhia) (r:38.5.3) (q:draft)
kisial = (t:v) (w:boast/brag) (d:speak proudly of oneself or of what one has done) (e:ci-in mi kiangah ~ hi/midik tangin a ~ ding uh hi | they will be found righteous and will boast/ut thu-a biak piaknate va pia-in va ~ un | go and give freewill offerings and brag about them/kei ka ~ thei ding hi | I will be able to boast) (s:kiphasak/kisathei/kisialh) (a:kiniamkhiat) (r:20.20.14/23.45.25/30.4.5/50.2.16) (q:draft)
kisial = (t:v) (w:lie/be laid) (d:lie or be laid down in a place) (e:a nunung pen gamlakah a ~ mateng/gan annekna kuang sungah a ~ na mu ding uh hi | you will find him lying in a manger) (r:4.14.33/42.2.16/42.2.12) (q:draft)
kisialh = (t:v) (w:boast/brag) (d:form of kisial, boast, used before words such as nading, nop, taak and leh) (e:~ nading uh a thu om lo hi/Mi khat peuhpeuh a ~ nop leh | if anyone wants to boast/pil ing, ci-in ~ nading bangmah om lo hi | there is no reason to boast, saying I am wise/a ~ taak mahmah thu hinapi-in | though it is a thing well worth boasting of) (s:kiphasak/kisathei) (a:kiniamkhiat) (b:kisial) (r:49.2.9/47.11.30/47.10.17/59.3.14/47.12.5) (q:draft)
kisialhna = (t:n) (w:boasting/arrogance/pride) (d:kisialh, boast, with the noun suffix na: boasting, proud talk about oneself) (e:a ~ leh a kiphatsakna daantat ding hi/hih ka ~ thu mah kizom paisuak ding hi | this boasting of mine will go on/Tu-a ~ kam ka hong pau ciangin | when I now speak words of boasting/mi gensiatna, ~, le haitatna | slander, arrogance and folly) (s:kiphatsakna/kisaktheihna/kihihsakna) (a:kiniamkhiatna) (b:kisialh) (r:23.10.12/47.11.10/47.11.17/41.7.22) (q:draft)
kisialhnate = (t:n) (w:boasts/boastings) (d:kisialhna, boasting, with the plural te: boasts, proud words) (e:ama ~ a mawkna ahi hi) (s:kiphatsaknate) (b:kisialhna) (r:23.16.6) (q:draft)
kisialhpih = (t:v) (w:boast of/boast about/take pride in) (d:kisialh, boast, with pih: boast on account of something or someone) (e:a mangmuh theihna uh ~ ngam loin/a siat gamtatna uh bang tanvei ~ lai ding | how long will they go on boasting of their evil deeds/kuamah in midangte’ siamna ~ kei un | let no one boast of the skill of others/Topa’ nasepnate bek ~ hen | let him boast only of the works of the Lord) (s:kisaktheihpih/kiphatsakpih) (b:kisialh) (r:38.13.4/19.94.4/46.3.21/47.10.17) (q:draft)
kisialhpihna = (t:n) (w:boasting about/pride in) (d:kisialhpih with the noun ending na: the boasting one does about someone) (e:note ka hong ~ uh a mawkna/note ka hong ~ uhah | in our boasting about you) (b:kisialhpih) (r:47.9.3/47.8.24) (q:draft)
kisialhpihpa = (t:n) (w:boaster/one who boasts of) (d:kisialhpih boast of, with pa for a man: the man who boasts of something) (e:Bangmah a piak lohpi a ~ in) (s:kisatheipa) (b:kisialhpih) (r:20.25.14) (q:draft)
kisialin = (t:v) (w:boast/show off/taunt) (d:connective form of kisial, making much of oneself before others; kei tungah hong kisialin, taunting me) (e:ci-in ~ thu a ngen hi/Mi mai-ah ~, gamtatna a pha mite muh dingin | showing off before people, doing good deeds for people to see/tua hi kei leh kei tungah Israelte ~ | otherwise Israel would boast against me/huaihamin, ~, kihisakin, mi zahko-in | greedy, boastful, proud, abusive) (b:kisial) (r:42.18.12/40.6.1/7.7.2/55.3.2) (q:draft)
kisialin = (t:v) (w:lie/be laid) (d:lying or laid down in something, said of the baby in the manger) (e:kuang sungah ~ a om) (b:kisial) (r:42.2.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisialna = (t:n) (w:place of lying/being laid) (d:kisial, lie or be laid down, with the noun suffix na; a kisialna mun, the place where he was laid) (e:amah a ~ mun hong en un/Zeisu’ luang a ~ a lu lam ah khat | one at the head of where the body of Jesus had lain) (b:kisial) (r:40.28.6/43.20.12) (q:draft)
kisialnuam = (t:v) (w:want to boast/wish to boast) (d:kisial boast, with nuam, want to) (e:na zuihna hangun ~ uh ahih manin) (r:48.6.13) (q:draft)
kisialsial = (t:v) (w:go on boasting/keep boasting) (d:kisial boast, with the second part doubled for an action that goes on) (e:ka ~ lai ding hi) (r:47.12.1) (q:draft)
kisialzia = (t:n) (w:how it was laid/manner of laying) (d:sial lay a body down, with the prefix ki and zia, manner: the way a body was laid in the tomb) (e:a luang ~ khempeuh zong a mu) (r:42.23.55) (q:draft)
kisiamai = (t:see) <kisiamai-sate>
kisiamai-sate = (t:n) (w:devastated places/ruins) (d:the things or places that have been laid waste; written kisiamaisate in the other text) (e:a ~ ding kiksak ding uh hi) (r:23.61.4) (q:draft)
kisiamaisa = (t:adj) (w:devastated/ruined/laid waste) (d:kisia be ruined, with mai and sa, already: that has been laid waste) (e:khang tampi sung a ~ khuapite puahkik) (s:kisiasa) (r:23.61.4) (q:draft)
kisiamaisate = (t:n) (w:devastated places/ruins) (d:the things or places that have been laid waste) (e:a ~ ding kiksak ding uh hi) (s:siasate) (b:kisiamaisa) (r:23.61.4) (q:draft)
kisiamang = (t:v) (w:be ruined/be destroyed/be lost) (d:siamang perish, come to complete ruin, with the prefix ki) (e:khempeuh uh ~ khinta hi/kongpite kisat khamin ~ khinta hi | the gates are battered and in ruins/a ~ khin dingin amaute puksak in | make them fall to their ruin) (s:kisiacip) (b:siamang) (r:24.48.36/23.24.12/19.35.8) (q:draft)
kisian = (t:v) (w:be cleansed/be purified/be sanctified) (d:shortened form of kisiang, written with an apostrophe before tho, suah or sak; kisian’ thosak, be made holy or clean) (e:a ~’ thosak nadingin biakna/tua nu a nin a ~’sak leh | when she is cleansed from her uncleanness/amau ~’suah nai lo uh a | they had not yet consecrated themselves/nomau ~’suah tawm un | purify yourselves/mi tampi in a ~’thosak nadingun | so that many might purify themselves) (b:sian) (r:3.14.32/26.44.26/3.15.28/14.30.3/23.52.11/43.11.55) (q:draft)
kisian'thosakna = (t:n) (w:purification/cleansing) (d:shortened spelling of kisiangthosakna: making oneself ritually clean; kisian'thosakna ni are the days of purification) (e:~ ni a cing sak hi) (s:kisiansuahna) (r:44.21.26) (q:draft)
kisiang = (t:v) (w:be cleansed/be purified/cleanse oneself) (d:siang clean, with the prefix ki, found with the causative sak written apart: kisiang tawm sak, have them cleanse themselves; mei tawh kisiang saksa kham, gold refined in fire) (e:mei tawh ~ saksa kham/amau mah na ~ tawm sak ding hi | you shall have them cleanse themselves) (b:siang) (r:66.3.18/4.8.7) (q:draft)
kisiangsak = (t:v) (w:be cleansed/be purified/purify oneself/consecrate oneself) (d:siangsak, make clean, with the prefix ki: be made ritually clean, or make oneself clean; nomau mah kisiangsak tawm un is consecrate yourselves) (e:Nomau mah ~ tawm un/a ~ ding mipa leh hih nate | the man to be cleansed and these things/amah a ~ lo mipa in | the man who does not purify himself/phak natna panin a ~ dingpa tungah | on the one to be cleansed from the skin disease) (s:kisiansak/kisiansuah/kisiangthosak) (a:kininsak) (b:siangsak) (r:6.3.5/3.14.11/4.19.20/3.14.7) (q:draft)
kisiangsakin = (t:v) (w:purify oneself/cleanse oneself) (d:kisiangsak with the linking ending in: purifying oneself, and then) (e:amahmah tui tawh ~) (b:kisiangsak) (r:4.19.12) (q:draft)
kisiangsaksa = (t:adj) (w:refined/purified) (d:kisiangsak, be purified, with the completive suffix sa; of silver and gold that has been refined) (e:a ~ ngun talen tulsagih/a ~ kham tawh kibawl | made of refined gold) (b:kisiangsak) (r:13.29.4/13.28.18) (q:draft)
kisiangtho = (t:v) (w:purify oneself/consecrate oneself) (d:siangtho holy or clean, with the prefix ki; found with the causative sak written apart, as kisiangtho sak and kisiangtho tawmsak) (e:amaute tawh na ~ sak in la/amaute mah ~ tawmsak hen | let them consecrate themselves) (b:siangtho) (r:44.21.24/2.19.22) (q:draft)
kisiangthosak = (t:v) (w:be cleansed/be purified/be made holy) (d:siangthosak, make clean or holy, with the passive prefix ki; a kisiangthosak ding mipa is the man who is to be cleansed) (e:na khempeuh sisan tawh ~ hi/a ~ ding mipa’ lu nilh ding hi | he shall anoint the head of the man to be cleansed/a ~ ding mipa’ taklam bil teep | the right ear lobe of the man to be cleansed/Israel mite lakah kei hong ~ ding hi | I will be held holy among the Israelites) (s:kisiangsak/kisiansak) (b:siangthosak) (r:58.9.22/3.14.29/3.14.18/3.14.14/3.22.32) (q:draft)
kisiangthosak = (t:v) (w:purify oneself/sanctify oneself) (d:siangthosak, make holy, with the reflexive prefix ki: make oneself clean or holy) (e:keimah ka ~ hi/amaute kisiansuahin a ~ | those who consecrate and purify themselves) (s:kisiansuah) (a:kininsak) (b:siangthosak) (r:43.17.19/62.3.3/23.66.17) (q:draft)
kisiangthosakin = (t:v) (w:purifying oneself/cleansing oneself) (d:kisiangthosak purify oneself, with in linking to the next verb) (e:lungsim kihhuainate khempeuh panin ~) (b:kisiangthosak) (r:47.7.1) (q:draft)
kisiangthosakpa = (t:n) (w:the one being cleansed) (d:kisiangthosak be cleansed, with pa for a man: the man who is to be made clean) (e:siampipa in a ~ adingin) (b:kisiangthosak) (r:3.14.31) (q:draft)
kisiangthosaksa = (t:adj) (w:purified/refined/consecrated) (d:kisiangthosak with sa, already: that has been made pure or holy; of metal, refined in fire) (e:mei sunga ~ sumngo tak tawh kibang hi/thungetna tawh ahi zongin a ~ ahi hi | it is consecrated by prayer as well) (s:kisiangsaksa) (b:kisiangthosak) (r:66.1.15/54.4.5) (q:draft)
kisiansak = (t:v) (w:purify oneself/be cleansed/be pronounced clean) (d:make oneself or be made ritually clean) (e:amah a ~ khit ciangin/amahmah a ~ kei leh | if he does not purify himself/a natui a kan ciangin a ~ nadingin | for his cleansing when his discharge has stopped/amah a ~ ni-in mi phakpa’ zuih ding ngeina | the rule for the diseased person on the day of his cleansing) (s:kisiangsak/kisiansuah) (a:kininsak) (b:siansak) (r:3.13.35/4.19.12/3.15.13/3.14.2) (q:draft)
kisiansak = (t:v) (w:be refined) (d:of silver or gold, be made pure in the furnace) (e:meikhukah ngun a ~ bangin/Ngun le khamte a ~ bangin | as silver and gold are refined) (b:siansak) (r:38.13.9/23.48.10/39.3.3) (q:draft)
kisiansakna = (t:n) (w:refining/purifying) (d:kisiansak be refined, with the noun suffix na; kham a kisiansakna mun is a place where gold is refined) (e:kham a ~ a mun mah om hi) (b:kisiansak) (r:18.28.1) (q:draft)
kisiansuah = (t:v) (w:consecrate oneself/purify oneself/be consecrated) (d:make oneself or be made ritually holy) (e:Levi mite amau mah ~ tawm uh hi/a sanggamte uh khawmin amau ~ uh a | they gathered their brothers and consecrated themselves/note le na galmatte uh na ~ ding uh hi | you and your captives must purify yourselves/na khempeuh sisan tawh ~ a | everything is cleansed with blood) (s:kisiangsak/kisiansak/kisiangthosak) (a:kininsak) (b:siansuah) (r:13.15.14/27.9.24/14.29.15/4.31.19/58.9.22) (q:draft)
kisiansuahin = (t:v) (w:purify oneself/be purified/be cleansed) (d:kisiansuah, purify oneself, with the linking ending in: purifying oneself, and then) (e:Mi tampite ~ a hoih leh a hoih lo/pumpi le lungsim a ninsak theite khempeuh panin ~ | purifying ourselves from all that defiles body and spirit/nomau ~, na puante uh khek un | purify yourselves and change your clothes/tua ciangin ~ a sam met ding hi | then, being cleansed, he shall shave his head) (b:kisiansuah) (r:27.12.10/47.7.1/1.35.2/4.6.9) (q:draft)
kisiansuahna = (t:n) (w:purification/ceremonial cleansing) (d:the act or rite of making oneself ritually clean) (e:Amah in ~ ni a cin mateng/~ a va bawl uh hi | they went and performed the purification/keimah ~ ka bawlkhit hun ciangin | when I had completed my purification/Amah a ~ hun a cin ciangin | when the time of her purification is completed) (s:kisian'thosakna) (b:kisiansuah) (r:3.12.4/44.21.26/44.24.18/3.12.6) (q:draft)
kisianthosak = (t:v) (w:be cleansed/be purified) (d:sianthosak with the prefix ki; kisianthosak nading is for his cleansing) (e:ama ~ nadingin tuate paipih ding hi/a ~ nadingin biakna a pia zo lopa | one who cannot afford the offering for his cleansing) (b:sianthosak) (r:3.14.23/3.14.32) (q:draft)
kisiasa = (t:adj) (w:ruined/desolate) (d:kisia, be ruined, with sa for a completed state: already ruined, placed before the noun) (e:A ~ na biakinnpi/a ~ amau’ teen’na mun panin | from their ruined homes/a ~ David’ ukna gam ka puahkik ding hi | I will rebuild the ruined kingdom of David) (s:siasa/kisiamaisa) (b:kisia) (r:27.9.17/19.109.10/44.15.16) (q:draft)
kisiasak = (t:v) (w:destroy oneself/be ruined/be defiled/be corrupted) (d:reflexive or passive of siasak; with tawm, bring ruin on oneself) (e:Bang hangin nang ~ tawm ding na hi hiam/khat leh khat na ~ ding uh hi | you will destroy one another/a sanggamnu uh ~ hi | their sister had been defiled/amau leh amau ~ uh hi | they have corrupted themselves) (b:siasak) (r:21.7.16/1.34.27/48.5.15/2.32.7) (q:draft)
kisiat = (t:v) (w:be destroyed/perish/be ruined) (d:form of kisia, be ruined, used before words such as nading, ding, manin and sangin) (e:Ka mite a ~ manin/naupangte khat a ~ nading a ut kei hi | he does not want one of the little ones to perish/Judah mite a ~ sangin a pha zaw | it is better than that the Jews perish/Gamsung khempeuh a ~ khit hangin | though the whole land has been laid waste) (s:mangthang) (b:kisia) (r:25.3.48/40.18.14/43.11.50/24.12.11) (q:draft)
