kisiathei = (t:adj) (w:perishable/that can perish) (d:kisia be ruined, with thei, can: that will not last) (e:a ~ pak a ngah nadingun) (s:siathei) (b:kisia) (r:46.9.25) (q:draft)
kisiatna = (t:n) (w:destruction/ruin/perdition) (d:kisiat, be destroyed, with the noun suffix na: the state of being destroyed or ruined; kisiatna-ah pai is go to destruction) (e:~ leh gimna a dim hi/Pasian bia lo mite ~ thukhen ni | the day of judgment and destruction of the ungodly/Amah in ~-ah a pai ding hi | he is going to destruction/amaute ~ in zong a ihmu kei hi | their destruction does not sleep either) (s:siatna/kisuksiatna) (b:kisiat) (r:45.3.16/61.3.7/66.17.11/61.2.3) (q:draft)
kisiatsak = (t:v) (w:harm one another/ruin one another/do evil to one another) (d:siatsak ruin, harm, with the reciprocal prefix ki) (e:Khat leh khat ~ nading vaihawm kei un/khat leh khat ~ nading na ngaihsut loh nading uh | that you should not think of harming one another/khatlekhat ~ nopna, hazatna, mi thahna | the wish to harm one another, envy, murder) (b:siatsak) (r:38.8.17/38.7.10/45.1.29) (q:draft)
kisiatsakna = (t:n) (w:harming one another/doing evil to one another) (d:kisiatsak with the noun ending na) (e:Khatlekhat ~ ding vaihawm kei unla) (b:kisiatsak) (r:38.8.17) (q:draft)
kisiatsakna = (t:n) (w:defilement/being violated) (d:the fact that someone has been ruined; in Genesis 34:5 of a woman who was defiled) (e:a tanu Dinah a ~ za hi) (b:kisiatsak) (r:1.34.5) (q:draft)
kisiatsiat = (t:v) (w:waste away/keep decaying) (d:kisiat be ruined, with the second part doubled for a process that goes on) (e:mi in a ~ hangin) (r:47.4.16) (q:draft)
