kisiazo = (t:v) (w:be ruined/lie in ruins) (d:kisia be ruined, with zo marking the act as completed) (e:Tu-in Jerusalem ~ ta a) (b:kisia) (r:25.1.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisiik = (t:v) (w:be required of/be exacted from) (d:passive of siik exact with the prefix ki: of blood shed, be demanded from those held responsible) (e:khang mite tungah a ~ ding hi) (b:siik) (r:42.11.51) (q:draft)
kisiincip = (t:v) (w:be covered tight/be sealed/be shut up) (d:siin cover with a lid, with the prefix ki and cip, tightly) (e:A ~ lo a kihong beel peuhmah/ka vankoihna sungah ~ hi lo ahi hiam | is it not sealed in my storehouse) (r:4.19.15/5.32.34) (q:draft)
kisiit = (t:v) (w:be left over/be spared/be kept back) (d:siit, keep back, with the passive prefix ki: be left over, spared or kept back; bangmah kisiit lo ding hi is nothing will be left) (e:bangmah ~ lo ding hi/mi khempeuh khat zong ~ lo ding hi | not one of all the men will be left/a ~ pen nang mai-ah hong kilui hi | what was kept back is set before you/mei tawh hal dingte lak panin a ~ | what is kept back from the things to be burned) (b:siit) (r:12.20.17/9.9.24/10.17.12/4.18.9) (q:draft)
kisiitsak = (t:v) (w:be kept for/be set aside for) (d:kisiit be kept back, with sak, for someone) (e:nang adingin hong ~ hi) (b:kisiit) (r:9.9.24) (q:draft)
kisik = (t:v) (w:regret/repent) (d:feel sorry for something done and turn from it; mawhna kisik is repent of sin) (e:Saul a koih manin Topa ~ hi/tu-in ka ~ kei hi | now I do not regret it/mite mawhna ~ nading thuhilhin | preaching that people should repent of sin/Zan diakin no na ~ kik uh a | recently you repented) (r:9.15.35/47.7.8/41.6.12/24.34.15)
kisikcip = (t:v) (w:be trampled/be trodden down/be oppressed) (d:be pressed down underfoot; a kisikcip mite are the downtrodden, the oppressed or humble) (e:A ~ mite zahhuaisak kei in la/Topa in a ~ mite laamto-in | the Lord lifts up the downtrodden/buhkungte a ~ bangin | as straw is trampled down/khe tawh a ~ si luang hawmte bangin | like corpses trampled underfoot) (s:kisikgawp/kituancil) (r:19.74.21/23.25.10/19.147.6/23.14.19) (q:draft)
kisikgawp = (t:v) (w:be trampled/be trodden down) (d:passive of sikgawp trample with the prefix ki) (e:kongzing buannawng bangin a ~ mu-in) (s:kisikcip/kituancil) (b:sikgawp) (r:33.7.10) (q:draft)
kisikh = (t:v) (w:be provided) (d:passive with the prefix ki of sikh, which the same verse uses of God providing) (e:mual tungah hong ~ ding hi) (r:1.22.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisikin = (t:v) (w:repenting/repent/turn back) (d:kisik with the linking suffix in: being sorry and turning from wrong, and then) (e:a mawhna panun ~ tui a kiphum nadingun/Amah hong ~ a nuntak ding | that he should repent and live/a mawhna uh ~ a kimaisak nading thu | the message of repenting of their sins and being forgiven/na lungsim ~ Pasian mai-ah na kiniamkhiat a | your heart repented and you humbled yourself before God) (b:kisik) (r:44.13.24/26.18.23/42.24.47/14.34.27) (q:draft)
kisikkha = (t:v) (w:trample on one another/tread on) (d:sik tread, with the prefix ki and kha, happen to touch; with khatlekhat, step on one another) (e:khatlekhat a ~ gawp dongin) (r:42.12.1) (q:draft)
