kisikkikna = (t:n) (w:repentance) (d:kisikkik, repent, with the noun suffix na: turning back from sin) (e:~ thu leh mawhmaisakna thu/Pasian mai-ah ~ thu ahi zongin | both repentance before God/Israel mipawl ~ leh mawh kimaisakna thu | repentance and forgiveness of sins for Israel/mawhnei mi khat a ~ hangin | because of the repentance of one sinner) (s:kisikna) (b:kisikkik) (r:42.24.47/44.11.18/44.20.21/44.5.31/42.15.10)
kisikna = (t:n) (w:repentance) (d:kisik, regret or repent, with the noun suffix na: sorrow for sin and turning from it) (e:nang ~ lamah hong zol/Na ~ uh a kilat nadingin gamta un | act so that your repentance is shown/mawhnei mi khat a ~ hangin | because of the repentance of one sinner/~ leh kiniamkhiatna lungsim a neite | those who have a contrite and humble heart) (s:kisikkikna) (b:kisik) (r:45.2.4/42.3.8/42.15.7/23.57.15)
kisiknuam = (t:v) (w:relent/be willing to relent) (d:kisik regret, with nuam, want to: ready to change one's mind about a punishment) (e:siatna tunsak ding a ~ Pasian) (r:32.4.2) (q:draft)
