kisilin = (t:v) (w:bathe/wash oneself) (d:kisil with the linking ending in: bathing, and then) (e:amahmah tui sungah ~/Satpiang tawh kei ~ | washing myself with soap/tui sungah amahmah ~, a nitak mateng | bathing himself in water, until evening) (b:kisil) (r:3.15.5/18.9.30/3.15.22) (q:draft)
kisilna = (t:n) (w:washing) (d:the act of washing oneself, from kisil; kisilna kuang is a washbasin) (e:Moab gam in ka ~ kuang hi/biakna tau kikal-ah ~ kuang koih a | he placed the washbasin before the altar/tuikuangpi pen siampite’ ~ ding ahi hi | the Sea was for the priests to wash in/~ kuang leh a ngakna | the basin and its stand) (b:kisil) (r:19.60.8/2.40.7/2.40.30/14.4.6/2.39.39) (q:draft)
kisilsak = (t:v) (w:wash one another's/wash for one another) (d:silsak wash for someone, with the reciprocal prefix ki; said of washing one another's feet) (e:khat leh khat’ khe na ~ ding) (b:silsak) (r:43.13.14) (q:draft)
