kising = (t:v) (w:quake/shake/be stirred/shake oneself) (d:of the earth, tremble and shake; of a town, be in an uproar; of a person, shake oneself, as from the dust) (e:leitang liingin ~ hi/mual bulpite zong lingin ~ damdam hi | the foundations of the mountains trembled and shook/khua zangpi-in ~ hehu uh a | the whole city was stirred/leivui panin ~ un la, ding to un | shake yourself from the dust and stand up) (s:liing/kiling/kilok/kiliing) (r:19.77.18/40.21.10/19.18.7/23.52.2) (q:draft)
kisingin = (t:v) (w:shaking/quaking/shaking oneself) (d:kising with the linking ending in, shaking and) (e:leitung ~ kilok a/mual bulpite zong ~ ling damdam hi | the foundations of the mountains also shook and trembled/keimah ~ suakta ning | I will shake myself free/leitung ~, nakpitakin kilokgawp a | the earth shook and quaked violently) (b:kising) (r:10.22.8/7.16.20/19.18.7) (q:draft)
kisingkhia = (t:v) (w:be shaken off/be shaken out) (d:passive ki- form of singkhia, shake something out or off; also said of the earth shaken from its place) (e:kauphe bangin kei hong ~ hi/Hih bangin ~ hen la, hawmsuak hen | so may he be shaken out and emptied/ama omna panin leitung ~ ding hi | the earth will be shaken out of its place/leivui panin ~ unla dingto un | shake off the dust and rise up) (b:singkhia) (r:19.109.23/16.5.13/23.13.13/23.52.2) (q:draft)
kisinin = (t:v) (w:being veiled/being covered) (d:kisin be covered or veiled, with in linking to the next verb) (e:mite tung bekah ~ a om hi) (b:kisin) (r:47.4.3) (q:draft)
kisinna = (t:n) (w:training/exercise/practice) (d:kisin train oneself, with the noun ending na) (e:Pumpi kisekin ~ manpha hi/kha thu-ah kisekin ~ pen | training in the things of the spirit) (s:sinna/kiseksakna) (b:kisin) (r:54.4.8) (q:draft)
kisinsa = (t:v) (w:have learned/trained) (d:kisin learn or train oneself, with sa, already: one who has learned) (e:a lungkimthei dingin a ~ ka hi hi/a lungkim thei dingin a ~ ka hih manin | because I have learned to be content) (s:sinsa) (b:kisin) (r:50.4.12/50.4.11) (q:draft)
kisinsak = (t:v) (w:train/teach/be trained) (d:kisin, learn or practise, with causative sak: make someone or something learn; also of a person who has been given training) (e:zuauthu gen dingin ~ uh a/hoih taka pilna ~, na a thei baih | well taught in knowledge, quick to understand) (s:sinsak/hilh) (b:kisin) (r:24.9.5/27.1.4) (q:draft)
kisisak = (t:v) (w:bring death on oneself/destroy oneself) (d:sisak cause to die, with the reflexive prefix ki) (e:na mawhna hangun ~ kei un) (s:kisusiatawm/kisiasak) (b:sisak) (r:26.18.30) (q:draft, low confidence)
