kisuankhia = (t:v) (w:be uprooted/be driven out/be conquered) (d:be pulled up or driven out of its place, said of a people or city that is uprooted or conquered; passive of suankhia with the prefix ki) (e:Edom mite ~ ding a/A galte ahi Sheir zong, ~ ding hi | Seir, his enemy, will also be conquered/a ~ ngei nawn kei ding hi | it will never again be uprooted) (s:kibotkhia/kizunglot/kihawlkhia) (a:kisuan) (b:suankhia) (r:4.24.18/24.31.40) (q:draft)
kisuankhiatna = (t:n) (w:being driven out/overthrow) (d:suankhiatna driving out, with the passive prefix ki) (e:a ~ ding le a kisiatna ding) (s:kihawlkhiatna) (b:suankhiatna) (r:24.31.28) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisuanna = (t:n) (w:self-reproach/guilty conscience/guilt) (d:the accusing of oneself in the heart for a wrong done) (e:ka lungsim-ah ~ om loin siang mahmah hi/Lungsim ~ a om lo, upna thu-ah a kip mite | people with a clear conscience, firm in the faith/a lungsim uhah ~ lungsim om nawn lo ding | they would no longer have a guilty conscience/Pasian mai-ah ~ ka nei het kei hi | I have no guilt before God) (r:18.27.6/62.3.21/54.3.9/58.10.2/44.23.1) (q:draft)
kisuanna = (t:n) (w:planting/place of planting) (d:being planted; a kisuanna mun is the place where a thing was planted) (e:Tua a ~ munah keutum lel ding) (s:suanna) (b:kisuan) (r:26.17.10) (q:draft)
