kisuksiatna = (t:n) (w:destruction/ruin) (d:the destroying of people or things, also people destroying one another) (e:ngongtatna leh ~ ka za ngitnget a/Khaldea gam sung mite a ~ kahna awging | the sound of crying at the destruction of the Chaldeans/thutang mi a ~ koi-ah na mu ngei hiam | where have you ever seen the upright destroyed/~ leh kisukgawpna in hong umcih a | destruction and violence surround me) (s:suksiatna/kisiatna/kisukgawpna) (a:kilamkikna) (b:suksiatna) (r:24.6.7/35.1.3/24.51.54/18.4.7) (q:draft)
kisuksiatsak = (t:v) (w:be destroyed/be demolished/be ruined) (d:passive ki- form of suksiatsak, destroy) (e:a innte uh ~ ding hi/Thakhat thu-in ka bukte hong ~ a | suddenly my tents are destroyed/migilote’ neih khempeuh ~ gawp a | all that the wicked own is destroyed/A hatna le a vangliatna teng ~ hi | all its strength and power is broken/na leenggahte hong ~ ta hi | your grapes have been destroyed) (s:kisusia/kisuksiat/kisiat) (b:suksiatsak) (r:36.1.13/24.4.20/18.22.20/24.48.25/24.48.32) (q:draft)
kisuktat = (t:v) (w:be cut off/be blotted out) (d:passive of suktat with the prefix ki; of the memory of a person, be wiped from the earth) (e:a kiphawkna a ~ nadingin) (s:kiphiatkhia/kitat) (b:suktat) (r:19.34.16) (q:draft)
kisuliam = (t:v) (w:wound oneself/cut oneself/gash oneself) (d:su strike and liam wound, with the reflexive prefix ki; no leh no kisuliam is wound yourselves) (e:no leh no ~ ding na hi) (s:kikui/ki-atkeh/kikuiliam) (r:24.47.5) (q:draft)
kisumai = (t:v) (w:be destroyed/be wiped out) (d:passive of sumai destroy with the prefix ki) (e:a vekpi-in ~ ding hi) (s:kisukmang/kisusiamang) (b:sumai) (r:38.5.4) (q:draft)
kisumit = (t:v) (w:be put out/be extinguished/be quenched) (d:passive of sumit, put out a fire or lamp) (e:Migilopa’ meivak ~ ding a/khuamial sunga meivak ~ na bang ding hi | you will be like a lamp put out in the dark/Tui tampi tawh ~ zo lo a | it cannot be quenched by many waters/a kuang ding a, a ~ kei ding hi | it will burn and will not be quenched/a ~ zo lo meikuang | a fire that cannot be put out) (s:kimitsak/kiphelh/kisukmit/mih) (a:kitawh/kuang) (b:sumit) (r:18.18.5/24.7.20/20.20.20/22.8.7/20.30.16) (q:draft)
kisun = (t:prep) (w:like) (d:like, resembling in appearance; a kisun lel ahi hi means he only looks like him) (e:a ~ lel ahi hi/Amah hi lo hi; a ~ lel ahi hi | it is not he; he only looks like him) (s:kibang/kibat) (r:43.9.9)
kisun = (t:adj) (w:similar) (d:similar, alike in appearance, said of one person who looks like another) (e:a ~ lel ahi hi) (s:kibat/kibanga) (a:tuam) (r:43.9.9)
kisun'napa = (t:n) (w:the one anointed) (d:the man on whom something has been poured; here the priest on whose head the anointing oil was poured) (e:a lu tungah nilh sathau a ~ leh | the one on whose head the anointing oil was poured) (r:3.21.10) (q:draft)
kisuncip = (t:v) (w:be thrown down/be thrust down/be struck down) (d:found with suk, down, of people struck down so that they cannot rise) (e:amaute ~ sukin, tho zo lo uh hi) (r:19.36.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisunen = (t:v) (w:be ground fine/be pounded fine) (d:su pound and nen fine, with the prefix ki; a kisunen paknamtui is finely ground incense) (e:a ~ paknamtui khut nih dim) (r:3.16.12) (q:draft)
kisung = (t:v) (w:be cast/be molten/be made of cast metal) (d:ki- form of sung, to cast metal; a kisung before a noun means cast or molten, as of an idol or object made from melted metal) (e:a ~ tua milim bia uh hi/a ~ milim bawngno khat bawlsak hi | he made a cast idol in the shape of a calf/A ~ pasiante note’ adingin na bawl kei ding | do not make cast gods for yourselves/a kalhna bulte khempeuh a ~ ahi hi | the hubs were all of cast metal) (b:sung) (r:19.106.19/11.7.23/2.32.4/2.34.17/11.7.33) (q:draft)
kisungin = (t:v) (w:being poured out/being cast) (d:passive of sung, pour, with the linking ending in, used of a drink offering, of anger, and of casting metal in a mould) (e:ka hehna ~ dai lo ding hi/biakna tau tungah ~ ka om lai hi | I am being poured out on the altar/A vekpi-in a kibangin ~ | all of them cast alike) (b:kisung) (r:14.34.25/11.7.37/55.4.6) (q:draft)
kisungkhawm = (t:v) (w:be cast together/be cast in one piece) (d:kisung be cast, of metal, with khawm, together) (e:tuikuangpi a kisunin ~ pah hi) (b:kisung) (r:14.4.3) (q:draft)
kisungsak = (t:v) (w:be made to pay) (d:said of interest on a debt: na leiba uh a meet hong kisungsak ding, you will be made to pay the interest on your debt) (e:na leiba uh a meet hong ~ ding hi) (r:35.2.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisungtawm = (t:adj) (w:cast/molten) (d:of an idol, made by pouring metal; a kisungtawm pasian is a cast god) (e:note in a ~ pasian-te) (r:3.19.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisunimsa = (t:adj) (w:bruised/crushed) (d:sunim bruise, with the prefix ki and sa, already) (e:a ~ pumpeng sukham lo ding) (r:23.42.3) (q:draft)
kisunin = (t:n) (w:likeness) (d:likeness; a kisunin after tawh means in the likeness of, as in Pasian tawh a kisunin, in the likeness of God) (e:Pasian tawh a ~ a kibawl/amah tawh a ~ a bawl hi | he made them in his own likeness) (s:kibatna/batna) (b:kisun) (r:1.5.1/59.3.9)
kisunnapa = (t:n) (w:the one anointed) (d:the man on whom something has been poured; here the priest on whose head the anointing oil was poured) (e:nilh sathau a ~) (r:3.21.10) (q:draft)
kisupaisa = (t:adj) (w:torn down/demolished/broken down) (d:ki with supai tear down and sa, already: that has been torn down) (e:biakna tau a ~ khat puah kik hi) (s:kicimsa/suksiatsa/kisusiasa) (r:11.18.30) (q:draft)
kisusia = (t:v) (w:be destroyed/be ruined) (d:passive of susia, destroy) (e:Moab gam ~ khin ta a/Migilote’ inn ~ ding a | the house of the wicked will be destroyed/bulpite ~ leh, midikte in bang cih thei | if the foundations are destroyed, what can the righteous do/amau’ hoihlohna tawh migilote ~ hi | the wicked are destroyed by their own evil/Tomno sungin amaute ~-in | in a moment they are destroyed) (s:kisiat/kisuksiat/kisugawp) (a:kilam/kilamkik) (b:susia) (r:24.48.4/19.73.19/20.14.11/19.11.3/20.11.3) (q:draft)
kisusiacip = (t:v) (w:be completely destroyed/be laid desolate) (d:kisusia, be destroyed, with cip marking that it is done completely) (e:Tu-in na innte ~ ding hi/mi gilote ~ khin a | the wicked have been completely destroyed/Gam sung makaite ~ ding a | the leaders of the land will be utterly ruined) (s:kisusiamang) (b:kisusia) (r:40.23.38/34.1.15/23.19.10) (q:draft)
kisusiagawp = (t:v) (w:be torn down/be utterly destroyed) (d:kisusia be destroyed, with gawp, completely) (e:galkidona hangin a ~ ding hih khuapi) (s:kisiatgawp) (b:kisusia) (r:24.33.4) (q:draft)
kisusiamang = (t:v) (w:be completely destroyed/be wiped out) (d:passive of susiamang, destroy completely) (e:Tua khuapi ~ ding a/thupalsatte ~ khin ding a | sinners will be completely destroyed/a ~ dingin a ki-apsa mi peuhmah | any person devoted to destruction/ama hauhna khempeuh a ~ ding ahi hi | all his wealth will be wiped out) (s:kisusiacip/kisukmang/kisumai/siamaimang) (b:susiamang) (r:24.49.2/3.27.29/19.37.38/18.20.28) (q:draft)
kisusiasa = (t:adj) (w:destroyed/broken down/ruined) (d:kisusia with sa, already: that has been destroyed) (e:a ~ kulh kongpi-a pai bangin) (s:kisupaisa/suksiatsa/kisiasa/siasa) (b:kisusia) (r:26.26.10) (q:draft)
kisusiatawm = (t:v) (w:destroy oneself/ruin oneself) (d:susia destroy, with the prefix ki and tawm, by oneself) (e:amau le amau a ~ ahi uh) (s:kisiasak/kisisak) (r:20.6.32) (q:draft)
kisut = (t:v) (w:be plundered/be robbed) (d:passive of sut, plunder, with the prefix ki: have one’s goods taken away by force) (e:na nate uh hong ~ niloh ding a/Amau’ neihsa khempeuh ~ ding a | all their wealth will be plundered/a kiluh, a ~ mite hi a | they are a people plundered and looted/Samaria khua sunga a ~ vante | the plunder taken in Samaria) (s:kiluh/kibuluh/kisuh) (b:sut) (r:5.28.29/36.1.13/23.42.22/23.8.4) (q:draft)
kisut = (t:v) (w:defend oneself/free oneself) (d:speak or act to get oneself clear of a charge) (e:ci-in a ~ hi/amah ~ nading golhguk a piak khak leh | in case he would give a bribe to free himself) (s:kiphel/kihut/kihutawm) (b:sut) (r:44.25.8/44.24.26) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisutkhia = (t:v) (w:be loosed/be released/be unfastened) (d:passive of sutkhia take off, release, with the prefix ki; of prisoners, have the bonds come off) (e:mi khempeuh ~ uh hi) (s:kikhah/kiphel/kikhahkhia) (a:kihen) (b:sutkhia) (r:44.16.26) (q:draft)
kisutkhia = (t:v) (w:be plundered/be taken away) (d:passive of sutkhia take away by force, with the prefix ki) (e:A thahatte’ neihsa nate ~ a/Lungsim khauhte’ neihsa nate ~ a | the stouthearted are stripped of what they own) (s:kisut/kiluh) (b:sutkhia) (r:19.76.5) (q:draft)
kisutkhiat = (t:v) (w:be plundered/be taken away) (d:kisutkhia, be plundered and carried off, in the form used before sak and other following words) (e:A kalaohte uh ~ sak ding a) (b:kisutkhia) (r:24.49.32) (q:draft)
kisutsak = (t:v) (w:let oneself be robbed/be deprived of) (d:kisut, be robbed, with sak: let something be taken from oneself; with kei un, do not let yourselves be robbed of it) (e:note lungdamna ~ kei un) (b:kisut) (r:51.2.18) (q:draft)
kisutte = (t:n) (w:plunder/spoils/loot) (d:kisut, be plundered, with the plural te: things taken by force, usually as van kisutte, plundered goods) (e:galte’ van ~ hawm uh a/van ~ ngahna sangin | than getting plunder/tuate sungah van ~ tam mahmah hi | there was very much plunder in them/mizawngte’ na a ~ note’ inn sungah om hi | what was plundered from the poor is in your houses) (s:vankisutte) (b:kisut) (r:19.68.12/14.14.14/20.16.19/23.3.14) (q:draft)
kisutuah = (t:v) (w:gather/assemble/come together) (d:of people, come together in one place, for work or to listen) (e:nasem ding bekin tua lai-ah ~ uh hi/ka mite hong ~ uh a | my people come together to you) (s:kikaikhawm/kikhop) (a:kithehthang) (r:16.5.16/26.33.31) (q:draft)
kisuvui = (t:v) (w:be ground/be crushed to powder) (d:passive of suvui with the prefix ki; a kisuvui mangbuh is ground wheat) (e:a ~ mangbuh beem tul sawmnih) (s:kigawivui) (b:suvui) (r:14.2.10) (q:draft)
kisuzan = (t:v) (w:be broken in pieces/be crushed/be shattered/be pressed) (d:passive of suzan, break in pieces: of idols and pots, be smashed; of olives, be pressed or beaten for oil) (e:a biak milim ~ ding hi/meibung hita leh belpei hita leh ~ ding hi | whether oven or cooking pot, it must be broken/a ~ oliv gah thau siangtho | pure oil of pressed olives/A milim manphate khempeuh ~ gawp ding a | all her precious idols will be broken to pieces) (s:kitamzan/kisukham/kitam) (b:suzan) (r:28.8.6/2.27.20/3.11.35/33.1.7) (q:draft)
kisuzanin = (t:v) (w:being broken to pieces/being smashed) (d:kisuzan be broken in pieces, with in linking to the next verb) (e:A milim manphate khempeuh ~) (b:kisuzan) (r:33.1.7) (q:draft)
kisuzante = (t:n) (w:pressed ones/crushed ones) (d:kisuzan with plural te: things that have been crushed; oliv gah a kisuzante are pressed olives) (e:oliv gah a ~ panin sathau siangtho) (b:kisuzan) (r:3.24.2) (q:draft)
kitaaklah = (t:v) (w:meddle/interfere/be a busybody) (d:busy oneself with matters that are not one's own) (e:kisai lo thute ah a ~) (r:53.3.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitaangko = (t:v) (w:be proclaimed/be announced) (d:passive of taangko, proclaim, with the prefix ki: be announced aloud for all to hear) (e:kisiatna ding thu hong ~ hi/peengkul aw tawh a ~ phawksakna | a memorial proclaimed with the sound of trumpets) (s:kitangko/kipulak) (b:taangko) (r:24.4.15/3.23.24) (q:draft)
kitaangsapna = (t:n) (w:need/want) (d:what a person is lacking and has to be helped with) (e:midangte’ ~ huh tawntung in) (s:kitangsapna/kisapna/tangsapna) (r:20.3.27) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitaat = (t:v) (w:be cut/be ground) (d:of gemstones, be worked or shaped before setting; taat is sharpen or whet) (e:onik suangte ~ a) (b:taat) (r:2.39.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitah = (t:v) (w:be applied/be put to/be used on) (d:of a blade being put to something; mulkiatna kitah lo is no razor shall touch the head) (e:ama lu-ah mulkiatna ~ lo ding hi/Ka lu tungah mulkiatna ~ ngei lo hi | no razor has ever been used on my head/ama lu tungah mul kiatna ~ lo ding hi | no razor shall be used on his head) (b:tah) (r:9.1.11/4.6.5/7.16.17) (q:draft)
kitah = (t:v) (w:snap/break) (d:of a thread that parts when fire touches it) (e:mei a suk khak ciangin a ~ bangin) (r:7.16.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitahkhak = (t:v) (w:strike against/hit against/dash against) (d:of a foot or a ship and a stone, knock against each other; ends in khak, happen to) (e:Na khete le suang a ~ loh nadingin/Ka teembaw uhleh suang a ~ ding lau uh | they feared our ship would strike the rocks) (s:suihkhak) (r:19.91.12/44.27.29) (q:draft)
kitai = (t:v) (w:be rebuked/be corrected/admonish one another) (d:tai, rebuke, with the prefix ki: be rebuked or corrected, or warn and correct one another) (e:~ ding ut lohna in haina hi/khat leh khat kihilhin, ~-in | teaching and admonishing one another/Tu ni in lungkham ni, hong ~ ni | today is a day of distress and rebuke) (s:kithuhilh) (r:20.12.1/51.3.16/12.19.3) (q:draft)
kitaisan = (t:see) <kitaisan-in>
kitaisan-in = (t:v) (w:being deserted/being forsaken) (d:taisan forsake, with the passive prefix ki and in linking to the next verb) (e:mun pen ~ kinusia hi) (r:23.27.10) (q:draft)
kitaisanin = (t:v) (w:being deserted/being forsaken) (d:taisan forsake, with the passive prefix ki and in linking to the next verb) (e:tenna mun pen ~ kinusia hi) (b:taisanin) (r:23.27.10) (q:draft)
kitaitehna = (t:see) <kitaitehna-ah>
kitaitehna-ah = (t:n) (w:in the race) (d:kitaitehna race, running contest, with ah, in or at) (e:i mai-ah a om ~ thakiamsak loin) (r:58.12.2) (q:draft)
kitam = (t:v) (w:be broken/be shattered) (d:said of pots and other things that break in pieces; beel kitam is a broken pot, a potsherd) (e:beel ~ khat tawh ka kibang hi/i tuikhaina beel ~ ding hi | our water pitcher will be broken/Job in beel ~ them khat la-in | Job took a piece of broken pot/tu-in tua sekpi kitanin ~ ta hi | now that hammer is broken and shattered) (s:kitamzan/kisuzan/kisukham) (r:19.31.12/18.2.8/21.12.6/24.50.23) (q:draft)
kitamin = (t:v) (w:splitting/breaking open/bursting) (d:kitam be broken, with the linking ending in) (e:Oliv Mual ~ phel nih suak ding a/a gilpi ~ a gil khempeuh a buakhia hi | his belly burst and all his intestines spilled out) (b:kitam) (r:38.14.4/44.1.18) (q:draft)
kitamkham = (t:v) (w:be shattered/be broken to pieces/crumble) (d:be broken apart, of mountains, of nations crushing one another and of the heart) (e:taanglai mualliante ~ a/keima sungah ka lungsim hong ~ a | my heart is broken within me/kido-in amaute ~ uh hi | fighting one another, they were crushed) (s:kitamzan/kitam) (b:tamkham) (r:35.3.6/24.23.9/14.15.6) (q:draft)
kitamkhia = (t:v) (w:burst/break apart) (d:kitam be broken, with khia, out; lungsim kitamkhia dektak is the heart nearly bursting, said of rage) (e:lungsim ~ dektak zahin heh uh) (b:kitam) (r:44.5.33) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitamkim = (t:v) (w:be made level/be levelled) (d:tamkim level, with the prefix ki; found with the causative sak written apart) (e:A tamkim lo munte ~ sak ding a) (b:tamkim) (r:23.40.4) (q:draft)
kitamnen = (t:v) (w:be broken to pieces/be crushed small) (d:kitam be broken, with nen, into small pieces) (e:ngun le khamte ~ gawp a) (s:kizangawp) (r:27.2.35) (q:draft)
kitamsak = (t:v) (w:split/break/shatter) (d:kitam be broken, with the causative sak: make something break; of the heart, break it with grief) (e:gam sungah suangpite ~ a/ka khuapi kisiatna in ka lungsim hong ~ hi | the ruin of my city breaks my heart) (b:kitam) (r:19.78.15/25.3.51) (q:draft)
kitamta = (t:v) (w:be shattered/be broken) (d:kitam be broken, with ta, now, marking a changed state) (e:tua sekpi kitanin ~ hi) (b:kitam) (r:24.50.23) (q:draft)
kitamte = (t:n) (w:broken ones/broken pieces) (d:kitam be broken with the plural te, those that are broken; lungsim kitamte are the brokenhearted and beelpei kitamte are potsherds) (e:Amah in lungsim ~ damsak a/beelpei ~ tawh kibang a | they are like broken potsherds/teembaw sing ~ lenin | holding on to broken planks of the ship) (s:kitamzante) (b:kitam) (r:19.147.3/18.41.30/44.27.44) (q:draft)
kitamvui = (t:see) <kitamvui-sak>
kitamvui-sak = (t:v) (w:grind to powder/crush fine) (d:cause to be broken into dust; written kitamvuisak in the other text) (e:amah in ~ lo hi) (s:gawivui) (r:23.28.28) (q:draft)
kitamvuisak = (t:v) (w:grind to powder/crush fine) (d:kitam be broken, with vui, dust, and sak, cause: cause to be broken into dust) (e:amah in ~ lo hi) (s:gawivui) (r:23.28.28) (q:draft)
kitamzan = (t:v) (w:be broken/be shattered/be crushed) (d:be broken in pieces; of the heart or spirit, broken and contrite, as in lungsim kitamzan mite, the brokenhearted) (e:ama mai-ah suangtumpi ~ hi/amaute tukin ~ gawp ding uh hi | they will fall and be completely broken/Efraim ~ gawp ding hi | Ephraim will be shattered/a ~, a kisik lungsim | a broken and contrite heart) (s:kitam/kisuzan/kitamkham) (r:34.1.6/19.51.17/23.8.15/23.7.8) (q:draft)
kitamzante = (t:n) (w:broken ones/shattered ones) (d:kitamzan with the plural te; lungsim kitamzante are the brokenhearted) (e:Lungsim ~ kiangah Topa om a/lungsim ~ a damsak ding | to heal the brokenhearted) (s:kitamte) (b:kitamzan) (r:19.34.18/23.61.1) (q:draft)
kitan = (t:v) (w:be broken/break) (d:of a bone, a bow or other long thing, be snapped in two) (e:A thahatte’ thalte ~ a/khat zong ~ lo hi | not one of them is broken/a thalte uh ~ ding hi | their bows will be broken) (r:9.2.4/19.34.20/19.37.15) (q:draft)
kitang = (t:v) (w:be opposite/face each other) (d:of two things, stand facing each other or lie opposite, often with khat leh khat, one another) (e:kongvangneute khat leh khat ~ hi/a bilvangte khat leh khat ~ hi | the loops are opposite each other/a gual thumin kongvangneu leh kongvangneu ~ hi | in three rows window faced window/Hamath khua lutna tawh a ~ ciang | as far as the point opposite the entrance of Hamath) (s:kimaituah/kimaingat) (r:11.7.4/26.47.20/2.36.12/11.7.5) (q:draft)
kitang = (t:v) (w:be kept/be observed) (d:of a holy day that is kept) (e:sabbathte zong ~ lo hi) (r:26.22.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitangawp = (t:v) (w:be broken in pieces/be shattered) (d:kitan be broken, with gawp, completely) (e:Merodak pasian ~ ta hi) (b:kitan) (r:24.50.2) (q:draft)
kitangcingsak = (t:v) (w:be made complete/be filled up) (d:of something still lacking, be brought to its full measure) (e:a kisam laiteng a ~ suak) (r:51.1.24) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitangko = (t:v) (w:be proclaimed/be announced) (d:passive of tangko, proclaim, with the prefix ki: be announced aloud for all to hear) (e:ci-in ngaih takin ~ hi/kisiat nading thu hong ~ hi | news of disaster is proclaimed) (s:kitaangko/kipulak) (b:tangko) (r:27.3.6/24.4.15) (q:draft)
kitangsak = (t:v) (w:be made straight/be straightened) (d:passive of tangsak make straight, with the prefix ki) (e:Lam kawite ~ ding a/Lam kawi khempeuh ~ ding hi | all the crooked roads will be made straight) (s:kimamsak) (b:tangsak) (r:42.3.5) (q:draft)
kitangsak = (t:v) (w:justify oneself) (d:tangsak make straight, with the reflexive prefix ki: make oneself out to be in the right) (e:amah ~ nuam ahih manin) (s:kidiksak) (b:tangsak) (r:42.10.29) (q:draft)
kitangsam = (t:v) (w:be in need/lack/be needy) (d:be without what one needs; a kitangsam mite are the needy, sum kitangsam is short of money) (e:amaute lakah sum ~ kuamah om lo uh hi/a ~ mite thumanna tawh thukhensak ding a | he will judge the needy with righteousness) (s:tasam/kisam) (a:hauh) (r:44.4.34/23.11.4) (q:draft)
kitangsapna = (t:n) (w:need/lack/want) (d:the state of lacking what one needs, or the thing that is lacking; kitangsapna nei lo is lack nothing) (e:midangte’ ~ huh tawntung in/note’ ~ khempeuh hong pia ding hi | he will supply all your needs/amah a zahtak mite in ~ nei lo hi | those who fear him lack nothing/keimah tunga ~ ngaihsunin | thinking of my own need) (s:kitaangsapna/kisapna/tangsapna) (a:hauhna) (b:tangsapna) (r:20.3.27/11.11.22/50.4.19/19.34.9/50.4.11) (q:draft)
kitanh = (t:v) (w:be redeemed/be ransomed/be bought back) (d:passive of tanh, redeem, with the prefix ki: be bought back or set free by payment; kitanh kik is be redeemed again) (e:tua pen ~ lo ding hi/ki-apsa mi peuhmah, ~ lo ding hi | no devoted person may be ransomed/kizuak lo ding, ~ lo ding hi | it shall not be sold or redeemed/amah ~ kik thei ding hi | he can be redeemed again) (s:kitankhia/kitat) (a:kizuak) (b:tanh) (r:3.27.33/3.27.29/3.27.28/3.25.48) (q:draft)
kitanhkik = (t:v) (w:be redeemed/be bought back/redeem oneself) (d:kitanh be redeemed, with kik back, again) (e:Tuate ~ thei ding a/a kizuak khit ciangin amah ~ thei ding a | after he has sold himself he can be redeemed/amahmah ~ thei ding hi | he may redeem himself) (s:kitatkik) (b:kitanh) (r:3.25.31/3.25.48/3.25.49) (q:draft)
kitanhkiksak = (t:v) (w:allow to be redeemed/let be bought back) (d:kitanhkik be redeemed, with sak, cause or allow) (e:na ~ thei ding uh hi) (b:kitanhkik) (r:3.25.24) (q:draft)
kitanhsak = (t:v) (w:let be redeemed/allow to be ransomed) (d:kitanh be redeemed, with sak, cause or allow) (e:amah in tua nu ~ ding hi) (b:kitanh) (r:2.21.8) (q:draft)
kitanin = (t:v) (w:being broken off/being cut off/snapping) (d:form of kitan with -in, followed by the result, as in kitanin kia, break off and fall) (e:a ngawng ~ si hi/amah pen ~ kia ding a | it will break off and fall/biakna tau kite ~ lei-ah kia ding hi | the horns of the altar will be cut off and fall to the ground/tua sekpi ~ kitam ta hi | that hammer is broken and shattered) (b:kitan) (r:9.4.18/30.3.14/23.22.25/24.50.23) (q:draft)
kitankhia = (t:v) (w:be redeemed/be ransomed) (d:be bought free by payment; a kitankhia mite are the redeemed) (e:sum pia loin note hong ~ ding hi/~ nai loin amah suahtakna a kipia nai lo | not yet ransomed and not yet given her freedom/a ~ mite’ kantan dingin | for the redeemed to cross over) (s:kitanh/kitatkhiat) (a:kizuak) (b:tankhia) (r:23.52.3/3.19.20/23.51.10) (q:draft)
kitankhiasa = (t:adj) (w:redeemed/ransomed) (d:kitankhia with sa, already: that has been redeemed) (e:leitungah a ~ mi tul za/midang khempeuh sung panin a ~ | redeemed from among all others) (s:tatkhiatsa/tatsa/hotkhiatsa) (b:kitankhia) (r:66.14.3/66.14.4) (q:draft)
kitankhiat = (t:v) (w:be cut off) (d:tan cut off, with the prefix ki and khiat, off; of a head, be severed) (e:lutang a ~ kei taak leh) (b:kitan) (r:12.6.31) (q:draft)
kitankhiazo = (t:v) (w:can be redeemed/be able to be ransomed) (d:kitankhia be redeemed, with zo, be able) (e:hing tawntung dingin ~ ngei lo hi) (b:kitankhia) (r:19.49.8) (q:draft)
kitanna = (t:n) (w:being cut off/being broken off) (d:kitan be broken or cut off with the noun suffix na; lu kitanna is beheading) (e:lu ~ a thuak mite/ki thum a ~ thu ka thei nuam hi | I wanted to know about the three horns that were broken off) (b:kitan) (r:66.20.4/27.7.20) (q:draft)
kitansa = (t:adj) (w:broken) (d:kitan be broken, with sa marking a completed state: already broken, said of an arm or a bone) (e:a dam lai leh a ~ zong/guh ~-in a hong nusia hi | he has left me with broken bones) (s:kikuaitansa) (b:kitan) (r:26.30.22/25.3.4) (q:draft)
kitansak = (t:v) (w:break/cut/cut off) (d:kitan, be broken or cut off, with sak, cause: make something break; of a navel cord, have it cut) (e:taamtaak singte ~ a/Na lai hong ~ lo a | your cord was not cut) (s:kuaitan) (b:kitan) (r:19.29.5/26.16.4) (q:draft)
kitante = (t:n) (w:broken ones/those broken off) (d:kitan with plural te; a hiang kitante are its broken branches) (e:a hiang ~ kia ding uh hi) (b:kitan) (r:26.31.12) (q:draft)
kitap = (t:v) (w:be torn down/be broken down) (d:in kitap zan, be broken to pieces) (e:a ~ zan nading ahi zongin) (r:24.31.28) (q:draft, low confidence)
