kitapkhapna = (t:n) (w:gap/breach) (d:a place left empty where one part of a whole is missing, as one tribe out of the twelve) (e:Topa in ~ omsak ahih manin) (r:7.21.15) (q:draft)
kitapna = (t:n) (w:discouragement/brokenness) (d:lungsim kitapna is a broken spirit, discouragement) (e:amau’ lungsim ~ le) (s:lungkiatna/kitapzanna) (b:kitap) (r:2.6.9) (q:draft)
kitapzanna = (t:n) (w:breaking down/brokenness) (d:being broken in pieces or torn down; lungsim kitapzanna is a broken spirit, discouragement) (e:amau’ lungsim ~ leh gitlohna sungah/a kibetkhiatna ding le a ~ ding ahi zongin | whether to uproot or to tear down) (s:kitapna/lungkiatna) (r:2.6.9/24.31.28) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitasam = (t:v) (w:be lacking/be in want/be missing/fail) (d:of food, water or goods: run short, not be there when needed; usually with lo, not be lacking) (e:a dawn ding tui ~ lo ding hi/annek tuidawn ~ lo ding uh hi | they will not lack food and drink/ka mai-a ding ding siampi ~ ngei lo ding hi | a priest to stand before me will never be lacking/~ loin ni simin amaute tungah pia sak un | have it given to them every day without fail) (s:kisam) (r:23.33.16/20.31.11/23.51.14/24.33.18/15.6.9) (q:draft)
kitat = (t:v) (w:be sharpened/be whetted) (d:of a blade; kitat hiam, sharpened to an edge) (e:Namsau khat ~ hiam a/~ hiamin kipuah siang hi | it is sharpened and polished) (r:26.21.9/26.21.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitat = (t:v) (w:be cut off/snap/be severed) (d:of a cord or thread) (e:na nuntakna khau uh ~ ta hi/khedap khau khat zong ~ lo hi | not one sandal strap is broken) (b:tat) (r:24.51.13/23.5.27) (q:draft)
kitat = (t:v) (w:be redeemed/redeem oneself/be ransomed) (d:tat, redeem, with the prefix ki: be bought back, or buy oneself free) (e:mizawngpa in ~ nading bangmah nei lo hi/a ~ kei leh, a kisehna bangin kizuak ding hi | if it is not redeemed, it shall be sold at its set value) (s:kitanh/kitankhia/kitatkhiat) (b:tat) (r:20.13.8/3.27.27) (q:draft)
kitatin = (t:v) (w:be severed/snap/break) (d:of a cord or rope, with the linking ending in) (e:i tuikhaina khau ~/ngun meivak khaina khau ~ | the cord of the silver lamp snapping) (b:kitat) (r:21.12.6) (q:draft)
kitatin = (t:v) (w:strike against/hit) (d:knock a part of the body against something hard) (e:suang tawh ~ a liam khak loh nadingin) (s:kitahkhak) (r:42.4.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitatkhiat = (t:v) (w:be redeemed/redeem oneself) (d:tatkhiat, redeem, with the prefix ki: be bought free or buy oneself free; the form found before nading and kei) (e:ama ~ nadingin pia kik ding hi/Hih bang danin amah a ~ kei leh | if he is not redeemed in these ways/ama ~ nadingin sum pia kik ding hi | he shall pay back money for his redemption) (s:kitanh/kitankhia) (b:tatkhiat) (r:3.25.51/3.25.54/3.25.52) (q:draft)
kitatkhiatna = (t:n) (w:redemption/ransom) (d:kitatkhiat, be redeemed, with the noun suffix na: redemption, or the price paid; kitatkhiatna sum is redemption money) (e:tung panin ~ sum la hi/~ sumte Aaron leh a tapate tungah | the redemption money to Aaron and his sons/a ~ uh Topa' tungah pia ding uh hi | they shall pay the Lord their ransom) (s:kitatna/tatkhiatna/tatna) (b:kitatkhiat) (r:4.3.49/2.30.12/4.3.51) (q:draft)
kitatkik = (t:v) (w:be redeemed/be bought back) (d:passive of tatkik with the prefix ki) (e:a ~ kei leh) (s:kitanhkik) (b:tatkik) (r:3.25.30) (q:draft)
kitatna = (t:n) (w:redemption/ransom) (d:the buying back of a person or thing; kitatna man is the redemption price and kitatna sum is redemption money) (e:a ~ ding bangmah nei lo hi/a ~ uh sumte Aaron leh a tapate tungah | their redemption money to Aaron and his sons/Tuate a ~ man | their redemption price) (s:kitatkhiatna/tatkhiatna/tatna) (b:kitat) (r:20.13.8/4.3.48/4.18.16) (q:draft)
kitatsat = (t:v) (w:be interrupted/be broken off/cease) (d:in the verses always with lo, not: kitatsat lo, unbroken, regular, continual) (e:a ~ lo meihal biakna ahi hi/a ~ lo-a meihal biakna, an tawh a biakna | the regular burnt offering and its grain offering) (b:tatsat) (r:4.28.6/4.29.16) (q:draft)
kitawh = (t:v) (w:be kindled/be lit) (d:of fire or anger, be set alight; kitawh kuang is be kindled and burn) (e:ka hehna ~ kuang a/hehna ~ kuang a, a mit nawn kei ding hi | anger is kindled and will not go out again) (s:kitawhkuang) (a:kimitsak) (b:tawh) (r:24.15.14/24.17.4) (q:draft)
kitawh = (t:v) (w:be dug/be dug out/be quarried) (d:of a pit, be dug; kitawh khiatna is the place something is dug out from, a mine or quarry) (e:Ngun a ~ khiatna ngunkhuk om a/note hong ~ khiatna khuk en un | look to the pit from which you were dug/migilote’ adingin gum khat a ~ hun matengin | until a pit is dug for the wicked) (r:18.28.1/19.94.12/23.51.1) (q:draft)
kitawhkhiatna = (t:n) (w:quarry/place of digging out) (d:tawh dig, with the prefix ki, khiat, out, and the noun suffix na: being dug out, or the pit from which something is dug) (e:note hong ~ khuk en un) (s:kitawhna) (r:23.51.1) (q:draft)
kitawhkuang = (t:v) (w:be kindled/blaze up/burn) (d:catch fire and blaze, in the verses always of anger) (e:ka hehna mei bangin ~ a/hih mun tungah ka hehna ~ ding a | my anger will burn against this place/ama mite tungah Topa’ hehna hong ~ a | the anger of the Lord was kindled against his people/ama hehna ~ pak hi | his anger flares up quickly) (s:kitawh) (a:kimitsak) (b:tawhkuang) (r:24.15.14/12.22.17/19.106.40/19.2.11) (q:draft)
kitawhna = (t:n) (w:quarry/place of quarrying) (d:kitawh be dug or quarried, with the noun ending na: the place where stone is dug out) (e:a ~ mun panin a kibawlsa suangte) (s:kitawhkhiatna/suangkhuk) (b:kitawh) (r:11.6.7) (q:draft)
kitawhnawina = (t:n) (w:confusion/turmoil/panic) (d:a state in which people strike at one another in disorder) (e:~ lianpi khat na om hi) (s:buaina/patauhna) (r:9.14.20) (q:draft)
kitawhzauna = (t:n) (w:confusion/panic/terror) (d:named with buaina, tumult, and tuatcil gawpna, trampling, as what comes on a day of disaster) (e:buaina leh tuatcil gawpna leh ~) (r:23.22.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitawi = (t:v) (w:be held/be carried/be brought) (d:passive of tawi, hold or carry) (e:khuk tungah hong ~ a/lupna nuai-ah koih ding ahi zongin hong ~ ahi hiam | is it brought in to be put under a bed) (b:tawi) (r:18.3.12/41.4.21) (q:draft)
