kiteen = (t:v) (w:dwell/be lived in) (d:in kiteen’na mun, a place that is lived in, an abode) (e:Daii tak-a a ~’na mun) (b:teen) (r:23.33.20) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiteeng = (t:v) (w:marry/be married) (d:of a man and a woman, come to live together as husband and wife; with tawh, marry someone) (e:numei dang tawh a ~ peuhmah in/~ kei leeng a pha ding hi | it would be better not to marry/A kat sangin ~ leh a phazaw hi | it is better to marry than to burn/sagihte in tua numei tawh a ~ zo hi | the seven had married that woman/innkuan pua lam khualmi tawh ~ lo ding hi | she shall not marry a stranger outside the family) (s:kiteng/kipi) (b:teeng) (r:41.10.11/40.19.10/46.7.9/41.12.23/5.25.5) (q:draft)
kiteengin = (t:v) (w:marrying/marry) (d:kiteeng with the linking ending in: marrying, and; kipi kiteengin is marrying and being given in marriage) (e:Tu lai khang mite ~/kipi ~ a om nawn kei ding uh hi | they will no longer marry or be given in marriage) (b:kiteeng) (r:42.20.34/42.20.35) (q:draft)
