kiteengsakin = (t:v) (w:giving in marriage/give in marriage) (d:kiteengsak with the linking ending in; kipi kiteengsakin is marrying and giving in marriage) (e:kipi ~ a om uh a/kipi, ~ a om uh hi | they were marrying and giving in marriage) (b:kiteengsak) (r:42.17.27/40.24.38) (q:draft)
kiteengte = (t:n) (w:those who marry) (d:kiteeng with plural te; with tawh, those who marry someone) (e:numei dang tawh a ~ in/numei dang tawh a ~ in angkawm ahi uh hi | those who marry another woman are adulterers) (s:tenpihte) (b:kiteeng) (r:42.16.18/40.19.9) (q:draft)
kiteenkhia = (t:v) (w:be snatched out/be pulled out/be plucked out) (d:said of a burning stick taken out of the fire; ends in khia, out) (e:meikhuk sung panin a ~ singkhuah/Meikhuk panin a ~ singkhuah khat tawh na kibang | you are like a stick snatched from the fire) (s:kitenkhia) (r:38.3.2/30.4.11) (q:draft)
kiteepsak = (t:v) (w:be suckled/be nursed/be given to suck) (d:passive of teepsak, give suck, with the prefix ki) (e:ka nu’ nawi hong ~ se ahi hiam/a nawi hong ~ se ahi hiam | why was I nursed at her breast) (b:teepsak) (r:18.3.12) (q:draft)
kiteeptumlam = (t:n) (d:the fact of being sucked dry, of having one's strength drained; teeptum with the prefix ki and lam) (e:a ~ phawkkha lo uh hi/ahi zongin a ~ phawkkha lo uh hi | but they do not notice that they are being drained) (r:28.7.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiteh = (t:v) (w:be measured) (d:teh, measure, with the passive prefix ki; kiteh zo lo is too much to be measured or weighed) (e:tuipi-a sehnelte a ~ zawh loh bangin/bang hang hiam cih leh ~ khin zo lo hi | because it could not all be measured/sumngote a gihna ~ zo lo hi | the weight of the bronze could not be measured/Vantung a ~ theih ciang | when the heavens can be measured) (b:teh) (r:24.33.22/1.41.49/24.52.20/24.31.37) (q:draft)
kiteh = (t:v) (w:be compared/compare with/be equal to) (d:with tawh, be set beside another as a match; kiteh theih loh is without equal) (e:nang tawh a ~ theih loh nadingin/kham citak pente tawh zong ~ thei tuan lo hi | nor can it be compared with the purest gold/vantung-a kua tawh ~ thei ding ahi hiam | who in heaven can be compared with him) (s:kibatpih) (b:teh) (r:11.3.13/19.89.6/18.28.19) (q:draft)
kitehin = (t:v) (w:comparing/measuring against) (d:kiteh be compared, with in linking to the next verb; with khat leh khat, comparing themselves with one another) (e:khat leh khat ~ kidem uh a/Tuate in khat leh khat ~ kidem uh a | they compare and measure themselves with one another) (b:kiteh) (r:47.10.12) (q:draft)
kitehna = (t:n) (w:measure/limit/measuring) (d:kiteh be measured, with the noun suffix na: the measure marked out for someone; kitehna khau is a measuring line) (e:Tua ~ in note dongin/Samaria a ~ khau leh Ahab’ innkuan khaukhai sikbawk | the measuring line of Samaria and the plumb line of the house of Ahab/Pasian in hong hawmsak ka nasep ding uh ~ sungah | within the field of work God has assigned to us) (s:tehna) (b:kiteh) (r:47.10.13/12.21.13) (q:draft)
kitehthei = (t:v) (w:can be compared/be comparable) (d:kiteh be compared, with thei, can; with tawh, be comparable to someone) (e:kua dang tawh ~ ding a/vantung a kua tawh ~ ding ahi hiam | who in heaven can be compared with him) (b:kiteh) (r:26.27.32/19.89.6) (q:draft)
kitei = (t:v) (w:be poured over/be transferred) (d:of wine, be poured from one jar into another) (e:thawl khatah a ~ kawikawi leenggahzu/thawl khat pan thawl khatah a ~ kawikawi leenggahzu | wine poured from one jar to another) (r:24.48.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitel = (t:adv) (w:clearly/plainly) (d:with takin, kitel takin, in a way that is clear to understand) (e:a ~ takin amaute kiangah a gen/suang kiphut tungah ~ takin na gelh ding uh hi | you shall write it very clearly on the stones set up/a ~ takin thu ka gen uh hi | I speak clearly/a ~ takin keima zakna-ah hong kisim khin hi | it has been read clearly in my hearing) (s:teltakin/kiteltakin/kitelin) (b:tel) (r:41.8.32/5.27.8/4.12.8/15.4.18) (q:draft)
kitel = (t:v) (w:be clear/be evident/be verified) (d:of a matter or a statement, become clear or be shown to be so) (e:na kam gente uh ~ ding a/a ~ lo kampaute tawh hi loin | not in sayings that are unclear/gu hiam gu lo hiam cih a ~ nadingin | to make clear whether he stole or not/Thu ~ loin bang tanvei koih hong sawm | how long will you leave the matter unclear) (s:kitelpha/kitelsiang) (b:tel) (r:1.42.20/46.15.27/4.12.8/2.22.8/43.10.24) (q:draft)
kiteldot = (t:v) (w:examine oneself) (d:teldot examine, with the reflexive prefix ki) (e:a pumpi a ~ khit ciangin/Mi khat in a pumpi a ~ khit ciangin | after a person has examined himself) (s:kisittel/ki-enpha) (b:teldot) (r:46.11.28) (q:draft)
kitelin = (t:adv) (w:clearly/distinctly/plainly) (d:kitel, be clear, with the adverb ending in: in a way that is easy to hear or understand) (e:a cihnopna a ~ gen uh a/a aw a ~ tum kei leh | if he does not sound it clearly/a aw a ~ ging sensen kei leh | unless their notes sound distinctly) (s:teltakin/kiteltakin/telin) (b:kitel) (r:16.8.8/46.14.8/46.14.7) (q:draft)
kitello = (t:adj) (w:unclear/unintelligible/obscure) (d:kitel be clear, with lo, not) (e:a ~ kampau a zang/Na theihtheih loh, a ~ kampau a zang | who use an obscure speech you cannot understand) (s:theihhak) (a:kiteltak) (b:kitel) (r:23.33.19) (q:draft)
kitelpha = (t:v) (w:be clear/become plain) (d:kitel be clear, with pha, well; with semsem, become clearer still) (e:hih thu hong ~ semsem hi) (s:kitel/kitelsiang) (r:58.7.15) (q:draft)
kitelsak = (t:v) (w:make clear/reveal/make known) (d:kitel, be clear, with the causative sak: make a matter clear, show it plainly) (e:a kithei zo lo thute ~ hi/bangmah ahih lohna tu ni-in na ~ hi | today you have made it clear that they are nothing/kiphawk tawmna lungsim in nakpitakin hong ~ hi | their conscience makes it very clear) (s:kilangsak/langsak/theisak) (b:kitel) (r:18.12.22/10.19.6/45.2.15) (q:draft)
kitelsiang = (t:v) (w:be clear/be clearly understood) (d:kitel be clear, with siang, clean, clear) (e:ka lungsim ngaihsutna ~ ding hi) (s:kitel/kitelpha) (b:kitel) (r:19.49.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiteltak = (t:adj) (w:definite/clear/certain) (d:kitel, be clear, with tak, truly: clear and certain; thu a kiteltak is definite information) (e:thu a ~ tawh kei kiangah/thu a ~ tawh kei kiangah hong paikik un | come back to me with definite information) (a:kitello) (b:kitel) (r:9.23.23) (q:draft)
kiteltakin = (t:adv) (w:plainly/clearly) (d:kiteltak clear, with the adverb ending in) (e:thu a ~ amaute lakah a kilang hi/Pasian’ thu a ~ amaute lakah a kilang hi | what is known of God is plainly shown among them) (s:teltakin/kitelin) (b:kiteltak) (r:45.1.19) (q:draft)
kiten = (t:v) (w:marry/be married/intermarry) (d:form of kiteng written kiten’ before leh, ma, na and other endings) (e:mi khat tawh a ~’ leh/a deih bangin midangte tawh a ~’ theih hangin | though she is free to marry whomever she wishes/a ~’ ma-in Kha Siangtho in a gaisak hi | before they married she was with child by the Holy Spirit/Kote tawh ~’na hong bawl un | make marriages with us/a ~’pih nu’ tate sangin tamzaw ding hi | more than the children of the married woman) (s:kipi) (b:ten) (r:3.22.12/40.1.18/46.7.39/1.34.9/23.54.1) (q:draft)
kiten = (t:v) (w:be settled/be inhabited) (d:passive of ten, dwell: of land, be lived in) (e:a ~’ theihna ciang dongah teeng uh hi) (b:ten) (r:13.5.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
