kitengkhia = (t:adj) (w:chosen/select/picked/best) (d:picked out from the rest, said of the best troops, chariots or officers) (e:a ~ leeng za guk leh Izipt/Israelte a ~ mi pawlkhat teel a | he selected some of the best men of Israel/a ~ ama uliante San Tuipi sungah tum hi | his best officers sank in the Red Sea/mite lak panin a ~ mi khat ka liansak | I have exalted one chosen from among the people) (s:kiteelteel/teelsa) (r:2.14.7/14.13.17/10.10.9/2.15.4/19.89.19) (q:draft)
kitengsak = (t:v) (w:give in marriage/marry off/be given in marriage) (d:cause two people to marry; with tawh for the partner) (e:amau’ tapate tawh ~ kei un/ahi zongin amah tawh ~ nai lo hi | but she had not yet been given to him in marriage/Syria kumpipa le ama tanu a ~ ding hi | he will give his daughter in marriage to the king of Syria/kumpinu Tahpenes’ sanggamnu tawh ~ hi | he gave him the sister of Queen Tahpenes in marriage) (s:kiteengsak) (b:kiteng) (r:15.9.10/1.38.14/27.11.6/11.11.19) (q:draft)
