kitenpih = (t:v) (w:be married/be taken as wife) (d:passive of tenpih with the prefix ki; a kitenpih numei is a married woman, one who has a husband) (e:a ~ zi tawh kibang ding hi/a ~ numeite’ tate sangin tamzaw ding hi | more than the children of married women) (s:pasalnei) (a:kinusia) (b:tenpih) (r:23.62.4/23.54.1) (q:draft)
Kitenpih = (t:v) (w:married/be married to) (d:kiteng marry with pih together with; here given as a name for the land, NIV Beulah) (e:na leitang pen a ~, kici ding hi) (b:kitenpih) (r:23.62.4) (q:draft)
kitep = (t:v) (w:be sapped/be drained) (d:tep sap or suck up, with the passive prefix ki) (e:a ~ tum lam phawk kha lo/a ~ tum lam phawk kha lo uh hi | they do not notice that they are being drained) (b:tep) (r:28.7.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitha = (t:v) (w:be scattered/be strewn/lie spread) (d:said of dung lying spread on the ground, as a picture of unburied bodies) (e:Lei laka ek ~ bang ahi lel/Gamlaka ~ ek bangin misiluang a kipaaithang ding a | dead bodies will be strewn like dung lying on the field) (s:kithehzak/kipaaithang/kipaithang) (r:24.16.4/24.9.22) (q:draft, low confidence)
kithadimsak = (t:v) (w:refresh oneself) (d:thadimsak refresh or strengthen, with the reflexive prefix ki) (e:nangmah ~ in/Kei tawh innah hong ciahin nangmah ~ in | come home with me and refresh yourself) (s:kitawldamsak) (b:thadimsak) (r:11.13.7) (q:draft)
kithah = (t:v) (w:kill/be killed) (d:thah, kill, with the prefix ki; the form of kithat used before bangin, nading, hun, lai takin and similar words, where it mostly means be killed) (e:Tua bangin mi a ~ lai takin/amau a thatte a ~ bangin | as those who killed them were killed/A ~ nading uh namsau | the sword to kill them/mawh nei lo Abel a ~ hun a kipanin | from the time innocent Abel was killed/a that mipa a ~ kei buang leh | unless the one who killed is himself killed) (b:thah) (r:26.9.8/23.27.7/24.15.3/40.23.35/4.35.33)
