kithahlupna = (t:n) (w:slaughter/slaying) (d:kithahlup with the noun ending na: the killing of many people) (e:ka mite’ ~ hangin a sun a zanin/~ hangin a sun a zanin kapkap mai ning | I would weep day and night because of the slaughter) (s:kithahna/kihonthahna) (b:kithahlup) (r:24.9.1) (q:draft)
kithahna = (t:n) (w:killing/bloodshed/murder/slaughter) (d:kithah, be killed, with the noun suffix na: the killing of people, bloodshed; before leitang or mun it names the place where someone was killed) (e:gam sungah mi ~ dim a/tua a ~ thukimpihin a thatte’ puante nangawn ka kepsak | I approved of his killing and guarded the clothes of those who killed him/tua mi ~ leitang sian’sak nading | to cleanse the land where that person was killed/mawhna nei lo mipa a ~ hanga mawhna | the guilt for the killing of an innocent man) (s:thahna/mithahna/kithahlupna) (b:kithah) (r:26.7.23/26.24.7/44.22.20/4.35.33/5.21.8) (q:draft)
kithahsak = (t:v) (w:make kill each other/cause to kill one another) (d:kithah kill one another, with the causative sak) (e:khat leh khat ~ theihna thu/leitung mi khat leh khat ~ theihna thu | power to make people on earth kill each other) (b:kithah) (r:66.6.4) (q:draft)
