kithatpa = (t:n) (w:the man who was killed) (d:kithat be killed, with pa marking a man) (e:Israel mi a ~’ min in/a kithat khawm, Israel mi a ~’ min in | the name of the Israelite man who was killed with her) (b:kithat) (r:4.25.14) (q:draft)
kithatsa = (t:adj) (w:slain/killed) (d:kithat with sa, already done: one that has been killed) (e:a ~ tawh kibang Tuuno/a ~ luanghawm khat bangin | like the corpse of one slain/amaute khempeuh a ~-in Israel mite tungah pia ding | I will hand them all over slain to Israel/a ~ a lawng peuhmahte in | all who have touched someone killed) (s:thahsa) (a:hing) (b:kithat) (r:66.5.6/6.11.6/19.89.10/4.31.19) (q:draft)
kithattawm = (t:v) (w:kill oneself) (d:that kill, with the prefix ki and tawm, by oneself) (e:amahmah ~ ding a cihna hi ding hiam/sem nuam lo ahih manin amahmah a ~ ahi hi | because he will not work he kills himself) (r:43.8.22/20.21.25) (q:draft)
kithatte = (t:n) (w:the slain/those killed) (d:kithat, be killed, with the plural te used as a noun: people who have been killed) (e:Gal sunga a ~ tawh si khawm ding/a ~ leh a kimante | the slain and the captives/a ~’ nate a hawkkhia dingin hong pai ciangin | when they came to strip the belongings of the slain/kamsang a ~ khempeuh hangin | for all the prophets who were killed) (s:thahte/site) (a:hingte) (b:kithat) (r:26.32.20/13.10.8/5.32.42/42.11.50) (q:draft)
