kithausakna = (t:n) (w:fattening of oneself) (d:kithausak fatten oneself, with the noun suffix na) (e:note ~ tawh kei sangin/note ~ tawh kei sangin na tapate pahtawi zaw | honoring your sons more than me by fattening yourselves) (b:kithausak) (r:9.2.29) (q:draft)
kithawh = (t:v) (w:be raised/rise) (d:thawh rise, with the prefix ki; found in kithawh kiksak, be raised up again, of rising from the dead) (e:hong ~ kiksak khit ciangin Galilee gam/hong ~ kiksak khit ciangin Galilee gam sung note mai-ah | after I am raised, ahead of you into Galilee) (b:thawh) (r:41.14.28/40.26.32) (q:draft)
kithawhkiksak = (t:v) (w:be raised/be raised from the dead/be resurrected) (d:passive ki- form of thawhkiksak, raise up again) (e:sihna panin amah a ~ ciangin/Sihna panin Mihing Tapa a ~ matengin | until the Son of Man has been raised from the dead/a ~ ciangin thahatin a melhoih hi | when it is raised it is strong and glorious/a ~ ciangin kha pumpi ahi hi | when it is raised it is a spiritual body/A ~ khit ciangin amah a mu mite’ thugen | the words of those who saw him after he was raised) (s:kithokiksak/kihingkiksak) (a:kiphum) (b:thawhkiksak) (r:43.2.22/46.15.43/40.17.9/46.15.44/41.16.14) (q:draft)
kithawhthawi = (t:v) (w:be stirred up/be roused) (d:be set in motion, said of nations and kings rising for war) (e:galsim dingin ~ hi/kumpi tampi leimong gamlapen panin galsim dingin ~ hi | many kings are stirring from the ends of the earth to make war) (s:kithawithawi/kihanthawn) (r:24.50.41) (q:draft, low confidence)
kithawi = (t:v) (w:prepare/get ready/make ready) (d:get oneself ready for something, often for war; after a verb with dingin it means be about to, as in puk dingin ka kithawi, I am about to fall) (e:amah in a leeng ~ sakin/na beh uh tawh kizui-in ~ un la | prepare yourselves according to your families/galdo dingin kua ~ thei ding ahi hiam | who will get ready for battle/galsim ding a ~ hih mite khempeuh | all these men who were ready for war/Note hong susia dingin a ~ | who is ready to destroy you) (s:kiging/kigalging/kigingkhol) (r:2.14.6/19.38.17/14.35.4/46.14.8/13.12.38/23.51.13) (q:draft)
kithawina = (t:n) (w:readiness/being about to) (d:kithawi get ready with the noun suffix na: the state of being ready or about to do something) (e:note susia dingin a ~ hangin ka lau hi/a lungkim het lohna, note susia dingin a ~ hangin | his displeasure, because he was ready to destroy you) (b:kithawi) (r:5.9.19) (q:draft)
kithawisa = (t:adj) (w:ready/prepared/made ready) (d:kithawi with sa, already done: having been made ready, also appointed and standing ready for a task) (e:galdo dingin ~-in Izipt leitang panin/a Lawmnu a ~-in omkhin ahih manin | because his bride has made herself ready/a paikhiatpih dingin a ~ mipa khut tawh | by the hand of a man standing ready to lead it away/Kigingsa le ~-in om un | take your positions and be ready/si ding ciang dongin a ~ ka hi hi | I am ready even to die) (s:kigingsa/baihsa) (b:kithawi) (r:2.13.18/66.19.7/3.16.21/24.46.14/44.21.13) (q:draft)
kithawisak = (t:v) (w:make ready/get ready/prepare) (d:kithawi with causative sak: have people or things made ready, of a chariot hitch up) (e:amaute in a leeng ~ uh hi/teipi tawi galkap zanih tawh ~ in | get ready two hundred spearmen/Amah sim dingin gamdangte ~ un | prepare the nations to attack her/a hong susia ding mi ka ~ ding a | I will prepare destroyers against you) (b:kithawi) (r:12.9.21/44.23.23/24.51.28/24.22.7) (q:draft)
kithawisakin = (t:v) (w:making ready/having made ready) (d:kithawisak make ready, with the linking ending in; of a chariot, having it made ready) (e:a leeng ~ ama galkapte la-in/Tua ciangin Josef in a leengte ~ | then Joseph had his chariots made ready) (b:kithawisak) (r:2.14.6/1.46.29) (q:draft)
kithawithawi = (t:v) (w:be making ready/be preparing/be astir) (d:kithawi get ready, with thawi doubled to show that the action goes on; said of a nation preparing for war) (e:galsim dingin ~ uh hi/gam lian khat galsim dingin ~ hi | a great nation is making ready for war) (s:kithawhthawi) (r:24.50.41/24.6.22) (q:draft)
kithawn = (t:v) (w:resound/ring out) (d:thawn with the prefix ki: of a sound, ring out as far as a place) (e:mong dongah ~ ding hi/A awging in leitung mong dongah ~ ding hi | the noise will resound to the ends of the earth) (b:thawn) (r:24.25.31) (q:draft)
kitheh = (t:v) (w:be sprinkled/be spattered/be splashed) (d:theh, sprinkle, with the passive prefix ki: of blood or water, be sprinkled or splashed on something; kitheh kha is be spattered onto) (e:Sisan tawh ~ puanza a silh hi/biakna tau tung kimkotah a si ~ ding hi | its blood shall be splashed against the sides of the altar/puan tungah a si a ~ khak ciangin | when its blood is spattered on a garment/sisan pawlkhat kulh tung leh sakolte tungah ~ a | some of her blood spattered the wall and the horses/a nin mite tungah a ~ ciangin | when it is sprinkled on those who are unclean) (s:kibuak) (b:theh) (r:66.19.13/3.6.27/3.7.2/12.9.33/58.9.13) (q:draft)
kithehgawp = (t:v) (w:be spattered/be splashed all over) (d:kitheh be sprinkled or spattered, with the intensifier gawp) (e:amaute’ si hong ~ a/Ka puan tungah amaute’ si hong ~ a | their blood spattered my garments) (b:kitheh) (r:23.63.3) (q:draft)
kithehkek = (t:v) (w:be spilled out/be scattered about) (d:burst and scatter, said of intestines) (e:a sungkua khempeuh ~ hi/Amah kitamzan a, a sungkua khempeuh ~ hi | he burst open and all his intestines spilled out) (r:44.1.18) (q:draft)
kithehkha = (t:v) (w:be spattered on) (d:be splashed onto something, said of blood on a garment) (e:tua si a ~ pen kisawp ding/tua si a ~ pen kisawp ding hi | what the blood has spattered on must be washed) (r:3.6.27) (q:draft)
kithehkhak = (t:v) (w:be spattered on) (d:form of kithehkha used before ciangin) (e:a si a ~ ciangin/Puan tungah a si a ~ ciangin | when its blood is spattered on a garment) (b:kithehkha) (r:3.6.27) (q:draft)
kithehna = (t:n) (w:sprinkling/application) (d:kitheh be sprinkled with the noun suffix na: the sprinkling of blood) (e:sisan tawh ~ ahi zongin/thu hoihzaw a gen sisan a ~ mun | the sprinkling of the blood that speaks a better word) (s:thehna) (b:kitheh) (r:58.11.28/58.12.24) (q:draft)
kithehthang = (t:v) (w:be scattered/scatter/be dispersed) (d:thehthang, scatter, with the prefix ki: of people, animals or things, be scattered in all directions) (e:a tate uh ~ hi/nangma thawhtohna hangin minamte ~ hi | when you rise up the nations scatter/gam khempeuh ah a ~ mite | those who had been scattered through every land/a ~ ka mite nangawn in biakna hong puak | even my scattered people will bring me offerings/Leinuai’ kongvang ah amau guhte ~ ding hi | their bones will be scattered at the mouth of the grave) (s:kikhenthang/kizelthang/kithehzak) (a:kikaikhawm/kikaihkhop) (b:thehthang) (r:18.4.11/23.33.3/44.8.4/36.3.10/19.141.7) (q:draft)
kithehthangin = (t:v) (w:being scattered/scattered) (d:form of kithehthang with -in, linking to what follows) (e:Kei kiang panin mite ~/pawlkhat ka suaktasak ding a, minam dangte lakah ~ | I will let some escape, scattered among the nations/gam sung khempeuh ah ~ an ne, tui dawn | scattered over the whole land, eating and drinking/a galkap khempeuh ~ amah a taisan uh hi | all his soldiers scattered and deserted him/Leitung mun khempeuhah ~ a om minam sawm le nihte | the twelve tribes scattered all over the world) (a:kikaikhawmin) (b:kithehthang) (r:9.13.11/26.6.8/9.30.16/24.52.8/59.1.1) (q:draft)
kithehthangna = (t:n) (w:scattering/dispersion/place of scattering) (d:kithehthang with -na; before mun, gam or minamte it means where they were scattered) (e:a ~ mun khempeuh panin/a ~ minamte lak panin Izipt mite ka kaikhawm kik | I will gather the Egyptians again from the nations where they were scattered/Na ~ uh gam tuamtuam panin | from the various countries where you were scattered/a ~ uh mun khempeuh panin ka kaikhawm ding hi | I will gather them from all the places where they were scattered) (s:thehthangna) (a:kikaihkhopna) (b:kithehthang) (r:24.40.12/26.29.13/26.20.41/26.34.12) (q:draft)
kithehthangsa = (t:adj) (w:scattered/dispersed) (d:kithehthang be scattered with sa, already done: that have been scattered) (e:leimong dongah a ~ na mite uh/leimong dongah a ~ na mite uh kaikhawmin | gathering your people who were scattered to the ends of the earth) (b:kithehthang) (r:16.1.9) (q:draft)
kithehthangsak = (t:v) (w:scatter/disperse/cause to scatter) (d:kithehthang, be scattered, with the causative sak: make people or animals scatter, drive them apart) (e:ngia in tuute manin a ~ hi/Israel mite a ~ pa in a kaikhawm kik | he who scattered Israel will gather them again/Pasian tho hen la, ama galte ~ hen | let God arise and let his enemies be scattered/Keimah tawh a khawmkhawm lote in a ~ hi | whoever does not gather with me scatters/a thaltangte lawn a, a galte ~ hi | he shot his arrows and scattered his enemies) (s:thehthang/khenthang) (a:kaikhawm) (b:kithehthang) (r:43.10.12/24.31.10/19.68.1/42.11.23/19.18.14) (q:draft)
kithehthangte = (t:n) (w:scattered ones/those who are scattered) (d:kithehthang be scattered with the plural te) (e:mi a ~ hong ciahkik ding a/Topa tatsa mi a ~ hong ciahkik ding a | the scattered ones the Lord has redeemed will return) (b:kithehthang) (r:23.51.11) (q:draft)
kithehzak = (t:v) (w:be scattered/be strewn) (d:be scattered about over an area, said of dead bodies left lying in the wilderness) (e:amaute’ luanghawm ~ hi/gam sung tengah amaute’ luanghawm ~ hi | their bodies were strewn all over the wilderness) (s:kithehthang/kipaithang/kitha) (r:46.10.5) (q:draft)
kithei = (t:v) (w:knew/be known) (d:thei, know, with the prefix ki: be known, or know something about oneself; kithei lo is unknown, not noticed) (e:bangmah ~ lo hi/Tua thu in Joppa khua-ah ~ khin a | this became known all over Joppa/sumngo a gik zah ~ zo lo hi | the weight of the bronze could not be known/nate a nei na hihlam uh ~ na hih manun | because you knew that you had those possessions/A ~ lo ding a ki-imcip bangmah om lo | there is nothing hidden that will not be known) (a:kiseel) (b:thei) (r:10.17.19/1.3.7/44.9.42/14.4.18/58.10.34/42.12.2)
kithei = (t:v) (w:be acquainted with) (b:thei)
Kithei = (t:v) (w:be known) (d:capitalised in an inscription; A Kithei lo Pasian is the unknown God) (e:A ~ lo Pasian a’ ding/~-lo Pasian Ading | to an unknown God) (b:kithei) (r:44.17.23) (q:draft)
kitheih = (t:v) (w:be known/know/be recognized) (d:form of kithei used before kei leh, ciangin and similar endings; kitheih theihna lungsim is conscience) (e:a that a ~ kei leh/amah a gai lam a ~ ciangin | when she knew that she was pregnant/amau’ gamtatnasa khialhna a ~ ciangin | when the sin they committed becomes known/na thu gen uh bangci ~ ding ahi hiam | how will what you say be known/A thu kikanin a manna a ~ ciangin | when the matter was investigated and found to be true) (b:kithei) (r:5.21.1/1.16.4/3.4.14/46.14.9/17.2.23) (q:draft)
kitheihmawh = (t:v) (w:disown/ignore deliberately) (d:used with bawl: act as if not knowing, so deliberately forget a matter or disown a person) (e:a ~ bawl thei kei hi/Amaute in a ~ bawl uh thu pen | what they deliberately ignore is this/amah leh amah a ~ bawl thei kei hi | he cannot disown himself) (r:55.2.13/61.3.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitheihna = (t:n) (w:conscience) (d:in kitheihna lungsim, one's own inner knowledge of right and wrong) (e:nomau ~ lungsim hangin na mang uh hi/Keima pumpi ~ lungsim in Kha Siangtho tawh kibangin | my own conscience, together with the Holy Spirit/~ lungsim tawh ngaihsunin na ne kei un | for the sake of conscience do not eat it) (b:theihna) (r:45.13.5/46.10.25/45.9.1/46.10.28) (q:draft)
kitheihna = (t:n) (w:sign/token/assurance) (d:something by which a thing is known or made known) (e:amau omzia a ~ lim pawlkhat/vanging pen ama hong pai nading a ~ ahi | thunder is the sign of his coming) (s:theihsakna/limlahna) (b:kitheih) (r:9.17.18/18.36.33) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitheihsak = (t:v) (w:make known/reveal/show) (d:kitheih be known with the causative sak: make something known, as God making his power known) (e:a vangliatna a ~ nadingin/a ~ nading a deih maninah | because he wanted to make it known/ama vangliatna a ~ nadingin | to make his power known) (s:pulak/langsak/kilangsak) (a:seel/im) (b:kitheih) (r:19.106.8/45.9.22) (q:draft)
kitheihsakna = (t:n) (w:making known/revealing) (d:kitheihsak make known with the noun suffix na: the making known of something; damlenat kitheihsakna is asking after how someone is) (e:na liante khempeuh na ~ ah/damlenat ~-in hong hawh ding | will come to ask how you are) (s:latsakna) (b:kitheihsak) (r:13.17.19/24.15.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitheihtel = (t:v) (w:be clearly known/be fully known/be proved) (d:theihtel know clearly with the passive prefix ki: be clearly known or proved, as obedience that has been fully shown) (e:na cihtakna uh a ~ khit ciangin) (b:theihtel) (r:47.10.6) (q:draft)
kitheihthang = (t:v) (w:become widely known/spread abroad/be made public) (d:theihthang with the passive prefix ki: of news or an order, become known everywhere) (e:Tua thupiakna a ~ phetin/hih thute a ~ thuah loh nadingin | so that these things do not spread any further) (s:kizel/kizeel/kizelh) (b:theihthang) (r:14.31.5/44.4.17) (q:draft)
kitheihtheih = (t:v) (w:can be known/be knowable) (d:kitheih be known with theih can: able to be known; a kitheihtheih nading is the means by which something can be known) (e:khempeuh a ~ nading ahi hi) (b:kitheih) (r:51.2.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitheikhia = (t:v) (w:be found out/be comprehended/be understood) (d:kithei be known with khia out: be found out or fully understood; with zo lo, cannot be found out) (e:i hahkat hangin ~ zo lo hi) (s:kimukhia) (b:kithei) (r:21.8.17) (q:draft)
kitheikim = (t:v) (w:be known to all/be well known/be seen by all) (d:theikim know by all with the passive prefix ki: be known or seen by everyone) (e:mite’ lakah a ~ mi khat/hih thu ~ a, mi tampi in | this became known to all, and many people/hong taanzaih mah bangin ~ ding hi | he will be seen by all, just as it flashes) (b:theikim) (r:20.31.23/42.17.24/44.9.42) (q:draft)
kitheisak = (t:v) (w:make known/proclaim/reveal) (d:theisak make known with the prefix ki: make something known among people; with a person as subject and no object, make oneself known) (e:mite lakah ~ un/Topa in ama gupkhiatna ~ khin zo a | the Lord has made his salvation known/leitung khempeuh ah hih thu ~ un | make this known in all the earth/amaute’ tungah kei ka ~ kei hi | I did not make myself known to them/keima min a ~ ding | to make my name known) (s:pulak/langsak/kilangsak/taangko) (a:seel/im) (b:theisak) (r:13.16.8/19.98.2/23.12.5/2.6.3/44.9.15) (q:draft)
kitheisakin = (t:v) (w:be made known/be proclaimed) (d:kitheisak make known with the linking ending in: being made known to people, and then the next action follows) (e:gam khempeuh ah kihawmin mi khempeuh ~) (b:kitheisak) (r:17.8.13) (q:draft)
kitheite = (t:n) (w:those who are known/those well known) (d:kithei be known with the plural te: people who are known for something, as for good deeds) (e:a gamtat hoihna a ~) (b:kithei) (r:54.5.10) (q:draft)
kitheithang = (t:v) (w:become known/spread/be heard everywhere) (d:of news or a matter, be heard about everywhere) (e:hih thu a ~ hi/inn-ah a omna thu hong ~ hi | the news that he was at home became known/Jesuh’ thu ~ semsem zawsop a | the news about Jesus spread more and more/Hih thu nakgen lua-in ~ gawp ahih manin | because he talked about it so much that it spread everywhere) (s:kizel/kizeel/kizelh) (b:theithang) (r:42.1.65/41.2.1/42.5.15/41.1.45) (q:draft)
kitheithangsak = (t:v) (w:make known/announce/reveal) (d:kitheithang become known with the causative sak: make something known openly) (e:a thuciamna amau tungah ~ hi/keima kam panin tuate gingkhia-in ka ~ hi | from my mouth I announced them and made them known) (s:pulak/langsak/taangko/kitheisak) (a:seel) (b:kitheithang) (r:19.25.14/23.48.3) (q:draft)
kithoihna = (t:n) (w:sacrifice/offering) (d:an animal sacrifice of which the meat is eaten, named beside meihal biakna, burnt offering; kithoihna bawl is make a sacrifice) (e:~ bawl dingin thu ka pia kei hi/Moab gam mual sang tunga ~ bawl-a | making sacrifices on the high places of Moab/leh na ~ sate un | and your sacrificial meat) (s:biakpiakna/biakna) (r:24.7.22/24.48.35/24.11.15) (q:draft)
kithoihnate = (t:n) (w:sacrifices/offerings) (d:kithoihna sacrifice, with the plural te) (e:an tawh biakna leh ~ a hih tawntung/sa nek theih ~ tawh kibangin ne vet un | eat them like the sacrifices whose meat may be eaten/meihal biakna leh ~, an tawh biakna | burnt offerings and sacrifices, grain offerings) (s:biakpiaknate/thoihnate/biaknate) (b:kithoihna) (r:24.33.18/24.17.26/24.7.21) (q:draft)
kithokiksak = (t:v) (w:be raised/be raised to life/be raised from the dead) (d:thokiksak raise again with the passive prefix ki: be raised again from death) (e:Pasian’ mi a sisa tampite zong ~ hi/Khrih zong a ~ lo hi ding hi | then Christ has not been raised either/Amah ~ khin a | he has been raised/sihna panin a ~ Tapa cil | the firstborn raised from the dead/sihna panin a ~ Khrih tawh | with Christ who was raised from the dead) (s:kithawhkiksak/kihingkiksak/kithosak) (b:thokiksak) (r:40.27.52/51.1.18/46.15.13/41.16.6/45.7.4) (q:draft)
kithosak = (t:v) (w:be raised/be raised up/be raised to life) (d:thosak raise with the passive prefix ki: be raised to life from death, often after sihna panin, from death) (e:sihna panin a ~ Jesuh Khrih/Hih lai-ah om nawn lo hi; ~ zo hi | he is not here; he has been raised/Sihna panin Jesuh ~ khin a | Jesus has been raised from the dead/dikkisakna i ngah nadingin a ~ kik hi | he was raised again so that we might be justified) (s:kithokiksak/kithawhkiksak/kihingkiksak) (b:thosak) (r:55.2.8/42.24.6/40.28.7/45.4.25) (q:draft)
kithu = (t:v) (d:found in kithu tuak, written apart for kithutuak: be of one mind, be in agreement; thu word or matter with the reciprocal prefix ki) (e:Amaute tungah ~ tuakin thumanna lungsim) (b:thu) (r:26.11.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
kithuah = (t:v) (w:be attached/be fitted with/be joined) (d:of a thing that has another thing fastened to it, tawh marks what is attached) (e:Savun khau tawh a ~ hakkol bawl in/namsau tawh a ~ kawnggak khat om a | there was a belt fitted with a sword) (s:kizom) (b:thuah) (r:24.27.2/10.20.8) (q:draft)
kithuah = (t:v) (w:accompany/keep company with/go with/join) (d:of people, be together with someone, tawh marks the companion) (e:Kei tawh a ~ Titus nangawn/a uisante tawh ~ kha kei in | do not keep company with gluttons/Amau tegel tawh hong ~ dingin | to come along with those two/amah tawh hong ~ ka sanggam tegel uh | our two brothers who come with him/amah tawh a ~ dingin | to go along with him) (s:kikhawl/tonpih/kipawl) (b:thuah) (r:48.2.3/20.23.20/47.8.22/47.8.23/47.12.18) (q:draft)
kithuahkha = (t:v) (w:join/associate with/keep company with) (d:kithuah be together with, with kha happen to: fall into the company of someone; with kei in, do not join them) (e:a uisante tawh ~ kei in) (s:kikhawl) (r:20.23.20) (q:draft)
kithuahpih = (t:v) (w:accompany/be a companion of) (d:kithuah keep company with the ending pih, do together with: a kithuahpih nungakte are the young women who accompany her) (e:lakah a ~ nungakte leh amah) (s:tonpih/kikhawl) (b:kithuah) (r:19.45.14/19.45.13) (q:draft)
kithuahpihte = (t:n) (w:companions/associates) (d:kithuahpih accompany with the plural te: the people who keep company with someone) (e:ka lawmte le ka ~/Kei le ka ~’ kisapna khempeuh | all the needs of me and my companions/ka lawmte leh ka ~ kidaang koih uh a | my friends and companions keep away) (s:lawmte/kikholhpihte/tonpihte) (a:galte) (b:kithuahpih) (r:19.38.11/44.20.34) (q:draft)
kithuahsak = (t:v) (w:send along with/cause to accompany) (d:kithuah be together with, with the causative sak) (e:zong ka hong ~ uh hi) (s:tonsak/zuisak) (b:kithuah) (r:47.8.18) (q:draft)
kithuak = (t:v) (w:bear with one another/be suffered/be endured) (d:thuak bear, endure, with the prefix ki: put up with each other; kithuak bawlsiatna is the persecution being suffered) (e:a om ciangin ~ un la/~ bawlsiatna hangin | because of the distress being suffered) (b:thuak) (r:51.3.13/46.7.26) (q:draft, low confidence)
