kituaka = (t:adj) (w:fitting/proper/right) (d:kituak be fitting, with the linking ending a) (e:a kilawm a ~ gamtat ding) (s:kilawm/akilawm) (b:kituak) (r:47.8.21) (q:draft)
kituakin = (t:prep) (w:according to/in accordance with/in keeping with) (d:placed after tawh; kituak with the suffix in) (e:biakinn shekel tawh ~/nang kong thupiakte khempeuh tawh ~ | according to all that I have commanded you/Nangma itna kip tawh ~ kei hong hon in | save me according to your unfailing love/kumpipa’ hauhna tawh ~ | in keeping with the king’s wealth/eite’ mawhna tawh ~ hong thukkik lo hi | he does not repay us according to our sins) (b:kituak) (r:2.30.24/2.29.35/19.109.26/17.1.7/19.103.10) (q:draft)
kituakin = (t:adv) (w:fittingly/rightly/aptly) (d:kituak be fitting with the ending in: in a way that fits, rightly; a kituakin a gen is spoke rightly) (e:note tungah a ~ a gen khol hi/na pate kiang uh ah a ~ a gen hi | he spoke rightly to your fathers) (s:kilawmin) (b:kituak) (r:40.15.7/44.28.25) (q:draft, low confidence)
kituakpa = (t:n) (w:the man who met with) (d:the man who encountered something, in the verse robbers; kituak meet, with pa marking a man) (e:misuamte tawh a ~’ lawm ahi hiam) (b:kituak) (r:42.10.36) (q:draft)
kituaksak = (t:v) (w:make agree/bring into harmony) (d:kituak agree or match, with the causative sak) (e:na lungsim uh na ~ un) (b:kituak) (r:45.12.16) (q:draft)
kituakte = (t:n) (w:those that agree/things in accord) (d:kituak match, agree with, with the plural te: the things that agree with something) (e:deihna tawh a ~ bek kimang ding hi) (b:kituak) (r:20.19.21) (q:draft)
kituakzah = (t:n) (w:fitting measure) (d:the amount that is fitting for someone; kituak be fitting, with zah amount) (e:Note tawh a ~ valin) (r:45.12.3) (q:draft)
kituam = (t:v) (w:wrap oneself/cover oneself/be covered) (d:tuam cover with the prefix ki: wrap or cover oneself, or be covered with something; kituam nading is a covering) (e:khuavak tawh nang na ~ a/taamtaak sing tawh ~ hi | it was covered with cedar/a kituamna silhin amah ~ a | she put on her veil and covered herself/amau’ ~ nadingin puanhampi ka bawl hi | I make sackcloth their covering/numei’ sam in ama ~ nading ahi hi | a woman’s hair is her covering) (s:kikhuh) (b:tuam) (r:19.104.2/11.7.3/1.38.14/23.50.3/46.11.15) (q:draft)
kituamcip = (t:v) (w:be wrapped up/be covered completely) (d:tuamcip cover completely with the prefix ki: be wrapped in something as in a cloak) (e:maizumna tawh ~ ta uh hen) (b:tuamcip) (r:19.109.29) (q:draft)
kituamcipsak = (t:v) (w:be covered over/have covered) (d:kituamcip be wrapped up tight, with sak; said of sin) (e:ama mawhna a ~ pa in) (b:kituamcip) (r:19.32.1) (q:draft)
kituamin = (t:v) (w:being wrapped/wrapped) (d:Kituam, be wrapped, with the linking ending in: being wrapped, as the hands and feet of a dead body in strips of cloth.) (e:a khe dial tawh ~) (s:kitunin) (b:kituam) (r:43.11.44) (q:draft)
kituamkoih = (t:v) (w:be set apart/be set aside) (d:Passive of tuamkoih, set apart, with the prefix ki: be kept separate from the rest, as a share of land set aside for the Lord, or people who hold themselves apart from others.) (e:Topa’ tanh dingin seh khat ~ ding hi/Tua a ~ leitang pen | that land which is set apart/Note kiang panin kote hong ~ ahih manin | because we are set apart from you) (s:kisehkhia) (b:tuamkoih) (r:26.45.1/23.65.5) (q:draft)
kituamna = (t:n) (w:covering/cloak/veil) (d:Kituam, wrap oneself, with the noun suffix na: the cloth a person wraps or covers himself with, such as a cloak or a veil; kituamna puan is a garment wrapped around the body.) (e:amah a ~ puan tawh kibang hen/ama' ~ in tua bek hi a | that is his only covering/a ~ silhin amah kituam a | she put on her veil and covered herself/Nangmah na ~ na puanza kiu lite tungah | on the four corners of the cloak you cover yourself with) (s:kikhuhna) (b:kituam) (r:19.109.19/1.38.14/2.22.27/5.22.12) (q:draft)
kituancil = (t:v) (w:be trampled/be trodden underfoot) (d:Passive of tuancil, trample, with the prefix ki: be trodden down under the feet, said of a vineyard, a crown, the sanctuary or grass.) (e:tua kumpi lukhu ~ ding hi/a gawl ka susia ding a, ~ ding hi | I will break down its wall, and it will be trampled/biakinnpi bang tan vei ~ ding ahi hiam | how long will the sanctuary be trampled/lopa bangin amaute ~-in keutumsak in | let them be trampled like grass and wither) (s:kisikcip) (b:tuancil) (r:23.28.3/23.5.5/27.8.13/19.58.7) (q:draft)
kituangsakin = (t:v) (w:being mounted/being made to ride) (d:Tuangsakin, making someone ride, with the passive prefix ki: couriers being put on horses, after which the next action follows.) (e:sakolte tungah laitaite ~ lai kihawmsak hi) (b:tuangsakin) (r:17.8.10) (q:draft)
kituh = (t:v) (w:be sown/be planted) (d:Passive of tuh, sow, with the prefix ki: of seed, be put into the ground; khaici kituh is seed is sown, and a kituh is what has been sown.) (e:khaici ~ kik ding hi/Nail gun kianga ~ khempeuh | everything sown along the Nile/Pumpi a ~ ciangin muat theihna a om hi | when the body is sown, it is perishable/A ~ ciangin leitung pumpi ahi hi | when it is sown, it is a natural body/note’ lung sungah a ~ Pasian’ thu | the word of God planted in your hearts) (s:kivawh/kisuan) (b:tuh) (r:26.36.9/46.15.44/23.19.7/46.15.42/59.1.21) (q:draft)
kituh = (t:v) (w:contend/compete/dispute/strive) (d:Strive against one another for something, as for a throne or in a case at law, or strive to be the first to do something.) (e:kumpigam khat leh khat kumpi-za ~ ding hi/a paikhia masa ding ~ un | strive to be the first to leave) (s:kidem/kitot/kinial) (r:23.19.2/24.50.8) (q:draft)
kituhin = (t:v) (w:disputing over/contending for) (d:Kituh, contend, with the linking ending in: disputing over something, which stands before the word.) (e:luanghawm ~ Dawimangpa tawh a kitot laitakin) (b:kituh) (r:65.1.9) (q:draft)
kituhin = (t:v) (w:being sown/being planted) (d:Kituh, be sown, with the linking ending in: of a grain, being put into the ground before something else happens.) (e:tang khat leilakah ~ si masa kei leh) (b:kituh) (r:43.12.24) (q:draft)
kituhkik = (t:v) (w:be sown again) (d:Kituh, be sown, with kik, again: of seed, be sown once more in land that lay waste.) (e:khaici ~ ding hi) (b:kituh) (r:26.36.9) (q:draft)
kituhna = (t:n) (w:dispute/contention/lawsuit) (d:Kituh, contend, with the noun suffix na: a dispute between people; thu kituhna is a dispute over a matter, a case at law.) (e:Amau’ thu ~ pen amau’ biakna thu/khat leh khat thu ~ | a dispute between one person and another) (s:kinialna/kiselna) (b:kituh) (r:44.25.19/5.17.8) (q:draft)
kituhnate = (t:see) <kituhnate-ah>
kituhnate-ah = (t:n) (w:in disputes/in arguments) (d:Kituhnate, disputes, with the place ending ah: in matters that people contend over.) (e:thu ~ tua thuciamna pen) (r:58.6.16) (q:draft)
kituhte = (t:n) (w:things sown/seeds sown) (d:Kituh, be sown, with the plural te: the things that were sown; khai kituhte are the seeds that were sown.) (e:huan in a ~ a posak mah bangin/khai ~ lei sungah keucip a | the seeds that were sown dried up in the ground) (b:kituh) (r:23.61.11/29.1.17) (q:draft)
kituhteh = (t:v) (w:press in/strive eagerly for/force a way in) (d:Of many people, struggle eagerly to get hold of something or to get into it; probably kituh, contend, with an intensifying ending.) (e:mi khempeuh hong ~ uh hi/vantung ki-ukna thu hong ~ gawp uh a | they have been forcing their way into the kingdom of heaven) (r:42.16.16/40.11.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
kituiphum = (t:v) (w:be baptized) (d:Passive of tuiphum, baptize, with the prefix ki; literally be immersed in water.) (e:Jesuh zong a ~ hi/Mi khempeuh a ~ khit uh ciangin | after all the people had been baptized/Jesuh a ~ khit phetin | as soon as Jesus had been baptized/Pasian kiangah thu ngenin ~ inla | pray to God and be baptized/a innkuanpih mi khempeuh a ~ pah uh hi | all his household were baptized at once) (s:kibaptaiz/kiphum) (b:tuiphum) (r:42.3.21/40.3.16/44.22.16/44.16.33) (q:draft)
kituiphumna = (t:n) (w:baptism) (d:Kituiphum, be baptized, with the noun suffix na: the baptism that a person receives.) (e:na ~ dan uh bangci bang) (s:kibaptaizna/tuiphumna/baptaizna) (b:kituiphum) (r:44.19.3) (q:draft)
kituisak = (t:v) (w:be melted) (d:Passive of tuisak, melt, with the prefix ki: said of metal made liquid in a furnace.) (e:Meiphual sungah ngunte a ~ bangin) (b:tuisak) (r:26.22.22) (q:draft)
kituk = (t:v) (w:fall/topple/stumble) (d:Tuk, fall, with the prefix ki: of a person, stumble and fall; of an idol, topple over.) (e:milim khat a ~ lo dingin/Khangnote nangawn gim-in ~ ding a | even youths will grow weary and stumble) (s:puk) (b:tuk) (r:23.40.20/23.40.30) (q:draft)
kitukalhsak = (t:v) (w:confuse/confound) (d:Mix up the speech or the minds of people so that they no longer understand one another or think clearly.) (e:amau’ kampau va ~ ni/Topa in tua munah leitung khempeuh kampau ~ hi | there the Lord confused the language of the whole earth/Topa in amaute lungsim ~ khin zo hi | the Lord has confused their minds) (r:1.11.7/23.19.14/1.11.9) (q:draft)
kitukna = (t:n) (w:stumbling/cause of stumbling) (d:Kituk, stumble, with the noun suffix na: stumbling, or the thing that makes people stumble, as a stone in the way.) (e:mite’ ~ leh puk theihna suangtum) (b:kituk) (r:23.8.14) (q:draft)
kitum = (t:v) (w:be blown/be sounded/sound) (d:Passive of tum, blow, with the prefix ki: said of a trumpet or horn, or of the signal given with it.) (e:peengkul a ~ ciangin/A nih-in a ~ ciangin | when both are blown/Peengkul ~ na zakna peuhpeuh panun | from wherever you hear the trumpet sounded/din’ khiat ding peuhpeuh ciangun theihsakna ~ ding hi | whenever they are to set out, the signal shall be blown) (s:kimut) (b:tum) (r:18.39.24/4.10.3/16.4.20/4.10.6) (q:draft)
kitumna = (t:n) (w:blowing/blast/sounding) (d:Kitum, be blown, with the noun suffix na: the sounding of a trumpet.) (e:otna leh peengkul ~ lak) (s:mutna/tumna) (b:kitum) (r:30.2.2) (q:draft)
kitumpih = (t:v) (w:be brought in/be led in) (d:Passive of tumpih, take in with one, with the prefix ki: of people or things, be led or carried into a place.) (e:tua nazatte hong ~ ciang/Paul hong ~ nadingin thu a pia hi | he gave the order for Paul to be brought in/lungdamna leh nuamna tawh amaute ~ hi | they are led in with joy and gladness) (s:kilutpih) (b:tumpih) (r:13.9.28/19.45.15/44.25.23) (q:draft)
kitun = (t:v) (w:be wrapped/be bound up/wrap oneself) (d:Be wrapped in cloth, as a baby in cloths or a dead body in grave clothes; also wrap oneself in something; the cloth takes tawh or the ending in.) (e:naungeek puanin ~ a/puan tawh zong hong ~ lo hi | nor were you wrapped in cloths/a khut a khe han puan tawh ~ a | his hands and feet wrapped in grave cloths/kinna puan tawh ~ ding hi | he will wrap himself in zeal as in a cloak) (s:kituam) (r:42.2.12/43.11.44/26.16.4/23.59.17) (q:draft)
kitun = (t:v) (w:succeed/be accomplished) (d:Written kitun’ in the phrase ma kitun’, make progress, be brought to success; from tun, arrive.) (e:ngaihsut piaknate tawh ma ~’ zo hi) (b:tun) (r:20.15.22) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitung = (t:v) (w:arrive/reach) (d:Of a group of people, get as far as a place; dong, as far as, follows the place.) (e:Tahpanhes khua dong ~ hi) (b:tung) (r:24.43.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitung = (t:v) (w:be laid/be set) (d:Of a noose or snare, be laid on the ground to catch someone.) (e:khauzak ~ a) (r:18.18.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitung = (t:v) (w:rise up) (d:Of a cloud of dust or smoke, rise into the air.) (e:leivui khu hong ~ a) (r:23.14.31) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitungsak = (t:v) (w:be fulfilled/be carried out) (d:Passive of tungsak, bring to pass, with the prefix ki: said of vows that are carried out.) (e:thuciamsate hong ~ ding hi) (s:tangtung) (b:tungsak) (r:19.65.1) (q:draft)
kitunin = (t:v) (w:being wrapped/wrapped up) (d:Kitun, be wrapped, with the linking ending in: being wrapped in cloth; the cloth takes tawh.) (e:puan tawh ~ hih lai-ah/a maitang dial tawh ~ a paikhia hi | he came out with his face wrapped in a cloth) (s:kituamin) (b:kitun) (r:9.21.9/43.11.44) (q:draft)
kitunna = (t:n) (w:wrapping/grave clothes) (d:Kitun, be wrapped, with the noun suffix na; a kitunna puan is the cloth in which a body was wrapped.) (e:a ~ puante a om mu a/a ~ puan bek na om hi | only the cloths he had been wrapped in were there) (b:kitun) (r:43.20.5/42.24.12) (q:draft)
kitunpih = (t:v) (w:be brought/be brought to/be led to) (d:Passive of tunpih, bring to a place, with the prefix ki: of people or things, be taken to someone or into a place.) (e:Sihna Kumpipa kiangah ~ hi/tua khuapisung hong ~ ding hi | will be brought into that city/mihon mawkmawk pawlkhat zong hong ~ hi | some of the common crowd were also brought) (s:kipaipih) (b:tunpih) (r:18.18.14/66.21.26/26.23.42) (q:draft)
kitunsa = (t:see) <kitunsa-in>
kitunsa-in = (t:v) (w:wrapped around/bound) (d:Kitun, be wrapped, with sa, already, and the linking ending in: having been wrapped, said of a face bound with a cloth.) (e:puan tawh a ~ hong pusuak hi) (r:43.11.44) (q:draft)
kitunsak = (t:v) (w:let oneself be brought into) (d:Tunsak, cause to arrive, with the prefix ki; in the verse it is said of idols that a person brings into sin.) (e:mawhna sungah milimte ~ a) (b:tunsak) (r:26.14.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitunzo = (t:v) (w:succeed/be accomplished) (d:Used in the phrase maa kitunzo, be able to reach the goal, succeed; zo is be able.) (e:geelna tawh maa ~ bek hi) (r:20.15.22) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitup = (t:v) (w:box/fight with fists) (d:Strike each other with the fists, as boxers do; tawh marks the opponent.) (e:Mi tawh ka ~ ciangin) (r:46.9.26) (q:draft)
kitut = (t:v) (w:be brought/be delivered) (d:Be brought to a place or handed over; zum kitut is take one another to court, and kitut kik is be brought back or restored.) (e:sing a ~ nadingin siampite/Note khatlekhat zum na ~ mahmah uh | you take one another to court/a gam uh a ~ kik zawh | after their land was restored) (r:16.10.34/46.6.7/26.38.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitutkik = (t:v) (w:be brought back/be restored) (d:Kitut, be brought, with kik, back: said of a land or people restored after war.) (e:a gam uh a ~ zawh) (b:kitut) (r:26.38.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitutna = (t:n) (w:place taken to/place of deportation) (d:Kitut, be brought, with the noun suffix na; galmatin a kitutna is the place to which people were taken as captives.) (e:amaute galmatin a ~) (b:kitut) (r:14.6.38) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiu = (t:n) (w:corner/angle) (d:The point where two sides or edges meet, as of a garment, a building or an altar; kiu li is the four corners.) (e:na puanza ~ lite tungah/inn khang nisuahna lam ~-ah tuikuangpi koih hi | he placed the Sea at the south-east corner of the house/sumngo siklen ~ lite tung ading kual li | four rings for the four corners of the bronze grating/A ~ lite-ah ki na bawl ding hi | make horns on its four corners) (s:kiukawi) (r:5.22.12/14.4.10/2.38.5/2.27.2) (q:draft)
kiu = (t:v) (w:knock) (d:Knock on a door to be let in; kong or kongkhak, door, stands before the word, and the form kiuh is used before ciangin and leh.) (e:Piter in kong ~ lailai a/Kongkhak na ~ un | knock on the door/kongkhak kiangah ding-in ~-in ka om hi | I stand at the door and knock/Peter in inntual kongpi hong ~ a | Peter knocked at the outer gate) (r:44.12.16/40.7.7/66.3.20/44.12.13) (q:draft)
Kiu = (t:n) (w:Corner/Angle) (d:Kiu, corner, written with a capital in the names of parts of the wall of Jerusalem: a Kiu is the Angle, and Kiu Kongpi the Corner Gate.) (e:a ~ Kongpi leh a Kuam Kongpi/a ~ panin siampi lian Eliashib’ inn kongkhak ciang | from the Angle to the door of the house of Eliashib the high priest/nitumna lam khua kulh ~ Kongpi dongin | as far as the Corner Gate of the city wall on the west) (b:kiu) (r:14.26.9/16.3.20/24.31.38) (q:draft)
kiuh = (t:v) (w:knock) (d:Form of kiu, knock, used before ciangin, leh and similar words.) (e:Piter in kong a ~ ciangin/Na ~ uh leh, hong hon’ ding hi | if you knock, it will be opened to you/ka ngaihno in ka kong hong ~ ka za hi | I hear my beloved knocking at my door/a ~ ciangin thakhatin ama ading kong hon’ thei | able to open the door for him at once when he knocks) (b:kiu) (r:44.12.13/40.7.7/22.5.2/42.12.36) (q:draft)
kiuhkeuh = (t:adv) (w:thoroughly/completely/utterly) (d:Intensifier placed after a verb or descriptive word: to the full, altogether; with lo it means not at all.) (e:kei hong silsiang ~ in la/amaute tui ~-in hing sitset uh hi | they stay fresh and green/note in amaute lawnthal mang ~-in | you must demolish them completely/paubaanna om ~ lo uh ahih manin | because there is no fault in them at all) (r:19.51.2/2.23.24/19.92.14/66.14.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiuhkeuhin = (t:adv) (w:utterly/completely/thoroughly) (d:Kiuhkeuh, thoroughly, with the adverb ending in: completely, to the full, after a verb of ruin or of flourishing.) (e:leitang pen gamkhing suak ~/amaute tui ~ hing sitset uh hi | they stay fresh and green/note in amaute lawnthal mang ~ | you must demolish them completely) (b:kiuhkeuh) (r:23.6.11/2.23.24/19.92.14) (q:draft)
kiukawi = (t:n) (w:corner) (d:The corner of a building; kiukawi bul suang is the cornerstone.) (e:a nung cianga ~ bul a suakkik) (s:kiu) (r:44.4.11) (q:draft)
kiukeu = (t:adv) (w:rounded/roundly) (d:Used after uk to describe a round hollow shape like a bowl or goblet.) (e:hai bangin uk ~ hi) (r:22.7.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiukiau = (t:adj) (w:sparkling/glittering) (d:Describes the crystal vault above the living creatures; whether it refers to the shine or to the arched shape is not confirmed.) (e:a kibawl a kuum ~ pian khat) (r:26.1.22) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiukiu = (t:v) (w:keep knocking/knock) (d:Kiu, knock, said twice: knock again and again at a door.) (e:a kong mah hong ~ lai a) (r:44.12.16) (q:draft)
kiuli = (t:n) (w:four corners/four quarters) (d:Kiu, corner, with li, four: the four corners or quarters; leitung kiuli is the four quarters of the earth.) (e:leitung ~ panin Judah mi) (r:23.11.12) (q:draft)
kiumcih = (t:v) (w:be besieged/be surrounded/be fortified) (d:Passive of umcih, besiege, with the prefix ki: be surrounded by an army; kulhpi tawh a kiumcih khuapi is a city surrounded with walls, a fortified city.) (e:Tua khuapi a ~ hi-in/kulhpi tawh a ~ khuapite luh zo-in | capturing the cities fortified with walls) (s:ki-umcip) (b:umcih) (r:26.4.3/27.11.15) (q:draft)
kiumcihna = (t:n) (w:siege) (d:Kiumcih, be besieged, with the noun suffix na: the besieging of a city.) (e:Jerusalem khuapi a ~ sal gega in/tua khuapi a ~ na lah nadingin | to show the siege of that city) (s:umcihna) (b:kiumcih) (r:26.4.7/26.4.2) (q:draft)
kiute = (t:n) (w:corners/angles) (d:Kiu, corner, with the plural te.) (e:Biakbuk nung lam ~’ adingin/tausang omna munte leh a ~ ah koih ding | to be placed on the towers and on the corners) (b:kiu) (r:2.26.23/2.36.28/14.26.15) (q:draft)
kiute = (t:n) (w:those who knock) (d:Kiu, knock, with the plural te; a kiute are the ones who knock at a door.) (e:A ~ khempeuh ading kongkhak) (b:kiu) (r:40.7.8/42.11.10) (q:draft)
kivaak = (t:v) (w:be fed/be provided for/get a living/be served) (d:Vaak, feed, with the prefix ki: feed oneself or be fed and supplied by others; a kivaak nading is what one has to live on.) (e:Lungdamna Thu pan a ~ nadingun/a tate an ngen tawm-a ~ hita leh | or his children living by begging food/mite’ khut tawh ~ ahi kei hi | he is not served by human hands/a ~ nading khempeuh nangawn a khia hi | she put in even all she had to live on) (s:kivak) (b:vaak) (r:46.9.14/19.37.25/44.17.25/42.21.4) (q:draft)
kivaikhak = (t:v) (w:be arranged/be ordered) (d:Passive of vaikhak, give an order or send word, with the prefix ki: be arranged or ordered beforehand.) (e:Tua bangin ~ hi zenzen leh) (b:vaikhak) (r:40.26.54) (q:draft, low confidence)
kivak = (t:v) (w:feed oneself/support oneself/live on) (d:Provide food for oneself, make a living; the food takes in or tawh, live on it, and kivak nading is what one has to live on.) (e:Kauphe leh gamlak khuaizu-in ~ hi/note bangin amah a ~ zawh kei leh | if he cannot support himself as you do/ama ~ nading nangawn sit loin a khia zo | she gave even what she had to live on, holding nothing back/gampa lak khuaizu in a ~ hi | he lived on wild honey) (s:kivaak) (r:41.1.6/3.25.35/41.12.44/40.3.4) (q:draft)
kivak = (t:v) (w:be lit/burn/shine) (d:Passive of vak, light, with the prefix ki: said of a lamp that is lit and gives light; kivak suak is be kept burning.) (e:a tawntungin a ~ suak theih nadingin/nang sungah cikmah hunin ~ nawn lo ding hi | it will never shine in you again) (s:kuang) (b:vak) (r:3.24.2/66.18.23) (q:draft)
kivakin = (t:v) (w:feeding/nourished/supporting) (d:Kivak, feed oneself, with the linking ending in: feeding oneself or others, or being nourished by something, which takes tawh.) (e:amau pumpi bek mah ~ ka tuute vak lo/nang na zuih thuhilhna a hoih tawh ~ | nourished by the good teaching you have followed/amau sum tawh amaute ~ a zui uh hi | they followed, supporting them out of their own money/lau loin amaute kham tak ~ | feeding themselves to the full without fear) (b:kivak) (r:26.34.8/54.4.6/42.8.3/65.1.12) (q:draft)
kivakin = (t:v) (w:burning/lit/shining) (d:Kivak, be lit, with the linking ending in: said of lamps that are alight.) (e:meivak sagih ~ a om uh hi) (b:kivak) (r:66.4.5) (q:draft)
kivakna = (t:n) (w:feeding/food supply/provision) (d:Kivak, feed, with the noun suffix na: the giving out or taking of food, or the place of feeding; nisim kivakna is the daily distribution of food.) (e:nisim ~ a ngah loh manun/Humpinelkai note an a ~ mun | the place where the lion cubs were fed/ganhing khempeuh in ~-in nei uh hi | all the creatures feed on it) (s:vaakna/vakna) (b:kivak) (r:44.6.1/34.2.11/19.80.13) (q:draft)
kivaksuak = (t:v) (w:be kept burning/stay alight) (d:Kivak, be lit, with suak, continue: said of a lamp that keeps giving light.) (e:a tawntungin a ~ theih nadingin) (r:3.24.2) (q:draft)
kivalh = (t:v) (w:be swallowed) (d:Passive of valh, swallow, with the prefix ki; kivalh tum is be swallowed up completely.) (e:Zawhna sungah sihna ~ tum zo hi) (b:valh) (r:46.15.54) (q:draft)
kivalhtum = (t:v) (w:be swallowed up/be destroyed) (d:Passive of valhtum, swallow up, with the prefix ki: be completely destroyed, said of a king and his people.) (e:mite khempeuh hong ~ ding hi) (b:valhtum) (r:10.17.16) (q:draft)
kivat = (t:v) (w:be struck down/be struck) (d:Passive of vat, strike, with the prefix ki; kivat tuk is be struck down and fall.) (e:amah ~ tukin a sihtheih nadingin/eite mai-ah amaute ~ tuk gawp taktak hi | they are truly being struck down before us) (s:kisat) (b:vat) (r:10.11.15/7.20.39) (q:draft)
kivattuk = (t:v) (w:be struck down/be cut down) (d:Passive of vattuk, strike down, with the prefix ki: be cut down in battle.) (e:amaute ~ gawp taktak hi) (s:kisatpuk) (b:vattuk) (r:7.20.39) (q:draft)
kivawh = (t:v) (w:be sown/be planted) (d:Passive of vawh, sow, with the prefix ki: of seed or of a word, be sown; of land, be sown with seed.) (e:amau sungah a ~ thu a lakkhiatte/a ~ ding khaici tungah a tuk leh | if it falls on seed that is to be sown/a kikho nai lo, khaici a ~ nai lo | not yet plowed, not yet sown with seed/a sin sunga ~ khaici a lakhia hi | he takes away the seed sown in his heart) (s:kituh/kisuan) (b:vawh) (r:41.4.15/3.11.37/5.21.4/40.13.19) (q:draft)
kivawh = (t:v) (w:be saddled/be loaded/be yoked) (d:Of a donkey, horse or ox, have a saddle, load or yoke put on its back.) (e:tuan’na a ~ la nih/a tungah nasepna kol a ~ ngei nai lo | on which a yoke has never been put/a pua van a ~ la nih tawh | with two donkeys loaded with goods) (b:vawh) (r:7.19.10/4.19.2/10.16.1) (q:draft)
kivawhin = (t:v) (w:being sown) (d:Kivawh, be sown, with the linking ending in.) (e:khaici kilemna tawh ~ a om hi) (b:kivawh) (r:59.3.18) (q:draft)
kivawhin = (t:v) (w:being tied/being fastened) (d:Kivawh, have something fastened on, with the linking ending in: said of a sheet let down with a rope tied at each corner.) (e:a kiu li-ah khau ~/a kiu ciatah khau ~ leitungah a hong kikhaisuk | let down to earth with a rope tied at each corner) (b:kivawh) (r:44.11.5/44.10.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiveei = (t:v) (w:quake/sway) (d:Said of the earth shaking; another spelling of kivei, sway.) (e:leitung kipumpei in, ~ a) (s:kivei/kiliing) (r:19.18.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
kivei = (t:v) (w:be waved) (d:Be waved to and fro before the Lord, said of the part of a sacrifice presented as a wave offering; a kivei sa-iik is the breast that was waved.) (e:a ~ sa-iik le a taklam phei/a ~ a sa-iik le a kipia a phei tawh | with the breast that was waved and the thigh that was presented/a iik a ~ theih nadingin | so that the breast may be waved) (s:kiveii) (r:4.18.18/2.29.27/4.6.20/3.7.30) (q:draft)
kivei = (t:v) (w:swing/sway/shake) (d:Move to and fro, said of the earth quaking or of men hanging on ropes; kivei suk kivei to is swing down and up.) (e:leitung kipumpei-in ~ a/khauhual tawh ~ suk ~ to uh hi | they swing down and up on ropes) (s:kiveei/kiliing) (r:19.18.7/18.28.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiveii = (t:v) (w:be waved) (d:Passive of veii, wave, with the prefix ki; a kiveii sa-iik is the breast that was waved before the Lord as an offering.) (e:a ~ sa-iik leh a taklam phei/a ~ a sa-iik leh a kipia a phei tawh | with the breast that was waved and the thigh that was presented/a ~ a iik leh a kipia a phei pen | the breast that is waved and the thigh that is presented/a iik a ~ theih nadingin | so that the breast may be waved) (s:kivei) (b:veii) (r:4.18.18/4.6.20/3.7.34/3.7.30) (q:draft)
kiveisuk = (t:v) (w:swing down/dangle down) (d:Kivei, swing, with suk, downward; paired with kiveito of men who swing down and up on ropes.) (e:khauhual tawh ~ kiveito uh hi) (b:kivei) (r:18.28.4) (q:draft)
kiveito = (t:v) (w:swing up/dangle up) (d:Kivei, swing, with to, upward; paired with kiveisuk of men who swing down and up on ropes.) (e:kiveisuk ~ uh hi) (b:kivei) (r:18.28.4) (q:draft)
kivel = (t:v) (w:be examined/be checked/be searched out) (d:Passive of vel, look over, with the prefix ki: be checked carefully or searched out.) (e:a ki-ap ciangin lim takin ~ a/leinuai-a leitung bulte a ~ theih ciang | when the foundations of the earth below can be searched out) (s:kikan/kisit) (b:vel) (r:15.8.34/24.31.37) (q:draft)
kivelsak = (t:v) (w:show oneself/have oneself examined) (d:Kivel, be examined, with sak: let someone examine one, said of a healed person who shows himself to the priest.) (e:Pai unla siampite va ~ un/Siampipa kiangah paisuak pahin amah ~ in | go straight to the priest and show yourself to him/siampipa kiangah va paisuak pahin va ~ inla | go straight to the priest and show yourself) (s:kilak) (b:kivel) (r:42.17.14/41.1.44/40.8.4) (q:draft)
kiveng = (t:v) (w:be settled/be decided) (d:Said of disputes that are brought to an end by a ruling; in the verse it is followed by sak.) (e:amau’ thu tawh ~ sak ding hi) (r:5.21.5) (q:draft)
kivengsak = (t:v) (w:be settled/be decided) (d:Kiveng, be settled, with sak: of disputes, be decided by the word of the priests.) (e:amau’ thu tawh ~ ding hi) (b:kiveng) (r:5.21.5) (q:draft)
kivial = (t:v) (w:coil around/entwine/be wound around) (d:Vial, encircle, with the prefix ki: of a snake or of roots, wind around something.) (e:khut tunga gul ~ a muh uh ciangin/suangtum lakah a zung a ~ | its roots wind among the rocks) (s:kancip) (b:vial) (r:44.28.4/18.8.17) (q:draft)
kivialgawp = (t:v) (w:entwine/coil around) (d:Kivial, wind around, with the intensifier gawp: said of roots that twist all around stones.) (e:suangtum lakah a zung a ~) (b:kivial) (r:18.8.17) (q:draft)
kivil = (t:v) (w:be guarded/be watched) (d:Passive of vil, watch, with the prefix ki; a kivil inn is a house kept under guard.) (e:a ~ inn khat sungah amaute) (s:kicing/kikemcing) (b:vil) (r:10.20.3) (q:draft)
kivom = (t:v) (w:be worn/be carried) (d:Passive of vom, carry on oneself, with the prefix ki; a kivom aite are charms worn on the body.) (e:paknamtui bungte leh a ~ aite) (b:vom) (r:23.3.20) (q:draft, low confidence)
kivui = (t:v) (w:be buried) (d:Passive of vui, bury, with the prefix ki: of a dead person, be laid in a grave; the place takes ah.) (e:David khuapi sungah ~ hi/Ibzan si a, Bethlehem-ah ~ hi | Ibzan died and was buried in Bethlehem/Jair si-in Kamon-ah ~ hi | Jair died and was buried in Kamon/La si ~ bang lelin | just as a dead donkey is buried/Judah mite’ ~ ngeina bangin | according to the burial custom of the Jews) (s:kiphum) (b:vui) (r:11.2.10/7.12.10/7.10.5/24.22.19/43.19.40) (q:draft)
kivuina = (t:n) (w:burial place/grave/burial) (d:Kivui, be buried, with the noun suffix na: the place where someone is buried, usually followed by mun, place, or han, tomb.) (e:amau’ ~ munah kei hong vui in/Pasian’ mipa a ~ hanah kei hong vui un | bury me in the grave where the man of God is buried/mi mawkmawkte’ ~ munah a paai hi | he threw it into the burial place of the common people/a ~ han in tuni dongin eite kiangah a om hi | his tomb is with us to this day) (s:hanphual/kiphumna) (b:kivui) (r:1.47.30/11.13.31/24.26.23/44.2.29) (q:draft)
kivuk = (t:v) (w:be covered/be buried/be filled in) (d:Passive of vuk, cover, with the prefix ki: be covered over with earth; kivuk dim, said of a valley, is be filled up.) (e:Mualkuam thuk khempeuh ~ dim ding a/lei tawh ~ hi | he is covered with earth/Kuam khempeuh ~ dim ding a | every valley shall be filled in) (b:vuk) (r:42.3.5/18.21.33/23.40.4) (q:draft)
kivukcip = (t:v) (w:be filled up/be blocked up/be buried) (d:Kivuk, be covered, with cip, completely: of a valley, be filled or blocked up; the English of this verse follows another reading.) (e:Hinnom kuam sung ~ ding a/Uzziah’ hun lai-a zin lin-a ~ mah bang ding | just as it was blocked up by the earthquake in the days of Uzziah) (s:kivukdim) (b:kivuk) (r:38.14.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
kivukdim = (t:v) (w:be filled in/be filled up) (d:Kivuk, be covered, with dim, full: said of a valley filled up with earth.) (e:Kuam thuk khempeuh ~ ding a) (s:kivukcip) (r:42.3.5) (q:draft)
kiza = (t:v) (w:be heard/sound) (d:Passive of za, hear, with the prefix ki: of a sound, voice or cry, be heard; awging kiza is a sound is heard.) (e:amau aw ~ lo hi/a kahna aw uh Zoar khua dongin ~ hi | their cry is heard as far as Zoar/tum theih awgingte khempeuh zong ~ nawn lo ding hi | the sound of all the instruments will be heard no more/ama awging hong ~ a | his voice is heard) (b:za) (r:19.19.3/24.50.22/24.48.4/26.26.13/18.37.4) (q:draft)
kizahhuaisak = (t:v) (w:be put to shame/be disgraced) (d:Passive of zahhuaisak, put to shame, with the prefix ki.) (e:a zongte ~ khin a) (s:kimaizumsak/kimindaisak) (a:kipahtawi) (b:zahhuaisak) (r:19.71.24) (q:draft)
kizahko = (t:v) (w:be insulted/be mocked) (d:Passive of zahko, mock, with the prefix ki: have insults thrown at one.) (e:Amah a ~ ciangin) (s:kikosiat/kinuihsan) (b:zahko) (r:60.2.23) (q:draft)
kizahkona = (t:n) (w:disgrace/reproach/insults) (d:Zahkona, ridicule, with the prefix ki: the state of being mocked, or the insulting of one another.) (e:ama mite a ~ lakhia ding hi/hazatna, lungsim kituah lohna, ~ | envy, discord, insults) (s:mindaina/simmawhna) (b:zahkona) (r:23.25.8/54.6.4) (q:draft)
kizahtak = (t:v) (w:be respected/be honored/be esteemed) (d:Passive of zahtak, respect, with the prefix ki: of a person or a name, be held in honor; hong kizahtak mahmah is highly esteemed.) (e:mite’ lakah ~ hi/na min siangtho ~ hen | may your holy name be honored/Daniel hong ~ mahmah pa aw | Daniel, you who are highly esteemed/kisimmawhna leh ~ lohna tampi piangsak ding hi | it will cause much contempt and disrespect/Misiangthote kikhopna sungah a ~ Pasian | God who is revered in the assembly of the holy ones) (s:kipahtawi) (a:kisimmawh) (b:zahtak) (r:20.31.23/27.10.11/40.6.9/17.1.18/19.89.6) (q:draft)
kizahtakbawl = (t:v) (w:be honored/be treated with respect) (d:Kizahtak, be respected, with bawl, treat: be treated with honor by others.) (e:note hong ~ na kisa uh hi) (s:kipahtawi) (a:kisimmawhbawl) (b:kizahtak) (r:46.4.10) (q:draft)
kizahtakin = (t:v) (w:being respected/being honored) (d:Kizahtak, be respected, with the linking ending in: being respected, followed by another verb.) (e:~ pahtawina a ngah hi) (b:kizahtak) (r:40.13.57/41.6.4) (q:draft)
kizahtakna = (t:n) (w:fear/reverence/respect) (d:The fear or respect in which someone is held; Topa a kizahtakna is the fear of the Lord, and khat leh khat kizahtakna is respect for one another.) (e:tungah Topa a ~ hong om hi/Topa a ~ in siang a, kip tawntung hi | the fear of the Lord is pure and endures forever/Note hong ~ leh note hong kikihtakna | the fear of you and the dread of you/khat leh khat ~ om nawn lo hi | there is no longer any respect for one another) (s:kikihtakna/kihtakna) (a:simmawhna) (b:zahtakna) (r:14.20.29/19.19.9/1.9.2/23.33.8) (q:draft)
kizak = (t:v) (w:be heard/be reported) (d:Form of kiza, be heard, used before ciangin, hun, nawn loh and other dependent endings.) (e:Izipt gamah hih thu a ~ ciangin/Khazih’ min a ~ ngeilohna munah | where the name of Christ has never been heard/David’ kampaute a ~ ciangin | when what David said was heard/a hawkna a ~ nawn loh nadingin | so that his roar would no longer be heard/galdona aw a ~ hun ka tung sak ding hi | I will bring the time when the battle cry is heard) (b:kiza) (r:23.23.5/26.19.9/45.15.20/9.17.31/24.49.2) (q:draft)
kizakim = (t:v) (w:be equal/be of equal rank) (d:Be equal to or on the same level as another, used with tawh; of two workers, count the same) (e:Pasian tawh a ~ theihna dingin/vawh pa le tuibuak pa a ~ ahi hi | the one who plants and the one who waters are equal) (r:50.2.6/46.3.8) (q:draft)
kizakim = (t:v) (w:be heard everywhere/be heard all around) (d:Be heard everywhere, said of news: kiza be heard with kim, all around) (e:gam khempeuhah ama thu ~ hi) (s:kizaza) (r:42.4.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
kizaksak = (t:v) (w:be informed/be told) (d:Be informed or told of something: zaksak make hear with the passive prefix ki) (e:thu hong ~ ciangin) (b:zaksak) (r:44.23.30) (q:draft)
kizal = (t:v) (w:be spread out/be outstretched) (d:of wings or a covering, stretched out wide; a kizal is also a thing spread overhead, a canopy) (e:kherubte’ khate ~ a/gunkuang puan ~ thei lo hi | the sail cannot be spread/~ ama khate in i gam hong hu ding | his outspread wings will cover our land/tung khempeuh ah a ~ khat om ding hi | over everything there will be a canopy) (b:zal) (r:11.6.27/23.8.8/23.33.23/23.4.5) (q:draft)
kizalhtam = (t:v) (w:be levelled/be made a plain) (d:of rough and stony ground, be laid out flat) (e:suanghum omna munte ~ ding hi) (s:kitamkim) (b:zalhtam) (r:23.40.4) (q:draft)
kizalin = (t:v) (w:outspread/spread out) (d:kizal be spread out with the linking ending in; kha a kizalin is the wings when spread out, the wingspan) (e:kha a ~ tong sawmnih ahi hi) (b:kizal) (r:14.3.11) (q:draft)
kizalsak = (t:v) (w:stretch out/spread wide) (d:kizal be spread out with the causative sak, said of tent curtains) (e:na tenna puanbukte ~ in) (b:kizal) (r:23.54.2) (q:draft)
kizan = (t:v) (w:be stretched out/stretch out/straighten up) (d:Be stretched out, said of a hand or arm, or of the body, straighten up; a kizan khut is an outstretched arm) (e:kei lamah khut khat hong ~ a/a pum neukha beek a ~ thei kei hi | she could not straighten her body at all/minam khempeuh daanpiak nadingin a ~ ahi hi | it is stretched out to punish all nations/a ~ khut leh thukhenna nasep lian tawh | with an outstretched arm and mighty acts of judgment) (s:kizankhia) (r:26.2.9/42.13.11/23.14.26/2.6.6) (q:draft)
kizan = (t:v) (w:be crushed/be broken to pieces) (d:Be smashed to pieces, often as kizan gawp; of the heart, be broken) (e:leivui bangin ~ gawp ding hi/kapin ka lungsim ~ nading na hih uh hiam | are you weeping to break my heart) (s:kizangawp/kitamzan/kisuzan) (r:42.20.18/40.21.44/44.21.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
kizang = (t:v) (w:be used/be practised/be the custom) (d:Be used: zang use with the passive prefix ki; kizang lo is not used, not the custom, and a kizang thei is useful) (e:munah thuman ~ lo a/nauzaw piak ding ko’ gamah ~ lo hi | giving the younger one is not the custom in our land/na dangin ~ thei ding a | it may be used for other things/kei leh nang adingin a ~ thei ding mi | a man who can be useful to me and to you) (s:kimang) (b:zang) (r:23.59.14/2.27.19/1.29.26/3.7.24/57.1.11) (q:draft)
kizanga = (t:v) (w:used/being used) (d:kizang be used, with the linking ending a) (e:do nadingin ~ a kisusia gawp) (b:kizang) (r:24.33.4) (q:draft)
kizangawp = (t:v) (w:be crushed/be broken to pieces) (d:kizan be crushed with gawp, thoroughly) (e:mi khempeuh ~ ding a/a deen’ khak peuhmahte ~ ding hi | anyone it falls on will be crushed) (s:kitamzan/kisuzan) (b:kizan) (r:42.20.18/40.21.44) (q:draft)
kizangin = (t:v) (w:be used) (d:kizang be used with the linking ending in: being used, and then the next action follows) (e:a nam tuamtuamte ~ a kizeem suangphah) (b:kizang) (r:17.1.6) (q:draft)
kizangsa = (t:adj) (w:used/made use of) (d:kizang be used, with sa already) (e:thong dingin a ~) (b:kizang) (r:24.37.15) (q:draft)
kizangsak = (t:v) (w:be used up/be spent/be wasted) (d:kizang be used with sak; a mawkna-in kizangsak is be used to no purpose, wasted) (e:a mawkna-in a ~ hiam/Paknamtui bang dingin a mawkna-in ~ hiam | why was the perfume wasted) (b:kizang) (r:40.26.8/41.14.4) (q:draft)
kizankhia = (t:v) (w:be stretched out/outstretched) (d:zankhia stretch out, with the prefix ki; said of the arm) (e:na khut ~ tawh vantung teng) (s:kizan) (b:zankhia) (r:24.32.17) (q:draft)
kizanlai = (t:v) (w:be still stretched out/be still upraised) (d:of the hand, kizan, be stretched out, with lai, still) (e:ama khut ~ hi/a hehna damzo nai loin ama khut ~ hi | his anger is not turned away, his hand is still upraised) (r:23.9.12/23.5.25) (q:draft)
kizap = (t:v) (w:be blown/be fanned) (d:zap fan with the prefix ki; pum a kizap is the bellows are worked) (e:Nakpi takin pum a ~ hangin) (b:zap) (r:24.6.29) (q:draft)
kizapkhiat = (t:v) (w:be blown away) (d:kizap be fanned with khiat, out, away: be driven off like chaff by the wind) (e:Ansi bangin hong ~ ma) (b:kizap) (r:36.2.2) (q:draft)
kizaptel = (t:v) (w:be limber/be agile) (d:said of arms; in the verse followed by sak) (e:a khutte ~ sak hi) (r:1.49.24) (q:draft, low confidence)
kizaptelsak = (t:v) (w:make limber/make agile) (d:kizaptel with the causative sak; said of arms) (e:a khutte ~ hi) (b:kizaptel) (r:1.49.24) (q:draft, low confidence)
kizapzap = (t:v) (w:be blown again and again/keep being fanned) (d:kizap be blown with zap doubled for a repeated action, said of bellows) (e:Pum a ~ hangin a mawkna a suak hi) (r:24.6.29) (q:draft)
kizasak = (t:v) (w:be made heard/be reported/let be heard) (d:Be made heard: zasak make hear with the prefix ki; of a voice or sound, let it be heard, and of news, be reported) (e:amah phatna aw ~ un/tua ni mahmahin kumpipa kiangah ~ hi | was reported to the king that very day/amau’ innte panin kahna aw ~ in | let a cry be heard from their houses/Kote lakah na aw hong ~ kei in | do not let your voice be heard among us) (b:zasak) (r:19.66.8/17.9.11/24.18.22/7.18.25) (q:draft)
kizasakin = (t:v) (w:making heard/causing to be heard/proclaiming) (d:kizasak be made heard, let be heard, with the linking ending in) (e:giahphual khempeuhah thu ~/ama liatna minthan’na aw ~ | causing his majestic voice to be heard) (b:kizasak) (r:2.36.6/23.30.30) (q:draft)
kizat = (t:v) (w:be used) (d:form of kizang used before nading, ciangin and similar words; kizat nading is what a thing is to be used for) (e:sisan a ~ ciangin thu suak thei pan/A ~ nading bangmah om nawn lo a | it is no longer of any use/thuman bekbek a ~ nading mun | a place where only righteousness is practised/Ka biakinn a ~ nading ngeina om khempeuh | all the regulations for the use of my temple) (s:kimang) (b:zat) (r:58.9.18/23.54.16/40.5.13/61.3.13/26.44.5) (q:draft)
kizatna = (t:n) (w:use/usage) (d:the use made of something, or the thing in which a material is used) (e:savun a ~ na khatpeuh peuh tungah/buan-a ~ inn sunga teeng mite | those who live in houses where clay is used/Thukham ~ sungah na khempeuh | in the practice of the law, everything) (s:zatna) (b:kizat) (r:3.13.51/18.4.19/58.9.22) (q:draft, low confidence)
kizato = (t:v) (w:be heard up to/rise up) (d:said of a sound; kiza be heard, with to upward) (e:awging vantung dongah ~ hi) (b:kiza) (r:9.5.12) (q:draft)
kizawh = (t:v) (w:be finished/be completed) (d:passive of zawh finish, said of work, a harvest or a building) (e:nasep a ~ loh nading/nasep a ~ mateng amaute huh uh hi | they helped them until the work was finished/anlak a ~ ma-in lo khawhkik hun tungin | before the harvest is finished, ploughing time comes again/Biakna tau a ~ khit ciangin | when the altar has been completed) (s:kikhit) (b:zawh) (r:16.6.9/14.8.16/14.29.34/30.9.13/26.43.18) (q:draft)
kizawh = (t:v) (w:be subdued/be conquered) (d:passive of zawh overcome, said of a land or people) (e:note mai-ah tua gam a ~ leh) (s:guallel) (a:gualzo) (b:zawh) (r:4.32.29) (q:draft)
kizawhgawp = (t:v) (w:be utterly defeated) (d:kizawh be overcome, with the intensifier gawp) (e:galte a ~ khit ciangin) (b:kizawh) (r:38.14.16) (q:draft)
kizawhna = (t:n) (d:in Eufrates gun lang khat a kizawhna gam, the territory beyond the Euphrates; perhaps kizawh be subdued with the noun suffix na, the land that was conquered, meaning not confirmed) (e:lang khat a ~ gam sunga om mite) (b:kizawh) (r:15.4.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
kizawn = (t:v) (w:say to one another/urge one another/invite one another) (d:with khat leh khat, one another; said of people calling each other to come along and hear) (e:khat leh khat ~ uh hi) (r:26.33.30) (q:draft, low confidence)
kizawn = (t:v) (w:become poor/come to poverty) (d:in kizawn’lawh, become poor as a result: zawn, form of zawng poor, with the prefix ki and lawh) (e:letsong pia leeng ~’lawh a) (b:zawn) (r:20.22.16) (q:draft)
kizawng = (t:v) (w:be carried) (d:be carried along by bearers; in these verses Solomon comes carried on a royal litter, luai) (e:kumpi luai-in hong ~ hi/Kumpi Solomon hong ~ hi | King Solomon comes carried) (s:kipua) (r:22.3.7/22.3.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
kizawngsak = (t:v) (w:pretend to be poor/make oneself poor) (d:zawng poor with the prefix ki and sak: make oneself out to be poor; the opposite in the verse is kihausak) (e:hau napi-in ~ uh hi) (a:kihausak) (r:20.13.7) (q:draft)
kizawnlawh = (t:v) (w:become poor/come to poverty) (d:become poor as a result of what one does; zawn poor, with lawh as a consequence) (e:letsong pia leeng ~ a) (a:kihauhlawh) (r:20.22.16) (q:draft)
kizaza = (t:v) (w:be heard everywhere/be heard again and again/be widely heard) (d:kiza be heard, with za doubled to show that it goes on or happens widely; of a name, be famed) (e:na min ~ a/thuman tecite’ kam ~ ding hi | the word of true witnesses will go on being heard) (s:kizakim) (b:zaza) (r:22.1.3/20.21.28) (q:draft)
kizazo = (t:v) (w:can be heard) (d:kiza be heard, with zo be able) (e:a pualamah a ~ kei hi) (b:kiza) (r:25.3.8) (q:draft)
kize = (t:see) <kize-et>
kize-et = (t:v) (w:be tested/be tried/be put to the test/be tempted) (d:Be tested or tried, as metal is tried in fire, or be tempted: ze-et test with the passive prefix ki) (e:mihing ahih leh phatna tawh ~ hi/Kham leh ngunte, mei sungah ~ a | gold and silver are tested in the fire/A masa-in ~ phot ding a | they must first be tested/ahoih lo tawh Pasian a ~ zo kei hi | God cannot be tempted by evil) (s:kisit) (r:20.27.21/20.17.3/54.3.10/59.1.13) (q:draft)
kize-etna = (t:n) (w:testing/test/trial) (d:kize-et be tested with the noun suffix na) (e:na upna uh hong ~ na thuakzawh/amaute pen Israelte a ~ hi | they were there for the testing of the Israelites/note’ upna hong ~-in gimna haksate na thuak | you suffer hardships as a testing of your faith) (s:ze-etna) (r:59.1.3/7.3.4/60.4.12) (q:draft)
kize-etsa = (t:adj) (w:tested/tried) (d:that has been tested; ze-et test with the prefix ki and sa, already done) (e:a ~ suang, a manpha innkiu suang) (r:23.28.16) (q:draft)
kizeel = (t:v) (w:spread/spread abroad) (d:of news or a smell, go out over a whole area) (e:ka paknamtui hong ~ hi/ama thu in Galile gam sung khempeuh ~ hi | news of him spread through all Galilee/Zeisu thu ~ semsem a | the news about Jesus spread all the more/a kiim-a minam khempeuh lakah ~ hi | it spread among all the surrounding nations) (s:kizel/kizelh) (b:zeel) (r:22.1.12/41.1.28/42.5.15/11.4.31) (q:draft)
kizeelin = (t:v) (w:spreading/spreading out) (d:kizeel spread, with the linking ending in) (e:taklam leh veilamah nangmah ~/note kiangah a piang mah bangin ~ | spreading just as it happened among you/a kimkot gam khempeuh ah ~ a thang hi | it spread and became known through all the surrounding country) (s:kizelin/kizelhin) (b:kizeel) (r:23.54.3/53.3.1/42.4.14) (q:draft)
kizeelsak = (t:v) (w:spread/spread abroad/make known everywhere) (d:kizeel spread, with the causative sak: make news or a smell go out over a whole area) (e:khua sung khempeuh thu a ~ hi/a thu genthangin a ~ hi | he talked about it and spread the news/ko hangin mun khempeuh ah a ~ | spreads it everywhere through us) (s:kizelsak/thangsak) (b:kizeel) (r:42.8.39/41.1.45/47.2.14) (q:draft)
kizeem = (t:v) (w:be dressed/be adorned/adorn oneself/be decorated) (d:Be dressed in fine clothes or adorn oneself, and of a thing, be decorated with something: zeem with the prefix ki) (e:puan hoih tawh ~ a/suangmanpha a pawlpawl tawh ~ hi | were decorated with every kind of precious stone/tua unok khat bangin ~ lo hi | was not dressed like one of these lilies/tang lai-in tua bangin a ~ uh hi | in the past they adorned themselves in this way) (s:kizem/kizep) (b:zeem) (r:42.7.25/66.21.19/40.6.29/60.3.5) (q:draft)
kizeemin = (t:v) (w:adorned/being adorned) (d:kizeem be adorned, with the linking ending in) (e:kep suangmanpha tawh ~) (s:kizemin) (b:kizeem) (r:66.17.4) (q:draft)
kizeemsa = (t:see) <kizeemsa-in>
kizeemsa-in = (t:v) (w:adorned/dressed) (d:having been adorned; kizeem with sa already and the linking ending in) (e:a pasal ading a ~ a om) (r:66.21.2) (q:draft)
kizeemte = (t:n) (w:decorations/adorned things) (d:things that are decorated; kizeem be adorned, with the plural te) (e:biakinn na ~ khempeuh) (b:kizeem) (r:19.74.6) (q:draft)
kizekaisak = (t:v) (w:delay/put off) (d:zekaisak make late, with the prefix ki) (e:Amaute a huh ding ~ ding ahi hiam) (b:zekaisak) (r:42.18.7) (q:draft)
kizel = (t:v) (w:spread/be spread abroad) (d:Of news, a message or a reputation, go out through a whole region) (e:tua gam khempeuh ah a ~ hi/Pasian’ thu in khangto a, a ~ semsem hi | the word of God grew and spread more and more/leitung gam khempeuh ah ~ ahih ciangin | because it has spread through all the world/gam khempeuh ah ama minthan’na ~ hi | his fame spread through all the provinces) (s:kizeel/kizelh) (b:zel) (r:44.13.49/44.6.7/44.12.24/45.1.8/17.9.4) (q:draft)
kizelh = (t:v) (w:spread/be spread) (d:of mould, disease or news, extend over a wider area) (e:inn sungah a natna a ~ leh/tua inn kawm tungah a natna a ~ leh | if the mold has spread on the walls of the house/inn sungah natna a ~ kei leh | if the mold has not spread in the house/ka min leitung khempeuh ah a ~ nading | so that my name may spread in all the earth) (s:kizel/kizeel) (b:zelh) (r:3.14.44/44.4.17/3.14.39/3.14.48/45.9.17) (q:draft)
kizelhin = (t:v) (w:spreading/having spread) (d:kizelh spread, with the linking ending in) (e:A natna pen puan tungah ~) (s:kizeelin/kizelin) (b:kizelh) (r:3.13.51) (q:draft)
kizelhthang = (t:v) (w:spread widely/spread abroad) (d:Spread out widely in every direction, said of a people growing in number) (e:~ zaw uh hi/amaute tampi pha zaw-in ~ zaw uh hi | they multiplied more and spread more) (s:kizelthang) (r:2.1.12) (q:draft)
kizelin = (t:v) (w:spreading/being spread abroad) (d:Spreading, said of news, a teaching or a people: kizel spread with the linking ending in) (e:thu ~ a khang semsem hi/tua thu Judah mite lakah ~ | that story spread among the Jews/taklam le veilamah nangmah ~ | you spreading out to the right and to the left/Pasian’ thu ~ hong khang semsem hi | the word of God spread and kept growing) (s:kizeelin/kizelhin) (b:kizel) (r:44.12.24/40.28.15/23.54.3/44.6.7) (q:draft)
kizelsak = (t:v) (w:spread/cause to spread) (d:kizel be spread, with the causative sak) (e:Khrih thu theihna a ~ dingin) (s:kizeelsak) (b:kizel) (r:47.2.14) (q:draft)
kizelthang = (t:v) (w:spread out/be scattered/spread abroad) (d:of peoples or descendants spreading over the earth in every direction) (e:tung panin leitungah minamte ~ hi/leitaw lamah na ~ ding uh hi | you will spread out to the south/Tua khit ciangin Kanaan mite ~ hi | afterwards the Canaanites scattered/amaute tampi phazaw-in ~ zaw uh hi | they multiplied more and spread more) (s:kizelhthang) (r:1.10.32/1.28.14/1.10.18/2.1.12) (q:draft)
kizem = (t:v) (w:be adorned/be decorated/be embroidered/adorn oneself) (d:Be adorned or decorated: zem with the prefix ki; of cloth, be embroidered, and of people, put on ornaments) (e:kuamah ~ lo uh hi/kham peek kiseekin khau-in ~ hi | gold sheets were hammered and worked in as thread/a ~ a kiphan puan hoihte | fine embroidered and woven clothes/phim tawh kikhui-in a ~ kawnggak khat | a sash embroidered with needlework) (s:kizeem/kizep) (b:zem) (r:2.33.4/66.18.16/2.39.3/26.16.18/2.28.39) (q:draft)
kizemin = (t:v) (w:being adorned/dressed/decorated) (d:connective form of kizem, adorning oneself or being adorned with fine clothes, gold or jewels) (e:kumpi puan tawh ~ om uh hi/Ofir gam khamte tawh ~ kumpinu a ding hi | the queen stands adorned with gold of Ophir/saihadial puan tawh ~ | dressed in fine linen/gamlak lonona munte tuuhon tawh ~ | the meadows are clothed with flocks) (s:kizeemin) (b:kizem) (r:11.22.10/19.45.9/14.5.12/19.65.13) (q:draft)
kizemsak = (t:v) (w:adorn oneself) (d:kizem be adorned, with the causative sak) (e:puansilhna ahi pualam ~ loin) (b:kizem) (r:60.3.3) (q:draft)
kizemte = (t:adj) (w:embroidered/decorated/carved) (d:kizem with plural -te, said of several decorated things, as embroidered cloth or carved work) (e:saihadial puan ~ tawh na puankhai kibawl/biakinn na a ~ khempeuh | all the carved work of the temple) (b:kizem) (r:26.27.7/19.74.6) (q:draft)
kizen = (t:adj) (w:diligent/industrious/hardworking) (d:careful and busy at work) (e:a khangno mipa a ~ mi hi/a gamtat siangtho, inn nasep a ~ | pure in conduct, busy with the work of the house) (s:thanuam) (a:thadah) (r:11.11.28/56.2.5) (q:draft)
kizen = (t:v) (w:be cut into strands) (d:in Exodus 39:3 only, of beaten gold made into thread; sense uncertain) (e:kham peek kiseekin khau-in ~ hi) (r:2.39.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
kizep = (t:v) (w:adorn oneself/deck oneself/dress up) (d:put ornaments or fine things on oneself; na kizep nading, for your adornment) (e:kham tawh na ~ liatluat hangin/mo thaknu a suangmanphate tawh a ~ mah bangin | as a bride adorns herself with her jewels/na ~ nading zong ngun tawh bawl ni | let us make your adornment with silver too/a hoihpenin a ~ ciangin zong | even when he was dressed in his best) (s:kizem/kizeem) (b:zep) (r:24.4.30/28.2.13/23.61.10/22.1.11/40.6.29) (q:draft)
kizepna = (t:n) (w:ornament/adornment/jewelry/decoration) (d:a thing worn or set to make beautiful; also the setting of a stone) (e:~ a manphate nang kong pia a/na hoih nadingin ~ hi ding hi | they will be an ornament for your beauty/a kiphatsakpih uh ~ a manphate | the precious jewelry they took pride in/~ kham bilbah tawh kibang hi | is like an ornament, a gold earring) (s:zepna) (b:kizep) (r:26.16.11/20.3.22/26.7.20/20.25.12) (q:draft)
kizepnate = (t:n) (w:ornaments/jewelry/finery) (d:Ornaments or jewelry worn on the body: kizepna ornament with the plural te) (e:amau’ ~ suahkhia uh hi/a manpha na ~ zong hong laksak ding | they will also take your precious jewelry/Nungak khat in a ~ a mangngilh thei hiam | can a young woman forget her jewelry/kham leh ngun kibawl ~ | jewelry made of gold and silver) (s:zepnate) (b:kizepna) (r:2.33.6/26.23.26/24.2.32/26.16.17) (q:draft)
kizia = (t:v) (w:stretch out/sprawl/lounge) (d:lay the body down at ease, as a person lounging on a couch or a lion settling down to rest) (e:tutphah nip tungah a ~ hiathiat/Humpinelkai bangin ~-in a lumsuk hi | like a lion he stretches out and lies down) (r:30.6.4/1.49.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
kizial = (t:v) (w:be rolled up/roll up) (d:passive of zial: be rolled like a scroll; lai kizial is a rolled book, a scroll) (e:laidal bangin vantungte ~ ding hi/tua khut in tua lai ~ hong phel a | that hand unrolled the scroll/Van in laidal zial bangin ~ mang hi | the sky rolled away like a scroll) (s:kihial) (b:zial) (r:23.34.4/26.2.10/66.6.14) (q:draft)
kizialcip = (t:v) (w:be rolled up/be rolled shut) (d:kizial be rolled, with cip tight) (e:lai kigelhin a ~ khit ciangin) (b:kizial) (r:66.5.1) (q:draft)
kizialin = (t:v) (w:being rolled up/rolled up) (d:kizial be rolled up, with the linking ending in) (e:bangin vanpi ~ maimang a/a tuamtuak a, ~ a om a mu hi | he saw it lying apart, rolled up) (b:kizial) (r:66.6.14/43.20.7) (q:draft)
kizialto = (t:v) (w:roll upward/billow up/rise up) (d:kizial roll, with to upward, said of smoke rising in rolls) (e:van lamah ~ uh hi/Pasian’ mite’ thungetna van lam manawhin ~ hi | the prayers of God's people rose up toward heaven) (b:kizial) (r:23.9.18/66.8.4) (q:draft)
kizim = (t:v) (w:be hemmed/be edged) (d:of the opening of a garment, be bound round with a woven edge so that it does not tear) (e:a kigan tawh a ~) (r:2.28.32) (q:draft, low confidence)
kizo = (t:v) (w:be defeated/be subdued/be overcome) (d:Be defeated or overcome, said of enemies, a people or a ruler: zo overcome with the passive prefix ki) (e:Geel siamna tawh galte ~ a/tua hunin Israel mite ~ hi | at that time the Israelites were subdued/kamnem-a pauna tawh aana neite ~ thei hi | those in authority can be won over by gentle speech/nih pha leh ~ zo lo hi | if there are two they cannot be overcome) (s:guallel) (a:gualzo) (b:zo) (r:20.24.6/9.7.13/14.13.18/20.25.15/21.4.12) (q:draft)
kizo = (t:v) (w:be finished/be completed) (d:Be finished or completed, said of a building or a piece of work) (e:ni-in a inn ~ hi/kote’ Pasian’ huhna tawh hih nasep ~ ahihna | that this work was done with the help of our God/thu khempeuh ~ khin zo cih a theih ciangin | knowing that everything was now finished/a kulhte ~ khin leh | if its walls are completed) (s:kikhit) (b:zo) (r:15.6.15/14.8.16/16.6.16/43.19.28/15.4.16) (q:draft)
