kizolsak = (t:v) (w:be led astray/let oneself be enticed) (d:zol entice with the prefix ki and sak; kuamah kizolsak kei un is do not let anyone lead you astray) (e:kuamah ~ kei un) (r:62.3.7) (q:draft)
kizolsak = (t:v) (w:be smeared/be covered) (d:of a sword, be coated or made slick with fat) (e:kal thau tawh a ~ bang ding hi) (r:23.34.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
kizom = (t:v) (w:be joined/be connected/be attached/join) (d:be joined to or connected with something, usually after tawh; also belong to, have to do with or share in) (e:amau’ pawl tawh ka ~ kei ding hi/taamtaak singte-in a inn tawh ~ hi | they were attached to the house with cedar beams/A hiang pen a gui tawh ~ kei leh | if the branch is not joined to the vine/Khrih tawh a ~ khempeuh | all who are joined to Christ) (s:kituah) (a:kikhenkhia) (b:zom) (r:1.49.6/14.3.12/11.6.10/43.15.4/46.15.22) (q:draft)
