kizoma = (t:v) (w:connected/in succession) (d:kizom be joined, with the linking ending a; in the verse of descent from the fathers) (e:a pate tawh ~ piang mi) (b:kizom) (r:45.9.5) (q:draft)
kizomin = (t:adv) (w:joined together/in order/in succession) (d:kizom with the linking ending in; a kizom a kizomin, one thing after another in order) (e:inn khempeuh in ~ khang a/Piter in a kizom a ~ a gen-inah | Peter told it in order, one thing after another/tual pualam kawm tawh ~ inndei sawmthum om a | there were thirty rooms adjoining the outer wall of the court) (s:kizomzomin/banbanin) (b:kizom) (r:49.2.21/44.11.4/26.40.17) (q:draft)
