kizomsuak = (t:v) (w:continue/endure) (d:go on without a break, said of a reign) (e:tu-in na ukna ~ lo ding a) (b:zomsuak) (r:9.13.14) (q:draft)
kizomtawm = (t:v) (w:join oneself to/yoke oneself to) (d:attach oneself to someone of one's own accord, used with tawh) (e:Baal tawh Israel mite va ~ hi/Peor-a Baal tawh a va ~ na mite | your people who joined themselves to the Baal of Peor) (r:4.25.3/4.25.5) (q:draft)
kizomte = (t:n) (w:those joined to/those who belong to/those united with) (d:kizom with plural te, after tawh: the people connected with someone) (e:amaute tawh a ~ khempeuh/Topa tawh a ~ pen | those who are united with the Lord/tua nu tawh a ~ khempeuh | all who belonged to her) (b:kizom) (r:6.2.13/46.6.17/6.6.25) (q:draft)
kizomto = (t:v) (w:continue upward) (d:kizom be joined or continue, with to upward) (e:a tungnung dongin ~ hi) (b:kizom) (r:26.41.7) (q:draft)
kizomzomin = (t:adv) (w:in order/consecutively) (d:one thing following another) (e:a thu a ~ nang a dingin) (s:kizomin/banbanin) (r:42.1.3) (q:draft)
kizong = (t:v) (w:be searched/be sought/be looked for) (d:Be searched for or looked for, and of a place, be searched: zong seek with the passive prefix ki) (e:Judah gamah mawhna ~ ding a/lai manphate a kisen’na innte sung ~ hi | the houses where the valuable records were kept were searched/Ka to kumpipa’ adingin nungakno khat ~ hen | let a young woman be sought for my lord the king/Israel gamah khialhna ~ ding a | guilt will be searched for in Israel) (s:kikan) (b:zong) (r:24.50.20/15.6.1/11.1.2) (q:draft)
Kizongkhia = (t:v) (w:be sought out/be sought after) (d:zong seek with the prefix ki and khia out; used as a name given to Zion, Sought After) (e:nang pen a ~, a kinusia lo khuapi) (r:23.62.12) (q:draft)
kizop = (t:v) (w:be joined/be attached/be connected) (d:form of kizom used before words such as theih and khawm; kei tawh na hong kizop uh is you remain joined to me) (e:A ~ khawm theih nadingin/Kei tawh na hong ~ uh a | if you remain joined to me/Adam tawh a ~ manin mi khempeuh si a | because they are joined to Adam all die/kei tawh na ~ kei uhleh | unless you remain joined to me) (b:zop) (r:2.28.7/43.15.7/46.15.22/43.15.4) (q:draft)
kizop = (t:v) (w:continue/be carried on) (d:go on without a break, as a family line) (e:khang a ~ theih nadingin/nangma mai-ah a ~ tawntung theih nadingin | so that it may continue forever before you/ama migitna a ~ paisuak theih nadingin | so that his kindness may continue) (b:zop) (r:40.22.24/13.17.27/45.11.22) (q:draft)
kizopkhak = (t:v) (w:have contact with/be involved with) (d:Have contact or dealings with something, used after tawh; built on kizop be joined) (e:a sia peuhmah tawh na ~ hetloh) (r:45.16.19) (q:draft)
kizopna = (t:n) (w:relationship/connection/fellowship/alliance) (d:a being joined together with others, by dealings, marriage or trade) (e:kuamah tawh ~ nei lo uh hi/Ahab tawh numei-a ~ bawl hi | he made a marriage alliance with Ahab/sum lei sum zuakna-in ~ hong nei uh hi | they had trading relations with you/note in kei tawh ~ hangin | because of your fellowship with me) (s:kipawlna) (b:kizop) (r:7.18.28/14.18.1/26.27.23/50.4.14) (q:draft)
kizopsak = (t:v) (w:continue/preserve/keep going) (d:kizop be joined with sak, cause, make a line go on; suan-le-khak kizopsak is preserve the family line) (e:i pa tawh suan-le-khak i ~ theih nadingin) (b:kizop) (r:1.19.32/1.19.34) (q:draft)
kizosak = (t:v) (w:let prevail/let overcome) (d:allow someone or something to win, in the verses always negated, do not let them prevail) (e:gitlohna ~ kei unla/Mi, ~ ke’n | do not let man prevail/mite ~ kei in | do not let men prevail) (b:kizo) (r:45.12.21/19.9.19/14.14.11) (q:draft)
kizuak = (t:v) (w:be sold/sell oneself) (d:Be sold, or sell oneself to someone: zuak sell with the prefix ki) (e:sila-a ~ mi khat/Gitta nga in dangkasan peek nih tawh ~ | five sparrows are sold for two pennies/nangma tungah amahmah hong ~ leh | if he sells himself to you/sumbuka ~ khempeuh teldot loin na ne un | eat everything sold in the market without asking) (a:kilei) (b:zuak) (r:19.105.17/12.7.16/42.12.6/3.25.39/46.10.25) (q:draft)
kizuakin = (t:v) (w:being sold/be sold) (d:kizuak, be sold, with the linking suffix in, which joins it to the next action: being sold for a price) (e:paknamtui dangka za thumin ~/annel lawh khat shekel khatin ~ | a measure of fine flour being sold for a shekel/sathau namtui ngun peek za thumin ~ | this perfume being sold for three hundred silver coins) (b:kizuak) (r:41.14.5/12.7.16/43.12.5) (q:draft)
kizuakna = (t:n) (w:selling/sale) (d:kizuak, be sold, with the noun suffix na: selling; van kizuakna phualpi is the place where goods are sold, the market square) (e:van ~ phualpi-ah pilna hong kiko hi) (s:zuakna) (a:leina) (b:kizuak) (r:20.1.20) (q:draft)
kizuaksa = (t:adj) (w:sold) (d:kizuak, be sold, with sa, already done: having been sold; sal-a kizuaksa is sold as a slave) (e:tungah sal-a ~ i Judah mipihte) (s:zuaksa) (a:leisa) (b:kizuak) (r:16.5.8) (q:draft)
kizuaksak = (t:v) (w:sell/cause to be sold) (d:kizuak, be sold, with the causative sak: have someone sold, sell) (e:Judah mite tungah ka ~ ding a) (s:zuak) (b:kizuak) (r:29.3.8) (q:draft)
kizualsak = (t:v) (w:be tamed/be made tame) (d:zualsak, tame, with the prefix ki: be tamed; a kizualsak zo lo is one that cannot be tamed, stubborn) (e:A ~ zo lo bawngla bangin) (b:zualsak) (r:28.4.16) (q:draft)
kizuansak = (t:v) (w:be gathered to/be made to go to) (d:passive of zuansak with the prefix ki; a pu a pate kiang kizuansak is be gathered to the ancestors, die) (e:a pate uh kiang ~ hi) (b:zuansak) (r:7.2.10) (q:draft)
kizui = (t:v) (w:accord with/be in keeping with/agree with) (d:zui, follow, with the prefix ki: be in keeping with something; the phrase tawh kizui-in means according to) (e:A beh tawh ~-in Dan minam adingin/Mordekai’ laigelhna tawh ~-in | according to what Mordecai had written/Elisha’ kampauna tawh ~-in tu ni dongin | according to the word of Elisha, to this day/a gik zah tawh ~-in ngun shekel zali | four hundred shekels of silver according to the weight) (b:zui) (r:6.19.40/19.119.149/17.9.23/12.2.22/1.23.16) (q:draft)
kizuih = (t:v) (w:be followed/be obeyed/be kept) (d:passive of zuih: be followed, obeyed or observed, of a word, a law, advice or an agreement) (e:a thuciam bawlna uh a ~ nading/ngat taka a ~ kul ding hi | it must be strictly obeyed/ama thugen a ~ loh a muh ciangin | when he saw that his advice was not followed/ama thuhilhnate limtakin a ~ ding a deih hi | he wants his teachings to be carefully followed/Pasian’ lamlahna a ~ lohna gam-ah | in a land where God’s guidance is not followed) (a:kipalsat) (b:zuih) (r:26.17.14/27.6.8/10.17.23/23.42.21/20.29.18) (q:draft)
kizuihna = (t:n) (w:keeping/observance) (d:kizuih be kept, be observed, with the noun suffix na: the keeping of an agreement) (e:a thuciam bawlna uh a ~ ding) (s:zuihna) (b:kizuih) (r:26.17.14) (q:draft)
kizuisak = (t:v) (w:take along/make accompany/cause to go with) (d:have a person or animal go along; also of an offering that is to go together with another) (e:sathau bing dim khat tawh ~ ding hi/ganhing dang ka ~ kei hi | I took no other animal with me/tuutal khat ciangin an bung khat ~ ding a | an ephah of grain is to go with each ram/Zeisu’ singlamteh pua dingin a ~ uh hi | they made him go along to carry the cross of Jesus/kuamah dang ~ nawn lo hi | he let no one else go with him) (s:tonpih) (b:kizui) (r:26.46.5/16.2.12/41.15.21/41.5.37) (q:draft)
kizuizaw = (t:v) (w:be accompanied all the more) (d:kizui go together with, accord with, and zaw more; minthanna tawh kizuizaw is come with still greater glory) (e:minthanna lian tawh hong ~ kan ding) (b:kizui) (r:47.3.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
kizung = (t:v) (w:be uprooted) (d:zung root with the prefix ki, used in kizung bawh, be pulled up by the roots) (e:hehna tawh leenggui ~ bawh a) (s:kizungbawh/kizunglot/kibotkhia) (a:kisuan) (b:zung) (r:26.19.12) (q:draft)
kizungbawh = (t:v) (w:be uprooted/be pulled up by the roots) (d:passive of zungbawh uproot, with the prefix ki) (e:hehna tawh leenggui ~ a) (s:kizunglot/kibotkhia/kizung) (a:kisuan) (b:zungbawh) (r:26.19.12) (q:draft)
kizunglot = (t:v) (w:be uprooted/be rooted out) (d:passive of zunglot uproot, with the prefix ki) (e:ama inn thakhatin ~ ka mu ngei hi) (s:kizungbawh/kibotkhia) (a:kisuan) (b:zunglot) (r:18.5.3/42.17.6) (q:draft)
kizunglotin = (t:v) (w:being uprooted/uprooted) (d:kizunglot be uprooted with the linking suffix in) (e:~ a keutum singkungte) (b:kizunglot) (r:65.1.12) (q:draft)
kizut = (t:v) (w:be coated/be overlaid/be smeared/be plastered) (d:passive of zut: be covered with a layer of oil, metal, paint, whitewash or plaster) (e:Ngun leh kham tawh a ~ hangin/sathau tawh a ~ mohpheng hi ding hi | it is to be wafers brushed with oil/a inn a ~ khit ciangin | after the house has been plastered/Leikang tawh ~ suangcian’ aw | you whitewashed wall/suangkangtui a ~, han tawh kibang | like whitewashed tombs) (s:kinuh) (b:zut) (r:35.2.19/3.2.4/3.14.48/44.23.3/40.23.27) (q:draft)
kizutna = (t:n) (w:overlay/coating/plaster) (d:kizut with the noun suffix na: what is smeared or laid on a surface, as the plaster of a wall or the metal overlay of a post top; also the act of smearing) (e:a khuamlu zepnate a ~ zong ngun/a kiat khiat a ~ themte | the plaster that is scraped off/sisan a ~ zong upna hang mah ahi hi | the applying of the blood was also by faith) (s:zutna) (b:kizut) (r:2.38.17/3.14.41/58.11.28) (q:draft)
kizutnate = (t:n) (w:plaster/coatings) (d:kizutna plaster with the plural te: all that a house is plastered with) (e:inn a ~ khempeuh phel ding hi) (b:kizutna) (r:3.14.45) (q:draft)
kizutnelh = (t:v) (w:degrade/defile) (d:in the verse, of a woman who ruins her own beauty; likely smear and soil oneself, exact sense not confirmed) (e:beelmang na ~ hi) (r:26.16.25) (q:draft, low confidence)
Klandia = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Claudia) (d:Christian woman in Rome whose greetings Paul sends to Timothy) (r:55.4.21)
Klaudia = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Claudius) (d:Roman emperor who ordered all Jews to leave Rome) (e:~ kumpipa in Judah mi khempeuh) (r:44.18.2) (q:draft)
Klaudias = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Claudius) (d:name of two men in Acts, the Roman emperor Claudius and the commander Claudius Lysias) (r:44.11.28/44.23.26)
Klaudis = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Claudius) (d:Claudius Lysias, the Roman commander in Jerusalem who sent Paul to the governor Felix) (r:44.23.26)
Klement = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Clement) (d:fellow worker of Paul at Philippi) (r:50.4.3)
Kleopas = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Cleopas) (d:one of the two disciples who met the risen Jesus on the road to Emmaus) (r:42.24.18)
Klopas = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Clopas) (d:husband of one of the women named Mary who stood by the cross of Jesus) (r:43.19.25)
ko = (t:pron) (w:we/us) (d:first person plural pronoun that leaves out the person spoken to; the English form, we, us or our, depends on its place in the sentence) (e:tua khomun ~ hong pia tawntung in/na itna kip ~ tungah hong omsak in | let your steadfast love be upon us/~ tawh numei hong omsak lai in | let the girl stay with us a while/Tui, ~ aa hi | the water is ours/~ huh dingin hong pai in | come to help us) (s:kote/komau) (r:43.6.34/19.33.22/1.24.55/1.26.20/19.44.26)
Ko = (t:see) <Ko-laiah>
Ko-laiah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Kolaiah) (d:father of the false prophet Ahab in the time of Jeremiah) (r:24.29.21) (q:draft)
Koa = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Koa) (d:a people named together with Pekod and Shoa among those brought against Jerusalem; Koa mite is the men of Koa) (r:26.23.23) (q:draft)
kobawlin = (t:v) (w:insult/revile/hurl insults at) (d:kobawl, abuse someone with words, with the linking suffix in) (e:mittaw ngei pa ~) (r:43.9.28) (q:draft)
kobawlna = (t:n) (w:taunt/insult/abuse) (d:kobawl, abuse with words, with the noun suffix na) (e:hong ~ za nawn loin) (s:kosiatna/zahkona/simmawhna) (a:phatna) (r:26.36.15) (q:draft)
koh = (t:v) (w:express/offer/give) (d:say or present something to someone; with lungdam or lungdamna it means give thanks) (e:Topa tungah lungdam ~ ding hoih hi/nangma tungah lungdamna kong ~ theih nadingun | so that we may give thanks to you/na min siangtho tungah lungdamna kong ~ | we give thanks to your holy name/Topa tungah lungdam ~ biakna na piak uh ciangin | when you offer a thank offering to the Lord/Lungdam ~ piaknate pia-in | offering thank offerings) (r:14.5.13/19.106.47/13.16.35/3.22.29/19.107.22) (q:draft)
koh = (t:v) (w:report/appeal/bring up) (d:bring a matter or complaint before someone, cry to someone for help) (e:thu dang na ~ nop uh leh/kumpipa’ kiangah i ~ kul ding hi | we must report it to the king/thukhen mangte kiangah a ~ uh ciangin | when they reported it to the magistrates/kumpipa tungah ka ~ ding thu | a matter for me to bring before the king) (s:zasak) (r:44.19.39/24.36.16/44.16.38/10.19.28) (q:draft)
Kohath = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Kohath) (d:second son of Levi, ancestor of the Kohathite clans of the Levites) (r:1.46.11/13.6.1)
Kohathte = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Kohathites) (d:the Levite clans descended from Kohath, who carried the holy things of the tabernacle) (b:Kohath) (r:4.3.29/4.3.27)
kohkhit = (t:v) (w:have given/have offered) (d:koh utter or offer with khit finish; in the verses always lungdamna a kohkhit ciangin, after he had given thanks) (e:lungdamna a ~ ciangin/Pasian tungah lungdam a ~ ciangin balnen a | when he had given thanks to God he broke it/Pasian tungah lungdamna a ~ ciangin balnenin | after giving thanks to God he broke it and/lungdamna a ~ ciangin a nungzuite tungah pia a | when he had given thanks he gave it to his disciples) (r:40.26.27/42.24.30/46.11.24/41.14.23) (q:draft)
kohna = (t:n) (w:expressing/announcing/giving notice) (d:act of reporting or expressing, from koh; lungdam kohna is thanksgiving, patau kohna an alarm or warning) (e:Pasian tungah lungdam ~ a makai-in/patau ~ za napi-in don lo | though he heard the warning he did not heed it/lungdam ~ la a gingin sa-in | singing aloud a song of thanksgiving) (b:koh) (r:16.12.46/26.33.5/19.26.7) (q:draft)
koi = (t:adv) (w:where) (d:question word for place, usually followed by a place word as in koi-ah, at what place, koi lai, whereabouts, and koi pan, from where) (e:Na sanggampa Abel ~-ah om ahi hiam/mi lianpa’ inn, ~-ah om ta ahi hiam | where now is the house of the great man/pumpi ~-a om ding hiam | where would the body be/huhna ~ lai pan hong pai ding ahi hiam | where will help come from/Piter ~ lamah a om hiam | where Peter was) (s:koiah/koilai) (r:1.4.9/18.21.28/46.12.19/19.121.1/44.12.18)
koiah = (t:adv) (w:where) (d:koi, where, with the place marker ah: at what place) (e:tu-in ~ om uh ahi hiam/Adang kua teng ~ om ahi uh hiam | where are the other nine/na pasiante uh ~ om ahi hiam | where are your gods) (s:koi/koilai) (b:koi) (r:24.37.19/43.11.34/42.17.17/24.2.28) (q:draft)
koici = (t:adv) (w:how/in what way) (d:question word asking the manner of an action, how, in what way; koici bang asks how a matter stands) (e:~ gamtat ding cih mihing in/hong ~ maisak ding ka hi hiam | how can I forgive you/nek ding an ~ ngahtheih ding ihi hiam | how can we get food to eat/Ute naute aw, ~ bang ahi hiam | brothers and sisters, how is it then/hong ~ et kik thei ding ka hi hiam | how can I look again) (s:bangci) (r:20.20.24/24.5.7/43.6.5/46.14.26/32.2.4) (q:draft)
koih = (t:v) (w:put) (e:keelte a veilam a ~ ding hi/thong sungah ni thum sung amaute ~ hi | he put them in prison for three days/a bawngtal sem nenin a sing tungah ~ hi | he cut up the bull and put it on the wood/khuamial dingin khuavak ~ a | putting light for darkness) (s:omsak) (a:lakhia) (r:40.25.33/1.42.17/11.18.33/23.5.20) put in a particular position.
koih = (t:v) (w:place) (d:set something or someone in a certain spot or position) (e:hihtengah na ~ in/amaute laizang ah a ~ khit ciangin | after he had placed him among them/mai-ah ciangkhutte ~ hi | he placed the staffs in front/Dan ah adang khat ~ hi | he placed the other one in Dan) (s:omsak) (r:1.1.17/40.18.2/4.17.7/11.12.29)
koih = (t:v) (w:deposit) (d:leave something in a safe place or with someone for keeping, as a writing before the Lord or money in a bank) (e:laibu khat sungah gelhin Topa mai-ah ~ hi | he wrote them on a scroll and deposited it before the Lord/sumkholna-ah ka sumte na ~ lo na hi hiam | did you not deposit my money in the bank) (r:9.10.25/42.19.23)
koih = (t:v) (w:lay down) (d:set a person or thing down, as a body on a bed or in a tomb; also lay a foundation) (e:milim khat la-in lupna tungah ~ a | she took an idol and laid it on the bed/Pasian’ mipa’ lupna tungah amah ~ a | she laid him on the bed of the man of God/ama hanah a luanghawm ~ hi | he laid the body in his own tomb/leitung bulpi na ~ a | you laid the foundation of the earth) (s:sial) (r:9.19.13/12.4.21/11.13.30/19.102.25)
koihcing = (t:v) (w:store up/reserve/keep/save) (d:put something by and keep it safe for later use) (e:a hoih leenggahtui tudongin na ~ hi/gal om hun ciang adingin ka ~ ahi hi | I keep them in reserve for the time of war/Nate na ~ uh hangin phatuam lo ding hi | though you store things up it will be of no use/limtakin kemin ~ un | guard them well and keep them safe) (s:khol/koihkhol) (r:43.2.10/18.38.23/33.6.14/23.8.16) (q:draft)
koihcip = (t:v) (w:isolate/shut up/keep shut away/confine) (d:koih, put, with cip, tightly closed: put away and keep closed in; also of keeping the hand held back in the fold of the garment) (e:ni sagih sung ~ ding hi/na khut taklam na ang-ah ~ na hi hiam | do you keep your right hand in your bosom/ni sagih sung mah tua na ~ ding hi | he shall isolate that article for seven days/Ni lianpi ngakin Pasian in a ~ hi | God has kept them shut up to await the great Day) (s:khakcip) (a:khahkhia) (b:koih) (r:3.13.50/19.74.11/3.13.54/65.1.6) (q:draft)
koihdakna = (t:n) (w:leaving neglected/neglect) (d:the leaving of a thing as it is without caring for it; a siapi-in na koihdakna is your leaving it in ruins) (e:a siapi-in na ~ hang uh ahi hi) (r:37.1.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
koihin = (t:v) (w:put/place/set) (d:koih with the linking suffix in, joining it to the next action) (e:Amah in Beth-el ah khat ~/keelmul lukham khat a lu-ah ~ puan silhsak hi | she put a goat hair pillow at its head and covered it with a cloth/biakbuk kongkhak mai-ah meihal biaknatau ~ | placing the altar of burnt offering before the entrance of the tabernacle/ama lu tungah a dialpi ~ | putting the turban on his head) (b:koih) (r:11.12.29/3.1.7/9.19.13/2.40.6/3.8.9) (q:draft)
koihkhawm = (t:v) (w:put together/join/place with) (d:koih, put, with khawm, together) (e:Judah ciangkhut tawh ka ~ ding hi/Laban’ tuuhonte tawh ~ lo hi | he did not put them with the flocks of Laban/a lutang leh a thau tawh ~ ding hi | he shall arrange it together with the head and the fat) (s:gawm) (a:koihtuam/khenkhia) (b:koih) (r:26.37.19/1.30.40/3.1.12) (q:draft)
koihkhia = (t:v) (w:put out/remove/take away/get rid of) (d:koih, put, with khia, out: put someone out, or take away and get rid of something such as an idol or a sin) (e:Ka omna panin hih numei ~ in la/Mualtung a biaknate ~ lo hi | he did not remove the high places/Topa in zong na khialhna ~ zo hi | the Lord has taken away your sin/Baal-te le Ashtaroth ~-in Topa bek a bia | they put away the Baals and Ashtoreths and served the Lord only) (s:lakhia/paaikhia) (a:koihkik) (b:koih) (r:10.13.17/12.3.2/12.14.4/10.12.13/9.7.4) (q:draft)
koihkhit = (t:v) (w:have put/finish putting) (d:koih put with khit, finished: the putting is completed) (e:a khenuai-ah a ~ hun dong) (s:koihzo) (r:46.15.25) (q:draft)
koihkhol = (t:v) (w:store up/lay up/keep in advance) (d:koih put with khol, beforehand: put aside or prepare for a later time) (e:na tampi tak ~ hi/hih paknamtui ~ ta hen | let her keep this perfume) (s:koihcing) (r:13.22.5/43.12.7) (q:draft)
koihkholh = (t:v) (w:lay down beforehand/set down in advance) (d:form of koihkhol; thu koihkholh is a word laid down or declared beforehand) (e:ci-in thu a ~ mah bangin) (b:koihkhol) (r:58.7.21) (q:draft, low confidence)
koihkhong = (t:v) (w:leave alone/let be/leave as is) (d:leave a person as he is without doing anything about it) (e:Hih mi i ~ leh/tagahte gilkialin ka ~ ngei kei hi | I have never left the fatherless hungry/amah a demte ~ lo a | he does not let his opponents be) (s:koihmawk/khahkhong) (r:43.11.48/18.31.17/34.1.2) (q:draft)
koihkik = (t:v) (w:put back/return/restore/replace) (d:koih, put, with kik, again, back: put a thing back where it was, or restore a person to a former place or office) (e:inndei sungah tuate ~ zel uh hi/Dagon la-in a omna mun-ah ~ uh hi | they took Dagon and put him back in his place/an piapi pa an piak nasepah ~ a | he restored the chief cupbearer to his post/na upate ka ~ ding hi | I will restore your elders/hih munah ka ~ ding hi | I will put them back in this place) (a:koihkhia) (b:koih) (r:11.14.28/15.5.15/9.5.3/1.40.21/23.1.26/24.27.22) (q:draft)
koihkikin = (t:v) (w:restore/put back/replace) (d:koihkik put back with the linking suffix in) (e:biakna tau zong ~ tua tungah) (b:koihkik) (r:14.33.16) (q:draft)
koihleh = (t:v) (w:store/keep) (d:apparently koih, put or store, written together with leh, and: the storing of valuables and) (e:inn van manpha ~ a ki-ap letsong) (r:13.26.20) (q:draft, low confidence)
koihmawk = (t:v) (w:tolerate/let be/leave alone) (d:koih put, leave, with mawk carelessly; with lo, not put up with) (e:le migilote ~ loin) (s:koihkhong/khahkhong) (r:66.2.2) (q:draft)
koihna = (t:n) (w:storehouse/store/holder) (d:place where something is put or kept, as in humpinelkai koihna lions' den and meivak koihna lampstand) (e:ka van ~ sungah kisincip/humpinelkai ~ khukah a va pai pah hi | he went at once to the lions’ den/a galvan ~ inn khempeuh | his whole armory/meivak ~ tungah | on the lampstand) (s:vankoihna/kholna) (b:koih) (r:5.32.34/27.6.19/23.39.2/42.11.33) (q:draft)
koihnate = (t:n) (w:storehouses/treasuries/stores) (d:koihna with the plural te: places where things are kept; van manpha koihnate are treasuries) (e:inn van manpha ~ a uk ahi/Kumpipa’ van manpha ~ ah Adiel’ tapa Azmaveth | over the king’s storehouses was Azmaveth son of Adiel/van manpha ~ tawh kisai-in | concerning the treasuries) (s:vankoihnate/sumkoihnate) (b:koihna) (r:13.9.26/14.32.28/13.27.25/14.8.15) (q:draft)
koihpa = (t:n) (w:one who appointed/one who put/man appointed) (d:koih, put, with pa for a male person: the one who put, set or appointed, or the man who was put in a post) (e:amah a ~ mai-ah a diktat hi/a dang thumte cing dinga a ~ kiangah | to the man set to guard the other three/thuciamna a ~ in thuman mi ahi hi | he who made the promise is faithful) (b:koih) (r:58.3.2/27.1.11/58.10.23) (q:draft)
koihsa = (t:adj) (w:laid up/stored up/set/placed) (d:koih with -sa, already put; a koihsa before a noun is that which someone has put, set or laid down) (e:Nangma ~ ngeina kipte in/Nang hong zahtakte’ adinga na ~ | which you have stored up for those who fear you/Pa in ama ukna-ah a ~ a hun | the times the Father has set by his own authority/a ~ anthul kungte lakah | among the stalks of flax she had laid out) (b:koih) (r:19.119.138/19.31.19/44.1.7/6.2.6) (q:draft)
koihsak = (t:v) (w:put for/place for/set up for) (d:koih, put, with sak: put or appoint something for someone, or cause it to be put) (e:ama lungsim sungah a ~ pilna/Babilon khua-ah kamsang hong ~ hi | he has raised up prophets for us in Babylon/a moi pen’ van gong-ah ~ in | put it in the mouth of the youngest one’s sack/nang adingin na duhduh kong ~ hi | I have stored up for you all that you like/ama khe nuai-ah amaute a ~ matengin | until he put them under his feet) (b:koih) (r:14.9.23/24.29.15/1.44.2/22.7.13/11.5.3) (q:draft)
koihsakin = (t:v) (w:keep for/set up for) (d:koihsak put for someone with the linking ending in: keeping something for someone, and then the next action follows) (e:hih a lian itna kip ~) (b:koihsak) (r:11.3.6) (q:draft)
koihsim = (t:v) (w:hide/set secretly) (d:koih put with sim, secretly: lay a trap where it is not seen) (e:kei hong siahna-in tehlop ~ uh a) (s:seel) (r:19.140.5) (q:draft)
koihsuk = (t:v) (w:put down/set down/put under) (d:koih put with suk, down) (e:ka nuai-ah mite a ~ Pasian/note’ Pasian mai-ah na ~ ding uh a | you shall set it down before your God) (a:koihto) (b:koih) (r:10.22.48/5.26.10) (q:draft)
koihte = (t:n) (w:those placed/things set aside) (d:koih, put, with the plural te: people or things that someone has put, stationed, kept or set aside) (e:kulhnei khuapite ah a ~ banah/a siangtho inn adingin ka ~ khempeuh banah | besides all that I have set aside for the holy house/Jabeshgilead numei a hing-a a ~ uh | the women of Jabesh Gilead whom they had kept alive) (b:koih) (r:14.17.19/13.29.3/7.21.14) (q:draft)
koihto = (t:v) (w:put up/set on top/build up) (d:koih put with to, upward: set something up on top of another) (e:tua tungah tausangte ~ a) (a:koihsuk) (b:koih) (r:14.32.5) (q:draft)
koihtuam = (t:v) (w:set apart/set aside) (d:koih put with tuam separate: put apart from the rest for a special use) (e:Hih na ~ tuununo sagihte/nasepna-a dingin ~ uh hi | they set them apart for the service/Topa in miphate ama adingin a ~ lam | that the Lord has set apart the faithful for himself) (s:tuamkoih/khenkhiat) (a:koihkhawm) (r:1.21.29/13.25.1/19.4.3) (q:draft)
koihzaw = (t:v) (w:put instead/put rather) (d:koih put with zaw, rather: put in one place rather than another) (e:Meivakna mun sangah ~ a/meivak koihna tungah a ~ hi | instead he puts it on the lampstand) (b:koih) (r:40.5.15/42.11.33) (q:draft)
koihzo = (t:v) (w:have put/have placed/have set ready) (d:koih put with zo, which shows that the action is done) (e:note’ mai-ah leitang ~ hi/ama galhiamte a baihsa-in a ~ hi | he has made his weapons ready/sing le suang zong ka ~ hi | I have also laid up wood and stone/note’ mai-ah leitang ka ~ hi | I have set the land before you) (s:koihkhit) (b:koih) (r:5.1.21/19.7.13/13.22.14/5.1.8) (q:draft)
koilai = (t:adv) (w:where/whereabouts/which place) (d:question word for place; koilai panin is from where, and repeated as koilai mun koilai gam it means in whatever place) (e:thumu pa’ inn ~ ahi hiam/~ panin a hong pai na hi uh hiam | where do you come from/~ mun ~ gam a om hitaleh | in whatever place or land they live/zintun nading inndei ~ ahi hiam | where is the guest room) (s:koi/koiah) (r:9.9.18/42.13.25/15.1.4/41.14.14) (q:draft)
koilam = (t:adv) (w:where/which way) (d:koi, where, with lam, direction: to which place, in which direction) (e:amah ~ pai ding hiam/~ pai ding cih na thei kei hi | you do not know where it is going) (s:koi) (r:43.7.35/43.3.8) (q:draft)
koimah = (t:adv) (w:anywhere/nowhere/everywhere) (d:koi where with mah: with a negative verb, nowhere or not anywhere; koimah peuh, anywhere at all, everywhere) (e:Na nasempa ~ pai lo hi/a ~ peuhah mi khempeuh in gensia uh | people everywhere speak against it/a ~ peuhah kitotna le lungkhamna om kawikawi | on every side there are conflicts and fears/awging ~ ah kiza nawn lo ding hi | the voice will be heard nowhere any more) (s:koimahah) (b:koi) (r:12.5.25/44.28.22/47.7.5/34.2.13) (q:draft)
koimahah = (t:adv) (w:anywhere/nowhere) (d:koimah with the place marker ah; used with a negative verb: not anywhere, nowhere) (e:inn panin ~ a paikhia kei hi/a luptheih nading mun ~ nei lo hi | he has nowhere to lay his head/khuamial khuazing ~ om lo hi | there is no deep darkness anywhere/ahi zongin ~ nong mu kei ding uh hi | but you will not find me anywhere) (s:koimah) (b:koimah) (r:42.1.24/18.34.22/42.9.58/20.1.28) (q:draft)
koin = (t:v) (w:expressing/giving) (d:apparently ko, utter or express, with the linking suffix in, elsewhere written ko-in; lungdamna koin is giving thanks) (e:lungdamna ~ Topa phatin) (r:13.23.30) (q:draft, low confidence)
koipan = (t:adv) (w:from where/whence) (d:koi where with pan from) (e:hihpa ~ hong pai cih i thei hi) (r:43.7.27) (q:draft)
koizaw = (t:pron) (w:which/which one) (d:koi with zaw, more: question word asking which of two) (e:amau’ kammal ~ a manin tung/~ ka khah ding deih na hi uh hiam | which one do you want me to release) (b:koi) (r:24.44.28/40.27.17) (q:draft)
kol = (t:n) (w:shackles/chains/fetters/stocks) (d:iron or wooden restraint put on a prisoner; kol bulh is put in chains) (e:Amah in ~ hong bulh a/Amah in ka khe ~ hong bulh a | he puts my feet in shackles/amau khe ah ~ a bulh hi | he fastened their feet in the stocks/na khete ~ kibulh lo hi | your feet were not fettered) (s:sikkol) (r:25.3.7/24.39.7/18.33.11/44.16.24/10.3.34) (q:draft)
kol = (t:n) (w:yoke) (d:wooden yoke laid on the neck of a working animal) (e:nasepna ~ a kivawh ngei nai lo/~ a kai nai lo bawngla khat | a heifer that has never pulled a yoke/a tungah ~ a kibaang ngei lo bawngpi | cows that have never been yoked) (s:hakkol) (r:4.19.2/5.21.3/9.6.7) (q:draft)
kol = (t:v) (w:come loose/hang loose/loosen) (d:come loose or hang slack, of a belt, a rope or something tied on) (e:dialkaih khat zong ~ lo hi/awmdal a ~ theih loh nadingin | so that the breastpiece does not come loose/Gal teembaw khaute ~ a | the ropes of the warship hang loose) (r:23.5.27/2.28.28/23.33.23) (q:draft)
Kolaiah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Kolaiah) (d:name of two men, a Benjamite ancestor of Sallu and the father of the false prophet Ahab) (r:16.11.7/24.29.21)
kolbulh = (t:n) (w:fetters/shackles/irons) (d:kol, shackles, and bulh, put on: fetters fastened on the feet of a prisoner) (e:~ leh sikkhau tawh tamveipi/~ a kuai tan hi | he broke the fetters in pieces) (s:kol/sikkol) (r:41.5.4/42.8.29) (q:draft)
kolbulh = (t:v) (w:shackle/put in fetters) (d:kol, shackles, with bulh, put on: fasten the feet of someone in fetters) (e:Amah in ka khe ~ a) (r:18.33.11) (q:draft)
kolbulhna = (t:n) (w:stocks/shackling/fetters) (d:kolbulh put in fetters with the noun suffix na: the being put in fetters, or the stocks in which a prisoner is held) (e:amaute in ~ thuak ding uh a/a ~ panin Jeremiah a khah khit ciangin | when he released Jeremiah from the stocks) (s:singkol) (b:kolbulh) (r:28.11.7/24.20.3) (q:draft)
koleko = (t:pron) (w:ourselves) (d:ko we, repeated with le and: we ourselves as the object of our own action, excluding the hearer) (e:~ a kiphattawm ka bang zel uh hiam/~ a hong kiphattawm zel ka hi kei uh | we are not commending ourselves to you again) (s:komau) (r:47.3.1/47.5.12) (q:draft)
kolh = (t:adj) (w:bald/bare) (d:bare of hair or of growth; tal kolh is a bald forehead and mual kolh a bare hilltop; of plants or forest it is stripped bare) (e:amah a tal ~ hi a/Mual ~ tungah lan khat khai to un | raise a banner on a bare hilltop/a tal ~ tung hita leh | or on his bald forehead) (s:tol) (r:3.13.41/23.13.2/3.13.42) (q:draft)
kolhna = (t:n) (w:baldness/bareness) (d:kolh bald or bare with the noun suffix na; lu kolhna is baldness of the head and mun kolhna a bare, ruined place) (e:lim tak-a kizem sam tangin lu ~/mun ~-a om simbu tawh ka kibang hi | I am like an owl in a bare place) (b:kolh) (r:23.3.24/19.102.6) (q:draft)
Kolhozeh = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Kol-Hozeh) (d:father of Shallun who repaired the Fountain Gate, and an ancestor of Maaseiah of Judah) (r:16.3.15/16.11.5)
kolhsak = (t:v) (w:make bald/strip bare) (d:kolh bald or bare with sak, cause) (e:amau’ lutang ~ ding hi/gammang tulak hawkkhia-in ~ hi | he strips the forest bare) (s:tolsak) (b:kolh) (r:23.3.17/19.29.9) (q:draft)
kolhsiang = (t:v) (w:be stripped bare/be laid flat) (d:kolh bare with siang clean: of a forest, be cleared completely) (e:tulak ~ ding a) (b:kolh) (r:23.32.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
