kolte = (t:n) (w:yokes) (d:kol, yoke, with the plural te: yokes of working oxen, also the yoke of bondage) (e:a bawngtal ~ la-in/ancilna peekte leh bawngtal ~ hih lai-ah om hi | here are threshing sledges and ox yokes/a sate bawngtal ~ tawh huanin | cooking the meat with the ox yokes/a kikhihna ~ uh ka sutsak khit ciangin | when I have loosed the yokes that bind them) (s:hakkolte) (b:kol) (r:11.19.21/10.24.22/26.34.27) (q:draft)
kolte = (t:n) (w:shackles/fetters) (d:kol, shackles, with the plural te: irons fastened on the hands or feet of a prisoner) (e:Ama khete pen ~ in nasak a/na khuta kibulh ~ | the chains fastened on your hands/a khe-a kibulh ~ a sukham gawp hi | he smashed the irons on his feet) (s:sikkhaute) (b:kol) (r:19.105.18/24.40.4/41.5.4) (q:draft)
komau = (t:pron) (w:ourselves/we/us/our) (d:first person plural excluding the hearer, emphatic form of ko, we ourselves; before a noun, our own; the English form depends on its place in the sentence) (e:Teembaw sungah a om ~ khempeuh in/Athen khuapi-ah ~ bek ka om lai nading uh | that we should stay on in Athens by ourselves/Hih pa in ~ tapa hi a | this is our son/~’ kihotkhiatna Pasian | God our Savior) (s:koleko/ko) (r:44.27.37/47.3.5/52.3.1/43.9.20/19.65.5) (q:draft)
komdep = (t:n) (w:hollow place/hollow) (d:a hollow or basin in the ground or rock; in Judges 15.19 God split one open at Lehi and water came out of it) (e:om ~ khat hong a) (r:7.15.19) (q:draft)
kona = (t:n) (w:scorn/reproach) (d:reproach or scorn that a person has to bear, in kona thuak, bear reproach; likely ko, shout at, with the noun suffix na) (e:nangma hangin ~ ka thuak a) (s:kosiatna/simmawhna) (r:19.69.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
