Krete = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Crete) (d:large island in the Mediterranean Sea, where Paul left Titus to appoint elders) (r:56.1.12/44.2.11)
Krispas = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Crispus) (d:ruler of the synagogue at Corinth, who believed with his household and was baptised by Paul) (r:44.18.8/46.1.14)
kristal = (t:n) (c:stone) (w:crystal) (d:loanword from English: a clear, bright precious stone, used in comparisons for what is clear and shining) (e:~ tawh kibang limlang tuipi/a vang in ~ bangin jasper suangmanpha bangin | its brightness like crystal, like a jasper stone/~ suangmanpha tawh kibangin tangin | shining like a crystal gem) (r:66.4.6/66.21.11/66.22.1) (q:draft)
Kristal = (t:name) (w:Kristal/crystal) (d:kristal, crystal, written with a capital in Kristal suangmanpha, crystal gem; a kind of clear stone, not a personal name) (r:66.21.11/66.4.6)
ku = (t:v) (w:howl/snarl/growl) (d:of dogs, howl or snarl; ui bangin ku is howl like a dog) (e:ui bangin ~ uh a) (r:19.59.6/19.59.14) (q:draft)
kua = (t:num) (w:nine) (d:the number nine; kum kua is nine years, and sawmkua-le-kua is ninety-nine) (e:ni ~/leh Elifelet, ~ pha uh hi | and Eliphelet, nine in all/amah in kum ~ sung uk hi | he reigned for nine years/kha ~ leh ni sawmnih | nine months and twenty days) (r:13.3.8/12.17.1/10.24.8)
kua = (t:pron) (w:who) (d:question word for a person: who; before a noun it asks whose, as in kua min, whose name) (e:Pasian kihel loin ~ in an ne-in/Topa longal, Pasian ~ hiam | who is God besides the Lord/Hih ~ min, ~ lim ahi hiam | whose name and whose image is this/ka sanggamte ~ ahi uh hiam | who are my brothers) (r:21.2.25/1.3.11/19.18.31/40.22.20/40.12.48)
kuah = (t:v) (w:strap on/gird on/wear) (d:fasten a weapon at the waist, or wear it there; in the verses almost always with namsau, sword) (e:David in zong a namsau ~ hi/na namsau ~ in | gird on your sword/a namsau uh ~ uh hi | they strapped on their swords/A vekpi-in namsau ~ kim uh a | all of them wearing swords/namsau thak khat a ~ Ishbibenob | Ishbi-Benob, who wore a new sword) (r:9.25.13/19.45.3/22.3.8/10.21.16) (q:draft)
kuahawm = (t:n) (w:pit/den/cave) (d:a hollow in the ground or in rock, such as the den where a lion hides; kuahawm thukpi, the very deep pit, is the Abyss) (e:~ thukpi sung panin a hong paikhia/humpinelkai in a ~ sung pan a buk bangin | like a lion lying in wait in its den/tua ~ thukpi a hon ciangin | when he opened the Abyss/~ thukpi honna tawhtang | the key to the Abyss) (r:66.11.7/19.10.9/66.9.2/66.9.1) (q:draft)
kuahin = (t:v) (w:strapping on/carrying/bearing) (d:kuah, strap on, with the linking ending in: wearing a weapon at the waist while the next action follows, as in lum leh namsau kuahin, carrying shield and sword) (e:lum leh namsau ~ thal a tawi) (b:kuah) (r:13.5.18) (q:draft)
kuahkuah = (t:adv) (w:strutting) (d:descriptive word placed after pai, walk, for the proud strutting walk of a rooster) (e:a kihihsak pai ~ aklui) (s:kuankuan) (r:20.30.31) (q:draft, low confidence)
kuahpa = (t:n) (w:one who puts on/one who girds on) (d:kuah strap on, gird on, with pa, the man who does it; galhiam a kuahpa is one who puts on his armor) (e:galhiam a ~ kiphasak kei hen) (b:kuah) (r:11.20.11) (q:draft)
kuai = (t:v) (w:bend/bow down/droop) (d:bend over, as ripe grain heavy on the stalk; kuai tan is break by bending, snap) (e:kolbulh a ~ tan hi/A awnsa pumpeeng ~ tan lo a | he will not break a bruised reed/gah a min zo a, ~ gawp zo hi | the crop is ripe and bending over) (r:41.5.4/66.14.15/40.12.20) (q:draft)
kuai = (t:v) (w:be captivated) (d:in lung kuai, of the heart, be won over or moved with longing) (e:na mit hah in ka lung ~ a) (r:22.4.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
kuaih = (t:v) (w:break/snap) (d:form of kuai bend, used in kuaih tan, break in two) (e:khe a ~ tan khit uh ciangin) (b:kuai) (r:43.19.32) (q:draft)
kuaihtan = (t:v) (w:break/snap) (d:break a rigid thing in two, said of a yoke or a rod; in the verses always followed by sak) (e:a ~ sak hi/a hakkolte uh ka ~ sak ding a | I will break their yokes/a satna ciangkhut na ~ sak a | you have broken the rod that struck them/ngawng panin ka ~ sak ding hi | I will break it off the neck) (s:kuaitan/sutan) (r:24.28.10/24.30.8/23.9.4/24.28.11) (q:draft)
kuaihtansak = (t:v) (w:break/shatter/snap off) (d:cause to break in two, of an arm, a branch or a tree, from kuaihtan) (e:amau gamsung singte ~ hi/Izipt kumpipa Faro’ khut ka ~ zo hi | I have broken the arm of Pharaoh king of Egypt/a kisatna ciangkhut na ~ a | you have broken the rod that beat them/ka hakkol hong lakkhiat sakin hong ~ hi | he took my yoke off and broke it) (s:kuaitan/sutan) (b:kuaihtan) (r:19.105.33/26.30.21/23.9.4/24.28.10) (q:draft)
kuaitan = (t:v) (w:break/snap/break in two) (d:break something long and rigid in two, such as a staff, an arm, a leg, a bow or a yoke) (e:ban ~ in la/Lebanon mual taamtaak singte ~ hi | he breaks the cedars of Lebanon/a khe a ~ kei uh hi | they did not break his legs/Babilon kumpipa’ hakkol ka ~ zo hi | I have broken the yoke of the king of Babylon) (s:kuaihtan/sutan) (r:19.10.15/38.11.10/19.29.5/43.19.33/24.28.2) (q:draft)
kuaitanin = (t:v) (w:break/snap/shatter) (d:connective form of kuaitan, breaking a long thing such as a bow, a leg bone or a yoke bar in two) (e:amah in thalpi ~, teipi susia a/ka hakkol ~ ka ukna nong nial a | you broke my yoke and refused my rule/a hiangte ~, keutumsak ding | break off its branches and make it wither/a khe ~ a luang a paihkhiat nading | to have the legs broken and the bodies taken down) (b:kuaitan) (r:19.46.9/43.19.31/24.2.20/26.17.9) (q:draft)
kuaitanzo = (t:v) (w:have broken/manage to break) (d:kuaitan break with zo, showing the act is achieved or completed) (e:kibawl hakkol na ~ hi) (b:kuaitan) (r:24.28.13) (q:draft)
kuak = (t:n) (w:hollow/cavity) (d:a hollow or bowl-shaped space: khut kuak is the hollow of the hand, lo kaihna kuak a furrow; a kuak-in means hollow inside) (e:ama khut ~ sungah tuite tehin/lo kaihna ~ dung tawn | along the length of a furrow/Singpekte tawh ~ nei-in biakna tau na bawl ding a | make the altar hollow, out of boards/a om khuamluzepna ~ nihte | the two bowl-shaped capitals) (r:23.40.12/2.38.7/9.14.14/2.27.8/11.7.41) (q:draft)
kuakin = (t:adv) (w:hollow) (d:kuak hollow with the ending in; a kuakin bawl is make something hollow inside) (e:Singpekte tawh a ~ na bawl ding hi/singpekte tawh biakna tau a ~ a bawl hi | he made the altar hollow, out of boards) (b:kuak) (r:2.27.8/2.38.7) (q:draft)
kuakte = (t:see) <ma-kuakte>
kuakua = (t:pron) (w:whoever/whosoever) (d:kua who doubled; kuakua ahih hangin is whoever he may be) (e:~ ahih hangin ama mawhna dan/note pen ~ hita le-uh cin | whoever you may be) (s:peuhmah) (r:48.5.10/45.2.1) (q:draft)
kual = (t:n) (w:ring) (d:a ring or loop, such as the gold rings that hold poles or chains) (e:kiu lite tung ading ~ li sung hi/kham ~ li na bawl ding a | you shall make four gold rings/a pang khatah ~ nih | two rings on one side/kham ~ nih bawl uh a | they made two gold rings) (r:2.38.5/2.39.17/2.25.26/2.37.3/2.39.19) (q:draft)
kual = (t:adv) (w:around/roundabout) (d:going round in a circuit or curve rather than straight: kual pai is go around, and of a boundary it means curve or turn) (e:ni sagih sung a ~ paikhit uh ciangin/nung lamah ~ pai in la | circle around behind them/Dan panin ~ pai-in Sidon tung uh a | from Dan they went around and reached Sidon/Seir Mual-ah gamgi ~ a | the boundary curved round to Mount Seir) (r:12.3.9/10.5.23/10.24.6/6.15.10) (q:draft)
kualah = (t:n) (w:to the ring/at the ring) (d:kual ring with ah, at or to) (e:siampipuan’ ~ khaudum khatin) (b:kual) (r:2.28.28) (q:draft)
kualin = (t:adv) (w:around/round about) (d:kual, around, with the ending in: going round in a circle or curve; kawi kualin is turning round) (e:Millo panin a ~ khuapi lam hi/Shikkeron-ah gamgi kawi ~ | the boundary turned round toward Shikkeron/laikung tawh a ~ a ciamteh hi | he marks it in a circle with a marker) (b:kual) (r:13.11.8/6.15.11/23.44.13) (q:draft)
kualpai = (t:v) (w:go around/go round about) (d:kual around with pai go: go by a roundabout way; kualpai sak is send around) (e:Jeroboam in ~ sak hi) (r:14.13.13) (q:draft)
kualte = (t:n) (w:rings) (d:plural of kual, ring: the rings on the ark, the table and the altar through which the carrying poles pass) (e:a zawl gei-ah a ~ om hi/a zawlpeek gei-ah a ~ om ding hi | the rings are to be close to the rim/a kiu li, a khe lite-ah a ~ gak hi | he fastened the rings to the four corners, where the four legs were) (b:kual) (r:2.37.14/2.25.14/2.25.27/2.37.13) (q:draft)
kualte = (t:n) (w:rims) (d:rims of wheels) (e:Tua leengpei ~ tungah mittang vive) (b:kual) (r:26.1.18) (q:draft)
kuam = (t:n) (w:valley/gorge/plain) (d:low ground between hills: a valley, gorge or plain; kuam sung is the inside of the valley) (e:Filistiate in ~ sung luh kik lai uh hi/Jordan ~ khempeuh teel a | he chose the whole plain of the Jordan/Arnon ~ mong-a om Aroer pan | from Aroer on the rim of the Arnon Gorge/kei zong ~ sungah ka va pai a | so I went out to the plain) (s:guam/mualkuam) (a:mual) (r:13.14.13/6.13.9/1.13.11/26.3.23) (q:draft)
Kuam = (t:n) (w:valley) (d:kuam, valley, written with a capital as part of a place name, as in Zered Kuam and Ci Kuam, the Valley of Salt) (e:Zered ~ ah giahphual sat uh hi/tua mun pen Eshkol ~ kici hi | that place was called the Valley of Eshkol/Edom mite tulsawm Ci ~ ah thatin | he struck down ten thousand Edomites in the Valley of Salt) (b:kuam) (r:4.21.12/4.13.24/12.14.7) (q:draft)
kuama = (t:pron) (w:anyone/no one) (d:form of kuamah used before a noun as a possessive or before a verb it governs, mostly in negative clauses) (e:Pasian in ~ maitang a zahtak kei hi/~ an ka ne kei uh hi | we did not eat anyone’s food/Hih thu ~ theih loh nadingin kikeem un | see that no one knows about this/~ delh lopi-in migilote taimang a | the wicked flee though no one pursues) (s:kuamah) (r:45.2.11/24.41.4/53.3.8/40.9.30/20.28.1) (q:draft)
Kuama = (t:n) (w:valley) (d:Kuam valley with a, in the Valley; Aven Kuama teng mi are those who live in the Valley of Aven) (e:Aven ~ teng mi khempeuh) (b:Kuam) (r:30.1.5) (q:draft)
kuamah = (t:pron) (w:no one/nobody) (d:no one, nobody: used with a negative verb, so that kuamah om lo is there is no one; kuamah in marks it as the subject) (e:Lei piancil akipanin ~ in suahpih mittaw/a mai-ah ~ om ngam lo hi | no one dares to stand before it/Zeisu longal ~ dang a mu kei uh hi | they saw no one else except Jesus/~ in tua mizawngpa phawk kha lo hi | nobody remembered that poor man) (s:kuama) (a:mikim/mikhempeuh) (r:43.9.32/2.23.26/18.41.10/40.17.8/21.9.15)
Kuamah = (t:n) (w:valley) (d:Kuam, valley as part of a place name, with the place marker ah: in the Valley or to the Valley) (e:amaute Eshkol ~ paito-in tua gam/Ci ~ Edom mite tulsawm leh tulgiat that hi | he struck down eighteen thousand Edomites in the Valley of Salt/phutin Kumpipa’ ~ om hi | he set it up, and it stands in the King’s Valley) (b:Kuam) (r:4.32.9/13.18.12/10.18.18) (q:draft)
kuamahdang = (t:pron) (w:no one else/nobody else) (d:kuamah, anyone, no one, with dang other; used with a negative) (e:~ awk loin) (r:20.1.18) (q:draft)
kuamahpeuh = (t:pron) (w:anyone)
kuami = (t:pron) (w:who/what people) (d:kua who with mi person: asks who someone is or where he belongs) (e:Note ~ na hi uh hiam) (b:kua) (r:42.13.25/42.13.27) (q:draft)
kuamkeu = (t:n) (w:valley/dry valley) (d:kuam, valley, with keu, dry: a dry valley; in Psalm 84 it stands for the Valley of Baka) (e:Amaute in ~ mun kantanin) (r:19.84.6)
Kuamkeu = (t:n) (w:dry valley) (d:kuam valley with keu dry; used as a place name, NIV Valley of Baka) (e:Amaute in ~ mun kantanin) (b:kuamkeu) (r:19.84.6) (q:draft)
kuampi = (t:n) (w:valley/great valley) (d:kuam, valley, with -pi, great: a large or deep valley) (e:a kikalah ~ om ding hi/a kidim-a om ~ khatah hong koih hi | he set me down in a valley that was full) (b:kuam) (r:38.14.4/26.37.1) (q:draft)
kuampi = (t:n) (w:abyss/bottomless pit) (d:the deep pit in which Satan is shut up) (e:~ sungah a khiatsuk khit ciangin/~ kong khak cipin a tungah a ciamteh hi | he shut the door of the Abyss and sealed it over him/~ kong hon’na tawh leh sikkhau lian khat | with the key to the Abyss and a great chain) (s:kuamthuk) (b:kuam) (r:66.20.3/66.20.1) (q:draft)
kuampite = (t:n) (w:valleys) (d:kuam valley with pi, great, and the plural te) (e:~ an tawh kidim a/guam thukte, leh ~ kiangah | to the ravines and the valleys) (s:kuamte/guamte) (a:mualte) (b:kuampi) (r:19.65.13/26.6.3) (q:draft)
kuamsung = (t:n) (w:valley/plain) (d:the inside of a valley, low ground between hills, set against mualtung, the hilltop) (e:Refaim ~ dim uh hi/Lonona ~ a zuansuk bawngte bangin | like cattle that go down to the plain/amah pen ~ pasian hi lo hi | he is not a god of the valleys/Shitthim ~ khempeuh a kawtsak ding hi | it will water the whole valley of Shittim) (s:kuam) (a:mualtung) (r:10.5.18/11.20.28/23.63.14/29.3.18) (q:draft)
kuamte = (t:n) (w:valleys/plains/ravines) (d:plural of kuam: valleys, ravines or plains) (e:Nangmah in ~ sung panin ciktui na phulkhiasak hi/Judah ~ pen sakol leeng tawh kidim a | the valleys of Judah are full of chariots/Saupi a kiphah ~ tawh kibang a | like valleys that spread out far/tua khuapite, ~ khempeuh | those cities and the entire plain) (s:guamte/kuampite) (a:mualte) (b:kuam) (r:19.104.10/23.22.7/4.24.6/1.19.25) (q:draft)
kuamthuk = (t:n) (w:abyss/deep pit/bottomless pit) (d:kuam valley, hollow, with thuk deep) (e:~ sung pan a hong pusuakkhia ding) (s:kuampi) (r:66.17.8) (q:draft)
Kuamthuk = (t:n) (w:valley/deep valley) (d:kuam valley with thuk deep) (e:~ khempeuh kisangtosak ding a) (b:kuamthuk) (r:23.40.4) (q:draft)
kuan = (t:v) (w:go out/set out/march/go to war) (d:set out for a task: go out to war against an enemy, or go out to work in the field) (e:Jehoshafat a sim dingin hong ~ uh hi/galdona ah a ~ galkapte tungah | to the soldiers who had gone into battle/Edrei-ah amaute do dingin ~ uh hi | they marched out to fight them at Edrei/ci-a tua mite a ~ uh hi | so those men went) (s:kuankhia) (a:ciahkik) (r:14.20.1/7.20.21/4.31.21/4.21.33/40.20.4) (q:draft)
kuana = (t:num) (w:ninth) (d:kua nine with the ordinal ending -na; sawm-le-kuana is nineteenth) (e:a giatna Johanan, a ~ Elzabad/a ~ Jeshua tung, a sawmna Shekaiah tung | the ninth to Jeshua, the tenth to Shekaniah/kha ~ a ni sawmnih leh nili ni | the twenty-fourth day of the ninth month/a sawm-le-~ Pethahiah tung | the nineteenth to Pethahiah) (b:kua) (r:13.12.12/13.24.11/37.2.18/13.24.16) (q:draft)
kuancil = (t:v) (w:set out/first set out) (d:kuan set out, go to war, with cil, at the beginning) (e:a do dingin na ~ lai-in) (r:7.8.1) (q:draft)
kuang = (t:n) (w:basin/bowl/trough) (d:an open vessel: a bowl for food, a basin for washing, or a trough) (e:Kei tawh ~ sungah an/kisilna ~ leh a ngakna | the basin for washing and its stand/na annel mekna ~ sungte-ah | into your kneading troughs/ngun ~ khat ciangin shekel sawmsagih gik a | each silver bowl weighed seventy shekels) (r:40.26.23/2.40.11/2.8.3/4.7.85) (q:draft)
kuang = (t:v) (w:burn/blaze) (d:burn with a flame, blaze; also said of anger that burns like fire) (e:Amaute tungah mei-am ~ zusak in/en in, sawlpang ~ hi | look, the bush was on fire/mei in mual kang-in ~ hi | the mountain was ablaze with fire/Nangma hazat hehna, mei bangin ~ paisuak ding ahi hiam | will your jealousy burn like fire forever) (s:kang) (r:19.140.10/2.3.2/5.9.15/19.79.5) (q:draft)
kuanga = (t:v) (w:burning) (d:kuang burn with the linking suffix a) (e:Amah in ~ a taang meivak hi) (b:kuang) (r:43.5.35) (q:draft)
kuangah = (t:n) (w:in the pouch/in the bowl) (d:kuang bowl with the place marker ah; saili kuangah is in the pouch of a sling) (e:Saili ~ sailungtang khihcip lehang) (b:kuang) (r:20.26.8) (q:draft)
kuangdai = (t:n) (w:plate/dish/platter) (d:a wide shallow dish, larger than kuang bowl) (e:shekel za leh sawmthum a gik ngun ~ khat/ngun ~ sawm-le-nih, ngun kuang sawm-le-nih | twelve silver plates, twelve silver bowls/~ khat sungah a lutang hong paipihin | he brought his head on a platter) (s:dalkuang) (r:4.7.13/4.7.84/41.6.28) (q:draft)
kuangdaite = (t:n) (w:plates/dishes) (d:kuangdai with plural -te, the flat dishes of the table in the tabernacle) (e:tua tungah a ~, paknamtui pakante/paknamtui’ adingin ~ leh pakante | the plates and dishes for incense/mei-am luahna ~, kuangte, beelte | the censers, the bowls and the pots) (b:kuangdai) (r:4.4.7/2.37.16/24.52.19) (q:draft)
kuangin = (t:v) (w:burn/blaze/break out) (d:kuang, burn with flame, with the linking suffix -in) (e:meivak bangin ~ a taang hi/~, giahphual nawl kimkhat kangtum hi | it burned and consumed part of the outskirts of the camp/Mei ~ gam kang a | a fire breaks out and burns the land/Tua sung panin mei hong ~ | from there a fire will break out/meilah kuang bangin ~ a om aksi lianpi khat | a great star blazing like a torch) (b:kuang) (r:43.5.35/2.22.6/4.11.1/26.5.4/66.8.10) (q:draft)
kuangkhia = (t:v) (w:blaze out/flare up/burn forth) (d:kuang burn with khia out) (e:Ama kam panin mei ~ a/ama tung panin mei-am san ~ hi | burning coals blazed out from him/ka hehna mei bangin hong ~ ding a | my wrath will flare up like fire/Itna in mei bangin ~ a | love blazes like fire) (b:kuang) (r:18.41.19/24.4.4/19.18.8/22.8.6) (q:draft)
kuangkik = (t:v) (w:burn again/flame up again) (d:kuang burn with kik, again) (e:cikmah hunin ~ nawn lo ding hi) (b:kuang) (r:18.18.5) (q:draft)
kuangkuang = (t:v) (w:burn/keep burning/blaze) (d:kuang burn, doubled for an action that goes on) (e:bang tanvei meikuang bangin ~ ding) (r:19.89.46) (q:draft)
kuanglekeute = (t:n) (w:vessels/utensils/dishes) (d:household vessels and utensils of all kinds, a pair-word built on kuang, bowl, with plural te) (e:sing tawh kibawl ~ ahihleh/umlebeel, ~, hai a kipan thawl dongin | pots and vessels, from the cups to the jars) (r:3.15.12/23.22.24) (q:draft)
kuangpi = (t:n) (w:large basin/basin/Sea) (d:kuang basin with pi big; tui kuangpi is the great bronze basin of the temple, called the Sea) (e:~ sung khatah tui sung a/bawngtalte tung panin tui ~ lakhia sukin | he took the Sea down from the bulls/khuampi nih ~ khat | the two pillars and the Sea) (s:tuikuangpi) (b:kuang) (r:43.13.5/12.16.17/24.52.20) (q:draft)
kuangsak = (t:v) (w:kindle/set on fire/make burn) (d:kuang burn with causative sak; also of anger, make it blaze) (e:sing in mei ~ a/Leitungah mei ~ dingin hong pai ka hi hi | I have come to kindle fire on the earth/Gamlak lopa phate ~ a | it sets the forest thickets ablaze/mai-ah meivakte ~ ding uh hi | they are to keep the lamps burning before him) (s:kangsak/tawhkuang/halsak) (a:sumit/phelh/mitsak) (b:kuang) (r:20.26.21/42.12.49/23.9.18/2.27.21) (q:draft)
kuangsakin = (t:v) (w:set ablaze/kindle) (d:kuangsak make burn with the linking suffix in) (e:mei in selkeu ~ mei in tui) (b:kuangsak) (r:23.64.1) (q:draft)
kuangte = (t:n) (w:bowls/basins/trays/troughs) (d:plural of kuang: bowls, basins or trays) (e:a taitehte leh a ~ kham citak/sisan kimkhat la-in, ~ sungah koih a | he took half of the blood and put it in bowls/in lupnate, ~, leh leibeelte | bedding, bowls and clay pots/ngun ~, meitehte, haite, peengkulte | silver basins, wick trimmers, bowls, trumpets) (b:kuang) (r:2.25.38/10.17.28/2.24.6/12.12.13) (q:draft)
kuangtuahte = (t:n) (w:sistrums/castanets) (d:a percussion instrument played in worship, listed between timbrels and cymbals; plural te) (e:~ leh daltuahte tumin lungdamin) (r:10.6.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
