kuankhiasak = (t:v) (w:send out/march out) (d:kuankhia set out, with the causative sak: make soldiers go out to war) (e:galkap tul khat ~ a) (b:kuankhia) (r:30.5.3) (q:draft)
kuankhiat = (t:v) (w:go out/march out/set out) (d:form of kuankhia used before words such as ciang and khit or before a noun) (e:nangma mite’ mai-ah na ~ ciang/kote do dingin hong ~ uh ciangin | when they come out to fight us/nang a do dingin hong ~ ciangun | when they come out against you/amaute hong ~ simin | as often as they went out) (b:kuankhia) (r:19.68.7/6.8.5/7.9.33/9.18.30) (q:draft)
kuankhiate = (t:n) (w:those who set out/those who go out) (d:kuankhia, set out, with plural te: the people who set out) (e:a ~ bangin na lungdam ding uh hi) (b:kuankhia) (r:23.30.29) (q:draft)
kuankhiatna = (t:n) (w:going out/setting out/undertaking) (d:kuankhiat go out with the noun suffix na, a going out to battle or to a task) (e:a ~ khempeuh ah mavang hi/David a ~ Saul in a muh ciangin | when Saul saw David going out/le ~ le ciahkik nadingin | for going out and coming back) (s:kuanna) (a:ciahkikna) (b:kuankhiat) (r:12.18.7/9.17.55/6.14.11) (q:draft)
kuankhiatpih = (t:v) (w:lead out/march out with) (d:kuankhiat, set out, with pih, together with: go out to war at the head of others) (e:Israel a ~ leh a ciahpih) (a:ciahpih) (b:kuankhiat) (r:13.11.2) (q:draft)
kuankhiazo = (t:v) (w:have come out/have set out) (d:kuankhia go out with zo, showing the act is completed) (e:a bukna sawlkawm panin hong ~ a) (b:kuankhia) (r:24.4.7) (q:draft)
kuankhop = (t:v) (w:go out together/go along with) (d:kuan, set out for work, with khop, together) (e:ama numeite tawh na ~ hoih mahmah hi) (s:kuankhawm) (r:8.2.22) (q:draft)
kuankik = (t:v) (w:go again/go back/return) (d:kuan set out with kik, again or back) (e:a lungsim kikheelin a ~ hi/Benjamin mite a sim dingin ~ lai ding ka hi uh hiam | shall we go out again to fight the Benjamites/kulh tungah ka vekpi-un ka ~ uh hi | we all went back to the wall) (b:kuan) (r:40.21.29/7.20.28/16.4.15) (q:draft)
kuankikin = (t:v) (w:set out again/go again) (d:kuankik set out again with the linking suffix in) (e:Syria kumpipa khatvei ~) (b:kuankik) (r:27.11.13) (q:draft)
kuankuan = (t:adv) (w:strutting) (d:descriptive word after pai walk, of the proud walk of a rooster) (e:A kihisak pai ~) (s:kuahkuah) (r:20.30.31) (q:draft, low confidence)
kuankuanta = (t:adv) (d:apparently shows that something is steadily on its way to happening, with ta, now; maimang kuankuanta is now passing away, coming to nothing) (e:tu-in a maimang ~ ding) (r:46.2.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
kuanlamin = (t:adv) (w:on the way in/when going) (d:kuan set out, go, with lamin, in the direction or at the time of) (e:Gam uk ulianpa in a ~ a tot lampiteng) (r:26.46.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
kuanna = (t:n) (w:setting out/marching out/coming) (d:the act of setting out, especially to war; hong kuanna lampi, the way by which he came) (e:Hong ~ lampi mahah amah ciahkik ding/Ammon kumpipa Nahash hong ~ na muh uh ciangin | when you saw Nahash king of the Ammonites coming against you/Izipt galkap honpi tawh hong ~ thu | the report that he was marching out with a great Egyptian army/nong ~ lampi lam mahah | by the very way you came) (s:kuankhiatna) (b:kuan) (r:23.37.34/9.12.12/23.37.9/23.37.29) (q:draft)
kuansak = (t:v) (w:send out/send into battle/bring against) (d:kuan, set out, with the causative -sak: make someone set out, especially to war) (e:gal sungah na ~ ding uh hi/gam khat kong ~ ding hi | I will send a nation against you/namsau khat kong ~ ding hi | I will bring a sword against you/a do dingin gal ka ~ ding hi | I will send war against them) (s:sawlkhia) (b:kuan) (r:4.31.4/24.5.15/26.6.3/30.7.9) (q:draft)
