lahsa = (t:v) (w:shown/have shown) (d:lah, show, with sa for a completed action: have shown; before a noun, that which was shown) (e:Topa in Moses tungah a ~ lim tawh/Mual tungah nang kong ~ lim bangin | according to the pattern I showed you on the mountain/note mai-a kong ~ ka thukham bangin | according to my law that I set before you/ka Pa’ hong ~ thute bek | only the things my Father has shown me) (s:lakkhin) (b:lah) (r:4.8.4/58.8.5/24.26.4/43.8.38) (q:draft)
lahsan = (t:v) (w:shake at/raise against) (d:lah, show, with san, toward: hold up the fist against someone) (e:Pasian langpangin a khuttum a ~) (b:lah) (r:18.15.25) (q:draft)
lahsate = (t:n) (w:things shown/what was shown) (d:lahsa shown, with the plural te) (e:kong ~ khempeuh tawh kituakin/amau tunga nalamdang a ~ | the wonders he had shown them) (b:lahsa) (r:2.25.9/19.78.11) (q:draft)
lahte = (t:n) (w:things shown) (d:lah show with the plural te, making a noun, the things that someone shows; nalamdang lahte are the signs shown) (e:nang’ tungah kong ~ khempeuh tawh kituakin/Zeisu in nalamdang a ~ | the signs that Jesus was performing/a lamdang nate, ama nalamdang ~ | his wonders, the miracles he showed) (b:lah) (r:2.25.9/43.2.23/19.105.5) (q:draft)
lahtel = (t:v) (w:show clearly/prove/demonstrate) (d:lah, show, with tel, clearly: make something plain or prove it; lahtel nading is evidence or proof) (e:kilawm mi ahihna a ~ theih leh/~ nadingin tua ganhing paipihsak in | let him bring the animal as evidence/a ~ theih uh bangmah om lo hi | there was nothing they could prove/na ~ nopna teng uh gen un | set forth what you want to prove) (s:laktel) (r:11.1.52/2.22.13/44.25.7/23.41.21) (q:draft)
lahtelnate = (t:n) (w:declarations/explanations) (d:lahtel, show clearly, with na and plural te: things set out plainly) (e:ka ~ na za un) (b:lahtel) (r:18.13.17) (q:draft)
lahtheih = (t:v) (w:be able to show/can show) (d:lah, show, with theih, be able; lahtheih nadingin means so that one may show) (e:ama tungah migitna ka ~ nadingin/ka sianthona ka ~ nadingin | so that I may show my holiness/a hehna le a vangliatna a ~ nading | to show his wrath and his power/ama minthanna a ~ nadingin | so that he might show his glory) (s:lakthei) (b:lah) (r:10.9.1/45.9.22/26.38.16/45.9.23) (q:draft)
lai = (t:n) (w:writing) (d:written words, a document or anything set down in writing) (e:~ nasim in/thu piakna ~ a hawmkhia hi | he issued the written decree/Hih ~ sim dih in | read this, please) (r:27.6.9/23.29.12) of a composing text
lai = (t:n) (w:letter) (d:a written message sent to someone) (e:~ hong khak ve/Joab kiangah ~ khat gelh a | he wrote a letter to Joab/kamtaite’ tung panin a ~ sangin sim hi | he received the letter from the messengers and read it/Hih ~ na sim khit uh ciangin | after you have read this letter) (s:laikhak) (r:10.11.14/12.19.14/51.4.16)
Lai = (t:n) (w:Scripture/writing) (d:lai, writing, with a capital in Lai Siangtho, Holy Scripture, the Bible) (e:tua ~ Siangtho pan akipan Zeisu thu/~ Siangtho a theih nadingun | so that they could understand the Scriptures/~ Siangtho sungah a kigelh mah bangin | as it is written in the Scriptures/~ Siangtho simin | reading Scripture) (b:lai) (r:44.8.35/42.24.45/46.15.4/54.4.13) (q:draft)
Laia = (t:n) (w:lyre/harp) (d:a stringed instrument, named beside harp and laiza; probably the English word lyre) (e:~ khausai lasakna tawh Topa phat unla/~ lasakna tawh Topa’ tungah phatna late sa unla | sing songs of praise to the Lord with the harp) (s:laiza) (r:19.33.2/19.98.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
laiah = (t:adv) (w:there/at that place) (d:lai place with the place marker ah, in tua laiah, there; more often written lai-ah) (e:tua ~ va si ni/tua ~ ka teeng ding uh hi | we will live there) (s:laitakah) (r:24.8.14/24.42.14) (q:draft)
laibawl = (t:v) (w:make a will/draw up a document) (d:lai, writing, with bawl, make; a laibawl pa is the man who made the will) (e:a ~ pa a sih phot ding kisam hi/A ~ pa a hin laiteng | as long as the one who made the will is alive) (b:lai) (r:58.9.16/58.9.17) (q:draft)
laibu = (t:n) (w:book) (d:a book or scroll that holds writing) (e:Nuntakna ~ sungah a min om lo/thukham kammalte ~ sunga gelh a man ciangin | when he had finished writing the words of the law in a book/Hih ~ sungah a kigelh lo lim dang tampi | many other signs that are not written in this book/kumpipa mai-ah tua ~ sim hi | he read the book before the king) (r:66.20.15/5.31.24/43.20.30/12.22.10)
laibu = (t:n) (w:record) (d:a written account or register of people and events) (e:Hih pen Adam’ suanlekhakte’ ~ ahi hi/amah in tuate ~ khat sungah gelhin | he wrote them down in a record) (r:1.5.1/9.10.25)
Laibu = (t:n) (w:book/record) (d:book, capitalised as part of the title of a named book) (e:Israel Kumpite’ Khang Tangthu ~ sungah kigelh/Judah leh Israel Kumpite’ ~ sungah kigelh hi | it is written in the book of the kings of Judah and Israel/Khang Tangthu ~ sungah kigelh hi | it is recorded in the book of the annals) (b:laibu) (r:12.15.11/14.16.11/16.12.23) (q:draft)
laibute = (t:n) (w:books/scrolls) (d:plural of laibu: books or scrolls) (e:amau ~ hong paipih uh a/~ a kiphen hi | the books were opened/ka puanza leh ~ | my cloak and the scrolls/mipi’ zakin Moses’ ~ sim uh a | they read the books of Moses in the hearing of the people) (b:laibu) (r:44.19.19/27.7.10/55.4.13/16.13.1) (q:draft)
laidal = (t:n) (w:scroll/writing tablet/sheet) (d:a sheet or surface to write on; a scroll when it is rolled up) (e:Zekhariah in zong ~ khat ngen a/~ bangin vantungte kizial ding hi | the heavens will be rolled up like a scroll/Van in ~ zial bangin kizial mang hi | the sky rolled away like a scroll being rolled up) (s:laizial) (r:42.1.63/23.34.4/66.6.14) (q:draft)
laidalte = (t:n) (w:scrolls/sheets/parchments) (d:plural of laidal; savun laidalte are sheets of skin, parchments) (e:savun ~ tawh zong hong pua in) (b:laidal) (r:55.4.13) (q:draft)
laigawp = (t:v) (w:batter/strike violently) (d:strike or knock about with force; gawp marks violent or thorough action) (e:tua tuutal ~ a) (r:27.8.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
laigelh = (t:v) (w:write/write a letter) (d:lai writing and gelh write as one word; laigelh nading is something to write with) (e:thukimna tawh kumpipa tungah ~ uh a/Pilat in ~ a, singlamteh tungah a suang hi | Pilate wrote a notice and fastened it to the cross/~ nading a tawi mi khat | a man who carried a writing kit) (s:gelh) (r:15.4.7/43.19.19/26.9.2) (q:draft)
laigelhna = (t:n) (w:writing/letter/what is written) (d:the act of writing or the thing written) (e:Mordekai’ ~ tawh kizui-in/Tua ka hong ~ sungah ka cihnopna pen | what I meant in what I wrote to you/A ~ sungah a telhak thu tampi om a | in his letters there are many things hard to understand/tua ka hong ~ hangin ka kisik kei hi | I do not regret that letter of mine) (s:laikhak) (b:laigelh) (r:17.9.23/46.5.11/61.3.16/47.7.8) (q:draft)
laigelhna = (t:n) (w:writing kit/inkhorn) (d:the tool for writing carried by a scribe) (e:~ a tawi mipa in) (b:laigelh) (r:26.9.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
laigelhnate = (t:n) (w:writings) (d:laigelhna, a writing, with the plural te: written works, as the writings of the prophets) (e:kamsangte’ ~ le a nungta tawntung) (s:laigelhte) (b:laigelhna) (r:45.16.26) (q:draft)
laigelhte = (t:n) (w:secretaries/scribes/writers) (d:laigelh, writer, with the plural te: people whose work is writing, such as secretaries and scribes) (e:pawlkhatte in ~, leh za neite/Levi mi pawlkhatte pen ~, le za neite | some of the Levites were secretaries and officers) (s:laitheite/atte) (b:laigelh) (r:14.34.13) (q:draft)
laigelhte = (t:n) (w:letters/writings/dispatches) (d:laigelh with the plural te: things that someone has written, such as letters, dispatches and the writings of the prophets) (e:Paul’ ~ khauhin nasia mahmah a/Haman in a ~ dawhkik nadingin | to revoke the letters that Haman wrote/kamsangte’ ~ siksanin a gen hi | he spoke on the basis of the writings of the prophets) (s:laikhakte/laite/laigelhnate) (b:laigelh) (r:47.10.10/17.8.5/44.28.23) (q:draft)
laigui = (t:n) (w:umbilical cord) (d:the cord that joins a child to its mother before birth; laigui zoppihte, those joined by the same cord, are children of the same mother) (e:ka sanggam, ka ~ zoppihte ahi uh hi) (r:7.8.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
laih = (t:v) (w:replace/succeed/exchange/substitute) (d:take the place or office of another, or put one thing in place of another; galvil laih is change the guard) (e:Porsias Festas in Feliks za a ~ hi/Jehoiada leh Abiathar in ~ uh hi | Jehoiada and Abiathar succeeded him/hakkol khat tawh ka ~ ding hi | I will replace it with a yoke/Kei hong ~ pa pil taleh hai taleh | whether the one who succeeds me is wise or foolish/amaute in galvil a ~ khit phet | just after they had changed the guard) (s:kheek/khek) (r:44.24.27/3.27.10/13.27.34/24.28.13/21.2.19/7.7.19) (q:draft)
laihilh = (t:n) (w:teacher/teaching) (d:lai, writing, with hilh, teach: one who teaches, or the work of teaching; laihilh za is the office of teacher) (e:~ za-ah ahi zongin kei hong koih zo/A vekpi-un ~, thuhilh hi lo uh a | not all are teachers or preachers/pawlpi kem Sia za leh ~ za | the office of pastor and of teacher/pawlkhatte ~ nasep a sem dingin | some to do the work of teaching) (s:sia/siapa) (r:55.1.11/49.4.11/46.12.29) (q:draft)
laihilhna = (t:n) (w:teaching/instruction/lecture) (d:laihilh, teach, with the noun suffix na: teaching; laihilhna sanginn is a school or lecture hall) (e:Tirannas ~ sanginn ah ni simin) (s:thuhilhna/hilhna) (b:laihilh) (r:44.19.9) (q:draft)
laihilhte = (t:n) (w:teachers) (d:laihilh, teacher, with the plural te: those who teach in the church) (e:A om khempeuh in ~ ahi uh hiam/a thumna ~, tua khit ciangin | third teachers, and after that) (s:siate) (b:laihilh) (r:46.12.29/46.12.28) (q:draft)
laihin = (t:v) (w:succeeding/replacing/taking the place of) (d:laih replace, with the linking suffix in: taking the place or office of another) (e:a pa Herod’ za ~ Judea gam) (b:laih) (r:40.2.22) (q:draft)
laihnuam = (t:v) (w:want to replace/want to change) (d:laih, replace, with nuam, want: wish to put one thing in place of another, as changing the gospel for another message) (e:thudang tawh ~ uh ahih manin) (r:48.1.7) (q:draft)
laikhak = (t:n) (w:letter) (d:a written message sent to someone; laikhak sim is read a letter) (e:a kamtaipa in ~ khat hong pia hi/Israel kumpipa in a ~ a sim ciangin | when the king of Israel read the letter/Mite in tua ~ a sim uh ciangin | when the people read that letter/ama kiangah ~ khat hong tung a | a letter came to him) (s:lai/laikhakna) (r:16.6.5/24.29.29/12.5.7/44.15.31/14.21.12) (q:draft)
laikhak = (t:v) (w:send a letter/write to) (d:lai, letter, with khak, send: send a letter to someone; more often written as two words, lai khak) (e:kumpi Darias’ tungah ~ uh hi) (r:15.5.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
laikhakna = (t:n) (w:letter/writing) (d:laikhak, send a letter, with the noun suffix na: the letter sent or the sending of it) (e:hih kong ~ sungah/Zefaniah’ kiangah a ~ thu tawh kisai | concerning the letter he sent to Zephaniah) (s:laikhak/laigelhna) (b:laikhak) (r:45.15.15/24.29.28) (q:draft)
laikhakte = (t:n) (w:letters) (d:laikhak, letter, with the plural te: written messages sent to someone; laikhakte gelh is write letters) (e:kumpipa’ ~ amaute tungah ka pia hi/Tobiah’ ~ zong amaute tungah tung hi | the letters of Tobiah also reached them/amah in Ahab’ minin ~ gelhin | she wrote letters in the name of Ahab/Manasseh mite tungah zong ~ gelh hi | he also wrote letters to the people of Manasseh) (s:laite/laigelhte) (r:16.2.9/14.30.1/16.6.17/11.21.8) (q:draft)
laikhia = (t:v) (w:tear down/demolish/pull down) (d:pull a building apart and clear it away; built with khia, out) (e:a inn a ~ uh hi) (s:phelkhia/susia) (r:14.23.17) (q:draft, low confidence)
laikung = (t:n) (w:pen/stylus/marker) (d:a tool for writing or for marking a line; sik laikung is an iron pen) (e:~ leh laitui tawh gelh ding/ka leii in lai theipa’ ~ tawh kibang hi | my tongue is like the pen of a skilled writer/khau khungin ~ tawh ciamteh hi | he stretches a line and marks it with a marker/sik ~ khat tawh kigelh hi | it is written with an iron pen) (r:64.1.13/23.44.13/19.45.1/24.17.1) (q:draft)
lailai = (t:adv) (w:still/yet/keep on) (d:placed after a verb: keep on doing, still do in spite of something) (e:Piter in kong kiu ~ a/na zum thei kei ~ hi | you still cannot feel shame/ama tungah amaute khial ~ uh a | they kept on sinning against him/note na kisik nuam kei ~ uh hi | you still would not repent/um zo lo ~-in | while they still could not believe) (s:veve) (r:44.12.16/19.78.17/24.3.3/37.2.17/42.24.41) (q:draft)
lailaina = (t:part) (d:lailai, still, with the noun-forming ending na, placed after a verb: the going on doing it, as in gen ngam lailaina, daring to keep on speaking) (e:thu kong gen ngam ~ hong maisak in) (b:lailai) (r:1.18.31) (q:draft)
laimal = (t:n) (w:letter/written character/writing/inscription) (d:lai, writing, with mal, a single item: a written letter or word, or what is written) (e:~ gol pipi-in lai ka hong gelh/suangpek tungah a kigelh ~ hi a | it was letters written on stone tablets/Tua a kigelh ~ in hi bang ahi hi | the writing that was written is this) (r:48.6.11/27.5.25/47.3.7) (q:draft)
laimalin = (t:adv) (w:in letters/with letters) (d:laimal written letter, with the marker in showing means) (e:suangpeek tungah ~ kigelh sihna) (b:laimal) (r:47.3.7) (q:draft)
laimalte = (t:n) (w:letters/writing/inscription) (d:laimal, written letter, with the plural te) (e:Bang zah a lian ~ tawh ka khutin/hih ~ tua khut a hong gelh sak hi | he made that hand write these letters) (b:laimal) (r:48.6.11/27.5.24) (q:draft)
laina = (t:part) (d:lai, still, with the noun-forming ending na, placed after a verb, the being still so, as in a om laina, those still remaining, a nuntak laina, their living on) (e:a nuntak ~ ding uh hun/a suakta a om ~ a om leh | if any who escaped are still left/tu dongin na huh ~ uh tawh | with your still helping until now/nupi khempeuhte kiangah a gen ~-ah | as he went on speaking to all the women) (r:27.7.12/30.6.9/58.6.10/24.44.24) (q:draft, low confidence)
lainat = (t:v) (w:have compassion/feel pity/be concerned) (d:feel pain within for someone; nang’ lainat nading is something for you to be troubled about) (e:hehpih lo, ~ lo, it loin ka sisak ding/nang’ ~ nading bang om ahi hiam | what is there for you to be concerned about) (s:hehpih/hehpihhuaisa) (r:24.13.14/18.19.4) (q:draft)
lainatna = (t:n) (w:compassion/tenderness/concern) (d:lainat, feel compassion, with the noun suffix na: tender feeling or concern for someone) (e:Na lungduaina leh nong ~ kote’ adingin/nang’ ~ ding bang om ahi hiam | what concern is it of yours) (s:hehpihna) (b:lainat) (r:23.63.15/18.19.4) (q:draft)
laipek = (t:n) (w:time/days) (d:in khanglui laipek panin, from the days of old; the exact sense of laipek alone is not clear from the verse) (e:khanglui ~ panin tuni dongin) (r:41.7.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
laiphai = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:papyrus) (d:a tall water plant that grows in marshes; laiphai kungte are papyrus plants) (e:~ kungte po thei ahi hiam) (s:laisah) (r:18.8.11)
laipi = (t:conj) (w:while still/right when) (d:lai, time or midst, with the intensifier pi, usually followed by mahin: at the very time when, right in the midst of; sunkim laipi is high noon or broad daylight) (e:amah naupang ahih ~ mahin/amau kam sungah an om ~ mahin | while the food was still in their mouths/sunkim ~ mahin leitungah khua ka mialsak ding | I will darken the earth in broad daylight/note tawh kei a nungta khawm ~ mahin | while I am still alive with you/amau ha kawmah sa baang ~ mahin | while the meat was still between their teeth) (s:kimlai) (r:14.34.3/30.8.9/19.78.30/5.31.27/4.11.33) (q:draft)
laisah = (t:n) (w:papyrus) (d:in pumpeng laisah, the reed of which boats are made in Isaiah 18; with a capital, Laisah is a place name) (e:pumpeng ~ tawh kibawl gunkuangpite) (s:laiphai) (r:23.18.1) (q:draft, low confidence)
Laisah = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Laishah) (d:town in Benjamin near Gallim and Anathoth, named in the advance of the Assyrian army toward Jerusalem) (r:23.10.30)
Laish = (t:name) (c:city/male) (w:Laish) (d:name of the city in the far north that the tribe of Dan captured and renamed Dan, and of the father of Paltiel from Gallim) (r:7.18.29/10.3.15)
laisim = (t:v) (w:read/study) (d:lai, writing, with sim, read: read a text; laisim ngei lo is never having studied) (e:Hih mi in ~ ngei lo napi-in/Na ~ a khiatna na thei hiam | do you understand what you are reading) (s:sim) (r:43.7.15/44.8.30) (q:draft)
laisun = (t:adj) (w:remaining/still left) (d:what is still left of a time or a group) (e:Ka hun neih ~ teng nuam takin) (s:omlaisun) (r:18.10.20) (q:draft, low confidence)
laisunte = (t:n) (w:those remaining/survivors) (d:laisun, remaining, with the plural te; a nungta laisunte are those who are still alive) (e:A nungta ~ zong pulnatna tawh si ding) (s:omlaite) (b:laisun) (r:18.27.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
laita = (t:adj) (w:middle/center) (d:the one in the middle of a set, as the middle floor, middle court or center crossbar; also the middle of a place) (e:a dawl ~ panin a thumna ah kipai hi/inntual ~ panin Isaiah a paikhiat ma-in | before Isaiah had left the middle court/mong khat dongin a zawl ~ paisuaksak hi | he made the center crossbar run to the other end/a ~ tong guk zai a | the middle one was six cubits wide) (s:laizang) (r:11.6.8/2.26.28/12.20.4/2.36.33/11.6.6) (q:draft)
laitaak = (t:v) (w:enclose/have in the middle) (d:lie on both sides of something so that it is in the center) (e:leitang in hihte ~ ding hi) (r:26.48.21) (q:draft, low confidence)
laitah = (t:todo) (q:draft, describes how Jesus died after crying out in Mark 15:39, perhaps breathe one's last, the word itself is not clear)
laitai = (t:n) (w:letter carrier/messenger) (d:lai letter with tai run; laitai sak is to make someone the bearer of a letter) (e:mi na deihte uh ~ sakin) (s:kamtai) (r:46.16.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
laitaite = (t:n) (w:couriers/runners/messengers) (d:men who carry letters and messages at speed) (e:sakolte’ tungah ~ tuangin/Israel khempeuh leh Judah sungah ~ pai uh a | the couriers went throughout all Israel and Judah/Kumpipa’ thupiakna tawh ~ kinawh sawl a | the couriers were sent out in haste by the command of the king/kumpipa’ sakolte tungah ~ kituangsakin | mounting the couriers on the horses of the king) (s:kamtaite/tangmite/taangmite) (b:laitai) (r:17.8.14/14.30.10/14.30.6/17.3.15/17.8.10) (q:draft)
laitak = (t:conj) (w:while/at the very time) (d:placed after a verb or a time word: at the very time when something is happening; zankim laitak is at midnight) (e:a om ~-in Topa in hopih a/Jeremiah a kikalhcip ~ mahin | while Jeremiah was still shut up/hih numei a khialh ~ kimu hi | this woman was caught in the act of sinning/Nangmah in ka sep ~ ahi a | whether I am at work/zankim ~ ahi zongin, ak khuan’ ~ ahi zongin | whether at midnight or when the rooster crows) (s:kimlai/kawm) (r:24.39.15/43.8.4/24.33.1/19.139.3/41.13.35)
laitaka = (t:adv) (w:at the time/at that very time/while) (d:laitak, the very time or point, with the linking a that joins it to the following word; zan laitaka, in the night) (e:tua ~ a om Khaldea galkapte/hong sap ~ na om bangun | as you were at the time you were called/zan ~ vuksan vukngo tuam dingin | to be covered by frost in the night) (b:laitak) (r:24.41.3/46.7.24/24.36.30) (q:draft)
laitakah = (t:adv) (w:there/right here/at that very place) (d:laitak with the place marker ah, after tua, hih or koi: at exactly that place; tua laitakah is there, hih laitakah is here, koi laitakah is where) (e:Note hih ~ om hithiatin/tua ~ na si ding uh hi | there you will die/Topa aw, koi ~ tua thute hong piang ding | Lord, where will these things happen/Tua ~ tawlet honsa-in | there, with the windows open) (b:laitak) (r:4.32.6/42.17.37/24.22.26/27.6.10) (q:draft)
laitakin = (t:conj) (w:while/as/when) (d:laitak with the suffix in, placed after a verb: at the very time that; tua hun laitakin is at that time) (e:a pai ~ David leh a mite/Israel mi a kikhawmte khempeuh a din’ ~ | while all the assembled Israelites were standing/a om ~ Kanaan gamsungah Abram teng hi | while he stayed there, Abram lived in Canaan/khuamial sungah ka pai ~ Pasian in khuavak hong pia | while I walked in darkness God gave me light/Tua hun ~ Babilon kumpipa’ galkapte in | at that time the army of the king of Babylon) (s:kimlai/kawm) (b:laitak) (r:9.29.2/14.6.3/1.13.12/18.29.3/24.32.2) (q:draft)
laitakpi = (t:adv) (w:at that very time/right at) (d:laitak, at the time, with the intensifier pi) (e:Tua zankim ~ mahin thongcing pa in) (b:laitak) (r:44.16.33) (q:draft)
laitakun = (t:conj) (w:while/as/when) (d:at the very time when, placed after the verb; the form seen with plural subjects) (e:thu a gen ~ ka za ding hi/khuaneu ah a pai ~ Zeisu in | while they were walking to the village, Jesus/Amau in an a nek ~ Zeisu in khomun la a | while they were eating, Jesus took bread/mual tungah a paitoh ~ amaute in | as they were going up the hill, they) (b:laitak) (r:23.65.24/41.14.22/41.16.12/9.9.11) (q:draft)
laitat = (t:v) (w:breathe one's last/expire/die) (d:stop breathing at death, breathe out the last breath) (e:nakpitakin Jesuh kiko-in a ~ hi/a lupna tungah ~ a | he breathed his last on his bed) (s:si) (r:41.15.37/1.49.33) (q:draft)
laite = (t:n) (w:the rest/remnant/those remaining) (d:in a om laite, those that are still there: the rest of a group or of a thing, the remnant) (e:A om ~ in a nasemte manin/a sa leh anlum a om ~ mei tawh | the rest of the meat and bread with fire/Jakob’ innkuan a om ~ | the remnant of the house of Jacob/ulianpa’ mi a om ~ paisuk uh a | the remnant of the nobles came down) (s:omlaite/laiteng) (r:40.22.6/23.10.21/3.8.32/7.5.13) (q:draft)
laite = (t:n) (w:letters/writings) (d:lai, letter, with the plural te: letters or other written documents) (e:Amah in a ~ sungah/ama min gelhna tawh tua ~ tungah gelh a | she marked those letters with his seal/uliante tungah tua ~ khak hi | she sent those letters to the nobles) (s:laikhakte/laigelhte) (b:lai) (r:11.21.9/11.21.8) (q:draft)
laitei = (t:adv) (w:still/all the same) (d:after a verb, says that the action is surely still done; here of leaving some grapes behind) (e:a sangte nusia ~ hi lo) (r:31.1.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
laiteng = (t:conj) (w:as long as/while) (d:placed after a verb, for all the time that it still goes on; ahih theih laiteng, as far as possible) (e:Pasian’ hu, ka nakah ka diik ~/Leitungah ka om ~ kei pen | as long as I am in the world, I/Ahih theih ~ mi khempeuh tawh | as far as possible, with everyone/A laibawl pa a hin ~ | as long as the one who made the will is alive/Na gam sung uhah na ten ~ uh | as long as you live in your land) (r:18.27.3/58.9.8/43.9.5/45.12.18/58.9.17/5.12.19) (q:draft)
laiteng = (t:n) (w:the rest/remainder) (d:after om or nungta: all that is still left, or all who are still alive) (e:a si a om ~ sung ding/a si lo a nungta ~ pen | those who have not died and are still alive) (s:laite/omlaiteng/omlaite) (r:3.4.30/24.21.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
laitengin = (t:conj) (w:as long as/while) (d:laiteng with the linking suffix in) (e:a pasal a nuntak ~ a pasal tawh) (b:laiteng) (r:46.7.39) (q:draft)
laitengun = (t:conj) (w:as long as/while) (d:laiteng with the plural ending un, said of several people) (e:na paina uh gamah na nuntak ~) (b:laiteng) (r:5.31.12) (q:draft)
laithei = (t:n) (w:scribe/teacher of the law) (d:lai, writing, with thei, know: a person who knows letters, a scribe or learned man; in the Gospels the teachers of the law) (e:Pasian siampi leh ~ upa teng khawm a/thuthei mi le ~ mi ahih manin | because he was a man of insight and a scribe/Jabez-ah a teeng ~ minamte | the clans of scribes living at Jabez/Farisaite leh ~ kimkhatte in | the Pharisees and some of the teachers of the law) (s:atpa/thuvanpi) (b:lai) (r:40.2.4/13.2.55/13.27.32/41.7.1) (q:draft)
laitheih = (t:n) (w:literacy/knowledge of letters/learning) (d:lai writing with theih know; laitheih siamna is skill in literature) (e:tua khangno lite ~ siamna le pilna) (b:lai) (r:27.1.17) (q:draft)
laitheipa = (t:n) (w:scribe/teacher of the law/expert in the law) (d:laithei, one who knows writing, with pa for a man) (e:amau ~ khat in Zeisu ze-et a/Tua lai takin ~ khat hong pai a | just then a teacher of the law came) (s:atpa) (b:laithei) (r:40.22.35/40.8.19) (q:draft)
laitheite = (t:n) (w:scribes/teachers of the law) (d:laithei with the plural te, literally those who know writing) (e:Tua munah a tu ~ kimkhat in/Farisaite leh ~ in Moses’ tokhom tungah | the Pharisees and teachers of the law, on the seat of Moses/thuman lo ~ in tua thukham zuauthu a suah | the lying scribes have turned the law into a lie/siampi liante, ~ leh upate in | the chief priests, teachers of the law and elders) (s:laigelhte/atte) (b:laithei) (r:41.2.6/40.23.2/24.8.8/40.27.41) (q:draft)
laitui = (t:n) (w:ink) (d:lai, writing, with tui, liquid: the ink used for writing) (e:laikung leh ~ tawh gelh ding/ke’n zong laizial sungah ~ tawh ka gelh | and I wrote it with ink on the scroll/lai tungah ~ tawh gelh ding ka deih kei | I do not want to write with ink on paper) (r:64.1.13/24.36.18/63.1.12) (q:draft)
laiza = (t:n) (w:lyre/harp) (d:a stringed instrument played with the hand; usually in the phrase laiza lasakna, the lyre as an instrument of song) (e:khuang leh ~ lasakna tawh/Harp lasakna leh ~ lasakna aw, tho un | awake, harp and lyre/~ lasakna tawh a khiatna ka gentel ding | with the harp I will explain its meaning/gialhek kungte tungah i ~ lasaknate i khai | we hung our harps on the poplars) (r:19.149.3/14.20.28/19.108.2/19.49.4/19.137.2) (q:draft)
laizang = (t:prep) (w:midst) (d:the middle of a place or a group; followed by ah or a to say in the middle of, in the midst of) (e:Israelte tua tui ~ a kantan sakpa tungah/humpinelkaite ~ ah ka om hithiat hi | I am in the midst of lions/tokhom ~, ganhingte ~ | in the midst of the throne and of the living creatures) (r:19.136.14/19.57.4/66.5.6)
laizang = (t:adj) (w:middle/mid) (e:Jordan gun ~ leikeu tungah ding uh hi/Huan ~-a om singgah na ne kei ding | you must not eat the fruit of the tree in the middle of the garden/kuam ~-a om khuapi | the town in the middle of the valley) (s:laita) (r:6.3.17/1.3.3/6.13.9)
laizang = (t:v) (w:centre)
laizanga = (t:prep) (w:in the midst of/among/in the middle) (d:laizang midst, with the linking a before om, be: that is in the middle, that is among) (e:A ~ om inndei sung a teh ciangin/Amau’ ~ om ka biakbuk | my dwelling place that is among them/a mipa in a ~ om inndei-ah hong paipih | the man brought me to the hall in the middle) (s:laka) (b:laizang) (r:26.41.2/3.15.31/26.41.1) (q:draft)
laizangah = (t:n) (w:midst/centre/midpoint) (d:laizang, middle, with the place marker ah: in the middle of, in the midst of) (e:Huan ~ zong nuntakna singkung/leitung ~ a po singkung | a tree growing in the middle of the earth/tua mun ~ pan’mun la-in | taking his stand in the middle of that field/Naupang khat samin, amau ~ a koih | he called a child and placed him among them) (b:laizang) (r:27.4.10/1.2.9/10.23.12/41.9.36)
laizial = (t:n) (w:scroll/roll) (d:a book or document in the form of a roll) (e:a leeng ~ khat ka mu hi/ka nek dingin a ~ hong pia hi | he gave me the scroll to eat/Baruk in a gelh ~ kumpipa in a haltum | the king burned the scroll that Baruch wrote/tua khut in ~ tawn khat a tawi | that hand was holding a scroll) (s:laidal) (r:38.5.1/26.3.2/24.36.27/26.2.9) (q:draft)
lak = (t:prep) (w:on/in/among) (d:the midst of a group or a place; lak panin is from among, and lakah is among) (e:Ganhing ~ pan a hatpen/Israel mite ~ panin tacil khempeuh tangdingin | in place of all the firstborn from among the Israelites/Tuuhon ~ pan a sitbaang lo tuutal khat | a ram without defect from the flock/David’ suan ~ panin kumpi dingin | from the line of David, to be king) (r:20.30.30/1.1.30/4.8.18/3.5.18/24.23.5)
lak = (t:n) (w:inside/midst) (d:the inner part or midst of something, as of a cloud, the ground or the dark) (e:meii ~ panin Moses sam hi/lei ~ panin amah tho-in | he got up from the ground/Moses in lei ~ lamah a lu kunsuk | Moses bowed his head toward the ground/khuamial ~ a mei taang bangin | like a lamp shining in the dark) (r:2.24.16/9.28.23/2.34.8/61.1.19)
lak = (t:v) (w:take/gather/reap) (d:take or gather; the form of la, take, used before endings and other words; an lak is reap the harvest) (e:Na ~ ding khat teel in/an ~ hun-a a ihmu-pa | one who sleeps at harvest time/na leitang panun an na ~ uh ciangin | when you reap the harvest of your land/na puan ak ~ ding na khaam kei un | do not stop him from taking your shirt) (a:pia) (r:13.21.11/20.10.5/3.23.22/42.6.29) (q:example wanted)
laka = (t:prep) (w:among/of/in) (d:lak with the linking a before a following word: among, one of, in the midst of) (e:Note ~ tua bang ahi kei hi/amaute ~ khat Nikodemas in | Nicodemus, one of them/huih ~ leeng kha a nei vasa | a winged bird that flies in the air/sawm-le-nihte ~ Judas Iskariot in | Judas Iscariot, one of the Twelve/Note ~ milian a suak nuamte | those among you who want to become great) (b:lak) (r:40.20.26/5.4.17/43.7.50/40.26.14) (q:draft)
lakah = (t:prep) (w:among) (d:lak, midst, with the place marker ah: among a group, or out in a place such as the wilderness) (e:Note ~ a lianpen in/~ keimah teengin amau’ Pasian ka hi ding | I will live among them and be their God/Ngia hon ~ tuuno kikhahte bangin | like lambs sent out among wolves/Kha Siangtho in Zeisu gampa ~ a sawl pah | the Spirit at once sent Jesus into the wilderness/Levi mite ~ Kohath minamte | the Kohathite clans among the Levites) (b:lak) (r:40.23.11/4.4.18/2.29.45/42.10.3/41.1.12)
lakha = (t:v) (w:take) (d:la, take, with kha, which shows the act as something one ends up doing or should not do) (e:tuate iplahin ka ~ hi/leiba tavuan ~ kei un | do not take on responsibility for debts) (r:6.7.21/20.22.26) (q:draft)
lakhawm = (t:v) (w:take together/take on together) (d:la take, with khawm together; here of taking on a duty jointly) (e:ukna tavuan a ~ uh hi) (b:la) (r:15.3.9) (q:draft)
lakhia = (t:v) (w:extract/pull out) (d:la, take, with khia, out: take or pull something out of the place where it is) (e:thakhatin a ~ lo ding note lakah/Amah in a suangte ~-in a inn kiatin | after he has pulled out the stones and scraped the house/ka nu’ gil sung panin hong ~-pa na hi | you are the one who brought me out of the womb of my mother) (r:42.14.5/3.14.43/19.71.6)
lakhia = (t:v) (w:taken out/take out/bring out) (d:take a person or thing out of a place or out of the hand of someone) (e:sung panin Jeremiah a ~ uh hi/singlamteh tung pan a ~ uh a | they took him down from the cross/hihpa khut sung pan ~ un la | take it out of the hand of this man/note’ khut sung panin hoina hai ka ~ khin | I have taken the cup of staggering out of your hand) (r:24.39.14/44.13.29/42.19.24/23.51.22)
lakhia = (t:v) (w:remove/take away) (d:take something away so that it is no longer there, as a burden, a disgrace, a cover or an idol) (e:Nong vuakna ma ka tung panin ~ in/Pasian in kei hong kikona teng ~ khin ta | God has taken away my disgrace/biak piaknate leh Asherah milimte ~ lai hi | he also removed the high places and Asherah poles/Na kumpi lukhu le na dialkhip ~ in | take off your crown and turban/Noah in teembaw khuhna ~ a | Noah removed the covering of the ark) (s:paaikhia) (r:19.39.10/1.8.13/1.30.23/14.17.6/26.21.26)
lakhiakhawm = (t:v) (w:take away together with) (d:lakhia take out, with khawm together) (e:migilote tawh kei hong ~ kei in) (b:lakhia) (r:19.28.3) (q:draft)
lakhiakik = (t:v) (w:take away again/take back) (d:lakhia take out, with kik again or back) (e:amaute ka ~ khin hi) (b:lakhia) (r:28.13.11) (q:draft)
lakhiasak = (t:v) (w:have brought out/cause to bring out) (d:lakhia, take out, with sak, cause) (e:gam panin sumngo ~ in la) (b:lakhia) (r:19.68.31) (q:draft)
lakhiasuk = (t:v) (w:bring down/take down) (d:lakhia take out, with suk downward) (e:tua lai mun panin kong ~ veve ding) (b:lakhia) (r:24.49.16) (q:draft)
lakhiato = (t:v) (w:bring up/lift out) (d:lakhia, take out, with to, upward) (e:lei thukpi sung panin nong ~ kik ding hi) (b:lakhia) (r:19.71.20) (q:draft)
lakhiazo = (t:v) (w:be able to take out/deliver) (d:lakhia take out, with zo be able) (e:Keima khutsung panin a ~ kuamah om lo) (s:honkhiazo) (b:lakhia) (r:23.43.13) (q:draft)
Lakhish = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Lachish) (d:fortified city in the lowlands of Judah, taken by Joshua and later besieged by the kings of Assyria and Babylon) (r:24.34.7/6.10.3)
lakik = (t:v) (w:take back/get back/bring back/restore) (d:la, take, with kik, back or again: take or bring back what was given, lost or sent away) (e:hih gamah ka ~ ding hi/Topa mah in hong ~ hi | the Lord himself has taken it back/a hong laksakte tung panin ~ kei un | do not take it back from those who took it from you/hehpihna lianpi tawh nang kong ~ ding hi | with great compassion I will take you back/khut tung panin a khapna a ~ dingin | to get his pledge back from her hand) (s:lakkik/ngahkik) (a:piakik) (b:la) (r:24.24.6/1.38.20/18.1.21/42.6.30/23.54.7) (q:draft)
lakin = (t:v) (w:showing/pointing out) (d:lak, show, with the linking ending in: showing or pointing out, of showing a thing to someone and of making a matter known) (e:a an top teng a teeknu ~/Na paina ding lampi ~ kong hilh ding | I will teach you, showing the way you should go/na topa uh Saul tungah hih thumanna ~ | showing this kindness to Saul your master/Ka it khempeuhte a mawhna uh ~ ka hilh | I show those I love their sins and teach them) (b:lak) (r:8.2.18/19.32.8/10.2.5/66.3.19) (q:draft)
lakkhak = (t:v) (w:happen to take/take wrongly) (d:lak take, with khak, by chance or by mistake) (e:Mi khatpeuh na ka ~ leh) (r:42.19.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
lakkhia = (t:v) (w:reveal/show forth/make known) (d:lak, show, with khia, out: bring out into view what was hidden or unseen) (e:ka dikna hong ~ ding ka hih manin/thu thukpite leh thu simte a ~ hi | he reveals deep and hidden things/Topa aw, na hehna hong ~ in | Lord, show forth your wrath/thu thukpi a ~ Pasian in | God who reveals mysteries) (s:langsak/kilangsak/pulak) (a:seel/im) (b:lak) (r:23.56.1/18.36.9/27.2.22/19.94.1/27.2.29) (q:draft)
lakkhial = (t:v) (w:mislead/lead astray) (d:lak, show, with khial, wrong: show the way wrongly, as in lam lakkhial, lead astray) (e:Mittaw pa lam a ~ mipa/Amaute in lam hong ~ uh a | they led you astray/na makaite un note lam hong ~ a | your leaders lead you astray/Mang khiathei-a kineite in lam ~ uh a | those who claim to interpret dreams mislead) (s:lampialsak/pialsak/khialsak) (a:lamlak) (r:5.27.18/23.3.12/25.2.14/38.10.2) (q:draft)
lakkhiat = (t:v) (w:take/take out/take away) (d:the form of lakhia, take out, used before endings and following words) (e:tung panin a ~ nakguh pen/tung panin hih sihna a ~ ding | to take this death away from me/Siria kumpipa khut sung panin i ~ lohna | our not taking it back from the hand of the king of Aram/vangik kong ~ sak a | I removed the burden) (r:1.2.22/2.10.17/11.22.3/19.81.6)
lakkhiatna = (t:n) (w:taking out/removal) (d:lakkhiat with the noun suffix na; before gam, the land from which someone was taken away) (e:note kong ~ gam mahah kong tunpih kik ding) (b:lakkhiat) (r:24.29.14) (q:draft)
lakkhiatsa = (t:adj) (w:taken away/taken out) (d:lakkhiat, take out, with sa, already done; before a noun, that which someone has taken away) (e:Pasian in a ~ neihsa khempeuh) (b:lakkhiat) (r:1.31.16) (q:draft)
lakkhiatsak = (t:v) (w:took/taken out/take away from) (d:lakkhiat, take out, with sak: take something away from someone) (e:ama tung panin ~ hi/nei-a a kingaihsut nangawn ~ ding hi | even what he thinks he has will be taken from him/Amah in ka hauhna khempeuh hong ~ a | he has stripped me of all my wealth/amaute sunga a kivawh thute ~ hi | he takes away the word sown in them/a gil sung nangawn panin Pasian in a ~ hi | God takes it out even from his stomach) (b:lakkhiat) (r:13.20.2/66.22.19/42.8.18/18.19.9/41.4.15/18.20.15)
lakkhiatsakin = (t:v) (w:taking away from/stripping of/removing) (d:lakkhiatsak, take something out or away from someone, with the linking ending in) (e:na suang lungtang uh hong ~ mihing lungtang/a manpha na kizepnate hong ~ | taking your fine jewelry from you) (b:lakkhiatsak) (r:26.36.26/26.16.39) (q:draft)
lakkhiatsakkik = (t:v) (w:take back out of/make give back) (d:lakkhiatsak with kik back: take out again what another has taken) (e:a na guksa teng ka ~ ding hi) (b:lakkhiatsak) (r:24.51.44) (q:draft)
lakkhiatte = (t:n) (d:lakkhiat, take away, with plural te: here the people from whom something is taken away) (e:pan thu a ~ ahi uh hi/amau sungah a kivawh thu a ~ ahi uh hi | they are those from whom the word sown in them is taken) (b:lakkhiat) (r:42.8.12/41.4.15) (q:draft)
lakkhin = (t:v) (w:have shown/have revealed) (d:lak, show, with khin, already: have shown or revealed something to someone) (e:Topa in kei tungah hong ~ zo hi/Pasian in kei tungah a thu hong ~ zo hi | God has shown me this/a hu taktakpa ahihna Pasian in a ~ hi | God has shown that he is her true defender/a sih taktak ding kei kiangah hong ~ hi | he has revealed to me that he will surely die) (s:lakzo/lahsa) (b:lak) (r:12.8.13/19.48.3/44.10.28/12.8.10) (q:draft)
lakkhit = (t:v) (w:have taken/have received) (d:lak take, with khit finished; lakkhit ciangin is after receiving) (e:kumpi za a ~ ciangin) (s:sankhit/ngahkhit) (r:42.19.12) (q:draft)
lakkhol = (t:v) (w:show beforehand/reveal in advance) (d:lak show, with khol beforehand) (e:a piang ding thu a hong ~ zo hi) (r:27.2.29) (q:draft)
lakkholzo = (t:v) (w:have shown beforehand/reveal in advance) (d:lakkhol with zo, marking the action as accomplished) (e:a piang ding thu a hong ~ hi) (b:lakkhol) (r:27.2.29) (q:draft)
lakkik = (t:v) (w:take back/take again/bring back) (d:lak, take, with kik, again or back: take up again or bring back; phu lakkik is take revenge) (e:kumpipa ~ ding bangmah gen lo/Ka nuntakna paaikhia-a ~ theih nading thu | authority to lay down my life and take it up again/phu a ~ ni, a galte a thuk ni | the day he takes vengeance and repays his foes) (s:lakik) (b:lak) (r:10.19.10/43.10.18/24.46.10) (q:draft)
lakkiksa = (t:adj) (w:taken back/reclaimed) (d:lakkik, take back, with sa, already done) (e:Haman’ tung panin a ~ minthuhna zungbuh) (b:lakkik) (r:17.8.2) (q:draft)
Lakkum = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Lakkum) (d:town on the border of the territory of Naphtali, near the Jordan) (r:6.19.33)
laklak = (t:adv) (d:descriptive word placed after dian’, leap, for the bounding of a deer) (e:thang zuanin a dian’ ~ bangin) (r:20.7.22) (q:draft, low confidence)
laklawhin = (t:adv) (w:in between/halfway/lukewarm) (d:being neither one thing nor the other, here neither cold nor hot) (e:a ~ om na hih manun) (r:66.3.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
lakna = (t:n) (w:taking/extortion) (d:lak, take, with the noun suffix na: the act of taking; sumgolh lakna is taking a bribe, a meet lakna taking interest, phu lakna taking revenge, and tui lakna a channel that draws water) (e:Sumgolh ~ in a lapa’ gamtat hoihna/A meet a pung ~ tawh a hau mipa | a man who grows rich by taking interest/a phu ~ uh nasia lua ahih manin | because their taking of revenge was very severe/bual tungnung tui ~ mongah | at the end of the aqueduct of the upper pool) (r:21.7.7/19.62.10/20.28.8/26.25.12/23.7.3) (q:draft)
laknate = (t:n) (w:taking/takings) (d:lakna taking, with the plural te; sumgolh laknate is the taking of bribes, sakol a laknate the horses he obtained) (e:leh sumgolh ~ deih lo hi/Solomon in gamdang panin sakol a ~ | the horses Solomon obtained from abroad) (b:lakna) (r:14.19.7/14.1.16) (q:draft)
laknop = (t:v) (w:want to take/want to marry) (d:lak take, with nop want; here of taking a woman as wife) (e:a sanggampa’ zi a ~ kei leh) (r:5.25.7) (q:draft)
lakpa = (t:n) (w:one who shows/adviser/guide) (d:the one who shows, lak with -pa marking a male person; lam a lakpa, one who shows the way, is a guide or adviser) (e:itna kip a ~ ka hi hi/ka gamtatna khempeuh hong ~ en un | see the man who told me everything I did/siampi leh kumpipa lam a ~ ahi hi | he was priest and adviser to the king/David lam a ~, Arkhi mi Hushai | Hushai the Arkite, David’s adviser) (r:5.5.10/11.4.5/43.4.29/10.16.16) (q:draft)
lakpan = (t:prep) (w:from among/out of) (d:lak, among, with pan, from) (e:misite ~ Ta upa a suak hi/hih thukhamte ~ a neupente khat | one of the least of these commands) (s:lakpanin/sungpan) (r:51.1.18/40.5.19) (q:draft)
lakpanin = (t:prep) (w:from among/out of) (d:lakpan with the linking suffix in) (e:Ukpa sawmthumte ~ mi thumte paisukin) (s:lakpan/sungpanin) (b:lakpan) (r:10.23.13) (q:draft)
laksa = (t:adj) (w:taken/captured/seized) (d:lak, take, with -sa, already taken; a laksa before a noun is what someone has taken or captured) (e:David in Amalekte’ ~ khempeuh ngah kik hi/na ~ numei’ hangin | because of the woman you have taken/a pa Asa in a ~ Efraim khuapite | the towns of Ephraim that his father Asa had captured/gal sungah Hazael in a ~ khuapite | the towns Hazael had taken in battle) (b:lak) (r:9.30.18/14.17.2/1.20.3/12.13.25) (q:draft)
laksak = (t:v) (w:take away from/seize/plunder) (d:lak, take, with sak: take something away from someone, by force or as plunder) (e:Izipt kumpipa’ neih khempeuh ~ khin/Pasian in amaute’ nuntakna a ~ hun ciangin | when God takes away their life/a na khempeuh uh ~ uh hi | they took all their goods as plunder/a manpha na kizepnate zong hong ~ ding uh hi | they will also take your fine jewelry/a sum a paite ~ kei un | do not seize their wealth) (s:sut) (a:pia) (b:lak) (r:12.24.7/4.31.9/18.27.8/26.23.26/31.1.13) (q:draft)
laksak = (t:v) (w:take for/get for) (d:lak, take, with sak: take or get something on behalf of another, as a wife for a son) (e:ama adingin zi nih ~ a/Hih numei ka zi dingin hong ~ in | get me this girl as my wife/Tua nu hong ~ in | get her for me/eite adingin hong paisakin hong ~ ding ahi hiam | who will go and get it for us?) (b:lak) (r:14.24.3/1.34.4/7.14.3/5.30.12) (q:draft)
laksakin = (t:v) (w:taking away/seizing/robbing) (d:laksak take from someone with the linking ending in: taking away, having seized) (e:Topa in a neih khempeuh ~/A nu a pa’ neihsa ~ | robbing his father and mother of their property/a neih khempeuh ~ a satgawp khit uh ciangin | after they took all he had and beat him/Ka mite’ leitang ~, bawlsia lo ding hi | he shall not take my people’s land and wrong them/a hong hehsak mite’ neihsa sutin ~ | plundering and seizing the goods of the people who anger me) (s:sutin) (b:laksak) (r:38.9.4/20.28.24/42.10.30/26.46.18/23.10.6) (q:draft)
laksakmang = (t:v) (w:take away completely/plunder) (d:laksak take away from, with mang, so that it is gone) (e:na nate uh hong ~ khin ding hi) (r:35.2.7) (q:draft)
laksakte = (t:n) (w:those who take away/those who seize) (d:laksak, take away from, with plural te) (e:a hong ~ tung panin lakik kei un/a gam uh a ~’ kiang panin | from those who took their land) (b:laksak) (r:42.6.30/24.49.2) (q:draft)
laksakzo = (t:v) (w:be able to plunder/be able to take away) (d:laksak take away from, with zo be able) (e:ciang bekin ~ pan bek ding hi) (s:sutzo/luhgawpzo) (b:laksak) (r:41.3.27) (q:draft)
laksate = (t:n) (w:captives/those captured) (d:laksa, taken, with plural te: the people someone has taken) (e:galmatin na ~ that ding na hi hiam) (s:galmatte/salte) (b:laksa) (r:12.6.22) (q:draft)
laksuk = (t:v) (w:take down/bring down) (d:lak take, with suk downward) (e:Zeisu’ luang a ~ khit ciangin) (a:lato) (b:lak) (r:41.15.46) (q:draft)
lakte = (t:n) (w:things taken/plunder/takings) (d:lak take or get with the plural te: the things or people taken or received; na lakte, things taken, plunder) (e:Hih in David’ na ~ ahi hi/a na ~ uh hawm ding uh hi | they will divide the things they have taken/Solomon’ sakol ~ Izipt leh Kue pan hi a | Solomon’s horses were obtained from Egypt and Kue/mite kiang panin na sum ~ uh | the money you receive from the people) (b:lak) (r:9.30.20/11.10.28/38.14.1/12.12.7) (q:draft)
lakte = (t:n) (w:those who show/guides/counselors) (d:lak show with the plural te; thu hong lakte, those who show me what to do) (e:tuate in keimah thu hong ~ ahi hi) (s:lamlakte) (r:19.119.24) (q:draft, low confidence)
laktel = (t:v) (w:show clearly/make plain/prove/point out) (d:make something plainly known, as the truth of a word or the fault of a person) (e:nang’ khialhna hong ~ kik leh/mawhna thu, thuman thu leh thukhenna thu ~ ding hi | he will show clearly the truth about sin, righteousness and judgment/a beisa huna nate kua in ~ thei ahi hiam | who can make plain the things of the past?/Thuman na hihna hong ~ inla | show plainly that you are in the right/a cingtakin amaute tungah ~ in la | make it fully known to them) (s:lahtel/telsak) (a:seel) (r:20.25.8/23.43.26/43.16.8/23.43.9/26.43.11) (q:draft)
laktelsak = (t:v) (w:let show clearly/make plain to) (d:laktel show clearly, with sak cause or allow) (e:geelsa teng hong ~ dih un) (b:laktel) (r:18.27.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
lakteng = (t:n) (w:all that was taken) (d:lak take, with teng all; a galvan lakteng is all the goods he has taken, his spoil) (e:a galvan ~ tawh a gamah ciahkik ding) (b:lak) (r:27.11.28) (q:draft, low confidence)
lakthei = (t:v) (w:be able to show/prove) (d:lak show with thei can) (e:a manna thu hong ~ het lo ding/kua in ka mawhna na hong ~ uh hiam | which of you can prove me guilty of sin?/bang lim tawh hong ~ ding na hi hiam | what sign can you show us?/Jesuh pen Khrih hi, ci-in teltakin ~ ahih manin | because he could show clearly that Jesus is the Christ) (b:lak) (r:44.24.13/44.9.22/43.8.46/43.2.18) (q:draft)
laktheih = (t:v) (w:be able to take/be able to capture) (d:lak take with theih, the form of thei can before nadingin, so that one can take; phu laktheih is be able to take revenge) (e:Amaute in khuapi a ~ nadingin/Jezebel’ tungah phu ka ~ nadingin | so that I can take revenge on Jezebel/a luang a ~ nadingin Josef tungah thu a pia | he gave Joseph leave to take the body) (b:lak) (r:14.32.18/12.9.7/41.15.45) (q:draft)
laktheih = (t:v) (w:be able to present/be able to show) (d:lak show with theih, the form of thei can before nadingin) (e:ama kiangah hong ~ nadingin) (b:lak) (r:51.1.22) (q:draft)
lakthuah = (t:v) (w:take in addition/marry also) (d:lak, take, with thuah, in addition: take another wife besides the one already had) (e:zi dang khat a ~ leh/a zi’ nu tawh zong a ~ leh | if he also marries his wife’s mother) (s:lathuah) (r:2.21.10/3.20.14) (q:draft)
lakto = (t:v) (w:raise/lift up/hold up) (d:lak with to, up: hold something up high to be seen, as a banner) (e:mite tungah ka lim ka ~ ding hi/Mualkolh tungah lim khat ~ unla | raise a banner on a bare hilltop) (s:laamto) (b:lak) (r:23.49.22/23.13.2) (q:draft)
lakzawhna = (t:n) (w:conquest/capture) (d:lak take, with zawh succeed and the noun suffix na: the taking of a town) (e:Lodebar khua bang lel na ~ uhah) (r:30.6.13) (q:draft)
lakzo = (t:v) (w:have shown/make known) (d:lak show, with zo, marking the action as accomplished) (e:ka gen ding thu nong ~ hi) (b:lak) (r:27.2.23) (q:draft)
lal = (t:v) (w:migrate/move/wander/sojourn) (d:move from one place to live in another, or wander from place to place; lal-a om is to live as a sojourner away from home, and lal hun the season when birds migrate) (e:Amaute nisuahna lamah ~ uh a/mual kuam, leihawm, ken hawm sungah a ~ kawikawi | they wandered about in mountain valleys, caves and holes in the rocks/leitungah ~-a na om lai tengun | as long as you live as sojourners on earth/tui vapite nangawn in ~ hun ding a thei | even the storks know the time to migrate/kikhen thangin ~-a om mite kiangah | to those who live scattered as sojourners) (s:peem/kikhin) (r:1.11.2/60.1.17/58.11.38/24.8.7/60.1.2) (q:draft)
lalcin = (t:n) (w:lantern) (d:a lamp carried in the hand to give light at night, named beside meilah, torch) (e:~ leh meilah de-in) (r:43.18.3) (q:draft)
lalsak = (t:v) (w:move/resettle/cause to migrate) (d:lal, migrate, with sak, cause) (e:hih gamah tua khua panin a ~ hi) (b:lal) (r:44.7.4) (q:draft)
lam = (t:n) (w:way) (d:the way a person goes or lives; lam pial is to turn off the way and lam hilh to teach someone the way) (e:~ ka pial ngei kei hi/mimawhte ~ hilh hi | he teaches sinners the way/~ man panin pialkha kei un | do not turn aside from the right way) (s:lampi) (r:18.23.11/19.25.8/58.13.9)
lam = (t:n) (w:path) (e:~ hong lak ding meivak hi a | it is a lamp to show me the path/~ pamah hong delh khia a | he dragged me off the path) (s:lampi/lamzin) (r:19.119.105/25.3.11)
lam = (t:n) (w:direction) (d:the side toward which someone goes or something faces; after a place name, toward that place) (e:koi ~ pai ding?/a utna ~ peuhpeuh ah pai thei uh hi | they could go in whatever direction they wished/Negeb gam ~ manawhin pai lai hi | he went on toward the Negev) (s:lamsang) (r:1.2.8/4.3.29/26.1.17/1.12.9)
Lam = (t:n) (w:road/way) (d:lam, road or way, written with a capital at the start of a sentence; Lam kawi is a crooked road, Lam lianpi a main road and Lam gei the roadside) (e:~ kawi khempeuh kitangsak ding hi/~ lianpi panin amah a kilakkhiat khit ciangin | after he had been removed from the main road/~ gei Enaim-a om numei paktat nu | the shrine prostitute who was beside the road at Enaim/~ a pialna hang uh | because they have turned from the way) (b:lam) (r:42.3.5/10.20.13/1.38.21/24.3.21) (q:draft)
lam-ethuai = (t:adj) (w:worth hoping for/to be looked forward to) (d:lam-et hope, with huai worthy of) (e:a ~ bangmah a om kei hi) (s:lamethuai) (r:21.11.8) (q:draft)
lama = (t:prep) (w:on the side of/toward/facing) (d:lam, side or direction, with the suffix a joining it to what follows; nisuahna lama om is that is on the east side) (e:biakinn nisuahna ~ om kongpi-ah hong paipih a/nisuahna ~ om kulh kongpi-ah pai a | he went to the gate facing east/Assiria gam nisuahna ~ a luang a thumna gun | the third river, which flows east of Assyria/A mailam, nisuahna ~ dingin | for the front, the east side/leilu ~ om mah tawh kibang hi | they were like those on the north side) (b:lam) (r:26.43.1/1.2.14/26.40.6/2.38.13/26.42.11) (q:draft)
lama = (t:ppm) (d:lam with the suffix a, showing time or manner; after a verb, at the time of doing, as a kuan lama, as he goes in; nitak lama is in the evening and a sia lama in a bad way) (e:a kuan ~ a tot lampi teng mah/nitak ~ a om niliim tawh kibang | like a shadow at evening/minam dangte lakah a sia ~ gentehna | a byword among the nations) (b:lam) (r:26.46.8/19.102.11/19.44.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
Lama = (t:adv) (w:why) (d:Aramaic word quoted untranslated in the cry of Jesus on the cross, NIV lema) (e:Elio, Elio, ~ Sabakthani | Eloi, Eloi, lema sabachthani) (r:41.15.34) (q:draft)
lamah = (t:n) (w:direction) (d:lam, direction, with the marker ah: toward, in the direction of) (e:nisuahna ~/Ahab mahmah mun khat ~ pai-in | Ahab went in one direction/gamlak ~ tai-in | fleeing toward the wilderness/San Tuipi ~ pai uh a | they went toward the Red Sea) (b:lam) (r:11.18.6/6.8.20/4.21.4)
lamah = (t:n) (w:side/area) (d:lam, side, with the marker ah: on the side of, in the part lying that way) (e:hih ~ hong pai ve/ei ~ Topa hong pang lo hi leh | if the Lord had not been on our side/nisuahna, nitumna, leilu, leh leitaw ~ om uh hi | they were on the east, west, north and south sides) (b:lam) (r:1.3.24/19.124.2/13.9.24)
lambaangin = (t:adv) (w:turning aside/stopping on the way) (d:leaving one's road to call on someone; the exact sense of baang is not confirmed) (e:hong ~, damlenat kitheihsakna-in hong hawh ding) (r:24.15.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
lambehte = (t:n) (w:side rooms/annexes) (d:rooms built on against the wall of a house; plural te) (e:a inn buppi tungah a ~ zomin) (r:11.6.10) (q:draft)
lamdan = (t:adj) (w:wonderful/marvellous/amazing) (d:lamdang written short, with an apostrophe, before mahmah) (e:mangmatnate a ~’ mahmah hangin | because the revelations are so wonderful) (r:47.12.7) (q:draft)
lamdang = (t:n) (w:surprise) (d:the feeling that something is strange or unexpected; lamdang sa is to feel surprise at something) (e:ka cihna ~ sa kei in/Farisaipa in a muh ciangin ~ a sa hi | when the Pharisee saw it he was surprised) (r:43.3.7/42.11.38)
lamdang = (t:n) (w:shock) (e:A nu leh pate in ~ a sa uh hi | her parents were astonished) (r:42.8.56)
lamdang = (t:v) (w:astonish/amaze/nonplus/startle/astound/stun) (d:be wonderful or astonishing; with sa, lamdang sa, be astonished at something) (e:a thuhilhna ~ a sa uh hi | they were astonished at his teaching/Pasian’ vangliatna ~ a sa uh hi | they were amazed at the greatness of God/eite’ mit-ah ~ hi | it is marvelous in our eyes/Na thuhilhnate ~ mahmah a | your statutes are very wonderful) (r:40.22.33/42.9.43/19.118.23/19.119.129)
lamdangdang = (t:adj) (w:strange/various strange) (d:lamdang, strange, with its last syllable repeated: strange things of many kinds) (e:a ~ thuhilhna thak zui kei un/Na mitah na ~ hong suak ding a | strange things will appear to your eyes) (r:58.13.9/20.23.33) (q:draft)
lamdangin = (t:adv) (w:wonderfully/marvellously/strangely) (d:lamdang, wonderful or strange, with in: in a wonderful or strange way; pau lamdangin is in a strange tongue) (e:meel ~ kilang uh a/a itna kip a ~ kei tungah hong lak | he showed me his steadfast love in a wonderful way/na nasepnate ~ lian mahmah hi | your deeds are wonderfully great/kikhopna sungah pau ~ a pau nuam pa | the one who wants to speak in a strange tongue in the meeting) (b:lamdang) (r:42.9.30/19.31.21/66.15.3/46.14.28) (q:draft)
lamdanglua = (t:adj) (w:too wonderful/too amazing) (d:lamdang with lua, too much) (e:kei a dingin a ~ thu) (b:lamdang) (r:18.42.3) (q:draft)
lamdangpi = (t:adj) (w:very strange/marvellous/foreign) (d:lamdang with the intensifier pi; thu lamdangpi is a strange thing, a lamdangpi khatin is in a wonderful way) (e:thu ~ khatin ngaihsun lel uh hi/Amah a thahat dong a ~ khatin kihuh | he was wonderfully helped until he became strong/a thu ~-in ngaihsun kei unla | do not think it a strange thing/ko a dingin a ~ khat hi a | to us it is something strange) (b:lamdang) (r:28.8.12/14.26.15/60.4.12/44.17.20) (q:draft)
lamdangpipi = (t:adj) (w:very marvellous/most wonderful) (d:lamdangpi with pi repeated for emphasis; na lamdangpipi are marvellous things) (e:na ~ piang a) (b:lamdangpi) (r:18.37.5) (q:draft)
lamdangsa = (t:v) (w:be amazed/be astonished/be surprised/wonder) (d:find something strange or wonderful, lamdang with sa) (e:note hong muhdah uh leh, ~ kei un/Pasian’ thu ~-in a um hi | amazed at the word of God, he believed/Tua gama mi khempeuh in ~-in | all the people of that land were astonished/tua banga piangte ~-in innah a ciah hi | he went home wondering at what had happened) (b:lamdang) (r:62.3.13/40.12.23/44.13.12/42.24.12) (q:draft)
lamdangsak = (t:v) (w:be surprised at/find strange/wonder at) (d:form of lamdangsa used before ding and huai: lamdangsak ding hi lo hi, it is no wonder) (e:Tua pen ~ ding hi lo hi/a kibawl manin ~ ding hi lo hi | it is no wonder that they disguise themselves/~ huaina ahi ci-in ngaihsun kei un | do not think it something to be surprised at) (b:lamdangsa) (r:47.11.14/30.5.13/47.11.15/60.4.12) (q:draft)
lamdangsakna = (t:n) (w:spectacle/astonishment/wonder/amazement) (d:lamdangsak with the noun suffix na: the feeling of wonder or astonishment; lamdangsakna tawh en is look at in astonishment) (e:mite in ~ tawh nang hong en ding/~ tawh amaute khat leh khat ki-en uh hi | they looked at one another in astonishment/~ leh lungman’na tawh a kidim uh hi | they were filled with wonder and amazement/amah ~ tawh ding ta uh hen | let them stand in awe of him) (b:lamdangsak) (r:34.3.6/1.43.33/44.3.10/19.33.8)
lamdangte = (t:n) (w:wonders/wonderful deeds/marvels) (d:plural of lamdang wonderful, after na thing or nasepna deed) (e:nangma nasepna ~ ka gen kawm hi/Pasian’ bawl na ~ ngaihsun in | consider the wonders God has done/a lian a nasia lim leh na ~ | great and terrible signs and wonders/ama hih a ~, a genkhiat thukhennate phawk un | remember the wonders he has done and the judgments he pronounced) (s:nalamdangte) (b:lamdang) (r:19.26.7/18.37.14/5.6.22/13.16.12) (q:draft)
lamding = (t:v) (w:build) (d:lam, build, with ding written as one word: to build, going to build) (e:inn ~ kipan napi-in zozo lo hi/inn lianpi khat ~ a sawm le | if he plans to build a large house) (b:lam) (r:42.14.30/42.14.28) (q:draft)
lamdung = (t:n) (w:street/roadside/wayside) (d:the length of a road: the streets of a town where people pass, or the ground along the side of a path) (e:~ tengah vak tawntung hi/pawlkhatte ~ tu a | some fell along the path/a delhte in ~ khempeuh zongin | the pursuers searched all along the road/hih ~ a suangte in phatin awng veve ding | the stones along this road will cry out in praise) (s:lampidung) (r:20.7.11/20.7.12/41.4.4/6.2.22/42.19.40) (q:draft, low confidence)
Lamdungah = (t:adv) (w:along the road/along the path/on the street) (d:lamdung, the length of a road, street, with the marker ah; written with a capital at the start of a sentence) (e:~ khaici a tukna munte/~ amah a vak lai takin | while he was walking along the street) (r:42.8.12/20.7.8) (q:draft)
Lamek = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Lamech) (d:name of two men: a descendant of Cain who had two wives, and the son of Methuselah and father of Noah) (r:1.5.28)
lamen = (t:v) (w:hope for/expect/look forward to) (d:look ahead to something with hope or expectation; the form lamet is used before endings such as leh, loh, ding and na) (e:midang khat ka ~ lai ding uh hiam/Cidamna i ~-a siatna bek i ngah hi | we hoped for healing but got only ruin/van thak leh lei thak eite in i ~ | we look forward to a new heaven and a new earth/bulpi kip a nei khuapi a ~ hi | he was looking forward to the city with firm foundations) (r:40.11.3/61.3.13/24.8.15/58.11.10) (q:draft)
lamenin = (t:v) (w:hoping for/expecting/waiting for) (d:lamen with the linking ending in, hoping or expecting while another action follows) (e:a ngah ding ~ sawltakte a ento hi/nangma thuciamna hong tun’ ding ~ ka om hi | I wait in hope for your promise to come/Pasian’ tate a kilat ding ~ | waiting in hope for the children of God to be revealed/Topa ~ ka ngak ngiungeu a | I waited patiently in hope for the Lord) (b:lamen) (r:44.3.5/45.8.19/19.119.147/19.40.1) (q:draft)
lamenpa = (t:n) (w:one who hopes for/one who waits for) (d:lamen with pa, the man who looks forward to something) (e:Pasian Gam a ~ hong pai-in) (b:lamen) (r:41.15.43) (q:draft)
lamente = (t:n) (w:those who wait for/those who look forward to) (d:lamen expect with the plural te) (e:amah a ~ gum dingin/kei sungah a ~ maizum lo ding hi | those who hope in me will not be put to shame/ama kilat ding thu a ~ khempeuh | all who look forward to his appearing) (b:lamen) (r:58.9.28/55.4.8/23.49.23) (q:draft)
lamet = (t:v) (w:hope/hope for/expect/look for) (d:form of lamen used before endings such as leh, loh and ding; also a noun stem, hope, as in lamet tun’lohna, hope not fulfilled) (e:I muh loh nate i ~ leh/nang kong ~ uh mah bangin | even as we hope in you/a ~ loh ni leh a theih loh kalin | on a day he does not expect and at an hour he does not know/mai lamah ~ ding bangmah nei lo hi | they have nothing to hope for in the future) (r:45.8.25/18.30.26/19.33.22/42.12.46/20.24.20) (q:draft)
lametet = (t:v) (w:hope for/expect eagerly/long for) (d:lamet, hope, with its last syllable repeated: keep hoping for over a long time) (e:i ~ David’ suan hi lo ding/pen ka deihdeih, ka ~ bulpi ahi hi | this is my earnest desire and chief hope) (r:40.12.23/50.1.20) (q:draft)
lamethuai = (t:adj) (w:hopeful/worth hoping for) (d:lamet, hope, with huai, worthy of; a lamethuai bangmah om lo is there is nothing to hope for) (e:Mailamah a ~ bangmah a om kei hi/a ~ bangmah om nawn lo hi | there is nothing left to hope for) (s:lam-ethuai) (r:21.11.8/25.2.13) (q:draft)
lametin = (t:adv) (w:as one's hope) (d:lamet, hope, with in; lametin nei is to have as one's hope, put one's hope in) (e:amah bek mah ~ nei ding uh hi/suhgawpnate ~ nei kei in | do not put your hope in plunder) (b:lamet) (r:40.12.21/19.62.10) (q:draft)
lametna = (t:n) (w:hope/expectation) (d:lamet, hope, with the noun suffix na: what a person looks forward to or trusts will come) (e:Mihoihte’ ~ in lungdamna hi a/Ka ~ ama tung pan ahih manin | because my hope comes from him/Tua bang hi lecin ~ om a | if so, there is hope/migilote’ ~ in a hawmpi hi | the hope of the wicked comes to nothing) (r:20.10.28/25.3.29/19.62.5/20.23.18) (q:draft)
lametnate = (t:n) (w:hopes/things hoped for) (d:plural of lametna) (e:Upna in ~ telcianna hi a) (s:lamette) (b:lametna) (r:58.11.1) (q:draft)
lametnateng = (t:n) (w:all hope/every expectation) (d:lametna with teng, all) (e:A pi’ ~ beita hi) (b:lametna) (r:26.19.5) (q:draft)
lametpa = (t:n) (w:hope/the one hoped in) (d:lamet with pa, the male person in whom others hope; said of the Lord) (e:Israel mite’ ~ aw) (b:lamet) (r:24.17.13) (q:draft)
lametsakna = (t:n) (w:giving of hope/cause for hope) (d:lamet, hope, with sak, cause, and na: that by which someone is made to hope) (e:Keimah nong ~ ahi na nasempa’) (r:19.119.49) (q:draft)
lamette = (t:n) (w:things hoped for) (d:lamet with the plural te, the things one hopes for) (e:i ~ ngah takpi ding) (s:lametnate) (b:lamet) (r:58.11.1) (q:draft)
lamgal = (t:n) (w:side/bank) (d:the land on one side of a river; hih lamgal is this side) (e:Jordan hih ~ nisuahna lam) (r:4.32.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
lamgei = (t:see) <lamgei-ah>
lamgei-ah = (t:adv) (w:by the roadside/beside the road) (d:lam road and gei edge, with ah at) (e:kulh kongpi ~ tu zel hi) (r:10.15.2) (q:draft)
lamhilh = (t:n) (w:guide) (d:one who shows the way, lam, way, with hilh, teach) (e:kote a dingin ~ nong hi ding hi) (r:4.10.31/40.23.16) (q:draft)
lamhilhte = (t:n) (w:guides) (d:lamhilh, guide, with the plural te; mittaw lamhilhte are blind guides) (e:Amau in mittaw ~ ahi uh hi/Mittaw a bang ~ aw | you blind guides) (s:lamlakte/makaihte) (b:lamhilh) (r:40.15.14/40.23.16) (q:draft)
lamin = (t:v) (w:building/build) (d:verb lam, build, with the linking suffix in) (e:Solomon in inn ~ zo hi/inn hoihte ~ tuate sungah na teen’ uh ciang | when you build fine houses and live in them/Moses in biakna tau khat ~ | Moses built an altar/an tuh inn ~ a om uh hi | they were planting and building) (b:lam) (r:11.6.14/5.8.12/2.17.15/42.17.28) (q:draft)
lamin = (t:ppm) (d:lam, side or way, with the suffix in, showing direction, manner or time; a hoih lamin is favourably, nitak lamin is in the evening) (e:adang tuuno khat nitak ~ na pia ding hi/Tuuno khat zingsang ~ na pia ding a | offer one lamb in the morning/a hoih ~ kei hong phawk in | remember me with favor/a sia ~ na zang kei ding uh hi | you shall not use it wrongly/Khatvei nitak ~ a lupna panin David tho-in | one evening David got up from his bed) (b:lam) (r:2.29.39/16.13.31/2.20.7/10.11.2) (q:draft)
lamka = (t:n) (w:crossroads/fork in the road/road junction) (d:the place where roads part or meet) (e:~ lai-ah na ding kei ding hi/~ citeng mun khempeuh ah ding a | she stands at every crossroads/~-ah pai un la | go to the street corners) (s:kabom) (r:31.1.14/26.21.21/20.8.2/40.22.9) (q:draft)
lamkabom = (t:n) (w:public square/square/open place) (d:an open place in a town where roads meet and people gather) (e:Mihon omna ~ khempeuh ah/~ khempeuh nawkin leeng kawikawi uh hi | they rush back and forth through all the squares) (s:tualpi) (r:30.5.16/34.2.4) (q:draft)
lamkabomah = (t:n) (w:in the marketplace/in the public square) (d:lamkabom, public square, with the place marker ah) (e:Mihon omna ~ a tu naupang) (b:lamkabom) (r:42.7.32/40.11.16) (q:draft)
lamkabomte = (t:see) <lamkabomte-ah>
lamkabomte-ah = (t:n) (w:in the public squares/in the streets) (d:lamkabom, public square, with plural te and the place marker ah) (e:kongzing leh ~ a tu dingin) (r:38.8.4) (q:draft)
lamkaih = (t:v) (w:guide/lead) (d:lead along the way, lam, way, with kaih, lead) (e:amaute a hehpihpa in amaute ~ ding a) (s:lamlak/makaih) (r:23.49.10) (q:draft)
lamkal = (t:n) (w:way/journey) (d:the stretch between setting out and arriving; lamkal-ah om is be on the way) (e:Amaute ~-ah a om lai takin/Gilgal panin inn zuanin ~-a om ahi uh hi | they were on their way home from Gilgal/gamlak ~-a suak mite khempeuh | all the people born on the way in the wilderness/~ a zat ding a kisam khempeuh | everything needed for the journey) (r:10.13.30/12.2.1/6.5.5/44.28.10) (q:draft)
lamkalah = (t:adv) (w:on the way/on the road/along the way) (d:lamkal, the course of a journey, with the place ending -ah) (e:~ mite lungkia uh hi/gilkialin ciahsak leng, ~ cimawh kha ding uh hi | if I send them home hungry they will collapse on the way/Obadiah ~ a om laitakin | while Obadiah was on the way/~ note hong cing dingin | to guard you along the way) (r:4.21.4/41.8.3/11.18.7/2.23.20) (q:draft)
lamkhial = (t:v) (w:take the wrong road) (d:leave the right way, lam, way, with khial, err; lamkhial mite are people who have gone astray) (e:~ mite' nasepna ka mudah a) (s:lampial) (r:19.101.3)
lamkhial = (t:v) (w:misroute)
lamkhial = (t:v) (w:veer)
Lamkhial = (t:v) (w:go astray/take the wrong road) (d:lam way with khial err; Lamkhial mite are people who have left the right way, NIV faithless people) (e:~ mite’ nasepna ka mudah a) (b:lamkhial) (r:19.101.3) (q:draft)
lamkhialin = (t:adv) (w:astray/going the wrong way) (d:lamkhial with the linking suffix in) (e:mualtung tengah ~ a gammanpih uh hi) (b:lamkhial) (r:24.50.6) (q:draft)
lamkhialsak = (t:v) (w:lead astray/mislead) (d:lamkhial with sak, cause to take the wrong road) (e:amah in ~ kamkaihna pen) (s:lampialsak/pialsak/khialsak) (b:lamkhial) (r:23.30.28) (q:draft)
lamkik = (t:v) (w:rebuild) (d:build again what was destroyed, lam, build, with kik, again) (e:biakinn ~ ding hun nai lo hi/nidanga ka suksiatna ka ~ leh | if I rebuild what I once destroyed/Judah khuapite ~ ding a | he will rebuild the cities of Judah/Hih inn a ~ nading | to rebuild this house) (s:bawlkik/puahkik) (a:susia) (r:37.1.2/48.2.18/19.69.35/15.5.9)
lamkik = (t:v) (w:reconstruct) (e:biakinn ~ ding hi | he will build the temple again/Tua singte tawh biakinn ~ le uh cin | if you rebuild the temple with that timber) (r:38.6.12/37.1.8)
lamkikin = (t:v) (w:rebuilding/rebuild) (d:form of lamkik with -in, linking to what follows) (e:in a siasa khuapite ~/Amaute in khuapi ~ a sungah teng uh hi | they rebuilt the city and lived in it/mual dawn-a biak piaknate amah in ~ | he rebuilt the high places/hih inn ~ a nate na bawl nading uh | for you to rebuild this house and finish its work) (b:lamkik) (r:26.36.36/14.33.3/7.18.28/15.5.3) (q:draft)
lamkikna = (t:n) (w:rebuilding/restoration) (d:lamkik with the noun suffix na) (e:Jerusalem ~ ding thu a kipiak hun) (s:kilamkikna/puahkikna) (a:suksiatna) (b:lamkik) (r:27.9.25) (q:draft)
lamkikpa = (t:n) (w:rebuilder/one who rebuilds) (d:lamkik, rebuild, with pa, which marks a man: the man who rebuilds something) (e:hih Jerikho khuapi a ~ in) (b:lamkik) (r:6.6.26) (q:draft)
lamkippa = (t:n) (w:builder/one who establishes) (d:lam, build, and kip, firm, with pa, which marks a man: the one who builds up firmly, said of God as the Builder of Zion) (e:nang hong ~ in nang hong tenpih ding) (s:lampa) (r:23.62.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
lamlah = (t:v) (w:guide/counsel/direct) (d:show the way, give guidance or advice; the form of lamlak used before na, ding and nading; lamlah khial is to lead astray) (e:thu ~ siamna leh vangliatna Kha/~ nading zong a | he sought guidance/vankah khat thu dongin a ~ ding | consulting a medium to guide him/note hong ~ khialhna-ah Hezekiah thu ngai kei | do not listen to Hezekiah when he misleads you) (s:lamkaih/makaih) (r:23.11.2/14.20.3/13.10.13/12.18.31) (q:draft)
lamlahna = (t:n) (w:guidance/direction/counsel) (d:a showing of the way: lam way, lah show, with -na; Topa tung panin lamlahna dong is to inquire of the Lord) (e:Topa tung panin ~ dong lo uh hi/thu ~-ah lamdang a | wonderful in counsel/Ama hong ~ citakin ka zui a | I have faithfully followed his guidance/Topa tung panin ~ a zon’ lohna | his not seeking guidance from the Lord) (s:makaihna) (b:lamlah) (r:6.9.14/18.23.11/23.28.29/13.10.14) (q:draft)
lamlahnate = (t:n) (w:instructions/directions/guideposts) (d:lamlahna, guidance, with plural te; on a road, the signs that show the way) (e:hih bang ~ kong piak uh/Lampi-ah ciamtehnate bawl unla, ~ phut un | set up road signs, put up guideposts) (s:vaikhaknate) (b:lamlahna) (r:52.4.2/24.31.21) (q:draft)
lamlak = (t:v) (w:guide/counsel/advise/direct) (d:show the way; thu lamlak is to give counsel and thu lamlak pa a counselor) (e:minamte leitungah ~ na hih manin/Topa in a mite ~ ahih manin | because the Lord guided his people/thu ~ pa bangin kua in amah hilh | who has taught him as his counselor/thu ~ tampi neihna in lungmuan’ na hi | having many advisers is safety/thu ~ amaute lakah om lo hi | there is no one among them to give counsel) (s:lamkaih/makaih) (a:lampialsak/lakkhial) (r:19.67.4/20.11.14/23.63.14/23.40.13/23.41.28) (q:draft)
lamlakin = (t:v) (w:guiding/directing/instructing) (d:lamlak, guide, with the linking ending in) (e:leitung minamte khempeuh ~ makai na hih manin/kumpipa’ uliante ama ut bangin ~ | directing the king's officials as he pleased) (b:lamlak) (r:19.67.4/19.105.21) (q:draft)
lamlakpa = (t:n) (w:counselor/adviser) (d:lam way and lak show, with pa for a man, one who shows the way; thu lamlakpa is a counselor) (e:amah thu ~ Ahuzzath leh a galkap mangpa/thu ~ bangin kua in amah hilh | who has taught him as his counselor/thu ~ leh khut siampa | the counselor and the skilled craftsman) (s:thulamlakpa/vaihawmpa) (b:lamlak) (r:1.26.26/23.40.13/23.3.3) (q:draft)
lamlakte = (t:n) (w:advisers/counselors/guides) (d:those who show the way, lamlak with plural -te; thu lamlakte are advisers) (e:a thu ~ in/Faro’ mipil thu ~ in thu haihuai gen | Pharaoh's wise counselors give senseless advice/kumpipa le a thu ~ le a uliante | the king, his advisers and his officials) (s:thulamlakte) (b:lamlak) (r:15.7.15/23.19.11/15.8.25) (q:draft)
lamlam = (t:adv) (d:descriptive word placed after kot, circle around, for birds hovering round and round overhead) (e:A kot ~ vasate bangin) (r:23.31.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
lamlian = (t:n) (w:main road/highway/street) (d:lam road with lian big; contrasted with lamneu, a lane or small path) (e:~ lam tawnin ka pai to ding/Khua sung ~ ah ahi zongin | whether in the streets of the town/~ kiu khempeuh ah amaute lum uh hi | they lie at every street corner/bawngpite ~ dung zui-in Bethshemesh lamah | the cows followed the road toward Beth Shemesh) (s:lamlianpi/kongzing) (a:lamneu) (r:4.20.19/42.14.21/23.51.20/9.6.12) (q:draft)
Lamlian = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Lamlian/Highway) (d:the Highway, in Kumpipa' Lamlian the King's Highway, the main road through Edom and the Amorite land east of the Jordan) (r:4.20.17/4.21.22)
lamlianpi = (t:n) (w:main road/highway/street) (d:lamlian main road, with pi big; set against lamneu, small path) (e:Nasemte zong ~-ah va pai uh a/~-ah va pai unla | go out to the main roads/Nangma ~ tuipi tung hi a | your highway was through the sea) (s:lamlian) (a:lamneu) (b:lamlian) (r:40.22.10/19.77.19/40.22.9) (q:draft)
lamliante = (t:n) (w:main roads/highways/roads) (d:lamlian, main road, with the plural te; set against lamneute, lanes) (e:Gam sung ~ le lamneute-ah va pai inla) (a:lamneute) (b:lamlian) (r:42.14.23) (q:draft)
lammat = (t:v) (w:seize/compel/press into service) (d:lam way with mat seize: lay hold of a passer-by and force him to do something) (e:a pua dingin ~ uh hi) (r:41.15.21) (q:draft)
lammatin = (t:v) (w:seizing/compelling) (d:lammat with the linking suffix in) (e:amah ~ Jesuh’ singlamteh a puasak uh hi) (b:lammat) (r:40.27.32) (q:draft)
lamna = (t:n) (w:building/construction) (d:the act of building a house, altar or temple) (e:biakna tau khat ~ tawh/biakinn khat a ~ thu | the news of the building of a temple/tua a ~-in kum sagih bei hi | he spent seven years building it) (s:innlamna/kilamna) (b:lam) (r:6.22.16/15.4.1/11.6.38) (q:draft)
lamna = (t:n) (w:dancing/dance) (d:the act of dancing, as a sign of joy and in praise; another spelling of laamna) (e:bawngno leh ~ a muh phetin/Khuang le ~ tawh amah phat unla | praise him with timbrel and dancing/a gualnuamte’ ~-ah na va kihel ding hi | you will join in the dance of the joyful/ka taunate ~ tawh nong heisak a | you turned my wailing into dancing) (s:laamna) (r:2.32.19/19.150.4/24.31.4/19.30.11) (q:draft)
lamnal = (t:n) (w:slippery path/slippery way) (d:lam way with nal slippery) (e:khuamial lak ~ hi ding a) (r:24.23.12) (q:draft)
lamnasa = (t:adj) (d:lam, build or set up, with the endings na and sa: where something has been built or pitched; a puanbuk lamnasa leitang is the ground where he had pitched his tent) (e:a puanbuk ~ leitang dangka zakhat tawh) (b:lamna) (r:1.33.19) (q:draft)
lamnawl = (t:n) (w:roadside/side of the road) (d:lam, road, with nawl, edge; lamnawl lam tawnin pai is to pass by along the far side of the road) (e:~ lam tawnin a paisan hi/~ lam tawnin a paisan leuleu hi | he too passed by on the other side) (r:42.10.31/42.10.32) (q:draft)
lamneu = (t:n) (w:lane/alley/small path) (d:lam, road, with neu, small; set against lamlian, main road) (e:~ ah ahi zongin pai in la/nangma ~ in tui liante tung ahi hi | your path was through the great waters) (a:lamlian/lamlianpi) (r:42.14.21/19.77.19) (q:draft)
lamneute = (t:n) (w:lanes/small paths) (d:lamneu, small path, with the plural te; set against lamliante, main roads) (e:nangma ~ zong luiliante’ tung mah ahi hi/lamliante le ~-ah va pai inla | go out to the roads and the lanes) (a:lamliante) (b:lamneu) (r:19.77.19/42.14.23) (q:draft)
lamnop = (t:v) (w:want to build/wish to build) (d:lam build with nop, the form of nuam want; a lamnop khempeuh is all that he wished to build) (e:Solomon in a ~ khempeuh a lamkik hi/kumpi inn le a ~ khempeuh | the royal palace and all he wished to build/ama ukna gam sung khempeuhah a ~ khempeuh | all he wished to build throughout his realm) (r:11.9.19/11.9.1/14.8.6) (q:draft)
lamnopna = (t:n) (w:desire to build/will to build) (d:lamnop want to build, with the noun suffix na) (e:biakinn ~ lungsim a guan hi) (b:lamnop) (r:37.1.14) (q:draft)
lamnu = (t:n) (w:builder) (d:lam build, with nu, the woman who built) (e:Uzzenerah khua a ~ ahi hi) (b:lam) (r:13.7.24) (q:draft)
lampa = (t:n) (w:builder) (d:lam, build, with pa, which marks a man: the man who builds; inn lampa is the builder of a house) (e:Inn ~ in inn sangin) (s:lamkippa) (b:lam) (r:58.3.3) (q:draft)
lampai = (t:v) (w:walk/travel/go on a journey) (d:lam, road, and pai, go, also used as a noun, journey) (e:Tuipi nuai leitam tungah ~ ngei/tua khuavak sungah ~ leh pukkha cih om lo | whoever walks in that light does not stumble/zan khuamial sungah ~ leh | if one walks in the dark of night/~ kawmin lungdamna a ko dingin | to give thanks while walking/lungdam takin a ~ a zom hi | he went on his way rejoicing) (s:khualzin) (r:18.38.16/43.11.9/43.11.10/16.12.31/44.8.39) (q:draft)
lampaina = (t:n) (w:marching/journey/way) (d:lampai, walk or travel, with na: the act of walking, or the way someone goes) (e:Lungli kungte’ dawnah ~ kheging na zak ciangin/amau’ ~ khua a vaksak dingin | to light the way they were to go) (s:khualzinna) (b:lampai) (r:10.5.24/16.9.12) (q:draft)
lampang = (t:n) (w:side) (d:the side lying in a given direction, as in leilu lampang, north side) (e:Leilu ~ a ding zong/nisuahna ~ teh a | he measured the east side/Leitaw ~ a dingin khuam sawmnih | twenty frames for the south side/Leilu ~ a om kulhkongpi thumte | the three gates on the north side) (s:pang) (r:2.38.11/26.48.10/26.42.16/2.36.23/26.48.30) (q:draft)
lampangah = (t:n) (w:on the side/at the side) (d:lampang side with the place marker ah; with a direction word, on the south side, on the north side) (e:biakbuk leitaw ~ giahphual sat ding uh a/biakna tau tung leilu ~ go ding a | he is to slaughter it at the north side of the altar/tua ~ thaltang thum ka lawn ding hi | I will shoot three arrows to that side/leitaw ~ nga omin | five being on the south side) (b:lampang) (r:4.3.29/9.20.20/3.1.11/11.7.49) (q:draft)
lampangte = (t:see) <lampangte-ah>
lampangte-ah = (t:adv) (w:on the sides) (d:lampang side, with the plural te and ah at) (e:hih lampang le hua ~ kaisuk ding hi) (r:2.26.13) (q:draft)
lampangteng = (t:n) (w:whole side/all of the side) (d:lampang, side, with teng, all of: the whole area on that side) (e:nisuahna ~ Gilead gam hi a/Jordan Gun nitumna ~ Israel gam hi-in | the whole west side of the Jordan being the land of Israel) (s:lamteng) (b:lampang) (r:26.47.18) (q:draft)
lampha = (t:v) (w:rebuild/build up/restore) (d:build again what was ruined, from lam, build) (e:tang lai-a a siasate ~ ding uh/Elath khua zo kikin ~ a | he retook Elath and rebuilt it/a kisia a khuapite uh ~ kikin | rebuilding their ruined cities/Solomon in ~-in tuate sungah Israel mite teeng sak | Solomon rebuilt them and settled Israelites in them) (s:lamkik/puahkik/bawlpha) (a:susia/phel) (r:23.61.4/12.14.22/30.9.14/14.8.2) (q:draft)
lamphei = (t:see) <lamphei-ah>
lamphei-ah = (t:n) (w:on a level path/on level ground) (d:lamphei, a level or even road, with the place marker ah) (e:ka galte hangin ~ hong kha in/Kei hong hehpih in la, ~ hong kha in | have mercy on me and lead me on level ground) (r:19.27.11/19.143.10) (q:draft)
lampi = (t:n) (w:way) (d:the way to a place, and the way of life a person follows) (e:Nopna ~ amau in a thei kei/pai nading mun ~ na thei uh hi | you know the way to the place I am going/thuman ~ ka zui a | I follow the way of righteousness) (s:lam/lamzin) (b:lam) (r:45.3.17/1.3.24/43.14.4/20.8.20)
lampi = (t:n) (w:footpath/path) (e:thutang ~ ka tawn hi | I walk along the paths of justice) (b:lam) (r:20.8.20)
lampi = (t:n) (w:road) (e:~-ah puante a phah uh hi/Tua ~ ah siampi khat paikha zenzen a | a priest happened to be going along that road) (b:lam) (r:42.19.36/42.10.31)
Lampi = (t:n) (w:way/road/path) (d:lampi written with a capital, mostly at the start of a sentence, also as a title, the Way as a name for the Christian faith, and in Lampi Siangtho, the Way of Holiness) (e:~ thu hangin thusia a piang hi/~ a pai lai takun tui omna-ah | as they went along the road they came to water/~ man panin ka pial a | if I have turned from the right path/nuntakna ~ nong hilh zo a | you have made known to me the path of life) (b:lampi) (r:44.19.23/23.35.8/44.8.36/18.31.7/44.2.28) (q:draft)
lampial = (t:v) (w:stray/turn aside/go astray) (d:leave the right way, lam way with pial turn off) (e:themkhat zong ~ lo hi/ka kalsuan uh ~ nai lo hi | our steps had not strayed/a teek dongin ~ nawn lo ding hi | even when old he will not turn from it/a gamtatna khempeuhah ~ het lo hi | in all his conduct he does not stray at all) (s:pial/pialkhia/gammang) (r:14.34.2/19.44.18/20.22.6/19.37.31) (q:draft)
lampial = (t:adj) (w:perverse/warped/wayward) (d:having left the right way, said of a perverse generation) (e:a ~ khang mite hi a/a ~, lungsim kawi khang mite | a warped and crooked generation) (r:5.32.20/5.32.5) (q:draft)
lampialgawp = (t:v) (w:be thrown off course/go wildly astray) (d:lampial leave the way, with gawp marking violent action; here of the heavenly bodies) (e:pai thei loin ~ ding hi) (b:lampial) (r:40.24.29) (q:draft)
lampialin = (t:v) (w:turning aside/going astray) (d:lampial turn aside, stray, with the linking ending in) (e:Kote khialin ~ ka gitloh tat uh hi/amah ~ a va et leh | when he turned aside to look) (s:pialin) (b:lampial) (r:11.8.47/7.14.8) (q:draft)
lampialna = (t:n) (w:straying/going astray/fall) (d:lampial, stray, with the noun suffix na: a leaving of the right way, a fall from where one stood) (e:na ~ uh phawkin) (s:pialna) (b:lampial) (r:66.2.5) (q:draft)
lampialsak = (t:v) (w:lead astray/mislead) (d:lampial, go astray, with sak, cause) (e:omsak a, Judah mite ~ hi/amaute’ makaite in ~ uh hi | their leaders lead them astray) (s:pialsak/lakkhial/khialsak) (a:lamlak) (b:lampial) (r:14.21.11/23.9.16) (q:draft)
lampialte = (t:n) (w:strays/those who go astray) (d:lampial stray, with the plural te; of sheep that have strayed, and of people who have left the right way) (e:A ~ na khiang kei uh a/a mangte zongin, a ~ kaikhawmin | searching for the lost and gathering the strays) (s:pialte/pialkhiate) (b:lampial) (r:26.34.4/66.21.8/26.34.16) (q:draft)
lampidung = (t:n) (w:along the path/roadside) (d:lampi road with dung length, the stretch along a road) (e:pawlkhatte ~ tu a) (s:lamdung) (r:42.8.5) (q:draft)
lampih = (t:v) (w:build with/help build) (d:lam build, with pih together with) (e:Topa in inn ~ kei leh) (b:lam) (r:19.127.1) (q:draft)
lampite = (t:n) (w:ways/paths/roads) (d:lampi, way, with the plural te: roads and paths, also the ways of God, the conduct he asks for) (e:na ~ hong hilh in/nangma ~ ka mitsuan ding hi | I will fix my eyes on your ways/ama ~ i zuih theih nadingin | so that we may walk in his paths/note’ ~ in gamkhing suak ding hi | your roads will become deserted) (b:lampi) (r:19.25.4/23.41.3/19.119.15/23.2.3/3.26.22) (q:draft)
lampiteng = (t:n) (w:the same way/the whole way) (d:lampi way with teng, all of it; a tot lampiteng is the way by which he came) (e:a kuanlamin a tot ~ mah) (b:lampi) (r:26.46.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
lamsa = (t:adj) (w:built) (d:lam build with sa, already done: that someone has built, placed after the builder and before the thing built) (e:Mihingte’ ~ khuapi leh tausangpi/ama ~ a inn | the palace he had built/a ~ khuapi min Samaria phuak hi | he named the city he had built Samaria/ama ~ saiha inn | the ivory palace he built) (s:kilamsa) (r:1.11.5/11.10.4/11.16.24/11.22.39) (q:draft)
lamsak = (t:v) (w:build for) (d:lam, build, with sak: build something for someone) (e:kei adingin inn khat hong ~ ding a/inn khat hong ~ ding na hi hiam | are you the one to build me a house/ama adingin inn khat a ~ dingin | to build a house for him/puanbuk khat ~ hi | he pitched a tent for it/Biakinn khat a ~ dingin Babilon gamah | to build a temple for it in Babylonia) (r:13.17.12/42.7.5/10.7.5/13.14.1/13.15.1/38.5.11) (q:draft)
lamsakkik = (t:v) (w:rebuild/have rebuilt) (d:lamsak with kik, again: have something built again, let it be rebuilt) (e:Ama mun ngei mahah a biakinn ~ un/meihal biakna a kipaipihna munah biakinn ~ un | let the temple be rebuilt at the place where burnt offerings are brought) (s:lamkik) (b:lamsak) (r:15.6.7/15.6.3) (q:draft)
lamsang = (t:n) (w:side/direction/respect) (d:with ah, on the side of, in the matter of, with regard to) (e:A pha ~ ah gamta a/mi ~ ah bang phattuamna a ngah | what did he gain on the human side/Thusia ~ a deih mite | people who want what is evil/lokhawhna ~ a lunghimawh kumpi | a king who cares about farming) (r:45.2.7/45.4.1/20.24.8/21.5.9) (q:draft)
lamsangah = (t:prep) (w:as regards/concerning/in respect of/according to) (d:lamsang, side or aspect, with ah; after a noun it means in the matter of) (e:Ci-le-sa ~ Israelte na en ta un/pilna ~ pil lo mi ka hi kei | in knowledge I am not untrained/thukham ~ mawhsakna a om lo | blameless as regards the law/piakna ~ cingh thei mahmah uh hi | in giving they were very generous) (s:tungtangah) (b:lamsang) (r:46.10.18/47.11.6/44.22.12/47.8.2) (q:draft)
lamsate = (t:n) (w:things built/buildings) (d:lamsa built, with the plural te: what someone has built) (e:keimah in ka ~ ka phelkik a/midangte’ inn ~ sutin a tang hi | he seized houses that others built) (b:lamsa) (r:24.45.4/18.20.19) (q:draft)
lamtak = (t:conj) (w:will be/that) (d:lam with tak, truly: placed after a clause and before thei or phawk, know, it marks what is known as a sure fact, as in Topa ka hih lamtak, that I am the Lord) (e:Topa ka hih ~ mi khempeuh in thei ding | everyone will know that I am the Lord/Topa ahih ~ thei uh ahih manin | because they knew that it was the Lord/thaman a ngah ding ~ phawk un | know that he will surely receive a reward/a guallelh ding ~ theitel hi | he knows well that they will be defeated) (r:26.11.10/43.21.12/40.10.42/19.112.8)
lamte = (t:n) (w:builders) (d:those who build, lam, build, with the plural te; inn lamte are the builders of a house) (e:Inn ~ in a nilkhiat suang pen/nang hong ~ in teembaw hoih bangin hong bawl | your builders made you like a fine ship) (s:innlamte) (b:lam) (r:19.118.22/26.27.4) (q:draft)
lamte = (t:n) (w:possessions/belongings) (d:in a neih a lamte, what one has and owns) (e:a neih a ~ uh a zuak khit) (s:neihsate) (r:44.2.45) (q:draft, low confidence)
lamteng = (t:n) (w:whole side/all the part toward) (d:lam side, direction, with teng all: the whole of the side that is named) (e:Tua gam leitaw ~ Efraim/a leilu ~ Manasseh a’ hi a | the whole north side was Manasseh's) (s:lampangteng) (b:lam) (r:6.17.10) (q:draft)
lamteng = (t:n) (w:possessions/goods) (d:in a neih a lamteng, all that one owns, property and goods) (e:a neih a ~ uh zuak uh a) (s:neihsate) (r:44.2.45) (q:draft, low confidence)
lamthuah = (t:v) (w:build more/build in addition) (d:lam build, with thuah add) (e:kulhnei khuapi tampi a ~ uh hi) (r:28.8.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
lamto = (t:v) (w:lift up/raise) (d:lift something upward, said of raising the hand and of raising a person up from a low place) (e:na khut ~ in la/leivui panin mizawngte ~-in | raising the poor from the dust/a khut taklam vantung lamah ~ a | he raised his right hand toward heaven/a khut ~-in thupha a pia hi | he lifted up his hands and blessed them) (s:domto/laamto) (r:19.10.12/19.113.7/66.10.5/42.24.50) (q:draft)
lamun = (t:adv) (d:lam way, direction, with un, the ending in as used with a plural subject: in the direction of, in the course of; a nung leh lamun is backwards, an a zonna lamun is while they looked for food) (e:a nung leh ~ pai-in/an a zon’na ~ siampite leh makaite | while searching for food the priests and elders) (b:lam) (r:1.9.23/25.1.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
lamval = (t:n) (w:surplus/abundance) (d:paired with neihval, what one has over and above one's need) (e:a neihval a ~ sung panun a khia uh) (s:neihval) (r:41.12.44) (q:draft, low confidence)
lamzan = (t:v) (w:succeed/prosper) (d:go well on one's way, written with a final apostrophe before theih) (e:hoih takin na ~’ theihna dingin) (s:lawhcing) (r:6.1.7) (q:draft)
lamzin = (t:n) (w:path/way) (d:the road one travels, lam, road, with zin, travel; here set beside lampi) (e:lampi nusia-in, ~ panin pial un la) (s:lampi) (r:23.30.11) (q:draft)
lamzingte = (t:n) (w:streets) (d:the streets of a town, where people pass and gather) (e:Ko khua ~ ah thu na hilh ngei hi) (s:kongzingte) (r:42.13.26) (q:draft)
lamzo = (t:v) (w:be able to build) (d:lam build, with zo be able) (e:kua in biakinn ~ ding ahi hiam) (b:lam) (r:14.2.6) (q:draft)
lan = (t:n) (w:banner/flag/signal) (d:a flag raised as a signal) (e:minamte’ adingin ~ khat khai ding a/Mual kolh tungah ~ khat khai to un | raise a banner on a bare hilltop/mualte tungah ~ khat hong kilah ciangin | when a banner is raised on the mountains) (s:dial/dialkhai) (r:23.11.12/23.13.2/23.18.3) (q:draft)
lan = (t:adj) (w:lustful/oversexed) (d:of strong sexual desire, said of men and of a stallion; the NIV speaks of large genitals here) (e:A ~ mahmah na veng Izipt mite/a ~ mahmah mi khempeuh ngai pahpah hi | she kept lusting after every very lustful man) (r:26.16.26/26.23.20) (q:draft, low confidence)
lang = (t:n) (w:half) (d:one of the two equal parts of a thing; a lang is half of it) (e:puan a ~ a val pen/Israelte in a ~ a ngah | the half that the Israelites received/mihonte in a ~ a ngah teng | all of the half the community received) (s:alang/phelkhat) (r:2.26.12/4.31.42/4.31.43) (q:draft)
lang = (t:n) (w:side/opposing side) (d:one of two sides; lang pang is to take the side against someone, and lang khatah is against) (e:Zeisu ~ pangin a zahko uh hi/Mihingte ei ~ pangin hong thawh ciangin | when people rose up against us/a gun ~ nih tuakah singkung tampi | many trees on both sides of the river) (s:pang) (r:42.22.65/2.20.16/19.124.2/26.47.7) (q:draft)
langa = (t:prep) (w:against/on the side opposite) (d:lang side with a; langa pang is to take a stand against someone) (e:nangma ~ a pang mi khempeuh) (s:langah/langkhatah) (b:lang) (r:23.54.17) (q:draft)
langah = (t:prep) (w:against) (d:on the opposing side of, after a possessive as in ka langah against me) (e:teci man lote ka ~ pang khin a/leitung in ama ~ teci pang hi | the earth testifies against him/Na ~ siat nading vaihawm a | they plot harm against you/Na galte ~ kuanin | going out against your enemies) (s:langkhatah/langpangin) (b:lang) (r:19.27.12/18.20.27/19.21.11/5.23.9) (q:draft)
langaih = (t:n) (w:melody/music/sweet song) (d:pleasing song, la, song, with ngaih, lovely; langaih sa is to make music) (e:ama tungah ~ sa un/laiza lasakna leh ~ tawh phat un | praise with the music of the harp and with melody) (r:19.149.3/19.98.5) (q:draft)
langbawl = (t:v) (w:turn against/oppose/be hostile to) (d:lang side with bawl make: set oneself against someone) (e:a gamtatsia mite Topa in a ~ hi/nangawn in kei hong ~ uh hi | even they have turned against me/mi khempeuh ~ uh hi | they are hostile to everyone) (s:langpang/galbawl/langneih) (b:lang) (r:60.3.12/18.19.19/52.2.15) (q:draft)
langbawlna = (t:n) (w:opposition/hostility) (d:langbawl turn against, with the noun suffix na; in Proverbs 28:21 mi langbawlna is taking sides between people, partiality) (e:mawhnei mite’ ~ a thuaknate ngaihsun unla/Mi ~ hoih lo a | showing partiality is not good) (s:langpanna/kilangbawlna) (b:langbawl) (r:58.12.3/20.28.21) (q:draft)
langgen = (t:v) (w:show partiality/take the side of/favor) (d:lang, side, with gen, speak: speak for one side in a judgment) (e:mizawngte ~ loin, a liante thu zui loin) (s:angvan) (r:3.19.15) (q:draft)
langkhat = (t:n) (w:one side/other side/half) (d:one of two sides or of a pair, as in khut langkhat, one hand, and gam langkhat, half the kingdom) (e:pang ~ zong na dawh lai un/ka gam ~ dongin kong pia ding hi | I will give you up to half my kingdom/a khut ~ mah bangin a dam hi | it was restored like the other hand) (r:40.5.39/41.6.23/40.12.13) (q:draft)
langkhatah = (t:prep) (w:against) (d:on the opposite side; langkhatah pang is stand against, langkhatah teci pang is testify against) (e:na vengpa ~ teci pang kei in/note’ ~ teci ka pang ding hi | I will testify against you/Mihonpite in amau ~ a ding uh a | the crowd rose up against them/no ~ teci na pang uh hi | you testify against yourselves) (s:langah/langpangin) (r:20.24.28/23.14.22/19.50.7/44.16.22/40.23.31) (q:draft)
langkhiasak = (t:v) (w:display/make known/reveal) (d:lang, appear, with khia, out, and sak, cause: bring something out into open view) (e:mite lakah nangma vangliatna a ~ khin Pasian) (s:langsak/kilangsak) (r:19.77.14) (q:draft)
langmuh = (t:see) <langmuh-a>
langmuh-a = (t:adv) (w:with partiality/taking sides) (d:lang side and muh see, with a: looking to one side, showing favour) (e:Mi ~ thukhenna hoih lo hi) (r:20.24.23) (q:draft)
langneih = (t:v) (w:be against/oppose/take sides) (d:lang side with neih have: take a side about someone, mostly against; na langneih mite is your enemies; in Exodus 23:3 of taking sides over a poor man in a lawsuit) (e:mote in a teeknu uh ~ uh hi/Na ~ mite’ bawngtal | your enemies' ox/mizawng pa na ~ kei ding uh hi | you shall not take sides over a poor man) (s:langbawl) (r:33.7.6/2.23.4/2.23.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
langnih = (t:n) (w:both sides/two sides) (d:lang, side, with nih, two; langnih a hiam is sharp on both sides, double-edged; of a pair, as feet or parties, it means both) (e:~ a hiam namsau khat/a khe a ~-in a bai hi | he was lame in both feet/a pang ~ tuakah a kigelh suangpeekte | tablets written on both sides/thuneite a ~ tuakin | both parties to the dispute) (r:66.1.16/10.9.13/2.32.15/5.19.17) (q:draft)
langnihin = (t:adv) (w:on both sides/both) (d:langnih, both sides, with in; of a sword, double-edged; of feet, both) (e:a ~ a hiam mahmah namsau/a khe a ~ a zaw hi | he was lame in both feet) (b:langnih) (r:66.2.12/10.9.13) (q:draft)
langpa = (t:n) (w:opponent/other party/adversary) (d:lang, opposing side, with pa, which marks a man: the man on the other side) (e:a ~ in a thuk mateng/namsau tawh a ~’ pang dawt ciat uh hi | each thrust his sword into his opponent's side) (s:galpa) (b:lang) (r:20.18.17/10.2.16) (q:draft)
langpan = (t:v) (w:oppose/rise against/rebel against) (d:form of langpang, written langpan’ before a following word) (e:Mi tampi in kei hong ~’ nainai hi/kote in nang ka hong ~’ uh hi | we have rebelled against you/Hong ~ mi zong tampi a om uh hi | there are also many who oppose me/mi lehdote in ~’ kei uh hen | let the rebellious not rise against him) (s:langbawl/galbawl/lehdo) (r:19.3.1/27.9.9/46.16.9/19.66.7) (q:draft)
langpang = (t:v) (w:oppose/resist/rebel against) (d:take a stand against someone, lang, side, with pang, stand; the one opposed comes directly before it) (e:Amaute bangin hong ~ kei in/Topa ~ na hih manin | because you opposed the Lord/Izipt mite in ama thu ~ uh hi | the Egyptians rebelled against his word) (s:langbawl/galbawl/lehdo) (a:panpih) (r:26.2.8/19.35.1/24.50.24/19.105.28) (q:draft)
langpang = (t:n) (w:adversary/opponent) (d:one who stands against another, an opponent or enemy) (e:Solomon’ lang khatah ~ khat/hong ~ ahi a, thusia ahi zongin om lo | there is neither adversary nor disaster) (s:galpa/langpa) (r:11.11.14/11.5.4) (q:draft)
langpanga = (t:adv) (w:against/in opposition to) (d:langpang oppose, with a) (e:keimah ~ hong dingte kiang panin) (b:langpang) (r:19.59.1) (q:draft)
langpangin = (t:prep) (w:against) (d:langpang, oppose, with the linking suffix in; opposing, in opposition to) (e:na sanggamte ~ thu na gen uh hi/Topa leh ama sathau nilhpa ~ vaihawm uh a | they plot against the Lord and his anointed/keimah ~ kikaikhawm uh hi | they gathered against me/Pasian ~ a khuttum a lahsan | he shakes his fist against God) (s:langah/langkhatah) (b:langpang) (r:19.50.20/19.35.15/19.2.2/18.15.25) (q:draft)
langpangte = (t:n) (w:foes/adversaries/enemies/opponents) (d:langpang, oppose, with the plural te: those who stand against someone) (e:amah a ~ daantatin/a kimkot-a om ama ~ kangtum hi | it burns up his foes all around/amah ~ in leivui liak ta uh hen | may his foes lick the dust/Amah in, a ~ zo a | he defeated his foes) (s:galte/demte) (a:lawmte) (b:langpang) (r:34.1.2/19.97.3/19.72.9/19.78.66) (q:draft)
langpanin = (t:v) (w:opposing/against/defying) (d:form of langpan with -in; after its object it can be translated against) (e:Saul in Topa’ nungzuite ~ tawng a/amah in Topa ~ kiliansak hi | he exalted himself against the Lord/Zeisu’ min ~ ahi thei zahzaha sep ding | to do all that is possible against the name of Jesus/~ lim leh nalamdang na bawl hi | you performed signs and wonders against them) (b:langpan) (r:44.9.1/24.48.26/44.26.9/16.9.10) (q:draft)
langpanna = (t:n) (w:opposition/rebellion/protest) (d:langpan, oppose, with the noun suffix na: the act of standing against someone, rebellion against God) (e:Paul in ~ tawh ama puan singkhia-in/Topa ~ thu gen na hih manin | because you have preached rebellion against the Lord/a hong ~ khempeuhte uh ka maisak ding hi | I will forgive all their rebellion against me) (s:langbawlna/lehdona) (b:langpan) (r:44.18.6/24.33.8/24.28.16) (q:draft)
langsak = (t:v) (w:reveal/show/make known/bring to light) (d:cause to appear or be seen openly) (e:Mihaite in a hehna uh ~ pah a/ama thumanna ~ khin hi | he has revealed his righteousness/minam khempeuh tungah ka ~ ding a | I will make it known to all nations/keima minthan’na hong ~ ding hi | he will reveal my glory) (s:kilangsak/pulak) (a:seel) (r:20.12.16/55.1.10/19.98.2/26.38.23/43.16.14) (q:draft)
langsakin = (t:v) (w:showing/revealing/making known) (d:langsak make known with the linking ending in; a dikna langsakin is showing him to be in the right) (e:a dikpa a dikna ~ ama dikna tawh/na lungkhamna uh ~, leivui lakah kikhuk un | showing your grief, roll in the dust) (s:theisakin) (b:langsak) (r:11.8.32/33.1.10) (q:draft)
langsakkik = (t:v) (w:show again/renew) (d:langsak, show, with kik, again: show once more, renew, as of concern for someone shown again after a long time) (e:na hong ~ thei uh hi) (b:langsak) (r:50.4.10) (q:draft)
langsakpa = (t:n) (w:vindicator/one who reveals) (d:langsak, show, with pa, the man who does it; ka thumanna a langsakpa is he who shows that I am in the right, my vindicator) (e:ka thumanna a ~ Pasian a nai-ah) (b:langsak) (r:23.50.8) (q:draft)
langsakpah = (t:v) (w:show at once/reveal immediately) (d:langsak, show, with pah, at once: let something be seen immediately) (e:Mihaite in a hehna uh ~ uh a) (r:20.12.16) (q:draft)
langsakta = (t:v) (w:have revealed/have shown) (d:langsak, show, with ta marking a state now reached: has now shown or revealed) (e:na mawhna hong ~ hi) (b:langsak) (r:18.15.6) (q:draft)
langtang = (t:see) <langtang-a>
langtang-a = (t:adv) (w:openly/in the open) (d:in an open way, not hidden; a langtang-a taina is open rebuke) (e:a ~ taina hoihzaw hi) (s:langtangin/kilangin) (a:simthamin/thusimin) (r:20.27.5) (q:draft)
langtangin = (t:adv) (w:openly/publicly/plainly) (d:langtang, open, with the ending in, used as a langtangin: openly, in plain view, without hiding) (e:Sodom bangin amaute a ~ gamta uh a/a ~ thuman takin ka gamta uh a | we live openly and truthfully/a ~ kulh ciangte’ mai-ah nang hong hehsak uh | they provoked you openly in front of the builders/a ~ taina hoihzaw hi | open rebuke is better) (s:langtang-a/kilangin) (a:simthamin/thusimin) (r:23.3.9/47.4.2/16.4.5/20.27.5) (q:draft)
langte = (t:n) (w:half) (d:one side or half of a group, as in Manasseh minam a langte, the half-tribe of Manasseh) (e:Manasseh minam a ~ tungah/leh Manasseh minam a ~ simin | and summoning the half-tribe of Manasseh) (s:alangte) (b:lang) (r:6.1.12/6.22.1) (q:draft)
langte = (t:n) (w:enemies/foes/adversaries) (d:lang, opposing side, with the plural te: those on the other side, enemies) (e:Tui in amau’ ~ tummang a/ka ~’ kiang panin kei hong honkhia in | rescue me from my enemies/Tuikhang in a suksiat bangin a ~ susiagawp a | as a flood destroys, he wipes out his foes/Kei hong bawlsiate leh ka ~ tam mahmah a | my persecutors and my foes are very many) (s:galte/langpangte/mudahte/dote) (a:lawmte) (b:lang) (r:19.106.11/19.143.9/34.1.8/19.119.157) (q:draft)
langtuakah = (t:adv) (w:on each side/on both sides/on each) (d:lang, side, with tuak, each, and ah, at: on each of the two sides, as in a khut langtuakah, on each of his hands) (e:a khut ~ khutme guk/le a khe ~ kheme guk | and six toes on each foot/ama ~ zong midang khat tuak mah khai-in | they also crucified one other man on each side of him/a ~ galkapte in lenin | with soldiers holding him on each side) (s:langnihin) (r:10.21.20/43.19.18/44.12.6) (q:draft)
langva = (t:todo) (q:draft, part of a measure of oil in Luke 16:6, sathau langva phel zakhat, the meaning of langva alone is not clear)
lanlan = (t:adv) (d:descriptive word placed after pai, walk, for the stately walk of a king before his people, beside kuahkuah for the rooster and gangan for the he-goat) (e:a mite mai-ah a pai ~ kumpipa) (r:20.30.31) (q:draft, low confidence)
lanluat = (t:n) (w:lewdness/debauchery/excessive lust) (d:lan, lustful, with luat, too much: shameless excess in sexual behaviour; lanluat khialhna is a lewd offence) (e:kihhuaina le ~ khialhna gamta uh hi/Numei tawh mawhna, thangtatna, ~ mana khialhna | sexual immorality, impurity and the sin of debauchery) (s:lanna/hukna/thangtatna) (r:7.20.6/48.5.19) (q:draft)
lanluatna = (t:n) (w:lewdness/outrageous act) (d:lanluat with the noun suffix na) (e:Israel-te sungah ~ tawh a khialhna uh) (s:lanna/hukna) (b:lanluat) (r:7.20.10) (q:draft)
lanna = (t:n) (w:lewdness/debauchery/lust) (d:lan, lustful, with the noun suffix na: shameless sexual behaviour, often paired with hukna) (e:hukna, ~ kihhuaina ahi zongin/hukna ~, a hoih lo lunggulhna | impurity, lust and evil desires/amau’ ~ tawh kizui-in gamta tawntung hi | they keep acting according to their lewdness) (s:hukna/lanluat/thangtatna) (b:lan) (r:45.13.13/26.22.9/51.3.5) (q:draft)
lannate = (t:n) (w:lewd acts/debauchery) (d:plural of lanna) (e:numei tawh mawhna, hukna, ~ hangin) (s:huknate) (b:lanna) (r:47.12.21) (q:draft)
lano = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:colt/young donkey/foal) (d:the young of a donkey: la, donkey, with no, young or little) (e:Zeisu in ~ khat ngah a/~ khat kikhihsa a muh uh ciangin | when they found a colt tied up/Amaute in ~ Zeisu kiangah paipih uh a | they brought the colt to Jesus) (s:laano) (b:la) (r:43.12.14/41.11.4/41.11.7) (q:draft)
Lano = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:colt/young donkey) (d:lano, colt, written with a capital at the start of a sentence or a line of verse) (e:~ tungah tuangin hong pai ding hi/~ khau sut un la | untie the colt) (b:lano) (r:43.12.15/41.11.2) (q:draft)
lante = (t:n) (w:banners/flags) (d:lan banner with the plural te) (e:i Pasian’ min tawh i ~ khai ni) (s:dialte/dialkhaite) (b:lan) (r:19.20.5) (q:draft)
lante = (t:n) (w:lusty ones) (d:lan, lustful, with the plural te; sakol gilvah a lante are well-fed, lusty stallions) (e:Sakol gilvah a ~ bangin) (r:24.5.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
lanu = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:female donkey) (d:la donkey, with nu female) (e:numei nasem, ~, le kalaohte a pia hi) (s:lapi) (a:latal) (r:1.12.16) (q:draft)
Laodikia = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Laodicea) (d:city in the Lycus valley of Asia Minor near Colossae and Hierapolis, home of one of the seven churches of Revelation) (r:51.4.15/51.4.16)
Laodisia = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Laodicea) (d:city in the Lycus valley of Asia Minor near Colossae and Hierapolis, home of one of the seven churches of Revelation) (r:51.4.15/51.4.16)
lap = (t:v) (w:overtake/catch up with) (d:catch up with and come upon someone, as darkness overtaking a traveller) (e:Khuamial in no hong ~ loh nadingin) (r:43.12.35) (q:draft, low confidence)
lapa = (t:n) (w:one who takes/gatherer/taker) (d:la, take, with pa: the man who takes or gathers something, as an lapa, one who gathers food, and thuciamna a lapa, one who takes an oath) (e:A hun-a an ~ in mipil hi a/An tampi a ~ in an hau lua tuan lo | the one who gathered much did not have too much/leitungah thuciamna a ~ in | whoever takes an oath in the land) (b:la) (r:20.10.5/26.18.7/47.8.15/23.65.16) (q:draft)
laphuah = (t:v) (w:compose songs/write poetry) (d:la, song, with phuah, compose; laphuah siampa is a poet, and ama laphuah is the songs he composed) (e:note sung panin ~ siampa khat in/ama ~ dawng tul le dawng nga ahi hi | the songs he composed numbered a thousand and five) (s:laphuak) (r:44.17.28/11.4.32) (q:draft)
laphuak = (t:v) (w:compose songs) (d:la song with phuak compose; laphuak siampa is a skilled maker of songs) (e:Israel ~ siampa David’ kam nunungte) (s:laphuah) (r:10.23.1) (q:draft, low confidence)
lapi = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:female donkey) (d:la donkey with pi female; the male is latal) (e:~ sawmnih leh latal sawm la hi/an a pua ~ sawm puak hi | he sent ten female donkeys loaded with food/bawngtal kap zanga, ~ zanga le nasem tampi | five hundred yoke of oxen, five hundred donkeys and many servants/~ tung le lano tungah tuangin hong pai hi | he comes riding on a donkey and on a colt) (s:lanu) (a:latal) (r:1.32.15/1.45.23/18.1.3/40.21.5) (q:draft)
Lapi = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:donkey/female donkey) (d:Lapi’ ta lano is the foal of a donkey) (e:~’ ta lano leh la tungah) (b:lapi) (r:40.21.5) (q:draft)
laplap = (t:adv) (w:more and more) (d:after a verb, apparently of something that keeps piling up; the sense is not certain from one verse) (e:thu mah kibeh ~ hi) (r:21.5.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
lapna = (t:n) (w:raising/lifting) (d:lap raise, with the noun suffix na; khut lapna is the lifting of the hand) (e:ka khut ~ tawh) (s:laptohna) (r:18.31.27) (q:draft, low confidence)
lapnuam = (t:v) (w:want to reach in time/want to be in time for) (d:lap catch up with, with nuam want) (e:Pentekos Pawi hun ~ ahih manin) (r:44.20.16) (q:draft)
Lappidoth = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Lappidoth) (d:husband of the prophetess Deborah) (r:7.4.4)
laptoh = (t:v) (w:lift up/raise up) (d:lap, raise, with toh, upward: lift a person up, raise to honour) (e:note hong ~ theih nadingin) (s:domto/phongto/sangsak) (a:niamsak) (r:60.5.6) (q:draft)
laptohna = (t:n) (w:lifting up/raising) (d:laptoh, lift up, with na) (e:ka khutte ka ~ pen nitak biak piakna) (s:lapna) (b:laptoh) (r:19.141.2) (q:draft)
lasa = (t:n) (w:singer) (d:person who sings, especially one appointed to sing; lasa pawl is a group of singers) (e:~ numei leh pasal mihing zanih/~ numei leh pasal za nih leh sawmli-le-nga | two hundred and forty-five female and male singers/~ pawl a nihna a makaipa hi | he was the leader of the second group of singers) (s:lasiam) (r:15.2.65/16.7.67/13.6.39) (q:draft)
lasa = (t:v) (w:sing) (d:sing a song, from la, song, and sa, sing) (e:ka nasemte in lungdamin ~ ding uh a/a tunga teeng mite aw, ~ un | sing, you who live on them/~ kawmin Jerusalem hong tung ding uh hi | they will come to Jerusalem singing/Pasian tungah ~-in phat un | praise God with singing/amaute lungdamin ~ khawm uh hi | they sing together for joy) (s:lasak) (r:23.65.14/23.35.10/23.42.10/51.3.16/23.52.8) (q:draft)
lasak = (t:v) (w:have brought/send for/let take) (d:la, take, with the causative sak: have something or someone fetched, or let someone take a thing) (e:puanza zong na ~ un/Tangvalte khat hong paisak inla hong ~ in | let one of the young men come over and get it/a vekin amah ~ in | let him take it all/hih lai munah nang kong ~ ding hi | I will send for you to come back here) (r:40.5.40/17.6.8/9.26.22/10.19.30/1.27.45) (q:draft)
lasak = (t:v) (w:sing) (d:la, song, and sak, sing: sing a song; also the act of singing, as in lasak hun, the time of singing) (e:~ hun hong tung ta a/Miriam in amaute ~ hi | Miriam sang to them/biakna ~ nadingin lasakna nate nei uh hi | they had instruments for singing sacred songs/biakbuk mai-ah ~ na sem uh hi | they served with song before the tabernacle) (s:lasa) (r:22.2.12/2.15.21/13.16.42/13.6.32) (q:draft)
lasakin = (t:v) (w:having brought/letting fetch) (d:lasak have something brought, with the linking suffix in) (e:tui tawmkhat ~ na khe uh sil unla) (b:lasak) (r:1.18.4) (q:draft)
lasakna = (t:n) (w:instrument/music/musical instrument/singing) (d:lasak, sing, with the noun suffix na: singing or music, and an instrument for making music; it follows the name of an instrument, as harp lasakna, the harp, and laiza lasakna, the lyre) (e:tamngai leh harp ~ aw tawh kituakin/khausai ~ i tum ding hi | we will play stringed instruments/na ~ uh a gingte ka za nuam kei | I do not want to hear the sound of your music/tu-a ka zak pen ~ awging ahi hi | what I hear is the sound of singing) (s:tumtheih) (b:lasak) (r:18.21.12/23.38.20/30.5.23/2.32.18)
lasaknate = (t:n) (w:musical instruments/instruments) (d:lasakna, instrument, with the plural te; often after the name of an instrument, as in laiza lasaknate, lyres) (e:~ tawh Levi mite ding uh a/ka bawlsa ~ tawh | with the instruments I have made/zawl la sa-in ~ a tum mipa | a man who sings love songs and plays instruments) (s:tumtheihte) (b:lasakna) (r:14.29.26/14.20.28/13.23.5/26.33.32) (q:draft)
lasaknate = (t:n) (w:songs/singing) (e:ka ~ in amah lungdamsak ta hen) (s:late) (b:lasakna) (r:19.104.34) (q:draft, low confidence)
lasakolte = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:mules) (d:la donkey and sakol horse, with the plural te) (e:Galte’ phual-a om sakolte, ~, kalaohte) (r:38.14.15) (q:draft)
lasate = (t:n) (w:singers/musicians) (d:lasa, singer, with the plural te: the singers and musicians, especially those of the temple) (e:~ Heman, Asaf, leh Ethan-te in/Levi mi ~ hong kikaikhawm uh hi | the Levite singers were gathered together/kongcingte, ~, leh Levi mite a kiseh khit ciangin | after the gatekeepers, the singers and the Levites were appointed/~ in sa uh a, peengkul tumte in tum uh | the singers sang and the trumpeters played) (r:13.15.19/14.35.25/16.12.28/16.7.1/14.29.28) (q:draft)
Lasha = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Lasha) (d:place on the border of the land of the Canaanites, named after Sodom, Gomorrah, Admah and Zeboyim) (r:1.10.19)
