lasiam = (t:n) (w:singer/skilled singer) (d:la, song, with siam, skilled: one who is good at singing) (e:la a sa ding ~ numei leh pasal tampi) (s:lasa) (r:21.2.8) (q:draft)
lasuk = (t:v) (w:bring down/take down) (d:la, take, with suk, downward: bring or take down) (e:vantung panin Khrih a ~ ding) (s:laksuk/lakhiasuk) (a:lato) (b:la) (r:45.10.6) (q:draft)
lasukin = (t:v) (w:taking down) (d:lasuk take down, with the linking suffix in) (e:Zeisu’ luang ~ saihadial puan tawh) (b:lasuk) (r:42.23.53) (q:draft)
latal = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:male donkey) (d:la donkey with tal male; the female is lapi) (e:lapi sawmnih leh ~ sawm la hi/Amah in tuu, bawngtal, ~, pasal nasem | he gave sheep, cattle, male donkeys, male servants) (a:lapi/lanu) (r:1.32.15/1.12.16) (q:draft)
late = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:donkeys/asses) (d:la, donkey, with the plural te) (e:a ~ uh antang suan-in paikhia uh/a ~ uh tawh mite kisawlkhia hi | the men were sent off with their donkeys/kalaohte, ~, leh ganhing om khempeuh tungah | on the camels, the donkeys and all the animals) (s:laate) (b:la) (r:1.42.26/1.44.3/38.14.15) (q:draft)
late = (t:n) (w:songs) (d:la, song, with the plural te) (e:ama ~ in tul-le-nga a hi hi/lungdam ~ tawh amaute gen sak un | let them tell of it with songs of joy) (s:lasaknate) (b:la) (r:11.4.32/19.107.22) (q:draft)
late = (t:n) (w:reapers/harvesters) (d:those who take, la with the plural marker te; an late are those who take in the grain, the reapers, and leitawi a late are those who take a loan, borrowers) (e:an ~ a uk a nasempa kiangah/an ~’ nung lo sungah ansanghte tawm hi | she gleaned in the field behind the harvesters) (s:anlate/atte) (b:la) (r:8.2.5/20.22.7/8.2.3) (q:draft)
