Latin = (t:name) (w:Latin) (d:the language of the Romans, one of the three languages of the notice on the cross of Jesus) (r:43.19.20)
lato = (t:v) (w:take up/lift up/draw up) (d:la, take, with to, upward: take, lift or draw up) (e:tuipi panin tuite ~ a/Jehu in leeng sungah amah ~ hi | Jehu took him up into the chariot/Pasian in ama kiangah ~ ahih manin | because God took him up to himself/a nungta-in nong ~ veve hi | yet you brought me up alive) (s:lakto) (a:lasuk/laksuk) (b:la) (r:18.36.27/12.6.7/12.10.15/58.11.5/32.2.6) (q:draft)
latsak = (t:v) (w:show/testify/make known) (d:make something seen; of honesty, speak for a person afterwards) (e:hong kinung ~ ding hi) (s:langsak) (r:1.30.33) (q:draft, low confidence)
latsakna = (t:n) (w:showing/making known) (d:latsak show, with the noun suffix na) (e:Pasian thu a ~ tawh a kipawl) (s:lahna/muhsakna) (b:latsak) (r:56.1.1) (q:draft, low confidence)
lau = (t:adj) (w:afraid/frightened/fearful) (d:feeling fear; lau mahmah is very afraid) (e:Kei ka ~ ciangin/huan sungah ka za a, ka ~ hi | I heard it in the garden and I was afraid/khua mial bekbak a, ~ mahmah hi | it grew very dark and he was greatly afraid/Pilat in a zak ciangin ~ semsem a | when Pilate heard it he was even more afraid) (s:meidawi) (a:hang/lungmuang) (r:19.56.3/1.3.10/1.15.12/43.19.8)
lau = (t:v) (w:fear/scare/be afraid) (d:feel fear of someone or of something that may happen; lau kei in and lau kei un are the commands do not be afraid) (e:~ lo dingin thu nong pia hi/Keimah ka hi hi, ~ kei un | it is I, do not be afraid/Thuman mite in mu-in, ~ ding uh a | the righteous will see and fear/hong thah khit khak ding ka ~ hi | I fear he will kill us all/Abram aw, ~ kei in | do not be afraid, Abram) (s:kihta/kihtak) (r:25.3.57/43.6.20/19.52.6/1.32.11/1.15.1)
laugawp = (t:v) (w:be terrified/be greatly afraid) (d:lau fear with the intensifier gawp; with sak, terrify) (e:kote hong ~ sak hi) (s:laulua/kihtalua) (b:lau) (r:19.90.7) (q:draft)
laugawpsak = (t:v) (w:frighten/terrify) (d:laugawp be terrified, with the causative sak) (e:note a hong ~ nuam ka) (s:lausakgawp/dipkuasak) (a:hehnem) (b:laugawp) (r:47.10.9) (q:draft)
lauhlauh = (t:adv) (d:descriptive word placed after tuan, ride, for the jolting and bouncing of a chariot being driven) (e:sakol leeng tuan ~ gingte) (r:34.3.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
lauhuai = (t:adj) (w:dreadful/terrible/fearful/awesome) (d:lau, fear, with huai, causing: causing fear or awe, dreadful; of anger, fierce) (e:a ~ taktak thu ahi hi/tua a ~ hun hong tun’ ma-in | before that dreadful time comes/a ~ nate na bawl ngei a | you did awesome things/Hih mun bangzahin ~ ahi hiam | how awesome is this place) (s:kihtakhuai/mulkimhuai/dipkuathuai) (a:lungmuanhuai) (r:58.10.31/23.64.3/29.2.31/1.28.17) (q:draft)
lauhuaina = (t:n) (w:terror/danger/dread) (d:lauhuai, dreadful or dangerous, with the noun suffix na: terror, or danger that threatens) (e:~ tuak kha nawn lo ding uh hi/kei tungah ~ lianpite hong om nawn lo ding | great terrors will no longer be upon me/Pasian' kiang panin ~ lianpi khat tung ahih manin | because a great terror from God fell on them/zan-a ~, sun-a thaltang leengte | the terror of night, the arrows that fly by day) (s:launa/kihtakna) (a:bitna/lungmuanna) (b:lauhuai) (r:38.14.11/45.8.35/18.9.34/1.35.5/19.91.5) (q:draft)
lauhuainate = (t:n) (w:terrors/dangers) (d:lauhuaina, terror or danger, with the plural te) (e:tui leh mei ~ ka thuak uh hi) (s:launate) (b:lauhuaina) (r:19.66.12) (q:draft)
lauhuaipi = (t:adj) (w:fierce/most dreadful/terrible) (d:lauhuai dreadful with pi, great; said of anger) (e:Topa’ hehna ~ eite’ kiang pan/hehna a ~ kilehkik lo ding hi | the fierce anger will not turn back) (b:lauhuai) (r:24.4.8/24.30.24) (q:draft)
lauhuaite = (t:adj) (w:terrible/fearsome/cruel/fierce) (d:lauhuai with plural te, after a noun: mi lauhuaite the cruel, ganhing lauhuaite fierce beasts) (e:tua lai-ah ganhing ~ kimu lo ding hi/mi ~’ khut kol pan nang kong tankhia ding | I will redeem you from the grasp of the cruel/tuihual ~ in tuam ta hi | the fearsome waves have covered her/tuilian ~, leh gamdang mite’ vangliatna panin | from the mighty waters and from the power of foreigners) (s:kihtakhuaite) (b:lauhuai) (r:23.35.9/24.15.21/24.51.42/19.144.7) (q:draft)
lauhuaizaw = (t:adj) (w:more dreadful/more terrible/more severe) (d:lauhuai dreadful, with zaw, more) (e:thukhenna ~ na thuak ding uh) (b:lauhuai) (r:40.23.14) (q:draft)
lauin = (t:v) (w:being afraid/fearing) (d:lau fear, with the connective suffix in) (e:Bang hangin ~ lungmang na hi) (s:kihtakin) (b:lau) (r:42.24.38) (q:draft)
laukawm = (t:adv) (w:fearfully/afraid/in fear) (d:lau fear with kawm while: being afraid and something else at the same time, as laukawm lingkawmin, fearing and trembling, and laukawm nuamkawmin, afraid yet glad) (e:~ lingkawmin hong pai-in/numeite zong ~, nuamkawmin | the women, afraid yet glad/thong sungah tai-in ~ lingkawmin | he ran into the prison, fearing and trembling) (r:41.5.33/40.28.8/44.16.29) (q:draft)
laukawmin = (t:adv) (w:in fear/fearfully) (d:laukawm while being afraid, with the connective suffix in) (e:Amah in zong ~ vantungmi en a) (b:laukawm) (r:44.10.4) (q:draft)
laulau = (t:v) (w:dread/keep fearing) (d:lau, fear, said twice; ka laulau is the very thing I fear) (e:ka ~ ka tuak ta hi) (s:kihtaktak) (r:18.3.25) (q:draft)
laulua = (t:v) (w:be very afraid/be terrified) (d:lau fear with lua, too much, exceedingly) (e:~ mahmah ka hih manin) (s:laugawp/kihtalua/naklau) (b:lau) (r:27.8.17) (q:draft)
laumai = (t:v) (w:look afraid/show fear) (d:lau, fear, with mai, face: of the face, show fear) (e:a mai put uh ~ ding uh hi) (r:26.27.35) (q:draft)
launa = (t:n) (w:fear/terror/dread) (d:lau, fear, with the noun suffix na: fear, dread or terror) (e:ka ~ khempeuh panin hong honkhia hi/~ in kei hong vukcip hi | horror has overwhelmed me/~ hong thuaksak nawn kei in | do not make me suffer terror any longer/Amaute pen ~ lianpi sungah om ding uh hi | they will be in great dread) (s:kihtakna/lauhuaina/patauhna) (a:lungmuanna/hanna) (b:lau) (r:19.34.4/19.55.5/18.13.21/19.14.5) (q:draft)
Launa = (t:n) (w:terror/fear) (d:launa, fear, written with a capital at the start of a sentence, and in the name Mun khempeuhah Launa, Terror on Every Side) (e:Mun khempeuhah ~ ci-in hong sam ta hi/~ tawh ka kidim a | I am filled with terror/~ om loin nuam takin na lum ding a | you will lie down in comfort without fear/~ in dantatna piangsak thei ahih ciangin | because fear brings punishment) (b:launa) (r:24.20.3/18.30.15/20.3.24/62.4.18) (q:draft)
launate = (t:n) (w:terrors/fears) (d:launa, fear, with the plural te; sih ding launate are the terrors of death) (e:sih ding ~ kei tung hong tung zo hi) (s:lauhuainate) (b:launa) (r:19.55.4) (q:draft)
laupa = (t:n) (w:one who fears) (d:lau fear with pa marking a man: the man who is afraid) (e:A ~ in itna sungah) (b:lau) (r:62.4.18) (q:draft)
laupih = (t:v) (w:be afraid of/fear) (d:lau, fear, with pih: be afraid on account of someone or something) (e:bang ~ ding ka hi hiam) (s:kihta) (b:lau) (r:19.27.1) (q:draft)
lausak = (t:v) (w:frighten/terrify/make afraid) (d:lau, fear, with the causative sak: make someone afraid) (e:na huihpi tawh amaute ~ in/bangmah in note hong ~ lo ding hi | nothing will make you afraid/a lauhuai maangmuhna tawh nong ~ hi | you terrify me with dreadful visions/Ama vangliatna in note hong ~ ding a | his majesty will terrify you/inn a lam lai ding uh ~ uh hi | they made them afraid to go on building) (s:patausak/dipkuasak/laugawpsak) (a:hehnem/hangsak) (b:lau) (r:19.83.15/24.17.17/3.26.6/18.7.14/18.13.11/15.4.4) (q:draft)
lausakgawp = (t:v) (w:terrify/frighten greatly) (d:lausak, frighten, with gawp, severely) (e:Topa in amaute ~ ding a/Gimna a tuamtuamte tawh Gog ka ~ ding hi | I will terrify Gog with every kind of affliction) (s:laugawpsak/lingsakgawp) (b:lausak) (r:36.2.11/26.38.21) (q:draft)
lausakin = (t:v) (w:frightening/terrifying) (d:lausak frighten with the linking ending in) (e:vantung ~ ka lingsak ding a/mi khempeuh ~ ka lingsakgawp ding hi | I will terrify everyone and make them tremble/a gam sung ~ gimsak hi | he terrified and afflicted its territory/sek tawi lite in ~ a lawnthal ding | the four craftsmen will terrify them and throw them down) (b:lausak) (r:23.13.13/38.1.21/26.30.13/9.5.6) (q:draft)
lausakzaw = (t:v) (w:terrify/frighten the more) (d:lausak make afraid, with zaw, more, rather) (e:mai-ah kong ~ lai ding hi) (b:lausak) (r:24.1.17) (q:draft)
lausakzo = (t:v) (w:be able to terrify/succeed in frightening) (d:lausak frighten, with zo, be able, manage to) (e:mite na ~ kha ding hi/midangte a ~ ngeite ahi uh hi | they were men who once terrorized others) (b:lausak) (r:23.47.12/26.32.26) (q:draft)
laute = (t:n) (w:those who fear) (d:lau fear with the plural te: the ones who are afraid) (e:gimthuak ding a ~ pen itna) (s:kihtate) (b:lau) (r:62.4.18) (q:draft)
lauthawng = (t:n) (w:fear/anxiety/apprehension/trepidation/nervousness/unease) (d:sudden fear or alarm; lauthawng kawmin is with fear) (e:~ kawmin na hehpih un) (s:launa/kihtakna) (r:65.1.23)
lauthawng = (t:v) (w:frighten/scare/panic/startle) (d:be struck with sudden fear or alarm, as in lungsim lauthawng mite, people whose hearts are fearful) (e:Lungsim ~ mite kiangah | to those with fearful hearts) (r:23.35.4)
lauthawngna = (t:n) (w:alarm) (d:lauthawng with the noun suffix na: sudden alarm or fright) (s:patauhna) (b:lauthawng) (r:19.31.22)
Lauthawngna = (t:n) (w:alarm) (d:lauthawngna written with a capital at the start of a sentence) (s:patauhna) (b:lauthawngna) (r:19.31.22) (q:draft)
lautheih = (t:v) (w:be able to fear/take warning) (d:lau fear with theih, can; with nadingin, so that they may fear) (e:upa dangte a ~ nadingin) (b:lau) (r:54.5.20) (q:draft)
lauzaw = (t:adj) (w:more afraid) (d:lau, afraid, with zaw, more) (e:bangzahin ~ ding i hi hiam) (b:lau) (r:9.23.3) (q:draft)
lawh = (t:v) (w:call/call on/name) (d:say a name aloud: call on the name of someone, or name a price; min lawh is to call on or mention a name) (e:a min ~ ding kipan uh hi/Hit mite’ zakna-ah a min ~ zah | the amount he had named in the hearing of the Hittites) (r:1.4.26/1.23.16)
