Lawkite = (t:n) (w:pagans/unbelievers/the ungodly) (d:lawkite written with a capital: pagans, people outside the faith, here as those asked to judge a dispute between believers) (e:~ a khensak ngam ding) (s:thu-umlote) (b:lawkite) (r:46.6.1) (q:draft)
lawm = (t:n) (w:friend/companion) (d:a friend or companion; lawm ngaih is a lover or beloved) (e:mihaute in ~ tampi nei hi/kumpipa’ ~ hong suaksak hi | it makes one the king’s friend/ka ~ theih mahmah, nangmah na hi hi | my close friend, it is you/~ gina lo tawh a kikhawl mi | one who keeps company with worthless friends) (s:lawmpa) (a:gal) (r:20.14.20/20.18.24/20.22.11/19.55.13/20.28.7) (q:draft)
lawma = (t:adv) (w:as a friend) (d:lawm friend with the ending a, as: take or win someone as a friend) (e:galte nangawn ~ kaihzawhna ahi hi/Blatas amau ~ a mat khit uh ciangin | after they had won Blastus as their friend) (b:lawm) (r:20.16.7/44.12.20) (q:draft)
lawmin = (t:n) (w:as a friend/as friends) (d:lawm friend, with the marker in, as) (e:note ama ~ a hong bawl) (b:lawm) (r:51.1.22) (q:draft)
lawmlawm = (t:adv) (w:so/to such a degree) (d:intensifier after a verb or descriptive word in a reproachful question: how can you be so) (e:hici hai ~ na hi uh hiam/A bangci ~ na hi hiam | how can you be like this/phawk thei lo ~ na hi uh hiam | how can you be so unable to understand/nungkin paisuak ~ uh ahi hiam | why do they keep turning away so) (r:48.3.3/26.16.30/40.16.11/24.8.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
