Lawmnu = (t:n) (w:bride/beloved) (d:lawmnu written with a capital: the bride of the Lamb, and the beloved woman in a section heading of the Song of Songs) (e:a ~ a kithawisa-in omkhin ahih manin) (b:lawmnu) (r:66.19.7/22.6.3) (q:draft)
lawmpa = (t:n) (w:friend/companion) (d:lawm with pa, a male friend) (e:Arkhi mi Hushai in kumpipa’ ~ ahi hi/ka ~ Abraham’ suan leh khak | descendants of Abraham my friend/I ~ Lazaras ihmu-in a om hi | our friend Lazarus is asleep/na ~ kiangah ka pia hi | I gave her to your companion) (s:lawm) (a:galpa) (b:lawm) (r:13.27.33/23.41.8/43.11.11/7.15.2) (q:draft)
Lawmpa = (t:n) (w:beloved/friend) (d:male friend, here the lover of the young woman; capitalised in a section heading) (e:Nungak in a ~ Phat) (b:lawmpa) (r:22.5.8) (q:draft)
lawmsam = (t:n) (w:one without a mate) (d:lawm companion, mate, with sam, lack: an animal that lacks its mate) (e:~ khat zong om lo ding) (r:23.34.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
