lawmte = (t:n) (w:friends/companions) (d:plural of lawm: friends, companions, the people one keeps company with) (e:ama ~ tawh a gilkial lai takin/Ka behte leh ka ~ bei ta hi | my relatives and my friends are gone/Nang leh na ~ tungah | to you and your friends/ka ~ na hi ding uh hi | you will be my friends) (s:lawmta) (a:galte) (b:lawm) (r:40.12.3/18.19.14/18.35.4/43.15.14) (q:draft)
lawmvakna = (t:n) (w:feast/banquet) (d:a meal to which guests are invited, mo la lawmvakna is a wedding feast) (e:ama innah ~ pawi a bawl hi/mo la ~ om a | there was a wedding feast/~ pawi ukpa kiangah paipih un | take it to the master of the banquet/Zeisu leh a nungzuite zong ~-ah a sam uh hi | Jesus and his disciples were also invited to the feast) (r:42.5.29/43.2.1/43.2.8/43.2.2) (q:draft)
lawn = (t:v) (w:throw/cast/hurl) (d:throw something or someone away from oneself, into or onto a place) (e:Buannawng sungah kei hong ~ a/amah in lei lakah ~ a | he threw it on the ground/sakol leh a tuangpa tuipi sungah ~ hi | horse and rider he has thrown into the sea/dum sung khatah ~ uh hi | they threw him into a cistern) (s:lot) (r:18.30.19/1.37.24/2.4.3/2.15.21) (q:draft)
lawn = (t:v) (w:touch) (d:form of lawng written with an apostrophe before ciangin and similar words) (e:a puan mongteep a ~’ ciangin/a khut a ~’ ciangin a nattun’ dam a | when he touched her hand the fever left her/mualte a ~’ ciangin tua mualte meikhu a suak | when he touches the mountains they smoke/mi khat in a ~’ ciangin | when anyone touches it) (s:lawng) (r:42.8.44/40.8.15/19.104.31/3.15.23) (q:draft)
lawng = (t:v) (w:touch) (d:put the hand or a part of the body on something or someone; before some endings it is written lawn) (e:zong na ~ kei ding uh hi/a khutin ~ a | he touched them with his hand/Ka sathau nilhte ~ kei un | do not touch my anointed ones/a sisa a ~ peuhmahte | all who touch their carcasses) (s:sukha) (r:1.3.3/40.17.7/13.16.22/3.11.24)
lawnga = (t:v) (w:touched) (d:lawng touch, with the connective a) (e:bang hangin Zeisu ~ thakhatin) (b:lawng) (r:42.8.47) (q:draft)
lawngin = (t:v) (w:touch) (d:lawng, touch, with the linking suffix -in, touching and then doing the next action) (e:a khut tawh ~ a damsak hi/vantungmi khat in amah ~ ama kiangah | an angel touched him and said to him/tua tawh Moses ~ | touching Moses with it/leitung ~ leitung in tuisuak a | he touches the earth and it melts) (b:lawng) (r:42.22.51/11.19.5/2.4.25/30.9.5) (q:draft)
lawngkha = (t:v) (w:touch) (d:lawng touch with kha, come into contact with, often without intending it) (e:Ka pa in kei hong ~ leh/A puan mong nangawn va ~ leng, dam ning | if I just touch his clothes I will be healed/hong ~ kei un | do not touch us/Tuate a sisa a ~ peuhmahte | whoever touches their carcasses) (s:lawnkhak) (r:1.27.12/41.5.28/25.4.15/3.11.27) (q:draft)
lawngpa = (t:n) (w:one who touches/he who touches) (d:lawng touch with pa, the man who, whoever touches) (e:pumpi a ~ ni sagih sung/a sisa a ~ pen | the one who touches its carcass) (b:lawng) (r:4.19.11/3.11.39) (q:draft)
lawngpi = (t:n) (w:beam/rod) (d:in siam lawngpi, the beam of a weaver's loom, a picture of a very thick spear shaft) (e:A teibul in siam ~ cia bang hi a/a teipi siamgante’ siam ~ cia a pha | whose spear was as thick as a weaver’s beam) (r:9.17.7/10.21.19) (q:draft)
lawngsak = (t:v) (w:let touch/make touch) (d:lawng touch with sak, cause or allow) (e:innpi a do khuampite hong ~ in/nangmah kong ~ kei hi | I did not let you touch her) (b:lawng) (r:7.16.26/1.20.6) (q:draft)
lawngsim = (t:v) (w:touch secretly/touch) (d:lawng touch with sim, secretly or quietly: touch without being noticed) (e:a puan mongteep a ~ hi/Jesuh’ puanmongteep ~ a | she quietly touched the edge of Jesus’ cloak) (r:40.9.20/42.8.44) (q:draft)
lawngte = (t:n) (w:the one who touched/those who touched) (d:lawng touch with the plural te) (e:amah a ~ a theih nadingin) (b:lawng) (r:41.5.32) (q:draft)
lawnin = (t:v) (w:throw/cast/hurl/toss) (d:lawn with the linking suffix -in, throwing and then doing the next action) (e:~ Filistiapa’ taltang kha hi/ka khut nihte’ sung panin ~ | throwing them out of my two hands/meikuang sungah ~ kangtum sak in | throw them into the fire and burn them up/suang ~ ai san uh a | they cast lots) (b:lawn) (r:9.17.49/5.9.17/26.5.4/40.27.35) (q:draft)
lawnkhak = (t:v) (w:touch/happen to touch/come in contact with) (d:lawn, form of lawng touch, with khak, happen to) (e:mu loin a ~ leh/a gamgi na ~ loh nadingun kidawm un | be careful that you do not touch its edge/Ama puanmongteep beek a ~ theih nadingun | so that they might just touch the edge of his cloak) (s:lawngkha) (r:3.5.3/40.14.36/2.19.12) (q:draft)
lawnkhia = (t:v) (w:throw out/cast away/hurl/cast off) (d:lawn, throw, with khia, out) (e:Tobiah’ van teng ka ~ hi/Teek hun ciangin keimah hong ~ kei in | do not cast me away when I am old/a puan ~ a | throwing off his cloak/khuapi sung panin kong ~ ding hi | I will drive you out of the city) (s:paaikhia) (b:lawn) (r:16.13.8/19.71.9/41.10.50/26.11.7) (q:draft)
lawnkhiamang = (t:v) (w:cast away/reject/throw away) (d:lawn throw with khia, out, and mang, away, lost) (e:hangin ka ~ pan ding hi) (r:24.31.37) (q:draft)
lawnkhiasuk = (t:v) (w:cast down/throw down) (d:lawnkhia throw out, with suk, downwards) (e:hehna tawh tua mite ~ in) (b:lawnkhia) (r:19.56.7) (q:draft)
lawnkhit = (t:v) (w:have touched) (d:lawn touch with khit, after, finished; with phetin, as soon as she had touched) (e:A va ~ phetin a siluang) (r:41.5.29) (q:draft)
