leengmasel = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:mint) (d:a garden herb of which a tenth was given; also written lengmasel) (e:~ leh anis leh meh namkim/~, anis leh, kummin | mint, dill and cumin) (s:lengmasel) (r:42.11.42/40.23.23) (q:draft)
leengpei = (t:n) (w:wheel) (d:wheel of a cart or chariot: leeng cart with pei wheel) (e:Tua kherubte gei-ah ~ khat ciat omin/~ gingte ka za a | I heard the sounds of the wheels/~ khat ciat a neih lam uh ka mu | I saw that each of them had a wheel) (s:pei/lengpei/peei) (r:26.10.9/26.3.13/26.1.15) (q:draft)
leengpeite = (t:n) (w:wheels) (d:leengpei wheel with the plural te) (e:Tua ~ a pianzia kibang kim a/tua ~ suangmanpha bangin tee hi | those wheels gleamed like a precious stone/a ~ in zong zui uh hi | their wheels also followed/a ~ leilak ah kinga hi | their wheels rested on the ground) (s:peite) (b:leengpei) (r:26.10.10/26.1.15/26.10.9/26.10.16) (q:draft)
leengpeizawlte = (t:n) (w:axles) (d:leengpei wheel with zawl, the bar on which it turns, and the plural te) (e:leengpeite leh ~ nei ciat hi) (r:11.7.30) (q:draft)
leengsuk = (t:v) (w:fly down/swoop down/fall) (d:leeng fly with suk, down) (e:ka omna munah a hong ~ hi/leitungah aksi khat a ~ ka mu hi | I saw a star that had fallen to the earth/a ~ a leengto phialphiah tawh kibang lel hi | is just like a swallow that flies down and up) (s:lengsuk) (a:leengto) (b:leeng) (r:27.9.21/20.26.2/66.9.1) (q:draft)
leengte = (t:n) (w:chariots/carts/carriages) (d:leeng, chariot or cart, with the plural te) (e:sakolte leh ~ man a/sakolte leh a ~ tawh Na-aman hong pai-in | Naaman came with his horses and chariots/Moses in ~ leh bawngtalte sangin | Moses took the carts and the oxen/amah puak nadinga a khak ~ a muh ciangin | when he saw the carts sent to carry him) (s:sakolleengte) (b:leeng) (r:11.20.21/4.7.6/12.5.9/1.45.27) (q:draft)
leengthei = (t:v) (w:be able to fly/fly) (d:leeng fly with thei, can: a leengthei vasate, the birds that fly) (e:a ~ vasate nangawn in mu thei lo/gul gu nei leh a ~ gulpi a omna | where poisonous snakes and flying serpents live) (s:leentheih) (b:leeng) (r:18.28.21/23.30.6) (q:draft)
leengto = (t:v) (w:fly up/soar/rise up) (d:leeng, fly, with to, upward) (e:muvanlai bangin kha tawh ~-in/leivui bangin van-ah ~ ding hi | it will fly up into the sky like dust/Tua ciangin hih kherub-te ~ uh a | then these cherubim rose up/a kha uh zalin leilak panin ~ uh a | they spread their wings and rose from the ground) (a:leengsuk) (b:leeng) (r:23.40.31/26.10.15/23.5.24/26.10.19) (q:draft)
leengtui = (t:n) (w:wine/new wine/grape juice) (d:juice pressed from grapes, tui water; leengtui suk is tread out wine) (e:an le ~ a hauh cianga/kuamah in ~ suk lo hi | no one presses out wine/leenggah cilna-ah ~ a sukkhia ding hi | he will press out the wine in the winepress) (s:leenggahtui/leenggahzu) (r:19.4.7/23.16.10/66.19.15) (q:draft)
leenin = (t:v) (w:flying/soaring) (d:leen fly, with the connective suffix in) (e:Muvanlai in sang ~ mualtungah) (s:leengin/lengin) (b:leen) (r:18.39.27) (q:draft)
leenkawmin = (t:adv) (w:while flying) (d:leen fly with kawm, while, and the connective suffix in) (e:muvanlai khat a ~ nakpi-in ham) (r:66.8.13) (q:draft)
leenkhia = (t:v) (w:carry away/sweep away/blow away) (d:leen fly with khia, out: of wind, carry something off through the air) (e:huih in ~-in om nawn lo ding/Nisuahna huihpi in amaute ~-in | the east wind carries them off/a inn panun gamlapi-ah ~ ding hi | it will sweep them far away from their home) (s:leenmang/mutkhia/mutmang) (b:leen) (r:23.19.7/18.27.21) (q:draft)
leenkhiamang = (t:v) (w:sweep away/carry off) (d:of wind, carry something away so that it is gone) (e:hehpih ngaihsut hetloin ~ ding hi) (s:leenmang/leenkhia) (r:18.27.22) (q:draft, low confidence)
leenkhiat = (t:v) (w:fly away) (d:leen fly with khiat, out, away; form used before theih and nading) (e:Moab mite a ~ theih nadingun) (b:leen) (r:24.48.9) (q:draft)
leenlak = (t:v) (w:swoop on/pounce on) (d:leen fly with lak take: come down on prey or an enemy as an eagle does) (e:muvanlai bangin ka gam a ~ dingin/a galte a ~ uh hi | they swoop on their enemies) (r:28.8.1/35.1.8) (q:draft)
leenmang = (t:v) (w:sweep away/blow away/be swept away) (d:leen, form of leeng fly, with mang, out of sight: of the wind carrying things off, and of what is carried off by it) (e:Huih in ~ khin ahih manin/Huihpi a nun’ ciangin migilote ~ a | when the storm blows, the wicked are swept away/deih theih peuhpeuh ~ ding hi | it will sweep away everything desirable) (s:leenkhia/mutmang/mutkhia) (r:27.2.35/20.10.25/28.13.15) (q:draft)
leenna = (t:n) (w:flying/flight) (d:leen fly with the noun suffix na) (e:amaute’ ~ a khaging uh ka za) (b:leen) (r:26.1.24) (q:draft)
leenpih = (t:v) (w:fly away with/carry off flying) (d:leen fly with pih, together with: take something along in flight) (e:Babylon gamah a ~ ding ahi uh hi/Koi lai-ah ~ ding ahi uh hiam | where are they flying off with it) (b:leen) (r:38.5.11/38.5.10) (q:draft)
leenpihin = (t:v) (w:carrying off in flight/lifting up and taking) (d:leenpih fly away with, with the connective suffix in) (e:Pasian’ kha in hong ~ Babylon gamah) (b:leenpih) (r:26.11.24) (q:draft)
leenpihto = (t:v) (w:fly up with/carry up) (d:leenpih fly away with, with to, upwards) (e:tua ciangpi a ~ uh hi) (b:leenpih) (r:38.5.9) (q:draft)
leensak = (t:v) (w:make fly/blow along) (d:leen fly with the causative sak: of wind, drive something through the air) (e:huih na hong ~ a) (s:lensak) (b:leen) (r:18.30.22) (q:draft)
leentheih = (t:v) (w:be able to fly) (d:leen fly with theih, can) (e:munah a ~ nadingin muvanlai) (s:leengthei) (b:leen) (r:66.12.14) (q:draft)
leentheihna = (t:n) (w:flight/ability to fly) (d:leen fly with theih, can, and the noun suffix na) (e:Vanah musane a ~ zia/leitaw lamah a ~ ding | its flying toward the south) (b:leentheih) (r:20.30.19/18.39.26) (q:draft)
leetkhiate = (t:n) (w:overflow/outflow) (d:what flows out of the harvest and the presses, given as an offering; apparently leet overflow with khia out and the plural te) (e:a ~ piak ding na zekai kei) (r:2.22.29) (q:draft, low confidence)
Legion = (t:name) (w:Legion) (d:name by which the many demons in a possessed man answered Jesus, taken from the Roman army unit of several thousand soldiers) (r:41.5.9/41.5.15/42.8.30)
leh = (t:conj) (w:and) (d:joins words and phrases; also written le) (e:vantung ~ leitung a piangsak hi/Edom, Moab ~ Ammon mite | Edom, Moab and the Ammonites/khuakhal ~ phalbi, sun ~ zan | summer and winter, day and night/Na molhtum ~ na ciangkhut | your rod and your staff) (s:le) (r:1.1.1/24.25.21/1.8.22/19.23.4)
leh = (t:ppm) (d:postpositional marker to indicate objective case) (e:Bang hang hiam cih ~/cih ~ Pasian in amah la hi | because God took him/cih ~ amah in mihing khempeuh’ nu ahi hi | because she is the mother of all people/cih ~ Pasian in ama’ lim bangin mi bawl | because God made man in his own image) (r:1.2.3/1.5.24/1.3.20/1.9.6)
leh = (t:conj) (w:if/when) (d:placed after the verb of a clause to make it a condition; bang hang hiam cih leh, literally if one asks why, means because) (e:khatpeuh in Kain a thah ~ tua pa tungah a zah sagihin kithuk ding hi/Na khut in hong puksak ~, na sattan in | if your hand makes you stumble, cut it off/A ta in khomun ngen ~ | if his child asks for bread/Kei nong it uh ~ | if you love me) (s:aleh/le) (r:41.9.43/1.4.15/40.7.9/43.14.15) (q:term added from the example, Genesis 4.15)
Lehab = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Lehabim/Lehabites) (d:a people descended from Egypt, the son of Ham, called the Lehabites) (r:1.10.13/13.1.11)
lehang = (t:conj) (w:if we) (d:conditional ending for the first person plural including the hearer, placed after the verb, if we or when we) (e:Tua bang silh ~ puan nei loin/zekai lo hi ~ | if we had not delayed/tu ~ eite i si veve ding hi | if we stay, we will die all the same/an lah la kei ~ | if we do not gather a harvest) (r:47.5.3/12.7.4/1.43.10/3.25.20) (q:draft)
lehbawlin = (t:v) (w:turning against/betraying) (d:leh, back or against, with bawl do and the linking ending in: act against someone who trusted one) (e:amah ~ a siasak ding uh hi) (s:lehheekin/lehhekin) (r:27.11.26) (q:draft)
lehbawlna = (t:n) (w:betrayal/treachery) (d:acting against someone, from leh against, bawl do and the noun suffix na) (e:hong ngawng kawina pen hong ~ ahi hi) (r:20.27.6) (q:draft)
lehbawlnate = (t:n) (w:acts of unfaithfulness/betrayals/treacheries) (e:kei hong ~ uh leh a mindainate uh) (s:lehheknate) (b:lehbawlna) (r:26.39.26) (q:draft)
lehbuk = (t:todo) (q:draft, appears to be leh, and, run together with buk, tent, in buk tual, courtyard; probably a misprint and not a word)
lehdelh = (t:v) (w:chase back/turn and pursue) (d:leh back, in return, with delh, chase: turn on those who were chasing) (e:hong kihei-in ~ kik uh hi) (r:6.8.20) (q:draft)
lehden = (t:v) (w:hit back/strike in return) (d:leh back with den, strike: of a stone, come back on the one who rolled it) (e:amau mah ~ kha zaw hi) (r:20.26.27) (q:draft, low confidence)
lehdo = (t:v) (w:rebel/revolt) (d:rebel against, the one opposed stands directly before the verb) (e:Moab gam in Israel ~ hi/kong theih ni-a kipan Topa na ~ uh hi | since the day I knew you, you have rebelled against the Lord/Moab kumpipa in Israel kumpipa ~ hi | the king of Moab rebelled against the king of Israel/gam lakah amah ~ zelzelin | rebelling against him again and again in the wilderness) (s:langpan/lehpan) (a:thumang/mang) (r:12.1.1/5.9.24/12.3.5/19.78.40) (q:draft)
lehdokha = (t:v) (w:rebel against) (d:lehdo rebel with kha, marking that the act reached its object) (e:hong ~ ka hih manun) (r:25.3.42) (q:draft)
lehdokik = (t:v) (w:rebel again) (d:lehdo rebel with kik, again) (e:tua minamte in ~ nawn loin) (b:lehdo) (r:26.17.14) (q:draft)
lehdona = (t:n) (w:rebellion/revolt) (d:lehdo rebel with the noun suffix na: the act of rising against a ruler or against God) (e:amau ~ hangin hailawh uh hi/Korah’ ~ bangin a kisia uh hi | they perish as in the rebellion of Korah/~ in aisan mawhna bangmah hi a | rebellion is just like the sin of divination/amaute in ~ lungsim vom uh a | they held to a rebellious mind) (s:langpanna) (b:lehdo) (r:19.107.17/19.106.43/65.1.11/9.15.23) (q:draft)
lehdote = (t:n) (w:rebels/the rebellious) (d:lehdo with plural te, those who rebel, often as mi lehdote) (e:mi ~ in langpan’ kei uh hen/Na uliante, mi ~ hi a | your rulers are rebels/mi ~ ahih leh keugaw gamah teeng uh hi | but the rebellious live in a parched land/Amah a ~ a cihna ahi hi | it means those who rebelled against him) (b:lehdo) (r:19.66.7/19.68.6/23.1.23/58.3.18) (q:draft)
lehdozaw = (t:v) (w:rebel more/rebel all the more) (d:lehdo rebel with zaw, more) (e:bangzah takin ~ lai ding) (b:lehdo) (r:5.31.27) (q:draft)
lehgamtat = (t:v) (w:act contrary/disobey) (d:leh opposite, against, with gamtat, behave: do the opposite of what was commanded) (e:Bang hangin ~ na hi uh hiam) (r:7.2.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
lehgen = (t:v) (w:speak against) (d:leh against with gen speak: answer good with words against someone) (e:amaute in kei hong ~ zawsop uh hi) (r:28.7.13) (q:draft)
lehhanthot = (t:v) (w:urge the contrary/encourage wrongly) (d:leh, contrary, with hanthot urge: encourage someone in the opposite of what is right) (e:na ~ zawsop uh hi) (r:26.13.22) (q:draft)
lehheek = (t:v) (w:betray) (d:hand over someone who trusts one to his enemies; also written lehhek) (e:kei hong ~ ding hi/note lakah khat in kei hong ~ ding hi | one of you will betray me/A ~ ding pa theikhol ahih ciangin | since he already knew the one who would betray him/Zeisu a ~ nadingin lungsim a guan’ khit ciangin | after putting it into his heart to betray Jesus) (s:lehhek/lehpei) (r:40.26.23/43.13.11/40.26.21/43.13.2) (q:draft)
lehheekin = (t:v) (w:betraying/dealing treacherously) (d:lehheek betray, with the connective suffix in) (e:A lehheekpa in ~) (s:lehhekin/lehbawlin) (b:lehheek) (r:23.21.2) (q:draft)
lehheekpa = (t:n) (w:betrayer/traitor) (d:lehheek with -pa, the man who betrays) (e:Kei hong ~ hong nai zo hi/Topa ~ Judas Iskariot | Judas Iscariot, the betrayer of the Lord/A ~ Judas in amaute tawh a ding khawm | Judas the betrayer stood together with them) (b:lehheek) (r:40.26.46/43.12.4/42.6.16/43.18.5) (q:draft)
lehhei = (t:v) (w:turn around/turn back/overturn) (d:turn someone or something about to face the other way; also overthrow the wise, twist the law; with sak, make out to be the opposite) (e:Nang hong ~-in, na khaguh ah sikkawi/a sakol kamkaih ~-in tai a | he turned the reins of his horse around and fled/Pasian’ thukham ~ uh hi | they twist the law of God/na lungsim uh na ~ kik leuleu uh a | you changed your minds back again/mi pilte ~ kikin | turning the wise back) (r:26.38.4/36.3.4/12.9.23/24.34.16/23.44.25) (q:draft)
lehheisak = (t:v) (w:turn against/prove perverse) (d:lehhei turn around, with the causative sak: of a man's own words, be turned against him) (e:keima kampau hong ~ ding hi) (b:lehhei) (r:18.9.20) (q:draft, low confidence)
lehhek = (t:v) (w:betray/deceive) (d:hand someone over treacherously or deal falsely with him; a lehhek pa is the betrayer) (e:amah a ~ pa in gimna thuak ding/napna tawh Mihing Tapa na ~ ding hiam | will you betray the Son of Man with a kiss/ka langte tungah kei a ~ dingin hong pai | come to betray me to my enemies/Kei hong ~ ding pa hong naita hi | the one who will betray me has come near) (s:lehheek/lehpei/hek) (r:42.22.22/20.14.25/42.22.48/13.12.17/40.26.46) (q:draft)
lehhekin = (t:v) (w:betraying) (d:lehhek betray, with the connective suffix in) (e:tua nasempa ~ na that leuleu) (s:lehheekin) (b:lehhek) (r:44.7.52) (q:draft)
lehheknate = (t:n) (w:betrayals/acts of treachery/backslidings) (d:lehhek betray with the noun suffix na and plural te) (e:kei hong ~ panin ka suaktasak ding hi) (s:lehbawlnate) (b:lehhek) (r:26.37.23) (q:draft)
Lehi = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Lehi) (d:place in Judah where Samson struck down the Philistines with the jawbone of a donkey) (r:7.15.9/7.15.19/7.15.14)
lehkaih = (t:v) (w:pull back/draw back/bring back) (d:leh back with kaih pull; often followed by kik, again) (e:a liim kal sawm ~ kik hi/sih nading mun a zuan mipa ~ kik in | pull back the man heading for the place of death) (r:12.20.11/20.24.11) (q:draft)
lehkhak = (t:v) (w:shut behind/close behind) (d:leh back with khak shut: close a door behind oneself) (e:mite kiangah pai-in kong ~ a) (r:1.19.6) (q:draft)
lehkiat = (t:v) (w:fall back into/fall in oneself) (d:leh back, in return, with kiat, fall: fall into the pit dug for another) (e:sung mahah ~ zawsop uh a) (r:20.26.27) (q:draft)
lehlamin = (t:adv) (w:upside down/the wrong way round/the opposite way) (d:leh, reverse, with lam, side, and the ending in: a lehlamin koih is turn upside down, a lehlamin hei is twist into its opposite) (e:na khempeuh a ~ na koih uh hi/Pasian’ hehpihna thupha a ~ hei-in | twisting the grace of God into its opposite) (r:23.29.16/65.1.4) (q:draft)
lehleh = (t:adv) (d:descriptive word after san, red: showing bright or glowing red) (e:hong san ~ hi) (r:22.4.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
lehmat = (t:v) (w:capture in turn/take captive in return) (d:leh back, in return, with mat, seize: make captives of former captors) (e:tu-in amaute in ~ ding uh) (r:23.14.2) (q:draft)
lehmut = (t:v) (w:blow against) (d:of wind, blow from the opposite side, be contrary; leh back and mut blow) (e:huih in amaute ~ ahih manin/a deih lohna uh lam panin huih in ~ | the wind blew against them from the side they did not want) (r:40.14.24/41.6.48) (q:draft)
lehna = (t:todo) (q:draft, appears to be leh, and, run together with na, your, in na pilna leh na theihnate; probably a misprint and not a word)
lehnawh = (t:v) (w:repulse/drive back) (d:leh back with nawh, push, drive) (e:galkap ukpa khat ~ zo ding) (s:lehnawt/notkik) (r:12.18.24) (q:draft)
lehnawhzo = (t:v) (w:be able to repulse/drive back) (d:lehnawh repulse with zo, be able, overcome) (e:galkap ukpa khat ~ ding na hi) (b:lehnawh) (r:12.18.24) (q:draft)
lehnawt = (t:v) (w:push back/drive back/push out) (d:leh back with nawt push) (e:note mai-ah amaute ~ ding a) (s:lehnawh/notkik) (r:6.23.5) (q:draft)
lehneih = (t:v) (w:subjugate in turn/possess in return) (d:leh back, in return, with neih, have: hold as slave the one who held others) (e:amah salin a ~ kik ding) (r:24.27.7) (q:draft)
lehngaihsut = (t:v) (w:think of on the contrary/regard wrongly instead) (d:leh opposite with ngaihsut, think: take something in the opposite way to what was meant) (e:kei hong ~ zawsop na hi) (r:47.11.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
lehngat = (t:v) (w:turn away/turn the back) (d:leh opposite with ngat, face; with san, turn away from, forsake) (e:Nang a hong ~ san mite) (s:nungngat) (r:24.17.13) (q:draft)
lehngatsan = (t:v) (w:turn away from/forsake) (d:lehngat turn away, with san, from, leaving behind) (e:Nang a hong ~ mite leivui) (s:taisan) (b:lehngat) (r:24.17.13) (q:draft)
lehpan = (t:v) (w:rebel against/oppose/disobey) (d:turn against a person or a command; usually written with an apostrophe before uh or hi) (e:Sangpen pa a ~ uh hi/Kumpipa ~’ na hi uh hiam | are you rebelling against the king/keima thu nong ~’ hi | you disobeyed my word) (s:langpan/lehdo) (a:thumang/mang) (r:19.78.17/16.2.19/4.27.14) (q:draft)
lehpei = (t:v) (w:betray) (d:turn against a master and hand him over) (e:kuateng in amah ~ ding cih thu/amah a ~ ding ahih manin | because he was going to betray him) (s:lehheek/lehhek) (r:43.6.64/43.6.71) (q:draft)
lehpiak = (t:v) (w:give in return/give back) (d:leh back, in return, with piak, give; with thupha, bless in return for a curse) (e:ciangin thupha ka ~ uh a) (r:46.4.12) (q:draft)
lehsawm = (t:v) (w:plot against/scheme against) (d:leh against with sawm, plan or intend) (e:amaute in kei hong ~ zawsop uh hi) (r:28.7.15) (q:draft)
lehsuak = (t:v) (w:turn out instead/become on the contrary) (d:leh opposite with suak, become) (e:keimah hong kikona ~ zawsop hi) (r:19.69.10) (q:draft)
lehsuh = (t:v) (w:plunder in turn/plunder back) (d:leh, in return, with suh, take by force: plunder those who once plundered) (e:nate hong ~ kik ding uh hi) (r:38.2.9) (q:draft)
lehsuksiat = (t:v) (w:destroy in turn/turn and destroy) (d:leh back, in return, with suksiat, destroy) (e:khut mah in kei hong ~ hi) (r:18.10.8) (q:draft)
lehtai = (t:v) (w:rebuke in return/rebuke) (d:leh back with tai, scold: answer a rebuke with a rebuke) (e:a nungzuite a etkawmin Peter ~ a) (r:41.8.33) (q:draft)
lehtai = (t:v) (w:run back/come running back) (d:leh back with tai run) (e:khat hong ~ kik a) (s:taikik) (r:42.17.15) (q:draft)
lehtatte = (t:n) (w:the faithless/the unbelieving) (d:those who have turned back from their faith, the unbelieving; the verse lists them between the cowardly and those who have gone astray) (e:a meidawite, a ~, a lampialte) (a:umte) (r:66.21.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
lehthuak = (t:v) (w:suffer in turn/suffer instead) (d:leh, in return, with thuak, suffer: suffer in the place of another the harm that was prepared for him) (e:migilote mah in ~ zawsop uh hi) (r:20.21.18) (q:draft)
lehthuk = (t:v) (w:repay/pay back) (d:leh, in return, with thuk, repay: pay someone back for what he has done; in the verse of repaying kindness with harm) (e:amaute in kote hong ~ zawsop uh hi) (s:thukkik) (r:14.20.11) (q:draft)
lehtuk = (t:v) (w:fall back on/come back upon/recoil on) (d:leh, back, with tuk, fall: of a plot or an insult, come back on the head of the one who made it; lehtuk sak is make it fall back) (e:amau lu tungah ~ sak in la/Haman’ lutung mah a ~ nading | so that it would come back on the head of Haman himself) (s:tukik) (r:16.4.4/17.9.25) (q:draft)
lehtukna = (t:n) (w:falling back upon/recoil) (d:lehtuk, fall back on, with the noun suffix na: the coming back of an evil plan on the one who made it) (e:lu tung mah a ~ ding) (b:lehtuk) (r:17.9.25) (q:draft)
lehtuksak = (t:v) (w:turn back on/make fall back upon) (d:lehtuk, fall back on, with the causative sak: make an insult or a plot come back on the one who made it) (e:amau’ lu tungah ~ inla) (b:lehtuk) (r:16.4.4) (q:draft)
lehzuih = (t:v) (w:go back along/return by) (d:leh, back, with zuih, follow: follow a road back again; ka lehzuih nawn loh ding lampi is the road by which I shall not return) (e:ka ~ nawn loh ding lampi) (r:18.16.22) (q:draft)
