lei = (t:n) (w:land) (d:the land or ground as opposed to water; lei keu is dry land) (e:~ keu kidawk hen/Tui om lohna ~ keu gamah | in a dry land without water/Mihing a om lohna mun ~ lakah | on land where no one lives) (s:leitang) (r:1.1.9/26.19.13/18.38.26)
lei = (t:n) (w:soil/ground/earth) (d:the earth or soil in which plants grow; lei sung is in the ground and lei lak is on the ground) (e:~ pan-a piang gah piakna/Kimkhatte ~ tam lohna suang lakah kia a | some fell among rocks where there was not much soil/~ sungah a zungte a teek zongin | though its roots grow old in the ground/~ lakah khuaizu om hi | there was honey on the ground) (s:leitang) (r:1.4.3/40.13.5/18.14.8/9.14.25)
Lei = (t:n) (w:ground/land/field) (d:lei written with a capital: in the name Si Lei, Field of Blood, and at the start of a line) (e:~ hamte a kinelsak ding hi/~ lak panin gimna hong piang tawm lo | hardship does not come up from the ground by itself/~ lakah lum dildel a | she lies on the ground/~ keu tunga pai bang keekin | as if walking on dry land) (b:lei) (r:42.3.5/40.27.8/18.5.6/30.5.2/58.11.29) (q:draft)
leiah = (t:adv) (w:on the ground) (d:lei, ground, with the place marker ah: on the ground) (e:a khutme tawh ~ lai a gelh hi/kun kikin a khutme tawh ~ a gelh hi | he stooped again and wrote on the ground with his finger) (b:lei) (r:43.8.6/43.8.8) (q:draft)
leiba = (t:n) (w:debt) (d:what a person owes to another; leiba loh is pay a debt, leiba maisak is cancel a debt, and leiba a nei is someone who is in debt) (e:a ~ khempeuh maisakin a khah hi/a ~ khempeuh a loh khit matengin | until he had paid all his debt/mizawngte’ tate ~ taangin la uh hi | they take the children of the poor for a debt/~ a nei mi khempeuh | all who were in debt/tua kumin ~ khempeuh i maisak ding hi | in that year we will cancel all debts) (s:batna/thangba) (r:40.18.27/20.22.26/40.18.30/18.24.9/9.22.2/16.10.31) (q:draft)
leibapa = (t:n) (w:debtor) (d:leiba, debt, with pa marking a man: the man who owes a debt) (e:a topa un ~ sam a) (b:leiba) (r:40.18.32) (q:draft)
leibate = (t:n) (w:debts) (d:leiba, debt, with the plural te; leibate loh is pay off the debts) (e:a sathau zuakin na ~ loh in) (s:batnate) (b:leiba) (r:12.4.7) (q:draft)
leibate = (t:n) (w:debtors/borrowers) (d:people who owe a debt, set against sumneite, those who have money to lend) (e:sum neite leh ~/~ kiangpan a laksak uh leenggahzu dawn uh | they drink wine taken from debtors/sumneite le ~, a hau a zawng | creditors and debtors, rich and poor) (s:bate) (a:sumneite) (b:leiba) (r:23.24.2/30.2.8) (q:draft)
leibatna = (t:n) (w:debt/owing) (d:the owing of a debt; a leibatna pa is his creditor, the man to whom he owes, and leibatna lai is the written record of a debt, a bill) (e:a ~ pa hong pai hi/Ama ~ pa in a neih khempeuh man hen | may his creditor seize all that he has/Na ~ lai va la in | go and take your bill) (s:batna/leiba) (r:12.4.1/19.109.11/42.16.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
leibatnate = (t:n) (w:creditors/debts) (d:leibatna owing of a debt, with the plural te; in the verse, those to whom one owes) (e:nang kong zuakna ka ~ koi pan) (s:batnate/sumneite) (b:leibatna) (r:23.50.1) (q:draft, low confidence)
leibeel = (t:n) (w:clay pot/earthen vessel/earthenware) (d:pot made of clay; lei earth with beel pot) (e:~ sungah a vasa khat go ding a/~ bang lel-in a kibawl hi | they are treated as mere clay pots/cimbeng kizut ~ tawh kibang hi | is like earthenware coated with dross/ka thahatna in ~ phel bangin keu a | my strength is dried up like a piece of broken pot) (s:leibel) (r:3.14.50/25.4.2/20.26.23/19.22.15) (q:draft)
leibeelte = (t:n) (w:clay pots/earthen vessels) (d:leibeel, clay pot, with the plural te: pots and other things made of clay) (e:lupnate, kuangte, leh ~, mangbuh) (b:leibeel) (r:10.17.28) (q:draft)
leibel = (t:n) (w:clay jar/earthen pot/earthenware) (d:pot made of clay, lei earth with bel pot; also written leibeel) (e:~ khat sungah koih in/cimbeng kizut ~ tawh kibang hi | is like earthenware coated with dross) (s:leibeel) (r:24.32.14/20.26.23) (q:draft)
leibuk = (t:n) (w:earthly tent) (d:lei, earth, with buk, tent or hut: the body as the dwelling in which a person lives on earth) (e:Kote omna ahi ~ in a siat leh) (r:47.5.1) (q:draft)
