leikikta = (t:v) (w:buy again/buy back) (d:leikik buy back, with ta marking a change of state) (e:mite in a ~ ding uh hi) (b:leikik) (r:24.32.15) (q:draft)
leilak = (t:n) (w:the ground) (d:the surface of the ground; leilak panin is from the ground) (e:~ pan-a leivui tawh mihing bawl a/Na sanggampa’ sisan, ~ panin keitungah hong kiko hi | your brother's blood cries out to me from the ground/migilote ~ den’na hi | he casts the wicked to the ground/a tuite luumsak dingin ~ ap hi | she leaves her eggs to the ground to be warmed) (r:1.2.7/1.4.10/19.147.6/18.39.14)
leilaka = (t:adj) (w:on the ground/of the ground) (d:leilak, the ground, with the ending a, of or at: describes what is or lives on the ground) (e:~ ganhingte in a ne ding uh hi/~ thangah vasa mawk awk ahi hiam | is a bird caught for nothing in a trap on the ground) (b:leilak) (r:24.16.4/30.3.5) (q:draft)
leilakah = (t:n) (w:the ground/on the ground) (d:leilak, the ground, with the place marker ah: on the ground or onto the ground) (e:~ mihonte a tut nadingin a sawl hi/puteekte in pau loin ~ tu uh a | the elders sit on the ground in silence/tui bangin ~ a si na buakhia ding uh | you shall pour its blood out on the ground like water/Vasa-kalaoh in ~ a tui nusia a | the ostrich leaves her eggs on the ground) (b:leilak) (r:40.15.35/25.2.10/5.15.23/18.39.14)
