leipa = (t:n) (w:buyer) (d:lei, buy, with pa marking a man: the man who buys, the opposite of zuakpa, the seller) (e:Van ~ in van zuakpa kiangah/a ~’ khut sungah om ding hi | it shall remain in the hand of its buyer/a ~ in khang tawntungin a neih dingin | for its buyer to own for all generations/amah a ~ tawh tuat ding a | he shall reckon with his buyer) (s:Vanleipa) (a:zuakpa) (r:20.20.14/3.25.30/3.25.28/3.25.50) (q:draft)
leipi = (t:n) (w:earth/the whole earth) (d:lei, earth, with pi, great: the whole earth, paired with vanpi, the heavens) (e:vanpi leh ~ liing damdam hi/Amau’ mai-ah ~ liing a | before them the earth shakes/vanpi leh ~, tuipi leh leitung ka lokgawp ding | I will shake the heavens and the earth, the sea and the dry land) (s:leitung) (a:vanpi) (b:lei) (r:29.3.16/37.2.6/29.2.10) (q:draft)
leisa = (t:adj) (w:bought/purchased) (d:that someone has bought, from the verb lei buy with sa marking a finished action) (e:Abraham in a ~ han sungah/a ~ lo pen Topa tungah a ap leh | if he dedicates to the Lord a field he has bought/nangma' ~ mite in a khen’ mateng | until the people you bought pass by/a ~ tuuno a nu khat nei hi | he had one little ewe lamb that he had bought) (a:zuaksa) (r:44.7.16/3.27.22/2.15.16/10.12.3) (q:draft)
leisak = (t:v) (w:buy for) (d:lei buy with sak, on behalf of: buy something for someone) (e:paknamtui nong ~ nai kei a) (r:23.43.24) (q:draft)
leiseek = (t:n) (w:brick) (d:block of moulded clay for building; leiseek bawl and leiseek seek are make bricks) (e:suang taangin ~ nei uh a/~ bawl nadingin mite' tungah buhtu | straw to the people for making bricks/buan leh ~ tawh a haksa nasepna | hard labor with mortar and brick/~ seekin lim takin hal ni | let us make bricks and bake them thoroughly) (s:leisek) (r:1.11.3/2.5.7/2.1.14) (q:draft)
Leiseek = (t:n) (w:brick) (d:leiseek, brick, written with a capital at the start of a sentence; Leiseek seek and Leiseek bawl are make bricks) (e:~ seek dingin buan cilin/~ bawl un | make bricks) (b:leiseek) (r:34.3.14/2.5.16) (q:draft)
leiseekna = (t:n) (w:brick-making) (d:leiseek brick with the noun suffix na; leiseekna kuang is the trough or mould in which bricks are made) (e:~ kuang a baihsa-in) (b:leiseek) (r:34.3.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
Leiseekte = (t:n) (w:bricks) (d:leiseek, brick, with the plural te, written with a capital at the start of a sentence) (e:~ kicim khin hi) (s:Leisekte) (b:Leiseek) (r:23.9.9) (q:draft)
leisek = (t:n) (w:brick/clay block) (d:block of moulded clay; also written leiseek; leisek sekna is brickmaking) (e:~ khat la-in na mai-ah koih in/~ sekna-ah amaute nasem sak hi | he made them work at brickmaking) (s:leiseek) (r:26.4.1/10.12.31) (q:draft)
Leisekte = (t:n) (w:bricks) (d:leisek, brick, with the plural te, written with a capital at the start of a sentence; another spelling of Leiseekte) (e:~ kicim khin hi) (s:Leiseekte) (r:23.9.9) (q:draft)
leisung = (t:n) (w:ground/depths of the earth/underground) (d:lei, earth, with sung, inside: the inside of the earth, under the ground; leisung panin is out of the ground) (e:tulkhat a ngah pa in ~ to-in/~ panin sikha’ aw bangin hong ging ding | it will sound from the ground like the voice of a ghost/Vantung sang lua-in ~ a thuk luat mah bangin | as the heavens are high and the earth is deep/~ panin a hong pusuak ganhing adang khat | another beast coming up out of the earth) (r:40.25.18/23.29.4/20.25.3/66.13.11) (q:draft)
leitam = (t:n) (w:sea bed/bottom of the deep) (d:with tuipi nuai, the ground under the sea) (e:Tuipi nuai ~ tungah lampai ngei) (r:18.38.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
leitang = (t:n) (w:surface) same as leitangtung
leitang = (t:n) (w:soil/ground) (d:the soil of a land, which is worked and bears crops) (e:~ a kho ding mi om lo/amau ~ pan-a a gah khempeuh | all the produce of their soil/na ~ un ama gah piangsak loin | your soil will not yield its crops) (s:lei) (r:1.2.5/1.4.12/19.105.35/3.26.20)
leitang = (t:n) (w:land) (d:a land or territory, and the land that a person owns or inherits) (e:na ~ hoih hi/~ in tampi piangsak a | the land produced plentifully/a tate in ~ nei ding uh hi | his children will possess the land/Thuman mi in ~ luah ding a | the righteous will inherit the land) (s:gam) (r:1.41.47/29.2.18/19.25.13/19.37.29)
leitanga = (t:n) (w:of the land/in the land) (d:leitang, land, with the ending a, of or in, placed before what is in or comes from the land) (e:tua ~ gah pawl khat/tua ~ gahte amaute lak uh hi | they showed them the fruit of that land/Na paina ~ a teng mite tawh thuciamna bawl | make a treaty with those who live in the land you go to/~ piangte na kaihkhop khit uh | after you have gathered the crops of the land) (b:leitang) (r:4.13.20/3.23.39/4.13.26/2.34.12) (q:draft)
leitangah = (t:n) (w:in the land/to the land) (d:leitang, land, with the place marker ah: in the land or to the land) (e:kong gen ding ~ teng in/Isaak in tua ~ khai tuh a | Isaac sowed seed in that land/Note kong piak ~ a teeng dingin | to live in the land I am giving you/Seir ~ a om a sanggampa Esau | his brother Esau who was in the land of Seir) (b:leitang) (r:1.26.2/1.21.34/1.26.12/4.15.2/1.32.3) (q:draft)
leitangte = (t:n) (w:lands) (d:leitang, land, with the plural te: lands, pieces of land) (e:tua ~ a hawm khit uh ciangin/hih ~ kong pia ding a | I will give these lands/Amaute in ~ amau min a puaksak hangun | though they named lands after themselves/ama neih ~ Pasian in samsia a | God curses the land that he owns) (s:gamte) (b:leitang) (r:6.19.49/1.26.3/19.49.11/18.24.18) (q:draft)
leitaw = (t:n) (c:direction) (w:south) (d:the south, the opposite of leilu, north; mostly in leitaw lam, the south side or southward) (e:biakbuk ~ lam pangah giahphual satin/inn ~ lamah kongkhakte om hi | there were doors on the south side of the building/nisuahna, nitumna, leilu, leh ~ lamah om uh hi | they were on the east, west, north and south/Entappuah mite’ ~ lamah gamgi pai hi | the boundary ran south of the people of En Tappuah) (s:khanglam) (a:leilu/saklam) (r:4.3.29/6.15.2/26.42.12/13.9.24/6.17.7) (q:draft)
Leitaw = (t:n) (c:direction) (w:south) (d:leitaw written with a capital at the start of a sentence or a line of verse, and for the south country) (e:~ lam gam en in la/~ lam-ah huih nungin | the wind blows to the south/~ lam ka zon’ hangin zong | even though I search the south/~ lam huihvot a nun’ lai takin | while the south wind is blowing) (a:Leilu) (b:leitaw) (r:26.20.46/18.23.9/21.1.6/18.37.17) (q:draft)
leitawi = (t:n) (w:loan/debt) (d:something taken or given on loan; leitawi pia is lend and leitawi la is borrow) (e:~ a late in a piate’ sila suak/~ na piakna mipa | the man to whom you make the loan/minam tampi tungah ~ na pia ding uh hi | you will lend to many nations/a meet-in sum ~ pia loin | not lending money at interest/Cingh gamtatin mi tungah ~ pia a | he is generous and lends to others) (s:leitawina) (r:20.22.7/5.24.11/5.15.6/3.25.37/19.112.5) (q:draft)
leitawi = (t:v) (w:borrow) (d:take something on loan, to be paid back later; said of what one does for another person it also means give on loan, lend) (e:Migilo in ~ a, lohkik zo lo hi/kuama’ aa lah ~ lo napi | though I have borrowed from no one/ama kisap zah na ~ ding uh hi | you shall lend him as much as he needs/a vengte tungah ~ a, a piaksate maisak ding | he shall cancel what he has lent to his neighbors) (r:19.37.21/24.15.10/5.15.8/5.15.2) (q:draft)
leitawina = (t:n) (w:borrowing/loan) (d:leitawi borrow, with the noun suffix na) (e:sum ~ hangin a puan kepsakte) (s:leitawi) (b:leitawi) (r:30.2.8) (q:draft)
leitawisak = (t:v) (w:lend) (d:leitawi, borrow, with the causative sak: let someone borrow, lend) (e:khomun pum thum hong ~ in/Midangte sum na ~ uh ciangin | when you lend money to others/lamen loin na ~ un | lend without hoping for anything/Ka sumte kuamah lah ~ loin | I have lent my money to no one) (a:leitawi) (b:leitawi) (r:42.11.6/42.6.35/42.6.34/24.15.10) (q:draft)
leitawite = (t:n) (w:those who borrow/borrowers) (d:leitawi borrow with the plural te) (e:A hong ~ na nungngat kei un) (b:leitawi) (r:40.5.42) (q:draft)
leitawm = (t:v) (w:buy some/buy a little) (d:lei buy with tawm, a little, some) (e:ding va ~ zaw un) (r:40.25.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
leite = (t:n) (w:buyers) (d:lei, buy, with plural -te: those who buy) (e:sunga sumzuakte leh sum ~ khempeuh hawlkhia/~ in Egypt gamah sal dingin a na zuaksawn | those who bought him sold him on as a slave into Egypt/a hong ~ i khem nuam hi | we want to cheat those who buy from us/van ~ le van zuakte | buyers of goods and sellers of goods) (s:sumleite/vanleite) (a:zuakte) (r:41.11.15/44.7.9/30.8.5/23.24.2) (q:draft)
leite = (t:n) (w:tongues) (d:lei, tongue, with plural -te) (e:amau ~ in namsau hiamte ahi hi) (s:leiite) (r:19.57.4) (q:draft)
leithuk = (t:n) (w:depths of the earth/deep ground/pit) (d:lei earth with thuk deep; leithuk sung is deep under the ground) (e:~ sung panin nang na pau ding a/~ sungah khauhual tawh kivei suk kivei to uh | deep in the earth they swing down and up on ropes) (r:23.29.4/18.28.4) (q:draft)
leitsek = (t:n) (w:brick/clay block) (d:spelling of leisek, block of moulded clay, which stands earlier in the same verse) (e:tua ~ tung git in) (s:leisek) (r:26.4.1) (q:draft)
leitung = (t:n) (w:earth/world) (d:the earth, the world and all who live in it; often paired with vantung, heaven) (e:Amah in ~ lokgawp a/Pasian in vantung leh ~ a piangsak hi | God created the heavens and the earth/~ buppi in kampau khat | the whole world had one language/~ pen ama bulpi tungah na phut hi | you set the earth on its foundations) (s:le/leipi) (a:vantung) (r:1.1.1/18.9.6/1.11.1/19.104.5)
Leitung = (t:n) (w:earth/world/land) (d:leitung written with a capital at the start of a line of verse, or as the name God gave to the dry ground) (e:Pasian in lei keu pen ~ ci a/~ in amah a thei kei hi | the world did not know him/~ khempeuh tawlnga-in gamdai takin om ta uh | all the lands are at rest and at peace/~ in an, leenggahzu, leh sathaute piangsak ding hi | the earth will produce grain, new wine and oil) (b:leitung) (r:1.1.10/58.1.10/43.1.10/23.14.7/28.2.22) (q:draft)
leitunga = (t:adv) (w:on earth/on the earth) (d:leitung with -a, the short form of ah; leitunga om means that is on the earth) (e:~ om mi khempeuh kong sam hi/~ i nuntaknate in niliim bang hi lel hi | our days on earth are only a shadow/~ om mi khempeuh sangin lungnem zaw hi | he was more humble than anyone on earth/~ thukhen Pasian khat om taktak hi | truly there is a God who judges on earth) (a:vantunga) (b:leitung) (r:20.8.4/36.1.2/18.8.9/4.12.3/19.58.11) (q:draft)
leitungah = (t:phrase) (w:on the land/on earth) (d:leitung, earth, with the place marker ah: on the earth, in the world) (e:~ guah zu hi/~ mihing a om cil-a kipanin | ever since mankind was first on the earth/Amah in ~ kialpi tungsakin | he brought famine on the land/A hehsa-in ~ na pai a | in wrath you strode through the earth) (a:vantungah) (b:leitung) (r:1.7.12/18.20.4/19.105.16/35.3.12)
Leitungah = (t:phrase) (w:into the world/on earth) (d:leitungah, on the earth or into the world, written with a capital at the start of a sentence) (e:~ hong pai ding Pasian’ Tapa/~ kei na hong sawl mah bangin | as you sent me into the world/~ tuiciin a tun’in | when the flood came on the earth/~ kam pawl tampi om a | there are many languages in the world) (b:leitungah) (r:43.11.27/43.17.18/1.7.6/46.14.10) (q:draft)
leitungbup = (t:n) (w:the whole world) (d:leitung, earth, with bup, whole: the whole world, all its lands and peoples) (e:~ galsim dingin thu pia un) (s:leitungteng) (r:24.51.27)
leitungbup = (t:n) (w:all the earth) (d:all the earth, meaning everyone who lives on it) (e:~’ pahtawi Babilon khuapi kila ta hi) (s:leitungteng) (r:24.51.41)
Leitungbup = (t:n) (w:the whole world/the whole earth) (d:leitungbup written with a capital at the start of a sentence) (e:~ galsim dingin thu pia un/~’ pahtawi Babilon khuapi kila ta hi | Babylon, the praise of the whole earth, has been taken) (s:leitungteng) (b:leitungbup) (r:24.51.27/24.51.41) (q:draft)
leitungmi = (t:n) (w:earthly man/person of this world/mortal/worldly person) (d:leitung, earth, with mi, person: a human being who belongs to this world, as against vantungmi, a heavenly one) (e:~’ lim i neih mah bangin/~’ pilna in Pasian mai-ah haina ahi hi | the wisdom of this world is foolishness before God/a si thei ~ ka hi hi | I am a mortal man of this world/~ khempeuhte in Pasian mai-ah mawhsakna a thuak ding | all the people of the world will be held guilty before God) (a:vantungmi) (b:leitung) (r:46.15.49/46.3.19/45.7.14/45.3.19) (q:draft)
leitungmite = (t:n) (w:people of the world/the world/earthly people) (d:plural of leitungmi: those who belong to this world; often simply the world, meaning its people) (e:~ in note hong muhdah uh leh/~’ mawhna ciamteh loin | not counting the sins of the people of the world/~ in amaute thu gen a ngai uh hi | the people of the world listen to what they say/a Tapa ~’ Gumpa a suah nadingin | his Son to be the Saviour of the world) (a:vantungmite) (b:leitungmi) (r:62.3.13/46.15.48/47.5.19/62.4.5/62.4.14) (q:draft)
leitungte = (t:n) (w:worlds/universe) (d:plural of leitung, earth, world; in the verse, the whole created universe) (e:~ in Pasian’ thupiakna tawh a piang) (b:leitung) (r:58.11.3) (q:draft)
leitungteng = (t:n) (w:the whole earth/all the earth) (d:leitung, earth, with teng, all of: the whole earth, every part of it) (e:Pai unla, ~ va en un/mi’ tenna ~, ganhingteng le vasate | the whole earth where people live, all the animals and the birds) (s:leitungbup/leipi) (b:leitung) (r:38.6.7/27.2.38) (q:draft)
leivang = (t:n) (w:hole in the ground/hole) (d:lei ground with vang, opening: a hole or hollow in the earth used as a hiding place) (e:a bukna uh ~ panin Hebru mite) (r:9.14.11) (q:draft)
leivui = (t:n) (w:dust) (d:fine dry earth; also the dust of the ground from which man was made and to which he returns) (e:mihingte, ~ suakkik ding hi/guallel-in ~ lakah ka om hi | laid low, I am in the dust/~ zahin ngun leh kham hau a | she has silver and gold as plentiful as dust/a sawt loin ~ suak pak ding hi | before long it will turn to dust) (r:18.34.15/1.2.7/18.16.15/38.9.3/18.20.11)
leivui = (t:n) (w:dirt) (d:loose earth picked up from the ground and thrown) (e:~ a theh lai takin David) (r:10.16.13)
Leivui = (t:n) (w:dust) (d:leivui written with a capital at the start of a sentence or a line of verse) (e:Kua in ~ banga a tam/~ panin kei nong bawlna phawkkik in | remember that you made me from dust/~ bangin amaute ka satvui a | I beat them as fine as dust/~ in nang hong phat ding ahi hiam | will the dust praise you/~ pen gulpi’ an hita ding a | dust will be the food of the serpent) (b:leivui) (r:4.23.10/18.10.9/10.22.43/19.30.9/23.65.25) (q:draft)
leivuineel = (t:n) (w:fine dust) (d:leivui, dust, with neel, fine: very fine dust that the wind carries off) (e:gal honpite ~ leeng bang ding uh) (r:23.29.5) (q:draft)
leivuite = (t:n) (w:dust) (d:plural form of leivui; English uses the singular) (e:a ~ sungah kham om hi/na khepeek nuai-a ~ na singkhia un | shake off the dust under your feet/na khe-a ~ liak ding uh hi | they will lick the dust at your feet/a ~ nangawn pammaih sa uh hi | they feel pity even for her dust) (b:leivui) (r:18.28.6/19.102.14/42.9.5/23.49.23) (q:draft)
leivuithem = (t:n) (w:speck of dust/refuse/scum) (d:leivui dust with them, a small bit; in the verse a picture of something worthless) (e:ninbulom le ~ bang bek ka hi) (r:46.4.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
leivumte = (t:n) (w:ridges/mounds of earth) (d:lei earth with vum, heaped up, and plural te: the raised ridges of a ploughed field) (e:~ zalh mai-in, guahtui tawh na nipsak a) (r:19.65.10) (q:draft)
leizang = (t:n) (w:flatland/plain) (d:lei, land, with zang, flat: a plain, a wide stretch of flat low land) (e:Moab ~ sunga a om/Jerikho ~-ah a phak uh ciangin | when they overtook him in the plains of Jericho/Arabah ~ lam a manawh uh hi | they headed toward the plain of the Arabah) (s:zanglei) (r:4.33.49/24.52.8/24.52.7)
leizang = (t:n) (w:level ground) (d:ground that is even, where the foot stands firm) (e:~ mun-ah ka ding hi) (r:19.26.12)
leizangah = (t:adv) (w:on the plains/in the plain) (d:leizang, plain, with the ending ah, at or in: on the plains) (e:Jordan kiang Moab ~ Topa in/Moab ~ giahphual sat uh hi | they camped on the plains of Moab/Jerikho ~ Zedekiah a pha uh hi | they overtook Zedekiah in the plains of Jericho/Moab ~ amaute tungah thu gen a | spoke to them on the plains of Moab) (b:leizang) (r:4.33.50/4.33.48/24.39.5/4.26.3) (q:draft)
leizawh = (t:v) (w:can be bought/be able to buy) (d:lei buy with zawh, be able; with hi lo, cannot be bought) (e:nate tawh zong ~ hi lo hi) (r:18.28.17) (q:draft)
leizo = (t:v) (w:be able to buy/can buy) (d:apparently lei buy with zo be able, in a proverb: only skin can buy skin; the NIV has skin for skin) (e:Vun bek in vun mah ~ bek) (r:18.2.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
leizum = (t:n) (w:cape/headland/point of land) (d:apparently lei land with zum pointed, a point of land running into the sea; the NIV names only Salmone) (e:Salmone ~ tawh a kitang takin) (s:leidawk) (r:44.27.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
lek = (t:v) (w:weigh enough/have weight) (d:of something put on a balance: be heavy enough to bring the scale down; lek lo and lek zo kei are too light, found wanting; also written leek) (e:tawikhaina-ah amaute in ~ lo uh hi/nang hong kitawikhai-in na ~ zo kei hi | you have been weighed and found too light) (s:leek) (r:19.62.9/27.5.27) (q:draft)
Lekah = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Lekah) (d:place in Judah whose founder was Er son of Shelah, named only in the genealogy of Judah) (r:13.4.21) (q:draft)
leklek = (t:adv) (w:skipping along/bounding) (d:placed after diang leap, of a flock of goats moving down a hill, skipping along, bounding again and again) (e:keelhon diang ~ bangin/Gilead mual tunga keelhon diang ~ bangin | like a flock of goats skipping down Mount Gilead) (r:22.6.5/22.4.1) (q:draft, low confidence)
lekuana = (t:num) (w:nineteenth) (d:second part of sawm lekuana, the nineteenth: le and, kua nine, with the ordinal ending na) (e:A sawm ~ Mallothi) (r:13.25.26) (q:draft)
lel = (t:adv) (w:only/merely/just) (d:placed after a verb or a noun phrase: nothing more than that; most often as hi lel, is merely, and bang hi lel ahi hiam, what is it after all) (e:niliim bang hi ~ hi/mihing’ ta bang hi ~ ahi hiam | what is a mere son of man/huihlakah a maimang suak ~ ding hi | it will just vanish into the air/thu pia ~ lecin zong | if you just give the word/leivui leh vut ahi ~ keimah in | I who am nothing but dust and ashes) (s:bek) (r:18.8.9/19.8.4/46.14.9/40.8.8/1.18.27) (q:draft)
lel = (t:v) (w:be defeated/be overcome/lose) (d:lose to an enemy or an opponent, the opposite of zo, win; gal lel is lose a war; the form lelh is used before some endings) (e:Gitlohna na ~ kei un/na galte uh na ~ ding uh hi | you will be defeated by your enemies/gal a ~ ding hi | he will be defeated in battle/gal ~ ding ihi ta hi | we are about to be defeated) (s:guallel/kizo) (a:zo/gualzo) (r:45.12.21/5.1.42/27.11.26/24.4.13) (q:draft)
lela = (t:adv) (w:brightly/radiantly) (d:placed after taang shine or taangsak make shine) (e:khuavak bangin taang ~ a/ama minthan’na in leitung taangsak ~ hi | his glory made the earth shine brightly) (r:20.13.9/26.43.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
lelh = (t:v) (w:be overcome/be no match for/fail) (d:form of lel: lose to someone, or be unable to manage a load or a duty) (e:Siria mite ka ~ tuak leh/Ammon mite nang na ~ tuak leh | if the Ammonites are too strong for you/khat vei awk kikin a ~ uh leh | if they are entangled again and overcome/Ahithofel’ thugen hoih in a ~ ding | that the good advice of Ahithophel would be defeated/keima tavuan ka ~ hetloh nading | that I may in no way fail in my duty) (s:guallelh) (a:gualzawh) (b:lel) (r:13.19.12/61.2.20/10.17.14/50.1.20) (q:draft)
lelhlam = (t:n) (w:defeat/being beaten) (d:lelh be overcome, with lam, the fact or state of: a lelhlam a kitheih ciangin is when he saw that he was beaten) (e:Moab kumpipa in a ~ a kitheih ciangin/Israel-te a ~ uh a kitheih uh ciangin | when they saw that they had been beaten by Israel) (r:12.3.26/13.19.16) (q:draft)
lelhna = (t:n) (w:defeat) (d:lelh, be overcome, with the noun suffix na: defeat; lelhna thuak is suffer defeat, be defeated) (e:~ na thuak ding uh hi/~ kikona aw ahi zongin hi lo | nor is it the cry of defeat/na mai uhah ~ thuak sak ding hi | he will make them suffer defeat before you/sihna mangpa in ~ a thuak ding hi | death will suffer defeat) (s:guallelhna) (a:zawhna/gualzawhna) (b:lelh) (r:3.26.17/2.32.18/5.28.7/46.15.26) (q:draft)
