lelhtaak = (t:v) (w:begin to lose to/begin to fall before) (d:lelh, be overcome, lose to someone, with taak; spelling of lelhtak; of the person before whom one has begun to fall) (e:Tu-a na ~ Mordekai in) (s:lelhtak) (r:17.6.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
lelhtak = (t:v) (w:begin to lose to/begin to fall before) (d:lelh, be overcome, lose to someone, with tak; of the person before whom one has begun to fall) (e:Tu-a na ~ Mordekai pen) (s:lelhtaak) (b:lelh) (r:17.6.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
lelhtuak = (t:v) (w:be overcome by/be no match for) (d:lelh, lose, with tuak, meet with: find an enemy too strong) (e:Syria mite ka ~ leh/Ammon mite nang na ~ leh | if the Ammonites are too strong for you) (r:13.19.12) (q:draft)
lelin = (t:adv) (w:merely/just/only) (d:lel with the adverbial suffix in; bang lelin means as no more than) (e:Mihingte bang ~ gamta na hi hiam/na kham neihte leivui bang ~ ngaihsunin | counting your gold as no more than dust/bawng bang ~ kote hong ngaihsun a | you regard us as mere cattle/kote’ aa tan bang ~ ngaihsun na hi hiam | do you count it as no longer than ours) (s:bekin) (b:lel) (r:18.10.4/18.22.24/18.18.3/18.10.5) (q:draft)
lellelte = (t:adj) (w:mere) (d:lel only, merely, doubled and with the plural te: mihing lellelte is those who are no more than human, mere mortals) (e:Mihing ~ in kei, bang hong cihzo ding/mihing tate ~ bang hangin kihta na hi uh hiam | why do you fear mere mortals) (s:lelte) (r:19.56.11/23.51.12) (q:draft)
lelna = (t:n) (w:being only/being merely) (d:lel, only or merely, with the noun-forming ending na, the fact of being merely so, as in mi ahih lelna, their being only human) (e:mihing na hih ~ kilang ding hi/Mi ahih ~ uh minamte theisak in | let the nations know that they are only human/vun ki-at ~ hang hi loin | not because of merely being circumcised) (b:lel) (r:26.28.9/19.9.20/45.4.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
lelsak = (t:v) (w:condemn/make lose/deny justice) (d:lel lose, with the causative sak: make someone lose his case before the judges) (e:a dikpa khahin a mawhpa ~ a/a thutang kimlai na ~ kei ding uh hi | do not make him lose his case when he is in the right) (s:mawhsak) (a:diksak) (b:lel) (r:5.25.1/2.23.6) (q:draft)
leltak = (t:adv) (w:merely/just/mere) (d:emphatic form of lel, only, often in questions that make little of something, bang hi leltak ahi hiam, what are they really) (e:tungah bang hi ~ ahi hiam/Amaute ~ banga simtham ding ahi hiam | are mere creatures like them worth counting/hih pasian-te bang hi ~ ahi hiam | what are these gods after all/no’ thu neuneute ~ na khentheih zawk | how much more can you judge mere small matters) (b:lel) (r:23.1.11/23.2.22/23.57.11/46.6.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
