len = (t:v) (w:hold/take hold of/grasp) (d:take or keep in the hand; also of a ring that holds a carrying pole, and of holding on to what is good or to God; kip takin len is hold firmly) (e:Zeisu in numeino’ khut ~ a/ahoih nate na ~ tawntung un | always hold on to what is good/Esau’ khetul ~ hi | he grasped the heel of Esau/biakna tau kite ~ hi | he took hold of the horns of the altar/Sabuai puak nading zawlte a ~ dingin | to hold the poles for carrying the table) (s:tawi) (a:khah/khahsuah) (r:42.8.54/52.5.21/1.25.26/11.1.50/2.37.14) (q:draft)
