lianin = (t:adj) (w:great/large/exalted) (d:lian with the linking ending in, used when another verb follows; a lianin kikoih means be exalted, lungsim lianin means with a proud heart) (e:Topa bek a ~ kikoih ding hi/Khuapi ~ zai a | the city was large and spacious/Nebukhadnezzar kumpi ~ koih a | he made Nebuchadnezzar a great king/amah a ~ kikoihin kilaam to ding a | he will be exalted and lifted up) (b:lian) (r:23.2.17/16.7.4/27.5.18/23.52.13) (q:draft)
liankik = (t:v) (w:grow big again/become great again) (d:lian great, big, with kik again) (e:A hiangte ~ nawn lo ding a) (b:lian) (r:26.19.14) (q:draft)
lianlian = (t:adv) (w:unfailingly/outright) (d:placed after a verb: without missing, every time; of archers who kill whenever they shoot) (e:a kap uh teh kaplum ~ uh a/Thal tawh a kap uh ciangin sisak ~ uh a | when they shoot with the bow they kill every time) (r:24.5.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
lianlua = (t:adj) (w:too great/very great/overwhelming) (d:lian great with lua, too much; of a burden, too heavy) (e:kei a dingin tavuan ~ hi/Ka lungsim dahna ~ mahmah ahih manin | because the sorrow of my heart is overwhelming/Ka thuakna uh ~ mahmah ahih manin | because our suffering was very great/kong tunsak ding siatna ~ ahih manin | because the disaster I will bring is so great) (b:lian) (r:4.11.14/41.14.34/47.1.8/24.19.3) (q:draft)
lianpa = (t:n) (w:great one/great man) (d:lian great with pa marking a male person; after a noun it means the great or the chief, as in kumpi lianpa the great king and siampi lianpa the high priest) (e:kumpi ~’ thu za un/Tuucing ~ ahi, i Topa Zeisu | our Lord Jesus, the great Shepherd/Kumpi ~’ khuapi | the city of the great King/mi ~’ inn, koi-ah om ta ahi hiam | where now is the house of the great man) (b:lian) (r:12.18.28/4.35.28/58.13.20/19.48.2/18.21.28) (q:draft)
Lianpa = (t:n) (w:great one/the great) (d:lianpa written with a capital in titles: Vang Lianpa the Great Power, Tuucing Lianpa the great Shepherd) (e:Ama sihna hangin Tuucing ~ suakin) (b:lianpa) (r:58.13.20/44.8.10) (q:draft)
lianpen = (t:adj) (w:greatest/most important/highest) (d:lian, great, with pen, most: the greatest, the highest in rank or the most important; siampi lianpen is the high priest) (e:Note lakah a ~ in, na nasem uh/a masapen leh a ~ thukham ahi hi | it is the first and greatest commandment/mual tunga biakna mun ~ ahi hi | it was the most important high place/a ~ in a neupen bangin om ta hen | let the greatest be like the least) (s:lianbel/golpen) (a:neupen) (b:lian) (r:40.23.11/40.22.38/11.3.4/42.22.26) (q:draft)
Lianpen = (t:adj) (w:Most High/greatest) (d:lian great with pen most, written with a capital in titles: A Lianpen Pasian, the Most High God, and Siampi Lianpen, the High Priest) (e:A ~ Pasian in kei tungah lim/A ~ Pasian’ Tapa kici ding hi | he will be called the Son of the Most High God/tua bang Siampi ~ khat a nei ihi hi | we have such a high priest) (s:Sangpen) (b:lianpen) (r:27.4.2/42.1.32/58.8.1) (q:draft)
lianpenin = (t:adv) (w:as the greatest/as the highest) (d:lianpen greatest with the ending in, used with verbs of making and thinking) (e:leitung kumpite lakah a ~ ka bawl ding/kua a ~ kingaihsun ding | who should be considered the greatest/Pasian in a ~ amah koih a | God set him in the highest place/amau’ khuapi a ~ ngaihsun uh hi | they thought their city the greatest) (s:sangpenin) (b:lianpen) (r:19.89.27/42.22.24/50.2.9/36.2.15) (q:draft)
lianpenpa = (t:n) (w:chief/highest) (d:lianpen greatest, with pa marking a man: the man highest in rank, placed after a title, as siampi lianpenpa, chief priest) (e:siampi ~ Seraiah tawh/Innsung mang ~ in amaute minthak phuah a | the chief official gave them new names) (b:lianpen) (r:24.52.24/27.1.7) (q:draft)
lianpente = (t:n) (w:greatest ones/chiefs/largest) (d:lianpen with plural te: the highest in rank or the biggest of their kind) (e:a galkap mang ~ khat/Tarshish teembaw ~ pawl in a honhonin pua uh hi | fleets of the largest ships of Tarshish carried them) (s:lianbelte) (b:lianpen) (r:27.11.5/26.27.25) (q:draft)
Lianpente = (t:adj) (w:highest/chief) (d:lianpen greatest with plural te; Siampi Lianpente are the high priests) (e:Jew Siampi ~ amau’ sisan ahi lo) (b:Lianpen) (r:58.9.25) (q:draft)
lianpi = (t:adj) (w:great/large/big) (d:lian with the strengthening ending pi; lam lianpi is a highway and awging lianpi a loud voice) (e:hauhna ~ a piangsak thei hi/suangtum ~ khat hualin | rolling a big stone/tulak-a dum ~ khat sungah amah paai uh-a | they threw him into a big pit in the forest/tuuhon ~, numei-nasem, kalaoh leh late nei hi | he owned large flocks, female servants, camels and donkeys) (s:lian/golpi) (b:lian) (r:54.6.6/5.27.14/40.27.60/10.18.17/1.30.43) (q:draft)
lianpipi = (t:adj) (w:great/very great/mighty) (d:lianpi great with the last part doubled, said of several great things or to stress the greatness; placed after the noun) (e:nalamdang ~ a bawl hi/mi tampi thatin gal ~ na sim hi | you have killed many and fought great wars/Tua ganhing nihna in nalamdang ~ bawl a | the second beast performed great signs) (b:lianpi) (r:44.19.11/13.22.8/66.13.13) (q:draft)
lianpipite = (t:adj) (w:very great/huge) (d:plural form of lianpipi, said of several very large things; inn lianpipite, great houses, stands for palaces and fortresses) (e:a inn ~ uh luh gawp ding uh hi/Gimna ~ hong tuaksak nangmah in | you who have made me see great troubles/inn ~ lam uh hi | they built great houses) (b:lianpipi) (r:30.3.11/19.71.20/28.8.14) (q:draft)
lianpite = (t:adj) (w:great/mighty/large) (d:lianpi with plural -te, used after a noun for several great things; na lianpite, great things) (e:eite’ adingin na ~ bawl khin ta/nasepna ~ kua in genkhia thei-in | who can tell the mighty acts/Suangtum ~ leihawm gong lik nelh un la | roll large stones to the mouth of the cave/Tua inn pen suang ~ tawh kilamin | that house is being built with large stones) (b:lianpi) (r:19.126.3/19.136.7/19.106.2/6.10.18/15.5.8) (q:draft)
liansa = (t:see) <liansa-in>
liansa-in = (t:v) (w:regarding as great/considering great) (d:lian great with sa, consider, feel to be, and the ending in) (e:Hih innte ~ thupi na sa mahmah) (r:41.13.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
liansak = (t:v) (w:make great/exalt/promote) (d:lian great with the causative sak) (e:na huhna in kei hong ~ hi/leitang luah dingin nang hong ~ ding hi | he will exalt you to inherit the land/Topa in Joshua ~ hi | the Lord exalted Joshua/Amah in minamte thahatsakin ~ a | he makes nations strong and great) (s:liatsak/pahtawi/sangsak) (a:niamsak/neusak) (b:lian) (r:10.22.36/19.37.34/6.4.14/18.12.23) (q:draft)
liansakin = (t:v) (w:making great/exalting/raising up) (d:liansak, make great, with the linking ending in) (e:Mite lak panin nang hong ~/Topa in a thukham ~ vanglian sak nuam hi | the Lord was pleased to make his law great and glorious) (b:liansak) (r:11.14.7/23.42.21) (q:draft)
liansakpa = (t:n) (w:one who makes great/one who makes grow) (d:liansak make great with pa, the male one who does it; in the verse, he who makes the low tree grow tall) (e:singkung neute a ~) (b:liansak) (r:26.17.24) (q:draft)
liansakzo = (t:v) (w:have exalted/have made great) (d:liansak make great, exalt, with zo marking a completed action) (e:mi khat ka ~ hi) (b:liansak) (r:19.89.19) (q:draft)
liante = (t:adj) (w:great/chief/large) (d:form of lian after a plural noun; siampi liante is the chief priests) (e:Pilat in siampi ~, upate leh mite sam a/inn ~ kisatzanin, inn neute kisatnen ding hi | the great houses will be smashed and the small houses broken to bits/no gunpi ~ leh tuipi thuk khempeuh | you great sea creatures and all ocean depths/siampi ~ leh upate’n a sawl mi honpite | a crowd sent by the chief priests and elders) (a:neute) (b:lian) (r:42.23.13/44.19.11/30.6.11/19.148.7/40.26.47) (q:draft)
lianzaw = (t:adj) (w:larger) (d:lian, big, with zaw, more: bigger in size or number) (e:note sangin ~-in a thahat zaw minamte/amau’ gam in note’ gam sangin ~ ahi hiam | is their land larger than your land) (s:golzaw) (a:neuzaw) (b:lian) (r:5.11.23/30.6.2)
lianzaw = (t:adj) (w:greater) (d:lian, great, with zaw, more: greater in power, rank or worth; what it is compared with takes sangin, than) (e:Pasian biakna inn sangin a ~ khat/Pasian pen mihing sangin ~ hi | God is greater than man/itna ~ kuamah in a nei kei hi | no one has greater love/Nasempa in a topa sangin ~ lo hi | a servant is not greater than his master) (s:thupizaw) (a:neuzaw) (b:lian) (r:40.12.6/1.1.16/18.33.12/43.15.13/40.10.24)
lianzawin = (t:adv) (w:greater/higher) (d:lianzaw greater with the ending in: as greater, in a higher place than others) (e:khempeuh sangin a ~ amah a koihna) (b:lianzaw) (r:17.5.11) (q:draft)
lianzawsak = (t:v) (w:make greater) (d:lianzaw greater with the causative sak) (e:ama tokhom ~ hen) (b:lianzaw) (r:11.1.37) (q:draft)
lianzawte = (t:n) (w:greater ones/those who are greater) (d:lianzaw greater with te, those who) (e:A ~ in a neuzawte thupha/amau sang a ~ tawh a kiciam thei uh hi | they swear by those greater than themselves) (s:golzawte) (a:neuzawte) (b:lianzaw) (r:58.7.7/58.6.16) (q:draft)
liat = (t:v) (w:be great/be big/become great) (d:form of lian great, big, used before hangin, ciangin, nading and na; migilote a liat ciangin, when the wicked rise to power) (e:migilote a ~ ciangin/ama ~ mahmahna tawh kituakin amah phat un | praise him according to his surpassing greatness/a pumpi a ~ hangin | though his body has grown big) (r:20.28.12/19.150.2/18.15.27) (q:draft)
liatluat = (t:v) (w:be very great/be too great) (d:liat be great with luat too much, the forms used before hang and hangin: so great, so much) (e:na mawhna a ~ hang ahi hi) (r:24.13.22/24.4.30) (q:draft)
liatluatna = (t:n) (w:greatness/great extent) (d:liatluat be very great with the noun suffix na; na mawhna a liatluatna, the greatness of your sin) (e:na mawhna a ~ hang ahi hi) (b:liatluat) (r:24.13.22) (q:draft)
liatna = (t:n) (w:great/greatness/majesty) (d:liat, be great, with the noun suffix na: greatness or majesty; also the great extent of something, as of wickedness) (e:Pasian a ~ gen un/ama ~ ngaihsut zawh ding hi lo hi | his greatness no one can fathom/Pasian’ ~ a kicingin i thei zo kei a | we cannot fully know the greatness of God/na minthan’na leh na ~ tawh | with your splendor and majesty) (s:thupina) (a:neuna) (b:liat) (r:5.32.3/1.6.5/19.145.3/18.36.26/19.45.3)
liatnate = (t:n) (w:majesty/greatness/splendor) (d:liatna greatness, with the plural te) (e:Pahtawina leh ~ ama mai-ah om a/le min ~ nangma a’ ahi hi | and majesty are yours) (b:liatna) (r:19.96.6/13.29.11) (q:draft)
liatnateng = (t:v) (w:glory and honour) (d:liatna, greatness, with teng, all: all the greatness or splendour of something) (e:hauhna le ~ tua khuapisung hong kitunpih ding hi) (b:liatna) (r:66.21.26)
liatsak = (t:v) (w:exalt/make great/magnify) (d:liat, be great, with the causative sak: make someone great or honoured) (e:nang ~ ding ka kipan ding hi/~ nading leh thakhauhsak nading | to make great and to give strength) (s:liansak/sangsak) (a:niamsak/neusak) (b:liat) (r:6.3.7/13.29.12) (q:draft)
liatsakna = (t:n) (w:exaltation/making great) (d:liatsak, make great, with the noun suffix na: the act of making someone or something great) (e:ama kumpigam a ~ kiphawktel hi/~ ding le thakhauhsakna ding | to make great and to make strong) (b:liatsak) (r:10.5.12/13.29.12) (q:draft)
liattheih = (t:v) (w:be able to increase/be able to become great) (d:liat be great with theih be able, used before nadingin: so that it may become great) (e:Pasian’ hehpihna a ~ nadingin) (b:liat) (r:45.6.1) (q:draft)
liatzawk = (t:v) (w:be greater/be superior) (d:form of lianzaw, greater, used before mah bangin) (e:a piak min a ~ mah bangin) (r:58.1.4) (q:draft)
liatzawkna = (t:n) (w:being greater/superiority) (d:liatzawk, be greater, with the noun suffix na: the fact that one is greater than others) (e:pasian dang khempeuh sangin a ~/na thu a ~ na lak hi | you have shown that your word is greater) (b:liatzawk) (r:2.18.11/19.138.2) (q:draft)
liau = (t:v) (w:pay/pay a fine) (d:pay what is owed or imposed, such as a fine, a debt or a tax) (e:ngun talen khat na ~ ding hi/amah in thukhente’ khenna bangin ~ ding hi | he shall pay as the judges decide/Na ~ ding dangkasan na piak khit matengin | until you have paid the coin you owe/biakna innpi siah hamu ~ lo ahi hiam | does he not pay the temple tax) (r:11.20.39/40.17.24/2.21.22/42.12.59) (q:draft)
liausak = (t:v) (w:fine/make pay) (d:liau pay with the causative sak: make someone pay a sum as a penalty) (e:ngun shekel zakhat ~ ding uh a) (b:liau) (r:5.22.19) (q:draft)
liausum = (t:n) (w:fine/money owed) (d:liau pay with sum money: the money one has to pay; the NIV has the last penny) (e:na ~ uh na piak khit matengun) (r:42.12.59) (q:draft)
