Libnah = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Libnah) (d:name of two places: a camping place of Israel in the wilderness, and a town in the lowland of Judah taken by Joshua and given to the priests) (r:4.33.20/6.15.42)
Libnath = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Libnah) (d:camping place of Israel in the wilderness between Rimmon Perez and Rissah, spelled Libnah in the NIV) (e:~ panin amaute ding khia uh a) (r:4.33.21) (q:draft)
Libni = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Libni) (d:name of two Levites: a son of Gershon, and a descendant of Merari) (r:4.3.18)
Libya = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Libya) (d:land in North Africa west of Egypt) (r:44.2.10/34.3.9)
Licia = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Lycia) (d:region on the south coast of Asia Minor, where Paul landed at Myra on the voyage to Rome) (r:44.27.5)
Lidda = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Lydda) (d:town near Joppa where Peter healed Aeneas) (r:44.9.35/44.9.32)
Lidia = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Lydia) (d:seller of purple cloth from Thyatira, who became a believer at Philippi and received Paul in her house) (r:44.16.14/44.16.40)
lihleh = (t:adv) (d:descriptive word after a verb of colour or blooming, brightly, in full glow, san lihleh is glowing red, palh lihleh is in full bloom) (e:na kho hong san ~ hi/a palh ~ paak hoihte tawh kibang hi | he is like fine flowers in full bloom) (r:22.6.7/22.1.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
lii = (t:num) (w:four) (d:longer spelling of li) (e:gun hong kikhenin ~ hong pha hi) (s:li) (r:1.2.10) (q:draft)
liik = (t:v) (w:lift/raise/move) (d:lift or move a hand, foot, tool or weapon; khut liik is raise the hand, often against someone) (e:ka khut ka ~ khin hi/a khe nangawn uh ~ lo ding uh hi | they shall not lift even a foot/a ciangkhut uh hong ~ ciangin | when they lift their club against you/kumpipa’ lang khatah a khut a ~ mite | those who raised their hand against the king) (s:domto) (r:26.16.27/1.41.44/23.10.24/10.18.28) (q:draft)
liik = (t:n) (d:in kha-liik, a phase of the moon; the verse sets kha-det and kha-liik where the English has new moon and full moon, so probably the full moon) (e:Kha-det, kha-~, i pawi ni-in) (r:19.81.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
liikto = (t:v) (w:lift up/raise/wield) (d:liik lift with to, up: raise a tool or weapon to use it) (e:ciangkhut-in a ~ ding bang keek-in/Amah a ~-pa pen molhtum-in a zang ding | as if the club would use the one who lifts it) (s:likto/domto) (b:liik) (r:23.10.15) (q:draft)
liim = (t:n) (w:shadow/shade) (d:the shadow cast by something, or the shade and protection it gives) (e:Vanglianpa’ ~ sungah a om mi in/nitak lam-a ~ om tawh kibang a | is like the evening shadow/Ama ~-ah ka tu nuam a | I love to sit in his shade/Sihna ~ gam sungah a tute | those who sit in the land of the shadow of death) (r:19.91.1/19.102.11/22.2.3/40.4.16) (q:draft)
liimah = (t:adv) (w:in the shadow/in the shade) (d:liim, shadow, with -ah, in or at; inn liimah is at the porch or gateway of a house) (e:na kha ~ kong bu ding hi/Mihing tate na kha ~ bu uh hi | people take refuge in the shadow of your wings/na kha ~ hong seel in | hide me in the shadow of your wings/Piter inn ~ a paikhiat khit ciangin | after Peter went out to the gateway) (s:limah) (b:liim) (r:19.57.1/40.26.71/19.36.7/19.17.8) (q:draft)
liimnuai = (t:n) (w:shade/shelter) (d:liim shade and nuai under, the place under the shade of something, used of protection) (e:a ~ belhin a nei uh hi/Ama ~ a belte khempeuh | all who sheltered in its shade/a ~ beel dinga na paina | under whose shelter you have come to take refuge) (s:limnuai) (r:26.31.6/8.2.12/26.31.17) (q:draft)
liimsun = (t:v) (w:overshadow/shade/cover) (d:throw a shadow over something, liim is shade) (e:hehpihna tokhom ~ uh hi/Ama liim in mual liante hoihtakin ~ a | its shade covered the great mountains well/amau’ khate tawh hehpihna tokhom ~ uh a | they overshadowed the atonement cover with their wings) (r:58.9.5/19.80.10/2.37.9) (q:draft)
liimsun = (t:n) (w:overhang/canopy) (d:a covering that gives shade over an entrance) (e:singpeek tawh ~ khat kibawl hi) (r:26.41.25) (q:draft)
liimsunin = (t:v) (w:overshadowing/shading) (d:liimsun overshadow with the ending in) (e:khate tawh hehpihna tokhom ~) (b:liimsun) (r:2.25.20) (q:draft)
liimte = (t:n) (w:shadows) (d:liim, shadow, with the plural te) (e:Mual ~ mi bangin a mu na hi hi/i ~ sau keei ta hi | our shadows are growing long) (b:liim) (r:7.9.36/24.6.4) (q:draft)
liin = (t:v) (w:tremble/shake) (d:written liin’ before na; liin’na is trembling, often paired with launa fear) (e:Launa leh ~’na ka tung hong tung a/ka pumpi ~’na in kei hong lausak hi | the trembling of my body frightened me/Moab makaite, ~’na in mancip hi | trembling seized the leaders of Moab/Midian gam mite a ~’na uh ka mu hi | I saw the trembling of the people of Midian) (s:liing/lin) (r:19.55.5/18.4.14/2.15.15/35.3.7) (q:draft)
liing = (t:v) (w:tremble/shake/quake) (d:shake or tremble, of the earth in an earthquake or of people in fear) (e:na mai-ah mualte a ~ hi/leitung in mu-in a ~ hi | the earth sees and trembles/thong innbul zong ~ a | the foundations of the prison also shook/za khin uh a, amaute ~ uh hi | they have heard, and they tremble) (s:liin/lin) (r:23.64.3/19.97.4/44.16.26/2.15.14) (q:draft)
liinga = (t:v) (w:shake/quake) (d:liing tremble, quake, with the linking a, and) (e:Ziin ~ suangpite zong a kitam hi) (b:liing) (r:40.27.51) (q:draft)
liingcipin = (t:v) (w:trembling/shaking) (d:liing tremble with cip, completely, and the ending in: of hands shaking with fear; the NIV has go limp) (e:launa hangin a khut uh ~) (s:lingcipin) (r:26.21.7) (q:draft)
liinggawp = (t:v) (w:tremble violently/shake with fear) (d:liing tremble with gawp, severely) (e:amaute ~ uh hi) (s:linggawp) (b:liing) (r:19.48.6) (q:draft)
liingin = (t:v) (w:trembling/shaking/quaking) (d:liing with -in, linking it to the next verb: trembling, with trembling) (e:a phual kip panun ~ hong paikhia uh hi/thanemin, lau-in, ~ ka om hi | I was weak, afraid and trembling/leitang ~ kising hi | the earth trembled and quaked/~ hong pai a, Zeisu mai-ah bokin | she came trembling and fell down before Jesus) (s:lingin) (b:liing) (r:10.22.46/46.2.3/19.77.18/42.8.47) (q:draft)
