lohte = (t:part) (d:negative loh with the plural te, after a verb: those that are not, the things not done or not approved; hoih sak lohte is things not found good, evil) (e:Pasian’ hoih sak ~ hong sem hi/na phawk nawn ~ tawh ka kibang hi | I am like those you remember no more/hoih ka sak ~ a bawl teitei leh | if it keeps doing what I do not find good/na nek ~ nangawn uh na tuancil gawp uh hi | you even trample what you do not eat) (b:loh) (r:24.52.2/5.13.13/19.88.5/24.18.10/26.34.18) (q:draft)
lohteng = (t:part) (d:loh, not, with teng, all, after a verb: all that one does not do, whatever is not; na dawn lohteng is all that you do not drink) (e:Ka hih nop ~ ka hih veve ciangin/Ka gamtat nop ~ ka gamtat veve ciangin | when I still do what I do not want to do/na dawn ~ uh na siknin uh hi | you muddy all that you do not drink) (b:loh) (r:45.7.16/26.34.18/45.7.20) (q:draft)
lohun = (t:part) (d:the negative loh with the ending un used for a plural subject: without your doing; na teltheih lohun, in a way that you cannot understand) (e:na teltheih ~ a pau bualbual) (b:loh) (r:23.33.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
