luankik = (t:v) (w:flow back) (d:luan flow with kik back, again) (e:tui hong ~ theih nadingin) (s:luangkik) (b:luan) (r:2.14.26) (q:draft)
luanna = (t:n) (w:flowing/flow/shedding) (d:luan, flow, with the noun suffix na: the flowing of tears or blood, and the place where something flows, as in bawngnawi le khuaizu a luanna gam, the land flowing with milk and honey) (e:ka khitui ~ hong mu-in/Bawngnawi leh khuaizu a ~ leitangah paito un | go up to the land flowing with milk and honey/ama sisan ~ in ama khialhna hang ahi hi | the shedding of his blood is his own fault/ama si ~ panin tua nu a siang hi | she is clean from her flow of blood/ahih hangin sisan ~ om hi | but there was bloodshed) (b:luan) (r:18.16.20/2.33.3/26.33.5/3.12.7/23.5.7) (q:draft)
luannate = (t:n) (w:flowing/shedding) (d:luanna, flowing, with the plural te; khitui luannate is the tears a person has shed) (e:Na khitui ~ phawk ka hih manin) (b:luanna) (r:55.1.4) (q:draft)
luantheihna = (t:n) (w:being able to flow) (d:luan flow with theih can and the noun suffix na; with ding, so that it may flow) (e:i khitui a ~ ding) (r:24.9.18) (q:draft)
luat = (t:adv) (w:too/too much/so very) (d:form of lua used before leh, manin, mah bangin and aw) (e:Gilkial ~ manin cisa-in ka nattun uh a/Siria mite kei adingin a hat ~ leh | if the Arameans are too strong for me/ganno khat’ adingin innkuan a tawm ~ leh | if the household is too small for one lamb/ka gim ~ manin ka phun ding hi | because I am so distressed I will complain/lei sung a thuk ~ mah bangin | just as the earth is so deep) (b:lua) (r:25.5.10/10.10.11/2.12.4/18.7.11/20.25.3) (q:draft)
luata = (t:adv) (w:too/too much) (d:lua too, with ta marking a state that has now been reached) (e:pasal nei dingin ka teek ~ hi/a khut uh zaw ~ ahih manin | because their hands are too weak) (b:lua) (r:8.1.12/24.47.3) (q:draft)
luate = (t:n) (d:lua, too or very, with plural -te; after a descriptive word it means those that are too much so, as in a hat luate, those who are too strong, and a tom luate, those that are too short) (e:ama adinga a hat ~ kiang panin/a lian lua leh a lamdang ~ | things too great and too wonderful/a saulua ahih kei leh a tom ~ | those that are too long or too short) (b:lua) (r:19.35.10/3.22.23/19.131.1) (q:draft, low confidence)
luatna = (t:n) (w:excess/great intensity/zeal) (d:noun of luat, too much; after a feeling or action it names the great degree of it, as heh luatna great anger, it luatna great love or zeal) (e:ka heh ~ tawh Israel gamah/Topa’ deih ~ in hih thu hong tungsak ding hi | the zeal of the Lord will bring this about/inn ka deih ~ in kei hong netum ding hi | zeal for the house will consume me/Jerusalem mite ka it ~ hangin | because of my great love for the people of Jerusalem/Sumduh ~ tawh na kipelh un | keep away from the love of money) (b:luat) (r:26.38.19/20.25.27/12.19.31/43.2.17/38.8.2/58.13.5) (q:draft)
luatnate = (t:n) (w:excess/great intensity) (d:luatna excess, with the plural te, after a verb: the great degree of it, as hong mudah luatnate, how greatly they hate me) (e:keimah hong mudah ~ ngaihsun in) (b:luatna) (r:19.25.19/47.12.21) (q:draft)
Lud = (t:name) (c:male/people) (w:Ludim/Lud/Ludites) (d:name of a son of Shem, and of a people descended from Egypt, the Ludites; in the prophets Lud mite are archers, the men of Lydia) (r:1.10.13)
luguh = (t:n) (w:skull) (d:lu head with guh bone) (e:a ~ leh a khete leh a khut peekte/a ~ a suktap sak zo hi | they have cracked his skull) (r:12.9.35/24.2.16) (q:draft)
luh = (t:v) (w:raid/invade/break into/plunder) (d:enter a place by force to attack or rob it) (e:Refaim kuam sung ~ uh hi/a ciamtehsa teng zan-in inn ~ uh a | at night they break into the houses they have marked/mite paikhia uh a, Siriate’ phual ~ uh hi | the people went out and plundered the camp of the Arameans/a ancilnate uh ~ uh hi | they are looting their threshing floors/a pawlte in Pasian’ inn ~ uh hi | her followers broke into the house of God) (s:sut/buluh) (r:13.14.9/18.24.16/12.7.16/9.23.1/14.24.7) (q:draft)
luha = (t:v) (w:break in/raid) (d:luh break into with -a, linking it to the next verb: breaking in) (e:gutate in ~ a guk theih lohna) (b:luh) (r:40.6.20) (q:draft)
