luhgawpin = (t:v) (w:plunder/loot/raid) (d:luhgawp with the linking suffix in) (e:minam dangte in ~ a ciamnuihbawl khuapite/vante na ngah nadingin ~ a sutgawp ding | to plunder and loot in order to get goods) (b:luhgawp) (r:26.36.4/26.38.13) (q:draft)
luhgawpte = (t:n) (w:plunderers/looters) (d:those who plunder, luhgawp with plural te) (e:a ~ tungah Israel pia ahi hiam/eite hong susia-in eite a hong ~ | those who ruin us and plunder us) (b:luhgawp) (r:23.42.24/23.17.14) (q:draft)
luhgawpzo = (t:v) (w:plunder/be able to plunder) (d:luhgawp plunder with zo, be able or succeed) (e:a galte in ~ ahi hiam) (b:luhgawp) (r:24.2.14) (q:draft)
luhin = (t:v) (w:raid/break into/invade/sack) (d:luh with -in, linking it to the next verb: raiding, having broken in) (e:Gutate in ka biakinn ~ ninsak ding uh hi/inn ~ na gu uh a | they break into houses and steal/Izipt gam ~ a nate uh sut ding a | he will invade Egypt and plunder its goods/gutate in ~ a guktheihna hih leitungah | on this earth where thieves break in and steal) (b:luh) (r:26.7.22/28.11.6/28.7.1/26.29.19/40.6.19) (q:draft)
luhinna = (t:n) (w:support/sustenance) (d:paired with nuntakna in the verse for what a people lives on, NIV supply and support; not the same as luhin raid) (e:nuntakna le ~) (r:23.3.1) (q:draft, low confidence)
