luhzo = (t:v) (w:capture/storm/break into) (d:luh raid with zo, be able: attack a stronghold and take it) (e:galte’ kulhpi a ~ ding hi/a ki-umcih khuapite ~-in a la khin ding hi | he will storm the fortified cities and take them) (b:luh) (r:27.11.10/27.11.15) (q:draft)
lui = (t:n) (w:streamlet/brook/creek/stream) (d:a small river; also the valley in which it runs, as in Kidron lui and Kherith lui) (e:~ panin tui na dawn ding hi/tawl khat khit ciangin a ~ kang hi | after a while the brook dried up/~ gei-a gialheek kungte | the poplars beside the stream/mualtung pan-a hong luangsuk ~ sungah | into the stream that flowed down from the mountain) (s:luitui) (r:11.17.4/11.17.7/18.40.22/5.9.21)
