Lui = (t:n) (w:Wadi/stream/ravine/brook) (d:lui, stream, written with a capital as part of a place name or at the start of a sentence: Izipt Lui is the Wadi of Egypt and Gialheek Lui the Ravine of the Poplars) (e:Izipt ~ panin Eufrates gun dong/Azmon panin Izipt ~ lamah kawi-in | turning from Azmon toward the Wadi of Egypt/Hamath lutna panin Izipt ~ dong | from the entrance of Hamath to the Wadi of Egypt/Gialheek ~-ah paipih uh hi | they carry it to the Ravine of the Poplars/~ khempeuh tuipi-in luangsuk a | all streams flow down to the sea) (b:lui) (r:12.24.7/4.34.5/11.8.65/23.15.7/21.1.7) (q:draft)
