lumcipsak = (t:v) (w:lay low/make lie prostrate) (d:lumcip lie prostrate with the causative sak: make someone lie down so as not to rise again) (e:a tho thei nawn lo dingin amaute a ~) (b:lumcip) (r:23.43.16) (q:draft)
lumgol = (t:n) (w:large shield) (d:lum shield with gol big; contrasted with lumneu small shield) (e:~ leh teipi a tawi galkap) (s:lumpi) (a:lumneu) (r:14.14.8) (q:draft)
lumin = (t:v) (w:lying down/lying) (d:lum lie down with the linking suffix in) (e:Nuam takin ~ ka ihmu ding hi/Simon’ sungnu nattun’a, ~ a om hi | the mother-in-law of Simon lay sick with fever/puanhampi leh vut tungah ~ | lying on sackcloth and ashes/Amah a lupna tungah ~ a mai hei a | he lay on his bed and turned his face away) (b:lum) (r:19.4.8/41.1.30/23.58.5/11.21.4) (q:draft)
lumkhawm = (t:v) (w:sleep with/lie with/have sexual relations) (d:lum, lie down, with khawm, together: lie down together; of a man and a woman, have sexual relations) (e:kuamah tawh a ~ nai lo/na vengpa’ zi tawh na ~ kei ding a | you shall not sleep with the wife of your neighbour/mi nih ~ leh khua lum hi | if two lie down together they are warm/amau’ note ~ ding uh hi | their young will lie down together) (s:lupkhawm/lupkhop) (b:lum) (r:1.24.16/3.18.20/21.4.11/23.11.7) (q:draft)
lumkhawmin = (t:v) (w:sleep with/lie with) (d:lumkhawm with the linking suffix in) (e:numei khat tawh ~) (b:lumkhawm) (r:3.20.18) (q:draft)
lumkhawmsa = (t:adj) (w:having slept with) (d:lumkhawm lie with, with sa marking a completed act; before a noun, who has slept with someone) (e:pasal tawh a ~ numei peuhmah/pasal tawh a ~ numei khempeuh | every woman who has slept with a man) (b:lumkhawm) (r:4.31.17/28.3.1/7.21.11) (q:draft)
lumkhop = (t:v) (w:be warm enough) (d:lum warm with khop enough; a lumkhop ding is enough to be warm) (e:a ~ ding na nei kei uh hi) (r:37.1.6) (q:draft)
lumkik = (t:v) (w:lie down again/go back to sleep) (d:lum lie down with kik again) (e:tuate ne-in dawnin ~ hi/Kong sam kei hi; ~ in | I did not call; lie down again/a hausa-in a ~ nawn kei ding uh hi | they will not lie down rich again) (b:lum) (r:11.19.6/9.3.5/18.27.19) (q:draft)
lumlet = (t:v) (w:overturn/overthrow/turn upside down) (d:turn something upside down: overturn a table or a dish, overthrow a city or a kingdom) (e:a hehna tawh mualte ~ hi/na gensa khuapi ka ~ loh nading | so that I do not overthrow the town you spoke of/keimah in Jerusalem nulin ka ~ ding hi | I will wipe Jerusalem and turn it upside down/Topa in hehpih loin a ~ khuapite | the towns the Lord overthrew without pity) (s:lawnthal) (r:18.9.5/1.19.21/12.21.13/24.20.16) (q:draft)
lumlet = (t:v) (w:pervert/distort/twist) (d:turn a message or a matter upside down so that it is no longer true; of a person, wrong him by deceit) (e:Lungdamna Thu a ~ nuam mi/amaute in khemna tawh kei hong ~ uh hi | they have wronged me with deceit/Pasian’ thu im loin, ~ loin | not hiding or distorting the word of God/innkuanpih khempeuh ~ thei uh hi | they can upset whole households) (s:kawihei) (r:48.1.7/19.119.78/47.4.2/56.1.11) (q:draft)
lumletgawp = (t:v) (w:distort/pervert utterly) (d:lumlet turn upside down with gawp, which marks a thorough or violent action) (e:Vanglian Topa’ thugennate na ~ uh hi) (b:lumlet) (r:24.23.36) (q:draft)
lumletin = (t:v) (w:overturn/overthrow) (d:lumlet with the linking ending in: overturning) (e:zan khat thu-in amaute ~ susia gawp hi/Kumpi gam khempeuh ~ a vangliatna uh a beisak ding | I will overturn all the kingdoms and end their power) (b:lumlet) (r:18.34.25/37.2.22) (q:draft)
lumletin = (t:v) (w:distort/pervert/unsettle) (d:lumlet with the linking ending in: turning a teaching, justice or a mind upside down) (e:Lai Siangtho khiatna ~ amau pumpi uh/Thutang ~ thuman mite lei a den’na | turning justice upside down and casting the upright to the ground/note lungsim uh hong ~, hong gimsak zo | they have unsettled your minds and troubled you) (b:lumlet) (r:61.3.16/30.5.7/44.15.24) (q:draft)
lumletsak = (t:v) (w:overturn/overthrow/frustrate) (d:lumlet with sak: turn over tables, bring plans to nothing) (e:geelna zong a ~ hi/vakhu zuakte’ tutnate a ~ gawp hi | he overturned the seats of those selling doves) (b:lumlet) (r:18.5.13/40.21.12) (q:draft)
lumlum = (t:v) (w:keep sleeping/lie around/keep lying down) (d:doubled form of lum, lie down, for an action that goes on and on) (e:Mi thadahte inn-ah ~ a/Thadahpa aw, bang tanvei ~ ding a | sluggard, how long will you keep lying there/A thadahte ~ a | the lazy keep lying down/Mot paupau, ~, lususu in om ding bek | only to babble, lie around and doze) (r:20.22.13/20.6.9/20.19.15/23.56.10) (q:draft)
lumna = (t:n) (w:warmth/warming) (d:warmth, from lum, warm, with the noun suffix na; khua lumna ding means for getting warm) (e:khua ~ ding mei-am hi lo a) (a:votna) (b:lum) (r:23.47.14) (q:draft)
lumneu = (t:n) (w:small shield) (d:a small shield, from lum, shield, and neu, small; carried by archers) (e:Benjamin mite ~ pua-in thal a keek) (a:lumpi/lumgol) (r:14.14.8) (q:draft)
lumneute = (t:n) (w:small shields) (d:plural of lumneu: small shields, named beside lum lian, large shields) (e:lum lian leh ~ pia hi) (b:lumneu) (r:14.23.9) (q:draft)
lumpa = (t:n) (w:man who lies with/man who slept with) (d:lum, lie, with pa, which marks a man: the man who lay with a woman) (e:numei tawh a ~ in nungak’ pa tungah/numei tawh a ~ leh a numei | the man who slept with the woman and the woman) (b:lum) (r:5.22.29/5.22.22) (q:draft)
lumpi = (t:n) (w:large shield) (d:a large shield, from lum, shield, and pi, big) (e:kham a kiseek ~ zanih bawl hi) (s:lumgol) (a:lumneu) (b:lum) (r:14.9.15) (q:draft)
lumsa = (t:adj) (w:lying dead/slain/laid low) (d:lum, lie, with sa, already: lying where it fell, said of one that has been killed, as in a kigo lumsa and a kithat lumsa) (e:a kigo ~ tawh kibang a/a kithat ~ luanghawm khat bangin | like the corpse of one lying slain) (b:lum) (r:66.5.6/19.89.10) (q:draft)
lumsak = (t:v) (w:make lie down/lay down) (d:lum, lie down, with the causative sak: make a person or an animal lie down, let someone sleep in a place) (e:Lo nona-ah keimah hong ~ a/lei lakah amaute ~ hi | he made them lie down on the ground/kongzing lakah ka ~ ngei kei hi | I never made them sleep in the street/tua lai-ah a tuute ~ lo ding hi | will not rest their flocks there) (b:lum) (r:19.23.2/10.8.2/18.31.32/23.13.20) (q:draft)
lumsuk = (t:v) (w:lie down/lay oneself down) (d:lum, lie, with suk, downward: lie down on the ground or in bed, said of people and animals) (e:Balaam nuai-ah ~ hi/Samuel pai-in ama omna-ah ~ hi | Samuel went and lay down in his place/a khe lam puan leemsakin ~ hi | she uncovered his feet and lay down/Lungkhamin na ~ ding uh hi | you will lie down in torment/humpinelkaipa bangin ~ uh hi | they lie down like a lion) (s:lum/lup) (a:tho) (b:lum) (r:4.22.27/5.25.2/9.3.9/8.3.7/23.50.11/4.24.9) (q:draft)
lumsukin = (t:v) (w:lie down/lying down) (d:lumsuk, lie down, with the ending in, which links it to the next verb: lying down, he did something else) (e:amah ~ a ihmu hi/kung khat nuai-ah amah ~ | he lay down under a bush) (b:lumsuk) (r:11.19.5) (q:draft)
lumsuksakin = (t:v) (w:make lie down) (d:lumsuk, lie down, with the causative sak and the ending in, which links it to the next verb: having someone lie down) (e:thukhen pa in amah ~) (b:lumsuk) (r:5.25.2) (q:draft)
lumta = (t:v) (w:lie down/have lain down) (d:lum, lie down, with ta, which shows that the state has now come about: they now lie there, said of the dead) (e:hih lai-ah ~ uh hi) (b:lum) (r:26.32.21) (q:draft)
lumta = (t:v) (w:be warm/have become warm) (d:lum, warm, with ta, which shows that the state has now come about; ka khua lumta means I am warm now) (e:Ah, ka khua ~, mei mu khin ing) (b:lum) (r:23.44.16) (q:draft)
lumte = (t:n) (w:shields) (d:plural of lum, shield) (e:kham kibawl ~ la-in Jerusalem ah/Na ~ uh la un la | take up your shields/David’ aa ahi teipite leh ~ pia hi | he gave the spears and shields that had been David’s/tho un, ~ sathau nuh un | get up, oil the shields) (b:lum) (r:13.18.7/24.46.3/12.11.10/23.21.5) (q:draft)
luna = (t:n) (w:sickness/ailment) (d:sickness, used in the pair cina, luna for the sick and every kind of illness; literally lu, head, with na, be in pain) (e:cina, ~ khempeuh a damsak hi/cina, ~, bawlsiatna a thuak mite in | those who suffered from sickness, disease and affliction) (b:lu) (r:40.9.35/41.3.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
lunatna = (t:n) (w:sickness/disease) (d:sickness, used in the pair cinatna lunatna, sicknesses and diseases) (e:eite cinatna ~ a thuak hi) (s:cinatna/natna) (a:cidamna) (r:40.8.17) (q:draft, low confidence)
lung = (t:n) (w:heart/mind) (d:the heart or mind as the seat of feeling and thought, mostly in set expressions: lung kham, be troubled; lung dam, be glad; lung muang, be secure; lung kituak, be of one mind) (e:Ka ~ khamin ka lungsim hong nat/a ~ kituak nadingun ka thuum hi | I plead with them to be of one mind/thuhoih zakna in ~ damsak hi | good news gladdens the heart/~ muangin ka om hi | I rest secure) (s:lungsim/lungtang) (r:19.73.21/42.21.19/50.4.2/20.15.30/19.16.9) (q:draft)
lung-amsak = (t:v) (w:terrify/trouble/unsettle) (d:make the heart, lung, disturbed or afraid, with the causative sak; also written lungamsak) (e:ahih hangin kei hong ~ kei in/Amaute ~ inla | let them be terrified/note hong buaisakin hong ~ hi | they disturbed you and troubled your minds) (s:lungamsak/lausak) (a:lungmuangsak) (r:24.17.18/44.15.24) (q:draft)
lungam = (t:v) (w:be humiliated/be dismayed) (d:be cast down in heart from shame; in the verse it follows mai zum, be ashamed; probably the same word as lunggam) (e:mai zumin ka ~ hi) (s:lunggam) (r:24.31.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
lungamsak = (t:v) (w:terrify/dismay) (d:lungam, be dismayed, with the causative sak: make someone lose courage, terrify; also written lung-amsak) (e:Amaute na ~ in/ahih hangin kei hong ~ kei in | but do not terrify me) (s:lung-amsak/lausak) (a:lungmuangsak) (b:lungam) (r:24.17.18) (q:draft)
lungdahna = (t:n) (w:sorrow/grief) (d:sorrow, from lung, heart, with dah, be sad, and the noun suffix na) (e:a ~ leh lungman’na a kipan hi) (s:dahna/lungkhamna/lunggimna) (a:lungdamna) (r:40.26.37) (q:draft)
lungdam = (t:adj) (w:happy/glad/joyful) (d:glad or happy at heart, from lung, heart, and dam, well) (e:numeite in kei a ~ hong ci ding/Kei ~ ing | I am happy/amaute in ne-in dawnin ~ uh hi | they ate and drank and were happy/a ~ lo mah bang ding uh hi | as if they were not happy) (s:nuam) (r:1.30.13/46.7.30/11.4.20)
lungdam = (t:n) (w:joy/gladness) (d:joy or gladness, as in lungdam la, song of joy, and lungdam ko, express joy or give thanks) (e:ama nasepnate ~ late tawh | his works with songs of joy/Ama tungah ~ ko un la | give thanks to him) (s:lungdamna/kipahna) (a:dahna) (r:19.107.22/19.100.4)
lungdam = (t:v) (w:delight/rejoice/be glad) (d:be glad, rejoice, or take delight in someone or something) (e:A tawntungin na ~ ta un/leitungah ka ~ a | I rejoice in the world/mi citakte tungah ~ hi | he delights in trustworthy people/thuhoih vaihawmte ~ hi | those who plan what is good rejoice) (s:kipak/nuam) (a:dah) (r:52.5.16/20.8.31/20.12.22/20.12.20)
Lungdam = (t:v) (w:rejoice/be glad) (d:lungdam written with a capital at the start of a sentence or in a title; Lungdam nading Thu, word for rejoicing, is the gospel, and Lungdam kohna is thanksgiving) (e:~ nading Thu gen ding a nei/~ kohna tawh ama kongpi-ah lut un la | enter his gates with thanksgiving/~ biakpiakna Pasian’ tungah pia un la | offer a thank offering to God/~ kohna-in silngo sawh anlum va pia un la | go and offer leavened bread as a thank offering) (b:lungdam) (r:66.14.6/19.100.4/19.50.14/30.4.5) (q:draft)
lungdamhuai = (t:adj) (w:blessed/pleasing/gladdening) (d:lungdam, glad, with huai, causing or worthy of a feeling: bringing joy; it renders both blessed and pleasing) (e:Kei hong umte pen a ~ mahmah ahi hi/Pasian tungah a ~ | pleasing to God/nang a dingin a ~ hong hi ding hi | it will be a blessing for you/hong umte a dingin ~ mahmah zaw ding hi | it will be more blessed for those who believe) (a:dahhuai) (r:40.11.6/50.4.18/42.14.14/43.20.29) (q:draft)
lungdamin = (t:adv) (w:joyfully/gladly/with joy) (d:lungdam, be glad, with the adverb ending in: with joy, gladly) (e:~ a liangko ah pua a/~ a mang pah uh hi | they at once receive it with joy/Pasian’ tapate ~ kiko uh hi | the sons of God shouted for joy/~ ka mawh kiphelna thu kong gen ding hi | I will gladly make my defense) (s:kipakin/lungdamtakin) (a:dahin) (b:lungdam) (r:42.15.5/19.118.24/41.4.16/18.38.7/44.24.10) (q:draft)
lungdamkoh = (t:v) (w:give thanks/thank) (d:lungdam, joy, with koh, express: give thanks; lungdamkoh nading is thanksgiving and lungdamkoh biakpiakna a thank offering) (e:Pasian’ tungah ~ nading zong/~ nadingin thunuam-a ama biakpiakna tawh | with his fellowship offering of thanksgiving/~ piaknate pia-in | sacrificing thank offerings/~ biakpiakna nang tungah kong pia ding a | I will sacrifice a thank offering to you) (r:47.9.12/19.107.22/3.7.13/19.116.17) (q:draft)
lungdamkohna = (t:n) (w:thanksgiving/thanks/gratitude) (d:the giving of thanks, from lungdamkoh, give thanks, with the noun suffix na; lungdamkohna la is a song of thanksgiving) (e:~ la a sak ding seh masa hi/Pasian tungah ~ kam na pauzaw un | rather speak words of thanksgiving to God/~ le lasakna awging om ding hi | thanksgiving and the sound of singing will be there/a sanggamte tawh ~ late a uk hi | with his associates he was in charge of the songs of thanksgiving) (b:lungdamkoh) (r:13.16.7/47.1.11/49.5.4/23.51.3/16.12.8) (q:draft)
lungdamna = (t:n) (w:joy/gladness) (d:joy or gladness, from lungdam, be glad, with the noun suffix na) (e:Tua khua sungah ~ tampi a piang hi/suahtakna, ~, leh pahtawina ngah uh hi | they had freedom, joy and honor/~ leh nuamna tawh amaute kitumpih hi | they are led in with joy and gladness/Topa tungah ~ aw ging sak un | shout for joy to the Lord) (s:kipahna/kipakna/nuamna/lungnopna) (a:dahna/lungdahna) (b:lungdam) (r:44.8.8/19.51.8/17.8.16/19.45.15/19.100.1) (q:draft)
lungdamna = (t:n) (w:thanksgiving/thanks) (d:thanks given to God, the same word as lungdamna, joy; lungdamna ko is to give thanks) (e:~ tawh amah ka pahtawi ding hi/Ama omna-ah ~ ko-in pai ni | let us come before him with thanksgiving) (s:lungdamkohna) (b:lungdam) (r:19.69.30/19.95.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
Lungdamna = (t:n) (w:joy/good news) (d:lungdamna, joy, written with a capital at the start of a sentence or in Lungdamna Thu, the Good News or gospel) (e:tua gamah ~ Thu a hilh uh hi/Zeisu Khazih’ ~ Thu a kipatna | the beginning of the good news of Jesus Christ/hansuahna tawh ~ Thu mite kiangah a hilh hi | with exhortation he proclaimed the good news to the people/~ leh kipahna hong pia in la | give me joy and gladness) (b:lungdamna) (r:44.14.7/41.1.1/42.3.18/19.51.8) (q:draft)
lungdamnate = (t:n) (w:joys/pleasures) (d:plural of lungdamna: joys, also the pleasures of life) (e:leitung ~ in dep gawp a/na ~ uh maigumna suaksak zaw un | change your joy to gloom) (a:dahnate) (b:lungdamna) (r:42.8.14/59.4.9) (q:draft)
lungdampah = (t:v) (w:be glad readily/be pleased) (d:lungdam, be glad, with pah, at once; in the verse it is negated: he takes no pleasure in doing so) (e:amah ~ sam lo hi) (r:25.3.33) (q:draft, low confidence)
lungdampih = (t:v) (w:rejoice with/congratulate) (d:lungdam, be glad, with pih, together with: share someone’s joy, congratulate him on his good fortune) (e:Hong ~ ta un/A lungdam mite ~ unla | rejoice with those who rejoice/note in zong hong ~ ta un | you too rejoice with me/a ~ dingin Kumpi David kiangah | to King David to congratulate him) (a:dahpih) (b:lungdam) (r:42.15.6/13.18.10/45.12.15/50.2.18) (q:draft)
lungdampih = (t:v) (w:rejoice in/delight in/be glad about) (d:take pleasure in a thing; lungdampih khuapi is a city one delights in, a city of revelry) (e:Mihaite in a hai mah uh ~ a/hih khuapi nomau’ ~ khuapi mah ahi hiam | is this your city of revelry) (b:lungdam) (r:20.15.21/23.23.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
lungdampihna = (t:n) (w:rejoicing with) (d:lungdampih, rejoice with someone, with the noun suffix na; with ding it means in order to rejoice together) (e:hong nekpihin hong ~ dingun na sam) (b:lungdampih) (r:38.3.10) (q:draft)
lungdamsak = (t:v) (w:make glad/please/gladden) (d:lungdam, be glad, with the causative sak: make someone glad, please someone) (e:Pasian a ~ zo kei uh hi/a zi ~ nadingin leitung thu a ngaihsun hi | he thinks about worldly things to please his wife/nangma nasepna tawh kei hong ~ a | you make me glad by your deeds/kei kua in hong ~ ding hiam | who will make me glad) (s:kipaksak/nuamsak/lungkimsak/lungnuamsak) (a:dahsak/lungkhamsak) (b:lungdam) (r:45.8.8/19.51.8/46.7.33/19.92.4/47.2.2) (q:draft)
lungdamsakkik = (t:v) (w:make glad again/restore joy) (d:lungdamsak, make glad, with kik, again: give someone back his joy) (e:a citak thupuak pa in mi ~ hi/Nong hotkhiatna hangin hong ~ inla | restore to me the joy of your salvation) (b:lungdamsak) (r:20.13.17/19.51.12) (q:draft)
lungdamsakna = (t:n) (w:pleasing/making glad) (d:lungdamsak, make glad, with the noun suffix na; with ding it means in order to please, to seek the favor of) (e:nang kong ~ ding uh hanciam loin) (b:lungdamsak) (r:27.9.13) (q:draft)
lungdamsakpa = (t:n) (w:the man who made glad) (d:lungdamsak, make glad, with pa, which marks a man: the man who made someone glad) (e:a ~ in haamsiatna thuak ta hen) (b:lungdamsak) (r:24.20.15) (q:draft)
lungdamsakte = (t:n) (w:those who please) (d:lungdamsak, make glad, with te, the people who do so; amah a lungdamsakte means those who please him) (e:amah a ~ tungah pilna/amah a ~ tungah piaksak hi | he hands it over to those who please him) (b:lungdamsak) (r:21.2.26) (q:draft)
lungdamtakin = (t:adv) (w:gladly/joyfully) (d:lungdam, glad, with takin, which makes an adverb: gladly, most willingly) (e:~ ka neih khempeuh kong piaknop) (s:lungdamin/kipakin) (a:dahin) (b:lungdam) (r:47.12.15) (q:draft)
lungdamte = (t:n) (w:those who rejoice/the joyful) (d:lungdam, be glad, with the plural te, used as a noun: people who rejoice) (e:Mi ~ tawh kibangin na lungdam khawm un/a ~ in a lungdam lo mah bang | those who are happy, as if they were not/pawi hun sunga mi ~ bang ding hi | will be like people rejoicing at a festival) (s:gualnuamte) (a:dahte/kapte) (b:lungdam) (r:45.12.15/46.7.30/36.3.18) (q:draft)
lungdamzaw = (t:adj) (w:happier/more joyful) (d:lungdam, glad, with the comparative zaw, more; as a command with un it means rejoice rather, rejoice all the more) (e:a ~ ding hi ci-in ka um/vantungah na min uh a kigelh manin ~ un | rejoice rather that your names are written in heaven/a kigen thei loin ka ~ hi | my joy is greater than can be told) (b:lungdam) (r:46.7.40/42.10.20/47.7.4) (q:draft)
lungduai = (t:adj) (w:patient/slow to anger) (d:patient, slow to become angry, from lung, heart, and duai; lungduai-in is patiently) (e:~ a ka omna dingin/Itna in a ~ thei hi | love is patient/Topa a ~ mahmah a | the Lord is very slow to anger/mi khempeuh tungah na ~ un | be patient with everyone) (s:duai) (a:lungtom/hehbaih) (r:18.6.11/19.37.7/46.13.4/34.1.3/52.5.14) (q:draft)
lungduaina = (t:n) (w:patience/forbearance/longsuffering) (d:patience or forbearance, from lungduai, patient, with the noun suffix na) (e:kiphatsakna sangin ~ hoihzaw hi/upna le ~ a nei mite bangin | like those who have faith and patience/ka upna, ka ~, ka itna | my faith, my patience, my love) (s:thuakzawhna) (a:lungtomna) (b:lungduai) (r:21.7.8/48.5.22/58.6.12/55.3.10) (q:draft)
lungduaisak = (t:v) (w:make patient) (d:lungduai, patient, with the causative sak: make someone patient) (e:Pilna in mi ~ a) (b:lungduai) (r:20.19.11) (q:draft)
lungduaitakin = (t:adv) (w:patiently) (d:lungduai, patient, with takin, which makes an adverb: patiently) (e:~ i ngak thei hi) (b:lungduai) (r:45.8.25) (q:draft)
lungduaite = (t:n) (w:the patient/patient people) (d:lungduai, patient, with the plural te: those who are patient) (e:A ~ mipil hi a) (b:lungduai) (r:20.14.29) (q:draft)
lungduaizo = (t:v) (w:be able to be patient/bear with) (d:lungduai, patient, with zo, be able; in the verse it is negated: could no longer be patient with them) (e:amaute tungah ka ~ nawn kei a) (b:lungduai) (r:38.11.8) (q:draft)
lunggai = (t:v) (w:consider/think about) (d:turn something over in the mind, consider; probably the same word as lungngai) (e:bang zah a lian na ~ un) (s:lungngai/ngaihsut) (r:58.7.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
lunggam = (t:v) (w:be disgraced/be dismayed) (d:be cast down in heart from shame; in the verse it follows maizum, be ashamed; probably the same word as lungam) (e:na gitlohna uh hangin maizum-in na ~ ding) (s:lungam) (r:24.22.22) (q:draft, low confidence)
lunggim = (t:v) (w:be troubled/be distressed/be weary/be in anguish) (d:be heavy or worn out in heart from worry, fear or grief, from lung, heart, and gim, be weary) (e:~ lungkhamin si uh hi/Hit numeite’ hangin ka ~ a | I am weary because of the Hittite women/mi khempeuh note mai-ah ~ uh hi | all the people are melting in fear before you/a ~ mite tha a pia thei kammal | a word that can give strength to the weary) (s:lungkham) (a:lungdam/lungnuam) (r:18.21.25/20.30.1/1.27.46/6.2.9/23.50.4) (q:draft)
lunggimhuai = (t:adj) (w:wearisome/troubling/distressing) (d:lunggim, be troubled, with huai, which marks what causes a feeling: wearying or troubling to the heart) (e:Na khempeuh ~ a, kuama genzawh ding/a ~ mahmah nasep khat hong suak a | it became a very troubling task) (s:lungkhamhuai) (a:lungdamhuai) (r:21.1.8/19.73.16) (q:draft)
lunggimin = (t:v) (w:be distressed/be in anguish) (d:lunggim, be distressed, with the linking ending in: in distress, in bitterness of heart) (e:~ a si uh hi/amaute ~, a tawpna-ah a mawhna hangun beimang | in distress, they will in the end waste away because of their sin/mi khempeuh ~ a mai-ah si teeng lo hi | all are in anguish and their faces grow pale) (s:lungkhamin) (b:lunggim) (r:18.21.25/26.4.17/34.2.10) (q:draft)
lunggimna = (t:n) (w:anguish/distress/grief) (d:anguish or distress of heart, from lunggim, be troubled, with the noun suffix na) (e:Ka ~ kitawikhai hen la/~ leh natna in kei hong sugawp a | anguish and pain overwhelm me/nakpitakin dahin ka ~ a khang hi | I grieve greatly and my anguish grows/~ leh gentheihna thonginn sungah a hong kalhkhum hi | he has shut me in a prison of bitterness and hardship) (s:lungkhamna/dahna/lungdahna) (a:lungdamna/lungnopna) (b:lunggim) (r:18.6.2/18.30.27/45.9.2/25.3.5) (q:draft)
Lunggimna = (t:n) (w:distress/anguish/grief) (d:lunggimna, distress, written with a capital at the start of a sentence or in a section heading such as Kikhen Man-a Lunggimna, distress because of parting) (e:Kikhen Man-a ~ Nungak/~ thuakin, thuumin, kapin, om un | grieve, mourn and wail) (b:lunggimna) (r:22.5.1/59.4.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
lunggimnate = (t:n) (w:distresses/troubles/anguish) (d:plural of lunggimna: the distresses that someone suffers) (e:ka thuaknate, ka ~ hong en in/thong sungah i thuak i ~ a hong thei hi | he knows the distresses we suffer in prison) (s:lungkhamnate) (b:lunggimna) (r:25.1.20/25.3.34) (q:draft)
lunggimpih = (t:v) (w:be anxious for/be distressed for/be in anguish over) (d:lunggim, be troubled, with pih, together with or for another person: be anxious or in anguish for someone) (e:note ka hong ~ ding hi/mawhna-ah a pukkha a om ciangin dahin ka ~ hi | when someone falls into sin, I grieve in anguish for him/pawlpi a tuamtuamte a dingin lunghimawhin ka ~ lai hi | I am still anxious and distressed for the various churches) (b:lunggim) (r:48.4.19/47.11.29/47.11.28) (q:draft)
lunggimsak = (t:v) (w:weary/trouble/burden/dishearten) (d:lunggim, be troubled, with the causative sak: make someone weary or heavy in heart) (e:mi hoihte na ~ uh a/Bang thu-ah note hong ~ ka hi hiam | how have I burdened you/ka Pasian zong ~ lai na hi uh hiam | will you weary my God also/a nute uh ka ~ ding hi | I will bring anguish on their mothers) (s:lungkhamsak/gimsak) (a:lungdamsak/lungnuamsak) (b:lunggim) (r:26.13.22/33.6.3/23.7.13/24.15.8) (q:draft)
lunggimzaw = (t:v) (w:be more distressed) (d:lunggim, be distressed, with zaw, more: be more distressed than someone else) (e:nakpitakin kei ka ~ hi) (b:lunggim) (r:8.1.13) (q:draft)
lunggulh = (t:v) (w:desire/long for/lust after) (d:want something strongly, long for it; also used of sexual desire) (e:Khazih tawh ka om ding ka ~ hi/na pa’ inn nakpi takin ~ na hih manin | because you longed greatly for your father’s house/amaute ~ mahmah pah a | she at once lusted after them/a lawm ngaihte ~ mahmah hi | she lusted after her lovers) (s:deih) (r:50.1.23/1.31.30/26.23.16/26.23.5)
