lungkham = (t:v) (w:be troubled/be distressed/worry/grieve) (d:be anxious, troubled or distressed in mind, from lung, heart, and kham; a lungkham mite are people in trouble) (e:~-in ka pau thei kei hi/A ~ mite tawh kei kap khawmin | I wept together with those in trouble/a ~ mahmahte, leenggahzu pia in | give wine to those who are in anguish/Hau napi-a ~ sangin | than to be rich and troubled) (s:lunggim/lunghimawh) (a:lungdam/lungnuam) (r:19.77.4/14.15.4/18.30.25/20.31.6/20.15.16) (q:draft)
lungkhamhuai = (t:adj) (w:distressing/wretched/grievous) (d:causing worry or sorrow, from lungkham, be troubled, with huai, worthy of or causing a feeling) (e:tu laitak a ~ thu ka ngaihsut ciangin/a hehpihhuai, a ~ na hih lamtak uh | that you are pitiful and wretched/bangzahin ~ ding ahi hiam | how distressing will it be) (s:dahhuai/lunggimhuai) (a:lungdamhuai) (r:46.7.26/66.3.17/60.4.17) (q:draft)
