lungkhamna = (t:n) (w:distress/trouble/anguish/sorrow) (d:distress, trouble or anguish, from lungkham, be troubled, with the noun suffix na) (e:ama tungah ~ lianpen tung ding hi/a nuntak hun tom a, ~ tawh kidim hi | their life is short and full of trouble/natna leh ~ ka thuak hi | I suffered pain and distress/Ethiopia gamah ~ lianpi om ding hi | there will be great anguish in Cush) (s:lunggimna/dahna/haksatna) (a:lungdamna/lungnopna/lungmuanna) (b:lungkham) (r:18.20.22/18.14.1/19.116.3/26.30.4) (q:draft)
Lungkhamna = (t:n) (w:trouble/distress) (d:lungkhamna, trouble, written with a capital at the start of a sentence or in Lungkhamna Kuam, Valley of Trouble, the Valley of Achor) (e:~ Kuam pen lametna kongpi ka suaksak/~ a thuak uh ciangin | when distress comes upon them/~ na tuah uh ciangin lungnopna na zong ding uh a | when trouble comes you will seek peace) (b:lungkhamna) (r:28.2.15/18.27.9/26.7.25) (q:draft)
lungkhamnate = (t:n) (w:troubles/distresses/anxieties) (d:plural of lungkhamna: troubles, distresses) (e:na ~ khempeuh uh ama kiang tunpih un/gimna, haksatna, ~ ka thuak uh hi | we endure troubles, hardships and distresses/Na ~ uh le na zawnnate uh ka thei hi | I know your afflictions and your poverty) (s:lunggimnate) (b:lungkhamna) (r:60.5.7/47.6.4/66.2.9) (q:draft)
