lungkhamsak = (t:v) (w:distress/trouble/grieve/cause sorrow) (d:lungkham, be troubled, with the causative sak: make someone troubled or sad, bring trouble on someone) (e:a pian’na a nu zong ~ hi/Keimah in Israel mite ka ~ kei hi | I have not troubled Israel/Kamtai ginalo in mi ~ a | a wicked messenger brings people trouble/na galte un hong ~ nading | the distress your enemies will cause you) (s:dahsak/lunggimsak) (a:lungdamsak/lungnuamsak/hehnem) (b:lungkham) (r:20.17.25/5.28.53/11.18.18/20.13.17) (q:draft)
