lungkhauh = (t:adj) (w:stubborn/stiff-necked/hard-hearted/harsh) (d:literally hard of heart: lung heart with khauh hard; said of people who will not listen, and in 1 Peter 2:18 of harsh masters) (e:a ~ mite ahi uh hi/note in ~ mi na hi uh hi | you are a stiff-necked people/~ mite ka hita zongun | although we are a stiff-necked people/~ nei uh ahi zongin na mang un | obey them even if they are harsh) (s:paupeng) (a:lungnem/lungsimnem) (r:2.32.9/5.21.18/2.33.3/2.34.9/60.2.18) (q:draft)
lungkhauhin = (t:adj) (w:stubborn/hard-hearted) (d:lungkhauh with the linking ending in, used when another verb follows) (e:ka tapa uh ~ lehdo thei a/amah a ~ kiphasak a | he became hard-hearted and proud) (b:lungkhauh) (r:5.21.20/27.5.20) (q:draft)
