lungkiasak = (t:v) (w:discourage/dishearten) (d:lungkia, lose heart, with -sak, cause) (e:ka sanggamte in mite ~ uh/Israel mite bang hangin ~ ding | why discourage the Israelites/Ama hangin kuamah ~ kei in | let no one lose heart because of him/Hih ka thugenna in note hong ~ ahi hiam | does this teaching of mine offend you) (s:thazawsak) (a:lungkipsak/hansuah) (b:lungkia) (r:6.14.8/4.32.7/9.17.32/43.6.61) (q:draft)
lungkiasakin = (t:v) (w:discourage/dishearten) (d:lungkiasak discourage with -in, linking it to the next verb) (e:Judah mite ~) (b:lungkiasak) (r:15.4.4) (q:draft)
lungkiat = (t:v) (w:lose heart/be discouraged/give up) (d:form of lungkia used before nading, loh and ngei) (e:kuamah a ~ loh nadingin/a ~ ngei loh nading uh | that they should never give up/~ nading, thanem nading a om loh nadingin | so that they do not lose heart or grow weak) (b:lungkia) (r:52.3.2/42.18.1/51.3.21) (q:draft)
lungkiatna = (t:n) (w:discouragement/loss of heart/dismay) (d:lungkiat lose heart with the noun suffix na: the state of having lost courage or hope) (e:thanem ~ ka nei kei uh hi/Thakiamna ~ a om loh nadingin | so that there is no weariness or loss of heart/~ na thuak veve ding uh hi | you will be shattered all the same) (a:hanna) (b:lungkiat) (r:47.4.1/58.12.3/23.8.9) (q:draft)
lungkim = (t:v) (w:be satisfied/be pleased/be content) (d:lung heart with kim complete: be satisfied, pleased or content with someone or something; with kei or lo, be displeased) (e:tua thu a zak ciangin a ~ hi/kei tungah ~ ahih manin hong honkhia hi | he rescued me because he delighted in me/na zi tawh ~ in | be content with your wife/Jonah ~ het loin a heh hi | Jonah was not pleased at all and was angry) (s:nuamsa) (r:3.10.20/58.10.6/19.18.19/20.5.18/32.4.1) (q:draft)
lungkimhuai = (t:adj) (w:pleasing/acceptable/satisfying) (d:lungkim, be satisfied, with huai, worthy of: such as pleases; with lo, displeasing) (e:mai-ah a ~ hi ding hi/muhna-ah ~ lo a | it was displeasing in his sight/Topa tungah a ~ na khat | something pleasing to the Lord) (s:lungdamhuai) (r:39.3.4/1.38.10/11.14.13) (q:draft)
lungkimin = (t:adv) (w:contentedly/with contentment/willingly/confidently) (d:form of lungkim with -in, being content or assured) (e:a om zah tawh ~ i om ding hi/Hehpihna a pia mi in ~ pia ta hen | let the one who gives give willingly/thu-upna ah ~ lau loin | confident in faith and without fear/eite ~, lau lohna lungsim nei-in | we, with confidence and a fearless heart) (b:lungkim) (r:54.6.8/54.6.6/45.12.8/50.1.14/49.3.12) (q:draft)
lungkimlo = (t:adj) (w:displeased/sullen/discontented) (d:lungkim be pleased with lo, not) (e:a innah ~) (s:maigum) (b:lungkim) (r:11.20.43) (q:draft)
lungkimlohna = (t:n) (w:displeasure/indignation) (d:lungkim be pleased with loh, not, and the noun suffix na; in the verse beside hehna and thangpaihna for God's wrath) (e:ka ~ lianpi tawh) (a:lungkimna) (r:24.32.37) (q:draft)
lungkimna = (t:n) (w:pleasure/delight/favour/satisfaction) (d:being pleased with someone or something) (e:amau sungah ka ~ teng om hi/na ~ gun panin | from your river of delights/ama sungah ka ~ ka nasempa en un | see my servant in whom I delight) (a:lungkimlohna) (b:lungkim) (r:19.16.3/19.147.10/19.36.8/23.42.1) (q:draft)
lungkimpih = (t:v) (w:be pleased with/approve/consent to) (d:lungkim with pih: be pleased about a thing, agree to it) (e:Pasian in hong ~ kha ding hi) (s:thukimpih) (b:lungkim) (r:4.23.27) (q:draft)
lungkimsak = (t:v) (w:please/satisfy) (d:lungkim be satisfied with the causative sak: please someone, or give them all they need) (e:a ngetna in Topa ~ hi/na itna kip tawh kote hong ~ in | satisfy us with your unfailing love/Nuntak sau tawh amah ka ~ ding a | with long life I will satisfy him/Pilat in mihonte ~ nuam ahih manin | because Pilate wanted to satisfy the crowd) (s:lungdamsak) (a:hehsak) (b:lungkim) (r:11.3.10/19.90.14/19.91.16/41.15.15) (q:draft)
lungkimsakin = (t:v) (w:please/satisfy) (d:lungkimsak with the linking suffix in) (e:amaute ~ amaute tungah kam hoih pau lecin/bangte in amah ~ | what pleases him) (b:lungkimsak) (r:14.10.7/45.12.2) (q:draft)
lungkimte = (t:n) (w:those who are satisfied/the complacent) (d:lungkim be satisfied, with the plural te) (e:Nomau tumtakin a ~ aw, linglawng un/amau ngahsa tawh a ~’ thumong ahi hi | it is the end of those content with what they have) (s:lungmuangte) (b:lungkim) (r:23.32.11/19.49.13) (q:draft)
lungkimthei = (t:v) (w:be able to be content) (d:lungkim be content with thei, can) (e:a ~ dingin a kisinsa ka hi hi) (b:lungkim) (r:50.4.12) (q:draft)
lungkimzo = (t:v) (w:be satisfied) (d:lungkim with zo, be able, in the verses always negated, lungkimzo nai lo, still not satisfied) (e:na ~ nai sam kei hi/a dangte tawh ~ nai lo na hih manin | because you were still not satisfied with the others/hih thu-ah ~ nai lo na hih uhleh | if you are still not satisfied in this matter/na ~ tuan nai sam kei hi | you were still not satisfied) (b:lungkim) (r:26.16.28/26.16.29/44.19.39) (q:draft)
lungkip = (t:v) (w:stand firm/be steadfast/be strong in heart) (d:lung heart with kip firm) (e:ka ~ hi ci-in a ki-um mi/umin na ~ uh leh | if you believe and hold firm/Note na ~ theih nadingun | so that you may be made strong/a ~ nading, upna lamah a kip nading | to be steadfast and firm in faith) (s:kip) (a:lungkia/lungsi) (r:46.10.12/45.1.11/46.15.2/56.2.2) (q:draft)
lungkipin = (t:adv) (w:steadfastly/firmly/with perseverance) (d:lungkip be steadfast, with the adverb ending in) (e:a manin ~ a thuakzawh nadingun/~ a gahte ahi uh hi | they are those who bear fruit by persevering/~, kicingin, kiam loin | steadfastly and fully, without slackening) (s:kipin/kiptakin) (b:lungkip) (r:56.2.2/46.15.58/42.8.15) (q:draft)
lungkipna = (t:n) (w:steadfastness/firmness/endurance) (d:lungkip firm of heart with the noun suffix na) (e:itna ka neihna, ka ~/note ~ uh pan na puk loh nadingun | so that you do not fall from your steadfastness) (s:kipna) (a:lungkiatna) (b:lungkip) (r:55.3.10/61.3.17) (q:draft)
lungkipsak = (t:v) (w:encourage/strengthen/make steadfast) (d:lungkip be steadfast, with the causative sak) (e:nungzuite a ~ uh a/thu tampi hilhin, a ~ uh hi | they said much and strengthened them/amaute a ~ khit uh ciangin a paikhia uh | after encouraging them they left) (s:hansuah) (a:lungkiasak) (b:lungkip) (r:44.14.21/44.15.32/44.16.40) (q:draft)
lungli = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:poplar/balsam tree/mulberry tree) (d:a kind of tree, named with kung as lungli kung; English versions differ on which tree is meant) (e:~ kungte gal panin amaute hih in/~ kungte gal khat lam panin | from the side opposite the poplar trees) (r:10.5.23/13.14.14) (q:draft)
lungman = (t:v) (w:be troubled/be perplexed/be amazed) (d:form of lungmang written with an apostrophe before na; lungman’na is trouble of heart, anxiety or amazement) (e:a ~’na leh dahna a kipan hi/lamdangsakna leh ~’na tawh a kidim uh hi | they were filled with wonder and amazement/hih nuntakna leh ~’na hangin | because of this life and its anxieties/~’na om lo dingin hong kha un | send him on without anxiety) (r:41.14.33/44.3.10/42.21.34/46.16.11) (q:draft)
lungmang = (t:v) (w:be troubled/be perplexed/be dismayed) (d:be upset or at a loss in the heart, from worry, fear or wonder) (e:Note ~ kei un/Bangmah thu-ah ~ loin | not anxious about anything/Mari in tua thugenna hangin ~ a | Mary was troubled at these words/Lokhote a ~ uh a | the farmers are dismayed) (s:lungkham/patau) (r:43.14.1/48.4.20/50.4.6/42.1.29/24.14.4) (q:draft)
Lungmang = (t:v) (w:be troubled/be dismayed/be amazed/wonder) (d:lungmang written with a capital at the start of a sentence; Lungmang kei in is do not be troubled) (e:~ un la, taimang un/~ kei in, upna bek nei in | do not be troubled, only believe/~ kei in, upna na neih leh | do not be troubled; if you have faith) (b:lungmang) (r:44.13.41/41.5.36/42.8.50) (q:draft)
lungmangin = (t:v) (w:be perplexed/be troubled/be in anguish) (d:form of lungmang with -in, being at a loss or deeply troubled) (e:tawlnga loin ~ gimin ka om hi/~, gimna a thuak ding uh hi | perplexed, they will suffer anguish/lunghimawhin ~ om kei un | do not be alarmed or troubled/a sin sungah khuisa-a ~ | deeply moved within and troubled) (b:lungmang) (r:45.9.2/42.21.25/53.2.2/43.11.33) (q:draft)
lungmangsak = (t:v) (w:unsettle/upset/trouble) (d:lungmang be troubled, perplexed, with the causative sak; in the verse of upsetting the faith of believers) (e:thu um mi pawlkhat ~ uh hi) (b:lungmang) (r:55.2.18) (q:draft)
lungmanhuai = (t:adj) (w:surprising/astonishing) (d:lungmang be amazed with huai, which marks what causes or deserves a feeling; negated in the verse: it is no wonder) (e:Hih thu in ~ hi lo hi) (r:47.11.14) (q:draft)
lungmuan = (t:v) (w:be secure/be confident/be at peace) (d:form of lungmuang used before na; lungmuan'na is security, confidence, peace of mind) (e:~’na tawh ama kiangah i om/galvilna tausangte’ huam sungah ~’na om ta hen | may there be security within your citadels/Gitlohna in ~’na piangsak lo a | wickedness does not bring security/daihna leh ~’ tawntungna om ding hi | there will be quietness and lasting confidence) (r:62.2.28/19.122.7/20.12.3/23.32.17) (q:draft)
lungmuang = (t:adj) (w:secure/safe/at ease/confident) (d:free from fear or danger; lungmuang takin means safely, in safety) (e:~ takin na nungta ding a/~ lungnuamin om uh a | they are secure and at ease/~ takin Jakob hong tung hi | Jacob arrived safely/~ takin mi teeng ding uh a | people will live there in safety) (s:bit/lungmuanhuai) (r:20.3.23/18.21.23/1.33.18/38.14.11) (q:draft)
lungmuanga = (t:adv) (w:securely/at ease/without care) (d:lungmuang with a, used before om: living in safety) (e:hutna sungah ~ om dingin/~ a om mite’ puantualpi | the robes of those living at ease) (s:lungmuangin) (b:lungmuang) (r:19.61.4/33.2.8) (q:draft)
lungmuangin = (t:adv) (w:securely/safely/confidently) (d:with a mind at rest, without fear: lungmuang with the adverb ending -in) (e:thuman mite ~ om tawntung uh hi/thuman mite in beelin ~ om thei uh hi | the righteous take refuge and are safe/kuamah in su loin ~ a om kik uh | they live securely again with no one disturbing them/~ a om lai takin gutate in buluh ding | while he is at ease robbers will attack) (s:lungmuanga) (b:lungmuang) (r:20.10.25/20.18.10/26.39.26/18.15.21) (q:draft)
lungmuangsak = (t:v) (w:make secure/keep safe/give confidence) (d:lungmuang secure, with the causative sak) (e:Topa muanna in hong ~ hi/pilna in zong hong ~ hi | wisdom also gives security) (s:lungmuansak/lungmuanhuaisak) (a:lunghimawhsak) (b:lungmuang) (r:20.29.25/21.7.12) (q:draft)
lungmuangte = (t:n) (w:those at ease/the complacent) (d:lungmuang at ease, secure, with the plural te) (e:a ~ aw, liinglawng un) (s:lungkimte) (b:lungmuang) (r:23.32.11) (q:draft)
lungmuanhuai = (t:adj) (w:safe/secure/reassuring) (d:giving peace of mind, free from danger; lungmuang at ease with huai, which marks what causes or deserves a feeling) (e:ka lampi ~ sak hi/note a dingin ~ zaw lai hi | it is safer for you/nang adingin ~-in launa om lo hi | you are safe and there is no danger) (s:lungmuang/bit) (a:lauhuai) (r:10.22.33/9.20.21/50.3.1) (q:draft)
lungmuanhuaina = (t:n) (w:safety/security) (d:lungmuanhuai safe with the noun suffix na; a lungmuanhuaina mun is a place of safety) (e:a ~ mun) (s:bitna/lungmuanna) (b:lungmuanhuai) (r:51.1.13) (q:draft)
lungmuanhuaisak = (t:v) (w:make secure/make safe) (d:lungmuanhuai safe with the causative sak) (e:ka lampi khempeuh ~ hi) (s:lungmuangsak/lungmuansak) (b:lungmuanhuai) (r:10.22.33) (q:draft)
lungmuanna = (t:n) (w:security/safety/confidence/peace of mind) (d:lungmuan be secure with the noun suffix na: freedom from fear and danger, a mind at rest) (e:Topa a zahtak mi in ~ nei a/nopna leh ~ om ding hi | there will be peace and security/~ sungah Israel bek teeng hi | Israel dwells alone in safety/ka thugenna a ngaite in ~ ngah ding a | those who listen to me will have security) (s:bitna/lungmuanhuaina) (a:launa/lunghimawhna) (b:lungmuan) (r:20.14.26/23.39.8/5.33.28/20.1.33) (q:draft)
lungmuannate = (t:n) (w:securities/things trusted in) (d:plural of lungmuanna; in the verse beside hauhna wealth, of what the wicked rely on) (e:hauhna le ~ haksa loin beimang ding) (b:lungmuanna) (r:26.7.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
lungmuansak = (t:v) (w:give security/make secure) (d:lungmuan be secure with the causative sak) (e:Sum in hong ~ bangin) (s:lungmuangsak/lungmuanhuaisak) (b:lungmuan) (r:21.7.12) (q:draft)
lungneemna = (t:n) (w:gentleness/meekness/patience) (d:lung heart with neem soft and the noun suffix na) (e:sin kiniamsakna, ~, heh baih lohna lungsimte/a ~ tawh a thuak leh | if he bore them with patience) (s:lungnemna) (a:lungkhauhna) (r:51.3.12/45.9.22) (q:draft)
lungnem = (t:adj) (w:meek/gentle/humble) (d:of a soft and mild heart, from lung, heart, and nem, soft) (e:A ~ mite in Pasian’ ciamsa leitang/Pasalpa Moses ~ mahmah a | the man Moses was very humble/I Pasian ~ mahmah a, hehpihna hong nei hi | our God is very tender and has mercy on us/a khial mite tungah ~ takin na sem thei | he can deal gently with those who go astray) (s:lungsimnem/nem) (a:lungkhauh) (r:40.5.5/4.12.3/42.1.78/58.5.2) (q:draft)
lungnemin = (t:adv) (w:meekly/patiently) (d:lungnem with in: with a gentle heart, without resisting) (e:~ na thuak uh leh/na thuak uh ciangin ~ na thuak uh leh | if you endure it patiently when you suffer) (b:lungnem) (r:60.2.20) (q:draft)
lungnemna = (t:n) (w:gentleness/meekness/humility) (d:noun from lungnem, a soft and gentle heart; also patience in waiting) (e:Khazih’ ~ leh hehpihna tawh/kiniamsakna tawh, ~ tawh, lungduaina tawh dimin | filled with humility, gentleness and patience/pilna, ~ tawh ama gamtatnate lak ta hen | let him show his deeds with wisdom and gentleness/~ tawh, thusimna lungsim tawh | with gentleness and respect) (s:lungneemna/nemna) (a:lungkhauhna) (b:lungnem) (r:47.10.1/49.4.2/59.3.13/60.3.15) (q:draft)
lungnemnate = (t:n) (w:gentleness/meekness) (d:lungnemna with te, which here closes a list of qualities) (e:thuakzawhna, ~ na phak matengin) (b:lungnemna) (r:54.6.11) (q:draft)
lungnemsak = (t:v) (w:please/win the favor of) (d:lungnem soft-hearted with the causative sak: soften the heart of someone, win them over; mite lungnemsak mi is one who pleases people) (e:Mite ~ mi bangin) (b:lungnem) (r:49.6.6) (q:draft)
lungnemte = (t:n) (w:the meek/the gentle/the humble) (d:lungnem with plural te) (e:~ in leitang luahin/Topa aw, ~ deihna na ngai ding hi | Lord, you hear the desire of the meek/a kiniamkhiat, mi ~ bek | only the humble and meek) (s:kiniamkhiatte/niamkhiatte) (a:kisatheite) (b:lungnem) (r:19.37.11/36.3.12/19.10.17) (q:draft)
lungnemzaw = (t:adj) (w:more humble/meeker) (d:lungnem humble with the comparative zaw) (e:mi khempeuh sangin a ~ ahi hi) (b:lungnem) (r:4.12.3) (q:draft)
lungngai = (t:v) (w:ponder/consider/think about) (d:think over in the heart; also have in mind or intend to do something) (e:a lungsim sungah a ~ hi/Bangci na ~ uh hiam | what do you think/bangci gamtatin a si uh teltakin ~ un la | consider carefully how they lived and died/na lungsim sung uhah ~ kei un | do not think in your hearts) (s:ngaihsun) (r:42.2.19/44.15.37/40.18.12/58.13.7/40.3.9) (q:draft)
Lungngai = (t:v) (w:remember/think about) (d:lungngai written with a capital at the start of a quoted line; with nawn lo it means remember no more) (e:~ nawn loin ka om ding hi) (b:lungngai) (r:58.10.17) (q:draft)
lungngaih = (t:v) (w:meditate/ponder/reflect) (d:think deeply about something; lungngaih kik is come to one’s senses) (e:Ka ~ ciangin ka lung so semsem hi/A ~ kik ciangin | when he came to his senses/amah in thu a ~ laitak | he is deep in thought) (b:lungngai) (r:19.39.3/42.15.17/11.18.27) (q:draft)
lungngaih = (t:n) (w:thought/intention) (d:what a person thinks or plans in the heart) (e:Ama ~ hoih lo pen ama lu tungah) (s:lungngaihna) (b:lungngai) (r:19.7.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
lungngaihna = (t:n) (w:thought/inner thought) (d:lungngaih ponder with the noun suffix na: what a person thinks in the heart) (e:mite’ selsim ~ a khen Ni ciangin/mi tampi a ~ a kilat nading | so that the thoughts of many are revealed) (b:lungngaih) (r:45.2.16/42.2.34) (q:draft)
lungngaihngaih = (t:v) (w:meditate on/keep thinking about) (d:lungngaih ponder, with the last part doubled) (e:Sun tawntungin ka ~ ahi hi/zanthapai-in kong ~ ciangin | when I meditate on you through the night) (s:lungngaingai/ngaihsunsun) (r:19.119.97/19.63.5) (q:draft)
lungngaingai = (t:v) (w:meditate/ponder/reflect on) (d:keep thinking something over; the doubled ngai shows continued action) (e:Nangma thuciamna a ~ dingin/na ngeina kipte ka ~ ding hi | I will meditate on your decrees/itna kip ~ ta hen | let him ponder the steadfast love/na teci pan’na ke’n ka ~ ding hi | I will ponder your statutes) (s:ngaihsunsun/lungngaihngaih) (r:19.119.148/19.145.5/19.119.48/19.107.43/19.119.95) (q:draft)
lungniam = (t:v) (w:be dismayed/be discouraged/be downcast) (d:lung heart with niam low: the heart sinks) (e:nang hong su a, na ~ hi) (s:lungkia/lungsi) (a:lungkip) (r:18.4.5) (q:draft)
Lungniamkhiat = (t:adj) (w:humble/meek) (d:lung heart with niam low and khiat; Lungniamkhiat mite are the humble) (e:~ mite in Topa sungah) (s:lungnem/lungsimniam) (r:23.29.19) (q:draft)
lungniamkhiatna = (t:n) (w:humility/humbleness) (d:lung heart, niam low and khiat bring down, with the noun suffix na: bringing the heart low) (e:~ na nei un) (s:kiniamkhiatna) (a:kisaktheihna/kiphatsakna) (r:60.3.8) (q:draft)
lungniamsakte = (t:n) (w:the humble) (d:those who make the heart low: lung heart, niam low, the causative sak and the plural te) (e:a ~ kiangah hehpihna thupha a pia hi) (s:kiniamkhiatte/lungnemte/niamkhiatte) (a:kisatheite) (r:60.5.5) (q:draft)
lungno = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:worm/maggot) (d:a small crawling creature such as a worm or maggot; also a picture of what is low and weak) (e:in ~ khat bang ka hi lel a/Pasian in tua umgui ~ khat nesak-a | God had a worm eat the plant/~ in samul puan a pehtum bangin | as a worm eats up wool) (s:than) (r:19.22.6/32.4.7/23.51.8) (q:draft)
lungnop = (t:v) (w:delight/be glad/be cheerful) (d:form of lungnuam used before nading and ciangin: be glad, cheerful or at ease in the heart) (e:Ka ~ nadingin la a sa ding/zu nekna hangin a ~ ciangin | when he was merry from drinking wine/ka ~ theih nadingin | so that I may be glad/note thu thei-in ka ~ tuam nadingin | so that I too may be cheered by news of you) (r:21.2.8/17.1.10/19.39.13/50.2.19)
lungnopmawhna = (t:n) (w:distress/offence/unease) (d:a heart that is not at ease: lung heart, nop pleasant, mawh hard or wrong, with the noun suffix na) (e:~ na piansak uhleh itna lungsim) (r:45.14.15) (q:draft)
lungnopmawhsak = (t:v) (w:offend/distress/cause to stumble) (d:make the heart of someone uneasy, with the causative sak) (e:na ~ loh nadingun na gamta un) (r:46.10.32) (q:draft)
lungnopna = (t:n) (w:peace/contentment/joy) (d:a glad and easy heart) (e:~ in pumpi cidamsak a/Nangma thu a deihte in ~ lianpi ngah uh | those who love your law have great peace/ka ~ leh ka kisaktheihna lukhu | my joy and my crown of pride/~ na zong ding uh a | you will seek peace) (s:lungdamna/nopna) (a:lungkhamna/dahna) (b:lungnop) (r:20.14.30/25.5.15/19.119.165/50.4.1/26.7.25) (q:draft)
lungnopnate = (t:n) (w:peace/joys) (d:plural of lungnopna, here of the kinds of peace the world gives) (e:a kip lo ~ pawl hi lo hi) (b:lungnopna) (r:43.14.27) (q:draft)
lungnopsak = (t:v) (w:refresh/gladden/cheer) (d:lungnop be glad at heart with the causative sak) (e:note hong ~ mah bangin) (s:lungnuamsak/lungdamsak) (a:lungkhamsak) (b:lungnop) (r:46.16.18) (q:draft)
lungnuam = (t:v) (w:delight/be glad/be at ease/be at peace) (d:lung heart with nuam pleasant: be glad and at ease; lungnuam takin means happily, in peace or safely) (e:~ takin kumpipa tawh pai in/a mite a ~ dingin ka bawl hi | I make its people to be glad/~ takin ka pa’ innah ka ciahkik leh | if I return safely to my father’s house/~ takin moh keu themkhat nekna | eating a little dry bread in peace) (s:lungdam) (a:lungkham) (r:17.5.14/23.65.18/1.28.21/20.17.1)
lungnuamin = (t:n) (w:integrity) (d:lungnuam with the ending in, used before a verb: gladly, at ease, in peace or safely, as in lungnuamin om, live in peace) (e:Thuman mite ~ om hithiat a | the upright live securely/zong ~ an a ne uh hi | they too ate with good cheer/meigong numeite ~ ka omsak hi | I made the widows glad) (r:20.10.9/44.27.36/18.29.13)
lungnuamsak = (t:v) (w:cheer/gladden/comfort/refresh) (d:lungnuam with causative sak: make someone glad or at ease) (e:tamveipi kei hong ~ ahih manin/a dahte ~ hi | he gladdens those who mourn/pasiante leh mite a ~ ka leenggahzu | my wine, which cheers gods and men/Note in nakpitakin kei na hong ~ uh a | you have greatly gladdened me) (s:lungnopsak/lungdamsak) (a:lungkhamsak) (b:lungnuam) (r:55.1.16/18.5.11/7.9.13/50.4.1) (q:draft)
lungphamawh = (t:v) (w:be concerned about/care for) (d:have something on the heart as a care or a need: lung heart with phamawh be of concern) (e:a nongek neite ka ~ hi) (r:1.33.13) (q:draft)
