lungsi = (t:v) (w:lose heart/be dismayed/falter) (d:literally the heart dies, lung heart with si die; said of sudden fear or loss of courage) (e:~ lo, lungkia lo ding hi/Hih thu hangin amaute ~ uh a | at this their hearts sank) (s:lungkia/lungniam) (a:lungkip) (r:23.42.4/1.42.28) (q:draft)
lungsiangtho = (t:n) (w:righteousness/purity of heart) (d:lung heart with siangtho holy, pure; in the verse the thing hungered for, righteousness in the English) (e:an duh banga ~ a deihte in) (r:40.5.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
