lususu = (t:adv) (d:describes the manner of lying asleep or drowsing on, in a row with lumlum lying about) (e:~ in om ding bek nuam) (r:23.56.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
lut = (t:v) (w:enter/go in) (d:go or come into a place; the place entered is usually marked with sungah, into, and the opposite is pusuak, go out) (e:Kongpi pan a ~ mi in tuucing ahi hi/Inn sungah na ~ uh ciangin | when you enter the house/inn sungah a ~ nuam kei hi | he would not go into the house/Zeisu Jerikho khuapi sungah ~ a | Jesus entered the city of Jericho) (s:sungtum) (a:pusuak/paikhiat) (r:43.10.2/40.12.9/40.10.12/42.15.28/42.19.1) (q:draft)
lutang = (t:n) (w:head) (d:the head of a person or animal, and also the head or leader of a tribe or family) (e:pumpeeng la-in a ~ a sat uh hi/amau’ ~ kolhsak ding hi | he will make their heads bald/Pumpeeng tawh ama ~ sat uh a | they struck his head with a staff/a beh sungah a ~ ahi mi khat | a man who is head of his clan) (s:lu) (b:lu) (r:40.27.30/1.3.15/23.3.17/41.15.19/4.1.4)
Lutang = (t:n) (w:head) (d:lutang written with a capital, at the start of a sentence or in a name; Lutang Guh, head bone, is the Skull, the name of the hill Golgotha) (e:Golgotha a kici ~ Guh mualah/~ sagih in tua numei tutna mual sagih ahi | the seven heads are the seven hills where the woman sits/~ ahi Khrih’ ukna tawh | under the rule of Christ, the head) (b:lutang) (r:43.19.17/66.17.9/51.2.19) (q:draft)
lutanga = (t:n) (w:on the head) (d:lutang head with a, on, at) (e:a ~ ki sawm leh) (b:lutang) (r:27.7.20) (q:draft)
Lutangguh = (t:n) (w:skull) (d:lutang head with guh bone; Lutangguh Mun is the Place of the Skull, Golgotha) (s:luguh) (r:41.15.22/43.19.17) (q:draft)
lutangin = (t:adv) (w:as head/as leader/as chief) (d:lutang, head, with the ending in: in the position of head over others) (e:note’ ~ amaute ka koih ding hi/minamte’ ~ kei nong bawl hi | you made me head of the nations/tuate khempeuh tungah nang a ~ hong kisangsak hi | you are exalted as head over all/amau’ ~ amah nei uh hi | they had him as their head) (b:lutang) (r:5.1.13/10.22.44/13.29.11/7.3.27) (q:draft)
lutangpi = (t:n) (w:head/chief) (d:lutang head with pi great: the one who is head over others) (e:amah a ~ hi lai hi) (b:lutang) (r:51.2.10) (q:draft)
lutangte = (t:n) (w:heads/chiefs/leaders) (d:lutang, head, with the plural te: the heads of tribes, clans and families, as in beh lutangte, clan heads, and innkuan lutangte, heads of families) (e:Moses in Israel minam ~ tungah/Hihte in amau’ innkuan ~ ahi hi | these were the heads of their families/Levi mi beh ~ ahi uh hi | they were heads of the Levite clans/Israel behte’ ~ ahi uh hi | they were the heads of the clans of Israel) (s:makaite/ukpite) (b:lutang) (r:4.30.1/13.9.34/2.6.14/4.1.16) (q:draft)
lutangte = (t:n) (w:heads) (d:lutang, head, with the plural te: the heads of people as parts of the body) (e:a galte’ ~ sukham ding hi/Oreb leh Ze-eb ~ paipih uh hi | they brought the heads of Oreb and Zeeb/kumpipa’ suan-le-khakte’ ~ hong paipih uh hi | they have brought the heads of the king’s sons) (s:lute) (b:lutang) (r:19.68.21/7.7.25/12.10.8) (q:draft)
lute = (t:n) (w:heads) (d:lu head, with the plural te) (e:A ~ tungah kumpilukhu sagih a nei hi/khua kongpite aw, na ~ uh sangsak un | lift up your heads, you gates) (s:lutangte) (b:lu) (r:66.12.3/19.24.7) (q:draft)
lutin = (t:v) (w:entering/going in/coming in) (d:lut with in, entering and then doing the next action) (e:Ka biakinn sungah amaute ~/Zekhariah’ innah ~ Elisabeth va hopih hi | she entered Zechariah’s house and greeted Elizabeth/Paul in kikhopna innah ~ | Paul entered the synagogue/mihonte mah tawh ~, amaute mah tawh pusuak khawm ding | he shall go in with the people and go out with them) (a:pusuakin) (b:lut) (r:26.44.16/42.1.40/44.19.8/26.46.10) (q:draft)
lutkhawm = (t:v) (w:enter together/go in with) (d:lut enter with khawm together) (e:biakna innpi sungah a ~ hi/mopawi bawlna sungah a ~ pah uh hi | they went in with him to the wedding feast/inntual dongah Jesuh tawh a ~ hi | he went into the courtyard with Jesus) (s:tumkhawm) (b:lut) (r:44.3.8/40.25.10/43.18.15) (q:draft)
lutkhit = (t:v) (w:have entered) (d:lut enter with khit, finished; lutkhit ciangin is after going in) (e:inn sungah a ~ ciangin/inn sungah a ~ uh ciangin | after they had gone into the house) (s:tumkhit) (r:44.9.17/41.9.33) (q:draft)
lutkik = (t:v) (w:go back in/re-enter/return into) (d:lut enter with kik, again or back) (e:khuapi sungah ka ~ hi/hih khua sungah ~ kei in | do not go back into this village/khua sungah a ~ hi | he went back into the town/Na paai sungah ~ inla | go back into your sheath) (b:lut) (r:16.2.15/24.47.6/41.8.26/44.14.20) (q:draft)
lutkikin = (t:v) (w:go back in/enter again) (d:lutkik with the linking suffix in) (e:kumpi inn huang sungah ~ Jesuh kiangah/A nu’ sungah ~ suakkik thei ding ahi hiam | can he enter his mother’s womb again and be born again) (b:lutkik) (r:43.19.9/43.3.4) (q:draft)
lutlah = (t:v) (w:fail to enter/fall short of entering) (d:lut enter with lah, not manage to) (e:a ~ na suahkhak loh nadingun) (r:58.4.1) (q:draft, low confidence)
lutlam = (t:n) (w:entering/way in) (d:lut enter with lam way, manner: the act of going in) (e:khuapi sungah a ~ uh) (r:10.17.17) (q:draft)
lutna = (t:n) (w:entrance/entry/way in) (d:lut, enter, with the noun suffix na: the place where one goes in, such as a gateway or doorway, or the act of entering) (e:kulh kongpi ~-ah ding uh hi/khuapi ~ lampi gei-ah | beside the road leading into the city/kikhopna puanbuk ~ ah kongcingpa ahi hi | he was gatekeeper at the entrance of the tent of meeting/kulh kongpi ~ dongah | as far as the entrance of the gate) (s:tumna) (a:pusuahna) (b:lut) (r:7.18.16/20.8.3/13.9.21/7.9.40) (q:draft)
lutnop = (t:v) (w:want to enter) (d:lut enter with nop want, the form of lutnuam used before leh, if) (e:sungah na ~ leh thukhamte na zui in) (r:40.19.17) (q:draft)
lutnuam = (t:v) (w:want to enter) (d:lut enter with nuam want) (e:Note lah na ~ kei uh a) (r:40.23.13) (q:draft)
lutnuamte = (t:n) (w:those who want to enter) (d:lutnuam want to enter with the plural te) (e:a ~ lah na lutsak kei uh hi) (b:lutnuam) (r:40.23.13) (q:draft)
lutol = (t:n) (w:bald head/bald crown) (d:lu head with tol bald: the bald top of the head, set beside talkolh, the bald forehead) (e:a ~ tung hitaleh a talkolh tung hitaleh) (r:3.13.42/3.13.43) (q:draft)
lutpa = (t:n) (w:possessed man) (d:lut enter with pa, marking a man: the man whom something has entered; found as dawi lutpa, a demon-possessed man) (e:dawi ~ in amah tawh omkhawm nading/dawi ~ in bangci cidamna ngah hiam | how the demon-possessed man was healed/dawigilo ~ in tuate tungah diangin | the man with the evil spirit jumped on them) (b:lut) (r:41.5.18/42.8.36/44.19.16) (q:draft)
lutpah = (t:v) (w:enter at once) (d:lut enter with pah, at once, immediately) (e:ama sungah Satan hong ~ hi) (s:tumpah) (r:43.13.27) (q:draft)
lutpih = (t:v) (w:bring in/take in) (d:lut, enter, with pih, do together with: go in taking a person or thing along, bring or carry in) (e:Ama innah ~ a, an vaak a/galkap huang sungah Paul a ~ dektak laitakun | as they were about to take Paul into the barracks/Jerusalem khua kongpite-ah bangmah hong ~ kei un | do not bring anything in through the gates of Jerusalem/Hanan’ tate’ inndei sungah ka ~ hi | I brought them into the room of the sons of Hanan) (s:tumpih) (b:lut) (r:44.16.34/24.17.21/44.21.37/24.35.4) (q:draft)
lutsak = (t:v) (w:let in/bring in/send into/admit) (d:lut, enter, with sak, cause or allow: let someone in, bring in or send into a place) (e:Piter a ~ hi/vok hon sungah hong ~ in | send us into the herd of pigs/a numei’ pa in amah ~ lo hi | her father would not let him go in/a khuapi sung uh ah amaute ~ kei un | do not let them enter their cities) (s:tumsak) (b:lut) (r:43.18.16/7.15.1/40.8.31/6.10.19) (q:draft)
lutsate = (t:n) (w:those who have entered) (d:lut enter with sa, already, and plural te; NIV has her guests) (e:a ~ sihna gam thuk sungah a om) (r:20.9.18) (q:draft)
lutsim = (t:v) (w:slip in/creep in/enter secretly) (d:lut enter with sim, secretly) (e:note’ lakah hong ~ uh hi) (s:simlut/tumsim) (r:65.1.4) (q:draft)
lutsuk = (t:v) (w:go down into/go in/enter) (d:lut, enter, with suk, downward) (e:kha lei-ah ~ hi/Mi sungah a pua lam pan a ~ na | a thing that goes into a person from outside/teembaw sung a tawng lamah na ~ a | he had gone down into the bottom of the ship/ahi zongin ~ lo hi | but he did not go in) (a:kahto) (b:lut) (r:21.3.21/32.1.5/41.7.15/43.20.5) (q:draft)
lutsukin = (t:v) (w:go down into/go inside) (d:lutsuk with the linking suffix in) (e:Jonah na ~ a na ihmu hithiat hi/nungzui dang pa zong ~ a thupiangte mu | the other disciple also went in and saw what had happened) (b:lutsuk) (r:32.1.5/43.20.8) (q:draft)
lutsukpah = (t:v) (w:go straight down into) (d:lut enter with suk downward and pah at once) (e:han sungah a ~ hi) (r:43.20.6) (q:draft)
lutte = (t:n) (w:those who enter) (d:lut, enter, with the plural te: the people who go in) (e:leitaw lam kongpi panin a ~/Leilu lam kongpi panin a ~ | those who enter by the north gate) (b:lut) (r:26.46.9) (q:draft)
lutte = (t:n) (w:possessed people) (d:in dawi lutte, those whom demons have entered, the demon-possessed) (e:a sungah dawi ~ Zeisu kiangah paipih/dawi ~’ thu a kipan thu khempeuh | everything, including what happened to the demon-possessed) (b:lut) (r:41.1.32/40.8.33) (q:draft)
lutthei = (t:v) (w:can enter/be able to enter) (d:lut enter with thei be able) (e:tua khuapi sungah ~ ding uh hi/a gamtateng bek ~ ding uh hi | only those who do it will be able to enter/Pasian’ Ukna sungah ~ het lo ding hi | will never be able to enter the kingdom of God/vantung ki-ukna sungah ~ kim lo ding uh | not all will be able to enter the kingdom of heaven) (b:lut) (r:66.21.27/40.7.21/46.6.10) (q:draft)
luttheih = (t:v) (w:be able to enter) (d:the form of lutthei used before nading; luttheih nading is so that one may enter, the right to enter) (e:Tua vokte sungah a ~ nadingun/Siangtho Pen Munah ut utin ~ nading | to be able to enter the Most Holy Place freely/Khuapi kulhkongpi sungah a ~ nading | so that they may enter through the city gates/hih lai-ah hong bangci ~ na hi hiam | how were you able to come in here) (b:lutthei) (r:42.8.32/58.10.19/66.22.14/40.22.12) (q:draft)
