lutuk = (t:v) (w:fall headlong) (d:lu head with tuk fall: fall head first, a fall worse than puk, stumble) (e:Amah a puk hangin ~ lo ding hi) (r:19.37.24) (q:draft)
lutung = (t:n) (w:head/top of the head) (d:lu, head, and tung, top or upon, mostly of something that is put or falls on the head of a person) (e:a ~ uh ah a khut uh nga-in/Na ~ uha om na sammal | the hairs on your head/Ama sisan Joab ~ leh ama innkuante khempeuh tungah | his blood on the head of Joab and on all his family/Haman’ ~ mah a lehtuk nading | to come back on Haman’s own head) (s:luzang) (r:44.6.6/10.3.29/42.12.7/17.9.25) (q:draft)
lutunga = (t:n) (w:on the head) (d:lutung top of the head with a, on, at) (e:leihoih zangkuam i ~ kisuang) (b:lutung) (r:23.28.1) (q:draft)
lutungah = (t:n) (w:on the head/upon the head) (d:lutung top of the head, with the place marker ah) (e:sathau thawl khat la-in ama ~ buak a/a ~ a khut koihin paikhia a | she put her hand on her head and went away/ulian ahi mipa’ ~ tung hen | let it come on the head of the prince) (b:lutung) (r:9.10.1/10.13.19/5.33.16) (q:draft)
lutzawh = (t:v) (w:be able to enter) (d:lut enter with zawh be able; a lutzawh lohna is their not being able to enter) (e:a ~ lohna uh i thei hi) (r:58.3.19) (q:draft)
luum = (t:v) (w:be stirred/be in an uproar) (d:in luum lialua, of a whole town moved and noisy with excitement) (e:a khuazangpi-un ~ lialua uh hi) (r:8.1.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
