luzang = (t:n) (w:crown of the head/top of the head) (d:the crown or top of the head; a khenuai a kipan a luzang dongin is from the sole of the foot to the top of the head) (e:a khetul pan a ~ dongin/A khenuai a kipan a ~ dongin | from the sole of his foot to the crown of his head/na khenuai panun na ~ dong uhah | from the soles of your feet to the top of your head/ama gamtatsia pen ama ~ mah ah tu hi | his violence comes down on his own head) (s:lutung) (a:khenuai) (r:18.2.7/5.28.35/10.14.25/19.7.16) (q:draft)
luzepnate = (t:n) (w:tops/capitals) (d:lu head with zepna, ornament, and plural te: the ornamented tops of posts) (e:tuate’ ~ kham tawh zutin) (r:2.36.38) (q:draft)
