Maakath = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Maakath/Maakathite) (d:the Maakathites, the people of the small kingdom of Maakah beside Geshur, east of the Jordan) (r:5.3.14/13.4.19)
maan = (t:adj) (w:true/honest/right/just) (d:true, right or honest, without falsehood, said of scales, words, paths and offerings; often a maan before the noun) (e:A ~ tawikhaina leh tawitehnate/Ka thugente a ~ bekbek hi | my words are nothing but true/A ~ biakna piaknate lui un | offer right sacrifices/tua hi leh lampi ~ hong lak ding hi | then he will show you the right path) (s:man/dik) (a:manlo) (r:20.16.11/20.8.7/19.4.5/20.3.6) (q:draft)
maan = (t:v) (w:reign/rule/be king) (d:to reign as king; in the verses written maan’ with an apostrophe, before laitakin for during the reign of, or before zawh, as in a maan’ zawh kum li, the fourth year of his reign) (e:Zedekiah a ~’ zawh kum sawm/Kumpipa Josiah a ~’ laitakin | during the reign of King Josiah/Judah kumpipa Hezekiah a ~’ laitakin | while Hezekiah king of Judah reigned/Jehoiakim a ~’ zawh kum li | the fourth year of the reign of Jehoiakim) (s:maang) (r:24.39.2/24.26.18/24.3.6/24.36.1) (q:draft)
maana = (t:n) (w:manna) (d:manna, the bread from heaven that God gave Israel in the wilderness, the borrowed word in one of its Zolai spellings) (e:a kiseel ~ ahi zongin) (s:manna/mana) (r:66.2.17) (q:draft)
maang = (t:n) (w:vision) (d:something seen in a vision or trance, most often with mu, see: maang ka mu hi is I saw a vision) (e:Ka ~ sungah, Pasian in Israel/a nih veina ~ ka mu hi | I saw a second vision/ka ~-a ka muh bang teekteekin | exactly as I had seen in my vision/thu ngenin ka om laitakin ~ ka mu hi | while I was praying I saw a vision) (s:maangmuhna/mangmuhna/maangmu/mumaang) (r:26.40.2/26.8.4/27.8.1/44.22.17) (q:draft)
maang = (t:v) (w:reign/rule/be king) (d:to reign as king or ruler, said of God and of kings) (e:Minamte tungah Pasian ~ hi/Khazih in a ~ ding hi | Christ will reign/thumanna tawh kumpi khat hong ~ ding a | a king will reign in righteousness/Jakob’ tungah Pasian ~ hi | God rules over Jacob) (s:maan) (r:19.47.8/46.15.25/23.32.1/19.59.13) (q:draft)
maangin = (t:v) (w:reign/be king) (d:maang, reign, with the linking suffix in, which joins it to the verb that follows: he will reign and) (e:Na tapa Solomon in keima nungah ~/Keima nungah Adonijah ~ ka kumpi tokhom tungah | Adonijah will reign after me, on my throne/David kumpi tokhom tungah ~ ama gam sungah | reigning on the throne of David over his kingdom) (b:maang) (r:11.1.17/23.9.7/11.1.24) (q:draft)
maangkhawm = (t:v) (w:reign together/reign with) (d:to reign together with someone, from maang, reign, and khawm, together) (e:amah tawh i ~ ding hi) (s:ukkhawm) (b:maang) (r:55.2.12) (q:draft)
maangmu = (t:n) (w:vision) (d:something seen in a vision, also the seeing of it; maangmu kineih is to pretend to have visions) (e:Zuau thu tawh ~ kineihin/amau’ lungsim bangin thugen tawmin, ~ kineih uh hi | they speak from their own mind and pretend to have visions/~ ahi hiam ka thei kei hi | whether it was a vision I do not know) (s:maangmuhna/mangmuhna/maang/mumaang) (r:26.13.9/47.12.3/26.13.3/47.12.2) (q:draft)
maangmuh = (t:n) (w:vision) (d:something seen as in a dream and taken as a message from God) (e:~ ommun lo hi/Na ~ pen hun beina ding lahna ahi hi | your vision shows the time of the end/Zan ka ~ hun sungin ka khuadak leh | in my vision at night I looked/ka ~ masak sunga ka muh mipa Gabriel | Gabriel, the man I had seen in my earlier vision) (s:maangmuhna/mangmuh/maang/maangmu) (b:maangmu) (r:9.3.1/27.8.19/27.7.13/27.9.21) (q:draft)
maangmuhna = (t:n) (w:vision/revelation) (d:something seen in a vision or a dream, a revelation from God; maangmuh with the noun suffix na) (e:a lauhuai ~ tawh nong lausak hi/hih ~ khempeuh tawh a kizui-in | in accordance with all this revelation/mang le ~ sungah Pasian in thu a gen hi | God speaks in dreams and visions/A ~ Eli’ kiangah a gen ding Samuel lau hi | Samuel was afraid to tell Eli the vision) (s:mangmuhna/maangmuh/maangmu/maang) (b:maangmuh) (r:18.7.14/26.12.24/10.7.17/18.33.15/9.3.15) (q:draft)
maangmuhnate = (t:n) (w:visions) (d:plural of maangmuhna: the visions that a prophet sees) (e:Na ~ uh zuaupi hi a/Amaute’ ~ in zuaupi hi a | their visions are false/Ka ~ in hong linglawng sakin | my visions troubled me/tua zan a ka ~ ka ciaptehna | my record of the visions I saw that night) (s:mangmuhnate) (b:maangmuhna) (r:26.13.7/27.7.1/26.13.6/27.7.15) (q:draft)
maangte = (t:n) (w:officials/officers/eunuchs) (d:plural of maang, a ruler or official; innsung maangte are the officials of the palace, called eunuchs in the English versions) (e:tulguk pen ~ le thukhente hi ding a/Inn sung ~ nih khawng thum khawng in | two or three palace officials/Babilon kumpipa’ inn sungah innsung ~ hi ding uh hi | they will be eunuchs in the palace of the king of Babylon) (s:mangte/innsungmangte/uliante) (b:maang) (r:13.23.4/12.9.32/12.20.18) (q:draft)
maanin = (t:adv) (w:rightly/justly/uprightly/truly) (d:in a right, just or true way, from maan, true or right, with the adverb suffix in; a maanin gamta is to act rightly) (e:thu a ~ ka khen ding hi/Siatna peelin a ~ gamta in la | avoid evil and walk rightly/a ~ gamtat ding thei thei tuan lo uh | they still do not learn to act rightly/Ahih hangin a mawhsakna thu ~ | but if the charge is true) (s:thumanin/diktakin) (a:khialin) (b:maan) (r:19.75.2/20.4.27/23.26.10/5.22.20) (q:draft)
maanna = (t:n) (w:reign/seat of rule) (d:the reign of a king or the place where he reigns, from maan, reign, with the noun suffix na; a maanna ngei is where he once reigned) (e:Sihon kumpipa a ~ ngei Heshbon khua) (b:maan) (r:24.48.45) (q:draft)
maap = (t:v) (w:spare/pity) (d:to hold back from killing or harming someone out of pity; in the verses it is always negated with kei) (e:A tangvalte uh ~ kei unla/hehpih loin, zong a ~ kei ding a | he will show no mercy and will not spare them) (s:hehpih/khasiat) (r:24.51.3/24.21.7) (q:draft)
maapai = (t:v) (w:prosper/succeed) (d:to go forward and do well, from maa, success, and pai, go) (e:tua hangin amaute ~ lo uh a) (s:maavang/mavang/daupai) (r:24.10.21) (q:draft)
Maarath = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Maarath) (d:town in the hill country of Judah) (r:6.15.59)
Maasai = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Maasai) (d:a priest, son of Adiel, who lived in Jerusalem after the exile) (r:13.9.12)
Maaseiah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Maaseiah) (d:name of many men, among them a Levite musician in the time of David and a priest at the dedication of the wall of Jerusalem) (r:16.12.42/13.15.18)
Maath = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Maath) (d:an ancestor of Jesus in the genealogy of Luke) (r:42.3.26)
maavang = (t:v) (w:prosper/succeed/be successful) (d:to prosper or succeed, said of a person or of work that goes well, from maa, success, and vang; also written mavang) (e:a sepna khempeuhah ~ hi/na lungdamin na ~ ding hi | you will be happy and prosper/na nasep peuhpeuh ~ ding hi | all your work will succeed/na hihnate uhah na ~ kei ding uh hi | you will not succeed in what you do) (s:mavang/maapai/daupai/vang) (r:12.18.7/19.128.2/20.4.26/5.28.29) (q:draft)
maavanna = (t:n) (w:success/prosperity) (d:success or prosperity, from maavang, prosper, in the form maavan before the noun suffix na) (e:kote tungah ~ hong pia in/Tu-in kei tungah ~ hong pia inla | give me success today/a ~ ding uh hanciam kei un | do not seek their prosperity) (s:daupaina/maa) (r:23.26.12/16.1.11/15.9.10) (q:draft)
Maaz = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Maaz) (d:son of Ram, the firstborn of Jerahmeel, of the tribe of Judah) (r:13.2.27) (q:draft)
Maaziah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Maaziah) (d:head of the twenty-fourth division of priests in the time of David; also a priest who sealed the covenant with Nehemiah) (r:16.10.8/13.24.18)
maban = (t:n) (w:continuation/what lies ahead/the rest) (d:the part still ahead of a work or course already begun; maban zom is carry on what others began, maban sem is go on with the work ahead) (e:i pu i pate’ ~ zomto vet un/Pai san in la, na ~ sem in | pass it by and go on your way/Mi khatpeuh in a patsa nasep ~ | the rest of a work that someone else has begun/ama thusia sawmna a ~ sot sak kei in | do not let his evil plan go any further) (r:40.23.32/20.4.15/45.15.20/19.140.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
Madai = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Madai) (d:son of Japheth, ancestor of the Medes) (r:1.10.2)
madawk = (t:adj) (w:foremost/at the front) (d:being at the front or the nearest edge; a madawk teng is the foremost part, in Numbers the outskirts of the camp as seen from a height) (e:amaute a ~ teng bek na mu ding/Israel mi a ~ pente gal muh thei hi | he could see from afar the foremost of the Israelites) (r:4.23.13/4.22.41) (q:draft, low confidence)
madawkah = (t:adv) (w:at the front/in the front line) (d:madawk foremost with ah, at: at the very front, in the verse of a battle) (e:~ Uriah koih in la) (s:madawkin) (b:madawk) (r:10.11.15) (q:draft)
madawkin = (t:adv) (w:forward/in front/at the front) (d:madawk foremost with in; hong madawkin is coming forward) (e:a ~ Uriah koih inla/kha khat hong ~ Topa’ mai-ah ding a | a spirit came forward and stood before the Lord) (s:madawkah) (b:madawk) (r:10.11.15/11.22.21) (q:draft)
madawkte = (t:n) (w:front ranks/those in front/vanguard) (d:madawk foremost with plural te; the front part of an army, set against nungdalte the rear) (e:A ~ in a haltum thei meikuang/a ~ uh nisuahna tuipi sungah khia-in | throwing its front ranks into the eastern sea) (a:nungdalte) (b:madawk) (r:29.2.3/29.2.20) (q:draft)
madiak = (t:adv) (w:just before/shortly before) (d:ma before with diak: a little short of, just before reaching a place) (e:Efrath tun’ ~, Kanaan gam) (r:1.48.7) (q:draft)
madiakin = (t:adv) (w:just before/shortly before) (d:madiak just before with in; a tun madiakin is when he had almost arrived) (e:Jesuh a tun ~ galkap bupa in) (b:madiak) (r:42.7.6) (q:draft)
Madmannah = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Madmannah) (d:town in the far south of Judah) (r:6.15.31/13.2.49)
Madmen = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Madmen) (d:a town of Moab named in the prophecy of Jeremiah against Moab) (r:24.48.2) (q:draft)
Madmenah = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Madmenah) (d:town north of Jerusalem whose people fled before the Assyrian advance) (r:23.10.31)
Madon = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Madon) (d:Canaanite royal city in the north whose king Jobab joined Jabin of Hazor against Joshua) (r:6.11.1)
Magadan = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Magadan) (d:place on the shore of the Sea of Galilee to which Jesus went by boat) (r:40.15.39)
Magbish = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Magbish) (d:town whose people returned from the exile with Zerubbabel) (r:15.2.30)
Magdala = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Magdala) (d:town on the western shore of the Sea of Galilee, home of Mary Magdalene) (r:40.27.61/41.15.47)
Magdalene = (t:name) (w:Magdalene) (d:byname of Mary of Magdala, a follower of Jesus from whom seven demons had gone out) (r:42.8.2/42.24.10)
Magdiel = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Magdiel) (d:one of the chiefs of Edom descended from Esau) (r:1.36.43/13.1.54)
Magog = (t:name) (c:male/land) (w:Magog) (d:son of Japheth; also the land of Gog in the prophecy of Ezekiel) (r:1.10.2)
Magpiash = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Magpiash) (d:one of the leaders of the people who sealed the covenant with Nehemiah) (r:16.10.20)
mah = (t:ppm) (d:postpositional marker to indicate objective case) (e:tua pen ~ hoih/amaute’ mawhna ~ thuaksak ding hi | he will make them bear their own guilt/a etna mun ~ en denin | staring on at the very spot he was looking at) (r:28.12.14/12.8.11)
mah = (t:ppm) (d:postpositional marker to indicate selective case) (e:tua ~~/Khazih in pawlpi a it ~ bangin | just as Christ loved the church/Moses in tua ni ~-in mite thuhilhin | on that same day Moses instructed the people/Josef khiat ~ bangin an huanpipa khailum hi | he hanged the chief baker just as Joseph had interpreted/Tua ~ bangin siampi liante | in the same way the chief priests) (r:49.5.25/5.27.11/1.40.22/40.27.41)
mahah = (t:ppm) (w:right in/right at) (d:emphatic mah with the place marker ah, in, at or upon that very place or person) (e:ama mawhna thang sung ~ amah awk hi/ama tung ~ kithuk kik ding a | it shall be done back to that very person/lutna kong zong tua lam ~ om hi | the entrance too was on that same side/tua lai ~ kivui hi | she was buried right there) (b:mah) (r:20.5.22/3.24.19/26.42.4/4.20.1) (q:draft)
Mahalab = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Mahalab) (d:town on the border of the territory of Asher, near Akzib) (r:6.19.29)
Mahalale = (t:see) <Mahalale-el>
Mahalale-el = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mahalalel) (d:son of Kenan and father of Jared in the line from Adam to Noah, an ancestor of Jesus) (e:~ in Kainan’ ta hi) (r:42.3.37) (q:draft)
Mahalaleel = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mahalalel) (d:son of Kenan and father of Jared in the line from Adam to Noah, an ancestor of Jesus) (r:42.3.37)
Mahalalel = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mahalalel) (d:son of Kenan and father of Jared in the line from Adam to Noah) (r:1.5.12)
Mahalate = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mahalate/Mahalalel) (d:first part of Mahalate-el, a spelling of Mahalalel, the father of Jared, in the genealogy of Luke) (r:42.3.37)
Mahalath = (t:name) (c:male/female) (w:Mahalath) (d:name of two women: a daughter of Ishmael whom Esau married, and a granddaughter of David who married Rehoboam) (r:1.28.9)
Mahalelel = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mahalalel) (d:son of Kenan and father of Jared in the line from Adam to Noah) (r:1.5.16)
Mahanaim = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Mahanaim) (d:town east of the Jordan in Gilead, where Ish-Bosheth ruled and where David stayed during the revolt of Absalom) (r:6.13.26/11.4.14)
Mahanasim = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Mahanaim) (d:a spelling of Mahanaim, the town east of the Jordan in Gilead) (r:6.13.30)
Mahanehdan = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Mahaneh Dan) (d:place between Zorah and Eshtaol, west of Kiriath Jearim, where the men of Dan camped; the name means camp of Dan) (r:7.13.25/7.18.12)
Maharai = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Maharai) (d:one of David's mighty warriors, from Netophah, commander of the army division for the tenth month) (r:10.23.28/13.11.30)
Mahath = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mahath) (d:name of two Levites, a Kohathite son of Amasai and a temple overseer in the time of Hezekiah) (r:14.29.12/14.31.13)
Mahavah = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Mahavah/Mahavite) (d:place from which Eliel, one of David's mighty warriors, came; the NIV has Eliel the Mahavite) (r:13.11.46)
Mahazioth = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mahazioth) (d:son of Heman, a temple musician in the time of David) (r:13.25.4)
Mahershalahashbaz = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Maher-Shalal-Hash-Baz) (d:son of the prophet Isaiah, whose name means quick to the plunder, swift to the spoil) (r:23.8.3/23.8.1)
Mahershalalhasbaz = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Maher-Shalal-Hash-Baz) (d:son of the prophet Isaiah, whose name means quick to the plunder, swift to the spoil) (r:23.8.3/23.8.1)
Mahil = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mahli) (d:son of Merari and grandson of Levi, a spelling of Mahli) (r:13.6.29)
mahin = (t:ppm) (w:very/same/just) (d:emphatic mah with the marker in; after a time word, on that very day, at that very time, just now) (e:Tua ni ~ Faro in nasem ukte/tua ni ~ ama ngaihsutnate bei ta hi | on that very day his plans come to nothing/tu kum sung ~ na si ding hi | within this very year you will die/Tu ~ kei nong sam a | just now you have called to me) (b:mah) (r:2.5.6/24.3.4/19.146.4/24.28.16) (q:draft)
Mahlah = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Mahlah) (d:eldest of the five daughters of Zelophehad of the tribe of Manasseh; also a child of Hammoleketh in the same tribe) (r:4.36.11/4.26.33)
Mahli = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mahli) (d:name of two Levites, a son of Merari and a son of Mushi) (r:13.6.47)
Mahlon = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mahlon) (d:son of Elimelek and Naomi, the first husband of Ruth) (r:8.1.2/8.1.5)
mahmah = (t:adv) (w:the very thing/very/indeed) (d:emphasises the word before it: after a describing word or verb it means very or indeed, after a noun the very one) (e:Pasian bawlsate ~ hoih lua ing/mipil suak lecin, ka lungdam ~ ding hi | if you become wise I will be very glad/ama thupiaknate muan’taak ~ hi | his commands are very trustworthy/ka hun nai ~ ta a | my time is now very near/ama nasepna ka phattuampih ~ hi | his work is very helpful to me) (s:nakpi/nakpitakin) (r:20.23.15/19.111.7/18.16.22/55.4.11)
mahmah = (t:adv) (w:exactly) (d:marks the word before it as exactly the one meant: that very night, the very word, I myself) (e:Tua zan ~ in Babilon kumpipa Belshazzar kithat a | that very night Belshazzar king of Babylon was killed/Tu ni ~-in Nob khua-ah galte tungin | this very day the enemy reaches Nob/Pasian’ kammal ~ bangin kingaihsun hi | it was regarded as the very word of God/Kei ~ in tua mipa ka maisiat ding a | I myself will set my face against that man) (s:teekteek) (r:27.5.30/23.10.32/10.16.23/3.20.3)
mahmah = (t:adj) (w:only/just) (e:Nangma tung ~-ah khialin/na maitang ~-ah nang hong samsia pah ding hi | he will curse you right to your face/ka muhna ~-ah om gige uh hi | they are always right before my eyes) (r:19.51.4/18.1.11/28.7.2)
mahmaha = (t:adv) (w:very/exceedingly/greatly) (d:mahmah, very, with a linking it to the verb that follows) (e:Gim ~ nasem zaw mi/Tui kihot pha ~ kiliing ahih ciangin | because we were tossed so violently by the storm) (s:mahmahin/nakpi/nakpitakin) (b:mahmah) (r:47.11.23/44.27.18) (q:draft)
mahmahah = (t:adv) (w:right at/at the very) (d:mahmah, exactly, with the place marker ah: at the very place, right in or on) (e:kongkhak gei ~ om uh a/hih lai ~ hong pia in | give it to me right here/Kumpi khua Susa khuapi sung ~ | right inside the royal city of Susa/Khrih tung ~ a khial na hi uh hi | you sin against Christ himself) (s:takah) (b:mahmah) (r:44.5.9/40.14.8/17.9.6/46.8.12) (q:draft)
mahmahin = (t:adv) (w:very/exceedingly/greatly) (d:mahmah, very, with the adverb suffix in, after a describing word or verb: very, greatly) (e:nuam ~ Topa a tungsak hi/Faro' kiang panin amah heh ~ paikhia hi | he left Pharaoh in great anger/A nungzuite dah ~ | the disciples were very sad/a haihuai ~ ka gamta khin hi | I have acted very foolishly) (s:mahmaha/nakpi/nakpitakin) (b:mahmah) (r:42.19.6/4.11.10/2.11.8/40.26.22/13.21.8) (q:draft)
mahmahin = (t:adv) (w:on that very) (d:after a time word: tua ni mahmahin is on that very day, tu mahmahin is right now) (e:Tua ni ~ Topa in Moses kiangah/Tua ni ~ Abraham leh a tapa Ishmaelte | on that very day Abraham and his son Ishmael/tua ni ~ amaute’ vun dawn atsak hi | on that very day he circumcised them/tu ~ nang hong that khinin | by now I would have killed you) (b:mahmah) (r:5.32.48/1.17.26/1.17.23/4.22.33) (q:draft)
mahmahlam = (t:adv) (w:how very) (d:mahmah very with lam way, manner, after a descriptive word: how very much it is so) (e:nuntak hun a tom ~ hong phawk in) (r:19.89.47) (q:draft, low confidence)
mahmahna = (t:part) (d:intensifier mahmah with the noun-forming suffix na; the phrase before it becomes a noun meaning great or extreme, as in heh mahmahna, great anger) (e:lau ~ tawh a liing kawmsa-in/Vanglian Pasian’ heh ~ tawh | with the great wrath of God Almighty/a keu ~ ka mu hi | I saw that they were very dry/Kush gam mite a lau ~ | the great fear of the people of Cushan) (b:mahmah) (r:26.12.18/26.37.2/66.19.15/35.3.7) (q:draft)
mahmahpa = (t:n) (w:the very one) (d:mahmah very, truly with pa marking a man: the man who truly did what the verb before it says) (e:a gitloh gamtat ~ in keimah ka hi hi) (b:mahmah) (r:13.21.17) (q:draft, low confidence)
mahmahpi = (t:see) <mahmahpi-in>
mahmahpi-in = (t:adv) (w:exceedingly/very greatly) (d:mahmah very with pi great and in making an adverb, after a descriptive word) (e:a zumhuai ~ a gamta uh hi) (s:mahmahin) (r:45.1.24) (q:draft)
mahmahsa = (t:adv) (w:very much/greatly) (d:mahmah very, with sa, already: of a state fully reached) (e:a heh ~-in a paikhia hi/note ka hong muan gen ~ ahih manin | because I have spoken of you so very confidently) (s:mahmahin) (b:mahmah) (r:2.11.8/47.9.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
