maisiatin = (t:v) (w:set one's face against/be hostile to) (d:maisiat with the linking suffix in) (e:mipa le ama innkuanpihte ~) (b:maisiat) (r:3.20.5) (q:draft)
maisuah = (t:n) (w:countenance/expression/look) (d:the look on the face that shows what one feels) (e:a ~ dahmai nawn lo hi/a ~ uh dahmai mahmah lai hi | their faces were still very sad/Migilo in kiphatsakna ~ tawh | the wicked, with a proud look) (s:maiput/maipuak) (r:9.1.18/42.24.17/19.10.4) (q:draft)
maitai = (t:adj) (w:cheerful/radiant/bright-faced) (d:of a bright, glad face; maitai takin is cheerfully; in Proverbs 7:13 of a bold face put on) (e:Khatlekhat ~ takin zinleleeng na kido un/Amah en un la, ~ un | look to him and be radiant/nangmah in mu-in na ~ ding a | you will look and be radiant/~ takin hih ni | let us do it cheerfully) (a:maigum/maimial) (r:60.4.9/19.34.5/23.60.5/45.12.8) (q:draft)
maitaii = (t:v) (w:be cheerful/brighten) (d:of the face, be bright and glad) (e:Kumpipa ~ leh nuntakna hi a) (a:maikhing) (r:20.16.15) (q:draft)
maitaiina = (t:n) (w:brightness/cheerfulness) (d:maitaii be bright of face with the noun suffix na) (e:khuamial ni hi a, ~ om lo) (s:maitaina) (a:maigumna) (b:maitaii) (r:30.5.20) (q:draft)
maitaina = (t:n) (w:cheerfulness/cheerful look/brightness) (d:maitai cheerful, bright of face with the noun suffix na; in Amos 5:20 brightness as opposed to gloom) (e:~ in lung nuamsak a/~ in ci damsak a | cheerfulness makes the body well/~ a om lo lungzin’ ni ahi hi | it is a day of gloom with no brightness) (s:maitaiina) (a:maigumna) (b:maitai) (r:20.15.30/30.5.20/20.17.22) (q:draft)
maitaisak = (t:v) (w:brighten the face/make cheerful) (d:maitai cheerful, with the causative sak) (e:Pilna in mipilte ~ a/Lungdamna in ~ a | joy makes the face cheerful) (s:taiisak) (a:maigumsak) (b:maitai) (r:21.8.1/20.15.13) (q:draft)
maitang = (t:n) (w:face) (d:the face of a person or of God; maitang kituahin is face to face) (e:a ~ a mu ding uh hi/~ li leh kha li nei ciat uh hi | each had four faces and four wings/na ~ hong taangsak in | make your face shine/a ~ a seel Topa | the Lord who hides his face) (s:mai) (r:66.22.4/26.1.6/19.119.135/23.8.17)
maitang = (t:n) (w:surface) (d:the outer face of a thing, most often lei maitang, the surface of the ground) (e:leitung ~ khempeuh ah a om/lei ~ khempeuh a buah hunin | when it watered the whole surface of the ground/lei ~ panin tuite a kiam khin | the waters had gone down from the surface of the ground) (r:1.1.29/1.2.6/1.8.8)
maitangah = (t:adv) (w:in the presence of/before/on the face) (d:maitang face with the place marker ah) (e:Mite ~ vantung panin leitung dongin/keimah ~ tham loin | not only in my presence/ka khialh simnate uh na ~ na koih hi | you set our secret sins before your face/Moses’ ~ a kilang vangliatna hangin | because of the glory that shone on the face of Moses) (b:maitang) (r:66.13.13/50.2.12/19.90.8/47.3.7) (q:draft)
maitangte = (t:n) (w:faces) (d:maitang face with plural te) (e:a ~ uh meikuang bang ding hi/Khebar Gun gei-a ka muhsa ~ mah tawh kibang | the same as the faces I had seen by the Kebar River) (b:maitang) (r:23.13.8/26.10.22) (q:draft)
maitheih = (t:v) (w:be forgiven/be pardoned) (d:mai forgive with theih, can; mawhna a maitheih nading is for the forgiveness of sin) (e:i mawhna a ~ nadingin a Tapa/Israel mite’ mawhna a ~ nadingin | so that the sins of the Israelites may be forgiven) (s:kimaisak) (r:62.4.10/26.45.17) (q:draft)
maitheihna = (t:n) (w:forgiveness/atonement) (d:maitheih be forgiven with the noun suffix na; mawhnate a maitheihna ding is for the forgiveness of sins) (e:na mawhnate uh a ~ ding ahi hi) (s:maisakna/mawhmaisakna) (b:maitheih) (r:26.45.15) (q:draft)
maivil = (t:v) (w:seek the favour of/court) (d:come to someone with gifts to win his goodwill) (e:letsong tawh nang hong ~ ding uh hi) (r:19.45.12) (q:draft)
maizum = (t:adj) (w:ashamed) (d:feeling shame, from mai, face, and zum, be ashamed; maizum sak is put to shame) (e:guaktangin om uh a, ~ lo uh hi/Na gamtatnasate hangin na ~ ding a | you will be ashamed because of what you have done/A ~ thei lo minam aw | O nation that cannot feel shame) (s:maisia) (r:1.2.25/56.2.8/26.16.54/36.2.1)
maizumhuai = (t:adj) (w:shameful/disgraceful) (d:maizum be ashamed with huai for what causes a feeling) (e:a ~ a gamtatnate uh ah/Pasian thei het lo na hih manun ~ mahmah hi | it is very shameful that you do not know God at all) (s:zumhuai/mindaihuai) (r:50.3.19/46.15.34) (q:draft)
maizumhuaina = (t:n) (w:shame/disgrace) (d:maizumhuai shameful with the noun suffix na) (e:haina leh ~ ahi hi) (s:zumhuaina/maizumna) (b:maizumhuai) (r:20.18.13) (q:draft)
maizumin = (t:adv) (w:in shame/ashamed) (d:maizum, ashamed, with the ending in: feeling shame, in shame) (e:Zion a mudahte khempeuh ~ kinungkiksak ta hen/Amaute ~ lungkia densak in | let them be ashamed and dismayed forever/kong et ding ~ ka mai san hi | I blush with shame to look to you/~ mindai ding uh hi | they will be ashamed and disgraced) (b:maizum) (r:19.129.5/19.83.17/15.9.6/33.3.7) (q:draft)
maizumlawh = (t:v) (w:be put to shame by/be ashamed because of) (d:maizum ashamed with lawh, suffer on account of something) (e:a milim uh a ~ uh hi/a milimte uh a ~ uh hi | they are put to shame by their idols) (r:24.51.17/24.10.14) (q:draft)
maizumna = (t:n) (w:shame/disgrace) (d:maizum, ashamed, with the noun suffix na; maizumna thuak and maizumna ngah mean be put to shame) (e:~ ka thuak kei ding hi/an lak hun-a a ihmu-pa in ~ ngah hi | he who sleeps at harvest time gets shame/~ tawh amah na kidimsak hi | you have filled him with shame/Milim a bawl amaute khempeuh in ~ thuakin | all the makers of idols are put to shame) (s:zumna/mindaina/zahhuaina) (a:pahtawina) (b:maizum) (r:19.119.46/20.10.5/19.89.45/23.45.16) (q:draft)
maizumpi = (t:adj) (w:humiliated/greatly ashamed) (d:maizum ashamed with pi great; with in, in great shame) (e:tutna munah ~ in na tusuk ding uh hi) (b:maizum) (r:42.14.9) (q:draft)
maizumpih = (t:v) (w:be ashamed of) (d:maizum ashamed with pih: be ashamed about someone or something) (e:ci-in sap ding a ~ kei hi) (b:maizum) (r:58.2.11) (q:draft)
maizumsak = (t:v) (w:shame/put to shame/humiliate) (d:maizum ashamed with the causative sak; in Luke 9.26 be ashamed of someone) (e:kei hong ~ kei in/nang hong ~ ding a | he will put you to shame/hong ~ ngei kei in | never let me be put to shame/na nasemte khempeuh na ~ hi | you have humiliated all your servants) (s:zumsak/maisiasak/mindaisak) (b:maizum) (r:19.25.20/20.25.10/19.31.1/10.19.5) (q:draft)
mak = (t:n) (w:son-in-law) (d:the husband of a daughter; a mak ding is a man who is going to marry the daughter) (e:Ahih hangin amah a ~ dingte tungah/a tanute a ten’pih ding a ~ dingte | the men who were to marry his daughters) (s:makpa) (r:1.19.14)
makai = (t:n) (w:leader/chief/prince/ruler) (d:one who goes in front and is at the head of a tribe, a clan or a group of people) (e:Dan minam sung panin ~ khat/Gad mite a ~, De-uel’ tapa Eliasaf | the leader of the people of Gad, Eliasaph son of Deuel/Bashan-ah beh ~ ahi uh hi | they were clan chiefs in Bashan/Reuben mite’ ~ khat ahi | he was a chief of the Reubenites) (s:makaipa/ukpi/ulian) (r:4.34.22/13.23.2/4.7.42/13.5.12/13.11.42) (q:draft)
makaih = (t:v) (w:lead/guide) (d:go before others and show them the way; the verb that belongs to makai, leader) (e:tuuhon bangin na ~ hi/na thumanna tawh hong ~ in la | lead me in your righteousness/Topa bek mah in amaute ~ a | the Lord alone led them/nang a hong ~ ding om lo a | there was no one to guide you) (s:lamkaih/lamlak) (a:zui) (b:makai) (r:19.77.20/5.32.12/19.5.8/23.51.18) (q:draft)
makaihin = (t:v) (w:leading/lead/guide) (d:makaih lead with the linking ending in: leading someone, after which the next action follows) (e:amaute ~ amah kuankhia-in hong ciah hi/mi zathum leh sawm-le-giatte ~ Dan ciang dong | leading the three hundred and eighteen men as far as Dan/Amaute ~ ka hehnem ding a | I will guide them and comfort them) (b:makaih) (r:9.18.16/1.14.14/23.57.18) (q:draft)
makaihna = (t:n) (w:leadership/direction/supervision/guidance) (d:the act of leading, makaih lead with the noun ending na; makaihna tawh and makaihna nuai-ah mean under the leadership of someone) (e:Moses leh Aaron’ ~ tawh/amau’ ~ tawh a nasep uh telh mahmah uh hi | under their direction the work makes good progress/a pa uh Jeduthun’ ~ nuai-ah | under the supervision of their father Jeduthun/kumpipa’ ~ nuai-ah mai lam thu a genkhol | who prophesied under the supervision of the king) (s:lamlahna) (b:makaih) (r:4.33.1/13.25.2/15.5.8/13.25.3) (q:draft)
makaihpa = (t:n) (w:leader/director) (d:makaih lead with pa marking a man: the one who leads, in the verse the director of the musicians) (e:theihte hong ~ ahi hi) (s:makaipa/makai) (b:makaih) (r:35.3.19) (q:draft)
makaihte = (t:n) (w:leaders/guides) (d:makaih lead with the plural te: those who lead or guide a people) (e:hih minam a ~ in lam khialsak) (s:makaite/lamlakte) (b:makaih) (r:23.9.16) (q:draft)
makaipa = (t:n) (w:leader/chief) (d:makai leader with pa marking a man: the man at the head of a tribe or group) (e:Benjamin mite a ~ in/Gad mite a ~ in Re-u-el’ tapa Eliasaf | the leader of the people of Gad is Eliasaph son of Reuel/Shallum in amau’ ~ ahi hi | Shallum was their chief/Zebulun mite ~ in Helon’ tapa Eliab | the leader of the people of Zebulun is Eliab son of Helon) (s:makai/makaihpa) (b:makai) (r:4.2.22/4.2.7/4.2.14/13.9.17) (q:draft)
makaipi = (t:n) (w:chief leader/chief/champion) (d:makai leader with pi great: the foremost leader, as a champion among warriors; la makaipi is the chief musician) (e:Heman in la ~ hi a/a ~ Goliath min nei-pa | their champion, the man named Goliath) (s:makaipipa) (b:makai) (r:13.6.33/9.17.23) (q:draft)
makaipipa = (t:n) (w:chief/leader/head) (d:makaipi chief leader with pa marking a man: the head man of a place or of a group of workers) (e:a ~ Iddo kiangah va pai-in/Saul’ gancing ~, Edom mi ahi hi | chief of the herdsmen of Saul, an Edomite) (s:makaipi/makaipa) (b:makaipi) (r:15.8.17/9.21.7) (q:draft)
makaite = (t:n) (w:leaders/chiefs/princes) (d:makai leader with the plural te: the leaders, chiefs or princes of a people) (e:Israel ~, a beh ukpite/Israel ~ khempeuh in a tapa Solomon a huh nading | that all the leaders of Israel should help his son Solomon/Moab ~, liin’na in mancip hi | trembling seizes the leaders of Moab/A ~ uh, lonona mun mu lo a | her princes find no pasture) (s:uliante/ukpite/makaihte) (b:makai) (r:4.7.2/2.35.27/13.22.17/2.15.15/25.1.6) (q:draft)
Makaz = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Makaz) (d:town in the second district of Solomon, governed by Ben-Deker) (r:11.4.9)
Makbannai = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Makbannai) (d:warrior of the tribe of Gad, the eleventh of those who joined David in the wilderness) (r:13.12.13)
Makbenah = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Makbenah) (d:town in Judah founded by Sheva, a descendant of Caleb) (r:13.2.49)
Makedonia = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Macedonia) (d:Roman province in the north of Greece, with the cities of Philippi, Thessalonica and Berea, where Paul founded churches) (r:47.8.1/44.27.2)
makeng = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:tamarisk) (d:the tamarisk, a tree of dry country; makeng kung is a tamarisk tree) (e:~ kung nuai-ah vui uh a/Be-ersheba-ah ~ kung khat suan a | he planted a tamarisk tree in Beersheba/sangna mun ~ kung nuai-ah Saul tu hi | Saul sat under the tamarisk tree on the height) (r:9.31.13/1.21.33/9.22.6) (q:draft)
Makhael = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Michael) (d:spelling of Michael in this verse: a man of Benjamin, son of Beriah) (r:13.8.16)
makhawm = (t:v) (w:send away together/divorce together) (d:apparently ma, divorce or send away, with khawm, together: the wives are sent away together with their children) (e:a tate uh tawh a ~ uh hi) (r:15.10.44) (q:draft, low confidence)
makhelh = (t:v) (w:outrun/overtake) (d:get ahead of someone who is running the same way) (e:Kush mipa ~ hi) (r:10.18.23) (q:draft)
makhelhin = (t:v) (w:outrunning/outrun) (d:makhelh outrun with the linking ending in: getting ahead of someone, after which the next action follows) (e:Piter ~ han a tung masa hi) (b:makhelh) (r:43.20.4) (q:draft)
Makheloth = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Makheloth) (d:place where the Israelites camped in the wilderness, between Haradah and Tahath) (r:4.33.25/4.33.26)
Makhi = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Maki) (d:father of Geuel, the man of Gad sent to spy out Canaan) (r:4.13.15) (q:draft)
Makhijah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Malkijah) (d:spelling of Malkijah: name of several men, among them a Levite ancestor of Asaph and a priest who sealed the covenant with Nehemiah) (r:13.6.40/16.10.3)
Makhir = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Machir/Makir) (d:son of Manasseh and father of Gilead; also the son of Ammiel of Lo Debar who sheltered Mephibosheth) (r:1.50.23)
Makhiram = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Malkiram) (d:spelling of Malkiram, a son of King Jehoiachin of Judah) (r:13.3.18)
Makhirte = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Makir/Makirites) (d:the clan descended from Makir son of Manasseh, who took Gilead) (b:Makhir) (r:4.32.39)
Makhishua = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Malki-Shua) (d:spelling of Malki-Shua, a son of King Saul) (r:13.9.39)
Makkedah = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Makkedah) (d:Canaanite royal city in the lowland of Judah, with the cave where five Amorite kings hid from Joshua) (r:6.10.16/6.15.41)
makna = (t:n) (w:divorce) (d:the putting away of a wife, mak divorce with the noun ending na; makna lai is a certificate of divorce) (e:a zi tungah ~ lai pia ta hen/~ lai gelhin numei khut sungah koih a | he writes a certificate of divorce and puts it in her hand/Zi ~ ka deih kei a | I do not want the divorcing of a wife) (s:kimakna/kikhenna) (r:40.5.31/39.2.16/5.24.3) (q:draft)
Maknadebai = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Maknadebai) (d:man of the family of Binnui who had married a foreign wife in the time of Ezra) (r:15.10.40)
makpa = (t:n) (w:son-in-law) (d:a son-in-law, and more widely a man related to a family by marriage; mak with pa marking a man) (e:Horonaim khuami Sanballat’ ~ na hi hi/kumpipa’ ~ ahih ding David lungkim sak hi | David was pleased to become the son-in-law of the king/Arah’ tapa Shekaniah’ ~ hi a | he was son-in-law to Shekaniah son of Arah/Keimah in kumpipa’ ~ ka hih nadingin | that I should be the son-in-law of the king) (s:mak) (b:mak) (r:16.13.28/9.18.26/16.6.18/9.18.18) (q:draft)
Makpelah = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Machpelah) (d:the field with a cave near Mamre at Hebron that Abraham bought as a burial place for his family) (r:1.23.17/1.23.19)
Makri = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mikri) (d:spelling of Mikri, a man of Benjamin whose descendant Elah lived in Jerusalem after the exile) (r:13.9.8)
maksa = (t:adj) (w:divorced) (d:mak divorce with sa marking a completed act: divorced, as in a maksa numei, a divorced woman; not the word mak, son-in-law) (e:a pasal in a ~ numei/A ~ numei a teen’pihte | those who marry a divorced woman) (s:kimasa/kikhensa) (r:3.21.7/40.5.32) (q:draft)
maksim = (t:v) (w:divorce quietly/divorce) (d:put away a wife or betrothed; the verse shows a divorce without public disgrace, and sim may add the sense secretly) (e:~ ding a lungngai hi) (r:40.1.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
makte = (t:n) (w:son-in-law/sons-in-law) (e:~, tapate, tanute, ahih kei leh) (b:mak) (r:1.19.12) plural form of <mak>
Makte = (t:n) (w:sons-in-law) (d:makte written with a capital at the start of a sentence) (e:~, tapate, tanute, ahih kei leh) (b:makte) (r:1.19.12) (q:draft)
maktheih = (t:v) (w:may divorce/can divorce) (d:mak divorce with theih can, be allowed) (e:zi ~ ding mah ahi hiam) (s:mathei) (r:40.19.3) (q:draft)
mal = (t:n) (w:item/unit/single one/number) (d:a single one of things that are counted, such as an article, a word or a strand; a mal sim is to count one by one, a mal zah the full number, and mal khat a single word) (e:a ~ zah simin sazian bawlsak hi/Jakob mite a ~ sim zo ding a | can count the people of Jacob one by one/a ~ zah a sim ding uh kisam hi | they had to count the full number/leiseek a ~ ngeina zah mah na piakhia ding | you shall hand over the usual number of bricks/thu peuhmah ~ khat zong i mang kei ding hi | we will not heed a single word he says) (r:15.1.8/4.23.10/13.9.28/2.5.18/24.18.18) (q:draft, low confidence)
Malakhi = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Malachi) (d:prophet through whom the Lord spoke to Israel after the exile; the last book of the Old Testament bears his name) (r:39.1.1)
malam = (t:adv) (d:placed after a verb, apparently for doing something readily or straight off, as na sang malam, you so readily accept) (e:thudang khat na sang ~/bang tum lo tawh kipan pah ~ uh a) (r:48.1.6/21.10.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
maleep = (t:n) (w:deposit/pledge/guarantee/first instalment) (d:something given in advance as assurance that the rest will follow; in the verses always said of the Holy Spirit) (e:eite luahna ~ ahi hi/Kha Siangtho ahi ~ eite hong pia zo hi | he has given us the Holy Spirit as a deposit/Kha Siangtho ~ a ngah eite | we who have received the Holy Spirit as a first instalment) (r:49.1.14/47.5.5/45.8.23) (q:draft)
malgol = (t:n) (w:large drop/drop) (d:a big drop of liquid; sisan malgol is drops of blood) (e:lei tungah sisan ~ bangin a kia hi) (r:42.22.44) (q:draft)
malin = (t:adv) (w:one by one/individually/by number) (d:mal a single counted one with in: taken one at a time, person by person or item by item; a mi malin is man by man) (e:a ~ simzawh loh ding siatna tampite/Matri innkuan a mi ~ hong paipih a | he brought forward the family of Matri man by man/a mi ~ tampi pha uh hi | counted man by man they were many) (s:khatkhatin) (b:mal) (r:19.40.12/9.10.21/58.7.23) (q:draft)
Malkam = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Malkam) (d:man of Benjamin, a son of Shaharaim and his wife Hodesh) (r:13.8.9)
Malkhas = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Malchus) (d:servant of the high priest whose right ear Peter cut off when Jesus was arrested) (r:43.18.10)
malkhat = (t:n) (w:one item/one word) (d:mal a single item with khat one; malkhat khit malkhat is one item after another, where the English has rule on rule or precept upon precept) (e:~ khit ~, gualkhat khit gualkhat) (r:23.28.10/23.28.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
Malkhiah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Malkijah) (d:name of two men in Jeremiah: the father of Pashhur, an official of King Zedekiah, and the son of the king who owned the cistern into which Jeremiah was thrown) (r:24.21.1/24.38.6) (q:draft)
Malkhiel = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Malchiel/Malkiel) (d:son of Beriah and grandson of Asher, ancestor of the Malkielite clan) (r:1.46.17/13.7.31)
Malkhijah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Malchijah/Malkijah) (d:name of several men, among them a Levite ancestor of Asaph, the head of the fifth division of priests and a priest who sealed the covenant with Nehemiah) (r:13.6.40/16.10.3)
Malkhiram = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Malkiram) (d:son of King Jehoiachin of Judah) (r:13.3.18)
Malkhishua = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Malki-Shua) (d:son of King Saul, killed with his father and brothers by the Philistines on Mount Gilboa) (r:9.14.49/13.8.33)
Malkhus = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Malchus) (d:servant of the high priest whose right ear Peter cut off when Jesus was arrested) (r:43.18.10)
Mallothi = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mallothi) (d:son of Heman, head of the nineteenth division of temple musicians in the time of David) (r:13.25.4)
Malluk = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Malluk) (d:name of several men, among them a Levite of the family of Merari and a priest who returned from exile with Zerubbabel) (r:13.6.44/16.12.2)
Mallukhi = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Malluchi/Malluk) (d:priestly family in the days of the high priest Joiakim, headed by Jonathan) (r:16.12.14)
malneu = (t:adj) (w:fine/thin) (d:mal a single strand with neu small: thin or fine, said of cord in khau malneu; the exact sense is not clear from one verse) (e:khau ~ leh khau dupsan tawh) (r:17.1.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
Malta = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Malta) (d:island in the Mediterranean Sea south of Sicily where Paul and his companions came ashore after the shipwreck) (r:44.28.1)
malte = (t:n) (w:words/letters/items) (d:mal a single one with the plural te: the single words of a song or writing, or the items of a list) (e:hih la ~ khempeuh sut hi/hih la ~ a bei dongin | the words of this song to the end/a kisim van ~ ahi hi | these are the counted items of the materials/hih lai ~ tua khut a hong gelhsak hi | he made that hand write these words) (s:kammalte) (b:mal) (r:5.32.44/27.5.24/5.31.30/2.38.21) (q:draft)
Maluk = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Malluk) (d:name of several men, among them a descendant of Bani who had married a foreign wife and a priest who returned from exile with Zerubbabel) (r:15.10.29/16.12.2)
Maluk = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Malluch/Malluk) (d:name of several men, among them a descendant of Harim who had married a foreign wife and a priest who sealed the covenant with Nehemiah) (r:15.10.32/16.10.4)
Malukhi = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Malluk) (d:priestly family in the days of the high priest Joiakim, headed by Jonathan) (r:16.12.14)
malzah = (t:n) (w:number/total number/count) (d:mal a counted one with zah amount: how many there are of things that are counted one by one) (e:a ~ tawh kizui-in/a ~ simin sazian bawlsak hi | he counted their number and had a list made/a ~ a sim ding uh kisam hi | they had to count their number) (s:phazah/nambat/omzah) (r:4.15.12/13.9.28/15.1.8) (q:draft)
mam = (t:adj) (w:straight/smooth) (d:said of legs, where the English has straight) (e:A khete uh ~ zeza a) (a:kawi) (r:26.1.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
Mamre = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Mamre) (d:place near Hebron with great trees where Abraham lived and built an altar; also the name of an Amorite who was an ally of Abram) (r:1.35.27/1.18.1) (q:?)
mamsak = (t:v) (w:straighten/make straight) (d:mam straight with the causative sak: make straight what is crooked or uneven) (e:ama lampi khempeuh ka ~ ding hi/kua in ~ kik thei ahi hiam | who can straighten it again) (s:tangsak) (b:mam) (r:23.45.13/21.7.13) (q:draft)
mamsakkik = (t:v) (w:straighten again/make straight again) (d:mamsak straighten with kik again, back) (e:kua in ~ thei ahi hiam) (b:mamsak) (r:21.7.13) (q:draft)
man = (t:adj) (w:true/right/correct) (d:true or right, in agreement with the facts or with what ought to be; a man lo is false or wrong) (e:ka teci pan’na thu a ~ kei hi/na thukham zong ~ tawntung hi | your law too is true for ever/a hoih leh a ~ na sem hi | he did what was good and right/a ~ lo teci na pang kei ding hi | you shall not give false testimony) (s:maan/mantak) (a:manlo) (r:43.5.31/19.119.142/14.14.2/2.20.16) (q:draft)
man = (t:v) (w:finish/complete) (d:placed after another verb to say that the action is finished; a man khit ciangin means after finishing) (e:hih thute a gen a ~ ciangin/Amah tawh a kiho a ~ khit ciangin | when he had finished talking with him/Moses in nasep ~ ta hi | Moses finished the work/laibu sunga gelh a ~ ciangin | when he had finished writing in the book) (s:mankhit/zawhkhit) (a:kipan) (r:5.32.45/1.17.22/2.40.33/5.31.24) (q:draft)
man = (t:n) (w:price/value/cost/payment) (d:what is paid or owed for something: its price, its value or the payment for it; man pia is to pay) (e:a ~ zah seh ding hi/lo ~ ding kong pia ding hi | I will pay the price of the field/a ~ na khangsak ding uh hi | you shall raise the price/Izipt ah ~ pia loin i nek ngasate | the fish we ate in Egypt without paying) (s:manzah) (r:3.27.12/4.11.5/1.23.13/3.25.16) (q:draft)
man = (t:v) (w:seize/arrest/catch/capture) (d:take hold of with the hand, or catch and arrest a person) (e:Topa ~ dingin palikte a sawl uh hi/tua nu in a puan-in amah ~ a | she caught him by his cloak/a khut zan-in vakhu ~ a | he reached out his hand and took the dove/a khut zanin ~ a | he reached out his hand and took hold of it) (a:khah) (r:43.7.32/14.23.15/1.39.12/1.8.9/2.4.4) (q:draft)
Man = (t:see) <Man-a>
man'suahsa = (t:adj) (w:lost) (d:that had been lost, mansuah lose with sa already) (e:ka ~ tuu ka mukik zo hi/ka ~ dangka ka mukik zo hi | I have found my lost coin) (s:mansuahsa/mangsa) (r:42.15.6/42.15.9) (q:draft)
Man-a = (t:prep) (w:because of/on account of) (d:man reason or cause with a; in the section heading Kikhen Man-a Lunggimna, distress because of parting) (e:Kikhen ~ Lunggimna Nungak) (r:22.5.1) (q:draft, low confidence)
man-unah = (t:conj) (w:because) (d:man because, with un for a plural subject and ah: because they or because you, placed at the end of the clause that gives the reason) (e:Judah mite a kihtak ~/nangma mi ahih ~ amau ading thu ka ngen | because they are yours I pray for them/Zeisu a een’ ~ a piak uh a thei hi | he knew they had handed Jesus over out of envy/ci-in mite in a up ~ | because the people believed so) (s:manunah) (r:43.20.19/43.17.9/40.27.18/42.19.11) (q:draft)
mana = (t:n) (w:manna) (d:the food God gave Israel in the wilderness) (e:~ koihna kham beel tawh) (s:manna) (r:58.9.4) (q:draft)
mana = (t:conj) (w:because/because of) (d:man reason with a; follows the clause that gives the reason, like manin) (e:midangte sangin ka pil zawk ~) (b:man) (r:27.2.30/48.5.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
Manaen = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Manaen) (d:prophet and teacher in the church at Antioch who had been brought up with Herod the tetrarch) (r:44.13.1)
manah = (t:adv) (w:rightly/in the right way) (d:man right with the place marker ah: in the right way; lampi manah is on the right path) (e:lampi ~ amaute a paipih hi/lampi ~ kei hong kha hi | he leads me on the right path/lampi ~ kei a hong paipih | he led me on the right road/tawikhaina ~ hong tawikhai hen | let him weigh me on honest scales/lungsim kiniamkhiatte a ~ paipihin | guiding the humble in what is right) (b:man) (r:19.107.7/19.25.9/19.23.3/1.24.48/18.31.6) (q:draft)
Manahath = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Manahath) (d:son of Shobal, a descendant of Seir the Horite; also a place to which men of Benjamin were deported) (r:1.36.23/13.1.40)
Manaseeh = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Manasseh) (d:spelling of Manasseh in this verse: the tribe descended from the elder son of Joseph) (r:66.7.6)
Manason = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mnason) (d:spelling of Mnason, a man from Cyprus and an early disciple, in whose house Paul stayed on the way to Jerusalem) (r:44.21.16)
Manasseh = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Manasseh) (d:elder son of Joseph and ancestor of the tribe of Manasseh; also a king of Judah, the son of Hezekiah) (r:1.41.51/1.46.20)
Manassehte = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Manasseh) (d:Manasseh with the plural te: the people of the tribe of Manasseh) (b:Manasseh) (r:7.12.4/6.17.7)
manawh = (t:v) (w:head for/go toward/make for) (d:go in the direction of a place or an end; often after lam, direction) (e:Arabah leizang lam a ~ uh hi/Gilead gam mualtung lam a ~ hi | he headed for the hill country of Gilead/Aroer panin kipanin Gad lam ~ uh a | starting from Aroer they headed toward Gad/Jesuh in Jerusalem khua ~ sawm ahih manin | because Jesus meant to head for Jerusalem) (s:zuan) (r:24.39.4/42.9.53/1.31.21/10.24.5) (q:draft)
manawhin = (t:prep) (w:toward/in the direction of/heading for) (d:manawh head for with the linking ending in: in the direction of, usually after lam, direction) (e:nisuahna lam ~ Tui Kongpi dongah/Negeb gam lam ~ pai lai hi | he went on toward the Negev/San Tuipi lam ~ gamlak lamah | toward the Red Sea by way of the wilderness/Sidon panin kipanin Gerar lam ~ Gaza ciang dong | from Sidon toward Gerar as far as Gaza) (b:manawh) (r:16.12.37/1.12.9/2.13.18/1.10.19) (q:draft)
mancip = (t:v) (w:seize/grip/hold fast) (d:man seize with cip tightly; said of anguish, fear or trembling taking hold of people) (e:Leinuai sihna in kei hong ~ a/Filistia-ah a teng mite gimna in ~ hi | anguish grips the people living in Philistia/khuamial sahpi in ~ hen | may thick darkness seize it/mawhna thu-ah kei hong ~ hi | it holds me fast under sin) (s:lencip) (b:man) (r:19.116.3/2.15.14/18.3.6/45.7.23) (q:draft)
Manean = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Manaen) (d:spelling of Manaen, a prophet and teacher in the church at Antioch who had been brought up with Herod the tetrarch) (r:44.13.1)
manek = (t:v) (w:eat first/eat ahead) (d:ma before with nek eat: eat ahead of others without waiting) (e:kuamah kingak loin na ~ tek uh a) (r:46.11.21) (q:draft)
mang = (t:v) (w:obey) (e:Ka thu hong ~ lo minamte tungah/amaute in hong ~ uh a | they obey me/na thupiaknate ~ lo uh hi | they did not obey your commands/siate’ thu ka ~ nuam kei a | I would not obey my teachers) (s:zui/thumang/thungai) (r:33.5.15/20.5.13/19.18.44/16.9.16) obey an order; listen to advice
