mangbuhvui = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:head of wheat/ear of grain) (d:mangbuh, wheat, with vui, ear: the head of a wheat plant, which holds the grain) (e:a nungzuite in ~ a zut uh hi) (s:buhvui/anvui) (r:41.2.23) (q:draft)
mangbuhvuite = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:heads of grain/ears of wheat) (d:mangbuhvui, head of wheat, with the plural te) (e:~ zutin a ne uh hi/A nungzuite in ~ zut uh a | his disciples picked heads of grain) (s:buhvuite/anvuite) (r:40.12.1/42.6.1) (q:draft)
mangbuk = (t:n) (w:tavern/inn) (d:a roadside inn or tavern; in the Bible only in the place name Mangbuk Thum, Three Taverns) (e:~ Thum dongin hong pai uh hi) (r:44.28.15)
Mangbuk = (t:n) (w:tavern/inn) (d:mangbuk, tavern, written with a capital in the place name Mangbuk Thum, Three Taverns, a stopping place on the road to Rome) (e:kimkhatte in ~ Thum dongin hong pai uh hi) (b:mangbuk) (r:44.28.15) (q:draft)
mangin = (t:v) (w:listen to/pay attention/obey) (d:mang, obey, with the linking ending in: obeying, and then; thu mangin is obeying what someone says) (e:Topa na Pasian uh thupiaknate ~/Israel mite in ama thu ~ | the Israelites obeyed him/ka thukham zui-in ka thupiaknate ~ | following my decrees and obeying my commands/kote in hong ~ ka sem ding uh hi | we will obey and do it) (b:mang) (r:5.28.13/1.28.7/5.34.9/3.26.3/5.5.27)
manginn = (t:n) (w:governor's residence/praetorium/palace) (d:mang, ruler, with inn, house: the governor's official residence, the Praetorium; manginn tual is its courtyard) (e:galkapte in ~ tual ah Zeisu paipih/mangpa’ galkapte in ~ tualah Zeisu paipih uh | the governor's soldiers took Jesus into the Praetorium) (r:41.15.16/40.27.27) (q:draft)
mangkawlsing = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:pomegranate) (d:the pomegranate, both the tree and its fruit; also the pomegranate shapes that decorated the temple pillars) (e:~ a pak nai hiam/amah in ~ zakhat bawlin | he made a hundred pomegranates/~ tui, kong tulh ding hi | I would give you pomegranate juice to drink/~ cin’na huan tawh kibang hi | it is like an orchard of pomegranates) (r:22.6.11/14.3.16/22.8.2/22.4.13) (q:draft)
mangkawlsingte = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:pomegranates) (d:plural of mangkawlsing, pomegranate; here the bronze pomegranates around the capital of a pillar) (e:simsiam leh ~ khuamluzepna kimkotah om hi) (b:mangkawlsing) (r:12.25.17) (q:draft)
mangkha = (t:v) (w:give in to/yield to/heed) (d:mang, obey, with kha, happen to: come to follow what someone says, be won over by persuasion or pressure) (e:tua zolna a ~ hi/amau’ thu ~ ka hih manin | because I gave in to them) (r:20.7.21/9.15.24) (q:draft)
mangkhiat = (t:v) (w:interpret dreams) (d:mang, dream, with khiat, bring out: explain the meaning of a dream; mangkhiat siamna is skill in interpreting dreams) (e:maangmuhna le ~ siamna a pia hi/~ siamna, thudotna haksa nonote dawntheihna | skill in interpreting dreams, the ability to answer hard questions) (r:27.1.17/27.5.12) (q:draft)
mangkhin = (t:adv) (w:completely/utterly/away) (d:placed after a verb to show that the action is finished and the thing is gone, as in bei mangkhin, come to an end altogether) (e:Lungnopna khempeuh bei ~ ta a/amaute ka susia ~ ding a | I will completely destroy them/Huih in leen’ ~ ahih manin | because the wind swept them away/gam khempeuh a zo ~ ding uh hi | they will conquer all the lands completely/gamdang mite’ khut sungah tung ~ a | it has passed entirely into the hands of foreigners) (b:mang) (r:25.5.15/35.1.6/24.25.9/27.2.35/25.5.2) (q:draft)
mangkikin = (t:v) (w:obey again) (d:mang, obey, with kik, again, and the linking ending in: obeying once more) (e:thu ~, tuni-a kong gen/Note in Topa’ thu ~ | you will again obey the Lord) (r:5.30.8) (q:draft)
manglian = (t:n) (w:commander/high officer) (d:mang, officer, with lian, great: a high officer; galkap manglian is the field commander of an army) (e:a galkap ~ in amaute kiangah) (s:mangpa/galkapmang) (r:23.36.4) (q:draft)
mangliante = (t:n) (w:officials/rulers/governors) (d:plural of manglian, a high official or ruler) (e:tua ~ khempeuh milim apna dingin/na ~ uh bawlin) (s:uliante/mangpite/mangte) (b:manglian) (r:27.3.3/23.60.17) (q:draft)
mangman = (t:n) (w:dreamer) (d:one who has dreams and tells what they mean; mang, dream, with man, catch, as in mang man, have a dream; often followed by pa, mangman pa, the dreamer) (e:~ khat ahi zongin hong khangin/Hih lai-ah ~ pa hong pai hi | here comes the dreamer/~ pa ahi zongin kithat ding hi | or the dreamer, he must be put to death) (s:mangmanpa) (r:5.13.1/1.37.19/5.13.5) (q:draft)
mangmanpa = (t:n) (w:dreamer) (d:mangman dreamer with pa marking a man) (e:Hih lai-ah ~ hong pai hi) (s:mangman) (b:mangman) (r:1.37.19) (q:draft)
mangmat = (t:n) (w:dream) (d:a dream seen in sleep; mang, dream, with mat, the second form of man, catch, as in mang man, have a dream) (e:Na ~ pen tu-a teng ahi hi/zan ~ hun lai takin | at the time of dreams in the night/Ka ~ a khiatna a hong hilh dingin | to tell me the meaning of my dream/zan-a ~ bang leh mumaang bangin | like a dream of the night and like a vision) (r:27.2.36/18.20.8/18.4.13/27.4.6) (q:draft)
mangmatna = (t:n) (w:vision/dream) (d:mangmat dream with the noun suffix na: what is seen in a dream or vision) (e:Topa hong muhsak ~ leh thupiakkholhna thu) (s:mangmuhna/maangmuhna) (b:mangmat) (r:47.12.1) (q:draft)
mangmatnate = (t:n) (w:visions/revelations) (d:plural of mangmatna: visions or revelations received from God) (e:Ka ngah ~ a) (s:mangmuhnate/maangmuhnate) (b:mangmatna) (r:47.12.7) (q:draft)
mangmu = (t:n) (w:tribute/tax/levy) (d:a payment required by a ruler or for the house of God, named together with siah, tax, and losap, duty) (e:siah leh ~ leh losapte/siah ahi a, ~ ahi a | whether tax or tribute/~ piak dingte tungah pia-in | pay tribute to those who are owed tribute/Moses in Israel mite a piaksak ~ | the tax Moses required of the Israelites) (s:siah/phiangsiah) (r:15.4.20/14.24.9/15.4.13/45.13.7) (q:draft)
mangmu = (t:v) (w:see a vision/fall into a trance) (d:mang, dream, with mu, see: see a vision while awake, fall into a trance) (e:~ a kisa hi/lai takun amah in ~-in | just then he fell into a trance/Nikai nai thum ciangin ~-in | at about three in the afternoon he saw a vision) (r:44.12.9/44.10.10/44.10.3) (q:draft)
mangmuh = (t:n) (w:vision) (d:what is seen as in a dream, a prophetic vision; mang dream with muh, the form of mu see) (e:ka ~ masak sunga ka muh mipa/~ muhna om lo hi | there were no visions/Zan ka ~ hun sungin ka khuadak leh | in my vision at night I looked) (s:maangmuh/mumaang) (b:mangmu) (r:27.9.21/9.3.1/27.7.13) (q:draft)
mangmuhna = (t:n) (w:vision/revelation) (d:mangmuh, vision, with the noun suffix na: something seen in a dream or in a vision from God) (e:~ khat ka nei a/mang leh ~ sungah Pasian in thugen hi | God speaks in a dream and in a vision/a lauhuai ~ tawh nong lau sak hi | you terrify me with frightful visions/Piter in a ~ a ngaihsut lai takin | while Peter was thinking about the vision) (s:maangmuhna/mangmatna) (b:mangmuh) (r:27.4.10/18.7.14/18.33.15/44.10.19) (q:draft)
mangmuhnate = (t:n) (w:visions) (d:plural of mangmuhna: the visions seen by a prophet or in sleep) (e:Ka ~ in hong linglawng sakin/na ~ uh zuaupi hi a | your visions are false/tua zana ka ~ ka ciamtehna | the record of my visions of that night/Hih ~ khempeuh pen note’ adingin | for you all these visions) (s:maangmuhnate/mangmatnate) (b:mangmuhna) (r:27.7.15/23.1.1/26.21.29/27.7.1/23.29.11) (q:draft)
mangna = (t:n) (d:noun form of mang, away or completely, after a verb: a suksiat mangna is their destroying completely) (e:a suksiat ~ thu na za khin hi) (r:12.19.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
mangngilh = (t:v) (w:forget) (d:no longer remember, or fail to keep in mind; mangngilh kei is not forget) (e:ama migitna ka ~ kei ding hi/nangma thu ka ~ kei hi | I do not forget your law/a thuakte ~ kei in | do not forget the helpless/Pasian a ~ minam khempeuh | all the nations that forget God/khomun puak ding a ~ uh a | they forgot to bring bread) (a:phawk) (r:19.103.2/1.40.23/19.119.61/19.10.12/19.9.17/41.8.14) (q:draft)
mangngilhin = (t:v) (w:forget) (d:mangngilh, forget, with the linking ending in: forgetting, and then) (e:Nangmah in kei hong ~ hong nungngat/a zawn’na uh ~ | forgetting their poverty/Topa na Pasian uh ~ pasian dangte nung zui-in | forgetting the Lord your God and following other gods/note tawh hong bawl thuciamna ~ | forgetting the covenant he made with you) (a:phawkin) (b:mangngilh) (r:26.23.35/5.8.19/20.31.7/5.4.23) (q:draft)
mangngilhkha = (t:v) (w:happen to forget/forget) (d:mangngilh, forget, with kha, happen to: come to forget) (e:Hihte nangawn in ~ thei ding a) (r:23.49.15) (q:draft)
mangngilhna = (t:n) (w:forgetting/forgetfulness/oblivion) (d:mangngilh forget with the noun suffix na; mangngilhna gam is the land of oblivion) (e:~ gam sungah na hotkhiat huhna/a Pasian uh a ~ hang uh ahi hi | it is because they forgot their God) (a:phawkna) (b:mangngilh) (r:19.88.12/24.3.21) (q:draft)
mangngilhte = (t:n) (w:those who forget) (d:mangngilh forget with the plural te: the ones who forget) (e:Pasian a ~ tua bangmah ahi hi) (b:mangngilh) (r:18.8.13) (q:draft)
mangpa = (t:n) (w:commander/captain/officer/chief) (d:a man in command or in office: galkap mangpa is an army commander or centurion, inncing mangpa the captain of the guard, thukhen mangpa a judge) (e:Saul’ galkap ~ in/Galkap ~ in Paul kiangah pai a | the commander went to Paul/inncing ~’ inn sungah | in the house of the captain of the guard/galkap ~ leh galkapte a muh uh ciangin | when they saw the commander and the soldiers) (s:galkapmang/ukpa) (r:10.2.8/41.15.45/44.22.27/1.40.3/44.21.32) (q:draft)
Mangpa = (t:n) (w:official/governor/lord) (d:capitalised form of mangpa used as a title: the Ethiopian official of Acts 8, the governor Festus, and Christ as the author or prince of life) (e:Festas ~ tua gamah/~ in leeng khawlsak a | the official had the chariot stopped/nuntakna hong pia ~ na that tazen uh hi | you killed the author of life/~ Festas aw, ka hai kei hi | most excellent Festus, I am not insane) (b:mangpa) (r:44.25.1/44.8.38/44.3.15/44.26.25) (q:draft)
mangpah = (t:v) (w:disappear at once/vanish) (d:mang, disappear, with pah, at once: vanish in a moment) (e:muhna panin Jesuh a ~ hi) (r:42.24.31) (q:draft)
mangpha = (t:n) (w:goodbye/farewell) (d:the parting greeting; mangpha khak is to say goodbye, and mangpha kikhak to say goodbye to each other) (e:amaute ~ khakin Makedonia gamah ka pai hi/khat-le-khat ~ ka kikhak khit uh ciangin | after we had said goodbye to each other/ka innah a om mite ~ ka vaikhak | I go and say goodbye to those at my home/~ a kikhak uh ciangin | when they said goodbye to each other) (r:47.2.13/44.21.6/42.9.61/44.20.37) (q:draft)
mangpi = (t:n) (w:governor) (d:mang, ruler, with pi, great: the governor of a land under the emperor) (e:Pontias Pilat ~ hi a) (s:mangpipa) (r:42.3.1) (q:draft)
mangpipa = (t:n) (w:governor) (d:mangpi, governor, with pa marking a man) (e:~ leh amau tawh a tukhawmte/~’ vaihawmna leh thukhente tungah a piak nadingun | so that they might hand him over to the governor's rule and the judges) (s:mangpi/menzipa) (r:44.26.30/42.20.20) (q:draft)
Mangpipa = (t:n) (w:governor/His Excellency) (d:mangpipa, governor, written with a capital as a title before or after the name, as Mangpipa Feliks, Governor Felix) (e:~ in lai a sim ciangin/~ Feliks kiangah lungdamna lai kong khak hi | I send a letter of greeting to Governor Felix/Feliks ~ in thong sungah khumin | Governor Felix having put him in prison/Alian ~ Feliks aw | most excellent Governor Felix) (b:mangpipa) (r:44.23.34/44.23.26/44.25.14/44.24.2) (q:draft)
mangpite = (t:n) (w:governors/officials/high officers) (d:plural of mangpi, a high official) (e:kumpite leh ~ mai-ah hong paipih ding uh/thukhente, ~, thuvante, uliante | the judges, officials, administrators and leaders/gam ukpi huhte, ~, sumkem mangte | the prefects, the governors, the treasurers) (s:mangliante/uliante) (b:mangpi) (r:42.21.12/27.3.2/15.4.9) (q:draft)
mangsa = (t:adj) (w:lost) (d:mang, be lost, with sa, already: that has gone missing; a mangsa is the lost one) (e:A ~ ka tuu mukik ka hih manin/A ~ ahih hangin tu-in kimu kik hi | he was lost but now is found/a ~ hong tungkik ahih manin | because the lost one has come back/a ~ na muh | the lost thing that you find) (s:mansuahsa) (r:42.15.6/42.15.24/42.15.32/5.22.3) (q:draft)
mangsak = (t:v) (w:drive away/get rid of/waste/make vanish) (d:mang, disappear, with the causative sak: make disappear, get rid of or waste; often follows another verb, as mut mangsak, blow away, and tum mangsak, plunge into ruin) (e:huih in hong mut ~ ding a/silngo lui na ~ khin un | get rid of the old yeast/mite kisiatna sungah a tum ~ thei hi | it can plunge people into ruin/na sum na pai a ~ | who wasted your money) (s:maimangsak/mangthangsak) (r:24.22.22/42.15.30/46.5.7/54.6.9) (q:draft)
mangsakte = (t:n) (w:those who lose) (d:mangsak cause to be lost, lose, with te, the people who do so) (e:hangah a nuntakna a ~ in/Kei hangin a nuntakna a ~ in | those who lose their life for my sake/Lungdamna Thu hang ahi zongin nuntakna a ~ in | those who lose their life for the gospel) (b:mangsak) (r:42.9.24/40.16.25/41.8.35) (q:draft)
mangsan = (t:v) (w:practise sorcery/divine) (d:in mangsan theite, where the English has sorcerers; perhaps divining by dreams) (e:na ~ theite uh) (r:24.27.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
mangte = (t:n) (w:officials/officers/commanders/magistrates) (d:plural of mang, officer: men in office or command, as galkap mangte, army commanders, and thukhen mangte, magistrates) (e:Thukhen ~ kiangah a tun’ uh ciangin/ama' nuai-a ~ nih' tungah Faro heh a | Pharaoh was angry with his two officials/amaute’ munah galkap ~ koih in | put army officers in their places/thukhen ~ in palik bute pai sakin | the magistrates sent the police officers) (s:uliante/ukte/mangpite) (b:mang) (r:44.16.20/1.40.2/11.20.24/44.16.35) (q:draft)
mangte = (t:n) (w:dreams) (d:plural of mang, dream) (e:ka ~ uh hong khiatsak a/a ~ bang a suak hiam i mu ding hi | we will see what becomes of his dreams/a ~ leh a thugente hangin | because of his dreams and his words/a ~ in a khiatna tuam ciat nei hi | the dreams each had their own meaning) (b:mang) (r:1.41.12/1.37.20/1.37.8/1.41.11) (q:draft)
mangte = (t:n) (w:those who obey/those who accept) (d:mang, obey, with the plural te: a mangte, the ones who obey or accept a word) (e:Ama teci pan’na thu a ~ in/a ~ in thupha a ngah zaw ding hi | those who obey it will be more blessed/Pasian’ thu za-a a ~ in | those who hear the word of God and obey it/ama thu a ~ a piaksa Kha Siangtho | the Holy Spirit given to those who obey him) (s:zuite/mangzote) (b:mang) (r:43.3.33/42.11.28/42.8.21/44.5.32) (q:draft)
mangthang = (t:v) (w:disappear/vanish/perish/pass away) (d:go out of sight or out of existence: disappear, be lost, perish) (e:Van leh lei a ~ ding hi/Milimte ~ khin ding hi | the idols will totally disappear/Khua a lum ciangin tua tui ~ a | when it is warm that water vanishes/A manlo tecite ~ ding a | false witnesses will perish/a kicing lote a ~ ding uh hi | what is incomplete will disappear) (s:maimang/beimang) (a:kilang) (r:40.24.35/23.2.18/18.6.17/20.21.28/46.13.10) (q:draft)
mangthangin = (t:v) (w:disappear/vanish) (d:mangthang, disappear, with the linking ending in: disappearing, and then) (e:khuamial sung mah-ah ~ kiphawk nawn lo) (b:mangthang) (r:21.6.4) (q:draft)
mangthangpak = (t:v) (w:disappear quickly/vanish soon) (d:mangthang disappear with pak, quickly, for a short while) (e:a ~ daitui tawh kibang lel hi) (r:28.6.4) (q:draft)
mangthangsak = (t:v) (w:lose/destroy/make vanish) (d:mangthang, be lost, with the causative sak: lose something, or cause it to perish) (e:ama nuntakna ~ leh/na bawl uh nate ~ loin | without losing what you have worked for/a itte in nuntakna a ~ ding hi | those who love it will lose their life/Tui luangkhiate bangin amaute ~ in la | make them vanish like water that flows away/siampi liante khempeuh a ~ ding hi | he will destroy all the chief priests) (s:mangsak/maimangsak) (a:gum) (b:mangthang) (r:41.8.36/63.1.8/43.12.25/19.58.7/27.11.22) (q:draft)
mangthangte = (t:n) (w:the lost/lost ones) (d:mangthang be lost or perish, with plural te: those who are lost) (e:a ~ zong loin, a liamte bawl loin/a ~ a zong ding le a honkhia dingin | to seek and to save the lost) (b:mangthang) (r:38.11.16/42.19.10) (q:draft)
mangthei = (t:adj) (w:obedient) (d:mang obey with thei able: who obeys; thu a mangthei naupangte, obedient children) (e:thu a ~ naupangte bangin piang un) (b:mang) (r:60.1.14) (q:draft)
