mankhia = (t:v) (w:seize and bring out/hunt down/catch) (d:man seize with khia out: catch and take out of a hiding place) (e:amaute zongin ka ~ ding a) (r:30.9.3) (q:draft)
mankhin = (t:v) (w:finish/complete/be finished) (d:man, finish, with khin, already: have finished, be completed) (e:a nasep a ~ hinapi-in/tua ahih ciangin amaute ~ hi | so they finished) (s:khinta) (b:man) (r:58.4.3/2.39.32) (q:draft)
mankhit = (t:v) (w:finish/have finished) (d:man finish with khit, which marks the action as completed; a mankhit ciangin is when he had finished) (e:A thunget a ~ ciangin a nungzuite khat in/Jesuh in a thugen a ~ ciangin | when Jesus had finished speaking/a gingte’ thugen a ~ phetin | as soon as the thunders had finished speaking) (s:zawhkhit) (r:42.11.1/42.11.37/66.10.4) (q:draft)
mankim = (t:adj) (w:all true/wholly true) (d:man true with kim, all, every one) (e:khempeuh a vekpi-in ~ hi) (r:43.10.41) (q:draft)
manlah = (t:v) (w:be busy/be occupied) (d:be taken up with work, with no time left for other things) (e:a tawntungin ~ den hi/Martha bek in na semin ~ mahmah ahih manin | because Martha alone was very busy working/nomau’ inn ding ciat lamin na ~ uh a | each of you is busy with your own house/Martha pen anpia-in a ~ hi | Martha was busy serving the food/meihal biaknate pia-in ~ uh hi | they were busy offering the burnt offerings) (r:20.31.27/37.1.9/42.10.40/43.12.2/14.35.14) (q:draft)
manlahin = (t:adv) (w:busily/being busy) (d:manlah be busy, with in; manlahin om is to be busy, taken up with one's affairs) (e:hua lai-ah ~ a om kalin/a haute zong ~ a om laitakun | while the rich too are busy) (b:manlah) (r:11.20.40/59.1.11) (q:draft)
manlahpih = (t:v) (w:be busy with/occupy oneself with/devote oneself to) (d:manlah be busy, with pih which adds the thing one is busy with) (e:tua bang thute a ~ loh nadingun/eite’ ~ dinga hong piak nasep | the work he has given us to be busy with) (b:manlah) (r:54.1.4/21.3.10) (q:draft)
manlan = (t:adv) (w:quickly) (d:form of manlang quick, used before pak) (e:hong hici ~ pak na hi hiam) (r:1.27.20) (q:draft)
manlang = (t:adv) (w:quick/swift/fast/rapid) (d:quick or swift, said of feet, days or help; hong manlang in is come quickly, and manlang takin is rapidly) (e:mi sisan suah dingin a ~ hi/keimah huh dingin hong ~ in | come quickly to help me/siamgante’ siam ciangtang sangin ~ zaw a | swifter than a weaver’s shuttle/Topa’ thu ~ takin kizel pakin | that the word of the Lord may spread rapidly) (r:45.3.15/19.38.22/18.7.6/53.3.1)
manlangin = (t:phrase) (w:at once/right away/quickly) (d:with a before it, a manlangin: at once, without delay) (e:Ka kiangah a ~ na hong pai/a ~ hong kum in | come down at once/nangma kiangah a ~ mi kong paisak hi | I sent for you at once/Jerusalem khua pan a ~ na paikhia in | leave Jerusalem at once) (b:manlang) (r:55.4.9/42.19.5/44.10.33/44.22.18)
manlangin = (t:adv) (w:immediately/quickly/in a hurry) (d:manlang, quick, with in: quickly, in a hurry, placed before the verb) (e:Judah khuapi khatah ~ pai a/Josef ~ paikhia a | Joseph hurried out/~ amaute delh un | pursue them quickly/mipa ~ hong pai-in Eli kiangah gen hi | the man came quickly and told Eli/~ hong kuan un la | come quickly) (s:thakhatin) (a:damdamin) (b:manlang) (r:42.1.39/1.43.30/6.2.5/9.4.14/29.3.11)
manlangte = (t:n) (w:those who are quick) (d:manlang quick with the plural te; here of feet quick to do evil) (e:gamtat siat ding a ~) (b:manlang) (r:20.6.18) (q:draft)
manlo = (t:adj) (w:false/untrue) (d:man, true, with lo, not: false, not true, said of words, witnesses and visions) (e:A ~ tecite mangthang ding a/Thu ~ na gen khia kei ding uh hi | do not spread false reports/hong gen uh thute a ~ mangmuhna | the things they tell you are false visions) (a:man/maan) (b:man) (r:20.21.28/2.23.1/24.14.14) (q:draft)
manlo = (t:adj) (w:worthless) (d:in bangmah manlo mite, good-for-nothing men) (e:bangmah ~ mite in Jefthah pawmin) (b:man) (r:7.11.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
manlohna = (t:n) (w:wrong/untruth/falsehood) (d:man true or right with loh not and the noun suffix na: what is not right; NIV evil) (e:siatna leh ~ thugenin nei hi) (a:manna) (r:19.10.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
manlote = (t:adj) (w:false) (d:plural of manlo; pasian manlote are false gods, idols) (e:Izipt mite’ pasian ~ tawh/pasian ~ lamah a paikhial lo mi | one who does not go astray to false gods) (s:zuaute) (b:manlo) (r:26.20.7/19.40.4) (q:draft)
manman = (t:adj) (w:regular/due/proper) (d:of what comes at its fixed time or in its fixed amount; a hun manman is the appointed time) (e:a hun ~-a a hong tun’ loh theih nadingin) (r:24.33.20/12.25.30) (q:draft, low confidence)
manmanin = (t:adv) (w:regularly/at the proper time/continually) (d:at each set time without fail, as of daily meals or regular offerings; a hun manmanin is at the proper time) (e:a ~ an ne hi/a hun ~ amaute’ nekzah ding ciat | each their share of food at the proper time/a ~ meihal biakna | the regular burnt offering/a ~ a hong tun loh theih nadingin | so that they no longer come at their set time) (b:manman) (r:12.25.29/12.25.30/40.24.45/16.10.32/24.33.20) (q:draft)
manna = (t:n) (w:manna) (d:the food God gave Israel in the wilderness, the Hebrew word kept in Zolai) (e:~ kici an zusak-in/daitui a kiat ciangin ~ tawh kia khawm hi | when the dew fell, it fell together with the manna/hih ~ sim loh bangmah om peuhmah lo hi | there is nothing at all except this manna) (s:mana/maana) (r:19.78.24/4.11.9/4.11.6) (q:draft)
manna = (t:n) (w:truth/uprightness/integrity) (d:man, true or right, with the noun suffix na: the fact of being true, or uprightness of heart) (e:na lungsim ~ hang uh tawh/hih thu a ~ hong kilangsak hi | it shows that this is true/hih thu a ~ teci a pang hi | testifies to the truth of this) (s:thutak) (a:manlohna/zuauna) (b:man) (r:5.9.5/20.30.5/64.1.12/62.5.6) (q:draft)
mannop = (t:v) (w:be willing to listen/be willing to obey) (d:man, the form of mang obey, with nop want; in the verses always with kei, refuse to listen) (e:thu nangawn a ~ kei leh/Moses le kamsangte’ thu a ~ kei uhleh | if they do not listen to Moses and the Prophets/na thu uh a hong ~ kei leh | if he will not listen to you/tua mite’ thu a ~ kei leh | if he refuses to listen to them) (r:40.18.17/42.16.31/40.18.16) (q:draft)
