manpa = (t:n) (w:dreamer) (d:in mang manpa, the man who has dreams; mang man is to dream a dream) (e:mang ~ ahi zongin kithat ding hi/tua kamsangpa ahi a, mang ~ thu ahi zongin | whether the word of that prophet or of the dreamer) (s:mangmanpa/mangman) (b:man) (r:5.13.5/5.13.3) (q:draft)
manpah = (t:v) (w:seize at once/arrest immediately) (d:man seize or arrest, with pah at once) (e:Amaute in tua pa ~ uh a/Jesuh ~ nuam uh hi | they wanted to arrest Jesus at once/mihonte kihta uh ahih manin ~ ngam lo uh hi | being afraid of the crowd they did not dare arrest him at once) (r:42.23.26/42.20.19) (q:draft)
manpha = (t:adj) (w:precious/valuable/costly) (d:of great worth or dearly valued; suang manpha is a precious stone, and manpha zaw is more valuable) (e:suang ~ pen a muh ciangin/suang ~ phutin a inn zeem hi | he adorned the house with precious stones/Mi khat in tuu sangin a ~ zaw hi | a person is more valuable than a sheep/Kham banga ~ Jerusalem tangval note | you young men of Jerusalem, precious as gold/Na a ~ a namkimin i sut ding a | we will plunder all kinds of valuable things) (s:amanpha) (a:mawkna) (r:40.13.46/19.116.15/14.3.6/40.12.12/25.4.2/20.1.13) (q:draft)
manphapen = (t:adj) (w:most precious/most valuable) (d:manpha precious with the superlative pen) (e:na neihsa a ~ bangin na kep ding/a mit nauta bangin a ~ khat | one most precious, like the pupil of his eye/a ~ suangmanpha nangawn sangin | than even the most precious jewels) (b:manpha) (r:20.4.23/38.2.8/20.3.15) (q:draft)
