manphate = (t:adj) (w:precious/valuable) (d:plural of manpha, placed after the noun it describes; van manphate are valuable goods, treasures) (e:kumpipa’ inn-a van ~ lakhia hi/namtui nate tampi tak, leh suang ~ pia hi | she gave many spices and precious stones/letsong ~ tawh huh thuah uh hi | they also helped with valuable gifts/Hezekiah kiangah na ~ hong puak uh a | they brought valuable things to Hezekiah) (b:manpha) (r:11.14.26/14.36.10/11.10.10/15.1.6/14.32.23) (q:draft)
manphateng = (t:adj) (w:all precious/all valuable) (d:manpha precious with teng, all of: na manphateng, all the valuable things) (e:na ~ khempeuh a la ding hi) (b:manpha) (r:27.11.43) (q:draft)
manphatna = (t:n) (w:value/worth/preciousness) (d:manphat, precious, with the noun suffix na: how much something is worth or how precious it is) (e:a ~ phawk thei lo uh hi/amah in pilna mu-in a ~ entel a | he saw wisdom and appraised its worth/A ~ a kigen zo lo Pasian’ hong piak | the gift of God whose worth cannot be told/a nasepte a ~ thei a | she knows the value of her work) (s:man) (b:manphat) (r:20.23.9/18.28.17/18.28.27/47.9.15/20.31.18) (q:draft)
manphazaw = (t:adj) (w:more valuable/more precious/worth more) (d:manpha, precious, with the comparative zaw: worth more; used with sangin, than) (e:kham sangin ~ hi/Gitta tampi sangin note na ~ uh hi | you are worth more than many sparrows/Zi hoih pen suangmanpha sangin ~ pek a | a good wife is worth far more than jewels/Suangmanpha sangin pilna ahi keimah ka ~ a | I, wisdom, am more precious than jewels) (b:manpha) (r:20.3.14/40.10.31/20.31.10/20.8.11) (q:draft)
mansa = (t:see) <mansa-in>
