mate = (t:n) (w:wounds/injuries/fractures) (d:ma, wound, with the plural te; also of nail marks and of cracks in the ground) (e:amah a liamsakna ~ Jezre-el ah/a kitam ~ mat kik in | mend its fractures/siktukkilh tawh a kikilhna ~ mu-in | seeing the marks where the nails were driven) (s:liammate/liamnate) (r:12.8.29/19.60.2/43.20.25) (q:draft)
mate = (t:n) (d:those who divorce, from ma divorce or send away a spouse, with the plural ending te) (e:zi a ~ in midang tawh) (r:40.5.32) (q:draft, low confidence)
mateng = (t:conj) (w:until/til/till) (d:placed after a verb: up to the time when something happens) (e:amaute a beitum ~ ka kileh kei hi/khapi a bei ~ nopna om ta hen | may prosperity abound till the moon is no more/a topa innah hong ciah ~ | until his master came home/a langpa in a thuk ~ | until the other side answers) (r:10.22.38/19.72.7/1.39.16/20.18.17)
mateng = (t:ppm) (d:postpositional marker indicating a certain span of time or distance, equivalent in usage to the prepositions up to, as far as, to) (e:nong ciahkik ~, an nelo ding hi ung/nitak ~ na sem uh hi | they work until evening/tuite a keu ~ leeng kawikawi hi | it kept flying about until the water dried up/a nitak ~ a nin hi ding hi | he will be unclean till evening/zingsang khuavak ~ amaute va sugawp ni | let us plunder them till dawn) (r:19.104.23/1.8.7/3.11.31/9.14.36)
matengin = (t:conj) (w:until/til/till) (d:mateng, until, with the linking ending in, placed after a verb) (e:a leiba a loh khit ~/Topa in hong en sukin a hong muh ~ | until the Lord looks down and sees/ama thugente a tun’ ~ | until his words came true/a vekpi-un a kisiat khit ~ ka ciahkik kei hi | I did not turn back till they were all destroyed) (b:mateng) (r:40.18.34/19.105.19/25.3.50/19.18.37)
matengin = (t:prep) (w:up till/up until/until) (d:mateng, up to, with the linking ending in, placed after a word of time) (e:zingsang ~ a inn kongkhak pua-ah kuamah paikhia lo ding | no one shall go out of the door of his house until morning/a kilaktoh ni dong ~ | until the day he was taken up/migilote’ adingin gum khat a kitawh hun ~ | until the time a pit is dug for the wicked/Hehna hun a kicing ~ amah gualzo ding hi | he will succeed until the time of wrath is completed) (b:mateng) (r:2.12.22/44.1.2/19.94.12/27.11.36)
matengun = (t:conj) (w:until/till) (d:form of mateng used when the subject is plural, placed after the verb) (e:tua khua pan na paikhiat ~ tua innah/tua inn ah na paikhiat ~ na om un | stay in that house until you leave/Na sih ~ hih mawhna hong kimaisak lo | till you die this sin will not be forgiven/leitang na luah ~ | until you take possession of the land) (b:mateng) (r:41.6.10/42.9.4/23.22.14/2.23.30) (q:draft)
