matin = (t:adv) (w:as captive/captured) (d:mat seize with in, in the state of being seized; gal matin is taken captive in war) (e:a tanute gal ~/Israel mite, gal ~ kipai khiatpih ding hi | the Israelites will be led away as captives/a hong mante, ~ om zaw ding uh hi | those who seized you will themselves be captives) (b:mat) (r:4.21.29/24.30.16/30.7.17) (q:draft)
matkhak = (t:v) (w:happen to catch/get hold of) (d:mat seize with khak, happen to: whoever one happens to lay hold of) (e:a gei-a a ~ mite manin) (r:38.14.13) (q:draft)
