maw = (t:intj) (d:word expressing surprise, joy or sudden emotion) (e:hotkhiatna hong tung taleh ~/ka mite nusia-in taisan thei hi leng ~ | oh that I could leave my people and go away/Topa in hong that khin hizaw taleh ~ | if only the Lord had killed us instead) (r:19.14.7/24.9.2/2.16.3)
mawh = (t:v) (w:sin/do wrong/be guilty) (d:do wrong against God or a person and so be guilty; with tawh also said of unlawful sexual relations) (e:~ i hih manin gimna i thuak hi/i sanggampa tawh kisai-in eite i ~ hi | we are guilty concerning our brother/ka mite a ~ semsem uh ut uh hi | they want my people to sin more and more/numei tungah a ~ hi | he sins against the woman/A ~ mi daan a pia thukhenpa | a judge who punishes the guilty man) (s:khialh) (r:25.5.16/1.42.21/28.4.8/41.10.11/20.24.25)
