mawhnate = (t:n) (w:sins/iniquities/transgressions) (d:mawhna, sin, with the plural te) (e:kote’ ~ na mai-ah na koih a/a ~ maisakin a khialhnate a seelcipsak mite | those whose sins are forgiven and whose wrongs are covered/ka ~ uh hong sawpkhiatsakin | washing away our sins) (s:khialhnate) (b:mawhna) (r:19.90.8/58.10.17/45.4.7/33.7.19) (q:draft)
mawhnateng = (t:n) (w:all sins/sins) (d:mawhna, sin, with teng, all: the whole of the sins) (e:Na ~ uh tu-in hong kipholak hi/a hauhnateng un a ~ uh loh zo lo hi | all their wealth cannot pay for all their sins) (s:khialhnateng) (b:mawhna) (r:26.21.24/28.12.8) (q:draft)
mawhnei = (t:n) (w:sinner) (d:mawh, sin, with nei, have: one who has sin, a sinner; often placed before mi, person) (e:siahdongte leh ~ tampite va pai uh/hih mi in ~ mi ahih | that this man is a sinner/Pasian aw, ~ keimah hong hehpih in | God, have mercy on me, a sinner) (s:mimawh/mawhneimi) (a:midik) (r:40.9.10/43.9.24/42.18.13)
