mawhneite = (t:n) (w:wrongdoer/wrongdoers) (d:those who are guilty of doing wrong) (e:~ tawh vak kawikawi hi/migilo leh ~, gimna kipiazaw kan ding hi | how much more will the wicked and wrongdoers be given suffering) (s:khialte) (b:mawhnei) (r:18.34.8/20.11.31)
mawhnopna = (t:n) (w:sinful desire/lust/immorality) (d:the desire to sin; with tawh, sexual sin with someone, adultery or fornication) (e:thukham ka theih ciangin ~ lungsim hong khangin/~ lungsim i neihnateng i sucip a | we put down all the sinful desire we had/zilepasal neisate tawh ~ | adultery with married people) (r:45.7.9/40.15.19/45.6.6/41.7.21) (q:draft)
mawhnopnate = (t:n) (w:sinful desires/sinful passions) (d:mawhnopna, the desire to sin, with the plural te) (e:i hihnop semsem ~ i gamta a) (b:mawhnopna) (r:45.7.5) (q:draft)
mawhpa = (t:n) (w:the guilty/guilty man/wrongdoer) (d:mawh sin or be in the wrong, with pa, a man: the one found guilty, opposite of a dikpa, the one in the right) (e:a dikpa khahin a ~ lelsak a/a ~ satna thuak dinga kilawm ahih leh | if the guilty man deserves to be beaten/a ~ mawhna thuaksakin | making the guilty man bear his guilt) (s:khialpa/mimawh) (a:dikpa) (b:mawh) (r:5.25.1/11.8.32/5.25.2) (q:draft)
