meeingo = (t:n) (w:bright cloud/white cloud/cloud) (d:meii cloud with ngo white; written meiingo in Matthew 17:5) (e:~ khat in amaute tuam a) (s:meiingo) (r:41.9.7) (q:draft)
meek = (t:v) (w:knead) (d:press and work dough with the hands) (e:annel lom la-in ~ a/~ manin mohin hong bawl in | knead it and make bread/moh bawlna ding annel ~ uh a | they knead dough to make cakes/a annel lom ~ a pawm mateng | from kneading the dough till it rises) (r:10.13.8/1.18.6/24.7.18/28.7.4) (q:draft)
meek = (t:v) (w:squeeze/strangle) (d:squeeze tight; gawl meek is squeeze the throat, strangle) (e:a gawl ~ kithat sa ahi zongin) (s:gawlmek) (r:44.15.28) (q:draft, low confidence)
meeka = (t:v) (w:strangle/squeeze) (d:meek, squeeze, with the linking a: gawl meeka kithat is killed by strangling) (e:gawl ~ kithat sa tawh) (s:gawlmek) (b:meek) (r:44.21.25) (q:draft)
meekin = (t:v) (w:kneading) (d:meek knead, with the linking ending in: kneading, and then) (e:annel ~ silngo sawhloh anlum em a) (b:meek) (r:9.28.24) (q:draft)
meekin = (t:v) (w:squeezing/choking) (d:meek squeeze, with the linking ending in; a gawl meekin is gripping him by the throat) (e:a muh ciangin a gawl ~) (b:meek) (r:40.18.28) (q:draft)
meekmeek = (t:v) (w:churn/keep squeezing/press) (d:meek squeeze said twice: press or work something again and again) (e:~ lehang thawhbat hong suak a) (r:20.30.33) (q:draft)
meekna = (t:n) (w:kneading) (d:meek, knead, with the noun suffix na; annel meekna kuang is a kneading trough) (e:na annel ~ kuangte uhah thupha om/na annel ~ kuangte un zong samsiatna ngah ding hi | your kneading troughs too will be cursed) (s:mekna) (b:meek) (r:5.28.5/5.28.17) (q:draft)
meel = (t:adj) (w:apparent) (d:the look of a person or thing, its form or colour: a hing meel is greenish, meel hoih is good-looking, and meel seel is hide the face or disguise oneself) (e:a hing ~ ahih kei leh a san ~ | greenish or reddish in appearance/A ~ kheksak gawpin na hawl mang hi | you change his countenance and send him away/a ~ na mu ngei kei uh hi | you have never seen his form) (r:3.14.37/18.14.20/43.5.37)
meelhoih = (t:adj) (w:beautiful/good-looking) (d:meel, appearance, with hoih, good: beautiful to look at) (e:zahin a ~ leitungah numei dang khat) (s:melhoih) (a:melsia) (r:18.42.15) (q:draft)
meelhoihna = (t:n) (w:beauty/good looks) (d:meelhoih, beautiful, with the noun suffix na) (e:thei lo numei ~ in) (s:melhoihna/etlawmna) (b:meelhoih) (r:20.11.22) (q:draft)
meelte = (t:n) (w:appearances/looks) (d:meel, appearance, the look of a thing, with the plural te) (e:a kilawmna a ~ zong a mangthang thei hi) (b:meel) (r:59.1.11) (q:draft)
meeltheihte = (t:n) (w:acquaintances/friends) (d:meel, face, with theih, know, and the plural te: people one knows by sight) (e:a behte a ~ lakah a zong uh a) (s:meltheihte) (r:42.2.44) (q:draft)
meen = (t:see) <meen'na>
meen'na = (t:n) (w:that on which something hangs/dependence) (d:meen, hang on, depend on, with the noun suffix na: a meen’na bulpi, the root on which all the rest hangs) (e:khempeuh a ~ bulpi hi) (r:40.22.40) (q:draft, low confidence)
meeng = (t:v) (w:sprout/bud/put out shoots) (d:of a tree or branch, to come out with new tender growth) (e:Theikung a hiang ~ a/hiang gol a ~ thei hi | it can put out big branches/Amaute ~ thakin oliv kung bangin | sprouting anew like an olive tree/leitung in a dawn ~ sakin | as the soil makes the sprout come up) (s:sel/po/dawnkhia) (r:41.13.28/28.14.6/41.4.32/23.61.11) (q:draft)
meengin = (t:v) (w:sprouting/budding) (d:meeng, sprout, with in, linking to the next verb) (e:Thei a hiang hong ~ a teh/kungnote ~ selkhia sak a | making the young plants bud and sprout) (s:mengin) (b:meeng) (r:40.24.32/23.55.10) (q:draft)
meengkhia = (t:v) (w:extend/branch out/project) (d:grow or stick out from the side of something, as the branches of the lampstand) (e:A pangte panin hiang guk ~ a/meivakkhuam hiang thum mah ~ ding hi | three branches of the lampstand shall likewise extend/a hiang gukte meivakkhuam panin ~ hi | the six branches extend from the lampstand/a pangpi uh panin a ~ mihing khut | human hands coming out from their sides) (b:meeng) (r:2.37.18/2.25.32/2.37.19/26.1.8) (q:draft)
meengmeeng = (t:adv) (w:quickly/in haste) (d:placed after a verb: do it at once, hurry to do it, as in delh meengmeeng, run quickly) (e:Puan hoih bel hong la ~ un/hehpihhuai sa-in delh ~ a | filled with compassion, he ran quickly) (s:mengmeng/meegmeeng/meng) (a:damdamin) (r:42.15.22/42.15.20) (q:draft)
meengmeenga = (t:adv) (w:quickly/hastily) (d:meengmeeng, quickly, with the linking a) (e:amah tho ~ a paikhiat a muh uh ciangin) (b:meengmeeng) (r:43.11.31) (q:draft)
meengsakin = (t:v) (w:make sprout/cause to bud) (d:meeng, sprout, with the causative sak and the linking suffix in) (e:leitung in a dawn ~) (s:selkhiasak/selsak) (b:meeng) (r:23.61.11) (q:draft)
meet = (t:n) (w:interest/profit/usury) (d:gain taken on money or goods lent) (e:A ~ a pung lakna tawh/A ~ bekbek lunggulhna-in sum leitawi pia lo | he does not lend money out of desire for interest/tung panin a ~ na dok kei ding uh hi | you shall not exact interest from him/a ~ ngah nading ka bawl ding uh hi | we will work to make a profit) (s:met/meetna) (a:supna) (r:20.28.8/26.18.8/2.22.25/59.4.13) (q:draft)
meet = (t:v) (w:shave/shear) (d:cut off hair or wool close to the skin: shave the head, shear a sheep) (e:a lu ~-in a cinte tan ding/a mul na ~ kei ding uh hi | you shall not shear their wool/a sam lom sagihte ~ sak hi | she had his seven braids shaved off/na ~ masak uh na tuumul na pia ding | you shall give the first wool you shear) (s:met) (r:5.21.12/5.18.4/5.15.19/7.16.19) (q:draft)
meetin = (t:adv) (w:at interest/for profit) (d:meet, interest or profit, with in: a meetin leitawi pia is lend at interest; in Philippians 3:9 it is said of gaining Christ) (e:tungah a ~ leitawi na pia thei/ama tungah a ~ sum leitawi pia loin | not lending him money at interest/ama sum a ~ a kha lo | who does not lend his money at interest/a ~ na lak uh sum | the money you took as interest) (b:meet) (r:5.23.20/3.25.37/19.15.5/16.5.11) (q:draft)
meetna = (t:n) (w:gain/profit/benefit) (d:meet, profit, with the noun suffix na: what one gets out of something, in the verses often dishonest gain) (e:~ lamah kihei uh hi/bang ~ om ahi hiam | what gain is there/amau ading ~ a zong bek ahi uh hi | they only seek gain for themselves/amau’ ~ ding bek ngaihsun uh hi | they think only of their own gain) (s:metna/phattuamna) (a:supna) (b:meet) (r:9.8.3/1.37.26/27.11.34/26.33.31) (q:draft)
meetsak = (t:v) (w:earn/gain/make a profit) (d:meet, profit, with the causative sak: make money bring in more, or bring gain to someone) (e:zakhat tawh tulkhat ka ~ hi/Hih lai-ah tulnga mah ka ~ hi | see, I have gained five thousand more/bangzah ciat a na ~ uh hiam | how much each of them had gained/sumsungte a ~ thei hi | he brought profit to the craftsmen) (b:meet) (r:42.19.16/44.19.24/40.25.20/42.19.15) (q:draft)
meette = (t:n) (w:shearers) (d:meet, shear, with the plural te: those who shear; gan mul meette are those who shear the wool of the animals) (e:ka gan mul ~ a dingin) (s:mette/mulmette) (b:meet) (r:9.25.11) (q:draft)
Mefa = (t:see) <Mefa-ath>
Mefa-ah = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Mephaath) (d:spelling of Mefa-ath in Joshua 13:18: town in the territory of Reuben east of the Jordan) (e:leh Kedemoth, leh ~) (r:6.13.18) (q:draft)
Mefa-ath = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Mephaath) (d:town on the plateau east of the Jordan in the territory of Reuben, given to the Levites of Merari and later held by Moab) (e:leh ~ a lonona gamte tawh) (r:6.21.37/24.48.21) (q:draft)
Mefaath = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Mephaath) (d:town on the plateau east of the Jordan in the territory of Reuben, given to the Levites of Merari and later held by Moab) (r:6.13.18/13.6.79)
Mefibosheth = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mephibosheth) (d:son of Jonathan and grandson of Saul, lame in both feet, to whom David showed kindness; also a son of Saul and Rizpah) (r:10.4.4/10.9.12)
Meggiddon = (t:name) (c:place/city) (w:Megiddo) (d:spelling of Megiddo in 1 Kings 9:15, a city that Solomon built up) (r:11.9.15)
Megiddo = (t:name) (c:land/city) (w:Megiddo) (d:city in the territory of Manasseh on the edge of the plain of Jezreel, with the plain and the waters named after it) (r:7.5.19/38.12.11)
meh = (t:n) (w:stew/soup/cooked dish) (d:cooked food eaten along with the staple, such as stew or vegetables; a kha meh is bitter herbs) (e:Khat vei Jakob in ~ huan hi/Tua ~ san tawm khat hong nesak in | let me eat a little of that red stew/Amaute khat ~ zong dingin gamlakah pai a | one of them went to the field to gather herbs/a kha ~ tawh ne ding uh hi | they shall eat it with bitter herbs) (r:1.25.29/4.9.11/1.25.30/12.4.39) (q:draft)
mehbeel = (t:n) (w:cooking pot/pot of stew) (d:meh, a cooked dish eaten with rice, with beel pot) (e:hong pai-in ~ sungah atnen hi) (r:12.4.39) (q:draft)
Mehetabel = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Mehetabel) (d:wife of Hadad king of Edom, daughter of Matred; the name also of an ancestor of Shemaiah in the time of Nehemiah) (r:1.36.39/13.1.50)
Mehida = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mehida) (d:ancestor of a family of temple servants who returned from the exile) (r:15.2.52/16.7.54)
Mehir = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mehir) (d:son of Kelub and father of Eshton, in the family line of Judah) (r:13.4.11)
Meholah = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Meholah) (d:home of Adriel, the husband of Merab daughter of Saul; Meholah mi is a man of Meholah, a Meholathite) (e:~ mi Adriel tungah a zi dingin) (r:9.18.19/10.21.8) (q:draft)
mehteh = (t:n) (w:herbs/leaf vegetables) (d:meh, a cooked dish, with teh, leaf: leaf vegetables or herbs; a kha mehteh is bitter herbs) (e:leh a kha ~ tawh amaute in) (s:anteh) (r:2.12.8) (q:draft)
mehtui = (t:n) (w:broth/soup) (d:meh, a cooked dish, with tui, water: the liquid of a stew, broth) (e:dawi biakna sa ~ a nei mite) (s:satui) (r:23.65.4) (q:draft)
Mehujael = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mehujael) (d:son of Irad and father of Methushael, a descendant of Cain) (r:1.4.18)
Mehuman = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mehuman) (d:one of the seven eunuchs who served King Xerxes) (r:17.1.10)
mei = (t:n) (w:fire) (d:fire, the flame that burns wood or an offering; also a lamp or light, and the first part of many words such as meikuang, flame, and meikhu, smoke) (e:Ama kam panin ~ kuangkhia a/Ama mai-ah ~ pai a | fire goes before him/Sing om kei leh ~ mit a | without wood a fire goes out/Biakna tau tungah ~ kikuangsak tawntung ding hi | the fire must be kept burning on the altar) (s:meikuang) (r:18.41.19/3.9.11/19.97.3/20.26.20/3.6.13) (q:draft)
mei-amsa = (t:n) (w:heat of flame/burning heat) (d:mei-am flame with sa hot; said of a body burning with fever) (e:ka pumpi uh ~ a bang hi) (r:25.5.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
mei-amte = (t:n) (w:burning coals/live coals/coals of fire) (d:plural of mei-am, a burning coal or ember: live coals, and in the Psalms flashes of fire from heaven) (e:lu tungah ~ a koih na hi/khuapi tungah a ~ theh in | scatter the coals over the city/a taang sung panin ~ kuangkhia hi | out of the brightness burning coals blazed) (r:45.12.20/26.10.2/10.22.13) (q:draft)
meiam = (t:n) (w:flame/live coals) (d:meiam luahna kuang, a pan for holding fire, NIV censer) (e:~ luahna kuang daite) (r:24.52.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
meibung = (t:n) (w:oven) (d:a closed fireplace for baking bread, from mei, fire) (e:nupi sawm in ~ khat sungah/~ sunga ki-em an tawh biakna | a grain offering baked in an oven/~ hita leh belpei hita leh kisuzan ding hi | whether oven or cooking pot, it must be broken up) (r:3.26.26/3.2.4/3.11.35) (q:draft)
meidawi = (t:adj) (w:fainthearted/cowardly/timid/afraid) (d:without courage, losing heart from fear; a meidawi is one who is faint or hangs back) (e:A lawmte ~ lawh kha ding/a lungsim ~ kua om na hi uh hiam | is anyone among you fainthearted/na galhangte a ~ ding uh hi | your warriors will be terrified/ka mite ~ sakin puk sak hi | it makes my people lose heart and fall/a ~ khat beek om lo hi | there is not one straggler) (s:lau) (a:hang) (r:5.20.8/26.21.15/31.1.9/23.14.31) (q:draft)
meidawilawh = (t:v) (w:become disheartened too/catch fear) (d:meidawi, fainthearted, with lawh, catch from another: lose courage because someone else has) (e:A lawmte ~ kha ding ahih manin) (r:5.20.8) (q:draft)
meidawina = (t:n) (w:timidity/cowardice/fear) (d:meidawi, fainthearted, with the noun suffix na: lack of courage) (e:~ lungsim hong guan lo a) (s:launa) (a:hanna) (b:meidawi) (r:55.1.7) (q:draft)
meidawisuah = (t:v) (w:turn cowardly/lose courage) (d:meidawi fainthearted with suah become: give way out of fear; NIV joined in hypocrisy) (e:Jew midangte zong hong ~ a) (r:48.2.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
meidawite = (t:n) (w:the fainthearted/the cowardly) (d:meidawi, fainthearted, with the plural te: those who have lost heart or have no courage) (e:a ~ hanthawnin/a ~, a lehtatte, a lampialte | the cowardly, the unbelieving, the vile) (b:meidawi) (r:52.5.14/66.21.8) (q:draft)
meigon = (t:see) <meigon'na>
meigon'na = (t:n) (w:widowhood) (d:meigong, widow, with the noun suffix na: the state of being a widow) (e:ta khuaisuahna leh ~/leh ~ hanga hong kikonate | and the reproach of your widowhood) (s:meigonna) (r:23.47.9/23.54.4) (q:draft)
meigong = (t:n) (w:widow) (d:a woman whose husband has died, also said as meigong numei; often named together with pa nei lote, the fatherless) (e:A zawng ~ khat hong pai a/a zi pen ~ numei hi ta hen | may his wife become a widow/ka nute uh a ~ khin uh hi | our mothers have become widows) (s:meigongnu) (r:41.12.42/42.21.2/19.109.9/25.5.3)
meigongin = (t:adv) (w:as a widow) (d:meigong, widow, with in: meigongin om is live as a widow) (e:kum li sung ~ a om ahi hi/~ om kei ning | I will never live as a widow) (b:meigong) (r:42.2.37/23.47.8) (q:draft)
meigongnu = (t:n) (w:widow) (d:a woman whose husband has died; nu marks a woman) (e:~ ka hi kei hi/nopsa-a a om ~ ahih leh | but the widow who lives for pleasure/Karmel khuami Nabal zi ~ Abigailte | Abigail, the widow of Nabal of Carmel/~ taktak ahi-te pawlpi in a vaak thei | the church can care for those who are truly widows) (s:meigong) (b:meigong) (r:66.18.7/54.5.9/54.5.6/9.30.5/54.5.16) (q:draft)
meigongnute = (t:n) (w:widows) (d:meigongnu, widow, with the plural te) (e:a khangno ~ in pasal a neih nading/A khangno lai ~ ahih uh leh | as for the younger widows) (s:meigongte) (b:meigongnu) (r:54.5.14/54.5.11) (q:draft)
meigongpa = (t:n) (w:widower) (d:meigong widow with pa marking a man; the verse has the son of a meigongpa where the NIV has the son of a widow) (e:Naftali minam ~’ tapa hi a | he was the son of a widow from the tribe of Naphtali) (b:meigong) (r:11.7.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
meigongte = (t:n) (w:widows) (d:meigong, widow, with the plural te) (e:misiangthote leh ~ sam a/~’ neihsa a ne mang uh a | they devour the property of widows/Judah mi ~ in nisim kivakna a ngah loh | the Jewish widows did not get the daily distribution/siampite’ zi ~ ten’pih ding uh hi | they may marry the widows of priests) (s:meigongnute) (b:meigong) (r:44.9.41/24.22.3/41.12.40/44.6.1/26.44.22)
meigonna = (t:n) (w:widowhood) (d:meigong, widow, with the noun suffix na: the state of being a widow) (e:ta khuaisuahna le ~/na ~ hangin hong kikonate | the reproach of your widowhood) (s:meigon'na) (r:23.47.9/23.54.4) (q:draft)
meihal = (t:adj) (w:burnt) (d:burned with fire, from mei, fire, and hal, burn; used in meihal biakna, burnt offering) (e:Amah in ~ biakna paipihin/~ biakna tau a nazatte khempeuh tawh | the altar of burnt offering with all its utensils/amah in ~ biakna ganhing a vun hawk-in | he shall skin the animal of the burnt offering/biakna tau tungah ~ biakna tawh tuate halkhawm hi | he burned them with the burnt offering on the altar) (r:3.9.16/3.1.6/2.31.9/3.9.14) (q:draft)
meihalna = (t:n) (w:burning) (d:mei, fire, and hal, burn, with the noun suffix na: a burning with fire, also the burning of offerings) (e:Topa in thukhenna leh ~ tawh/Judah mite in ~ tawh Baal bia-in | the people of Judah worshiped Baal with burning) (s:halna) (b:meihal) (r:23.4.3/24.11.17) (q:draft)
meihol = (t:n) (w:charcoal/coal) (d:charcoal, wood coal used for a fire; meihol cih is make a charcoal fire) (e:~ in mei am ding piangsak a/nasemte le palikte in ~ cih a | the servants and officials had made a charcoal fire) (r:20.26.21/43.18.18) (q:draft)
meii = (t:n) (w:cloud) (d:a cloud in the sky; meii lak panin is from within the cloud) (e:~ in mual tuam hi/~ tawh kha a khuh hi | he covers the moon with cloud/Leitung’ tungah ~ kong kaisak ciangin | when I bring clouds over the earth/~ sungah sakhituihup a kimuh leh | when the rainbow is seen in the cloud) (s:meiipi) (r:2.24.15/18.26.9/1.9.14)
meiilom = (t:n) (w:thick cloud/clouds) (d:meii, cloud, with lom, mass or bundle: a thick mass of cloud) (e:Amah in ~ lakah tuite khol a) (r:18.26.8) (q:draft)
meiilum = (t:n) (w:cloud/mist/morning mist) (d:a light cloud or mist that soon disappears, as in zingsang meiilum, the morning mist) (e:na khialhnate ~ bangin ka phiatkhia/zingsang ~ bangin theng pak a | it clears away quickly like the morning mist/leitung panin ~ kaaito-in | a mist rising up from the earth/~ in ka sam kawtsak hi | the mist has drenched my hair) (s:tuikhu/meiizun) (r:23.44.22/28.6.4/1.2.6/22.5.2)
meiingo = (t:n) (w:bright cloud/white cloud) (d:meii, cloud, with ngo, white: a bright cloud) (e:~ hong kaai vatin amaute hong khuh a) (s:meeingo) (r:40.17.5) (q:draft)
meiipi = (t:n) (w:cloud) (d:meii, cloud, with pi, great: a large or heavy cloud, such as a rain cloud) (e:tung san panin ~ a kilakkhiat/tuk-guah a zusak ~ tawh kibang hi | it is like a cloud that brings the spring rain/a liah dingin ~ kaaisak a | he spread a cloud as a covering/Amah in ~ nomsak a | he loads the clouds with moisture) (s:meii) (b:meii) (r:4.12.10/20.25.14/20.16.15/19.105.39/18.37.11)
meiipite = (t:n) (w:clouds) (d:meiipi, cloud, with the plural te) (e:vanpite pen ~ tawh tuamin/na thumanna in ~ banto hi | your faithfulness reaches to the clouds/~, na leeng dingin na bawl a | you make the clouds your chariot) (s:meiite) (b:meiipi) (r:19.147.8/19.108.4/19.104.3)
meiite = (t:n) (w:clouds) (d:meii, cloud, with the plural te) (e:~ in leitungah guahzu sak hi/amah in vantungah ~ kipsakin | when he established the clouds above/~ leh huih tawh van hong vom a | the sky grew black with clouds and wind/Van-a om ~ in guah hong zuksak theih nading | that the clouds in the sky may pour down rain) (s:meiipite) (b:meii) (r:20.3.20/20.8.28/11.18.45/18.38.34) (q:draft)
Meiite = (t:n) (w:clouds) (d:meiite, clouds, written with a capital at the start of a sentence or a line of verse) (e:~ bangzah takin sang ahi hiam/~ tungah a tuang pa la sak un | sing to him who rides on the clouds/~ a pai henhanna thu hita leh | how the clouds spread out) (b:meiite) (r:18.35.5/19.68.4/18.36.29) (q:draft)
meiivom = (t:n) (w:dark cloud/black cloud) (d:meii, cloud, with vom, black: a dark cloud) (e:ama khenuai-ah ~ sahpi a om hi) (s:meivom) (r:19.18.9) (q:draft)
meiizun = (t:n) (w:mist/dew/dampness) (d:fine moisture from cloud or night air that wets what it settles on) (e:~ in ka sam kawtsak hi/anlak nisa sunga ~ bangin | like a cloud of dew in the heat of harvest) (s:meiilum) (r:22.5.2/23.18.4) (q:draft)
meika = (t:see) <mu-meika>
