menzi = (t:n) (w:governor/tetrarch) (d:ruler of a province under a king or emperor: a governor, or a tetrarch such as Herod) (e:Galile gamah Herod ~ hi a/Kurinias in Siria gam ~ ahih lai takin | while Quirinius was governor of Syria/kumpi Agrippa le ~ Festas hong ding uh a | King Agrippa and Governor Festus rose/Abilene gamah Lisanias ~ hi a | Lysanias was tetrarch of Abilene) (s:mangpi) (r:42.3.1/44.26.30/42.2.2) (q:draft)
menzipa = (t:n) (w:governor/ruler/tetrarch) (d:menzi, governor, with pa marking a man; used of Felix the Roman governor and of Herod the tetrarch) (e:~ kiangah a lai puak uh pia-in/~ Feliks kiangah pai-in | going to Governor Felix/~ in a khut tawh a lah ciangin | when the governor motioned with his hand) (b:menzi) (r:44.23.33/42.3.19/44.24.1/44.24.10) (q:draft)
