met = (t:v) (w:shave/shear/cut hair) (d:cut hair or wool off close to the skin; sam met is cut the hair, lu met is shave the head, and tuu mul met is shear sheep) (e:a sam ~ ta hen/Laban a tuu mul ~ dingin pai khia a | Laban had gone out to shear his sheep/na baa samte uh ~ loin | do not cut the hair at the sides of your head/A kilawm ciang bek khat-in ~ ding uh hi | they are to trim it only to a fitting length/na dahna lim-un na sam uh ~ un la | shave your heads as a sign of your mourning) (s:meet/kiat) (r:46.11.6/18.1.20/1.31.19/3.19.27/26.44.20/33.1.16) (q:draft)
met = (t:n) (w:profit/gain/interest) (d:what is earned on money that is lent or traded: profit, interest) (e:dangka teng leh a ~ ka ngah khop/tawi sawm a ~ kingah zo hi | ten more have been gained as profit/a ~ bangzah a ngah uh hiam | how much profit they had made/a ~ lakna tawh hauh lawh uh hi | they grow rich by taking interest) (s:meet/metna/phattuamna) (a:supna) (r:42.19.23/42.19.16/42.19.15/26.22.12) (q:draft)
metbawl = (t:v) (w:trade/do business/make a profit) (d:met, profit, with bawl, make: trade with money so that it earns more) (e:a sangpa in a ~ leh) (b:met) (r:40.25.16) (q:draft)
