Methuselah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Methuselah) (d:son of Enoch, father of Lamech and grandfather of Noah) (r:1.5.21)
Methushael = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Methushael) (d:descendant of Cain, son of Mehujael and father of Lamech) (r:1.4.18)
metin = (t:v) (w:shaving/having shaved) (d:met, shave, with the linking ending in: shaving, having shaved, followed by another action) (e:a lu ~ a cinte tan ding hi/a khamul uh ~ a puan uh bal kek-in | having shaved off their beards and torn their clothes) (b:met) (r:5.21.12/24.41.5) (q:draft)
metkhia = (t:v) (w:shave off/cut off) (d:met, shave, with khia, out or off: shave hair off completely) (e:a khamul zong ~ ding hi/a mul khempeuh ~ ding hi | he must shave off all his hair/a puante sawpin, a mul khempeuh ~-in | washing his clothes and shaving off all his hair) (b:met) (r:23.7.20/3.14.9/3.14.8) (q:draft)
metna = (t:n) (w:shearing/shaving) (d:met, shear or shave, with the noun suffix na: the shearing of sheep or the shaving off of hair) (e:Nabal in a tuumul a ~/Sam at tanna, sam ~ a zum huai ahih leh | if it is a disgrace to have the hair cut or shaved off) (b:met) (r:9.25.4/46.11.6) (q:draft)
metna = (t:n) (w:profit/gain/benefit) (d:met, profit, with the noun suffix na: gain or benefit; bang metna om ahi hiam is what is gained) (e:ka sihna-ah bang ~ om ahi hiam/i thahna iim lehang bang ~ om ahi hiam | what do we gain if we cover up his death/keima ~ hong suak ding hi | it will turn out for my benefit) (s:met/meetna/phattuamna) (a:supna) (b:met) (r:19.30.9/1.37.26/23.38.17) (q:draft)
metsak = (t:v) (w:shave/shave off/have shaved) (d:met, shave, with the causative sak: shave another person's hair or beard, or have one's own hair cut off) (e:a khamul uh ~ a/a lu tunga a sam lom sagihte ~ hi | she had the seven braids of his hair shaved off/Kenkhrea munah a sam a ~ hi | at Cenchreae he had his hair cut off) (b:met) (r:13.19.4/7.16.19/44.18.18) (q:draft)
mette = (t:n) (w:shearers) (d:met, shear, with the plural te: those who shear; used after mul, hair or wool, as in tuumul mette, sheepshearers) (e:tuumul ~ khawm a/ka ganmul ~’ adingin ka gawh ka sate | the meat I have slaughtered for my shearers/a mul ~ mai-ah a kipaipih tuu | a sheep led before its shearers/Ganmul ~ na neihna ka za hi | I hear that you have shearers) (s:meette/mulmette) (b:met) (r:10.13.23/9.25.11/23.53.7/9.25.7) (q:draft)
mettol = (t:v) (w:shave/shave bald) (d:met, shave, with tol, bare: shave the head completely bald, often as a sign of mourning) (e:a lu uh ~ uh a/Amaute in a lu uh ~ loin | they must not shave their heads/na sam uh zong na ~ kei ding uh hi | you must not shave off your hair/a sam leh a khemul ~ ding a | he will shave the head and the hair of the legs) (r:26.27.31/5.14.1/3.21.5/23.7.20) (q:draft)
mettolna = (t:n) (w:shaving/shaving bald) (d:mettol, shave bald, with the noun suffix na; sam mettolna is shaving off the hair in mourning) (e:sam ~ leh puanhampi silh ding) (b:mettol) (r:23.22.12) (q:draft)
mettom = (t:v) (w:crop/cut short/shave short) (d:met shave or cut hair with tom short; a sam uh a mettom are those who crop their hair, where the NIV has those in distant places) (e:A sam uh a ~ amaute mun khempeuhah/a sam uh a ~ sehnel gam-a omte khempeuh | all who live in the desert and crop their hair) (s:tommet) (r:24.49.32/24.9.26) (q:draft, low confidence)
