Mezahab = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Me-Zahab) (d:grandparent of Mehetabel, the wife of King Hadad of Edom) (r:1.36.39/13.1.50)
mi = (t:n) (w:person/human being/people) (d:a human being, man or woman; with a number or quantity word it counts people, as in mi khat, one person, and mi tampi, many people) (e:Johan kici ~ khat Pasian in/~ a thatpa kithat ding hi | whoever kills a person must be put to death/a om bangin ~ khempeuh om ta uh hen | let every person remain as he was/~ tampi in a up beh uh hi | many more people believed) (s:mihing) (r:43.1.6/2.21.12/3.24.21/46.7.20/43.4.41)
Mi = (t:n) (w:person/man/one) (d:mi, person, written with a capital at the start of a sentence or in a title such as Mi Siangtho, the Holy One) (e:~ tawh kibatna-ah a suak hi/~ khat in tapa nih a nei hi | a man had two sons/~ khat in pawipi kham a | a man was preparing a great banquet/~ khat sangin mi nih hoihzaw hi | two people are better than one) (b:mi) (r:50.2.7/44.3.14/42.15.11/42.14.16/21.4.9) (q:draft)
miaimuai = (t:adv) (w:in throngs/in a great crowd) (d:descriptive word for a countless crowd standing close together) (e:a ding ~ vantung mite’ awging) (r:66.5.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
mial = (t:adv) (d:without being able to see or continuous) (e:zan bangin ~ a zawt uh hi | they grope blindly as in the night) (r:18.5.14)
mial = (t:adj) (w:dark) (d:without light; khua mial is it is dark, and of the eyes mial means dim) (e:khua~/Ni leh kha ~ a | the sun and moon are darkened/nai thum dongin leitung khempeuhah khua ~ hi | darkness was over all the land until three/Ni tumin khua a ~ khit ciangin | when the sun had set and it was dark/Dahna hangin ka mit ~ a | my eyes grow dim with grief) (r:1.15.17/19.35.6/29.3.15/40.27.45/19.6.7)
mial = (t:adj) (w:invisible)
mial = (t:adj) (w:lose face) (e:mai~)
miala = (t:adj) (w:dark) (d:mial dark with the linking a, and: khua miala, it was dark and) (e:khua ~ Zeisu amaute kiang) (b:mial) (r:43.6.17) (q:draft)
mialcipsak = (t:v) (w:darken completely/shroud in darkness) (d:mial dark, cip completely and the causative sak: make wholly dark) (e:ka pai nading lampi khua ~ hi/Topa in a heh manin Jerusalem khuapi a ~ hi | in his anger the Lord has covered Jerusalem in darkness) (s:mialsak) (a:khuavaksak) (r:18.19.8/25.2.1) (q:draft)
mialin = (t:v) (w:be dark/become dark/grow dark) (d:mial, dark, with the linking suffix -in: being or becoming dark, followed by another verb) (e:ni hong ~, kha, sisan hong bang/a taina lampi uh ~ nalsak in | make the path they flee on dark and slippery/tua meikhu hangin ni ~ khim a zing hi | because of the smoke the sun was darkened and it grew dark/ni hong ~ kha hong taang nawn lo ding a | the sun will be darkened and the moon will no longer shine) (b:mial) (r:29.2.31/19.35.6/66.9.2/40.24.29) (q:draft)
mialna = (t:n) (w:darkness/dark place) (d:mial, dark, with the noun suffix na: darkness; mialna mun is a dark place) (e:tua ~ pen nasia mahmah ding hi/leitung mun ~ khempeuh | all the dark places of the land/A ~ mun sunga sum kikoihte | treasures stored in dark places/thong sung a ~ mun a, a tu mite | those who sit in the darkness of the prison) (s:khuamial/khuamialna/khim) (a:khuavak/khuavakna) (b:mial) (r:40.6.23/23.45.3/19.74.20/23.42.6) (q:draft)
mialpha = (t:adj) (w:very dark/deeply dark) (d:mial dark with pha; said of how great a darkness is) (e:tua khuamial in a ~ mahmah hi) (r:40.6.23) (q:draft, low confidence)
mialsak = (t:v) (w:darken/make dark/dim) (d:mial, dark, with the causative sak: make dark, take the light away; of the eyes, make dim) (e:khitui in i mit hong ~ hi/amau mit ~ in la | darken their eyes/Vantung khuavak khempeuh ka ~ ding a | I will darken all the lights of heaven/leitungah khua ka ~ ding hi | I will make it dark on the earth/Topa in khua ~ a | the Lord brings darkness) (s:zingsak/ziingsak) (a:khuavaksak/vaaksak) (b:mial) (r:25.5.17/19.69.23/26.32.8/30.8.9/24.13.16) (q:draft)
mialta = (t:v) (w:become dark/be darkened) (d:mial be dark, with ta which marks a change that has now come about; khua hong mialta is it had grown dark) (e:Ni le kha ~ a/Ni le kha zong ~ a | the sun and moon too have grown dark/Khua hong ~ a | it had grown dark) (b:mial) (r:29.3.15/43.6.17/29.2.10) (q:draft)
mialzawt = (t:v) (w:grope/feel one's way) (d:mial dark with zawt feel about with the hands: grope as in the dark) (e:suntangpi-in zan bangin ~ uh hi/Khuamial lakah amaute in ~ uh a | they grope in the darkness) (s:zawt/zawtzawt) (r:18.5.14/18.12.25) (q:draft)
miamua = (t:adv) (d:describes insects settled close together in a swarm, after bawm) (e:kulh tungah a bawm ~) (r:34.3.17) (q:draft, low confidence)
Mibhar = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mibhar) (d:son of Hagri, one of David's mighty warriors) (r:13.11.38)
Mibsam = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mibsam) (d:name of two men: a son of Ishmael, and a descendant of Simeon) (r:13.1.29/13.4.25)
mibum = (t:n) (w:sorcery/enchantment/spell) (d:mi person with bum bewitch: casting spells on people; mibum theite are enchanters, mibum siamna is skill in spells) (e:mitphial siamte, ~ theite, le khongkhai siamte/~ siamna vang lianpi na neih hangin | although you have great power in casting spells) (s:bum/mibumna/bumna) (r:27.2.2/23.47.9) (q:draft)
mibumna = (t:n) (w:sorcery/witchcraft/magic spell) (d:mibum cast spells on people, with the noun suffix na) (e:na ~ le na aisannate ah/milim biakna, ~, kitot na’ng bawlna | idolatry, witchcraft, stirring up quarrels) (s:bumna/mibum/khongkhaina/aisan) (b:mibum) (r:23.47.12/48.5.20) (q:draft)
mibuppite = (t:n) (w:whole people/all the people) (d:mi people with bup whole, pi great and the plural te) (e:Israel ~’ adingin tuiphih biaknate) (s:minambup) (r:26.45.17) (q:draft)
Mibzar = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mibzar) (d:chief of Edom descended from Esau) (r:1.36.42/13.1.53)
micinate = (t:n) (w:sick people/the sick) (d:mi person with cina sick, plural te) (e:tua ~ khempeuh in damna) (s:cinate/veite) (r:44.5.16) (q:draft)
micing = (t:n) (w:guard/watchman) (d:mi person with cing keep watch) (e:Note in ~ pawlkhat na nei uh hi/Tuate in ~ pawlte tawh pai uh a | they went with the guard) (s:galvil/cingpa) (r:40.27.65/40.27.66) (q:draft)
micitakte = (t:n) (w:faithful people/faithful ones/saints) (d:mi person with citak faithful, plural te) (e:ka ~ ka kiangah hong khawm un) (r:19.50.5) (q:draft)
midang = (t:pron) (w:other/another/someone else) (d:another person, someone else; midang' before a noun is another person's) (e:Nang zong ~ na samsiat zelzelna/mi in ~ pilsak thei hi | one person sharpens another/amah pai-in ~ khat’ zi va suak a | she goes and becomes the wife of another man/~ kuamah in hong phawkpih kha lo hi | no one else can share it) (r:21.7.22/46.14.17/20.27.17/5.24.2/20.14.10) of people
midangpi = (t:n) (w:stranger/outsider/foreigner) (d:midang other person with the intensive pi: a complete stranger) (e:Ka sanggamte lakah ~ ka suak a/amau’ mai-ah ~ ka suak hi | in their eyes I have become a stranger) (s:khualmi/mikhual/gamdangmi) (b:midang) (r:19.69.8/18.19.15) (q:draft)
midangte = (t:pron) (w:others) (d:midang, another person, with the plural te: other people, the others) (e:~ in amah that ding hi/~’ noptuamna zong hen | let him seek the good of others/Ka khawhsa ante ~’ nek suak hen la | may others eat what I have sown/~ in sittel uh hen | let the others weigh what is said) (s:adangte) (b:midang) (r:1.9.6/46.10.24/18.31.8/46.14.29) of people
Middin = (t:name) (c:land/city) (w:Middin) (d:town in the wilderness of Judah) (r:6.15.61)
Midian = (t:name) (c:male/people/land) (w:Midian) (d:son of Abraham and Keturah, and the people and land named after him) (r:1.25.2/1.25.4)
Midiante = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Midianites) (d:Midian with the plural te: the people of Midian, a desert people who oppressed Israel until Gideon defeated them) (b:Midian) (r:7.6.1/7.6.7)
midik = (t:n) (w:righteous person/upright person/the righteous) (d:mi, person, with dik, right: a person who does what is right, one who is righteous before God) (e:~ khat in mawhna bawl leh/~ khempeuh lungdam a | all the righteous rejoice/~ Lot a gumkhia hi | he rescued righteous Lot/~ khat beek a om kei hi | there is not even one righteous person) (s:mipha/midikpa) (a:migilo/misia) (r:26.33.12/45.3.10/20.21.15/61.2.7) (q:draft)
Midik = (t:n) (w:righteous person/the righteous/Righteous One) (d:midik, righteous person, written with a capital at the start of a sentence or in the title Midik Pa, the Righteous One) (e:Tu-in tua ~ Pa a heekte/~ in migilopa’ inn sung encik a | the Righteous One takes note of the house of the wicked/~ tungah thu na khen uh a | you have condemned the innocent one) (b:midik) (r:44.7.52/20.21.12/59.5.6) (q:draft)
midikin = (t:n) (w:as righteous) (d:midik righteous person with in: as a righteous person; midikin sang is to count as righteous) (e:Pasian in amah ~ a sang hi/Pasian in mi khat ~ a sanna hangin | because God counts a person as righteous) (b:midik) (r:48.3.6/45.4.6) (q:draft)
midikpa = (t:n) (w:righteous man/the righteous) (d:midik righteous person with pa marking a man) (e:nangmah in ~’ lampi na neel sak hi/~’ lampi tamkim a | the path of the righteous is level) (s:dikpa/thumanpa/mihoihpa) (a:migilopa/gilopa) (b:midik) (r:23.26.7) (q:draft)
midiktatte = (t:n) (w:upright people/the blameless/the righteous) (d:mi person with diktat upright, plural te) (e:~ a hu hi) (s:midikte/mihoihte/thumante) (a:migilote) (r:20.2.7) (q:draft)
midikte = (t:n) (w:the righteous/the upright/righteous people) (d:midik, righteous person, with the plural te: the righteous, often set against migilote, the wicked) (e:Topa in ~ hu a/~ in migilote mudah a | the righteous detest the wicked/Topa in ~’ thungetna ngai a | the Lord hears the prayer of the righteous/~ a man-in gamta uh hi | the upright act rightly) (s:mihoihte/thumante/miphate/midiktatte) (a:migilote/misiate) (r:20.10.29/20.29.27/20.15.29/20.21.8) (q:draft)
Mifibosheth = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mephibosheth) (d:son of Jonathan and grandson of Saul, lame in both feet, who ate at King David's table; a spelling of Mefibosheth) (r:10.9.13)
Migdalel = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Migdal El) (d:fortified town in the territory of Naphtali) (r:6.19.38)
Migdalgad = (t:name) (c:land/city) (w:Migdal-gad/Migdal Gad) (d:town in the western foothills of Judah) (r:6.15.37)
Migdel = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Migdol) (d:town in northern Egypt where Jews settled after the fall of Jerusalem; a spelling of Migdol) (r:24.44.1)
Migdol = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Migdol) (d:place in northern Egypt near which the Israelites camped before they crossed the sea; later a town where Jews lived) (r:4.33.7/2.14.2)
migi = (t:adj) (w:kind/good/gracious) (d:good and kind in character, gracious; migi tuucing is the good shepherd; in Matthew 5:48 it stands for perfect) (e:~ tuucing ka hi hi/A thudik a ~ na tote | your masters who are fair and kind/Ama tungah kuamah ~ kei hen la | may no one be kind to him/a heh hak, a ~ mahmah | slow to anger and very gracious) (a:gilo) (r:43.10.14/56.2.5/60.2.18/19.109.12/32.4.2) (q:draft)
migilo = (t:n) (w:wicked person/the wicked/evildoer) (d:mi, person, with gilo, evil: a wicked person, one who does evil) (e:~ kiphasak khat ka mu hi/~ banga kampau ahihna | that he talks like a wicked man/mi kiphasak khempeuh leh ~ khempeuh | all the arrogant and every evildoer/Gilead pen ~ hontangte’ omna khuapi hi a | Gilead is a city of evildoers) (s:misia/gilomi/gilopa) (a:midik/mipha) (r:19.37.35/18.34.36/39.4.1/28.6.8) (q:draft)
migiloin = (t:n) (w:as wicked/as evil) (d:migilo wicked person with in: as a wicked person) (e:~ kei hong seh uh hi/hong simmawhin ~ hong seh ciangin | when they insult you and count you as evil) (b:migilo) (r:18.17.8/42.6.22) (q:draft)
migilopa = (t:n) (w:wicked man/the wicked) (d:migilo with pa marking a man, the wicked one) (e:Mi dang a nengniam ~ in/Midik in ~’ inn sung encik a | the Righteous One takes note of the house of the wicked man/Mizawngte a uk ~ in | a wicked man who rules over the poor/~’ deihnate tangtungsak kei in la | do not grant the wicked man his desires) (s:gilopa) (a:midikpa/dikpa) (b:migilo) (r:18.15.20/20.21.12/20.28.15/19.140.8) (q:draft)
migilote = (t:n) (w:the wicked/evildoers/sinners) (d:migilo, wicked person, with the plural te: the wicked, evildoers; in the Gospels also sinners) (e:Pasian in ~ khut sungah kei hong pia hi/~ tawh ka tukhawm kei ding hi | I will not sit with the wicked/siahdongte leh ~ khempeuh | all the tax collectors and sinners/~’ suan-le-khakte kipuaseh ding hi | the descendants of the wicked will be cut off) (s:misiate/gamtatsiate) (a:midikte/mihoihte) (b:migilo) (r:18.16.11/20.10.29/19.26.5/42.15.1/19.37.38) (q:draft)
migina = (t:n) (w:worthy man/man of standing/respectable person) (d:mi person with gina worthy; migina lo is a nobody, a worthless person) (e:nang ~ na hi a/Boaz min nei a hau ~ khat | a rich man of standing named Boaz/~ lote pen miliante tungah kiphasak ding uh hi | the nobody will be insolent to the honoured) (r:11.1.42/8.2.1/23.3.5) (q:draft)
miginalo = (t:n) (w:worthless person/scoundrel/good-for-nothing) (d:migina, a worthy person, with the negative lo: a worthless or bad person; in Hebrews 5:3 it is said of a weak, imperfect man) (e:~ pa, a gilo pa, thuzuau genin/Ui bangin a ~, a gitloh gamtat | worthless like dogs, acting wickedly/Amah zong ~ mi mah ahih manin | because he too is a weak man) (a:migina) (b:migina) (r:20.6.12/50.3.2/58.5.3) (q:draft)
miginate = (t:n) (w:the blameless/people of integrity/worthy people) (d:plural of migina: people of worth and good character, the blameless) (e:mi thuman, ~, hih i leitungah) (s:ginate/mawhbaanglote) (a:migilote) (b:migina) (r:20.2.21) (q:draft)
migit = (t:v) (w:show favor/be gracious/be kind) (d:the form of migi, kind, used before hangin, nading and mahmahna: be kind or gracious to someone, the person taking tungah) (e:Mi gilote tungah na ~ hangin/kei tungah hih kumpipa hong ~ nading | so that this king may be kind to me/Pasian a ~ mahmahna le a khauh mahmahna | the great kindness and the great sternness of God) (b:migi) (r:23.26.10/16.1.11/45.11.22) (q:draft)
migitna = (t:n) (w:kindness/goodness/benefit) (d:migit, be kind, with the noun suffix na: kind and generous dealing with others; migitna lak is show kindness) (e:ama ~ ka mangngilh kei ding hi/Ama tungah ~ kuamah in lak kei hen | may no one show him kindness/ama tungah ~ ka lah theih nading | so that I may show him kindness/lungduaina, ~, hoihna, cihtakna | patience, kindness, goodness, faithfulness) (s:gitna) (b:migit) (r:19.103.2/19.109.12/10.9.1/48.5.22) (q:draft)
Migron = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Migron) (d:place in Benjamin near Gibeah, on the Assyrian line of march toward Jerusalem) (r:9.14.2/23.10.28)
mih = (t:v) (w:go out/be quenched/be extinguished) (d:of fire, go out; the form of mit, go out, used in mei a mih ngei lohna, where the fire never goes out) (e:Mei a ~ ngei lohna hell) (r:41.9.43) (q:draft)
mihai = (t:n) (w:fool/foolish person/madman) (d:mi, person, with hai, foolish: a fool, the opposite of mipil, a wise person) (e:a cih uh hangin ~ suak uh a/mi a gensiate in ~ ahi hi | whoever slanders others is a fool/makaite pen ~ bangin gamta sak hi | he makes leaders act like fools/Zuau gen-a ~ hihna sangin | than being a fool who tells lies) (s:mimawl) (a:mipil) (r:45.1.22/18.12.17/20.10.18/20.19.1) (q:draft)
mihaipa = (t:n) (w:fool/foolish man) (d:mihai, fool, with pa marking a man: a foolish man, often set against mipilpa, the wise man) (e:~ adingin lametna om zawlai hi/~ in a ngah zahzah zangkhia pah hi | the fool uses up at once all he gets/~’ leenggui lo ka nawk kha hi | I passed the vineyard of a fool/~ sangin mipilpa a hamphat zawkna | the advantage of the wise man over the fool) (s:haipa) (a:mipilpa) (b:mihai) (r:20.29.20/18.5.2/20.21.20/20.24.30/21.6.8) (q:draft)
mihaipi = (t:n) (w:great fool/fool/stupid person) (d:mihai, fool, with pi, great: a great fool, a thoroughly stupid person) (e:a tawpna-ah ~ a suak ding hi/~-in kote hong seh na hi hiam | do you count us as stupid) (b:mihai) (r:24.17.11/18.18.3) (q:draft)
mihaite = (t:n) (w:fools) (d:plural of mihai: fools, often set against mipilte, the wise) (e:~ in haina thu gen hi/~ in satna thuak hi | fools receive beatings/~ in a haina tangkoko hi | fools proclaim their folly/ki-itna lungsim tawh ~ na thuak uh hi | you gladly put up with fools) (s:haite/pillote) (a:mipilte) (b:mihai) (r:20.15.2/21.10.6/20.19.29/20.13.16/47.11.19) (q:draft)
mihatte = (t:n) (w:the strong/strong men/the mighty) (d:mi, person, with hat, strong, and the plural te: strong or mighty people) (e:~ in a hatna uh kisak theihpih/amah in ~ tawh nate a hawm ding hi | he will divide the spoils with the strong) (s:thahatte/hatte) (a:thanemte) (r:24.9.23/23.53.12) (q:draft)
mihau = (t:n) (w:rich person/wealthy person) (d:mi, person, with hau, rich: a rich or wealthy person, the opposite of mizawng, a poor person) (e:amah ~ mahmah khat ahi hi/~ ahi Josef a kici mi khat | a rich man called Joseph/milian mineu, ~ mizawngte aw | great and small, rich and poor/Khatvei, ~ mahmah khat om a | once there was a very rich man) (a:mizawng) (r:10.19.32/19.49.2/40.27.57/42.16.19) (q:draft)
mihaupa = (t:n) (w:rich man) (d:mihau, rich person, with pa marking a man) (e:~ pen amah pil kisa a/amah a hu dingin ~ in ngaihsun kha hi | the rich man imagines it will protect him/A cingh ~’ maipha ngah ding ki-ut ciat a | everyone wants the favour of a generous rich man) (s:haupa) (a:mizawngpa) (b:mihau) (r:20.28.11/20.13.8/20.18.11/20.19.6) (q:draft)
mihaute = (t:n) (w:the rich/rich people) (d:plural of mihau: rich people, often set against mizawngte, the poor) (e:~ in lawm tampi nei hi/Hauhna in ~ hu a | wealth protects the rich/~ kiniam koih suk hi | the rich are put in low places/mizawngte sangin ~ thupi ngaihsut zaw tuan lo | he does not regard the rich above the poor) (s:haute) (a:mizawngte) (b:mihau) (r:20.14.20/20.10.15/21.10.6/18.34.19) (q:draft)
mihing = (t:n) (w:human/human being) (e:Gam sung late ~ suak ngei ding/Kei’ kitotpihpa in ~ hi lo hi | the one I argue with is not a human being/Topa in ~ lungsim meivak bangin zang a | the Lord uses the human spirit as a lamp) (s:mi) (r:18.11.12/18.21.4/20.20.27)
mihing = (t:n) (w:man/mankind) (e:leitungah ~ a om cil-a kipanin/~ in ama lungkham nading mah piangsak hi | man brings about his own trouble/~’ tapa ahi zongin muang kei un | do not trust in a son of man) (r:18.20.4/1.1.26/18.5.7/19.146.3) where it is not necessarly referring to just a male man
Mihing = (t:n) (w:Man) (d:mihing, man, written with a capital in the title Mihing Tapa, the Son of Man) (e:~ Tapa hong kum ciangin/~ Tapa in Nipi ni ukpa ahi hi | the Son of Man is Lord of the Sabbath/~ Tapa a kilat ni ciangin | on the day the Son of Man is revealed) (b:mihing) (r:40.24.37/43.3.14/42.6.5/42.17.30) (q:draft)
mihingin = (t:adv) (w:as a human/as a human being/as a man) (d:mihing, human, with the marker in: as a human being, in human life) (e:leitungah ~ i suah laitakin/Leitungah ~ Jesuh a omlai-in | while Jesus lived on earth as a man/~ a pian’ ni a samsia hi | he cursed the day he was born as a human) (b:mihing) (r:54.6.7/58.5.7/18.3.1) (q:draft)
mihingte = (t:n) (w:humans/human beings/mankind) (e:~ lakah nuam ka sa hi/Pasian in ~ ze-et hi | God tests human beings/~’ khut tawh a kibawl | made by human hands) (b:mihing) (r:20.8.31/19.78.60/21.3.18/19.135.15) plural form of <mihing>
mihoih = (t:adj) (w:righteous) (e:~ pawlkhat in tua puante silhin/mi in ~ ahih manin nungta ding hi | because that man is righteous he will live/~ khat in a gamtat hoihna teng khawlin | if a righteous person stops doing good) (s:thuman/dik) (a:gilo) (r:18.27.17/20.25.26/26.18.9/26.18.24)
mihoih = (t:adj) (w:upright) (e:mi citak ~ ahihna | that he is honest and upright/Leitungah ~ teng bei khin ta a | the upright have all vanished from the land) (s:thutang/diktat) (r:20.20.11/33.7.2)
mihoihin = (t:adj) (w:righteous) (d:mihoih, a good or righteous person, with the marker in: as righteous; with sang, accept, it says that God counts someone righteous) (e:Pasian in ~ a sang hi/i upna hangin ~ hong kisang ding hi | because of our faith we will be counted righteous/Topa’ thu sungah ~ na sang unla | receive her in the Lord as a good person) (b:mihoih) (r:45.4.3/45.4.24/45.16.2)
mihoihpa = (t:n) (w:good man/righteous man/the righteous) (d:mihoih, good person, with pa marking a man, often set against migilopa, the wicked man) (e:Mawhneipa sangin ~ hampha zaw tuan lo/~, ama hoihtatna in hu hi | the good man is protected by his good conduct) (s:midikpa/miphapa) (a:migilopa) (b:mihoih) (r:21.9.2/20.14.32) (q:draft)
mihoihte = (t:n) (w:the righteous/the upright/good people) (d:plural of mihoih: good or righteous people, often set against migilote, the wicked) (e:~ in thupha ngah a/Topa in ~ a gil kialin koih lo a | the Lord does not let the righteous go hungry/~ in a deihdeih uh ngah uh hi | the righteous get what they desire/~’ gamtat bangin na gamta ding a | you will walk in the ways of the good) (s:midikte/miphate) (a:migilote/misiate) (b:mihoih) (r:20.10.6/20.10.7/20.10.3/20.10.24/20.2.20) (q:draft)
mihoihteng = (t:n) (w:the good/all good people) (d:mihoih, good person, with teng, all: all the good people there are) (e:Leitungah ~ bei khinta a/~ si khinta hi | all the good people have died) (b:mihoih) (r:33.7.2) (q:draft)
mihon = (t:n) (w:community/congregation/assembly/crowd) (d:mi, person, with hon, flock or group: a gathered body of people, a community, congregation or crowd) (e:Israel ~ khempeuhin hih ding uh hi/~ lakah ding-in huhna ka ngen hi | I stand in the assembly and ask for help/~ tampi sungah Topa ka phat ding hi | in the great congregation I will praise the Lord/Israel ~ buppi phun uh a | the whole community of Israel grumbled) (s:mipi/honpi) (r:2.12.47/18.30.28/19.26.12/2.16.2) (q:draft)
Mihon = (t:n) (w:assembly/congregation/crowd) (d:mihon written with a capital at the start of a sentence or a line of verse) (e:~ laizangah nangmah phatna la ka sa ding hi/~ tampi in amah zui uh a | large crowds followed him/~ a paina a zak ciangin | when he heard the crowd going by) (b:mihon) (r:58.2.12/40.19.2/42.18.36) (q:draft)
mihonpi = (t:n) (w:crowd/multitude) (d:mihon, crowd, with pi, great: a large crowd, a multitude) (e:~ lei tungah tusak un/~ in a nung a zui uh hi | large crowds followed him/kuama sim zawh loh ~ | a great multitude that no one could count/siampi liante in ~ a hansuah uh hi | the chief priests stirred up the crowd) (s:honpi/mipi) (b:mihon) (r:40.15.35/40.23.1/40.8.1/66.7.9/41.15.11) (q:draft)
mihonpite = (t:n) (w:crowds/multitudes) (d:plural of mihonpi: great crowds, multitudes) (e:~ in Zeisu tawh a paikhawm uh hi/~ in Topa’ thuhilhna lamdang a sa uh hi | the crowds were amazed at his teaching/Zeisu in ~ sam a | Jesus called the crowd/vantungah a om ~’ aw | the voice of a great multitude in heaven) (s:mipite/mihonte) (b:mihonpi) (r:42.14.25/40.7.28/40.15.10/66.19.1) (q:draft)
Mihonpite = (t:n) (w:crowds/multitudes/hosts) (d:mihonpite written with a capital at the start of a sentence; Mihonpite’ Pasian is the God of hosts, NIV God Almighty) (e:~’ Pasian min nei Topa in ci hi/~ in lampi-ah amau puante a phah uh hi | the crowd spread their cloaks on the road/~ lakah mi khat in | a man in the crowd) (b:mihonpite) (r:30.5.27/40.21.8/41.9.17) (q:draft)
mihonte = (t:n) (w:crowds/assembly/community/congregation) (d:plural of mihon: crowds, or the whole body of a community or assembly) (e:~ in tua thu a zak uh ciangin/kikhopna buk kongah Israel ~ khempeuh khawm in | gather the whole assembly of Israel at the entrance to the tent of meeting/siatna bawl ~ ka mudah a | I hate the assembly of evildoers/~ khempeuh’ muhin Hor Mual tungah | on Mount Hor in the sight of the whole community) (s:mihonpite/mipite) (b:mihon) (r:40.22.33/3.8.3/19.26.5/4.20.27) (q:draft)
Mijamin = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mijamin) (d:name of several men, among them the head of the sixth priestly division and a priest who sealed the covenant with Nehemiah) (r:16.10.7/16.12.5)
Mika = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mika) (d:name of several men, among them the young son of Mephibosheth and a Levite who sealed the covenant with Nehemiah) (r:10.9.12/16.11.22) (q:draft)
Mikah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Micah) (d:name of several men, among them an Ephraimite who made a shrine in the days of the judges and the prophet from Moresheth) (r:7.17.12/13.5.5)
Mikaiah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Micaiah) (d:name of several people, among them the prophet, son of Imlah, who foretold the death of Ahab, and the son of Gemariah who reported what Baruch read) (r:24.36.11/24.36.13)
Mikhael = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Michael) (d:name of several men, and of the chief angel who fights for Israel) (r:4.13.13/13.6.40)
Mikhal = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Michal) (d:younger daughter of King Saul and wife of David) (r:10.6.23/9.18.28)
mikhat = (t:pron) (w:someone/anyone/a person) (d:mi, person, with khat, one, written as one word: someone, anyone; with suak or ahi it means one people, one and the same) (e:Zeisu sam dingin ~ a sawl uh hi/ka kisaktheihna ~ in hong sukgawp sangin | rather than have anyone destroy my boast/a suanpa leh tui buakpa in ~ ahi uh a | the one who plants and the one who waters are one/note tawh kote hong tengin ~ i suak ding hi | we will live with you and become one people) (r:41.3.31/46.8.3/46.9.15/46.3.8/1.34.16) (q:draft)
mikheemte = (t:n) (w:deceivers/impostors) (d:mi, person, with kheem, deceive, and the plural te: deceivers, impostors) (e:~ bang ahi zongin) (s:mikhemte/kheemte/khemte) (r:47.6.8) (q:draft)
mikhem = (t:v) (w:deceive people/be deceitful/cheat) (d:mi person with khem deceive; mikhem theite and mikhem hatte are deceivers, the treacherous) (e:~ theite aw, note’ tungah bang/~ hatte gualzo sese ahi uh hiam | why do the treacherous prosper) (r:19.120.3/24.12.1) (q:draft)
mikhempeuh = (t:pron) (w:everyone/all people/everybody) (d:mi person with khempeuh all, written as one word; usually written mi khempeuh) (e:mi ukte leh ~ tungah) (s:mikim/milip) (a:kuamah) (r:16.4.14/60.2.17) (q:draft)
mikhemte = (t:n) (w:deceivers/deceitful people) (d:mikhem deceive people, with plural te: those who deceive) (e:mizuaute leh ~ kiang panin/mi a thatte leh ~ pen | the bloodthirsty and the deceitful) (s:khemte/kheemte/mikheemte) (b:mikhem) (r:19.120.2/19.55.23) (q:draft)
mikhial = (t:n) (w:falsehood)
mikhialte = (t:n) (w:falsehoods) (b:mikhial)
Mikhialte = (t:n) (w:deceitful people/false people) (d:mi person with khial go wrong and the plural te; in the verse the people the psalmist does not sit with, the deceitful in the NIV) (e:~ tawh tukhawm loin, thusim neite tawh) (s:mikhemte/kheemte) (b:mikhialte) (r:19.26.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
mikhual = (t:n) (w:stranger/foreigner/sojourner) (d:mi, person, with khual, guest: a person from elsewhere who stays among others, often paired with peemta) (e:~ bangin hong bawl a/~ leh peemta bangin | like a foreigner and a stranger/ka gamsung uhah ~ bangin om-in | being like a stranger in our land/kei tawh a omkhawm ~ leh peemtate | foreigners and strangers who live with me) (s:khualmi/peemta/gamdangmi) (a:tualsuak/gammi) (r:18.19.15/3.25.23/3.25.35/24.14.8) (q:draft)
mikhualpi = (t:n) (w:complete stranger/utter stranger) (d:mikhual stranger with the intensifying pi) (e:kiangah ~ ka suak hi) (s:midangpi) (b:mikhual) (r:18.19.13) (q:draft)
mikhualte = (t:n) (w:strangers/foreigners/sojourners) (d:plural of mikhual: foreigners who live among another people, paired with peemtate) (e:nangma mai-ah ~ leh peemtate ka hi) (s:khualmite/peemtate/khualte) (b:mikhual) (r:13.29.15) (q:draft)
mikician = (t:n) (w:capable person/able man/reliable person) (d:mi person with kician sound, reliable; in the verse of several men) (e:siamna a nei ~ ahi uh hi) (s:misiam) (r:13.26.8) (q:draft)
mikim = (t:pron) (w:each one/everyone/each person) (d:mi, person, with kim, every: each person, everyone; mikim tungah is to each one) (e:~ tungah a pia hi/ama deihna bangin ~ tungah a hawmsak hi | he distributes to each one as he wills/Pasian in ~ tunga hong hawmsak upna | the faith God has distributed to each one/~ in a sapna tawh kituakin | each according to his need) (s:milip/mikhempeuh) (r:46.12.7/45.14.5/46.12.11/45.12.3/44.4.35) (q:draft)
Mikloth = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mikloth) (d:Benjamite of Gibeon, father of Shimeah, in the family line of King Saul) (r:13.9.38/13.9.37)
Mikmas = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Mikmash) (d:town of Benjamin north of Jerusalem, also written <Mikmash>) (e:~ khua-ah a van uh hong seng) (r:23.10.28/15.2.27) (q:draft)
Mikmash = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Mikmash) (d:town of Benjamin north of Jerusalem, where Jonathan attacked the Philistine outpost at the pass) (r:9.13.23/16.11.31)
Mikmethath = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Mikmethath) (d:place east of Shechem on the border between Ephraim and Manasseh) (r:6.17.7/6.16.6)
Mikneiah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mikneiah) (d:Levite gatekeeper who played the harp when David brought the ark to Jerusalem) (r:13.15.21/13.15.18)
Mikonah = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Mekonah) (d:town in the south of Judah settled again after the exile) (r:16.11.28)
Mikri = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mikri) (d:Benjamite, ancestor of Elah who lived in Jerusalem after the exile) (r:13.9.8)
miksite = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:ants) (d:plural of miksi, ant) (e:~ kiangah pai in la/~: a hat het lo ganhing hi napi-in | ants: creatures with no strength at all, yet) (r:20.6.6/20.30.25) (q:draft)
Milalai = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Milalai) (d:musician in the procession at the dedication of the wall of Jerusalem under Nehemiah) (r:16.12.36)
Miletas = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Miletus) (d:port city on the west coast of Asia Minor, where Paul met the elders of the church of Ephesus) (r:44.20.17/44.20.15)
milian = (t:n) (w:great person/the great) (d:mi, person, with lian, great: a person of high standing or power, the opposite of mineu) (e:Tua lai-ah ~ mineu omkhawm a/Note laka ~ a suak nuamte | those among you who want to become great/~ kineih kei in | do not make yourself out to be great/Tua ta in ~ hi ding a | that child will be great) (s:lianpa) (a:mineu) (r:18.3.19/58.7.7/40.20.26/20.25.6/42.1.32) (q:draft)
milianin = (t:n) (w:great person/the great) (d:milian great person with the marker in, here as or into: made them great) (e:mineute, ~ a bawl hi) (b:milian) (r:42.1.52) (q:draft)
milianpi = (t:n) (w:great man/very great person/somebody) (d:milian, great person, with the intensive pi: a very great person, somebody of importance) (e:a neupente ~ suak ding hi/~ a suak mipa | the man who became great/Nektawm ding nei lopi-in ~ bang-a omna sangin | than living like somebody great with nothing to eat) (b:milian) (r:23.60.22/10.23.1/20.12.9) (q:draft)
miliante = (t:n) (w:nobles/great men/princes) (d:plural of milian: great or high-ranking people, nobles) (e:~ sila bangin a khe-un pai uh hi/~ tawh kimusak thei hi | it can bring one before the great/~’ tutna ding munah tu kha kei in | do not sit in the place of the great/silate in, ~ a uk ding | for slaves to rule over princes) (s:uliante/mithupite) (a:mineute) (b:milian) (r:21.10.7/13.17.8/20.18.16/20.25.6/20.19.10) (q:draft)
Miliante = (t:n) (w:the great/the exalted/nobles) (d:miliante written with a capital at the start of a sentence) (e:~ hong neu ta ding hi/~ kiangah pai-in ka va kiho ding uh hi | I will go to the leaders and speak with them/~ in zuauthu gen ngei lo a | nobles never speak lies) (b:miliante) (r:26.21.26/24.5.5/20.17.7) (q:draft)
milim = (t:n) (w:idol/image) (d:mi, person, with lim, likeness: an image made to be worshipped, an idol; milim biakna is idolatry) (e:~ biakna na taisan un/~ biak nadingin ka tate pia | giving my children for the worship of idols/~ a bia mi khempeuhte | all who worship images/ka kham ~ koih mai-ah | before the gold image I have set up) (s:lim) (r:46.10.14/27.3.3/26.16.21/19.97.7/27.3.14) (q:draft)
milimin = (t:n) (w:into an idol/as an idol) (d:milim idol, image with the marker in; milimin bawl is make something into an idol) (e:Amau’ ngunte ~ bawl uh a/khutsiampa in a hei tawh ~ a bawl hi | the craftsman shapes it into an idol with his tool/kham seekte in ~ bawl uh a | the goldsmiths make it into an idol) (b:milim) (r:28.13.2/24.10.3/24.10.9) (q:draft)
milimte = (t:n) (w:idols/images) (d:plural of milim: idols, images made to be worshipped) (e:Ka ta neute aw, ~ na tang un/~ pen mihingte’ khut tawh a kibawl | idols are made by human hands/Ehud tai-in suang ~ kheng a | Ehud fled and passed the stone images/a kihhuai ~ a koih uh a | they set up their detestable idols) (s:limte) (b:milim) (r:62.5.21/23.2.18/19.135.15/7.3.26/24.32.34) (q:draft)
milip = (t:pron) (w:each one/everyone/every man) (d:each person individually, usually as a milip-in, each of them) (e:a ~-in a van uh suah uh hi/a ~-in a kham zah ding khawm uh | each gathered as much as he needed/Joshua in a ~-in amau’ gam ciatah | Joshua sent each to his own land/pasal peuhmah a ~-in sim in | count every male one by one) (s:mikim) (r:1.44.11/2.32.27/2.16.18/6.24.28/4.1.2) (q:draft)
milipin = (t:adv) (w:one by one/per head/individually) (d:person by person, counting or assessing each individual; used with a before it, a milipin) (e:a ~ a phazah sim un/a ~ piak dingin a kiseh sum | the money each person is assessed to give/a ~ a inn ciat uh ah ciah uh | each one went back to his own home/a ~ a minin a mi phazah zui-in | individually by name according to their number) (s:mimi-in/khatkhatin/malin) (r:4.1.2/12.12.4/10.20.22/13.23.24) (q:draft)
milipun = (t:pron) (w:each one/every one/all of them) (d:milip everyone with the plural ending un; usually a milipun, each and every one of them) (e:a ~ a paknamtui beel ciat uh/a ~ a sumte uh a van sung | each one’s money in his sack/na ~ an huanin na ne thei ding | each of you may cook food and eat/Na ~ na galhiam uh tawh na kithawi uh | every one of you put on his weapons) (b:milip) (r:4.16.18/1.42.35/2.12.16/5.1.41) (q:draft)
Milkah = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Milcah/Milkah) (d:wife of Nahor, the brother of Abraham, and grandmother of Rebekah; also one of the five daughters of Zelophehad) (r:1.11.29/1.24.24)
Milkom = (t:name) (w:Milkom/Molek) (d:god of the Ammonites, called Molek in the NIV) (r:11.11.5/36.1.5)
Millo = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Millo) (d:part of the defences of the City of David in Jerusalem, built up by David and Solomon; the NIV has the terraces, and Beth Millo for Millo inn) (r:11.9.24/12.12.20) (q:draft)
milmel = (t:adv) (w:tender) (d:after moi young, tender: a moi milmel, delicately tender) (e:a moi ~, a ngeek dikdek) (r:23.47.1) (q:draft, low confidence)
milmial = (t:adv) (w:dimly/dully/faintly) (d:not clear or bright: of seeing, dimly; after a colour word, dull, as a kang milmial, dull white) (e:a kitel pha loin i mu ~ a/a kang ~ ahih leh | if they are dull white) (r:46.13.12/3.13.39) (q:draft)
mimah = (t:n) (w:man/human being) (d:mi person with the emphatic mah: himself a man, truly human) (e:Pasian leh mite kikal ah ~ ahi) (b:mi) (r:54.2.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
mimal = (t:n) (w:individual/person/number of people) (d:mi person with mal single unit: individual persons; in the verse the number of members that grows) (e:ni simin ~ a khang semsem uh) (r:44.16.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
mimat = (t:n) (w:captive/prey) (d:mi person with mat seize: a person taken; galte’ mimat, captive of the enemy) (e:galte’ ~ suak ding hi) (s:sal/galmat) (r:5.1.39) (q:draft)
mimawh = (t:n) (w:sinner/guilty person/the guilty) (d:mi, person, with mawh, sin: a sinner, a guilty person; mimawh lo is an innocent person) (e:~ mah ka hihna uh ka thei uh hi/mi tampi ~ a suahsak mah bangin | just as the many were made sinners/kei ~ mi khial pa hong hehpih in | have mercy on me, a sinner/~ lote’ sisan luan’ nading | to shed the blood of the innocent) (s:mawhnei/mawhneimi) (a:midik) (r:48.2.17/20.24.24/45.5.19/42.18.13/24.22.17) (q:draft)
mimawhte = (t:n) (w:sinners/the guilty) (d:plural of mimawh: sinners, guilty people, often set against midikte, the righteous) (e:~ lam hilh hi/~ nangma lamah hong kihei kik ding uh hi | sinners will turn back to you/~ sumgolh tawh khah a | who acquit the guilty for a bribe/~’ lampi-a ding lo mi | one who does not stand in the way of sinners) (s:mawhneite) (a:midikte) (b:mimawh) (r:19.25.8/23.5.23/19.51.13/19.1.1) (q:draft)
mimawl = (t:n) (w:senseless person/fool) (d:mi, person, with mawl, dull: a senseless person, paired with mihai, fool) (e:mihai ~ ahi uh hi) (s:mihai) (a:mipil) (r:24.10.8) (q:draft)
mimi = (t:see) <mimi-in>
mimi-in = (t:adv) (w:man by man/person by person/one by one) (d:mi person doubled, with in: each person in turn, like a behbehin clan by clan and a innkuankuanin family by family) (e:ama innkuanpihte a ~ hong paipih a/a innkuan sung panin a ~ hong pai ding | from that family they shall come forward man by man/Zerah-te beh a ~ hong paipih a | he brought the clan of the Zerahites forward man by man) (s:milipin/khatkhatin) (r:6.7.18/6.7.14/6.7.17) (q:draft)
miminthang = (t:adj) (w:celebrity)
mimkhau = (t:n) (w:thread) (d:a thread, a thin strand of spun fibre used for weaving and sewing) (e:~ bangin khauhualte botsat ziau hi/~ ahi a, khedap khau ahi a | whether a thread or a sandal strap/ka sam lom sagihte ~ tawh gan khawmin | weaving the seven braids of my hair with thread) (r:7.16.12/1.14.23/7.16.13) (q:draft)
min = (t:n) (w:name) (e:Keturah ~ nei zi dang khat la hi/Asher’ tanu’ ~ in Serah ahi hi | the name of Asher’s daughter was Serah/Levi’ tapate’ ~ in | the names of the sons of Levi/Hihte in amaute’ ~ ahi hi | these are their names) (r:1.25.1/4.26.46/4.3.17/11.4.8)
Min = (t:n) (w:Name) (d:min, name, written with a capital for the name of God, as in Min Siangtho, the holy Name, and at the start of a sentence) (e:~ Siangtho gensia-in samsia hi/~ gamlapi panin kimu thei hi | the Name is seen coming from afar/~ Siangtho a gensiat ciangin kithat ding hi | when he blasphemes the holy Name he shall be put to death) (b:min) (r:3.24.11/23.30.27/3.24.16) (q:draft)
mina = (t:n) (w:mina) (d:a unit of weight for silver and gold, sixty shekels in Ezekiel 45:12) (e:shekel sawmguk ciangin ~ khat hi ding hi/ngun ~ tul nih | two thousand minas of silver/lum khat ciangin kham ~ thum bei hi | three minas of gold went into each shield) (s:minas) (r:26.45.12/16.7.72/11.10.17) (q:draft)
minam = (t:n) (w:native) (e:Israel ~ taktakte mah bangin na ngaihsun ding | you are to consider them as native-born Israelites) (s:tualsuak) (r:26.47.22)
minam = (t:n) (w:ethics)
minambup = (t:n) (w:whole nation/whole people/whole community) (d:minam nation with bup whole) (e:i ~ zong hong sugawp ding/i ~ tangin mi khat si leh | if one man dies for our whole nation/~ khat sal dingin manin | taking a whole people captive) (r:43.11.48/30.1.6/43.11.50) (q:draft)
minamdang = (t:n) (w:foreigner)
minamdang = (t:n) (w:immigrant)
minamdangte = (t:n) (w:other nations/nations/foreign peoples) (d:minamdang foreigner, another people, with plural te) (e:~ lakah nong thehthang khin hi/a kiima om ~ khempeuh a susia ding uh | they will destroy all the surrounding peoples/Note in ~ lakah na daisaksa uh | which you have profaned among the nations) (s:namdangte/gamdangte) (b:minamdang) (r:19.44.11/26.36.23/38.12.6) (q:draft)
minamin = (t:n) (w:nation/people) (d:minam, nation, with the marker in: as a nation, into a nation, nation by nation; minamin bawl is make into a nation) (e:a thahat zaw ~ nang kong bawl ding hi/a beh, a ~ om uh hi | they lived by their clans and nations/Israel mite a thahat ~ ka bawl kik ding | I will make the Israelites a strong nation again/Moab mite pen ~ dingzo nawn lo ding | the Moabites will no longer stand as a nation) (b:minam) (r:4.14.12/1.10.5/26.29.21/26.25.10) (q:draft)
minamte = (t:n) (w:nations/peoples) (d:plural of minam: the nations or peoples of the world) (e:Mi ahih lelna uh ~ theisak in/na mai-ah ~ thu khen in | let the nations be judged before you/~ i khe nuai-ah amah in hong zawhsak hi | he subdued nations under our feet/Topa in ~’ thu ngaihsutna a mawkna suah a | the Lord brings the plans of the nations to nothing) (s:mipawlte) (b:minam) (r:19.9.20/19.9.19/19.47.3/19.33.10) (q:draft)
minamte = (t:n) (w:tribes) (d:plural of minam used for the tribes of Israel) (e:Israel ~ khat bangin Dan in/no Israel ~ lakah hawm un | divide it among you, the tribes of Israel) (b:minam) (r:1.49.16/26.48.2/26.47.21) (q:draft)
Minamte = (t:n) (w:tribe/people of a tribe) (d:capitalised form of minamte placed after a tribal name in the land allotments of Ezekiel 48, as in Asher Minamte the tribe of Asher) (e:a zomah Asher ~/a zomah Efraim ~ | next, the tribe of Ephraim) (b:minamte) (r:26.48.2/26.48.21/26.48.5) (q:draft)
minas = (t:n) (w:minas/mina) (d:unit of weight for gold and silver, written as in English) (e:kham ~ thum bei hi) (s:mina) (r:11.10.17) (q:draft)
minautangte = (t:n) (w:common people/ordinary people) (d:mi nautang, common people, with the plural te; minautangte’ tutna mun, the seat of the common people, is the lowest place at a feast) (e:~’ tutna munah na tuzaw un/~’ tutna munah maizumpi in na tusuk ding | in shame you will go down to the lowest seat) (s:nautangte/mineute) (a:miliante) (r:42.14.10/42.14.9) (q:draft)
mindai = (t:v) (w:be disgraced/be put to shame) (d:lose one's good name, be shamed before others; often mindai-in together with maizum, be ashamed) (e:Israel ~-in maizum ding uh hi/na nu uh a ~ ding hi | your mother will be disgraced/a tapate ~ ta leh zong | even if his children are brought low/amaute ~-in siasak in | let them perish in disgrace/tu-in amaute si-in ~-in om uh | now they are dead and lie in disgrace) (s:minsiat/zahhuai) (a:kipahtawi) (r:28.10.6/24.50.12/18.14.21/19.83.17/26.32.24) (q:draft)
mindai = (t:n) (w:shame/disgrace/dishonor) (d:loss of one's good name; mindai ni is a day of disgrace) (e:a ~ paisuak ding hi/tai ngah ni, ~ ni ahi hi | it is a day of rebuke, a day of disgrace/na nu’ ~ nadingin | to the shame of your mother) (s:mindaina/minsiatna/maizumna) (a:minphatna/pahtawina) (r:20.6.33/23.37.3/9.20.30) (q:draft, low confidence)
mindaihuai = (t:adj) (w:shameful/disgraceful/detestable) (d:mindai, be disgraced, with huai, deserving of: shameful, said of detestable conduct) (e:a ~ zaw nangawn na mu/migilote’ gamtat bangin a ~ | shameful, as the wicked act/numei paktat nuntakna tawh a ~-in na om | you lived shamefully in a life of prostitution) (s:zumhuai/maizumhuai/kihhuai/muhdahhuai) (r:26.8.6/26.18.24/26.16.22) (q:draft)
mindaihuaite = (t:n) (w:detestable things/shameful things) (d:mindaihuai, shameful, with the plural te: shameful or detestable deeds) (e:a ~ khempeuh gamta ahih manin) (s:kihhuaite/kihhuainate) (b:mindaihuai) (r:26.18.13) (q:draft)
mindaina = (t:n) (w:disgrace/shame/dishonor/reproach) (d:mindai, be disgraced, with the noun suffix na: the loss of one's good name; mindaina tun is to bring dishonor on someone) (e:zumna leh ~ a piang sak tapa/minsiatna ngah leeng ~ tawh kizom pah | with a bad name comes disgrace/mihaite in maizumna leh ~ ngah ding | fools will get shame and disgrace/ka maizumna leh ka ~ nang na thei | you know my shame and my disgrace/na pa’ sanggampa tungah ~ na tun’ kei ding | do not bring dishonor on your father's brother) (s:maizumna/minsiatna/zumna) (a:minphatna/pahtawina) (b:mindai) (r:20.19.26/20.18.3/20.3.35/19.69.19/3.18.14) (q:draft)
mindainate = (t:n) (w:disgraces/shame) (d:plural of mindaina: the disgraces a people has suffered or brought on itself) (e:a ~ uh mangngilh thei ta ding) (b:mindaina) (r:26.39.26) (q:draft)
mindainateng = (t:n) (w:all the disgrace/disgrace) (d:mindaina, disgrace, with teng, all: the whole of one's disgrace) (e:Tu-in na ~ na thuak kul hi) (b:mindaina) (r:26.16.52) (q:draft)
mindaisak = (t:v) (w:disgrace/dishonor/put to shame) (d:mindai, be disgraced, with the causative sak: bring shame or dishonor on someone) (e:mawhna in minam ~ hi/mipa in a pa a ~ suak hi | the man has dishonored his father/Mari ~ nuam loin, maksim ding a lungngai | not wanting to disgrace Mary, he planned to divorce her quietly/amah in a sanggampa a ~ ahi hi | he has dishonored his brother/Kei hong sawmte mai zumin ~ ta in | put to shame those who seek my life) (s:minsiasak/maizumsak/zahhuaisak/zumsak) (a:minthangsak/pahtawi) (b:mindai) (r:20.14.34/3.20.11/40.1.19/3.20.21/19.35.4) (q:draft)
mindaisakna = (t:n) (w:scorn/insult/shaming) (d:mindaisak, put to shame, with the noun suffix na: the scorn or insults by which others shame someone) (e:a hong ~ uh na thuak nawn) (s:simmawhna/kosiatna) (b:mindaisak) (r:26.36.15) (q:draft)
mindang = (t:n) (w:other name/another name) (d:min, name, with dang, other: a second name of a person, or a name other than the one just mentioned) (e:a ~ Justas ahi Josef/~ khat beek van nuai mite lakah | even one other name among people under heaven) (s:minno) (r:44.1.23/44.4.12) (q:draft)
mineu = (t:n) (w:lowly person/the small/common person) (d:mi, person, with neu, small: a person of low standing, usually paired with milian, the great) (e:Tua lai-ah milian ~ omkhawm a/milian ~, mihau mizawngte aw | great and small, rich and poor/mizawngte tawh kikhawlin ~ a om hoihzaw | it is better to be lowly and keep company with the poor/milian ~, a kuamah peuh tungah | to great and small, to everyone) (s:miniam) (a:milian) (r:18.3.19/19.49.2/20.16.19/44.26.22) (q:draft)
mineupen = (t:n) (w:the least/lowliest person/least person) (d:mineu lowly person with the superlative pen) (e:hih ~ khat tungah) (b:mineu) (r:40.25.40) (q:draft)
mineute = (t:n) (w:the lowly/the small/common people) (d:plural of mineu, people of low standing, the opposite of miliante) (e:miliante leh ~ a si ding uh a/Kiphasak loin ~ tawh kikhawlthei unla | do not be proud, but associate with the lowly/~, milianin a bawl hi | he has made the lowly great/a kiniamkhiat, ~ bek, ka suaktasak lai ding | I will leave only the humble and lowly) (s:miniamte/nautangte/minautangte) (a:miliante) (b:mineu) (r:24.16.6/19.62.9/45.12.16/42.1.52/36.3.12) (q:draft)
miniam = (t:n) (w:lowly person/person of low position) (d:mi, person, with niam, low: a person of low position; miniam i hih laitak is when we were lowly) (e:~ i hih laitak-a hong phawkpa tungah) (s:mineu) (a:milian) (r:19.136.23) (q:draft)
Miniam = (t:n) (w:lowly person/humble person) (d:miniam, lowly person, written with a capital at the start of a verse; Miniam ihih laitakin is when we were lowly) (e:~ ihih laitakin a hong phawk pa tungah) (s:mineu) (b:miniam) (r:19.136.23) (q:draft)
Miniamin = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Miniamin) (d:name of several men, among them a Levite under King Hezekiah and a priest in the time of Nehemiah) (r:16.12.41/16.12.17)
miniamte = (t:n) (w:the humble/the lowly/humble people) (d:plural of miniam: people of low position or humble spirit, whom God lifts up) (e:Amah in ~ sang koih a/nangmah in ~ na honkhia a | you save the humble/~ gualzo sakin a pahtawi hi | he honors the humble with victory) (s:mineute/kiniamkhiatte) (a:kiphasakte) (b:miniam) (r:18.5.11/19.18.27/19.149.4) (q:draft)
minih = (t:n) (w:two men/two people) (d:mi person with nih two, written as one word) (e:Moab galhang ~ vat lum hi) (r:13.11.22) (q:draft)
minin = (t:n) (w:by name/in the name of/name) (d:min, name, with the marker in: by name or in the name of someone; also as subject, the name is) (e:na ~ dawite nangawn ka zo uh/Amah in tuute a ~ sam a | he calls the sheep by name/nang pen na ~ kong sam a | I call you by your name/hih thu khempeuh David ~ Nabal kiangah gen | they told Nabal all this in David's name/ama zi’ ~ Ma-akah ahi hi | his wife's name was Maakah) (b:min) (r:42.10.17/23.45.4/43.10.3/9.25.9/13.8.29) (q:draft)
mininte = (t:n) (w:the unclean/unclean people) (d:mi, person, with nin, unclean, and the plural te; paired with misiangte, the clean) (e:misiangte leh ~, biakna piate) (a:misiangte) (r:21.9.2) (q:draft)
minkhem = (t:n) (w:figurative name/byname/nickname) (d:a name borne in place of the real one; in the verse the city is figuratively called Sodom and Egypt) (e:Egypt ~ a pua khuapi kongzingah) (r:66.11.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
minlian = (t:adj) (w:exalted/renowned/great in name) (d:min, name, with lian, great: having a great name, exalted) (e:amah bek a ~ hi a) (s:minthang) (r:19.148.13) (q:draft)
minliat = (t:v) (w:be honoured/be great in name) (d:form of minlian used before nading: na minliat nading, your being honoured) (e:na ~ nading panin Topa in) (r:4.24.11) (q:draft)
minliatna = (t:n) (w:majesty/glory/honour/renown) (d:minliat, be great in name, with the noun suffix na: majesty, the greatness and honour of a king or of God) (e:Pahtawina leh ~ in amah umcih a/hoihna leh ~ ama tungah na pia hi | you have bestowed splendor and majesty on him/minthan’na leh ~ nei in | clothe yourself with glory and majesty/na ~ tawh gualzo-in hong pusuak in | in your majesty ride out victoriously/Israel-te’ ~ teng vasa bangin leengmang ding | all Israel's glory will fly away like a bird) (s:minthanna/vangliatna) (a:mindaina) (b:minliat) (r:13.16.27/19.111.3/19.21.5/18.40.10/19.45.4/28.9.11) (q:draft)
minmin = (t:v) (w:ripen/be ripening) (d:min ripe, doubled: beginning to ripen, said of figs) (e:Theite zong ~ ta a) (r:22.2.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
minnei = (t:adj) (w:named/called) (d:min, name, with nei, have: bearing the name, placed after a personal name) (e:Zekhariah ~ siampi khat a om hi/Anna ~ kamsang numei khat a om hi | there was a prophetess named Anna) (r:42.1.5/42.2.36) (q:draft)
Minni = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Minni) (d:kingdom summoned with Ararat and Ashkenaz to make war on Babylon) (r:24.51.27) (q:draft)
Minnith = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Minnith) (d:place east of the Jordan, as far as which Jephthah struck down the Ammonites) (r:7.11.33)
minno = (t:n) (w:nickname/other name) (d:min, name, with no, small: a second name by which a person is known) (e:Unau Peeng ~ a nei Thomas) (s:mindang) (b:min) (r:43.20.24/43.21.2) (q:draft)
minpha = (t:n) (w:good name/good reputation) (d:min, name, with pha, good: a good name, a good reputation) (e:paknamtui sangin ~ hoihzaw a) (a:minsia) (r:21.7.1) (q:draft)
minphat = (t:v) (w:praise/honor/be praised) (d:min, name, with phat, praise: praise the name of someone; minphat ding, to be praised, is set against minsiat ding, to be disgraced) (e:ama ~ un la/~ ding sangin minsiat ding utzaw uh hi | they would rather be disgraced than praised) (a:minsiat) (r:19.105.1/28.4.18) (q:draft)
minphathuai = (t:adj) (w:praiseworthy/approved/of good repute) (d:minphat, praise, with huai, worthy of: deserving praise, well thought of) (e:mite mai-ah ~ ahi hi) (s:phathuai) (r:45.14.18) (q:draft)
minphatna = (t:n) (w:honor/good name/praise) (d:being well spoken of, the opposite of mindaina) (e:mi in ~ leh pahtawina ngah hi/Mipilte in ~ leh pahtawina ngah ding a | the wise will receive honor/hauhna leh ~ tawh si hi | he died with wealth and honor/lungdamna, ~ leh minthan’na ahi ding hi | will be joy, praise and glory/note in Pasian’ ~ kilangsakin | showing forth the praise of God) (s:pahtawina/minthanna/phatna) (a:mindaina/minsiatna) (b:minphat) (r:20.13.18/20.8.18/20.3.35/13.29.28/24.33.9/45.15.7) (q:draft)
minphatnate = (t:n) (w:honors/greatness) (d:plural of minphatna: the honors given to a person) (e:Mordekai tungah a piak ~) (b:minphatna) (r:17.10.2) (q:draft)
minsa = (t:adj) (w:cooked/boiled/prepared) (d:of meat or food, already cooked: min, cooked or ripe, with sa, already; the opposite of sial, raw) (e:sa ~ hong sang loin a sial/a ~ bawngno sa la-in | taking the cooked meat of the calf/a han’ ~ tuu nga | five sheep already dressed and cooked/nitak an a ~-in a om | the dinner is cooked and ready) (s:huansa) (a:sial) (r:9.2.15/1.18.8/9.25.18/40.22.4) (q:draft)
minsia = (t:n) (w:bad name/disgrace/ill repute) (d:min, name, with sia, bad; minsia tun is to bring a bad name on someone and minsia sak is to disgrace) (e:Israel nungak tungah ~ tun’ hi/tua nu tungah ~ a tut leh | if he brings a bad name on her/kei hong ~ sakin hong simmawh ding uh | they would give me a bad name and mock me/nungkiksak in la ~ sak in | turn them back and disgrace them) (s:minsiatna/mindai/mindaina) (a:minpha) (r:5.22.19/19.40.14/5.22.14/16.6.13) (q:draft)
minsiasak = (t:v) (w:disgrace/dishonor/shame/defame) (d:minsia, bad name, with the causative sak: give someone a bad name, bring disgrace on someone) (e:ka mite mai-ah kei nong ~ uh hi/a pa in amah ~ ahih manin | because his father had disgraced him/Pasian in hong ~ lo ding hi | God will not disgrace us/Note’ haina zahin kong ~ kei ding | I will not disgrace you as your folly deserves/Keimah hong ko mi leh hong ~ mite’ kam | the voice of those who taunt and revile me) (s:mindaisak/maizumsak/zahhuaisak) (a:minthangsak) (b:minsia) (r:26.13.19/9.20.34/33.2.6/18.42.8/19.44.15) (q:draft)
minsiat = (t:v) (w:be disgraced/get a bad name) (d:form of minsia, bad name, used as a verb before ding: get a bad name; set against minphat, be praised) (e:Minphat ding sangin ~ ding utzaw uh hi) (s:mindai) (a:minphat) (b:minsia) (r:28.4.18) (q:draft)
minsiatna = (t:n) (w:disgrace/dishonor/shame/reproach) (d:the spoiling of one's name, loss of good reputation) (e:Mi kiphasakte in ~ ngah pak ding/simmawhna leh ~ in tuamcip ta hen | may scorn and disgrace cover them/na ~ bei ngei lo ding hi | your bad name will never end/na ~ uh ka zial khia hi | I have rolled away your reproach/nangma’ hangin ~ thuak ka hih lam | that I suffer reproach for your sake) (s:mindaina/maizumna/zumna/minsia) (a:minphatna) (b:minsiat) (r:20.11.2/19.71.13/20.25.10/6.5.9/24.15.15) (q:draft)
minta = (t:v) (w:be ripe/have ripened) (d:min, ripe, with ta, now: has become ripe, said of fruit ready for harvest) (e:na singgahte uh ~ a/Leitung mite leenggah bangin ~ ahih manin | because the people of the earth are ripe like grapes) (r:23.16.9/66.14.18) (q:draft)
minte = (t:n) (w:names) (d:plural of min, name) (e:sawltak sawm leh nihte’ ~ kigelh hi/Israel’ tapate’ ~ in | the names of the sons of Israel are/Israel tapate’ ~ tawh kizui-in | according to the names of the sons of Israel/a ~ khel ding | their names were to be changed) (b:min) (r:66.21.14/2.1.1/2.39.6/4.32.38) (q:draft)
minthak = (t:n) (w:new name) (d:min, name, with thak, new; minthak phuah is to give a new name) (e:amaute ~ phuah a) (r:27.1.7) (q:draft)
minthan = (t:adj) (w:glorious/famous/renowned) (d:form of minthang, famous or glorious, used before a suffix; found mostly in minthan’na, glory or honour) (e:Mite piak ~’na ka sang kei hi/David in ~’na ngah hi | David won fame/ama ~’na sa un la | sing of his glory/minamte lakah ka ~’na genthang ding uh | they will proclaim my glory among the nations) (s:minthang/minlian) (r:43.5.41/48.1.5/10.8.13/19.66.2/23.66.19) (q:draft)
minthang = (t:adj) (w:popular/famous/well known) (d:known and spoken of by many people, held in honor among them) (e:Mihing sawmthumte lakah amah ~ a | he was famous among the Thirty/Bethlehem ah na ~ ta hen | may you be famous in Bethlehem/amau’ beh sungah a ~ mi | men famous in their own clans) (s:minlian) (r:10.23.23/8.4.11/13.12.30)
minthang = (t:adj) (w:renown/renowned/glorious/majestic) (d:of great name, glorious, said of a city, a throne or the name of God) (e:A ~ khuapi kisusia ta a/a ~ kumpi tokhom tawh kibang hi | is like a glorious throne/a ~ na min ka phat uh hi | we praise your glorious name/na taklam khut, vangliatna-ah ~ hi | your right hand is majestic in power) (r:26.26.17/24.49.25/24.17.12/13.29.13/2.15.6)
minthang = (t:n) (w:fame/renown) (d:a great name known far and wide) (e:Lebanon gam leenggahzu bangin ~ ding uh hi) (s:minthanna) (r:28.14.7)
Minthang = (t:adj) (w:glorious/majestic/renowned) (d:minthang, glorious, written with a capital in titles of God: Minthang Kumpipa is the King of glory and Vanglian Minthang pa the Majestic Glory) (e:Vanglian ~ pa in/~ Kumpipa kua ahi hiam | who is this King of glory/~ Kumpipa hong tum theih nadingin | that the King of glory may come in) (b:minthang) (r:61.1.17/19.24.8/19.24.7) (q:draft)
minthangin = (t:adv) (w:gloriously/in glory/famously) (d:minthang, glorious, with the suffix in: in a glorious way, with honor) (e:amah in ~ zo khin/amau’ hankhuk sung ciat uhah ~ lum uh hi | they lie in glory, each in his own tomb/nidangin ~ a vangtaang mahmah i cih pen | what we once called so glorious/vanglian ~ hong kilatna tawh | by his mighty and glorious appearing) (b:minthang) (r:2.15.21/23.14.18/47.3.10/53.2.8) (q:draft)
minthangsa = (t:adj) (w:renowned/once famous) (d:minthang, famous, with sa, already: that has been famous, once renowned) (e:a ~ hih inn a nawkkha khempeuh) (b:minthang) (r:14.7.21) (q:draft)
minthangsak = (t:v) (w:glorify/exalt/honor) (d:minthang, famous or glorious, with the causative sak: give glory or honor to someone) (e:Pasian in Tapa a ~ ding a/Thumanna in minam ~ a | righteousness exalts a nation/nangma kiangah kei hong ~ in | glorify me in your presence/Jakob tapate khempeuh aw, amah ~ un | all you descendants of Jacob, honor him/Topa in nang hong ~ khin ahih manin | because the Lord has glorified you) (s:pahtawi/thangsak/liansak) (a:mindaisak/minsiasak) (b:minthang) (r:43.13.32/20.14.34/43.17.5/19.22.23/23.60.9) (q:draft)
minthangte = (t:n) (w:renown/famous men/the renowned) (d:plural of minthang: famous people; mi minthangte are men of renown) (e:tang lai-a mi thahat, mi ~/a thahat galhangte, mi ~ | brave warriors, famous men/kumpi ~ a thatpa tungah | to him who killed famous kings) (b:minthang) (r:1.6.4/13.5.24/19.136.18)
minthanna = (t:n) (w:glory/splendor/fame/honor) (d:minthan, glorious, with the noun suffix na: glory, splendor or fame, of God or of a person; also written minthan’na) (e:na ~ ka gen tawntung hi/I Pa Pasian in a tawntungin ~ ngah tahen | may our God and Father have glory forever/na ~ le na liatna tawh | with your splendor and majesty/David’ ~ in gam khempeuh zel a | David's fame spread through every land/na melhoihna le na ~ a sia lamin zangin | using your beauty and your fame for evil) (s:minliatna/vangliatna/pahtawina) (a:mindaina) (b:minthan) (r:19.71.8/50.4.20/19.45.3/13.14.17/26.16.15) (q:draft)
minthannate = (t:n) (w:glories/glory/splendor) (d:minthanna, glory, with the plural te: glories, all the splendor of a person or kingdom) (e:a ~ uh lopa pak tawh kibang hi/na vangliatna na ~ kei hong musak in | let me see your power and your glory/ka gam ~ a hong kipia kik hi | the glories of my kingdom were given back to me) (b:minthanna) (r:60.1.24/19.145.12/19.63.2/27.4.36) (q:draft)
minthanzawk = (t:v) (w:be more honoured/have greater glory) (d:minthang, renowned, with the comparative zaw, in the form used before mah bangin: have greater honor than) (e:a inn sangin a ~ mah bangin) (r:58.3.3) (q:draft)
minthuhna = (t:n) (w:seal/signet) (d:min, name, with thuh, stamp, and the noun suffix na: a seal for stamping a name on a document; minthuhna zungbuh is a signet ring) (e:kumpipa’ ~ zungbuh tawh thuh in/khutsung panin a ~ zungbuh suahin | taking his signet ring from his finger/kumpipa’ ~ tawh a kithuh khinsa lai | a document already sealed with the king's seal) (r:17.8.8/17.3.10) (q:draft)
minu = (t:n) (w:woman) (d:mi, person, with nu marking a female) (s:numei) (a:mipa)
minuamsa = (t:n) (w:blessed person/happy person/fortunate person) (d:mi, person, with nuamsa, happy or at ease: a person who is well off, blessed) (e:a taii mite ~ hizaw ahih manin) (r:18.5.17) (q:draft)
minun = (t:n) (w:by name) (d:min name with un, the plural marker joined to in: by their names) (e:amaute khempeuh a ~ a sampa ahi hi) (b:min) (r:23.40.26) (q:draft)
mipa = (t:n) (w:man) (d:mi, person, with pa marking a male: a man, the man just spoken of) (e:tua ~ la-in sat ding uh hi/Josef' sawl bangin ~ in sem a | the man did as Joseph told him/Topa Pasian in ~ la-in | the Lord God took the man/A citak ~ in thupha tampi ngah ding | a faithful man will receive many blessings) (s:pasal) (a:minu/numei) (b:mi) (r:5.22.18/1.43.17/1.2.15/20.28.20)
Mipa = (t:n) (w:man) (d:mipa, the man, written with a capital at the start of a sentence or as a title of Christ, the Man from heaven) (e:vantung panin a hong pai ~’ lim/~ in a lu kunin Topa bia a | the man bowed his head and worshiped the Lord/~ leh a zi guaktangin om uh a | the man and his wife were naked) (b:mipa) (r:46.15.49/1.24.26/1.2.25) (q:draft)
Mipaktat = (t:n) (w:adulterous person/immoral person) (d:mi, person, with paktat, sexually immoral: an adulterous person, here of an unfaithful generation) (e:~ leh mi gilo khang mite in) (r:40.12.39) (q:draft)
mipawl = (t:n) (w:nation/people/group of people) (d:mi, person, with pawl, group; mipawl khempeuh, all nations) (e:a masa belin ~ khempeuh a kihilh ding hi/Israel ~ tampi amau Topa Pasian kiangah | many of the people of Israel to the Lord their God/Kanaan gam sung ~ sagih a suksiat khit ciangin | after he destroyed seven nations in Canaan/tuite in ~, mihon, gam, kamte ahi uh hi | the waters are peoples, multitudes, nations and languages) (s:minam) (r:41.13.10/42.1.16/44.13.19/66.17.15) (q:draft)
Mipawl = (t:n) (w:nation/people) (d:mipawl, nation, written with a capital at the start of a sentence; Mipawl khempeuh is all nations) (e:~ khempeuh in na mai-ah hong thuumin/~ khempeuh lakah amah kihta uh a | in every nation those who fear him/~ khempeuh a heh uh a | all the nations were angry) (b:mipawl) (r:66.15.4/44.10.35/66.11.18) (q:draft)
mipawlpawlte = (t:n) (w:nations/peoples/groups of people) (d:mi, person, with pawl, group, doubled, and the plural te: the various peoples, the nations) (e:~ a kheem kik zawh loh nadingin) (r:66.20.3) (q:draft)
mipawlte = (t:n) (w:people/peoples/nations) (d:a people or nation taken together, or groups of people; plural of mipawl) (e:Hih ~ in amau’ kam uh tawh/~ tungah ukna aana ka pia ding a | I will give authority over the nations/ama ~ tawh na lungdam khawm un | rejoice together with his people/Tua ~ a kisim ciangin | when those peoples are counted) (s:minamte) (b:mipawl) (r:40.15.8/66.2.26/45.15.10/66.20.8) (q:draft)
mipha = (t:n) (w:good person/the good/righteous person) (d:mi, person, with pha, good: a good or upright person; the opposite of misia) (e:~ in phatna thaman ngah hi/Barnabas in ~ hi a | Barnabas was a good man/Pasian mai-ah ~ ahi uh hi | they were righteous before God/misia, ~, hong encik kim hi | he watches both the wicked and the good) (s:midik) (a:misia/migilo) (r:20.14.14/42.1.6/44.11.24/20.15.3) (q:draft)
miphak = (t:n) (w:leper) (d:mi, person, with phak, leprosy: a person who has leprosy) (e:~ khat in Zeisu kiangah/~ sawm in amah dawn uh a | ten lepers met him/~ Simon’ inn sungah | in the house of Simon the Leper/amah in ~ hi a, a nin ahi hi | he is a leper, he is unclean) (s:phakpa/miphakpa) (r:40.8.2/42.17.12/40.26.6/3.13.44) (q:draft)
miphakpa = (t:n) (w:leper) (d:miphak, leper, with pa marking a man) (e:Tua natna a nei ~ in) (s:phakpa/miphak) (b:miphak) (r:3.13.45) (q:draft)
miphakte = (t:n) (w:lepers/people with leprosy) (d:miphak, leper, with the plural te) (e:~ in damna a ngah kik uh hi/misite hingsakin, ~ damsakin | raise the dead, cleanse the lepers/khebaite paithei kikin, ~ damkik a | the lame walk, the lepers are healed/hih ~ hong tun uh ciangin | when these lepers arrived) (s:phakte) (b:miphak) (r:40.11.5/40.10.8/12.7.8) (q:draft)
miphapa = (t:n) (w:good man/innocent man) (d:mipha, good person, with pa marking a man: a good or innocent man) (e:Tua ~ tawh bangmah kikumin/Hih ~’ si tungah kei ka mawh kei hi | I am innocent of this good man's blood) (s:mihoihpa/dikpa/phapa) (b:mipha) (r:40.27.19/40.27.24) (q:draft)
miphate = (t:n) (w:the righteous/good people/the upright) (d:plural of mipha, a good person: those who are good or faithful, set against migilote, the wicked) (e:~ lakah a min uh kikhumsak kei in/Pasian in ~ leh migilote tungah | God, on the good and the wicked/Note lakah ~ a kilat nadingin | so that the good among you may be shown/~’ omna-ah na min ka taangko ding hi | I will proclaim your name where the faithful are) (s:midikte/mihoihte) (a:migilote/misiate) (b:mipha) (r:19.69.28/42.5.32/40.5.45/46.11.19/19.52.9) (q:draft)
mipi = (t:n) (w:people/public/crowd/multitude) (d:mi, person, with the augmentative pi: the people as a body, the general public; mipi mai-ah is in public and mipi kikhopna is the great assembly) (e:~ kikhopna sungah Topa Pasian phat un/amaute in ~’ zakin Moses’ laibute sim uh | they read the books of Moses in the hearing of the people/a tengtawm nuam khempeuhte ~ in pakta uh hi | the people commended all who were willing to settle/~ mai-ah Lai Siangtho simna | the public reading of Scripture/~ mai-ah Peter thu sit dingin | to try Peter before the people) (s:mihonpi/mihon) (b:mi) (r:19.68.26/16.13.1/16.11.2/54.4.13/44.12.4) (q:draft)
mipi = (t:adj) (w:noble/generous) (d:in mipi lungsim, a noble or great-hearted mind) (e:~ lungsim a nei mi in/Berea khuamite in ~ lungsim neizaw uh hi | the people of Berea were more noble-minded) (r:23.32.8/44.17.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
mipih = (t:n) (w:fellow countryman/own people/kinsman) (d:a person or people of the same nation as oneself; the suffix pih marks sharing, like English fellow) (e:na ~ Israel mite kiangah/Ka ~ Israel mite aw | my fellow Israelites/ama ~ Hebru mi khat a sat | beating a Hebrew, one of his own people/Ama ~ Israelte in a muhdah theih nadingin | so that his own people Israel would hate him) (b:mi) (r:26.3.5/27.9.20/44.3.12/2.2.11/9.27.12) (q:draft)
mipihte = (t:n) (w:fellow countrymen/own people/kinsmen) (d:plural of mipih: people of one's own nation, tribe or kind) (e:na ~ in hong dot uh ciangin/a Judah ~ uh tungah | against their fellow Jews/note leh na Levi ~ uh | you and your fellow Levites/Na ~’ bawngtal ahi a, a tuu ahi zongin | whether the ox or the sheep of your fellow countryman) (r:26.37.18/16.5.1/13.15.12/5.22.1) (q:draft)
mipil = (t:n) (w:wise person/wise man) (d:mi, person, with pil, wise: a wise person; mipil suak is to become wise) (e:Ka ta aw, ~ suak lecin/mailam ah ~ na hi ding hi | in the end you will be wise/~ khat in kumpipa lungdamsak thei hi | a wise person can appease the king/ka thu ngai in la ~ suak in | listen to me and become wise) (s:mipilpa) (a:mihai) (r:20.23.15/20.10.19/20.19.20/20.16.14/20.23.19) (q:draft)
mipilin = (t:n) (w:wise person) (d:mipil, wise person, with the marker in; mipilin bawl is to make someone wise) (e:Eite ~ a hong bawl) (b:mipil) (r:18.35.11) (q:draft)
mipilpa = (t:n) (w:wise man) (d:mipil, wise person, with pa marking a man; set against mihaipa, the fool) (e:~ in dam taka a gen hiathiat/~ ahih leh ki-ip-in a hehna dam sak | but the wise man holds back and calms his anger/mihaipa sangin ~ a hamphat zawkna | the advantage of the wise man over the fool) (s:mipil) (a:mihaipa) (b:mipil) (r:21.9.17/20.29.11/21.6.8) (q:draft)
mipilpi = (t:n) (w:very wise person/great sage) (d:mipil wise person with the augmentative pi) (e:~ mah hong kisa zaw ding) (a:mihaipi) (b:mipil) (r:18.13.5) (q:draft)
mipilsate = (t:n) (w:the wise/wise people) (d:mi, person, with pilsa, already wise, and the plural te: those who are already wise) (e:Mi ciimsate ciimsak semsemin, ~ pilsak semsem-in) (s:mipilte) (r:20.1.5) (q:draft)
mipilte = (t:n) (w:the wise/wise men) (d:plural of mipil: wise people; also the wise men, the Magi, whom Herod called) (e:~ in pilna thu gen a/Herod in ~ sam sim a | Herod secretly called the wise men/~ in pilna mah ngah thuah hi | the wise gain knowledge/~’ hong taina hoihzaw hi | the rebuke of the wise is better/Nang’ pau bangin ~ pau ngei lo | the wise never speak as you do) (s:pilte/lungpilte) (a:mihaite) (b:mipil) (r:20.15.2/20.15.24/40.2.7/20.14.18/21.7.5/18.15.2) (q:draft)
mipilteng = (t:n) (w:all the wise men/wise men) (d:mipil wise person with teng, all of them) (e:Babylon gam sunga ~ a thatlum dingin) (b:mipil) (r:27.2.14) (q:draft)
mipite = (t:n) (w:people/crowds/multitude) (d:mipi, the public, the mass of people, with the plural te) (e:~ in Jesuh a sawlkhia uh hi/hihte zong ~ mai-ah a lui nadingun | to set these also before the people) (s:mihonte/mihonpite) (b:mipi) (r:41.5.17/23.5.14/41.8.7) (q:draft)
Mipite = (t:n) (w:the people/the public) (d:Mipite’ Kongpi is the Gate of the People) (e:~’ Kongpi leh Jerusalem khua kongpi khempeuh) (b:mipite) (r:24.17.19) (q:draft)
mipoite = (t:n) (w:the crippled/the maimed) (d:people with injured or disabled bodies, named with the lame and the blind) (e:mizawngte, ~, khebaite leh mittawte/mizawngte, ~, mittawte, khebaite hong tumpih in | bring in the poor, the crippled, the blind and the lame) (r:42.14.13/42.14.21) (q:draft)
mipum = (t:n) (w:human body/flesh) (d:mi person with pum body: a person in bodily form; mipum bangin, in the flesh) (e:Zeisu Khazih ~ bangin hong pai zo hi) (r:62.4.2) (q:draft)
Miriam = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Miriam) (d:sister of Moses and Aaron, daughter of Amram, a prophetess who led the women in song after the crossing of the sea) (r:2.15.20/4.12.1)
Mirmah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mirmah) (d:son of Shaharaim and Hodesh, head of a family of the tribe of Benjamin) (r:13.8.10)
mirrah = (t:n) (w:myrrh) (d:a fragrant resin used as perfume and in preparing a body for burial; often mirrah paknamtui, myrrh perfume) (e:paknamtui leh ~ a pia uh hi/~ paknamtui bangin namtui viauviau hi | is fragrant like myrrh perfume/~ leh aloes kihel paknamtui a paipih hi | he brought a mixture of myrrh and aloes) (s:mor/myrrh) (r:40.2.11/22.1.13/43.19.39) (q:draft)
Mirrah = (t:name) (w:Mirrah/myrrh) (d:myrrh, a fragrant resin, written with a capital; Mirrah paknamtui is myrrh perfume) (r:20.7.17/1.37.25)
Mishael = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mishael) (d:name of several men, among them a son of Uzziel the Levite and the companion of Daniel who was renamed Meshach) (r:2.6.22)
Mishal = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Mishal) (d:town in the territory of Asher, given to the Levites) (r:6.21.30/6.19.26)
Misham = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Misham) (d:son of Elpaal of the tribe of Benjamin) (r:13.8.12)
Mishamannah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mishmannah) (d:warrior of the tribe of Gad who joined David in the wilderness, fourth in rank) (r:13.12.10)
Mishma = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mishma) (d:name of two men, a son of Ishmael and a descendant of Simeon) (r:1.25.14)
Mishmannah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mishmannah) (d:warrior of the tribe of Gad who joined David in the wilderness, fourth in rank) (r:13.12.10)
Mishrai = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Mishraite) (d:one of the clans of Kiriath Jearim in Judah) (r:13.2.53)
Mishrefoth = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Misrephoth) (d:first part of the name Mishrefoth-maim, a place near Sidon at the northern limit of the land) (r:6.13.6)
Mishrefoth-maim = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Misrephoth Maim) (d:place near Sidon, named with Lebanon as the northern limit of the land still to be taken) (e:Lebanon leh ~ kikal-a teeng) (r:6.13.6) (q:draft)
misi = (t:n) (w:dead person/the dead/corpse) (d:mi, person, with si, die: someone who has died, or the body of a dead person; misi vui is bury the dead) (e:Naupang in ~ tawh kibang ahih ciangin/na ~ vui in | bury your dead/~ tawh kibangin a sibup uh hi | they became like dead men/~ honte’ lakah tung hi | he ends up in the company of the dead) (s:sipa/siluang) (r:41.9.26/20.21.16/1.23.11/40.28.4) (q:draft)
misia = (t:n) (w:bad person/wicked person/the wicked) (d:mi, person, with sia, bad: a bad or wicked person, the opposite of mipha, a good person) (e:~ in siatna thaman ngah a/~, mipha, hong encik kim hi | he keeps watch on the wicked and the good/mihoih leh ~, a kibangin | the good and the bad alike/Bangmah-a kimang lo ~ honte | a band of worthless bad people) (s:migilo) (a:mipha) (r:20.14.14/20.15.3/5.29.19/18.30.8) (q:draft)
misiam = (t:n) (w:skilled man/able man/capable person) (d:mi, person, with siam, skilled: a skilled or capable person) (e:~ mahmahte in nang hong hawl uh hi/minam bup khempeuh lak panin ~ nga | five able men from the whole tribe) (s:mikician) (r:26.27.8/7.18.2) (q:draft)
misiamte = (t:n) (w:capable men/skilled people/the learned) (d:misiam, skilled person, with the plural te: capable men, and in the Gospels the learned) (e:mipilte leh ~ kiangah im-inah/Moses in mipil ~ teel a | Moses chose wise and capable men/~ na teelkhia ding hi | you shall choose capable men) (b:misiam) (r:40.11.25/2.18.21/2.18.25) (q:draft)
misiangte = (t:n) (w:the clean/clean people) (d:mi, person, with siang, clean, and the plural te: those who are ritually clean, paired with mininte, the unclean) (e:~ leh mininte, biakna piate) (a:mininte) (r:21.9.2) (q:draft)
misiangtho = (t:n) (w:holy person/saint/holy one) (d:mi, person, with siangtho, holy: a holy person, one who belongs to God; Pasian’ misiangtho is a holy man of God or the Holy One of God) (e:Pasian’ ~ na hi ci-in/hong nawk tawntungpa in Pasian’ ~ hi | the one who often passes by is a holy man of God/~ tul sawmte kiang panin hong pai hi | he came from among tens of thousands of holy ones/mi mai-ah ~ bangin na om uh hi | before people you appear like holy men) (s:siangthopa) (r:43.6.69/49.1.15/12.4.9/5.33.2/40.23.28) (q:draft)
Misiangtho = (t:n) (w:Holy One/holy person) (d:misiangtho written with a capital, of the Holy One of God or at the start of a sentence) (e:Na ~ zong muatna na thuaksak kei ding hi/~ in mi siangtho ahih maninah | because the holy person is a holy person) (b:misiangtho) (r:44.2.27/40.10.41) (q:draft)
misiangthote = (t:n) (w:saints/holy people/God’s people) (d:misiangtho, holy person, with the plural te: the people who belong to God) (e:~ khempeuh in note hong hopih uh hi/a sisa ~’ luang tampi hong tho kik uh | many bodies of holy people who had died rose again/~ vaakin Jerusalem khuapi-ah ka pai ding hi | I am going to Jerusalem to serve the saints/Topa Zeisu’ hehpihna thupha ~ tawh omkhawm ta hen | the grace of the Lord Jesus be with the saints) (r:47.13.13/40.27.52/45.15.25/66.22.21) (q:draft)
misiapa = (t:n) (w:ruined man/broken man/wretched man) (d:mi person with sia bad, ruined, and pa marking a man) (e:ahih thei nawn lo ~, bang hangin) (b:misia) (r:18.30.24) (q:draft, low confidence)
misiate = (t:n) (w:bad people/the evil/the wicked) (d:misia, bad person, with the plural te; set against mihoihte and miphate, good people) (e:mihoihte le ~ tungah a kibangin/miphate le ~ a kibangin sihna panin hingkiksak khawm | raise both the good and the bad from death together/mihoihte leh ~, misiangte leh mininte | the good and the bad, the clean and the unclean) (s:migilote) (a:mihoihte/miphate) (b:misia) (r:40.5.45/21.9.2/44.24.15) (q:draft)
misiluang = (t:n) (w:dead body/corpse) (d:misi, dead person, with luang, body: a dead body) (e:ek bangin ~ a kipaaithang ding a) (s:siluang/luanghawm) (r:24.9.22) (q:draft)
Misiluangte = (t:n) (w:corpses/dead bodies/carcasses) (d:misiluang, dead body, with the plural te, here with a capital at the start of a sentence) (e:~ huih laka leeng vasate) (s:siluangte/luanghawmte) (r:24.7.33) (q:draft)
misimna = (t:n) (w:census/counting of people/numbering) (d:mi, person, and sim, count, with the noun suffix na: a count of the people; misimna bawl is take a census) (e:Israel mite ~ bawl-a, amaute na sim ciangin) (s:kisimna) (r:2.30.12/2.30.13) (q:draft)
misimtatte = (t:n) (w:hypocrites) (d:mi, person, with simtat, as in simtatna, hypocrisy, and the plural te: people who pretend to be good) (e:~ tawh a omkhawmsak ding hi) (s:simtatte/kineihkhemte) (r:40.24.51) (q:draft, low confidence)
misipa = (t:n) (w:dead man) (d:misi dead person with pa, a man: the dead man) (e:~ tho a, thu a gen hi/~ Josiah kah kei un la | do not weep for the dead man Josiah) (s:sipa) (b:misi) (r:42.7.15/43.11.39/24.22.10) (q:draft)
misite = (t:n) (w:the dead/dead people) (d:misi, dead person, with the plural te; misite’ gam is the land of the dead, the grave) (e:~ a thokik lo hi leh/amau ~ na vui ta hen | let them bury their own dead/Khazih in ~ lakah a gah masabel suak a | Christ became the firstfruits among the dead/~ tho kik ngei lo ding a | the dead will never rise again) (s:site) (a:nungtate) (b:misi) (r:46.15.16/18.26.5/40.8.22/46.15.20/18.14.12) (q:draft)
Misite = (t:n) (w:the dead) (d:misite written with a capital at the start of a sentence or in the name Misite’ Gam, the Land of the Dead, Hades) (e:Sihna le ~’ Gam, meiphualpi sungah a kilawn/~’ thawhkikna om lo hi | there is no resurrection of the dead/~’ gam kiling a | the land of the dead trembles) (b:misite) (r:66.20.14/66.20.13/40.22.23/18.26.5) (q:draft)
Mispah = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Mizpah) (d:region at the foot of Mount Hermon where the Hivites lived in the time of Joshua) (r:6.11.3)
Mispar = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mispar) (d:one of the leaders who returned from exile in Babylon with Zerubbabel) (r:15.2.2)
Mispereth = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mispereth) (d:one of the leaders who returned from exile in Babylon with Zerubbabel, called Mispar in the book of Ezra) (r:16.7.6)
Misrefothmaim = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Misrephoth Maim) (d:place near Sidon as far as which Joshua pursued the kings of the north) (r:6.11.8/6.13.6)
misuam = (t:n) (w:robber/bandit/insurrectionist) (d:one who attacks people with violence: a robber, and in the Gospels a rebel such as Barabbas) (e:~ buluhte’ bukna mun bang-a/~ thong kiate lakah | among the rebels who were in prison/Barabbas kici ~ minthang khat | a notorious rebel called Barabbas) (s:buluh/galgu) (r:24.7.11/41.15.7/40.27.16) (q:draft)
misuam = (t:v) (w:riot/rebel/make an insurrection) (d:rise up and attack people, take part in an uprising) (e:Tua Barabbas in khua sungah ~ a/Judah mi khempeuh ~ dingin a hansuah | he stirs up all the Jews to riot) (r:42.23.19/44.24.5) (q:draft)
misuampa = (t:n) (w:robber/insurrectionist/bandit) (d:misuam robber, rebel, with pa marking a man) (e:Barabbas in ~ ahi hi) (b:misuam) (r:43.18.40) (q:draft)
misuamte = (t:n) (w:robbers/bandits/rebels) (d:misuam, robber or rebel, with the plural te: men who attack and rob) (e:gutate leh ~ a hong pai a/Jerikho khua-ah a paisuk lai takin, ~ tawh kituak hi | going down to Jericho he fell among robbers/Zeisu tawh ~ nih, a ziatlam khat a veilam khat | two rebels with Jesus, one on the right and one on the left/tuikhang lauhuaina, ~ lauhuaina | danger from rivers, danger from bandits) (s:buluhte/suamte) (b:misuam) (r:31.1.5/42.10.36/42.10.30/41.15.27/47.11.26) (q:draft)
Misusia = (t:name) (w:Misusia) (d:word addressed to Babylon in Psalm 137, written with a capital: mi, person, with susia, destroy; the NIV has doomed to destruction) (r:19.137.8)
mit = (t:n) (w:eye) (d:the organ of sight; mit tawh en is look with the eyes) (e:khitui in i ~ hong mialsak hi/eite’ ~-ah lamdang hi | it is marvelous in our eyes/na ~ tawh en in | look with your eyes/tu-in na ~ hak in la | now let your eyes be open) (s:mittang) (r:25.5.17/1.19.11/19.118.23/14.6.20/14.6.40)
mit = (t:v) (w:put out/go out) (d:of a fire or a lamp, go out; also put a fire out) (e:mei na ~ ung/thu ngen a, mei a ~ hi | he prayed and the fire went out/Sing om kei leh mei ~ a | without wood a fire goes out/a meivak ~ ding hi | his lamp will go out) (s:mitsak/sumit) (r:4.11.2/20.26.20/18.18.6)
mit = (t:adv) (w:off)
mit = (t:v) (w:kill)
mitah = (t:n) (w:in the eyes/in the sight/on the eyes) (d:mit, eye, with the place marker ah: on the eyes or in the eyes; after Topa or a pronoun it means in the sight of) (e:Topa’ ~ a man gamta lo a/ka ~ a nuh khit ciangin | after he put it on my eyes/eite’ ~ lamdang hi | it is marvelous in our eyes/keima ~ a man thu lim takin na sepna | you have done well what is right in my eyes) (b:mit) (r:14.28.1/43.9.11/19.118.23/12.10.30) (q:draft)
mitang = (t:n) (w:eye/eyesight) (d:apparently the same as mittang, eye) (e:Na ~ bangci a hong vak hiam) (s:mittang) (r:43.9.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
mite = (t:v) (w:people) (e:Moses in tua ni mah-in ~ thuhilhin/tua gam ~’ maiah kun hi | he bowed before the people of the land/siampi liante, upate leh ~ sam a | he called the chief priests, the rulers and the people/Tua ~ a kisim ciangin pasal sawm-le-nih pha hi | when those men were counted there were twelve) (b:mi) (r:5.27.11/1.4.26/1.23.12/42.23.13/44.19.7) plural form of <mi>
Mite = (t:n) (w:people) (d:mite written with a capital at the start of a sentence or in a title: Jew Mite’ Kumpipa, King of the Jews; Mite’ Kongpi, Gate of the People) (e:Jew ~’ Kumpipa hi/~’ Kongpi le Jerusalem khua kongpite | the Gate of the People and the gates of Jerusalem/~ in khatvei bek si-in | people die only once/~ in meivak a vak khit uh ciangin | when people have lit a lamp) (b:mite) (r:42.23.38/24.17.19/58.9.27/40.5.15) (q:draft)
mitei = (t:n) (w:discerning person/person of insight) (d:mi, person, with tei, clever: a person of insight, paired with mipil, wise person) (e:mipil ~ peuhpeuhte in hih ganhing nambat) (r:66.13.18) (q:draft, low confidence)
miteite = (t:n) (w:the intelligent/the clever) (d:mi, person, with tei, clever, and the plural te: clever or learned people, named beside mipilte, the wise) (e:~’ teina ka heikhiatsak ding hi/tuhuna mipilte, ~, le thusel a siamte | the wise, the clever and the skilled debaters of this age) (r:46.1.19/46.1.20) (q:draft)
mitepen = (t:n) (w:people/men) (d:mite people with the topic marker pen, written as one word) (e:a vanglian na ~ gal sungah) (b:mite) (r:23.3.25) (q:draft)
mithagolte = (t:n) (w:giants) (d:mi, person, with thagol, big and strong, and the plural te: the giants of Gath, where the NIV has Rapha and Rephaites) (e:~ sung pana hong piang ahi uh hi/~’ suante khat ahi Saf that hi | he killed Saph, one of the descendants of the giants/Amah zong ~’ sung panin a piang ahi hi | he too was born of the giants) (s:thagolte) (r:13.20.8/13.20.4/10.21.18/10.21.20) (q:draft)
Mithagolte = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Mithagolte/Rephaites) (d:the giants, a race of very big men in Philistia, called Rapha or the Rephaites in the NIV; mithagolte written with a capital) (r:10.21.16)
mithah = (t:n) (w:bloodshed/murder/killing) (d:mi, person, with thah, kill: the killing of a person; mithah mawhna is the guilt of bloodshed) (e:~ nading pan leh nangma khut/Saul leh a innkuan tungah ~ mawhna om hi | the guilt of bloodshed is on Saul and his house) (s:mithahna/thahna) (r:9.25.26/10.21.1) (q:draft)
mithahna = (t:n) (w:murder/killing/bloodshed) (d:mithah, killing of a person, with the noun suffix na: murder, bloodshed) (e:Zuauna leh ~ tawh a kidim khuapi/a hoih lo ngaihsutna, ~, mi’ zi tungah mawhna | evil thoughts, murder, adultery/Jerusalem khua sung panin ~ teng a beisak ciangin | when he has removed all the bloodshed from Jerusalem) (s:thahna/kithahna/mithah) (b:mithah) (r:34.3.1/40.15.19/23.4.3) (q:draft)
mithak = (t:n) (w:new person/new self/new creation) (d:mi, person, with thak, new: the new self of one who is in Christ) (e:a om mi in ~ a suak hi/~ a sillh mi na hi uh hi | you are people who have put on the new self) (r:47.5.17/51.3.9) (q:draft)
mithat = (t:n) (w:murderer/killer) (d:mi, person, with that, kill: one who kills people, a murderer; the NIV has bloodthirsty and criminal) (e:~ bangin sikkol hong kibulh hi/~ theite, kei kiang panin paikhia sak in | make the bloodthirsty go away from me) (s:thatpa) (r:55.2.9/19.139.19) (q:draft)
mithatpa = (t:n) (w:murderer/killer) (d:mithat murderer with pa marking a man) (e:khuavak ma-in ~ kuankhia a) (s:thatpa) (b:mithat) (r:18.24.14) (q:draft)
mithatte = (t:n) (w:killers/manslayers/murderers) (d:mithat, killer, with the plural te; mithatte’ bukna khuapi is a city of refuge for those who have killed someone) (e:~’ bukna khuapi Hebron/~’ ading khuapi Shekhem a lonona gamte tawh | Shechem, the city for manslayers, with its pasturelands) (s:thatte) (b:mithat) (r:6.21.13/6.21.38/6.21.21) (q:draft)
mitheek = (t:n) (w:wink/signal with the eye) (d:mit, eye, with heek: a sign made with the eye; mitheek pia is wink at someone) (e:Simon Peter in a ~ tawh amah hopih a/a ~ hong pia-in | he winks at you/kei hong mudahte, ~ kipiasak kei in | do not let those who hate me wink) (r:43.13.24/20.6.13/19.35.19) (q:draft)
Mithkah = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Mithkah) (d:place in the wilderness where the Israelites camped between Terah and Hashmonah) (r:4.33.28/4.33.29)
Mithni = (t:name) (w:Mithni) (d:home or clan of Joshaphat, one of the mighty warriors of David, who is called the Mithnite in the NIV) (r:13.11.43)
Mithredath = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mithredath) (d:name of two Persian officials: the treasurer of King Cyrus, and a man who wrote to King Artaxerxes against Jerusalem) (r:15.1.8/15.4.7)
mithumante = (t:n) (w:the righteous/upright people) (d:mi person with thuman truthful, upright, plural te) (e:~ ahihleh humpinelkai bangin a hang uh hi) (s:midikte/thumante) (a:migilote) (r:20.28.1) (q:draft)
mithupite = (t:n) (w:nobles/important people/dignitaries) (d:mi person with thupi important, plural te) (e:milian ~ in keima huhna bek tawh) (s:miliante) (r:20.8.16) (q:draft)
Mitilena = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Mitylene) (d:chief city of the island of Lesbos, where the ship of Paul called after Assos; also spelled Mitylene) (r:44.20.14)
mitin = (t:n) (w:with the eyes/with one's own eyes) (d:mit, eye, with the marker in, showing the eye as the means of seeing: with the eyes) (e:Ka ~ ka mu zo hi/note’ ~ nong mu uh a | you see it with your own eyes/a omdan khempeuh uh ka ~ ka mu a | I see all their ways with my eyes/kumpipa in a ~ a etna tawh | the king with the look of his eyes) (b:mit) (r:42.2.32/1.45.12/24.16.17/20.20.8) (q:draft)
mitkhu = (t:n) (w:eyelid) (d:mit eye with khu cover; mitkhu mul, the hair of it, stands for the eyebrows in Leviticus 14:9) (e:i ~ a kawt theih nadingin/a khamul leh a ~ mul | his beard and his eyebrows) (r:24.9.18/3.14.9) (q:draft)
mitkhuk = (t:n) (w:eye socket) (d:mit eye with khuk pit, hollow) (e:a ~ sung uhah a mittangte uh muatin) (s:mitkua) (r:38.14.12) (q:draft)
mitkhute = (t:n) (w:eyelids) (d:mitkhu eyelid with plural te) (e:ka ~ ka kikhupsak kei ding hi/ka ~ bawkin hong liahcip hi) (b:mitkhu) (r:19.132.1/18.16.16) (q:draft)
mitkua = (t:n) (w:eye socket) (d:mit eye with kua hole) (e:a ~ sung uhah a mittangte uh muatin) (s:mitkhuk) (r:38.14.12) (q:draft)
mitlawt = (t:v) (w:lose one's sight/have the eyes fail) (d:mit eye with lawt; mitlawt dongin kap, weep until the eyes fail) (e:~ dongin a kap ding) (r:9.2.33) (q:draft, low confidence)
mitmangin = (t:v) (w:grow dim/lose one's sight) (d:mit eye with mang lost, dim, and the linking marker in: the eyes growing dim) (e:na ~ khua na lim muh theih) (r:21.12.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
mitnauta = (t:n) (w:pupil of the eye/apple of the eye) (d:the pupil of the eye, used in comparisons for something guarded with great care: mitnauta bangin kem, keep as the apple of the eye) (e:ama ~ bangin amaute kem hi/~ bangin hong kem in la | keep me as the apple of your eye/na ~ bangin hoih takin kem in | guard them well as the apple of your eye) (r:5.32.10/19.17.8/20.7.2) (q:draft)
mitpak = (t:v) (w:go out suddenly/be snuffed out) (d:mit go out, of a light, with pak at once) (e:migilote meivak bangin ~ hi) (r:20.13.9) (q:draft)
mitphial = (t:n) (w:magic/sorcery/witchcraft) (d:magic arts that deceive the eye; mitphial siamte are magicians and mitphial bawl is practise sorcery) (e:Amah in ~ bawlin/~ siamte in amau' siamna tawh | the magicians by their own arts/tua khua sungah ~ dawi bawlin | practising sorcery in that city/Na ~ siamnate uh susia-in | I will destroy your witchcraft) (r:44.8.11/27.2.2/2.8.7/44.8.9/33.5.12) (q:draft)
mitphiat = (t:n) (w:blink/twinkling of an eye/moment) (d:the closing and opening of the eyelid, hence a very short time: mitphiat kal and mitphiat sung, in a moment) (e:tomkha sung ~ kikalin/~ kalin bei mang thei a | it can vanish in the blink of an eye/~ sung nangawn ka mang ka ngai kei uh hi | we did not give in to them even for a moment) (s:tomkha) (r:46.15.52/20.23.5/48.2.5) (q:draft)
mitsak = (t:v) (w:quench/extinguish/put out) (d:mit, go out, with the causative sak: make a fire or lamp go out) (e:meikuang a ~ uh hi/Kha Siangtho’ huhna na ~ kei un | do not quench the help of the Holy Spirit/meivak khau kisumit bangin a ~ Topa | the Lord who put them out like a snuffed wick) (s:sumit/phelh) (b:mit) (r:58.11.34/52.5.19/23.43.16) (q:draft)
mitsi = (t:v) (w:close the eyes/shut the eyes) (d:of the eyes, be shut; with sak, make someone's eyes shut so that he cannot see) (e:nomau’ mit ahi kamsangte ~ sak-in) (r:23.29.10) (q:draft)
mitsicip = (t:v) (w:shut the eyes tight/close the eyes) (d:mitsi close the eyes with cip tightly) (e:a bil uh humcip uh a, ~ uh hi) (b:mitsi) (r:44.28.25) (q:draft)
mitsuan = (t:v) (w:look to/fix the eyes on/watch) (d:keep the eyes on someone or something, in trust or attention) (e:nangma lampite ka ~ ding hi/nangmah bek kong ~ uh hi | we look to you alone/Amaute’ an lakna lo na ~ in la | keep your eyes on the field they are harvesting/kimu thei lo nate a ~ ka hi uh hi | we fix our eyes on what is unseen) (r:19.119.15/14.20.12/8.2.9/47.4.18) (q:draft)
mitsuanin = (t:adv) (w:with eyes fixed on/looking to) (d:mitsuan fix the eyes on, with in; mitsuanin nei is to keep the eyes fixed on, to hold in view) (e:hong cingtaaksak Jesuh ~ nei ni/nangma thupiakte khempeuh ~ nei khin ka hih manin | because I keep all your commands in view) (b:mitsuan) (r:58.12.2/19.119.6) (q:draft)
mitta = (t:v) (w:go out/have gone out) (d:mit go out, of fire or a lamp, with ta marking a change that has come about) (e:Ka mei uh ~ ahih manin) (b:mit) (r:40.25.8) (q:draft)
mittang = (t:n) (w:eye) (d:the eye, the eyeball; a fuller word for mit) (e:Na ~ in hong puksak leh/leengpei kualte tungah ~ vive a dimin om hi | the rims of the wheels were full of eyes/Zedekiah’ ~ a khelkhiat sak khit ciangin | after he had the eyes of Zedekiah put out/Ka ~ hong vaksak hi | he opened my eyes) (s:mit) (r:41.9.47/27.7.8/26.1.18/24.39.7/43.9.30) (q:draft)
mittangin = (t:n) (w:with the eye/by sight) (d:mittang eye with the marker in: with the eyes) (e:~ kimu loin a hong tung hi) (b:mittang) (r:42.17.20) (q:draft)
mittangte = (t:n) (w:eyes) (d:mittang, eye, with the plural te) (e:A ~ in meikuang bangin ahi uh a/a ~ nisuak tung bangin taang hi | its eyes shine like the dawn/a ~ in mei bangin a kuang zalzal hi | his eyes blazed like fire/a mu ~ in thupha a ngah ding uh hi | the eyes that see it will be blessed) (s:mitte) (b:mittang) (r:66.1.14/18.41.18/27.10.6/42.10.23) (q:draft)
mittaw = (t:adj) (w:blind) (d:mit, eye, with taw, blind: blind; also used as a noun for a blind person) (e:Amaute ~ bangin kongzing lakah vak uh a/a nu’ sung pan ~ khat a mu hi | he saw a man blind from birth/a suahpih ~ ahih ka thei uh hi | we know he was born blind/~ in khuamial lakah khua a zawt bangin | as a blind man gropes in the dark) (s:taw) (r:25.4.14/43.9.1/43.9.20/5.28.29) (q:draft)
mittawpa = (t:n) (w:blind man) (d:mittaw, blind, with -pa, marking a man) (e:Amaute in ~ sam uh a/tua ~ Farisaite kiangah a paipih uh hi | they brought the blind man to the Pharisees/Zeisu in ~ a khut tawh kai a | Jesus took the blind man by the hand) (b:mittaw) (r:41.10.49/43.9.13/41.8.23) (q:draft)
mittawpite = (t:n) (w:blind ones/the blind) (d:mittaw blind with pi and the plural te: the ones that are blind, here of animals brought as offerings) (e:Ganhing a ~ tawh kei nong biak) (b:mittaw) (r:39.1.8) (q:draft)
mittawsa = (t:adj) (w:blind/formerly blind) (d:mittaw blind with sa, already: one who had been blind) (e:nidang lai ~ a nung ciangin) (b:mittaw) (r:43.9.19) (q:draft)
mittawsak = (t:v) (w:blind/make blind) (d:mittaw blind with the causative sak) (e:bilngongsak, musak, ~ ahi hiam) (s:tawsak) (b:mittaw) (r:2.4.11/23.29.9) (q:draft)
mittawt = (t:v) (w:be blind/become blind) (d:form of mittaw blind used before nading and before a joined word) (e:khua mu theite in ~ nading/~ le pau theih loh a thuah dawivei mi khat | a demon-possessed man who was blind and mute) (b:mittaw) (r:43.9.39/40.12.22) (q:draft)
mittawte = (t:n) (w:the blind/blind people) (d:mittaw, blind, with the plural te: blind people) (e:~ lam hilh mi/~’ mit kihong ding a | the eyes of the blind will be opened/khebaite leh ~ na sam in | invite the lame and the blind/Topa in ~, khua musak hi | the Lord gives sight to the blind) (s:tawte) (b:mittaw) (r:45.2.19/23.35.5/42.14.13/19.146.8) (q:draft)
Mittawte = (t:n) (w:the blind/blind people) (d:mittawte written with a capital at the start of a sentence or a line) (e:~ in khua a muh kik theih nading/~ in mittawte lam a hilh zo ding hiam | can the blind lead the blind/~’ adingin mit ka hi a | I was eyes to the blind) (b:mittawte) (r:42.4.18/42.6.39/18.29.15) (q:draft)
mittawtna = (t:n) (w:blindness) (d:mittawt, be blind, with the noun suffix na: the state of being blind) (e:Hih mite ~ tawh vatgawp in/haina leh ~ leh lungsim buaina tawh | with madness, blindness and confusion of mind/hih pa a ~ ama mawhna hang ahi hiam | is the blindness of this man because of his own sin) (b:mittawt) (r:12.6.18/5.28.28/43.9.2) (q:draft)
mitte = (t:n) (w:eyes) (e:a ~ mangin khua mu thei lo hi/Tu-in ka ~ hakin | now my eyes will be open/ama' ~ leenggahzu sangin vom zaw ding a | his eyes will be darker than wine) (s:mittangte) (b:mit) (r:9.4.15/1.3.5/14.7.15/1.49.12) plural form of <mit>
mituam = (t:n) (w:special people/own people) (d:mi person with tuam separate: a people set apart; said by God of Israel where the English has Virgin Israel) (e:Ka ~ Israel in a mulkimhuai na khat) (r:24.18.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
Mitylene = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Mitylene) (d:chief city of the island of Lesbos, where the ship of Paul called after Assos) (r:44.20.14)
mitzo = (t:v) (w:go out/be quenched) (d:mit go out with zo be able; with lo, cannot be quenched) (e:i phumcip hangin ~ tuan lo hi) (b:mit) (r:22.8.7) (q:draft)
mitzung = (t:n) (w:eyesight/sight) (d:mit eye with zung root; ka mitzung zaw is my eyes grow weak) (e:ka ~ zaw semsem hi) (r:19.6.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
mivanglianpa = (t:n) (w:mighty man/hero) (d:mi person with vanglian mighty and pa marking a man) (e:~ leh galkappa, thukhenpa leh kamsangpa) (r:23.3.2) (q:draft)
mivomte = (t:n) (w:black people) (d:mi person with vom black and the plural te; Ethiopia mivomte is the Ethiopians) (e:Ethiopia ~ in a vun uh) (r:24.13.23) (q:draft)
Mizar = (t:name) (c:mountain) (w:Mizar) (d:hill or mountain in the region of Mount Hermon, named in Psalm 42) (r:19.42.6)
mizawng = (t:n) (w:poor person/the poor/beggar) (d:mi, person, with zawng, poor: a poor person or a beggar; also used to say that someone is poor) (e:Lazaras kici ~ khat in/Amah ~ ahih leh | if he is a poor man/Amaute lakah ~ khat beek a om kei uh hi | there was not one needy person among them/bangmah a nei lo ~ pawlkhat | some poor people who owned nothing) (s:zawngpa) (a:mihau) (r:42.16.20/18.29.12/5.24.12/44.4.34/24.39.10) (q:draft)
mizawngin = (t:n) (w:poor person) (d:mizawng poor person with the marker in, here as: became poor) (e:note’ hangin ~ hong kibawl ahih manin) (b:mizawng) (r:47.8.9) (q:draft)
mizawngpa = (t:n) (w:poor man/beggar) (d:mizawng poor person with pa marking a man) (e:Tua nung ciangin ~ si a/kuamah in tua ~ phawk kha lo hi | nobody remembered that poor man/~ in kitat nading bangmah nei lo hi | the poor man has nothing to ransom himself with) (s:zawngpa) (a:mihaupa) (b:mizawng) (r:42.16.22/21.9.15/20.13.8) (q:draft)
mizawngpen = (t:n) (w:poorest people/the poorest) (d:mizawng poor person with the superlative pen) (e:~ pawlkhat tawh) (b:mizawng) (r:24.52.15) (q:draft)
mizawngte = (t:n) (w:the poor/poor people/the needy) (d:mizawng, poor person, with the plural te: poor people, the opposite of mihaute, the rich) (e:zawn’na in ~ siasak hi/Kuamah in ~ ngai lo a | no one cares for the poor/A cingh mite in ~ an pia a | the generous give food to the poor/Mihaute in ~ uk a | the rich rule over the poor) (s:zawngte/cimawhte/gentheite) (a:mihaute) (r:20.10.15/18.34.28/20.14.20/20.22.9/20.22.7) (q:draft)
Mizpah = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Mizpah) (d:name of several places, among them the town in Benjamin where Samuel gathered Israel and the place in Gilead where Jacob and Laban made their covenant) (r:16.3.19/1.31.49)
Mizpeh = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Mizpah) (d:spelling of Mizpah used for a town in the lowland of Judah, a town in Benjamin and a place in Moab where David took his parents) (r:6.18.26/6.15.38)
