Mnanhath = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Manahath) (d:place to which men of Benjamin living in Geba were deported; the NIV spells it Manahath) (r:13.8.6)
Mnason = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mnason) (d:man from Cyprus, an early disciple, at whose house Paul stayed on the way to Jerusalem) (r:44.21.16)
mo = (t:n) (w:bride) (d:a woman who is being married; mo la is to take a bride, so a wedding, and mo-man is the bride price) (e:Kana khua-ah ~ la lawmvakna om a/a kipi ~ bangin kiging kholin | made ready like a bride adorned/Tuuno’ zi ahi ~ kong lak ding hi | I will show you the bride, the wife of the Lamb/~ la lawm an vakna pan hong ciah | returns from the wedding banquet) (s:mothak) (r:43.2.1/1.34.12/66.21.2/66.21.9/42.12.36) (q:draft)
mo = (t:n) (w:daughter-in-law) (d:the wife of one’s son) (e:a ~ tegel tawh tua nu dingkhia a) (s:monu) (r:8.1.7) (q:draft)
Mo = (t:n) (w:bride) (d:mo, bride, written with a capital, in Revelation for the bride of the Lamb and at the start of a sentence) (e:Kha Siangtho leh a kipi ~ in/~ leh Mopipa’ aw nang sungah | the voice of bride and bridegroom in you/~ pen zinei ding tangvalpa a’ ding | the bride belongs to the bridegroom) (s:Mothak) (b:mo) (r:66.22.17/66.18.23/43.3.29) (q:draft)
