Moabte = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Moab/Moabites) (d:the people of Moab, descendants of Lot, living east of the Dead Sea) (b:Moab) (r:12.3.23/4.21.28)
Moadiah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Moadiah) (d:head of a priestly family in the days of the high priest Joiakim) (r:16.12.17)
Moan = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Maon) (d:spelling of Maon, the desert in the hill country of Judah where David hid from Saul) (r:9.23.25)
moh = (t:n) (w:cake/loaf/bread) (d:a baked cake or loaf of bread; thei moh is a cake of pressed figs and silngo sawhloh moh is unleavened bread) (e:Anlum sawm, ~ pawlkhat, leh khuaizu/leh thei ~ zanih la-in | and took two hundred cakes of figs/biakna in ~ khat na pia ding uh hi | you shall present a loaf as an offering/silngo sawhloh ~ leh ankan ne uh hi | they ate unleavened bread and roasted grain) (r:11.14.3/28.7.8/9.25.18/4.15.20/6.5.11) (q:draft)
mohbawl = (t:v) (w:bake bread/make bread) (d:moh, bread, with bawl, make: make bread; mohbawl pa is the baker) (e:~ pa in a anlom meek) (b:moh) (r:28.7.4) (q:draft)
mohin = (t:adv) (w:into cakes/into loaves) (d:moh, cake or loaf, with the marker in: into cakes or loaves, as in mohin bawl, make into loaves) (e:beelin huan uh a, ~ a bawl uh hi/meek manin ~ hong bawl in | knead it and make it into cakes) (b:moh) (r:4.11.8/1.18.6) (q:draft)
mohkeu = (t:n) (w:dry bread/dry crust) (d:moh, bread, with keu, dry: a dry piece of bread, a crust) (e:lungnuam takin ~ themkhat nekna hoihzaw hi) (r:20.17.1) (q:draft)
mohlawh = (t:n) (w:basket of bread/bread basket) (d:moh, bread, with lawh, basket: a basket of bread) (e:Ka lu tungah ~ thum om a) (r:1.40.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
mohneu = (t:n) (w:small loaf/little cake) (d:moh, bread, with neu, small: a small loaf or cake) (e:Kei a dingin ~ khat hong bawlsak masa-in) (r:11.17.13) (q:draft)
mohpheng = (t:n) (w:wafer/thin cake/thin loaf) (d:moh, cake, with pheng, flat: a thin flat cake of bread, a wafer) (e:khuaizu tawh a kibawl ~ tawh kibang hi/~ khat, zong na la ding hi | you shall also take one thin loaf/sathau tawh a kizut ~ hi ding hi | it shall be thin loaves brushed with oil/silngo sawhloh ~ khat la-in | taking one thin loaf made without yeast) (s:pheng) (r:2.16.31/2.29.23/3.2.4/4.6.19) (q:draft)
mohphengte = (t:n) (w:thin cakes/wafers/flat loaves) (d:plural of mohpheng: thin flat cakes or wafers of bread) (e:a bawlsa ~ la-in inndei sung/silngo sawhloh ~ la in | take thin loaves made without yeast/ama muhna-ah ~ bawlin em hi | she made cakes in his sight and baked them) (s:pheengte) (b:mohpheng) (r:10.13.10/2.29.2/10.13.8) (q:draft)
mohte = (t:n) (w:cakes/loaves) (d:plural of moh: cakes or loaves; thei mohte are cakes of pressed figs) (e:sathau tawh a kihel silngo sawhloh ~/an tampi tak, thei ~, leenggahkeu bawkte | plenty of food, fig cakes and raisin cakes/silngo kisawh anlum ~ ama biakna-in | loaves of bread made with yeast as his offering/sathau tawh a kibawl annel ~ | loaves of fine flour made with oil) (b:moh) (r:2.29.2/13.12.40/3.7.13/4.6.15) (q:draft)
moi = (t:adj) (w:young/small) (d:young in age, the opposite of ham, old; a moi pen is the youngest, and a moi a ham is young and old alike) (e:a ~ pen tawh tawp hi/Sodom khuamite, a ~ a ham-in | the men of Sodom, young and old/na sanggam a ~ pen hong paisuk khop kei leh | unless your youngest brother comes down with you/a ~ ahi a, a ham ahi a | whether young or old) (s:khangno) (a:ham) (r:1.44.12/1.19.4/1.44.23/14.15.13) (q:draft)
moilai = (t:adj) (w:young/youthful) (d:still in the time of youth, said of a boy or young man) (e:sanggam pasal ~ khat ka nei uh hi) (s:khangno) (r:1.44.20) (q:draft)
moipen = (t:adj) (w:youngest) (d:moi, young, with pen, most: the youngest of a group, the opposite of hampen, the oldest) (e:a hampen panin kipanin a ~ tawh tawp a/a ~ panin a hampen dongin | from the youngest to the oldest/na sanggam uh a ~ hong paisuk khop kei leh | unless your youngest brother comes down with you/a ~ Kanaan gamah ka pa uh tawh om | the youngest is with our father in Canaan) (s:khangnopen) (a:hampen/teekpen) (b:moi) (r:1.44.12/12.3.21/1.44.23/1.42.32) (q:draft)
moisuahin = (t:adj) (w:youthful/in the bloom of youth) (d:moisuah newly grown up, in full youth, with the linking marker in) (e:A pumpi ~ a thahat hangin) (r:18.20.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
moken = (t:n) (w:dowry/wedding gift) (d:a gift given with a bride at her marriage, from mo, bride) (e:Pasian in ~’ hoih kei hong guan hi/a tanu’ tungah ~’ in a khuapi pia hi | he gave the city to his daughter as a wedding gift) (r:1.30.20/11.9.16) (q:draft)
mokenin = (t:n) (w:as a wedding gift/as a dowry) (d:moken, wedding gift, with the marker in: as a wedding gift) (e:a tanu’ tungah ~ a khuapi a piak) (b:moken) (r:11.9.16) (q:draft)
mokhak = (t:v) (w:give in marriage/send off as a bride) (d:mo, bride, with khak, send: give a daughter in marriage to another family) (e:tanu sawmthum ~ a) (r:7.12.9) (q:draft)
Moladah = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Moladah) (d:town in the far south of Judah, allotted to the tribe of Simeon) (r:13.4.28/16.11.26)
molakna = (t:n) (w:wedding/marriage) (d:mo, bride, with lak, take, and the noun suffix na: the taking of a bride, a wedding; molakna puan is wedding clothes) (e:~ puan silh lo-a om mi khat/~ puan silh loin | without wearing wedding clothes) (s:mopina) (r:40.22.11/40.22.12) (q:draft)
molakpawi = (t:n) (w:wedding feast/wedding banquet) (d:mo, bride, with lak, take, and pawi, feast: a wedding feast) (e:a tapa ading ~ a kham kumpipa) (s:mopawi) (r:40.22.2) (q:draft)
Molek = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Molech/Molek) (d:god of the Ammonites, to whom children were sacrificed) (r:3.20.4/3.18.21)
molhtum = (t:n) (w:club/rod/cudgel) (d:a heavy stick used as a weapon or for beating, a club) (e:namsau leh ~ tawi-in na hong pai uh/Ama adingin ~ pen buhkung bang hi lel a | to him a club is only like straw/kumminte ~ tawh kisat hi | cumin is beaten out with a stick/~, namsau, ahih kei leh thaltang hiam | a club, a sword or a sharp arrow) (r:41.14.48/2.21.20/18.41.29/23.28.27/20.25.18) (q:draft)
molhtumin = (t:n) (w:as a club/club) (d:molhtum, club, with the marker in: as a club) (e:~ a zang ding bangkeek) (b:molhtum) (r:23.10.15) (q:draft)
molhtumte = (t:n) (w:clubs/cudgels) (d:plural of molhtum; kulh sukkhap nading molhtumte are battering rams) (e:namsau leh ~ tawi-in amau tawh hong tonkhawm/thaltangte, ~, leh teipite | arrows, clubs and spears/kulh sukkhap nading ~ bawl in | set up battering rams against the wall) (b:molhtum) (r:40.26.47/26.4.2/26.39.9) (q:draft)
moliah = (t:n) (w:best man/groomsman/wedding companion) (d:one who attends the bridegroom at his wedding; moliah pa, the man who does so) (e:a ~ pa’ zi dingin na kipia hi) (r:7.14.20) (q:draft)
moliahpa = (t:n) (w:best man/groomsman/wedding companion) (d:moliah with pa marking a man: the companion who attends the bridegroom) (e:a ~’ zi dingin kipia hi) (b:moliah) (r:7.14.20) (q:draft)
Molid = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Molid) (d:son of Abishur and Abihail, of the tribe of Judah) (r:13.2.29)
Molok = (t:name) (w:Molek) (d:spelling of Molek in Acts, the god to whom Israel carried a shrine in the wilderness) (r:44.7.43)
mom = (t:see) <mom-ai>
mom-ai = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:scorpion) (d:a small creature with a poisonous sting in its tail, also written momai) (e:gul gunei leh ~ lak/~ laka om na bang ding hi | you will be like one living among scorpions) (s:momai/aikam) (r:5.8.15/26.2.6) (q:draft)
momai = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:scorpion) (d:a small creature with a poisonous sting in its tail, also written mom-ai) (e:aktui tangin ~ a pia ding/A mei un ~’ mei tawh kibang a | their tails were like the tail of a scorpion/~ in mi a sut ciangin | when a scorpion stings a person/gul gunei le ~ lak | among venomous snakes and scorpions) (s:mom-ai/aikam) (r:42.11.12/66.9.5/66.9.10/5.8.15) (q:draft)
momaite = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:scorpions) (d:plural of momai, scorpion) (e:Gulpi le ~ na sikgawp nading uh/leitungah a om ~’ vangliatna bang | like the power of the scorpions of the earth) (s:aikamte) (b:momai) (r:42.10.19/66.9.3) (q:draft)
moman = (t:n) (w:bride-price/dowry) (d:mo, bride, with man, price: the price paid to the father of a bride) (e:kumpipa in ~ deih lo hi/tua nu’ man ding ~ letsong pia ding a | he shall pay the bride-price for her/~ le letsong tampi hong ngen un | ask of me a great bride-price and gift) (r:9.18.25/2.22.16/1.34.12) (q:draft)
mong = (t:n) (w:end/edge/hem/corner) (d:the far end, outer edge or corner of something; puan mong is the hem of a garment and mong nei lo is without end) (e:na nuntak kumte in ~ nei lo hi/puantualpi ~ kimkotah | all around the hem of the robe/Leitaw lam a gamgi in Ci Tuipi ~ | the southern border, from the end of the Salt Sea/awmdal ~ nih, siampi puan tawh a kizom | the two corners of the breastpiece, next to the ephod) (r:19.102.27/2.28.34/6.15.2/2.28.26) (q:draft)
monga = (t:adv) (w:at the edge/at the end) (d:mong, edge, with the place marker a, a short form of ah: at the edge or end of a place) (e:gam ~ om Etham ah giahphual sat/Refaim kuam leilu lam ~ a om | at the northern end of the Valley of Rephaim) (s:mongah) (b:mong) (r:4.33.6/6.18.16) (q:draft)
mongah = (t:adv) (w:at the end/at the edge/at the corner) (d:mong, end or edge, with the place marker ah: at the end, edge or far part of a place) (e:awmdal ~ tua kual nihte na bulh ding/kuam ~ amaute na mu ding uh hi | you will find them at the end of the gorge/bual tungnung tui lakna ~ | at the end of the aqueduct of the Upper Pool/Efraim mualtung gam ~ peemin | living in a remote part of the hill country of Ephraim) (s:monga) (b:mong) (r:2.28.23/14.20.16/23.7.3/7.19.1) (q:draft)
mongciik = (t:n) (w:farthest end/extremity/uttermost part) (d:the very edge of a land; leitaw lam mongciik, the southernmost part) (e:Leitaw lam ~, Edom gamgi lamah) (s:mongdong) (r:6.15.21) (q:draft)
mongdong = (t:n) (w:end/farthest end) (d:mong, edge, with dong, as far as: the farthest end; lei mongdong is the ends of the earth) (e:lei ~ ah amaute khempeuh phul ding hi) (s:mongciik) (r:5.33.17) (q:draft)
mongin = (t:adv) (w:by the hem/by the edge) (d:mong, edge or hem, with the marker in: by the edge, said of what is taken hold of) (e:Saul in a puantualpi ~ len a/Zing khuavak in leitung a ~ manin | the morning light taking the earth by its edges) (b:mong) (r:9.15.27/18.38.13) (q:draft)
mongkhat = (t:n) (w:one end/one edge) (d:mong, end or edge, with khat, one: one end; mongkhat panin mongkhat dong is from one end to the other) (e:van ~ panin phia a/Egypt ~ panin a ~ dongin | from one end of Egypt to the other/leimong khat pan ~ dong taan’ hi | it shines from one end of the earth to the other) (r:42.17.24/1.47.21/18.37.3) (q:draft)
mongte = (t:n) (w:ends/edges/corners/hems) (d:plural of mong: the ends of poles, the edges of a beard, the corners or hem of a garment) (e:a puan ~ uhah a teep bawlin/na khamul ~ uh zong na tan kei ding | you shall not clip the edges of your beard/biakinn sungnung mai-ah a ~ kidawk hi | their ends showed in front of the inner sanctuary/Siangtho Mun panin a zawl ~ kimu hi | the ends of the poles could be seen from the Holy Place) (b:mong) (r:4.15.38/14.5.9/3.19.27/11.8.8) (q:draft)
mongteep = (t:n) (w:hem/edge/fringe) (d:the border or fringe at the edge of a garment; puan mongteep is the edge of a cloak) (e:a puan ~ a lawngsim hi/Zeisu’ puan ~ a lawn’ nadingun a ngen uh hi | they begged to touch the edge of Jesus’ cloak/a puan ~ tungah khau dum khat | a blue cord on the fringe of the garment) (s:puanmongteep) (r:40.9.20/42.8.44/40.14.36/4.15.38) (q:draft)
monu = (t:n) (w:daughter-in-law) (d:mo, bride or son’s wife, with nu marking a woman: the wife of one’s son) (e:teeknu leh ~, khat leh khat/Naomi in a ~ Ruth kiangah | Naomi to her daughter-in-law Ruth/Nangmah in na ~ na mawhpih kei ding hi | you shall not have sexual relations with your daughter-in-law/a ~ a hih lam thei lo hi | he did not know that she was his daughter-in-law) (s:mo) (b:mo) (r:40.10.35/3.18.15/8.2.22/1.38.16) (q:draft)
monute = (t:n) (w:daughters-in-law) (d:plural of monu: the wives of the sons of a family) (e:~ le teeknute a kidosak dingin) (s:mote) (b:monu) (r:40.10.35) (q:draft)
mopawi = (t:n) (w:wedding feast/wedding banquet/wedding) (d:mo, bride, with pawi, feast: a wedding feast; mopawi sim is to attend a wedding) (e:~ siim dingin a khohsa mite/a topa uh ~ simna panin hong tungin | their master coming back from a wedding banquet/~ bawlna sungah a lutkhawm pah uh hi | they went in together to the wedding banquet) (s:molakpawi) (r:40.22.3/42.14.8/42.12.36/40.25.10) (q:draft)
mopina = (t:n) (w:wedding/marriage) (d:a wedding, the taking of a bride; mopina pawi is a wedding feast) (e:~ pawi sungah mi a dim hi/~ pawi ding teng a baihsa-in a om hi | everything for the wedding banquet is ready/nungakte tawh ~ pawi sungah a lut khawm | went in with the virgins to the wedding banquet) (s:molakna/zipina) (r:40.22.10/40.25.10/40.22.8) (q:draft)
mopipa = (t:n) (w:bridegroom) (d:the man who is taking a bride) (e:Mo leh ~’ aw nang sungah) (s:zipipa/zineipa) (r:66.18.23)
Mopipa = (t:n) (w:bridegroom) (d:mopipa, bridegroom, written with a capital) (e:Mo leh ~’ aw nang sungah) (s:zipipa/zineipa) (b:mopipa) (r:66.18.23) (q:draft)
mor = (t:n) (w:myrrh) (d:a fragrant resin used as a spice and perfume, in mor paknamtui, myrrh spice) (e:singnai, ~ paknamtui, pistakhio gah/puante, ~ paknamtuite, a kum kumin tampi tak | robes and myrrh spices, in great amount year after year) (s:mirrah/myrrh) (r:1.43.11/11.10.25) (q:draft)
Mordekai = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mordecai) (d:Jew of the tribe of Benjamin living in Susa, cousin and guardian of Queen Esther) (r:17.2.5/17.2.7)
Moreh = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Moreh) (d:place near Shechem known for its great tree; also a hill in the Valley of Jezreel near which Midian camped) (r:5.11.30/7.7.1)
Moreseth = (t:see) <Moreseth-gath>
