Moseste = (t:name) (w:Moses) (d:Moses with the plural te: Moses and the one named with him, here Aaron and Moses) (b:Moses) (r:2.6.26)
mot = (t:adv) (w:idly/aimlessly/senselessly) (d:without thought, sense or purpose; mot pau is to talk idly or foolishly and mot om is to live on aimlessly) (e:~ pau loin na om uh leh/thei lopi-in a ~ om ding | to live on aimlessly without knowing/~ paupau, lum lum | babbling idly and lying around/thu thei loin a ~ paupau mihaite | foolish people who talk idly without knowledge) (s:mawk) (r:23.58.13/60.2.15/18.3.23/23.56.10) (q:draft)
mote = (t:n) (w:daughters-in-law) (d:plural of mo: the wives of the sons of a family) (e:~ in a teeknu uh lang neih/na ~ un midang tawh mawhna a bawl uh hi | your daughters-in-law commit adultery/na ~ uh midang tawh a mawh manin | because your daughters-in-law commit adultery/pawlkhat in a ~ mawhpihin | another defiles his daughter-in-law) (s:monute) (b:mo) (r:33.7.6/28.4.14/28.4.13/26.22.11) (q:draft)
mothak = (t:n) (w:bride) (d:mo, bride, with thak, new: a newly married woman, a bride; mothak nu is the bride) (e:~ in a pasal kiang inn-ah hong ciah/na ~ lai-a nong itna | the love you had as a bride/zipipa ~ nu tungah a lungdam mah bangin | as a bridegroom rejoices over his bride/~ nu in a zat bangin | as a bride does) (s:mo) (r:10.17.3/23.62.5/24.2.2/23.49.18) (q:draft)
Mothak = (t:n) (w:bride) (d:mothak written with a capital for the bride of the Lamb) (e:Kha Siangtho le ~ in Jesuh kiangah/Tuuno zi, a ~ ka hong lak ding hi | I will show you the bride, the wife of the Lamb/~ khat a pasal tawh a kituah dingin | like a bride ready to meet her husband) (s:Mo) (b:mothak) (r:66.22.17/66.21.9/66.21.2) (q:draft)
mothaknu = (t:n) (w:bride) (d:mothak, bride, with nu marking a woman) (e:zi nei thak pa leh ~’ awte) (s:mo) (b:mothak) (r:24.25.10) (q:draft)
mothakte = (t:n) (w:brides) (d:plural of mothak, bride, itself mo, bride, with thak, new) (e:zi nei thakte leh ~’ awte/leh ~’ awte kiza kik ding hi | and the voices of brides will be heard again) (b:mothak) (r:24.33.11/24.7.34) (q:draft)
motpau = (t:v) (w:talk idly/speak idle words) (d:mot, idly, with pau, speak: talk idly or foolishly) (e:~ loin na om uhleh) (r:23.58.13) (q:draft)
Moza = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Moza) (d:name of two men, a son of Caleb by his concubine Ephah and a descendant of King Saul) (r:13.9.43/13.2.46) (q:draft)
Mozah = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Mozah) (d:town in the territory of Benjamin) (r:6.18.26)
mu = (t:v) (w:see) (d:perceive with the eyes) (e:khuapi ~-in kap a/Thuman mite in ~-in, lau ding uh a | the righteous will see and fear/thudang khat ka ~ leuleu hi | I saw yet another thing/suangmanphate ~ uh hi | they see precious stones) (r:1.1.4/42.19.41/19.52.6/21.4.7/18.28.10)
mu = (t:v) (w:detect) (d:notice or discover something)
mu = (t:v) (w:saw/found/find) (d:come upon someone or something that was looked for or lost; maipha mu is to find favor) (e:amah in tua nu ~ zo lo hi/Noah in Topa’ maipha ~ hi | Noah found favor with the Lord/suang kilikkhia a, om ~ uh a | they found the stone rolled away/Amah ka ~ kei hi | I did not find her) (r:1.38.20/1.38.22/1.6.8/42.24.2) as in lost object discovered.
mu-meika = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:kite/red kite) (d:a bird of prey in the lists of unclean birds, also written mumeika) (e:mupi, ~, amau namciat) (s:mumeika) (r:5.14.13/3.11.14) (q:draft)
mua = (t:see) <mua-mua>
mua-mua = (t:adv) (w:teeming/swarming) (d:descriptive word for countless creatures moving about together; in the verse with na, the place where they teem) (e:sim zawh loh-a a tam, a vak ~-na | where creatures beyond number swarm about) (s:muamua) (r:19.104.25) (q:draft, low confidence)
muaimuai = (t:adv) (w:in a mass/in swarms/in great numbers) (d:placed after a verb of movement, of a great crowd or swarm moving together) (e:mihonpi hong pai ~ a muh ciangin/mihonte a kikhin ~ a mu uh hi | they saw the crowd moving off in a mass/kauphe honpi hong leeng ~ hi | a great swarm of locusts comes flying in a mass) (s:muamua) (r:43.6.5/29.2.2/9.14.16) (q:draft)
muak = (t:v) (w:come to meet/seek out/welcome) (d:go out to meet or receive someone) (e:ka thudot mite in hong ~ uh a) (r:27.4.36) (q:draft)
mual = (t:n) (w:mountain/hill) (d:a mountain or hill; mual tung is on the mountain, mual sang a high mountain and mual neu a small hill) (e:~ siangtho tungah ama phuhsa khuapi/Judah gamah a omte in ~ tungah tai ta hen | let those in Judea flee to the mountains/alian ~ sangte khempeuh | all the great high mountains/meii in ~ tuam hi | the cloud covered the mountain) (a:guam/kuam) (r:19.87.1/23.2.14/40.24.16/2.24.15) (q:draft)
Mual = (t:n) (w:Mount/Mountain) (d:mual, mountain, written with a capital after the name of a mountain, as in Sinai Mual, Mount Sinai) (e:Zeisu Oliv ~ ah a pai hi/Topa in Sinai ~ tungah Moses kiangah | the Lord to Moses on Mount Sinai/Edom gamgi Hor ~ ah | at Mount Hor on the border of Edom/ama it, Zion ~ | Mount Zion, which he loved) (a:Kuam) (b:mual) (r:43.8.1/2.19.20/3.25.1/4.20.23/19.78.68) (q:draft)
muala = (t:n) (w:on the mountain/of the mountain) (d:mual mountain with the ending a, at or on: Lebanon muala om, that are on Mount Lebanon) (e:Lebanon ~ om taamtak singte/Bashan le Karmel ~ singtehte pulhmang khinta hi | the leaves on the hills of Bashan and Carmel have fallen) (s:mualah) (b:mual) (r:19.104.16/23.33.9) (q:draft)
Muala = (t:n) (w:Mount/mountain) (d:Mual with a, of or on the Mount; Oliv Muala lam is the road on the Mount of Olives) (e:Oliv ~ lam suktuah a kipatna panin) (b:Mual) (r:42.19.37) (q:draft)
mualah = (t:n) (w:on the mountain/to the mountain) (d:mual mountain or hill with the place marker ah, on, at or to the mountain) (e:Oliv kici ~ a om Bethfage khua/~ kahto-in a tu hi | he went up on the mountain and sat down/Oliv kici ~ a giak hi | he spent the night on the hill called Olives/Zeisu in a vaikhakna ~ a pai uh hi | they went to the mountain where Jesus had told them to go) (s:muala) (b:mual) (r:42.19.29/40.15.29/42.21.37/40.28.16) (q:draft)
Mualah = (t:n) (w:to the Mount/at the Mount) (d:Mual Mount with the place marker ah, in Oliv Mualah, to or at the Mount of Olives) (e:Oliv ~ a paikhia uh hi/Oliv ~ a om Bethfage khua leh Bethani khua-ah | to Bethphage and Bethany at the Mount of Olives) (b:Mual) (r:40.26.30/41.11.1) (q:draft)
mualbo = (t:n) (w:hill/hilltop/knoll) (d:a hill or rise of ground, used after the name of the hill, as Ofel mualbo, the hill of Ophel) (e:Ofel ~-ah teeng uh a/Areopagas ~-ah paipih uh a | they brought him to the hill of the Areopagus/Ofel ~ kulh ciang | as far as the wall of the hill of Ophel) (s:mualno/mualneu) (r:16.11.21/16.3.27/44.17.19) (q:draft)
mualciang = (t:n) (w:pass/mountain pass) (d:the place where a line of hills is crossed, from mual hill) (e:Amaute in ~ kantanin Geba khua-ah) (s:ciangka) (r:23.10.29) (q:draft)
mualdawn = (t:n) (w:hilltop/mountain top/high place) (d:mual hill with dawn top; also the high places where offerings were made) (e:tua hunin Gibeon ~ ah om lai hi/Karmel ~ dum dide teng kausan ta hi | the green top of Carmel withers/David in ~ a khen’ khit tawmvei ciangin | when David had gone a little beyond the summit/~ a, biak piaknate kila khia lo hi | the high places of offering were not removed) (s:mualvum) (r:13.21.29/2.34.2/30.1.2/10.16.1/14.15.17) (q:draft)
mualdawnzang = (t:n) (w:mountaintop/hilltop) (d:mual hill with dawn top and zang level ground: the open top of a hill) (e:mual sang tung teng, ~ teng) (s:mualdawn) (r:26.6.13) (q:draft)
mualh = (t:v) (w:fade/grow dim) (d:of a mark, stain or colour: become faint, fade) (e:khit ciangin a natna a ~ leh) (r:3.13.56) (q:draft)
mualin = (t:adj) (w:faded/dim) (d:said of a spot on the skin that has grown faint, in mualin om be faded; not the word mual mountain) (e:~ a om leh/a vun sung lawh loin ~ a om leh | if it has not spread in the skin but has faded) (r:3.13.21/3.13.28) (q:draft, low confidence)
mualkhin = (t:v) (w:fade away/pass away/vanish) (d:mual disappear from sight with khin already; said of the fading brightness of the face of Moses) (e:a taang mahmah pen ~ tei napi-in) (r:47.3.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
Mualkolh = (t:n) (w:bare hilltop/bare hill) (d:mual hill with kolh, apparently bare) (e:~ tungah lim khat lakto unla) (s:mualpawn) (r:23.13.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
mualkuam = (t:n) (w:valley/ravine) (d:low ground between hills, from mual, hill, and kuam, valley; also used in the names of valleys) (e:~ leh zangleite a kisia ding uh hi/~ sunga a om unok pak | a lily that grows in the valley/Ga-ash ~ mi Hurai | Hurai from the ravines of Gaash/Kithahna ~ a kici zaw ding hi | it will be called the Valley of Slaughter instead) (s:guam/kuam) (a:mual) (r:24.48.8/24.7.31/22.2.1/13.11.32/24.7.32) (q:draft)
Mualkuam = (t:n) (w:valley) (d:mualkuam, a valley between hills, written with a capital in the names of valleys such as Ben-Hinnom Mualkuam, the Valley of Ben Hinnom, and at the start of a sentence) (e:Kithahna ~ a kici zaw ding hi/Ben-Hinnom ~ ahi zongin | or the Valley of Ben Hinnom/~ thuk khempeuh kivuk dim ding a | every deep valley will be filled in/~ zang-a na lampi totte en dih in | look at the way you went in the valley) (s:Kuam) (b:mualkuam) (r:24.19.6/24.32.35/42.3.5/24.2.23) (q:draft)
Mualkuamah = (t:n) (w:to the Valley/in the Valley) (d:Mualkuam, valley, with the place marker ah: to or in the Valley, as in Ben-Hinnom Mualkuamah, to the Valley of Ben Hinnom) (e:Ben-Hinnom ~ pai-in) (s:Kuamah) (b:Mualkuam) (r:24.19.2) (q:draft)
mualleguamte = (t:n) (w:hills and valleys) (d:mual, hill, le, and, guam, valley, with the plural te: the hills and valleys, the shape of the land that daylight makes stand out) (e:Khuavak in ~ kilangkhia sak a) (r:18.38.14) (q:draft)
mualliante = (t:n) (w:mountains/great mountains) (d:mual, hill, with lian, great, and the plural te: the great mountains, often set beside mualneute, the hills) (e:~ tuutal bangin diang uh a/~ in khuainun bangin tui suak uh hi | the mountains melt like wax/Ama mai-ah ~ liing a | the mountains quake before him/meikuang in ~ a kuan’sak mah bangin | as a flame sets the mountains ablaze) (s:mualsangte) (a:mualneute) (r:19.114.4/19.83.14/19.97.5/34.1.5) (q:draft)
mualmang = (t:v) (w:fade away/lose luster/grow dull) (d:mual, fade, with mang, away: lose its brightness altogether, said of something that once shone) (e:a tee daldalte a ~ khin zo hi) (s:mualkhin) (r:25.4.1) (q:draft)
mualmual = (t:adv) (w:indistinctly/in a mutter) (d:doubled word after pau speak: speaking in a low unclear voice, muttering) (e:a pau ~ vankah theite leh aisan theite) (r:23.8.19) (q:draft)
mualneu = (t:n) (w:hill/small hill) (d:mual, hill, with neu, small: a hill as against a great mountain) (e:a sang ~ khempeuh) (s:mualno) (a:mualpi/mualsang) (r:23.2.14) (q:draft)
mualneute = (t:n) (w:hills/small hills) (d:mualneu, hill, with the plural te: the lower hills, often set beside mualliante, the great mountains) (e:~ tuuno bangin a diang uh hi/~ kileh kawikawi uh hi | the hills were swaying/Mualliante leh ~ khempeuh | mountains and all hills/~ a kibawl ma pekin ka om khin hi | long before the hills were made I already was) (a:mualliante/mualsangte) (b:mualneu) (r:19.114.4/24.4.24/19.148.9/20.8.25) (q:draft)
Mualneute = (t:n) (w:hills/small hills) (d:mualneute, the hills, written with a capital at the start of a clause) (e:~ tuisuak hi) (a:mualliante) (b:mualneute) (r:34.1.5) (q:draft)
mualno = (t:n) (w:hill/small hill) (d:mual, hill, with no, small: a small hill; Areopagas mualno is the hill of the Areopagus in Athens, Mars Hill) (e:Areopagas ~ tungah a paipih khit uh ciangin/Paul in Areopagas ~ tungah ding-in | Paul, standing on the hill of the Areopagus) (s:mualneu) (a:mualpi) (b:mual) (r:44.17.19/44.17.22) (q:draft)
mualpang = (t:n) (w:hillside/mountainside/slope/ridge) (d:the side or slope of a hill or mountain, also a ridge of land; mualpang khatah is on one side of the mountain) (e:A ~ khatah Saul pai a/~ to-ah vok honpi khat gamta-in a om hi | a large herd of pigs was feeding on the hillside/Pisgah ~ nuai-a Ci Tuipi | the Salt Sea below the slopes of Pisgah/Amor mite’ khut tung panin ka lak ~ khat | one ridge that I took from the hand of the Amorites) (r:9.23.26/5.3.17/42.8.32/1.48.22) (q:draft)
mualpangah = (t:n) (w:on the hillside/at the hillside) (d:mualpang hillside with the place marker ah) (e:tua nai-a om ~ vok hon tampi/ama galkhat ~ Shimei pai a | Shimei went along the hillside opposite him/David’ suante’ han paina ~ amah vui uh hi | they buried him on the hill where the tombs of David’s descendants are) (b:mualpang) (r:41.5.11/10.16.13/14.32.33) (q:draft)
mualpawn = (t:n) (w:bare hill/barren height) (d:mual, hill, with pawn, bare: a hill or height with no trees on it) (e:a sang ~ khatah amah pai hi/~ a sang munte khempeuh ah | on all the high bare hills) (r:4.23.3/23.49.9) (q:draft)
mualpi = (t:n) (w:great mountain/mountain) (d:mual, mountain, with pi, great: a great mountain) (e:~ banga lian a/mei in a kat ~ bang na khat | something like a great mountain burning with fire/kulh ~ bukna-a a zang ding mipa | the man whose refuge will be the mountain fortress) (s:mualsang) (a:mualneu/mualno) (b:mual) (r:24.51.25/66.8.8/23.33.16) (q:draft)
mualsang = (t:n) (w:high mountain/height/high hill) (d:mual, mountain, with sang, high: a high mountain or hill, a height) (e:~ leh mual neute tung khempeuh ah/~ tungah, gam daihna munah paipih a | he led them up a high mountain, to a quiet place/Sehnel gam ~ panin a susia dingte hong pai | destroyers come from the heights of the desert/~ tung khempeuh leh singniim nuai khempeuh ah | on every high hill and under every spreading tree) (s:mualpi) (a:mualneu) (r:23.30.25/40.17.1/24.12.12/12.17.10) (q:draft)
mualsangte = (t:n) (w:high hills/heights/high mountains) (d:plural of mualsang: the high hills or heights, often as places where offerings were made) (e:~ in sathak’ ading hi a/na ~ tungah kithat | slain on your heights/~ tung leh mualneute tung leh singniim nuai | on the high mountains, on the hills and under spreading trees/~ dawna biakna munte-ah biakna pia uh a | they sacrifice at the shrines on the mountaintops) (s:mualliante) (a:mualneute) (b:mualsang) (r:19.104.18/24.17.2/10.1.19/5.12.2/28.4.13) (q:draft)
mualsuang = (t:n) (w:memorial stone/pillar/tombstone) (d:a stone set up in memory of someone, as over a grave; suang is stone) (e:ama han tungah ~ khat a phut hi/Rachel’ han ~ khuam ahi hi | it is the pillar of Rachel’s tomb) (r:1.35.20) (q:draft)
mualsuangte = (t:n) (w:memorial stones/pillars/monuments) (d:plural of mualsuang: the monuments of the dead, and the sacred pillars of Egypt) (e:Heliopolis khua-a ~ a susia ding a/a sisate’ ~ hoihtakin na zem uh a | you decorate the monuments of the dead) (b:mualsuang) (r:24.43.13/40.23.29) (q:draft)
mualtan = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:viper/poisonous snake) (d:a poisonous snake; in the verses always in the address mualtan’ suante, brood of vipers) (e:No ~’ suante aw/~’ suante aw, no gilo na hih uh ciangin | you brood of vipers, since you are evil) (r:40.12.34/40.3.7) (q:draft)
mualte = (t:n) (w:mountains/hills) (d:plural of mual: mountains or hills) (e:~ ka et leh kiliing damdam uh a/nangma thahatna tawh ~ a bawl | who formed the mountains by your power/~ kantanin kei hong zuan hi | he comes to me bounding over the hills/Topa mai-ah ~ kiliing hi | the mountains quaked before the Lord) (s:mualtungte) (a:guamte/kuamte) (b:mual) (r:24.4.24/19.65.6/22.2.8/7.5.5) (q:draft)
mualteng = (t:n) (w:all the mountains/all the hills) (d:mual, hill, with teng, all: all the hills, paired with guamteng, all the valleys) (e:~ guamteng na sisan tawh kidim ding hi/~ guamteng, na sa ka dimsak ding hi | I will fill all the hills and valleys with your flesh) (b:mual) (r:26.32.6/26.32.5) (q:draft)
Mualteng = (t:name) (w:Mualteng)
mualtung = (t:n) (w:hill/mountain/hill country) (d:the top of a hill or the high land, from mual, hill, and tung, top; mualtung gam is hill country) (e:Efraim ~ gam mi Mikah a kici/Gamsate a omna ~ panin | from the hills where the wild animals are/Efraim ~ gam sungah Benhur | Ben-Hur in the hill country of Ephraim/Tua ciangin ~ gamah, Shamir, Jattir, Sokoh | and in the hill country: Shamir, Jattir, Sokoh) (s:mual) (a:kuam/zanglei) (r:7.17.1/18.24.8/18.40.20/11.4.8/6.15.48) (q:draft)
Mualtung = (t:n) (w:Mount/hill country/mountains) (d:mualtung written with a capital, in a place name such as Seir Mualtung, Mount Seir, or at the start of a sentence) (e:Seir ~ gam khempeuh gamkhing/Seir ~ gam aw, kei, nangma lang ka hi hi | Mount Seir, I am against you/~ pan-a hong zu guahtui | the rain that falls from the mountains/~ tawnin hong tai a | he comes running over the mountains/~ khempeuh si luanghawm tawh ka kidimsak ding a | I will fill all the mountains with corpses) (b:mualtung) (r:26.35.7/26.35.3/18.24.8/22.2.8/26.35.8) (q:draft)
mualtunga = (t:adv) (w:on the hill/on the hilltop) (d:mualtung with the place marker a: located on a hill; mualtunga biaknate are the high places of worship) (e:~ om khuapite khat zong/tua kuam ~ om Zereth-shahar | Zereth Shahar on the hill in the valley/~ biaknate kikoih khia lo hi | the high places were not removed/~ dial tawh kibangin | like a banner on a hill) (b:mualtung) (r:6.11.13/12.15.35/6.13.19/23.30.17) (q:draft)
mualtungah = (t:adv) (w:on the mountain/in the hill country/to the hills) (d:mualtung, hill or mountain, with the place marker ah: on or to the mountain, in the hill country) (e:Jakob in ~ biak piakna pia-in/~ Moses paito a, meii in mual a tuam hi | Moses went up the mountain and the cloud covered it/Judea gam a om mite, ~ tai hen la | let those who are in Judea flee to the mountains/thungen dingin ~ a kahto hi | he went up the mountain to pray) (b:mualtung) (r:1.31.54/40.24.16/2.24.15/41.6.46) (q:draft)
mualtungte = (t:n) (w:mountains/hills) (d:mualtung with the plural te: the mountains or hills of a land, as in Israel mualtungte, the mountains of Israel) (e:mihonpi lungdam bangin ~ ah gamlumna/Israel ~ gamkhing suak ding ahih manin | because the mountains of Israel will become desolate/Israel ~, lui geite, le mite’ tenna mun khempeuhah | on the mountains of Israel, by the streams and in all the settlements/~ le mual sang tung khempeuhah vakmang uh hi | they wandered over all the mountains and every high hill) (s:mualte) (b:mualtung) (r:23.13.4/26.35.12/26.33.28/26.34.13/26.34.6) (q:draft)
mualvum = (t:n) (w:mountain top/summit/peak) (d:the top of a mountain, its summit) (e:Lebanon ~ bangin ahi zongin na hoih hi/~ dawn-ah a kangtum thei meikuang | a consuming fire on top of the mountain) (s:mualdawn) (r:24.22.6/2.24.17) (q:draft)
mualzang = (t:n) (w:plateau/tableland) (d:level high ground, from mual, hill, and zang, flat: a plateau) (e:~ tunga om a khuapite khempeuh/Dibon ciang dong Medeba ~ khempeuh | the whole plateau of Medeba as far as Dibon/~ khuapite khempeuh leh Gilead khempeuh | all the towns of the plateau and all Gilead/Reuben mite adingin ~ gamlakah Bezer khua | for the Reubenites, Bezer in the wilderness plateau) (r:6.13.17/6.13.9/5.3.10/5.4.43) (q:draft)
muam = (t:v) (w:hold in the mouth/keep in the mouth) (d:keep something in the mouth without swallowing it; doubled as muam muam, go on holding it there) (e:amah in ~ muam nuamin siakhia nuam lo a) (r:18.20.13) (q:draft)
muammuam = (t:v) (w:keep in the mouth/savour) (d:muam hold in the mouth, doubled: go on holding and tasting something) (e:amah in ~ nuamin siakhia nuam lo a) (r:18.20.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
muamua = (t:adv) (w:in great numbers/in swarms/teeming) (d:follows a verb to picture many people or creatures moving or gathered together) (e:minamte khempeuh pai ~ ding uh a/simzawh lohin a tam, a vak ~-na | countless, moving about in swarms/Jerusalem-a tuu honpi om ~ bangin | like the great flocks of sheep in Jerusalem) (s:muaimuai/mua-mua) (r:23.2.2/26.36.38/19.104.25) (q:draft)
muan = (t:v) (w:trust/rely on/put hope in) (d:second stem of muang, trust, used before endings such as nading; muan’na is trust or confidence, and muan’huai is trustworthy) (e:Mi i ~’ sangin Topa belh/Uliante i ~’ sangin Topa belh ding hoihzaw hi | it is better to take refuge in the Lord than to trust in princes/misite a thosak Pasian ~ nadingin | so that we might trust in God who raises the dead/Leitung hauhna ~’ leh suan’in ka nei ngei kei | I have never made worldly wealth my trust) (a:muanlah) (r:19.118.8/19.71.5/19.118.9/47.1.9/18.31.24) (q:draft)
muan'huaisak = (t:v) (w:make firm/make secure/make trustworthy) (d:muan’huai trustworthy with the causative sak) (e:ka khe sikna ~ hi) (s:muanhuaisak) (r:19.40.2) (q:draft)
muang = (t:v) (w:trust/rely on/hope in) (d:put one’s trust or hope in God, a person or a thing; the second stem is muan) (e:nangmah ka hong ~ hi/Topa ~ un | trust in the Lord/Judah mi kicihna ngah a, Thukham ~ a | you are called a Jew and rely on the law/Amah a ~ khempeuh adingin Topa in a hoih hi | the Lord is good to all who trust in him/ka pumpi uh ~ loin | not relying on ourselves) (s:um) (a:muanglah) (r:19.56.3/45.2.17/19.4.5/25.3.25/47.1.9) (q:draft)
muanga = (t:adj) (w:secure/at ease/unafraid) (d:muang with the linking a; lung muanga, with the heart at rest) (e:a note lung ~ a omna mun) (s:lungmuang) (b:muang) (r:34.2.11) (q:draft)
muangin = (t:v) (w:trusting/trusting in/relying on) (d:muang, trust, with the linking ending in: trusting, and so; lung muangin is with a secure heart) (e:Mite in a hauhna uh ~/Topa ~, Topa a beel mi | the one who trusts in the Lord and takes refuge in him/Nang hong ~ na nai-ah hong teeng na vengpa | your neighbor who lives near you trusting you/nangma thu ~ ka lamen hi | trusting in your word, I hope/lung ~ ka om hi | I rest secure) (b:muang) (r:19.49.6/24.17.7/20.3.29/19.119.81/19.16.9) (q:draft)
muangkha = (t:v) (w:trust/depend on/rely on) (d:muang trust with kha, which marks an action one falls into: come to put trust in, often wrongly) (e:na galkap tamna uh ~ na hih manun/na Topa uh ~ kei un | do not be led to trust in your Lord) (r:28.10.13/23.36.15) (q:draft)
muanglah = (t:v) (w:doubt/lack trust) (d:muang trust with lah, be short of: be unsure, waver) (e:A ~ mite pen huih nunna lam) (s:muanlah) (a:muang) (r:59.1.6) (q:draft)
muangngam = (t:v) (w:trust confidently/dare to trust) (d:muang trust with ngam dare) (e:a hong ciam thu ~ ihih manin) (r:58.10.23) (q:draft)
muangpa = (t:n) (w:one who trusts/he who trusts) (d:muang trust, with pa marking a man: the man who trusts) (e:a ~ in mi lungdam ahi hi) (b:muang) (r:19.146.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
muangsak = (t:v) (w:cause to trust/let trust) (d:muang trust with sak cause: make or let someone rely on; said of widows who may depend on God) (e:numeite uh zong kei hong ~ un) (b:muang) (r:24.49.11) (q:draft)
muangte = (t:n) (w:those who trust) (d:muang with plural te: people who trust or hope in someone) (e:Topa a ~ ahih leh itna kip in/ama itna kip a ~ tungah lungkim hi | he delights in those who hope in his unfailing love/amaute a ~ khempeuh | all who trust in them/nangmah hong ~ keima hangin zahhuaisak kei in | may those who hope in you not be disgraced because of me) (b:muang) (r:19.32.10/19.115.8/19.147.11/19.69.6) (q:draft)
muangzo = (t:v) (w:be able to trust) (d:muang trust, with zo be able; in the verse negated: not able to trust) (e:nasemte mahmah ~ loin) (s:muantheih) (b:muang) (r:18.4.18) (q:draft)
muanhuai = (t:adj) (w:fortified/secure/strong) (d:safe to rely on, said of a place; mun muanhuai is a stronghold and khuapi muanhuai a fortified city) (e:mun ~ sungah David om hi/a ~ kulhte khempeuh | every fortified wall/tausang ~ tawh kibang a | it is like a fortified tower/David kiang mun ~ ah hong pai uh hi | they came to David at the stronghold) (r:13.11.16/23.2.15/20.18.10/13.12.16) (q:draft)
muanhuai = (t:adj) (w:trustworthy/reliable) (d:said of a person or thing that can be trusted or relied on, from muan, trust, and huai, worthy of) (e:a ~ mi leh sumgolh a mudah mi/a ~ mite tung bekah thusim kigen ngam hi | secrets can be told only to trustworthy people/Eite i ~ loh hangin | though we are not faithful) (s:muantaak/citak) (r:2.18.21/20.11.13/55.2.13) (q:draft)
muanhuaina = (t:n) (w:safety/security/place of safety) (d:muanhuai, secure, with the noun suffix na: the state or place of being safe; mun muanhuaina is a fortress) (e:a ~ munah amaute paipih/mun ~ sungah David teeng hi | David lived in the fortress/Assiria gam mun ~ sunga om mite | the people in the fortresses of Assyria) (s:bitna) (b:muanhuai) (r:19.78.53/13.11.7/30.3.9) (q:draft)
muanhuaina = (t:n) (w:faithfulness/trustworthiness) (d:muanhuai, trustworthy, with the noun suffix na: the quality of being faithful and reliable) (e:Ama ~ a kip den hi) (s:cihtakna) (b:muanhuai) (r:55.2.13) (q:draft)
muanhuainate = (t:n) (w:fortified places/strongholds) (d:muanhuai secure, with the noun suffix na and plural te) (e:amau’ mun ~ mei tawh na hal ding a) (b:muanhuaina) (r:12.8.12) (q:draft)
muanhuainna = (t:n) (w:stronghold/fortress) (d:secure place; apparently a spelling of muanhuaina, which stands earlier in the same verse) (e:Izipt gam mun ~ sunga om mite) (r:30.3.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
muanhuaipen = (t:adj) (w:most secure/strongest) (d:muanhuai secure, with the superlative pen: the most strongly fortified) (e:khuapi ~ ahi Pelusium khuapi) (b:muanhuai) (r:26.30.15) (q:draft)
muanhuaisak = (t:v) (w:make secure/make firm) (d:muanhuai secure, with the causative sak) (e:ka khesikna mun a ~ hi) (s:muan'huaisak) (b:muanhuai) (r:19.40.2) (q:draft)
muanhuaite = (t:adj) (w:fortified/strong/secure) (d:plural of muanhuai, placed after the noun it describes; khuapi muanhuaite are fortified cities, kulh muanhuaite strongholds) (e:amau’ khuapi ~ pen/Moab mite’ kulh ~ suksiat sakin | bringing down the fortified walls of Moab/khuapi ~ va beel ni | let us flee to the fortified cities/leihawmte leh mun ~ bawl uh hi | they made caves and strongholds) (b:muanhuai) (r:23.17.9/30.5.9/23.25.12/24.8.14/7.6.2) (q:draft)
muanhuaite = (t:adj) (w:trustworthy/reliable) (d:plural of muanhuai said of people who can be relied on, here of allies) (e:Lot suan-le-khakte’ pawl ~ ahi uh hi) (b:muanhuai) (r:19.83.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
muanin = (t:v) (w:trust/depend on/rely on) (d:muan, trust, with the ending in, used in muanin nei, have as one’s trust, put one’s trust in) (e:Mihingte ~ nei nawn kei un/Tua hileh Topa ~ na nei ding uh a | so that your trust may be in the Lord/mihing ~ nei loin Pasian bek muang ding uh hi | they will not rely on man but trust in God alone/Pasian ~ na nei tawntung ding a | you will always have God as your trust) (b:muan) (r:23.2.22/33.5.7/20.22.19/18.22.26) (q:draft)
muanlah = (t:v) (w:doubt/waver/distrust) (d:be unable to trust, be in doubt, from muan trust) (e:Pasian’ thuciamna ~ dingin ngaihsun lo a/bang ci-a hong tuaci ~ na hi hiam | why did you doubt like this) (s:muanglah) (a:muang/muan) (r:45.4.20/40.14.31) (q:draft)
muanlesuan = (t:n) (w:mainstay/those relied on) (d:muan trust, le and, suan rely: the ones a people depends on; in the verse the strong young men of Israel) (e:Israel-te’ ~ teng a vatlum hi) (r:19.78.31) (q:draft, low confidence)
muanmuan = (t:v) (w:trust in/rely on) (d:muan trust doubled, used before a noun: muanmuan kulhpi is the stronghold that is trusted in) (e:amau’ ~ kulhpi nangawn susia zo hi) (r:20.21.22) (q:draft)
muanna = (t:n) (w:trust/confidence/reliance) (d:muan, trust, with the noun suffix na: trust in or reliance on someone or something, confidence) (e:Topa ~ in hong lungmuangsak hi/omna leh ~ in nomau’ thahatna hi ding hi | quietness and trust will be your strength/amah i ~ hangin kimuang takin | through our trust in him, with confidence/lungsim hanna le ~ tawh i omsuak nakleh | if we continue in courage and confidence) (b:muan) (r:20.29.25/49.3.12/23.30.15/58.3.6) (q:draft)
muanpa = (t:n) (w:the one trusted) (d:muan trust, with pa marking a man: the man in whom someone trusts) (e:na ~ uh Moses ahi hi) (b:muan) (r:43.5.45) (q:draft)
muanpi = (t:n) (w:trust/reliance/security) (d:muan trust, with pi: the one greatly relied on) (e:keima ~ na hi a) (b:muan) (r:19.16.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
muansuam = (t:v) (w:ambush/waylay) (d:attack a person who suspects nothing) (e:Mi ommuang khat va ~ ni) (r:20.1.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
muantaak = (t:adj) (w:trustworthy/reliable) (d:worthy of trust, muan trust with taak worthy) (e:a thupiaknate ~ mahmah hi/Hih thute thumanin ~ ahih manin lai-ah gelh in | write this down, for these words are true and trustworthy/Hih thute ~ a, thuman ahi hi | these words are trustworthy and true/Topa’ hehpihna tawh a ~ ahi keima ngaihsutna | my judgment as one who by the Lord’s mercy is trustworthy) (s:muanhuai/citak) (r:19.111.7/66.22.6/66.21.5/46.7.25) (q:draft)
muante = (t:n) (w:trusted ones/trusted friends) (d:muan trust with plural te, the people one relies on; lawm muante is trusted friends) (e:Na lawm ~ in nang hong khem uh a/mi’ ~ a pau thei loin bawl a | he silences those whom people trust) (b:muan) (r:24.38.22/18.12.20) (q:draft)
muantheih = (t:v) (w:be able to trust/can rely on) (d:muan trust with theih can; muantheih ding is something or someone that can be trusted) (e:Pasian ka ~ nadingun/Note pen ~ ding na hihlohna uh | that you are not to be trusted/tua bang nate ~ ding a nei pa | one who has such things to rely on) (s:muangzo) (b:muan) (r:47.1.9/23.48.8/50.3.4) (q:draft)
muap = (t:v) (w:breathe into/blow) (d:said of breath given to an image) (e:a hu a ~ ciangin hong pauthei a) (r:66.13.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
muat = (t:v) (w:rot/decay/perish) (d:rot or decay, of flesh, wood or goods; muat thei is perishable, and muat theih lohna and muat lohna are imperishability) (e:~ nading a piang ding hi/Na sum na paaite uh ~ gawpin a om hi | your wealth has rotted away/a ~ lo ding sing teel hi | he chooses wood that will not rot/a nung ciangin a ~ nawn kei ding hi | afterwards he will never decay) (s:ngot) (r:51.2.22/46.15.53/59.5.2/23.40.20/44.13.34) (q:draft)
muatcip = (t:v) (w:rot/rot away) (d:muat rot with cip, firmly, completely: lie and rot where it is) (e:a luanghawm uh leilakah ~ ding hi) (b:muat) (r:36.1.17) (q:draft)
muatgawp = (t:v) (w:rot away/decay completely) (d:muat rot with gawp, done to the point of ruin) (e:amaute’ zung pen ~ ding a/lei lakah a luang uh a ~ Midian mite | the Midianites whose bodies rotted on the ground) (s:muatmang) (b:muat) (r:23.5.24/19.83.9) (q:draft)
muatin = (t:v) (w:rot/rotting) (d:muat rot with the linking ending in, and) (e:a mittangte uh ~, a kam sung uhah) (b:muat) (r:38.14.12) (q:draft)
muatlam = (t:n) (w:decay/wasting away) (d:muat rot, with lam direction: the way of decay) (e:damdamin ~ ding a manawh ahi zongin) (r:47.4.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
muatmang = (t:v) (w:rot away/decay completely/dissolve) (d:muat rot with mang away, lost) (e:Vantunga a om khempeuh ~ ding a/a sa uh ~ ding a | their flesh will rot away) (s:muatgawp) (r:23.34.4/38.14.12) (q:draft)
muatna = (t:n) (w:decay/corruption/rot) (d:muat, rot, with the noun suffix na: the rotting of a body, also ruin as the result of sin; muatna thuak is see decay) (e:~ a thuak kei hi/kivui khawm a, ~ a thuak hi | he was buried and saw decay/Na Misiangtho zong ~ na thuaksak kei ding hi | you will not let your Holy One see decay/ama ci-le-sa hangah ~ a at ding hi | from his flesh he will reap destruction) (b:muat) (r:44.13.37/48.6.8/44.13.36/44.2.27) (q:draft)
muatsa = (t:adj) (w:rotten/decayed) (d:muat rot, with sa already done) (e:sing ~ bang lel hi) (b:muat) (r:18.41.27) (q:draft)
muatsak = (t:v) (w:rot/cause to rot/make decay) (d:muat rot with the causative sak) (e:a khut leh a khete ~ ta hi/hazatna in guh ~ natna ahi hi | envy is a disease that rots the bones) (b:muat) (r:18.18.13/20.14.30) (q:draft)
muatsakmang = (t:v) (w:rot away/eat away) (d:muat rot, with causative sak and mang away: cause to rot away entirely) (e:a khete ~ khinta hi) (r:18.18.13) (q:draft)
muatthei = (t:adj) (w:perishable/corruptible) (d:muat rot with thei can: able to decay) (e:A ~ pumpi pen a muat thei lo) (b:muat) (r:46.15.53/46.15.54) (q:draft)
muattheih = (t:v) (w:be subject to decay/be perishable) (d:muat rot, with theih can) (e:nikhat ni ciangin ~ nading thu panin) (b:muat) (r:45.8.21) (q:draft)
muattumta = (t:v) (w:have rotted away) (d:muat rot, with tum completely and ta marking a completed change) (e:Na neihsate uh ~ a) (r:59.5.2) (q:draft)
mudah = (t:v) (w:hate/detest/abhor) (d:hate or detest a person or a thing; the form muhdah is used before certain endings) (e:Esau ka ~ hi/Midikte in migilote ~ a | the righteous detest the wicked/Topa in zuau gen mite ~ a | the Lord detests those who tell lies/siatna bawl mihonte ka ~ a | I abhor the assembly of evildoers/mi khempeuh in note hong ~ ding uh hi | everyone will hate you) (s:hua/kih) (a:it) (r:45.9.13/43.15.23/20.29.27/20.12.22/19.26.5/42.21.17) (q:draft)
mudahhuai = (t:adj) (w:detestable/hateful) (d:mudah hate, with huai worthy of) (e:a ~ in a gamtatna thu) (s:muhdahhuai/kihhuai) (a:ithuai) (r:26.16.2) (q:draft)
mudahin = (t:v) (w:hate/dislike/detest) (d:mudah with the linking suffix in, hating and then) (e:Gitlohna ~ gamtat hoih beel un/Na biakna pawite uh ~ ka deih kei a | I hate and reject your religious festivals/a vengpa ~, amah pang sim a | hating his neighbor, he lies in wait for him/amah a luppih khit ciangin amah ~ | after sleeping with her he dislikes her) (b:mudah) (r:45.12.9/5.22.13/30.5.21/5.19.11) (q:draft)
mudahpa = (t:n) (w:one who hates/enemy) (d:mudah hate, with pa marking a man: the man who hates) (e:a hong ~’ la a van tawh a puk | the donkey of one who hates you fallen under its load) (s:galpa) (a:itpa) (b:mudah) (r:2.23.5) (q:draft)
mudahsak = (t:v) (w:cause to hate/turn against) (d:mudah hate, with the causative sak) (e:thu um mite a ~ uh hi) (b:mudah) (r:44.14.2) (q:draft)
mudahte = (t:n) (w:haters/foes/enemies) (d:mudah, hate, with the plural te: those who hate someone or something, foes) (e:Zion a ~ khempeuh maizumin/kei hong ~ ka susia hi | I destroyed those who hate me/thuman ~ kidantat ding hi | the foes of the righteous will be condemned/amah a ~ ama mai-ah tai uh hen | may those who hate him flee before him) (s:galte) (a:itte/lawmte) (b:mudah) (r:19.129.5/19.18.40/19.34.21/19.68.1) (q:draft)
muh = (t:v) (w:see) (d:form of mu, see, used before endings such as ciangin, nading and matengin) (e:Moses in tua lamdang na a ~ ciangin/Mipilte in tua aksi a ~ uh ciangin | when the wise men saw the star/a lawng pen a ~ nadingin a kimkot a en hi | he looked around to see who had done it/Topa in hong en sukin a hong ~ matengin | until the Lord looks down and sees) (r:44.7.31/1.3.6/40.2.10/41.5.32/25.3.50)
muh = (t:adj) (w:found)
muhah = (t:adv) (w:in the sight of/before the eyes of) (d:muh see with the place marker ah; mit muhah is before one's eyes, in one's sight) (e:note’ mit ~ a hih bangin/Egypt gam sung note’ mit ~ | before your eyes in Egypt/Izipt gam sungah note mit ~ a hih bangin | as he did in Egypt before your eyes) (b:muh) (r:5.1.30/5.29.2/5.1.31) (q:draft)
muhdah = (t:v) (w:hate) (d:form of mudah used before endings such as leh, ma-in and cihtakin, and before a noun as in a muhdah khuampi the pillar he hates) (e:leitungmite in note hong ~ uh leh/Topa na Pasian un a ~ khuampi | a sacred pillar that the Lord your God hates/It hun om a, ~ hun om hi | there is a time to love and a time to hate/amaute in amah ~ semsem na-in nei uh hi | they hated him all the more) (s:huat) (a:it) (r:62.3.13/5.16.22/21.3.8/1.37.5) (q:draft)
muhdahhuai = (t:adj) (w:detestable/abominable/disgusting/vile) (d:deserving to be hated, from muhdah, hate, and -huai, worthy of) (e:a ~ milimte khempeuh a nilkhia ding/a ~ zaw na mu lai ding hi | you will see things even more detestable/a ~ a gitloh gamtatnate uh va en in | go and see the detestable and wicked things they do) (s:kihhuai/mudahhuai) (a:ithuai) (r:26.11.18/26.8.13/26.8.15/26.8.9) (q:draft)
muhdahhuaina = (t:n) (w:detestableness/abomination) (d:muhdahhuai detestable with the noun suffix na: the hatefulness of what was done) (e:a gamtatnasate uh a ~ phawkin) (b:muhdahhuai) (r:26.12.16) (q:draft)
muhdahin = (t:adj) (w:hated/odious/obnoxious) (d:muhdah hate with in, as: after a possessor, as one hated by him) (e:David’ ~ amau mah a kibawl tawmna uh) (b:muhdah) (r:13.19.6) (q:draft)
muhdahluat = (t:v) (w:hate greatly) (d:muhdah hate, with luat too much, the form of lua used before another word) (e:note in kei nong ~ manun) (r:28.9.7) (q:draft)
muhdahna = (t:n) (w:hatred/hate/malice) (d:muhdah, hate, with the noun suffix na: hatred or ill will; muhdahna tawh is out of hatred) (e:~ in sihna piangsak hi/itna’ adingin ~ tawh kei hong thuk uh hi | they repay me hatred for love/Amaute in ~ kamte pau-in kei hong gensia uh a | they speak against me with words of hatred/Amah in ~ tawh sunin | if he pushes someone out of hatred) (a:itna) (b:muhdah) (r:18.5.2/4.35.20/19.109.5/19.109.3) (q:draft)
muhdahte = (t:n) (w:hated ones) (d:muhdah hate, with plural te: those who are hated) (e:na it hitaleh na ~ hitaleh) (b:muhdah) (r:26.16.37) (q:draft)
muhin = (t:prep) (w:in the sight of/before the eyes of/in the presence of) (d:muh, sight, with the marker in, placed after the people who are watching) (e:mihonte khempeuh’ ~ Hor Mual tungah/a khialhna zahin ama ~ sat sak ding hi | he shall have him flogged in his presence as the crime deserves/mite’ ~ na khut sungah tawi in la | hold them in your hand before their eyes/Haman’ ~ ai kisaan a | the lot was cast in the presence of Haman) (b:muh) (r:4.20.27/24.19.10/5.25.2/26.37.20/17.3.7) (q:draft)
muhkha = (t:v) (w:notice/catch sight of) (d:muh see, with kha happen to) (e:ka lim ~ hi) (s:mukha) (r:20.7.7) (q:draft)
muhkhak = (t:v) (w:see/catch sight of) (d:the form of muhkha used before ciangin and ding; mu see with kha, which marks that the act happens to reach its object) (e:note hong ~ uh ciangin/Israel mite in a ~ ding uh a deih lohna-in | not wanting the Israelites to see it/Nang kong ~ kik ciangin | when I saw you again) (b:muhkha) (r:26.5.14/47.3.13/26.16.8) (q:draft)
muhkhiatnate = (t:n) (w:findings/discoveries) (d:muhkhiat find out, with the noun suffix na and plural te: what has been found out) (e:na ~ uh ka thei hi) (r:66.2.2) (q:draft)
muhkhit = (t:v) (w:have seen/after seeing) (d:muh, see, with khit, finish: having seen; used before phetin, as soon as, and ciang, when, for after someone has seen) (e:Paul in maang a ~ phetin/Kei na hong ~ ciang bekin | only when you have seen me) (r:44.16.10/43.20.29) (q:draft)
muhkik = (t:v) (w:see again/find again) (d:muh, see, with kik, again: see or find someone or something again; khua muhkik is regain sight) (e:note in amah na ~ uh ciangin/khua na ~ theih nading | so that you may see again/kuamah in nong ~ nawn loh ding uh | none of you will see me again/mittawte in khua a ~ theih nading | so that the blind may see again) (b:muh) (r:50.2.28/44.9.17/44.20.25/42.4.18) (q:draft)
muhmasakna = (t:n) (w:earlier seeing/former vision) (d:muh see, masak first, with the noun suffix na: what was seen before) (e:maang ka ~ sungate mah tawh kibang hi) (r:26.10.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
muhna = (t:n) (w:sight) (d:muh, see, with the noun suffix na: seeing, sight; after a possessive, muhna-ah means in the sight of, in the eyes of) (e:Topa ~ ah a sia gamta hi/Pasian’ ~-ah leitung sia a | the earth was corrupt in the sight of God/mit’ ~ tawh hi loin | not by sight/Topa’ ~-ah hoih lo a | he was wicked in the sight of the LORD) (b:muh) (r:12.21.20/47.5.7/1.6.11/1.38.7)
muhna = (t:n) (w:belief) (b:muh)
muhna = (t:n) (w:opinion) (d:the way someone sees or judges a person or a matter: keima muhna-ah is in my eyes, in my opinion) (e:Nang in keima ~ ah/kei’ ~-ah Sodom khua mite tawh kibang khin | to me they are all like the people of Sodom/amau’ ~-ah siam a kisate | those who are clever in their own eyes) (b:muh) (r:9.29.9/24.23.14/23.5.21)
muhnate = (t:n) (w:visions/things seen/sights) (d:plural of muhna, seeing or what is seen: maang muhnate are visions, and zakna muhnate are the senses of hearing and sight) (e:na maang ~ leh na thugen kholhnate/Babilon siatna ding tawh kisai a ~ | what he saw concerning the ruin of Babylon/zakna ~ zangin | by using hearing and sight) (s:maangmuhnate/mangmuhnate) (b:muhna) (r:26.12.27/23.13.1/58.5.14) (q:draft)
muhnop = (t:v) (w:want to see/long to see) (d:muh, see, with nop, want: want or long to see someone or something) (e:amah a ~ sawt mahmah khinta/note’ muhte a ~ uh hangin mu ngei lo | though they wanted to see what you see, they never saw it/na ~ hun uh hong tung ding a | the time will come when you long to see it/Na ~ uh kamtai pa hong pai-in | the messenger you long to see will come) (r:42.23.8/42.17.22/42.10.24/39.3.1) (q:draft)
muhnopna = (t:n) (w:longing to see/desire to see) (d:muhnop, want to see, with the noun suffix na: the longing to see someone) (e:Note in kei na hong ~ thu uh/note in zong kote na hong ~ uh thute | how you too long to see us) (b:muhnop) (r:47.7.7/52.3.6) (q:draft)
muhnopzia = (t:n) (w:the way one wants to see) (d:muhnop, want to see, with zia, manner: how someone wishes to find a person or thing) (e:keima maisuah na ~ bangun) (r:47.12.20) (q:draft)
muhpa = (t:n) (w:the one seen/the one found) (d:muh see or find with pa, the man: the man whom someone sees or finds) (e:tua na ~ uh kamsang mawkmawk ciang bek/na semin a om a ~ pen | the one whom he finds at work) (b:muh) (r:40.11.9/40.24.46) (q:draft)
muhphetin = (t:adv) (w:as soon as seen) (d:muh see, with phet as soon as and in: the moment someone sees it) (e:mi khatpeuh in a ~ lo in) (r:23.28.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
muhsa = (t:adj) (w:seen/already seen) (d:muh, see, with sa, already: seen; with a pronoun before it, what someone has seen) (e:thu khempeuh uh ka ~ hi a/A ~ leh a zaksa thute teci a pang | he testifies to what he has seen and heard/ka ~ uh, ka theihsa uh thute | the things we have seen and known/a zaksa a ~ uh khempeuhte hangin | for all they had heard and seen) (s:kimusa) (b:muh) (r:18.13.1/40.11.4/43.3.32/44.4.20/42.2.20) (q:draft)
muhsak = (t:v) (w:show/reveal/cause to see) (d:muh, see, with the causative sak: make or let someone see, show; often of what God shows in a vision) (e:Nang ka hong ~ thu khempeuh/Topa hong ~ mangmatna leh thupiakkholhna thu | the visions and revelations the Lord has shown me/Nangma maipha nong ~ zawh leh | if you have shown me your favor/amaute a ~ loh nading thu | that he would not let them see it/Pasian’ ~ mangmuhnate thei thei lo uh a | they cannot understand the visions God shows) (s:kilangsak/lah) (a:seel/im) (b:muh) (r:35.2.2/47.12.1/9.27.5/6.5.6/23.28.7) (q:draft)
muhsakna = (t:n) (w:revelation/showing) (d:muhsak show, with the noun suffix na) (e:Topa in maang hong ~ le ka muhte) (b:muhsak) (r:47.12.1) (q:draft)
muhsaksa = (t:adj) (w:shown/revealed) (d:muhsak show with sa, already: that has been shown, placed before a noun) (e:Topa in kei hong ~ thute khempeuh) (b:muhsak) (r:26.11.25) (q:draft)
muhsate = (t:n) (w:things already seen) (d:muhsa already seen, with plural te) (e:a ~ kua in a lamen nawn ding hiam) (b:muhsa) (r:45.8.24) (q:draft)
muhsung = (t:n) (w:sight/time of being watched) (d:muh see, with sung within: while someone is looking) (e:amaute’ ~ bekin tuaci gamtat kei unla) (r:49.6.6) (q:draft)
