Musite = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:hawks/falcons) (d:musite, hawks or falcons, written with a capital at the start of a sentence) (e:~ zong kikhawm tuahin) (b:musite) (r:23.34.15) (q:draft)
musuk = (t:v) (w:look down and see/see below) (d:mu, see, with suk, downward: see what is below, as God looking down from heaven) (e:Pasian in hong ~ thei lo ding hi) (b:mu) (r:18.22.14) (q:draft)
mut = (t:v) (w:blow/blow on) (d:of wind or breath: blow on or against something; also blow a trumpet, as in peengkul mut) (e:Huih in ka mai hong ~ a/Nang in na huih tawh na ~ a | you blew with your wind/hu in a ~ ciangin lopa vul-in | when the breath blows on it the grass withers/huih in gamlak-a singte a ~ bangin | as the wind blows the trees of the forest/tua inn a ~ ciangin | when it blew against that house) (s:nun/seem) (r:18.4.15/40.7.25/2.15.10/23.40.7/23.7.2) (q:draft)
mute = (t:n) (w:those who see/those who find/onlookers) (d:mu, see or find, with the plural te: the people who see or find someone) (e:a ~ khempeuh nakpitakin lau mahmah/Amau a ~ in na negawp uh hi | those who found them devoured them/konglak-a hong ~ in kei hong pelin | those who see me in the street avoid me) (s:mukhate) (b:mu) (r:66.11.11/24.50.7/19.31.11) (q:draft)
mutel = (t:v) (w:discern/see clearly) (d:mu, see, with tel, clearly: see into a matter and understand it; thu mutel theite are the discerning) (e:amau’ thu ~ theite’ thu muhtel theihna) (s:theitel/khentel) (r:23.29.14) (q:draft)
mutgawp = (t:v) (w:blow violently/blow hard) (d:mut blow with gawp, which marks violent or thorough action; said of a storm wind) (e:huihpi hat in ~ ding hi/a susia dingin ~ hi | it blows hard to destroy them/huihpi’ ~ buk bangin awn ding hi | it will sway like a hut battered by the storm) (b:mut) (r:26.13.11/18.27.23/23.24.20) (q:draft)
mutgawpin = (t:v) (w:blowing hard on/driving back) (d:mutgawp blow violently, with in linking to the next verb) (e:nisuahna huihpi hat tawh tuipi ~) (b:mutgawp) (r:2.14.21) (q:draft)
mutgawpna = (t:n) (w:blasting/blight) (d:mutgawp blow violently with the noun suffix na; huihpi mutgawpna is the blasting of crops by wind) (e:huihpi ~, leh a nom tawh) (b:mutgawp) (r:5.28.22) (q:draft)
mutgawpsak = (t:v) (w:be blown about violently) (d:mutgawp blow violently, with sak: said of a ship caught by the wind) (e:Teembaw hong ~ ahih manin) (b:mutgawp) (r:44.27.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
muthei = (t:v) (w:be able to see/can see/see) (d:mu, see, with thei, can: be able to see; khua muthei is to have sight, said of the blind who are healed) (e:thakhatin khua ~ pah a/amah ka ~ pah hi | at once I was able to see him/khua zong hong ~ hi | he could also see/khua ~ nawn lo ka hih manin | because I could no longer see/Mipilte in a lauhuai thu ~-in pelh uh a | the wise see danger and avoid it) (b:mu) (r:42.18.43/44.22.13/40.12.22/44.22.11/20.27.12) (q:draft)
