mutheite = (t:n) (w:seers/those who see) (d:muthei, able to see, with the plural te; thu mutheite are those who see or discern things, the seers) (e:nomau’ lutang ahi thu ~ khuhcip hi/amaute in thu ~ tungah | they say to the seers/thu ~’ adingin siang mahmah hi | to those who discern they are very clear) (s:thumute) (b:muthei) (r:23.29.10/20.8.9/23.30.10) (q:draft)
mutin = (t:v) (w:blowing) (d:mut blow, with the linking ending in: of wind blowing, or of blowing a trumpet) (e:peengkul ~ awng unla, va gen un/huih in hong ~ tui gei lamah | the wind blowing us toward the shore/huihpi’ ~ Mediterranean tuipi tungah | driven by the storm on the Mediterranean sea) (b:mut) (r:24.4.5/44.27.40/44.27.27) (q:draft)
mutkhak = (t:v) (w:blow on/blow against) (d:mut blow, with khak touch, reach) (e:a ~ loh nadingin leitung huih lite) (r:66.7.1) (q:draft)
mutkhia = (t:v) (w:blow away/carry off) (d:mut, blow, with khia, out or away: of wind, carry something off) (e:huih in amaute ~ ding a/Huih in amaute ~-in | the wind carries them off) (s:mutmang/leenkhia) (b:mut) (r:23.41.16/23.57.13) (q:draft)
