mutkhiamang = (t:v) (w:blow away/sweep away) (d:mut blow, khia out, with mang away: said of a storm) (e:huihpi in amaute ~ ding hi) (s:mutmang/mutkhia) (r:18.27.20) (q:draft)
mutkhiat = (t:v) (w:blow away/blow off) (d:form of mutkhia used before ciangin and before a noun, said of wind) (e:huihpi in a ~ buhsi bangin/huihpi in theipuam a ~ bangin | as a strong wind blows unripe figs off/Nisuahna huihpi in a ~ ciangin keutum ding | when the east wind blows on it, it will wither/huih in a ~ meiipi tawh kibang uh a | they are like clouds blown away by the wind) (s:letkhiat/mutmang) (b:mutkhia) (r:18.21.18/66.6.13/26.17.10/61.2.17) (q:draft)
mutkhiatsak = (t:v) (w:blow away) (d:mutkhiat blow away with sak; kong mutkhiatsak is I blew it away from you) (e:kong ~ mang khin hi) (b:mutkhiat) (r:37.1.9) (q:draft)
mutlum = (t:v) (w:slay with breath/blow down) (d:mut blow, with lum to death: kill by blowing) (e:tua A Gilopa ~ ding a) (r:53.2.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
mutmang = (t:v) (w:blow away/scatter/winnow) (d:mut, blow, with mang, away out of sight: said of wind driving off chaff or dust, and of God scattering a people) (e:huih in buhvai a ~ bangin/huihpi’ mut bangin note kong ~ ding hi | I will scatter you as the storm blows/Nisuahna lam huih in nin a ~ bangin | as the east wind blows dust away) (s:mutkhia/leenmang/letkhiat) (r:24.13.24/24.15.7/24.18.17) (q:draft)
mutmangsak = (t:v) (w:cause to blow away) (d:mutmang blow away, with the causative sak) (e:huihpi ka ~ ding a) (b:mutmang) (r:24.49.36) (q:draft, low confidence)
mutna = (t:n) (w:blowing/blast) (d:mut, blow, with the noun suffix na: the blowing of the wind, or the blast of a trumpet) (e:huih ~ lam ka zui uh hi/peengkul ~ aw, gal kisimna aw ka za hi | I hear the trumpet blast and the battle cry/huih ~ tawh damdamin a paisak uh hi | they let it drift slowly with the wind) (s:nunna) (b:mut) (r:44.27.15/24.4.19/44.27.17) (q:draft)
