n = (t:ppm) (d:short form of in written after an apostrophe on a word ending in a vowel, marking the doer of the action, as in ke’n for kei in, kua’n for kua in and humpi’n for humpi in) (e:Ke’~ aman takpi kong cih-inah/ke’~ ka ne hi | I ate it/Ka galte’~ gim a thuak teh | when my enemies suffered/kua’~ ci thei ding ahi hiam | who can say/ke’~ ka kheelkik thei kei hi | I cannot change it) (r:40.24.47/19.146.1/1.3.12/18.31.29/18.9.12/4.23.20) (q:draft)
na = (t:pron) (w:you/your) (d:second person marker: before a verb it means you, before a noun your) (e:~ thu/leh ~ pa’ inn panin | and from your father’s house/Koi lai-ah om ~ hi hiam | where are you/bang hangin ~ mai sia ahi hiam | why is your face downcast/huan sung singkung khempeuh ~ nethei ding hi | you may eat from every tree in the garden) (s:nang) (r:2.20.3/1.12.1/1.3.9/1.4.6/1.2.16)
na = (t:n) (w:object/article/item/thing/goods) (d:a thing, object or possession; na khempeuh is everything, all the goods someone owns) (e:Amah in ~ liante leh kuama phawk/~ khempeuh leh a an khempeuh uh la-in | taking all the goods and all their food/leh ama ~ khempeuh zong la uh a | and they also took all his possessions/tua natna a ban’na ~ pen | the article the disease has spread to) (r:18.5.9/1.14.11/1.14.12/3.13.50)
Na = (t:pron) (w:your/you) (d:na written with a capital at the start of a sentence or quoted line; second person marker placed before a noun or verb) (e:~ galte na khe nuai-ah ka koih/~ min bang ahi hiam | what is your name/~ zi Sarah koi-ah om ahi hiam | where is your wife Sarah/~ si taktak kei ding uh hi | you will not surely die/~ sam uh zong a kisim khin hi | even your hairs are all numbered) (b:na) (r:42.20.42/1.32.27/1.18.9/1.3.4/40.10.30) (q:draft)
na'ng = (t:part) (w:for/in order to/so that) (d:short form of nading, placed after a verb to show purpose or what something is for) (e:tui dawn ~ thuneihna nei lo/Pasian’ tate suah theih ~ thu a pia hi | he gave the right to become children of God/i lawmte noptuam ~ ngaihsunin | thinking of what is good for our neighbours/ngasa khuh ~ ngen paai in | let down the nets to catch fish) (r:46.9.4/49.1.12/43.1.12/45.15.2/42.5.4) (q:draft)
na'ngin = (t:conj) (w:so that/in order to) (d:shortened form of nadingin, placed after a verb to show purpose; spelling of the 1932 text) (e:nalamdang a kibawl theih ~ hong hehpih in/thupha hehpihna khat peuhmah kong piak ~ | so that I may give you some gift of grace/thu ka gen theih ~ thu hong pia in | give me leave so that I may speak/si-le-sa nopsak ~ tua suahtakna zang kei un | do not use that freedom to indulge the flesh) (s:nangin) (r:44.4.30/45.1.11/44.21.39/48.5.13) (q:draft)
