nading = (t:v) (w:dedicate) devote time or effort to a particular task or purpose
nading = (t:prep) (w:for/to/in order to) (d:placed after a verb to say what something is for or what an action aims at: giah nading mun is a place for spending the night) (e:paknamtui hal ~ leh Ompihna Anlum/giah ~ mun zong ka nei uh hi | we also have a place to spend the night/Sabuai puak ~ zawlte | the poles for carrying the table/Ka kalsuan ~ mun tanzau nong pia a | you gave me a broad place for my steps) (s:ading) (r:14.2.4/1.1.14/1.24.25/2.25.27/19.18.36)
nadinga = (t:prep) (w:for/in order to) (d:nading with the linking a, joining a purpose to the clause or noun that follows: amah puak nadinga a khak leengte, the carts he sent for carrying him) (e:amah puak ~ a khak leengte/gualnop ~ na bawl Awle | Leviathan, which you made to play/teen’ ~ hong piak na khuapite | the towns he gives you to live in/ka khutmete galkap ~ a hilh | who trains my fingers for battle) (b:nading) (r:1.45.27/19.104.26/5.13.12/19.144.1) (q:draft)
nadingah = (t:ppm) (d:nading, which turns a verb into its place or purpose, with the place marker ah; pai nadingah is to where someone is going, on his way) (e:a pai ~ pai hi/ama pai ~ Topa pai a | the Lord went on his way/ama pai ~ kumpipa kha uh hi | they sent the king on his way/Topa’ na sep ~ tuni-in | for the service of the Lord today) (b:nading) (r:1.25.34/1.18.33/10.19.40/2.32.29) (q:draft)
nadingin = (t:prep) (w:for/so that/in order to) (d:nading with the ending in: after a verb it states the purpose of the action that follows, so that, in order to) (e:khialhna hanga biak ~ keel a pa khat/A mite thu a khen theih ~ | so that he may judge his people/an lei ~ sum dang zong kong pua | we have also brought other money to buy food/Nang tungah kong khialh loh ~ | so that I might not sin against you) (s:ading) (b:nading) (r:4.7.16/19.50.4/1.43.22/19.119.11)
nadingte = (t:part) (d:nading, for the purpose of, with plural te: closes a phrase to mean the things that are for or that lead to something, as biak nadingte, things for offering) (e:leenggahzu tawh biak ~ lei nading bekin/kisuan’ ~ panin ka kikem hi | I have kept myself from what leads to guilt/thong sung khiat ~ in kei hong ngak hi | imprisonment awaits me) (b:nading) (r:15.7.17/19.18.23/44.20.23) (q:draft)
nadingun = (t:conj) (w:so that/in order that) (d:nading with the plural ending un: placed after a verb whose subject is plural to state a purpose, so that they or you may) (e:Kha Siangtho a ngah ~/na kipuk loh ~ hih thu kong genkhol hi | I have told you this so that you will not fall away/mawhsakna tawh a kipelh ~ hih thute vaikhak in | give these instructions so that they may be free of blame/Levi mite na mangngilh loh ~ kingaihsun un | take care that you do not forget the Levites) (b:nading) (r:44.8.15/43.16.1/54.5.7/5.12.19) (q:draft)
Nafath = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Naphoth) (d:place named third in the list of Manasseh’s towns within Issachar and Asher, connected with Dor) (r:6.17.11) (q:draft)
Nafathdor = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Naphoth Dor) (d:region around Dor on the Mediterranean coast south of Mount Carmel) (r:11.4.11)
Nafish = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Naphish) (d:son of Ishmael, and the tribe descended from him) (r:13.1.31)
Nafith = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Naphish) (d:spelling of Nafish, a son of Ishmael) (r:1.25.15)
Nafothdor = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Naphoth Dor) (d:region around Dor on the Mediterranean coast south of Mount Carmel) (r:6.11.2)
Naftali = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Naphtali) (d:son of Jacob and Bilhah, ancestor of the tribe of Naphtali) (r:1.30.8/4.13.14) (q:?)
Naftuh = (t:name) (c:male/people) (w:Naphtuhim/Naphtuhites) (d:people descended from Egypt, the son of Ham; written Naftuh mite) (r:1.10.13)
Naggai = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Naggai) (d:ancestor of Jesus in the genealogy of Luke) (e:Esli in ~’ ta hi) (r:42.3.25/42.3.26) (q:draft)
Nahalal = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Nahalal) (d:town in the territory of Zebulun given to the Levites) (r:6.19.15/6.21.35)
Nahaliel = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Nahaliel) (d:stopping place of the Israelites east of the Dead Sea, between Mattanah and Bamoth) (r:4.21.19)
Nahalol = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Nahalol) (d:town in Zebulun whose Canaanite inhabitants were not driven out, the same as Nahalal) (r:7.1.30)
Naham = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Naham) (d:man of Judah whose sister was the wife of Hodiah) (r:13.4.19)
Naharai = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Naharai) (d:man of Beeroth, armor-bearer of Joab and one of David’s mighty warriors) (r:13.11.39/10.23.37)
Nahash = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Nahash) (d:king of the Ammonites who besieged Jabesh Gilead and was defeated by Saul; also the name of other men) (r:13.19.1/10.17.27)
Nahath = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Nahath) (d:name of several men, among them a son of Reuel and grandson of Esau, and a Levite descended from Kohath) (r:13.1.37/13.6.26)
Nahbi = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Nahbi) (d:son of Vophsi, the spy sent from the tribe of Naphtali to explore Canaan) (r:4.13.14)
nahoih = (t:n) (w:good thing/good things) (d:na, thing, with hoih, good: a good thing or good things, such as food or what God has promised) (e:a gilkialte ~ tawh vah sak hi/na nasempa tungah hih ~ na ciam khin hi | you have promised this good thing to your servant/note tawh kisai ~ hong ciam khempeuh | all the good things he promised concerning you) (b:hoih) (r:19.107.9/10.7.28/6.23.14) (q:draft)
Nahor = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Nahor) (d:name of two men: the son of Serug and grandfather of Abraham, and a brother of Abraham) (r:1.11.22)
nahpa = (t:n) (w:stubble/chaff) (d:dry stalks or husks that the wind carries off; nahpa keu is dry stubble) (e:huihpi in ~ keu bangin amaute/ama thal tawh ~ leeng bang sak hi | with his bow he makes them like flying chaff) (r:23.40.24/23.41.2) (q:draft)
Nahshon = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Nahshon) (d:son of Amminadab, leader of the tribe of Judah in the wilderness and ancestor of David) (r:4.1.7/13.2.11)
nahteh = (t:n) (w:leaves/fallen leaves) (d:nah and teh both mean leaf; nahteh muat is rotten leaves, used where the English has scum and refuse) (e:a kihhuai ~ muat bangin na hong bawl hi) (r:25.3.45) (q:draft, low confidence)
nahthel = (t:n) (w:dry leaf) (d:a dry or fallen leaf that the wind blows about) (e:huih letkhiat ~ keu ka bang uh hi/~ ging in amaute tai sak ding a | the sound of a leaf will make them flee) (r:23.64.6/3.26.36)
Nahum = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Nahum) (d:prophet from Elkosh whose vision about Nineveh is the book of Nahum; also an ancestor of Jesus in the genealogy of Luke) (r:34.1.1/42.3.25)
nai = (t:part) (d:particle prefixed to a verb to convey a negative sense, as not yet) (e:guah zusak ~ lo/Sarai in ta nei ~ lo hi | Sarai had not yet borne a child/mite’ mawhna kicing ~ lo hi | the sin of the people is not yet complete/tu ni dong ka za ~ kei hi | I had not heard of it until today) (r:1.2.5/43.2.4/1.16.1/1.15.16/1.21.26)
nai = (t:n) (w:watch) (d:a watch or clock, the instrument that shows the hour)
nai = (t:n) (w:time/hour/o'clock) (d:an hour, or the hour of the day by the clock; nai khat is one hour and nitak nai thum is three in the afternoon) (e:~ bangzah ahia?/~ khat bek na a sem uh hi | they worked only one hour/~ khat nangawn kei tawh ngakkhawm zo lo | not able to keep watch with me even one hour/nitak ~ thum ciangin khatvei pai kik a | he went again at three in the afternoon) (r:40.20.12/40.26.40/40.20.5)
naih = (t:v) (w:approach/draw near/come near) (d:form of nai near used as a verb with an object or before endings such as ciangin) (e:Zeisu in a ~ ciangin khuapi mu-in/a Pasian ~ nuam lo hi | she does not want to draw near to her God/eite in Pasian i ~ theih nading | so that we can draw near to God/luppih dingin na ~ kei ding hi | you shall not approach her to lie with her) (s:neh) (a:kihem) (b:nai) (r:42.19.41/36.3.2/58.7.19/3.18.19) (q:draft)
naihin = (t:v) (w:approaching/drawing near/coming near) (d:naih with the linking ending -in, used when another action follows: approached and) (e:Tua ciangin Abraham in hong ~/kulh kongpi-ah Samuel va ~ | approached Samuel in the gateway/Aaron in biakna tau ~ | Aaron came near the altar and/Esther in hong ~ tua ciangkhut dawn va lawng | Esther approached and touched the tip of the scepter) (s:nehin) (b:naih) (r:1.18.23/3.9.8/9.9.18/17.5.2) (q:draft)
naihkik = (t:v) (w:approach again/go up again) (d:naih approach, with kik again) (e:gal phualah ka ~ ding uh hiam) (b:naih) (r:7.20.23) (q:draft)
naihuai = (t:adj) (w:close/near/related) (d:nai near with huai: close to one in kinship or friendship; also the close person himself, as i naihuai, our kinsman) (e:na lawm ~ pente uh nangawn in/Amah i ~ ahi hi | he is our kinsman/Abimelek pen note’ ~ ahihna hangin | because Abimelek is your kinsman) (r:40.6.3/7.9.3/7.9.18) (q:draft)
naikuan = (t:v) (w:draw near/be close at hand) (d:nai near, with kuan go toward) (e:Ka bei ding ~ ta hi) (s:naita) (r:18.17.1) (q:draft, low confidence)
Nail = (t:name) (c:land/river) (w:Nile) (d:the great river of Egypt, called Nail gun or Nail gunpi) (r:2.7.25/23.19.5)
nailo = (t:adv) (w:not yet/never yet) (d:nai yet with the negative lo, written as one word after a verb; usually written nai lo) (e:lupkhopna tawh pasal a thei ~ numei/pasal tawh a lum khawm ~ | had not yet slept with a man/tua bang thu a dong ngei kuamah om ~ hi | no one has ever yet asked such a thing) (b:nai) (r:4.31.35/7.11.39/27.2.10) (q:draft)
nailung = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:mulberry) (d:a tree, the mulberry or sycamine of Luke 17; nailung kung is a mulberry tree) (e:hih ~ kung kiangah) (r:42.17.6) (q:draft)
Nain = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Nain) (d:town in Galilee where Jesus raised a widow's son to life) (r:42.7.11) (q:draft)
naina = (t:n) (w:nearness/approach) (d:the fact of being near or having come close, said of a time or an event) (e:amau adingin siatna a ~ thu thei lo/Topa’ hong pai ding Ni hong ~ thu | that the Day of the Lord's coming is near/amau’ siat nading a ~ thei uh hi | they realized that their ruin was near/Pasian’ Uk nading hun a hong ~ thu | that the time of God's rule has come near) (r:7.20.34/26.12.23/58.10.25/7.20.41/42.10.11) (q:draft)
nainai = (t:adv) (w:closer and closer/more and more) (d:placed after a verb to show an action that presses in or keeps building up) (e:Mi tampi in kei hong langpan’ ~ hi/a kimkot pan a tuk ~ uh | they keep attacking from all around/A hehna hong kinuai ~-in hong paikhia ta) (r:19.3.1/24.12.9/24.23.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
nainawn = (t:see) <nainawn'sak>
nainawn'sak = (t:v) (w:bother/trouble/weary) (d:nainawng troublesome, with the causative sak) (e:hih meigong in kei hong ~ man-inah | because this widow keeps bothering me) (s:nawngkaisak/nainawngsak) (r:42.18.5) (q:draft)
nainawng = (t:adj) (w:tiresome/wearying) (d:said of speech that goes on and on; kam nainawng ci is to babble) (e:Gentailte bangin kam ~ ci tuan kei un) (r:40.6.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
nainawngsak = (t:v) (w:encumber/burden/trouble) (d:nainawng troublesome, with the causative sak: in the verse a barren tree burdening the soil) (e:Bang hangin lei a ~ hiam) (s:nawngkaisak/nainawn'sak) (b:nainawng) (r:42.13.7) (q:draft)
Naioth = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Naioth) (d:place in Ramah where Samuel lived and where David fled from Saul) (r:9.19.19/9.19.18)
naipen = (t:adj) (w:nearest/closest) (d:nai near, with the superlative pen; said of a relative) (e:i tanau ~ khat ahi hi) (s:kinaipen) (a:gamlapen) (r:8.2.20) (q:draft)
naipente = (t:n) (w:nearest ones/closest relatives) (d:naipen nearest, with plural te) (e:i tanau ~ khat ahi hi) (b:naipen) (r:8.2.20) (q:draft)
naipuan = (t:n) (w:silk/silk cloth/costly fabric) (d:a costly fine cloth, with puan cloth) (e:~ tungsilh kong silhsak hi/saihadial puan, ~, leh a kiphan a kizem | fine linen, silk and embroidered cloth) (r:26.16.10/26.16.13) (q:draft)
naisakin = (t:v) (w:bringing near) (d:nai near, with causative sak and in linking to the next verb) (e:i theih theih nadingin ~ tungsak ni) (r:23.5.18) (q:draft)
naisan = (t:n) (w:gore) (d:found only in the pair sisan naisan, the blood in which a newborn child lies; the meaning of naisan by itself is not clear) (e:sisan ~ lak-a na kitomtom) (r:26.16.6/26.16.22) (q:draft, low confidence)
naita = (t:v) (w:be near/draw near/be at hand) (d:nai near with ta, which marks a change of state: has come near, of a time or event) (e:Buk Pawi hun hong ~ ahih manin/Kei hong lehhek ding pa hong ~ hi | my betrayer has come near/Topa hong pai ding hun ~ ahih manin | because the time of the Lord's coming is near/Ka gualzawh ding hun hong ~ hi | the time of my victory has come near) (s:naizo/naikuan/nehta) (r:43.7.2/26.30.3/40.26.46/59.5.8/23.51.5) (q:draft)
naite = (t:n) (w:those who draw near) (d:nai near, come near, with plural te) (e:Pasian kiangah a ~’ taang a) (r:58.7.25) (q:draft)
naizaw = (t:adj) (w:nearer/closer) (d:nai near with zaw more; of time and of kinship) (e:kei sangin a ~ tanau khat/tu-in hong ~ ahih ciangin | because it is nearer now) (a:gamlazaw) (b:nai) (r:8.3.12/45.13.11) (q:draft)
naizo = (t:v) (w:be near/have drawn near) (d:nai near, with zo) (e:ka thukhenna ding ni a ~ hi) (s:naita) (r:31.1.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
nak = (t:n) (w:nostril/nose) (d:the nose or a nostril, the organ of breathing and smelling) (e:A ~ panin meikhu suak a/a ~ sungah nuntakna hu a om | that had the breath of life in its nostrils/~ nei napi-in nam thei lo uh hi | they have noses but cannot smell/Na ~ leh na bilte hong atkhiatsakin | they will cut off your nose and your ears) (s:nakvang) (r:18.41.20/1.7.22/19.115.6/26.23.25)
nakah = (t:n) (w:in the nose/in the nostrils) (d:nak nose, nostril with the place marker ah) (e:na ~ nakpheh hong bulhin/na ~ sikkawi bulhin | putting a hook in your nose/Pasian’ hu, ka ~ ka diik laiteng | as long as I breathe the breath of God in my nostrils) (b:nak) (r:12.19.28/18.27.3/23.37.29) (q:draft)
nakbah = (t:n) (w:nose ring/ring) (d:nak nose with bah ring; an ornament worn in the nose) (e:a nak tungah ~ ka batsak a/shekel lang a gik kham ~ khat | a gold nose ring weighing half a shekel/vokpi muk-a om kham ~ tawh kibang | is like a gold ring in a pig's snout) (r:1.24.47/20.11.22/1.24.22) (q:draft)
Nakbahte = (t:n) (w:nose rings) (d:plural of nakbah, an ornament worn in the nose) (e:~, bilbahte leh na khuk ding kumpi lukhu) (s:nakbuhte) (r:26.16.12) (q:draft)
nakbuhte = (t:n) (w:nose rings) (d:nak nose with buh ring, as in zungbuh finger ring, and the plural te) (e:min gelhna zungbuhte leh ~) (s:Nakbahte) (r:23.3.21) (q:draft)
nakdeih = (t:v) (w:love greatly/desire strongly) (d:deih want, love, with the intensive nak before it) (e:tuate ka ~ mahmah hi) (r:19.119.167) (q:draft)
nakgen = (t:v) (w:tell much/talk freely about/keep telling) (d:gen tell with nak before it, strongly, much; nakkham le nakgen is the more he forbade the more they told) (e:Hih thu ~ lua-in kitheithang gawp/nakkham le ~ semsem zawsop uh hi | the more he forbade them, the more they told it) (r:41.1.45/41.7.36) (q:draft)
nakging = (t:n) (w:snorting/snort/blast of the nostrils) (d:nak nose with ging sound: the noise of breath forced through the nostrils) (e:galte’ sakol ~ kiza hi/na ~ tawh tuipi taw kimu a | at the blast of your nostrils the bottom of the sea was seen/mawhsakna, ama ~ tawh | at his rebuke, at the blast of his nostrils) (r:24.8.16/19.18.15/10.22.16) (q:draft)
nakguh = (t:n) (w:rib) (d:one of the curved bones of the chest) (e:a lakkhiat ~ pen numei khatin bawl/a ha kikalah ~ thum pet a | holding three ribs between its teeth) (r:1.2.22/27.7.5)
nakguhte = (t:n) (w:ribs) (e:a ~ khat la-in tua mun) (b:nakguh) (r:1.2.21) plural form of <nakguh>
nakkham = (t:v) (w:forbid strongly) (d:kham forbid, with the intensive nak before it) (e:~ le nakgen semsem zawsop uh hi) (r:41.7.36) (q:draft)
nakkhiat = (t:v) (w:breathe out) (d:in the verse, breathe out threats) (e:nakpi-in a ~ lai takin) (r:44.9.1) (q:draft, low confidence)
nakkin = (t:adj) (w:very zealous/very keen) (d:kin eager, with the intensive nak before it) (e:tang ngeinate a ~ mahmah ka hihna) (r:48.1.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
naklau = (t:v) (w:be very afraid) (d:lau fear, with the intensive nak before it) (e:Amah le a lawmte ~ mahmah uh) (s:laulua/kihtalua) (r:41.9.6) (q:draft)
naklauhuai = (t:adj) (w:terrifying) (d:lauhuai fearful, with the intensive nak before it) (e:Tua pen ~ mahmah ahih manin) (s:dipkuathuai) (r:58.12.21) (q:draft)
nakleh = (t:conj) (w:if/as long as/provided that/whenever) (d:placed after the verb of a condition: if indeed, as long as that is so; ahih nakleh is if it is so) (e:khat a khialh ~ a vekpi-in/nikten puansilh i neih ~ a phazo | if we have clothing, that is enough/lungmuanna kiptakin i let ciat ~ | if we each hold our confidence firmly/a nungta dingin ka deih ~ | if I want him to stay alive/Na hihzawh ding ahih ~ | if it is in your power to do) (r:59.2.10/13.28.7/54.6.8/58.3.14/43.21.23/20.3.27) (q:draft)
nakliat = (t:adj) (w:very great) (d:liat, a form of lian great, with the intensive nak before it) (e:Pasian’ hong hehpihna ~ mahmah a) (s:lianlua) (r:45.11.33) (q:draft)
nakngeek = (t:n) (w:nostril) (d:apparently the nose or nostrils, filled with a stench) (e:a uihna na ~ uh kong zensak hi | I filled your nostrils with the stench) (s:nakngek) (r:30.4.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
nakngek = (t:n) (w:nostril) (d:apparently the nose or nostrils, filled with a stench; the other Bible text writes nakngeek) (e:na ~ uh kong zensak hi | I filled your nostrils) (s:nakngeek) (r:30.4.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
naknuam = (t:v) (w:rejoice greatly/be very glad) (d:nuam glad, with the intensive nak before it) (e:sungah amah ~ mahmah hi) (r:19.21.1) (q:draft)
Nakon = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Nakon) (d:owner of the threshing floor where Uzzah touched the ark of God and died) (r:10.6.6)
nakpau = (t:v) (w:insist/speak strongly) (d:pau speak, with the intensive nak before it) (e:nawhsa takin ~ semsem uh a) (r:42.23.5) (q:draft)
nakpheh = (t:n) (w:nose/nostril) (d:part of the nose through which a cord or ring is passed) (e:A ~-ah khau vawh zo ding/Kua in a ~-ah khau vawh zo ding | who can put a cord through its nose) (r:18.41.2/18.40.24) (q:draft, low confidence)
nakpheh = (t:n) (w:nose hook/nose ring) (d:hook or ring put in the nose to lead an animal or a captive) (e:na nak ah ~ hong bulhin) (r:12.19.28) (q:draft, low confidence)
nakpi = (t:adv) (w:greatly/very much/loudly/bitterly) (d:with great force or to a great degree, usually as nakpi-in or nakpi takin) (e:~-in a kap hi/Saul in ~ takin amah it a | Saul loved him greatly/~ takin kap kawmin khua sungah vak | went about the city weeping bitterly/~-in a lungkim kei hi | he was very unhappy/mite ~-in kap uh hi | the people wept aloud) (s:nakpitakin) (r:42.22.62/41.15.37/9.16.21/17.4.1/42.18.23/7.2.4) (q:draft)
nakpi = (t:adj) (w:great/intense/loud) (d:placed before a noun: great in force or degree, as nakpi launa great fear and nakpi aw a loud voice) (e:~ launa tawh a dim uh hi/~ aw tawh kiko a | he shouted with a loud voice/Ramah gamah ~ kahna kiza hi | great weeping is heard in Ramah) (r:44.5.11/66.10.3/40.2.18) (q:draft, low confidence)
nakpipi = (t:see) <nakpipi-in>
nakpipi-in = (t:adv) (w:very strongly/vehemently) (d:nakpi strongly, repeated for emphasis, with the adverb marker in) (e:a kam uh tawh ~ hawk uh a) (r:19.59.7) (q:draft)
nakpitakin = (t:adv) (w:very/so/greatly/very much/loudly) (d:nakpi strongly with tak and the adverb ending in, written as one word: to a great degree or with great force) (e:Note a dingin ~ na a sem Mary/Saul in amah ~ it a | Saul loved him greatly/Tua ciangin ~ Jesuh kiko-in | then Jesus cried out loudly/hih leitungah ~ na ka sepna | my hard labor on this earth) (s:nakpi) (b:nakpi) (r:45.16.6/23.31.6/9.16.21/41.15.37/21.2.20)
naksiat = (t:v) (w:be badly ruined/be utterly destroyed) (d:siat be ruined with nak before it, strongly, greatly: the ruin was great) (e:Tua inn ~ mahmah hi/tua inn pen ~ mahmah hi | that house was utterly ruined) (r:40.7.27/42.6.49) (q:draft)
naksiatzaw = (t:adj) (w:much worse/more vile) (d:naksiat very bad, with the comparative zaw) (e:nangma mawhnate ~ lua ahih manin) (b:naksiat) (r:26.16.52) (q:draft)
naksuk = (t:n) (w:breath/breathing) (d:nak nose or breathe with suk downward; used in the pair naksuk naktoh, breathing down and up, for breath or the power to breathe) (e:~ naktoh akipan na khempeuh hong pia) (b:nak) (r:44.17.25/19.135.17) (q:draft)
nakthuk = (t:adj) (w:very deep) (d:thuk deep, with the intensive nak before it) (e:a thu theihnate ~ mahmah hi) (s:thuklua) (r:45.11.33) (q:draft)
naktoh = (t:n) (w:breath/breathing) (d:nak nose or breathe with toh upward; used in the pair naksuk naktoh, breathing down and up, for breath or the power to breathe) (e:naksuk ~ theihna nei lo uh hi) (b:nak) (r:19.135.17/44.17.25) (q:draft)
naktohna = (t:n) (w:breathing/breath) (d:naktoh breathe upward, with the noun suffix na; naksuk naktohna is breathing in and out) (e:kam sungah naksuk ~ theihna nei lo uh hi) (b:naktoh) (r:19.135.17) (q:draft, low confidence)
nakvang = (t:n) (w:nostril/nostrils) (d:nak nose with vang opening) (e:A ~ panin meikhu pusuak a/Ama’ ~ sungah husan’na a om mipa | the man who has breath in his nostrils) (s:nak) (r:10.22.9/23.2.22) (q:draft)
nakvangte = (t:n) (w:nostrils) (e:Ama ~ panin meikhu pusuak a) (b:nakvang) (r:19.18.8) (q:draft)
nakzat = (t:v) (w:use much/make much of) (d:zat use, with the intensive nak before it) (e:thuneihna hong ~ lua-in ka kisialhpih hangin) (r:47.10.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
nakzuih = (t:v) (w:follow zealously/be zealous for) (d:nak, strongly, with zuih follow: keep a law or teaching with great zeal) (e:thukham ~ mahmah uh hi) (r:44.21.20) (q:draft)
nal = (t:adj) (w:slippery) (d:nal sak is make slippery) (e:lampi uh mial-in ~ sak in/khuamial lak lam ~-a pai tawh a kibang | like walking a slippery path in the dark) (r:19.35.6/24.23.12) (q:draft)
nalamdang = (t:n) (w:miracle/wonder/sign) (d:na thing with lamdang wonderful: a wonderful deed, a miracle or sign; also used for more than one) (e:sawltakte in ~ tampi leh lim tampi/Pasian in Paul’ khut tungah ~ liante lak | God showed great miracles by the hands of Paul/Judah mite in ~ a ngen thei uh hi | the Jews ask for signs/Tua zah ~ tampi amaute mai-ah a lah hangin | though he showed so many signs before them) (b:lamdang) (r:44.2.43/43.12.37/44.19.11/46.1.22) (q:draft)
nalamdangte = (t:n) (w:wonders/miracles/signs/marvelous deeds) (d:plural of nalamdang: wonderful deeds, often paired with limte signs) (e:Nangmah in ~ a bawl/ka limte leh ~ ka tamsak hangin | though I multiply my signs and wonders/Filip hih ~ a muh ciangin | when they saw the wonders Philip did/nangma ~ ka ciamteh ding hi | I will remember your wonders) (s:lamdangte) (b:nalamdang) (r:19.77.14/19.135.9/2.7.3/44.8.6/19.77.11) (q:draft)
nalamgdang = (t:n) (w:wonder/miracle) (d:seen once in a list after lim, sign; probably a misprint of nalamdang, a wonderful thing) (e:ze-etna, lim, ~, gal) (r:5.4.34) (q:draft, low confidence)
nalna = (t:see) <nalna-ah>
