nam = (t:n) (w:type/class) (e:tehna ~ nih/khaici ~ nih na pawi kei ding uh hi | you shall not sow two kinds of seed/tawisuang ~ nih, a gik leh a zang | two kinds of weights, a heavy and a light) (r:5.25.14/3.19.19/5.25.13)
naman = (t:adj) (w:true/genuine) (d:seen once in a naman lo sum, wealth that is not true or right, set against sum taktak, real riches; the part na is unclear) (e:leitunga a ~ lo sum tungah) (b:man) (r:42.16.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
nambat = (t:n) (w:number) (d:a number as a figure or a count, from English number) (e:Tua ~ in zaguk sawmguk-guk ahi hi/Tua kisimna ~ ka za hi | I heard the number of that count/sahang’ ~ sim ta hen | let him calculate the number of the beast) (r:66.13.18/66.9.16) (q:draft)
