namin = (t:v) (w:kiss) (d:nam, kiss, with the linking ending -in, kissing or having kissed) (e:Orpah in a teeknu ~ ciah a/a tute leh a tanute ~ amaute thupha pia | kissed his grandchildren and daughters and blessed them/kumpipa in Barzillai ~ thupha pia a | the king kissed Barzillai and blessed him/a khete ~ a sathau puak a nuh | kissed his feet and put her perfume on them) (r:8.1.14/8.1.9/1.31.55/10.19.39/42.7.38) (q:draft)
namin = (t:adv) (d:second part of nam-namin, tribe by tribe or kind by kind) (e:a nam-~ Israelte giahphual sat a mu hi) (b:nam) (r:4.24.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
