namnih = (t:n) (w:two kinds) (d:nam, kind, with nih, two: two different kinds of one thing, as two kinds of seed sown in the same field) (e:khaici ~ na vawh kei ding hi/Na leenggui lo-ah khaici ~ | two kinds of seed in your vineyard) (r:5.22.9) (q:draft)
nampi = (t:adj) (w:noble/excellent) (d:nam, kind, with pi, great: of high kind, noble; said of the holy people, whom the English calls the noble ones) (e:amaute ~ hi a) (b:nam) (r:19.16.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
