namte = (t:n) (w:kinds) (d:nam, kind, with the plural te: the kinds or sorts of creatures and things, and also the families or classes of people) (e:Hih bang dawi ~ thungetna leh/ganhing ~ khempeuh | all the kinds of livestock/kumpi nam leh mi lian ~ lak pan | from among the royal family and the noble families) (b:nam) (r:41.9.29/1.2.20/27.1.3) plural form of <nam>
namtuam = (t:adj) (w:of another kind/different/foreign/strange) (d:nam, kind, with tuam, different: of another kind; pau namtuam is a tongue, a kind of speech the hearers do not understand, and a namtuam khat is one of a different tribe) (e:Pau ~ tawh thu ka nget leh/pau ~ a gen mi in | the one who speaks in a tongue/i Topa pen a ~ khat hi a | our Lord is one of a different tribe/pau ~ tawh kong gen hangin | though I speak to you in a tongue) (s:namdang) (r:46.14.14/46.14.13/58.7.13/46.14.6) (q:draft)
