nan = (t:v) (w:support/prop up) (d:hold something up from below; the noun form with -na is a support or prop, as under a basin stand) (e:a ~’na li om ciat hi/a kiu lite-ah tuikuangpi ~’nate om hi | at the four corners were supports for the basin) (s:nang) (r:11.7.34/11.7.30) (q:draft, low confidence)
nana = (t:see) <nana-ah>
nana-ah = (t:phrase) (d:seen once in nangma deih nana-ah, for whatever you wish, at your service; apparently na thing with the noun ending na and the place marker ah) (e:nangma deih ~ kizang ding hi) (r:23.60.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
nane = (t:phrase) (w:you eat) (d:na, you, and ne, eat, written as one word; nane kei ding is you shall not eat) (e:a kisawh peuhmah ~ kei ding uh hi) (b:ne) (r:2.12.20) (q:draft)
