nang = (t:v) (w:prop up/support) (d:hold up something that leans or bends; in the Bible text also stand up against, as in nang zo, be able to withstand) (s:nan) of bent trees, objects, etc
Nang = (t:pron) (w:you) (d:second person singular, written with a capital at the start of a sentence or when God is addressed) (e:~ na om tawntung ding hi/~ leh na lawmte tungah | to you and your friends/~ in khuapi nga na uk in | you take charge of five cities/~ tawh a kiho keimah | I who am speaking with you) (b:nang) (r:58.1.11/42.1.77/18.35.4/42.19.19/43.4.26) (q:draft)
nanga = (t:pron) (w:you) (d:nang you with the ending a before kipan: nanga kipan, beginning from you, you and the others as well) (e:Kei in ~ kipan na u na nau) (b:nang) (r:66.22.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
nangawn = (t:adv) (w:even/also) (d:placed after the word or phrase it stresses, marking an extreme or unexpected case) (e:Nipi ni ~ ukpa ahi hi/galhang pente ~, tai mang ding uh hi | even the bravest warriors will flee/No ~ hong kheem zo ahi hiam | has he deceived even you/Khangnote ~ gim-in kituk ding a | even youths will grow tired and stumble) (s:nangnawn) (r:41.2.28/14.16.12/30.2.16/43.7.47/23.40.30) (q:draft)
nangawnah = (t:adv) (w:even) (d:nangawn with the place marker ah: even in, even on, even to) (e:tua lai ~ lungnopna hun nei lo ding/singlamteh tung ~ sih ding a ut hi | he was willing to die even on a cross/sing beel leh suang beel khempeuh sung ~ | even in all the vessels of wood and stone/nasem pasalte tung ~ ka kha ka sung ding | even on the male servants I will pour out my Spirit) (b:nangawn) (r:23.23.12/29.2.29/50.2.8/2.7.19) (q:draft)
nangawnin = (t:adv) (w:even) (d:nangawn even with the suffix -in, placed after the word or phrase it stresses) (e:Zan hun ~ sun khuavak bek/Tu ~ Moses’ lai a sim uh ciangin | even today when they read Moses/tua bang hun ciang ~ | even in those days/khedap khau phel ding ~ ka kilawm kei hi | I am not worthy even to untie his sandal strap) (b:nangawn) (r:38.14.7/47.3.15/24.5.18/43.1.27) (q:draft)
nangawnun = (t:adv) (w:even) (d:nangawn even with the plural ending un, stressing an extreme or unexpected case) (e:gimna a thuak ciang ~ ama huh/a khang sawmna dong ~ | even to the tenth generation/na khutme khat ~ na lawng nuam kei uh | you will not lift even one finger/a ihmut sung ~ a pia hi | he gives even while they sleep) (b:nangawn) (r:18.36.13/5.23.3/42.11.46/19.127.2) (q:draft)
nangin = (t:pron) (w:you) (d:nang you with the subject marker in, written as one word) (e:Tua nung ciangin ~ an ne-in) (b:nang) (r:42.17.8) (q:draft)
nangin = (t:conj) (w:in order to/so that) (d:after a verb, for the purpose of; apparently a short form of nadingin) (e:ama dikna thu kilat ~ ahi zongin) (r:45.3.25) (q:draft, low confidence)
nangma = (t:det) (w:your) (d:possessive form of nang, placed before a noun; nangma aa is yours) (e:vantungah ~ thu kip tawntung hi/~ thahatna tawh mualte a bawl | who formed the mountains by your power/zan-in ~ min ka phawk a | in the night I remember your name/hihte khempeuh ~ aa ahi ding hi | all these will be yours) (s:nangmah) (b:nang) (r:19.119.89/19.119.60/19.65.6/19.119.55/42.4.7)
Nangma = (t:det) (w:your/you) (d:nangma written with a capital, for God or at the start of a line; your before a noun, you before sungah, hang and the like) (e:Pa aw, ~ min siangtho ta hen/~ thu tatsat lo-in ka zui ngitnget ding hi | I will always obey your law/~ gen bangin ka maisak hi | I have forgiven them as you asked/~ thu a nusia migilote | the wicked who forsake your law) (b:nangma) (r:42.11.2/19.3.8/19.119.44/4.14.20/19.119.53) (q:draft)
nangmah = (t:pron) (w:you/yourself) (d:emphatic form of nang: you yourself, you and no other; common in prayer) (e:Kei ka lau ciangin ~ ka hong muang hi/Sunthapai-in ~ kong phat a | all day long I praise you/~ in ka ngaihsutnate gamlapi pek panin na thei hi | you know my thoughts from afar/Thuman mi tungah ~ na thuman a | to the faithful you show yourself faithful) (s:nang) (b:nang) (r:19.56.3/19.123.1/19.71.8/19.139.2/19.18.25)
nangmah = (t:det) (w:your) (d:nangmah used before a noun as a possessive, more often written nangma) (e:~ min bek mah kote in ka zahtak uh | your name alone we honour/~ ngeina kipte zuihna-ah | in obeying your decrees) (s:nangma) (r:23.26.13/19.119.5)
Nangmah = (t:pron) (w:you/yourself) (d:nangmah, emphatic you, written with a capital when God is addressed and at the start of quoted speech) (e:~ in tuate khempeuh hih na hih manin/~ ka hong bel hi | I cling to you/~ in kei hong hilh khin na hih manin | because you yourself have taught me/~ in na vengpa’ zi tawh na lumkhawm kei | you shall not lie with the wife of your neighbour) (b:nangmah) (r:24.14.22/24.36.29/19.63.8/19.119.102/3.18.20) (q:draft)
nangmahmah = (t:pron) (w:you yourself/yourself) (d:emphatic form of nangmah, one person addressed) (e:~ in na thei hi/~ zong hih lai-ah hong om in | be here yourself as well/~ in na khen tawm hi | you have pronounced it yourself/~ in gilnatna lianpi khat na nei ding hi | you yourself will have a severe disease of the bowels) (s:nangpipi) (b:nangmah) (r:1.30.29/14.21.15/10.20.4/11.20.40) (q:draft)
nangnawn = (t:adv) (w:even) (d:placed after the word or phrase it stresses; another spelling of nangawn) (e:a inn gei ~-ah pai kha kei un/a khulte ~ meikuang in a hul lum hi) (s:nangawn) (r:20.5.8/27.3.22) (q:draft)
