nangpipi = (t:pron) (w:you yourself) (d:nang you with the emphatic pipi: one as great as you, you in person) (e:keima inn-ah ~ nong pai dingin) (s:nangmahmah) (r:40.8.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
nangun = (t:part) (d:seen once after theih, be able, apparently a short form of nadingun, in order that, so that) (e:na thuman ka zuih theih ~) (r:27.9.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
nangzo = (t:v) (w:withstand/resist/stand against) (d:nang, resist, with zo, be able: be able to withstand; mostly used with a negative) (e:a galte uh ~ nawn lo uh hi/Ama hehna kua in ~ ding a | who can withstand his anger/mi khat beek in hong ~ nai lo hi | not one has yet been able to withstand you/na galte uh na ~ kei ding uh hi | you will not be able to stand against your enemies) (s:thuakzo/dozo) (b:nang) (r:7.2.14/6.23.9/34.1.6/6.7.13) (q:draft)
nangzote = (t:n) (w:those who persevere/those who withstand) (d:nangzo withstand with the plural te: the ones who stand firm under trial) (e:a ~ a hampha mahmah ahi hi/Tua bangin a ~ in | those who persevere in this way) (b:nangzo) (r:59.1.12) (q:draft)
nanna = (t:n) (w:support/prop) (d:nan support with the noun suffix na: a part that holds something up, as the supports of a basin stand or the ledges that carry beams) (e:kiu ciatah a ~ li om ciat a/a ~ singbekte a bawl hi | he made the supporting ledges) (b:nan) (r:11.7.34/11.6.6) (q:draft)
nanna = (t:n) (w:resistance/withstanding) (d:nan withstand with the noun suffix na: holding out against something, as against a siege) (e:Jerusalem umcihna na ~ ding uh) (b:nan) (r:14.32.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
nannan = (t:n) (w:manna/coriander) (d:in the Bible text the plant whose small round seed manna is compared to: nannan tang is coriander seed) (e:Manna pen ~ tang tawh kibang a | the manna was like coriander seed/tua pen ~ tang tawh kibangin | it was like coriander seed) (r:4.11.7/2.16.31)
nannate = (t:n) (w:supports/props) (d:plural of nanna, a part that holds something up) (e:a kiu lite-ah tuikuangpi ~ om hi/tua a ~ a ngakna tawh sakhat ahi hi | those supports were of one piece with the stand/Tua ~ a kisung hi a | those supports were cast) (b:nanna) (r:11.7.30/11.7.34) (q:draft)
nanzawh = (t:v) (w:withstand/resist/stand against) (d:nan withstand with zawh be able; the form of nangzo used before ding and nading) (e:eite in bangci ~ ding ihi hiam/na galte uh ~ nading vangliatna na nei kei | you will have no strength to stand before your enemies) (s:thuakzo/dozo) (r:12.10.4/3.26.37) (q:draft)
Naomi = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Naomi) (d:wife of Elimelek of Bethlehem and mother-in-law of Ruth) (r:8.1.3/8.1.2)
nap = (t:v) (w:kiss) (d:touch with the lips as a greeting or a sign of love) (e:Ka ~ pen pa amah hi ding hi/Ka ~ pa pen Jesuh hi ding hi | the one I kiss is Jesus/ka khe a ~ khawl nai lo hi | she has not stopped kissing my feet) (s:tawp) (r:40.26.48/41.14.44/42.7.45) (q:draft)
nap = (t:v) (w:smell/sniff) (d:take in a smell through the nose) (e:a namtui gimnam a ~ ciangin) (s:diik) (r:1.8.21) (q:draft)
nap = (t:n) (w:nasal mucus/snot) (d:in nap nit, blow the nose at, a gesture of contempt; rendered sniff at in English) (e:~ nong nitsan lel uh hi) (s:naptui) (r:39.1.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
napa = (t:see) <pian'napa>
napi = (t:conj) (w:though/although/yet/but) (d:placed after a verb, often as napi-in: even though this is so) (e:na tampi a om ~-in pumpi khat/Ta taktak ahi ~-in | although he was truly a son/kei thuman ~ thuzuau genin hong seh hi | though I am right I am counted a liar/kumpi nei lo ~-in | though they have no king) (s:hinapi) (r:46.12.20/58.5.8/18.34.6/20.30.27) (q:draft)
napia = (t:phrase) (w:you give) (d:na, you, and pia, give, written as one word; napia kei ding is you shall not give) (e:khatpeuh peuh ~ kei ding a) (b:pia) (r:3.18.21) (q:draft)
napna = (t:n) (w:kiss) (d:nap, kiss, with the noun suffix na: a kiss, especially one given as a greeting) (e:a siangtho ~ tawh na kihopih un/nang in ~ tawh Mihing Tapa na lehhek ding hiam | will you betray the Son of Man with a kiss/Khat leh khat ki-itna ~ tawh kihopih un | greet one another with a kiss of love/Nang in ~ tawh leengla na hong do kei a | you did not welcome me with a kiss) (s:kinapna) (b:nap) (r:47.13.12/42.22.48/60.5.14/42.7.45) (q:draft)
nappa = (t:n) (w:the one kissed) (d:nap kiss with pa, the man: ka nappa is the man I kiss) (e:Ka ~ in Zeisu ahi hi) (b:nap) (r:40.26.48/41.14.44) (q:draft)
Naptali = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Naphtali) (d:son of Jacob and Bilhah, ancestor of the tribe of Naphtali) (r:1.46.24)
naptui = (t:n) (w:nasal mucus) (d:used in the pair khitui naptui, tears and running nose, for bitter weeping) (e:khitui ~ tawh Pasian’ inn mai-ah kunin/khitui ~ tawh a khe mai-ah va puk a | she fell at his feet weeping/khitui ~ tawh thumin na kiko hi | he cried out and pleaded with tears/kiniamkhiatna le khitui ~ tawh | with humility and with tears) (s:nap) (r:15.10.1/44.20.19/17.8.3/58.5.7) (q:draft)
nard = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:nard/spikenard) (d:a fragrant plant and the costly perfume made from it, a loanword) (e:henna leh ~ sing namtuite a po hi/a manpha mahmah ~ sathau namtui thawl khat | a jar of very costly nard perfume/~ paknamtui suangngo thawl khat | an alabaster jar of nard perfume) (s:mard) (r:22.4.13/41.14.3/43.12.3) (q:draft)
Nariah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Neriah) (d:father of Baruch, the scribe of Jeremiah, and son of Mahseiah) (r:24.32.12)
Narkissas = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Narcissus) (d:man in Rome whose household Paul greets) (r:45.16.11)
Narsissas = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Narcissus) (d:man in Rome whose household Paul greets; another spelling of Narkissas) (r:45.16.11)
nasa = (t:part) (d:the endings na and sa together on a verb, written after an apostrophe or hyphen, marking the place where something was or was done before; teen’nasa mun, the place once lived in) (e:a teen’~ mun-ah ama gui zom ding/Na ten’~ Zion Mual phawk in | remember Mount Zion where you dwelt/siampite’ khe a din’~ mun | the place where the feet of the priests had stood/David in a seh-~ mun ahi | it is the place David had appointed) (r:18.18.19/6.4.9/19.74.2/14.3.1) (q:draft)
nasaepna = (t:see) <nasaepna-a>
nasaepna-a = (t:n) (w:service/work) (d:seen once, in the service of the tabernacle; apparently nasepna, work or service, with the ending a, in, and ae probably a misprint for e) (e:biakbuk ~ a nazat khempeuh) (r:2.39.40) (q:draft, low confidence)
nasak = (t:v) (w:afflict/hurt/cause pain) (d:na, be painful or ill, with the causative -sak: make a part of the body hurt or sick) (e:natna tawh a gil ~ hi/Ama khete pen kolte in ~ a | the shackles hurt his feet/tua tuisia pen ama sungah tumin ~ velval ding a | the bitter water will enter her and cause sharp pain/Tua numei a ~ velval thei ding tuisia | the bitter water that can cause the woman sharp pain) (r:14.21.18/19.105.18/4.5.27/4.5.24) (q:draft)
nasak = (t:phrase) (d:na sak written as one word, you consider or you feel; hoih nasak leh means if it seems good to you) (e:kumpipa in hoih ~ leh/hih ka ngaihsutna man ~ a | and if you think this plan of mine right/hoih ~ kei leh hong pai kei in | if it does not seem good to you, do not come) (r:17.7.3/24.40.4/17.8.5) (q:draft)
nasakna = (t:phrase) (d:na sak, you consider, with the noun ending na; hoih nasakna mun is the place that seems good to you) (e:nangmah in hoih ~ munah teng in) (b:nasak) (r:1.20.15) (q:draft)
nasate = (t:n) (w:former ways/things done before) (d:the endings na and sa with the plural te after a verb: the things formerly done; gamtat nasate, the ways walked before) (e:a pa’ gamtat ~ zui ahih manin) (b:nasa) (r:14.17.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
naseemte = (t:n) (w:servants) (d:nasem, servant, with the plural te, here spelled with ee; the same verse also has nasemte) (e:tua ~ an ne dingin tusak a) (s:nasemte) (r:42.12.37) (q:draft)
nasem = (t:n) (w:servant/worker) (d:one who works for or serves another, from na, work, and sem, do; also a hired worker) (e:Ama ~ Abraham’ suante/a lianpen in, na ~ uh ahi ding hi | the greatest shall be your servant/ama ~ Moses leh ama teelsa Aaron sawl hi | he sent his servant Moses and Aaron whom he had chosen/a kicial ~ hita leh | or a hired worker) (s:nasempa/sila) (a:topa) (b:sem) (r:13.16.13/40.23.11/19.105.26/2.12.45) (q:draft)
nasem = (t:v) (w:serve/work) (d:do work, or serve a master or God; na, work, with sem, do, written as one word) (e:amah in kum guk sung ~ ding a/Note ~ dingin adang pawlpite tung pan | from other churches in order to serve you/Ama ~ ding mihing tulza om a | countless thousands were there to serve him/buh at ~ ding mi hong sawl in | send people to work at the harvest) (s:sem) (b:sem) (r:2.21.2/4.8.15/47.11.8/27.7.10/40.9.38) (q:draft)
Nasem = (t:n) (w:servant) (d:nasem written with a capital at the start of a sentence, and once of Jesus as the Servant of God) (e:Pasian in a ~ dingin Jesuh teelin/~ gilopa aw | you wicked servant/~ mi in phattuamna a ngah ciangin | when a worker receives his reward/~ ukte in kin ngaihsut uh a | the overseers of the workers kept pressing them) (b:nasem) (r:44.3.26/42.19.22/45.4.4/2.5.13) (q:draft)
nasemin = (t:v) (w:serve/work/minister) (d:nasem with the linking ending in: serving, working, and then) (e:ka biakna tau-ah ~/sun tawh, zan tawh ~ | working day and night/a mawkna-in ~ hahkat ka hi kei hi | I did not labour in vain/note adingin aana tawh ~ | doing forced labour for you) (b:nasem) (r:26.44.16/52.2.9/50.2.16/5.20.11) (q:draft)
nasemin = (t:adv) (w:as a servant/as a worker/as forced labour) (d:nasem servant or worker with in, as: in the role of a servant, or put and kept as workers) (e:Kanaan mite ~ koih uh a/Faro’ ~ a tum ciangin | when he entered the service of Pharaoh/a sanggamte khempeuh ama tungah ~ ka pia khin a | I have given him all his brothers as servants/Zanin galvil, sunin ~ | as guards by night and as workers by day) (b:nasem) (r:6.17.13/1.41.46/1.27.37/16.4.22) (q:draft)
nasemkhawm = (t:n) (w:fellow servant/fellow worker) (d:nasem servant or work with khawm together: one who serves alongside another) (e:Pasian sungah ~ khat ihi hi/na sanggamte khempeuh tawh ~ khat ka hi hi | I am a fellow servant with all your brothers/a zui mite tawh ~ khat ka hi hi | I am a fellow servant with those who keep them) (s:naseppih) (b:nasem) (r:48.2.9/66.22.9/66.19.10) (q:draft)
nasemna = (t:n) (w:service/work) (d:nasem, serve, with the noun suffix na) (e:kumpipa’ ~ ah uk uh hi) (s:nasepna) (b:nasem) (r:13.26.30) (q:draft)
nasemnangma = (t:see) <numei-nasemnangma>
nasemnu = (t:n) (w:maidservant/female servant/handmaid) (d:a female servant; also used by a woman of herself when speaking humbly) (e:Na ~ khialhna hong maisak in/numei ginalo bangin na ~ hong ngaihsun kei in | do not take your servant for a worthless woman/a nasempa, a ~, a bawngtal, a la | his male servant, his female servant, his ox, his donkey/Tu-in na ~ keimah in | now I, your servant) (s:silanu) (a:tonu) (b:nasem) (r:9.25.28/9.1.16/5.5.21/9.25.27) (q:draft)
nasemnute = (t:n) (w:maidservants/female servants) (d:plural of nasemnu, a female servant) (e:na nasempate, na ~, na ganhing uh) (b:nasemnu) (r:2.20.10/5.5.14) (q:draft)
nasempa = (t:n) (w:servant) (d:a male servant, nasem with pa marking a man; na nasempa, your servant, is also a humble way of speaking of oneself) (e:na thuciamna bangin na ~ na limbawl hi/na ~ hong kheng kei in | do not pass your servant by/ka ~ Jakob aw, ka teelsa Israel aw | Jacob my servant, Israel whom I have chosen/~ damin a om a mu uh hi | they found the servant well) (s:silapa/nasem) (a:topa) (b:nasem) (r:19.119.65/1.24.66/1.18.3/23.44.1/42.7.10) (q:draft)
Nasempa = (t:n) (w:servant) (d:nasempa, male servant, written with a capital at the start of a sentence, and of Jesus as the Servant of God) (e:a siangtho na ~ Jesuh’ min tawh/~ in a topa sangin lianzaw lo hi | a servant is not greater than his master/a siangtho na ~ Jesuh thah dingin | to kill your holy servant Jesus/~ in a topa thupiak bangin a hih maninah | because the servant did as his master ordered) (b:nasempa) (r:44.4.30/44.4.27/40.10.24/42.17.9) (q:draft)
nasempate = (t:n) (w:male servants/menservants) (d:plural of nasempa, a male servant) (e:na tanute, na ~, na nasemnute) (b:nasempa) (r:2.20.10/5.5.14) (q:draft)
nasemsak = (t:v) (w:make work/put to work) (d:nasem, work, with the causative sak) (e:Israel mite gim mahmahin ~ uh a) (s:semsak) (b:nasem) (r:2.1.13) (q:draft)
nasemte = (t:n) (w:servants/officials/attendants) (d:plural of nasem: the servants of a master, and the attendants or officials of a king) (e:A om laite in a ~ manin/Kumpipa Hezekiah’ ~ Isaiah kiangah a tun ciangin | when the officials of King Hezekiah came to Isaiah/Faro leh a ~, a kumpi uliante | Pharaoh, his attendants and his officials/Saul’ ~ in ama kiangah | the attendants of Saul said to him) (s:silate) (a:topate) (b:nasem) (r:40.22.6/23.37.5/24.25.19/9.16.15) (q:draft)
nasep = (t:n) (w:work/job/service/duty) (d:the work a person does or is given to do: a task, a duty, an occupation; from na, work, and sep, do) (e:na ~ ding khempeuh na hih ding hi/Amah in mihingte’ ~ khawlsak a | he stops the work of all people/Thatang ~ lah ka ngap kei a | I am not strong enough for manual work) (r:5.5.13/14.34.13/18.37.7/42.16.3)
nasepah = (t:n) (w:position/post) (d:nasep, work or office, with the place marker ah: in or to the work) (e:an piak ~ koihkik a) (b:nasep) (r:1.40.21) (q:draft)
nasepin = (t:adv) (w:as work/as occupation) (d:nasep work with in; nasepin nei is have as one's trade or occupation) (e:savunnim ~ a nei Simon/savunnim ~ nei-in tuipi gei-ah a teng | who is a tanner by trade and lives by the sea) (b:nasep) (r:44.9.43/44.10.6/44.10.32) (q:draft)
nasepna = (t:n) (w:workplace) (e:~ ah hong pai in) (b:nasep)
nasepna = (t:n) (w:work) (e:Pasian ~/vanpi in ama ~ taangko hi | the skies proclaim his work/Gimpi-a ~ in hauhna hi a | hard work brings wealth/Pasian hong sawlpa upna in Pasian ~ ahi hi | to believe in the one he has sent is the work of God) (b:nasep) (r:19.19.1/1.2.3/20.14.23/43.6.29)
nasepna = (t:n) (w:task) (e:a pualam ~ ah kiseh hi/amau’ ~ ah a kiseh bangin | as they were assigned to their tasks/ka ~ ka zawh theih nadingin | so that I may complete my task) (b:nasep) (r:13.26.29/13.24.3/44.20.24)
nasepna = (t:n) (w:creation) (e:hihte Pasian ~ hi/Na khutmete’ ~, na bawlsa kha leh aksite | the work of your fingers, the moon and stars you made/pian’sak ~ ama nasep khempeuh panin | from all his work of creating) (b:nasep) (r:1.2.3/19.8.3)
Nasepna = (t:n) (w:work/service/acts/deeds) (d:nasepna written with a capital at the start of a sentence or in a title; Solomon’ Nasepna Laibu is the book of the acts of Solomon) (e:Solomon’ ~ Laibu sungah kigelh hi/~ atuam atuam a om hangin | though there are different kinds of working/~ za i ngah leh, tua na sem ni | if we have received the office of serving, let us serve/~ ding a kithawi khit uh ciangin | when the service had been prepared) (b:nasepna) (r:11.11.41/46.12.6/45.12.7/14.35.10) (q:draft)
nasepnasa = (t:n) (w:work already done) (d:nasep work with the endings na and sa: the place or thing already worked) (e:midangte’ ~ sungah zong) (b:nasep) (r:47.10.16) (q:draft)
nasepnate = (t:n) (w:works/deeds/acts) (d:plural of nasepna: the things someone has done, in the Psalms mostly the mighty works of God) (e:Ama ~ mite lakah gen un/ama ~, Israel mite a musak hi | he showed his deeds to the people of Israel/a lamdang na ~ ka gengen lai hi | I still declare your marvellous deeds/A khang a khangin nangma ~ kiphatphat ding a | from generation to generation your works will be praised) (s:sepnate) (b:nasepna) (r:19.9.11/19.111.2/19.103.7/19.71.17/19.145.4) (q:draft)
naseppih = (t:n) (w:fellow worker/co-worker/fellow servant) (d:one who works together with another; nasep work with pih together with) (e:ka ~ Marka, Aristarkhas, Demas/Ka ~ Timoti in note hong hopih a | Timothy my co-worker greets you/a ~ a lawmte satgawp hen la | and he beats his fellow servants/A ~ pa zong a mai-ah bokin hong thum a | his fellow servant fell down before him and begged) (s:nasemkhawm) (b:nasep) (r:57.1.24/40.18.33/45.16.21/40.24.49/40.18.29) (q:draft)
naseppihte = (t:n) (w:fellow workers/co-workers/fellow servants) (d:plural of naseppih, one who works or serves together with another) (e:adang ka ~ tawh Lungdamna Thu/Pasian’ Gam ading ka ~ ahi uh a | they are my co-workers for the kingdom of God/a ~ uh le a sanggamte uh | their fellow servants and their brothers) (s:semkhawmte) (b:naseppih) (r:50.4.3/51.4.11/66.6.11) (q:draft)
nasepsa = (t:n) (w:product of labour/produce/earnings) (d:nasep work with sa, already done: what one has worked for and produced) (e:gahte leh na ~ khempeuh uh/a ~ uh khempeuh | all that they have produced) (b:nasep) (r:5.28.33/24.20.5) (q:draft)
nasepsak = (t:v) (w:work for/do work for) (d:nasep, work, with sak, here doing something on behalf of another; hong nasepsak, the work he did for me) (e:ama hong ~ ka thuhna-in) (b:nasep) (r:26.29.20) (q:draft, low confidence)
nasepte = (t:n) (w:work/works/duties) (d:nasep, work, with the plural te: the things done, or the duties of a service) (e:amaute in ama ~ mangngilh pah uh a/a lamdang ama ~ khempeuh gen un | tell of all his wonderful works/Amah in a ~ a manphatna thei a | she sees that her work is profitable/a siangthopen nate tawh kisai ~ | the work concerning the most holy things) (b:nasep) (r:19.106.13/19.105.2/20.31.18/4.4.4) plural form of <nasep>
nasepteng = (t:n) (w:all the work/the whole work) (d:nasep work with teng all) (e:innlam siamte’ ~ semin) (b:nasep) (r:46.3.10) (q:draft)
Nashon = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Nahshon) (d:son of Amminadab and father of Salmon, leader of the tribe of Judah in the wilderness and an ancestor of David) (r:40.1.4)
nasia = (t:adj) (w:severe/grievous/intense) (d:very great in a bad or painful way, of famine, sin, grief or punishment; nasia takin is severely, bitterly) (e:Tu-in gamsungah kialpi ~ semsem hi/Topa in ~ takin kei hong thuhilh a | the Lord has disciplined me severely/amaute’ khialhna ~ mahmah hi | their sin is very grievous/Tu-in Samaria ah kialpi ~ hi | now the famine was severe in Samaria) (r:1.43.1/19.118.18/1.18.20/11.18.2) (q:draft)
nasialua = (t:adj) (w:too severe/so terrible) (d:nasia, severe, with lua, too much: so severe or terrible, said of a plague) (e:Tua gimna ~ ahih manin) (b:nasia) (r:66.16.21) (q:draft)
nasiapen = (t:adj) (w:most severe/worst) (d:nasia, severe, with pen, most: the most severe, the worst of what is suffered) (e:Ka thuak ding uh a ~ pen teng) (b:nasia) (r:25.4.22) (q:draft)
nasiasak = (t:v) (w:make severe/make worse/aggravate) (d:nasia, severe, with the causative sak: make suffering or trouble more severe) (e:ka mite’ gimna ~ semsem uh hi) (b:nasia) (r:38.1.15) (q:draft)
nasiat = (t:adj) (w:severe/intense/great) (d:the form of nasia severe used before ma-in and lam; a nasiat ma-in is before it grows severe) (e:a ~ ma-in kitot khawl pak in/ama thuakna a ~ mahmah lam tak mu uh | they saw how very great his suffering was) (b:nasia) (r:20.17.14/18.2.13) (q:draft)
nasiazaw = (t:adj) (w:more severe/worse/greater) (d:nasia severe with the comparative zaw) (e:a thuak ding a ~ omlai a/na gim thuak ding uh ~ kan lai ding hi | the punishment you suffer will be even more severe) (b:nasia) (r:23.15.9/40.23.14) (q:draft)
nasim = (t:v) (w:respect/regard/esteem) (d:used with lo not: nasim lo is show no respect for, count as nothing; perhaps na thing with sim count) (e:unau khat ahih uh ciangin ~ lo/~ lo, thudon loin, om kei uh hen | let them not be disrespectful or careless/a lian dawi-numei Diana biakna inn ~ lo a | the temple of the great goddess Diana is not respected) (s:zahtak) (a:simmawh) (r:54.6.2/44.19.27) (q:draft)
nasuhte = (t:n) (w:plunder/spoils) (d:seen once in van nasuhte, the goods you seized from your enemies; apparently na, you, with suh, seize, and the plural te) (e:na galte uh van ~ uh) (r:6.22.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
nasut = (t:phrase) (w:rob/plunder) (d:the verb particle na and sut, rob, written as one word) (e:mi khempeuhte’ na ~ uh hi) (b:sut) (r:7.9.25) (q:draft, low confidence)
nat = (t:v) (w:be ill/hurt/be in pain) (d:form of na, be sick or in pain, used before a following word such as ciangin, hun or nading; said of the body, as ci nat, be ill, and of the heart) (e:ka lungsim hong ~ ciangin/a ci ~ ciangin | when he is ill/natna tawh Elisha a ~ ciangin | when Elisha was ill with the sickness/ama ~ nading nangawn-ah a ciampel lo mi | one who does not break his oath even when it hurts/a ~ hun tung hi | her time of pain came) (a:dam) (r:19.73.21/19.41.3/12.13.14/19.15.4/9.4.19) (q:draft)
natapate = (t:n) (w:sons) (d:tapate, sons, with na, your; in the one verse it follows another na, so the doubled na is probably a misprint) (b:tapate) (r:1.6.18) (q:draft, low confidence)
natawlngasak = (t:phrase) (w:you make rest) (d:na, you, and tawlngasak, cause to rest, written as one word: you are making them stop work) (e:nasepnate panin amaute ~ uh hi) (b:tawlngasak) (r:2.5.5) (q:draft)
nate = (t:n) (w:things/goods) (d:plural of na, thing: things, goods or deeds; a hoih nate is the good things) (e:Tua ~ khempeuh zatna hangin/Tua ~ thei-in na hih le-uh teh | if you know these things and do them/ahoih ~ na len tawntung un | hold fast to the good things/Hih ~ a neipa tawh nau ka nei hi | I am with child by the man who owns these things) (b:na) (r:51.2.22/52.5.21/43.13.17/1.38.25) (q:draft)
nate = (t:n) (w:members/parts) (d:plural of na in the sense of a part of the body: the parts or members of a body, also said of believers as members of the body of Christ) (e:Topa’ pum tung ~ i hi hi/A kilawmna om ~ | the presentable parts/tua ~ in nasepna-za khat guak a neih loh uh | these members do not all have one function) (b:na) (r:49.5.30/46.12.24/45.12.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
nateng = (t:n) (w:whole thing/all the parts) (d:na thing with teng all; pasal nateng, the whole male member) (e:a pasal ~ nangawn uh atkhia) (b:na) (r:48.5.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
Nathan = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Nathan) (d:name of several men, among them the prophet at the court of David and a son of David) (e:Attai in ~’ pa hi a) (r:13.2.36/10.23.36) (q:draft)
Nathanael = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Nathanael) (d:disciple of Jesus from Cana in Galilee) (r:43.1.49/43.1.47)
Nathanmelek = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Nathan-Melek) (d:official of the king of Judah whose room stood near the entrance to the temple in the days of Josiah) (r:12.23.11)
natna = (t:n) (w:disease/sickness/plague/illness) (d:sickness, disease or pain of the body; pul natna is a plague and phak natna a defiling skin disease) (e:ka ~ khempeuh hong dam sak hi/sih nading ~ ahi kei hi | it is not a sickness that leads to death/Pul ~ tawh amaute vat gawpin | striking them down with a plague/a kiciamteh lo ~ leh gimna khempeuh | every sickness and disaster not recorded) (s:cinatna) (a:cidamna) (r:19.103.3/42.14.2/43.11.4/4.14.12/5.28.61) (q:draft)
natnate = (t:n) (w:diseases/pains/sicknesses) (d:plural form of natna; lungsim natnate are pains of the heart) (e:Ka lungsim ~ hong damsak in la/Izipt ~ note tungah hong tungsak kik ding hi | he will bring the diseases of Egypt on you again/A pumpi sunga a ~ leh a lungsim gimna | the pains of his body and the grief of his heart/a ~ uh damin | their illnesses were cured) (s:cinatnate) (b:natna) (r:19.25.17/5.28.60/18.14.22/44.19.12) (q:draft)
natsak = (t:v) (w:afflict/make sick) (d:nat, be ill, with the causative sak: make sick, strike with disease) (e:Topa in a ~ cinatnate) (s:cinasak) (a:damsak) (b:nat) (r:5.29.22) (q:draft)
natsakna = (t:n) (w:affliction/infliction of pain) (d:nat be ill or in pain with sak cause and the noun suffix na: a making sick or causing of pain) (e:Pasian in ci ~ tawh mihing thuhilh a/Topa in a ~ cinatnate a muh uh ciangin | when they see the diseases with which the Lord afflicted it) (s:gimsakna) (b:natsak) (r:18.33.19/5.29.22) (q:draft)
natsia = (t:n) (w:wasting disease/grievous sickness) (d:nat sickness with sia bad) (e:amaute lakah ~ a tungsak hi) (r:19.106.15) (q:draft)
nattun = (t:n) (w:fever) (d:also used as a verb, have a fever; often written with an apostrophe) (e:a lawn’ ciangin a ~’ dam a/cisa-in ka ~ uh a | we are burning with fever/Piter’ sungnu ~’ a, lum a mu hi | he saw Peter’s mother-in-law lying with a fever/a phot leh, a ~’ dam a | when he helped her up, the fever left her) (s:cisa) (r:40.8.15/25.5.10/40.8.14/41.1.31) (q:draft)
nattunin = (t:adv) (w:with a fever/sick with fever) (d:nattun fever with in: being ill with fever) (e:sungnu ~ lupna tungah a lum/Simon’ sungnu ~ lupna ngak a | Simon’s mother-in-law was in bed with a fever/Simon’ sungnu ~ na gim mahmah a | Simon’s mother-in-law was suffering greatly with a fever) (b:nattun) (r:40.8.14/41.1.30/42.4.38) (q:draft)
nattutna = (t:n) (w:fever/sickness) (d:seen once of the illness that left Simon's mother-in-law; apparently nat, be ill, tut, lie down, and the noun suffix na) (e:a ~ dampah a) (s:nattun/cisa) (r:42.4.39) (q:draft, low confidence)
natui = (t:n) (w:discharge/bodily discharge/semen) (d:fluid that comes out of the body; in Leviticus 15 a discharge caused by illness and also an emission of semen) (e:tungah a ~ a tukna puan le savun/A ~ a paikhia mipa’ lupna | the bed of the man who has a discharge/Mi khat in a ~ a teh leh | if a man has an emission of semen) (r:3.15.17/3.15.4/3.15.16) (q:draft)
nau = (t:n) (w:child) (d:a baby or small child, also the child in the womb; nau paai is to be pregnant and nau suak to give birth) (e:gimna tawh ~ na suak ding hi/~ hoih khat hi ci-in a muh ciangin | when she saw that he was a fine child/paktatna tawh ~ nei hi | she is with child through prostitution/Sarah in ~ nawi pia ding | that Sarah would nurse a child) (s:naungek/naungeek) (r:1.3.16/2.2.2/1.38.24/1.21.7)
naubu = (t:n) (w:womb) (d:nau, child, with bu, nest: the womb; naubu hong, open the womb, is said of conceiving and of a firstborn) (e:a ~ sungah nih om hi/~ a hong masa khempeuh | every first one to open the womb/a ~ hon’sak hi | he opened her womb) (s:naugil) (r:1.38.27/2.34.19/2.13.12/1.30.22) (q:draft)
naucil = (t:n) (w:firstborn/first child) (d:nau child with cil, first or early; stands beside ta upa, eldest child) (e:Izipt gam sunga ~ khempeuh) (s:tacil) (r:19.78.51) (q:draft, low confidence)
naucing = (t:n) (w:nurse/nursemaid) (d:nau child with cing look after: a woman who nurses and cares for a baby) (e:naupang hong khoisak dingin ~ khat) (s:Naucingnu/cingnu) (r:2.2.7) (q:draft)
Naucingnu = (t:n) (w:nurse/nursemaid) (d:a woman who looks after a small child; nau child, cing tend, with nu marking a woman) (e:~ in nawi ne naungek a puak) (s:naucing/cingnu) (r:4.11.12) (q:draft)
naudom = (t:n) (w:midwife) (d:nau child with dom lift up, hold: one who helps at a birth; followed by nu, woman) (e:a gim mahmah laitakin ~ nu in ama kiangah) (s:naudomnu) (r:1.35.17/1.38.28) (q:draft)
naudomnu = (t:n) (w:midwife) (d:naudom, midwife, with nu, woman: a woman who helps at a birth) (e:~ in khausan khat la-in a khut tungah/a gim mahmah lai takin ~ in | as she was in great difficulty the midwife) (s:naudom) (b:naudom) (r:1.38.28/1.35.17) (q:draft)
naudomte = (t:n) (w:midwives) (d:plural of naudom, midwife) (e:Pasian in ~ lim bawl hi/~ in Pasian zahtak uh a | the midwives feared God/Izipt kumpipa in ~ sam in | the king of Egypt summoned the midwives) (b:naudom) (r:2.1.20/2.1.19/2.1.17/2.1.18) (q:draft)
naugil = (t:n) (w:womb) (d:nau, child, with gil, belly: the womb) (e:~ khakcip ding ka hi hiam/kei hong kipaaina ~ na khakcip lo a | it did not shut the womb that bore me) (s:naubu) (r:23.66.9/18.3.10) (q:draft)
naungeek = (t:n) (w:baby/infant/child) (d:a baby or very young child, born or unborn; another spelling of naungek) (e:ka gil sunga om ~ in lungdamna tawh/om ~ a mu uh hi | they found the baby/Naomi in ~ la-in a angah tawi a | Naomi took the child and held him in her arms/Nawine ~ in gulgilo’ kuavangah kimawl ding a | the nursing infant will play by the cobra’s hole) (s:naungek) (r:42.1.44/8.4.16/42.2.16/23.11.8) (q:draft)
naungeekte = (t:n) (w:infants/babies/newborn children) (d:plural of naungeek, baby) (e:~ in amau uk ding uh hi/a ~ uh leilak kiden’ gawp nading hi | their infants will be dashed to the ground/Naupangte leh ~ kongzing lakah a sibup uh hi | children and infants faint in the streets) (s:naungekte) (b:naungeek) (r:23.3.4/23.13.16/25.2.11) (q:draft)
naungek = (t:n) (w:baby/infant/child) (d:a baby or very young child; nawi ne naungek is a baby still at the breast) (e:a ~ vun dawn ki-at ding hi/en in, ~ kap hi | look, the baby was crying/David in ~ adingin Pasian tungah thum hi | David pleaded with God for the child/Naucingnu in nawi ne ~ a puak bangin | as a nurse carries a nursing infant) (s:naungeek) (r:3.12.3/2.2.6/10.12.16/4.11.12) (q:draft)
naungekte = (t:n) (w:infants/babies) (d:plural of naungek, baby) (e:nawine lai ~ zong paipih un/~ leh naupangte’ kam tawh | by the mouths of infants and children/gil sung pana piang ~ hehpih lo ding uh | they will have no mercy on newborn infants) (s:naungeekte) (b:naungek) (r:29.2.16/19.8.2/23.13.18) (q:draft)
Naungekte = (t:name) (w:Naungekte)
naunu = (t:n) (w:younger sister/sister) (d:nau younger sibling with nu, which marks a woman) (e:A ~ amah sangin hoihzaw/a ~ Mary va huausim a | she called her sister Mary aside/Na unu le na ~ na ngahkik ciangin | when you receive your older and your younger sisters) (a:unu) (b:nau) (r:7.15.2/42.10.40/43.11.28/26.16.61) (q:draft)
naupa = (t:n) (w:younger brother) (d:nau, younger sibling, with pa, which marks a male: a younger brother) (e:Kaleb’ ~ Kenaz’ tapa Othniel/Piter leh a ~ Andru | Peter and his brother Andrew/a ~ amah sangin lianzaw ding a | his younger brother will be greater than he) (s:nauzawpa) (a:u) (b:nau) (r:7.3.9/62.3.12/42.6.14/1.48.19) (q:draft)
naupaai = (t:v) (w:be pregnant/become pregnant/conceive) (d:nau, child, with paai, carry in the womb: be or become pregnant; numei naupaai is a pregnant woman) (e:Ahih hangin tua nu in ~ a/tua sunga om numei ~ khempeuh phel kham hi | he ripped open all the pregnant women in it/~ amau’ numeite na phelkham ding hi | you will rip open their pregnant women) (s:gai) (r:12.4.17/12.15.16/12.8.12) (q:draft)
naupaaite = (t:n) (w:pregnant women) (d:naupaai, be pregnant, with the plural te) (e:a nupi ~ uh kikuikham ding hi) (s:naupaiite/gaite) (b:naupaai) (r:28.13.16) (q:draft)
naupaii = (t:n) (w:pregnancy) (e:~ cih zong om nawn lo ding hi/Tua numei ~ hi a | the woman was pregnant/~ numei a hun a nai ciangin | when a pregnant woman is near her time) (s:gaina) (v:naupai) (r:28.9.11/66.12.2/23.26.17) the spelling naupai is not correct
naupaii = (t:n) (w:gestation/gravidity/parturiency) (e:Mite kitawngin numei ~ khat liamsak a | men who are fighting injure a pregnant woman/~ nupi in ta a suah ding | a pregnant woman about to give birth) (r:2.21.22/48.4.19)
naupaiina = (t:n) (w:childbearing) (e:~-ah na gimna nakpitakin ka khangsak ding a) (s:naupaina) (b:naupaii) (r:1.3.16)
