Nebo = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Nebo) (d:name of a town east of the Jordan, of the mountain from which Moses saw the promised land, of a Babylonian god, and of an ancestor of some who returned from exile) (r:4.32.3)
Nebukhadezzar = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Nebuchadnezzar) (d:spelling of Nebukhadnezzar, Nebuchadnezzar, the king of Babylon who destroyed Jerusalem) (r:27.3.7)
Nebukhadnazzar = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Nebuchadnezzar) (d:spelling of Nebukhadnezzar, Nebuchadnezzar, the king of Babylon who destroyed Jerusalem) (r:27.3.24)
Nebukhadnezzar = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Nebuchadnezzar) (d:king of Babylon who captured Jerusalem, destroyed the temple and took the people of Judah into exile) (r:12.24.1/27.4.28)
Nebukhadzezzar = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Nebuchadnezzar) (d:spelling of Nebukhadnezzar, Nebuchadnezzar, the king of Babylon who destroyed Jerusalem) (r:24.25.9)
Nebukhadznezzar = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Nebuchadnezzar) (d:spelling of Nebukhadnezzar, Nebuchadnezzar, the king of Babylon who destroyed Jerusalem) (r:24.51.34)
Nebukkhadnezzar = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Nebuchadnezzar) (d:spelling of Nebukhadnezzar, Nebuchadnezzar, the king of Babylon who destroyed Jerusalem) (r:27.2.28)
Nebushazban = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Nebushazban) (d:a chief officer of Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon at the fall of Jerusalem) (r:24.39.13)
Nebuzaradan = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Nebuzaradan) (d:commander of the guard of Nebuchadnezzar, who burned Jerusalem and the temple and carried the people into exile) (r:12.25.20/24.39.11)
Nedabia = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Nedabiah) (d:spelling of Nedabiah, a son of King Jehoiachin of Judah) (r:13.3.18) (q:draft)
Nedabiah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Nedabiah) (d:a son of Jehoiachin, also called Jeconiah, king of Judah) (r:13.3.18)
neek = (t:v) (w:eat) (d:form of ne, eat, used before ding, theih and nading; neek ding is something to eat, food) (e:~ ding, puansilh ding a om zah tawh/an pawl khempeuh ~ theih nadingin upna a nei hi | he has faith to eat every kind of food/an ~ na’ng, tui dawn na’ng thuneihna | the right to eat food and drink water/a ~ khit uh ciangin | after they had eaten) (r:54.6.8/45.14.2/46.9.4/44.20.11) (q:draft)
neel = (t:adj) (w:smooth/fine/soft) (d:smooth to the touch; of dust or cloth, fine) (e:keimah in ci ~ mi ka hi hi/midikpa’ lampi na ~ sak hi | you make the way of the righteous smooth/leivui ~ leeng bang ding uh a | they will be like fine blowing dust/kam khum kam ~ tawh amah zol a | she led him on with sweet and smooth talk) (s:nel) (a:tamkimlo) (r:1.27.11/23.26.7/23.29.5/20.7.21) (q:draft)
neellua = (t:adj) (w:too delicate/very tender) (d:neel, smooth or soft, with lua too much; a ci neellua, her body is so delicate) (e:amah ngek-in a ci ~ ahih manin) (b:neel) (r:5.28.57) (q:draft)
neelna = (t:n) (w:smoothness) (d:neel smooth with the noun suffix na; a neelna mun is the smooth part, the place where it is smooth) (e:a ~ mun a ngawng sanah silhsak a) (b:neel) (r:1.27.16) (q:draft)
neelsak = (t:v) (w:make smooth/make level) (d:neel smooth with the causative sak) (e:midik pa’ lampi na ~ hi) (b:neel) (r:23.26.7) (q:draft)
neelte = (t:adj) (w:fine) (d:neel, fine, with the plural te; an neelte is fine flour) (e:um-le-beel, an ~, leenggahzute) (b:neel) (r:13.9.29) (q:draft, low confidence)
neem = (t:adj) (w:soft/gentle/weak) (d:not hard or strong: tha neem is become weak, kam neem a gentle word, mit-hah neem weak eyes) (e:ka pumpi a tha ~ hi/Kam ~-a dawn’na in hehna damsak a | a gentle answer turns away wrath/Leah’ mit-hah ~ a | Leah had weak eyes/ka tha ~ ding a | I will become weak) (s:nem) (a:khauh/hat) (r:19.32.3/20.15.1/1.29.17/7.16.7) (q:draft)
Nefeg = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Nepheg) (d:name of two men: a son of Izhar of the tribe of Levi, and a son of David born in Jerusalem) (r:2.6.21)
Nefilim = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Nephilim) (d:people of great size and strength who lived before the flood and were later seen in Canaan, from whom the descendants of Anak came) (r:1.6.4/4.13.33)
Nefisim = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Nefisim/Nephusim) (d:family of temple servants who returned from the exile, called Nephusim in the NIV) (r:15.2.50)
Neftoah = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Nephtoah) (d:spring, the waters of Nephtoah, on the border between Judah and Benjamin) (r:6.15.9/6.18.15)
Nefushesim = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Nefushesim/Nephusim) (d:family of temple servants who returned from the exile, the same family as Nefisim, called Nephusim in the NIV) (r:16.7.52)
negawp = (t:v) (w:devour/eat up) (d:ne eat with gawp, severely, completely) (e:humpi khat in ~ ding hi/Amau a mute in na ~ uh hi | those who found them devoured them) (s:netum/nemang) (b:ne) (r:23.15.9/24.50.7) (q:draft)
Negeb = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Negev) (d:the dry southern region of Judah, toward the desert) (r:6.15.21)
neh = (t:v) (w:press hard/close in on/come near) (d:to push forward against someone or come up close, of an enemy, a battle or a crowd) (e:galte in amaute ~ mahmah uh hi/Gal in Saul nakpi takin ~ a | the battle pressed hard on Saul/nakpi takin Lot’ lam hong ~ uh a | they pressed hard toward Lot/na kiang nai hong ~ lo ding hi | it will not come near you/pangte hong ~ peuhpeuh kithat ding hi | anyone who comes up to the ranks will be killed) (s:naih) (r:9.13.6/9.31.3/1.19.9/19.91.7/12.11.8) (q:draft)
neh = (t:v) (w:prevail/win/gain the upper hand) (d:to gain the upper hand in a battle, said of the side that is pressing the other back) (e:peuhmah ciangin Israel in ~ hi/ciangin Amalekte in ~ hi | then the Amalekites were winning/Israel mite in ~ a | the Israelites were winning) (s:zo/gualzo) (a:lel/guallel) (r:2.17.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
Nehamani = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Nahamani) (d:one of the leaders who returned from the exile in Babylon with Zerubbabel) (r:16.7.6)
nehcih = (t:v) (w:hem in/press in on/crowd) (d:neh, press close, with cih, tightly on every side: of enemies closing in around a city) (e:hong umcihin hong ~ hun hong tung ding hi) (s:nehcip/uumcip) (r:42.19.43) (q:draft)
nehcihlam = (t:n) (w:crowding/pressing in) (d:nehcih, press in on, with lam, the fact or manner: that people are crowding in on someone) (e:nang hong ~ na thei hi) (r:41.5.31) (q:draft)
nehcip = (t:v) (w:crowd around/press upon/surround closely) (d:neh, press close, with cip, tightly: of a crowd pushing in around a person, or of trouble closing in) (e:zui uh ahih manin Jesuh a ~ uh hi/Jesuh hong ~ uh hi | they crowded around Jesus/nang hong umcihin hong ~ uh hi | they surround you and press upon you/gitlohna in kei hong ~ ciangin | when wickedness closes in on me/mihonte in ~ lua uh ahih manin | because the crowd pressed in too hard) (s:nehcih/uum/umcih) (r:41.5.24/42.5.1/42.8.45/19.49.5/44.21.35) (q:draft)
nehcipgawp = (t:v) (w:crush/crowd hard) (d:nehcip, crowd around, with gawp, violently) (e:Jesuh a ~ khak loh nadingin) (b:nehcip) (r:41.3.9) (q:draft)
Nehelam = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Nehelam) (d:home or clan of the false prophet Shemaiah, who is called the Nehelamite) (r:24.29.24/24.29.31)
Nehemiah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Nehemiah) (d:son of Hakaliah, cupbearer to the king of Persia and governor of Judah who rebuilt the wall of Jerusalem; also the name of two other men) (r:16.1.1/16.10.1)
nehin = (t:v) (w:come near/approach/step forward) (d:neh come near with the linking ending in, used when another verb follows; mai lam nehin pai is step forward) (e:mai lam ~ hong pai uh hi/ama kiangah ~ | going up to him/a inn vengte’ zite uh ~ | drawing close to their neighbors’ wives) (b:neh) (r:4.12.5/43.19.3/24.5.8) (q:draft)
nehkawmin = (t:adv) (w:keeping close/close along) (d:neh, come close, with kawm, while, and the ending in: staying close to something while going, as a ship along a shore) (e:~ ka pai uh hi) (r:44.27.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
nehpen = (t:see) <nehpen-a>
nehpen-a = (t:adj) (w:nearest) (d:seen once of the part of a gateway on the temple side; apparently neh, be close, with pen most and the ending a) (e:biakinn lam ~ om kawm pen) (r:26.40.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
nehphei = (t:v) (w:lean against/lean over to) (d:neh, come close, with phei sideways) (e:Jesuh ~ lai deuhin) (r:43.13.25) (q:draft)
nehpiksan = (t:v) (w:sneer at/scorn/despise) (d:purse the lips at someone in contempt, from neh, lip, and piksan, purse: sneer at, treat with scorn) (e:amah in ~ lel hi) (s:simmawh) (a:zahtak) (r:19.10.5) (q:draft)
nehta = (t:v) (w:draw near/close in on) (d:neh, come close or press upon, with ta, now) (e:mite in kei hong ~ uh a) (b:neh) (r:19.119.150) (q:draft)
nehthawh = (t:v) (w:confront/come against/attack) (d:neh, press upon, with thawh, rise) (e:kei hong ~ uh hangin) (r:19.18.18) (q:draft)
Nehum = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Nehum) (d:one of the leaders who returned from the exile in Babylon with Zerubbabel, called Rehum in Ezra) (r:16.7.6)
Nehushta = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Nehushta) (d:mother of King Jehoiachin of Judah, daughter of Elnathan of Jerusalem) (r:12.24.8) (q:draft)
Nehushtan = (t:name) (w:Nehushtan) (d:name given to the bronze snake that Moses had made, which King Hezekiah broke into pieces) (r:12.18.4)
Nehusta = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Nehushta) (d:spelling of Nehushta in the older Tedim text: mother of King Jehoiachin of Judah) (r:12.24.8)
nei = (t:v) (w:have) (d:have something or someone, as a child, a wife, a quality or a thought; with tawh it means have a child by someone) (e:maitang li leh kha li ~ ciat uh hi/pasian dang na ~ kei ding hi | you shall have no other gods/Sarah in tapa khat ~ ding hi | Sarah will have a son/a khiatna tuam ciat ~ hi | each had its own meaning) (a:tasam) (r:2.20.3/26.1.6/1.18.14/1.41.11)
nei = (t:v) (w:possess/own/hold) (d:have as one’s own property, as land, a house, animals or money) (e:tuuhon leh bawnghon tampi ~ hi | he owned very many sheep and cattle/Saipras mi khat in lo ~ a | a man from Cyprus owned a field/tawlkhat sung bek na biakinn ~ a | they possessed your sanctuary only a little while) (r:10.12.2/44.4.37/23.63.18)
nei = (t:v) (w:experience/undergo) (d:have a state or feeling come upon one, as sickness, fear or trouble) (e:a khete-ah natna ~ hi | he had a disease in his feet/sihbup natna ~-in gim mahmah hi | he has seizures and suffers greatly/bangmah launa ~ loin | without having any fear) (r:11.15.23/40.17.15/60.3.6)
Neiel = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Neiel) (d:town on the border of the territory of Asher) (r:6.19.27)
neih = (t:v) (w:have/own/possess) (d:form of nei, have, used in relative and dependent clauses and before loh, leh and hangin) (e:Abraham in a ~ khempeuh Isaak pia hi/Pasian itna lungsim na ~ loh uh | that you do not have the love of God in your hearts/Paubaan’ na ka ~ loh hangin | although I have no fault/Note in na ~ uh leitang khempeuh | all the land that you possess/Mi khatpeuh in bil a ~ leh | if anyone has an ear) (b:nei) (r:1.25.5/66.13.9/43.5.42/18.9.21/3.25.24) (q:draft)
neih = (t:n) (w:possession/property) (d:what someone has or owns; a neih khempeuh is all that he has) (e:Jakob mi honte’ ~ dingin/a ~ khempeuh a khiakhin ahi hi | she has put in everything she had/Ka ~ khempeuh | all that I have) (s:neihsa) (b:nei) (r:5.33.4/3.25.24/41.12.44/18.31.12) (q:draft)
neihdang = (t:n) (w:other possession/anything else owned) (d:neih possession with dang other) (e:Topa longal ~ nei lo ka hih manin) (r:25.3.24) (q:draft)
neihin = (t:v) (w:having/holding as) (d:neih, have or hold, with the ending in; ciamnuih-a neihin, holding someone as an object of mockery) (e:mite lakah ciamnuih-a ~ kote) (b:neih) (r:19.44.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
neihkhak = (t:v) (w:have/happen to have) (d:neih have with khak, form of kha, happen to; kisapna neihkhak loh nading, so that they have no lack) (e:kisapna bangmah a ~ loh nading uh) (r:56.3.13) (q:draft)
neihkhakna = (t:n) (w:reliance/having) (d:neihkhak, happen to have, with the noun suffix na; muanin neihkhakna, having someone as one's trust) (e:a zuautat mi muanin ~ pen) (b:neihkhak) (r:20.25.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
neihkhawm = (t:v) (w:share/have together/own jointly) (d:neih have with khawm together) (e:midang tawh na ~ ding hi lo hi/nang tawh i ~ na pianzia mah | the very glory that I shared with you) (b:neih) (r:20.5.17/43.17.5) (q:draft)
neihkik = (t:v) (w:have again/take again/marry again) (d:neih have with kik again; pasal neihkik is to marry again) (e:a zi in pasal a ~ leh/pasal a ~ nop uh ciangin | when they want to marry again/ama khuapi-in Zion a ~ nading | that he will again take Zion as his city) (b:neih) (r:40.5.32/38.1.17/54.5.11) (q:draft)
neihkikna = (t:n) (w:having again/taking again) (d:neihkik, have or take again, with the noun suffix na; of the Lord taking Jerusalem as his city again) (e:ama khuapi-in a ~ ding) (b:neihkik) (r:38.1.17) (q:draft)
neihlai = (t:v) (w:still have) (d:neih, form of nei, have, with lai, still) (e:Gen ding tampi ka ~ hangin/na ~ sunte uh a beimang ma-in | before the little you still have is gone) (r:63.1.12/66.3.2) (q:draft)
neihlam = (t:n) (d:the fact that someone has something; neih, the form of nei have, with lam, which turns the clause into the thing known or seen) (e:theihna na ~ ka thei hi/matutzawhna lianpi a ~ Saul in a muh ciangin | when Saul saw that he had great success/thu ka ~ phawk lo na hi hiam | do you not realize that I have the authority/leengpei khat ciat a ~ uh ka mu a | I saw that each of them had a wheel) (r:27.5.14/43.19.10/9.18.15/26.1.15) (q:draft)
neihlelam = (t:n) (w:wealth/possessions/property) (d:wealth and goods taken together, all that a person owns; also written neih leh lam) (e:a inn dimin ~ ka pia hi/Pasian in mi khat ~ guanin | when God gives a person wealth/inn sungah ~ a dimin om a | in the house there is wealth in plenty) (s:neihsa/hauhna) (a:zawnna) (r:20.8.21/21.5.19/20.21.20) (q:draft)
neihna = (t:n) (w:having/possession) (d:the act or state of having; thu neihna is a lawsuit or dispute) (e:thuman-a tawmno ~ hoihzaw hi/ama' thu ~-ah mi zawngpa | a poor man in his lawsuit/khut khat dim ~ hoihzaw hi | having one handful is better/vangliatna khempeuh na ~ | that you have all power) (b:neih) (r:20.16.8/2.23.3/21.4.6/18.42.2) (q:draft)
neihnate = (t:n) (w:possessions/belongings) (d:also the plural noun form of neih have, as in hazatna a neihnate, the jealousy that one holds) (e:hauhnate, ~, leh pahtawina zong/Efraim in hazatna a ~ bei ding a | the jealousy that Ephraim holds will end) (s:neihsate) (b:neihna) (r:14.1.12/23.11.13) (q:draft)
neihnateng = (t:n) (w:all that one has) (d:neihna, having, with teng all; lungsim i neihnateng, the whole of the mind we had) (e:mawhnopna lungsim i ~ i sucip a) (b:neihna) (r:45.6.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
neihsa = (t:n) (w:property/possessions/wealth) (d:what a person owns) (e:a ~ khempeuh nusia-in a nung a zui/nomau ~ ciat na ngah kik ding uh hi | each of you will get back your own property/Kumpi David’ ~ a kemte ahi uh hi | they were the keepers of King David’s property/~ tampi tawh amaute paikhia ding uh hi | they will come out with great possessions) (s:neihlelam/hauhna) (b:neih) (r:42.5.28/3.25.13/13.27.31/1.15.14) (q:draft)
neihsak = (t:v) (w:let have/give/provide) (d:neih have with the causative sak: cause or allow someone to have) (e:meihal biakna kote nong ~ kul hi) (s:ngahsak) (b:neih) (r:2.10.25/19.137.9) (q:draft)
neihsakpa = (t:n) (w:one who deals out/one who makes have) (d:neihsak, cause to have, with pa marking a man: the man who does this to someone) (e:hong ~ in lungdamna ngah ta hen) (b:neihsak) (r:19.137.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
neihsate = (t:n) (w:possessions/wealth/property/goods) (d:neihsa, property, with the plural te: the things a person owns, his goods and wealth) (e:Na ~ leh na anpalte tawh/a ~ kip lo ding hi | his wealth will not endure/amau’ ~ tam lua hi | their possessions were too many/Inn leh ~ in pate tung panin a kiluah | houses and wealth are inherited from fathers) (s:hauhnate) (b:neihsa) (r:20.3.9/18.15.29/1.36.7/20.19.14) (q:draft)
neihsateng = (t:n) (w:all possessions/all one has/whole property) (d:neihsa possessions with teng all) (e:a ~ a uk dingin/a nauzawpa in ama ~ zuakin | the younger son sold all he had/Namdangte in a ~ a puakkhiat ni-in | on the day foreigners carried off all his wealth/a ~ a nasemte’ kep dingin a ap hi | he entrusted all his property to his servants) (b:neihsa) (r:42.16.1/31.1.11/42.15.13/40.25.14) (q:draft)
neihse = (t:v) (w:take/marry) (d:seen once in pasal a neihse sangin, rather than taking a husband; neih have with se, whose force is unclear) (e:pasal a ~ sangin tuaci om leh) (r:46.7.40) (q:draft, low confidence)
neihsuak = (t:v) (w:own permanently/own outright) (d:neih, own, with suak, through to the end: have for good) (e:~ dingin leitang kizuak lo ding hi) (r:3.25.23) (q:draft)
neihsun = (t:adj) (w:only/sole) (d:the only one that a person has, as an only son; a neihsun teng is the little that one has) (e:Tapa khat ~ sih suah bangin/a nu’ tanu ~ hi a | she is her mother’s only daughter/ka nu leh ka pa’ tapa ~ | the only son of my mother and father/ama ta khat ~ ahi hi | she was his only child) (r:24.6.26/20.19.4/22.6.9/20.4.3/7.11.34) (q:draft)
neihsunte = (t:n) (w:only possessions/the little one has) (d:neihsun the only one that a person has, with plural te) (e:Mi tagahte’ la ~ guksak uh a/Na ~ nangawn uh inn na tun’pih uh hangin | though you brought home even the little you had) (b:neihsun) (r:18.24.3/37.1.9) (q:draft)
neihte = (t:n) (w:possessions/what one has/things had) (d:the things someone has, of goods and also of plans or disputes; thu neihte are cases people have) (e:nang’ ~ nangma adingin kem in/gamlak-a na ~ khempeuh | everything you have in the field/Na sanggamte uh thu ~ za un la | hear the cases that your brothers have/na kham ~ leivui bang lelin ngaihsunin | counting the gold you have as mere dust) (b:neih) (r:1.33.9/24.29.11/2.9.19/5.1.16/18.22.24) (q:draft)
neihteng = (t:n) (w:all that one has/everything owned) (d:neih have with teng all of: the whole of what is had, placed after the thing owned) (e:vangliatna le aana a ~ uh/na aana ~ khempeuh zang kawm in | use all the authority you have/a an ~ khempeuh uh laksak | taking away all the grain they have) (s:neihzah) (b:neih) (r:66.17.13/30.5.11/56.2.15) (q:draft)
neihtheih = (t:v) (w:be able to have/can have) (d:neih, have, with theih, be able; often followed by nading, so that one may have) (e:Sarah a ta ~ ding hun beikhin napi-in/suanlekhak a ~ ma-un | before they can have offspring/na kisap khempeuh uh na ~ nading uh | so that you may have all you need/lungdamna cingtaak a ~ nadingun | so that they may have full joy) (b:neih) (r:58.11.11/47.9.8/28.9.12/43.17.13) (q:draft)
neihtheihna = (t:n) (d:neihtheih, be able to have, with the noun suffix na; with ding it means so that one may have) (e:lungnopna na ~ dingun hih thu/gamtat hoih a ~ dingun | so that they may have good conduct) (b:neihtheih) (r:43.16.33/56.3.8) (q:draft)
neihthuah = (t:v) (w:have in addition/have more besides) (d:neih have with thuah, add on top) (e:zong na ~ theih nadingun) (r:47.9.8) (q:draft)
neihtuam = (t:n) (w:special possession/treasured possession/very own) (d:neih possess with tuam apart: what is owned specially and set apart as one's own) (e:Topa’ ~ hong suakkik ding a/keima ~ taktak mite hi ding uh hi | they will be my very own people/ama hong ~ dingin | to make us his very own) (r:38.2.12/39.3.17/56.2.14) (q:draft)
neihval = (t:n) (w:surplus/abundance/wealth) (d:what one has over and above one's needs, from neih have and val excess) (e:a ~ a lamval sung panun) (r:41.12.44) (q:draft)
neihzah = (t:n) (w:all that one has/as much as one has) (d:neih, form of nei, have, with zah, amount: the whole amount that one has; a aw neihzah tawh is at the top of his voice, na tha neihzah tawh with all your strength) (e:na tha ~ tawh sem in/a aw ~ tawh Paul kiko a | Paul shouted at the top of his voice/na ~ uh tawh lungkim un | be content with what you have/sathau na ~ uh sung pan | out of the oil that you have) (s:neihteng) (r:21.9.10/44.16.28/58.13.5/26.45.14) (q:draft)
neihzawh = (t:v) (w:attain/manage to have) (d:neih have with zawh be able, come to possess) (e:lungnemna na ~ nadingin hanciam in) (r:54.6.11) (q:draft)
neikha = (t:v) (w:have/have a share in) (d:nei have with kha, which marks that the act reaches its object; in the verses always negated, not have at all, and ngaihsutin neikha lo is not even have in mind) (e:nuntakna ~ het lo uh hi/siatna, ngaihsutin zong ka ~ kei ding hi | I will not even have evil in mind/amaute in ngaihsutin ~ lo uh hi | they do not even consider it/hauhnate muan le suanin ~ loin | without putting their trust in riches) (r:49.4.18/19.101.4/28.7.2/54.6.17) (q:draft)
neikhawm = (t:v) (w:have together/share/hold in common) (d:have two or more things at once, or own something jointly with others) (e:a neih khempeuh uh a ~ uh hi/a gik leh a zang, na ~ kei ding | you shall not have both a heavy and a light one/nupi sagih in papi khat ~ ding uh a | seven women will share one man/Pa leh Tapa a nihin a ~ hi | he has both the Father and the Son/a neihsate uh zong a ~ uh hi | they also held their possessions in common) (b:nei) (r:44.4.32/63.1.9/5.25.13/23.4.1/44.2.44) (q:draft)
neikhin = (t:v) (w:already have/have already) (d:nei have with khin already) (e:thukimna ~ uh ahih manin/sum tulkhat ~ hi lo ahi hiam | does he not already have a thousand coins/Na deih khempeuh uh ~ na kisa uh a | you think you already have all you want/Pasian’ Tapa Jesuh ~ ihih manin | since we already have Jesus the Son of God) (b:nei) (r:43.9.22/42.19.25/58.4.14/46.4.8) (q:draft)
neikik = (t:v) (w:have again/get back/regain) (d:nei have with kik again) (e:tapa sagih le tanu thum ~ a/mizawngte in lametna ~ uh a | the poor have hope again/nang, zi-in kong ~ ding a | I will take you as my wife again/teh le gah hong ~ ding uh a | they will again bear leaves and fruit) (s:ngahkik) (b:nei) (r:18.42.13/28.2.19/18.5.16/26.36.8) (q:draft)
neikim = (t:v) (w:have in full/have every one) (d:nei have with kim complete, have all of something) (e:siamna nam khempeuh na ~ uh hi) (r:46.1.5) (q:draft)
neilai = (t:v) (w:still have/have besides/also have) (d:nei have with lai still or more) (e:tanu le tapa dang ~ hi/khat in ukna aana ~ a | one still holds the power to rule/tanu khat zong amah in ~ hi | he also had a daughter/hun tomno bek a ~ ahihlam | that he has only a short time left) (r:1.11.25/66.12.12/66.17.10/13.3.9) (q:draft)
neilo = (t:v) (w:not have/lack/be without) (d:nei have with the negative lo, written as one word; usually written nei lo) (e:mawh ~ mite na mawhsak kei ding uh hi/To ~ na hih uh hangin | though you are people without a master/pumpi tung poina ~ | without any defect of the body/a kalhna siktawn lah ~ uh a | and they have no bars) (s:tasam) (a:nei) (b:nei) (r:40.12.7/27.5.23/60.2.16/27.1.4/24.49.31) (q:draft)
neilote = (t:n) (w:those who do not have/those without) (d:neilo, not have, with the plural te; pa neilote is the fatherless) (e:A ~ kiang pan a neihsa/Minam dangte, pa ~ leh meigongte | foreigners, the fatherless and widows) (a:neisate) (b:neilo) (r:40.13.12/24.22.3) (q:draft)
neinu = (t:n) (w:woman who has) (d:nei have with the female suffix nu; nin a neinu is a woman who has uncleanness, a woman in her monthly period) (e:nin a ~ ading zong ahi hi) (b:nei) (r:3.15.33) (q:draft)
neipa = (t:n) (w:owner/possessor) (d:the man who has or owns something; ta a neipa is the father of a child) (e:Ta hoih a ~ in a lungdam ding/a ~' tungah amah in ditkikna bawl ding hi | he must make restitution to its owner/inn ~ pai-in siampipa kiangah | the owner of the house goes to the priest/lo ~ a tun’ ciangin | when the owner of the field comes) (s:teekpa) (b:nei) (r:20.23.24/2.22.12/3.14.35/40.21.40) (q:draft)
neipah = (t:v) (w:have at once/hold immediately) (d:nei have or hold with pah at once, said here of holding a meeting) (e:kikhopna ~ uh a) (r:41.3.6) (q:draft)
neisa = (t:adj) (w:having/possessing) (d:nei have with sa already; pasal neisa numei is a woman who has a husband, zi neisa a man who has a wife) (e:pasal ~ numei khatpeuh hangin/zi ~-in hong pai leh | if he comes having a wife/A ~ mipa tungah Pasian in piathuah ding a | God will give more to the one who has) (b:nei) (r:3.21.4/2.21.3/41.4.25) (q:draft)
neisak = (t:v) (w:given/give/grant) (d:nei, have, with the causative sak: cause someone to have, give; ta neisak is give a child) (e:Topa in amah ta ~ lo ahih manin/hih numei tawh nang ta hong ~ hi | he gives you children by this woman/suan-le-khak tampi kong ~ ding hi | I will give you many descendants/A zite uh ta ~ kei inla | do not let their wives have children) (b:nei) (r:9.1.5/9.2.20/1.17.6/24.18.21) as in God has given
neisak = (t:v) (w:have/let have/cause to have) (d:nei, have, with the causative sak: let or make someone have a thing, as power, hope or a desire) (e:tungah ukna ~ ni/a deih khempeuh ~ napi-in | though he lets them have all they desire/vangliatna lianpi ~ a | he gave him great power/lametna lianpi hong ~ | it gives us great hope/Mawh bawlnopna lungsim hong ~ kei inla | do not let me have a heart that wants to do wrong) (b:nei) (r:1.1.26/21.6.2/44.6.8/45.5.4/19.141.4) as in let them have
neisate = (t:n) (w:those who have/the ones who have) (d:nei have with sa already and plural te; said of spouses it means the married) (e:a ~ tungah kipia thuahin/zilepasal ~ tawh mawhnopna | adultery with married people/a ~ kipiathuah ding a | those who have will be given more/A ~ tungah, kei’ ngaihsutna hi lo | to the married, not my own judgment) (a:neilote) (b:neisa) (r:40.13.12/46.7.10/41.7.21/40.25.29) (q:draft)
neisun = (t:v) (w:have/happen to have) (d:nei, have, with sun; in the verse, should one have any at all) (e:Mavanna khatpeuh ~ leng zong) (r:18.10.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
neita = (t:v) (w:got/be given/now have) (d:nei, have, with ta, which marks a new state: now have, have come to have) (e:Levi mite khat ka ~ hi/a mi thak ngeina a ~ ahi hi | he now has the new way of life/luttheih nading thu i ~ hi | we now have the right to enter/vasa namkim in omna-in ~ uh hi | every kind of bird now has it as a dwelling) (b:nei) (r:7.17.13/47.5.17/58.10.19/66.18.2) taken or given by someone
neita = (t:v) (w:earn) (e:pilna ~) (b:nei)
neitawm = (t:v) (w:have of one's own accord) (d:nei have with tawm by oneself, have without being told) (e:huhnopna lungsim ~ ahih manin) (r:47.8.17) (q:draft)
neite = (t:det) (w:those have got/those who have) (d:nei, have, with the plural te: those who have something; mawh neite is sinners) (e:pasal leh zi ~/A ~ kipia beh ding a | those who have will be given more/ganhing a ~’ pian’na pupi ahi hi | he was the ancestor of those who keep livestock/leitung mawh ~ a susia dingin | to destroy the sinners of the land/phe leh lip a ~ peuhmah | any that have fins and scales) (b:nei) (r:40.13.12/1.4.20/23.13.9/3.11.9)
neithakte = (t:n) (w:newlyweds) (d:those who have newly taken, from nei have, thak new and plural te; pasal neithakte are brides, women who have newly taken a husband) (e:pasal ~’ awte ka gingsak nawn) (r:24.16.9) (q:draft)
neithuah = (t:v) (w:have in addition/have besides/have more) (d:nei, have, with thuah, in addition) (e:tampi tak ka ~ hi/thudang bang ~ nawn ding ka hi hiam | what further matter do I still have) (r:21.2.7/10.19.28) (q:draft)
neizaw = (t:v) (w:have more/have greater) (d:nei have with zaw more, used with sangin than) (e:vangliatna a ~ ding hi/note sangin tam ka ~ uh hi | we have more than you/Gentail mite sangin bang hamphatna ~ a | what advantage do they have over the Gentiles) (b:nei) (r:47.3.11/10.19.43/45.3.1) (q:draft)
neizo = (t:v) (w:be able to have/manage to have/have obtained) (d:nei have with zo, which marks ability or completion; thu neizo lo is have no force) (e:ka deih zahzah zong ka ~ hi/amah zahin vang a ~ kei ding uh hi | they will not manage to have power like his/Leinuai tawh thukimna khat i ~ hi | we have reached an agreement with the world below/Thukham in thu ~ loin | the law has no force) (b:nei) (r:21.2.8/35.1.4/27.11.4/23.28.15) (q:draft)
nek = (t:v) (w:to eat/eat) (d:form of ne, eat, used before ding, theih and nading) (e:~ dinga a hoih singkung nam khempeuh/~ ding sa tampi ka nei hi | I have much meat to eat/Note theih loh an ~ ding ka nei hi | I have food to eat that you do not know/na ~ theih ding uh ganhingte | the animals that you may eat) (b:ne) (r:1.2.9/20.7.14/43.4.32/5.14.4)
nek = (t:v) (w:ate/eaten) (d:form of ne, eat, used in relative and time clauses, as with lai takin, while, and khit ciangin, after) (e:amaute in a ~ lai takun/Izipt ah man pia loin i ~ ngasate | the fish we ate in Egypt at no cost/inn sungah an a ~ lai takin | while he was eating in the house/tuate a ~ khit ciangun | after they had eaten them) (b:ne) (r:1.18.8/1.41.21/4.11.5/40.9.10)
nekbaang = (t:n) (w:leavings/remains of a kill) (d:what is left from the eating of another, here an animal torn and partly eaten by wild beasts) (e:gamsate’ ~ ahi zongin ka ne) (r:26.4.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
nekha = (t:v) (w:eat/get to eat) (d:ne eat with kha, which marks that the act reaches its object, eat any of something; na nekha kei ding is you will not get to eat it) (e:nang in na ~ kei ding hi/bang khat peuhpeuh a ~ mi peuhmah | anyone who eats anything at all/na khamtakun na ~ kei ding uh hi | you will not get to eat your fill) (r:12.7.19/3.23.29/28.9.2) (q:draft)
nekhawm = (t:v) (w:eat together/eat with/dine with) (d:ne eat with khawm together) (e:amau tawh an a ~ hi/amau tawh ~ dawnkhawm dingin | to eat and drink together with them/Bawngpi leh vompi in an ~ ding uh a | the cow and the bear will feed together/Saul in Samuel tawh an ~ hi | Saul ate with Samuel) (s:nekpih) (b:ne) (r:42.15.2/20.23.1/24.16.8/23.11.7/9.9.24) (q:draft)
nekhawmin = (t:v) (w:eating together) (d:nekhawm, eat together, with in, linking to the next verb; an nekhawm renders breaking bread) (e:amaute tawh an ~/a innte uhah an ~ | eating together in their homes) (b:nekhawm) (r:44.2.42/44.2.46) (q:draft)
nekhawmte = (t:n) (w:those eating together/dinner guests) (d:nekhawm eat together with plural te) (e:amah tawh an a ~ a nuam) (b:nekhawm) (r:41.6.22) (q:draft)
nekik = (t:v) (w:eat again/return to eat) (d:ne eat with kik again or back) (e:Ui in a luak ~ hi) (b:ne) (r:61.2.22) (q:draft)
nekin = (t:v) (w:eating/as food) (d:nek, form of ne, eat, with in: note’ nekin is as food for you, uang nekin is eating to excess) (e:uang ~ na noptat mahmah uh hi/note’ ~ ka omsak nawn kei ding hi | I will no longer let them be food for you) (b:nek) (r:59.5.5/26.34.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
nekkhak = (t:v) (w:eat by mistake/eat unintentionally/swallow by accident) (d:nek, form of ne, eat, with khak, happen to) (e:an khat peuhpeuh a ~ leh) (r:3.22.14/20.23.7) (q:draft)
nekkhawm = (t:v) (w:eat together) (d:nek eat with khawm together) (e:an a ~ laitakun/note tawh an a ~ a dawn khawm | eating and drinking together with you/Tua banga ~ ding pen | to eat together in that way) (s:nekpih) (b:nek) (r:24.41.1/65.1.12/1.43.32) (q:draft)
nekkhawm = (t:n) (w:shared meal/common meal) (d:a meal eaten together, used of the Lord's Supper) (e:~ ne dingin na kikhop uh/~ bawlna-ah leenggahzu hangin | over the wine at the shared meal) (s:nekkhawmna) (r:46.11.33/46.10.16) (q:draft)
nekkhawmna = (t:n) (w:shared meal/supper/communion) (d:eating together; Topa’ Nekkhawmna is the Lord's Supper) (e:~ ne dingin na pai uh ciangin/dawi tawh ~ hai sung panin | from the cup of fellowship with demons/~ a bawl dingin note na kikhop uh ciangin | when you gather to hold the shared meal) (b:nekkhawm) (r:46.11.21/46.11.20/46.10.21) (q:draft)
Nekkhawmna = (t:n) (w:Supper/shared meal) (d:eating together; Topa’ Nekkhawmna is the Lord's Supper) (e:Topa’ ~ a ne dingin) (b:nekkhawmna) (r:46.11.20) (q:draft)
nekkhit = (t:v) (w:finish eating/have eaten) (d:nek eat with khit finish; with ciangin, after eating) (e:an a ~ ciangin a tha hong hatkik hi/An a ~ uh ciangin Jesuh in Simon Peter kiangah | when they had finished eating, Jesus said to Simon Peter/nitak an a ~ uh ciangin hai la a | after supper he took the cup/ka ~ ciangin ka gil sung thuk velvalsak hi | when I had eaten it, it turned my stomach sour) (r:44.9.19/42.22.20/43.21.15/46.11.25/66.10.10) (q:draft)
nekkhop = (t:v) (w:eat together/eat with) (d:form of nekhawm used before ding and ut) (e:note tawh ~ ka ut mahmah hi/hih Paisan Pawi an i ~ ding ka ut mahmah | I greatly want us to eat this Passover meal together) (s:nekpih) (r:42.22.15) (q:draft)
nekkhopna = (t:n) (w:eating together) (d:nekkhop eat together with the noun suffix na) (e:Jesuh in an a ~ Farisi mite) (b:nekkhop) (r:41.2.16) (q:draft)
