Nergal = (t:name) (w:Nergal) (d:god worshipped by the people of Kuthah whom the king of Assyria settled in Samaria) (r:12.17.30)
Nergalsharezer = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Nergal-Sharezer) (d:name of two officials of the king of Babylon who sat in the Middle Gate when Jerusalem fell) (r:24.39.3/24.39.13)
Neri = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Neri) (d:ancestor of Jesus in the genealogy of Luke, son of Melki and father of Shealtiel) (e:Shealtiel in ~’ ta hi) (r:42.3.27/42.3.28) (q:draft)
Neriah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Neriah) (d:son of Mahseiah and father of Baruch, the scribe of Jeremiah, and of Seraiah) (r:24.32.16/24.36.8)
nesak = (t:v) (w:feed/give to eat/make eat/let eat) (d:ne eat with the causative sak: give someone something to eat, make someone eat, or allow someone to eat) (e:an kha a hong ~ hi/Tua meh san tawm khat hong ~ in | let me eat some of that red stew/amau’ satak mah ka ~ ding a | I will make them eat their own flesh/migilote a duh uh ~ lo hi | he does not let the wicked eat what they crave/anteh bek hong ~ in la | give us only vegetables to eat) (s:neksak) (b:ne) (r:25.3.15/24.19.9/1.25.30/23.49.26/20.10.3/27.1.12) (q:draft)
nesakin = (t:v) (w:feeding/serving food/making eat) (d:ne eat with causative sak and the linking ending in; also let something be eaten, as crops by blight) (e:amaute amau guakin ~/Milim biakna ante ~, nulepa paktatna piangsak a | making them eat food offered to idols and leading them into sexual sin) (b:nesak) (r:1.43.32/66.2.14) (q:draft)
nesim = (t:v) (w:eat secretly) (d:ne, eat, with sim, secretly) (e:amah in tuate ~ ding hi) (s:neksim) (r:5.28.57/5.28.56) (q:draft)
nesuak = (t:v) (w:enjoy/eat the fruit of) (d:ne eat with suak, come to eat or enjoy what one has worked for) (e:nate lungdamin ~ ding uh hi) (r:23.65.22) (q:draft, low confidence)
Netaim = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Netaim) (d:town in Judah where potters lived who worked for the king) (r:13.4.23)
netcip = (t:v) (w:press down/crush) (d:press tightly under a weight, as a loaded cart does) (e:bawngleeng a ~ suk bangin) (s:nengcip) (r:30.2.13) (q:draft)
netcipsuk = (t:v) (w:crush down/press down) (d:netcip press tightly with suk downward) (e:a pua bawngleeng a ~ bangin) (s:nengcipsuk) (b:netcip) (r:30.2.13) (q:draft)
nete = (t:n) (w:eaters/those who eat) (d:ne eat or drink with -te, the ones who do so, usually after a; zu ne nete are those who keep drinking wine) (e:keimah hong ~ in kei hangin a nungta ding/hih khomun a ~ in a nungta tawntung ding | those who eat this bread will live forever/Leenggah thuk a ~’ ha bek a kim ding | only the teeth of those who eat sour grapes will be set on edge/Zu ne ~ tawh kikhawl kei in la | do not keep company with those who drink too much wine) (b:ne) (r:43.6.57/20.23.20/43.6.58/24.31.30) (q:draft)
neteng = (t:n) (w:all who eat) (d:ne eat with teng all, everyone who eats) (e:a ~ hong ninsak ding hi) (b:ne) (r:28.9.4) (q:draft)
Nethanel = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Nethanel) (d:name of several men, among them the son of Zuar, leader of the tribe of Issachar in the wilderness, and the fourth son of Jesse) (r:4.7.18/13.2.14)
Nethaniah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Nethaniah) (d:name of several men, among them the father of Ishmael who killed Gedaliah, a son of Asaph, and the father of Jehudi) (r:24.41.15/24.41.12)
Nethanniah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Nethaniah) (d:spelling of Nethaniah in this verse, the father of Ishmael who killed Gedaliah) (r:24.41.9)
nethei = (t:v) (w:can eat/may eat) (d:ne, eat, with thei, be able or be allowed to) (e:singkung khempeuh na ~ ding hi/Antak ~ nai loin nawi bek a ~ lai | not yet able to eat solid food, still able to take only milk/na ututun na ~ ding uh hi | you may eat as you wish) (s:nektheih/nezo) (b:ne) (r:1.2.16/58.5.12/46.10.25) (q:draft)
netniam = (t:v) (w:oppress) (d:press down, treat harshly and unjustly; also written nengniam and nenniam) (e:Egypt-te in amaute a ~ uh ciangin) (s:nengniam/nenniam) (r:9.12.8) (q:draft)
netniamna = (t:n) (w:oppression) (d:netniam, oppress, with the noun suffix na: the act of oppressing or the state of being oppressed; netniamna thuak is suffer oppression) (e:Judah mite in ~ a thuak uh a/~ le ngong hihna panin amaute a honkhia hi | he rescues them from oppression and violence/Izipt mite in amaute a ~ ka mu khin | I have seen how the Egyptians oppress them/~ a thuakte a’ dingin munkip hi a | he is a stronghold for the oppressed) (s:nenniamna/kinetniamna) (b:netniam) (r:24.50.33/2.3.9/19.72.14/19.9.9) (q:draft)
netniamnate = (t:n) (w:oppressions) (d:netniamna oppression with plural te) (e:hong ~ uh a mu hi) (s:nenniamnate) (b:netniamna) (r:5.26.7) (q:draft)
Netofah = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Netofah/Netophah) (d:town near Bethlehem in Judah, home of Maharai and Heled, two of the mighty warriors of David) (r:10.23.28/13.27.13)
netum = (t:v) (w:devour/eat up/consume) (d:ne eat with tum, wholly: eat something completely, said of animals, of enemies and of anything that consumes a person) (e:gamsa khat in amah ~ khin zo hi/an nek bang a ka mite a ~ | they devour my people as if eating bread/Ka mite’ sa na ~ uh hi | you eat the flesh of my people/ka deih luatna in kei hong ~ ding hi | my zeal will consume me/a ~ dingin hong pai un | come to devour) (s:nektum/nemang/valhtum) (r:1.37.33/1.41.20/19.14.4/33.3.3/43.2.17/23.56.9) (q:draft)
netumin = (t:v) (w:devouring/eating up/consuming) (d:netum devour, with the linking ending in, eating up and then the next action follows) (e:a hut in amah ~ a si hi/kote hong ~ suksiat ding a vaihawmpa | the man who consumed us and planned to destroy us) (b:netum) (r:44.12.23/10.21.5) (q:draft)
netummang = (t:v) (w:eat up completely/devour) (d:netum eat up with mang away, eat until nothing is left) (e:theikungteng khempeuh ~ khin uh hi) (r:29.1.7) (q:draft)
netumte = (t:n) (w:devourers/those who eat up) (d:netum eat up with plural te, those who have eaten something bare) (e:Leenggui lo a ~, note na hi uh) (b:netum) (r:23.3.14) (q:draft)
neu = (t:adj) (w:small) (d:not large in size, amount or importance; a neu a lian means small and great, everyone) (e:a lian leh a ~/puantual ~ khat bawlin | making a little robe/inndei ~ khat bawlin | making a small room/A ~ mahmah ganhing nam li leitungah om a | there are four very small creatures on earth) (s:neuno) (a:lian/gol) (r:5.25.14/20.30.24/9.2.19/12.4.10) as in appearance
neu = (t:adj) (w:tiny) (e:kimkhat a ~ mahmahin na satnen ding a | you shall grind some of it very fine) (s:neucik/neuno) (r:2.30.36)
neu = (t:adj) (w:mini) as in products
neu = (t:adj) (w:little) (d:small in degree or importance, as little faith or a small matter) (e:Upna ~ mite aw/a thukhenna thu ~ ka sa hi | I count that judgment a small matter/moh ~ khat hong bawlsak masa-in | first make me a little loaf) (a:lian) (r:40.16.8/46.4.3/11.17.13)
neu = (t:adj) (w:sloping/narrow) (d:too small in width or room: narrow, of a road or a blanket; cramped, of a place to live) (e:lam ~ a, mi tawmcik a lut uh hi | the road is narrow and only a few enter/silh dingin puanza ~ lua | the blanket is too narrow to wrap in/kote’ adingin ~ lua hi | it is too small for us) (s:kawcik) (a:zai) (r:40.7.14/23.28.20/12.6.1)
neubawl = (t:v) (w:make small/bring low) (d:neu small with bawl make; reduce to nothing) (e:~ gawp ding hi) (s:neusak) (b:neu) (r:36.2.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
neubel = (t:adj) (w:least/smallest) (d:neu, small, with bel, most) (e:a ~ akipan a golbel dongin/a ~ sawltak ka hi a | I am the least of the apostles) (s:neupen) (a:golbel/lianbel) (r:58.8.11/46.15.9) (q:draft)
neucik = (t:adj) (w:tiny/very small/little) (d:neu, small, with cik, very: very small, of little size or worth) (e:letsong ~ khat hangin) (s:neuno) (a:lianpi) (r:20.28.21) (q:draft)
neucil = (t:n) (w:childhood/early youth) (d:the earliest part of life, when a person is still small: neu, small, with cil, beginning; a neucil panin is from childhood) (e:a ~ panin gilo hi) (s:neutung/neulai) (r:1.8.21) (q:draft)
neukha = (t:adv) (w:a little/a bit/slightly) (d:to a small amount or degree; neukha beek with a negative means not even a little, not at all, and neukha bek is only a little) (e:Kilamdan’na ~ beek a om kei hi/Ka haina ~ note in na thuak le-uh | if you would put up with a little of my foolishness/~ bek a neuzaw ka hi kei hi | I am not even a little inferior/vantungmite nuai-ah a ~ na nuaikhiat zo hi | you made him a little lower than the angels) (s:zek/themcik) (r:45.3.22/47.11.1/47.11.5/58.2.7) (q:draft)
neulai = (t:n) (w:youth/childhood) (d:the time when a person is small or young: neu, small, with lai, the time when; neulai a kipan is from youth on) (e:i ~ akipan tu ni ciang dong/Ka ~ a kipan tuni dong | from my youth until this day/ka ~ huna ka gamtatna | what I did in the time of my youth/Naupang khat a ~-in lampi man tawnsak lecin | if you set a child on the right way while he is young) (s:neutung/neucil/khangnolai) (a:khanghamna) (r:24.3.25/20.22.6/9.12.2/18.13.26) (q:draft)
neulua = (t:adj) (w:too small) (d:neu, small, with lua, too much: too small for what is needed or for the people who use it) (e:note a dingin ~ ahih ciangin/kote’ tenna mun kote a dingin ~ hi | the place where we live is too small for us/sumngo biakna tau ~ ahih manin | because the bronze altar was too small) (a:lianlua) (b:neu) (r:6.17.15/12.6.1/11.8.64) (q:draft)
neuna = (t:n) (w:smallness/small size) (d:neu, small, with the noun suffix na: how small something is; a golna leh a neuna is its size, whether large or small) (e:a golna leh a ~ tawh kizui-in) (a:golna) (b:neu) (r:16.12.44) (q:draft)
neuneu = (t:adj) (w:small/little) (d:neu, small, doubled: said of several things that are each small; inndei neuneu are small side rooms) (e:biakinn kimkotah inndei ~ om a) (a:lian) (r:26.41.5) (q:draft)
neuneute = (t:adj) (w:small/minor/trivial) (d:neuneu, small, said of several things, with the plural te; thu neuneute are small matters) (e:no’ thu ~ leltak na khentheih) (a:liante) (b:neuneu) (r:46.6.3) (q:draft)
neuno = (t:adj) (w:small/little/tiny) (d:neu, small, with the diminutive no: small or slight; na neuno khat is a small thing or a small request) (e:na ~ khat nget ding ka nei hi/mei-ek ~ khat pan kipanin | starting from one small spark/nangma mit-ah na ~ khat hi lai hi | in your eyes this is still a small thing/I pumpi na sung panin a ~ khat hinapi-in | though it is a small one among the parts of our body) (a:lian/gol) (b:neu) (r:11.2.20/59.3.5/10.7.19/59.3.6) (q:draft)
neupa = (t:n) (w:one who is small/man of little) (d:neu, small, with the male suffix pa: a man who is small in something; upna neupa is a man of little faith) (e:Upna ~ aw, bang hangin um khial) (b:neu) (r:40.14.31) (q:draft)
neupen = (t:adj) (w:smallest/least/youngest) (d:neu, small, with pen, most: the smallest of all, the least in rank, or the youngest) (e:tang khempeuh lakah a ~ hi/a lianpen in a ~ bangin om ta hen | let the greatest be like the youngest/a golpen pana kipan a ~ dongin | from the greatest to the least/a tapa ~ Jehoahaz simloh | except Jehoahaz, his youngest son) (s:neubel/ngekpen) (a:lianpen/golpen) (b:neu) (r:41.4.31/42.22.26/32.3.5/14.21.17) (q:draft)
neupente = (t:n) (w:the smallest/the least/the lowliest) (d:neupen, smallest, with the plural te: those who are smallest or lowest of all, whether people or things) (e:a ~ nangawn kumpi a suaksak thei/a ~ milianpi suak ding hi | the smallest will become a mighty people/hih thukhamte lakpan a ~ khat bek | even one of the least of these commands) (a:lianpente) (b:neupen) (r:27.4.17/23.60.22/40.5.19) (q:draft)
neusak = (t:v) (w:make small/humble/bring low) (d:neu, small, with the causative sak: make small in number, or bring low in standing) (e:minamte lakah note kong ~ ding a/kiphasak-a gamtate a ~ hi | he humbles those who walk in pride/gamdangte sangin nang kong ~ zaw a | I will make you smaller than the other nations/ka ~ kei ding hi | I will not make them small) (s:neubawl/niamsak/niamkhiat) (a:liansak/liatsak) (b:neu) (r:31.1.2/27.4.37/24.49.15/24.30.19) (q:draft)
neuseekin = (t:v) (w:making smaller) (d:reducing the size of something, here a measure for grain, with the linking suffix in) (e:I antehna seu ~ sum tampi) (r:30.8.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
neuta = (t:v) (w:become small/be brought low) (d:neu, small, with ta, marking a change of state: become small, be brought low from a high standing) (e:miliante hong ~ ding hi) (s:kiniam) (a:liat) (b:neu) (r:26.21.26) (q:draft)
neute = (t:adj) (w:small/little) (d:neu, small, with the plural te, said of several things: khua neute are villages, ta neute little children, thu neute small matters) (e:a khuapite leh a khua ~ tawh/inn ~ kisatnen ding hi | the small houses will be smashed to bits/a ta ~ leh a ganhingte | their little children and their livestock/thu ~ tungah diktat na hih maninah | because you have been faithful in small matters) (a:liante) (b:neu) (r:6.15.45/62.5.21/30.6.11/7.18.21/42.19.17) (q:draft)
neuto = (t:adj) (w:smaller upward/narrowing) (d:neu small with to upward, becoming smaller level by level going up) (e:a nuai-ate sangin ~ zaw tektek hi) (b:neu) (r:26.42.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
neutung = (t:n) (w:childhood/infancy) (d:the time when a person was small: neu, small, with tung, the time of; ka neutung a kipanin is since I was a child) (e:ka ~ a kipanin hih thukhamte/Lai Siangtho pen na ~ a kipanin a theisa | the Holy Scriptures, known to you since childhood/A ~ a kipan ahi hi | it has been so since his childhood) (s:neulai/neucil) (r:41.10.20/55.3.15/41.9.21) (q:draft)
neuzaw = (t:adj) (w:smaller/lesser/inferior) (d:neu, small, with zaw, more: smaller or lesser than another, also lower in rank; what it is compared with is followed by sangin, than) (e:khuavak ~ pen zan a uk dingin/Note sangin ka ~ tuan kei hi | I am not inferior to you/a nuai-ate sangin ~ hi | they were smaller than the lower ones/nang sanga ~ kumpi gam adang khat | another kingdom, inferior to yours) (a:lianzaw/golzaw) (b:neu) (r:1.1.16/18.13.2/26.42.5/27.2.39)
neuzawte = (t:n) (w:lesser ones/smaller ones/the least) (d:neuzaw smaller, lesser, with the plural te: those who are lesser in rank or strength) (e:a ~ in zakhat val/A lianzawte in a ~ thupha a na piakna | the blessing of the lesser by the greater) (a:lianzawte/golzawte) (b:neuzaw) (r:13.12.14/58.7.7) (q:draft)
Neziah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Neziah) (d:ancestor of a family of temple servants who returned from the exile with Zerubbabel) (r:15.2.54/16.7.56)
Nezib = (t:name) (c:land/city) (w:Nezib) (d:town in the western foothills of Judah) (r:6.15.43)
nezo = (t:v) (w:be able to eat/manage to eat) (d:ne, eat, with zo, be able: be able to eat, mostly used with a negative) (e:an nangawn ka ~ kei hi/Note in antak ~ nai lo na hih manun | because you were not yet able to eat solid food) (b:ne) (r:19.102.4/46.3.2) (q:draft)
ng = (t:see) <na'ng>
nga = (t:num) (w:five) (d:the number five; it follows the thing that is counted, as in tul nga, five thousand) (e:ni ~/pasal bek tul ~ a pha hi | the men alone numbered five thousand/Nang in khuapi ~ na uk in | you take charge of five cities/amah in mi ~ la-in | he took five men) (r:41.6.44/26.41.9/42.19.19/1.47.2)
nga = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:fish) (d:a fish, as a living creature and as food; the fuller word is ngasa) (e:~ emsa tum khat a pia uh hi/ngen tawh ~ khuhin a om a mu hi | he saw them catching fish with a net/~ a hoihte teelin bawm sungah a guang uh hi | they picked out the good fish and put them in baskets) (s:ngasa) (r:42.24.42/40.4.18/40.13.48)
nga = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:bird) (e:~ bang leng) (s:va/vasa) usually found in lyric
ngaam = (t:v) (w:grow weak/waste away) (d:lose strength and waste away; in the verse it is said of the bones of a suffering person) (e:ka tha kiam a, ka guhte ~ hi) (r:19.31.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngabeng = (t:n) (w:fisherman) (d:a person who catches fish: nga, fish, with beng, hunt; compare sabeng, hunter) (e:~ tampi ka khah ding a/~ Peter a kici Simon le a nau Andru | the fishermen Simon called Peter and his brother Andrew) (r:24.16.16/40.4.18) (q:draft)
ngabengte = (t:n) (w:fishermen/fishers) (d:ngabeng, fisherman, with the plural te) (e:~ ahih uh ciangin tui sungah/~ in tui geiah kaikhia uh a | the fishermen pulled it up on the shore/~ thuumin tau ding uh a | the fishermen will groan and lament) (s:bengte) (b:ngabeng) (r:41.1.16/40.13.48/23.19.8) (q:draft)
ngah = (t:v) (w:receive/get/obtain) (d:come to have something that is given or gained, such as a blessing, an inheritance, wages or favour) (e:thupha ~ minam/Amaute in a ~ khit uh ciangin | when they had received it/Efraim mite in amau’ gamhluah ~ uh hi | the people of Ephraim received their inheritance/a gahte a ~ masapen ahi ding hi | he should be the first to receive the crops/Isaak in hehnepna ~ hi | Isaac received comfort) (a:pia) (r:40.20.11/6.16.4/55.2.6/1.24.67)
ngahbeh = (t:v) (w:receive as well/gain in addition) (d:ngah receive with beh in addition) (e:minphatna ~ hi) (s:ngahthuah) (r:10.23.18) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngahbuang = (t:v) (w:get at least) (d:ngah get with the limiting particle buang, get at least or after all) (e:naupangte’ khamvalteng ~ hi lo ahi hiam) (r:41.7.28) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngahin = (t:v) (w:receive/get/obtain/find) (d:ngah, receive or get, with the linking ending in: used when another verb follows, receiving something and then doing something else) (e:mite mai-ah maipha ~ na ma vang ding/Josef in ama’ mai-ah maipha ~ ama na sem a | Joseph found favour in his eyes and served him/a sihna uhah nopna ~ tawlnga uh hi | in their death they find peace and rest/kiphasak teng mah in thupha ~ nuamsa uh hi | it is the arrogant who get blessing and are happy) (b:ngah) (r:20.3.4/54.2.4/1.39.4/23.57.2/39.3.15) (q:draft)
ngahkhak = (t:v) (w:happen to get/incur) (d:ngah, get, with khak, by chance: come to get something unwanted; with loh nading, so as not to incur) (e:maizumna a ~ loh nadingun) (s:ngahlawh/tuaklawh/thuaklawh) (r:66.16.15) (q:draft)
ngahkhawm = (t:v) (w:receive together/share in/receive along with) (d:ngah, receive, with khawm, together: receive along with others, share in what they receive) (e:a bulpi le a meet ka ~ ding hi/amaute tawh tanh ~ ding hi | he is to receive a share together with them/Topa Jesuh Khrih tawh minthanna na ~ theih nadingun | so that you may share in the glory with the Lord Jesus Christ/a tapate tawh gamh ~ uh hi | they received an inheritance together with the sons) (b:ngah) (r:40.25.27/5.18.8/53.2.14/6.17.6) (q:draft)
ngahkhin = (t:v) (w:have received/have already received) (d:ngah, receive, with khin, already done) (e:nopsakna ~ na hih manun/a ciamsa Kha Siangtho zong a ~ hi | he has also received the promised Holy Spirit) (s:ngahkhit/sankhit) (b:ngah) (r:42.6.24/44.2.33) (q:draft)
ngahkhit = (t:v) (w:have received) (d:ngah, receive, with khit, finish: have received; ngahkhit ciangin is after receiving) (e:thu a ~ ciangin Damaskas khua-ah) (s:ngahkhin/sankhit) (r:44.9.14) (q:draft)
ngahkhop = (t:v) (w:receive together/share in) (d:form of ngahkhawm, receive together with others) (e:Khrih hangin a ~ theihna uh ahi hi) (r:49.3.6) (q:draft)
ngahkik = (t:v) (w:regain/recover/get back/receive back) (d:ngah, get, with kik, again: get back what was lost, taken away or given up) (e:David in Amalek-te’ laksa khempeuh ~ a/ama vangliatna ~ lo hi | he did not regain his power/a zuaksa van ~ lo ding hi | he will not get back the goods he sold/sihna panin a tapa a ~ ahi hi | he received his son back from death) (s:neikik/lakik) (b:ngah) (r:9.30.18/14.13.20/26.7.13/58.11.19) (q:draft)
ngahkikin = (t:v) (w:getting back/recovering/receiving back) (d:ngahkik get back, with the linking ending in) (e:numeite leh mihingte ~ ciahpih hi/a nusiate in a zah zakhat ~ | those who have left them receiving back a hundred times as much/Note in nomau’ neihsa ciat ~ | each of you getting back your own property) (b:ngahkik) (r:1.14.16/3.25.10/40.19.29) (q:draft)
ngahkikna = (t:n) (w:regaining/recovery) (d:ngahkik get back, with the noun suffix na; a ngahkikna dingin is in order to regain) (e:a kumpi gam a ~ dingin/Israel a dingin a ~ | his recovering them for Israel) (b:ngahkik) (r:11.12.21/12.14.28) (q:draft)
ngahkim = (t:v) (w:all receive/receive in full) (d:ngah receive with kim complete, every one receives) (e:hotkhiatna a ~ uh ciangin) (r:45.11.12) (q:draft)
ngahlah = (t:v) (w:fail to obtain/fall short of) (d:ngah get with lah fail to) (e:Pasian’ hehpihna a ~ na hihkhak loh) (r:58.12.15) (q:draft)
ngahlai = (t:v) (w:receive besides/still receive) (d:ngah receive with lai still, further) (e:nuntak tawntungna ~ ding uh hi) (r:41.10.30) (q:draft)
ngahlawh = (t:v) (w:incur/get as a result/bring upon oneself) (d:ngah, receive, with lawh: receive trouble or harm as a consequence) (e:huhau-in siatna a ~ hi/kiat lawhin gimna ~ uh hen | may they fall and bring suffering on themselves) (s:ngahkhak/thuaklawh/tuaklawh) (r:19.106.32/45.11.9) (q:draft)
ngahmun = (t:n) (w:ford/crossing) (d:a shallow place where a river is crossed on foot, as on the Jordan, the Jabbok and the Arnon) (e:Jabbok ~ kantan hi/Jordan lamah ~ dong delh uh hi | they pursued them toward the Jordan as far as the ford/Jordan ~ kantanin Gad leh Gilead gamah | crossing the ford of the Jordan to the land of Gad and Gilead/gun-a ~ teng la khinmang uh a | they have seized all the river crossings) (r:1.32.22/6.2.7/9.13.7/24.51.32) (q:draft)
ngahmunah = (t:n) (w:at the ford/at the crossing) (d:ngahmun ford with the place marker ah) (e:Arnon guntui ~ Moab mite om uh hi) (b:ngahmun) (r:23.16.2) (q:draft)
ngahmunte = (t:n) (w:fords/crossings) (d:ngahmun, ford, with the plural te; with ah it means at the fords) (e:Jordan ~ la uh hi/gamlak tui ~-ah ka ngak ding hi | I will wait at the fords in the wilderness/amah manin Jordan ~-ah that uh hi | they seized him and killed him at the fords of the Jordan) (b:ngahmun) (r:7.12.5/10.15.28/7.12.6) (q:draft)
ngahna = (t:n) (w:gain/getting/obtaining) (d:ngah, get, with the noun suffix na: the getting of something or the means of getting it; thuman lo-a ngahna is ill-gotten gain and pahtak ngahna is a way to honour) (e:thuman lo-a ~ a deih lo mipa/Kitot khak ding pelhna in pahtak ~ hi a | avoiding a quarrel is a way to gain honour/Thuman lo-a ~-ah phattuamna om lo a | there is no profit in ill-gotten gain/~ ding bekah awnsak kei in | do not turn it only toward gain) (s:meetna) (a:taanna/supna) (b:ngah) (r:20.28.16/20.20.3/20.10.2/19.119.36) (q:draft)
ngahnop = (t:v) (w:want to get/wish to receive) (d:ngah, get, with nop, want; found before man, because, as in sum ngahnop manin, because of wanting money) (e:sum ~ manin mi khat in/a natna uh panin damna a ~ manun | because they wanted to be healed of their diseases/na puansungsilh a ~ manin | because he wants to get your shirt/na tampi ka ~ man hi lo a | it is not that I want to get many things) (r:18.17.5/42.6.18/40.5.40/50.4.17) (q:draft)
ngahnopna = (t:n) (w:desire to get/greed for) (d:ngahnop want to get with the noun suffix na; sum ngahnopna, desire for money) (e:Sum ~ bek tawh a sem hi loin) (b:ngahnop) (r:60.5.2) (q:draft)
ngahpa = (t:n) (w:receiver/finder/one who gets) (d:ngah, get, with pa, the man: the man who receives, gets or finds something; cidamna a ngahpa is the man who was healed) (e:cidamna a ~ in kua ahi hiam/Van-kinusia tampi a ~ bangin | like a man who finds great spoil/mi in thupha ~ ahi hi | that person is one who is blessed) (s:sangpa) (b:ngah) (r:43.5.13/19.119.162/19.112.1) (q:draft)
ngahpak = (t:v) (w:get soon/quickly receive) (d:ngah get with pak quickly) (e:minsiatna ~ ding ahih manin) (r:20.11.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngahsa = (t:adj) (w:received/obtained/acquired) (d:ngah, receive, with sa, already done: what has been received or gained; it stands before a noun, or alone after a possessor) (e:note in na ~ khempeuh uh/Tanglai-a na ~ nangma mihonte | your people whom you acquired long ago/a ~ uh leh a kholsa uh na tampite | the many things they have acquired and stored up/tu-in na ~ uh thuhilhna | the teaching you have now received) (s:sansa) (b:ngah) (r:66.2.25/19.74.2/23.15.7/45.6.17) (q:draft)
ngahsak = (t:v) (w:cause to receive/bring/grant/give) (d:ngah, receive, with the causative sak: make someone get or have something, whether good or bad) (e:kampauna in pahtawina ~ a/leitung khempeuhah pahtawina kong ~ ding hi | I will give you honour in all the earth/lungdamna kei hong ~ kik in la | give me joy again/mihonte le amau’ ganhingte tui na ~ ding | you shall get water for the people and their livestock) (s:neihsak/pia) (b:ngah) (r:21.10.12/5.8.17/23.58.14/19.51.12/4.20.8) (q:draft)
ngahsakin = (t:v) (w:causing to receive/inflicting) (d:ngahsak cause to receive with the linking suffix in; gim ngahsakin, making someone suffer) (e:mizawngte gim ~) (b:ngahsak) (r:21.5.8) (q:draft)
ngahsakthei = (t:v) (w:be able to give/enable to receive) (d:ngahsak cause to receive with thei be able) (e:hotkhiatna a hong ~ Lungdamna Thu) (b:ngahsak) (r:49.1.13) (q:draft)
ngahsakzo = (t:v) (w:manage to get for) (d:ngahsak cause to receive with zo be able, succeed in getting something for someone) (e:galsimna sungah ka ~ kei uh a) (b:ngahsak) (r:7.21.22) (q:draft)
ngahsawn = (t:v) (w:receive in turn/receive a share from) (d:ngah receive with sawn onward, receive out of what another has received) (e:Simeon minam in gamh ~ uh hi) (r:6.19.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngahsunte = (t:n) (w:those gained/converts) (d:the ones who have been won, from ngah get, with plural te) (e:na ~ uh zong note zah nihin) (r:40.23.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngahta = (t:v) (w:received) (d:ngah, receive, with ta, marking that the action has now taken place) (e:thupha ~)
ngahtawm = (t:v) (w:get by oneself) (d:ngah get with tawm by oneself, without the help of another) (e:huhna bangci ~ theih ding ka hi) (r:18.6.13) (q:draft)
ngahte = (t:n) (w:those who receive/recipients) (d:ngah, receive, with the plural te: the people who receive or have something; gupna ngahte are those who are saved) (e:gupna ~ tawm ding ahi uh hiam/hih mihonpite in kosiatna ~ ahi uh hi | this crowd are people under a curse/gupna a ~ tungah ahi zongin | among those who are being saved/Hehpihna tampi a ~ tung panin tampi kingen ding | from those who have received much, much will be asked) (s:sangte) (b:ngah) (r:42.13.23/43.7.49/47.2.15/42.12.48) (q:draft)
ngahte = (t:n) (w:things received/gains) (d:ngah, receive, with the plural te: the things that have been received or taken, as in na ngahte uh, what you receive) (e:Keima kiang panin na ~ uh/a van ~ khempeuh uh | all the goods they had taken/na thupha ~ uh tungah samsiatna ka tungsak | I have sent a curse on the blessings you received/gamsung a ukte tung panin a ~ banah | besides what he received from the governors of the land) (b:ngah) (r:20.8.19/14.24.23/39.2.2/11.10.14) (q:draft)
ngahthei = (t:v) (w:be able to receive/can get) (d:ngah, receive, with thei, can: be able to receive or get) (e:vun ki-at lote in zong ~ uh hi/bangmah ~ tuan nawn lo hi | he could no longer get anything/nopsakna a ~ ding mi a om leh | if there is someone there who can receive peace/koi lai panin hih bang thuteng ~ ahi hiam | where could he get all these things from) (s:ngahzo/sangthei) (b:ngah) (r:45.4.9/58.12.17/42.10.6/40.13.56) (q:draft)
ngahtheih = (t:v) (w:be able to receive/can obtain/may get) (d:form of ngahthei, be able to receive, used before nading: so that one may receive) (e:Sum ~ nading bekin/Kha Siangtho a ~ nadingin | so that they may receive the Holy Spirit/Nuntak tawntung ~ nading lametna tawh | in the hope of obtaining eternal life/a kimtakin na ~ nadingun limtakin kidawm un | watch carefully so that you may receive it in full) (s:ngahzawh) (b:ngah) (r:56.1.11/56.2.11/44.8.19/43.5.39/63.1.8) (q:draft)
ngahtheihna = (t:n) (w:obtaining/means of getting) (d:ngahtheih be able to get, with the noun suffix na; sum ngahtheihna ding is in order to get money) (e:sum ~ ding ngaihsutna bek tawh/sumgolh ~ ding ngaihsutna bek tawh thu khen a | they judge only with a view to getting a bribe) (s:ngahna) (b:ngahtheih) (r:33.3.11) (q:draft)
ngahthuah = (t:v) (w:gain in addition/gain more) (d:ngah, receive, with thuah, in addition) (e:a meet tulnih mah a ~ hi/a meet tulnga mah a ~ hi | he gained five thousand more as profit) (s:ngahbeh) (r:40.25.17/40.25.16) (q:draft)
ngahthuap = (t:v) (w:receive regularly/receive as allowance) (d:receive a portion again and again; ngahthuapna is an allowance) (e:Tua ciangin ama ~ dingin) (r:12.25.30) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngahthuapna = (t:n) (w:allowance/provision) (d:what a person is regularly given to live on) (e:~ ama tungah kumpipa in pia hi) (b:ngahthuap) (r:12.25.30) (q:draft)
ngahtoto = (t:v) (w:keep gaining/receive more and more) (d:ngah receive with toto, going on and increasing) (e:mite’ maipha a ~ hi) (r:9.2.26) (q:draft)
ngahzah = (t:n) (w:portion/share) (d:ngah, receive, with zah, amount: the amount a person receives, a share or portion, also pay) (e:a dangte’ ~ nih ngah ding uh hi/ama ~ tang ding a va la dingin | to go and collect his share/na khasum ~ uh tawh lungkim un | be content with the pay you get/minam dangte’ ~ tan mah hi ding a | it will be the same as the portions of the other tribes) (s:tanh/seh) (r:26.47.13/42.20.10/42.3.14/26.48.8) (q:draft)
ngahzahzah = (t:n) (w:whatever one gets/as much as one gets) (d:ngah get with zahzah as much as) (e:mihai pa in a ~ zangkhia pah hi) (r:20.21.20) (q:draft)
ngahzaw = (t:v) (w:receive/receive more/get more) (d:ngah, receive, with zaw, more: receive or get more than others; the others are followed by sangin, than) (e:adangte sangin tam ~ ding ci-in/tapa dangte sangin thupha ~ hen | may he be blessed more than the other sons/gamlak ganhing khempeuhte sangin samsiatna na ~ hi | you are cursed more than all the wild animals/Jesuh in Johan sangin mi tam ~ in | Jesus was gaining more people than John) (b:ngah) (r:40.20.10/5.33.24/1.3.14/43.4.1)
ngahzawh = (t:v) (w:win/gain/obtain/manage to get) (d:ngah, get, with zawh, form of zo, be able: succeed in getting; this form is used before nading and nak-uhleh) (e:thaman na ~ nadingun na tai un/mi a tam theithei ka ~ nadingin | so that I may win as many people as possible/amaute ka ~ nadingin amaute mah bangin ka gamta hi | to win them I live just as they do/A tungah a tuang ding mi na ~ nak-uhleh | if you can find men to ride on them) (s:ngahtheih) (r:46.9.24/46.9.19/46.9.22/23.36.8) (q:draft)
ngahzo = (t:v) (w:be able to get/obtain/attain) (d:ngah, get, with zo, be able or succeed: manage to get, obtain) (e:a deih khempeuh ~ hi/kua in hotkhiatna ~ ding ahi hiam | who then can obtain salvation/taina lel tawh pilna ~ uh hi | they gain knowledge by a mere rebuke/Thadah mi in a deih ~ lo a | the lazy person does not get what he wants) (s:ngahthei) (b:ngah) (r:20.13.4/42.18.26/20.19.25) (q:draft)
ngai = (t:v) (w:listen/hear/pay attention) (d:give ear to what is said and take it to heart; ngai in is the command to one person and ngai un to several) (e:tu-in ka thutheihte na ~ in/keima thugen ~ un | hear my word/bil a neih leh, ~ ta hen | if he has ears, let him hear/ka thugente don in la ka kammalte ~ in | pay attention to what I say and listen to my words) (s:don/ngaihsak) (r:18.15.17/26.34.9/66.13.9/20.4.20) (q:draft)
Ngai = (t:v) (w:listen/hear/pay attention) (d:ngai written with a capital at the start of a call) (e:Kumpipa’ innkuante aw, ~ un/~ un, khaici vawhpa in khaici vawh dingin a kuankhia | listen, a sower went out to sow seed/~ un, leitung a teeng khempeuh | listen, all who live on the earth/~ un la, na bil uh ngat un | hear and give ear) (s:don/ngaihsak) (b:ngai) (r:28.5.1/41.4.3/19.49.1/24.13.15) (q:draft)
