ngaihbaan'na = (t:n) (w:loveliness/charm) (d:ngaih baang lovely with the noun suffix na; the English versions have breasts here) (e:ama ~ tawh lungdamin) (s:ngaihbaanna/ngaihban'na) (r:20.5.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngaihbaang = (t:adj) (w:beautiful/handsome/lovely/attractive) (d:pleasing to look at, said of women and of men) (e:a ~ mahmah khat ahi hi/Rachel melhoihin ~ hi | Rachel was beautiful and lovely/A ~ na mai hong musak inla | show me your lovely face/a vekpi-in a ~ Assiria mi tangval | Assyrian young men, all of them handsome) (s:melhoih/etlawm/ngaihhuai) (a:melsia) (r:1.24.16/26.23.12/1.29.17/22.2.14) (q:draft)
ngaihbaangin = (t:adj) (w:lovely/handsome/attractive) (d:ngaihbaang, pleasing to look at, with in, linking to what follows) (e:Tu-in Josef ~ a mel hoih hi/A it-huai a ~ ngaihsun tawntung inla | always think of her as lovable and lovely) (s:melhoihin) (b:ngaihbaang) (r:1.39.6/20.5.19) (q:draft)
ngaihbaanna = (t:n) (w:charm/loveliness/attractiveness) (d:ngaihbaang lovely, attractive, with the noun suffix na: the charm of a woman) (e:ama ~ tawh lungdamin/numei dangte’ ~ iplah ding na hi hiam | why would you covet the charms of other women) (s:ngaihban'na/ngaihbaan'na/melhoihna) (r:20.5.19/20.31.30/20.5.20) (q:draft)
