ngaihsun = (t:v) (w:think/consider/think about) (d:use the mind: think about something, consider it, or regard a person or thing in a certain way; ngaihsun un is the command to several people) (e:note in na ~ kei un/Tu laitak-a na omzia uh lim takin ~ un | think carefully about how you are living now/gal bangin hong ~ na hi hiam | do you consider me an enemy/Ka gamtatnate ka ~ a | I have considered my ways) (s:lungngai) (r:45.13.14/37.1.5/18.13.24/19.119.59)
ngaihsuna = (t:v) (w:thinking of/considering) (d:ngaihsun, think, with the linking a: while thinking about something, or with someone in mind) (e:Ka mangmuhna ~ ka om lai takin/mawhna a thuak mi bek ~ gelh | writing with only the injured person in mind) (b:ngaihsun) (r:27.4.13/47.7.12) (q:draft)
ngaihsunin = (t:v) (w:thinking/considering/meaning/having in mind) (d:ngaihsun, think, with the linking suffix in: having something in mind while doing the next action, or meaning something by what is said) (e:siat nading bek ~ sem uh a/mi tampite ~ thu a pia kei hi | he did not speak as meaning many people/upna tawh a piang ding nate ~ | by faith, with the things to come in mind/siat nading thu ~, gitlohna na piangsak uh hi | planning trouble, you give birth to evil) (b:ngaihsun) (r:18.15.35/48.3.16/58.11.20/23.59.4) (q:draft)
ngaihsunkawm = (t:v) (w:think at the same time/hope meanwhile) (d:ngaihsun, think, with kawm, while: think or hope something at the same time as doing something else) (e:hong pia thei leh ci-in ~ ahih manin) (r:44.24.26) (q:draft)
ngaihsunkha = (t:v) (w:suppose/imagine/think) (d:ngaihsun, think, with kha: come to think that something is so, often of a mistaken idea; ngaihsunkha kei un is do not suppose) (e:Pasian a kikhemzo dingin ~ kei un/no tawh a kibangin nong ~ uh hi | you thought I was just like you/a hu dingin mihau pa in ~ hi | the rich man imagines it will protect him/zong ka ~ ngei beek kei hi | nor did it ever even enter my mind) (s:upmawh) (r:48.6.7/19.50.21/20.18.11/24.7.31) (q:draft)
ngaihsunkhial = (t:v) (w:think wrongly/be mistaken/be in error) (d:ngaihsun, think, with khial, wrongly: have a mistaken idea) (e:thei lo na hih manun na ~ uh hi) (r:40.22.29) (q:draft)
ngaihsunsak = (t:v) (w:let think/make think) (d:ngaihsun, think, with the causative sak: let or make someone think; bangmah ngaihsunsak thei lo is leave one unable to perceive anything) (e:khuamial in bangmah ~ thei lo) (b:ngaihsun) (r:62.2.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngaihsunsun = (t:v) (w:meditate/ponder/keep thinking about) (d:ngaihsun, think, with the last part doubled for thinking again and again: meditate on, ponder) (e:ama thu a ~ mi ahi hi/nangma nasepna lamdangte ka ~ ding hi | I will meditate on your wonderful deeds/ama hihsate ~ ding uh hi | they will ponder what he has done/a lungsimah hih thute ciamtehin a ~ hi | she kept these things in her heart and pondered them) (s:lungngaingai/lungngaihngaih) (r:19.1.2/42.2.19/19.119.27/19.64.9) (q:draft)
ngaihsunsunin = (t:v) (w:pondering/thinking over and over) (d:ngaihsunsun, keep thinking about, with in, linking to the next verb) (e:Ka lupna tungah nangmah hong ~/ka muhsa thute ~ | pondering the things I had seen) (b:ngaihsunsun) (r:19.63.5/26.3.15) (q:draft)
ngaihsunte = (t:n) (w:those who think/those who plan/those who consider) (d:ngaihsun, think, with plural te: the people who think, plan or consider something; thusia ngaihsunte are those who plot evil) (e:Thusia ~ lungkham a/thu ~ in taina lel tawh pilna ngah | the discerning gain knowledge by a mere rebuke/kote a hong ~ tungah hangtakin ka gamta ding hi | I will act boldly toward those who think so of us) (b:ngaihsun) (r:20.12.20/47.10.2/20.19.25) (q:draft)
ngaihsut = (t:v) (w:think/consider/think about) (d:form of ngaihsun, think, used before ciangin, ding, na, theihna and in dependent clauses) (e:Keima tunga thu piang ka ~ ciangin/ka ~ khak ciangin amah ka kihta hi | when I think of it, I fear him/kei pen na lawmpa banga nong ~ leh | if you consider me your partner/Piter in a mangmuhna a ~ lai takin | while Peter was thinking about the vision/Bangci ~ na hi uh hiam | what do you think) (r:18.21.6/26.38.10/18.23.15/57.1.17/44.10.19/40.26.66) (q:draft)
ngaihsutin = (t:v) (w:think about/consider/take to heart/pay attention to) (d:ngaihsut, think, with the linking ending in; ngaihsutin nei is set the mind on something, take it to heart) (e:Vantungah a om thute ~ nei unla/hih thute ~ zong nei nuam lo uh hi | they did not want to take these things to heart/~ zong ka nei ngei kei hi | I have never even thought of it/tua thu ~ nei nawn lo hi | he gave the matter no more thought/leitung nate bek ~ nei uh | they set their minds only on earthly things) (b:ngaihsut) (r:51.3.2/2.7.23/38.7.11/18.31.27/50.3.19) (q:draft)
ngaihsutkha = (t:v) (w:regard/think of/happen to think) (d:ngaihsut, think, with kha, happen to: come to regard something in a certain way; neu ngaihsutkha is think little of, show contempt for) (e:a hong thuaknate neu ~ na hi uh hiam) (r:45.2.4) (q:draft)
ngaihsutkhak = (t:v) (w:think/suppose/have in mind) (d:form of ngaihsutkha, happen to think, come to think, used in dependent clauses) (e:ka ~ beek zong ahi lo/a valin hong thupi ~ ding uh | that they should think too highly of me/ci-in a ~ uh | which they suppose to be so) (b:ngaihsutkha) (r:24.19.5/47.12.6/54.6.20) (q:draft)
ngaihsutna = (t:n) (w:idea/thought) (d:ngaihsut, think, with the noun suffix na: what a person thinks, a thought or idea) (e:~ kihhuai sa a/mi sung pan a hoih lo ~ | evil thoughts from within a person) (s:thungaihsutna) (b:ngaihsut) (r:20.15.26/41.7.21)
ngaihsutna = (t:n) (w:plan/purpose/counsel) (d:ngaihsut, think, with the noun suffix na: what has been thought out, a plan or purpose; also the advice that one gives) (e:thu ~ a mawkna suah a/a lungsim ~ khang tawntungin kip hi | the plans of his heart stand firm through all generations/Ka ~ hong pia leng | if I give you my counsel) (s:geelna/ngimna/vaihawmna) (b:ngaihsut) (r:19.33.10/19.33.11/24.38.15)
ngaihsutnate = (t:n) (w:thoughts/plans) (d:plural of ngaihsutna: thoughts or plans, of God or of people) (e:Na ~ thuk mahmah/Pasian aw, na ~ kei adingin bangzah takin manpha | O God, how precious your thoughts are to me/tua ni mahin ama ~ bei ta hi | on that very day his plans come to nothing/ka ~ gamlapi pek panin na thei hi | you know my thoughts from far away) (s:geelnate/ngimnate) (b:ngaihsutna) (r:19.92.5/19.146.4/19.139.17/19.139.2) (q:draft)
ngaihsutpi = (t:n) (w:goal/chief concern/main aim) (d:ngaihsut, think, with pi, great or main: the main thought or aim; ngaihsutpi-in nei is set the heart on something, make it the chief concern) (e:lampi man zuih ding ~-in nei in/Topa lungdamsak ding ~-in a kinei ahi hi | pleasing the Lord is made the chief aim/tangthu phuahtawm peuh ~-in nei ding uh hi | they will set their minds on made-up stories/a pha kibawl ding ~-in na nei un | make it your aim to do good to one another) (s:tupna) (b:ngaihsut) (r:20.23.19/47.5.9/55.4.4/52.5.15) (q:draft)
ngaihsutsa = (t:n) (w:plan/purpose/decision) (d:ngaihsut, think, with sa, already done: what has already been thought out or decided, a plan or decision) (e:a ~ thu tawh kizui-in/Sawt pek lai-in ka ~ ahihna | that I decided it long ago/kumpipa kiangah puak dingin ka ~ ahi hi | I have decided to send him to the emperor/a ~ uh gitlohnate semkhia uh hi | they carry out the evil they have planned) (b:ngaihsut) (r:49.1.11/27.2.8/12.19.25/44.25.25/33.2.1) (q:draft)
ngaihsutsak = (t:v) (w:consider on behalf of/regard as) (d:ngaihsut, consider, with sak: think of something on behalf of another, or regard something in a certain way) (e:midangte’ phattuam nading ~ zaw un/gimnate hong neu ~ kei in | do not regard the hardships as small) (b:ngaihsut) (r:50.2.4/16.9.32) (q:draft)
ngaihsutsiam = (t:adj) (w:discerning/thoughtful/capable) (d:ngaihsut, think, with siam, skilled: good at thinking, discerning; thu ngaihsutsiam mi is a capable, sensible man) (e:thu ~ mi ahi Sherebiah) (r:15.8.18) (q:draft)
ngaihsuttawm = (t:adj) (w:self-devised/made up/of his own invention) (d:ngaihsut think, with tawm, by oneself: thought up on his own; ngaihsuttawm thu is what someone says on his own authority, not what he was given to say) (e:Ama ~ thu hong gen ding hi lo/le amau’ ~ thute ahi hi | and things of their own invention/amau’ ~ thu gen napi-in | though they speak words they made up themselves) (r:43.16.13/24.23.31/24.14.14) (q:draft)
ngaihsutte = (t:n) (w:those who regard/those who consider) (d:those who think of or regard something in a certain way; a thupi ngaihsutte, those who regard something as important) (e:Mawkna milim a thupi ~ na mudah hi) (b:ngaihsut) (r:19.31.6) (q:draft)
ngaihsutte = (t:n) (w:thoughts/what people think) (d:ngaihsut, think, with plural te: the things that people think, plan or take to be so) (e:ci-in a ~ pen sihna lampi/pilna hi, ci-in a ~ | what they take to be wisdom/a manpha mahmahin a ~ pen | what they regard as very valuable/kei a dingin a ~ hong tungsak ding hi | he will fulfil what he has planned for me) (b:ngaihsut) (r:20.14.12/46.3.19/42.16.15/19.138.8) (q:draft)
ngaihsutzaw = (t:v) (w:consider more/regard more highly) (d:ngaihsut, consider, with zaw, more; thupi ngaihsutzaw is consider more important, value above another) (e:midangte thupi ~ un/nangmah hong thupi ~ uh a | they valued you more highly/mizawngte sangin mihaute thupi ~ tuan lo hi | he does not favor the rich over the poor/a kituakzah valin kilian ~ kha kei un | do not think of yourselves more highly than is fitting) (b:ngaihsut) (r:50.2.3/18.34.19/5.33.9/45.12.3) (q:draft)
ngaihsutzawh = (t:v) (w:fathom/comprehend) (d:ngaihsut, think, with zawh, form of zo, be able: be able to think through; with ding hi lo, beyond understanding) (e:ama liatna ~ ding hi lo hi/thu a theihtelna pen ~ ding hi lo hi | his understanding is beyond fathoming) (r:19.145.3/19.147.5) (q:draft)
ngaihsutzia = (t:n) (w:way of thinking/philosophy) (d:ngaihsut, think, with zia, manner) (e:Stoik thu ~ a um mite pawlkhat/Epikuras thu ~ le Stoik thu | the Epicurean way of thinking and the Stoic) (r:44.17.18) (q:draft)
ngaihtakin = (t:adv) (w:loudly/aloud) (d:ngaih, loud, with takin, which makes an adverb: loudly; said of singing or shouting for joy) (e:mual tungah ~ la a sa ding uh a) (r:24.31.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngaihte = (t:n) (w:lovers/beloved ones) (d:ngaih, dear or beloved, with plural te; used after lawm, friend, as lawm ngaihte: lovers, and as a figure for allies) (e:Na lawm ~ in nang hong paaikhia uh/a lawm ~ lunggulh mahmah hi | she lusted after her lovers/Na lawm ~ un hong mangngilh khin uh a | your lovers have forgotten you) (b:ngaih) (r:24.4.30/26.23.5/24.30.14) (q:draft)
ngaihzawk = (t:v) (w:listen rather/heed) (d:ngaih, listen, with zawk, rather or more: listen to or heed instead; said of what should have been heeded) (e:keima thu nong ~ ding uh hinapi-in) (r:26.34.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngaikik = (t:v) (w:listen again/hear again) (d:ngai, listen, with kik, again) (e:tu nung ciangin ka ~ nuam uh hi) (s:zakik) (b:ngai) (r:44.17.32) (q:draft)
ngailai = (t:v) (w:keep listening/bear with longer) (d:ngai, listen, with lai, still: go on listening, bear with someone a little longer) (e:Lungduai takin tawmkhat hong ~ in) (r:18.36.2) (q:draft)
ngailua = (t:v) (w:love too much/be obsessed with) (d:ngai, long for or love, with lua, too much: be so in love as to be obsessed) (e:Ammon in ~ mahmah ahih manin) (r:10.13.2) (q:draft)
ngaingai = (t:v) (w:keep listening/listen on) (d:ngai, listen, said twice for continued action: keep on listening) (e:~ napi-in za thei lo/lungduai takin kong ~ a | I kept listening to you patiently) (s:ngaihngaih) (r:40.13.13/18.32.11) (q:draft)
ngainuam = (t:v) (w:want to listen/be willing to listen) (d:ngai, listen, with nuam, want) (e:amaute in ka thu ~ loin/thuman thutak ~ nawn loin | no longer willing to listen to the truth) (r:38.1.4/55.4.4) (q:draft)
ngaisak = (t:v) (w:make obey/make listen) (d:ngai, listen or heed, with the causative sak: make someone or something obey) (e:Khazih’ thu ka ~ uh hi) (s:thumangsak) (b:ngai) (r:47.10.5) (q:draft)
ngaisim = (t:v) (w:listen secretly/overhear) (d:ngai, listen, with sim, secretly: listen in on what others are saying) (e:Rebekah in na ~ hi) (s:zasim) (r:1.27.5) (q:draft)
ngaisun = (t:v) (w:think/consider) (d:another spelling of ngaihsun, think; bangci na ngaisun hiam is what do you think) (e:Bangci na ~ hiam) (s:ngaihsun) (r:43.9.17) (q:draft)
ngaite = (t:n) (w:those who listen/those who heed/those who welcome) (d:ngai, listen or heed, with plural te: the ones who listen to someone; also of those who welcome a person) (e:Note thu a ~ in ka thu a ngai/ka thugenna a ~ in lungmuanna ngah ding a | those who listen to me will find safety/No hong ~ in kei hong ngai hi | whoever welcomes you welcomes me/Lungdamna Thu a ~ sum beisak lo dingin | so as not to cost those who hear the gospel any money) (b:ngai) (r:42.10.16/20.1.33/40.10.40/46.9.18) (q:draft)
ngaizo = (t:v) (w:obey/heed) (d:ngai, listen, with zo, carry through: do what one was told; thu ngaizo is obey a word) (e:na nasemnu in na thu hong ~ hi) (s:mangzo) (b:ngai) (r:9.28.21) (q:draft)
ngak = (t:v) (w:wait/wait for/keep watch) (d:wait for someone or something, also stay awake and keep watch; Topa ngak is wait for the Lord in hope) (e:Na hotkhiatna ka ~ hi/Troas khua-ah kote hong ~ uh hi | they waited for us at Troas/Topa ~ in; tha khauh in la | wait for the Lord; be strong/hong hehpihna phatin ~ un | keep watch, giving thanks/Topa i ~ hi | we wait for the Lord) (r:1.49.18/44.20.5/19.27.14/51.4.2/19.33.20) (q:draft)
ngakin = (t:v) (w:waiting/waiting for) (d:ngak, wait, with the linking suffix in: waiting, while waiting; often followed by om, be) (e:tuate lungnemna tawh ~ i om hi/Silas leh Timoti ~ a om lai takin | while he was waiting for Silas and Timothy/ni sagih sung ~ | waiting for seven days/Zeisu Khazih hong kilat ding ~ na om lai takun | as you wait for Jesus Christ to be revealed) (b:ngak) (r:45.8.25/44.17.16/1.8.10/46.1.7) (q:draft)
ngakkawmin = (t:v) (w:while waiting) (d:ngak, wait, with kawm, while, and the linking suffix in: while waiting for something) (e:a hong suahtaksak ding i ~ thumin) (r:45.8.23) (q:draft)
ngakkawmun = (t:v) (w:while waiting) (d:ngak, wait, with kawm, while, and un, the linking suffix for more than one person: while you wait) (e:hong piak ding na ~ Pasian’ itna sungah) (r:65.1.21) (q:draft)
ngakkhawm = (t:v) (w:keep watch with/wait together) (d:ngak, wait or watch, with khawm, together) (e:kei tawh ~ zo lo na hi hiam/nai khat nangawn kei tawh ~ zo lo | not able to keep watch with me even one hour) (b:ngak) (r:41.14.37/40.26.40) (q:draft)
ngakkhit = (t:v) (w:have laid on) (d:ngak, lay or rest upon, with khit, finish: have laid on, said of laying hands on someone; ngakkhit ciangin is after laying on) (e:amaute tungah a khut a ~ ciangin) (r:44.19.6) (q:draft)
ngaklah = (t:v) (w:long for/wait eagerly/be eager) (d:wait for or want something with impatience, be eager for it; an ngaklah is be greedy for food) (e:Topa ka ~ zaw hi/ni hong tun’ ding a ~ note’ adingin | for you who long for the day to come/zumkhak hun bei ding i ~ hi | we are impatient for the festival to be over/An ~ thei mi na hih leh | if you are a person greedy for food/leitung teng a et ding uh ~ mahmah uh hi | they were very eager to go and see the whole earth) (s:lunggulh) (r:19.130.6/38.6.7/30.5.18/30.8.5/20.23.2) (q:draft)
ngaklahin = (t:v) (w:longing/yearning) (d:ngaklah, long for, with the linking suffix in: longing, while longing) (e:~ ka khuisasa uh hi) (b:ngaklah) (r:47.5.2) (q:draft)
ngaklai = (t:v) (w:still wait/wait longer/go on waiting) (d:ngak wait, with lai still, any longer) (e:bang tanvei ~ ding ka hi hiam/a sep ding ~ ding ka hi hiam | should I still wait for him to act/bang ~ ding ka hi hiam | what do I still wait for) (r:19.119.84/12.6.33/19.39.7) (q:draft)
ngakna = (t:n) (w:stand/rest/base) (d:ngak, rest or lay upon, with the noun suffix na: the thing on which something rests, as the stand of a basin; khe ngakna is a footstool) (e:kisilna kuang leh a ~ zong/leitung in keima khe ~ ahi hi | the earth is my footstool/ama khe ~ munah bia un | worship at his footstool/kuang leh a ~ | the basin and its stand) (s:kingakna) (r:2.40.11/19.99.5/23.66.1/2.31.9) (q:draft)
ngaknate = (t:n) (w:stands/rests/supports) (d:plural of ngakna: things on which something rests; ban ngaknate are armrests, and the ngaknate of a basin are its stand) (e:ban ~ pangah humpinelkai nih ding a/kuang leh a ~, ap dingin sathau nuh hi | he anointed the basin and its stand to consecrate them/sumngo tuikuang le a ~ suzan gawp uh a | they broke up the bronze Sea and its stands/tutna pang tuakah ban ~ | armrests on both sides of the seat) (s:kingaknate) (b:ngakna) (r:11.10.19/3.8.11/24.52.17/14.9.18) (q:draft)
ngaknate = (t:n) (w:waiting/perseverance) (d:plural of ngakna in the sense of waiting: the times one waits patiently, perseverance) (e:lungduai takin a ~ uh) (b:ngakna) (r:46.13.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngakngak = (t:v) (w:keep waiting for/wait and wait) (d:ngak, wait, doubled to show that the waiting goes on) (e:hun ding a ~ mi khat ahi hi/na ~ uh Topa | the Lord you keep waiting for/hun lamenin a ~ mi khat ahi hi | he was a man waiting in hope for the time) (r:42.2.25/39.3.1/42.23.50) (q:draft)
ngakngakna = (t:see) <ngakngakna-in>
ngakngakna-in = (t:n) (w:long waiting/longing) (d:ngak wait, said twice for continued action, with the noun suffix na and in marking the cause: because of waiting and waiting) (e:Ka Pasian ka ~ ka mitte maang ta hi/Nong hotkhiat ding ka ~ ka tha bei ta hi | my strength is spent from waiting for you to save me) (r:19.69.3/19.119.81) (q:draft)
ngaksak = (t:v) (w:lay on/place on) (d:ngak, rest upon, with the causative sak: lay or place on; khut ngaksak is lay a hand on a person) (e:ama tungah a khut a ~ nadingin/ama tungah na khut hong ~ in | lay your hand on her) (s:ngasak) (r:41.7.32/41.5.23) (q:draft)
ngaksakin = (t:v) (w:laying on/casting upon) (d:ngaksak, lay on, with the linking suffix in; lupna ngaksakin is laying someone on a bed) (e:lupna ~ nakpitakin gimna ka thuaksak ding) (b:ngaksak) (r:66.2.22) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngaksate = (t:n) (w:those laid upon) (d:those on whom something has been laid, here the hands, from ngak lay upon, sa already and plural te) (e:Keima khut a tungah ka ~ in) (r:44.8.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngakte = (t:n) (w:those who wait/those who hope) (d:ngak, wait, with plural te: people who wait for someone or put their hope in him) (e:Topa a ~ in leitung luah ding/nang hong ~ kuamah zahhuaisak kei in | let none who wait for you be put to shame/itna tawh a ~ khempeuh tungah | to all who wait with love/lawptakin a ~ ihi hi | we are those who eagerly wait) (s:lamente) (b:ngak) (r:19.37.9/19.25.3/55.4.8/50.3.20) (q:draft)
ngakzaw = (t:v) (w:wait rather/wait instead) (d:ngak, wait, with zaw, rather: wait instead of doing something else) (e:Topa’ hong huh ding ~ in) (b:ngak) (r:20.20.22) (q:draft)
ngakzo = (t:v) (w:be able to wait/manage to wait/wait through) (d:ngak wait, keep watch, with zo, be able, manage to) (e:a khan khit dong ~ ding/Nai khat sung nangawn hong ~ lo | not able to keep watch even for one hour) (b:ngak) (r:8.1.13/40.26.40) (q:draft)
ngal = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:wild boar/boar) (d:a wild pig that lives in the forest) (e:Gamlak a om ~ in susiagawp a) (r:19.80.13) (q:draft)
ngal = (t:part) (d:placed after kei, not, and before leh, if, to stress the condition: kei ngal leh is unless, if indeed not) (e:thu i muh kei ~ leh) (r:27.6.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
Ngal = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:wild boar/boar) (d:a wild pig that lives in the forest; the same word as ngal, written with a capital in one text) (e:Gamlak-a om ~ in susia gawpin) (b:ngal) (r:19.80.13) (q:draft)
ngaltak = (t:n) (w:jointed leg/hind leg) (d:the jointed upper leg above the foot that an insect such as a locust uses for hopping) (e:khepek uh tawh kizom ~ tawn a neite) (r:3.11.21) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngaltuam = (t:n) (w:greaves) (d:armour worn on the lower legs, in the verse made of bronze) (e:a khete tungah sumngo ~ nei a) (r:9.17.6) (q:draft)
Ngalvangte = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:hyraxes/conies) (d:plural with te: small animals of little strength that make their home among the rocks) (e:~: a thahat lo ganhing hi napi-in | hyraxes, though they are creatures of little strength) (r:20.30.26) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngam = (t:v) (w:dare) (d:have the courage to do something; placed after the main verb, and very often used with kei or lo, not dare) (e:a mai-ah kuamah om ~ lo hi/thudang a dong ~ nawn kei uh hi | they no longer dared to ask anything more/kua in phensak ~ ahi hiam | who dares to open it/khat beek in a pawlpih ~ loh uh hangin | though not one dared to join them/Pasian’ mai-ah migilote’ pai ~ lo | the wicked do not dare come before God) (s:ngap) (a:ngamlah) (r:18.41.10/42.20.40/18.41.14/44.5.13/18.13.16) (q:draft)
ngamin = (t:v) (w:daring/risking) (d:ngam, dare, with the linking suffix in; follows the verb that names what is dared, as in nuntakna pia ngamin, risking life) (e:ka nuntakna pia ~, ka nuntakna ka ap ngam hi/amah in a nuntakna pia ~ Filistiapa that a | he risked his life and killed the Philistine/thongkia mite thuakpih ~ | daring to suffer with those in prison/note a dingin a pia ~ ka om uh hi | we were ready to give them for you) (b:ngam) (r:18.13.14/9.19.5/58.10.34/52.2.8) (q:draft)
ngamlah = (t:v) (w:be afraid to/hesitate) (d:ngam, dare, with lah, fail to: not have the courage to do something, hold back from it) (e:amah tenpih ~ kei in) (a:ngam) (r:40.1.20) (q:draft)
ngamna = (t:n) (w:boldness/daring/courage) (d:ngam, dare, with the noun suffix na: being bold enough to do something; placed after the verb, as in gen ngamna, daring to speak) (e:thutang gen ~ lungsim ka nei hi/thu kong gen ~ hong maisak in | forgive my boldness in speaking/Lawmte’ tang ding sih ~ sangin | than daring to die for one’s friends/hang tak-a hilh ~ in nopna piangsak hi | boldly daring to correct brings peace) (s:hanna) (a:launa) (b:ngam) (r:33.3.8/1.18.27/43.15.13/20.10.10) (q:draft)
ngamnate = (t:n) (w:acts of daring/boldness) (d:ngamna, daring, with plural te; mawh gamtat ngamnate is their daring to act sinfully) (e:amaute’ mawh gamtat ~ a seelna-un) (b:ngamna) (r:65.1.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngampa = (t:n) (w:one who dares) (d:ngam, dare, with pa, the male one: the one who dares to do something) (e:amaute a mawhsak ~ in Pasian ahi hi) (b:ngam) (r:18.34.18) (q:draft)
ngamte = (t:n) (w:those who dare/those who risk) (d:ngam, dare, with plural te: the ones who dared to do something; ngawng a dawh ngamte are those who risked their necks) (e:amau ngawng a dawh ~ ahi uh hi) (b:ngam) (r:45.16.4) (q:draft)
ngamzaw = (t:v) (w:would rather dare/be more willing) (d:ngam, dare, with zaw, more or rather; sum ngamzaw is be willing rather to lose) (e:na dang khempeuh ka sum ~ lai hi/sum ~ mai lo na hi uh hiam | why not rather accept the loss) (b:ngam) (r:50.3.8/46.6.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngana = (t:num) (w:fifth) (d:nga, five, with na, which makes an ordinal number: fifth; sawm-le-ngana is fifteenth) (e:Jakob tawh tapa a ~ nei hi/a lina Nethanel, a ~ Raddai | the fourth Nethanel, the fifth Raddai/a ~ Malkhijah tung | the fifth to Malkijah) (b:nga) (r:13.2.14/1.30.17/13.24.9)
nganeu = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:small fish) (d:nga, fish, with neu, small) (e:khomun pum nga leh ~ tawn nih) (r:43.6.9) (q:draft)
ngangngang = (t:adv) (w:throbbing) (d:placed after a verb of pain, describing a continual throbbing ache; tum ngangngang is ache without stopping) (e:meima nai tawm bangin hong tum ~ hi) (r:19.42.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngap = (t:v) (w:dare/be up to/venture) (d:have the courage or the strength to do something; na ngap nak leh is if you dare, ka ngap kei is I am not up to it) (e:Na ~ nak leh na minthan’ nading/Thatang nasep lah ka ~ kei a | I am not strong enough for manual work/bang ciang taktak a hihzo ~ uh hiam | how much they are really able to do) (s:ngam) (r:18.40.10/42.16.3/46.4.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngap = (t:v) (w:ford/wade across/cross) (d:cross water on foot, as at a ford; ka ngap zo kei hi, I could not get across) (e:amaute in ngahmun ~ uh hi/ka ~ zo kei hi | I could not wade across) (s:ngaptan) (r:10.19.18/26.47.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngapi = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:great fish/huge fish/whale) (d:nga, fish, with pi, big: the great fish that swallowed Jonah) (e:Jonah in tua ~ gil sung panin/Jonah in ~’ gil sungah ni thum a om | Jonah was three days in the belly of the great fish/Topa in tua ~ sawl a | the Lord commanded the great fish/Topa in ~ khat a geelkholh sa hi a | the Lord had prepared a great fish) (b:nga) (r:32.2.1/32.1.17/40.12.40/32.2.10) (q:draft)
ngaptan = (t:v) (w:wade through/ford/cross on foot) (d:ngap ford, with tan, cut across: go through water on foot; with sak, lead someone through) (e:a tui kei hong ~ sak hi/tua lai-ah a tui hong ~ sak a | there he led me through the water) (s:ngap) (r:26.47.3/26.47.4) (q:draft)
ngaptansak = (t:v) (w:lead through water/make wade through) (d:ngaptan wade through, with sak, cause to: take someone across water on foot) (e:a tui kei hong ~ hi/a tui hong ~ a, khuk ciang tum hi | he led me through water that came up to the knees) (b:ngaptan) (r:26.47.3/26.47.4) (q:draft)
ngapzo = (t:v) (w:be able to wade across/be able to ford) (d:ngap, wade across, with zo, be able) (e:a tui thuklua ta ahih manin ka ~ kei hi) (b:ngap) (r:26.47.5) (q:draft)
ngasa = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:fish) (d:a fish, as a living creature and as food; ngasa bengte are fishermen) (e:khomun leh ~ a lak khit ciangin/~ ngen leh, gul a pia ding | if he asks for a fish, will he give a snake/Tu-a na mat uh ~ kimkhat hong paipih un | bring some of the fish you have just caught/~ tam mahmah khuh kha a | they caught a great many fish) (s:nga) (r:43.21.13/40.7.10/43.21.10/42.5.6)
Ngasa = (t:n) (w:Fish) (d:capitalised form of ngasa fish, in the name Ngasa Kongpi, the Fish Gate of Jerusalem) (e:tapate in ~ Kongpi bawl uh hi/Jerusalem khua ~ Kulh kongpi-ah | at the Fish Gate of Jerusalem) (b:ngasa) (r:16.3.3/16.12.39/36.1.10) (q:draft)
ngasak = (t:v) (w:make face/turn toward/lay on) (d:nga, face or be turned toward, with the causative sak: make a thing face a direction; of hands, lay them on someone) (e:lu tungah amau’ khut ~ inla/a tehte zong tua lam mah ~ hi | it turned its branches toward him too/a vomte khempeuh’ lam ~ hi | he made them face all the dark ones) (s:ngatsak/ngaksak) (b:nga) (r:3.24.14/1.30.40/26.17.7) (q:draft)
ngasalip = (t:n) (w:fish scale/scales) (d:ngasa, fish, with lip, scale) (e:~ tawh a kibang na pawlkhat kia a) (r:44.9.18) (q:draft)
ngasate = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:fish) (e:tui sung ~ zong va dong un/tui sunga om ~ | the fish in the sea/a ~ uh sisak hi | he made their fish die/Nail gun sunga ~ si hi | the fish in the Nile died) (s:ngate) (b:ngasa) (r:18.12.8/19.105.29/19.8.8/2.7.21) plural form of <ngasa>
ngasiahna = (t:n) (w:fishing/angling) (d:catching fish with a hook; ngasiahna sikkawi is a fish hook) (e:Nail gun sungah ~ sikkawi a khia ngei) (r:23.19.8) (q:draft)
ngasuk = (t:v) (w:lower/let down/set down) (d:put a carried thing down, with suk, downward: lower a jar or a sack to the ground) (e:a van uh leilakah ~ uh a/na beel hong ~ in | let down your jar) (s:koihsuk) (r:1.44.11/1.24.14) (q:draft)
ngat = (t:v) (w:turn toward/incline/face) (d:turn a part of the body toward something; bil ngat is incline the ear, pay attention, mai ngat is set the face toward, and nung ngat is turn the back on) (e:Na bil uh hong ~ un la/kei lamah na bil hong ~ in la | turn your ear toward me/a maitang gamlak lam ~ hi | he turned his face toward the wilderness/kei hong nung ~-in hong thudon lo uh a | they turned their backs on me and paid no heed) (s:maingat) (r:23.28.23/14.6.40/19.71.2/4.24.1/24.32.33) (q:draft)
ngate = (t:n) (w:fish) (b:nga) plural form of <nga>
ngatin = (t:v) (w:facing/turning toward) (d:ngat, turn toward, with the linking ending in: with the face or ear turned toward something while another action follows) (e:a mai kawm lam ~ Topa tungah thungen/leilak lam mai ~ kunin | bowing with her face to the ground/Na bil uh hong ~, mipilte’ thugen ngai un la | turn your ear and listen to the sayings of the wise/a maitang uh lei lam ~ | with their faces to the ground) (b:ngat) (r:12.20.2/1.42.6/11.1.31/20.22.17) (q:draft)
ngatna = (t:n) (w:direction faced/facing) (d:ngat, face or turn toward, with the noun suffix na; the side or direction toward which a thing is turned) (e:Na ~ san peuhpeuh vat gawp in/biakinn ~ nisuahna lamah luang sukin | flowing down eastward, the way the temple faced) (b:ngat) (r:26.21.16/26.47.1) (q:draft)
ngato = (t:see) <ngato-in>
ngato-in = (t:v) (w:lifting up/raising onto) (d:with to, upward, and in, linking to the next verb: lifting a load up onto the shoulder) (e:a liangko tung uhah ~ pua uh a) (r:23.46.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngatsak = (t:v) (w:make face/turn toward) (d:ngat, face, with the causative sak: make something face a certain way) (e:khempeuhte’ kimai ~ hi) (s:ngasak) (b:ngat) (r:1.30.40) (q:draft)
ngattakin = (t:adv) (w:strictly/firmly) (d:strictly, without exception: ngat with takin, which makes an adverb; said of a law that must be strictly obeyed) (e:~ zuih ding thukham khat/~ a kizuih kul ding hi | it must be strictly obeyed) (s:khauhtakin/kiptakin) (r:27.6.7/27.6.8) (q:draft)
