ngawg = (t:n) (w:neck) (d:probably a spelling of ngawng, neck; a ngawg kuaitan is break its neck) (e:a ~ na kuaitan ding uh hi) (s:ngawng) (r:2.13.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngawh = (t:v) (w:hold accountable/blame/charge/accuse) (d:lay the guilt for something on someone; sihna sisan ngawh is hold someone accountable for a death) (e:ama sihna sisan nang kong ~ ding hi/amaute’ sihna sisan pen galvilpa ka ~ ding hi | I will hold the watchman accountable for their blood/ka pa’ innkuante khempeuh ahi zongin ~ kei in | do not accuse any of my father’s family either/amau’ sihna amau mah ~ ding ahi hi | their death is to be charged to themselves/Israelte’ khialhna kua ~ ding i hi hiam | whom shall we blame for the sin of Israel) (s:mawhsak) (r:26.33.8/26.33.6/9.22.15/3.20.11/33.1.5) (q:draft)
ngawh = (t:adv) (w:harshly/roughly/angrily) (d:placed before or after a verb, harshly or in anger; ngawh dawn is answer harshly) (e:kumpipa in amaute ~ dawnin/kumpipa in mite ~ dawn’ a | the king answered the people harshly/Na pa in nang hong ~ dawn’ leh | if your father answers you harshly/ka heh ~ pah ding a) (r:14.10.13/11.12.13/9.20.10/3.26.28) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngawhdawn = (t:v) (w:answer harshly/reply roughly) (d:ngawh, harshly, with dawn, answer: give someone a harsh answer) (e:kumpipa in mite ~ a) (r:11.12.13) (q:draft)
ngawhin = (t:v) (w:blaming/accusing) (d:ngawh, blame, with the linking suffix in: blaming; Topa ngawhin heh is be angry and put the blame on the Lord) (e:Topa ~ mawk heh uh hi) (s:mawhsakin) (b:ngawh) (r:20.19.3) (q:draft)
ngawhpiak = (t:v) (w:give in anger) (d:ngawh, in anger, with piak, give: give something in anger) (e:Na kumpi dingte uh kong ~ a) (r:28.13.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngawl = (t:v) (w:go without/abstain from/fast) (d:go without something; an ngawl is go without food, fast) (e:tua zan tawntung an ~ a) (r:27.6.18) (q:draft)
ngawlin = (t:v) (w:going without/fasting/abstaining from) (d:ngawl, go without, with the linking suffix in; an ngawlin is going without food, fasting) (e:An ~, ippi puan silhin/ni sawm-le-li tawntung an ~, gil kialin | going without food for fourteen days, hungry/an ~ a puksi veve ding ahi hi | he will surely starve to death/tua zan tawntung an ~ gualnopna zong | going without food all that night) (b:ngawl) (r:27.9.3/44.27.33/24.38.9/27.6.18) (q:draft)
ngawn = (t:part) (w:indeed/surely) (d:word of emphasis placed after a verb or after kei, stressing that something is surely so or surely not so; na ngawn is another way of writing nangawn, even) (e:hehna tawh daantat ~ ding hi/ka Pasian ka phatkik ~ ding hi | I will surely praise my God again/Pasian in hong mu kei ~ | God surely does not see us/Abraham’ suante ihi ~ hi | we are indeed descendants of Abraham/Pasian in amaute’ thu khen ~ ding hi | God will surely judge them) (r:18.20.23/24.12.4/19.43.5/40.3.9/46.5.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngawng = (t:n) (w:neck) (d:the neck of a person or animal; ngawng tan is behead, and puan ngawng is the collar of a garment) (e:thong sungah Johan’ ~ a tan sak hi/A ~ thakhauh mahmah ahih manin | because its neck is very strong/ama ~ pen sikkol sungah kikoih hi | his neck was put in irons/ka puan ~ pan hong manin | seizing me by the collar of my garment) (s:gawl) (r:40.14.10/18.41.22/19.105.18/18.30.18) (q:draft)
