ngawngin = (t:n) (w:by the neck) (d:ngawng, neck, with the marker in: by the neck; ngawngin man is seize by the neck) (e:keimah in a ~ manin vatgawpin) (b:ngawng) (r:9.17.35) (q:draft)
ngawngkawi = (t:see) <ngawngkawi-in>
ngawngkawi-in = (t:v) (w:embracing/hugging/throwing the arms around) (d:ngawng, neck, with kawi, embrace, and the linking suffix in: putting the arms around the neck of someone) (e:a ta ~ a nam hi) (r:42.15.20) (q:draft)
ngawngzangah = (t:n) (w:on the neck) (d:ngawngzang, the neck or nape, with the place marker ah: on the neck, said of a yoke or load) (e:lomkhat suahin ka ~ hong khih a/a etlawm a ~ kol bulhin | putting a yoke on her fair neck) (s:ngawngah) (r:25.1.14/28.10.11) (q:draft)
ngeek = (t:adj) (w:tender/delicate/very young) (d:soft and very young; said of infants, young animals and new grass, and in a ngeek dikdek of a delicate woman) (e:a ~ dikdek Zion tanu ka susia ding hi/no ~ a neite pen dam takin paipih ding | he will gently lead those that have young/lo ~ tunga guah phin | light rain on tender grass/Naupangte a ~ sih om lo ding | no child will die in infancy) (s:ngek) (r:24.6.2/23.40.11/5.32.2/23.65.20) (q:draft)
ngeekte = (t:adj) (w:tender/newborn/very young) (d:ngeek, tender, with the plural ending te, of what is very young and soft; ta ngeekte is newborn babies and lopa ngeekte is tender grass) (e:a ta ~ uh a sih nadingin/lo lai-a kungnote leh lopa ~ | young plants in the field and tender grass/A ta ~ nangawn uh kikaikhia takpi ding | even their little ones will surely be dragged away/a ta ~ uh gilkial dangtakin sisak uh | they let their infants die of hunger and thirst) (b:ngeek) (r:44.7.19/23.37.26/24.50.45/25.4.4) (q:draft)
ngeen = (t:n) (w:net/fishing net) (d:another spelling of ngen, a net for catching fish) (e:tui tungah ~ a paii mite/ngasa nam tampi a awk thei ~ tawh kibang | is like a net that can catch many kinds of fish) (s:ngen) (r:23.19.8/40.13.47) (q:draft)
ngei = (t:part) (w:have been/ever) (d:placed after a verb: have ever done or been so; with kei or lo it means never) (e:tua thute thei~ lo hi ung/kua in Pasian tungah pia ~ hiam | who has ever given to God/A ling ~ lo dingin | so that it will never shake/Sun lai takin kongkhak kikhak ~ lo hi | by day the gates are never shut/keimah hong zahhuaisak ~ kei in | never let me be put to shame) (r:45.11.35/19.104.5/66.21.25/19.71.1)
ngei = (t:part) (w:culture/tradition) (e:hih pen ka ~na uh hi)
