ngeii = (t:see) <ngeii-ngai>
ngeii-ngai = (t:adv) (d:expressive word after ot shout, describing loud ringing shouting) (e:ci-in a ot ~ lai takin) (s:ngeingai) (r:38.4.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngeikei = (t:adv) (w:never) (d:ngei, ever, with kei, not, placed after a verb: will never, or may it never, be so) (e:a kumpi gam a bei ~ ding hi/zingsang phalvak mu ~ hen | may it never see the first light of dawn) (s:ngeilo/cikmah) (a:den/tawntunga) (r:27.7.14/18.3.9) (q:draft)
ngeilo = (t:adv) (w:never) (d:ngei, ever, with lo, not, placed after a verb: has never done or has never been so) (e:hih bang om ~ ahih manin/a kine ~ nawite in thupha a ngah ding | the breasts that never nursed will be blessed/khatvei beek sim ~ na hi uh hiam | have you never once read it/Amah guallel-in zahhuai ~ ding hi | he will never be put to shame in defeat) (s:ngeikei/cikmah) (a:den/tawntunga) (b:ngei) (r:14.30.26/42.23.29/40.21.42/19.127.5) (q:draft)
ngeiloh = (t:adv) (w:never) (d:form of ngeilo, never, used inside a dependent clause, as before hangin, although, or before a noun) (e:na muh ~ uh hangin na it uh hi/kote in ka zak ~ uh thu | things that we have never heard) (b:ngeilo) (r:60.1.8/44.17.20) (q:draft)
ngeilohna = (t:n) (w:never before) (d:ngeiloh, never, with the suffix na joining it to a following noun: a kizak ngeilohna mun is a place where it has never been heard) (e:min a kizak ~ munah Lungdamna Thu) (b:ngeiloh) (r:45.15.20) (q:draft)
ngeina = (t:n) (w:culture/tradition/custom/regulation) (d:the customary way of doing things, handed down from the ancestors; biakna ngeina is a fixed rule of worship) (e:Na tanglai ~ uh zui-in/note in na ~ uh na zuih theih nadingun | so that you may keep your own tradition/biakna ~ kip-in na nei tawntung ding uh hi | you shall keep it as a lasting rule of worship/Hih in mawhna hanga biakna ~ ahi hi | this is the regulation for the guilt offering) (b:ngei) (r:40.15.6/41.7.9/2.12.24/3.7.1)
ngeinate = (t:n) (w:customs/regulations/statutes) (d:ngeina, custom, with the plural te: the customs of a people, or the rules laid down for worship) (e:nangma ~ zuih ding ka kiciam hi/minamte’ ~ na zui kei ding uh hi | you must not follow the customs of the nations/hih Purim bawl nading ~ kipsak a | it confirmed these regulations for keeping Purim/amaute’ tat ~ zui kei un | do not follow their customs) (s:tatziate) (b:ngeina) (r:19.119.59/3.20.23/17.9.32/26.20.18) (q:draft)
ngeinazah = (t:n) (w:usual amount/usual degree) (d:ngeina, custom, with zah, amount: as much as is usual; ngeinazah sangin is more than usual) (e:A sat ~ sangin a zah sagihvei) (r:27.3.19) (q:draft)
ngeingai = (t:adv) (d:expressive word placed after a verb, showing that the action goes on in a noisy stir or commotion, often by many people at once) (e:hangin mihonte phun ~ uh a/Inn tung khawngah kahto ~ uh a | they swarm up onto the houses/ci-in a awng ~ uh hi | they kept shouting/amau tegel vuakpih ~ uh a | they all joined in beating the two of them/tua ganhing a zui ~ uh hi | they all went after the beast) (s:ngeii-ngai) (r:43.6.41/29.2.9/40.27.23/44.16.22/66.13.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngeingeisa = (t:adj) (w:heard before/already experienced) (d:ngei said twice, with sa, already: what has been done or heard time and again before) (e:a genna ka zak ~ ahi hi) (r:19.62.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngeingeite = (t:n) (w:common experiences/usual things) (d:ngei said twice, with the plural te: things that happen again and again; mite tuah ngeingeite is what people commonly meet with) (e:tuah ~ mah ahi hi) (r:46.10.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngeipa = (t:n) (d:ngei, have done or been before, with pa, the male one; after a verb or descriptive word, the man who did so or was so before, as in a mittaw ngeipa, the man who had been blind) (e:a mittaw ~ sam kik uh a/kei hong huh ~ na hi hi | you are the one who has helped me/hong mu ~ in kei hong mu nawn lo | the one who has seen me will see me no more) (b:ngei) (r:43.9.24/19.27.9/18.7.8) (q:draft)
ngeisa = (t:adj) (w:former/previous/past) (d:placed after a verb or noun for what has been, or was done, before; from ngei, ever, and sa, already) (e:Joel in a hilh ~ thu ahi hi/hauhna ~ khempeuh Izipt gamsungah kimangngilh ding hi | all the former abundance will be forgotten in Egypt/Na hih ~ na liante | the great deeds you did before/a inn masa a mu ~ siampite | the priests who had seen the first house) (s:beisa) (b:ngei) (r:44.2.16/1.41.30/35.3.2/15.3.12) (q:draft)
ngeisate = (t:n) (w:former things/past things) (d:ngeisa, former, with the plural te; ka pianzia ngeisate is my former way of life) (e:ka pianzia ~ khempeuh na zaksa) (b:ngeisa) (r:48.1.14) (q:draft)
ngeite = (t:part) (d:ngei with the plural te after a verb: the things one is used to doing, or the ones who have done so before; gamtat ngeite is the accustomed ways) (e:a nasep ~ uh nusia-in/Migilote’ gamtat ~ mah gamtat ding | to walk in the very ways the wicked have walked/mi khempeuh a lausak ~ hi uh a | they were the ones who had terrified everyone/khuk zaw mite na hatsak ~ ngaihsun in | think of the weak knees you have strengthened) (b:ngei) (r:16.13.10/18.22.15/26.32.24/18.4.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
