niamkhiatin = (t:v) (w:humbling/bringing low) (d:niamkhiat, humble or bring low, with the linking ending in, joining it to the next verb) (e:amah in note hong ~ hong gilkial sak a/a lungsim uh ~ | humbling their hearts/note hong ~ hong ze-et theih nadingin | to humble you and test you/ka Pasian in kei hong ~ | my God humbling me) (b:niamkhiat) (r:5.8.3/5.8.16/3.26.41/47.12.21) (q:draft)
niamkhiatna = (t:n) (w:humiliation/abasement) (d:niamkhiat, bring low, with the noun suffix na: the state of being brought low; niamkhiatna thuak is be humbled) (e:A kiphasakte in ~ thuak ding a/a kilamsang peuhmah in ~ a thuak ding hi | whoever exalts himself will be humbled/vantungmite nuai-ah neukha bek ~ a thuak mi Zeisu | Jesus, who was made a little lower than the angels/~ a ngah ding uh hi | they will be humbled) (s:niamsakna) (a:pahtawina) (b:niamkhiat) (r:20.29.23/40.23.12/58.2.9/42.14.11) (q:draft)
niamkhiatna = (t:n) (w:humility/lowliness) (d:in lungsim niamkhiatna, a humble mind) (e:lungsim ~ tawh pilna kingah hi/lungsim ~ tawh khat leh khat na kingaihsun un | in humility consider one another) (s:kiniamkhiatna/lungniamkhiatna) (a:kiphatsakna) (b:niamkhiat) (r:20.11.2/50.2.3) (q:draft)
niamkhiatte = (t:n) (w:the humble/the lowly) (d:niamkhiat bring low, with plural te; lungsim niamkhiatte is those lowly in spirit) (e:Lungsim ~ in thupha a ngah ding) (s:kiniamkhiatte/miniamte) (a:kiphasakte) (b:niamkhiat) (r:40.5.3) (q:draft)
niamkoih = (t:v) (w:bring low/humble/abase) (d:niam low, with koih put: put someone in a low place) (e:Topa in Judah mite ~ hi/Kei nong ~ mahmah hi | you have brought me very low) (s:niamkhiat/niamsak) (a:sangkoih) (r:14.28.19/7.11.35) (q:draft)
niamkoihsuk = (t:v) (w:bring down/lay low/cut down) (d:niamkoih bring low, with suk downward) (e:a kitengkhia mite ~ hi) (b:niamkoih) (r:19.78.31) (q:draft)
niamna = (t:n) (w:lowland/low place/foothills) (d:niam, low, with the noun suffix na: a low place; lei niamna is the lowland or foothills, as against mualtung gam, the hill country) (e:ciangin lei ~ lamah Eshtaol/lei ~-a teeng Kanaan mite | the Canaanites living in the lowland/a ~ mun leivui sung panin | from the low place, out of the dust/mualtung gam leh lei ~ gam | the hill country and the lowland) (a:sangna) (b:niam) (r:6.15.33/7.1.9/23.29.4/6.9.1) (q:draft)
niamnate = (t:see) <kinen'niamnate>
niampen = (t:adj) (w:lowest) (d:niam, low, with pen, most: lowest in place or least in rank) (e:zumna tawh a ~ munah na tu/Benjamin minam innkuan khempeuh sung panin a ~ | the least of all the clans of the tribe of Benjamin) (a:sangpen) (b:niam) (r:42.14.9/9.9.21)
niampenna = (t:n) (w:lowest part/lowest point) (d:niampen lowest, with the suffix na; mun niampenna is the lowest place) (e:kulh nung lam mun ~ mun awng tengah) (a:sangpenna) (b:niampen) (r:16.4.13) (q:draft)
niamsak = (t:v) (w:lower/bring down/humble) (d:niam, low, with the causative sak: make low, lower a thing such as the hands, or humble a person) (e:Nasep haksatna tawh amaute’ lungsim ~ hi/mihing khat a sangsak, mihing khat a ~ | he exalts one and brings another down/amah in a khut a ~ peuhmah ciangin | whenever he lowered his hands/mi kiphasakte na ~ hi | you bring the proud low/keima pumpi ka ~ a | I lowered myself) (s:niamkhiat/niamkoih) (a:sangsak/sangtosak) (b:niam) (r:19.107.12/19.75.7/2.17.11/19.18.27/47.11.7) (q:draft)
niamsakin = (t:v) (w:lowering/bowing down) (d:niamsak make low, with the linking ending in; vantungte niamsakin is bowing the heavens, where the NIV has parted) (e:vantungte ~ hong paisuk a/Amah in vanpi ~ hong kumsuk a | he bowed the heavens and came down) (b:niamsak) (r:10.22.10/19.18.9) (q:draft)
niamsakna = (t:n) (w:humiliation/being brought low) (d:niamsak, make low, with the noun suffix na; niamsakna a thuak mite are those who are bowed down) (e:~ a thuak mite sangto sak a/~ a ngah mite khempeuh sangto sak hi | he lifts up all who are bowed down) (s:niamkhiatna) (b:niamsak) (r:19.146.8/19.145.14) (q:draft)
niamsuk = (t:v) (w:go down low/sink) (d:niam low, with suk downward; niamsuk sak is bring down) (e:Pasian in ~ sak ding hi) (b:niam) (r:23.25.11) (q:draft)
niamsuksakin = (t:v) (w:lowering/letting down) (d:niamsuk, go down low, with sak, cause, and in, linking to the next verb) (e:a khut tungah a beel ~ amah) (b:niamsuk) (r:1.24.18) (q:draft)
niamta = (t:v) (w:have become low) (d:niam low, with ta now, already; ni niamta is the sun is now low, the day is nearly over) (e:tu-in nitak nai-in ni ~ hi) (b:niam) (r:7.19.9) (q:draft)
niamte = (t:adj) (w:lowly/humble/low) (d:with the plural ending te; mi niamte, the humble or lowly people) (e:Amah in mi ~ sangkoih a/Nangmah in mi ~ na honkhia a | you save the humble/mi ~ gum hi | he saves the lowly) (b:niam) (r:18.5.11/10.22.28/18.22.29) (q:draft)
niamzaw = (t:adj) (w:lower/inferior) (d:niam low, with zaw more; used with sangin, than) (e:tual sangin ~ hi/note sangin themkhat zong ka ~ tuan kei hi | I am not in the least inferior to you) (a:sangzaw) (b:niam) (r:26.40.18/18.12.3) (q:draft)
niangnuangte = (t:adj) (w:feeble/weak) (d:with the plural te, said in contempt of people who look weak) (e:Hih Judah mi ~ in bang hih dinga kipan) (r:16.4.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
Nibhaz = (t:name) (w:Nibhaz) (d:idol made by the Avvites whom the king of Assyria settled in Samaria) (r:12.17.31)
Nibshan = (t:name) (c:land/city) (w:Nibshan) (d:town in the wilderness of Judah, listed with the City of Salt and En Gedi) (r:6.15.62)
nidang = (t:adv) (w:formerly/in the past/before) (d:in former times, in the past; nidang lai is the time gone by and nidang bangin is as before) (e:Laban in ~ bangin maipha tawh/~ lai a, a sukgawpsa upna thu | the faith he once tried to destroy/~-a a om ngei bangun | as they were before/a ~ hun uh ka bangsak kik ding hi | I will restore their former days/~ lai a, gamlapi-ah a om note | you who once were far away) (s:tuma/tumasiah) (r:1.31.2/45.15.4/48.1.23/24.33.7/29.3.1/49.2.13) (q:draft)
nidanga = (t:adv) (w:formerly/earlier/in the past) (d:nidang with the ending a: formerly, at an earlier time; before a noun it means former, of earlier days) (e:~ na vangliatna na ngahkik ding a/~ na omzia uh phawkkik dih un | remember how you formerly lived/a ~ ngeina bangin gamta uh hi | they act according to their former customs/A ~ Zeisu kiangah hong pai | who had earlier come to Jesus/~ a thupitnate a nung phawk kik uh hi | they remember her former glories) (s:tumasiah) (b:nidang) (r:33.4.8/43.7.50/49.2.11/12.17.34/25.1.7) (q:draft)
Nidanga = (t:name) (w:Nidanga) (d:the adverb nidanga, formerly, written with a capital at the start of a sentence)
nidangin = (t:adv) (w:formerly/in the past/before) (d:nidang, former time, with the marker in: in the past, before now, often set against tu-in, now) (e:~ a kiho thei kei uh hi/~ nang adingin kiman’na om lo mi | a man formerly useless to you/Debir min pen ~ Kiriathsefer ahi hi | the name of Debir was formerly Kiriath Sepher/~ hih bang piang ngei lo hi | nothing like this has happened before/Hor mite zong Seir-ah ~ teeng ngei a | the Horites also used to live in Seir) (s:tuma/tumasiah) (b:nidang) (r:42.23.12/57.1.11/7.1.11/9.4.7/5.2.12) (q:draft)
nidangte = (t:n) (w:the other days/other days) (d:ni, day, with dang, other, and the plural te: the rest of the days of a year or a month) (e:kha khat sunga ~ lakah/Kum khat sunga ~ tawh kisim khawm kei hen | let it not be counted with the other days of the year) (r:18.3.6) (q:draft)
Nidas = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Cnidus) (d:port city on the south-west coast of Asia Minor, passed by the ship that carried Paul toward Rome) (r:44.27.7)
Niger = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Niger) (d:byname of Simeon, one of the prophets and teachers in the church at Antioch) (r:44.13.1)
niguk = (t:n) (w:six days) (d:ni, day, with guk, six, written together; niguk sung is for six days) (e:Tua bangin ~ sung hih uh hi/Tua bangin ~ sung na pai ding uh hi | you shall march like this for six days) (r:6.6.14/6.6.3) (q:draft)
nih = (t:num) (w:two) (d:the number two; it follows the noun it counts, and sawm-le-nih is twelve) (e:ni ~/Mi khat in tapa ~ a nei hi | a man had two sons/unau numei ~ om hi | there were two sisters/Mi ~ thukimna om masa lopi-in | unless two people have first agreed) (r:42.15.11/1.1.16/26.23.2/30.3.3)
Nih = (t:num) (w:two/twin) (d:nih, two, written with a capital in Pasian Nih, the Two Gods, the twin gods Castor and Pollux carved as the figurehead of a ship) (b:nih) (r:44.28.11) (q:draft)
nihin = (t:adv) (w:both/in two/two by two/in pairs) (d:nih, two, with in: a nihin is both of them, nih nihin is two by two, and gual nihin or pawl nihin is in two rows or groups) (e:Pa leh Tapa a ~ a neikhawm hi/nih ~ Noah tawh teembaw sungah pai uh hi | they went into the ark with Noah two by two/tua um gahte gual ~ om a | the gourds were in two rows/Israel mite pawl ~ kikhen uh hi | the people of Israel split into two groups/a ~ sun khawm hi | he speared both of them together) (b:nih) (r:63.1.9/1.7.15/14.4.3/11.16.21/4.25.8) (q:draft)
nihna = (t:num) (w:second) (d:nih, two, with the ordinal suffix na: second; sawm-le-nihna is twelfth) (e:ni ~ ahi hi/a tacil Joel, a ~ Abijah ahi uh hi | Joel the firstborn and Abijah the second/A ukpi Ezer, a ~ Obadiah | Ezer the chief, Obadiah the second/a ~ Jedaiah tung | the second fell to Jedaiah) (b:nih) (r:1.1.8/13.12.9/13.6.28/13.24.7)
Nihna = (t:num) (w:second) (d:nihna, second, written with a capital at the start of a sentence or in a name: Veng Nihna is the Second Quarter of Jerusalem, in the NIV the New Quarter, and Jeroboam Nihna is Jeroboam the Second) (e:tua khuapi Veng ~ sungah mite’ kahna/~ gimna a bei zo hi | the second woe has passed/~ vantungmi in peengkul a tum ciangin | when the second angel blew his trumpet/Jerusalem khua sung a Veng ~ ah teng hi | she lived in the Second Quarter of Jerusalem) (b:nihna) (r:36.1.10/12.15.1/66.11.14/66.8.8/12.22.14) (q:draft)
nihnapa = (t:n) (w:the second) (d:nihna, second, with pa marking a man: after a name, the second man of that name, as Jeroboam the Second; also the man second in rank) (e:Jeroboam a ~ a tu hi/a tapa Jeroboam a ~ in uk hi | his son Jeroboam the Second reigned/Judah in khuapi uk a ~ ahi hi | Judah was second in charge of the city) (b:nihna) (r:12.13.13/16.11.9/12.14.16) (q:draft)
nihnate = (t:n) (w:those second in rank/seconds) (d:nihna, second, with the plural te: the men who rank next after the chief) (e:amah zomah a ~ in Zekhariah) (b:nihna) (r:13.16.5) (q:draft)
nihta = (t:num) (w:two each) (d:nih, two, with ta, each: two at a time, as two lambs each day) (e:kum khat a pha tuuno ~ hi ding hi) (b:nih) (r:2.29.38) (q:draft)
nihte = (t:num) (w:two/both) (d:nih, two, with the plural te: the two, both of them; Sawm-le-nihte is the Twelve) (e:a tapa ~ leh a pasal in/nungzui ~ in ama thu a zak uh ciangin | when the two disciples heard him speak/a kal ~ a thau tawh | both kidneys with their fat/kham khau ~ na khum ding hi | you shall fasten the two gold chains) (b:nih) (r:8.1.5/42.9.30/43.1.37/3.4.9/2.28.24) (q:draft)
nihun = (t:pron) (w:both/the two together) (d:nih, two, with the plural ending un; used after a, na, ka or i: a nihun is both of them, na nihun both of you, ka nihun the two of us) (e:a ~ a pukkhawm uh hi/a ~ tui sungah a pai uh a | they both went down into the water/na ~ hong kiphiatkhia ding hi | both of you will be swept away/a ~ hawkguam sungah kiakhawm ding uh hi | both will fall into a pit/ka ~ tua mite kiangah pai-in | we two will come to them) (b:nih) (r:24.46.12/9.12.25/44.8.38/40.15.14/43.14.23) (q:draft)
nihvei = (t:adv) (w:twice/a second time) (d:nih, two, with vei, time: two times, or for the second time; khatvei nihvei is once or twice) (e:vantung panin ~ aw in hong ci hi/khatvei ~ khawng Jerusalem pua lamah giak uh hi | once or twice they spent the night outside Jerusalem/tuzan aak ~ a khuan’ ma-in | tonight before the rooster crows twice/Saul in a teipi-in David ~ khawh hi | Saul hurled his spear at David twice) (r:44.11.9/16.13.20/41.14.30/9.18.11) (q:draft)
nihveina = (t:num) (w:second time/second) (d:nihvei, twice, with the ending na: the second time something is done; a nihveina is for the second time) (e:Israel mite a ~ vun at kik in/Topa in Jonah tungah a ~ thu gen a | the Lord spoke to Jonah a second time/Tua phetin ~ aak a khuang hi | immediately the rooster crowed the second time/Amah in a ~ sawl a | he sent a second time) (b:nihvei) (r:6.5.2/40.26.42/32.3.1/41.14.72/10.14.29) (q:draft)
niim = (t:adj) (w:overcast/gloomy/dim) (d:dull and dark, said of the sky or the day in khua niim; the same word as nim) (e:Van sanin khua ~ ahih manin/Khua ~ leh khuamial in khuhcip hen | may gloom and darkness cover it) (s:nim) (r:40.16.3/18.3.5) (q:draft)
niin = (t:n) (w:on the day) (d:ni day, with the marker in; usually written ni-in) (e:a ni sagih ~ Topa na) (b:ni) (r:2.20.10) (q:draft)
niinpa = (t:n) (w:stubble) (d:dry stalks left in a field, which fire burns up quickly; also written ninpa; the build of the word is not clear) (e:Esau innkuante ~ ahi ding uh a) (s:ninpa/buhtu/nahpa) (r:31.1.18) (q:draft, low confidence)
niinsak = (t:v) (w:defile/desecrate/make unclean) (d:make a holy place or thing unclean; a spelling of ninsak with a long vowel) (e:biakinnpi huang a ~ ding uh hi) (s:ninsak/nitsak) (a:siangsak) (r:27.11.31) (q:draft)
nik = (t:n) (w:skirt) (d:a woman's lower garment; to lift or strip off the nik is a picture of putting someone to shame) (e:Keimahmah in na ~ kong hawksak ding a/na ~ hong kihawk gawp sak a | your skirts have been torn off/Na ~ kong hawkkhiatsak ding a | I will lift up your skirts) (r:24.13.26/23.47.2/24.13.22/34.3.5) (q:draft)
Nikai = (t:name) (w:Nikai) (d:nikai, afternoon, written with a capital at the start of a sentence; Nikai nai thum is three in the afternoon) (r:44.10.3)
Nikanor = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Nicanor) (d:one of the seven men chosen in Jerusalem to oversee the daily distribution of food) (r:44.6.5)
nikhat = (t:n) (w:one day/a day) (d:ni, day, with khat, one: a single day; nikhat sung is within one day, nikhat sung lam is a day's journey, and nikhat ni ciangin is one day, some day) (e:~ sung lam a pai khit ciangin/~ ni ciangin muattheih nading thu panin suakta-in | one day being set free from decay/ni sawmnih leh ~ sung a hong nial hi | he resisted me for twenty-one days/~ sunga mi thennih le tulthum tak | twenty-three thousand people in one day) (r:32.3.4/18.1.6/45.8.21/27.10.13/46.10.8) (q:draft)
Nikoda = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Nekoda) (d:ancestor of a family of temple servants who returned from the exile) (r:16.7.50)
Nikodemas = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Nicodemus) (d:Pharisee and member of the Jewish council who came to Jesus by night and later helped to bury him) (r:43.3.1/43.7.50)
Nikolas = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Nicolas) (d:convert to Judaism from Antioch, one of the seven chosen in Jerusalem; Nikolas pawlte are the Nicolaitans of Revelation) (r:44.6.5)
Nikopolis = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Nicopolis) (d:city in western Greece where Paul planned to spend the winter) (r:56.3.12)
nikten = (t:n) (w:clothing/garments) (d:clothes, what a person wears; found in the pair nikten puansilh, clothing of every kind, beside annek tuidawn, food and drink) (e:annek tuidawn, ~ puansilh i neih nakleh/annek tuidawn, ~’ puansilh nei loin | without food and clothing) (r:54.6.8/18.27.16/59.2.15) (q:draft)
nikum = (t:n) (w:last year) (d:the year before this one; nikum pekin is since last year) (e:~ pekin a khol zo uh hi) (a:kumkik) (r:47.9.2) (q:draft)
nikumin = (t:adv) (w:last year) (d:nikum, last year, with the time marker in: in the past year) (e:~ lungsim hanciamna-ah zong note in) (b:nikum) (r:47.8.10) (q:draft)
nil = (t:v) (w:throw/cast/hurl) (d:throw something away from oneself; nil suk is throw down, nil khia is cast away or reject) (e:guam sungah ka ~ suk ding a/Pasian in mawhbaang lo mi ~ khia lo ding | God will not reject a blameless person) (s:lawn/paai) (r:33.1.6/18.8.20) (q:draft)
nilang = (t:n) (w:half a day) (d:ni, day, with lang, half; nithum leh nilang is three and a half days) (e:Nithum leh ~ a cin’ khit ciangin/nithum leh ~ tawntung a en ding uh hi | they will gaze for three and a half days) (r:66.11.11/66.11.9) (q:draft)
nilh = (t:v) (w:anoint/smear/rub on) (d:put oil on a person or thing, especially to set apart a king, priest or prophet, usually as sathau nilh; nilh sathau is anointing oil) (e:ap dingin amah sathau ~ hi/amah na ~ ding hi | you shall anoint him/Nimshi’ tapa Jehu sathau na ~ ding hi | you shall anoint Jehu son of Nimshi/Pasian in teelin sathau a ~ mi nihte | the two men God has chosen and anointed) (s:nuh) (r:3.8.12/2.29.7/11.19.16/38.4.14) (q:draft)
nilhin = (t:v) (w:anoint/rub on) (d:nilh, anoint, with the linking ending in, used before a following verb, usually with sathau, oil) (e:amah sathau ~ na ap ding hi/amaute sathau ~, nasem dingin kipsakin | anointing them and ordaining them to serve/kumpi-in nang sathau hong ~ | I anointed you king/tho-in kisil a, sathau ~ a puante khek hi | he got up, washed, put on oil and changed his clothes/Jehoiada leh a tapate in amah sathau ~ | Jehoiada and his sons anointed him) (s:nuhin) (b:nilh) (r:2.40.13/10.12.20/2.28.41/10.12.7/14.23.11) (q:draft)
nilhkhol = (t:v) (w:anoint beforehand) (d:nilh, anoint, with khol, in advance: anoint ahead of time, as a body before its burial) (e:tawh a hong ~ zo hi) (s:nuhkhol) (r:41.14.8) (q:draft)
nilhna = (t:n) (w:anointing) (d:nilh, anoint, with the noun ending na: the act of anointing or the anointing received; sathau nilhna is anointing with oil) (e:Kha Siangtho sathau ~ in/kumpi-in amah sathau a ~ thu a zak ciangin | when he heard that he had been anointed king/Kha Siangtho sathau ~ in thuman thutak hi a | the anointing of the Holy Spirit is true) (s:kinilhna) (b:nilh) (r:62.2.27/11.5.1) (q:draft)
nilhpa = (t:n) (w:anointed one) (d:the man who has been anointed, usually sathau nilhpa, the one anointed with oil; nilh with pa marking a man) (e:na sathau ~ nial kei in/na sathau ~’ maitang en in | look on the face of your anointed one/Topa leh ama sathau ~ langpangin vaihawm uh a | they plot against the Lord and his anointed/na sathau ~ tungah hehna tawh na kidim hi | you are full of anger against your anointed one) (s:kinilhpa) (b:nilh) (r:19.132.10/19.2.2/19.84.9/19.89.38) (q:draft)
nilhsa = (t:adj) (w:anointed) (d:nilh, anoint, with sa, already done; sathau nilhsa is one who has been anointed with oil) (e:sathau ~ na hi uh a/Topa in sathau a ~ Nimshi’ tapa Jehu | Jehu son of Nimshi, whom the Lord had anointed/sathau na ~ na Sila siangtho Zeisu | your holy servant Jesus, whom you anointed) (b:nilh) (r:62.2.20/14.22.7/44.4.28) (q:draft)
nilhsak = (t:v) (w:anoint/put on/pour on/apply) (d:rub or pour oil or perfume on a person, and so anoint a king or priest; nilh with sak, done to or for another) (e:ka khe paknamtui tawh hong ~ hi/Ka lu sathau nong ~ kei hi | you did not put oil on my head/siampi Zadok leh kamsang Nathan sathau ~ un | let Zadok the priest and Nathan the prophet anoint him/Topa’ lu tangah a ~ hi | she poured it on the Lord's head/a min kong genpa sathau nong ~ ding hi | you shall anoint for me the one I name) (b:nilh) (r:42.7.46/11.1.34/41.14.3/9.16.3) (q:draft)
nilhte = (t:n) (w:anointed ones) (d:nilh, anoint, with the plural te: those who have been anointed, as sathau nilhte, those anointed with oil) (e:Ka sathau ~ sukha kei un/Ka sathau ~ lawng kei un | do not touch my anointed ones) (b:nilh) (r:19.105.15/13.16.22) (q:draft)
nilhte = (t:n) (d:those who anoint themselves, users of perfumed oil) (e:sathau namtui ~ hau lo hi) (b:nilh) (r:20.21.17) (q:draft, low confidence)
nilhzo = (t:v) (w:have anointed) (d:nilh, anoint, with zo marking a completed action) (e:lungdamna sathau nang hong ~ a) (s:nuhkhit) (b:nilh) (r:19.45.7) (q:draft)
nili = (t:num) (w:four days/fourth day) (d:ni, day, and li, four, written together; in dates it follows the tens: nisawm leh nili ni is the fourteenth day, ni sawmnih leh nili ni the twenty-fourth) (e:ni sawmnih leh ~ ni-in Tigris gunpi gei-ah/Kha masa a nisawm leh ~ ni in | on the fourteenth day of the first month/ni sawm leh ~ ni nitakin na kham ding | you shall keep it on the evening of the fourteenth day) (r:27.10.4/4.28.16/4.9.3) (q:draft)
niliim = (t:n) (w:shadow/shade) (d:the shadow or shade made when the sun is blocked, from ni, sun, and liim, shadow; also a picture of what passes quickly) (e:~ bangin pai hanhanin mangthang uh hi/Nitak lam-a ~ bangin kei ka bei a | I fade away like an evening shadow/nisa panin ~ na hi hi | you are a shade from the heat/Sila nasemte in ~ lunggulhin | as slaves long for the shade) (s:nilim/liim) (r:18.14.2/23.25.4/19.109.23/18.7.2) (q:draft)
nilim = (t:n) (w:shade/shadow) (d:the shade or shadow made when the sun is blocked, also a picture of a life that passes quickly; a spelling of niliim) (e:nisa panin ~ na hi hi/a tai dandan ~ tawh kibang hi | they are like a fleeting shadow/ka hunte uh leitungah ~ bang hi a | our days on earth are like a shadow/a nuntak hun uh ~ bangin bei pak ding | their lifetime will pass quickly like a shadow) (s:niliim/liim) (r:23.25.4/19.144.4/13.29.15/21.8.13) (q:draft)
