nilkhiamang = (t:v) (w:sweep away/cast away utterly) (d:nil, throw, with khia, out, and mang, away and lost: sweep away completely) (e:lau mahmahna in amaute ~ ding hi) (r:19.73.19) (q:draft)
nilkhiat = (t:v) (w:reject/cast out/throw away) (d:form of nilkhia used before a noun or an ending: a nilkhiat suang is the stone that was rejected) (e:Inn lamte in a ~ suang pen/Inn lamte’n a ~ suang in | the stone the builders rejected/No innlamte in na ~ uh suangtum pen | the stone you builders rejected) (b:nilkhia) (r:19.118.22/60.2.4/41.12.10/44.4.11) (q:draft)
niloh = (t:adv) (w:continually/always/constantly) (d:placed after a verb: keep on doing without ceasing, as thungen niloh, pray continually) (e:na lungsimah ciamteh ~ in/Thungen ~ un | pray continually/thusia bekbek ngaihsun ~ a | he is always plotting evil/note thu tawh zomin thu ka ngen ~ hi | I pray constantly concerning you) (s:den/gige/ngitnget/tawntunga) (r:20.6.21/52.5.17/20.6.14/45.1.9) (q:draft)
nilohin = (t:adv) (w:continually/all day long/regularly) (d:niloh, continually, with the ending in; sun nilohin is all day long) (e:Pasian kiangah thungen ~ a om hi/Sun ~ ka galte in kei hong zahko a | all day long my enemies taunt me/Sun ~ nakpi na sem a, nisa thuak kote | we who worked hard all day and bore the heat/sun ~ na mit un enin gim ding hi | your eyes will grow weary watching all day long) (s:den/gige) (b:niloh) (r:44.10.2/19.102.8/40.20.12/5.28.32) (q:draft)
