nin = (t:adj) (w:unclean/defiled/impure) (d:dirty; mostly of ritual uncleanness under the law, the opposite of siang, clean) (e:a kihong beel peuhmah a ~ ahi hi/ni sagih sung a ~ hi ding hi | he will be unclean for seven days/amaute a ~ suak uh a | they became unclean/a siangtho lo na leh a ~ na | anything unholy or unclean) (s:nit/kihhuai) (a:siang/siangtho) (r:4.19.15/41.7.2/4.19.11/19.106.39/44.10.14) (q:draft)
