nopmawhna = (t:n) (w:unease/trouble/discomfort) (d:lungsim nopmawhna is a troubled conscience) (e:nangma lungsim ~ a om loh nadingin) (r:46.10.28) (q:draft)
nopna = (t:n) (w:peace/well-being/happiness/pleasure) (d:a state of peace, well-being or enjoyment; nopna om ta hen is a greeting, peace be with you) (e:Note tungah hehpihna, ~ leh itna khang semsem/Nang tungah ~ om ta hen | peace be upon you/mi gilote’ adingin ~ om lo hi | there is no peace for the wicked/mihaite, ~ lakah om tual hi | fools stay where there is pleasure) (s:nopsakna/lungnopna/nuamna) (a:dahna) (b:nop) (r:65.1.2/9.25.6/23.48.22/21.7.4) (q:draft)
nopna = (t:n) (w:wish/desire/intention) (d:after a verb, the wish or intention to do it; cih nopna, what one wants to say, is the meaning of a word or name) (e:minam tampi suksiat ~ thu om hi/pumpi uh ka nusiat ~ hang uh hi loin | not because we wish to leave our body) (s:deihna) (b:nop) (r:23.10.7/40.27.33/47.5.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
Nopna = (t:n) (w:peace/well-being) (d:Nopna lampi is the way of peace) (e:~ lampi ah eite hong kha ding/~ lampi amau in a thei kei uh hi | the way of peace they do not know/~ ngah ta un | peace be with you/~ i zonga ~ hong pai lo hi | we looked for peace but no peace came) (b:nopna) (r:42.1.78/45.3.17/42.24.36/24.8.15) (q:draft)
nopnate = (t:n) (w:wishes/desires/intentions) (d:after a verb, the things one wants to do, as nget nopnate, requests) (e:na nget ~ uh Pasian kiangah/kei nong siatsak ~ uh ka tel mahmah hi | I know very well how you wish to harm me/leitung lunghihmawhna le hauh ~ in Pasian’ thu vuknelh | the worries of the world and the wish to be rich choke the word of God) (s:deihnate) (b:nopna) (r:50.4.6/18.21.27/40.13.22) (q:draft)
nopnate = (t:n) (w:peace/happiness/joys) (d:plural of nopna: peace and well-being, named together with glory and honour) (e:minthan’na leh vangliatna leh ~ a tung ding) (b:nopna) (r:45.2.10) (q:draft)
nopnehte = (t:n) (w:the humble/the meek) (d:plural with te; the build of the word is not clear) (e:Mi’ ~ in Topa) (r:23.29.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
nopsa = (t:see) <nopsa-a>
nopsa-a = (t:adv) (w:in pleasure/enjoying oneself) (d:nopsa find pleasant, enjoy, with the linking a; nopsa-a om is live for pleasure) (e:~ a om meigongnu ahih leh) (r:54.5.6) (q:draft)
nopsak = (t:v) (w:go well/prosper/be well off/enjoy) (d:fare well or enjoy good things; na nopsak theih nadingun means so that it may go well with you, and nopsak nading is for the well-being of) (e:Note na ~ theih nadingun/hih in na ~ nading | this is so that it may go well with you/Jerusalem khuapi’ ~ nading thu ngen un | pray for the well-being of Jerusalem/~ cih thei kha ngei loin | never having known what it is to enjoy good) (s:nuamsa) (b:nop) (r:5.19.13/18.21.25/5.22.7/19.122.6) (q:draft)
nopsaklawh = (t:v) (w:enjoy instead/get the enjoyment of) (d:nopsak, enjoy, with lawh, get as gain: another person gets the enjoyment of what someone owns) (e:midang khat in ~ laizang hi) (r:21.6.2) (q:draft)
nopsakna = (t:n) (w:peace/rest/well-being/comfort) (d:nopsak, fare well, with the noun suffix na: peace, rest and well-being; ka nopsakna mun is my place of rest) (e:Mi gilote’ adingin ~ om lo hi/ka ~ mun-ah amaute a lut lo dingin | that they would not enter my place of rest/Nangma ~ pen gunpi bang ding a | your peace would be like a river/Pasian’ mite ading Nipi ni ~ a om lai | a Sabbath rest still remains for the people of God) (s:nopna/lungmuanna) (a:gimna) (r:23.57.21/58.4.9/19.95.11/23.48.18) (q:draft)
Nopsakna = (t:n) (w:peace) (d:nopsakna, peace, written with a capital at the start of a sentence and in the title Nopsakna Kumpi, Prince of Peace) (e:Tawntung Pa, ~ Kumpi/~ a hong pia Pasian in note khempeuh hong ompih | may the God who gives peace be with you all/~ a om hi, launa om lo hi | there is peace, there is no danger) (b:nopsakna) (r:23.9.6/45.15.33/52.5.3) (q:draft)
nopsaknate = (t:n) (w:fortunes/riches/pleasures/comforts) (d:plural of nopsakna: good times, prosperity and the good things enjoyed) (e:Hauhna leh ~ ama inn sungah dim ding/Jakob’ ~ a ngeina na bangsak kik hi | you restored the fortunes of Jacob/hauhna, le ~ in depgawp ahih manin | because riches and pleasures choke them/kote’ ~ a ngei hong bangsak kik ta in | restore our fortunes) (s:hauhnate) (b:nopsakna) (r:19.112.3/19.85.1/42.8.14/19.126.4) (q:draft)
nopsaknateng = (t:n) (w:all comforts/all well-being) (d:nopsakna, comfort or well-being, with teng, all of) (e:na ~ a lakhia dingin) (b:nopsakna) (r:26.16.27) (q:draft, low confidence)
