noptat = (t:v) (w:revel/indulge/live for pleasure) (d:live for pleasure without restraint; noptat nuamte are lovers of pleasure and noptat khamna is self-control) (e:zu dawnin a ~ lo mi/uang nekin na ~ mahmah uh hi | you have lived in luxury and self-indulgence/A ~ nuamte zawng a | those who love pleasure become poor/amau kheemna tawh ~ lua-in | reveling greatly in their deceptions) (r:54.3.8/61.2.13/59.5.5/20.21.17) (q:draft)
noptatin = (t:v) (w:reveling/living for pleasure) (d:noptat, revel, with in linking it to the next verb) (e:~ a om uh hi) (b:noptat) (r:61.2.13) (q:draft)
noptatna = (t:n) (w:indulgence/dissipation/wild living) (d:noptat with the noun suffix na; living for pleasure without restraint; noptatna khamna, the holding back of it, is self-control) (e:a kihhuai ~ ah gamta-in/~ khamna tungah thuakna | to self-control, perseverance/~-ah kihhuaina na bawl lohna uh | that you do not join in the shameful acts of wild living) (s:uangtatna) (b:noptat) (r:65.1.7/61.1.6/60.4.4) (q:draft)
nopte = (t:n) (w:those one wants to) (d:nop want with plural te, after a verb: the ones whom, or the things which, someone wishes to) (e:a hehpih ~ a hehpih hi/ka hehpih ~ ka hehpih ding hi | I will have mercy on those I want to have mercy on/a lungkhauhsak ~ a lungkhauhsak hi | he hardens those he wants to harden/Tapa in a theihsak ~ longal | except those to whom the Son wants to make him known) (s:nuamte) (b:nop) (r:45.9.18/40.11.27/45.9.15) (q:draft)
