noptheihna = (t:n) (w:being cheered/refreshment) (d:noptheih, be cheered, with the noun suffix na; with dingin: so that the mind may be glad) (e:Titus lungsim a ~ dingin ama tungah) (b:noptheih) (r:47.7.13) (q:draft)
noptuak = (t:adj) (w:pleasant/comfortable/agreeable) (d:of land or a place that is good to be in) (e:a leitang ~ sa hi/a ~ munte-ah ganhing hon omin | with herds in the pleasant pastures) (s:omnuam) (r:1.49.15/19.65.12) (q:draft)
noptuam = (t:n) (w:benefit/good/relief/advantage) (d:what makes someone better off; noptuam nading is for the good of) (e:midangte’ ~ nadingin khat leh khat/i lawmte ~ na’ng ngaihsunin | thinking of the good of our neighbours/Note ~ nadingin ka ci hi | I say it for your own good/ka gimna pan ~ ngah nading om nawn lo | there is no more relief from my suffering/tuate zuihna-ah ~ lian om hi | in keeping them there is great reward) (s:noptuamna/phattuamna) (r:50.2.4/18.30.16/45.15.2/46.7.35/19.19.11) (q:draft)
noptuam = (t:v) (w:get better/improve/recover) (d:become better, of a sick person or a sore) (e:Bang hunin a ~ a kipan hiam/a ~ lo tham loin a gim semsem | not only did she not get better, she grew worse) (s:nuamtuam) (r:43.4.52/41.5.26) (q:draft)
noptuamin = (t:v) (w:getting better/easing) (d:noptuam, get better, with in linking it to what follows; of a sore that has eased and not spread, where the English has unchanged) (e:a natna ~ a natna in a vun) (b:noptuam) (r:3.13.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
noptuamna = (t:n) (w:benefit/profit/good/reward) (d:what is to someone's advantage or comfort) (e:bang ~ ngah ahi hiam/midangte’ ~ zong hen | let him seek the good of others/Thuman mi’ ading ~ om taktak a | there truly is a reward for the righteous/~ ngah loin a om kei ding hi | he will not go without a reward) (s:phattuamna/thaman) (a:supna) (b:noptuam) (r:21.1.3/46.10.24/19.58.11/41.9.41) (q:draft)
noptuamsak = (t:v) (w:make well/refresh/relieve) (d:noptuam, get better, with sak, cause: make a sick person well or put a mind at ease) (e:upna thungetna in cinate a ~ ding a/Titu’ lungsim na ~ zo uh a | you have refreshed the spirit of Titus) (s:damsak/nuamtuamsak) (b:noptuam) (r:59.5.15/47.7.13) (q:draft)
noptuamsakin = (t:v) (w:making well/raising up) (d:noptuamsak, make well, with in linking it to the next verb) (e:Topa in cinate ~, damsak ding a) (b:noptuamsak) (r:59.5.15) (q:draft)
