nuaisiah = (t:v) (w:subdue/bring under/overcome) (d:put a defeated people under one's rule) (e:David in Filistiate zoin ~ a/Kanaan kumpi Jabin ~ hi | he subdued Jabin king of Canaan/tua gam-a teeng Kanaan mite na ~ a | you subdued the Canaanites who lived in that land/a ~ minamte khempeuh | all the nations he had subdued) (r:13.18.1/7.4.23/16.9.24/10.8.11) (q:draft)
nuaisiah = (t:adv) (w:and under/below/downward) (d:after a number, an age or a part of the body, from that point downward) (e:kum sawmnih ~ a pha mite/kum nih ~ pasalno khempeuh a thatsak hi | he had all the boys of two years and under killed/A kawng ~ ding teng meikuang tawh kibang a | from his waist down he looked like fire) (a:tungsiah) (r:13.27.23/40.2.16/26.8.2) (q:draft)
nuaisiahin = (t:v) (w:subduing/bringing under) (d:nuaisiah, subdue, with in linking it to the next verb) (e:migilote ~, leivui bangin na tuancil ding) (b:nuaisiah) (r:39.4.3) (q:draft)
nuaisiahna = (t:n) (w:oppression/subjugation) (d:nuaisiah, bring under, with the noun suffix na; mi nuaisiahna is the oppression of people) (e:mi ~ leh ngongtat nading ahi zongin) (s:nenniamna/netniamna) (b:nuaisiah) (r:24.22.17) (q:draft)
nuaite = (t:see) <nuaite-ah>
nuaite-ah = (t:prep) (w:under/beneath) (d:nuai, the underside, with plural te and ah, at: in the places under several things) (e:suanghawm ~ a tate uh a that) (r:23.57.4) (q:draft)
nuak = (t:v) (w:sulk/take offence) (d:be offended and withdraw; nuak ciah seems to be go home in resentment, the English versions do not render the word) (e:a inn-ah ~ ciah hi) (r:10.17.23) (q:draft, low confidence)
nuam = (t:v) (w:want) (d:want or be willing to do something, placed after the verb; with kei or lo, not want to) (e:a hawh ~ kei uh hi/a that ~ hangin that zo lo hi | though she wanted to kill him she could not/Balaam in kote hong zui ~ lo hi | Balaam does not want to come with us/a gilkialte an na pia ~ kei hi | you would not give food to the hungry) (s:deih/nop) (r:40.22.3/41.6.19/4.22.14/18.22.7)
nuam = (t:v) (w:delight) (d:find pleasant; nuam sa is take delight in) (e:mihingte lakah ~ ka sa hi/migilote tawh kikholh ~ sa a | he delights in keeping company with the wicked/migilote in gitloh tatna ~ sa uh hi | the wicked delight in doing evil) (r:20.8.31/18.34.8/20.19.28)
nuam = (t:adj) (w:happy/glad/pleasant) (d:happy or glad; nuam mahmah is very glad, and lung nuam is glad at heart) (e:Zion in za-in ~ a/Thuman na gen ciangin, ka ~ mahmah ding hi | when you speak what is right I will be very glad/aksi a muh uh ciangin ~ mahmah uh a | when they saw the star they were overjoyed/na lung uh ~ mahmah ding hi | you will be very happy) (r:19.97.8/20.23.16/40.2.10/43.13.17)
Nuam = (t:adj) (w:pleasant/fair/peaceful) (d:nuam, pleasant or at peace, written with a capital in the place name Khawlmun Nuam, Fair Havens, and at the start of the farewell Nuam takin pai in, go in peace) (e:Khawlmun ~ kici mun khatah/~ takin na ciah in | go home in peace/~ takin pai in | go in peace) (b:nuam) (r:44.27.8/44.27.13/41.5.34/12.5.19) (q:draft)
nuama = (t:v) (w:wanting/wishing) (d:nuam want with the linking ending a, joined to the verb before it; that nuama, wanting to kill) (e:Naupang that ~ a zongte) (b:nuam) (r:40.2.20) (q:draft)
nuama = (t:adj) (w:at ease/comfortable/pleasant) (d:nuam with the linking ending a, describing how one lives) (e:Zion-ah nuntak ~ a om hithiat) (b:nuam) (r:30.6.1) (q:draft, low confidence)
nuama = (t:adj) (d:second part of thu-nuama, of fellowship or peace, as in thu-nuama biakna the fellowship offering) (e:meihal biaknate leh thu-~ biaknate a piak/thu-~ biakna pia-in | offering fellowship offerings) (b:nuam) (r:13.16.2/14.29.35/14.30.22) (q:draft)
nuamah = (t:adj) (w:pleasant/good/level) (d:nuam pleasant with the place marker ah; gam nuamah in the pleasant land, lam nuamah on an easy path) (e:gam ~ teeng in la thumanin/lam ~ paipih-in a tuk kei ding uh | led on a level path they will not stumble/Hih lai-ah tutna ~ hong tu in | sit here in this good seat) (b:nuam) (r:19.37.3/24.31.9/59.2.3) (q:draft)
nuamin = (t:adj) (w:contrary)
nuamkawmin = (t:adv) (w:joyfully/while glad) (d:nuam, be glad, with kawmin, while; laukawm nuamkawmin is afraid and glad at the same time) (e:numeite zong laukawm, ~ nungzuite kiangah) (r:40.28.8) (q:draft)
nuamkik = (t:v) (w:be comforted/be glad again) (d:nuam, be glad, with kik, again; said of the lungsim, mind) (e:a lungsim uh ~ mahmah hi) (s:nuamtuam) (b:nuam) (r:44.20.12) (q:draft)
nuamlua = (t:adj) (w:overjoyed/very glad) (d:nuam, happy, with lua, too much) (e:Amaute ~ kisa-in lamdangsa-in um zo lo/~ ahih manin inntual kong nangawn hong loin | being so overjoyed she did not even open the gate) (b:nuam) (r:42.24.41/44.12.14) (q:draft)
nuammawh = (t:v) (w:bother/trouble/pick on) (d:be ill-disposed towards someone, find fault with) (e:Hih numei bang ~ na hi uh hiam/kote bang hong ~ na hi hiam | why are you troubling us) (r:40.26.10/41.5.7/40.8.29) (q:draft, low confidence)
nuammawh = (t:v) (w:fret/be uneasy) (d:with lung, heart: be troubled in mind) (e:Migilote’ hangin lung ~ kei inla) (r:20.24.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
nuamna = (t:n) (w:joy/gladness/pleasure) (d:nuam, happy, with the noun suffix na: joy or gladness, often paired with lungdamna) (e:lungdamna leh ~ tawh amaute kitumpih hi/lungdamna leh ~ om nawn lo hi | joy and gladness are no more/launa tawh, ~ tawh han panin | from the tomb with fear and with joy/ka ~ sangin nuam zawkna a om kei hi | there is no joy greater than this joy of mine) (s:lungdamna/kipahna) (a:dahna) (b:nuam) (r:19.45.15/64.1.4/23.16.10/40.28.8) (q:draft)
nuampa = (t:n) (w:one who wants to) (d:nuam, want, with pa, the male one; after a verb, the man who wants to do it) (e:an la ~ na hi hi/mite kiangah a kithei ~ in | one who wants to be known among people/a hehna tawh phu la ~ in | the man who in his anger wants to take revenge) (b:nuam) (r:42.19.21/43.7.4/5.19.6) (q:draft)
nuampen = (t:adj) (w:best/most pleasant/most comfortable) (d:nuam, pleasant, with pen, most; of seats, the most desirable) (e:tutphah ~ ah na tunuam uh a) (b:nuam) (r:42.11.43) (q:draft)
nuampente = (t:adj) (w:best/most pleasant) (d:nuampen, most pleasant, with plural te; of seats, the most desirable ones) (e:uliante tutna tutphah ~ tungah) (b:nuampen) (r:40.23.6) (q:draft)
nuampipi = (t:v) (w:want greatly/long) (d:nuam, want, with pipi: while wanting very much; nei nuampipi is though longing to have a husband) (e:Nei ~ a neih loh tentan sangin) (r:46.7.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
nuamsa = (t:v) (w:be happy/enjoy/be content) (d:nuam, pleasant, with sa, feel or deem: be happy, enjoy something; mi nuamsa is a blessed or happy person) (e:~ mahmahin ka om hi/kua in an ne-in ~ thei ding ahi hiam | who can eat and find enjoyment/Amah ~ tawntung ding a | he will always live in well-being/Nuntakna ~ kei ing | I find no pleasure in life/Amah in mi samsiat ~ hi | he loved to curse people) (s:nopsak/lungkim) (b:nuam) (r:27.4.4/21.2.25/19.25.13/21.12.1/19.109.17) (q:draft)
nuamsak = (t:v) (w:gladden/cheer/make happy) (d:nuam, glad, with causative sak; lung nuamsak is gladden the heart) (e:zu in lung ~ a/mihing lungsim a ~ ding leenggahzu | wine that gladdens the human heart/Na lung ~ in | cheer up/Maitaina in lung ~ a | a cheerful face gladdens the heart) (s:lungdamsak/lungnuamsak) (a:dahsak/lungkhamsak) (b:nuam) (r:21.10.19/11.21.7/19.104.15/41.10.49/20.15.30) (q:draft)
nuamsakin = (t:v) (w:gladdening/cheering/making merry) (d:nuamsak, gladden, with the linking ending in; lung nuamsakin om is enjoy oneself) (e:zu nekna tawh ka lung ~/a lung uh ~ a om lai takun | while they were enjoying themselves) (b:nuamsak) (r:21.2.3/7.19.22) (q:draft)
nuamsasak = (t:v) (w:make content/give rest/make happy) (d:nuamsa, be content, with sak, cause) (e:inn tuakah hong ~ ta hen) (b:nuamsa) (r:8.1.9) (q:draft)
nuamsate = (t:n) (w:happy people/those who live at ease) (d:nuamsa be happy, enjoy, with the plural te: mi nuamsate is people who are happy or blessed, and also people who live in comfort) (e:Amah a bel khempeuh mi ~ ahi hi/mi ~ in kumpite’ inn sungah a om uh | those who live in luxury are in the palaces of kings) (b:nuamsa) (r:19.2.11/42.7.25) (q:draft)
nuamtak = (t:adv) (w:pleasantly/comfortably/at ease/safely) (d:nuam with tak, which makes an adverb; nuamtak sa-in means finding it easy or pleasant to do, without scruple) (e:sun teng ~ hong zangsak in/~ sa-in, mizawngte’ neihsa mawksut kei in | do not take advantage of the poor and rob them of what they own/peemtate tungah ~ sa-in khualna mel nei loin | taking advantage of foreigners without any regard) (s:nuamtakin) (b:nuam) (r:18.10.20/15.8.23/20.22.22/26.22.29) (q:draft)
nuamtakin = (t:adv) (w:peacefully/in peace/safely/comfortably) (d:nuam, pleasant, with takin, which makes an adverb: in peace, in comfort or in safety) (e:~ inn-ah a si dingin/~ na pate’ kiang na zuan ding hi | you will go to your fathers in peace/launa nei loin ~ om hithiat ding uh hi | they will live at ease in safety, without fear/hanah ~ ka lum hithiat khin ding hi | I would be lying peacefully in the grave) (s:nuamtak/lungmuangin) (b:nuam) (r:18.29.18/1.15.15/20.1.33/18.3.13) (q:draft)
nuamtaksa = (t:v) (w:take advantage of/exploit/seize the opportunity) (d:nuamtak with sa, deem: find something easy or convenient and so make use of it) (e:Satan in ~-in eite tungah hong gualzo kha/Meigong numeite tungah ~-in a neihsate laksakin | taking advantage of widows and taking what they own/mawhna in ~ a, kei hong khemin | sin seized the opportunity and deceived me/Titus in ~-in note tungah bang hong ngen | did Titus exploit you and ask anything of you) (b:nuamtak) (r:47.2.11/45.7.11/41.12.40/47.12.18) (q:draft)
nuamte = (t:n) (w:those who want/whoever wants) (d:nuam, want, with plural te, placed after a verb: those who want to do it) (e:makai a suak ~ in note sila/Kei hong that ~ in a thang uh zakin | those who want to kill me set their traps/mi that ~’ kiang panin keimah hong hon in | save me from those who want to kill/Mi a that ~ in a thuman mi mudah a | those who want to kill hate a person of integrity) (s:nopte/deihte/utte) (b:nuam) (r:40.20.27/20.29.10/19.38.12/19.59.2) (q:draft)
nuamthei = (t:v) (w:be able to be at ease/can be glad) (d:nuam, be glad, with thei, be able; lungsim nuamthei nawn lo is the mind could no longer be at ease) (e:David a lungsim ~ nawn lo hi) (b:nuam) (r:9.24.5) (q:draft)
nuamtuam = (t:v) (w:be relieved/be comforted/get better) (d:feel easier after pain, grief or sickness; with sak, give relief to) (e:a ihmut leh, a ~ ding hi/a lung ~ ding hi | he will be consoled/Thu gen leng ka natna ~ lo a | if I speak my pain is not relieved/mi tampi ~ sak a | they bring relief to many) (s:noptuam/nuamkik) (r:43.11.12/18.16.6/26.32.31/20.10.21) (q:draft)
nuamtuamin = (t:adv) (w:restfully/in relief) (d:nuamtuam, be relieved, with in: being at ease, said of one who sleeps a healing sleep) (e:a ~ a ihmu hi) (b:nuamtuam) (r:43.11.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
nuamtuamsak = (t:v) (w:comfort/give relief to/refresh) (d:nuamtuam, be relieved, with sak, cause) (e:thugente in mi tampi ~ a/nong ~ kik ding hi | you will comfort me again) (s:hehnem/noptuamsak) (b:nuamtuam) (r:20.10.21/19.71.21) (q:draft)
nuamzaw = (t:v) (w:prefer/would rather) (d:nuam want with zaw more, used with sangin than) (e:ka thuak sangin ka si ~ hi/ka Pasian’ inn kongcingpa ka hi ~ hi | I would rather be a doorkeeper in the house of my God/mawkna a suah ding sangin ka si ~ hi | I would rather die than have it come to nothing) (s:utzaw/deihzaw/nopzawk) (b:nuam) (r:18.7.15/19.84.10/46.9.15) (q:draft)
nuamzaw = (t:adj) (w:better/more pleasant/more comfortable) (d:nuam pleasant with zaw more) (e:ka om sangin ama kiang ~ ding hi/tuni sangin ~ lai ding hi | it will be even better than today) (s:hoihzaw) (b:nuam) (r:28.2.7/23.56.12) (q:draft)
nuangnuang = (t:adv) (w:limply/feebly/droopingly) (d:describes weak hands that hang down limply; used after zaw, weak, in zaw nuangnuang, weak and drooping) (e:a zaw ~ na khutte uh) (r:58.12.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
Nubiate = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Cushites/Nubians) (d:the Nubians, the people of Cush south of Egypt, named together with the Libyans; called Cushites in the NIV) (r:27.11.43)
Nubukhadnezzar = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Nebuchadnezzar) (d:king of Babylon who captured Jerusalem and carried its people into exile; a spelling of the name used in this verse) (r:24.52.29)
nuh = (t:v) (w:smear/anoint/rub on/apply) (d:put oil, blood or ointment on something by smearing or rubbing; sathau nuh is anoint with oil) (e:a ngakna zong sathau ~-in na ap ding hi/biakna tau kite ~ ding a | he shall put it on the horns of the altar/na khutme tawh na ~ ding a | you shall put it on with your finger/ap dingin sathau ~ hi | he anointed them with oil to consecrate them) (s:nilh) (r:2.40.11/3.8.23/3.4.30/2.29.12/3.8.11) (q:draft)
nuhin = (t:v) (w:anoint/smear/rub on) (d:connective form of nuh, putting oil, perfume or blood on something, followed by another verb) (e:a nazatte khempeuh sathau ~ ap a/a sunga om khempeuh ~ tuate a ap hi | he anointed everything in it and consecrated them/Zeisu’ khe ~ a sam tawh a nul hi | she anointed the feet of Jesus and wiped them with her hair/biakna tau kite a khutme tawh ~ | putting it on the horns of the altar with his finger) (s:nilhin) (b:nuh) (r:4.7.1/43.12.3/3.8.10/3.8.15) (q:draft)
nuhkawmin = (t:v) (w:putting on/smearing on) (d:nuh, smear or rub on, with kawmin, while doing: as he put it on) (e:mitah tua buannawi a ~) (r:43.9.6) (q:draft)
nuhkhit = (t:v) (w:have anointed/have smeared) (d:nuh, smear or rub on, with khit, finished; nuhkhit ciangin is after anointing) (e:a ~ ciangin a sam tawh) (s:nilhzo) (r:43.12.3) (q:draft)
nuhkhol = (t:v) (w:anoint beforehand) (d:nuh, smear or rub on, with khol, in advance) (e:paknamtui a hong ma ~ hi a) (s:nilhkhol) (r:41.14.8) (q:draft)
nuhsak = (t:v) (w:apply/smear on/put on) (d:put mud, ointment or oil on someone; nuh smear with sak, for another) (e:mittawpa’ mit ah buan ~ a/na damkik nadingin na meimate ~ in | apply it to your sores so that you recover/ka khe nangawn sathau namtui hong ~ hi | she has put perfume even on my feet/buan bawlin ka mitte hong ~ a | he made mud and put it on my eyes) (s:nilhsak) (b:nuh) (r:43.9.6/42.7.46/23.38.21/43.9.11) (q:draft)
