nuih = (t:v) (w:laugh) (d:form of nui used before another word such as hun, time) (e:Kah hun om a, ~ hun om hi) (a:kah) (b:nui) (r:21.3.4) (q:draft)
nuihna = (t:n) (w:laughter/laughing) (d:nuih, laugh, with the noun suffix na: laughing, laughter) (e:Na muk-ah ~ hong omsak ding a/Note’ ~ pen dahna suahsak un | turn your laughter into mourning/lungdamin ~ leh simmawhna tawh | gladly, with laughter and contempt) (a:kahna/dahna) (b:nuih) (r:18.8.21/21.7.3/59.4.9/26.36.5) (q:draft)
nuihnate = (t:n) (w:laughter) (d:nuihna, laughter, with plural te) (e:Na ~ uh kahna suaksak zaw unla) (b:nuihna) (r:59.4.9) (q:draft)
nuihpih = (t:v) (w:laugh with) (d:nuih, laugh, with pih, together with someone) (e:peuhmah in nuamin hong ~ ding uh hi) (b:nuih) (r:1.21.6) (q:draft)
nuihsan = (t:v) (w:laugh at/mock/ridicule/deride) (d:nuih, laugh, with -san, at or toward someone) (e:tua mite in zahpihin a ~ uh hi/Vantunga tu-pa in ~ a | the One enthroned in heaven laughs at them/kei hong muh uh ciangin hong ~ uh hi | when they see me they laugh at me/Mite in sun tawntung hong ~ uh a | people laugh at me all day long) (s:zahko/zahpih) (b:nuih) (r:40.9.24/19.37.13/19.2.4/18.19.18/25.3.14) (q:draft)
nuihsanin = (t:v) (w:laugh at/mock/scorn) (d:nuihsan with the linking ending in) (e:amaute ~ zahpih uh a/lau mahmah ding uh a, nang hong ~ | they will be greatly afraid and laugh at you/Minam dangte in note hong ~ | the other nations will laugh at you) (b:nuihsan) (r:14.30.10/19.52.6/33.6.16) (q:draft)
nuihsat = (t:n) (w:laughingstock/derision/scorn) (d:someone who is laughed at by others) (e:amah pen a vengte’ ~ a suak hi/ka kim uh-a omte’ ~ leh thusim lohin | a laughingstock and a byword to those around us/Ka langte khempeuh’ ~ hi-in | I am the laughingstock of all my enemies/Ni simin mite’ ~ lel ka hi a | every day I am nothing but a laughingstock to people) (s:ciamnuihna) (r:19.89.41/19.79.4/19.44.13/19.31.11/24.20.7) (q:draft)
nuihsat = (t:v) (w:smile at/laugh at) (d:smile or laugh toward someone; in this verse a kindly smile, not mockery) (e:itna tawh ka ~ ciangin lungnuam uh a) (r:18.29.24) (q:draft, low confidence)
nuihsatin = (t:n) (w:object of scorn/laughingstock) (d:nuihsat, being laughed at, with in; used with om or bawl: be or make a laughingstock) (e:Mihaite’ ~ kei hong bawl kei in/amaute’ ~ ka om a | I am an object of scorn to them/amaute’ ~ hong omsak kei in | do not let us be their laughingstock) (b:nuihsat) (r:19.39.8/19.109.25/29.2.17) (q:draft)
nuihsatna = (t:n) (w:mockery/scorn/ridicule) (d:nuihsat, laugh at, with the noun suffix na) (e:amau’ hong ~ leh hong simmawhnate panin/a hong ~ uh hong phawk in | remember how they mock) (s:zahpihna/zahkona/simmawhna) (b:nuihsat) (r:19.119.22/19.89.50) (q:draft)
nuihzak = (t:v) (w:laugh) (d:nuihzak nading is something to laugh for, a cause of laughter) (e:nuamin ~ nading hong bawlsak khin hi) (r:1.21.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
nuinui = (t:v) (w:laugh on/keep laughing/rejoice) (d:nui, laugh, said twice for an action that goes on) (e:Uzmite aw ~ mai un/Uz mite aw, tu-in ~ mai unla | people of Uz, laugh on for now) (r:25.4.21) (q:draft, low confidence)
nukik = (t:n) (w:stepmother) (d:nu, mother, with kik, again: the wife a father took later) (e:ama ~ nangawn a luppihna thu) (b:nu) (r:46.5.1) (q:draft)
nul = (t:v) (w:wipe/wipe dry) (d:wipe something dry or clean, such as feet, tears or a dish) (e:a sam tawh a ~ hi/maitang khempeuh panin khitui ~ ding hi | he will wipe the tears from all faces/mi khat in pakan a ~ bangin | as one wipes a dish/mittang pan khitui khempeuh a ~ siang ding hi | he will wipe away every tear from their eyes) (r:42.7.38/43.13.5/23.25.8/12.21.13/66.7.17) (q:draft)
nulepa = (t:n) (w:couple) (d:a husband and wife together; in the verses nulepa mawhna and nulepa khialhna mean adultery or sexual sin) (e:midangte’ zi tawh ~ mawhna bawl uh a | they commit adultery with the wives of others/note lakah ~ khialhna | sexual immorality among you) (s:nupa) (r:26.22.11/49.5.3)
nulin = (t:v) (w:wiping) (d:nul, wipe, with in linking it to the next verb) (e:keimah in Jerusalem ~ ka lumlet ding hi) (b:nul) (r:12.21.13) (q:draft)
nulkeusak = (t:v) (w:wipe dry) (d:nul, wipe, with keu, dry, and sak, cause or do for someone) (e:a sam tawh hong ~ hi) (r:42.7.44) (q:draft)
nulkhia = (t:v) (w:wipe off/wipe away) (d:nul, wipe, with khia, out or off) (e:note langkhat ah ka ~ uh hi/note hilhkholhna-in ka ~ uh hi | we wipe it off as a warning to you) (b:nul) (r:42.10.11) (q:draft)
nulsak = (t:v) (w:wipe/wipe away/wipe dry) (d:nul, wipe, with sak, do it for another) (e:a sam tawh a ~ hi/Amaute’ mit panin khitui khempeuh ~ ding hi | he will wipe every tear from their eyes/Pasian in a khitui khempeuh uh ~ ding hi | God will wipe away all their tears/a sam tawh ~ a | she wiped them with her hair) (b:nul) (r:43.12.3/66.21.4/66.7.17/42.7.38) (q:draft)
nulsaknu = (t:n) (w:woman who wiped) (d:nulsak, wipe for another, with nu marking a woman: the woman who wiped) (e:a sam tawh a ~ hi) (b:nulsak) (r:43.11.2) (q:draft)
numei = (t:n) (w:woman) (d:an adult female person) (e:A nung ciangin ~ zong a si hi/hih ~ a khialh laitak kimu hi | this woman was caught in the act of sin/~ nausuak na a sa bangin | like a woman in the pain of childbirth) (a:pasal) (r:42.20.32/43.8.4/19.48.6)
numei = (t:n) (w:female) (e:amah in pasal leh ~ piangsak hi/pasal leh ~ a piangsak hi | he made them male and female/Tua mi in ~ ahih leh | if that person is a female) (a:pasal) (r:1.1.27/41.10.6/3.27.4)
Numei = (t:n) (w:woman) (d:numei written with a capital at the start of a sentence or where the word is given as a name) (e:a kilakhia ahih manin ~ kici ding hi/~ in a tuiphel nusia-in | the woman left her water jar/~ khempeuh hing khawi na hi uh hiam | have you kept all the women alive) (b:numei) (r:1.2.23/66.17.5/43.4.28/4.31.15) (q:draft)
numei-nasemnangma = (t:todo) (q:draft, numei-nasem female servant run together with nangma yourself, probably a missing space in the text of Genesis 16:6)
numeino = (t:n) (w:girl/little girl/young girl) (d:numei, female, with no, young or small: a girl) (e:tua ~ a piak khit ciangin/Israel panin ~ khat ciahpih uh a | they carried off a young girl from Israel/~ pai-in naupang’ nu va sam hi | the girl went and called the mother of the child/Sanggam ~ khat ka nei uh a | we have a little sister) (b:numei) (r:41.6.28/42.8.54/12.5.2/2.2.8/22.8.8) (q:draft)
numeinu = (t:n) (w:woman) (d:numei, woman, with nu marking a female person: the woman, one particular woman) (e:a lawng hih ~ a bangci mi/Kumpipa in ~’ thugente a zak ciangin | when the king heard the words of the woman) (b:numei) (r:42.7.39/12.6.30) (q:draft)
numeipihte = (t:n) (w:fellow women) (d:numei, woman, with pih, fellow, and plural te: other women like themselves) (e:a ~ mah uh lunggulhin lumkhawm uh a) (r:45.1.26) (q:draft)
numeite = (t:n) (w:women) (d:numei, woman, with the plural te) (e:~ sam bangin sam a nei uh hi/tua gam ~' kiangah hawh dingin paikhia hi | she went out to visit the women of that land/Topa in Jerusalem ~ lutang meima sakin | the Lord will bring sores on the heads of the women of Jerusalem/No Israel ~ aw, Saul’ hangin kap un | women of Israel, weep for Saul) (s:nupite) (a:pasalte) (b:numei) (r:66.9.8/54.5.3/1.34.1/23.3.17/10.1.24) (q:draft)
nun = (t:n) (w:bud/knob) (d:in the verses a bud-shaped ornament of the lampstand, named together with pak flower) (e:a ~ leh a pak tawh a om/tungah a ~ leh a pak a om | on it are its bud and its blossom/tua tawh sakhat ahi ~ khat om hi | there is one bud of one piece with it) (r:2.37.20/2.25.35/2.25.33) (q:draft)
nun = (t:v) (w:blow) (d:of wind or storm: blow; written nun’ before words such as ciangin, lai takin and ni) (e:Huihpi a ~’ ciangin migilote len’mang a/nisuahna huihpi a ~’ ni-in | on the day the east wind blows/Khang lam huih in damtakin hong ~’ ciangin | when the south wind blew gently/gamlapi panin huihpi hong ~’ ciangin | when the storm comes from far away) (r:20.10.25/18.37.17/23.27.8/44.27.13/23.10.3) (q:draft)
Nun = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Nun) (d:father of Joshua, of the tribe of Ephraim) (e:Moses’ nasem ahi ~’ tapa Joshua) (r:6.1.1/4.13.8) (q:draft)
nung = (t:n) (w:back/rear) (d:the back or the place behind; a nung zui means follow behind him) (e:Simon Piter in a ~ zui a/nangmah in ka ~ na mu ding hi | you will see my back/Saul ~ zui-in Samuel kileh kik hi | Samuel went back, following Saul/Zeisu’ ~ a zui uh hi | they followed Jesus) (s:nunglam) (a:mai) (r:43.20.6/42.5.28/2.33.23/9.15.31/43.1.37) (q:draft)
nung = (t:prep) (w:after) (d:after in time, in tua nung ciangin after that and a nung ciangin afterward) (e:Tua ~ ciangin, ama zi Elisabeth/Tua ~ ciangin kamsangpa Samuel dongin | after that, until the prophet Samuel/a ~ ciangin tui a duh kik ding | afterward they will be thirsty again/a ~ ciangin minthan’na tawh keimah nong sang ding | afterward you will receive me with glory) (a:ma) (r:42.1.24/42.20.32/44.13.20/43.4.13/19.73.24) (q:draft)
nunga = (t:prep) (w:behind/after) (d:at the back of or following after, nung with the place ending a; follows a possessive) (e:a ~ hong po ki lite/amau ~ a suan leh a khakte uh | their descendants after them/ama ~ Judah kumpite khempeuh lak | among all the kings of Judah after him/a ~ om Lot’ zi nunghei a | the wife of Lot, who was behind him, looked back) (a:maiah) (b:nung) (r:27.8.22/1.19.26/5.1.8/12.18.5) (q:draft)
nunga = (t:v) (w:blow) (d:of wind, the verb nung blow followed by the linking a) (e:huihpi hong ~ tuipi tung a seem/huih ~ kilok thei tui kilok tawh kibang | like a wave of water tossed by the blowing wind) (r:27.7.2/59.1.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
nungah = (t:prep) (w:behind/after) (d:placed after the noun, of place or of time) (e:Ama ~ Bethlehem khuami Ibzan in/nitumna lam biakbuk ~ giahphual satin | camping on the west, behind the tabernacle/Abner ~ Benjaminte kikaikhawm uh a | the Benjamites gathered behind Abner/a mai-ah la sate, a ~ tamngai tumte | the singers in front, the musicians behind) (a:maiah) (b:nung) (r:7.12.8/4.3.23/10.2.25/19.68.25) (q:draft)
nungak = (t:n) (w:virgin/maiden/young woman/girl) (d:a young unmarried woman, a virgin) (e:a zi dingin ~ la ding hi/Timnah-ah Filistia mi ~ khat mu hi | in Timnah he saw a young Philistine woman/A kidongsa ~ khat om a | there is a virgin pledged to be married/sim zawh lohin ~ om kha mah ding a | there may be young women beyond number) (a:tangval) (r:3.21.13/19.148.12/7.14.1/5.22.23/22.6.8) (q:draft)
Nungak = (t:n) (w:young woman/maiden) (d:nungak, young woman, with a capital at the start of a sentence and in the speaker headings of the Song of Songs, Nungak the woman, Nungak dangte the other young women) (e:~ leh tangval aw/~ leh tangvalte, teeksiate leh naupangte | young women and young men, old people and children/~ lak-a hoihpen nu aw | most beautiful of young women) (b:nungak) (r:22.5.1/22.5.8/19.148.12/22.6.1) (q:draft)
nungakin = (t:adv) (w:as a young woman/as a maiden) (d:nungak young unmarried woman with the ending in, telling the state someone is in; nungakin a om, while still an unmarried girl) (e:a pa inn sungah ~ a om/pasal tawh a lumkhawm nai lo, ~ khansih hi | she died a virgin, never having slept with a man/Izipt gamah ~ na om lai-in | when you were a young woman in Egypt/~ a sih nading hangin mualte tungah kapin | weeping on the hills because she would die unmarried) (b:nungak) (r:4.30.16/26.23.21/7.11.39/7.11.38) (q:draft)
nungakna = (t:n) (w:virginity) (d:nungak with -na, the state of being a virgin; nungakna lim is the sign or proof of it) (e:numei’ sungah ~ lim a kimuh kei leh/ama sungah ~ lim ka mu kei hi | I did not find proof of virginity in her/a tanu uh’ ~ lim a kilatna puan | the cloth that shows the proof of their daughter’s virginity) (b:nungak) (r:5.22.20/26.23.8/5.22.14/5.22.15) (q:draft)
nungakno = (t:n) (w:young woman/young girl/young virgin) (d:nungak, young unmarried woman, with no, young; nungakno hun is the time of a woman’s youth) (e:~ khat kizong hen la/pasal a thei nai lo ~ zali mu uh | they found four hundred young women who had not known a man/a ~ hun lai mah bangin | as in the days of her youth) (b:nungak) (r:11.1.2/7.21.12/28.2.15) (q:draft)
nungaknote = (t:n) (w:young women/girls/maidens) (d:nungakno, young unmarried woman, with the plural te) (e:Jerusalem ~ a kun ngelhngalh uh hi/tuitawi dingin hong paikhia ~ tuak uh a | they met young women coming out to draw water/pasal a thei nai lo ~ khempeuh | all the girls who have not known a man) (s:nungakte) (b:nungakno) (r:25.2.10/9.9.11/4.31.18) (q:draft)
nungaknu = (t:n) (w:young woman/girl) (d:nungak, young woman, with nu marking a female person: the young woman, one particular girl) (e:Tua ciangin ~ a inn-ah tai-in) (b:nungak) (r:1.24.28) (q:draft)
nungakte = (t:n) (w:virgins/young women/maidens/girls) (d:nungak, young unmarried woman, with the plural te; Jerusalem nungakte is the daughters of Jerusalem) (e:tangvalte leh ~/tua ~ tho-in a meivak ciat a bawl uh | those virgins got up and trimmed their lamps/~ leh tangvalte, dangtakin puk ding uh hi | young women and young men will faint from thirst/Jerusalem ~ aw, ka vom hangin | young women of Jerusalem, though I am dark) (s:nungaknote) (a:tangvalte) (b:nungak) (r:24.51.22/40.25.7/30.8.13/22.1.5) (q:draft)
nungcianga = (t:adv) (w:afterwards/later/in the future) (d:nung, after, with ciang, time, and a; a nungcianga piang ding is what will happen afterwards) (e:a ~ piang ding thu na genkhol) (s:nungciangin) (r:66.10.11) (q:draft)
nungciangin = (t:adv) (w:afterward/later/then) (d:nung, after, with ciangin, when; tua nungciangin is after that, a nungciangin is afterward or in turn) (e:Tua ~ vantungmi in kuang la-in/a ~ amaute hauhna in note’ zawn’na hong huhin | afterward their plenty will supply your need) (s:nungcianga) (r:66.8.5/47.8.14) (q:draft)
nungdalin = (t:n) (w:as rear guard) (d:nungdal, what shields the rear, with in, as: marching last to guard those in front) (e:adang khempeuh’ ~ Dan mite’ giahphual) (r:4.10.25) (q:draft, low confidence)
nungdalte = (t:n) (w:rear guard/rear troops) (d:the men who come behind or are posted at the back of an army; plural with te) (e:thuciamna singkuang nungah a ~ pai uh hi/na galte uh delhin a ~ bawh un | pursue your enemies and attack their rear/a ~ in mei-am alh tawh kibang hi | their rear ranks are like a blazing flame/a ~ uh nitumna tuipi sungah ka khia ding | I will drive their rear ranks into the western sea) (a:madawkte) (r:6.6.9/6.10.19/29.2.3/29.2.20) (q:draft)
nungdelh = (t:v) (w:pursue/chase after/run after) (d:nung, behind, with delh, chase) (e:Assiria mite na ~ lai hi/Gehazi in Naaman ~ hi | Gehazi ran after Naaman/Khaldea galkapte in Zedekiah kumpipa a ~ uh a | the Chaldean soldiers pursued King Zedekiah/galphualah nakpitakin a ~ uh hi | they pursued them hard in the battle) (s:delh/nawhdelh) (r:26.16.28/25.3.43/12.5.21/24.52.8/9.14.22) (q:draft)
nungdelhin = (t:v) (w:running after/pursuing) (d:nungdelh, run after, with in linking it to the next verb) (e:amah ~ ama tung panin) (b:nungdelh) (r:12.5.20) (q:draft)
nungdelhsak = (t:v) (w:make pursue/send in pursuit) (d:nungdelh pursue, with sak, cause to: namsau ka nungdelhsak ding is I will make the sword pursue them) (e:namsau ka ~ ding hi/a sih khit dong uh namsau ka ~ ding | I will make the sword pursue them until they are dead/amaute a that dingin namsau ka ~ ding hi | I will send the sword after them to kill them) (b:nungdelh) (r:24.49.37/26.12.14/24.9.16) (q:draft)
nunggen = (t:v) (w:speak later/speak afterwards) (d:nung, after, with gen, speak) (e:nidang khat thu ~ nawn lo ding hi) (r:58.4.8) (q:draft)
nungguh = (t:n) (w:backbone/spine) (d:nung, back, with guh, bone) (e:a ~ ciangah a ki-attan a mei thau) (r:3.3.9) (q:draft)
nunghei = (t:v) (w:look back/turn around) (d:turn the head or the body to look behind) (e:zi ~ a, amah cikhuam suak hi/~ kei un la | do not look back/khat beek ~ lo uh hi | not even one of them turns back/Benjamin mite ~ uh hi | the Benjamites looked back) (r:1.19.26/1.19.17/34.2.8/7.20.40)
nungin = (t:v) (w:blowing/blow) (d:of the wind; nung blow with -in, linking it to the next verb) (e:huih hong ~ a mut siang hi/Leitaw lam-ah huih ~, leilu lam-ah nung leuleu a | the wind blows to the south and then to the north/Topa kiang pan huih ~ | a wind blew from the Lord/sehnel gam panin huihpi pingpei hong ~ | a whirlwind came blowing from the desert) (r:18.37.21/21.1.6/4.11.31/18.1.19) (q:draft)
nungkiat = (t:v) (w:fall backward/tumble backward) (d:nung, back, with kiat, fall) (e:petin a tuangpa ~ hi) (r:1.49.17) (q:draft)
nungkik = (t:v) (w:retreat/withdraw/turn back/draw back) (d:go back from where one has advanced, as an army retreats or a river turns back) (e:gal kido ni-in ~ uh hi/zo zo loin a ~ ding hi | unable to win, he will retreat/Khaldea galkapte a ~ uh hi | the Chaldean army withdrew/ama kiang panin ~ un | withdraw from him) (s:nungkin) (a:mainawt) (b:nung) (r:19.78.9/24.37.11/27.11.9/10.11.15) (q:draft)
nungkikin = (t:v) (w:turn back/go back/shrink back) (d:form of nungkik with -in, linking to what follows) (e:Jerusalem khua-ah ~ a zong uh hi/a galte uh mai-ah ~, tai uh hi | they turn back before their enemies and flee/amau’ kiang panin ~ a gamah ciahkik uh | they withdrew from them and returned to their land/Eite pen ~ a maimang mite ihi kei a | we are not those who shrink back and perish) (b:nungkik) (r:42.2.45/58.10.39/6.7.12/12.3.27) (q:draft)
nungkikna = (t:n) (w:turning back/retreat) (d:nungkik, turn back, with the noun suffix na) (e:Jordan gun aw, na ~ ding) (b:nungkik) (r:19.114.5) (q:draft)
nungkiksak = (t:v) (w:turn back/drive back/make retreat) (d:nungkik go back with sak, cause) (e:Galte kiang panin kote nong ~ a/Ka galte na ~ a | you made my enemies turn back/liim pen kalsawm ka ~ ding hi | I will make the shadow go back ten steps/keima siat nading a deihte ~ in la | turn back those who desire my ruin) (b:nungkik) (r:19.44.10/23.38.8/19.18.40/19.40.14) (q:draft)
nungkin = (t:v) (w:go backward/shrink back/turn back) (d:draw back instead of going forward, set against mainawt, go forward) (e:mainawt loin a ~ zaw uh hi/a ~ mite lakah i om kei hi | we are not among those who shrink back/hih mite lam khial-in ~ paisuak lawmlawm uh | these people have gone astray and keep going backward) (s:nungkik) (a:mainawt) (r:24.7.24/58.10.39/24.8.5) (q:draft)
nungkinin = (t:v) (w:drawing back/shrinking back) (d:nungkin, go backward, with in linking it to the next verb) (e:amaute ~ a puk uh hi/vunatte a kihtak maninah ~ a tuam om hi | fearing the circumcised, he drew back and kept apart) (b:nungkin) (r:43.18.6/48.2.12) (q:draft)
nunglam = (t:n) (w:back/rear/behind) (d:nung back with lam side, direction: the back side, the direction behind; of a ship the stern; nunglam en is look back) (e:Nitumna lam biakbuk ~ adingin/letsan len kawm a, ~ a en mi | one who holds the plow and looks back/ka thute na ~ uhah na pai uh hi | you cast my words behind you/na ~ panun na bil un a za ding | your ears will hear it from behind you) (s:nung) (a:mailam) (r:2.36.27/42.9.62/19.50.17/23.30.21) (q:draft)
nunglamah = (t:adv) (w:backward/to the rear) (d:nunglam, the back side, with ah, to) (e:amaute ~ kin uh a) (b:nunglam) (r:43.18.6) (q:draft)
nungngat = (t:v) (w:turn away from/turn the back on/reject) (d:turn the back toward someone, from nung back and ngat face toward) (e:kei nong ~ niloh hi/A hong leitawite na ~ kei un | do not turn away from those who want to borrow from you/amah ka lehdo kei a, ka ~ kei hi | I did not rebel against him or turn away/kei hong mangngilhin hong ~ na hih manin | because you have forgotten me and turned your back on me) (a:maingat) (r:24.15.6/40.5.42/23.50.5/26.23.35) (q:draft)
nungngatin = (t:v) (w:turn one's back on/face away from) (d:nungngat with the linking ending in: with the back turned to someone, the opposite of maingat, to face; also said of God turning away from his people) (e:kei hong ~ hong maingat lo uh a/biakna tau ~ nisuahna lam nga-in | with their backs to the altar and facing east/Amah ~ a tut lai takin | as she sat with her back turned/amaute ~, a galte uh khut sungah pia-in | turning away from them and giving them into the hands of their enemies) (b:nungngat) (r:24.32.33/1.21.16/26.8.16/26.39.23) (q:draft)
nungnung = (t:v) (w:keep blowing/blow on and on) (d:nung, blow, of the wind, said twice for an action that goes on) (e:mah zui-in, ~ niloh hi) (r:21.1.6) (q:draft)
nungpai = (t:v) (w:go afterward/come later/follow later) (d:nung, behind or after, with pai, go: go or come after others have gone) (e:Buk Pawi siim dingin a ~ hi/A hong ~ Adonikam-te beh zong hi uh a | they were of the clan of Adonikam, who came later) (a:mapai) (r:43.7.10/15.8.13) (q:draft)
nungpen = (t:adj) (w:remotest/farthest/hindmost) (d:nung, back, with pen, most: farthest in) (e:a gam tawng ~ ah ka lut a) (b:nung) (r:12.19.23) (q:draft)
nungphawk = (t:v) (w:realize afterwards/remember later) (d:nung, after, with phawk, remember or realize) (e:piang ahihna thu a ~ uh hi) (r:43.12.16) (q:draft)
nungphiat = (t:v) (w:set aside/annul/cancel afterwards) (d:nung, after, with phiat, erase: undo an agreement once it has been made) (e:kuamah in tua thukimna ~ thei lo) (r:48.3.15) (q:draft)
nungsak = (t:v) (w:make blow/cause to blow/stir up/send) (d:of wind: make it blow; nung, blow, with the causative -sak) (e:amah in a huih ~ a/Pasian in leitungah huih ~ a, tui kiam hi | God made a wind blow over the earth and the water went down/tuipi hualte piangsaka, huihpi ~ hi | he raised the waves of the sea and made a storm blow/a saal sung panin huih a ~ hi | he brings the wind out of his storehouses) (r:19.147.18/24.51.1/1.8.1/19.107.25/24.51.16) (q:draft)
nungsakin = (t:v) (w:make blow/cause to blow/send a wind) (d:nung blow, said of wind, with causative sak and the linking ending in) (e:vantungah nisuahna huih ~/Ka hehna tawh huihpi ~, guahpi zusakin | in my anger making a storm blow and heavy rain fall/Topa in ama huihsa ~ | the Lord will send his scorching wind) (b:nungsak) (r:19.78.26/26.13.13/23.11.15) (q:draft)
nungsang = (t:conj) (w:now that/since/after) (d:placed at the end of a clause, after ahih or khit) (e:lungnuamin inn hong tung khin ahih ~/Topa in ka lampi ma-vangsak khin ahih ~ | now that the Lord has made my journey succeed/Nang hong kiniam koih khit ~ | now that you have been laid low/Khrih’ thu gen uh ahih ~, kei ka lungdam | since they preach Christ, I rejoice) (r:10.19.30/23.14.8/1.24.56/50.1.18) (q:draft)
nungsuk = (t:v) (w:blow down/sweep down) (d:of wind: nung blow, with suk downward; paired with nungto, blow upward) (e:Tuipi tungah huihpi nakpi ~ a/Saklam huih aw, hong ~ in la | north wind, blow down) (a:nungto) (r:42.8.23/22.4.16) (q:draft)
nungta = (t:adj) (w:alive) (e:Mite in tangvalnopa a ~-in innah a paipih uh/ka tapa Josef ~ lai hi | my son Joseph is still alive/Amah a ~ lai hiam | is he still alive) (s:hing) (a:sisa) (r:44.20.12/1.45.28/1.43.27)
nungta = (t:adj) (w:living) (e:A ~ Pasian khut sungah/a ~ Pasian’ Tapa, Khazih na hi hi | you are the Christ, the Son of the living God/mi ~ leh misite thu khen dingin | to judge the living and the dead) (s:ahing) (a:sisa) (r:58.10.31/1.1.20/40.16.16/44.10.42)
nungta = (t:v) (w:alive/live/be alive) (d:live, be alive; a nungta lai is still living) (e:tangvalnopa a ~-in innah a paipih uh/Khazih sungah mi khempeuh a ~ uh hi | in Christ all are made alive/a tawntungin ka ~ a | I am alive for ever/a pusuak thu khempeuh tawh a ~ hi | he lives by every word that comes out) (a:si/sih) (r:44.20.12/27.6.21/46.15.22/66.1.18/5.8.3)
nungtakik = (t:v) (w:live again/come back to life/revive) (d:nungta, live, with kik, again; with sak, raise to life again) (e:a sih hangin a ~ ding hi/hih misi guhte a ~ thei ding hiam | can these dead bones live again/a bul sel kikin ~ thei hi | its stump sprouts again and it can live again/Pasian in Zeisu ~ sak a | God raised Jesus to life again) (s:hingkik/nuntakkik/hinkik) (b:nungta) (r:43.11.25/18.14.7/26.37.3/44.13.32) (q:draft)
nungtalai = (t:v) (w:be still alive/survive/remain alive) (d:nungta live with lai still; a nungtalai is one who is still alive, a survivor) (e:a ~ kuamah om nawn kei hen/a hong thah khak loh a ~ note aw | you who are still alive, whom it has not killed/galte sung panin a ~ mite | the survivors from among the enemies) (s:hinlai) (r:24.44.7/24.51.50/38.14.16) (q:draft)
nungtasak = (t:v) (w:let live/keep alive/revive) (d:cause to live, spare the life of, give life again) (e:kei hong ~ in/nau pasalte ~ uh hi | they let the baby boys live/hong ~ in, nangmah kong phat ding uh hi | revive us and we will praise you/Kha Siangtho in eite hong ~ khinta ahih manin | since the Holy Spirit has given us life) (s:nuntaksak) (a:sisak/that) (b:nungta) (r:11.20.32/19.85.6/2.1.17/19.80.18/48.5.25) (q:draft)
nungtasakkik = (t:v) (w:revive/bring back to life/make live again) (d:nungtasak make live, with kik again) (e:note kong ~ ding hi/na mite hong ~ lo ding na hi hiam | will you not revive your people again/hu hong guan in kong ~ ding hi | I will put breath in you and make you live again) (s:hingkiksak/thokiksak) (b:nungtasak) (r:26.37.5/19.85.6/26.37.6) (q:draft)
nungtasuak = (t:v) (w:survive/go on living/stay alive) (d:nungta, alive, with suak, come out as) (e:mawhna bawl leh ~ tuan lo ding hi) (r:26.33.12) (q:draft)
nungtate = (t:n) (w:living/the living) (d:those who are alive, living people or creatures) (e:leitungah a gamtaang, a ~ khempeuh/a ~’ Pasian ahi hi | he is the God of the living/misite leh mi ~’ Topa a suah nadingin | so that he might be Lord of the dead and the living/A ~’ laibu sung panin amaute kiphiatsak in | blot them out of the book of the living) (a:misite) (b:nungta) (r:41.12.27/1.1.28/45.14.9/19.69.28) plural form of <nungta>
nungtazaw = (t:v) (w:outlive/live longer) (d:nungta, alive, with zaw, more; with sangin, than) (e:Joshua sangin sau a ~ upate khempeuh) (b:nungta) (r:6.24.31) (q:draft)
nungtazo = (t:v) (w:be able to live/survive) (d:nungta live, with zo, be able, manage to) (e:kua ~ ding ahi hiam/amah hong kilaak ciangin kua ~ ding ahi hiam | who can survive when he appears/Faro in a piak tawh amaute ~ uh | they could live on what Pharaoh gave them) (b:nungta) (r:4.24.23/39.3.2/1.47.22) (q:draft)
nungto = (t:v) (w:blow up/blow upward) (d:of wind: nung, blow, with to, upward; paired with nungsuk, blow down, and said to the south wind in the verse) (e:khanglam huih aw, hong ~ in) (a:nungsuk) (r:22.4.16) (q:draft)
nungzang = (t:n) (w:back) (d:the back of the body) (e:ka ~ kuikeek uh a/ka ~ uh-ah vangikpi nong suan hi | you laid a heavy burden on our backs/mihaite’ ~ ah ciangduai kinga hi | a rod is for the back of fools/ka mawhna khempeuh na ~ ah na koih hi | you have put all my sins behind your back) (s:nung) (r:19.129.3/20.10.13/19.66.11/23.38.17) (q:draft)
nungzangah = (t:adv) (w:on the back) (d:nungzang, the back of a person or animal, with the place marker ah) (e:mihaite’ ~ ciangduai kinga hi/A ~ vasa-kha tawh a kibang kha li | on its back four wings like the wings of a bird/amau’ hauhnate la ~ | their riches on the backs of donkeys) (b:nungzang) (r:20.10.13/27.7.6/23.30.6) (q:draft)
nungzui = (t:n) (w:disciple/follower/attendant) (d:one who follows behind; nungzui honpi is a retinue or caravan) (e:A ~ nihte in ama thu/Simon Piter’ nau Andru a kici ama ~ khat | one of his disciples, Andrew, the brother of Simon Peter/Zeisu in a it ~ khat | the disciple whom Jesus loved/a ~ khempeuh kithehthang a | all his followers were scattered) (s:thuzui) (r:43.1.37/11.10.2/43.6.8/43.13.23/44.5.36) (q:draft)
nungzuih = (t:v) (w:follow/follow after) (d:nung, behind, with zuih, a form of zui, follow: go after someone, follow behind) (e:Peter in zong a kihalin ~ hi/Jesuh a zong dingin ~ uh a | they went after Jesus to look for him) (s:zuih/sulzuih) (b:nungzui) (r:42.22.54/41.1.36) (q:draft)
nungzuihin = (t:v) (w:following/following after) (d:nungzuih, follow, with in linking it to the next verb) (e:leh mihonte in hong ~) (b:nungzuih) (r:44.21.36) (q:draft)
nungzuihpihte = (t:n) (w:fellow disciples/fellow followers) (d:nungzuih, follow, with pih, together with, and plural te: those who follow along with one) (e:ci-in a ~ a zawn hi) (r:43.11.16) (q:draft)
nungzuipa = (t:n) (w:disciple/follower) (d:nungzui, disciple, with pa marking a man: one particular disciple, as in a it nungzuipa, the disciple he loved) (e:Piter leh adang ~ paikhia uh a/Zeisu’ it ~ in Piter kiangah | the disciple whom Jesus loved said to Peter/adang ~ in Piter makhelhin han a tung masa hi | the other disciple outran Peter and reached the tomb first/Tua ~ a si kei ding hi | that disciple will not die) (s:nungzui/thuzui) (b:nungzui) (r:43.20.3/43.19.27/43.21.7/43.20.4/43.21.23) (q:draft)
nungzuite = (t:n) (w:disciples/followers) (d:nungzui, disciple, with plural te: the disciples of Jesus, or the followers of any leader) (e:~ tawh sawtpi a omkhawm uh hi/Nitak ciangin a ~ tuili-ah paisuk uh a | when evening came his disciples went down to the lake/Zeisu leh a ~ zong lawmvakna-ah a sam uh hi | Jesus and his disciples were also invited to the wedding/a ~ tawh a hawm ding uh hi | he will share it with his followers) (b:nungzui) (r:44.14.28/43.6.16/43.2.2/27.11.24) (q:draft)
nunna = (t:n) (w:blowing) (d:nun, blow, of wind, with the noun suffix na; huih nunna lam is where the wind blows, huihpi nunna gam a land swept by storms) (e:sehnel gam, huihpi ~ gam sungah/huih ~ lam peuhah a kinil kawikawi tuihualte | waves tossed wherever the wind blows) (b:nun) (r:5.32.10/59.1.6) (q:draft)
nuno = (t:n) (w:aunt/mother's sister) (d:nu, mother, with no, young: the younger sister of one's mother) (e:ama nu; ama ~ ahi) (b:nu) (r:43.19.25) (q:draft)
nuntak = (t:v) (w:live) (d:form of nungta, live, used before words such as khit, sung, lai, ding and theih; a nuntak sung tawntung is all the days of his life) (e:kum nga a ~ khit ciangin/Topa a ~ bangin | as surely as the Lord lives/Samuel in a ~ sung tawntung Israelte thukhen hi | Samuel judged Israel all the days of his life/Pa hangin ka ~ mah bangin | just as I live because of the Father/Na ~ theih nadingin Babilon kumpipa’ hakkol pua in | bear the yoke of the king of Babylon so that you may live) (s:hin) (a:sih/si) (b:nungta) (r:1.5.6/24.5.2/9.7.15/43.6.57/24.27.12)
nuntakdan = (t:n) (w:way of life/conduct/manner of living) (d:nuntak, live, with dan, manner: the way a person lives and behaves) (e:lungsim kikhat leh ~ kikhat ka pia ding hi/amau’ ~ leh a nasepna gahte tung tawnin | according to their conduct and the fruit of their deeds) (s:nuntakzia/omdan/gamtatzia) (r:24.32.39/24.32.19) (q:draft)
nuntakdante = (t:n) (w:ways of life/ways) (d:nuntakdan, way of life, with plural te) (e:tu-in na ~ uh leh na gamtatziate uh) (s:nuntakziate) (b:nuntakdan) (r:24.26.13) (q:draft)
nuntakkik = (t:v) (w:live again/come back to life) (d:nuntak, live, with kik, again; nuntakkik sak is raise to life again) (e:Ka ~ theih nadingin si ngam/Pasian in sihna panin a ~ sakpa | the one whom God raised from the dead) (s:hingkik/hinkik/nungtakik/thokik) (b:nuntak) (r:43.10.17/44.13.37) (q:draft)
nuntaklawh = (t:v) (w:live as a result/be kept alive) (d:nuntak, live, with lawh, get as gain: come to live because of what was done) (e:sat le-uhcin ~ zaw ding uh hi) (r:20.23.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
nuntakna = (t:n) (w:living) (d:the state of being alive; nuntakna a nei is living, having life) (e:~ a nei a gamtang thei ganhing/~ a nei khempeuhte’ deihna na lungkim sak hi | you satisfy the desires of every living thing/mi in ~ a nei mihing hong suak pah hi | the man became a living being/Pasian’ teel ~ suangpi ahi | he is the living stone chosen by God) (s:hinna) (r:19.145.16/1.1.21/1.2.7/60.2.4)
nuntakna = (t:n) (w:life) (e:Lung kipna tawh ~ na ngah ding/tu-in ka ~ hong la in | now take my life/Huan laizangah zong ~ singkung | the tree of life also in the middle of the garden/~ a ngah kei ding hi | he will not have life) (s:hinna/hin) (a:sihna) (r:42.21.19/32.4.3/1.2.9/43.3.36)
nuntakna = (t:n) (w:livelihood) (d:what a person lives on, the means of making a living) (e:khapna-in ~ a la hi ding hi | he would be taking a livelihood as security) (r:5.24.6)
nuntakna = (t:n) (w:way of life) (d:the way a person lives, conduct) (e:bangmahin a kimang lo ~ panin | from the empty way of life/~ siangtho nei ta un | lead a holy life/a ~ hoihlote panin kikhel sakin | turning them from their evil ways) (s:nuntakzia/nuntakdan/omzia) (r:60.1.18/45.6.19/24.23.22)
Nuntakna = (t:n) (w:life) (d:nuntakna written with a capital, at the start of a sentence or as a title for the life that is in Jesus; Nuntakna laibu is the book of life) (e:hih ~ thu mite kiangah va hilh un/~ khomun ka hi hi | I am the bread of life/Thuman, le ~ zong ka hi hi | I am the truth and the life/~ laibu sungah a min om lo mi peuhmah | anyone whose name is not in the book of life) (b:nuntakna) (r:44.5.20/43.14.6/43.6.48/66.20.15) (q:draft)
nuntaknate = (t:n) (w:lives/days of life) (d:nuntakna, life, with plural te) (e:leitunga i ~ in niliim bang hi) (b:nuntakna) (r:18.8.9) (q:draft)
nuntaksa = (t:v) (w:already living/have lived) (d:nuntak, live, with sa, already done) (e:na ~ uh ahih mah bangin) (b:nuntak) (r:52.4.1) (q:draft)
nuntaksak = (t:v) (w:keep alive/give life/preserve/spare) (d:nuntak, live, with the causative sak: give life to someone or keep someone alive) (e:a pilte a ~ theihna ahi hi/mi sisate nangawn thosakin a ~ mah bangin | just as he raises the dead and gives them life/ka ~, ka nusiat lai mite | the people I keep alive and leave) (s:hingsak/nungtasak) (a:that) (b:nuntak) (r:21.7.12/43.5.21/24.50.20) (q:draft)
nuntaksaknop = (t:v) (w:want to spare/want to keep alive) (d:nuntak, live, with sak, cause, and nop, want) (e:a ~ leh a nungtasak hi) (a:thahnop) (r:27.5.19) (q:draft)
nuntaksung = (t:n) (w:lifetime) (d:nuntak, live, with sung, during; a nuntaksung tawntung is as long as he lived) (e:amah a ~ tawntung nisimin tanh khat) (s:khansung/hunsung) (r:12.25.30) (q:draft)
nuntakzia = (t:n) (w:way of life/ways/conduct) (d:nuntak, live, with zia, manner: the way a person or a people live, often paired with gamtatna, deeds) (e:Mite’ ~ khempeuh na mu a/Na ~ uh leh na gamtatnate uh kikhel un | reform your ways and your actions/amau’ ~ va en in | go and consider its ways/Na pu na pate uh ~ | the way of life of your ancestors) (s:nuntakdan/omdan/gamtatzia) (r:24.32.19/24.7.3/20.6.6/60.1.18) (q:draft)
nuntakziate = (t:n) (w:ways of life/conduct) (d:nuntakzia, way of life, with plural te) (e:note’ upna hangin na ~ uh) (s:nuntakdante) (b:nuntakzia) (r:52.1.3) (q:draft)
nunte = (t:n) (w:buds/knobs) (d:bud-shaped ornaments on the lampstand, plural of nun) (e:a haite, a ~ leh a pakte/a ~ leh a pakte tawh a om | with its buds and blossoms/Amau’ ~ leh a hiangte in sakhat hi ding a | their buds and branches shall be of one piece) (b:nun) (r:2.37.17/2.25.34/2.25.36) (q:draft)
nunung = (t:adj) (w:last/latter/final) (d:a nunung penin and a nunung belin are last of all, finally) (e:A ~ penin a numei zong/a masa lam sangin a ~ lamah | in the latter part more than in the former/A ~ kim khatte in a masa ding uh hi | some who are last will be first/A ~ belin a hun cing lopi-a suak keima kiangah | last of all to me, one born at the wrong time) (s:tawp) (a:masa) (r:40.22.27/18.42.12/42.13.30/46.15.8) (q:draft)
nununga = (t:adj) (w:latter/later/last) (d:nunung, last, with a, describing the noun that follows; opposite of a masa, the first) (e:a ~ na gamtatnate in a masa) (a:masa) (b:nunung) (r:66.2.19) (q:draft)
nunungin = (t:adv) (w:last/behind/afterwards) (d:nunung, last, with in; opposite of a masa-in, in front) (e:lasate, a ~ tamngai tumte) (a:amasa) (b:nunung) (r:19.68.25) (q:draft)
nunungna = (t:n) (w:the last/latter one) (d:nunung, last, with the noun suffix na, after a verb: the later time of doing; khem nunungna is the last deception) (e:sangin a khem ~ uh hong husiazaw) (a:masakna) (b:nunung) (r:40.27.64) (q:draft)
nunungpen = (t:adj) (w:last/very last/lowest) (d:nunung, last, with pen, most; in Luke 22.26 of the follower of lowest rank, the one who serves) (e:a tum ~ pan a kipanin/a nungzui ~ bangin om ding hi | he shall be like the lowest follower) (a:masapen) (b:nunung) (r:40.20.8/42.22.26) (q:draft)
nunungte = (t:n) (w:the last/last ones) (d:those who come last; also after a noun, as in kam nunungte, last words) (e:A tum ~ in nai khat bek/a ~ in a masa ding uh hi | the last will be first/hihte in David’ kam ~ ahi hi | these are the last words of David/a masa le a ~ | the first and the last) (a:masate) (b:nunung) (r:40.20.12/10.23.1/40.20.16/14.35.27) (q:draft)
nupa = (t:n) (w:couple/pair) (d:husband and wife; of animals a male and female pair, as in nupa kop) (e:Sapfira min nei ~ khat in/Ganhing siangtho ~ kop sagih | seven pairs of clean animals, male and female/amau ~ in ta nei lo uh a | the couple had no children/a ~ ciat-un om ding uh hi | each will be with its mate) (s:nulepa/zilepasal) (r:44.5.1/1.7.2/42.1.7/23.34.15)
nupate = (t:n) (w:married couple/husband and wife) (d:nupa, couple, with plural te: a husband and wife; tua nupate is that couple, the two of them) (e:Tua ~ tawh a kimu dingin/tua ~ mah bangin Paul zong | Paul too, like that couple/~ thu in hih bang ahih leh | if this is how it is between husband and wife) (s:zilepasal) (b:nupa) (r:44.18.2/40.19.10/44.18.3) (q:draft)
nupi = (t:n) (w:woman/married woman) (d:grown or married woman; papi, nupi leh naupangte is men, women and children) (e:papi, ~ leh naupangte i susia hi/~ nau suak ding bangin na i sa hi | we feel pain like a woman in labour/papi, ~-a kipan mi khempeuh kiangah | to all the people, men and women/inn sung ~ ahi numei’ tapa a cina hi | the son of the woman who owned the house became ill) (s:numei) (a:papi) (b:nu) (r:5.3.6/24.6.24/24.44.20/11.17.17) (q:draft)
nupite = (t:n) (w:women) (d:plural of nupi, grown or married women) (e:~ leh naupangte a muh ciangin/Inn-a om ~ in galte’ van kisutte hawm uh a | the women at home divide the plunder/Midian ~ leh a tate uh man uh hi | they captured the Midianite women and their children/~ nute bangin | older women as mothers) (s:numeite) (a:papite) (b:nupi) (r:1.33.5/19.68.12/4.31.9/54.5.2) (q:draft)
nusia = (t:v) (w:leave/forsake/abandon/leave behind) (d:go away from a person or place, or let something stay behind; of God or his law, forsake) (e:a nu leh a pa ~-in a zi/note tagahte bangin kong ~ kei ding a | I will not leave you as orphans/tuute ~-in tai a | he leaves the sheep and runs away/Nangma thu a ~ migilote hangin | because of the wicked who forsake your law/lei sungah a bul leh a zungte ~ in | leave the stump and its roots in the ground) (s:taisan) (r:1.2.24/43.14.18/43.10.12/19.119.53/27.4.23)
nusia = (t:v) (w:pass away) (d:leave this world, depart from life, as in leitung nusia) (e:hih leitung ~-in a Pa kiangah a pai ding | to leave this world and go to the Father/tu-in leitung ~ leuleu-in Pa kiang a zuankik ding | now leaving the world again and going back to the Father) (r:43.13.1/43.16.28)
nusiacip = (t:v) (w:abandon/leave behind/forsake) (d:nusia, leave, with cip, firmly: leave and not come back for it) (e:gamah kei nong ~ kei ding a/tua singkung phukin a ~ ding uh hi | they will cut down the tree and leave it) (s:taisan) (b:nusia) (r:44.2.27/26.31.12) (q:draft)
nusiakha = (t:v) (w:neglect/leave out/leave behind) (d:nusia, leave, with kha, happen to) (e:a thupiteng na ~ uh a) (r:40.23.24) (q:draft)
nusiakhawm = (t:v) (w:leave together with) (d:nusia, leave, with khawm, together) (e:gamlak lopate tawh ~ in) (b:nusia) (r:27.4.23) (q:draft)
nusiakik = (t:v) (w:desert/turn away from/leave again) (d:nusia, leave, with kik, back or again) (e:note a hong sam Pasian ~ pakin) (b:nusia) (r:48.1.6) (q:draft)
nusialai = (t:v) (w:leave behind/leave remaining) (d:nusia, leave, with lai, still) (e:a zawngpente pawlkhat a ~ hi) (r:24.52.16) (q:draft)
nusian = (t:n) (w:goddess) (d:a female deity; used of Ashtoreth, Asherah and Artemis) (e:Sidon mite’ ~ Ashtoreth/Artemis ~ biakna innpi | the temple of the goddess Artemis/a ~ uh Asherah milimte | the images of their goddess Asherah/i ~ zong bangmah gensiatna nei lo | nor have they blasphemed our goddess) (s:pasiannu) (r:11.11.5/24.17.2/44.19.27/44.19.37) (q:draft)
nusiapa = (t:n) (w:deserter/one who abandons) (d:nusia, leave, with pa marking a man: the man who leaves) (e:a tuuhonte a ~ in gimna ngah ta hen) (b:nusia) (r:38.11.17) (q:draft)
nusiat = (t:v) (w:leave/forsake/abandon) (d:form of nusia used before a following word such as hangin, or to describe a noun) (e:ka pa in hong ~ hangin/Topa ~ ding ka ngaihsun kei ding uh hi | we would never think of forsaking the Lord/bangmah ~ nei kei un | leave nothing behind/Joshua a sih lai-in a ~ minamte | the nations Joshua left when he died) (s:nutsiat/taisan) (b:nusia) (r:19.27.10/7.2.21/6.24.16/24.50.26) (q:draft)
nusiate = (t:n) (w:those who forsake/those who leave) (d:people who have left or abandoned someone or something) (e:Topa a ~ pen kibeimangsak ding hi/amah a ~ khempeuh tungah amah heh hi | he is angry with all who forsake him/tua teng a ~ khempeuh in | everyone who has left all these) (b:nusia) (r:23.1.28/40.19.29/15.8.22) (q:draft)
nusiatin = (t:v) (w:left lying/abandoned) (d:nusiat, leave, with in: in the manner of a thing left lying; ek nusiatin is like dung left on the ground) (e:leilakah ek ~ a kinusia ding uh hi) (b:nusiat) (r:24.25.33) (q:draft, low confidence)
nusiatkhak = (t:v) (w:come to abandon/happen to forsake) (d:nusiat, leave, with khak, form of kha, happen to) (e:na ~ ding uh ka lunghimawh hi) (r:47.11.3) (q:draft)
nusiatlai = (t:adj) (w:left behind/remaining/spared) (d:nusiat, leave, with lai, still: describes people or things that someone has left where they were) (e:ka nuntaksak, ka ~ mite a mawhna uh/a ~ khuampite, tuikuangpite, a kingaknate | the pillars, the Sea and the stands that were left) (s:omlaisun) (r:24.50.20/24.27.19) (q:draft)
nusiatlam = (t:n) (w:having left behind) (d:nusiat, leave, with lam, the fact that: that they had left someone behind) (e:a ~ uh thei lo uh hi) (r:42.2.43) (q:draft)
nusiatna = (t:n) (w:forsaking/abandonment/desertion) (d:nusiat, forsake, with the noun suffix na; kei hong nusiatna uh is their forsaking me) (e:kei hong ~ uh leh keimah sangin milim) (s:taisatna) (b:nusiat) (r:26.6.9) (q:draft)
nusiatte = (t:n) (w:what is left/things left behind/those left behind) (d:nusiat, leave, with plural te: the people or things someone has left behind; van nusiatte is goods left behind, plunder) (e:a ~ tungah a uk dingin/gamlak ganhingte in amau’ ~ ne thei ding uh hi | the wild animals may eat what they leave/amau’ van ~ kikaikhawm a | their plunder is gathered) (s:kinusiate) (b:nusiat) (r:12.25.22/2.23.11/23.33.4) (q:draft)
nusiazo = (t:v) (w:have forsaken/have abandoned/have left) (d:nusia, leave or forsake, with zo showing that the act has been carried through) (e:Na tate un kei hong ~ uh a/Pasian in amah ~ a | God has forsaken him/Topa in a mite ~ hi | the Lord has left his people) (s:taisanzo) (b:nusia) (r:24.5.7/19.71.11/24.25.38) (q:draft)
nuta = (t:n) (w:mother and young/mother and child) (d:nu, mother, with ta, child; a mother together with her young, as in la nuta, a donkey and her colt) (e:la ~ thakhatin na mu ding uh/la ~ hong paipih uh a | they brought the donkey and her colt) (b:nu) (r:40.21.2/40.21.7) (q:draft)
nutate = (t:n) (w:mother and daughter/mother and child) (d:nuta, mother and child, with the plural ending te; in the verse a woman and her mother who are married to one man) (e:tuapa leh a ~, mei tawh kihallum ding hi) (b:nuta) (r:3.20.14) (q:draft)
nute = (t:n) (w:mothers) (d:nu with plural te; na nute na pate, your parents) (e:ka ~ uh a meigong khin uh/~ a phat lo mi pawlkhat om hi | there are some who do not bless their mothers/na ~ uh tawh om un | stay with your mothers/na ~ na pate thu uh na mang un | obey your parents) (a:pate) (b:nu) (r:25.5.3/20.30.11/8.1.8/49.6.1) (q:draft)
nutsiat = (t:v) (w:leave/leave behind/abandon) (d:spelling of nusiat, the form of nusia, leave, used before ding and khit and to describe a noun) (e:thong sungah khumin a ~ mi khat/tuipi sungah a ~ khit uh ciangin | after they left them in the sea/ka pumpi nuntakna ka ~ ding | that I will leave my bodily life) (s:nusiat) (r:44.25.14/44.27.40/61.1.13) (q:draft)
Nymfas = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Nympha) (d:Christian at Laodicea in whose house a church met) (r:51.4.15)
O = (t:intj) (w:O/oh) (d:exclamation placed before a name in address or lament, as English O) (e:~ Moab! gimna na ngah hi/~ Naftali, maipha tawh nuam a sa | O Naphtali, content with favour/~ Khemosh mite! na mangthang uh hi | O people of Chemosh, you are destroyed) (s:Aw) (r:4.21.29/10.7.20/5.33.23) (q:draft)
Obadiah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Obadiah) (d:name of several men, among them the prophet whose book bears his name and the palace administrator of Ahab) (r:13.12.9/16.10.5)
Obal = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Obal) (d:son of Joktan, a descendant of Shem) (r:1.10.28)
Obed = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Obed) (d:son of Boaz and Ruth, father of Jesse and grandfather of David; also the name of several other men) (r:8.4.17/13.2.12)
Obededom = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Obed-Edom) (d:the Gittite in whose house the ark of the covenant stayed for three months; also a Levite gatekeeper) (r:13.26.15/13.26.4)
Obil = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Obil) (d:the Ishmaelite in charge of the camels of King David) (r:13.27.30)
Oboth = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Oboth) (d:camping place of Israel in the wilderness, between Punon and Iye Abarim) (r:4.21.10/4.33.43) (q:draft)
Oded = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Oded) (d:father of the prophet Azariah in the time of King Asa; also a prophet in Samaria in the time of King Ahaz) (r:14.15.1/14.15.8)
odia = (t:see) <eu-odia>
Ofel = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Ophel) (d:the hill of Ophel in Jerusalem, near the temple, where the temple servants lived; Ofel mualbo is the hill of Ophel) (e:~ mualbo-ah teeng uh a/~ kulh tungah zong inn tampi lam hi | he also built much on the wall of Ophel) (r:16.11.21/14.27.3) (q:draft)
Ofir = (t:name) (c:male/land) (w:Ophir) (d:son of Joktan; also a land famous for its fine gold, as in Ofir kham, gold of Ophir) (r:1.10.29)
Ofni = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Ophni) (d:town in the territory of Benjamin) (r:6.18.24)
Ofrah = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Ophrah) (d:town in the territory of Benjamin; also the town of the Abiezrites, the home of Gideon) (r:6.18.23/7.8.32)
Ofraih = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ophrah) (d:son of Meonothai in the tribe of Judah) (r:13.4.14)
Og = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Og) (d:king of Bashan, defeated by Israel under Moses) (e:Bashan kumpipa ~ leh Kanaan kumpipa) (r:19.135.11/16.9.22) (q:draft)
oh = (t:intj) (w:oh) (d:exclamation that opens a plea, written Oh at the start of speech) (e:~, ka Topa aw, hong thum ing/~, ka Topa aw, tu-ma-siah hita leh | oh, my Lord, whether in the past) (r:2.4.13/2.4.10) (q:draft)
Ohad = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ohad) (d:third son of Simeon) (r:1.46.10/2.6.15)
Ohah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ohad) (d:a son of Simeon; the text spells the name Ohah) (r:1.46.10) (q:draft)
Ohel = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ohel) (d:descendant of David, listed among the children of Zerubbabel) (r:13.3.20)
Ohilibamath = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Oholibamah) (d:spelling of Oholibamah in this verse, a chief of Edom) (r:13.1.52)
Oholah = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Oholah) (d:symbolic name of Samaria, the elder of the two sisters in the parable of Ezekiel) (r:26.23.5/26.23.44)
Oholiab = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Oholiab) (d:son of Ahisamak of the tribe of Dan, the craftsman who helped Bezalel make the tabernacle) (r:2.35.34)
Oholibah = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Oholibah) (d:symbolic name of Jerusalem, the younger sister of Oholah in the parable of Ezekiel) (r:26.23.11/26.23.36)
Oholibahte = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Oholibah) (d:Oholibah with te, naming Oholah and Oholibah together as a pair) (b:Oholibah) (r:26.23.44)
Oholibamah = (t:name) (c:male/female) (w:Oholibamah) (d:wife of Esau, daughter of Anah; also the name of a chief of Edom) (r:1.36.41)
Oholimah = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Oholibamah) (d:spelling of Oholibamah in this verse, the daughter of Anah) (r:1.36.25)
ok = (t:v) (w:wear around the neck/hang around the neck/bind on) (d:put something on the neck as a chain or necklace) (e:na ngawng-ah tuate ~ in/ka ngawng-ah ka ~ ding a | I will wear it around my neck/kiphatsakna khainiang bangin ~ uh a | they wear pride like a necklace/amaute khempeuh kizepna-in na ~ ding hi | you will wear them all as ornaments) (s:awh) (r:20.3.3/19.73.6/18.31.36/23.49.18) (q:draft)
okin = (t:v) (w:bind around the neck/wear around the neck) (d:ok, wear around the neck, with in linking it to the next verb) (e:na ngawngah tuate ~, na lungtang tungah) (b:ok) (r:20.3.3) (q:draft)
Okran = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Okran) (d:father of Pagiel, the leader of the tribe of Asher in the wilderness) (r:4.1.13/4.10.26)
oksak = (t:v) (w:put around the neck/hang on) (d:ok, wear around the neck, with the causative sak: put a chain or necklace on someone) (e:a ngawng-ah kham khainiang khat ~ hi/khainiang kong ~ hi | I put a necklace on you/minphatna khamkhi a ngawngah a ~ hi | he put the gold chain of honour around his neck/minphatna khamkhi a ngawngah ka ~ ding a | I will put the gold chain of honour around his neck) (b:ok) (r:1.41.42/26.16.11/27.5.29/27.5.7) (q:draft)
oksakin = (t:v) (w:put around the neck/hang on) (d:oksak, put around someone's neck, with in linking it to the next verb) (e:na ngawngah hong ~, kumpi gam sungah) (b:oksak) (r:27.5.16) (q:draft)
ol = (t:adj) (w:easy/at ease/common) (d:easily had or done; ol tak-a is easily, ol sak is make plentiful) (e:suang bangin ngun ~ sak a/~ tak-a nuntakna na mu kei ding uh a | you will find no life of ease/~ tak-a hauh pakna in kiam kik pah a | wealth gained easily soon dwindles) (s:baih) (a:haksa) (r:11.10.27/20.13.11/5.28.65) (q:draft)
ol = (t:adj) (w:slow/lingering) (d:slow to come or to act; of speech that does not come readily; ol lo is not delayed) (e:ka kam pau ~-in, ka pau awk hi/tang lai-a kipanin ~ lo, zekai lo a | from long ago it has not been slow or delayed) (s:hak) (r:2.4.10/61.2.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
Olimpas = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Olympas) (d:Christian in Rome greeted by Paul) (r:45.16.15)
oliv = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:olive) (d:the olive tree and its fruit; oliv kung is an olive tree, oliv thau olive oil and oliv sing olive wood) (e:~ teh a tukkhiat thak khat/~ sing tawh kherub nih bawl a | he made two cherubim of olive wood/~ kungte leh khuaizu a omna leitang | a land of olive trees and honey/leh ~ thau bung khat | and a hin of olive oil) (s:olive) (r:1.8.11/66.11.4/11.6.23/5.8.8/2.30.24)
Oliv = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:olive) (d:oliv written with a capital, mostly in Oliv Mual, the Mount of Olives) (e:Zeisu ~ Mual ah a pai hi/~ Mualah a paikhia uh hi | they went out to the Mount of Olives/~ kici mualah a giak hi | he spent the night on the hill called Olives) (b:oliv) (r:43.8.1/42.19.29/40.26.30/42.21.37) (q:draft)
olive = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:olive) (d:spelling of oliv, the olive tree and its fruit) (e:~ kungte gah lo a) (s:oliv) (r:35.3.17) (q:draft)
olna = (t:n) (w:ease/easiness) (d:ol, easy, with the noun suffix na; nuntak olna gam is a land where living is easy, a good land) (e:nuntak ~ gam hiam, haksatna gam hiam) (s:baihna) (a:haksatna) (b:ol) (r:4.13.19) (q:draft)
olno = (t:adj) (w:easy) (d:ol, easy, with no; found as olno takin, easily, with little effort) (e:thungaihsun theite in ~ takin ngah thei) (s:baih) (a:haksa) (b:ol) (r:20.14.6/27.11.17) (q:draft)
oloes = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:aloes) (d:a fragrant substance used as perfume) (e:~ paknamtui leh kinnamon paknamtui tawh) (s:aloes/alo) (r:20.7.17) (q:draft)
olsak = (t:v) (w:make common/make plentiful) (d:ol, easy, with the causative sak; make a thing easy to get, as common as stones) (e:suang bangin ngun ~ a/suang bangin ngun leh kham ~ a | he made silver and gold as common as stones) (s:tamsak) (b:ol) (r:11.10.27/14.1.15) (q:draft)
oltak = (t:adv) (w:easily/at ease) (d:ol, easy, with tak making an adverb; oltak a nuntakna is a life of ease, rest) (e:Hih minamte lakah ~ a nuntakna na mu kei/hauhpakna ~ mahin kiamkik pah a | quick wealth just as easily dwindles away) (s:nuamtak) (b:ol) (r:5.28.65/20.13.11) (q:draft)
oltakin = (t:adv) (w:easily/with ease) (d:oltak, easily, with the adverb suffix in: without effort of one’s own, as when building on work that another has begun) (e:~ zomin a sem mi) (a:haksapipi-in) (b:oltak) (r:45.15.20) (q:draft)
Olympas = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Olympas) (d:Christian in Rome greeted by Paul at the end of his letter to the Romans) (r:45.16.15)
olzaw = (t:adj) (w:easier/more bearable) (d:ol, easy, with zaw, more: easier, or lighter to bear; used after sangin, than) (e:van le lei a manthan ding ~ lai hi/Sodom khua le Gomorrah khuamite’ thuakna ~ lai ding | it will be more bearable for the people of Sodom and Gomorrah/a pehkik ding ~ mahmah lai ding hi | it will be much easier to graft them back) (s:baihzaw) (a:haksazaw) (b:ol) (r:42.16.17/40.10.15/45.11.24) (q:draft)
om = (t:v) (w:be) (d:exist, be present, be in a place or in a state; a om is there is, om lo is there is not) (e:Hih lai takah ~ nawn lo hi/tuipi tung tengah khuamialna ~ a | darkness was over the surface of the deep/Kahna leh ha gawina a ~ ding hi | there will be weeping and gnashing of teeth/Kilamdan’na neukha beek a ~ kei hi | there is no difference at all) (r:42.24.6/1.1.2/40.13.50/45.3.22)
om = (t:v) (w:become) (d:come to be, come into existence or come upon someone, often with hong or pah) (e:tua ciangin khuavak ~ pah hi | and at once there was light/ganhing tungah thokang hong ~ hi | gnats came upon the animals) (r:1.1.3/2.8.17)
om = (t:v) (w:make) (d:in instructions om ding hi, there is to be, stands where the English says make) (e:khuampeek khatah a zang nih ciat ~ ding hi | each frame is to have two projections) (r:2.26.17)
om = (t:v) (w:happen/occur) (d:of an event such as war, famine or mourning: take place, there is) (e:Gam dang khempeuhah kialpi ~ hi | there was famine in all the other lands/Izipt gam sungah kahna lianpi ~ hi | there was loud wailing in Egypt/kulh kongpi sungah gal ~ pah hi | war came to the city gates/Filistiate tawh nakpi tak-a kidona ~ hi | there was bitter war with the Philistines) (r:1.41.54/2.12.30/7.5.8/9.14.52)
om = (t:v) (w:abide) (d:stay or live in a person or a place, remain there) (e:Mihingte sungah ka Kha ~ paisuak nawn lo ding hi/Kei sungah ~ un | remain in me/ka itna sungah ~ un | remain in my love/note sungah ~ ta hen | let it dwell in you) (r:1.6.3/43.15.4/43.15.9/51.3.16)
Om = (t:v) (w:be/exist) (d:om written with a capital, at the start of a sentence or in the name Kumpi Gam Om Lo, No Kingdom There) (e:Kumpi Gam ~ Lo, ci-in amaute in/~ hit-hiat un la, Pasian ka hihna thei un | be still, and know that I am God/~ mah hi | yes, there is/~ dih ni | let him be) (b:om) (r:23.34.12/19.46.10/24.37.17/40.27.49) (q:draft)
Omar = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Omar) (d:son of Eliphaz and grandson of Esau, a chief of Edom) (r:1.36.11/13.1.36)
omcip = (t:v) (w:remain/stay still/keep silent) (d:om, be, with cip, firmly: stay as one is without moving, answering or changing) (e:Jesuh pau loin a ~ hi/kuamah in dawng loin ~ uh hi | no one answered, they kept silent/bangmah hih loin na ~ leh | if you stay as you are and do nothing/a namsau a khut sungah ~ hi | his sword stayed fast in his hand/misi tawh kibangin ~ ahih manin | because he lay still like a dead man) (s:ommawk) (b:om) (r:41.14.61/42.14.4/17.4.14/10.23.10/41.9.26) (q:draft)
omcipin = (t:v) (w:remaining still/being left speechless) (d:omcip, stay still, with the linking suffix in: remaining without a move or a word, and) (e:a cih nading thei loin ~) (b:omcip) (r:26.7.27) (q:draft)
omdan = (t:n) (w:ways/conduct/way of life) (d:om, be, with dan, manner: how a person or a people live and behave; also how someone is getting on) (e:a ~ khempeuh uh ka mit-in ka mu a/Gamdangte’ ~ ciing kei un | do not learn the ways of the nations/ka mite’ ~ hoih takin a sin uh a | they learn well the ways of my people/Na ute’ ~ va mu inla | go and see how your brothers are) (s:omzia/nuntakzia) (r:24.16.17/24.10.2/24.12.16/9.17.18) (q:draft)
omden = (t:v) (w:remain/continue/stay on) (d:om, be, with den, continually: go on being so, stay as it is) (e:Tua bangin ~ hi/Leitungah tuiciin ni sawmli sung ~ hi | the flood stayed on the earth for forty days/a hehin ka ~ hi | I stayed full of indignation/nang pen a sangna-ah a ~ na hihna | that you remain on high) (s:omsuak) (r:4.9.16/1.7.17/24.15.17/19.92.6) (q:draft)
Omega = (t:name) (w:Omega) (d:last letter of the Greek alphabet, used with Alpha as a title of God and of Christ, the beginning and the end) (r:66.22.13/66.1.8)
omer = (t:see) <Khedorla-omer>
omgawp = (t:v) (w:carry on/behave without restraint) (d:om, be, with gawp, severely or to excess: be present and behave grossly) (e:zumna mel nei loin hong ~ uh) (b:om) (r:65.1.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
omin = (t:v) (w:being/staying/living) (d:om, be or stay, with the linking suffix in, joining it to the next clause) (e:in note lakah ~ note’ Pasian hi-in/Gampa lakah ni sawmli ~ | being in the wilderness forty days/amah tawh Topa ~ | the Lord being with him/Kha Siangtho huhna tawh ~ a khang semsem uh | living with the help of the Holy Spirit, they kept growing/Sidonte kiang panin gamla ~ | being far from the Sidonians) (b:om) (r:3.26.12/9.3.19/41.1.13/44.9.31/7.18.7) (q:draft)
omkha = (t:v) (w:happen to be/be there by chance) (d:om, be, with kha, by chance: happen to be somewhere; with ding or thei, there may be) (e:mi ginalo khat hong ~ hi/Gilboa Mual-ah ka ~ a | I happened to be on Mount Gilboa/Buaina lianpi hong ~ thei ding ahih manin | because there may be a great riot/Kei sungah siattheihna a ~ hiam hong en inla | see if there is any harmful way in me/Saul’ nasemte mi khat tua lai-ah na ~ hi | one of Saul’s servants happened to be there) (r:10.20.1/19.139.24/10.1.6/40.26.5/9.21.7) (q:draft)
omkhak = (t:v) (w:happen to be/chance to be) (d:form of omkha used before leh, loh and pen: be or exist by chance, mostly in if-clauses and warnings) (e:a phamawh a ~ zenzen leh/Hih bang lungsim a nei lo i ~ leh | if we happen to think differently/a gilo na ~ loh nadingun | so that none of you turns out to be evil/Hih thu a nialnuam a ~ zenzen leh | if anyone should want to dispute this/Note lakah ka ~ pen | that I happen to live among you) (b:omkha) (r:15.7.20/58.3.12/50.3.15/46.11.16/19.120.5) (q:draft)
omkhawm = (t:v) (w:be with/stay together/live together) (d:om, be, with khawm, together: be, stay or live with someone; tawh marks the companion) (e:Nungzuite tawh sawtpi a ~ uh hi/Amah in a kipatcil-in Pasian tawh a ~ hi | he was with God in the beginning/Pasian in note khempeuh tawh ~ ta hen | may God be with you all/a teeknu tawh amah ~ hi | she lived with her mother-in-law/nangmah tawh ka ~ ngitnget a | I am always with you) (s:ompih/ton) (b:om) (r:44.14.28/19.73.23/43.1.2/45.15.33/8.2.23) (q:draft)
omkhawmin = (t:v) (w:be with/stay with/live with) (d:omkhawm with the linking ending in: being together with someone, tawh marks the companion) (e:tu-in note tawh ~ ka kam pauna/Kha Siangtho in note tawh ~ | the Holy Spirit lives with you/amaute tawh ~ na a semkhawm uh hi | he stayed with them and they worked together/na zite uh tawh ~ | living with your wives) (s:ompihin) (b:omkhawm) (r:48.4.20/43.14.17/44.18.3/60.3.7) (q:draft)
omkhawmna = (t:n) (w:being together/standing together) (d:omkhawm, be together, with the noun suffix na) (e:kiptakin na ~ uh ka theih manin) (b:omkhawm) (r:51.2.5) (q:draft)
omkhawmsak = (t:v) (w:cause to be with/put together with) (d:omkhawm, be together, with sak, cause: make or let someone be in the same place as others) (e:misimtatte tawh a ~ ding hi/ka omna-ah na ~ dingin ka deih hi | I want you to let them be with me where I am) (b:omkhawm) (r:40.24.51/43.17.24) (q:draft)
omkhawmte = (t:n) (w:companions/those who are with) (d:omkhawm, be together, with plural -te: those who are with someone) (e:amah tawh a ~ a lusu uh hi/amah tawh a ~ in ne-in dawnin | those who were with him ate and drank/sawm-le-nihte tawh a kimkot a ~ in | the Twelve and the others around him/keimah tawh a ~ hong vaak | supplied those who were with me) (s:tonpihte/kikholhpihte) (b:omkhawm) (r:42.9.32/44.20.34/1.24.54/41.4.10) (q:draft)
omkhin = (t:v) (w:have already been/already exist) (d:om, be, with khin, already: have been somewhere or in a state up to now, be there already) (e:ni thum bang hong ~ uh a/keima suah ma-in amah ~ ahih manin | because he was before I was born/na theihsa uh thumanah kiptakin na ~ uh | you are already firmly established in the truth you know/Zebah le Zalmunna na khut sungah ~ ahi hiam | are Zebah and Zalmunna already in your hand) (b:om) (r:41.8.2/43.1.30/61.1.12/7.8.6) (q:draft)
omkhit = (t:v) (w:have been/have stayed) (d:om, be or stay, with khit, finished; mostly as omkhit ciangin, after being or staying) (e:kha thum ka ~ uh ciangin/an ne loin sauveipi a ~ uh ciangin | after they had gone a long time without food/leitung pumpi a ~ ciangin | after the natural body has been/amaute lakah kamsang khat a ~ lamtak | that a prophet has been among them) (s:omzawh) (r:44.28.11/46.15.46/44.27.21/26.2.5) (q:draft)
omkhitna = (t:n) (w:having been) (d:omkhit, have been, with the noun suffix na: the fact of having been something for a time) (e:thukhenin sauveipi na ~ thu) (b:omkhit) (r:44.24.10) (q:draft)
omkhol = (t:v) (w:be ready/be prepared) (d:om, be, with khol, beforehand: be in readiness for what is to be done) (e:sihna nangawn thuak dingin ka ~ hi/lam kalah that dingin ka ~ ding uh hi | we will be ready to kill him on the way) (s:kigingkhol/kiging) (r:44.21.13/44.23.15) (q:draft)
omkhong = (t:v) (w:keep still/stay still/be at rest) (d:keep still, be at rest; in the verses always negated with thei lo: cannot keep still, restless) (e:peengkul a kitum ciangin ~ thei lo uh hi/a ~ thei lo leii | the restless tongue/a huaiham mi in kiphasakin ~ thei lo a | the greedy man is arrogant and never at rest/A ~ thei lo, a kihtakhuai Khaldea mite | the restless and dreaded Chaldeans) (s:ommawk) (r:18.39.24/59.3.8/35.2.5/35.1.6) (q:draft)
omkhop = (t:v) (w:be together/stay with/dwell with) (d:form of omkhawm used before loh, ding, theih and nading) (e:amah tawh na ~ tawntung nadingin/kei tawh a ~ theih nadingun | so that they may dwell with me/lupkhop ding hita leh ~ ding hita leh | whether to lie with her or to be with her/biakna innpi sungah note tawh ka ~ lai takin | while I was with you in the temple courts/ka pumpi-in ka hong ~ loh hangin | though I am not with you in body) (s:tenkhop) (r:57.1.15/19.101.6/1.39.10/42.22.53/46.5.3) (q:draft)
omkhopna = (t:n) (w:being together) (d:omkhop, be together, with the noun suffix na) (e:mi nih nangawn a ~ om nawn lo hi) (b:omkhop) (r:9.11.11) (q:draft)
omkik = (t:v) (w:be again/happen again/exist again) (d:om be with kik, again or back: return to an earlier state; with lo, be no more) (e:Tua ciangin gal hong ~ hi/Hamsiatna cikmah hunin ~ lo ding hi | there will never again be any curse/a pasal tawh kilemin ~ hen | let her be reconciled and live with her husband again/A tate uh nidang bang mahin a ~ ding | their children will be again as in former days/a tu dingin puteekte ~ ding a | old people will again be there to sit) (b:om) (r:9.19.8/66.22.3/46.7.11/24.30.20/38.8.4) (q:draft)
omkim = (t:v) (w:be all present/be everywhere) (d:om, be, with kim, complete: all are there, or be present throughout a place) (e:mun khempeuhah a ~ khit theih nadingin/hih lai-ah a ~ mah ahi hiam | are they all here/siampite le mi khempeuh a ~ laitakin | while the priests and all the people were present/Tua gam maitang tung khempeuhah galkikapna ~ hi | the battle spread over the whole countryside) (r:49.4.10/9.16.11/24.28.1/10.18.8) (q:draft)
omlai = (t:v) (w:remain/be left) (d:om, be, with lai, still: still be there, be left; a omlai is the rest, what remains) (e:a ~ mite tawh/A ~ leitang | the land that remains/biakpiakna sa a ~ teng mei tawh kihal ding | any meat of the sacrifice left over must be burned/Jakob amah guak bek ~ a | Jacob alone was left/A nautum pen ~ a | the youngest still remains) (s:kinusialai/vallai) (r:24.39.9/26.9.8/6.13.2/3.7.17/1.32.24/9.16.11) (q:draft)
omlaipi = (t:v) (w:still be there/still remain) (d:omlai, remain, with pi; omlaipi mahin is even while it was still there) (e:kam sungah an a ~ mahin) (b:omlai) (r:19.78.30) (q:draft, low confidence)
omlaisun = (t:adj) (w:remaining/left over) (d:omlai, remain, with sun: still left; a omlaisun teng or a omlaisun khempeuh is all who are still left, the remnant) (e:A ~ teng khatlekhat kisanek un/Israel mi a ~ khempeuh | all the remnant of Israel/Judah gamah a ~ teng | all who were left in Judah) (s:laisun/nusiatlai) (r:38.11.9/26.9.8/24.43.5) (q:draft)
omlaite = (t:n) (w:the rest/remnant/those remaining) (d:omlai, remain, with plural te: the people or things that are left; in Kings, the remaining acts of a reign) (e:Jakob innkuan a ~ a vanglian Pasian/Amaziah’ nasepna a ~ | the other events of Amaziah’s reign/ama mi a ~ a dingin | for the remnant of his people/Ai khuami a ~ namsau tawh a vatgawp uh | they struck down with the sword the people of Ai who were left) (s:laisunte/sunte/suaktate) (b:omlai) (r:23.10.21/12.16.19/12.14.18/23.28.5/6.8.24) (q:draft)
omlaiteng = (t:n) (w:the rest/remainder/all that remain) (d:omlai, remain, with teng, all: everyone or everything that is still left) (e:mi a ~ kaikhawm inla/Edom gam a ~ | the remnant of Edom/mun a ~ khempeuh | all the remaining land/Nisuahna lam mi galkap khempeuh sung pan a ~ | all that were left of the armies of the eastern peoples) (s:valteng/omlaite/laiteng) (b:omlai) (r:10.12.28/26.48.18/30.9.12/26.45.8/7.8.10) (q:draft)
omlaiteng = (t:conj) (w:as long as) (d:after a noun and a, for as long as that thing still exists) (e:Ni le kha a ~, khang tawntungin/ka sungah nuntakna a ~ | as long as there is life in me/vanpi a ~ | as long as the heavens exist/ka omna-ah migilote a ~ | as long as the wicked are in my presence) (s:laiteng) (b:omlai) (r:19.72.5/18.14.12/18.27.3/19.39.1) (q:draft)
omlam = (t:det) (w:that) (d:om, be, with lam: the fact that someone or something is there; follows a clause and stands before a verb of knowing, seeing or hearing) (e:kei ~ theilo maw?/Kha Siangtho a ~ nangawn ka za nai kei | we have not even heard that there is a Holy Spirit/a guaktangin a ~ uh kithei uh hi | they realized that they were naked/mi tampi tak a hong ~ a theih ciangin | when he saw that a great crowd was around him/khangno mi khat a ~ ka phawk hi | I noticed that there was a youth) (r:21.4.15/43.9.32/44.19.2/1.3.7/40.8.18)
omlo = (t:adj) (w:without/lacking) (d:om, be, with lo, not: where something is not present, as mi omlo, without people, and silngo-omlo, without yeast, unleavened) (e:na inn uh mi ~ gam simthamin kinusia/Silngo-~ Anlum pawikham hun ahi hi | it was the time of the Festival of Unleavened Bread) (b:om) (r:40.23.38/44.12.3) (q:draft)
omlohna = (t:n) (w:absence/lack/not being) (d:om, be, with loh, not, and the noun suffix na: the fact that there is none) (e:bangmah phattuamna a ~ ka phawk hi) (r:21.2.11) (q:draft)
omlopi = (t:see) <omlopi-a>
omlopi-a = (t:adv) (w:without cause/without reason) (d:om, be, with lo, not; thu omlopi-a is when there is no matter, for no reason) (e:Thu ~ kei hong mudah mi) (s:mawkin) (r:19.69.4) (q:draft)
ommah = (t:v) (w:indeed be/be just so) (d:om, be, with mah for emphasis: a ommah ding is there must indeed be, a ommah bangin is just as one was) (e:kikhenna a ~ ding ahi hi/a guaktangin a ~ bangin | naked, just as she was) (b:om) (r:46.11.19/28.2.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
ommawk = (t:v) (w:be idle/do nothing/stay still/delay) (d:remain without acting or speaking; ommawk kei in warns not to neglect or put off a duty) (e:gen ding thei nawn loin ~ uh hi/na sep ding don loin ~ kei in | do not neglect what you have to do/na ciamna uh tungsak loin na ~ kei ding | do not be slow to fulfil your vow/dai dide-in ~ kei in | do not remain silent/Leii in a ~ thei lo | the tongue cannot stay still) (s:omcip) (r:18.32.16/15.4.22/5.23.21/19.109.1/59.3.8) (q:draft)
ommawkna = (t:n) (w:idleness/sitting idle/inaction) (d:ommawk, be idle, with the noun suffix na; khutzepin ommawkna is sitting idle with folded hands) (e:khutzepin ~ hangin/lungkia-in a ~ ding | that they are left dismayed, doing nothing) (s:tutmawkna/thadahna) (a:thanuamna) (b:ommawk) (r:20.24.33/23.37.26) (q:draft)
ommuang = (t:adj) (w:harmless/unsuspecting) (d:of a person or animal that is quietly minding its own business and expects no harm) (e:ui ~ khat a bil-a kaihsak/Mi ~ khat va muan suam ni | let us ambush some harmless person) (r:20.26.17/20.1.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
ommun = (t:v) (w:be frequent/be often) (d:om, be, with mun, often; ommun lo is be rare) (e:maangmuh ~ lo hi) (r:9.3.1) (q:draft, low confidence)
omna = (t:v) (w:locate/find) (d:om, be, with the noun suffix na: the place where someone or something is; omna peuhah is wherever there is, and omna panin is from the presence of) (e:Sapul ~ peuhah musanete hong kikhawm/Faro’ ~ panin paikhia hi | he went out from Pharaoh’s presence/Ka ~ mun nong tung zo kei ding | you will not be able to come to the place where I am/Israel mite a ~ Goshen gam bekah | only in the land of Goshen, where the Israelites were/kham a ~, Havilah gambup | the whole land of Havilah, where there is gold) (b:om) (r:40.24.28/1.2.11/1.47.10/43.7.34/2.9.26) where there is
Omna = (t:n) (w:dwelling place/place where one is) (d:omna written with a capital: the place where someone is or sits; note’ omna peuhah is wherever you are) (e:Note’ ~ peuhah Kuamah lungmuang thei lo/~ pha hih lai-ah na tu in | sit here in a good place) (b:omna) (r:23.59.8/59.2.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
omnai = (t:v) (w:be yet/exist so far) (d:om, be, with nai, yet; in a question: is there any so far) (e:na theih uh ~ ahi hiam) (r:43.7.48) (q:draft, low confidence)
omnasa = (t:n) (w:former place/former site) (d:om, be, with na and sa, already: the place where someone or something was before; often followed by mun, place) (e:a puanbuk ~ mun Bethel le Ai/kumpipa’ inn zong a ~ mahah omkik ding hi | the palace will stand again in its former place/ama ~ kherubte tung panin | from above the cherubim, where it had been/Israel mite a ~ mun mahah ka omsakkik ding | I will bring Israel back to their former place) (b:om) (r:1.13.3/24.30.18/26.9.3/24.50.19) (q:draft)
omnate = (t:n) (w:standing firm/endurance) (d:om, be or remain, with the noun suffix na and plural te; kiptakin omnate is remaining steadfast) (e:kiptakin na ~ uh ka phawk tawntung) (b:om) (r:52.1.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
omnawn = (t:v) (w:be any more/still be) (d:om, be, with nawn, any more or further) (e:bang thudang ~ ahi hiam) (b:om) (r:1.23.15) (q:draft)
omngei = (t:v) (w:have been/once was/used to be) (d:om, be, with ngei, ever or once: have existed or been present at an earlier time; a omngei bangin is as it was before, omngei nai lo is has never been) (e:Nidangin ~ a, ahi zongin tu-in/amaute lakah kamsang khat ~ ahihlam | that a prophet has been among them/khuamial sungah a ~ hinapi-in | though you were once in darkness/kamsang man lo a ~ mah bangin | just as there were false prophets/hih bang zinling ~ nai lo hi | there has never been such an earthquake) (r:66.17.11/26.33.33/49.5.8/61.2.1/66.16.18) (q:draft)
omnop = (t:v) (w:want to be/wish to live) (d:om, be, with nop, form of nuam, want) (e:Ukna thu a neite kihta loin na ~ uhleh) (r:45.13.3) (q:draft)
omnopna = (t:n) (w:longing to be/desire to be) (d:omnop, want to be, with the noun suffix na) (e:ka ~ uh lianlua mahmah ahih manin) (b:omnop) (r:47.5.2) (q:draft)
omnuam = (t:v) (w:want to be/want to stay) (d:om, be, with nuam, want) (e:Thukham nuai-ah a ~ mite aw) (r:48.4.21) (q:draft)
omnuam = (t:adj) (w:pleasant/agreeable) (d:om, be, with nuam, pleasant: of a person who is pleasant to be with; the English has fine-looking) (e:a ~ mi khat ka mu a) (r:9.16.18) (q:draft, low confidence)
omom = (t:v) (w:keep on being/still remain/go on) (d:doubled form of om, be, for a state that continues, often followed by lai, still) (e:a nu sung mahah ~ lai hi/Na gen ding uh ~ lai ahi hiam | do you still have more to say/na khempeuh a kibang mahin ~ lai hi | everything still goes on just the same/lungdamin ~ lai ding ahi uh hiam | will they go on being jubilant/Hih bangin ~ sak lehang | if we let him go on like this) (r:28.13.13/19.94.3/18.16.3/61.3.4/43.11.48) (q:draft)
omomin = (t:v) (w:as still being/being there still) (d:omom, go on being, with in; a omomin ngaihsun is think that he is still there) (e:honlak mahah a ~ ngaihsun uh) (b:omom) (r:42.2.44) (q:draft)
ompa = (t:n) (w:he who is/the one who is) (d:om be, with pa marking a man: the one who is in a place or with someone) (e:Vantung-a a ~ aw/Na tapa David, tuute tawh a ~ | your son David, who is with the sheep/eite tawh a ~ lianzaw hi | the one who is with us is greater) (b:om) (r:19.123.1/9.16.19/14.32.7) (q:draft)
ompah = (t:v) (w:be at once/stay right away) (d:om, be, with pah, at once; pau loin ompah is fall silent at once) (e:pau loin ka ~ ding hi) (r:18.6.24) (q:draft)
ompak = (t:v) (w:stay for a while/lodge/sojourn) (d:om, be, with pak, for a short while) (e:ama inn sunga ~ mite’ kiang panin) (s:taam/peem) (r:2.3.22) (q:draft)
ompakna = (t:n) (w:sojourn/temporary stay) (d:ompak, stay for a while, with the noun suffix na; ompakna gam is the land where one is living for a time) (e:a ~ uh gam panin ka lakhia ding) (s:tenpakna) (b:ompak) (r:26.20.38) (q:draft)
ompi = (t:v) (w:be there/be present) (d:om, be, with pi; in a ompi mahin, even though they were there; what pi adds is not clear) (e:Khaldea mite khuapi kiimah a ~ mahin) (b:om) (r:12.25.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
ompih = (t:v) (w:be with/stay with/accompany) (d:om, be, with pih, together with: be with someone and stand by him, said above all of God; the person is the object) (e:Vanglian Pasian in kei hong ~ a/Topa in amah ~ hi | the Lord was with him/note bang tanvei hong ~ ding | how long shall I stay with you/ka lungsim in note hong ~ lai ahih manin | because my Spirit is still with you) (s:omkhawm/ton) (b:om) (r:18.29.5/10.5.10/9.18.14/41.9.19/37.2.5) (q:draft)
ompihin = (t:v) (w:be with/stand by/accompany) (d:ompih with the linking ending in: being with someone to help and support) (e:kamsangte in amaute ~ huh uh hi/Topa in Josef ~ | the Lord was with Joseph/nang hong ~ na paina peuhah kong kem ding | I am with you and will keep you wherever you go/a tupa in amaute ~ a hu ding hi | he who sits there will be with them and shelter them) (s:omkhawmin) (b:ompih) (r:15.5.2/1.39.21/1.28.15/66.7.15) (q:draft)
ompihlai = (t:v) (w:still be with/remain with) (d:ompih, be with, with lai, still) (e:note hong ~ ka hih manin) (r:37.2.5) (q:draft)
ompihna = (t:n) (w:presence/being with) (d:ompih, be with, with the noun suffix na: someone’s being with a person, especially the presence of God) (e:ama ~ zong den un/nangma ~ lungdamna tawh | with the joy of your presence/Ama ~ vantungmi in amaute honkhia hi | the angel of his presence saved them/Topa in David a ~ | that the Lord was with David) (b:ompih) (r:13.16.11/19.21.6/23.63.9/9.18.28) (q:draft)
Ompihna = (t:n) (w:presence) (d:ompihna written with a capital in Ompihna Anlum, the bread of the Presence that is set before God) (e:~ Anlum adingin sabuai kham/~ Anlum na koih tawntung ding hi | you shall always set out the bread of the Presence/sabuai leh a nazat khempeuhte leh ~ Anlum | the table with all its articles and the bread of the Presence) (r:13.28.16/2.25.30/2.39.36) (q:draft)
Omri = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Omri) (d:king of Israel who built Samaria, father of Ahab; also the name of three other men) (r:11.16.30/11.16.25)
omsa = (t:adj) (w:existing/already there/established) (d:om, be, with sa, already: that which already is or was there before; thu omsa bangin is according to the word already given, ngeina kip omsa is the established rule) (e:na thu ~ bangin kei hong hingsak in/ngeina kip ~ bangin pia hi | he offered it in the prescribed way/a ~ ki thumte a bot khia hi | it uprooted three of the horns that were already there/a ~ vive ahi hi | it is all something that was already there) (a:thak) (b:om) (r:19.119.25/3.9.16/27.7.8/21.1.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
omsak = (t:v) (w:put) (d:om, be, with sak, cause: cause to be somewhere, put) (e:kikalah kilangneihna ka ~ ding hi/a sisante tua ci-in ka ~ hi | I put her blood there/giahphual pua-ah na ~ ding hi | you shall put them outside the camp/Egypt leitang tungah uiphukte ~ uh hi | they brought frogs upon the land of Egypt) (s:koih) (b:om) (r:1.3.15/26.24.8/4.5.3/2.8.7)
omsak = (t:v) (w:place) (d:set or keep someone or something in a place, let remain there) (e:bek-ah ka ~ hi/Puanbuk kimkotah amaute ~ hi | he stationed them around the tent/ama kiangah David ~ a | he kept David with him/meivakte a ngeina bangin Topa’ mai-ah ~ tawntung ding | he shall keep the lamps before the Lord continually) (s:koih) (b:om) (r:18.38.10/4.11.24/9.18.2/3.24.4)
omsakin = (t:v) (w:putting/placing/causing to be) (d:omsak, cause to be, with the linking suffix in) (e:a vante uh ~, amaute paikhia uh hi/a suakta pawlkhat hong ~ | leaving us a remnant/Na kimkot-ah amaute ~ | placing them all around you/nidanga a ngei bangin ~ ka hausakkik ding hi | making it as it was before, I will restore its fortunes) (b:omsak) (r:7.18.21/15.9.8/26.16.37/24.49.39) (q:draft)
omsakkik = (t:v) (w:restore/reestablish/bring back) (d:omsak with kik, again: cause to be as before, put back in its place; ki-omsakkik is the passive) (e:amaute a gam uhah ka ~ ciangin/a nidanga a om ngei bangun ka ~ ding | I will make them as they were before/amaute a gam mah uhah ka ~ ding hi | I will bring them back to their own land/Topa’ biakinn sungah nasepna ki-~ hi | the service of the temple of the Lord was reestablished) (s:koihkik) (b:omsak) (r:24.31.23/24.33.7/24.32.44/14.29.35) (q:draft)
omsaklai = (t:v) (w:let remain/leave alone still) (d:omsak, let be, with lai, still: leave a thing as it is for a while longer) (e:hih bangmahin ~ phot in) (r:42.13.8) (q:draft)
omsakzo = (t:v) (w:be able to keep/establish) (d:omsak, make be, with zo, be able; nuamtakin omsakzo is keep in peace) (e:kumpi gam, nuamtakin a ~ hi) (b:omsak) (r:18.25.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
omsate = (t:n) (w:existing ones/earlier ones/those already there) (d:omsa already existing, with the plural te; after a noun it describes it, as pawlpi omsate, the churches already there) (e:amah in a ~ tawh a kilamdang mahmahin/pawlpi ~ kipsakin | strengthening the churches already there/ka tuu ~ tawh honkhat suakkhawm ding uh hi | they will become one flock with the sheep I already have) (b:omsa) (r:27.7.24/44.15.41/43.10.16) (q:draft)
omsawm = (t:v) (w:intend to stay/plan to be) (d:om, be or stay, with sawm, intend) (e:phalbi sung ~ ka hih manin) (r:56.3.12) (q:draft)
omsuak = (t:v) (w:remain/continue/stay on) (d:om, be, with suak, onward: go on being in the same place or state, stay on) (e:Singkuang’ kualte sungah a zawlte ~ ding a/mi khempeuh in Pasian’ adingin ~ ta uh hen | let everyone remain so before God/na zintunna inn mah uhah ~ unla | stay in the house where you lodge/Hih gamah note na ~ uhleh | if you stay in this land/A thuman lo mi in thuman loin ~ hen | let the one who does wrong go on doing wrong) (s:omden) (r:2.25.15/46.7.24/42.10.7/24.42.10/66.22.11) (q:draft)
omsuakin = (t:v) (w:remaining/staying on) (d:omsuak, remain, with in linking it to what follows) (e:ama gam mahah Judah ~/myrrh paknamtui a omna mualtungah ~ | staying on the mountain of myrrh) (b:omsuak) (r:6.18.5/22.4.6) (q:draft)
omsuakna = (t:n) (w:staying on/remaining) (d:omsuak, stay on, with the noun suffix na) (e:Judah gamah ~ ding Topa’ thugenna) (b:omsuak) (r:24.43.4) (q:draft)
omsuakte = (t:n) (w:those who remain/survivors) (d:omsuak, stay on, with plural te) (e:tua gam a ~ in haksatna lianpi) (s:omlaite/sunte) (b:omsuak) (r:16.1.3) (q:draft)
omsung = (t:n) (w:stay/time of staying) (d:om, be, with sung, within or during: the time while someone is in a place; ka omsung khempeuh is all the time I was there) (e:amaute tawh ka ~ khempeuh uh/ka pate tawlkhat a ~ uh | the time my fathers lived as sojourners) (r:9.25.16/1.47.9) (q:draft)
omta = (t:v) (w:be/exist/have come) (d:om be with ta, which marks a state that now holds: now is, has come to be; koi-ah omta ahi hiam asks where something is now) (e:paikhiatpih Topa koi-ah ~ ahi hiam/a taktak ahi Khrih hong ~ hi | the reality, Christ, has come/midangte a khem tampi hong ~ a | many deceivers have now appeared/Amah koi-ah ~ ahi hiam | where is he now) (b:om) (r:23.63.11/51.2.17/63.1.7/18.20.7) (q:draft)
omte = (t:v) (w:be) (d:om, be, with plural te: those who are in a place or state; a omte is the ones who are) (e:Judah gamah a ~ in mual tungah/Tui sunga a ~ sung panin | of all those living in the water/khuamial sungah a ~ khuavaksak mi | a light for those who are in the dark/ka mai lamah a ~ zamin | straining toward what is ahead/ka kim uh-a ~’ nuihsat | the scorn of those around us) (b:om) (r:40.24.16/3.11.12/45.2.19/50.3.13/19.44.13)
omte = (t:v) (w:have) (b:om)
omte = (t:part) (d:particle used in making a comparison) (e:sunga ~ khempeuh/amah tawh a ~ sangin | than those who are with him) (r:1.2.1/14.32.7)
omteng = (t:n) (w:all that is/everything in/all who are) (d:om, be, with teng, all: all that there is in a place, all who are there) (e:a gam sunga ~ ka suksiat ciangin/amah tawh teembaw sunga a ~ bek a suakta | only those with him in the ark survived/a khuapi le a sunga a ~ | the city and everything in it/laizial sunga thu ~ khempeuh atkik in | write again all the words that were on the scroll) (b:om) (r:26.32.15/1.7.23/30.6.8/24.36.28) (q:draft)
omthei = (t:v) (w:can be/be able to remain) (d:om, be, with thei, can: can be, be able to stay as it is) (e:a nawkgawp hangin nuamtakin ~ veve hi/a omngei bangin ~ nawn lo ding hi | they will no longer be able to stay as they were/na khempeuh ama mun sansanah hoihtakin a ~ hi | all things hold together, each in its place/ama mai-ah lungmuang takin a ~ ding | that we can be at rest before him/Eite nuamtakin ~-in | so that we can live in peace) (b:om) (r:18.40.23/41.13.25/51.1.17/62.3.19/54.2.2) (q:draft)
omtheih = (t:v) (w:be able to be/may be) (d:form of omthei, can be, used before nading; a omtheih nadingin is so that it may be) (e:lungmuang takin i ~ nading/Ka nasemte keima omna-ah a ~ nadingin | so that my servants may be where I am/kiptakin na ~ nadingun | that you may stand firm/siangtho-in i ~ nadingin | so that we may be holy/phattuamna a ~ nadingin | so that there may be benefit) (b:om) (r:62.2.28/43.12.26/51.4.12/58.12.10/46.12.7) (q:draft)
omto = (t:v) (w:be up above/rise above/stay on) (d:om, be, with to, up or onward; be high above a thing, and of time, go on being in a place) (e:Mual liante tungah tui ~ lai a/kumpi inn-ah Daniel ~ paisuak hi | Daniel stayed on at the royal court/Meiite bangzah takin sang ~ ahi hiam | how high above are the clouds/inndei neute sungah kahlei ~ a | a stairway went up in the side rooms) (b:om) (r:1.7.20/27.1.21/18.35.5/26.41.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
omtoh = (t:v) (w:come up onto/be up on) (d:form of omto, be up on, used before ciangin, when) (e:lei keu tungah hong ~ ciangin) (b:omto) (r:6.4.18) (q:draft, low confidence)
omtual = (t:v) (w:stay/dwell/keep to) (d:om, be, with tual; in the verse the wise keep among mourning and fools among pleasure) (e:Mipilte dahna lakah ~ a) (r:21.7.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
omtuam = (t:v) (w:be separate/be set apart) (d:om, be, with tuam, separate; hun omtuam lo is there is no separate time) (e:a kiseh hun ~ lo hi) (r:18.34.23) (q:draft, low confidence)
omvat = (t:v) (w:appear suddenly/be there all at once) (d:om, be, with vat, suddenly) (e:Moses le Elijah hong ~ uh a/mihing nih tawh a kiho-in hong ~ hi | two men suddenly appeared, talking with him) (s:dingvat) (r:40.17.3/42.9.30) (q:draft)
omzah = (t:n) (w:number/amount/quantity) (d:om, be, with zah, amount: how many or how much there is of something) (e:tuipi gei-a sehnel ~ bang ahi hi/Tuipi a sehnel ~ sangin | more than the amount of sand of the sea/puanbuk sung uhah mi ~ tawh kituakin | according to the number of people in your tent/mite tu-a a ~ za khatin | a hundred times the present number of people) (s:malzah/phazah) (r:7.7.12/2.16.16/24.15.8/10.24.3) (q:draft)
omzaw = (t:v) (w:be rather/be instead) (d:om, be or live, with zaw, rather: be or live in one way instead of another) (e:Kha Siangtho tawh a kidimin ~ un/amau’ thuthu-in a ~ uh a | instead they went their own way/matin ~ ding uh hi | they will be seized instead) (s:hizaw) (b:om) (r:49.5.18/24.7.24/24.30.16) (q:draft)
omzaw = (t:v) (w:be more) (d:there is more of something, used with sangin than) (e:mihaite a dingin lametna ~ lai hi/mihai pa a dingin lametna ~ lai hi | there is more hope for a fool/Eleazar’ suante lakah ukpi tam ~ ahih manin | because there were more leaders among the descendants of Eleazar) (b:om) (r:20.26.12/13.24.4/20.29.20) (q:draft)
omzawh = (t:v) (w:have been/have stayed) (d:om, be or stay, with zawh, completed: the time that one has spent in a state, followed by a count of days or years) (e:thong sungah a ~ kum sawmthum/Salin ka ~ uh a kum sawm le nih | the twelfth year that we had been in exile/lungkhamin na ~ uh tu-in ni sawm le li | you have now been in suspense fourteen days) (s:omkhit) (r:12.25.27/26.33.21/44.27.33) (q:draft)
omzia = (t:n) (w:condition/state/ways/way of life/welfare) (d:how a person is or lives, both his circumstances and his conduct; omzia dong, ask how someone is, means greet) (e:Tu laitak-a na ~ uh lim takin ngaihsun/ama ~ dong uh hi | they asked how he was/amaute’ ~ lunghimawh hi | he was concerned about their condition/a ~ khempeuh, a patna panin a tawpna dong | all his ways from beginning to end) (s:nuntakzia/omdan) (r:37.1.5/7.18.15/2.2.25/14.28.26) (q:draft)
omziate = (t:n) (w:ways/conditions/features) (d:omzia, how a person or thing is, with the plural te; of a person, his ways, and of a land, what it is like) (e:a leitang ~ hong gelhin/leh a galsimnate, leh a ~ | and his wars and his ways) (b:omzia) (r:6.18.4/14.27.7) (q:draft)
omzo = (t:v) (w:be able to stand/be able to be/be able to remain) (d:om, be or stay, with zo, be able: be able to be, remain or stand in a certain state or place) (e:Topa’ mai-ah kua ~ ding ahi hiam/Lungkip takin ka ~ hi | I am able to stand firm/mi khatpeuh paubaang loin ~ ngei ding ahi hiam | can anyone ever be blameless/sitbaang loin ~ ngei ding ahi hiam | can he ever be without fault) (s:omtheih) (b:om) (r:9.6.20/18.4.17/46.10.12) (q:draft)
omzote = (t:n) (w:those who are able to live so) (d:omzo, be able to be or remain, with plural te: those who can live in that way) (e:Geh bangin a ~ om ta hen) (b:omzo) (r:40.19.12) (q:draft)
On = (t:name) (c:city) (w:On) (d:city in Egypt, also called Heliopolis, whose priest Potiphera was the father-in-law of Joseph) (e:~ khua siampipa Potifera’ tanu Asenath) (r:1.41.50/26.30.17) (q:draft)
On = (t:name) (c:male) (w:On) (d:son of Peleth of the tribe of Reuben, who joined the revolt of Korah) (r:4.16.1) (q:draft)
Onam = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Onam) (d:name of two men: a son of Shobal the Horite, and a son of Jerahmeel of the tribe of Judah) (r:1.36.23/13.2.26)
Onan = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Onan) (d:second son of Judah, who died in Canaan) (r:1.38.4/4.26.19)
Onesiforas = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Onesiphorus) (d:Christian whose household Paul greets, who often refreshed Paul and was not ashamed of his chains) (r:55.1.16/55.4.19)
Onesimas = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Onesimus) (d:slave of Philemon who became a believer through Paul and was sent back to his master) (r:57.1.10)
onik = (t:n) (c:stone) (w:onyx) (d:a precious stone, usually in the phrase onik suang, onyx stone, set on the ephod and breastpiece of the priest) (e:~ suang/~ suang nih la-in | take two onyx stones/leh ~ suang om hi | and onyx stone is there/beril suang, ~ suang leh jasper suang | beryl, onyx and jasper) (r:1.2.12/2.25.7/2.28.9/2.39.13)
Onik = (t:n) (c:stone) (w:onyx) (d:onik, onyx, written with a capital in a list of precious stones) (e:Beril, leh ~, Safeiros, Karbankel) (b:onik) (r:26.28.13) (q:draft)
onikh = (t:n) (w:onycha) (d:a fragrant substance, one of the ingredients of the holy incense) (e:stakte, ~ leh galbanum) (s:onikha) (r:2.30.34) (q:draft)
onikha = (t:n) (w:onycha) (d:a fragrant substance, one of the ingredients of the holy incense; spelling of onikh in the older text) (e:stakte, ~, le galbanum) (s:onikh) (r:2.30.34) (q:draft)
Ono = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Ono) (d:town in the territory of Benjamin near Lod, with a plain named after it) (e:leh ~ khuami za sagih) (r:16.7.37/16.11.35) (q:draft)
op = (t:v) (w:brood/sit on eggs/hatch) (d:of a bird: sit on eggs or cover the young to keep them warm) (e:a ~ sim vasa tawh kibang hi/a ~ ahi zongin na muh khak zenzen leh | or if you happen to see her sitting on them) (s:keuh) (r:24.17.11/5.22.6) (q:draft)
op = (t:n) (w:deposit/scum/rust) (d:only in kang-op, the burnt crust stuck inside a cooking pot) (e:a kang-~ nin teng kangtumin/a kang-~ in bun lua ahih manin | because its deposit is too heavy/a kang-~ a kinawtkhia ngei lo beel | a pot whose deposit has never been scoured off) (r:26.24.11/26.24.12/26.24.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
opa = (t:todo) (q:draft, not a word of its own, the rest of Topa where the 1932 text prints T opa with a space)
OPA = (t:n) (w:Lord) (d:part of TOPA, the Lord, printed in the text as T OPA with a space) (r:2.3.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
opsim = (t:v) (w:brood/sit on eggs) (d:said of a bird that sits on eggs to hatch them; in the verse, eggs that are not its own) (e:a ~ vasa tawh kibang hi) (s:op) (r:24.17.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
Oreb = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Oreb) (d:a Midianite leader killed in the time of Gideon) (e:uliante ~ leh Ze-eb hong pia zo hi) (r:7.8.3/7.7.25) (q:draft)
Oreb = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Oreb) (d:the rock of Oreb, Oreb suangpi, where the Midianite leader Oreb was killed) (e:~ suangpi-ah Midian mite a sukgawp bangin) (r:23.10.26/7.7.25) (q:draft)
Oren = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Oren) (d:son of Jerahmeel of the tribe of Judah) (r:13.2.25)
Ornan = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Araunah) (d:the Jebusite whose threshing floor David bought as the site for the altar, called Araunah in the NIV) (r:13.21.25/13.21.15)
Orpah = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Orpah) (d:Moabite woman, daughter-in-law of Naomi, who went back to her own people) (r:8.1.4/8.1.14)
ot = (t:v) (w:shout/cry out/call aloud) (d:shout or call out loudly, in battle, in joy or in prayer) (e:galdo kikona a ~ lai takun/kong ~’ ciangin hong za in la | hear me when I call/ci-in a ~ ngeii-ngai lai takin | while they shout loudly) (s:awng/kiko) (a:daih) (r:9.17.20/19.27.7/38.4.7) (q:draft)
Othiel = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Othniel) (d:spelling of Othniel in 1 Chronicles 4.13: son of Kenaz) (r:13.4.13)
Othni = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Othni) (d:son of Shemaiah, a Levite gatekeeper of the family of Obed-Edom) (r:13.26.7) (q:draft)
Othniel = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Othniel) (d:son of Kenaz and kinsman of Caleb, who took Kiriath Sepher and became the first judge of Israel) (r:6.15.17/7.1.13)
otkhai = (t:see) <otkhai-in>
otkhai-in = (t:v) (w:shouting after/shouting at) (d:ot, shout, with khai and the linking in; of people who shout as they chase a thief away; what khai adds is not clear) (e:Gutate ~ a kidelh bangin) (r:18.30.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
otna = (t:n) (w:shout/shouting/roar) (d:noun from ot shout; a loud cry of many people, in joy or in uproar) (e:~ leh saki tumna awging tawh/lungdam ~ awging | the sound of a shout of joy/minamte’ ~, tui lianpi ging bang | the roar of the peoples, like the roar of great waters/ka ~ aw hong ngai in | listen to my cry) (s:kikona/awtna) (b:ot) (r:10.6.15/18.3.7/23.17.12/19.17.1) (q:draft)
otsan = (t:v) (w:shout to/call out to/shout after) (d:ot, shout, with san, toward: shout to or after a person) (e:vantungmi in kei hong ~ a/Amaute in Dan mite ~ uh a | they shouted after the Danites) (b:ot) (r:38.6.8/7.18.23) (q:draft)
otsanin = (t:v) (w:shouting to/calling out to) (d:otsan, shout to, with in linking it to the words that are shouted) (e:Amah dingin Israel uliante ~) (b:otsan) (r:9.17.8) (q:draft)
Ozem = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ozem) (d:name of two men: the sixth son of Jesse, and a son of Jerahmeel) (r:13.2.15/13.2.25)
Ozni = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ozni) (d:son of Gad, ancestor of the Oznite clan) (r:4.26.16)
pa = (t:n) (w:father) (d:male parent; with a possessive, as in ka pa, my father, and a pa, his father) (e:a nu leh a ~ nusia-in/Salmon in Boaz’ ~ | Salmon was the father of Boaz/Ta pilte in a ~ lungdam sak a | wise children make their father glad/a ~ leh a sanggamte' kiangah a gen ciangin | when he told his father and his brothers) (a:nu) (r:1.2.24/8.4.21/20.15.20/1.37.10)
pa = (t:n) (w:man) (d:a man or male person, mostly after tua or hih: tua pa, that man, hih pa, this man) (e:tua ~ in khua mu thei a/Tua ~ hong paipih un | bring that man here/tua ~ in a puante sawp ding a | that man shall wash his clothes/tua ~ in ama mawhna pua ding hi | that man shall bear his sin) (s:mipa/pasal) (a:nu) (r:40.12.22/42.18.40/3.15.8/3.20.17)
pa = (t:n) (w:male) (d:male, said mostly of animals for sacrifice; a pa khat is one male) (e:a sitbang lo keel ~ khat paipih ding/biak nadingin keel a ~ khat | one male goat for the offering/Siampipa in tuuno a ~ khat la-in | the priest shall take one male lamb/tuuno a ~ nih na pia ding uh hi | you shall offer two male lambs) (a:nu/pi) (r:3.4.23/1.7.3/4.7.16/3.14.12/3.23.19)
pa = (t:n) (w:masculine) (d:marks the masculine gender, in contrast to nu, feminine) (a:nu)
Pa = (t:n) (w:Father) (d:God the Father, written with a capital) (e:ka ~ tawh pumkhat ka hi uh hi/ka ~ zong a mudah hi | he hates my Father also/Ta a nial mi in ~ a nei kei hi | whoever denies the Son does not have the Father/A hi mah hi, ka ~ aw | yes, my Father) (b:pa) (r:43.10.30/43.15.23/62.2.23/40.11.26) (q:draft)
Pa = (t:n) (w:One) (d:the male one, in titles of God such as Siangtho Pa the Holy One) (e:Israelte’ Siangtho ~ ahi hi/nang Siangtho ~ na hi a | you are the Holy One/Israelte’ Siangtho ~ phin uh hi | they provoked the Holy One of Israel) (b:pa) (r:23.47.4/19.22.3/19.78.41) (q:draft, low confidence)
PA = (t:n) (w:man) (d:pa, man or male person, written in capitals in the inscription on the cross; hih pa is this man) (e:HIH ~ IN JUDAHTE’ KUMPIPA ZEISU HI) (r:40.27.37) (q:draft)
Pa-arai = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Paarai) (d:Paarai the Arbite, one of the mighty warriors of David) (r:10.23.35) (q:draft)
paai = (t:v) (w:throw/cast/throw away) (d:throw, cast or throw away; nuntakna paai is lay down the life) (e:Eufrates gun sungah ~ in/Vok mai-ah suangmanphate na ~ kei un | do not throw your pearls before pigs/tui sungah ngen ~ a om uh a mu hi | he saw them casting a net into the water/sat tan inla, ~ in | cut it off and throw it away) (s:lawn/paii/lot) (r:24.51.63/43.10.11/40.7.6/41.1.16/40.5.30) (q:draft)
paai = (t:n) (w:sheath/scabbard) (d:the case that holds the blade of a sword) (e:a ~ panin dok a/namsau a ~ panin dokin | drawing the sword from its sheath/Na ~ sungah lut kik in la | go back into your sheath/Na namsau a ~ sungah siat kik in | put your sword back in its sheath) (r:9.17.51/3.26.33/24.47.6/40.26.52) (q:draft)
paai = (t:v) (w:be pregnant/carry) (d:carry a child in the womb, in the phrase nau paai) (e:Nau ka ~ hi/nau na ~ a, tapa khat na nei ding hi | you are pregnant and will have a son/ka nu in hong ~ lai-a kipan | from the time my mother carried me/nau ~-in suak dektak hi | she was pregnant and about to give birth) (s:naupaai/paii) (r:10.11.5/1.16.11/19.22.10/9.4.19) (q:draft)
paaikhia = (t:v) (w:throw away/cast out/reject/remove) (d:paai, throw, with khia, out: throw out or away, and so reject people or remove what is not wanted) (e:ama mite a ~ kei hi/vante tui sungah a ~ uh hi | they threw the cargo into the water/Nangma omna panin kei hong ~ kei inla | do not cast me from your presence/Ngun a ek teng ~ lehang | if we remove the dross from the silver) (s:paihkhiat/lawnkhia) (b:paai) (r:45.11.2/44.27.19/44.27.18/19.51.11/20.25.4) (q:draft)
paaikhiasak = (t:v) (w:take out for/remove for) (d:paaikhia, throw out or remove, with sak, do it for another; hong paaikhiasak in is let me take it out for you) (e:a om ninneng tang hong ~ in) (b:paaikhia) (r:40.7.4/42.6.42) (q:draft)
paaimang = (t:v) (w:throw away/cast off/abandon) (d:paai, throw, with mang, away or lost: throw away for good, abandon or do away with) (e:ka luahsa mite ka ~ ta hi/na sam uh ~ un | throw away your hair/eite kikal sung pan a ~ hi | he took it away from among us/Lungpil a neite a lungpilna ka ~ ding hi | I will do away with the intelligence of the intelligent) (s:paaikhia/paihkhiat) (r:24.12.7/24.7.29/51.2.14/46.1.19) (q:draft)
paaipaai = (t:v) (w:keep throwing/throw again and again) (d:paai, throw, doubled for repeated action) (e:meikhuk sungah a ~ hi) (r:24.36.23) (q:draft)
paaite = (t:n) (w:riches/possessions/goods) (d:with sum, money, the two together mean wealth) (e:Na sum na ~ uh muat gawpin) (r:59.5.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
paak = (t:n) (w:flower/blossom) (d:the flower of a plant, often as a picture of what soon fades) (e:Sharon gam sunga om gamlak ~/Lopa vul a, ~ pulh hi | the grass withers and the flower falls/leenggah ~ gim namtui zong kiza ta hi | the fragrance of the vine blossom is in the air/lopa ~ bangin mangthang hi | he passes away like a flower of the grass) (s:pak/pakpalh) (r:22.2.1/23.40.8/22.2.13/59.1.10) (q:draft)
paak = (t:adj) (w:white/bright) (d:shining white, as snow or bright clothing) (e:vuuk bangin a ~ hi/a hate bawngnawi sangin ~ zaw ding hi | his teeth will be whiter than milk/zah dongin a ~ mahmah hi | it was so very white/a siangtho a ~ saihadial silhin | dressed in clean white linen) (s:kang/kaang/ngo) (a:vom) (r:40.28.3/42.9.29/1.49.12/41.9.3/66.19.14) (q:draft)
Paak = (t:n) (w:flower/blossom) (d:Unok Paak is the lily flower) (e:Unok ~ bangin amaute palh ding a) (b:paak) (r:28.14.5) (q:draft)
paakin = (t:v) (w:blossoming/blooming) (d:paak, flower, used as a verb, with in linking it to the next verb) (e:~, almond min gah a gah hi) (s:palhin) (b:paak) (r:4.17.8) (q:draft)
paaknamtui = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:spice/fragrant flower) (d:paak, flower, with namtui, sweet-smelling) (e:~ kung a pona) (r:22.6.2) (q:draft)
paaksak = (t:v) (w:make white/whiten/bleach) (d:paak, be white, with the causative sak: make white, as in washing or bleaching clothes) (e:kuamah in a ~ zawh loh ding/Na puante siangin ~ tawntung in la | always keep your clothes clean and white/Tuuno sisan tawh a ~ uh ahi hi | they made them white in the blood of the Lamb) (a:vomsak) (b:paak) (r:41.9.3/21.9.8/66.7.14) (q:draft)
paakte = (t:n) (w:flowers/blossoms) (d:plural of paak, flower; also of flower shapes made in gold) (e:Gam sung tengah ~ palh a/a ~ a pulhmang khin oliv kung | an olive tree that has shed its blossoms/Gamlak a om ~ a nuntakzia ngaihsun dih un | consider how the flowers of the field live/Lopate vulin ~ pulh a | the grass withers and the flowers fall) (s:pakte) (r:22.2.12/2.25.34/18.15.33/40.6.28/60.1.24) (q:draft)
paam = (t:n) (w:surroundings/neighbourhood/area around) (d:found in the pair kiim and paam, each with its own pronoun: i kiim i paam and ka kiim ka paam, all around us) (e:ka kiim ka ~ uh a mite khempeuh/I kiim i ~-a mi namdangte’ kiang pan hong paite | those who came from the foreign nations around us) (s:kim) (r:27.9.16/16.5.17) (q:draft)
paampaih = (t:adj) (w:outcast/cast aside/rejected) (d:paampaih mi is an outcast) (e:note ~ mi pawl, hong ci-in) (r:24.30.17) (q:draft)
paang = (t:n) (w:cheek/jaw/temple of the head) (d:the side of the face or head: the cheek that is slapped, the jaw, and the temple; in Leviticus 13.41 used of the front part of the head from which hair is lost) (e:hong kai mite tungah ka ~ ka dawh hi/ka ~ a beng dingin | to slap my cheek/Na ~ langkhat a hong bengte | those who slap you on one cheek/amah in phelkhamin a ~ sun hi | she shattered and pierced his temple) (s:biang) (r:23.50.6/7.4.21/18.16.10/42.6.29/7.5.26) (q:draft)
paangah = (t:n) (w:into the temple of the head/in the temple of the head) (d:paang, the temple of the head, with ah, at or into) (e:a ~ a khensuk hi/Sisera a ~ puanbuk khetphim tawh | Sisera with the tent peg in his temple) (b:paang) (r:7.4.21/7.4.22) (q:draft)
Paarai = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Paarai) (d:Paarai the Arbite, one of the mighty warriors of David) (r:10.23.35)
paat = (t:v) (w:be worn out/wear thin/be thin) (d:become thin through wear, said of clothes and sandals, of eyes worn by weeping, and of a wall that narrows) (e:khual gamlapi zinna-in ~ gawp hi/Ka kah kahna-in ka mit ~ gawp a | my eyes are worn out with weeping/a ~ ngingeisa khat | one who is utterly worn out/a biakinn kawm a ~ tektek mah bangin) (r:6.9.13/26.41.7/25.2.11/26.23.43) (q:draft, low confidence)
paatgawp = (t:v) (w:be badly worn out/fail) (d:paat, be worn out, with gawp, badly or thoroughly; said of eyes worn by weeping) (e:ka mit ~ ta a) (b:paat) (r:25.2.11) (q:draft)
paatgawpta = (t:v) (w:be badly worn out) (d:paatgawp with ta, marking that the state has now been reached; said of clothes and sandals) (e:khual gamlapi zinna-in ~ hi) (b:paatgawp) (r:6.9.13) (q:draft)
paatkhia = (t:v) (w:wear out/become worn out) (d:paat, be worn thin, with khia, out: wear out, said of cloth that grows old and thin) (e:amaute pen puan bangin ~ ding hi/amaute khempeuh puan bangin ~ ding uh hi | they will all wear out like a garment/leitung in puan bangin ~ ding a | the earth will wear out like a garment) (r:19.102.26/23.51.6/23.50.9) (q:draft)
paatsa = (t:adj) (w:worn-out/old/tattered) (d:paat, be worn out, with sa, already: of sacks, wineskins, sandals and clothes that are old and falling apart) (e:a ~ puante tawh pai uh hi/a late uh tungah a ~ ip | worn-out sacks on their donkeys/a ~, a kiphop khedapte bulhin | wearing worn and patched sandals) (s:luisa) (a:thak) (b:paat) (r:6.9.5/6.9.4) (q:draft)
paatsak = (t:v) (w:wear out/wear down/exhaust) (d:paat, be worn out, with sak, cause) (e:Pasian aw, kei nong ~ ngiingei a) (b:paat) (r:18.16.7) (q:draft)
Padaiah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Pedaiah) (d:man of Rumah, father of Zebidah the mother of King Jehoiakim) (r:12.23.36)
Paddan = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Paddan) (d:first part of Paddan-aram, Paddan Aram, the region where Laban lived) (r:1.28.2/1.35.26) (q:draft)
Paddan-aram = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Paddan Aram) (d:region in northern Mesopotamia where Laban lived and where Jacob found his wives) (r:1.28.2/1.35.26) (q:draft)
Paddanaram = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Paddan-aram/Paddan Aram) (d:region in northern Mesopotamia where Laban lived and where Jacob found his wives) (r:1.25.20/1.31.18)
Padon = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Padon) (d:ancestor of a family of temple servants who returned from the exile) (r:15.2.44/16.7.47)
Pafos = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Paphos) (d:city on the west coast of Cyprus where Paul met the sorcerer Bar-Jesus) (r:44.13.6)
Pagiel = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Pagiel) (d:son of Okran, leader of the tribe of Asher in the wilderness) (r:4.1.13/4.10.26)
pah = (t:adv) (w:immediately/at once/right away/instantly) (d:placed after a verb: the action happens at once, without delay) (e:a dam ~ hi/Kha Siangtho in Zeisu gampa lakah a sawl ~ hi | the Spirit at once sent Jesus into the wilderness/Mihaite in a hehna uh langsak ~ a | fools show their anger at once/amaute ka sap ciangin amaute omkhawm ~ uh hi | when I call them they stand together at once) (s:pahpah/thakhatin/pak) (r:41.1.42/41.1.12/20.12.16/23.48.13)
pah = (t:conj) (w:as soon as) (d:after a verb and followed by leh: as soon as the action happens) (e:a cih ~ leh | as soon as he said it) (s:phetin/phetun) (r:40.14.27)
Pahathmoab = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Pahath-Moab) (d:ancestor of a large family that returned from the exile; also a leader who sealed the covenant with Nehemiah) (r:15.8.4/16.10.14)
Pahathmoabte = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Pahath-Moab) (d:Pahathmoab with the plural te: the family descended from Pahath-Moab) (b:Pahathmoab) (r:15.2.6/16.7.11)
pahin = (t:adv) (w:immediately/at once/straightaway) (d:pah with the linking suffix in, after a verb: doing it at once, and then) (e:meivak a nget khit ciangin lut ~/Jerusalem ah amaute pai ~ | they went at once to Jerusalem/thukhenna tokhom tungah tu ~ | I at once took my seat on the judgment seat/a mun lui mah-ah biakna tau phut ~ | they at once set up the altar on its old site) (s:pakin) (b:pah) (r:44.16.29/44.25.17/15.4.23/15.3.3) (q:draft)
pahpah = (t:adv) (w:immediately) (d:pah doubled: at once, each time or each one without delay) (e:a min hi ~ hi/kihei kul loin a pai thei ~ uh hi | they could go straight on without needing to turn/a gei-ah ciamtehna khat bawl ~ ding uh hi | they will at once set up a marker beside it/pasian a hilote’ siampi suak ~ hi | he at once becomes a priest of what are not gods) (s:pah/thakhatin) (r:1.2.19/26.1.12/26.39.15/14.13.9)
pahpah = (t:adv) (w:straight away/at once/right away/instantly) (d:pah doubled: readily, without stopping to think, as in heh pahpah, be quick to anger) (e:Heh ~ kei in, hehna in haihuai hi/thu ngaihsun masa loin gamta ~ hi | he acts at once without thinking first/lungdam takin na sang ~ uh a | you gladly accept it right away) (s:pah/pakin) (r:21.7.9/20.14.16/47.11.4)
pahpah = (t:conj) (w:as soon as)
pahpahin = (t:adv) (w:immediately/at once/right away) (d:pahpah with the adverbial ending in) (e:khialhnate kimu ~ mawhsakna thuakpah uh a) (b:pahpah) (r:54.5.24) (q:draft)
pahpahpa = (t:n) (w:one who acts at once) (d:pahpah, immediately, with pa, the one who: hong huh pahpahpa is the one who helps at once) (e:haksat hunin hong huh ~ ahi hi) (b:pahpah) (r:19.46.1) (q:draft)
pahpahte = (t:n) (w:those who are quick to) (d:pahpah at once, readily, with the plural te, making a noun of the verb phrase before it: those who are quick to do something; a heh pahpahte is those who are quick to anger) (e:A heh ~ in kitotna piangsak a/thukhen zum hong tun ~ | those who readily take you to court) (b:pahpah) (r:20.29.22/59.2.6) (q:draft)
pahtaak = (t:n) (w:favour/approval) (d:the good opinion of others; spelling of pahtak) (e:mihing ~ ding ut-a) (s:pahtak/pahtakna) (r:51.3.22) (q:draft)
pahtak = (t:v) (w:favour/be pleased with/delight in/approve of) (d:be pleased with someone and hold him in regard) (e:pa in a ~ a tapa/Amah ka ~ mahmah mi khat ahi hi | he is a man I am very pleased with/kumpipa in amah a ~ manin | because the king favoured him/ama ~ leitung mite tungah | on the people of the earth whom he favours) (r:20.3.12/9.16.22/17.5.11/42.2.14) (q:draft)
pahtak = (t:n) (w:favour/approval/honour) (d:the good opinion of others; pahtak ngah is to gain honour) (e:Mite’ ~ ding hanciam ka hi hiam/Kitot khak ding pelhna in ~ ngahna hi a | avoiding a quarrel brings honour/a sanggamte’ ~ hi hen la | let him be the favourite of his brothers) (s:pahtakna/pahtaak) (r:48.1.10/20.20.3/5.33.24) (q:draft)
pahtakbawl = (t:v) (w:speak well of/praise/treat with favour) (d:pahtak, favour or approval, with bawl, do or make: show someone approval) (e:kamsang zuaute a ~ uh hi/Mi khempeuh in note hong ~ ciangin | when everyone speaks well of you) (b:pahtak) (r:42.6.26) (q:draft)
pahtakhuai = (t:adj) (w:honoured/admirable/worthy of honour) (d:pahtak, favour or honour, with huai, worthy of: deserving honour or admiration) (e:a deihhuai, le a ~ thute ahi hi/keima mit-ah manpha-in, ~ in | precious and honoured in my sight) (s:pahtawihuai/phathuai) (r:50.4.8/23.43.4) (q:draft)
pahtaklam = (t:n) (w:favour/the fact of favouring) (d:pahtak, favour or be pleased with, with lam, the fact or manner of) (e:Nangma nong ~ na pa in) (r:9.20.3) (q:draft)
pahtakna = (t:n) (w:approval/favour/honour/praise) (d:pahtak, favour, with the noun suffix na: the approval, favour or honour that someone gives; pahtakna ngah is win favour) (e:a topa a kempa in ~ ngah hi/Thuhoih a hanciamte in ~ ngah a | those who seek good find favour/ama ~ in tuk-guah a zusak meiipi tawh kibang hi | his favour is like a cloud that brings spring rain/thuakzawh hatna in Pasian’ ~ hong ngahsak a | endurance gains us the approval of God) (s:pahtak) (b:pahtak) (r:20.27.18/45.5.4/20.11.27/20.16.15) (q:draft)
pahtawi = (t:v) (w:honor/exalt/glorify) (d:show honour to someone or lift him up in rank or praise; of God and his name, exalt and glorify) (e:lungdamna tawh amah ka ~ ding hi/ama min ~ khawm ni | let us exalt his name together/Kumpipa in a ~ nop mipa adingin | for the man the king wishes to honour/Topa a zahtakte a ~ mi | one who honours those who fear the Lord) (s:liansak/minthangsak/zahtak) (a:simmawh/mindaisak) (r:19.69.30/17.6.7/19.34.3/19.15.4) (q:draft)
pahtawihuai = (t:adj) (w:honourable/worthy of honour) (d:deserving honour or respect: pahtawi, honour, with huai, worthy of) (e:a sanggamte sangin ~ zaw hi/Topa’ ni siangtho pen ~ na cih uh a | you call the holy day of the Lord honourable) (s:pahtakhuai/zahtakhuai) (a:mindaihuai/zumhuai) (r:13.4.9/23.58.13) (q:draft)
pahtawina = (t:n) (w:honor/respect) (d:pahtawi, honor, with the noun suffix na: the respect or high standing given to a person; pahtawina ngah is receive honor) (e:hauhna leh ~ zong hong pia hi/lungdamna, leh ~ ngah uh hi | they received joy and honor/kiniamkhiatna in ~ hong ngah sak hi | humility brings honor/na khan’ sau-in, ~ na ngah ding hi | you will live long and receive honor) (s:pahtakna/zahtakna) (a:mindaina/simmawhna) (b:pahtawi) (r:20.3.16/17.8.16/20.15.33/20.21.21) (q:draft)
Pahtawina = (t:see) <Pahtawina-a>
Pahtawina-a = (t:n) (w:to the honor of/in honor of) (d:pahtawina honor with the marker a, at or for) (e:Siangtho Pa ~ hong puak uh ahi) (r:23.60.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
pahtawinate = (t:n) (w:praises/honors) (d:pahtawina, honor or praise, with the plural te: the praises given to someone) (e:Israelte’ ~ tungah na tu hi) (s:phatnate) (b:pahtawina) (r:19.22.3) (q:draft)
pahtawipa = (t:n) (w:one who honors) (d:pahtawi, honor or exalt, with pa, the one who) (e:hong ~ in Pasian ahi hi) (b:pahtawi) (r:47.1.21) (q:draft)
pahtawite = (t:n) (w:those who honor) (d:pahtawi, honor, with te, those who) (e:kei hong ~ ka pahtawi ding a) (a:simmawhte) (b:pahtawi) (r:9.2.30) (q:draft)
pahtawizawk = (t:v) (w:honor more/be honored more) (d:pahtawi, honor, with zawk, more, the form of zaw used before ding) (e:Moses sangin Jesuh ~ ding ahi hi) (r:58.3.3) (q:draft)
pahte = (t:adv) (d:pah, at once or readily, after a verb, with te, those who: a zuak pahte, those who sell readily, a mang pahte, those who accept at once) (e:lei nop hun-a a zuak ~ kiphat hi/lungdamin a mang ~ ahi uh hi | they are the ones who gladly accept it at once) (b:pah) (r:20.11.26/42.8.13) (q:draft)
pai = (t:v) (w:come) (d:move toward the speaker or the place spoken of, usually with hong before it: hong pai, come here) (e:Hong ~-in ka damsak ding hi/a manlangin na hong ~ nading hahkat in | do your best to come quickly/Tua lai takin laitheipa khat hong ~ a | then a teacher of the law came/lei mong panin hong ~ nadingin a sam hi | he calls them to come from the ends of the earth) (r:40.8.7/55.4.9/40.8.19/23.5.26)
pai = (t:v) (w:go) (d:move from one place to another, go or walk to a place) (e:Oliv Mual ah a ~ hi/tuute kiangah na ~ zaw un | go rather to the sheep/a utna lam peuhpeuh ah ~ thei uh hi | they could go in any direction they wished/Kikhopna buk mai lamah Moses leh Aaron ~ a | Moses and Aaron went to the front of the tent of meeting) (r:43.8.1/40.10.6/26.1.17/4.16.43)
Pai = (t:v) (w:go) (d:pai, go, written with a capital at the start of quoted speech) (e:Lau kei un, ~ un la/~ un. Ngia hon lakah tuuno kikhahte bangin | go, like lambs let loose among wolves/~ in, na pasal sam in la | go, call your husband/~ kik-in eite’ ading an tawm va lei un | go back and buy a little food for us) (b:pai) (r:40.28.10/12.2.18/42.10.3/43.4.16/1.44.25) (q:draft)
Pai = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Pau/Pai) (d:the city of Hadad king of Edom; Pau in the NIV, Pai in older English Bibles) (e:ama khuapi min in ~ hi a) (r:13.1.50) (q:draft)
paidak = (t:v) (w:forsake/abandon/cast off) (d:give up or abandon someone for good; used in parallel with nusia, forsake) (e:ama luahte ~ lo ding hi/bang ci-a hong ~ thei ding ka hi hiam | how can I give you up) (s:nusia/taisan) (r:19.94.14/28.11.8) (q:draft)
paih = (t:v) (w:throw away/cast/throw off/reject) (d:form of paai used before khit, nading and other endings) (e:Amah in a puan a ~ khit ciangin/a nin mun khatah a ~ nadingun | to throw them into an unclean place/amau in ngen a ~ uh leh | when they cast the net/buite leh bakte ~ ding uh hi | they will throw them to the moles and bats/innlam note in na ~ uh | which you builders rejected) (s:lawn) (r:41.10.50/3.14.40/43.21.6/23.2.20/44.4.11) (q:draft)
paihdak = (t:v) (w:cast away/throw down) (d:paih, throw away, with dak; in the verse of God casting his people into deep darkness; what dak adds is not clear) (e:khuamialpi sungah nong ~ dinga kilawm zahin) (r:19.44.18) (q:draft, low confidence)
paihkhiat = (t:v) (w:throw away/cast out/thrust out/forsake) (d:throw away, drive out or give up: the form of the verb used before words such as bangin, dongin, hun and thu) (e:Kep hun om a, ~ hun om hi/Siriate in nawhsa-in a ~ uh puante | the clothes the Arameans had thrown away in their haste/ama muhna panin amaute a ~ dongin | until he thrust them from his presence/na neih itna na ~ thu ahi hi | it is that you have forsaken the love you had/note’ mai-a ka ~ ding minamte | the nations I am going to drive out before you) (s:hawlkhiat/nusiat) (a:kep) (b:paih) (r:21.3.6/12.17.20/12.7.15/66.2.4/3.18.24) (q:draft)
paihkhiatna = (t:n) (w:casting out/rejection/setting aside) (d:paihkhiat, throw out, with the noun suffix na: being thrown out, rejected or set aside; paihkhiatna thuak is be rejected) (e:ahih ciangin ~ a ngah zo hi/~ thuakin hamsiat a thuak nadingin | to be rejected and cursed/pukna thu in ~ a thuak zo hi | the offense has been done away with) (s:nialna) (b:paihkhiat) (r:58.7.18/12.24.20/58.6.8/48.5.11) (q:draft)
paihkhiatpih = (t:v) (w:bring out/lead out) (d:used in the verse beside paikhiatpih with the same meaning; perhaps a misprint of that word) (e:Filistia mite ka ~ a) (r:30.9.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
paihkhiatsak = (t:v) (w:remove/take away/deprive of) (d:paihkhiat, throw out, with the causative sak: take something away from someone, remove it for him) (e:khanghamte’ pilna ~ hi/hih gam mite’ mawhna ka ~ ding hi | I will remove the sin of the people of this land/Topa in na galte hong ~ khin a | the Lord has taken away your enemies/minam makaite’ pilna ~ a | he takes away the understanding of the leaders of nations) (b:paihkhiat) (r:18.12.20/38.3.9/36.3.15/18.12.24) (q:draft)
paihkhiatsakin = (t:v) (w:removing/taking away) (d:paihkhiatsak remove, take away from someone, with the linking ending in) (e:suang lungtang ~ mihing lungtang ka guan ding hi/i hamphatnate hong ~ | taking away our rights/Tua hun ciangin na sakolte uh hong ~ | in that day I will remove your horses) (b:paihkhiatsak) (r:26.11.19/33.5.10/25.3.35) (q:draft)
paihmang = (t:v) (w:throw away/cast out/abandon) (d:paih, throw, with mang, away or lost) (e:a ~ nadingun) (s:paimang) (r:44.7.19) (q:draft)
paihmawk = (t:v) (w:throw away/throw out) (d:paih, throw, with mawk, simply or to no purpose) (e:~ a kul hi) (r:42.14.35) (q:draft)
paihna = (t:n) (w:throwing/casting down) (d:paih, a form of paai, throw, with the noun suffix na; the act of throwing or casting down, and before a noun the place where a thing was thrown) (e:luang khempeuh a ~ tuikhuk pen/~ ding ahi zongin vangliatna nei hi | he has power also to overthrow) (b:paih) (r:24.41.9/14.25.8) (q:draft)
paihsak = (t:v) (w:throw away/cast/hurl) (d:throw away or cast down something that belongs to another; paih with sak) (e:tuipi sungah ~ ding a/tuipi taw-ah nong ~ ding hi | you will hurl them to the bottom of the sea/pasian-te pen meikhuk sungah ~ khin hi | they have thrown the gods into the fire/leivui lakah ama kumpi lukhu na ~ hi | you have cast his crown into the dust) (b:paih) (r:38.9.4/33.7.19/23.37.19/19.89.39) (q:draft)
paihsakin = (t:v) (w:throwing/casting) (d:paihsak with the ending in, linking it to the following verb: throwing) (e:meikhuk sungah ~ susia khin hi) (b:paihsak) (r:23.37.19) (q:draft)
paihtuam = (t:n) (w:partiality/discrimination) (d:setting one person aside from the rest; paired with guptuam for favouritism and partiality) (e:kuamah guptuam ~ nei hetloin) (r:54.5.21) (q:draft, low confidence)
paii = (t:v) (w:conceive/be pregnant with/carry in the womb) (d:carry a child in the womb, conceive; nau paii is be with child) (e:Nang hong ~ gil leh na teep nawi/Lopa keu na ~-a buhkung na suaksak hi | you conceive chaff and give birth to straw/Keimah in hih mite khempeuh ~ ka hi hiam | did I conceive all these people) (s:gai) (r:42.11.27/23.33.11/4.11.12) (q:draft)
paii = (t:v) (w:throw/cast/throw away) (d:throw something down or away, as a net onto the water; also written paai) (e:tui tungah ngeen a ~ mite thanem ding/na khut na khe sattan in la, ~ in | cut off your hand or your foot and throw it away/phuk ~-in mei sungah kikhul ding hi | it will be cut down and thrown into the fire) (s:lawn) (r:23.19.8/40.18.8/40.3.10) (q:draft)
paiite = (t:n) (w:goods/valuables/treasures) (d:used together with sum, money, as sum leh paiite and na sum na paiite, money and possessions; compare sumlepai) (e:a neihsa uh sum leh ~/na sum na ~ uh man ngah loin | your money and your treasures, without payment) (s:vante/neihsate) (r:37.2.7/24.15.13) (q:draft)
paikawm = (t:v) (w:while going/while walking) (d:pai, go, with kawm, while: as one goes along, at the same time as another action) (e:Mihaite lampi-ah a ~ nangawnin hai tat uh/lam ~ diangkawmin Pasian a phat hi | walking and jumping, he praised God) (r:21.10.3/44.3.8) (q:draft)
paikawmin = (t:v) (w:while going/going along) (d:pai go with kawm, at the same time, and the linking suffix -in: doing something else while on the way) (e:manawhin a ~ thu a hilh hi/Lampi-ah i ~ Lai Siangtho khiatna hong gen laitakin | while he explained the Scriptures to us as we went along the road/a ~ samsia-in suang tawh amah dengin | as he went he cursed and threw stones at him/khuapi kiimah na ~ na namsau tawh satnen in | strike it with your sword as you go around the city) (b:paikawm) (r:42.13.22/18.22.14/42.24.32/10.16.13/26.5.2) (q:draft)
paikawmun = (t:v) (w:as they go/while going/on the way) (d:pai with kawm, while, and the plural ending un: as they went along, doing something else at the same time) (e:A ~ hih thupiangte kikumkum uh hi/a ~ ham uh hi | they lowed as they went/lampi-ah a ~ a kap uh hi | they weep as they go along the road/Amaute a ~ a tha uh hat semsem a | as they go their strength grows more and more) (b:paikawm) (r:42.24.14/9.6.12/24.48.5/19.84.7) (q:draft)
paikha = (t:v) (w:happen to go/pass by/go near) (d:pai go with kha, happen to or come upon) (e:siampi khat ~ zenzen a/na kiangah kong ~ a | I passed by you/a inn gei nangawnah ~ kei un | do not even go near her house/hong cih leh zong va ~ kei un | even if they tell you so, do not go there) (r:42.10.31/20.5.8/26.16.6/40.24.26) (q:draft)
paikhak = (t:v) (w:go near/happen to go/come near) (d:form of paikha used before ciangin) (e:biakinn nai-ah Israel mite a ~ ciangin) (b:paikha) (r:4.8.19) (q:draft)
paikhawm = (t:adv) (w:together with/go together/accompany) (d:pai, go, with khawm, together: go or come together with someone) (e:keimah tawh a ~ ding uh hi/mihonpite in Zeisu tawh a ~ uh hi | large crowds were going along with Jesus/Tua ahih ciangin amaute gel ~ uh hi | so the two of them went on together/kumpite kikaikhawm in, hong ~ uh hi | the kings assembled and advanced together) (b:pai) (r:46.16.4/42.14.25/1.22.8/19.48.4)
paikhawmin = (t:v) (w:go together/go with) (d:paikhawm with the linking ending in, going together) (e:Andru le Filip ~ Jesuh kiangah/Judah mite zong Simeon mite tawh ~ | the men of Judah went together with the Simeonites/Solomon’ nasemte tawh Ofir-ah ~ | going to Ophir together with the servants of Solomon/amah tawh hong ~ note kong mu ding uh hi | I will come with him and see you) (b:paikhawm) (r:43.12.22/7.1.17/14.8.18/58.13.23) (q:draft)
paikhawmpa = (t:n) (w:one who goes with) (d:paikhawm, go together, with pa, the one who) (e:note tawh hong ~ in Topa) (b:paikhawm) (r:5.20.4) (q:draft)
paikhawmsak = (t:v) (w:send together with/let go with) (d:paikhawm, go together, with sak, make or let) (e:keima nasemte ~ in/Antiok khua-ah a ~ ding uh a vaihawm uh hi | they decided to send them along to Antioch) (b:paikhawm) (r:11.22.49/44.15.22) (q:draft)
paikhawmte = (t:n) (w:companions/those who go with) (d:paikhawm, go together, with plural te) (e:kei tawh hong ~ kimkot ah) (b:paikhawm) (r:44.26.13) (q:draft)
paikhia = (t:n) (w:getout/go out/leave/depart) (d:pai, go, with khia, out: go out of a place or away from someone) (e:Tuate ~ uh a/Zeisu in khua nawl ah a ~ hi | Jesus went out of the city/Faro’ omna panin ~ hi | he went out from the presence of Pharaoh/Tua mun pan ~ a | he went on from that place) (r:41.6.12/41.11.19/1.47.10/40.12.9) see <pai> and <khia>
paikhial = (t:v) (w:go astray/turn aside) (d:pai, go, with khial, wrongly) (e:pasian manlote lamah a ~ lo mi) (r:19.40.4) (q:draft)
paikhiapa = (t:n) (w:one who has gone out) (d:paikhia, go out, with pa, the man who) (e:hih mun pan-a ~ Shallum’ thu) (b:paikhia) (r:24.22.11) (q:draft)
paikhiapih = (t:v) (w:bring out/lead out) (d:paikhia, go out, with pih, together with: go out taking someone along) (e:amaute ka ~ lai-in) (b:paikhia) (r:3.23.43) (q:draft)
paikhiasak = (t:v) (w:send away/let go/make go out) (d:paikhia, go out, with causative sak) (e:khut guak tawh a ~ zo hi/Tua numei na ~ ta in | send that woman away/zing ciangin nang kong ~ ding hi | tomorrow I will send you off/sila suaktasakin ~ ding hi | he shall let the slave go free) (s:ciahsak/paisak) (b:paikhia) (r:42.1.53/42.14.4/40.15.23/10.11.12/2.21.27) (q:draft)
paikhiasakin = (t:v) (w:send away/send out) (d:paikhiasak with the ending in, linking it to the following verb: sending out) (e:a nin numei le pasal ~) (b:paikhiasak) (r:4.5.3) (q:draft)
paikhiasuak = (t:v) (w:go out/pass out) (d:paikhia, go out, with suak, right on through) (e:tua panin ~ hi lo ahi hiam) (r:40.15.17) (q:draft)
paikhiasuk = (t:v) (w:go out/go away/leave) (d:paikhia, go out, with suk, downward) (e:Amalek mite lak panin ~ un) (b:paikhia) (r:9.15.6) (q:draft)
paikhiat = (t:v) (w:go out/come out/leave/depart) (d:form of paikhia used before lai, ding, phetin and in dependent clauses) (e:Bethani khua pan a ~ lai takin/Izipt panin na ~ lai-un lampi ah | on the way when you came out of Egypt/Jordan panin hong ~ nading thu pia in | command them to come up out of the Jordan/mi sung pan a ~ khit ciangin | after it has gone out of a person/tua inn ah na ~ matengun na om un | stay in that house until you leave) (s:kuankhiat/pusuah) (a:lut) (b:paikhia) (r:41.11.12/6.2.7/5.24.9/6.4.16/42.11.24/42.9.4) (q:draft)
paikhiata = (t:v) (w:come out/go out) (d:paikhia, go out, with ta, marking a completed event; a paikhiata kipan is since they came out) (e:Israel mite a ~ kipan tuni dongin) (b:paikhia) (r:7.19.30) (q:draft)
paikhiate = (t:n) (w:things that come out) (d:paikhia, come out, with the plural te; a paikhiate, the things that come out) (e:Kam sung pan a ~ in/sung pan a ~ in mi a ninsak thei hi | what comes out from within defiles a person) (s:pusuakte) (b:paikhia) (r:40.15.18/41.7.20) (q:draft)
paikhiatin = (t:v) (w:go out/set out/leave) (d:paikhiat with the ending in: when or as someone set out) (e:Haran panin a ~ Abram) (b:paikhiat) (r:1.12.4) (q:draft)
paikhiatkhak = (t:v) (w:slip out/get out) (d:paikhiat, go out, with khak, happen to; with loh nading, so that no one gets out) (e:kuamah a ~ loh nading thei un) (r:12.9.15) (q:draft)
paikhiatlam = (t:n) (w:going out/departure/leaving) (d:paikhiat go out, with lam, the fact or manner of: that someone has gone out, the leaving of someone) (e:na ~ mi khempeuh musak in/a vangliatna a ~ phawkpah ahih manin | because he noticed at once that power had gone out/a ~ uh le amaute ahihlam uh | that they were leaving and that it was they) (s:paikhiatna) (r:26.12.3/41.6.33/41.5.30) (q:draft)
paikhiatna = (t:n) (w:departure/exodus/going out) (d:paikhiat, go out, with the noun suffix na: the act of leaving, or before gam or mun the place someone came out from) (e:Israel mipawlte ~ thu lakin/Zebulun aw, na ~ ah lungdam in | rejoice, Zebulun, in your going out/a ~ gam uh a ngaihsun kik hi le-uh | if they had thought back to the country they left/khuamial hong ~ mun ahi zongin | or the place darkness comes out from) (s:kuankhiatna/pusuahna/paikhiatlam) (b:paikhiat) (r:58.11.22/58.11.15/5.33.18/18.38.19) (q:draft)
paikhiatnapa = (t:n) (w:man from whom something went out) (d:paikhiatna, going out, with pa marking a man: in the verses the man out of whom the demons had gone) (e:Dawite a ~ in Zeisu tawh/dawi ~ puan silhin mipil bangin | the man the demons had left, clothed and in his right mind) (b:paikhiatna) (r:42.8.38/42.8.35) (q:draft)
paikhiatnasa = (t:adj) (w:left/gone out from) (d:paikhiat, go out, with na, place, and sa, already: that one has gone out from) (e:Ka ~ inn mahah ciahkik ning) (b:paikhiat) (r:40.12.44) (q:draft)
paikhiato = (t:v) (w:come up out/go up out) (d:paikhia, go out, with to, upward) (e:pasian khat hong ~ ka mu hi) (b:paikhia) (r:9.28.13) (q:draft)
paikhiatosak = (t:v) (w:send up/make go up out) (d:paikhiato, go up out, with causative sak) (e:kote hong ~ kei in) (b:paikhiato) (r:2.33.15) (q:draft)
paikhiatpih = (t:v) (w:bring out/lead out/take out) (d:paikhiat, go out, with pih, together with: go out taking someone or something along, bring or lead out) (e:Izipt panin amaute ~ hi/Israel mite ami’ honpi-in ~ in | bring the Israelites out by their divisions/a sa na ~ kei ding uh hi | you shall not take the meat out/Ka Topa a ~ zo uh a | they have taken my Lord away/Eufrates galkhat-a Siria mite ~ hi | he brought out the Arameans from beyond the Euphrates) (a:lutpih/tumpih) (b:paikhiat) (r:4.23.22/2.12.51/2.6.26/2.12.46/43.20.13/10.10.16) (q:draft)
paikhiatpihin = (t:v) (w:bringing out/leading out/taking out) (d:paikhiatpih with the linking ending in, followed by another verb: bringing out, brought out and) (e:leenggah lo nawlah ~ a that uh hi/amaute ~ amaute a ciahpih ding | who will lead them out and bring them home/Egypt gam panin amaute ~ gamlak ka tunpih a | I led them out of Egypt and brought them into the wilderness/Izipt gam panin hong ~ | bringing you out of Egypt) (b:paikhiatpih) (r:40.21.39/12.10.26/4.27.17/26.20.10/30.2.10) (q:draft)
paikhiatpihna = (t:n) (w:bringing out/leading out) (d:noun from paikhiatpih: the act or fact of bringing or leading someone out; also the place or people to which one is led out) (e:Israel mite a ~ thu za hi/Topa in note hong ~ mite lakah | among the peoples to which the Lord will lead you away/Izipt panin ~ tawh kote' tungah bang hong bawl | what have you done to us by bringing us out of Egypt) (b:paikhiatpih) (r:2.18.1/5.28.37/2.14.11) (q:draft)
paikhiatpihpa = (t:n) (w:one who brought out) (d:the one who led or brought someone out; -pa marks a man) (e:note a hong ~ ka hi hi/amau sung pan Israelte a ~ tungah | to him who brought Israel out from among them/Khaldea gam Ur khua panin a hong ~ | the one who brought you out of Ur of the Chaldeans) (b:paikhiatpih) (r:3.22.33/2.16.6/19.136.11/1.15.7) (q:draft)
paikhiatpihsak = (t:v) (w:let bring out) (d:paikhiatpih, bring out, with sak, cause or allow; in the verse a request to be allowed to bring someone out) (e:amaute hong ~ unla) (b:paikhiatpih) (r:1.19.8) (q:draft)
paikhiatpihte = (t:n) (w:those led out/those taken away) (d:paikhiatpih, lead out, with plural te) (e:a ~ khempeuh hong kilehhei kikin) (b:paikhiatpih) (r:24.41.14) (q:draft)
paikhiatpihto = (t:v) (w:bring up out) (d:paikhiatpih, bring out, with to, upward) (e:Leinuai panin kei nong ~ khin a) (b:paikhiatpih) (r:19.30.3) (q:draft)
paikhiatsak = (t:v) (w:send out/send away/dismiss/let go) (d:paikhiat, go out, with the causative sak: make or let someone go out, send away or set free) (e:Zeisu in mihonte a ~ lai takin/Na kiang panin a suakta-in na ~ ciangin | when you let him go free from you/mihonpite a ~ khit ciangin | after he had dismissed the crowds/ama leitang panin Israel mite a ~ nading | to let the Israelites go out of his land) (s:ciahsak/khahkhia) (b:paikhiat) (r:40.14.22/2.6.11/5.15.13/40.14.23) (q:draft)
paikhiazo = (t:v) (w:have gone out/have come out/have set out) (d:paikhia, go out, with zo marking the action as done) (e:na tanu sung panin dawi a ~ hi/gamte a susia ding pa hong ~ hi | the destroyer of nations has set out) (b:paikhia) (r:41.7.29/24.4.7) (q:draft)
paikhin = (t:v) (w:have gone/gone already) (d:pai go with khin, marking the action as already done) (e:lui gal khatah ~ zo uh hi/mual sangpen munah ka ~ a | I have gone up to the highest mountain/ni khat lam ~ uh a | they went a day’s journey/Elijah hong ~ takpi a | Elijah has indeed come) (b:pai) (r:10.17.20/12.19.23/42.2.44/41.9.13) (q:draft)
paikhit = (t:v) (w:have gone/finish going) (d:pai go with khit, completed; a paikhit ciangin is after he had gone) (e:pawikhamna-ah a ~ uh ciangin/puanbuk sungah a ~ mateng Moses’ nung en uh hi | they watched Moses until he had gone into the tent/Na-aman tom khat a ~ ciangin | when Naaman had gone a little way/ni sagih sung a kual ~ uh ciangin | after they had marched around for seven days/kei ka ~ mateng | until I have passed by) (r:43.7.10/12.5.19/2.33.8/12.3.9/2.33.22) (q:draft)
paikhop = (t:v) (w:go together with/come with/accompany) (d:pai, go, with khop, together; form of paikhawm used before ciangin and lai takin) (e:vantungmite tawh hong ~ ciangin/thukhen mangpa kiangah na ~ lai takin | while you are going with him to the magistrate) (r:40.25.31/42.12.58) (q:draft)
paikhopna = (t:n) (w:going together/accompanying) (d:paikhop, go together with, with the noun suffix na; nong paikhopna is your going with us) (e:kote tawh nang nong ~ hi lo) (b:paikhop) (r:2.33.16) (q:draft)
paikik = (t:v) (w:return/go back/come back) (d:pai, go or come, with kik, back or again: go back or come back to where one was; hong paikik is come back) (e:na pasal sam in la, hong ~ in/amah in zui-in hong ~ a | he went back with him/no kiangah kong ~ ding a | I will come back to you/khatvei kong ~ ding hi | I will come back again) (s:ciahkik/kilehkik) (b:pai) (r:43.4.16/11.13.19/43.14.3/44.18.21) (q:draft)
paikikin = (t:v) (w:returning/going back/coming back) (d:paikik with the linking ending -in, used when another action follows: returned and) (e:tua ciangin amaute hong ~ puanbuk dang khatah/Amaute hong ~ ama kiangah a gen uh ciangin | when they went back and told him/zingsang ciangin ~ Kaisaria khua-ah ka tung uh a | in the morning we went on and reached Caesarea/Amah Kumpi-in hong ~ ukna hong kipan ding | he will come again as King and begin his rule) (s:ciahkikin) (b:paikik) (r:12.7.8/11.20.5/12.9.36/44.21.8/55.4.1) (q:draft)
paikikna = (t:n) (w:return/coming back/coming again) (d:paikik, return, with the noun suffix na) (e:Zion-ah Topa hong ~ amaute in maitang/a hong ~ thu ahi zongin | and about his coming again) (s:ciahkikna) (b:paikik) (r:23.52.8/61.1.16) (q:draft)
paikim = (t:v) (w:all come/all go) (d:pai, go or come, with kim, all without exception: come every one of them) (e:a ~ ciat dingin sapna thu) (r:27.3.2) (q:draft)
pailai = (t:v) (w:go farther/go on/be still to come) (d:pai go or come with lai, more or still) (e:suanglot khat tan bang ~ a/Amah tawmkhat ~-in leilakah boksuk a | going a little farther he fell to the ground/gamlakah ni khat lam ~-in | going a day’s journey farther into the wilderness/a lianzaw khat hong ~ ding hi | one who is greater is still to come) (r:42.22.41/42.3.16/41.14.35/11.19.4) (q:draft)
pailam = (t:n) (w:coming/going) (d:pai go, come, with lam, the fact of: that someone has come or is coming) (e:Pasian hong ~ na phawk lohna hang ahi hi/galkapte tawh hong ~ a muh uh ciangin | when they saw him coming with the soldiers/ama kiangah na ~ kitheisak kei in | do not let him know that you have come) (r:42.19.44/8.3.3/44.21.32) (q:draft)
pailet = (t:v) (w:pierce through/pass through/penetrate) (d:pai go, with let through: go right through a body) (e:Thaltang khat in a pumpi ~ a/guhngeek ahi zongin, khenin ~ thei a | even joints and marrow it can pierce and divide) (s:sunlet) (r:18.20.25/58.4.12) (q:draft)
pailetin = (t:v) (w:piercing/passing through) (d:going right through something; pailet with the linking suffix -in) (e:a lungtang ~ a leeng sungah/a numei’ pumpi ~ a nihin sun khawm hi | he speared both of them, right through the body of the woman/na lungtang ~ hong sun hi | it pierces right through your heart) (b:pailet) (r:12.9.24/18.22.14/4.25.8/24.4.18) (q:draft)
paimang = (t:v) (w:throw away/cast away) (d:in the verse, of hair cut off and thrown away) (e:Na sam uh ~ unla) (s:paihmang) (r:24.7.29) (q:draft)
paimangpih = (t:v) (w:take away/carry off) (d:paimang with pih, together with: go away taking something along) (e:Hih nate na ~ un) (b:paimang) (r:43.2.16) (q:draft)
paimangta = (t:v) (w:abandon/forsake/cast off) (d:paimang with ta, marking that the act is now done) (e:ka luahsa mite ka ~ hi) (b:paimang) (r:24.12.7) (q:draft)
paina = (t:v) (w:walking/going/where one goes) (d:pai, go, with the suffix na: the going of someone, a journey, or the place where one goes; na paina khempeuh ah is wherever you go) (e:Topa Pasian a ~ ging/Na ~ khempeuh ah kong zui ding hi | I will follow you wherever you go/ganhingte’ ~ peuhpeuh ah pai uh hi | they went wherever the creatures went/ni thum ~ a gamlapi-ah tuute paipih hi | he took the sheep a three-day journey away) (b:pai) (r:1.3.8/42.9.57/26.1.20/1.30.36)
painasa = (t:v) (w:have gone/have passed through) (d:pai with na and sa, already, used before a noun of place: the place where someone has gone; a painasa-ah means where it has passed, in its wake) (e:Israel khempeuh tawh ka ~ mun khempeuh/kote ka va ~ uh leitang | the land we went through/A ~-ah tuihual om dandan a | where it has passed the water is left in waves/note kiangah ka hong ~ thu | our coming to you) (b:pai) (r:13.17.6/4.14.7/18.41.32/52.2.1) (q:draft)
paingei = (t:v) (w:usually go/be used to going) (d:pai, go, with ngei, be accustomed to; a paingei bangin is as was his custom) (e:a ~ bangin kikhopna inn-ah) (r:42.4.16) (q:draft)
painop = (t:v) (w:want to go/be willing to go) (d:pai go, with nop, the form of nuam want used in dependent clauses, as before kei leh and ciangin) (e:Jerusalem-ah a ~ kei leh/Egypt mite a ~ kei leh | if the Egyptians are not willing to go/a ~ uh ciangin | when they wanted to go) (r:38.14.17/26.1.12/38.14.18) (q:draft)
painopna = (t:n) (w:wish to go/place one wants to go) (d:painop, want to go, with the noun suffix na; the wish to go, and the place where one wants to go) (e:na ~ peuhpeuhah na pai thei hi/Ama ~ mun a tun ciangin | when he reached the place he wanted to go to/mipihte lakah ~ lungsim a nei hi | he had it in his heart to go to his own people) (b:painop) (r:24.40.4/44.7.23/42.22.40) (q:draft)
painuam = (t:v) (w:want to go/be willing to go/want to come) (d:pai go, come, with nuam want) (e:kei kiangah nong ~ kei veve uh hi/mihonte mai-ah thugen dingin ~ a | he wanted to go and speak before the crowd/Jerusalem ah a ~ khempeuh in | all who wish to go to Jerusalem) (r:43.5.40/44.19.30/15.7.13) (q:draft)
paipa = (t:n) (w:one who comes/one who goes) (d:pai with -pa, the man who goes; hong paipa is he who comes) (e:min tawh hong ~ in thupha ngah ta hen/Ka nungah hong ~ in kei om ma-in om | he who comes after me was before me/Pasian kiang pan hong ~ longal | except the one who comes from God) (b:pai) (r:41.11.9/43.6.46/43.1.15) (q:draft)
paipah = (t:v) (w:go at once/hurry/go quickly) (d:pai go with pah at once) (e:humpinelkai kikhumna-ah a va ~ hi/hong tun phetin Jesuh kiangah ~ a | as soon as he arrived he went straight to Jesus/manlang takin hong ~ hi | they come swiftly, at once/a lupna pheek la-in a ~ hi | he picked up his mat and went at once) (r:27.6.19/42.1.39/41.14.45/23.5.26/43.5.9) (q:draft)
paipahin = (t:v) (w:going at once/coming straight up) (d:paipah, go at once, with in linking it to the next verb) (e:Judas zong Jesuh kiangah hong ~/amau’ lawmte hong ~ amaute kiangah | their associates came straight to them) (b:paipah) (r:40.26.49/15.5.3) (q:draft)
paipai = (t:v) (w:keep going/go on/go about) (d:pai go, said twice to show that the action continues; kot paipai, keep going round) (e:kulhpi tungah kot ~ uh a/David leh a mite lampi-ah ~ uh hi | David and his men kept going along the road/meikuang sungah mihing li a kawi ~ | four men walking about in the fire/David a huh dingin mi hong ~ hi | men kept coming to help David/a na tui a ~ a | whether his discharge keeps flowing) (r:19.55.10/3.15.3/10.16.13/27.3.25/13.12.22) (q:draft)
paipaina = (t:see) <paipaina-ah>
paipaina-ah = (t:adv) (w:wherever it goes) (d:pai, go, doubled, with na, place, and ah, at or to: to whatever place one goes) (e:a pei’ ~ adangte in zui-in) (r:26.10.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
paipak = (t:v) (w:come soon/come for a while) (d:pai, go or come, with pak, quickly or for a short while) (e:ka hong ~ theih lohna) (r:45.15.22) (q:draft, low confidence)
paipel = (t:n) (w:basket) (d:large carrying basket; in the accounts of the feeding of the crowds, the baskets filled with the pieces left over) (e:~ sawm le nih a dim hi/~ lian sagih a dim hi | seven large baskets were filled/~ sawm le nih dim a pha hi | they filled twelve baskets) (s:bawm/seeng) (r:40.14.20/41.8.8/43.6.13) (q:draft)
paiphei = (t:v) (w:go across/run along) (d:pai, go, with phei, crosswise or level; in the verse of a row of rooms running along one level of a building) (e:dawl khat gual ~ suak-ah inndei neu sawmthum) (r:26.41.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
paipih = (t:phrase) (w:go along with) (d:pai, go, with pih, together with: go along with someone, or make someone go along) (e:tai khat hong ~ nuamte tai nih na zui un | go two miles with those who want to make you go one mile with them) (b:pai) (r:40.5.41)
paipih = (t:v) (w:brought/bring/take/lead) (d:go taking a person or thing along: hong paipih is bring here, and paipih with a place is take or lead there) (e:khomun leh ngasa hong ~ un/Tua pa hong ~ un | bring that man here/tua mittawpa Farisaite kiangah a ~ uh hi | they brought the blind man to the Pharisees/lei pan-a piang gah piakna Topa tungah ~ a | he brought an offering of the fruits of the soil to the Lord) (b:pai) (r:40.14.18/1.2.22/42.18.40/43.9.13/1.4.3)
paipihin = (t:v) (w:bringing/taking/leading) (d:paipih, take along, with the linking ending in: bringing or leading someone and then doing the next action) (e:a luang ~ hankhuk sungah a vui/Siampipa in tua nu va ~ | the priest shall bring that woman/Kikhopna buk mai-ah Levi mite ~ | bringing the Levites before the tent of meeting/hih leitangah eite hong ~ | leading us into this land) (b:paipih) (r:41.6.29/3.8.6/4.5.16/4.8.9/4.14.8) (q:draft)
paipihkha = (t:v) (w:bring along/take along/happen to bring) (d:paipih, take along, with kha, happen to; paipihkha loin means so as not to bring a thing somewhere by mistake) (e:biakna sa le ante ~ loin/biakna sa le ante ~ loin | so as not to bring the sacrificial meat and food) (r:26.46.20) (q:draft)
paipihkik = (t:v) (w:bring back/lead back) (d:paipih, take along or lead, with kik, back: bring or lead someone back) (e:amaute’ gamah ka ~ ding hi/Tui omna lui gei-ah amaute ka ~ ding a | I will lead them back beside streams of water/sehnel gamah amah ka ~ ding a | I will lead her back into the wilderness) (s:tunpihkik/ciahpihkik) (b:paipih) (r:26.37.21/24.31.9/28.2.14) (q:draft)
paipihmang = (t:v) (w:bring along/bring in) (d:paipih, take along, with mang, wholly; in the verse, bring everyone in) (e:mi khempeuh hong ~ khin in) (r:42.14.23) (q:draft, low confidence)
paipihna = (t:n) (w:bringing/leading/taking along) (d:paipih, take along, with the noun suffix na: the act of bringing; before a noun, the place to which one is brought, as in kong paipihna gam, the land I am bringing you to) (e:Note kong ~ gamah tungin/kong ~ na mu khin uh hi | you have seen how I brought you/note hong ~ lampi khempeuh | all the way by which he led you/note kong ~ Kanaan gamah | in the land of Canaan where I am bringing you) (s:tunpihna) (b:paipih) (r:4.15.18/2.19.4/5.8.2/3.18.3) (q:draft)
paipihpa = (t:n) (w:the one who led/he who brought) (d:paipih, take along or lead, with pa, the male one: he who led, said of God who led his people) (e:gamlak nawkin ama mite a ~ tungah/tui om lohna lei keu-ah hong ~ | he who led you through the dry land without water) (b:paipih) (r:19.136.16/5.8.15) (q:draft)
paipihsak = (t:v) (w:have someone bring/let bring/let carry) (d:paipih, bring along, with the causative sak: make or let someone bring or carry a person or thing) (e:na sanggampa uh hong ~ un/tua naupangte ka kiangah hong ~ unla | let those children be brought to me/kuamah bangmah ~ lo hi | he let no one carry anything/a tecite uh hong ~ unla | let them bring their witnesses) (b:paipih) (r:1.42.16/41.11.16/40.19.14/23.43.9) (q:draft)
paipihsuk = (t:v) (w:bring down/take down) (d:paipih, take along, with suk, downward: take someone down to a place; in Acts, bring a man down before the council) (e:amaute upa vaihawmte kiangah ka ~ hi/tuangsakin Gihon-ah ~ un | have him ride and take him down to Gihon/hih mihonte kiangah nang kong ~ ding hi | I will take you down to this band/upa kikhopna-ah Paul hong ~ a | bring Paul down to the council of elders) (s:puaksuk/paisukpih) (a:paipihto) (b:paipih) (r:44.23.28/45.10.7/11.1.33/9.30.15/44.23.20) (q:draft)
paipihto = (t:v) (w:take up/bring up/lead up) (d:paipih, take along, with to, upward: take or lead someone up, or bring a thing up to a higher place) (e:dawimangpa in Zeisu ~ a/dei tungnung sungah a ~ uh hi | they took him up to the upper room/Hih mite ~ in | lead these people up/Mual sangpi dawnah Zeisu ~ a | he took Jesus up to the top of a very high mountain) (s:puato) (a:paipihsuk) (b:paipih) (r:42.4.5/14.1.4/44.9.39/2.33.12/40.4.8) (q:draft)
paipihtoh = (t:v) (w:bring up/take up/lead up) (d:form of paipihto, bring up, used before words such as a kipan and theih) (e:Israel-te ka ~ a kipan tuni dongin/Thuciamna Singkuang na ~ theih nadingun | so that you may bring up the ark of the covenant) (b:paipihto) (r:13.17.5/13.15.12) (q:draft)
paipite = (t:todo) (q:draft, follows singhiang, branch, in a list of leafy boughs; the meaning of paipi is not clear from one verse)
paisak = (t:v) (w:send/let go/send away) (d:pai, go, with the causative sak: make someone go, send; or allow someone to go, let go) (e:Zeisu in tua pa thakhatin ~ a/Joppa khua-ah mi na ~ in | send men to Joppa/amah in amaute ~ lo hi | he did not let them go/Judas leh Silas kong ~ uh hi | we are sending Judas and Silas) (s:sawl) (b:pai) (r:41.1.43/2.9.17/44.10.5/2.10.27/44.15.27) (q:draft)
paisakin = (t:v) (w:sending/letting go) (d:paisak, send or let go, with the linking ending in: sending, and then; hong paisakin is letting me go) (e:Efesa khua-ah mi ~ pawlpi upate a sam/hong ~ ka sanggamte hong musak in | let me go and see my brothers/Kote Jordan ah hong ~ | let us go to the Jordan/inn ukpa in amaute kiangah ~ | the ruler of the synagogue sent word to them) (b:paisak) (r:44.20.17/9.20.29/12.6.2/44.13.15) (q:draft)
paisakkik = (t:v) (w:send back/send again/let come again) (d:paisak, send or let go, with kik, again or back) (e:kiangah hong ~ inla/Pasian in kei hong ~ baih theih nadingin | so that God may soon send me back) (b:paisak) (r:7.13.8/58.13.19) (q:draft)
paisakna = (t:n) (w:sending/letting go) (d:paisak, send or let go, with the noun suffix na: the act of sending or of letting go) (e:a Tapa a hong ~ thu/Israel mite ka ~ dingin | that I should let the Israelites go/khuapi-ah nong ~ ding kong thum hi | I ask you to send me to the city) (b:paisak) (r:62.4.14/16.2.5/2.5.2) (q:draft)
paisan = (t:v) (w:depart/go away/leave) (d:pai, go, with san, away from: go away from a person or place and leave it behind) (e:hong ~ uh hi/amaute nusia-in a ~ hi | he left them and went away/a si dektaksa-in a ~ uh hi | they went away leaving him half dead/Jesuh bangmah cih loin a ~ uh hi | they did nothing to Jesus and went away) (s:nusia) (r:24.5.23/40.16.4/42.10.30/41.12.12)
Paisan = (t:n) (w:Passover) (d:the yearly feast that recalls how the Lord passed over the houses of Israel in Egypt; often Paisan pawi, the Passover feast) (e:A kiseh hunin ~ pawi/~ kici silngo om lo khomun pawikham ding | the feast of unleavened bread called the Passover/Judah mite’ ~ pawikham hun a nai zo hi | the Passover feast of the Jews was near) (s:Paisan Pawi/Paisanna) (r:4.9.2/42.22.1/43.6.4)
Paisan Pawi = (t:n) (w:Passover) (d:Paisan, Passover, with pawi, feast: the Passover feast, kept on the fourteenth day of the first month) (e:hong ciahkik mite in ~ bawl uh hi/hih ~ kibawl hi | this Passover was celebrated/Jerusalem ah Topa adingin ~ kibawl hi | the Passover was celebrated to the Lord in Jerusalem) (s:Paisan/Paisanna) (r:15.6.19/14.35.19/12.23.23)
paisanin = (t:v) (w:leaving/going away from/going off) (d:paisan, go away from, with the linking ending in: leaving a person, place or thing and then doing the next action) (e:amaute ~ khua sung pan paikhia a/pawlkhat in a sumbukah na ~ | another went off to his business/milim ~ Pasian’ lamah na kiheina uh | how you left idols and turned to God) (s:taisanin) (b:paisan) (r:40.21.17/52.1.10/40.22.5) (q:draft)
paisanna = (t:n) (w:departure) (d:paisan, go away from or pass by, with the noun suffix na) (b:paisan)
Paisanna = (t:n) (w:Passover/passing over) (d:paisan pass over with the noun suffix na; Topa’ Paisanna is the Lord's Passover) (e:~ hangin biakpiakna ahi hi) (s:Paisan/Paisan Pawi) (b:Paisan) (r:2.12.27) (q:draft)
paisawm = (t:v) (w:intend to go/plan to go) (d:pai, go, with sawm, intend) (e:hih mipa koi lai-ah ~ hi ding) (r:43.7.35) (q:draft)
paisim = (t:v) (w:go secretly/go in secret) (d:pai go, with sim, secretly, without being seen) (e:Zeisu zong a kilang loin a ~ hi/Izipt gamah mi ~ sak hi | he secretly sent men to Egypt) (s:simpai) (r:43.7.10/26.17.15) (q:draft)
paisuak = (t:adj) (w:nonstop) (d:going on without a break; after a verb, keep on doing it without stopping) (e:Topa na zahtakna zom ~ in/dantuahna, kip ~ ding hi | their punishment will last forever/na kumpi tokhom tungah tu ~ ding uh | they will sit on your throne forever) (s:tawntung) (r:20.23.17/19.81.15/19.132.12)
paisuak = (t:adv) (w:forever) (d:after a verb: on and on without end; with lo, not forever) (e:Mihingte sungah ka Kha om ~ nawn lo ding hi/amah heh ~ lo ding hi | he will not stay angry forever/hong nial ~ lo ding hi | he will not reject us forever/Khapi bangin tua pen kip ~ ding a | like the moon it will stand firm forever) (s:ngitnget/tawntunga/atawntungin) (r:1.6.3/19.103.9/25.3.31/19.89.37)
paisuakah = (t:adv) (w:all the way along/right around) (d:paisuak, going straight on, with ah, at; in the verse, along the whole circuit of the city) (e:Khuapi kimkot ~ pi zali sawmnih) (b:paisuak) (r:26.48.17) (q:draft, low confidence)
paisuakin = (t:adv) (w:forever/for good/continually) (d:paisuak, on without end, with the linking ending in; after a verb: forever, for good, without turning back) (e:Topa in hong nial ~/ka kumpi gam sungah amah kipsak ~ | I will establish him in my kingdom forever/Ama itna kip bei ~ | has his steadfast love ceased forever) (s:ngitnget/atawntungin) (b:paisuak) (r:19.77.7/13.17.14/19.77.8) (q:draft)
paisuakin = (t:v) (w:going on/passing on/continuing on) (d:paisuak, go straight on, with the linking ending in: going on through or beyond a place and then doing the next action) (e:Tua gamah ~ thu-um mite a hansuah/Jesuh ~ amau kikhopna inn sungah a lut hi | Jesus went on and entered their synagogue/Hazaraddar lamah ~ Azmon dongah pai ding a | it will continue to Hazar Addar and go on to Azmon/Efraim mualtung gamah ~ Mikah’ inn-ah a tung uh hi | they went on to the hill country of Ephraim and came to the house of Micah) (b:paisuak) (r:44.20.2/6.18.18/40.12.9/4.34.4/7.18.13) (q:draft)
paisuaknop = (t:v) (w:want to go straight on) (d:paisuak, go straight on, with nop, want, the form of nuam used before uh hangin) (e:ka ~ uh hangin) (r:44.27.7) (q:draft)
paisuakpah = (t:v) (w:go straight at once/go directly) (d:pai, go, with suak, right through, and pah, at once: go straight there without delay) (e:Siampipa kiangah ~ inla kivelsak in/Andru’ inn-ah ~ uh a | they went straight to the house of Andrew) (r:42.5.14/41.1.29) (q:draft)
paisuaksak = (t:v) (w:let through/make pass through/let pass) (d:paisuak, go right through, with the causative sak: let someone pass through, or make a thing reach from one end to the other) (e:mong khat dongin a zawl laita ~ hi/amaute in hong ~ theih nadingun | so that they will let me pass through/siampite leh mite ~ kei in | do not let the priests and the people pass through) (b:paisuak) (r:2.36.33/16.2.7/2.19.24) (q:draft)
paisuaksak = (t:v) (w:make continue/make last) (d:paisuak, go on without end, with the causative sak: make a state last, keep someone in it for good) (e:khang tawntungin siampi hi ~ ding hi/biakpiakna a bawlna tawh siangtho ~ hi | by the sacrifice he made he has made them holy forever) (b:paisuak) (r:2.40.15/58.10.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
paisuakzawh = (t:v) (w:be able to continue/manage to go on) (d:paisuak, right on or continuing, with zawh, be able; placed after another verb, as thuak paisuakzawh, be able to go on enduring) (e:gimna i thuak ~ leh amah tawh i ukkhawm/A om ~ kei leh | if she is not able to stay that way) (r:55.2.12/46.7.11) (q:draft)
paisuakzo = (t:v) (w:be able to get through/be able to carry on) (d:paisuak go right through, go on without stopping, with zo, be able; after another verb, manage to keep on doing it to the end) (e:nangmah in na sem ~ ding hi/Kua in khauhtakin nial a, nial ~ ahi hiam | who has resisted him and come through/ka lampi khaktan a, ka ~ kei hi | he has blocked my way and I cannot get through) (b:paisuak) (r:2.18.23/18.19.8/18.9.4) (q:draft)
paisuk = (t:v) (w:go down/come down/descend) (d:pai, go, with suk, downward: go or come down to a lower place) (e:Samson Timnah-ah ~ a/lei thukpi sungah ~ ding hi | they will go down into the depths of the earth/Sinai Mual dawn-ah Topa hong ~ hi | the Lord came down on the top of Mount Sinai/ka tapa a sih ma-in hong ~ in | come down before my son dies) (s:kumsuk/tuaksuk/kuansuk) (a:paito/kahto) (b:pai) (r:7.14.1/1.11.5/19.63.9/2.19.20/43.4.49) (q:draft)
paisukin = (t:v) (w:going down/go down) (d:paisuk, go down, with the linking ending in, used when another verb follows: going down and then) (e:amah ~ a numei tawh kiho hi/Moses ~ amaute' kiangah gen hi | Moses went down and spoke to them/kote ~ nang’ ading an ka lei ding uh hi | we will go down and buy food for you/ka pate uh Izipt ah na ~ | our fathers went down to Egypt) (b:paisuk) (r:7.14.7/2.19.25/1.43.4/4.20.15) (q:draft)
paisukna = (t:n) (w:way down/descent/slope) (d:paisuk, go down, with the noun suffix na: the place where a road goes down, a descent) (e:Oliv Mual tung pan a ~ mun/Silla ~ lampi Millo inn sungah | in the house of Millo on the road down to Silla/Arabah lam ~-ah zing tungin paikhia uh hi | they went out early to the descent toward the Arabah) (a:paitohna) (b:paisuk) (r:42.19.37/12.12.20/6.8.14) (q:draft)
paisukpa = (t:n) (w:one who goes down) (d:paisuk, go down, with pa, the one who) (e:Leinuai-a ~ hong ciahkik ngei nawn lo) (b:paisuk) (r:18.7.9) (q:draft)
paisukpih = (t:v) (w:bring down/take down) (d:paisuk, go down, with pih, together with) (e:i pa hong ~ un) (s:paipihsuk) (b:paisuk) (r:1.45.13) (q:draft)
paisuksak = (t:v) (w:let go down/make go down/bring down) (d:paisuk, go down, with the causative sak: make or let someone go or come down) (e:zang gamah ~ lo uh hi/Leinuai-ah ama lutang ~ kei in | do not let his head go down to the grave/Leinuai-ah a hingtangin amaute ~ in la | let them go down alive to the grave/tua mipa kei kiangah hong ~ un | have that man come down to me) (a:paitosak) (b:paisuk) (r:7.1.34/11.2.6/19.55.15/9.17.8) (q:draft)
paisukte = (t:n) (w:those who go down) (d:paisuk, go down, with the plural te: those who go down, often of the dead who go down to the pit) (e:Leihawm sunga ~ tawh a kibang/misite kiang-a ~ tawh ka kibat loh nadingin | so that I may not be like those who go down to the dead/Gum sunga a ~ in nangma thumanna hong muang thei lo | those who go down into the pit cannot hope in your faithfulness) (b:paisuk) (r:19.28.1/23.14.19/19.143.7/23.38.18) (q:draft)
paita = (t:v) (w:come now/be coming/have come) (d:pai, come, with ta, marking that the coming has now begun or happened; hong paita in is an urgent request to come) (e:hih lai-ah hong ~ hi/omkhin ahih manin hong ~ un | come, for everything is ready/keimah huh dingin hong ~ in | come now to help me/amah hong ~ ding a | he is coming) (b:pai) (r:9.9.17/66.1.7/42.14.17/23.38.14) (q:draft)
paitawm = (t:v) (w:come on one's own/come of one's own accord) (d:pai, go or come, with tawm, by oneself; come without being sent by another) (e:ama thu tawh hong ~ leh/Keima thu-in a hong ~ ka hi kei a | I have not come on my own/piaknopna a nei mi khempeuh hong ~ uh a | everyone who was willing to give came of his own accord) (r:43.5.43/43.8.42/2.35.21) (q:draft)
paite = (t:n) (w:those who come/those who go) (d:pai with the plural ending -te, the people who come or go; with hong before it, those coming this way) (e:leilu lam pan-a hong ~ en dih in/Pasian bia dinga hong ~ lakah | among those who came to worship God/tua lai-a ~ tam mahmah hi | those who went there were very many) (b:pai) (r:24.13.20/43.12.20/1.50.9) (q:draft)
paithei = (t:v) (w:can go/can come/be able to walk) (d:pai, go, with thei, can or may: be able or allowed to go or come; lam paithei is be able to walk) (e:Pa Pasian kiangah i ~ hi/giahphual sungah hong ~ ding hi | he may come into the camp/khebaite lam ~ a | the lame can walk/ka hong ~ kei zongin | even if I cannot come) (b:pai) (r:49.2.18/40.11.5/5.23.11/42.7.22/50.1.27) (q:draft)
paitheih = (t:v) (w:be able to come/be able to go) (d:pai go or come with theih can; mostly in paitheih nading, so that one may come) (e:note kiangah ka hong ~ nading/kei mahmah zong ka hong ~ nadingin | so that I myself also may come/Pasian kiangah ~ nading hun i nei hi | we have the chance to approach God/tua khua-ah nong ~ nadingin hong hanciam in | do your best to come to me in that town) (s:paizo) (b:pai) (r:45.1.10/49.3.12/50.2.24/56.3.12) (q:draft)
paitheihna = (t:n) (w:ability to walk/being able to go) (d:paitheih, be able to go, with the noun suffix na; lam a paitheihna ding a hilh is teach to walk) (e:lam a ~ ding a hilh pa) (b:paitheih) (r:28.11.3) (q:draft)
paito = (t:v) (w:go up/ascend) (d:pai, go, with to, upward: go up to a higher place; of God or Christ, ascend) (e:Tua lai mun panin amah Be-ersheba-ah ~ hi/Aw ging tawh Pasian ~ a | God has gone up with a shout/kiang panin Pasian ~ hi | God went up from him/Ka Pa kiangah a ~ nai lo ka hi hi | I have not yet gone up to my Father) (s:kahto/kuanto) (a:paisuk/kumsuk) (b:pai) (r:1.26.23/19.47.5/1.35.13/43.20.17) (q:draft)
paitoh = (t:v) (w:go up/come up/ascend) (d:form of paito used before words such as ciangin and leh) (e:Jerusalem khua-ah a ~ ciangin/vantung lamah meikuang a ~ ciangin | when the flame went up toward heaven/A sangna munah a ~ ciangin | when he ascended on high/Joab a ~ lai-in | when Joab had gone up) (s:kahtoh) (b:paito) (r:44.11.2/7.13.20/49.4.8/11.11.15) (q:draft)
paitohna = (t:n) (w:ascent/way up/going up) (d:paitoh, go up, with the noun suffix na: the act of going up or the place where a road goes up, as in Bethhoron paitohna lampi, the road going up to Beth Horon) (e:Bethhoron ~ lampi-ah amaute delhin/Bethhoron ~-ah a paisuk lai takun | as they were going down the ascent of Beth Horon/biakinn-ah ka ~ ding a lim | the sign that I will go up to the temple) (s:kahtohna) (a:paisukna) (b:paitoh) (r:6.10.10/19.122.3/6.10.11/12.20.8) (q:draft)
paitosak = (t:v) (w:bring up/let go up/make go up) (d:paito go up, with sak, cause or allow) (e:Egypt panin kote hong ~ na hi hiam/tu-in kei hong ~ in la | now let me go up) (a:paisuksak) (b:paito) (r:4.20.5/1.50.5) (q:draft)
paizaw = (t:v) (w:go rather/go instead) (d:pai, go, with zaw, rather) (e:Israel mite lakah va ~ un/Arabia gamah ka ~ a | I went to Arabia instead) (b:pai) (r:40.10.6/48.1.17) (q:draft)
paizia = (t:n) (w:way/course) (d:pai, go, with zia, manner: the way someone goes or acts; thu paizia is the course of a matter and biakna paizia the way of religion) (e:nomau’ ~ bang hi lo hi/Na thu ~ khek nadingin | to change the course of the matter/i biakna ~ tawh a kilehngatin | contrary to the way of our religion) (s:zia) (r:23.55.8/10.14.20/54.6.3) (q:draft)
paiziate = (t:n) (w:ways/courses) (d:paizia, way, with the plural ending te; Pasian thu paiziate is the ways of God) (e:ka ~ nomau’ paizia bang hi lo hi/Pasian’ thu ~ a mantakin a hilhtel uh hi | they explained the ways of God accurately/Topa’ thu ~ gensia gawp uh | they spoke evil of the ways of the Lord) (s:ziate) (b:paizia) (r:23.55.8/23.55.9/44.18.26/44.19.9) (q:draft)
paizo = (t:v) (w:be able to come/get in) (d:pai, come or go, with zo, be able) (e:David hong ~ peuhmah lo ding hi) (s:paitheih) (b:pai) (r:10.5.6) (q:draft)
paizo = (t:v) (w:have come) (d:pai, come, with zo marking the action as done) (e:a susia dingte hong ~ uh hi) (b:pai) (r:24.12.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
pak = (t:n) (w:flower/blossom) (d:the flower of a plant; lopa pak is the flower of the grass) (e:a nun leh a ~ tawh a om/unok ~ bangin | like a crocus flower/lopa ~ tawh kibang hi | it is like the flower of the grass) (s:paak/pakpalh) (r:2.37.20/60.1.24/23.35.1) (q:draft)
pak = (t:adv) (w:quickly/at once/soon) (d:placed after a verb, the action is done quickly, at once or for a short while) (e:a lu kunsuk ~ a, bia hi/Amau’ galte ka zawhsak ~ ding a | I would quickly subdue their enemies/pakpalh bangin khangin keu ~ uh a | they grow like a flower and soon wither/tuikuang sungah a tui bung ~ a | she quickly emptied her water into the trough/ka thupiakna lampi panin kiheikhia ~ uh hi | they have quickly turned from the way I commanded) (s:pah/mengmeng) (a:damdamin) (r:2.34.8/19.81.14/18.14.2/1.24.20/2.32.8) (q:draft)
pak = (t:v) (w:bloom/blossom/bud) (d:of a plant or tree: come into flower) (e:leengguite a ~ nai hiam/anthul kungte a ~ laitak ahi hi | the flax was in bloom/leenggui a ~ nai hiam cih a en ding | to see whether the vine had blossomed/leengguite ~ ta ahih manin | because our vines are in bloom) (s:palh) (a:vul) (r:22.7.12/2.9.31/22.6.11/22.2.15) (q:draft)
pakan = (t:n) (w:dish/plate) (d:small dish or bowl; in Numbers a gold dish holding incense) (e:kham ~ khat paknamtui a dim tawh/kham ~ sawm-le-nih | twelve gold dishes) (r:4.7.14/4.7.20/4.7.84) (q:draft)
pakante = (t:n) (w:dishes/plates) (d:small dishes or ladles among the temple vessels, in these verses for incense) (e:taitehte leh paknamtui adingin ~ leh biakinn sung/a kuangdaite, paknamtui ~, kuang-ukte | its plates, incense dishes and bowls/paknamtui adingin ~, leh vutluahna | dishes for incense and censers) (b:pakan) (r:12.25.14/2.37.16/4.4.7/14.4.22) (q:draft)
pakin = (t:adv) (w:quickly/suddenly/at once) (d:pak with the ending in, after a verb: happening fast or all at once) (e:tuate bei ~, kote ka maimang uh hi/Pasian nusiakik ~ lungdamna thudang khat | so quickly deserting God for a different gospel/Lauhuai lianpi hong tung ~ sihna a om ciangin | when great disaster comes suddenly and there is death/kuama don lohin si ~ | they die suddenly with no one taking notice) (s:thakhatin/pah/mengmeng) (a:damdamin) (b:pak) (r:19.90.10/18.9.23/48.1.6/18.4.20) (q:draft)
pakkhia = (t:v) (w:blossom/bloom/come into flower) (d:pak, bloom, with khia, out) (e:A sel phetin ~ pah a) (s:palhkhia) (b:pak) (r:1.40.10) (q:draft)
pakkual = (t:n) (w:wreath/garland) (d:pak, flower, with kual, ring; a ring of flowers, in the verses a carved or cast ornament) (e:a pang ciatah ~ om hi/a kimkotah ~ bawl hi | he made wreaths all around) (r:11.7.30/11.7.36) (q:draft)
pakkualte = (t:n) (w:wreaths/garlands) (d:pakkual, wreath, with the plural ending te) (e:bawngtalte le ~ hong paipih hi/tua bawngte go-in ~ a pianuam uh hi | they wanted to kill the bulls and offer the wreaths) (b:pakkual) (r:44.14.13) (q:draft)
pakna = (t:n) (d:pak, quickly or for a short while, with the noun suffix na; after a verb it names the doing of it quickly or briefly, as in hauh pakna, getting rich quickly, and ten’ pakna, staying for a while) (e:Ol tak-a hauh ~ in kiam kik/na teen’ ~ uh gam sungah | in the land where you stay for a while/A baihlam-a hauh ~ in | wealth gained quickly and easily/a om ~ uh gam panin | from the land where they are staying for a time) (b:pak) (r:20.13.11/24.35.7/20.20.21/26.20.38) (q:draft)
paknamtui = (t:n) (w:incense/perfume/spice) (d:pak, flower, with namtui, fragrant: a sweet-smelling substance, burned as incense or used as perfume) (e:tua tungah a namtui ~ hal hi/kham pakan khat ~ a dim tawh | one gold dish full of incense/ka ~ hong kizeel hi | my perfume spread its fragrance/kawngtente, ~ bungte leh a kivom aite | sashes, perfume bottles and charms) (r:2.40.27/42.23.56/4.7.14/22.1.12/23.3.20) (q:draft)
paknamtuite = (t:n) (w:spices/perfumes/incense) (d:paknamtui, incense or perfume, with the plural ending te: spices, perfumes, kinds of incense) (e:na ~ tawh na siam tawpin/oliv thau leh ~, milim biakna-in na zang hi | you used the olive oil and incense for idol worship/Sheba gam panin ~ hong pai a | incense comes from Sheba/puante, mor ~ | robes, myrrh and spices) (b:paknamtui) (r:23.57.9/11.10.25/26.16.18/24.6.20) (q:draft)
pakpak = (t:adv) (w:quickly/easily/readily) (d:pak, quickly, doubled; placed after a verb, be quick to do it, as in heh pakpak, be easily angered) (e:heh ~ lo, mite’ mawhna ciamteh lo/pau pahpah kei unla, heh ~ kei un | do not be quick to speak or quick to get angry/Mi that ~ uh a | they are quick to kill/amah heh ~ hi | his anger flares up quickly) (s:pahpah) (r:46.13.5/45.3.15/59.1.19/19.2.11) (q:draft)
pakpalh = (t:n) (w:open flower/blossom/flower in bloom) (d:pak, flower, with palh, open out) (e:umgah le ~ lim kigelh hi/nisuh kungte, leh ~ lim kibawlte tawh | with carved palm trees and open flowers/Amaute ~ bangin khangin keu pak uh a | they grow up like a flower and soon wither) (s:pak/paak) (r:11.6.18/18.14.2/11.6.32) (q:draft)
pakpalhte = (t:n) (w:flowers/blossoms/open flowers) (d:pakpalh, open flower, with the plural ending te) (e:nisuh kungte le ~ bawl a/Lebanon Mual-a ~ vul hi | the blossoms of Lebanon wither/amaute’ ~ leivui bangin vanah leengto ding hi | their blossoms will fly up like dust) (s:paakte/pakte) (b:pakpalh) (r:11.6.35/34.1.4/23.5.24) (q:draft)
pakta = (t:v) (w:praise/commend/admire/approve of) (d:think well of someone or of what he does and say so) (e:a pasal in zong ~ mahmah a/Thukham zui lo mite in migilote ~ uh a | those who do not keep the law praise the wicked/Pasian in a na ~ hi | God commended them/ama ngiansiamna hangin a topa in a ~ hi | his master commended him for his shrewdness) (s:phat/pahtak) (a:simmawh/gensia) (r:20.31.28/58.11.2/20.28.4/42.16.8) (q:draft)
paktat = (t:adj) (w:promiscuous/loose/immoral) (d:sexually immoral, placed after the noun; numei paktat is a prostitute or harlot, and pasal paktat a male prostitute) (e:numei ~ nih kumpipa kiangah hong pai uh/numei ~ khat ten’pih in la | marry a promiscuous woman/a om lai pasal ~ pawlte | the male prostitutes who were left/Tua ahih ciangin numei ~ aw | therefore, you prostitute) (r:11.3.16/11.22.46/28.1.2/26.16.35) (q:draft)
paktat = (t:v) (w:prostitute oneself/commit prostitution) (d:act as a prostitute or be sexually immoral; also said of Israel being unfaithful to God) (e:Na tanute uh a ~ manun/Moab tanute tawh ~ ding kipan uh hi | they began to commit immorality with the Moabite women/a nungak lai-in Izipt gamah a ~ mah bangin | as she was a prostitute in Egypt in her youth/numei tawh a ~ mite tawh | with people who are immoral with women) (s:thangtat) (r:28.4.14/4.25.1/26.23.19/46.5.9) (q:draft)
paktatin = (t:v) (w:committing prostitution/acting immorally) (d:paktat, prostitute oneself, with in linking it to the next verb; paktatin gamta is behave as a prostitute) (e:Na monu Tamar ~ gamta hi/Amah tawh ~ a kiphasak khawm leitung kumpite | the kings of the earth who were immoral with her and shared her luxury) (b:paktat) (r:1.38.24/66.18.9) (q:draft)
paktatna = (t:n) (w:prostitution/promiscuity/sexual immorality) (d:paktat, be promiscuous, with the noun suffix na: prostitution or sexual immorality; also used of unfaithfulness to God through idol worship) (e:~ pana piang tate ahih manin/na ~ tawh kei nong hehsak hi | you made me angry with your prostitution/a aisanna, a ~, le a guktaknate uh | their sorcery, their immorality and their thefts/numei tawh ~ i gamta kei ding hi | we must not commit sexual immorality) (s:hukna) (b:paktat) (r:28.2.4/26.16.26/66.9.21/46.10.8) (q:draft)
paktatnate = (t:n) (w:prostitutions/immoral acts) (d:paktatna, prostitution, with the plural ending te; in the verse of Jezebel, where the English has idolatry) (e:~ leh aisannate tua zahin a tam) (b:paktatna) (r:12.9.22) (q:draft)
paktatnu = (t:n) (w:female prostitute/harlot) (d:paktat, promiscuous, with nu, marking a woman) (e:A ~ a kiguaihna sum ahi a) (b:paktat) (r:5.23.18) (q:draft)
paktatpa = (t:n) (w:male prostitute) (d:paktat, promiscuous, with pa, marking a man) (e:a ~ a kiguaihna sum ahi zongin) (b:paktat) (r:5.23.18) (q:draft)
paktatsak = (t:v) (w:lead into prostitution/make unfaithful) (d:paktat, prostitute oneself, with causative sak) (e:na tapate uh ~ kha ding uh hi) (b:paktat) (r:2.34.16) (q:draft)
paktatte = (t:n) (w:prostitutes/promiscuous women) (d:paktat with the plural ending -te, usually as numei paktatte) (e:numei ~ tua sungah kisil uh hi/Numei ~ sum tawh kiguai a | prostitutes are hired with money/note mahmah numei ~ tawh na mawh uh a | you yourselves sin with prostitutes) (b:paktat) (r:11.22.38/20.23.27/26.16.33/28.4.14) (q:draft)
pakte = (t:n) (w:flowers/blossoms) (d:pak, flower, with the plural ending te; also the flower ornaments of the lampstand) (e:a nunte leh a ~ tawh a om/a ~ a pulh mangkhin oliv kung | an olive tree that has shed its blossoms/a bul akipan a ~ dongin a kiseek ahi hi | it was hammered work from its base to its blossoms) (s:paakte/pakpalhte) (b:pak) (r:2.25.34/18.15.33/4.8.4) (q:draft)
pakzaw = (t:adv) (w:all the sooner/rather quickly) (d:pak, quickly, with zaw, more or rather; follows a verb, in the verse si, die) (e:pilna ngah ngei loin si ~ ding) (b:pak) (r:18.4.21) (q:draft, low confidence)
palai = (t:n) (w:envoy/mediator/go-between/ambassador) (d:one who goes between two sides to speak for them or make peace; palai sem is to act as an envoy or mediator) (e:kilemna ding ~ semte nakpitakin kap uh hi/thukhente in ~ sem ding hi | the judges will mediate for him) (s:kamtai/tangmi) (r:23.33.7/9.2.25) (q:draft)
palai = (t:v) (w:intervene/mediate) (d:step in between two sides to settle a matter or make peace) (e:Finehas dingin hong ~ a) (r:19.106.30) (q:draft)
Palal = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Palal) (d:son of Uzai, who helped repair the wall of Jerusalem in the time of Nehemiah) (r:16.3.25)
palepa = (t:phrase) (w:man with man) (d:pa le pa, man and man; palepa mawhna is the sin of a man with a man, homosexual practice) (e:~ mawhna a bawlte) (r:54.1.10) (q:draft)
palh = (t:v) (w:bloom/blossom/flourish) (d:of flowers, open; of people, thrive like a plant in flower) (e:Gam sung tengah paakte ~ a/Thuman mi in nisuh kung bangin ~ a | the righteous flourish like a palm tree/Unok Paak bangin amaute ~ ding a | they will blossom like a lily/lo lai a paakte bangin amah ~ hi | he flourishes like the flowers of the field) (s:pak) (a:vul) (r:22.2.12/19.92.12/28.14.5/19.103.15) (q:draft)
palhin = (t:v) (w:blooming/blossoming) (d:palh, open out in bloom, with the linking ending in) (e:Israel ~ dawnkhia ding a/zingsangin ~ thaksuak kik a | in the morning it blooms and is fresh again) (b:palh) (r:23.27.6/19.90.6) (q:draft)
palhkhia = (t:v) (w:blossom/bloom/burst into bloom) (d:palh, open out in bloom, with khia, out) (e:sehnel gam lungdamin ~ ding hi/tampi takin ~ ding a | it will bloom abundantly) (s:pakkhia) (b:palh) (r:23.35.1/23.35.2) (q:draft)
palhngulh = (t:v) (w:be unfaithful to/commit adultery against) (d:break faith with a husband or wife by going with another) (e:a pasal a ~ ahi hi/a zi a ~ ahi hi | he is unfaithful to his wife/zi vak vai-in a pasal ~ a | a wife goes astray and is unfaithful to her husband) (r:41.10.12/4.5.12/41.10.11) (q:draft)
palhngulhna = (t:n) (w:unfaithfulness/adultery) (d:palhngulh, be unfaithful to, with the noun suffix na; in the verse of a people unfaithful to God) (e:gamtatnate tawh ~ a bawl uh hi) (s:angkawmna) (b:palhngulh) (r:19.106.39) (q:draft)
palhte = (t:n) (w:blooms/open flowers) (d:palh, bloom, with the plural ending te; pak palhte is flowers in bloom) (e:nisuh kungte leh pak ~ bawl hi/amaute’ pak ~ pen leivui bangin | their open flowers like dust) (s:pakpalhte) (b:palh) (r:11.6.29/23.5.24) (q:draft)
palik = (t:n) (w:officer/guard/police) (d:loanword from English police: an officer who keeps order or guards; palik bu and palik mang are officers of the guard) (e:thukhen mangte in ~ bute pai sakin/siampi liante leh biakna innpi ~ mangte kiangah | to the chief priests and the officers of the temple guard/ci-in ~ bute kiangah a gen hi | he said to the officers) (r:44.16.35/42.22.4/44.16.37) (q:draft)
palikbute = (t:n) (w:officers/police officers) (d:palik police, a loanword from English, with bu and the plural te; in Acts 16 the officers sent by the Roman magistrates) (e:Rom thukhen uliante in ~ samin/Paul in ~ kiangah | Paul said to the officers) (r:44.16.35/44.16.38/44.16.37) (q:draft)
palikmangte = (t:n) (w:officers/guard officers) (d:palik, police or guard, with mang, chief or officer, and the plural ending te; biakinncing palikmangte is the officers of the temple guard) (e:siampi liante le biakinncing ~ tawh va kiho/siampi liante, biakinncing ~, le upate kiangah | to the chief priests, the officers of the temple guard and the elders) (r:42.22.4/42.22.52) (q:draft)
palikte = (t:n) (w:guards/officers/police) (d:plural of palik, from English police; in the New Testament the temple guards and court officers) (e:~ tawh mei a awi khawm hi/Topa man dingin ~ a sawl uh hi | they sent guards to arrest the Lord/thongah ~ a va tun uh ciangin | when the officers arrived at the prison/~ in thong sungah hong khum ding hi | the officers will throw you into prison) (b:palik) (r:41.14.54/40.5.25/43.7.32/44.5.22) (q:draft)
Pallu = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Pallu) (d:son of Reuben and father of Eliab, ancestor of the Palluite clan) (r:1.46.9/4.26.8)
palsat = (t:v) (w:transgress/violate/break) (d:break a law, command or covenant) (e:ngeina kipte ~ uh a/a thuciamna ~ hi | he breaks his covenant/Pasian’ thukham bang hang ~ na hi uh hiam | why do you break the command of God/na thukhamte khempeuh a ~ khin zo uh hi | they have transgressed all your laws) (s:peel) (a:zui/mang) (r:23.24.5/27.9.11/19.55.20/40.15.3) (q:draft)
palsatin = (t:v) (w:transgressing/violating/breaking) (d:palsat, break a law or covenant, with the linking ending in: breaking it and so doing the next thing) (e:ka thukhamte ~, ka thupiaknate mang lo uh a/thukham ~ Pasian’ min na daisak uh hi | by breaking the law you dishonor the name of God/a kiciamna leh a thuciamnasa ~ | breaking his oath and his covenant/ama thuciamna ~ | breaking his covenant) (b:palsat) (r:26.20.21/5.17.2/45.2.23/26.17.18) (q:draft)
palsatkhak = (t:v) (w:break/transgress/violate) (d:palsat, break or transgress, with khak, happen to: break a promise or command, even without meaning to; na palsatkhak loh nadingun is so that you do not break it) (e:na thuciamna uh na ~ loh nadingun) (a:zuih) (r:39.2.15) (q:draft)
palsatna = (t:n) (w:transgression/rebellion/offence) (d:palsat, transgress, with the noun suffix na: the breaking of a law or command, usually in the phrase thu palsatna) (e:Ka thu ~ khempeuh panin/note’ thu ~ hong maisak lo ding hi | he will not forgive your rebellion/mawhna leh thu ~ maisak a | forgiving sin and rebellion/amau’ thu ~ hang | because of their rebellion) (s:thupalsatna/khialhna/mawhna) (b:palsat) (r:19.39.8/2.23.21/4.14.18/3.16.16) (q:draft)
palsatnate = (t:n) (w:transgressions/offenses) (d:plural of palsatna, transgression; usually in the phrase thu palsatnate, the acts by which a person breaks the law of God) (e:ka thu ~ ka thei a/ka thu ~ hong phiatkhiat sak in | blot out my transgressions/amau’ thu ~ hang | because of their transgressions) (s:thupalsatnate/mawhnate) (b:palsatna) (r:19.51.3/19.51.1/3.16.16) (q:draft)
palsatte = (t:n) (w:transgressors/those who break) (d:palsat transgress, with the plural te: those who break a command; thu palsatte is transgressors) (e:thu ~ na zia ka hilh ding a/a ~ in a kilawm bangin gim thuak ding | those who break it will suffer as they deserve/thu ~ kisusia mang khin ding a | transgressors will be utterly destroyed) (s:thupalsatte) (b:palsat) (r:19.51.13/58.2.2/19.37.38) (q:draft)
paltan = (t:v) (w:pass through/go through/cross) (d:go across a land from one side to the other) (e:Amah in Samaria gam ~ a/Sidon gam a ~ khit ciangin | after he had passed through the region of Sidon) (s:kantan) (r:43.4.4/41.7.31) (q:draft)
paltanin = (t:v) (w:pass through/go through) (d:paltan with the ending in, linking it to what follows: passing through) (e:Galile gam ~ kuamah in) (b:paltan) (r:41.9.30) (q:draft)
palte = (t:n) (w:firstfruits/first ripe ones) (d:the first of a crop to ripen, pal with the plural te; an palte is the firstfruits of grain and leenggah a palte the first ripe grapes) (e:leenggah a ~ a min hun/Topa tungah amau piak an ~ | the firstfruits of grain they give to the Lord/ama’ an lakna-ah an ~ ahi uh hi | they are the firstfruits of his harvest) (s:anpalte) (r:4.13.20/4.18.12/24.2.3) (q:draft)
Palti = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Palti) (d:name of two men: the son of Raphu, the spy sent from the tribe of Benjamin, and the son of Laish to whom Saul gave his daughter Michal, called Paltiel in the NIV) (r:4.13.9/9.25.44)
Paltiel = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Paltiel) (d:name of two men: the son of Azzan, leader of the tribe of Issachar, and the son of Laish, the husband to whom Saul gave Michal) (r:4.34.26/10.3.15)
pam = (t:n) (w:vicinity/side/surroundings/edge) (d:the place beside or close to something; a kim a pam and ka kiim ka pam mean all around) (e:thakhatin a kim a ~ en uh a/Bethani khua ~ a tun’ uh ciangin | when they reached the vicinity of Bethany/Ka kiim ka ~ enin ka khuadak a | I look all around me/kulh kongpi ~-ah paikhiatpih a | he took him aside to the city gate) (s:gei/pang) (r:41.9.8/41.13.3/42.24.50/19.142.4/10.3.27) (q:draft)
pama = (t:adv) (w:around/nearby/beside) (d:pam side or vicinity with the place ending a; usually paired with kim or kiim, a kim a pama, all around) (e:Kiim le ~ minam dangte’ kiang pan/A kim a ~ pai mi khempeuh kiangah | to all who pass by round about/na kim na ~ mi namte khempeuh | all the nations around you/Ka ~ ding mite khat kiangah | to one of those standing beside me) (s:kimkotah/kimkot) (b:pam) (r:16.5.17/25.1.12/31.1.16/27.7.16) (q:draft)
pamah = (t:prep) (w:beside/alongside/around) (d:pam, side or edge, with ah: at or along the side of something; a kiim a pamah means all around, round about) (e:A kiim a ~ a pai mi khempeuh/lam ~ hong delh khia a | he chased me off to the side of the path/Krete gam ~ pai-in | sailing along the coast of Crete/ka kiim ka ~ launa om hi | there is terror all around me) (s:geiah/kiimah) (b:pam) (r:25.1.12/44.27.8/25.3.11/19.31.13) (q:draft)
Pamfilia = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Pamphylia) (d:Roman province on the south coast of Asia Minor, between Lycia and Cilicia, visited by Paul) (r:44.14.24/44.2.10/44.27.5)
pammaih = (t:adj) (w:too precious to lose/dear/precious) (d:used with sa, feel: pammaih sa is to hold something dear, be unwilling to lose or give it up, spare it, or be zealous for it) (e:amaute ~ sa ahih manin/a khial vantungmite ~ sa loin | not sparing the angels who sinned/tuate zuakkhiat dingin ~ lua hi | they are too precious to sell/nangmah zong ~ hong sa ding ahi kei hi | he will not spare you either) (r:19.72.14/45.11.21/61.2.4/20.23.23) (q:draft)
pammaihsa = (t:v) (w:spare/hold dear/be zealous for) (d:pammaih too precious to lose, with sa feel: be unwilling to lose or give up; pammaihsa loin is without sparing) (e:Amah in amaute ~ ahih manin/Tang lai leitung zong ~ loin | not sparing the ancient world either/amah in ~ ahih ciangin | because he was zealous) (b:pammaih) (r:19.72.14/61.2.5/4.25.11) (q:draft)
pammaihsak = (t:v) (w:be zealous for/hold dear) (d:pammaih with sak, the form of sa, feel, used before bangin) (e:keima ~ bangin amah in pammaih sa a) (b:pammaih) (r:4.25.11) (q:draft)
pampaih = (t:v) (w:forsake/reject/cast aside) (d:leave aside as of no account; mite in a pampaih mite is people rejected by others, outcasts) (e:Pasian’ thu na ~ uh hi/Bang hanga sau veipi hong ~ na hi hiam | why do you forsake us for so long/mite in a ~ mite a sam dingin | to call the people whom others reject/note, ~ mi pawl, hong ci-in | calling you an outcast people) (s:nusiat/nolh) (a:saang) (r:41.7.13/25.5.20/40.9.13/24.30.17) (q:draft)
pampam = (t:see) <pampam-in>
pampam-in = (t:adv) (w:from side to side/glancing about) (d:describes eyes turned this way and that, in mit hei pampam-in) (e:a mit uh hei ~ hi tuihtuihsa-in) (r:23.3.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
pampamin = (t:adv) (w:from side to side/glancing about) (d:describes eyes turned this way and that, in mit hei pampamin) (e:a mit uh hei ~ hi tuihtuihin) (r:23.3.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
pamte = (t:n) (w:neighbours/those around) (d:pam side, vicinity, with the plural te; used in the pairs a veng a pamte and na kiim na pamte, the people living all around) (e:na kiim na ~ uh kiang panin/a veng a ~ un thatang tawh a huh uh | their neighbours helped them with their strength) (s:gamvengte/vengte/innvengte) (b:pam) (r:24.49.5/15.1.6) (q:draft)
pan = (t:prep) (w:from/out of/by way of) (d:placed after a noun to show the starting point or the way through, short form of panin) (e:Amaute khua sung ~ paikhia uh a/Han vang ~ suang kilikkhia a | the stone rolled away from the mouth of the tomb/Kongpi ~ a lut mi | the one who enters by the gate/vantung ~ lim a ngen uh hi | they asked for a sign from heaven) (s:panin) (a:dong) (r:43.4.30/42.24.2/43.10.2/42.11.16)
pan = (t:v) (d:take a stand or act as, in teci pan bear witness) (e:note’ teci ~ nading ahi hi) (r:42.21.13)
pan'pihna = (t:n) (w:support/help) (d:panpih, side with or support, with the noun suffix na) (e:nangmah ~ hong pia ta hen) (s:panpihna/huhna) (r:19.20.2) (q:draft)
pana = (t:prep) (w:from) (d:pan, from, with the linking suffix a, joining the starting point or source to the word that follows) (e:leitung ~ hong khangkhia ding/Jerusalem khua ~ Babilon khua-a kong puakkhiat | whom I sent away from Jerusalem to Babylon/Khaldea gam ~ hong pai mite | those who come from the land of the Chaldeans/lei ~ piang gah | fruit that comes from the soil) (s:panin/pan) (b:pan) (r:27.7.17/24.29.20/24.51.54/1.4.3)
pana = (t:prep) (w:within)
paneah = (t:see) <Zefenath-paneah>
pang = (t:n) (w:side) (d:the side or flank of a thing, a place or the body; lam pang after a direction word is the side facing that way) (e:biakbuk a ~ nihna lam/leitaw lam ~ adingin khuampeek sawmnih | twenty frames for the south side/na veilam ~ delhphahin lum in | lie down on your left side/biakbuk leilu lam ~ | the north side of the tabernacle) (s:lampang/gei/lang) (r:2.26.20/2.37.5/2.26.18/26.4.4/2.40.22) (q:draft)
pang = (t:v) (w:testify/bear witness) (d:take a stand as, in the fixed phrase teci pang, be a witness, testify) (e:teci na ~ ding uh hi/kote in thei-in teci ka ~ uh hi | we have seen and we testify/teci ~ dingin nasem hi a | he served in order to bear witness/kei a dingin teci a ~ hi a | they bear witness for me) (r:43.15.27/62.4.14/58.3.5/43.5.36) (q:draft)
pang = (t:v) (w:take position/take a side/stand against) (d:take up a position, in battle or for or against someone; lang khatah pang is stand against and lamah pang is be on the side of) (e:Baaltamar-ah a gualin ~ uh hi | they took up positions in line at Baal Tamar/mi khat beek hong ~ zo lo ding hi | not one will be able to stand against you/hong ~ lo hi leh | if he had not been on our side/Gibeah lang khatah ~ uh hi | they took up position against Gibeah) (r:7.20.33/5.7.24/19.124.1/7.20.30) (q:draft, low confidence)
panga = (t:prep) (w:on the side of/beside/along) (d:pang side with the suffix -a: at or on the side) (e:Arnon gun ~ om khuapite khempeuh/nisuahna lam ~ giahphualate ding khia ding uh hi | the camps on the east side shall set out/singkuang ~ kualte sungah | into the rings on the sides of the ark/nitumna lam biakbuk nung lam ~ a khuampeekte | the frames on the west side, at the rear of the tabernacle) (s:geiah) (b:pang) (r:7.11.26/2.37.5/4.10.5/2.36.32) (q:draft)
pangah = (t:adj) (w:aside/at the side/on the side) (d:pang, side, with ah, at: at or on the side of something, often after a direction word, as leitaw lam pangah, on the south side) (e:tua lam ~ thaltang thum ka lawn ding hi/biakbuk leitaw lam ~ giahphual satin | camping on the south side of the tabernacle/leilu lam kongpi lam ~ omin | being at the side of the north gate) (b:pang) (r:9.20.20/4.3.29/26.40.44)
pangbetna = (t:n) (w:discipline/chastening) (d:correction of a child, in the verse matching the rod of discipline) (e:deihtakin ~ in mihoih suaksak thei hi) (r:20.22.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
pangin = (t:v) (w:taking sides/standing against/taking position) (d:pang, take a position, with the linking ending in; lang pangin is taking the opposite side, against, and gal pangin is drawn up for battle) (e:Zeisu lang ~ a zahko uh hi/Mihingte ei lang ~ hong thawh ciangin | when people rose up against us/Babylon khua kimkotah gal ~ | taking up battle positions around Babylon/na itte lang ~ thu kikum uh hi | they plot against those you love/Kei hong ~ lampi ah na din’ lam | that you stood in the road to oppose me) (b:pang) (r:42.22.65/19.83.3/19.124.2/24.50.9/4.22.34) (q:draft)
pangin = (t:v) (w:testifying/bearing witness) (d:pang with the linking ending in, in the phrase teci pangin, acting as a witness, testifying) (e:ama ading teci ~ a kikona in/note kiangah teci ~ kong hilh uh hi | we testify and proclaim it to you/thakhatin teci ~ thu ka khen ding hi | I will be quick to testify and judge/ci-in teci ~ hih lai a tomin ka gelh | testifying so, I have written this letter briefly) (b:pang) (r:43.1.15/62.1.2/39.3.5/60.5.12) (q:draft)
pangkhat = (t:n) (w:one side) (d:pang, side, with khat, one; set against pang langkhat, the other side) (e:a ~ lama om nisuh kung/Biakbuk ~ a khuampeek a’ ding zawl nga | five bars for the frames on one side of the tabernacle/Tua inn ~ pen | one side of that building) (s:langkhat) (r:26.41.19/2.26.27/26.42.3) (q:draft)
pangkhatah = (t:adv) (w:on one side) (d:pangkhat, one side, with ah, at or on) (e:~ pi khat le alang) (b:pangkhat) (r:2.26.13) (q:draft)
pangkhawm = (t:v) (w:side with/stand with/join with) (d:pang, take a side, with khawm, together) (e:amaute zong David tawh ~ uh a/kei tawh a hong ~ na hih manun | because you have stood together with me) (s:pawlpih/panpih) (b:pang) (r:9.22.17/50.1.7) (q:draft)
pangkik = (t:v) (w:take up position again) (d:pang, take position, with kik, again; gal pangkik is to line up again for battle) (e:mun mah uhah gal ~ uh hi) (b:pang) (r:7.20.22) (q:draft)
pangpi = (t:n) (w:side/flank) (d:the side of the body, pang with pi; said of the side of Jesus pierced by the spear) (e:a khutte le a ~ zong a lak hi/a teipi tawh Jesuh’ ~ a sut leh | when he pierced the side of Jesus with his spear/Na khut zan inla ka ~ zong lawng in | reach out your hand and put it into my side/a khaphung nuai a ~ uh panin | from their sides under their wings) (b:pang) (r:43.20.20/43.19.34/43.20.27/26.1.8) (q:draft)
pangsak = (t:v) (w:deploy/station/post/appoint) (d:pang, take position, with the causative sak: make someone take up a position, as soldiers against an enemy or workers at their posts) (e:Siriate a do dingin ~ hi/Ammon mite’ lang khatah amaute ~ hi | he deployed them against the Ammonites/a innkuankuan-un ka mite ka ~ hi | I stationed my people by families/Ama langah migilo khat ~ in la | appoint a wicked man against him) (b:pang) (r:13.19.10/16.4.13/10.10.10/19.109.6) (q:draft)
pangsakkik = (t:v) (w:station again/put back in position) (d:pangsak, station, with kik, again) (e:mun ciatah ka ~ hi) (b:pangsak) (r:16.13.11) (q:draft)
pangsim = (t:v) (w:ambush/lie in wait) (d:hide and wait in order to attack someone by surprise) (e:zan-in pai un la gamlakah ~ un/amah ~ dingin mual dawn-ah | to ambush him on the hilltops/amaute in kei hong ~ uh hi | they lie in wait for me/Gibeah kiim-ah a ~ dingin mi koih uh hi | they set men around Gibeah to lie in ambush) (s:buksim) (r:7.9.32/7.20.29/7.9.25/19.59.3)
pangsim = (t:n) (w:lure/ambush) (e:a ~ mite manlangin hong pai-in | the men in ambush came quickly/Israel mite leh a ~ mite | the Israelites and the men in ambush) (r:7.20.37/7.20.38)
pangsimin = (t:v) (w:lie in wait/ambush) (d:pangsim, lie in wait for someone, with the linking ending in) (e:hong ~ kei do dingin) (b:pangsim) (r:9.22.13) (q:draft)
pangsimte = (t:n) (w:men in ambush/ambushers) (d:pangsim, ambush, with the plural te; a pangsimte, those who lie in ambush) (e:a ~ amau’ nungah om hi/a koih uh a ~ muang uh hi | they relied on the men they had set in ambush) (s:buksimte) (b:pangsim) (r:14.13.13/7.20.36) (q:draft)
pangsuk = (t:n) (w:slope) (d:pang, side, with suk, downward; mual pangsuk is a mountain slope) (e:lei niamna mun leh mual ~) (s:mualpang) (b:pang) (r:6.10.40) (q:draft)
pangtat = (t:adj) (w:adulterous/unfaithful) (d:perhaps a misprint of paktat) (e:Gilo a ~ khang mite in) (r:40.16.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
pangtatte = (t:n) (w:prostitutes) (d:in numei pangtatte, immoral women; pangtat appears to be another spelling of paktat, with the plural te) (e:mawh mite leh numei ~) (r:23.57.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
pangte = (t:n) (w:sides) (d:plural of pang, side: the sides of an object such as the altar or the lampstand) (e:a kimkotah a ~ leh a kite/biakna tau ~-a om kualte sungah | into the rings on the sides of the altar/A ~ panin hiang guk meengkhia a | six branches came out from its sides) (b:pang) (r:2.37.26/2.38.7/2.37.18) (q:draft)
pangte = (t:n) (w:those who stand/those who take a position) (d:those who take up a position: langah pangte, those who stand against someone, and teci pangte, those who bear witness) (e:Nang’ langah hong ~ ke’n kih/kei hong ~ langpang in la | oppose those who oppose me/Zeisu’ teci ~’ sisan ahi zongin | and the blood of the witnesses of Jesus/a man lopi-a teci ~ | those who bear false witness) (b:pang) (r:19.139.21/40.27.13/19.35.1/66.17.6/39.3.5) (q:draft)
pangzo = (t:v) (w:be able to stand against) (d:pang, take position for or against, with zo, be able) (e:kua hong ~ ding ahi hiam) (b:pang) (r:23.50.8) (q:draft)
panin = (t:prep) (w:from/out of) (d:placed after a noun to show the starting point, source or origin; the full form of pan) (e:khuamial ~ khuavak khenkhia hi/Efraim minam ~ Nun’ tapa Hoshea | from the tribe of Ephraim, Hoshea son of Nun/a thukpi sung ~ nang tungah kong kiko hi | out of the depths I cry to you/Eden ~ gun khat luang khia a | a river flowed out from Eden) (s:pan/akipan) (a:dong) (b:pan) (r:1.1.4/15.10.38/4.13.8/19.130.1/1.2.10)
pankhia = (t:v) (w:begin/start/set about) (d:pan, begin, with khia, out: start off a work, be the one to begin it) (e:nasep hoih a hong ~ Pasian in/a ~ masate na hih uh mah bangin | as you were the first to begin) (s:kipan) (a:tawp) (b:pan) (r:50.1.6/47.8.10) (q:draft)
pankik = (t:v) (w:take up again/declare again) (d:pan, take a stand or begin, with kik, again; teci pankik is testify again, and of a thing given up, take it up again) (e:teci ka ~ inah/ka phiatsa uh thu tu-in ~ leuleu leng | if I now take up again what I did away with) (b:pan) (r:48.5.3/48.2.18) (q:draft, low confidence)
panmun = (t:n) (w:position/place/post) (d:the place where one stands to do a duty; panmun la or len, take one’s place) (e:amau’ ~ ngei hong la uh hi/thukhenna munah ama ~ hong la a | he takes his place in the court/Siampite amau’ ~ uhah ding uh hi | the priests stood at their posts/na ~ uh la-in taang loin ding un | take up your positions and stand firm) (r:14.30.16/23.3.13/14.7.6/14.20.17) (q:draft)
panmunkip = (t:n) (w:stronghold/fortress) (d:panmun, a position or post, with kip, firm) (e:~ na bawl khin hi) (s:munkip/kulhpi) (r:19.8.2) (q:draft)
panmunkipte = (t:n) (w:strongholds/fortresses) (d:plural of panmunkip, a firm position: fortified places; gal panmunkipte are strongholds of war) (e:ama gal ~ a sia na suah khin hi) (s:kulhpite/phualpite) (b:panmunkip) (r:19.89.40) (q:draft)
panmunte = (t:n) (w:posts/positions/stations) (d:plural of panmun, the place where one stands to serve or fight: the duties of priests and Levites, and gal panmunte, defences or strongholds) (e:siampite amau’ ~ ah seh a/ka ~ uh na sukham khin hi | you have broken down our defences/a gal ~ uh ka susia hi | I have destroyed their strongholds/Levi mite phatna ~ leh nasepna | the posts of praise and service of the Levites) (b:panmun) (r:14.35.2/36.3.6/19.60.1/14.8.14) (q:draft)
panna = (t:n) (w:testimony/witness) (d:noun from pan, used in teci panna, the bearing of witness) (e:Hih thumte’ teci ~ kibang kim hi/teci khat bek’ teci ~ siksanin | on the testimony of only one witness/Johan’ teci ~ sangin a lianzaw | greater than the testimony of John/mihingte’ teci ~ a kisam ka hi kei a | I do not need human testimony) (s:tecipanna) (b:pan) (r:62.5.8/43.5.36/4.35.30/43.5.34) (q:draft)
panna = (t:n) (w:position/battle line/station) (d:noun from pan, take a stand: the place or line where fighters take their stand for battle) (e:galdona ding ~ a bawl uh hi/a ni masa ni-a a ~ mun mah uhah | in the same place where they had taken position the first day/a nung le a mai panin a ~ | the battle lines drawn up behind and in front) (s:panmun) (b:pan) (r:14.14.10/7.20.22/13.19.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
pannate = (t:n) (w:testimonies/statutes) (d:plural of panna, found only in teci pannate, the testimonies of God, what he has borne witness to as his will) (e:na teci ~ ka deih hi/Na teci ~ a tawntungin thuman hi | your statutes are always righteous/na teci ~ ka ngaihsunsun hi | I meditate on your statutes/na teci ~ ka zuih theih nadingin | so that I may obey your statutes) (s:tecipannate) (b:panna) (r:19.119.119/19.119.88/19.119.144/19.119.99) (q:draft)
pano = (t:n) (w:uncle) (d:uncle, the brother of the father; pa, father, with no, younger) (e:Saul’ ~ Ner’ tapa ahi hi/Saul’ ~ in amah leh a nasempa kiangah | the uncle of Saul said to him and his servant/Saul in a ~ kiangah | Saul said to his uncle/David’ ~ Jonathan in thu thei mi | Jonathan the uncle of David, a man of insight) (b:pa) (r:9.14.50/9.10.15/9.10.14/9.10.16/13.27.32) (q:draft)
pano = (t:n) (w:young male/male calf) (d:after an animal name, a young male, as bawng pano bull calf) (e:biak nadingin bawng ~ khat) (b:pa) (r:3.9.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
panpa = (t:n) (w:one who began) (d:pan, begin, with pa, the one who) (e:a pha nasep hong ~ in) (b:pan) (r:50.1.6) (q:draft)
panpih = (t:v) (w:side with/support/take the part of) (d:stand with someone, pan with pih together with; also join in with others and show partiality to) (e:Jew mite in zong ~ uh a/Topa in hong ~ lo hileh | if the Lord had not been on our side/Amaute in Adonijah zui-in amah ~ uh hi | they followed Adonijah and supported him/Topa in amaute ~ ding a | the Lord will take up their case) (s:pawlpih/pangkhawm/huh) (a:langpang) (b:pan) (r:44.24.9/20.23.11/19.124.1/11.1.7/20.22.23) (q:draft)
panpihin = (t:v) (w:siding with/supporting/favouring) (d:panpih, take the part of, with the linking ending in) (e:pawlkhat in Jew mite ~/simmawh bawlin, migilote’ vai ~ | despising it and favouring the plans of the wicked) (b:panpih) (r:44.14.4/18.10.3) (q:draft)
panpihna = (t:n) (w:support/upholding) (d:panpih, take the part of, with the noun suffix na: the taking of someone’s side, upholding of a cause) (e:a thuak mite’ thu a ~) (s:pan'pihna/huhna) (b:panpih) (r:19.140.12) (q:draft)
panpihpa = (t:n) (w:defender/supporter) (d:panpih, side with, with pa, the one who; in the verse, one who pleads for others at the gate) (e:kongtual sungah mi a ~ thang siahin) (s:hupa) (b:panpih) (r:23.29.20) (q:draft)
pansa = (t:todo) (q:draft, in pansa kikin with amaute as object; the single verse does not make the meaning clear)
pansimna = (t:n) (w:ambush/hiding place) (d:a lying in wait and the place of it; pansim, lie in wait, with the noun suffix na) (e:a ~ panun dingto uh hi/galte le ~ a tuamtuamte tawh hong kipelhsak hi | he kept us from enemies and from every kind of ambush) (s:buksimna) (r:7.9.35/15.8.31) (q:draft)
pantah = (t:v) (w:bring up/rear/raise/nurture) (d:raise a child or a young animal) (e:A no dang khat ~ leuleu a/taii-in hilhin ~ un | bring them up with discipline and teaching) (s:khoi) (r:26.19.5/49.6.4) (q:draft)
panun = (t:prep) (w:from/out of) (d:pan, from, with the plural ending un, used when those spoken of are many; placed after the noun) (e:a phual kip ~ liingin hong paikhia uh hi/a inn ~ gamlapi-ah len khia ding hi | it will sweep them far away from their home/a haksakna khempeuh ~ amaute honkhia hi | he delivers them from all their troubles/na gamtatsiatna khempeuh ~ khawl un | turn away from all your evil deeds) (s:panin/pan) (b:pan) (r:10.22.46/20.20.11/18.27.21/19.34.17/26.18.30) (q:draft)
pap = (t:v) (w:swamp/sweep over/cover) (d:said of waves covering a boat) (e:tui kilok-in gunkuang a ~ hi) (r:40.8.24) (q:draft, low confidence)
papi = (t:n) (w:man/grown man/men) (d:grown men as a group, paired with nupi, women) (e:~, nupi leh naupangte i susia hi/nupi sagih in ~ khat nei khawm ding uh | seven women will take hold of one man/a dawng kik ~, nupi-a kipan mi khempeuh | all the people, men and women, who answered) (s:pasal) (a:nupi) (b:pa) (r:5.3.6/24.44.15/23.4.1/24.44.20) (q:draft)
papite = (t:n) (w:grown men/older men/married men) (d:plural form of papi, a grown or married man; set beside nupite, married women, and beside tangvalte, young men, where English has old men) (e:tangvalte leh ~ zong a nuam ding uh hi/~ le nupite, khanghamte le khangnote | men and women, old and young/kei hong zahtakna limin ~ na ding uh hi | the old men rose to their feet out of respect for me/~ in a tapate’ sa ne-in | fathers will eat the flesh of their sons) (a:nupite) (b:papi) (r:24.31.13/24.6.11/24.51.22/18.29.8/26.5.10) (q:draft)
