Parsin = (t:name) (w:Parsin) (d:last word of the writing on the wall at the feast of Belshazzar, explained by Daniel as divided; the NIV has Peres in the explanation) (r:27.5.25/27.5.28)
PARSIN = (t:n) (w:Parsin/Peres) (d:word of the writing on the wall at the feast of Belshazzar, written in capitals and explained as your kingdom is divided) (e:MENE, MENE, TEKEL, ~) (r:27.5.25/27.5.28) (q:draft)
Parthia = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Parthia) (d:land south-east of the Caspian Sea; Parthians were among those who heard the apostles at Pentecost) (r:44.2.9)
Paruah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Paruah) (d:father of Jehoshaphat, the district governor of Solomon in Issachar) (r:11.4.17)
Parvaim = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Parvaim) (d:place from which the gold used in the temple of Solomon came; its location is not known) (r:14.3.6)
Pasak = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Pasak) (d:son of Japhlet, of the tribe of Asher) (r:13.7.33)
pasal = (t:n) (w:man) (d:a man, an adult male person, as distinct from numei, a woman) (e:~ in a nu a pa nusia-in/Kum za a pha ~ khat | a man a hundred years old/numei in ~ pan piang ahi hi | woman came from man) (s:mipa) (a:numei) (r:41.10.7/1.17.17/46.11.8)
pasal = (t:n) (w:male) (e:~ leh numei a piangsak hi/a tungsiah ~ peuhmah tulguk leh zanih | every male from there upward, six thousand two hundred/Note’ lak panin ~ peuhmah vun ki-at ding hi | every male among you shall be circumcised/sila numei le sila ~ | female and male slaves) (a:numei) (r:41.10.6/1.1.27/4.3.34/1.17.10/3.25.44)
pasalin = (t:n) (w:as husband) (d:pasal, man or husband, with in, as: pasalin nei is have as husband) (e:thu um lo mi khat ~ a neih leh) (b:pasal) (r:46.7.13) (q:draft)
pasalkhat = (t:n) (w:a man/a husband) (d:pasal, man, with khat, one) (e:~ tawh kiteng a) (r:4.30.6) (q:draft)
pasalnei = (t:v) (w:take a husband/be married) (d:pasal man, husband, with nei have, said of a woman; paired with zinei, take a wife; pasalnei thak is a bride) (e:zinei ~ cih om lo ding/zinei thakte, ~ thakte’ awte | the voices of bridegrooms and brides) (r:40.22.30/24.16.9) (q:draft)
pasalno = (t:n) (w:boy/male child) (d:pasal, male, with no, young) (e:kum nih nuaisiah ~ khempeuh a thatsak hi) (s:naupangpa) (a:numeino) (b:pasal) (r:40.2.16) (q:draft)
Pasalpa = (t:n) (w:man) (d:pasal man, male, with pa marking a man; Pasalpa Moses is the man Moses) (e:~ Moses lungnem mahmah a) (r:4.12.3) (q:draft)
pasalte = (t:n) (w:husbands) (d:plural of pasal in the sense of husband, set beside zite, wives) (e:na ~ uh ukna na mang un/a ~ uh ukna khempeuh mang ta uh hen | let them submit to their husbands in everything/~ hong ukna na mang un | submit to the rule of your husbands) (a:zite) (b:pasal) (r:49.5.22/49.5.25/49.5.24/51.3.18) (q:draft)
pasalte = (t:n) (w:men/males) (d:nasem pasalte are male servants) (e:nasem numei leh nasem ~ tung nangawn-ah/Grik numeite leh ~ in thu a um uh hi | Greek women and men believed/sila numei le sila ~ la-in Abraham pia a | he took female and male slaves and gave them to Abraham/nau ~ nungtasak uh hi | they let the baby boys live) (a:numeite) (b:pasal) (r:29.2.29/44.17.12/1.20.14/2.1.17) (q:draft)
Pasdammim = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Pas Dammim) (d:place in Judah where David and his mighty men stood against the Philistines, called Ephes Dammim in 1 Samuel) (r:13.11.13)
Pasdammin = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Pas Dammim) (d:place in Judah where David and his mighty men stood against the Philistines; another spelling of Pasdammim) (r:13.11.13)
Paseah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Paseah) (d:name of several men, among them a son of Eshton of Judah and the father of Joiada who repaired the Jeshanah Gate; also the head of a family of temple servants) (r:13.4.12/16.3.6)
Pashhur = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Pashhur) (d:name of several men, among them the priest, son of Immer, who had Jeremiah beaten and put in the stocks, and the head of a priestly family) (r:24.20.1/13.9.12)
pasian = (t:n) (w:god) (d:a god or deity other than the one God, written without a capital; pasian dang is another god) (e:Keimah longal ~ dang na nei kei ding/amaute kiangah gamdang ~ om lo hi | no foreign god was with them/Tuate ~ hi lo hi | they are not gods/Note lakah ~ dang om lo ding a | there shall be no other god among you) (r:2.20.3/5.32.12/24.16.20/19.81.9)
Pasian = (t:n) (w:God) (d:the one true God, written with a capital; Topa Pasian is the Lord God) (e:~ in vantung leh leitung a piangsak hi/~ in hih thute khempeuh gen a | God spoke all these words/Tua ciangin ~ in Noah’ kiangah | then God said to Noah/Topa ~ in ka bil hong honsak a | the Lord God has opened my ear) (r:1.1.1/41.11.22/2.20.1/1.8.15/23.50.5)
PASIAN = (t:n) (w:God) (d:Pasian written in capitals after Topa: Topa PASIAN, Sovereign Lord in the NIV, where older English Bibles print Lord GOD) (e:Topa ~ aw, bang hong pia ding/Topa ~ in minam khempeuh mai-ah | the Sovereign Lord, before all nations) (r:1.15.2/2.23.17/23.61.11) (q:draft)
pasiannu = (t:n) (w:goddess) (d:pasian, god, with nu, marking a female) (e:eite ~ a kosia lo hih mite) (s:nusian) (b:pasian) (r:44.19.37) (q:draft)
pasiante = (t:n) (w:gods) (d:pasian, god, with the plural te: gods, also of household gods and idols) (e:inn sung ~ gu hi/Note kiim-a om mite’ ~ | the gods of the peoples around you/Note in komau’ ~ na hi uh hi | you are our gods) (b:pasian) (r:5.32.37/1.31.19/5.6.14/23.42.17)
pat = (t:v) (w:begin/start) (d:form of pan, begin, used before ciangin, lai and theih; follows another verb for begin to) (e:khua a vak ~ lai takin/kitot nading a ~ ciangin | when they start a quarrel/nasep nading hong ~ khit ahih mah bangin | just as he had already begun the work/ka nuntakna uh ka thak ~ theih nading uh | so that we can begin our life anew) (s:kipat) (r:40.28.1/20.18.6/47.8.6/15.9.8) (q:draft)
pata = (t:n) (w:father and son/father and child) (d:pa, father, with ta, child; pata bang is like father and son) (e:nasepna-ah ~ bang ka hih manun) (b:pa) (r:50.2.22) (q:draft)
Patara = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Patara) (d:port city of Lycia in Asia Minor where Paul changed ships on his way to Jerusalem) (r:44.21.1)
patau = (t:v) (w:be troubled/be alarmed/be dismayed) (d:be greatly disturbed in mind by fear, worry or anger; patau kohna is an alarm, a warning call) (e:A lungsim ~ lua mahmah ahih manin/Siria kumpipa nakpi takin ~ hi | the king of Aram was greatly troubled/Israel mite aw, ~ kei un | do not be dismayed, people of Israel/mi khempeuh ~-in guah lakah liingin tu uh hi | all the people sat trembling in the rain, greatly distressed) (s:lungmang/lungkham) (r:27.2.1/12.6.11/24.30.10/15.10.9) (q:draft)
patauh = (t:v) (w:be alarmed/be dismayed) (d:form of patau used before huai and nading: patauh huai, alarming, shocking) (e:bangmah ~ nading om lo hi/A dipkuat huai, a ~ huai thu khat | a horrible and shocking thing) (b:patau) (r:52.5.3/24.5.30) (q:draft)
patauhhuai = (t:adj) (w:shocking/alarming) (d:patau, be alarmed, with huai, causing such a feeling) (e:a ~ thu khat gam sungah) (r:24.5.30) (q:draft)
patauhna = (t:n) (w:alarm/panic/terror) (d:state of being alarmed and thrown into confusion) (e:kumpi inn sungah ~ om hi/Launa leh ~ aw ka za a | I hear a cry of fear and terror/sun ciangin gal ~ aw za ta hen | let him hear a battle alarm at noon) (s:launa/lauthawngna) (a:lungnopna/lungmuanna) (b:patauh) (r:34.2.6/24.30.5/24.20.16) (q:draft)
pataukoh = (t:v) (w:sound the alarm/signal) (d:patau, alarm, with koh, call out: give the alarm call, as with trumpets in war) (e:leh ~ nadingin peengkulte) (r:4.31.6) (q:draft)
pataukohna = (t:n) (w:alarm/alarm call) (d:a loud signal of danger or war, sounded on a trumpet) (e:mual siangtho tungah ~ tum un/Beth-aven khua-ah ~ gingsak un | sound the alarm in Beth Aven/peengkulte tawh ~ aw na gingsak ding uh | you shall sound the alarm with the trumpets/Amah in ~ za napi-in don lo | he heard the alarm but did not heed it) (s:theihsakna) (b:pataukoh) (r:29.2.1/4.10.9/28.5.8/26.33.5) (q:draft)
pataulua = (t:v) (w:be greatly troubled/be very alarmed) (d:patau, be troubled, with lua, very much) (e:A lungsim ~ mahmah ahih manin) (b:patau) (r:27.2.1) (q:draft)
patausak = (t:v) (w:alarm/frighten/disturb) (d:cause to be alarmed or to panic; patau with the causative sak) (e:kuamah in ~ nawn lo ding hi/saklam panin thupiang in amah ~ ding a | reports from the north will alarm him/a hong ~ mahmah hi | they disturbed me greatly) (s:lausak) (b:patau) (r:33.4.4/27.11.44/27.7.15) (q:draft)
pate = (t:n) (w:fathers/ancestors/parents) (d:pa, father, with the plural te: fathers; pu leh pate or pute pate means ancestors, and nu leh pate means parents) (e:Na pu na ~’ phuhsa gi-suang/~ in tate’ minthan’na ahi hi | parents are the pride of their children/A nu leh ~ in kum simin | every year his parents/Na pute na ~ un gampa lakah | your ancestors, in the wilderness) (s:pulepate) (a:nute) (b:pa) (r:20.22.28/20.30.11/20.17.6/42.2.41/43.6.49) (q:draft)
Pathahiah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Pethahiah) (d:one of the Levites who led the people in praise and confession in the time of Nehemiah) (r:16.9.5)
Pathros = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Pathros/Upper Egypt) (d:Upper Egypt, the southern part of the land of Egypt) (r:23.11.11/26.29.14)
Pathru = (t:name) (c:male/people) (w:Pathrusim/Pathrusites) (d:people descended from Mizraim son of Ham, the inhabitants of Pathros in Upper Egypt) (r:1.10.14)
Pathrus = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Pathrusite/Pathrusites) (d:people descended from Mizraim son of Ham, the inhabitants of Pathros in Upper Egypt) (r:13.1.12)
patkhaute = (t:n) (w:threads/strings) (d:pat, cotton, with khau, cord, and the plural te: cotton thread, a strand of tow) (e:~ in mei a suk khak ciangin) (r:7.16.9) (q:draft)
patkhiat = (t:v) (w:begin/lead off/start) (d:pat, begin, with khiat, out; form of patkhia used before ding: start off a prayer or song for others to follow) (e:koh thungetna ~ ding a makai Asaf) (b:pat) (r:16.11.17) (q:draft)
patkhit = (t:v) (w:have begun) (d:pat, begin, with khit, finished; patkhit ciangin is after beginning) (e:Kha Siangtho tawh na ~ uh ciangin) (r:48.3.3) (q:draft)
patlom = (t:n) (w:tinder/tow) (d:a bunch of cotton or fibre that catches fire easily; pat, cotton, with lom, bundle) (e:mipa pen ~ tawh kibang ding a) (r:23.1.31) (q:draft)
Patmos = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Patmos) (d:small island in the Aegean Sea where John was when he received the Revelation) (r:66.1.9)
patna = (t:n) (w:beginning/start) (d:pat, begin, with the noun suffix na: the beginning; often in a patna pan a tawpna dong, from beginning to end) (e:a ~ pan a tawpna dong/a ~ panin a ban banin gen a | he told it in order from the beginning/a ~ panin a tawp dongin upna hang bek | by faith alone from first to last) (s:kipatna/cilna) (a:tawpna/beina) (b:pat) (r:14.16.11/9.3.12/44.11.4/45.1.17) (q:draft)
patpuan = (t:n) (w:linen/cotton cloth) (d:pat, cotton, with puan, cloth; the Bible uses it where English has linen) (e:~ dialkaih khat na lei khit ciangin/~ a gante lungkham ding uh hi | the weavers of linen will lose heart) (s:saihadial) (r:24.13.1/23.19.9) (q:draft)
Patrobas = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Patrobas) (d:Christian in Rome to whom Paul sends greetings) (r:45.16.14)
patsa = (t:adj) (w:begun/already started) (d:pat, begin, with sa, already done; a patsa, what has been begun) (e:na ~ uh thu a bei dongin/Judah mite in a ~ uh hih banga | as the Jews had begun/Mi khatpeuh in a ~ nasep maban | work that someone else has already begun) (b:pat) (r:47.8.11/17.9.23/45.15.20) (q:draft)
pattahsa = (t:v) (w:reared/brought up) (d:pattah, bring up or nurture a child, with sa marking the action as done: whom one has reared) (e:Ka ~ tapate in kei hong lehdo) (r:23.1.2) (q:draft)
patun = (t:v) (d:pat, begin, with the ending un; found in the pair na pian’ na patun, from birth and beginning, that is by birth) (e:ka pian’ ka ~ Jew mi ka hi/na pian’ na ~ Gentail mi ahi note | you who are Gentiles by birth) (b:pat) (r:48.2.15/49.2.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
pau = (t:n) (w:language/speech/word) (d:the language a people speaks, or what a person says; kam pau is speech or language, and pau lamdang is speaking in tongues) (e:a innkuan, a kam ~, a leitang/amau’ kam ~ ciat zangin | each using their own language/Amaute’ ~ kuamah in thei lo a | no one understands their speech/vantung mite’ ~ nangawn ka pautheih hangin | though I can speak even the language of angels) (s:kampau) (r:1.10.20/1.10.5/46.14.2/46.13.1)
Pau = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Pau) (d:city of Hadad, one of the kings who reigned in Edom) (r:1.36.39) (q:draft)
paubaan = (t:v) (w:be at fault/be blameworthy) (d:form of paubaang used before na; paubaan’na is fault or blame, and paubaan’na om lo is blameless) (e:Amau gamtatna-ah ~’na om lo a/zawng napi-in ~ neih lohna hoihzaw hi | it is better to be poor and without fault/~ nading bangmah om het lo hi | there was nothing at all to blame/ka ~ hetlohna hong mu ding hi | he will see that I am without fault) (r:19.119.1/19.101.6/20.28.6/52.2.10/18.31.6) (q:draft)
paubaang = (t:v) (w:be free from/without)
paubaang = (t:v) (w:keep away from/stay away from)
paubaang = (t:v) (w:blame) (d:find fault with or hold to blame; mostly with lo or kei, not to be blamed, blameless) (e:~ lo/hoih takin gamta in la, ~ kei in | walk faithfully and be blameless/Note na ~ kei uh hi | you are not to blame/ka ~ kei ding uh hi | we will not be to blame/Topa in ~ lote’ ni thei a | the Lord knows the days of the blameless) (s:genbaang/mawhsak) (a:phat) (r:18.2.3/19.37.18/1.17.1/12.10.9/6.2.17)
paubaang lo = (t:adj) (w:blameless) (d:paubaang, blame, with the negative lo: not to be blamed, without fault; of the heart, wholly devoted) (e:A ~, a thutang, Pasian zahtakin/Asa’ lungsim ~ hi | Asa’s heart was blameless/kei dikin ~ napi hong nuihsan uh hi | though I am righteous and blameless they laugh at me) (b:paubaang) (r:18.2.3/18.4.6/14.15.17/18.12.4)
paubaanna = (t:n) (w:fault/blame/defect/blemish) (d:something to find fault with; paubaanna om lo is blameless or without defect) (e:~ a om kei leh sem thei pan/~ a om lo bawngtal khat | a young bull without defect/Amaute ~ a om loh nadingin | so that they may be without blame/~ mahmah ka nei kei hi | I had no fault at all) (s:pauban/paubanna/sitbaanna/kawkbaanna) (b:paubaan) (r:54.3.10/26.46.6/54.5.7/50.3.6) (q:draft)
pauban = (t:n) (w:blemish/defect/fault) (d:a flaw in body or character, mostly in the form pauban’na and with a negative: without blemish, blameless) (e:ama tungah ~’na om lo hi/zawng napi-a ~’ neih lohna hoihzaw hi | it is better to be poor and without fault/~’na a om lo tuuno guk leh tuutal khat | six lambs and a ram without defect) (s:paubaanna/paubanna/sitbaanna/sit) (r:10.14.25/20.28.6/26.46.4) (q:draft)
paubang = (t:adj) (w:blameless) (d:used with lo or kei: paubang lo is blameless, not to be blamed; of the heart, wholly devoted) (e:khang-ah ~ lo hi/Note na ~ kei uh hi | you are not to blame/a lungsim a ~ lo mite’ tangin | on behalf of those whose hearts are wholly his) (r:1.6.9/12.10.9/14.16.9)
paubanna = (t:n) (w:blemish/defect) (d:pauban, blemish, with the noun suffix na; with om lo, without defect) (e:~ a om lo bawngtal khat/~ a om lo keeltal khat | a male goat without defect) (s:paubaanna/pauban/sitbaanna) (b:pauban) (r:26.43.23/26.43.25) (q:draft)
paudang = (t:n) (w:foreign language/strange tongue) (d:pau, language, with dang, other) (e:innkuanpihte ~ a zang mite kiang) (s:kamtuam) (r:19.114.1) (q:draft)
paukha = (t:v) (w:speak rashly/blurt out) (d:pau, speak, with kha, happen to: say something without meaning to) (e:Thakhatin kamguh a ~ Moses in) (r:19.106.32) (q:draft)
paukhia = (t:v) (w:speak out/speak up/utter) (d:pau, speak, with khia, out: break silence and say something aloud) (e:Tua ciangin ka ~ a/Vanglian, Topa Pasian hong ~ a | the Mighty One, God the Lord, speaks/a teen’na siangtho panin hong ~ ding hi | he will speak out from his holy dwelling/lungsim sunga a om bangbang a hong ~ uh | they speak out whatever is in the heart) (s:genkhia/pulakkhia) (a:daih) (b:pau) (r:19.39.3/19.50.1/24.25.30/42.6.45) (q:draft)
paukhial = (t:v) (w:blaspheme/speak wrongly) (d:pau, speak, with khial, wrongly; in the verse, against God) (e:Pasian’ tungah a ~ zo hi) (s:kosia/gensia) (r:40.26.65) (q:draft)
paukhialhna = (t:n) (w:blasphemy) (d:pau, speak, with khialh, go wrong, and the noun suffix na; wrong speaking, in the verses speaking against God) (e:Pasian tungah ~ min a dim/Pasian’ tungah a ~ na zazo uh hi | you have heard his blasphemy against God) (s:gensiatna) (r:66.17.3/40.26.65/41.14.64) (q:draft)
paukhiat = (t:v) (w:utter/speak out/say aloud) (d:form of paukhia, speak out, used before words such as ma-in and ciangin) (e:paunak thuhilhnate a ~ ciangin/kam khat bek nangawn ka ~ ma-in | before I utter even a single word) (s:genkhiat) (b:paukhia) (r:20.26.9/19.139.4) (q:draft)
paukhiatna = (t:n) (w:utterance/speaking) (d:paukhiat, speak out, with the noun suffix na; the act of speaking a word aloud) (e:A kilawm hun-a kammal khat ~ in/a nungta Pasian a ~ awging za-in | hearing the voice of the living God speaking) (b:paukhiat) (r:20.25.11/5.5.26) (q:draft)
Paul = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Paul) (d:apostle to the Gentiles, earlier called Saul of Tarsus, who wrote many of the New Testament letters) (r:44.17.33/46.16.21) (q:draft)
paulam = (t:n) (w:pretext/excuse) (d:a reason put forward to cover what one wants to do; paulam zong is to look for an excuse) (e:~ zonna-in nei kei unla) (s:paulap) (r:48.5.13) (q:draft)
paulamin = (t:prep) (w:in the name of/on account of/with reference to) (d:placed after a noun: naming or appealing to that person or thing as the ground for what is said or done) (e:Topa ~ note thu kong pia uh hi/note ~ hehpihna ka phat niloh a | I never stop giving thanks for you/min ~ zuauthu gen na hih manin | because you have told lies in the name/Pasian’ kamsangte lai ~ thu hilhin | teaching from the writings of the prophets) (b:paulam) (r:52.5.27/49.1.16/38.13.3/44.28.23) (q:draft, low confidence)
paulap = (t:n) (w:pretext/excuse/occasion) (d:a reason looked for in order to do or to avoid something; paulap zong is to look for an excuse) (e:Filistia mite tungah ~ a zong ahi hi/~ zong ciat uh hi | each of them looked for an excuse/a ~ ding uh bangmah om nawn lo hi | they no longer have any excuse/~ khatpeuh na zong uh hi | you look for some pretext) (s:paulam) (r:7.14.4/42.14.18/43.15.22/18.19.28) (q:draft)
Paulus = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Paulus) (d:Sergius Paulus, the Roman proconsul of Cyprus who sent for Barnabas and Saul to hear the word of God) (r:44.13.7)
paumawl = (t:adj) (w:hardly able to talk/speech-impaired) (d:pau, speak, with mawl, dull: speaking with difficulty) (e:bengngong, ~ mi khat) (r:41.7.32) (q:draft)
pauna = (t:n) (w:speech/words/speaking) (d:pau, speak, with the noun suffix na: what a person says, or the act of speaking) (e:~ leh kammal om lo a/na ~ khempeuh in na mawhna hong langsak | everything you say shows your guilt/amau’ ~ zaknophuai semsem hi | their speech is more and more pleasant to hear/amau muk tawh a ~ thu hangin | because of the words of their lips) (s:kampau/thugenna/genna) (b:pau) (r:19.19.3/18.15.6/20.16.23/19.59.12) (q:draft)
paunak = (t:n) (w:proverb/saying/byword) (d:a short wise saying handed down among a people; also a person or nation that others make a byword; Paunak is the name of the book of Proverbs) (e:Amah in ~ tul thum zong genkhia/Taang-ate’ ~ in | as the old saying goes/kei tungah hih ~ hong bulh uh a | they have made me a byword/a cikzet-huai, ~, leh ciamnuihna na suak ding uh | you will become a horror, a byword and a laughingstock) (r:11.4.32/18.17.6/9.24.13/5.28.37) (q:draft)
paunakte = (t:n) (w:proverbs/sayings) (d:paunak, proverb, with the plural te) (e:Israel kumpi Solomon’ ~/~ leh thugentehnate thei-in | understanding proverbs and parables/Amah in ~, lim takin sin a | he studied proverbs carefully) (b:paunak) (r:20.1.1/20.1.6/21.12.9) (q:draft)
paunam = (t:n) (w:language/language group) (d:pau, language, with nam, kind: a language, or the people who speak one language; paunam tuamtuamte is people of every language) (e:minam tuamtuamte leh ~ tuamtuamte khempeuh tungah/mi khat kiangah ~ tampi gen theihna thu | to another the ability to speak many kinds of languages/minam tuamtuamte, ~ tuamtuamte khempeuh in | all peoples of every language) (s:kampau/pau) (r:27.6.25/27.4.1/46.12.10/27.7.14) (q:draft)
paunasate = (t:n) (w:things said/words spoken) (d:pau, speak, with the noun suffix na, sa for what is already done, and the plural te: the things one has said) (e:ka ~ khempeuh hangin ka maizum a) (s:gensate) (r:18.42.6) (q:draft)
paunate = (t:n) (w:words/utterances) (d:pauna, speech, with the plural te: the things a person says) (e:kong ~ hong ngai in la/na kiphatsak ~ khempeuh a vekin ka za | I have heard all your boastful words/na kam ~ uh khauh mahmah hi | your words have been very harsh/a kisaktheih ~ uh ka za khin hi | I have heard their boastful words) (s:kammalte/thugente/gennate) (b:pauna) (r:19.5.1/39.3.13/26.35.13/36.2.8) (q:draft)
paupah = (t:v) (w:begin to speak/speak at once) (d:pau, speak, with pah, straight away) (e:zong hong tuto-in hong ~ hi/Amaute in pau lamdang hong ~ uh a | they at once began to speak in tongues) (r:42.7.15/44.19.6) (q:draft)
paupakna = (t:n) (w:rash talk/hasty speech) (d:speaking out without thought; pau, speak, with pak, hastily, and the noun suffix na) (e:migilote’ ~ in thusia tawh kizom hi) (r:20.15.28) (q:draft, low confidence)
paupau = (t:v) (w:keep talking/babble/talk on) (d:pau, speak, said twice: talk on and on, often with mawk or pheng, without thought) (e:Job aw, mawk ~ kei in/bangtan vei ~ ding na hi hiam | how long will you keep on talking/Thu ngaihsun lo-a pheng ~ mipa sangin | than a man who talks on without thinking/thu thei loin a mot ~ mihaite | foolish people who talk on in ignorance) (r:18.15.2/20.29.20/18.8.2/60.2.15) (q:draft)
paupaute = (t:n) (w:talkers/those who talk on) (d:paupau, keep talking, with te, those who: kihisak-a paupaute, those who talk on proudly) (e:kihisak-a kam ~ buaina ding a zongzong) (b:paupau) (r:20.17.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
paupeeng = (t:adj) (w:stubborn/obstinate) (d:refusing to listen or give way; said together with lungsim khauh, hard of heart) (e:lungsim uh khauhin ~ uh hi) (s:paupeng/lungkhauh/genhak) (r:26.2.4) (q:draft)
paupeengin = (t:adj) (w:stubborn/obstinate) (d:paupeeng with the ending in, linking it to what follows: being stubborn) (e:Note pen ~ na ngawng uh) (s:lungkhauhin) (b:paupeeng) (r:23.48.4) (q:draft)
paupeengsak = (t:v) (w:make stubborn/harden) (d:paupeeng, be stubborn or obstinate, with the causative sak) (e:a paupeensak nopte ~ hi/a lungsim khauhsakin, amah ~ hi | he hardened his spirit and made him obstinate) (s:paupeensak/lungkhauhsak/khauhsak) (r:45.9.18/5.2.30) (q:draft)
paupeensak = (t:v) (w:harden/make stubborn) (d:paupeeng, stubborn, with causative sak; written paupeengsak later in the same verse) (e:a ~ nopte paupeengsak hi) (s:paupeengsak/lungkhauhsak) (r:45.9.18) (q:draft)
paupeng = (t:adj) (w:stubborn/obstinate/contentious) (d:of people who will not listen or give way) (e:a lungsim uh khauhin ~ uh hi/Note pen ~-in, na ngawng uh sik thagui bang | you are stubborn, your neck like an iron sinew/~ lungsim mi, thuman thutak a ngai lo mi | a stubborn-hearted person who does not heed the truth) (s:paupeeng/lungkhauh/genhak) (r:26.2.4/45.2.8/23.48.4) (q:draft)
paupih = (t:v) (w:speak to/say to) (d:pau, speak, with pih, to or with: say something to someone, or with ngam and a negative, dare to speak against) (e:kam khat beek a ~ ngam kei/Mi khatpeuh in hong ~ leh | if anyone says anything to you/Jesuh in kam khat beek ~ lo hi | Jesus did not say a word to her/a ~ ngam kuamah om lo hi | no one dared to say a word against them) (s:hopih/genpih) (b:pau) (r:18.2.13/40.21.3/40.15.23/6.10.21) (q:draft)
pausak = (t:v) (w:let speak/make speak/allow to speak) (d:pau, speak, with the causative sak: allow someone to speak, or make someone able to speak) (e:kam khat beek a ~ kei hi/tu-a khatvei bek hong ~ lai in | let me speak just once more/pau thei lote a ~ thei zo hi | he can even make the mute speak/kong ~ thei kik ding a | I will make you able to speak again) (s:gensak) (b:pau) (r:42.4.41/41.7.37/7.6.39/26.3.27) (q:draft)
pausia = (t:n) (w:profane talk/evil speech) (d:pau, speak, with sia, bad; pausia gen is to speak profanely) (e:~ a gen thei mi) (s:kamsia) (r:54.1.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
paute = (t:n) (w:languages/tongues/words) (d:pau, language or word, with the plural te: languages, tongues, or the words someone speaks) (e:tua ~ a khiatna gen theihna/Josef in amau’ ~ a tel lam | that Joseph understood their words/amau ~ a khiatna a gen theih nading uh | so that they can interpret what they say) (b:pau) (r:46.12.10/1.42.23/46.14.13) (q:draft)
paute = (t:n) (w:talkers/those who speak) (d:pau, speak, with te, those who: people who talk; pau lamdang a paute is those who speak in tongues) (e:Kam tam ~, tampi khial a/pau lamdang a ~ sangin | than those who speak in tongues/tua banga mihai ~ tawh kikhawl kei in | do not keep company with such foolish talkers/a hai ~ in lungkhamna tuak hi | those who talk foolishly come to grief) (r:20.10.19/20.20.19/46.14.5/20.10.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
pauthei = (t:v) (w:be able to speak/can talk) (d:pau, speak, with thei, be able; pauthei lo means mute, unable to speak) (e:Zekhariah hong ~ kik a, Pasian a phat hi/nuamtakin a ~ hi | he could speak plainly/Bengngong leh ~ lo dawi aw | you deaf and mute spirit/dawi a veina hangin a ~ lo mi khat | a man who could not speak because of a demon) (b:pau) (r:42.1.64/41.9.25/41.7.35/40.9.32) (q:draft)
pautheih = (t:v) (w:be able to speak/can speak) (d:form of pauthei, be able to speak, used before words such as ding, nading and hangin) (e:pau lamdang na ~ ding uh/vantung mite’ pau nangawn ka ~ hangin | though I can speak even the language of angels/kam khel nono a ~ nading | so that it could speak boastful words/pau lamdang ~ siamnate a om hangin | though there are gifts of speaking in tongues) (b:pauthei) (r:46.14.5/46.13.1/66.13.5/46.13.8) (q:draft)
pautheikik = (t:v) (w:be able to speak again) (d:pauthei, be able to speak, with kik, again) (e:tua mipa hong ~ pah hi) (b:pauthei) (r:40.9.33) (q:draft)
pautheilote = (t:n) (w:the mute/the dumb) (d:pau thei lo, not able to speak, with the plural te: people who cannot speak) (e:Mi ~ a pau thei uh hi/khezawte, mittawte, mi ~, mi cingtak lote | the lame, the blind, the mute, the crippled) (r:40.15.31/40.15.30) (q:draft)
pautuam = (t:n) (w:tongue/unknown tongue) (d:speech in another, unknown language, speaking in tongues; mostly as pautuam dang) (e:pawlpi lakah ~ dang tawh/keimah in ~ dang gen thei ka hih ciangin | because I can speak in other tongues/~ tampi gen theite ahi uh hiam | are they able to speak in many tongues) (s:kamtuam) (r:46.14.19/46.13.8/46.14.18/46.12.30) (q:draft)
pauzaw = (t:v) (w:speak rather/speak instead) (d:pau, speak, with zaw, more or rather: prefer to speak one thing instead of another) (e:kammal nga bek ka ~ ding hi/Pasian tungah lungdamkohna kam na ~ un | speak words of thanksgiving to God instead) (s:genzaw) (b:pau) (r:46.14.19/49.5.4) (q:draft)
pawh = (t:part) (w:if only/oh that) (d:sentence-final word after leng or leh, expressing a strong wish) (e:Vakhu bangin kha nei hi leng ~/ka deih bangin Israel gamta leh ~ | if only Israel would walk as I wish/ka mitte khitui nak hi tazen leh ~ | oh that my eyes were a fountain of tears) (r:19.55.6/19.81.13/24.9.1) (q:draft)
pawi = (t:n) (w:festival/feast) (d:a feast or festival kept with eating and rejoicing; pawi bawl and pawi kham both mean hold a feast, and pawi hun is festival time) (e:keimah adingin ~ na bawl ding uh hi/mi khempeuh kaikhawmin ~ khat bawl hi | he gathered all the people and gave a feast/a kha sagihna-a ~ hun sung | at the time of the festival in the seventh month/Kha-det, kha-liik, i ~ ni-in pengkul tum un | blow the horn at the new moon, at the full moon, on our festival day) (s:pawikhamna) (r:2.23.14/19.81.3/1.29.22/14.5.3) a day or period of celebration
Pawi = (t:n) (w:festival/feast) (d:capitalised in the name of a feast; Paisan Pawi is the Passover) (e:hih Paisan ~ kibawl hi/sawm-le-li ni-in Paisan ~ bawl na kipan ding uh | on the fourteenth day you shall begin to keep the Passover/~ kibawlna innah na pai kei ding a | you shall not go into a house where there is feasting) (s:pawikhamna/pawikhawmna) (b:pawi) (r:14.35.19/14.35.17/26.45.21/24.16.8) (q:draft)
pawibawl = (t:v) (w:hold a festival/celebrate a feast) (d:pawi, festival, with bawl, make; pawibawl ni is a festival day) (e:Topa ading ~ ni hi ding hi) (s:pawikham) (b:pawi) (r:2.32.5) (q:draft)
pawibawlna = (t:n) (w:feasting/celebration) (d:pawibawl, hold a festival, with the noun suffix na) (e:~ leh lungdam ni dingin) (s:pawikhamna/gualnopna) (b:pawibawl) (r:17.9.19) (q:draft)
pawikham = (t:v) (w:feast/celebrate a festival/hold a feast) (d:pawi, festival, and kham, keep: keep a feast or festival; also of the festival itself, as in pawikham ni, the feast day) (e:Pentekost ~ ni dongin Efesa khua/Tua mite in sun lai takin ~ uh a | they feast in broad daylight/Amaute in ni sagih sung tua ~ uh a | they kept the festival for seven days/Judah mite’ Buk ~ ding a nai zo hi | the Jewish Festival of Tabernacles was near) (s:pawibawl) (r:46.16.8/61.2.13/16.8.18/43.7.2) (q:draft)
pawikhamna = (t:n) (w:feast/festival/celebration) (d:the keeping of a feast; Paisan pawikhamna is the Festival of the Passover) (e:~ sungah Pasian bia dinga hong paite/Paisan ~ Jerusalem khua ah a pai uh hi | they went to Jerusalem for the Festival of the Passover/Jerusalem khua-ah ki-apna ~ a om lai takin | when the Festival of Dedication was held in Jerusalem/Judah mite’ ~ a tun’ lai takin | when a festival of the Jews came) (s:pawi/pawikhawmna/pawibawlna) (b:pawikham) (r:43.12.20/42.2.41/43.10.22/43.5.1) (q:draft)
pawikhawm = (t:v) (w:sow together/mix) (d:pawi, sow, with khawm, together: sow two kinds of seed together in one field) (e:khaici nam nih na ~ kei ding uh) (r:3.19.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
pawikhawmna = (t:n) (w:festival/feast) (d:pawi, festival, with khawmna, gathering) (e:Tua ~ ah no na pai un) (s:pawikhamna/pawi) (r:43.7.8) (q:draft)
pawina = (t:n) (w:ceremony/observance) (d:pawi festival, with the noun suffix na: the keeping of a feast) (e:hih bangin ~ hih ding uh hi) (b:pawi) (r:2.13.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
pawina = (t:n) (w:sowing) (d:pawi, sow, with the noun suffix na: a pawina leitang is the land sown with a given measure of seed) (e:mangbuhham beem khat a ~ leitang) (r:3.27.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
pawipi = (t:n) (w:great feast/banquet) (d:pawi, festival or feast, with pi, great) (e:Mi khat in ~ kham a/Jesuh vakna annek ~ bawl a | he held a great banquet for Jesus/Kitawng kawmin ~ sungah an nekna sangin | than eating at a great feast with strife) (s:lawmvakna/anvakna) (b:pawi) (r:42.14.16/20.17.1/42.5.29) (q:draft)
pawipuan = (t:n) (w:festal garment/set of clothes/change of clothes) (d:fine clothing worn at a feast, counted as a set; pawi feast with puan cloth) (e:le ~ sawm a keng hi/~ silh sawmthum note kong pia ding hi | I will give you thirty sets of clothes/ngun talen khat le ~ nih pia in | give them a talent of silver and two sets of clothing) (r:12.5.5/7.14.12/12.5.22) (q:draft)
pawipuante = (t:n) (w:festal garments/fine robes/sets of clothes) (d:pawipuan, festal garment, with the plural te) (e:mite tungah a ~ a pia hi/~, puanza neute, puanpite le khutkhai ipte | the fine robes, the capes, the cloaks and the purses) (b:pawipuan) (r:7.14.19/23.3.22) (q:draft)
pawisiim = (t:v) (w:attend a feast/keep a festival) (d:pawi, festival, with siim, attend: go to a festival and take part in it) (e:~ dingin note va pai un/ka galte ~ ding bangin na sam a | you summoned my enemies as if to a feast) (r:43.7.8/25.2.22) (q:draft)
Pawisimna = (t:n) (w:feasting/keeping of a feast) (d:pawi festival, feast, with sim and the noun suffix na; set against sigalna, mourning for the dead) (e:~ sangin sigalna hoihzaw hi) (s:pawibawlna) (a:sigalna) (r:21.7.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
pawisimte = (t:n) (w:wedding guests/guests) (d:those who attend a feast; pawi, feast, with sim, attend, and the plural te) (e:zineipa le ~ a omkhawm laitakin/a ~ an tangsak thei ding | can you make the guests fast) (s:leenglate/kisamte) (r:42.5.34) (q:draft)
pawite = (t:n) (w:festivals/feasts) (d:pawi, festival, with the plural te: festivals or feasts, the appointed religious celebrations of the year) (e:Na biakna ~ uh mudahin ka deih kei/na ~ uh ka mudah hi | I hate your festivals/note ki-itna ~ ah note tawh | with you at your love feasts) (b:pawi) (r:30.5.21/23.1.14/65.1.12) (q:draft)
pawkhat = (t:det) (w:some/a part of) (d:placed after a noun: some of them, a part of it) (e:Judah minamte’ gamh ngahsa ~ huam hi/Efraim mi ukpite ~ | some of the leaders of Ephraim) (s:kimkhat/khenkhat) (r:6.19.1/14.28.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
pawl = (t:n) (w:group/division/company/party) (d:a group of people, as a division of an army, a company or a party; pawl khat, one group, is also used for some) (e:Babilon mite ~ khat pai-in/ama ~ tul sawmli leh zanga pha hi | his division numbers 40,500/Farisai ~ lakah a um kimkhat | some believers from the party of the Pharisees/amaute ~ khat suakin mual dawn khatah | they formed one group on a hilltop) (s:hon) (r:27.3.8/4.2.19/44.15.5/10.2.25) (q:draft)
Pawlas = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Paulus) (d:Sergius Paulus, the Roman proconsul of Cyprus who sent for Barnabas and Saul to hear the word of God) (r:44.13.7)
pawlbawl = (t:v) (w:welcome/accept/take in) (d:pawl, group or companion, with bawl, make; receive a person into one's company or service) (e:Upna neu mite ~ unla/hoihtakin na ~ un | welcome him well/limtakin a na ~ nading uh | so that they would welcome him warmly/ama galkap dingin ~ pahpah hi | he at once took him in as his soldier) (a:nolh) (b:pawl) (r:45.14.1/9.14.52/51.4.10/44.18.27) (q:draft)
pawlcing = (t:v) (w:become numerous/grow in number) (d:said of a people growing into a large body; apparently pawl, group, with cing, full) (e:Mite khangin ~ semsem uh hi) (s:pung) (a:kiam) (r:2.1.20) (q:draft, low confidence)
pawldang = (t:n) (w:other group/other company) (d:pawl, group, with dang, other) (e:a ko a ~ khat pen/ama ~ nihte in gamlak a om mite delhin | his two other companies chased the people in the fields) (r:16.12.38/7.9.44) (q:draft)
pawlin = (t:v) (w:join/side with) (d:pawl used as a verb with the linking ending in: joining someone or taking the side of someone) (e:Amaute in note hong ~/khual mite in amaute ~ Jakob innkuan beel | foreigners will join them and cling to the house of Jacob/Amaute in nang hong ~ | they will join you) (s:pawlpih/kipawlin) (r:4.18.4/23.14.1/4.18.2) (q:draft)
pawlin = (t:adv) (w:in groups/by divisions) (d:in the doubled form a pawl pawlin, group by group) (e:a pawl ~ ding khia uh hi/a pawl ~ a puanbuk uh lam ding | they shall pitch their tents by divisions/giahphual dialkhai a neite a pawl ~ | those under the camp standard, division by division) (s:pawlpawlin/honhonin) (b:pawl) (r:4.10.18/4.1.52/4.10.22) (q:draft)
pawlin = (t:adv) (w:about/around) (d:about the time of, as in nitum pawlin, around sunset) (e:Nitum ~ galkapte lakah kikona khat) (r:11.22.36) (q:draft, low confidence)
pawlkhat = (t:n) (w:a group/some) (d:pawl, group, with khat, one: one group; after a noun it means some of them) (e:Levi mite ~ Benjamin gamah kigawm hi/Gamsung upa ~ in zong | some of the elders of the land also/~ za, ~ sawmnga, a pawlpawlin a tu | they sat in groups, some of a hundred and some of fifty/Jew mi ~ thu kiseel uh hi | some Jews had a dispute) (s:honkhat) (r:16.11.36/24.26.17/41.6.40/43.3.25)
pawlkhatah = (t:v) (w:foregather) (d:pawlkhat, one group, with the place ending ah: in one group, to one group) (e:~ za, ~ sawmnga, cih bangin | in groups of a hundred and of fifty/~ Esau pai-in a suksiat leh | if Esau comes to one group and destroys it) (b:pawlkhat) (r:41.6.40/1.32.8)
pawlkhatin = (t:adv) (w:as one group/in fellowship/united) (d:pawlkhat, one group, with the ending in: being one company with someone, in fellowship; pawlkhatin bawl is make into one) (e:Gentail mite le Jew mite ~ hong bawl/Pasian tawh kilemin ~ na om nadingun | so that you may be reconciled and at one with God/Jesuh Khrih tawh kote ~ ka om uh | we are in fellowship with Jesus Christ) (s:kikhatin) (b:pawlkhat) (r:49.2.14/62.1.3/47.5.20) (q:draft)
pawlkhatte = (t:pron) (w:some/others) (d:pawlkhat, some, with the plural te: some people, some of them; often after mi or the name of a people) (e:~, teembaw tawh tuipi-ah pai uh a/Mi ~ in an lei nadingin | some people, in order to buy grain/Levi mi ~ in laigelhte | some of the Levites were secretaries/Mi ~’ khialhnate kimu pahpahin | the sins of some people are seen at once) (b:pawlkhat) (r:19.107.23/40.13.8/16.5.2/14.34.13/54.5.24) (q:draft)
pawlmat = (t:v) (w:win over/enlist/make an ally of) (d:pawl, group, with mat, catch: get someone onto the side of a party, gather people as a party) (e:ahi Blastus a ~ phot uh hi/migilo honkhat kaikhawmin a ~ uh hi | they gathered a band of bad men and formed a party) (r:44.12.20/44.17.5) (q:draft)
pawlpawl = (t:adj) (w:various/of every kind/all kinds of) (d:pawl, group or kind, doubled: of many different kinds, in every way; often written a pawlpawl after the noun) (e:cinatna ~ a neite khempeuh/suangmanpha a ~ tawh kizeem hi | it was adorned with every kind of precious stone/deihgawhna a ~ leh gualnop uukna’ sila | slaves of all kinds of passions and pleasures/A ~ phattuamna tampi a om hi | there is much benefit of every kind) (s:apawlpawl/namcin/atuamtuam) (r:42.4.40/45.3.2/66.21.19/56.3.3) (q:draft)
pawlpawlin = (t:adv) (w:in groups/by divisions/group by group) (d:pawl, group, doubled, with the ending in: group by group, each in its own division) (e:lopa hing tungah a ~ tusak un/a ~ a tu uh hi | they sat down in groups/siampite a ~ a kikhennate | the divisions of the priests, group by group/a ~ a puanbuk uh lam ding uh hi | they shall pitch their tents by divisions) (s:honhonin/pawlin/honin) (b:pawlpawl) (r:41.6.39/14.8.14/41.6.40/4.1.52) (q:draft)
pawlpawlte = (t:n) (w:all kinds/various groups) (d:pawlpawl, group by group, with the plural te; the various groups of people or kinds of a thing) (e:leitungah mi a ~ in tuipi lian/Thungetna ~, thuumna ~ | all kinds of prayers and requests/lungdamna, noptuamna a ~ tawh na dim nadingun | so that you may be filled with all joy and peace) (s:apawlpawlte) (b:pawlpawl) (r:42.21.25/49.6.18/45.15.13) (q:draft)
pawlpi = (t:n) (w:church/congregation) (d:pawl, group, with pi, great: the church, the body of those who believe in Christ, or a local congregation) (e:Khazih in ~ a it mah bangin/~ upate a sam hi | he called the elders of the church/~ khempeuh lunghihmawhna tawh | with concern for all the churches/Amaute in ~ omsate kipsakin | strengthening the existing churches) (b:pawl) (r:49.5.25/44.15.41/44.20.17/47.11.28) (q:draft)
Pawlpi = (t:n) (w:church/congregation) (d:pawlpi, church, written with a capital letter at the start of a sentence or in a title; Pawlpi siapa is the overseer of the church) (e:~ siapa in Pasian’ neihsa kempa bangin/~ buppi akipan tua thu a zate | the whole church and those who heard this/~ kiangah vaikhakna lai gelhin ka pia | I wrote a letter to the church/~ khempeuh kiangah hih thukham ka pia hi | I give this rule to all the churches) (b:pawlpi) (r:56.1.7/44.5.11/64.1.9/46.7.17) (q:draft)
pawlpih = (t:v) (w:join/side with/ally with) (d:pawl, group, with pih, together with: be of one party with someone, take the side of someone) (e:Assiria mite in zong amaute ~ hi/Midangte khat beek in a ~ ngam loh | not one of the others dared to join them/Judah mite in Israel mite hong ~ ding uh | the people of Judah will join the people of Israel/nang hong ~ minam tampite | the many nations that side with you) (s:kipawlin/panpih/pawlin) (a:langpan) (b:pawl) (r:19.83.8/44.5.13/24.3.18/26.38.9) (q:draft)
pawlpihna = (t:n) (w:siding with/alliance) (d:pawlpih, side with, with the noun suffix na: the fact of having taken the side of someone) (e:Jessi’ tapa na ~ thu/Adonijah a na ~ hang ahi hi | it was because he had sided with Adonijah) (s:kipawlna) (b:pawlpih) (r:9.20.30/11.2.28) (q:draft)
pawlpite = (t:n) (w:churches) (d:pawlpi, church, with the plural te) (e:Kha Siangtho in ~ a thupiakna/~’ upna a kip semsem a | the churches grew stronger in faith/~ kimkhat a kibawlsiat theih nadingin | so that some of the church might be persecuted) (b:pawlpi) (r:66.3.13/60.5.3/44.16.5/44.12.1) (q:draft)
pawlsung = (t:n) (w:within the group/in the party) (d:pawl, group, with sung, inside: within a party, among its members) (e:Farisi mite ~ a om) (r:44.23.9) (q:draft)
pawlte = (t:n) (w:companions/followers/company) (d:those who belong to one group or side; also bands or groups of people) (e:nang leh na ~ khempeuh/Korah leh a ~ khempeuh in | Korah and all his followers/Abiram’ ~ vukcip hi | it buried the company of Abiram/galsim ~ a makai mi nih | two men who led raiding bands) (s:kipawlte) (b:pawl) (r:4.16.11/19.106.17/4.16.6/10.4.2) (q:draft)
pawlthum = (t:n) (w:three companies/three groups) (d:pawl, group, with thum, three) (e:~ suahin gamlakah pangsim uh hi) (s:honthum) (r:7.9.43) (q:draft)
pawltuam = (t:n) (w:faction/separate party) (d:pawl, group, with tuam, separate: pawltuam lungsim is a factious or party spirit) (e:~ lungsim neihna) (r:48.5.20) (q:draft)
pawm = (t:v) (w:join/accompany/take part in) (d:go in with others, join a battle, a leader or a song) (e:galkidona ah va ~ hi/Gilgal-ah Saul a ~ dingin mite kisamkhia | the people were called out to join Saul at Gilgal/David’ lasaknate in peengkulte ~ hi | the instruments of David accompanied the trumpets) (s:pawlpih) (r:14.35.22/14.29.27/9.13.4) (q:draft)
pawm = (t:v) (w:swell/rise) (d:of the body swelling up, and of dough rising with yeast) (e:na pumpi ~ sakin na pheipi teem/a pumpi ~-in, a pheipi teem ding | her body will swell and her thigh waste away/a annel lom meek a ~ mateng | until the kneaded dough has risen/buhneel seeng thum a ~ khit mateng | until the three measures of flour had all risen) (a:teem) (r:4.5.22/42.13.21/4.5.27/28.7.4) (q:draft)
pawmin = (t:v) (w:joining/siding with/rallying around) (d:pawm, join, with the linking ending in: taking the side of someone, gathering around a leader) (e:mite in Jefthah ~ amah tawh/a sanggam uh ahi, amau’ makaite ~ | joining their leaders, who are their brothers) (s:pawlin) (b:pawm) (r:7.11.3/16.10.29) (q:draft)
pawmsak = (t:v) (w:make swell/leaven/make rise) (d:pawm, swell, with the causative sak: said of yeast making dough rise and of a body made to swell) (e:a annel lom khempeuh a ~ hi/Silngo themkhat in annel lompi a ~ theih | a little yeast can leaven the whole lump of dough/na pumpi a ~ ciangin | when he makes your body swell/silngo in zelin a ~ tawh kibang | it is like yeast that spreads through it and makes it rise) (b:pawm) (r:42.13.21/4.5.21/46.5.6/40.13.33) (q:draft)
pawmsakin = (t:v) (w:making swell) (d:pawmsak make swell, with the linking suffix in) (e:na pumpi ~ na pheipi teemsak hen) (b:pawmsak) (r:4.5.22) (q:draft)
pawn = (t:n) (w:scar/mark) (d:the mark left by a boil, burn or wound) (e:meimatum ~ ahi hi/tua in meikangma ~ ahi hi | it is the scar of the burn/A khut a, sikkhetna ~ mu-in | seeing the nail marks in his hands) (s:meimapawn) (r:3.13.23/3.13.28/43.20.25) (q:draft)
pawn = (t:n) (w:wasteland/bare land) (d:open land that is bare or newly cut, often as pawn lak) (e:~ lak hong suaksak uh a/~ lak lopa tunga guah kia | rain falling on the grass of a mown field/~-a om Bezer a lonona gamte tawh | Bezer in the wilderness with its pasturelands) (s:pawnlak/gamkhing) (r:24.12.11/19.72.6/13.6.78) (q:draft)
pawnlak = (t:n) (w:wasteland/desolate place) (d:paired with gamlak, wilderness, for a field laid waste) (e:ka leenggah lo ~) (s:pawn/gamkhing/gamsia) (r:24.12.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
pawpite = (t:see) <pawpite-ah>
pawpite-ah = (t:n) (w:in the churches) (d:apparently pawlpite churches with ah in; pawpite looks like a misprint of pawlpite) (e:Masedonia gam ~ Pasian’ hehpihna hangin) (r:47.8.1) (q:draft, low confidence)
pawta = (t:n) (w:measure/quart) (d:a small dry measure for grain) (e:tang ~ thumah hamu man hen/Mangbuh ~ khatah hamu) (r:66.6.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
Pedahel = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Pedahel) (d:son of Ammihud, the leader from the tribe of Naphtali chosen to help divide the land of Canaan) (r:4.34.28)
