peei = (t:n) (w:wheel) (d:another spelling of pei wheel) (e:~ dang khat ciat nei thuah uh hi) (s:pei/leengpei) (r:26.10.10) (q:draft)
peek = (t:n) (w:piece/coin/leaf) (d:a flat piece; used as a counter for coins, tablets and door leaves) (e:denarias ~ khat hong paipih uh hi/dangka ~ sawmthum ama ading a tawikhai uh hi | they weighed out thirty silver pieces for him/kongkhak ~ nih nei-a kibawl ahi hi | it was made with two door leaves/ngun ~ khat ahi a, anlum lum khat | a piece of silver and a loaf of bread) (r:40.22.19/26.41.24/40.26.15/9.2.36) (q:draft)
peek = (t:v) (w:swim) (d:move through water by swimming; tui peek is swim in water) (e:Tui ~ siamte in/~ masa uh a, lei tungah a tung masa | swim first and reach land first/a tui i ~ loh buangin | unless one swam the water) (s:tuipeek) (r:44.27.43/26.47.5) (q:draft)
peek = (t:v) (w:kick/kick against) (d:strike back with the foot or heel) (e:na khe tawh ~ leteh a haksa hi/a khetul tawh keimah hong ~ hi | he has kicked me with his heel/Bawngtal in a hawlte’ ciangzum ~ le | when an ox kicks against the goad of its driver) (r:44.26.14/19.41.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
peeka = (t:v) (w:swimming) (d:peek swim with a linking it to the next verb: tui peeka a taimang, escape by swimming) (e:tui ~ a taimang ding uh) (b:peek) (r:44.27.42) (q:draft)
peekin = (t:v) (w:swimming/swim) (d:peek, swim, with the linking ending in; tui peekin, by swimming) (e:mi khempeuh tui ~ a taimang ding/teembaw panin a nawlah tui va ~ | from the ship, swimming to the shore) (b:peek) (r:44.27.42/44.27.43) (q:draft)
peekkhat = (t:n) (w:one coin/a coin) (d:peek, counter for coins, with khat, one: a single coin, a denarius) (e:~ tek a ngah uh hi/a kam na phen ciangin ~ na mu ding | when you open its mouth you will find a coin) (r:40.20.9/40.17.27) (q:draft)
peekpi = (t:n) (w:expanse/sheet/broad flat surface) (d:peek, flat piece, with pi, great: van peekpi is the expanse of the sky, limlang peekpi a great sheet of glass, sing peekpi a large board) (e:limlang ~ kiphah tuipi tawh a kibang/Limlang bangin a sak van ~ | the expanse of the sky, hard as a mirror/sing ~ khihna khaute zong a sut uh hi | they also untied the ropes that held the steering boards) (b:peek) (r:66.15.2/18.37.18/44.27.40) (q:draft, low confidence)
peeksat = (t:v) (w:break apart/snap/tear apart) (d:break a chain or bond in pieces; also written peksat) (e:kihen ngei hangin sikkhau a ~ a/a kikhum hangin, a sikkhau ~ a | though he was kept under guard, he broke his chains) (s:peksat/kuaitan) (r:41.5.4/42.8.29) (q:draft)
peekte = (t:n) (w:boards/planks/tablets) (d:peek, flat piece, with the plural te: boards or planks of wood, and the stone tablets of the law) (e:taamtaak ~ tawh inndap bawl hi/taaksan ~ tawh inn sual tuam hi | he covered the floor with juniper planks/A ~ in Pasian’ bawl hi a | the tablets were the work of God/tong sawmnih taamtaak ~ tawh lam a | he built twenty cubits with cedar boards) (b:peek) (r:11.6.9/2.32.16/11.6.15/11.6.16) (q:draft)
peekte = (t:n) (w:palms) (d:with khut, hand: khut peekte, the palms, the flat of the hands) (e:ka khut ~ sungah nang kong gelh) (b:peek) (r:23.49.16) (q:draft)
peel = (t:v) (w:avoid/shun/keep away from/beware of) (d:stay clear of a person or thing, turn away from) (e:Gitlohna ~ in/Topa zahtakin a sia ~ in | fear the Lord and shun evil/gamtat hoih lo peuhmah ~ hi | he shunned every evil deed/gilo-a gamtate na ~ un | watch out for the evildoers) (s:pelh/pel/kipelh) (r:20.4.15/50.3.2/20.3.7/18.1.1) (q:draft)
peel = (t:v) (w:fail to keep/evade/break) (d:of a covenant or an appointed observance: evade it, not keep it; peel loin is without fail) (e:tawntung thuciamna ~ uh hi/hih ni nihte ~ loin a tan’ nading uh | so that they keep these two days without fail) (s:palsat/pelh) (a:zui) (r:23.24.5/17.9.27) (q:draft, low confidence)
peelhem = (t:v) (w:be missing/be lacking) (d:be absent from a counted number; also written pelhem) (e:mi khat zong a ~ om lo hi) (s:pelhem/pelem) (r:4.31.49) (q:draft)
peelin = (t:v) (w:avoiding/passing by/turning from) (d:peel, avoid or go around, with the linking suffix in) (e:tua pa a muh ciangin ~ a nusia hi/a muh ciangin ~ a pai leuleu hi | when he saw him, he too passed by/Gitlohna ~, gitna bawl hen | let him turn from evil and do good/Siatna ~ a maanin gamta in | avoid evil and walk rightly/kei hong ~ hong taisan uh hi | they avoid me and flee from me) (s:pelhin/pelin) (b:peel) (r:42.10.31/60.3.11/42.10.32/20.4.27/19.31.11) (q:draft)
peem = (t:v) (w:sojourn/reside as a foreigner/migrate/settle) (d:live in a place that is not home, as an incomer among another people) (e:note lakah khualmi khat hong ~ leh/amah tua lai-ah ~ hi | he was living there as a sojourner/note' lakah hong ~ khual mi’ adingin | for the foreigner who resides among you/amau lakah a ~ khualmi zong kimaisak ding hi | the foreigner living among them will also be forgiven) (r:3.19.33/7.17.7/2.12.49/4.15.26) (q:draft)
peemin = (t:v) (w:sojourning/residing as a foreigner) (d:peem, live in a place as an incomer, with the linking ending in) (e:Note lakah khualmi khat hong ~/Efraim mualtung gammongah ~ | living in a remote part of the hill country of Ephraim) (b:peem) (r:4.9.14/7.19.1) (q:draft)
peemna = (t:n) (w:lodging/place of stay) (d:peem, live somewhere as an incomer, with the noun suffix na: where or with whom one is staying; ka peemna meigongnu, the widow I am staying with) (e:tawh ka ~ meigongnu’ tung nangawnah) (s:zintunna) (b:peem) (r:11.17.20) (q:draft)
peempak = (t:n) (w:sojourner/exile/temporary resident) (d:one who lives for a time in a place that is not home; peem, sojourn, with pak, for a short while) (e:a ~ bangin kingaihsun unla) (s:peemta) (r:60.2.11) (q:draft)
peemta = (t:n) (w:foreigner/sojourner/stranger/temporary resident) (d:one who lives in a land that is not his own; peemta-in om is live as a foreigner) (e:gen taak loin, ~ hi uh a/leitungah ~ ka hi hi | I am a stranger on earth/Note lakah a om ~ mite sang semsem ding | the foreigners among you will rise higher and higher/tu ni dongin tua lai-ah ~-in om uh hi | they have lived there as foreigners to this day) (s:khualmi/mikhual/gamdangmi) (a:tualsuak) (r:13.16.19/10.4.3/19.119.19/5.28.43) (q:draft)
peemtate = (t:n) (w:foreigners/sojourners/strangers) (d:peemta, sojourner, with the plural te: people living in a land that is not their own, often paired with mikhualte) (e:Topa in ~ kem a/mikhualte leh ~ ka hi uh hi | we are foreigners and strangers/amau lakah a teeng ~ mai-ah | before the foreigners living among them/mikhual leh ~ na hi uh hi | you are strangers and sojourners) (s:khualmite/mikhualte/pemtate/peemte) (b:peemta) (r:19.146.9/3.25.23/13.29.15/6.8.35) (q:draft)
peemte = (t:n) (w:foreigners/sojourners/resident aliens) (d:used after mi as mi peemte, people who have moved in and live in a land not their own) (e:Izipt gamah mi ~ na hi uh hi/mi ~ itin an leh puan a pia hi | he loves the foreigners and gives them food and clothing/khualzinte, mi ~ bang ahi note | you who are like travellers and sojourners/note lakah a ~’ adingin bukna hi ding | it will be a refuge for those who reside among you) (s:peemtate/khualmite/mikhualte) (b:peem) (r:5.10.19/5.10.18/60.2.11/4.35.15) (q:draft)
peeng = (t:n) (w:twin) (d:two born together; sakhi peeng, twin gazelles, and Ta Peeng, the Twin Sons, the figurehead of a ship) (e:a takhawm helhel sakhi ~/a takhawm hialhial sakhi ~ tawh | with twin gazelles feeding together) (r:22.7.3/44.28.11/22.4.5) (q:draft)
Peeng = (t:n) (w:twin) (d:one of two born together; Unau Peeng, the Twin, is the byname of Thomas, Didymus, and Ta Peeng milim is the image of the twin gods Castor and Pollux) (e:Unau ~ minno a nei Thomas/Ta ~ milim a om | bearing the image of the Twin Sons) (b:peeng) (r:43.20.24/44.28.11) (q:draft)
peengkhul = (t:n) (w:trumpet) (d:apparently another spelling of pengkul trumpet) (e:hong gen ~ aw banga nakpi-a) (s:peengkul/pengkul) (r:66.4.1) (q:draft, low confidence)
peengkul = (t:n) (w:trumpet) (d:a trumpet or horn blown as a signal in war and in worship; peengkul tum or peengkul mut is blow the trumpet) (e:Zion mual tungah ~ tumin/~ a kitum ciangin omkhong thei lo uh hi | when the trumpet sounds they cannot stand still/Bang tan vei ~ aw ka za lai ding | how long must I still hear the sound of the trumpet/~ mut dingin a kisa khol hi | they prepared to blow the trumpets) (s:pengkul/peengkhul) (r:29.2.15/66.8.6/18.39.24/24.4.21)
peengkulte = (t:n) (w:trumpets) (d:peengkul, trumpet, with the plural te) (e:~ tawh siampite ding uh hi/harp lasaknate leh laiza lasaknate leh ~ tawh | with harps, lyres and trumpets/awging pha, leh otna, leh ~, leh sakite tawh | with a loud voice, shouting, trumpets and horns/~ a tum paisuak ding uh ahi hi | they were to blow the trumpets regularly) (s:Pengkulte) (b:peengkul) (r:14.29.26/14.15.14/14.20.28/13.16.6) (q:draft)
peh = (t:v) (w:graft/graft in) (d:join a branch or shoot onto another plant; peh kik is graft in again) (e:Pasian in amaute khatvei a ~ kik thei hi/Kei hong ~ nadingin hiangte a kitan hi | branches were broken off so that I could be grafted in/amau oliv kungah zomin ~ kik nading | to be grafted back into their own olive tree/a kung tungah zom kikin ~ kik nading | to be joined again and grafted back onto the tree) (r:45.11.23/45.11.19/45.11.24) (q:draft)
pehin = (t:v) (w:grafting/grafted in) (d:peh, graft, with the linking ending in) (e:kung namdangte tawh ~/amau pum tungah ~ kibulh a | grafted and fixed onto their trunk) (b:peh) (r:23.17.10/45.11.17) (q:draft)
pehkik = (t:v) (w:graft in again/graft back) (d:peh, graft, with kik, again or back) (e:amau’ mun ngei mahah ~ ding hi/Pasian in a ~ theih nading vangliatna nei | God has the power to graft them in again/amau omna ngei-ah a ~ ding olzaw mahmah | it is far easier to graft them back where they were) (b:peh) (r:45.11.23/45.11.24) (q:draft)
pehsakin = (t:v) (w:crossing) (d:of the hands or arms, laying one across the other; pehsak with the linking suffix in) (e:a khut kipaih ~ Manasseh’ lutang tungah) (s:kipaihpehsakin) (r:1.48.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
pehtum = (t:v) (w:eat up/devour) (d:said of a worm eating cloth away completely) (e:lungno in samul puan a ~ bangin) (s:nektum/netum) (r:23.51.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
pei = (t:n) (w:wheel) (d:wheel of a cart or chariot, as in leengpei) (e:lamin ~ khat ciat nei thuah uh/a ~ buppi dimin mittang om hi | the whole wheel was full of eyes/sakol leeng gingte leh a ~ kigawi gingte | the noise of the chariots and the rumble of their wheels) (s:leengpei/lengpei/peei) (r:26.1.16/26.10.12/24.47.3) (q:draft)
pei = (t:v) (w:shake/wag) (d:with lu, head: shake the head from side to side, in mockery) (e:ka lu hong ~ sanin/lamdang sa-in a lu uh a ~ uh hi | amazed, they shake their heads/lu ~-in a zahko uh hi | they mocked him, shaking their heads) (r:18.16.4/41.15.30/24.18.16) (q:draft)
peigawpin = (t:v) (w:sweeping over/whirling upon) (d:pei, whirl as a whirlwind does, with the intensive gawp and the linking suffix in) (e:note hong ~) (r:20.1.27) (q:draft, low confidence)
peikalhna = (t:n) (w:spoke) (d:the bars of a wheel between hub and rim; pei, wheel, with kalhna, crossbar) (e:a ~, leh a kalhna bulte khempeuh) (r:11.7.33) (q:draft, low confidence)
peikual = (t:n) (w:rim) (d:the round outer part of a wheel; pei, wheel, with kual, circle) (e:a peizawl, a ~, a peikalhna) (r:11.7.33) (q:draft, low confidence)
peisan = (t:v) (w:shake at/toss at/wag at) (d:pei, shake, with san, at: used with lu, head; lu peisan is shake or toss the head at someone in scorn) (e:a lu hong ~ uh hi/na nungah a lu hong ~ hi | she tosses her head behind you/a lu uh ~ ding uh hi | they will shake their heads/na nungah a lu hong ~ lel uh hi | they only toss their heads behind you) (b:pei) (r:19.22.7/12.19.21/19.64.8/23.37.22) (q:draft)
peisanin = (t:v) (w:shaking at/wagging at) (d:peisan with the linking ending in; lu peisanin, shaking the head at someone in scorn) (e:peuhmah in a lu uh ~/Note ka lu hong ~ thu tampi tak mah | shaking my head at you, with a great many words) (b:peisan) (r:40.27.39/18.16.4) (q:draft)
peite = (t:n) (w:wheels) (d:pei, wheel, with the plural te) (e:A ~ pen sakol leengpei bangin kibawl hi/amau’ leeng ~ tumsak ahih manin | because he made the wheels of their chariots stick) (s:leengpeite) (b:pei) (r:11.7.33/2.14.25) (q:draft)
peizawl = (t:n) (w:axle) (d:a part of a wheel, first in a list that the English gives as axles, rims, spokes and hubs) (e:a ~, a peikual, a peikalhna) (r:11.7.33) (q:draft, low confidence)
pek = (t:adv) (w:far/long ago) (d:placed after a word of time or distance to stress how far off it is, as in sawt pek long ago, tanglai pek ancient times and gamlapi pek far away) (e:tanglai ~ panin a piang nai lo nate/sawt ~ lai-a kumte ka phawk hi | I remember the years of long ago/Leimong ~-ah leengin, tuipimong ~-ah om taleng zong | though I fly to the end of the earth or stay at the far end of the sea/gamla ~-ah ka vakthap ding a | I would wander far away) (r:23.46.10/19.139.9/19.77.5/19.55.7) (q:draft)
peka = (t:adv) (w:far away/far off/long ago) (d:pek, far, with the ending a: far in place as gam peka, or far in time as tanglai peka, long ago) (e:Tua gam in tanglai ~ a om sa/Leilu lam gam ~ om Gomer | Gomer in the far north/tanglai ~ na geelnate | the things you planned long ago/A gamlapi Ethiopia gam ~ om | in far-off Ethiopia) (b:pek) (r:24.5.15/26.38.6/23.25.1/36.3.10) (q:draft)
pekah = (t:adv) (w:far off/far away/to the farthest part) (d:pek, far, with the place ending ah: at or to a point far away, far above or deep within) (e:giahphual panin a gamla ~ lam thei zel/a gamla ~ va pai uh hi | they went far away/meiite’ tung ~ ka kahto ding a | I will ascend far above the clouds/mihingte’ sungtawng ~ tumsuk pahpah hi | it goes straight down to the inmost parts of a person/vanmong ~ a om leh zong | even if they are at the far end of the heavens) (s:gamlapi) (b:pek) (r:2.33.7/5.30.4/11.12.30/23.14.14/20.26.22) (q:draft)
Pekah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Pekah) (d:son of Remaliah, an officer who killed King Pekahiah and reigned over Israel in Samaria until he was killed by Hoshea) (e:Remaliah’ tapa ~ sawl ding kipan hi) (r:12.15.37/12.15.31) (q:draft)
Pekahiah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Pekahiah) (d:son of Menahem, king of Israel in Samaria for two years, killed by his officer Pekah) (r:12.15.22/12.15.26)
pekin = (t:adv) (w:long ago/long before/already) (d:pek with the adverb ending in; stresses how far back in time something was so, as in ma pekin, long before, and lai pekin, back when) (e:mualneute a kibawl ma ~ ka om khin hi/sawt ~ kibawl khin zo hi | it was prepared long ago/Hih thu sawt ~ kua in genkhol ahi hiam | who foretold this long ago/Tanglai ~ Pasian in ama kampauna tawh | long ago God, by his word) (b:pek) (r:20.8.25/44.15.7/23.30.33/23.45.21/61.3.5) (q:draft)
Pekod = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Pekod) (d:region of Babylonia and the people living there, named together with Shoa and Koa) (r:24.50.21/26.23.23)
pekpak = (t:adv) (d:descriptive word used with tuk, fall: dropping down limp, as people who faint in the streets) (e:kongzing tengah a tuk ~ uh hi/kongzing lakah tuk ~ uh a | they drop limp in the streets) (r:25.2.12/25.4.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
pekpek = (t:adv) (w:very far/by far/long ago) (d:pek, far, said twice for emphasis: after lui, old, very long ago or ancient; after a comparative with zaw, far more) (e:Khrih nasem a hoihzaw ~ ka hi hi/tuanthu lui ~ ahi hi | it is a very ancient record) (r:47.11.23/13.4.22) (q:draft)
peksat = (t:v) (w:break/snap/annul) (d:break a chain apart; of a covenant, break or set aside; also written peeksat) (e:tua a thuciamna ~ sawm lo hi/a kikepcip hangin a sikkhaute ~ a | though he was kept under guard, he broke his chains) (s:peeksat) (r:48.3.17/42.8.29) (q:draft)
peksatin = (t:v) (w:breaking/annulling) (d:peksat, break or set aside, with the linking suffix in) (e:tua thuciamna ~ phiat thei lo ding) (b:peksat) (r:48.3.17) (q:draft)
pel = (t:v) (w:avoid/shun/turn away from/dodge) (d:keep away from, turn aside from; pel loin, without avoiding, means without fail or surely) (e:thum vei dong hong ~ hi/Topa zahtakin, a sia ~ in | fear the Lord and shun evil/gamtat hoih lo peuhmah ~ hi | he shunned every evil deed/~ loin nungta ding hi | he will surely live/Kei hong ~ kei leh | if it had not turned away from me) (s:peel/pelh/kipelh) (r:4.22.33/20.3.7/18.1.1/26.18.21) (q:draft)
Pelaiah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Pelaiah) (d:name of two men: a descendant of David, son of Elioenai, and a Levite who explained the Law and sealed the covenant in the time of Nehemiah) (r:13.3.24/16.10.10)
Pelaih = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Pelaliah) (d:priest in the ancestry of Adaiah, who served in the temple after the exile; the spelling Pelaliah is also used) (r:16.11.12)
Pelaliah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Pelaliah) (d:priest in the ancestry of Adaiah, who served in the temple after the exile) (r:16.11.12)
Pelatiah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Pelatiah) (d:name of several men, among them a grandson of Zerubbabel, a leader of the Simeonites who went to Seir, and a leader who sealed the covenant with Nehemiah) (r:13.3.21/16.10.22)
Pelatiahte = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Pelatiah) (d:Pelatiah son of Benaiah, a leader of the people seen by Ezekiel at the temple gate; the plural te joins him with Jaazaniah, named just before) (b:Pelatiah) (r:26.11.1)
Peleg = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Peleg) (d:son of Eber and father of Reu, a descendant of Shem in whose time the earth was divided) (r:1.11.18)
pelem = (t:v) (w:be missing/be lacking/be lost) (d:be absent from a group or number, drop out or be lost; pelem lo is not missing, and pelem sak is let someone be missing) (e:kuamah ~ sak kei un/minam khat a ~ nading | that one tribe should be missing/khat beek ~ lo hi | not even one is missing/a ~ peuhmah nungta lo ding hi | whoever is missing will not live/na pumpi na khat ~ leh | if one part of your body is lost) (s:pelhem/peelhem) (r:12.10.19/23.40.26/7.21.3/40.5.29) (q:draft)
pelemsak = (t:v) (w:let be missing/leave out) (d:pelem, be missing, with the causative sak: let someone be missing; kuamah pelemsak kei un is see that no one is missing) (e:kuamah ~ kei un) (b:pelem) (r:12.10.19) (q:draft)
Pelet = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Pelet) (d:name of two men: a son of Jahdai in the family of Caleb of Judah, and a son of Azmaveth, a warrior of Benjamin who joined David at Ziklag) (e:Azamveth’ tapate Jeziel leh ~ zong ahi hi) (r:13.12.3/13.2.47) (q:draft)
Peleth = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Peleth) (d:name of two men, a descendant of Jerahmeel of Judah and the father of On of Reuben; Peleth mite are the Pelethites, the bodyguard of David led by Benaiah) (r:13.2.33)
pelh = (t:v) (w:avoid/shun/keep away from/escape) (d:keep away from something bad or dangerous, or get out of its way; siatna pelh is shun evil) (e:gamtat sia khempeuh ka ~ hi/mipilte in tua lampi ~ uh hi | the wise avoid that path/Tuiciin ~ dingin | to escape the flood/milim biakna ~ un | keep away from the worship of idols/amah in Saul ~ a | he dodged Saul) (s:pel/peel/kipelh) (r:19.119.101/20.22.5/1.7.7/46.10.14/9.19.10) (q:draft)
pelh = (t:v) (w:break/go back on/revoke/fail) (d:fail to keep a promise or covenant; with a negative, pelh lo, without fail or unfailingly) (e:a ~ loh ding kiciamna taktak khat/na thuciamna na ~ khin a | you have broken your covenant/a ciamna a ~ leh phamawh lo hi | if he breaks his oath it does not matter/na kiciamnate uh ~ kei unla | do not break your oaths) (s:palsat/peel) (r:19.132.11/19.89.39/40.23.16/40.5.33) (q:draft)
pelhem = (t:v) (w:be missing/be lacking) (d:be absent from a counted number; also written peelhem) (e:mi khat zong a ~ om lo hi) (s:pelem/peelhem) (r:4.31.49) (q:draft)
pelhin = (t:v) (w:avoiding/escaping/turning away from) (d:pelh, avoid, with the linking ending in: avoiding or turning away from something, followed by what is done next) (e:Amah in namsau ~ a taina-ah/amaute in ~ a suksiat loh uh | they turned away and did not destroy them/Gitlohna ~ hoih gamtat uh hen la | let them turn from evil and do good) (s:pelin/peelin) (b:pelh) (r:18.20.24/14.20.10/60.3.11) (q:draft)
pelhin = (t:v) (w:breaking/violating) (d:going back on a covenant or promise) (e:ka thuciamna uh ~, ka thuhilhnate hong nial uh hi) (b:pelh) (r:28.8.1) (q:draft)
pelhna = (t:n) (w:avoiding/shunning) (d:pelh, avoid, with the noun ending na: the act of keeping away from something) (e:siatna ~ in thu theihna ahi hi/Kitot khak ding ~ in pahtak ngahna hi a | avoiding a quarrel brings honour) (s:kipelhna) (b:pelh) (r:18.28.28/20.20.3) (q:draft)
pelhna = (t:n) (w:breaking/breach) (d:going back on a covenant or promise) (e:na thuciamna uh na ~ hang uh ahi hi) (b:pelh) (r:39.2.14) (q:draft)
pelhsak = (t:v) (w:cause to avoid/keep away) (d:pelh, avoid, with the causative sak: make someone keep away from another) (e:ka lawmte keimah nong ~ khin a) (b:pelh) (r:19.88.18) (q:draft)
pelhthei = (t:v) (w:be able to escape/can avoid/elude) (d:pelh, avoid or escape, with thei, be able) (e:a nih vei mahin na ~ hi/tua bang numei ~ a | they can escape such a woman/A sih ding a ~ | one who can escape dying) (s:pengthei/suahtakzo) (b:pelh) (r:9.18.11/21.7.26/21.8.8) (q:draft)
pelhzah = (t:v) (w:break) (d:pelh, go back on a covenant, with zah, to the extent of: so far as to break it) (e:ka thuciamna a ~ dingin) (r:3.26.44) (q:draft, low confidence)
pelin = (t:v) (w:avoiding/shunning) (d:pel, avoid, with the linking ending in: keeping out of the way of someone) (e:kei hong ~ hong taisan uh hi) (s:pelhin/peelin) (b:pel) (r:19.31.11) (q:draft)
pelmawh = (t:adv) (w:surely/certainly/without fail) (d:placed after a verb, usually before ding: the thing will happen without fail and cannot be avoided) (e:daan tuak ~ ding a/nangma min hong phat ~ ding uh a | they will surely praise your name/ni a hong suah ~ mah bang | as sure as the sun rises/hoihna khempeuh zong ka tungsak ~ ding hi | I will surely bring all the good as well) (s:hamtang/takpi) (r:20.19.5/25.3.23/19.140.13/24.32.42) (q:draft)
Pelon = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Pelon) (d:home of Helez and Ahijah, two of the mighty warriors of David, who are called Pelonites in the NIV) (r:13.11.27/13.11.36)
Pelusium = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Pelusium) (d:fortress city on the eastern edge of the Nile delta, called the stronghold of Egypt by Ezekiel) (r:26.30.15/26.30.16)
pempam = (t:adv) (w:brightly/radiantly) (d:describes a bright glow, after taang shine or san be red: shining all around, a face flushed red) (e:a kimkot teng taang ~ hi/a mai a san ~ hi | his face flushed red/tua mah bangin taang ~ hi | it shone brightly in the same way) (s:heuhau) (r:26.1.4/27.3.19/26.1.27) (q:draft, low confidence)
pemtate = (t:n) (w:foreigners/sojourners/strangers) (d:pemta, a person who has moved in from elsewhere and lives among another people, with the plural te; paired with khualmite) (e:khualmite le ~ ka hi uh hi/~ kikhemgawp a | the foreigners are cheated) (s:peemtate/khualmite/peemte) (r:13.29.15/26.22.7) (q:draft)
pen = (t:ppm) (w:is) (d:marker placed after a noun or phrase to single it out as the topic of the sentence, the thing that is being spoken about; usually left untranslated) (e:khuavak ~/Israel a kempa ~ lusu lo a | he who watches over Israel does not slumber/Mi kihisak i cihte ~ | as for those we call proud/amah ~ mipa’ sung panin a kilakhia | she was taken out of the man/kei ~ Topa amau’ Pasian ka hi hi | I am the Lord their God) (r:1.1.5/19.121.4/20.21.24/1.2.23/3.26.44) postpositional marker to indicate objective case
Pen = (t:part) (w:most) (d:superlative marker placed after a describing word, written with a capital in titles of God such as Sang Pen Pasian, God Most High) (e:amah in Sang ~ Pasian’ siampi zong/Sang ~ Pasian in Abram thupha pia hen | may God Most High bless Abram/Sang ~ Pasian’ nasemte ahi uh hi | they are servants of the Most High God/Siangtho ~ Mun sung | inside the Most Holy Place) (b:pen) (r:1.14.18/44.7.48/1.14.19/44.16.17/11.8.6) (q:draft)
pena = (t:part) (d:pen, the marker of the superlative, most, with a: as the most; a thutang pena kineite, those counted the most upright) (e:a thutang ~ kineite) (r:33.7.4/26.40.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
penah = (t:ppm) (d:pen, marking the highest degree, with the place marker ah: at or in the most, as in a tawpna penah, last of all, and lei hoihna penah, in the best of the land) (e:inn sung tawngnung ~ kherubte koih hi/A tawpna ~ | last of all/na sanggamte lei hoihna ~ teengsak in | settle your brothers in the best of the land/kongpi laita ~ hong tu uh hi | they sat down in the Middle Gate) (b:pen) (r:11.6.27/46.15.8/1.47.6/24.39.3) (q:draft)
peng = (t:v) (w:be exempt/be free from/escape) (d:be clear of a duty, guilt or punishment; nasep a peng is to be off duty) (e:a tate a ~ uh hi/nasep ding uh panin na ~ ding uh hi | you will be free from your duty/kuamah ~ loin | no one being exempt/mawhna pan ~ ding | be free from guilt/tua hehna daan panin na ~ thei ding uh hi | you may escape the punishment of that anger) (s:suakta) (r:40.17.26/9.26.9/4.32.22/11.15.22/36.2.3) (q:draft)
pengin = (t:v) (w:being exempt/being off duty) (d:peng, be free of a duty, with the linking ending in) (e:nasep dangte panin ~ biakinn deite sungah) (b:peng) (r:13.9.33/12.11.5) (q:draft)
pengkul = (t:n) (w:trumpet/horn) (d:a horn or trumpet blown as a signal or in worship; another spelling of peengkul) (e:i pawi ni-in ~ tum un/~ aw tawh Topa paito hi | the Lord has gone up with the sound of the trumpet) (s:peengkul/peengkhul) (r:19.81.3/19.47.5) (q:draft)
Pengkulte = (t:n) (w:trumpets) (d:pengkul trumpet, also written peengkul, with plural te) (e:~ leh sa-ki aw tawh) (s:peengkulte) (r:19.98.6) (q:draft)
pengpelep = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:night hawk/screech owl) (d:an unclean bird in the food laws, in the place where English versions have night hawk or screech owl) (e:kalaoh-vasa, ~, vatawt, musi nam khempeuh) (r:3.11.16/5.14.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
pengsak = (t:v) (w:deliver/spare/keep safe) (d:peng, be free from, with the causative sak: make someone escape harm, or get a burden free) (e:siatna panin kei hong ~ in/mipilte’ pauna in sat nading pan ~ hi | the speech of the wise keeps them from a beating/amaute in vangik ~ thei lo uh a | they cannot rescue the burden) (s:suaktasak/honkhia) (b:peng) (r:16.13.22/20.14.3/23.46.2) (q:draft)
pengthei = (t:v) (w:be able to escape/be exempt) (d:peng, be free from or escape, with thei, can) (e:nang a ~ tuam dingin kingaihsun/a ~ kuamah om lo hi | there is no one who can escape) (s:pelhthei/suahtakzo) (b:peng) (r:24.45.5/21.8.8) (q:draft)
Peniel = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Peniel) (d:place by the Jabbok where Jacob wrestled with God and saw him face to face; the name means face of God, and it is also spelled Penuel) (r:1.32.30/1.32.31)
penin = (t:part) (d:pen, most, with the ending -in, after a descriptive word: as the most, in the first or last place; a masa penin, first; a nunung penin, last) (e:A nunung ~ a numei zong a si hi/numei-nasemte leh a tate a masa ~ | the female servants and their children first/Rachel leh Josef a nunung ~ koih hi | he put Rachel and Joseph last/leitung kumpite lakah a sang ~ ka bawl ding hi | I will make him the highest among the kings of the earth/ama gal lian ~ kei hong ngaihsun hi | he counts me as his greatest enemy) (r:40.22.27/1.33.2/19.89.27/18.19.11) (q:draft)
Peninnah = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Peninnah) (d:one of the two wives of Elkanah, who had children and provoked the childless Hannah) (r:9.1.2/9.1.4)
penna = (t:part) (d:pen, most, with the ending -na: follows a describing word to mark the highest degree, as in a gamla penna mun, the farthest place) (e:leihawm thuk ~ Leihawm sungah/leitaw lam a gamla ~ mun-ah | at the farthest place to the south/Izipt gam khempeuh a hoih ~ | the best of all the land of Egypt) (r:23.14.15/6.15.1/1.45.20) (q:draft, low confidence)
penpa = (t:part) (d:pen marks the highest degree and pa a man: placed after a describing word it names the man who is most so, as masa penpa the first one, lian penpa the greatest one) (e:ci-in a masa ~ a dong hi/galkap mang lian ~ in | the supreme commander/note lakah a neu ~ in milian ahi ding hi | the least among you will be the great one/Paul in thugen ~ ahih ciangin | because Paul was the chief speaker) (r:42.16.5/23.20.1/42.9.48/44.14.12) (q:draft)
Penpa = (t:n) (d:the one who is most, pen most with pa marking a male person; Sang Penpa is the Most High, a title of God) (e:Sang ~ bangin ka kibawl ding hi/Sang ~’ liahna sungah a om mi | one who lives in the shelter of the Most High/Sang ~’ tate, pasiante, na hi uh hi | you are gods, children of the Most High/Sang ~ tungah na thuciamnate uh bawl un | fulfil your vows to the Most High) (b:Pen) (r:23.14.14/19.91.1/19.82.6/19.50.14) (q:draft)
penpen = (t:part) (w:the very most) (d:doubled pen, most, placed after a descriptive word for a strong superlative: the very best, the worst ever) (e:Amah in leitang hoih ~ zong a/a nasia ~ gimna hun a hong tung ding hi | a time of the most severe distress will come/a it ~ khuapi hong hi kik ding hi | it will again be the most beloved city) (r:20.31.16/27.12.1/38.2.12) (q:draft)
penpen = (t:part) (d:placed after a verb phrase: whichever one, the very one that) (e:nih lakah na teel ~ hong lak in/a kimuhna ~ ka sila hi ding a | whoever it is found with will be my slave/tua hai a kimuhna ~ kithat hen la | let the one the cup is found with be put to death) (r:44.1.25/1.44.10/1.44.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
penpente = (t:part) (d:penpen, the very most, with the plural te, placed after a descriptive word: those who are the very strongest, wisest and so on) (e:a galkap thahat ~ in Shadrak/ahi zongin a pil ~ ahi hi | yet they are the very wisest) (b:penpen) (r:27.3.20/20.30.24) (q:draft)
pente = (t:part) (w:most) (d:superlative marker pen with the plural te, placed after a describing word, the most or the best ones) (e:Mi thupi ~ nangawn/Minam gilo ~ hong paipihin | bringing the most wicked nations/mi thahat ~ nangawn lau a | even the mightiest are afraid/Ka lawm it ~ nangawn in kei hong muhdah | even my dearest friends detest me/A galkap muanhuai ~, gal sungah si ding a | his most trusted soldiers will die in battle) (b:pen) (r:18.29.10/1.27.15/26.7.24/18.41.25/18.19.19/26.17.21) (q:draft)
Pentekos = (t:name) (w:Pentecost) (d:Jewish harvest feast held fifty days after Passover, the day on which the Holy Spirit came upon the believers in Jerusalem) (r:44.2.1/46.16.8)
Pentekost = (t:name) (w:Pentecost) (d:spelling of Pentekos with a final t: the feast held fifty days after Passover, the day on which the Holy Spirit came upon the believers) (r:46.16.8/44.2.1)
penteng = (t:part) (d:the superlative word pen, most, with teng, all: all of the most, as in a limci penteng, all the best) (e:a limci ~ le kei tungah) (r:26.44.30) (q:draft, low confidence)
Penuel = (t:name) (c:place/male) (w:Penuel) (d:town east of the Jordan whose tower Gideon tore down, the same place as Peniel; also the name of two men, a descendant of Judah and a son of Shashak of Benjamin) (r:7.8.8/13.8.25)
Peor = (t:name) (c:mountain) (w:Peor) (d:mountain in Moab to whose top Balak took Balaam; also the place where Israel joined in the worship of the Baal of Peor) (r:4.23.28)
Perazim = (t:name) (c:mountain) (w:Perazim) (d:mountain where the Lord broke out against the Philistines for David, the place also called Baal Perazim; found in Perazim Mual, Mount Perazim) (r:23.28.21) (q:draft)
Pere = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Perizzite) (d:spelling of the name of the Perizzites in Pere mite, one of the peoples who lived in Canaan before Israel) (e:Amor mite, ~ mite, Hiv mite) (r:2.3.17) (q:draft)
Peresh = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Peresh) (d:son of Makir and Maakah in the tribe of Manasseh, brother of Sheresh) (r:13.7.16)
Perez = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Rephaim)
Perez = (t:name) (c:land/people) (w:Perizzites) (d:in Perez mite, the Perizzites, one of the peoples who lived in Canaan before Israel) (r:1.15.20)
Perez-uzza = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Perez Uzzah) (d:place on the way to Jerusalem where Uzzah died after touching the ark; the name means outbreak against Uzzah) (e:tu ni dongin ~ kici hi) (r:13.13.11) (q:draft)
Perez-uzzah = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Perez Uzzah) (d:place on the way to Jerusalem where Uzzah died after touching the ark; the name means outbreak against Uzzah) (e:tua mun ~ kici hi) (r:10.6.8) (q:draft)
Perezuzza = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Perez Uzzah) (d:spelling of Perez-uzza without the hyphen: the place where Uzzah died after touching the ark) (e:tuni dongin ~ kici hi) (r:13.13.11) (q:draft)
Perezuzzah = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Perez Uzzah) (d:spelling of Perez-uzzah without the hyphen: the place where Uzzah died after touching the ark) (r:10.6.8)
Perga = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Perga) (d:city in Pamphylia in Asia Minor, visited by Paul and Barnabas on their first journey, where John Mark left them) (r:44.14.25/44.13.14)
Pergamum = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Pergamum) (d:city in Asia Minor, home of one of the seven churches addressed in Revelation) (r:66.2.12/66.1.11)
Perida = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Perida) (d:head of a family of the servants of Solomon whose descendants returned from the exile; called Peruda in Ezra) (r:16.7.57)
Persia = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Persia) (d:land and empire east of Babylonia, ruled by kings such as Cyrus and Darius, under whom the Jews returned from exile) (r:27.8.20/15.1.8)
Persian = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Persian)
Persian = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Persian) (d:a person of Persia, as Cyrus the Persian)
Persiate = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Persians) (d:the people of Persia, usually named together with the Medes in Mediate leh Persiate, the Medes and Persians) (b:Persia) (r:27.6.15/27.5.28)
