petin = (t:v) (w:biting) (d:pet, bite, with the linking ending in: biting, or holding something in the mouth or beak) (e:sakol’ khetul ~ a tuangpa nungkiat hi/a mukah ~ hong tunpih hi | it brought it back held in its beak) (b:pet) (r:1.49.17/1.8.11) (q:draft)
petin = (t:adv) (d:in tu pet petin, at this very moment, now at last; pet marks the exact time) (e:Tu pet ~ hih in keima guhte) (r:1.2.23) (q:draft, low confidence)
petkham = (t:v) (w:gnaw/bite to pieces/chew) (d:pet, bite, with kham, so that it breaks) (e:a hai na ~ ding hi) (r:26.23.34) (q:draft)
