phuk = (t:v) (w:cut down/fell) (d:cut down a tree, timber or a wooden idol with an axe; sing phuk is fell trees) (e:amaute in sing ~ uh hi/tulak singte hei tawh ~ ding a | he will cut down the forest trees with an axe/Ahih kei leh na ~ ding hi | if not, you shall cut it down/a gei-a om Asherah milim ~ in | cut down the Asherah pole beside it/singkung hoih khempeuh ~ uh hi | they cut down every good tree) (r:12.6.4/23.10.34/42.13.9/7.6.25/12.3.25) (q:draft)
phukgawp = (t:v) (w:hack down/demolish/cut down) (d:phuk cut down, with gawp roughly or violently) (e:zong hei tawh ~ ding uh hi) (b:phuk) (r:26.26.9) (q:draft)
phukha = (t:v) (w:press against/crowd/jostle/strike against/run into) (d:push or knock up against someone or something, as a crowd presses on a person or a ship strikes a sandbar; also meet with danger or hardship) (e:mihonpi in amah a ~ uh hi/mi tampite in a nung zui-in a ~ uh hi | many people followed and pressed against him/mihonpite in nang hong ~ a | the crowds are pressing against you/teembaw in sehnel hong ~-in a tum hi | the ship struck a sandbar and ran aground/haksatna a tuamtuam ~-in | meeting all kinds of hardship) (r:42.8.42/41.5.24/42.8.45/44.27.41/47.8.2) (q:draft)
phukham = (t:v) (w:burst/break open/break through) (d:break something by force or pressure, as a door, a wineskin or an enemy line; of a rash, break out on the skin) (e:a savun um ~ ding a/kongkhak a ~ zah dongin hong neh uh hi | they pressed forward until the door was about to break/Topa in ka mai-ah ka galte ~ hi | the Lord has broken through my enemies before me/leenggahzu in savun um ~ ding a | the wine will burst the wineskins/tua pen vun a ~ meima hi a | it is a rash that has broken out on the skin) (r:42.5.37/10.5.20/1.19.9/41.2.22/3.13.39) (q:draft)
phukhamin = (t:v) (w:break out/burst) (d:phukham break out, with the linking ending in, joining it to the next verb; of a disease breaking out over the skin) (e:tua natna in a vun ~) (b:phukham) (r:3.13.12) (q:draft)
phukhia = (t:v) (w:break out/break through/erupt) (d:phu, push against, with khia, out: force a way out or through; of a skin disease, break out on the skin) (e:meimatum sung tawnin hong ~ ahi hi/Edom kumpipa’ santak a ~ dingin | to break through to the king of Edom/amaute in ~ zo lo uh hi | they could not break through/meikangma tawnin hong ~ hi a | it has broken out in the burn) (b:phu) (r:3.13.20/12.3.26/3.13.25) (q:draft)
phukhong = (t:n) (d:found with vei, suffer from, in phukhong vei, be famished, faint with hunger and tiredness) (e:bang hang hiam cih leh ~ vei ing/gamlak panin hong ciahin ~ vei hi | he came in from the open country famished) (r:1.25.30/1.25.29) (q:draft, low confidence)
phukin = (t:v) (w:cutting down/felling) (d:phuk with the linking suffix -in; the action is followed by another verb) (e:milim ~ Kidron lui ah hal hi/singkung hoih khempeuh ~, tuinak khempeuh na khakcip ding a | you will cut down every good tree and stop up all the springs/na paknamtui biakna taute uh ~ | cutting down your incense altars/tua singkung ~ nusia cip ding uh hi | they will cut that tree down and leave it) (b:phuk) (r:11.15.13/12.3.19/3.26.30/26.31.12) (q:draft)
phukmai = (t:v) (w:cut down/chop down) (d:phuk cut down, with mai, apparently clear away; of felling a forest) (e:a singte uh a ~ sak teitei) (r:24.46.23) (q:draft, low confidence)
phukmaisak = (t:v) (w:cut down/chop down) (d:phukmai cut down and clear, with sak; of felling the trees of another) (e:a singte uh a ~ teitei ding uh hi) (b:phukmai) (r:24.46.23) (q:draft, low confidence)
phukmang = (t:v) (w:cut down/fell/clear away) (d:phuk cut down with mang, away or gone: cut trees down and clear them away) (e:A taamtak sangpente ka ~ khin a/a taaksan hoihpente zong ka ~ khin hi | I have also cut down its choicest junipers) (r:12.19.23) (q:draft)
phukpai = (t:v) (w:cut down/hew down/fell) (d:phuk fell with pai away, said of idols and sacred poles) (e:amau’ Asherah milimte na ~ ding hi/a kiseek amau’ pasiante’ limte na ~ ding uh a | you shall cut down the carved images of their gods/Asherah milim ~ hi | he cut down the Asherah pole) (r:2.34.13/5.12.3/12.18.4) (q:draft)
phuksak = (t:v) (w:cut down/fell) (d:phuk cut down, with sak: cut down trees or timber, or have them cut down) (e:A singte ~ unla/na sidar khuam hoihpente hong ~ ding uh a | they will cut down your fine cedar beams) (b:phuk) (r:24.6.6/24.22.7) (q:draft)
phuksakin = (t:v) (w:cutting down/felling) (d:phuksak, cut down, with the linking ending in) (e:a nu’ milim ~ satnen a/amau’ Asherah milimte ~ | cutting down their Asherah poles/hong ~ mei-ah hong khulsak ding uh hi | they will cut them down and throw them into the fire) (b:phuksak) (r:14.15.16/24.22.7/5.7.5) (q:draft)
phuktan = (t:v) (w:cut down/fell) (d:phuk cut down with tan cut off: cut a tree right down) (e:lai takin ~ ni) (s:sattan) (r:24.11.19) (q:draft)
phukte = (t:n) (w:cutters/woodcutters/fellers) (d:phuk cut down with the plural te: those who cut down; sing a phukte, those who fell timber) (e:nasem sing a ~) (s:singsuite) (b:phuk) (r:14.2.10) (q:draft)
phul = (t:v) (w:gush out/pour out/flow out/spring up) (d:of water, come out from a spring, well or rock; phul khia, gush out) (e:tua sung panin tui hong ~ hi/Tuikhuk panin tui siang hong ~ bangin | as a well pours out fresh water/Jerusalem khua panin siatna ~ hi | wickedness pours out of Jerusalem/tua suang panin tui hong ~ khia ding hi | water will come out of that rock/tuilim leh tuikha ~ khia khawm thei ahi hiam | can fresh water and salt water flow out together) (s:luangkhia) (r:7.15.19/24.6.7/2.17.6/59.3.11) (q:draft)
Phul = (t:v) (w:spring up/gush out) (d:of water, come up from a well or spring) (e:Tuikhuk aw, ~ in) (b:phul) (r:4.21.17) (q:draft)
phula = (t:v) (w:avenge/take vengeance/take revenge) (d:phu vengeance with la take, written here as one word) (e:a hehna tawh ~ nuampa in/a bawlsiat laitak a muh ciangin ~-in | when he saw him being mistreated he avenged him) (s:thuhkik/thukkik) (a:maisak) (r:5.19.6/44.7.24) (q:draft)
phulak = (t:v) (w:avenge/take vengeance) (d:pay back a wrong done; phulak ni is the day of vengeance) (e:keima khut tawh ~ nading panin/~ ni khat nei hi | he has a day of vengeance/a galte uh ~ ding hun hi ta hi | the time to take vengeance on their enemies has come/a galte tungah Pasian ~ ding hun | the time when God takes vengeance on his enemies) (s:thuhkik/thukkik) (a:maisak) (b:phula) (r:9.25.33/23.34.8/23.63.4/23.61.2) (q:draft)
phulakna = (t:n) (w:vengeance/revenge) (d:the act of taking revenge or avenging) (e:a ~ thu Zion khua-a tangko dingin/~ leh thukkikna kei’ aa ahi hi | vengeance and repayment are mine/~ a sem ding, Midiante a do dingin | to carry out vengeance, to fight the Midianites/Keima ~ zia Edom mite in thei ding uh hi | the Edomites will know my vengeance) (s:thukkikna/thuhkikna) (a:maisakna) (b:phulak) (r:24.50.28/5.32.35/4.31.3/26.25.14) (q:draft)
phulapa = (t:n) (w:avenger/avenger of blood) (d:the man who takes revenge, in the law the relative who avenges a killing; -pa marks a man) (e:a sih theih nadingin ~ tungah ap ding hi/mi thatpa leh a ~ kikalah | between the killer and the avenger/a ~ in mi thatpa a thah leh | if the avenger kills the killer/~ in amah a delh leh | if the avenger pursues him) (s:thukpa) (r:5.19.12/4.35.27/4.35.24/6.20.5) (q:draft)
phulet = (t:v) (w:break through/breach) (d:break right through a wall or barrier) (e:kumpipa’ khuapi kulh a ~ uh hi/gialpi leh mei-amte in ama meii sahpite ~ hi | hail and lightning broke through his thick clouds) (r:24.39.2/19.18.12) (q:draft)
phulin = (t:v) (w:break through/burst through) (d:phul break or burst through, with the linking ending in) (e:Filistiate’ giahphual ~ kulh kongpi gei-a) (b:phul) (r:10.23.16/13.11.18) (q:draft)
phulkham = (t:v) (w:break out against/burst upon) (d:break through and overwhelm, as a flood breaks out) (e:ka galte ~ hi) (r:13.14.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
phulkhap = (t:v) (w:break out/burst through) (d:said of flood water that bursts through what holds it back) (e:Tuikhang in a ~ bangin) (r:10.5.20/13.14.11) (q:draft)
phulkhia = (t:v) (w:gush out/burst forth/spring out) (d:of water, come out with force from rock or ground) (e:suangpi hong a, tui ~ hi/tui tampi ~-in | much water gushed out/gamlakah tui hong ~ ding a | water will gush out in the wilderness/tua suang sung panin tui hong ~ ding hi | water will come out of that rock) (s:luangkhia) (b:phul) (r:19.105.41/23.35.6/4.20.11/2.17.6) (q:draft)
phulkhiasak = (t:v) (w:make gush out/bring forth) (d:phulkhia burst out, with the causative sak: make water or springs burst out) (e:kuamte sung panin ciktui na ~ hi/hih suangpi panin note ading tui hong ~ ding | to bring water out of this rock for you) (s:phulsak) (b:phulkhia) (r:19.104.10/4.20.10) (q:draft)
phulsak = (t:v) (w:make gush out/open up/bring forth) (d:phul burst out, with the causative sak: make water or a spring break out) (e:suangpi panin tui na ~ a/ciktuite leh luite na ~ a | you opened up springs and streams) (s:phulkhiasak) (a:kangsak) (b:phul) (r:16.9.15/19.74.15) (q:draft)
phum = (t:v) (w:bury/hide in the ground) (d:put a dead person or a thing under the ground; sum phum is buried treasure) (e:amah a ~ dingin amaute a pai/kumpi inn lutna suangphah nuaiah ~ in | bury them under the pavement at the entrance of the palace/a ni mah-in na ~ ding uh hi | you shall bury him that same day/Saul leh a tapa Jonathan’ guhte ~ uh hi | they buried the bones of Saul and his son Jonathan/sum ~ zon’ sangin | more than searching for buried treasure) (s:vui) (a:tokhia) (r:12.9.35/18.3.21/24.43.9/5.21.23/10.21.14) (q:draft)
phum = (t:v) (w:baptize/immerse) (d:with tui, water: dip in water, baptize) (e:mite tui a ~ hi/tui sungah note kong ~ a | I baptize you in water/Kha Siangtho sungah note hong ~ ding hi | he will baptize you in the Holy Spirit/a nungzuite bek in a ~ ahi hi | it was only his disciples who baptized) (s:tuiphum/baptaiz) (r:43.3.22/43.4.2/41.1.8) (q:draft)
phumcip = (t:v) (w:bury/submerge/swallow up) (d:put completely under earth or water; phum with cip, tightly, completely) (e:Lei sungah amaute ~ in la/tui sungah i ~ hangin mit zo lo hi | even if we plunge it in water it does not go out/nuntakna sungah a ~ dingin | so that it may be swallowed up in life) (s:vukcip) (b:phum) (r:18.40.13/22.8.7/47.5.4) (q:draft)
phumin = (t:v) (w:baptize/immerse) (d:phum baptize, with the linking ending in; tui phumin, baptizing in water) (e:Johan in mite tui ~ a omna) (b:phum) (r:43.1.28) (q:draft)
phumin = (t:v) (w:bury/bow down) (d:phum bury, with the linking ending in; ka lu phumin, with my head buried in my bosom, of a person bowed in prayer) (e:Ka ang ah ka lu ~ thu ka ngen a) (b:phum) (r:19.35.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
phumlam = (t:n) (d:the burying or the way of burying; phum bury, with lam, the manner or fact of doing) (e:Na ~ Judah mi khempeuh musak in) (r:24.43.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
phumte = (t:n) (w:buried things/buried ones) (d:phum bury with the plural te: the things that have been buried; ka suang phumte, the stones I have buried) (e:hih ka suang ~’ tungah) (b:phum) (r:24.43.10) (q:draft)
phumtheih = (t:v) (w:can immerse/can baptize) (d:phum immerse, with theih can, the form used before nading; tui phum is baptize) (e:Johan in tui a ~ nading thu) (b:phum) (r:41.11.30) (q:draft)
phun = (t:v) (w:grumble/murmur/complain) (d:speak out one’s discontent, grumble or complain; with tungah, against someone) (e:puanbuk sung uh-ah ~ uh a/Moses' tungah mite ~ uh a | the people grumbled against Moses/ka gim luat manin ka ~ ding hi | I will complain because of my great distress/na puanbukte uh sungah na ~ uh a | you grumbled in your tents/Israel mihon buppi ~ uh a | the whole community of Israel grumbled) (a:lungkim) (r:19.106.25/2.16.2/2.15.24/18.7.11/5.1.27) (q:draft)
phung = (t:n) (w:wall/earthwork/ramp) (d:a wall or bank of earth or stone, as around a field or raised against a city) (e:mi’ ~ a phelsakte/a pang tuakah ~ a omna lam kawcik ah | in a narrow path with walls on both sides/khuapi dona-in ~ zong ciang lo ding hi | he will not build a siege ramp against the city) (s:kulh) (r:21.10.8/4.22.24/12.19.32) (q:draft)
phung = (t:n) (w:clan/family/lineage) (d:the family line a person belongs to) (e:ama nam leh ~ gen khia lo hi/amau’ ~ sung panin a makaite | the leaders from their ancestral clans/amau’ beh leh ~ a kan thei lo mite | those who could not trace their clan and lineage/a beh a ~, a suan a khakte khempeuh | all his clan and family, his offspring and descendants) (s:beh) (r:17.2.10/4.1.16/15.2.59/23.22.24) (q:draft)
phungah = (t:prep) (w:at the foot of/at the base of/at the root of) (d:phung with the place marker ah; khe phungah, at the feet of) (e:Tu-in zong sing ~ hei a om hi/ama khe ~ amah tuk hi | at her feet he sank/Ama khe ~ pukin | falling at his feet/hong pai-in ama khe ~ hong bok hi | she came and fell at his feet) (b:phung) (r:40.3.10/7.5.27/9.25.24/41.7.25) (q:draft)
phungah = (t:prep) (w:around/beside) (d:of people sitting by a pot to eat or drink: sabeel phungah, around the pot of meat; zu phungah, at the wine) (e:Kote sabeel ~ tu-in ka kham takun/Zu ~ lungdam a, la sakna om nawn lo a | there is no more rejoicing and singing over the wine) (r:2.16.3/23.24.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
phungcian = (t:v) (w:build up a wall/wall up) (d:phung wall with cian pile up: build a wall of piled stones; a phungcian suangte, the stones of its built wall) (e:a umna a ~’ suangte kicim khin hi) (r:20.24.31) (q:draft, low confidence)
phungin = (t:n) (w:ramp/earthwork/siege ramp) (d:phung earthwork with the ending in, as: phungin ciang, pile up as a ramp against a city) (e:khua sim nadingin ~ ciang un) (b:phung) (r:24.6.6) (q:draft)
phungmai = (t:n) (w:wall/rampart) (d:the wall or rampart of a city or building; hyssop is said to grow on it) (e:a kulh ~ hoihte ngaihsunin/~ a, a po puknahte dongin | to the hyssop that grows on the wall) (r:19.48.12/11.4.33) (q:draft, low confidence)
phungpi = (t:n) (w:seat of honour) (d:phung with pi great; in pahtawi ngahna phungpi, where the English has a seat of honour for the house of his father; the exact sense of phungpi itself is not clear from the verse) (e:pahtawi ngahna ~ suak ding hi) (r:23.22.23) (q:draft, low confidence)
phungsung = (t:n) (w:stock/stump/family line) (d:phung clan or lineage with sung inside; the single verse has it for the stump of Jesse) (e:~ panin a sel khat) (r:23.11.1) (q:draft, low confidence)
phungte = (t:n) (w:ramps/earthworks/siege mounds) (d:phung wall or bank of earth, with the plural te) (e:a kiim-ah dumte, ~, galpan’na phualte) (b:phung) (r:26.4.2) (q:draft)
phungte = (t:n) (w:relatives/kindred/clan) (d:phung clan or family line, with the plural te; na beh na phungte is your own people) (e:na beh na ~ kiang panin/a beh a ~ le a lawm itteng | his relatives and his close friends) (s:behte/tanaute) (b:phung) (r:44.7.3/44.10.24) (q:draft)
phunin = (t:v) (w:grumbling/complaining/murmuring) (d:phun, grumble, with the linking ending in, joining it to the next verb) (e:Moses’ tungah mite ~/Tua mite in ~ a mawhsak thei mi | these people are grumblers and faultfinders) (b:phun) (r:2.17.3/65.1.16) (q:draft)
phunkhak = (t:v) (w:grumble/complain/criticize) (d:phun grumble, with khak happen to, the form used before loh: so that no one may come to complain) (e:mi a ~ loh nadingun) (r:47.8.20) (q:draft)
phunna = (t:n) (w:grumbling/complaint/murmuring) (d:phun, grumble, with the noun suffix na: grumbling or a complaint) (e:Israel mite’ ~ ka za khin hi/tunga na ~ uh amah in za khin ahih manin | because he has heard your grumbling against him/ihmu leng ka ~ phatuam ding hi | if I sleep my complaint will be eased/a nungzuite’ ~ thei ahih manin | because he knew of his disciples’ grumbling) (b:phun) (r:4.14.27/18.7.13/2.16.7/43.6.61) (q:draft)
phunnate = (t:n) (w:grumblings/complaints/murmurings) (d:phunna, grumbling, with the plural te) (e:Israel mite’ ~ ka za khin hi/Amah in note’ ~ za khin ahih manin | because he has heard your grumblings/Note’ ~ in kote’ tung hi loin | your grumblings are not against us) (b:phunna) (r:2.16.12/2.16.8/2.16.9) (q:draft)
phunphun = (t:v) (w:complain/grumble/murmur) (d:phun doubled: keep on complaining or muttering; zi phunphun is a nagging wife) (e:bang hanga ~ ding i hi hiam/a ~ mite in thuhilhna ngai ta ding uh hi | those who complain will accept instruction/a lupna tung panun ~ bek uh hi | they only wail on their beds/zi ~ in a theu thei lo guahciin tawh | a nagging wife, like rain that does not stop dripping) (r:25.3.39/20.19.13/23.29.24/28.7.14) (q:draft)
phunpihna = (t:n) (w:grumbling/complaint) (d:phun grumble, with pih about or together and the noun suffix na) (e:a nungzuite in a ~ thu) (r:43.6.61) (q:draft)
phunsan = (t:v) (w:grumble against/murmur against/complain against) (d:phun grumble with san directed at someone) (e:Moses leh Aaron ~ uh a/bang tanvei kei hong ~ ding ahi uh hiam | how long will they grumble against me/Pasian i ~ kei ding hi | we must not grumble against God/Topa ~ kei hamtang un | only do not grumble against the Lord) (b:phun) (r:4.16.41/4.14.27/46.10.10/4.14.9) (q:draft)
phunsanna = (t:n) (w:grumbling/complaint/murmuring) (d:grumbling against someone) (e:amaute in nang hong ~/kei hong ~ uh ahi Israel mite’ phunna | the grumbling of the Israelites against me/Israel mite in Topa a ~ | where the Israelites grumbled against the Lord) (b:phunsan) (r:4.17.5/4.14.27/4.20.13) (q:draft)
phunsansak = (t:v) (w:make grumble against) (d:phunsan grumble against, with sak cause) (e:mihonte Topa a ~) (b:phunsan) (r:4.14.36) (q:draft)
phunsante = (t:n) (w:grumblers/those who grumble against) (d:phunsan grumble against, with the plural te: those who have grumbled against someone) (e:tungsiah, kei hong ~) (b:phunsan) (r:4.14.29) (q:draft)
phusak = (t:v) (w:drive toward/make head for) (d:phu head into or push against, with sak cause; of steering a ship toward the shore) (e:lamah teembaw a ~ uh hi) (b:phu) (r:44.27.40) (q:draft, low confidence)
phusuakin = (t:adv) (w:heading straight on/blundering on) (d:apparently phu head into with suak through and the ending in: going straight on into danger without turning aside) (e:mi mawkmawkte in ~ thuak uh hi) (r:20.27.12/20.22.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
phut = (t:v) (w:set up/erect/establish/plant) (d:set something firmly in place, as a pillar, a foundation or a people) (e:a inn ding khuampi sagih ~ hi/suang khat la-in khuamin ~ hi | he took a stone and set it up as a pillar/Topa in ama tokhom vantungah ~ khin a | the Lord has established his throne in heaven/tuipite tungah a bul ~ a | he founded it on the seas/a muhdah khuampi na ~ kei ding uh hi | you shall not set up a pillar that he hates) (s:dingsak) (r:20.9.1/19.104.5/1.31.45/19.103.19/19.24.2/5.16.22) (q:draft)
phutin = (t:v) (w:set up/erect/establish) (d:phut with -in, linking it to the next verb: setting up, having erected) (e:a khuam ~ a min Jakhin phuak hi/ama adingin phawkna mual khat ~ | setting up a monument for himself/thutan’na leh thumanna ~ a kipsak nadingin | to establish and uphold it with justice and righteousness/suang manpha ~ a inn zeem hi | he adorned the temple by setting precious stones) (b:phut) (r:11.7.21/9.15.12/23.9.7/14.3.6) (q:draft)
phutkhak = (t:v) (w:encounter/come upon/meet) (d:come up against someone or something on the way) (e:note’ ~ ding mi khempeuh/lungkhamna tuipi a ~ uh ciangin | when they come up against the sea of trouble) (r:2.23.27/38.10.11) (q:draft)
phutkhin = (t:v) (w:have established/have set up) (d:phut set up, with khin already done) (e:vantungah ama tokhom ~ a) (b:phut) (r:19.103.19) (q:draft)
phutna = (t:n) (w:press/onset) (d:phut with the noun suffix na; gal in a phutna, the place where battle presses hard, where the English has the heat of battle) (e:gal in a ~ panin hong tai uh) (r:23.21.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
phutsak = (t:v) (w:have set up/cause to be erected) (d:phut set up, with the causative sak: have someone set a thing up) (e:a khuam ~ hi/Pi sawmsagih-le-nga a sang khuam ~ in la | have a pole seventy-five feet high set up) (b:phut) (r:17.5.14) (q:draft)
phutthei = (t:v) (w:can lay/can set up) (d:phut set up, with thei can) (e:khuam thupi dang ~ nawn lo ding hi) (b:phut) (r:46.3.11) (q:draft)
pi = (t:n) (w:foot) (d:unit of length, a foot; where the English Bible has cubits the number is converted, one cubit counted as a foot and a half) (e:a tun’ ~ kua val a sang/a dung ~ sawmthum pha-in | being thirty feet long/tuate tungah ~ sawmnih le nih thuk-in tuumcip hi | it covered them to a depth of twenty-two feet/A dung ~ sawmkua hi a | its length was ninety feet) (r:9.17.4/1.6.15/38.5.2/1.7.20/14.3.3) (q:draft)
pi = (t:n) (w:mother/dam/female/grandmother) (d:with a before it, the mother of a young animal or the female of an animal, as vom a pi, a she-bear; of a person, a pi is the grandmother) (e:A ~’ lametna teng bei ta hi/a ~ na khah ding a | you shall let the mother go/a ~’ nawizu tawh keelno | a young goat in its mother’s milk/a ~ tawh ni sagih sung omkhawm ding hi | it shall stay with its mother for seven days/a ~ Ma-akah zong khinkhia hi | he also deposed his grandmother Maakah) (r:26.19.5/12.2.24/5.22.7/2.23.19/3.22.27/11.15.13) (q:draft)
pi = (t:part) (d:suffix added to a noun or adjective, big, great or chief) (e:kham milim ~ khat bawl saka/Zion khua ~ in nang hong simmawh a | the great city of Zion despises you) (r:27.3.1/12.19.21) (q:draft, low confidence)
pia = (t:v) (w:give/grant) (d:hand something over to someone or grant it; thu pia is give an order and thupha pia is bless) (e:Zingsol zong amah ka ~ ding hi/Dawimangpa hun na ~ kei un | do not give the devil an opportunity/Makhir tungah Gilead ka ~ a | I gave Gilead to Makir/A ta in khomun ngen leh, suang a ~ ding | if his child asks for bread, will he give a stone/ka khamkhop ding uh an hong ~ in | give us the food we need) (a:ngah/lak) (r:66.2.28/49.4.27/5.3.15/40.7.9/40.6.11)
Pia = (t:v) (w:give) (d:pia, give, written with a capital at the start of a sentence; pia khia is give up or hand over) (e:~ khia un, leitaw lam kiangah/~ ding ihi hiam | should we give/~ ta un | give it then) (b:pia) (r:23.43.6/41.12.15/40.14.9) (q:draft)
piagawp = (t:v) (w:inflict harshly) (d:pia give, with gawp roughly or severely; gim piagawp is punish severely) (e:khasiat loin gim ~ hi) (b:pia) (r:20.20.26) (q:draft, low confidence)
piak = (t:v) (w:gave/give/given) (d:form of pia, give, used in dependent clauses and before endings and words such as ding, ciangin and bangin) (e:hih bang lamlahnate kong ~ uh/Na ~ uh khuapite in | the towns that you give/Tu ni-a no kong ~ hih thute | these words that I give you today/Topa in thu a ~ ciangin | when the Lord gives the command/Kei tawh a om dinga nong ~ numei | the woman you gave to be with me) (b:pia) (r:52.4.2/1.3.12/4.35.13/5.6.6/30.6.11)
Piak = (t:v) (w:give) (d:piak, form of pia give used before a noun; Gim Piak Ni, the day suffering is given, is the day of punishment) (e:Gim ~ Ni | the Day of Punishment/~ nopna lungsim a nei mi peuhmah | everyone who had a heart willing to give) (b:piak) (r:42.21.22/2.35.21) (q:draft)
piakha = (t:v) (w:may give/happen to give) (d:pia give, with kha perhaps or happen to) (e:thupha hong ~ ding hi) (r:29.2.14) (q:draft)
piakhawm = (t:v) (w:give together/offer along with) (d:pia give with khawm together: give or offer one thing with another) (e:an-a biakna tawh ~ ding hi/nang tawh Filistiate khut sungah hong ~ ding hi | he will give them with you into the hands of the Philistines/dahna, gimna tawh ~ lo hi | he does not give sorrow and toil along with it/silngo tawh keimah biakpiakna si na ~ kei | do not offer the blood of my sacrifice along with yeast) (b:pia) (r:3.14.31/2.34.25/9.28.19/20.10.22) (q:draft)
piakhia = (t:v) (w:give out/give away/give up/hand over) (d:pia give with khia out) (e:sihna dongin a nuntakna ~ a/mihoihte cingh-in, ~ tawntung uh hi | the righteous are generous and keep on giving/leiseek a mal ngeina zah mah na ~ ding uh hi | you must hand over the same number of bricks as before/eite khempeuh a dingin hong ~ ahih manin | because he gave him up for us all/aksi honpite in khuavakna ~ lo ding hi | the constellations will not give out their light) (b:pia) (r:23.53.12/20.21.26/2.5.18/45.8.32/23.13.10) (q:draft)
piakhin = (t:v) (w:have given/have granted) (d:pia with khin, already: the giving is done) (e:deihna nang in na ~ a/ko hong hoisak leenggahzu nong ~ hi | you have given us wine that makes us stagger/i dawn dingin gutui hong ~ zo hi | he has given us poisoned water to drink/note tungah Kha Siangtho hong ~ ahih manin | because he has given you the Holy Spirit) (s:piazo) (b:pia) (r:19.21.2/62.2.20/19.60.3/24.8.14) (q:draft)
piakhol = (t:v) (w:command beforehand/give in advance) (d:pia give with khol beforehand; thu piakhol, give an order or a word ahead of time) (e:ci-in thu ~ ahih manin/ci-in thu a ~ hi | so he declared beforehand) (r:23.36.21/44.7.7) (q:draft)
piakik = (t:v) (w:give back/return/restore) (d:pia give with kik back, again) (e:nang tungah kong ~ ding hi/hong zon’ ciangin na ~ ding hi | when he comes looking for it you shall give it back/nitum ma-in ama' tungah na ~ ding hi | you shall return it to him before sunset/ama' tungah a zi Sarah ~ hi | he returned his wife Sarah to him/ama’ aa ahi khempeuh ~ in | give back everything that was hers) (a:lakik) (b:pia) (r:7.17.3/12.8.6/5.22.2/2.22.26/1.20.14) (q:draft)
piakkhawm = (t:v) (w:give together with/offer along with) (d:give one thing together with another, of the grain offering that goes with an animal offering; piak, give, with khawm, together) (e:tuutal khat tawh ~ dingin/tuunote tawh ~ ding pen | what is to be given along with the lambs) (b:piak) (r:4.15.6/26.46.11) (q:draft)
piakkhiat = (t:v) (w:give out/give up/lay down) (d:give away from oneself; nuntakna piakkhiat is lay down the life) (e:Ka nuntakna ~ theih nading/a neih khempeuh a ~ ngam kei leh | if he does not dare to give up all he has/lungkim takin a ~ zuahzuahte uh | what they have freely given) (b:piak) (r:43.10.18/15.7.16/42.14.33) (q:draft)
piakkhiatnate = (t:n) (w:givings/things given out) (d:piakkhiat give out, with the noun suffix na and plural te; paired with ngahna, receiving) (e:ka ngahna le ka ~) (b:piakkhiat) (r:50.4.15) (q:draft)
piakkhit = (t:v) (w:have given/have offered) (d:piak give, with khit finish; with ciangin, after having given or offered) (e:khatvei a ~ ciangin) (r:58.10.12) (q:draft)
piakkholh = (t:v) (w:command beforehand/tell in advance) (d:piak give with kholh beforehand; the form of piakhol used before bangin: thu a piakkholh bangin, just as he said beforehand) (e:Thu a ~ mah bangin/hong piang ding thu a ~ bangin | as you had decided beforehand would happen) (s:piakhol) (r:41.16.7/44.4.27) (q:draft)
piakkholhna = (t:n) (w:word given beforehand/promise) (d:piakkholh, give beforehand, with the noun suffix na; thu piakkholhna is a word spoken or given in advance, such as a promise or an oath) (e:ci-in thu ~ bangin/kiciamna thu ~ thu in | the word of the oath/a thu ~ aw in leitung a liingsak hi | his voice shook the earth) (b:piakkholh) (r:45.4.18/58.7.28/58.12.26) (q:draft, low confidence)
piakkhong = (t:n) (w:gift/free gift) (d:something given freely, a free gift, mostly of what God gives; also placed before letsong or na: a freely given gift or thing) (e:Pasian’ ~ na pen sum tawh lei/Pasian’ hong ~ pen nuntak tawntungna ahi hi | the gift of God is eternal life/Pasian’ hong ~ ahi hi | it is the gift of God/Pasian’ ~ Kha Siangtho na ngah ding uh hi | you will receive God’s gift of the Holy Spirit) (s:letsong) (r:44.8.20/47.9.15/45.6.23/49.2.8/44.2.38) (q:draft)
piakkhongin = (t:adv) (w:as a gift/as a free gift) (d:piakkhong free gift, with the suffix in) (e:~ kingaihsutsak lo hi) (s:letsongin) (b:piakkhong) (r:45.4.4) (q:draft)
piakkhongna = (t:n) (w:giving/gift/bestowal) (d:piakkhong, give freely, with the noun suffix na: the giving of something as a free gift, as of grace or of the Holy Spirit) (e:hehpihna hong ~ tawh kizui-in/Kha Siangtho a ~ thu a muh uh ciangin | when they saw that the Holy Spirit had been given/kei tungah hehpihna hong ~ hangin | because of the grace given to me) (b:piakkhong) (r:45.12.6/44.10.45/45.12.3) (q:draft)
piakkhop = (t:v) (w:give together with/offer along with) (d:give one thing along with another; another form of piakkhawm) (e:tuunote tawh ~ ding pen/Tuate tawh ~ dingin | to be given along with these) (s:piakkhawm/piakhawm) (r:26.46.7/26.46.5) (q:draft)
piakkik = (t:v) (w:give back/restore/give again) (d:piak, give, with kik, again or back: give something back to its owner, give again or restore; thu piakkik is give a further order) (e:Keimah in thu kong ~ mateng/a nu kiangah a sum a ~ ciangin | when he gave the money back to his mother/ama mite tungah nopsakna a ~ ciangin | when he restores well-being to his people/nang in tua numei na ~ kei le | if you do not give the woman back) (s:piakik) (b:piak) (r:15.4.21/19.14.7/7.17.4/1.20.7) (q:draft)
piakma = (t:v) (w:before giving) (d:piak give, with ma before: before he gives) (e:ama gamhluah dingteng a ~) (r:48.4.2) (q:draft)
piakna = (t:n) (w:offering) (d:piak, give, with the noun suffix na: something given to God, an offering) (e:lei pan-a piang gah ~ Topa tungah/Abel leh ama ~ thusim a | he looked with favor on Abel and his offering/biakna leh ~ bangmah nong nei kei uh hi | you brought me no sacrifices or offerings) (s:biakpiakna/letsong) (b:piak) (r:1.4.3/1.4.4/30.5.25)
piakna = (t:n) (w:contribution/donation) (d:a gift of money or goods given freely for a purpose; ut thu-a piakna is a freewill offering) (e:beh lutangte in ut thu-a ~ bawl uh a/ut thu-a ~ a piakte uh banah | besides their freewill offerings/hih na ~ lim takin ka koih khit ciangin | after I have safely delivered this contribution) (b:piak) (r:13.29.6/15.1.4/45.15.28)
piaknasa = (t:v) (w:have given/have offered) (d:piak give, with na and sa, already done: what has been given, or the place where one has given) (e:thupha hong ~ tawh kizui-in/tam veipi tak a ~ mun ahi hi | it was the place where he had offered a great many times) (b:piak) (r:5.16.17/11.3.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
piaknate = (t:n) (w:offerings/sacrifices/gifts) (d:plural of piakna: the offerings, sacrifices or gifts that are given to God) (e:A maan biakna ~ lui un la/Lungdamkoh ~ pia-in | offering thank offerings/biaknate leh ~ mite ading a pia dingin | to offer gifts and sacrifices for the people/cikmah hunin mawhna a maisak zo lo ~ | sacrifices that can never take away sins) (s:biakpiaknate/biaknate) (b:piakna) (r:19.4.5/19.107.22/58.5.1/58.10.11) (q:draft)
piaknop = (t:v) (w:want to give/be willing to give) (d:piak, give, with nop, want; ama piaknop zahzah is as much as he wants to give) (e:ka ~ peuhpeuh tungah ka pia thei/ama ~ zahzah hi ding hi | it shall be as much as he wants to give/lungdamtakin ka neih khempeuh kong ~ banah | besides gladly giving you all I have/a mite’ ~ zahzah hi ding hi | it shall be as much as the people want to give) (s:pianuam) (r:42.4.6/26.46.5/47.12.15/26.46.11) (q:draft)
piaknopna = (t:n) (w:willingness to give/willingness/generosity) (d:piaknop want to give, with the noun suffix na) (e:A lungsim-ah ~ a nei mi/~ lungsim tawh a pia mite | those who give with a willing heart/~ lungsim a nei khempeuh in | all whose hearts were willing) (s:utna/citna) (b:piaknop) (r:2.35.21/47.8.12/47.9.7/14.29.31) (q:draft)
piakpa = (t:n) (w:the one given to) (d:the man to whom something is given; piak, give, with pa marking a male person. Topa thupha piakpa is the one blessed by the Lord) (e:amah thupha ka ~ kua ahi hiam/ka diah khit ciangin ka ~ ahi hi | it is the one I give it to after dipping it/Topa’ thupha ~ aw | you who are blessed by the Lord) (b:piak) (r:1.27.33/43.13.26/1.24.31) (q:draft)
piakpah = (t:v) (w:give at once/give immediately) (d:piak give, with pah at once) (e:lutang nong ~ ding ka deih hi) (r:41.6.25) (q:draft)
piaksa = (t:adj) (w:given) (d:already given, piak with the completive suffix sa; thu piaksa is what was commanded) (e:tungah a ~ khuapite Solomon in/note kong ~ khuapite ah om ding uh a | they shall stay in the towns I have given you/Pasian in Noah a thu ~ bangin | as God had commanded Noah/lim khat a ~ tawh kizui-in | according to the sign he had given) (s:kipiaksa) (b:piak) (r:14.8.2/1.7.9/5.3.19/11.13.5) (q:draft)
piaksak = (t:v) (w:offer for/give on behalf of) (d:piak, give, with sak: give or offer something for another person, as a priest offers a sacrifice for someone) (e:amau’ adingin biakna ~ uh hi/Mi khatpeuh’ meihal biakna a ~ siampipa in | the priest who offers a burnt offering for anyone/biakna le letsong a ~ dingin | to offer sacrifices and gifts for them) (b:piak) (r:12.17.32/3.7.8/58.5.1) (q:draft)
piaksak = (t:v) (w:make give/have given) (d:piak, give, with causative sak: cause something to be given or handed over) (e:kikhamna sum a ~ khit uh ciangin/a zi lak sakin a lawmte tungah ~ hi | he had his wife taken and given to his companions/a zite uh midangte ka ~ ding a | I will give their wives to other men) (b:piak) (r:44.17.9/7.15.6/24.8.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
piaksate = (t:n) (w:things given/those given) (d:what has been given, also of orders given and loans made) (e:Ta’ khut sungah na ~ khempeuh/na hong ~ khat zong ka kisamsak kei hi | I have not lost one of those you gave me/a ~ maisak ding hi | he shall cancel the loans he has made/Topa in Moses a thu ~ khempeuh | all that the Lord commanded Moses) (b:piaksa) (r:43.17.2/6.11.15/43.18.9/5.15.2) (q:draft)
piaktawm = (t:v) (w:give of own accord/give voluntarily) (d:piak give, with tawm showing that the subject acts on his own) (e:utna tawh na ~ uh ahi kei hi) (r:7.21.22) (q:draft)
piakte = (t:n) (w:offerings/gifts/things given) (d:the things that someone gives or has given) (e:kei na hong ~ khempeuh in/Na khut sung uhah kong ~ khat peuhpeuh | any one of those I place in your hands/Kumpipa in ama neihsa sung panin a ~ | what the king gave from his own possessions/ama ~ in biakinn shekel tawh kizui-in | his offering, by the sanctuary shekel) (s:piaknate) (b:piak) (r:43.17.7/4.7.13/12.10.24/14.31.3) (q:draft)
piaktheih = (t:v) (w:can give/be able to give) (d:piak give with theih can; with nading, so that one may give or hand over) (e:Jesuh a ~ nading lampi zon ding/Pa in nuntakna a ~ mah bangin | just as the Father is able to give life/amaute tungah Jesuh a ~ nadingin | so that he might hand Jesus over to them/upate in gim a ~ nadingun | so that the elders might punish them) (s:piathei/piakzawh) (b:piak) (r:42.22.6/43.5.26/41.14.10/44.22.5) (q:draft)
piaktheihna = (t:n) (w:ability to give/means of handing over) (d:being able to give or hand over; piaktheih can give, with the noun suffix na; with dingzia, the way in which one might hand over) (e:Jesuh a ~ dingzia a kikum uh hi) (b:piaktheih) (r:42.22.4) (q:draft)
piaktuak = (t:adj) (w:fit to be given to) (d:piak give with tuak fitting; piaktuak sa is consider it right to give to) (e:~ ka sakte) (r:24.27.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
piakzah = (t:n) (w:amount given/as much as given) (d:piak, give, with zah, amount: the amount that was given; a piakzah mah, the same amount as was given) (e:Nang ka hong ~ mah/a ~ mah uh a ngahkik dingin | to get back the same amount they gave/note tungah upna hong ~ tawh kizui-in | in accordance with the measure of faith given to you) (s:kipiazah) (r:40.20.14/42.6.34/45.12.3) (q:draft)
piakzaw = (t:v) (w:give more) (d:piak give with zaw more: give more than before or more than to others) (e:a nunung lamah thupha lim ~ hi/note thupha hong kilim ~ ding hi | you will be blessed more) (s:piazaw/piathuah) (b:piak) (r:18.42.12/5.7.14) (q:draft)
piakzawh = (t:v) (w:be able to give/afford) (d:form of pia zo, can give, used before bangbang, ding and kei leh) (e:a ~ bangbang pia ding hi/tuazah a ~ kei leh | if he cannot afford that much/nangma sehzah a ~ kei leh | if he cannot pay the amount you set/Ama ~ zahzah a piak banah | besides whatever else he can afford) (s:piaktheih/piathei) (r:3.14.22/3.27.8/3.14.21/4.6.21) (q:draft)
piakzia = (t:n) (w:way of giving/manner of giving) (d:piak give, with zia manner; gim piakzia is the way punishment is dealt out) (e:gim a ~ hih bang ahi hi) (r:18.27.13) (q:draft)
pial = (t:v) (w:turn aside/stray/deviate) (d:leave the path or the right way, often as lam pial; with panin, turn away from a way, a teaching or a command) (e:lam ka ~ ngei kei hi/na thuhilhte panin kei ka ~ kei hi | I have not strayed from your precepts/ka ~ kei ding hi | I will not turn aside/amah lam ~ lo hi | he did not turn aside from the way) (s:lampial/pialkhia) (a:zui) (r:18.23.11/14.34.2/19.119.110/5.2.27) (q:draft)
pialin = (t:v) (w:turning aside/straying/departing) (d:pial, turn aside, with the linking ending in, joining it to the next verb) (e:thu-upna lam pan ~ mi kimkhatte’ upna/lampi panin lam ~ gam lakah pai hi | it turned off the road and went into the field/keimah zuihna panin ~ | turning away from following me/amah lam ~ a vakvai ahi hi | she strays from the way and wanders) (s:lampialin) (b:pial) (r:55.2.18/4.22.23/11.9.6/20.5.6) (q:draft)
pialkha = (t:v) (w:stray/turn aside/go astray) (d:pial, turn aside, with kha, happen to: leave the right way, often with kei in a warning) (e:lam man panin ~ kei un/thuman lampi panin themcik zong ~ kei in | do not stray even a little from the path of truth/note khatpeuh thuman lampi panin ~-in | if any one of you wanders from the way of truth) (s:pial/lampial) (r:58.13.9/20.4.27/59.5.19) (q:draft)
pialkhia = (t:v) (w:turn away/stray/depart from) (d:pial, turn aside, with khia, out or away: turn aside and leave a path, a command or a way of acting) (e:tua lampi panin ~ lo hi/na thupiaknate panin a ~ | those who stray from your commands/a mawkna kampauna lamah a ~ uh hi | they have turned aside to meaningless talk/siat gamtatna panin mihaite ~ nuam lo hi | fools do not want to turn from evil) (s:pial/lampial) (a:zui) (b:pial) (r:14.20.32/19.119.21/54.1.6/20.13.19) (q:draft)
pialkhiat = (t:v) (w:turn away/desert/depart from) (d:form of pialkhia used before zawh and endings) (e:kei kiangpan a ~ zawh uh) (b:pialkhia) (r:55.1.15) (q:draft)
pialkhiate = (t:n) (w:those who stray/strays) (d:pialkhia turn away with the plural te: those who turn away from a path or a rule) (e:A kilawm gamtatna panin a ~/Nangma ngeina kipte panin a ~ khempeuh | all who stray from your decrees) (s:pialte/lampialte) (b:pialkhia) (r:20.21.16/19.119.118) (q:draft)
pialkhiatpih = (t:v) (w:lead astray/turn away with) (d:pialkhiat turn away, with pih together with: draw someone away) (e:amaute a ~ ding gamdang mi) (b:pialkhiat) (r:18.15.18) (q:draft, low confidence)
pialkhin = (t:v) (w:have turned away/have departed) (d:pial turn aside, with khin already done) (e:lampi panin amaute ~ uh a) (b:pial) (r:55.2.18) (q:draft)
pialna = (t:n) (w:straying/turning aside/error) (d:pial, turn aside, with the noun suffix na; lam pialna, leaving the right way) (e:Lam a ~ hang uh/mawhnei mi’ lam ~ pan kihei kiksak a | turning a sinner back from the error of his way) (s:lampialna) (b:pial) (r:24.3.21/59.5.20) (q:draft)
pialpih = (t:v) (w:lead astray/mislead) (d:pial turn aside, with pih, take along: make someone leave the right way, as lam pialpih) (e:Israel ka mite lam a ~ uh hi/lungsim haina in amah lam ~ khin a | a deluded heart has led him astray) (s:pialsak/lampialsak) (b:pial) (r:24.23.13/23.44.20) (q:draft)
pialpual = (t:adv) (d:expressive word placed after satsak, make hot: heated through, inflamed; said of people heated by wine) (e:amaute a satsak ~ matengin) (r:23.5.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
pialsak = (t:v) (w:lead astray/cause to stray/mislead) (d:pial turn aside with sak cause; lam pialsak, lead off the right way) (e:na thupiaknate panin kei hong ~ kei in/migilote, a gamtatna un lam ~ hi | the way of the wicked leads them astray/theihnate in lam hong ~ a | your knowledge has misled you/pasian man lote mah in amaute lam ~ hi | false gods have led them astray) (s:pialpih/lampialsak/khialsak) (b:pial) (r:19.119.10/20.12.26/23.47.10/30.2.4) (q:draft)
