pian'napa = (t:n) (w:ancestor/forefather/father) (d:pian be born, come into being, with the noun suffix na, origin, and pa for a man: the man from whom a people descends) (e:leh Hamath mite’ ~ ahi hi/leh Jobab mite’ ~ ahi hi | he was the father of the people of Jobab) (s:pupi/pusawn) (r:13.1.16/13.1.23) (q:draft)
pian'saksate = (t:n) (w:creatures/created things) (d:piansaksa what has been created, with plural te; written with an apostrophe in this text) (e:Ama ~’ nuntakna a ukpa in Pasian ahi hi | it is God who rules the life of his creatures) (s:piansaksate/piansakte) (r:18.12.10) (q:draft)
