piancilna = (t:n) (w:origin/beginning/creation) (d:piancil with the noun suffix na: the first coming into being of something; piancilna mun, the place a people came from) (e:amaute’ ~ mun/Pasian’ ~ kipatna bulpi ahi pa | he who is the source of God’s creation) (s:piancil/piankhiatna) (b:piancil) (r:26.29.14/66.3.14) (q:draft)
piang = (t:v) (w:become/come into being/happen) (d:come into being: be born, be produced, come about or happen; with a noun before it, become that thing) (e:innkiu suang a ~ hi/Tua mah bangin ~ pah hi | and it was so/hih thu khempeuh hong ~ ding hi | all these things will happen/Topa deihna bang bekin na khempeuh a ~ hi | all things come about only as the Lord wills) (s:suak) (r:41.12.10/1.1.7/42.21.32/25.3.37) begin to be
piangin = (t:v) (w:coming into being/arising/springing up) (d:piang be born or come about, with the linking ending in) (e:zan khat thu-in hong ~/Nangma deihna hangin ~ a om uh | by your will they came to be and exist/Pasian hangin eite ~, hingin i gamtang hi | through God we have our being, live and move/a kipawlnate hangin thahatna ~ | gaining strength through its joints) (b:piang) (r:32.4.10/66.4.11/44.17.28/51.2.19) (q:draft)
piangkha = (t:v) (w:may be produced/may come about) (d:piang come into being, with kha perhaps or happen to) (e:an ~ ding a) (r:20.13.23) (q:draft)
piangkhia = (t:v) (w:come forth/arise/be born/break out) (d:piang, come into being, with khia, out: spring out of, originate from) (e:Amaute sungah mei hong ~ a/nang’ sung panin kumpite hong ~ ding hi | kings will come from you/Heshbon panin mei ~ a | fire went out from Heshbon/Kua’ sung panin tuikhal hong ~ a | from whose womb does the ice come) (s:suakkhia) (b:piang) (r:19.106.18/23.48.1/1.17.6/4.21.28/18.38.29) (q:draft)
piangkhiasak = (t:phrase) (w:bring forth/produce) (d:piangkhia, come forth, with the causative sak: cause to come out, said of the earth that brings forth plants) (e:kung tuamtuamte ~ a) (b:piangkhia) (r:1.1.12) (q:?)
