pianzia = (t:n) (w:glory/divine nature) (d:in the phrase Pasian’ pianzia, the nature of God that is seen as his glory; in John it stands where English has glory and glorify) (e:nang tawh i neihkhawm na ~ mah/Mihing Tapa in Pasian’ ~ a ngah ding hun | the time for the Son of Man to be glorified/Isaiah in Jesuh’ neih Pasian’ ~ mu ahih manin | because Isaiah saw the glory of Jesus/hih bangin Pasian’ ~ a neihna kilangsak a | in this way he revealed his glory) (s:minthanna) (r:43.17.5/43.12.23/43.12.41/43.2.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
pianziate = (t:n) (w:appearances/natures/characteristics) (d:plural of pianzia: the outward looks of people, or the qualities of a nature, as in Pasian’ pianziate, the divine nature) (e:a pualama kilang ~ siksanin/Pasian’ ~ na nei uh hi | you share in the divine nature) (b:pianzia) (r:59.2.1/61.1.4) (q:draft)
piapa = (t:n) (w:giver/one who gives) (d:pia, give, with pa, the man who gives; an piapa, the man who serves food and drink to the king, is the cupbearer) (e:Kumpite tungah gualzawhna a ~/a ~’ adingin lampi hon’sak a | it opens the way for its giver/Izipt kumpipa’ an ~ leh a an huanpa | the cupbearer and the baker of the king of Egypt/pilna a ~ in Topa hi a | the one who gives wisdom is the Lord) (a:ngahpa) (b:pia) (r:19.144.10/1.40.1/20.18.16/20.2.6) (q:draft)
piapi = (t:n) (w:chief cupbearer/chief server) (d:in an piapi pa, the chief of those who serve food and drink to the king: pia, give, with pi, chief) (e:an ~ pa in Josef phawk nawn lo a/~ pa in Josef kiangah a mang gen a | the chief cupbearer told Joseph his dream/An ~ pa le anhuan pipa ahi | the chief cupbearer and the chief baker/an ~ pa an piak nasepah koihkik a | he restored the chief cupbearer to his post) (s:piapipa) (b:pia) (r:1.40.23/1.40.2/1.40.9/1.40.21) (q:draft)
piapipa = (t:n) (w:chief cupbearer/chief butler) (d:in an piapipa, the chief man who serves food and drink to the king; pa marks a man) (e:an ~ in Josef phawk nawn loin/An ~ leh an huanpipa ahi | the chief cupbearer and the chief baker/an ~ in Josef' kiangah a mang genin | the chief cupbearer told Joseph his dream/Amah in an ~ anpiak nasep-ah koih kik a | he restored the chief cupbearer to his post) (s:piapi) (b:piapi) (r:1.40.23/1.41.9/1.40.2/1.40.9/1.40.21) (q:draft)
piasak = (t:v) (w:have someone give/let give/have given) (d:pia, give, with the causative sak: make or allow someone to give, or have a thing given to someone) (e:nasemte tungah a sum ~ in/nangma nung hong zui tangvalte hong ~ in | let it be given to the young men who follow you/Topa' tungah biakna hong ~ un | let us offer sacrifice to the Lord/kei' tungah amah hong ~ un | have him give it to me/ni simin anlum khat ta a ~ den hi | he had a loaf of bread given to him each day) (b:pia) (r:12.22.5/9.25.27/2.5.17/1.23.9/24.37.21) (q:draft)
piasawn = (t:v) (w:pass on/hand on/hand down) (d:pia, give, with sawn, onward: hand something on to those who come after, as land to one’s children) (e:tua gam na ~ thei ding uh hi) (r:15.9.10) (q:draft)
piasim = (t:v) (w:give secretly) (d:pia, give, with sim, secretly; kiciamna piasim is swear an oath to someone in secret) (e:kiciamna a hong ~ hi) (r:24.38.16) (q:draft)
piasuk = (t:v) (w:give down/send down) (d:pia, give, with suk, downward: send something down from above, as fire from heaven) (e:vantung panin meikuang a ~ hi) (b:pia) (r:13.21.26) (q:draft)
piata = (t:v) (w:have given/give over) (d:pia, give, with ta, marking that the act is now done; khut sungah piata is hand over into someone’s power) (e:khut sungah ka ~ hi) (b:pia) (r:24.12.7) (q:draft)
piate = (t:n) (w:givers/those who give) (d:pia, give, with the plural te: the ones who give; leitawi piate are lenders, an piate those who serve food and drink, biakna piate those who offer sacrifices) (e:Mizawngte tungah a ~ in/Nang thupha hong ~ thupha ka pia ding a | I will bless those who bless you/leitawi a late in a ~’ sila suak hi | the borrower is slave to the lender/biakna ~ leh a pia lote | those who offer sacrifices and those who do not) (a:late) (b:pia) (r:20.19.17/20.22.7/1.12.3/21.9.2) (q:draft)
piathei = (t:v) (w:be able to give/can give) (d:pia, give, with thei, be able: be able to give; nuntakna a piathei is life-giving) (e:lametna a hong ~ Pasian in/nek dingin ama sa hong ~ ding ahi hiam | can he give us his flesh to eat/Nuntakna a ~ pen Pasian’ Kha hi a | it is the Spirit of God that gives life/Itna le kilemna a ~ Pasian in | the God who gives love and peace) (b:pia) (r:45.15.13/43.6.52/43.6.63/47.13.11) (q:draft)
piathuah = (t:v) (w:give in addition/give more/give also) (d:pia, give, with thuah, add: give more on top of what someone already has) (e:tul sawm a nei pa tungah ~ un/A neisa mipa tungah Pasian in ~ ding a | to the one who has, God will give more/kisapna dangte uh zong Pasian in hong ~ ding hi | God will give you the other things you need as well/kuamah in biakinn adingin ~ nawn kei un | let no one give anything more for the sanctuary) (r:40.25.28/20.3.16/41.4.25/42.12.31/2.36.6) (q:draft)
piau = (t:n) (w:bank/riverbank) (d:the side of a river; a piau khempeuh, all its banks, is said of a river in flood) (e:Jordan a ~ khempeuh a dimlet laitak/a ~ khempeuh dimlet hi | it overflows all its banks/Jordan tuite hong luang kikin a ~ khempeuh tuum hi | the waters of the Jordan flowed back and covered all its banks) (s:gunpang/gungei) (r:13.12.15/23.8.7/6.4.18) (q:draft)
piazaw = (t:v) (w:give instead/give all the more/give more) (d:pia, give, with zaw, more or rather: give to one instead of another, or give more; with kan ding, how much more will he give) (e:midang khatpeuh ~ in/na sanggamte’ tung sangin nang’ tungah kong ~ hi | I give you more than your brothers/na dang khempeuh zong hong ~ kan ding | will he not all the more give us everything else/a ngente tungah Kha Siangtho ~ kan ding | how much more will he give the Holy Spirit to those who ask) (b:pia) (r:27.5.17/1.48.22/45.8.32/42.11.13) (q:draft)
piazo = (t:v) (w:have given/have granted) (d:pia, give, with zo, marking the action as completed: the thing has now been given) (e:Topa in khuapi note hong ~ hi/amau’ khut sungah tua leitang ka ~ hi | I have given the land into their hands/Topa in a mite tungah lungnopna ~ a | the Lord has granted rest to his people/tuate keima tungah hong ~ hi | he has given them to me) (s:piakhin) (b:pia) (r:6.6.16/1.31.9/7.1.2/13.23.25) (q:draft)
Pibeseth = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Bubastis) (d:city in the delta of Egypt, also called Bubastis, named in the prophecy of Ezekiel against Egypt) (r:26.30.17)
piciang = (t:n) (w:measuring rod/measure) (d:a rod used for measuring length; tehna piciang is a measuring rod, and piciang nam nih, two kinds of measures, means dishonest measuring) (e:tehna ~ la-in nisuahna lam pang teh/pikhau khat leh ~ khat tawi a | holding a linen cord and a measuring rod/Tawisuang nam nih leh ~ nam nih | two kinds of weights and two kinds of measures/tehna ~ la-in a kulh teh hi | he measured the wall with the measuring rod) (r:26.42.16/20.20.10/26.40.3/26.40.5) (q:draft)
picing = (t:adj) (w:mature/full-grown/grown up) (d:fully grown in body or in mind; picing sak is make mature) (e:a ~ mite’ ading ahi hi/na lungsim uh ~ sak un | make your minds mature) (s:cingtaak) (r:58.5.14/20.8.5) (q:draft)
pih = (t:part) (d:verb suffix meaning to do the action together with or for someone, written separately after a verb stem ending in an apostrophe, as in ten’pih, live with or marry, pan’pih, take the side of, and tun’pih, bring to) (e:meigong numei pan’~ un/Amaute in pa nei lote pan’~ lo uh a | they do not defend the fatherless/gamdang numei a ten’~ mite | the men who had married foreign women/Kish’ tapate in amaute ten’~ uh hi | the sons of Kish married them) (r:23.1.17/20.16.29/23.1.23/15.10.17/13.23.22) (q:draft)
Piha = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Pilha) (d:one of the leaders of the people who sealed the covenant in the time of Nehemiah) (r:16.10.24) (q:draft)
Pihahiroth = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Pi Hahiroth) (d:place in Egypt between Migdol and the sea, facing Baal Zephon, where Israel camped before crossing the sea) (r:4.33.7/2.14.2)
pihin = (t:part) (d:verb suffix pih, do together with or bring along, with the linking ending in; written after an apostrophe, as in ten’pihin, marrying, and tun’pihin, bringing) (e:tua nu ten’~ luppih a/amah in hih mun hong tun’~ | he brought us to this place/Kaleb in Efrath ten’~ | Caleb married Ephrath/Pasian’ Kha in hong leen’~ | the Spirit of God lifted me up) (b:pih) (r:1.38.2/5.26.9/13.2.19/26.11.24) (q:draft)
pihkik = (t:part) (d:pih, do together with someone, followed by kik back; tun pihkik is bring someone back to a place, normally written tunpih kik) (e:lampi-ah a tun ~ theih leh) (b:pih) (r:59.5.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
pihna = (t:see) <ten'pihna>
pihpa = (t:part) (d:the verb ending pih, together with or for someone, followed by pa for a man: the man who does the action with or for another; kipawl pihpa, ally, paikhiat pihpa, he who brings out) (e:Ka teel kipawl ~ in Babilon tungah/ka galte panin kei hong paikhiat ~ lian ta hen | exalted be he who brings me out from my enemies) (b:pih) (r:23.48.14/10.22.49) (q:draft)
pihsak = (t:part) (d:the verb ending pih, together with or taking along, followed by sak, cause or let: paikhiat pihsak, let someone be brought out; kiten’ pihsak, have someone married) (e:amaute hong paikhiat ~ un la/kiten’ ~ nop a neih leh | if he wishes to have her married) (b:pih) (r:1.19.8/46.7.36) (q:draft, low confidence)
pihte = (t:n) (w:companions/fellows) (d:pih with the plural te: those who do something together with someone; it follows a verb or noun, as kipawl pihte, allies or friends, innkuan pihte, fellow citizens, and teen’pihte, those who marry someone) (e:Ka kipawl ~ ka sapsap hangin/A kipawl ~ khempeuh in kheemin | all her friends have betrayed her/a paikhawm lo na innkuan ~ khempeuh uh | all your fellow citizens who did not go with you/A maksa numei a teen’~ in | those who marry a divorced woman) (b:pih) (r:25.1.19/24.29.16/25.1.2/40.19.9) (q:draft)
piikpeek = (t:adv) (w:completely/fully/utterly) (d:placed after a verb or describing word to show that something is complete or full to the limit, as kicing piikpeek, fully supplied; also written pikpek) (e:galhiam kicing ~ tawh a kuankhia ding/na lungkim ~ dongun | until you are fully satisfied/tu-in kisia khin ~ ta hi | now they are utterly ruined/Note’ hong piak nate kicing ~ hi | the gifts you gave me are more than enough) (s:pikpek/bikbek) (r:27.11.13/25.2.8/22.5.1/50.4.18) (q:draft, low confidence)
pik = (t:v) (w:gore) (d:of a bull, strike or pierce with the horn; ki tawh pik is gore with its horns) (e:a ki tawh a ~ leh/khat peuhpeuh a ki tawh a ~ leh | if it gores anyone with its horns) (s:nawt) (r:2.21.31/2.21.32) (q:draft)
pikhau = (t:n) (w:measuring line/measuring cord) (d:pi, the measure of length, with khau, cord: a cord for measuring, named beside piciang, the measuring rod; the English has linen cord) (e:~ khat leh piciang khat tawi a) (s:khauzang) (r:26.40.3) (q:draft)
pikhia = (t:v) (w:lead out/bring out) (d:pi, lead, with khia, out: lead people out of a place, as out of captivity) (e:panin ka ~ kik ding a) (s:paikhiatpih) (r:26.39.25) (q:draft)
pikik = (t:v) (w:lead back/bring back) (d:pi, lead, with kik, back: lead people back to where they came from) (e:keimah in hehnemin ka ~ ding hi) (s:tunpihkik/ciahpihkik) (r:24.31.9) (q:draft)
piklup = (t:v) (w:gore to death) (d:of a bull, strike with the horns so that the victim falls dead) (e:a ki tawh a ~ ciangin) (r:2.21.28) (q:draft)
pikpek = (t:adv) (w:completely/fully/utterly) (d:placed after a verb or describing word: to the full, altogether; also written piikpeek) (e:galhiam kicing ~ tawh a kuankhia ding hi/tu-in a kisia khin ~ ta hi | now they are utterly ruined) (s:piikpeek/bikbek) (r:27.11.13/25.2.8) (q:draft)
piksante = (t:n) (w:those who purse the lips at) (d:with neh, lips: those who press their lips together at someone; apparently pik with san, directed at, and the plural te, parallel to sitsante, those who wink at) (e:a neh hong ~ in thusia geel ahi hi) (r:20.16.30) (q:draft, low confidence)
pil = (t:adj) (w:wise/learned/sensible) (d:having wisdom or good sense; also used as a verb, be or become wise, and pil zaw is wiser) (e:Tua nungak lakah nga a ~ uh hi/A ~ kumpipa in migilote tengkhia a | a wise king winnows out the wicked/mihaite ~ ngei ding ahi hiam | can the witless ever become wise/Daniel sangin ~ na kisa zaw a | you think yourself wiser than Daniel) (s:lungpil) (a:hai) (r:40.25.2/26.28.3/20.20.26/18.11.12) (q:draft)
Pilat = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Pilate) (d:Pontius Pilate, the Roman governor of Judea who tried Jesus and handed him over to be crucified) (r:43.19.8/42.23.13)
Pildash = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Pildash) (d:son of Nahor, the brother of Abraham, and Milkah) (r:1.22.22)
pileser = (t:see) <Tiglath-pileser>
pilhuai = (t:adj) (w:wise/prudent) (d:pil, wise, with huai, worthy of: wise or sensible to do; pilhuai zaw is the wiser course) (e:ngaihsut masak ding ~ zaw hi) (a:haihuai) (r:21.10.10) (q:draft)
pilin = (t:adj) (w:wise/sensible) (d:pil with the linking suffix in: being wise, or as wise; a pilin kingaihsun is think oneself wise, and lungsim pilin is in his right mind) (e:amah ~ a vanglian hi/Nangmah mah a ~ kingaihsun tawm kei in | do not think of yourself as wise/a lungsim ~, puan silhin a om | in his right mind and dressed/No a ~ a kinei mite aw | you who count yourselves wise) (b:pil) (r:27.2.20/41.5.15/20.3.7/18.34.2) (q:draft)
pilkikna = (t:n) (w:return to one’s right mind/recovery of one’s senses) (d:pil, wise or sensible, with kik, again, and the noun suffix na: the state of being in one’s right mind again) (e:a ~ thu a muh uh ciangin) (r:42.8.35) (q:draft)
pillawh = (t:v) (w:gain wisdom/become wise) (d:pil, wise, with lawh, get as a result: become wise through what happens to another) (e:mi mawkmawkte in ~ uh a) (r:20.21.11) (q:draft)
pillohna = (t:n) (w:folly/foolishness) (d:pil, wise, with loh, not, and the noun suffix na: lack of wisdom, folly) (e:ka ~ na thei a) (s:haina) (a:pilna) (r:19.69.5) (q:draft)
pillote = (t:n) (w:fools/the simple/unwise people) (d:pil, wise, with lo, not, and plural te: those who are not wise) (e:mi ~ pilsak hi/Lung ~ aw, cik ciangin pil ding | you fools, when will you become wise) (s:mihaite/pilote) (a:mipilte/pilte) (r:19.19.7/19.94.8) (q:draft)
pilna = (t:n) (w:wisdom/knowledge/understanding) (d:pil, wise, with the noun suffix na: wisdom, and also knowledge and good understanding) (e:Sheba kumpinu in Solomon’ ~/Mipilte in ~ thu gen a | the wise speak words of wisdom/Khanghamte in ~ nei a | the aged have wisdom/Na ~ leh na siamna tawh | by your wisdom and your skill) (s:lungpilna/ciimna) (a:haina) (b:pil) (r:14.9.3/20.3.13/20.15.2/18.12.12/26.28.4) (q:draft)
Pilna = (t:n) (w:wisdom/understanding) (d:pilna written with a capital at the start of a sentence or line, and in Proverbs of Wisdom speaking as a person) (e:~ nei lo mipawlte hangin/~ in a inn lam a | Wisdom has built her house/~ tawh inn kilam a | by wisdom a house is built/~ thu ka thei kei a | I have not learned wisdom) (s:lungpilna/ciimna) (a:haina) (b:pilna) (r:45.10.19/42.11.49/20.9.1/20.24.3/20.30.3) (q:draft)
pilnate = (t:n) (w:wisdom/knowledge) (d:pilna with the plural te: the things one knows, kinds of wisdom) (e:Tua bang ~ vantung panin/kote in ka ~ uh ka ngah uh hi | we received our wisdom) (b:pilna) (r:59.3.15/18.15.10) (q:draft)
pilneser = (t:see) <Tilgath-pilneser>
pilote = (t:n) (w:fools/foolish people) (d:pil wise, lo not and plural te written as one word: those who are not wise) (e:No mi ~ aw) (s:mihaite/pillote) (a:mipilte/pilte) (r:42.11.40) (q:draft)
pilpen = (t:adj) (w:wisest/most wise) (d:pil, wise, with pen, most: the wisest of a group; a pilpen pen is extremely wise) (e:A numeite a ~ nu in dawng hiam/ahi zongin a ~ pente ahi uh hi | yet they are extremely wise) (b:pil) (r:7.5.29/20.30.24) (q:draft)
pilpennu = (t:n) (w:wisest woman) (d:pilpen wisest, with nu marking a woman) (e:A numeite a ~ in amah a dawng hiam) (b:pilpen) (r:7.5.29) (q:draft)
pilsak = (t:adj) (w:wise/make wise) (d:pil, wise, with the causative sak: make someone wise) (e:Khanghamna in mi ~ lo a/mi pillote ~ hi | it makes the simple wise/mi in midang ~ thei hi | one person can sharpen another/mipilsate ~ semsem-in | making the wise wiser still) (b:pil) (r:18.32.9/1.3.6/19.19.7/20.27.17/20.1.5)
pilsate = (t:n) (w:the wise/those already wise) (d:pil, wise, with sa, already, and the plural te: people who are already wise) (e:mi ~ pilsak semsemin) (s:mipilte/mipilsate/ciimsate) (a:mihaite) (r:20.1.5) (q:draft)
Piltai = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Piltai) (d:priest, head of the family of Moadiah in the days of the high priest Joiakim) (r:16.12.17)
pilte = (t:n) (w:the wise/wise ones) (d:pil, wise, with the plural te: the wise ones; after a noun it means wise, as numei pilte, wise women, and mi pilte, wise men) (e:A ~ ahih uh leh/Numei ~ in innsung nuntakna khangsak a | wise women build up the household/Ta ~ in a pa lungdam sak a | a wise son makes his father glad/Babilon sunga kumpi’ thudot mi ~ khempeuh | all the wise men of Babylon who advised the king) (s:mipilte/lungpilte) (a:haite/mihaite) (b:pil) (r:40.25.4/20.14.1/20.15.20/27.2.12) (q:draft)
pilvan = (t:v) (w:wake up/sober up) (d:form of pilvang written with a final apostrophe before ciangin: of a drunk man, wake and be clear-headed again) (e:Noah a zukhamna pan a ~’ ciangin/Ka ~’ ciangin zu ka ne kik ding hi | when I wake up I will drink again) (r:1.9.24/20.23.35) (q:draft)
pilvang = (t:v) (w:be alert/keep watch/be sober/be shrewd) (d:stay awake, watchful and ready; of a drunk man, become sober again) (e:khua phawkin ~ ni/kikemin ~ un | be on guard, be alert/gul bangin ~ unla | be as shrewd as snakes/thei lo na hih manun na ~ un | keep watch, because you do not know) (s:khuaphawk) (r:52.5.6/41.13.33/40.10.16/40.25.13) (q:draft)
pilvangin = (t:adv) (w:watchfully/alertly/soberly) (d:pilvang, be alert, with the ending in: staying watchful while doing the next action) (e:~ thu ngen un/eite ihmu loin, ~ kikem ni | let us not sleep but keep watch soberly/Note ~ khua phawk un | be alert and of sober mind) (b:pilvang) (r:41.14.38/52.5.6/60.5.8) (q:draft)
pilzaw = (t:adj) (w:wiser) (d:pil, wise, with zaw, more: wiser, used with sangin, than) (e:mite’ pilna sangin a ~ hi/midang khempeuh sangin amah ~ a | he was wiser than anyone else/midangte khempeuh sangin ka ~ hi | I am wiser than all the others/a ~-in kei hong bawl hi | it makes me wiser) (b:pil) (r:46.1.25/21.1.16/11.4.31/19.119.98) (q:draft)
pilzawk = (t:adj) (w:wiser) (d:form of pilzaw used before manin, because: being wiser) (e:midangte sangin ka ~ manin) (b:pilzaw) (r:27.2.30) (q:draft)
pingaihsut = (t:v) (w:have regard for/look on with favour/give heed to) (d:think of a person or thing with care or favour; built on ngaihsut, think) (e:Na thuciamna hong ~ in/Keimah in note ka hong ~ ding a | I will look on you with favour) (r:19.74.20/3.26.9) (q:draft)
pingpei = (t:n) (w:whirlwind/windstorm) (d:a wind that spins round, a whirlwind or violent windstorm; pingpei bangin is like a whirlwind) (e:Na vanging lianpi ~ sungah om-in/Topa in ~-in vantungah Elijah a lak ding | the Lord was about to take Elijah up to heaven in a whirlwind/a leengpeite uh ~ bangin manlang hi | their chariot wheels are swift like a whirlwind) (s:huihpi) (r:19.77.18/12.2.1/23.5.28) (q:draft)
pingpeipei = (t:v) (w:whirl round/roll round and round) (d:turn something round and round, as in rolling it into a ball before throwing) (e:hong ~ ding a) (r:23.22.18) (q:draft, low confidence)
Pingpeite = (t:n) (w:whirlwinds) (d:pingpei whirlwind with plural te) (e:~ leitaw lam panin hong kipat) (r:23.21.1) (q:draft)
Pinon = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Pinon) (d:one of the chiefs of Edom descended from Esau) (r:1.36.41/13.1.52)
pipa = (t:n) (w:chief/head/leader) (d:pi, chief, with pa for a man, placed after a title: tuucing pipa, chief shepherd, anhuan pipa, chief baker) (e:Tuucing ~ hong pai ciangin/biakinn uk ~ ahi | the chief officer in charge of the temple/An piapi pa le anhuan ~ ahi | the chief cupbearer and the chief baker/Shafan’ tapa thuvan ~ Gemariah’ inndei sungah | in the room of Gemariah son of Shaphan the secretary) (r:60.5.4/24.20.1/1.40.2/24.36.10) (q:draft)
pipa = (t:n) (w:bridegroom) (d:in zi pipa, the man who takes a wife) (e:a lawmpa in zi ~’ aw a zak manin) (s:zipipa/mopipa/zineipa) (a:mo) (r:43.3.29) (q:draft, low confidence)
pipi = (t:part) (w:very/huge) (d:intensifier placed after a describing word, often of several things: gol pipi, very large, lamdang pipi, very wonderful) (e:na lamdang ~ piang a/laimal gol ~-in lai ka hong gelh | I write to you in very large letters/suang gol ~ a khiat uh hi | they threw large stones at him/a gol ~-in bawlin | making them very large) (r:18.37.5/48.6.11/44.7.58/40.23.5) (q:draft)
pipi = (t:part) (d:placed after a verb or state word, often with in: while in that state, with that feeling; lunghimawh pipi-in, while doubting, ut lo pipi, unwillingly, dah pipi-in, with grief) (e:lunghimawh ~-in a ne a om leh/ut lo ~ hi loin | not unwillingly/dah ~-in na sem ding uh hi | they will do their work with grief/sing kitomsakin a lelh ~ uh a kipuasak hi | made to carry wood, they stagger under the load) (r:45.14.23/60.5.2/58.13.17/25.5.13) (q:draft)
Piram = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Piram) (d:Amorite king of Jarmuth, one of the five kings who attacked Gibeon and were defeated by Joshua) (r:6.10.3)
Pirathon = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Pirathon) (d:town in the hill country of Ephraim, home of the judge Abdon and of Benaiah, one of the mighty men of David) (r:7.12.15/10.23.30)
Pirras = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Pyrrhus) (d:father of Sopater of Berea, a companion of Paul) (r:44.20.4)
Pisgah = (t:name) (c:mountain) (w:Pisgah) (d:mountain ridge in Moab east of the Jordan, from whose top near Mount Nebo Moses saw the promised land) (r:4.21.20/6.13.20)
Pisgal = (t:name) (c:mountain) (w:Pisgah) (d:another spelling of Pisgah, the mountain ridge in Moab east of the Jordan) (r:5.4.47)
Pishon = (t:name) (c:river) (w:Pishon) (d:the first of the four rivers flowing out of Eden, which winds through the land of Havilah) (e:~ gun) (r:1.2.11)
Pisidia = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Pisidia) (d:mountainous region in the south of Asia Minor, north of Pamphylia, through which Paul and Barnabas travelled) (r:44.14.24/44.13.14)
Pispa = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Pispah) (d:son of Jether in the genealogy of the tribe of Asher) (r:13.7.38)
pistakhio = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:pistachio) (d:loan word; pistakhio gah, pistachio nuts) (e:~ gah leh almond gahte puaksuk un) (r:1.43.11) (q:draft)
pite = (t:n) (w:grandmothers/grandparents) (d:pi grandmother with the plural te; a pu a pite, grandfathers and grandmothers, grandparents) (e:a pu a ~ a huh nadingun) (b:pi) (r:54.5.4) (q:draft)
piteek = (t:n) (w:old woman) (d:pi grandmother or woman, with teek old; paired with puteek, old man) (e:~ puteekte zong kipaikhiatpih ding hi) (s:pitek) (a:puteek) (r:24.6.11) (q:draft)
pitek = (t:n) (w:old woman) (d:pi grandmother or woman, with tek old; paired with putek, old man; the 1977 text spells it piteek) (e:~ putekte zong a kipai khiatpih ding hi) (s:piteek) (a:puteek) (r:24.6.11) (q:draft)
Piter = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Peter) (d:the apostle Simon Peter, a fisherman of Galilee and brother of Andrew, one of the twelve disciples of Jesus) (r:44.11.4/43.6.8)
Pithom = (t:name) (c:land/city) (w:Pithom) (d:store city in Egypt built for Pharaoh by the Israelites during their slavery) (r:2.1.11)
Pithon = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Pithon) (d:son of Micah, a descendant of King Saul through Jonathan, of the tribe of Benjamin) (r:13.8.35/13.9.41)
po = (t:v) (w:sprout/grow/come up) (d:of a seed or plant, come up out of the ground and grow) (e:Taang ~ a, hong vuih khit ciangin/Lopate a ~ theih nadingin | so that grass may sprout/a kung ~ a, hong khangto hi | the plant sprouts and grows/laiphai kungte ~ thei ahi hiam | can papyrus grow) (s:sel) (r:40.13.26/41.4.27/18.38.27/18.8.11)
poding = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:broom bush/broom tree/juniper) (d:desert shrub; poding kung is the bush, poding zung its root) (e:~ kung khat nuaiah ihmu hi/~ kung nuai khatah tu hi | he sat down under a broom bush/~ zung nangawn ne uh hi | they ate even the root of the broom bush) (r:11.19.5/18.30.4/11.19.4) (q:draft)
poi = (t:v) (w:matter/be a loss) (d:be a matter of regret or loss; a poi sa is feel it as a loss, here of living with a hand or foot missing) (e:khe bui, a ~ sa-in nuntakna sungah) (r:40.18.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
poin = (t:v) (w:sprout/grow up) (d:po sprout, with the linking suffix in) (e:a kha kung a zung ~) (b:po) (r:58.12.15) (q:draft)
poina = (t:n) (w:defect/blemish/flaw) (d:noun from poi, be hurt or damaged: a bodily defect or injury in a person or an animal, which bars a priest from serving and an animal from being offered) (e:a khangin ~ a nei mi in/tuu ahi zongin ~ nei a | or a sheep that has a defect/amah in ~ nei ahih manin | because he has a defect/~ lian khatpeuh peuh a neih leh | if it has any serious flaw) (s:sitbaanna) (b:poi) (r:3.21.17/5.15.21/5.17.1/3.21.23) (q:draft)
poisak = (t:v) (w:injure/hurt/harm) (d:poi, be hurt or damaged, with the causative sak: cause bodily injury to someone) (e:a vengte khat a ~ leh/amah in mi khat a ~ bangin | as he has injured someone) (s:liamsak) (b:poi) (r:3.24.19/3.24.20) (q:draft)
Pokereth = (t:name) (w:Pokereth) (d:first part of the name Pokereth-Hazzebaim, head of a family of the servants of Solomon who returned from the exile) (r:15.2.57)
Pokereth-hazzebaim = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Pokereth-Hazzebaim) (d:head of a family among the descendants of the servants of Solomon who returned from the exile with Zerubbabel) (e:Hattil suante, ~ suante) (r:15.2.57) (q:draft)
pokhawm = (t:v) (w:grow together/grow up with) (d:po, sprout, with khawm, together: come up and grow together with other plants) (e:amau tawh ~ uh a) (s:khangkhawm) (b:po) (r:42.8.7) (q:draft)
Pokhereth = (t:see) <Pokhereth-hazzebaim>
Pokhereth-hazzebaim = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Pokereth-Hazzebaim) (d:head of a family among the descendants of the servants of Solomon who returned from the exile with Zerubbabel) (r:16.7.59) (q:draft)
Pokherethhazzebaim = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Pokereth-Hazzebaim) (d:a servant of Solomon whose descendants returned from the exile with Zerubbabel) (r:15.2.57/16.7.59)
pokhia = (t:adj) (w:sprung) (d:of plants, having come up out of the ground; po, sprout, with khia, out) (e:lo sung ankungte ~ lo hi) (b:po) (r:1.2.5)
pokhia = (t:v) (w:grow/spring up/sprout/come up) (d:po, sprout, with khia, out: of plants, come up out of the ground or the water; also of trouble or righteousness that springs up) (e:tui sung pan-a ~/lei sung panin kung dangte hong ~ hi | other plants spring up from the soil/Lei tungah an nek ding hong ~ a | food comes up on the earth/lungkhamna hong ~ tawm hi lo hi | trouble does not sprout by itself/thumanna le phatna a ~ sak hi | he makes righteousness and praise spring up) (s:selkhia/khangkhia) (b:po) (r:23.44.4/18.28.5/18.8.19/18.5.6/23.61.11)
pokhiasak = (t:v) (w:bring forth/produce/make grow) (d:pokhia, sprout forth, with the causative sak: make plants come up, said of the ground) (e:nang a dingin hong ~ ding a) (s:posak) (b:pokhia) (r:1.3.18)
pokhiasak = (t:n) (w:growth)
pokhiat = (t:v) (w:spring up/sprout forth) (d:form of pokhia used before theih and endings) (e:Hotkhiatna a ~ theih nadingin) (b:pokhia) (r:23.45.8) (q:draft)
pokhiatawm = (t:v) (w:sprout of itself/spring up by itself) (d:pokhia, sprout forth, with tawm, of its own accord: come up by itself, without a cause) (e:lungkhamna hong ~ lo hi) (s:piangtawm) (r:18.5.6) (q:draft)
pokhiato = (t:v) (w:spring up/sprout up) (d:pokhia, sprout forth, with to, upward: spring up; with sak, make spring up) (e:thumanna zong ~ sak un) (s:poto) (b:pokhia) (r:23.45.8) (q:draft)
pom = (t:v) (w:embrace/hold fast/clasp/cling to) (d:take or hold in the arms; also hold on to a teaching, a god or a person) (e:nangma thuhilhnate ka ~ hi/limtak ~ in, pahtawina hong ngah sak ding hi | embrace her and she will bring you honor/Na ang sungah meikuang ~ lecin | if you hold fire in your lap/pasian dangte ~ uh a | they embraced other gods/nangmah hong ~ dingin a hanciam tawm | who strives to take hold of you) (s:kawi/lenkip) (a:nusia) (r:19.119.31/1.33.4/20.4.8/20.6.27/14.7.22/23.64.7) (q:draft)
pomcipin = (t:v) (w:embrace tightly/hug) (d:pom embrace, with cip tight and the linking suffix in) (e:~ nam a, amaute a kap uh hi) (r:1.33.4) (q:draft)
pomin = (t:v) (w:take in the arms/embrace/hold) (d:pom embrace, with the linking suffix in) (e:Zeisu a ang-ah ~ Pasian) (b:pom) (r:42.2.28) (q:draft)
pomlai = (t:v) (w:still cling to/keep holding) (d:pom hold fast, with lai still) (e:khialhna mah ~ hi) (r:12.3.3) (q:draft)
pona = (t:n) (w:growing place/growth) (d:noun of po, sprout or grow; with mun, the place where a plant grows, as lingkung pona mun, a place overgrown with thorn bushes) (e:lingkung ~ mun tawh kibang ding a/Tua sing a ~ mun tui kawt a | streams flowed around the place where that tree grew/paknamtui kung a ~ mun | the place where spice plants grow/Tua ki ~ munah | in the place where that horn had grown) (b:po) (r:23.17.9/26.31.4/22.8.14/27.8.8) (q:draft)
pongkhaina = (t:n) (w:scales/balance) (d:instrument for weighing; the second part is khai, hang or weigh, with the noun suffix na) (e:~ tawh mual liante khai a) (s:tawikhaina/khaina) (r:23.40.12) (q:draft)
Pontas = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Pontus) (d:Roman province on the south coast of the Black Sea, in the north of Asia Minor) (r:44.2.9)
Pontias = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Pontius) (d:family name of Pilate, the Roman governor of Judea who tried Jesus) (r:44.4.27/42.3.1)
Ponun = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Punon) (d:place where the Israelites camped in the wilderness, between Zalmonah and Oboth) (r:4.33.43)
popah = (t:v) (w:spring up at once/sprout quickly) (d:po, sprout, with pah, at once: come up quickly, said of seed sown in shallow soil) (e:lum ahih manin a khaici ~ hi/lei sah lo ahih manin thakhatin ~ hi | it sprang up quickly because the soil was not deep) (r:40.13.5/41.4.5) (q:draft)
poplar = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:poplar) (d:the English tree name, used with kung, tree) (e:~ kung, almond kung/~ kung, leh terebinth kungte nuai-ah | under poplar and terebinth trees) (s:gialheek/gialhek) (r:1.30.37/28.4.13) (q:draft)
Poratha = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Poratha) (d:one of the ten sons of Haman, killed by the Jews in Susa) (r:17.9.7)
Porsias = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Porcius) (d:family name of Festus, who followed Felix as Roman governor of Judea) (r:44.24.27)
posak = (t:v) (w:be sprout/make grow/cause to sprout) (d:po, sprout, with the causative sak: make grass, trees or hair grow) (e:mualte tungah lopa ~ hi/na gam sung uhah lopa hong ~ ding a | he will make grass grow in your land/lei sung panin Topa Pasian in ~ hi | the Lord God made them grow out of the ground/oliv kungte ka ~ ding hi | I will make olive trees grow/Sakol zaangmul a ~ pa nang na hi hiam | are you the one who makes the horse’s mane grow) (s:khangsak/pokhiasak) (b:po) (r:19.147.8/5.11.15/1.2.9/23.41.19/18.39.19)
posakpa = (t:n) (w:one who makes grow) (d:posak make grow, with pa marking a male doer) (e:Sakol zangmul a ~ in nang na hi hiam) (s:khangsakpa) (b:posak) (r:18.39.19) (q:draft)
pote = (t:n) (w:what grows/growth/crops) (d:po grow with the plural te: the things that grow; a li pote, what grows of itself without sowing) (e:a li ~ zong la loin/tu kumin anli ~ na ne ding uh a | this year you will eat what grows by itself/ama thu-in a ~ na ne ding a | you will eat what grows of itself) (b:po) (r:3.25.11/12.19.29/23.37.30) (q:draft)
Potifar = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Potiphar) (d:Egyptian officer of Pharaoh, captain of the guard, who bought Joseph as a slave) (r:1.37.36/1.39.1)
Potifera = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Potiphera) (d:priest of On in Egypt, father of Asenath the wife of Joseph) (r:1.41.50/1.46.20)
poto = (t:v) (w:grow up/sprout up/spring up) (d:po sprout with to upward) (e:ki li hong ~ kik a) (s:pokhiato/khangto) (b:po) (r:27.8.8) (q:draft)
pound = (t:n) (w:pound) (d:unit of weight, the English word) (e:Nikodemas in ~ zakhat a khai) (r:43.19.39) (q:draft)
pozo = (t:see) <pozo-in>
pozo-in = (t:v) (w:overgrow/grow all over) (d:po sprout or grow with zo and the linking ending in: of thorns growing over a whole land) (e:sung uhah lingkung bek ~) (r:36.2.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
Prisilla = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Priscilla) (d:wife of Aquila and fellow worker of Paul) (r:44.18.2/45.16.3)
Prokhoras = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Procorus) (d:one of the seven men chosen to serve the church in Jerusalem) (r:44.6.5)
psap = (t:todo) (q:draft, stands before the first word of the verse and has no meaning in it, probably a stray formatting marker in the text and not a word)
pu = (t:n) (w:grandfather/ancestor/forefather) (d:grandfather or forefather; pu pa and pu leh pate mean ancestors) (e:Na ~ na pate’ phuhsa gi-suang/ka ~ Saul’ kumpigam kei hong pia kik ding hi | they will give me back my grandfather Saul’s kingdom/I ~ Abraham in mi lamsang ah | our forefather Abraham, according to the flesh/a ~ a pate’ Pasian | the God of his ancestors) (s:pupi/pulepa) (a:tupa) (r:20.22.28/14.29.2/10.16.3/45.4.1/12.21.22) (q:draft)
pua = (t:n) (w:outside) (d:the outer side, mostly as pua lam or pua lamah outside of) (e:giahphual ~ lamah mei tawh hal hi/Giahphual ~-ah mun khat na nei ding uh a | you shall have a place outside the camp/gialphual ~ lam a siangtho mun khatah | to a clean place outside the camp/giahphual ~ lamah na sanggamte uh puakhia un | carry your relatives outside the camp) (s:pualam) (a:sunglam) (r:3.9.11/5.23.12/3.6.11/3.10.4) (q:draft)
pua = (t:v) (w:carry/bear) (d:carry a load, a weapon or a message; mawhna pua is bear guilt) (e:Judah mi lum leh tei a ~/ama van ciat a ~ ding uh hi | each will carry his own load/amah in tua nu’ mawhna ~ ding hi | he shall bear her guilt/a galhiam ~-pa suak hi | he became his armor-bearer/Na sum uh a zah nih ~ un | take double the money with you) (s:tawi) (r:13.12.24/5.31.25/48.6.5/4.30.15/9.16.21/1.43.12) (q:draft)
puah = (t:v) (w:repair/mend/restore) (d:put right something damaged, such as a wall, a door or a house; in Nehemiah, repair a section of the city wall) (e:om siampite in ~ uh hi/Hur tapa Refaiah in ~ hi | Rephaiah son of Hur repaired it/biakinn kongkhakte hongin tuate ~ hi | he opened the doors of the temple and repaired them/siampite in inn ~ nai lo uh hi | the priests had not yet repaired the temple/paknamtui bawlpa Hananiah in ~ hi | Hananiah the perfume-maker repaired it) (s:bawlpha/bawlkik) (a:susia) (r:16.3.22/12.12.14/16.3.9/14.29.3/12.12.6/16.3.8) (q:draft)
Puah = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Puah) (d:name of a Hebrew midwife in Egypt, and of two men of the tribe of Issachar) (r:2.1.15)
puahin = (t:v) (w:mending/repairing/preparing) (d:puah mend with the linking ending in; of fishermen putting their nets in order) (e:gunkuang sungah ngen ~ a om) (b:puah) (r:40.4.21) (q:draft)
puahkik = (t:v) (w:renovate/repair/restore) (d:puah, repair, with kik, again: put a ruined place back in good order) (e:a sia teng ka ~ ding a/a om lai mun teng ~ hi | he restored the rest of the place/a kisiasa David’ ukna gam ka ~ ding hi | I will restore the fallen kingdom of David) (s:bawlkik/lamkik) (r:30.9.11/13.11.8/44.15.16)
puahkik = (t:v) (w:remodel/revamp/rebuild/renew) (d:rebuild or renew ruined towns and walls) (e:khuapi siate ~ ding uh hi | they will renew the ruined cities/a sia khempeuh na ~ ding uh hi | you will rebuild all the ruins/note pen, kulhsia a ~ | you, the repairer of broken walls) (r:23.61.4/26.36.10/23.58.12)
puahkikin = (t:v) (w:repair/rebuild/restore) (d:puahkik repair again, with the linking ending in, joining it to the next verb) (e:kote’ Pasian’ inn ~) (b:puahkik) (r:15.9.9) (q:draft)
puahkikna = (t:n) (w:repair/restoration/renovation) (d:puahkik repair again, with the noun suffix na; puahkikna nasepna, the work of repair) (e:amau khut sungah ~ nasepna in mainawt a) (s:puahna/lamkikna) (b:puahkik) (r:14.24.13) (q:draft)
puahna = (t:n) (w:repair/repairing/restoring) (d:puah repair, with the noun suffix na) (e:kulhpi siate ~ dingin innte na phel hi/inn ~ khat peuhpeuh a, zat dingin | to be used for any repair of the house/biakinn ~ ding le a ngei batsakkik nadingin | for repairing the temple and restoring it) (s:puahkikna/puahphatna) (a:suksiatna) (b:puah) (r:23.22.10/12.12.12/14.34.10) (q:draft)
puahpa = (t:n) (w:smoother/finisher) (d:puah put in good order with pa for a man: here the workman who smooths an idol with a hammer) (e:sek tawh milim a nel ~ in) (b:puah) (r:23.41.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
puahpha = (t:v) (w:restore/repair/put in order) (d:puah repair with pha good: mend something so that it is good again) (e:A kisia ama munte khempeuh ~-in/A kinusia na gam ~ in | restoring your abandoned land) (s:bawlpha/puah) (r:23.51.3/23.49.8) (q:draft)
puahphat = (t:v) (w:repair/put in order/set right) (d:form of puahpha used before ding, nading and hun: mend something so that it is good again) (e:biakinn ~ nading/a manin ~ ding a kisam lai a omte | the things that still needed to be put in order/Pasian in na khempeuh a ~ hun | the time when God sets all things right) (s:bawlphat) (b:puahpha) (r:12.12.5/56.1.5/58.9.10) (q:draft)
puahphatkik = (t:v) (w:rebuild/restore/repair again) (d:puahphat set right with kik again) (e:ka ~ theih nadingin Judah gam) (b:puahphat) (r:16.2.5) (q:draft)
puahphatna = (t:n) (w:repair/reform/improvement) (d:puahphat repair, set right, with the noun suffix na) (e:~ zong tampi tak kibawl khin hi/biakinn ~ ding a kisapna a kimuhna khempeuh | whatever is found to be needed for repairing the temple) (s:puahna) (b:puahphat) (r:44.24.2/12.12.5) (q:draft)
puahsak = (t:v) (w:repair/restore/set right) (d:puah, repair, with sak: have something repaired, or repair it for someone) (e:a sia khempeuh kong ~ kik ding hi/kisapna a kimuhna khempeuh ~ un | have every damage that is found repaired) (b:puah) (r:26.36.33/12.12.5) (q:draft)
puahsakkik = (t:v) (w:restore/rebuild/repair again) (d:puahsak repair, with kik again, back) (e:a sia khempeuh kong ~ ding hi) (b:puahsak) (r:26.36.33/26.36.34) (q:draft)
puahsiang = (t:v) (w:cleanse/purify) (d:put in order and make clean, said of the temple and its articles) (e:biakinn a ~ dingin/a nazatte khempeuh ka ~ khin uh hi | we have purified all its utensils) (s:siangsak/siansuah) (a:ninsak) (b:puah) (r:14.29.15/14.29.18) (q:draft)
puahte = (t:n) (w:dressers/tenders/keepers) (d:puah repair or tend, with te, those who; leenggui puahte are vinedressers) (e:leenggui ~ hi ding uh hi/lokhote leh leenggui ~ nei hi | he had farmers and vinedressers) (b:puah) (r:23.61.5/14.26.10) (q:draft)
