sa = (t:n) (w:meat) (d:the flesh of an animal as food; sa ne is eat meat and sa huan is cook meat) (e:Pasian in ~ pia hi/a ~ leh anlum a om laite | the rest of the meat and the bread/kikhopna buk kongah a ~ huan un | cook the meat at the entrance to the tent of meeting/a siang mi khempeuh in a ~ ne thei ding uh a | anyone who is clean may eat the meat) (s:sameh) (r:3.8.32/3.8.31/3.7.19)
sa = (t:n) (w:flesh) (d:the flesh of the body of a person or an animal; ci leh sa, flesh, also stands for human nature and for one’s own kin) (e:ci leh ~/vasate in na ~ ne ding uh hi | the birds will eat your flesh/A ci a ~ khempeuh kiam a | all his flesh wastes away/keima si keima ~ na hi takpi hi | you are truly my own flesh and blood) (s:satak/cilesa) (r:45.8.5/26.32.5/1.40.19/18.33.21/1.29.14)
sa = (t:n) (w:animal/creature/game) (d:a wild animal, especially one that is hunted or eaten, game or prey; sa beng is hunt game and gamsa is a wild animal) (e:gam~ na ne in/kei adingin ~ va beng in | go and hunt game for me/ka nek dingin ~ matsa hong paipih in la | bring me game to eat/humhamin a ~ nek ding uh man uh a | growling, they seize their prey) (s:ganhing) (r:1.27.3/1.27.7/23.5.29)
sa = (t:adj) (w:hot) (d:hot; a sa is the heat, the opposite of a vot, the cold) (e:an ~ na ne in/mei phualpi lah ~ lua mahmah ahih manin | because the furnace was so very hot/Ni hong ~ ding hi | it is going to be hot/sun-in a ~ in hong kang a | by day the heat consumed me/a vot leh a ~ | cold and heat) (a:vot) (r:27.3.22/42.12.55/1.31.40/1.8.22)
saal = (t:n) (w:storehouse/barn/storeroom) (d:a building or room where grain and goods are stored; also of the storehouses from which God brings out the wind) (e:a ~ sung panin huih/~ ahi zongin a nei kei uh hi | they have no barn either/a ~ sung panin huih a nungsak hi | he brings out the wind from his storehouses) (s:ansal/vankoihna) (r:24.10.13/42.12.24/24.51.16) (q:draft)
saalte = (t:n) (w:barns/storehouses) (d:saal, storehouse, with the plural te: buildings where grain and goods are stored) (e:ama ~ panin huih pusuak sak hi/ka ~ uh dimin an nam khempeuh | our barns full of every kind of food) (s:ansalte/ansaalte/koihnate) (b:saal) (r:19.135.7/19.144.13) (q:draft)
saam = (t:see) <saam-ek>
saam-ek = (t:n) (w:dross/slag) (d:the waste that separates from a metal when it is melted and refined; the second part, ek, means dung or dross) (e:na ~ teng uh tuikhia sakin) (s:ek) (r:23.1.25) (q:draft)
saan = (t:v) (w:cast lots/cast/practise divination) (d:used after ai, aai or lai-ai, a lot: cast lots to decide or share out something, and also practise divination) (e:kongpi ding ai ~ uh hi/ka puan hawm nadingin lai-ai ~ uh hi | they cast lots to share out my garment/Kei leh ka tapa Jonathan kikal-ah ai ~ un | cast the lot between me and my son Jonathan/note adingin aai ka ~ ding hi | I will cast lots for you/ai a ~, khong a khai | who practises divination or sorcery) (r:13.26.13/19.22.18/9.14.42/6.18.6/5.18.10) (q:draft)
saan = (t:v) (w:rise/mount up/rouse/rally) (d:rise up, as waves do; tha saan is rouse or rally one’s strength, and hat saan lai is the prime of life) (e:a ~’ ciangin na daisak hi/Na tha ~ in la | rouse your strength/Israel in a tha ~-in lupna tungah tu hi | Israel rallied his strength and sat up on the bed/na zak ciangin na tha ~ in | when you hear it, rouse yourself/Ka hat ~ lai takin a si ding | to die in the prime of my life) (r:19.89.9/19.80.2/1.48.2/10.5.24/23.38.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
saang = (t:v) (w:accept/receive/take) (d:take what is handed over or offered; also accept something as true, and approve of it) (e:a neipa in tua kiciamna ~ ding a/note’ khut panin a lawh hong ~ ding a | he will take the basket from your hands/a khut tawh a nasepnate ~ in | accept the work of his hands/Kumpipa in zuauthu ~-in na sem leh | if a ruler accepts lies and acts on them) (a:nial/nolh) (r:2.22.11/5.26.4/5.33.11/20.29.12) (q:draft)
saangin = (t:v) (w:receive/accept/take) (d:saang, receive, with the linking ending in: taking what is handed over, or accepting a plea, before a following verb) (e:Pasian in ama kutna ~, a thuumna ngai hi/kamtaite tung panin a lai puak uh ~ | receiving the letter from the messengers/leengte le bawngtalte ~ Levi mite a pia hi | he took the carts and oxen and gave them to the Levites/Jesuh in ~ amaute’ muhin a ne hi | Jesus took it and ate it in their presence) (b:saang) (r:14.33.13/23.37.14/4.7.6/42.24.43) (q:draft)
saanin = (t:v) (w:casting lots/casting) (d:saan, cast, with the linking ending in; ai saanin is casting lots) (e:keel nihte tungah ai ~) (b:saan) (r:3.16.8) (q:draft)
saanna = (t:n) (w:casting of lots/divination) (d:saan, cast, with the noun suffix na; ai saanna is the casting of lots, and also divination) (e:ai ~ na sem kei ding uh hi/vankahna leh ai ~ lamah kihei-in | turning to mediums and divination/ai ~ tawh nasepna tavuan la uh hi | they took up their duties by casting lots) (s:aisanna) (b:saan) (r:3.19.26/13.24.31/3.20.6) (q:draft)
saante = (t:n) (w:diviners/spiritists/soothsayers) (d:saan, cast, with the plural te; ai saante are those who cast lots to divine) (e:Vankahte leh ai ~ lamah kihei kei un/khong khaite leh ai ~’ thu ngai uh hi | they listen to sorcerers and diviners) (s:aisante) (b:saan) (r:3.19.31/5.18.14) (q:draft)
sabakte = (t:n) (w:pieces of meat/pieces) (d:sa, meat, with bak, piece, and the plural te: the cut pieces of a slaughtered animal) (e:a ~ le a lu tawh) (r:2.29.17) (q:draft)
sabakthani = (t:phrase) (w:sabachthani) (d:Aramaic word kept in the cry of Jesus on the cross, lama sabakthani, why have you forsaken me) (e:Eloi, Eloi, lama ~) (r:41.15.34/40.27.46) (q:draft)
Sabakthani = (t:phrase) (w:sabachthani) (d:Aramaic word kept in the cry of Jesus on the cross, lama sabakthani, why have you forsaken me) (e:Elio, Elio, Lama ~) (b:sabakthani) (r:41.15.34) (q:draft)
sabawh = (t:v) (w:pounce on prey/seize prey) (d:sa, animal or prey, with bawh, pounce on: of a beast of prey, spring on its kill) (e:a ~ nuam bangin amaute in) (r:19.22.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
sabbath = (t:n) (w:Sabbath) (d:the seventh day of the week, the day of rest; sabbath ni is the Sabbath day and sabbath tang is keep the Sabbath) (e:~ ni-in sing a tom mi khat/na siangthosak dingin ~ ni tang in | observe the Sabbath day by keeping it holy/Note in ka ~-te tangin | you shall keep my Sabbaths/~ ni-in na ten’na khempeuh uh-ah | in all your dwellings on the Sabbath day) (s:Nipi/Nipini) (r:4.15.32/2.35.3/5.5.12/3.19.30) (q:draft)
Sabbath = (t:n) (w:Sabbath) (d:the weekly day of rest, written with a capital letter; Sabbath ni is the Sabbath day) (e:ni in ~ ni ahi hi/~ ni a siangtho-a zat ding phawk in | remember to keep the Sabbath day holy/Tua ni in ~ ni ahi hi | that day was a Sabbath/~ ni leh kha det ni simin | on every Sabbath and New Moon) (s:Nipi/Nipini) (b:sabbath) (r:43.9.14/2.20.8/43.5.9/26.46.3) (q:draft)
sabbathte = (t:n) (w:Sabbaths) (d:sabbath with the plural te; used with tang, keep, and with palsat or siasak, desecrate) (e:ka ~ zong palsat lai uh hi/~ zong kitang lo hi | the Sabbaths are not kept either/ka ~ siasak uh hi | they desecrated my Sabbaths/~ na siangthosak un | keep the Sabbaths holy) (b:sabbath) (r:26.23.38/26.20.12/26.22.8/26.20.24/26.20.20) (q:draft)
sabbatth = (t:n) (w:sabbath) (d:the word sabbath, here spelled with a second t, probably a misprint) (e:leitang in Topa adingin ~ tang ding) (s:sabbath) (r:3.25.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
sabeel = (t:n) (w:pot of meat/meat pot/cooking pot) (d:sa, meat, with beel, pot: a pot in which meat is cooked) (e:~ phungah tu-in ka kham takun) (r:2.16.3) (q:draft)
sabeng = (t:n) (w:hunter) (d:sa, animal, with beng, hunt: one who hunts game; compare ngabeng, fisherman, in the same verse) (e:~ tampi ka khah ding a/~ pa’ kiang panin a suahtak nadingin | to get free from the hunter) (s:sabengpa/bengpa) (r:24.16.16/20.6.5) (q:draft)
sabengpa = (t:n) (w:hunter) (d:a man who hunts animals; sabeng with pa marking a male person) (e:a vanglian ~ zong ahi hi/~’ kiang panin a suahtak nadingin | to get free from the hunter) (s:sabeng/bengpa) (b:sabeng) (r:1.10.9/20.6.5) (q:draft)
sabengte = (t:n) (w:hunters/pursuers) (d:sabeng, hunter, with the plural te: those who hunt or chase game) (e:~ a muh ciangin) (b:sabeng) (r:25.1.6) (q:draft)
sabet = (t:n) (w:hunting/catching prey) (d:the hunting or catching of animals; sabet siam is skilled at hunting) (e:gamsung mi ~ siam khat hi a/~ zong hong siam a, mi hong ne hi | he learned to catch prey and devoured people) (s:betna) (r:1.25.27/26.19.3) (q:draft)
sabetna = (t:see) <sabetna-ah>
sabetna-ah = (t:n) (w:in hunting/when hunting) (d:sa, game animal, with bet, hunt, the noun suffix na and ah, in: in the hunting of game) (e:~, a kine thei ding gamsa) (r:3.17.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
sabit = (t:adj) (w:whole/single/entire) (d:kep sabit khat, one whole pearl: each gate made of a single pearl) (e:kep ~ khat ahi hi) (r:66.21.21) (q:draft, low confidence)
Sabta = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Sabta) (d:people descended from Sabta, a son of Cush; the name is written Sabtah in Genesis) (r:13.1.9) (q:draft)
Sabtah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Sabtah) (d:son of Cush and grandson of Ham) (r:1.10.7)
Sabteka = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Sabteca/Sabteka) (d:son of Cush and grandson of Ham) (r:1.10.7)
sabuai = (t:n) (w:table) (d:a table, for eating at or for setting things on; in the tabernacle, the table of the bread of the Presence) (e:~ leh a nazat khempeuhte/~ tungah Ompihna Anlum na koih tawntung ding hi | you shall always put the bread of the Presence on the table/Ompihna Anlum adingin ~ kham a gihna ciat | the weight of gold for each table for the bread of the Presence/~ khempeuh a luak uh tawh kidim a | all the tables are covered with their vomit) (r:2.39.36/13.28.16/2.25.30/23.28.8) (q:draft)
sabuaiah = (t:n) (w:at the table/at table) (d:sabuai, table, with the place marker ah; sabuaiah tu is sit at table for a meal) (e:Topa ~ a tut lai takin/~ a tut khawmpihte a zahtak manin | out of regard for those sitting at table with him) (b:sabuai) (r:40.26.7/40.14.9) (q:draft)
sabuaite = (t:n) (w:tables) (d:sabuai, table, with the plural te) (e:Hih ~ kimkotah khut peek cia/Ompihna Anlum adingin ~ | the tables for the bread of the Presence/ngun ~ adingin ngun a gihna | the weight of silver for the silver tables/sumkheekte’ dangkate bua-in amaute ~ a sawnpai hi | he scattered the money changers’ coins and overturned their tables) (b:sabuai) (r:26.40.43/14.4.19/13.28.16/43.2.15) (q:draft)
sabuk = (t:v) (w:lie in wait for prey/lurk) (d:seemingly sa prey with buk lie in ambush, of a young lion crouching in cover) (e:humpinelkai khanglai ~ tawh kibang uh) (r:19.17.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
Saddusi = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Sadducee) (d:member of a Jewish religious party, linked with the chief priests, that denied the resurrection of the dead) (r:41.12.18/40.3.7)
Saddusite = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Sadducees) (d:the Sadducees, a Jewish religious party that denied the resurrection, often named with the Pharisees) (b:Saddusi) (r:40.22.23/40.16.1)
Saf = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Saph) (d:descendant of Rapha, a Philistine giant killed by Sibbekai the Hushathite) (r:10.21.18) (q:draft)
