sahin = (t:adj) (w:thick) (d:sah, thick, with the linking ending in, joining it to the next description) (e:A kulh ~ sang mahmah a/tong guk ~, tong guk mah sang hi | six cubits thick and six cubits high) (b:sah) (r:66.21.12/26.40.5) (q:draft)
sahna = (t:n) (w:thickness) (d:sah, thick, with the noun ending na: how thick a thing is, used in measurements of walls and vessels) (e:A ~ in khutpeek mai cia ahi hi/Inndei neute a kawm ~ tong nga pha a | the wall of the side rooms was five cubits thick/a ~ zung li pha-in a sung hawm hi | it was four fingers thick, and hollow) (b:sah) (r:11.7.26/26.41.9/24.52.21) (q:draft)
sahpi = (t:adj) (w:thick/dense) (d:sah, thick, with the augmentative pi; said of cloud, darkness and a shield) (e:ama khe nuai-ah meivom ~ om hi/mual tungah meii ~ om a | there was a thick cloud over the mountain/a kihtakhuai khuamial ~ om hi | there was a thick and dreadful darkness/a lum ~ tawh lehdo hi | he charges against him with his thick shield) (b:sah) (r:19.18.9/2.19.9/2.19.16/1.15.12/18.15.26) (q:draft)
sahpite = (t:adj) (w:thick/dense) (d:sahpi, thick, with the plural te: said of thick clouds and thick darkness) (e:Meiipite leh khuamial ~ ama kiim-ah om a/gialpi leh mei-amte in ama meii ~ phulet hi | hailstones and bolts of lightning broke through his thick clouds) (b:sahpi) (r:19.97.2/19.18.12) (q:draft)
sai = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:elephant) (d:in the saying about the eye of a needle the Tedim text has sai where the English has camel) (e:~ khat phim vangah a khumhak sangin/~ khat in phim bil vangah a khumhak sangin | than for an elephant to go through the eye of a needle) (r:42.18.25/41.10.25/40.19.24) (q:draft)
sai = (t:v) (w:be in charge of/manage/attend to) (d:look after a household or task; kumpi-inn sung a sai, the one in charge of the palace; kigal sai, opposite each other, is a separate expression) (e:kumpi-inn sung a ~ Eliakim) (r:23.36.22) (q:draft, low confidence)
