sakna = (t:n) (d:noun form of the causative sak: the act, place or time of making something be so, as in lungdam sakna, what pleases, and kisian’ sakna mun, a place of refining) (e:Topa lungdam ~ in bang ahi hiam/kham a kisian’ ~ mun | a place where gold is refined/a kisehsa suahtak ~ hun | the appointed time of release) (b:sak) (r:49.5.10/18.28.1/5.31.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
sakna = (t:n) (w:singing) (d:noun form of sa, sing: singing, in la sakna, the singing of songs) (e:la ~ om nawn lo a/tua ka zak pen la ~ aw-ging ahi hi | what I hear is the sound of singing/lungdam kohna leh la ~ aw om ding hi | thanksgiving and the sound of singing will be there) (s:lasakna) (r:23.24.9/2.32.18/23.51.3) (q:draft)
sakna = (t:n) (d:noun form of sa, feel or regard as: the feeling so named, as in nuam sakna, delight, what one finds pleasant) (e:na thupiaknate pen nuam ka ~ ahi hi/nangma thu in nuam ka ~ ahi hi | your law is my delight/pammaih ka ~ tawh | in my zeal) (r:19.119.143/19.119.77/4.25.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
saknate = (t:n) (w:songs/singing/musical instruments) (d:sakna, singing, with plural te; la saknate, the singing of songs, and with tum, play, the instruments of song) (e:laiza tawh la ~ daii ta hi/la ~ na tum nuam uh hi | you love to play instruments of song) (b:sakna) (r:23.24.8/30.6.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
saknate = (t:n) (w:delights/pleasures) (d:in nuam a saknate, the things one finds pleasant, from sa, feel or regard as) (e:amah in nuam a ~ pen) (b:sakna) (r:19.147.10) (q:draft)
saknung = (t:adj) (w:upper) (d:seen once of a gate, Benjamin Kongpi saknung, where the English has the Upper Gate of Benjamin) (e:Benjamin Kongpi ~ gei) (s:tungnung) (a:nuainung) (r:24.20.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
