sakolpite = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:mares) (d:sakol horse with pi, female, and plural te) (e:Faro’ sakoltal in ~ a delh bangin) (b:sakol) (r:22.1.9) (q:draft)
sakoltal = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:stallion/male horse) (d:sakol horse with tal, the male of an animal) (e:Faro’ ~ in sakolpite a delh bangin) (r:22.1.9/26.23.20) (q:draft)
sakolte = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:horses) (d:sakol, horse, with the plural te) (e:Amau’ meel in ~ tawh kibang a/gam khempeuh panin ~ kila hi | horses were brought from all countries/na ~ tawh tuipi na tuancil a | you trampled the sea with your horses/Amau’ ~ zasagih leh sawmthum-le-guk | their horses were seven hundred and thirty-six) (b:sakol) (r:29.2.4/14.9.28/35.3.15/15.2.66) (q:draft)
sakpa = (t:part) (d:causative sak with the male ending pa, placed after a verb: the one who causes it or makes it happen, he who made; also the one to whom it was done, as in a nuntakkik sakpa, the one who was raised) (e:I mit a piang ~ in/sihna panin a nuntakkik ~ | the one who was raised from the dead/Khazih Zeisu a thokik ~ in | he who raised Christ Jesus from the dead/nang adinga hong do ~ | the one who fights for you) (b:sak) (r:19.94.9/44.13.37/45.8.11/5.3.22) (q:draft)
