saksa = (t:part) (d:the causative sak with sa, already done, after a verb: that has been made or caused to, as in kisiang saksa, refined) (e:mei tawh kisiang ~ kham ahi zongin/amah a it mite a dingin a bawlkholh ~ | what he has prepared for those who love him/Keima pian’~ sungah lungdamin kipakin om tawntung un | be glad and rejoice forever in what I have created) (b:sak) (r:66.3.18/23.65.18/46.2.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
