satnen = (t:v) (w:shatter/smash to pieces/crush/grind) (d:sat strike with nen fine, beat something until it is in small pieces or powder) (e:nang hong zangin gamdangte ka ~ a/kumpite leh ukpite ka ~ hi | I shatter governors and officials/Moses’ bawlsa sumngo gulpi ~ hi | he broke in pieces the bronze snake Moses had made/a neu mahmahin na ~ ding a | you shall grind it very fine) (s:satvui) (r:24.51.20/2.30.36/24.51.23/12.18.4) (q:draft)
satnenin = (t:v) (w:smashing/shattering) (d:satnen smash to pieces with the linking suffix in) (e:Sik in na khempeuh ~ a gawivui bangin) (b:satnen) (r:27.2.40) (q:draft)
satnenzo = (t:v) (w:be able to smash/break in pieces) (d:satnen smash to pieces with zo be able) (e:suangtum a ~ sek tawh) (b:satnen) (r:24.23.29) (q:draft)
satnim = (t:v) (w:bruise/beat sore) (d:sat strike with nim; satnim gawpnate is bruises or wounds from blows) (e:~ gawpnate leh meimapite) (r:23.1.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
satpa = (t:n) (w:striker/one who struck) (d:sat, strike, with pa marking a man: the one who struck) (e:Amaute a ~’ lamah mite kihei lo/a ~’ kiang panin a pasal a honkhia dingin | to rescue her husband from the one striking him) (b:sat) (r:23.9.13/5.25.11) (q:draft)
satpa = (t:n) (w:founder) (d:sat, build or found, with pa marking a man: the man who founded a town) (e:Gibeon khuapi a ~ Jeiel in Gibeon ah/Tehinnah in Irnahash khuapi ~ ahi hi | Tehinnah was the founder of the town of Ir Nahash/Gibeon-ah Gibeon khuapi a ~ Jeiel teeng a | Jeiel, the founder of Gibeon, lived in Gibeon) (b:sat) (r:13.8.29/13.9.35/13.4.12) (q:draft)
satpaai = (t:v) (w:strike/strike down) (d:sat strike with paai away; spelling of satpai in the 1932 text) (e:Pasian in kei hong ~ hi) (r:18.19.21) (q:draft)
satpai = (t:v) (w:strike/strike down) (d:sat strike with pai away) (e:Pasian in kei hong ~ ta hi) (r:18.19.21) (q:draft)
satpiang = (t:n) (w:lye/soap) (d:a cleansing agent used for washing the body and clothes) (e:~ tampi na zang zongin/puante a siangthosak ~ tawh kibang hi | he is like the soap that cleans clothes) (s:vuttui) (r:24.2.22/39.3.2)
satpuk = (t:v) (w:strike down/defeat) (d:sat, strike, with puk, fall: strike someone so that he falls, kill or defeat) (e:amah a mudahte ka ~ ding hi/Keimah in kumpipa bek ka ~ ding a | I would strike down only the king/Siria thum vei bek na ~ ding hi | you will defeat Aram only three times/amah ~ in la, phum in | strike him down and bury him) (s:sattuk/satlum) (r:19.89.23/12.13.19/10.17.2/11.2.31) (q:draft)
satpukin = (t:v) (w:striking down/attacking) (d:satpuk, strike down, with the linking ending in, joining it to the next verb: strike down and then) (e:amah ~ that a/Jabesh’ tapa Shallum ~ that a | he struck down Shallum son of Jabesh and killed him/Ibleam-ah amah ~ that a | at Ibleam he struck him down and killed him/Pasian in mite ~ sisak thei a | God can strike people down and make them die) (s:sattukin) (b:satpuk) (r:12.15.30/12.15.14/12.15.10/18.34.20) (q:draft)
satpukte = (t:n) (w:those who struck down/killers) (d:satpuk strike down with the plural te) (e:Amah a ~ pen ama nasemte) (b:satpuk) (r:12.12.21) (q:draft)
satsa = (t:adj) (w:built/rebuilt) (d:sat build with sa marking a completed action: that has been built) (e:amau’ ~ khuapite a min thak phuak) (s:lamsa) (b:sat) (r:4.32.38) (q:draft)
satsak = (t:v) (w:have flogged/have beaten) (d:sat, beat, with sak, cause: order someone to be flogged) (e:a ~ khit ciangin singlamteh tungah/Zeisu a sap khit ciangin a ~ hi | he sent for Jesus and had him flogged/a khialhna zahin ama muhin ~ ding hi | he shall have him flogged in his presence as the offence deserves/a theih nadingin a ~ hi | he had him flogged in order to find out) (b:sat) (r:40.27.26/43.19.1/5.25.2/44.22.24) (q:draft)
satsak = (t:v) (w:inflame/heat up) (d:of wine heating those who drink it) (e:leenggah zu in amaute a ~ pialpual matengin) (r:23.5.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
satsat = (t:v) (w:strike repeatedly/keep beating/pound) (d:sat, strike, said twice for a repeated action) (e:Namsau in ~ ding hi/a sih dek dongin na ~ hangin | though you pound him until he is nearly dead) (r:26.21.14/20.27.22) (q:draft)
sattan = (t:v) (w:cut off/cut down/chop off) (d:sat, strike, with tan, cut through: cut off a limb or cut something down with a blow) (e:hong puksak leh, na ~ in/na khut na khe ~ in la, paii in | cut off your hand or your foot and throw it away/a sikzawlte ka ~ ding hi | I will cut through the iron bars/mei tawh hal-in ~ uh hi | they burned it with fire and cut it down) (s:satkhia/sattat/attan) (r:41.9.43/20.26.6/40.18.8/23.45.2/19.80.16) (q:draft)
sattansak = (t:v) (w:cut off) (d:sattan cut off with sak, done to or for another person) (e:tua nu’ khut na ~ ding uh hi) (b:sattan) (r:5.25.12) (q:draft)
sattantawm = (t:v) (w:cut off one's own) (d:sat strike with tan cut through and tawm oneself: cut off a part of oneself) (e:ama khe mah a ~) (r:20.26.6) (q:draft)
sattat = (t:v) (w:cut off/sever/hamstring) (d:cut through with a blow; zagui sattat is to hamstring, cut the leg sinew of an animal) (e:bawngtalte zagui ~ uh hi/a sakolte uh a zagui na ~ ding a | you are to hamstring their horses/amau’ sakolte uh a zagui ~ sakin | he had their horses hamstrung) (s:sattan) (r:1.49.6/6.11.6/6.11.9) (q:draft)
sattatin = (t:v) (w:cutting/cutting loose/severing) (d:sattat, cut through, with the linking ending in: cutting and then going on to the next action) (e:a kikhihna khau ~ a khahkhia uh hi/sikkawipi khaute ~ tui sungah khiasuk uh a | cutting the anchor ropes they let them fall into the sea) (b:sattat) (r:44.27.32/44.27.40) (q:draft)
sattawm = (t:v) (w:clear for oneself/cut for oneself) (d:sat cut with tawm for oneself; gam sattawm is clear forest land for oneself) (e:nomau a dingin gam ~ un) (r:6.17.15) (q:draft)
satte = (t:n) (w:those who beat/smiters) (d:sat beat with te: the people who strike someone) (e:Hong ~ tungah ka nung ka dawh a) (b:sat) (r:23.50.6) (q:draft)
satthang = (t:v) (w:demolish/smash down/break down) (d:sat strike with thang: knock a building to pieces) (e:inn hoihpipite ~ gawp ding uh hi) (r:26.26.12) (q:draft)
satthanggawp = (t:v) (w:demolish utterly/smash to ruins) (d:satthang demolish with gawp, which marks a strong or thorough action) (e:inn hoihpipite ~ ding uh hi) (b:satthang) (r:26.26.12) (q:draft)
satthuak = (t:v) (w:be beaten/suffer a beating) (d:sat strike with thuak suffer; satthuak nading is deserving a beating) (e:~ nading a gamtakha nasem pa) (r:42.12.48) (q:draft)
sattuk = (t:v) (w:strike down/cut down/kill) (d:sat, strike, with tuk, fell: strike someone down, kill in battle or by attack) (e:Aijalon ciang dong Filistiate ~ uh hi/a khut a gim mateng Filistiate ~ a | he struck down the Philistines till his hand grew tired/kua in hihte khempeuh ~ ahi hiam | who struck down all these/Gibbethon ah amah ~ hi | he struck him down at Gibbethon) (s:satpuk/satlum) (r:9.14.31/11.15.27/10.23.10/12.10.9) (q:draft)
sattukin = (t:v) (w:striking down/cutting down) (d:sattuk, strike down, with the linking ending in, joining it to the next verb) (e:Elah ~ that a/nang hong ~ na lu ka tankhia ding hi | I will strike you down and cut off your head) (s:satpukin) (b:sattuk) (r:11.16.10/9.17.46) (q:draft)
satui = (t:n) (w:broth/soup) (d:sa, meat, with tui, water: the liquid in which meat was boiled) (e:a ~ beel sung khatah koih a/a tungah a ~ sung in | pour the broth over it) (s:mehtui) (r:7.6.19/7.6.20) (q:draft)
satvui = (t:v) (w:crush to powder/beat fine/pulverize) (d:sat, strike, with vui, dust: beat or grind something until it is like dust) (e:Leivui bangin amaute ka ~ a/Ashera milimte leh milim dangte ~ a | he crushed the Asherah poles and the other idols to powder/a suangte sukham a, tuate ~ hi | he broke up its stones and ground them to powder/Huihpi mai-ah leivui bangin amaute ka ~ a | I beat them as fine as dust before the wind) (s:gawivui/suvui) (r:10.22.43/14.34.7/12.23.15/19.18.42) (q:draft)
satzan = (t:v) (w:hack to pieces/cut to pieces/break down) (d:sat, strike or cut, with zan: strike until the thing is broken apart) (e:a namsau uh tawh hong ~ ding uh hi/sumngo kongkhakte ~-in a sikzawlte ka sattan ding hi | I will break down the bronze gates and cut through the iron bars/Rahab a ~ gawppa | the one who cut Rahab to pieces) (r:26.16.40/23.45.2/23.51.9) (q:draft)
satzanin = (t:v) (w:breaking down/hacking to pieces) (d:satzan hack to pieces with the linking suffix in) (e:sumngo kongkhakte ~ a sikzawlte ka sattan ding a) (b:satzan) (r:23.45.2) (q:draft)
sau = (t:adj) (w:long) (d:long in measure or in time; after a number of cubits it gives the length) (e:tong sawmli ~ hi/tong sawm leh thum ~ hi | it was thirteen cubits long/tong sawmli ~-in tong sawmthum zai a | forty cubits long and thirty cubits wide/Nuntak ~ tawh amah ka lungkim sak ding a | with long life I will satisfy him) (s:saupi) (a:tom) (r:11.6.17/26.40.11/26.46.22/19.91.16)
sau = (t:adj) (w:lengthy) (d:long in time, as in sau veipi, a very long while) (e:~ veipi sung peemta-in om hi/~ veipi thu a ngen uh hi | they make lengthy prayers) (s:saupi) (r:1.21.34/41.12.40)
saukik = (t:v) (w:grow long again) (d:sau long with kik again) (e:Na khamul uh a ~ mateng) (b:sau) (r:10.10.5) (q:draft)
Saul = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Saul) (d:first king of Israel, son of Kish of the tribe of Benjamin; also the Hebrew name of the apostle Paul) (e:~ in David encik hi) (r:9.18.9/9.14.51) (q:draft)
saulam = (t:n) (w:length) (d:sau long with lam side: the long side, set against zailam width) (e:a ~ tai sawm) (s:sauna/dunglam) (a:zailam) (r:26.45.3) (q:draft)
saulua = (t:adj) (w:too long/overgrown) (d:sau long with lua too much: of a limb or body part that is too long; the NIV has deformed) (e:a ~ ahih kei leh a tom luate/maihem, le khutlekhe ~ | disfigured, or with a limb too long/a ~-in zong hawi lo ding uh hi | nor shall they let it grow too long) (b:sau) (r:3.22.23/3.21.18/26.44.20) (q:draft)
sauna = (t:n) (w:length) (d:sau, long, with the noun suffix na: the length of a thing, paired with zaina for the width) (e:teembaw a ~ tong zathum/a ~ tong tul sawmnih leh tul nga hi-in | its length being 25,000 cubits/A ~, a zaina, a pianzia | their length, their width, their design/lampi ~ tong sawmnga pha hi | the length of the way was fifty cubits) (s:saulam/dung) (a:zaina) (b:sau) (r:1.6.15/26.48.13/26.42.11/26.40.15)
saupi = (t:adj) (w:long) (d:sau, long, with pi, great: very long, mostly of time, as in hun saupi sung, for a long time) (e:Hun ~ sung Israel in/tu ni dong hih hun ~ sung | for this long time, to this very day/hun ~ sung Israel mite om ding | the Israelites will live for a long time/hun ~, kum sawmnih bang pha a | a long time, some twenty years) (s:sau) (a:tom) (r:14.15.3/6.22.3/28.3.4/9.7.2)
saupi = (t:adj) (w:lengthy) (e:kum ~ zong nungta thei kha ding hi | he may live many years) (r:21.6.3)
saupi = (t:adj) (w:extended/prolonged/extensive) (e:amaute kikalah ~ a kihalin | with a wide space between them) (r:9.26.13)
saupipi = (t:adj) (w:very long/lengthy) (d:saupi long, with pi doubled for emphasis; thu saupipi ngen is make lengthy prayers) (e:thu ~ a ngen uh hi/kineihna tawh ~ thu na ngen uh hi | for a show you make lengthy prayers) (b:saupi) (r:42.20.47/41.12.40/40.23.14) (q:draft)
sausak = (t:v) (w:lengthen/prolong) (d:sau, long, with sak, cause: make long or longer, mostly of life, as in khan’ sausak, give long life) (e:na nuntakna hong ~ ding hi/Na khaute ~ inla | lengthen your cords/Kong thuhilhte in na khan’ hong ~ ding a | my teachings will prolong your life/Pilna in hong khan’ ~ a | wisdom gives you long life) (a:tomsak/khiapsak) (b:sau) (r:20.9.11/20.3.2/23.54.2/20.3.16) (q:draft)
saute = (t:adj) (w:long/lingering/prolonged) (d:sau long, with the plural te: nat saute are lingering illnesses and nuntak saute those who live long) (e:nuntak ~ in thu thei tel uh hi/a nasia, nat ~ hong tungsak ding hi | he will bring on you severe and lingering illnesses) (b:sau) (r:18.12.12/5.28.59) (q:draft)
sauvei = (t:adv) (w:for a long time/long) (d:sau, long, with vei, a while: for a long time; bang tan sauvei asks how long) (e:~ ka teeng lua khin ta hi/~ khop na pai khin ta uh hi | you have travelled long enough/Bang tan ~ ding ahi hiam | how long will it be/tua leitang tungah note ~ na hing kei ding | you will not live long in that land/Amah ~ hau lo ding a | he will not be rich for long) (s:sawtvei/sawtpi) (a:tawlkhat) (r:19.120.6/5.4.26/5.2.3/19.90.13/18.15.29) (q:draft)
sauveipi = (t:adv) (w:for a long time/very long) (d:sauvei, for a long time, with pi, great: for a very long time) (e:~ note tawh omkhawm dingin/Hih kumpite khempeuh tawh ~ sung Joshua kido hi | Joshua waged war against all these kings for a long time/gamlakah ~ na om uh hi | you lived in the wilderness for a long time/bangzahin ~ a nungta ahi zongin | however long he lives) (s:sawtveipi/sawtpi) (a:tawlkhat) (b:sauvei) (r:46.16.7/6.11.18/6.24.7/21.6.3) (q:draft)
sauveipipi = (t:adv) (w:for a very long time) (d:sauveipi for a long time with pi doubled for emphasis) (e:~ kinungta ding hi) (b:sauveipi) (r:23.65.20) (q:draft)
sauveizo = (t:v) (w:last long/go on long) (d:sauvei for a long time with zo; sauveizo lua ta hi is has gone on too long already) (e:na mawh gamtatna uh ~ lua ta hi) (b:sauvei) (r:26.45.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
sauzaw = (t:adj) (w:longer) (d:sau, long, with zaw, more) (e:a po masa sangin a ~ hi/a hun ~ ahi zongin | or for a longer time) (b:sau) (r:27.8.3/4.9.22) (q:draft)
savokphual = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:mole/weasel) (d:a small animal that moves along the ground and is counted unclean; the NIV has weasel) (e:~, zusa, innhikpi nam khempeuh | the weasel, the rat, every kind of great lizard) (r:3.11.29)
Savokphual = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:mole/weasel) (d:a small animal counted unclean; the NIV has weasel) (e:~, zusa, innhikpi nam khempeuh) (b:savokphual) (r:3.11.29) (q:draft, low confidence)
savun = (t:n) (w:skin/leather/hide) (d:sa, animal, with vun, skin: the skin of an animal, also leather and a skin bag for wine) (e:~ puan bawl a, amaute silhsak hi/puan leh ~ peuhmah tui tawh kisawp ding a | any clothing or leather must be washed with water/~ um lui sungah leenggahtui thak | new wine in old wineskins/Levi mite in ~ a hawk lai takun | while the Levites were skinning the animals) (s:vun) (b:vun) (r:1.3.21/4.4.10/3.15.17/42.5.37/14.35.11) of animals
savunnim = (t:n) (w:tanning/leather-working) (d:savun, animal skin, in the phrase savunnim nasep, the trade of preparing hides, the work of a tanner) (e:~ nasepin a nei Simon/~ nasepin nei-in tuipi gei-ah a teng Simon’ inn-ah | in the house of Simon the tanner, who lives by the sea) (r:44.9.43/44.10.6/44.10.32) (q:draft)
savunte = (t:n) (w:skins/hides/leather) (d:savun, animal skin, with the plural te: skins or leather used as coverings) (e:a kisansak tuutal vunte le ~/a kisansak tuutal vunte, ~ ahi zongin | ram skins dyed red or other leather/tuutal vunte leh ~ tawh a kibawl khuhna | the covering made of ram skins and leather) (s:vunte) (b:savun) (r:2.35.7/2.39.34/2.35.23) (q:draft)
sawh = (t:v) (w:add/mix in/season) (d:put an ingredient such as yeast or salt into food; silngo sawh means leavened and silngo sawh loh unleavened) (e:silngo ~ loh anlum pawi/na biaknate khempeuh ci na ~ ding hi | season all your offerings with salt/silngo ~ nai loh a annel lom uh | their dough before the yeast was added/silngo ~ anlum tawh | with bread made with yeast/silngo ~ loh kine ding hi | it is to be eaten without yeast) (s:hel) (r:14.30.13/3.2.13/2.12.34/2.23.18/3.6.16) (q:draft)
Sawh = (t:v) (w:add/mix in) (d:sawh written with a capital in the festival name Silngo Sawh loh Anlum Pawi, the feast of bread with no yeast mixed in, the Festival of Unleavened Bread) (e:Silngo ~ loh Anlum Pawi hun/Silngo ~ loh Anlum Pawi ni sagih sung bawl | keeping the Festival of Unleavened Bread for seven days/Silngo ~ loh Anlum Pawi a kipat ni-in | on the first day of the Festival of Unleavened Bread) (b:sawh) (r:42.22.1/40.26.17/14.35.17) (q:draft)
sawhin = (t:v) (w:mixing in/adding/seasoning) (d:sawh add an ingredient, with the linking ending in: seasoned with salt, made with yeast) (e:silngo ~ a ki-em/ci ~ a nin bang lo | salted and pure/silngo ~ a ki-em hi lo ding hi | it must not be baked with yeast) (b:sawh) (r:3.23.17/2.30.35/3.6.17) (q:draft)
sawhloh = (t:adj) (w:unleavened/without yeast) (d:sawh, mix in, with the negative loh: with nothing mixed in; silngo sawhloh anlum is bread made without yeast) (e:silngo ~ anlum ni sagih sung/silngo ~ moh leh ankan ne uh hi | they ate unleavened bread and roasted grain/ni sagih sung silngo ~ anlum kine ding hi | for seven days bread made without yeast is to be eaten/silngo ~ anlum leh a kha meh tawh | with unleavened bread and bitter herbs) (r:2.13.6/2.12.8/6.5.11/4.28.17/4.9.11) (q:draft)
sawhlohin = (t:adv) (w:without yeast/unleavened) (d:sawhloh unleavened with the suffix in; silngo sawhlohin is with no yeast mixed in) (e:silngo ~ biakna tau gei-ah ne un) (b:sawhloh) (r:3.10.12) (q:draft)
sawhsa = (t:adj) (w:mixed/mixed in) (d:sawh mix in with sa marking a completed action) (e:zatui a ~ uh leenggahzu) (s:helsa) (b:sawh) (r:41.15.23) (q:draft)
sawi = (t:see) <sawi-in>
sawi-in = (t:todo) (r:11.7.29) (q:draft, describes ornamental work on the temple stands in 1 Kings 7:29 where the English has wreaths of hammered or bevelled work, the meaning of sawi cannot be told from the one verse)
sawisak = (t:v) (w:let waver/cause to shake) (d:sawi shake or waver with sak cause; sawisak loin is without wavering) (e:~ loin lenkip ni) (r:58.10.23) (q:draft, low confidence)
sawk = (t:v) (w:dip/reach into/put the hand in) (d:put the hand into a dish, bag or hole to take something) (e:Kei tawh kuang sungah an ka ~ khawmpihpa/kei tawh ankuang ka ~ khawmpihpa ahi hi | the one who dips into the bowl with me/naupang in gul gunei’ bu a ~ hangin | though the child puts its hand into the viper’s nest/a sunga omsa teng ~ thei ahih hang hi | because he could help himself to what was in it/a khut-in ankuang sung ~ suk a | he thrusts his hand down into the dish) (r:40.26.23/41.14.20/23.11.8/43.12.6/20.26.15) (q:draft)
sawk = (t:v) (w:grasp/take hold of) (d:reach out and seize, said of Jacob taking hold of his brother in the womb) (e:a sanggampa ~ pah a) (r:28.12.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
sawkin = (t:v) (w:reaching in/reaching out/scooping out) (d:sawk put the hand into or out toward something, with the linking ending in) (e:a khut-in a thung-ip ~ suangtang khat la/meikhuk ~ mei-am pawlkhat la a | reaching into the fire he took some coals/a khut tawh tuate ~ paisuak a | he scooped it out with his hands and went on/hong ~ ka sam-in hong man hi | he reached out and took me by the hair) (b:sawk) (r:9.17.49/7.14.9/26.10.7/26.8.3) (q:draft)
sawkkhawmna = (t:n) (w:dipping together/sharing a dish) (d:sawk dip the hand in with khawm together and the noun suffix na) (e:kei tawh an a ~ thu thei un) (r:42.22.21) (q:draft)
sawkkhawmte = (t:n) (w:those who dip together) (d:sawk dip the hand in with khawm together and the plural te) (e:kei tawh an kuang a ~ mah) (r:41.14.20) (q:draft)
sawksuk = (t:v) (w:dip into/thrust down into) (d:sawk dip the hand in with suk downward) (e:a khutin ankuang ~ a) (b:sawk) (r:20.26.15) (q:draft)
