sawl = (t:v) (w:send) (d:make someone go to a place or a person, with a task or a message) (e:Pasian in hong ~ hi/tuuno kikhahte bangin no kong ~ hi | I send you out like lambs/amaute in mihing sawmnga ~ uh hi | they sent fifty men/a susia dingin Topa in kote hong ~ khin | the Lord has sent us to destroy it) (s:puak/paisak) (r:43.1.6/55.4.12/42.10.3/12.2.17/1.19.13) (q:draft)
sawl = (t:v) (w:command/order/tell) (d:tell someone to do something) (e:Topa in amah a ~ bangin/a kap nop pen a kha dingin ~ hi | he commands it to hit the mark he aims at/kong ~ thute mangngilh ngei kei in | never forget the things I command you/Jehoida’ tapa Benaiah ~ hi | he gave orders to Benaiah son of Jehoiada) (s:thupia/vaikhak) (r:4.17.11/18.36.32/20.7.1/11.2.25) (q:draft)
Sawl = (t:v) (w:send) (d:given as the meaning of the name Siloam, Sent) (e:Siloam a cih ciangin, ~, a cihna) (b:sawl) (r:43.9.7) (q:draft)
sawlbawk = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:bush/shrub) (d:a low bush or shrub of the open country) (e:~ nuai khatah naupang lawn hi/sehnel gam-a po ~ bang hi a | he is like a bush growing in the desert/~ lakah a teengpa’ maipha tawh | with the favor of him who dwelt in the bush) (s:sawlpang/sawlkawm) (r:1.21.15/24.17.6/5.33.16) (q:draft)
sawlbuk = (t:n) (w:booth/temporary shelter/hut) (d:a shelter built of leafy branches, as at the festival of the seventh month) (e:tual-ah ~ lam uh hi/~ sungah Israel mite a om nading thu | that the Israelites should live in booths/khempeuh in ~ lamin tuate sungah om uh hi | they all built booths and lived in them) (s:bukno) (r:16.8.16/16.8.14/16.8.17) (q:draft)
sawlin = (t:v) (w:sending) (d:sawl with the linking suffix -in; mi sawlin, sending someone) (e:Joab in mi ~ gal kidona thu khempeuh/Solomon in mi ~ Tai-ar panin Hiram samsak hi | Solomon sent men and had Hiram brought from Tyre/amah in a vantungmite ~ | he will send his angels/a tuancil dingin amaute ~ thu ka pia hi | I send them with orders to trample) (b:sawl) (r:10.11.18/41.13.27/11.7.13/23.10.6) (q:draft)
sawlkawm = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:bush/thicket/undergrowth) (d:a bush or thicket, low dense growth where people or animals can hide; in Luke and Acts the burning bush of Moses) (e:~ nuai-ah kilomin omkhawm uh hi/a bukna ~ panin hong kuankhiazo a | he has come out of the thicket where he hides/~ sungah a kilang vantungmi | the angel who appeared in the bush/Moses in ~ lakah Topa a hopih lai-in | when Moses spoke to the Lord at the bush) (s:sawlbawk/sawlpang) (r:18.30.7/42.20.37/24.4.7/44.7.35) (q:draft)
sawlkhia = (t:v) (w:send out/send away) (d:sawl, send, with khia, out: send someone out of a place or away from oneself) (e:kiang panin amaute ~ hi/Isaak in Jakob ~ hi | Isaac sent Jacob away/Eden huan panin amah ~ hi | he sent him out of the garden of Eden/zan-in tua mite ~ hi | he sent those men out by night) (s:khahkhia/paikhiasak) (b:sawl) (r:1.25.6/11.9.27/1.28.5/1.3.23/6.8.3)
sawlkhiat = (t:v) (w:send away/send out) (d:form of sawlkhia used before kei, nading and in dependent clauses) (e:Keimah in ka ~ hi lo napi-in/nang kong ~ kei taak leh | if I do not send you away/lungnuam takin kong ~ mah bangun | just as we sent you away in peace/khedap keng loin kong ~ lai-in | when I sent you out without sandals) (b:sawlkhia) (r:24.23.21/9.20.13/1.26.29/42.22.35) (q:draft)
sawlkhiatna = (t:n) (w:sending away) (d:sawlkhiat send away with the noun suffix na) (e:kei nong ~ in kei tungah) (s:ciahsakna) (b:sawlkhiat) (r:10.13.16) (q:draft)
sawlkhop = (t:v) (w:send with/send together) (d:sawl send with khop, form of khawm together) (e:kei tawh nong ~ ding mi) (r:2.33.12) (q:draft)
sawlkik = (t:v) (w:send back) (d:send someone back to where they came from) (e:inn-ah a ~ galkapte in/hih mipa ~ in | send this man back/Egypt-ah amaute ka ~ ding hi | I will send them back to Egypt) (s:puakkik/ciahsakkik/ciahkiksak) (b:sawl) (r:14.25.13/9.29.4/28.8.13) (q:draft)
sawlkik = (t:v) (w:send again/send another) (d:send once more, a second time) (e:zahtakhuai zaw uliante khatvei ~ hi/adang khat a mihing sawmnga tawh ~ hi | he again sent another with his fifty men) (b:sawl) (r:4.22.15/12.1.11) (q:draft)
sawlkikin = (t:v) (w:sending back/sending again) (d:sawlkik with the linking suffix in: sending back or again and then going on to the next action) (e:Esther in Hathak mah ~ Mordekai’ tungah/Ammon mite’ kumpipa kiangah kamtaite ~ | sending messengers again to the king of the Ammonites) (b:sawlkik) (r:17.4.10/7.11.14) (q:draft)
sawllam = (t:n) (w:sending) (d:sawl send with lam, the fact or matter of: that someone has sent; a sawllam na thei hiam is do you know that he has sent) (e:Ishmael a ~ na thei hiam) (r:24.40.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
sawlna = (t:n) (w:sending/mission/command) (d:the act of sending, or the order with which someone is sent) (e:Topa’ hong ~ bangin/nang kiangah kong ~ thu thei in | know that I am sending him to you/Saul in a ~ mun peuhpeuhah | wherever Saul sent him/nong ~ peuhpeuhah ka pai ding uh hi | wherever you send us we will go) (b:sawl) (r:24.13.5/6.22.3/12.5.6/9.18.5/6.1.16) (q:draft)
sawlnate = (t:n) (w:commands/requirements/orders) (d:sawlna command with plural te: the things someone has ordered to be done) (e:ka Pasian uh hong ~ ka zui uh) (s:thupiakte) (b:sawlna) (r:14.13.11) (q:draft)
sawlnop = (t:v) (w:wish to command/want to order) (d:sawl command with nop, form of nuam want) (e:kong ~ uh thu panin) (r:53.3.6) (q:draft)
sawlpa = (t:n) (w:the one who sent/sender) (d:the man who sends, as kei hong sawlpa the one who sent me; pa marks a man) (e:Kei hong ~ zong a um hi/kei hong ~ zong a ngai hi | he also receives the one who sent me/kei hong ~’ thu ahi hi | it is the word of the one who sent me/Sawltak in a ~ sangin a lianzaw kei hi | a messenger is not greater than the one who sent him) (b:sawl) (r:43.12.45/40.10.40/43.7.16/43.13.16) (q:draft)
sawlpa = (t:n) (w:the one sent/messenger) (d:the man whom someone sends, as ka sawlpa the one I send) (e:ka ~ a ngai mi in/Pasian hong ~ upna in | to believe in the one God has sent/na ~ Zeisu Khazih a theihna | knowing Jesus Christ whom you have sent/mipilte that dinga a ~ Ariok kiangah | to Arioch, whom he had sent to kill the wise men) (s:kamtaipa/sawltakpa) (b:sawl) (r:43.13.20/43.6.29/43.17.3/27.2.24) (q:draft)
