sawlpang = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:bush) (d:a bush; in Exodus 3 and Acts 7 the burning bush that Moses saw) (e:~ kawm panin Pasian in amah sam a/Bang hangin ~ kangtum lo hiam | why is the bush not burned up/~ kuang hi, ahih hangin kangtum lo hi | the bush was on fire, yet it did not burn up/~ lak a meikuang sungah | in the flame of fire in the bush) (s:sawlbawk/sawlkawm) (r:2.3.4/2.3.2/2.3.3/44.7.30) (q:draft)
sawlpangte = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:branches/leafy branches) (d:sawlpang with the plural te; here leafy branches cut in the fields and spread on the road) (e:a sat uh ~ na phah uh hi) (b:sawlpang) (r:41.11.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
sawlsa = (t:v) (w:commanded/ordered/directed) (d:sawl, command or send, with sa marking a completed action; a sawlsa bangin is as he had commanded) (e:Moses in amaute a ~ bangin/hong ~ bangin hihin | do as he has commanded you/tuipi gei teng sim dingin ka ~ ahi hi | I have ordered it to attack the whole coast) (s:thupiaksa) (b:sawl) (r:6.4.12/24.47.7/6.8.8) (q:draft)
sawlsak = (t:v) (w:send) (d:sawl send with sak, for someone: send a person at the request of another or on his behalf) (e:Lazaras nong ~ nadingin kong ngen hi/ka inn uhah Lazaras nong ~ nadingin | that you would send Lazarus to my house) (b:sawl) (r:42.16.28/42.16.27) (q:draft)
sawlsawn = (t:n) (w:go-between/mediator/intermediary) (d:sawl send with sawn pass on: one through whom something is passed on) (e:kuamah ~ nei loin amah bek in) (s:palai) (r:48.3.20) (q:draft, low confidence)
