se-alte = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:jackals) (d:plural of se-al, a wild animal of desolate places) (e:~ bangin a nak huhu uh hi/~ a kawivak uh hi | jackals prowl about/kumpi inn nuam sungah ~ ham ding uh hi | jackals will cry in the fine palaces/~’ teen’na ka suak sak ding hi | I will make it a haunt of jackals) (r:24.14.6/25.5.18/23.13.22/24.9.11) (q:draft)
Se-irah = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Seirah) (d:place to which Ehud escaped after killing Eglon king of Moab) (r:7.3.26) (q:draft)
Seba = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Seba) (d:son of Cush, and the people and land named after him) (r:1.10.7)
Sebam = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Sebam) (d:town east of the Jordan in the land asked for by the tribes of Reuben and Gad) (r:4.32.3)
Sedi = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Sodi) (d:man of the tribe of Zebulun, father of the spy Gaddiel) (r:4.13.10)
seek = (t:v) (w:hammer/forge/beat/shape) (d:shape or sharpen metal by beating it; with in on the noun, beat one thing into another, as swords into ploughshares) (e:Lo khawhna tuute namsau-in ~ un la/singhiang heuhna temkawite teipi-in ~ un | beat your pruning hooks into spears/biakna tau sitna-in ~ hi | he hammered them into a covering for the altar/singhiang heuhna temkawi-in ~ ding uh hi | they will beat them into pruning hooks/tuate na bawl ciangin na ~ ding hi | when you make them you shall hammer them out) (s:sek) (r:29.3.10/4.16.39/23.2.4/4.10.2) (q:draft)
seekin = (t:v) (w:forge/hammer out/chisel/shape) (d:seek, shape or forge, with the linking ending in: shaping metal by hammering, cutting stone tablets, or forming bricks from clay) (e:A masa-a bangin suangpeek nih ~/leiseek ~ lim takin hal ni | let us make bricks and bake them thoroughly/Sikseekpa in ~ hol tawh na sem hi | the blacksmith forges and works with the coals/ka pumpi ~ hoihtakin ka ki-uk hi | I beat my body and keep it under control) (b:seek) (r:5.10.1/1.11.3/23.44.12/46.9.27) (q:draft)
seekna = (t:n) (w:shaping/working/making) (d:the work or the place of shaping stone, metal or clay; suangte seekna is cutting of stones, leiseek seekna is brickmaking) (e:bulh ding suangte ~ leh sing zep/leiseek ~-ah amaute na semsak hi | he made them work at brickmaking) (b:seek) (r:2.31.3/10.12.31) (q:draft)
seekpa = (t:n) (w:potter/maker/smith) (d:seek, shape or forge, with pa, which marks a man: the man who shapes something; beel seekpa is the potter, kham seekpa the goldsmith and ngun seekpa the silversmith) (e:Beel ~ in beel lei uk hilo/beel ~’ lei khawk khat a lei uh hi | they bought a potter's field/nang in beel ~ bang na hi hi | you are like the potter/kham ~ cial a | they hire a goldsmith) (s:sekpa) (b:seek) (r:45.9.21/23.46.6/40.27.7/23.64.8) (q:draft)
seeksa = (t:adj) (w:dressed/hewn/cut) (d:of stone, already shaped with tools; seek, shape by beating, with sa, already) (e:Suang ~ tawh inn bulpi) (b:seek) (r:11.5.17) (q:draft)
seeksak = (t:v) (w:forge for/have forged/make) (d:seek, forge or beat metal, with sak, causing or for someone: have a smith make something, or make it for someone) (e:teipi ahi zongin hong ~ kha ding hi/tua nate pen pasian-in ~ hi | he has those things made into a god) (b:seek) (r:9.13.19/23.46.6) (q:draft)
seeksate = (t:n) (w:dressed stones/hewn stones) (d:in suang seeksate, stones already cut to shape; seeksa with the plural te) (e:suang ~ a bawl dingin) (s:suangseeksate) (b:seeksa) (r:13.22.2) (q:draft)
seekte = (t:n) (w:smiths/craftsmen/makers) (d:seek, shape or forge, with the plural te: those who shape a material; kham seekte are goldsmiths, suang seekte stonecutters and beel seekte potters) (e:kham ~ khempeuh in a milim uh/suang ~ koih hi | he appointed stonecutters/beel ~ in beelte a suk khap zan bangin | as potters dash pots to pieces/Khutsiamte le kham ~ in milimin bawl uh a | craftsmen and goldsmiths make it into an idol) (s:sekte) (b:seek) (r:24.51.17/13.22.2/66.2.27/24.10.9) (q:draft)
seektheih = (t:v) (w:be able to shape/can mould) (d:seek, shape, with theih, can; here of a potter shaping clay) (e:a ututin ~ nading thu a nei hi) (b:seek) (r:45.9.21) (q:draft)
seel = (t:v) (w:hide/conceal/cover) (d:put or keep something out of sight or out of knowledge; mai seel is to hide the face and meel seel is to hide what one looks like) (e:Eufrates gun geiah ka ~ hi/Ka mawhna na mai panin ~ in la | hide your face from my sins/kei kiang panin na thupiaknate ~ kei in | do not hide your commands from me/mite’ theih loh dingin ama meel ~ hi | he hides his face so that people will not know him/na maitang ~ kei in la | do not hide your face) (s:im/iim/seelcip) (a:pholak/langsak) (r:24.13.5/6.2.6/19.51.9/19.119.19/18.24.15/19.69.17) (q:draft)
seelbawl = (t:v) (w:hide/keep hidden) (d:seel, hide, with bawl, do: keep something concealed) (e:Itna i ~ sangin) (s:seel) (b:seel) (r:20.27.5) (q:draft)
seelcip = (t:v) (w:hide/conceal/cover up/keep hidden) (d:seel, hide, with cip, tightly: hide completely so that it stays out of sight) (e:a topa’ sum a ~ hi/amau’ thuvaihawmna a ~ | who hide their plans/Mainul khat tawh tunin ka ~ hi | I kept it hidden, wrapped in a cloth/kha thum sung a ~ ngamna uh | their daring to hide him for three months/kei hong kibawlna ~ kei in | do not cover up what was done to me) (s:imcip/iimcip/seel) (a:pholak) (b:seel) (r:40.25.18/58.11.23/23.29.15/42.19.20/18.16.18) (q:draft)
seelcipsak = (t:v) (w:cover/hide away/keep hidden) (d:seelcip, hide completely, with sak, for or from someone: of sins, cover them; of a right, keep it from someone) (e:a khialhnate a ~ mite/Keima dikna hong ~ Pasian | God, who has kept my right from me) (s:khuhsak) (b:seelcip) (r:45.4.7/18.27.2) (q:draft)
seelcipzo = (t:v) (w:can hide/be able to conceal) (d:seelcip, hide completely, with zo, be able) (e:ka maizumna koi-ah ~ ding ka hi hiam/Gamtatsia mite a buk theih nadingun a ~ ding | that could hide evildoers looking for cover) (b:seelcip) (r:10.13.13/18.34.22) (q:draft)
seelin = (t:v) (w:hide/conceal) (d:seel with the linking ending in, hiding something and then doing the next action) (e:sawmnga-in leihawm sungah ~) (b:seel) (r:11.18.13) (q:draft)
seelin = (t:v) (w:disguise) (d:in meel seelin or mel seelin, hiding the face or appearance, being in disguise) (e:a meel ~ gal sungah kuan hi/Saul in a mel ~ puan dang silh a | Saul disguised himself and put on other clothes/Kei ka meel ~ gal sungah kong kuan ding a | I will go into the battle in disguise) (s:kiselin) (b:seel) (r:11.22.30/9.28.8) (q:draft)
seello = (t:v) (w:not hide) (d:seel, hide, with lo, not; mai seello is not to hide the face from someone) (e:Ama kiang pan a mai ~ a) (b:seel) (r:19.22.24) (q:draft)
seello = (t:v) (w:not argue/not dispute) (d:seel, dispute or speak against, with lo not, said with thu word) (e:phattuamna om lo dingpi-in thu ~ uh hi) (r:18.15.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
seelloin = (t:v) (w:not talking back/without contradicting) (d:in thu seelloin: seel, here speak against, with lo, not, and the linking suffix in) (e:a tote uh thu ~) (r:56.2.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
seelna = (t:n) (w:hiding/covering/concealment) (d:the act or place of hiding; seelna mun is a hiding place, and mawhna seelna is the covering of sin) (e:a mawhna uh ~ a ngah mite/dialkaih ka ~ mun | the place where I had hidden the belt/Nuihna in cihmawh ~ zong hi thei a | laughter may also be a cover for sorrow) (b:seel) (r:45.4.7/24.13.7/20.14.13) (q:draft)
seelna = (t:n) (w:argument/dispute/case) (d:arguing against someone, apparently from another verb seel meaning dispute) (e:Na hong ~ ding limtakin kiging in/Thu kihai ~, thei lo pi-a thu kinialnate na pelh in | avoid foolish arguments and ignorant disputes) (s:kinialna/kiselna) (r:18.33.5/55.2.23) (q:draft, low confidence)
