semsemin = (t:adv) (w:more and more/increasingly) (d:semsem, more and more, with the linking suffix in) (e:David thahat ~, Saul’ innkuan thanem semsem hi/Note’ lungsimah itna khang ~ | that love may grow more and more in your hearts/a natna nasia mahmah ahih manin gim ~ | his illness was so severe that he grew worse and worse/Mi ciimsate ciimsak ~ | making the wise wiser still) (b:semsem) (r:10.3.1/11.17.17/50.1.9/20.1.5) (q:draft)
semsemna = (t:n) (w:increase/growing more) (d:the fact of being or becoming more and more so, after a descriptive word: pil semsemna growing wiser, gamlum semsemna ever-rising uproar) (e:gamlum ~ mangngilh kei ta in/pil ~-in nei ding a | he will become wiser still/amah muhdah ~-in nei uh hi | they hated him all the more/a san’ ~ tawh kizui-in | because of its growing height) (b:semsem) (r:19.74.23/20.9.9/1.37.5/26.31.10) (q:draft)
semsemzaw = (t:adv) (w:more and more/all the more) (d:semsem with zaw, more, placed after a verb or descriptive word) (e:noptuamzaw loin gim ~ hi/khatlekhat kihanthawn ~ ni | let us encourage one another all the more) (b:semsem) (r:41.5.26/58.10.25) (q:draft)
semsuak = (t:v) (w:keep on working/work right through) (d:sem, work, with suak, through: work on without stopping) (e:tu dong ~ hi) (r:8.2.7) (q:draft)
semtawm = (t:v) (w:take on oneself/do on one's own) (d:sem, do, with tawm, by oneself: take up a task or office of one's own accord) (e:nasep a ~ mawk hi loin) (r:58.5.5) (q:draft)
semte = (t:n) (w:those who work/those who serve/workers/doers) (d:sem, work or serve, with the plural te: the people who do the work or service named before it) (e:na a ~ leh patpuan a gante/Na a hoih a ~ | those who do good work/kumpipa’ na a ~ ahi hi | they were the ones who served the king/Ka na hong ~ in ka nung hong zui | those who serve me follow me) (b:sem) (r:23.19.9/43.12.26/20.14.22/14.17.19) (q:draft)
semthei = (t:v) (w:can work/be able to serve/can do) (d:sem, work or serve, with thei, can) (e:Pawlpi upa hoihtakin a ~ mite pen/na a manpha tampi ~ ding ka hih manin | because I will be able to do much fruitful work) (b:sem) (r:54.3.13/50.1.22) (q:draft)
semzaw = (t:v) (w:serve instead/do rather/serve more) (d:sem, work, serve or do, with zaw, rather or more: do or serve in preference to something else, or to a greater degree) (e:na zak bangun zui-in ~ un/Jehu in tampi ~ ding hi | Jehu will serve him much more/Babylon kumpipa’ na na ~ un | serve the king of Babylon instead) (b:sem) (r:59.1.22/24.27.17/12.10.18) (q:draft)
semzo = (t:v) (w:be able to do/accomplish/be able to serve) (d:sem, work or do, with zo, be able) (e:na lianpi ~ hi/Topa’ na na ~ kei ding uh hi | you are not able to serve the Lord/a hoih thu khempeuh genin a ~ dingin | to be able to say and do every good thing) (b:sem) (r:59.5.16/6.24.19/53.2.17) (q:draft)
sen = (t:see) <sen'na>
sen'na = (t:n) (d:in lupna sen’na inndei, bedroom or bedchamber; spelling of senna, apparently a place where something is laid or kept) (e:lupna ~ inndei sungah) (r:12.11.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
Sena = (t:see) <Sena-ah>
Sena-ah = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Senaah) (d:spelling of Senaah with a hyphen: town whose people returned from the exile in Babylon with Zerubbabel) (r:16.7.38/15.2.35) (q:draft)
Senaah = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Senaah) (d:town whose people returned from the exile in Babylon with Zerubbabel) (r:15.2.35/16.7.38)
Seneh = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Seneh) (d:one of the two cliffs at the pass of Mikmash, opposite the cliff Bozez, where Jonathan crossed to the Philistine outpost) (r:9.14.4)
seng = (t:v) (w:store/put away/stow) (d:put goods into a place for keeping) (e:ka neih khempeuh ka ~ ding hi/Mikmas khua-ah a van uh hong ~ uh hi | they store their supplies at Mikmash/um-le-beelte khempeuh a ~ hi | he stored all the vessels) (s:khol) (r:42.12.18/14.5.1/23.10.28) (q:draft)
sengsang = (t:adv) (d:descriptive word after kang white: stark or bare white, said of branches stripped of their bark) (e:a hiangte kang ~ hi) (r:29.1.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
Senir = (t:name) (c:mountain) (w:Senir) (d:Amorite name for Mount Hermon) (r:5.3.9/13.5.23)
senna = (t:n) (d:in lupna senna inndei, bedroom or bedchamber; apparently a place where something is laid or kept) (e:lupna ~ inndei sungah) (r:14.22.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
Sennakherib = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Sennacherib) (d:king of Assyria who invaded Judah in the time of King Hezekiah and then returned to Nineveh) (r:12.18.13/14.32.2)
sensen = (t:adv) (w:distinctly/clearly apart) (d:after ging, sound: sounding each one distinct from the other) (e:a aw a kitelin ging ~ kei leh) (r:46.14.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
Seorim = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Seorim) (d:priest, head of the fourth of the priestly divisions set up in the time of David) (r:13.24.8)
sep = (t:v) (w:work/serve/do) (d:form of sem, work, serve or do, used before ciangin, khit, ding, nading and theih, and as a noun in ama sep, his work) (e:Amaute in biakbuk ah a ~ uh ciangin/Ka ~ dinga nong piak na khempeuh | all the work you gave me to do/siampi na a ~ theih nadingin | so that he may serve as priest/nangma khut in a ~ ahihna | that your hand has done it/na a ~ khit ciangin si a | after he had done his work he died) (r:4.3.7/2.40.13/43.17.4/19.109.27/44.13.36) (q:draft)
sepbel = (t:v) (w:serve/be a servant of) (d:sep, work or serve, with bel: said by Paul of the gospel that he teaches and serves; the exact force of bel is not clear) (e:Paul in hilhin ka ~ hi a) (r:51.1.23) (q:draft, low confidence)
sepkhak = (t:v) (w:happen to do/come to do) (d:sep, do, with khak, by chance or wrongly; with loh nading, so as not to end up doing) (e:na ~ loh nadingun na kingaihsun un) (s:hihkhak) (r:40.6.1) (q:draft, low confidence)
sepkhawm = (t:v) (w:work together/serve together) (d:sep, work, with khawm, together: the form of semkhawm used before mah bangin, just as) (e:a pa tawh na a ~ mah bangin) (b:sep) (r:50.2.22) (q:draft)
sepkhiat = (t:v) (w:carry out/execute/perform/maintain) (d:sep, work, with khiat, out: put into practice, bring a command, justice or a judgment into effect; the form of semkhia used before ding, nading, theih and laitakin) (e:thutang leh thuman na ~ theih nadingin/kumpipa’ thupiakna bangin ~ nading hun | the time to carry out the command of the king/Pasian’ thukhenna a ~ laitakin | while he was carrying out the judgment of God/ka khennate ka ~ theih nadingin | so that I may carry out my judgments) (b:sep) (r:11.10.9/17.9.1/14.22.8/26.39.21) (q:draft)
sepkhiatna = (t:n) (w:carrying out/execution) (d:sepkhiat, carry out, with the noun suffix na) (e:kumpipa’ thupiakna bangin ~ ding hun) (b:sepkhiat) (r:17.9.1) (q:draft)
sepkhit = (t:v) (w:finish doing/have done) (d:sep, do, with khit, finish; sepkhit ciangin is when it has been done) (e:hong kisawlteng na ~ uh ciangin) (s:bawlkhit) (r:42.17.10) (q:draft)
sepkhoppih = (t:v) (w:work together with/be a fellow worker of) (d:sep, work, with khop, together, and pih, with; na ka sepkhoppih is my fellow worker) (e:Khrih Jesuh sungah na ka ~ Prisilla le Aquila/Khrih nasepna sungah na ka ~ uh ahi Urbanas | Urbanus, our fellow worker in the work of Christ) (s:seppih) (r:45.16.3/45.16.9) (q:draft)
sepkik = (t:v) (w:serve again/work again) (d:sep, work or serve, with kik, again) (e:biakinn sungah na a ~ theih nadingun) (b:sep) (r:26.44.27) (q:draft)
seploh = (t:v) (w:not worked/not toiled on) (d:sep, work, with loh, not: describes a thing that one did not work for) (e:Note in na ~ uh leitang) (r:6.24.13) (q:draft)
sepna = (t:n) (w:work/labour/toil/deed) (d:sep, work, with the noun suffix na: the work someone does, hard labour, or a deed that has been done) (e:a ~ khempeuh thamanin bang ngah/nakpi takin ka na ~ ka kisik hi | I despaired greatly over my labour/nangma ~ a liante ka ngaihsunsun ding hi | I will meditate on your mighty deeds/amau ~ tawh amaute a nin suak uh a | they became unclean by what they did) (s:nasepna/nasep) (b:sep) (r:21.3.9/21.4.9/21.2.20/19.77.12/19.106.39) (q:draft)
sepnate = (t:n) (w:deeds/works/acts) (d:plural of sepna: the things someone has done, in the Psalms mostly the mighty works of God) (e:na ~ bangzah takin lian/na ~ thupi mahmah hi | your deeds are mighty/A vanglian ama ~ hangin amah phat un | praise him for his mighty acts/nangma ~ ka lungngaingai ding hi | I will meditate on your works) (s:nasepnate/septe/sepsate) (b:sepna) (r:19.92.5/19.150.2/24.32.19/19.145.5) (q:draft)
sepnop = (t:v) (w:want to do/be willing to do/wish to serve) (d:form of semnuam, want to do, work or serve, used before kei, nading and in relative clauses) (e:ka ~ khempeuh ka sem ding hi/tanaute’ sep ding a ~ kei leh | if he is not willing to do the duty of a kinsman/Topa’ na na ~ kei uhleh | if you do not want to serve the Lord/ama deihna bangin na ~ nading uh | so that you are willing to act as he wishes) (s:hihnop/gamtatnop) (r:23.46.10/6.24.15/8.3.13/50.2.13) (q:draft)
sepnopna = (t:n) (w:desire to do/willingness to act) (d:sepnop, want to do, with the noun suffix na) (e:na a manin ~ lungsim nei) (s:bawlnopna/gamtatnopna) (b:sepnop) (r:58.13.18) (q:draft)
seppih = (t:v) (w:work with/work together with/help) (d:sep, work, with pih, together with: do a work alongside someone or help him in it) (e:nasemte in nangma nasemte ~ ding uh a/kuama ~ lohin leitung ka zal hi | I spread out the earth with no one working with me/Topa in zong amaute’ nasep ~ a | the Lord also worked with them/midang kuamah in hong ~ thei lo ding hi | no one else may work with you) (s:sepkhoppih) (b:sep) (r:11.5.6/23.44.24/41.16.20/4.18.4) (q:draft)
seppihna = (t:n) (w:working with/work done with) (d:seppih, work with, and the noun suffix na; Pasian in na a seppihna is what God did together with them) (e:Pasian in na a ~ thu/Pasian in na a ~ khempeuh | all that God had done with them) (b:seppih) (r:44.15.4/44.14.27) (q:draft)
seppihte = (t:n) (w:helpers/those who work with) (d:seppih work with and te: those who join someone in a work) (e:mawhna nasep a ~ daan a pia hi) (s:huhte) (b:seppih) (r:23.31.2) (q:draft)
sepsa = (t:n) (w:work/deed/thing done) (d:sep, work, with sa, already: what has been done, a work that is finished; often of the works of God) (e:Na khut tawh na ~ thaman/nangma ~ bangzah takin tam | how many are your works/nangma ~ thute ka za a | I have heard of your deeds/na khut in a ~ nate ka lungngaingai hi | I consider what your hands have done) (s:sepna/nasepna) (b:sep) (r:19.128.2/19.22.31/19.104.24/35.3.2/19.143.5) (q:draft)
sepsak = (t:v) (w:serve/work for) (d:sep, work, with sak, for someone: na sepsak is serve a master, a nation or a god) (e:kei in a na ka ~ Pasian’ vantungmi/na a ~ uh minam’ tungah | on the nation that they serve/pasian dang peuh bia-in a na a ~ man uh | because they worshipped and served other gods/a na na ~ ding peuhpeuh uh tuni-in teel un | choose today whom you will serve) (s:nasem) (b:sep) (r:44.27.23/24.22.9/1.15.14/6.24.15) (q:draft)
sepsak = (t:v) (w:make work/drive to work) (d:sep, work, with the causative sak: cause someone to work, drive him to work) (e:gilkialna in nak ~ semsem zaw hi) (s:nasemsak) (b:sep) (r:20.16.26) (q:draft, low confidence)
sepsakna = (t:n) (w:work done for/deed done for) (d:sepsak, do for someone, with the noun suffix na: what one has done on behalf of another) (e:nangma hong ~ hang ahi hi/ama a dingin Jesuh’ ~ thu khempeuh | all that Jesus had done for him) (b:sepsak) (r:23.26.12/42.8.39) (q:draft)
sepsaksa = (t:v) (w:served/worked for) (d:sepsak work for someone with sa marking a completed action) (e:nangma na kong ~ na thei hi) (b:sepsak) (r:1.30.26) (q:draft)
sepsan = (t:v) (w:be doing/carry on doing) (d:sep, work, with san; a sepsan laitak is while they are doing it; exact force of san not clear) (e:amaute in a ~ laitak uh ahi hi) (b:sep) (r:14.34.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
sepsate = (t:n) (w:works/deeds/things done) (d:plural of sepsa: the things someone has done, most often the works of God) (e:Mi khempeuh in Pasian’ ~ mu uh a/nangma ~ khempeuh ka ngaihsunsun hi | I meditate on all your works/Hong pai un la Pasian’ ~ mu un | come and see what God has done/Na khut tawh na ~ simmawh bawlin | despising the works of your hands) (s:sepnate/septe/nasepnate) (b:sepsa) (r:18.36.25/19.66.5/19.143.5/18.10.3) (q:draft)
sepsateng = (t:n) (w:all the work done/all the labour) (d:sepsa, work done, with teng, all of) (e:amau’ ~ khempeuh a khu-in leengmang hi) (b:sepsa) (r:35.2.13) (q:draft)
sepsawm = (t:v) (w:purpose to do/intend to do) (d:sep, do, with sawm, intend) (e:Khazih hanga a ~ a sehsa thuthuk) (r:49.1.9) (q:draft)
sepsepte = (t:n) (w:services/regular duties) (d:sep, work, doubled for what is done again and again, with the plural te: the things the priests keep doing) (e:Leitung a siampite’ ~ pen) (r:58.8.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
septe = (t:n) (w:deeds/works/acts) (d:sep, do, with the plural te: things done, deeds; a lamdang ama septe is his wonderful deeds) (e:a lamdang ama ~ mu uh hi/ama nalamdang ~, mi khempeuh lakah pulak un | proclaim his marvelous deeds among all peoples/a lamdang ama ~ khempeuh gen un | tell of all his wonderful acts/Ka Pa’ thu tawh na ka ~ | the works I do in the name of my Father) (s:sepnate/sepsate/nasepnate) (b:sep) (r:19.107.24/19.96.3/13.16.9/43.10.25) (q:draft)
septeng = (t:n) (w:all that one does/everything done) (d:sep, do, with teng, all: all the things that someone does) (e:Pa in a ~ mah a Tapa in/ama ~ mah lak a | he shows him all that he does) (b:sep) (r:43.5.19/43.5.20) (q:draft)
septheih = (t:v) (w:be able to do/be able to work) (d:sep, work or do, with theih, be able, used before nading: so that one can do or carry out) (e:na hoih na phate a ~ nadingun/na hoih namkim a ~ nadingun | so that they can do every kind of good work/limtakin na ~ nading lam tampi tak a om hi | there is a great opening for working well/Topa’ na na ~ nading uh | so that you can do the work of the Lord) (s:sepzawh/hihtheih) (b:sep) (r:56.3.14/55.3.16/46.16.9/46.7.35) (q:draft)
sepzaw = (t:v) (w:work more/work harder) (d:sep, work, with the comparative zaw) (e:Amaute sangin na ka nak ~ a) (b:sep) (r:47.11.23) (q:draft)
sepzawh = (t:v) (w:be able to do/accomplish) (d:sep, work or do, with zawh, the form of zo, be able, used before nading: have the strength or skill to do a work) (e:~ nading siamna pen Pasian hong piak/Hih bangin na ~ nadingin thatang hatna | strength to be able to do this work/Hih bang ~ nadingin kote in siamna nei ung | we have the skill to do such things) (s:septheih/hihzawh) (r:47.3.5/54.1.12) (q:draft)
sepzawhna = (t:n) (w:accomplishment/work done/deed) (d:sepzawh, be able to do, with the noun suffix na: what one has managed to do) (e:Eite’ ~ hang hi loin/Tua ka ~ pen keima hatna hang hi loin | what I achieved was not by my own strength/Eite in na hoih i ~ hangin | because of the good things we had done) (b:sepzawh) (r:55.1.9/46.15.10/56.3.5) (q:draft)
sepzia = (t:n) (w:way of working/manner of work) (d:sep, work, with zia, manner) (e:Kote in zong amau’ ~ mah bangin) (r:47.11.12) (q:draft)
serafim = (t:n) (w:seraphim/seraph) (d:heavenly beings with six wings seen by Isaiah; in the text followed by vanmite, heavenly beings) (e:Ama tungah ~ vanmite ding uh hi/Tua ciangin ~ vanmite khat | then one of the seraphim) (r:23.6.2/23.6.6) (q:draft)
