Seraiah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Seraiah) (d:name of several men, among them the secretary of David and the chief priest when Jerusalem fell to Babylon, father of Jehozadak) (r:13.6.14/10.8.17)
Sered = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Sered) (d:son of Zebulun, ancestor of the Seredite clan) (r:1.46.14/4.26.26)
Sergius = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Sergius) (d:Sergius Paulus, the Roman proconsul of Cyprus who sent for Barnabas and Saul to hear the word of God) (r:44.13.7)
Serug = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Serug) (d:son of Reu and father of Nahor, an ancestor of Abraham) (r:1.11.22)
sese = (t:adv) (w:ever/at all) (d:adds force to a question with bang hangin, why: why ever, why of all things; with loin, without any at all) (e:mi khem hatte gualzo ~ ahi hiam/a gil sung panin suak khia ~ ka hi hiam | did I ever come out of the womb/Kampau kul ~ loin | without any need of words) (r:24.12.1/24.20.18/60.3.1) (q:draft, low confidence)
sesing = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:cypress/broom tree) (d:a kind of tree; the verses use it for the cypress of Isaiah 44:14 and for the broom bush whose wood makes hot coals in Psalm 120:4) (e:~ kung khat ahi a/Galhangpa’ thaltang hiamte leh ~ hol am | the sharp arrows of a warrior and burning coals of the broom tree) (r:23.44.14/19.120.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
Seth = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Seth) (d:third son of Adam and Eve, father of Enosh) (r:1.5.6)
Sethur = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Sethur) (d:son of Michael, the man from the tribe of Asher sent to explore Canaan) (r:4.13.13)
sette = (t:n) (w:machines/engines/devices) (d:plural of set, machine, here war machines for shooting arrows and hurling stones) (e:mi a siamte in a bawltawm ~) (r:14.26.15) (q:draft)
seu = (t:n) (w:ephah) (d:a dry measure for grain and flour, used for the Hebrew ephah; tenths of it are counted with sehsawm suah) (e:annel ~ khat sehsawm suah sehthum/mangbuhham ~ khat bang pha hi | it came to about an ephah of barley/Lawhta khat in ~ khat seh-sawm-suah-seh-khat ahi hi | an omer is one tenth of an ephah) (r:4.15.9/28.3.2/8.2.17/2.16.36) (q:draft)
seuhseuh = (t:adv) (d:describes a quick repeated movement: of wine, bubbling up in the cup; of arrows, being shaken to and fro) (e:Hai sungah a phuan ~/a thaltangte sing ~-in | shaking his arrows to and fro) (r:20.23.31/26.21.21) (q:draft, low confidence)
seuhseuhin = (t:adv) (d:seuhseuh with the suffix in: with a quick shaking movement, here of arrows shaken to cast lots) (e:a thaltangte sing ~) (b:seuhseuh) (r:26.21.21) (q:draft, low confidence)
Sha = (t:see) <Sha-araim>
Sha-af = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shaaph) (d:name of two men in the family of Caleb: a son of Jahdai, and a son of Caleb by his concubine Maakah, the father of Madmannah) (r:13.2.47/13.2.49) (q:draft)
Sha-alabbin = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Shaalabbin) (d:town in the territory of the tribe of Dan, also called Shaalbim) (e:~, Aiialon, Ithlah) (r:6.19.42) (q:draft)
Sha-albim = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Shaalbim) (d:town in the territory of Dan where the Amorites held out against Israel) (r:7.1.35) (q:draft)
Sha-albon = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Shaalbon) (d:home town of Eliahba, one of the mighty warriors of David; Sha-albon khuami is a man of Shaalbon, the Shaalbonite) (r:13.11.33/10.23.32) (q:draft)
Sha-alim = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Shaalim) (d:district through which Saul passed when he searched for the lost donkeys of his father) (e:amaute in ~ gam teng zong uh a) (r:9.9.4) (q:draft)
Sha-araim = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Shaaraim) (d:town in the western foothills of Judah; the Philistines fled along the road from it to Gath and Ekron after Goliath was killed) (r:6.15.36/9.17.52) (q:draft)
Sha-ariam = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Shaaraim) (d:town of the tribe of Simeon; the text spells the name Sha-ariam) (r:13.4.31) (q:draft)
Sha-ashgaz = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shaashgaz) (d:eunuch of King Xerxes who had charge of the concubines) (e:kumpipa’ innsung mang ~ in kem hi) (r:17.2.14) (q:draft)
Shaaf = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shaaph) (d:name of two men in the family of Caleb: a son of Jahdai, and a son of Caleb by his concubine Maakah, the father of Madmannah) (r:13.2.47/13.2.49)
Shaalbim = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Shaalbim) (d:town in the territory of Dan where the Amorites held out against Israel, later in one of the districts of Solomon) (r:11.4.9)
Shaalbon = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Shaalbon) (d:home town of Eliahba, one of the mighty warriors of David) (r:10.23.32/13.11.33)
Shaalim = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Shaalim) (d:district through which Saul passed when he searched for the lost donkeys of his father) (r:9.9.4)
Shaaraim = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Shaaraim) (d:name of two towns, one in the western foothills of Judah and one of the tribe of Simeon) (r:6.15.36/13.4.31)
Shaarim = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Shaaraim) (d:spelling of Shaaraim, the town in Judah from which the Philistines fled to Gath and Ekron after Goliath was killed) (r:9.17.52)
Shaashgaz = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shaashgaz) (d:eunuch of King Xerxes who had charge of the concubines) (r:17.2.14)
Shabbethai = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shabbethai) (d:Levite in the time of Ezra and Nehemiah who helped explain the Law and had charge of the outside work of the house of God) (r:15.10.15/16.11.16)
Shadrak = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shadrach) (d:Babylonian name of Hananiah, one of the three friends of Daniel who were thrown into the blazing furnace) (r:27.3.30/27.3.16)
Shafam = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shapham) (d:a chief of the tribe of Gad in Bashan, second after Joel) (r:13.5.12)
Shafan = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shaphan) (d:secretary of King Josiah, son of Azaliah, who read the Book of the Law to the king; father of Ahikam and Gemariah) (r:24.26.24/12.22.3)
Shafat = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shaphat) (d:name of several men, among them the son of Hori sent from the tribe of Simeon to explore Canaan and the father of the prophet Elisha) (r:4.13.5)
Shafir = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Shaphir) (d:town named in the prophecy of Micah) (r:33.1.11)
Shagee = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shagee) (d:the Hararite, father of Jonathan, one of the mighty warriors of David) (r:13.11.34)
shah = (t:see) <Hada-shah>
shahar = (t:see) <Zereth-shahar>
Shaharaim = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shaharaim) (d:man of the tribe of Benjamin who had sons in Moab after he divorced his wives Hushim and Baara) (r:13.8.8)
Shahazumah = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Shahazumah) (d:town on the border of the territory of Issachar) (r:6.19.22)
Shalisha = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Shalisha) (d:district near the hill country of Ephraim through which Saul passed when he searched for the lost donkeys) (r:9.9.4)
Shallekheth = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Shalleketh) (d:gate on the west side of the temple in Jerusalem, on the upper road) (r:13.26.16)
Shallum = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shallum) (d:name of many men, among them the son of Jabesh who was king of Israel for one month and a high priest, son of Zadok) (r:13.6.12/12.15.14)
Shalma = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Salma) (d:descendant of Caleb, called the father of Bethlehem; the NIV spells the name Salma) (e:Bethlehem khuapi a sat ~) (r:13.2.51) (q:draft)
Shalmai = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shalmai) (d:ancestor of a family of temple servants who returned from the exile) (r:16.7.48)
Shalman = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shalman) (d:king who destroyed Beth Arbel in battle, named by the prophet Hosea) (r:28.10.14) (q:draft)
Shalmaneser = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shalmaneser) (d:king of Assyria who attacked King Hoshea of Israel and besieged Samaria) (r:12.17.3/12.18.9)
Shalum = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shallum) (d:spelling of Shallum, the name of many men, among them the father of Jehizkiah of Ephraim and a high priest, son of Zadok) (r:14.28.12/13.6.12)
Shama = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shama) (d:son of Hotham the Aroerite, one of the mighty warriors of David) (r:13.11.44) (q:draft)
Shamah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shammah) (d:son of Reuel and grandson of Esau, a chief of Edom) (r:1.36.17)
Shamai = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shamai/Shalmai) (d:ancestor of a family of temple servants who returned from the exile; the NIV spells the name Shalmai) (r:16.7.48)
Shamaneser = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shalmaneser) (d:spelling of Shalmaneser, the king of Assyria who attacked King Hoshea of Israel) (r:12.17.3)
Shamgar = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shamgar) (d:son of Anath, a judge of Israel who killed six hundred Philistines with an oxgoad) (r:7.3.31/7.5.6)
Shamhuth = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shamhuth) (d:the Izrahite, commander of the army division for the fifth month under David) (r:13.27.8)
Shamir = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Shamir) (d:name of a town in the hill country of Judah, of the town in Ephraim where the judge Tola was buried, and of a Levite, son of Micah) (r:6.15.48)
Shamlai = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shamlai/Shalmai) (d:ancestor of a family of temple servants who returned from the exile; the NIV spells the name Shalmai) (r:15.2.46)
Shamma = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shamma) (d:son of Zophah in the tribe of Asher) (r:13.7.37) (q:draft)
Shammah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shammah) (d:name of several men, among them a son of Reuel and grandson of Esau, and some of the mighty warriors of David) (r:13.1.37/10.23.25)
Shammai = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shammai) (d:name of several men in the tribe of Judah, among them a son of Onam and a son of Rekem) (r:13.2.28/13.2.44)
Shammoth = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shammoth) (d:the Harorite, one of the mighty warriors of David) (r:13.11.27)
Shammua = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shammua) (d:name of several men, among them the son of Zakkur sent from the tribe of Reuben to explore Canaan and a son of David born in Jerusalem) (r:4.13.4/13.14.4)
Shamsherai = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shamsherai) (d:son of Jeroham in the tribe of Benjamin) (r:13.8.26)
Shamua = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shammua) (d:son of Zakkur, the man from the tribe of Reuben sent to explore Canaan; the NIV spells the name Shammua) (r:4.13.4)
shar = (t:see) <Ja-shar>
Sharai = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Sharai) (d:one of the men who had married a foreign wife in the time of Ezra) (r:15.10.40)
Sharar = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Sharar) (d:a Hararite, father of Ahiam, one of the mighty warriors of David) (r:10.23.33)
Sharezer = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Sharezer) (d:son of Sennacherib king of Assyria who with his brother Adrammelek killed his father; also a man sent from Bethel to ask the priests about fasting) (r:12.19.37/23.37.38)
Sharom = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Sharon) (d:spelling of Sharon, the plain where the herds of King David grazed) (r:13.27.29)
Sharon = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Sharon) (d:fertile coastal plain and pasture land in Israel, known for its flowers and its herds; Sharon gam is the land of Sharon) (e:~ gam sunga om gamlak paak) (r:22.2.1/23.65.10) (q:draft)
Sharuhen = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Sharuhen) (d:town in the south of Judah given to the tribe of Simeon) (r:6.19.6)
Shashai = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shashai) (d:one of the men who had married a foreign wife in the time of Ezra) (r:15.10.40)
Shashak = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shashak) (d:a Benjamite, son of Beriah, whose sons were heads of families) (r:13.8.14/13.8.25)
Shaul = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shaul) (d:name of several men, among them a king of Edom from Rehoboth on the river and a son of Simeon) (r:1.36.37/1.36.38)
Shaveh = (t:name) (c:valley) (w:Shaveh) (d:valley near Salem, also called the Valley of the King, where the king of Sodom met Abram; in the text Shaveh Kuam, the Valley of Shaveh) (r:1.14.17) (q:draft)
Shavehkiriathaim = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Shaveh-kiriathaim/Shaveh Kiriathaim) (d:place east of the Jordan where Kedorlaomer defeated the Emites) (r:1.14.5)
Shavehkiriathain = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Shaveh Kiriathaim) (d:spelling of Shaveh Kiriathaim, the place east of the Jordan where Kedorlaomer defeated the Emites) (r:1.14.5)
Shavsha = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shavsha) (d:secretary of King David) (r:13.18.16)
Shawl = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shaul) (d:spelling of Shaul: a son of Simeon, ancestor of the Shaulite clan, and a king of Edom) (r:1.46.10/13.4.25)
She = (t:see) <She-erah>
She-erah = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Sheerah) (d:woman of the tribe of Ephraim who built Lower and Upper Beth Horon and Uzzen Sheerah) (e:Ama tanu in ~ hi a) (r:13.7.24) (q:draft)
Sheal = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Sheal) (d:descendant of Bani who had married a foreign wife in the time of Ezra) (r:15.10.29) (q:draft)
Shealtiel = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shealtiel) (d:son of King Jehoiachin, also called Jeconiah, and father of Zerubbabel, in the family line of Jesus) (r:13.3.17/40.1.12)
Sheariah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Sheariah) (d:one of the six sons of Azel, a Benjamite descendant of King Saul) (r:13.8.38/13.9.44)
