Shefatiah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shephatiah) (d:name of several men, among them a son of David and Abital born in Hebron and a son of King Jehoshaphat) (r:10.3.4/14.21.2)
Shefelab = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Shefelab/western foothills) (d:spelling of Shefelah, the western foothills of Judah, where olive and sycamore-fig trees grew) (r:13.27.28)
Shefelah = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Shefelah/foothills) (d:the low hill country between the coastal plain and the hills of Judah, known for its many sycamore-fig trees) (r:14.28.18/11.10.27)
Shefer = (t:name) (c:mountain) (w:Shepher) (d:mountain where the Israelites camped in the wilderness, between Kehelathah and Haradah) (r:4.33.23/4.33.24)
Shefi = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shepho) (d:son of Shobal, a descendant of Seir the Horite; spelled Shefo in Genesis) (r:13.1.40)
