Shehariah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shehariah) (d:a Benjamite, son of Jeroham, head of a family living in Jerusalem) (r:13.8.26)
Sheir = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Seir) (d:spelling of Seir, the hill country of Edom, in the prophecy of Balaam) (r:4.24.18)
Shekaiah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shekaniah) (d:spelling of Shekaniah, the priest to whom the tenth lot fell in the time of David) (r:13.24.11)
Shekaniah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shecaniah/Shekaniah) (d:name of several men, among them a priest who returned from exile with Zerubbabel and a descendant of David) (r:13.3.21/16.12.3)
Shekaniahte = (t:name) (w:Shekaniah) (d:the name Shekaniah with the plural te, Shekaniah and those named with him: a priest who helped distribute the offerings in the time of Hezekiah) (b:Shekaniah) (r:14.31.15)
shekel = (t:n) (w:shekel) (d:unit of weight of about eleven grams, used for weighing silver and gold and so also a unit of money; ngun shekel is a shekel of silver and biakinn shekel is the sanctuary shekel) (e:~ sawm a gik kham pakan khat/ngun ~ zali man hi | it is worth four hundred shekels of silver/ngun ~ sawmnih-in amah zuak uh hi | they sold him for twenty shekels of silver/ngun ~ sawmthum pia ding a | he shall pay thirty shekels of silver) (r:4.7.14/9.17.5/1.23.15/1.37.28/2.21.32) (q:draft)
Shekhem = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shechem) (d:son of Hamor the Hivite, who wanted to marry Dinah daughter of Jacob; also a descendant of Manasseh, son of Shemida) (r:1.34.6)
Shelah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shelah) (d:son of Arphaxad and father of Eber, a descendant of Shem; also the third son of Judah) (r:13.1.18)
Shelef = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Sheleph) (d:son of Joktan, a descendant of Shem) (r:1.10.26)
Shelemiah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shelemiah) (d:name of several men, among them the father of Jehukal, a Levite gatekeeper of the East Gate, and men who had married foreign wives in the time of Ezra) (e:~’ tapa Jehukal) (r:24.38.1/13.26.14) (q:draft)
Shelesh = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shelesh) (d:a descendant of Asher, one of four brothers named in the family list of the tribe) (r:13.7.35)
sheli = (t:see) <Eglath-sheli-shiah>
shelishiah = (t:see) <Eglath-shelishiah>
