Shema = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Shema) (d:town in the south of Judah; also the name of several men, among them a son of Hebron and a Benjamite family head of Aijalon) (r:6.15.26)
Shemaah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shemaah) (d:a man of Gibeah, father of Ahiezer and Joash, warriors who joined David) (r:13.12.3)
Shemai = (t:see) <Shemai-ah>
Shemai-ah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shemaiah) (d:Shemaiah the Nehelamite, a false prophet among the exiles in Babylon in the time of Jeremiah) (e:Nehelam khuami ~ leh a suan a khakte) (r:24.29.32/24.29.31) (q:draft)
Shemaiah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shemaiah) (d:name of many men, among them a son of Joel of the tribe of Reuben and priests and Levites after the exile) (r:16.12.6/16.12.34)
Shemakhiah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Semakiah) (d:a Levite gatekeeper, an able man of the family of Obed-Edom) (r:13.26.7)
Shemariah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shemariah) (d:name of several men, among them a son of King Rehoboam and men who had married foreign wives in the time of Ezra) (r:15.10.41/15.10.32)
Shemeber = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Shemeber) (d:king of Zeboyim, one of the five kings attacked by Kedorlaomer and his allies in the time of Abram) (r:1.14.2)
Shemed = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shemed) (d:a Benjamite, son of Elpaal, who built Ono and Lod) (r:13.8.12)
Shemer = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shemer) (d:owner of the hill of Samaria, which King Omri bought and named after him; also a Levite ancestor in the family of Merari) (r:11.16.24/13.6.46)
Shemiah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shemaiah) (d:spelling of Shemaiah, the father of Delaiah, an official of King Jehoiakim) (r:24.36.12)
Shemida = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shemida) (d:descendant of Manasseh, ancestor of the Shemidaite clan) (r:13.7.19/4.26.32)
Shemirahmoth = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shemiramoth) (d:spelling of Shemiramoth, a Levite sent by King Jehoshaphat to teach in the towns of Judah) (r:14.17.8)
Shemiramoth = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shemiramoth) (d:Levite musician who played the lyre when David brought the ark to Jerusalem) (r:13.15.20/13.15.18)
Shemuel = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shemuel) (d:son of Ammihud, the leader of the tribe of Simeon who helped divide the land of Canaan; also a son of Tola of the tribe of Issachar) (r:4.34.20/13.7.2)
Shenazzar = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shenazzar) (d:son of King Jehoiachin, also called Jeconiah) (r:13.3.18)
Sheol = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Sheol/realm of the dead) (d:the realm of the dead, the grave; in the text Sihna gam Sheol, Sheol the land of death) (r:32.2.2)
Sheraiah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Sheariah) (d:spelling of Sheariah, one of the six sons of Azel, a Benjamite) (r:13.9.44)
Sherebiah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Sherebiah) (d:name of Levites, among them a leader who came with Ezra and one who sealed the covenant in the time of Nehemiah) (r:15.8.24/16.10.12)
Sheresh = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Sheresh) (d:son of Makir and Maakah, grandson of Manasseh) (r:13.7.16)
Sheshai = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Sheshai) (d:one of the three descendants of Anak living in Hebron, driven out by Caleb) (r:6.15.14)
Sheshan = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Sheshan) (d:descendant of Jerahmeel of Judah who had no sons and gave his daughter in marriage to his Egyptian servant Jarha) (r:13.2.31/13.2.35)
Sheshbazzar = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Sheshbazzar) (d:prince of Judah to whom Cyrus gave the temple articles, who laid the foundations of the temple in Jerusalem) (r:15.1.8/15.5.16)
Sheth = (t:name) (w:Sheth) (d:in the prophecy of Balaam, Sheth suante is the descendants or people of Sheth, named together with Moab) (r:4.24.17) (q:draft)
Shethar = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shethar) (d:one of the seven nobles of Persia and Media closest to King Xerxes) (r:17.1.14) (q:draft)
Shetharbozenai = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shethar-Bozenai) (d:Persian official west of the Euphrates who with Tattenai wrote to King Darius about the rebuilding of the temple) (r:15.5.6/15.6.13)
Shethelah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shuthelah) (d:spelling of Shuthelah, son of Ephraim) (r:13.7.20)
Shethur = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Sethur) (d:son of Michael, the man from the tribe of Asher sent to explore Canaan) (r:4.13.4)
Sheva = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Sheva) (d:secretary of King David; also a son of Caleb by his concubine Maakah, founder of Makbenah and Gibea) (r:13.2.49/10.20.25)
shiah = (t:see) <Eglath-sheli-shiah>
Shibab = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shobab) (d:spelling of Shobab, a son of David and Bathsheba born in Jerusalem) (r:13.3.5)
Shibah = (t:name) (c:well) (w:Shibah) (d:well dug by the servants of Isaac, after which the town of Beersheba was named) (r:1.26.33) We have found water.
Shibboleth = (t:name) (w:Shibboleth) (d:word that the men of Gilead made the fleeing Ephraimites say at the fords of the Jordan; those who said Sibboleth were killed) (r:7.12.6)
Shifeam = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shimeam) (d:spelling of Shimeam, son of Mikloth, a Benjamite living in Jerusalem) (r:13.9.38)
Shifi = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shiphi) (d:a Simeonite, father of Ziza) (r:13.4.37)
Shifmoth = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Shifmoth) (d:home of Zabdi, who was in charge of the produce of the vineyards of King David; the NIV calls him the Shiphmite) (r:13.27.27)
Shifrah = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Shiphrah) (d:one of the two Hebrew midwives in Egypt, named with Puah) (r:2.1.15)
Shiftan = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shiphtan) (d:father of Kemuel, the leader of the tribe of Ephraim who helped divide the land of Canaan) (r:4.34.24)
Shihor = (t:name) (c:river) (w:Shihor) (d:river on the eastern border of Egypt, named as the southern limit of the land of Israel) (r:13.13.5/6.13.3)
Shihorlibnath = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Shihor Libnath) (d:place on the western boundary of the territory of Asher, near Carmel) (r:6.19.26)
Shikkeron = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Shikkeron) (d:town on the northern boundary of Judah, between Ekron and Mount Baalah) (r:6.15.11)
Shilhi = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shilhi) (d:the father of Azubah, the mother of King Jehoshaphat) (e:Azubah hi a, ~’ tanu ahi hi) (r:11.22.42/14.20.31) (q:draft)
Shilhim = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Shilhim) (d:town in the far south of Judah) (r:6.15.32)
Shillem = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shillem) (d:son of Naphtali, ancestor of the Shillemite clan) (r:1.46.24/4.26.49)
Shiloah = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Shiloah) (d:gently flowing stream in Jerusalem, also called Siloam) (r:23.8.6)
Shiloh = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Shiloh) (d:town in the hill country of Ephraim where the tabernacle stood in the days of Joshua, the judges and Samuel) (e:~ khua-a a omna nusia a) (r:19.78.60/9.4.12) (q:draft)
Shiloni = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Shilonite) (d:person from Shiloh, said of the prophet Ahijah; Shiloni mi is the Shilonite) (r:11.15.29/11.12.15)
Shilshah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shilshah) (d:son of Zophah, of the tribe of Asher) (r:13.7.37)
Shimea = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shimea) (d:name of several men, among them the third son of Jesse and brother of David, and a Levite of the family of Merari) (r:13.2.13/13.20.7) (q:draft)
Shimeah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shimeah) (d:name of two men: a brother of David and father of Jonadab, and a Benjaminite, son of Mikloth) (r:10.13.3/13.8.32)
Shimeath = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Shimeath) (d:Ammonite woman, mother of one of the officials who killed King Joash; Shimeath mite are the Shimeathites, a clan of scribes) (r:12.12.21)
Shimei = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shimei) (d:name of many men, among them the son of Gera who cursed David, and a governor of Solomon in Benjamin) (r:11.4.18)
Shimeon = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shimeon) (d:descendant of Harim who had married a foreign wife in the time of Ezra) (r:15.10.31)
Shimon = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shimon) (d:man of the tribe of Judah, father of Amnon, Rinnah, Ben-Hanan and Tilon) (r:13.4.20) (q:draft)
Shimrath = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shimrath) (d:Benjaminite, son of Shimei) (r:13.8.21)
Shimri = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shimri) (d:name of several men, among them a Simeonite, the father of one of David’s warriors, and a Levite in the time of Hezekiah) (r:13.4.37/13.11.45)
Shimrith = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Shimrith) (d:Moabite woman, mother of Jehozabad, one of the men who killed King Joash) (r:14.24.26)
Shimron = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shimron) (d:son of Issachar, ancestor of the Shimronite clan; also a town in the territory of Zebulun) (r:1.46.13/13.7.1)
Shimronmeron = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Shimron Meron) (d:Canaanite royal city whose king was defeated by Joshua) (r:6.12.20)
Shimshai = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shimshai) (d:secretary who wrote with Rehum to King Artaxerxes against the rebuilding of Jerusalem) (r:15.4.8/15.4.9)
Shinab = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Shinab) (d:king of Admah in the time of Abraham) (r:1.14.2)
Shinar = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Shinar) (d:the land of Babylonia, the plain where Babylon, Uruk and Akkad lay) (r:1.11.2/1.10.10)
Shion = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Shion) (d:town in the territory of Issachar) (r:6.19.19)
Shisha = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shisha) (d:father of Elihoreph and Ahijah, the secretaries of King Solomon) (r:11.4.3)
Shishak = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shishak) (d:king of Egypt who sheltered Jeroboam and attacked Jerusalem in the time of Rehoboam) (r:11.11.40/11.14.25)
Shitrai = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shitrai) (d:man of Sharon in charge of the herds of King David grazing in Sharon) (r:13.27.29)
Shitthim = (t:name) (c:valley) (w:Shittim) (d:valley of the acacia trees, watered by the stream from the house of the Lord in Joel 3:18) (r:29.3.18)
Shittim = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Shittim) (d:place in the plains of Moab east of the Jordan, the last camp of Israel before crossing the river) (r:4.25.1/6.3.1)
Shiza = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shiza) (d:Reubenite, father of Adina, one of David’s warriors) (r:13.11.42)
Shoa = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Shoa) (d:people named with Pekod and Koa among the allies of Babylon) (r:26.23.23)
Shobab = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shobab) (d:name of two men: a son of David born in Jerusalem, and a son of Caleb son of Hezron) (r:13.2.18/10.5.14)
Shobai = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shobai) (d:head of a family of temple gatekeepers who returned from exile) (r:15.2.42/16.7.45)
Shobak = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shobak) (d:commander of the army of Hadadezer king of Zobah, killed in battle against David; called Shophak in 1 Chronicles) (r:10.10.16/10.10.18)
Shobal = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shobal) (d:name of two men: a son of Seir the Horite and chief in Edom, and a descendant of Judah) (r:1.36.20/13.4.1)
Shobek = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shobek) (d:one of the leaders who sealed the covenant in the time of Nehemiah) (r:16.10.24)
Shobi = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shobi) (d:son of Nahash, from Rabbah of the Ammonites, who brought supplies to David at Mahanaim) (r:10.17.27)
Shofak = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shophak) (d:commander of the army of Hadadezer, killed in battle against David; called Shobak in 2 Samuel) (r:13.19.18/13.19.16)
shofan = (t:see) <Atoroth-shofan>
Shoham = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shoham) (d:Levite of the family of Merari, son of Jaaziah) (r:13.24.27)
Shomer = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shomer) (d:name of two men: a son of Heber of the tribe of Asher, and the parent of Jehozabad who killed King Joash) (r:13.7.32/13.7.34)
Shua = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shua) (d:a Canaanite man, father of the wife of Judah) (e:Kanaan mi ~’ tanu mu hi) (r:1.38.2/1.38.12) (q:draft)
Shua = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Shua) (d:daughter of Heber, sister of Japhlet, Shomer and Hotham) (r:13.7.32) (q:draft)
Shuah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shuah) (d:son of Abraham and Keturah; Shuah gammi is the Shuhite, said of Bildad the friend of Job) (r:1.25.2)
Shual = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shual) (d:a descendant of Asher, in the list of the sons of Zophah) (e:Suah, Harnerfer, ~, Beri, Imrah) (r:13.7.36) (q:draft)
Shual = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Shual) (d:Shual gam, the district of Shual near Ophrah) (e:pawlkhatte ~ gam Ofrah lamah kihei-in) (r:9.13.17) (q:draft)
Shubael = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shubael) (d:name of two Levites: a descendant of Amram, and a son of Heman who was a temple musician) (r:13.24.20)
Shuhah = (t:name) (w:Shuhah) (d:relative of Kelub in the genealogy of Judah) (r:13.4.11)
Shuham = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shuham) (d:son of Dan, ancestor of the Shuhamite clan) (r:4.26.42)
Shulam = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Shulam/Shulammite) (d:home of the young woman of the Song of Songs; Shulam numei is the Shulammite) (r:22.6.13)
Shullam = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shallum) (d:uncle of Jeremiah; the text spells the name Shullam) (e:na pano ~’ tapa Hananel) (r:24.32.7) (q:draft)
Shumath = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Shumathite) (d:one of the clans of Kiriath Jearim, descended from Caleb) (r:13.2.53)
Shunem = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Shunem) (d:town in the territory of Issachar, where the Philistines camped before the battle of Gilboa; home of Abishag) (r:6.19.18/11.2.21)
Shuni = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shuni) (d:son of Gad, ancestor of the Shunite clan) (r:1.46.16/4.26.15)
Shuppim = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shuppim) (d:name of a Benjaminite and of a Levite gatekeeper in the time of David) (r:13.26.16)
Shur = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Shur) (d:desert region on the north-eastern border of Egypt) (e:Kadesh leh ~ kikal Gerar-ah) (r:1.20.1/9.15.7) (q:draft)
Shuthelah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shuthelah) (d:son of Ephraim, ancestor of the Shuthelahite clan) (r:13.7.20/4.26.35)
si = (t:v) (w:die) (d:stop living; a si is he died and si lo is not die) (e:numei zong a ~ hi/tua ciangin amah ~ hi | and then he died/tua na nek ni-in na ~ ding hi | on the day you eat it you will die/Jair ~-in Kamon-ah kivui hi | Jair died and was buried in Kamon/Korah’ tapate ~ lo uh hi | the sons of Korah did not die) (a:nungta) (r:42.20.32/7.10.5/1.5.5/1.2.17/4.26.11)
si = (t:n) (w:blood) (d:blood, a short form of sisan, used mostly of the blood of a sacrifice) (e:biakna tau tung kimkotah a ~ theh hi/tuutal go-in, a ~ tawmkhat la-in | kill the ram and take some of its blood/kiciamna ~ ahi hi | it is the blood of the covenant/a ~ a om laiteng sung ding hi | he shall pour out the rest of the blood) (s:sisan) (r:3.8.19/2.29.20/41.14.24/3.4.30)
Si = (t:adj) (w:dead) (d:si, dead, written with a capital in the name Si Tuipi, the Dead Sea) (e:nisuahna lama om ~ Tuipi ah luang ding a/Jordan Kuam-ah luang sukin ~ Tuipi sung tung hi | it flows down into the Arabah and enters the Dead Sea/Hih tui in ~ Tuipi tui siangsak kikin | this water makes the water of the Dead Sea fresh again/Israel gam sung ~ Tuipi nisuahna lama om | in the land of Israel, east of the Dead Sea) (b:si) (r:38.14.8/26.47.8/26.47.9/26.39.11) (q:draft)
sia = (t:n) (w:sir) (d:respectful word used in speaking to a man, as in sia aw) (e:Kong thuum hi, ~ aw | pardon me, sir) (r:7.6.13)
sia = (t:n) (w:teacher/preacher) (d:one who teaches; sia leh a sinte is teacher and students) (e:~ in thuhilh/~ leh a sinte a kibangin | teacher and students alike/Pasian in ~ khempeuh lakah a lianpen ahi hi | God is the greatest of all teachers/kamsang pawlkhat le ~ pawlkhat om uh hi | there were some prophets and teachers) (s:siapa/thuhilhpa) (r:18.36.22/13.25.8/44.13.1)
sia = (t:n) (w:evil) (d:what is bad or wrong, the opposite of pha, good; a sia gamta is do evil) (e:a pha leh a ~/Topa muhna ah a ~ gamta hi | he did evil in the eyes of the Lord/gamtat ~ khempeuh ka pelh hi | I keep away from every evil way/kei’ tungah a ~ dingin na ngaihsun uh hi | you intended evil against me) (s:siatna) (a:phatna) (r:1.2.9/19.119.101/12.21.20/1.50.20)
sia = (t:n) (w:damage) (d:harm done to a thing so that it is spoiled or worn out; sia lo is undamaged) (e:ki~, na ~sak kei un/mangbuh leh mangbuhmante ~ lo hi | the wheat and the spelt were not damaged/na puan uh ~ loin | your clothes did not wear out) (s:kisia) (r:2.9.32/5.8.4)
sia = (t:n) (w:ruin) (d:the state of being destroyed, said of cities, houses and peoples) (e:na khuapite uh a ~ hi ding hi/a ~ dingin amaute na tuksak hi | you cast them down to ruin/inn ~ lak-a om ngiate | jackals among ruined houses/Minamte lakah note na ~ ding uh a | you will perish among the nations) (s:siatna) (r:3.26.33/19.73.18/26.13.4/3.26.38)
Sia = (t:n) (w:Teacher/teacher) (d:sia, teacher, written with a capital as a title or a form of address; Sia aw is Teacher, said to the person spoken to) (e:note Topa leh ~ ka hi napi-in/~ aw, hih numei a khialh laitak kimu hi | Teacher, this woman was caught in the act of sin/~ aw, a kituak mahmahin na gen zo hi | Teacher, you have spoken very well/~ a sem kote in a khauhzaw thukhenna thuak ding | we who teach will be judged more strictly) (s:Siapa/Rabbi) (b:sia) (r:43.13.14/59.3.1/43.8.4/42.20.39) (q:draft)
Sia = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Sia) (d:head of a family of temple servants who returned from exile, called Siaha in Ezra 2:44) (e:Keros’ suante, ~’ suante, Padon’ suante) (r:16.7.47) (q:draft)
sia-hil = (t:n) (w:sign/portent/wonder) (d:a person or thing that others look on with wonder or as a warning) (e:~ bang ka hih hangin) (s:siahil) (r:19.71.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
siacimit = (t:v) (w:perish/be destroyed/come to an end) (d:be ruined so as to be no more) (e:a ~ na hi nai kei uh hi) (s:siamang) (r:39.3.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
siacimitsak = (t:v) (w:ruin utterly/destroy completely) (d:siacimit, be utterly ruined, with the causative sak: bring to complete ruin) (e:Hih khuapi ka ~ ding a) (s:susiamang/siasakmang) (b:siacimit) (r:26.21.27) (q:draft)
siacip = (t:v) (w:be ruined/perish/be destroyed completely) (d:sia, be ruined, with cip, completely; also cried out as a ruin, a ruin) (e:Nineveh khuapi ~ ta hi/a kisusia ding teng ~ un | let those who are to perish perish/tu-in a ~ ding hi ta hi | now it is about to be utterly ruined/Jerusalem khuapi aw, a ~ ding na hita hi | O Jerusalem, you are doomed to ruin) (s:siamang/siagawp) (b:sia) (r:34.3.7/26.21.27/38.11.9/34.3.1/24.4.30) (q:draft)
siacipin = (t:v) (w:lie in ruins/be desolate) (d:siacip, be utterly ruined, with the linking ending in; a siacipin om is lie in ruins) (e:ka biakinn a ~ a om lai takin/Jerusalem khuapi a ~ om ding hi | Jerusalem will lie in ruins/amaute a tawntungin ~ simmawhna ka thuaksak ding hi | I will make them an everlasting ruin and an object of scorn) (b:siacip) (r:37.1.4/42.21.24/24.25.9) (q:draft)
siagawp = (t:v) (w:be ruined/lie in ruins/be spoiled) (d:sia, be spoiled, with gawp, severely: be badly damaged or brought to ruin) (e:ka pate a kivuina khuapi ~ a/Eite nasepna hong ~ ding tham loin | not only will our trade be ruined) (s:siacip) (b:sia) (r:16.2.3/44.19.27) (q:draft)
siagawppah = (t:v) (w:collapse at once/be ruined immediately) (d:siagawp, be ruined, with pah, at once) (e:thakhat thu-in ~ a) (b:siagawp) (r:42.6.49) (q:draft)
siah = (t:n) (w:tribute/tax) (d:payment required by a ruler; siah pia is pay tax and siah puak is bring tribute) (e:kumpipa tungah ~ piak dingin/Kaisar kumpipa kiangah ~ piak tuak ahi hiam | is it right to pay taxes to Caesar/Moab kumpipa Eglon tungah ~ puak uh hi | they sent tribute to Eglon king of Moab/kuate tung panin ~ kai ahi uh hiam | from whom do they collect taxes) (s:mangmu) (r:16.5.4/42.20.22/7.3.15/40.17.25) (q:draft)
siah = (t:v) (w:set a trap/lay a snare/ensnare) (d:set a trap or net for someone, mostly with thang, trap, as in thang siah) (e:kei thang hong ~ uh a/amah in thang hong ~ hi | he has set a trap for me/na mite thang ~ uh a | they lay a trap for your people/a ngenthang uh tawh kei hong ~ uh a | they set their net for me) (s:thangsiah) (r:19.119.110/18.19.6/19.83.3/19.35.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
Siaha = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Siaha) (d:head of a family of temple servants who returned from exile, called Sia in Nehemiah 7:47) (r:15.2.44) (q:draft)
siahah = (t:todo) (q:draft, in tua ban siahah, Numbers 32.19, apparently on the far side or beyond, NIV on the other side of the Jordan; the word siah here is not clear)
siahdon = (t:see) <siahdon'na>
siahdon'na = (t:n) (w:tax collection/collecting of taxes) (d:siah, tax, with don, collect, and the noun suffix na; siahdonna buk is the booth where taxes are collected) (e:Levi kici ~ bukah tu-in a om/Levi in ~ buk sungah tu-in a om | Levi was sitting in the tax booth) (s:siahdonna) (r:42.5.27/41.2.14) (q:draft)
siahdong = (t:n) (w:tax collector/publican) (d:siah, tax, with dong, ask or demand: one who collects taxes) (e:Thomas leh ~ Mattiu/Zakkhias a kici ~ ukpa khat na om a | there was a chief tax collector called Zacchaeus/~ dangte le thukham a khial midang tampite | other tax collectors and many other sinners) (s:siahdongpa) (r:40.10.3/42.19.2/40.9.10) (q:draft)
siahdongpa = (t:n) (w:tax collector/publican) (d:siahdong, tax collector, with pa, marking a man: a man who collects taxes) (e:Thomas le ~ Matthai/khat pen ~ ahi hi | the other was a tax collector/~ pen a gamla simah ding a | the tax collector stood at a distance/~ Levi, a zumah a tu a mu hi | he saw the tax collector Levi sitting at his office) (s:siahdong) (b:siahdong) (r:40.10.3/42.18.10/42.18.13/42.5.27) (q:draft)
siahdongte = (t:n) (w:tax collectors/publicans) (d:siahdong, tax collector, with the plural te) (e:~ leh migilote khempeuh in/~ leh mawhnei tampite va pai uh a | many tax collectors and sinners came/biakna innpi ~ Piter kiangah pai uh a | the collectors of the temple tax came to Peter/~ leh mawhneite tawh, bang hangin an nekhawm | why do you eat with tax collectors and sinners) (s:siahkhawmte) (b:siahdong) (r:42.15.1/42.19.2/40.9.10/40.17.24/42.5.30) (q:draft)
siahdonna = (t:n) (w:tax collecting/collection of taxes) (d:siah, tax, and don, collect, with the noun suffix na; siahdonna zum is the tax office) (e:a ~ zumah tu-in a om) (s:siahdon'na) (r:41.2.14) (q:draft)
siahil = (t:n) (w:portent/omen/warning sign) (d:something that serves as a sign or warning to others, used beside lim, sign) (e:lim le ~ dingin/a ~ bang ka hih hangin | though I have become like a portent) (s:sia-hil) (r:23.20.3/19.71.7) (q:draft)
siahin = (t:v) (w:setting a trap/ensnaring) (d:siah, set a trap, with the linking ending in; thang siahin, laying a snare) (e:mi a thuhilhpa thang ~) (s:thangsiahin) (b:siah) (r:23.29.20) (q:draft)
siahin = (t:n) (w:as tax/as tribute) (d:siah, tax, with the marker in, as; siahin pia, pay as tax) (e:~ na piak ding uh sum) (b:siah) (r:40.22.19) (q:draft)
siahkhawmte = (t:n) (w:tax collectors/revenue collectors) (d:siah, tax or tribute, with khawm, gather, and plural te: those who collect the tribute) (e:gamdang mi siahdongte leh ~) (s:siahdongte) (r:23.33.18) (q:draft)
siahna = (t:n) (w:trapping/trap/snare) (d:siah, set a trap, with the noun suffix na: trapping or the thing used to trap; ngasa siahna sikkawi is a fishhook) (e:ngasa ~ sikkawi tawh Awle man zo ding/Amah ~-in lei lakah khauzak kitung a | a noose is hidden in the ground to trap him/kei hong ~-in tehlop koihsim uh a | they have hidden a snare to trap me/mi kiphasakte in keimah ~ in gum to uh hi | the arrogant dig pits to trap me) (s:thangsiahna) (b:siah) (r:18.41.1/18.18.10/19.140.5/19.119.85) (q:draft)
siahsim = (t:v) (w:set a trap secretly/lay a hidden snare) (d:siah, set a trap, with sim, secretly) (e:tehlop khat tawh kei hong ~ uh hi/amaute in thang ~ ding gen uh a | they talk of laying hidden snares) (r:19.142.3/19.64.5) (q:draft)
siahsimna = (t:n) (w:hidden trap/hidden snare) (d:siahsim, set a trap secretly, with the noun suffix na) (e:Amau ngenthang ~ uh ah) (b:siahsim) (r:19.35.8) (q:draft)
siahsun = (t:v) (w:present tribute/offer tribute) (d:siah, tribute, with sun: hand over the tribute to a ruler) (e:Ehud in a ~’ a man khit ciangin) (r:7.3.18) (q:draft, low confidence)
siahte = (t:n) (w:taxes/revenues/tribute) (d:siah, tax, with plural te) (e:gam sung panin a kingah ~ ahi) (b:siah) (r:15.6.8) (q:draft)
siahuai = (t:adj) (w:wicked/vile/heinous/terrible) (d:sia, bad, with huai, worthy of: very bad, mostly of conduct or of a person; siahuai zaw is worse) (e:Tua bang mawhna in a ~ hi a/Hehna leh sinsona ~ a | anger and fury are terrible/Note ~ lua na hih manun | because you are so vile/Tua bang gamtatna pen a ~ ahi hi | such conduct is wickedness) (s:gilo) (a:hoih) (r:18.31.11/20.27.4/34.1.14/3.18.17) (q:draft)
