siate = (t:n) (w:ruins/broken parts) (d:sia, ruined or spoiled, with plural te: ruined things or places; khuapi siate are ruined cities) (e:kulhpi ~ puah nadingin innte na phel hi/kisia maisa khuapi ~ puahkik ding uh hi | they will repair the ruined cities laid waste/Israel gam khuapi ~ sunga teeng mite in | the people living in the ruined cities of Israel) (s:siasate/kisiamaisate) (b:sia) (r:23.22.10/23.61.4/26.33.24) (q:draft)
siate = (t:adj) (w:evil/bad) (d:sia bad or evil with the plural marker te, placed after the noun, as in gamtat siate evil ways; a siate is the evil things) (e:na gamtat ~ uh hangin/na gamtat ~ panun kihei-in | turning from your evil ways/A phate sia ci-in, a ~ pha ci a | calling good evil and evil good/a gamtat phate le a gamtat ~ tungah | on those who do good and those who do evil) (s:gilote) (a:hoihte) (b:sia) (r:24.23.2/12.17.13/23.5.20/40.5.45) (q:draft)
Siate = (t:n) (w:teachers) (d:sia teacher with plural te) (e:na ~ uh kiseel nawn lo ding) (s:thuhilhte/hilhte) (b:siate) (r:23.30.20) (q:draft)
siateng = (t:n) (w:all the evil things/every evil) (d:sia bad, evil, with teng all) (e:ngei loh a ~ gamta hi) (r:26.18.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
siatgamtatin = (t:v) (w:act corruptly/do evil) (d:siat bad, with gamtat behave and in; behaving corruptly) (e:ka sih khit ciangin note ~) (r:5.31.29) (q:draft)
siatgawp = (t:v) (w:be utterly ruined/be laid waste/be destroyed) (d:siat, be ruined, with gawp, completely) (e:hih nate khempeuh a ~ ding hun/keima mi Israel-te a ~ manin | because my people Israel were laid waste) (s:siamang/siacip) (b:siat) (r:42.21.6/26.35.15) (q:draft)
siatgawpna = (t:n) (w:devastation/ruin) (d:siatgawp be badly ruined, with the noun suffix na) (e:a ~ hangin lamdangsa-in) (s:kisiatna/siatna) (b:siatgawp) (r:24.49.17) (q:draft)
siathei = (t:adj) (w:perishable/corruptible) (d:sia, spoil or go bad, with thei, able; a siathei lo is imperishable. A siathei tawpin is as badly as they can) (e:a ~ pumpi pen a ~ lo pumpi/A ~ khamte nangawn | even gold, which perishes) (s:muatthei/kisiathei/sithei) (b:sia) (r:46.15.50/60.1.7) (q:draft)
siatkhak = (t:v) (w:come to ruin/be harmed/be corrupted) (d:siat, be ruined, with khak, happen to: fall into ruin or harm, mostly of something feared) (e:i nasepna a ~ ding lauhuai hi/note zong na ~ loh nadingun | so that you too do not come to harm) (r:44.19.27/65.1.23) (q:draft)
siatkik = (t:v) (w:sheathe/put back) (d:siat, thrust in, with kik, back: put a sword back into its sheath) (e:Na namsau a paai-ah ~ in/vantungmi in a namsau a pai sungah a ~ hi | the angel put his sword back into its sheath/a paai-ah ka ~ loh nading thu | that I will not put it back into its sheath/na namsau uh a paai-ah ~ zaw un | rather put your swords back into the sheath) (a:dok) (r:40.26.52/13.21.27/26.21.5/26.21.30) (q:draft)
siatlawh = (t:v) (w:be ruined by/come to ruin through) (d:siat, be ruined, with lawh: suffer ruin as the outcome of something, like sihlawh, die as the outcome) (e:dahlua-in ~ kha ding hi/lunghihmawhna a neih loh manun ~ uh hi | because they have no concern they come to ruin) (r:47.2.7/20.1.32) (q:draft)
siatlawhkhak = (t:v) (w:be destroyed/come to ruin) (d:siat be ruined, with lawh as a result and khak happen to; end up destroyed by it) (e:na vekpi-un na ~ ding uh) (r:48.5.15) (q:draft)
siatloh = (t:v) (w:not be ruined/not decay/not be bad) (d:siat, form of sia be bad or ruined, with the negative loh; a siatloh nadingin is so that it will not be ruined) (e:gam sung a ~ nadingin/Ama nu le ama pa zahin a ~ hangin | though he was not as bad as his father and mother/Jesuh’ luang a ~ nadingin | so that the body of Jesus would not decay/gunkuang a ~ nadingin | so that the lifeboat would not be wrecked) (r:1.41.36/43.19.39/12.3.2/44.27.16) (q:draft)
siatmai = (t:see) <siatmai-na>
siatmai-na = (t:n) (w:ruin/devastation) (d:siat, be ruined, with mai, wholly, and the noun suffix na: complete ruin, devastation) (e:na gam sungah ~ leh suksiatna) (s:siatmaina/suksiatna/kisiatna) (r:23.60.18) (q:draft)
siatmaina = (t:n) (w:ruin/devastation) (d:siat, be ruined, with mai, wholly, and the noun suffix na: complete ruin, devastation) (e:na gam sungah ~ le suksiatna) (s:siatmai-na/suksiatna/kisiatna) (r:23.60.18) (q:draft)
siatna = (t:n) (w:evil/wickedness) (d:siat, bad, with the noun suffix na: evil, wrongdoing; siatna bawl is do evil) (e:~ panin na leii kem in/Na kam uh, ~ na uksak uh a | you let evil rule your mouth/~ bawl mihonte ka mudah a | I hate the company of evildoers/Hih bang ~ nam khempeuh na gamta khin a | you have done every kind of evil like this) (s:gitlohna/hoihlohna/gilohna) (a:phatna) (b:siat) (r:19.34.13/19.50.19/19.26.5/26.16.23) (q:draft)
siatna = (t:n) (w:disaster/harm/ruin/destruction) (d:siat, be ruined, with the noun suffix na: ruin or disaster that comes on someone; siatna tung is disaster comes) (e:na tungah ~ hong tung lo ding/a gamtate tungah ~ leh gimna tungsak hi | he brings ruin and trouble on those who do it/~ in su dingin amah ngak gige hi | disaster is always waiting to strike him/amaute tungah ~ leh gimna tampi tung ding hi | many disasters and troubles will come on them) (s:tuahsiatna/kisiatna/suksiatna) (b:siat) (r:19.91.10/18.31.3/18.18.12/5.31.17) (q:draft)
siatnasate = (t:n) (w:evil deeds/evils done) (d:siatna, evil, with sa, already done, and plural te; na gamtat siatnasate uh, the evil things you have done) (e:na gamtat ~ uh hangin) (s:siatnate/gamtatsiatnate) (r:26.20.43) (q:draft)
siatnate = (t:n) (w:disasters/calamities/evils) (d:siatna, disaster, with plural te: the bad things that come on people) (e:hih ~ i tungah hong tung) (s:tuahsiatnate) (b:siatna) (r:5.31.17) (q:draft)
siatnate = (t:n) (w:evil deeds/wickedness) (d:siatna, evil, with plural te: evil deeds; often after gamtat, conduct, as in gamtat siatnate, evil doings) (e:na gamtat ~ uh paikhia un/amau gamtat ~ bangin amaute thukkik in | repay them according to their evil deeds/na gamtat ~ uh ka za hi | I hear of your evil deeds/ka hihnop loh ~ ka gamta zawsop hi | I keep doing the evil I do not want to do) (s:gamtatsiatnate/tatsiatnate/siatnasate) (b:siatna) (r:23.1.16/30.8.7/19.28.4/9.2.23/45.7.19) (q:draft)
siatnateng = (t:n) (w:all the wickedness) (d:siatna evil, wickedness, with teng all) (e:Nangma ~ hong kipholak ma) (b:siatna) (r:26.16.56) (q:draft)
siatni = (t:n) (w:day of ruin/day of doom) (d:siat be ruined, with ni day) (e:Izipt gam a ~ hun) (b:siat) (r:26.30.9) (q:draft)
siatsak = (t:v) (w:destroy/ruin/harm) (d:siat, be ruined, with the causative sak: destroy or ruin something, or do harm to someone) (e:an khempeuh a ~ ciangin/Topa in note mai-ah a ~ minamte bangin | like the nations the Lord destroyed before you/Nang kong ~ ding keima' thu ahi hi | it is in my power to harm you/ka vai ~ ding sunthapai-in hanciam uh a | all day long they strive to ruin my cause) (s:susia/siasak/suksiat) (a:puah/puahkik/lamkik) (b:siat) (r:19.105.16/5.8.20/1.31.29/19.56.5) (q:draft)
siatsakna = (t:n) (w:defilement/ruining) (d:siatsak ruin, defile, with the noun suffix na; the act of defiling) (e:a tanu Dinah a ~ za hi) (s:nitsakna) (b:siatsak) (r:1.34.5) (q:draft)
siatsakzawh = (t:v) (w:can break/be able to destroy) (d:siatsak destroy, break, with zawh be able) (e:na ~ ciang bekin) (s:susiazo) (r:24.33.20) (q:draft)
siatsuah = (t:v) (w:spoil/ruin) (d:bring to ruin; the NIV has blemishes at your love feasts) (e:hong ~ uh a) (r:65.1.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
siatsuk = (t:v) (w:plunge in/thrust down into) (d:siat, thrust, with suk, downward) (e:gil sungah ~ hi) (b:siat) (r:7.3.21) (q:draft)
siattat = (t:v) (w:do harm/do evil/act violently) (d:keep doing what is bad or destructive; siattat semsem, go from bad to worse) (e:mizuaute in ~ ding bek ut uh hi/mi khem theite zong ~ semsemin | impostors too going from bad to worse) (s:gamtatsiat) (r:20.13.2/55.3.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
siattheih = (t:v) (w:can be ruined/can ruin) (d:siat, be ruined, with theih, can, the form used before nading; siattheih nading, so as to be able to ruin or be ruined) (e:Jesuh’ min a ~ nadingin/~ nading gukhal tawh a kidim | full of deadly poison) (b:siat) (r:44.26.9/59.3.8) (q:draft)
siattheihna = (t:n) (w:wickedness/offensive way) (d:siat bad, with theih can and the noun suffix na; something that can be evil) (e:Kei sungah ~ a omkha hiam) (b:siattheih) (r:19.139.24) (q:draft, low confidence)
siatzaw = (t:adj) (w:worse/more wicked) (d:siat bad, evil, with the comparative zaw) (e:nangma mawhnate nak ~ lua ahih manin) (s:siazaw) (a:hoihzaw/phazaw) (b:siat) (r:26.16.52) (q:draft)
siavuan = (t:n) (w:doctor/physician) (d:a doctor, one who treats the sick) (e:Cidamte in ~ kisam lo uh a) (s:zato/siavuanpa) (r:42.5.31/41.5.26) (q:draft)
siavuanpa = (t:n) (w:doctor/physician) (d:siavuan doctor, with pa marking a man) (e:I it ~ Luka le Demas) (s:siavuan/zato) (b:siavuan) (r:51.4.14) (q:draft)
siavuante = (t:n) (w:doctors/physicians) (d:siavuan, doctor, with plural te) (e:a neih khempeuh ~ cialna-in) (s:zatote) (b:siavuan) (r:42.8.43) (q:draft)
siazaw = (t:adj) (w:worse/more evil) (d:sia bad with the comparative zaw; what it is compared with takes sangin) (e:pate uh sangin a ~ uh hi/a pian’ masak sangin a ~ hi | it is worse than it was at first/thu um lo mite sangin ~ lai hi | he is even worse than the unbelievers/amah sangin a ~ dawi sagih | seven spirits more wicked than itself) (s:siatzaw/siahuaizaw) (a:hoihzaw/phazaw) (r:24.7.26/40.12.45/54.5.8/42.11.26) (q:draft)
Sibbekai = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Sibbekai) (d:Sibbekai the Hushathite, one of David’s mighty warriors, who killed a Philistine giant and commanded the army division of the eighth month) (r:13.11.29/13.27.11)
Sibboleth = (t:name) (w:Sibboleth) (d:the way the men of Ephraim said Shibboleth, by which the men of Gilead knew them at the fords of the Jordan) (r:7.12.6)
Sibmah = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Sibmah) (d:town east of the Jordan in the territory of Reuben, known for its vines) (r:4.32.38/6.13.19)
