Sibraim = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Sibraim) (d:place on the northern border of the land in Ezekiel’s vision, between Damascus and Hamath) (r:26.47.16)
sibup = (t:v) (w:faint/swoon/lose consciousness) (d:become like dead from hunger or fear; sibup natna is an illness with seizures) (e:misi tawh kibangin a ~ uh hi/kihta-in a ~ ding uh hi | they will faint from fear/gilkial dangtakin amaute ~ uh hi | hungry and thirsty, they fainted/Naupangte leh naungeekte kongzing lakah a ~ uh hi | children and infants faint in the streets) (r:40.28.4/40.17.15/42.21.26/19.107.5/25.2.11) (q:draft)
sibupin = (t:adv) (w:in a faint/unconscious) (d:sibup, faint, with the adverbial ending in) (e:~ lei lakah ka tuk hi) (b:sibup) (r:27.8.18) (q:draft)
sicip = (t:v) (w:die) (d:si die, with cip, apparently all without exception or for good) (e:Eite khempeuh ~ ding i hi kei hi) (b:si) (r:46.15.51) (q:draft, low confidence)
sidaangsak = (t:v) (w:make pale/terrify) (d:of fear, make someone turn pale; the NIV has makes me tremble) (e:launa in hong ~ hi) (r:23.21.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
sidar = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:cedar) (d:the cedar tree, a loan from English cedar) (e:na ~ khuam hoihpente) (s:taamtak/taamtaak) (r:24.22.7) (q:draft)
Siddim = (t:name) (c:valley) (w:Siddim) (d:valley by the Dead Sea, full of tar pits, where the kings of Sodom and Gomorrah fought the four kings) (r:1.14.3/1.14.8)
sidek = (t:v) (w:be about to die/be dying) (d:si, die, with dek, almost: on the point of death; sidek tak, deathly) (e:a ~ mi tawh ka kibang ta a/a ~ tak a om lai-te hanthawn in | strengthen those that remain and are about to die) (s:sihkuan) (r:19.88.4/66.3.2) (q:draft)
Sidon = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Sidon) (d:firstborn son of Canaan; also the Phoenician port city north of Tyre that bears his name) (r:1.10.15/13.1.13)
Sidonte = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Sidonians) (d:the people of the Phoenician city of Sidon) (b:Sidon) (r:7.18.7)
Siene = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Aswan) (d:town on the southern border of Egypt next to Cush, also called Syene, the modern Aswan) (r:26.29.10/26.30.6)
Sifas = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Cephas) (d:Aramaic name meaning rock that Jesus gave to Simon Peter; the same man as Peter) (r:43.1.42)
Sifmoth = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Siphmoth) (d:town in the south of Judah to which David sent a share of the plunder) (r:9.30.28)
sigalna = (t:n) (w:mourning/funeral) (d:mourning for the dead, set against feasting; the NIV has house of mourning) (e:Pawisimna sangin ~ hoihzaw hi) (r:21.7.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
sigawp = (t:v) (w:die in great numbers/perish) (d:si die, with gawp heavily, in a mass) (e:gampa lakah a ~ uh hi) (b:si) (r:46.10.5) (q:draft)
sih = (t:v) (w:die) (d:form of si used before linking words and endings such as khit, ciangin, na and ding; a sih khit ciangin means after his death) (e:Ahab a ~ khit ciangin Moab gam/a ~ ni dongin ta nei lo hi | she had no children to the day of her death/Ahaz Kumpipa a ~ kumin | in the year King Ahaz died/Shawl a ~ ciangin ama tangin | when Shaul died, in his place) (b:si) (r:12.1.1/23.14.28/10.6.23/13.1.49) (q:draft)
sihbup = (t:n) (w:epilepsy/seizure) (d:used with natna illness for the falling sickness) (e:Amah in ~ natna nei-in gim) (r:40.17.15) (q:draft)
sihdaan = (t:n) (w:death sentence/death penalty) (d:sih, die, and daan, punishment; sihdaan pia, sentence to death) (e:~ piak tuak lo hi/thu hilh ahih manin ~ piak tuak hi | because he has preached, he deserves the death sentence/ka hehna tawh ~ kong pia ding hi | in my anger I will sentence you to death) (r:24.26.16/26.16.38/24.26.11) (q:draft)
sihin = (t:v) (w:die/when one dies/at death) (d:sih, form of si, die, with the ending in: at the time of dying, or dying in a certain state; a sihin kum za is he was a hundred years old when he died) (e:Hor Mual-ah Aaron a ~ kum za/Moses a ~ kum za le kum sawmnih pha hi | Moses was a hundred and twenty years old when he died/a ~ amah zahtakna bawl uh hi | they honored him when he died/a ~ kum za khat leh kum sawmthum pha hi | he was a hundred and thirty years old when he died) (b:sih) (r:4.33.39/14.24.15/5.34.7/14.32.33) (q:draft)
sihkhak = (t:v) (w:die) (d:sih die, with khak happen to; might die) (e:a ~ ding uh lau-in) (r:26.32.10) (q:draft)
sihkhawm = (t:v) (w:die together/die with) (d:sih, die, with khawm, together) (e:Khrih tawh i ~ leh amah tawh/Nang tawh ~ nading ciang dong ahi zongin | even if I have to die with you/Amah tawh i ~ le | if we died with him/thu a mang lo mite tawh a ~ lohna | that she did not die with the disobedient) (s:sikhawm) (a:hingkhawm) (b:sih) (r:45.6.8/41.14.31/55.2.11/58.11.31) (q:draft)
sihkhit = (t:v) (w:have died/be dead) (d:sih, die, with khit, completion; a sihkhit ma-in, before they have died) (e:Hih lai-a om mite a ~ ma-in/a nungta mi khempeuh a ~ ma-in | before all who are now living have died) (s:sikhin) (r:42.21.32/40.24.34/41.13.30) (q:draft)
sihkhitna = (t:n) (w:having died/death) (d:sihkhit, have died, with the noun suffix na: the fact that someone has already died) (e:Amah a ~ thei uh ahih manin/amah a na ~ thei uh ahih manin | because they knew he was already dead/a ~ thu a theih ciangin | when he learned that he had died) (b:sihkhit) (r:42.8.53/41.15.45/43.19.33) (q:draft)
sihkuan = (t:v) (w:be about to die/be dying) (d:sih, die, with kuan, be about to: be at the point of death) (e:Jakob a ~ ciangin) (s:sidek) (r:58.11.21) (q:draft)
sihlawh = (t:v) (w:die because of/perish because of/bring death on oneself) (d:meet death as the result of something; sih die with lawh get as a consequence) (e:pilna a don loh manun ~ uh a/Ama pumpi ki-uk zo lo ahih manin ~ a | he dies because he cannot control himself/Kumpipa heh leh mi khatpeuh in ~ thei a | when the king is angry someone may die for it/mihing mahmah in zong i ~ ding lauhuai hi | there is danger that we ourselves will lose our lives) (s:sihpih) (r:20.1.32/18.5.2/20.5.23/20.16.14/44.27.10) (q:draft)
sihlohna = (t:n) (d:sih die, with loh not and the noun suffix na; a sihlohna inn is a house where no one has died) (e:khat beek a ~ inn khat) (r:2.12.30) (q:draft)
sihmang = (t:v) (w:perish/die out) (d:sih, die, with mang, away or lost: die and be gone) (e:note sia-in na ~ khit matengun) (r:5.28.20) (q:draft)
sihna = (t:n) (w:death) (d:sih, die, with the noun suffix na: death; also the state of the dead, as in sihna pan thokik, rise from the dead) (e:~’ gu in mawhna ahi hi/ama ~ ding lim a genna ahi hi | he was showing what kind of death he would die/Ama misiangthote’ ~ pen | the death of his faithful ones/amaute, ~ kongpi nai ta uh hi | they drew near the gates of death) (a:nuntakna/hinna) (b:sih) (r:46.15.56/44.10.40/43.12.33/19.116.15/19.107.18) (q:draft)
Sihna = (t:n) (w:Death/Hades) (d:sihna, death, written with a capital when death is spoken of as a person or power; Sihna Gam, Hades, the land of the dead) (e:~ Kumpipa kiangah kitunpih hi/~ leh ~ Gam mei li sungah a kiasuk hi | Death and Hades were thrown into the lake of fire/sakol tung tuang mi’ min in ~ hi a | the name of the rider on the horse was Death/~ leh siatna nangawn in | even Death and Destruction) (b:sihna) (r:18.18.14/66.20.14/66.6.8/18.28.22) (q:draft)
sihnate = (t:n) (w:deaths) (d:sihna death, with the plural te; the NIV has sword) (e:~ khat peuhpeuh in) (b:sihna) (r:45.8.35) (q:draft)
Sihon = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Sihon) (d:king of the Amorites who ruled in Heshbon and was defeated by Israel under Moses) (r:4.21.21/19.135.11)
sihpah = (t:v) (w:die at once/wither at once) (d:sih die, with pah immediately) (e:theikung tuaci ~ ahi hiam) (s:sipah) (r:40.21.20) (q:draft)
sihpih = (t:v) (w:die for/die because of) (d:die on account of something, as one's own folly or another's sin, also die for the sake of another, as a shepherd for his sheep) (e:mihaite in a hai ~ uh hi/na mawhna uh na ~ ding uh hi | you will die in your sins/Babilon’ mawhna ~ kei un | do not die for the sin of Babylon/Tuucing hoih in a tuute ~ ngam hi | the good shepherd is ready to die for his sheep) (s:sihlawh) (b:sih) (r:20.10.21/43.10.11/43.8.21/24.51.6) (q:draft)
sihsak = (t:v) (w:kill/put to death/cause to die) (d:sih, die, with the causative sak: kill, put to death; teek sihsak is let someone die in old age) (e:amah satin liam sakin a ~ a/hih mipa ka ~ manun kote hong sisak kei in | do not let us die for killing this man/na pumpi uh a gamtatna na ~ uh leh | if you put to death the deeds of your body/Israel mi tampi a ~ manin | because she killed many of Israel) (s:that/sisak/thatlum) (a:hingsak/nungtasak/nuntaksak) (b:sih) (r:5.19.11/45.8.13/32.1.14/24.51.49) (q:draft)
