sikpuan = (t:n) (w:coat of armor/coat of mail/armor) (d:sik, iron, with puan, garment: armor worn on the body in battle; sikpuan silh is put on armor) (e:~ tawh amah kithawi a/sumngo lukhu khusakin, ~ silhsak hi | he put a bronze helmet on him and dressed him in a coat of armor/a thalte uh tawi-in ~ silhin ding uh hi | they stood holding their bows and wearing armor) (r:9.17.5/9.17.38/16.4.16) (q:draft)
sikpuante = (t:n) (w:coats of armor/coats of mail) (d:sikpuan, coat of armor, with the plural te) (e:siklukhute, ~, thalte) (b:sikpuan) (r:14.26.14) (q:draft)
siksan = (t:v) (w:rely on/base on/stand on) (d:take something as one's ground, support or claim; siksan ding is a ground or footing to stand on) (e:bang ~ na hi uh hiam/i ~ ding bangmah thu om het lo hi | we have no ground at all to stand on/mun siangtho ah ~ ding mun hong pia hi | he gave us a firm place in his holy place/na neih lohnate uh ~ hi loin | not on the basis of what you do not have) (s:bulphuh) (r:23.36.4/44.19.40/15.9.8/47.8.12) (q:draft)
siksanin = (t:prep) (w:on the basis of/based on/according to/from) (d:siksan with the suffix -in: taking something as the ground or support for what is said or done) (e:Lai Siangtho ~ mite tawh thu kikum a/tecite’ genna ~ mi thatpa kithat ding hi | the murderer shall be put to death on the testimony of witnesses/thu taktak ~ thu khenzaw un | judge instead by what is true/keima kam mah ~ kei hong man ding a | my own mouth would condemn me) (b:siksan) (r:44.17.2/4.35.30/43.7.24/18.9.20) (q:draft)
siksankha = (t:v) (w:rely on/judge by) (d:siksan rely on, with kha happen to; end up going by) (e:a kimu theiteng na ~ thei uh hi) (r:47.10.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
siksante = (t:n) (w:defenses/supports/things relied on) (d:siksan, rely on, with plural te: the grounds or arguments one stands on) (e:na ~ uh leikhal bang hi lel hi) (b:siksan) (r:18.13.12) (q:draft)
sikseek = (t:n) (w:blacksmith/smith) (d:sik, iron, and seek, forge: one who works iron) (e:~ khat zong om lo hi/~ khat zong kimu lo hi | not a blacksmith could be found/khutsiamte le ~ siamte | the craftsmen and the skilled smiths) (s:seekpa) (r:9.13.19/24.24.1) (q:draft)
sikseekpa = (t:n) (w:blacksmith/smith/metalworker) (d:a man who forges metal; sik, iron, and seek, forge, with pa marking a male person) (e:hiam a bawl ~ ka piangsak khin hi/~ in na hoihpi piangsak thei hi | the smith can produce a fine vessel) (s:seekpa) (b:sikseek) (r:23.54.16/23.44.12/20.25.4) (q:draft)
sikseekte = (t:n) (w:smiths/metalworkers/artisans) (d:plural of sikseek, one who forges metal) (e:khutsiamte leh ~ khempeuh ciahpih hi/khutsiamte leh ~ tulkhat | a thousand craftsmen and smiths/khutsiamte le ~, Jerusalem khua panin | the craftsmen and the smiths, from Jerusalem) (s:seekte) (b:sikseek) (r:12.24.14/24.29.2/12.24.16) (q:draft)
siksek = (t:n) (w:ironworking/smithing) (d:sik iron, with sek forge; siksek siamte are smiths) (e:khutsiamte leh ~ siamte) (r:24.24.1) (q:draft)
siksekpa = (t:n) (w:blacksmith/smith/metalworker) (d:sik, iron, with sek, forge, and pa for a man: a man who works metal, also of a silversmith) (e:hiam a bawl ~ ka piangsak khin hi/~ in na hoihpi piangsak thei hi | the smith can produce a fine vessel) (s:seekpa) (b:siksek) (r:23.54.16/20.25.4) (q:draft)
siksuk = (t:v) (w:tread down on/tread upon) (d:sik, tread, with suk, downward) (e:leitung mualsang dawnte hong ~ ding hi) (b:sik) (r:33.1.3) (q:draft)
siktawn = (t:n) (w:iron rod/iron bar) (d:sik, iron, with tawn, a whole long piece; kalhna siktawn is the bar that locks a gate) (e:~ khat tawh amaute na satkham ding a/a kalhna ~ lah neilo uh a | and they have no bars to lock them) (s:sikzawl) (r:19.2.9/24.49.31) (q:draft)
siktawnte = (t:n) (w:iron bars) (d:siktawn, iron bar, with plural te; the bars that lock a city gate) (e:kalhna ~ uh a kitan hi) (s:sikzawlte) (b:siktawn) (r:24.51.30) (q:draft)
sikte = (t:n) (w:iron/metals) (d:sik, iron, with plural te: iron things; in Malachi 3.2 the metals that are refined) (e:~ a siangthosak mei/a sumngote, a ~, a suangkangte | its bronze, its iron, its marble/Ama adingin ~, buhkung bangin nip a | to him iron is as soft as straw) (b:sik) (r:39.3.2/18.41.27/66.18.12) (q:draft)
siktukkilh = (t:n) (w:nail/iron nail) (d:a metal nail for fastening wood or for nailing something down) (e:tua milim ~ tawh khen kip uh hi/zat dingin ~ leh gak nadingin sik tampi | much iron for nails and for fittings/tua a ~ ma vangah ka khutmete | my fingers into the holes of those nail wounds) (r:23.41.7/13.22.3/43.20.25) (q:draft)
sikzawl = (t:n) (w:iron bar/iron rod) (d:sik, iron, and zawl, pole or bar) (e:a khete ~ bangin khauh hi/khua kongpi ~ khempeuh ka kuaitan ding a | I will break all the bars of the city gates) (s:siktawn) (r:18.40.18/23.43.14) (q:draft)
sikzawlte = (t:n) (w:iron bars/bars) (d:sikzawl, iron bar, with the plural te: the iron bars that lock a gate) (e:~ tum nih suah hi/a ~ ka sattan ding hi | I will cut through its iron bars/kulh sangpi, kongpi leh ~ tawh | with high walls, gates and bars) (s:siktawnte/kalhnate) (b:sikzawl) (r:19.107.16/5.3.5/23.45.2) (q:draft)
sikzumte = (t:n) (w:lances/spears) (d:sik, iron, with zum, pointed, and plural te: pointed iron weapons) (e:namsaute leh ~ tawh) (r:11.18.28) (q:draft)
sil = (t:v) (w:wash/bathe) (d:wash the body or a part of it, such as the hands and feet, with water) (e:tui tawh amaute a ~ hi/a khe uh tua tui tawh ~ ding uh | they shall wash their feet with that water/a pumpi khempeuh tui sungah ~ ding a | he shall bathe his whole body in water/dikna tawh ka khutte ka ~ siang hangin | though I have washed my hands clean in innocence) (s:sawp) (r:3.8.6/2.30.19/3.15.16/19.73.13) (q:draft)
sila = (t:n) (w:slave/servant/bondservant) (d:a person who belongs to a master and must serve him; sila suak is become a slave) (e:note ~ suak uh hen/~ lim la-in | taking the form of a servant/~ khat kumpi a suah ciang | when a slave becomes king/leitawi a late in a piate’ ~ suak hi | the borrower becomes the slave of the lender) (s:nasem/sal) (a:topa) (r:40.20.27/50.2.7/20.30.22/20.22.7) (q:draft)
Sila = (t:n) (w:servant/slave) (d:sila, servant or slave, written with a capital at the start of a sentence, and as a title of Jesus, the Servant of God) (e:na ~ siangtho Zeisu tungah/ama ~ Zeisu a min thangsak zo hi | he has glorified his servant Jesus/~ in inn sungah a om tawntung kei hi | a slave does not stay in the house forever) (b:sila) (r:44.4.28/44.3.13/43.8.35) (q:draft)
silanu = (t:n) (w:slave woman/female slave/bondwoman) (d:sila, slave, with nu marking a woman) (e:~ tawh a neih a tapa) (b:sila) (r:48.4.23/48.4.22) (q:draft)
silapa = (t:n) (w:servant/slave) (d:a male servant or slave; pa marks a man) (e:siampi ukpa’ ~ sat a/a ~ in a topa bangin ahih leh | if the servant is like his master/Tua ~ min in Malkhas ahi hi | the name of that servant was Malchus/ama ~ Johan kiangah hilh hi | he made it known to his servant John) (s:nasempa) (a:topa) (b:sila) (r:43.18.10/40.10.25/66.1.1) (q:draft)
Silapa = (t:n) (w:servant) (d:silapa, a male servant, written with a capital as a title of Jesus, the Servant of God) (e:Pasian in a ~ hong thawhsak khit) (b:silapa) (r:44.3.26) (q:draft)
Silas = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Silas) (d:leader in the church at Jerusalem who travelled with Paul on his second missionary journey) (r:44.15.22/44.15.40)
silate = (t:n) (w:slaves/servants) (d:sila, slave or servant, with the plural te) (e:Sakol tungah ~ tuang a/~ nangawn a topa’ kiangpan suakta hi | even the slaves are free from their master/Kam-a hilh lel tawh ~ pil zo lo | servants are not made wise by words alone/Pasian leh Tuuno’ ~ in Topa bia-in | the servants of God and of the Lamb will worship him) (s:nasemte/salte) (a:tote) (b:sila) (r:21.10.7/18.3.19/20.29.19/66.22.3) (q:draft)
silbawlin = (t:v) (w:toiling/laboring) (d:working hard, with the linking ending in; paired with nasem, work, as nasem silbawlin, laboring and toiling) (e:Nasem ~ ki-om tawntung a) (r:47.11.27) (q:draft)
silbawlnate = (t:n) (w:toils/labors/hardships) (d:hard work, with the noun suffix na and the plural te; paired with nasep, work, as ka nasep ka silbawlnate, our labor and toil) (e:ka nasep ka ~ khempeuh uh) (r:52.2.9) (q:draft)
silenai = (t:n) (w:blood and pus) (d:si blood, le and, nai pus; the NIV has defiled with blood) (e:~ tawh a dim uh hi) (r:25.4.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
sileng = (t:v) (w:die) (d:si, die, with leng, if I: if I were to die; ka nuntak sangin sileng is to die rather than to live) (e:ka nuntak sangin ~ kei a dingin) (r:32.4.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
silesa = (t:n) (w:flesh/body/flesh and blood) (d:si, blood, le, and, sa, flesh: the human body of flesh and blood; leitung silesa is the earthly body, human nature or human descent) (e:ka pumpi ~ zong kiamgawp khinta hi/hih leitung ~ pumpi lut thei lo ding | this earthly body of flesh and blood cannot enter/leitung ~ lam panin David’ suan hi a | as to his earthly life he was a descendant of David) (s:cilesa) (r:19.109.24/45.1.3/46.15.50) (q:draft)
silh = (t:v) (w:dress/clothe/wear/put on) (d:put on or wear clothes; puan silh is wear a garment) (e:Sisan tawh kitheh puanza a ~ hi/puan a nin mahmah ~ hi | he was dressed in very dirty clothes/a kigan khawm puan na ~ kei ding hi | you shall not wear cloth woven together/saihadial puansan vive ~ zo hi | she is clothed in fine linen and purple) (s:puansilh) (a:suahkhia) (r:66.19.13/5.22.11/38.3.3/20.31.22)
silhin = (t:v) (w:wearing/clothed in/dressed in) (d:silh, wear, with the linking ending in: wearing something while doing the next action) (e:puan khat bek ~ Zeisu nung zui a/saihadial siampi puan ~ Topa mai-ah na a sem | serving before the Lord wearing a linen ephod/Numei khat in ni ~ | a woman clothed with the sun/mi nih in puanpaak ~ amau kiangah dingin | two men dressed in white stood beside them) (b:silh) (r:41.14.51/44.1.10/9.2.18/66.12.1) (q:draft)
silhkawmin = (t:v) (w:wearing) (d:silh, wear, with kawm, while, and the linking ending in: while wearing) (e:puansan ~ hong pusuak a) (r:43.19.5) (q:draft)
silhkik = (t:v) (w:put on again/dress again) (d:silh, put on clothes, with kik, again) (e:Ka puante ~ ding ka hi hiam/a puan ~ a | he put his clothes back on) (b:silh) (r:22.5.3/43.13.12) (q:draft)
silhlai = (t:v) (w:be wearing) (d:silh, wear, with lai, still or at that time: be wearing at the moment) (e:ama ~ a puantualpi suahin) (r:9.18.4) (q:draft)
silhlo = (t:v) (w:not wear) (d:silh, wear, with lo, not) (e:samul puan peuhmah ~ ding uh hi/mo pawi siimna puan a ~ mi khat | a man who was not wearing wedding clothes/kuamah in ~ ding uh hi | no one will wear them) (b:silh) (r:26.44.17/40.22.11/23.59.6) (q:draft)
silhloin = (t:v) (w:not wearing/without wearing) (d:silhlo, not wear, with the linking ending in: without clothes on) (e:Zanin puan ~ lum uh a/sauveipi sung puan ~ omkhin a | for a long time he had worn no clothes/mizawngte in puan ~ na sem uh a | the poor work without clothes) (b:silhlo) (r:18.24.7/42.8.27/18.24.10) (q:draft)
silhlopi = (t:see) <silhlopi-in>
silhlopi-in = (t:adv) (w:without wearing) (d:silh, wear, with lo, not, and the ending pi-in: without having put a garment on) (e:mo pawi siimna puan ~/~ hih lai-ah hong bangci luttheih na hi hiam | how did you get in here without wearing it) (r:40.22.12) (q:draft)
silhna = (t:n) (w:wearing/clothing/putting on) (d:silh, wear, with the noun suffix na: the wearing or putting on of a garment, or what is worn) (e:saihadial puan ~ thu a ngah hi/a puan ~-ah minthan’na nei-in | glorious in his apparel/puanhampi ~ a zang dingin | to put on sackcloth) (s:puansilhna) (b:silh) (r:66.19.8/23.63.1/23.22.12) (q:draft)
silhnate = (t:n) (w:wearing/clothing) (d:silhna, wearing, with the plural te; puan hoihnono silhnate is the wearing of fine clothes) (e:puan hoihnono ~ na bulphuh kei unla) (b:silhna) (r:60.3.3) (q:draft)
silhnuam = (t:v) (w:like to wear/want to wear) (d:silh, wear, with nuam, like or want: like to go about wearing something) (e:Amaute in puantualpi ~ uh a/puantualpi ~ uh a, mihon lakah | they like to wear long robes, and among the crowd) (r:41.12.38/42.20.46) (q:draft)
silhpa = (t:n) (w:man clothed in/wearer) (d:silh, wear, with pa, which marks a man: the man who wears something, as saihadial puan a silhpa, the man clothed in linen) (e:Pasian in saihadial puan a ~ kiangah/Puanpaak ~ in a khut tegel vantung lamah lamto | the man clothed in linen lifted both his hands toward heaven/Topa in saihadial puan ~ a sawl ciangin | when the Lord commanded the man clothed in linen/puanhoih a ~ enin | looking at the man who wears fine clothes) (b:silh) (r:26.10.2/27.12.7/26.10.6/59.2.2) (q:draft)
silhsa = (t:v) (w:wearing/dressed in/clothed in) (d:silh, wear, with sa, already done: having put a garment on, dressed in it) (e:puanak leh puan tualpi ~ leh lukhu khusa-in/saihadial puan neel leh puansan ~-in | dressed in fine linen and purple) (b:silh) (r:27.3.21/17.8.15) (q:draft)
silhsak = (t:v) (w:clothe/dress/put on) (d:silh, wear, with the causative sak: put a garment on someone, dress or clothe a person) (e:Vantungte khuamial ka ~ a/savun puan bawl a, amaute ~ hi | he made garments of skin and clothed them/a ta nauzaw Jakob ~ hi | she put them on her younger son Jacob/puanza san a ~ khit uh ciangin | after they had clothed him in a purple robe/Daniel kumpi puansan ~ dingin thu pia pah a | he at once gave orders to clothe Daniel in royal purple) (s:puansilhsak) (a:suahkhiatsak) (b:silh) (r:1.3.21/23.50.3/1.27.15/43.19.2/27.5.29)
silhsakin = (t:v) (w:clothing/dressing/putting on) (d:silhsak, put clothing on someone, with the linking ending in: clothing someone and then doing something further) (e:puan siangthote Aaron ~/hotkhiatna puan kei hong ~ | he has clothed me with garments of salvation/siampi luite puanhampi ~ | clothing the leading priests in sackcloth/puantungsilhte ~, kawnggak tawh amaute gak a | he put tunics on them and tied sashes around them) (b:silhsak) (r:2.40.13/3.8.7/23.61.10/12.19.2/3.8.13) (q:draft)
silhsakkik = (t:v) (w:clothe again/put back on) (d:silhsak, clothe someone, with kik, again: put a person’s clothes back on him) (e:ama puan mah ~ uh a/ama puan ngeite a ~ uh hi | they put his own clothes back on him) (b:silhsak) (r:40.27.31/41.15.20) (q:draft)
silhtawm = (t:v) (w:wear/put on) (d:silh, wear, with tawm, which seems to mean for oneself: have a garment on) (e:puan thak khat na ~ a) (r:11.11.29) (q:draft, low confidence)
silhte = (t:n) (w:those who wear/wearers) (d:silh, wear, with the plural te: people who wear a certain kind of garment) (e:Puannel ~ in kumpipa’ inn sungah/Puannel ~ en dingin paikhia na hi uh hiam | did you go out to see people who wear fine clothes/sikpuan ~ dingsak man kei un) (b:silh) (r:40.11.8/24.51.3) (q:draft)
silhte = (t:n) (w:garments/clothes) (d:silh, wear, with the plural te, after puan: the clothes that someone wears) (e:a puan hoih ~ uh suah khia-in/na puan san a, na puan ~ | your clothing is red, the garments you wear) (s:puante/puansilhte) (b:silh) (r:26.26.16/23.63.2) (q:draft)
silhthuah = (t:v) (w:wear one over another/wear in layers) (d:silh, wear, with thuah, add a layer: wear one garment over another) (e:puanak nih ~ kei un) (r:41.6.9) (q:draft)
silhzo = (t:v) (w:have to wear/be clothed in/wear) (d:silh, wear, with zo, manage or be able: have something to wear; with bek, have only that to wear) (e:puansia bek ~ ding hi/saihadial puansan vive a ~ hi | she is clothed in nothing but fine linen and purple/Tuuvun peuh, keelvun peuh ~ bekin | having only sheepskins and goatskins to wear) (b:silh) (r:20.23.21/58.11.37/20.31.22) (q:draft)
silin = (t:v) (w:wash/bathe) (d:sil, wash, with the linking ending in, joining it to the next verb: washing and then; said of feet, the body and parts of an offering) (e:amaute in a khe uh ~/a sungkua leh a khete ~ | washing the internal organs and the legs/tui sungah a pumpi ~ | bathing his body in water/a pumpi tui sungah ~, a puante silh ding a | he shall bathe his body in water and put on his garments) (s:sawpin) (b:sil) (r:7.19.21/3.16.28/2.29.17/3.16.24) (q:draft)
