sillh = (t:v) (w:put on/wear) (d:apparently a misprint of silh wear) (e:mithak a ~ mi na hi uh hi) (r:51.3.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
silloin = (t:v) (w:without washing/not washing) (d:sil, wash, with loin, without; khut silloin, with unwashed hands) (e:khut ~ an a neklam uh/khut ~ an ne lo uh hi | they do not eat without washing their hands/khut ~ an ne ahi uh hiam | do they eat without washing their hands) (b:sil) (r:41.7.2/41.7.5/41.7.3) (q:draft)
silngo = (t:n) (w:yeast/leaven) (d:substance mixed into dough to make it rise; silngo sawhloh anlum is bread made without yeast, and silngo om lo is unleavened) (e:~ tawm khat in annel lom/Farisaite leh Saddusite’ ~ kikeem un | be on your guard against the yeast of the Pharisees and Sadducees/~ sawhloh anlum ni sagih sung na ne ding | you shall eat unleavened bread for seven days/Lungdam kohna-in ~ sawh anlum va pia un | offer leavened bread as a thank offering) (r:48.5.9/40.16.6/2.13.6/30.4.5) (q:draft)
Silngo = (t:n) (w:yeast/leaven) (d:silngo, yeast, written with a capital at the start of a sentence and in the festival name Silngo Sawh loh Anlum Pawi, the Festival of Unleavened Bread) (e:~ Sawh loh Anlum Pawi hun hong naita hi/Paisan Pawi, leh ~ Sawh loh Anlum Pawi | the Passover and the Festival of Unleavened Bread/~ a kisawh peuhmah nane kei ding uh hi | you shall eat nothing made with yeast) (b:silngo) (r:42.22.1/14.35.17/2.12.20) (q:draft)
silngote = (t:n) (w:leaven/yeast) (d:silngo, yeast, with the plural te; used as a picture of evil that spreads) (e:hai leh gilo ~ tawh hi loin) (b:silngo) (r:46.5.8) (q:draft)
silnngo = (t:n) (w:yeast/leaven) (d:apparently a misprint of silngo) (e:Farisaite leh Herod’ ~ kikeem un) (r:41.8.15) (q:draft)
Siloam = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Siloam) (d:pool in Jerusalem where Jesus sent a blind man to wash; a tower there fell and killed eighteen people) (r:43.9.11/42.13.4)
silsak = (t:v) (w:wash for/wash) (d:sil, wash, with sak, for someone: wash a part of another person’s body, said of feet, hands or head) (e:ka lu zong hong ~ in/a nungzuite’ khe ~ a | he washed his disciples’ feet/ka topa’ nasemte’ khe a ~ ding nasem | a servant to wash the feet of my lord’s servants/amaute’ khe a ~ khit ciangin | when he had finished washing their feet) (s:sawpsak) (b:sil) (r:43.13.9/43.13.5/9.25.41/43.13.12) (q:draft)
silsakin = (t:v) (w:washing for/washing) (d:silsak wash for someone, with in linking to the following verb; washing) (e:a nungzuite’ khe ~ a kawngah) (b:silsak) (r:43.13.5) (q:draft)
