simtat = (t:v) (w:be hypocritical/pretend/dissemble) (d:show an outward goodness that is not real; mi simtat, hypocrite; simtat loin, sincerely) (e:Isaiah in mi ~ note tungah/A ~ laitheite leh Farisaite aw | you hypocritical teachers of the law and Pharisees/A ~ mi in a kampi bek tawh thuhoih gen | a hypocrite speaks good words with his lips only/amau ~ manin Barnabas nangawn in amaute lam a zui | because of their hypocrisy even Barnabas followed them) (s:kineih/kineihkhem) (r:40.15.7/48.2.13/40.23.27/20.26.24) (q:draft)
simtatin = (t:adv) (w:stealthily/secretly) (d:simtat, act in secret, with the ending in: by stealth, without being noticed) (e:~ innte sungah a lut khit uh) (s:simthamin/thusimin) (a:kilangin) (b:simtat) (r:55.3.6) (q:draft)
simtatna = (t:n) (w:hypocrisy/insincerity) (d:acting falsely while appearing good; in Daniel 6 used of hidden wrongdoing) (e:~ leh gitlohna tawh na dim uh hi/Zeisu in amaute’ ~ a theih ciangin | when Jesus knew their hypocrisy/Mi ~ ahi Farisaite’ silngo kikem un la | beware of the yeast of the Pharisees, which is hypocrisy/maitang zahtakna leh ~ a om kei hi | there is no partiality or hypocrisy) (s:kineihkhemna/kineihna) (b:simtat) (r:40.23.28/42.12.1/41.12.15/59.3.17) (q:draft)
simtatpa = (t:n) (w:hypocrite) (d:simtat, pretend or deceive, with pa for a man: a man who pretends to be better than he is; nang mi simtatpa aw is the address you hypocrite) (e:Nang mi ~ aw) (s:thusimnei/thusimneimi) (b:simtat) (r:40.7.5/42.6.42) (q:draft)
simtatte = (t:n) (w:hypocrites/deceivers) (d:simtat, pretend or deceive, with the plural te, used after mi: people who pretend to be what they are not) (e:Mi ~ in a kampi bek tawh/mi ~ bangin na hih kei un | do not be like the hypocrites/Mi ~ aw, bang hangin kei hong ze-et | you hypocrites, why do you test me/mi ~ in phatna a ngah nop manun | because the hypocrites want to receive praise) (s:misimtatte/thusim neite) (b:simtat) (r:20.26.24/40.22.18/40.6.5/40.6.2) (q:draft)
simte = (t:n) (w:those counted/the numbered) (d:sim, count, with the plural te: the people who were counted; a simte lakah is among those he counted) (e:siampi Aaron in a ~ lakah) (s:kisimte) (b:sim) (r:4.26.64) (q:draft)
simte = (t:n) (w:scouts/spies) (d:in thukan simte, men sent out in secret to find out about an enemy) (e:David in thukan ~ sawl a) (s:thukante/kansimte) (r:9.26.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
simte = (t:n) (w:secret things/hidden deeds) (d:things done in secret, from sim, secretly; a simtham-a i hih simte is the things we do in hiding) (e:a simtham-a i hih ~ nangawn | even the things we do in secret) (r:21.12.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
simtham = (t:adj) (w:desolate/waste/deserted) (d:of land left empty with no one living in it; gam simtham is a wasteland) (e:kisia-in gam ~ suak ding a/A gam uh gam ~ a suah uh a | they have made his land a wasteland/gam ~ a suak ding hi | it will become a wasteland/teen’ lohna gam ~ na suak kha ding hi | you will become a wasteland where no one lives) (r:24.25.11/24.2.15/24.26.9/24.6.8) (q:draft)
simtham = (t:adj) (w:secret/hidden) (d:kept from the knowledge of others; a simtham-a means in secret) (e:A ~-a letsong piakna in/a ~-a i hih simte nangawn | even the things we do in secret) (r:20.21.14/21.12.14) (q:draft)
simthama = (t:adj) (w:secret/hidden) (d:simtham, secret, with the linking a; mun simthama is in a secret place) (e:mun ~ sum kiseelte) (b:simtham) (r:23.45.2) (q:draft)
simthamah = (t:adv) (w:in secret/in a hidden place/in a desert) (d:simtham, secret or desolate, with the place marker ah, after mun, place, or gam, land: mun simthamah is in a secret place and gam simthamah is in a desert) (e:mun ~ a koih mipa/gam ~ khat guak tangten’ hoihzaw hi | it is better to live alone in a desert/mun ~ zanin misite thu a dong mite | people who consult the dead at night in secret places/A thukna sung mun ~ kei hong kikhuituahin | when I was woven together in the secret place of the depths) (b:simtham) (r:5.27.15/20.21.19/23.65.4/19.139.15) (q:draft)
simthamin = (t:adv) (w:secretly/in secret) (d:simtham, secret, with the adverb ending in; usually a simthamin, in secret) (e:A ~ angvanna na zat uh leh/nangmah in a ~ na hih hi | you did it in secret/a ~ thu ka gen kei a | I have not spoken in secret/Kuama theih lohin a ~ a hihte uh | the things they do in secret without anyone knowing) (s:thusimin) (a:kilangin/langtangin) (b:simtham) (r:18.13.10/23.48.16/10.12.12/49.5.12) (q:draft)
simthamin = (t:adv) (w:desolate/deserted) (d:left empty and deserted, said of an abandoned place; gam simthamin kinusia is be left a wasteland) (e:mi omlo gam ~ kinusia ding hi/mi om lo gam ~ kinusia ding hi | it will be left a deserted land with no one in it) (s:gamkhingin/hawmguakin) (b:simtham) (r:40.23.38/42.13.35) (q:draft, low confidence)
simthei = (t:see) <simthei-in>
simthei-in = (t:v) (w:can read/be able to read) (d:sim, read, with thei, can, and the linking in: being able to read) (e:note in ~ a thu na theihtheih) (r:47.1.13) (q:draft)
simto = (t:v) (w:count off/count up/reckon) (d:count upward one after another; of a family line, reckon back through the forefathers) (e:Nipi kal sagih na ~ ding uh hi/kum sagih mun sagih vei na ~ ding | you shall count off seven times seven years/ni sawmnga dong na ~ ding uh a | you shall count off up to fifty days/a pupi Levi lam manawhin kileh ~ hi | it is traced back to his ancestor Levi) (b:sim) (r:5.16.9/13.6.39/3.25.8/3.23.16) (q:draft)
simun = (t:conj) (w:whenever/every time/as often as) (d:sim, every, after a verb, with the plural ending un: each time that they or you do something) (e:hih hai na dawn ~, Topa hong paikik matengin/misi guh a muh ~ | whenever they see a human bone/bangin na dawn ~, kei na hong phawk nadingun | whenever you drink it, in remembrance of me/Pa Pasian kiangah thu ka nget ~ | whenever we pray to God the Father) (s:sialun) (r:46.11.26/26.39.15/46.11.25/52.1.3) (q:draft)
simzawh = (t:v) (w:be able to count/count up) (d:sim, count, with zawh, be able; nearly always negative: simzawh loh is countless and simzawh lohin without number) (e:kuama ~ loh nalamdang tampi sem hi/kauphete le tangngolte, ~ lohin hong pai uh a | locusts and grasshoppers came without number/taamtak singte ~ hi lo hi | the cedar logs could not be counted/A kalaohte uh ~ hi lo a | their camels could not be counted) (r:18.9.10/19.105.34/13.22.4/7.7.12) (q:draft)
simzel = (t:v) (w:raid repeatedly/keep attacking) (d:sim, attack, with zel, again and again: raid a place repeatedly) (e:tua gam ~ uh hi) (r:12.13.20) (q:draft)
simzo = (t:v) (w:be able to count/can number) (d:sim, count, with zo, be able; mostly in questions and negatives: kua in simzo ding is who can count) (e:kua in a mal ~ ding a/ama kum phazah zong i ~ kei hi | we cannot count the number of his years/bangzah pha cih kua in ~ ding ahi hiam | who can count how many there are) (b:sim) (r:4.23.10/18.36.26/18.25.3) (q:draft)
simzo = (t:v) (w:be able to attack/overcome by attack) (d:sim, attack, with zo, be able or succeed: be able to attack and take a place) (e:Jerusalem a ~ ding kuamah om lo ding hi/Kua in eite hong ~ ding ahi hiam | who can attack us) (b:sim) (r:25.4.12/24.49.4) (q:draft)
simzuih = (t:v) (w:follow secretly) (d:sim, secretly, with zuih, follow: follow someone as a disciple in secret) (e:a ~ khat ahi hi) (r:43.19.38) (q:draft)
sin = (t:v) (w:learn/study) (d:gain knowledge or skill by study or by being taught; thu sin is learn a teaching) (e:thuakna tawh thuman’na a ~ hi/note in Khazih thu na ~ kei uh hi | you did not learn about Christ/Izipt mite’ pilna khempeuh ~ a | he learned all the wisdom of the Egyptians/Theikung kiangah thugentehna na ~ un | learn the lesson from the fig tree) (r:58.5.8/49.4.20/44.7.22/40.24.32) (q:draft)
sin = (t:v) (w:test/try/examine) (d:put to the test or look into closely, as silver is tried by fire; also try to do something) (e:hong ze-et in la hong ~ in/nangmah in kote nong ~ zo hi | you have tested us/Keima lungsim hong ~ in la | test my heart/Lai Siangtho tel takin a ~ uh hi | they examined the Scriptures carefully) (s:ze-et/entel/sit) (r:19.26.2/19.66.10/19.17.3/44.17.11) (q:draft)
sin = (t:n) (w:liver/heart) (d:the liver, also the seat of feeling; sin sung is the heart within and sin so is burn with anger) (e:a ~ tunga autok leh a kal nihte/a hehna hangin a ~ sung so hi | he burned inside with anger/biakna-in a gawh ganhing ~ vel ding hi | he will examine the liver of the sacrificed animal/Pasian’ itna eite ~ sungah hong sung zo hi | God has poured his love into our hearts) (r:2.29.13/19.85.3/17.1.12/26.21.21/45.5.5) (q:draft)
sin = (t:v) (w:cover/put a lid on/seal up) (d:close over with a lid or cover, and as a noun the lid itself; lu sin is cover the head and sin cip is seal off) (e:dum a tawh ciangin ~ loin om/a lu ~ pasalte khempeuh | every man who covers his head/lu ~ lo numei khempeuh | every woman who does not cover her head/tua mai sitna in a ~ hi | that veil covers them) (s:khuh/tuam) (a:hon) (r:2.21.33/18.9.7/46.11.4/46.11.5/47.3.14) (q:draft)
Sin = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Sin) (d:desert between Elim and Sinai that Israel crossed after leaving Egypt; Sin gamlak is the Desert of Sin) (e:~ gam lakah giahphual sat uh hi) (r:4.33.11/2.17.1) (q:draft)
Sin = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Sinites) (d:a people descended from Canaan son of Ham, named in Sin mite, the Sinites) (e:Hiv mite, Arki mite, ~ mite) (r:1.10.17/13.1.15) (q:draft)
Sinai = (t:name) (c:mountain) (w:Sinai) (d:mountain in the desert where God gave the law to Moses, and the desert around it; Sinai Mual is Mount Sinai and Sinai gamlak the Desert of Sinai) (e:Moses on Mount ~) (r:3.25.1)
sincip = (t:v) (w:cover over/seal off/shut in) (d:sin, cover, with cip, tightly: close over so that nothing shows or gets out) (e:suangtumpi tawh a hong ~ uh hi/thu pia a, aksite ~ hi | he gives the command and seals off the stars/a kithat ama mite ~ nawn lo ding hi | it will no longer cover its slain) (s:khuhcip) (b:sin) (r:25.3.53/18.9.7/23.26.21) (q:draft)
sing = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:tree) (d:a tree; also used after the name of a kind of tree, as in taamtaak sing, cedar) (e:Huan sung ~ khatpeuh peuh ne/Lebanon gam taamtaak ~ banga a sang | tall like a cedar tree of Lebanon/heipi tawh ~ a phuk bang uh hi | they were like men cutting down trees with axes) (s:singkung/kung) (r:1.3.1/19.37.35/19.74.5)
sing = (t:n) (w:wood/timber) (d:wood as a material for building and making things; singkha sing is acacia wood) (e:oliv ~ tawh kherub nih bawl a/singkha ~ zawlte bawl a | he made poles of acacia wood/mual tungah kuanto un la, ~ sui un | go up into the mountains and cut timber) (r:11.6.23/2.26.26/2.37.4/37.1.8)
sing-atnate = (t:n) (w:saws) (d:sing, wood, with at, cut, the noun suffix na and plural te: tools for cutting wood) (e:~ leh tuzumte leh heite tawh) (s:singatnate) (r:13.20.3/10.12.31) (q:draft)
sing-attem = (t:n) (w:saw) (d:sing, wood, with at, cut, and tem, blade: a saw) (e:~ in amah a zangpa’ tungah) (s:singatna) (r:23.10.15) (q:draft)
Singat = (t:n) (w:saw) (d:sing wood with at cut; singat tem, wood-cutting blade, is a saw) (e:~ tem zong amah a zang pa) (s:singatna/sing-attem) (r:23.10.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
singatna = (t:n) (w:saw) (d:sing, wood, with at, cut, and the noun suffix na: a tool for sawing) (e:~ tawh a ki-at a manpha suangte) (s:sing-attem) (r:11.7.9) (q:draft)
singatnate = (t:n) (w:saws) (d:singatna, saw, with plural te) (e:~ le tuzumte le heite tawh/~, tuzumte, le heite tawh na a sem dingin | to work with saws, picks and axes) (s:sing-atnate) (b:singatna) (r:13.20.3/10.12.31) (q:draft)
singbekte = (t:n) (w:wooden ledges/supporting beams) (d:sing, wood, with bek and plural te; with nanna, support, the offset ledges on the outside wall of the temple that the beams rested on) (e:a nanna ~ a bawl hi) (r:11.6.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
singbul = (t:n) (w:stump/tree stump) (d:sing, tree, with bul, base: the base of a tree left in the ground after it is cut down) (e:~ leh a zungte lei sungah nusia dingin/~ panin a sel a om mah bangin | as a shoot comes from a stump) (r:27.4.26/23.14.29) (q:draft)
singgah = (t:n) (w:fruit) (d:sing, tree, with gah, fruit: the fruit of a tree; singgah kung is a fruit tree) (e:Seeng sunga kikoih ~ min ka mu hi/nong piak numei in ~ hong pia a | the woman you gave me gave me fruit/khaici hita leh ~ hita leh | whether grain or fruit) (s:gah) (r:30.8.1/1.3.12/3.27.30)
singgahte = (t:n) (w:fruits) (e:Huan sung ~ ka ne thei ding uh hi/Note’ nek ding ~ leh note’ dawn ding bawngnawite | your fruit to eat and your milk to drink/A ~ an ding hi ding a | its fruit will be for food) (s:gahte) (b:singgah) (r:1.3.2/26.25.4/26.47.12) plural form of <singgah>
singhiang = (t:n) (w:branch/bough) (d:sing, tree, with hiang, branch: a branch of a tree) (e:~ satin lampi-ah a phah uh hi/~ bangin keu-in hing kik nawn lo ding hi | like a branch he will wither and not be green again/Na khut uh-ah ~ tawi-in | with boughs in your hands) (s:hiang) (r:40.21.8/18.15.32/19.118.27) (q:draft)
singhiangpite = (t:n) (w:boughs/large branches) (d:singhiang branch with pi, large, and plural te; a teh tam singhiangpite are the boughs of leafy trees) (e:a teh tam ~) (b:singhiang) (r:3.23.40) (q:draft)
singhiangte = (t:n) (w:branches) (d:singhiang, branch of a tree, with the plural te) (e:~ lakah amaute ham zaizai uh hi/lo lai-ah ~ satin a phah uh hi | they cut branches in the fields and spread them/mite kuan khia-in tua ~ hong pua-in | the people went out and brought back the branches) (s:hiangte) (b:singhiang) (r:19.104.12/41.11.8/16.8.16) (q:draft)
singin = (t:v) (w:shaking/shaking out) (d:sing, shake, with in linking to the next verb; lu singin is shaking the head, puan singin is shaking out the garment) (e:a lu uh ~ zahpihbawl uh a/kei zong ka puan ~ | I also shook out my robe/na khut ~ lei tuan in la | shake your hand and stamp the ground) (r:41.15.29/16.5.13/26.6.11) (q:draft)
singka = (t:n) (w:harrow/forked wooden tool) (d:in lei kalhkhapna singka, the wooden tool drawn over ploughed land to break up the clods) (e:lei kalhkhapna ~, Israel ka kaisak hi) (r:28.10.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
singkang = (t:n) (w:stick/firewood/brushwood) (d:dry sticks gathered for a fire) (e:Paul in ~ pawlkhat khawmin/~ nih khawng a tom ka hi a | I am gathering a couple of sticks) (r:44.28.3/11.17.12) (q:draft)
singkawm = (t:n) (w:thicket/undergrowth) (d:dense growth of trees and bushes, as on the banks of the Jordan) (e:Jordan gungei ~ lakah) (s:sawlkawm/tulak) (r:24.12.5) (q:draft)
singkha = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:acacia) (d:acacia tree; singkha sing is acacia wood) (e:amah in ~ sing zawlte bawl a/~ sing tawh zawlte bawlin | making poles of acacia wood/khuampeekte ~ sing na bawl ding hi | you shall make the frames of acacia wood) (r:2.37.4/2.25.5/2.37.28/2.26.15) (q:draft)
singkhia = (t:v) (w:shake off/shake out) (d:shake something so that it falls off, as dust from the feet or a snake from the hand) (e:meikhuk sungah tua gul ~ a/na khepeek nuai-a leivuite na ~ un | shake off the dust under your feet/Paul in gul mei sungah ~ a | Paul shook the snake off into the fire/langpanna tawh ama puan ~-in | he shook out his clothes in protest/a neihsa panin Pasian in ~ ta hen | may God shake him out of his possessions) (r:44.28.5/42.9.5/44.18.6/16.5.13) (q:draft)
singkhuah = (t:n) (w:firebrand/burning stick) (d:a piece of wood taken burning from the fire) (e:a kiteenkhia ~ tawh kibang hi/a kitenkhia, ~ khat tawh na kibang uh hi | you were like a burning stick snatched out) (r:38.3.2/30.4.11) (q:draft)
singkhuam = (t:n) (w:cross/wooden post/tree) (d:sing, wood, with khuam, post: the wooden post on which Jesus was put to death) (e:amah ~ tungah khai-in a that uh hi/~ tungah ama pumpi-in a thuak hi | he bore them in his body on the cross) (s:singlamteh) (r:44.10.39/60.2.24) (q:draft)
singkol = (t:n) (w:stocks) (d:sing, wood, with kol, shackles: the wooden frame in which the feet of a prisoner are locked) (e:~ lianpi sungah a khe uh) (r:44.16.24) (q:draft)
singkuang = (t:n) (w:tree)
Singkuang = (t:n) (w:ark) (d:singkuang, wooden chest, written with a capital at the start of a sentence and in Thuciamna Singkuang, the ark of the covenant) (e:Thuciamna ~ a pua Levi mite/Thuciamna ~ a pua siampite | the priests carrying the ark of the covenant/~ tungah hehpihna tokhom na koih ding hi | you shall put the atonement cover on the ark/~ a din’ khiat peuhmah ciangin | whenever the ark set out) (b:singkuang) (r:5.31.25/6.3.11/6.4.16/2.25.21/4.10.35) (q:draft)
singkuangte = (t:n) (w:ark/chest) (d:singkuang wooden chest with plural te; thuciamna singkuang is the ark of the covenant) (e:a kizut thuciamna ~ a om uh hi) (b:singkuang) (r:58.9.4) (q:draft)
singkung = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:tree/vegetation) (d:sing, tree, with kung, trunk or plant: a growing tree) (e:A kiphuksa ~ nangawn in lametna nei a/amaute ~ pai bangin ka mu hi | I see them like trees walking/~ tampi tak a po ka mu hi | I saw a great many trees growing/Midikte’ gah in nuntakna ~ hi a | the fruit of the righteous is a tree of life) (s:sing/kung) (r:18.14.7/1.1.12/41.8.24/26.47.7/20.11.30)
singkungno = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:young tree/sapling/young plant) (d:singkung, tree, with no, young) (e:~ bangin hong sel kik hi) (s:singno/kungno) (b:singkung) (r:18.14.9) (q:draft)
singkungnote = (t:n) (w:young trees/shrubs/bushes) (d:singkungno young tree, with the plural te) (e:Amaute in ~ botin ne uh a/Kuam sunga ~ a en ding | to look at the young trees in the valley) (s:singnote) (b:singkungno) (r:18.30.4/22.6.11) (q:draft)
singkungte = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:trees) (d:singkung, tree, with the plural te) (e:gah a nei ~ leh taamtaak/Tua ciangin ~ in theikung kiangah | then the trees said to the fig tree/tua ama ~ in guahtui tampi a ngah hi | his trees get plenty of rain/Lebanon mual taamtaak ~ khempeuh | all the cedar trees of Lebanon) (s:singte) (b:singkung) (r:19.148.9/7.9.10/19.104.16/23.2.13) (q:draft)
singlamteh = (t:n) (w:cross) (d:the cross; singlamteh tungah that or khai, kill or hang on the cross, means crucify) (e:Zeisu ~ tungah a thah laitakun/A ~ pua-a ka nung hong zui lote | those who do not carry their cross and follow me/~ tung panin hong kumsuk in | come down from the cross/~ tungah khai-in na thah uh Zeisu | Jesus, whom you killed by hanging on a cross) (s:singkhuam) (r:41.15.25/40.10.38/41.15.30/44.5.30) (q:draft)
singlesuang = (t:n) (w:wood and stone/timber and stone) (d:sing, wood, le, and, suang, stone, written as one word: wood and stone as materials for building or for making idols) (e:~ tawh a kibawl pasian/sing phuk le ~ nasep a sem uh hi | they cut timber and worked the wood and stone/~ a kibawl, ngunlekham a kibawl | made of wood and stone, made of silver and gold) (r:5.28.36/11.5.18/5.29.17) (q:draft)
singliante = (t:n) (w:great trees/mighty trees) (d:sing tree with lian great and plural te) (e:a hiang in taamtaak ~ khuh a) (r:19.80.10) (q:draft)
singliim = (t:n) (w:shade of a tree/shady tree) (d:sing, tree, with liim, shade; in Jeremiah for the spreading trees under which idols were worshipped) (e:~ nuai khempeuhah numei paktat bangin/mualsang tung teng leh ~ nuai tengah | on every high hill and under every spreading tree/Sunkim laitak a ~ bangin kote hong liah un | shelter us like the shade of a tree at noon) (s:singniim/singlim) (r:24.3.6/24.2.20/23.16.3) (q:draft)
singlim = (t:n) (w:shady tree/shade of a tree) (d:sing tree with lim shade; singlim nuai is under a spreading tree) (e:~ nuai khempeuh leh mualsangte’ tunga) (s:singliim/singniim) (r:24.17.2) (q:draft)
singluang = (t:n) (w:beam/plank/log) (d:a felled tree trunk or a large piece of timber such as a beam) (e:Na mit sungah ~ om napi-in/khat in ~ a tan lai takin | as one of them was cutting down a tree/kote in ~ khat ciat la-in | let each of us take a log/na mit sungah a om ~ paaikhia masa in | first take the plank out of your own eye) (r:40.7.4/12.6.5/12.6.2/40.7.5) (q:draft)
