sisakin = (t:v) (w:kill/destroy/cause to die) (d:sisak, cause to die, with the linking ending in: killing or destroying, and then) (e:Ka mite ~, a kikhenthangsak gam ukte) (s:thatin) (b:sisak) (r:24.23.1) (q:draft)
sisakmang = (t:v) (w:wipe out/destroy utterly) (d:sisak kill with mang, away to nothing) (e:ka innkuan khempeuh na ~ khin hi) (s:thatmang) (r:18.16.7) (q:draft)
sisakpa = (t:n) (w:destroyer/killer) (d:sisak kill with -pa for a man: the one who kills) (e:Ta upate a ~ in Israel mite’) (s:thatpa/mithatpa) (b:sisak) (r:58.11.28) (q:draft)
