sisante = (t:n) (w:blood) (d:sisan with plural te: blood of several animals, blood that was shed) (e:keel sisan le bawngno ~ va keng loin/ama tunga a luang ~ laakkhia ding a | it will disclose the blood shed upon it) (b:sisan) (r:58.9.12/26.24.7/23.26.21) (q:draft)
Sisar = (t:name) (w:Caesar) (d:Caesar, the title of the Roman emperor, to whom taxes were paid and to whom Paul appealed) (e:Rom kumpipa ~ tungah siah i piak ding) (r:40.22.17/44.26.32) (q:draft)
