sisate = (t:n) (w:the dead/dead people/carcasses) (d:plural: those who have died, also dead bodies of animals) (e:Pa in mi ~ a thosak/a ~ in bangmah thei nawn lo hi | the dead know nothing any more/a ~ a lawng peuhmah nin ding hi | whoever touches their carcasses will be unclean/Khazih’ thu-um a ~ in zong | also those who have died believing in Christ) (s:misite/site) (a:nungtate/hingte) (b:sisa) (r:43.5.21/3.11.36/21.9.5/46.15.18) (q:draft)
