sitban = (t:see) <sitban'na>
sitban'na = (t:n) (w:blemish/defect) (d:a flaw or mark, said of an animal for offering and of the fault of a people; from sit, blemish) (e:ama tungah ~ om lo ding hi/amaute’ ~ hangin | because of their blemish) (s:sitbaanna/poina/paubaanna) (r:3.22.21/5.32.5) (q:draft)
sitbang = (t:adj) (w:blemished/defective/flawed) (d:having a fault, said of an animal for offering; a sitbang lo is without defect) (e:a ~ lo keel pa khat paipih ding a/a ~ khatpeuh peuh na pia kei ding | you shall not offer anything that has a defect/a ~ lo apa khat na pia ding uh | you shall offer a male without defect/a ~ lo kum khat a pha tuuno | a lamb a year old without defect) (s:sitbaang) (r:3.4.23/3.22.25/3.22.20/3.22.19/3.23.12) (q:draft)
