Stakhus = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Stachys) (d:Christian in Rome whom Paul greets as his dear friend) (r:45.16.9)
stakte = (t:n) (w:stacte/gum resin) (d:a fragrant gum resin, one of the spices of the holy incense) (e:A namtui nate, ~, onikh leh galbanum) (r:2.30.34) (q:draft)
Stefanas = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Stephanas) (d:Christian of Corinth whose household, baptized by Paul, were the first converts in Achaia) (r:46.1.16/46.16.15)
Stefen = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Stephen) (d:one of the seven chosen to serve in the church at Jerusalem, a man full of grace and power, stoned to death as the first Christian martyr) (r:44.6.5/44.8.2)
Stoik = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Stoic) (d:school of Greek philosophers, some of whom debated with Paul in Athens) (r:44.17.18)
su = (t:v) (w:touch/lay a hand on/harm) (d:touch, lay a hand on, and so harm; often in the compound su-kha, touch) (e:hih in na muk ~-kha zo hi/siatna in nang hong ~ nawn lo ding hi | harm will not touch you again/ka pa Saul in nang hong ~-kha lo ding hi | my father Saul will not lay a hand on you/a ~-kha peuhmah kithat ding hi | anyone who harms them shall be put to death/sa leh silngo sawhloh mohte ~ hi | he touched the meat and the unleavened bread) (s:lawng/sukha) (r:23.6.7/18.5.19/9.23.17/1.26.11/7.6.21) (q:draft)
su = (t:v) (w:attack/strike/seize) (d:also the first part of compounds of forceful action such as su-tat cut off) (e:amaute ka ~ ding a/Na khut in na galte khempeuh ~ ding a | your hand will seize all your enemies/amah in amaute khetul ~ ding hi | he will attack them at their heels/tuate in nang hong ~ a | these things strike you/Topa mahmah in note hong ~ ding a | the Lord himself will strike you) (s:sim) (r:30.9.2/18.18.12/19.21.8/1.49.19/18.4.5/38.2.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
su = (t:v) (w:pound/crush/knead) (d:pound grain in a mortar, also work dough) (e:sum sungah ~-in, beel-in huan uh a/vantung kumpinu’ ading tangho a ~ uh a | they knead bread for the Queen of Heaven) (r:4.11.8/24.7.18) (q:draft, low confidence)
suah = (t:v) (w:be born/give birth) (d:form of suak used before ciangin, hun and other dependent endings) (e:A tapa Isaak a ~ ciangin/a ~ hun tung a | the time of the birth came/Tua nu a ~ hun a tun’ ciangin | when the time came for the woman to give birth/Ishmael a ~ ciangin | when Ishmael was born/keel khat a ~ ciangin | when a goat is born) (s:pian) (a:sih) (r:1.21.5/42.1.57/42.2.6/1.38.27/1.16.16/3.22.27) (q:draft)
suah = (t:v) (w:become) (d:form of suak used before ciangin, nadingin and other dependent endings) (e:sila khat kumpi a ~ ciang/a hau mahmah a ~ matengin | until he became very rich/mikhat ~ ding amau thukim uh hi | they agree to become one people) (r:20.30.22/58.2.17/1.26.13/1.34.22) (q:draft)
suah = (t:v) (w:shed/bring out) (d:cause to come out; sisan suah is to shed blood) (e:mi sisan ~ dingin a manlang hi/sisan ~ dongin na thuak nai kei uh | you have not yet resisted to the point of shedding blood) (s:luangsak) (r:45.3.15/58.12.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
suah = (t:part) (d:used in fractions between the number of parts and the part taken, as in seh-sawm-suah-seh-khat one tenth) (e:seu khat seh-sawm-~-seh-khat ahi hi/na khempeuh seh-sawm-~-seh-khat ama' tungah pia hi | he gave him a tenth of everything/seh-nga-~-seh-khat na pia ding uh | you shall give a fifth/na tuuhonte uh seh-sawm-~-seh-khat la ding a | he will take a tenth of your flocks) (r:2.16.36/1.14.20/1.47.24/9.8.17) (q:draft, low confidence)
suahhun = (t:n) (w:time of birth/time to give birth) (d:suah be born or give birth, with hun time) (e:a ta a ~ a tun ciangin) (r:43.16.21) (q:draft)
suahin = (t:v) (w:making into/dividing into) (d:suah with in, after a number of parts or groups, turning something into that many) (e:pawlthum ~ gamlakah pangsim uh hi/seh li ~ seh khat ciatin a hawm uh a | dividing them into four shares, they shared out one each/paisuk paito-in khen sagih ~ | going up and down and dividing it into seven parts/seh sawm-le-seh-nih ~ sem a | cutting her into twelve parts/eite pawlkhat hong ~ a hong kilemsak hi | making us one, he made peace) (b:suah) (r:7.9.43/7.19.29/43.19.23/6.18.9/49.2.15) (q:draft)
suahin = (t:v) (w:taking off/removing) (d:of clothing, taking it off before the next action) (e:a puanza ~ dial tawh a kawng/a puante ~ puan dang silh ding a | he shall take off his clothes and put on others/Elijah in a puantualpi ~ zial a | Elijah took off his cloak and rolled it up/a silh saihadial puante ~ | taking off the linen garments he had put on) (a:silhin) (r:43.13.4/3.16.23/3.6.11/12.2.8) (q:draft)
suahkhak = (t:v) (w:turn out to be/happen to become/prove) (d:suak become with kha, happen to: become something that was not intended; mostly in a suahkhak loh nadingin, so that it may not turn out to be) (e:thangzak a ~ loh nadingin/a mawkna a ~ loh nadingin | so that it may not prove empty/mi kiphasakte a ~ loh nading | so that they do not become proud people/sila na ~ loh nadingun kingaihsun un | take care that you do not end up as slaves) (s:suakkha) (r:2.34.12/48.4.11/47.9.3/18.33.17/51.2.8) (q:draft)
suahkhia = (t:v) (w:take off/strip off/remove) (d:take off clothes, sandals or ornaments) (e:Zeisu puan ~ uh a/na khe panin na khedapte ~ in | take your sandals off your feet/amau’ kizepnate ~ uh hi | they took off their ornaments/ama tung panin Aaron puante ~ in la | take the garments of Aaron off him/amah in a khedap ~ hi | he took off his sandal) (a:silh) (b:suah) (r:40.27.28/2.33.6/2.3.5/4.20.26/8.4.8) (q:draft)
suahkhia = (t:v) (w:bring out/take out/bring to light) (d:bring something out from where it was kept or hidden; also pour out what is in the heart) (e:a kiphumcip nate hong ~ uh hi/ngun leh kham kizepnate leh puante hong ~-in | bringing out silver and gold jewelry and clothing/Ka lungsim sung ka ~ a | I pour out my soul) (s:paikhiatpih/pusuaksak) (a:seel) (b:suah) (r:18.28.11/1.24.53/19.42.4) (q:draft)
suahkhiapa = (t:n) (w:one who takes off) (d:suahkhia take off, with -pa for a man: the man who takes off his armour) (e:Galhiam a ~ bangin galhiam a kuahpa) (b:suahkhia) (r:11.20.11) (q:draft)
