suakcilte = (t:adj) (w:newborn/newly born) (d:suak be born with cil, just begun, and plural te) (e:Naungek ~ na bang unla) (r:60.2.2) (q:draft)
suakgawp = (t:v) (w:become utterly/be reduced to) (d:suak become with gawp, utterly, badly) (e:innsia losia ~ ding a) (b:suak) (r:24.51.37) (q:draft)
suakin = (t:v) (w:becoming/turning into) (d:suak with the linking ending in: become, and then) (e:tua mipa a hau ~/kumpipa a heh ~ | the king becoming angry/Moab mite David’ nasem ~ siah hong puak uh hi | the Moabites became servants of David and brought tribute/Izipt gam khempeuhah leivui nel ~ | becoming fine dust over all the land of Egypt/a kha mahmah an ~ | turning into very bitter food) (b:suak) (r:1.26.13/18.20.14/10.11.20/13.18.2/2.9.9) (q:draft)
suakin = (t:v) (w:rising/coming out) (d:of the sun, rising) (e:Ni hong ~ ni tum a/A tung panin ni ~ eite kiangah hong tang ding | the sun will rise from on high and shine on us) (b:suak) (r:21.1.5/42.1.79) (q:draft)
suakkha = (t:v) (w:become/turn out to be/end up as) (d:suak, become, with kha, happen to: come to be something without meaning to) (e:kuama ten lohna gam simtham na ~ ding/ka gimnate a mawkna ~ ding hi | my labor will turn out to be in vain/Numei tawh a mawh mite ~ kei unla | do not become sexually immoral people/kote’ nasepna a mawkna ~ ding hi | our work would turn out to be in vain) (s:suahkhak/hikha) (r:24.6.8/58.12.16/18.39.16/52.3.5) (q:draft)
suakkhawm = (t:v) (w:become together/become one) (d:suak become with khawm, together) (e:honkhat ~ ding uh hi) (b:suak) (r:43.10.16) (q:draft)
suakkhia = (t:v) (w:come out/come forth/break out/be born) (d:suak with khia, out: said of a child at birth, of flames, of a disease on the skin, of light rising) (e:a kam panin meikuang ~ hi/Jakob sung pan aksi khat hong ~ ding a | a star will come out of Jacob/ama taltang ah phaknatna hong ~ hi | leprosy broke out on his forehead/a gil sung panin ~ sese ka hi hiam | why did I ever come out of the womb) (s:piangkhia/pusuak) (b:suak) (r:18.41.21/1.25.26/4.24.17/14.26.19/24.20.18) (q:draft)
suakkhiasak = (t:v) (w:bring forth/bring out/issue) (d:cause to come out: give birth to young, or issue an order) (e:a kikhah sakhipi hi a, sakhino ~ hi/Susa khuapi sungah hih thu ~ a | this decree was issued in Susa/nau a ~ keimah in naugil khakcip ding | shall I who bring to birth close the womb/bangmah ka ~ kei uh a | we have brought forth nothing) (s:pusuaksak) (b:suakkhia) (r:1.49.21/17.9.14/23.66.9/23.26.18) (q:draft)
suakkhin = (t:v) (w:have become/become wholly) (d:suak, become, with khin, already or completely) (e:Pumpi khempeuh mit ~ leh/kei a dingin vangikpi khat ~ a | they have become a burden to me/amau’ gam pen gam simtham ~ ahih manin | because their land has become a wasteland/Ka tanute uh pawlkhat zong sal ~ a | some of our daughters have already become slaves) (s:hikhin) (b:suak) (r:46.12.17/23.63.19/23.1.14/24.25.38/16.5.5) (q:draft)
suakkhin = (t:v) (w:have been born/be already born) (d:suak, be born, with khin, already) (e:Tuipite a om ma-in kei ka ~ a/leitung a pianin nang ~ na hih teh | since you were already born when the earth was made) (b:suak) (r:20.8.24/20.8.25/18.38.21) (q:draft)
suakkik = (t:v) (w:reform/turn back into/return to) (d:suak, become, with kik, again: become again what one was before) (e:mihingte, leivui ~ ding hi/ama' khut sungah ciangkhut ~ hi | it became a staff again in his hand/leivui mah ~ ding uh hi | they will return to dust) (b:suak) (r:18.34.15/2.4.4/21.3.20) return into previous status
suaklua = (t:v) (w:be very sleepy/be overcome) (d:with lua, too much; ihmut suaklua, sleepiness coming on too strongly) (e:a ihmut uh ~ mahmah ahih manin) (b:suak) (r:40.26.43) (q:draft, low confidence)
suakmangkhin = (t:v) (w:become completely/turn wholly into) (d:suak, become, with mang, away or utterly, and khin, completely) (e:leivui ~ ding hi/nek dingin a kiman ganhing ~ uh a | they have wholly become prey caught to be eaten) (r:23.25.12/23.42.22) (q:draft)
suakmasa = (t:n) (w:firstborn/born first) (d:suak be born with masa first) (e:amaute a ~ a suah hun tawh) (s:tacil/naucil) (a:nautum) (r:1.43.33) (q:draft)
suakmawk = (t:v) (w:turn out to be/become) (d:suak, become, with mawk, which marks something unexpected or regrettable: turn out to be, become after all) (e:khat pen dawi na ~ uh hi) (r:43.6.70) (q:draft)
suakna = (t:n) (w:continuing/lasting) (d:suak, right through, with the noun suffix na: a going on without end; piak suakna is giving that continues forever) (e:ukna za a piak ~ ding) (b:suak) (r:14.21.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
suaknuam = (t:v) (w:want to become/wish to be) (d:suak, become, with nuam, want: wish to become something, such as a teacher) (e:note tampi sia na ~ se kei un) (r:59.3.1) (q:draft)
suakpa = (t:n) (w:man who becomes/one who has become) (d:suak, become, with pa for a man: the man who becomes something; mi nin a suakpa is the man who becomes unclean) (e:mi nin a ~ adingin ngeina ahi hi) (b:suak) (r:3.15.32) (q:draft)
suakpah = (t:v) (w:become at once/become immediately) (d:suak, become, with pah, at once: become something immediately) (e:ka han ~ ding hi) (r:24.20.17) (q:draft)
suakpak = (t:v) (w:become quickly/soon become) (d:suak, become, with pak, quickly: become something in a short time) (e:a sawt loin leivui a ~ ding) (r:18.20.11) (q:draft)
suaksa = (t:adj) (w:having become/become) (d:suak, become, with sa, already: having become; sal a suaksa are those who had become captives, the exiles, and a khu suaksa is smoldering) (e:sal a ~ hong ciahkik mite in/sal ~ mihonte panin | from the assembly of the exiles/A khu ~ meivak khau | a smoldering wick/sal a ~ hong ciahkik mi khempeuh | all the exiles who had returned) (b:suak) (r:15.6.19/40.12.20/15.10.8/15.6.16) (q:draft)
suaksak = (t:v) (w:make/cause to become/turn into) (d:suak, become, with the causative sak: make someone or something become what is named, as make a man king or turn a land into a waste) (e:gamkhing ka ~ ding a/Amah kumpi a ~ dingin | to make him king/sehnel gam pen bualtuite ~ a | he turned the desert into pools of water/amau gunte amah in sisan a ~ hi | he turned their rivers into blood/Abimelek kumpi ~ uh hi | they made Abimelech king) (s:hisak) (b:suak) (r:26.35.7/14.10.1/19.107.35/19.78.44/7.9.6) (q:draft)
suaksakin = (t:v) (w:making/turning into/causing to become) (d:suaksak, cause to become, with the linking suffix in: making something become, and then) (e:Leitung pen sehnel gam ~/uliante a mawkna ~ | bringing princes to nothing/khuamial pen khuavak ~ | turning darkness into light/sun pen zan ~ | turning day into night) (b:suaksak) (r:23.14.17/26.32.15/23.40.23/23.42.16/30.5.8) (q:draft)
suaksakkik = (t:v) (w:turn back into/make become again) (d:suaksak, cause to become, with kik, again or back: turn something back into what it was) (e:Mi, leivui na ~ a/tuipi tui pen, tuisiang ~ hi | it makes the sea water fresh again) (b:suaksak) (r:19.90.3/26.47.8) (q:draft)
suaksakpa = (t:n) (w:one who makes/one who turns into) (d:suaksak, cause to become or bring out, with pa for a man: he who makes something become, or who brings out) (e:aisante pen mihai a ~/leitung ukte pen bangmah lo a ~ | he who reduces the rulers of the world to nothing/gilsung panin kei hong ~ na hi hi | you are the one who brought me out of the womb) (b:suaksak) (r:23.44.25/19.22.9/23.40.23) (q:draft)
suaksakte = (t:n) (w:those who made/those who turned into) (d:suaksak, cause to become, with te, those who: the ones who made something become) (e:gamsate’ phualpi a ~ pen Assiria mite) (b:suaksak) (r:23.23.13) (q:draft)
suaksakzo = (t:v) (w:be able to make/can turn into) (d:suaksak, cause to become, with zo, be able: be able to make someone become something) (e:Khristian hong ~ dingin kingaihsun na hi hiam) (b:suaksak) (r:44.26.28) (q:draft)
suaksate = (t:n) (w:those who made/those who have become) (d:suaksa with te, those who; in the verse those who turned the city into a place for wild animals) (e:gamsate’ phualpi a ~ in) (b:suaksa) (r:23.23.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
suaksuak = (t:see) <suaksuak-in>
suaksuak-in = (t:adv) (w:right through/on and on) (d:suak through, doubled, with in; pai suaksuak, keep passing through) (e:dimlet-in pai ~) (r:23.8.8) (q:draft)
suakta = (t:v) (w:alive/survive/stay alive) (d:come through danger alive, be spared from death) (e:a ~ dingin nam khatah nih ciat/teembaw sunga a om teng bek ~ hi | only those in the ark survived/nangma’ hangin ka ~ thei kha ding hi | my life may be spared because of you/tua hi leh ka ~ ding hi | then my life will be spared) (a:si) (r:1.6.20/1.7.23/1.12.13/1.19.20)
suakta = (t:v) (w:escape/e emancipated/be liberated/be freed) (d:be set free or released from a bond, an oath, guilt or a master) (e:amah taikhia-in ~ hi/a pasal tawh a lencip thukham panin a ~ hi | she is released from the law that bound her to her husband/silate nangawn a topa’ kiangpan ~ hi | even the slave is free from his master/ka thuciamna panin nang na ~ ding hi | you will be released from my oath/Pasal in mawhna panin ~ ding a | the man will be free of guilt) (r:9.19.12/27.11.42/45.7.2/18.3.19/1.24.41/4.5.31)
suakta = (t:v) (w:escape) (d:get away safely from an enemy, a danger or a trap) (e:amah taikhia-in ~ hi/David tai-in ~ hi | David fled and escaped/Izipt nangawn zong a ~ kei ding hi | even Egypt will not escape/ka galte kiang panin ka ~ hi | I am saved from my enemies/thangzak panin vasa a suahtak bangin eite i ~ hi | we have escaped like a bird from the snare/mi khat zong ~ lo hi | not one man escaped) (s:peng/taikhia) (a:kiman) (r:9.19.12/27.11.42/9.19.10/19.18.3/19.124.7/7.3.29)
suakta = (t:v) (w:free/be free) (d:be free, not a slave; suakta-in paikhia is go out free, and a suakta mi is a free person) (e:bangmah pia loin ~-in amah paikhia/a ~-in ka paikhia kei ding hi | I will not go out free/nang kiang panin ~-in amah na paikhia sak ding hi | you shall let him go free from you/Na kiang panin a ~-in na paikhiat sak ciangin | when you send him away free from you/sal leh a ~ mi a kibangin | slave and free alike) (r:2.21.2/5.15.12/2.21.5/5.15.13/11.14.10)
suakta = (t:v) (w:get away/get out/run away/run off/break out/break free) (d:get away from a place or from someone who holds or pursues) (e:amah in a ~-in amah paikhia/Abiathar a kici khat ~-in David kiangah a tai hi | one named Abiathar escaped and fled to David/Israel giahphual panin kong ~ hi | I have escaped from the camp of Israel/ama khut sung panin ka ~ ding hi | I will slip out of his hand/Jerubbaal’ tapa neu pen Jotham ~ hi | Jotham, the youngest son of Jerubbaal, escaped) (s:taimang/taikhia) (r:9.24.19/9.22.20/10.1.3/9.27.1/7.9.5)
Suakta = (t:v) (w:be freed/free) (d:suakta written with a capital in Sal Suakta, the Freedmen, slaves who were set free) (e:Tua lai takin Sal ~ a kici mipawlte) (b:suakta) (r:44.6.9) (q:draft)
suaktak = (t:v) (w:be free/go free/escape) (d:form of suakta used before nading and zo; suaktak nading is freedom or release) (e:na mipihte ciat uh ~ nading tangko-in/amau’ nuntakna ciat bek mah ~ zo ding uh hi | they could save only their own lives) (b:suakta) (r:24.34.15/26.14.14) (q:draft)
suaktakha = (t:v) (w:happen to escape/survive) (d:suakta, escape, with kha, happen to: happen to escape; a suaktakha are those who have survived) (e:a ~ sunsunte nangawn/a ~ a omlaite keimah in ka that ding hi | I will kill those who happen to survive) (r:26.5.10/23.14.30) (q:draft)
suaktakik = (t:v) (w:go free again/be released) (d:suakta, be freed, with kik, back or again: go free again, said of a vowed person redeemed by payment) (e:kitanh-in ~ thei ding hi) (b:suakta) (r:3.27.2) (q:draft)
suaktalai = (t:v) (w:survive/remain/be left) (d:suakta, escape or stay alive, with lai, still: be still left alive; a suaktalai is the remnant) (e:seh khat bek ~ ding hi/Judah minam sung panin a ~ mite in | the remnant from the people of Judah/tu-in a ~ hih minamte | now the remnant of this people/Minamte sung panin a ~ note aw | you survivors from the nations) (s:nungtalai) (r:38.13.8/23.37.31/38.8.11/23.45.20) (q:draft)
suaktasak = (t:v) (w:set free/free/deliver/spare) (d:suakta, be free or escape, with the causative sak: set someone free, let someone escape or spare a life) (e:kei hong ~ in/tua thuman thutak in note hong ~ ding hi | the truth will set you free/note ka hong ~ ding hi | I will set you free/migilote kiang panin amaute honin ~ hi | he delivers them from the wicked and saves them/amaute khat zong ~ kei un | do not let one of them escape) (s:honkhia/khah) (a:khum/man) (b:suakta) (r:19.119.154/43.8.32/38.9.11/19.37.40/11.18.40) (q:draft)
suaktasakin = (t:v) (w:setting free/freeing) (d:suaktasak, set free, with the linking suffix in: setting free and then doing the next action) (e:sila ~ paikhiasak ding hi) (b:suaktasak) (r:2.21.26/2.21.27) (q:draft)
suaktasakpa = (t:n) (w:one who lets escape/one who sets free) (d:suaktasak, set free or let escape, with pa for a man: the one who lets someone escape) (e:khat peuhpeuh a ~ in ama nuntakna) (b:suaktasak) (r:12.10.24) (q:draft)
suaktasun = (t:adj) (w:surviving/escaped) (d:suakta, escape, with sun, only those that: a suaktasun mite are those who survive) (e:A ~ mite in lungdamin la sa) (s:hinglai) (r:23.24.14) (q:draft)
suaktate = (t:n) (w:survivors/remnant) (d:those who escaped or are left alive) (e:khuapi sunga a ~ kisusia ding/Refaim panin a ~ lakah khat | one of the last of the Rephaites) (s:omlaite/omsuakte/laisunte) (b:suakta) (r:4.24.19/6.12.4) (q:draft)
suaktate = (t:n) (w:free people) (d:suakta, be free, with the plural te: those who are free) (e:~ taktak na hi ding uh hi/mi ~ hi khinta ihih manin | because we have become free people) (a:silate) (b:suakta) (r:43.8.36/48.5.1) (q:draft)
suaktazo = (t:v) (w:escape/survive) (d:suakta, escape, with zo, manage to: manage to escape or come through alive) (e:Sihna hankhuk panin kua ~ ahi hiam/a ~ kuamah om lo ding hi | no one would survive/a ~ khat beek a om kei hi | not one escaped/Tua bangin a gamtatna tawh ~ ding ahi hiam | will he who does such things escape) (s:nungtazo) (b:suakta) (r:19.89.48/41.13.20/25.2.22/26.17.15) (q:draft)
suakte = (t:n) (w:those born/children born) (d:suak, be born or come out, with plural te: the ones who are born) (e:Mihing sung panin a ~ mihing mah/numei sung pan a ~ lakah | among those born of women/Kha tawh a ~ pen kha mi ahi hi | those born of the Spirit are spirit/Jerusalem ah ama sung panin a ~’ min in | the names of those born to him in Jerusalem) (b:suak) (r:43.3.6/10.5.14/42.7.28) (q:draft)
suakte = (t:n) (w:women in labor/those giving birth) (d:with nau, child: nau suakte are women giving birth, women in labor) (e:Numei nau ~ in na a sak) (b:suak) (r:24.13.21) (q:draft, low confidence)
suakthei = (t:v) (w:can become/be able to become) (d:suak, become, with thei, be able: can become) (e:thu um mi ~ ding a/a tate uh thu um mi ~ lo ding uh hi | their children could not become believers) (b:suak) (r:46.7.14) (q:draft)
suakto = (t:v) (w:rise up/go up) (d:suak, come out, with to, upward; said of smoke rising from a city) (e:meikhu khuapi sung panin ~ dingin) (s:kahto) (b:suak) (r:7.20.40) (q:draft)
suaktungte = (t:n) (w:new converts/those who have just become) (d:suak, become, with tung, newly, and te, those who: those who have just become something, new converts) (e:Khristian a ~ zong hi lo ding) (r:54.3.6) (q:draft)
suakvat = (t:v) (w:become suddenly) (d:suak, become, with vat, suddenly: become something all at once) (e:kumpi a hong ~ ding hi) (r:27.11.21) (q:draft)
suakzo = (t:v) (w:become/turn out) (d:suak, become, with zo, which marks the change as complete: has become) (e:a mawkna ~ ta hi/mite’ nuihsat ding le lipkhap ding a ~ hi | has become an object of ridicule and horror to people) (b:suak) (r:24.2.30/24.48.39) (q:draft)
sual = (t:n) (w:floor) (d:floor of a building; ancilna sual is a threshing floor, and sual puan is a rug spread on the floor) (e:a ~ panin a innsun ciang dong/biakbuk ~ tunga om leivui | dust on the tabernacle floor/taaksan peekte tawh inn ~ tuam hi | he covered the floor of the house with juniper planks/~ tungah a topa uh na si hi | their lord lay dead on the floor) (a:innsun) (r:11.7.7/26.41.16/4.5.17/11.6.15/7.3.25) (q:draft)
sualphah = (t:n) (w:rug/mat/blanket) (d:something spread on the floor; sualphah puan is a rug, carpet or saddle blanket) (e:~ puan khat tawh amah khuh hi/~ puan hoih tungah a tute | you who sit on fine saddle blankets/a kizem puante, ~ puante | embroidered cloth and rugs) (r:7.4.18/26.27.24/7.5.10) (q:draft)
sualpuante = (t:n) (w:rugs/carpets) (d:sual, floor, with puan, cloth, and the plural te: rugs spread on the floor) (e:sabuai phahin, ~ phah uh a) (r:23.21.5) (q:draft)
sualsual = (t:adv) (d:placed after gingsak, make a sound, it describes a repeated tinkling or jingling, here of ornaments on the feet) (e:a khe uh tawh gingsak ~) (r:23.3.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
sualte = (t:n) (w:floors) (d:sual, floor, with the plural te) (e:inn ~ amah in kham tawh zut hi) (s:innsualte) (b:sual) (r:11.6.30) (q:draft)
suam = (t:v) (w:attack/assault/waylay/ambush) (d:fall on someone by force or from hiding in order to kill or rob; mi suam is used for an uprising and a suamte for the attackers) (e:nang hong ~ dingin Nethaniah’ tapa Ishmael/lamkalah migilote in na ~ a | robbers attacked him on the way/Mi ~ a, mi a thah maninah | for insurrection and murder/nidang lai-inah mi ~ ding hansuahin | who some time ago stirred up a revolt/Mi ommuang khat va muan ~ ni | let us ambush some harmless person) (r:24.40.14/42.23.25/42.10.30/44.21.38/20.1.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
suamin = (t:v) (w:attacking/assaulting) (d:suam, attack, with the linking suffix in; mi suamin thongkia is one in prison for attacking people) (e:Barabbas pen mi ~ thongkia khat ahi hi) (b:suam) (r:43.18.40) (q:draft)
suamlum = (t:v) (w:murder/kill/slay) (d:suam, attack or waylay, with lum as in thatlum: attack and kill) (e:pa nei lote ~ uh hi) (s:thatlum) (r:19.94.6/24.41.18) (q:draft)
suamte = (t:n) (w:bandits/robbers/attackers) (d:suam, attack or waylay, with plural te: those who fall on people by force) (e:gun galkah kihtakna, mi ~ kihtakna/a ~ tuili gampa lakah a paipih | who led the terrorists out into the wilderness) (s:misuamte/buluhte) (b:suam) (r:47.11.26/44.21.38) (q:draft)
suan = (t:n) (w:descendant/offspring/seed) (d:one who descends from an ancestor, or the descendants as a group; often in the pair suan leh khak, descendants) (e:Abraham ~ leh khakte na hi uh/Josef ~ Manasseh, leh Efraim mite | Manasseh and Ephraim, the descendants of Joseph/Aaron’ ~ khempeuh in a kikim-in hawm ding uh hi | all the sons of Aaron shall share it equally/Anak’ ~ leh khakte tua lai-ah ka mu uh hi | we saw the descendants of Anak there) (s:suanlekhak) (a:pu/pupa) (r:48.3.29/18.18.19/6.16.4/3.7.10/4.13.28) (q:draft)
suan = (t:v) (w:plant) (d:put a tree or plant in the ground to grow; also said of God planting his people in a land) (e:Be-ersheba-ah makeng kung khat ~ a/kung nam khempeuh na ~ uh ciangin | when you plant any kind of tree/nangma' mual tungah amaute na ~ ding a | you will plant them on your mountain/lei hoih mun khatah ~ hi | he planted it in good soil) (s:cin) (a:bot/botkhia) (r:1.21.33/3.19.23/2.15.17/26.17.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
suang = (t:prep) (w:in)
suang = (t:adv) (w:inside)
suanga = (t:v) (w:relying on/invoking) (d:suang, lean on, with the linking a: taking something as one's ground or authority; min suanga is in the name of) (e:kei’ min ~ thu a gen kamsangte) (r:24.14.15/24.17.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
suangah = (t:phrase) (w:in settings/in mountings) (d:with the place marker ah; kham tawh zepna suangah, in the gold settings in which the stones were mounted) (e:kham tawh zepna ~ tuate kikoih hi) (r:2.39.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
suangatna = (t:n) (w:stone saw) (d:suang, stone, with at, cut, and the noun suffix na: a tool for cutting stone) (e:a mai ~ tawh a ki-at) (r:11.7.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
