suanghawm = (t:n) (w:cave/cleft in the rock/rock hollow) (d:suang, stone, with hawm, hollow: a hollow place in rock, a cave or cleft) (e:~ sungah nang kong koih ding a/amah paisukin Etam ~ sungah om hi | he went down and stayed in the cave of Etam/~ sung leh leihawm sungah mite bu ding uh hi | people will hide in caves in the rocks and holes in the ground/a tanu nihte tawh ~ sung khatah teng uh hi | he lived in a cave with his two daughters) (r:2.33.22/7.15.8/23.2.19/1.19.30) (q:draft)
suanghawmah = (t:n) (w:to the cave/in the cave) (d:suanghawm, cave, with the place marker ah) (e:Etam ~ paisukin Samson kiangah) (b:suanghawm) (r:7.15.11) (q:draft)
