suangphah = (t:n) (w:pavement/stone floor) (d:suang, stone, with phah, spread: a floor or court laid with stones) (e:Faro kumpi inn lutna ~ nuaiah phum in/~ tungah lei lam maingatin kun uh a | they bowed on the pavement with their faces to the ground/Hih ~ pen a tual kimkotah om a | this pavement ran all around the court/a kizeem ~ kiphah tungah | on a decorated pavement) (s:suangphahpek) (r:24.43.9/43.19.13/14.7.3/26.40.18/17.1.6) (q:draft)
suangphahpek = (t:n) (w:pavement/paved stone floor) (d:flat stones laid as a floor) (e:tawh a kibawl ~ bang pian om) (s:suangphah) (r:2.24.10) (q:draft)
Suangphahpek = (t:n) (w:stone pavement) (d:a floor laid with flat stones; here the place called Gabbatha) (e:Gabbatha a kici ~ tunga thukhenna tokhom) (b:suangphahpek) (r:43.19.13) (q:draft)
