suankhia = (t:v) (w:drive out/dispossess/supplant) (d:take the place of a people by driving them out of their land; suan with khia, out) (e:tua sunga om Amor mite ~ uh hi/a thahat zaw minamte na ~ ding uh hi | you will dispossess nations stronger than you/tua mite ~-in tuni dongin amau’ mun-ah teeng uh hi | they drove those people out and live in their place to this day/amaute ~-in amau’ leitangah na teen’ uh ciangin | when you have driven them out and settled in their land) (s:hawlkhia/nawtkhia) (r:4.32.39/5.11.23/5.2.22/5.12.29) (q:draft)
suankhiat = (t:v) (w:drive out/dispossess) (d:form of suankhia, drive out and take the place of, used before ding and theih) (e:amaute bangci ~ theih ding i hi hiam/Na ~ ding uh minamte | the nations you are going to dispossess/a leitang na luah theih nadingin ~ ding kipan in | begin to drive him out so that you may possess his land/amah ~ ding kipan in la | begin to drive him out) (s:hawlkhiat) (b:suankhia) (r:5.7.17/5.12.2/5.2.31/5.2.24) (q:draft)
suankhiatna = (t:n) (w:driving out/displacing) (d:suankhiat, drive out, with the noun suffix na: the act or the place of driving something out and taking its place) (e:thuman thutang a ~ zong ka mu hi) (s:hawlkhiatna) (b:suankhiat) (r:21.3.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
suankhiatte = (t:n) (w:those driven out) (d:suankhiat, drive out, with the plural te: the peoples whom God has driven out, whose land is then possessed) (e:kote mai-ah a ~ kote in) (s:hawlkhiatte) (b:suankhiat) (r:7.11.24) (q:draft)
suankik = (t:v) (w:plant again/replant) (d:suan, plant, with kik, again: plant once more, or plant in a new place) (e:leenggah na ~ ding a/leenggui ci hoihte bangin nang kong ~ zo a | I planted you like a vine of good stock/a ~ hun hong tun’ ding | the time for planting again will come) (b:suan) (r:24.31.5/30.9.13/24.2.21) (q:draft)
