sumbawlin = (t:v) (w:trading/doing business) (d:sumbawl do business, trade, from sum money and bawl make, with the linking ending in) (e:minam khempeuh tawh ~ na kizom uh hi/kum khat tawntung omin ~ | staying a whole year and doing business/Tua khuapi sungah ~ a hauhlawh mite | those who grew rich by trading in that city) (b:sumbawl) (r:23.23.3/59.4.13/66.18.15) (q:draft)
sumbawlna = (t:n) (w:trade/commerce/business) (d:sum bawl, make money, with na: trading, and the place of trade) (e:Na ~ teng uh maimang khinta hi/leitung kumpigam khempeuh tawh kizomin ~ sem ding hi | she will trade with all the kingdoms of the earth) (s:sumbawl) (b:sumbawl) (r:23.23.10/23.23.17) (q:draft)
sumbawlpa = (t:n) (w:merchant/trader) (d:sumbawl trade with pa, a man: a man who trades) (e:~ in a zon kep hoihpente) (s:zuakpa) (b:sumbawl) (r:40.13.45/40.13.46) (q:draft)
sumbawlte = (t:n) (w:merchants/traders) (d:plural, people who make money by buying and selling) (e:kumpipa’ ~ in Kue panin/ama ~ leitungah a kipahtawite ahi | her traders are honoured in the earth/~ omna gamah pua-in | carrying it to a land of merchants) (s:sumbukte) (b:sumbawl) (r:11.10.28/26.17.4/23.23.8) (q:draft)
sumbawm = (t:n) (w:purse/money bag/bag) (d:a bag in which money or gold is carried) (e:~ panin khamte uang zatin/Note in ~, ip, le khedap keng loin | you carried no purse, bag or sandals) (s:khutkhai) (r:23.46.6/42.22.36/42.22.35) (q:draft)
sumbuk = (t:n) (w:market/marketplace) (d:place of buying and selling; sumbuk vante is merchandise, sumbuk bawlte are traders) (e:nasem loin ~ ah a ding mawkte/~ ah zahtakna tawh hopihna | respectful greetings in the marketplace/Na ~ vante tuipi tungah a pai ciangin | when your merchandise went out on the seas/khua ukte mai-a ~ lamah a paipih uh hi | they took them to the marketplace before the rulers) (s:sumzuakna/vanzuakna) (r:40.20.3/44.17.17/42.11.43/26.27.33/44.16.19) (q:draft)
Sumbuk = (t:n) (w:market/marketplace/forum) (d:sumbuk written with a capital, at the start of a sentence and in the place name Appias Sumbuk, the Forum of Appius) (e:kimkhatte in Appias ~ dongin/~ panin hong ciah uh ciangin | when they come back from the marketplace/~ ah zahtakna tawh hopihna | respectful greetings in the marketplace) (b:sumbuk) (r:44.28.15/41.7.4/41.12.39) (q:draft)
sumbuka = (t:n) (w:in the market/of the market) (d:sumbuk market with a, in or of) (e:~ kizuak khempeuh teldot loin/~ tangvalte a vatlum hi | it cuts down the young men in the public squares) (b:sumbuk) (r:46.10.25/24.9.21) (q:draft)
sumbukah = (t:adv) (w:in the marketplace/at the market) (d:sumbuk marketplace with the place marker ah) (e:~ zahtakna tawh hopih ahi zongin/mihon omna ~ pai leuleu a | he went again to the marketplace where the people were/pawlkhat in a ~ na paisanin | another went off to his business/mihon omna ~ a pai leh | when he went to the marketplace) (b:sumbuk) (r:40.23.7/40.20.3/40.22.5/40.20.6) (q:draft)
sumbukte = (t:n) (w:merchants/traders) (d:sumbuk, market, with the plural te: the people of the market, merchants) (e:~ tungah tuate zuak hi/Leitungah a om ~ in zong | the merchants of the earth also/khamseekte leh ~ in | the goldsmiths and the merchants/~ leh na nam tuamtuam a zuakte | merchants and sellers of all kinds of goods) (s:sumbawlte) (b:sumbuk) (r:20.31.24/66.18.11/16.3.32/16.13.20) (q:draft)
Sumdeihna = (t:n) (w:love of money) (d:sum money with deihna desire) (e:~ lungsim na neih leh lungkim hun) (r:21.5.10) (q:draft)
sumdek = (t:v) (w:bargain/haggle) (d:beat down a price; sumdek siam is good at bargaining) (e:~ siam mahmah ing) (r:20.20.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
Sumduh = (t:v) (w:crave money/love money) (d:sum money with duh crave; sumduh luatna is too great a love of money) (e:~ luatna tawh na kipelh un) (r:58.13.5) (q:draft)
sumgolh = (t:n) (w:bribe) (d:money or a gift given to turn a judgment) (e:mimawhte ~ tawh khah a/A ginalo thukhente in ~ sang sim uh a | corrupt judges accept bribes in secret/amaute in ~ la-in thuman heikhia uh hi | they took bribes and perverted justice/~ a deih lote a nuntak sauvei nuam hi | those who do not want bribes will live long) (s:golhguk) (r:23.5.23/20.17.23/9.8.3/20.15.27) (q:draft)
sumgu = (t:v) (w:steal money/steal) (d:sum money with gu steal; mi sumgu mi is a thief) (e:mi ~ mi bang ahi zongin) (r:60.4.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
sumgum = (t:n) (w:treasure/money) (d:money or wealth that is laid up; in Deuteronomy 23.19 money that is lent) (e:Topa kihtakna pen ama ~ hi ding hi/a meetin, ~ hita leh, ankhing hita leh | at interest, whether money or food) (r:23.33.6/5.23.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
sumh = (t:v) (w:lose/suffer loss) (d:be left without something one had, as animals that die or a slave who dies) (e:ganhingte pawlkhat i ~ kei ding hi) (a:ngah) (r:11.18.5/2.21.21) (q:draft)
sumhau = (t:adj) (w:rich/wealthy) (d:having much money, from sum money and hau rich) (e:~ mite in Pasian’ Gam sungah lut/~ na inn veengte ahi zongin | or your rich neighbours/upa, naupang, ~, mizawng, sila | great and small, rich and poor, slave) (s:hau/sumnei) (a:zawng) (r:42.18.25/59.1.10/42.14.12/66.13.16) (q:draft)
sumhaupa = (t:n) (w:rich/rich man) (d:sumhau, rich, with pa marking a man: a rich man) (e:Nidang lai-inah ~ khat a om hi) (s:mihaupa) (a:mizawngpa) (b:sumhau) (r:42.16.19)
sumhaupa = (t:n) (w:wealthy/wealthy man) (e:~’ kongbiang kiangah | at the gate of the rich man) (b:sumhau) (r:42.16.20)
sumhaupa = (t:n) (w:cash rich) (b:sumhau)
sumhaute = (t:n) (w:the rich/rich people) (e:~ in sumkholna sungah sum a khiat/~ in Vantung Gam sung lut nading | for the rich to enter the kingdom of heaven/galkap mangte, ~, thahatte, silate | the generals, the rich, the mighty, the slaves) (s:mihaute/haute) (a:mizawngte) (b:sumhau) (r:42.21.1/66.6.15/40.19.23) (q:draft)
sumin = (t:adv) (w:for money/with money) (d:sum money with the marker in) (e:~ amah zuak loin) (b:sum) (r:5.21.14) (q:draft)
sumit = (t:v) (w:put out/extinguish/snuff out) (d:make a lamp or fire go out) (e:kongkhakte zong khakin meivakte ~ uh a/A khu suaksa meivak khau a ~ kei ding hi | he will not snuff out a smoldering wick/meivak taangte ka ~ ding hi | I will put out the light of the lamps/a mawhna uh ~ kei in | do not blot out their sin) (s:sukmit/mitsak/phelh) (a:kuangsak) (r:14.29.7/40.12.20/24.25.10/16.4.5) (q:draft)
sumkeempa = (t:n) (w:steward/foreman/paymaster) (d:sum money with keem keep and pa man, the man who keeps the money and pays the workers) (e:~ kiangah thu a pia hi) (s:sumkempa) (r:40.20.8) (q:draft)
sumkem = (t:n) (w:treasurer/keeper of money) (d:one who keeps the money of a group, a king or a city; sum, money, with kem, keep) (e:amah ~ ahih manin a sumte gu-in/Amah ~ ahih manin | since he had charge of the money/gam ukpi huhte, mangpite, ~ mangte, thukhen mangte | prefects, governors, treasurers, judges/Ka omna khuapi ~ pa Erastas | Erastus, the treasurer of the city where I am) (s:sumkempa) (r:43.12.6/15.1.8/43.13.29/27.3.2/45.16.23) (q:draft)
sumkempa = (t:n) (w:treasurer/steward/manager) (d:a man who keeps and manages the money or goods of his master; pa marks a man) (e:~ Mithredath’ khut sungah ap hi/Sumhaupa khat in ~ khat a nei hi | a rich man had a manager/Thuman lo ~ in pilna tawh ahih ciangin | because the dishonest manager had acted shrewdly/A topa in ~ sam a | his master called the manager) (s:sumkeempa) (b:sumkem) (r:15.1.8/42.16.1/42.16.8/42.16.2) (q:draft)
sumkep = (t:n) (w:stewardship/management of money) (d:the keeping of another person's money and goods; sum, money, with kep, keep) (e:Na ~ ciamtehna lai hong pia in/~ na nasem nawn kei ding hi | you will no longer do the work of manager/ka topa in ~ za panin hong kiasak | my master is removing me from the post of manager) (s:Sumkepna) (r:42.16.2/42.16.3) (q:draft)
Sumkepna = (t:n) (w:stewardship/management of money) (d:sum money with kepna keeping; sumkepna za is the post of manager) (e:~ za hong kiatsak khit ciangin) (s:sumkep) (r:42.16.4) (q:draft)
sumkheekte = (t:n) (w:money changers) (d:sum money with kheek exchange and the plural te) (e:a zuakte leh ~ tu-a om/~’ dangkate bua-in | scattering the coins of the money changers) (s:sumkhekte) (r:43.2.14/43.2.15) (q:draft)
sumkhek = (t:v) (w:exchange/change money) (d:change money of one kind for another; sumkhek nasem mite are the money changers) (e:~ nasemin a om) (r:40.21.12) of currency
Sumkhek = (t:v) (w:exchange money) (d:sum money with khek change; sumkhek nasem mite are the money changers) (e:~ nasemin a om mite’ sabuai) (b:sumkhek) (r:40.21.12) (q:draft)
