sumkhotte = (t:n) (w:money/proceeds) (d:the money a person has got, in this verse the money from selling possessions; a plural form with te) (e:mizawngte tungah na ~ va pia in) (s:sumte) (r:41.10.21) (q:draft, low confidence)
sumkoihna = (t:n) (w:treasury/storehouse) (d:sum, money, with koihna, a place for keeping: the treasury or storehouse where money and valuables are kept) (e:~-ah tuate tung ding hi/inn-a ~-ah koih uh hi | they put them in the treasury of the house/biakinn ~ sungah ka koih hi | I put it in the temple treasury/na manpha a matte ~ inn-ah a koih hi | he put the captured valuables in the treasure house) (s:sumkholna/vankoihna/sumkuang) (r:6.6.19/38.11.13/6.6.24/27.1.2) (q:draft)
sumkoihnate = (t:n) (w:treasuries/storehouses) (d:sumkoihna, treasury, with the plural te: the places where money and valuables are kept) (e:kumpipa’ ~ ah a om kham khempeuh | all the gold in the treasuries of the king) (s:vankoihnate) (b:sumkoihna) (r:12.12.18) (q:draft)
sumkuang = (t:n) (w:treasury/offering chest/money box) (d:sum, money, with kuang, chest or trough: the chest into which money offerings are put; biakinn sumkuang is the temple treasury) (e:biakinn ~ sungah a letsong uh) (s:sumkholna/sumkoihna) (r:42.21.1) (q:draft)
sumkuangte = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:doves/turtledoves) (d:a migrating bird, plural; named where the NIV has dove, swift and thrush, so the exact bird is not certain) (e:~, phialphiahte leh gun vapite) (r:24.8.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
sumlakte = (t:n) (w:money received/money collected) (d:sum money with lak take and the plural te, the sums of money that someone takes in) (e:na ~ uh kem nawn kei unla) (r:12.12.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
sumlei = (t:v) (w:buy) (d:buy with money, mostly in the pair sumlei sumzuak, buying and selling) (e:~ sumzuak nasepna in/~ sumzuak, lokho, inn lamin | buying and selling, planting and building/nang tawh ~ sumzuakna-ah kizopna hong nei uh hi | they had trade relations with you/tua sungah sumzuak ~-a a omte | those who were selling and buying in it) (s:vanlei) (a:sumzuak) (r:26.7.12/42.17.28/26.27.23/41.11.15) of currency
sumleina = (t:n) (w:buying) (d:sumlei buy with the noun suffix na; sumzuak sumleina mun is the place of selling and buying, the market) (e:sumzuak ~ mun panin kisukcipna) (s:leina) (a:sumzuakna) (b:sumlei) (r:19.55.11) (q:draft)
sumleite = (t:n) (w:buyers) (d:sumlei buy with the plural te, those who buy) (e:sumzuakte leh ~ khempeuh hawlkhia in/~ in bangmah nei lo mah bang ding uh | buyers should be as though they owned nothing) (s:leite/vanleite) (a:sumzuakte) (b:sumlei) (r:40.21.12/46.7.31) (q:draft)
sumlepai = (t:n) (w:money/wealth/money and goods) (d:sum le pai, money and goods: money, wealth or payment; sumlepai vai is money matters) (e:Amah in ~ sang nuam vet lo a/Judah kumpite’ ~ khempeuhte | all the treasures of the kings of Judah/i suah laitakin ~ tawh i suak kei a | we were not born with money/annek tuidawn ~ vai-ah kong manlah ding uh | for us to be busy with food and money matters) (s:sum/neihsa) (r:20.6.35/54.6.7/24.20.5/44.6.2) (q:draft)
sumlepaite = (t:n) (w:possessions/money and goods) (d:sumlepai, money and goods, with the plural te: the things a person owns) (e:note’ ~ hi loin note mahmah) (s:neihsate) (b:sumlepai) (r:47.12.14) (q:draft)
