summet = (t:n) (w:profit/gain) (d:sum money with met profit; summet bawl is trade with money to make a profit) (e:~ na bawl un) (s:summeet/met/meet) (r:42.19.13) (q:draft)
summgo = (t:n) (w:bronze) (d:probably a misprint of sumngo bronze, which follows in the same verse) (e:Tai-ar khuami ~ seek na a sempa) (s:sumngo) (r:11.7.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
sumnei = (t:adj) (w:wealthy/having money) (d:sum money with nei have; sumnei pa is a man of means, the owner of a house and its store) (e:a lakhia thei ziauziau ~ pa) (s:sumhau/hau) (a:zawng) (r:40.13.52) (q:draft, low confidence)
sumneite = (t:n) (w:creditors/lenders) (d:sumnei having money with the plural te; set against leibate, debtors) (e:~ le leibate, a hau a zawng) (a:leibate) (b:sumnei) (r:23.24.2) (q:draft)
sumnen = (t:n) (w:small coin/coin) (d:a coin of little value; sumnen tang nih, two small coins) (e:~ tang nih hong khia hi/meigong khat in zong ~ tang nih a khiat | a widow also putting in two small coins/ngun ~ tang khat ka nei hi | I have one small silver coin) (s:sumtang) (r:41.12.42/9.9.8/42.21.2) (q:draft)
sumngah = (t:v) (w:make money/earn money/get money) (d:sum, money, with ngah, get: earn or make money; sumngah nading is a way of making money) (e:a ~ nading uh beita hi) (r:44.16.19) (q:draft)
sumngo = (t:n) (w:bronze) (d:a hard reddish-brown metal, bronze or copper, used for tools, vessels and weapons) (e:Ama guhte ~ bangin khauh a/tuate ~ tawh zut hi | he overlaid them with bronze/a taina-ah ~ thal in kaptuk ding hi | a bronze arrow will pierce him as he flees/kham, ngun, ~, sik, dal | gold, silver, bronze, iron, tin) (s:sumsan) (r:4.31.22/18.40.18/2.38.6/18.20.24)
sumngote = (t:n) (w:bronze/copper) (d:sumngo, bronze, with the plural te: bronze or copper things, also copper money) (e:A kipia ~ in talen sawmsagih/~ zong singmuatsa bang lel hi | bronze too is just like rotten wood/Kham, ngun, ~, na kawnggak sung uh ah | gold, silver or copper in your belts) (b:sumngo) (r:2.38.29/40.10.9/18.41.27) (q:draft)
sumpi = (t:n) (w:collection/offering/fund) (d:money given or collected for a common purpose, such as an offering or a collection for the poor; sumpi khiatna is the giving of an offering and sumpi keempa is a steward) (e:~ keempa in lungsim dik a nei/Mi siangthote ading ~ khiatna thu | about the collection for the saints/mihonte in ~ a khiat laitakun a en hi | he watched the crowd putting in their offerings/~ kaihkhop tawm a om loh nadingin | so that no collection need be made) (b:sum) (r:46.4.2/40.27.6/46.16.1/41.12.41/46.16.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
sumsan = (t:n) (w:copper/bronze) (d:sum, metal, with san, red: copper, or bronze made from it) (e:suang sung panin ~ huantui uh hi/mualte sung panin ~ na tawh theihna uh leitang | a land where you can dig copper from the hills/kham zah-a a manpha ~ hoih tawh a kibawl | made of fine bronze as precious as gold) (s:sumngo) (r:18.28.2/5.8.9/15.8.27) (q:draft)
sumsinte = (t:n) (w:bankers/money changers) (d:people who take money on deposit and pay interest; plural with te) (e:Ka dangka ~ pia leteh) (r:40.25.27) (q:draft)
Sumsungpa = (t:n) (w:metalworker/coppersmith) (d:sumsungpa, a man who casts or works metal, written with a capital at the start of a sentence; pa marks a man) (e:~ Alekzander in keimah tungah) (r:55.4.14) (q:draft)
sumsungte = (t:n) (w:silversmiths/craftsmen/metalworkers) (d:those who cast silver or metal, plural; sum sungpa is a silversmith) (e:~ leh tua bang nasemte/~ a meetsak thei hi | he brought profit to the craftsmen) (r:44.19.25/44.19.24) (q:draft)
sumtang = (t:n) (w:coin) (d:a piece of metal money; sumtang peek khat is one coin) (e:~ peek khat hong paipih uh hi) (s:dangka/sumnen) (r:40.22.19) (q:draft)
sumte = (t:n) (w:money/possessions/riches) (d:sum, money, with the plural te: sums of money, and also the goods and riches a person owns) (e:Topa inn sungah a kimu ~/~ Aaron leh a tapate tungah pia in | give the money to Aaron and his sons/ama ~ a bit hi | his possessions are safe/Mi khat in leitung ~ nei-in | if someone has worldly possessions) (s:dangkate/neihsate) (b:sum) (r:14.34.17/42.11.21/4.3.48/62.3.17) (q:draft)
sumteng = (t:n) (w:all the money/money) (d:sum money with teng, all of it) (e:na ~ tawh sikhawm in/a topa’ ~ phengzat gawp hi | he squandered all the money of his master) (b:sum) (r:44.8.20/42.16.1) (q:draft)
sumtui = (t:n) (w:molten metal) (d:sum metal, with tui liquid, metal melted for casting or joining; sumtui sunna is a mould into which it is poured) (e:~ sunna sungah sungin) (r:2.32.4/23.41.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
sumval = (t:n) (w:surplus money/abundance/spare wealth) (d:sum money with val extra, money beyond what is needed) (e:a ~ lak pan a khia uh hi) (s:neihval) (r:42.21.4) (q:draft)
sumzah = (t:n) (w:amount of money/sum) (d:sum money with zah amount; na sumzah mah is the full amount of your money) (e:na ~ mah om hi) (r:40.25.25) (q:draft, low confidence)
sumzuak = (t:v) (w:sell) (d:sell for money, often in the pair sumlei sumzuak, buying and selling) (e:sumlei ~ nasepna in/~ thei lo, lei thei lo dingin | so that he could neither sell nor buy/biakinn ah ~ van zuak cihte om nawn lo ding | there will be no more trading in the temple/~ sumlei-a a omte hawlkhiat ding kipan a | he began to drive out those selling and buying) (s:zuak) (a:sumlei) (r:26.7.12/42.17.28/66.13.16/38.14.21/41.11.15) of currency
