sunpa = (t:n) (w:one who pierced) (d:sun pierce with pa, the man who; not sun day) (e:gulpi a ~ nangmah hilo) (r:23.51.9) (q:draft)
sunsak = (t:v) (w:cast for/pour for) (d:sun pour or cast metal with sak, do for someone or something) (e:ngun khainiangte a ~ hi) (r:23.40.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
sunsuk = (t:v) (w:plunge/thrust down/stick into) (d:sun pierce or thrust with suk downward; said of a fork thrust into a pot) (e:beel sungah ahi zongin ~ hi) (r:9.2.14) (q:draft)
sunsun = (t:adj) (w:what little/the little) (d:follows a noun and limits it to the small amount there is: the little, whatever little; a neihsa sunsun is even what little he has) (e:a neihsa ~ nangawn kilaksak ding hi) (r:40.13.12/40.25.29) (q:draft, low confidence)
sunsunte = (t:n) (w:the few/the remaining ones) (d:after a verb, the few who did so or the little that is left; a suakta sunsunte, the few survivors) (e:a suakta ~ in kei pen Topa/khualmite in a om lai ~ sut ta hen | may strangers plunder what little he has left/a suakta kha ~ nangawn | even the few who escape) (s:sunte) (b:sunsun) (r:26.6.7/19.109.11/26.5.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
suntang = (t:n) (w:midday/noon/broad daylight) (d:the middle of the day, when the sun is high; suntang laipi is the very middle of the day) (e:~ laipi-in khuamial sung bangin i tuk a) (s:sunkim) (a:zankim) (r:23.59.10) (q:draft)
Suntang = (t:n) (w:midday/noon) (d:suntang, midday, written with a capital at the start of a sentence; suntang laipi is the very middle of the day) (e:~ laipi mahin khuamial lak bangin) (s:sunkim) (a:zankim) (b:suntang) (r:23.59.10) (q:draft)
suntangin = (t:adv) (w:in broad daylight/openly by day) (d:suntang, midday, with the adverb ending in: in the full light of day, where all can see) (e:~ amaute khai in) (a:zanin) (r:4.25.4) (q:draft)
suntangpi = (t:n) (w:broad daylight/daytime/midday) (d:suntang, daytime, with pi, great: the full light of day; suntangpi-in means in broad daylight) (e:muh dingin ~-in ka hih ding hi/~-in zan bangin mialzawt uh hi | at noon they grope as in the night/A ut bangbangun ~-in gamtat ding | to carouse in broad daylight as they please/Ashdod khuamite ~-in kihawlkhia ding a | the people of Ashdod will be driven out at midday) (s:suntang/sunkim) (a:zankim) (b:suntang) (r:10.12.12/18.5.14/61.2.13/36.2.4) (q:draft)
sunte = (t:n) (w:remnant/survivors/those who remain) (d:used after om lai, nungta lai or suakta for the few who are still left or have escaped; not related to sun day) (e:A om lai ~ gilkialin puksi ding/Josef minam a suakta ~ tungah | on the remnant of Joseph/A nungta lai ~ zong pulnatna tawh si ding | those who survive him will die of plague/a suakta ~ zong mun citengah kithehthang ding hi | the survivors too will be scattered everywhere) (s:omlaite/laisunte/omsuakte/laite) (r:26.6.12/30.5.15/18.27.15/26.17.21) (q:draft)
sunteng = (t:pron) (w:all who remain/all who/as many as) (d:placed after a clause with lai to mean all those who still are so; a omlai sunteng is all who are left, the survivors or remnant) (e:lakah a omlai ~ in ka hawlkhiatna munah/Israel mi a omlai ~ lo siang vet in | glean thoroughly all who are left of Israel/A cihmawh ni-in a hinglai ~ | those still alive in the day of trouble/Ammon gam sungah a omlai ~ a suakta ding uh hi | those left in Ammon will escape) (r:24.8.3/31.1.14/24.6.9/27.11.41) (q:draft)
sunthapai = (t:adj) (w:all day) (d:through the whole day, from morning to evening; mostly written sunthapai-in) (e:~-in kapin ka vak kawikawi hi/~-a ka tautauna hangin | because of my groaning all day long/~-in gimna ka thuak a | all day long I have been afflicted) (r:19.38.6/19.32.3/19.73.14)
sunthapai = (t:adj) (w:all day long) (e:nangmah phatna ~-in ka gengen ding hi/~-in ka galte in kei hong tuancil a | all day long my enemies trample me/Nangma hangin ~-in kote hong kithat a | for your sake we are killed all day long) (r:19.35.28/19.56.2/19.44.22)
sup = (t:v) (w:lose/suffer loss) (d:suffer loss or harm, the opposite of phattuam, gain or benefit; nangma sup nading is to your own loss) (e:nangma ~ nading ahi hi) (s:suplawh) (a:phattuam) (r:20.9.12) (q:draft)
supai = (t:v) (w:tear down/demolish/smash/break down) (d:knock down something that was built, such as towers, walls, altars and sacred pillars) (e:Kulhte ~-in inn hoihpipite satthang gawp/hih tausang ka ~ ding hi | I will tear down this tower/khuampite ~-in Asherah milimte phuk a | he smashed the sacred stones and cut down the Asherah poles/na tausangte ~ ding uh hi | they will pull down your towers) (s:phelkhia/lawnthal) (a:lamkik) (r:26.26.12/14.14.3/7.8.9/26.26.4) (q:draft)
supaisak = (t:v) (w:have torn down/tear down) (d:supai tear down with sak, cause to be done) (e:ama muhna-ah ~ hi) (b:supai) (r:14.34.4) (q:draft)
suplawh = (t:v) (w:lose/forfeit) (d:suffer the loss of something one had, such as life or wealth; the opposite of ngah, gain) (e:a nuntakna bulpi ~ leh bang phattuamna/a nuntakna bulpi nangawn tawh ~ ding a | he will lose even his very life/a neihsa teng uh ~ uh a | they lost all their wealth) (s:taanlawh/mansuah) (a:ngah) (r:42.9.25/21.5.14/42.9.24) (q:draft)
suplawhkhak = (t:v) (w:suffer loss because of/be burdened by) (d:sup lose with lawh and khak; come to bear a cost on account of someone) (e:nong ~ loh nadingun) (r:53.3.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
suplawhte = (t:n) (w:those who lose) (d:suplawh, lose, with plural te: the people who lose something) (e:a nuntakna a ~ in a nuntakna bulpi/hih a leitung nuntakna a ~ in | those who lose this earthly life) (s:taanlawhte) (b:suplawh) (r:42.9.24/40.16.25) (q:draft)
supna = (t:n) (w:loss) (d:what is lost or given up, the opposite of phattuamna, gain; supna thuak is suffer loss) (e:tua ~ keimahmah in ka thuak hi/~ hi ci-in ka ngaihsun hi | I consider it loss/~ tampi na thuak hangin | though you suffer much loss/hih siatna le ~ khempeuh tawh i kipelh ding hi | we would have escaped all this damage and loss) (s:taanna) (a:phattuamna) (b:sup) (r:1.31.39/50.3.7/31.1.5/44.27.21) (q:draft)
supnate = (t:n) (w:losses) (d:supna, loss, with the plural te: the things that are lost; supnate thuak is bear the losses) (e:Tua banga ~ kei mahmah in ka thuak hi) (b:supna) (r:1.31.39) (q:draft)
supngam = (t:v) (w:count as loss/be willing to lose) (d:sup lose with ngam dare, be ready to give something up) (e:Khrih hangin ~ dingin ka ngaihsun hi) (r:50.3.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
Sur = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Sur) (d:name of a gate in Jerusalem where a third of the guard was posted when Joash was made king) (r:12.11.6)
Susa = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Susa) (d:capital city of Elam and royal residence of the kings of Persia, where the story of Esther takes place) (e:Kumpi khua ~ khuapi sunga a kithat) (r:17.9.11/27.8.2) (q:draft)
Susanna = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Susanna) (d:one of the women who followed Jesus and supported him and the disciples out of their own means) (r:42.8.3)
Susi = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Susi) (d:man of the tribe of Manasseh, father of Gaddi, one of the twelve spies) (r:4.13.11/4.13.4) (q:draft)
susia = (t:v) (w:destroy) (d:bring to ruin or to an end: destroy a people, enemies, a city or idols) (e:tanu ka ~ ding hi/Tarshis kici teembaw liante nang na ~ hi | you destroyed the great ships of Tarshish/na milimte uh ka ~ ding hi | I will destroy your idols/kei hong mudahte ka ~ hi | I destroyed those who hate me) (s:siasak/sumai/sugawp) (a:honkhia) (r:24.6.2/1.6.13/19.48.7/33.5.14/19.18.40)
susia = (t:v) (w:demolish/tear down/break down) (d:pull down something built, such as a temple, a wall or an altar) (e:Baal inn ~ uh a/Jerusalem kimkota kulhpi ~ uh hi | they broke down the walls around Jerusalem/Amau’ biakna taute na ~ ding uh hi | you shall break down their altars/Tua kumpipa in hih biakinn ~ a | that king destroyed this temple) (s:supai/phelkhia) (a:lamkik) (r:12.10.27/12.25.10/7.2.2/15.5.12)
Susia = (t:v) (w:destroy) (d:susia, destroy, capitalised at the start of quoted speech and in A Susia pa, the Destroyer) (e:galte nawhkhia-in, ~ un, ci hi/A ~ pa | the Destroyer/amaute a ~ ding pa in en gige hi | the one who will destroy them keeps watch) (b:susia) (r:5.33.27/66.9.11/61.2.3) (q:draft)
susiagawp = (t:v) (w:destroy utterly/devastate/ruin) (d:susia, destroy, with gawp, thoroughly or violently: lay waste a land or wipe out enemies) (e:na gam khempeuh uh ka ~ ding hi/keimah in amaute ka ~ hi | I destroyed them utterly/ka gam sung khempeuh uh ~ khin uh hi | they have devastated our whole land/Gam uk mite in gam sungteng ~ ding a | the rulers will devastate the land) (s:suksiatgawp/sugawp) (b:susia) (r:39.4.6/26.16.39/10.22.41/19.79.7/38.11.6) (q:draft)
susiakhawm = (t:v) (w:destroy together with/destroy along with) (d:susia destroy with khawm together) (e:amaute tawh note kong ~ kha ding hi) (b:susia) (r:9.15.6) (q:draft)
susiamang = (t:v) (w:destroy completely/wipe out/annihilate) (d:susia, destroy, with mang, until gone: destroy so that nothing is left) (e:Amalekte ka ~ khin hi/mawhnei Amalek mite va ~ inla | go and completely destroy those sinners the Amalekites/a omlai mi khempeuh ka ~ ding hi | I will destroy all who remain/Kanaan mite va zo-in ~ uh hi | they defeated the Canaanites and totally destroyed them) (s:sumaimang/suksiatmang/thatmang) (r:9.15.20/7.1.17/9.15.18/26.25.16) (q:draft)
susiapa = (t:n) (w:destroyer) (d:susia destroy, with pa, the man who, the one who destroys) (e:mi a ~ aw/sehnel gam suaksakin, khuapite a ~ | who made it a desert and destroyed its cities/eite’ khut sungah i gam a ~ | into our hands the one who laid waste our land) (s:sugawppa) (b:susia) (r:23.33.1/23.14.17/7.16.24) (q:draft)
susiasak = (t:v) (w:let destroy/cause to destroy) (d:susia destroy with sak, cause or let: give something over to be destroyed) (e:biakinn kulhpi galte a ~ hi) (b:susia) (r:25.2.7) (q:draft)
susiate = (t:n) (w:destroyers) (d:susia destroy, with the plural te, those who destroy) (e:Nang hong bawlte in nang hong ~/amau a ~’ kiang panin amaute’ belh hi un | be their shelter from the destroyers) (s:siasakte/sugawpte) (b:susia) (r:23.49.17/23.16.4) (q:draft)
susiathei = (t:adj) (w:destroying/able to destroy) (d:susia destroy with thei can; a susiathei van mi is a destroying angel) (e:a ~ van mi honkhat a khah hi) (b:susia) (r:19.78.49) (q:draft)
