susiazo = (t:v) (w:can destroy/be able to destroy) (d:susia destroy with zo be able, manage to) (e:muanmuan kulhpi nangawn ~ hi/hong honkhiazo a, hong ~ hi | he is able to save and to destroy/leitung khempeuh a ~ Babylon aw | O Babylon, you who can destroy the whole earth/galte’ panmun phualpi a ~ ding | able to demolish the strongholds of the enemy) (b:susia) (r:20.21.22/59.4.12/24.51.25/47.10.4) (q:draft)
sut = (t:v) (w:plunder/rob/seize/take by force) (d:take what belongs to another by force: plunder goods, rob a person, carry off animals, or take away a right or a blessing) (e:a namkimin i ~ ding a/Egypt mite’ na na ~ ding uh hi | you will plunder the Egyptians/a inn leh a neihsa ~ uh hi | they rob people of house and inheritance/amah in ka thupha hong ~ leuleu hi | now he has taken my blessing as well/Khaldea mite honthum in kalaohte hong ~ a | three bands of Chaldeans carried off the camels) (s:suh/luh/laksak) (r:20.1.13/2.3.22/33.2.2/1.27.36/18.1.17) (q:draft)
sut = (t:v) (w:untie/loose) (d:undo a rope or set free an animal that is tied; khau sut is untie a rope) (e:Bang hangin khau ~ na hi uh hiam/A khau ~ unla, hih lai-ah hong kai un | untie it and bring it here/A la khau a ~ laitakun | as they were untying the colt/khihna khaute zong a ~ uh hi | they also untied the ropes) (s:phel) (a:khih) (r:42.19.33/41.11.5/42.19.30/44.27.40) (q:draft)
sut = (t:v) (w:recite/recount/tell) (d:speak out the words of something in full, as a song or the mighty deeds of God; thu sut is recount a matter) (e:na vangliatna thu ~ ding uh a/hih la malte khempeuh ~ hi | he recited all the words of this song/a lamdang na bawlnate ka ~ kikkik uh hi | we tell again and again of your wonderful deeds) (s:gen) (r:19.145.11/5.32.44/19.75.1) (q:draft, low confidence)
