sutan = (t:v) (w:break/break off/smash/break down) (d:break something hard in two or tear it down by force, such as teeth, bones, a gate bar or a yoke) (e:amau kam sunga hate ~ in la/migilote’ ha na ~ hi | you break the teeth of the wicked/a guh khat zong ~ lo ding uh hi | they must not break any of its bones/Damaskas khua kulhkongpi zawlte ka ~ ding a | I will break the gate bars of Damascus) (s:kuaitan/sukham) (r:19.58.6/1.27.40/19.3.7/4.9.12/30.1.5) (q:draft)
sutat = (t:v) (w:break off/tear off/snap) (d:break a cord or bond apart; also break off a treaty, kipawlna sutat) (e:a khaute ka ~ ding hi/note hong khihna sikkhaute ka ~ ding hi | I will tear away the shackles that bind you/Baasha tawh na kipawlna va ~ in | go and break your treaty with Baasha/migilote’ henna khaute ~ khinta hi | he has cut the cords of the wicked) (a:khih) (r:24.30.8/14.16.3/34.1.13/19.129.4) (q:draft)
sutatin = (t:v) (w:tearing off/breaking off/snapping) (d:sutat break a cord apart with in, which links it to the next verb) (e:hong kihenna khau ~) (b:sutat) (r:24.2.20) (q:draft)
sutgawp = (t:v) (w:plunder/loot/ravage) (d:sut plunder with gawp, which shows that the action is done thoroughly or violently) (e:ama nate ~ uh a/a nate uh na ~ ding hi | you will plunder their goods/ama mite’ na a ~ minam dangte | the nations that plundered his people/ka mite’ gam ~ dingin | to plunder the land of my people) (s:luhgawp) (b:sut) (r:19.89.41/26.38.13/26.38.12/38.2.8/36.2.8) (q:draft)
sutgawppa = (t:n) (w:plunderer/looter) (d:sutgawp plunder with pa, the man who does it) (e:Kua in a ~ tungah Jakob pia a) (b:sutgawp) (r:23.42.24) (q:draft)
