sutkhiat = (t:v) (w:loose/release/take off) (d:form of sutkhia used before khit, sak and other endings) (e:puan a ~ khit ciangin huih in/Pasian in sihna gimna a ~ khit ciangin | after God freed him from the agony of death/na khuta kibulh kolte, tu ni-in kong ~ sak | today I free you from the chains on your hands) (b:sutkhia) (r:44.27.17/44.2.24/24.40.4) (q:draft)
sutkhiatsak = (t:v) (w:free/release/loose) (d:sutkhiat, loose, with sak, do for another: take bonds or chains off someone) (e:Keimah hong kikhihnate nong ~ zo hi/na khuta kibulh kolte tuni-in kong ~ a | today I free you from the chains on your hands) (s:khahkhia/suaktasak) (b:sutkhiat) (r:19.116.16/24.40.4) (q:draft)
sutlup = (t:v) (w:pierce/stab) (d:pierce someone so that he dies; a sutlup uh mipa is the man whom they pierced) (e:a ~ uh mipa enin) (s:sunlum/dawt) (r:38.12.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
sutna = (t:n) (w:struggle/attack) (d:the act of laying a hand on something or fighting it, with the noun suffix na; tua na sutna thu is that struggle of yours) (e:tua na ~ thu na mangngilh nawn kei ding hi) (r:18.41.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
