sutsak = (t:v) (w:let plunder/give as plunder) (d:sut plunder with sak, cause or let) (e:Amau’ nate, gamdang mite ka ~ ding a/a neihsa khempeuh uh migilote ~ in | giving all their wealth to the wicked as loot) (b:sut) (r:26.7.21) (q:draft)
sutsak = (t:v) (w:untie/loosen/take off) (d:sut, untie, with sak, do for another: untie a strap or take off a yoke or bonds for someone) (e:kuamah in a kol ~ lo ding hi/a khedap khau a ~ ding nangawnin | even to untie the strap of his sandal/a kikhihna kolte uh ka ~ khit ciangin | when I have taken off the yokes that bind them/kei pen ama khedap khau a ~ ding | for me to untie the strap of his sandal) (s:phel) (a:khih) (b:sut) (r:28.11.7/26.34.27/41.1.7/43.1.27) (q:draft)
sutsakin = (t:v) (w:giving as plunder/letting plunder) (d:sutsak let plunder with in, which links it to the next verb) (e:a neihsa khempeuh uh migilote ~) (b:sutsak) (r:26.7.21) (q:draft)
