sutte = (t:n) (w:robbers/swindlers/extortioners) (d:sut, take by force, with plural te: those who seize what belongs to others; zawhthawh bawla sutte are those who take by force or fraud) (e:Zawhthawh thu tawh mi’ na a ~ in/zawhthawh bawla sum ~ in | those who take money by force/Na puantungsilh uh a hong ~ tungah | to those who take your coat/amau’ na a ~’ na sutin | plundering those who plundered them) (s:misuamte/suamte) (b:sut) (r:20.1.19/46.6.10/42.6.29/26.39.10) (q:draft)
