taikhiasim = (t:v) (w:flee secretly/slip away/run away) (d:taikhia run away with sim, secretly) (e:kongpi tawnin galkapte ~ uh a/Topa’ kiang pan amah a ~ ahihlam | that he was running away from the Lord) (s:taisim) (r:24.52.7/32.1.10) (q:draft)
taikhiat = (t:v) (w:flee/run away/leave/escape) (d:form of taikhia used before manin, ni, nading and zawh) (e:Amah a ~ manin ka dah lua a/Lot in Sodom khua sung pan a ~ ni-in | on the day Lot fled out of Sodom/hehna pan na ~ nadingun kua in hong hilhkhol | who warned you to flee from the wrath/~ zawh lohna kulhpi sungah a hong koih hi | he has put me inside a wall I cannot escape from/teembaw hawlte ~ sawm uh ahih manin | because the sailors were trying to escape) (b:taikhia) (r:22.5.6/42.17.29/40.3.7/25.3.7/44.27.30) (q:draft)
taikhiatna = (t:n) (w:flight/fleeing/running away) (d:taikhiat, flee, with the noun ending na: the act of fleeing, or the place one fled from) (e:inn panin a ~ a muh ciangin/a hong ~ khua-ah paikik thei ding hi | he may go back to the town he fled from) (s:taina/taisimna) (b:taikhiat) (r:1.39.13/6.20.6) (q:draft)
taikhiatzawh = (t:v) (w:be able to escape) (d:tai, flee, with khiat, out, and zawh, be able; taikhiatzawh hetlohna is a place from which there is no escape) (e:~ hetlohna kulhpi sungah hong koih) (r:25.3.7) (q:draft)
taikik = (t:v) (w:flee back/run back) (d:tai run with kik, back again) (e:uhah a ~ ding uh/a gam mah uhah a ~ ding uh hi | they will flee back to their own land) (s:lehtai) (b:tai) (r:24.50.16) (q:draft)
tailahpi = (t:see) <tailahpi-in>
tailahpi-in = (t:todo) (q:draft, describes how a hunted deer runs on before the hunters, perhaps exhausted or in panic; the verse does not fix the meaning)
tailam = (t:n) (w:flight/way of escape) (d:tai, flee, with lam, way or direction: the fact or direction of someone fleeing) (e:ama ~ thei napi-in) (r:9.22.17) (q:draft, low confidence)
