taksuak = (t:v) (w:come true/be carried out) (d:tak, real, with suak, become: come to be real; taksuak sak is make it happen, carry it out) (e:Tu-in ~ sak un) (r:10.3.18) (q:draft, low confidence)
taktak = (t:adv) (w:truly/surely/certainly/really) (d:placed after a verb to stress that something really is so or will surely happen; after a noun it means real or true, as in Israel mi taktak, a true Israelite) (e:itna in a kicing ~ hi/kheemna om lo Israel mi ~ ahi hi | he is a true Israelite in whom there is no deceit/Amah kiliing lo ~ ding a | surely he will never be shaken/Na si ~ kei ding uh hi | you will not surely die/amau’ kikona ka za ~ ding hi | I will certainly hear their cry) (s:takpi/taktakin/petmah) (r:62.2.5/1.2.17/43.1.47/19.112.6/1.3.4/2.22.23)
taktakah = (t:adv) (w:in the very/truly in) (d:taktak, truly, with the place marker ah; lungsim tawng taktakah is in the very depth of the heart) (e:Ka lungsim tawng ~ Pasian’ thukham) (b:taktak) (r:45.7.22) (q:draft)
taktakin = (t:adv) (w:truly/really/indeed/in fact) (d:taktak, truly, with the adverb ending in; mostly as a taktakin, truly or indeed, at the opening of a statement) (e:a ~ amah in ka sanggamnu mah/A ~ ci lehang, Abraham a pian’ ma-in | truly I say, before Abraham was born/Johan pen kamsang ~ ngaihsun uh | they held that John really was a prophet/A ~, Israelte’ Pasian, Honpa aw | truly, O God of Israel, the Saviour) (s:taktak/takpi/mantak) (b:taktak) (r:1.20.12/23.45.15/43.8.58/41.11.32) (q:draft)
taktakna = (t:n) (w:genuineness/sincerity/reality) (d:taktak, truly, with na, placed after a verb or adjective to make a noun: the fact of truly doing or being so, as in it taktakna, true love, and lungkim taktakna, full conviction) (e:note ka hong it ~ thu/lungkim ~ tawh a dim thu ahi hi | it is a message full of deep conviction/amah a sih ~ ding thu | that he will certainly die/i lungsim ah i up ~ hangin | because we truly believe in our heart) (s:takpina) (b:taktak) (r:50.1.8/52.1.5/12.8.10/45.10.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
taktakpa = (t:n) (w:the true one/the real one) (d:taktak, truly, with pa, the man who: after a verb, the one who truly does it, as a nei taktakpa, the true owner) (e:amah a hu ~ ahihna Pasian in/a nei ~ tung pan | from its true owner) (b:taktak) (r:19.48.3/18.31.38) (q:draft)
taktakta = (t:adv) (w:truly now/really) (d:taktak, truly, with ta, marking that a new state has come) (e:bei nading nai ~ hi) (b:taktak) (r:62.2.18) (q:draft)
