tampitak = (t:adj) (w:very many/a great number) (d:tampi many with the intensive tak) (e:~ nungzuite a suaksak khit uh/Kauphe bangin ~ na pha khin uh hi | you have become as many as the locusts) (s:tampipi) (b:tampi) (r:44.14.21/34.3.15) (q:draft)
tampite = (t:adj) (w:many/numerous) (d:many, with the plural marker te, placed after the noun it counts) (e:mi ~ in Topa a um uh hi/minam ~ vatmai-in kumpi vangliante that a | he struck down many nations and killed mighty kings/A um mi ~ in hong pai uh a | many of those who believed came/mi ~’ kikona, tuipi ging bang | the uproar of many peoples, like the roar of the sea) (s:tampi/tamte) (a:tawmte/tawmnote) (b:tampi) (r:43.10.42/19.135.10/44.19.18/23.17.12) (q:draft)
tamsak = (t:v) (w:multiply/increase/make numerous/make plentiful) (d:tam, many, with the causative sak: make many, increase the number of people or things) (e:vantung aksi zah-in note hong ~ hi/Izipt gamah ka limte leh nalamdangte ka ~ hangin | though I multiply my signs and wonders in Egypt/tuuhonpi bangin Israel mite ka ~ ding hi | I will make the people of Israel as many as a flock of sheep/note dikna’ gahte a ~ ding hi | he will increase the harvest of your righteousness) (s:pungsak/phasak/khangsak) (a:tawmsak/kiamsak) (b:tam) (r:5.10.22/2.7.3/26.36.37/47.9.10) (q:draft)
tamsakin = (t:v) (w:multiply/make numerous) (d:tamsak, make many, with the linking ending in: making numerous, and then) (e:vantung aksi bangin ~, keimah in) (b:tamsak) (r:2.32.13) (q:draft)
tamsakin = (t:v) (w:name after) (d:in min tamsakin, from min tam, bear the name of someone, with sak, cause: giving a place a person's own name) (e:ama min ~ tuni donga a kip) (r:5.3.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
tamsakzaw = (t:v) (w:make more numerous) (d:tamsak, make many, with the comparative zaw) (e:nupi meigong ka ~ ding hi) (b:tamsak) (r:24.15.8) (q:draft)
tamte = (t:adj) (w:many/numerous/large in number) (d:tam many with plural te: those that are many, the larger groups; opposite of tawmte) (e:minam ~ tungah luahna a tam/minam ~ tung panin tam la-in | take many from the tribes that have many/a ~ tungah a tam | much to those who are many) (s:tampite) (a:tawmte) (b:tam) (r:4.33.54/4.26.56/4.35.8) (q:draft)
tamvei = (t:adv) (w:many times/often/frequently) (d:tam many, with vei, time or occasion; tamvei zaw is more times) (e:sih dektakna ~ ka tuakzaw hi/satna ~ ka thuakzaw a | I was flogged more often/hih sangin a ~ zaw | more times than this) (s:tamveipi/zelzel) (r:47.11.23/5.25.3) (q:draft)
tamveipi = (t:adv) (w:often/many times/frequently) (d:tamvei, many times, with the intensive pi: very often, time and again) (e:thukhen mangpa kiangah ~ pai-in/tuasan takah ~ a pai uh hi | they often went there/kolbulh leh sikkhau tawh ~ a kihen ngei hangin | though he had often been bound with shackles and chains/kikhopna inn khat pan khat ah ~ ka pai hi | I often went from one synagogue to another/~ meikhuk sungah, ~ tui sungah a puksak hi | it has often thrown him into fire and into water) (s:tamvei/zelzel/veipi) (b:tamvei) (r:42.18.3/41.5.4/43.18.2/44.26.11/41.9.22) (q:draft)
tamzaw = (t:adj) (w:more/more numerous/greater) (d:comparative of tam, used with sangin for than) (e:sim leng sehnel sangin ~ hi/amaute sangin a ~ leh a zahtak-huai zaw uliante | officials more numerous and more distinguished than they/mi khempeuh sangin a sia ~ gamta hi | he did more evil than all the others/note sangin a ~ leh a vanglian zawte | those more numerous and mightier than you) (a:tawmzaw) (b:tam) (r:19.139.18/4.22.15/11.16.25/5.4.38) (q:draft)
tamzawk = (t:adj) (w:more/greater) (d:form of tamzaw, more, used before a following word) (e:gamtatnate sangin a ~ thu) (b:tamzaw) (r:66.2.19) (q:draft)
tamzawkna = (t:n) (w:being more numerous/greater number) (d:tamzawk, more, with the noun suffix na) (e:midangte sangin na ~ hang uh) (b:tamzawk) (r:5.7.7) (q:draft)
tamzawte = (t:n) (w:the majority/most/those who are more) (d:tamzaw more with the plural te: the larger number, most of the people; with sangin, those who are more than) (e:Mi ~ in amaute in bang hangin/tul za le tul sawmnih sangin a ~’ tenna | home to more than a hundred and twenty thousand) (b:tamzaw) (r:44.19.32/32.4.11) (q:draft)
tamzo = (t:v) (w:manage many/be able to do much) (d:tam, many, with zo, be able; thah tamzo is manage to kill many) (e:Filistia-te i thah ~ nai lo hi) (b:tam) (r:9.14.30) (q:draft, low confidence)
tan = (t:v) (w:fast/abstain) (d:abstain from, in an tan, go without food, usually written with a final apostrophe) (e:zan sawmli an a ~’ khit ciangin/amaute in an ~’ ding thu zasak uh a | they proclaimed a fast/deihgawhnate khempeuh na ~’ nadingun | that you abstain from all sinful desires/a ~’ nadingun a vaikhak ding | to instruct them to abstain) (s:antan) (r:40.4.2/11.21.12/60.2.11/44.15.20) (q:draft)
tan = (t:prep) (w:as far as/up to/as much as) (d:marks a measure of extent in time or distance: bang tan is how much or how long, and suang lot khat tan is about a stone’s throw) (e:Bang ~ sauvei ding ahi hiam/thal lot khat ~ bangah | about a bowshot away/suang lot khat ~ bang kikhen a | he withdrew about a stone’s throw/Saul’ hangin bang ~ vei dah ding na hi hiam | how long will you mourn for Saul) (r:19.90.13/42.22.41/1.21.16/9.16.1) (q:draft)
tan = (t:v) (w:cut off/sever/break off) (d:cut or break through, lu tan or ngawng tan is cut off the head, behead) (e:Johan’ ngawng ka ~ zo hi/na lu hong ~ ding a | he will cut off your head/amah satin that uh a, a lu ~ uh hi | they struck and killed him and cut off his head/khamul mongte uh zong na ~ kei ding uh hi | you shall not cut the edges of your beards/khat in singluang a ~ lai takin | as one of them was cutting down a tree) (s:sattan) (r:42.9.9/9.31.9/1.40.19/10.4.7/3.19.27/12.6.5) (q:draft)
tan = (t:v) (w:redeem/ransom/rescue) (d:buy back or bring out of the power of another, also as tan khia) (e:keima adingin ka ~ thei kei ding hi/Na tat ding leh ~ in | if you will redeem it, redeem it/a thuman Pasian aw, keimah nong ~ zo hi | O faithful God, you have redeemed me/hong nai in la hong ~ in | come near and redeem me/nang hong ~ khin ka hih ciangin | because I have redeemed you) (s:tankhia/honkhia/tanh) (r:8.4.6/18.6.23/8.4.4/19.31.5/19.69.18/23.44.22) (q:draft)
