tanau = (t:n) (w:relative/kinsman/kin/cousin) (d:a member of one's own family or clan) (e:kei sangin a naizaw ~ khat om lai hi/Boaz in i ~ hilo ahi hiam | is not Boaz our relative/i behte, i ~ naipente khat ahi hi | he is of our clan, one of our closest relatives/amau’ ~, Kish’ tapate in amaute ten’pih uh hi | their cousins, the sons of Kish, married them) (s:behpa/sanggam) (r:8.3.12/13.23.22/8.3.2/8.2.20) (q:draft)
tanaupa = (t:n) (w:kinsman/male relative) (d:tanau relative with pa marking a man; in Ruth the kinsman who has the right to redeem) (e:amah in ~ kiangah/a ~ in Boaz kiangah | the kinsman, to Boaz) (s:behpa) (b:tanau) (r:8.4.3/8.4.6/8.4.8) (q:draft)
tanaute = (t:n) (w:relatives/kinsmen/clan) (d:tanau, relative, with the plural te; used also of one relative together with his family) (e:a nu’ ~ kiangah pai-in/a lawmte le a ~ lak khawng | among his friends and relatives/Ga-al a ~ tawh Shekhem-ah hong kuan hi | Gaal came to Shechem with his clan/Naomi in a pasal’ ~, Elimelek innkuan sung mi | Naomi had a relative of her husband, of the family of Elimelek) (s:behte) (b:tanau) (r:7.9.1/8.2.1/42.2.44/7.9.26) (q:draft)
taneu = (t:n) (w:younger child/younger son) (d:ta child with neu small; in the verses the younger of two sons) (e:A ~ in a pa kiangah/a ~ in ama sum khempeuh khawm a | the younger son gathered all he had) (s:nauzawpa) (r:42.15.12/42.15.13) (q:draft)
taneute = (t:n) (w:little ones/little children/infants) (d:plural of taneu, small child; also used as a tender way of addressing people) (e:Ka ~ aw, ngasa na man uh hiam/a ~, a zite, leh a naupangte uh tawh | with their little ones, their wives and their children/Na ~ hong laksakin | seizing your infants/a ~ le a ganhingte le a vante uh | their little children, their livestock and their goods) (s:tanote/naupangnote/naungekte) (b:taneu) (r:43.21.5/14.20.13/19.137.9/7.18.21) (q:draft)
