tangeekte = (t:n) (w:little ones/infants/young of the flock) (d:the very young, said of small children and of the young of a flock) (e:A ~ nangawn uh kikaikhia ding hi/a ~ uh gilkial dangtak-in sisak uh a | they let their infants die of hunger and thirst/A ~ nangawn uh kikaikhia takpi ding a | even their little ones will surely be dragged away) (s:naungekte/naungeekte/taneute) (r:24.49.20/25.4.4/24.50.45) (q:draft)
