tangten = (t:v) (w:live alone/live apart/dwell alone) (d:live alone or apart from others; written with a final apostrophe before the next word) (e:gam simthamah khat guak ~’ hoihzaw hi/innkhumzang kiu khatah ~’ hoihzaw tham hi | it is far better to live alone on a corner of the roof/En in, a ~’ mite | see, a people who live apart) (r:20.21.19/4.23.9/20.21.9) (q:draft)
tangteng = (t:n) (w:share/portion due) (d:in ngah ding tangteng, the part that someone is to receive, as a share of an estate or of a harvest) (e:ama ngah ding ~ a la dingin/kei’ ngah ding ~ tu-in hong pia in | give me now the share that is to be mine) (s:tanh) (r:41.12.2/42.15.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
tangteuh = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:lizard) (d:a kind of lizard among the unclean creeping things, where the NIV has wall lizard; sehnel gam tangteuh, lizard of the sand country, stands for the skink) (e:sehnel gam ~ leh thankik ahi hi) (r:3.11.30) (q:draft)
