tangthu = (t:n) (w:history/annals/record) (d:a written record of past events; khang tangthu is the annals of a reign or a line) (e:khang ~ sungah kigelh hi/kamsang Iddo’ ~ sungah kigelh hi | it is written in the records of the prophet Iddo/Kumpi David’ khang ~ sungah | in the annals of King David) (r:14.20.34/14.13.22/13.27.24)
tangthu = (t:n) (w:generation/family line/genealogy) (d:the account of a family line, the descendants of a man told in order) (e:pa Esau’ ~ ahi hi/Noah’ suan-le-khakte ~ ahi hi | the account of the descendants of Noah/Abraham’ tapa Isaak’ suan-le-khakte ~ ahi hi | the account of the family line of Isaac son of Abraham) (r:1.36.9/1.6.9/1.25.19)
Tangthu = (t:n) (w:annals/chronicles/history) (d:capitalised in the title Khang Tangthu Laibu, book of the annals) (e:Judah Kumpite’ Khang ~ Laibu sungah kigelh/Israel Kumpite’ Khang ~ Laibu sungah kigelh hi | it is written in the book of the annals of the kings of Israel/nisim thupiang ciamtehna Khang ~ Laibu lasak a | he had the book of the chronicles, the record of daily events, brought) (b:tangthu) (r:12.14.18/17.6.1/12.15.11) (q:draft)
tangthute = (t:n) (w:stories/tales/myths/accounts) (d:tangthu, story, with the plural te; phuahtawm tangthute are myths) (e:Phuahtawm ~ le min tampipi/Hih in Adam’ suan-le-khakte’ ~ ahi hi | this is the account of the descendants of Adam/ahi mawkna ~ paaikhia in | throw away worthless tales) (s:tuanthute) (b:tangthu) (r:54.1.4/1.5.1/54.4.7) (q:draft)
