tanh = (t:n) (w:portion/share/allotment) (d:the part that falls to someone: a share of food, of land or of an inheritance) (e:Topa pen keima ~ ahi hi/~ leh luah nei lo ahih manun | because they have no allotment or inheritance/Benjamin’ ~ pen amaute’ aa zah nga pha hi | Benjamin’s portion was five times as much as theirs/tua in nangma' ~ hi ding hi | that will be your share) (s:seh/kaih) (r:19.119.57/5.14.27/1.43.34/2.29.26) (q:draft)
tanh = (t:v) (w:redeem/buy back) (d:buy back or set free by paying a price, said of land, of a firstborn and of a people) (e:a lo ~ nuam lo ahi a/tuuno khat tawh na ~ ding uh hi | you shall redeem it with a lamb/a sanggampa zuaksa ~ ding hi | he shall redeem what his brother has sold/thukhenna nasep lian tawh note kong ~ ding hi | I will redeem you with mighty acts of judgment) (s:tat/tankhia) (a:zuak) (r:3.27.20/3.25.26/2.13.13/3.25.25/2.6.6) (q:draft)
tanhkik = (t:v) (w:redeem/buy back) (d:tanh, redeem, with kik, back again) (e:amah in ~ thei ding a/amah in ~ thei nawn lo ding hi | he can no longer redeem it/i Jew mipihte ahizo zahzahin i ~ hi | we have bought back our fellow Jews as far as we could) (s:tatkik/leikik) (a:zuak) (b:tanh) (r:3.25.29/16.5.8/3.27.20) (q:draft)
