tawlet = (t:n) (w:window) (d:an opening in the wall of a house or ship for light and air; tawlet panin is from or through the window) (e:ka ~ panin ka khuadak a/Noah in ama bawlsa teembaw ~ hong a | Noah opened the window of the ark he had made/gutate bangin ~-ah hong lut uh hi | like thieves they come in at the windows/~ vangte panin sihna hong lutin | death has come in through the windows) (r:20.7.6/24.9.21/1.8.6/29.2.9) (q:draft)
tawlette = (t:n) (w:windows/openings/floodgates) (d:tawlet, window, with the plural te; vantung tawlette, the windows of heaven, where the English has floodgates) (e:le vantung ~ kikhak a/vantung ~ kihong hi | the floodgates of heaven were opened/a kimkotah ~ a nei hi | it had openings all around) (b:tawlet) (r:1.8.2/11.6.4/1.7.11/26.40.36) (q:draft)
tawlkhat = (t:adv) (w:a little while/for a while/briefly) (d:tawl, a while, with khat, one: for a short time; tawlkhat sung is for a while, tawlkhat khit ciangin after a little while) (e:Note tawh ~ bek ka om khit ciangin/~ khawlin ngai in la | stop a while and listen/hehna a dam matengin ~ sung bu un | hide for a little while until the wrath has passed/amah in nang tawh ~ a kikhen | he was parted from you for a little while) (a:sawtpi/sawtvei) (r:43.7.33/43.16.16/18.37.14/23.26.20/57.1.15) (q:draft)
Tawlkhatkhat = (t:adv) (w:for a while/for a time) (d:tawlkhat, a little while, with khat repeated) (e:~ khuavak kimu lo a) (r:18.37.21) (q:draft, low confidence)
tawllua = (t:v) (w:be too weary/be very tired) (d:tawl, be weary, with lua, too much) (e:mawhna a bawl manun ~ uh a) (s:gimlua) (b:tawl) (r:24.9.5) (q:draft)
tawlna = (t:n) (w:weariness/hardship/trouble) (d:tawl, be weary, with the noun ending na; used in the pair gimna tawlna, suffering and hardship) (e:gimna ~ a thuakna tawh/gimna ~ khempeuh lak pan gumkhia a | he rescued him from all his troubles/note tungah hong tung ding gimna ~ hangin | because of the misery that is coming on you) (s:gimna) (a:tawldamna) (b:tawl) (r:58.5.8/59.5.1/44.7.10) (q:draft)
tawlnga = (t:v) (w:rest) (d:stop working or moving in order to recover strength) (e:ni thum sung ka ~ uh hi/a ni sagih ni-in mite ~ hi | the people rested on the seventh day/ni sagih ni-in amah ~ hi | on the seventh day he rested/a gimte ~ hithiat ding hi | the weary will be at rest) (s:tawldam) (r:15.8.32/2.16.30/1.2.2/18.3.17)
tawlnga = (t:v) (w:relax) (d:be at ease, free from work or trouble) (e:Na inn-ah ciahsuk inla ~ in | go down to your house and relax/Leitung khempeuh ~-in gamdai takin om ta uh a | the whole earth is at rest and at peace) (r:10.11.8/23.14.7)
tawlnga = (t:v) (w:pause/cease/stop) (d:stop for a time; tawlnga loin is without stopping, unceasingly) (e:Lungdamna Thu ~ loin hilhin/khebaite nangawn in ~ loin kei hong gensia hi | they slandered me without ceasing/ka lungsim sungah ~ loin lungmangin | with unceasing anguish in my heart/Jerusalem khua panin siatna ~ lo hi | wickedness does not cease from Jerusalem) (r:44.5.42/19.35.15/45.9.2/24.6.7)
Tawlnga = (t:v) (w:rest/cease) (d:tawlnga, rest or cease, written with a capital in the text) (e:~ nai lo ding na hi hiam/~ loin mihingte satna a | that struck the peoples without ceasing) (b:tawlnga) (r:24.47.6/23.14.5) (q:draft)
tawlngak = (t:v) (w:rest/take a rest/come to rest) (d:form of tawlnga used before words such as khit, lai, theih and nading) (e:a sun ~ lai takin/thuciamna singkuang a ~ khit ciangin | after the ark came to rest/a ~ nading mun uh a zon’sak dingin | to find them a place to rest/ka pate tawh ka ~ khawm ciangin | when I rest with my fathers) (b:tawlnga) (r:10.4.5/13.6.31/4.10.33/1.47.30) (q:draft)
tawlngakna = (t:n) (w:rest/resting place/repose) (d:tawlngak, rest, with the noun ending na: rest, or a time or place of rest; tawlngakna mun is a resting place, tawlngakna sabbath a sabbath of rest) (e:note tungah ~ leh lungnopna hong pia/lungsim ~ hun nang kong pia ding hi | I will give you a time of rest/daii tak-a ~ munah om ding uh hi | they will live in quiet places of rest/a thupi-a ~ sabbath ni | a day of solemn sabbath rest) (s:tawldamna/khawlna) (r:23.28.12/5.12.9/2.33.14/23.32.18/2.31.15) (q:draft)
tawlngasak = (t:v) (w:make rest/give rest/let rest) (d:tawlnga, rest, with the causative sak; in Exodus 5:5 of making people stop their work) (e:nasepnate panin amaute na ~ uh hi) (s:tawldamsak) (b:tawlnga) (r:2.5.5/18.9.5) (q:draft)
tawlngasakin = (t:v) (w:let rest/leave fallow) (d:tawlngasak, make rest, with the linking in; of land left unplowed) (e:leitang ~, lokhulin na omsak ding) (b:tawlngasak) (r:2.23.11) (q:draft)
tawlngate = (t:n) (w:those who rest) (d:tawlnga, rest, with te, those who) (e:Pasian tawh a ~ khempeuh zong) (b:tawlnga) (r:58.4.10) (q:draft)
Tawlno = (t:n) (w:a little while/short time) (d:tawl, a while, with no, small; Tawlno khat khit ciangin is after a little while; written with a capital at the start of a sentence) (e:~ khat khit ciangin a hong tung ding/~ khat khit ciangin tua kumpipa kithat lum ding | after a little while that king will be killed) (s:tawmvei) (r:58.10.37/27.11.20) (q:draft)
tawm = (t:adj) (w:few/little/small) (d:small in number or amount; tawm khat is a little, a few, and tawm mahmah very few) (e:Silngo ~ khat in annel lom/a kiteel mite a ~ ding uh hi | those who are chosen will be few/eite’ ading an ~ va lei un | go and buy a little food for us/Amaute ~ mahmah-in | when they were very few) (s:tawmno) (a:tam) (r:48.5.9/19.105.12/40.22.14/1.44.25) (q:draft)
tawm = (t:part) (d:placed after a verb, often one that begins with ki, to show that the subject does the action himself, to himself or on his own: kigawt tawm is deny oneself) (e:a puan ding gan ~ hi/nomau mah na kigawt ~ ding uh hi | you must deny yourselves/amaute kisiangthosak ~ uh a | they purified themselves/Nomau tungah kiheh ~ kei un | do not be angry with yourselves) (r:20.31.19/4.30.3/3.23.32/4.8.21/1.45.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
tawm = (t:v) (w:pick up/gather/glean) (d:pick up from the ground, gather what lies scattered; ansang tawm is glean ears of grain, suang tawm pick up stones) (e:an late’ nung lo sungah ansanghte ~ hi/amah a den nading suang ~ uh a | they picked up stones to stone him/khamval a neng a themte ~ uh a | they picked up the broken pieces that were left over/midangte’ lo-ah ansang ~ dingin pai kei in | do not go to glean in another field) (s:tom/top) (r:8.2.3/41.8.19/43.8.59/40.14.20/8.2.8) (q:draft)
tawmbek = (t:adj) (w:few/only a few) (d:tawm, few, with bek, only) (e:sem ding mi ~ a om hi) (r:40.9.37) (q:draft)
tawmcik = (t:adj) (w:few/very few/little) (d:tawm, few, with cik, very small: very few, very little) (e:mi ~ bek na om lai ding uh hi/mi ~ a lut uh hi | only a few enter/~ bek na nei uh hi | you have only a little) (s:tawmno) (a:tampi) (r:5.4.27/37.1.9/40.7.14) (q:draft)
tawmcikkhat = (t:adj) (w:a few/a little/a very small amount) (d:tawmcik, very few, with khat, one: a very small number or amount) (e:sung panin ~ la leuleu inla) (s:tawmkhat) (r:26.5.4) (q:draft)
tawmin = (t:part) (d:tawm with the linking ending in, placed after a verb to show that the subject does the action himself, on his own: hanciam tawmin, making the effort oneself) (e:amah ki-ip ~/keimah mah hanciam ~ Ammon mite do dingin | making the effort myself to fight the Ammonites/mite amau mah kikaikhawm ~ | the people gathering themselves together/nomau mah kigawt ~ | denying yourselves) (b:tawm) (r:1.43.31/7.12.3/2.32.1/3.16.29) (q:draft, low confidence)
tawmin = (t:v) (w:pick up/take up) (d:tawm, pick up, with the linking ending in, followed by another verb: picking up and then) (e:~ a ne uh hi/amah ~ tua mun leitang tungah paai in | pick him up and throw him on that plot of ground/vasate in ~ a ne uh hi | the birds picked it up and ate it) (r:41.4.4/12.9.26/42.8.5) (q:draft)
tawmin = (t:adj) (w:few/little) (d:tawm, few, with the linking ending in: being few; tawm tawmin is little by little) (e:Amaute a mi-in ~/mai panin tawm ~ amaute ka hawlkhia ding hi | little by little I will drive them out from before you/hih minamte tawm ~ siang khiasak ding hi | he will clear away these nations little by little) (b:tawm) (r:13.16.19/2.23.30/5.7.22) (q:draft)
tawmkha = (t:adj) (w:a few/a little/some) (d:a small number or amount, placed after the noun: ni tawmkha, a few days) (e:Ngasa ~ nei uh ahih ciangin/nungzuite tawh ni ~ omkhawm a | he stayed some days with the disciples/phattuamna ~ a pia thei hi | it gives some benefit/nang in ~ thahatna nei-in | you have little strength) (s:tawmkhat) (a:tampi) (r:41.8.7/44.9.19/54.4.8/66.3.8) (q:draft)
tawmkha = (t:adv) (w:sparingly/little) (d:in a small amount or degree) (e:a vawhte in ~ a at ding hi/~-in a it thei hi | he loves little) (r:47.9.6/42.7.47) (q:draft)
tawmkhat = (t:adj) (w:a little/a few/some) (d:tawm, few, with khat, one: a small amount or number, some of a thing; tawmkhat sung is for a little while) (e:mi ~ bek kiniamkhiatin Jerusalem ah/sathau ~ a taklam khutme tawh | some of the oil with his right forefinger/bawngtal si ~ la-in | taking some of the blood of the bull/~ sung ihmu lai ning | let me sleep a little longer) (s:tawmkha) (r:14.30.11/20.6.10/3.14.27/3.4.5) (q:draft)
tawmkhate = (t:adj) (w:a few/few) (d:tawmkha a few with the plural te, placed after the noun: mi tawmkhate, a few people) (e:mi ~ in Izipt gam panin) (b:tawmkha) (r:24.44.28) (q:draft)
tawmkhatte = (t:adj) (w:a few/few) (d:tawmkhat a few with the plural te, placed after the noun) (e:cina ~ tungah khut nga-in/Tua tuu ~ gamlakah kua tawh nusia na hi | with whom did you leave those few sheep in the wilderness) (b:tawmkhat) (r:41.6.5/9.17.28) (q:draft)
tawmkik = (t:v) (w:pick up/gather up) (d:tawm, pick up, with kik, back or again; of gathering leftover pieces) (e:a neng a themte ~ uh a) (r:40.15.37) (q:draft)
tawmlua = (t:adj) (w:too little/too few) (d:tawm few, little, with lua, too much) (e:hihte ~ ahih leh tua zah mah/siampite a mi ~ uh ahih manin | because the priests were too few) (a:tamlua) (b:tawm) (r:10.12.8/21.12.3/14.29.34) (q:draft)
tawmluat = (t:adj) (w:too few/too small) (d:form of tawmlua used before leh, if) (e:innkuanmi a ~ leh amau’ innzom) (b:tawmlua) (r:2.12.4) (q:draft)
tawmna = (t:n) (d:the noun ending na on a verb followed by tawm, oneself: the act of doing something to oneself; kikhih tawmna is a pledge by which one binds oneself, kinitsak tawmna the defiling of oneself) (e:a kikhih ~ peuhmah ama tungah kip ding/a kikhih ~ kamciamna khempeuh zong kip ding hi | every pledge by which she bound herself will also stand/nomau mah na kinitsak ~ thute uh | the things by which you defiled yourselves) (b:tawm) (r:4.30.9/4.30.7/4.30.11/26.20.43) (q:draft, low confidence)
tawmnate = (t:n) (d:tawmna, the noun ending na on a verb followed by tawm, doing something to oneself, with the plural te; kiniamsak tawmnate are acts of humbling oneself) (e:nomau na kiniamsak ~ uh) (b:tawmna) (r:23.58.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
tawmno = (t:adj) (w:few/little/small) (d:tawm, few, with the diminutive no: a very small number or amount; tawmno khat is a little, a few) (e:Mi ~ bek a omna khua khat/a multe ~ khat la in la | take a few of the hairs/thuman-a ~ neihna hoihzaw hi | it is better to have a little with righteousness/ni ~ khat tawh kibang sa hi | they seemed to him like a few days) (s:tawmcik) (a:tampi) (b:tawm) (r:21.9.14/20.16.8/26.5.3/1.29.20) (q:draft)
tawmnote = (t:adj) (w:little/few) (d:tawmno with the plural te; tuuhon tawmnote, little flock, in address) (e:Tuuhon ~ aw, lau-in lunghimawh kei un) (b:tawmno) (r:42.12.32) (q:draft)
tawmpen = (t:adj) (w:fewest/smallest/least) (d:tawm, few, with pen, most: the smallest in number) (e:lakah a ~ na hi uh hi/Israel minamte sung panin a ~ Benjaminte | the Benjamites, the smallest of the tribes of Israel/a mi ~ Benjamin-te | Benjamin, the fewest in number) (a:tampen) (b:tawm) (r:5.7.7/9.9.21/19.68.27) (q:draft)
tawmsak = (t:v) (w:decrease/reduce/make less) (d:tawm, few, with the causative sak: make less; a man tawmsak is lower the price) (e:a man na ~ ding uh hi) (s:kiamsak) (a:tamsak) (b:tawm) (r:3.25.16) (q:draft)
tawmsak = (t:part) (d:placed after a verb that begins with ki: do the action to oneself, make oneself so, as kisiangtho tawmsak, consecrate oneself; tawm self with causative sak) (e:amaute mah kisiangtho ~ hen/nomau na kinin ~ kei ding uh hi | you shall not make yourselves unclean/Nangmah kilungso ~ ke’n | do not fret yourself/amau mah buhtu khawm ~ un | let them gather straw for themselves) (b:tawm) (r:2.19.22/19.35.13/3.11.43/19.37.8/2.5.7) (q:draft)
tawmsakin = (t:v) (w:let pick up/let glean) (d:tawm, pick up, with sak, let or cause, and the linking in) (e:ansang hong ~ anlate’ nungah) (r:8.2.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
tawmtawm = (t:adv) (w:a little/in small amounts) (d:tawm, little, doubled) (e:leenggahzu ~ na zang in) (r:54.5.23) (q:draft)
tawmte = (t:adj) (w:few/smaller/fewer) (d:tawm, few, with plural te: the few, the smaller groups) (e:Cina ~ tungah khut nga a/minam ~ tungah gamh a tawm na pia ding | to a smaller tribe you shall give a smaller inheritance/minam ~ tung panin tawm na la ding hi | from a tribe that has few you shall take few) (a:tamte) (b:tawm) (r:41.6.5/4.26.54/4.35.8) (q:draft)
tawmte = (t:part) (d:tawm, by itself, with plural te, after a verb: the things that do so of themselves, as in piang tawmte, what grows by itself without being sown) (e:Leitang sabbath kum-a piang ~ in/a piang ~ na ne ding uh hi | you shall eat what grows of itself/a milim bawl ~ uh | the images they made for themselves) (b:tawm) (r:3.25.6/3.25.12/24.8.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
tawmto = (t:v) (w:pick up/lift up/take up) (d:tawm pick up, with to, upward) (e:Amah ~ in la/tuikulhte pen leivui neel bangin ~ lel hi | he lifts up the islands like fine dust) (s:domto/lato) (b:tawm) (r:12.9.25/23.40.15) (q:draft)
tawmvei = (t:n) (w:short while/short time/little while) (d:tawm, few, with vei, time: a short stretch of time, used with sung, within, or ciangin, after) (e:~ khit ciangin tui a tehkik uh ciangin/Note kiangah ~ sung khuavak hong omlai ding hi | the light will be among you a little while longer/ni ~ sung thazaw gawpin | exhausted for some days/hun ~ sung a kingak lai nadingin | that he might be given a little more time) (s:Tawlno/tomkha/khano) (a:hunsau) (r:44.27.28/27.2.16/43.12.35/27.8.27) (q:draft)
tawmzaw = (t:adj) (w:less/fewer/smaller/scarcer) (d:tawm, few, with zaw, more: fewer, less; sangin marks what it is compared with) (e:a zawngte in ~ pia lo ding hi/a hawm guak sangin a ~-in | as less than nothing/a ~ hita leh a tamzaw hita leh | whether less or more/kham hoihte sangin a ~ | scarcer than fine gold) (a:tamzaw) (b:tawm) (r:2.30.15/23.13.12/23.40.17/4.22.18) (q:draft)
tawmzo = (t:part) (d:placed after a verb that begins with ki: be able to do the action for oneself; tawm, self, with zo, be able; kitankhia tawmzo, be able to redeem oneself) (e:a kitankhia ~ taktak) (b:tawm) (r:19.49.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
tawn = (t:v) (w:walk along/follow/go by way of) (d:travel along a path, and so follow a way of life; khekhap tawn is follow in the footsteps of someone) (e:thutang lampi ka ~ hi/a pa’ khekhap khempeuh ~ a | he followed all the ways of his father/Ahab innkuan lampite mah ~ hi | he too walked in the ways of the house of Ahab/Na u nu’ khekhap teng mah ~ | you have gone the way of your sister) (s:zui) (r:20.8.20/12.21.22/12.21.21/14.22.3/26.23.31) (q:draft)
tawn = (t:n) (d:counter for whole long objects such as a fish, a bar of gold or a scroll; ngasa tawn nih is two fish) (e:ngasa ~ nih longal a dang/shekel sawmnga a gik kham ~ khat | a bar of gold weighing fifty shekels/laizial ~ khat a tawi ka mu hi | I saw that it held a scroll/Sik ~ khat tawh | with a rod of iron) (r:40.14.17/6.7.21/26.2.9/19.2.9) (q:draft)
tawn = (t:v) (w:threaten) (d:say that one will do harm; written tawn’ with a final apostrophe, and tawn’na is a threat) (e:Amaute’ ~’na na lau kei un/mi khat’ ~’na tawh tulkhat tai-in | a thousand flee at the threat of one/khatvei a ~’ kik khit uh ciangin | after they had threatened them once more/~’na om loin na silate uh tungah | toward your slaves, without threatening) (s:tawng) (r:60.3.14/49.6.9/23.30.17/44.4.21) (q:draft)
tawna = (t:prep) (w:through/by means of) (d:tawn, go by way of, with the ending a; tung tawna, that came through a person, placed before a noun) (e:na nasem kamsangte tung ~ kote zuih dinga/keima tung ~ Topa’ thugennate | the words the Lord spoke through me) (b:tawn) (r:27.9.10/24.37.2) (q:draft)
tawng = (t:n) (w:inmost part/depth/bottom) (d:the deepest or innermost part: sung tawng is the inmost being, lungsim tawng the depth of the heart, tuipi tawng the bottom of the sea) (e:i sung ~ dong hong entel hi/i sung ~ hoih lohna teng siangsak hi | it cleanses the evil of our inmost being/tuipi ~ sungah bu ta le uh zong | though they hide at the bottom of the sea/ka lungsim ~ dongin hong nasak hi | it pains me to the depth of my heart) (s:sungtawng) (r:20.20.27/20.20.30/30.9.3/19.109.22) (q:draft)
tawng = (t:v) (w:threaten/intimidate/frighten) (d:frighten someone with words of harm) (e:sucip dingin mi ~ uh hi/note hong ~ bangin ka hi nuam kei hi | I do not want to seem to be frightening you/zuau genin kei hong ~ niloh uh hi | speaking lies, they keep threatening me) (s:tawn/lausak) (r:19.73.8/47.10.9/19.27.12) (q:draft)
tawngah = (t:n) (w:in the depths/in the inmost part) (d:tawng, inmost part or bottom, with the place marker ah: lungsim tawngah is deep in the heart, inn sung tawngah in the inner part of the house, dang tawngah on the roof of the mouth) (e:ka lungsim ~ ciimna hong hilh in/migilopa’ lungsim ~ thu gen a | it speaks deep in the heart of the wicked man/inn sung ~ lut un la | go into the inner part of the house/ka dang ~ ka leii toncip ta hen | let my tongue cling to the roof of my mouth) (b:tawng) (r:19.51.6/19.137.6/19.36.1/40.6.6) (q:draft)
tawnggawp = (t:v) (w:threaten) (d:tawng, threaten, with gawp, severely) (e:na ~ lo a) (b:tawng) (r:60.2.23) (q:draft)
tawngin = (t:adv) (w:in detail/thoroughly) (d:in the phrase a neng a tawngin, down to the smallest part, in full detail) (e:a neng a ~ i gen khinzo kei hi/a neng a ~ a lah kimna a lim | a drawing that showed it in every detail) (b:tawng) (r:58.9.5/12.16.10) (q:draft)
tawngin = (t:v) (w:threatening/warning) (d:tawng threaten, with the linking ending in, with a threat) (e:amaute ~ thu pia ni) (b:tawng) (r:44.4.17) (q:draft)
tawngkik = (t:v) (w:threaten back/threaten in return) (d:tawng, threaten, with kik, back) (e:lau nadingin ~ loin) (b:tawng) (r:60.2.23) (q:draft)
tawngnung = (t:n) (w:innermost part/inner part/far end) (d:the part furthest in, of a house, temple, prison or cave; often followed by sungah, inside) (e:thong ~ sungah khumin/leihawm ~ sungah na tu uh hi | they were sitting far back in the cave/inn sung ~ penah kherubte koih hi | he placed the cherubim in the innermost part of the house/Tua inndei ~ a teh ciangin | when he measured the inner room) (s:sungnung) (a:pualam) (r:44.16.24/9.24.3/11.6.27/26.41.4) (q:draft)
tawngnungah = (t:adv) (w:in the innermost part/into the inner part) (d:tawngnung, innermost part, with the place ending ah) (e:thong sung ~ amaute koihin/inndei ~ amah pai a | he went into the inner room/Topa’ biakinn sung ~ a siampite lut uh a | the priests went into the inner part of the temple of the Lord) (b:tawngnung) (r:44.16.24/26.41.3/14.29.16) (q:draft)
tawngtung = (t:adv) (w:forever/continually) (d:after kip, firm: last forever; apparently the word tawntung written with ng) (e:neihsa kip ~ lo a) (r:20.27.24) (q:draft, low confidence)
tawnin = (t:prep) (w:through/by way of/along) (d:tawn, go by way of, with the linking ending in: tung tawnin is through a person as agent, lam tawnin by the road of, khang tawnin all through a lifetime) (e:Topa in Malakhi tung ~ Israelte tungah/Heres kahtohna lam ~ ciahkik hi | he returned by the Pass of Heres/San Tuipi paina lampi ~ | along the route to the Red Sea/Beth-el ah hong paina lampi ~ ciahkik lo hi | he did not return by the way he had come to Bethel) (s:tungtawnin) (b:tawn) (r:39.1.1/12.3.8/7.8.13/4.14.25/11.13.10) (q:draft)
tawnlang = (t:n) (w:half/half the length) (d:of a furrow in a field: about half its length) (e:kuak dung ~ tan sungah) (r:9.14.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
tawnna = (t:n) (w:threat/rebuke) (d:tawn, threaten, with the noun ending na) (e:~ tawh mi tulkhat tai-in/mihing nga’ ~ tawh | at the threat of five) (b:tawn) (r:23.30.17/19.38.14) (q:draft)
tawnnate = (t:n) (w:threats/warnings) (d:tawnna threat with the plural te; in Jeremiah 17:15 of what the Lord has threatened) (e:kote hong ~ thei inla/Topa’ hong ~ koi lai takah om ahi hiam | where are the things the Lord has threatened) (b:tawnna) (r:44.4.29/24.17.15) (q:draft)
tawnpuk = (t:v) (w:fall full length/fall flat/fall prostrate) (d:fall down flat with the whole body on the ground; the second part is puk, fall) (e:leilakah Saul ~ pah hi) (s:puk) (r:9.28.20) (q:draft)
tawnsak = (t:v) (w:set on a path/make walk along/lead along) (d:tawn, walk along, with the causative sak: make someone walk along a path, as in lampi man tawnsak, start a child on the right way) (e:lampi man ~ lecin) (b:tawn) (r:20.22.6) (q:draft)
tawnsuk = (t:v) (w:go down along/flow down past) (d:tawn, go along, with suk, downward: run down along the side of something, said of water flowing down beside the altar) (e:leitaw lam pang ~ hi) (b:tawn) (r:26.47.1) (q:draft, low confidence)
tawntung = (t:adj) (w:continuously/nonstop/always/forever) (d:placed after a verb: going on without stopping or without end; uk tawntung is reign for ever) (e:mei kikuangsak ~ ding hi/Topa in uk ~ ding hi | the Lord will reign for ever/Topa in thupha ngah ~ ta hen | praise be to the Lord forever/Tua Pasian in minthan’na ngah ~ ta hen | to that God be glory for ever) (s:paisuak) (r:3.6.13/2.15.18/19.89.52/48.1.5)
tawntung = (t:prep) (w:throughout) (d:placed after a word for a span of time: through the whole of it, as nuntak sung tawntung, all through life) (e:a nuntak sung ~ Israelte thukhen hi/ama nuntak sung ~ Rehoboam leh Jeroboam kikalah | throughout his lifetime between Rehoboam and Jeroboam/Amau’ hun sung ~ Asa leh Israel kumpi Baasha | throughout their reigns Asa and Baasha king of Israel/sun ~ le zan ~ bangmah ne lo | he had eaten nothing all day and all night) (s:sungtengin) (r:9.7.15/11.15.6/11.15.16/9.28.20)
Tawntung = (t:adj) (w:everlasting/eternal) (d:tawntung, for ever, written with a capital in titles of God: Tawntung Pa, Everlasting Father, and Tawntung Pasian, the Eternal God) (e:tua lai munah ~ Pasian/~ Pasian in nangma omna hi a | the eternal God is your refuge/Vanglian Pasian, ~ Pa, Nopsakna Kumpi | Mighty God, Everlasting Father, Prince of Peace/~ Pasian’ min tawh thuciamna a bawl hi | he swore by the name of the eternal God) (b:tawntung) (r:1.21.33/23.9.6/5.33.27/27.12.7) (q:draft)
tawntunga = (t:adv) (w:always/forever/continually/throughout) (d:tawntung with the linking ending a, used before a verb or noun; a tawntunga kipan is from everlasting, khang tawntunga is throughout all generations) (e:a ~ thuman-a gamta mite in/Tuate a ~ kip dinga na bawl | you made them to stand forever/khang ~ kote omna mun na hi hi | you have been our dwelling place through all generations/hante pen khang ~ amau omna | their tombs are their dwelling for all generations) (s:ngitnget/den/gige) (b:tawntung) (r:19.106.3/19.90.2/19.119.152/19.90.1/19.49.11) (q:draft)
tawntungah = (t:prep) (w:all along/throughout/along the whole of) (d:tawntung, throughout, with the place marker ah, placed after the noun: along the whole length of it, as lam tawntungah, all the way) (e:lam ~ Topa na Pasian un/khuapi lampi laizang ~ a luang nuntakna gun | the river of life flowing down the middle of the city street) (b:tawntung) (r:5.1.31/66.22.1) (q:draft)
tawntungin = (t:adj) (w:continuously/nonstop/always/forever) (d:tawntung with the ending in; a tawntungin is always or for ever, and tu-a kipanin a tawntungin is from now on and for evermore) (e:A ~ na lungdam ta un/tu-a kipanin a ~ Topa muang in | from now on and forever trust in the Lord/ama mai a ~ zong un | seek his face always/Tua Pasian in a ~ vangliatna nei ta hen | to that God be the power for ever) (s:paisuak) (b:tawntung) (r:52.5.16/19.119.20/19.131.3/19.105.4/60.5.11)
tawntungna = (t:n) (w:eternity/everlastingness/endlessness) (d:noun form of tawntung, always: the state of lasting for ever; after a verb it names what goes on without end, as nuntak tawntungna, eternal life, and lungdam tawntungna, everlasting joy) (e:nuntak ~ kiciamna ahi hi/a umte khempeuh in nuntak ~ a ngah nading | that all who believe may have eternal life/lungdam ~ mai pua-in lasa kawmin | singing, with everlasting joy on their faces/tui a om ~ lei hoih mun khatah | in good soil where there is always water) (b:tawntung) (r:62.2.25/23.55.13/43.6.40/23.35.10/26.17.5) (q:draft)
tawntungnate = (t:n) (d:tawntungna, lasting for ever, with plural te; after a verb it names things that last for ever, as nop tawntungnate, eternal pleasures, and thukhen tawntungnate, eternal judgments) (e:na tak lam ah nop ~ om hi/misite’ thawhkikna, thukhen ~ | the resurrection of the dead and eternal judgment) (b:tawntungna) (r:19.16.11/58.6.1) (q:draft)
tawntungpa = (t:n) (d:tawntung, always, with pa, the man who; after a verb, the man who keeps doing it, as hong nawk tawntungpa, the man who often passes by) (e:hih i lampi hong nawk ~ in/i sanggamte mawhsakna a gen ~ | the one who keeps accusing our brothers) (b:tawntung) (r:12.4.9/66.12.10) (q:draft)
tawntungte = (t:n) (d:tawntung, always, with plural te; after a verb, those who always do it, as Topa a zahtak tawntungte, those who always fear the Lord) (e:Topa a zahtak ~ pen mi nuamsa hi/a thahat mite, leh gal a hang ~ khempeuh | the mighty men and all who are always brave in battle) (b:tawntung) (r:20.28.14/13.28.1) (q:draft)
tawntungun = (t:prep) (w:throughout/for all) (d:tawntung, throughout, with the plural ending un, used when several people are addressed; na khang tawntungun is throughout your generations) (e:na khang ~ thukham leh ngeina/Na khang ~ na an-ham uh a masa pen | throughout your generations the first of your ground meal/tua in na khang ~ na ten’na khempeuh uhah | this, throughout your generations, wherever you live/Topa in a thupiak-a kipanin na khang ~ | from the day the Lord gave the command and through your generations) (b:tawntung) (r:4.35.29/4.15.21/3.23.31/4.15.23) (q:draft)
tawnun = (t:prep) (w:throughout/all through) (d:tawn, along, with the ending un used of several people; in khan tawnun, all through life, as long as one lives) (e:Migilote a khan ~ khial uh hi/na khan’ ~ kilemna na hanciam kei ding uh hi | as long as you live you shall not seek peace with them) (b:tawn) (r:19.58.3/5.23.6) (q:draft)
tawnung = (t:adv) (w:forever/always) (d:in a nungta tawnung mipa, the one who lives forever, the Ancient of Days; possibly the word tawntung) (e:A nungta ~ mipa’ kiangah pai-in) (r:27.7.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
tawp = (t:v) (w:end/stop/finish/cease) (d:come to an end or bring to an end: a boundary ends at a place, a person stops doing something, a storm stops) (e:Tuipi ah ~ ding hi/amaute in akhuapi bawl uh ~ uh hi | they stopped building the city/A thuhilh a ~ khit ciangin | when he had finished teaching/Solomon a thunget a ~ ciangin | when Solomon finished praying/vanging leh gialpi ~ a | the thunder and hail stopped) (s:bei) (a:kipan) (r:4.34.5/1.44.12/1.11.8/42.5.4/14.7.1/2.9.33) (q:draft)
tawp = (t:adj) (w:last/final) (d:coming at the end, after all the others; Ni tawp Ni is the last day) (e:Ni ~ Ni-a thawhkikna-ah a thokik/Ni ~ ni ciangin ka thokik sak ding hi | I will raise them up at the last day/~ ni ciangin tua mi ka thokiksak ding hi | at the last day I will raise that person up) (s:nunung/tawpkhak) (a:masa) (r:43.11.24/43.6.39/43.6.54) (q:draft)
tawp = (t:v) (w:kiss) (d:touch with the lips in love or greeting) (e:tangvalpa thakhatin kawi-in ~ a/Na muk tawh nong ~ a | you kiss me with your lips) (s:nap) (r:20.7.13/22.1.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
tawpa = (t:v) (w:stop/cease/die down) (d:tawp, stop, with the linking a, and) (e:huihnung ~ a dai pah hi) (b:tawp) (r:41.4.39) (q:draft)
tawphah = (t:n) (w:foundation) (d:the base on which a wall is built; suangtawphah is a foundation stone) (e:kulh ~ suang sawm le nih) (s:nuaiphah/innbul) (r:66.21.14) (q:draft)
tawpin = (t:adv) (w:to the utmost/as much as possible) (d:after siam, hat or another quality, to the very limit of it; na siam tawpin is as well as you can, doing your best, and ka hat tawpin is with all my strength) (e:na siam ~ hanciam in/na siam ~ na kipuah hi | you adorned yourself as well as you could/Kidemna-ah ka hat ~ ka hih khin a | I have fought the contest with all my strength) (b:tawp) (r:55.2.15/23.57.9/55.4.7) (q:draft)
tawpin = (t:v) (w:stop/cease) (d:tawp with the linking ending in, stopping and then the next thing follows) (e:vanging ~ gialpi om nawn lo ding hi) (b:tawp) (r:2.9.29) (q:draft)
tawpkhak = (t:adj) (w:last/latter/final) (d:the one at the end, set against a masa, the first) (e:a lianzaw a ~ hih dikna) (s:nunung/tawp) (a:masa) (r:8.3.10) (q:draft)
tawpkhakna = (t:n) (w:end/conclusion/last) (d:the very end of a matter; a tawpkhakna-ah, at last, in the end, and a tawpkhakna kam in, finally) (e:A ~ kam in, note khempeuh/a sehsa bangin a ~-ah a hong bawl hi | in the end he has done as he planned) (s:tawpna/beina) (a:kipatna) (b:tawpkhak) (r:60.3.8/27.5.21/25.2.17) (q:draft)
tawpkik = (t:v) (w:fall away/turn back/give up again) (d:tawp stop with kik back: give up the faith after having begun in it) (e:amaute a ~ leh/A ~ khinsate a kisik kik nadingin | to bring back to repentance those who have fallen away) (b:tawp) (r:58.6.6/58.6.4) (q:draft)
tawpkikpah = (t:v) (w:fall away at once/give up quickly) (d:tawp, stop, with kik, back, and pah, immediately) (e:khat peuhpeuh a tun ciangin ~ uh) (s:pukpah) (r:40.13.21) (q:draft)
tawplam = (t:n) (w:ceasing/coming to an end) (d:tawp, stop, with lam: the fact of having stopped; ta neih a tawplam, that she had stopped bearing children) (e:ta neih a ~ a kimuh ciangin) (r:1.30.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
tawpna = (t:n) (w:end/last) (d:tawp, end, with the noun suffix na: the point where something finishes; a tawpna ah is in the end, finally) (e:a kipatna leh a ~ ka hi hi/a ~ ah phattuamna om lo hi | in the end there is no blessing/A ~-ah gulpi bangin hong tu ding a | in the end it will bite like a snake/amau’ thu ~ mu ding uh hi | they would see what their end will be) (s:beina/tawpkhakna) (a:kipatna) (b:tawp) (r:66.22.13/20.20.21/20.23.32/5.32.29) (q:draft)
Tawpna = (t:n) (w:end/last) (d:tawpna, end, written with a capital as a title of God, the End, beside Kipatna, the Beginning) (e:a Kipatna le a ~ ka hi hi) (a:Kipatna) (b:tawpna) (r:66.1.8) (q:draft)
tawpsak = (t:v) (w:stop/bring to an end/dismiss) (d:tawp, stop, with sak, cause: make work stop, or put someone out of his work) (e:ka nasepna panin hong ~ ding ahih manin/a lam khawl a, a nasep ~ hi | he stopped building and gave up his work) (s:khawlsak) (b:tawp) (r:42.16.3/14.16.5) (q:draft)
tawpta = (t:v) (w:have ceased/have stopped/be over) (d:tawp end with ta, marking a change that has now taken place) (e:a numei ngeina teng ~ hi) (b:tawp) (r:1.18.11) (q:draft)
tawptawp = (t:v) (w:kiss) (d:tawp, kiss, said twice: kiss again and again) (e:Na muk tawh nong ~ a/hong tuak taleng zong, kong ~ ding a | even if I met you outside I would kiss you) (s:nap) (r:22.1.2/22.8.1) (q:draft)
tawpun = (t:adv) (w:to the utmost/as much as possible) (d:placed after a word for strength or skill: to the limit of it, as in na siam tawpun, do your best; the subject is plural in all the verses) (e:Na siam ~ va hih unla/a nuntak laiteng a siam ~ gamta-in | doing as well as they can all their life/na siam ~ lamkalah hanciam un | try your very best on the way/a tha neih ~ kei tungah thu hong nget uh | they cry to me with all the strength they have) (b:tawp) (r:4.13.20/21.3.12/42.12.58/26.8.18) (q:draft)
tawsak = (t:v) (w:blind/make blind) (d:taw, blind, with the causative sak; used with mit, eye) (e:sumgolh in uliante mit ~ a/amaute in a mit uh ~ a | they struck their eyes blind/amaute’ mit ka ~ a | I have blinded their eyes/sakolte, a mit ka ~ ding hi | I will blind the eyes of the horses) (s:mittawsak) (b:taw) (r:2.23.8/1.19.11/43.12.40/38.12.4) (q:draft)
tawsakin = (t:v) (w:blind/make blind) (d:tawsak, make blind, with the linking ending in; said of the eyes, mit) (e:A mit uh ~, a lungsim uh/sumgolh in mi pilte’ mit ~ thumante’ thu heikhia | a bribe blinds the eyes of the wise and twists the words of the righteous/Kua in ama mit ~ man zo ding | who can blind its eyes and capture it) (b:tawsak) (r:43.12.40/5.16.19/18.40.24) (q:draft)
tawsaw = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:oak) (d:a large strong tree; tawsaw kung is an oak tree) (e:Bashan mual ~ kungte khempeuh/a teh a vul ~ kung | an oak whose leaves wither/~ khat kawm-ah Absalom kikhai ka mu hi | I saw Absalom hanging in an oak/Beth-el khang ~ nuai-ah amah kivui hi | she was buried under the oak below Bethel) (r:23.2.13/23.1.30/10.18.10/1.35.8) (q:draft)
Tawsaw = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:oak/tree) (d:tawsaw, oak, written with a capital at the start of a sentence and in the place name Aisaante’ Tawsaw, the diviners’ tree) (e:Aisaante’ ~ lam panin pawl khat/~ kung lak, singkung hing khempeuh nuai-ah | among the oaks, under every green tree) (b:tawsaw) (r:7.9.37/23.57.4) (q:draft)
tawsawte = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:oaks/great trees) (d:tawsaw, oak, with the plural te; Mamre tawsawte are the great trees of Mamre near Hebron) (e:Mamre ~ gei-ah hong pai-in/Mamre’ ~ gei-ah teng hi | he was living near the great trees of Mamre) (b:tawsaw) (r:1.13.18/1.18.1/1.14.13) (q:draft)
tawte = (t:n) (w:bottoms/depths/beds) (d:plural of taw, bottom; tuipi tawte, the bed of the sea) (e:tuipi ~ kimu a) (b:taw) (r:10.22.16) (q:draft)
tawte = (t:n) (w:the blind) (d:taw, blind, with plural te: a mit a tawte, those whose eyes are blind) (e:a mit a ~, bil nei napi-in) (s:mittawte) (b:taw) (r:23.43.8) (q:draft)
tazen = (t:part) (d:placed after a verb, before uh or hi, to stress with surprise or reproach that something really is so: actually, indeed, even; hi tazen leh is if only it were) (e:zuauthu na um ~ uh hi/nangawn in a thu a ngai ~ uh hi | even they obey him/thu-um lote mai-ah na kikhia ~ uh hi | you actually go to law before unbelievers/nangma pilna hangin kisia ~ hi | is actually destroyed by your knowledge) (r:24.7.8/40.8.27/46.6.6/46.8.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
tazo = (t:v) (w:hold/contain/have room for) (d:be large enough to take in an amount; contains zo be able) (e:khaici lawh nih a ~ dingin/a ~ dingin Topa’ mai-a sumngo biakna tau neulua | the bronze altar before the Lord was too small to hold them) (r:11.18.32/11.8.64) (q:draft)
te = (t:part) (d:particle suffixes to nouns indicating plural form) (e:mi~/lo~/pasian~/Israel mi~ leh Pasian kihta-~ aw | people of Israel and you who fear God/Baal~ leh Asheroth-~’ na sem uh hi | they served the Baals and the Asherahs/Binnui-~ beh panin Shimei | from the descendants of Binnui, Shimei) (r:44.13.16/7.3.7/15.10.38)
te = (t:ppm) (d:word indicating nominative case) (e:amau~/no~/Tua ciangin amau~ in | then they/leitang tungah amau~ teng lo ding uh hi | they shall not live in the land) (r:2.5.3/2.23.33)
Tebah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Tebah) (d:son of Nahor, the brother of Abraham, by his concubine Reumah) (r:1.22.24)
Tebaliah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Tabaliah) (d:Levite gatekeeper, the third son of Hosah of the clan of Merari) (r:13.26.11)
Tebeth = (t:name) (w:Tebeth) (d:tenth month of the Hebrew calendar, the month in which Esther was taken to King Xerxes) (r:17.2.16)
teci = (t:n) (w:witness/testimony) (d:a witness or what a witness says; teci pang and teci pan mean testify, teci pan’na means testimony) (e:Hih thute-ah ~ na hi uh hi/Thutak a gen ~ in nuntakna hu zo a | a truthful witness saves lives/kote khempeuh in ~ ka hi uh hi | we are all witnesses/Elna lungsim a nei ~ khat in | a malicious witness) (r:42.24.48/42.21.13/20.14.25/44.2.32/5.19.16) (q:draft)
Teci = (t:n) (w:witness) (d:teci, witness, written with a capital at the start of a sentence and as the name given to an altar) (e:biakna tau pen ~ phuak uh hi/~ nih bang thum bang kam hangin | by the word of two or three witnesses/~ tampi mai-ah keima kiang pan na zaksa nate | the things you heard from me before many witnesses) (b:teci) (r:6.22.34/47.13.1/55.2.2) (q:draft)
tecipan = (t:see) <tecipan'na>
Tecipan = (t:see) <Tecipan'na>
tecipan'na = (t:n) (w:testimony/witness) (d:the act or content of bearing witness; tecipan’na singkuang is the ark of the testimony, and in Deuteronomy 6:20 the plural sense is God's testimonies or stipulations) (e:Ahih hangin ~ om loin amahmah/~ singkuang a zawlte leh hehpihna tokhom tawh | the ark of the testimony with its poles and the atonement cover/Khazih’ thu ~ nomau lakah a kip ahih ciangin | because the testimony about Christ was confirmed among you/~ singkuang tungah hehpihna tokhom na koih ding hi | put the atonement cover on the ark of the testimony) (s:tecipanna) (r:44.14.17/2.39.35/46.1.4/2.26.34) (q:draft)
Tecipan'na = (t:n) (w:Testimony/covenant law) (d:tecipan, bear witness, with the noun suffix na; here the Testimony, the tablets of the covenant law before which the manna was kept) (e:kep dingin ~ mai-ah koih hi) (r:2.16.34) (q:draft)
tecipan'nate = (t:n) (w:testimonies/statutes/stipulations) (d:plural: the solemn declarations of God, listed together with his commands and decrees) (e:a ~ leh a thukhamte/ama ~ leh a thukhamte a zuihna ding | to keep his statutes and his decrees/amaute tungah a gen ~, thukhamte leh ngeina kipte | the stipulations, decrees and laws he gave them) (s:tecipannate) (r:5.6.17/12.23.3/14.34.31/5.4.46) (q:draft)
tecipanna = (t:n) (w:testimony/witness) (d:teci witness with pan and the noun ending na; in the verses the testimony, the decrees of God given to the king and set up in Israel) (e:Jakob sungah ~ khat a koih hi/kumpi hihna ~ lai amah a pia hi | he gave him the written testimony of kingship) (s:tecipan'na) (r:19.78.5/12.11.12) (q:draft)
tecipannate = (t:n) (w:testimonies/statutes) (d:tecipanna testimony with the plural te, named with the commands and decrees of God) (e:na ~, leh na thukhamte kemin/ama thupiaknate, ama ~, le a thukhamte a zuihna ding | to keep his commands, statutes and decrees) (s:tecipan'nate) (b:tecipanna) (r:13.29.19/14.34.31) (q:draft)
tecite = (t:n) (w:witnesses) (d:teci, witness, with the plural te; zuau tecite are false witnesses) (e:zuau ~ in khemna thu bek gen/Mi a el ~ hong kipan uh a | ruthless witnesses come forward/note in keima ~ na hi uh hi | you are my witnesses/A manlo ~ mangthang ding a | false witnesses will perish) (b:teci) (r:20.12.17/19.35.11/23.43.12/20.21.28) (q:draft)
tee = (t:v) (w:shine/sparkle/flash/gleam) (d:give off bright light, as polished metal or a precious stone; tee zalzal and tee daldal describe flashing and gleaming) (e:tua leengpeite suangmanpha bangin ~ hi/suangmanpha bangin ~ uh hi | they sparkled like a precious stone/luum leh teite ~ zalzal hi | spear and lance flash/sumngo zut siang bangin ~ daldal a | gleaming like burnished bronze) (s:taang) (r:26.10.9/27.2.31/26.1.16/18.39.23/27.10.6) (q:draft)
teei = (t:part) (d:placed after a verb for emphasis, still or at least; apparently a spelling of the particle tei) (e:a ngah ~ mah bangin/a sanghte nusia lai ~ uh hilo ahi hiam | would they not at least leave some gleanings) (s:tei) (r:30.3.12/31.1.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
teeiteei = (t:adv) (w:hard/persistently/with all effort) (d:placed after a verb: keep on doing with effort; apparently the word teitei written with ee) (e:lei lamah a hot ~ uh hi) (s:teitei) (r:32.1.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
teek = (t:adj) (w:old/aged) (d:advanced in years, said of people; also as a verb, grow old) (e:kei ka ~ hi/kumpipa ~ mahmah a | the king was very old/a khan’ ~ dongin ta a nei kei uh hi | they had no child until they were old/Lei sungah a zungte a ~ zongin | though its roots grow old in the ground) (s:ham/khangham) (a:khangno) (r:1.27.2/1.18.11/11.1.15/42.1.7/18.14.8) (q:draft)
teekin = (t:adj) (w:old/aged) (d:teek with the linking ending in: being old, having grown old) (e:Tu-in David ~ kum tampi pha a/Kumpi David ~ kum tam ta hi | King David was old and advanced in years/Jehoiada ~ a hun kicing a | Jehoiada was old and full of years/Tu-in kei ~ ka kum tampi pha ta hi | I am now old and well on in years) (b:teek) (r:13.23.1/11.1.1/14.24.15/6.23.2) (q:draft)
teeklua = (t:adj) (w:very old/too old) (d:teek, old, with lua, very or too much) (e:~ kisa-in ciangkhut khunin pai ding) (b:teek) (r:38.8.4) (q:draft)
teeknu = (t:n) (w:mother-in-law) (d:the mother of one's husband; teek old with nu marking a woman) (e:Ruth in a ~ beel hi/a ~ tawh amah omkhawm hi | she lived with her mother-in-law/A ~ kiangah a tun’ ciangin | when she came to her mother-in-law) (b:teek) (r:8.1.14/8.2.23/8.3.16) (q:draft)
teeknute = (t:n) (w:mothers-in-law) (e:monute le ~ a kidosak dingin) (b:teeknu) (r:40.10.35) (q:draft)
teekpa = (t:n) (w:master/owner/householder/landowner) (d:in inn teekpa, the master or owner of a house; teek with -pa for a man) (e:inn ~ a gensia uh hi/zingsanga a kuankhia inn ~ tawh kibang hi | is like a landowner who went out early in the morning/Tua lai takin inn ~ heh a | then the owner of the house became angry) (s:innteek) (b:teek) (r:40.20.11/40.20.1/42.14.21) (q:draft)
teekpa = (t:n) (w:father-in-law) (d:the father of a woman's husband) (e:Na ~ a tuute mul met dingin/amah in a ~ kiangah kam vaikhak a | she sent a message to her father-in-law/a ~ leh a pasal a sihna thu | the news of the death of her father-in-law and her husband) (b:teek) (r:1.38.13/9.4.19/1.38.25) (q:draft)
teekpen = (t:adj) (w:oldest/eldest) (d:teek, old, with pen, most: the oldest of a group, set against khangnopen, the youngest) (e:a ~ pan a khangnopen dongin) (s:hampen) (a:khangnopen) (b:teek) (r:43.8.9) (q:draft)
teeksak = (t:v) (w:make old/age) (d:teek, old, with the causative sak) (e:amah na ~ a) (b:teek) (r:19.89.45) (q:draft)
teeksiate = (t:n) (w:old people/old men/the aged) (d:contains teek old and the plural te; set against naupangte, children) (e:Nungak leh tangvalte, ~ leh naupangte) (s:teekte/khanghamte/puteekte) (a:naupangte) (r:19.148.12) (q:draft)
teeksih = (t:v) (w:die of old age/die old) (d:teek old with sih, form of si die: die at a good old age) (e:a khankhinin a ~ ta hi/Joash’ tapa Gideon ~ a | Gideon son of Joash died at a good old age) (r:18.42.17/7.8.32) (q:draft)
teeksihsak = (t:v) (w:let die of old age/give a full life span) (d:teeksih, die old, with the causative sak) (e:Note kong ~ ding hi) (b:teeksih) (r:2.23.26) (q:draft)
teekta = (t:adj) (w:old/aged) (d:teek, old, with ta, showing a state now reached: be old by now) (e:Kei ka ~ a, ka zi zong/tapa nei lo a, a pasal ~ hi | she has no son and her husband is old/a nih tuakun zong a ~ uh ahi hi | they were both old) (b:teek) (r:42.1.18/12.4.14/42.1.7) (q:draft)
teekte = (t:n) (w:the old/old people/the aged) (d:teek old, with the plural te; numei teekte are old women) (e:Numei ~ in a gen theih uh/A ~’ samkaang in minthan’na lukhu hi a | the gray hair of the old is a crown of glory) (s:khanghamte/puteekte) (a:khangnote) (b:teek) (r:54.4.7/20.16.31) (q:draft)
teekteek = (t:adv) (w:exactly/very/oneself) (d:emphasising word placed after another word: the very one, exactly so, in person) (e:keima kam ~ nangawn ngai lo ding uh/a kicihna leitang ~ mahah | in the very place where it was said/mite ~ in nang hong uk ni ciangin | when those very people rule over you/ka muhsa maitangte mah tawh kibang ~ a | they were exactly like the faces I had seen) (s:mahmah) (r:26.3.7/26.10.22/45.9.26/24.13.21) (q:draft)
teekteekin = (t:adv) (w:exactly/precisely/just) (d:after bang, exactly as; tua ni teekteekin is on that very day) (e:Esther’ sawl bang ~ gamta hi/Tua ni ~ Topa in | on that very day the Lord/numeite’ gen bang ~ va mu uh a | they found it just as the women had said/a thupiakna bang ~ amaute in sem uh hi | they did exactly as he had commanded) (b:teekteek) (r:17.4.17/2.12.51/42.24.24/14.8.15) (q:draft)
teel = (t:v) (w:choose/select/elect) (d:pick out one from among others: choose a person, a people, a place or the good; Pasian’ teel mite are those God has chosen) (e:Judah minam a ~ hi/minam khatah khat, note mi sawm-le-nih kong ~ hi | I chose twelve of you, one from each tribe/bukna khuapi dingin khuapite na ~ ding uh hi | you shall select towns to be cities of refuge/a hoihte a ~ theih hun ciangin | when he knows how to choose the good) (s:teelkhia/tengkhia) (a:nial) (r:19.78.68/19.78.67/5.1.23/4.35.11/23.7.15) (q:draft)
teelin = (t:v) (w:choose/select) (d:teel with the linking suffix in, choosing and then) (e:Makai khat ~ Izipt ah ciahkik ni/a hoihpen leh a kilawmpen ~ | choosing the best and most worthy/a nungzuite sam a, Sawm-le-nihte ~ | he called his disciples and chose the Twelve/Nangmah in Abram ~ Khaldea gam Ur khuapi panin | you chose Abram and from Ur of the Chaldeans) (b:teel) (r:4.14.4/16.9.7/12.10.3/42.6.13) (q:draft)
teelkhia = (t:v) (w:choose/select/set apart) (d:teel, choose, with khia, out: pick out from among others and set apart) (e:misiamte na ~ ding hi/ka nu’ gil sung pan hong ~ a | he set me apart from my mother’s womb/na suah ma-in kong ~ khin zo a | before you were born I had set you apart/a om lote nangawn a ~ hi | he chose even the things that are not) (s:tengkhia) (b:teel) (r:2.18.21/46.1.28/48.1.15/24.1.5) (q:draft)
teelkhiat = (t:v) (w:choose/choose out/select) (d:form of teelkhia used before a noun or in a dependent clause, as a teelkhiat mite, the people he chose) (e:a ~ khuapi Jerusalem ah/Pa Pasian’ theih kholh bangin a ~ mite | those chosen according to the foreknowledge of God the Father/Israel minam khempeuh sung panin ka ~ hih inn | this house which I have chosen out of all the tribes of Israel/Gentailte sung pan kimkhat a ~ ding | to choose some from among the Gentiles) (b:teelkhia) (r:11.14.21/60.1.2/12.21.7/44.15.14) (q:draft)
teelkhiatna = (t:n) (w:election/choosing/selection) (d:teelkhiat, choose out, with the noun ending na) (e:kei hong ~ thu na thei uh hi/Pasian ~ tawh kipawl hanciamna | the purpose that goes with God’s election) (s:teelna) (b:teelkhiat) (r:44.15.7/45.11.28/45.9.11) (q:draft)
teelkhin = (t:v) (w:have chosen/choose already) (d:teel, choose, with khin, already done) (e:na a sem dingin ~ ka hih manin) (b:teel) (r:44.9.15) (q:draft)
teelkholhsa = (t:adj) (w:chosen beforehand/foreknown) (d:teel, choose, with kholh, beforehand, and sa, already done) (e:Pasian in a ~ mite) (r:45.8.29) (q:draft)
