teembaw = (t:n) (w:ship) (d:a large vessel that sails on the sea; also written tembaw) (e:van pua ~ bangin/Tarshis kici ~ liante nang na susia hi | you destroyed the great ships of Tarshish/khut uh tawh ~ nate a paaikhia uh hi | they threw the ship’s tackle overboard with their own hands/amau upna ~ a siasak uh hi | they have shipwrecked their faith) (s:gunkuangpi/tembaw) (r:20.31.14/19.48.7/44.27.19/54.1.19)
teembaw-ahhong = (t:phrase) (w:to the ship/to the ark) (d:teembaw, ship, with ah, to, run together with hong, the verb prefix for motion toward the speaker, which belongs to the following verb; apparently a spacing misprint for teembaw-ah hong) (e:~ ciahkik hi/a khawl nading mu lo ahih manin ~ ciahkik | finding no place to rest, it came back to the ark) (r:1.8.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
