teen = (t:v) (w:dwell/live/reside) (d:form of teng written with an apostrophe before a suffix, as in teen’na, dwelling place) (e:Ama ~’na ngei mun panin/na ~’na mun bangzah takin etlawm ahi hiam | how lovely is your dwelling place/Jakob’ ~’na mun khempeuhte sangin | more than all the dwellings of Jacob/Khuamial sahpi sungah ~ ding a teel | who chose to dwell in thick darkness/tawl khat sung a ~’na leitang | the land where they lived for a while) (s:ten) (r:18.20.9/19.84.1/19.87.2/14.6.1/2.6.4) (q:draft)
teen'pihna = (t:n) (w:marrying/living together with) (d:teen, form of teng, dwell, with pih, together with, and the noun suffix na; of taking foreign women as wives) (e:gamdang numeite ~ tawh hih siatna) (s:ten'pihna/tenpihna) (r:16.13.27) (q:draft)
teeng = (t:v) (w:dwell/live/settle/inhabit) (d:live in a place, make one’s home there; a spelling of teng with a long vowel) (e:Amor mite’ gam sungah Israelte ~ hi/ama aituam innah ~ hi | he lived in his own house/lakah sauvei ka ~ lua khin ta hi | too long have I lived among them/Inn lam un la, a sungah ~ un | build houses and live in them/tua tungah ~ suak ding hi | they will dwell in it forever) (s:teng) (r:4.21.31/19.37.29/7.8.29/19.120.6/24.29.5) (q:draft)
teengin = (t:v) (w:dwell/live/settle) (d:teeng with the ending in, which links it to the following verb: dwelling, living there and) (e:tua sungah ~ sum bawl un la/keimah ~ amau’ Pasian ka hi ding hi | I will dwell there and be their God/Amaute hih gamah ~ | they have lived in this land/kumpipa ama inn sungah ~ | the king was settled in his house) (s:tengin) (b:teeng) (r:1.34.10/2.29.45/14.20.8/10.7.1) (q:draft)
teengkhawm = (t:v) (w:live together/live with/dwell with) (d:teeng, live, with khawm, together: live in the same place as someone; tawh marks the companion) (e:Jakob tawh bukte sungah ~ uh hi/nang tawh kumpi khuapi sungah ~ ding ahi hiam | should he live with you in the royal city) (s:tengkhawm/omkhawm) (b:teeng) (r:58.11.9/9.27.5) (q:draft)
teengmite = (t:n) (w:inhabitants/residents/dwellers) (d:teeng, live, with mi, person, and the plural te: the people who live in a place) (e:khuapi sungah a ~ in a khawh ding/Jerusalem khua a, ~ leh Judah mite tungah | to those who live in Jerusalem and to the people of Judah) (s:teengte/khuamite/tengte) (r:26.48.18/23.22.21) (q:draft)
