teenna = (t:n) (w:dwelling/dwelling place/home) (d:teen, dwell, with the noun suffix na: the place where someone lives; teenna mun is a dwelling place) (e:amau’ ~ mun khempeuh panin/na ~ vangtung panin | from heaven, your dwelling place/Pasian’ ~ na suah nadingun | so that you become a dwelling for God) (s:tenna) (b:teen) (r:14.11.13/49.2.22/14.6.39) (q:draft)
teenpih = (t:v) (w:marry/take as wife) (d:teen, live, with pih, together with: take a woman to live with as wife) (e:amah in Faro’ tanu ~ a/Rehoboam in Mahalath ~ hi | Rehoboam married Mahalath) (s:tenpih) (b:teen) (r:11.3.1/14.11.18) (q:draft)
teep = (t:n) (w:tassel/fringe/tip) (d:the hanging end or tip of something, as the tassel on the corner of a garment; bil teep is the lobe of the ear) (e:a puan mong ~ a lawng hi/a puan mong-a a ~ tungah khau dum khat | a blue cord on the tassel at the corner of the garment/taklam bil ~, a taklam khutpi | the lobe of the right ear, the right thumb/ama puan mong ~ beek a lawn’ nadingun | to touch even the edge of his cloak) (s:teepkai/mongteep/puanmongteep) (r:40.9.21/4.15.38/3.14.14/41.6.56) (q:draft)
teep = (t:v) (w:suck) (d:draw out with the mouth, as a baby at the breast; nawi teep is suck the breast, and guhtui teep kang is suck the marrow dry) (e:guhtui ~ kang hi/ama nawi a ~ naungek | the baby nursing at her breast/na ~ nawi in thupha a ngah ding hi | blessed are the breasts you sucked/gamlak singzung keu peuh ~ lel ding uh hi | they just suck the dry roots of the wilderness) (s:hup) (r:20.17.22/23.49.15/42.11.27/18.30.3) (q:draft)
teepin = (t:v) (w:sucking/nursing) (d:teep, suck, with the linking ending in; nawi teepin is sucking the breast) (e:nawi ~ nuam a sak mah bangin/a nu’ nawi ~, a ang-ah kipua a | nursing at their mother’s breast and carried in her arms) (b:teep) (r:23.66.10/23.66.12) (q:draft)
teepkai = (t:n) (w:tassel/fringe) (d:teep, tassel, with kai, hang: the tassel hanging at the edge of a garment) (e:a puan mong ~ a sausak uh hi) (s:teep/puanmongteep/mongteep) (r:40.23.5) (q:draft)
teepkang = (t:v) (w:dry up/suck dry) (d:teep, suck, with kang, dry up; of grief drying up the marrow) (e:maigum tawntungna in guhtui ~ hi) (s:teeptum) (r:20.17.22) (q:draft)
teepsak = (t:v) (w:suckle/nurse) (d:teep, suck, with the causative sak: give the breast to a baby) (e:naungek nawi a ~ ngei lo) (b:teep) (r:42.23.29) (q:draft)
teepte = (t:n) (w:tips/lobes) (d:teep, tip, with the plural te; bil teepte are the lobes of the ears and zangvun teepte are foreskins) (e:taklam bil ~ leh amau’ taklam khutpite/amaute’ zangvun ~ David in hong paipih hi | David brought their foreskins) (b:teep) (r:3.8.24/9.18.27) (q:draft)
