teh = (t:n) (w:leaf) (d:the leaf of a tree or plant) (e:a ~ a vul lo singkung tawh kibang hi/oliv ~ a tukkhiat thak khat | a freshly plucked olive leaf/a ~ longal bangmah a mu kei hi | he found nothing but leaves) (s:singteh) (r:19.1.3/1.8.11/41.11.13) (q:draft)
teh = (t:part) (d:particle with no English equivalent: after the conditional le-uh, if you, it links the condition to its result, and at the end of an exclamation it adds force) (e:Hong pai le-uh ~ na mu ding uh hi/Note in upna nei le-uh ~ | if you have faith/na hih le-uh ~, thupha na ngah ding | if you do them, you will be blessed/Khengval lua uh ~ | you have gone too far/A hai hi ~ | you are out of your mind) (r:43.1.39/47.11.1/40.17.21/43.13.17/4.16.3/44.12.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
