teldot = (t:v) (w:examine/question/inquire into) (d:tel, clearly, with dot, ask: question closely, look into; of a fault, call to account or rebuke) (e:Eite in i pumpi i ~ leh/sumbuka kizuak khempeuh ~ loin na ne un | eat anything sold in the market without asking questions/na mawhna hong ~ ciangin lungkia kei in | do not lose heart when he calls you to account for your sin/hong kilui khempeuh ~ loin na ne un | eat whatever is set before you without asking questions) (s:kantel/sittel) (r:46.11.31/46.10.25/58.12.5/46.10.27) (q:draft)
teldotna = (t:n) (w:examination/questioning/calling to account) (d:teldot, examine, with the noun suffix na) (e:thukhen ni ciangin ~ a thuak ding) (s:sittelna/thudotna) (b:teldot) (r:40.12.36) (q:draft)
teldotte = (t:n) (w:those who examine/those who question) (d:teldot, examine, with te, those who) (e:Keimah hong ~ kiangah) (b:teldot) (r:46.9.3) (q:draft)
Telem = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Telem) (d:town in the far south of Judah; also the name of a gatekeeper in the time of Ezra) (r:6.15.24)
telh = (t:v) (w:progress/advance/prosper) (d:of work or of a person’s way, go forward well; ma telh is make progress) (e:a nasep uh ~ mahmah uh hi/A ma uh a ~ loh manin | because they are making no progress) (r:15.5.8/38.4.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
telhak = (t:adj) (w:hard to understand/difficult to grasp) (d:tel, understand, with hak, hard: difficult to understand) (e:a ~ thu tampi om a/thuk lua a, ~ lua hi | it is too deep and too hard to understand) (s:theihhak/theihtelhak) (r:61.3.16/21.7.24) (q:draft)
Telharsha = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Tel Harsha) (d:town in Babylonia from which some exiles returned to Judah who could not show that their families were of Israel) (r:15.2.59/16.7.61)
telhsak = (t:v) (w:make prosper/give success/cause to advance) (d:telh, progress, with the causative sak; ma telhsak is make someone go forward, give success) (e:ka ma uh hong ~ ding a) (s:daupaisak/tuahphasak) (b:telh) (r:16.2.20) (q:draft)
telin = (t:adv) (w:clearly/thoroughly/with understanding) (d:tel clearly, with the adverb ending in; after en, look, or thei, know, look into or know a thing thoroughly) (e:hih thute thei ~ lim takin ciamteh ta hen/na khempeuh en ~ a thu kan ding | to look closely into everything and search it out/taktak a ~ hong kilat nai loh hangin | though it has not yet been clearly revealed/thu a ~ theihna | clear knowledge of things) (s:teltakin) (b:tel) (r:28.14.9/21.1.13/62.3.2/20.8.12) (q:draft)
telkheh = (t:v) (w:make plain/make clear/expose) (d:set a matter out openly so that it is clearly understood) (e:pawlkhatte-ah kong ~ mahmah hi/a ipcip uh thute hong ~ ding hi | he will expose the things they keep hidden/hangtakin genin ka ~ ding hi | I will speak boldly and make it plain) (s:laktel/pholak) (r:45.15.15/46.4.5/45.15.18) (q:draft)
telkhehna = (t:n) (w:making plain/plain speaking) (d:telkheh, make plain, with the noun suffix na) (e:Tua bangin ka hong ~ thu pen) (b:telkheh) (r:45.15.15) (q:draft)
tellam = (t:n) (w:understanding) (d:tel, understand, with lam: the fact that someone understands) (e:amau’ paute a ~ amaute in thei) (r:1.42.23) (q:draft, low confidence)
