teltakpi = (t:see) <teltakpi-in>
teltakpi-in = (t:adv) (w:very clearly/for certain) (d:tel, clearly, with takpi, truly, and the ending in: quite clearly, beyond any doubt) (e:tu-in ~ thei ta un) (s:teltakin/ciantakin) (r:24.42.22) (q:draft)
telthei = (t:v) (w:be able to understand/can understand) (d:tel, understand, with thei, be able) (e:leh thu ~ ding a kikhawm khempeuh/thu a ~ ding mite’ zakin | in the hearing of those who could understand/Theithei nai lo, ~ nai lo na hi uh hiam | do you still not see or understand) (s:theithei/theizo) (b:tel) (r:16.8.2/41.8.17/16.8.3) (q:draft)
teltheih = (t:v) (w:understand/be able to understand) (d:tel, understand, with theih, can: the form of telthei used before nading, ding and zawhna) (e:thu na ~ nadingun lim takin ngaihsun un/ngaihsunin a thu a ~ nading uh | so that they may consider and understand/mite in thukham a ~ nadingun | so that the people could understand the Law/a za ngei nai lote in ~ ding uh hi | those who have never heard will understand) (s:theihtheih/theihtel) (b:tel) (r:20.4.1/16.8.7/23.41.20/45.15.21) (q:draft)
teltheihna = (t:n) (w:understanding/ability to understand/discernment) (d:tel understand, with theih, be able, and the noun suffix na, the ability to understand) (e:thu ~ nei lo ahi hiam/a tapate leh a tanute, thu ~ a nei | their sons and daughters who are able to understand) (s:theihtelna/thutelna/telna) (b:teltheih) (r:19.53.4/16.10.28) (q:draft)
telzaw = (t:v) (w:understand better/understand more) (d:tel understand with the comparative zaw, used with sangin than) (e:Khanghamte sangin thu ka ~ hi/Ka siate khempeuh sangin thu ka ~ hi | I understand more than all my teachers/note in na ~ semsem ding uh hi | you will understand it more and more/siang takin na ~ semsem ding uh hi | you will understand it ever more clearly) (b:tel) (r:19.119.100/24.30.24/19.119.99/24.23.20) (q:draft)
telzawh = (t:v) (w:be able to understand/can understand) (d:tel understand with zawh, form of zo be able) (e:amaute’ ~ zah ciangciang thu a gen hi/a nasepna ziate kua’ ~ ding hi lo hi | no one can understand his ways) (s:telthei/theizo) (r:41.4.33/45.11.33) (q:draft)
tem = (t:n) (w:knife/blade/sword) (d:a knife or blade for cutting; meisuang tem is a flint knife, and Kha Siangtho tem is the sword of the Spirit) (e:a tapa that dingin ~ la hi/amah in ~ khat la a | he took a knife/Meisuang ~ bawl in la | make flint knives/Pasian’ Thu ahi Kha Siangtho ~ tawi un | take the sword of the Spirit, which is the word of God) (s:temta) (r:1.22.10/6.5.3/7.19.29/6.5.2/49.6.17) (q:draft)
