temta = (t:n) (w:knife/razor) (d:a knife; also a small knife for cutting a scroll and a razor for shaving) (e:a khut sungah mei leh ~ tawi hi/kumpipa in ~ neu khat tawh aat khia-a | the king cut it off with a small knife/a ha uh ~ tawh a kibang | their teeth are like knives/a kikawm ~ ahi Assiria kumpipa zangin | using a hired razor, the king of Assyria) (s:tem) (b:tem) (r:1.22.6/24.36.23/20.30.14/23.7.20) (q:draft)
ten = (t:v) (w:dwell/live/settle) (d:form of teng, live, written ten’ before words such as lai, hun and khit and before a suffix; ten’na is a dwelling place and ten’pih is live with or marry) (e:Tua gamah Israel a ~’ lai takin/Filistiate gam sungah David a ~’ hun sung | the time that David lived in Philistine territory/ama sanggamte khempeuh panin amah tuam ~’ hi | he lived apart from all his brothers/Kanaan leitangah Abram kum sawm a ~’ khit ciangin | after Abram had lived ten years in the land of Canaan) (s:teen) (r:1.35.22/11.8.49/9.27.7/1.25.18/1.16.3) (q:draft)
ten'pihna = (t:n) (w:marrying/marriage) (d:ten, dwell, with pih, together with, and the noun ending na: the taking of a woman to live with as wife) (e:teng gamdang numeite ~ tawh/Ammon numei, leh Moab numeite a ~ | that they had married women of Ammon and Moab/gamdang numei a ~ kimu hi | they were found to have married foreign women) (s:tenpihna/teen'pihna/kitenna) (a:kimakna) (r:15.10.2/16.13.23/15.10.18) (q:draft)
teng = (t:v) (w:live/dwell/settle) (d:have a home in a place or settle there; teng uh hi is they lived or settled) (e:a omna gamah Jakob ~ hi/Eden nisuahna lam Nod gamsungah ~ hi | he lived in the land of Nod, east of Eden/tua lai-ah ~ uh hi | they settled there/Tua hunin tua gamah Kanaan mite ~ lai hi | at that time the Canaanites were still living in the land) (s:teeng) (r:1.37.1/1.4.16/1.11.2/1.12.6)
teng = (t:v) (w:reside/stay/inhabit) (d:stay as a resident in a town, a land or a house) (e:ciangin Gerar-ah Isaak ~ hi/Judah gam sungah a ~ peemtate | the foreigners who resided in Judah/munmuanhuaina sungah David ~ hi | David took up residence in the fortress/kong gen ding leitangah ~ in | live in the land I will tell you of) (r:1.26.6/14.30.25/13.11.7/1.26.2)
tenga = (t:adj) (w:all/throughout/whole) (d:teng all, the whole of, with the linking a; follows a noun phrase: sung tenga is throughout, in all of) (e:gam sung ~ om Pasian biakna inn/Na gam sung ~ na bawl uh mawhna | the sins you have committed throughout your country/Ama nin neih hun sung ~ a lupna khempeuh | every bed she lies on during all the time of her discharge/hih bang ~ na gamtatnate tawh | with all these things you have done) (r:19.74.8/3.15.26/24.15.13/26.16.43) (q:draft, low confidence)
