tengkeek = (t:part) (d:after a clause, teng, all that, with keek: ka hih nop loh tengkeek, the very things I do not want to do; the force of keek is not clear from the verse) (e:ka hih nop loh ~ mah hih) (r:45.7.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
tengkha = (t:v) (w:live/happen to live/get to live) (d:teng live with kha, showing that the thing comes to happen; with kei, never get to live in) (e:inn sungah na ~ kei ding uh/mite lakah ka ~ hi | I live among a people) (r:30.5.11/23.6.5) (q:draft)
tengkhawm = (t:v) (w:live together/live with/dwell with) (d:teng, live, with khawm, together) (e:gamsate tawh na ~ ding hi/Mikah tawh a ~ dingin lungkim hi | he agreed to live with Micah/Jerusalem-ah Benjamin mite tawh a ~ uh hi | they live with the Benjamites in Jerusalem/a vak kawikawi mite a ~ ding uh hi | those who move about will live together) (s:teengkhawm/omkhawm) (b:teng) (r:27.4.32/7.17.11/7.1.21/24.31.24) (q:draft)
tengkhawmin = (t:v) (w:live together with/dwell with) (d:tengkhawm live together with the linking ending in: living with someone, and) (e:Gam sakolte tawh ~/Amaute tawh ~, amaute’ Pasian ka hi ding a | I will live with them and be their God) (s:omkhawmin) (b:tengkhawm) (r:27.5.21/26.37.27) (q:draft)
tengkhia = (t:v) (w:single out/pick out/select/separate) (d:choose and set apart from among others, for good or for punishment) (e:mi khempeuh lak panin amaute na ~ hi/Israel minam khempeuh lak panin amah ~ ding hi | he will single him out from all the tribes of Israel/A pil kumpipa in migilote ~ a | a wise king winnows out the wicked/thu ngaihsut siam mipil khat ~ in la | pick out a discerning and wise man) (s:teelkhia/khenkhia) (r:11.8.53/5.29.21/20.20.26/1.41.33) (q:draft)
tengkik = (t:v) (w:live again/resettle/settle again) (d:teng live, dwell, with kik, again or back) (e:nuamtakin a ~ ding uh hi/amau’ khuapite sungah a ~ masate | the first to resettle in their own towns/na khuapite sungah kuamah ~ nawn lo ding hi | no one will live in your towns again/Egypt gamah mi a ~ ding hi | people will live in Egypt again) (b:teng) (r:24.30.10/13.9.2/26.35.9/24.46.26) (q:draft)
tengkikin = (t:v) (w:live again/be inhabited again) (d:tengkik, settle again, with the linking in) (e:khuapite sungah ~ a sia khempeuh) (b:tengkik) (r:26.36.10) (q:draft)
tenglai = (t:v) (w:still live/go on living/remain) (d:teng live with lai still: continue to live or stay in a place) (e:Kanaan gammite tua leitangah ~ uh hi/lungsim sungah zuauthu bang tanvei ~ ding ahi hiam | how long will lies remain in their hearts) (s:omlai) (r:7.1.27/24.23.26) (q:draft)
tengpa = (t:n) (w:dweller/he who dwells) (d:teng live with pa, marking a man: the one who lives in a place; in both verses said of God) (e:a sungah a ~ tawh zong/sawlbawk lakah a ~’ maipha tawh | with the favor of him who dwelt in the bush) (s:teengpa) (b:teng) (r:40.23.21/5.33.16) (q:draft)
tengsak = (t:v) (w:settle/cause to live/make dwell) (d:teng, live, with the causative -sak: give someone a place to live) (e:tuate sungah Israel mite ~ hi/Amah in tua munah gilkialte ~ a | there he settled the hungry/Israel minamte amau’ buk sungah a ~ hi | he settled the tribes of Israel in their tents/a pa le a sanggamte a ~ hi | he settled his father and his brothers) (s:teengsak/tensak) (a:hawlkhia) (b:teng) (r:14.8.2/19.107.36/19.78.55/1.47.11) (q:draft)
tengsakin = (t:v) (w:let live/settle) (d:tengsak let live or settle with the linking ending in: letting someone live there, and) (e:~ sum bawlsak ni) (b:tengsak) (r:1.34.21) (q:draft)
tengsakkik = (t:v) (w:settle again/make dwell again) (d:tengsak, cause to live, with kik, again) (e:puanbuk sungah note kong ~ ding hi/na gam uhah kong ~ ding hi | I will settle you again in your own land/na gam sung uhah note kong ~ ding hi | I will settle you again in your land) (b:tengsak) (r:28.12.9/26.37.14/23.49.8) (q:draft)
tengsakkikin = (t:v) (w:resettle/make dwell again) (d:tengsakkik with the linking in) (e:uh sungah hong ~) (b:tengsakkik) (r:26.36.33) (q:draft)
tengsate = (t:n) (w:settlers/inhabitants) (d:those who had already settled in a place: teng live, with sa already and the plural te) (e:tua gamah a na ~ in) (s:teengsate) (r:15.4.6) (q:draft)
tengsuak = (t:v) (w:live on/dwell permanently) (d:teng live with suak through, onward: go on living in a place for good) (e:a khak dongun ~ ding uh hi) (s:tensuak) (r:26.37.25) (q:draft)
tengtawm = (t:v) (w:live of one's own accord/settle voluntarily) (d:teng live with tawm, which shows that the subject acts on his own) (e:amau’ thu-in a ~ nuam khempeuhte) (r:16.11.2) (q:draft)
tengte = (t:n) (w:inhabitants/those who live) (d:teng with plural -te, the people living in a place; the spelling of the 1932 text for teengte) (e:Babylon khua-ah a ~, a kumpi uliante/Zion khua-ah a ~ in gen ta uh hen | let the inhabitants of Zion say/Khaldea gamah a ~ khempeuh | all who live in Babylonia) (s:teengte/khuamite/teengmite) (b:teng) (r:24.50.35/13.8.13/24.51.35/24.51.24) (q:draft)
tengun = (t:adv) (w:as long as/all the while) (d:teng, all, the whole of, with the ending un used with a plural subject; after lai or sung, during all the time that) (e:pumpi-ah ka om lai ~ Pasian tawh/leitungah lal-a na om lai ~ | as long as you live as foreigners on earth/na paina gam uhah na nuntak lai ~ | as long as you live in the land you are going to/hih mun na tun’ ma sung ~ | all the time before you came to this place) (r:47.5.6/60.1.17/5.31.13/5.11.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
tengzo = (t:v) (w:manage to live/be able to dwell) (d:teng live with zo be able, succeed) (e:kumpi inn sungah ~ uh hi) (s:tentheih) (b:teng) (r:20.30.28) (q:draft)
tenin = (t:v) (w:living/dwelling) (d:ten live with the connective in: living, and then) (e:ama inn-ah tuam ~ kumpipa omna-ah) (b:ten) (r:10.14.24) (q:draft)
tenkhak = (t:v) (w:live/happen to live) (d:form of tengkha used before sangin, than: ten is the form of teng live, khak is happen to) (e:Meshek gam sungah ~ sangin haksazaw a/Kedar mite lakah ~ sangin siahuaizaw hi | it is worse than living among the people of Kedar) (r:19.120.5) (q:draft)
tenkhop = (t:v) (w:live together/live with/dwell together) (d:form of tengkhawm, live together, used before ding, sangin and khit) (e:eite tawh ~ ding/A phun hat zi gilo tawh ~ sangin | than to live with a quarrelsome wife/Phun bek a thei zi tawh inn sungah ~ sangin | than to share a house with a nagging wife/pasal tawh kum sagih sung a ~ khit ciangin | after she had lived with her husband seven years) (r:1.34.22/20.21.9/20.21.19/42.2.36) (q:draft)
tenma = (t:v) (w:before living) (d:ten live with ma before: before he lived or settled) (e:Haran khua-ah a ~) (r:44.7.2) (q:draft)
tenna = (t:n) (w:dwelling/dwelling place) (d:the place where one lives or has lived) (e:Zion khua sungah ama ~ mun kibawl hi/nangma ~ mun bangzah takin etlawm ahi hiam | how lovely is your dwelling place/vantung na ~ mun panin | from heaven, your dwelling place/amau’ ~ inn luhgawp kei in | do not raid their dwelling) (s:teenna) (b:ten) (r:19.76.2/1.37.1/19.84.1/11.8.49/20.24.15) (q:draft)
tennasa = (t:n) (w:former dwelling/place once lived in) (d:tenna, dwelling place, with sa, already done: the place where one has lived) (e:Na ~ Zion Mual hong phawk in/A pu a pate uh a ~ | where their ancestors lived/ama ~ munah ama gui a zom ding om lo | no one is left to carry on his line where he once lived) (b:tenna) (r:19.74.2/18.18.19/26.37.25) (q:draft)
tennopna = (t:n) (w:wish to live) (d:ten live, nop want, with the noun suffix na; na tennopna mun is the place where you want to live) (e:na ~ mun uhah namsau tawh) (r:24.42.22) (q:draft)
tenpakna = (t:n) (w:temporary stay/sojourn) (d:ten live, pak for a short while, with the noun suffix na: staying for a time, as nomads do) (e:na ~ uh gam sungah) (s:ompakna) (r:24.35.7) (q:draft)
tenpih = (t:v) (w:marry/take as wife) (d:live together with someone as husband and wife; ten with the ending pih, do together with) (e:numei dang a ~ leh/a pa’ zidangte ~ lo ding a | he shall not marry any wife of his father/Kanaan numeite na ~ kei ding hi | you shall not marry Canaanite women/siampite’ zi meigongte bek ~ thei ding uh hi | they may marry only widows of priests) (s:teenpih/kiteng) (b:ten) (r:42.16.18/15.10.17/5.22.30/1.28.1/26.44.22) (q:draft)
tenpihin = (t:v) (w:marrying/taking as wife) (d:tenpih marry, live with as spouse, with the linking suffix -in) (e:Amah in tua nu ~ luppih a/a sih ciangin Kaleb in Efrath ~ | when she died, Caleb married Ephrath/note in amau’ numeite ~ | you marrying their women/a nu’ tanu ~ a lupkhawm uhleh | if he marries the daughter of his mother and they lie together) (s:kitengin) (b:tenpih) (r:1.38.2/13.2.19/6.23.12/3.20.17) (q:draft)
tenpihkim = (t:v) (w:all marry) (d:tenpih live with, marry, with kim all, every one: each of them in turn married her) (e:tua nu ~ uh ahih manin) (r:40.22.28) (q:draft)
tenpihna = (t:n) (w:marrying/marriage) (d:tenpih, marry, with the noun suffix na: the act or fact of taking someone as wife) (e:gamdang numeite ~ tawh hih siatna/a nau Filip’ zi Herodias a ~ hangin | because he had married Herodias, the wife of his brother Philip/Moab numeite a ~ | that they had married women of Moab) (s:kitenna/ten'pihna/teen'pihna) (a:kimakna/makna) (b:tenpih) (r:16.13.27/42.3.19/40.14.3/16.13.23) (q:draft)
tenpihte = (t:n) (w:those who marry) (d:tenpih marry with the plural te: those who take someone as wife) (e:a kima numei a ~) (s:kiteengte) (b:tenpih) (r:40.5.32) (q:draft)
tensak = (t:v) (w:settle/cause to dwell) (d:ten dwell, with sak, cause, make someone or something live in a place; in Daniel 11.17 give in marriage) (e:Samaria khuapi-ah a hong ~ mite/Ka min ka ~ masakna Shiloh khua-a | at Shiloh, where I first made my Name dwell/Ama inn-ah amah tuam ~ in | let him live apart in his own house) (s:tengsak/teengsak) (b:ten) (r:15.4.10/24.7.12/10.14.24) (q:draft)
tensakna = (t:n) (w:causing to live/settling) (d:tensak make live with the noun suffix na: the fact of having made someone live somewhere) (e:buk sungah ka ~ thu) (b:tensak) (r:3.23.43) (q:draft)
tensuak = (t:v) (w:live on/dwell permanently) (d:ten live with suak through, onward: go on living in a place; another form of tengsuak) (e:na ~ theihna dingun) (s:tengsuak) (r:24.42.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
tentan = (t:adv) (w:stubbornly/obstinately/persistently) (d:placed after a verb: keep on doing it in a hard, unyielding way, as in zui tentan, follow stubbornly) (e:utna bang ciat na zui ~ uh a/Faro in eite paisak ding a nial ~ ciangin | when Pharaoh stubbornly refused to let us go/A vekpi-un hong langpan’ ~ uh a | they all stubbornly rebel/amau’ ngaihsutna bang bek-a a pai ~ nuam | who want to go on stubbornly in their own thoughts) (s:teitei) (r:24.16.12/24.6.28/2.13.15/24.13.10) (q:draft)
tentanin = (t:adv) (w:persistently/firmly/stubbornly) (d:placed after a verb: keeping on with it without letting go, as following one's own will or holding oneself in) (e:amau’ lungsim deihna zui ~/Ahi zongin Haman ki-iip ~ innah ciah hi | but Haman restrained himself and went home/ka hehna ki-ip ~ ka om lai takin | while I kept holding in my anger) (b:tentan) (r:24.9.14/17.5.10/38.1.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
tentheih = (t:v) (w:be able to dwell/be able to live) (d:ten, dwell, with theih, be able; na tentheih nadingun, so that you may live) (e:sawtveipi na ~ nadingun/lo kho-in a ~ nadingin | so that it may till the land and live there/a kiciamsa leitangah note na ~ nadingun | so that you may live in the land he swore to give) (s:tengzo) (b:ten) (r:24.35.7/5.30.20/24.27.11) (q:draft)
tentheihna = (t:n) (w:being able to stay) (d:tentheih be able to live with the noun suffix na; a tentheihna ding mun is a place where they can stay) (e:tuu cingin a ~ ding mun) (b:tentheih) (r:24.33.12) (q:draft)
tep = (t:v) (w:sap/drain/consume) (d:in tep tum, use up completely, said of foreigners who eat away a people's strength) (e:a thahatna teng uh ~ tum a) (r:28.7.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
tep = (t:v) (w:join/couple) (d:in tep nadingin singte, timber for the joists or couplings that hold a building together) (e:~ nadingin singte) (r:14.34.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
tepcip = (t:v) (w:trap/catch fast/ensnare) (d:of a snare, close on and hold tight; contains cip tightly) (e:thang bangin hong ~ a) (s:awksak) (r:21.7.26) (q:draft)
Terah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Terah) (d:father of Abraham, Nahor and Haran; also a camping place of Israel in the wilderness) (r:1.11.26/1.11.27)
terebinth = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:terebinth) (d:a tree, the English name kept in the text; terebinth kung is a terebinth tree) (e:poplar kung, leh ~ kungte nuai-ah) (r:28.4.13) (q:draft)
Teresh = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Teresh) (d:one of two officers of King Xerxes who guarded the doorway and plotted to kill the king) (r:17.2.21/17.6.2)
