tha = (t:n) (w:strength/power/energy) (d:the strength or energy of the body; tha neih khempeuh tawh is with all the strength one has, and tha neem is lose strength) (e:Ka ~ neih khempeuh tawh/tu-in i ~ bei ta a | now our strength is gone/a ~ ngeina zong kiam lo hi | his natural strength had not lessened/Zeisu’ ~ a hatsak hi | he strengthened Jesus/ka ~ neem ding a | my strength will grow weak) (s:thahatna/thatang/hatna) (a:thanemna) (r:1.31.6/42.22.43/4.11.6/5.34.7/7.16.7) (q:draft)
thacial = (t:n) (w:wages/hire/reward) (d:pay for labour; thacial nasempa is a hired labourer) (e:Pasian in ka ~ hong pia hi/~ nasempa’ aa bang hilo ahi hiam | is it not like that of a hired laborer) (s:thaman) (r:1.30.18/18.7.1) (q:draft)
thacialte = (t:n) (w:hired men/hired workers) (d:thacial wages with the plural te: those who work for wages) (e:gunkuang sungah ~ tawh a pa Zebedi) (s:cialte) (b:thacial) (r:41.1.20) (q:draft)
thacingin = (t:adv) (w:courageously/vigorously) (d:thacing, full of strength, with the connective in: being vigorous as a man is) (e:Pasal tawh kibangin ~) (r:46.16.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
thacingzaw = (t:adj) (w:stronger/sturdier) (d:thacing, full of strength, with zaw more: of better build or greater vigour) (e:a melhoihzaw, a ~ khat zong om lo) (s:thahatzaw/hatzaw) (r:9.9.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
thadah = (t:adj) (w:lazy/idle/slothful) (d:unwilling to work; mi thadah is a lazy person) (e:amaute ~ uh hi/Gilo, mi ~ nasempa aw | you wicked, lazy servant/Note na ~ uh hi | you are lazy/~ mi in a deih ngah zo lo a | the lazy person does not get what he wants) (a:thanuam/kizen) (r:2.5.8/40.25.26/2.5.17/20.13.4)
thadahhuai = (t:adj) (w:wearisome/loathsome/detestable) (d:thadah lazy, unwilling, with huai causing: such that one has no wish for it; zak thadahhuai sa is find it loathsome to hear) (e:Pasian in zak ~ sa hi) (s:kihhuai/muhdahhuai) (r:20.28.9) (q:draft)
thadahin = (t:adv) (w:lazily/idly) (d:thadah lazy with the adverb ending in) (e:mi pawlkhatte ~ na sem nuam lo/~ a zulhtat ute naute khempeuh na pel un | keep away from every brother who is idle and disorderly) (a:hahkatin) (b:thadah) (r:53.3.11/53.3.6) (q:draft)
thadahna = (t:n) (w:laziness/sloth/idleness) (d:thadah, lazy, with the noun suffix na: unwillingness to work) (e:Note khempeuh in ~ nei loin/~ in zawn’na hi a, thanuamna in hauhna hi | laziness brings poverty, but diligence brings wealth) (a:thanuamna/hahkatna) (b:thadah) (r:58.6.11/20.10.4) (q:draft)
thadahpa = (t:n) (w:sluggard/lazy man) (d:thadah, lazy, with pa marking a man: a lazy man, mostly as mi thadahpa) (e:Mi ~ in na sem nuam lo/Mi ~’ lo gei-ah ka va pai a | I went past the field of a sluggard/Lo khawh hun-a a kho nuam lo ~ in | the sluggard who will not plow in season/mi ~ a lupna tungah kiheihei hi | a sluggard turns on his bed) (a:hahkatpa) (b:thadah) (r:20.21.25/20.26.14/20.24.30/20.20.4)
thadahpa = (t:n) (w:idle/idler) (d:a man who is idle and will not work) (e:mi ~ ama ngaihsutna-ah pil kisa zaw hi | the idler thinks himself wiser) (b:thadah) (r:20.26.16)
thadahte = (t:n) (w:the lazy/sluggards/lazy people) (d:thadah lazy with te: those who are lazy) (e:a ~ sila suak hi/Mi ~ inn-ah lumlum a | the lazy lie about at home/Mi ~ in mun khempeuh ah haksatna tuak a | the lazy meet trouble everywhere/A ~ lumlum a | the lazy keep on sleeping) (a:thanuamte/thunuamte) (b:thadah) (r:20.12.24/20.19.15/20.22.13/20.15.19) (q:draft)
