thadim = (t:v) (w:be vigorous/be strong/be refreshed) (d:be full of strength; with sak, strengthen or refresh someone) (e:an lim tui lim ne-in ~ un la/cih leh amaute ~ uh a | because they are vigorous) (r:16.8.10/2.1.19) (q:draft)
thadimsak = (t:v) (w:strengthen/refresh/invigorate) (d:thadim, be full of strength, with sak, cause) (e:epel gah tawh hong ~ in/leenggahtui thak dawnna in nungakte ~ ding hi | new wine will make the young women thrive) (s:thahatsak/hatsak/thakhauhsak) (b:thadim) (r:22.2.5/38.9.17) (q:draft)
thaginalote = (t:n) (w:the weak/those who are feeble) (d:tha strength, gina adequate, lo not, with the plural te: those whose strength is not enough) (e:amaute lakah a ~ late tungah) (s:thanemte/zawngkhalte) (a:thahatte/mihatte) (r:14.28.15) (q:draft)
thagol = (t:adj) (w:huge/of great stature) (d:said of a very tall and big man) (e:Egypt mi khat, a ~) (s:thalian) (r:13.11.23) (q:draft, low confidence)
thagolte = (t:n) (w:giants) (d:plural of thagol, big and strong; mi thagolte, the giants, where the NIV has the name Rapha) (e:mi ~ sung panin apiang ahi hi/Gath-a mi ~’ sung pan-a piang ahi uh hi | they were descended from the giants in Gath/mi ~’ sung pana hong piang ahi hi | he was descended from the giants) (s:mithagolte) (b:thagol) (r:10.21.20/13.20.6/10.21.22) (q:draft)
thagui = (t:n) (w:sinew/tendon/muscle) (d:a sinew or tendon, the tough cord that joins muscle to bone; khel thagui is the tendon of the hip) (e:~ leh sazang in tua guhte tuam a/a om khel ~ ne lo uh hi | they do not eat the tendon of the hip/na ngawng uh sik ~ bang hi-in | your neck being like an iron sinew) (r:26.37.8/1.32.32/23.48.4) (q:draft)
thaguite = (t:n) (w:sinews/tendons) (d:thagui, sinew, with the plural te; guh leh thaguite is bones and sinews) (e:Guh leh ~ tawh ka pumpi ding) (b:thagui) (r:18.10.11) (q:draft)
Thagum = (t:n) (w:might/force/strength) (d:bodily strength or force, from tha, strength; written with a capital at the start of a sentence, and paired in the verse with vangliatna, power) (e:~ hat hang hi lo) (s:thahatna/thatang) (r:38.4.6) (q:draft)
thah = (t:n) (w:kill) (d:form of that, kill, used before ding, bangin, lai and the noun endings) (e:Lazaras zong ~ dingin a vaihawm uh hi/Zana Izipt mi na ~ bangin | as you killed the Egyptian yesterday/Judah mite in Saul ~ ding a vaihawm uh hi | the Jews plotted to kill Saul/~ dingin amah zong hi | he sought to kill him) (b:that) (r:43.12.10/1.4.15/44.7.28/44.9.23/2.4.24)
thah = (t:n) (w:killing) (d:the act of killing, in phrases such as thah khitna, the fact of having killed, and thah lai-in, while killing) (e:Topa siampite a ~ khitna thu/kamsangte a hon ~ lai-in | while she was killing off the prophets) (s:thahna/thatna) (b:that) (r:9.22.21/11.18.4)
thahat = (t:adj) (w:mighty) (d:tha, strength, with hat, strong: having great power, said of God and of warriors) (e:Pasian ~ mahmah napi-in kuamah simmawh lo hi/a ~ mi thumte’ ban-ah | beside the three mighty men) (s:vanglian/hat) (a:thanem/thaneem) (r:18.36.5/1.6.4/10.23.22)
thahat = (t:adj) (w:strong) (d:having strength of body or of faith; thahat un is the command be strong, and thahat lote are the weak) (e:Mi ~ in hiam tawi-in/A ~ eite in | we who are strong/Pasal tawh kibangin thacingin, ~ un | be courageous like men, be strong/a ~ kei hong honkhiapa aw | O my strong deliverer) (s:hat/thakhauh) (a:thanem/thaneem) (r:42.11.21/45.15.1/46.16.13/19.140.7)
thahatin = (t:adv) (w:strongly/with strength/firmly) (d:thahat, strong, with the adverb ending in: with strength, firmly; thahatin om is be strong) (e:Pasian ~ gualzo tawntung a/hehpihna thupha tawh ~ om in | be strong in the grace/A cidam a ~ kong om sak ding hi | I will make you healthy and strong/~ a gualzo ding uh hi | they will firmly prevail) (s:khauhtakin) (b:thahat) (r:18.12.16/49.6.10/55.2.1/23.58.11/27.11.32) (q:draft)
thahatna = (t:n) (w:strength/power/might) (d:thahat, strong, with the noun suffix na: the strength or power of God, a person or an animal) (e:Ka ~ ahi Topa aw/nangma ~ tawh mualte a bawl | who formed the mountains by your strength/ui’ ~ panin ka nuntakna hong hon in | deliver my life from the power of the dogs/Pasian in a ~ tawh mi vangliante susia a | God destroys the mighty by his power) (s:hatna/vangliatna/thatang/tha) (a:thanemna/thaneemna) (b:thahat) (r:19.18.1/19.65.6/19.22.20/18.24.22) (q:draft)
Thahatna = (t:n) (w:strength) (d:thahatna, strength, written with a capital at the start of a sentence or as a name by which God is addressed, my Strength) (e:Ka ~ aw, nangmah phatnate ka sa/~ sangin pilna hoihzaw a | wisdom is better than strength/~ thak kei hong guan hi | he gives me new strength/~ sangin lungduaina hoihzaw a | patience is better than strength) (a:thanemna) (b:thahatna) (r:19.59.9/19.59.17/20.24.5/19.23.3/20.16.32) (q:draft)
thahatnate = (t:n) (w:mighty deeds/achievements/strength) (d:thahatna, strength, with the plural te: deeds or displays of strength, as in ama thahatnate khempeuh, all his achievements) (e:na liatna leh na ~ na nasempa tungah/leh ama ~ khempeuh | and all his achievements/Judah kumpipa Amaziah a dona a ~ | his achievements in the war against Amaziah king of Judah/Israel-te’ ~ hong suksiatsak gawp a | he has destroyed the strength of Israel) (s:hatnate/vangliatnate) (b:thahatna) (r:5.3.24/12.10.34/12.13.12/25.2.3) (q:draft)
thahatnateng = (t:n) (w:all the strength) (d:thahatna, strength, with teng, all of: the whole of the strength of someone) (e:minam dangte in a ~ uh teeptum) (b:thahatna) (r:28.7.9) (q:draft)
thahatpa = (t:n) (w:strong man/mighty man/warrior) (d:thahat, strong, with pa, marking a man: a strong or mighty man, mostly as mi thahatpa) (e:En in, nang mi ~ aw/Mi ~ a hen khit ciangin | after he has tied up the strong man/Mi ~ bangin Topa kuankhia a | the LORD marches out like a mighty man/~ hen masa kei leh | unless he first ties up the strong man) (s:hatpa/galhangpa) (b:thahat) (r:23.22.17/7.14.14/41.3.27/23.42.13/40.12.29) (q:draft)
thahatpen = (t:adj) (w:strongest/most powerful) (d:thahat, strong, with pen, most: strongest; a thahatpen lai takin is at the height of its power) (e:a ~ lai takin a ki/a galkap mang lianpente khat ~ dinga | one of his chief commanders will become the strongest) (s:hatpen) (b:thahat) (r:27.8.8/27.11.5) (q:draft)
thahatpente = (t:n) (w:the strongest/the mightiest) (d:thahatpen, strongest, with plural te; galkap thahatpente, the best troops) (e:galkap ~ a thaneem ding uh hi/ka galkap ~ nuihsan lel a | he only laughed at my strongest soldiers) (s:hatpente) (b:thahatpen) (r:27.11.15/25.1.15) (q:draft)
thahatsak = (t:v) (w:strengthen/make strong) (d:thahat, strong, with sak, cause: give strength to a person, a people or the churches) (e:Ka mite ka ~ ding a/Judah mite, ka ~ ding a | I will strengthen the people of Judah/pawlpite hanthawnin a ~ hi | he encouraged and strengthened the churches/Ni nih sungin eite hong ~ ding a | in two days he will revive us) (s:hatsak/thakhauhsak/khauhsak) (a:thanemsak/thaneemsak) (b:thahat) (r:38.10.12/28.6.2/38.10.6/44.15.41) (q:draft)
thahatsakin = (t:v) (w:strengthening/making strong) (d:thahatsak, make strong, with the linking ending in: strengthening, and then) (e:Amah in minamte ~ liansak a/gamsung ~ kipsak uh hi | they make the country strong and stable/Note hong ~ hong cidamsak ding hi | he will make you strong and healthy) (s:thakhauhsakin) (b:thahatsak) (r:18.12.23/20.28.2/23.66.14) (q:draft)
thahatsakna = (t:n) (w:strengthening) (d:thahatsak make strong with the noun suffix na: the act of giving strength, also comforting) (e:nong ~ hangin) (s:thakhauhsakna/khauhsakna) (b:thahatsak) (r:19.86.17) (q:draft)
thahatsakpa = (t:n) (w:strengthener/one who gives strength) (d:thahatsak make strong with pa marking a male person: he who strengthens) (e:Hong ~ Khazih hangin) (b:thahatsak) (r:50.4.13) (q:draft)
thahatte = (t:n) (w:the strong/the mighty/mighty men/warriors) (d:thahat, strong, with the plural te: strong or mighty people, also warriors; often mi thahatte) (e:a ~ a hatna bei ding a/A ~’ thalte kitan a | the bows of the warriors are broken/mi ~ kiang panin mi cimawhte honkhia hi | he saves the needy from the powerful/mi ~ zong that thei hi | he can kill even the mighty) (s:hatte/mihatte/galhangte) (a:thanemte/thaneemte) (b:thahat) (r:30.2.14/9.2.4/18.5.15/18.34.20) (q:draft)
thahatthu = (t:n) (w:force/violence) (d:thahat strong with thu matter: the use of force; thahatthu ciam is try by force) (e:~ hong ciam uh hi) (s:zawhthawh) (r:40.11.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
thahatzaw = (t:adj) (w:stronger/mightier) (d:thahat, strong, with zaw, more: stronger; the thing compared is followed by sangin, than) (e:humpinelkal sangin ~ uh hi/amah sangin a ~ khat | one who is stronger than he/note sangin lianzaw-in a ~ minamte | nations larger and stronger than you) (s:hatzaw) (b:thahat) (r:10.1.23/5.11.23/21.6.10) (q:draft)
thahatzawte = (t:n) (w:the stronger ones) (d:thahatzaw, stronger, with the plural te: the stronger ones, in the verse the stronger animals of a flock) (e:Tuuhon sung panin a ~) (b:thahatzaw) (r:1.30.41) (q:draft)
thahin = (t:v) (w:being killed/slain) (d:thah kill with the connective in; thahin tuk is fall slain) (e:Gilboa Mual tungah ~ tuk uh hi) (b:thah) (r:9.31.1) (q:draft)
thahkha = (t:v) (w:to cause the death) see <thah> and <kha>
thahkhak = (t:v) (w:to cause the death) (d:thah, kill, with khak, happen to: come to kill; mostly in thahkhak loh nadingin, so that he would not kill) (e:a ~ loh nadingin Topa in/ta upa pen khempeuh a ~ loh nadingin | so that he would not kill any of the firstborn) (r:1.4.15/58.11.28) see <thah> and <khak>
thahkhawm = (t:v) (w:kill together with/put to death with) (d:thah, form of that, kill, with khawm, together: put to death together with others) (e:Jesuh tawh ~ dingin a paipih uh hi/migilote tawh thuman mite ~ ding | to kill the righteous with the wicked) (s:thatkhawm) (b:thah) (r:42.23.32/1.18.25) (q:draft)
thahkhit = (t:v) (w:have killed/finish killing) (d:thah, form of that, kill, with khit, finish; before ciang or mateng, after or until someone has been killed) (e:Paul ka ~ mateng uh/Paul i ~ ciang bekin | only after we have killed Paul/Paul a ~ mateng uh | until they have killed Paul/pumpi a ~ ciangin | after killing the body) (r:44.23.14/44.23.12/44.23.21/42.12.4) (q:draft)
thahloh = (t:v) (w:not kill) (d:thah, kill, with loh, not; thahloh nading, so as not to kill) (e:mi na ~ nading le nangma khut tawh/a nasempa namsau tawh a ~ nading | that he will not kill his servant with the sword/Kote le ka mite uh hong ~ nadingin | so that it will not kill us and our people) (r:9.25.26/11.1.51/9.5.11) (q:draft)
thahlohna = (t:n) (w:not killing/sparing) (d:thahloh not kill with the noun ending na: the fact of not killing someone) (e:nang kong ~ thu tawh thei-in/Nangmah in kei nong ~ ding ahi a | that you will not kill me) (b:thahloh) (r:9.24.11/9.30.15) (q:draft)
thahlup = (t:v) (w:kill/put to death/slaughter) (d:form of thatlum, kill, used before ding, khit, nang and sak) (e:mi pilte khempeuh ~ khit dingin/a tapate ~ sak a | he had his sons killed/mi pilte khempeuh ~ khit nang thu kipia a | the order was given to put all the wise men to death/A tangval hoihpente uh ~ dingin | their finest young men to be slaughtered) (s:thatlum) (a:nungtasak) (r:27.2.12/40.26.66/24.39.6/27.2.13/24.48.15) (q:draft)
thahlupsak = (t:v) (w:have killed/slaughter/kill) (d:thahlup, kill, with the causative sak: cause to be killed, as a king who has the sons of Zedekiah killed before his eyes) (e:muh mahin a tate ~ a/Zedekiah’ muh mahin a tapate ~ a | he had his sons killed before the eyes of Zedekiah) (s:thatlumsak/thatsak) (b:thahlup) (r:24.52.10/24.39.6) (q:draft)
thahmangna = (t:n) (w:killing off/destruction) (d:thah kill, mang away, utterly, with the noun suffix na: the act of killing so that none is left) (e:a ganhingin ka ~ ding thu) (r:26.25.13) (q:draft)
thahna = (t:n) (w:killing/murder/bloodshed/slaughter) (d:thah, form of that, kill, with the noun suffix na: the act of killing; mi thahna is murder or bloodshed) (e:mawhnei lo mi ~/Filistiapa a ~ panin David hong ciah ciangin | when David returned from killing the Philistine/Mi ~ leh thuman lohna tawh | with bloodshed and injustice/Saul’ innkuante na ~ hangin | because you killed the household of Saul) (s:thatna/mithahna) (b:thah) (r:20.6.17/33.3.10/9.17.57/10.16.8) (q:draft)
Thahna = (t:n) (w:killing/bloodshed) (d:thahna, killing, written with a capital at the start of a sentence and in the place name Mi Thahna Lo, the field of killing people, Field of Blood in the NIV) (e:Mi ~ Lo/~ a thuak Tuuno in | the Lamb who was slain) (b:thahna) (r:40.27.8/44.1.19/66.5.12) (q:draft)
thahnate = (t:n) (w:murders/killings) (d:thahna, killing, with the plural te: acts of murder) (e:amaute ~, mi bumnate) (b:thahna) (r:66.9.21) (q:draft)
thahnop = (t:v) (w:want to kill) (d:thah, form of that, kill, with nop, a form of nuam, want: wish to kill) (e:Mi khatpeuh a ~ leh that a) (s:thatnuam) (r:27.5.19) (q:draft)
thahnopna = (t:n) (w:desire to kill/bloodthirstiness) (d:thah, kill, with nop, want, and na: the wish to kill someone) (e:keimah hong ~ thu kikumkum uh hi/mi ~ lungsim le mi khemnopna lungsim | a bloodthirsty and deceitful mind/lungsim panin mi ~ | from the heart comes the wish to murder/Migilote’ thugente in mi ~ bekbek hi a | the words of the wicked seek only to kill) (b:thahnop) (r:19.71.10/20.12.6/19.5.6/40.15.19) (q:draft)
thahsa = (t:adj) (w:killed/slain) (d:thah, kill, with sa, already done: whom someone has killed; placed before the noun) (e:na pate un a ~ kamsangte’ han/Ishmael in a ~ misi luanghawm khempeuh | all the bodies of the men Ishmael had killed/na ~ uh misi luanghawmte | the bodies of those you have killed) (s:kithatsa) (b:thah) (r:42.11.47/24.41.9/26.11.7) (q:draft)
thahsak = (t:v) (w:have killed/kill/slay) (d:thah, form of that, kill, with sak: kill, or cause someone to be killed) (e:A galkap hangte khempeuh uh ~ un/a bia lo mi khempeuh a ~ theih na’ng | so that it could have all who did not worship killed/a tate uh ka ~ veve ding hi | I will still slay their children/Ka pate uh gal in hong ~ khin a | the enemy has killed our fathers) (s:thatsak/thatlumsak/thahlupsak) (b:thah) (r:24.50.27/28.9.16/66.13.15/25.5.3) (q:draft)
thahsakna = (t:n) (w:having killed/putting to death) (d:thahsak cause to be killed with the noun suffix na: the fact of having had someone killed) (e:ama nasemte a ~ hangin) (b:thahsak) (r:66.19.2) (q:draft)
thahsawm = (t:v) (w:plot to kill/plan to kill) (d:thah kill with sawm plan, intend) (e:Jew mite kikaikhawmin Saul ~ uh a) (r:44.9.23) (q:draft)
thahsawmna = (t:n) (w:plot to kill/plot/attempt on a life) (d:thahsawm, plan or try to kill, with the noun suffix na) (e:Jew mite in kei hong ~ hangin/hih a ~ thu uh | this plot of theirs/lamkalah amah a ~ thu za ahih manin | because he heard of the plot to kill him on the way/Jew mite pawlkhat in amah a ~ thu | the plot of some Jews to kill him) (b:thahsawm) (r:44.20.19/44.23.16/44.20.3/44.23.30) (q:draft)
thahsiang = (t:v) (w:kill off/make an end of) (d:thah kill with siang clean: kill until none is left) (e:Amaute ka ~ mateng namsau) (s:thatmang/thatlummang) (b:thah) (r:24.49.37) (q:draft)
thahte = (t:n) (w:the slain/those killed) (d:thah kill with the plural te: the people whom someone has killed) (e:a dang a ~ lakah namsau tawh) (s:kithatte) (b:thah) (r:6.13.22) (q:draft)
thahtheih = (t:v) (w:be able to kill) (d:thah, kill, with theih, can; in a thahtheih nading, so that they might kill him) (e:Jesuh a ~ nadingun a vaihawm uh hi/Amah ka ~ nadingin | so that I may kill him/Jesuh a ~ nading uh a vaihawm uh hi | they plotted how they might kill Jesus/Jesuh simmatin a ~ nading uh | to arrest Jesus secretly and kill him) (b:thah) (r:43.11.53/40.26.4/9.19.15/41.3.6) (q:draft)
thahzawh = (t:v) (w:be able to kill/put to death) (d:thah kill with zawh, a form of zo be able, overcome; thahzawh nading is the killing or death of someone, as a thing asked for) (e:na galte ~ nading) (r:11.3.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
thai = (t:n) (w:day after tomorrow/third day) (d:the day after tomorrow, the third day counting today; mostly thai ciangin, on the third day) (e:zing ciang leh ~ ciangin ka pai ding hi/A ~ ciangin teembaw vanzatte pawlkhat | on the third day some of the tackle of the ship/~ ciangin ka nasep ka man ding hi | on the third day I will finish my work) (r:42.13.33/44.27.19/42.13.32) (q:draft)
thai = (t:v) (w:rummage/scratch through) (d:search through a heap of rubbish) (e:nin buakna lak ~-in an a zong uh) (r:25.4.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
thak = (t:adj) (w:new/fresh) (d:new, not old or used before, also fresh; placed after the noun, as in la thak, a new song) (e:kumpi ~ khat Izipt gamah hong khang hi/la khaguh ~ khat mu a | he found a fresh jawbone of a donkey/Ama tungah la ~ sa un la | sing to him a new song/a keu nai lo thalkhau ~ sagih | seven fresh bowstrings not yet dried) (a:lui) (r:2.1.8/42.5.38/7.15.15/19.33.3/7.16.7) (q:draft)
Thak = (t:adj) (w:new) (d:thak, new, capitalised in the name Kongpi Thak, the New Gate of the temple) (e:lutna Kongpi ~-ah a tu uh hi/a Kongpi ~ tumna gei | by the entrance of the New Gate) (b:thak) (r:24.26.10/24.36.10) (q:draft)
thakah = (t:adj) (w:in the new/new) (d:thak new with the place marker ah, which belongs to the whole phrase: nuntakna thakah is in the new life) (e:hong piak nuntakna ~ a nungta ihi hi/a hon’ nuntakna lampi ~ | on the new way of life that he opened) (b:thak) (r:45.7.6/58.10.19) (q:draft)
Thakah = (t:adj) (w:new) (d:thak, new, with the place marker ah, in the name Kongpi Thak, at the New Gate) (e:biakinnpi lutna Kongpi ~ a tu uh hi) (b:Thak) (r:24.26.10) (q:draft)
thakbawl = (t:v) (w:renew/make new) (d:thak, new, with bawl, make: make new, renew) (e:ama hong itna tawh hong ~ ding hi/a hong ~ tawntung ahi hi | he is always renewing us) (s:bawlthak/thaksuaksak/thaksuahsak) (b:thak) (r:36.3.17/51.3.10) (q:draft)
thakhat = (t:adv) (w:suddenly/all at once/unexpectedly) (d:mostly in the phrase thakhat thu-in, suddenly, by surprise) (e:~ thu-in launa in hong buaisak hi/Joshua in ~ thu-in amaute sim gawp hi | Joshua attacked them by surprise/tomkha sungin ~ thu-in | suddenly, in an instant/~ thu-in keimah in ka sem a | suddenly I acted) (s:thakhatin/thakhatthu/vatin) (a:damdamin) (r:18.22.10/6.11.7/6.10.9/23.29.5/23.48.3) (q:draft)
thakhatin = (t:adv) (w:immediately/suddenly/at once) (d:thakhat, sudden, with the adverb ending in: suddenly, or at once without delay) (e:~ hong tung leh/~ a pumpi tang a | immediately she straightened up/Zeisu in tua pa ~ paisak a | Jesus sent the man away at once/amaute in ~ a ngen uh nusia-in | at once they left their nets) (s:thakhat/thakhatthu/vatin) (a:damdamin) (r:41.13.36/41.1.43/42.13.13/40.4.20) (q:draft)
thakhatthu = (t:adv) (w:suddenly/all at once/by surprise) (d:written with the ending -in, thakhatthu-in) (e:Joshua in ~-in amaute simgawp hi/~-in van panin ka kimkot hong taangzaih hi | suddenly a light from heaven flashed around me/~-in amaute tungah siatna hong tungvat ding hi | destruction will come on them suddenly/Tua bang mite ~-in kisugawp thei ding hi | such people can be destroyed suddenly) (s:thakhat/thakhatin) (a:damdamin) (r:6.10.9/18.22.10/44.22.6/52.5.3/20.24.22) (q:draft)
thakhauh = (t:adj) (w:strong/firm) (d:tha, strength, with khauh, firm: strong and firm; thakhauh un is the command be strong, and with sak it means strengthen) (e:~ un la, hang un/A ngawng ~ mahmah ahih manin | because its neck is very strong/Tangvalte aw, na ~ uh a | young men, you are strong) (s:thahat/hat) (a:thanem/thaneem) (r:6.10.25/18.41.22/62.2.14) (q:draft)
Thakhauhin = (t:name) (w:Thakhauhin/be strong) (d:thakhauh, strong, with the ending in, written with a capital at the start of a sentence: be strong and; not the name of a person or place)
thakhauhna = (t:n) (w:strength/encouragement) (d:thakhauh strong, firm, with the noun suffix na) (e:~ sangin thutheihna hoihzaw hi/note lungsimah ~ hong guan hen la | may he give strength to your hearts/~ le lametna a hong pia tawntung | who always gives us encouragement and hope) (s:thahatna/hatna) (a:thanemna) (b:thakhauh) (r:20.24.5/53.2.16/53.2.17) (q:draft)
thakhauhsak = (t:v) (w:strengthen/embolden/make strong) (d:thakhauh, strong, with sak, cause: make someone strong or firm, give courage) (e:nangma thu omsa bangin kei hong ~ in/Joshua thu pia in la, hanthawnin ~ in | commission Joshua, encourage and strengthen him/na thahatna tawh kei nong ~ hi | you strengthened me with your power/Babilon kumpipa ka ~ ding hi | I will strengthen the king of Babylon) (s:thahatsak/hatsak/khauhsak) (a:thanemsak/thaneemsak) (b:thakhauh) (r:19.119.28/5.3.28/19.138.3/26.30.25) (q:draft)
thakhauhsakin = (t:v) (w:strengthening) (d:thakhauhsak strengthen with the connective in) (e:Nang hong ~ ka hong huh ding) (s:thahatsakin) (b:thakhauhsak) (r:23.41.10) (q:draft)
thakhauhsakkik = (t:v) (w:revive/strengthen again) (d:thakhauhsak strengthen with kik again) (e:a kisik mite’ lungsim a ~ dingin) (s:nosuaksakkik) (b:thakhauhsak) (r:23.57.15) (q:draft)
thakhauhsakna = (t:n) (w:strengthening/giving of strength) (d:thakhauhsak strengthen with the noun ending na) (e:liatsakna ding le ~ ding na khut sungah/khut kha ban kha mite na ~ | your strengthening of those with feeble hands) (s:thahatsakna/khauhsakna) (b:thakhauhsak) (r:13.29.12/18.4.3) (q:draft)
thakhauhsakzaw = (t:v) (w:strengthen rather) (d:thakhauhsak strengthen with zaw more, rather; with loin: instead of strengthening) (e:amah ~ loin gimsakzaw hi) (b:thakhauhsak) (r:14.28.20) (q:draft)
thakiam = (t:v) (w:grow weary/weaken/lose strength) (d:tha strength and kiam decrease; a thakiam mi is a weak person) (e:~ loin ahoih nate na gamta un/zingsang khat khit zingsang khat ~ semsem | growing weaker morning after morning/a ~ mi leh a cimawh mite hehpih a | he takes pity on the weak and the needy/Tua bang thunget nading ~ loin | without tiring of such prayer) (s:thazaw/thakiat) (r:53.3.13/10.13.4/19.72.13/49.6.18) (q:draft)
Thakiamna = (t:n) (w:weariness/loss of strength) (d:thakiam, grow weary, with the noun suffix na: weariness; written with a capital at the start of a sentence) (e:~ lungkiatna a om loh nadingin) (s:tawlna) (r:58.12.3) (q:draft)
thakiamsak = (t:v) (w:weaken/make weary) (d:thakiam lose strength with the causative sak; thakiamsak loin is without letting strength fail) (e:~ loin kidem ni) (b:thakiam) (r:58.12.2) (q:draft)
thakiat = (t:v) (w:lose strength/fail in strength) (d:tha strength with kiat, a form of kia fall, used before ciangin) (e:ka ~ ciangin kei hong nusia kei in) (s:thakiam) (r:19.71.9) (q:draft)
thakin = (t:adv) (w:anew/afresh/newly) (d:thak, new, with the adverb ending in: anew; bawl thakin and a thakin bawl are make new, renew) (e:na lungsim uh bawl ~/na khempeuh a ~ ka bawl hi | I am making everything new/na khempeuh a ~ a kibawl hun dong | until the time when everything is made new) (b:thak) (r:45.12.2/28.14.6/66.21.5/44.3.21) (q:draft)
thakin = (t:v) (w:itching) (d:thak itch, with in; of ears that itch to hear something) (e:a bil uh ~) (r:55.4.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
thakna = (t:n) (w:renewal/newness) (d:thak, new, with the noun suffix na, usually after a verb: bawl thakna is renewal, kipat thakna a new start, nuntak thakna new life) (e:ni khat kibawl ~ a ngah hi/hih nuntak ~ thu mite kiangah va gen un | go and tell the people about this new life/kipat ~ a hong piak theih nadingin | so that he might give us a new start/Kha Siangtho’ hong bawlphat ~ tawh | by the renewal of the Holy Spirit) (s:thaksuahna) (b:thak) (r:47.4.16/15.9.9/44.5.20/56.3.5) (q:draft)
thaknu = (t:adj) (w:new) (d:thak new with nu marking a woman; mo thaknu is a new bride) (e:mo ~ a suangmanphate tawh a kizep) (b:thak) (r:23.61.10) (q:draft)
thakpa = (t:adj) (w:new) (d:thak new with pa marking a man; kumpi thakpa is the new king) (e:khuampi gei-ah kumpi ~) (b:thak) (r:12.11.14) (q:draft)
thakpat = (t:v) (w:begin anew/renew) (d:apparently thak new with pat begin: start again from new) (e:ka nuntakna uh ka ~ theih nading) (r:15.9.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
thaksiing = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:cassia) (d:a fragrant plant product traded together with thalsiing; the other text has taksing here) (e:a kihuansa sik, ~ leh) (s:thaksing) (r:26.27.18) (q:draft, low confidence)
thaksing = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:cinnamon/cassia) (d:a fragrant bark used as a spice; a namtui thaksing stands for cinnamon and thaksing nam khat, a kind of thaksing, for cassia) (e:a namtui ~ tua zah lang/~ nam khat za nga | five hundred shekels of a kind of cassia) (s:sinnamon/kinnamon) (r:2.30.23/2.30.24) (q:draft)
thaksuahna = (t:n) (w:renewal/refreshment) (d:thaksuah, a form of thaksuak become new, with the noun suffix na; lungsim thaksuahna is refreshment of heart) (e:lungsim ~ a ngah uh) (s:thathak/thakna) (r:57.1.7) (q:draft)
thaksuahsak = (t:v) (w:make new/renew) (d:thaksuah, a form of thaksuak become new, with the causative sak) (e:na ngaihsutna uh ~ un) (s:thaksuaksak/thakbawl/bawlthak) (r:26.18.31) (q:draft)
thaksuak = (t:v) (w:become new/be renewed) (d:become new or fresh again; with sak, make new, renew, refresh) (e:palhin ~ kik a, nitak ciangin/ka kha nuntakna uh a nini-in ~ semsem hi | our inner life is renewed day by day/zing nisuak bangin ~ tawntung a | new every morning like the sunrise/a tote’ lungsim ~ sak hi | he refreshes the spirit of his masters) (r:19.90.6/49.4.23/47.4.16/25.3.23/20.25.13) (q:draft)
thaksuakin = (t:v) (w:being refreshed/being renewed) (d:thaksuak become new with the connective in) (e:Saul ~ a ci dam a) (b:thaksuak) (r:9.16.23) (q:draft)
thaksuaksak = (t:v) (w:renew/make new/refresh) (d:thaksuak, become new, with sak, cause) (e:kicing a, nuntakna a ~ hi/na lungsim uh le na ngaihsutna uh ~ un | make your hearts and your minds new/lai mah bangin hong ~ kik in | renew us as in the days of old) (s:thakbawl/bawlthak/thaksuahsak) (b:thaksuak) (r:19.19.7/26.18.31/25.5.21) (q:draft)
thaksuaksakkik = (t:v) (w:renew/make new again) (d:thaksuaksak make new with kik again) (e:lai mah bangin hong ~ in) (s:nosuaksakkik) (b:thaksuaksak) (r:25.5.21) (q:draft)
thakte = (t:adj) (w:new/new ones/new things) (d:thak, new, with the plural -te, after a plural noun or alone as new things; zi nei thakte, the newly married) (e:a kizang nai lo khauhual ~ tawh/Delilah in khauhual ~ la-in | Delilah took new ropes/hong suak nunung pasian ~ | new gods that appeared recently/Tu-a kipanin, na a ~ | from now on, new things) (b:thak) (r:7.16.11/23.48.6/7.16.12/5.32.17) (q:draft)
thal = (t:n) (w:bow) (d:a bow, the weapon that shoots arrows; thal keek is bend the bow, and thal tawite are archers) (e:~ leh lum a tawi mi/sumngo ~ nangawn a keek zo hi | can bend even a bow of bronze/~ ginalo bangin amaute kihuiheek uh hi | they twisted like a faulty bow/a teipi uh, leh a ~ uh tawh | with their spears and their bows) (s:thalpi/thalpeu) (r:14.17.17/19.78.9/19.18.34/19.78.57/16.4.13) (q:draft)
thalawh = (t:v) (w:work for/earn/serve for) (d:work in order to get something as wages: a wife, flocks or food) (e:na tuuhonte kum guk sung kong ~ a/na tanu a nauzaw Rachel ~ nadingin | in return for your younger daughter Rachel/A gilvahte in an ~ uh a | those who were full hire themselves out for food/a khamkhop ding uh ~ zo lo uh hi | they cannot earn enough to be satisfied) (r:1.31.41/1.29.18/9.2.5/37.1.6) (q:draft)
