thangsak = (t:v) (w:glorify/make famous/spread abroad) (d:thang be famous with the causative sak: make widely known; with min name, glorify; of news, spread it abroad) (e:leitungah na min ka ~ zo hi/nangma min ka ~ ngitnget ding hi | I will glorify your name forever/tua thu gamsung khempeuh zelin a ~ uh hi | they spread the news through the whole region/zahtakin a min ka ~ hi | with honour I glorify his name) (s:minthangsak/thansak/pahtawi) (a:mindaisak) (r:43.17.4/40.9.31/19.86.12/27.4.37) (q:draft)
thangsakin = (t:v) (w:proclaiming/making known) (d:thangsak make widely known, with the linking suffix in; thu thangsakin is proclaiming a matter) (e:Nineveh khuasung khempeuhah thu ~ taangkosak a/antan’ ding thu ~ | proclaiming a fast) (b:thangsak) (r:32.3.7/32.3.5) (q:draft)
thangsakkik = (t:v) (w:glorify again) (d:thangsak glorify with kik again) (e:khatvei ka ~ ding hi) (b:thangsak) (r:43.12.28) (q:draft)
thangsakpa = (t:n) (w:one who glorifies) (d:thangsak glorify with pa marking a male person: he who glorifies) (e:Ka min a ~ in ka Pa ahi hi) (b:thangsak) (r:43.8.54) (q:draft)
thangsakte = (t:n) (w:those who glorify/those who bring honour) (d:thangsak glorify, make famous, with the plural te) (e:Khrih’ min a ~ ahi uh hi) (b:thangsak) (r:47.8.23) (q:draft)
thangsakzo = (t:v) (w:have glorified) (d:thangsak glorify with zo marking that the act is completed) (e:Ka ~ a, khatvei ka thangsakkik ding hi) (b:thangsak) (r:43.12.28) (q:draft)
thangsiah = (t:n) (w:fowler/trapper) (d:one who sets snares, especially for birds; thangsiah pa is the fowler) (e:vasa ~ bangin mite/~ pa’ thangzak le a lauhuai pulnatna panin | from the fowler’s snare and the deadly pestilence) (s:thangsiahpa) (r:24.5.26/19.91.3)
thangsiah = (t:v) (w:trap/ensnare/set a trap) (d:thang trap with siah set: set a trap for, try to catch someone by cunning) (e:migilote kihel uh a, vasa ~ bangin/bang hangin kei hong ~ se na hi uh hiam | why are you trying to trap me/khem siamna tawh na mite ~ uh a | with cunning they lay traps for your people/~ sim ding gen uh a | they talk of setting traps in secret) (s:awksak) (r:24.5.26/40.22.18/19.83.3/19.64.5)
thangsiahin = (t:v) (w:trapping/ensnaring/setting a trap) (d:thangsiah set a trap, with the linking ending in: by setting traps, trapping and then) (e:mite ~ a man uh hi/sila-in hong bawlin, note hong ~ | making slaves of you, ensnaring you/a kampau khialhnate a mattheih nadingun ~ a hanciam uh hi | they tried hard, setting traps to catch his mistakes in speech) (b:thangsiah) (r:24.5.26/42.11.54/47.11.20) (q:draft)
thangsiahna = (t:n) (w:trap/snare) (d:thangsiah set a trap with the noun suffix na: a trap laid for someone, or the laying of it) (e:a awk nadingin ~ ahi hi/Dawimangpa’ ~ tawh a kipelh nadingin | so that he escapes the devil’s trap/Jesuh a mawhsak theih nadingun a ~ uh ahi hi | it was their trap so that they could accuse Jesus/Jesuh a ~-in thu hong dong a | he asked a question to trap Jesus) (s:thang/thangzak/tehlop) (b:thangsiah) (r:20.29.5/54.3.7/43.8.6/40.22.35)
thangsiahpa = (t:n) (w:fowler/trapper) (d:thangsiah set a trap with pa marking a male person) (e:amah in ~’ thangzak leh) (s:thangsiah) (b:thangsiah) (r:19.91.3) (q:draft)
thangsiahte = (t:n) (w:fowlers) (d:plural of thangsiah fowler: those who set snares) (e:~ thangzak panin vasa a suahtak) (b:thangsiah) (r:19.124.7)
Thangsiahte = (t:n) (w:fowlers) (d:thangsiahte, those who set snares for birds, written with a capital at the start of a sentence) (e:~ thangzak panin vasa a suahtak bangin) (b:thangsiahte) (r:19.124.7) (q:draft)
thangtat = (t:v) (w:be sexually immoral/commit adultery) (d:a thangtat mite are adulterers or immoral people) (e:Pasian in a ~ mite le) (r:58.13.4) (q:draft)
thangtatin = (t:v) (w:being sexually immoral/living in debauchery) (d:thangtat be immoral with the connective in) (e:note tampi tak ~, numei tawh mawhna) (b:thangtat) (r:47.12.21) (q:draft)
thangtatna = (t:n) (w:debauchery/impurity/lewdness) (d:shameless sexual conduct, thangtat with the noun suffix na) (e:mawhna le ~, kitotna le kihazatnate-in/Numei tawh mawhna, ~ | sexual sin, debauchery) (s:hukna/lanna) (b:thangtat) (r:45.13.13/48.5.19) (q:draft)
thangte = (t:n) (w:snares/traps) (d:plural of thang trap) (e:sihna ~ in kei hong dawntuah hi/launa, dum leh ~ in no hong pang hi | terror, pit and snares await you) (s:thangzakte) (b:thang) (r:10.22.6/24.48.43) (q:draft)
thangzak = (t:n) (w:snare/trap) (d:a snare spread to catch birds or animals; also anything that entangles a person and brings him down) (e:a sabuai uh ~ suaksak in/Amau adingin ~ ahi | it is a snare to them/siatna bawlte’ ~ panin kei hong kem in | keep me from the snares of evildoers/lam gei-ah ~ tawh kei hong siah uh hi | they set a snare for me beside the path) (s:thangkhau/ngenthang/tehlop/thang) (r:19.69.22/2.10.7/19.106.36/19.141.9/19.140.5)
thangzakte = (t:n) (w:snares) (d:plural of thangzak snare) (e:gum le ~ om hi) (s:thangte) (b:thangzak) (r:23.24.17) (q:draft)
thangzaw = (t:adj) (w:more famous/more renowned) (d:thang, be famous, said of a name, with zaw, more) (e:mual liante sangin na min ~ a/Solomon’ min a ~-in bawl hen la | may he make Solomon’s name more famous) (r:19.76.4/11.1.47) (q:draft)
thankik = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:chameleon) (d:a kind of lizard, the last in the list of unclean creeping things, where the NIV has chameleon) (e:sehnel gam tangteuh leh ~ ahi hi) (r:3.11.30) (q:draft, low confidence)
thanop = (t:v) (w:be diligent/be eager) (d:form of thanuam eager, diligent, used before another verb or nading) (e:lawpin na ~ paisuak nading uh) (s:hahkat) (r:58.6.11) (q:draft)
thanopna = (t:n) (w:eagerness/enthusiasm/willingness) (d:thanop be eager, willing to work, with the noun suffix na; thanopna tawh is wholeheartedly) (e:~ tawh sem un/Note’ ~ lungsim in mi tampi a hansuah zo hi | your eagerness has stirred up many people) (s:lawpna/hahkatna) (a:thadahna) (b:thanop) (r:49.6.7/47.9.2) (q:draft)
thansak = (t:v) (w:glorify/make famous) (d:than, a form of thang be famous, with the causative sak; the same as thangsak) (e:Pasian’ min a ~ nading thu) (s:thangsak/minthangsak) (a:mindaisak) (r:43.21.19) (q:draft)
thante = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:worms/maggots) (d:plural of than) (e:~ in a ne uh a/~ pen nangma delhphah hi a | maggots are your bed/a sungah ~ om lo hi | there were no maggots in it/Tua hell khuk sungah ~ si ngei lo a | in that pit of hell the worms never die) (b:than) (r:44.12.23/2.16.24/23.14.11/41.9.48) (q:draft)
thanuam = (t:adj) (w:diligent/eager/willing) (d:glad to work, the opposite of thadah lazy; thanuam takin is eagerly, lungsim thanuam sak is encourage) (e:~ takin nasem hi/amaute’ lungsim ~ sakin a thahatsak uh hi | they encouraged and strengthened them) (s:lawp/thalawp) (a:thadah) (r:20.31.13/44.15.32) (q:draft)
thanuamin = (t:adv) (w:gladly/with encouragement) (d:thanuam eager, in good heart, with the connective in: being encouraged) (e:amaute ~ lungdam mahmah uh hi) (b:thanuam) (r:44.15.31) (q:draft)
thanuamna = (t:n) (w:diligence/industriousness) (d:thanuam diligent with the noun suffix na, the opposite of thadahna laziness) (e:~ in hauhna hi) (s:hahkatna) (a:thadahna) (b:thanuam) (r:20.10.4) (q:draft)
thanuamsak = (t:v) (w:stir up/encourage/make eager) (d:thanuam eager with the causative sak) (e:amaute tampi tak ~ hi) (s:hansuah/hanthawn) (b:thanuam) (r:47.9.2) (q:draft)
thanuamte = (t:n) (w:the diligent/diligent ones) (d:thanuam diligent with the plural te, set against thadahte the lazy) (e:Mi ~ vanglian a/~ in a deih ngah hi | the diligent get what they desire) (a:thadahte) (b:thanuam) (r:20.12.24/20.12.27) (q:draft)
thapai = (t:adv) (w:all through/throughout) (d:placed after zan night or sun day to mean the whole of it, all night long or all day long) (e:sun ~-in ama adingin thupha kingetsak ta hen/zan ~ lungkhamna in keima tanh ahi hi | nights of misery are my portion all night long/zan ~-in ki-itna bawlin | making love all night long/zan ~-in dahna lim puanhampi silh un | wear the sackcloth of mourning all night long) (r:19.72.15/18.7.3/20.7.18/29.1.13) (q:draft)
thasaan = (t:v) (w:rouse oneself/rise up) (d:apparently tha strength with saan: gather one's strength and rise to act; the verse has rise up in anger) (e:a hehsa-in ~ inla) (r:19.7.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
thasanpha = (t:v) (w:strengthen/take fresh strength) (d:said of making strong again what is about to die; built on tha strength) (e:a beimang ma-in ~ kik un) (s:thahatsak/thakhauhsak) (a:thanemsak) (r:66.3.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
that = (t:v) (w:kill/murder) (d:take the life of a person or animal, kill or murder) (e:Mi na ~ kei ding hi/tua khua mite ~ hi | he killed the men of that town/kumpi vangliante ~ a | he killed mighty kings/pasal khempeuh ~ uh hi | they killed every man) (s:thatlum/sisak) (a:nungtasak/hingsak) (r:2.20.13/41.6.19/7.8.17/19.135.10/4.31.7)
That = (t:v) (w:kill/destroy) (d:that, kill, capitalised in the title Mi That Vantungmi, the angel who kills people, the destroyer) (e:Mi ~ Vantungmi in Israel mite) (b:that) (r:58.11.28) (q:draft)
thatang = (t:n) (w:strength/physical strength/vigor) (d:bodily strength; thatang nasep is hard physical labour, where English has regular work) (e:a gim thei lo ~ nei hi/Na ~ teng numei tungah beisak kei in | do not spend all your strength on women/note’ ~ a mawkna-a bei hi ding hi | your strength will be spent in vain/Husan’ zawh nading ~ nangawn ka nei kei hi | I do not even have the strength to breathe) (s:tha/thahatna/thaneih) (a:thanemna) (r:18.41.22/3.23.35/20.31.3/3.26.20/27.10.17) (q:draft)
thatanghat = (t:n) (w:strength/force) (d:thatang strength with hat strong: sheer strength; thatanghat thu tawh is by force) (e:A ~ thu tawh mi tuahsia/~ thu tawh kumpi-in amah a koih sawmna thu | the plan to make him king by force/~ thu-in kong laksak ding hi | I will take it by force/~ thu tawh hihin amah luppih hi | he forced her and lay with her) (s:thahatna/thatang) (r:19.10.10/43.6.15/9.2.16/10.13.14)
thatanghatna = (t:n) (w:strength) (d:thatanghat sheer strength with the noun suffix na) (s:thahatna/thatang)
thatgawp = (t:v) (w:kill violently/destroy) (d:that kill with gawp, which adds force: kill without sparing) (e:Tua migilote ~ ding a) (b:that) (r:40.21.41) (q:draft)
thathak = (t:n) (w:new strength/refreshment) (d:tha strength with thak new; thathak ngah is be refreshed) (e:khual mite in ~ a ngah theih nadingin) (r:2.23.12) (q:draft)
thatin = (t:v) (w:killing/slaying) (d:that with the linking suffix in, joining it to the next action) (e:Izipt mipa ~ sehnel sungah seel hi/Judah mite in mi za nga ~ susia uh hi | the Jews killed and destroyed five hundred men/a tapate ~, Zedekiah’ mitte khelkhia uh a | they killed his sons and put out Zedekiah’s eyes/khuapi sunga teeng Kanaan mite ~ | killing the Canaanites who lived in the city) (b:that) (r:2.2.12/17.9.6/12.25.7/11.9.16) (q:draft)
thatkha = (t:v) (w:kill accidentally/happen to kill) (d:that kill with kha, which shows that the act comes to happen or reaches its object: kill someone without intending it; thatkha lo is did not get to kill) (e:sawm lopi-in mi khatpeuh a ~/Mi a ~ peuhpeuh a tai theih nadingin | so that anyone who kills a person may flee/tua nu in amah ~ lo hi | she did not get to kill him) (r:4.35.11/5.19.3/14.22.11) (q:draft)
thatkhate = (t:n) (w:those who kill accidentally) (d:thatkha happen to kill with the plural te) (e:mi khatpeuh a ~ a tai theih nadingin) (b:thatkha) (r:4.35.15) (q:draft)
thatkhawm = (t:v) (w:kill together with/kill along with) (d:that kill with khawm together) (e:lakah namsau tawh ~ uh hi) (s:thahkhawm) (b:that) (r:6.13.22) (q:draft)
thatkhin = (t:v) (w:kill/put to death) (d:that kill with khin marking a completed action: have killed, kill off) (e:namsau tawh gancingte ~ uh hi/tua Thukham mah in kei hong ~ | that very Law has put me to death) (b:that) (r:18.1.15/48.2.19) (q:draft)
thatkikin = (t:v) (w:killing again) (d:that kill, kik again, with the connective in; here of crucifying the Son of God a second time) (e:Pasian’ Tapa ~ a zumhuai dingin) (r:58.6.6) (q:draft)
thatlum = (t:v) (w:kill/slay/put to death) (d:that kill with lum: kill outright, put to death) (e:meigong numei leh khualmi ~ uh a/mi gilote namsau tawh a ~ ding hi | he will put the wicked to death by the sword/ama khut in a taikhia gulpi ~ hi | his hand killed the fleeing serpent/Judah gam kumpi ulian khempeuh zong a ~ hi | he also killed all the nobles of Judah) (s:that/sisak) (a:nungtasak) (r:19.94.6/24.39.6/24.25.31/18.26.13) (q:draft)
thatlumin = (t:v) (w:killing/slaying) (d:thatlum, kill, with the linking ending in: killing, before the next action in the sentence) (e:meigong numeite le khualmite ~/khualmite ~ pa nei lote suamlum uh hi | they slay the foreigner and murder the fatherless) (b:thatlum) (r:19.94.6) (q:draft)
thatlummang = (t:v) (w:kill off/wipe out) (d:thatlum, kill, with mang, away: kill off so that none are left) (e:na ganhingte ~ ding uh hi/na mite le na ganhingte ~ | they will kill off your people and your animals) (s:thatmang) (r:26.29.8) (q:draft)
thatlumsak = (t:v) (w:slaughter/have killed) (d:thatlum, kill, with the causative sak: have people killed, slaughter) (e:na heh ni-in na ~ hi/Amaute hehpih loin na heh ni-in na ~ hi | without pity you slaughtered them in the day of your anger) (s:thahlupsak/thatsak) (b:thatlum) (r:25.2.21) (q:draft)
thatmang = (t:v) (w:kill off/destroy completely/wipe out) (d:that, kill, with mang, gone: kill so that none are left) (e:mi khempeuh namsau tawh ~ hi/a dangte ka ~ khin uh hi | we totally destroyed the rest/namsau tawh amaute vatin ~ khin hi | he struck them with the sword and destroyed them completely/hun khat sungin ~ khin hi | he killed them all at one time) (s:thatlummang) (a:siit/hingkhawi) (r:9.15.8/9.15.9/9.15.15/6.11.12/10.23.8) (q:draft)
thatna = (t:n) (w:killing/slaying) (d:that, kill, with the noun suffix na: the act of killing; a thatna hangin is because he killed) (e:thu om lopi-in mi a ~ hangin/Midian kumpite a ~ uhah | when they killed the kings of Midian) (s:thahna/mithahna) (b:that) (r:11.2.31/4.31.8) (q:draft)
thatnuam = (t:v) (w:want to kill/seek to kill) (d:that, kill, with nuam, want: want or seek to kill someone) (e:upate in amah ~ uh hi/Herodias in Johan mudahin ~ a | Herodias hated John and wanted to kill him/a ~ mite’ khut sungah ka pia ding hi | I will hand them over to those who want to kill them/kei zong a hong ~ na hi hiam | do you want to kill me too) (r:42.19.47/41.6.19/24.34.20/44.7.28) (q:draft)
thatnuamte = (t:n) (w:those who want to kill) (d:thatnuam, want to kill, with the plural te: those who want to kill someone) (e:nang hong ~’ khut sungah/a ~’ khutlumin amaute ka sisak ding hi | I will make them die at the hands of those who want to kill them) (b:thatnuam) (r:24.22.25/24.19.7) (q:draft)
thatpa = (t:n) (w:killer/murderer/slayer) (d:that, kill, with pa marking a man: one who kills, a murderer; mi thatpa is a murderer and a thatpa is whoever kills) (e:Mi a ~ kithat ding hi/mi ~ khah nadingin na ngen uh a | you asked for a murderer to be released/nang mi ~, bangmah man lo mipa | you murderer, you worthless man/a topa a ~ aw | you murderer of your master) (s:mithatpa/mithat) (b:that) (r:3.24.17/44.3.14/10.16.7/12.9.31) (q:draft)
thatsak = (t:v) (w:have killed/put to death/have executed) (d:that, kill, with the causative sak: order or cause someone to be killed) (e:kumpi innkuan khempeuh ~ hi/thu a dot khit ciangin a ~ hi | after questioning them he had them put to death/James pen namsau tawh ~ hi | he had James put to death with the sword/a pate khia-in a ~ ding uh hi | they will hand over their parents and have them put to death) (s:sisak/thatlumsak) (b:that) (r:12.11.1/44.12.19/44.12.2/41.13.12) (q:draft)
thatsim = (t:v) (w:kill secretly/murder in secret) (d:that, kill, with sim, secretly: kill someone in secret) (e:A vengpa a ~ mipa in/a ~ mipa in gimna ngah ta hen | cursed be the man who kills in secret) (r:5.27.24) (q:draft)
thatte = (t:n) (w:murderers/killers) (d:that, kill, with the plural te: those who kill, usually said as mi thatte, murderers) (e:tua mi ~ khempeuh thatin/tu-in mi ~ bek a om hi | now only murderers live there/Mi ~ in zum innah thukhenna thuak ding hi | murderers will face judgment in court/mi ~’ tate that lo hi | he did not kill the children of the murderers) (s:mithatte) (b:that) (r:40.22.7/40.5.21/23.1.21/12.14.6) (q:draft)
thatthat = (t:v) (w:keep on killing) (d:that kill, doubled to show that the act goes on and on) (e:mi ~ ding uh ahi hiam/hehpihna mel nei loin mi ~ ding | to go on killing people without mercy) (r:35.1.17) (q:draft)
thatzaw = (t:v) (w:kill rather/kill instead) (d:that, kill, with zaw, rather: kill instead, as the better thing to do) (e:thakhatin hong ~ in/nong hehpih zawh leh, thakhatin hong ~ in | if you have mercy on me, kill me at once) (b:that) (r:4.11.15) (q:draft)
thatzo = (t:v) (w:manage to kill/succeed in killing) (d:that kill with zo be able, succeed; thatzo dektak is almost kill) (e:kei hong ~ dektak uh hi) (b:that) (r:19.119.87) (q:draft)
thau = (t:n) (w:fat) (d:the fat of an animal, especially the fat parts burned on the altar in an offering) (e:amah in a ~ khempeuh la-in/a ki-at nente leh a ~ hal hi | he burned the pieces and the fat/ganhing ~ a ne mi peuhmah | anyone who eats the fat of an animal/tuunote leh tuutalte’ ~ tawh | with the fat of lambs and rams) (s:sathau) (r:3.4.19/3.7.3/3.8.20/3.7.25/5.32.14) (q:draft)
thau = (t:adj) (w:fat/fattened) (d:well fed and full of flesh, said of animals; bawngno thau is a fattened calf) (e:a masa a ~ bawngpi sagihte/Bawngno a ~ hong paipihin go un | bring the fattened calf and kill it/bawngno ~ khat nei a | she had a fattened calf/a zol a ~ bawngpi sagihte | the seven sleek, fat cows) (a:gawng) (r:1.41.20/42.15.23/9.28.24/1.41.4) (q:draft)
thaukhal = (t:n) (w:curds/butter) (d:the thick, fatty part of milk, curds or butter, usually said as bawngnawi thaukhal) (e:bawngnawi ~ leh khuaizu ne ding hi/tua nu in bawngnawi ~ paipih hi | she brought him curdled milk/Bawnghon panin bawngnawi ~ | curds from the herd) (s:thawhbat) (r:23.7.22/7.5.25/5.32.14) (q:draft)
thaunate = (t:n) (w:oil/fatness/richness) (d:thau, fat, with the noun suffix na and the plural te: fatness, richness; said by the olive tree of its oil) (e:ka ~ nusia-in singkungte a uk dingin/pasiante leh mite a kipahtawina ahi ka ~ | my oil, by which gods and men are honored) (b:thau) (r:7.9.9) (q:draft)
thaute = (t:adj) (w:fat/fattened) (d:thau, fat, with the plural te: fat or fattened, said of animals) (e:tuu ~ leh tuu gawngte/bawngtalte, leh ganno ~ biakna-in pia-in | sacrificing cattle and fattened calves/Ganhing ~ tawh meihal biaknate | burnt offerings of fat animals) (a:gawngte) (b:thau) (r:26.34.20/26.39.18/11.1.9/19.66.15) (q:draft)
thaute = (t:n) (w:fat/fat portions) (d:thau, fat, with the plural te: the fat parts of a sacrificed animal) (e:a lutang leh a ~/a gilpi tuam a ~ | the fat that covers the internal organs/tuutal ~ sangin thungaih ding hoihzaw hi | to heed is better than the fat of rams/thunuam-a biakna ~ pia hi | he offered the fat of the fellowship offerings) (b:thau) (r:3.1.8/11.8.64/3.3.3/9.15.22/14.7.7) (q:draft)
thaute = (t:n) (w:oil/olive oil) (d:thau, fat, with the plural te, in oliv thaute, olive oil) (e:paknamtui leh oliv ~ koih uh hi/nek ding khuaizu leh oliv ~ | honey and olive oil for food/oliv ~ leh leenggahzute | olive oil and wine) (s:sathaute) (b:thau) (r:26.23.41/28.9.2/26.16.13) (q:draft)
thawh = (t:v) (w:rise/get up/arise) (d:form of tho, rise or get up, used before words such as ciangin, ma-in and sak; often paired with lup, lie down) (e:Saul lei pan a ~ ciangin/Zingsangin David a ~ ma-in | before David got up in the morning/na lup ciang leh na ~ ciangun | when you lie down and when you get up/Leitung liingsak gawp dingin Topa a ~ ciangin | when the Lord rises to shake the earth) (a:lup) (r:44.9.8/10.24.11/5.6.7/23.2.19) (q:draft)
thawhbat = (t:n) (w:butter) (d:butter, the fat that comes when milk is churned) (e:Ama kampau in ~ sangin nelzaw a/Bawngnawi, meekmeek lehang ~ hong suak a | when milk is churned it becomes butter) (s:thaukhal) (r:19.55.21/20.30.33) (q:draft)
thawhin = (t:v) (w:rising up) (d:thawh rise, rise against, with the connective in; said of an enemy that gains the upper hand and comes out) (e:kote hong zo ~ gam lakah) (b:thawh) (r:10.11.23) (q:draft, low confidence)
thawhkhiat = (t:v) (w:come up out/rise out) (d:thawh, rise, with khiat, out: come up out of something, as out of the water; the form used before khit and ciangin) (e:Jesuh a ~ khit phetin/Tui sung panin Jesuh a ~ khit phetin | just as Jesus came up out of the water) (b:thawh) (r:41.1.10) (q:draft)
thawhkik = (t:v) (w:rise again/rise from the dead/be raised) (d:thawh, rise, with kik, again: rise again, especially from death; the form used before khit, ciangin and nading) (e:Zeisu sihna pan a ~ khit ciangin/Amaute a ~ zawh loh nadingun ka sunlet a | I crushed them so that they could not rise again/sihna pan a ~ nading thu om a | he had to rise from the dead/ka ~ khit ciangin | after I have risen) (s:hingkik) (b:thawh) (r:43.21.14/40.22.30/19.18.38/44.17.3/41.14.28) (q:draft)
thawhkikna = (t:n) (w:resurrection) (d:thawhkik, rise again, with the noun suffix na: rising again from death, resurrection) (e:~ om lo hi leh/Misite’ ~ om lo hi | there is no resurrection of the dead/Ni tawp Ni-a ~-ah a thokik ding | he will rise again in the resurrection at the last day/sihna pan ~ thu a hilh | they taught the resurrection from the dead) (s:hinkikna) (a:sihna) (b:thawhkik) (r:46.15.13/43.11.24/40.22.23/44.4.2) (q:draft)
thawhkiksak = (t:v) (w:raise from the dead/raise again) (d:thawhkik, rise again, with the causative sak: make someone rise again from death) (e:Pasian in amah a ~ thu/sihna pan a ~ lai takin | when he raised him from the dead/a sisa a ~ Lazaras zong en dingin | to see Lazarus too, whom he had raised from the dead/Pasian in sihna panin a ~ Nazareth khuami Jesuh | Jesus of Nazareth, whom God raised from the dead) (s:thawhsakkik/hingsakkik/thosakkik) (b:thawhkik) (r:44.3.15/43.12.17/43.12.9/44.4.10) (q:draft)
thawhkiksakna = (t:n) (w:raising to life/resurrection) (d:thawhkiksak, raise again, with the noun suffix na: the fact of having raised someone from death) (e:Pasian in a ~ thu/Tua Zeisu Pasian in a ~ thu | that God raised this Jesus to life) (s:thawhsakkikna/hinkiksakna) (b:thawhkiksak) (r:44.2.32) (q:draft)
thawhkiksakpa = (t:n) (w:one raised to life) (d:thawhkiksak, raise again, with pa marking a man: in the verse, the man whom Jesus raised from the dead) (e:a sisa a ~ Lazaras omna) (b:thawhkiksak) (r:43.12.1) (q:draft)
thawhlam = (t:n) (w:rising/getting up) (d:thawh, rise, with lam: the fact or moment of getting up, paired with luplam, lying down) (e:a ~ hitaleh amah in phawk lo hi/A tanu a luplam hitaleh a ~ hitaleh | whether his daughter lay down or got up) (a:luplam) (r:1.19.33/1.19.35) (q:draft)
thawhsak = (t:v) (w:raise/raise up) (d:thawh, rise, with the causative sak: make someone rise, especially from death) (e:sihna panin a ~ Lazaras/Pasian in a Silapa hong ~ khit ciangin | when God had raised up his servant) (s:thosak/hingkiksak) (b:thawh) (r:43.12.1/44.3.26) (q:draft)
thawhsakkik = (t:v) (w:raise again/raise up/bring back to life) (d:thawhsak, make rise, with kik, again: raise someone from death) (e:sihna panin a ~ Lazaras zong/sihna panin Pasian in a ~ a Tapa Jesuh | his Son Jesus, whom God raised from the dead/sihna panin a ~ a mu mihonte | the crowd that saw him raise him from the dead) (s:thawhkiksak/thokiksak/hingkiksak) (b:thawhsak) (r:43.12.9/52.1.10/43.12.17) (q:draft)
thawhsakkikna = (t:n) (w:resurrection/raising again) (d:thawhsakkik, raise again, with the noun suffix na: the raising of someone from death) (e:vangliatna tawh a ~ hangin/misite lak panin vangliatna tawh a ~ hangin | by his being raised with power from among the dead) (s:thawhkiksakna/hinkiksakna) (b:thawhsakkik) (r:45.1.4) (q:draft)
thawhtoh = (t:v) (w:come up/rise up/go up) (d:thawh, rise, with toh, upward: come up, as out of the water; the form used before lai takin) (e:tui sung pan a ~ lai takin) (a:kumsuk) (b:thawh) (r:41.1.10/40.3.16) (q:draft)
thawhtohna = (t:n) (w:rising up/arising) (d:thawhtoh, rise up, with the noun suffix na: the act of rising up) (e:nangma ~ hangin minamte kithehthang hi) (b:thawhtoh) (r:23.33.3) (q:draft)
thawhzawh = (t:v) (w:be able to get up/recover) (d:thawh, rise, with zawh, a form of zo, be able: be able to get up again after an injury) (e:sila hong ~ leh/ni nih khit ciang ahi zongin sila hong ~ | if the slave gets up again after two days) (s:thozo/damkik) (r:2.21.21) (q:draft)
thawi = (t:v) (w:search/rummage through/ransack) (d:go through a house or belongings looking for something) (e:Ka van khempeuh na ~ khit hangin/nangma inn leh na nasemte’ inn sung ~-in | searching your house and the houses of your officials) (r:1.31.37/11.20.6) (q:draft)
thawl = (t:n) (w:bottle/jar/flask/skin) (d:container for liquids such as water, oil or wine; savun thawl is a wineskin, and thawl khat also renders the liquid measure hin) (e:~ sunga tui a bei ciangin/meivak leh ~ sungah namgimtui a tawikhawm uh hi | they took oil in jars along with their lamps/Samuel in sathau ~ khat la-in | Samuel took a flask of oil/leenggahzu savun ~ khat | a skin of wine) (r:1.21.15/40.25.4/9.10.1/9.16.20) (q:draft)
thawlkhat = (t:n) (w:one jar/a bottle) (d:thawl, bottle or jar, with khat, one, written as one word) (e:tuipi tuite ~ sunga thun bangin) (r:19.33.7) (q:draft)
thawlpi = (t:n) (w:large jar/measure) (d:thawl, jar, with pi, big: a large jar; in Haggai a measure of wine) (e:~ sawmnih dim bek a na pha hi/leenggahzu ~ sawmnga pha ding ci-in | expecting fifty measures of wine) (b:thawl) (r:37.2.16) (q:draft)
thawlsan = (t:n) (w:flask/jar) (d:a container of the thawl kind, here one filled with perfume; the part san is not explained by the verse) (e:~ kiuhkeuh tawh kibang hi) (b:thawl) (r:22.5.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
thawn = (t:v) (w:shake/quake/resound) (d:shake or ring with a loud noise, said of the ground or the shore) (e:awng uh a, lei ~ hi/kikona in tuipi gei teng ~ hi | the shore quakes at the cry/amau’ gamlumna in lei ~ kham hi | the ground shook with their noise) (s:liing) (r:9.4.5/26.27.28/11.1.40) (q:draft)
thawn = (t:v) (w:thunder against/startle) (d:strike with a loud noise so as to throw into panic) (e:tua ni-in Filistiate ~ gawpin/aw lianpi tawh tua ni-in Filistiate ~ gawpin | with a mighty voice he thundered against the Philistines that day) (r:9.7.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
thawnkham = (t:v) (w:shake/resound) (d:thawn, shake, written as one word with kham: of the ground, shake and ring with the noise of a crowd) (e:gamlumna in lei a ~ hi) (s:thawn/liing) (r:11.1.40) (q:draft)
thazaw = (t:v) (w:be weak/grow weak/fail/lose heart) (d:tha, strength, with zaw, weak: have no strength left, said of eyes, hands and courage; thazaw sak is weaken or discourage) (e:Na khut ~ sak kei in/ka mitte ~ ta hi | my eyes have grown weak/Damaska khua mite ~ uh a | the people of Damascus have become feeble/~ gawpin ka ci a na hi | I was worn out and ill) (b:tha) (r:36.3.16/19.119.82/24.49.24/27.8.27) (q:draft)
thazawm = (t:adj) (w:faint/weak) (d:tha, strength, with zawm, weak: faint and worn out, as with hunger) (e:gilkialin a ~ mite khempeuh) (s:thazawng/thanem/zawngkhal) (a:thahat/hat) (r:24.31.25) (q:draft)
thazawng = (t:adj) (w:weak/debilitated/feeble) (d:having little strength, weak; said of the body and of people) (e:pumpi a ~ hi/Lungsim a ut hangin pumpi a ~ hi | the spirit is willing but the body is weak/thazawngte ading ~ bang ka hi hi | to the weak I became as weak) (s:thanem/thaneem/zawngkhal) (a:thahat/hat) (r:41.14.38/40.26.41/46.9.22)
thazawngkhal = (t:adj) (w:powerless/feeble/weak) (d:tha, strength, with zawngkhal, weak, written as one word: without strength, powerless) (e:a ~ kei nong hotna) (s:thazawng/zawngkhal/thanem) (a:thahat) (r:18.26.2) (q:draft)
thazawngte = (t:adj) (w:weak/debilitated) (d:thazawng, weak, with the plural te: the weak, people who are weak) (e:~ ading thazawng bang ka hi/~ ka ngah nadingin | so that I might win the weak) (b:thazawng) (r:46.9.22)
thazawsak = (t:v) (w:weaken/discourage/let hang limp) (d:thazaw, be weak, with the causative sak: take away strength or courage; of hands, let them hang limp) (e:Na khut ~ kei in/mi khempeuhte lungkia sakin ~ hi | he discourages and weakens all the people) (s:thanemsak/thakiamsak/lungkiasak) (a:thahatsak/thakhauhsak) (b:thazaw) (r:36.3.16/24.38.4) (q:draft)
thazung = (t:n) (w:root) (d:said of the root of the olive tree whose sap feeds the branches; thazung tui is its sap) (e:oliv sing ~ tui zomin na neek leh) (s:zung) (r:45.11.17) (q:draft, low confidence)
Thebes = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Thebes) (d:chief city of Upper Egypt on the Nile, against which the prophets announced judgment) (r:26.30.14/26.30.15/34.3.8)
Thebez = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Thebez) (d:town near Shechem where Abimelek son of Gideon was killed by a millstone a woman dropped on him) (r:7.9.50/10.11.21)
theem = (t:adj) (w:thin/shrivelled/withered) (d:said of heads of grain that are poor and empty; which of the three English words it answers to is not certain) (e:a hawm, a ~ vui sagihte hong po a/a keusak, a hawm, a ~ vui | withered, empty and thin ears) (r:1.41.23) (q:draft, low confidence)
theemsak = (t:v) (w:scorch/blast/wither) (d:theem, thin, with the causative sak: of the east wind, make ears of grain thin and dried up) (e:nisuahna huih in a ~ a hawm vui/nisuahna huihpi in a ~ buhvui hawm sagihte | the seven empty ears scorched by the east wind) (s:keusak) (b:theem) (r:1.41.6/1.41.27) (q:draft)
theemsakin = (t:v) (w:scorching/withering) (d:theemsak cause to shrivel with the connective in; said of the east wind blasting ears of grain) (e:nisuahna huih in ~ a hawm vui sagih) (s:keusakin) (b:theemsak) (r:1.41.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
theh = (t:v) (w:sprinkle/splash) (d:throw a liquid in drops over something, as blood on the altar or oil before the Lord) (e:biakna tau tungah ~ hi/biakna tau tung kimkotah a si ~ hi | he splashed the blood against the sides of the altar/Topa mai-ah sagih vei ~ ding hi | he shall sprinkle it seven times before the Lord/tua mah bangin si tawh a ~ hi | in the same way he sprinkled them with blood) (r:2.24.6/3.8.19/3.14.27/58.9.21) (q:draft)
thehin = (t:v) (w:sprinkling/splashing/scattering) (d:theh, sprinkle, with the linking ending in: sprinkling, before the next action in the sentence) (e:tua ganhingte tungah ci ~/a lu uh leivui ~ | sprinkling dust on their heads/biakna tau tungah sagih vei ~ | sprinkling it on the altar seven times/biakna tau tungah a si ~ | splashing the blood on the altar) (b:theh) (r:26.43.24/3.16.19/26.27.30/3.17.6) (q:draft)
thehna = (t:n) (w:sprinkling/splashing) (d:theh sprinkle with the noun suffix na: the act of sprinkling blood) (e:sisan tawh ~ a ngah nading/biakna piakna ganhing site ~ tawh | with the sprinkling of the blood of the sacrificed animals) (b:theh) (r:60.1.1/26.43.18) (q:draft)
thehthang = (t:v) (w:scatter/disperse) (d:throw or drive apart in all directions: scatter a people among the nations, or scatter things such as frost and arrows) (e:minamdangte lakah nong ~ khin hi/minam khempeuhte lakah ka ~ ding hi | I will scatter them among all the nations/vut bangin vuukpaak hong ~ hi | he scatters the frost like ashes/Amah in thaltangte lawn khia-in ~ hi | he shot his arrows and scattered them) (s:khenthang) (a:kaikhawm) (r:19.44.11/26.30.23/19.147.16/10.22.15) (q:draft)
thehthangin = (t:v) (w:scattering/dispersing) (d:thehthang, scatter, with the linking ending in: scattering, before the next action in the sentence) (e:minam dangte lakah ~/hong ~ namsau tawh kong delh ding hi | I will scatter you and pursue you with the sword) (a:khawmin) (b:thehthang) (r:26.6.8/26.5.12) (q:draft)
thehthangna = (t:n) (w:scattering/dispersion) (d:noun of thehthang, scatter; before gam or with panin it names the place to which people were scattered, as note kong thehthangna gamte, the lands where I scattered you) (e:Amaute ka ~ gam panin khawm kikin/Note kong ~ gamte khempeuh ka susia khin ding | I will completely destroy all the nations where I scattered you/Gam khempeuh-a note kong ~ panin | from all the lands where I scattered you) (b:thehthang) (r:26.11.17/24.46.28/26.20.34) (q:draft)
thehthangpa = (t:n) (w:one who scattered) (d:thehthang scatter with pa marking a male person: he who scattered them) (e:gam dangah a ~ in keimah ka hi hi) (b:thehthang) (r:26.11.16) (q:draft)
thehthangzo = (t:v) (w:have scattered) (d:thehthang scatter with zo marking that the act is completed) (e:gam tuamtuamah na ~ hi/a nai a gamla gam tuamtuamah na ~ hi | you have scattered them to lands near and far) (b:thehthang) (r:27.9.7) (q:draft)
thei = (t:v) (w:know) (d:know a person, a fact or a way; thei kei is not know) (e:Nopna lampi amau in a ~ kei/Mi khempeuh’ lungsim a ~ Topa aw | Lord, you who know everyone’s heart/ka mawhsakna thu uh na ~ ding hi | you will know the charges we bring/Sia aw, ~ kei ing | sir, I do not know) (a:theilo) (r:45.3.17/44.1.24/44.24.8/38.4.13)
thei = (t:adj) (w:able/capable of/qualified to) (d:placed after a verb: able to do it, can; thei lo is unable) (e:oliv gah a gah ~ hiam/midangte a hilhsawn ~ ding mite | people who will be able to teach others/a gen ~ kuamah a om kei uh hi | there was no one who could tell it/Huan sung singgahte ka ne ~ ding uh hi | we may eat the fruit of the trees in the garden) (a:theilo) (r:59.3.12/55.2.2/27.5.8/1.3.2)
thei = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:fig) (d:the fig; thei gah is the fruit, thei kung the tree and thei moh a cake of pressed figs) (e:lingkungah mite in ~ gah a lo ngei/leenggui leh ~ kung leh mang kawlsing | vines, fig trees and pomegranates/~ zong tawm khat pua uh hi | they also carried some figs/leh ~ moh zanih la-in | and two hundred cakes of figs) (s:theigah) (r:42.6.44/5.8.8/4.13.23/9.25.18)
Thei = (t:v) (w:know/see/look) (d:thei, know, written with a capital at the start of a sentence or of quoted speech; thei in is the command know, often translated see or look) (e:~ in, kote’ adingin hih haksatna/~ in, na khut sungah | see, into your hands/~ in, na thugente hoihin man hi | look, your claims are good and right/~ mah ung | yes, we know him/~ lo na hi hiam | do you not know) (b:thei) (r:12.4.13/6.6.2/10.15.3/1.29.5/38.4.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
theiba = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:sycamore-fig/sycamore) (d:the sycamore-fig tree, common in the foothills; said as theiba sing or theiba kung) (e:Shefelah ~ sing bangin/Oliv leh ~ kungte tungah | in charge of the olive and sycamore-fig trees/~ huan puah tawh a thuah ka hi hi | I also took care of sycamore-fig trees) (s:theithek/theitheek) (r:11.10.27/13.27.28/30.7.14) (q:draft)
theigah = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:fig) (d:the fruit of the fig tree) (e:Leengkung in ~ a gah thei hiam/Thangling kungah ~ kilo thei hiam | are figs picked from thistles/hih ~ hoihte bangin | like these good figs/ka lunggulh ~ beita hi | the figs I crave are gone) (s:thei/theipum) (r:59.3.12/24.24.5/40.7.16/33.7.1) (q:draft)
theigahte = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:figs) (d:theigah, fig, with the plural te; in a list of crops it also stands for the fig trees) (e:Bawm khat sunga ~/kine thei lo ~ bangin ka bawl ding hi | I will treat them like figs that cannot be eaten/na ~ uh hong nek mangsak ding uh hi | they will devour your fig trees) (b:theigah) (r:24.24.2/24.24.8/24.5.17) (q:draft)
theih = (t:v) (w:be know/know/be able) (d:form of thei, know or be able, used before words such as ni, ma-in, loh, ding and nading; theih nadingin is so that one may) (e:Note kong ~ ni-a kipan/kuama’ ~ ma-in | before anyone knew/Note ~ loh an nek ding ka nei hi | I have food to eat that you do not know/A mite thu a khen ~ nadingin | so that he may judge his people/na nek ~ ding uh ganhingte | the animals you may eat) (b:thei) (r:5.9.24/40.24.50/24.41.4/43.4.32/19.50.4/5.14.4)
theihhak = (t:adj) (w:hard to understand/obscure) (d:theih, know, with hak, hard: difficult to know or understand, said of a saying or riddle) (e:Paunak thu ~ khat ka ngaihsun) (s:telhak/theihtelhak) (r:19.49.4) (q:draft)
theihin = (t:prep) (w:before/in the presence of/with the knowledge of) (d:theih, know, with the ending in, placed after a possessive: with that person knowing, in the hearing or sight of; mite’ theihin is before people, openly) (e:Mi tampite’ ~ ka thuhilh/mite’ ~ a genkhia mite | those who declare it before others/kumpipa’ ~ kumpi Khang Tangthu Laibu sungah kiciamteh hi | it was recorded in the book of the annals in the presence of the king/mi’ ~ a genkhia nuam lote | those who will not declare it before others) (s:muhin) (b:theih) (r:55.2.2/40.10.32/17.2.23/42.12.9) (q:draft)
theihkhak = (t:v) (w:come to know/learn/get to know) (d:theih, know, with khak, happen to: come to know or learn something) (e:thu panin na ~ uh hi lo hi/cih a ~ loh hangin | though it never came to know) (r:49.4.20/21.6.5) (q:draft)
theihkhiat = (t:v) (w:find out/discover/fathom) (d:theih, know, with khiat, out: come to know by searching; the form used before a noun or zawh) (e:kuama ~ zawh loh na lian tampi/Keima ~ thu in | this is what I have found out) (s:phawkkhiat/kankhiat) (b:theih) (r:18.9.10/21.7.29) (q:draft)
theihkhit = (t:v) (w:have come to know/know fully/finish learning) (d:theih, know, with khit, finished: theihkhit ciangin is after one has come to know, theihkhit phetin as soon as one knows) (e:Keima pianzia ding ka ~ phetin/a sin ding khempeuh a ~ ciangin | when he has learned all there is to learn/a kicing takin ~ zawh loh ding | not able to be fully known) (s:theikhin) (r:50.2.23/42.6.40/49.3.19) (q:draft)
theihkhitna = (t:n) (w:knowing already/full knowledge) (d:theihkhit have come to know, with the noun suffix na: the fact of already knowing) (e:na khempeuh na ~ thu ka phawk) (b:theihkhit) (r:43.16.30) (q:draft)
theihkhol = (t:v) (w:foreknow/know beforehand) (d:theih, know, with khol, beforehand: know in advance) (e:nidang lai-a a ~ mite/Pasian in nidang lai-a a ~ mite | those God foreknew long ago) (r:45.8.29) (q:draft)
theihkholh = (t:v) (w:know beforehand/find out in advance/foresee) (d:theih, know, with kholh, beforehand; theihkholh lohin, without knowing beforehand, means unexpectedly, suddenly) (e:amaute in a ~ uh ciangin/~ lohin ama tungah lungkhamna tung ding a | trouble will come on him unexpectedly/gutate bangin ~ lohin hong tung ding hi | it will come unexpectedly like a thief/namsau la-in ~ lohin khuapi va sim uh a | they took their swords and attacked the city by surprise) (s:mukhol) (b:theihkhol) (r:44.14.6/20.6.15/52.5.2/1.34.25) (q:draft)
