thokang = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:gnat/mosquito) (d:a small biting insect, a gnat; in Exodus the plague of gnats that came from the dust) (e:leivui teng ~ suak hi/Izipt gamsung khempeuhah ~ a om dingin | so that there will be gnats throughout the land of Egypt/mihing' tung leh ganhing' tungah ~ hong om hi | gnats came on people and animals/~ bangin si ding uh hi | they will die like gnats) (s:thovai) (r:2.8.17/23.51.6/2.8.16) (q:draft)
thokangte = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:gnats/lice) (d:thokang, a small biting insect, with the plural te) (e:thohonpi le ~ gam sung dimin hong om hi/mihing leh ganhing' tungah ~ om hi | the gnats were on people and animals) (b:thokang) (r:19.105.31/2.8.18) (q:draft)
thokhawm = (t:v) (w:rise together/be raised with) (d:tho, rise, with khawm, together: rise from death together with someone) (e:suakin i ~ ding hi/tuiphumna panin a ~ leuleu na hi uh hi | you were also raised with him out of baptism) (b:tho) (r:45.6.5/51.2.12) (q:draft)
thokhawmsak = (t:v) (w:raise up together with) (d:thokhawm, rise together, with the causative sak: raise someone up together with another) (e:sihna panin Pasian in a hong ~ hi/hih bangin a hong ~ ahi hi | this is how he raised us up together) (b:thokhawm) (r:49.2.6/49.2.7) (q:draft)
thokhia = (t:v) (w:get up/rise up) (d:tho, rise, with khia, out: get up out of bed or out of sleep) (e:cik ciangin ~ ding na hi hiam/Kong ~ thei kei a | I cannot get up) (s:thoto) (a:lum) (b:tho) (r:20.6.9/42.11.7) (q:draft)
thokik = (t:v) (w:rise again/be raised/wake again) (d:tho, rise, with kik, again: get up again, from sleep or from death) (e:Na sanggampa a ~ ding hi/Topa ~ takpi a | the Lord has truly risen/Topa in hong kem ahih manin ka ~ hi | I wake again because the Lord sustains me/sihna pan ~ in | rise from the dead/amau’ pumpi ~ ding hi | their bodies will rise) (s:hingkik) (a:si) (b:tho) (r:43.11.23/42.24.34/19.3.5/49.5.14/23.26.19) (q:draft)
thokikin = (t:v) (w:rising again/being raised) (d:thokik rise again, with the linking ending in, rising again and then doing the next action) (e:mi sisa khat hong ~ amaute kiangah/sihna panin ~ a hong tung ding hunah | in the age to come, after rising from the dead/ama thawhkik bangin ~ | rising again as he rose) (s:hingkikin) (b:thokik) (r:42.16.30/42.20.35/50.3.10) (q:draft)
thokiksak = (t:v) (w:raise/raise up/bring back to life) (d:thokik, rise again, with the causative sak: make someone rise again from death) (e:Pasian in misite a ~ ding hi/i pu i pate’ Pasian in hong ~ zo hi | the God of our ancestors has raised him/Ni tawp ni ciangin tua mi ka ~ ding hi | I will raise that person up on the last day/Pasian in sihna panin Topa ~ hi | God raised the Lord from the dead) (s:hingkiksak/thosak/thawhkiksak) (b:thokik) (r:44.26.8/44.5.30/43.6.54/46.6.14) (q:draft)
thokikzo = (t:v) (w:be able to rise again/get up again) (d:thokik, rise again, with zo, be able; in the verses always negated: thokikzo nawn lo is never able to rise again) (e:A lupna panin ~ nawn lo ding hi/A ~ nawn lo dingin | so that they can never rise again/amah pukin ~ ngei nawn lo ding hi | it falls, never to rise again) (s:dingkikzo) (b:thokik) (r:19.41.8/23.24.20/19.140.10) (q:draft)
Thomas = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Thomas) (d:one of the twelve apostles, also called Didymus, who doubted the resurrection until he saw Jesus) (r:43.20.28/42.6.15)
thona = (t:see) <sian'thona>
thong = (t:n) (w:prison/jail) (d:a place where prisoners are kept; thong sung is the inside of the prison) (e:Amah in ~ sungah ni thum sung/~ sungah a khum uh hi | they put them in jail/~ sungah Johan’ ngawng a tan sak hi | he had John beheaded in the prison/Josef a kikhumna ~ sung | the prison where Joseph was confined/~ panin suakta-in kumpi suak thei a | he may come out of prison and become king) (s:thonginn/kikhumna) (r:1.42.17/44.5.18/40.14.10/1.40.3/21.4.14) (q:draft)
Thong = (t:n) (w:prison) (d:thong, prison, written with a capital at the start of a sentence and in the name Thong Kongpi, a gate of Jerusalem called the Gate of the Guard in the NIV) (e:tua ciangin ~ Kongpi-ah khawl uh hi/~ ukpa in meivak a nget khit ciangin | after the jailer called for lights/~ sunga kikhum mite kikhah baih ding hi | those shut up in prison will soon be set free/~ huang sungah Jeremiah a kikalhcip laitak | while Jeremiah was shut up in the prison courtyard) (b:thong) (r:16.12.39/44.16.29/23.51.14/24.33.1) (q:draft)
thonga = (t:adv) (w:in prison) (d:thong, prison, with the place suffix a: in prison; thonga kikhum mi is a person held in prison) (e:~ kikhum mi nih zong) (s:thongah) (b:thong) (r:42.23.32) (q:draft)
thongah = (t:adv) (w:in prison/to prison/into prison) (d:thong, prison, with the place marker ah: in prison or into prison) (e:~ Johan’ lutang a tansak hi/~ a kia dingin a khumsak hi | he had him thrown into prison/Peter a kimat khit ciangin ~ kikoih a | after Peter was arrested he was put in prison/~ khiat dingin hong ki-ap ding a | you will be handed over to be put in prison) (s:thonga) (b:thong) (r:40.14.10/44.12.4/40.18.30/42.21.12) (q:draft)
thongcing = (t:n) (w:jailer/prison guard) (d:thong, prison, with cing, guard: one who guards a prison; usually followed by pa, thongcing pa, the jailer) (e:~ pa in thong sung tawngnungah amaute koihin/~ pa in amaute’ liammate sawpsiangsak a | the jailer washed their wounds/~ pa kiangah thu a pia uh hi | they gave orders to the jailer) (r:44.16.24/44.16.23/44.16.33) (q:draft)
thongcingte = (t:n) (w:prison guards/guards/sentries) (d:thongcing, prison guard, with the plural te: the guards who keep watch over a prison) (e:~ in a kongah cing lai uh hi/~ lakah buaina lianpi hong om hi | there was a great commotion among the guards/~ thu kisit a | the guards were cross-examined) (b:thongcing) (r:44.12.6/44.12.19/44.12.18) (q:draft)
thonginn = (t:n) (w:prison/jail) (d:thong, prison, with inn, house: a prison building) (e:~ kongkhak a hon’ khit ciangin/~ a bulpi dongin a lokgawp hi | the prison was shaken to its foundations/~ sungah kiseel hi | they are hidden away in prisons) (s:thong/kikhumna) (r:44.5.19/23.42.22/44.16.26) (q:draft)
thongkia = (t:v) (w:be imprisoned/be in prison) (d:thong, prison, with kia, fall: be put in prison, be a prisoner; thongkia mi is a prisoner) (e:Jeremiah ~ nai lo ahih manin/Kei tawh ~ khawm | in prison together with me/sikkol kibulhin gimna thuakin ~ uh hi | bound in iron chains and suffering, they were prisoners/Khazih Zeisu hanga ~ kei, Paul | I, Paul, a prisoner for Christ Jesus) (s:kikhum) (a:suakta) (r:24.37.4/44.16.25/45.16.7/19.107.10/57.1.1) (q:draft)
thongkiapa = (t:n) (w:prisoner) (d:thongkia, be imprisoned, with pa marking a man: a man who is in prison) (e:tua Topa’ ~ ahi keimah ah/Khazih Zeisu’ ~ kei Paul in | I, Paul, the prisoner of Christ Jesus) (s:kikhumpa) (b:thongkia) (r:55.1.8/49.3.1) (q:draft)
thongkiat = (t:v) (w:be imprisoned/be in prison) (d:form of thongkia, be imprisoned, used before nading, laitak and other endings) (e:ka ~ laitakin nong hawh uh hi/~ nading ahi a, sih nading ahi zongin | whether for imprisonment or for death/cikin na ~ hong mu a | when did we see you in prison) (s:kikhum) (b:thongkia) (r:40.25.36/44.26.31/40.25.44) (q:draft)
thongkiate = (t:n) (w:prisoners) (d:thongkia, be imprisoned, with the plural te: those who are in prison) (e:Topa in ~ khahkhia hi/~ in tui peeka a taimang ding uh | that the prisoners would swim away and escape/amah in ~ nopsakna munah tun hi | he leads the prisoners into well-being/~ khempeuh suakta khin hi ci-in | thinking that all the prisoners had escaped) (s:kikhumte) (b:thongkia) (r:19.146.7/1.39.20/44.27.42/19.68.6/44.16.27) (q:draft)
thongkiatna = (t:n) (w:imprisonment/chains/bonds) (d:thongkiat, be imprisoned, with the noun suffix na: being in prison; thongkiatna thuak is to suffer imprisonment) (e:Khazih’ thu thuk hangin ~ ka thuak a/sikkol bulhna le ~ zong a thuak uh hi | they also suffered chains and imprisonment/ka ~ in Khazih hang ahi hi | my imprisonment is for Christ) (s:khumna) (a:suahtakna) (b:thongkiat) (r:51.4.3/15.7.26/58.11.36/50.1.13) (q:draft)
thongkiatnate = (t:n) (w:imprisonments/imprisonment) (d:thongkiatna, imprisonment, with the plural te) (e:~ tawh ze-etna a thuak uh) (b:thongkiatna) (r:58.11.36) (q:draft)
thongkiatpih = (t:n) (w:fellow prisoner) (d:thongkiat be imprisoned with pih together with: one who was in prison with someone) (e:ka ~ ahi Andronikas le Junias) (b:thongkiat) (r:45.16.7) (q:draft)
thongmial = (t:n) (w:dungeon) (d:thong, prison, with mial, dark: a dark prison cell, a dungeon) (e:~ sunga a om a kiman mite’ tacil/manlang takin ~ sung panin amah paikhiatpih uh hi | they quickly brought him out of the dungeon) (r:2.12.29/1.41.14) (q:draft)
