thuahpah = (t:v) (w:follow at once with/add straight after) (d:thuah add on with pah at once: do a second thing right after the first) (e:keimah gensiat tawh ~ cih om) (r:41.9.39) (q:draft, low confidence)
thuahte = (t:n) (w:additional gifts/special gifts) (d:thuah in addition with the plural te, in piak thuahte: the things given on top of the tithe) (e:sawm-ah-khat le na piak ~ uh/nomau’ piak ~ ahi zongin | or your own special gifts) (b:thuah) (r:5.12.6/5.12.17) (q:draft)
thuahthuah = (t:adv) (w:one after another/again and again/more and more) (d:thuah said twice: one thing added on another, repeatedly) (e:Amah in kei hong liamsak ~ a/Mihaute in lawm mu ~ a | the rich find more and more friends/khialhna a bawl ~ | heaping sin upon sin/dan thuaksak ~ in la | add punishment upon punishment/suang a khiat ~ laitakun | while they kept on stoning him) (s:kikkik/zelzel) (r:18.16.14/20.19.4/23.30.1/19.69.27/44.7.59) (q:draft)
thuak = (t:v) (w:bear/suffer/undergo) (e:ka ~ zawh ding hi lo hi/ama mawhna ~ ding hi | she shall bear her sin/sihna daan a ~ ding hi | he must bear the penalty of death/baptaizna khat ~ ding ka nei hi | I have a baptism to undergo/thukhenna ~ dingin na mai-ah hong sam | you summon me before you to face judgment) (r:1.4.13/42.12.50/4.5.31/18.31.28/18.14.3) of punishment, suffering
thuak = (t:v) (w:endure) (d:hold out under something hard without giving way; thuak zo and thuak thei are be able to endure) (e:khempeuh in a ~ zawh loh thu thum/nangma hangin kona ka ~ a | for your sake I endure scorn/tua a votna kua in ~ zo ding ahi hiam | who can withstand his cold/na khempeuh a ~ thei hi | it bears all things) (r:20.30.21/19.69.7/19.147.17/46.13.7)
thuakhak = (t:adj) (w:cruel/harsh/hard to bear) (d:thuak, bear, with hak, hard: hard to endure, said of a harsh master) (e:A ~ topa’ khut sungah) (r:23.19.4) (q:draft)
thuakin = (t:v) (w:suffering/enduring/bearing) (d:thuak, suffer or bear, with the linking suffix in, used when another action follows; lungduai takin thuakin is enduring patiently) (e:amah in gimna tampi ~/hih bang teng ~ minthan’na a ngah nading | to suffer all this and so enter glory/Topa tawh kosiatna ~ | bearing disgrace with the Lord/Amaute in khialhna ~ si kha ding uh | they would bear their sin and die) (b:thuak) (r:42.17.25/58.6.15/42.24.26/58.13.13/4.18.22) (q:draft)
thuakkha = (t:v) (w:suffer/undergo/incur) (d:thuak, suffer, with kha, happen to: come to experience something bad) (e:gilkial na ~ nawn kei ding uh hi/amaute in lauhuaina ~ ngei lo uh hi | they never suffer terror/gimna na ~ ding hi | you will suffer for it/thukhenna ~ thei ding hi | will be liable to judgment) (s:thuaklawh) (r:26.36.29/20.30.10/18.21.9/40.5.22) (q:draft)
thuakkhak = (t:v) (w:suffer/undergo/incur) (d:form of thuakkha used before ding and loh nading: come to suffer something bad) (e:Pasian’ thukhenna na ~ loh nadingun/siatna na ~ ding uh deih loin | not wanting you to suffer destruction) (s:thuaklawh) (b:thuakkha) (r:59.5.12/61.3.9) (q:draft)
thuakkhawm = (t:v) (w:suffer together/suffer with/share in) (d:thuak, bear or suffer, with khawm, together: undergo something along with another) (e:natna ngah leh a vekpi-un ~ uh a/Amah tawh sihna i ~ zawh leh | if we have died with him/nang tawh ka ~ ngam ding hi | I am ready to suffer it with you/Topa tawh sihna ~ dingin pai ni | let us go to die with the Lord) (s:thuakpih) (b:thuak) (r:46.12.26/55.2.11/42.22.33/43.11.16) (q:draft)
thuakkhin = (t:v) (w:have suffered/have undergone) (d:thuak, suffer or bear, with khin marking a completed action: have already undergone) (e:thukhenna a ~ ahihna thu/a ~ pa kei ka hi hi | I am the man who has suffered it) (b:thuak) (r:43.16.11/25.3.1) (q:draft)
thuakkik = (t:v) (w:suffer in return/bear in turn/undergo again) (d:thuak, bear or undergo, with kik, back or again: have something come back on oneself, or undergo it again) (e:amah in a ~ ding hi/tu-in ~ ding uh hi | now they will suffer in return/Muatna a ~ ngei nawn lo dingin | never to undergo decay again) (b:thuak) (r:27.11.18/33.1.7/44.13.34) (q:draft)
thuaklahin = (t:v) (w:being unable to resist/being enslaved by) (d:thuak bear with lah and the linking suffix in; in the verse, being overcome by desires) (e:duhna deihna a tuamtuamte ~) (r:56.3.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
thuaklawh = (t:v) (w:suffer/incur/bring upon oneself) (d:have to bear something, such as harm or suffering, as the result of what one does) (e:ahih manin siatna ~ uh hi/thakhat thu-in siatna ~ ding uh hi | they will swiftly bring destruction on themselves/gimna lungkhamna tampi a ~ uh hi | they have brought many griefs on themselves/simmawhna le zahpihna ka ~ hi | I incur insult and mockery) (s:thuakkha) (r:65.1.10/52.1.6/61.2.1/54.6.10/24.20.8) (q:draft)
thuakma = (t:see) <thuakma-in>
thuakma-in = (t:adv) (w:before suffering) (d:thuak, suffer, with ma, before, and the suffix in: before suffering something) (e:Sihna ka ~ note tawh hih) (r:42.22.15) (q:draft)
thuakna = (t:n) (w:suffering/affliction/endurance) (d:thuak, suffer or bear, with the noun suffix na: what a person suffers, and also the patient bearing of it) (e:Hih in ka ~-ah keima kihehnepna hi a/Ka ~ hong en in la | look on my suffering/~ sung panin a cimawhte laamto a | he lifted the needy out of affliction/Zeisu upna a zui misiangthote ~ | the endurance of the saints who keep faith in Jesus) (s:gimna/gimthuakna/gentheihna) (a:nopna) (b:thuak) (r:19.119.50/47.6.4/19.119.153/19.107.41/66.14.12) (q:draft)
thuaknasa = (t:n) (w:past suffering) (d:thuakna suffering with sa already: what someone has already suffered) (e:Note’ ~ a zah nihin) (b:thuakna) (r:38.9.12) (q:draft)
thuaknate = (t:n) (w:sufferings/afflictions) (d:thuakna, suffering, with the plural te) (e:amau’ ~ ka lunghimawh a/Ka gimna leh ka ~ ngaihsun in la | consider my affliction and my sufferings/Tuhuna i ~ pen | our present sufferings/amau’ ~ amah in a muh khitna thu | that he had seen their sufferings) (s:gimnate) (b:thuakna) (r:2.3.7/19.25.18/45.8.18/2.4.31) (q:draft)
thuakngap = (t:v) (w:bear/dare to endure) (d:thuak, bear, with ngap, dare; with lo it is could not bear) (e:ahih manin ~ lo uh hi) (r:58.12.20) (q:draft)
thuaknuam = (t:adj) (w:willing to suffer) (d:thuak suffer with nuam willing, wanting) (e:thuakna-ah zong a ~ hizaw in) (r:55.1.8) (q:draft)
thuakpa = (t:n) (w:one who bears/sufferer) (d:thuak bear, suffer with pa marking a man: the man who undergoes something) (e:a tawntung khialhna ~ ahi ding hi/gimna a ~-in i ngaihsun hi | we considered him one who suffers affliction) (b:thuak) (r:41.3.29/23.53.4) (q:draft)
thuakpah = (t:v) (w:suffer at once/undergo immediately) (d:thuak bear, undergo with pah at once) (e:pahpahin mawhsakna ~ uh a) (r:54.5.24) (q:draft)
thuakpih = (t:v) (w:bear with/put up with/suffer with) (d:thuak, bear, with pih, together with: share in another person’s trouble, or be patient with his weakness) (e:thahat lote a thanemna i ~ ding hi/ka haina mah hong ~ le-uhcin ka ut hi | I wish you would bear with my foolishness/i lungkhamna hong ~ dinga piang ahi hi | born to share our troubles/thongkia mite ~ ngamin | daring to suffer with those in prison) (s:thuakkhawm) (b:thuak) (r:45.15.1/47.11.1/58.10.34/20.17.17) (q:draft)
thuaksak = (t:v) (w:make suffer/inflict/afflict) (d:thuak, suffer, with the causative sak: make someone undergo something, bring suffering on someone) (e:launa hong ~ nawn kei in/na mite haksatna na ~ khin hi | you have made your people suffer hardship/Faro leh a innkuanpihte gimna lianpi ~ hi | he inflicted great suffering on Pharaoh and his household/Dahna gimna a hong ~ ciangin | when he brings grief and suffering on us/Bang hangin kote hong ~ a | why have you afflicted us) (s:gimsak/tuaksak) (b:thuak) (r:18.13.21/25.3.33/19.60.3/1.12.17/24.14.19) (q:draft)
thuaksakgawp = (t:v) (w:make suffer severely/pour out on) (d:thuaksak make suffer with gawp thoroughly, violently; of anger, pour it out on someone) (e:Egypt gam sungah ~ ning/gamlakah a ~ dingin ka kithawi hi | I prepared to pour it out on them in the wilderness) (b:thuaksak) (r:26.20.8/26.20.13) (q:draft)
thuaksakin = (t:v) (w:making suffer/making bear) (d:thuaksak make suffer with the linking suffix in) (e:a mawhpa mawhna ~ ama lu) (b:thuaksak) (r:11.8.32) (q:draft)
thuakta = (t:v) (w:suffer/bear/undergo) (d:thuak, bear, with ta marking that the state has now come: now suffer, come to bear) (e:ka hehna tu-in na ~ ding uh hi/na ngah dinga kilawm gimna a ~ na hi hi | you now suffer the punishment you deserve) (b:thuak) (r:26.7.3/18.36.17) (q:draft)
thuakte = (t:n) (w:those who suffer/the afflicted/the oppressed) (d:thuak, suffer or bear, with the plural te: people who undergo hardship or oppression, often in gimna thuakte, the afflicted) (e:a ~ mangngilh kei in/gimna ~ zasak un la lungdam uh hen | let the afflicted hear and rejoice/ze-etna a ~ a huh nadingin | to help those who are being tempted/Gimna ~ in kham takin ne ding | the afflicted will eat and be satisfied) (s:gentheite/kinengniamte) (b:thuak) (r:19.10.12/19.9.9/19.34.2/58.2.18/19.22.26) (q:draft)
thuakthuak = (t:v) (w:keep suffering/suffer again and again/face repeatedly) (d:thuak, bear or suffer, doubled for repeated action: suffer something again and again, as in sihna a thuakthuak, one who faces death daily) (e:sihna a ~ ka hi hi) (r:46.15.31) (q:draft)
thuakzaw = (t:v) (w:suffer more/bear more) (d:thuak, suffer, with zaw, more: suffer more than another; also rather suffer, as in thuakzaw mai lo, why not rather be wronged) (e:Sodom khuapi sangin na ~ ding hi/Sodom leh Gomorrah khuate sangin a ~ ding hi | it will suffer more than the towns of Sodom and Gomorrah/thong sungah khiatna a ~ mi | one who has suffered imprisonment more/Bang hangin ~ mai lo a | why not rather suffer wrong) (b:thuak) (r:40.11.24/46.6.7/40.10.15/47.11.23) (q:draft)
thuakzawh = (t:v) (w:endure/bear/persevere) (d:be able to bear, endure; the form of thuakzo used before nading and in noun phrases, where English often has endurance or perseverance) (e:eite in lametna nei-in i ~ nading/Khrih thuak bangin na ~ nadingun | so that you may endure as Christ endured/na ~ nading uh thahatna hong guan ding | he will give you strength to endure it/Leitung mi khempeuh in a ~ loh thu thum | three things that all the earth cannot bear) (s:thuakzo) (a:lungkiat) (r:45.15.4/53.3.5/46.10.13/20.30.21) (q:draft)
thuakzawhna = (t:n) (w:perseverance/endurance/patience) (d:thuakzawh, be able to bear, with the noun suffix na: the strength to endure hardship without giving up) (e:nang in ~ nei-in ka min hangin/gimna in ~ a piangsak hi | suffering produces perseverance/upna uh hong ze-etnate in ~ hong khangsak hi | the testing of your faith makes perseverance grow/Lai Siangtho pan i ngah ~ leh hehnepna | the endurance and encouragement we get from the Scriptures) (s:lungduaina/kithuakzawhna) (a:lungtomna) (b:thuakzawh) (r:66.2.3/45.5.4/45.5.3/59.1.3/45.15.4) (q:draft)
thuakzawhnate = (t:n) (w:endurance/perseverance) (d:plural of thuakzawhna) (e:na nasepnate, na ~ ahi zongin) (b:thuakzawhna) (r:66.2.19) (q:draft)
thuakzo = (t:v) (w:endure/withstand/be able to bear) (d:thuak, bear, with zo, be able: be able to bear something, hold out to the end) (e:kua in ~ ding ahi hiam/keima min hangin ~-in, lungkia hetloin | enduring for my name without losing heart/a tawp dongin a ~ mite | those who endure to the end/Mihingte’ lungsim in cinatna ~ sak a | a person’s spirit lets him endure sickness) (s:thuakzawh/nangzo) (a:lungkia) (b:thuak) (r:19.147.17/40.20.22/66.2.3/40.10.22/20.18.14) (q:draft)
thuakzote = (t:n) (w:those who endure/those who stand firm) (d:thuakzo, endure, with the plural te: the people who hold out) (e:a bei dongin a ~ in hotkhiatna/a sih dongun a ~ in | those who stand firm until they die) (s:kipte) (b:thuakzo) (r:40.24.13/41.13.13) (q:draft)
thuambuak = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:rue) (d:rue, a strong-smelling garden herb; named after lengmasel, mint, in the list of herbs on which the Pharisees paid a tenth) (e:lengmasel, ~ a kipan anteh theipuam dongin | from mint and rue to every garden herb) (r:42.11.42) (q:draft, low confidence)
thuap = (t:v) (w:patch/add on top/overlay/layer) (d:put one thing on or over another as a further layer: patch cloth, panel a wall with boards; koih thuap is add one thing on top of another) (e:puanthak tawh a ~ kei uh hi/Tua banga a ~ leh | if he patches it like that/puan lui a ~ ngei kei uh hi | no one ever patches an old garment with it/Taamtaak singpek tawh ~ sawm a | he plans to panel it with cedar boards/ki-itna hahkat mahmahin na koih ~ un | add love on top with all diligence) (s:phop) (r:41.2.21/61.1.7/42.5.36/24.22.14) (q:draft)
thuap = (t:n) (w:layer/fold/course/storey) (d:one thickness of something folded, laid or built one on another; thuap nih is two layers or folded double, suang thuap thum three courses of stone, inn thuap thum the third storey of a house) (e:A ning kikim-in ~ nih hi ding a/sing ~ khat tawh a kibawl | built with one course of timber/inn ~ thum tung pan kiasuk a | he fell down from the third storey/~ nih-in awmdal kibawl a | the breastpiece was made folded double) (r:2.28.16/15.6.4/44.20.9/2.39.9) (q:draft)
thuapna = (t:n) (w:patch/patching) (d:thuap put on as a further layer, with the noun suffix na: the piece put on, or the act of patching; thuapna puan is the patch) (e:a ~ puanthak in puanlui keeksakin/a ~ puan in a luisa kai keek semsemin | the patch pulls at the old cloth and tears it more/puan lui ~-in nei lo hi | does not use it as a patch for an old garment) (b:thuap) (r:41.2.21/42.5.36/40.9.16) (q:draft)
thuapthuapin = (t:adv) (w:doubly/layer upon layer) (d:thuap layer, doubled, with the suffix in; in the verse of sin heaped on sin) (e:a ~ a mawhna hangun) (r:28.10.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
thubul = (t:n) (w:theme) (d:the main subject of a speech, song or piece of writing) (e:~ hoih khat tawh ka lungsim) (r:19.45.1)
thubul = (t:n) (w:subject/topic)
thubul = (t:n) (w:subject matter)
Thubul = (t:n) (w:theme/subject) (d:thubul written with a capital at the start of a sentence) (e:~ hoih khat tawh) (b:thubul) (r:19.45.1) (q:draft)
thubulpi = (t:n) (w:sum/essence/main substance) (d:thubul subject with pi great: the main substance of what is said, here of the word of God) (e:Nangma ~ in thumanna hi a) (b:thubul) (r:19.119.160) (q:draft, low confidence)
thuciam = (t:n) (w:promise/vow/covenant/oath) (d:a solemn promise: a vow made to God, a promise given by God, or a covenant between two parties) (e:Nangma ~ muang ka hih manin/Topa tungah ka ciamsa ka ~ | the vow I made to the Lord/Pasian in Abraham kiangah a ~ | the promise God made to Abraham/ka ~ ahi nopsakna amah ka pia hi | I give him my covenant of peace) (s:thuciamna/kiciamna/kamciam/kamciamna) (r:19.119.74/4.25.12/10.15.7/44.7.17) (q:draft)
thuciam = (t:v) (w:promise/vow/swear) (d:make a solemn promise or vow; thuciam khin is has promised) (e:Topa in ~ khin ahih manin/Ama biakinn sungah Pasian in ~ khin hi | God has promised in his sanctuary/Vanglianpen Topa tungah thuman ding ~ ding hi | they will swear to be true to the Lord Almighty/Amah in pasal’ inn sungah ~ ahi a | if she makes a vow in her husband’s house) (s:kiciam/ciam/kamciam) (r:13.27.23/19.108.7/23.19.18/4.30.10) (q:draft)
Thuciam = (t:n) (w:covenant/testament) (d:thuciam written with a capital in titles: Thuciam Lui, the old covenant or Old Testament; Thuciam Gam, the land of the covenant, Beautiful Land in the NIV) (e:~ Lui sunga late, la thakte/Amah in ~ Gam zong sim ding a | he will also invade the Land of the Covenant/~ lui thu in hin’na a that thei hi | the word of the old covenant can kill) (s:Thuciamna) (b:thuciam) (r:51.3.16/27.11.41/47.3.6) (q:draft)
thuciamin = (t:v) (w:promising/vowing) (d:thuciam promise with the linking ending in: making a promise, having promised) (e:Topa aw, ama tungah ~/na cihtak tawntung nading uh Pasian tungah ~ | having vowed before God to stay faithful/nang tungah hong thuum ing, nangmah in ~ | I pray to you, as you have promised) (b:thuciam) (r:14.6.16/39.2.14/4.14.18) (q:draft)
thuciammna = (t:n) (w:covenant/promise) (d:the covenant terms given at the exodus; probably a misprint of thuciamna) (e:ka lakkhiat ni-a ka ~ ahi hi) (s:thuciamna) (r:24.11.4) (q:draft)
thuciamna = (t:n) (w:covenant) (d:a solemn binding agreement, above all the covenant between God and his people; thuciamna bawl is make a covenant) (e:David tawh ~ khat bawl hi/Horeb ah eite tawh ~ khat bawl hi | he made a covenant with us at Horeb/Abraham tawh a bawl ~ | the covenant he made with Abraham/i kamciamna leh i ~ don lo | despising our oath and our covenant) (s:thuciam/thukimna) (b:thuciam) (r:9.18.3/1.6.18/5.5.2/13.16.16/26.16.59)
thuciamna = (t:n) (w:deal) (d:an agreement or treaty that people make with one another) (e:thu genin ~ bawl uh hi) (s:thukimna) (b:thuciam) (r:28.10.4)
Thuciamna = (t:n) (w:covenant/promise) (d:capitalised in titles such as Thuciamna Singkuang, the ark of the covenant, Thuciamna thak, the new covenant, and Thuciamna Gam, the promised land) (e:~ Singkuang a pua Levi mite/~ singkuang la un la | take up the ark of the covenant/~ Abraham leh a suan a khakte tungah | the promises to Abraham and his descendants) (s:Thuciam) (b:thuciamna) (r:5.31.25/58.8.8/6.3.6/48.3.16) (q:draft)
thuciamnasa = (t:n) (w:vow made/promise made/covenant made) (d:thuciamna, promise or covenant, with sa, already done: the vow, promise or covenant that has been made) (e:Topa’ tungah ka ~ pen ama mite/a kiciamna leh a ~ palsatin | breaking his oath and his covenant/Paul in Pasian tungah ~ nei ahih manin | because Paul had made a vow to God/ka ~ ka pia ding hi | I will pay my vows) (s:thuciamsa) (b:thuciamna) (r:19.116.14/26.17.18/44.18.18) (q:draft)
thuciamnate = (t:n) (w:promises/vows) (d:plural of thuciamna; God's promises or the vows a person has made) (e:na ~ na tungsak ding hi/Na ~ lim takin ki-entel zo a | your promises have been thoroughly tested/a phazaw ~ tungah kip-a a kikoih | established on better promises) (s:thuciamte/kiciamnate/kamciamnate) (b:thuciamna) (r:18.22.27/19.119.140/58.8.6) (q:draft)
thuciampih = (t:n) (w:covenant partner) (d:thuciam covenant with pih together with: one who is in covenant with someone) (e:Keima ~ pa bangin kua) (s:thuciampihpa) (b:thuciam) (r:23.42.19) (q:draft)
thuciampihpa = (t:n) (w:covenant partner) (d:thuciampih with pa marking a man: the man in covenant with someone) (e:Keima ~ bangin kua a mit) (s:thuciampih) (b:thuciampih) (r:23.42.19) (q:draft)
thuciamsa = (t:n) (w:promise made/vow made/what was promised) (d:thuciam, promise, with sa marking a completed action: what has been promised or vowed) (e:Pasian in a ~ tungsakzo taktak ding hi/ka ~ ka tangtung sak ding hi | I will fulfil my vows/Isaak tunga a ~ | the promise he made to Isaac/ka pa David tawh na ~ kipsak in | keep what you promised my father David) (s:thuciamnasa) (b:thuciam) (r:45.4.21/19.116.18/19.105.8/14.6.16) (q:draft)
thuciamsate = (t:n) (w:vows/promises made) (d:thuciamsa what has been vowed, with the plural te) (e:nangma tunga ~ hong kitungsak ding) (s:thuciamnate/thuciamte) (b:thuciamsa) (r:19.65.1) (q:draft)
thuciamte = (t:n) (w:promises/covenants/vows) (d:thuciam, promise or covenant, with the plural te) (e:Ama ~ a bei paisuak ding ahi hiam/a ~ uh palsat uh hi | they break their covenants/ka kam-a ka ~ nangma tungah | to you the vows my mouth made/Pasian in i pu i pate tawh a ~ | the covenants God made with our fathers) (s:thuciamnate/kiciamnate/kamciamnate) (b:thuciam) (r:19.77.8/44.3.25/28.4.2/19.66.13) (q:draft)
thuciamteh = (t:n) (w:recorder) (d:thu, matter, with ciamteh, record; in the verses always followed by pa: thuciamteh pa, the official who keeps the king's records) (e:Asaf’ tapa ahi ~ pa Joah/Ahilud’ tapa Jehoshafat pen ~ pa ahi hi | Jehoshaphat son of Ahilud was the recorder) (s:thuciamtehpa) (r:23.36.3/13.18.15) (q:draft)
thuciamtehna = (t:n) (w:record/records) (d:the writing down of matters, thuciamteh note down a matter with the noun suffix na; thuciamtehna laibu is a book of records, an archive) (e:~ laibute a ki-et theih nadingin/~ laibute sung en lecin | if you look in the books of records) (s:ciamtehna/kiciamtehna) (b:thuciamteh) (r:15.4.14) (q:draft)
thuciamtehpa = (t:n) (w:recorder/chronicler) (d:thuciamteh with pa, the man: the court official who keeps the records) (e:Ahilud’ tapa Jehoshafat in ~ hi/leh ~ ahi, Asaf tapa Joah | and the recorder, Joah son of Asaph/Asaf tapa ahi ~ Joah hong paikhia uh hi | Joah son of Asaph the recorder came out) (s:thuciamteh) (b:thuciamteh) (r:10.8.16/23.36.3/12.18.18) (q:draft)
thudam = (t:n) (w:gentleness/peaceable manner) (d:thu, word or manner, with dam, gentle: a gentle, peaceable way; thudam tawh is gently, without force) (e:ngongbawl loin ~ tawh a paipih) (s:lungnemna/thunem/nemna) (a:ngongbawlna) (r:44.5.26) (q:draft)
thudamin = (t:adv) (w:peaceably/peacefully) (d:thudam with the adverb suffix in: without a quarrel) (e:tu-in ~ hong pia kik in) (b:thudam) (r:7.11.13) (q:draft)
thudang = (t:n) (w:another thing/another matter/anything else) (d:thu, matter, with dang, other) (e:adang khat in ~ khat gen hi/a kum kik ciangin ~ khat kigen lel hi | the next year another thing is said/kei’ deih loh ~ khat in | another thing that I do not want/na phawk ding ~ khat om hi | there is one more thing for you to note) (s:nadang) (r:11.22.20/46.2.2/24.51.46/45.7.23/21.12.12) (q:draft)
thudangte = (t:n) (w:other matters/other things) (d:thudang other matter with the plural te) (e:sungthu lobuang ~ lunghihmawh dingin) (s:nadangte) (b:thudang) (r:1.39.6) (q:draft)
Thudas = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Theudas) (d:man who claimed to be somebody and gathered about four hundred followers before he was killed, cited by Gamaliel) (r:44.5.36)
thudawnna = (t:n) (w:answer/reply) (d:thu, word, with dawnna, answering: the answer given to a question) (e:ama ~ hangin lamdangsa-in a om/ama ~ hangin lamdang a sa mahmah uh hi | they were greatly amazed at his answer/keima ~ kam ngah ding uh hi | they will get my own answer) (s:dawnkikna) (a:thudotna/dotna) (r:42.20.26/41.12.17/26.14.4) (q:draft)
thudik = (t:adj) (w:upright/just/fair/trustworthy) (d:thu, matter, with dik, right: dealing rightly and fairly with others, worthy of trust) (e:A ~ a migi na tote/~ mi ci-in Topa in hong ciamteh a | the Lord counted me a trustworthy man) (s:dik/thutang/diktat) (a:gilo/gitloh) (r:60.2.18/54.1.13) (q:draft)
