thukte = (t:n) (w:those who repay) (d:thuk, pay back, with plural te: the ones who return good or evil for what was done) (e:hoihna pen siatna tawh hong ~/Thuhoih kimlai thusia tawh a ~’ inn sungah | in the house of those who repay good with evil) (b:thuk) (r:19.38.20/20.17.13) (q:draft)
thuktheih = (t:v) (w:be able to take revenge/can avenge) (d:thuk, take revenge, with theih, be able; used before nadingin) (e:Filistia mite ka ~ nadingin hong thahatsak in) (b:thuk) (r:7.16.28) (q:draft)
thuktum = (t:adj) (w:deep/deep-seated/deep-rooted) (d:going deep in, as a sore deeper than the skin or a word taking root in a person) (e:amaute sungah ~ lo ahih manin/ama vun sangin a natna ~ zaw-in a kimuh leh | if the sore appears deeper than the skin/a thaltang a ~ theithei dingin a hong kap hi | he shot his arrows to sink in as deep as they could/amaute sungah ~ zo lo ahih manin | since it cannot take root in them) (r:41.4.17/3.13.3/25.3.13/40.13.21) (q:draft)
thukuppihte = (t:n) (w:advisers/counsellors) (d:thukup take counsel with pih together with and plural te: those with whom the king takes counsel) (e:a om kumpipa’ ~ mi nga la hi) (s:thulamlakte/thudotte/lamlakte) (r:12.25.19) (q:draft)
