thumin = (t:adv) (w:in three/into three) (d:thum, three, with the marker in; pawl thumin khen, divide into three groups; a thumin, all three) (e:mihing zathumte pawl ~ khenin/galsimte pawl ~ hong kuankhia uh hi | the raiders came out in three groups/leitang seh ~ khenin | dividing the land into three parts/Saul in mite pawl ~ koih hi | Saul put the men in three groups/kum ~ khat vei hong pai-in | coming once every three years) (b:thum) (r:7.7.16/5.19.3/9.13.17/9.11.11/11.10.22) (q:draft)
thumin = (t:v) (w:groan/moan/wail) (d:thum, groan or plead, with the linking suffix in: groaning; thumin kap is wail and thumin tau is groan) (e:~ kap un/~ na tau ding uh a | you will groan/ka lungsim gimna hangin ~ ka tautau hi | I groan because of the anguish of my heart/a nasemte ~ kap uh a | her servants moan and weep/mi cimawhte ~ tau uh ahih ciangin | because the needy groan) (s:thuumin) (b:thum) (r:23.23.14/2.2.23/20.5.11/19.38.8/34.2.7/19.12.5) (q:draft)
thumletau = (t:n) (w:moaning and groaning/woe) (d:apparently thum moan and tau groan joined by le, and; thumletau thute are words of woe) (e:dahlekah thu le ~ thute vive) (r:26.2.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
Thummim = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Thummim) (d:one of the two sacred lots, the Urim and Thummim, kept in the breastpiece of the high priest and used to seek a decision from God) (r:3.8.8)
Thummin = (t:name) (w:Thummim) (d:spelling of Thummim in Ezra 2:63: the sacred lot used with the Urim by a priest to seek a decision from God) (e:Urim leh ~ aisanna tawh ai) (r:15.2.63) (q:draft)
thumna = (t:num) (w:third) (d:thum, three, with the ordinal suffix na: the third in a series) (e:ni ~ ahi hi/a nihna Obadiah, a ~ Eliab | the second Obadiah, the third Eliab/a ~ Harim tung, a lina Seorim tung | the third to Harim, the fourth to Seorim/Ni tampi khit a kum ~ kumin | after many days, in the third year) (b:thum) (r:1.1.13/13.12.9/13.24.8/11.18.1)
Thumna = (t:num) (w:third) (d:thumna, third, written with a capital at the start of a sentence and in the place name Ansai Thumna, given in the NIV as Three Taverns) (e:pawlkhat in “Ansai ~,” ciang hong ban uh hi/~ vantungmi in peengkul a tum ciangin | when the third angel sounded his trumpet) (b:thumna) (r:44.28.15/66.8.10) (q:draft)
thumnate = (t:num) (w:third) (e:leh a dawl ~ bawl in) (b:thumna) (r:1.6.16) plural form of <thumna>
thumnop = (t:v) (w:want to plead/wish to beg) (d:thum, beg, with nop, want; kong thumnop thu is the thing I wish to plead for, my petition) (e:kong ngetnop kong ~ thu in/kong nget kong ~ thu pen | what I ask and plead for) (r:17.5.7/17.7.3) (q:draft)
thumong = (t:n) (w:fate/destiny/lot/end) (d:thu, matter, with mong, end: what a person comes to in the end, the outcome of a life) (e:Hih in mihingte’ ~ ahi hi/Mi khempeuh’ ~ kibang kim a | the same destiny comes to all/amaute’ ~ bang hong hi hiam | what their end will be) (r:21.5.18/21.9.2/21.9.3/5.32.20) (q:draft)
thumongte = (t:n) (w:outcomes/end/consequences) (d:thumong, the end a matter comes to, with the plural te) (e:a ~ zong na phawkkha kei hi) (b:thumong) (r:23.47.7) (q:draft)
thumsak = (t:v) (w:intercede/pray for/plead for) (d:thum, beg, with sak, do for another: ask or pray on behalf of someone) (e:Kei adingin hong ~ in/mite a dingin Moses in ~ hi | Moses prayed for the people/Pasian’ mite a dingin hong ~ ahih manin | because he intercedes for the people of God/khialhna a neite a dingin a ~ hi | he interceded for the transgressors/kei’ tungah hong ~ kei in | do not plead with me) (s:ngetsak/thuumsak/thungetsak) (b:thum) (r:2.8.28/45.8.27/4.21.7/23.53.12/24.7.16) (q:draft)
thumsuah = (t:num) (w:three parts) (d:thum three with suah: divided into three; seh thumsuah seh khat is one part out of three, a third) (e:mi seh ~ seh khat thah nading) (r:66.9.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
thumte = (t:num) (w:three/the three) (d:thum, three, with the plural marker te: a group of three already known) (e:tua mi ~ ama mai-ah/a upapen ~ in Saul zui uh a | the three oldest followed Saul/hiang ~ in ni thum ahi hi | the three branches are three days/amah leh a tapa ~ leh a innkuan khempeuh | he and his three sons and all his house) (b:thum) (r:27.3.13/9.17.14/1.40.12/13.10.6) (q:draft)
thumthum = (t:v) (w:plead/beg earnestly/keep asking) (d:thum, beg, doubled to show that the asking is repeated or urgent) (e:A sun a zanin ama tungah a ~/ci-in hong ~ uh hi | they kept pleading with us, saying) (r:42.18.7/47.8.4) (q:draft)
thumthum = (t:v) (w:moan/coo) (d:of doves, make a low mournful sound) (e:vakhu bangin i ~ hi) (r:23.59.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
thumu = (t:n) (w:seer/one with insight) (d:one who sees or understands matters, usually with pa as thumu pa, a seer) (e:David’ ~ pa Gad tungah/~ pa’ inn koilai ahi hiam | where is the house of the seer/a paupau khol lote ~ taktak hizaw hi | those who do not talk much are the truly discerning/Keimah, ~ pa ka hi hi | I am the seer) (s:mupa) (r:13.21.9/20.17.27/9.9.18/9.9.19) (q:draft)
Thumu = (t:n) (w:seer) (d:thumu, seer, capitalised as a title with pa before a name: Thumu pa Iddo, Iddo the seer) (e:~ pa Iddo’ Maangmuhna sungah kigelh hi/~ pa hih lai-ah a om hiam | is the seer here/~ pa Samuel, Kish’ tapa Saul | Samuel the seer, Saul son of Kish) (b:thumu) (r:14.9.29/14.12.15/9.9.11/13.26.28) (q:draft)
thumuh = (t:n) (w:insight/understanding) (d:thu, matter, with muh, see: seeing into matters, insight; used before nading) (e:~ nading hahkat takpi in) (r:20.2.3) (q:draft)
thumuhkholhna = (t:n) (w:foresight) (d:thu matter, muh see, kholh beforehand, with the noun suffix na: seeing matters ahead of time) (e:nong kepna leh na ~ tawh) (r:44.24.2) (q:draft)
thumuhna = (t:n) (w:insight/understanding) (d:thumuh, seeing into matters, with the noun suffix na: insight, understanding) (e:Siangtho Pa theihna in ~ ahi hi/~, na lawm itpen dingin nei in | take insight as your closest friend/Lungsim pilte ~ tawh kampau uh a | the wise in heart speak with insight/theihna le ~ a nei khat beek om lo hi | no one has knowledge or understanding) (s:thutelna/theihtelna) (b:thumuh) (r:20.9.10/20.7.4/20.16.21/23.44.19) (q:draft)
thumuhnate = (t:n) (w:insights/visions) (d:thumuhna, what one sees or perceives of a matter, with plural te; of a prophet, the things seen in a vision) (e:ka pilna leh ka ~/Pasian in a pilna le a ~ zangin | God, using his wisdom and insight/Babylon siatna ding tawh kisai a ~ | the things he saw about the ruin of Babylon) (b:thumuhna) (r:20.5.1/23.13.1/49.1.9) (q:draft)
thumun = (t:num) (w:the three/all three) (d:thum three with un, the plural ending on those who act: the three of them) (e:A pawl ~ peengkul tumin beelte sukham uh a/tua pawi-ah a ~ a pai uh hi | the three of them went to the festival) (b:thum) (r:7.7.20/42.2.42) (q:draft)
thumute = (t:n) (w:seers) (d:thumu, seer, with the plural te) (e:kamsangte khempeuh le ~ khempeuh tungtawnin/thu a gen ~’ thugente | the words of the seers who spoke) (s:mutheite) (b:thumu) (r:12.17.13/14.33.18) (q:draft)
Thumute = (t:n) (w:seers) (d:Thumu, seer, with the plural te; in the title of a book of records of the seers) (e:~’ Khang Tangthu sungah kigelh hi) (b:Thumu) (r:14.33.19) (q:draft)
thumvei = (t:adv) (w:three times/thrice) (d:thum, three, with vei, time; also the third time) (e:Tua mah bangin ~ a hih khit ciangin/~ kei na hong nial ding hi | you will disown me three times/~ a dot man-inah Piter dah a | Peter was grieved because he asked three times) (r:44.10.16/40.26.34/43.21.17) (q:draft)
thumveina = (t:num) (w:third time) (d:thumvei, three times, with the ordinal suffix na: the third time, for the third time) (e:~ hong paikik a/~ thu a ngen hi | he prayed the third time/Saul in mi a ~ sawl a | Saul sent men a third time/ci-in ~ a dong hi | he asked the third time) (b:thumvei) (r:41.14.41/40.26.44/9.19.21/43.21.17) (q:draft)
thumveita = (t:adv) (w:three times) (d:thumvei, three times, with ta; nisimin thumveita is three times every day) (e:Nisimin ~ thu a ngen tawntung hi) (b:thumvei) (r:27.6.13) (q:draft)
thun = (t:v) (w:put into/pour into/fill) (d:put a liquid or other thing into a container such as a skin, a jar or a horn; used with sungah, into) (e:ka khituite na thawl sungah ~ in/Na sathau biing-ah sathau ~ in la | fill your horn with oil/leenggahtui thak a ~ ngei kei hi | no one ever pours in new wine/tuipi tuite thawlkhat sunga ~ bangin khawm a | he gathers the waters of the sea as into a jar/leenggahzu umte ka ~ lai takun | when we filled the wineskins) (s:guang) (r:19.56.8/42.5.37/9.16.1/19.33.7/6.9.13) (q:draft)
Thunei = (t:n) (w:dispute/case) (d:a matter that someone has against another, brought to be judged; thu, matter, with nei, have) (e:~ khat peuhpeuh a om ciangin) (r:26.44.24) (q:draft, low confidence)
thuneih = (t:v) (w:have authority/have power) (d:thu, word, with neih, have; thuneih theihna is power or authority) (e:a ~ theihnate uh a man lopi-in) (r:24.23.10) (q:draft)
thuneihna = (t:n) (w:authority/right/power) (d:thuneih, have authority, with the noun suffix na: the right or authority to command or decide; thuneihna tawh is by the authority of) (e:Topa Zeisu’ ~ tawh hih bang lamlahnate/tui dawn na’ng ~ nei lo ka hi uh hiam | do we not have the right to drink/~ pawl khat amah na guan ding hi | you shall give him some of your authority/Hih nate bang ~ tawh bawl na hi hiam | by what authority are you doing these things) (s:aana) (b:thuneih) (r:52.4.2/46.9.4/4.27.20/40.21.23) (q:draft)
thuneihpih = (t:v) (w:have a dispute with/be at law with) (d:thuneih, have a case, with pih, together with; na thuneihpih is the one you have a dispute with) (e:Na ~ na vengpa bek mah tawh) (b:thuneih) (r:20.25.9) (q:draft)
thuneite = (t:n) (w:authorities/rulers/those in authority) (d:those who hold authority, from thu matter and nei have, with te plural; ukna thuneite, the governing authorities) (e:ukna ~ a nialte pen Pasian’ koihsa/kumpipa in a sawl ~ khempeuh’ thu | the word of all the governors the king sends/Ukna ~ pen note’ hoih nadingin Pasian’ nasemte | the authorities are servants of God for your good) (r:45.13.2/45.13.4/60.2.14) (q:draft)
thuneite = (t:n) (w:parties/those involved) (d:those who have a matter or case, such as the two sides of a dispute) (e:~ a langnih tuakin/~ a khensak dingin Levi mite le siampite | Levites and priests to settle disputes) (r:5.19.17/46.6.9/14.19.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
thunem = (t:n) (w:gentle word/gentleness) (d:thu, word, with nem, soft; thunem tawh and thunem zangin are gently) (e:~ zangin na huh un/~ tawh a langte’ hoih lohna a puahtheite | able to correct opponents gently) (s:thudam/lungnemna) (r:48.6.1/55.2.25) (q:draft)
thunemin = (t:adv) (w:gently/with gentleness) (d:thunem, gentleness, with the linking ending in: gently) (e:Kiniamkhiatin, ~, lungduai-in om tawntung un) (s:damtakin) (b:thunem) (r:49.4.2) (q:draft)
thuneu = (t:n) (w:small matter/trifle/easy thing) (d:thu, matter, with neu, small: something of little weight or difficulty; thuneu sa is think it a small thing) (e:Topa muhna ah a ~ khat ahi hi/makpa suah ding a ~ sa na hi uh hiam | do you think it a small thing to become a son-in-law/hih in note adingin a ~ hi loin | this is no small matter for you) (a:thulian) (r:12.3.18/9.18.23/5.32.47) (q:draft)
thuneute = (t:n) (w:small matters/little things/trivial cases) (d:thuneu, small matter, with the plural te) (e:Nang ~ tungah na diktat zo hi/~ a khen dingin kilawm lo na hi uh hiam | are you not fit to judge small matters/~ amaute in khen tawm uh hi | the small matters they decided themselves) (a:thuhaksate) (b:thuneu) (r:40.25.21/46.6.2/2.18.26) (q:draft)
thung = (t:see) <thung-ip>
thung-ip = (t:n) (w:bag/pouch/satchel) (d:a bag carried on a journey or by a shepherd, named beside dangka-ip, the money bag) (e:a ~ sawkin suangtang khat la a/Dangka-ip, ~, khedap, tuate na keng kei un | do not carry a purse, a bag or sandals/~ a nei mi in la ta hen | let the one who has a bag take it) (s:thungip/ip) (r:9.17.49/42.10.4/42.22.36) (q:draft)
thungai = (t:v) (w:obey/be obedient/heed) (d:thu, word, with ngai, listen: listen to what is said and do it; thungai lo is disobedient) (e:tu-in ~ loin a om uh hi/upna tawh ~-in a paikhia hi | by faith he obeyed and went out/ka muh lohna-ah zong ~-in | obeying also in my absence/~ lote tawh kisia khawm loin | not perishing with the disobedient/~ dingin biakinn-a paina hoihzaw hi | going to the temple to listen is better) (s:thumang/mang) (a:lehdo) (r:45.11.31/58.11.8/50.2.12/58.11.31/21.5.1) (q:draft)
thungaih = (t:v) (w:obey/heed/listen) (d:form of thungai, obey or listen, used before ding, nading and lohna; thungaih lohna is disobedience) (e:tuutal thaute sangin ~ ding hoihzaw hi/mi khempeuh ~ lohna sungah a khumcip hi | he has shut up all people in disobedience/~ nading, thu hilh nading sim loh | except listening to and telling things/zuih khialhna leh ~ lohna apawl apawlte | every violation and disobedience) (b:thungai) (r:9.15.22/45.11.32/44.17.21/58.2.2) (q:draft)
thungaihna = (t:n) (w:obedience) (d:thungaih, obey or listen, with the noun suffix na: obedience; thungaihna ngah is be heard) (e:Note ~ in a kicin’ khit ciangin/Pasian kihtakna lungsim hangin ~ ngahin | he was heard because of his reverence for God) (b:thungaih) (r:47.10.6/60.1.1/58.5.7) (q:draft)
thungaihsun = (t:v) (w:consider/reflect/discern) (d:think matters over; thungaihsun theite, those able to think things through, are the discerning) (e:~ theite in pilna zong a/~ theite in olno takin ngah thei uh hi | the discerning gain it easily/~ theite in pil gamtatna nuamsa uh hi | the discerning delight in wise conduct/~ theite in taina lel tawh pilna ngahzo uh hi | the discerning gain knowledge by a mere rebuke) (r:20.15.14/20.14.33/20.14.6/20.10.23/20.19.25) (q:draft)
thungaihsut = (t:n) (w:thinking/reasoning/consideration) (d:thought given to a matter; thungaihsut theihna, the ability to think a matter through, is good judgment, discretion or understanding) (e:Na ~ theihna le na thutelna in/Leenggahzu in ka mite’ ~ theihna beisak hi | wine takes away the understanding of my people/pilna, siamna, ~ theihna lei in | buy wisdom, instruction and insight) (r:20.2.11/20.13.15/28.4.11/20.23.23) (q:draft)
thungaihsutna = (t:n) (w:plan/thought/planning) (d:thungaihsut, think a matter over, with the noun suffix na: a plan or purpose, planning) (e:minamte’ ~ a mawkna suahin/Topa’ ~ kip ngitnget a | the plans of the Lord stand firm/nasepna leh ~, pilna leh theihna cihte om lo hi | there is no work or planning, wisdom or knowledge) (s:ngaihsutna/geelna) (b:thungaihsut) (r:19.33.10/21.9.10/19.33.11) (q:draft)
thungaite = (t:n) (w:hearers/listeners) (d:thungai, listen to what is said, with the plural te: those who listen to the word) (e:~ bek hi kei un) (b:thungai) (r:59.1.22) (q:draft)
thungeek = (t:n) (w:elementary principles/rudiments/elemental things) (d:thu matter with ngeek infant, tender: the first and basic things; leitung thungeek is the elemental things of the world) (e:leitung ~ khut nuai-ah sila in/leitung ~ zui-in | following the elemental things of the world/thahat lo, nopna hong pia thei lo ~ lamah | to the weak elemental things that give no joy) (r:48.4.3/51.2.8/48.4.9) (q:draft)
thungen = (t:v) (w:pray) (d:thu, word, with ngen, ask: speak to God in prayer; thungen ding is to pray) (e:a zi adingin ~ hi/tua milim tungah ~ a | he prays to that idol/~ dingin mual tungah a kahto hi | he went up the mountain to pray/Pasian tungah i lungsim pia-in ~ ni | let us lift our hearts to God and pray/a om lai mite adingin ~ in | pray for the remnant) (r:1.25.21/23.38.2/23.44.17/41.6.46/25.3.41/12.19.4)
thungenin = (t:v) (w:praying/pray) (d:thungen, pray, with the linking suffix in: praying, or prayed and then) (e:Topa mai-ah ~ a om lai takin/Zan kim lai takin Paul leh Silas in ~ | about midnight Paul and Silas were praying/Stefen in Pasian kiangah ~ | Stephen prayed to God/Kha Siangtho tawh ~ | praying in the Holy Spirit) (b:thungen) (r:9.1.12/23.37.15/44.16.25/44.7.59/65.1.20) (q:draft)
thungennate = (t:n) (w:words/sayings) (d:the things said, here by the seers; apparently thu word and gen speak with nate, written as one word) (e:thu-mu-te’ ~, en in) (r:14.33.18) (q:draft, low confidence)
