thungente = (t:n) (w:those who pray/those who call on) (d:thungen pray with the plural te; tua min tawh thungente is those who pray in that name) (e:tua min tawh ~ a bawlsiapa) (b:thungen) (r:44.9.21) (q:draft)
thungentehna = (t:n) (w:parable) (d:thu word, gen speak, teh compare, with the noun suffix na: a saying told as a comparison) (e:a nungzuite in tua ~ a dong uh hi) (s:thugentehna) (r:41.7.17) (q:draft)
thungentna = (t:n) (w:prayer) (s:thungetna)
thunget = (t:v) (w:pray) (d:form of thungen, pray, used in dependent clauses and before endings; also as a noun, praying) (e:Solomon a ~ a tawp ciangin/Pasian’ kianga ~ a phattuamna om kei | there is no gain in praying to God/Tua banga a ~ a khit ma-in | before he had finished praying/note adingin Topa tungah ~ lohna tawh | by failing to pray to the Lord for you/eite in ~ ding a kilawm bangin | as we ought to pray) (r:14.7.1/18.21.15/1.24.15/9.12.23/45.8.26) (q:draft)
thungetna = (t:n) (w:prayer/plea) (d:thunget, pray, with the noun suffix na: a prayer, what is asked of God) (e:Topa in ka ~ hong sang hi/Ka ~ hong za in la | hear my prayer/mi cimawhte’ ~ kin-in | he regards the prayer of the destitute/ka ~ hong ngai in | listen to my prayer) (s:thuumna/kutna) (r:19.6.9/19.102.17/19.88.2/19.61.1) (q:draft)
thungetnate = (t:n) (w:prayers/pleas) (d:thungetna, prayer, with the plural te) (e:Jessi’ tapa David’ ~ bei ta hi/Pasian in na ~ hong za a | God has heard your prayers/Pasian in amau’ ~ don lo hi | God pays no heed to their prayers/ama ~ zong mawhna suak sak in | let his prayers too be counted as sin) (s:thuumnate/ngetnate) (b:thungetna) (r:19.72.20/19.109.7/44.10.31/18.24.12) (q:draft)
