thunin = (t:v) (w:putting in/filling) (d:thun, put into a container, with the linking ending in; a dimtakin thunin is having filled it full) (e:a dimtakin ~ a pai uh hi) (b:thun) (r:40.25.4) (q:draft)
thunthuah = (t:v) (w:put in/pour in/add into) (d:thun put into with thuah, add: fill a vessel with something, here oil into a lamp) (e:a tui ~ lopi-in pai uh a) (r:40.25.3) (q:draft)
thunuam = (t:n) (w:peace/fellowship/goodwill) (d:peace or good terms between people or with God; thunuam gen is proclaim peace and thunuam-a biakna is the fellowship or peace offering) (e:Sum a pia zo mite kiangah ~ gen a/hong zui khate in ~ mu ngei lo uh hi | those who follow them never know peace/piak theih ding ~-a biakna ngeina ahi hi | it is the law of the fellowship offering that may be presented) (s:kilemna) (r:33.3.5/3.7.11/23.59.8) (q:draft)
thunuam = (t:v) (w:be good to/be kind to/be favourable to/be gracious to) (d:used with tungah for the person who is treated kindly) (e:kei tungah Topa hong ~ hi/Persia kumpite ko tungah a ~ dingin hong bawlsak hi | he made the kings of Persia favourable to us/mihonpite’ Pasian hong ~ kha thei ding hi | perhaps the God of hosts will be gracious/a uliante kei tungah a ~ dingin a bawl | who made his officials favourable to me) (r:19.116.7/15.9.9/30.5.15/15.7.27) (q:draft)
thunuama = (t:adj) (w:of fellowship/of peace) (d:thunuam with the linking suffix a, describing the next noun; thunuama biakna is the fellowship or peace offering) (e:meihal biakna le ~ biakna bawngtalte/~ biakna a pia uh hi | they presented fellowship offerings/~ biakna ngeina hih bang ahi hi | this is the law of the fellowship offering) (b:thunuam) (r:2.24.5/3.7.33/7.21.4/3.7.11) (q:draft)
thunuamte = (t:n) (w:the diligent/the willing) (d:mi thunuamte stands where the NIV has diligent hands, set against a thadahte, the lazy) (e:Mi ~ a vang lian a) (s:thanuamte) (a:thadahte) (r:20.12.24) (q:draft, low confidence)
Thupalsat = (t:v) (w:transgress/break the law) (d:thu, word or law, with palsat, transgress; thupalsat mite are transgressors) (e:~ mite tawh amah a kisimkhawm hi) (r:41.15.28) (q:draft)
thupalsatna = (t:n) (w:transgression/rebellion/offence/wrongdoing) (d:thu, word or law, with palsat, transgress, and the noun suffix na: the breaking of a law or command) (e:mawhna, ~ leh khialhna maisakin/Ka ~ khempeuh panin kei hong honkhia inla | save me from all my transgressions/Na sanggamte’ ~ leh a khialna na maisak in | forgive the transgression and sin of your brothers/Topa aw, keima ~ hang hi lo | not for any offence of mine, Lord) (s:palsatna/mawhna/khialhna) (r:2.34.7/1.50.17/19.39.8/19.59.3) (q:draft)
thupalsatnate = (t:n) (w:transgressions/offenses) (d:thupalsatna, transgression, with the plural te) (e:leh ka ~ ka thei a/Na ~ meiipi bangin | your offenses like a cloud/amau’ ~ khempeuh maisakin | forgiving all their offenses) (s:palsatnate/mawhnate) (b:thupalsatna) (r:19.51.3/23.43.25/23.44.22/11.8.50) (q:draft)
thupalsatte = (t:n) (w:transgressors) (d:thu, word or law, with palsat, transgress, and the plural te: those who break the law) (e:~ kisusiamang khin ding a/~ na zia na tong ka hilh ding a | I will teach transgressors your ways) (s:palsatte/mimawhte) (r:19.37.38/19.51.13) (q:draft)
thupang = (t:v) (w:plead a case/contend) (d:take part in a case at court; the verse has the Lord taking his place to do so) (e:Topa in ~ dingin ama panmun) (r:23.3.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
thupeelin = (t:adv) (w:shrewdly/craftily) (d:how God deals with the devious, thukawi mi; the base thupeel is not otherwise attested) (e:a thukawi mi tungah ~ na gamta hi) (r:10.22.27) (q:draft, low confidence)
thupha = (t:v) (w:bless) (d:thu, word, with pha, good: a blessing; thupha pia is bless and thupha ngah is be blessed) (e:Hong phuisamte tungah ~ na pia un/Topa in note ~ hong pia ta hen | may the Lord bless you/Topa a beel mi in ~ a ngah hi | the one who takes refuge in the Lord is blessed/~ zong pia peuhmah kei in | do not bless them at all either) (a:phuisam/hamsiat) (r:42.6.28/1.1.22/19.115.15/24.17.7/4.23.25)
thupha = (t:v) (w:good news) (e:gamlapi-a om lawmte kiang pan-a ~ zak | hearing good news from friends far away/thuhoih ~ a hong puak | who brings good tidings) (s:thuhoih) (r:20.25.25/23.52.7)
Thupha = (t:n) (w:blessing/blessed) (d:thupha, blessing, written with a capital at the start of a sentence or as a title: Thupha a ngah is receive blessing or be blessed, and Thupha a nei is the Blessed One) (e:mite in ~ a ngah uh hi/~ om ta hen | let there be blessing/~ ngah ta in, ka tapa David | may you be blessed, my son David/Pasian’ mawhsakna tawh kipelh mi in ~ a ngah hi | the one whom God does not count guilty is blessed) (a:samsiatna) (b:thupha) (r:45.4.7/41.14.61/40.10.12/9.26.25/45.4.8) (q:draft)
thuphate = (t:n) (w:blessings) (d:thupha, blessing, with the plural te; Kha Siangtho piak thuphate are the blessings the Holy Spirit gives, the spiritual gifts) (e:hih ~ khempeuh no tungah hong tungin/ang sung leh gil sung ~ tawh | with blessings of the breast and womb/Pasian in a hong piak ~ | the blessings that God gives) (s:daupainate) (a:samsiatnate) (b:thupha) (r:5.28.2/46.14.1/1.49.25/45.1.11) (q:draft)
thuphawk = (t:v) (w:take heed/be aware/pay attention) (d:thu, matter, with phawk, notice: be aware of how things stand and take them to heart; thuphawk loin is heedlessly or complacently, and thuphawk theih lohna is a heart that cannot take things in) (e:~ loin, a ngeina bangun omcip a/a ~ theih lohna uh hangin | because of their inability to take it to heart) (s:phawk) (r:36.1.12/41.3.5) (q:draft)
thuphawkna = (t:n) (w:warning/awareness/heed) (d:thuphawk, take heed, with the noun suffix na: a warning that makes one aware; thuphawkna ngah is be warned) (e:a nasem pa in ~ ngah a) (s:hilhkholhna) (b:thuphawk) (r:19.19.11) (q:draft)
thuphawksa = (t:adj) (w:experienced/discerning/respected) (d:thuphawk, be aware of matters, with sa, already: experienced, having come to know how things are; said of men fit to lead) (e:a pil, thuthei, ~ mite teel unla) (s:phawksa) (b:thuphawk) (r:5.1.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
thupi = (t:adj) (w:important/great/special/solemn) (d:thu, matter, with pi, great: of great weight or worth; a thupi lo is unimportant, thupi takin is solemnly, and thupi ngaihsut is count as important) (e:hih ding bek a ~ ahi hi/na sepnate ~ mahmah hi | your deeds are very great/Tu lai takin nasep ~ ka nei hi | right now I have an important work/A ~ lo tawh a kibang pumpi nate | the parts of the body that seem unimportant) (s:lian/phamawh) (b:thu) (r:48.6.15/1.43.3/24.32.19/16.6.3/46.12.23) (q:draft)
thupia = (t:v) (w:give an order/command/issue an order) (d:thu, word, with pia, give: give an order or command; the form used before another word is thupiak) (e:Kumpipa Darias in ~ a/Topa in ~ khin hi | the Lord has commanded it/Moses in amaute ~ in | Moses commanded them/a kisuksiat nading Topa in ~ zo hi | the Lord has given the order for it to be destroyed) (s:sawl/vaikhak) (r:15.6.1/1.12.20/3.8.34/5.31.10/23.23.11) (q:draft)
thupiak = (t:v) (w:command/order) (d:form of thupia, give an order, used before another word; a thupiak bangin is just as he commanded) (e:Amah in a ~ bangin/Topa in Moses a ~ bangin | as the Lord commanded Moses/nangma ~ bangin ka mite khempeuh gamta ding uh hi | all my people will act as you command/dawi gilote ~ nading aana nei a | he has authority to command evil spirits) (s:sawl/vaikhak) (b:thupia) (r:4.20.9/1.7.5/4.36.10/1.41.40/41.1.27)
thupiakkholhna = (t:n) (w:warning/advance instruction/revelation) (d:thupiak, command, with kholh, beforehand, and the noun suffix na: a word given in advance about what is to come, a warning or revelation) (e:thute-ah ~ a ngah khit ciangin/Topa hong muhsak mangmatna leh ~ thu | the visions and revelations the Lord has shown) (s:hilhkholhna) (r:58.11.7/47.12.1) (q:draft)
thupiakna = (t:n) (w:command/commandment/order) (d:thupiak, command, with the noun suffix na: a command or order; thupiakna zui or mang is keep a command) (e:ka ~ na mang ding uh hi/Hih in keima ~ ahi hi | this is my command/kumpipa’ ~ tawh nasem uh a | they worked under the king’s orders/a ~ a zuite tungah | to those who keep his commands) (s:sawlna/vaikhakna) (b:thupiak) (r:43.14.15/5.4.13/43.15.17/16.11.23/5.7.9) (q:draft)
thupiaknate = (t:n) (w:commands/commandments/orders) (d:thupiakna, command, with the plural te) (e:nangma ~ zuih ding ka zekai kei/Na ~ ka lunggulhna-in | in my longing for your commands/kumpipa’ ~ zong va gen uh hi | they also delivered the king’s orders/ka ~ mangin tuate na sep uh leh | if you obey my commands and do them) (s:thupiakte/sawlnate/thukhamte) (b:thupiakna) (r:19.119.60/15.8.36/19.119.131/3.26.3) (q:draft)
thupiaksa = (t:v) (w:commanded) (d:thupiak, command, with sa, already: what has been commanded; a thupiaksa bangin is just as he had commanded) (e:amah a ~ khempeuh tawh kituakin/Topa in Moses a ~ bangin | as the Lord had commanded Moses/Topa in Moses a ~ khempeuh tawh kituakin | in keeping with all that the Lord had commanded Moses/~ bangin amaute in sem khin hi | they had done it just as commanded) (s:sawlsa) (b:thupiak) (r:2.40.16/4.29.40/2.39.42/2.39.43) (q:draft)
thupiaksate = (t:n) (w:commands/things commanded/instructions) (d:thupiaksa, what has been commanded, with the plural te) (e:Pasian’ nasem Moses’ ~ khempeuh bangin/hih ka hong ~ amaute tungah gensawn in | pass on to them these things I have commanded you) (s:thupiakte/thupiaknate) (b:thupiaksa) (r:13.6.49/54.5.7) (q:draft)
thupiakte = (t:n) (w:commands/commandments/orders) (d:thupiak, command, with the plural te) (e:ka ~ a zui mi/Nangma ~ um ka hih manin | because I trust your commands/Moses tungah a piak ~ ahi hi | are the commands he gave to Moses/Ka ~ leh ka thute zuih ding | to keep my commands and my instructions) (s:thupiaknate/sawlnate/thukhamte) (b:thupiak) (r:5.5.10/19.119.66/3.27.34/2.16.28) (q:draft)
thupiang = (t:n) (w:event/happening/occurrence) (d:thu, matter, with piang, happen: what has happened or will happen; thupiang khempeuh is everything that happened) (e:~ khempeuh siampi liante a zasak/amau tunga ~ khempeuh ama tungah gen uh hi | they told him everything that had happened to them/hih lai-a ~ khempeuh note kiangah hong gen ding | will tell you everything that is happening here/~ dingte ka hong lak ding hi | I will show you what is going to happen) (r:40.28.11/27.8.19/6.2.23/51.4.9) (q:draft)
thupiangsate = (t:n) (w:things that have happened/past events) (d:thupiang, what happens, with sa, already, and the plural te: the things that have happened) (e:A ~ hangin lau-in lunghimawhin) (r:47.7.11) (q:draft)
thupiangte = (t:n) (w:events/happenings/things that happened) (d:thupiang, event, with the plural te: the things that happen or have happened) (e:Mordekai in hih ~ khempeuh lai-in ciamteh/kote tunga, ~ hong phawk in | remember what has happened to us/A paikawmun hih ~ kikumkum uh hi | as they went they talked over these events/leitunga ~ ka theih ciangin | when I came to know the things that happen on earth) (b:thupiang) (r:17.9.20/25.5.1/42.24.14/21.8.16) (q:draft)
thupiangteng = (t:n) (w:all that happened/the whole matter) (d:thupiang, event, with teng, all: everything that has happened, the whole matter) (e:a ~ na mipihte tungah gen in) (b:thupiang) (r:26.33.2/27.2.17) (q:draft)
thupilak = (t:v) (w:take seriously/regard as important/honor) (d:thupi, important, with lak, take: take seriously, treat as important; the same verse also writes it as thupi takin lak) (e:ka thupiaknate ~ lo na hih manun) (s:thupisak/thupisan/thupisim) (a:simmawh) (r:39.2.2) (q:draft)
thupina = (t:n) (w:dignity/splendor/honor/greatness) (d:thupi, great or honorable, with the noun suffix na: dignity or splendor; lungsim thupina is integrity of heart) (e:ka ~ teng huih letkhiat bangin beimang/khanghamte’ sam kan’na in amau’ ~ lim ahi hi | gray hair is the splendor of the old/lungsim ~ leh thumanna tawh ka mai-ah gamta-in | walk before me with integrity of heart and uprightness/tua biakinn a ~ zia a lak uh hi | they pointed out the splendor of the temple) (s:thupitna/minthanna) (b:thupi) (r:18.30.15/11.9.4/20.20.29/40.24.1) (q:draft)
thupinate = (t:n) (w:glories/splendors/great things) (d:thupina, greatness, with the plural te: the splendors or precious things someone once had, where the NIV has treasures) (e:nidanga a ~ a nung phawkkik hi) (s:thupitnate/minthannate) (b:thupina) (r:25.1.7) (q:draft)
thupipen = (t:adj) (w:greatest/most important) (d:thupi, great, with pen, most: the greatest or most important) (e:lak panin a ~ tu-in sal-in) (s:lianpen/lianbel) (b:thupi) (r:25.1.1) (q:draft)
thupisak = (t:v) (w:value highly/regard as important) (d:thupi, important, with sak, hold to be: value highly, set great store by something) (e:Grik mite in pilna a ~ uh hi) (s:thupilak/thupisan) (b:thupi) (r:46.1.22) (q:draft)
thupisan = (t:v) (w:respect/take seriously/regard as important) (d:thupi, important, with san, take as: take seriously, not make light of; the NIV turns it round as do not despise) (e:Vanglianpa’ taiina ~’ in | take the discipline of the Almighty seriously) (s:thupilak/thupisak) (a:simmawh) (b:thupi) (r:18.5.17) (q:draft, low confidence)
thupisim = (t:v) (w:regard/heed/take seriously/pay attention to) (d:count as important, pay heed to; with kei or lo it means disregard or not listen to) (e:Amaute ka ~ kei hi/kamsangte’ thu na ~ kei uh leh | if you do not heed the words of the prophets/amaute in ~ loin a hong mang kei uh hi | they paid no heed and did not obey/kulhpi a dal pasian a ~ zaw ding hi | he will rather honor a god of fortresses) (s:thupilak/thupisan) (a:simmawh) (r:5.33.9/24.29.19/24.26.5/27.11.38) (q:draft)
thupite = (t:adj) (w:important/great/chief) (d:plural of thupi, said of persons or things of high rank or importance; mi thupite is the great, the mighty) (e:vantungmi ~ khat ahi Mikhael/mi ~’ kihihsakna beisak hi | he puts an end to the pride of the mighty/milian mi ~ in keima huhna bek tawh | nobles and great men, only by my help/lai ~ sungah hih thu kiciamteh hi | this was written down in the official records) (b:thupi) (r:27.10.13/18.12.21/20.8.16/17.9.32) (q:draft)
thupiteng = (t:n) (w:important things/valuables) (d:thupi important with teng all of: the things that matter most, the valuable things) (e:a ~ na nusiakha uh a/a neih a lam a ~ khempeuh uh | all their valuable possessions/a khuam ~ ka phut a | I set up the main pillar) (b:thupi) (r:40.23.24/24.20.5/46.3.10) (q:draft)
thupitna = (t:n) (w:majesty/greatness/glory) (d:thupi, great, with the noun suffix na: majesty, greatness) (e:a ~ leh a liatna mu-in/minthan’na, ~, vangliatna leh ukzawhnate | glory, majesty, power and authority) (s:thupina/minliatna/vangliatna) (r:61.1.16/65.1.24) (q:draft)
thupitnate = (t:n) (w:glories/splendors/great things) (d:thupitna, greatness, with the plural te: the splendors or precious things someone once had, where the NIV has treasures) (e:nidanga a ~ a nung phawk kik uh hi) (s:thupinate/minthannate) (b:thupitna) (r:25.1.7) (q:draft)
thupizaw = (t:adj) (w:greater/more important/better) (d:thupi, great or important, with the comparative zaw: greater, worth more; the thing compared is marked by sangin, than) (e:pumpi pen puan sangin ~ hi/Nuntakna pen an sangin ~ a | life is more than food/a lui sangin hoih zawin ~ ding hi | it will be better and greater than the old one/tapa sagih sangin a ~ | who is better than seven sons/biakna tau ~ ahi hiam | or is the altar greater) (s:lianzaw) (a:neuzaw) (b:thupi) (r:42.12.23/37.2.9/8.4.15/40.23.19) (q:draft)
thupuak = (t:n) (w:message/news/report) (d:thu, word, with puak, carry or send: a message or news brought to someone, also an order sent; thupuak pa is a messenger) (e:Jezebel’ ~ bangin hih uh hi/ama ~ thaman ka piakna-in | as the reward I gave him for his news/a citak ~ pa in mi lungdamsakkik hi | a faithful messenger makes people glad again/Amah in tua ~ pa sat a | he struck that messenger down) (s:thuzak/thuthak) (r:11.21.11/10.4.10/20.13.17/10.1.15) (q:draft)
thupuakte = (t:n) (w:messengers/bearers of the word) (d:thupuak, word that is carried, with the plural te: those who bring the message) (e:vangliatna tawh thu a gen ~’ tung panin) (s:kamtaite) (b:thupuak) (r:60.1.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
thuseel = (t:v) (w:quarrel/argue/dispute) (d:thu, matter, with seel, argue: quarrel or dispute; thuseel lo stands where the NIV has will not quarrel; also written thusel) (e:Amah in ~ lo kiko lo ding a) (s:thusel/kisel) (r:40.12.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
thusel = (t:v) (w:dispute/debate/argue) (d:argue a matter against someone; thusel a siamte are skilled debaters, thusel zo lo is unable to out-argue) (e:amaute in ~ zo lo uh hi/mipilte, miteite, le ~ a siamte | the wise, the scholars and the skilled debaters) (s:thuseel/kisel/kinial) (r:44.6.10/46.1.20) (q:draft)
thusia = (t:n) (w:evil/mischief/wicked scheme) (d:thu, matter, with sia, bad: evil that is planned, spoken or done; thusia bawl is do evil and thusia geel is plot evil) (e:~ bawl mi kici hi/~ bawl ding ngaihsutna | a mind that plans to do evil/migilote in ~ bekbek gen hi | the wicked speak only evil/a lung sung uh ah ~ geelgeel uh a | they keep devising evil in their hearts) (s:gilohna/hoihlohna) (a:thuhoih) (r:20.24.8/19.64.2/20.6.18/20.10.6/19.140.2) (q:draft)
thusia = (t:n) (w:disaster/harm/trouble/calamity) (d:something bad that happens to someone, misfortune) (e:Thumante tungah ~ tung lo a/mi ngongtatpa pen ~ in sulzuih mengmeng ta hen | may disaster hunt down the violent man/~ ahi zongin om lo hi | nor is there any disaster/Amah in ~ zak ding lau lo hi | he is not afraid of hearing bad news) (s:tuahsiatna/siatna) (r:20.12.21/21.11.2/19.140.11/11.5.4/19.112.7) (q:draft)
thusiapi = (t:n) (w:grievous thing/bitter thing/great evil) (d:thusia, evil matter, with pi, great: a grievous or bitter thing; here the bitter things sought against someone) (e:kei tungah ~ nong zong a) (b:thusia) (r:18.13.26) (q:draft)
thusiate = (t:n) (w:bad news/distressing words) (d:thusia, bad matter, with the plural te: bad news, words that bring distress) (e:Mite in hih ~ a zak uh ciangin) (b:thusia) (r:2.33.4) (q:draft)
thusim = (t:v) (w:attentive/mindful/be careful/regard/respect) (d:thu, matter, with sim, count: pay regard to a person or thing, look on with favor; thusim lo is disregard or show contempt for) (e:Abel leh ama piakna ~ a/Kain leh ama piakna ~ lo hi | he did not look with favor on Cain and his offering/amau’ a Honkhiapa ~ lo uh hi | they showed no regard for their Savior/a mit in ginalote ~ lo a | in whose eyes the vile have no regard) (s:thupisim) (a:simmawh) (r:1.4.4/1.4.5/5.32.15/19.15.4)
thusim nei = (t:n) (w:hypocrite) (d:thusim, secret, with nei, have: one who keeps hidden motives, a hypocrite) (s:simtatpa/thusimnei/thusimneimi)
thusim neite = (t:n) (w:hypocrites) (d:thusim nei, hypocrite, with the plural te) (e:~ tawh ka kipawl kei hi) (s:simtatte/misimtatte/kineihkhemte) (b:thusim nei) (r:19.26.4)
thusimin = (t:adv) (w:secretly/in secret) (d:thusim, secret, with the adverb ending in: secretly; thusimin a kikoih is what is kept hidden) (e:~ a kikoih peuhmah/~ a kikoih peuhmah khatvei teitei thulang a suak | whatever is kept secret will one day come to light) (s:simthamin) (a:kilangin/langtangin) (r:41.4.22/42.8.17) (q:draft)
thusimlohna = (t:n) (w:contempt/scorn/mockery) (d:thusim, regard, with loh, not, and the noun suffix na: contempt, treating someone with no respect) (e:ka galte un hong ~ tawh/Topa aw, galte in hong ~ leh | Lord, how the enemy has mocked you) (s:simmawhna/zahkona) (a:thusimna/zahtakna) (r:19.80.6/19.74.18) (q:draft)
thusimna = (t:n) (w:respect/esteem/regard) (d:thusim, pay regard to, with the noun suffix na: the respect or esteem shown to someone) (e:mi’ hong ~ deihhuai zaw hi/lungnemna tawh, ~ lungsim tawh | with gentleness and a respectful heart) (s:zahtakna) (a:thusimlohna/simmawhna) (b:thusim) (r:20.22.1/60.3.15) (q:draft)
thusimnei = (t:n) (w:hypocrite) (d:thusim, secret, with nei, have: one who hides his real motives, a hypocrite; also written thusim nei) (s:simtatpa/thusim nei/thusimneimi)
thusimneimi = (t:n) (w:hypocrite) (d:thusim nei, having hidden motives, with mi, person: a hypocrite) (s:simtatpa/thusim nei/thusimnei)
thusimte = (t:n) (w:secrets/mysteries/hidden things) (d:thusim, secret, with the plural te: things kept secret or not yet made known) (e:Pasian’ Gam ~ na theihtheih nadingun/Pasian’ ~ a gengen ahi uh hi | they keep speaking the mysteries of God/~ khatvei teitei thulang suak ding hi | hidden things will one day come to light/amah in ~ hong pholakin | he will bring hidden things to light) (s:thuthukte/kiseelte) (b:thusim) (r:42.8.10/27.2.22/46.14.2/42.12.2/46.4.5) (q:draft)
thusimteng = (t:n) (w:whole secret/mystery) (d:thusim, hidden matter, with teng, all of) (e:Khrih zangin a sepnop ~ eite tungah) (s:thuthuk) (r:49.1.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
thusit = (t:v) (w:try/judge/put on trial) (d:thu, matter, with sit, examine: examine a case in court, put someone on trial) (e:~ dingin amah a kipaipih ciangin/~ dingin amau’ uliante kiangah ka paipih hi | I brought him to their leaders to be tried/amah ~ ding ka geel zo uh hi | we had planned to try him) (s:thukhen) (r:19.37.33/44.24.6/44.23.28) (q:draft)
thusitin = (t:v) (w:trying a case/sitting in judgment) (d:thusit, examine a case in court, with the linking ending in) (e:thukhen zumah ~ a om hunsung mahun) (b:thusit) (r:40.27.19) (q:draft)
thusitna = (t:n) (w:trial/examination/account) (d:thusit, try a case, with the noun suffix na: the examining of a case or of a person’s conduct; thusitna thuak is stand trial or give account) (e:~ thuak dingin mawhna zong mipa khat/hih lai-ah ~ ka thuak hi | I am on trial here/kampaunate uh khempeuh bangin ~ a thuak ding uh hi | they will have to give account for all their words/~ a thuak dingin thukhen zumah hong kipaipih ciangin | when you are brought to court to stand trial) (s:sittelna/thusuahna) (b:thusit) (r:19.109.6/44.25.9/44.23.6/40.12.36/41.13.11) (q:draft)
thusuahna = (t:n) (w:account/giving account) (d:thu matter with suah, bring out, and the noun suffix na: having to state one's case before a judge) (e:mai-ah ~ a thuak ding uh hi) (s:thusitna) (r:60.4.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
thutak = (t:n) (w:truth) (d:thu, word, with tak, true: truth, what is true; most often paired with thuman as thuman thutak) (e:Thuman ~ ka gen ciangin/thuman ~ ah a lungdam thei hi | it rejoices in the truth/thuman ~ ngai loin, tangthu ngai-in | not listening to the truth but listening to myths/khat leh khat tungah thuman ~ kam kipau un | speak the truth to one another) (s:thumanna) (a:thuzuau/zuauthu) (b:thu) (r:43.8.45/19.119.138/46.13.6/55.4.4/38.8.16) (q:draft)
thutakin = (t:adv) (w:truthfully/faithfully/justly) (d:thutak, truth, with the adverb ending in; often paired with thuman) (e:Thuman ~ gamta tawntung lecin/khatlekhat kikalah thuman le ~ na vaihawm uh a | you deal justly and truthfully with one another/Amah ~, it tawntungna nei ahih manin | because he is faithful and ever loving) (s:thumanin/citakin/mantakin) (b:thutak) (r:20.21.21/24.7.5/19.98.3) (q:draft)
thutakna = (t:n) (w:faithfulness/truthfulness) (d:thutak, truth, with the noun suffix na: faithfulness, being true to one’s word; often paired with itna kip, steadfast love) (e:Itna kip leh ~ kigawm ding a/Leilak panin ~ hong po khiato ding a | faithfulness will spring up from the earth/na ~, vantung bangin kip tawntung hi | your faithfulness stands firm like the heavens/itna kip leh ~ tawh a dim | abounding in steadfast love and faithfulness) (s:thumanna/cihtakna) (b:thutak) (r:19.85.10/19.89.2/19.85.11/2.34.6) (q:draft)
thutakpa = (t:n) (w:the true one) (d:thutak truth with pa marking a man: he who is true; paired as thuman thutakpa) (e:Pasian in thuman ~ hi ta hen) (s:taktakpa) (b:thutak) (r:45.3.4) (q:draft)
thutakte = (t:n) (w:truths/true things) (d:thutak truth with the plural te, often in the pair thuman thutakte) (e:i zaksa thuman ~/a hoih, a man, a ~ hong piangsak hi | it produces what is good, right and true) (b:thutak) (r:58.2.1/49.5.9) (q:draft)
thutan = (t:see) <thutan'na>
thutan'na = (t:n) (w:justice/uprightness/fair judgment) (d:the quality of judging and acting rightly; from thutang just, upright, with na) (e:Amah in thumanna leh ~ deih a/kicin’na leh ~ in kei hong kem ta hen | may integrity and uprightness protect me/keima ~ nong kipsak a | you have upheld my right/Keima la in nangma itna leh ~ hi a | my song is of your love and justice) (s:thutang/diktatna) (a:diklohna) (r:19.33.5/2.23.6/19.25.21/19.9.4/19.101.1) (q:draft)
thutan'nate = (t:n) (w:justice/judgments) (d:thutan'na, justice, with the plural te; another spelling of thutannate) (e:thumanna leh ~ in ama tokhom’ bulpi ahi hi | righteousness and justice are the foundation of his throne) (s:thutannate) (r:19.97.2) (q:draft)
thutang = (t:n) (w:justice/uprightness) (d:what is just and right, justice; often paired with thuman, righteousness, and used with zang, practise, or heikhia, pervert) (e:~ lampi ka tawn hi/Pasian in ~ zang lo ahi hiam | does God not practise justice/thuman leh ~ tawh zuih ding ahi hi | to be kept with faithfulness and uprightness/a mite khempeuh tungah ~ leh thuman zang hi | he did what was just and right for all his people) (s:thutan'na/diktatna) (a:diklohna) (r:20.8.20/21.3.16/18.8.3/19.111.8/10.8.15) (q:draft)
thutang = (t:adj) (w:upright/just) (d:just and upright in character; lungsim thutang is upright in heart) (e:lungsim ~ mite a hon hi/Topa hoihin ~ hi | the Lord is good and upright/A paubaang lo a ~, Pasian zahtakin | blameless and upright, fearing God/lungsim ~ mite’ gam sungah | in the land of the upright in heart) (s:dik/maan) (a:thukawi/thumanlo) (r:19.7.10/20.2.8/19.25.8/18.1.8/23.26.10) (q:draft)
thutangin = (t:adv) (w:justly/with justice/uprightly) (d:thutang, just, with the adverb ending in: justly; often in the pair thuman thutangin, in righteousness and justice) (e:~ a gamta mipa tungah/thuman, ~ thu a khen hi | he judges with righteousness and justice/mite tungah ~ na sem hi | he deals justly with people/nang tungah thuman ~ kong gamta ding hi | I will deal with you in righteousness and justice) (s:thumanin/diktakin/maanin) (b:thutang) (r:19.112.5/28.12.6/19.103.6/18.37.23/28.2.19) (q:draft)
thutangte = (t:n) (w:the upright/upright people) (d:thutang, upright, with the plural te: those who are upright; most often lungsim thutangte, the upright in heart) (e:Pahtawina in ~ tawh kilawm kituak hi/lungsim ~ tungah na hotkhiatna hong zom in | continue your salvation to the upright in heart/Lungsim ~ in hih thu mu in kipak uh hi | the upright in heart see this and rejoice/Lungsim ~ khempeuh in amah phat ding uh hi | all the upright in heart will praise him) (s:midikte/thumante/mihoihte) (a:migilote) (b:thutang) (r:19.33.1/19.73.1/19.36.10/19.107.42/19.64.10) (q:draft)
thutanna = (t:n) (w:judgment/condemnation/verdict/sentence) (d:thu, case, with tan, decide, and the noun suffix na: the deciding of a case and the sentence given; mawhna thutanna is condemnation and thutanna thuak is suffer judgment; in some texts also a spelling of thutan'na, justice) (e:sung bekinah ~ na thuak ta hi/mawhna ~ nasepna in vangliatna a neih leh | if the ministry of condemnation had glory/hih ~ thuak dingin | to suffer this judgment) (s:thukhenna) (r:66.18.10/47.3.9/65.1.4) (q:draft)
thutannate = (t:n) (w:justice/judgments) (d:thutanna judgment with the plural te) (e:thumanna le ~ ama tokhom bulpi ahi hi) (s:thutan'nate) (b:thutanna) (r:19.97.2) (q:draft)
thutawng = (t:n) (w:deep things/depths) (d:thu matter with tawng, the inmost part: the deepest part of a matter; thutawng dongtakin is right to the depths) (e:a ki-imcip a ~ dongtakin a kankhia hi) (r:46.2.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
thutawpna = (t:n) (w:end/final outcome/destiny/fate) (d:thu matter with tawpna end: how things end for someone) (e:a ~ uh a vekpi-in kibang lel hi/a ~ dongte ka tel hi | I understood their final end/Pasian a ngaihsun lote a ~ uh | the end of those who give no thought to God) (s:thumong/beina) (r:21.9.2/19.73.17/18.18.21) (q:draft)
thute = (t:n) (w:words/things/matters) (d:thu, word or matter, with the plural te: words, things, matters; hih thute is these words or these things) (e:Pasian in hih ~ khempeuh gen a/Ka lungsim sunga om ~ | the words that are in my heart/Hih ~ vaikhak in la, hilh in | command and teach these things/Hih ~-ah teci na hi uh hi | you are witnesses of these things) (s:thugente/kammalte) (b:thu) (r:2.20.1/42.24.48/18.33.2/54.4.11) (q:draft)
Thute = (t:n) (w:things/words) (d:thute, words or matters, capitalised for the message that was preached) (e:na zak uh ~ mah kamsangte in) (b:thute) (r:60.1.12) (q:draft)
thutelna = (t:n) (w:understanding/discernment/insight) (d:thu, matter, with tel, understand, and the noun suffix na: understanding, insight into matters) (e:ngaihsut pilna leh ~ nang tungah/na ~ in, nangmah hong hu-in | your understanding will guard you/ka lungsim’ ngaihsutna in ~ hi ding hi | the meditation of my heart will be understanding/~ nei-in, kei ka thahat hi | I have insight, I have strength) (s:theihtelna/thutheihna/pilna) (r:13.22.12/20.2.11/19.49.3/20.8.14) (q:draft)
thuteng = (t:n) (w:all the words/all the things/matters) (d:thu word or matter with teng all; hih thuteng is all this, all these things) (e:Hih ~ a genkhit ciangin/Hih ~ khempeuh kumpi Nebukhadnezzar’ tungah hong tung hi | all this happened to King Nebuchadnezzar/ka gen ding ~ a hong piak ahi hi | he has given me all that I am to say/a ~ a gen ciangin | when he told the whole matter) (b:thu) (r:44.19.41/27.4.28/43.12.49/9.4.13) (q:draft)
thuthak = (t:n) (w:news/new message/new thing) (d:thu, word or matter, with thak, new; thuthak hoih is good news) (e:~ hoih khat note a’ ding/Tu ni-in ~ a hoih i theih ni ahi hi | today is a day on which we know good news/hih ~ a ko dingin | to proclaim this news/Bang ~ hilh tuan ahi hiam | what new teaching is this) (s:thuzak/thupuak) (r:42.2.10/12.7.9/13.10.9/41.1.27) (q:draft)
Thuthak = (t:n) (w:news/tidings) (d:thuthak, news, capitalised in Lungdamna Thuthak, the Good News, the gospel) (e:hih Lungdamna ~ um un/Pasian kiang panin hong pai Lungdamna ~ gen a | proclaiming the Good News that comes from God/Abraham tungah Lungdamna ~ na ma hilhkhol a | announced the Good News to Abraham beforehand) (b:thuthak) (r:41.1.15/41.1.14/48.3.8) (q:draft)
thuthakte = (t:n) (w:new teachings/new things/news) (d:thuthak, new word or matter, with the plural te) (e:Tu-a na gengen ~ ka theinuam uh hi) (b:thuthak) (r:44.17.19) (q:draft)
thuthei = (t:adj) (w:knowledgeable/learned/understanding/prudent) (d:knowing or understanding matters, from thu and thei know; thuthei mi is a man of learning or insight, thuthei lopi-in is without knowledge) (e:no ~ mite aw/a pil, ~, thuphawksa mite teel unla | choose wise, understanding and experienced men/Jonathan pen ~ mi le laithei mi | Jonathan was a man of insight and a scribe/Note lakah pilin ~ a kisa a om leh | if anyone among you thinks himself wise and understanding) (s:pil/pilhuai) (a:hai) (b:thu) (r:18.34.2/13.27.32/5.1.13/59.3.13) (q:draft)
thutheih = (t:n) (w:knowledge) (d:thu matter with theih know; thutheih siamna is the gift of knowledge) (e:~ siamna a om hangin maimang ding hi/eite’ neih ~ siamnate | the gifts of knowledge that we have) (s:thutheihna) (b:thuthei) (r:46.13.8/46.13.9) (q:draft)
thutheihna = (t:n) (w:knowledge/understanding) (d:thu, matter, theih, know, with na: knowing and understanding of things) (e:thakhauhna sangin ~ hoihzaw hi/kham hoihpen sangin ~ deihzaw un | choose knowledge rather than the finest gold/Koi lai-ah ~ nak om ahi hiam | where does understanding dwell/siatna pelhna pen ~ hi | to shun evil is understanding) (s:theihna/thutelna/pilna/theihtelna) (b:thutheih) (r:20.24.5/18.28.12/20.8.10/18.28.28) (q:draft)
thutheihte = (t:n) (w:knowledge/things known/learning) (d:thu matter with theih know and the plural te: the things one knows) (e:amau’ ~ haina a suaksak pa/tu-in ka ~ na ngai in | now listen to what I know) (b:thutheih) (r:23.44.25/18.15.17) (q:draft)
thutheite = (t:n) (w:experts/those who know) (d:thuthei, knowing matters, with the plural te) (e:upadi le biakna lam ~ khempeuh) (s:siamte) (b:thuthei) (r:17.1.13) (q:draft)
thuthu = (t:see) <thuthu-in>
thuthu-in = (t:adv) (w:as one pleases/according to one's own will) (d:after a possessive: following only one's own mind, as in ama thuthu-in, as he pleases) (e:ama ~ a gamta ding hi/amau’ ~ a omzaw uh a | they chose rather to live as they pleased) (s:ututin/duhduhin) (r:27.11.3/24.7.24) (q:draft)
thuthuin = (t:adv) (w:of oneself/by nature) (d:another spelling of thuthu-in, by one’s own will; ama thuthuin is of himself, as he is, where the NIV has physically) (e:ama ~ Thukham a zuih leh) (r:45.2.27) (q:draft, low confidence)
thuthuk = (t:n) (w:mystery/secret/deep matter) (d:thu matter with thuk deep: something hidden or hard to understand) (e:~ khat kong gen ding hi/Pasian’ ~ thei khin zo ding na hi hiam | can you fully know the mysteries of God/Pasian’ ~ a kemte bangin | as those entrusted with the mysteries of God/~ mu theite bekin suak khia thei hi | only those who can see deep matters can draw it out) (s:thuthukpi/thuthukna/thusimteng) (r:46.15.51/49.1.9/18.11.7/46.4.1/20.20.5) (q:draft)
thuthukna = (t:n) (w:mystery/deep matter) (d:thuthuk, deep or hidden matter, with the noun suffix na) (e:tua ~ hilh dinginah lau loin) (s:thuthuk) (b:thuthuk) (r:49.6.19) (q:draft)
thuthukpi = (t:n) (w:mystery/deep mystery/profound matter) (d:thuthuk with pi, great: a great or deep mystery) (e:Hih thu in ~ ahi hi/tua ~ Daniel’ tungah kihilh a | the mystery was revealed to Daniel/~ a lakkhia Pasian in | God, who reveals mysteries/Hih ~ hong genthei na hih manin | because you were able to tell this mystery) (s:thuthuk/thuthukna) (b:thuthuk) (r:49.5.32/27.2.19/27.2.29/27.2.47) (q:draft)
thuthukpite = (t:n) (w:deep things/mysteries) (d:thuthukpi, deep mystery, with the plural te) (e:Amah in ~ le thusimte a lakkhia hi/~ gentel theihna a nei hi | he has the ability to explain mysteries) (s:thuthukte/thusimte) (b:thuthukpi) (r:27.2.22/27.5.12) (q:draft)
thuthukte = (t:n) (w:mysteries/deep things/hidden things) (d:thuthuk, deep or hidden matter, with the plural te) (e:khuamial sung panin ~ kalkhia a/taanglai-a ~ kong genkhia ding hi | I will utter hidden things from of old/Khazih’ ~ ka theih note in na thei ding uh hi | you will understand what I know of the mysteries of Christ) (s:thuthukpite/thusimte/kiseelte) (b:thuthuk) (r:18.12.22/49.3.5/19.78.2/49.3.4) (q:draft)
thuum = (t:v) (w:plead/beseech/beg) (d:ask earnestly, plead or beg, often with tungah, to or before someone; kong thuum hi is I beg you, please) (e:Topa tungah ka ~ hi/keimah in Topa tungah ka ~ a | I pleaded with the Lord/hawlkhiat loh nadingin nakpi-in a ~ uh hi | they begged him earnestly not to drive them out/Pasian aw, kong ~ hi | O God, I beg you) (s:thum/ngenngen) (r:19.142.1/44.25.3/5.3.23/41.5.10/4.12.13) (q:draft)
thuum = (t:v) (w:mourn/lament/wail) (d:mourn or wail for the dead or over bad news, often with hangin, because of) (e:nakpi-in mite ~ uh hi/a zak uh ciangin amaute ~ uh hi | when they heard it they mourned/Absalom’ hangin kumpipa kapin ~ hi | the king is weeping and mourning for Absalom/Zeisu hangin nakpi a ~ numei tampite | many women who mourned greatly for Jesus) (s:dah/mau) (a:kipak) (r:4.14.39/2.33.4/10.19.1/42.23.27) (q:draft)
thuumin = (t:v) (w:groan/mourn/wail) (d:thuum, mourn, with the linking ending in: groaning or lamenting, used before another verb as in thuumin tau and thuumin kap) (e:silh nadingin ~ ka om uh hi/Na sih kuan uh ciangin ~ na tau ding uh a | at the end of your life you will groan/na muan uh khuapi kisia ahih manin ~ kap un | wail, for the city you trusted is destroyed/nakpi-in a kap uh a, ~ a om uh hi | they were weeping loudly and mourning) (b:thuum) (r:47.5.2/23.23.14/20.5.11/42.8.52) (q:draft)
thuumna = (t:n) (w:supplication/plea/entreaty) (d:thuum, plead, with the noun suffix na: an earnest plea or supplication, often paired with thungetna, prayer) (e:Keima ~ in nangma kiang hong ban hen/na mi Israelte’ hong ~ ngai in | hear the supplication of your people Israel/amau’ ~ simmawh lo ding hi | he will not despise their plea/Ka ~ aw hong za ahih manin | because he has heard the sound of my plea) (s:thungetna/kutna) (b:thuum) (r:19.119.170/25.3.56/11.8.30/19.102.17/19.28.6) (q:draft)
thuumna = (t:n) (w:mourning/lamentation/wailing) (d:thuum, mourn, with the noun suffix na: mourning or lamentation for the dead or in distress) (e:~ leh kahna aw bek ka za ta hi/Moses hangin kahna leh ~ veng hi | the weeping and mourning for Moses came to an end/mi khempeuh adingin ~ suak hi | it turned into mourning for all the people/Izipt mite’ adingin a nasia ~ ahi hi | this is a grievous mourning for the Egyptians) (s:dahna/kahna/tamlawhna) (a:lungdamna/kipahna) (b:thuum) (r:18.30.31/5.34.8/10.19.2/1.50.11) (q:draft)
thuumnate = (t:n) (w:supplications/pleas/cries for mercy) (d:thuumna, plea, with the plural te; often paired with thungetna, prayer) (e:ka ~ hong ngai hi/amau’ thungetna leh ~ za in la | hear their prayer and their pleas/hih thungetna leh ~ khempeuh Topa tungah | all these prayers and supplications to the Lord/Israelte’ hong ~ nangmah in ngai in | hear the supplications of Israel) (s:thungetnate/ngetnate) (b:thuumna) (r:19.116.1/14.6.39/11.8.54/14.6.21) (q:draft)
thuumsak = (t:v) (w:plead for/intercede/petition for) (d:thuum, plead, with sak: plead or pray on behalf of another) (e:kei ading hong ~ leh ka ut hi/Mi khat in a lawmpa’ ading a ~ bangin | as a man pleads for his friend/ama adingin kua in va ~ ding ahi hiam | who will intercede for him/amau’ taangin ~ kei in | do not plead on their behalf) (s:ngetsak/thumsak/thungetsak) (b:thuum) (r:18.16.21/24.7.16/9.2.25/24.11.14) (q:draft)
thuumthuum = (t:v) (w:moan/coo) (d:repeated form: make a low moaning sound again and again, as a dove does) (e:vakhu bangin i ~ hi) (s:thumthum/tautau) (r:23.59.11) (q:draft)
thuvaante = (t:n) (w:officials/administrators) (d:another spelling of thuvante: holders of a court office, with the plural te) (e:thukhente, mangpite, ~, uliante) (s:thuvante) (r:15.4.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
thuvaihawm = (t:n) (w:council) (d:thu matter with vaihawm, plan or deliberate: the body that deliberates; ulian thuvaihawm is the council of the leaders) (e:ulian ~ sunga kihel hi a) (s:vaihawmte) (r:42.23.50) (q:draft)
thuvaihawmna = (t:n) (w:plan/counsel) (d:thuvaihawm, deliberate on matters, with the noun suffix na) (e:amau’ ~ a seelcip) (s:vaihawmna/geelna) (b:thuvaihawm) (r:23.29.15) (q:draft)
thuvan = (t:n) (w:official/officer/secretary) (d:a court office; thuvan pa and thuvan pipa stand where the NIV has staff officer and secretary) (e:Zedekiah kumpipa’ ~ pa ahi hi/Shafan’ tapa ~ pipa Gemariah’ inndei sungah | in the room of the secretary Gemariah son of Shaphan) (s:thuvanpa) (r:24.51.59/24.36.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
thuvanpa = (t:n) (w:staff officer/officer/official) (d:thuvan, a court office, with pa marking a man: an officer in the service of the king) (e:Zedekiah kumpipa’ ~ ahi hi) (b:thuvan) (r:24.51.59) (q:draft, low confidence)
thuvanpi = (t:n) (w:secretary/scribe) (d:official who keeps the writings of the king; followed by pa for a man) (e:~ pa Elishama’ inndei sungah/kumpi ~ pa Jonathan’ inn-ah | in the house of Jonathan the royal secretary/Shafan’ tapa ~ pa Gemariah’ inndei sungah | in the room of the secretary Gemariah son of Shaphan/~ pa’ inndei sungah paisuk a | he went down to the room of the secretary) (r:24.36.20/24.37.15/24.36.10/24.36.12) (q:draft)
thuvanpipa = (t:n) (w:scribe/secretary) (d:an official who writes and keeps records for the king; pa marks a man) (e:~ Elishama’ inndei sungah tua laizial/kumpi ~ Baruk leh kamsangpa Jeremiah man dingin | to arrest Baruch the scribe and Jeremiah the prophet/Neriah’ tapa ~ Baruk a pia hi | he gave it to the scribe Baruch son of Neriah/kumpi ~ Jonathan’ innah | in the house of Jonathan the royal secretary) (b:thuvanpi) (r:24.36.20/24.36.26/24.36.32/24.37.15) (q:draft)
thuvante = (t:n) (w:officials/administrators) (d:thuvan, a court office, with the plural te) (e:thukhente, mangpite, ~, uliante) (b:thuvan) (r:15.4.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
thuvum = (t:n) (w:hump) (d:the hump on the back of a camel) (e:amau sumte kalaoh ~ tungah suanin) (r:23.30.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
thuzak = (t:n) (w:news/report/what is heard) (d:thu, word, with zak, hear: what one hears, a message, report or news) (e:Mihaite in a ~ peuh um pahpah a/gamlapi-a om lawmte’ kiang panin ~ nuam | good news from friends in a distant land/a ~ uh amaute a dingin a phattuamna om lo | the message they heard was of no value to them) (s:thupuak) (r:20.14.15/58.4.2/20.25.25) (q:draft)
thuzaksakna = (t:n) (w:proclamation/announcement/report) (d:thu, word, with zaksak, cause to hear, and na: the making known of something) (e:Minamte tungah hih bangin ~ bawl in/Judah leh Jerusalem sung khempeuh ah ~ kibawl hi | a proclamation was made throughout Judah and Jerusalem/~ lai hih bangin a gelh uh hi | they wrote the report as follows) (s:zaksakna/taangkona) (r:29.3.9/15.5.7/14.24.9) (q:draft)
thuzang = (t:n) (w:trivial matter/light thing) (d:thu, matter, with zang, light: a small thing of little weight, here of sin that is treated as trivial) (e:a ~ tawh a kibat mah bangin) (r:11.16.31) (q:draft, low confidence)
thuzawh = (t:v) (w:overrule/prevail over/win over/gain control over) (d:get the better of someone by words, whether by command or by persuasion) (e:kumpipa in Joab ~ hi/tua biakna a nusia mite a ~ theih nadingin | so that he may win over those who have forsaken the covenant/numeite na ~ uh hi | they gain control over women) (s:zolzawh) (r:13.21.4/27.11.32/55.3.6) (q:draft)
thuzia = (t:n) (w:way/manner/nature) (d:thu matter with zia manner: how a thing is or works) (e:tua khuavak ~ a thei lo) (r:18.24.13) (q:draft)
thuzol = (t:n) (w:smooth words/flattery/pleasant things) (d:thu word with zol coax: words that please but are not true) (e:~ bek hong gen unla) (s:kamzol/mawkphatna) (r:23.30.10) (q:draft)
thuzuau = (t:n) (w:lie/falsehood/false word) (d:untrue speech; thuzuau gen means tell a lie, thuzuau teci is false witness) (e:~ teci a zong uh hi/Pasian’ thuman thutak pen ~ tawh a kheek uh | they exchanged the truth of God for a lie/~ a gen teci in mi lehhek hi | a witness who tells lies deceives/~ genna tomno sung bek kimang hi | lying speech lasts only a moment) (s:zuauthu) (a:thutak) (r:40.26.59/20.12.19/45.1.25/20.14.25) (q:draft)
Thuzuau = (t:n) (w:lie/falsehood) (d:thuzuau, lie, at the start of a clause; thuzuau gen is tell a lie) (e:~ a gen ngei lo Pasian/~ teci pangte tampi hong pai uh hangin | though many false witnesses came forward) (b:thuzuau) (r:56.1.1/40.26.60) (q:draft)
thuzuaupa = (t:n) (w:liar) (d:thuzuau lie with pa marking a man) (e:zuauthu gen leh ~ lah ahi hi) (s:zuaugen/Mizuau) (b:thuzuau) (r:43.8.44) (q:draft)
Thuzuaute = (t:n) (w:lies/deceit) (d:Thuzuau, lie, with the plural te) (e:~ leh kheemna pawl khempeuh tawh a dim) (s:zuauthute) (b:Thuzuau) (r:44.13.10) (q:draft)
thuzui = (t:n) (w:disciple/follower) (d:thu word with zui follow: one who follows the teaching) (e:Vantung Gam ~ a suak laithei khempeuh) (s:nungzui) (r:40.13.52) (q:draft)
Tiberias = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Tiberias) (d:city on the western shore of the Sea of Galilee, after which the lake is also called the Sea of Tiberias) (r:43.6.23/43.6.1)
Tiberius = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Tiberius) (d:Roman emperor, Tiberius Caesar, in the fifteenth year of whose reign John the Baptist began to preach) (r:42.3.1)
Tibhath = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Tebah) (d:town of Hadadezer king of Zobah, from which David took a great quantity of bronze) (r:13.18.8)
Tibni = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Tibni) (d:son of Ginath, who was the rival of Omri for the throne of Israel) (r:11.16.22/11.16.21)
Tidal = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Tidal) (d:king of Goyim, one of the four kings allied with Kedorlaomer in the time of Abram) (r:1.14.1)
Tidalte = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Tidal) (d:Tidal, king of Goyim, written with the ending te that closes a list of names) (b:Tidal) (r:1.14.1)
Tifsah = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Tiphsah) (d:town on the Euphrates that marked the far limit of the rule of Solomon) (r:11.4.24)
Tiglath = (t:see) <Tiglath-pileser>
Tiglath-pileser = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Tiglath-Pileser) (d:king of Assyria who took Gilead and Galilee from Israel in the time of Pekah and to whom Ahaz of Judah turned for help) (e:Assiria kumpipa ~ hong pai-in) (r:12.15.29/12.16.7) (q:draft)
Tiglathpileser = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Tiglath-Pileser) (d:king of Assyria who carried people of Israel into exile and to whom Ahaz of Judah turned for help) (r:14.28.20/13.5.6)
Tigris = (t:name) (c:river) (w:Tigris) (d:great river of Mesopotamia, the third river of Eden, beside which Daniel saw a vision) (r:27.10.4/1.2.14)
Tikhikas = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Tychicus) (d:companion of Paul from the province of Asia, who carried his letters to the Ephesians and the Colossians) (r:51.4.7/55.4.12)
Tikoa = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Tekoa) (d:town in Judah south of Bethlehem, home of the prophet Amos) (r:24.6.1)
Tikvah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Tikvah) (d:father of Shallum the husband of the prophet Huldah; also the father of Jahzeiah in the time of Ezra) (r:12.22.14/15.10.15)
Tilgath = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Tiglath) (d:first part of Tilgath-pilneser, the spelling of the name of Tiglath-Pileser king of Assyria used in Chronicles) (r:13.5.6/14.28.20)
Tilgath-pilneser = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Tiglath-Pileser) (d:king of Assyria, the spelling of Tiglath-pileser used in Chronicles) (e:Assiria kumpipa ~ hong kuan hi) (r:14.28.20/13.5.6) (q:draft)
Tilon = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Tilon) (d:son of Shimon in the genealogy of the tribe of Judah) (r:13.4.20)
Timeus = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Timaeus) (d:father of the blind beggar Bartimaeus of Jericho) (r:41.10.46)
Timias = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Timaeus) (d:father of the blind beggar Bartimaeus of Jericho) (r:41.10.46)
Timna = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Timna) (d:sister of Lotan the Horite and concubine of Eliphaz son of Esau, mother of Amalek; also the name of a chief of Edom) (r:1.36.22)
Timnah = (t:name) (c:land/city) (w:Timnah) (d:name of two towns: one in the hill country of Judah, and one on the border of Judah and Dan where Samson sought a Philistine wife) (r:1.38.12/6.15.57)
Timnathheres = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Timnath Heres) (d:town in the hill country of Ephraim where Joshua was buried, also called Timnath Serah) (r:7.2.9)
Timnathserah = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Timnath Serah) (d:town in the hill country of Ephraim that was given to Joshua, where he lived and was buried) (r:6.19.50/6.24.30)
Timon = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Timon) (d:one of the seven men chosen in the church at Jerusalem to serve at the daily distribution of food) (r:44.6.5)
Timoti = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Timothy) (d:fellow worker of Paul from Lystra, to whom two letters of the New Testament are addressed) (r:57.1.1/44.16.1)
Tirannas = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Tyrannus) (d:man of Ephesus in whose lecture hall Paul taught daily) (r:44.19.9)
Tiras = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Tiras) (d:son of Japheth and grandson of Noah) (r:1.10.2)
Tirath = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Tirathite) (d:the Tirathites, a clan of scribes who lived at Jabez, counted among the Kenites) (r:13.2.55)
Tirhakah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Tirhakah) (d:king of Cush who marched out against Sennacherib of Assyria in the days of Hezekiah) (r:12.19.9/23.37.9)
Tirhanah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Tirhanah) (d:son of Caleb by his concubine Maakah) (r:13.2.48)
Tiria = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Tiria) (d:son of Jehallelel in the genealogy of the tribe of Judah) (r:13.4.16)
Tirzah = (t:name) (c:land/city) (w:Tirzah) (d:city that was the capital of the northern kingdom of Israel from Jeroboam to Omri; also the name of a daughter of Zelophehad) (r:11.15.21/11.16.6)
Tishbe = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Tishbe) (d:town in Gilead, the home of the prophet Elijah) (r:11.17.1)
Titu = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Titus) (d:Greek fellow worker of Paul, sent by him to Corinth, to whom the letter to Titus is addressed) (e:~ tawh kong sawl khawm uh hi) (r:47.8.18/48.2.3) (q:draft)
Titus = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Titus) (d:Greek fellow worker of Paul, sent by him to Corinth, to whom the letter to Titus is addressed) (r:48.2.3/47.7.6)
Tiz = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Tiz) (d:home of Joha the Tizite, one of the mighty warriors of David; the place is not otherwise known) (r:13.11.45)
to = (t:part) (w:up/upward) (d:placed after a verb to show upward movement, as in en to, look up, la to, take up, and leeng to, fly up) (e:Vantung en ~ dih in/tuipi panin tuite la ~ a | he draws up the water from the sea/hih kherubte leeng ~ uh a | these cherubim rose upward/leihawm thukpi taw panin ka hong kiko ~ hi | I called up to you from the depths of the pit) (a:suk) (r:18.35.5/25.3.55/18.36.27/26.10.15) (q:draft)
to = (t:v) (w:dig) (d:dig a hole, pit or well) (e:Amah in gum ~-in/tua kuam sung ~-in tuikhuk a muh uh | they dug in the valley and found a well/tuikhuk dang khat ~ uh a | they dug another well/keimah siahna in gum ~ uh hi | they dig pits to trap me) (r:19.7.15/1.26.19/1.26.21/19.119.85) (q:draft)
to = (t:n) (w:lord/master) (d:lord or master, a person who has authority over others; ka to kumpipa is my lord the king) (e:Ka ~ kumpipa in gen hen | let my lord the king speak/Hihte in ~ nei lo hi | these people have no master/ka ~ kumpipa kiangah hih thu gen dingin | to say this to my lord the king) (s:topa) (a:sila) (r:10.14.18/14.18.16/10.14.15) (q:draft)
To = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Tou) (d:first part of the name of the king of Hamath who sent gifts to David after the defeat of Hadadezer, written To-i in 2 Samuel and To-u in 1 Chronicles) (e:Hamath kumpipa ~-i in Hadadezer’ galkap) (r:10.8.9/13.18.9) (q:draft)
Toah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Toah) (d:Levite of the clan of Kohath, an ancestor of Samuel and of the singer Heman) (e:a pa Eliel, a pa ~) (r:13.6.34) (q:draft)
Tob = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Tob) (d:region east of the Jordan where Jephthah lived after he fled from his brothers) (r:7.11.3/7.11.5)
Tobadonijah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Tob-Adonijah) (d:Levite sent by King Jehoshaphat to teach in the towns of Judah) (r:14.17.8)
Tobiah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Tobiah) (d:Ammonite official who with Sanballat opposed Nehemiah and the rebuilding of the wall of Jerusalem; also the head of a family of returned exiles) (r:16.6.18/16.2.10)
Tobijah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Tobijah) (d:name of two men: a Levite sent by Jehoshaphat to teach in Judah, and an exile who came back from Babylon in the time of Zechariah) (r:14.17.8/38.6.10)
Tofel = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Tophel) (d:place in the wilderness east of the Jordan, named with Paran where Moses spoke to Israel) (r:5.1.1)
Tofeth = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Topheth) (d:place in the Valley of Ben Hinnom outside Jerusalem where children were burned as sacrifices to Molek) (r:12.23.10/24.19.14)
togarmah = (t:see) <Beth-togarmah>
Togarmah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Togarmah) (d:son of Gomer and grandson of Japheth, ancestor of a people of the far north) (r:1.10.3)
toh = (t:part) (w:up/upward) (d:placed after a verb for upward movement; a spelling of to used before a following word such as ni, ciangin or ding) (e:meikhu lianpi a suahsak ~ uh ciangin/meii a kilakkhiat ~ peuhpeuh ciangin | whenever the cloud lifted/Izipt panin ka paikhiatpih ~ ni-a kipan | from the day I brought them up out of Egypt/meii a kilak ~ khit ciangin | after the cloud had lifted) (b:to) (r:7.20.38/2.40.36/10.7.6/4.9.17) (q:draft)
tohkik = (t:adv) (w:back up) (d:toh up with kik back, placed after a verb: bring up again, here the hand from the dish to the mouth) (e:an a bah ~ ding nangawn) (b:toh) (r:20.19.24) (q:draft, low confidence)
tohna = (t:part) (d:toh up or upward with na, which makes a noun; placed after a verb it names the going up or rising that the verb tells of, or the place gone up to: kah tohna a climbing up, sap tohna a calling up, khan’tohna growth or progress, san’tohna a being raised high) (e:na kah ~ mual tungah si in/haksapi-a hauh ~ in khang semsem hi | wealth gathered with hard work keeps growing/khuapi meikhu a kah ~ | the smoke of the city going up/keimah sap ~ tawh hong nawngkaisak na hi hiam | have you disturbed me by calling me up) (b:toh) (r:5.32.50/54.4.15/20.13.11/6.8.21/9.28.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
tohsak = (t:part) (d:toh up with sak, cause or do for another, placed after a verb: sap tohsak is call up, bring up for someone) (e:kei adingin hong sap ~ in) (b:toh) (r:9.28.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
tohtoh = (t:part) (d:placed after a verb for an action that goes on and on: a gen tohtoh ciangin is as he went on speaking) (e:Thukhenna Hunte a gen ~ ciangin) (r:44.24.25) (q:draft, low confidence)
Tohu = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Tohu) (d:son of Zuph of Ephraim, an ancestor of Elkanah the father of Samuel) (r:9.1.1)
Toi = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Tou) (d:king of Hamath who sent his son with gifts to David after the defeat of Hadadezer) (r:10.8.9)
toin = (t:part) (w:up/upward) (d:the particle to with the linking ending in; after a verb, doing it upward and then the next action follows) (e:Moses in a khut laam ~ a ciangkhut tawh/Humpinelkaipi bangin tho ~ | rising up like a lioness/dom ~ ka biang ciangah ka tawi a | I lifted them up and held them to my cheek/leitung khempeuh khang ~ kiamsuk ding hi | the whole land will rise and then sink) (a:sukin) (b:to) (r:4.20.11/28.11.4/4.23.24/30.8.8) (q:draft)
tok = (t:v) (w:stir up/churn/trouble) (d:stir water so that it becomes rough or muddy) (e:tuipi ~ gawpin tuihualte a hawksak/gun sung ~ gawpin gun a ninsak | churning the streams and making them muddy) (r:23.51.15/26.32.2) (q:draft)
tok = (t:v) (w:be missing/fall out) (d:said of a tooth that is gone and leaves a gap) (e:Na ha khat zong ~ lo a/A ~ khat zong om lo a | not one of them is missing) (r:22.4.2/22.6.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
tokgawpin = (t:v) (w:stirring up/churning up) (d:tok stir with gawp violently and the linking suffix in: stirring water until it is rough or muddy) (e:kei pen tuipi ~ tuihualte a hawksak/nang pen gunsung ~ a ninsak | you churn up the streams and make them muddy) (r:23.51.15/26.32.2) (q:draft)
Tokhath = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Tokhath) (d:father of Shallum the husband of the prophet Huldah, called Tikvah in 2 Kings) (r:14.34.22)
Tokhen = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Token) (d:village of the tribe of Simeon) (r:13.4.32)
tokhia = (t:v) (w:dig out/dig up/quarry/mine) (d:to dig with khia out: take stone or metal out of the ground) (e:lei sung panin sik ~ a/a manpha suangtumte suangkhuk panin ~ uh hi | they cut costly blocks of stone out of the quarry/khuamial thuk tawng sung pan suang ~ uh hi | they dig stone out of the deepest darkness/mualte’ bul lei sung panin ~ uh hi | they dig it out of the ground at the roots of the mountains) (b:to) (r:18.28.2/11.5.17/18.28.3/18.28.9) (q:draft)
tokhiate = (t:n) (w:those who quarry/those who dig out) (d:tokhia dig out with the plural te) (e:Suang a ~ suang mah in liamsak ding a) (b:tokhia) (r:21.10.9) (q:draft)
tokhom = (t:n) (w:throne/seat) (d:seat of a king or person of rank, as in kumpi tokhom royal throne; hehpihna tokhom is the atonement cover of the ark) (e:Solomon in kumpi ~ tungah tu hi/a ~ siangtho tungah Pasian tu hi | God is seated on his holy throne/Moses’ ~ tungah a tu uh hi | they sit in the seat of Moses/Topa in ama ~ vantungah phut khin a | the Lord has established his throne in heaven) (s:kumpitokhom/tutna) (r:11.1.46/2.39.35/19.47.8/40.23.2/19.103.19) (q:draft)
Tokhom = (t:n) (w:throne) (d:tokhom, throne, capitalised for the throne of God and in Kumpi Tokhom Innpi, the Throne Hall of Solomon) (e:~ laizangah a om Tuuno/~ tungah a tu eite Pasian | our God who sits on the throne/Kumpi ~ Innpi a kici khat lam a | he built what is called the Throne Hall) (b:tokhom) (r:66.7.17/11.7.7/66.7.10) (q:draft)
tokhomah = (t:n) (w:on the throne/to the throne) (d:tokhom throne with the place marker ah) (e:Israel kumpi ~ kong tu a/ka Pa’ ~ ka tutkhawm uh mah bangin | just as I sat down with my Father on his throne) (b:tokhom) (r:14.6.10/66.3.21) (q:draft)
tokhomkip = (t:phrase) (w:throne be established) (d:tokhom throne and kip, firm or established, written as one word in this verse) (e:ama kumpi ~ paisuak ding hi) (r:13.17.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
tokhomte = (t:n) (w:thrones/seats) (d:tokhom, throne, with the plural te; kumpi tokhomte are royal thrones) (e:Tua lai takin kumpi ~ ka mu hi/Na kumpi ~ tung panin hong tuaksuk un | come down from your thrones/kumpi ~ a hong kikoih hi | thrones were set in place) (s:tutnate) (b:tokhom) (r:66.20.4/66.4.4/24.13.18/27.7.9) (q:draft)
tokin = (t:v) (w:stirring/churning) (d:tok stir with the linking suffix in) (e:Amah in tuipi ~ beel sunga tuiso) (b:tok) (r:18.41.31) (q:draft)
toklo = (t:v) (w:stir up/incite/arouse) (d:stir people up against someone; lo here does not seem to be the negative) (e:a heh nadingin ~ hi) (b:tok) (r:14.21.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
toknawi = (t:see) <toknawi-in>
toknawi-in = (t:v) (w:troubling/throwing into confusion) (d:tok stir up with nawi, and the linking ending in: stir up and unsettle the mind) (e:note’ lungsim hong ~) (s:buaisakin) (r:48.1.7) (q:draft)
toksuah = (t:v) (w:incite/stir up) (d:tok stir with suah, bring out: move someone to act against another) (e:nang hong ~ pa pen Topa ahihleh) (s:hansuah/hanthawn) (r:9.26.19) (q:draft)
toksuahpa = (t:n) (w:one who incites/inciter) (d:toksuah incite with pa marking a man) (e:nang hong ~ in Topa ahih leh) (b:toksuah) (r:9.26.19) (q:draft)
toktok = (t:v) (w:churn/keep stirring) (d:repeated form of tok, stir: stir again and again, as milk to make butter) (e:Bawngnawi ~ lehang thawhbat hong suak a) (r:20.30.33) (q:draft)
toktol = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:slug/snail) (d:a soft creature that leaves slime as it moves) (e:a naai a bei ~) (r:19.58.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
tol = (t:adj) (w:bald/bare) (d:of the head, without hair, whether from loss of hair or from shaving; met tol, shave bare) (e:a lu a ~ hangin amah a siang/a lu ~ tung hita leh | whether it is on his bald head/a lu uh met ~ uh a | they shave their heads bare) (s:kolh/lukolh) (r:3.13.40/24.48.37/3.13.42) (q:draft)
Tola = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Tola) (d:eldest son of Issachar and ancestor of the Tolaite clan; also a judge of Israel, the son of Puah) (r:1.46.13/13.7.1)
Tolad = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Tolad) (d:town of the tribe of Simeon in the south of Judah, also called Eltolad) (e:Bilhah, Ezem, ~) (r:13.4.29) (q:draft)
Tolef = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Tophel) (d:spelling of Tofel, a place in the wilderness east of the Jordan named with Paran where Moses spoke to Israel) (r:5.1.1)
Tolemais = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Ptolemais) (d:seaport on the coast north of Mount Carmel, the Old Testament Akko, where Paul stayed one day) (r:44.21.7)
Tolemias = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Ptolemais) (d:seaport on the coast north of Mount Carmel, the Old Testament Akko, where Paul stayed one day) (r:44.21.7)
tolen = (t:v) (w:fly upward/fly up) (d:to, up, with len, fly: fly upward, as sparks from a fire) (e:mei-ek a ~’ ngei mah bangin) (s:leengto/lengto) (a:leengsuk/lengsuk) (r:18.5.7) (q:draft)
tolh = (t:v) (w:miscarry) (d:lose the young before the time of birth, said of animals and of a woman; mostly with ta, young, written ta tolh or ta-tolh) (e:ta ~ cih zong om lo hi/a ~ om kei ta hen | let there be none that miscarry/na tuupi leh na keelpite ta-~ nai lo a | your ewes and she-goats have not miscarried/numei naupaii khat liamsak a, ta-~-in | they hurt a pregnant woman and she miscarries) (s:tatolh/nausia) (r:18.21.10/1.31.38/19.144.14/2.21.22) (q:draft)
tolh = (t:v) (w:slip out/come out) (d:slip or come out of its place, said of the bowels; followed by khia, out) (e:a gil ~ khia a) (r:14.21.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
tolhkhia = (t:v) (w:slip off/drop off/come out) (d:tolh slip out with khia out: of bonds falling from the hands, of bowels coming out of the body) (e:a kikhihnate a khut panin ~ hi/a natna hangin a gil ~ a | because of his disease his bowels came out) (b:tolh) (r:7.15.14/14.21.19) (q:draft)
tolhkhiat = (t:v) (w:come out/slip out) (d:form of tolhkhia used before dongin and other following words; of bowels coming out of the body) (e:na gil a ~ dongin) (b:tolhkhia) (r:14.21.15) (q:draft)
tolsak = (t:v) (w:make bald/shave bald) (d:tol, bald, with the causative sak: shave the head bare as a sign of mourning) (e:na lu uh ~ un) (s:kolhsak/mettol) (b:tol) (r:33.1.16) (q:draft)
tom = (t:adj) (w:short) (d:short in length, distance or time: lampi tom is a short road and hun tom a short time) (e:Topa a ban ~ lo a/a hun a ~ ahih ciangin | because the time is short/Mihingte a nuntak hun ~ a | the life of mortals is short/lampi ~ pen hita se leh | though that road was the shortest) (a:sau/sawt) (r:23.59.1/24.25.23/46.7.29/18.14.1/2.13.17) (q:draft)
tom = (t:v) (w:gather/pick up/collect) (d:gather firewood or sticks, as in sing tom; of a bird, bu tom is build a nest) (e:sabbath ni-in sing a ~ mi khat/meigongnu khat in sing na ~ hi | a widow was gathering sticks/singkang nih khawng a ~ ka hi a | I am gathering a couple of sticks/Sing a ~ laitak a mu mite in | those who found him gathering wood/mual tungah bu a ~ nading | that it should build its nest on the height) (s:tawm) (r:4.15.32/11.17.10/11.17.12/4.15.33/18.39.27) (q:draft)
tomin = (t:adv) (w:briefly/in short) (d:tom, short, with the ending in: a tomin is in short, in few words; also being short, said of time) (e:hih lai a ~ ka gelh khit ciangin/keimah in a ~ gelhin hong zasak | I have written to you briefly/ka hong gennop thu a ~ | what I want to say to you, in short/ka nuntak hun ~ siatna bek om a | my years have been few and full of trouble) (b:tom) (r:60.5.12/58.13.22/46.14.26/1.47.9) (q:draft)
tomin = (t:v) (w:gathering/building) (d:tom, gather, with the linking ending in: sing tomin is gathering wood and bu tomin is building a nest) (e:munah keising in bu ~/Naupangte in sing ~ | the children gather wood/amau a’ ding ciat selkeu ~ Abimelek zui-in | each gathered dry branches for himself and followed Abimelek) (b:tom) (r:23.34.15/24.7.18/7.9.49) (q:draft)
tomkha = (t:n) (w:short while/little while/moment) (d:a short time, usually as tomkha sung, for a little while; also a short distance, as in tomkha pai, go a little farther) (e:a kiang panin ~ sung a paikhia hi/Migilopa ~ sung a liat hangin | though the wicked man is great for a little while/amah ~ sung a khahkhia ding hi | he will be set free for a short time/Zeisu mai lamah ~ pai-in | Jesus went a little farther) (s:tawmvei/Tomnokhat) (a:hunsau) (r:42.4.13/41.14.35/18.24.24/66.20.3) (q:draft)
tomkhano = (t:n) (w:brief moment/very short while) (d:tomkha, short while, with the diminutive no: a very short moment, used with sung, within) (e:a siangtho nate ~ sung bek nangawn) (s:Tomnokhat) (b:tomkha) (r:4.4.20) (q:draft)
tomlam = (t:n) (w:shortness/brevity) (d:tom, short, with lam: how short something is, said of the length of life) (e:a nuntak ~ phawkin nei kha lo/ka nuntak hun uh a ~ ka theih nadingun | so that we may know how short our life is) (s:tomna) (r:21.5.20/19.90.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
tomluate = (t:n) (w:those that are too short/stunted ones) (d:tom short with lua, too much, and the plural te; of an animal with a limb too short) (e:a saulua ahih kei leh a ~ pen) (r:3.22.23) (q:draft)
tommet = (t:v) (w:cut short/crop) (d:tom short with met, shave or clip: a sam uh a tommet is those who clip their hair short; the NIV text has who are in distant places) (e:a sam uh a ~ khempeuhte) (s:mettom) (r:24.25.23) (q:draft, low confidence)
tomna = (t:n) (w:shortness/brevity) (d:tom short with the noun suffix na: the fact of being short in time) (e:migilote’ nopsak hun a ~ thu/Pasian a thudon lote’ lungdam hun a ~ thu | that the joy of the godless is brief) (s:tomlam) (b:tom) (r:18.20.5) (q:draft)
tomna = (t:n) (w:nest building) (d:tom gather, in bu tom build a nest, with the noun suffix na; bu a tomna ding is that it should build its nest) (e:mualtungah bu a ~ ding) (b:tom) (r:18.39.27) (q:draft)
tomno = (t:adj) (w:brief/short/momentary/few) (d:very short, mostly of time: tomno sung is a moment, a short while, tomno sungin is in a moment, soon, and ni tomno is a few days) (e:Ama hehna ~ sung bek hi a/thuzuau genna ~ sung bek kimang hi | a lying tongue lasts only a moment/Pasian in ~ sungin hong tungsak ding hi | God will soon bring it about/Ni ~ khit ciangin | after a few days) (a:sawt) (b:tom) (r:19.30.5/19.73.19/20.12.19/1.41.32/41.2.1) (q:draft)
Tomnokhat = (t:n) (w:moment/short time) (d:a very short time; Tomnokhat sungin is in a moment) (e:~ sungin minam khat piangkhia ngei) (s:tomkha/tomkhano) (r:23.66.8) (q:draft)
tomsak = (t:v) (w:shorten/cut short) (d:tom, short, with the causative sak: make shorter, cut short, said of days or of a time of life) (e:Topa in tua nite a ~ kei leh/a teelsate adingin a ~ ding hi | for the sake of his chosen ones he will shorten them/ama tangval a thahat hun na ~ a | you have cut short the time of his youthful strength) (s:khiapsak) (a:sausak) (b:tom) (r:41.13.20/19.89.45) (q:draft)
tomsakin = (t:v) (w:gathering for) (d:tom gather firewood with sak, do for someone, and the linking ending in: gathering wood for another) (e:na sing uh hong ~ na tui uh) (b:tom) (r:5.29.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
tomtheihna = (t:n) (w:being able to nest/place to nest) (d:tom, build a nest, with theih, be able, and the noun suffix na: bu a tomtheihna is that birds are able to nest, said of the branches of a tree) (e:a hiang tungah bu a ~ zah ding) (r:40.13.32) (q:draft, low confidence)
ton = (t:v) (w:accompany/be with/go together with) (d:be in the company of someone, come or go along with; tawh, with, marks the companion) (e:tangvalpa kei tawh hong ~ kei leh/Na sanggampa uh tawh nong ~ kei uh leh | unless you come with your brother/a lawmte tawh naupang ~ hi ci-in | thinking the boy was with his friends/Tua huihpi tawh a hong ~ meiipi | the great cloud that came with that windstorm) (s:kithuah/ompih/tonkhawm) (r:1.44.34/42.2.44/1.43.3/26.1.4) (q:draft)
tonbucip = (t:see) <tonbucip-a>
tonbucip-a = (t:adv) (w:cringing/crouching/bowed down) (d:tonbucip, crouch down small, with a linking it to the verb om, be) (e:Thongkiate’ lakah ~ om ding leh) (r:23.10.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
tonbucipin = (t:adv) (w:cringing/crouching/bowed down) (d:tonbucip, crouch down small, with the linking ending in) (e:Thongkiate’ lakah ~ om ding le) (r:23.10.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
toncip = (t:v) (w:stick to/cling to/cleave) (d:hold fast against something, as the tongue sticking to the roof of the mouth or people pressing themselves against a rock) (e:ka leii zong ~ hi/ka dang tawngah ka leii ~ ta hen | may my tongue cling to the roof of my mouth/suangpi pang peuh belin ~ uh hi | they cling to the side of the rocks) (r:19.22.15/18.24.8/19.137.6) (q:draft)
tong = (t:n) (w:cubit) (d:unit of length, from the elbow to the tip of the fingers; the number follows, as in tong sawmnga, fifty cubits) (e:inn sung in ~ sawmli sau hi/nisuahna lam adingin ~ sawmnga ahi hi | on the east side it was fifty cubits/inndung ~ za khat hi a | the building was a hundred cubits long/a kawm sahna ~ nga pha a | the wall was five cubits thick) (r:11.6.17/2.38.13/26.42.2/26.41.9) (q:draft)
tongguk = (t:n) (w:six cubits) (d:tong cubit with guk six, written as one word) (e:a vai lam ~ a gol) (r:27.3.1) (q:draft)
tongkua = (t:n) (w:nine cubits) (d:tong cubit with kua nine, written as one word) (e:a sauna ~ hi a) (r:5.3.11) (q:draft)
tongli = (t:n) (w:four cubits) (d:tong cubit with li four, written as one word) (e:a zaina ~ ahi hi) (r:5.3.11) (q:draft)
tongte = (t:see) <le-tongte>
tonin = (t:v) (w:folded/creased) (d:ton, draw together in folds, with the linking ending in; said of cloth) (e:puan a ~ a kikoih tawh) (r:18.38.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
tonkhawm = (t:v) (w:go together/accompany/come along with/travel together) (d:ton, go in company, with khawm, together: travel or walk along with someone; tawh, with, marks the companion) (e:keimah tawh a ~ Titu in/lampi-ah ~ ahi hiam | do they walk the road together/Saul tawh a ~ mite in | the men who were travelling with Saul/kote tawh hong ~ dingin pawlpite in teelin | chosen by the churches to travel with us) (s:kithuah/ton) (b:ton) (r:48.2.3/30.3.3/44.9.7/47.8.19) (q:draft)
tonkhawmte = (t:n) (w:companions) (d:tonkhawm, go together, with the plural te: those who travel along with someone) (e:Keimah tawh a ~ in khuavak) (s:tonpihte/lawmte) (b:tonkhawm) (r:44.22.9) (q:draft)
tonna = (t:n) (w:wrinkle) (d:ton, draw together in folds, with the noun suffix na; sa tonna is a wrinkle of the skin) (e:sa ~ om loin) (r:49.5.27) (q:draft)
tonpih = (t:v) (w:take along/accompany/go with) (d:have someone with oneself on a journey, take along; the person taken is the object) (e:Paul in amah a ~ nuam hi/siampi upa pawlkhat ~ in la | take along some of the senior priests/Titus zong ka ~ hi | I took Titus along too/Peter le Zebedi tapa tegel ~ a | he took Peter and the two sons of Zebedee with him) (r:44.16.3/46.9.5/24.19.1/48.2.1/40.26.37) (q:draft)
tonpihin = (t:v) (w:taking along/accompanied by) (d:tonpih, take along, with the linking ending in) (e:a min thak Johan ~) (b:tonpih) (r:44.12.25) (q:draft)
tonpihpa = (t:n) (w:companion) (d:tonpih, go with, with pa marking a man: the man who is with someone) (e:Zeisu a ~ khat in a khut zan a) (s:lawmpa/kikhawlpa) (b:tonpih) (r:40.26.51) (q:draft)
tonpihte = (t:n) (w:companions/those who go with) (d:tonpih go with, with plural te: the people who are with one on the way) (e:ka ~ in khut tawh hong kai-in/na ~’ muhin na beel sukham in la | break the jar in the sight of those who go with you) (s:tonkhawmte/lawmte) (b:tonpih) (r:44.22.11/24.19.10) (q:draft)
tonsak = (t:v) (w:send along with/cause to accompany) (d:ton, accompany, with the causative sak: send someone along with others) (e:tawh zong ka hong ~ uh hi) (s:kithuahsak/zuisak) (b:ton) (r:47.8.22) (q:draft)
tonsak = (t:v) (w:draw back/bring back) (d:ton, draw in, with the causative sak; with kik, back, it is draw a stretched-out hand back to the body) (e:a khut ~ kik thei nawn lo hi) (s:kaiton/lehkaih) (r:11.13.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
tonsakkik = (t:v) (w:draw back/pull back) (d:tonsak, draw in, with kik back: bring a stretched-out hand back to the body) (e:a khut ~ thei nawn lo hi) (s:kaiton/lehkaih) (a:zankhia) (b:tonsak) (r:11.13.4) (q:draft)
tonu = (t:n) (w:mistress/lady) (d:to, lord or master, with nu marking a woman: a woman who is head of a household or has servants; also a queen, and a polite word for a lady) (e:nasem numeino in a ~’ za a suan ciang/Na ~’ kiangah ciahkik in la | go back to your mistress/kiphasakin a ~ simmawh bawl hi | she became proud and despised her mistress/Ka ~ Sarai’ kiang panin a taikhia ka hi hi | I am running away from my mistress Sarai) (a:nasemnu) (b:to) (r:20.30.23/1.16.9/1.16.4/1.16.8) (q:draft)
Tonu = (t:n) (w:lady/queen) (d:tonu, lady or mistress, written with a capital: the lady to whom 2 John is addressed, and Babylon speaking of herself as queen) (e:a kiteel ~ leh a tate/Tu-in ~ aw, thupiakna thak hong gelh bang hi loin | now, lady, it is not as though I write you a new command/~ ka hi tawntung ding hi | I will be queen forever) (b:tonu) (r:63.1.1/63.1.5/23.47.7) (q:draft)
top = (t:v) (w:pick up/gather/glean) (d:pick up things left lying: of grain, glean; of food, gather up what is left over; van top is take plunder) (e:ama ~ dingin nusia un la/a an ~ teng a teeknu lakin | she showed her mother-in-law all the grain she had gleaned/a neng a themte a ~ uh ciangin | when they gathered up the broken pieces/van ~ ding tampi a omna khuapi | a city where there is much plunder to take) (s:tawm) (r:8.2.16/34.3.1/8.2.18/43.6.13) (q:draft)
Top = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Tob) (d:region east of the Jordan, also written Tob, whose men were hired by the Ammonites to fight against David) (e:Rehob-a Siria mite, ~ mite, leh Ma-akahte) (r:10.10.8) (q:draft)
topa = (t:n) (w:master/lord) (d:a human master or owner, the husband or lord one serves; topa aw is a polite form of address, and Topa with a capital is the Lord) (e:a ~ in hehpih a/a theih loh kalin a ~ hong tung ding a | his master will come at an hour he does not know/a ~ a kempa in pahtakna ngah hi | whoever looks after his master will be honoured/Na ~ ahih ciangin ama mai-ah kun in | since he is your lord, bow before him) (s:to) (a:nasem/sila/nasempa) (b:to) (r:40.18.27/1.43.20/40.24.50/20.27.18/19.45.11) (q:draft)
Topa = (t:n) (w:Lord) (d:the Lord, the name by which God is called throughout the Bible text, and the title of Jesus as Lord; written with a capital to set it apart from topa, a human master) (e:~ in lam hong lakding hi/~ in Moses kiangah | the Lord said to Moses/~ in tuu cin’ bang-a kei hong cingpa hi a | the Lord is the one who tends me like a shepherd/Ka ~ leh ka Pasian aw | my Lord and my God) (s:Pasian/mangpa) (r:5.2.17/2.6.10/19.23.1/43.20.28)
topate = (t:n) (w:lords/masters) (d:topa with the plural te; in the verses always in the title Lord of lords) (e:pasiante’ Pasian, ~’ Topa ahi hi/kumpite’ Kumpi, ~’ Topa | King of kings, Lord of lords/Lungdamna pen ~’ Topa tungah ko un | give thanks to the Lord of lords) (s:tote) (b:topa) (r:5.10.17/66.17.14/66.19.16/19.136.3) (q:draft)
topaz = (t:n) (c:stone) (w:topaz) (d:a precious stone, the English name; one of the stones of the breastpiece of the high priest, where the NIV has chrysolite) (e:Ethiopia gamah a piang ~ suangmanphate/a kuana in ~ suangmanpha | the ninth was topaz/Sardis suang, ~ suang, leh kabankel suang | carnelian, topaz and carbuncle) (r:18.28.19/66.21.20/2.39.10) (q:draft)
Topaz = (t:n) (c:stone) (w:topaz) (d:topaz, a precious stone, capitalised in the text) (e:Ethiopia gam-a piang ~ suangmanphate tawh) (b:topaz) (r:18.28.19) (q:draft)
topsa = (t:n) (w:gleanings/what was gathered) (d:top glean with sa, already done: what has been gleaned) (e:a ~ teng satkhia a) (b:top) (r:8.2.17) (q:draft)
tosak = (t:v) (w:strengthen/make firm) (d:make strong and firm, said of the bars of a city gate) (e:na kulh kongpi zawlte ~ a) (s:khauhsak) (r:19.147.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
tosak = (t:v) (w:send up/cause to go up) (d:to upward with the causative sak, after a verb of movement: paikhia tosak is make someone go up out of a place) (e:kote hong paikhia ~ kei in) (a:paisuksak) (b:to) (r:2.33.15) (q:draft)
tosukin = (t:v) (w:digging down) (d:to dig with suk, downward, and the linking ending in) (e:Lei ~ misite’ omna Leinuai-ah) (r:30.9.2) (q:draft)
tot = (t:v) (w:walk/tread/travel along) (d:walk along a path or road, and so follow a way of life; the form of tawn used before a noun or ding, as in tot lampi, the path walked) (e:ama ~ lampi in sihna mun tun’na lampi/ama lampite ~ ding, amah it ding | to walk in his ways, to love him/Ama khe in a ~ ngei loh lampite | paths that his feet have never walked/Na pa David in a ~ bangin | as your father David walked/a ~ ngei uh lampi lui zui nawnloin | no longer following the old path they used to walk) (s:tawn) (r:20.5.5/24.18.15/5.10.12/23.41.3/11.3.14) (q:draft)
totai = (t:v) (w:run up) (d:to up with tai run; a suktai a totai kawikawi is running down and up, here and there) (e:A suktai a ~ kawikawi kalaoh huk) (s:taito) (a:suktai) (r:24.2.23) (q:draft, low confidence)
totawm = (t:v) (w:dig for oneself/dig) (d:to, dig, with tawm, by oneself or for oneself: tuikhuk totawm is dig cisterns of their own) (e:Tuikhuk ~ uh a) (s:to) (r:24.2.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
tote = (t:n) (w:masters/lords/sirs) (d:plural of to, master or lord: the masters of slaves or servants; ka tote aw is the polite address my lords, sirs) (e:na ~ uh thu na mang un/Hi lo hi, ka ~ aw | no, my lords/kihtakna tawh na ~ uh ukna na mang un | submit with reverence to the rule of your masters/silate leh a ~, vanleite leh van zuakte | slaves and their masters, buyers and sellers) (s:topate) (a:silate/nasemte) (r:49.6.5/44.16.30/1.19.18/60.2.18/23.24.2) (q:draft)
tote = (t:n) (w:diggers/those who dig) (d:to, dig, with te, the people who dig) (e:Gum a ~, gum sung mah-ah kia ding/Mi siahna-in gum a ~ | those who dig a pit to trap others) (b:to) (r:21.10.8/20.26.27) (q:draft, low confidence)
totna = (t:n) (w:treading/walking/stepping) (d:tot, walk along, with the noun suffix na: the act of treading or walking; a totna mun is the place where the foot treads, and lampi totna is walking in the ways of someone) (e:na khe in a ~ mun khempeuh/Topa na Pasian uh itna, ama lampite ~ | loving the Lord your God, walking in his ways/Jeroboam’ khekhap a ~ | his walking in the footsteps of Jeroboam) (b:tot) (r:6.1.3/5.30.16/11.16.18) (q:draft)
toto = (t:adv) (w:more and more/continually/onward) (d:to, upward, said twice and placed after a verb to show that an action or state goes on and increases) (e:mite’ maipha a ngah ~ hi/na nuamsa ~ ding hi | you will go on prospering) (s:semsem) (b:to) (r:9.2.26/27.4.27) (q:draft)
totsa = (t:adj) (w:trodden/walked on) (d:tot with sa, already done: describes land or a path on which someone has walked) (e:na khe in a ~ leitang/a tate tungah ama ~ leitang ka pia ding hi | I will give his children the land he has walked on) (b:tot) (r:6.14.9/5.1.36) (q:draft)
totte = (t:n) (w:ways/paths walked) (d:tot walk along with the plural te: the paths one has walked, one's conduct) (e:na lampi ~ en dih in) (b:tot) (r:24.2.23) (q:draft, low confidence)
tovang = (t:v) (w:dig through/dig into) (d:to dig with vang hole: dig a hole through a wall) (e:Kei zong kulh ka ~ a/hih kulh ~ in | dig through this wall) (s:tawhvang) (r:26.8.8) (q:draft)
tovungin = (t:v) (w:dig around/dig) (d:dig up the soil around a plant, with the connective ending in) (e:a phung kimkot ah ~) (r:42.13.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
Trakhonis = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Traconitis) (d:region south of Damascus and east of Galilee, ruled by the tetrarch Philip) (r:42.3.1)
Trakhonitis = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Traconitis) (d:region south of Damascus and east of Galilee, ruled by the tetrarch Philip) (r:42.3.1)
Trifana = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Tryphena) (d:Christian woman in Rome whom Paul greets as a worker in the Lord, named together with Tryphosa) (r:45.16.12)
Trifosa = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Tryphosa) (d:Christian woman in Rome whom Paul greets as a worker in the Lord, named together with Tryphena) (r:45.16.12)
Troas = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Troas) (d:port city on the north-west coast of Asia Minor, where Paul saw the vision of the man of Macedonia) (r:44.16.8/44.20.5)
Trofimas = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Trophimus) (d:Christian from Ephesus who travelled with Paul to Jerusalem and was later left sick at Miletus) (r:44.21.29/55.4.20)
Trofosa = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Tryphosa) (d:Christian woman in Rome whom Paul greets as a worker in the Lord, named together with Tryphena) (r:45.16.12)
tu = (t:adj) (w:this/present) (d:this, the present, said of time: tu ni is today, tu-in is now, and tu-a kipan is from now on) (e:~ ni dongin Israel in David innkuan/Abib kha, ~ ni-in note a paikhia ding | in the month of Abib, today you are going out/~-a kipanin a tawntungin Topa muang in | from now on and forever trust in the Lord) (r:14.10.19/2.13.4/19.131.3)
tu takin = (t:phrase) (w:at the moment/at present/just now/right now/at the present time)
tua = (t:pron) (w:that/those) (d:points to a person or thing already mentioned or known; before a noun it means that or those, and tua ciangin is then, after that) (e:~ khua sungah lungdamna tampi a piang hi/~ nungakte tho-in a meivak ciat a bawl uh hi | those young women got up and trimmed their lamps/~ gam mi ahi Hit mite’ lamah kun hi | he bowed to the Hittites, the people of that land/Kei ~ pa ka hi hi kong ci zo hi | I have told you that I am that man) (a:hih) (r:44.8.8/40.25.7/1.23.7/43.18.8) referring to a specific thing previously mentioned, known, or understood
Tua = (t:pron) (w:that/those) (d:tua, that, written with a capital at the start of a sentence; it stands before a noun, or before bang and ciangin, as in Tua bangin, in that way, and Tua ciangin, then) (e:~ bangin na zuih uh leh/~ ni a kipanin Saul in David encik hi | from that day on Saul kept his eye on David/~ ni mahmahin Topa in Moses kiangah | on that very day the Lord said to Moses/~ ciangin Job in | then Job said) (b:tua) (r:50.4.9/9.25.3/9.18.9/5.32.48/18.3.2) (q:draft)
tuaci = (t:conj) (w:like/just as/so/like that) (d:in that way, as it is: a tuaci bang is such a thing, a tuaci mah is just like that, and tuaci omsak is leave someone or something as it is) (e:A ~ bang kua’n za ngei/Amah ~ omsak un | leave him as he is/amah zong a ~ mah ahi hi | he too is just like that/Bang hangin ~ hih na hi hiam | why do you do so) (r:23.66.8/12.23.18/9.25.25/10.16.10)
tuacih = (t:v) (w:do so/do that/be so) (d:tuaci, in that way, in the form used as a verb: act in the way just spoken of, do so) (e:Na ~ kei uhleh na bawl uh/ka ~ uh ciangin an tampi ka nei uh a | when we did so we had plenty of food/nong ~ ngitnget uh a | you have kept on doing so/Bang hangin ~ ka hi hiam | why did I do so) (b:tuaci) (r:24.4.4/24.44.17/24.22.21/37.1.9) (q:draft)
tuah = (t:v) (w:join/bring together) (d:bring two things together so that they touch or are joined: khui tuah is sew together, and kimai tuah is come face to face) (e:a khut uh a kam-ah a ~ mi zathum | three hundred men who put their hands to their mouths/a kikhui ~ a nihna puan | the second set of curtains sewn together/khat leh khat kimai ~ ni | let us meet each other face to face) (s:gawm) (r:7.7.6/2.36.11/14.25.17)
tuah = (t:v) (w:bring/meet with/encounter/come upon) (d:meet with or come upon something, most often trouble, an enemy or a fate; haksatna tuah is meet hardship and gal tuah is face war) (e:lungkhamna na ~ uh ciangin | when you meet with trouble/Amaute in gal a ~ ciangin | when they face war/a gammang na ~ uh leh | if you come upon it straying/Haksatna na ~ ciangin na lung a kiat leh | if you lose heart when you meet hardship) (s:tuak/tuakkha) (r:20.1.26/2.13.17/2.23.4/20.24.10)
tuahin = (t:adj) (w:together) (d:tuah, join or meet, with the linking ending in, placed after a verb: khui tuahin is sewing together and kimai tuahin is face to face) (e:zong kikhawm ~ a nupa/theitehte khui ~ puansilh dingin a bawl uh hi | they sewed fig leaves together and made coverings/Topa in kimai ~ note hong hopih hi | the Lord spoke with you face to face) (b:tuah) (r:23.34.15/1.3.7/5.5.5)
tuahin = (t:adj) (w:attach) (d:tuah, put against, with the linking ending in: putting one thing against another so that they touch) (e:ama kam le naupang’ kam ~ | putting his mouth to the mouth of the boy) (r:12.4.34)
tuahkhak = (t:v) (w:meet/encounter/come upon/fall into) (d:tuah, meet, with khak, happen to: happen to meet a person or meet with an event; a tuahkhak peuh is whoever one happens to meet) (e:Ze-etna na ~ loh nadingun thu ngen un/Mihaite a hai gamtatna uh i ~ sangin | than that we meet fools in their folly/Kote’ ~ kamsiatna khempeuh na thei hi | you know all the hardship that has come on us/Mihai a ~ peuh tha cial-a a neipa | one who hires any fool he happens to meet) (s:tuakkha) (r:42.22.40/20.17.12/4.20.14/20.26.10) (q:draft)
tuahlawh = (t:v) (w:incur/meet with/suffer) (d:tuah, meet with, with lawh, as a result: bring upon oneself, come to suffer) (e:haksatna le siatna a ~ uh hi) (s:tuaklawh/thuaklawh) (r:54.6.9) (q:draft)
tuahmang = (t:v) (w:carry off/plunder) (d:tuah come upon, with mang away; followed by sak, let someone carry off, give as plunder) (e:na galte uh ka ~ sak ding hi) (r:24.17.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
tuahmangsak = (t:v) (w:give as plunder/let carry off) (d:tuahmang with the causative sak; let the enemy carry everything off) (e:na galte uh ka ~ ding hi) (s:tuahsakmang/sutsak) (b:tuahmang) (r:24.17.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
tuahna = (t:n) (w:encounter/experience) (d:tuah, meet with, with the noun suffix na: meeting with or going through something; na tuahna mun peuh is any place you happen upon) (e:Na ~ mun peuh uhah/Lungkhamna guk vei dong na ~-ah | in six troubles that you meet/amah a ~ peuhah that ding hi | he shall kill him wherever he meets him/gim a ~ ding uh a hun tungta | the time has come for them to meet punishment) (b:tuah) (r:5.12.13/18.5.19/4.35.19/26.21.29) (q:draft)
tuahpha = (t:v) (w:meet with good/fare well) (d:tuah meet with and pha good: have good come to one, set against tuahsiatna, misfortune) (e:midikte ~ kawikawi hi) (a:tuahsia) (r:20.13.21) (q:draft, low confidence)
tuahphasak = (t:v) (w:give success/make prosper) (d:tuahpha meet with good, with the causative sak) (e:Pasian in kei hong ~ hi) (s:daupaisak) (b:tuahpha) (r:1.27.20) (q:draft)
tuahphat = (t:v) (w:prosper/fare well/meet with good) (d:form of tuahpha used before ciangin) (e:Midikte a ~ ciangin khua sungah) (s:daupai/cithei) (a:tuahsiat) (b:tuahpha) (r:20.11.10) (q:draft)
tuahsa = (t:adj) (w:experienced/met with) (d:tuah meet with, with sa already done; tuahsa thute is the things one has gone through) (e:pute pate’ ~ thute ngaihsun in/A beisa huna na ~ uh thute khempeuh | all the things you went through in the past/Israel mite in a ~ bangin | as the Israelites experienced) (b:tuah) (r:18.8.8/48.3.4/58.12.18) (q:draft)
tuahsak = (t:v) (w:let come upon/hand over) (d:tuah meet, come upon, with the causative sak; with mang, give away as plunder) (e:na galte uh ka ~ mang ding hi) (b:tuah) (r:24.15.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
tuahsakmang = (t:v) (w:give as plunder/let carry off) (d:tuah come upon, with the causative sak and mang away) (e:na galte uh ka ~ ding hi) (s:tuahmangsak/sutsak) (r:24.15.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
tuahsia = (t:adj) (w:unfortunate/hapless/afflicted) (d:tuah, meet with, and sia, bad: meeting with misfortune; mi tuahsia or tuahsia mi is a victim, one struck by trouble) (e:~ mi in nangma tungah ama pumpi) (s:kamsia) (a:hampha) (r:19.10.14/19.10.10) (q:draft)
tuahsia = (t:v) (w:meet disaster/suffer ruin) (d:be struck by calamity; tuahsia-in, in calamity) (e:~-in kisuksiat gawp ni) (a:tuahpha) (r:36.1.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
tuahsiat = (t:v) (w:meet with disaster/suffer misfortune) (d:form of tuahsia used before ni, ciangin and other following words; a tuahsiat ni is the day of their disaster) (e:A ~ ni-in a thuaknate uh/Na sanggamte a ~ ni-un munuam dah hoh un | do not gloat on the day of your brothers’ misfortune/A ~ ni-un a sum a paite laksak kei un | do not seize their wealth on the day of their disaster/Iziptte a ~ ciangin | when Egypt meets with disaster) (a:tuahphat) (b:tuahsia) (r:31.1.13/31.1.12/26.29.16) (q:draft)
tuahsiate = (t:n) (w:victims/unfortunate ones) (d:tuahsia unfortunate with the plural te; mi tuahsiate, people struck by misfortune) (e:Ama mit in mi ~ encik sim a) (b:tuahsia) (r:19.10.8) (q:draft)
tuahsiatna = (t:n) (w:misfortune/disaster/calamity/trouble) (d:tuahsiat, meet with disaster, with the noun suffix na: something bad that befalls a person; tuahsiatna tuak is meet with calamity) (e:~ in mawhneite sulzuih kawikawi a/migilote ahih leh ~ tuakin kithallot hi | but the wicked are brought down when calamity strikes/midangte ~-ah a lungdam mipa | the man who is glad at the misfortune of others/~ panin thuman mipa kilakhia a | the righteous man is taken away from calamity) (s:kamsiatna/siatna/thusia) (b:tuahsiat) (r:20.13.21/20.24.16/20.17.5/23.57.1) (q:draft)
tuahsiatnate = (t:n) (w:disasters/calamities/misfortunes) (d:tuahsiatna, disaster, with the plural te) (e:na ~ uh leh na lungkhamnate uh khempeuh panin | from all your disasters and distresses) (s:kamsiatnate/siatnate) (b:tuahsiatna) (r:9.10.19) (q:draft)
tuahsuk = (t:v) (w:go down/descend) (d:go down a slope toward a place, the opposite of kahto, go up) (e:khua-ah a ~ laitakun) (s:paisuk/kumsuk/tuaksuk) (a:kahto/paito) (r:24.48.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
tuahsukna = (t:n) (w:slope/descent) (d:tuahsuk, go down, with the noun suffix na: the way down, a slope; tuahsukna mun is the place where the road goes down) (e:~ mun-ah amaute that uh hi | they killed them on the slope) (s:paisukna) (b:tuahsuk) (r:6.7.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
tuahtuah = (t:v) (w:come upon/find) (d:reduplicated tuah, meet: wherever one comes upon something; a tuahtuah munah is right on the spot where they found them) (e:a ~ munah that uh hi) (r:9.14.32) (q:draft, low confidence)
tuahtuahna = (t:n) (d:tuahtuah, come upon, with the noun suffix na: the place where one comes upon something; a tuahtuahna munah is on the very spot) (e:a ~ munah go uh a) (b:tuahtuah) (r:9.14.32) (q:draft, low confidence)
tuahun = (t:adv) (w:at that time/then/in those days) (d:tua, that, with hun, time: at that time; of the past it is followed by lai-in or laitakin, of the future by ciangin) (e:~ laitakin Farisi mi pawlkhat hong pai-in/~ lai-in na gamtat manun | because of what you did at that time/~ ciangin maitang kimu-in i kiho ding hi | then we will talk face to face/~ lai-in thu a gen ciangin leitung kiling a | at that time the earth shook when he spoke/~ laitakin zanin lupna tungah a lumkhawm mi nih | at that time two people lying on one bed at night) (r:42.13.31/49.2.12/45.6.21/64.1.14/58.12.26/42.17.34) (q:draft)
tuak = (t:v) (w:be lawful/be right/be proper/be fitting) (d:be right, fitting or allowed, placed after another verb: piak tuak is right to give, and with lo it is not allowed) (e:a zi a mak ~ hiam/siah piak ~ ahi hiam | is it right to pay tax/Nipi ni-in phatna bawl ~ hiam | is it lawful to do good on the Sabbath/ahih manin sihdaan piak ~ hi | so he should be sentenced to death/nopna leh lungdamna bawl ~ hi | it is right to celebrate and be glad) (r:41.10.2/42.20.22/41.3.4/24.26.11/42.15.32) (q:draft)
tuak = (t:adv) (w:each/both) (d:each of them, both alike, placed after a noun, a number or a verb) (e:a mang khiatna a tuam ~ ahi hi/amaute kikhen ~ uh hi | they parted from each other/omzia kidong ~ uh a | they each asked how the other was/amau’ paknamtui beel ~ la-in | each taking his censer/om kawmte tong nga ~ sah hi | the walls were each five cubits thick) (s:ciat/tek) (r:1.40.5/2.32.15/1.13.11/2.18.7/3.10.1/26.41.2) (q:draft)
tuak = (t:v) (w:meet/meet with/come upon/experience) (d:come upon a person or thing, or meet with an experience such as trouble, fear or punishment) (e:ka laulau ka ~ ta hi/a lung khauh mipa in lungkhamna ~ ding hi | the hard-hearted man will meet with trouble/Thuman lo khaici a vawhte in lungkhamna ~ a | those who sow injustice meet with trouble/lungkhamna lianpi khat ka ~ hi | I have met with great distress/a bel sek laitak ka ~ hi | I found him making a pot) (s:tuakkha/kimu) (r:18.3.25/1.4.15/20.28.14/20.22.8/13.21.13/24.18.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
tuaka = (t:adv) (w:each/both) (d:tuak, each, with the ending a, used after pang, side: pang tuaka om is being on each side or on both sides) (e:gun pang ~ ding mi nih/a pang ~ om kawmte | the walls on each side/a pang ~ om lai leitang | the land that remains on both sides/Lampi pang ~ kawmte tungah | on the walls on each side of the gateway) (b:tuak) (r:27.12.5/26.41.2/26.48.21/26.40.31) (q:draft)
tuakah = (t:adv) (w:on both sides/on each side/on either side) (d:tuak, each or both, with the place marker ah, used after pang or lang, side: on both sides, on each of the two) (e:a gun lang nih ~ singkung tampi/a pang ~ phung a omna lam kawcik | a narrow path with a wall on both sides/Amah tawh a lang ~ mi nih | with him two men, one on each side/a khut lang ~ khutme guk a nei | he had six fingers on each hand/a lang nih ~ lai kigelhin | written on both sides) (s:langtuakah) (b:tuak) (r:26.47.7/4.22.24/43.19.18/13.20.6/26.2.10) (q:draft)
tuakin = (t:v) (w:meeting/coming upon/finding) (d:tuak, meet, with the linking ending in: meeting a person, or meeting with death or trouble, and then the next action follows) (e:Migilote in sihna ~ ci-mang a/a kidong nai lo nungak khat ~ | meeting a girl who is not yet betrothed/khuapi sungah tua nu ~ amah tawh a lup | meets her in the town and sleeps with her/Bezek-ah Adonibezek ~ amah tawh kido uh a | they found Adoni-Bezek at Bezek and fought him/a kidongsa nungak khat gam lakah ~ | meeting a betrothed girl out in the country) (r:20.12.7/5.22.28/5.22.23/7.1.5/5.22.25) (q:draft)
tuakin = (t:adv) (w:both/each) (d:tuak, each, with the ending in, mostly after a number: a nih tuakin is both of the two; a tuam tuakin is each one apart) (e:a nih ~ Topa in deih lo hi/A nih ~ mun khatah tungkhawm ding uh a | both go to the same place/a nih ~ a sitbang lo | both without defect/thuneite a langnih ~ | both parties to the dispute/mi khempeuh a tuam ~ hong kikhensak ding hi | he will separate all people, each apart) (s:tegel) (b:tuak) (r:20.17.15/5.19.17/21.3.20/3.9.2/40.25.32) (q:draft)
tuakin = (t:v) (w:getting down/alighting/plunging) (d:tuak with the linking ending in: getting down from an animal or a chariot, or plunging down into something) (e:la tung panin ~ David mai-ah maipuk a/Sisera a leeng tung pan ~ a khe-in tai | Sisera got down from his chariot and fled on foot/tuili sungah ~ a si khin uh hi | they plunged into the lake and all died) (r:9.25.23/7.4.15/42.8.33) (q:draft, low confidence)
tuakkha = (t:v) (w:meet with/come upon/happen to meet/find) (d:tuak, meet, with kha, happen to: come upon a person by chance, find someone doing something, or meet with trouble) (e:haksatna ~ lo ding hi/David’ nasemte in Absalom ~ uh hi | David’s men happened to meet Absalom/na ihmut laitakun hong ~ ding hi | he will find you sleeping/tuu khempeuh in lauhuaina ~ loin | no sheep will meet with danger/beel a sek laitak ka va ~ hi | I found him making a pot) (s:tuak) (r:21.8.5/24.18.3/10.18.9/41.13.36/43.10.9) (q:draft)
tuakkhia = (t:v) (w:get off/disembark/get out) (d:tuak, get down, with khia, out: come out and down from a ship or boat) (e:teembaw tung pan ka ~ uh hi/a gunkuang panun ~-in | having got out of their boats) (s:kumkhia) (r:44.21.3/42.5.2) (q:draft)
tuaklawh = (t:v) (w:incur/meet with/suffer) (d:tuak, meet with, and lawh, as a result: bring something bad upon oneself) (e:siatna a ~ uh hi) (s:thuaklawh/thuakkha) (r:61.3.16) (q:draft)
tuaklo = (t:v) (w:not meet with/not suffer) (d:tuak meet with and lo not, written as one word) (e:lungkhamna ~ ding hi) (b:tuak) (r:23.28.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
tuaklo = (t:v) (w:not be possible/not be proper) (d:tuak be fitting with lo not, placed after another verb) (e:omtheih ~ hi) (b:tuak) (r:10.13.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
Tuakna = (t:n) (d:tuak, each or meet, with the noun suffix na; in the text it is part of a section heading, A Kideih Tuakna, apparently the desire of each for the other) (e:Tangval A Kideih ~) (r:22.7.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
tuakpa = (t:n) (w:one who meets) (d:tuak meet with pa, the man: the man who meets or runs into something) (e:vompi a ~ tawh kibang ding hi) (b:tuak) (r:30.5.19) (q:draft)
