tulgiat = (t:num) (w:eight thousand) (d:tul, thousand, with giat, eight; tulsawm leh tulgiat is eighteen thousand) (e:mihing tulsawm leh ~ tuk uh hi/Edom mite tulsawm leh ~ that hi | he struck down eighteen thousand Edomites/pasal tul sawmthum leh ~ pha hi | the men numbered thirty-eight thousand) (r:7.20.44/4.4.48/13.18.12/13.23.3) (q:draft)
tulguk = (t:num) (w:six thousand) (d:tul, thousand, with guk, six; joined to other numbers with leh, as tul sawmnih leh tulguk, twenty-six thousand) (e:tul sawmnih leh ~ khawm uh hi/~ in mangte leh thukhente hi ding a | six thousand are to be officials and judges/kalaoh ~, bawngtal kap tulkhat | six thousand camels and a thousand yoke of oxen/kham shekel ~, leh pawi puan sawm | six thousand shekels of gold and ten festive garments) (r:7.20.15/13.23.4/18.42.12/12.5.5) (q:draft)
tulh = (t:v) (w:give to drink/feed) (d:give someone something to drink, as milk to an infant or wine to a guest) (e:nawizu bek kong ~ hi/mangkawlsing tui, kong ~ ding hi | I would give you pomegranate juice to drink) (s:dawnsak) (r:46.3.2/22.8.2) (q:draft)
tulin = (t:adv) (w:by thousands/in thousands) (d:tul, thousand, with the ending in: a tulin is by the thousand, in thousands, and a tul tulin thousand upon thousand) (e:Saul in a ~ that/tuu a tul ~ va puakin | bringing rams by the thousands/Judah sung pan a ~ a ukte | from Judah, the commanders of thousands/na minam nam uh leh a tul ~ | by your tribes and by your thousands) (s:tultulin) (b:tul) (r:9.18.7/33.6.7/14.17.14/9.10.19) (q:draft)
tulkhat = (t:num) (w:one thousand/a thousand) (d:tul, thousand, with khat, one; it follows the thing counted, as kum tulkhat, a thousand years) (e:khang ~ adingin a thupiakna kammal/kum ~ tawntung hen cipin | binding him for a thousand years/a golzawte in ~ val uk uh hi | the greatest commanded more than a thousand/tul sawmli leh ~ leh zanga pha hi | they numbered 41,500) (r:13.16.15/15.2.37/66.20.2/13.12.14/4.1.41) (q:draft)
tulkhatte = (t:num) (w:a thousand) (d:tulkhat, one thousand, with the plural te: a group of a thousand men, the thousand of them) (e:~ Benjaminte’ gamsung Gibeah-ah) (b:tulkhat) (r:9.13.2) (q:draft)
tulkua = (t:num) (w:nine thousand) (d:tul, thousand, with kua, nine) (e:tul sawmnga leh ~ leh zathum pha hi/tul sawmnga leh ~ leh zathum pha hi | they numbered 59,300) (r:4.2.13/4.1.23) (q:draft)
tulli = (t:num) (w:four thousand) (d:tul, thousand, with li, four; tul sawmnih leh tulli is twenty-four thousand) (e:Levi mite sung panin ~ leh zaguk/~ in kongcingte | four thousand are to be gatekeepers/galphual sungah mi ~ bang that uh hi | they killed about four thousand men on the battlefield/ama khen sungah tul sawmnih leh ~ om hi | in his division there were twenty-four thousand) (r:13.12.26/13.23.5/9.4.2/13.27.7) (q:draft)
tullite = (t:see) <thenli-tullite>
tulnga = (t:num) (w:five thousand) (d:tul, thousand, with nga, five) (e:pasal teng ~ bang a pha uh hi/amah in mi ~ bang paipihin | he took about five thousand men/sumngo shekel ~ ahi hi | it was five thousand shekels of bronze/galhang mihing tul sawmnih leh ~ ahi hi | twenty-five thousand valiant men) (r:44.4.4/6.8.12/9.17.5/7.20.46) (q:draft)
tulnih = (t:num) (w:two thousand) (d:tul, thousand, with nih, two; it follows the higher number with leh, as in tulsawm leh tulnih, twelve thousand) (e:a vekpi in ~ leh zaguk ahi hi/a vekpi-in tulsawm leh ~ ahi hi | in all there were twelve thousand/mite tul sawmnih leh ~ lei-ah that uh hi | they cut down twenty-two thousand Israelites/tul sawmnih leh ~ leh za nih ahi hi | they were 22,200) (r:14.26.12/6.8.25/7.20.21/4.26.14) (q:draft)
tulnihte = (t:num) (w:two thousand) (d:tulnih, two thousand, with the plural te: a group of two thousand men, the two thousand of them) (e:~ Mikmash leh Beth-el mualtung gamah) (b:tulnih) (r:9.13.2) (q:draft)
tulpih = (t:todo) (q:draft, only in nang zong hong tulpih lo ding numei paktat, Hosea 1:2, perhaps be faithful to or stay with; meaning not clear from the verse)
tulsagih = (t:num) (w:seven thousand) (d:tul, thousand, with sagih, seven) (e:mihing ~ Israel sungah ka siit ding hi/tuu ~, kalaoh tulthum | seven thousand sheep and three thousand camels/mi ~ a si uh hi | seven thousand people died/a kisiangsaksa ngun talen ~ | seven thousand talents of refined silver) (r:11.19.18/13.29.4/18.1.3/66.11.13) (q:draft)
tulsawm = (t:num) (w:ten thousand) (d:tul, thousand, with sawm, ten; tulsawm leh tulnih is twelve thousand) (e:mi ~ lakah tehpih ding dang om lo/talen ~ a ba nasempa khat | a servant who owed ten thousand talents/galhang mihing ~ leh tulgiat tuk uh hi | eighteen thousand valiant men fell/hong umcih mi ~ tampite ka kihta kei hi | I do not fear the many tens of thousands who surround me) (s:then/thenkhat) (r:22.5.10/7.20.44/40.18.24/19.3.6) (q:draft)
tulsawmgiat = (t:num) (w:eighty thousand) (d:tul, thousand, with sawmgiat, eighty; tulza leh tulsawmgiat leh tulnga is 185,000) (e:tulza leh ~ leh tulnga that hi) (r:23.37.36) (q:draft)
tulsawmguk = (t:num) (w:sixty thousand) (d:tul, thousand, with sawmguk, sixty; tulsawmguk leh tulkhat is sixty-one thousand) (e:kham darik ~ leh tulkhat) (r:15.2.69) (q:draft)
tulsawmin = (t:adv) (w:by tens of thousands) (d:tulsawm, ten thousand, with the ending in: by tens of thousands; a tulsawmin that is killed his tens of thousands) (e:David in a ~ that/David tungah a ~ pia-in | they have credited David with tens of thousands) (s:thenin/thenthenin) (b:tulsawm) (r:9.18.7/9.18.8) (q:draft)
tulsawmli = (t:num) (w:forty thousand) (d:tul, thousand, with sawmli, forty) (e:sakol tuang mi ~ thatin/~ leh tulnih leh zathum leh sawmguk pha uh | they numbered 42,360) (s:thenli) (r:10.10.18/15.2.64) (q:draft)
tulsawmnih = (t:num) (w:twenty thousand) (d:tul, thousand, with sawmnih, twenty) (e:mi ~ ahi hi/Siria mite ~ leh tulnih that hi | he struck down twenty-two thousand Arameans/tulza leh ~ sanga tam zawte | more than a hundred and twenty thousand) (s:thennih) (r:10.18.7/10.8.5/32.4.11) (q:draft)
tulsawmthum = (t:num) (w:thirty thousand) (d:tul, thousand, with sawmthum, thirty) (e:khe galkap mi ~ puk hi) (r:9.4.10) (q:draft)
tulthum = (t:num) (w:three thousand) (d:tul, thousand, with thum, three) (e:bawngtal zaguk leh tuu ~ ahi hi/tua ni-in mi ~ bang a kibehlap uh hi | that day about three thousand people were added/~ bang tua lai-ah kuanto uh hi | about three thousand went up there/Ofir gam kham ahi kham talen ~ | three thousand talents of gold of Ophir) (r:14.29.33/44.2.41/6.7.4/13.29.4) (q:draft)
tultul = (t:num) (w:thousands/by thousands) (d:tul, thousand, said twice: thousand by thousand, thousands; a tultul a ukte are commanders of thousands) (e:a ~ a ukte leh a zaza a ukte-in/a kisim ciangin ~, thenthen ahi uh hi | when counted they were thousands and tens of thousands/a ~ a thenthenin gamlakah suak ta hen | may they increase by thousands and tens of thousands in the fields/a ~ leh a zaza-a a ukte tung | to the commanders of thousands and of hundreds) (r:10.18.1/19.144.13/66.5.11/14.1.2) (q:draft)
tultulin = (t:adv) (w:by thousands) (d:tultul, thousands, with the ending in: in groups of a thousand; a zaza a tultulin is by hundreds and by thousands) (e:a zaza a ~ a pai laitakin/a zaza le a ~ a paikhiat laitakun | while they marched out by hundreds and by thousands) (s:tulin) (b:tultul) (r:9.29.2/10.18.4) (q:draft)
tulum = (t:v) (w:bite to death/kill by biting) (d:tu, bite or strike, said of a snake, with lum, dead: kill by biting) (e:Gul in amaute na ~ hi) (s:petlum) (r:46.10.9) (q:draft)
tulza = (t:num) (w:hundred thousand) (d:tul, thousand, with za, hundred: one hundred thousand; further numbers follow with leh, as tulza leh tulgiat, 108,000) (e:mihing ~ leh tulsawmgiat leh tulnga that hi/~ leh tulgiat leh zakhat pha hi | they number 108,100/mi ~ leh tul sawmnih si khin hi | a hundred and twenty thousand men had died/Ama nasem ding mihing ~ om a | a hundred thousand were there to serve him) (r:23.37.36/4.2.24/7.8.10/27.7.10) (q:draft)
