tulzum = (t:n) (w:spade/digging tool) (d:a small tool for digging the ground, carried along with a soldier’s weapons) (e:~ khat na nei ding uh hi) (r:5.23.13) (q:draft)
tum = (t:v) (w:play/blow/sound) (d:play a musical instrument or sound a trumpet; the instrument stands before the verb, as peengkul tum, blow the trumpet) (e:hoih takin khausai ~ un/David in a laiza lasakna ~ hi | David played the lyre/Joab in peengkul ~ hi | Joab blew the trumpet/siampite in peengkul ~ ding uh hi | the priests shall blow the trumpets) (s:mut) (r:19.33.3/9.19.9/10.2.28/6.6.4) of instruments
tuma = (t:adv) (w:ago/before/formerly/previously) (d:before now; tuma kum is years ago, tuma lamin some time ago, and tuma-in earlier, set against tu-in, now) (e:~ kum sawm leh li lai takin/~-in a si hi, tu-in a nungta kik hi | he was dead before, now he is alive again/~ ni li lai-in tubang hun | four days ago at this hour/~ lamin kumpi lehdo dingin | some time ago, to revolt against the ruler/~, tu laitak, le a tawntungin | before, now and forever) (s:nidang/tumasiah) (r:47.12.2/42.15.32/44.10.30/44.21.38/65.1.25) (q:draft)
tumahin = (t:adv) (w:just now/right now/even now) (d:tu, now, with the emphatic mah and the ending in: at this very time) (e:~ kei nong sam a/Haman’ inn-ah ~ om hi | it stands at Haman’s house right now) (s:tuhunin) (r:24.3.4/17.7.9) (q:draft)
