tumin = (t:v) (w:entering/going in) (d:tum enter or go down into, with the linking suffix in) (e:puan dalna sungah ~/Hih mite Mikah’ inn sungah ~ | these men went into Micah’s house/Kei zong a sungah ~ ka khuadak hi | I too went in and looked/na innsung uhah ~ kong khak unla | go into your room and shut the door/a kulhpi sungah ~ | entering his fortress) (s:lutin/sungtumin) (a:pusuakin) (b:tum) (r:58.6.19/4.5.24/7.18.18/26.8.10/40.6.6/27.11.7) (q:draft)
tumkhawm = (t:v) (w:enter together/go in together) (d:tum, enter, with khawm, together: go or come in together) (e:Jeim kiangah ka ~ uh a/na kikhopna inn sung uhah hong ~ uh ciangin | when they come into your meeting together) (s:lutkhawm) (r:44.21.18/59.2.2) (q:draft)
