tumsan = (t:v) (w:set on/go down on) (d:of the sun, tum, set, with san, leaving behind: set on someone and leave them in the dark) (e:ni in hong ~ ta ding hi) (r:33.3.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
tumsiam = (t:adj) (w:skilled in playing) (d:tum play an instrument with siam skilled; a tumsiam is a skilled player, a musician) (e:a ~ pa in a tum ciangin/laiza lasakna a ~ mi khat | someone skilled in playing the lyre/lasakna a ~ khat hong paipih in | bring me a skilled player/Jessi’ tapa, a ~, a thahat | a son of Jesse, skilled in playing, strong) (r:12.3.15/9.16.18/9.16.16) (q:draft)
tumsim = (t:v) (w:enter secretly/infiltrate/sneak in) (d:tum enter, with sim secretly) (e:kheemna tawh a hong ~) (s:lutsim/simlut) (r:48.2.4) (q:draft)
tumsuak = (t:v) (w:keep blowing/blow continually) (d:tum blow an instrument, with suak, go on doing) (e:peengkulte ~ uh hi) (r:6.6.13) (q:draft)
tumsuk = (t:v) (w:go down/descend/sink into) (d:go down into something, as food into the stomach or people into the grave) (e:a hing tangun Leinuai-ah ~ uh hi/a lut khempeuh in gil sungah ~ a | everything that enters goes down into the stomach/buannawng thuk sungah ka ~ a | I sink in deep mire/mihingte’ sungtawng pekah ~ pahpah hi | they go straight down to a person’s inmost parts) (s:paisuk/kumsuk) (a:kahto/paito) (r:4.16.33/40.15.17/19.69.2/20.26.22) (q:draft)
tumsukin = (t:v) (w:sinking/going down) (d:tumsuk sink down, with the connective ending in) (e:Babylon khuapi zong ~) (b:tumsuk) (r:24.51.64) (q:draft)
tumsukna = (t:n) (w:sinking/going down) (d:tumsuk go down or sink, with the noun suffix na) (e:Buannawng thuk sungah ~ ding panin) (b:tumsuk) (r:19.69.14) (q:draft)
tumsukte = (t:n) (w:things that go down/things that enter) (d:tumsuk go down into, with plural te: the things that go down, here what goes into the mouth) (e:Kam sungah a ~ pen gil sung) (b:tumsuk) (r:40.15.17) (q:draft)
tumtakin = (t:adv) (w:complacently/self-contentedly) (d:in nomau’ tumtakin a lungkim, said of women who feel secure and are satisfied with themselves; the part tum is not clear) (e:Nomau’ ~ a lungkim numeite aw/Nomau’ ~ a lungkim tanute aw | you daughters who feel secure) (r:23.32.10/23.32.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
tumte = (t:n) (w:instrument) (d:tum, play an instrument, with the plural te; in the verses it follows the name of an instrument and means those who play it, as peengkul tumte, trumpeters) (e:peengkul ~ leh lasate’ nasep | the work of the trumpeters and singers/a nungah tamngai ~ | after them the pipe players/tamngai ~ leh mihonpi gamlum a | the pipe players and the noisy crowd) (b:tum) (r:14.5.13/19.68.25/40.9.23)
tumtheih = (t:n) (w:musical instrument/instrument) (d:something that can be played or sounded, from tum play and theih can; used for instruments of all kinds) (e:~ awgingte khempeuh zong kiza nawn lo/~ gingte a zak phetun | as soon as they heard the sound of the instruments/~ a tuamtuamte a hong kitum ciangin | when all kinds of instruments are played/gawsem, le ~ dang a gingte | pipes and the other instruments that sound) (s:lasakna) (b:tum) (r:26.26.13/27.3.5/27.3.7/27.3.15) (q:draft)
tumtheih = (t:v) (w:be able to enter/can come in) (d:tum enter with theih can; hong tumtheih nadingin, so that he may come in) (e:Minthang Kumpipa hong ~ nadingin) (s:luttheih) (r:19.24.7) (q:draft)
tumtheihte = (t:n) (w:musical instruments/instruments) (d:plural of tumtheih, things that can be played) (e:~ a hong kitum khit phetin) (s:lasaknate) (b:tumtheih) (r:27.3.10) (q:draft)
tumzaw = (t:see) <tumzaw-in>
tumzaw-in = (t:adv) (w:deeper/more deeply) (d:tum go in, with zaw more and the linking ending in: going in further, of a sore that looks deeper than the skin) (e:a natna thuk ~ a kimuh leh) (r:3.13.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
tumzel = (t:v) (w:set again/keep setting) (d:tum, of the sun go down, with zel again and again; the NIV has hurries back) (e:a suakkik dingin ~ hi) (r:21.1.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
tun = (t:v) (w:arrive/reach/come) (d:form of tung, arrive, used before ciangin, ma and other dependent endings; often written with a final apostrophe) (e:Isaiah kiangah a ~ ciangin/Zoar-ah Lot a ~ ciangin | by the time Lot reached Zoar/Izipt gamsungah Abram a ~ ciangin | when Abram came to Egypt/Jerusalem khua ka ~’ uh ciangin | when we arrived in Jerusalem/hih mun na ~’ ma sung tengun | all the time before you reached this place) (r:23.37.5/16.2.11/1.19.23/1.12.14/15.8.32/5.11.5) (q:draft)
tun = (t:v) (w:come/come to pass/be fulfilled) (d:of a time, a word or a promise: come, come about; the form of tung used before ciangin, ma and matengin) (e:ama thugente a ~’ matengin/A hun hong ~’ ciangin | when the time comes/kicin’na a ~’ ciangin | when completeness comes/A hun a ~’ ma-in | before his time comes) (s:tangtung) (r:19.105.19/12.4.16/46.13.10/18.15.32) (q:draft, low confidence)
tunai = (t:adj) (w:near/soon/close at hand) (d:of time, near to now, tu, now, with nai, near; tunai hun hi lo is it is not a near time) (e:ahih hangin ~ hun hi lo hi) (r:4.24.17) (q:draft, low confidence)
tunbaih = (t:v) (w:come soon/arrive quickly) (d:tun arrive with baih early, quickly) (e:Pasian’ Ni hong ~ theih nadingin) (s:hawhbaih) (r:61.3.12) (q:draft)
tuncip = (t:v) (w:wrap up/bundle up) (d:wrap something tightly in a cloth) (e:puanin tuite ~ ahi hiam) (s:vialcip) (r:20.30.4) (q:draft)
tuncipsak = (t:v) (w:blindfold/cover up) (d:tuncip wrap tightly, with the causative sak; mit tuncipsak is cover the eyes) (e:thukhen mangte’ mit a ~ hi) (s:tuamsak) (b:tuncip) (r:18.9.24) (q:draft)
tung = (t:v) (w:arrive/reach/come) (d:come to a place or person, arrive; also of a time, a word or a feeling that comes upon someone; before ciangin the form is tun) (e:kei ~ ka hi maw/Grik gam a ~ hi | he arrived in Greece/Nitak hong bei-in, zingsang hong ~ a | evening passed and morning came/Launa leh liin’na ka tung hong ~ a | fear and trembling have come upon me/a pa’ tuute tawh Rachel hong ~ hi | Rachel came with her father’s sheep) (a:paikhiat) (r:15.7.8/43.20.8/44.20.2/1.1.5/19.55.5/1.29.9)
tung = (t:prep) (w:over/on/upon) (d:the top or upper side of something, placed after the noun, alone or with ah or a: mual tung is on the mountain, the hill country) (e:Tuipi ~ ah lampai/Moses mual ~ panin mite’ kiangah paisuk a | Moses went down from the mountain to the people/Seir mual ~ gamah Esau teng hi | Esau settled in the hill country of Seir/amau ~ a san’na munah tu in | sit on high over them) (r:1.1.2/1.1.26/2.19.14/1.36.8/19.7.7)
tung-ua = (t:ppm) (d:tung in the sense at the time of, with plural uh and the linking a; na neu tung-ua kipan is from the time you were young) (e:Na neu ~ kipan nong tua) (r:24.22.21) (q:draft, low confidence)
tunga = (t:adv) (w:over) (d:tung with the linking a: over, in authority over, placed after the people who are ruled) (e:Israelte ~ a lian/galkap tul tampite ~ uliante | the officers over the thousands of the army/Amau ~ kumpipa | the king over them) (s:tungah) (b:tung) (r:19.68.34/4.31.48/66.9.11)
tunga = (t:prep) (w:above/on top of/on) (d:tung, top, with the linking a: on, upon or above, placed after the noun and before what is there) (e:vante ~ om tuite aw/leikeu ~ a om | that were on dry land/a ~ ama hiangte a si ta hi | above, his branches wither) (s:tungah) (a:nuaiah) (b:tung) (r:19.148.4/1.1.7/1.7.22/18.18.16)
tungah = (t:adv) (w:over) (d:tung with the place marker ah: over, in authority over, placed after the people or land that is ruled) (e:Israel khempeuh ~ kumpi hi a/Topa in minam khempeuhte ~ uk a | the Lord rules over all the nations/amaute ~ a uk ding kumpipa | the king who will reign over them/Levi mi makaite ~ a ukpi hi ding a | he shall be chief over the leaders of the Levites) (s:tunga) (b:tung) (r:11.4.1/19.113.4/9.8.9/4.3.32)
tungah = (t:prep) (w:above/on top of/on/upon) (d:tung, top, with the place marker ah: on, upon or above, placed after the noun) (e:tua ~ a namtui paknamtui hal hi/kumpi tokhom ~ tu hi | he sat on the royal throne/kigelhna lai a ~ a om hi | there was a written notice above him/ama’ lu ~ dialpi khimsakin | put the turban on his head) (s:tunga/dawnah) (a:nuaiah) (b:tung) (r:2.40.27/11.1.46/42.23.38/2.29.6)
tungdap = (t:n) (w:rafter/roof beam) (d:the sloping timbers that carry the roof of a house; inn tungdap is the rafters of the house) (e:i inn ~ hi ding hi) (s:innkam) (r:22.1.17) (q:draft)
tunghak = (t:v) (w:be late in coming/be delayed/be a long time coming) (d:tung, arrive, with hak, slow or hard: be a long time in arriving) (e:Zineipa hong ~ ahih manin) (s:zekai) (r:40.25.5) (q:draft)
tungin = (t:adv) (w:early/at the start of) (d:at the very start of something: zingsang tungin is early in the morning, and after a verb it means when something has only just begun, as in kumpi a suah tungin, early in his reign) (e:a mite tawh zingsang ~ dingkhia uh a/zingsang ~ Abraham va pai hi | early in the morning Abraham went there/Zingsang ~ Laban tho-in | early in the morning Laban got up/Judah gamah kumpi a suah ~ | early in his reign as king in Judah/Mi khat in zi a neih ~ | when a man has newly taken a wife) (s:baihin/baih) (r:9.29.11/24.27.1/1.19.27/1.31.55/5.24.5) (q:draft)
tungin = (t:v) (w:arriving/reaching/coming) (d:tung, arrive or come, with the linking ending in, which joins it to the next action: having arrived, or coming and then) (e:Sirakhas khua ~ ni thum ka taam uh hi/Amah mun khat ~ | he came to a certain place/kialpi kum sagih sung hong ~ | seven years of famine will come/Nitak ciangin vamimte hong ~ giahphual tuam hi | in the evening quail came and covered the camp/hih thuphate khempeuh no tungah hong ~ | all these blessings will come upon you) (b:tung) (r:44.28.12/1.28.11/1.41.30/2.16.13/5.28.2) (q:draft)
tungkha = (t:v) (w:fall into/end up in) (d:tung, arrive, with kha, happen to: end up in a bad state, as in mawhna sungah tungkha, fall into sin) (e:mawhna sungah na ~ hi) (r:26.28.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
tungkhawm = (t:v) (w:arrive together/end up together/come to the same place) (d:tung, arrive, with khawm, together: come to the same place) (e:mun khatah ~ ding uh a) (b:tung) (r:21.3.20) (q:draft)
tungkhin = (t:v) (w:have arrived/have come/have reached) (d:tung, arrive, with khin for an action already completed: has already come or reached) (e:Leitungah khuavak hong ~ napi-in/tu-in a hun hong ~ hita a | the time has now come/note kiang panin Timoti hong ~ a | Timothy has now come from you/keima innsung hong ~ uh ahih manin | because they have come into my house/midang khat a bual sung na ~ pahpah hi | someone else has already got into the pool) (s:tungzo/tungta) (b:tung) (r:43.3.19/43.5.25/52.3.6/1.19.8/43.5.7) (q:draft)
tungkhuh = (t:n) (w:awning/covering) (d:tung, above, with khuh, cover: a cloth cover spread overhead, such as the awning of a ship) (e:kumpi mel puante tawh na ~ kibawl hi) (r:26.27.7) (q:draft)
tungkhuhna = (t:n) (w:covering/roof/canopy) (d:tungkhuh, cover over, with the noun suffix na: what covers something from above, such as the covering of a tent or an overhanging roof) (e:Biakbuk tungah a ~ zal a/tuate mai-ah a ~ khat om hi | in front of them was an overhanging roof) (s:khuhna) (b:tungkhuh) (r:2.40.19/11.7.6) (q:draft)
tungkhum = (t:n) (w:roof) (d:the roof of a house, from tung, top, and khum, roof; inn tungkhum is the roof of the house) (e:inn ~ hongletin) (s:innkhum/khum/innkhumzang) (r:41.2.4) (q:draft)
tungkik = (t:v) (w:return/arrive back/come back) (d:tung, arrive, with kik, again or back: reach a place again, come back to a person, or of a deed or a right, come back upon someone) (e:teembaw tuangin Antiok khua a ~ uh hi/Tua ciangin Jerusalem ~ leuleu uh hi | then they arrived in Jerusalem again/Na naupa hong ~ hi | your brother has come back/kei kiangah hong ~ lo ding a | it will not return to me/ama lu tungah ~ a | it comes back on his own head) (s:ciahkik/paikik) (b:tung) (r:44.14.26/27.4.34/41.11.27/42.15.27/23.55.11/19.7.16) (q:draft)
tungkikin = (t:v) (w:come upon/come back upon) (d:tungkik, come back upon, with the linking ending in: coming upon someone and then, said here of the anger of God) (e:Pasian’ hehna ~ amah in amaute) (b:tungkik) (r:19.78.31) (q:draft, low confidence)
tungkiksak = (t:v) (w:bring back upon/make return upon) (d:tungkik, come back upon, with the causative sak: make a wrong fall back on the one who did it) (e:ama lu tung mahah ~ hi) (s:tungsakkik) (b:tungkik) (r:9.25.39) (q:draft)
tungkim = (t:v) (w:come upon all/reach everyone) (d:tung, come upon, with kim, all alike: come upon every one of a group) (e:ka hehna ~ ding ahih manin) (r:26.7.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
tunglam = (t:adv) (w:above) (d:the upper side or the direction above, opposite of nuailam; tunglam panin is from above, and tunglam mi is one who is from above) (e:Kei in ~ mi ka hi hi/~ panin thuman zusak unla | rain down righteousness from above/~ panin a kingah pilna | the wisdom that comes from above/~ vantung leh leitung a sam hi | he summons the heavens above and the earth) (a:nuai/nuailam) (r:43.8.23/19.50.4/23.45.8/59.3.17)
tunglamah = (t:adv) (w:up on/on the upper part) (d:tunglam, the upper side, with the place marker ah; mual tunglamah is up on the mountainside) (e:mual ~ a paito hi) (b:tunglam) (r:40.14.23) (q:draft)
tungman = (t:n) (w:clay/baked clay) (d:clay or earthenware as a material, what a potter works and what is baked hard; often named beside sik, iron, and tungman peek is a clay tablet for writing on) (e:kote ~ bang hi-in/khenkhat sik leh khenkhat ~ kigawm ahi hi | partly iron and partly clay mixed together/Sik leh ~ kigawm na muh mah bangin | just as you saw iron mixed with clay/sik leh ~ kigawm milim khete | the statue’s feet of iron and clay mixed) (r:23.64.8/27.2.33/27.2.43/27.2.34) (q:draft)
tungnak = (t:v) (w:pant/gasp) (d:breathe hard with the mouth open, as a woman in labour does) (e:ka kam ka-in ka ~ ding hi) (s:husam) (r:23.42.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
tungnun = (t:see) <tungnun'na>
tungnun'na = (t:n) (w:distinction/being set above) (d:what sets someone above or apart from others; spelling of tungnunna in the 1932 text) (e:kote ka ~ uh in | what sets us apart) (r:2.33.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
tungnung = (t:adj) (w:upper/higher/upstairs) (d:the one above or on top, opposite of nuainung, lower: an upper room, gate, millstone or town) (e:Inn dei ~ kote kikhopna-ah/an gawina suangpeek ~ | an upper millstone/biakinn kulh kongpi ~ lam a | he built the upper gate of the temple/Bethhoron nuainung leh a ~ | Lower and Upper Beth Horon) (a:nuainung) (r:44.20.8/13.7.24/7.9.53/14.27.3) (q:draft)
tungnunga = (t:adj) (w:upper/in the upper) (d:tungnung upper with the marker a: that is in the upper part) (e:a Kongpi Thak tumna gei, a dei ~ | in the upper room by the entrance of the New Gate) (b:tungnung) (r:24.36.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
tungnungah = (t:adj) (w:upper/upstairs) (d:tungnung, upper, with the place marker ah: in or on the upper, said of a room or floor) (e:inndei ~ a sial uh hi/inn dawl ~ kahto kikin | going back up to the upper floor/inn dawl ~ Jerusalem lam a nga tawlet thum | on the upper floor, three windows facing Jerusalem/inndei ~ a na paipihto pah uh | they took him straight up to the upstairs room/A cial ~ a om inndeite | the rooms on the upper level) (b:tungnung) (r:44.9.37/44.20.11/27.6.10/44.9.39/26.42.5) (q:draft)
tungnungte = (t:n) (w:upper parts/upper ones/upper rooms) (d:tungnung, upper, with the plural te; after a noun, the upper ones: tuikhuk tungnungte is the upper springs, and inn dawl tungnungte the upper rooms) (e:tuikhuk ~ leh tuikhuk nuainungte a pia hi/a inn dawl ~ kham tawh zut hi | he overlaid the upper rooms with gold/Gihon tui ~ khaktanin | blocking the upper outlet of the Gihon spring/cik tui ~ leh cik tui nuainungte | the upper springs and the lower springs) (a:nuainungte) (b:tungnung) (r:7.1.15/14.3.9/14.32.30/6.15.19) (q:draft)
tungnunna = (t:n) (w:distinction/being set above) (d:what sets someone above or apart from others) (e:nangma mite ka ~ uh pen) (r:2.33.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
tungpah = (t:v) (w:arrive at once/reach immediately) (d:tung, arrive, with pah, at once: reach a place straight away) (e:pai nading mun uh a ~ uh hi) (r:43.6.21) (q:draft)
tungpan = (t:prep) (w:from/from upon) (d:tung upon with pan from, written as one word) (e:mual siang ~ na hehna na lakhia in) (r:27.9.16) (q:draft)
tungpanin = (t:prep) (w:from) (d:tungpan with the ending in; after a possessor, from that person) (e:Hit mite' ~ a kilei ahi hi) (b:tungpan) (r:1.49.32) (q:draft)
tungsa = (t:adj) (w:happened/come upon/befallen) (d:tung arrive, come upon, with sa already done: that has come upon someone) (e:tungah hong ~ thu khempeuh ah/na tungah hong ~ siatna khempeuh sangin | than all the calamities that have come upon you) (b:tung) (r:16.9.33/10.19.7) (q:draft)
tungsak = (t:v) (w:establish/bring upon/bring about/cause to come) (d:tung, arrive, with the causative sak: make something come upon someone, as disaster, sickness or blessing, or make a thing come about) (e:note tungah hong ~ kik ding hi/kote tungah na thupha hong ~ inla | let your blessing come upon us/Anathoth khua mite tungah siatna ~ a | I will bring disaster on the people of Anathoth/gamtate tungah siatna leh gimna ~ hi | he brings ruin and trouble on those who do wrong/deih luatna in hih thu hong ~ ding hi | his zeal will bring this about) (b:tung) (r:5.28.60/18.31.3/19.90.17/24.11.23/23.9.7)
tungsakin = (t:v) (w:bring upon/send upon/cause to come) (d:tungsak with the linking ending in: bringing a thing such as famine, plague or war upon a land, followed by a further action) (e:Tua gamah pulpi ~/Tua gam sungah gal ~ | bringing war on that land/Amah in leitungah kialpi ~ | he brought famine on the land/Egypt tungah gimna ~ | bringing affliction on Egypt) (b:tungsak) (r:26.14.19/19.105.16/26.14.17/2.7.5) (q:draft)
tungsakkik = (t:v) (w:bring back upon/bring upon again) (d:tungsak, bring upon, with kik, back or again: make a wrong fall back on the one who did it, or bring a thing on someone again) (e:ama lu tung mahah ~ ding hi/Egypt natnate note’ tungah hong ~ ding a | he will bring the diseases of Egypt on you again) (s:tungkiksak) (b:tungsak) (r:11.2.32/5.28.60) (q:draft)
tungsakkikin = (t:v) (w:bring back upon/repay) (d:tungsakkik with the linking ending in: making wrongs come back on those who did them) (e:amau’ tung mahah ~) (b:tungsakkik) (r:19.94.23) (q:draft)
tungsakpa = (t:n) (w:one who fulfills/one who brings about) (d:tungsak make come about, with pa for a male doer: he who has made the promise come true) (e:ka pa David tungah a ~ na hi hi) (b:tungsak) (r:14.6.15) (q:draft)
tungsakte = (t:n) (w:those who receive/hosts) (d:tungsak, let arrive, with the plural te: those who take a traveller into their house) (e:a inn-ah hong ~’ inn mahah om paisuak un | stay on in the house of those who take you in) (b:tungsak) (r:42.9.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
tungsakzo = (t:v) (w:be able to bring about/be able to fulfil/have brought upon) (d:tungsak bring about with zo, be able, finish; in Malachi 2:2 said of a curse already brought) (e:Pasian in a thuciamsa ~ taktak ding hi/uh tungah samsiatna ka ~ hi | I have already brought a curse on them) (b:tungsak) (r:45.4.21/39.2.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
tungsan = (t:prep) (w:above/right over) (d:above, directly over: ama omna tungsan innkhum is the roof above the place where he was) (e:ama omna ~ innkhum a vuhlet) (s:tungah) (r:41.2.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
tungsiah = (t:adv) (w:upward/and above/or more) (d:from a stated age or number upward, usually after panin or pan: kum sawmnih panin a tungsiah is twenty years old or more) (e:kum sawmnih panin a ~ peuhmah/kha khat panin a ~ pasal peuhmah | every male a month old or more/kum sawmthum panin a ~ teng kisim a | those thirty years old or more were counted/Pasal khempeuh kha khat pan ~ | all the males a month old or more) (a:nuaisiah) (r:2.30.14/4.3.22/4.3.34/13.23.3/4.3.28) (q:draft)
tungsiahte = (t:n) (w:those above/those older) (d:tungsiah upward with the plural te: the people from a stated age upward) (e:Kum sawmguk pan a ~ pen/Levi mi kum sawmnih leh a ~ | the Levites twenty years old and above) (b:tungsiah) (r:3.27.7/14.31.17) (q:draft)
tungsilh = (t:n) (w:outer garment/garment) (d:tung, over, with silh, wear: a garment worn on top of the others) (e:naipuan ~ kong silhsak hi/puanak ~ guak tawh tuili sungah a tuaksuk hi | with only his outer garment on he jumped into the lake) (s:puantungsilh) (r:26.16.10/43.21.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
tungsuk = (t:v) (w:come down to/go down to/reach down to) (d:tung, arrive, with suk for movement downward: come down to a place or down upon someone) (e:Kaisaria khua-ah hong ~ uh a/ama thu manlangin leitung hong ~ hi | his word comes swiftly down to the earth/keima kiangah hong ~ hi | it came down to where I was/mite khempeuh tungah Kha Siangtho hong ~ hi | the Holy Spirit came down on all the people/tua huan sungah ~ hi | they reach down into that garden) (a:tungto) (b:tung) (r:44.24.1/19.147.15/44.11.5/44.10.44/22.4.15) (q:draft)
tungta = (t:v) (w:has arrived/has come) (d:tung, arrive, with ta, showing that the time or event has now come; common in hun hong tungta, the time has come) (e:A beina hong ~ hi/Siatna ding hun hong ~ hi | the time of disaster has come/tu-in na hun hong ~ hi | now your time has come/a daantuah nading uh hun ~ ahih manin | because the time of their punishment has come/pianzia a ngah ding hun hong ~ hi | the hour has come for him to receive glory) (s:tungzo/tungkhin) (b:tung) (r:26.7.6/26.7.10/26.22.3/26.21.29/43.12.23) (q:draft)
tungtang = (t:n) (w:matter/concern) (d:the matter that concerns someone or something; with ah after a noun or pronoun it means concerning, over, about: kei tungtang ah is over me) (e:kei ~ ah lungdam kei un/tua ~-ah zong amaute kitawng uh hi | they quarreled over that one too) (r:33.7.8/1.26.21) (q:draft)
tungtangah = (t:prep) (w:concerning/about/over/because of) (d:tungtang, matter, with the place marker ah, placed after the noun: in the matter of, over, because of) (e:tua ~ amaute kitawng lo uh hi/Korah’ ~ a site sim loh | not counting those who died because of Korah/hih ~ na thupiakna khat zong ka khial kei | in this matter I have not broken one of your commands/tua ~ zong amaute kitawng leuleu uh hi | over that one too they quarreled again) (s:tungtangin) (b:tungtang) (r:1.26.22/4.16.49/5.26.13/1.26.21) (q:draft)
tungtangin = (t:prep) (w:concerning/in connection with) (d:tungtang, matter, with the ending in, placed after the noun; tua tungtangin is in that connection) (e:tua ~ a kamtai pa in) (s:tungtangah) (b:tungtang) (r:16.6.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
tungtawn = (t:prep) (w:through/by means of) (d:placed after a noun, through or by means of: upna tungtawn is through faith) (e:Khazih Zeisu sunga upna ~ a) (r:55.3.14) (q:draft)
tungtawnin = (t:prep) (w:through/by means of) (d:placed after the noun or a possessor, through, by the agency of a person: Moses tungtawnin is through Moses) (e:Pasian in Paul’ ~ nalamdang lianpipi/Topa in Malakhi ~ Israel-te tungah thu gen hi | the Lord spoke to Israel through Malachi/Elijah’ ~ Topa’ thugen bangin | according to the word of the Lord spoken through Elijah/Moses ~ Topa in a piak thupiaknate | the commands the Lord gave through Moses/kamsangte ahi a nasemte’ ~ gen a | he spoke through his servants the prophets) (s:tawnin) (r:44.19.11/39.1.1/11.17.16/4.36.13/12.21.10) (q:draft)
tungte = (t:n) (w:tops/heights) (d:plural of tung in the sense top or upper surface; mual tungte ah is on the mountains) (e:Israel mual ~ ah a hawkna/mual ~ ah gamlumna | a noise on the mountains/Israel mual ~ gamkhing suak ding | the mountains of Israel will become desolate) (b:tung) (r:26.19.9/23.13.4/26.33.28) (q:draft)
tungte = (t:n) (w:arrivals/those who arrive) (d:tung arrive with te, the people who arrive or have come) (e:gal sung panin hong ~’ lang khatah pang a) (b:tung) (r:14.28.12) (q:draft)
tungteng = (t:n) (w:every top/all the tops) (d:tung top with teng all; mual sang tungteng is on every high hill) (e:mual sang ~, mual dawnzangteng) (b:tung) (r:26.6.13) (q:draft)
tungtham = (t:n) (w:surface/outside/outward show) (d:what is only on the top or outside and not within; tungtham bek-a thugenna is talk that is only on the surface, flattery) (e:~ bek-a thugenna in siatna bek piangsak hi/a ~ bek muhna tawh thu khen lo ding | he will not judge only by what appears on the surface/~-a phatna sangin | rather than praise that is only on the surface/a ~ buan tawh na zut uh hi | you smear its surface with whitewash) (r:20.26.28/26.13.10/23.11.3/20.28.23) (q:draft)
tungthama = (t:adj) (w:outward/superficial/on the surface) (d:tungtham surface with the marker a: that is only on the outside; tungthama phatna is flattery, a tungthama kimu nate outward appearances) (e:A ~ kimu nate siksanin/~ phatna sangin | rather than flattering praise/A ~ a hoihin a kilangkhem note’ thu | about you who outwardly make yourselves look good) (s:puatham) (b:tungtham) (r:43.7.24/20.28.23/41.7.6) (q:draft)
tungthamah = (t:adv) (w:outwardly/on the surface) (d:tungtham surface with the place marker ah; a tungthamah, on the outside) (e:Amaute in a ~ tuu lim hong pua-in/~ a kimu theiteng na siksankha thei uh hi | you tend to rely on what can be seen on the surface) (s:tungthamin) (b:tungtham) (r:40.7.15/47.10.7) (q:draft)
tungthamin = (t:adv) (w:outwardly/on the surface) (d:tungtham the outside, with the adverb ending in: looking only at the surface) (e:a ~ i et ciangin) (s:tungthamah) (b:tungtham) (r:51.2.23) (q:draft)
tungthamun = (t:adv) (w:outwardly) (d:tungtham the outside, with un for plural you: in your outward show, of hypocrites) (e:Na ~ mihoih a kineihkhem mite aw) (b:tungtham) (r:40.15.7) (q:draft)
tungto = (t:v) (w:come up/go up/arrive up) (d:tung arrive with to upward: reach a place by going up) (e:Babylon panin hong ~ hi/Jerusalem-ah Ezra tawh ~ uh hi | they came up to Jerusalem with Ezra/Pasian mai-ah ~ hi | it went up before God) (a:tungsuk) (b:tung) (r:15.7.6/66.8.4/15.7.7) (q:draft)
tungtuan = (t:see) <tungtuan'na>
tungtuan'na = (t:n) (w:excellence/pre-eminence) (d:being above others, with the noun suffix na; see tungtuang, excel) (e:vangliatna ah ka ~ na hi hi | you are my excellence in power) (r:1.49.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
tungtuang = (t:v) (w:excel/be foremost) (d:be above others) (e:na ~ kei ding hi) (r:1.49.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
tunguh = (t:prep) (w:on them/upon them) (d:tung upon with plural uh written as one word; a tunguh ah is on them) (e:a ~ ah a khut uh a ngak) (b:tung) (r:44.13.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
tungun = (t:conj) (w:when/as soon as) (d:tung, at the moment of, after a verb, with the plural marker un: when they did so) (e:Job a muh ~ amah thei pah lo uh hi) (r:18.2.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
tungvat = (t:v) (w:come suddenly/arrive suddenly) (d:tung arrive, come upon, with vat suddenly) (e:amaute tungah siatna hong ~ ding hi/huihpi nung bangin huging khat hong ~ a | a sound like a violent wind suddenly came/siatna na tungah hong ~ ding hi | disaster will suddenly come upon you) (r:52.5.3/44.2.2/23.47.11) (q:draft)
tungzang = (t:n) (w:top/upper surface/outside) (d:the top or outer side of a thing) (e:Amah in a ~, a kimkota a pangte/a ~ a om a khuhna tuuvun | the leather covering that is on the outside of it) (r:2.37.26/4.4.25) (q:draft, low confidence)
tungzangah = (t:prep) (w:on top of/above) (d:tungzang the top side, with the place marker ah) (e:Tua kuum ~, sapfaia suangmanpha tawh) (s:tungah) (b:tungzang) (r:26.1.26) (q:draft)
tungzaw = (t:v) (w:come upon instead/fall on rather) (d:tung come upon with zaw rather, instead) (e:migilote tungah lungkhamna ~ hi/na galte tungah ~ hen | may it come upon your enemies instead) (b:tung) (r:20.11.8/27.4.19) (q:draft)
tungzo = (t:v) (w:have come/have arrived) (d:tung arrive with zo marking completion: has already come, of people, a time or an event) (e:a thukhen ding hun a ~ hi/kumpipa’ tapate hong ~ hi | the king’s sons have come/sih ding launate kei tungah hong ~ hi | the terrors of death have come upon me/tu nitakin hih lai-ah hong ~ hi | they have come here tonight/a thuak ni ding uh hong ~ ta | the day for them to suffer has come) (s:tungkhin/tungta) (b:tung) (r:66.14.7/6.2.2/10.13.35/19.55.4/24.50.27) (q:draft)
tuni = (t:n) (w:today) (d:this day, from tu, this, and ni, day; with the time marker in it means today, and tuni dongin is to this day) (e:~-in hih inn sungah gupna a tung hi/zanni, ~, atawntungin kikheel loin a om hi | he is the same yesterday, today and forever/~ dongin ka om a | I stand to this day/~ in nang kong piang sak khin zo hi | today I have become your father) (r:42.19.9/58.13.8/44.26.22/19.2.7)
Tuni = (t:see) <Tuni-in>
Tuni-in = (t:adv) (w:today/this day) (d:tuni, today, with the time marker in, written with a capital at the start of a sentence) (e:~ na Pa ka suak zo hi/~ nangma innah kong taam ding hi | today I must stay at your house/~ aak a khuan’ ma-in | today before the rooster crows/~ note in ama aw na zak uh leh | today if you hear his voice) (r:58.1.5/42.19.5/42.22.61/58.4.7) (q:draft)
tunin = (t:v) (w:wrapping/wrapped/bundling) (d:tun, wrap in a cloth or cover, with the linking ending in, joining it to the next verb: wrapping a thing and then; not the tun that means arrive) (e:puan a dum khat tawh ~/puan tawh ~ gan annekna kuang sungah a sial | she wrapped him in cloths and laid him in a manger/Ka dial ah ~ ka kepsa na sum | your money that I kept wrapped in my cloth/puan tawh ~ a liangko uh-ah pua uh hi | they carried them on their shoulders wrapped in cloth) (s:tuamin) (b:tun) (r:4.4.12/42.19.20/42.2.7/2.12.34) (q:draft)
tunitak = (t:adv) (w:tonight/this evening) (d:tu, this, with nitak, evening: this very evening) (e:~ mahmahin pasal nei-in) (s:tuzan) (r:8.1.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
tunkhak = (t:v) (w:happen to come/end up in) (d:tun arrive with khak, happen to: come to a place or state, usually an unwanted one) (e:thumang loin i ~ ding a lauhuai/hih lai munah hong ~ loh teitei nadingun | so that they will by no means come to this place) (r:58.10.31/42.16.28) (q:draft, low confidence)
tunkhit = (t:v) (w:have arrived/have come) (d:tun arrive with khit, finished: after arriving, after it has come) (e:Masedonia gam ka ~ uh ciang/Tua gimna hun a ~ phetin | immediately after that time of distress has come) (r:47.7.5/40.24.29) (q:draft)
tunkhitna = (t:n) (w:arrival/having arrived) (d:tunkhit have arrived with the noun suffix na: the fact that someone or something has arrived; tunkhitna thu is the news that one has come) (e:Keilah-ah David a ~ thu/Hih lai nong ~ thu | the news that you have come here/ka bilah hong ~ hangin | because it has reached my ears) (b:tunkhit) (r:9.23.7/44.21.22/12.19.28) (q:draft)
tunkik = (t:v) (w:return/come back/arrive back) (d:tun arrive with kik again, back) (e:A hong ~ ciangin hoihtakin kiphiat siangin/Nong ~ mateng ka na om ding hi | I will wait until you return/galkap bupa inn-ah hong ~ ciangin | when they returned to the centurion’s house/a sanggamte uh kiangah hong ~ uh ciangin | when they came back to their brothers) (s:ciahkik/paikik) (b:tun) (r:42.11.25/42.7.10/7.6.18/7.18.8) (q:draft)
tunkim = (t:v) (w:all arrive/reach everywhere) (d:tun arrive with kim, all, complete: of people, all reach; of famine, reach every part) (e:Leilak ka ~ khit uh ciangin/gam khempeuhah kialpi a ~ ciangin | when the famine had spread over the whole land) (r:44.28.1/1.41.56) (q:draft, low confidence)
tunkuan = (t:v) (w:be about to arrive/come near) (d:tun arrive with kuan, on the point of: just before reaching a place) (e:Jerusalem khua a ~) (r:42.19.37) (q:draft, low confidence)
tunlam = (t:n) (w:arrival/time of coming) (d:tun arrive with lam, the fact or manner of: that or when someone arrives) (e:ka hong ~ nangawn na thei kei) (r:66.3.3) (q:draft)
tunma = (t:adv) (w:before coming/before arriving) (d:tun, arrive, with ma, before, usually followed by the time marker in: hong tunma-in is before someone or something came) (e:tua khua-ah a hong ~-in Peter in/Phalbi ~-in nong pai theih nadingin | so that you can come before winter/Hih lai mun hong ~-in | before he gets here/upna thu hong ~ hun sungteng | all the time before faith came) (r:48.2.12/44.2.20/55.4.21/44.23.15/48.3.23) (q:draft)
tunna = (t:n) (w:arrival/coming) (d:tun, arrive, with the noun suffix na: the arriving of someone or something, or the place it reaches; a tunna ding hun is the time for it to come about, and tunna lampi the way that leads to a place) (e:Hih thu a ~ ding hun/Titus hong ~ tawh kote hong thakhauhsak hi | he strengthened us by the coming of Titus/Kumpipa’ thupiakna a ~ gam | the province that the king’s order reached/khuapi ~ lampi mu zo lo uh hi | they could not find the way to a city) (b:tun) (r:35.2.3/17.4.3/47.7.6/19.107.4) (q:draft)
tunna = (t:n) (w:wrapping/covering) (d:tun, wrap, with the noun suffix na: what a thing is wrapped in; lu tunna puan is the cloth wrapped around the head) (e:a lu ~ puan tawh omkhawm loin/A luang ~ puan mu a | he saw the cloths that had wrapped the body) (s:tuamna) (r:43.20.7/43.20.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
tunnasa = (t:n) (w:place already reached) (d:tunna arriving, with sa already done; a tunnasa munte are the places it has come to) (e:Thuciamna Singkuang a ~ munte a siangtho) (b:tunna) (r:14.8.11) (q:draft)
tunni = (t:n) (w:day of arrival) (d:tun arrive with ni day; a tunni zanin is on the night of the day he arrived) (e:Troas khua-ah a ~ zanin) (b:tun) (r:44.16.9) (q:draft)
tunphetin = (t:adv) (w:as soon as he arrived/on arriving) (d:tun arrive with phetin as soon as) (e:Jesuh a ~ tua nu’ natna thu) (r:41.1.30) (q:draft)
tunpi = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:hornet) (d:a large stinging insect, called a kind of khuaipi in Deuteronomy 7:20) (e:mai-ah ~ ka sawl ding hi/amaute’ lakah ~ khah ding hi | he will send the hornet among them) (r:2.23.28/5.7.20) (q:draft)
tunpih = (t:v) (w:bring/bring to/lead to) (d:tun, arrive, with pih, together with: bring or lead someone to a place or into a state) (e:amaute paikhiatpihin gamlak ka ~ a/ama vantung gamah muanhuai takin hong ~ ding hi | he will bring me safely to his heavenly kingdom/thongkia mite nopsakna munah a ~ hi | he brings the prisoners to a place of joy/Israel mualtung gamah kong ~ ding hi | I will bring you to the mountains of Israel/a lawmte zol a, lungkhamna sung ~ hi | he entices his friends and leads them into trouble) (s:paipih) (b:tun) (r:26.20.10/1.8.11/55.4.18/19.68.6/26.39.2/20.16.29) (q:draft)
tunpihin = (t:v) (w:bringing/bringing to/having brought) (d:tunpih bring to a place, with the linking ending in: brought and then) (e:Amah in hih mun hong ~/Jabesh-ah ~ tua lai-ah a hal uh hi | they brought them to Jabesh and burned them there/a siahuaizaw dawi sagih hong ~ | bringing seven spirits more wicked than itself) (b:tunpih) (r:5.26.9/9.31.12/40.12.45) (q:draft)
tunpihkik = (t:v) (w:bring back/lead back) (d:tunpih, bring to a place, with kik, back: bring someone back to a place or a person) (e:Jerusalem khua sungah ka ~ ding hi/amau’ Topa Pasian’ kiangah ~ ding hi | he will bring them back to the Lord their God/Israel gam kong ~ ding hi | I will bring you back to the land of Israel/A pa’ kiang a ~ theih nadingin | so that he could bring him back to his father/amaute’ leitangah ka ~ ding hi | I will bring them back to their own land) (s:ciahpihkik) (b:tunpih) (r:38.8.8/42.1.16/26.37.12/1.37.22/26.34.13) (q:draft)
tunpihna = (t:n) (w:bringing/leading to) (d:tunpih bring to a place, with the noun suffix na; nong tunpihna is your bringing me) (e:hih ciang dong kei nong ~) (b:tunpih) (r:13.17.16) (q:draft)
tunpihsuk = (t:v) (w:bring down) (d:tunpih, bring to a place, with suk, downward) (e:i kiangah hong ~ uh a) (s:paipihsuk) (b:tunpih) (r:5.1.25) (q:draft)
tunpite = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:hornets) (d:plural of tunpi) (e:~ keimah in note mai-ah ka sawl hi) (b:tunpi) (r:6.24.12) (q:draft)
tunsa = (t:see) <tunsa-in>
tunsa-in = (t:adv) (w:covered/wrapped) (d:tun wrap with sa, already done, and the ending in; mit tunsa-in, with the eyes covered) (e:mit ~ khuamial lakah paikhia in) (s:tuamsa-in) (r:26.12.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
tunsak = (t:v) (w:bring upon/cause to come) (d:tun, arrive, with the causative sak: make something, usually disaster or sickness, come upon someone) (e:a ~ ding siatna tungsak nawn lo hi/amaute tungah siatna ~ ding ka ngaihsun a | I planned to bring disaster on them/Egypt mite’ tungah ka ~ natnate | the diseases I brought on the Egyptians/Faro’ tungah a ~ uiphukte | the frogs he had brought on Pharaoh/hih mun tungah ka ~ ding siatna khempeuh | all the disaster I will bring on this place) (b:tun) (r:2.32.14/38.8.14/2.15.26/2.8.12/12.22.20) (q:draft)
tunsak = (t:v) (w:fulfil/carry out/bring about) (d:make a vow or a promise come true; thuciamna tunsak is fulfil a vow) (e:Na thuciamna bangin na ~ loh ding sangin/a thuciamna a ~ ding a nai kuan ciangin | as the time drew near for him to fulfil his promise/thuciamna ~ nadingin | to fulfil a vow/David a dingin ka ~ kei taak leh | if I do not carry it out for David/a ciamsa thu a ~ theih nadingin | so that he may bring about what he has promised) (s:tangtunsak) (b:tun) (r:21.5.5/44.7.17/4.15.3/10.3.9/1.18.19) (q:draft)
tunsakin = (t:v) (w:cover/blindfold) (d:tun wrap, cover, with the causative sak and the linking ending in; mai tunsak is cover the face) (e:a mai ~ beeng uh a) (r:41.14.65) (q:draft)
tunsakkik = (t:v) (w:bind up again/bind up) (d:of wounds: tun wrap with sak and kik, again or back) (e:i liammate hong ~ ding hi lo ahi hiam) (s:tuamsak) (r:28.6.1) (q:draft, low confidence)
tunsakkik = (t:v) (w:bring again/cause to come again) (d:tunsak cause to come with kik again) (e:tuiciin ka ~ ngei nawn loh nadingin) (b:tunsak) (r:1.9.11) (q:draft)
tunsakna = (t:n) (w:fulfilment/bringing about) (d:tunsak, cause to arrive, with the noun suffix na: the bringing about of something; thuciamna tunsakna is the fulfilling of a vow) (e:thuciamna ~ a piak dingin/thuciamna ~-in biakpiak nading ahi a | or as a sacrifice in fulfilment of a vow/hoihna le hauhna ka ~ thu | the news of the good and the prosperity I bring/note tungah siatna ~ | bringing ruin on you) (s:tangtunna) (b:tunsak) (r:3.22.23/24.33.9/4.15.8/5.28.63) (q:draft)
tunsaknop = (t:v) (w:be willing to receive/be willing to welcome) (d:tunsak, let arrive, take in as a guest, with nop, want to) (e:note hong ~ kei leh/innsunga mite in note hong ~ leh | if the people of the house are willing to receive you) (r:42.10.10/40.10.14/40.10.13) (q:draft)
tunsate = (t:n) (w:those wrapped up/things tucked away) (d:tun, wrap up or tuck in, with sa, already done, and the plural te: the things already tucked away, here the hairs kept in the fold of the garment) (e:na ~ sung panin) (r:26.5.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
tunsuk = (t:v) (w:come down/arrive down) (d:tun, arrive, with suk, downward: come down and arrive, as from a mountain) (e:Moses hong ~ hakna mite in) (s:kumsuk/paisuk) (a:tungto) (b:tun) (r:2.32.1) (q:draft)
tuntheih = (t:v) (w:be fulfilled/come to pass) (d:tun, arrive or come to pass, with theih, can: a tuntheih nadingin means so that it might be fulfilled, said of a word of Scripture or a prophecy) (e:a genna thu a ~ nadingin/Lai Siangtho sungah a kigelh thu a ~ nadingin | so that what is written in Scripture might be fulfilled/kamsangte’ thugente a ~ nadingin | so that the words of the prophets might be fulfilled/ama thugente a ~ nadingin | so that his words might be fulfilled) (s:tangtung) (b:tun) (r:43.19.36/43.18.32/43.19.28/40.26.56/66.17.17) (q:draft)
tuntheih = (t:v) (w:be able to reach/can arrive/come upon) (d:tun, arrive, with theih, can: be able to get to a place; of a blessing or a punishment, be able to come upon someone) (e:Ka pai nading mun ~ nading lampi/hong pai peuhpeuh ciangin a ~ nadingin | so that he can come in whenever he comes/Israel mite’ inn sungah ka thupha a ~ nadingin | so that my blessing may come on the house of Israel/Shekhem mite tungah thukkikna hong ~ nadingin | so that vengeance might come on the men of Shechem) (s:tunzo/batzawh) (b:tun) (r:43.14.4/12.4.10/26.44.30/7.9.24) (q:draft)
tuntom = (t:adj) (w:short) (d:short in height, said of a person: mi tuntom is a short man) (e:amah mi ~ khat ahih manin) (s:tom) (a:sang) (r:42.19.3) (q:draft)
tunu = (t:n) (w:granddaughter) (d:tu, grandchild, with nu, female: the daughter of one’s son or daughter) (e:Israel kumpi Omri’ ~ ahi hi/Mezahab’ ~ hi a, Matred’ tanu ahi hi | granddaughter of Me-Zahab and daughter of Matred) (r:12.8.26/13.1.50) (q:draft)
tunuam = (t:v) (w:like to sit/love to sit/want to sit) (d:tu, sit, with nuam, want or like: be fond of sitting in a certain place, as in the seats of honour) (e:uliante’ tutna mun hoihte bekah ~ uh hi/tutphah nuampen ah na ~ uh a | you love to sit in the best seats/tutphah nuamte tungah ~ uh a | they like to sit on the best seats/uliante’ tutna dinga a kibawl munah ~ se uh a | they love to sit in the places made for the great) (r:42.20.46/41.12.39/42.11.43/40.23.6) (q:draft)
tunung = (t:adv) (w:hereafter/in the future/from now on) (d:the time after now, usually as tunung ciangin, in time to come, from now on) (e:~ ciangin a hong piang ding khuapi/~ ciangin zong hong gum ding hi | he will deliver us in the future too/~ ciangin zong ka lung a dam lai ding | I will go on rejoicing in time to come/~ ciangin Mihing Tapa in Vanglian Pa’ ziat lamah | from now on the Son of Man at the right hand of the Mighty One) (s:Mailamah/nungcianga) (a:nidang/nidangin/tumasiah) (r:58.13.14/40.26.64/47.1.11/50.1.18) (q:draft)
tunvat = (t:v) (w:come suddenly/arrive unexpectedly) (d:tun, arrive, with vat, suddenly: come upon someone without warning) (e:tua Ni hong ~ ciangin) (s:tungvat) (r:52.5.4) (q:draft)
tunzaw = (t:v) (w:succeed more/do better/get further ahead) (d:tun, arrive, with zaw, more: in the phrase ma tunzaw, get further ahead, be more successful than others) (e:David in a maa ~ hi) (r:9.18.30) (q:draft, low confidence)
tunzawh = (t:v) (w:have arrived/manage to reach) (d:tun, arrive, with zawh, the form of zo, finish or be able: tunzawh ni thum ciangin is three days after arriving, and tunzawh nading is so as to manage to reach) (e:Festas hong ~ ni thum ciangin/A ~ ni thum khit ciangin | three days after he arrived/Foenik teembaw khawlna ciang ~ nading hanciam ding | to try to reach the harbour of Phoenix) (s:tunkhit) (r:44.25.1/44.27.12/44.28.17) (q:draft)
tunzo = (t:v) (w:be able to reach/attain) (d:tun, reach, with zo, be able: na ma na tunzo ding is you will reach what lies before you, you will succeed) (e:na ma na ~ ding hi) (s:batzawh/tuntheih) (b:tun) (r:38.4.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
tup = (t:v) (w:intend/aim/purpose) (d:set the mind on something: tup lohpi is without meaning to, unintentionally, and a tup is what a person aims at) (e:~ lohpi leh theih lohna hangin/ka ngim ka ~ thute na hong zui hi | you have followed my aims and purposes/Thadahte, a ~ tung ngei lo a | the lazy never reach what they aim at/A tawntungin keima ~ thu in | it has always been my aim) (s:ngim) (r:26.45.20/20.12.27/55.3.10/45.15.20) (q:draft)
tup = (t:v) (w:knock/strike/hit) (d:strike, knock: a ha a tup khiat, with khiat, out, is knock out his tooth) (e:a ha a ~ khiat leh) (s:sat) (r:2.21.27) (q:draft, low confidence)
tupa = (t:n) (w:grandson) (d:tu, grandchild, with pa, male: the son of one’s son or daughter) (e:tapa sawmli leh ~ sawmthum nei hi/tapa tampi leh ~ tampi a neite | men who had many sons and grandsons/a tapa leh a ~’ na a sepsak ding | they will serve his son and his grandson/na topa’ ~’ tungah ka pia khin hi | I have given it to your master’s grandson) (b:tu) (r:7.12.14/24.36.11/13.8.40/24.27.7/10.9.9) (q:draft)
tupa = (t:n) (w:one who sits/the one seated/the one enthroned) (d:tu, sit, with pa, the male agent suffix: he who sits or is enthroned, written a tupa) (e:Kherubte tunga a ~ aw/Vantunga a ~ in amaute na nuihsan a | the One enthroned in heaven laughs at them/thukhen a, a ~ tungah thutang lungsim guan ding a | he will give a spirit of justice to the one who sits in judgment/Sabuai ah a ~ lianzaw hilo ahi hiam | is not the one who sits at the table greater) (b:tu) (r:23.37.16/23.28.6/19.2.4/42.22.27) (q:draft)
tupate = (t:n) (w:grandsons) (d:tupa, grandson, with the plural te; the NIV has the singular here) (e:na tapa leh na ~ in zong) (b:tupa) (r:7.8.22) (q:draft)
tupcip = (t:v) (w:engulf/overwhelm/sweep away) (d:of flood water, close over people and cover them completely; cip adds the sense of tightly or completely) (e:tui in mi khempeuh a ~ hun) (s:tumcip/tuumcip) (r:40.24.39) (q:draft, low confidence)
tupeek = (t:n) (w:hoe) (d:a hoe, the hand tool used for digging and breaking up the ground) (e:~ tawh a kikho ngei mual) (r:23.7.25) (q:draft)
tupi = (t:adj) (w:dense/thick) (d:thick, dense, said of forest: gammang tupi is the dense forest) (e:gammang ~ sing teng kiphuk ta hi) (s:sah) (r:38.11.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
tupkhiat = (t:v) (w:knock out) (d:tup, strike, with khiat, out: knock out, said of a tooth) (e:a ha a ~ leh) (s:betkhiatsak) (b:tup) (r:2.21.27) (q:draft)
tupna = (t:n) (w:purpose/aim/goal/intention) (d:tup, aim, with the noun suffix na: what a person sets out to do or reach, a purpose or goal) (e:A lungsim sunga a ~ teng/note upna’ ~ mun na ngah uh hi | you are receiving the goal of your faith/ama ~ hutpih ding na hi uh hiam | are you going to defend his cause) (s:ngimna/geelna) (b:tup) (r:24.30.24/60.1.8/7.6.31) (q:draft)
tupna = (t:n) (w:beating/blow) (d:tup, strike, with the noun suffix na: a blow; it occurs in the pair satna tupna, beatings) (e:satna ~ thuakna, thong sung khumna | suffering beatings, being put in prison/satna ~ kisim zo lo a thuak mi | one who has suffered beatings beyond counting) (s:satna/vuakna) (r:47.6.5/47.11.23) (q:draft, low confidence)
tupsak = (t:v) (w:wring/twist/press hard) (d:said of the nose, pressed, twisted or struck until it bleeds; probably tup, strike, with the causative sak) (e:nak ~ lehang si hong luang a) (r:20.30.33) (q:draft, low confidence)
tuptup = (t:n) (w:the very thing aimed at/just what was wanted) (d:tup, aim, said twice for emphasis: exactly what one was aiming at; i tuptup tung ei is we have got just what we wanted) (e:Ha, i ~ tung ei) (r:19.35.25) (q:draft, low confidence)
tusak = (t:v) (w:seat/make sit/install) (d:tu, sit, with the causative sak: make someone sit down; of a king, set him on the throne) (e:Mihonpi lei tungah ~ un/kumpi tokhom tungah kumpipa ~ uh hi | they seated the king on the royal throne/Zion tungah ka Kumpi ka ~ khin hi | I have installed my King on Zion/a kisam mite lak tutna bul lamah a ~ hi | he seated them at the head of the invited guests/a mial sungah hong ~ hi | he makes me sit in darkness) (s:tutsak) (r:40.15.35/14.23.20/19.2.6/9.9.22/19.143.3) (q:draft)
tusakin = (t:v) (w:bringing down on/making rest on/laying on) (d:tusak, make sit, with the linking ending in: making a deed come down on the head of the one who did it) (e:ama lu tung mah-ah ~ thuk in la) (b:tusak) (r:14.6.23) (q:draft, low confidence)
tusakzaw = (t:v) (w:seat instead/give the seat to) (d:tusak, make sit, with zaw, rather: seat this one in preference to another) (e:Hih lai-ah amah ~ ni) (b:tusak) (r:42.14.9) (q:draft)
tusawn = (t:n) (w:great-grandson/great-grandchild) (d:the generation after tu, grandchild: a great-grandchild, the child of a grandchild) (e:Kushi’ ~ ahi, Shelemiah’ tupa) (r:24.36.14) (q:draft)
tusawng = (t:adv) (w:these days/recently/lately) (d:tusawng tenga means during these last days, in the days just past) (e:~ tenga tua lai-a thupiang) (r:42.24.18) (q:draft, low confidence)
tusawnte = (t:n) (w:great-grandchildren) (d:tusawn, great-grandchild, with the plural te: the children of one’s grandchildren) (e:a ~ dong a mu hi) (b:tusawn) (r:18.42.16) (q:draft)
tusuk = (t:v) (w:sit down) (d:tu, sit, with suk, downward: sit down, take a seat) (e:Boaz paito-in tua mun-ah ~ hi/tua ahih ciangin amaute ~ uh hi | so they sat down/mualtung lamah kahto-in ~ a | he went up on the mountainside and sat down/tokhom om lohna lei lakah hong ~ in | sit on the ground without a throne/Tu mahmahin ~ inla | sit down right now) (s:tucip) (a:tuto/dingto) (r:8.4.1/23.47.1/8.4.2/40.5.1/42.16.6) (q:draft)
tusukin = (t:v) (w:sitting down/sat down) (d:tusuk, sit down, with the linking ending in: sitting down, having sat down) (e:~ ka kap niloh a/Babilon luite gei-ah eite ~ i kapkap hi | by the rivers of Babylon we sat down and wept) (b:tusuk) (r:16.1.4/19.137.1) (q:draft)
tut = (t:v) (w:sit/be seated) (d:the form of tu, sit, used before endings and linking words such as ciangin, khit, lai and nading) (e:kumpi tokhom tungah a ~ khit phetin/Mi liante tawh an nekhawm dingin na ~ ciangin | when you sit down to eat with great men/Amaute sabuai-ah a ~ lai takun | while they were sitting at the table/kongvangneu gei-ah a ~ lai takin lusu-in | dozing as he sat by the window/na inn sung uhah na ~ ciang | when you sit in your house) (a:din) (b:tu) (r:11.16.11/20.23.1/11.13.20/44.20.9/5.6.7) (q:draft)
tutak = (t:v) (w:just now)
tutak = (t:adv) (w:at the moment/at present/just now/right now/at the present time) (d:tu, now, with tak, exactly: at this very moment) (s:tumahin/tadihin)
tutak = (t:adj) (w:now)
tutakin = (t:conj) (w:just now) (d:tutak, just now, with the ending in: at this moment, for the time being) (e:~ anlum mawkmawk ka nei kei hi) (b:tutak) (r:9.21.4)
Tutakin = (t:adv) (w:now/at present/just now) (d:tutakin, at this moment, written with a capital at the start of a sentence) (e:~ anlum mawkmawk ka nei kei hi) (s:tumahin/tadihin) (b:tutakin) (r:9.21.4) (q:draft)
tutding = (t:v) (w:to sit/sitting) (d:tut, sit, with ding, to or for: the act of sitting that is to be; here the sitting at the right hand and the left) (e:ka veilama ~ pen) (b:tut) (r:40.20.23) (q:draft)
tute = (t:n) (w:grandchildren) (d:tu, grandchild, with the plural te: the children of one’s sons and daughters) (e:Na ~ a mu dingin/a ~ leh a tanute namin | he kissed his grandchildren and his daughters/na tate leh na ~’ zakna-ah | in the hearing of your children and grandchildren/a ~ ciang bek hi loin | not only his grandchildren) (r:19.128.6/1.31.55/2.10.1/18.42.16) (q:draft)
tute = (t:n) (w:those sitting/those seated) (d:tu, sit, with the plural te: the ones who sit, written a tute) (e:a ~ lakah a hawmsak hi/sualphah puan hoih tungah a ~ | you who sit on fine saddle blankets/Sihna liim gam sungah a ~ tungah | on those sitting in the land of the shadow of death) (r:43.6.11/7.5.10/40.4.16) (q:draft)
tutkhawm = (t:v) (w:sit together/sit with) (d:tut, sit, with khawm, together: sit down together with others; also of people living together as one) (e:Sabuai-ah amaute tawh a ~ lai takin/a ~ khit uh ciangin | when they had sat down together/sanggam bangin mite pumkhat suakin a ~ ciangin | when people sit together as one like brothers/ka Pa’ tokhomah ka ~ uh mah bangin | just as I sat down with my Father on his throne) (s:tukhawm/tutpih) (b:tut) (r:42.24.30/19.133.1/42.22.55/66.3.21) (q:draft)
tutkhawmpih = (t:v) (w:sit together with) (d:tutkhawm, sit together, with pih, along with: a tutkhawmpih mite are those sitting with him) (e:sabuai-ah a ~ mite in) (s:tutpih) (b:tutkhawm) (r:43.13.28) (q:draft)
tutkho = (t:v) (w:stay up late/sit long) (d:tut, sit, with kho, lasting long: sit on for a long time; nitakin a tutkho mite are those who stay up late at night) (e:nitakin a ~ mite in gimna) (r:23.5.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
tutmawkna = (t:n) (w:idle sitting/idleness) (d:tut, sit, with mawk, aimlessly, and the noun suffix na: sitting about doing nothing) (e:kam bek pau-in ~ pen zawnna ahi hi) (s:ommawkna) (a:thanuamna) (r:20.14.23) (q:draft)
tutna = (t:n) (w:seat/sitting place) (d:tut, sit, with the noun suffix na: a seat, a place or thing to sit on; tutna mun is the place where one sits or dwells) (e:Pawikhamna sungah ~ phabel leh/a ~ mun panin amah hong dakkhia-in | from his dwelling place he looks out/kumpi dangte sangin a sangzaw ~ a pia hi | he gave him a seat higher than the other kings/amau ~ inn a dim sak hi | it filled the house where they were sitting/a ~ panin amah ding to hi | he rose from his seat) (s:tutphah/tokhom) (b:tut) (r:40.23.6/19.33.14/24.52.32/44.2.2/7.3.20) (q:draft)
tutnasa = (t:n) (w:place sat on/thing sat on/former seat) (d:tutna, seat, with sa, already: the thing or place where someone has been sitting) (e:annek sabuai-ah a ~ mun hong zuanin/mipa’ ~ na khatpeuh peuh tungah a tu mi | anyone who sits on anything the man has sat on) (b:tutna) (r:43.13.12/3.15.6) (q:draft)
tutnate = (t:n) (w:seats/benches) (d:tutna, seat, with the plural te: seats, benches) (e:vakhu zuakte’ ~ a lumletsak gawp hi | he overturned the benches of those selling doves) (s:tutphahte) (b:tutna) (r:40.21.12) (q:draft)
tutnopna = (t:n) (w:wish to sit/wanting to sit) (d:tut, sit, with nop, want, and the noun suffix na: the wish to sit somewhere, here the guests wanting the seats of honour) (e:munah a ~ uh a muh ciangin) (r:42.14.7) (q:draft)
tuto = (t:v) (w:sit up/move up/sit higher) (d:tu, sit, with to, upward: sit up from lying down, or come up to sit in a higher place) (e:Misi pa zong hong ~-in hong paupah hi/Lawm aw, a sangah na ~ in | friend, move up to a higher place/hih lai-ah hong ~ in | come up and sit here/Peter a muh ciangin a ~ hi | when she saw Peter she sat up/tu-in ~ inla, ka sa matsa ne in | now sit up and eat my game) (a:tusuk/lumsuk) (r:42.7.15/42.14.10/20.25.7/44.9.40/1.27.19) (q:draft)
tutphah = (t:n) (w:saddle/seat/stool/cushion) (d:tut, sit, with phah, spread: something laid or set to sit on; la tutphah is a donkey’s saddle and nausuahna tutphah the delivery stool) (e:kalaoh ~ sungah koihin/Balaam tho-in a la ~ vawh a | Balaam got up and saddled his donkey/nausuahna ~ tungah a tu na muh uh ciangun | when you see them sitting on the delivery stool/Kikhopna inn sungah ~ nuampen ah | in the best seats in the synagogue) (s:tutna/tutphat) (r:1.31.34/4.22.21/2.1.16/42.11.43) (q:draft)
tutphahte = (t:n) (w:seats/benches) (d:tutphah, seat, with the plural te) (e:vakhu zuakte’ ~ sawnpaih sak hi/dangka kheekte’ sabuaite leh vakhu zuakte’ ~ | the tables of the money changers and the benches of those selling doves) (s:tutnate) (b:tutphah) (r:41.11.15/40.21.12) (q:draft)
tutphat = (t:n) (w:saddle/seat for riding) (d:the thing a rider sits on, a saddle; the other Tedim text has tutphah in this verse) (e:a tutna ~ khatpeuh peuh in) (s:tutphah/tuanna) (r:3.15.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
tutpih = (t:v) (w:sit with/sit together with) (d:tut, sit, with pih, together with: a tutpih mite are those who sit with him) (e:An ne-a a ~ mite khat in/Bernis le a ~ midangte zong | Bernice and the others sitting with them/na ~ pa limtakin en un | look carefully at the man you sit with) (s:tutkhawmpih/tukhawm/tutkhawm) (b:tut) (r:42.14.15/44.26.30/20.23.1) (q:draft)
tutpihpa = (t:n) (w:the man one sits with/table companion) (d:tutpih, sit with, with pa for a man: the man with whom one sits at table) (e:na ~ lim takin en in) (b:tutpih) (r:20.23.1) (q:draft)
tutsak = (t:v) (w:seat/make sit) (d:tut, sit, with the causative sak: give someone a seat, make him sit; ama taklamah a tutsak is seat him at his right hand) (e:ama taklamah a ~ nadingin) (s:tusak) (b:tut) (r:49.1.18) (q:draft)
tutsukna = (t:n) (w:sitting down/staying) (d:tut, sit, with suk, down, and the noun suffix na: sitting down, staying in a place; set beside pusuahna, going out, and sungtumna, coming in) (e:na ~ leh na pusuahna leh) (r:12.19.27) (q:draft)
tutte = (t:n) (w:revenues/things brought in) (d:what merchants and traders bring in or deliver: tut, bring in or deliver, as in kitut, with the plural te; not from tut, sit) (e:sumbawlte leh sumbukte’ ~ a kisim lo) (r:14.9.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
tuttheih = (t:v) (w:be able to bring/be able to deliver) (d:tut, bring or deliver, with theih, can, the form used before nading; not from tut, sit) (e:Lungdamna Thu ka ~ nading/minamte’ hauhna na kiang hong ~ nadingin | so that they can bring you the wealth of the nations) (r:46.9.23/23.60.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
tuttohkik = (t:v) (w:bring back up/lift back) (d:tut, bring, with toh, upward, and kik, back: of the hand, bring it back up from the dish to the mouth) (e:a kam sungah a ~ ding nangawn) (r:20.19.24) (q:draft, low confidence)
tutu = (t:v) (w:keep sitting/sit on and on) (d:tu, sit, said twice to show that the sitting goes on or is a habit) (e:Bang hangin ~ lai i hi hiam/Ngettawm suangin a ~ mipa hi lo ahi hiam | is this not the man who used to sit and beg) (r:24.8.14/43.9.8) (q:draft)
Tutung = (t:adv) (w:this time/now) (d:tu, now, with tung: this time, at this point; tutung peuhmahin is this very time; written with a capital at the start of a sentence) (e:~ peuhmahin Topa ka hihna thu) (s:tuhunin) (r:24.16.21) (q:draft, low confidence)
tutungin = (t:adv) (w:this time) (d:tutung, this time, with the ending in: on this occasion, now) (e:Topa aw, ~ Israel minamte tungah/~ nang kong that kei ding hi | this time I will not put you to death/~ kimanna a nei lo tuucing nasep sem in | this time do the work of a worthless shepherd) (s:tuhunin) (r:44.1.6/11.2.26/38.11.15)
tuu = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:sheep) (d:a sheep, the animal kept in flocks by a shepherd for its wool, milk and meat) (e:bawngtal zaguk leh ~ tulthum ahi hi/bawng, ~, keel | the ox, the sheep, the goat/Laban a ~ mul met dingin pai khia a | Laban had gone out to shear his sheep/~ leh bawng khempeuh | all sheep and cattle) (r:14.29.33/5.14.4/1.31.19/19.8.7)
Tuu = (t:n) (w:Sheep) (d:tuu, sheep, written with a capital in the name Tuu Kongpi, the Sheep Gate of Jerusalem, and at the start of a sentence) (e:nasep kipanin ~ Kongpi bawl uh hi/tua ciangin ~ Kongpi-ah pai uh a | then they went on to the Sheep Gate/inndei tungnung leh ~ Kongpi kikal puah uh hi | they repaired between the upper room and the Sheep Gate/~ Kongkhak tawh kinai | near the Sheep Gate/~ gawh ding bangin kote nang nong bawl a | you made us like sheep for slaughter) (b:tuu) (r:16.3.1/16.12.39/16.3.32/43.5.2/19.44.11) (q:draft)
Tuubuk = (t:n) (w:sheep pen/sheepfold/fold) (d:tuu, sheep, with buk, hut or shelter: an enclosure for sheep; written with a capital at the start of a sentence) (e:~ sunga tuu khum bangin) (s:tuukhawk/tuukulh/tuukhumna) (r:33.2.12) (q:draft)
tuubukte = (t:n) (w:sheep pens/sheepfolds) (d:tuu, sheep, with buk, shelter, and the plural te) (e:leh ~ bawl hi/~ panin la-in, ama nasem David a teel hi | he chose David his servant and took him from the sheep pens) (s:tuukhawkte) (r:14.32.28/19.78.70) (q:draft)
tuucin = (t:n) (w:shepherd/shepherding) (d:short form of tuucing, shepherd or tend sheep, used before another word: tuucin’ thung-ip is a shepherd’s bag and tuucin’ thaman a shepherd’s pay) (e:suangmai tang nga tengin a ~’ thung-ip/ka ~’ thaman hong pia un | give me my pay as shepherd/Topa pen ~ bangin hong cing hi a | the Lord tends me like a shepherd/eite khempeuh ~’ banga hong Cingpa Pasian’ piak | given by God, who keeps us all like a shepherd) (s:tuucingpa) (r:9.17.40/38.11.12/19.23.1/21.12.11) (q:draft)
tuucing = (t:v) (w:shepherd) (d:tuu, sheep, with cing, keep or tend: one who tends sheep; migi tuucing is the good shepherd) (e:Migi ~ ka hi hi/Kongpi pan a lut mi in ~ ahi hi | the one who enters by the gate is the shepherd/Ka lungsim bang ~ kong pia ding-a | I will give you shepherds after my own heart/Kha khat sungin ~ thumte ka notkhia hi | in one month I got rid of the three shepherds) (r:43.10.14/43.10.2/24.3.15/38.11.8)
Tuucing = (t:n) (w:Shepherd) (d:tuucing, shepherd, written with a capital as a title of Christ and at the start of a sentence; Tuucing Ukpa is the Chief Shepherd) (e:~ Ukpa hong kilat ciangin/~ lianpa ahi, i Topa Zeisu | our Lord Jesus, the great Shepherd/~ a nei lo tuute bangin | like sheep without a shepherd/~ hoih in a tuute sihpih ngam hi | the good shepherd is ready to die for his sheep) (s:Tuucingpa) (b:tuucing) (r:60.5.4/58.13.20/11.22.17/43.10.11) (q:draft)
tuucingpa = (t:n) (w:shepherd) (d:tuucing, shepherd, with pa, the male suffix: a man who tends sheep) (e:Amah in ~ bangin a tuuhonte/Sairas kumpipa in ka ~ hi a | King Cyrus is my shepherd/~’ puanbuk gei-ah hong cing in | graze them beside the shepherd’s tents/Kiman’na a neilo ~, a tuuhonte a nusiapa | the worthless shepherd who deserts the flock) (s:gancingpa/cingpa) (b:tuucing) (r:23.40.11/23.44.28/22.1.8/38.11.17)
Tuucingpa = (t:n) (w:Shepherd) (d:tuucingpa, shepherd, written with a capital as a title of God or Christ and at the start of a sentence; pa marks a male person) (e:Israel ~ aw, ngai in/note kha uh hong Ukpa leh ~ kiangah | to the Overseer and Shepherd of your souls/~ ka satlum a, tuute a kithehthang ding hi | I will strike the shepherd and the sheep will be scattered/~ in a tuuhonte, lauhuaina pan a hot bangin | as a shepherd saves his flock from danger/~ sat in | strike the shepherd) (s:Tuucing) (b:tuucingpa) (r:19.80.1/60.2.25/41.14.27/38.9.16/38.13.7) (q:draft)
tuucingte = (t:n) (w:shepherds) (d:tuucing, shepherd, with the plural te) (e:no ~ aw, keima thugen ngai un/Tua gamah ~ in gam lakah giakin | in that region shepherds were camping in the fields/~ in tuikhuk kong panin suang khukkhia uh a | the shepherds rolled the stone from the mouth of the well/~ khut sung panin kote hong honkhia-a | he rescued us from the hand of the shepherds) (s:gancingte) (b:tuucing) (r:26.34.9/42.2.18/42.2.8/1.29.3/2.2.19) (q:draft)
Tuucingte = (t:n) (w:shepherds) (d:tuucingte, shepherds, written with a capital at the start of a sentence and in the place name Tuucingte’ Buk, Beth Eked of the Shepherds in the NIV) (e:~’ buk a tun’ lai takin/~’ thugenna zate khempeuh in | all who heard what the shepherds said/~ hong pai-in amaute hawlkhia hi | shepherds came and drove them away/~ in a kithehthang tuute kaikhawmin a kep bangin | as shepherds gather and look after the scattered sheep) (b:tuucingte) (r:12.10.12/42.2.18/2.2.17/26.34.12) (q:draft)
tuucinna = (t:n) (w:tending sheep/shepherding/sheep pasture) (d:tuucin, tend sheep, with the noun suffix na: the work of a shepherd, or a place where sheep are kept) (e:Ka ~ panin Topa in kei/amaute in ~-in nei-in | they will have it as pasture for their sheep) (b:tuucin) (r:30.7.15/36.2.7) (q:draft)
tuuhon = (t:n) (w:flock) (d:tuu, sheep, with hon, flock or herd) (e:Abraham in a ~ sung panin/~ leh ganhon leh puanbukte nei a | he had flocks, herds and tents/na mite, ~ bangin na makaih hi | you led your people like a flock/a ~ tacilte leh a sa limcite paipih hi | he brought the firstborn of his flock and their fat portions) (s:ganhon) (b:tuu) (r:1.21.28/1.4.4/1.13.5/19.77.20) of sheeps
tuuhonnote = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:young of the flock/lambs) (d:tuuhon, flock of sheep, with no, young, and the plural te: the lambs of the flock) (e:na ~ uh tungah thupha om ding/na ~ uh zong hong nusiat lo ding | they will not leave you even the lambs of your flocks) (s:tuunote) (r:5.28.4/5.28.51) (q:draft)
tuuhonpi = (t:n) (w:great flock/large flock of sheep) (d:tuuhon, flock of sheep, with pi, great) (e:~ bangin Israel mite ka tamsak ding hi/Jerusalem-a ~ om muamua bangin | like the great flocks in Jerusalem) (b:tuuhon) (r:26.36.37/26.36.38) (q:draft)
tuuhonte = (t:n) (w:flocks) (d:tuuhon, flock of sheep, with the plural te) (e:Na ~ hoih takin thei in la/a pa uh’ ~ cing dingin | to tend their father’s flocks/Gawh dinga kikoih ~ va cing in | go and tend the flock marked for slaughter/Amah in na ~ uh seh-sawm-suah-seh-khat la ding a | he will take a tenth of your flocks) (s:ganhonte) (b:tuuhon) (r:20.27.23/1.37.12/38.11.4/9.8.17) (q:draft)
tuukhawk = (t:n) (w:sheep pen/sheepfold) (d:tuu, sheep, with khawk, pen: an enclosure where sheep are kept or lie down) (e:dangte zong ~ ka suaksak ding hi/Lam gei-a ~ omna-ah a pai hi | he came to the sheep pens by the road/~ sungah mawk om na hi uh hiam | do you stay idle among the sheep pens) (s:tuukulh/tuukhumna/Tuubuk) (r:26.25.5/19.68.13/9.24.3) (q:draft)
tuukhawkte = (t:n) (w:sheep pens/sheepfolds) (d:tuukhawk, sheep pen, with the plural te) (e:na tuute uh a dingin ~ bawl unla/tuute a dingin ~ a bawl uh hi | they built pens for the sheep/ka tuute uh a dingin ~ bawlin | building pens for our sheep) (s:tuubukte) (b:tuukhawk) (r:4.32.24/4.32.36/4.32.16) (q:draft)
tuukhumna = (t:n) (w:sheep pen/sheepfold) (d:tuu, sheep, with khum, shut in, and the noun suffix na: the place where sheep are shut in) (e:Hih ~ sunga om lo tuute/keimah in ~ kongpi ka hi hi | I am the gate of the sheepfold/~ sungah kongpi lam pan lut lo a | not entering the sheep pen by the gate) (s:tuukulh/tuukhawk/Tuubuk) (r:43.10.16/43.10.1/43.10.7) (q:draft)
tuukong = (t:n) (w:sheep gate/door of the sheepfold) (d:tuu, sheep, with kong, door: the gate of the sheepfold; tuukong cing pa is the gatekeeper) (e:~ cing pa in a kong hon a) (r:43.10.3) (q:draft)
tuukulh = (t:n) (w:sheep pen/sheepfold) (d:tuu, sheep, with kulh, wall or enclosure: a walled pen for sheep) (e:Hih ~ sungah a om lo tuu dang/~ kong tawnin a lut mipa | the man who enters by the gate of the sheep pen/~ panin a tuute a pusuah khiatpih hi | he leads his sheep out of the pen/Tuate zong ~ sungah ka khum ding a | I will bring them too into the sheep pen) (s:tuukhawk/tuukhumna/Tuubuk) (r:43.10.16/43.10.1/43.10.2/43.10.3) (q:draft)
tuulak = (t:n) (w:forest/thicket/woodland) (d:thick forest or undergrowth where wild animals live, as the thickets along the Jordan) (e:~ panin humpi khat in amaute that ding/Jordan gam ~ pan a, a hong paito humpi | a lion coming up from the thickets of the Jordan/A ~ inn uh kisusia khin ahih manin | because their forest home is ruined) (s:tulak/gamlak) (r:24.5.6/24.49.19/38.11.3) (q:draft)
tuulebawngte = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:flocks and herds/sheep and cattle) (d:tuu, sheep, le, and, bawng, cattle, with the plural te, written as one word) (e:i pu i pate’ biakna ahi ~) (r:24.3.24) (q:draft)
tuulekeel = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:sheep and goats/flock) (d:tuu, sheep, le, and, keel, goat, written as one word; tuulekeel hon is the flock, beside bawnghon, the herd) (e:~ hon panin ahi zongin/Bawnghon leh ~ hon sawm-ah-khat khempeuh | every tenth of the herd and the flock) (r:3.22.21/3.27.32) (q:draft)
tuulekeelno = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:lambs and kids/young of the flock) (d:tuulekeel, sheep and goats, with no, young one) (e:na ~ honte uh zong thupha pia) (s:tuuhonnote) (b:tuulekeel) (r:5.7.13) (q:draft)
tuum = (t:v) (w:cover over/submerge/overwhelm) (d:of water or a load: close over something and bury it) (e:Tui in amaute ~ a/tuipi in amaute ~ hi | the sea covered them/sihna tuihualte in kei hong ~ a | the waves of death swept over me/ka mawhnate in ka lu ~ zo a | my sins have gone over my head/na tuihual liante in kei hong ~ hi | your great waves have swept over me) (s:tuumcip/vukcip/khuhcip) (r:2.15.5/10.22.5/2.15.10/19.38.4/19.42.7) (q:draft)
tuumcip = (t:v) (w:cover/submerge/overwhelm/flood over) (d:tuum, cover over, with cip, tightly or completely: of water, cover something completely) (e:tuikhang in nang hong ~ hi/mual lian a sangte khempeuh ~ hi | all the high mountains were covered/tuite in mualte ~ hi | the waters covered the mountains/Tui in hong ~ gawp ahih manin | because the waters closed over me/a ~ ding tuiciin in hong nawk ciangin | when the overwhelming flood sweeps by) (s:tumcip/khuhcip/vukcip) (b:tuum) (r:18.22.11/1.7.19/19.104.6/25.3.54/23.28.18) (q:draft)
tuummang = (t:v) (w:engulf/swallow up/submerge) (d:tuum, cover over, with mang, out of sight: of water, cover something so that it is lost; also sink and be lost in the sea) (e:Tui in amau’ langte ~ khin a/tuipi husiate in hong ~ khin ding hi | the raging waters would have swept us away/nang tawh tuipi sungah ~ khin uh hi | they have sunk with you into the sea) (s:tummang/tumcip) (r:19.106.11/26.27.27/19.124.5) (q:draft)
tuumsak = (t:v) (w:make cover/cover/overwhelm) (d:tuum, cover over, with the causative sak: make water cover and bury someone) (e:tuipi luangsakin amaute ka ~ hi/amaute tungah tuipi paisakin amaute ~ hi | he brought the sea over them and covered them/Topa in tuipi tuite amaute ~ kik hi | the Lord brought the waters of the sea back over them) (b:tuum) (r:6.24.7/2.15.19) (q:draft)
tuumsakin = (t:v) (w:overwhelming/covering over) (d:tuumsak, make water cover, with the linking ending in: making water close over something) (e:San Tuipi tui tawh amaute ~/lei nuai-a tuite ~ ka thuumsak ding hi | covering the waters under the earth I will make them mourn) (b:tuumsak) (r:5.11.4/26.31.15) (q:draft)
tuumsakkik = (t:v) (w:bring back over/make cover again) (d:tuumsak make water cover, with kik back or again) (e:tuipi tuite amaute ~ a) (b:tuumsak) (r:2.15.19) (q:draft)
tuumul = (t:n) (w:wool/fleece) (d:tuu, sheep, with mul, hair: the wool of a sheep, a fleece) (e:Amah in ~ bangin vukkhal hong pia a/~ panin tui hai khat dim suk khia hi | he wrung a bowlful of water out of the fleece/Tuu nawi ne-in, ~ silhin | you eat the milk and wear the wool/ka ngah ~ puan kibawl ka pia hi | I gave clothing made from the wool I got) (s:ganmul/samul) (r:19.147.16/9.25.4/7.6.38/26.34.3/18.31.20) (q:draft)
tuumulte = (t:n) (w:fleece/wool) (d:tuumul, wool or fleece, with the plural te) (e:a ~ a tui suk a) (b:tuumul) (r:7.6.38) (q:draft)
tuumzo = (t:v) (w:overwhelm/cover completely) (d:tuum, cover over, with zo, showing that the action is carried through: of guilt, rise right over the head) (e:ka lu dong hong ~ a) (s:tuumcip) (b:tuum) (r:19.38.4) (q:draft)
tuunawi = (t:n) (w:sheep's milk/milk of the flock) (d:tuu, sheep, with nawi, milk) (e:cing napi-in a ~ a ne lo/tuuhon panin ~, tuunote leh tuutalte’ thau tawh | milk from the flock, with the fat of lambs and rams) (r:46.9.7/5.32.14) (q:draft)
tuung = (t:adv) (w:just beginning/very early) (d:just at the start, at the very first moment: zingsang tuung is very early in the morning, ni suak tuung the sun as it is just rising) (e:ni suak ~ na bia uh hi/ni kipat ni, zingsang ~, nisuah lai takin | on the first day, very early in the morning, at sunrise) (r:26.8.16/41.16.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
tuuno = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:lamb) (d:tuu, sheep, with no, young: a young sheep; kum khat a pha tuuno is a lamb a year old) (e:kum khat a pha ~ a pa khat/Ngia hon lakah ~ kikhahte bangin | like lambs sent out among wolves/a biak nadingin ~ khat a piak leh | if he offers a lamb as his offering/mualneute ~ bangin a diang uh hi | the hills skipped like lambs) (b:tuu) (r:4.7.15/42.10.3/3.3.7/19.114.4) (q:draft)
Tuuno = (t:n) (w:Lamb) (d:tuuno, lamb, written with a capital as a title of Christ, the Lamb of God, mostly in Revelation) (e:~ paina teng a zui mite/leitung’ mawhna a puakhia Pasian’ ~ | the Lamb of God who takes away the sin of the world/~ in nihna ciamtehna a hon’ ciangin | when the Lamb opened the second seal/~ sisan le thuman a genna uh tawh | by the blood of the Lamb and the word of their testimony) (b:tuuno) (r:66.14.4/66.12.11/43.1.29/66.6.3) (q:draft)
tuunote = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:lambs) (d:tuuno, lamb, with the plural te) (e:siah dingin ~ puak uh hi/lonona munah ~ an vak bangin | like feeding lambs in a pasture/bawngtalte, tuutalte, leh ~ tawh piak dingin | to be offered with the bulls, rams and lambs) (s:tuuhonnote) (b:tuuno) (r:23.16.1/4.29.24/28.4.16) (q:draft)
tuununo = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:ewe lamb) (d:tuu sheep with nu female and no young: a young female sheep) (e:Hih na koihtuam ~ sagihte/a tuuhon sung panin ~ sagih tuam koih hi | he set apart seven ewe lambs from his flock/hih ~ sagihte na la ding hi | you shall take these seven ewe lambs) (r:1.21.29/1.21.28/1.21.30) (q:draft)
