tuupite = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:ewes) (d:tuupi, ewe, with the plural te; no a nei tuupite are ewes that have young) (e:no a nei ~ a cinna) (a:tuutalte) (b:tuupi) (r:19.78.70) (q:draft)
tuusa = (t:n) (w:mutton/sheep meat) (d:tuu sheep with sa meat, flesh: what the owners sell after slaughtering their sheep) (e:Amaute in a ~ zuak uh a) (b:tuu) (r:38.11.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
tuusiah = (t:n) (w:tribute of sheep) (d:tuu sheep with siah tribute, tax: the share of the sheep given as tribute) (e:Topa’ ~ pen tuu zaguk) (r:4.31.37) (q:draft)
tuutal = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:ram) (d:tuu, sheep, with tal, male: a male sheep, often named among the animals for sacrifice) (e:tuupi za nih leh ~ sawmnih/a kisansak ~ vunte | ram skins dyed red/Mualliante ~ bangin diang uh a | the mountains skipped like rams/bawngtal sawm, ~ nih | ten bulls, two rams) (a:tuupi) (r:1.32.14/2.25.5/19.114.4/4.29.23) (q:draft)
tuutalte = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:rams) (d:tuutal, ram, with the plural te) (e:tuuhonte' sung pan ~ ka ne kei hi/nangmah in ~ khat la-in | you shall take one of the rams/Bashan panin ~, tuunote, keelte leh bawngtal thaute | rams, lambs, goats and fat bulls from Bashan) (a:tuupite) (b:tuutal) (r:1.31.38/26.39.18/2.29.15) (q:draft)
tuute = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:sheep/flock) (d:tuu, sheep, with the plural te; also a picture of people under the care of a shepherd) (e:Israel pawl a gammang ~ kiangah/Ka ~ in keima aw a ngai uh a | my sheep listen to my voice/~ adingin tuu-khawkte bawl uh hi | they built pens for the sheep/a pa’ ~ a vak dingin | to tend the sheep of his father) (b:tuu) (r:40.10.6/4.32.36/43.10.27/9.17.15) (q:draft)
tuuvun = (t:n) (w:sheepskin/sheep's clothing) (d:tuu, sheep, with vun, skin: the skin of a sheep, worn as clothing or used as a covering) (e:~ keelvun silhin a kawivak uh hi/~ silh a, no kiangah hong pai | they come to you wearing sheepskin) (r:58.11.37/40.7.15) (q:draft)
tuzan = (t:adv) (w:tonight/this night) (d:tu now, this, with zan night; also used as a noun, the present night) (e:~ mahmahin na si ding hi/~ aak nihvei a khuan’ ma-in | tonight, before the rooster crows twice/~ nai kua hunin ding khia un | be ready to set out at nine tonight/Galvil pa aw, ~ bangci hiam | watchman, how is the night) (s:tunitak) (r:42.12.20/41.14.30/44.23.23/23.21.11) (q:draft)
tuzanin = (t:adv) (w:tonight/last night/this night) (d:tuzan with in: during this night, either the night now coming or the one just past) (e:keimah kuankhia-in ~ David ka delh ding hi/Topa in ~ kei kiangah hong gen thu | what the Lord said to me last night/vantungmi khat in ~ ka kiangah ding a | last night an angel stood beside me/~ amah, nang tawh hong lumkhawm thei ding hi | tonight he may sleep with you) (s:tunitak) (b:tuzan) (r:10.17.1/9.15.16/44.27.23/1.30.15) (q:draft)
