Ufaz = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Uphaz) (d:place known for its gold, of unknown location) (r:24.10.9)
uh = (t:ppm) (d:postpositional marker to indicate objective case) (e:leitung khua a vaksak dingin vantungah khuavak hi ~ hen/Mi khempeuh in a ne ~ a | they all ate/tua san takah tu-in a en ~ hi | sitting there, they watched him/Na sam ~ zong a kisim khin hi | even your hairs are all counted) (r:1.1.15/41.6.42/40.27.36/40.10.30)
uha = (t:part) (d:the plural marker uh joined with -a, the short form of ah, at, in, on or of; it follows a noun that belongs to several people and links it to the next word, as na mai uha om, that are in front of you) (e:ka kiim ~ omte’ nuihsat/Na mai ~ om hihte kua-a’ ahi hiam | whose are these that are in front of you/a khe ~ leivui bangte sinkhiat sanin | shaking the dust off their feet/na kim ~ a om minam dangte khempeuh | all the other nations that are around you) (b:uh) (r:19.44.13/1.32.17/44.13.51/26.5.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
uhah = (t:ppm) (d:plural marker uh joined with the place marker ah, after a noun owned by several people, in or to their or your) (e:na lungsim ~ om ding hi/na gam ~ kong tun’pih kik ding hi | I will bring you back into your land/Na inn sung ~ tehna nam nih | two kinds of measures in your house/Na puanbuk ~ ciah un | return to your tents) (b:uh) (r:5.6.6/5.5.30/26.36.24/5.25.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
uhahi = (t:part) (d:plural marker uh and ahi, it is, written together at the end of a question) (e:dam thei lo ~ hiam) (r:24.8.22) (q:draft, low confidence)
uhamte = (t:n) (w:the old/elders/old people) (d:older people, set against khangnote the young) (e:khangnote pen ~ tungah) (s:khanghamte/teekte/teeksiate) (a:khangnote/khangmoite) (r:23.3.5) (q:draft)
uhcin = (t:det) (w:if you) (d:follows le, if, after a verb, written le uhcin or le-uhcin: if you do so, said to several people; uh marks the plural and cin the second person) (e:tua bang hih le ~ na si ding uh hi | if you do so you will die/Guta khat mu le ~ ama lawm | when you see a thief you are his friend/Pia le-~ hong pet zawsop ding hi | if you give, they will tear you to pieces) (r:1.3.3/19.50.18/40.7.6) (q:?)
uhleh = (t:conj) (w:if/unless) (d:plural marker uh written together with leh, if, after a verb whose subject is plural; with kei before it, unless) (e:na zuih ~ na lung uh nuam/na gamtat ~ ka lawmte na hi uh hi | if you do so you are my friends/na mawhna panun na kisik kei ~ | unless you repent of your sins/naupang na bat kei ~ | unless you become like children) (r:43.13.17/42.13.3/43.15.14/40.18.3) (q:draft)
uhleh = (t:conj) (w:and) (d:plural possessor marker uh written together with leh, and, joining two nouns) (e:A kumpipa ~ a uliante uh) (r:30.1.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
uhteh = (t:part) (d:in le uhteh, also written le-uhteh, placed after a verb: if you do, when you do, said to several people; uh marks the plural and le with teh the condition) (e:Amau gah en le ~/ankamtang khat cia bang upna nei le-~ | if you have faith as small as a mustard seed/ci le ~ amau in thakhatin hong khah ding hi | if you say so they will let it go at once) (r:40.7.16/41.11.3/42.17.6) (q:draft)
ui = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:dog) (d:a dog; in the Bible mostly an animal that roams and scavenges, and a picture of someone despised) (e:~ in a luak a zuat kik bangin/~ bangin ku uh a | they snarl like dogs/~’ thahatna panin ka nuntakna hong hon in | deliver my life from the power of the dog/~ ommuang khat a bil-a kaihsak tawh kibang hi | is like seizing a stray dog by the ears) (r:20.26.11/19.22.20/19.59.6/20.26.17) (q:draft)
uih = (t:v) (w:stink/smell bad/reek) (d:give off a bad smell, as of rotting flesh or a festering wound) (e:ka liamnate nai-in ~ a/a si-luanghawmte ~ semsem ding hi | their dead bodies will stink more and more/gamsung teng ~ hi | the whole land stank/Nail gun ~ a | the Nile stank) (s:ning) (r:19.38.5/23.34.3/2.8.14/2.7.21) (q:draft)
uihgawp = (t:v) (w:stink badly/reek) (d:uih stink with gawp, thoroughly, badly) (e:gun tui ~ ding ahih manin/a luanghawmte uh ~ ding hi | their corpses will stink badly) (b:uih) (r:2.7.18/29.2.20) (q:draft)
uihin = (t:v) (w:stink/smell bad) (d:uih with the linking ending in) (e:Lei zui-a tui kilate ~) (b:uih) (r:23.19.6) (q:draft)
uihna = (t:n) (w:stench/stink/bad smell) (d:uih stink with the noun suffix na) (e:Paknamtui tangin ~/a ~ na nakngeek uh kong zensak hi | I made its stench fill your nostrils) (b:uih) (r:23.3.24/30.4.10) (q:draft)
uihsak = (t:v) (w:make stink/give a bad smell) (d:uih stink with the causative sak) (e:a om paknamtui ~ thei a) (b:uih) (r:21.10.1) (q:draft)
uihta = (t:v) (w:stink already/have begun to smell) (d:uih stink with ta, marking a state already reached) (e:ni li phakhin ahih manin ~ ding hi) (b:uih) (r:43.11.39) (q:draft)
uihte = (t:n) (w:those that stink/rotting ones) (d:uih stink with plural te; misi a uihte are the stinking dead) (e:a kithat misi a ~) (b:uih) (r:23.14.19) (q:draft)
uikai = (t:n) (c:star) (w:the Bear) (d:second part of the star name Khawlei-uikai, the Bear, also written Khawlei uikai as two words) (e:Khawlei ~ a pai nading lampi) (r:18.38.32) (q:draft, low confidence)
uili = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:flea) (d:a tiny biting insect; David uses it as a picture of someone too small to be worth hunting) (e:~ bang lel keimah a that dingin/Uisi maw! ~ maw | a dead dog? a flea?) (r:9.26.20/9.24.14) (q:draft)
uilut = (t:n) (w:tumor/boil) (d:a swelling or boil on the body; uilut vei is to suffer from tumors) (e:mite in ~ vei uh a/amaute tungah ~ piang hi | tumors broke out on them/a ~ nuh un | apply it to his boil/kham simbeng leh ~ limte | the gold rats and the models of the tumors) (s:meimatum) (r:9.5.12/12.20.7/9.5.9/9.6.11) (q:draft)
uilutte = (t:n) (w:tumors) (d:plural of uilut) (e:tungah a piak uh kham ~ in) (b:uilut) (r:9.6.17) (q:draft)
uiphuk = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:frog) (e:~ tawh a kibang kha gilo thum/a tun’saksa ~ tawh kisai thu | the matter of the frogs he had brought) (r:66.16.13/2.8.12) (q:draft)
uiphukte = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:frogs) (d:uiphuk, frog, with the plural te) (e:huang sung leh lote panin ~ si hi/~ hong pai-in Izipt leitang tuam hi | the frogs came up and covered the land of Egypt/na gam khempeuh ~ tawh ka gimsak ding hi | I will plague your whole country with frogs/~ amau lakah a sawl hi | he sent frogs among them) (b:uiphuk) (r:2.8.13/19.78.45/2.8.6/2.8.2) (q:draft)
uisan = (t:adj) (w:gluttonous/greedy) (d:of a person greedy for food) (e:a thadah a ~ mi ahi uh hi) (r:56.1.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
uisante = (t:n) (w:gluttons) (d:uisan greedy for food, with plural te: those who eat too much) (e:Zu nete leh a ~ zawng ding uh a/a ~ tawh kithuah kha kei in | do not keep company with gluttons) (b:uisan) (r:20.23.21/20.23.20) (q:draft)
uisi = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:dead dog) (d:ui dog with si die; said of a person as a term of contempt) (e:hih ~ a banglel mi khat in/~ maw! Uili maw | a dead dog? a flea?) (r:10.16.9/9.24.14) (q:draft)
uite = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:dogs) (d:ui, dog, with the plural te; also said of evil people) (e:~ piak ding kilawm lo hi/~ in nangma sisan liak ding uh hi | dogs will lick up your blood/Tua ~, gilo-a gamtate na peel un | watch out for those dogs, those evildoers) (b:ui) (r:40.15.26/42.16.21/11.21.19/50.3.2) (q:draft)
uk = (t:n) (w:dominion) (e:Amah in a tawntungin a ~ ding hi | he will rule forever/Kote' tungah nang in hong ~ ding na hi hiam | will you reign over us) (r:27.4.3/1.37.8)
uk = (t:n) (w:rule) (e:minamte tungah amah in ~ hi/Topa in ~ tawntung ding hi | the Lord will rule forever/Beor’ tapa Bela in Edom gamsung ~ hi | Bela son of Beor ruled Edom/amah in nang' tungah hong ~ ding hi | he will rule over you) (r:19.22.28/2.15.18/1.36.32/1.3.16)
uk = (t:n) (w:control) (e:Kamkaih tawh ~ loh-a phamawh | that must be controlled with a bridle/nang hong ~ nuam hi | it wants to control you) (r:19.32.9/1.4.7)
uk = (t:n) (w:govern) (e:khuavak lianzaw pen sun a ~ ding/sun leh zan a ~ ding | to govern the day and the night/Khuapi a ~ mihing sawm sangin | than ten men who govern a city) (r:1.1.16/1.1.17/21.7.19)
Uk = (t:n) (w:kingdom/reign/rule) (d:uk, rule, written with a capital for the reign of God: Pasian’ Uk ding hun is the time when God will rule, the kingdom of God) (e:Pasian’ ~ ding hun zong a lamen/Pasian’ ~ nading hun note a dingin hong naita hi | the time of the rule of God has come near to you/Pasian’ ~ ding a deihna hangin | for the sake of the kingdom of God) (s:Ukna/Gam/Kumpigam) (b:uk) (r:41.15.43/61.1.11/42.10.9/42.18.29) (q:draft)
ukcip = (t:v) (w:subdue/control completely/hold in one's power) (d:uk rule with cip tightly: bring fully under one's rule or power) (e:~ dingin na hanciam uh mite) (s:nuaisiah/zogawp) (b:uk) (r:26.13.20/24.27.8) (q:draft)
ukcipsak = (t:v) (w:make subdue completely/bring fully under rule) (d:ukcip bring fully under one's rule, with the causative sak) (e:amah ka ~ mateng namsau tawh) (b:ukcip) (r:24.27.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
ukgawp = (t:v) (w:rule harshly/rule over) (d:uk rule with gawp, done severely or with force) (e:a galte un amaute ~ uh hi/ngong bawlin na ~ zawsop uh hi | you have ruled them harshly and brutally/ka hehna tawh note kong ~ taktak ding hi | with my wrath I will surely rule over you) (b:uk) (r:16.9.28/26.34.4/26.20.33) (q:draft)
ukin = (t:v) (w:rule/be in charge of/command) (d:form of uk with the linking ending in; a ukin koih is put in charge of) (e:lasak nasep a ~ David in a koih mite/ka kumpipa un kote hong ~ kote mai-ah pai-in | our king ruling us and going before us/tuate in leitung ~ a om ding uh hi | they will reign on the earth/Izipt leitang tung khempeuh a ~ amah koih hi | he put him in charge of the whole land of Egypt) (b:uk) (r:13.6.31/13.11.25/9.8.20/66.5.10/1.41.43) (q:draft)
ukkha = (t:v) (w:get to rule/come to rule) (d:uk rule with kha, happen to: in the negative, not get to rule) (e:ama gam a ~ kei ding uh hi) (r:27.11.4) (q:draft)
ukkhawm = (t:v) (w:reign together/rule together) (d:uk rule with khawm together) (e:amah tawh i ~ ding hi/vantungah amah tawh i ~ theih nadingin | so that we may reign with him in heaven) (s:maangkhawm) (b:uk) (r:55.2.12/49.2.6) (q:draft)
ukkhial = (t:v) (w:misrule/manage wrongly) (d:uk rule with khial wrongly; of one who brings trouble on his own household) (e:A innkuan sung a ~ mite) (r:20.11.29) (q:draft)
ukkik = (t:v) (w:rule again/rule in turn) (d:uk rule with kik again, back) (e:midikte in ~ ding hi) (b:uk) (r:20.28.28) (q:draft)
uklah = (t:v) (w:consume/eat up) (d:used with sak of zeal that consumes the heart) (e:ka lungsim hong ~ sak hi) (r:43.2.17) (q:draft, low confidence)
uklam = (t:n) (w:ruling/the fact of ruling) (d:uk rule with lam, the fact or manner of: that someone rules) (e:na khempeuh a ~ i thei nai) (r:58.2.8) (q:draft)
ukna = (t:n) (w:dominion) (d:uk, rule, with the noun suffix na: rule, authority or dominion; ukna gam is the land that someone rules) (e:~ in Topa aa hi a/Israel gam in ama ~ gam a suak hi | Israel became his dominion/Ama ~ mun khempeuh ah | in all places of his dominion) (s:thuneihna/aana) (b:uk) (r:19.22.28/19.114.2/19.103.22)
ukna = (t:n) (w:dominance) (d:the authority one person has over another, as in ukna nuai-ah, under the authority of) (e:Na pasal’ ~ nuai-ah na om sungin | while you are under the authority of your husband/Kote’ tungah ~ nei ding na hi hiam | will you have dominion over us) (b:uk) (r:4.5.19/1.37.8)
ukna = (t:n) (w:domination) (e:Faro’ ~ nuai-ah antangte kholin | storing grain under the authority of Pharaoh/siampi Aaron’ tapa Ithamar’ ~ nuai hi ding hi | it shall be under the direction of Ithamar son of Aaron the priest) (b:uk) (r:1.41.35/4.4.28)
ukna = (t:v) (w:subdue) (d:used with nei, have: ukna nei is have dominion over, rule over) (e:a nungtate khempeuh' tungah ~ nei ta un | have dominion over every living thing/leitunga a bokvakte khempeuh' tungah ~ neisak ni | let us give them rule over all that creep on the earth) (b:uk) (r:1.1.28/1.1.26)
Ukna = (t:n) (w:kingdom/reign) (d:ukna, rule, written with a capital in Pasian’ Ukna, the kingdom of God) (e:Pasian’ ~ bang tawh genteh leuleu ding/Pasian’ ~ thu a hilh ding | to proclaim the kingdom of God/Pasian’ ~ sungah hih bang mite a om ahi hi | the kingdom of God belongs to such as these) (s:Uk/Gam/Kumpigam) (b:ukna) (r:42.13.20/42.9.2/41.10.14) (q:draft)
uknate = (t:n) (w:dominions/powers/authorities) (d:ukna rule, dominion with plural te; in 1 Kings 14:19 a gam uknate is how he ruled the land) (e:vangliatna leh ~ a laksak khit ciangin/kumpi tokhomte ahi zongin ~ ahi zongin | whether thrones or powers/a galsimna a gam ~ | his wars and how he ruled the land) (s:vangliatnate/thuneite) (b:ukna) (r:51.2.15/11.14.19/51.1.16) (q:draft)
ukpa = (t:n) (w:ruler/commander/captain/governor) (d:the man who rules or is in charge; siampi ukpa is the high priest) (e:mihingte a ~ in amah khah hi/na mite uh a ~ | the ruler of your people/Biakna innpi ~ leh siampite in | the captain of the temple and the priests/a makai ding leh a ~ dingin ka koih hi | I made him a leader and commander) (s:mangpa/makai/ulianpa) (b:uk) (r:19.105.20/44.5.24/2.22.28/23.55.4) (q:draft)
Ukpa = (t:n) (w:Ruler/Chief/Overseer/Prince) (d:capitalised form of ukpa as a title of Christ: Siampi Ukpa is the high priest, Tuucing Ukpa the Chief Shepherd) (e:Tuucing ~ hong kilat ciangin/note kha uh hong ~ leh Tuucingpa kiangah | to the Overseer and Shepherd of your souls/tua mi in ~ leh Gumpa a suah na’ngin | that he might be Prince and Savior/a kip tawntung Siampi ~ a suah khit ciangin | having become high priest forever) (b:ukpa) (r:60.5.4/44.5.31/60.2.25/58.6.20) (q:draft)
ukpi = (t:n) (w:chief/leader/head) (d:uk, rule, with pi, great: the head of a clan or tribe, a chief) (e:a beh ~ in Uzziel’ tapa Elizafan/A ~ Ezer, a nihna Obadiah | Ezer was the chief, Obadiah the second/amau’ behte sungah ~ ahi hi | he was head of their clan/amah tawh ~ sawm | with him ten chiefs) (s:makai/makaipa/ukpipa) (b:uk) (r:4.3.30/13.12.9/13.5.15/6.22.14) (q:draft)
Ukpi = (t:n) (w:Prince/ruler/chief) (d:ukpi, chief, written with a capital as a title of Jesus, the Prince, and before the name of a chief) (e:~ le Honpa-in tua Jesuh bawlin/~ Joel, a zom Shafam | Joel the chief, Shapham the second) (b:ukpi) (r:44.5.31/13.5.12) (q:draft)
ukpipa = (t:n) (w:chief/ruler/chief officer) (d:ukpi with -pa for a man: the man who is head of or in charge of a group or place) (e:mihing sawmthum a ~ Amasai tungah/Meshek leh Tubal minamte a ~ Gog aw | Gog, chief prince of Meshek and Tubal/Pasian’ inn sung a ~ | the official in charge of the house of God/Babilon mipil thu dotte ~ dingin a koih hi | he placed him as chief over the wise men of Babylon) (s:ukpi/makaipa) (b:ukpi) (r:13.12.18/27.2.48/26.38.3/13.9.11) (q:draft)
ukpite = (t:n) (w:chiefs/leaders/rulers) (d:ukpi, chief, with the plural te) (e:hihte in Edom ~ ahi uh hi/Edom ~ lungkia uh a | the chiefs of Edom are dismayed/Hori mite’ ~ in | the chiefs of the Horites were/a zai mahmah leitungah ~ susia ding hi | he will crush rulers over the wide earth) (s:makaite/lutangte/uliante) (b:ukpi) (r:13.1.54/1.36.29/2.15.15/19.110.6) (q:draft)
uksak = (t:v) (w:let rule/make rule/put in control) (d:uk, rule, with causative sak: give someone or something control over) (e:Eufrates Gunpi dong amah ka ~ ding hi/a sum khempeuh tua nasempa a ~ ding hi | he will put that servant in charge of all his possessions/Khazih’ nopna na ~ un | let the peace of Christ rule/i ngaihsutna, Kha Siangtho ~ lehang | if we let the Holy Spirit rule our mind) (b:uk) (r:19.89.25/51.3.15/40.24.47/45.8.6) (q:draft)
uksakin = (t:v) (w:make ruler over/put in charge of) (d:uksak let rule, with the linking ending in) (e:Babylon gamteng ~) (b:uksak) (r:27.2.48) (q:draft)
uksakpa = (t:n) (w:one who makes rule) (d:uksak make rule with pa, the male one who does it: he who set the sun to rule the day and the moon and stars to rule the night) (e:sun pen ni a ~ tungah/zan pen kha leh aksite a ~ tungah | to him who made the moon and stars rule the night) (b:uksak) (r:19.136.8/19.136.9) (q:draft)
uksawn = (t:v) (w:govern/administer) (d:rule a province or region under a higher king; a uksawn mite are governors and uksawn kumpi is a tetrarch or regional ruler) (e:Eufrates Gungal gam a ~ mite kiang/Galilee gam sungteng a ~ kumpi Herod in | Herod, the king who governed all Galilee/gam sung khempeuh a ~ dingin | to govern throughout the kingdom/kumpipa’ nuai-ah a ~ a lian pente | the highest governors under the king) (r:16.2.9/40.14.1/27.6.1/15.8.36) (q:draft)
uksawnte = (t:n) (w:governors/satraps) (d:uk rule with sawn in turn and plural te: those who rule a land under the king) (e:ama nuai-ah gam a ~ a om laitakin/kumpipa’ nuai-ah gam tampi a ~ | those who govern many lands under the king) (s:mangpite/mangliante) (b:uksawn) (r:17.1.3/17.3.12) (q:draft)
uksung = (t:n) (w:jurisdiction/realm) (d:the area under someone's rule, from uk rule and sung inside) (e:Zeisu Herod’ ~ mi ahih lam) (r:42.23.7) (q:draft)
uktawm = (t:see) <ki-uktawm>
ukte = (t:n) (w:commanders/captains/rulers/officers) (d:those who rule or are in charge of people or of a land) (e:leitung gam ~ aw, thu phawk un/a leengte a ~ | the commanders of his chariots/leitung ~ pen bangmah lo a suaksakpa | he who reduces the rulers of the earth to nothing/ama nuai-ah a ~, a galkapmangte | his officers, his captains) (s:mangte/uliante/thuneite) (b:uk) (r:19.2.10/13.13.1/14.8.9/23.40.23/11.9.22) (q:draft)
uktheih = (t:v) (w:be able to rule/can rule) (d:uk rule with theih can) (e:khempeuh tungah ~ nading aana a kipia) (b:uk) (r:66.13.7) (q:draft)
ukzaw = (t:v) (w:rule all the more/reign more) (d:uk rule with zaw more) (e:nuntakna a ~ ding uh hi) (b:uk) (r:45.5.17) (q:draft)
ukzawh = (t:v) (w:reign/rule over) (d:rule as king; a ukzawh kum with a number is the year of a king's reign) (e:a ~ kum li a phakna kumin/Zedekiah in a ~ kum sawm le kum khat | in the eleventh year of the reign of Zedekiah/Sisar Tiberius in a ~ a kum sawm le ngana | in the fifteenth year of the reign of Tiberius Caesar/Kumpi Zedekiah in Judah gamah a ~ kum li ciangin | in the fourth year of the reign of King Zedekiah over Judah) (s:maang/maan) (b:ukzaw) (r:24.36.1/24.52.5/42.3.1/24.51.59) (q:draft)
ukzawh = (t:v) (w:control/master) (d:with ki- before it, control oneself, be self-controlled) (e:amau pumpi a ki-~ nadingun/a pumpi uh a ki-~ kei ding uhleh | if they cannot control themselves) (s:ukzo) (b:ukzaw) (r:56.2.6/46.7.9) (q:draft)
ukzawhna = (t:n) (w:control/mastery/rule) (d:the power to rule over something; ki-ukzawhna or pumpi ki-ukzawhna is self-control) (e:khuapi khat ~ sangin/eimah ki-~ hoihzaw hi | self-control is better/dikna le pumpi ki-~ hi a | gentleness and self-control/thahatna, ki-itna, pumpi ki-~ lungsim | a spirit of power, love and self-control) (b:ukzawh) (r:20.16.32/48.5.23/55.1.7) (q:draft)
ukzawhnate = (t:n) (w:dominion/authority/power to rule) (d:ukzawhna, the power to rule, with te, which here closes a list of nouns: dominion and authority) (e:vangliatna leh ~ tu-ma hun khempeuh) (b:ukzawhna) (r:65.1.24) (q:draft)
ukzia = (t:n) (w:way of managing/way of ruling/how to manage) (d:uk, rule, with zia, manner: the way to rule or manage something; ukzia ding a theih kei leh is if he does not know how to manage) (e:a innkuan sung ~ ding a theih kei leh) (r:54.3.5) (q:draft)
ukzo = (t:v) (w:rule/govern/manage/control) (d:uk, rule, with zo, be able: be able to rule or manage, have control over; ki-ukzo is to control oneself) (e:a sakol pumpi buppi i ~ hi/keima huhna bek tawh ~ uh a | they govern only by my help/minam dang kuamah ~ nawn lo ding uh hi | they will never again rule over other nations/na mite kua in ~ ding ahi hiam | who is able to govern your people/A innkuan sung hoihtakin a ~ mi | a man who manages his own household well) (b:uk) (r:59.3.3/20.8.16/26.29.15/11.3.9/54.3.4) (q:draft)
ukzote = (t:n) (w:those who manage/those who rule) (d:ukzo, be able to rule, with the plural te: those who manage or rule well) (e:a innkuansung hoihtakin a ~ hi ding hi) (b:ukzo) (r:54.3.12) (q:draft)
ul = (t:see) <khua-ul>
Ulai = (t:name) (c:river) (w:Ulai) (d:river or canal beside the city of Susa in Elam, where Daniel saw a vision) (e:~ gun gei-ah ka ding hi) (r:27.8.2/27.8.16) (q:draft)
Ulam = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ulam) (d:name of two men, a descendant of Manasseh and a Benjaminite who was the firstborn of Eshek) (r:13.7.16/13.8.39) (q:draft)
ulenau = (t:n) (w:brothers/siblings/brother) (d:u, elder sibling, le, and, nau, younger sibling, written as one word: brothers and sisters, also the people close to one) (e:a ~ le a mipihte kiangah) (s:unau/sanggam) (r:58.8.11) (q:draft)
ulenaute = (t:n) (w:brothers and sisters/brothers) (d:u older sibling, le and, nau younger sibling, with plural te; used of fellow believers) (e:Rom khua-a om ~ in/~ khempeuh tungah nopsakna le itna | peace and love to all the brothers and sisters) (s:unaute/sanggamte/Khristianpihte) (b:ulenau) (r:44.28.15/49.6.23) (q:draft)
ulian = (t:n) (w:official/ruler/prince/leader) (d:a man of high rank who rules or who serves under a king: an official, a prince or a ruler) (e:a nuai-a ~ khempeuh zong/Amaute’ ~ dingin naupangte ka bawl ding a | I will make boys their officials/Filistia ~ ngate in | the five rulers of the Philistines/kote’ lakah a vanglian ~ khat na hi hi | you are a mighty prince among us) (s:makai/ukpa) (r:20.29.12/23.3.4/9.6.16/1.23.6) (q:draft)
ulianin = (t:n) (w:as ruler/as prince/as leader) (d:ulian ruler, official with the marker in: into or in the position of a ruler, after bawl make or koih appoint) (e:Israel-te tungah ~ nang hong koih/ama mite’ ~ a bawl hi | he makes them princes of his people/Kote’ tungah nangmah ~ kibawl tawmin | making yourself ruler over us) (b:ulian) (r:9.25.30/19.113.8/4.16.13) (q:draft)
ulianpa = (t:n) (w:prince/ruler/commander) (d:ulian, official, with pa, which marks a man: a man of high rank who rules or commands, a prince, ruler or commander) (e:Gam uk ~ zong mihonte mah tawh lutin/amau a uk ~ tungah puak ding uh hi | they shall bring it to the prince who rules them/tua gam ~ in amah a muh ciangin | when the ruler of that land saw her/a ~ dingin Judah pau-in a gingin kiko a | the commander stood and called out loudly in Hebrew) (s:ukpa/mangpa/ukpipa) (b:ulian) (r:26.46.10/1.34.2/26.45.16/12.18.28) (q:draft)
ulianpen = (t:n) (w:highest official/most noble prince) (d:ulian, official, with pen, most: the highest in rank among the officials) (e:kumpipa’ ~ khat tungah) (b:ulian) (r:17.6.9) (q:draft)
ulianpi = (t:n) (w:great official/great man/high official) (d:ulian, official, with pi, great: a man of very high rank) (e:kumpipa’ maipha a ngah ~ khat ahi hi/kumpi inn sungah Mordekai ~ khat suak a | Mordecai became a great man in the palace) (s:milianpi) (b:ulian) (r:12.5.1/17.9.4) (q:draft)
ulianpihte = (t:n) (w:fellow officers/fellow officials/staff) (d:ulian official with pih, fellow, and plural te: the officers who serve together with someone) (e:Jehu in a ~ kiangah/A ~, a thulamlakte, le amah a cingte | his fellow officers, his advisers and his guards) (r:12.9.15/26.12.14) (q:draft)
ulianpipi = (t:n) (w:high officials/men of high rank) (d:ulianpi, great official, with pi doubled to show that there are many: men of high rank) (e:a vekpi-un ~, sakol tung tuang) (s:ulianpite) (b:ulianpi) (r:26.23.23) (q:draft)
ulianpite = (t:n) (w:chief officials/chief officers/high officials) (d:plural of ulianpi, a senior official; pi marks the higher rank) (e:Solomon’ nasep a uk ~ ahi hi/Babilon kumpipa’ ~ khempeuh in | all the chief officers of the king of Babylon/Pasian’ innah ~ ahi Hilkiah | Hilkiah, one of the chief officials in the house of God) (s:ulianpipi) (b:ulianpi) (r:11.9.23/14.35.8/24.39.13) (q:draft)
uliante = (t:n) (w:officials/princes/rulers/leaders) (d:plural of ulian: the officials, princes or rulers of a king or of a people) (e:Israel ~ hih bangin tamlawh in/kumpipa uh leh a ~ salin kiman ding hi | their king and his officials will be taken captive/a ~ ka that ding hi | I will kill her officials/leitung ~ leh thukhente khempeuh | all princes and judges of the earth) (s:makaite/ukte/miliante/mangliante) (b:ulian) (r:26.19.1/30.1.15/30.2.3/19.148.11) (q:draft)
Uliante = (t:n) (w:rulers/princes) (d:uliante, rulers, written with a capital at the start of a sentence or where rulers are addressed) (e:na bil uh ngat un, ~ aw/~ i muan’ sangin Topa belh ding hoihzaw hi | it is better to take refuge in the Lord than to trust in princes/~ in thu om lopi-in kei hong bawlsia | rulers persecute me without cause) (b:uliante) (r:7.5.3/19.118.9/19.119.161) (q:draft)
ulianzaw = (t:n) (w:higher official/more distinguished person) (d:ulian, person of rank, with zaw, more: someone of higher rank or more distinguished than another) (e:note sangin a ~ khat hong omkha) (b:ulian) (r:42.14.8) (q:draft)
Ulla = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ulla) (d:man of the tribe of Asher, father of Arah, Hanniel and Rizia) (e:~’ suante in: Arah, Hanniel, leh Rizia) (r:13.7.39) (q:draft)
um = (t:v) (w:believe/have faith in/trust) (d:accept something as true, or put faith and trust in God, a person or a word; the form up is used before a suffix) (e:mi tampite in Topa a ~ uh hi/Tu-in nong ~ uh hiam | do you now believe/kei hong mu napi-in nong ~ kei uh hi | you have seen me and still do not believe/zuauthu na ~ tazen uh hi | you are trusting in lies) (s:muang/taksang) (a:muanglah/muanlah) (r:43.10.42/41.11.22/43.16.31/43.6.36/24.7.8) (q:draft)
umcih = (t:v) (w:besiege/surround) (d:close in on a person or place from all sides: surround someone, or besiege a city in war; also the siege itself, as in galte’ umcih) (e:Minam khempeuh in kei hong ~ uh hi/Bawngtal tampi in kei hong ~ a | many bulls surround me/Jerusalem khuapi simin a ~ hi | he attacked Jerusalem and besieged it/Joab in khuapi a ~ ciangin | when Joab besieged the city/note in tua khua na ~ ding uh hi | you shall besiege that city) (s:uumcip/uum) (r:19.118.10/27.1.1/19.22.12/10.11.16/5.20.12) (q:draft)
umcihin = (t:v) (w:surrounding/besieging) (d:umcih, surround, with the linking ending in: surrounding or besieging, followed by a further action) (e:Amah in tua khua ~/tu-in amaute in kei hong ~ | now they surround me/amah paito-in Samaria ~ sim hi | he went up, besieged Samaria and attacked it/amaute in tua mun ~ | they surrounded the place) (b:umcih) (r:21.9.14/6.10.31/19.17.11/11.20.1/7.16.2) (q:draft)
umcihna = (t:n) (w:siege/siege works) (d:umcih, besiege, with the noun suffix na: the act of surrounding a city, or the works built for it) (e:tua khuapi ~ a kiman mateng/a tuk mateng ~-in na zat dingun | for you to use as siege works until it falls/Hong ~ leh na galte un hong lungkhamsak nading | the siege and the distress your enemies bring on you) (s:kiumcihna) (b:umcih) (r:26.4.8/5.20.20/5.28.53) (q:draft)
umcihte = (t:n) (w:besiegers) (d:umcih besiege with plural te: those who besiege) (e:nang pen a ~’ lim ding) (b:umcih) (r:26.4.3) (q:draft)
umcip = (t:see) <ki-umcip>
umgah = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:gourd) (d:um, gourd, with gah, fruit: the fruit of a gourd plant; umgah lim is a carved figure of a gourd) (e:a ang dimin ~ lo a/~ le pakpalh lim kigelh hi | gourds and open flowers were carved) (r:12.4.39/11.6.18) (q:draft)
umgui = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:gourd vine/gourd plant) (d:climbing plant that bears gourds, from um gourd and gui vine; the plant that shaded Jonah) (e:tua ~ hangin Jonah a lungdam mahmah hi/~ khat a tungah a zaamsak hi | he made a gourd vine grow up over him/tua ~ lungno khat nesak-a a keu hi | he had a worm eat the plant and it withered) (r:32.4.6/32.4.7) (q:draft)
umin = (t:v) (w:believing/trusting) (d:um with the linking ending in, followed by another verb: believing, believed and) (e:thupiakna ~ a ciah hi/Dawi gilote in zong ~ | even the demons believe/~ a kibaptaiz uh hi | they believed and were baptized/Keimah in ~, ka gen hi | I believed, therefore I spoke) (s:muanin) (b:um) (r:43.4.50/59.2.19/44.18.8/47.4.13) (q:draft)
umkha = (t:v) (w:believe/be taken in) (d:um, believe, with kha, happen to: come to believe, be taken in; umkha kei in is do not believe it) (e:hong cih leh zong ~ kei un/kam khum takin a pau manin ~ kei in | do not believe him because he speaks sweetly) (r:40.24.26/20.26.25) (q:draft)
umkhawmin = (t:v) (w:share/eat together) (d:with ankuang dish: sharing a dish, feasting together with someone) (e:note tawh ankuang hong ~) (r:61.2.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
umkhialsak = (t:v) (w:deceive/mislead) (d:um believe with khial wrongly and causative sak: make someone believe what is false) (e:mi tampi tak ~ ding uh hi) (s:khem/khialsak/pialsak) (r:40.24.11/40.24.5) (q:draft)
Umlah = (t:name) (w:Umlah)
umlebeel = (t:n) (w:articles/vessels/utensils/containers) (d:um gourd, le and, beel pot: household vessels and containers in general; in the verses the articles of the temple and storage vats) (e:~ a nam tuamtuam sawmnih le kua/Topa’ biakinn-a ~ pawlkhatte zong Babylon-ah pua-in | he also carried some articles of the temple of the Lord to Babylon/ngun tawh a kibawl ~ zakhat | a hundred articles made of silver/na koihna uh ~ khempeuh | all your storage vats) (s:beellekuang) (r:15.1.9/14.36.7/15.8.26/29.2.24) (q:draft)
umlebeelte = (t:n) (w:articles/vessels/utensils) (d:plural of umlebeel, pots and containers of all kinds; in the verses the articles used in the temple) (e:ngun le kham le ~/Hih ~ paipih inla | take these articles/ngun, kham, le ~ a hong sang uh hi | they received the silver, the gold and the articles) (s:beellekuangte/kuanglekeute/beelte) (b:umlebeel) (r:15.8.25/15.7.19/15.5.15/15.8.30) (q:draft)
umlote = (t:see) <thu-umlote>
Ummah = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Ummah) (d:town in the territory of the tribe of Asher) (r:6.19.30)
ummawh = (t:v) (w:suspect/sense/surmise) (d:think that something is so without knowing it for certain; bangmah a ummawh lo mite, people who suspect nothing) (e:bangmah a ~ lo mite kiangah na tung/bangmah a ~ lo mite omna Laish | Laish, where an unsuspecting people lived/ci-in teembaw nasemte in ~ uh a | the sailors sensed that) (s:upmawh) (r:7.18.10/44.27.27/7.18.27) (q:draft)
ummawhin = (t:v) (w:hoping/supposing/expecting) (d:ummawh suspect, surmise, with the linking ending in: thinking that something may happen) (e:ci-in ~ tam veipi samin) (s:lamenin) (b:ummawh) (r:44.24.26) (q:draft)
umna = (t:n) (w:enclosure/enclosing wall/surrounding wall) (d:um enclose with na: what surrounds a place; khua umna kulh, the wall enclosing a town) (e:Amah khua ~ kulh hi leh/a ~ a phungcian’ suangte kicim khin hi | its stone wall was broken down) (r:22.8.9/20.24.31) (q:draft)
umpihte = (t:n) (w:table companions) (d:in na ankuang umpihte, those who share your dish, who eat with you; pih together with, plural te; the sense of um here is not confirmed) (e:Na ankuang ~ in na nuai-ah) (r:31.1.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
umsak = (t:v) (w:persuade/convince/make believe) (d:um, believe, with the causative sak: make someone believe something, persuade or convince) (e:hih mite zuauthu na ~ hi/zuauthu hong ~ ahih manin | because he has made you trust in lies/mi tampi tak a ~ hi | he has convinced a great many people) (s:zol) (b:um) (r:24.28.15/44.19.26/24.29.31) (q:draft)
umsakzo = (t:v) (w:be able to convince/can persuade) (d:umsak make believe, with zo be able) (e:a va gen hangin ~ tuan lo ding hi) (b:umsak) (r:42.16.31) (q:draft)
umta = (t:v) (w:believe now/have come to believe) (d:um believe with ta, marking a state now reached) (e:Tu-in hong ~ na hi uh hiam) (b:um) (r:43.16.31) (q:draft)
umte = (t:n) (w:believers/those who believe) (d:um, believe, with the plural te: those who believe; thu umte is the usual word for believers) (e:ama min a ~ khempeuh in/Kei hong ~ in a sih hangin | those who believe in me, though they die/Tapa mu a, a ~ khempeuh in | everyone who sees the Son and believes in him/a ~ ading lim ahi hi | it is a sign for those who believe) (a:thu-umlote/lawkite) (b:um) (r:43.1.12/43.6.40/43.11.25/46.14.22) (q:draft)
umzaw = (t:v) (w:believe more/trust rather) (d:um believe with zaw more: believe one more than another) (e:teembaw nei pa’ thugen ~ hi) (b:um) (r:44.27.11) (q:draft)
umzo = (t:v) (w:be able to believe) (d:um believe with zo, be able; umzo taktak lo is could not really believe, doubted) (e:pawlkhat in ~ taktak lo uh hi) (s:uptheih/upzawh) (b:um) (r:40.28.17) (q:draft)
un = (t:ppm) (d:postpositional marker to indicate nominative case) (e:ci ~/na pu na pate ~ a theih loh manna | manna which your ancestors had not known/na galte ~ tuate ne ding hi | your enemies will eat them/Topa na Pasian ~ note a hong piaksa | which the Lord your God has given you) (r:19.128.4/5.8.16/3.26.16/5.28.53)
un = (t:v) (w:let) (d:word that closes a command or wish addressed to more than one person) (e:ci ~/bil a nei teng in za ta ~ | let those who have ears hear/Kei tawh Topa nak phat ~ | glorify the Lord with me/Ka thugente limtak ngai ~ | listen carefully to my words) (r:40.13.9/19.34.3/18.13.17)
unah = (t:see) <man-unah>
unau = (t:n) (w:brothers/siblings/brothers and sisters) (d:older and younger siblings of one family taken together, from u, elder, and nau, younger; unau numei is sisters) (e:~ sagih a om uh hi/Simeon leh Levi-te in ~ hi a | Simeon and Levi are brothers/Jekhoniah leh a ~ teng hi | Jeconiah and his brothers/Simon leh Andru te ~ | the brothers Simon and Andrew) (s:sanggam/ulenau) (r:41.12.20/26.23.2/1.49.5/40.1.11/41.1.16) (q:draft)
Unau = (t:n) (w:siblings) (d:unau, siblings, capitalised in Unau Peeng, twin siblings, the Twin, the byname of Thomas that the NIV gives as Didymus) (e:~ Peeng minno a nei Thomas) (b:unau) (r:43.20.24/43.21.2) (q:draft)
unaute = (t:n) (w:brothers/siblings/brothers and sisters) (d:plural of unau; also used for fellow believers and fellow countrymen) (e:tua ~ gel tungah a heh uh hi/Jakob’ tapa Judah, leh a ~ teng hi | Judah son of Jacob, and his brothers/amau ~’ khut tung uh panin | from the hands of their own brothers/~ lakah milian ahi uh Barsabbas | Barsabbas, a leader among the brothers) (s:sanggamte/ulenaute) (b:unau) (r:40.20.24/44.14.2/40.1.2/58.7.5/44.15.22) (q:draft)
ung = (t:part) (w:we) (d:verb-final marker for a first person plural subject that excludes the hearer, as in hi ung, we are; le ung is if we) (e:nangma mite hi ~/Thei mah ~ | yes, we know him/Kanaan gam panin hong pai hi ~ | we have come from the land of Canaan/Haran pan hi ~ | we are from Haran/Note kiang panin gamla mahmah ~ | we live very far from you) (r:28.8.2/1.42.7/1.29.5/1.29.4/6.9.22) (q:draft)
unla = (t:ppm) (d:postpositional marker to indicate nominative case) (e:ci ~/Kha Siangtho nasepna dongtangsak kei ~ | do not quench the work of the Holy Spirit/Unau ki-itna lungsim nei ~ | have brotherly love/Lungsim takpi tawh thu ngen tawntung ~ | pray always with your whole heart) (r:65.1.22/52.5.19/45.12.10/51.4.2)
Unni = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Unni) (d:name of two Levites, a musician in the time of David and one who returned from exile with Zerubbabel) (r:16.12.9/13.15.20)
Unno = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Unni) (d:Levite who returned from exile with Zerubbabel; the NIV spells the name Unni) (r:16.12.9)
unok = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:lily) (d:lily; unok pak or paak is the lily flower) (e:~ paakte lakah a tuu cing a/ling lak-a om ~ paak tawh kibang hi | like a lily among thorns/mual kuam sunga ~ paak ka hi lel hi | I am a lily of the valleys/A khuampite dawnah ~ pak a kibawl om hi | on top of the pillars was work in the shape of lilies) (r:22.2.16/11.7.22/22.2.2/22.2.1) (q:draft)
unu = (t:n) (w:older sister/elder sister) (d:u, elder sibling, with nu, which marks a woman: an older sister) (e:Mary le a ~ Martha’ omna Bethany khua-ah/Na ~ pen leilu lama om Samaria | your older sister is Samaria to the north/A ~’ min Oholah hi a | the older one was named Oholah/A ~ pai-in a pa tawh lum hi | the older daughter went and lay with her father) (a:naunu) (r:43.11.1/26.16.46/26.23.4/1.19.33) (q:draft)
up = (t:v) (w:believe/trust) (d:form of um, believe, used before a suffix or another word such as nading, loh or beh; also think or suppose; a up loh manun is because of their unbelief) (e:Tua thu a tun’ ciangin na ~ nadingun/mi tampi in a ~ beh uh hi | many more believed/amah ka ~ nadingin Pasian’ Tapa kua ahi hiam | who is the Son of God, that I may believe in him/amaute in a ~ uh Pasian’ khut sungah | into the hands of God, in whom they believed) (s:muan) (r:43.14.29/58.3.19/43.4.41/43.9.36/44.14.23) (q:draft)
upa = (t:n) (w:elder/leader) (d:an elder or leader of a people, a town or a church; pawlpi upa is a church elder and upa vaihawmte are the ruling council) (e:Gamsung ~ pawlkhat in zong/Judah leh Jerusalem ~ khempeuh kaikhawm hi | he gathered all the elders of Judah and Jerusalem/tokhom tungah a tu uh ~ sawmnih leh lite | the twenty-four elders seated on their thrones/pawlpi ~ khempeuh a na om uh hi | all the elders of the church were present/~ vaihawm tampite nangawn in | even many of the leaders) (s:makai) (r:24.26.17/64.1.1/14.34.29/66.11.16/44.21.18/43.12.42) (q:draft)
upa = (t:adj) (w:elder/older/firstborn) (d:the older one among siblings; tapa upa pen is the eldest or firstborn son and ta upa zaw the older of two children) (e:Ama tapa ~ pen in/a tapa ~ zaw Esau samin | he called his older son Esau/Ishmael’ ta ~ in Nebaioth ahi hi | the firstborn of Ishmael was Nebaioth/a uk ding a tapa ~ pen la-in | he took his firstborn son, who was to reign) (s:uzaw) (a:khangnozaw) (r:13.8.30/1.27.1/1.25.13/12.3.27) (q:draft)
Upa = (t:adj) (w:firstborn/elder) (d:upa, elder, capitalised in ta Upa, the firstborn child, said of the Son) (e:mai-ah zong ta ~ ahi hi) (b:upa) (r:51.1.15) (q:draft)
upadi = (t:n) (w:law/statute/legal code) (d:law of a state or ruler, a word taken from Burmese; in the verses the law of the Medes and Persians and matters of law) (e:Mediate leh Persiate’ ~ bangin/~ tawh kizui-in bangci kihih ding ahi hiam | according to the law, what must be done/~ siam a mi pilte thu dong hi | he consulted the wise men skilled in the law) (s:thukham) (r:27.6.15/17.1.13/17.1.15) (q:draft)
upapen = (t:adj) (w:eldest/oldest/firstborn) (d:upa elder with pen most: the oldest of the brothers or sons) (e:ama u a ~ Eliab in za hi/a ~ thumte in Saul zui uh a | the three oldest followed Saul/Efraim in ka tapa ~ ahi hi | Ephraim is my firstborn son) (s:upen) (a:neupen) (b:upa) (r:9.17.28/9.17.14/24.31.9) (q:draft)
upapente = (t:n) (w:firstborn/eldest sons) (d:upapen, eldest, with the plural te: in tapa upapente, firstborn sons) (e:i tapa ~ leh i bawngte’ tacilte/a tapa ~ uh zong biakna-in ka pia sak | I made them offer even their firstborn sons) (s:cilte) (b:upapen) (r:16.10.36/26.20.26) (q:draft)
upate = (t:n) (w:elders) (d:plural of upa: the elders of a people, a town or a church) (e:Moses leh Israel ~ giahphual ah/tua khua ~ in tua mipa la-in | the elders of that town shall take the man/Sawltakte leh ~ in tua thu vaihawm dingun | the apostles and elders, to consider this matter/siampi liante, laitheite leh ~ in | the chief priests, the teachers of the law and the elders) (b:upa) (r:4.11.30/40.27.41/5.22.18/44.15.6) (q:draft)
upen = (t:adj) (w:oldest/eldest) (d:u, older sibling, with pen, most: the oldest of the brothers and sisters) (e:ama u a ~ Eliab in/Jessi’ tapa a ~ thumte in galdona-ah Saul zui | the three oldest sons of Jesse followed Saul to the war) (s:upapen) (a:neupen) (r:9.17.28/9.17.13) (q:draft)
Uphaz = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Uphaz) (d:place from which gold was brought, its location unknown) (r:24.10.9)
uphuai = (t:adj) (w:trustworthy/worthy of belief/credible) (d:up, believe, with huai, worthy of: deserving to be believed) (e:a ~ a sanhuai thu ahi hi) (s:muanhuai/muantaak) (r:54.1.15) (q:draft)
uphuaina = (t:n) (w:assurance/confidence/certainty) (d:uphuai trustworthy with the noun suffix na; uphuaina tawh ci is say with assurance, assert) (e:ci-in ~ tawh a ci hi) (s:telcianna) (b:uphuai) (r:42.22.59) (q:draft, low confidence)
upin = (t:v) (w:trust/believe) (d:up believe with the suffix in; thu upin nei is hold what someone says as trustworthy, put trust in) (e:thu ~ nei kei inla) (s:muanin) (b:up) (r:33.7.5) (q:draft)
Upkhialh = (t:n) (w:wrong belief/doubt) (d:up, believe, with khialh, err; upkhialh lungsim is apparently a doubting or mistaken mind) (e:~ lungsim nei kei un) (r:42.12.30) (q:draft, low confidence)
upkhialhna = (t:n) (w:doubt/unbelief/wavering) (d:up, believe, with khialh, go wrong, and the noun suffix na: doubt, wavering or lack of faith) (e:a tawp dongin ~ nei loin/~ a nei mi in | the one who doubts/~ tawh Pasian’ thuciamna lungka loin | not wavering in unbelief at the promise of God/amaute’ ~ leh lungkhauhna hangin a mawhsak hi | he rebuked them for their unbelief and stubbornness) (s:uplahna) (a:upna) (r:58.6.11/59.1.6/45.4.20/41.16.14) (q:draft)
uplahna = (t:n) (w:doubt/unbelief) (d:the state of doubting or not believing, the opposite of upna faith; uplahna lungsim is an unbelieving heart) (e:Note in ~ nei hetloin/na lungsim sung uhah ~ om loin | with no doubt in your hearts/mawh nopna ~ lungsim tawh | with a sinful, unbelieving heart) (s:upkhialhna) (a:upna) (r:40.21.21/41.11.23/58.3.12) (q:draft)
uploh = (t:v) (w:not believe/disbelieve/not expect) (d:up, the form of um believe used before a suffix, with loh not: not believing, unbelief; a uploh manin is because they did not believe, and uploh hun is a time that is not expected) (e:Amaute in amah a ~ manin/Amaute in kei hong ~ manun | because they do not believe in me/na hong ~ mah ding uh ahi hi | you should indeed not believe me/~ hun khatin hong tung ding hi | he will come at a time that is not expected) (r:41.6.6/43.16.9/43.10.37/42.17.26) (q:draft)
upmanin = (t:adv) (w:because of believing/through faith) (d:up believe with man, reason, and in: because one believes) (e:i ~ Pasian’ vangliatna in) (r:60.1.5) (q:draft)
upmawh = (t:v) (w:suppose/expect/suspect/think) (d:believe something to be so without being sure) (e:a zi a ~ ciangin/ka ~ bangin thusia a koih kei uh hi | they did not bring the charges I had expected/a neihsa a ~ nangawn kilakhia ding hi | even what he thinks he has will be taken away/note’ ~ loh hun laitakin hong pai ding | he will come at a time you do not expect) (s:ummawh) (r:4.5.30/44.25.18/42.8.18/40.24.44) (q:draft)
upmawhna = (t:n) (w:suspicion/jealousy) (d:suspicion of wrongdoing, in the verses a husband's jealous suspicion of his wife) (e:a pasal in ~ lungsim nei-in/~ hanga an tawh biakna | the grain offering for jealousy/~ thute ah zat ding ngeina | the law to be applied in cases of jealousy) (b:upmawh) (r:4.5.14/4.5.25/4.5.30) (q:draft)
upmawhnate = (t:see) <ki-upmawhnate>
upmawhzah = (t:n) (w:as much as expected/amount supposed) (d:upmawh suppose or expect with zah, amount; na upmawhzah sangun is than you expected) (e:na ~ sangun an na tawmzaw) (r:37.2.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
upna = (t:n) (w:faith/belief) (d:up, believe, with the noun suffix na: faith or belief, trust in God; upna tawh is by faith) (e:~ tawh ka nungta uh hi/Mi kimkhat in tua ~ a nial uh a | some have rejected that faith/thuman thutak na ~ uh tawh | through your belief in the truth/~ thu thukpi a zang ding uh hi | they must hold the deep truths of the faith) (a:uplahna/upkhialhna) (b:up) (r:47.5.7/58.11.2/54.1.19/53.2.13/54.3.9) (q:draft)
upnate = (t:n) (w:beliefs/faith) (d:upna belief with the plural te; a thu upnate uh is the things they believe, their faith) (e:a thu ~ uh ka khawlsak hi) (b:upna) (r:44.26.11) (q:draft)
upnop = (t:v) (w:be willing to believe/be willing to accept) (d:up believe with nop, be willing) (e:Tua thu kigensa na ~ uhleh) (r:40.11.14) (q:draft)
uppa = (t:n) (w:the one believed/the one trusted) (d:up believe with pa, male person: he in whom one believes) (e:ka ~ ka thei a) (s:muanpa) (b:up) (r:55.1.12) (q:draft)
uppih = (t:v) (w:believe together with/share faith with) (d:up believe with pih together with; thu uppih mi, fellow believer) (e:thu ~ mite na it unla/thu ~ mi khat hihna tawh hilhbawl zaw un | rather warn him as a fellow believer/Thu ~ mi khempeuh | all the fellow believers/thu ~ mite it ding tawh kisai-in | about loving fellow believers) (b:up) (r:60.2.17/53.3.15/52.5.26/52.4.9) (q:draft)
upsa = (t:v) (w:believed/convinced of) (d:up believe with sa already: what one has come to believe) (e:na theihsa na ~ thute ah kip) (b:up) (r:55.3.14) (q:draft)
uptheih = (t:v) (w:be able to believe/can believe/may believe) (d:up believe with theih can; mostly as uptheih nading, so that someone may believe) (e:Amah ka ~ nadingin amah kua ahi hiam/ka thugente na ~ nadingun | so that you may believe what I say/hong bangci ~ mah ding na hi uh hiam | how will you be able to believe me/tua khuavak a ~ nadingun | so that they might believe in that light) (s:umzo/upzawh) (b:up) (r:43.9.36/44.15.7/43.14.29/43.5.47/43.1.7) (q:draft)
upzawh = (t:v) (w:be able to believe/come to believe) (d:up believe with zawh, form of zo be able, used before nading) (e:thu a ~ nadingun nakpitakin a gen hi) (s:uptheih/umzo) (r:44.19.8) (q:draft)
Ur = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Ur) (d:city of the Chaldeans in Mesopotamia, the home of Abram before he set out for Canaan) (e:Khaldea gam ~ khua panin) (r:1.15.7/1.11.28) (q:draft)
Ur = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ur) (d:father of Eliphal, one of David's warriors) (r:13.11.35) (q:draft)
Urbanas = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Urbanus) (d:Christian in Rome whom Paul greets as a fellow worker in Christ) (r:45.16.9)
Uri = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Uri) (d:name of several men, among them the son of Hur and father of Bezalel, of the tribe of Judah) (e:Hur’ tapa ahi ~’ tapa Bezalel) (r:2.31.2/13.2.20) (q:draft)
Uriah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Uriah) (d:Hittite, one of the mighty warriors of David and husband of Bathsheba, whom David had killed in battle; also the name of other men) (r:10.23.39/13.11.41)
Uriel = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Uriel) (d:name of two men, a leader of the Kohathite Levites in the time of David and a man of Gibeah, grandfather of King Abijah) (r:13.15.5/14.13.2) (q:draft)
Urijah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Uriah) (d:priest in Jerusalem who built an altar for King Ahaz after the pattern of the one in Damascus) (r:12.16.16/12.16.10)
Urim = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Urim) (d:sacred object kept with the Thummim in the breastpiece of the high priest and used to ask the will of God) (r:3.8.8/9.28.6)
ut = (t:n) (w:desire) (e:ka ~ bang bangin omin ka gamta/tua pen nomau’ ~ ahi hi | that is your own desire/note tawh nekkhop ka ~ mahmah hi | I greatly desire to eat it with you) (s:utna/deihna/lunggulhna) (r:21.2.10/2.10.11/42.22.15)
ut = (t:n) (w:wish) (e:hong dawngkik leh ~ mahmah ing | how I wish he would answer you/note na maang takpi le-uh teh ka ~ hi | I wish you really did reign) (s:utna/deihna) (r:18.11.5/46.4.8)
ut = (t:n) (w:want) (e:khah leeng na ~ uh hiam | do you want me to release him/hong vaksak leteh ka ~ uh hi | we want you to make them see/a ~ mi peuhmah a sam hi | he summoned everyone who was willing) (r:41.15.9/40.20.33/2.36.2)
utbang = (t:n) (w:own wish/own way/what one wants) (d:ut, want, with bang, as: what a person wants, his own way; a utbang peuhin gamta is he does just as he pleases) (e:A ~ peuhin gamta ding a/note’ ~ hithei ngei lo ding hi | what you want will never happen/amau ~ ciatin hong gamtasak hi | he let each of them go their own way) (s:utthu) (r:27.11.28/44.14.16/26.20.32) (q:draft)
utbangin = (t:adv) (w:as one wishes/as one likes) (d:utbang, what one wants, with the ending in: according to one's own wish) (e:note’ ~ gamtat theih nading) (s:ututin/thuthu-in) (b:utbang) (r:46.8.9) (q:draft)
ute = (t:n) (w:elder siblings/elder brothers/brothers) (d:u, elder sibling, with the plural te; ute naute, older and younger siblings, is the usual way of addressing fellow believers as brothers and sisters) (e:~ naute aw, kote ading thu/Ka it ka ~ ka naute aw | my dear brothers and sisters/~ naute in lungdamna tawh hong tungsak uh hi | the brothers and sisters received us gladly/~ naute khempeuh kiangah na simsak nadingun | so that you have it read to all the brothers and sisters) (r:52.5.25/58.13.1/59.1.16/44.21.17/52.5.27) (q:draft)
Uthai = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Uthai) (d:name of two men: a descendant of Judah who lived in Jerusalem after the exile, and a descendant of Bigvai who returned with Ezra) (r:13.9.4/15.8.14)
utin = (t:v) (w:to desire) (d:ut, want, with the linking ending in; mostly doubled as ut utin, as one pleases, freely) (e:thu ka ut ~ ka gen ding/Na ut ~ huan sung singkung khempeuh na nethei | you may freely eat from every tree in the garden/amaute in a ut ~ kei hong bawlsia uh hi | they mistreat me as they please/Kua in khahin a ut ~ vaksak ahi hiam | who untied it and let it roam as it pleases/mi lakah ka ut ~ ka vak kawikawi hi | I went about freely among the people) (b:ut) (r:18.10.1/18.30.11/1.2.16/18.39.5/24.37.4)
utluatna = (t:n) (w:lust/excessive desire) (d:ut, desire, with luat, too much, and the noun suffix na: desire that goes too far, lust) (e:note in ~ tawh na zuih theihzel) (s:duhluatna/deihgawhna) (r:4.15.39) (q:draft)
utna = (t:n) (w:willingness/desire/wish) (d:ut, want, with the noun suffix na: willingness or wish; utna tawh means willingly, of one's own free will, and utna lungsim is a willing mind) (e:~ lungsim tawh pia uh ahih manin/na lungsim khempeuh leh ~ lungsim tawh | with all your heart and a willing mind/mite amau mahmah ~ tawh kipia uh hi | the people offered themselves willingly/ama ~ peuhah na paisak ding hi | you shall let her go wherever she wishes) (s:deihna) (b:ut) (r:13.29.9/7.5.2/13.28.9/5.21.14) (q:draft)
utok = (t:n) (w:lobe of the liver) (d:the lobe attached to the liver of a sacrificed animal, in a sin tunga a utok) (e:a sin tunga a ~ le a kal nihte/a sin pan a ~, a kal nihte | the lobe of the liver and both kidneys) (r:2.29.13/2.29.22) (q:draft)
utong = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:peacock) (d:bird brought by the ships of Tarshish with gold, silver, ivory and apes; the NIV has baboons here, older English versions peacocks) (e:zawngmaw, le ~ hong puak zel hi) (r:14.9.21) (q:draft, low confidence)
utongte = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:peacocks) (d:animals brought by the ships of Tarshish together with apes; the NIV has baboons at this place) (e:zawngmaw, leh ~ hong puak zel hi) (b:utong) (r:11.10.22) (q:draft)
utpi = (t:n) (w:great desire/chief wish) (d:ut desire with pi, great or chief: what one wants most) (e:ka kibat ding ka ~ pen ahi hi) (b:ut) (r:50.3.10) (q:draft)
utsak = (t:v) (w:make willing/prompt/move) (d:ut desire with the causative sak: cause to want, said of the heart) (e:lungsim in a ~ mi peuhmah) (b:ut) (r:2.25.2) (q:draft)
uttawmna = (t:n) (w:free will/own choice/willingness) (d:ut want with tawm, of oneself, and the noun suffix na: what one wants of one's own accord, not forced) (e:nangma ~ tawh na sep/amau lungsimah a ~ uh tawh | of their own accord in their hearts) (s:utthu) (r:57.1.14/47.8.3) (q:draft)
utte = (t:n) (w:those who want/those who love) (d:with a before it: people who are willing or who like to do something) (e:kithuhilh ding a ~ pil semsem hi/Na hotkhiat ding a ~ in | those who long for your salvation/Khialh ding a ~, lungkham ding a ut hi | those who love to do wrong love trouble) (s:deihte/nuamte) (b:ut) (r:20.15.32/20.17.19/19.70.4) (q:draft)
utthu = (t:n) (w:own will/free will/own accord) (d:what one oneself wishes; utthu-a biakpiakna is a freewill offering) (e:Keima ~ tawh a sem hi leng/keima ~ tawh thu a mawkgen ka hi kei | I did not speak on my own/amau ~ tawh hi loin | not by their own choice/~-a biakna-in Topa’ tungah hong paipih uh hi | they brought it to the Lord as a freewill offering) (s:uttawmna) (r:46.9.17/30.4.5/43.12.49/45.8.20/2.35.29) (q:draft)
utun = (t:adv) (w:as they please) (d:in a ut utun, however they wish: ut want, said twice, with un, the plural form of the linking ending in) (e:a ut ~ hong hihsak uh a/amau a mudahte a ut ~ hihgawp uh hi | they did as they pleased to those who hated them/amaute in a ut ~ kei hong bawlsia uh hi | they mistreat me as they please) (s:ututun) (b:ut) (r:16.9.37/17.9.5/18.30.11) (q:draft)
utut = (t:adv) (w:whatever one wants/as one pleases) (d:ut want, doubled: ka utut is whatever I wish) (e:ka ~ ka sep ding) (r:21.2.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
ututin = (t:adv) (w:as one pleases/freely/at will) (d:doing whatever one wants, without restraint or hindrance) (e:a ~ a gamta ding uh hi/a sumte gu-in a ~ a zang zel | he stole the money and used it as he pleased/hangtakin a ~ genin a hilh hi | he spoke and taught boldly and freely/a ~ seektheih nading thu a nei hi | he has the right to shape it as he pleases/na galte un a ~ zang ding uh hi | your enemies will use it as they please) (s:ututun/thuthu-in) (b:utut) (r:27.11.16/44.28.31/43.12.6/45.9.21/26.26.12) (q:draft)
ututna = (t:see) <ututna-ah>
ututna-ah = (t:adv) (w:wherever one wishes/where one likes) (d:ut wish doubled, with the noun suffix na and ah, at: in whatever place one chooses) (e:ama ~ a om theih nadingin) (r:44.28.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
ututun = (t:adv) (w:as one pleases/at will/freely) (d:a ututun is just as they wish, said of more than one person) (e:mi pawlkhatte in a ~ amah a bawl uh hi/na ~ na nethei ding uh hi | you may eat as you please/a ~ sungtumin pusuakin | going in and out as they please/khualna mel nei loin a ~ gamta uh hi | they act as they please, showing no regard/Lai Siangtho sung thu a ~ a kawihei uh | they twist the Scriptures as they please) (s:ututin/thuthu-in) (b:utut) (r:41.9.13/46.10.25/43.10.9/26.22.29/61.3.16) (q:draft)
utzaw = (t:v) (w:prefer/would rather/want more) (d:ut, want, with zaw, more: want one thing more than another) (e:gui-awk ding ka ~ a/man’ loh ding mah na ~ uh a | you preferred not to obey/milim biak ding ~ uh ahihna hang ahi hi | because they preferred to worship idols/Minphat ding sangin minsiat ding ~ uh hi | they prefer shame to honour/mite’ pahtak ding ~ uh ahih manin | because they preferred the praise of people) (s:deihzaw/nuamzaw/teelzaw) (b:ut) (r:18.7.15/23.65.12/26.20.16/28.4.18/43.12.43) (q:draft)
uuk = (t:v) (w:be keen on/be devoted to/delight in/love) (d:be eager for or given over to something; uuk delh, pursue eagerly, hunt down) (e:milim biak ~ lua uh a/gal a ~ mite, thehthang gawp in | scatter the people who delight in war/lei nasep ~ ahih manin | because he loved working the soil/mizawngte ~ delh uh hi | they hunt down the poor) (r:28.4.17/19.68.30/14.26.10/19.10.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
uuklua = (t:v) (w:be too devoted to/be too keen on) (d:uuk be devoted to with lua, too much) (e:milim biak ~ uh a) (b:uuk) (r:28.4.17) (q:draft)
uukna = (t:n) (w:love of/devotion/passion) (d:uuk be keen on with the noun suffix na; gualnop uukna is love of pleasure) (e:gualnop ~’ sila i hi a) (b:uuk) (r:56.3.3) (q:draft)
uuksak = (t:v) (w:win over/make keen) (d:uuk be devoted to with the causative sak: cause people to take to something, said after zol persuade) (e:mi tampi zol a, a ~ cih na mu uh) (b:uuk) (r:44.19.26) (q:draft, low confidence)
uum = (t:v) (w:surround/encircle/crowd around/fence in) (d:be all around a person or place, or put a wall or fence around it; ki-uum is walled, enclosed) (e:mi tampite in amaute ~ uh a/a ithuai khuapi a ~ uh ciangin | when they surrounded the beloved city/teci pan’nate in ei hong ~ ahih ciangin | since witnesses surround us/gawlin ~ a, leenggah cil nading to a | he put a fence around it and dug a winepress) (s:umcih/kiimkot) (r:41.9.14/58.11.30/66.20.9/58.12.1/41.12.1) (q:draft)
uumcip = (t:v) (w:surround/besiege/hem in) (d:uum surround with cip tightly: close in on all sides) (e:Jerusalem khuapi galkapte in a ~/na kimkot ah kan bawlin hong ~ a | they will build an embankment around you and hem you in/Jason’ innah a ~ uh a | they surrounded the house of Jason) (s:umcih) (b:uum) (r:42.21.20/42.19.43/44.17.5) (q:draft)
uumin = (t:v) (w:surrounding/standing around) (d:uum surround with the linking ending in; ki-uumin, with kulh wall, is being walled around, fortified) (e:Judah mite in amah ~/kulh tawh ki-~ lian mahmah hi | fortified with walls and very large) (b:uum) (r:44.25.7/4.13.28) (q:draft)
uun = (t:see) <aw-uun>
Uz = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Uz) (d:name of three men: the firstborn son of Nahor, a son of Aram, and a son of Dishan the Horite) (e:~ in a u pen hi) (r:1.22.21/1.10.23) (q:draft)
Uz = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Uz) (d:land where Job lived, east of Israel and linked with Edom) (e:~ gam sunga kumpite khempeuh) (r:24.25.20) (q:draft)
Uzai = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Uzai) (d:father of Palal, who helped repair the wall of Jerusalem) (e:~’ tapa Palal in a Kiu gal san teng) (r:16.3.25) (q:draft)
Uzal = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Uzal) (d:son of Joktan, a descendant of Shem) (r:1.10.27)
uzaw = (t:adj) (w:older/elder) (d:older of two, or older than another person, the opposite is nauzaw) (e:ka tanu ~ Merab om hi/A ~’ min Leah hi a | the name of the older was Leah/a tapa ~ pen lo kuan hi a | the older son had gone to the field/A ta ~ in a ta nauzaw’ na sem ding hi | the older child will serve the younger) (s:upa) (a:khangnozaw) (r:9.18.17/45.9.12/1.29.16/42.15.25) (q:draft)
Uzmite = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Uz) (d:the people of the land of Uz, named together with Edom) (b:Uz) (r:25.4.21)
uzza = (t:see) <Perez-uzza>
Uzza = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Uzzah/Uzza) (d:name of several men, among them the son of Abinadab who died when he touched the ark, a Merarite Levite and the head of a family of temple servants) (e:~ tungah Topa hehin daan pia) (r:13.13.11/15.2.49) (q:draft)
uzzah = (t:see) <Perez-uzzah>
Uzzah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Uzzah) (d:son of Abinadab who drove the cart carrying the ark and died when he took hold of it) (r:10.6.3/10.6.6)
Uzzenerah = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Uzzen Sheerah) (d:town built by Sheerah, a daughter of the family of Ephraim) (r:13.7.24)
Uzzensheerah = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Uzzen Sheerah) (d:town built by Sheerah, a daughter of the family of Ephraim) (r:13.7.24)
Uzzi = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Uzzi) (d:name of several men, among them a priest, son of Bukki and descendant of Aaron, and an overseer of the Levites in Jerusalem) (r:13.6.5/15.7.4)
Uzzia = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Uzzia) (d:the Ashterathite, one of the mighty warriors of David) (e:Ashterath khuami ~, Aroer khuami Hotham’ tapate) (r:13.11.44) (q:draft)
Uzziah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Uzziah) (d:king of Judah, son of Amaziah and father of Jotham, also called Azariah; also the name of several other men) (r:40.1.9/40.1.8)
Uzziel = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Uzziel) (d:name of several men, among them a son of Kohath and grandson of Levi, uncle of Moses and Aaron) (r:2.6.22)
va = (t:part) (w:go and) (d:placed before a verb to show that the doer goes to another place to do the action: va pai is go there, va dong is go and ask) (e:Ama omna mun-ah ~ pai ni/ama khe-ngakna-ah ~ bia ni | let us go and worship at his footstool/leenggui lo-ah ~ giak ni | let us go and spend the night in the vineyards/gamsate ~ dong un, hong hilh ding uh hi | go and ask the animals and they will teach you/Zeisu ~ dawn hi | she went to meet Jesus) (r:19.132.7/7.11.5/22.7.11/18.12.7/43.11.29) (q:draft)
va = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:bird) (d:first part of bird names such as va-ak raven) (e:~-ak nam khempeuh) (r:3.11.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
va-aknote = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:young ravens) (d:va-ak raven with no, young, and the plural te) (e:a ham ~ an a vak hi) (r:19.147.9) (q:draft)
va-akte = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:ravens/crows) (d:va-ak, raven, with the plural te) (e:~ in ama kiangah zingsangin anlum/hong vaak dingin ~ thu ka pia zo hi | I have ordered the ravens to feed you/keising le ~ om ding uh hi | owls and ravens will live there/~ na lungngai un | consider the ravens) (r:11.17.6/42.12.24/11.17.4/23.34.11) (q:draft)
