vakin = (t:v) (w:lighting/growing light) (d:form of vak, light, with the linking suffix in: lighting a lamp, or of the day growing light) (e:meivak ~ a muh matengin/Meivak ~, a innsung teng phiatin | lighting a lamp and sweeping the whole house/na mei uh ~ a kigingsa-in om unla | keep your lamps lit and be ready/Cik ciangin khua hong ~ zing ka tho tam | when will it grow light so that I may get up) (s:tawhin) (b:vak) (r:42.15.8/42.12.35/18.7.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
vakkhia = (t:v) (w:go out/walk out/wander off) (d:vak, walk about, with khia, out: go out and walk about outside, or wander away from someone) (e:kongzing lakah ka ~ ngam kei uh hi/zanin ~-in mi tawmkhat ka tonpih hi | I set out by night with a few men/kei kiang panin ~ kawikawi nuam uh a | they love to wander away from me) (s:kuankhia/pusuak) (a:lut) (r:25.4.18/16.2.12/24.14.10) (q:draft)
vakkhiat = (t:v) (w:go out/come out/prowl) (d:form of vakkhia, go out, used before a noun such as hun, time: a vakkhiat hun is the time when they come out) (e:ganhing khempeuh a ~ hun in zan) (s:kuankhiat) (b:vakkhia) (r:19.104.20) (q:draft)
vakkhiatkik = (t:v) (w:walk about outside again/go out again) (d:vakkhiat, go out, with kik, again: be up and walking about outside again, as after an injury) (e:ama ciangkhut tawh a ~ zawh nakleh) (b:vakkhiat) (r:2.21.19) (q:draft)
vakkhit = (t:v) (w:finish lighting/have lit) (d:vak, light, with khit, finish: a vakkhit ciangin is after he has lit it) (e:Kuamah in meivak a ~ ciangin) (r:42.11.33) (q:draft)
vakmang = (t:v) (w:wander off/stray/go astray) (d:vak, wander, with mang, away, lost: wander off and be lost, as sheep without a shepherd) (e:mual sang tung khempeuhah ~ uh hi) (s:gammang/zauvak) (r:26.34.6) (q:draft)
vakmawk = (t:v) (w:go about idly/roam aimlessly) (d:vak go about with mawk, idly, for nothing) (e:a ~ uh tawh maisak loin) (r:54.5.13) (q:draft)
vakna = (t:n) (w:feeding/provision/relief) (d:noun of vak, feed: the giving of food or support; an vakna is a meal or provisions, and misiangthote vakna the service of supplying the saints) (e:Misiangthote’ ~ thu note kiangah kong gelh/an ~ a ngah theih nadingin | so that he might receive provisions/misiangthote’ ~ huhna a nasep theih nading uh | to share in the service of helping the saints/gamlakah note kong ~ an | the bread with which I fed you in the wilderness) (s:vaakna/anvakna) (r:47.9.1/42.12.36/44.27.3/47.8.4/2.16.32) (q:draft, low confidence)
vakna = (t:n) (w:light/lighting) (d:noun of vak, give light: the giving of light; mei vakna is lighting by a lamp) (e:Mei ~ meivak khuam pen/Mei ~ meikhuam pen, a meivakte | the lampstand for light and its lamps) (b:vak) (r:4.4.9) (q:draft)
vakpa = (t:n) (w:sustainer/nourisher/provider) (d:vak, also written vaak, feed, with pa, male person: the one who feeds and provides) (e:na khanghamna-ah hong ~ hi ding hi) (s:vaakpa) (r:8.4.15) (q:draft)
vakpih = (t:v) (w:lead about/walk about with) (d:vak walk about with pih, together with: take someone along while walking about) (e:Tua guhte lakah hong ~ kawikawi a) (r:26.37.2) (q:draft)
vaksa = (t:see) <vaksa-in>
vaksa-in = (t:adv) (w:lit/burning) (d:vak light with sa, already done, and in: with the lamp already lit) (e:meivak ~ na om un) (r:42.12.35) (q:draft)
vaksak = (t:v) (w:be light/give light/light up) (d:vak, be light, with the causative sak: make light, give light to a place, a lamp or the eyes; mit vaksak is to give sight) (e:leitung khua a ~ dingin vantungah/leitung a, piang mi khempeuh a ~ hi | it gives light to everyone born in the world/Ka Pasian in ka khuamial ~ hi | my God lights up my darkness/Zeisu in buan bawlin mit a ~ ni | the day Jesus made mud and opened the eyes/Ka mittang hong ~ hi napi-in | though he opened my eyes) (a:mialsak) (b:vak) (r:1.1.15/43.1.9/10.22.29/43.9.14/43.9.30)
vaksakkikin = (t:v) (w:giving light again/brightening again) (d:vaksak give light with kik, again, and the suffix in; said of the eyes) (e:ka mit uh hong ~ ka salsuahna uhah) (r:15.9.8) (q:draft)
vaksakpa = (t:n) (w:the one who opened/the one who gave sight) (d:vaksak give light with pa, male person; with mit, the man who made the eyes see) (e:Na mit hong ~ kua tawh kibang) (b:vaksak) (r:43.9.17) (q:draft)
vaksuk = (t:v) (w:go about/go to and fro) (d:vak, walk, with suk, downward; used in the pair vaksuk vakto, walk down and up, meaning go here and there through a place) (e:amaute va kuankhia-in ~ vakto-in/mi gensia-in ~ vakto loin | without going about slandering people/na ~ na vaktohna-ah nang hong kem ding hi | he will watch over your coming and going/Na omna mun, na ~ na vaktohna | where you stay and your coming and going) (r:6.18.4/3.19.16/19.121.8/23.37.28) (q:draft)
vakthap = (t:v) (w:wander/roam/go about) (d:go about from place to place; in 2 Thessalonians 3:11 of idle people who go about meddling in the affairs of others) (e:Gamla pekah ka ~ ding a/a ~ mi kimkhat a om hi | there are some who go about meddling) (s:kawivak) (r:19.55.7/53.3.11) (q:draft)
vakto = (t:v) (w:go up/go about) (d:vak, walk, with to, upward; used in the pair vaksuk vakto, walk down and up, meaning go to and fro or travel all over a place) (e:Vaksuk ~-in leitang ciamtehna hong gelh un/va kuankhia-in vaksuk ~-in | going out and walking all over it/mi gensia-in vaksuk ~ loin | without going about slandering people) (r:6.18.8/3.19.16/6.18.4) (q:draft)
vaktohna = (t:n) (w:going up/going about) (d:vakto, walk up, in its form vaktoh with the noun suffix na; used in the pair na vaksuk na vaktohna, your going down and going up, all your coming and going) (e:na vaksuk na ~ le keima tungah/na vaksuk na ~-ah nang hong kem ding hi | he will watch over your coming and going) (r:23.37.28/19.121.8) (q:draft)
vakvai = (t:n) (w:wanderer) (d:a person with no settled home who goes from place to place) (e:leitunga a ~ na hi ding hi/leitungah a ~ ka hi ding a | I will be a wanderer on the earth/Minam dangte lakah a ~ mite suak ding uh | they will become wanderers among the nations/Israelte mi ~ ka hi sak nawn kei ding | I will not make Israel wanderers again) (r:1.4.12/28.9.17/1.4.14/12.21.7)
vakvai = (t:n) (w:traveller)
vakvaisak = (t:v) (w:make wander/cause to wander) (d:vakvai, wander, with the causative sak: make someone wander without a path) (e:lampi om lohna gamlakah ~ hi/lampi om lohna gam sungah amaute a ~ hi | he made them wander in a trackless land) (s:kawikawisak) (b:vakvai) (r:18.12.24/19.107.40) (q:draft)
vakzau = (t:see) <vakzau-in>
vakzau-in = (t:v) (w:roam about/go around freely) (d:vak go about with zau and the suffix in; here of going about with other men, the Zolai text differs from the NIV; force of zau not confirmed) (e:Pasal dang tawh va ~ kongzing lakah) (r:20.5.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
vakzaw = (t:v) (w:feed rather/nourish instead) (d:vak, also written vaak, feed, with zaw, rather, more) (e:hoihtakin kemin a ~ hi) (r:49.5.29) (q:draft)
vakzo = (t:v) (w:be able to feed) (d:vak, also written vaak, feed, with zo, be able) (e:leitung bup a ~ ding gah) (r:27.4.21) (q:draft)
val = (t:v) (w:exceed/be more than/be left over) (d:be more than a number or amount, or be left over as a surplus; after a number it means more than, as sawmli val, more than forty) (e:sawmli ~ pha hi/kicing a, ~ zaw lai hi | it was enough and more than enough/kamgen bangin pawlkhat ~ lai hi | some was left over, as he had said/a tam a kaikhawmpa aa dim ~ lo a | the one who gathered much had nothing over/a kicing ding zah ~ tampi | much more than enough) (s:vallai) (a:dimlah/kitasam) (r:44.23.13/2.36.7/12.4.44/2.16.18/2.36.5) (q:draft)
valh = (t:v) (w:swallow/devour) (d:take food or drink down the throat; also of the earth, fire or an enemy that swallows people up; valh tum is swallow whole) (e:a kam ka-in a ~ hi/saipi na ~ uh hi | you swallow a camel/vantung panin mei kia-in tua mite a ~ hi | fire fell from heaven and devoured them/Korah tawh amaute ~ tum a | it swallowed them together with Korah) (s:valhtum/nawmvalh) (a:luakhia) (r:66.12.16/4.16.32/40.23.24/66.20.9/4.26.10) (q:draft)
valhcip = (t:v) (w:swallow up/engulf/hold captive) (d:valh swallow with cip, tightly, completely: hold fast as if swallowed) (e:mawhna in hong ~ mi khat) (b:valh) (r:44.8.23) (q:draft)
valhtum = (t:v) (w:swallow/swallow up/devour) (d:valh, swallow, with tum, go in: swallow whole, so that nothing is left) (e:lei kihongin Dathan ~ a/Aaron’ ciangkhut in amau’ ciangkhutte a ~ hi | Aaron’s staff swallowed their staffs/Bang hangin Topa’ gamhluah ~ ding na hi hiam | why would you swallow up the Lord’s inheritance/Leitang in hong ~ kha in teh | the earth will swallow us too) (s:valh/nawmvalh/netum) (a:luakhia) (r:19.106.17/23.49.19/2.7.12/10.20.19/4.16.34) (q:draft)
valhtumin = (t:v) (w:swallowing/swallowing up/devouring) (d:valhtum swallow up with the linking ending in) (e:neih khempeuh tawh hih mite ~/Jerusalem khua hong ~, hong sukham gawp hi | he has devoured Jerusalem and crushed it) (s:netumin) (b:valhtum) (r:4.16.30/24.51.34) (q:draft)
valin = (t:adv) (w:extra/in excess/beyond) (d:val, be over, with the adverb ending in; a valin is more than what is asked or needed) (e:puan-ak zong a ~ kengthuah kei un/a ~ tai khat sung mah na puaksak lai | carry it for him one more mile/a kituakzah ~ kilian ngaihsutzaw kha kei un | do not think of yourselves more highly than is fitting/banah a ~ hong thupi ngaihsutkhak ding uh | that they might think more of me than that) (b:val) (r:42.9.3/40.5.41/45.12.3/47.12.6) (q:draft)
valkhia = (t:v) (w:extend beyond/be left over/overhang) (d:val exceed with khia, out: the part that goes beyond) (e:Puanbuk puan a ~, puan a lang) (b:val) (r:2.26.12) (q:draft)
valkhong = (t:adv) (w:for nothing/to no purpose) (d:in a valkhong a, namsau tawi ahi kei hi: he does not carry the sword for nothing; the parts of the word are not confirmed) (e:a ~ a, namsau tawi ahi kei hi | he does not bear the sword for nothing) (s:mawk) (r:45.13.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
valkhongsak = (t:v) (w:neglect/let go to waste) (d:let something lie unused; with kei, do not neglect a gift or an opportunity) (e:nangma hihtheih siamnate na ~ kei in/na ngah khempeuh uh na ~ ngei kei un | never let anything you are given go to waste) (b:valkhong) (r:54.4.14/51.4.5) (q:draft)
vallai = (t:v) (w:be left over/remain/exceed) (d:val, be over, with lai, still: be still left when the rest is used or counted; a vallai teng is the rest, what is left) (e:gensa bangin pawlkhat a ~ hi/a ~ mite tung panin kitatkhiatna sum la a | he took the redemption money from those who were over/a kicing nei-in tampi ~ hi | we had enough and plenty was left over/a si ~ teng a sungkhia hi | he poured out the rest of the blood) (s:val/omlai) (a:dimlah) (r:12.4.44/23.44.17/4.3.49/14.31.10/3.9.9) (q:draft)
valmawk = (t:v) (w:be void/be of no effect) (d:with sak, make void, nullify, set aside) (e:Pasian’ thukham na ~ sak uh hi) (r:40.15.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
valsak = (t:v) (w:waste/make void/nullify) (d:with mawk, for nothing: let something be left over to no purpose, make it of no effect) (e:bangmah mawk ~ kei ni/Pasian thu na mawk ~ uh hi | you make the word of God void) (b:val) (r:43.6.12/41.7.13) (q:draft)
valte = (t:n) (w:those more than/those over) (d:val exceed with the plural te; mi zanga valte is the more than five hundred people) (e:Tua mi zanga ~, pawlkhat a sih) (b:val) (r:46.15.6) (q:draft)
valteng = (t:n) (w:rest/remainder/what is left) (d:val, be left over, with teng, all of: all that remains after a part is taken) (e:An tawh biakna a ~ pen/a nek ~ a khe tawh a tuancilgawp hi | it trampled underfoot what was left of what it ate) (s:omlaiteng/laiteng) (b:val) (r:3.2.10/27.7.7) (q:draft)
valun = (t:v) (w:exceeding/going beyond) (d:val exceed with un, the suffix in for more than one person; zah valun is beyond the measure) (e:kingaihsut ding zah ~ kithupi ngaihsut kei un) (b:val) (r:45.12.3) (q:draft)
valzaw = (t:v) (w:be more than enough/be in excess) (d:val exceed with zaw, more) (e:kicing a, ~ lai hi) (b:val) (r:2.36.7) (q:draft)
vamimte = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:quails) (d:plural form: quails, the birds God sent as food for Israel in the wilderness) (e:Nitak ciangin ~ hong tungin giahphual tuam/tuipi panin ~ hong puak a | it brought quail from the sea/mite ding-in ~ khawm uh hi | the people went out and gathered quail/~ leh vantung panin anlum tampi a pia hi | he gave them quail and plenty of bread from heaven) (r:2.16.13/4.11.32/4.11.31/19.105.40) (q:draft)
van = (t:n) (w:heaven/sky) (d:the sky and heaven above the earth; van leh lei is heaven and earth) (e:na itna kip in ~ ban a/Topa aa ci un, ~ mite aw | ascribe to the Lord, you heavenly beings/dikna a om ~ thak leh lei thak | a new heaven and a new earth where righteousness dwells/tua ~ kuumpi in tui leh tui kikhensak hen | let that vault of the sky separate water from water) (s:vantung/vanpi) (a:lei/leitung) (r:19.36.5/1.1.6/19.29.1/61.3.13)
van = (t:n) (w:point)
Van = (t:n) (w:heaven/sky) (d:van, heaven, at the start of a clause; van nuai is under heaven) (e:~ nuai leitungah lim ka lak ding hi/~ leh lei a bawl Topa | the Lord, the Maker of heaven and earth/~ sangpente leh vante tunga om tuite aw | you highest heavens and you waters above the skies/~-a aksi sangin a tam zaw-in | more numerous than the stars of the sky) (s:Vantung/vanpi) (a:leitung) (b:van) (r:44.2.19/19.115.15/19.148.4/34.3.16) (q:draft)
vana = (t:n) (w:heaven/of the sky) (d:van, heaven or sky, with the ending a, of or in: of the sky, as in vana vasate, the birds of the air, and vana aksi, the stars of the sky) (e:~ vasate zong a leengmang khin uh hi/~ aksi zah leh tuipi gei-a sehnel zahin | as many as the stars of the sky and the sand by the sea/kua’ sung panin ~ vukte hong suak | from whose womb comes the frost of heaven/~ vasate in a hiangah a tuang thei uh | the birds of the air can perch on its branches) (b:van) (r:24.4.25/18.38.29/58.11.12/42.13.19) from heaven
vanah = (t:adv) (w:in heaven/in the sky) (d:van, heaven or sky, with the place marker ah; vanah vasate are the birds of the air) (e:~ a om vangliatnate a kiliing ding/~ vasate in a lim belh dingin | so that the birds of the air can shelter in its shade/Mihingte’ kha ~ kahto-in | the human spirit rises upward/lim lamdang adang khat mah ~ hong kilang leuleu | another strange sign appeared in heaven/Pasian’ Kha in ~ hong leen’pih to-in | the Spirit of God lifted me up into the air) (s:vantunga) (a:leitunga) (b:van) (r:41.13.25/66.12.3/41.4.32/21.3.21/26.8.3) (q:draft)
vandaituite = (t:n) (w:dew of heaven) (d:van heaven with daitui dew and the plural te) (e:vantung pan ~ na ngah kei ding hi) (r:1.27.39) (q:draft)
vandak = (t:v) (w:look upward/look up to the sky) (d:van sky with dak, look up) (e:a Pasian uh hamsiatin ~ ding uh hi) (s:ento) (r:23.8.21) (q:draft)
vang = (t:n) (w:opening/hole/gap) (d:an opening, hole or gap; kong vang is a gate or doorway, han vang the mouth of a tomb, and kulh vang a gap in a wall) (e:sak lamah kong ~ thum/Han ~ pan suang kilikkhia a | the stone was rolled away from the mouth of the tomb/kulh ~ teng huk ding a kipat khitna thu | that the gaps in the wall were being closed/puan ngawng ~ bangin | like the opening of a collar) (s:kuavang/gong) (r:66.21.13/42.24.2/16.4.7/2.39.23) (q:draft)
vang = (t:n) (w:power/might/glory) (d:power or might, and the shining glory of God; minthanna vang is glorious splendour, and a vang lian means he is powerful) (e:Pasian’ ~ in tua khuapi a tangsak a/Topa’ ~ tawh amaute ka sugawp hi | by the power of the Lord I cut them down/Nangma ~ lian mahmah a | your power is very great/amaute’ ~ a beina | that their strength is gone/keima ~ in tua mun siangthosak ding hi | my glory will make that place holy) (s:vangliatna/vaang/thahatna) (a:thanemna) (r:66.21.23/19.118.11/19.89.13/5.32.36/2.29.43) (q:draft)
vang = (t:v) (w:prosper/succeed) (d:used after ma or maa, the way ahead: ma vang is to go forward well, to succeed in what one does) (e:a nasepna khempeuh ah a ma ~ hi/na lungdamin na ma ~ ding hi | you will be happy and prosper/lungsim khempeuh tawh sem a, a ma ~ hi | he worked with all his heart and prospered/na maa ~ ding a, na nasep tangtung ding | you will prosper and your work will succeed) (s:maavang/mavang) (r:14.32.30/19.128.2/14.31.21/6.1.8) (q:draft)
vangah = (t:n) (w:in the hole/at the opening) (d:vang opening with ah, at or into the opening; phim vangah is through the eye of a needle and han kong vangah at the mouth of the tomb) (e:Sai khat phim ~ a khumhak sangin/han kong ~ suangpeek lian khat lik a | he rolled a big stone against the entrance of the tomb/A ~ lim kigelhte om hi | around its opening there were engravings/Sakol Kongpi ~ paikhiatpihin | taking her out to the entrance of the Horse Gate) (s:gongah) (b:vang) (r:42.18.25/40.27.60/11.7.31/14.23.15) (q:draft)
vangik = (t:n) (w:burden/load/weight) (d:a heavy load that is carried; also a person or task that is hard to bear) (e:kei adingin ~ na hi ding hi/kei adingin ~ lua hi | it is too heavy a burden for me/amaute in ~ hong puakpih ding uh hi | they will share the load with you/ama tunga ~ teng kisia ding hi | the load hanging on it will be destroyed) (r:10.15.33/19.81.6/4.11.14/2.18.22/23.22.25) (q:draft)
vangikpi = (t:n) (w:heavy burden/burden/heavy load) (d:vangik, burden, with pi, great: a heavy burden; with suan, lay a heavy burden on someone) (e:mite tungah ~ suan uh a/ka nungzang uh-ah ~ nong suan hi | you laid heavy burdens on our backs/na liangko panun ama ~ kinkhia ding a | his burden will be lifted from your shoulders/kei a dingin ~ khat suakkhin a | they have become a heavy burden to me) (b:vangik) (r:16.5.15/19.66.11/23.10.27/23.1.14) (q:draft)
vangiksak = (t:v) (w:burden/weigh down) (d:vangik, burden, with the causative sak: lay a burden on someone, weigh someone down) (e:Piakna tawh nang kong ~ nai kei a) (s:gimsak) (b:vangik) (r:23.43.23) (q:draft)
vangikte = (t:n) (w:burdens/loads) (d:plural of vangik, burden) (e:na khut uha ~ ka hong khiasak/na liangko uha om na ~ uh | your burdens that are on your shoulders) (b:vangik) (r:19.81.6) (q:draft)
vangin = (t:v) (w:thunder/rumble) (d:van sky with gin sound; written vangin’na, with the noun suffix na, for thunder) (e:~’na tawh a pusuak uh hi) (r:66.4.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
vangin = (t:n) (w:might/power) (d:vang power with the marker in: vaihawmna le vangin ngaihsun is to count something as counsel and might) (e:galdo nadingin vaihawmna le ~ ngaihsun) (b:vang) (r:23.36.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
vanging = (t:n) (w:thunder) (d:thunder, the loud sound from the sky in a storm; from van, sky, and ging, sound) (e:~ tate a cihnopna/~ pen ama hong pai nading a kitheihna ahi | the thunder is the sign of his coming/~ sagihte in amau kam awte a gen uh | the seven thunders spoke with their voices/Na ~ lianpi pingpei sungah om-in | your mighty thunder was in the whirlwind) (r:41.3.17/18.36.33/66.10.3/19.77.18) (q:draft)
vangingte = (t:n) (w:thunders/thunder/peals of thunder) (d:plural of vanging, thunder: peals of thunder, often named together with khuaphialepte, flashes of lightning) (e:zingsang ciangin ~ leh khuaphialepte omin/khuaphialepte, awte, ~ a piang uh hi | there came flashes of lightning, rumblings and peals of thunder/mite khempeuh in ~, khuaphialepte, peengkul aw | all the people perceived the thunder, the lightning and the trumpet sound/~’ zuih ding lampi a bawlsak laitak | when he made a path for the thunder) (b:vanging) (r:2.19.16/66.16.18/2.20.18/18.28.26) (q:draft)
vanglian = (t:adj) (w:mighty/powerful/almighty) (d:vang, power, with lian, great: having great power; a vanglian Topa is the Lord Almighty) (e:a ~ Pasian kiangah ciahkik ding hi/Nimrod in leitungah a ~ masa mi ahi hi | Nimrod was the first mighty man on earth/amah pilin a ~ hi | he is wise and powerful/A ~ Topa in a cih-inah | this is what the Lord Almighty says) (s:thahat/hat) (a:thanem/zawngkhal) (r:23.10.21/1.10.8/27.2.20/24.49.35)
Vanglian = (t:adj) (w:Almighty/Mighty) (d:capitalised as a title of God: Vanglian Pasian, God Almighty) (e:~ Pasian in kei hong ompih a/~ Pasian in ka lungsim hanna hong maimangsak hi | the Almighty has made my heart faint/Lebanon mual pen ~ Pa’ mai-ah puk ding hi | Lebanon will fall before the Mighty One/Thutang a deih, ~ Kumpipa aw | O mighty King, lover of justice) (s:Vanglianpen) (b:vanglian) (r:18.29.5/23.10.34/18.23.16/19.99.4) (q:draft)
vanglianin = (t:adv) (w:powerfully/mightily/with power) (d:vanglian, mighty, with the ending in: being mighty, in a mighty way) (e:thungetna in nakpi ~ muibun mahmah hi/amah ~, kipahtawi ding hi | he will be mighty and honoured) (b:vanglian) (r:59.5.16/19.112.9) (q:draft)
vanglianpa = (t:n) (w:mighty one) (d:vanglian, mighty, with pa, male person: a mighty man, a warrior or hero) (e:A ~ bangci-in tuk/a ~’ lum nin hi | the shield of the mighty was defiled/a ~ bangin amau kumpite ka sugawp hi | like a mighty one I subdued their kings) (s:hatpa) (b:vanglian) (r:10.1.19/10.1.25/10.1.21/23.10.13)
Vanglianpa = (t:n) (w:Almighty/Mighty One) (d:vanglianpa written with a capital, title of God) (e:~’ liim sungah a om mi/~’ hehpih ding thuum lecin | if you plead with the Almighty for mercy/~ in thuman zang lo ahi hiam | does the Almighty pervert what is right/~, Topa ahi Pasian, hong pau a | the Mighty One, God, the Lord, speaks) (b:vanglianpa) (r:19.91.1/18.8.5/18.8.3/19.50.1) (q:draft)
Vanglianpen = (t:adj) (w:Almighty/most powerful) (d:title of God, literally the most powerful; Vanglianpen Topa renders the Lord Almighty or the Lord of hosts) (e:~ Topa in kei tungah thu hong gen/~ Topa in amah tawh om ahih manin | because the Lord Almighty was with him/~ Topa aw, na teen’na mun | Lord Almighty, your dwelling place/~ Topa zong lo uh hi | they have not sought the Lord Almighty) (s:Vanglian) (b:Vanglian) (r:38.8.1/13.11.9/19.84.1/23.9.13) (q:draft)
vanglianpi = (t:n) (w:great power/might/majesty) (d:vanglian, mighty, with pi, great: vanglianpi tawh is with great power; in Hebrews 8:1 the Majesty in heaven) (e:~ tawh Pasian’ Ukna hong tung/~ tawh hong bawlphatna bangin semin | working as he powerfully works in me/vantung ~ tokhom ziat lamah tu-in a om hi | he is seated at the right hand of the throne of the Majesty in heaven) (s:vangpi) (b:vanglian) (r:41.9.1/58.8.1/51.1.29) (q:draft)
vangliante = (t:adj) (w:mighty) (d:plural form of vanglian, the mighty ones, or after a plural noun as in kumpi vangliante, mighty kings) (e:minam tampite vatmai-in kumpi ~ that a/Amah in mi ~ mindaisak a | he puts the mighty to shame/mihaute le mi ~, silate le sila ahi lote | the rich and the mighty, slave and free/thu kan kul loin mi ~ sugawp a | without inquiry he shatters the mighty) (b:vanglian) (r:19.135.10/18.34.24/18.12.21/66.6.15) (q:draft)
vanglianzaw = (t:adj) (w:mightier/stronger/more powerful) (d:vanglian mighty with zaw more) (e:Amaute sangin a ~, a tamzaw minamin/hatzaw-in a ~ vantung mite nangawn in | even angels, who are stronger and more powerful) (s:hatzaw/thahatzaw) (b:vanglian) (r:5.9.14/61.2.11) (q:draft)
vangliat = (t:adj) (w:powerful/mighty/glorious) (d:form of vanglian used before zawk, nading, mahmahna and the like) (e:a hat zawk, a ~ zawk uh hangin/Pasian a ~ mahmahna limtakin phawktel in | consider well how very mighty God is/khuamial sung a uk Satan’ ~ hunsung ahi hi | it is the time of the power of Satan, who rules in the darkness/ama ~ tawntung minthan’na ah hong sam | who called you into his eternal glory) (r:61.2.11/18.36.22/42.22.53/60.5.10) (q:draft)
vangliatna = (t:n) (w:power/might/strength) (d:vangliat, the form of vanglian, mighty, with the noun suffix na: great power or might, above all the power of God) (e:Pasian’ ~ lamdang a sa uh hi/a tawntungin ~ nei ta hen | to him be the power forever/na ~ thu sut ding uh a | they will speak of your might/Nangma ~ la sa-in kong phat ding uh hi | we will sing and praise your might/~ tawh hih mun panin note hong paikhiatpih hi | he brought you out of this place by his power) (s:thahatna/hatna/vang) (a:thanemna) (r:42.9.43/60.5.11/19.145.11/19.21.13/2.13.3) (q:draft)
vangliatna = (t:n) (w:glory/majesty) (d:the greatness and splendour of God that is shown to people) (e:A ~ a lah nading) (s:minthanna) (r:45.9.23) (q:draft, low confidence)
vangliatnate = (t:n) (w:powers/authorities) (d:plural of vangliatna, power; beings or forces that hold power, in heaven or on earth) (e:a ukte leh ~ in ama nuai-ah/vantung a, om ~, leh leitung kumpite | the powers in the heavens and the kings on the earth/vantungah a om ukna leh ~ in | the rulers and authorities in the heavenly realms) (s:vangneite) (b:vangliatna) (r:60.3.22/23.24.21/49.3.10) (q:draft)
vangliatnate = (t:n) (w:miracles/mighty works) (d:plural of vangliatna, power: deeds that show the power of God, miracles) (e:nalamdangte leh dipkuat huaite, ~ tawh | with signs, wonders and miracles/nangma sungah a kilak ~ | the miracles that were performed in you/Tua ahih manin hih ~ nei hi | that is why he has these miraculous powers) (s:nalamdangte) (b:vangliatna) (r:47.12.12/40.11.23/41.6.14) (q:draft)
vangneite = (t:n) (w:powers/powerful ones) (d:vang power with nei have and the plural te: those who have power; in Galatians 4:3 of the spiritual powers ruling the air) (e:huihlak a uk ~’ khutnuai-ah) (s:vangliatnate) (r:48.4.3) (q:draft)
vangneu = (t:n) (w:small opening/narrow window) (d:vang opening with neu small; khua-etna vangneu is a narrow window to look out through) (e:pangah khua-etna ~ om a) (r:26.40.16) (q:draft)
vangneute = (t:n) (w:small openings/narrow windows) (d:vangneu small opening with the plural te) (e:a kong ~, leh nisuh kung lim) (b:vangneu) (r:26.40.22) (q:draft)
vangpi = (t:n) (w:great power/great might) (d:vang power with pi great) (e:Nangma ~ le na khut tawh/Nangma’ ~ leh na khut kizankhia tawh | by your great power and outstretched arm) (s:vanglianpi) (b:vang) (r:24.32.17) (q:draft)
vangsak = (t:v) (w:make successful/prosper/grant success) (d:used with ma or lampi, the way ahead: make a journey or undertaking succeed) (e:tu ni-in ka ma hong ~ in/na lampi hong ~ ding hi | he will make your journey a success/ka maa hong ~ khin ahih nungsang | now that he has made my journey succeed/khualzinna ma ~ ding hiam ~ lo ding hiam | whether or not he would make the journey succeed) (s:mavangsak) (b:vang) (r:1.24.12/1.24.40/1.24.56/1.24.21) (q:draft)
vangsung = (t:n) (w:inner width/diameter) (d:vang opening with sung, inside: the measure across the inside of a basin) (e:tuikuang ~ pi guk ciat pha) (r:11.7.38) (q:draft, low confidence)
vangtaang = (t:n) (w:glory/splendour/radiance) (d:shining glory, usually after minthanna; a vangtaang is glorious) (e:minthanna ~ i kilangsak hi/Topa’ minthanna ~ Pasian’ biakinn sung a dim hi | the glory of the Lord filled the temple of God/A maitang panin a ~ a beilam | the fading of the radiance from his face/nidangin minthangin a ~ mahmah i cih | what we once called glorious) (s:minthanna) (r:47.3.18/14.5.14/47.3.13/47.3.10) (q:draft)
vangte = (t:n) (w:openings/gaps/breaches) (d:plural of vang, opening; kong vangte is gates, tawlet vangte is windows) (e:tawlet ~ panin sihna hong lutin/khuapi kong ~, kulhte teh nadingin | to measure the city gates and walls/a pa David khuapi a ~ hu hi | he closed the gaps in the city of David his father/tawlet ~ bawl a, Taamtaak singpek tawh thuap | he makes windows and panels it with cedar) (b:vang) (r:24.9.21/11.11.27/66.21.15/24.22.14) (q:draft)
vangtung = (t:n) (w:heaven) (d:another spelling of vantung, heaven, the dwelling place of God) (e:na teenna ~ panin) (s:vantung/van) (a:leitung) (r:14.6.39)
vangtungah = (t:n) (w:on heaven/in heaven/in the sky) (d:vangtung, heaven, with the place marker ah: in the sky, in heaven) (e:Pasian in tuate ~ koih hi) (b:vangtung) (r:1.1.17)
vangtungmi = (t:n) (w:angel) (d:vangtung, heaven, with mi, person: an angel, a messenger from heaven; another spelling of vantungmi) (e:Topa’ ~ khat hong kilang a/Pasian in a ~ Gabriel a sawl hi | God sent his angel Gabriel) (s:vantungmi) (b:vangtung) (r:42.1.11/42.1.27) (q:draft)
vangvang = (t:adv) (w:bitterly/intensely) (d:placed after a verb to show that the action is done strongly or without letting go; kap vangvang is wail bitterly) (e:sih suah bangin kap ~ in/kumpipa’ mit la ~ hi | it holds the eyes of the king captive) (r:24.6.26/22.7.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
Vaniah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Vaniah) (d:one of the descendants of Bani who had married a foreign wife in the time of Ezra) (r:15.10.36)
vanin = (t:v) (w:waving/motioning/gesturing) (d:move the hand through the air as a sign, with the linking ending in; a khut vanin is waving or motioning with the hand; also written vaanin) (e:a natna mun tungah a khut ~/a khut ~ thugen ding hong kipan a | motioning with his hand he began to speak/Mangpipa in a khut ~ | the governor motioning with his hand) (s:vaanin) (r:12.5.11/44.24.10/44.13.16) (q:draft)
vankah = (t:n) (w:medium) (d:a person who calls up the spirits of the dead; often as vankah thei, one who is able to do this) (e:~ khat thu dongin a lamlah ding/Edor-ah ~ thei khat om hi | there is a medium in Endor/~ thei numei khat kei adingin hong zon’sak un | find me a woman who is a medium/~ theite leh aisante tawh na sem hi | he worked with mediums and spiritists) (s:vankahthei) (r:13.10.13/9.28.7/14.33.6)
vankahna = (t:n) (w:divination/spiritism/consulting of mediums) (d:vankah, medium, with the noun suffix na: the practice of seeking word from the spirits of the dead) (e:~ leh aisanna zang uh a/Mi khat ~ leh ai saanna lamah kihei-in | if a person turns to mediums and spiritists) (s:aisan) (b:vankah) (r:12.17.17/3.20.6) (q:draft)
vankahte = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:gecko)
vankahte = (t:n) (w:medium/mediums) (d:vankah, medium, with the plural te) (e:~ leh aisante a gamsung panin beisak/gam sung panin ~ leh aisante a suksiatna | his cutting off the mediums and spiritists from the land/~, aisante, innsung pasiante, milimte | mediums, spiritists, household gods, idols) (s:vankahtheite) (b:vankah) (r:9.28.3/12.23.24/9.28.9)
vankahthei = (t:n) (w:medium/spiritist) (d:vankah, medium, with thei, be able: a person who is able to call up the spirits of the dead) (e:Endor-ah ~ khat om hi/~ numei khat kei a dingin hong zonsak un | find me a woman who is a medium) (s:vankah) (b:vankah) (r:9.28.7) (q:draft)
vankahtheite = (t:n) (w:mediums/spiritists) (d:vankahthei, medium, with the plural te) (e:~ leh aisante tawh nasem hi) (s:vankahte) (b:vankahthei) (r:12.21.6) (q:draft)
vankemte = (t:n) (w:treasurers) (d:van, goods, with kem, keep, and the plural te: the officials who keep the stores and money of a king) (e:kumpi ~ khempeuh tungah hih bangin) (r:15.7.21) (q:draft)
vankhai = (t:n) (w:peg/hook) (d:van, thing, with khai, hang: a peg or hook on which things are hung) (e:~ ah a kikhai bangin/a kikheen ~ in lel ding hi | the peg that was driven in will give way/khuampi tunga ~ nadingin bawlin | making it into hooks for the posts) (s:khaina) (r:23.22.24/23.22.25/2.38.28) (q:draft)
vankhaina = (t:n) (w:peg/hook/hanger) (d:van, things, with khai, hang, and the noun suffix na: a peg or hook to hang things on) (e:a kician mun khatah ~ bangin ka khenkip/kham kibawl ~ nei-in | having hooks made of gold) (s:khaina) (b:vankhai) (r:23.22.23/2.26.32) (q:draft)
vankhainate = (t:n) (w:hooks/clasps) (d:plural of vankhaina, a thing on which something is hung or fastened, as the hooks and clasps of the tabernacle) (e:a ~ leh a gaknate in ngun/a ~ ngun hi-in a bullente sumngo | its hooks are silver and its bases bronze/a ~ leh a khuampeekte | its clasps and its frames/a khuampi ngate a ~ tawh bawl hi | he made the five posts with their hooks) (s:kilhnate) (b:vankhaina) (r:2.38.10/2.35.11/2.27.17/2.36.38) (q:draft)
vankia = (t:n) (w:plunder/spoil) (d:goods taken in war; the other text has vankila in the same verse, so this may be a misprint of it) (e:Shinar panin ~ lakah puanhoih khat) (s:vankila) (r:6.7.21) (q:draft, low confidence)
vankiate = (t:n) (w:plunder/spoil/loot) (d:goods taken by enemies, set beside mat ding mi, people to be captured) (e:mat ding mi le ~ suak ding uh) (s:vankinusiate/vankisutte) (b:vankia) (r:12.21.14) (q:draft)
vankila = (t:n) (w:plunder/spoil) (d:van, goods, with kila, taken: goods taken in war) (e:Shinar panin ~ lakah puan hoih khat) (s:vankia) (r:6.7.21) (q:draft)
vankim = (t:n) (w:midair/middle of the sky/air) (d:the middle of the sky, the open air above the earth; used with lai-ah: vankim lai-ah is in midair) (e:~ lai-ah a leeng vasa khempeuh/~ lai-ah muvanlai khat a leenkawmin | an eagle flying in midair/vantungmi adang khat in ~ lai-ah a leeng | another angel flying in midair/~ lai-ah Topa a dawn dingin | to meet the Lord in the air) (r:66.19.17/6.10.13/66.8.13/66.14.6/52.4.17) (q:draft)
Vankim = (t:name) (w:Vankim) (d:vankim, the middle of the sky, written with a capital at the start of a sentence) (r:6.10.13)
vankinusia = (t:n) (w:spoil/plunder) (d:van, goods, with kinusia, left behind: goods left by a defeated enemy) (e:Judah mite in ~ tampi tak pua) (s:vankila) (r:14.14.13/19.119.162) (q:draft)
vankinusiate = (t:n) (w:plunder/spoils/loot) (d:goods left behind by a defeated enemy and taken by the victors) (e:Gal sungah a ngah ~ sung panin/Moabte aw, ~ va la ni | Moab, let us go and take the plunder/tuate sungah ~ tam mahmah hi | there was very much plunder in them/Bang hangin ~ bawhin | why did you pounce on the plunder) (s:vankisutte/vanlakte/kisutte) (b:vankinusia) (r:13.26.27/9.15.19/12.3.23/14.14.14) (q:draft)
vankisutte = (t:n) (w:plunder/spoils/loot) (d:van, goods, with kisut, be plundered, and the plural te: goods taken by force) (e:mite in ~ a hawm ciangun/Mi kihisak tawh kipawlin ~ ngahna sangin | than to get plunder together with the proud/~ suak khin ta uh hi | they have become plunder) (s:vankinusiate/vanlakte/kisutte) (r:23.9.3/23.42.22/20.16.19) (q:draft)
vankoihna = (t:n) (w:storehouse/storeroom/treasury) (d:van, goods, with koihna, place of keeping: a storehouse or storeroom, often as vankoihna inn) (e:a tapa tungah ~ inn kipia hi/~ kongpite a cing kongcingte | the gatekeepers who guarded the gates of the storerooms/i Pasian’ inn sung ~ inndeite | the storerooms of the house of our God/kumpipa’ inn-ah pai-in ~ sungah a lut | went to the palace and entered the storeroom) (s:sumkoihna/kholna/koihna) (r:13.26.15/12.16.8/16.12.25/16.13.4/24.38.11) (q:draft)
vankoihnate = (t:n) (w:storehouses/storerooms/treasuries) (d:vankoihna, storehouse, with the plural te) (e:sathau koihna ding ~ zong a bawl hi/kumipa’ inn ~ a, a om ngun khempeuh | all the silver in the treasuries of the palace) (s:sumkoihnate/koihnate) (b:vankoihna) (r:14.32.28/12.18.15) (q:draft)
vankuumpi = (t:n) (w:vault of the sky/dome of heaven) (d:van sky with kuum, arch or vault, and pi, great: the sky seen as a great cover over the earth) (e:~ tawh leitung a khuhsuk hi) (r:30.9.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
vanlakte = (t:n) (w:plunder/spoils) (d:van, goods, with lak, taken, and the plural te: the things taken in war) (e:a ~ uh sung pan puante silhsak) (s:vankinusiate/vankisutte) (r:14.28.15) (q:draft)
vanlei = (t:v) (w:buy/buy goods) (d:van, goods, with lei, buy; vanlei vanzuak is buying and selling, trade) (e:~ vanzuakin paikhia thei lo uh hi) (s:sumlei) (a:vanzuak) (r:66.13.17) (q:draft)
Vanleipa = (t:n) (w:buyer) (d:van, goods, with lei, buy, and pa marking a male person; set against vanzuakpa, the seller) (e:~ in vanzuakpa kiangah) (s:leipa) (a:vanzuakpa) (r:20.20.14) (q:draft)
vanleite = (t:n) (w:buyers) (d:vanlei, buy goods, with the plural te: those who buy) (e:a tote, ~ leh van zuakte) (s:leite) (a:zuakte) (b:vanlei) (r:23.24.2) (q:draft)
vanlelei = (t:n) (w:sky and earth/heaven and earth) (d:van, sky, le, and, lei, earth, written as one word; vanlelei kikalah is between sky and earth, in midair) (e:~ kikalah amah a kikhai-in/~ na et uh ciangin | when you look at the sky and the earth) (r:10.18.9/42.12.56) (q:draft)
vanmanpha = (t:n) (w:treasure/valuables/precious things) (d:van, goods, with manpha, precious; vanmanpha koihna is the treasury, the place where valuables are kept) (e:~ koihna ah kham darik/Topa’ biakinn sung ~ koihna-ah a pia uh hi | they gave it to the treasury of the temple of the Lord/~ koihna a ukte lakah a ukpi | the chief among those in charge of the treasury/~ koihnate a bawl hi | he made treasuries) (r:16.7.71/13.26.22/13.29.8/13.26.24/14.32.27) (q:draft)
vanmanphate = (t:n) (w:treasures/valuables/precious things) (d:vanmanpha, valuable thing, with the plural te: the treasures of a temple or a palace) (e:kumpipa’ inn-a ~ lakhia hi/kumpipa leh a uliante’ ~ khempeuh | all the treasures of the king and his officials/kumpipa’ inn-a ~ la-in | taking the treasures of the palace/uliante’ inn panin ~ la-in | taking the valuables from the houses of the officials) (b:vanmanpha) (r:14.12.9/14.36.18/14.25.24/14.28.21) (q:draft)
vanmite = (t:n) (w:heavenly beings/celestial beings/angels) (d:van, heaven, with mi, person, and plural te) (e:Ama tungah serafim ~ ding uh hi/~ lakah kua pen tawh kibang ahi hiam | who among the heavenly beings is he like/ukna thu nial-in, ~ a gensia uh hi | they reject authority and slander celestial beings/Tua ciangin serafim ~ khat | then one of the seraphim) (s:vantungmite) (r:23.6.2/19.89.6/65.1.8/23.6.6) (q:draft)
vanmong = (t:n) (w:end of the heavens/horizon) (d:van, sky, with mong, end or edge: the farthest edge of the sky) (e:Ama suahna ~ khat pan hi a/na mite uh ~ pekah a om leh zong | even if your people are at the far end of the heavens) (r:19.19.6/5.30.4) (q:draft)
vanna = (t:n) (w:hole/opening) (d:kulh a vanna mun is a place where the wall has a hole; probably related to vang, opening) (e:kulh a ~ mun khat hong lak hi) (r:26.8.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
vannuai = (t:todo) (q:draft, mi vannuai khempeuh stands where the NIV has all the rest of the people; meaning of vannuai not clear from one verse)
vannusiatte = (t:n) (w:spoils/goods left behind) (d:van goods with nusiat, leave behind, and the plural te: what a defeated king left) (e:Hadadezer’ ~ sung panin a ap) (s:vankinusiate) (r:10.8.11) (q:draft)
vanpi = (t:n) (w:heavens/sky) (d:van, sky, with pi, great: the great expanse of the sky, the heavens; paired with leipi, the earth) (e:~ in ama nasepna taangko hi/Amah bek in ~ zal a | he alone stretches out the heavens/~ leh leipi, tuipi leh leitung ka lokgawp ding | I will shake the heavens and the earth, the sea and the dry land/Amah in ~ niamsak-in hong kumsuk a | he bowed the heavens and came down) (s:vantung) (a:leipi) (b:van) (r:19.19.1/18.9.8/37.2.6/19.18.9) (q:draft)
vanpite = (t:n) (w:heavens/skies) (d:vanpi, the heavens, with the plural te) (e:na ~ niamsak in la hong paisuk in/Amah in ~ pen meiipite tawh tuamin | he covers the skies with clouds) (s:vantungte/vante) (b:vanpi) (r:19.144.5/19.147.8) (q:draft)
vanpua = (t:adj) (w:load-carrying/goods-carrying) (d:van, goods, with pua, carry; vanpua leeng is a wagon and vanpua mi a carrier, a porter) (e:Solomon in ~ mi tul sawmsagih/leeng galkap leh ~ leeng tampi | chariots and many wagons/~ sakolte, sakol galkapte, le late | draught horses, cavalry horses and mules) (r:11.5.15/26.23.24/26.27.14) (q:draft)
vanpuakte = (t:n) (w:cargo/goods carried/baggage) (d:van, goods, with puak, carry, and the plural te: the things a ship or a traveller carries) (e:teembaw le a ~ a siat/a ~ uh suahkhia uh a | they brought out the things they carried) (r:44.27.10/40.2.11) (q:draft)
vansak = (t:v) (w:make successful/prosper) (d:in maa vansak, make a journey or undertaking go well; probably vang succeed with the causative sak) (e:ka maa nong ~ ding le) (s:vangsak) (r:1.24.42) (q:draft, low confidence)
vante = (t:n) (w:goods/wares/cargo/merchandise) (d:van, goods, with the plural te: goods for trade, the cargo of a ship) (e:~ tui sungah a paaikhia uh hi/na ~ tampi tak hong lei a | they bought very many of your goods/Na sumbuk ~ tuipi tungah a pai ciangin | when your merchandise went out on the seas/Na ~ leh na mi khempeuh | your wares and all your people) (b:van) (r:44.27.18/26.27.33/26.27.18/26.27.34) (q:draft)
vante = (t:n) (w:heavens/skies) (d:van, heaven, with the plural te) (e:~ tunga om tuite aw) (s:vantungte/vanpite) (b:van) (r:19.148.4) (q:draft)
vantumgmi = (t:n) (w:angel) (d:apparently a misprint of vantungmi, angel) (e:Sagihna ~ in peengkul tum ding) (s:vantungmi) (r:66.10.6) (q:draft)
vantung = (t:n) (w:heaven) (d:the dwelling place of God and the angels) (e:~ panin Topa in hong en sukin/~ pan lim a ngen uh hi | they asked for a sign from heaven/~ panin Abraham a nih veina sam a | called to Abraham from heaven a second time/Pasian in ~ leh leitung a piangsak hi | God created the heavens and the earth) (s:van) (a:leitung) (r:25.3.50/42.11.16/1.22.15/1.1.1) the promised land
vantung = (t:n) (w:sky) (d:the sky above the earth, where the birds fly and from which the rain falls) (e:van kuumpi pen ~ ci hi/~ pan-a guahte kikhawlsak hi | the rain from the sky was stopped/~ a om lai teng kip ding hi | it will stand firm as long as the sky remains) (s:vanpi) (r:1.1.8/1.1.20/1.8.2/19.89.37) the upper atmosphere
Vantung = (t:n) (w:heaven/sky) (d:vantung written with a capital, mostly in Vantung Gam, the kingdom of heaven) (e:~ Gam in ama nasemte ciamtehna lai/Pasian in van kuumpi pen ~ ci hi | God called the vault sky/~ nuai-a om tuite | the waters under the sky/~ panin vantungmi khat hong pai a | an angel came from heaven) (b:vantung) (r:40.18.23/1.1.8/1.1.9/42.22.43) (q:draft)
vantunga = (t:adv) (w:in heaven) (d:vantung, heaven, with the place ending a: in heaven, in the sky; vantunga om is that is in heaven) (e:~ a om kote Pa aw/~ om kha lite | the four spirits that are in heaven/~ aksite bangin | like the stars in the sky/~ lim lamdangte | the strange signs in the heavens) (s:vanah) (a:leitunga) (b:vantung) (r:40.6.9/25.3.41/38.6.5/50.2.15/24.10.2) (q:draft)
vantungah = (t:phrase) (w:in heaven/in the sky) (d:vantung, heaven, with the place marker ah) (e:~ a om thei nawn kei uh hi/~ nangma thu kip tawntung hi | your word stands firm in heaven forever/Topa in ama tokhom ~ phut khin a | the Lord has set up his throne in heaven/~ a om na Pa uh | your Father who is in heaven) (a:leitungah) (b:vantung) (r:66.12.8/40.5.48/19.119.89/19.103.19)
Vantungah = (t:phrase) (w:in heaven) (d:Vantung, heaven, with the place marker ah) (e:~ a om na Pa uh khat bek/~ eite’ Pasian om a | our God is in heaven/~ kua in a kahto ding hiam | who will go up into heaven/~ na deihna a kicin’mah bangin | as your will is done in heaven) (b:Vantung) (r:40.23.9/19.115.3/45.10.6/40.6.10) (q:draft)
vantunggam = (t:n) (w:heavenly realm/heaven) (d:vantung heaven with gam, land or kingdom) (e:~ tawh kipawl hong sapna thupha) (r:58.3.1) (q:draft)
vantungmi = (t:n) (w:angel) (d:vantung, heaven, with mi, person: a messenger from heaven, an angel) (e:Zekhariah in ~ a muh ciangin/Vantung panin ~ khat hong pai a | an angel came from heaven/Ama ~ khempeuh aw, amah phat un | praise him, all his angels/hehnepna kam tawh ~ dawng a | he answered the angel with comforting words) (s:vangtungmi) (b:vantung) (r:42.1.12/1.22.15/42.22.43/19.148.2/38.1.13) (q:draft)
Vantungmi = (t:n) (w:angel) (d:vantungmi, angel, written with a capital at the start of a sentence or in a title such as Mi That Vantungmi, the destroying angel) (e:Mi That ~ in Israel mite/~ khat in ka inn sungah ding-a om | an angel standing in my house/~ in, tua numeite kiangah | the angel, to those women) (b:vantungmi) (r:58.11.28/44.11.13/40.28.5) (q:draft)
vantungmite = (t:n) (w:angels/heavenly beings) (d:vantungmi, angel, with the plural te: angels, literally people of heaven; also those who belong to heaven) (e:Pasian’ ~ in amah dawn hi/~ in Abraham’ ang ah a pua uh hi | the angels carried him to the side of Abraham/Mihingte in ~’ an ne a | human beings ate the bread of angels/Amaute in ~ tawh kibang ding uh hi | they will be like the angels) (s:vanmite) (a:leitungmite) (b:vantungmi) (r:1.32.1/42.12.9/42.16.22/19.78.25/40.22.30) (q:draft)
vantungte = (t:n) (w:heavens) (e:na ~ ka et ciangin/Amah in ~ niamsakin hong paisuk a | he bowed the heavens and came down/~ pen puanbuk bangin na zal hi | you stretch out the heavens like a tent) (s:vanpite/vante) (b:vantung) (r:19.8.3/10.22.10/19.104.2) plural form of <vantung>
vantungte = (t:n) (w:skies) (e:tung-a om ~ thu pia-in/om ~ in sumngo bangin | the skies above, like bronze/na ~ uh sik bangin bawlin | making your skies like iron) (s:vanpite) (b:vantung) (r:19.78.23/5.28.23/3.26.19) plural form of <vantung>
vanvan = (t:adv) (w:rushing/pounding) (d:placed after a verb for hurried, restless or rushing movement: rushing, pounding) (e:Ka lungtang kisai ~ a/a sia-in gamta nuam ~ uh a | they rush to do evil/a leeng ~ tuikhang | the rushing torrent) (r:24.4.19/20.1.16/7.5.21) (q:draft, low confidence)
vanvan = (t:v) (w:stretch out/spread out) (d:doubled form of van, stretch out the hands, again and again) (e:amaute in a khut uh ~ ding uh a/Hong huh un ci-a khut ka ~ hangin | though I stretch out my hands crying, help me/ka khut hong ~ napi-in | though I stretched out my hand to you) (r:23.25.11/25.1.17/20.1.24) (q:draft, low confidence)
vanzatte = (t:n) (w:equipment/gear/tackle) (d:van, goods, with zat, use, and the plural te: things in use; teembaw vanzatte is the tackle of a ship) (e:A thai ciangin teembaw ~ pawlkhat) (s:nazatte) (r:44.27.19) (q:draft)
vanzuak = (t:v) (w:sell goods/trade) (d:van, goods, with zuak, sell; sumzuak vanzuak is selling and trading) (e:sumzuak ~ cihte om nawn lo ding hi) (s:sumzuak) (a:vanlei) (r:38.14.21) (q:draft)
vanzuakin = (t:v) (w:selling/trading) (d:vanzuak sell goods with the suffix in) (e:vanlei ~ paikhia thei lo uh hi) (b:vanzuak) (r:66.13.17) (q:draft)
vanzuakna = (t:n) (w:market/selling of goods) (d:vanzuak, sell goods, with the noun suffix na; vanzuakna phual is a marketplace) (e:Mihon omna ~ phual, lamdung citeng) (s:sumbuk) (b:vanzuak) (r:20.7.12) (q:draft)
vanzuakpa = (t:n) (w:seller) (d:vanzuak, sell goods, with pa, marking a man: the seller, set against Vanleipa, the buyer) (e:Vanleipa in ~ kiangah) (s:zuakpa) (a:Vanleipa/leipa) (b:vanzuak) (r:20.20.14) (q:draft)
vapai = (t:v) (w:go/go there) (d:pai go with va before it, marking movement away to another place) (e:Amaute a ~ lai takun ka ngen tawh) (r:28.7.12) (q:draft)
vapi = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:stork) (d:va bird with pi big: large bird; in the verses always gun vapi, river big bird, for the stork) (e:gun ~ bangin kalaoh vasa leng thei lo/gun ~, gun vazonei nam khempeuh | the stork, every kind of heron) (b:va) (r:18.39.13/3.11.19) (q:draft)
vapite = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:storks/large birds) (d:plural of vapi, large bird; gun vapite and tui vapite, large water birds, are used for the stork and the ibis) (e:gun ~ in bu a tom uh hi/Van-ah tui ~ nangawn in | even the storks in the sky/Nail gun a khan’ ding a thei gun ~ | the ibises that know when the Nile will rise) (s:gunvapite) (b:vapi) (r:19.104.17/24.8.7/18.38.36) (q:draft)
vasa = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:bird) (d:a bird of any kind) (e:innkhum dawn-a ~ khatguak om tawh ka kibang/a bu panin a leengkhia ~ tawh kibang hi | is like a bird that flies away from its nest/leibeel sungah a ~ khat go ding a | he shall kill one of the birds in a clay pot/~ siah bangin thang a hong siah uh | they set a trap for me as for a bird) (r:19.102.7/3.14.50/20.27.8/25.3.52)
vasabu = (t:n) (w:nest/bird's nest) (d:vasa, bird, with bu, nest) (e:~ khat, sing tung ahi a) (r:5.22.6)
Vasabu = (t:n) (w:nest/bird's nest) (d:vasabu, nest, at the start of a sentence) (e:~ khat, sing tung ahi a) (b:vasabu) (r:5.22.6) (q:draft)
vasam = (t:v) (w:go and call/call) (d:sam call with va before it, marking going over to do it) (e:Tua pa ~ un) (r:41.10.49) (q:draft)
vasapi = (t:see) <kalaoh-vasapi>
vasate = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:birds) (d:vasa, bird, with the plural te) (e:a bokvak ganhingte leh a leeng ~/Sasialne ~ tua sate' tungah hong tuksuk ciangin | when birds of prey came down on the carcasses/huih lak ~ om uh a | the birds of the air live there/Ganhing siangthote, a siangtho lo ganhingte, ~ | clean animals, unclean animals, birds) (b:vasa) (r:19.148.10/1.1.20/1.15.11/19.104.12/1.7.8)
vasateng = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:all the birds/birds) (d:vasa bird with teng, all of them) (e:a hiang tunga ~ hawlkhia in) (b:vasa) (r:27.4.14) (q:draft)
Vashti = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Vashti) (d:queen of Persia, wife of King Xerxes, who lost her place as queen when she refused to come before the king) (r:17.1.9/17.2.4)
vat = (t:v) (w:strike/strike down/attack/smite) (d:strike a person or attack a place, of God, a fighter or an army; namsau tawh vat is strike with the sword) (e:Topa in Nabal ~ hi/namsau tawh a kumpipa ~ hi | he struck its king with the sword/Topa in amah ~ a, amah si hi | the Lord struck him and he died/gan omna puanbukte ~ uh a | they attacked the tents of the herders) (s:sat) (r:9.25.38/2.17.13/6.11.10/14.13.20/14.14.15) (q:draft)
vatak = (t:see) <vatak-um>
vatak-um = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:wild gourd) (d:a wild plant with a vine, gui, and gourds, umgah, not fit to eat) (e:~ gui khat mu-in) (r:12.4.39) (q:draft)
vatawt = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:duck/water bird) (d:kind of bird; in the lists of unclean birds gam vatawt and tui vatawt stand where English has owl, swan, pelican or gull) (e:kalaoh-vasa, pengpelep, ~, musi nam khempeuh/leh tui ~, samuat ne musane leh tuimu) (r:3.11.16/3.11.18/5.14.17) (q:draft, low confidence, the English bird names differ from verse to verse)
vatgawp = (t:v) (w:strike down/smite/defeat) (d:vat, strike, with gawp, thoroughly: strike down or defeat completely) (e:Gezer ciang dong Filistiate ~ hi/Midian mite na ~ ding hi | you will strike down the Midianites/Amah in hang takin hih-in Amalekte ~ a | he acted bravely and defeated the Amalekites/gimna lianpi khat tawh mite ~ hi | he struck the people with a great plague) (s:vatmai) (b:vat) (r:10.5.25/7.6.16/9.14.48/4.11.33) (q:draft)
vatgawpin = (t:v) (w:striking down/attacking/defeating) (d:vatgawp, strike down, with the linking ending -in) (e:la-in amaute ~ that hi/a ngawngin manin ~ ka that hi | I seized it by the neck, struck it and killed it/Israel mite sawmthum bang ~ | striking down about thirty Israelites/natna tawh nang le na mite hong ~ | striking you and your people with disease) (b:vatgawp) (r:6.11.17/6.15.16/9.17.35/7.20.39/2.9.15) (q:draft)
vatin = (t:v) (w:striking/attacking/striking down) (d:vat, strike, with the linking ending in: striking or having struck; often namsau tawh vatin, with the sword) (e:namsau tawh ~ a khuapi hal uh hi/namsau tawh amaute ~ mei tawh a khuapi hal | they struck them with the sword and burned the city/Joab in Rabbah khua ~ lumlet hi | Joab attacked Rabbah and overthrew it/mipa in amah satin, ~ amah liamsak hi | the man struck him and wounded him) (b:vat) (r:7.1.8/11.20.37/7.18.27/13.20.1) (q:draft)
vatin = (t:adv) (w:suddenly/all at once) (d:after a verb, of something that comes on abruptly; khuamial hong suak vatin, darkness came suddenly) (e:khuamial hong suak ~ khua na mu/dipkua ~ tai uh hi | they fled in sudden terror) (s:thakhatin) (r:18.22.11/19.48.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
vatkhia = (t:see) <vatkhia-in>
vatkhia-in = (t:v) (w:sweeping away/striking off) (d:vat strike with khia, out, away, and the suffix in) (e:sehkhat ~ leilak a denna hi) (r:66.12.4) (q:draft)
vatlum = (t:v) (w:strike dead/kill/slay) (d:strike so that the person dies, often with the sword) (e:namsau tawh mi khempeuh ~ ding uh hi/Pasian in tua lai-ah amah ~ hi | God struck him dead there/tacil khempeuh ka ~ ding a | I will strike down every firstborn/Namsau tawh Izipt mite ~ ding uh a | they will kill the Egyptians with the sword) (s:thatlum/that) (r:26.26.11/10.6.7/2.12.12/26.30.11) (q:draft)
vatmai = (t:v) (w:strike down/smite/cut down/defeat) (d:kill or defeat in great numbers, as with a sword) (e:ama mite namsau tawh ~ hi/Israelte in amaute ~ uh hi | the Israelites cut them down/mihing leh ganhing tacil khempeuh ~ hi | he struck down all the firstborn of people and animals/ni khat thu-in a ~ hi | he cut them off in a single day) (s:vatgawp) (r:2.17.13/19.135.8/6.8.22/23.9.14) (q:draft)
vatmaipa = (t:n) (w:one who struck down/slayer) (d:vatmai, strike down, with pa, the male one who does it: a vatmaipa is he who struck down) (e:Kumpi liante a ~ tungah/Egypt gam tacil khempeuh a ~ tungah | to him who struck down all the firstborn of Egypt) (b:vatmai) (r:19.136.17/19.136.10) (q:draft)
vatmaisak = (t:v) (w:strike down/destroy) (d:vatmai strike down with sak, done to what belongs to someone: cut down all that he has built) (e:amaute in hong ~ ding uh hi) (b:vatmai) (r:26.28.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
vatmang = (t:v) (w:cut off/strike down/sweep away) (d:vat strike with mang, away, gone: strike so that the person is no more; of death taking the children from the streets) (e:Kong zinga naupangte a ~ a) (r:24.9.21) (q:draft)
vattansak = (t:v) (w:strike down/cut down) (d:vat strike with tan cut off and sak: strike vines and trees so that they break off) (e:leengguite leh theikungte ~ a) (r:19.105.33) (q:draft)
vattuk = (t:v) (w:strike down/cut down/fell) (d:vat, strike, with tuk, fall: strike so that the person falls) (e:Jonathan in amaute ~ a/Topa in amah a ~ hang ahi hi | it is because the Lord struck him down/namsau in mi khempeuh a ~ hi | the sword strikes down everyone) (r:9.14.13/24.46.15/24.12.12) (q:draft)
vattum = (t:v) (w:cut down/slay) (d:vat strike with tum, completely; said of the sword) (e:note uh namsau in ~ ding a) (r:34.2.13) (q:draft)
vawh = (t:v) (w:call/title/name) (d:give a name, with min, name: min vawh is to name a person, an animal or a place) (e:nau min ~/gamsung ganhing khempeuh min ~ hi | he gave names to all the wild animals/amau’ min mah ~ pah uh a | they gave them their own names) (s:phuak) (r:1.2.20/1.36.43)
vawh = (t:v) (w:sow) (d:scatter seed on the ground; khaici vawh is to sow seed) (e:khaici ~/in thu a ~ hi | he sows the word/Mi khat in a ~ hi | one person sows/taang lakah a ~ khit ciangin | after he had sown among the wheat/ling lakah ~ kei un | do not sow among thorns) (s:tuh) (a:at) (r:41.4.3/40.13.24/41.4.14/43.4.37/40.13.25/24.4.3)
vawhin = (t:v) (w:saddle/load) (d:form of vawh with the linking suffix in, putting a saddle or load on a pack animal) (e:la van ~ a nasempa kiangah/la khat a van ~ a silate a zong | he saddled a donkey and looked for his slaves/a la tutphah ~ | saddling his donkey) (r:12.4.24/1.22.3/11.2.40) (q:draft)
vawhin = (t:v) (w:sow/plant) (d:form of vawh with the linking suffix in, sowing seed) (e:khaici ~ na khe tawh tui/taang lakah tahum tang ~ a paikhia hi | he sowed weeds among the wheat and went away) (s:tuhin) (b:vawh) (r:5.11.10/40.13.25) (q:draft)
vawhpa = (t:n) (w:sower/farmer) (d:vawh, sow, with pa, marking a man: the man who sows, in khaici vawhpa) (e:Khaici ~ in thu a vawh hi/khaici ~ thugentehna na ngai un | listen to the parable of the sower/khaici ~ in khaici vawh dingin a kuankhia hi | a sower went out to sow his seed) (s:khaivawhpa) (b:vawh) (r:41.4.14/40.13.18/41.4.3) (q:draft)
vawhsa = (t:adj) (w:sown/planted) (d:vawh sow with sa, already done; na vawhsa an is the crop you have sown) (e:vawh lecin na ~ an leh na leenggui) (b:vawh) (r:5.22.9) (q:draft)
vawhsak = (t:v) (w:saddle) (d:in laa van vawhsak, put the gear on a donkey for someone, saddle it) (e:Kei adingin laa van hong ~ un/kamsangpa’ adingin laa van ~ hi | he saddled the donkey for the prophet/Amaute in ~ uh hi | they saddled it) (r:11.13.13/11.13.23/11.13.27) (q:draft)
vawhsakin = (t:v) (w:saddling/having saddled) (d:vawhsak saddle for someone with the linking ending in) (e:ama a dingin la van ~ a tungah) (b:vawhsak) (r:11.13.13) (q:draft)
vawhte = (t:n) (w:sowers/those who sow) (d:vawh, sow, with the plural te: the people who sow seed) (e:Thuman lo khaici a ~ in lungkhamna tuak a/a ~ leh a atte a lungdam khawm ding | the sowers and the reapers will be glad together/Khaici tawmkha a ~ in tawmkha a at ding | those who sow little seed will reap little) (s:tuhte) (a:atte) (b:vawh) (r:20.22.8/47.9.6/43.4.36) (q:draft)
vawhzo = (t:v) (w:be able to put through/be able to thread) (d:vawh, thread or put a cord through, with zo, be able: be able to pass a cord through, as through the nose of an animal; not from vawh call or sow) (e:a nakpheh-ah khau ~ ding ahi hiam/A nakpheh-ah khau ~ ding a | can you put a cord through its nose) (r:18.40.24/18.41.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
vazonei = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:heron) (d:in gun vazonei, a river bird in the list of unclean birds) (e:gun vapi, gun ~ nam khempeuh) (r:3.11.19/5.14.18) (q:draft)
ve = (t:part) (d:sentence-final particle of emphasis or urging; after a command, often as dih ve, it presses the hearer to go ahead, and after hi, as hi ve’n, it stresses a statement) (e:Kumpi Solomon en dih ~ un/na kiciamna uh bangin sem dih ~ un | go ahead and do as you vowed/note tawh Topa om ta ~ | the Lord be with you indeed/Kuanto inla va gualzo ~ | go up and be victorious) (r:22.3.11/24.44.25/2.10.10/11.22.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
ve'ng = (t:part) (d:sentence-final words after hi in the speech of one person about himself, here I would surely have given; apparently an emphatic ve with a shortened first person ending) (e:kawnggak khat hong pia ngel ding hi ~ | I would surely have given you a belt) (r:10.18.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
veeng = (t:n) (w:quarter/neighbourhood) (d:a part of a town or village; Naioth veeng is the Naioth quarter of Ramah) (e:Ramah khua sung Naioth ~ panin David/Ramah khua sung Naioth ~ a tun’ mateng | until he reached Naioth in Ramah) (s:veng) (r:9.20.1/9.19.23) (q:draft)
veengah = (t:n) (w:in the quarter/in the neighbourhood) (d:veeng, a quarter or neighbourhood of a town, with the place marker ah, in or to: Naioth veengah is in Naioth, a quarter of Ramah; veeng is the long-vowel spelling of veng) (e:Ramah khua sung Naioth ~ David om hi/Ramah khua sung Naioth ~ om uh hi | they are at Naioth in Ramah/Ramah khua sung Naioth ~ amah pai hi | he went to Naioth in Ramah) (s:vengah) (b:veeng) (r:9.19.19/9.19.23/9.19.22) (q:draft)
veengte = (t:n) (w:neighbors) (d:plural of veeng; inn veengte is those who live in the houses nearby) (e:a lawmte leh a inn ~ sam a/na ~ khempeuh’ beel va kawm in | go and borrow jars from all your neighbors/sumhau na inn ~ ahi zongin | or your rich neighbors/mi khempeuh in a ~ ciat | everyone against his neighbor) (s:vengte/innvengte) (b:veeng) (r:42.15.6/12.4.3/42.14.12/23.3.5) (q:draft)
veh = (t:v) (w:visit/look after/care for) (d:go to see someone who is sick or in need and care for them; said also of God coming to help his people) (e:ka om lai takin nong ~ uh hi/hong mu-in hong ~ a | saw you and visited you/hong phawk in la, hong ~ in | remember me and care for me/Ahab tapa Joram a ~ dingin | to visit Joram son of Ahab/Ama mi pawlte hong ~ in | he has come to visit his people) (s:hawh) (r:40.25.36/42.1.73/40.25.39/24.15.15/12.8.29) (q:draft)
veh = (t:part) (d:sentence-final word of exclamation that calls attention to something happening now, as in listen, people are crying out) (e:Horonain khua-ah mi kiko ~/Ngai dih un, thu khat kigen ~ | listen, a report is being told/buaina lianpi khat hong pai ~ | a great commotion is coming) (r:24.48.3/24.10.22) (q:draft, low confidence)
vei = (t:n) (w:time) (d:an occasion or instance, counted with a number word before it: khat vei is once, thum vei is three times) (e:khat ~, thum ~/an lei dingin khat ~ kong pai uh hi | we came once to buy food/Kum khat in thum ~ | three times a year/Topa kiangah thum ~ dongin ka ngen hi | three times I pleaded with the Lord) (r:2.23.14/1.43.20/47.12.8)
veii = (t:v) (w:wave) (d:move an offering to and fro before the Lord; veii-a biakna is a wave offering) (e:Topa mai-ah tuate ~ hi/Moses in a iik la-in ~ a | Moses took the breast and waved it/amaute ~-a biakna-in na pia ding hi | you shall present them as a wave offering) (r:3.8.27/3.9.21/3.8.29/4.8.13) (q:draft)
veikhoi = (t:adj) (w:left-handed) (d:using the left hand rather than the right; said of Ehud and of the slingers of Benjamin) (e:Gera tapa a ~ Ehud/mi a kiteng khia a ~ zasagih om hi | there were seven hundred chosen left-handed men) (r:7.3.15/7.20.16) (q:draft)
veilam = (t:n) (w:left/left side) (d:the left-hand side; before a noun it means left, as in veilam khut, left hand) (e:keelte a ~ a koih ding hi/A ~ khut hong khamsak a | his left hand is under my head/amahmah’ ~ khut sungah | into his own left hand/a ziatlam khat a ~ khat | one on his right and one on his left) (a:taklam/ziatlam) (r:40.25.33/22.8.3/3.14.26/41.15.27) (q:draft)
veilama = (t:n) (w:on the left/at the left side) (d:veilam, left side, with the place ending a, at or on: ka veilama is on my left) (e:A ~ omte ne uh a/ka taklama tut ding le ka ~ tut ding | to sit at my right and at my left/ka taklam le ka ~ tutding | to sit at my right and my left) (a:taklama) (b:veilam) (r:23.9.20/41.10.40/40.20.23) (q:draft)
veilamah = (t:adv) (w:on the left/to the left) (d:veilam, the left side, with the place ending -ah; often paired with taklam, the right) (e:ka taklam leh ka ~ tut nading/ama taklam leh ~ om hi | they were on his right and left/a ~ a omte kiangah | to those on his left/A taklamah khat, a ~ khat | one on his right, one on his left/keel a bang mite a ~ koih ding hi | he will put those who are like goats on his left) (a:taklamah/ziatlamah) (r:41.10.40/23.54.3/10.16.6/40.25.41/41.15.27/40.25.33) (q:draft)
veilamin = (t:adv) (w:with the left/on the left) (d:veilam left side with the suffix in; a khut veilamin is with his left hand) (e:a khut ~ khat lenin/a khut taklamin khat, a khut ~ khat | his right hand on one, his left hand on the other) (a:taklamin) (b:veilam) (r:7.16.29) (q:draft)
veina = (t:n) (w:version)
veina = (t:n) (w:time) (d:vei, time, with na: after a number word it gives the order of an occasion, a nih veina is the second time) (e:Topa in a nih ~ hong hopih a/Abraham a nih ~ sam a | called to Abraham a second time/hih nih ~ lai kong gelh hi | this is the second letter I write/kong pai ding a thum ~ ahi hi | this is the third time I am coming) (b:vei) (r:24.13.3/1.22.15/61.3.1/47.13.1)
veina = (t:part) (d:particle showing number of times) (e:khat ~, thum ~/Jonah tungah a nih ~ thu gen a | spoke to Jonah a second time/a nih ~ maang ka mu hi | I saw a second vision) (b:vei) (r:1.22.15/32.3.1/27.8.1)
