viik = (t:v) (w:brandish/swing/wave) (d:swing a sword or the arm in order to strike; viik suk is swing down) (e:Ka namsau ka ~ ciangin kumpite/Amah in a khut ~-in amaute do ding hi | he will fight them with the swing of his arm/ama khut a ~ sukna kimusak ding hi | he will show his arm coming down) (s:vik) (r:26.32.10/23.30.32/23.30.30) (q:draft)
vik = (t:v) (w:swing/wield) (d:move the arm or a staff with a sweep; vik to is swing up and vik suk bring down) (e:amah in ciangkhut ~ to-in Nail gun/ama khut a ~ sukna kimusak ding hi | he will show his arm coming down/Ka namsau ka ~ ciangin kumpite lau-in | when I brandish my sword the kings will be afraid) (s:viik) (r:2.7.20/23.30.30/26.32.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
vikin = (t:v) (w:swinging/wielding) (d:vik swing with the suffix in; a khut vikin is swinging his arm) (e:a khut ~ amaute a do ding hi) (b:vik) (r:23.30.32) (q:draft, low confidence)
vil = (t:v) (w:watch/guard/keep watch) (d:keep watch over a place or a person, look out for an enemy, or watch closely for a chance) (e:gal ~ dingin mi khat seh uh hi/ka mukte’ kongkhak a ~ ding khat koih in | set a guard over the door of my lips/Na kan uhah pang un la, lampi ~ un | guard your fortress and watch the road/Kongpite a ~ kongcingte | the gatekeepers who watched the gates/a hunhoih ngakin ~ gige uh a | they kept watching for the right moment) (s:cing) (r:26.33.2/16.11.19/19.141.3/34.2.1/42.20.20) (q:draft)
vilin = (t:v) (w:watching/keeping watch) (d:vil watch, with the linking ending in) (e:piak dong mateng uh ~ kem un/lampi gei-ah a ~ ama tutna-ah Eli na tu | Eli was sitting on his seat by the road, watching) (b:vil) (r:15.8.29/9.4.13) (q:draft)
vilna = (t:n) (w:watch/vigil/guard duty) (d:noun of vil, watch over: keeping watch; with mun, the place of watching) (e:amaute tungah ~ nasep leh zingsang simin/ka ~ munnah zankhuavak ka om hi | I stay at my post all night/hih zan mah zan ~-in nei uh hi | they keep this night as a night of vigil/Thongcingte’ ~ mun a khatna le a nihna | the first and second guard posts) (s:galvilna) (b:vil) (r:13.9.27/23.21.8/2.12.42/44.12.10) (q:draft)
vilpa = (t:n) (w:watchman/sentinel/lookout) (d:vil, watch, with pa, a man who does it; gal vilpa is the man who keeps watch for the enemy) (e:Gal ~ aw, tu zan bangci hiam) (s:galvilpa/galvil) (b:vil) (r:23.21.11/23.21.12) (q:draft)
vilsim = (t:v) (w:stalk/spy on/watch secretly) (d:keep watching someone's steps so as to catch him) (e:Galte in hong ~ uh ahih manin) (s:ensim) (r:25.4.18) (q:draft)
vilte = (t:n) (w:watchmen/guards) (d:vil watch with the plural te; gal vilte is those who keep watch for enemies) (e:Efraim mualtung panin gal ~ in) (s:galvilte) (b:vil) (r:24.31.6) (q:draft)
vilvel = (t:see) <vilvel-in>
vilvel-in = (t:adv) (w:specially/distinctly) (d:after a tuam, separate: a tuam vilvel-in is quite apart from the ordinary, as a special vow) (e:a tuam ~ kiciamna a bawl ciangin) (s:vilvelin) (r:3.27.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
vilvelin = (t:adv) (w:specially/particularly) (d:in a tuam vilvelin, quite separately, in a special way) (e:a tuam ~ kiciamna a bawl ciangin/Pasian in a tuam ~ ama vangliatna tawh | God, in a special way, by his power) (s:vilvel-in) (r:3.27.2/49.3.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
vingveng = (t:adv) (w:hurriedly/straight away) (d:after ciah pah, go home at once: describes hurrying off) (e:a innah ciah pah ~ hi) (r:17.6.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
vive = (t:adv) (w:only/all/nothing but/entirely) (d:placed after a word to say that everything is of that kind) (e:ka gen khempeuh thumaan ~ ahi hi/mi si luanghawm ~ na hi hi | there were only dead bodies/amaute khempeuh zuaupi ~ ahi hi | they are all nothing but lies/Zadok’ suan Levi mite ~ ahi uh hi | they are all Levites descended from Zadok/leengpei kualte tungah mittang ~ a dimin om hi | the rims were full of eyes all over) (r:20.8.6/19.119.69/14.20.24/23.41.29/26.40.46/26.1.18) (q:draft)
Vofsi = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Vophsi) (d:father of Nahbi, the spy sent from the tribe of Naphtali) (r:4.13.14)
vok = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:pig) (d:a pig; vok hon is a herd of pigs) (e:~ honkhat gamta-in a om uh hi/~ hon sungah hong lutsak in | send us into the herd of pigs/~ an nek begapte nangawn | even the pods that the pigs ate/~ honpi khat gamta-in a om uh hi | a large herd of pigs was feeding) (s:vokpi) (r:40.8.30/42.15.15/40.8.31/42.15.16/41.5.11)
vok = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:boar) (s:ngal)
vokcing = (t:v) (w:tend pigs/feed pigs) (d:vok pig with cing, tend, look after) (e:a innteek pa in ~ dingin ama lo-ah) (r:42.15.15) (q:draft)
