vokno = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:piglet) (d:vok, pig, with no, young: a young pig)
vokpi = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:pig) (d:vok, pig, with pi, big or female: a full-grown pig) (e:~ muk-a om kham nakbah tawh kibang) (s:vok) (b:vok) (r:20.11.22)
vokpi = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:gilt/sow) (d:a female pig, a sow) (e:~ in a kisil khit ciangin buan) (b:vok) (r:61.2.22)
voksa = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:pork) (d:vok, pig, with sa, meat: the flesh of pigs) (e:~ ne-in amau beel sungah/~ leh kihhuaina leh zusa a nete | those who eat pork, unclean things and rats) (b:vok) (r:23.65.4/23.66.17)
vokte = (t:n) (w:pigs/swine) (d:plural of vok, pig) (e:~ sungah a lut uh leh/Kote tua ~ sungah ka lut nadingun | so that we may go into those pigs/~ kisim leh, tulnih bang pha ding hi | if the pigs were counted there would be about two thousand/hua ~ sungah hong lutsak in | send us into those pigs) (b:vok) (r:40.8.32/41.5.12/41.5.13/40.8.31) (q:draft)
vom = (t:adj) (w:black/dark) (d:black or dark in colour, said of horses, hair, skin and the sky) (e:a nihna, sakol ~ in kai a/ama' mitte leenggahzu sangin ~ zaw ding a | his eyes will be darker than wine/ka ~ hangin ngaih baang ing | I am dark, yet lovely/tua sungah mul ~ a om kei leh | if there is no black hair in it/ka et ciangin sakol ~ khat ka mu hi | I looked and saw a black horse) (a:kang/paak) (r:38.6.2/1.49.12/22.1.5/3.13.31/66.6.5) (q:draft)
vom = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:bear) (d:a bear, named beside the lion as a dangerous wild animal) (e:gamlak panin ~ a pi nih hong pai-in/humpinelkai ahi a, ~ ahi zongin hong pai-in | when a lion or a bear came/Humpinelkai khecin leh ~ khecin panin | from the paw of the lion and the paw of the bear/Eite khempeuh ~ bangin i humham a | we all growl like bears) (s:vompi) (r:12.2.24/9.17.34/9.17.37/23.59.11) (q:draft)
vom = (t:v) (w:carry/keep/hold/harbor) (d:keep or carry something inside, as money in a belt, or a word, a teaching or a rebellious mind in the heart) (e:na kawnggak sung uh ah na ~ kei un/lungsim sung uhah keima thu a ~ mite aw | you people who keep my word in your hearts/amaute in lehdona lungsim ~ uh a | they harbored a rebellious heart/kawnggak sungah dangkasan na ~ kei un | do not carry money in your belts/hih thu a ~ kei leh | if he does not bring this teaching) (r:40.10.9/23.51.7/19.106.43/41.6.8/63.1.10) (q:draft)
