vuai = (t:v) (w:wither/wilt) (d:of a tree or plant, dry up and droop) (e:theikungte ~ ta hi) (r:29.1.12) (q:draft)
vuak = (t:v) (w:hit/strike/beat) (d:form of vua, beat or strike; hong vuak is they hit me, and in Isaiah 53:4 it is said of one struck by God) (e:Hong ~ hangun ka liam kei a/Pasian in a gimsak, a ~, gimna a thuakpa-in | as one punished by God, struck and afflicted) (s:sat) (b:vua) (r:20.23.35/23.53.4) (q:draft)
vuakna = (t:n) (w:beating/blow/scourge/flogging) (d:vuak, beat, with the noun suffix na: the act of beating or the blow received) (e:nakpi tak-a ~ in i sung tawng/Nong ~ ma ka tung panin lakhia in | remove your scourge from me/na khut tawh nong ~-in ka tha bei ta | by the blow of your hand my strength is gone) (s:satna) (b:vuak) (r:20.20.30/19.39.10) (q:draft)
vuakpih = (t:v) (w:join in beating/join in attacking) (d:vuak, beat, with pih, together with: take part with others in beating someone) (e:amau tegel ~ ngeingai uh a) (b:vuak) (r:44.16.22) (q:draft)
vuang = (t:v) (w:sway/be shaken) (d:of a reed, pumpeeng, move to and fro when the wind blows on it) (e:Huih mut a, ~ pumpeeng en dingin/Huih mut a, a ~ pumpeeng en ding | to see a reed swayed by the wind) (r:40.11.7/42.7.24) (q:draft, low confidence)
