vuite = (t:n) (w:buriers/those who bury) (d:vui, bury, with the plural te: the people who bury or have buried someone) (e:Na pasal ~’ khe in kongkhak kiangah/Saul a ~ in Jabeshgilead mite hi | those who buried Saul are the men of Jabesh Gilead) (b:vui) (r:44.5.9/10.2.4) (q:draft)
vuite = (t:n) (w:ears of grain/heads of grain) (d:in a vuite, the ears of standing grain, which may be picked by hand; vui is the ear or head of a grain plant) (e:na khut uh tawh a ~ na zut thei) (s:anvuite/buhvuite) (r:5.23.25) (q:draft, low confidence)
vuk = (t:n) (w:snow) (d:snow; vuk bangin is like snow, said of what is very white) (e:~ bangin pak hi/~ sangin ka ngozaw ding hi | I will be whiter than snow/Zalmon mual tunga ~ kia tawh kibang hi | it is like snow fallen on Mount Zalmon) (s:vuuk) (r:4.12.10/18.37.6/19.51.7/19.68.14) (q:draft)
vuk = (t:v) (w:cover/bury) (d:cover something over completely, as with earth; lei vuk is fill in or cover with earth) (e:leivui tawh ~ ding hi/Komau hong ~ un | cover us/mihing guh tawh a dim tua munte a ~ hi | he covered those sites with human bones/na ek uh na ~ ding uh hi | you shall cover up your excrement) (s:vuh/khuh) (r:3.17.13/42.23.30/12.23.14/5.23.13) (q:draft)
vukcip = (t:v) (w:overwhelm/bury/cover over) (d:vuk, cover, with cip, tightly: cover completely so that nothing shows, as earth or waves do; also of fear or sorrow that overwhelms a person) (e:launa in kei hong ~ hi/na tuihualte khempeuh tawh kei nong ~ hi | you have overwhelmed me with all your waves/Abiram’ pawlte ~ hi | it buried the company of Abiram/Kulh kongpite cim gawpin lei in ~ a | the gates have collapsed and the earth has buried them) (s:khuhcip/tuumcip) (b:vuk) (r:19.55.5/19.106.17/19.88.7/25.2.9) (q:draft)
vukkhal = (t:n) (w:frost/ice/sleet) (d:frozen moisture: frost lying on the ground, or ice and sleet that damage crops) (e:a theithekte uh ~ tawh susia hi/tuumul bangin ~ hong pia a | he gives snow like wool/~ banga a pa dildel leitungah om hi | something thin like frost lay on the ground) (r:19.78.47/2.16.14/19.147.16) (q:draft)
vukkhalte = (t:n) (w:melting snow/snow/ice) (d:vukkhal, frost or ice, with the plural te; in Job 24:19 the snow and ice that vanish in heat and drought) (e:khuakhal hunin ~ a manthan bangin) (b:vukkhal) (r:18.24.19) (q:draft)
vukkia = (t:n) (w:snowfall/falling snow) (d:vuk, snow, with kia, fall: snow that falls) (e:Tuk lai tak-a ~) (r:20.26.1) (q:draft)
vukkiat = (t:n) (w:snowfall/frost) (d:vuk, snow, with kiat, fall: falling snow or frost, listed with khuadam, cold) (e:khuadam, ~ cihte om nawn lo ding) (b:vukkia) (r:38.14.6) (q:draft)
vuknelh = (t:v) (w:overwhelm/cover over/surpass/choke) (d:vuk, cover, with nelh, over: cover over completely; in 1 Kings 10:7 wisdom and wealth far exceed the report that was heard, in Matthew 13:22 worries and riches choke the word) (e:in ka zak thute ~ hi/hauh nopnate in Pasian’ thu ~ ahih manin | because the desire for riches chokes the word of God) (s:vukcip) (r:11.10.7/40.13.22) (q:draft)
vuknelhin = (t:v) (w:overwhelming/rising over) (d:vuknelh, cover over, with the linking ending in: said of sins piled higher than the head) (e:ka lu dawn uh hong ~ vantung dong) (b:vuknelh) (r:15.9.6) (q:draft)
vukngo = (t:n) (w:frost) (d:the cold of the night that covers a body left outside, set against nisa the heat of the day) (e:zan laitaka vuksan ~ tuam dingin) (r:24.36.30) (q:draft)
vukpak = (t:n) (w:frost/hoarfrost) (d:vuk, snow, with pak, flower: the white frost that is scattered on the ground) (e:vut bangin ~ hong thehthang hi) (s:vuukpaak) (r:19.147.16) (q:draft)
vuksan = (t:n) (w:frost) (d:used in the pair vuksan vukngo for the cold frost of the night) (e:zan laitaka ~ vukngo tuam dingin) (b:vuk) (r:24.36.30) (q:draft, low confidence)
vukte = (t:n) (w:frost/snows) (d:vuk, snow, with the plural te; van-a vukte is the frost or snow of the sky) (e:kua’ sung panin vana ~ hong suak) (b:vuk) (r:18.38.29) (q:draft)
vul = (t:v) (w:wither/fade/wilt) (d:of grass, leaves and flowers, dry up and lose life; also of glory or strength that fades) (e:Lopa ~ a, paak pulh hi/a ~ thei lo vangliatna lukhu | the crown of glory that cannot fade/Lebanon Mual-a pakpalhte ~ hi | the blossoms of Lebanon wither/leitung buppi thanemin ~ gawp hi | the whole world grows weak and withers) (s:vuai/keugaw/keutum) (a:palh) (r:23.40.8/42.8.6/60.5.4/34.1.4/23.24.4) (q:draft)
