vulgawp = (t:v) (w:wither/wilt/languish) (d:vul, wither, with gawp, completely: dry up and droop, grow faint) (e:lopa bangin kei ka ~ hi/zung kha zo lo ahih manin a ~ hi | it withered because it had no root/Lebanon mual-a tulak singte ~ a | the trees of Mount Lebanon wither/na luah mite ~ ahih manin | because your inheritance was weary) (s:keugaw/keutum) (a:palh) (b:vul) (r:19.102.11/41.4.6/23.33.9/19.68.9) (q:draft)
vulgawpin = (t:v) (w:withering/wither) (d:vulgawp, wither completely, with the linking ending in) (e:~ a si dingin kei a hong nusia hi) (b:vulgawp) (r:18.19.10) (q:draft)
vulin = (t:v) (w:wither/fade/wilt) (d:vul, wither, with the linking ending in: withering, and so) (e:nitak ciangin ~ keu uh hi/Leengguite ~, leenggahzu kang a | the vines wither and the wine dries up/Leitung ~ keugaw a | the earth withers and dries up/tua ankungnote ~ a keu hi | those young plants withered and dried up) (b:vul) (r:19.90.6/23.24.4/23.24.7/40.13.6) (q:draft)
vulkhawm = (t:v) (w:wither together/languish together) (d:vul, wither, with khawm, together) (e:a nih tuakin ~ hi) (b:vul) (r:23.24.4) (q:draft)
vulkik = (t:v) (w:wither away/wither) (d:vul, wither, with kik, back: of a plant that has come up, wither and die back) (e:ahih manin a ~ pah hi) (b:vul) (r:42.8.6/18.24.24) (q:draft)
vulpak = (t:v) (w:wither soon/wither quickly) (d:vul, wither, with pak, quickly) (e:lopa bangin amaute ~ ding uh a) (r:19.37.2) (q:draft)
vulsak = (t:v) (w:make wither/blight) (d:vul, wither, with the causative sak: cause plants to wither; mai vulsak is make the face look drawn and gloomy) (e:na mai uh ~ kei un/Na ankungte uh lung ne sakin ka ~ a | I let worms eat your crops and made them wither) (b:vul) (r:30.4.9/40.6.16) (q:draft)
vum = (t:v) (w:be piled up/be heaped) (d:lie in a heap; vum venvan is piled high) (e:sing a sangpi-in ~ venvan hi/kiciangin ~ venvan | piled up high) (r:23.30.33/34.3.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
vumah = (t:n) (w:on top/on the roof) (d:vum, top, with ah, at or on: innkhum vumah is on the housetops) (e:innkhum ~ kiko-in na gen un/innkhum ~ a kiko ding uh hi | it will be proclaimed on the housetops) (r:40.10.27/42.12.3) (q:draft)
vumin = (t:v) (w:heap up/pile up) (d:vum, be piled up, with the linking ending in: piling up earth) (e:a kulh pua-ah lei sung ~) (b:vum) (r:35.1.10) (q:draft)
vun = (t:n) (w:skin) (d:the skin of a person or an animal; vun at, cut the skin, is circumcise, and vun dawn is the foreskin) (e:Ka ~ vomin dulh khia a/ka ~ tung khempeuh meima in tuamcip hi | my skin is covered all over with sores/meihal biakna ganhing a ~ hawk-in | skinning the animal of the burnt offering) (r:18.30.30/3.13.18/18.7.5/3.1.6) of animals, people
vunat = (t:v) (w:circumcise/be circumcised) (d:vun, skin, with at, cut; vunat mi is a circumcised man, vunat lo is uncircumcised and vunatna is circumcision) (e:Nang in ~ lote kiangah pai-in/~ mi hong sap leh | if a circumcised man is called/a ~ dingin thu a pia kei uh hi | they did not order him to be circumcised/note ~ nading a deih uh hi | they want you to be circumcised) (r:44.11.3/46.7.18/48.2.3/48.6.13) (q:draft)
vunatna = (t:n) (w:circumcision) (d:vunat, circumcise, with the noun suffix na; vunatna thuak is be circumcised) (e:~ hangin phattuamna om lo hi/~ a thuak mite lakah | among those of the circumcision/Moses in ~ thu no hong pia hi | Moses gave you circumcision/~ in phattuamna a om kei hi | circumcision has no value) (b:vunat) (r:46.7.19/48.5.2/56.1.10/43.7.22/48.6.15) (q:draft)
