vung = (t:v) (w:hold/contain) (d:of a cistern, hold water without leaking) (e:tui a ~ thei kei hi) (r:24.2.13) (q:draft)
vunte = (t:n) (w:skins/hides) (d:vun, skin, with the plural te: skins of animals, used as coverings) (e:a kisansak tuutal ~/A kisansak tuutal ~ leh keel ~ tawh | with ram skins dyed red and goat skins) (s:savunte) (b:vun) (r:2.25.5/3.9.11/2.26.14) (q:draft)
vut = (t:n) (w:ashes/ash) (d:the grey powder left after something is burned; sitting in ashes or putting them on the head is a sign of grief or repentance) (e:~ lakah bual uh hi/~ bangin vuukpaak hong thehthang hi | he scatters the frost like ashes/~ lakah tu hi | he sat among the ashes/Tamar in a lu tungah ~ koihin | Tamar put ashes on her head) (s:vu) (r:26.27.30/19.147.16/18.2.8/10.13.19) (q:draft)
vut = (t:v) (w:pierce/prick) (d:pierce or bore through; of the heart, be cut or pierced by pain; of the ears, tingle at shocking news) (e:a bil na ~ ding/kha-in na lungtang hong ~ hi | it is bitter and pierces your heart/a za mite khempeuh’ bilte a ~ ding siatna | a disaster that will make the ears of all who hear it tingle/a lung uh ~ a | they were cut to the heart) (s:vuhsak/sunlet) (r:5.15.17/9.3.11/24.4.18/12.21.12/44.2.37) (q:draft)
vute = (t:n) (w:ashes) (d:vu, ashes, with the plural te; English uses ashes) (e:Bawngla ~ a khawm mipa in/a kihal khialhna hanga biakna ~ la-in | taking ashes of the burned sin offering/a ~ Beth-el ah pua hi | he carried their ashes to Bethel/bawngla kihaltum ~ | the ashes of a burned heifer) (s:vutte) (b:vu) (r:4.19.10/12.23.4/4.19.17/58.9.13) (q:draft)
vutkhu = (t:n) (w:ashes/ash dust) (d:vut ashes, probably with khu smoke: fine ash, a picture of what is worthless) (e:Na thugente uh ~ bang hi lel a) (r:18.13.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
vutlet = (t:v) (w:break into/break through) (d:vut pierce with let through: of a thief, break through into a house) (e:Guta khat in inn ~ a) (r:2.22.1) (q:draft)
vutlevai = (t:n) (w:ashes/dust and ashes) (d:vut ashes joined with vai; vutlevai suak is be reduced to ashes) (e:tu-in ~ khu-in nakpitakin ka kisik hi/mi khempeuh’ muhna-ah ~ ka hong suah hi | I turned you to ashes in the sight of all/minamte’ hanciamnate ~ a suak hi | the efforts of the nations turn to ashes/a milimte uh ~ suakin | their idols turning to ashes) (r:18.42.6/26.28.18/24.51.58/26.6.6) (q:draft)
vutluahna = (t:n) (w:firepan/censer) (d:vut, ashes, with luahna, a thing for scooping up: a pan for taking up ashes or carrying burning coals at the altar) (e:sikkate le ~ peekte a bawl hi/kham citak ~ | firepans of pure gold/biakna tau nazat khempeuh, a ~ peek | all the utensils of the altar, its firepans) (r:2.38.3/11.7.50/4.4.14) (q:draft)
vutluahnate = (t:n) (w:firepans/censers/shovels) (d:vutluahna, firepan, with the plural te) (e:~ zong, leh haite lakhia uh hi/beelte, ~, taitehte, kuangte | pots, shovels, wick trimmers, bowls) (b:vutluahna) (r:12.25.15/24.52.18) (q:draft)
vutte = (t:n) (w:ashes) (d:vut, ashes, with the plural te; English uses ashes) (e:biakna tau panin a ~ kibuakhia hi/a tunga om ~ kibuakhia ding hi | the ashes on it will be poured out/meiphualpi panin ~ la-in | taking ashes from the furnace/a siangtho mun khatah ~ puakhia ding hi | he shall carry the ashes out to a clean place) (s:vute) (b:vut) (r:11.13.5/4.4.13/11.13.3/2.9.10/3.6.11) (q:draft)
