zagukte = (t:num) (w:the six hundred/six hundred) (d:zaguk, six hundred, with the plural te: the six hundred, said after the noun of a group of people already mentioned) (e:galhiam a tawi Dan mi ~/amah tawh a om mihing ~ | the six hundred men who were with him/amah a zui Gath mi ~ khempeuh | all the six hundred Gittites who followed him) (b:zaguk) (r:7.18.16/9.27.2/10.15.18) (q:draft)
zah = (t:part) (d:numerical classifier used in counting the number of times per equal amount) (e:a ~ sagih/a ~ sawmthumin a gah hi | it bore fruit thirty times over/a tuuno a ~ li-in loh ding hi | he must pay for the lamb four times over/Na sum uh a ~ nih pua un | take double the money with you) (r:40.13.8/1.4.15/10.12.6/1.43.12)
zah = (t:n) (w:amount/number/quantity) (d:the amount, number or quantity of something; zah tawh kituakin is according to the number of) (e:a kum pha ~ tawh kituakin/sumngo a gik ~ kithei zo lo hi | the weight of the bronze could not be known/a om mi ~ tawh kituakin | according to the number of people there/a kham ~ ding khawm uh hi | they gathered as much as they needed) (r:3.25.15/14.4.18/2.16.16/2.16.18)
zah = (t:n) (w:fold) (d:a multiple of an amount, with a number after it: a zah zakhat is a hundredfold and a zah nih is double) (e:a ~ zakhat la hi/a ~ zakhat a gah hi | it bore fruit a hundredfold/a khop ngei ~ nih pha ding hi | it will be twice as much as they usually gather) (r:1.26.12/41.4.8/2.16.5)
zah = (t:n) (w:time) (d:used with a number for how many times over something is repaid or done) (e:a ~ sagih vei-in note kong thuhilh/ang sungah a ~ sagih-in thuk in | pay back seven times into their laps/a ~ li-in ka loh kik ding hi | I will pay back four times as much) (r:3.26.18/19.79.12/42.19.8)
zaha = (t:adv) (w:so/such/to that extent) (d:zah, amount, with the linking a, used after hih, tua or bang and before a describing word or a noun: hih zaha tam is so many, bang zaha lian is how great) (e:bang ~ lian kidemna/hih ~ tam teci pan’nate | so many witnesses/tua ~ nopsaknate a beisak ta hi | such great wealth has been brought to ruin) (s:zahta) (b:zah) (r:51.2.1/58.12.1/66.18.17) (q:draft)
Zaham = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zaham) (d:son of King Rehoboam of Judah and his wife Mahalath) (r:14.11.19)
Zahaziel = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Jahaziel) (d:father of Shekaniah, of the descendants of Zattu, who returned from exile with Ezra) (r:15.8.5)
zahhuai = (t:v) (w:be put to shame/be ashamed/be disgraced) (d:be put to shame or disgraced, said mostly of enemies who are defeated; zahhuai sak is put someone to shame) (e:Ka galte khempeuh ~ in genthei mahmah/Amah guallel-in ~ ngeilo ding hi | he will never be defeated and put to shame/Kei hong mawhsakte ~-in beimang uh hen | may my accusers perish in shame/hong mudahte in mu-in a ~ nadingin | so that those who hate me may see it and be put to shame) (s:zum) (r:19.6.10/19.127.5/19.71.13/19.86.17) (q:draft)
zahhuaigawp = (t:v) (w:be utterly put to shame/be thrown into confusion) (d:zahhuai be put to shame, with gawp completely; with sak, put someone utterly to shame) (e:maizumsak inla, ~ sak in) (b:zahhuai) (r:19.35.26) (q:draft)
zahhuaina = (t:n) (w:shame/disgrace/scorn) (d:zahhuai, be put to shame, with the noun suffix na: shame or disgrace that comes on a person or a people) (e:Israel tungah ~ ka tungsak a/nomau’ ~ hi ding hi | it will be your disgrace/hong cite ~ tawh maikhing sak in | let those who say it to me be appalled with shame) (s:maizumna/mindaina/zumna) (a:pahtawina) (b:zahhuai) (r:23.43.28/23.30.3/19.40.15) (q:draft)
zahhuaisak = (t:v) (w:put to shame/disgrace/treat shamefully) (d:zahhuai, be put to shame, with the causative sak: put someone to shame, disgrace or treat shamefully) (e:kei hong ~ kei in/keimah hong ~ ngei kei in | never let me be put to shame/A kisikcip mite ~ kei in la | do not let the oppressed be put to shame/satin a ~ khit uh ciangin | after they had beaten him and treated him shamefully) (s:maizumsak/mindaisak/zumsak) (a:pahtawi) (b:zahhuai) (r:19.119.31/41.12.4/19.71.1/19.74.21/42.20.11) (q:draft)
zahin = (t:prep) (w:as much as/as many as/like) (d:zah, amount, with the marker in, placed after the thing compared: to the same amount or degree as) (e:ama pumpi a it ~/Jonathan in ama pumpi ~ it hi | Jonathan loved him as himself/Pilna in hauhna ~ hoih a | wisdom is as good as wealth/ni danga ~ mi tampi ka phasak ding hi | I will make them as many as before/Kei ~ nang hat na hi hiam | are you as strong as I am) (b:zah) (r:9.20.17/38.10.8/9.18.1/21.7.11/18.40.9) (q:draft)
Zahin = (t:prep) (w:as much as/as) (d:zahin, as much as, capitalised in a section heading, love is as strong as death) (e:Itna in Sihna ~ Khauh) (b:zahin) (r:22.8.4) (q:draft)
zahko = (t:v) (w:mock/ridicule/scoff at/insult) (d:make fun of someone with scorn, laugh at and insult; often said of enemies) (e:tua Topa in amaute ~ hi/Judah mite hong ~ hi | he ridiculed the Jews/zahtakna mel nei loin hong ~ uh a | they mocked me without any respect/Zeisu simmawhin a ~ uh a | they treated Jesus with contempt and mocked him) (s:zahpih/nuihsan/simmawhbawl) (a:zahtak) (r:19.2.4/16.4.1/19.35.16/42.23.11) (q:draft)
zahkohna = (t:n) (w:mockery/reproach/contempt/insult) (d:zahko, mock, with the noun suffix na: mockery or contempt shown to someone; also written zahkona) (e:namdangte’ ~ i ngah loh nadingin/Nabal khut tung panin ka ngah ~ | the contempt I received from the hand of Nabal) (s:zahkona/zahpihna/simmawhna) (a:zahtakna) (r:16.5.9/9.25.39) (q:draft)
zahkoin = (t:v) (w:mocking/ridiculing) (d:zahko mock, with in linking it to the next verb) (e:amah ~ a sat uh hi/amah ~, cil tawh phihin, satin | mocking him, spitting on him and flogging him) (s:zahpihin) (b:zahko) (r:42.22.63/41.10.34) (q:draft)
zahkona = (t:n) (w:ridicule/reproach/contempt/taunt) (d:zahko, mock, with the noun suffix na: mockery, ridicule or a taunt; zahkona kam is a taunting saying) (e:minam dangte’ ~ i ngah loh nadingin/hih ~ kam na zang ding uh hi | you will use this taunt/a nungta Pasian a ~ | his ridicule of the living God/nang hong ~ mah tawh | with the very contempt they showed you) (s:zahkohna/zahpihna/simmawhna) (a:zahtakna) (b:zahko) (r:16.5.9/19.123.4/23.14.4/23.37.17/19.79.12) (q:draft)
zahkonate = (t:n) (w:mockeries/ridicule/taunts) (d:zahkona mockery with plural te) (e:simmawhna leh ~ ka thuaksak ding a) (s:simmawhnate) (b:zahkona) (r:24.24.9/24.29.18) (q:draft)
zahkote = (t:n) (w:mockers/those who taunt) (d:zahko mock, with plural te: those who mock) (e:kei hong ~ tungah ka dawn’ nading) (b:zahko) (r:19.119.42) (q:draft)
zahla = (t:v) (w:be ashamed/feel disgrace) (d:feel shame for what one has done; found once, paired with maizum, ashamed) (e:na hih manin ~ in la, maizum in) (s:zum) (r:26.16.52) (q:draft, low confidence)
zahnih = (t:adv) (w:double/twice as much/twofold) (d:zah, amount, with nih, two: twice the amount; used as a zahnih, double of it) (e:Ama gamtatna a ~ thukkik in/amah ading a ~ bawlsak in | mix a double portion for her) (r:66.18.6) (q:draft)
zahpi = (t:n) (w:so great a number/so many) (d:zah amount with pi great; hih zahpi is this great a number) (e:Mi hih ~ kham ding khomun) (b:zah) (r:40.15.33) (q:draft)
zahpih = (t:v) (w:mock/scoff at/ridicule/jeer at) (d:treat with scorn, often paired with simmawh despise and nuihsan laugh at) (e:minam khempeuh na ~ hi/nitak dong a hong ~ uh hi | they mock me until evening/na ut uh leh hong ~ un | mock me if you wish/amaute nuihsanin ~ uh a | they laughed at them and mocked them) (s:zahko/nuihsan/zahpihbawl) (a:zahtak) (r:19.59.8/25.3.63/18.21.3/14.30.10) (q:draft)
zahpihbawl = (t:v) (w:mock/ridicule/sneer at/make fun of) (d:zahpih, mock, with bawl, do or treat) (e:Galkapte in zong ~ uh a/mi pawlkhat in ~ uh a | some of them sneered/a lu uh singin ~ uh a | they shook their heads and mocked him) (s:zahpih/zahko/simmawhbawl) (a:zahtakbawl) (b:zahpih) (r:42.23.36/44.17.32/41.15.29) (q:draft)
zahpihhuai = (t:adj) (w:contemptible/despicable) (d:deserving to be mocked or looked down on; with zaw, more contemptible) (e:Silate sangin a ~ zaw mite in) (s:simmawhhuai) (a:zahtakhuai) (r:25.5.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
zahpihin = (t:v) (w:mocking/laughing at/scoffing at) (d:zahpih with the linking suffix in: making fun of someone, and) (e:tua mite in ~ a nuihsan uh hi/Zeisu ~ a nuihsan uh hi | they laughed at Jesus in mockery/amaute in Pasian’ kamtaite ~ | they mocked God’s messengers/Elijah in amaute ~ | Elijah taunted them) (s:zahkoin/nuihsanin) (b:zahpih) (r:40.9.24/14.36.16/42.8.53/11.18.27) (q:draft)
zahpihna = (t:n) (w:mockery/ridicule/reproach/taunt) (d:zahpih, mock, with the noun suffix na: mockery or a taunt; zahpihna tawh is mockingly) (e:simmawhna leh ~ ka thuak lawh hi/kote ~ leh simmawhna tawh | with mockery and contempt for us/ci-in ~ tawh a hopih uh hi | they addressed him in mockery/mihingte’ ~ ka sungah ka thuakna | how I bear in my heart the taunts of people) (s:zahkona/zahkohna/nuihsatna) (a:zahtakna) (b:zahpih) (r:24.20.8/16.2.19/40.27.29/19.89.50) (q:draft)
zahsak = (t:v) (w:tell/inform/let hear) (d:cause someone to hear, tell or report news; from zak, hear, with the causative sak) (e:hih thu hong ~ thei dingin) (s:zasak/zaksak/theihsak) (r:18.1.15) (q:draft)
zahta = (t:adv) (w:so much/this much/such) (d:follows hih or tua: to such an extent, so much or so many; often written zahta-in) (e:sisan tua ~ luangsak na hih manin/Pasian in tua ~-in eite hong it ahihleh | since God so loved us/Kampau hih ~ hong kidawng lo ding | so many words going unanswered/Tua ~-in mawhnei mite’ langbawlna | such opposition from sinners) (s:zaha) (b:zah) (r:13.22.8/18.6.10/62.4.11/18.11.2/58.12.3) (q:draft)
zahtak = (t:v) (w:respect/honor/fear/revere) (d:show respect, honor or reverent fear to God, parents, rulers or other people) (e:Kumpipa na ~ un/Na nu leh na pa ~ in | honor your father and mother/ka tapa a ~ ding uh hi | they will respect my son/Topa na ~ nuam kei uh a | you did not choose to fear the Lord/na anpalte tawh Topa ~ in | honor the Lord with your firstfruits) (s:zaktak/pahtawi/zahtakbawl) (a:simmawh/zahko) (r:60.2.17/20.3.9/40.19.19/40.21.37/20.1.29) (q:draft)
Zahtak = (t:v) (w:fear/revere/honor) (d:zahtak, fear or honor, written with a capital at the start of a sentence and in Isaac’ Zahtak pa, the One whom Isaac feared, a name of God, the Fear of Isaac in the NIV) (e:le Isaac’ ~ pa in kei hong ompih/~ ding a kilawmte | those who ought to be honored/~ lecin nang a dingin thu hong hoihin | if you honor them it will go well with you) (b:zahtak) (r:1.31.42/1.31.53/45.13.7/49.6.2) (q:draft)
zahtaka = (t:v) (w:respect/fear/revere) (d:zahtak respect, with a linking it to what follows: respecting and) (e:Pasian ~ ama deihna a zui mite/Mite’ ~ a kinei mite in | those who are held in respect by people) (b:zahtak) (r:43.9.31/18.17.9) (q:draft)
zahtakbawl = (t:v) (w:respect/honor/show respect to) (d:zahtak respect with bawl do, treat someone with respect) (e:a tote uh ~ ta uh hen/ka tapa na ~ ding uh hi | they will respect my son/Keimah in ka Pa ka ~ a | I honor my Father/amah a ~ lohna a theih ciangin | when he saw that he paid him no honor) (s:zahtak/pahtawi) (a:simmawhbawl/zahpihbawl) (b:zahtak) (r:54.6.1/54.5.3/41.12.6/43.8.49/17.3.5) (q:draft)
zahtakhuai = (t:adj) (w:honorable/respected/awesome) (d:deserving honor or reverence, from zahtak respect and huai worthy of; with taka, in a dignified way) (e:mi ginalote pen mi ~ kici nawn lo/a minthang, ~ min | glorious and awesome name/ama biakinn sungah ~ mahmah a | he is very awesome in his sanctuary/mizawng hi-in a ~ lo ka hihna | that I am poor and not respected) (s:kihtakhuai/pahtakhuai) (a:zahpihhuai/simmawhhuai) (r:23.32.5/5.28.58/19.68.35/9.18.23) (q:draft)
zahtakin = (t:v) (w:fear/revere/respect) (d:zahtak with the linking ending in, followed by another verb: fearing, revering) (e:Pasian ~ gamtat hoih lo a pel/Topa ~, a sia pel in | fear the Lord and shun evil/na nu leh na pa uh ~ | respecting your mother and father/puteekte’ maitang ~ | showing respect to the elderly/kei hong ~ hong kihta takpi uh hi | they revered me and truly feared me) (a:simmawhin) (b:zahtak) (r:18.1.8/20.3.7/3.19.3/3.19.32/39.2.5) (q:draft)
zahtakna = (t:n) (w:fear/reverence/respect/honour) (d:reverent fear or respect, Topa zahtakna is the fear of the Lord) (e:Topa ~ in khan’sausak a/Khazih ~ hangin | out of reverence for Christ/sumbukah ~ tawh hopih | to be greeted with respect in the marketplace/Topa na ~ zom paisuak in | continue always in the fear of the Lord) (s:kihtakna/pahtawina) (a:simmawhna/zahkona) (b:zahtak) (r:20.10.27/49.5.21/40.23.7/20.23.17) (q:draft)
Zahtakpa = (t:n) (w:Fear/the One feared) (d:Zahtak, fear or revere, with -pa, the male one: the One who is feared; Isaak’ Zahtakpa is a name of God, the Fear of Isaac in the NIV) (e:Abraham’ Pasian leh Isaak’ ~ in/ama' pa Isaak' ~ tawh kiciam hi | he swore by the Fear of his father Isaac) (b:Zahtak) (r:1.31.42/1.31.53) (q:draft)
zahtakte = (t:n) (w:those who fear/worshippers) (d:zahtak with plural te, those who fear or revere; mostly Topa a zahtakte, those who fear the Lord) (e:Topa a ~ aw, Topa phat un/Topa in amah a ~ hong hehpih hi | the Lord has compassion on those who fear him/Amah in amah ~ an pia a | he gives food to those who fear him) (s:kihtate) (b:zahtak) (r:19.135.20/19.118.4/19.103.13/19.111.5) (q:draft)
zahtaktheih = (t:v) (w:be able to respect/be respected) (d:zahtak respect with theih can: mite’ zahtaktheih dingin, so that people can respect it) (e:mite’ ~ dingin thu na hilh inla) (b:zahtak) (r:56.2.7) (q:draft)
zahtaktuam = (t:n) (w:partiality/special regard) (d:zahtak respect with tuam separate: respect shown to one person above others; zahtaktuam nei lo is show no partiality) (e:Mite kuamah ~ nei lo na hih manin) (s:deidanna/angvanna) (r:40.22.16) (q:draft)
zahtakzaw = (t:v) (w:fear more/respect more) (d:zahtak respect, with zaw more) (e:Pasian a ~ mi khat ahi hi) (s:kihtazaw) (b:zahtak) (r:16.7.2) (q:draft)
zahtuan = (t:v) (w:spare/have regard for) (d:show regard or mercy to someone; found in the negative, zahtuan lo, not spare) (e:a sanggampa ~ lo hi) (r:23.9.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
zahun = (t:conj) (w:as much as/as far as/to the extent that) (d:zah, amount, with the plural ending un, after a clause whose subject is plural: na hih zawh zahun is as far as you are able) (e:na hih zawh ~ mi khempeuh tawh/na hih zawh ~ cingsak un | make it as secure as you can/Kote in note ka hong it ~ | just as much as we love you/a tha neih ~ gualnopna a bawl uh hi | they celebrated with all their might) (b:zah) (r:45.12.18/52.3.12/40.27.65/13.13.8) (q:draft)
zahval = (t:adv) (w:more than/beyond) (d:zah amount with val exceed, after a phrase naming an amount: more than that amount) (e:a kilawm ~ na dong kei un/a kicing ding ~ | more than enough/na pau ding a kilawm ~ pau kei in | do not say more than you should/Ka gen dinga kilawm ~ genkha ka hih manin | because I have said more than I should) (r:42.3.13/2.36.5/21.5.2/18.40.5) (q:draft)
zahzah = (t:adv) (w:as many as/as much as/whatever amount) (d:placed after a verb, to the full number or amount that is so) (e:Tui zong duh ~ hi loin/na duh ~ uh sa na ne thei ding | you may eat as much meat as you want/na khua om ~ uh pasian na nei uh a | you have as many gods as you have towns/na deih ~ la in | take as much as you want) (r:26.4.11/24.11.13/5.12.20/9.2.16) (q:draft)
zahzaha = (t:adv) (w:as much as/to the full extent) (d:zahzah with the ending a; ahi thei zahzaha is as much as is possible) (e:ahi thei ~ sep ding mah hi) (b:zahzah) (r:44.26.9) (q:draft)
zahzahin = (t:adv) (w:as much as/as far as) (d:placed after a verb to mean to the full extent of what is wanted or possible) (e:mite’ deih ~ a hawm uh/ahi zo ~ i tanh kik hi | as far as possible we have bought them back/ka deih ~, tuate ka tang ding hi | I will take of them as much as I want) (b:zahzah) (r:43.6.11/16.5.8/2.15.9) (q:draft)
zahzahun = (t:adv) (w:as much as/as many as) (d:zahzah, as much as, with the plural ending un, used when the subject is plural: a duh zahzahun is as much as they want) (e:a duh ~ sa ne-in si dawn ding/vasate khempeuh in a nekzawh ~ | all the birds, as much as they could eat) (b:zahzah) (r:26.39.17/66.19.21) (q:draft)
zai = (t:adj) (w:wide/broad/spacious) (d:wide, also used after a measure to give the width) (e:tong sawmli sau-in tong sawmthum ~ a/Khuapi lianin ~ a | the city was large and spacious/Ka lungsim uh zong a ~ hi | our hearts too are wide open/tong li sau, tong li ~, tong thum sang hi | four cubits long, four wide and three high) (a:kawcik/kawciik) (r:26.46.22/16.7.4/47.6.11/11.7.27) (q:draft)
Zai = (t:adj) (w:broad/wide) (d:zai written with a capital in Kulh Zai, the Broad Wall of Jerusalem) (e:amaute in Kulh ~ ciang dong/Meikhuk Tausang pan Kulh ~-ah | from the Tower of the Ovens to the Broad Wall) (b:zai) (r:16.3.8/16.12.38) (q:draft)
zailam = (t:n) (w:width/breadth) (d:zai wide with lam side, the measure across, set against saulam the length) (e:a ~ tai li kisehkhia ding hi) (s:zaina/vailam) (a:saulam) (r:26.45.3) (q:draft)
zaina = (t:n) (w:breadth) (d:zai, wide, with the noun suffix na: breadth or largeness, here of understanding) (e:sehnel bangin lungsim ~ pia a) (b:zai) (r:11.4.29)
zaina = (t:n) (w:width) (d:zai, wide, with the noun suffix na: the measure of a thing from side to side, paired with sauna for the length) (e:a ~ tong sawmnga/a ~ tong tul sawm hi ding hi | its width will be ten thousand cubits/inn ~ zahin tong sawmnih sau a | twenty cubits long, the same as the width of the house) (s:zailam/vailam) (a:sauna) (b:zai) (r:1.6.15/26.48.13/11.6.3)
zaipi = (t:adj) (w:very wide/extensive/vast) (d:zai wide with pi great) (e:Amah in gam ~ tak uk ding a/I nasepna lian a, ~ tak huam hi | our work is great and covers a very wide area/leitang ~ a ngah theih nadingun | so that they may get a wide stretch of land) (b:zai) (r:27.11.3/16.4.19/18.24.2) (q:draft)
Zair = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Zair) (d:place in or near Edom where King Jehoram of Judah fought the Edomites) (r:12.8.21)
zaisak = (t:v) (w:widen/broaden/make wide) (d:zai wide with sak cause; after a measure, make so many wide) (e:Keima theihna nong ~ ciangin/tong nga sau-in tong nga na ~ ding hi | you shall make it five cubits long and five cubits wide) (b:zai) (r:19.119.32/2.27.1) (q:draft)
zaizai = (t:adv) (d:expressive word placed after a verb, describing many small things flashing, sparkling, crackling or flying out at once) (e:a tee ~ suangmanphate lakah na vak kawikawi/mei-ek leengkhia ~ hi | sparks of fire fly out/A hetthiai ciangin taang ~ a | when it sneezes, light flashes out/Mual tungah a tuan ~ laitakun | as they leap over the mountaintops) (r:26.28.14/18.41.19/18.41.18/29.2.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
zaizaw = (t:adj) (w:wider/broader) (d:zai wide, with zaw more) (e:tuipi sangin ~ hi) (b:zai) (r:18.11.9) (q:draft)
zak = (t:v) (w:hear) (d:form of za used before ciangin, ding and other dependent endings) (e:Moses in tua thu a ~ ciangin/Khua ~ nading bil nei mi | whoever has ears to hear/Tua thu Pilat in a ~ ciangin | when Pilate heard this/Amaute in hih thu a ~ uh ciangin | when they heard this) (b:za) (r:4.16.4/13.19.8/40.11.15/43.19.8/44.19.5) (q:draft)
zakha = (t:v) (w:happen to hear/overhear) (d:za hear with kha, by chance) (e:hong samsiatna na ~ ding hi) (s:zakkhak) (r:21.7.21) (q:draft)
Zakhariah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zechariah) (d:father of Abijah, the mother of King Hezekiah) (r:14.29.1)
zakhat = (t:num) (w:one hundred/hundred) (d:za, hundred, with khat, one; tul zakhat is one hundred thousand) (e:Note nga in ~ zo-in/a vekpi-in a kimkotah ~ om a | there were a hundred in all around it/ngun talen ~ tawh | for a hundred talents of silver/mi tul ~ hing mat uh hi | they took a hundred thousand people alive) (s:za) (r:3.26.8/24.52.23/14.25.6/13.5.21) (q:draft)
zakhatin = (t:adv) (w:a hundred times/a hundredfold) (d:zakhat one hundred, with the marker in) (e:om zah ~ a tamna behlap hen) (s:zavei) (b:zakhat) (r:10.24.3) (q:draft)
zakhatte = (t:num) (w:hundred/one hundred) (d:zakhat one hundred, with plural te for the people or things counted; tul leh zakhatte is eleven hundred) (e:ngun peek tul leh ~ a nu kiangah/Mihing ~’ mai-ah | before a hundred men) (b:zakhat) (r:7.17.3/12.4.43) (q:draft)
zakhin = (t:v) (w:have heard/hear) (d:za hear with khin marking the action as completed) (e:ama hihsa thute ~ uh ahih manin/Pasian in na thungetna hong ~ a | God has heard your prayer/A thu ~ nai lopi-a dawn’kikna | answering before having heard the matter/amaute in pel loin ~ ding uh ahih manin | since they will certainly hear of it) (b:za) (r:41.3.8/42.1.13/20.18.13/44.21.22) (q:draft)
Zakhur = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zakkur) (d:a son of Asaph, a temple musician in the time of David; spelled Zakkur in the NIV) (r:13.25.2)
zakiasak = (t:v) (w:dethrone/depose/remove from office) (d:za, rank or office, with kiasak, cause to fall: bring a ruler down from his position) (e:Amah in kumpite ~ a/Jerusalem ah amah ~ a | he dethroned him in Jerusalem) (r:18.12.18/14.36.3) (q:draft)
zakiat = (t:v) (w:fall from power/lose position) (d:za rank with kiat fall; set against liat, become great) (e:amaute a ~ ciangin) (r:20.28.28) (q:draft)
zakiatna = (t:n) (w:downfall/fall from power) (d:zakiat fall from power, with the noun suffix na) (e:a gilo uliante’ ~ mu ding uh hi) (s:kiatna) (b:zakiat) (r:20.29.16) (q:draft)
zakik = (t:v) (w:hear again) (d:za hear with kik again) (e:Hih thu khatvei ~ nuam lai ung) (s:zakkik/ngaikik) (b:za) (r:44.17.32) (q:draft)
zakin = (t:prep) (w:in the hearing of) (d:placed after the hearer: while that person listens, to the ears of) (e:Hih laibu mite’ ~ na sim khit ciangin/Keima ~ thu na gen khin a | you have spoken in my hearing/mipi’ ~ Moses’ laibute sim uh a | they read the Book of Moses in the hearing of the people/ama ~ tua laibu kisim hi | the book was read to him) (b:zak) (r:24.51.63/5.31.30/18.33.8/16.13.1/17.6.1) (q:draft)
Zakkai = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zakkai) (d:ancestor of a family of 760 people who returned from exile with Zerubbabel) (r:15.2.9/16.7.14)
zakkhak = (t:v) (w:happen to hear/come to hear) (d:zak hear with khak, by chance or as it turns out) (e:nang kong hopihlam a ~ uh a) (s:zakha) (r:24.38.25) (q:draft)
Zakkhias = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zacchaeus) (d:chief tax collector in Jericho, a rich man who welcomed Jesus into his house) (r:42.19.2/42.19.5)
zakkhit = (t:v) (w:have heard/finish hearing) (d:zak, hear, with khit, finished: used before ciangin or phet for after hearing, as soon as one has heard) (e:a cinat a ~ ciangin tua lai-ah/Ama thugen teng a ~ uh ciangin | after they had heard all he said/a ~ phetun Satan hong pai-in | as soon as they hear it Satan comes) (r:43.11.6/41.4.15/44.21.20) (q:draft)
Zakkhur = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zakkur) (d:leader of the third group of temple musicians in the time of David, a son of Asaph) (r:13.25.10)
zakkik = (t:v) (w:hear again) (d:zak hear with kik again) (e:a ~ nawn loh nadingun a thum uh hi) (s:zakik/ngaikik) (b:zak) (r:58.12.19) (q:draft)
Zakkur = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zaccur/Zakkur) (d:name of several men, among them the father of Shammua, the spy from the tribe of Reuben) (r:4.13.4)
zakma = (t:v) (w:before hearing) (d:zak hear with ma before: before one hears or heard) (e:Thu dang na ~ un) (r:51.1.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
zakna = (t:n) (w:hearing) (d:zak with na, the act of hearing or what is heard) (e:upna in thu ~ hangin a piang hi/Hit mite’ ~-ah | in the hearing of the Hittites/a bil-a a ~ tawh thu khentat lo ding hi | he will not decide by what his ears hear) (b:zak) (r:45.10.17/20.15.30/1.23.16/23.11.3) (q:draft)
zaknop = (t:v) (w:want to hear/long to hear) (d:form of za hear with nop want; after a possessive, what someone likes to hear) (e:a ~ uh hangin a za kei/amaute’ ~ thute bek a gen ding sia | teachers who say only what they want to hear/mi’ ~, mi’ ngaihnop dingin na pau un | speak in a way that people like to hear and listen to/Topa’ thu ~ mahmahna kialpi | a famine of longing to hear the word of the Lord) (s:zanuam) (r:40.13.17/55.4.3/51.4.6/30.8.11) (q:draft)
zaknophuai = (t:adj) (w:pleasant to hear/pleasing/gracious) (d:of words or speech, sweet to listen to; from zak hear, nop pleasant and huai worthy of) (e:amau’ pauna ~ semsem hi/Thugen Siampa in a ~ kammal khawm a | the Teacher gathered pleasing words) (r:20.16.23/21.12.10) (q:draft)
zakphetin = (t:v) (w:as soon as one hears/on hearing) (d:zak hear with phet, the very moment, and the marker in) (e:thu Ahab in a ~) (r:11.21.16) (q:draft)
zaksa = (t:v) (w:heard/already heard) (d:zak with -sa, already; with a pronoun before it, what one has heard) (e:ka bil-in ka ~, ka theihsa thu/A muhsa leh a ~ thute teci a pang hi | he testifies to what he has seen and heard/Keima kiangah na ~ | what you heard from me/Baruk in a sim a ~ thu teng khempeuh | everything he had heard Baruch read) (s:zasa) (b:zak) (r:18.13.1/40.11.4/43.3.32/55.1.13/24.36.13) (q:draft)
zaksak = (t:v) (w:tell/report/proclaim/make known) (d:zak, hear, with the causative sak: cause to hear, tell, report or proclaim news) (e:nungzui dangte a ~ uh hangin/Gentailte kiheina thu a ~ uh ciangin | when they told how the Gentiles had turned/bangci a piang ci-in amaute a ~ uh ciangin | when they told them how it had happened/Topa’ hehpihna kum ahi, ci-in ~ nading | to proclaim that it is the year of the Lord’s favor) (s:zasak/zahsak/theihsak/pulak) (b:zak) (r:41.16.13/42.4.19/44.15.3/41.5.16) (q:draft)
zaksakna = (t:n) (w:announcement/proclamation/notice/report) (d:zaksak make hear with na: making something known, by word, letter or signal) (e:ci-in Aaron in ~ bawl hi/Jerusalem sung khempeuhah thu ~ kibawl hi | a proclamation was made throughout Jerusalem/Nang thu ~ lai | a letter of report about you/Dinkhiat nading ~ na tum ciangin | when you blow the signal for setting out) (s:theihsakna/thuzaksakna) (b:zaksak) (r:2.32.5/44.28.21/14.24.9/4.10.5) (q:draft)
zaktak = (t:v) (w:fear/revere/respect/honor) (d:show reverence or respect to God or to a person; another spelling of zahtak) (e:Topa i Pasian ~ ni/Keimah in Pasian ~ ka hih manin | because I fear God/na Pasian uh na ~ ding uh hi | you shall fear your God/tu-in Topa ~ un la | now fear the Lord) (s:zahtak/kihta) (a:simmawh) (r:24.5.24/1.42.18/3.19.14/6.24.14) (q:draft)
zaktakin = (t:adv) (w:reverently/with awe) (d:zaktak revere, with the ending in; zaktakin kihta is stand in awe of) (e:Israel’ Pasian ~ kihta ding uh hi) (b:zaktak) (r:23.29.23) (q:draft)
zakte = (t:n) (w:things heard/what one hears) (d:zak, hear, with the plural te, placed after the one who hears: the things that someone hears) (e:Na ~ uh a zaknop uh hangin/genthangna thu ka ~ hoih lo hi | the report I hear is not good/na ~ uh le na muh uh thute | the things you hear and see/thu ka ~ no kong theisak zo hi | I have made known to you what I heard) (b:zak) (r:40.13.17/43.15.15/9.2.24/40.11.4) (q:draft)
zakthadahhuai = (t:adj) (w:detestable/hateful to hear) (d:zak hear with thadahhuai, wearisome or loathsome: not worth listening to) (e:Pasian in ~ sa hi) (r:20.28.9) (q:draft)
zaktheih = (t:v) (w:be able to hear/can hear) (d:zak hear with theih can, the form used before ding, nading and hangin) (e:a hong ~ nadingin a gingin ka kiko hi/a huging na ~ hangin | though you can hear its sound/nangma thugente a ~ nadingin | so that he may hear what you say/a ~ dingun kua’ kiangah va gen ding | to whom shall I speak so that they can hear) (b:zak) (r:19.77.1/43.3.8/44.10.22/24.6.10) (q:draft)
zakua = (t:num) (w:nine hundred) (d:za, hundred, with kua, nine) (e:ni ~/kum ~/sik leeng ~ nei a | he had nine hundred iron chariots/kum ~ leh kum sawmnga | nine hundred and fifty years) (r:7.4.3/1.5.5/1.9.29)
zakzah = (t:adv) (w:as much as) (d:placed after zawh, be able: puak zawh zakzah is as much as can be carried) (e:amau’ puak zawh ~ guang in la) (s:zahzah) (r:1.44.1) (q:draft, low confidence)
zakzak = (t:v) (w:keep hearing/hear again and again) (d:zak hear, said twice for repeated or continued action; in Isaiah 42:2 gen zakzak is speak out so as to be heard) (e:Na ~ uh hangin na tel kei ding/numeite in thu a ~ uh hangin | though such women keep hearing the word/kongzing lakah zong thu gen ~ lo ding | he will not make his voice heard in the streets) (s:zaza) (r:40.13.14/55.3.7/23.42.2) (q:draft)
zakzakna = (t:see) <zakzakna-un>
zakzakna-un = (t:n) (w:at their hearing/when they hear) (d:zakzak keep hearing, with the noun suffix na and un for a plural subject: as they hear it) (e:hih thu a ~ a bil uh ngong) (r:33.7.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
zakzaksa = (t:v) (w:have heard/already heard) (d:zakzak keep hearing, with sa marking what is already done) (e:na ~ uh thu ahi hi/ka bil-in ka ~, ka theihtheihsa thu ahi hi | it is what my ears have heard and understood) (s:zaksa/zasa) (b:zakzak) (r:62.2.7/18.13.1) (q:draft)
zal = (t:v) (w:spread out/stretch out) (d:open something out wide, as God spreads out the sky and the earth, or as one spreads a tent or wings) (e:Amah bek in vanpi ~ a/Pasian in mun awng tungah vanpi ~ a | God spreads the sky over empty space/vantungte pen puanbuk bangin na ~ hi | you stretch out the heavens like a tent/kuama seppih lohin leitung ka ~ hi | I spread out the earth with no one helping) (s:zalh) (r:18.9.8/26.1.23/18.26.7/19.104.2/23.44.24) (q:draft)
Zalaf = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zalaph) (d:father of Hanun, who helped repair the wall of Jerusalem in the time of Nehemiah) (r:16.3.30)
zalesawmnga = (t:num) (w:one hundred and fifty) (d:za hundred, le and, sawmnga fifty; in 1 Kings 7:2 a length counted in pi, feet, where the NIV has a hundred cubits) (e:A sauna pi ~ hi a) (r:11.7.2) (q:draft)
zalh = (t:v) (w:spread out/stretch out/lay flat) (d:to spread something out flat, used of stretching out the heavens, spreading grain and levelling ridges of soil) (e:ama’ siamna tawh vantung a ~ hi/tua tungah an ~ hi | she spread grain over it/leivumte ~ mai-in, guahtui tawh na nipsak a | you level its ridges and soften it with showers) (s:zal) (r:24.10.12/10.17.19/19.65.10) (q:draft)
zalhmai = (t:see) <zalhmai-in>
zalhmai-in = (t:v) (w:level/flatten/make level) (d:zalhmai, make flat and even, with the linking ending in, which joins it to the following verb; zalh is spread flat) (e:leivumte ~, guahtui tawh na nipsak a/Nangma mai-ah kei pai-in mualte ~ | I will go before you and level the mountains) (s:zalhtam) (r:19.65.10/23.45.2) (q:draft)
zalhtam = (t:v) (w:level/make level) (d:make the ground flat before sowing) (e:Amah in lei a ~ khit ciangin) (r:23.28.25) (q:draft)
zali = (t:num) (w:four hundred) (d:za, hundred, with li, four) (e:ni ~/kum ~/amaute in kum ~ a bawlsia ding uh hi | they will mistreat them for four hundred years/amah tawh mihing ~ hong pai | four hundred men coming with him/ngun shekel ~ man hi | it is worth four hundred shekels of silver) (r:44.7.6/1.11.13/1.33.1/1.23.15)
zalian = (t:n) (w:high rank/rank) (d:za rank or title with lian great; zalian a neipa is a man of rank) (e:mi sawmnga a uk bupa leh ~ a neipa) (s:zaliatna) (a:zaneu) (r:23.3.3) (q:draft)
zalianpi = (t:n) (w:high position/very high rank) (d:zalian high rank, with pi great) (e:Mihaite, ~ kipia a) (s:zaliatna) (b:zalian) (r:21.10.6) (q:draft)
zaliatna = (t:n) (w:high rank/high position/dignity) (d:za, rank, with liatna, greatness: a great office or exalted standing) (e:Amah a ~ panin sukniam ding/a sangte minphatna, ~ pia-in | giving honour and high rank to those who accept him) (s:zalian) (a:zaneu) (r:19.62.4/27.11.39) (q:draft)
zalin = (t:v) (w:spread out/stretch out) (d:zal with the ending in, which links it to the following verb: spreading, stretching out, said of wings and of the heavens) (e:Simbung in a kha ~ leitaw lamah/Kherubte in a khate uh a tungah ~ | the cherubim spread their wings above/Vanpi ~, leitung piangsak a | stretching out the sky and founding the earth/vantungte puan bangin ~ | stretching out the heavens like a cloth) (b:zal) (r:18.39.26/38.12.1/2.37.9/23.40.22) (q:draft)
zalite = (t:num) (w:four hundred) (d:zali with plural -te, the four hundred, placed after the noun it counts) (e:amah leh mi ~ a delhin paisuak/kalaoh tungah tuangin a tai tangval ~ | the four hundred young men who fled on camels/Asherah kamsang ~ hong khawm in | gather the four hundred prophets of Asherah/mangkawlsing gah ~ | the four hundred pomegranates) (b:zali) (r:9.30.10/11.7.42/9.30.17/11.18.19) (q:draft)
zalkhia = (t:v) (w:spread out/stretch out) (d:zal spread out, with khia out) (e:tungah vanpi hong ~ a) (b:zal) (r:18.26.7) (q:draft)
Zalmon = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zalmon) (d:the Ahohite, one of the thirty mighty warriors of David) (e:Ahoah mi ~, Netofah khuami Maharai) (r:10.23.28) (q:draft)
Zalmon = (t:name) (c:mountain) (w:Zalmon) (d:mountain near Shechem where Abimelek and his men cut branches; also the snow-covered mountain of Psalm 68) (e:~ mual tunga vuk kia tawh kibang) (r:19.68.14/7.9.48) (q:draft)
Zalmonah = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Zalmonah) (d:place where the Israelites camped in the wilderness after leaving Mount Hor) (r:4.33.41/4.33.42)
Zalmunna = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zalmunna) (d:king of Midian whom Gideon pursued, captured and killed, always named together with Zebah) (r:7.8.12/7.8.21)
Zalmunnate = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zalmunna) (d:Zalmunna with the plural te, used when Zebah and Zalmunna are named together as a pair) (b:Zalmunna) (r:7.8.10)
zalpa = (t:n) (w:one who spreads out) (d:zal spread out, with pa marking a male: he who spreads out) (e:tuite tungah leitung a ~ tungah/teen theih nadingin puanbuk bangin a ~ | he who spreads them out like a tent to live in) (b:zal) (r:19.136.6/23.40.22) (q:draft)
zalzal = (t:adv) (w:flashing/glittering/in flashes) (d:describes repeated flashing or darting; placed after tee or phe, glitter, and after kin, quick) (e:na teipi tee ~ a muh ciangin/luum leh teite tee ~ hi | the spear and lance flash/khuaphia mah bangin kin ~ kawikawi uh hi | they darted back and forth like lightning/Khuaphia bangin a tee ~ | it flashes like lightning) (s:zialzial) (r:35.3.11/26.1.14/18.39.23/26.21.15) (q:draft)
zalzo = (t:v) (w:be able to spread out) (d:zal spread out, with zo be able) (e:ama hih bangin ~ na hi hiam) (b:zal) (r:18.37.18) (q:draft)
zam = (t:v) (w:reach out/stretch out/spread) (d:stretch the hand toward something to take or touch it; of branches and vines, spread out or climb over) (e:a hiangte kulh tungah ~ hi/puanbuk khetphim a khutin ~ a | she reached for the tent peg with her hand/Topa in a khut tawh hong ~ phei-in | the Lord reached out his hand to me/leenggah gui ~ bangin na hiangte in tuipi kantan | like a spreading vine your branches crossed the sea) (r:1.49.22/7.5.26/24.1.9/24.48.32) (q:draft)
Zamari = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Zemarites) (d:Canaanite people descended from Canaan son of Ham, listed with the Arvadites and Hamathites) (r:1.10.18)
zamin = (t:v) (w:reaching out/stretching out/straining toward) (d:zam reach or stretch out with the linking suffix -in, followed by another verb) (e:a khut tawh ~ kei hong la/ka mai lamah a omte ~ | straining toward what is ahead/tuipi lamah a hiangte ~ | its branches reaching to the sea/a khut tawh Peter ~ len a | he reached out his hand and caught Peter) (b:zam) (r:19.18.16/50.3.13/19.80.11/40.14.31) (q:draft)
zamsuak = (t:v) (w:reach as far as/spread out to) (d:zam spread or reach out, of branches, with suak come out to) (e:Jezer khua dongah na ~ hi) (r:24.48.32) (q:draft)
Zamzummim = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Zamzummites) (d:name the Ammonites gave to the Rephaites, a tall and numerous people who lived in their land before them) (r:5.2.20)
zan = (t:n) (w:night) (d:the dark part of the day, the opposite of sun, day; sun leh zan is day and night and zan khat is one night) (e:Tua ~ mahmah in Babilon kumpipa Belshazzar kithat a/Sun sawmli leh ~ sawmli sung | for forty days and forty nights/~ simin theihtelna pulaklak hi | night after night they reveal knowledge/~ mangmat hun lai takin | at the time of dreams in the night) (a:sun) (r:1.7.12/27.5.30/19.19.2/18.4.13)
Zan = (t:n) (w:night) (d:zan, night, written with a capital at the start of a sentence, and in Genesis 1:5 as the name God gave to the darkness) (e:khuamial pen ~ ci hi/~ khat amaute gel in mang man uh hi | one night the two of them had a dream/~ sialin ka khitui in ka lupna tum a | all night long my tears flood my bed/~ lai takin Topa in mang sungah | one night the Lord in a vision) (a:Sun) (b:zan) (r:1.1.5/1.40.5/19.6.6/44.18.9) (q:draft)
zana = (t:adv) (w:yesterday/last night) (d:zan night with a: in the night just past, yesterday; tua zana is of that night) (e:~ Izipt mi na thah bangin/tua ~ ka mangmuhnate | my visions of that night) (s:zani) (a:zingciang) (b:zan) (r:44.7.28/27.7.1) (q:draft)
Zanaan = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Zaanan) (d:town of Judah named by the prophet Micah among the towns that face judgment) (r:33.1.11)
zancip = (t:v) (w:be broken/be crushed) (d:said of Jerusalem brought to ruin, followed by gawp utterly) (e:Jerusalem khuapi ~ gawp hi) (r:26.26.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
zaneite = (t:n) (w:officials/officers) (d:za nei, hold a rank or title, with plural -te: those who hold office) (e:khuapi sung ~ khawmin/kumpipa’ zite, ama nuai-ah a ~ | the wives of the king and the officials under him/a kumpi inn-a ~ kipia hi | his palace officials surrendered/minamte sungah ~ | the officers over the tribes) (s:uliante) (r:14.29.20/12.24.15/12.24.12/13.28.1) (q:draft)
zaneu = (t:n) (w:low rank/lowest place) (d:za rank with neu small; a zaneu pen is the lowest in rank) (e:Pasian in a ~ penin hong koih) (a:zalian) (r:46.4.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
zang = (t:v) (w:use/employ) (d:make use of a thing, a name or a person for some purpose; zat is the form used before ding and nading) (e:tehna man ~ ding uh hi/leenggahzu tawm na ~ in | use a little wine/ciamsiatna-in ka min ~ uh hi | they use my name as a curse/Baalte’ adingin ~ uh hi | they used them for the Baals/Sumbukte in tawi tehna man lo ~ uh a | the merchants use dishonest scales) (r:26.45.10/26.16.15/54.5.23/19.102.8/14.24.7/28.12.7) (q:draft)
zang = (t:n) (w:middle) (d:the very middle, used after lai as lai zang) (e:puan a lai ~ pan a kikeek hi/amaute lai ~ pan paikhia-in | going out from the middle of them) (r:42.23.45/42.4.30) (q:draft, low confidence)
zanga = (t:num) (w:five hundred) (d:za, hundred, with nga, five) (e:ni ~/kum ~/Khat in dangka ~, khat in dangka sawmnga | one owed five hundred denarii, the other fifty/Simeon mi ~, Seir Mual-ah pai uh a | five hundred Simeonites went to Mount Seir) (r:42.7.41/1.5.30/13.4.42)
zangah = (t:prep) (w:in the middle of/among/in the midst of) (d:zang with the place marker ah, mostly as lai zangah) (e:amaute lai ~ ding a/gunkuang in tuili lai ~ a om hi | the boat was in the middle of the lake/thuhilhte lai ~ tu a | sitting among the teachers/inntual lai ~ mei cih uh a | they kindled a fire in the middle of the courtyard) (s:lakah) (b:zang) (r:42.24.36/41.6.47/42.2.46/42.22.55) (q:draft)
zangah = (t:prep) (w:on top of/on/upon) (d:zang flat open surface with the place marker ah: innkhum zangah is on the flat roof of a house, kulh zangah on top of the wall) (e:innkhum ~ tua mite paipih to-in/Israel kumpipa kulh ~ a pai lai takin | as the king of Israel was walking on the wall/na innkhum ~ tangban na khung ding hi | you shall make a parapet on your roof/ka ngawng ~ hong khih a | he bound it on my neck) (s:tungah) (r:6.2.6/12.6.26/5.22.8/25.1.14) (q:draft)
zangawp = (t:v) (w:waste away/be worn out) (d:said of a garment eaten by moths and of a person who wastes away) (e:puan bangin ka ~ hi) (r:18.13.28) (q:draft, low confidence)
zangawpte = (t:n) (w:those who are crushed/the worn out) (d:zangawp with the plural te; lungsim zangawpte is those crushed in spirit) (e:lungsim ~ a hon hi) (b:zangawp) (r:19.34.18) (q:draft, low confidence)
zangin = (t:v) (w:using/by means of/with) (d:verb zang, use, with the linking suffix in; min zangin is invoking a name) (e:Amaute in a namsau uh ~/thugentehna vive ~ thu hilh a | he taught using only parables/Topa in kamsang khat ~ Izipt panin Israelte paikhiatpih | using a prophet the Lord brought Israel out of Egypt/Na vangliatna leh na za liatna ~ | by your power and your high rank) (s:zatin) (b:zang) (r:35.1.17/18.22.8/40.13.34/28.12.13) (q:draft)
zangkha = (t:v) (w:get to use/enjoy) (d:zang use, with kha happen to, get to; in the verses always denied: not get to use) (e:a thau na ~ kei ding uh a/a hauhna khempeuh ~ man lo ding hi | he will not get to enjoy all his wealth) (r:33.6.15/18.20.18) (q:draft)
zangkhai = (t:adv) (w:lightly/in vain) (d:literally light, not heavy; before zat use or ngaihsut think it means to treat as unimportant, to misuse or make light of) (e:hong thuhilhna ~ ngaihsut kei inla/Topa na Pasian’ min na ~ zat kei ding | you shall not misuse the name of the Lord your God/ama' min a ~ ngaihsut mi | one who treats his name lightly) (r:58.12.5/5.5.11/2.20.7) (q:draft)
zangkhawm = (t:v) (w:share/use together/have in common) (d:zang, use, with khawm, together) (e:neihsa khempeuh gawmin a ~ uh hi/amah a hilh pa tawh ~ tahen | let him share with the one who teaches him/tuiphumna khat bek mah a ~ ihi hi | we share one baptism only) (s:neikhawm) (b:zang) (r:44.2.44/48.6.6/49.4.5) (q:draft)
zangkhia = (t:v) (w:use up/spend) (d:zang use, with khia out) (e:a ngah zahzah ~ pah hi) (s:zangkhin/zangmang/zatmang) (b:zang) (r:20.21.20) (q:draft)
zangkhin = (t:v) (w:use up/spend all) (d:zang use with khin, completely) (e:a sum neih khempeuh ~ napi-in) (s:zangkhia/zangmang/zatmang) (b:zang) (r:41.5.26) (q:draft)
zangkik = (t:v) (w:use again/take up again) (d:zang use with kik again) (e:kikhihna ~ nawn kei un) (b:zang) (r:48.5.1) (q:draft)
zangkuam = (t:n) (w:valley) (d:zang plain with kuam valley; leihoih zangkuam is a fertile valley) (e:kisaktheihna leihoih ~ i lutunga kisuang) (s:kuam/mualkuam) (r:23.28.1/23.28.3) (q:draft)
zanglei = (t:n) (w:plain/lowland/flat land) (d:zang, flat, with lei, ground: a stretch of level land, a plain or lowland, as the plain of the Jordan and the plains of Moab) (e:Jordan ~ sung Sukkoth leh Zeredah/Shinar gamsungah ~ mun khat mu uh a | they found a plain in the land of Shinar/Jerikho ~ lamah Topa mai-ah pai uh hi | they went before the Lord toward the plains of Jericho/Moab ~-ah Moses in a hawm gamhte | the inheritances Moses gave out in the plains of Moab) (r:14.4.17/6.13.32/1.11.2/6.4.13) (q:draft)
Zanglei = (t:n) (w:plain) (d:zanglei, plain or lowland, capitalised as the name of a region, the Plain of the Jordan valley and the coastal plain of Philistia) (e:Negeb gam, leh ~ zong/Filistia ~-a om lai mi khempeuh | all who remain on the Philistine plain) (b:zanglei) (r:5.34.3/26.25.16) (q:draft)
zangleite = (t:n) (w:plains/lowlands/plateau) (d:zanglei plain, with plural te) (e:mualkuam leh ~ a kisia ding uh hi) (b:zanglei) (r:24.48.8) (q:draft)
zanglo = (t:v) (w:not use) (d:zang use with the negative lo, written as one word; thutang zanglo is not deal justly) (e:Vanglianpa in thuman a ~ sa na hi hiam/Samaria mite’ na zatte ~ uh ahih manin | because they do not use the things of Samaritans/Pasian in thutang a ~ sa na hi hiam | do you think God does not deal justly) (b:zang) (r:18.8.3/43.4.9) (q:draft)
zangmang = (t:v) (w:squander/use up/waste) (d:zang, use, with mang, away or lost: use up until it is gone; in Mark 12:40 of consuming the property of widows) (e:numei paktatte tungah ~ khin a/a neihsate laksakin ~ uh a | they take their property and use it up) (s:zatmang/zangkhin/zangkhia) (r:42.15.30/41.12.40) (q:draft)
zangmul = (t:n) (w:mane) (d:the long hair on the neck of a horse; mul is hair) (e:Sakol ~ a posakpa in) (s:zaangmul) (r:18.39.19) (q:draft)
zangnuam = (t:v) (w:want to use/wish to devote) (d:zang use with nuam want) (e:Topa a dingin ~ uh ahih manin) (r:46.7.34) (q:draft)
zangpa = (t:n) (w:user/one who uses) (d:zang, use, with pa, the male one who does it: a zangpa is the one who uses or wields it) (e:Mihai khat kamtai-a a ~ in/amah a ~’ tungah kisial thei ding ahi hiam | can it boast against the one who uses it) (b:zang) (r:20.26.6/23.10.15) (q:draft)
zangpah = (t:v) (w:use at once/put to use immediately) (d:zang use with pah at once) (e:sum bawlna-in ~ a) (r:40.25.16) (q:draft)
zangpi = (t:see) <zangpi-in>
zangpi-in = (t:adv) (w:all together/as a whole) (d:used after khua town: khua zangpi-in is the whole town, all the people of the town) (e:khua ~ kongkhak kiangah a kikhawm uh hi/khua ~ kising hehu uh a | the whole city was stirred) (r:41.1.33/40.21.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
zangsak = (t:v) (w:lighten/make lighter/ease) (d:zang, light in weight, with the causative sak: make a load, a yoke or a punishment less heavy) (e:teembaw a ~ uh hi/kote tungah hong koih hakkol ~ in | lighten the yoke put on us/kote’ adingin hong ~ in | make it lighter for us/hong gawtna hong ~ kha ding hi | perhaps he will lighten his punishment on you) (a:giksak) (r:44.27.38/14.10.10/11.12.9/9.6.5) (q:draft)
zangsak = (t:v) (w:let use/let enjoy/cause to be used) (d:zang, use, with the causative sak: let someone use or enjoy something, or make a thing serve as something) (e:sun teng nuamtak hong ~ in/tua nate nuamtakin ~ loin | not letting him enjoy those things/leitung gam khempeuhte’ kihaamsiatna-in ka ~ ding hi | I will make it a curse for all the nations of the earth) (b:zang) (r:18.10.20/21.6.2/24.26.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
zangsawm = (t:adj) (w:ten-stringed) (d:of a harp or lyre with ten strings; sawm is ten) (e:harp ~ khausai lasakna nang kong tum/~ khausai lasakna le harp lasakna | the ten-stringed instrument and the harp) (r:19.144.9/19.92.1) (q:draft)
zangsial = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:wild ox) (d:a wild ox, named as a picture of strength; sial is the mithun) (e:nangmah in ~ bangin kei nong hatsak) (s:gamsial) (r:19.92.10) (q:draft)
zangsung = (t:n) (w:field/open country) (d:zang plain or level land with sung inside; zangsung sa is the creatures of the field) (e:~ sa khempeuh in kivakna-in nei uh hi) (r:19.80.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
zangte = (t:n) (w:those who use/users) (d:zang use with plural te, after a; a zangte is the people who use something) (e:hih leitung a ~ in a zang lo/Sumgolh a ~ in ai bangin ngaihsun uh a | those who use a bribe think of it as a charm/tawikhaina man a ~ tungah lungkim hi | he is pleased with those who use accurate scales/Tawisuang nam nih a ~, Topa in mudah a | the Lord detests those who use two kinds of weights) (b:zang) (r:46.7.31/20.11.1/20.17.8/20.20.23) (q:draft)
zangteep = (t:n) (w:foreskin) (d:the foreskin, cut off in circumcision; zangvun is the same) (e:Filistia-te’ ~ zakhat cih simloh) (s:vundawn/zangvun) (r:9.18.25) (q:draft)
zangthei = (t:v) (w:can use/be able to use) (d:zang, use, with thei, can) (e:a ut bangin ~ nawn loin/a kilawm ciang ah ~ lehang | if we use it properly) (b:zang) (r:46.7.4/54.1.8) (q:draft)
zangvun = (t:n) (w:foreskin) (d:with vun skin; here in zangvun teepte, foreskins) (e:amaute’ ~ teepte David in hong paipih hi) (s:vundawn/zangteep) (r:9.18.27) (q:draft)
zangzaw = (t:adj) (w:lighter) (d:zang, light in weight, with zaw, more; after sangin, than) (e:a kigawmin husan’ sangin ~ hi) (a:gikzaw) (r:19.62.9) (q:draft)
zangzaw = (t:v) (w:use rather/use instead) (d:zang, use, with zaw, rather: use it for this and not for that) (e:itna tawh khatlekhat kikhualna-in ~ un) (b:zang) (r:48.5.13) (q:draft)
zanhak = (t:v) (w:stay awake at night/keep awake) (d:zan night with hak be awake) (e:zan khuavak-in ka ~ hi) (r:19.119.148) (q:draft)
zanhal = (t:adv) (w:the other day/a few days ago) (d:on a day not long past) (e:~ a kei kiangah hong pai mipa) (r:7.13.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
zani = (t:adv) (w:yesterday) (d:the day before today; zani, tuni is yesterday and today) (e:Khrih pen ~, tuni, a tawntungin) (s:zana) (a:zingciang) (r:58.13.8) (q:draft)
zanih = (t:num) (w:two hundred) (d:za, hundred, with nih, two) (e:a kiseek lumpi ~ bawl hi/a gim lua mi ~ kinusia uh hi | two hundred men who were too tired were left behind/tuu tul ~ leh tul sawmnga | two hundred and fifty thousand sheep/mihing ~ leh sawmnga ahi uh hi | they were two hundred and fifty men) (r:14.9.15/4.4.44/9.30.10/13.5.21/14.8.10) (q:draft)
zanihte = (t:num) (w:two hundred) (d:zanih, two hundred, with the plural te, of people: mi zanihte is the two hundred men) (e:A kisam mi ~ Jerusalem panin/Besor lui-ah a kinusia mihing ~ kiangah David pai hi | David came to the two hundred men left at the Besor/mihing ~ van tawh om uh hi | two hundred men stayed with the supplies) (b:zanih) (r:10.15.11/9.30.21/9.25.13) (q:draft)
zanin = (t:adv) (w:at night/during the night) (d:zan, night, with the marker in) (e:~ hih numei’ tapa si hi/amau tuu honte ~ a cing uh hi | they kept watch over their flocks at night/amaute ding-in tua ~ paikhia uh hi | they got up and left that night/~ thungenin gim het loin ka khut ka zan | at night I prayed and stretched out untiring hands) (b:zan) (r:11.3.19/42.2.8/9.28.25/19.77.2) (q:draft)
zanin = (t:v) (w:stretch out/reach out) (d:the verb zan, stretch out, with the linking ending in; said of the hand) (e:a khut ~ la hi/na khut ~ ama neihsa khempeuh suksak lecin | if you stretch out your hand and strike all he has/amah in a khut ~ a vakhu man a | he reached out his hand and took the dove/Israel in a taklam khut ~ | Israel reached out his right hand/tuipi tungah na khut ~ tuipi khenkham in | stretch out your hand over the sea and divide it) (r:12.6.7/18.1.11/1.8.9/1.48.14/2.14.16) (q:draft)
zaninah = (t:adv) (w:on the night/at night) (d:zanin at night, with the place and time marker ah; after a day count, on the night of that day) (e:Ni sawm-le-li ni ~ Andria tuipi sungah) (b:zanin) (r:44.27.27) (q:draft)
zankhang = (t:n) (w:late night/dead of night) (d:used paired with zankim midnight: zankim zankhang dongin is far into the night) (e:zankim ~ dongin a meivak mit lo) (r:20.31.18) (q:draft, low confidence)
zankhia = (t:v) (w:stretch out/reach out) (d:zan stretch out a hand or arm, with khia out; lift a finger against someone) (e:ka khutmeno khat zong ka ~ kei ding) (a:dokkik) (r:10.18.12) (q:draft)
zankhiat = (t:v) (w:stretch out/reach out) (d:form of zankhia used before a noun: a zankhiat a khut is the hand he stretched out) (e:amah langpangin a ~ a khut keu cip) (b:zankhia) (r:11.13.4) (q:draft)
zankhua = (t:see) <zankhua-in>
zankhua-in = (t:adv) (w:all night/the whole night) (d:zan night with khua, and the marker in) (e:kote in ~ ka hahkat uh hangin) (s:zanthapai/zankhuavak) (r:42.5.5) (q:draft)
zankhuavak = (t:adv) (w:all night/through the night) (d:zan night with khuavak daylight: the whole night until it is light) (e:ka vilna munnah ~ ka om hi) (s:zanthapai/zankhua-in) (r:23.21.8/21.10.16) (q:draft)
zankim = (t:n) (w:midnight) (d:zan, night, with kim, half: the middle of the night; zankim lai takin is right at midnight) (e:~ lai takin ka tho hi/~ dongin thu a hilh hi | he taught until midnight/~ ciang dong Samson lum a | Samson lay until midnight/~ lai takin Topa in vat gawp hi | at midnight the Lord struck them down) (a:sunkim) (r:19.119.62/2.12.29/44.20.7/7.16.3)
zankimpi = (t:see) <zankimpi-in>
zankimpi-in = (t:adv) (w:in the middle of the night/at midnight) (d:zan kim midnight with pi and the marker in) (e:a nu ~ samkhia a) (r:40.2.14) (q:draft)
zanna = (t:n) (w:stretching out/holding out) (d:zan stretch out, hold out, with the noun suffix na; teipi a zanna a khut is the hand with which he held out the spear) (e:amah in teipi a ~ a khut dokkik lo) (r:6.8.26) (q:draft)
Zannes = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Jannes) (d:one of the Egyptian magicians who opposed Moses, named together with Jambres) (r:55.3.8)
zanni = (t:n) (w:yesterday) (d:the day before today; with in, zanni-in, it tells when something happened) (e:Khazih in ~, tuni, atawntungin kikheel loin/Jessi’ tapa ~ hita leh, tuni hita leh | the son of Jesse, whether yesterday or today/a bei ciangin ~ ahi a | once it is past it is as yesterday/~-in nai sawm leh nai khat lai takin | yesterday at the eleventh hour) (r:58.13.8/43.4.52/9.20.27/19.90.4) (q:draft)
Zanoah = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Zanoah) (d:name of two towns of Judah, one in the western foothills and one in the hill country) (r:6.15.34/6.15.56)
zanpah = (t:v) (w:stretch out at once) (d:zan, stretch out, with pah, at once: stretch out the hand immediately) (e:A mipa in zong a khut ~ a) (r:40.12.13) (q:draft)
zanpi = (t:n) (w:night/dead of night) (d:zan, night, with pi, great: zanpi mahin is in the night itself, while it was still night) (e:a nu tawh ~ mahin ding khia/a ~ mahin kuam lamah pai-in | I went toward the valley while it was still night) (a:sun/suntangpi) (b:zan) (r:40.2.14/16.2.15) (q:draft)
zansak = (t:v) (w:make stretch out/cause to hold out) (d:zan stretch out the hand, with causative sak) (e:Ethiopia gam a khut ~ mengmeng in) (r:19.68.31) (q:draft)
zantaamsak = (t:v) (w:keep overnight) (d:zan night, taam stay and sak cause: let something stay with one through the night) (e:hong khap puan na ~ kei ding uh a) (r:5.24.12) (q:draft)
zanthapai = (t:adv) (w:all night/the whole night) (d:through the whole night, often followed by in) (e:tu ~ ngasa ka khuh uh hangin/~-in lungkhamna bek keima tanh ahi hi | nights of misery are my lot/~-in ki-itna bawlin | making love all night long/~-in dahna lim puanhampi silh un | wear sackcloth all night in mourning) (s:zankhuavak/zankhua-in) (r:42.5.5/20.7.18/18.7.3/29.1.13) (q:draft)
zantuam = (t:v) (w:become lighter/be lightened) (d:said of a ship whose cargo is thrown out) (e:Teembaw a ~ nadingin) (r:32.1.5) (q:draft)
zanuam = (t:v) (w:want to hear/like to hear) (d:za hear with nuam want or like) (e:a thugen ~ veve hi/Pasian’ thu ~ ahih manin | because he wanted to hear the word of God/hih mipa’ thugen ~ ing | I would like to hear this man speak/nangma ngaihsutna taktak ka ~ uh hi | we want to hear what you really think/note’ zakte ~ mahmah napi-in za lo uh hi | they longed to hear what you hear but did not hear it) (s:zaknop) (r:41.6.20/44.25.22/44.13.7/44.28.22/40.13.17) (q:draft)
zanuamin = (t:v) (w:wanting to hear) (d:zanuam want to hear, with the linking ending in) (e:Pasian’ thu ~ Jesuh hong nehcip uh hi) (b:zanuam) (r:42.5.1) (q:draft)
zap = (t:v) (w:flap/flutter/beat) (d:move the wings up and down: kha a zap, flap the wings) (e:a note tungah a kha a ~/a kha a ~, a kam a ka | flapped a wing or opened its mouth/bangzah takin nawh ~ thei ahi hiam | how fast they can flap them) (r:5.32.11/23.10.14/18.39.13) (q:draft)
zap = (t:v) (w:winnow/fan) (d:blow or fan away chaff; buhphual zap siang, clear the threshing floor by winnowing) (e:ama buhphual ~ siang ding a/khualkhal hun-a ansi ~ bangin a lengmang hi | it blew away like chaff winnowed in summer/A ~ siang ding mi Babilon-ah ka sawl | I will send winnowers to Babylon/a khutah anzapna tawi-in a ante ~ a | with the winnowing fork in his hand he winnows his grain) (s:zapsiang/haih) (r:40.3.12/27.2.35/24.51.2) (q:draft)
zapa = (t:n) (w:hearer/one who hears) (d:za hear with pa, the male one who does it; thungetna a zapa is the one who hears prayer) (e:Thungetna a ~ na hi a) (b:za) (r:19.65.2) (q:draft)
Zaphon = (t:name) (c:mountain) (w:Zaphon) (d:mountain in the far north, to whose heights Mount Zion is compared) (r:19.48.2)
zapi = (t:adj) (w:wide/spacious/vast) (d:of rooms and of a realm: very wide, of great extent) (e:Amah in gam ~ tak uk ding a/Inn dei tungnung ~ a awng inn gol khat | a great house with spacious upper rooms) (s:zai/zaipi/tanzau) (a:kawcik) (r:27.11.3/24.22.14) (q:draft)
zapin = (t:v) (w:fanning/blowing) (d:zap fan, with the linking ending in; pum zap is work the bellows to blow a fire) (e:pum ~ ama kizatna ding ciatin) (s:zaap-in) (b:zap) (r:23.54.16) (q:draft)
zapna = (t:n) (w:flapping/beating) (d:zap flap, with the noun suffix na; kha zapna is the beating of wings) (e:huih lakah a kha ~ leh leengpei gingte) (s:khazapna) (b:zap) (r:26.3.13) (q:draft)
zapsiang = (t:v) (w:winnow/fan clean/clear) (d:clean grain or a threshing floor by fanning away the chaff) (e:tua gam a ~ ding uh hi/Ama buh phual a ~ nadingin | to clear his threshing floor/an vaite ~ dinga a nung huih | a wind blowing to winnow the chaff) (s:haih/zap) (b:zap) (r:24.51.2/42.3.17/24.4.11) (q:draft)
zaptel = (t:adj) (w:swift/fast/quick) (d:able to move very fast, said of horses, runners and pursuers) (e:muvanlai sangin ~ zaw uh a/Sakol ~ tungah i tuang ding hi | we will ride on swift horses/note hong delh mite zong ~ ding hi | those who pursue you will also be swift/No a ~ kamtaite aw | you swift messengers) (s:taihat) (r:10.1.23/23.30.16/23.18.1) (q:draft)
zaptelsak = (t:v) (w:make swift/make nimble) (d:zaptel swift, with causative sak) (e:sakhi khe bangin ka khe hong ~ a) (b:zaptel) (r:35.3.19) (q:draft)
zaptelte = (t:n) (w:swift ones/swift horses) (d:zaptel swift, with plural te; sakol zaptelte is swift horses) (e:a kisapna munah sakolte leh sakol ~) (b:zaptel) (r:11.4.28) (q:draft)
zaptelzaw = (t:adj) (w:swifter/faster) (d:zaptel swift, with zaw more) (e:muvanlai sangin ~ uh) (b:zaptel) (r:10.1.23) (q:draft)
Zarah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zerah) (d:son of Judah and Tamar, twin brother of Perez) (r:1.46.12)
Zarefat = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Zarephath) (d:Phoenician town on the coast near Sidon, named in Obadiah as the northern limit of the land) (e:Kanaan gam ~ ciang dong) (r:31.1.20) (q:draft)
Zarefath = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Zarephath) (d:town belonging to Sidon, where Elijah stayed with a widow) (r:11.17.9/11.17.10)
Zarephat = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Zarephath) (d:town in the region of Sidon, where Elijah was sent to a widow) (r:42.4.26)
Zarethan = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Zarethan) (d:town in the Jordan valley, near Adam and Sukkoth) (r:11.4.12/11.7.46)
zasa = (t:v) (w:have heard/heard) (d:za hear, with sa marking what is already done) (e:nangma minthan’na a ~ minamte in) (s:zaksa/zakhin/zazo) (b:za) (r:4.14.15) (q:draft)
zasagih = (t:num) (w:seven hundred) (e:ni ~/kum ~/zi ~, leh zineu zathum nei hi | he had seven hundred wives and three hundred concubines/namsau tawi mihing ~ la hi | he took seven hundred swordsmen) (r:11.11.3/7.20.16/12.3.26)
zasak = (t:v) (w:inform/announce/proclaim/report) (d:za, hear, with causative sak: cause to hear, make known; thu zasak is to report or announce a matter) (e:an tan’ ding thu ~ uh a/Khlo-e te innkuanpih kimkhat in hong ~ uh hi | some of Chloe’s household have informed me/tuate hong pian’ ma-in note tungah kong ~ khol hi | before they happened I announced them to you/kulh kongpi cingte in thu ~ uh a | the gatekeepers reported the news) (s:zaksak/zahsak/theihsak) (b:za) (r:11.21.12/42.2.10/46.1.11/23.48.5/12.7.11) (q:draft)
zasakin = (t:v) (w:report/announce/inform) (d:zasak, make known, with the linking ending in, which joins it to the following verb: thu zasakin is reporting the matter, letting someone hear it) (e:Tua ciangin galvilpa in thu ~/a thu ~, man mah hi, cisak un | let them hear it and say, It is true) (b:zasak) (r:12.9.18/23.43.9) (q:draft)
zasakkhol = (t:v) (w:announce beforehand/tell in advance) (d:za hear, sak cause and khol beforehand: let someone hear ahead of time) (e:note tungah kong ~ hi) (s:genkhol) (r:23.48.5) (q:draft)
zasakkik = (t:v) (w:report back/let hear again) (d:zasak cause to hear, inform, with kik back or again) (e:kiangah thu hong ~ a/kei kiangah thu hong ~ in | bring word back to me/kumpipa in na deihna hong ~ in | let the king send us back his decision/kote’ Pasian’ aw hong ~ kei in | do not let us hear the voice of our God again) (b:zasak) (r:26.9.11/5.18.16/1.37.14/15.5.17) (q:draft)
zasakkikin = (t:v) (w:reporting back/report) (d:zasakkik report back, with in linking it to the words that follow) (e:Galvil pa in thu ~/amaute in eite kiangah thu hong ~ | they brought word back to us) (b:zasakkik) (r:12.9.20/5.1.25) (q:draft)
zasan = (t:n) (w:red paint/vermilion) (d:red colour smeared on a house; san is red) (e:~ a zut mi in gimna thuak ta hen) (r:24.22.14) (q:draft)
zasate = (t:n) (w:those who have heard) (d:zasa have heard, with plural te) (e:ama pilna a ~ hong pai uh hi) (b:zasa) (r:11.4.34) (q:draft)
zasawm = (t:num) (w:ten hundred/one thousand) (d:za hundred with sawm ten; tul zasawm, thousand times ten hundred, stands for a countless host) (e:mihing tul ~ a ding uh hi) (r:27.7.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
zasim = (t:v) (w:overhear/hear secretly) (d:za hear with sim secretly) (e:a hong ~ kuamah a om kei uh hi) (s:ngaisim) (r:24.38.27) (q:draft)
zasimin = (t:v) (w:listening in/overhearing) (d:zasim hear secretly, with the linking ending in) (e:Pasian’ vaihawmnate a ~ kingaihsun na hi hiam) (b:zasim) (r:18.15.8) (q:draft)
zat = (t:v) (w:use) (d:form of zang, use, taken before ding, nading and similar words) (e:nasepna ah ~ ding kham tawh kibawl/Kikhopna buk nasepna ah ~ dingin | to be used in the work of the tent of meeting/keima kiangah na ~ theih keima sum | money of mine that you could have used/Zatui tampi na ~ khit uh hangin | though you have used many medicines) (r:13.28.14/43.13.29/4.7.5/41.7.11/24.46.11) (q:draft)
zate = (t:n) (w:hearers/those who heard) (d:za, hear, with plural te: a zate is those who heard) (e:Tua thu a ~ in/Tuucingte’ thugenna ~ khempeuh in lamdang a sa uh hi | all who heard what the shepherds said were amazed/Ka thu hong ~ kiangah | to those who heard what I said/Thukham a ~ in | those who hear the law) (s:thungaite) (b:za) (r:42.18.26/44.5.11/42.2.18/43.18.21/45.2.13) (q:draft)
zathei = (t:v) (w:be able to hear/can hear) (d:za hear with thei can) (e:bilngongte in khua ~ kik a) (b:za) (r:42.7.22) (q:draft)
zathum = (t:num) (w:three hundred) (e:ni ~/kum ~/teembaw a sauna tong ~ | the length of the ark three hundred cubits/mihing ~ leh sawmguk that uh hi | they killed three hundred and sixty men) (r:1.5.22/10.2.31/1.6.15)
zathumte = (t:num) (w:the three hundred/three hundred) (d:zathum with te, for a group of three hundred people already counted or known) (e:mihing ~ pawl thumin khenin/amah tawh a om mi ~ | the three hundred men who were with him/Tui a liak mi ~ tawh | with the three hundred men who lapped the water) (b:zathum) (r:7.7.16/7.8.4/7.7.7) (q:draft)
zatin = (t:v) (w:using/spending) (d:zat use, with in linking it to the next verb; uang zatin is using lavishly) (e:Sumbawm panin khamte uang ~) (b:zat) (r:23.46.6) (q:draft)
zatkhak = (t:v) (w:happen to use/have to use) (d:zat use with khak, as it turns out) (e:note tungah khauhtakin ka hong ~ loh nadingin) (r:47.13.10) (q:draft)
zatmang = (t:v) (w:spend all/squander/use up) (d:zat use with mang, away until it is gone) (e:A sum neih khempeuh a ~ khit ciangin) (s:phengzat/lawnmang) (a:khol) (r:42.15.14) (q:draft)
zatna = (t:n) (w:use/using/way of using) (d:zat, use, with the noun suffix na: the using of something, or the way it is used) (e:Tua nate khempeuh ~ hangin muat nading/Peengkul ~ in na khang tawntungun | the use of the trumpets throughout your generations/Ashdod kampau a ~ | their use of the language of Ashdod/ka vangliatna ka ~ dan | the way I use my power) (s:kizatna/zatzia) (b:zat) (r:51.2.22/4.10.8/16.13.24/26.39.21) (q:draft)
zatnate = (t:n) (w:uses/practices) (d:zatna, use, with the plural te: kam kihhuai zatnate is the use of filthy language, tawitehna man lo zatnate the use of false measures) (e:kam kihhuai ~ ahi zongin/ka deih loh tawitehna man lo ~ | the use of false measures, which I hate) (b:zatna) (r:51.3.8/33.6.10) (q:draft)
zatnop = (t:v) (w:want to use) (d:zat use with nop want) (e:kong ~ manin kumpi a hong suaksak) (r:45.9.17) (q:draft)
zato = (t:n) (w:physician/doctor) (d:one who heals the sick; often zato siam or zato mangpa) (e:Cidamte in ~ deih lo uh hi/kuamah a damsak zolo ~ siam-a kineite | those who pose as skilled physicians but can heal no one/Itna a ngah ~ mangpa Luka | Luke, the beloved physician/~ tampi khut tungah gimna tampi thuak a | she had suffered much at the hands of many doctors) (s:siavuan/siavuanpa) (r:42.5.31/51.4.14/18.13.4/41.5.26) (q:draft)
Zatopa = (t:name) (w:Zatopa/Physician) (d:zato, physician, with pa, used as a form of address in the proverb Physician, heal yourself) (r:42.4.23)
zatote = (t:n) (w:physicians/doctors) (d:zato, physician, with the plural te) (e:a neihsa tengin ~ a guaih hangin) (s:siavuante) (b:zato) (r:42.8.43) (q:draft)
zatpen = (t:n) (w:agent/one most used) (d:zat use with pen most: the one a person makes most use of; kumpipa zatpen is the king’s agent) (e:khempeuh ah kumpipa ~ ahi hi) (b:zat) (r:16.11.24) (q:draft, low confidence)
zatsak = (t:v) (w:put to use/make use of) (d:zat use with sak cause) (e:a hoihlamin hong ~ ahih manin) (b:zat) (r:47.7.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
zatsiamte = (t:n) (w:good stewards/those who use well) (d:zat use, siam skilled and the plural te) (e:Pasian’ piak na a ~ bangin) (r:60.4.10) (q:draft)
zattawm = (t:v) (w:use for oneself) (d:zat, use, with tawm, by or for oneself; zattawm dingin koih is keep for one’s own use, said of the chariots and horses Solomon kept) (e:~ dingin koih hi) (r:11.10.26) (q:draft, low confidence)
zatte = (t:n) (w:things used/tools/utensils) (d:zat, use, with the plural te, the things that are used; na zatte, also written na-zatte, is tools or furnishings) (e:sik tawh a kibawl na ~/Samaria mite’ na ~ zanglo uh ahih manin | because they do not use the things Samaritans use/A kham ~ Parvaim kham ahi hi | the gold he used was gold of Parvaim/a ~ uh hihte sungah silsiang ding uh a | they were to rinse in these the things they used) (s:nazatte) (b:zat) (r:5.27.5/14.4.6/43.4.9/14.3.6) (q:draft)
zattheih = (t:v) (w:can be used/be usable/be able to use) (d:zat use with theih can, mostly before ding or nading: so that it can be used, fit for use) (e:~ ding hi nawn lo hi/ut bangin ka ~ ding hi lo ahi hiam | may I not use it as I wish/a hoihin a hong ~ nadingin | so that he can use you for good/aana a ~ nadingin thu kipia hi | it was allowed to exercise authority) (b:zat) (r:24.13.7/45.6.13/40.20.15/66.13.5) (q:draft)
Zattu = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zattu) (d:head of a family whose descendants returned from the exile with Zerubbabel; also a leader who sealed the covenant under Nehemiah) (r:15.8.5/16.10.14)
zatui = (t:n) (w:medicine/balm/ointment) (d:a healing substance such as medicine, balm or ointment; zatui siam is a physician and zatui tawh bawl is to embalm a body) (e:Gilead-ah ~ om lo ahi hiam/damna ~ va la un | go and get healing balm/~ tawh amah a muat loh nadingin bawl uh a | they embalmed him so that he would not decay/A liammate adingin ~ la un | get balm for her wounds) (r:24.8.22/1.50.2/24.46.11/1.50.26/24.51.8) (q:draft)
zatval = (t:n) (w:surplus/excess) (d:zat use with val over: what is left over beyond what one uses) (e:adangte in a ~ uh sumte a khia uh) (s:neihval/lamval) (r:42.21.4) (q:draft)
zatzia = (t:n) (w:usage/way of using) (d:zat use with zia manner; kam zatzia is the use of words) (e:hih thu pen kam ~, min le) (s:zatna/kizatna) (r:44.18.15) (q:draft)
zau = (t:v) (w:spread out/spread wide) (d:of branches, spread wide; vak zau is wander about everywhere) (e:a hiang ~ a) (r:26.31.7/20.5.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
zausak = (t:v) (w:make spread out/make abundant) (d:zau spread wide, with causative sak, said of branches) (e:a hiang ka ~ a) (b:zau) (r:26.31.9) (q:draft)
zauvak = (t:v) (w:wander off/go astray) (d:zau spread about with vak walk about: wander each his own way) (e:amau’ tum ciatah ~ uh hi) (r:23.47.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
zavei = (t:adv) (w:a hundred times) (d:za hundred with vei time) (e:Mawhnei khat in ~ dong siatna bawl napi-in/~ a kisatna sangin | than being beaten a hundred times) (s:zakhatin) (r:21.8.12/20.17.10) (q:draft)
zaw = (t:prep) (w:than/more) (d:marks the comparative, more or rather; it follows the describing word, and the thing compared stands before it with sangin) (e:Topa ka ngaklah ~ hi/a si khinsa mite hampha ka sa ~ hi | I consider the dead more fortunate/pilna in mi khat hatsak ~ hi | wisdom makes one person stronger/mihaite’ adingin lametna om ~ lai hi | there is more hope for fools) (r:19.130.6/21.4.2/21.7.19/20.26.12)
zaw = (t:adj) (w:weak) (d:without strength, limp or feeble, said mostly of the hands and of bodily strength) (e:A ~ khutte khauhsak un | strengthen the feeble hands/a gil kialin a tha ~ a | he gets hungry and his strength fails/Mi khempeuh’ khut ~ dakdakin | every hand will go limp/pate in a khut uh ~ lua ta ahih manin | because the fathers’ hands have become too weak) (s:thanem/thazawng) (a:hat/thahat/khauh) (r:23.35.3/23.44.12/26.7.17/24.47.3)
zawcipsak = (t:v) (w:make bent/make weak for good) (d:zaw, weak, with cip, firmly or for good, and causative sak: make limp or bent for good, said of the back or loins) (e:a kawngte uh ~ in) (s:kulsak) (r:19.69.23) (q:draft, low confidence)
