zawdeuhte = (t:n) (w:those who are more) (d:zawdeuh rather more, with the plural te, after a descriptive word: khangham zawdeuhte is the more senior ones) (e:siampi khangham ~ puanhampi silhsakin) (s:zawdiakte/deuhte) (b:zawdeuh) (r:12.19.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
zawdiakte = (t:n) (w:those who are more) (d:zaw more with diak especially and plural te; khangham zawdiakte is those who are older, the elders) (e:no a khangham ~ aw) (s:zawdeuhte/deuhte) (r:29.1.2) (q:draft)
zawh = (t:v) (w:rule over/win/overcome/defeat) (d:form of zo, win or overcome, used before ding, uh ciangin and similar words) (e:Ahih hangin nang in tua mawhna na ~ ding ahi hi/note in amaute na ~ uh ciangin | when you have defeated them/dawite na ~ uh hangin lungdam kei un | do not rejoice that you overcome the spirits/thu ka ~ ding ka tel theih hi | I know that I will win my case) (s:gualzawh/gualzo) (a:guallel/guallelh) (r:1.4.7/5.7.2/42.10.20/18.13.18)
zawhgawp = (t:v) (w:overpower/conquer/defeat completely) (d:zawh overcome with gawp marking forceful or thorough action) (e:amah simin a ~ khit ciangin/Pasian’ mite simin a ~ theih nading | to make war on God’s people and conquer them/ama galte khempeuh a ~ khit ciangin | after he has overpowered all his enemies/Minam dangte a ~ nading namsau hiam khat | a sharp sword with which to strike down the nations) (s:galzawh) (b:zawh) (r:42.11.22/66.13.7/46.15.24/66.19.15) (q:draft)
zawhin = (t:v) (w:having finished/being able to) (d:zawh, the form of zo, be able, overcome or finish, with the linking suffix in; a teek zawhin is after he had grown old, hehnep zawhin om lo is could not be comforted) (e:a teek ~ Abraham tawh tapa khat/amah hehnep ~ om lo a | he could not be comforted/a teek ~ a neih sanggam pasal moilai khat | a young brother born to him in his old age) (b:zawh) (r:1.21.2/1.37.35/1.44.20) (q:draft, low confidence)
zawhkhit = (t:v) (w:finish/complete) (d:zawh finish with khit done; a zawhkhit ciangin is when it has been finished) (e:teci panna a ~ uh ciangin) (s:mankhit/zosiang) (r:66.11.7) (q:draft)
zawhleh = (t:conj) (w:if possible/if able) (d:zawh be able with leh if; ahih zawhleh is if it can be) (e:ahih ~, a teelsa mite nangawn) (r:41.13.22) (q:draft)
zawhloh = (t:adj) (w:unable/that cannot be done) (d:zawh be able with loh not, after a verb; sim zawhloh is too many to count) (e:sim ~ thukham tampi gelh ta leng) (s:theiloh) (r:28.8.12) (q:draft)
zawhna = (t:n) (w:victory/conquest) (d:the act of overcoming or of being able to do something) (e:na ~ koi lai-ah om hiam/Eite upna in leitung ~ ahi hi | our faith is the victory over the world/Na ~-ah eite lungdamin awng-in | may we shout for joy over your victory/na lak ~ uhah na lungdam uh a | you rejoice in your conquest) (s:gualzawhna/galzawhna) (a:guallelhna/lelhna) (b:zawh) (r:46.15.55/19.18.50/62.5.4/19.20.5/30.6.13) (q:draft)
zawhnop = (t:adj) (w:easy to overcome) (d:zawh overcome with nop easy) (e:Mi khat bek hileh ~ kisa a) (r:21.4.12) (q:draft)
zawhpih = (t:v) (w:help finish/help complete) (d:zawh finish, with pih do together with or for someone) (e:note lakah hong ~ vet dingin) (b:zawh) (r:47.8.6) (q:draft)
zawhpih = (t:v) (w:help conquer/help subdue) (d:zawh win, overcome, with pih do together with someone) (e:tua gam hong ~ leh) (b:zawh) (r:4.32.29) (q:draft)
zawhsa = (t:adj) (w:conquered/subdued) (d:zawh, overcome, with sa for a completed state: already conquered) (e:a omlai minamte pen ka ~ minamte tawh/Ka ~ kumpite’ sumkholna panin | from the treasuries of the kings I had conquered/amaute mai-ah gam ~-in om hi | the land lay subdued before them) (b:zawh) (r:6.23.4/21.2.8/6.18.1) (q:draft)
zawhsa = (t:adj) (w:finished/completed) (d:zawh, finish, with sa for a completed state: already completed) (e:lamin a ~ ahi hi) (s:kiman) (b:zawh) (r:15.5.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
zawhsak = (t:v) (w:subdue/make subject) (d:zawh, overcome, with sak: cause to be overcome, or overcome on behalf of someone) (e:galte ka ~ pak ding a/minamte i khe nuai-ah amah in hong ~ hi | he subdued nations under our feet/ka nuai-ah mite hong ~ Pasian | the God who subdues peoples under me/ama mai-ah minam dangte a ~ dingin | to subdue nations before him) (s:nuaisiah/ukcip) (b:zawh) (r:19.81.14/19.47.3/19.18.47/23.45.1) (q:draft)
zawhte = (t:n) (w:things finished/completed works) (d:zawh finish, with plural te: the things he completed) (e:Pasian’ inn a bawl nasep a ~ in) (b:zawh) (r:14.4.11) (q:draft)
zawhthawh = (t:n) (w:force/compulsion/coercion) (d:zawhthawh thu tawh or thu-in means by force) (e:~ thu tawh hong zol uh hi/~ thu tawh Zeisu’ singlamteh pua dingin | to carry the cross of Jesus under compulsion/~ thu bang hi loin, na ut thu-a | not by compulsion but of your own will/Paul amaute lak pan ~ thu-in la a | he took Paul from among them by force) (s:zawhthawhna/sawlzawh) (a:utthu/uttawmna) (r:48.6.12/40.5.41/41.15.21/57.1.14/44.23.10) (q:draft)
zawhthawh = (t:v) (w:force/compel/oppress) (d:press hard on someone, force or oppress; more often found with bawl, as zawhthawh bawl) (e:nang kong ~ nading om lo hi) (s:hahbawl) (r:18.33.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
zawhthawhna = (t:n) (w:compulsion/force/oppression) (d:forcing someone against his will; zawhthawhna tawh is by force, under compulsion) (e:~ tawh cing loin/amaute ~ tawh hong tumsak in | compel them to come in/~ leh khemna suangin | relying on oppression and deceit/kuama kiangah ~ tawh la kei un | do not take from anyone by force) (s:zawhthawh/sawlzawh) (a:uttawmna) (b:zawhthawh) (r:60.5.2/42.14.23/23.30.12/42.3.14) (q:draft)
zawhtheih = (t:v) (w:be able to overcome/can subdue) (d:zawh win over, with theih can) (e:in nang hong ~ nadingin) (s:zawhzawh) (b:zawh) (r:7.16.6) (q:draft)
zawhtheihna = (t:n) (w:ability to accomplish/being able to do) (d:zawhtheih be able to overcome or accomplish, with the noun suffix na) (e:na khempeuh na ~ dingun) (b:zawhtheih) (r:53.1.11) (q:draft)
zawhzah = (t:adv) (w:as much as one is able) (d:zawh be able with zah amount; a piak zawhzah is as much as they could give) (e:a piak ~ dingun a kilawm sangin) (r:47.8.3) (q:draft)
zawhzawh = (t:v) (w:be able to overcome/prevail against) (d:form of zo overcome followed by zo be able, used before loh, lohna or nading) (e:Kuamah in Pasian a ~ lohna/a ~ loh khutte sung pan | from the hands of those too strong for him) (s:zawhtheih) (r:18.9.2/24.31.11) (q:draft)
zawhzawh = (t:v) (w:be able to finish/be able to complete) (d:form of zo finish followed by zo be able) (e:a ~ nading dangka a nei hiam) (r:42.14.28) (q:draft, low confidence)
zawin = (t:adv) (w:more) (d:comparative zaw, more than, with the adverb suffix in; after a descriptive word, more so, to a greater degree) (e:Mu ak bawh sanga manlang ~/a tam ~ a hong pia ding hi | he will give you even more/a lui sangin hoih ~ thupizaw ding hi | it will be better and more glorious than the old one) (b:zaw) (r:25.4.19/41.4.24/37.2.9) (q:draft)
zawk = (t:adv) (w:more) (d:form of zaw used after a descriptive word or verb when leh, ding, nading or kei follows; more, to a greater degree, as in a thuk zawk deeper) (e:kawm maitang sangin a thuk ~ tuak leh/amaute sangin a hat ~ | stronger than they/hoih ~ nading hi loin | not for the better/midangte khempeuh sangin mawhna a hauh ~ uh | more sinful than all the others) (b:zaw) (r:3.14.37/42.13.2/61.2.11/46.11.17) (q:draft)
zawkan = (t:adv) (w:how much more/all the more/even more) (d:placed after a verb in a comparison to say that something applies to an even greater degree; after a negative verb, how much less) (e:hong huam zo lo ~ ding hi/mihingte ngaihsutna telmuh ~ ding hilo ahi hiam | how much more does he see through human thoughts/amaute bangzahin siangtho ~ ding ahi hiam | how much more holy will they be/note hong honkhia zo lo ~ ding hi | how much less will he be able to deliver you) (s:zawtham/kanzaw) (r:14.6.18/20.15.11/9.21.5/14.32.15) (q:draft)
zawkna = (t:n) (w:being more/advantage/preference) (d:zawk more with the noun ending na; after a descriptive word or verb it names the fact of being more so, as in tam zawkna being more numerous, nuam zawkna greater joy and deih zawkna preference) (e:midangte sangin na tam ~ hang uh/mipilpa a hamphat ~ bang om tuan ahi hiam | what advantage has the wise man/ka nuamna sangin nuam ~ a om kei hi | I have no greater joy than this/pasian khempeuh sangin a liat ~ | that he is greater than all gods) (b:zawk) (r:5.7.7/21.6.8/64.1.4/2.18.11) (q:draft)
zawl = (t:n) (w:pole/bar/crossbar) (d:a long piece of wood: a pole for carrying a load, a crossbar that holds frames together, or the bar of a city gate) (e:Amah in singkha sing ~/mi nih in ~ khat-in zawng uh hi | two men carried it on a pole/kulh kongpi leh a kalhna ~ a nei khua | a town with gates and bars/Nangmah in singkha sing ~ na sui ding a | you shall make poles of acacia wood) (s:singzawl) (r:2.36.31/2.26.26/4.13.23/9.23.7/2.25.13) (q:draft)
zawl = (t:n) (w:rim/ledge/border) (d:the raised edge or ledge that runs round a table or an altar) (e:a ~ gei-ah a kualte om hi/khut peek cia a pha ~ khat | a rim a handbreadth wide/a ~ kimkotah kham geihual khat bawl hi | he made a gold molding around the rim/biakna tau ~ nuai panin na bulh ding hi | you shall put it under the ledge of the altar) (s:zawlpeek) (r:2.37.14/2.27.5/2.37.12) (q:draft)
zawl-aikungte = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:mandrakes/mandrake plants) (d:zawl-ai, mandrake, with kung, plant, and the plural te: mandrake plants, which Reuben found in the field) (e:~ kimkhat kei hong pia in) (r:1.30.14) (q:draft)
zawlah = (t:n) (w:on the beam/on the pole) (d:zawl, pole or beam, with the place marker ah: on the beam; in bangtung zawlah birds perch on the top beams of a ruined building) (e:Gunva le gunvapite bangtung ~ tuangin) (b:zawl) (r:36.2.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
zawlai = (t:adv) (w:even more/still more/more) (d:zaw, more, with lai, still: placed after a verb or descriptive word to say even more or still more so) (e:mihaipa adingin lametna om ~ hi/Topa tungah citak lo ~ hi | he became even more unfaithful to the Lord/bangzah takin lehdo ~ ding na hi uh hiam | how much more will you rebel/langpangin thu tam gen ~ uh hi | they spoke still more against him/mi hoihlote a hanthawn ~ uh hi | they encourage evildoers all the more) (s:semsem/kanzaw) (r:20.29.20/14.28.22/5.31.27/14.32.16/24.23.14) (q:draft)
zawlin = (t:adv) (w:as a friend) (d:zawl, friend or companion, with the suffix in: as a friend; zawlin kiman is be friends with, and zawlin man is receive as a friend, welcome) (e:mi gilote tawh ~ a kiman hi/gam ente ~ manin a inn tungsak | she welcomed the spies as friends and took them into her house/Siahdongte leh migilote tawh ~ a kiman hi | he is a friend of tax collectors and sinners) (r:40.11.19/58.11.31/42.7.34) (q:draft, low confidence)
