zawm = (t:adj) (w:weak/faint/feeble) (d:without strength, said of the body and of the conscience) (e:a tha ~ mite khempeuh an ka vak/amau kitheihna lungsim a ~ manin | because their conscience is weak) (s:thanem/thaneem/zawngkhal/thazawng) (a:thahat/hat) (r:24.31.25/46.8.7) (q:draft)
zawmte = (t:n) (w:the weak/the faint) (d:zawm, weak, with the plural te: those who are weak; lungsim zawmte is the fainthearted) (e:lungsim ~ na hansuah un) (s:thanemte/thaneemte/zawngkhalte) (a:thahatte) (b:zawm) (r:52.5.14) (q:draft)
zawn = (t:v) (w:be poor) (d:form of zawng, poor, written zawn’ before na, mahmah and similar words; zawn’na is poverty) (e:na ~’ mahmah khit hangin/Thadahna in ~’na hi a | laziness brings poverty/citak-a ~’ khiukheuna hoihzaw hi | it is better to be poor and honest/~’na in mizawngte siasak hi | poverty ruins the poor/mizawngte ~’na a huh tham loin | not only helping the poor in their need) (a:hauh) (r:18.8.7/20.10.4/20.19.1/20.10.15/47.9.12) (q:draft)
zawng = (t:adj) (w:poor/needy) (d:having little money or property; also used as a verb, be poor or become poor) (e:A ~ meigong khat hong pai a/Lumlum lecin na ~ ding a | if you keep on sleeping you will become poor/A ~ mite tungah amah cingh a | she is generous to the poor/A noptat nuamte ~ a | those who love pleasure become poor) (s:cimawh/genthei) (a:hau) (r:41.12.42/20.20.13/20.31.20/20.21.17) (q:draft)
zawngin = (t:v) (w:being poor/becoming poor) (d:zawng, poor, with the linking ending in: being or becoming poor, and so something else follows) (e:sanggampa ~ a neihsa leitang khenkhat a zuak leh/amah ~ tua zah a piak zawh kei leh | if he is poor and cannot afford that much/kei ~ ka cimawh hi | I am poor and needy/Na gei-a na sanggampa ~ | your brother beside you becoming poor) (b:zawng) (r:3.25.25/3.14.21/19.70.5/3.25.39) (q:draft)
zawngkhal = (t:adj) (w:weak/feeble/powerless/helpless) (d:without strength or power; also used as a verb, grow weak or be worn out) (e:a tha ~ kei nong hotna/a ~ mite huh unla | help the weak/a thahat leh a ~ kikalah | between the mighty and the powerless/minam tawm hi-in ~ mahmah uh ahih manin | because they are a small people and very weak) (s:thanem/thaneem/thazawng/zawm) (a:thahat/hat) (r:18.26.2/30.7.5/52.5.14/14.14.11) (q:draft)
zawngkhalin = (t:adv) (w:destitute/in helplessness) (d:zawngkhal weak and helpless, with the ending in) (e:Nakpi-in ~, bawlsiatna thuakin) (b:zawngkhal) (r:58.11.37) (q:draft)
zawngkhalna = (t:n) (w:infirmity/sickness/weakness) (d:weakness or sickness of the body; of crops, ankung zawngkhalna is blight or mildew) (e:ankung ~ ahi a, kauphe ahi a/cinatna, ~ leh, dawi gilo a vei mi tampi | many who had diseases, sicknesses and evil spirits) (s:thanemna/thaneemna) (a:thahatna/hatna) (b:zawngkhal) (r:11.8.37/42.7.21) (q:draft)
zawngkhalna = (t:n) (w:poverty) (d:the state of being poor and without power) (e:a hau napi-in ~ a thuakna tawh/note tangdingin ~ a thuak | he suffered poverty for your sake) (s:zawnna) (a:hauhna) (b:zawngkhal) (r:47.8.9) (q:draft)
zawngkhalsak = (t:v) (w:make weak/weaken) (d:zawngkhal, weak, with the causative sak: make weak or powerless) (e:Pasian in kei hong ~ hong cimawhsak) (s:zawsak/thanemsak/thaneemsak/thazawsak) (a:thahatsak/hatsak) (b:zawngkhal) (r:18.30.11) (q:draft)
zawngkhalte = (t:n) (w:the weak/weak ones) (d:zawngkhal, weak or feeble, with the plural suffix te) (e:Tuu ~ na khoi kei uh a/upna ~’ ginat lohna i thuakpih ding | we ought to bear with the failings of those weak in faith/a ~ huh ding hi hang | we must help the weak) (s:thanemte/thaneemte/zawmte) (a:thahatte) (b:zawngkhal) (r:26.34.4/45.15.1/44.20.35) (q:draft)
zawnglua = (t:adj) (w:too poor/very poor) (d:zawng, poor, with lua, too or very) (e:~ leuleu leng mi’ na guksakin/a haulua lo, a ~ loin hong bawl inla | make me neither too rich nor too poor/Mi khatpeuh ~-in nangma sehzah a piakzawh kei leh | if anyone is too poor to pay the amount you set) (a:haulua) (b:zawng) (r:20.30.9/3.27.8/20.30.8) (q:draft)
zawngmaw = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:ape/monkey) (d:animal brought by the ships of Tarshish together with ivory and peacocks) (e:saiha, ~, leh utongte hong puak zel hi/saiha, ~, leh zawngpi hong puak zel hi | they used to bring ivory, apes and baboons) (r:11.10.22/14.9.21) (q:draft)
