zeem = (t:v) (w:adorn/decorate/dress up) (d:make beautiful: used of a building, a tomb or the hair, and of dressing a person in fine clothes) (e:suang manpha phutin a inn ~ hi/miphate’ han na ~ uh hi | you decorate the tombs of the righteous/a mitte zutin a lutang ~ a | she painted her eyes and arranged her hair/kumpi puante leh sakol la-in Mordekai ~ a | he took the royal robe and the horse and robed Mordecai) (s:zem) (r:14.3.6/40.23.29/12.9.30/17.6.11) (q:draft)
