Zefo = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zepho) (d:son of Eliphaz and grandson of Esau, a chief of Edom) (r:1.36.11/1.36.15)
Zefon = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zephon) (d:son of Gad, ancestor of the Zephonite clan) (e:~ pan ~ behte ahi) (r:4.26.15) (q:draft)
zehphi = (t:adj) (w:defiled/unclean) (d:ritually defiled or unclean; in 1 Corinthians 8:7 said of people of weak conscience who think of themselves as defiled after eating food offered to idols) (e:a ~ mahin kingaihsun uh hi) (s:nin/kihhuai) (a:zehsiang/siang) (r:46.8.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
zehphitna = (t:n) (w:abomination/defilement) (d:a thing that defiles what is holy; a lipkhaphuai zehphitna is the abomination that causes desolation spoken of by Daniel) (e:Ama om loh nading pi-ah a lipkhaphuai ~/lipkhaphuai ~ a hong om na muh uh ciangin | when you see the abomination that causes desolation appear) (s:kihhuaina/nitna) (r:41.13.14/40.24.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
zehsiang = (t:adj) (w:ceremonially clean/purified) (d:clean according to the ritual law and so fit to take part in worship; said of priests and Levites who had purified themselves) (e:a vekpi-un ~ khin uh hi) (s:siang) (a:zehphi/nin) (r:15.6.20) (q:draft)
