ZEISU = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Jesus) (d:Zeisu, Jesus, written in capital letters in the notice placed above him on the cross) (e:NAZARETH KHUAMI ~ AHI HI) (r:43.19.19/40.27.37) (q:draft)
zeizai = (t:adv) (w:all over/spread about) (d:expressive word placed after a verb, describing many things lying, falling, hanging or shining spread out over a wide area: paak zeizai is strewn everywhere, tuk zeizai is fall dead all over a field) (e:minthan’na taang ~ hi/puante leh nate tawh paak ~ hi | it was strewn all over with clothing and equipment/gamlakah na tuk ~ ding uh hi | you will fall all over the open field/Gilboa Mual tungah tuk ~ uh hi | they fell slain all over Mount Gilboa/a zam ~ a hiangte heuhkhia ding hi | he will cut away the spreading branches) (r:26.10.4/12.7.15/26.39.5/13.10.1/23.18.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
zeizaina = (t:n) (d:zeizai, spread all over, with the noun suffix na: a place where many things hang or lie all about; in Song of Songs 4:4 the tower on which a thousand shields hang) (e:lum tangzang tulkhat a kikhai ~) (b:zeizai) (r:22.4.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
zek = (t:adv) (w:a little/slightly) (d:placed after a word of time, amount or distance: a little, a short while; a den zek ciangin is a little later, kumkhat val zek is a little over a year) (e:kumkhat val ~ khit ciangin/a den ~ ciangin teh leuleu-in | a little later they measured again/lei tawh tawm a kigamla ~ dingin | to be a little way out from the land) (s:neukha/themcik) (r:23.32.10/44.27.28/42.5.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
zekai = (t:v) (w:delay/be late/be slow) (d:be late or slow in doing something, put it off; mostly with a negative, zekai lo, without delay) (e:nangma thupiaknate zuih ding ka ~ kei hi/~ lo hi lehang | if we had not delayed/amah a mudah mi tungah ~ loin | not being slow toward the one who hates him/ka hotkhiatna ~ lo ding hi | my salvation will not be delayed/bang tanvei ~ ding na hi uh hiam | how long will you delay) (a:kinawh) (r:19.119.60/10.20.5/1.43.10/5.7.10/23.46.13/6.18.3) (q:draft)
zekaisak = (t:v) (w:delay/detain/hinder) (d:zekai, be late, with the causative sak: make someone late, hold someone back) (e:kei hong ~ nawn kei un) (b:zekai) (r:1.24.56) (q:draft)
Zekhariah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zechariah) (d:name of many men, among them the prophet Zechariah son of Berekiah and the priest who was the father of John the Baptist) (r:38.7.8/13.9.37)
