zel = (t:adv) (w:repeatedly/habitually/again and again) (d:placed after a verb for an action done time after time or by custom) (e:A pai ngei ~ mah bangin Paul/hong luangsuk kik ~ hi | they flow down again/amah in amah hilhkhol ~ a | he warned him time and again/Ramah-ah amah ciahkik ~ hi | he always went back to Ramah/kum bei simin amah in met ~ hi | he cut it at the end of every year) (s:zelzel/zeel/kikkik) (r:44.17.2/44.9.28/21.1.7/12.6.10/9.7.17/10.14.26) (q:draft)
zel = (t:v) (w:spread over/pervade) (d:of fame, news or praise: spread and reach throughout a land) (e:minthan’na in gam khempeuh ~ a/Izipt gamgi ciang dong nangawn ~ hi | it spread even as far as the border of Egypt/ama minthan’na in gamlapi ~ hi | his fame spread far away/nangmah hong kiphatna in zong a ~ hi | your praise also spreads) (s:zeel/kizel) (r:13.14.17/45.10.18/14.26.8/14.26.15/19.48.10) (q:draft)
Zela = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Zelah/Zela) (d:town of Benjamin where Saul and Jonathan were buried in the tomb of Kish) (r:6.18.28/10.21.14)
