zelh = (t:v) (w:spread over/reach) (d:form of zel spread over, used before bangin) (e:na min in leimong dong a ~ bangin) (b:zel) (r:19.48.10) (q:draft)
zelin = (t:adv) (w:throughout/all over) (d:zel, spread over, with the marker in: spreading through a whole area) (e:gam sung khempeuh ~ a thang hi/tua thu gamsung khempeuh ~ a thangsak uh hi | they spread the news all over that region) (b:zel) (r:40.9.26/40.9.31) (q:draft)
zelin = (t:adv) (w:again and again/repeatedly) (d:zel, repeatedly, with the linking marker in after a verb) (e:tuinak-ah tuite tung kik ~/sih nading panin honkhia kik ~ | rescuing them again and again from death/Paul kiangah va pai ~ | going to Paul again and again/thu zong dong ~ a om | he was asking questions again and again) (s:zelzelin/kikkik) (b:zel) (r:21.1.7/18.33.30/44.24.26/42.2.46) (q:draft)
Zelofehad = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zelophehad) (d:son of Hepher of the tribe of Manasseh, who had no sons and whose five daughters received his inheritance) (r:4.26.33/4.36.11)
zelpak = (t:v) (w:spread quickly) (d:zel spread through, with pak quickly, of news) (e:khempeuh thakhatin a ~ hi) (r:41.1.28) (q:draft)
Zelzah = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Zelzah) (d:place on the border of Benjamin near the tomb of Rachel) (r:9.10.2)
zelzel = (t:adv) (w:repeatedly/again and again/often) (d:placed after a verb to show that the action happens over and over) (e:gamlakah amah lehdo ~ uh a/na hotkhiat kik ~ kul ding hi | you will have to rescue him again and again/kong sawl ~ ka nasem kamsangte | my servants the prophets whom I sent again and again/tua munah pai ~ uh ahih manin | because they often went to that place/Farisi mite in an tang ~ napi-in | though the Pharisees fast often) (s:zel/zeel/kikkik/tamvei) (r:19.78.40/18.33.29/20.19.19/24.26.5/43.18.2/40.9.14) (q:draft)
zelzelin = (t:adv) (w:again and again/repeatedly/often) (d:zelzel, repeatedly, with the ending in, placed after a verb) (e:in gam lakah amah lehdo ~/Nitak simin amaute hong paikik ~ | every evening they come back again) (s:zelin/kikkik) (b:zelzel) (r:19.78.40/19.59.6) (q:draft)
zelzelna = (t:n) (w:frequent occurrence/repeated doing) (d:zelzel, again and again, with the noun suffix na: the fact that something is done or happens many times; na nat mun zelzelna is your frequent illnesses) (e:na nat mun ~ hangin/midang na samsiat ~ | the many times you have cursed others) (b:zelzel) (r:54.5.23/21.7.22) (q:draft)
zelzelte = (t:n) (w:those who often/those who repeatedly) (d:zelzel again and again, with the plural te, after a verb: a khialthei zelzelte, those who err again and again) (e:a khialthei ~ vive ihi hi) (b:zelzel) (r:59.3.2) (q:draft)
zelzul = (t:adj) (w:disorderly/confused) (d:in disorder, confused; in 1 Corinthians 14 said of what God did not call his people to be, set against hoihtak nuamtakin, in a good and peaceful way) (e:ahi ~ dingin a hong sam) (r:46.14.32) (q:draft, low confidence)
zem = (t:v) (w:decorate/adorn) (d:make something beautiful by adding ornament, as overlaying an idol with silver and gold, decorating a tomb or working cloth with coloured thread) (e:kham leh ngun tawh a ~ uh a/mualsuangte hoihtakin na ~ uh a | you decorate the tombstones beautifully/saiha pak tawh ~ uh hi | they adorned it with ivory/puan engdup leh puan sandup tawh ~ uh hi | they dress it in blue and purple cloth/na siampite, gupna tawh ~ in la | clothe your priests with salvation) (s:zep/zeem/etlawmsak) (r:24.10.4/40.23.29/26.27.6/24.10.9/14.6.41)
