zemin = (t:v) (w:adorning/decorating/dressing/painting) (d:zem, decorate or adorn, with the linking marker in; of a person, dressing in fine clothes, and of the eyes, putting on paint) (e:puan hoih mahmah tawh amah ~/na mitte ~ na golsak hangin | though you enlarge your eyes with paint/Puanphan kizem hoihte tawh nang hong ~ | I clothed you with fine embroidered cloth/a mit uh ~ | painting their eyes) (s:zeemin) (b:zem) (r:1.41.42/26.16.10/24.4.30/26.23.40) (q:draft)
Zemirah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zemirah) (d:son of Beker and grandson of Benjamin) (r:13.7.8)
zemsak = (t:v) (w:robe/dress/adorn) (d:zem, decorate, with the causative sak: dress another person in fine clothes) (e:amah ~ inla) (s:zeemsak) (b:zem) (r:17.6.9) (q:draft)
zen = (t:part) (w:really/even) (d:emphatic word placed after a verb: really, even, to such a degree) (e:na lampi na hilh ~ hi/laano hukte na bang ~ hi | you are just like a wild donkey in heat/hong langpan’ ~ uh hi | they have gone so far as to rebel/zuauthu na um ta ~ uh hi | you have really come to trust lies/luang kham ~ mahin an zong dingin | to seek food even at the risk of life) (r:24.2.33/24.2.24/24.5.23/24.7.8/25.5.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
