zensak = (t:v) (d:with causative sak; in Amos 4:10 said of making the stench of the camps fill or reach the nostrils) (r:30.4.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
zenzen = (t:adv) (w:at all/really/by chance) (d:emphatic word placed after a verb: in questions and negatives really or at all, before kei leh if it were not so, and of an event happening by chance) (e:Tua bang hi ~ lo ding hi/Tua hi ~ kei leh | if that had not been so/Tua bang i ci ~ kei ding hi | we shall certainly not say that/siampi khat paikha ~ a | a priest happened to pass by/Sila namte ahi ~ hiam | is he really a slave by birth) (r:45.3.6/42.10.31/18.3.13/45.9.14/24.2.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
zep = (t:v) (w:decorate/adorn/ornament) (d:make beautiful with ornament; sing zep nasep is ornamental work in wood, carving; in Titus 2 said of adorning the teaching by good conduct) (e:na biakna mun ~ nadingin na zang a/sing ~ nasep a sem dingin | to do the work of carving wood/mihing khutsiamte in bawlin a ~ ngunte | silver made and adorned by human craftsmen/thuhilhna khempeuh ah a ~ theih nadingun | so that they may adorn the teaching in everything) (s:zem/zeem/etlawmsak/hoihbawl) (r:26.16.16/2.31.3/56.2.9/44.17.29) (q:draft)
zepin = (t:v) (w:folding) (d:fold the hands, with in linking it to the next verb; khut zepin om is sit with folded hands) (e:na sem loin a khut ~ om uh a) (r:21.4.5) (q:draft)
zepna = (t:n) (w:setting/ornament/decoration) (d:something made to adorn or to hold a stone, as the gold settings on the priestly garments and carved decoration on a wall, from zep adorn) (e:kham tawh ~ suangah tuate kikoih hi/khau mong nihte ~ tawh na zom ding a | you shall join the two ends of the cords to the settings/kham tawh a kibawl ~ nih | two settings made of gold/kham tawh ~ sungah tuate kibulh ding hi | they shall be mounted in gold settings) (s:kizepna) (b:zep) (r:2.39.13/2.28.25/2.39.16/2.28.20) (q:draft)
