ziatlam = (t:n) (w:right/right side/right hand) (d:the right-hand side; the opposite is veilam, left) (e:a ~ khat a veilam khat/Tuute a ~, keelte a veilam a koih ding hi | he will put the sheep on his right and the goats on his left/vangliatna ~ ah tu a | sitting at the right hand of power/a ~ khut lenin | taking him by the right hand) (s:taklam/ziat) (a:veilam) (r:41.15.27/40.25.33/41.14.62/44.3.7) (q:draft)
ziatlamah = (t:adv) (w:on the right/at the right side) (d:ziatlam right side, with ah at) (e:a ~ a omte kiangah) (a:veilamah) (b:ziatlam) (r:40.25.34) (q:draft)
ziau = (t:adv) (w:swiftly/easily/at once) (d:placed after a verb to show that the action is done quickly and lightly in one movement: la ziau, snatch away; botsat ziau, snap off; paikhia ziau, slip away) (e:mimkhau bangin khauhualte botsat ~ hi/amah in thalkhaute botsat ~ hi | he snapped the bowstrings/mihingte’ hauhna ka la ~ hi | I snatched the wealth of the peoples/Jesuh paikhia ~ ahih manin | because Jesus had slipped away) (s:pak) (r:7.16.12/43.5.13/7.16.9/23.10.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
