ziazua = (t:adv) (w:all about/rattling) (d:expressive word placed after a verb, describing many things together making a rattling or crackling noise, lying or seen all over a place, or shining brightly: ging ziazua is rattle, om ziazua is lie all about, tee ziazua is shine all over) (e:a kigawi ~ a ging ka za a/kangin a puak ~ tawh kibang uh a | they are like the crackling of a fire/siluang hawm om ~ kawikawi ding hi | corpses will lie all about/biak milim khempeuh a kisuai ~ ka mu hi | I saw all the idols drawn all over/Pasian’ vang tawh tee ~ a | it shone with the glory of God) (r:26.37.7/26.6.13/29.2.5/26.8.10/66.21.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
