zin = (t:n) (w:earthquake) (d:a shaking of the earth; zin liing or zin ling is the earth quakes) (e:thakhatin ~ nakpi liing a/nakpi-in ~ a liing hi | there was a great earthquake/Thakhatin ~ nakpitakin hong ling hi | suddenly there was a violent earthquake/Mun tuamtuamah ~ hong ling ding a | there will be earthquakes in various places) (s:ziin/zinling/zinliing) (r:44.16.26/66.6.12/40.28.2/41.13.8) (q:draft)
zin = (t:n) (w:guest/stranger/sojourner/traveller) (d:one who is away from home, a guest in a house or a foreigner in a land; zin do is to show hospitality and zin tunna inn is a guest room or an inn) (e:gam dangah ~ ahi ding uh a/~ khat hong tung a | a traveller arrived/~ na hih lai takin cika hong mu a | when did we see you a stranger/Khualmite hoihtakin ~ na do ding uh | to show kind hospitality to strangers/na ~, na peemta ka hi hi | I am your guest, a sojourner with you) (s:khualmi/leengla/mikhual) (r:44.7.6/60.4.9/10.12.4/40.25.38/58.13.2/19.39.12) (q:draft)
