zing = (t:n) (w:dwell) (d:of a cloud, settle and stay over a place) (e:Tua ni-in meiipi ~ hen la) (r:18.3.5)
zinga = (t:n) (d:second part of kong zing, street, with a, at: kong zinga, in the streets) (e:Kong ~ naupangte a vatmang a) (r:24.9.21) (q:draft, low confidence)
zingciang = (t:adv) (w:tomorrow/the next day) (d:also the day after an event: a zingciang ni) (e:tu ni leh ~ sung teng/Tu-ni ahi zongin, ~ ahi zongin | whether today or tomorrow/Paisan pawi khit a ~ ni teekteekin | on the very day after the Passover/En in, ~ in kha det ni hi a | look, tomorrow is the New Moon/tho honpite ~ a paikhiat theih nadingin | so that the swarms of flies may leave tomorrow) (a:zani) (r:2.19.10/6.5.11/59.4.13/9.20.5/2.8.29) (q:draft)
zingciangin = (t:adv) (w:tomorrow/the next day/the next morning) (d:zingciang, tomorrow, with the suffix in; a zingciangin is on the following day) (e:a ~ Khios tuikulh kiangah ka tung/~ bang thu a piang ding | what will happen tomorrow/a ~ Topa hong sawl bang tektekin | the next morning, just as the Lord had commanded me/~ kumpipa kiangah gen in | speak to the king in the morning) (a:zani) (b:zingciang) (r:44.20.15/59.4.14/26.24.18/17.5.14) (q:draft)
zinggawp = (t:v) (w:grow utterly dark) (d:zing dark or cloudy, with gawp thoroughly: khim zinggawp, darkness falls completely) (e:khuapi-ah khim ~ ding a) (b:zing) (r:26.30.18) (q:draft)
zingin = (t:v) (w:be dark/be gloomy) (d:zing dark or cloudy, with the linking suffix in: khua zingin, the day being dark) (e:khua ~ mai mial ni) (s:ziingin/mialin) (b:zing) (r:36.1.15) (q:draft)
zingsak = (t:v) (w:darken/make dark) (d:zing dark, cloudy, with causative sak) (e:leitung khim a ~ hi/meii sahpi le tui tawh a ~ hi | he made it dark with thick clouds and water) (s:ziingsak/mialsak) (a:taangsak) (b:zing) (r:19.105.28/19.18.11) (q:draft)
zingsang = (t:n) (w:morning) (d:the early part of the day; a zingsang ciangin is in the morning or the next morning, and zingsang tungin is early in the morning) (e:A ~ ciangin Topa in kei kiangah/Nitak hong bei-in, ~ hong tung a | evening passed and morning came/~ khuavak dong mi khat in amah lai hi | a man wrestled with him until daybreak/~ a kipan nitak dongin | from morning until evening) (a:nitak) (r:26.12.8/1.1.19/1.32.24/2.18.13)
zingsanga = (t:adv) (w:in the morning/of the morning) (d:zingsang, morning, with the suffix a, in or of; zingsanga meihal biakna is the morning burnt offering) (e:~ a kuankhia inn teekpa tawh kibang hi/~ kipan nitak dongin | from morning until evening/~ kai meiilum | the morning mist/~ meihal biakna banah | in addition to the morning burnt offering) (s:zingsangin) (a:nitakin) (b:zingsang) (r:40.20.1/4.28.23/2.18.14/28.13.3) (q:draft)
zingsangin = (t:adv) (w:in the morning) (d:zingsang, morning, with the suffix in: in the morning; often followed by tho baih, get up early) (e:Tuuno khat ~ na pia ding uh a/~ palhin thaksuak kik a | in the morning it sprouts and grows new/~ Balaam tho-in a la tutphah vawh a | in the morning Balaam got up and saddled his donkey/~ Joshua thobaih a | Joshua got up early in the morning) (s:zingsanga) (a:nitakin) (b:zingsang) (r:4.28.4/19.90.6/4.22.21/6.6.12) (q:draft)
zingsol = (t:n) (c:star) (w:morning star) (d:the bright star seen before dawn, zing, morning, with sol) (e:Amaute tungah ~ zong ka pia ding hi/~ suak a, khua hong vak dongin | until the morning star rises and the day dawns) (r:66.2.28/66.22.16/61.1.19) (q:draft)
Zingsol = (t:n) (c:star) (w:Morning Star) (d:zingsol, the morning star, written with a capital as a title) (e:a taang khuavak ~ ka hi hi/~ zong amah ka pia ding hi | I will also give him the morning star) (b:zingsol) (r:66.22.16/66.2.28) (q:draft)
zingtho = (t:v) (w:rise early/get up early) (d:zing morning, with tho rise: get up early in the morning) (e:Phalvak tungin ~ a) (s:ziingtho/thobaih) (r:20.31.15) (q:draft)
zingtungin = (t:adv) (w:early in the morning/at dawn) (d:zingtung early morning with the marker -in) (e:kimkhatte ~ hanah pai uh/khuavak ma ~ Magdala khua Mari hanah pai a | early, before it was light, Mary Magdalene went to the tomb/Arabah lam paisukna-ah ~ a kuankhia uh hi | they went out early in the morning at the descent toward the Arabah/a zing ciang ~ amaute a thawh ciangin | when they got up early the next morning) (s:zingtuungin) (r:42.24.22/42.24.1/43.20.1/6.8.14/9.5.4) (q:draft)
zingtuungin = (t:adv) (w:early in the morning) (d:zing morning, with tuung and in) (e:~ a thawhkik khit ciangin) (s:zingtungin) (r:41.16.9) (q:draft)
zinin = (t:v) (w:travelling/journeying) (d:zin, travel, with the linking suffix in; khual zinin is travelling away from home) (e:Paul khual hong ~ Efesa khua/Akhaia gamah Paul ~ Jerusalem-ah paisuak ding a ngaihsun hi | Paul decided to travel through Achaia and go on to Jerusalem) (s:khualzinin) (b:zin) (r:44.19.1/44.19.21) (q:draft)
zinin = (t:adv) (w:as a guest/as a stranger) (d:zin, guest or sojourner, with the suffix in; zinin om is stay as a guest or live as a foreigner) (e:ama ~ ka om uh hi/Media gamah ~ a om hi | he lived as a foreigner in Midian) (b:zin) (r:44.28.7/44.7.29) (q:draft)
zinkhia = (t:v) (w:go away on a journey/set out/leave home) (d:zin, travel, with khia, out) (e:Inn panin gamlapi-ah a ~ mipa/a ap khit ciangin a ~ hi | after entrusting it to them he went away on his journey) (b:zin) (r:20.27.8/40.25.15) (q:draft)
zinkik = (t:v) (w:travel again/journey back) (d:zin travel, with kik again or back) (e:Note na ~ ngei nawn kei) (b:zin) (r:5.28.68) (q:draft)
zinleleeng = (t:n) (w:guests/visitors/strangers) (d:zin and leeng, guests and visitors of every kind; zinleleeng do is show hospitality) (e:~ do a siam mi/Khatlekhat maitai takin ~ na kido un | cheerfully offer hospitality to one another) (s:zinte) (r:56.1.8/60.4.9) (q:draft)
zinliing = (t:n) (w:earthquake) (d:zin earthquake, with liing shake) (e:vanging, ~, a ging lianpi) (s:zinling/ziinling/ziin) (r:23.29.6) (q:draft)
zinliingte = (t:n) (w:earthquakes) (d:zin liing the earth quakes, with plural te) (e:khuaphelepte leh ~ a piang hi/vangingte, ~, nakpi gialkiatnate a piang uh hi | there came thunder, earthquakes and heavy hail) (b:zinliing) (r:66.8.5/66.11.19) (q:draft)
zinlin = (t:n) (w:earthquake) (d:zinling, earthquake, written without the final g and with an apostrophe before ma, before, and before the suffix na) (e:~’ ma kum nih hun laitakin/a haksa mahmah ~’na a piang hi | a very severe earthquake took place) (r:30.1.1/66.16.18) (q:draft)
zinling = (t:n) (w:earthquake/quake) (d:zin, earthquake, and ling, shake; also written apart as a clause, zin hong ling is the earth quaked) (e:~ khit ciangin meikuang om a/vanging, ~, a ging lianpi | thunder, earthquake and great noise/tua ~ in mi tulsagih a sisak hi | that earthquake killed seven thousand people/~ zahin gin’ ngaih mahmah hi | it was as loud as an earthquake) (s:zinliing/ziinling/ziin) (r:11.19.12/23.29.6/66.11.13/26.3.13) (q:draft)
zinlinna = (t:n) (w:earthquake) (d:zinlin earthquake, with the noun suffix na) (e:galkapte in ~ le a thupiangte a muh) (s:zinling) (b:zinlin) (r:40.27.54/38.14.5) (q:draft)
zinna = (t:n) (w:journey/travel/travelling) (d:zin, travel, with the noun suffix na; ka zinna khempeuhah is everywhere I travelled) (e:khual gamlapi ~-in paat gawp hi/Illyrikam gam ciang dong ka ~ khempeuhah | everywhere I travelled, as far as Illyricum) (s:khualzinna/lampaina) (b:zin) (r:6.9.13/45.15.18) (q:draft)
zinpa = (t:n) (w:guest/visitor) (d:zin guest, with pa for a man: the male guest) (e:~’ zineu om hi) (b:zin) (r:7.19.24) (q:draft)
zinsuk = (t:v) (w:travel down/go down) (d:zin travel, with suk downward; a zinsuk a zintohna is their travelling to and fro) (e:a ~ a zintohna uhah lungmuanna om lo) (b:zin) (r:14.15.5) (q:draft)
zinte = (t:n) (w:guests/strangers/visitors) (d:plural of zin; people who come from elsewhere, guests in a house or foreigners in a place) (e:~ vui nading beel seekpa’ lei/Ka inn-ah hong tung ngei ka ~ | my guests who used to come to my house/Rom khua pan hong pai ~ | visitors who had come from Rome/ute naute tungah ahi zongin, ~ tungah ahi zongin | whether to the brothers or to strangers) (s:khualmite/leenglate/zinleleeng) (b:zin) (r:40.27.7/64.1.5/18.19.15/44.2.10) (q:draft)
zintohna = (t:n) (w:travelling up/going up) (d:zin travel, with toh upward and the noun suffix na; a zinsuk a zintohna is their travelling to and fro) (e:a zinsuk a ~ uhah lungmuanna om lo) (r:14.15.5) (q:draft)
zintun = (t:v) (w:lodge/stay as a guest/put up) (d:zin, guest, with tun, arrive: arrive and stay somewhere as a traveller; zintun inn is an inn and zintun nading mun a place to lodge) (e:~ nading mun dang khempeuh mi dim/~ nading inndei koilai ahi hiam | where is the guest room/~’ inn ukpa a piak khit ciangin | after giving them to the innkeeper) (s:giak/taam) (r:42.2.7/42.10.35/41.14.14) (q:draft)
zintunna = (t:n) (w:lodging/place of stay) (d:the place where a traveller stays as a guest; before inn, mun or pa it means the house, the place or the host where one is staying) (e:ka ~ inn-ah hong tung uh hi/Paul a ~ munah | at the place where Paul was staying/Keima ~ pa | my host/Na ~ inn uh kheel themthum kei un | do not keep changing the house where you stay) (s:peemna) (b:zintun) (r:44.11.11/45.16.23/44.28.23/42.10.7) (q:draft)
zinzin = (t:v) (w:travel about/journey) (d:zin travel, doubled for going on and on or from place to place; used with khual, away from home) (e:amah tawh khual a ~ khawm ngei mite) (s:khualzinzin) (r:44.13.31) (q:draft)
zinzinna = (t:n) (w:travels/journeying) (d:zinzin travel about, with the noun suffix na) (e:Khual ka ~ lamin tuikhang lauhuaina) (s:khualzinna) (b:zinzin) (r:47.11.26) (q:draft)
Zion = (t:name) (c:mountain) (w:Zion) (d:the hill of Jerusalem with the fortress David captured, the City of David; also a name for Jerusalem and its people) (e:~ a mudahte khempeuh maizumin kinungkiksak ta hen) (r:19.129.5/19.78.68) (q:draft)
Zior = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Zior) (d:town in the hill country of Judah) (r:6.15.54)
Ziph = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Ziph) (d:town and desert in the hill country of Judah, written Zif in the Tedim Bible)
zipi = (t:n) (w:wedding/marriage) (d:zi, wife: the taking of a wife; zipi hun is the time of the wedding and zipi pa the bridegroom) (e:Tuuno’ ~ hun a tung zo hi/~ pa mothak nu tungah a lungdam mah bangin | as a bridegroom rejoices over his bride) (s:zipina/zineihna/mopina) (b:zi) (r:66.19.7/23.62.5) (q:draft)
zipih = (t:n) (w:co-wife/rival wife) (d:zi wife with pih fellow: another wife of the same husband) (e:amah a el a ~ in amah nakpitakin) (b:zi) (r:9.1.6) (q:draft)
zipil = (t:n) (w:prudent wife/wise wife) (d:zi wife, with pil wise) (e:~ ahih leh Topa bek in) (r:20.19.14) (q:draft)
zipina = (t:n) (w:wedding/marriage) (d:zipi wedding, with the noun suffix na; zipina pawi is a wedding feast) (e:Tuuno’ ~ pawi-ah a kisam mite) (s:zipi/zineihna/mopina/kitenna) (b:zipi) (r:66.19.9) (q:draft)
zipipa = (t:n) (w:bridegroom) (d:the man who is taking a wife; -pa marks a male) (e:~ hong pai zo hi/~ dawn dingin | to meet the bridegroom/sisan tawh ~ na hi hi | you are a bridegroom of blood/~ hong tung a | the bridegroom arrived) (s:zineipa/mopipa) (b:zipi) (r:40.25.6/42.5.34/40.25.1/2.4.26/40.25.10) (q:draft)
Zippor = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zippor) (d:father of Balak king of Moab) (e:~’ tapa Balak in mu hi) (r:4.22.2/4.22.10) (q:draft)
Zipporah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zipporah) (d:daughter of Jethro the priest of Midian and wife of Moses) (r:2.4.25)
Zipporah = (t:name) (c:female) (w:Zipporah) (d:daughter of Jethro the priest of Midian and wife of Moses) (r:2.2.21)
zite = (t:n) (w:wives) (e:na ~ uh na it un/Esau in a ~, a tapate, a tanute | Esau took his wives, his sons and his daughters/ka ~ leh ka tate hong pia in la | give me my wives and my children) (b:zi) (r:49.5.25/51.3.19/1.36.6/1.30.26) plural form of <zi>
Ziv = (t:name) (w:Ziv) (d:second month of the Hebrew year, in which Solomon began to build the temple) (r:11.6.1/11.6.37)
Ziz = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Ziz) (d:place named in Ziz kahtohna lampi, the way going up at Ziz, the Pass of Ziz in the NIV) (e:~ kahtohna lampi tawnin amaute hong kuanto) (r:14.20.16) (q:draft)
Ziza = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ziza) (d:name of two men, a leader of the tribe of Simeon and a son of King Rehoboam and Maakah) (r:13.4.37/14.11.20)
zo = (t:n) (w:zomi) the people of zomi
zo = (t:v) (w:win/defeat/overcome) (d:get the better of an enemy or opponent; gal zo is win a battle) (e:galhang thahatte in gal ~ tawntung lo hi/amaute in kei hong ~ nai lo uh hi | they have not yet prevailed over me/note zakhat in tulsawm na ~ ding uh hi | a hundred of you will defeat ten thousand/Moab gam sungah Midian mite a ~ | who defeated the Midianites in the land of Moab) (s:gualzo) (a:lel/guallel) (r:21.9.11/19.129.2/3.26.8/1.36.35)
zo = (t:v) (w:gain) (d:after ngah, get: succeed in getting, gain) (e:taina lel tawh pilna ngah ~ uh hi | they gain knowledge by a mere rebuke/a deih khempeuh ngah ~ hi | he gains all that he desires) (r:20.19.25/20.13.4)
Zoan = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Zoan) (d:ancient city in the Nile delta of Egypt, also called Tanis) (r:26.30.14/19.78.12)
Zoans = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Zoan) (d:spelling of Zoan, the city in the Nile delta of Egypt, found in Isaiah 30:4) (r:23.30.4)
Zoar = (t:name) (c:land/city) (w:Zoar) (d:small town near the Dead Sea, earlier called Bela, to which Lot fled from Sodom) (r:1.19.23)
Zobah = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Zobah) (d:Aramean kingdom north of Damascus, ruled by Hadadezer and defeated by David) (r:13.18.9/10.23.36)
Zobebah = (t:name) (w:Hazzobebah) (d:descendant of Judah, child of Koz) (r:13.4.8)
Zobehah = (t:name) (w:Hazzobebah) (d:descendant of Judah, child of Koz; another spelling of the same name in 1 Chronicles 4:8) (r:13.4.8)
Zofah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zophah) (d:son of Helem, a chief of the tribe of Asher) (r:13.7.35/13.7.36)
Zofai = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zophai) (d:Levite of the family of Kohath, son of Elkanah and ancestor of the prophet Samuel) (r:13.6.26)
Zofar = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zophar) (d:Zophar the Naamathite, one of the three friends of Job) (r:18.2.11/18.11.1)
Zofim = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Zophim) (d:field on the top of Mount Pisgah in Moab, where Balak took Balaam to curse Israel) (r:4.23.14)
zogawp = (t:v) (w:crush/overpower/subdue) (d:zo, overcome, with gawp, thoroughly or violently: crush an enemy or bring a people completely under control) (e:amah in kumpite ~ ding hi/na thahatna tawh na galte na ~ hi | with your strength you crushed your enemies/Edom mite leh Moab mite ~ ding uh a | they will subdue Edom and Moab/gal in kei hong bawlsia a, hong ~ hi | the enemy has persecuted me and crushed me) (s:sugawp) (b:zo) (r:19.110.5/19.143.3/19.89.10/23.11.14) (q:draft)
zogawpin = (t:v) (w:overpowering/crushing/defeating completely) (d:zogawp, defeat utterly, with the linking suffix -in, followed by another verb: crush and then drive out, kill or destroy) (e:a gal khempeuh uh ~ a susiamang/mi khat ~ na hawlkhia a | you overpower a person and drive him away/tua teci pangte simin ~ that ding a | will attack those witnesses, overpower and kill them/gamdang khempeuhte ~ a kip tawntung ding hi | it will crush all other kingdoms and stand forever) (b:zogawp) (r:33.5.9/27.2.44/18.14.20/66.11.7) (q:draft)
zogawpsak = (t:v) (w:let conquer/cause to be conquered) (d:zogawp, crush or overpower, with the causative sak: let one people conquer another) (e:nisuahna lam mite ka ~ ding a) (b:zogawp) (r:26.25.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
Zohar = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zohar) (d:name of several men, among them the father of Ephron the Hittite and a son of Simeon) (r:1.23.8/1.46.10)
Zoheth = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zoheth) (d:son of Ishi, of the tribe of Judah) (r:13.4.20)
zoin = (t:v) (w:overcome/defeat/conquer/triumph over) (d:zo with the linking suffix -in, overcoming and then doing the next action; after another verb, being able to do it) (e:David in Filistiate ~ nuaisiah a/keimah in amah ~ ka thah leh | if I overcome him and kill him/Filistia mite in Israelte ~ | the Philistines defeated the Israelites/Hehpihna in thukhenna ~ a kisathei thei hi | mercy triumphs over judgment) (b:zo) (r:13.18.1/9.17.9/9.4.2/59.2.13) (q:draft)
zokhin = (t:v) (w:have overcome/have won/have finished) (d:zo, win, overcome or finish, with khin, already, showing a completed action) (e:Dawimangpa ~ na hihna hang uh ahi hi/tua bang kamsang kineihkhemte a ~ na hi uh hi | you have overcome such false prophets/Dawimangpa ~ na hih manun | because you have overcome the evil one/upna thu khotakin lenin ka ~ hi | holding fast to the faith, I have finished) (b:zo) (r:62.2.14/62.4.4/62.2.13/55.4.7) (q:draft)
zokik = (t:v) (w:conquer again/overrun again) (d:zo, overcome, with kik, again: conquer a place once more) (e:gamdang mite in ~ nawn lo) (b:zo) (r:29.3.17) (q:draft)
zol = (t:v) (w:persuade/entice/coax) (d:win someone over by words, whether to believe or do something good or to do wrong; the same word covers persuade, coax and entice) (e:mihoih lote in hong ~ ciangin/Judah mi leh Grik mite a ~ hi | he tried to persuade Jews and Greeks/A ngongtat mite in a lawmte ~ a | violent people entice their neighbors/Keimah in amah ka ~ ding hi | I will entice him/na pasal ~ in | coax your husband) (s:umsak) (r:20.1.10/44.18.4/20.16.29/11.22.21/7.14.15) (q:draft)
zolbawl = (t:v) (w:plead with/persuade) (d:zol, persuade, with bawl, do: work at persuading someone, plead with a person to change) (e:na nu uh ~ un) (b:zol) (r:28.2.2) (q:draft)
zolin = (t:v) (w:persuading/enticing/seducing) (d:zol, persuade or entice, with the linking suffix -in, followed by another verb) (e:nungak khat ~ amah tawh a lup/minamte ~ a khem hi | she entices and deceives the nations/midangte’ zite ~ luppih hi | he seduces other men's wives and sleeps with them/~, lau loin a hilh hi | persuading, he taught without fear) (b:zol) (r:2.22.16/44.19.8/34.3.4/26.18.11) (q:draft)
zolkhia = (t:v) (w:draw away/entice away) (d:zol, persuade, with khia, out or away: draw people away from where they belong) (e:Nungzuite a ~ dingin thuzuau a gen mite/na pial nadingun hong ~ het lo ding hi | he will never entice you to turn aside) (b:zol) (r:44.20.30/48.5.8) (q:draft)
zolkhiat = (t:v) (w:draw away/entice away) (d:form of zolkhia used before a noun such as hun, time) (e:thu um mite khemin a ~ hun) (b:zolkhia) (r:44.20.30) (q:draft)
zolkik = (t:v) (w:win back/allure) (d:zol, persuade or coax, with kik, back or again: win someone back with kind words) (e:itna kam tawh hopihin ka ~ ding hi) (b:zol) (r:28.2.14) (q:draft)
zolna = (t:n) (w:enticement/persuasion/temptation) (d:zol, persuade or entice, with the noun suffix na: the act of persuading, or an enticement to do wrong) (e:amau’ ~ zui kei in/Tua bang numeite’ ~ mang kei un | do not heed the enticement of such women/~ a thuak ciangin | when he is enticed/Ka ~ uh hong man’ loh ciangin | when he would not accept our persuasion) (s:zolzolna) (b:zol) (r:20.1.10/48.5.8/20.7.25/59.1.14/44.21.14) (q:draft)
zolo = (t:v) (w:cannot/be unable to) (d:zo, be able, with the negative lo, written as one word after a verb: not able to do it) (e:kuamah a damsak ~ zato siam-a kineite/a kithei ~ thute kitelsak hi | he makes clear the things that cannot be known/a ki-uk ~ mi leh a gamtat sia khat | a man without self-control and of bad conduct) (a:hizo) (b:zo) (r:18.13.4/18.12.22/9.25.3) (q:draft)
zolopa = (t:n) (w:one who cannot/man who is unable) (d:zolo, be unable, with pa for a man: a ki-uk zolopa is the man who cannot control himself) (e:Ama lungsim a ki-uk ~ in) (b:zolo) (r:20.25.28) (q:draft)
zolsak = (t:v) (w:make shine) (d:make something shine or glisten, with the causative sak; said of oil that makes the face shine) (e:maitang a ~ ding sathau) (r:19.104.15) (q:draft)
zolsimna = (t:n) (w:persuasion/enticement) (d:apparently zol persuade, with sim and the noun suffix na: the urging of others, which a person heeds) (e:mite’ ~ a mang ding hi) (s:zolna) (r:27.11.30) (q:draft, low confidence)
zolua = (t:v) (w:defeat utterly) (d:zo overcome, with lua very, exceedingly) (e:Babylon galkap khempeuh ~ kisa-in) (b:zo) (r:24.37.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
zolzawh = (t:v) (w:persuade/win over) (d:zol, persuade, with zawh, be able or succeed: succeed in persuading, win someone over) (e:mite ka ~ nadingun ka hanciam uh hi) (s:umsak) (r:47.5.11) (q:draft)
zolzolna = (t:n) (w:persuasion/coaxing) (d:zol, persuade, said twice for continued action, with the noun suffix na: patient and repeated persuading) (e:~ tawh gam ukte kizo thei a) (s:zolna) (r:20.25.15) (q:draft)
zom = (t:v) (w:continue/go on/carry on) (d:carry on with what was being done, such as a journey or a speech; often as zom lai, still continue) (e:Elihu in a thugen ~ lai a/Abram in a khualzin ~ lai a | Abram continued his journey/Jakob in a khualzinna ~ a | Jacob continued his journey/mawhna a bawl ~ thei kei hi | he cannot go on sinning/a khualzin ~ dingin | to continue his journey) (s:zomlai/zomsuak) (a:tawp) (r:18.36.1/1.12.9/1.29.1/62.3.9/7.19.27) (q:draft)
zom = (t:v) (w:join/attach/fasten) (d:join one thing to another, fasten the end of one thing onto another) (e:khau mong nihte ~ uh hi/a mong nihte gel-ah ~ uh hi | they attached them to its two corners/khau mong nihte zepna tawh na ~ ding a | you shall fasten the two ends of the cords to the settings/mai lamah tua bangin na ~ ding hi | you shall attach them in this way at the front) (a:khen) (r:2.39.18/2.39.4/2.28.25) (q:draft)
zom = (t:n) (w:next/second) (d:the one that comes next in place, order or rank; ama zom-ah means next to him or after him) (e:Ama ~-ah phual a sat dingte/leh ama ~-ah Abinadab | and next to him Abinadab/kumpipa ~-ah aana a nei Elkanah | Elkanah, who held authority next to the king/amah in Absalom ~-a a suak ahi hi | he was born next after Absalom) (r:4.2.27/9.23.17/9.17.13/14.28.7/11.1.6) (q:draft)
zomah = (t:prep) (w:next to/after) (d:zom, next, with the place marker ah: next to or after a person or thing in a row or a list, with a, ama or amaute before it) (e:Ama ~ Jerusalem kiim nai-a om siampite/Ama ~ Henadad’ tapa Binnui in | next to him Binnui son of Henadad/Amaute’ ~ Jerusalem gam phel khat a uk | next to them the ruler of a half-district of Jerusalem/a ~ Asher minamte | next to it the tribe of Asher) (b:zom) (r:16.3.22/26.48.2/16.3.24/16.3.9) (q:draft)
zomang = (t:v) (w:crush completely/wipe out) (d:zo, overcome, with mang, gone: overcome so that nothing is left) (e:A vekpi-in ~ khin ni) (s:susiamang) (r:19.74.8) (q:draft)
zomin = (t:v) (w:joining on/continuing/adding to) (d:zom, join or continue, with the linking suffix -in: joining on to something already there, as in building upon a foundation, sharing in one loaf or keeping on in good conduct) (e:Tua khuam tungah ~ a lam mi/Midangte in a ban ~ a lam uh hi | others are building on it/tua khomun ~ i ne ahih ciangin | because we share in that one loaf and eat/a pha a gamtatna uh ~ | continuing in their good conduct) (b:zom) (r:46.3.14/49.2.20/46.3.10/46.10.17/60.4.19) (q:draft)
zomkhawm = (t:v) (w:share together/join together in) (d:zom, join, with khawm, together: have a share in something together with others) (e:thuciamna a ~ mi a suak uh hi) (b:zom) (r:49.3.6) (q:draft)
zomlai = (t:v) (w:continue/go on/keep on) (d:carry on with what was being done or said; a thugen zomlai, he continued speaking) (e:Elihu in a thugen ~ a/Jesuh in a thugen ~ a | Jesus went on speaking/biakinn a lam ~ ding uh | to go on building the temple/thah dingin a hanciamna ~ hi | he kept up his efforts to kill them) (s:zom/zomsuak) (a:tawp) (r:18.36.1/44.9.1/42.4.24/15.4.4) (q:draft)
zomna = (t:n) (w:continuing/continuation) (d:zom continue, with the noun suffix na; nasep zomna is going on with the work) (e:a nasep ~ uh kikhaktan lo hi) (b:zom) (r:15.5.5) (q:draft)
zompa = (t:n) (w:the next man/one next to) (d:zom next, with pa marking a male: the man who comes next after someone) (e:amah a ~ in Ahoah mi Dodo’ tapa/amah a ~ in Ahoah-te beh Dodo’ tapa Eleazar | next to him was Eleazar son of Dodo the Ahohite) (b:zom) (r:10.23.9/13.11.12) (q:draft)
zomsak = (t:v) (w:let continue/make continue) (d:zom, continue, with the causative sak: let something go on) (e:a nuntakna haksa mah ~ hoh in) (s:zomzomsak) (b:zom) (r:18.14.6) (q:draft)
zomsuak = (t:v) (w:continue/keep on/carry through) (d:zom, continue, with suak, through: go on with something without stopping, carry it through to the end) (e:na ki-itna uh na ~ un/na patsa uh thu a bei dongin ~ unla | carry on what you began until it is finished/a thuhilh zankim ciang dong a ~ hi | he kept on teaching until midnight) (s:zom/zomlai) (a:tawp) (r:58.13.1/47.8.11/44.20.7) (q:draft)
zomto = (t:v) (w:carry on/continue/keep up) (d:zom, continue, with to, onward: carry on what others began; innkuan zomto is carry on a family line) (e:i pu i pate’ maban ~ vet un/A sanggampa’ innkuan a ~ lo mipa | the man who will not carry on his brother's family) (s:zom) (b:zom) (r:40.23.32/5.25.9) (q:draft)
zomzom = (t:v) (w:go on and on/continue) (d:zom, continue, doubled for an action that keeps going on and on) (e:Paul in a thugen ~ ahih manin) (s:zomlai) (r:44.20.9) (q:draft)
zomzomsak = (t:v) (w:let go on/let continue) (d:zomzom, go on and on, with the causative sak: let something keep going) (e:a nuntak haksapi mah ~ hoh in) (s:zomsak) (b:zomzom) (r:18.14.6) (q:draft)
zon = (t:v) (w:seek/search/look for) (d:form of zong used before a suffix or another word, usually written with a final apostrophe) (e:~’ hun om a, mansuah hun om hi/Topa ~’ ding a lungsim ah koih lo | he did not set his heart on seeking the Lord/a kiseel sum manpha ~’ bangin | as one searches for hidden treasure/ka ~’ hangin amah kimu lo hi | though I looked for him, he could not be found/teci a ~’ uh hangin | though they looked for evidence) (s:kan) (r:21.3.6/14.12.14/20.2.4/19.37.36/41.14.55) (q:draft)
zong = (t:adv) (w:also) (d:placed after the word or phrase it adds: this one as well as those already named) (e:Zingsol ~ amah ka pia ding hi/Galkapte ~ pai uh a | the soldiers also came/a nungzuite ~ lawmvakna-ah a sam uh hi | they also invited his disciples to the wedding/Na sanggampa uh ~ sam-in ding un la | take your brother also and set out) (r:66.2.28/42.23.36/43.2.2/1.43.13)
zong = (t:adv) (w:in addition) (d:adds a further person or thing to those already mentioned) (e:huih lak vasate ~ nupa kop sagih | and in addition seven pairs of the birds of the air/ganhing tampi ~ amau tawh pai uh hi | many animals also went with them/Singkha singzawlte ~ bawl a | he also made poles of acacia wood/a khuampeek nih ~ a bawl uh hi | they also made two frames) (r:1.7.3/2.12.38/2.37.4/2.36.28)
zong = (t:adv) (w:too) (d:shows that what was said of one person or thing is true of another) (e:A nung ciangin numei ~ a si hi | finally the woman died too/No Ethiopia mite ~ | you Cushites too/Amah in amah ~ that hi | he put him to death too/Faro’ innkuante in ~ za hi | Pharaoh's household heard it too) (r:42.20.32/36.2.12/1.38.10/1.45.2)
zong = (t:adv) (w:as well) (d:placed after the subject: this one does the same as another) (e:Lot in ~ tuuhon, ganhon, le puanbukte nei hi | Lot had flocks, herds and tents as well/Jethro ~ ama’ gamah a ciah hi | Jethro went back to his own land as well/Jakob ~ ama lampi-ah paisuak a | Jacob went on his way as well/Noah in ~ Topa’ thupiak khempeuh a hih hi | Noah as well did all that the Lord commanded) (r:1.13.5/2.18.27/1.32.1/1.7.5)
zong = (t:v) (w:look/seek/look for/search for) (d:try to find someone or something; Topa zong is seek the Lord, and thah dingin zong is seek to kill) (e:Topa leh ama hatna ~ un la/thah dingin ~ hi | he seeks to kill him/hahkatin pilna ~ in | search diligently for wisdom/ka ngaihno ka ~ a | I looked for my beloved/kei hong ~ ding uh hi | they will seek me) (s:kan) (r:13.16.11/19.37.32/20.2.4/22.3.2/28.5.15) looking for something such as a job or an object
zonga = (t:v) (w:seek/look for) (d:zong seek, with the linking a: i zonga, we sought and; not the adverb zong, also) (e:Nopna i ~ nopna hong pai lo hi) (r:24.8.15) (q:draft)
zongin = (t:conj) (w:although/but/yet/even if) (d:zong, also or even, with in: after a verb, although or even if; ahi zongin at the start of a clause is but or yet, and after each of several nouns it is whether or) (e:Ahi ~ tu-in na ngah dinga/satpiang tampi na zang ~ | although you use much soap/ahi ~ thuzuau gente lawnkhia hi | but he overthrows those who speak lies/tagah ahi ~ na gimsak kei ding uh hi | or an orphan, you shall not mistreat them/Ahi ~ ama hun sung khempeuh | yet all his life) (s:napi/hinapi) (r:18.36.17/24.2.22/20.22.12/2.22.22/11.15.14)
zongkhia = (t:v) (w:search out/track down/find) (d:zong, seek, with khia, out: search until the person or thing is found) (e:amah ka ~ teitei ding hi) (s:kankhia) (b:zong) (r:9.23.23) (q:draft)
zongkik = (t:v) (w:seek again/look for again) (d:zong seek, with kik again) (e:lampi mah limtakin ~ un/zi ~ kei in | do not look for a wife again) (s:kankik) (b:zong) (r:24.31.21/46.7.27) (q:draft)
zongpa = (t:n) (w:seeker/one who seeks/searcher) (d:zong seek with pa, the one who does it: he who seeks or searches) (e:Lungsim sung a ~ in Kha Siangtho’ lungsim/Pilna a ~ in | the one who seeks wisdom/ama adingin thusia ~ ahi hi | he is one who seeks trouble for himself/siatna a ~ ahi hi | he is one who seeks harm) (b:zong) (r:45.8.27/20.19.8/20.29.24/20.26.6) (q:draft)
zongpah = (t:v) (w:seek at once/begin to look for) (d:zong seek, with pah at once, straight away) (e:hunhoih a ~ hi) (r:40.26.16) (q:draft)
zongpahin = (t:v) (w:seek at once/look for straight away) (d:zongpah seek at once, with the linking suffix in) (e:a u Simon ~ ama kiangah) (b:zongpah) (r:43.1.41) (q:draft)
zongpak = (t:v) (w:hurry to seek/seek quickly) (d:zong seek, with pak quickly) (e:bukna ka ~ ding hi) (r:19.55.8) (q:draft)
zongsak = (t:v) (w:order a search/have someone search for/cause to seek) (d:zong seek with sak cause: have someone look for a person or thing; mawhna zongsak, have charges brought) (e:Herod in amah ~ a/a meel hoih nungak khangnote ~ in | have beautiful young women sought/ama lang khatah mawhna ~ in | have them bring a charge against him/na topa hong ~ in | let them search for your master/laibu koihna innte sung ~ in | have a search made in the archives) (b:zong) (r:44.12.19/17.2.2/11.21.10/12.2.16/15.5.17) (q:draft)
zongsang = (t:v) (w:be accustomed/be used to/make a habit of) (d:be practised in something or given to it through constant doing) (e:siatna bawl ding a ~ khin note/mawhna ah a ~ kei hi | he does not make a habit of sin/zakna muhnate zangin ~ a | by using their senses they have become practised) (r:24.13.23/62.3.6/58.5.14) (q:draft)
zongsatna = (t:n) (w:habit/addiction/depravity) (d:something a person has grown used to and is mastered by; here of evil habits that bring ruin) (e:siatna a piangsak thei ~ lelin) (r:61.2.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
zongtawm = (t:v) (w:forage/search for) (d:zong seek, with tawm by oneself: look for what one needs wherever it can be found) (e:a an ding uh ~ uh a) (r:18.24.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
zongte = (t:n) (w:those who seek/seekers) (d:zong seek with plural te; the people who look for or try to get someone or something) (e:nangmah hong ~ nusia lo na hih manin/kei thah dingin a hong ~ | those who seek to kill me/Dikna a zui, Topa a ~ aw | you who pursue righteousness and seek the Lord/Nangmah hong ~ khempeuh lungdamin | may all who seek you rejoice) (r:19.9.10/19.70.4/19.63.9/23.51.1) (q:draft)
zongun = (t:conj) (w:even though/although/even if) (d:zong even, also, with un for a plural subject, closing a clause) (e:lungkhauh mite ka hita ~/ka mai-ah a hong ding zawzen ~ | even if they were to stand before me) (s:napi) (b:zong) (r:2.34.9/24.15.1) (q:draft)
zongzaw = (t:v) (w:seek rather/seek instead/seek all the more) (d:zong, seek, with zaw, rather or more) (e:midangte’ phattuam nading ~ un/a gim ngah nading uh a ~ ahi hi | he is seeking their ruin instead/bangzahin tu-in hong ~ kan ding ahi hiam | how much more will he now seek me) (b:zong) (r:46.10.24/24.38.4/10.16.11) (q:draft)
zongzong = (t:v) (w:keep seeking/look for/search for) (d:zong seek said twice, for seeking that goes on or is done persistently) (e:Bang ~ na hi hiam/Migilote in siat nading bek ~ a | the wicked look only for ways to harm/kei hong sukna ding thu ~ a | he keeps looking for grounds against me/kihisak-a paupaute, buaina ~ ahi hi | those who speak proudly are looking for trouble) (s:kan) (r:1.37.15/20.16.27/20.17.19/18.33.10) (q:draft)
zonkhiatsak = (t:v) (w:search out for/find for) (d:zon seek, with khiat out and sak for another: search out something for someone) (e:amaute a dingin ka ~) (s:zonsak) (r:26.20.6) (q:draft)
zonkik = (t:v) (w:seek again/return to seek) (d:zon seek, with kik again, back) (e:kei hong ~ mateng) (s:kankik) (b:zon) (r:28.5.15) (q:draft)
zonna = (t:n) (w:seeking/search) (d:the act of seeking or looking for something; with ding, a means or purpose of seeking) (e:pilna ~ ding sum tampi/Kei tawh kitotna ding a ~ thei un | see how he is seeking a quarrel with me/a lamlah ding a ~ | his seeking of guidance/A nuntakna ding uh an a ~ lamun | while searching for food to keep themselves alive) (b:zon) (r:20.17.16/12.5.7/13.10.13/25.1.19) (q:draft)
zonpih = (t:v) (w:help look for/seek together with) (d:zon seek, with pih together with) (e:Amah hong ~ nung) (b:zon) (r:22.6.1) (q:draft)
zonsak = (t:v) (w:seek for/find for/provide) (d:zon seek with sak, here doing it for someone else: look for and get something on behalf of another) (e:amaute a dingin zi zong a ~ hi/A tawlngak nading mun uh a ~ dingin | to find them a place to rest/vankahthei numei khat kei a dingin hong ~ un | find me a woman who is a medium/a omna ding uh mun ka ~ ding hi | I will find a place for them to stay) (s:zonkhiatsak) (b:zon) (r:14.11.23/26.34.15/4.10.33/9.28.7) (q:draft)
zontheih = (t:v) (w:be able to seek/can seek) (d:zon, seek, with theih, can, the form used before nading: so that one can seek or find) (e:na min hong ~ nadingin/paulap a ~ nading uh om lo hi | they have no way to find an excuse/Topa a ~ nadingun | so that they may seek the Lord) (b:zon) (r:19.83.16/45.1.20/44.15.16) (q:draft)
zonzaw = (t:v) (w:seek more/search for rather) (d:zon seek, with zaw more: seek one thing more than another) (e:sih ding a lim ~) (b:zon) (r:18.3.21) (q:draft)
zonzon = (t:v) (w:keep searching/search and search/look for) (d:zon, form of zong seek, doubled to show continued or repeated searching) (e:ka ~ hangin ka mu zo kei hi/na thugen dingte uh na ~ laitakun | while you were searching for words/Kei a hong hehpih ding mi ka ~ hangin | though I looked for someone to pity me/a sihtheih nading uh a ~ uh hangin | though they seek a way to die) (s:kan) (r:22.3.2/19.37.36/18.32.11/19.69.20/66.9.6) (q:draft)
zop = (t:v) (w:carry on/continue) (d:form of zom join or continue used before ding, zawh and nading; to carry on a name or go on with a work; zop zawh is be able to carry through, to finish) (e:inn a ~ zawh kei leh/min Israel sungah a ~ ding ut lo hi | he is unwilling to carry on the name in Israel/na ~ paisuak kei uhleh | if you do not continue in it) (r:42.14.29/5.25.7/45.11.22) (q:draft)
zop = (t:v) (w:share in/join in) (d:to be joined to something and so have a part in it) (e:eite in i ~ nadingin) (r:58.12.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
zopa = (t:n) (w:one who is able/he who can) (d:zo be able with pa, the one who: follows a verb, as honkhia zopa, the one who is able to save) (e:sihna pan a honkhia ~ kiangah/hel khua sungah a khul ~ | the one who can destroy in hell) (s:theipa) (r:58.5.7/40.10.28) (q:draft)
zopa = (t:n) (w:conqueror/victor/one who subdues) (d:zo win or defeat with pa: the one who defeated or subdues) (e:Moab gam sungah Midian a ~/ka nuai-ah mite a ~ ahi hi | he is the one who subdues peoples under me) (b:zo) (r:13.1.46/19.144.2) (q:draft)
zopna = (t:n) (w:sharing/partnership/fellowship) (d:zop join or share in, with the noun suffix na) (e:Upna na ~ a vanglian-in) (s:kizopna) (b:zop) (r:57.1.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
zoppihte = (t:n) (d:zop join, with pih together with and the plural te: those joined with one; laigui zoppihte, those of the same umbilical cord, are brothers born of the same mother) (e:ka sanggam, ka laigui ~ ahi uh hi) (r:7.8.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
zoptheih = (t:v) (w:be able to continue) (d:zop continue, with theih be able; used before nading) (e:a khualzinna uh nuamtakin a ~ nadingun/nuamtakin a khualzin a hong ~ nadingin | so that he may continue his journey in peace) (b:zop) (r:64.1.6/46.16.11) (q:draft)
Zorah = (t:name) (c:land/city) (w:Zorah) (d:town in the lowland of Judah allotted to the tribe of Dan, the home of Manoah, father of Samson) (r:6.19.41/16.11.29)
zosak = (t:v) (w:bring to completion/make complete) (d:zo, finish, with the causative sak: bring a work to its completion) (e:hong ~ ding hi ci-in ka lungkim hi) (s:kicingsak) (b:zo) (r:50.1.6) (q:draft)
zosak = (t:v) (w:give victory over/make win) (d:zo, win, with the causative sak: make someone win, give victory over enemies) (e:na galte khempeuh ka hong ~ hi) (s:gualzosak) (a:guallelhsak) (b:zo) (r:10.7.9) (q:draft)
zosakhi = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:antelope/ibex) (d:a clean wild animal of the deer or goat kind, named in a list beside sakhi deer; which animal is meant is not certain) (e:sathak, saza, ~, le gamtuu ahi hi) (r:5.14.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
zosiang = (t:v) (w:finish/complete) (d:zo finish, with siang clean: bring a matter fully to an end) (e:hih thu na ~ un) (s:mansiang/zawhkhit/mankhit) (b:zo) (r:47.8.11) (q:draft)
zota = (t:v) (d:zo be able, finish, with ta marking a change now complete, placed after another verb: has now come to pass, have now managed to) (e:a minthanna teng a maimang ~ hi/daitakin ka om dide ~ hi | I have now come to be calm and still) (b:zo) (r:25.1.6/19.131.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
zote = (t:n) (w:those who are able/those who manage) (d:zo be able or succeed with plural -te, after a verb: those who manage to do it, as a thuak zote, those who endure) (e:A tawp dongin a thuak ~ in/Kampau a ki-ip ~, lungkhamna tawh kipelh hi | those who can guard their speech keep clear of trouble/thu a mang ~ in na mang ta un | let those who can accept this accept it/Zi a mu ~ na hoih a mu hi | those who find a wife find a good thing) (b:zo) (r:41.13.13/20.18.22/20.21.23/40.19.12) (q:draft)
zothawhin = (t:v) (w:overpower/get the better of) (d:zo overcome, with thawh and the linking suffix in) (e:Mite in kote hong ~ gamlakah) (r:10.11.23) (q:draft, low confidence)
Zozabad = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Jozabad) (d:a head of the Levites in Jerusalem in the time of Nehemiah, in charge of the outside work of the house of God) (r:16.11.16)
zozaw = (t:v) (w:prevail/overcome/triumph) (d:zo win with zaw more: be the stronger, get the upper hand) (e:Topa’ vangliatna in kei hong ~ hi/a hehpihna in ~ ding hi | his mercy will prevail/amah in nang hong ~ ding hi | he will prevail over you/kumpipa’ kamgente in Joab le galkap ukte ~ hi | the king's word prevailed over Joab and the army commanders) (s:gualzo/zozo) (a:lel/guallel) (b:zo) (r:26.3.14/59.2.13/17.6.13/10.24.4) (q:draft)
zozaw = (t:v) (w:be more able/can all the more) (d:after a verb, zo be able with zaw more: be able to do it even more, how much more) (e:kihel khawm kuaitan ~ ding ahi hiam/na tam semkhia ~ ding a | will be able to accomplish far more) (s:theizaw) (r:24.15.12/58.9.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
zozo = (t:v) (w:overcome/prevail/tame) (d:reduplicated zo, win or be able; with a negative, cannot manage at all) (e:lunghimawh kei un, leitung ka ~ hi/kuamah in a ~ kei hi | no one can tame it/inn lamding kipan napi-in ~ lo hi | he began to build but could not finish/kua in eite hong ~ ding ahi hiam | who can prevail against us) (s:gualzo) (a:lel/guallel) (b:zo) (r:43.16.33/59.3.8/42.14.30/45.8.31) (q:draft)
zu = (t:n) (w:wine/strong drink/beer) (d:fermented drink that can make a person drunk; zu kham is be drunk, and kham theih zu is strong drink) (e:kham theih ~ nek a hatte/~ ne-a a tut khote | those who sit long over drink/Ammon in ~ a kham hun | when Amnon is drunk with wine/~ khamna in haina ahi hi | getting drunk is folly) (s:khamtheihzu) (r:23.5.22/20.23.30/10.13.28/20.20.1) (q:draft)
zu = (t:v) (w:rain/fall) (d:of rain, fall; guah zu, it rains) (e:leitungah guah ~ hi/Topa hong heh-in guah ~ loin | the Lord will be angry and no rain will fall/vantung panin guah ~ hi | rain fell from the sky/guah tampi tak a ~ sak hi | he makes heavy rain fall/Ka thuhilhna in guahmal bangin ~-in | let my teaching fall like rain) (s:guahzu) (r:1.7.12/5.11.17/7.5.4/18.37.6/5.32.2) (q:draft)
zuahzuah = (t:adv) (w:freely/generously/lavishly) (d:placed after a verb of giving or distributing: give out widely without holding back) (e:Amah in hawmkhia ~ a/citna tawh mizawngte pia ~ a | he gives freely to the poor) (s:ziahziah) (a:tawmkha) (r:19.112.9/47.9.9) (q:draft)
zuahzuahte = (t:n) (w:freewill offerings/things freely given) (d:zuahzuah freely, with the plural te, after a verb of giving: the things given freely) (e:lungkim takin a piakkhiat ~ uh tawh) (b:zuahzuah) (r:15.7.16) (q:draft)
zuak = (t:v) (w:sell) (d:give something to another person for money; also sell a person as a slave, as in sila-in zuak) (e:Izipt gamah a ~ uh hi/sumbukte tungah tuate ~ hi | she sells them to the merchants/a tanu sila-in a ~ ciangin | when he sells his daughter as a slave/a leitang uh ~ lo uh hi | they did not sell their land/Ishmael mite kiangah amah ~ ni | let us sell him to the Ishmaelites) (s:sumzuak) (a:sumlei) (r:44.7.9/20.31.24/2.21.7/1.47.22/1.37.27) (q:draft)
zuakin = (t:v) (w:sell) (d:zuak, sell, with the linking ending in: sell something and then do the next action) (e:a neih khempeuh ~ tua lo a va lei/a sathau ~ na leibate loh in | sell the oil and pay your debts/na neihsa teng ~ mizawngte na pia in | sell what you have and give to the poor/Hih paknamtui dangka zathum tawh ~ | selling this perfume for three hundred silver coins) (b:zuak) (r:40.13.44/12.4.7/40.19.21/43.12.5) (q:draft)
zuakkhia = (t:v) (w:sell off/export) (d:zuak, sell, with khia, out: sell something off, or sell goods on to other countries) (e:A neihsa a ~ pa in/Syria kumpite khempeuh tungah ~ uh hi | they sold them on to all the kings of Syria) (b:zuak) (r:26.7.13/11.10.29) (q:draft)
zuakkhiat = (t:v) (w:sell off/sell/export) (d:zuak, sell, with khiat, out or away; the form of zuakkhia used before ding and similar words) (e:tuate ~ dingin pammaih lua hi/amaute in ~ kik dingin | so that they could sell them on again) (b:zuakkhia) (r:20.23.23/14.1.17) (q:draft)
zuakkhit = (t:v) (w:have sold/finish selling) (d:zuak sell, with khit finished; zuakkhit ciangin is after selling) (e:na ~ ciangin a sum zong) (r:44.5.4) (q:draft)
zuakkik = (t:v) (w:sell back) (d:zuak, sell, with kik, back: sell someone back to her family, so that she is bought back) (e:a pa kiang mahah ~ ding hi) (a:leikik) (b:zuak) (r:2.21.8) (q:draft)
zuakma = (t:see) <zuakma-in>
zuakma-in = (t:adv) (w:before selling) (d:zuak sell, with ma before and in: before it was sold) (e:Tua lo na ~ nangma) (r:44.5.4) (q:draft)
zuakna = (t:n) (w:sale/selling) (d:the act of selling; a zuakna mipa is the man it was sold to, zuakna mun the place sold to) (e:a gamluah a ~ pan a sum ngahte/a ~ mipa tungah | to the man he sold it to/amaute na ~ uh mun | the place where you sold them/tua ni-in a an ~ uh hangin | because of their selling food on that day) (s:sumzuakna) (a:leina) (b:zuak) (r:5.18.8/3.25.27/29.3.7/16.13.15) (q:draft)
zuakpa = (t:n) (w:seller/merchant/trader) (d:zuak, sell, with pa, the man who sells; sum zuakpa is a merchant) (e:Van leipa in van ~ kiangah/sum ~ tawh kibang hi | it is like a merchant/an a ~ amah ahi hi | he was the one who sold grain) (s:vanzuakpa/sumbawlpa) (a:leipa) (b:zuak) (r:20.20.14/40.13.45/1.42.6) (q:draft)
zuakpahte = (t:n) (w:those who sell readily) (d:zuak sell, with pah at once and the plural te: those who sell without holding back) (e:leinop hunin a ~ kiphat hi) (r:20.11.26) (q:draft)
zuaksa = (t:adj) (w:sold) (d:zuak, sell, with sa, already done; that which has been sold) (e:a ~ van ngah kik lo ding hi/a sanggampa ~ tanh ding hi | he shall redeem what his brother has sold) (s:kizuaksa) (a:leisa) (b:zuak) (r:26.7.13/3.25.25) (q:draft)
zuaksawn = (t:v) (w:sell on/resell) (d:zuak, sell, with sawn, pass on: sell on to another what one has bought) (e:Seba minamte tungah ~ ding uh hi/Egypt gamah sal dingin a na ~ uh hi | they sold him on to Egypt as a slave) (r:29.3.8/44.7.9) (q:draft)
zuakte = (t:n) (w:sellers/those who sell) (d:zuak sell with the plural te: the people who sell something) (e:Vakhu ~ kiangah zong/na nam tuamtuam a ~ | sellers of all kinds of goods/bawngte, tuute, vakhute a ~ | those who were selling cattle, sheep and doves/vanleite leh van ~ | buyers and sellers) (s:sumzuakte) (a:leite) (b:zuak) (r:43.2.16/16.13.20/43.2.14/23.24.2) (q:draft)
zuaktheih = (t:v) (w:be able to sell) (d:zuak sell, with theih can; used before nading) (e:I mangbuhte i ~ nadingin) (b:zuak) (r:30.8.5) (q:draft)
zual = (t:adj) (w:tame/tamed) (d:of an animal, used to people, broken in; zual nai lo is not yet tamed, wild) (e:la a ~ nai lo bang ding a) (a:gamsung) (r:1.16.12) (q:draft)
zualsak = (t:v) (w:tame/subdue) (d:zual, tame, with the causative sak: make a wild animal tame) (e:kuamah in ~ zo lo/mite in a ~ zo uh hi | people have been able to tame them) (b:zual) (r:18.39.7/59.3.7) (q:draft)
zualsakin = (t:v) (w:tame) (d:zualsak, tame, with the linking ending in: tame something and then do the next action) (e:ganhing khempeuh ~ ukzo uh hi/leii pen ~ a ukzo kuamah om lo hi | no one can tame the tongue and rule it) (b:zualsak) (r:59.3.7/59.3.8) (q:draft)
zuan = (t:v) (w:go to/head for/make for/turn to) (d:move toward a place or person; with kiang, go or come to a person, as in Pasian kiang zuan, draw near to God) (e:a dawnngekte in Gunpi lam ~ hi/Zeisu kiang ~ dingin tui tungah a pai hi | he walked on the water to go to Jesus/Tarshish khua a ~ ding teembaw khat | a ship bound for Tarshish/Abimelek in amah ~ nai lo hi | Abimelek had not yet gone near her/Pasian kiang a ~ mite | those who draw near to God) (s:manawh) (r:19.80.11/22.2.8/40.14.29/32.1.3/1.20.4/58.10.1) (q:draft)
zuanin = (t:v) (w:heading for/making for/going to) (d:zuan, head for, with the linking ending in: making for a place while another action follows) (e:Jerusalem khuapi ~ a zin hi/Gilgal panin inn ~ lamkal-a om | they were on the road from Gilgal, heading home/i gam ciat ~ ciah ni | let us each go back to our own land/Ammon gam lam ~ a paikhiatpih hi | he took them away toward the land of Ammon) (b:zuan) (r:42.13.22/12.2.1/24.51.9/24.41.10) (q:draft)
zuankik = (t:v) (w:return to/go back to/turn back toward) (d:zuan, head for, with kik, back or again: go back to the place or person one came from) (e:na khuapi uh hong ~ un/a muanhuai na mun ngei uh ~ un | return to your former place of safety/Pa kiang a ~ ding ka hi hi | I am going back to the Father/a kulhpi ~ dingin a gamah hong ciah ding | he will go home to return to his fortress/salsuahna panin inn hong ~ mite | those who had come back home from captivity) (s:ciahkik/paikik) (b:zuan) (r:24.31.21/38.9.12/43.16.28/27.11.19/15.8.35) (q:draft)
zuanpah = (t:v) (w:head for at once/go straight to) (d:zuan go to, with pah at once) (e:tua lai a va ~ ahi hi) (r:23.37.8) (q:draft)
zuansak = (t:v) (w:let go to/cause to go to/send to) (d:zuan, head for, with the causative sak: make or let someone go to a place or person) (e:na pate kiang nang kong ~ ding/a Pasian kiang uh ~ thei lo hi | does not let them go back to their God/Leinuai nong ~ kei a | you will not let me go down to the realm of the dead) (b:zuan) (r:12.22.20/28.5.4/19.16.10) (q:draft)
zuansuk = (t:v) (w:go down to/head down to) (d:zuan go to, with suk downward) (e:Lonona kuamsung a ~ bawngte bangin) (s:paisuk) (b:zuan) (r:23.63.14) (q:draft)
zuante = (t:n) (w:those who come to/those who go to) (d:zuan go to, with the plural te) (e:Pasian kiang a ~ khempeuh) (b:zuan) (r:58.7.25) (q:draft)
Zuar = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zuar) (d:father of Nethanel, the leader of the tribe of Issachar in the wilderness) (r:4.7.18/4.10.15)
zuat = (t:v) (w:go to/head for/return to) (d:make one's way toward a place or person; the form used in dependent clauses and before nading) (e:tuikhuk a ~ uh leh tui/bawngtal in a sih nading mun a ~ bangin | like an ox going to the place of its death/na pate kiang na ~ ciangin | when you go to your fathers/amaute in inn lam a ~ uh ciangin | when they were heading home) (s:manawh) (r:24.14.3/20.26.11/20.7.22/13.17.11/9.18.6) (q:draft)
zuatkik = (t:v) (w:return to/go back to) (d:zuat, head for, with kik, back or again) (e:Ui in a luak a ~ bangin/mothak in a pasal kiang a ~ mah bangin | just as a bride returns to her husband/a ~ nop uh ahi Judah gamah | to the land of Judah, to which they long to return) (b:zuat) (r:20.26.11/10.17.3/24.44.14) (q:draft)
zuatna = (t:n) (w:way to/going to) (d:the act of heading for a place; with lampi or lam, the road that leads to a place) (e:Zion ~ lampi a om mite/sihna gam ~ hi a | it is the way to the land of death/A inn ~ ding lampi a thei lo | who does not know the way to his home/ka topa’ behte’ inn ~ lampi-ah | on the way to the house of my master’s relatives) (b:zuat) (r:19.84.5/20.7.27/21.10.15/1.24.27) (q:draft)
zuau = (t:v) (w:evil/lie/deceive/tell lies) (d:say what is not true; often with gen, speak, as zuau gen, tell a lie, and before a noun, as zuau teci, a false witness) (e:~ gen mi suakta lo ding hi/A ~ dingin Pasian in mihing hi lo hi | God is not a man, that he should lie/~ genna panin na muk kem in | keep your lips from telling lies/khatlekhat tungah ~ na kigen kei ding uh hi | you shall not lie to one another) (s:zuaugen/khem) (r:20.19.5/19.34.13/4.23.19/3.19.11)
zuau-tatin = (t:v) (w:be unfaithful/act falsely) (d:zuau lie, with tat act and the linking suffix in; the same word as zuautat) (e:Amaute ~ citak lo uh hi) (r:28.7.4) (q:draft)
zuaugen = (t:v) (w:lie/tell lies/deceive) (d:zuau, false, with gen, speak: say what is not true; zuaugen mi is a liar) (e:Topa in ~ mite mudah a/a leii uh tawh ama tungah ~ uh hi | they lied to him with their tongues/~ mi in sihna thuak ding hi | one who tells lies will perish/~ nuamsa-in zuau a gengen mite | those who love lying and keep telling lies) (s:zuau) (r:20.12.22/62.2.4/19.78.36/20.19.9/66.22.15) (q:draft)
zuaugen = (t:n) (w:liar) (d:one who tells lies; also said as zuaugen mi and zuaugen pa) (e:Pasian pen ~ a suaksak/na khuasung mi khempeuh uh ~ vive ahi uh a | all the people of your city are liars/Thuman gen hinapi-in ~ bangin hong kingaihsun a | though we speak the truth, we are regarded as liars) (s:Mizuau/thuzuaupa) (r:62.1.10/62.5.10/33.6.12/47.6.8) (q:draft)
zuaugenin = (t:v) (w:lie/tell lies) (d:zuaugen tell lies, with the linking suffix in) (e:zong ~ nitum ding uh hi) (b:zuaugen) (r:20.29.12) (q:draft)
zuaugenna = (t:n) (w:lying/lie/falsehood) (d:zuaugen, tell lies, with the noun suffix na) (e:~ tawh hauhnate beimang pak a/Migilote in a ~ uh awkpih a | evildoers are trapped by their own lying) (s:zuauna/zuauthu/thuzuau) (b:zuaugen) (r:20.21.6/20.12.13) (q:draft)
zuaugente = (t:n) (w:liars) (d:zuaugen liar, with the plural te) (e:le ~ om nading mun) (s:mizuaute/zuautheite) (b:zuaugen) (r:66.21.8) (q:draft)
zuauna = (t:v) (w:evil/lie/deceive) (e:thuman genna sangin ~ na deihzaw hi) (b:zuau) (r:19.52.3)
zuauna = (t:n) (w:falsehood/lie/deceit) (d:zuau, lie, with the noun suffix na: what is false, lying or deceit) (e:~ ah i bu hi/thuman genna sangin ~ na deihzaw hi | you love falsehood rather than speaking the truth/~ leh khemna bekbek tawh | with nothing but lies and deceit/Gulpi in ama ~ tawh Evua a kheem | the serpent deceived Eve with his lies) (s:zuauthu/thuzuau/zuaupi) (a:thutak/thumanna) (b:zuau) (r:19.52.3/23.28.15/28.11.12/47.11.3)
zuaunate = (t:n) (w:falsehoods) (d:zuauna, falsehood, with the plural te) (e:~ zadahin ka kih a) (s:zuauthute) (b:zuauna) (r:19.119.163)
Zuaunate = (t:n) (w:falsehoods/lies) (d:zuaunate written with a capital at the start of a sentence) (e:~ zadahin ka kih a) (s:zuauthute) (b:zuaunate) (r:19.119.163) (q:draft)
zuauphuah = (t:n) (w:intrigue/deceit/fabrication) (d:zuau lie with phuah make up: the making up of lies) (e:~ siamna tawh a hih khempeuh/~ hat kumpi khat a hong om ding hi | a king strong in intrigue will arise) (s:zuausiamna/khemsiamna) (r:27.8.25/27.8.23) (q:draft)
zuaupi = (t:n) (w:lie/falsehood/great lie) (d:zuau, lie, with pi, great: something wholly false or empty) (e:a kisialhna teng ~ hi-in/a kiciam uh hangin a ~ uh ahi hi | though they swear, it is a lie/Amaute’ maangmuhnate in ~ hi a | their visions are false/a ~ teng uh tawh kumpipa lungdamsak uh a | they make the king glad with all their lies) (s:zuauthu/thuzuau) (b:zuau) (r:24.48.30/24.5.2/26.13.6/28.7.3) (q:draft)
zuaupiteng = (t:n) (w:lies/all the lies) (d:zuaupi lie, with teng all) (e:a ~ uh tawh kumpipa lungdamsak) (b:zuaupi) (r:28.7.3) (q:draft)
zuausiamna = (t:n) (w:intrigue/deceit/cunning) (d:zuau lie, with siam skilled and the noun suffix na: skill in lying) (e:~ tawh kumpi a hong suakvat) (s:zuauphuah/khemsiamna) (r:27.11.21) (q:draft)
zuautat = (t:v) (w:be unfaithful/act treacherously/deal falsely) (d:zuau, lie, with tat, act: break faith with God or with people, act disloyally) (e:a ~ mite ahih leh puk ding uh hi/Haksat hunin a ~ mi muan-a neih khakna | relying on an unfaithful person in a time of trouble/i Pasian tungah hong ~ ding ka hi uh hiam | are we to be unfaithful to our God/a ki-ap nate tawh kisai-in ~ uh hi | they were unfaithful in regard to the devoted things) (r:20.28.18/20.25.19/16.13.27/6.7.1) (q:draft)
zuautatin = (t:v) (w:being unfaithful/acting falsely) (d:zuautat be unfaithful, with in linking it to the next verb) (e:Amaute ~ citak lo uh hi/Nang ~ kei na hong phawk kei hi | you were false and did not remember me) (b:zuautat) (r:28.7.4/23.57.11) (q:draft)
zuautatna = (t:n) (w:unfaithfulness/treachery/falsehood/deceit) (d:zuautat, be unfaithful, with the noun suffix na: acting falsely or disloyally) (e:Hoshea a ~ mu hi/~ in lungkhamna bek piangsak hi | unfaithfulness brings only trouble/Keima ~ in Pasian a thumanna kilangsakin | my falsehood shows up the truthfulness of God) (s:cihtaklohna) (a:cihtakna) (b:zuautat) (r:12.17.4/45.3.7/20.13.15) (q:draft)
zuautatsak = (t:v) (w:cause to be unfaithful/lead astray) (d:zuautat be unfaithful, with causative sak) (e:Topa’ tungah Israel mite ~ hi) (b:zuautat) (r:4.31.16) (q:draft)
zuaute = (t:adj) (w:false/lying) (d:zuau, false, with the plural te, placed after a noun: pasian zuaute is false gods, kamsang zuaute is false prophets) (e:tua bangmahin kamsang ~ a pahtakbawl uh hi/Gamdang pasian ~ lakah | among the false gods of the nations) (s:manlo) (b:zuau) (r:42.6.26/24.14.22) (q:draft)
zuauthei = (t:adj) (w:deceitful/deceiving/lying) (d:zuau, lie, with thei, able or given to; one that deceives) (e:kam sungah ~ kha khat koih khin hi/a lehdo mite, a ~ tapate | rebellious people, deceitful children/Krete gam mite a ~ tawntung | the people of Crete are always liars) (a:citak) (b:zuau) (r:11.22.23/23.30.9/56.1.12) (q:draft)
zuautheite = (t:n) (w:liars/false ones) (d:zuauthei, liar, with plural te; after a noun it means false: kamsang zuautheite is false prophets) (e:Kamsang ~ hong piang ding uh a/~ in zuauthu mah ngaih-in nei hi | liars pay attention to lies/Khazih ~ hong piang ding uh a | false Christs will appear) (s:zuaugente/mizuaute) (b:zuauthei) (r:40.24.11/20.17.4/40.24.24) (q:draft)
zuauthu = (t:n) (w:lie/falsehood/false word) (d:zuau, false, with thu, word: a lie, something said that is not true; zuauthu gen is tell lies) (e:Thuman mi in ~ deih lo a/~ a hilh kamsangte | the prophets who teach lies/Na gen thu khempeuh uh ~ bek hi lel | everything you say is nothing but lies/teci in ~ bekbek gen tawntung hi | the witness always tells nothing but lies) (s:thuzuau/zuauna/zuaupi) (a:thutak) (r:20.13.5/20.6.17/23.9.15/18.21.34/20.14.5) (q:draft)
zuauthute = (t:n) (w:lies/false words/deceptive words) (d:zuauthu, lie, with the plural te) (e:a kicici ~ um kei un/~ a don loh nadingin | so that they pay no attention to lies) (s:zuaunate/Thuzuaute) (b:zuauthu) (r:24.7.4/2.5.9) (q:draft)
zuazua = (t:adv) (w:roaring/with a roar) (d:expressive word placed after a verb for a loud, continuous rushing or roaring, said of water, waves, flames and the noise of a crowd; ging zuazua is roar) (e:tuihualte ging ~ a/tui lianpite phuan ~ hi | the great waters foamed and roared/Lei nuai-a om tuite ging ~ a | the waters under the earth roared/mi honpi kiko tawh kibangin a ging ~ hi | it sounded like the roar of a great crowd) (r:24.31.35/35.3.15/35.3.10/27.10.6) (q:draft)
zuazuate = (t:n) (d:zuazua, expressive word for a loud rushing sound or a continuous stream, with plural te making a noun of the phrase before it: ging zuazuate, things that rattle loudly; a piak khiat zuazuate, the things given freely one after another) (e:sakol leeng ging ~ le gamlak) (b:zuazua) (r:29.2.5/15.7.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
Zubeel = (t:n) (w:wine jar/wineskin) (d:zu, wine or beer, with beel, pot: a vessel for wine; written here with a capital at the start of a sentence) (e:~ khempeuh leenggahzu tawh a kidim ding hi) (r:24.13.12) (q:draft)
Zuf = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zuph) (d:ancestor of Elkanah and Samuel, from the hill country of Ephraim; also the district of Zuph through which Saul passed) (r:9.1.1/13.6.35)
zuhai = (t:n) (w:drunkard) (d:zu, liquor: one given to heavy drinking; paired with anhai, glutton) (e:amah in anhai ~ ahi hi) (s:zukhampa/khampa) (r:5.21.20/42.7.34) (q:draft)
zui = (t:v) (w:follow/obey/keep) (d:go after or behind someone, as in a nung zui, follow him; also keep or obey a word, law or teaching) (e:nusia-in a nung a ~ hi/nangma thu ka ~ hi | I keep your law/Ama hong lamlahna citakin ka ~ a | I have faithfully followed his guidance/thukham a ~ lote si ding hi | those who do not keep the commandments will die/Nangma thuhilhnate ka ~ a | I obey your statutes) (s:nungzuih/mang) (a:palsat) (r:42.5.28/19.119.55/18.23.11/20.19.16/19.119.167) (q:draft)
zuibup = (t:v) (w:follow completely/follow wholly) (d:zui follow, with bup whole) (e:a pa David bangin Topa ~ lo hi) (r:11.11.6) (q:draft)
zuih = (t:v) (w:follow/obey/keep/observe) (d:form of zui used before ding, nading, man and in dependent clauses) (e:nangma thupiaknate ~ ding ka zekai kei hi/Baal nung a ~ man uh ahi hi | it is because they followed the Baals/midang kuamah ~ nadingin thu a pia kei hi | he did not allow anyone else to follow him/na thuhilhte ka ~ theih nadingin | so that I may keep your statutes) (s:nungzuih) (a:palsat) (b:zui) (r:19.119.60/24.9.14/41.5.37/19.119.146) (q:draft)
zuihbeh = (t:v) (w:follow/ensue/result) (d:zuih, follow, with beh, in addition: come after as a further consequence) (e:Siatna khatpeuh in a ~ leh/siatna in a ~ kei nakleh | if no further harm follows) (r:2.21.23/2.21.22) (q:draft)
zuihin = (t:v) (w:follow/observe) (d:zuih follow or observe, with the linking suffix in: zuihin nei, hold to as a rule) (e:cihte ~ nei na hi uh hiam) (b:zuih) (r:51.2.21) (q:draft, low confidence)
zuihkhak = (t:v) (w:fall into following/come to follow) (d:zuih follow, with khak happen to: take up the ways of others) (e:mihoih lote’ gamtatna a ~ ciangin/Amau’ hoih lohnate na ~ loh nadingun | so that you do not fall into their evil ways) (r:20.25.26/20.22.25) (q:draft)
zuihlah = (t:v) (w:be unable to follow/fail to keep) (d:zuih follow or keep, with lah fail, not manage) (e:na ~ ding uh zong hi lo hi) (r:5.30.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
zuihlahna = (t:n) (w:failure to keep) (d:zuihlah fail to keep, with the noun suffix na: Thukham zuihlahna, not keeping the Law) (e:Thukham ~ hangin samsiatna panin) (b:zuihlah) (r:48.3.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
zuihlam = (t:n) (w:following) (d:zuih follow, with lam, the fact or manner of: a zuihlam a muh ciangin, when he saw them following) (e:amau tegel in a ~ a muh ciangin) (r:43.1.38) (q:draft, low confidence)
zuihna = (t:n) (w:following/obeying/observance) (d:the act of following or obeying; tuu zuihna is tending sheep) (e:amah ~ panin kihemkhia lo a/Nangmah ngeina kipte ~-ah ka gamtatna kip ta hen | may my ways be steadfast in keeping your decrees/keimah ~ panin na tapate uh amaute in heikhia | they will turn your sons away from following me/Topa ~ panin Israel hawlkhia-in | driving Israel away from following the Lord) (a:palsatna) (b:zuih) (r:12.18.6/19.119.5/5.7.4/12.17.21) (q:draft)
zuihnop = (t:v) (w:want to follow/want to obey) (d:zuih, the form of zui, follow or obey, with nop, want to) (e:Mi khat in thukham a ~ kei leh/a ~ hangin zong zui thei lo hi | even if it wants to obey, it cannot/Mi khatpeuh in kei hong ~ leh | if anyone wants to follow me/amaute’ deihna bek a ~ hun | a time when they want to follow only their own desires) (r:20.28.9/45.8.7/42.9.23/55.4.3) (q:draft)
zuihpah = (t:v) (w:follow at once/go with readily) (d:zuih follow, with pah at once; used before nading) (e:amaute ka ~ nadingin Kha Siangtho in) (r:44.11.12) (q:draft)
zuihpih = (t:v) (w:follow along with/go along with) (d:zuih, follow, with pih, together with: follow a practice along with others, or go with someone along a path) (e:a phuahtawm ngeinate ~ uh hi/amau’ theih ngei loh sul ~-in | going with them along paths they have never known) (s:zuikhawm) (b:zuih) (r:12.17.19/23.42.16) (q:draft)
zuihpihin = (t:v) (w:go along with/lead along) (d:zuihpih follow along with, with the linking suffix in: go with someone along a path) (e:sul ~ ka kha ding hi) (b:zuihpih) (r:23.42.16) (q:draft)
zuihsa = (t:v) (w:have followed/have kept) (d:zuih, follow or keep, with sa, already done: what one has already followed or kept) (e:Hihte khempeuh ka ~ ahi hi/hih thukhamte khempeuh ka ~ ahi hi | I have kept all these commandments/na ~ upna thu le thuhilhna man | the faith and the true teaching that you have followed) (s:zuikhin) (b:zuih) (r:40.19.20/54.4.6/42.18.21) (q:draft)
zuihsak = (t:v) (w:let go with/send along) (d:zuih follow, with causative sak: let someone accompany) (e:amah nong ~ kei leh kote ka paisuk) (s:paikhawmsak) (b:zuih) (r:1.43.5) (q:draft)
zuihtheih = (t:v) (w:be able to follow/be able to obey) (d:zuih follow or obey with theih can; the form used before nading, so that one may follow or obey) (e:ama khekhap na ~ nadingun/Na khanglui ngeina uh na ~ nadingun | so that you can keep your own traditions/Gentail mite in Pasian thu a ~ nadingun | so that the Gentiles might obey God/mi khempeuh in Pasian umin a ~ nadingin | so that all people might believe and obey God) (s:zuihzawh) (b:zuih) (r:60.2.21/41.7.9/45.15.18/45.16.26) (q:draft)
zuihzawh = (t:v) (w:be able to follow/be able to keep) (d:zuih follow, obey, with zawh be able; used before ding and nading) (e:mi khempeuh in a ~ ding hi lo a/ama deihna na ~ nadingun | so that you can carry out his will) (s:zuihtheih) (r:40.19.11/50.2.13) (q:draft)
zuihzawhna = (t:n) (w:keeping/observance) (d:zuihzawh be able to keep, with the noun suffix na; Thukham zuihzawhna is keeping the Law) (e:Thukham ~ hang hi loin upna hang hi/Thukham ~ hangin Pasian tawh kipawl theihna | being right with God through keeping the Law) (b:zuihzawh) (r:45.3.28/48.2.21) (q:draft)
zuikha = (t:v) (w:follow/be led to follow) (d:zui follow with kha happen to: follow by mistake or be drawn into following, often in warnings) (e:Tua bang mite’ nung ~ kei un/Ka mite in thu hoih lo ~ uh ahih manin | because my people have followed what is not good/ngeina man zui lo mite’ khemna ~-in | being carried away by the error of lawless people/Israel-te’ khialhnateng ~ na hih manun | because you followed the sins of Israel) (r:42.21.8/61.3.17/28.11.6/33.1.13) (q:draft)
zuikhawm = (t:v) (w:follow together/go along with) (d:zui follow, with khawm together) (e:tua pa nung a ~ uh hi/dikna, upna, itna leh nopna delhin na ~ in | pursue righteousness, faith, love and peace together with them) (s:zuihpih) (b:zui) (r:40.9.19/55.2.22) (q:draft)
zuikhin = (t:v) (w:have kept/have fulfilled/keep fully) (d:zui, follow or keep, with khin, completely or already) (e:hih thukhamte khempeuh ka ~ hi/Thukham deihna teng a ~ ahi hi | has fulfilled all that the Law requires/a vekpi-in a ~ tawntung lote | those who do not always keep all of it) (s:zuihsa) (b:zui) (r:41.10.20/45.13.8/48.3.10) (q:draft)
zuikik = (t:v) (w:go back with/follow back) (d:zui, follow, with kik, back or again: go back with someone; in Daniel 11:20 follow after in turn, succeed) (e:nadingin kei hong ~ in/kumpi dang khat in ama nung hong ~ | another king will follow after him) (s:lehzuihkik) (b:zui) (r:9.15.30/27.11.20) (q:draft)
zuinuam = (t:v) (w:want to follow/be willing to keep) (d:zui follow or keep, with nuam want to) (e:Thukham ~ tuan lo uh hi) (r:48.6.13) (q:draft)
zuipah = (t:v) (w:follow at once/follow immediately) (d:zui follow with pah, at once, without delay) (e:Jesuh nung a ~ uh hi/a ngen uh nusia-in Jesuh a ~ uh hi | they left their nets and followed Jesus at once/amah zong dingin a ~ hi | he too got up and followed at once/lunghiang loin amaute ~ in | go with them without hesitating) (r:40.20.34/41.1.18/40.9.9/44.10.20) (q:draft)
zuisak = (t:v) (w:let follow/make follow/send along with) (d:zui, follow, with the causative sak: let or make someone follow or go along; also make someone keep a covenant) (e:Kei zong hong ~ in/Ka sanggampa uh hong ~ lecin | if you send our brother with us/kuamah dang, inn sungah ~ lo hi | he let no one else come into the house with him/thuciamna kong ~ ding hi | I will make you keep the covenant) (s:tonsak) (b:zui) (r:42.8.38/1.43.4/42.8.51/26.20.37) (q:draft)
zuisakpa = (t:n) (w:one who makes follow/one who subjects) (d:zuisak make follow with pa marking a male person: the one who made the creation subject, whose will it follows) (e:~’ deihna bang bek a zui uh hi) (b:zuisak) (r:45.8.21) (q:draft, low confidence)
zuisuak = (t:v) (w:go on with/keep following/continue in) (d:zui, follow, with suak, through or onward: go along with someone all the way, keep on following) (e:Balaam in Balak’ uliante a ~ hi/Nang hong ~ lecin | if you go on with me/a ~ mi in thu a zak ciangin | when the one who continues in it hears the word) (r:4.22.35/59.1.25/10.15.33) (q:draft)
zuisuk = (t:v) (w:follow down/go down along/descend with) (d:zui, follow, with suk for movement downward) (e:sihna lampi ~ lo uh hi/a minthan’na in amah ~ lo ding hi | his splendor will not go down with him/ka tapa in note hong ~ lo ding hi | my son will not go down with you/Jordan Gun ~ a | going down along the Jordan River) (a:zuito) (b:zui) (r:20.15.24/19.49.17/1.42.38/26.47.18) (q:draft)
zuite = (t:n) (w:followers/those who follow/those who keep/those who obey) (d:zui, follow or keep, with the plural te, used after a: the people who follow someone or keep a law) (e:Thukham a ~ a khan’ sau ding a/Topa nung a ~ | those who follow the Lord/A mai pai, a nung a ~ in | those who went ahead and those who followed/citakin amah a ~ in | those who faithfully follow him) (s:nungzuite) (b:zui) (r:20.19.16/45.16.11/41.11.9/66.17.14) (q:draft)
zuito = (t:v) (w:follow upward/climb after) (d:zui, follow, with to, upward: follow someone up, or go up along a path or border) (e:Ka nung hong ~ in/Mipilte in nuntakna lampi ~ uh a | the wise follow the path of life upward/Egypt gamgi ~-in | going up along the border of Egypt) (a:zuisuk) (b:zui) (r:9.14.12/20.15.24/26.47.19) (q:draft)
zuizaw = (t:v) (w:follow rather/follow instead) (d:zui follow with zaw rather, more: follow one way in preference to another) (e:Israel kumpite’ khekhap ~ hi) (b:zui) (r:14.28.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
zuizo = (t:v) (w:be able to follow/be able to keep/manage to obey) (d:zui follow or obey with zo be able) (e:mi tawmno bek in a ~ uh hi/Kua in ~ ding ahi hiam | who is able to follow it/nangma ngeina kipte a kicing takin a ~ mi | one who is able to keep your decrees fully/a sehte bek in a ~ ding uh ahi hi | only those appointed will be able to keep it) (s:mangzo) (b:zui) (r:40.7.14/43.6.60/19.119.80/40.19.11) (q:draft)
zuk = (t:v) (w:fall/rain) (d:of rain; the form of zu used before loh, nading, mateng and similar words) (e:guah ~ loh kum ciangin zong/guah a ~ nading mun | the place where rain is to fall/guah ~ loh nading nakpi-in thu a nget ciangin | when he prayed earnestly that it would not rain/guah a ~ loh ciang | when there is no rain) (b:zu) (r:24.17.8/59.5.7/18.28.26/59.5.17/14.7.13) (q:draft)
zukham = (t:adj) (w:drunk/drunken/intoxicated) (d:overcome by zu, alcoholic drink; also used for a drunk person, a drunkard) (e:amaute ~ bangin hoisuk hoito uh a/zu ne lopi-a ~ a bang note | you who seem drunk without having drunk wine/~ thei mi ahi lo | not a man given to drunkenness/nang zong ~ bangin khua na phawk kei ding a | you too will be senseless like a drunkard) (s:kham) (r:19.107.27/23.51.21/56.1.7/34.3.11) (q:draft)
zukhamin = (t:adv) (w:drunk/in a drunken state) (d:zukham, drunk, with the linking ending in) (e:hih mite in ~ a om kei/Eli in tua numei ~ ngaihsun hi | Eli thought the woman was drunk/kumpi sawmthum le nihte tawh ~ a om laitak | while he was getting drunk with the thirty-two kings/Arza’ inn-ah ~ Tirzah-ah a om laitak | while he was in Tirzah, getting drunk in the house of Arza) (b:zukham) (r:44.2.15/9.1.13/11.20.16/11.16.9) (q:draft)
zukhamna = (t:n) (w:drunkenness/intoxication) (d:the state of being drunk; zukhamna pan a pilvan is to wake from a drunken sleep) (e:~ pen haina ahi hi/Noah a ~ pan a pilvan’ ciangin | when Noah awoke from his drunkenness/Gualnopna le ~, mawhna le thangtatna | carousing and drunkenness, immorality and debauchery) (s:khamna) (b:zukham) (r:20.20.1/1.9.24/45.13.13) (q:draft)
zukhampa = (t:n) (w:drunkard/drunken man) (d:zukham drunk with pa marking a male person) (e:~ pen ama luak sung mahah) (s:zuhai/khampa) (b:zukham) (r:23.19.14) (q:draft)
zukhamsak = (t:v) (w:make drunk/intoxicate) (d:zukham drunk with sak, cause to be) (e:tua ahih manin amah ~ hi) (s:khamsak) (b:zukham) (r:10.11.13) (q:draft)
zukhamte = (t:n) (w:drunkards) (d:zukham, drunk, with the plural te: people who get drunk) (e:No ~ aw, tho un la kap un/~ in keimah la-in hong sa uh hi | drunkards make songs about me/~ tawh an ne, zu dawn khawm a | he eats and drinks with drunkards) (s:guite) (b:zukham) (r:29.1.5/19.69.12/40.24.49) (q:draft)
zukna = (t:n) (w:raining/falling of rain) (d:zuk fall, of rain, with the noun suffix na; guah zukna ding mun is the place where rain is to fall) (e:guah ~ ding mun thu pia-in) (s:guahzukna) (b:zuk) (r:18.28.26) (q:draft)
zuksak = (t:v) (w:make rain/send rain/bring rain) (d:zuk, fall as rain, with the causative sak: make rain fall, used with guah, rain) (e:Leilu lam huih in guah a ~ bangin/Topa in leitungah guah a ~ ni matengin | until the day the Lord sends rain on the land/meiite in zong guah a ~ loh nadingin | so that the clouds do not rain on it/a tungah guah ka ~ lohna leitang | a land on which I have sent no rain) (s:guahzusak) (b:zuk) (r:20.25.23/26.22.24/11.17.14/23.5.6) (q:draft)
zuksakna = (t:n) (w:sending of rain/making rain fall) (d:zuksak, make rain fall, with the noun suffix na: the sending of rain; guah zuksakna ding is in order to send rain) (e:guah hong ~ ding nangmah in sawl) (b:zuksak) (r:18.38.34) (q:draft)
zul = (t:todo) (r:26.15.4) (q:draft, one verse only, in a zul kat teng for the charred middle part of a stick whose ends are burnt; the meaning of zul alone is not clear)
zulesa = (t:n) (w:drink and meat) (d:apparently zu, drink, le, and, sa, meat: strong drink and meat as at a feast; zulesa tawh kidiah, soaked with drink and meat, describes people who are drunk) (e:~ tawh kidiahin a om laitakun) (r:34.1.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
zulhtat = (t:adj) (w:unruly/undisciplined/disorderly) (d:lacking restraint or discipline; khuaval zulhtat lo is sober and self-controlled, and thadah zulhtat mite are people who are idle and disorderly) (e:khuaval ~ lo mi, a dik mi/khuaval ~ loh nading na hilh in | teach them to be self-controlled/thadah ~ mite a kikep nadingun na hilh un | warn those who are idle and disorderly/thadahin a ~ ute naute khempeuh na pel un | keep away from every brother who is idle and disorderly) (r:56.1.8/52.5.14/56.2.6/53.3.6) (q:draft)
zulhtatin = (t:adv) (w:in a disorderly way/idly) (d:zulhtat, unruly, with the adverb ending in; thadah zulhtatin gamta is behave in an idle and disorderly way) (e:note lakah thadah ~ ka gamta kei uh hi) (b:zulhtat) (r:53.3.7) (q:draft)
zulhtatna = (t:n) (w:unruliness/wantonness/lack of restraint) (d:zulhtat unruly with the noun suffix na; in the verse the unrestrained conduct of youth that brings shame) (e:na ~ le na meigonna hangin) (b:zulhtat) (r:23.54.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
zulhzau = (t:adj) (w:faithless/backsliding/unfaithful) (d:turning away from the one to whom loyalty is owed and not keeping faith; in Jeremiah said of Israel and of other peoples addressed as an unfaithful daughter) (e:Hong kilehkik in, a ~ Israel aw/Hong kilehkik un, a ~ ka tate aw | return, my faithless children/A ~ numei aw | O unfaithful daughter/a ~ ka tanu aw | my unfaithful daughter) (a:cihtak/citak) (r:24.3.12/24.3.11/24.3.22/24.49.4/24.31.22) (q:draft)
zulhzauna = (t:n) (w:backsliding/faithlessness) (d:zulhzau, faithless, with the noun suffix na: turning away from God, backsliding) (e:na ~ uh kong damsak ding hi) (s:cihtaklohna) (a:cihtakna) (b:zulhzau) (r:24.3.22) (q:draft)
zulim = (t:n) (w:good wine/choice wine) (d:zu wine with lim tasty, parallel to anlim choice food; the verse has new wine) (e:~ nekna in nungakte thadimsak ding hi) (r:38.9.17) (q:draft, low confidence)
zulkatteng = (t:n) (w:charred part/burnt remainder) (d:apparently zul with kat burn and teng all, the whole: the remaining middle of a stick that the fire has charred; written as three words a zul kat teng in the other text) (e:a omlai a ~, bangin kimang nawn) (r:26.15.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
zum = (t:v) (w:be ashamed/feel shame/be put to shame) (d:feel shame; often with mai, face: mai zum is be ashamed or be put to shame, and zum kei is not be ashamed) (e:na mai uh ~ ngei lo ding hi/ka nget ding ka mai a ~ hi | I was ashamed to ask/note na mai uh ~ ding hi | you will be put to shame/na ~ thei kei lailai hi | you still refuse to be ashamed/a galte a vekpi-un a ~ uh hi | all his opponents were ashamed) (s:zahla/kisuang/zahhuai) (r:19.34.5/60.4.16/15.8.22/23.65.13/24.3.3/42.13.17) (q:draft)
zum = (t:n) (w:court/office/law court) (d:government office or court of law, as in zum inn, court house, thukhen zum, law court, and zum nasemte, officials) (e:~ innah hong heekte puanza zong/thukhen ~ tun’ pah kei in | do not hastily go to court/~ sungah a kisel ciangin | when they dispute in court/a langpang dingin ~ nasemte golhguk pia uh hi | they bribed officials to work against them) (r:40.5.40/18.9.32/20.25.8/20.18.18/15.4.5) (q:draft)
zum = (t:adj) (w:pointed/sharp) (d:tapering to a point: mualdawn zum is a mountain peak, ciangkhut zum a pointed goad) (e:mualdawn ~ tampi a nei/ciangkhut ~ tawh Filistia mite zaguk | six hundred Philistines with an ox goad/Mualdawn ~ tampi a nei mual aw | O mountain of many peaks) (r:19.68.15/7.3.31/19.68.16) (q:draft)
zuma = (t:n) (w:of the court/at the court) (d:zum court or office with the marker a, of or at: zuma thukhente are the judges of the court) (e:~ thukhente mai-ah hong kaigawpin) (b:zum) (r:42.12.58) (q:draft, low confidence)
zumah = (t:n) (w:in court/at the court) (d:zum, court or office, with the place marker ah; thukhen zumah is in the law court) (e:Thukhen ~ amah samin hong pai leh/Thukhenna ~, a langpa in a thuk mateng | in court, until the other side answers/Zeisu amau ~ a paipih uh hi | they led Jesus to their council/kuamah thukhen ~ na pai kei uh hi | none of you goes to court) (b:zum) (r:18.9.16/30.5.10/20.18.17/42.22.66/23.59.4) (q:draft)
zumcingte = (t:n) (w:guards/court guards) (d:apparently zum court or office with cing guard and the plural te: those who guard the court; zumcingte omna is the court of the guard) (e:~’ omna ahi tausang tungnung teng) (r:16.3.25) (q:draft, low confidence)
zumhuai = (t:adj) (w:shameful/disgraceful) (d:causing shame, disgraceful; zumhuai-in gamta is act shamefully) (e:na ~ gamtatna teng na thuak kul hi/gen ding nangawn a ~ ahi hi | it is shameful even to speak of/pawlpi lakah thu a gen ding uh a ~ hi | it is shameful for them to speak in the church/Pasian in amaute ~ lunggulhna khut sungah a pia hi | God gave them over to shameful lusts) (s:mindaihuai/maizumhuai) (a:zahtakhuai) (r:26.16.58/49.5.12/46.14.35/45.1.26) (q:draft)
zumhuaina = (t:n) (w:shame/disgrace/nakedness) (d:zumhuai, shameful, with the noun suffix na: a shameful thing, a disgrace; also the shame of being seen naked) (e:~ thuak khin zo hi/na ~ teng kimu ding hi | your shame will be seen/na ~ a kilat loh nadingin | so that your shameful nakedness is not exposed/sam sau a neih leh, ~ ahi | if he has long hair, it is a disgrace) (s:maizumna/mindaina/zumna/minsiatna) (a:pahtawina/minthanna) (b:zumhuai) (r:24.48.20/34.3.5/23.47.3/66.3.18/46.11.14) (q:draft)
zumhuaipi = (t:see) <zumhuaipi-in>
zumhuaipi-in = (t:adv) (w:shamefully/disgracefully) (d:zumhuaipi, very shameful, with the adverb ending -in: in a shameful way) (e:a ~ a gamta uh hi/Amaute khan’sih uh a, ~ bei uh hi | they die young and perish in shame/a ~ a gamtat theih nadingun | so that they might act shamefully/a ~ guaktanga na omna uh | your shameful nakedness) (r:45.1.27/18.36.14/45.1.26/66.3.18) (q:draft)
zumhuaisak = (t:v) (w:disgrace/put to shame) (d:zumhuai, shameful, with the causative suffix sak: make shameful, bring disgrace on) (e:A gam buppi ka ~ ding a) (s:maizumsak/mindaisak/zumsak/minsiasak) (a:pahtawi/minthangsak) (b:zumhuai) (r:24.51.47) (q:draft)
zumin = (t:v) (w:being ashamed/in shame) (d:zum, be ashamed, with the linking ending in; mai zumin is with shame of face, put to shame) (e:mai ~ ka lungam hi/Kei hong sawmte mai ~ mindaisak ta in | may those who seek my life be put to shame and disgraced/Tua ahih manin, ~ lum ni | so let us lie down in shame) (b:zum) (r:24.31.19/24.3.25/19.35.4) (q:draft)
zumkhak = (t:n) (w:holiday) (d:apparently zum office with khak shut, a day on which business is closed; in the verse zumkhak hun stands for the New Moon festival when grain could not be sold) (e:~ hun sung i ngak lah hi) (r:30.8.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
zumkhakna = (t:n) (w:holiday/day off) (d:zumkhak holiday with the noun suffix na: the keeping of a holiday, with work stopped) (e:pawi bawlna leh nasep khawlin ~ om hi) (b:zumkhak) (r:17.8.17) (q:draft, low confidence)
zumlai = (t:n) (w:office records/register) (d:apparently zum office with lai writing: galkap zumlai a kem is the one who keeps the army records, the officer who enrols the people) (e:galkap ~ a kem galkap mangpa’ lai-at) (r:24.52.25) (q:draft, low confidence)
zumna = (t:n) (w:shame/disgrace) (d:zum, be ashamed, with the noun suffix na: shame or disgrace; zumna thuak is be put to shame) (e:~ a thuak kei ding hi/~ leh mindaina a piang sak tapa | a son who brings shame and disgrace/thu-mu theite in ~ thuak ding uh hi | the diviners will be disgraced/a tawntung ~ leh minsiatna a ngah ding uh hi | they will receive everlasting shame and contempt) (s:maizumna/mindaina/zumhuaina/minsiatna) (a:pahtawina/minthanna) (b:zum) (r:45.10.11/20.19.26/33.3.7/27.12.2) (q:draft)
Zumna = (t:n) (w:shame) (d:zumna, shame, written with a capital at the start of a line or sentence; zumna mel thei lo is shameless) (e:~ a thuak kei ding hi/~ mel thei loin hih bangin na paktat hi | shamelessly you played the prostitute like this) (b:zumna) (r:60.2.6/26.16.30) (q:draft)
zumsak = (t:v) (w:shame/put to shame/humiliate) (d:zum, be ashamed, with the causative sak: make someone ashamed) (e:Lawpna in hong ~ lo ding hi/Kong ~ nadingin hih bangin gelh ka hi kei hi | I am not writing this to shame you/Pasian in lungpilte ~ nadingin leitung mihaite a teelkhia hi | God chose the foolish of the world to shame the wise/a nei lote na ~ uh hiam | do you humiliate those who have nothing) (s:maizumsak/mindaisak/zumhuaisak/minsiasak) (a:pahtawi/minthangsak) (b:zum) (r:45.5.5/46.1.27/46.4.14/46.11.22) (q:draft)
zun = (t:n) (w:urine) (d:the liquid waste of the body; in the verses paired with ek, excrement) (e:amau’ ~ mah dawn dingin/amau’ ek mah ne-in amau’ ~ mah dawnin | eating their own excrement and drinking their own urine) (r:12.18.27/23.36.12) (q:draft)
zun = (t:v) (w:be ripe/be fully ripe) (d:of fruit on the tree or vine, often after min ripe: a min a zun, min zun mahmah, very ripe; used where the English has first ripe or early fruit; exact sense not certain) (e:a gah a ~ theikung tawh kibang ding/gah a ~ kiuhkeuh leenggah tawh kibang hi | it was like grapes bearing ripe fruit/a min a ~ sitset theigah muh tawh kibang hi | it was like seeing fully ripe figs/theigah min ~ mahmah tawh kibang ding a | they will be like very ripe figs) (s:minta) (r:34.3.12/28.9.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
zune = (t:v) (w:drink/feast/carouse) (d:drink liquor, from zu, fermented drink, and ne, consume; mostly in the pair anne zune, eat and drink) (e:Anne ~ dingin mite tu uh a/zukham thei mite tawh anne ~-in na om leh | and eats and drinks with drunkards/Tua hun lai-in zong anne ~-in om uh a | in those days too they were eating and drinking/~ anne le leitung nuntakna lunghimawhin | with drinking, eating and the worries of life in the world) (r:46.10.7/21.10.16/40.24.49/42.17.28/42.21.34) (q:draft)
zunek = (t:v) (w:drink liquor/drink wine) (d:form of zune, drink liquor, used before another word: zunek a hatte is those strong at drinking, zunek ding is what is to be drunk) (e:khamtheih ~ a hatte/Na ~ ding teng uh beimang khinta hi | all that you would drink is gone/~ kiphamawhte ahih loh nading | not to be people addicted to drink) (b:zune) (r:23.5.22/56.2.3/29.1.5) (q:draft)
zunekna = (t:n) (w:drinking/wine drinking/drunkenness) (d:zunek, drink liquor, with the noun suffix na: the drinking of wine or other alcoholic drink, also heavy drinking) (e:~ tawh ka lung nuamsakin/annekna, ~, le na khat peuhpeuh | eating meat, drinking wine or anything else/~ hangin a lung a nop ciangin | when he was merry with wine) (b:zunek) (r:21.2.3/60.4.3/45.14.21/17.1.10) (q:draft)
zung = (t:n) (w:root) (d:the part of a plant or tree that grows in the ground; zung kha means take root) (e:a sat ciangin ~ kha zo lo/a ~ in tui omna lei thukpi sung ban hi | its roots reached down to the deep waters/poding ~ nangawn ne uh hi | they ate even the roots of the broom bush/Mihaipa in lim takin ~ kha ngei napi | though the fool had taken root well) (s:singzung/zungpi) (r:41.4.6/23.11.10/26.31.7/18.30.4/18.5.3) (q:draft)
Zung = (t:n) (w:root) (d:zung, root, written with a capital in the title David’ Zung, the Root of David, and at the start of a quotation) (e:David’ ~, Judah pawl pan Humpinelkai/~ tawh kibotkhia-in tuipi sungah na po in | be pulled up by the root and planted in the sea) (b:zung) (r:66.5.5/42.17.6) (q:draft)
zungbawh = (t:v) (w:uproot/pull up by the roots) (d:zung, root, with bawh, pull up: tear a plant out with its roots) (e:singkung ~ bangin mawhneite botkhia ding hi/mi khatpeuh in a phung pan ~ a | someone tears it from its place) (s:zunglot/botkhia/bawhkhiat) (a:suan) (r:20.2.22/18.8.18) (q:draft)
zungbawhin = (t:v) (w:uprooting/pulling up by the roots) (d:zungbawh, uproot, with the linking ending in: uprooting and then) (e:Muvanlai masa pen in ~) (b:zungbawh) (r:26.17.9) (q:draft)
zungbuh = (t:n) (w:ring/signet ring) (d:a ring worn on the finger; min gelhna zungbuh or min thuhna zungbuh is a signet ring used for sealing) (e:Faro in a min gelhna ~/ama khut tung panin a min thuhna ~ suahin | taking his signet ring from his hand/ka taklam khut-a khut ~ na hih hangin | even if you were the signet ring on my right hand/sum leh kham ~ khatciat | a piece of silver and a gold ring each) (s:khutbuh) (r:1.41.42/17.8.2/17.3.10/24.22.24/18.42.11) (q:draft)
zungbuhin = (t:n) (w:as a ring/as a signet ring) (d:zungbuh ring with the marker in, here as or like: make someone as a signet ring) (e:ka min gelhna ~ kong bawl ding hi) (b:zungbuh) (r:37.2.23) (q:draft)
zungbuhte = (t:n) (w:rings) (d:plural of zungbuh finger ring; min gelhna zungbuhte are signet rings) (e:min gelhna ~ leh nakbuhte/Ama khut ah ~ hong butsak un | put a ring on his finger/banbuhte leh taute, min gelhna ~, bilbahte | armlets and bracelets, signet rings, earrings/suangmanpha a kiphut ~ a bulh hi | he wears rings set with jewels) (b:zungbuh) (r:23.3.21/42.15.22/4.31.50/22.5.14) (q:draft)
zungkha = (t:v) (w:take root/be rooted) (d:zung, root, with kha: strike root, become firmly fixed; also written apart as zung kha) (e:a thuk lamah ~ kikin/itna thu-ah ~-in, khuam zong kiphut kipin | rooted in love and firmly established) (s:zungthuk) (r:12.19.30/49.3.17) (q:draft)
zungkha = (t:n) (w:bitter root) (d:apparently zung, root, with kha, bitter: in Hebrews 12.15 zungkha a nei singkung is a plant with a bitter root that grows up and harms many, where the other text has a kha kung a zung) (e:~ a nei singkung hong khangin) (r:58.12.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
zunglot = (t:v) (w:uproot/pluck up/root out) (d:pull out by the roots; of people, remove them completely from their land) (e:leitang panin nang hong ~ ding hi/a khuate uh na ~ hi | you have uprooted their cities/a leitang panun amaute ~ a | he uprooted them from their land/hih gam hoih panin Israel ~ ding a | he will uproot Israel from this good land) (s:zungbawh/botkhia/bawhkhiat) (a:suan) (r:19.52.5/5.29.28/19.9.6/11.14.15) (q:draft)
zungpi = (t:n) (w:root/main root) (d:zung, root, with pi, great: the main root that keeps the branches alive) (e:a ~ in note a hong hingsak/note in a ~ a hingsak hi loin | it is not you who keep the root alive) (s:zung) (b:zung) (r:45.11.18) (q:draft)
zungte = (t:n) (w:roots) (d:plural of zung: the roots of a tree or plant) (e:Lei sungah a ~ a teek zongin/Lei sunga ama ~ keu in | his roots dry up in the ground/a ~ panin a hiang khat hong gah ding hi | from his roots a branch will bear fruit/lei sungah a bul leh a ~ nusia in | leave the stump and its roots in the ground) (b:zung) (r:18.14.8/18.18.16/23.11.1/27.4.23) (q:draft)
zungthuk = (t:v) (w:take root/be rooted) (d:zung, root, with thuk, deep, used with kha: strike deep roots, be firmly rooted) (e:amah in ~ kha-in gam sung a dim hi/ama sungah ~ kha unla | be deeply rooted in him) (s:zungkha) (r:19.80.9/51.2.7) (q:draft)
zungzung = (t:adv) (w:very/exceedingly/so) (d:intensifier placed after a describing word: nuam zungzung very pleasant, lim zungzung very tasty, khum zungzung very sweet, gim zungzung very tiring) (e:kingah an in lim ~ a/na meel muh, nuam ~ hi | the sight of you is very pleasant/A kampaute, khum ~ a | his words are very sweet/a bahtoh ding nangawn gim ~ kisa hi | he finds it too tiring even to lift it/leenggahzu bangin khum ~ hi | very sweet, like wine) (s:mahmah) (r:20.20.17/22.7.6/22.5.16/20.26.15/22.7.9) (q:draft)
zuphung = (t:n) (w:banquet/feast) (d:found only in zuphung pa, the man in charge of a wedding feast, master of the banquet; zu is wine) (e:~ pa kiangah va paipih un) (r:43.2.8/43.2.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
Zur = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zur) (d:name of two men: a Midianite chief, father of Kozbi, killed by the Israelites, and a Benjamite of Gibeon, a brother of Kish) (r:4.31.8/13.8.30) (q:draft)
Zuriel = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zuriel) (d:son of Abihail, leader of the Merarite clans of the Levites) (r:4.3.35)
Zurishaddai = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zurishaddai) (d:father of Shelumiel, the leader of the tribe of Simeon in the wilderness) (r:4.1.6/4.10.19)
zusa = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:mouse/rat) (d:small gnawing animal, a rat or mouse, counted among the unclean animals) (e:voksa leh kihhuaina leh ~ a nete/savokphual, ~, innhikpi nam khempeuh | the weasel, the rat, every kind of great lizard) (s:simbeng) (r:3.11.29/23.66.17)
zusak = (t:v) (w:drop/let fall/send down) (d:zu, fall, with the causative sak: make rain, hail or food fall from the sky) (e:meiite in leitungah guah ~ hi/leitungah guah ka ~ ding hi | I will send rain on the earth/Topa in Izipt gamsungah gialpi ~ hi | the Lord rained hail on the land of Egypt/vantung panin an kong ~ ding hi | I will rain down bread from heaven for you) (s:zuksak/guahzusak) (b:zu) (r:20.3.20/1.7.4/2.9.23/2.16.4)
zusak = (t:v) (w:cause) (d:cause something to fall or come down from above, said of God sending rain, fire or manna) (e:Gomorrah tungah kaat leh meikuang ~ hi | he rained sulfur and fire on Gomorrah/kua in guah ~ ahi hiam | who makes the rain fall/guah tampi tak a ~ hi | he makes heavy rain fall/misiangtho lote tungah guah a ~ kim hi | he sends rain on the unrighteous alike) (b:zu) (r:1.19.24/18.38.26/18.37.6/40.5.45)
zusakin = (t:v) (w:raining down/sending rain/making fall) (d:zusak, cause to fall or rain, with the linking ending in: sending down, and so) (e:amau tungah manna an ~/a nget kik ciangin vantung in guah ~ | when he prayed again the heavens gave rain/guah tampi ~ na nosuak sak kik hi | you sent abundant rain and refreshed it/Amah in van panin guah hong ~ | he gives you rain from heaven/guahpi ~, gialpi kiasak in | pouring down heavy rain and making hail fall) (b:zusak) (r:19.78.24/26.13.13/59.5.18/19.68.9/44.14.17) (q:draft)
zusuk = (t:v) (w:fall/rain down/pour down) (d:zu, fall, said of rain, with suk, downward: pour down) (e:leitungah guah-in hong ~ a) (b:zu) (r:21.11.3) (q:draft)
zut = (t:n) (w:paint/coat/smear) (d:coat or smear a surface with pitch, plaster or the like) (e:kultal tui tawh ~ in/tua lawh pen buan leh kultal tui tawh ~ hi | she coated the basket with tar and pitch/a tungtham buan tawh na ~ uh hi | you daub it over with plaster) (r:1.6.14/2.2.3/26.13.10)
zut = (t:n) (w:cover/overlay/plate) (d:cover a surface with a layer of gold or bronze) (e:tuate kham tawh na ~ ding hi/Amah in kham tawh tua kherubte ~ hi | he overlaid the cherubim with gold/kham citak tawh ~ hi | he overlaid it with pure gold/sumngo tawh tuate na ~ ding hi | you shall overlay them with bronze) (r:2.25.13/11.6.28/14.9.17/2.27.6)
zute = (t:n) (w:wines/drinks) (d:zu wine or fermented drink with the plural te; leenggah zute is wine of grapes) (e:leenggah ~, khuakhal ante leh sathaute) (b:zu) (r:24.40.10) (q:draft)
zuthawl = (t:n) (w:betrothal pledge/engagement) (d:pledge given to seal a promise of marriage, literally a flask of zu, rice beer; zuthawl piaksa means pledged to be married, betrothed) (e:Josef a dingin ~ piaksa hi a/~ a piaksa a lawmnu Mary tawh | with Mary, his betrothed/midang khat in ~ a piaksa | promised in marriage to another man) (r:40.1.18/42.1.27/42.2.5/3.19.20) (q:draft, low confidence)
zutin = (t:v) (w:overlay/smear/rub/paint) (d:zut, overlay or smear, with the linking ending -in: coat with gold, rub with oil, paint the eyes) (e:tuate kham tawh ~/kham citak tawh a sung leh a pua ~ | he overlaid it inside and out with pure gold/A khuampeekte kham tawh ~ | overlay the frames with gold/amah in a mitte ~ a lutang zeem a | she painted her eyes and arranged her hair/mi tampi sathau tawh ~ a damsak uh hi | they anointed many with oil and healed them) (b:zut) (r:2.37.4/41.6.13/2.37.2/2.26.29/12.9.30) (q:draft)
zutkhat = (t:todo) (r:24.46.22) (q:draft, one verse only, said of Egypt becoming like a fleeing snake where the NIV has hiss; cannot tell whether it names the sound or the gliding movement)
zutkhia = (t:see) <zutkhia-in>
zutkhia-in = (t:v) (w:strip off/pull off) (d:connective form of zutkhia, from zut rub or strip with khia out: stripping fruit off a plant and then) (e:a gahte ~, a hiangte kuaitanin) (r:26.17.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
zutna = (t:n) (w:plaster/coating) (d:zut, smear, plaster or overlay, with the noun suffix na; the material for plastering a wall, or the overlaying of a surface) (e:~ dang la-in inn zut ding hi/a ~ kongkhak mungte panin khamte hawkkhia-in | stripping the gold from the doorposts he had overlaid) (s:kizutna) (b:zut) (r:3.14.42/12.18.16) (q:draft)
zutsiang = (t:adj) (w:burnished/polished) (d:apparently zut rub with siang clean: rubbed bright, said of bronze) (e:a khete sumngo ~ bangin tee daldal hi) (s:kinawtngil) (r:27.10.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
Zuzim = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Zuzites) (d:people living in Ham, east of the Jordan, who were defeated by Kedorlaomer) (r:1.14.5)
